crawling about the vents and explained that Tommy was. (Because that made it all so much better...) Then I made sure she understood that I just wanted to be sure it was hers and to make sure she knew it had been found. In hindsight, I'm really am glad I did talk to her about it. Clearly the sanctity of her sleeping spot is very important to her. She declared that she was going to have to find another spot and scurried off pretty quickly (possibly to move her lair right then and there). I am going to have to ask Tommy not to poke about in the other dark, hard to find and reach corners of the house next time I don't see him. I really don't want this to turn into some Byzantine game of hide and seek between them. <br /> <br /> The rest of the day was much like the previous and then opening night was upon us. Everyone who was anyone was there. There were over forty Changelings in attendance and quite a few mundanes of note from local media. So yeah, it was pretty fucking do or die. I worked the floor while Gawain manned the door. We had representatives from all the courts that had invested of course. Plus the day and night court sent a pair. They sat together and seemed more interested in scowling at each other than much else. I did my best to play hostess and I managed not to put my foot or any other appendage in my mouth. I finally met Madam Spidertoes and she was as regal and aloof as I'd been told. I don't think I impressed her but I didn't offend her either. <br /> <br /> Lori came out and made the rounds as well, doing a far better job of meeting and greeting than I did. Before the show, I headed backstage and gathered all the performers. Joan had warned that two of our Changelings, Chalcedony and Ginny, were relative unknowns, which in her guilty until proven innocent mindset made them possible loyalists. Given the sheer number of of us in one place, I did decide not to ignore her. Better safe than sorry and it was simple enough to get a feel for them while building a simple pledge to boost everyone's performance in exchange for a promise not to harm the patrons or house. The results were interesting. I only used my oath contact on the ones I didn't know. Lori's got the motley pledge after all. I couldn't get a read on Annika, she's too powerful and strong willed. But she also wasn't suspect. Both Chalcedony and Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne had broken their word in the past year and a day, but not a binding vow so it seemed unlikely they were going to break the one they'd just made. And Ginny's worst oath breaking was to violate some user agreements. Hardly indicative of a loyalist spy in my book. What was interesting was Austin. At some point he has broken a binding vow, longer than a year and a day but it's a strong taint that it still lingers on him. Still, his position in the Spring Court makes him unlikely to be a spy. But he is someone to watch closely. <br /> <br /> With the pledge in place, I headed to stand near the stage area while Gawain moved inside as the doors were shut. I was pretty fucking nervous as things began. But from the moment Ace stepped out everything went absolutely brilliantly. Ace's over the top crazy energy might get to be a bit much at the breakfast table but on stage he was perfect. Everyone came together and delivered. I'll admit, I did find myself watching Annika a bit more closely than some of the others and seeing her up there just made her suggestion of teaching me seem even more ridiculous. Even if she can teach me to dance, there is no way I can ever hope to deliver that sheer presence. She fucking owned that stage when she was on it. <br /> <br /> Lorelei used her glamour to make herself even more alluring than normal. It was like watching an angel descend and deign to grace us mortals with her presence and voice. While Annika demanded the audience's attention, Lorelei just drew it to herself irresistibly. They're like night and day really, but both are goddamn idols up there. <br /> <br /> There were a couple of flies in the ointment. The first one is an ogre by the moniker Captain Jack. Seems he's the local dusk court and latched onto Gawain as his rival, or as he put it 'nemesis'. I didn't sit through the entire explanation but apparently they hatched some sort of plan to have Gawain throw him out. I confirmed that Gawain had this under control and that I should just stay out of the way and left them to their Wrestlemania plotting. And sure enough, at the end of the show (apparently so that El Capitan could see the whole thing first) Jack starting getting loud and after a really poorly choreographed 'fight' Gawain bodily carried him to the door and threw him out. On one hand, it was a bit of a disturbance and I am going to make sure Gawain and his frienemy don't make a habit of staging their rivalry at the House. But on the other hand, the man seems pretty harmless and Gawain seemed to really find the whole idea really fun. <br /> <br /> Our other problem was far less jovial and is going to have to be dealt with promptly. The Dream House has a fucking ghost and the ethereal bitch decided to put in an appearance opening night in the backstage area where she scared the piss out of some of our mundane dancers. As luck would have it, Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne was thrashing on stage so I barely heard the commotion and none of the guests did. Also, Lorelei was quick to hit the girls with a the show must go on speech and calm them down. But seriously, we do not need rumors spreading among our talent pool and scaring off performers. More than that, we don't need this ghost to disrupt the show or decide to show her hanged neck to one of the patrons. And yeah, murder/suicide might be on the table. If anyone is killing someone in my bedroom, it's going to be me dammit.<br /> <br /> Once the show ended, things dissolved into an informal mingling since it was opening night. We were all eager to get the courts' reactions and happy to find they all seemed quite pleased with how things went. As changed as things were from the show, love (or at least lust) was certainly in the air. There was quite a bit of pairing off happening. Lori was the belle of the ball there unsurprisingly. She drifted through the room basking in the attention and leisurely deciding who was going to blessed with her company. Man, I sound like a jealous bitch don't I? But I'm not. Envious perhaps, but I don't begrudge Lorelei. I'd sure as hell do the same if I was that irresistible. But the fact of the matter is that she's all that and I'm the bag of chips. <br /> <br /> I had business before pleasure anyway. Once I'd paid my respects to the royalty it was time to speak to Madam Spidertoes about the ghost. Tommy had told me they sent a gravewright in to check for ghosts and the place had come up clean. Well, it was dirty now and I needed to know who to call. What I wasn't expecting was for her to send her messenger spider out to fetch the errant ghostbuster and call him to the carpet right then and there. Gunnar Friday is a fellow Autumn but he was sitting at the Summer King's table. He answered promptly, of course, and as soon as Madam Spidertoes told him there was a ghost I felt like shit. He started apologizing to us both and assuring us that he'd gone over every inch of the place and assuring us there had been nothing less than a decade old. The poor thing was practically groveling and I felt kinda like I was going to be sick because I'd caused it. I tried to help. I assured him that I believed him and I do. I suggested maybe that since the house was empty the ghost had been dormant or something. At last I pointed out that what mattered was that there was clearly something going on and that I needed his help because the only thing I know about ghosts is that I can't punch them in face with my knife to make them go away. That seemed to steer things to a more positive note though Madam Spidertoes still seemed unhappy with him when she ordered him to come out and deal with it. He promised he'd be out before week's end. Maybe I can make it up to him somehow when I speak to him privately. At the very least I can apologize for being a fucking tattle-tail.<br /> <br /> At that point I was thinking about the hell of Snow Globe. They'd deserved what they got. And if it hadn't been me, someone would have told on them. We were all bad people there and it didn't matter. Bad girls enjoy hurting people... Fuck but I'm a goddamn hot mess sometimes. So clearly it was time to distract myself. Picking a fight wasn't really an option so it was time to find someone to make me forget. And there was Becky Wan, the alabaster goddess from the pier with the wicked claws. My mind shifted gears right quick as I looked over to her table. Things had gone well before so I moved over and took a seat. We struck up a little conversation and I laid it on a little more directly. She just gave me that wonderfully wicked grin and flirted right back. It wasn't long before she said she was a little tipsy and needed a ride home. I told her that if she gave me a second to change into something more suitable I could take her home on my bike. And with that, the deal was sealed.<br /> <br /> I hurried back to my room and changed quick as I could. Again, magic dress for the win. As I was heading back through the kitchen I spotted Ace and took a moment to wink and remind him he'd promised to bite me. Of course, trying to tease Ace is an exercise in futility. He promptly won the banter by saying sure, he'd do it since I was pretty. Then he did pause to ask if I was still talking about poison because he'd do it if I really wanted but it was pretty fucking dangerous. I told him I liked danger and that I was going to hold him to it one of these days. And I will.<br /> <br /> I returned to the main room just in time to see Monica pick Gawain up and toss him over her shoulder. I bristled but from the way they were both laughing it was clearly all in good fun so I relaxed. I've never seen Gawain make a move on anyone and I've been afraid he was too caught up in me to. Of course, he wasn't the one carrying someone out off but at least he wasn't holding back. And Monica seems nice enough. Of course, I'll have to look deeper into her later, especially if this isn't just a fling. <br /> <br /> And speaking of flings, I had my own to see to. Becky was ready to go and met me halfway across the floor so I took her hand and walked her to the garage where I brought out my bike. I mounted up and threw her my best wicked grin as I crooked a finger. She lifted an eyebrow at the gesture but she walked over with a grin of her own. \u201cGet on and hold on tight baby.\u201d<br /> <br /> Oh did she ever... She threw a leg over the bike and nestled up against my back, pressing every contour of that amazing body against me as she wrapped her legs around my waist and her arms around my ribs. I felt her nuzzle at my neck so I turned my head to help her find my ear. \u201cYou know,\u201d she purred, \u201cYou should be careful what you ask for girl... I might not let go.\u201d Then her feet that had been rubbing along my inner thigh shifted until her heel found and dug into my crotch. I gasped but before I could do or say anything her hands had slipped up to seize my breasts, squeezing them hard and curling her fingers to sink those claws in deep. At the same moment, she bit down fiercely, jerking my head back with her teeth and tearing my earlobe. I arched and groaned, squirming under her sudden assault but she was wrapped around me like a second skin. Damn in just a couple of seconds she'd revved me up from ready to on the bleeding edge. No one has EVER hit my buttons that hard and that fast and that damn perfectly. I was trying hard not to thrash or cry out but fuck. We were still there in the garage and it was fairly dark but we were within plain sight of the mother-loving parking lot. But she apparently didn't care who saw or maybe she even wanted them to because she continued to dig in that heel and knead my breasts and worry at my ear. I was soaked. My nose was full of the smell of sex and blood and it jumped my pulse up another notch. I was whimpering louder and louder, flat out unable to keep quiet under that coordinated assault.<br /> <br /> And that was when I felt it. Rope was my first thought but it was soft and warm. And nobody else was there and every inch of her was already working me over so she couldn't be holding it. But whatever it was, it was wrapping around my throat and pulling tight. Suddenly my fear of being heard was gone as I couldn't breathe. I gave a tiny squeak and felt it touch my cheek. That's when I saw it and realized it was her fucking <i>hair!</i> Somehow she was even using her hair to play my body like an overtightened cello. I bucked and she just ground herself on my tailbone harder. I don't think it went on long but it sure felt like an eternity. An absolutely, mind-wreckingly, incredible eternity. Even once I exploded, she just kept coaxing and riding me like a goddamn thoroughbred. The wench was relentless and knew exactly what she was doing. My vision was starting blur when she finally let up, relaxing her hair's grip slowly as she brought me back down from the single most intense peak of my entire life. <br /> <br /> Seriously. Mount. Fucking. Everest. <br /> <br /> While I was trying to recall how to breathe and not fall off my bike, she kept holding me. Her hair stayed around my neck like a loose scarf and she let my bleeding ear go but kept her claws sunk into my flesh. \u201cLooks like first blood is mine Calamity darling,\u201d she whispered with a low chuckle, \u201cNow carry me home and we'll set the world on fire.\u201d<br /> <br /> I have no idea how we didn't get pulled over but I broke every traffic law short of the speed of light doing just that. Turns out she lives in a small but nice little place, not that I was paying attention at the time. We pulled up and she uncurled herself from me. Despite the California heat, I suddenly felt cold without her and I shivered as I watched her unlock and open the door. She looked back curiously, I guess because I hadn't followed yet. I took another deep breath and pushed up to dismount. I joined her there on the porch and looked up to her eyes.<br /> <br /> \u201cLook, I want this. Fuck, I <i>need</i> this...\u201d<br /> <br /> She frowned slightly. \u201cBut?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut I don't do relationships. I like you and I don't want things to be weird but I'm not making any promises. Tonight is just tonight.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cFair enough. No promises then, just a night of wild passion. I can accept that, but there is just one little thing Calamity...\u201d<br /> <br /> I tensed. Here it fucking came. I wasn't sure what but I just knew that it was going to be little like Thor's Hammer. The thought of having to ride away was physically painful but I kept my expression calm. \u201cYes?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou're already behind and you're certainly never going to catch up standing there talking.\u201d<br /> <br /> So yeah... We did keep score for a while but that went about as well as trying not to ruin the bed. (Note to self, call Becky and see if I owe her a frame on top of the new mattress and sheets.) At some point before the sun came up we managed to wear each other out and I ended up gathering her and holding her. I was tired but I just rested and stroked her hair (which stroked back, a very interesting experience...) while she slept. I found myself trying to imagine what sort of dreams she was having and the idea of using my contract with dreams to see was surprisingly tempting. I didn't, but I did certainly think about doing it. I also wondered about what sort of experience had formed the exquisite sexual creature in my arms. Yeah, sometimes I really wish I could turn my stupid brain off when it gets going but once the fighting or fucking stops it spins right the fuck back up. I had the urge to bolt, just to move to ride to do something but I wasn't going to slink out like a thief in the night. I mean, there is a difference between casual and callous. That and as delightfully fucked up as I was from the night I couldn't really move gracefully enough to not wake her.<br /> <br /> And like magic, her eyes fluttered open and she looked up at me. \u201cYou need to go,\u201d she said softly. I could tell from her voice it wasn't her telling me to but that she could sense my sudden restlessness. I nodded and she pushed up, stretching gloriously in the half light and groaning. She leaned in and reached for me, which I thought for a moment might be a renewal of things. But instead she touched me, tracing the deepest and worst of the marks and murmuring softly. I felt warm, not like from the temp but from inside. And when she moved back I found everything was still sore but the injuries themselves were healed. She gave this odd look, a sad little smile as she untangled herself from me so I could rise from the bed and start dressing. <br /> <br /> \u201cThat was amazing. Thank you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course it was,\u201d she answered as she rose and moved to her closet. She tossed me a shirt and crossed her arms as she leaned against the wall and continued to watch me. \u201cI always am.\u201d<br /> <br /> I caught the shirt and pulled it on, realizing my own from earlier was in tatters somewhere. Maybe from anyone else her comment would have seemed arrogant but her tone was matter-of-fact and maybe just a little sad. Or maybe she was just tired and my brain was reading in from the narratives it kept trying to write. I finished dressing and stepped over to where she remained. Before I could say anything or maybe lean in to give her a goodbye kiss she lifted a finger and put it over my lips.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo promises,\u201d she reminded me, \u201cBut maybe we'll do this again sometime.\u201d<br /> <br /> The ride in the predawn air was nice. I slipped in quietly and writing things down seemed like the best way to sort my head. I still feel as fucked up as ever though, so I wonder if this is really helping or if it's just a waste of damn time. Whatever, the sun's starting to come up. I'm going to grab something from the bar and watch it. Katt used to fucking love watching the sunrise... and at least I can remember feeling that way.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> The last couple of days just seemed to fly by. We did a more in depth inventory of what we had and what we needed to replenish. Cognac and cheese were at the top of the list. I guess Insincere Marguerite went through more of those two items than anything else. The bar had been pretty well stocked otherwise. We also, on Gawain\u2019s suggestion picked up some other food items just for us. Figured if we\u2019re going to make a \u201cthing\u201d of eating breakfast together then we\u2019d need the ingredients to make the food. I was all for the idea. I\u2019m not above admitting that I\u2019m still not over the novelty of hot food. Just sayin\u2019. So, one morning Gawain made dollar pancakes. Good stuff. I know he\u2019s probably cooking all this stuff mainly for Calamity and the rest of us just kind of luck out, but I still think we should do something to compensate him for his time. I\u2019ve been taking care of making coffee and doing some of the dishes. Maybe we, or those of us who are not too bad at cooking, can help him some time, or give him a morning off. <br /> <br /> Later, Lorelei asked the group of us, as we ate those delicious dollar pancakes, what kind of music we could recommend to her. She said that she was taken in May of 1978 and needed to update her music library, to kind of catch up. The others made suggestions of music that they liked, some specific songs and some just bands. I tried to remember the kind of music that I listened to when I was a kid, but I honestly couldn\u2019t. I remembered bits of Russian rock, a few refrains of American metal, but nothing substantial. When I was in Arcadia I seemed to lose my sense of self. I remembered my childhood, my family, heck even driving lessons, but it all seemed so distant. After I entered The Lady\u2019s service it was all gone. I think it happened in the cave that she found me in. I don\u2019t remember exactly, but that was where I agreed to be hers. After that I just forgot everything. The only thing that took up my thoughts was her. Guess It\u2019s a good thing that ogre in Claire Falls hit so hard. Knocked some sense into me. Also gave me a concussion, but what\u2019s a little head trauma when it brings back your common sense?<br /> <br /> Anyhoo\u2026I really didn\u2019t know what to tell her. I was wracking my brain while the others at least came up with something. Then it hit me. I remembered a singer that my sister really liked and admired, Tori Amos, so I suggested her. I think I remember something about her being attacked by a fan and rising above it. It seemed appropriate so I named her as my suggestion. We\u2019re all victims right? We just need to rise above what was done to us and keep on going. Yeah, keep telling yourself that Rime! Not everyone can overcome it. Not everyone wants to. I want to believe that these people that I\u2019ve pledged to support have that drive. We all made it out. That has to count for something. I have to make it count. I remember bringing people back to The Lady who screamed and cursed and fought me with every fiber of their being. I also remember those that thanked me from the bottom of their heart for returning them to her. I don\u2019t honestly know which was worse. I think I need a drink. I probably need several drinks. I should probably at least write down something of what happened before I get blitzed though. Maybe just one drink\u2026<br /> <br /> Also along the unexpected line, Ace asked if Insincere Marguerite had ever stolen a turtle from a pet store in Arcadia. It seemed completely of nowhere from my perspective but she took the question in stride and answered that she had. She also boasted a bit about being the best non-Gentry thief in Arcadia. And something about turtles being cool because they are houses that eat lettuce, or something along those lines. Ace took it all in stride. He said that the thought he remembered something like that happening. From what he said he seems to be missing some of his memories as well. I\u2019m not sure if he\u2019s missing the memories of his mortal life as well, but he didn\u2019t seem too sure on exactly how he got out of Arcadia. In his attempt to escape he poisoned his keeper and was thrown against a wall for his trouble. He was helping someone else get out. Sounds like they might have returned the favor. Anyhoo, Lorelei seemed to get uncomfortable with Insincere Marguerite\u2019s declaration so we didn\u2019t let the conversation go on too much longer. Probably for the best. She doesn\u2019t know us too well, we don\u2019t know her too well, and what happened to each of us in Arcadia is not something you just share with anyone. It\u2019s moments like that, that make me feel horrible. She almost flinches at the mention of Arcadia. She seemed to accept the \u201clittle revelations\u201d in the Hollow with little to no trouble. I\u2019m thinking to be more accurate, she hasn\u2019t thought of what the Mirror House showed us at all. What happened in the Hedge stays in the Hedge\u2026 so what happened to her in the Hedge? What does she want to forget so badly? Is she scared? She\u2019s repressing it, whatever \u201cit\u201d is. Logically I know that is not the healthiest way to deal with trauma, but my solution isn\u2019t much better. See, I can be honest with myself. I\u2019m a mess. I compartmentalize my memories. Stuff \u2018em in a box and hide \u2018em away. I have to. I can\u2019t see the faces every night when I dream. I can\u2019t see them when I close my eyes. So, I lock them away. It\u2019s not foolproof, as my deep need for alcohol is attesting to, but it works well enough.<br /> <br /> Goddess! What the hell is wrong with me? I should be happy. We had a great opening night. Groups from the four seasonal courts and some of the others came to show their support. Hell, even the monarchs for the seasonal courts came.We had a good showing too. Ace was on fire, not literally. His opening was just wow. Annika had guys, and girls, drooling. And Lorelei\u2026damn\u2026.she was hot in that red wine dress. It flowed as she moved, and damn can she move. Insincere Marguerite looked great in that spiderweb dress. Skinny thing that she is, she filled it out very nicely. And Calamity, she wore that purple lightning dress, and she wore it well! When she tried it on earlier in the day I think the whole room went silent when she walked in. She looked nervous for a moment and then Gawain, our resident knight in shining armor, rather literally, asked her to dance. It was suggested that the tux might be more appropriate attire, and he ran off to change. In the meantime I looked up some medieval music for them to dance to.In those few minutes I think Calamity was nervous. She didn\u2019t look nervous, nah\u2026she\u2019s as good at not showing her emotions on her face as I am, but I could tell. She was nervous. Maybe it was just the dancing that she wasn\u2019t sure of. Maybe the outfit. I\u2019ve never seen her wear anything like that before, and she seemed a bit shy when she asked Insincere Marguerite to help her with the dress. I think it wrong footed me for a second to realize that. She comes across as so confident and secure, that I have to remind myself that she\u2019s just as frail on the inside as the rest of them. Not that it\u2019s a bad thing. We all have our breaking points. We all have feelings. Huh, I say \u201cthem\u201d like I\u2019m not fragile too. What\u2019s the saying, if you\u2019ve already been broken before you can\u2019t be broken again? Or does that just make it easier? How many drinks have I had? Fuck!<br /> <br /> There was something I meant to mention. I think I did tell Lorelei about it. Something about a swan. Oh, yeah! Annika mentioned something to me during rehearsal the other day about someone named Golden Swan. Used to run a really successful cabaret/burlesque house years ago. She thought that some of his stuff may have been left with the Spring Court before he died. I mentioned it to our resident Spring Cortier Courtier so she could look into it, or someone she knows could. Makes sense right? Anyhoo\u2026I think at some point Joan came to visit Ace before the opening show. I overheard her saying something to him about keeping an eye on Chalcedony and maybe Ginny. She said that they were newly escaped from the hedge and she wasn\u2019t sure of their loyalties as of yet. Ace promised to keep an eye on them. I think he enlisted Calamity to help with that too. Later Calamity came to me and asked me if I knew how to use guns. I said \u201cno.\u201d She pointed out the shotgun under the bar and told me to grab her if there was trouble. Sounded fair to me. I think it was after the show\u2026yeah, after, that I talked to Joan. Wait, I think the order of those events is wrong. Different day? I think Joan talking to Ace happened a day before Ace talked to Calamity. \u2018Cause the reverse just doesn\u2019t make sense. Then there was something about Haley, I think, warning Calamity about Andromeda. Apparently she doesn\u2019t believe the other woman\u2019s story about escaping. I think that was after the show?Ah\u2026who cares about the order of events. It happened. Something to keep an eye on anyway. <br /> <br /> Anyhoo..After the show I talked to Joan about The Director and her belief that there are loyalists in town trying to \u201crecruit\u201d people. Apparently some loyalists have been caught in town that work for Him. I\u2019m not sure of The Director\u2019s gender, if they have one, so I\u2019m going to use \u201cHim.\u201d It\u2019s not unknown for Him to do stuff like this, so I figured it would be good to find out as much as I can. She also mentioned to me the same worry she expressed to Ace about Ginny and Chalcedony. They don\u2019t act like loyalists to me, but then I didn\u2019t either. Or don\u2019t. No, past tense. I\u2019m not loyal to her anymore. Diane helped me remember myself again and I don\u2019t want to go back to being that cold person I was before. Not really. I did have fun sometimes. Rook and me made a great team and I know we had fun. Well, sometimes I remember it as fun, other times, not so much. We were good at what we did though.I sometimes miss that feeling of closeness. Someone that understands. I don\u2019t know if I want the folks I\u2019m with now to understand what I had with Rook. He was like a brother to me. We were not good people, when I look back it\u2019s clear as day. I don\u2019t honestly know if I\u2019m a good person yet. I think I\u2019m better than I was. Maybe. I think I\u2019ve had too much to drink. Damn I\u2019m a lightweight. I am kinda wiry, but it\u2019s mostly that I don\u2019t usually drink so much. I think I need to get some air.<br /> <br /> Okay\u2026back. I went up to the roof to get some fresh air. I was not alone on the roof either. Insincere Marguerite came up there tooa little while after I did. I think she was trying to clear her own head of things, not alcohol, but inner problems. I was clearing out both. The company was nice. We just sat there, looking at the stars and not talking. Insincere Marguerite was wrapped up in her robe, knees tucked up under her chin. She didn\u2019t really seem to be in the mood to talk, and I know I wasn\u2019t. It looked like she was working through her own issues anyway.She seemed a little surprised to find me up on the roof. It was rather late, or early, depending on your perspective. Concern crossed her face and it took me a second to realize why. I hadn\u2019t taken my usual care to blank my face. Who knows what she saw written there? Probably wasn\u2019t comforting. She asked if I was okay. I told her I just needed to clear my head. I thought about making my smile seem more confident, more \u201creal,\u201d but she\u2019d already seen me without my \u201cmask\u201d so there didn\u2019t seemed to be a point. She nodded and sat down next to me. I couldn\u2019t help by notice how pale she is. Maybe it\u2019s just the moonlight that makes it stand out more than it does in the daytime? I also noticed her eyes. They\u2019re normally a very pale blue, but this morning they seemed to have a hint of green in them. I thought it looked pretty. Then as she was heading back down she gave me a hug and smiled. I must look bad.<br /> <br /> Anyhoo\u2026while I was up there, I thought back over some of the stuff I\u2019d written and it seemed so depressing. Actually, it kind of reminded me of my fetch. Sort of. He\u2019s kind of doing the angsty/angry rebel thing. I only saw him for a bit when I was making my way south, but I heard him talking to his bandmates (yeah\u2026he\u2019s in a metal band\u2026hilarious) and he was just bitching about the dumbest stuff like it was gonna fuck up his life forever. Part of me really wanted to show him just how bad things could get so he\u2019d start to appreciate what he had, but I don\u2019t know if that might be a bit too much backsliding? Yeah, probably would be. Still tempting though. But I left him to wallow in his teenage angst. <br /> <br /> Back to the present. The other day while I was watching Gawain practice with his sword, Calamity came up to him and mentioned that she planned on going back to the Hollow to strengthen some of the security measures. Gawain, almost literally, dropped what he was doing to go along with her. I volunteered too. Making that place safer is good, plus I was curious about it. We got a good bit of work done patching up or repairing walls and such, and just moving debris out of the way. It\u2019s going to take a lot more work to get this place up to snuff, but we made a dent. Calamity seemed keen on shoring up the defenses of the place, as did Gawain. I think security is on pretty much everyone\u2019s mind right now. Most of us haven\u2019t been back \u201cin the world\u201d for all that long and still have fresh memories of the Lords, Ladies and Others that determined our fate up until recently. We\u2019ll probably have to discuss the particulars as a group when it comes to the defenses of the place. I personally don\u2019t think we should mess around\u2026any traps we make should be lethal. Maybe. I don\u2019t know. It seems like such a logical idea, but I got a flash of some scared changeling fleeing their keeper and wandering into our place to hide only to get killed. Maybe not lethal. Fuck\u2026what\u2019s happening to me? I keep second guessing myself. I used to be so sure of what I needed to do and how to do it. Now I\u2019m not so sure. Maybe I\u2019ll see what the others suggest as far as security and traps go and see how far from my ideas they are.<br /> <br /> Oh, something I missed from earlier, but is probably just as well considering how drunk I was\u2026 Calamity did a pledge with all of the performers. The idea was to give everyone a bit of a leg up (no pun intended) during their performances. What she said she was going to do to all those that weren\u2019t in the motley was to \u201cread them,\u201d I guess, and get an idea if any of them had broken any oaths. Mostly minor stuff came up, one person, I think Austin, had broken a pledge, but it was a while ago. Made me think. I had gotten so used to having powers and abilities that have to do with ice and snow, or others controlling darkness and knives. I hadn\u2019t really thought about someone being able to look into your past like that to see if you\u2019d ever broken your word. It\u2019s just a bit scary if you ask me. Yeah, I know I have things to hide, that\u2019s why it\u2019s scary! Would it pick up me betraying The Lady? Or maybe all the people I lied to when I assured them that I was taking them to a safe place? Some of those people I don\u2019t even have the excuse of saying that I believed I was taking them somewhere safe. Some of those people I deliberately led deep into the ice and snow to die. They betrayed The Lady, and I carried out the sentence with kind words and a reassuring smile on my face. I can\u2019t even say those were isolated instances either. I lost count. Goddess, I feel sick.<br /> <br /> I seriously need to get out of this depressive pit I\u2019ve found myself in. I could be the poster boy for the Winter Court, depressed icicle. Ha! While I was up on the roof I had an idea of how I can get to know my fellow motley-mates better. I can ask each one what kinds of things they like to do, and go do that thing with them. I have no idea what kinds of things these guys will come up with either, but I thought this might be a way for me to figure them out. Hell, I\u2019ll even go shopping with Lorelei if that\u2019s what she wants to do. Maybe doing normal stuff with folks will help separate the \u201cbefore\u201d from the \u201cnow\u201d in my head. Part of me is tempted to guess what each person will decide on, but the truth is I really don\u2019t know them that well. I know Calamity can fight. Gawain cooks some mean pancakes. Lorelei likes music, Ace is keen on not doing things halfway\u2026just not sure what things he does in his spare time, and Insincere Marguerite seems to like rooftops and cognac. Not the best mix, but separately, not bad. I guess I just want to find out who these guys are, what they\u2019re capable of and if I can trust them or not. Easy, right? Yeah, not likely. Ah, the irony. All these things I want to know about them, and me doing my best to hide that same information from them. Well, I guess except for the \u2018trust\u2019 bit. I really don\u2019t intend to hurt any of them. I was even ready to \u201crescue\u201d Insincere Marguerite the other night if it came to that. <br /> <br /> I guess I need to rediscover who I am. Figure out what kind of person Jacob Stojanovic really is, or can be. I don\u2019t think I\u2019m quite there yet though, and in the meantime I don\u2019t want the others to find out what kind of monster I have been.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T01:20:38-07:00","id":131851,"title":"","content":"<br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> Today was fairly busy.<br /> <br /> After my return, I met the rest of the Motley in the kitchen. Ace was going on about angry girl bands. Jacob was arranging to get the drinks better stocked, including more Cognac. Good Jacob. Lorelei wanted to know more about post 1978 music. I recommended nine inch nails for a band I greatly enjoyed, along with Caravan Palace, and Jolie Coquine for a song for her, since she wanted a specific song (also, closer, which makes me think of my Dearest). The mood was good and I enjoyed the interaction.<br /> <br /> While I was in there Ace asked me about robbing a pet store. I noted of course I had. It seems the pet shop in Arcadia that had the reputation for making excellent pets was his pet shop. He as a pet. I stole a turtle from there. I confirmed it was I, and noted I did so as it is a walking house that eats lettuce, and that is just neat. I perhaps got a bit proud, and declared I was the greatest non-Gentry thief in Arcadia. When Arcadia came up, Lorelei seemed to withdraw, so I sort of dropped it\u2026though I did make sure Ace was okay with the fact that I did not steal him. I mean, I am not sure what would have happened to him if I had. Mama Lion got the turtle, so I am unsure what happened to him, either.<br /> <br /> When that was done, Calamity shyly came up and requested that I help her with the lightning gown. She had allowed me to wear the spider gown on opening night, so helping her was the very least I could do. She is very hard on herself\u2026she was quite striking. I told her so. She seemed to accept my opinion, especially when Gawain came in and really liked it.<br /> <br /> Honestly, while she can be a bit prickly, I like Calamity. She seems eager to prove herself, strong yet vulnerable enough. She and Gawain make a good team. I hesitate to use the word\u2026trust\u2026but those two are probably the ones I trust the most, fond as I may be of Jacob or Lorelei. Not that I distrust or dislike any of us, exactly. Well, I do but not in a bad way. Well no more than they do I. Maybe that is better.<br /> <br /> I spent the evening getting everything ready for tomorrow. Julia called to say she would be at the opening night. She told me that this morning. I wonder why she called again? We spoke of art. We may have her do some posters for the Dream House.<br /> <br /> No matter, it is time for contented little grubs to sleep. I hope very much we can get over this \u201cgetting up in the AM\u201d thing once we are running the place. Getting up in the morning is a thing for the pedestrian.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> I had a most disconcerting conversation with Calamity. She found my nest. Well, not she, but worse someone else found my nest and told her about it. I hope they cannot read French. I like being able to sleep where I cannot be found. I am weak, vulnerable in my sleep. So easy to choke the life from. To stab. No, I must not be found while asleep. I must re-hide my nest.<br /> <br /> It is sad, the tight area smelled a little like me, and that meant it was mine.<br /> <br /> While I momentarily mistook Calamity\u2019s telling me this for boasting, I quickly realized that no, she simply sought assurance that it was me in the ventilation shafts. Understandable. I must still move my nest.<br /> <br /> How dreadful.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> I feared concerns about my nest being found would distract me tonight. I need not have worried. The evening went swimmingly. My sole distraction was something else.<br /> <br /> The problem with the gorgeous spiderweb gown is I am on catwalks above people\u2019s heads. I realize how shadows cling to me, but it\u2019s still uncomfortable. But opening night, I soldiered on, and reminded myself why I often don\u2019t wear skirts. Next time I hope it will be a social event with my feet on the ground. I also can only assume from below my fancy dress must have looked odd with my bare feet. At least I got to wear my stripy socks with it.<br /> <br /> The room gathered and let me say it was an absolute menagerie out there. There were over 40 of the Kind in the room, plus several on and around stage. From normal to nightmare in appearance. I spotted Julia in the audience and scampered out to speak to her. She had sat where I suggested for ease of being found, and had her sheets for sketching the acts and guests. Even some materials for watercolor. She kissed my hand when I approached, and while we said nothing about hooking up, her eyes smoldered as she looked at me. I do make an impression on people, it seems.<br /> <br /> I slunk back into position and the show began. Ace was quite awesome in his showmanship. Songs, stand up, all sorts of working the audience and performing. Anyone who would accuse him of being cold blooded because of his serpentine aspects would be very very wrong. Lorelei was quite a talented singer. She did Lady Marmalade, probably because it was covered in the bizarre American story of <i>Moulin Rouge</i>. She did an Army of Lovers song, which I enjoyed, as well.<br /> <br /> The others were good. Annika was positively mouthwatering and had most of the audience in the palm of her hand for most of the show. I have to say if I ever really think I am sexy I can remember her and remind myself I am a pallid little grub. Ginny Green did several torch songs, and Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne raised the roof with her music. Austin mostly filled in dancing and dueted with Lorelei, while Chalcedony was never a featured dancer but led the mundane women in some of their dances.<br /> <br /> There was a ghost at some point. We will probably need to do something about that.<br /> <br /> When the show ended, I stepped out and caught Julia\u2019s eye. She got the message and came backstage. She sashayed up with a grin, and was quite bold in her manner. I told her she was spending the night with me. Her boldness slipped slightly as she admitted she hoped I would say that. I took her to my room. I locked the door behind us. She was nervous!<br /> <br /> I left only a little light in my room and the shadows enveloped us. The detached artist was once again a timid girl. I laid her on my bed, and I took her. It was what she desired. I knew the exact moment her reserve broke, when she would do anything, anything for me. I pushed harder. She was delicious. It was glorious.<br /> <br /> Now Julia is asleep in my bed, and she smells like me. She no longer cares who knows about our relationship. Whether I am a man or a woman. What her sexuality is. As long as it does not end she is happy. I don\u2019t want her to leave. I want her. Well, her, Yvette, maybe a few others to be in my little web, where they will always, always be mine. This is very very bad. I must gather my willpower and send her on her way in the morning. Warn her of the danger. I must be strong. I must not be just like Mama Lion.<br /> <br /> Not that Mama Lion was like me. She did not take people into her bed. She was not a dirty, filthy little grub. Nonetheless, this path leads only to madness. I must act.<br /> <br /> Filthy filthy filthy.<br /> <br /> I did go to the roof to clear my head. Jacob was there. He was sad. I was unable to comfort him. I must check on him tomorrow morning. I hope he did not fall off the roof. He was buttered.<br /> <br /> But now, I am going to crawl back in bed and smell Julia some more. So sweet\u2026<br /> <br /> <i>End Session III</i><br /> <br /> So, a note on dates. We actually made an error figuring out what night would be Walpurgis. The 30<sup>th</sup> was actually a Wednesday, not Tuesday. I don\u2019t know how I got it mixed up but it happened. In world, we decided Monday was a day of preparation nothing really happened on.<br /> <br /> The nocturnal meeting between Jacob and Insincere Marguerite was determined entirely after the fact\u2026a second version of Insincere Marguerite\u2019s journal was actually sent out to add the encounter in after consultations with Jacob\u2019s player.<br /> <br /> During the show, I literally had almost 40 pictures out on the table, arranged in small groups based on what cliques were sitting together. I did not attempt to mimic their locations relative to each other, however.<br /> <br /> Calamity used Contracts of Oath and Punishment from <i>Winter Masques</i> to determine the past sins. She is not an Ogre, obviously, but her player got permission to start with the Contract. Also out of favored is Insincere Marguerite and Reflections from <i>Equinox Road</i>. The reference to a Contract to curse AIDS is referring to Healing Sacrifice from <i>Rites of Spring</i>.<br /> <br /> I think that covers things. Write ups for Summer and Winter Courts in a week, but even before then comments and questions welcome..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 05-11-2014, 06:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T18:43:09-07:00","id":144008,"title":"","content":"How well does Ace sing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T23:28:02-07:00","id":144218,"title":"","content":"We haven't really touched on his singing much. He is not at Lorelei's social level but about on par with Insincere Marguerite. He did pretty well at the show, but Willpower was spent and he used his ability to beef up his Presence with Glamour as a beast. While Expression is broad, in-setting he is better as a barker and comedian than singer, but a decent enough singer.<br /> <br /> I am behind all around on Journals, as I had work for one of my books I had to finish Thursday, and Thursday I also got hit with an awful toothache I only recovered from yesterday. I will be getting caught up with journal recaps asap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T00:33:15-07:00","id":144236,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time for our off week message for Changeling to go up. Rather than go straight into the Summer/Winter Courts, though, I am going to put up an email exchange that took place between the sessions for your viewing pleasure. Those Court outlines will go up in 2 weeks<br /> <br /> --<br /> From: Captain Jack Martinez<br /> To: Gawain Vert<br /> <br /> Gawain,<br /> <br /> Good work tossing me out last night. Not even an Ogre and you can lift like one! Good work! Definitely got some people talking!<br /> <br /> If you were not planning to go to the Beltane party tonight, I'll say you probably should. Your option, but it is a good place to meet people. Since neither of us are security tonight, I think we should restrict ourselves to some tough talk if the other comes up, but nothing that will get us &quot;in trouble&quot; as it were. If there is any specific &quot;trash talk&quot; that a gentleman might say but would nonetheless actually bother you let me know, would not want to impugn upon your honor. As for me just keep it above the belt and we are good.<br /> <br /> But maybe on Friday if you have time we can meet and chat? There is a place in Malibu called Koashi's that serves Kobe Beef, the good stuff. My treat! Just meet me at about 13:00 on Friday for lunch. I'll give you a view of the locals from outside the Courts, stuff that might be handy to know. I doubt anyone will be crass enough to confront us having lunch together, but we will kayfabe something or other about sizing up our opponent or whatever. I don't expect a problem though.<br /> <br /> Again, good work and let me know about Friday.<br /> <br /> Jack<br /> <br /> From: Gawain Vert<br /> To: Captain Jack Martinez<br /> <br /> Thanks, dude! That was tons of fun. I think this nemesis thing is gonna be awesome.<br /> <br /> I was totally planning to go to the Beltane thing. I mean, we just had an awesome party where everyone showed up, so it seems like it's just polite to go to other people's awesome parties too. Since it's all for fun and stuff, I can't think of anything that would bother me really. It's all cool.<br /> <br /> Lunch sounds great! I haven't hung out too much in Malibu proper, since I got back at least. It'd be sweet to talk with somebody about stuff around here. I've mostly been trying to get on my feet and stuff, but it's nice to find more chill people.<br /> <br /> Gawain<br /> --<br /> <br /> That sets up the meeting between those two massive fellows that takes place during session 4. You should get the whole session soon; I\u2019ve already got four journals and I am sure the last is coming. I\u2019ll see you then<br /> <br /> Comments and Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T11:30:59-07:00","id":145852,"title":"","content":"Not being in this game, I'm also waiting for the next update much like a spoon man waiting for his fix.<br /> /twitch","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is just my bright, shiny two cents.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing. I try not to argue in forums. It's like pouring concrete in a river. It doesn't get you anywhere in the short term and it poisons the environment long term.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2668-asmenedas","name":"Asmenedas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2668_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T01:51:07-07:00","id":149223,"title":"","content":"Glad you are enjoying man. And now your fix<br /> <br /> The grand opening has taken place! Now our heroes have a couple days to unwind and recover. Also, it\u2019s Beltane and we can\u2019t not enjoy that! Ace\u2019s player had to miss due to family commitments (he has to miss from time to time, it\u2019s not unusual) but everyone else was present.<br /> <br /> <i>Session IV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> May 1st<br /> <br /> Today was pretty chill for starters. I mean, there was the big Beltane party in the evening, which made Lori go all crazy, but what with the success of opening night and everything, I was feeling much more relaxed at least. Waking up next to Monica was nice for that too. She was all set to get up and make breakfast, but it\u2019s kinda gotten to be routine at this point, that I show up and make breakfast for the motley, so I didn\u2019t take her up on that. I did make sure I\u2019d see her tonight at the party. She was working security though, so it went a little backwards to opening night. Though I went home by myself this time. Not cause of anything bad or anything, I didn\u2019t piss her off. I think. I hope? Maybe I should have... I mean, wait til she got done and maybe invite her back to mine, not piss her off. I\u2019d need to clean up first though. I really wish I remembered how this works. I feel like I\u2019m missing something somewhere. Hopefully we figure out how this sort of thing works and soon.<br /> <br /> Anyways, Captain Jack was at the Beltane party too. We didn\u2019t even play fight or anything this time, but we kept making comments back and forth, me about how he could come back and get thrown out anytime, and him about how I took advantage of him being drunk and all. I did warn the motley about him, over breakfast. Lori was real confused, but at least everybody got the idea that Captain Jack was not actually a douchebag, and I wasn't being mean back, that it was a show kinda thing. Jacob showed up in the middle, so he was a little confused too, but he was mostly hungover. I tried to offer him some of the bacon and eggs I had left, but the smell made him a little sick. I thought greasy foods helped with hangovers. When he got back, I made him some plain toast, and that seemed to stay down ok.<br /> <br /> Which was good, cause we went skateboarding later! I had forgotten how much fun it was, but the circle between the garages makes a killer course and there were enough odds and ends to make a couple of ramps and grindboxes. See, we went shopping, cause Lori was all worried about the Beltane party. But she was being all girly about the shopping, talking about boutiques, and getting something fancy, and it being a pool and everything, so she\u2019d need a bathing suit and something to wear over it, and you know, girly stuff. Well, Jacob and I both gave each other a look when she used the work \u2018boutique\u2019 and so Lori decided that we boys should go shopping for boy\u2019s party clothes at whatever non-boutique places we wanted, and the girls would go to the boutiques. I was kinda sad - I mean, I certainly wouldn\u2019t have been able to find anything I could get at a place like that, but I totally would have been willing to carry the girls bags to watch Calamity try on bathing suits. And watching Insincere Marguerite and Lori try them on wouldn\u2019t have been the end of the world either.<br /> <br /> But, the girls had decided, so I took Jacob to the thrift shop near my apartment. The guy who runs it is cool. He\u2019s friends with the guy who runs the pawnshop under my apartment. We found some bathing suits and pool-kinda shirts pretty quick, but Jacob had mentioned wanting to do something with people in the motley, to get to know everybody better. So when we walked past the pawn shop, I saw the perfect thing - 2 skateboards, just sitting there waiting for us. Money was a little tight for it, but since I mostly eat at the House anyway, I really only have the usual bills, not much other expenses. And like I said, it was a rocking time, and I think Jacob had some fun too.<br /> <br /> We had plenty of time for it too. The girls still weren\u2019t home, even though they just went down the road and we went all the way to Santa Monica. Even when they got back, a good 3 hours before the party, Lori went inside immediately, saying she had to hurry and get ready. She kept giving me looks, especially when I mentioned we had 3 hours to go. I don\u2019t think she liked my Hawaiian print stuff.<br /> <br /> The party was great, though, even for all Lori\u2019s fretting. She relaxed alot once we got there, especially after she joined me for a bit of a smoke. There were tons of warm springs, some inside, some outside, a room with all kinds of food, and one of the springs even had this big fruit thing floating in it. Also! There were totally a whole bunch of dinosaur skeletons hanging around, cause they\u2019d been dug up there at the springs. It was sweet.<br /> <br /> Monica and Becky were both working security, and I got a hug from Monica. I tried not to bother her too much though. I mostly just wandered around, talking with people. There were lots of us there. Not as many as our opening night, but we are awesome like that. I talked some with Mary-Helene. I was just thinking of talking about music, cause I really liked her songs, but it turns out she skateboards too! She might join me a time or two after her rehearsal type things at the House, seeing as we just made up this awesome skateboarding area. She wound up going home with Lori after the party - I thought Lori was going to wind up with the Spring Princess, but the Princess left with Queen Charlotte, so I guess Lori lost out. She didn\u2019t seem too upset or anything though.<br /> <br /> Everybody except Lori headed back to the House though. Calamity brought someone with her, one of the alien ladies. She seemed really nice, but I think she tried to matching Calamity in her drinking and that didn\u2019t work out too great for her. Or maybe it worked out pretty well, I think they had some... fun as well as booze. I stuck around until everyone left, in case they wanted a ride back to the House, but Jacob and Insincere Marguerite thought a bike ride would be nice. I left a bit after that and headed back to my apartment.<br /> <br /> You know, I hope Ace is ok. He left breakfast real quick, and we hadn\u2019t seen him since. I think we were all afraid to actually open the door to his room, after he ran off muttering something about \u2018getting it\u2019 and \u2018that\u2019s perfect\u2019 when I wondered out loud if we could make it so piranhas could eat ghosts. I mean, it seems like an easier plan than a cow anyway. Cows are expensive (according to Lori) and take up lots of space. With a ghost, we\u2019d just need a small tank with a piranha in it. I\u2019m totally going to have dreams about piranha ghosts now, aren\u2019t I?<br /> <br /> <br /> May 2nd<br /> <br /> I got back to the House at my usual time, even though there wasn\u2019t anything specific going on. Well, except for lunch with Captain Jack, and I guess the House made a decent halfway point, you know? Plus, like I said yesterday, it\u2019s kinda our tradition now. Jacob did make sure I didn\u2019t feel like I had to make breakfast or something, that I could take a break sometime. But it\u2019s good, being able to do something for Calamity and the rest of them, to have a routine. Kinda like a family.<br /> <br /> Anyways, I made crepes, and Insincere Marguerite said they were good! I was a little worried, cause it\u2019s French and everything and she can be kinda particular about that sort of thing, but I guess mine \u201clived up to the name\u201d after all. Jacob asked me to teach him a little. It shouldn\u2019t be too hard. I mean, I mostly just cooked over campfires, but apparently I do good enough for everybody. Lori wasn\u2019t around when I started making breakfast, but she\u2019d showed up by the time Insincere Marguerite joined us, and I still had some batter left over, so I made her some too.<br /> <br /> Andromeda, that\u2019s the alien girl Calamity brought home last night, stuck around for a little bit. She is very tiny and kinda adorable. Apparently though, people don\u2019t like her. I guess Haily, the other alien girl, had been saying some stuff about her, that she liked doing stuff back in Arcadia. Which doesn\u2019t seem fair. I mean, after long enough there, things get... different, you know? She got out, so that should count for something. Though, I guess mostly people are suspicious she didn\u2019t \u2018get out\u2019 but was let out or something. She seemed nice enough to me. Anyways, she\u2019d started talking with Calamity last night cause she wanted an escort to go get goblin fruit. Goblin fruit seems really cool, so that sounds awesome, and if we\u2019re all there, or even mostly there (Jacob said he wanted to go, and Calamity was for it) then even if she\u2019s not on the up and up, then we can handle it. And if she is, goblin fruit!<br /> <br /> The others were making plans for the afternoon when I left for lunch with Captain Jack, and none too soon. I think if I\u2019d stayed much longer, Lori might have stabbed me with the butter knife. Not that it\u2019s my fault, she\u2019s the one who mentioned \u201cbanging out an act\u201d with Mary-Helene. Anyways, Captain Jack had invited me to this awesome place called Koashi's down in Malibu. His treat, which was good, cause I sure couldn\u2019t afford the place. He gave me the rundown on the area, and on him. L.A. is apparently crazy with the Day/Night stuff. Maybe I should ask Insincere Marguerite what\u2019s up with that. More locally, he said the Winter Court was really creepy, except for Lowjack, who\u2019s the guy that own the bar the others went to a few times. Not that they\u2019d done anything bad, just, you know, gave him an off feeling. I haven't talked with any of them really.<br /> <br /> He also warned me about the Summer Court. I usually get along well with them, what with the armor and the sword thing, but I guess they don\u2019t really like the non-seasonal Courts much. They don\u2019t want us to get comfortable, was how he put it mostly. The Lucian fellow is in charge of that, I guess, so the King guy doesn\u2019t have to worry about it. Also, apparently the guy named Percival is kinda an asshole, likes making people angry. Captain Jack approved of Monica though.<br /> <br /> He didn\u2019t have too much to say about the Spring and Autumn Courts, except that the monarchs were a couple kinda. Also, apparently, the Autumn Queen Charlotte sometimes eats people after she has sex with them. I think Calamity really likes her too. Like, like likes her. I should maybe warn her. I don\u2019t think it\u2019ll change anything though... The Spring Princess maybe kidnapped some girls, or maybe Queen Charlotte ate them. They are a little scarier than I would have thought. Well, I guess it\u2019s not a surprise with Queen Charlotte, being a spider, and Autumn being all about fear and everything.<br /> <br /> Oh, also Madame Spidertoes and Tommy Rawhead are both really old Autumn Court people. Calamity had mentioned them. Madame Spidertoes seemed pretty nice at opening night, but she stuck up with the monarchs the whole night, and I avoided having to deal with all the politics stuff.<br /> <br /> He also told me some about him. He\u2019d been a manager for professional wrestlers, before he was taken, which kinda explains his crazy nemesis idea, you know? He had a nemesis before, Red Madness (his real name is Miguel) but Captain Jack fired him out of a cannon. Not for real, of course, but Miguel was moving away, so they pulled this awesome trick and faked shooting him from a cannon into the ocean. We\u2019re gonna have to do some serious work to be that awesome as nemesises. But they were both part of an Entitlement thing, that\u2019s all about being talk about, so they had lots of practice with that kind of thing.<br /> <br /> We talked some about our Durances too. Captain Jack\u2019s captor apparently was confused about gladiator stuff, cause he had a big gladiator ring and all different kinda of gladiator type people, from different times - Jack, with his professional wrestling, actual Roman gladiators, some guy in a astronaut suit. He said there was all kinds of people that came to the Gentry\u2019s ring. I guess it does kinda makes sense, with the wrestling-gladiator connection. I dunno about space suit guy though.<br /> <br /> At some point we got to talking about swords - he had seen mine behind me at the House, and asked me about it. Eventually though, we had to head on, so I went back to the House to check on what was going on. When I got there, Annika was giving Calamity dancing lessons, though really, they were walking lessons. They were hot, anyway. I introduced myself to Insincere Marguerite\u2019s friend, Julia, and then decided the bar area needed sweeping. Alot of sweeping. It was going to take me hours, or whenever Calamity stopped moving like that on stage, whichever happened first, as long it was the latter.<br /> <br /> They did have to stop at some point, but Annika will be back on Wednesday to check up on her lessons, and plan out her next show I think. I will have to make sure I have nothing to do that is not in that room Wednesday. Before too long after that, Gunnar showed up to check about the ghost thing. I hadn\u2019t heard any details, so I tagged along when Lori told him about it.<br /> <br /> Gunnar shared some stuff too, about how the suicide stuff had gone done. There was some big mass suicide, then after that, women at the House said they were being watched, and sometimes heard whispers telling them they should hang themselves. One even got attacked by something she couldn\u2019t see, but managed to get away from what felt like a noose. Another girl probably had the same thing happen, but she didn\u2019t get away. After that, the House got closed down.<br /> <br /> There had also been another ghost, one that was more mischievous. Madame Spidetoes had thought the ghosts were both gone, and Gunnar had doubled checked, but now he thinks one of them is awake, and the other is dormant, in Calamity\u2019s room? I didn\u2019t like that one bit, but Gunnar did show us how to banish ghosts. I took to it ok - some of the concepts were a little over my head, but everything was pretty clear at least. He thinks the one that\u2019s awake is the mischievous one, since no one has mentioned whispering or anything like that, but that means the one in Calamity\u2019s room will try to kill her... Maybe I ought to stay here, at least until we deal with it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Okay, so things seem to be going well, both for the Dream House and for me personally.<br /> <br /> De la Rocha slipped out quietly yesterday morning while the others were having breakfast, with a quip, a kiss, and a promise to see me at the revel that night. I couldn\u2019t help smiling as I watched her dress. As I said in my last entry, there\u2019s nothing serious between us\u2026 but of all my dalliances since I came to the Golden State, she\u2019s the one I enjoy being with the most (well, her and Calamity, who is quickly becoming one of my best friends). There\u2019s a warmth between D and me that I don\u2019t often see, and I like it.<br /> <br /> In any case, her reference to the Beltane party gave me a wake-up call. I\u2019d been so focused on the Grand Opening that I hadn\u2019t given much thought to the next night. And of course, I had worn all of my best outfits in front of everyone during the show, so the question of what to wear was complicated. Sigh\u2026 when I was growing up in Defiance, I never had to worry about things like that. Ever since the Empress, it\u2019s almost like I have a pathological need to impress people by making myself as attractive as possible.<br /> <br /> This was on my mind as I walked into the kitchen to join the others for breakfast (bacon and eggs). Ace brushed past me on his way out, muttering something about \u201cghost-eating piranhas,\u201d but I figured it was just Ace being Ace. Gawain had more interesting things to say. He was telling everyone about his \u201cnemesis,\u201d Captain Jack. Apparently the two of them have decided to fabricate a rivalry for the entertainment of the masses, or something like that. Who knows why... Gawain compared the situation to professional wrestling, in that it was all show and no substance.<br /> <br /> That brought me up short, and we spent the next twenty minutes or so discussing the evolution of the game of wrestling during my absence from the world. It\u2019s <u>amazing</u> what\u2019s happened to that sport! It\u2019s been completely revitalized. It\u2019s like someone decided to synergize a boring old competition with comic book superheroes or something\u2026 they all have flamboyant names, colorful costumes, and pithy catchphrases. The drama is scripted, and therefore more interesting than anything that might occur simply due to random chance. Finally, something that jocks and theater types can enjoy together! I have to learn more about this fascinating invention.<br /> <br /> It was some time during this conversation that Jacob finally staggered downstairs and into the kitchen. I was a little surprised; usually he\u2019s one of the early risers, but yesterday he was bleary-eyed and miserable. I think he might have been hung over, but I opted not to inquire too deeply into his personal affairs.<br /> <br /> So we finished eating breakfast a little after lunchtime, and I brought up the notion of going out to pick up some new outfits for the evening\u2019s soiree. As expected, I got blank looks from the guys, but Calamity and Marguerite showed the appropriate amount of interest. I at least managed to convince the guys that they should get new bathing suits (the party was held at Glamour Springs), but they balked at the notion of shopping at a proper boutique, and opted to go off on their own.<br /> <br /> We only had to go to three or four stores before each of us found an outfit that suited us. Marguerite chose a pretty (if somewhat sedate) one-piece, while Calamity\u2019s selection was a shade more daring. I found a bikini in a dappled blue-green pattern that looked like sunlight on Caribbean water. It went well with my wings, and with the way my eyes look through the Mask, so it seemed a good choice. Luckily I was able to slip the back of it under my wings without it bunching up or looking strange.<br /> <br /> Jacob and Gawain were already back when we returned to the Dream House, even though they\u2019d gone all the way into Santa Monica to pick up their bathing suits. They were\u2026 interesting fashion choices. Gawain\u2019s was a bright floral pattern that didn\u2019t clash <u>too</u> badly with the Hawaiian shirt he\u2019d bought to go with it. Jacob\u2019s ensemble was more sedate, if not particularly exciting\u2026 pale grey trunks and a plain T-shirt.<br /> <br /> Guys are weird.<br /> <br /> So anyway, they had set up a series of makeshift ramps in the driveway and were zipping around on skateboards when we got back. Skateboarding was popular on the West Coast when I was Taken, but it hadn\u2019t really made a big splash in Iowa yet, so I watched fascinated for a few minutes while they rolled back and forth, doing three-sixties, and aerials, and kick-flips, and ollies, and\u2026 and faceplants, or something like that. I can\u2019t claim I understood much of what they said or did, but it was very visually striking.<br /> <br /> Of course, I couldn\u2019t just stand around and watch the boys play with the party looming a scant three hours away, so I dashed back into the house and started primping. In the end it didn\u2019t take that long, but I wanted to make sure I looked my best, so I took my time. Based on the reactions I got from the rest of the motley when I emerged from my bathroom dressed in my new bikini (and wrapped in a sarong that complimented its colors), I\u2019d say my efforts were successful.<br /> <br /> So once everything was ready, I hopped into my \u2018vette and drove down to Glamour Springs. We\u2019d talked it over earlier and decided to arrive separately, as many of us wanted the option of leaving separately later should the need arise. I think privately a lot of us were hoping to hook up with someone.<br /> <br /> I was too nervous for \u201cfashionably late\u201d last night, so I showed up a few minutes early, parked, and walked into the spa. My fellow Spring Courtiers really outdid themselves on this one. Glamour Springs was decked out with lights and colors like I\u2019d never seen before. Changelings and mortals alike were hob-nobbing, laughing, schmoozing, and drinking\u2026 though certain areas were roped off for \u201cVIPs only\u201d (meaning mortals were denied access). Buffet tables were laid out at strategic intervals, and there was even one large platter of fruit floating in one of the more placid hot springs.<br /> <br /> I did the supermodel thing and reached out a hand without looking only to find it holding a mimosa a second later. I took a sip and started to mingle. I met a lot of people last night, but honestly a lot of it is kind of a blur, for a couple of reasons. I know that I stopped by and chatted with de la Rocha and Monica for a bit, but Monica was working security, and I didn\u2019t want to distract her from her duties. D gave me a friendly little peck on the cheek before telling me to \u201cdo the Spring Court thing,\u201d by which I assume she meant I should go and be sociable.<br /> <br /> I traded in my empty mimosa glass for straight champagne and began to make the rounds. Eventually I found myself in the smoking section of the spa. Now, I\u2019ve been in California long enough to know that most public buildings don\u2019t <u>have</u> a smoking section anymore, and I\u2019d been to enough parties in high school to recognize that most of the room\u2019s occupants weren\u2019t smoking <u>tobacco</u>. It had been a while since I got high, and I figured I could use a little something to loosen me up, so I took an offered joint and stood quietly while the smoke drained the tension from my body.<br /> <br /> I had a pretty good buzz going on by the time I tossed the roach in one of the spa\u2019s temporary ashtrays. I\u2019m not sure if it was the drinks, the joint, or the combination of the two, but I was feeling no pain as I approached Princess Jolie and Queen Charlotte as they watched the guests enjoy themselves. They invited me to sit with them, and soon we were chatting and laughing like old friends.<br /> <br /> At some point \u2013 not sure how \u2013 I found myself reclining in Princess Jolie\u2019s arms. I\u2019d been flirting pretty heavily with both of the monarchs, and Jolie at least seemed to be responding favorably to my advances. Queen Charlotte offered plenty of risqu\u00e9 repartee in return, but I could tell she only had eyes for her co-monarch. She didn\u2019t seem to mind when the Princess started kissing me, though\u2026 which was good, because I don\u2019t think I could have stopped making out with her if I\u2019d wanted to.<br /> <br /> Which I didn\u2019t, of course. I\u2019ve harbored a major crush on Princess Jolie ever since I migrated to California three months ago, and when she had me in her arms last night, it was like nothing else existed except the two of us. I thought that was going to be it\u2026 that we were going to head into one of her private rooms at the spa and make love, and a part of me was a little sad about that, because I knew I\u2019d lose my image of her as the perfect woman after that\u2026 but we didn\u2019t. I don\u2019t know if it was out of respect for Queen Charlotte or for some other reason, but the Princess broke things off before they went too far, and left me flushed, panting, and wetter than the Pacific.<br /> <br /> Maybe that explains what happened next, at least in part. I was a little bit drunk, a teensy bit high, and extremely horny. I wandered off into the crowd. I think on some level I was looking for D, but I was also being fairly receptive to any flirts thrown in my general direction. I got a lot of come-ons and corny one-liners (some of which were old even when I was Taken), mostly from mortal guys, but a few of the guests seemed genuinely interested in me. One or two even shared some of my interests, and I got drawn into several interesting conversations about music and theater. Before I knew it I was deep in a conversation about the evolution of various musical styles with Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, I did more listening than talking, since I\u2019ve still got a lot of catching up to do as far as the music scene goes. Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne knows a lot about metal and punk, but can actually talk about nearly any kind of music you can think of, from classical to hip-hop. We\u2019d been talking for quite some time before I noticed that the crowd was starting to thin. I hadn\u2019t realized it had gotten so late.<br /> <br /> I glanced over at D, and she gave me a smirk, a raised eyebrow, and a thumbs-up. I couldn\u2019t help but smile and chuckle a little, which prompted Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne to ask if everything was okay. I apologized for my lapse in attention, and she took it with good grace. \u201cIt <u>is</u> getting pretty late,\u201d she commented with a theatrical yawn. \u201cYou want to get out of here?\u201d I nodded, slipped an arm around her waist, and told her that I\u2019d love to.<br /> <br /> We went back to her place, since she\u2019d already seen the Dream House (and I don\u2019t have my room quite the way I like it yet anyway). She lives in a nice house on the outskirts of Santa Monica. It seems to be the epitome of \u201crock star lifestyle.\u201d She has an incredible sound system, the function of most of which was entirely beyond my comprehension.<br /> <br /> She ushered me into the master bedroom, which featured an enormous bed covered in satin and velvet, and mirrors on all the walls and the ceiling. I later discovered that this wasn\u2019t the bedroom where she actually <u>sleeps</u> most of the time, it\u2019s the one she uses for\u2026 \u201centertaining.\u201d<br /> <br /> To go into details on the evening that followed would be tasteless\u2026 even in my private diary. Suffice to say that we spent a very enjoyable night together, and we kept each other busy until we both fell asleep from sheer exhaustion.<br /> <br /> When we woke up, we shared a simple breakfast (cereal, toast, and half a grapefruit each) and started talking about our act for this weekend. We decided to perform a punk version of Patti Smith\u2019s \u201cBecause the Night,\u201d a song that was getting a lot of radio play when I was Taken. It\u2019s familiar to both of us, and it lends itself well to adaptation, so changing it to suit Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne\u2019s signature style shouldn\u2019t be too difficult.<br /> <br /> Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne started in on the whole \u201cnot looking for a relationship\u201d speech at some point, and I just couldn\u2019t help it this time: I laughed out loud. Then I had to explain the joke to her. Since nobody in town actually <u>does</u> seem to be looking for a lasting relationship, the speech itself seems oddly unnecessary to me.<br /> <br /> I said my farewells after that and headed back to the Dream House\u2026 just in time to realize that I\u2019d missed out on Gawain\u2019s crepes! Gawain, big sweetie that he is, went back to the stove and made another small batch for my lunch. It was so nice of him that I can almost forgive the endless snickering he served up when I said that Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne and I had been \u201cbanging out an act\u201d for this weekend. It was an honest slip of the tongue.<br /> <br /> Oh god, I just read that last sentence out loud. At least I didn\u2019t say <u>that</u> in front of the others!<br /> <br /> The rest of today has been pretty normal. Apparently Calamity hooked up with Andromeda last night\u2026 she\u2019s one of the recent arrivals Joan warned us about, a girl who looks sort of like one of those grey aliens. She seems nice enough, but very shy. Apparently she\u2019s interested in going into the Hedge to pick up some magic fruit or something, but she\u2019s understandably scared to go in alone. Calamity offered to go with her, and said she\u2019d ask the rest of us if we wanted to tag along.<br /> <br /> I\u2026 don\u2019t want to tag along. I <u>really</u> don\u2019t. But I think I will anyway. If my friends are going into danger, they might need my newly discovered healing talents, and I\u2019d hate to think what might happen if one of them got hurt and I wasn\u2019t there to help them out.<br /> <br /> We had a little bit of business to take care of this afternoon as well. First of all, Annika decided to grace us with her presence again. She was impressed enough with the Dream House that she has decided to come out of retirement officially, and she wanted to hash out a contract. Calamity took care of most of the details, but when it came to creative decisions, she said that she didn\u2019t want to finalize anything without my input.<br /> <br /> I was floored. I mean, I know I\u2019m <u>working</u> as a performer at the Dream House, and I had a lot of input on the setup and content of our opening night show, but I didn\u2019t really think I\u2019d be taking on the role of \u201ccreative director,\u201d or anything like that. But I think I managed to conceal my nerves fairly well. We even managed to wrangle Annika into a pretty good contract, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> Hey, I might not like the queen bitch very much, but I can\u2019t deny that her presence will fill seats, and the good of the House has to come first. Annika will be performing in one show per week with an option to add a second show, and will not repeat any of her acts for at least a month. I\u2019m not sure what Calamity is paying her, but I\u2019m confident that we can afford it. And it looks like Calamity is getting dancing lessons out of this deal as well.<br /> <br /> I witnessed the first of these lessons. Well, to be perfectly honest, it was more of a \u201cwalking lesson\u201d than a dancing lesson. Annika was teaching Calamity how to command the crowd, how to draw their attention to her body and to tantalize and titillate them with her movements. And even though I think the whole spectacle was a little \u2013 oh, okay, I\u2019ll go ahead and say \u201cwhorish,\u201d while I\u2019m in my bitchy mode \u2013 I confess that I took a few notes. Annika knows as much about instilling desire in an audience as anyone I\u2019ve ever encountered.<br /> <br /> One thing that I found oddly touching is that Calamity seemed to think it was necessary to ask if I was okay with her taking dance lessons from Annika. She seemed so nervous and unsure about it, and for a while I wasn\u2019t certain whether she was asking because she knows I don\u2019t like Annika, or because she thought I might object to her \u201cstealing the spotlight\u201d from my own performances.<br /> <br /> It was a sweet gesture, but I assured her that her concern was unnecessary. There\u2019s more than enough adoration for everyone in our ensemble cast, and most of our acts are solo numbers anyway, so nobody\u2019s sharing the stage with anyone else. And just because I don\u2019t <u>like</u> that so-and-so doesn\u2019t mean I\u2019m <u>blind</u>. She\u2019s an incredible dancer, and if she\u2019s willing to pass her skills on to Calamity, then my friend would be hard-pressed to find a more capable teacher.<br /> <br /> After washing the taste of making nice with Annika out of my mouth, I had a much more pleasant conversation with Marguerite and Julia Oldacre. Julia has offered to sketch out some posters for our lobby. Having seen some of her work, I know she\u2019ll have some stunning promotional material for us in no time. She asked (sort of timidly, and only with a bit of prodding from Marguerite) if she could sketch me. I was flattered, and of course I agreed almost immediately. I asked if she wanted me to pose for her, or if I should provide her with some photographs from my modeling portfolio, and she told me that she prefers to sketch from life, so we\u2019re going to set up a few sessions over the next week or so and see what she comes up with.<br /> <br /> Just after the sun went down, Gunnar Friday showed up to look into our little ghost problem. He seems like such a nice guy; I\u2019m not sure why everyone calls him Ghoul. Oh, wait\u2026 \u201cGhoul Friday.\u201d I get it now; it\u2019s Autumn Court humor. In any case, I told him exactly what I saw in the dressing room the other night in as much detail as I could. He went over the house again, and found a bit more ectoplasmic activity this time around.<br /> <br /> Gunnar thinks there are two spirits inhabiting the house. One of them is murderous, the other merely mischievous. If his guess is correct, then it was the mischievous spirit that visited the girls in the dressing room the other night. It was just trying to scare us, after all, and didn\u2019t do any real, lasting harm.<br /> <br /> The other spirit poses a greater danger, and there\u2019s at least a chance that it\u2019s living in Calamity\u2019s room (which is apparently the place where several performers hanged themselves back in the 20s). Gunnar urged Calamity to move her belongings to another part of the house, and I quietly agreed with this suggestion, but we\u2019ll see what she decides\u2026 I think she believes that if she moves out of that room, the ghosts will somehow \u201cwin.\u201d Gunnar taught us a few simple rituals to help deal with angry spirits, but most of it was over my head. Oddly enough, Gawain seemed to understand the basics of ghost-hunting better than the rest of us, which is weird considering his usual down-to-earth personality.<br /> <br /> It was getting pretty late by that point, and none of us had had anything to eat since the crepes, so I offered to take us all out to dinner to celebrate the conclusion of our first week as an official motley. Everyone said that sounded like a fine idea, and we\u2019ve been getting ready ever since. I was thinking high-end Chinese\u2026 maybe Kaishin down in Malibu. That should make everyone happy.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 05-26-2014, 04:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T01:52:01-07:00","id":149226,"title":"","content":"<b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> <b><u><b><u>Friday May 2<sup>nd</sup>, 2014</u></b></u></b><br /> <br /> Days without stabbing: 5<br /> <br /> I put the sign up on the office door yesterday morning. At first I was just thinking of it as a joke but it's still there and I updated the count this morning (well, I think it might have actually been after noon before I got to the sign but I have been a busy little monster.) After watching the sunrise, I was struck, rather literally, by just how much I do not care for the Sun's angry gaze. I was also struck by the fact that I was sitting there with a bottle of Jameson's feeling angsty and letting my thoughts spin out of control like some sort of emo princess. Well, fuck that noise, there was shit that needed doing so I picked my sorry ass up and marched inside. I put on some coffee to cut the whiskey, fired up one of my nice cigars, and started to tackle the paperwork from our opening night's door.<br /> <br /> By the time Gawain popped in to make breakfast I had my game face on and my head straight again. I was a bit surprised that he was there around the usual time but he certainly looked like the night had gone well. When I asked he wouldn't say too much but he did confirm it was a good. I smiled at that and finished up while he got to work on some classic bacon and eggs. Monica really does seem to be a nice girl and she suits Gawain well. There was some real affection in the hug she gave him at Beltane. Of course, if she breaks his heart I will tear hers out and I still need to speak to some people about making sure it's not likely to come to that. Maybe Insincere Marguerite would help if I asked her. She seems fond enough of Gawain and her morals appear as flexible as the rest of her... I also bet Tommy might know a few things, he seems to have dirt on everyone after all. Hmm, I wonder just what he knows and tells people about me? Anyway, next chance I get I shall ask him about Monica. He might not share that as freely as some of the other things he's told me but I am sure I can work something out if I need to. Hopefully she really is the nice girl she seems to be and things will work out and they'll have the sort of relationship Gawain deserves. That would be wonderful. Of course, I also need to see what I can dig up on Captain Jack. He took Gawain out on a lunch date today, presumably to plan their rivalry or what not. Gawain was right happy and pleased when he got back. Hmm... Man, neither of Gawain's potential paramours are lightweights but Jack is fucking huge. If worst comes to worst, I will definitely need to recruit some help to move that ogre's body.<br /> <br /> So, everyone filtered in for the morning meal, though Jacob seemed rather worse for wear and wasn't up to anything more than black coffee and eventually a bit of dry toast. It seemed to be naught worse than a righteous hangover but I honestly have no idea what prompted his drinking. He seemed his usual cheerful self when I left with Becky (not that I was paying that much attention to be honest). But then, he's like me, he doesn't show what's inside. On the one hand, I'm a bit worried that what he's keeping buried is making him crack but as private as he is, I really don't know how to approach him about it. It's not like my shoulder is ideal for crying on anyway... The others didn't seem too concerned, except for Insincere Marguerite, who stared pretty deeply into his eyes for a bit and looked worried. I suppose she was feeling something much like I was, concerned but unsure how to do anything about it. Maybe I should try to talk to him later... start some sort of monster group therapy or something. Fuck, it would probably help me to share some of my damnable baggage with someone else... I don't know, fuck it, we'll see what happens tonight after dinner. Maybe we'll all get wasted and tell each other embarrassing personal secrets.<br /> <br /> Ace came and went, taking off while muttering something about having a brilliant idea that might take a little time. I fear it involves ghost piranha or feeding a ghost to piranha or something along that vein. He's barely poked his head out of the basement since and quite frankly I am worried. Hades only knows what he's cooking up down there. I'm going to see about dragging him out when we leave for dinner. He's a part of the motley and ought to be included in our celebration.<br /> <br /> Also, yesterday was Beltane (I apparently need a pagan holiday calendar for this fairy gig. I bet Google has something, the Internet provides after all.) And, as Lorelei reminded us, that meant a big party at the Spring Court's hot springs. Despite living so close to the beach, I didn't own a bathing suit. Apparently, neither did Insincere Marguerite. I guess it is a Darkling thing. Lori decided to fix that right up. At first, it was looking like a full group outing but I think Lori scared the fellows off with her loving use of the word boutique. Hell, she just about scared me off but I had no fucking clue what to wear and I didn't want to embarrass her in front of her court. So I figured the best course of action was to let her dress me up and then to stand around and try not to stab anyone. Besides, as long as she was buying it didn't matter how outrageous the prices were. (And they were. I swear, the less suit there was the more it cost...) I ended up with a few new outfits as did Insincere Marguerite (who also ended up short a few of her ill gotten credit cards. I really should mention to her that the shredder in the office can handle those things.)<br /> <br /> When we got back, Gawain and Jacob were skateboarding. They had set up a makeshift park in the private driveway circle between the garages and were going to town. They were also wearing some loud Hawaiian print shirts and trunks that didn't exactly match up. While I do understand how important the night and making a good impression on her court was to her, I still cannot help but giggle recalling the look on Lori's face when she saw them. For my part, it was nice too see Gawain enjoying himself and I think Jacob's smile was at least partially genuine. Gawain is seriously infectious when he's enjoying himself like that. Sometimes he can even make me forget what a monster I am... of course, he still doesn't know the truth about that night in Belleview and my parents. It's as good as lying to not tell him at this point but I'm just not fucking ready to handle the disappointment. I'm vain enough that I like the goddamn pedestal even if I don't fucking deserve to be on it.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I didn't stick around to watch them (though I think Insincere Marguerite may have) and went in to get ready. I hadn't filed the shards down recently, so that took a while. But I figured if I was going to rub shoulders with the Spring Court and other notables it'd be best not to cut any of them (at least not by accident...) Lori suggested that we travel separately, in case we didn't end up leaving together. Because it was a Spring Court affair and so, you know, there was going to be the sex. So I hopped on the bike and we were all on our way. It was everything I expected it to be. The hot springs are lovely, naturally sculpted and decorated with the replicas of the dinosaurs found when it was a tar pit. The main courtyard was enclosed with smaller areas sectioned off to allow privacy. The drinks and food and weed were flowing freely. My queen was there in a one piece suit, black with a red hourglass of course. She was with the princess, who was in a very tiny bikini (and of course wore what there was it perfectly). Becky was present, working security with Monica. I did greet her briefly but did not linger because she was on the job. Though unless I am mistaken nothing marred the evening. Gawain and his rival were both present and made a show of speaking about each other quite loudly, though they carefully avoided ever coming into direct contact with each other. I mostly just drifted about from drink tray to snack tray and made a few passing greetings here and there. At least until Andromeda approached me.<br /> <br /> The little dear is so cute and she has a certain earnestness and eagerness and shyness all mixed together in a delicious combination. I've heard from Joan about Haily's concerns about her but after spending the evening in her company, that dainty morsel is harmless. She was looking for an escort into the hedge to hunt for goblin fruits and apparently hasn't been able to find anyone willing to go with her. When I told her I would and I'd see if any of my motley were interested, she seemed surprised and pleased. I guess with everyone else giving her the cold shoulder she was expecting me to as well. We got to talking after that. Well, she did most of the talking, I just listened and prompted her and kept the drinks flowing. She got quite animated as she started to talk about the sex toys she's created and it was fucking adorable to watch. Also, some of the things she's built sound mighty damn impressive. I won't lie, there was also something a bit wicked about talking about the thrusting force and speed of her inventions in a public setting (even one that featured a bathtub full of condoms). Well, maybe it was the topic or the copious amounts of alcohol but after a while she screwed her courage together and made a play for me. The poor little sweetling was so deliciously shy and nervous... fuck if I was going to turn that chance down. I took her hand and lead her to one of the private areas, which surprised her a bit. I don't think she'd quite expected me to take her hints that far but I was sure as hell not in the mood to stop with just a bit of making out. I swear I think I could hear her heart beating. Once we were alone, she confessed that she hadn't been with anyone since returning and that she'd been drawn to me because I was a bad girl. I just laughed a bit and told her I'd show her just how bad I was. And that's exactly what I did. Well, we were in a semi-public place and both a bit drunk but I still worked her hard. She didn't resist and before long she actually warmed up to it right nicely. It was quite delightful but once we'd finished, she passed out soundly. I'd like to take credit for that but I am pretty sure the booze had as much a hand in it as than I did.<br /> <br /> So, I couldn't leave her there and I didn't know where she lived so I ended up bundling her up and carrying her out with me. Lori was making time with the princess so I did not bother her. (Apparently it was Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne she wound up spending the night with however. Also they apparently worked on a routine at some point as well, yay for multitasking.) I let the others know I was leaving and headed home. Andromeda is even lighter than she looks like she should be, and given that she's tiny that makes her mighty easy to carry and gather onto the bike. I got us both back to the house and to my room. I propped myself up against the headboard and gathered her into my lap. She was so tiny and fragile laying there and it didn't escape me that there wasn't anyone else in the house to hear her. But she was out cold and I was tired. Fuck if I didn't dream about doing <i>things</i> to that precious little sweetling though. Yeah, <i>she's</i> a real menace to us all...<br /> <br /> This morning came earlier than I would have liked but once my little toy stirred I woke up. She was understandably confused and hung over and embarrassed. It was cute listening to her timidly asking where she was and what happened. I tried to be comforting with the little darling and took her down to breakfast before giving her a ride back to her car. I suggested we should do it again, only at her place where we could try out some of her toys. She blushed but she clearly liked the idea. When I got back, Insincere Marguerite and Lorelei had joined us and Gawain (because he is thoughtful that way) made them some crepes from the batter he'd kept aside for them. I told the group that Andromeda was looking for escorts into the hedge. They agreed that she did at least seem harmless enough and that if she wasn't we could deal with it. They were also quite against me going alone. I wasn't sure how I felt about that but it was pointed out that she was much more likely going to lead her escorts into an ambush than try something herself. I still think she's on the level, though I suppose she might have been reprogrammed like some sort of cold war mole or, as odd as it seems to me, she might honestly think she's helping by trying to get us back where we belong. Well, if she is a loyalist I will just have to get medieval on her ass and take her apart, all slowly and painfully.<br /> <br /> After that Gawain was off to his lunch date and Insincere Marguerite asked about having Julia over to do some sketching of the theater for promotional work. (Is that what the kids are calling it these days...) I told her I certainly didn't mind. Hmm... I thought she had her eye on Lori. Guess maybe she's looking for someone a bit less unfettered. I mean, she and Julia certainly seemed to be rather lovey dovey.<br /> <br /> Annika came in in the early afternoon to work out a contract. Lori and I worked out the performing details of it with her and then she and I nailed down the professional side of things. And at that point, she was just like, time to start your training. Clearly she was dead fucking serious about it the other day. I'd spoken to Lori (as I know she's not terribly fond of Annika) but she seemed genuinely alright with me taking lessons and joining the show at some point. I didn't expect her to be a bitch about it but better safe than sorry and that's not the kind of shit you just spring on someone without warning. The instruction was all focused on attitude and how to sway my hips just so while walking. If the amount of 'sweeping' Gawain was doing was any indication, I was apparently doing something right on that front. I did also try to project the confidence she was talking about but I don't know that I will ever have quite the same level of well, whatever exactly Annika has. Maybe some of her will rub off on me during these lessons... Mmm... now that's a thought certainly, though I don't know if it's a good one on any level but it's certainly tempting. I think, for once, I shall at least try to exercise this self control thing I hear so much about. Lords know I've been getting around lately, might not kill me to dial it back a bit. Then again, why take that chance?<br /> <br /> At any rate, I am certainly feeling something less fun in my hips right now. I would not have thought that just walking could make one sore in such... interesting places. But Annika will be back on Wednesday and I'm to practice between now and then. Should be easy enough really, I just make sure I sway whenever I walk till then. I doubt anyone here is going to mind watching and I've sashayed my way through much more serious aches without batting an eye.<br /> <br /> After Annika left, I joined everyone in the seating area and got introduced to Julia. She seems nice enough and quite taken with Insincere Marguerite but I didn't get to speak to her much before Gunnar showed up to look into the ghost. Lori went over what she'd seen and he started checking the house carefully. He didn't encounter the ghost but he did find proof of active spirits in the basement (some sort of ectoplasmic pool apparently) and a presence in my room, which as it is the hanging room makes sense. There was some sort of mass suicide, followed later by a harmless trouble-making poltergeist and a suicide whispering ghost that attacked two girls and hanged one of them. It's all theory but he suspects the one we saw was the playful one and he thinks she and the hangman (hangwoman? You never know?) don't get along. Of course, they might also be the same ghost. (And still might not get along...) So, honestly not much in the solid answers department but Gunnar did go over some rituals to drive ghosts away and said he was going to confer with Madame Spidertoes as she's also a gravewright and old enough to have been around during the murders. He did suggest I might should switch rooms for my safety. I hate to let the damn things chase me out of my room but given how not punchable ghosts are it might be the wiser plan. Plus I didn't follow a lot of the finer points of the ritual work very well. I'm pretty sure Gawain was the only one of us that really grokked it.<br /> <br /> I'll think about it I guess. But right now, Lori's decided to take the whole group out to celebrate our one week anniversary and the opening night success. We're not opening for regular business until tomorrow so we have the night off and I can't say I'm not in the mood for a nice meal.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Ah yes, I\u2019m paying for that binge now. I got up much later than my usual and wandered down to the kitchen only to come in during the middle of a conversation about nemesis\u2019 and pretending to dislike one another. Something to do with Gawain and that guy he chucked out of the club the other night. Our resident cook offered me a plate of bacon and eggs and it was all I could do to excuse myself and run to the nearest bathroom. I\u2019m pretty sure I turned green. Which would have been interesting considering my tendency toward pale blue. Anyhoo\u2026after my stomach finished rebelling I went back to kitchen. This time Gawain offered me some plain toast and that seemed to sit much better with my stomach. And coffee\u2026can\u2019t forget about the coffee. I told him that we all appreciated him making breakfast in the mornings, but that he shouldn\u2019t feel obligated. We can trade out who cooks. I offered to do so after I\u2019d learned to cook something more than rabbit over an open fire.<br /> <br /> After a bit, Insincere Marguerite came down. Lorelei was going on about needing to get new clothes for the Beltane party tonight, so our resident French-woman came in quietly. Who am I kidding, she is always quiet. She barely makes a sound when she walks, which is a skill I can appreciate. As Lorelei was going on about shopping , Insincere Marguerite looked closely at me before looking away. She seemed intent, and I couldn\u2019t help but think that she was looking at me to see if I might break. I think I was a little annoyed at that, but I of course did not let that show on my face. It wasn\u2019t until later that it hit me. She wasn\u2019t looking for weakness, she was looking for the \u201cface\u201d she saw on the roof. The \u201cme\u201d without a mask on. Then I felt bad for my earlier thoughts. Insincere Marguerite is not one to show pity, at least not as far as I\u2019ve seen. She saw me with my walls down early this morning, drunk, depressed, and honestly thinking some less than personally healthy thoughts, but she didn\u2019t look at me with pity when she came up. I only saw an honest curiosity and concern in her eyes. Part of me wants to try and make up for seeming so cold at breakfast. It\u2019s just that it\u2019s so ingrained to keep up those walls, those masks, that I don\u2019t even realize when I\u2019m doing it anymore. That may be something to work on. The making it up to Insincere Marguerite thing, not the taking down my \u201cmask\u201d thing. I don\u2019t think I can do that just yet.<br /> <br /> Right now I need to focus on stuffing those depressing thoughts back down into their box. It was all I could do to stay sane after Rook brought me back to The Lady. I created those boxes in my head and tried to keep certain memories safe, uncorrupted. Others I just wanted to hide away and not see anymore. I couldn\u2019t completely keep out the memories of what she did to me in her anger, or what Rook did. Rook almost always used his knives. He knew knows how to inflict the maximum amount of pain without letting you die. Most of my scars come from him. Not all, but enough to give me nightmares. Yeah, gotta cram those memories back down into their boxes. Then there was The Lady. Goddess, the pain she could inflect with the wave of a hand. The things she did with ice. I\u2019m almost positive that I was just about to die several times, or maybe I did, but she brought me back time after time. Sometimes I wish that she\u2019d just let me die. Then that last time with Rook. He started to run his blade across my throat. He didn\u2019t usually start with something so possibly lethal. I\u2019m a little afraid of what he had planned if that was the \u201copener.\u201d I\u2019m pretty sure it would have worked too. He would have broken me and I\u2019d have given my soul just to stop the pain. I thank the Goddess every day that he was called away at that moment and the servant left the door unlatched. I don\u2019t know if it was dumb luck, divine intervention, or a combination of the two. I remember thinking in that moment that more than anything in the world I just wanted to go home and be safe. And here I am, \u201chome\u201d and mostly safe. My old life was taken over by a puppet, so I had to find a new one. I guess this counts. I have a place to stay. I have people who have said that they\u2019ll watch my back. I still feel on edge though. Not sure if that\u2019s going to change any time soon, but at least the need to run and hide far, far away is not as strong as it was when I first got out. Goddess, I\u2019m so screwed.<br /> <br /> Okay\u2026had to take a break. Took a moment (or two or three) to meditate and stuff all those thoughts and memories into the boxes and close \u2018em up. I can\u2019t let myself go down that road just now. Not sure when will be a good time, honestly. Just not now. It\u2019s getting harder and harder to keep it all contained. I know I have to do something better than my boxes. Something to actually get past the shit that they did to me, and that I did to others. I have to keep it together. I just don\u2019t know how.<br /> <br /> Anyhoo\u2026after breakfast wrapped up Ace wandered in and was kind of mumbling ideas to himself. I think Gawain mentioned something about wondering if ghosts could be eaten by piranha. Then Ace ran out of the room with a gleam in his eye and exclamations on his tongue. I told Gawain that whatever came of that was all his fault. And then, after the manic interlude we broke into two groups to go shopping. Gawain and I went by ourselves to look for clothes and swim trunks. Lorelei seemed keen on going to fancy boutiques and getting clothes and bathing wear to impress folks at the party. Calamity and Insincere Marguerite didn\u2019t look quite as excited as our dear Fairest, but they did look interested. It did look like Insincere Marguerite was planning on having some fun. I saw her going through several credit cards, keeping some and throwing away others. I\u2019m pretty certain her name from before (or now) is not Philip or Janice. To each his own. I\u2019d have done the same thing, but I\u2019m not nearly as good at picking pockets. Maybe I should ask for lessons? I can get lessons in larceny from Insincere Marguerite and lessons in cooking from Gawain.<br /> So, Gawain and I went to a thrift store that he knew of. Right below his apartment I think. It had some good stuff and we both found swim trunks and shirts to go with. Bright personality that he is, Gawain found trunks and a shirt to match that exuberance. Very bright. Very Hawaiian. I approved. On me it would look ridiculous, but it just seemed to work for him. I also mentioned while we were out that I wanted to get to know the members of the motley better and was thinking of seeing what kinds of things folks like to do in order to do that. Right after I said that Gawain got a big smile on his face, ran off for a second and came back with two skateboards. I smiled. The mental image of a large suit of armor skateboarding was too much. I had to agree. So, we took the boards back to the house and built some ramps and grindboxes in the driveway, and proceeded to have fun. It\u2019s been a long time since I had done anything with a skateboard, and even when I was a snotty kid I wasn\u2019t that good. If nothing else, I have become much more coordinated and light on my feet since entering The Lady\u2019s service, so skateboarding seemed almost easy.<br /> <br /> After a while the ladies got back from their shopping trip. Lorelei announced, and seemed rather concerned, that there was only three hours until the party and that she needed to get ready. I looked at Gawain and we shrugged. By my count it wouldn\u2019t take more than half an hour to shower and get dressed, but then I don\u2019t have wings or nearly that much hair. So, Gawain and I continued skating for a bit before Insincere Marguerite came out and watched us while painting her toenails. When she was done she seemed satisfied with her work and I asked if she\u2019d like to join us. I told her I could teach her how. She declined, but stayed to watch some more. After a bit we went back inside and went our separate ways. I thanked Gawain for the clothes and the board, and he thanked me for the afternoon. I thought it was a good exchange. Now I just need to see what kinds of things the others want to do. I hope Lorelei doesn\u2019t suggest shopping. She looked too gleeful at the idea before she left earlier. I mean, I\u2019ll do it if that\u2019s what she picks, but I can hope for something else, right?<br /> <br /> So that night was Beltane. We all took separate transport to the party so we would have the option of leaving separately later if need be. Insincere Marguerite and I road our bikes, Lorelei took her fancy car, Calamity took her motorcycle and Gawain drove his van. Though, before I get into everything that happened I should probably make note of the results of all that shopping the ladies did. Lorelei wore a bikini. Nice. With a wrap around her waist that complemented the colors of her suit. Just nice. Insincere Marguerite got a bathing suit that well, suited her just fine. And I do mean Fine. Calamity got a two piece suit that was a bit more daring than we usually see her wear, but again, very nice. I must say, it is nice to be surrounded by so many pretty ladies.<br /> <br /> So, the Beltane party was held at a hot springs run by the Spring Court. Very fancy. There were courtiers of all flavors around as well as some mortals. There was food, drink, weed, hell even a bathtub full of condoms. There were private rooms where folks could go to have a good time, and there were, as the place suggested, pools to swim in. Would it sound bad of me to say that while I did look at all the lovely ladies walking by, I was drawn to the hot spring? Seriously. A whole pool of water big enough to fit a dozen people easily, and not even cold. It was warm! I know. It seems so petty. The party was to ostensibly celebrate Beltane, though it was actually more of a social networking opportunity. Anyone who is \u201canyone\u201d was there, schmoozing. I did do some schmoozing, but had to spend some time in the hot spring. The novelty was too much. While enjoying the not frozen water, I saw Lorelei and Gawain smoking joints in the \u201csmoking section.\u201d Somehow I just wasn\u2019t surprised. I think Lorelei got more out of it though. It could have been the alcohol she consumed too, but she spent some time hanging out and flirting with Princess Jolie and Queen Charlotte. The two ladies were obviously into each other, but they flirted right back with Lorelei and I think they all had fun.<br /> <br /> Calamity spent a good bit of time talking to Andromeda. Not sure what the conversation was about, but they were both enjoying each other\u2019s company and eventually left for one of those private rooms together. Yeah, don\u2019t really need to guess too hard on what happened next. Let\u2019s see. Gawain had fun it seems. He and his \u201cnemesis\u201d had words a few times. Light threats, banter, that kind of thing. Knowing Gawain, at least for a short while, I knew it didn\u2019t really seem like him, but they put on a good show of it. I am glad that the gentle giant told us about his supposed rivalry between him and Captain Jack though. Things made much more sense. I think they\u2019re doing it because of some sort of rivalry/hostility between the Dawn and Dusk courts. As for myself, I\u2019m trying not to get too involved in the political stuff\u2026for any courts.<br /> <br /> So, after relaxing in the pool I sought out Ginny. Some folks are unsure of her intentions and/or loyalties since she\u2019s so fresh, so I thought I\u2019d have a chat with her myself. You\u2019d think folks would be unsure about me since I\u2019ve only been back a few months, but apparently I\u2019ve been vetted. I\u2019m pretty sure if there were any doubts about my loyalties I wouldn\u2019t have been given this job. Anyhoo\u2026talking to Ginny. She\u2019s a nice girl. Likes music. I mentioned some stuff that had been brought up by others in the motley and suggested that she get together with Lorelei if she wants to really get into the details. I am not a font of knowledge about music. I think I was in my own teenager way before I was taken, but that was so long ago. I feel so detached from that person. So, I\u2019m working on building up that store of knowledge that is a normal part of life. Ginny also mentioned that she likes singing. Lorelei is good for that kind of advice too. I said as much. She seems pretty straightforward to me, at least so far. We had a short chat and it was mostly trying to get to know each other a bit better. Nothing overly directed about her questions or comments. If she\u2019s not what she seems, then she\u2019s playing a long game.<br /> <br /> After talking to Ginny, Insincere Marguerite came over to talk to chat to me. She mentioned, in kind of vague terms something of her past. It didn\u2019t sound like her time spent in Arcadia was too bad all things considered. I decided then to ask if she had worked out whatever issue she\u2019d been contemplating on the roof the other night. She said that she thought she had. She also said that she was trying to resist her darker impulses. I got the impression that she used to indulge those impulses when she was in Arcadia. I can understand that. I certainly cannot claim to have remained virtuous while in the Ladies\u2019 realm. I think I made some comments along the lines that we do our best to get back to what we were before we were taken, but looking back I\u2019m not sure exactly what I said. I remember thinking that I had to say something encouraging to my new friend and I know I did, but it felt like my mind was being pulled in another direction. Back to memories best forgotten. I forced my attention on the young darkling and my vision seemed to clear.<br /> <br /> About the time that I was coming back to myself Flores came over to talk to Insincere Marguerite. Actually it was more that she was trying to pick up the quiet girl. Insincere Marguerite for her part looked really uncomfortable with the idea, so I thought I\u2019d step in. I explained that Insincere Marguerite and I already had plans. I realized later that my comments might have sounded more like we had a date planned rather than something friendly, but it worked. Flores left and Insincere Marguerite looked a lot more at ease. I brought up my idea of trying to get to know everyone better and she told me about her interest in \u201curban exploring\u201d as she called it. It seems to involve exploring places in a city regardless of whether or you\u2019re supposed to be there or not. Old abandoned buildings, empty rich people\u2019s houses, etc. Sounded like fun, so I said so. Insincere Marguerite brought up a couple of options for places to check out. I thought the abandoned hospital sounded like a neat place to explore. She seemed disappointed that I didn\u2019t want to break into those rich houses, but was content with securing company to check out the hospital.<br /> <br /> It was getting late by that point and some of the others had already left, or hooked up with partners for the evening. Gawain, the gentleman that he is, stayed until the end to see if anyone needed a ride back to the house before he left with his own date. Insincere Marguerite and I declined the kind offer and said we\u2019d ride our bikes back to the house. It was a beautiful night, and the ride would be nice. I will admit that I was looking for an excuse to be able to look at the stars in the night sky. Sounds silly, huh? It was always twilight in The Lady\u2019s realm, never full night, so I didn\u2019t really get to see much in the way of stars while I was there. It\u2019s just another of those utterly boring things that I am still finding extraordinary. Just like the pool and hot coffee. Hell, three meals a day is a blessing that I still almost can\u2019t believe. Sometimes I even come close to eating that much in one day. I eat breakfast because Gawain is nice enough to make it, and for the coffee. I don\u2019t have much of anything for lunch, because honestly I\u2019m not hungry so soon after eating breakfast. Then there\u2019s dinner. So much food in one day. I will admit that sometimes I find myself about to stash an apple or granola bar for later. In case the meals run out. It\u2019s just been so ingrained that it\u2019s hard not to do. Even in service to The Lady I had to make do with infrequent meals. We got the pick of the food that was available, but there wasn\u2019t much to be had. The Lady didn\u2019t really eat, so there would be food when she remembered. We were never bitter though. We were thankful for her bounty and took what she remembered to provide with loving thanks.<br /> <br /> Yeah\u2026depressing thoughts again. Well, maybe more bitter. Anyhoo\u2026 Insincere Marguerite and I got back to the house and she mentioned that she wanted to go up to the roof and eat some ice cream. I thought it sounded like a fantastic idea and asked if I could join her. We brought our ice cream up to the roof and admired the view while we enjoyed our dessert. It was nice. Looking up at the stars is always kind of relaxing. Being up there with Insincere Marguerite made it better I think.<br /> <br /> New day, new pot of coffee. Well, that and a bunch of other stuff. Let\u2019s see. Gawain came over and made breakfast again. Crepes this time. They were pretty tasty. Not sure if I\u2019d had them before. They must have been pretty authentic though \u2018cause Insincere Marguerite pronounced them good. I think our resident cook was a bit relieved at that pronouncement. It was kind of interesting to see Calamity bring her date from last night downstairs for breakfast. Andromeda seemed a bit shy, and Calamity was rather protective of her. It was really kind of sweet to watch. Calamity sat really close to her guest and stroked her hair and just radiated protective and gentle. I\u2019m pretty sure Calamity has had a couple partners since we moved into the house, but this is the first person that I\u2019ve seen her this way with. Anyway\u2026after Andromeda left Calamity told the rest of us about the other girl\u2019s desire to go into the hedge to collect goblin fruit. Apparently she is too afraid to go by herself, but most of the others in this town won\u2019t go with her. They are unsure of her motives and assume that she will betray them. Calamity seemed inclined to accompany her to keep her safe. I thought it would be interesting. Sources of goblin fruit are always good. I think Gawain was game too. Not sure about Insincere Marguerite, Ace or Lorelei. Lorelei looked positively green at the idea of going back into the hedge for any reason, but I got the impression she was gonna suck it up and come with us anyway.<br /> <br /> Around noon-ish Gawain left to go have lunch with Captain Jack. I guess they were going to plan out their encounters. Not exactly sure of the details. I\u2019ll have to ask him later. Then later in the day Annika came over to give Calamity dancing lessons. Apparently she starts dancing lessons with instruction in how to walk sexy and project the right kind of image. I will admit that I enjoyed watching those two strut across the stage. Gawain was quite happy to sweep the same section of floor for a goodly while so he would have an excuse to be near the stage so he could watch. I eventually stopped pretending to do work and sat down with Insincere Marguerite and Julia to watch. Damn they were a fine sight to see.<br /> <br /> That was the pleasant part of the day. A little after Annika left Gunnar came over to the house to check out our ghost problem. Yeah, I forgot to mention that. Apparently the dancers, including Lorelei, saw a ghost in the changing room during the opening night. Freaky, right? So, he comes over to check things out. While he was doing this he told us the history of the house. Apparently several decades ago there was a mass suicide at the house. A whole bunch of women hanged themselves. Then years later dancers would hear voices, some trying to convince the ladies to take their own lives. Once dancer felt something grab her and start to wrap something around her neck. She managed to escape. Another dancer was not so lucky and was found dead. About that time the house was closed, until we opened it back up that is. Gunnar said that he could feel a presence in Calamity\u2019s room and recommended that she sleep somewhere else until the issue could be resolved. He was not sure if the presence that he sensed was the mischievous one or the malicious one.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m pretty sure Gunnar went on to explain something else, but I\u2019m not sure what it was. I\u2019ll have to listen to the others and see if I can pick up what they discussed. Truth is, I\u2019m not sure what happened. I was standing with the others, leaning on a door frame toward the back of the group. I think he made some gesture and the light hit his face just the right, or maybe wrong way, and everything just kind of fell away. I was suddenly thrust into the memory of one day with The Lady, after I betrayed her. She was standing before me in her blinding white dress, hair pulled up and a terrifying smile on her face. The whole front of her was covered in bright red blood. My blood. I think that was the first time that I prayed, really prayed, for death. I prayed that They Lady would go too far and would not be able to heal me. I remember the cold manacles around my wrists, chained to the ceiling, holding me up. The metal was so cold it stuck to my skin and pulled small patches off. Then the blood would run, and freeze to the manacle. The drips of blood sometimes made it all the way down my arm. Sometimes they froze before they got that far. Part of me was aware that I was leaning against a door frame in the dance house, and yet I could feel the cold metal on my wrists. I could feel the rivulets of blood running down my arms. I could feel\u2026.<br /> <br /> I came back to myself with a soft gasp I think. At least no one looked at me like I\u2019d made a loud noise. I did my best to cover it up with a cough and continued like nothing had happened. I need to spend more time securing those boxes apparently, if I\u2019m having waking nightmares, or flashbacks. Whatever you want to call it. I can\u2019t let it happen again. I really wanted to be able to say that I would not be suddenly broken by a place to stay, warm food and friendly faces if The Lady could not break me, but I don\u2019t think that\u2019s true. I think she did break me. In that instance that I was praying for death. I think she accomplished what she was going for. I think she won. Goddess help me. I need to try and put myself back together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 05-26-2014, 05:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T01:53:44-07:00","id":149227,"title":"","content":"<b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> Today went reasonably well.<br /> <br /> The morning was awkward. Julia asked me to be in a committed relationship with her. I declined, noting I am still not prepared for such yet, having been only a few days since we agreed we were not ready. I managed to tell her there was a woman I was not over, and that I was fighting a major possessive streak. I could not bring myself to tell her of Arcadia though, or my desire to keep her. I simply told her that to try and be committed while not over this other girl would be unfair to her, and that I was worried if I did commit my possessive streak would make our relationship unhealthy. I assured her, however, that I still wanted a relationship with her, and if she wanted to call me her girlfriend she could but\u2026it was not exclusive, though I won\u2019t be sharing my body with just anyone.<br /> <br /> Right now there are only four people really that I am attracted to. My Dearest, Julia, Lorelei and Jacob. Lorelei does not seem the sort for committed relationships until her beauty begins to fail, which as she is a Changeling could be quite a long time. Julia I am involved with, my Dearest I am trying to not seek out, and Jacob, well, he is a boy and I don\u2019t foresee settling down with him. Assuming he even likes girls.<br /> <br /> Oh yes, and Annika, but saying I am attracted to Annika is like saying I breathe air. Is anyone not attracted to Annika?<br /> <br /> I do suppose I am fortunate I fell in with a GLBT-friendly Motley. As a queer woman, I was somewhat worried about things in the States, but apparently if one is going to be a GLBT I am in the right state for it. There are other good ones, but they are cold.<br /> <br /> I came down after Julia slipped out, mulling the whole girlfriend thing over. She was too disappointed for breakfast. I don\u2019t want anyone to get the wrong impression about us, but throwing in that we are still available seems crass. I wandered into the dining area to hear talk about ghost eating piranha, and as the ghostliest member of the Motley started to walk back out but was called back in. It was ham and eggs. I searched Jacob\u2019s eyes for the Jacob I saw the night before, but he was not there, and Jacob was confused, as was I. We went shopping.<br /> <br /> Lorelei likes shopping. I like shopping with other people\u2019s money. Calamity liked getting new stuff. It worked out. The boys went elsewhere. I was frankly surprised Gawain was not eager to follow Calamity around, but maybe he saw the wild glint Lorelei got in her eye when shopping came up and fled. I could have, I suppose, but it seemed rude to blow her off and shop alone myself. Social stuff is awkward.<br /> <br /> I got a bathing suit and some more upscale clothes. I also got some black and magenta checkered socks. I did not get a car. I need one for getting to places for glamour gathering.<br /> <br /> When I returned the boys were skateboarding. I went out and watched while I painted my toenails. My toenails are perfect.<br /> <br /> The Beltane gathering was interesting. I spoke to Flores, Julia\u2019s friend, and hung out with Jacob. Flores was curious about Julia and I. I told her that Julia and I were romantically involved, but was not committed to anyone. Julia apparently also spoke of my unusual physical capabilities, as Flores wanted to ask about them. I was not comfortable with this line of questioning and told her so, then found Jacob. Jacob was talking to Ginny Green, the Ogre. We hung out. I spoke of my enjoyment of urban exploring and seeing the inside of places. He expressed interest in doing some urban exploring with me. He was less interested in breaking into rich people houses. Shame, they sometimes have valuable flatware.<br /> <br /> Not that I am a thief.<br /> <br /> Oh, and also while I was there De La Rocha, Monica\u2019s purple friend, told me Madame Spidertoes wished to meet me, since we did not meet at Walpurgis. I must ask Calamity what to expect. Maybe I can bring Calamity along. We can do Darkling things. Maybe.<br /> <br /> Around then Flores returned and tried to pick me up. Apparently the awkwardness of me sleeping with my lover\u2019s closest friend did not occur to her. While Flores smells very very good, I did not need that awkwardness, or to hurt Julia\u2019s feelings (it would have) so I turned her down.<br /> <br /> Jacob made comments that briefly made me think he was flirting with me. He was not. His loss. I would have slept with him. It was Beltane, after all. Elementals are confusing, I have decided.<br /> <br /> After Jacob and I hung out awhile, we returned to the house on our bikes. We got some ice cream and ate it on the rooftop. It was nice. Rooftops, I have decided, are better with Jacob.<br /> <br /> And now I sleep. Snug in a hidden bed.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Everyone gets up two hours before I do, and that is a bad thing. But Gawain set aside crepes for me, and for that he should be commended, even if his Court needs a better name.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Gawain, I am given to understand the alien looking girl named Andromeda was here last night and slept with Calamity. I hope that did not upset Gawain. Of course, he went off to meet someone named \u201cCaptain Jack\u201d who he cheerfully said was his nemesis but not really. Jack was buying him lunch. Was it a date? I am not sure. How do you tell if a suit of armor is gay? Same way as anyone else I suppose.<br /> <br /> Maybe I should just ask who is a LGBT in the group. I would not want to make anyone uncomfortable though.<br /> <br /> Annika, Julia, and Gunnar all came over today. All Darklings. Annika came to negotiate a coming out of retirement (did opening night not do that?) and begin training Calamity as an understudy (she could do a lot worse). Julia came to do some sketching and painting of the stage and such, and to see me. I introduced her to everyone, including Gawain when he returned.<br /> <br /> Of course, Julia mostly kept sketching my eyes. She did describe Annika as a recluse, which surprised me somewhat. Apparently she took the death of Golden Swan very very badly. Julia came long after his time, but heard of Annika and her self-imposed isolation.<br /> <br /> Gunnar came to look for the ghost. He did not find her. He did talk to us about how to deal with her, but it involves channeling faith as much as anything, and I am as terrible a Pagan as I was Catholic. I guess I am still a terrible Catholic, just a more terrible Catholic being also Pagan.<br /> <br /> Gunnar did pop up in the Catwalks while I was up there with Julia. I am sure it looked shady. I was just showing her my puppets.<br /> <br /> Mostly.<br /> <br /> With Gunnar gone, we are going to have a late dinner. We have been together a week as of two this afternoon. Speeding toward Walpurgis like a freight train and relaxing after it did not seem like a week, but that is good, right?<br /> <br /> I have revised my opinion of Gawain little. I still like him, despite my misgivings over his Court. I still think he and Calamity are a good match, though possibly a doomed one. He appears to be a good guy. A little clueless, though I am given to understand that is not uncommon with Elementals, as evidenced with my conversation with Flores. I am glad he is with us; I fear some might take advantage of his helpfulness and generosity. Maybe he will even move in with us at some point. I don\u2019t see why he hasn\u2019t; I do not smell bad. Not at all.<br /> <br /> Lorelei is nice, and I still find her attractive. To say she is full of herself would be unfair, but I will say she is acutely aware of her attractiveness in a way that is slightly off-putting. Maybe it is my feelings about Day Courtiers, but I feel she is in opposition with me when she isn\u2019t, and that is a shame. She was flirty at first but has grown considerably less so. Have I been cold? Perhaps. Has my newness worn off? Perhaps. Is it because I did not melt into her arms? Perhaps. Regardless, I hold no ill will toward Lorelei, and hope our friendship improves. I\u2019d hate to think the mystique put her off.<br /> <br /> Ace I also have become less wary of, much like Gawain. He is certainly bombastic, but not annoyingly so\u2026while he represents light to my darkness he is not my enemy. I apparently robbed the pet store he was in, which still amuses me. Ace seems to busy himself with his own projects a lot, and I know him least well. He seems the least sane of our number, or perhaps that is the notorious Beast tendency to be direct. Still, madness begets creativity, just sometimes it is an awesome routine on stage, sometimes it is a fixation with cows and piranha. Still, I like him well enough. He does seem quite fearless, which will be handy when we eventually face threats.<br /> <br /> I still really like Calamity. She along with Jacob I feel kinship toward, and this has grown into a fair amount of trust. Maybe partially because I think that if Calamity did not want me to be here, I wouldn\u2019t. Maybe. But she is a Darkling, she understands the need to be part of the shadows, she understands our changed souls. And while I am sure she feels closer to Gawain then I, there seems an unspoken bond of respect between us. Honestly, I like that. <br /> She is free to make it spoken and tell me how wonderful I am though. Calamity may not be as fierce as Gawain or Ace, but she is no less dangerous. Which is good.<br /> <br /> Jacob is an intriguing mystery, which of course makes me somewhat interested in him. On the other hand, I do not like being cold. I am skinny; I can\u2019t trap heat. Jacob likes rooftops much like I do, and seems eager to get to know us thus also I. He is quiet but not unfriendly. Still, the meeting on the roof two nights ago keeps coming back to mind. He won\u2019t let me in, so I don\u2019t know what is going on, and it just makes me what to know more. Which may be deliberate. If anyone in the group is dangerous to I, it is Jacob. But I don\u2019t think he is. Maybe.<br /> <br /> Well off to dinner, this Motley and I.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session IV</i><br /> <br /> Mostly socializing this time. Beltane was one of the two big \u201cNPC dumps\u201d in which we introduce a whole bunch of NPCs so the players have context for who they are, the other was the previous session opening night. Really now with the opening night done I am letting the players into the drivers seat, but I will still be dropping them some hooks.<br /> <br /> The version of \u201cBecause the Night\u201d discussed was inspired by the version with Garbage and Screaming Females, which is hella good if you have not heard it.<br /> <br /> They spent some group XP to raise the Wards on the Hollow to 1 after the work last session done there.<br /> <br /> The ghost stuff discussed was the rules in the core New WoD book. Ironically, the group is rather comically bad at them. Gawain was best, and he was mediocre. Some of them had chance dice. But as I noted before, this group seems to lean away from the more scholarly types, so not too big a shock, but an interesting contrast to, say, my Geist or Vampire games.<br /> <br /> That should cover this session, but comments and questions are welcome. In a week we will get around to those Summer and Winter write ups. Then in two weeks the next session, which takes place entirely that night and includes a great deal of confession and backstory for the characters, as they sit around and have dinner, play games, drink and talk. You might be surprised what comes out! See you then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T15:52:36-07:00","id":155246,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s \u201cOff Week\u201d again, and time to cover the other two Courts. I have two journals in had, 3 coming down the pipe.<br /> <br /> As before, they are spoilered as some info is not known by some players, though admittedly it is a little better known now it\u2019s mostly for consistency sake with the previous document. As before, It is the original handout plus bonus material, so there may be a slight tone change.<br /> <br /> Summer Court Handout<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Some stereotype the Summer Court as religious fanatics, but that is not true. Some are religious, some not, but they enjoy the trappings nonetheless. The Summer Court is based out of the Old Methodist Mission just outside Santa Monica between Santa Monica and Malibu. The Church is entirely run by Changelings, and has no regular human congregation but sometimes hosts gatherings.<br /> <br /> Viscount Augustine is the monarch of Summer, a powerful Ogre Gargantuan Render. Known for his gold armor, he is named for the Saint who, among other things, has his mother\u2019s name attached to the city, St. Monica. Viscount Augustine is Christian but not terribly fanatical. He sees the Gentry as abominations, but Faerie he does not judge so long as they do not side with the Gentry.<br /> <br /> Joan may be the best-known member of the Summer Court. A Fairest Bright One and Soldier, she is fairly religious and very popular, and often pursued. She tends to distrust the Spring Court, given the number of members who have tried to relieve her of her virginity, and otherwise pledged to steal her heart. There is even a betting pool. Fortunately, Joan is a formidable woman as well as a master of melee weapons, which with her beauty only has more people pursuing her.<br /> <br /> The Summer Court is on guard against the Faerie but also the chaos in LA. Santa Monica and Malibu have more Faerie coming and going than they can track, but at least the Courts are organized. The chaos in LA and Hollywood, with the Day and Night Courts closer and mad Hollywood Seasonal Courts farther, are seen as influences to keep out. The Summer Court is not concerned about the Directional Courts, who seem disinterested in expansion and who dislike the same courts the Summer do for the same reasons. They do not necessarily want to bar members of the Courts from the city, but distrust them, and come down hard on any attempt to establish a Court.<br /> <br /> Viscount Augustine and Joan are in favor of the Cabaret, of course, but worry others, especially the Winter Court, have agendas with it. They have warned Ace to not trust Master Darke for any reason. Also to watch out for Vampires, as they know some are out there and may be driven West by misguided hunts that are all the rage in Hollywood right now. They may look for new feeding grounds. While Augustine is not crazy about vampires, he has bigger problems than wanting to provoke them.<br /> <br /> o o o o<br /> <br /> While at Court you briefly met Old Billy, A Beast Steepscrambler and Riddleseeker. Old Billy is, well, old; he is apparently well over 90, which makes him a decent advisor to the Summer King despite his being a Beast. Old Billy seemed to see a lot of potential in you, so don\u2019t prove him wrong.<br /> <br /> There is also a rather aggressive Beast Roteater/Broadback named TJ. You don\u2019t know much about TJ just yet, just that he is around, an enforcer, and does not seem even remotely Jesus oriented.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Winter Court Handout<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> The Winter Court in Santa Monica is not as powerful as it is in many places. Let me rephrase that, it is not obviously powerful compared to some places. In fact, its tendrils are all over both cities.<br /> <br /> The base of the Winter Court is a local rehab center, which is ironic given the Court\u2019s role in drug trafficking. Drugs are an excellent source of sorrow, after all, possibly the biggest in tinseltown. The Santa Monica Community Rehabilitation Hospital makes a pretty good cover, and lets them keep an eye on how much the local drug use is, or is not, in check.<br /> <br /> Master Darke is the local Winter King. He is a Manikin Blightbent, looking like a man in a dark suit, fedora and sunglasses smoking heavily. His features seem almost plastic, and he never raises his voice. Master Darke is a quiet voice when the monarchs meet, but when he talks, they listen. It is fair to say many fear him more than any Autumn King.<br /> <br /> Master Darke is interested in how the Cabaret can further the Winter Court\u2019s goals, and is interested in supplying Jacob with drugs in exchange for a small cut of the profits. Master Darke guarantees there will be no trouble from law enforcement. If Jacob is interested, he can keep him supplied. If not, He won\u2019t consider Jacob an enemy, but he may not\u2026work as hard to look out for the club if it serves fewer of his needs.<br /> <br /> Also at the SMCRH is Doctor Bright, a second Manikin Blightbent. While it is difficult to say for sure, he really seems to bear a strong resemblance to Master Darke. Of course, no one has ever seen Doctor Bright in anything but his white work clothes, and he never wears a hat or sunglasses. Doctor Bright also never raises his voice, but his voice is gentle, not cold like Master Darke. As far as you can tell, he actually tries to take care of the patients at the clinic. As far as you can tell.<br /> <br /> o o o o<br /> <br /> Unrelated to Darke and Bright, there is a Wizened Brewer named John Lowjack who runs a bar that caters to the Fae called \u201cLowjack\u2019s,\u201d He is not really a part of the Court proper\u2019s organization but it a fairly well liked member of the Court, certainly the least creepy.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Session 5 journals in a week. Not much time advanced, but our heroes learn quite a bit about each other. See you then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T14:24:17-07:00","id":161976,"title":"","content":"One week after first meeting as a Motley, the PCs had a nice dinner and went back to play party games like Truth or Dare to get to know each other. They discovered more about each other than they were ready for.<br /> <br /> <i>Session V</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> May 3rd, very very early<br /> <br /> Wow. I\u2019m looking back at my last entry thing and I\u2019m glad I decided to write that stuff down <u>before</u> we went to dinner, cause that feels like forever ago. I mean, there\u2019s been alot of booze since then, so I better put down tonight before things get hazy or something, you know? I mean, I didn\u2019t even have <u>that</u> much, I started out just drinking beer even, but Calamity... I mean, I had to, you know, make sure she didn\u2019t finish the second and third bottle of rum by herself, you know, like she did the first. And, then, man... things got heavy. Like, seriously.<br /> <br /> Before all that, dinner was nice, fancy Chinese. Like, super fancy, you know? Lori paid, or there was no way I could have gone. She\u2019s really, really nice you know. While we were there, Insincere Marguerite had the idea to play a game, like the one where you ask questions in a dark room, or Truth or Dare, you know, the kid games where you learn things about people. She actually put shoes on, you know, to go in to the place. I think she took them off at the table though. The weirdest things keep popping into my head. Like, Lori can glide, with her wings, I don\u2019t think I knew that. Maybe I\u2019m just trying not to think about the important things, the big things.<br /> <br /> You know, like that Calamity killed her parents.<br /> <br /> I... I\u2019d known her visit home didn\u2019t go well. She was really quiet after - I was glad I remembered something about Santa Monica, to have something to do, somewhere to go. But I didn\u2019t expect... I didn\u2019t think... she\u2019d have done that. I mean, you know, I can\u2019t really throw stones I killed plenty of people, just cause they got shoved into some stupid story and had to make a stupid deal. Hell, I killed them if they didn\u2019t make the deal. But parents are <u>supposed</u> to love their kids, their <u>real</u> kids, not some fake, just because they wanted her to be some popular jerk instead of a quiet, smart, beautiful girl. It\u2019s not fair, what they took from us, what they keep taking.<br /> <br /> She feels really bad about it. She kept calling herself a monster, no matter how much we told her not. Kept saying killing was all she was good at. But it\u2019s not! She\u2019s smart, and sexy, and thoughtful, and focussed. She\u2019s really good at dancing too, well just walking so far but... damn. She\u2019s just amazing. I don\u2019t know where I\u2019d be or what I would have done if I hadn\u2019t found her. There was nothing pulling me out, no one I was going home to. I probably would have stayed lost in the hedge til the Dreamer found me again if I hadn\u2019t had her there, if I hadn\u2019t had a reason to...<br /> <br /> I told her that, well not that very last bit, and told her she wasn\u2019t a monster whenever she said it, but mostly I just held her close. She\u2019d moved to sit next to me when I started sharing the rum and I had a hand on her shoulder since Jacob asked about her rooms in the Hollow House. Thinking about it, that\u2019s when she started drinking for real, finishing off the first bottle by herself, when Ace started off asking everybody about their rooms there. She didn\u2019t answer then - took Dare. Jacob dared her to kiss me. If things hadn\u2019t gotten so... if Calamity weren\u2019t hurting so bad... that kiss by itself would make this the best night ever. It was a serious, awesome kiss, not some dare-kiss-on-the-cheek or anything. I couldn\u2019t help sitting closer to her after. I mean, not some \u201cI kissed you so now I\u2019m your boyfriend\u201d kid kinda thing, but she was still upset about the question, so I put a hand on her shoulder and it was so nice just being close to her...<br /> <br /> It made me feel a little bad later when Calamity asked if I \u201clike-liked\u201d Monica. If she\u2019d asked me at the pools, or even just before that kiss, I might have been able to say yes and not smell bad but... I mean, I like Monica alot. She\u2019s pretty and kind and gentle and strong but she\u2019s not... I guess, it\u2019s not really fair, you know? I don\u2019t, for certain.<br /> <br /> For all my gloom and doom, it was fun, for the most part, the Truth or Dare. Lots of talk of Arcadia and sex and stuff. Only Calamity and Jacob ever took Dare, so we learned alot about everybody. Lori had Jacob take his shirt off cause he didn\u2019t want to say his greatest regret. He\u2019s got lots of scars, and this brand thing, like a snowflake, on his chest. Calamity seemed to be getting to feeling better, after the question, though she kept drinking lots. But it was like, a calm in a storm. After the game, Calamity asked Lori about the whole church going thing - she goes cause her dad is the preacher. He doesn\u2019t know it\u2019s her - he thinks she used to be Catholic cause she keeps calling him Father. It was pretty hilarious at the time, but that was even later. Also, Jacob mentioned his sister was at the college in Santa Monica and Insincere Marguerite\u2019s dad is a cop in Paris and that\u2019s why she left. I didn\u2019t say anything, cause I don\u2019t remember mine. Nothing at all. Everything else has flashes, bit and pieces scattered - SCA, school, stuff about smithing and swords, even being in Paris as a little kid, but none of it had family in it. Not even being in a foreign country as a little kid! None. I was distracted enough thinking about it I didn\u2019t even notice Calamity getting tense until she crushed her cigar to bits.<br /> <br /> \u201cMy parents are dead. I did it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSome things can\u2019t be fixed.\u201d<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t wanna <u>fix</u> her or her life or anything like that. That\u2019s the bullshit abusers and dickheads shovel around to control people. I just want her to be safe. From herself, from her Keeper. I didn\u2019t like it, not at all, when she talked about them hurting her. I don\u2019t care if they were never angry and it was always measured and exacting. Those fuckers will burn in hell before they touch her again. I will move heaven and earth, I will fight to my last breath and beyond to keep them away from her. I will... be helpless to stop the scars they left from hurting her. It was their fault, THEIRS! that her parents are dead, with their lies that have just enough truth and their creations and their tortures. She\u2019s not a monster. She\u2019s not.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> After... well, after, it kinda turned into confession time. Lori had promised her friends they\u2019d all escape together and left them behind. It made me think of that final dream. I hope the Gawain woke up. Hope\u2019s all I really can do - there\u2019s no way to find him. I might recognize him but... where? Anyway, we might for look for Lori\u2019s friends, when we\u2019re even more awesome. Insincere Marguerite might try stealing rescuing them - not stealing, that\u2019s bad, cause Insincere Marguerite might turn into a Keeper if she keeps being so awesome at stealing, that\u2019s what her Keeper said. Her Keeper sounded much nicer, and maybe was a Changeling once too, and that\u2019s how she knows.<br /> <br /> Talking about things, joking around, seemed to give Calamity some space. Insincere Marguerite even joked about anyone else having something to get off their chest and Calamity had calmed down, well, drunk enough more to say that her shirt was still on. She was really, really drunk. Really. So after Ace took his pants off and threw them over the edge of the deck (he didn\u2019t have underwear on (I didn\u2019t want to know that)), I went to go get us some crackers and water. Jacob seemed to want to talk with her alone, so I slid out and let him take over being-leaned-on duties. We had to wake her up a little to get her to have some crackers - if my half-memories of SCA drinking sessions tell me anything, she\u2019s gone far enough those crackers will be back up again later. Better than throwing up nothing but alcohol, you know? I got her all set up in the spare bedroom though, the one without evil ghosts. It seemed good, cause there\u2019s this corridor that is just for that room. I\u2019m gonna sit right here, nap in this soft corner. In case she needs me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Dairy</b><br /> <br /> I had four beers before I turned in last night, and that was probably about three too many. I guess I play the part of the party girl pretty well most of the time\u2026 but I need to remember that I\u2019m kind of a lightweight when it comes to alcohol.<br /> <br /> So I took the gang out to dinner last night to celebrate our one week anniversary as a motley. We had great Chinese food and good conversation. Insincere Marguerite put shoes on before we went in and took them off under the table while we ate. At some point, Insincere Marguerite suggested we play a game when we got back to the house\u2026 a sort of \u201cquestions in the dark\u201d scenario. We Americaned her idea up a bit and settled on Truth or Dare.<br /> <br /> As anyone who has ever played this grade-school staple should have expected, things started out innocently enough, but quickly devolved as the night wore on. Before the game started, Insincere Marguerite laid out a simple pledge binding us all to tell the truth. If anyone lied in response to a direct question as part of the game, that person would be plagued by a terrible odor for the rest of the night. We played by the commonly accepted rules: one person would ask another a question, and their target could either tell the truth in response, or accept a dare to avoid answering entirely.<br /> <br /> Things were innocuous enough at first. Gawain asked me if I\u2019d ever been in love, and I had to admit that I have not. I asked Ace what he missed the most about his life before being Taken, and he got this sort of wistful look on his face and said that he missed his dad.<br /> <br /> I couldn\u2019t possibly remember every question and answer that was exchanged last night\u2026 even aside from the alcohol, we played long enough so that everyone got to ask everyone else at least one question. I think it was Ace who turned up the heat a bit when he started asking questions about the rooms in the Hollow House. I think we all got a little nervous at that, but most of us managed to cover it up pretty well.<br /> <br /> Marguerite explained that she used to be a thief in Arcadia\u2026 the greatest non-Gentry thief in all the realm. She said that she occasionally kept the things she stole for her Mistress\u2026 and some of those things were Changelings, hence the restraints in her room in the Hollow. She was quick to point out that she never stole <u>mortals</u> for the Gentry\u2026 she just took those who had already been Taken from other Gentry.<br /> <br /> Gawain\u2019s space in the garage was full of severed heads because he was forced to act out some old medieval fairy tale called \u201cSir Gawain and the Green Knight,\u201d which was apparently pretty gruesome to hear him tell it. It was obvious that the big lug felt nothing but regret for the things he did in Arcadia, and the conversation quickly moved on after his awkward admission.<br /> <br /> Once the ball was rolling, everyone seemed to feel more comfortable with asking the deeper questions. Jacob asked Calamity about the blood in her room, and she took a very long swig of rum before choosing the dare option. Jacob dared her to kiss Gawain (which I think we all wanted to see). She didn\u2019t give him some half-assed peck on the cheek, either\u2026 it was a real, deep, soul-kiss. Both of them looked pretty pleased afterward.<br /> <br /> After that, Calamity asked me what I missed most about my life before I was Taken. I had to think about that for a minute before I answered, but there was really only one true response I could give. I tried to keep the moisture out of my eyes as I talked about my two best friends, Melissa and Jane. And with every word, I saw their faces more and more clearly, staring at me through the gilded bars of our cage as I flew away into the Hedge.<br /> <br /> The next time the game came around to me, Jacob asked me why I was so afraid of going into the Hedge, and hazarded a guess that someone was hunting me. His guess was too close for me to edge away from that part of it, so I told him about Hunting Hawk. I don\u2019t <u>know</u> if he\u2019s still after me, but he certainly was when I left the Hedge. Jacob gave me a kindly, concerned look, and opined that we might need to do some hunting of our own soon.<br /> <br /> I was actually relieved when the game moved away from questions of Arcadia and the Gentry, and began to relax a bit. That sense of contentment evaporated when Insincere Marguerite turned her captivating eyes toward me with another question. \u201cYou are obviously a lover of women,\u201d she began innocently. \u201cWhat is the most depraved thing you have ever done \u2013 consensually \u2013 with another woman?\u201d<br /> <br /> I was shocked into silence for a minute or two. My mind drifted back to that night with Imogene a couple of weeks ago\u2026 and what she asked me to do to her. It was easily the kinkiest, dirtiest thing I\u2019ve ever done. The fact that she obviously loved it \u2013 and that doing it to her turned me on more than a little bit as well \u2013 was completely beside the point. It was a private moment, as intimate in its way as the time I spent with my friends in Arcadia, and I wasn\u2019t entirely comfortable discussing it.<br /> <br /> And there\u2019s also the fact that I didn\u2019t want my new friends thinking of me as some cheap, depraved whore, of course.<br /> <br /> I knew that I could take the dare and avoid answering the question\u2026 but honestly, I sort of wanted to save that option for when talk inevitably turned toward my time in Arcadia. I figured that if I told the truth about my sex life here in California, no matter how depraved it was, my friends would take the hint when we came to something I <u>really</u> didn\u2019t want to talk about. It\u2019s sort of ironic, in retrospect.<br /> <br /> So I downed the rest of the beer I\u2019d been drinking, took a deep breath, and spat out the vulgar term for the sex act in question. There was a vaguely uncomfortable silence from most of the group, followed by Insincere Marguerite applauding my daring and imploring me not to be ashamed of my dedication to my bedmates\u2019 pleasure. I appreciate that she was trying to help\u2026 but at the time I sort of wished she would just shut up and let the game move on.<br /> <br /> I thought I would lighten the mood a bit after that, so I asked Jacob what his greatest regret was. It surprised the hell out of me when he refused to answer and took the dare option. I hadn\u2019t expected him to balk at what I considered a softball question, so I didn\u2019t have a good dare ready. The beers were starting to go to my head, and the memories Marguerite\u2019s question had stirred in me were making me a little hot, so I just told him to take off his shirt.<br /> <br /> He has a lot of scars, and a brand in the shape of a snowflake. I should have known that even silly-horny-girl dares would be revealing in this context, I guess.<br /> <br /> The questions and answers seemed to skip me for a while after that. I remember Marguerite asking Gawain how he made love\u2026 like, physically, how it was possible. I\u2019d been curious about this myself, since he\u2019s basically a suit of armor. The answer was cryptic and not particularly satisfying (\u201cit\u2019s like a codpiece but it feels real\u201d). Calamity also asked Gawain if he likes Monica, and I had to giggle at his teeny-bopper answer (\u201cI like her but I don\u2019t like-like her\u201d).<br /> <br /> I\u2019d started to relax when Ace turned to me with a question. \u201cWhat did your Keeper look like?\u201d he asked, as though it was the easiest thing in the world to talk about. I have to remember that his time in Arcadia was easier than mine, and he doesn\u2019t mind talking about it as much.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe Empress,\u201d I answered slowly. \u201cShe was beautiful. And she was purple.\u201d That didn\u2019t seem to satisfy people, so I elaborated. \u201cIt wasn\u2019t just that she wore purple, or that her skin or hair or eyes were purple. She <u>was</u> purple, in every sense of the word. It\u2019s like\u2026 every symbol or concept or emotion that we associate with the color purple\u2026 we think in those terms because she embodies those things.\u201d It didn\u2019t really come close to describing Her Majesty, but it was the best I could do with three beers in me.<br /> <br /> I asked Calamity if she had ever been in love, and she told me that she thought she had, but that it had been before she was Taken, and she didn\u2019t give any details.<br /> <br /> The game sort of wound down after that point, but the evening didn\u2019t end there. We were just sort of chilling out on the balcony deck, still drinking and chatting, when talk turned toward our schedule. Since we\u2019ll mostly be operating the Dream House at night, and Insincere Marguerite and Calamity are more comfortable working in darkness, most of the group is resolved to keeping third-shift hours. I told them that I\u2019d be happy to adjust my schedule most of the time, but that I\u2019d need to get up on Sunday mornings for church.<br /> <br /> My religious habits had obviously been bothering Calamity for some time, so she came out and asked me why I go to church, as I apparently don\u2019t seem the type. I didn\u2019t have to answer her. I could have even lied without breaking the pledge, since the question wasn\u2019t posed as part of the game. But for some reason \u2013 maybe the moonlight, or the beer, or the fact that I actually <u>like</u> these strange new friends of mine \u2013 I decided to tell her the truth.<br /> <br /> I told her about dad. I told her about growing up under his strict Methodist preacher parenting, and how I\u2019d hated every minute of my childhood. I told her about how living in Arcadia had given me a new perspective on those years, and how his estrangement from the fetch who replaced me seemed to have mellowed him somehow. I told her that he was the preacher at the church I attend, and that we have a good relationship now, even though he doesn\u2019t know I\u2019m really his daughter.<br /> <br /> Jacob chimed in at some point with a similar story. He has a twin sister (who is now ironically much younger than him). She goes to college in Santa Monica, and he visits her from time to time. She doesn\u2019t know who he is either.<br /> <br /> These stories set Calamity off in a way I couldn\u2019t have anticipated. She\u2026 she killed her parents. When she got back from Arcadia, she went to see them, and they had never realized she had been gone. She had been a quiet, studious girl before she was Taken, and her fetch was more outgoing and vibrant\u2026 more interested in making friends and being popular. It was exactly the sort of person she had always hated\u2026 and apparently exactly the sort of daughter her parents had always wanted.<br /> <br /> I imagine that was pretty hard to take. Calamity snapped, and\u2026 did something she can never take back. I admit that a part of me was horrified to hear this from her. A part of me wanted to rail against her, and accuse her of actually being the monster she believes she is. But most of me\u2026 looking at her\u2026<br /> <br /> I pity her. I feel <u>so</u> <u>sorry</u> for her. I know she\u2019s not the vicious beast she claims to be. And I know just as surely that none of us will ever be able to convince her of that. She killed her parents. In her mind, there\u2019s nothing more to say on the subject. At least not yet. But there\u2019s something her friends can do for her. Even if we can\u2019t convince her that she\u2019s a good person, we can let her know that we still love her and want to associate with her anyway.<br /> <br /> I wanted to show her that we all have secrets. I wanted to commiserate with her. And my defenses were down due to the alcohol. So I blurted out my darkest secret; the one thing I would have taken a dare to avoid talking about while the game was still going on.<br /> <br /> Calamity had told me earlier in the evening that I should watch out for Austin. Now, Austin has always been a real sweetheart to me, so I asked her what she meant. Apparently, she can sort of sense when someone is an oathbreaker, and she used that power on Austin (and most of the other performers) just before our opening night show. Austin has broken a solemn oath to another Changeling at some point in the past.<br /> <br /> I reminded Calamity of this conversation, and then told her that I\u2019m also an oathbreaker. I told the group about Jane and Melissa, and how we all swore that we\u2019d escape Arcadia together or not at all. And then I told them about how I left them there to rot when I won my own freedom. A part of me wanted to mention that Jane told me to go, that she forgave me even before I left\u2026 but bringing that fact up would have just been making excuses for my selfishness.<br /> <br /> My friends\u2019 reaction stunned me. They started talking about mounting a rescue mission into Arcadia itself. Marguerite hemmed and hawed about how she had vowed never to steal another Changeling, but Calamity assured her that this would be a rescue, not a theft. They were all so gung-ho about going back to get Missy and Jane that I\u2019m not sure if they noticed my less-than-enthusiastic response to this plan or not.<br /> <br /> Of course I want to free them. I\u2019m going to get that out of the way up front. They are my best friends, and they have been my lovers and my sisters since I was first Taken. But\u2026 I don\u2019t know if I can go back there. Hunting Hawk is still looking for me; I <u>know</u> it. And if we came across the Empress, I know in my heart that she\u2019d never let me go again. And I\u2019m not sure I could bring myself to leave her this time anyway.<br /> <br /> And then there\u2019s the question of Missy and Jane. Missy was already so far gone when I escaped that she couldn\u2019t have left the Empress even if she\u2019d <u>won</u> that stupid contest. And Jane won\u2019t leave Missy; she\u2019s already proven that she\u2019s more loyal and faithful than I\u2019ll ever be. What if we go back into Arcadia only to find that the girls I knew are gone forever? What if I get my motley captured or killed in a vain attempt to rescue the ghosts of two memories?<br /> <br /> I finished my fourth beer with thoughts like that running through my head. After a while, I made a decision. The Empress turned me into a songbird. In Arcadia, all I had to do to survive was make myself beautiful and sing pretty songs. And it occurred to me that I\u2019m <u>still</u> doing that, even now that I\u2019ve gotten away from her. Is that all there is to me? Am I nothing more than what she\u2019s made me? No, dammit. I refuse to believe that. I <u>will</u> go back to Arcadia. I <u>will</u> rescue Missy and Jane, if I can. And if it turns out that the whole thing is pointless\u2026 then at least I will have tried, and maybe that\u2019ll earn me some redemption.<br /> <br /> I felt better after that little epiphany, and so I did something I\u2019d wanted to do for <u>weeks</u>. I spread my wings and jumped off the deck, gliding across the grounds in lazy circles until I lightly touched down. I had to go back in through the front door and climb back up to the balcony, of course, but I felt better for having stretched my wings a bit. Gliding isn\u2019t as nice as flying, but it\u2019ll do in a pinch.<br /> <br /> I said my goodnights after that, and the group started to disperse. I\u2019d been sort of idly flirting with Jacob for a while, but he didn\u2019t seem interested, so I let him be. He and Gawain carried Calamity to the room she\u2019s been sleeping in while we de-ghostify her old bedroom, and Ace tore off his pants in a fit of high spirits and made a grand exit I don\u2019t think any of us are likely to forget.<br /> <br /> I stumbled back to my bedroom, stripped, and flopped onto my bed. I had thought I wanted to be alone, to absorb everything I\u2019d heard and come to terms with everything I\u2019d said. Apparently, that wasn\u2019t the case. I found myself crying a little, wishing I had someone with me. I didn\u2019t want sex; not really. After the night\u2019s emotional roller-coaster, I <u>so</u> wasn\u2019t in the mood. I wanted someone to hold, and I wanted to have someone hold me. I wanted to kiss and cuddle and chase the dark, serious thoughts away with warm fuzzies.<br /> <br /> As I drifted off to sleep, my mind\u2019s-eye gave me a flash of purple\u2026 not the violet and indigo of the Empress, but a softer, lighter pink-purple streak popping out of a sea of lustrous black strands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T14:25:29-07:00","id":161977,"title":"","content":"<b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> <b><u>May 3rd</u></b><br /> <br /> What in the fucking hell was I thinking? Oh by Bacchus' bloated balls I shouldn't have drunk so damn much. My head is throbbing... my throat feels like sandpaper... my eyes hurt... my abs feel like I pulled something from all the heaving even though there's nothing left to vomit up... Serves me right for last night. Or was it early this morning? Fuck what does when it happened matter? <br /> <br /> Okay, I need to sort my shit all out before Gawain wakes up. Before I have to face the others. Hopefully writing it down will help, give me something to focus on besides how wretched I feel right this minute. Geebus, I've never let myself get that far gone before and I swear by whatever god or devil might be listening that I will NEVER fucking drink that much again. That is not how I want them to see me. That is not how I should have told them.<br /> <br /> Fuck, it seemed like a harmless enough idea when Insincere Marguerite suggested it. Okay, well the others seemed to think so. I knew what was going to come up. I joked about being able to handle whatever dare they threw at me. That was at dinner. Dinner was nice. Very upscale. The General Tso's was excellent, nice and spicy. I wish I could say it was as good coming back up as going down. We coaxed Ace back out and all went as planned. It was a good little celebration. At some point Insincere Marguerite asked me to go with her to see Madam Spidertoes. Apparently the Darkling Matriarch hasn't met her and wants to. I think she was a bit nervous about it. Can't blame her, that woman is intimidating. I guess we'll be going sometime after the shows this weekend. Well, assuming she still wants me there. I have no fucking idea where I stand with any of them for certain right now. <br /> <br /> So we got home and headed out to the back deck with assorted libations. I grabbed a bottle of Captain Morgan's liquid courage myself. I figured maybe if I got a bit liquored up I'd be able to tell them about my parents. Yeah, classic stupid plan. But fuck it, I was scared. There, I fucking said it. Well, wrote it. It was Insincere Marguerite's idea so we decided she should go first. I guess I lucked out, since she picked me and at that point things were just warming up.<br /> <br /> I admitted that alcohol was the hardest drug I've ever had. I mean, Katt was thirteen and too much of a goody two shoes to mess with anything. And there certainly weren't any drugs in Snow Globe... well, I wonder now if the candy would have counted? I never thought of it as drug but that stuff did cause some serious warm fuzzy feelings. Gah, my head is all over the place. Well I passed to Jacob, asking about his weapon of choice and discovering throwing knives. Not a huge surprise there. <br /> <br /> It kept going around. Ace got to asking folks about their rooms in the Hollow House (I knew that would come up) Gawain told the others about being the green knight and having to cut off heads. He was fairly calm with it, but I know it haunts him. Still, what happened in Arcadia is another life. Everyone did things there. It's expected. It's forgivable. And that seems to be where my own crimes stand as far as the others are concerned. I think. I mean, no one tried to put me down like a rabid dog last night. That counts for something, right? I should sort out the other details before I get into that can of Shoggoths.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite's answers told us more about her life as the star apprentice to a gentry thief known as Mama Lion. She was pretty proud of her accomplishments and her skills. She was also drinking, but I'm pretty sure she was drunker on pride than cognac. It seems that her room was because she got to keep some of the changelings she stole for her Keeper as trophies. That brings up some interesting ideas... Also, apparently her Keeper told her that because she was so good a thief that she'd be just like her someday. That's a chilling thought there, that we could become those things. I mean, I'm already a monster but even I couldn't imagine inflicting the sort of torment and pain the Whispers did... fuck... okay, I guess I can imagine it but my head is spinning way too much to go down that road right now. <br /> <br /> Fuck, I'm rambling and out of order here. But screw it, what matters is what came up. I think everyone shed at least a little light on their past. Some more than others. Jacob played it close, big surprise there. His biggest reveal was unintentional. Lori dared him to take his shirt off and we all saw that he's got some impressive scars and a snowflake shaped brand. At least some of them came from someone he used to call friend. I just wish I hadn't been fucking drooling and petting them when that came up. Maybe he'll just think I was horny and not fondling the lasting proof of his torture at a former friend's hands. While I'm at it, maybe Santa Claus will bring me a unicorn for Christmas... wait, scratch that, I'm sure the damnable things are real and I don't really want to think about how fucked up they really are right now. <br /> <br /> Um, Ace was apparently rather blissfully unaware of being anything but a snake until he got knocked out of his cage and bit his keeper. He does seem to harbor some lingering feelings for his rock. I imagine it's more that contentment he misses. I wonder if it's like that in Snow Globe after one fades? I seem to be the only one that doesn't have any mixed feelings about Arcadia. <br /> <br /> Lorelei was the other one with secrets. Funny, it was actually after the game that it all came pouring out. We were talking about the shows and being up so early and all. Church came up and I asked her why she goes. It just seemed a bit odd to me that it's clearly so important to her and I was drunk enough to ignore personal bounderies. Turns out her father preaches there. Seems that she wasn't close to him before and was about to run away to California to be a singer before being taken. And her fetch did, and he moved after her, and then she moved back to Ohio (I think). So, she found him and has managed to reconnect (even though he doesn't know she's his real daughter). What matters is the reconnection. She fixed her relationship with him. Jacob found his twin sister and has been watching over her (also, does not know who he really is).<br /> <br /> And that was when I lost it. I fucking spilled my guts like a disgraced samurai. The words just refused to stay inside. These people found the ones they lost and they're making the best of it. Better than before in Lori's case. I told them. I told them that I killed my parents. I was shaking and not just from the rum. Gawain... Gawain wrapped those strong metal arms around me and held me. I was past resisting. Fuck knows I didn't want to and I... I fucking needed it. He didn't turn away. He didn't yell. He just held me while I confessed my sins. And after I had finished my drunken antics he made me drink water and crackers and put me to bed, then cleaned me up when I got sick. I think he was sleeping in the hallway outside my door. I made him take me to bed and stay after that. I woke up curled up against him this morning. I just laid there for while. It may seem weird, but it really doesn't bother me that he's metal. He's solid enough to touch me without getting cut. After a while, I slipped out of the bed and went to my room to clean myself up and put on some fresh clothes. But I couldn't leave him to wake up alone so I grabbed this dairy to write in and now I'm sitting here watching him sleep. After everything that happened last night we're seriously going to have to talk once he wakes up. <br /> <br /> And speaking of last night, once I'd started things, Lori admitted that she'd been taken with two of her friends. They made a vow to escape together or not at all. She's here. They're not. I told her I'd help her go back for them. We all did. Insincere Margeurite said she'd help even though she's not supposed to steal changelings anymore. I pointed out this would be a rescue and thus not the same thing but I don't know if it helped. I didn't leave anyone behind because I didn't have anyone. But I guess that's why she refused to stay behind when we went into the Hedge. She doesn't want to let us down. I can certainly understand that. <br /> <br /> They all kept telling me that I wasn't a monster last night. But what I did was monsterious. I murdered my parents in a fit of rage. I tasted their fear and I enjoyed it. It felt good. It always does. I like the pain. I savor that moment when they realize that their life is in my hands... my jagged bloody hands... Maybe that's why Annika's lessions appeal to me, it's not the same but there is the control and power. Maybe I can learn to make due with that. Maybe.<br /> <br /> I have tried to find the girl I used to be since returning but the things that mattered so much to her mean nothing to me. Well, except for Anastasia. But even that is... strange now. I am strange now. I crave pain and violence. I crave the fear of others. This is what I am now. Katt is dead, the fucking Whispers killed her, night by night they murdered her and left me in her place. I can't change what I am and I won't pretend to be someone else. <br /> <br /> They think I'm not a monster, but they're wrong. I am pain. I am violence. I am the thing you fear in the dark. I am Calamity.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> I think it is official. I have put my boot in my mouth. Is that the phrase? Something like that. I used to know a whole bunch of American turns of phrase, but after speaking Russian for so long in the Lady\u2019s realm I\u2019ve forgotten so much. Anyway\u2026As I said I left something to be desired when it came to tact last night. We all went out to dinner at this fancy Chinese restaurant. Very nice. Much better than the cheap take out stuff I\u2019ve had before. Lorelei covered the tab. I don\u2019t think I thanked her for that. I thought it, in my head, but didn\u2019t say it out loud. I should do that. Later today perhaps. Insincere Marguerite actually slipped on some shoes to wear into the restaurant. She promptly slipped them right back off once seated, but it was interesting to see her wear them in the first place. It was a night of firsts all around. I saw Lorelei glide from the balcony, and Ace pull off his pants, throw them over the same balcony and walk starkers from the waist down back into the house. I think he really had wanted to be dared to do that, but hadn\u2019t been, so he just did it. Which leads to the game. Insincere Marguerite came up with the idea of playing truth or dare. We made a quick little pledge agreeing to tell the truth if asked a question or we would smell bad for a couple of hours. It did not go as expected.<br /> <br /> I thought we would all ask some silly questions, mostly light stuff, some harder and come out of it a little more knowledgeable about each other and have something to strengthen that burgeoning trust. Yeah\u2026.kinda worked out differently than that. Oh, there were plenty of innocent questions and answers. Ace misses his rock, Lorelei has never been in love, and Insincere Marguerite has five reasons for not wearing shoes, all practical. Gawain learned to use a long sword in the SCA, Calamity thinks she was in love once, and I admitted the thing I missed the most was my sister. The other stuff that came up was not so innocent.<br /> <br /> Ace had been asking people what the sights in their Hollow rooms meant. He asked Gawain about all the heads in the garage and our resident knight revealed that he\u2019d been forced to carry out the story of Gawain and the Green Knight over and over. He had tried to resist at first but had been hurt in turn, and after a while he stopped fighting it. I can\u2019t blame him for that. We were all conditioned in one way or another to carry out certain roles. Some were easy, some were not. Ace was a snake. He didn\u2019t know he wasn\u2019t a snake, so his life was peaceful and uneventful. Lorelei was a songbird of sorts for her Keeper. Insincere Marguerite was a thief for hers. I wish I could say that I became a killer because The Lady made me, but that\u2019s not the truth. I became a killer before I met her. I just became better at it after that. <br /> <br /> The Brit also asked Insincere Marguerite about the restraints in her room. I will admit that I\u2019d been curious about that myself. She said that as the best non-gentry thief in Arcadia she had stolen a lot of things. Some of those things were Changelings from other keepers. She assured us that she did not take people from \u201cthe world\u201d to become Changelings, she only stole those already in captivity by rival Gentry. She also admitted that she kept some of those Changelings for her own. She did not give details, and that\u2019s fine. She was truthful about the whole thing. Insisted that she was not a loyalist like others might presume for her theft of other Lost.<br /> <br /> Some time into the game, after alcohol had been consumed I asked Calamity about the blood in her room in the hollow. She shut right down. Seriously. Then she took dare. I respected that. Some questions you just don\u2019t want to answer. Some you\u2019re just not ready to talk about. So, I dared her to kiss Gawain. I thought that they both might enjoy it. I know Gawain is seriously crushing on Calamity, and she is very protective her him. She seems interested in him, but holds herself back, so I thought I\u2019d give them a nudge. It wasn\u2019t a chaste kiss either. Very passionate, though a little desperate on Calamity\u2019s part. I think she needed the contact, or maybe she just needed to express her feelings for him while she dared. After the game was over some of us were talking about our families. Apparently Lorelei\u2019s father, who was a preacher in Iowa has moved to California and Lorelei has been going to his services. He doesn\u2019t know who she is. I told everyone about Elena going to school in Santa Monica and about how we met at the restaurant I used to work at. Same as Lori\u2019s dad, Elena doesn\u2019t know who I really am. <br /> <br /> Then the floodgate opened. Calamity, who had been oddly quiet and tense since my \u2018room question,\u2019 just flat said that her parents were dead, and she had been the one to kill them. I will admit it was something of a sucker punch, but only for an instant. It was very clear that she harbored a tremendous amount of guilt over it. And once she started talking she just kept going. She told us about Snow Globe. Everyone was \u201cperfect.\u201d Think \u201cBrady Bunch,\u201d or \u201cLeave it to Beaver.\u201d If you did not act the way you were supposed to you were punished. You were rewarded if you told on your friends and family, and the more you toed the line the more you faded. People would lose color and definition and then suddenly be replaced by a new person like nothing had happened. The new person would fill the same role and keep going. <br /> <br /> Calamity kept fighting back, kept trying to remember who she was. In the end she managed to literally break her way out of Snow Globe, with a rock. She grabbed a shard of glass and stabbed her Keeper and ran. I guess the glass became a part of her as she fled through the hedge. Then when she got home, she discovered that a double had been sent to take her place. Her parents didn\u2019t even realize she had been replaced. She found out through conversation that her fetch had become the \u201cperfect daughter,\u201d that her parents always wanted. Forsaking the quiet academic personality for a more outgoing, cheerleader, \u201cpopularity queen\u201d one. Sounded like a bitch to me. And she snapped. She discovered in that moment when she attacked her parents that she could make knives come out of her fingers, and she killed them.<br /> <br /> That is not what I was expecting to hear. I knew there was pain in her past. I knew she was bottling up some emotions, some memories that made her want to get into fights in the hedge and drink like a Russian. She has been exhibiting textbook PTSD symptoms, such as self-destructive behavior and avoidance. Yeah, yeah\u2026pot, kettle. Anyway\u2026I knew all this when I asked the question. I knew that if she could talk about the trauma she could start to heal. I thought the blood was hers!! I thought she had been made to bleed. I thought someone had hurt her. She was just a girl when she was taken. An innocent girl! I thought the blood was hers! I swear by Morena I thought the blood was Calamity\u2019s! I wanted her to talk about it so she could start to heal, and if need be I could go stab her attacker. I did not know it would be someone else\u2019s blood. She calls herself a monster. She honestly believes it too. She isn\u2019t. I told her this, as did the others but I don\u2019t think she believes us. Monsters don\u2019t feel bad for the deeds they do. They revel in it. She is so far from what a monster really is, but she can\u2019t see that. She can only see the bodies of her parents and the blood on her hands. She is absolutely repulsed by the memory of what happened. I tried to tell her that we all have a dark side and sometimes we act on it, but it doesn\u2019t make us monsters. Well, I didn\u2019t say \u201cwe.\u201d I said it didn\u2019t make her a monster to have done something she regrets. I didn\u2019t want to purjor myself and then stink like a liar, in case the contract was still active. So, I didn\u2019t say \u201cwe.\u201d I didn\u2019t include myself in the description of those that are not monsters. I know what I am. I mentioned the pot and the kettle earlier. I do regret my actions now, but my sins are so much worse than reacting violently once in anger. <br /> <br /> After Calamity\u2019s confession, Lorelei made a confession of her own. She admitted that she had made a pact with her two friends, who had been taken at the same time as her. They all promised that they would escape together or not at all. Things didn\u2019t work out the way they planned. Apparently Lorelei won a boon from her keeper, The Empress, for winning some sort of singing competition between the three girls. For her boon, our Spring courtier asked to return home and was granted her wish. Of course now she feels bad for leaving her friends behind. I can understand that, but when it comes to the Gentry you have to get out while you can. She mentioned having been sold to the keeper by another man, and that The Empress also had a man that worked for her, a hawk. Presumably his job was to keep any pretty birds from escaping. I suggested that if she wanted to get her friends back that we\u2019d first have to go hawk hunting. I\u2019m not sure if she was terrified or interested in the idea of getting her friends back. Insincere Marguerite looked interested at first, but then said that she probably shouldn\u2019t steal any more changelings. Her keeper had complemented her several times and intimated that Marguerite could be just like her someday. I think Insincere Marguerite wants to keep from falling into that trap. I can understand that. It is tempting to go back to doing what we\u2019re good at.<br /> <br /> Earlier, during the game, Lorelei asked me the question what was the thing I regretted the most. I couldn\u2019t answer that. I thought of several things I could have said, but realized that the contract we all took would know I wasn\u2019t being completely honest, so I took dare. I suppose that fact told quite a bit, but I\u2019m not sure how they will all interpret it. Lorelei for her part dared me to take off my shirt. I almost laughed with relief. I had no idea what she was going to ask me to do, but I thought it would be worse than that. So, everyone got a show. I realized as I pulled my t-shirt over my head that not only would they see The Lady\u2019s mark, they\u2019d see the scars. I have several. Not everything The Lady did to me left a mark, and some she did away with, but others she left as a reminder. I could see recognition in Calamity\u2019s eyes when she saw my scars. She knew which ones were made with a knife. Thankfully no one made any comments about them, or the brand. I don\u2019t know how I\u2019d react. If they\u2019d asked me how I got them, the contract would tell them if I lied. Though I suppose I could just say my keeper gave them to me and it would be enough.<br /> <br /> Later, after Ace stalked off to retrieve his pants and Lorelei flew around the backyard, which is just pretty neat by the way. Gawain and I got Calamity back to her room. Gawain went to get some crackers and water and I sat with Calamity to make sure she\u2019d be okay. I also wanted to talk to her in private. I sat next to her and apologized for asking the question. I felt bad for bringing such bad memories. She mumbled some reply and traced some of the scars on my side with her fingers. She found a long one and I told her that it had been given to me by someone I had once called friend. She replied that friends are apt to betray you. I felt bad for a couple of reasons after that. I\u2019m sorry that her experiences had taught her that lesson. I learned it as well, and did not enjoy the experience. I also felt bad because I felt like I\u2019d betrayed her, and the rest of the motley. I didn\u2019t tell them anything about my stay in Arcadia. Just little hints, vague comments on how I learned to fight with knives there. I couldn\u2019t say anything else. My throat closed and I just couldn\u2019t. I considered it for a brief moment, but shot down the idea just as fast.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve only known this group for a short time. A week or so, but already I don\u2019t want to see the look in their eyes when they find out what I\u2019ve been. If they find out. Insincere Marguerite had a good rant about shame, and how other people used your shame to control you. That you shouldn\u2019t feel shame for that very reason. I wish I could go with that. While I worked for The Lady I felt no shame whatsoever. I was doing Her bidding and I was Her loyal Knight. That\u2019s all that mattered. When I first escaped I don\u2019t know if I thought much about it. Kind of like I recognized that my actions were bad, and didn\u2019t feel great about them, but it felt distant. It\u2019s just lately that it keeps coming to mind. Little things here and there keep reminding me and I feel like shit. Goddess, how can they stand to have me in their midst? <br /> <br /> Anyhoo\u2026after Gawain came back with water and crackers for Calamity I left. I went back to my room with the intention of getting well and truly shit-faced. I think that\u2019s the right term. Very drunk. Only, Insincere Marguerite was there, waiting outside my room for me. She had asked me during the game about my preference in sexual partners, and I guess she was acting on that information. I admitted, once we were in my room that I had some experiences, but not all of them pleasant. I didn\u2019t elaborate. I didn\u2019t want to tell her that some of my former lovers may have not been entirely willing. It seemed so at the time, but fear can make you do things you wouldn\u2019t normally, and at that point in my life I used fear to make people do a lot of things. So, undeserving as I was, Insincere Marguerite was convincing and damn sexy and won me over. She was so gentle and sweet, and flexible. Damn flexible. I tried to compare the experience to any other and they just didn\u2019t. The times before felt good and were a release, but with Marguerite it was so much more. It was like she wanted nothing more than to make me feel good. I don\u2019t deserve her. I don\u2019t deserve any of them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> Last night was illuminating. I have learned much of my motley-mates, and taken a second lover. We will see how I handle these responsibilities. We had dinner, then a sort of truth or dare game, then just talked\u2026well a lot of the talking was Calamity, but still. And drinking, which makes for talking. Usually.<br /> <br /> I am almost unique in my Motley. Everyone except Ace and I (and maybe Jacob) had very unpleasant Durances. This is normal, of course, but I felt a little\u2026guilty\u2026that mine was so much easier. Mine was, after all, fun, dangerous collection of enemies besides. But if you are not making enemies, you are not doing anything meaningful, no?<br /> <br /> Next to Jacob, Gawain I learned the least about. He had played the part of the Green Knight, as I had surmised, but I learned next to nothing else about his Durance. Certain physiological questions were answered, and he kissed Calamity, which was the sweetest thing to happen all night. His fetch apparently isn\u2019t so bad. He was quiet, focused mostly on Calamity, so volunteered less than many.<br /> <br /> Still his behavior toward Calamity was telling. She has him wrapped around her finger, but I truly believe she is not trying to do so. Probably. It just happened. Even her later drunken revelations failed to phase him, and he put her to bed sweetly and watched over her. At least I think they did. Elementals are hard to read.<br /> <br /> I did find out he played the role of the Green Knight many times. He killed many Gawains. Was his taking that name in honor of them? I wonder.<br /> <br /> Lorelei\u2026oh boy. She left her friends when she escaped Arcadia, and feels incredibly guilty about it. She did not betray them, apparently, but won her freedom when they did not. Faerie kept coming up but she never failed to be uncomfortable when it did. Frankly I felt awful for her. I offered my help retrieving her friends, which was\u2026not good. I don\u2019t steal Changelings anymore. But to come out of retirement for one last job? That could not backfire\u2026could it? Part of I wondered if it was a trap. Part of I still does.<br /> <br /> I also discovered via personal questions she is probably a talented lover, which I suspected. Too often the pretty ones don\u2019t need to bother to learn to please their partners, so I was glad she was not one of those. Probably.<br /> <br /> I feel a little bad for Lorelei. She got flirty near the end but retired alone. Reading her eyes, I don\u2019t think she was really in the mood for intimate company. Possibly. I should, perhaps, have gone to speak with her but\u2026I fear it would have been awkward. Perhaps she will want to talk later. Perhaps. Or perhaps she will not want it mentioned again.<br /> <br /> Ace had the closest to me of an idyllic Durance. He was happy until he bit his keeper, to which I say bravo. I suppose there is a lesson there about animals always turning on you, but I will choose to ignore it. What was revealing about Ace was his bombastic way of asking people about what happened that caused their rooms in the Hollow House to take on the appearances they did. He apparently did not see any issue with asking almost everyone about Arcadia. I\u2019d say his directness was revealing, but there was little there to discover, he has always been direct.<br /> <br /> Then he took off his pants and ran around nude from the waist down. Beasts are strange. I\u2019d say the British are strange, but that behavior was not similar to other Brits I had encountered. Oh well. He seemed happy, I suppose that it what matters. Probably.<br /> <br /> Calamity being the other side of the Gawain/Calamity pair also had a lot revealed, possibly the most. Early on she took a dare rather than answer a question from Jacob (I found out he felt bad about asking later) about the innocent blood, and wound up kissing Gawain. She then drank heavily and seemed a bit morose for a while, though she got more questions at the end. She was from a place called Snowglobe (which I never visited) with American 1950s style people and houses, and a dark, unseen Keeper who punished you if you did not play your part. Calamity actually killed people there only to see them replaced and be tortured by her Keeper. I don\u2019t like her Keeper. I do, however, respect her willingness to break Arcadia\u2019s rules. That is how you win.<br /> <br /> She fought her way out in the end, stabbed her Keeper with glass from shattering the wall of Snowglobe. That made me smile. She is better than her Keeper. She met Gawain on the way out in the Hedge and they have been together since. Mostly. Except when she murdered her parents. Her parents apparently traded her for a more perfect daughter, her Fetch, which frankly to me absolves her of guilt. I have killed for less. Maybe that says more about me than her. Maybe.<br /> <br /> She was very, very drunk in the end, so Gawain took her to bed to watch over her. Good man. I don\u2019t think anything bad happened, she was too drunk, Gawain too honorable. She is interested in seeing Madame Spidertoes with me, but not while she is hung over. Probably after the weekend.<br /> <br /> Jacob was downright cagy. The only one besides Calamity who took a dare (Lorelei got him to take off his shirt) he managed to avoid telling\u2026anything\u2026really about his Durance. I even had a better idea of Gawain\u2019s than Jacob\u2019s, and he only remembers so much. I feel that this is deliberate\u2026Jacob is holding out. There could be many reasons, only a few of them sinister.<br /> <br /> I am slightly worried he could be a Manchurian Candidate. He seemed to have a personality shift of sorts a few times, though his behavior seems consistent. I am unsure about this, though, and don\u2019t want to bring it up until I have some sort of proof. No need to make him distrusted unless necessary.<br /> <br /> After the games, I met Jacob outside his room and seduced him. He is the first man I have made love to since being Taken, and I had missed being filled by a man. Men smell very different than women, and taste different, and the experience of sex with a man is different. I had almost forgotten it. He was\u2026shy\u2026about a few things, but I think I will get him to try them in time. He was somewhat new at this, so I tried to be gentle and as pleasing as possible. He also has my scent on him now. And yet\u2026I don\u2019t feel as possessive of him as Julia. Perhaps I have been conditioned to see men as more dominant. Maybe. This may require experimentation. Tee-hee.<br /> <br /> The old me would have never allowed a Slav to mingle with her, but here I am quite content after a night with Jacob. Being taken improved me. It may have also damned me. Time will tell.<br /> <br /> Regardless, last night went well. Time to get ready to have our regular show tonight! The girls will do my number I think. I am excited.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session V</i><br /> <br /> <br /> I spent a few hours before the session in the Emergency Room and was a bit drugged when the session happened. I was just fine with it being a session for the PCs to sit around and talk. And make no mistake, we played the full four hours.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite\u2019s obsession with Shame in a negative way has to do with the Day/Night (Sun/Moon) dichotomy, she has a very high Mantle, after all. Her pronoun misuse is deliberate by the player.<br /> <br /> I did not wind up doing any Clarity checks over any of the rolls/revelations.<br /> <br /> So yea, the fallout will be interesting this next session. Check that out in two weeks. Speaking of revelations, I wrote an ugly little story that answers a lot of questions some folks may have about the history of the area and, well, why the heck the Courts would create a local Cabaret to begin with. That content will be at your door in a week. In the meantime, comments and questions are welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T03:02:38-07:00","id":162317,"title":"","content":"Nicely done Herr Baron. Also, I hope you feel better. In fact I shall make an official request: Feel Better. Will you require triplicate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T12:41:09-07:00","id":162609,"title":"","content":"I definitely on the mend. Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T12:58:06-07:00","id":162626,"title":"","content":"Something amusing. I Finished off my night last night/early this morning with reading the new journals. I turn on my Pandora and the first that plays is Wounds by Masterplan.<br /> <br /> Also, Dang you! Your truth or dare making me think of all the things I wouldn't want to tell were I in that situation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","user":"omenseer","date":". 06-08-2014, 04:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T14:01:08-07:00","id":162681,"title":"","content":"Heh. There was some chatter about the fact that game would be upcoming which gave all the players time to consider questions and answers. The original proposal was Insincere Marguerite entering a dark room and one could enter and ask her a question, but would be asked one in return. They decided to go the Truth or Dare route instead, which I think ultimately worked better.<br /> <br /> Ace's player can't make the game tonight, but should hopefully be a good game regardless.The short story &quot;Swan Song&quot; will be along in a week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T01:49:44-07:00","id":171502,"title":"","content":"I apologize for the delay in getting this out, it has been a difficult few days. Hell, a difficult month honestly.<br /> <br /> For the between session story, this is a little story I wrote that covers events about 15 years earlier and explains some of the motives behind some of the folks the PCs have encountered and, indeed, to some degree why the Dream House exists. It\u2019s an ugly little story, about anger and pain at the loss of a good man to AIDS and the death of a dream. I wrote it in my head while tossing and turning in bed, unable to sleep due to chest pain, and the story reflects its origin.<br /> <br /> It does not have real spoilers per say, but as I note it is an ugly little story so it goes behind tags. If you want to skip it, it is not required to enjoy the <i>Malibu Dream House</i> campaign. If you read it, however, you may find certain NPCs make a little more sense. It is worth noting that, short of their abductions maybe not even then, this is the lowest point in their lives for most of these NPCs, and their behavior reflects that.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Swan Song</b></u><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <u>November 1998, Upstairs office room of the Hat and Cane</u><br /> <br /> \u201cThen you are betraying him and everything he made, everything he tried to do!\u201d<br /> <br /> The chanteuse in the top hat stood at the table, slamming her gloved hands, palm down, against the top. Annika was dressed, as always, in a tux and tails, top hat and cigar, as she stared at the furry almost badger looking man glaring back across the table. Chance, a Beast, was dressed similarly, his hat placed on the table in front of him, as he sat smoking a cigarette. To his left, a willowy pale woman whose clothes were reminiscent of the nineteen twenties smoked a cigarette in a holder while looking at Annika, while across from her a frowning satyr sat staring at the table, smoking a cigar and wearing a brown suit with an undone bow tie. He looked tired.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou don\u2019t understand, Annika,\u201d Chance rumbled slowly. \u201cI see Gary everywhere. Everything here reminds me of him. I cannot stay here. Living without him is hell enough. I can\u2019t stay where everything is a memory of him.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou owe it to him. You owe it to us.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t owe you a GODDAMN THING,\u201d The badger stood, looking the taller Darkling in the eye. \u201cGary loved this club. He wanted it to do well. But being here is killing me. And giving it to someone else is giving away something I cannot give. His Highness won\u2019t take it. He probably shouldn\u2019t have it. And fuck if I am giving it to a stranger.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, I can\u2019t do it. I failed at this,\u201d Austin said quietly.<br /> <br /> Madame Spidertoes turned from looking at Annika to Austin. \u201cPrince Austin, you did everything you could. By the time Golden Swan told us, you simply did not have enough time. Even reckless oaths are not enough when a man is dying so quickly.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe did not even know,\u201d the Hunterheart started, \u201cThe first test was negative and,..\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m not Prince Austin anymore,\u201d Austin said quietly. \u201cI am stepping down. When March comes someone else will run the Court.\u201d<br /> <br /> Spidertoes studied Austin\u2019s face almost detachedly. \u201cIf that is what you wish, Prince Austin. It is not for me to say if your choice is best for you. It is not best for the Court, however.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWith all due respect, My Lady, fuck the Court right now!\u201d Chance roared. Spidertoes did not turn immediately, but slowly moved her head to face the Beast. \u201cI\u2019m in pain,\u201d the Hunterheart continued, \u201cI\u2019m pissed as hell His Highness did not save Gary, but he has put himself though a hell of a curse trying because he was the only one with the balls to go out and try, especially given the Summer bullshit. The Court should have fucking done something, or maybe Annika, if she even comprehended what was going on.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI loved Swan too, you pig,\u201d Annika spat out, glaring at Chance. \u201cHe is the only man I have ever loved in almost eighty years.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd he was the man in my life. Of my life. He was my boyfriend. My fucking husband you cunt. He was your lay!\u201d<br /> <br /> Annika, still standing, pointed across the table. \u201cI am upset too, of course everything reminds me of him. But he had vision. A dream! You are letting him down! You are unworthy of him!\u201d<br /> <br /> With one fluid motion, Chance backhanded Annika across the face, sending her sprawling to the floor. Austin tensed, but Spidertoes did not move, or even turn to face the Hunterheart, but merely spoke, her tone cold.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou are in pain. I understand why you did that. But if you strike my woman again, you will have physical pain to match your emotional suffering, and only crawling back to your Keeper would cure it, which you would do to end what I will do to you, for even your death would not.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYour girlfriend is a bitch.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know. It is one reason she is my girlfriend. But this is not about her, involved as she may be. You do not need our approval. I\u2019ve lost people before. I will again. Follow the road ahead. Don\u2019t let it kill you. Golden Swan would not want that,\u201d The Antiquarian spoke evenly, without looking up at him.<br /> <br /> Austin\u2019s eyes turned to where Annika was lying stunned on the floor. He wanted to get up and help her, but the pressure in the room seemed to hold him to his seat. Even so, her partner had made no move to help her. Chance spoke again, breaking the silence and the Prince\u2019s reverie.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe should be glad to be alive. If it were not for His Highness\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI am no longer your King,\u201d Austin said.<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026she would still have HIV and sooner or later you would too.\u201d<br /> <br /> Madame Spidertoes looked impassively at the Hunterheart, but did not speak.<br /> <br /> Chance Sighed. \u201cI need to get out of this place. Get away. It\u2019s killing me. Making me an asshole. I can\u2019t keep this open. I need a new start. Somewhere else. Maybe Frisco, maybe Manhattan. Your\u2026Austin, can you arrange for this place to be sold? And maybe the records kept?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll try.\u201d The goat said quietly.<br /> <br /> \u201cWill you see fucking Lord Sunheart punished for telling the Summer Court not to help?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI can make no promises.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI need to go, Austin. I swear I will forgive you for this,\u201d Chance put on the top hat at the table. \u201cYou tried to save him, after all. But not yet. I\u2019m sorry, my friend.\u201d<br /> <br /> The Badger left. The room was silent for several moments.<br /> <br /> \u201cWas ist passiert? Wo bin ich?\u201c Annika mumbled, slowly rising.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou are among friends, my sweet,\u201d Spidertoes had a hint of affection in her voice, but it was still cool.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo what\u2026what was decided?\u201d The Dancer found her top hat and put it on, trying to regain some dignity.<br /> <br /> \u201cHe cannot remain and run the club. The pain is too much. I can\u2019t blame him, I am debating leaving too,\u201d Austin replied softly.<br /> <br /> Spidertoes looked to Austin, \u201cIt will have to close down. You can\u2019t run it, my woman can\u2019t run it. I won\u2019t run it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cStop calling me your woman!\u201d Annika demanded.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo. Hush.\u201d<br /> <br /> Austin looked into Annika\u2019s eyes. \u201cListen, Annika, let\u2019s flip a deal. You are too close to this now, I am too close to this. And any club now is going to fail because Swan is not running it. None of us have his gift; you know that. But right now no one is going to get a fair chance. But I think something can happen. We can have another club, like he would have wanted. Not now. Maybe not in five years. But it will happen.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo. I will not dance again. No one is worthy.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd you accused Chance of giving up?\u201d<br /> <br /> Annika glared at Austin.<br /> <br /> \u201cLook, Annika, here is my end. I will look for a time when we have new people who won\u2019t beat themselves up about how different, or not, their club is from Swan\u2019s. That won\u2019t do any good and it is better anyway if they go their own way. A copy will always be inferior, but someplace new will shine. When it happens, I will use all my power to get the Court to pave the way for a new Club for the Freehold. When it happens, you will show, you will be polite and encouraging, and you will dance to get people coming. Once. After that you are welcome to dance but not bound to do so.\u201d<br /> <br /> The chanteuse chewed her Cigar. \u201cYou saved my life, Prince. Fine. Deal.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou won\u2019t regret this, Annika.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBetter not. And Austin\u2026.Thanks. For me. For trying. Now stop beating yourself up. You are a goddamn hero,\u201d Annika said, her voice uncharacteristically gentle.<br /> <br /> Austin blinked. \u201cThank You Annika,\u201c He turned to face both Annika and Spidertoes. \u201cLadies.\u201d The Steepscrambler bowed and existed<br /> <br /> Annika chewed her cigar, her eyes distant. Madame Spidertoes coughed once, quietly and delicately.<br /> <br /> \u201cI need to quit smoking.\u201d<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This weekend we update things from the last <i>Malibu Dream House</i> session. Ace\u2019s player had to miss again, and our protagonists move on from an awkward night. See you in a few days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 06-17-2014, 04:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T02:35:00-07:00","id":176877,"title":"","content":"So it's time to catch back up with the kids at the Malibu Dream House. Slower session, I was low on sleep and Ace's player had to miss, but advanced the timeline a bit and some good RP<br /> <br /> <i>Session VI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain's Memories</b><br /> <br /> May 4th -<br /> <br /> I guess I shouldn\u2019t be surprised the nightmares came back. Really, I should be surprised they didn\u2019t come back the night before last with all the... stuff. It was a nice break anyway. But last night it was back to the usual, back to the Dream, over and over again. There were even new people for me to kill - the motley, Monica, Captain Jack. The weirdest one was definitely when I was the Gawain, and Calamity was the Green Knight, and she killed me on the first blow with her glass axe cause I flirted with her husband, Captain Jack. Dreams are so weird. Mostly it was me killing Calamity, and sometimes Monica. I tried to stop it, over and over again, but all that happened was that all the non-existent bones in my non-existent arms got broken, mangled up in the vambraces of this fucking armor. I feel more stiff now that I did waking up yesterday, and yesterday I spent hours sitting on the floor tucked into a corner I didn\u2019t really fit in.<br /> <br /> Yesterday at least started off nice. Well, yesterday morning, after some real sleeping. First, Calamity got sick, a few hours after I put her to bed. I kinda figured she would, it\u2019s why I stayed. I helped her get cleaned up a bit, and get to the other spare bedroom. She was more with it than when I put her to bed before, so she told me if I really had to stay nearby, I should sleep on the bed with her. It was just that, nothing happened or anything, but it was nice, being there with her. And waking up with her there.<br /> <br /> She wasn\u2019t still sleeping, which makes sense since it was something like 1 in the afternoon. She was up reading the diary she\u2019d picked up from her parent\u2019s house, that day. I hope she hadn\u2019t been stewing in anything, but she said she was alright, just regretting having drunk so much. She offered me and hand getting out of bed, and we went down for breakfast.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite was climbing around the kitchen when we got there, up on the stove rummaging through cabinets. She looked at me hopefully when she noticed me, asking if I could make something. Specifically, crepes. She was pretty adorable asking too, drawing out the r real far, you know? Jacob had coffee ready and waiting and I also got a glass of water, and made some dry scrambled eggs, mostly as a vehicle for salt. I ate slow, but everything seemed to settle pretty well.<br /> <br /> We talked some about plans for the rest of the afternoon. Doors opened at 6, so we had about 4 hours or so to kill. Lori was really big on wanting to go out somewhere, like the beach or a movie or something. I really just wanted to work, to do something physical and sweat out some of the tension everything had stirred up. I think Calamity was the same, she didn\u2019t really wanna sit still at all. I thought about offering to go with her when she went to clean up the first guest room she\u2019d slept in, but I\u2019d already said I was thinking about doing some forge work, and I didn\u2019t want to hover, you know? I\u2019d kinda already, what with the sleeping outside her door, but, I dunno... I guess there\u2019s a line.<br /> <br /> Speaking of lines, there are apparently some Insincere Marguerite will not cross. She was going to watch a French movie, she told us, and we could too - she would even turn on subtitles. She would not change the language track though. That would be going too far. None of us took her up on it, though that might be fun sometime. My French is a little rusty but watching movies is always good practice.<br /> <br /> So we all kinda split up. Lori did wind up going out, a bit later. Dinner with De la Roche, I think she said. After a bit, Jacob and Calamity came down to the forge to ask for some of my unfinished knives, ones that were just missing the edge. Apparently, they\u2019d decided to spar a bit, them both using knives, you know? It makes sense, knives versus knives is a very different fight that knives versus flammenschwert. And it keeps you moving. I had plenty - soon now that I have space I need to start up on that second flammenschwert, but after I had that talk with Jacob about various forms of knives, I wanted to get some practice. I think they\u2019d both make their own knives for an actual fight, but at the least I\u2019ll have some backups for them. Jacob did let me know the balance had worked out well.<br /> <br /> I kept on making knives and tooling around until just before we opened, leaving enough time for a quick shower. We had a nice showing of Changelings, even with it not being a big event thing. A couple of the creepy Winter Court folks were there, and a bunch of Spring Court ladies. And Austen, even though he wasn\u2019t performing tonight. Monica and De la Roche both showed up, and Julia. She had her sketching stuff, and did some more work on folks\u2019 pictures. Queen Charlotte showed up too, along with Madame Spidertoes. Calamity talked a bit with her, about ghost stuff, you know. Apparently, there is in fact a sleeping murder ghost in Calamity\u2019s old room, but now we know what she looks like. The ghost in the changing rooms is nice-ish? She likes scaring people, but also wants to protect the girls by scaring them away from the murder ghost. Also, there\u2019s ghost juice in our basement. Ectoplasmic residue, or something like that. We\u2019re going to see about bottling it up, and selling it at the goblin market. But it\u2019s apparently safe though.<br /> <br /> After the show was real awkward though. I\u2019d been talking some with Monica (that was awkward at first, cause I wasn\u2019t really sure where things stood with Calamity and I dunno... but she didn't make like she was going to pick me up again, literally or otherwise, so it wasn't too awkward) and then Calamity called a motley meeting to tell us about the ghost stuff. After, the other ladies wandered off with their girlfriends, and Jacob wandered off too, and it was just me and her. I\u2019m not very good about coming up with conversation, so there was lots of awkward pauses. It kinda explained how things stood with Calamity, cause she was telling me I ought to call Monica - not like, right now, but later. I offered to help move furniture and stuff around if she wanted them different in the room she was moving too, but she said it was all set up ok, and since it\u2019s not like she needs my help moving her things from one room to another, I didn't push it or anything.<br /> <br /> When she commented about how awkward the conversation was, I figured I\u2019d better go ahead and go home. Thinking about it now, I maybe missed something there. Maybe I could have gone for a kiss, or a hug or said something about us, about the night before. But I didn\u2019t. Whatever. I think I\u2019ve killed enough time here. Gotta be at the house in time for post-church breakfast.<br /> <br /> (Later)<br /> <br /> Alright, breakfast got me a bit more on track. At the worst, things are kinda like they were before, which I guess is pretty alright. My grumbly mood was apparently pretty obvious, cause they asked about it as soon as I got there. When I said I hadn\u2019t slept well, Lori decided to rub it in that she\u2019d had her girlfriend over. I may have glared at her a little, but mostly it was a mock glare, cause I am happy that she is. Especially when Calamity came over and patted my hand. So at least I didn\u2019t screw anything up by being dumb last night. Jacob brought me an extra large coffee, and the both of them helped me out with making omelets. Jacob made some killer toast, just perfectly browned, you know? And Calamity chopped up the vegetables.<br /> <br /> De la Roche joined us but Julia didn\u2019t, cause she\u2019s shy so she snuck out earlier. I did give Lori an even less serious, even more teasing glare for De la Roche, since she offered her breakfast, then asked me if it was ok if she stayed. I didn\u2019t mind a single bit - one more pretty lady at the table is never a bad thing, but it\u2019s fun teasing Lori, especially when she\u2019s dressed up so... churchy.<br /> <br /> It really was fun having De la Roche at breakfast. She told us some gossip about L.A. It seems the Night Court had organized a zombie orgy to interrupt the Day Court\u2019s May Day celebration. They were reenacting something from a movie, I guess. Insincere Marguerite knew about the plans and was happy they finally put them into motion. It certainly sounded, well, I\u2019ll go with special. Also, De la Roche mentioned there was a lazer tag place run by Changelings! Lazer tag is super awesome, and it\u2019s a Summer Court place, so they have, like, training courses set up. I\u2019m not really any good with a gun, it\u2019s mostly just fun for me, but I\u2019m totally going to convince folks to go one day, even if Insincere Marguerite likes hiding better than guns. In the sweet black light rooms and stuff, that\u2019s a pretty awesome way to win anyway. I bet she\u2019d kick ass with how sneaky she is.<br /> <br /> While we were speaking of ambushes, I brought up the alien lady again. So Calamity made a call, and we set it up so that we would meet her at 8:30 Monday night, at Glamour Springs. There\u2019d be a show and all, but we decided that Lori and Ace don\u2019t need to be on stage every single night, so they\u2019ll be taking Monday off so we can go Hedge exploring. It sounds like tons of fun, even if the Winter and Summer Courts both think Andromeda is a traitor. I mean, I\u2019ll be watching out and stuff, but she doesn\u2019t seem like a traitor and I think we can take on an ambush, as long as we\u2019re not actually ambushed, you know? And between all of us, I think we\u2019ll be super prepared for, like, everything. And goblin fruit sound super cool.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei's Diary</b><br /> <br /> So yesterday dawned bright and early around noon for me. I woke up with a splitting headache, but luckily managed to avoid the other common symptoms of a hangover. Digging deep into my pre-Arcadia memories, I came up with one of Dad\u2019s old remedies that didn\u2019t seem too disgusting. There didn\u2019t seem to be any Goody\u2019s powder in the house, so I crushed up four aspirin and mixed them in with a tall glass of orange juice. I\u2019m not sure if it actually worked due to some inherent property of the mixture, or if it was just some sort of placebo effect, but I actually did feel a bit better after finishing the drink.<br /> <br /> Gawain made crepes again after Insincere Marguerite gave him some pretty effective puppy-dog eyes. The crepes were good, of course \u2013 Gawain\u2019s never cooked anything that wasn\u2019t delicious \u2013 but I wasn\u2019t much in the mood for breakfast at 1:00pm. I asked the others if they wanted to go out and do something, but I didn\u2019t get any takers. Gawain wanted to work at his forge, Calamity and Jacob were going to spar with practice knives, Insincere Marguerite said she was going to watch some French film I\u2019d never heard of, and Ace sort of slunk back into hibernation when nobody was looking.<br /> <br /> So I was bored, and I had a couple of hours to kill. More than that, really, since while most of the motley had to make sure they were ship-shape by 6:00 for the opening, I wasn\u2019t actually required to be on-deck until closer to 8:00. In fact, most of the others thought it would be a good idea for me to make myself scarce, to keep anticipation high in the audience. So I decided to call up D.<br /> <br /> \u201cHey babe,\u201d she said when she picked up the call, \u201cwhat\u2019s up?\u201d<br /> <br /> I thought about how to sound suave and cool and all that shit, but in the end I just went with the truth. \u201cI have a couple of hours to kill, and I\u2019m bored,\u201d I admitted. \u201cYou free?\u201d<br /> <br /> She seemed to consider for a minute. \u201cI\u2026 can be,\u201d she said. \u201cGimme an hour and I\u2019ll meet you somewhere. I was gonna come to the show tonight anyway; you wanna get some dinner first?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSounds perfect,\u201d I said. \u201cYou got a favorite restaurant?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cRoselli\u2019s makes a hell of a chicken marsala,\u201d she said.<br /> <br /> \u201cRoselli\u2019s at 4:00 sound good?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSounds perfect. See you there, beautiful,\u201d she shot back.<br /> <br /> \u201cRight back at you,\u201d I replied, and we disconnected.<br /> <br /> I spent the next few hours primping, and trying to make myself look as though I hadn\u2019t spent a few hours primping. I think it mostly just gave me something to do. I wandered out of the house, calling a hasty farewell up to Insincere Marguerite in the rafters (I heard muffled French movie dialog drifting down as I walked through the theater). I hopped in my car, and twenty minutes later I was being shown to a seat in a nice \u2013 if not ostentatiously so \u2013 Italian bistro.<br /> <br /> D strutted in a few minutes later, leather creaking and chains jingling, and looking for all the world like she was <u>seriously</u> enjoying the looks she got from the other patrons. She leaned in and gave me a quick soft kiss on the lips before taking her seat. \u201cSo, what\u2019s new with you, Lori?\u201d she asked, the picture of innocence.<br /> <br /> We had an hour or so of light conversation over really good ziti, and eventually talk turned toward past relationships. I didn\u2019t have too much to say at this point, but D talked a lot about the first serious relationship she had after returning from Arcadia. Apparently, she dated Madame Spidertoes for a while, but didn\u2019t enjoy their time together much. It seems that at the time, Madame Spidertoes was still hung up on her previous flame\u2026 none other than our headlining dancer, Annika.<br /> <br /> I dropped a few pointed comments about Annika at that\u2026 enough to make my less-than-charitable feelings about her known. D didn\u2019t have any particular feelings about Annika (other than a sort of lingering vague resentment over Spidertoes\u2019 preoccupation with her), and in fact mentioned that opening night was the only time she\u2019d ever actually seen Annika. Apparently everyone\u2019s favorite dancer has been something of a shut-in for the past decade and a half.<br /> <br /> We let the conversation turn to more pleasant subjects after that, and I think we both had a lot of fun. We talked about music and movies and things like that, and then I asked her what she liked to do for fun. She mentioned working out and going to the beach, but her eyes really lit up when she talked about something called \u201claser tag.\u201d I\u2019m not sure I fully understood the concept, but apparently it\u2019s a game where people shoot at each other with guns that emit harmless beams of invisible light. The Summer Court has a building set up where people can play this game, which also serves as a sort of training facility for their more martial activities.<br /> <br /> It sounded like fun, even though I know I\u2019ll be terrible at it. We sort of tentatively planned to go try it out together some time in the next few days. Privately, I thought some of the others in the motley might enjoy the experience too\u2026 but I didn\u2019t bring that up just yet, since I sort of wanted an excuse to spend time with D privately.<br /> <br /> I declined dessert, as I didn\u2019t want to be too full when I performed later that night. D had a small bowl of gelato, and kept smirking at me over it like she knew how much I wanted it. She can be such a tease sometimes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Before we left the restaurant, she asked me if I wanted her to stay with me after the show. She still had that cocky, brash exterior, but there was something underneath the swagger\u2026 I\u2019d almost swear she was nervous or shy about the question. Or maybe I\u2019m just projecting\u2026 who can say? I took her hands in mine and told her that I\u2019d love it if she could stay with me, and that settled the matter.<br /> <br /> She followed me back to the house about 7:00 and took a seat with Monica up in the balcony section, while I went backstage to dress and prepare. I only had two numbers tonight\u2026 a solo torch song and my duet with Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne. So I spent most of my time organizing and motivating the other performers. Most of the girls who were here on Wednesday night had pretty much convinced themselves that the \u201cphantom\u201d they saw was some sort of trick of the light, so at least I didn\u2019t have to cook up an explanation for that.<br /> <br /> It was a good show, even if it didn\u2019t quite have the grandeur of opening night. I did one solo number in the first set, a slow sultry version of the Eddie Cantor classic \u201cMakin\u2019 Whoopee.\u201d One of the fans suggested it on opening night, based on a scene from a movie called <u>The Fabulous Baker Boys</u>. I watched that scene on the internet a couple of days ago, and thought I might be able to improve upon the actress\u2019 performance. I wore a slinky green dress slit high up the left thigh, swayed around the stage as best I could. I think it went well.<br /> <br /> My second number didn\u2019t come around until after midnight, near the end of the third set. Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne and I performed a punk-rock update of the Patti Smith song \u201cBecause the Night,\u201d a track that was getting some heavy play just before I was Taken. We totally rocked that number, and brought the house down afterward. I\u2019d changed into a leather skirt and corset by that time, and I played off the chemistry between Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne and myself to charge the number with sexual energy. I think the crowd picked up on that.<br /> <br /> In any case, the take wasn\u2019t quite as big as it had been on our opening night, but we still did respectable business last night. Figuring in food and drink sales as well as the gate, we turned a pretty tidy profit. There was no trouble with ghosts during the show, and no \u201cnemesis\u201d hijinks in the audience either, so I\u2019ll call it a success.<br /> <br /> Madame Spidertoes was there last night, and she took a brief tour of the premises with Calamity to check for ghostly presences. She pretty much confirmed what we had already suspected. There is a murderous ghost lying dormant in the room Calamity had originally claimed as her own, and a more mischievous ghost which roams the house. The woman I encountered on opening night was the latter. Madame Spidertoes thinks she might even be benign; it\u2019s possible she was trying to scare our dancers away from the house to save them from the other ghost.<br /> <br /> Oh, and apparently our basement is something called a \u201chaunt,\u201d or a place where deathly energy is focused into a sort of\u2026 goo, or something like that. I don\u2019t claim to understand everything the lady said, but I registered the fact that a haunt isn\u2019t dangerous in and of itself. The Autumn Court is going to see what they can do about our other supernatural problems.<br /> <br /> Jacob spent a lot of time talking to a younger woman\u2026 well, younger than him, but older than me\u2026 well, younger than I <u>really</u> am, but older than I look\u2026 you know what, never mind. She was college-aged. I didn\u2019t find out if she was a friend, a lover, or what\u2026 but I noticed that he got pretty scowly whenever some young buck looked like he was going to put the moves on her.<br /> <br /> Gawain and I once more joined Monica and D at their table for a little light banter. Gawain seemed oddly shy and nervous around Monica at first, but he seemed to mellow as the night wore on. Or at least that was my take on it; I confess I only had eyes for D. When I first walked up to the table, she stood up, kissed me, and said \u201cwell, my ride\u2019s here\u201d to Monica. Monica \u2013 the exemplary straight man \u2013 asked if D hadn\u2019t driven herself over, and D just smirked.<br /> <br /> Eventually we drifted up to my bedroom. We made out for a while, and we made love for a while, and I found myself falling asleep with my head pillowed on her breast. I know she stayed awake longer than me, because I remember her stroking my hair ever so lightly as I was drifting off.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe fuck is that?\u201d she murmured in my ear a few hours later as the alarm blared in our ears.<br /> <br /> \u201cTime for church,\u201d I managed to yawn out.<br /> <br /> \u201cShit,\u201d D muttered. \u201cYou don\u2019t expect me to go with you, do you Lori?\u201d<br /> <br /> I chuckled. \u201cGo back to sleep, D,\u201d I said, kissing her softly. \u201cYou can stay as long as you like. If you\u2019re still here around noon, I\u2019ll see you when I get back.\u201d<br /> <br /> I put on a button-up white top and a prim grey skirt, pulled my hair back, and put on my glasses. After applying a little sedate make-up, I turned from my bureau mirror to see D sitting up on the bed, leaning on one arm. \u201cDamn,\u201d she said softly, \u201cI actually <u>do</u> kinda want to go to church with you now, babe\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled. \u201cYou\u2019re sweet,\u201d I said, \u201cbut I have to motor if I\u2019m going to make the service.\u201d<br /> <br /> I made it to the church with minutes to spare, got into my robe, and entered the sanctuary with the rest of the choir. I had a solo in the second interlude (\u201cHow Great Thou Art\u201d), and I think it went pretty well. Of course, I wasn\u2019t pouring the glamour into the number like I do at the Dream House\u2026 instilling desire into church-goers doesn\u2019t seem exactly proper to me. Dad seemed pleased with the number, though, and he launched into his sermon (The Importance of Family) with gusto.<br /> <br /> I arrived back at the Dream House a little after noon, and found Gawain busy at the stove with breakfast. I asked him if he could prepare an extra plate for D\u2026 well, in truth, I sort of told him that she\u2019d be staying for breakfast. He gave me a look, and I realized that I was taking advantage of his good nature, and had to apologize immediately. He told me not to worry about it, and he cheerfully made an extra plate\u2026 but I need to find some way to make it up to him. He\u2019s so good to us, and he never asks for anything in return.<br /> <br /> I found D teasing Julia mercilessly about her relationship with Insincere Marguerite. I felt the need to chide her about that\u2026 but Julia had already fled the premises, red-faced and mumbling to herself. I\u2019m sure she\u2019ll be fine, but maybe I should apologize on D\u2019s behalf the next time I see her.<br /> <br /> As we were noshing on omelets, D shared a bit of gossip about the local Changeling scene, including the latest incident in the apparently endless rivalry between Los Angeles\u2019 Day and Night Courts. The Night Court took it into their head to crash the Day Court\u2019s recent May Day celebration\u2026 with zombies! Real live (well\u2026 not \u201clive,\u201d obviously) zombies! They had the zombies reenacting an orgy scene from a Stanley Kubrick movie called \u201cEyes Wide Shut.\u201d Golly.<br /> <br /> When D got ready to go, I asked her to call me about the laser tag thing, and she said she would. I kind of wish I\u2019d kept my mouth shut now, since Gawain in particular seemed really excited about the prospect, and I\u2019d kind of hoped to make it a thing just for me and D. Well, we\u2019ll see how it goes.<br /> <br /> After giving me a fairly intense kiss goodbye, D took her leave, and the rest of us began discussing how and when we were going to help Andromeda harvest her goblin fruits. Calamity called her up and told her we could accompany her into the Hedge tomorrow night at around 8:30. There\u2019s a show scheduled then, but we\u2019ve all agreed that the motley doesn\u2019t need to be present for <u>every</u> show the Dream House runs, so we\u2019re going to give that one a miss and help out our fellow Lost.<br /> <br /> I really hope this isn\u2019t a trap.<br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei Grace</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 06-22-2014, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T02:35:46-07:00","id":176878,"title":"","content":"<b>Calamity's Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> <b><u>May 4th -</u></b><u>Days without stabbing: 7</u><br /> <br /> Well, yesterday wasn't perfect but it certainly went better than expected. Gawain woke up and I was there and all. I tried to talk to him but despite what felt like hours of going over what I was going say in my head I just couldn't seem to start. And he didn't seem to want to talk about things yet. Maybe it just wasn't the right time. I know I felt too wretched to really press it and the call of coffee was mighty tempting. So in the end we just went to breakfast.<br /> <br /> And we walked in to find Insincere Marguerite standing on the counter going through the cabinets and Jacob handing out coffee, already fixed the way we like it. I managed a chuckle and took the mug quite happily. Gawain made crepes again, at my Darkling sister's adorable request. I was a bit nervious after the previous night but everything went forward more or less like normal. Lorelei was restless and looking to get out before the show. Insincere Marguerite announced she was going to watch a movie and invited us to join her. She even offered to put on the subtitles but would not switch the language track. Good to know she stands on the right side of that one. There really are some lines that where not meant to be crossed. I don't think anyone took her up on the offer and that's unfortunate. I should see about watching something with her sometime. Maybe get her to teach me some proper French while we're at it. It's such a lovely language and I would dearly love to be able to threaten someone with such style and grace.<br /> <br /> But instead I was on clean up detail. I mean, I was not going to leave cleaning up after my midnight wretching to someone else. Gawain looked like he wanted to volunteer, but he'd already said he was going to be working in the forge and Jacob had offered to help out. It was brief but it was there, the first awkward moment and not last of the day. That shit is not okay and I will fucking sort it out this afternoon.<br /> <br /> So, while cleaning up, Jacob asked me about what I did for fun. It was a bit amusing as he was very clearly trying not to sound like he was trying to pick me up. But he's been trying to find things that the rest of us like to do and share in them to get to know us better. I had to admit it was not a bad plan. We do need to know about each other to best support and protect each other after all. I kinda stammered a bit at first. I mean, I don't exactly do <i>fun</i> things. That's Gawain's department most of the time. But after a moment I did have a thought. I hadn't had a proper workout against another knife fighter since the last time I saw Luna... Damn, I haven't had time to go hunting with her in way too fucking long. Now that things are settling down here, I am going to have to take a night off to head out to the woods and visit her. Don't get me wrong, Gawain is a good fighter but sparring with his majestic sword just isn't the same. So I suggested that we could grab a couple of Gawain's finished but unsharpened knives to practice with. I don't think it was quite what he had in mind but Jacob seemed to like the idea so once we finished cleaning the bedroom we changed and headed to the forge and then out to the outdoor stage since it had plenty of space and wouldn't be in the way of anyone else.<br /> <br /> Despite still feeling a bit hung over I was more than a little giddy as I limbered up and gave my blade a few test swings. Once we were out in the sun, Jacob peeled off his shirt and gave me another look at those pretty scars... Guess the damned fireball isn't completely worthless. Our fight with the Harvestman was over so fast, I hardly got to see any of my Russian comrade's moves and I was really looking forward to learning what he could do. Once we dropped into stances everything just slipped away except for the pair of us. There was no Snow Globe, no night in Belleview, nothing but a pair of blades glinting in the light. Fuck but I love that feeling, that moment when everything is so perfectly clear and still. I should have started off slow since I was facing a new partner and didn't know exactly what his skill level was but fuck it, that's not how a real fight works and that's certainly not how Luna taught me. Besides, I was pretty sure he could keep up and if not, I could have dialed it back. But hot damn if it wasn't the other way around. I came in hard and fast and he danced around me like Fred fucking Astair. I mean, knife fighting is supposed to be about speed and finesse instead of power but it's always nice to fight someone as nimble as myself. He's no Luna, but Jacob most definitely made me bring out my A game. And once we got going, we fucking <i>danced</i> out there.<br /> <br /> I think he'd planned to hold back and work up slowly but after that intial rush of mine, Jacob switched gears and met my intensity swing for swing. It was fucking glorious. Turns out we're pretty evenly matched so the fight went back and forth a good while. Damn but there's nothing like a good opponent to really bring it out in you. I was in the zone slashing and dodging and blocking flawlessly. I sweated out the last of the hangover right quick and I could feel every fucking inch of my body singing. I couldn't help but laugh as we went at it, it just felt so damn good.<br /> <br /> After a while, I realized that fienting or darting past his guard wasn't going to get the job done. The man's just too damn quick and focused to fall for that shit. So I decided it was time to stop playing around and damn the torpedoes. I waited until he came in low and rather than block or sidestep I just twisted a bit and lunged in hard. I flipped the knife around since there wasn't a way to pull the force of that thrust with my whole body behind it like that (and yeah, I <i>did</i> want him to feel the blow and know it was hard enough to have gone through his ribs to his heart). He saw it coming but he was committed. There was a flash in his eyes, surprise and well... maybe just a hint of fear. I thought he was worried that I was about to actually stab him. I took a pretty good scratch to the bottom edge of my ribs on the side but I planted the base of my dagger to his chest, right on target above his heart. And then it clicked. It was where I'd aimed that caught him off guard. In going for the heart I'd planted the hilt pretty soildly atop his brand and it clearly hurt. He clenched his teeth hard and jerked, almost dropping his knife before he recovered his composure. That brought me up a bit short. I mean, it was a pretty hard hit but I know how well he hides things and that was a lot of pain to make him slip like that. I looked and didn't see any blood on him or the handle of my knife, so it wasn't that. I almost let it go since he clearly hadn't intended to let me see how it effected him. But fuck, I know all too well how hard it is to open up and how keeping that shit inside makes it fester. So I asked him if he was alright. He started to wave me off with an automatic, \u201cNo I'm fine.\u201d at first, but then he hesitated and slowly straightened up.<br /> <br /> \u201cI was just taken by surprise. It's The Lady's mark. She puts it on things that She considers Hers. It... aches sometimes.\u201d<br /> <br /> Then it was my turn to pause. He'd spoken calmly, but I could hear the capital letters. The ones we all use when speaking of our Keepers. He'd offered me a truth, a secret he'd kept to himself before. I was tempted to ask more, but I didn't think it was time yet. So I just reached for his shoulder and told him that if he wanted to talk about it, I knew a thing or two about pain. I was trying to keep from getting too heavy but I did want to make it a clear offer. Maybe he'll take me up on it. Maybe he won't. But once I'd put that out there, I let it drop and turned to talking about the fight and thanking him for the workout. We exchanged our observations and spoke lightly for a few moments before he offered to take the blades back to Gawain and let him know they'd handled well. We both said we should do it again and I seriously hope he meant it because it was a hell of good way to blow off some steam and it left me feeling focused and alive for the rest of the day.<br /> <br /> The night's show went smoothly. We had a good turnout with several changelings. Queen Charlotte was there with Madam Spidertoes. A small knot of Winter Courtiers claimed a table as did Becky and her usual cohort. Austin was in as were Julia and De la Roche and Monica. I made the rounds, checking in with mundane and fae alike. I am not entirely comfortable with this whole smoozing thing yet but I seem to be getting better at it and someone has to play the part of manager, which I guess I did volunteer myself for. I just didn't think about this side of it really. I did take the opportunity to spend some time at Becky's table, chatting with my favorite dragon lady and actually meeting Dark Kimberly and White Maria. They both seem nice, though I think Maria was a little intimidated by me at first. I didn't catch back up with them after the show as Madam Spidertoes had said she wanted to look into the ghost situation.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite joined me as she had not been presented to the Darkling Matriarch yet. We showed her to my room and she performed a ritual to call up an echo of the ghost there and speak to it. I did not recognize it as the woman from the dressing room and Madam confirmed that this was the murdering ghost and to be wary of her if we saw her. We moved to the dressing room next and Madam Spidertoes waited 'patiently' while Lori moved the girls along and cleared it for us. She performed the ritual again and called up the echo of the ghost that disrupted things on opening night. Turns out she is the mischivious one but that while she does like scaring people (which I can respect, fear is <i>delicious</i> after all) she's also acting to protect people from the murdering ghost by driving them away so she can't kill them. Hopefully once we've dealt with the hanging bitch we can do something gentle with her. The last stop was the basement, where Madam Spidertoes informed us that there was indeed a pool of what she called plasm, which is apparently ghost residue and harmless. There has been some talk of trying to collect it and sell at a goblin market, but I'm not sure how we would do such a thing. Guess I should hit the lighthouse's libary sometime and see what I can find out about it.<br /> <br /> So, once Madam Spidertoes departed, I called a quick motley meeting to bring everyone up to speed on the ghost situation. It went quickly enough and everyone slipped away until it was just Gawain and I. I mentioned that he should make sure to call Monica some time. He offered to move furniture or help me move my things to the spare bedroom and I told him it was fine since it was just temporary. Yeah, it was as stilted and awkward as it sounds there. I commented on that, hoping that calling it out might open the door to talking about things but Gawain took it as me dismissing him I think. I should have called him back or chased after him but I just let him go. Fuck I hate this awkward shit going on between us and I am not going to let it continue. I've talked to him before about learning some of his contracts sometime and I'm going to call him on that this afternoon before tonight's show. And while we are alone together I am going to get this fucking shit out in the open and we are going to have a fucking conversation about it. Also, I am going to learn the contract of stone from him so I can actually fire the Mad Max suicide special without breaking my damn arm.<br /> <br /> It had been a day at that point, so I decided to pack it in and do the books in the morning. Soon as I was alone in the spare room I heard that familiar rasp from the vent. It's always nice when Tommy visits and I had wanted to speak to him about Gawain's new friends. First off, he warned me that my assocation with Andromedia had brought me to the attention of both the Winter Court and the Summer Court. Apparently she has (or they at least believe she does) some sort of Arcadian device that she escaped with that they are both keen on getting ahold of. The Summer Court alegedly has some sort of evidence beyond Hailey's heresay that she's a loyalist but they've not shown it so who knows. And I've apparently been honored with a file in the desk of Lucien Torrez, the Summer Court's resident dirty handyman. Meanwhile, the Winter Court is apparently not above just taking what they, or more specifically Master Darke, wants by whatever means. So yeah, looks like I'm in the middle of some sort of powder keg of intrigue centered on that poor little grey lamb. Well, personally I say (and did to Tommy) fuck 'em all. If they want a piece of me they can punch my dance card whenever they damn well please and we'll see who winds up on the floor in a pool of their own blood crying. But it's not just my ass on the line these days. I swore to protect the motley and they me, so whatever shitstorm comes down on me comes down on them as well. I mentioned the situation at breakfast when Andromeda and our Goblin Fruit expedition came up. Nobody seemed inclined to bail on my pretty little sweetling yet so we're meeting her at Glamour Springs tomorrow night at sundown. We're going in locked and loaded since there could be betrayal or ambush from one (or both) of the interested courts. Or hey, maybe we'll only get to fight some hobgoblins. At any rate, it's going to be one hell of an adventure and I am pretty much garunteed my fill of bloodshed any way it falls out. I cannot fucking wait.<br /> <br /> Once that was out of the way, we had some pleasant chatting. I asked him about Monica and Captain Jack. Tommy seems to actually like Captain Jack, had plenty of good things to say about him and really only warned that he's fearless and overconfident so we shouldn't rely on him to warn us off something too dangerous. Sounds like my kind of guy and if Tommy likes him that's enough for me to trust the ogre to be on the level.<br /> <br /> Monica, on the other hand, does apparently have a skeleton in her closet. Well, maybe I should say her water closet... Seems that she wasn't exactly asked or invited to join the Bishops but rather told she had to after she ate the one that tried to help her out of the Hedge. Tommy says he's square with her, but I can tell he's not fond of the woman. Her victim was one of us, a fellow Darkling, a Mirrorskin named Tussaud (after the wax museum I'm sure). He was apparently a friend of Tommy's, so I can understand his dislike of her. But to his credit, he admitted that since getting free of the Hedge she really has been the good samaritan everyone claims. He's too much of a gentleman to let his personal feelings cloud his judgement. I have to say, if it happened in the Hedge then I can't really judge her too harshly. Kettles and pots and all. Plus she certainly seems to have gotten her shit together since then. So it does seem she really might be good enough for Gawain. They do make a nice couple. I think she could be the princess for the happily ever after he deserves but only time will tell for sure.<br /> <br /> Well, once Tommy left I crashed out and slept through the rest of the night and the next morning while Lori was at church. I woke up feeling reasonably decent and headed to brunch. It was pretty clear that Gawain had a rough one last night, he looked downright ragged. Then Lori joked about not getting much sleep either, but I think she was just being playful. At least Gawain took it that way and so I followed suit. Plus she doesn't know about the nightmares. I'm the only one he's really talked to about them I think. Now that we've got the Hollow secured, I should ask him if I can try to help him with them, at least on nights before we've got something important planned like tonight. It would be nice to be able to help him get a good rest and he can't argue that it's not worth making sure he's at his best for the trip into the Hedge tomorrow. At any rate, Jacob and I pitched in to help him with breakfast. Jacob was on toast duty and I chopped the veggies for the omlettes. De la Rocha joined us for breakfast and was entertaining company, but Julia apparently was a bit shy and slipped out quietly. De la Rocha talked about the Night Court's prank sending zombies to crash the Day Court's formal with a reinactment of an orgy scene. It sounded like a pretty serious amount of effort for a prank, but apparently there is a real Spy vs Spy thing going on with those courts. Insincere Marguerite seemed quite pleased that they'd actually pulled it off which was nice. There was also talk of a laser tag place run by the Summer Court. I was surprised to hear those were still around but Gawain really lit up so I have no doubt that we're going to be running about in the blacklight with toy guns at some point. Insincere Marguerite seemed skeptical as she's more about hiding than fighting, but we did point out that camping is a valid and successful strategy. I'm sure we'll manage to drag her with us when we go. After that we talked about Andromeda and once it was decided that we were still in I called her and set things up.<br /> <br /> Since then I've settled up last night's accounts and taken a few minutes to get this diary caught up. Goes to show I was tired that I didn't write anything last night I guess. But at this point, work is done till opening and I've put off talking with Gawain as long as I can. I don't want to confront him or put him off but I won't let this weirdness between us continue. Fuck, the only reason I haven't fucked him yet is because I was afraid it'd make things awkward. I really hope we can sort the shit out and get back to being relaxed and comfortable around each other again. I mean, I really want... no, let's be ab-so-fucking-lutly honest here, I goddamn fucking <i>need</i> him around. He's probably the only reason I didn't just drift away and let go of my human side after what happened with my parents. Yes, I've got the motley and the Dream House to protect now and that responsibility helps to keep me grounded now but he's been my anchor since I escaped and I fucking care about him. Hell, maybe I even love him...<br /> <br /> And there's the whole damnable problem. He's strong and trustworthy and loyal and kind and... Hell, he's a fucking fairytale prince. I want him to be happy and if I thought I could be the one that gave him what he needed and deserved I would happily be his. But he doesn't get it. Yes, I am broken but while he wants to fix me, I understand that I can't ever be right again. I became this way because it was the only way to survive what the Whispers did to me. And I did survive. As far as I know I'm the only one that never gave up. The only one that escaped. I beat Them. I tasted Their blood. I fucking <i>won</i>. I am strong now and I will die fighting before I give that up. I'm a weapon, forged in misery and suffering and pain. I wish I'd known what I was before going to Katt's home. I wish I'd understood then what I do now. But I didn't and since then I have learned to control what's inside me rather than be controlled by it. But my heart is scarred. It is twisted and dark and hateful. How can I share something so ugly with anyone let alone someone so bright?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob's Journal</b><br /> <br /> I have to say it was an interesting day all around. We all got up late since we\u2019d been up so long with the game, and the drinking and the talking. We all stumbled downstairs around 2:00pm-ish. I immediately set to work making coffee. My brain felt like cotton batting, so I can only guess what Calamity and Lorelei\u2019s felt like. No, I know what theirs felt like. I had my hangover morning just the other day. I don\u2019t think today counts as a full hangover for me though, just uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> Speaking of uncomfortable, things were just a bit tense when we all gathered in the kitchen. Most of us revealed things that were rather personal to the rest of the group last night and today was the day to deal with the fallout from all of that. And as luck would have it, there really wasn\u2019t all that much in the way of fallout. Calamity was nervous when she first walked in. Didn\u2019t really show much, but I could tell. Lorelei was too. For my part I continued on as if nothing out of the ordinary had happened and handed out the coffee. Everyone else pretty much did the same thing.<br /> <br /> As far as \u2018other things\u2019 go, I\u2019ve gotten the impression that Insincere Marguerite does not want to be exclusive, but is picky about her partners, so I tried not to be too \u201ctouchy-feely\u201d this morning, but did want to let her know that I enjoyed what we had last night, and may have again sometime. I hope I got that across with the looks here and there and a smile. I\u2019m not good at subtle positive emotional displays. Still working on it. Well, genuine positive emotions. I\u2019m much better at intimidating people and making them uncomfortable. Had a lot of practice with that. But life is all about choices right? Well, I\u2019m choosing to not be an asshole. Not sure if it\u2019s working so far. Making Calamity cry last night was not really a step in the right direction, but at least I wasn\u2019t intending to do that. I was just an asshole by accident? Somehow doesn\u2019t sound comforting does it? Sigh.<br /> <br /> We had breakfast as usual, or do you call it brunch if it\u2019s breakfast food eaten at lunch time? Anyway, Gawain did his usual wonderful job on the food, we had crepes and eggs. Most of us ate our fill. Lorelei didn\u2019t join us. I think she was still feeling a bit queasy from the night of drinking. She only drank beer, but she did have a good collection of bottles at the end of the night. After that Gawain expressed an interest in working out some tension at the forge, and Calamity said that she needed to clean up the guest room she had used. No one really needed to ask why it needed cleaning, so I volunteered to help her out. Gawain briefly looked like he was going to change his mind, but stayed quiet. I think he didn\u2019t want to appear too clingy. I\u2019m glad he was there for her last night, well early this morning. They have a history and she needed someone to lean on I\u2019m sure.<br /> <br /> So, the cleaning went quickly. Between the two of us we had things back to rights in no time. Not the most enviable job, but I\u2019ve done far worse, so it really wasn\u2019t all that bad. Calamity was quiet the whole time. I\u2019m not sure if she was just concentrating on cleaning, on not feeling sick, or just reluctant to talk. Could have been a combination of all three. After we were done and had put away the cleaning supplies I asked her what she liked to do for fun. It came out kind of awkward because I was trying not to sound like I was trying to ask her on a date. I just wanted to see what she liked to do in her spare time. I explained I was trying to do stuff with everyone in the motley that they thought was fun to get to know everyone better.<br /> <br /> Calamity admitted that she didn\u2019t really have any hobbies or things she did for fun. She did say that the two things she enjoyed the most were drinking and fighting, and that drinking was off the table for the foreseeable future. She suggested sparring out back, and I said that sounded like fun. As soon as she said that I was thinking about how I was going to assess Calamity\u2019s fighting ability and if I would need to pull back to keep from hurting her. I figured we\u2019d both get cut since we\u2019d be fighting with knives. You don\u2019t do that and not get cut. It\u2019s just a matter of how badly. But that issue was solved right up front when she said that she thought Gawain had some blunt knives at his forge. So, we both changed clothes, she in her bike shorts and sports bra (hot) and me in my sweat pants. I figured it\u2019d be too hot to wear a shirt, and there was no point in hiding the scars anymore. Anyhoo\u2026after changing we went down to the forge. Gawain was working on something, but stopped when he spotted us. We asked if he had any still blunt knives so we could practice and he pointed to the ones he had. We each picked a pair that suited us and went out back.<br /> <br /> Now something I don\u2019t think I\u2019ve mentioned in writing before is that there is a stage in the back. I had been thinking of sparring in the yard, but we just looked at the stage, then each other and headed in that direction. I had been planning on starting off slow, see what she can do and adjust accordingly. Yeah, that plan went right out the window from the get go. Calamity started off hard and fast and it was all I could do to get out of the way. I think I managed to do kind of a spinning side step to dodge her attack, and used the momentum to power my own. Nothing light or easy about that fight either. She started fast, saw I could keep up and kept on going. No wasted movements on her part, or mine for that matter. Block one blade, attack with the other. Spin around behind, thrust, dodge the incoming blade. She\u2019s good. Really good. And she fights like me. No strong-arming, just quick, agile attacks. Constantly moving, turning a block into an attack if the opportunity arises.<br /> <br /> I really want to know where she learned to do that. Seriously\u2026she had a good teacher. If she picked it up herself, then I\u2019m impressed. I think she must have had a teacher for some of it though. There\u2019s some flourishes to some moves that seem practiced, and there\u2019s a block or two that she uses that isn\u2019t intuitive. I\u2019ve always been quick, but I had a teacher to show me the subtleties of knife fighting. Maybe it\u2019s a razorhand thing? Rook was my teacher, and he is really good with his knives. Scary good. Calamity\u2019s not quite to that level yet, which is just fine. I need more practice before I go up against someone that good again.<br /> <br /> So, how did the fight end you ask? Yeah, probably not healthy to be asking myself questions in my own journal. Anyhoo\u2026short answer is, Calamity won. It\u2019s not that short or that simple though. I hadn\u2019t planned on giving so much away in our first fight. I figured I\u2019d ease into it and reveal more skill later. Yeah, that didn\u2019t happen. She\u2019s good, she\u2019s fast, and she knows where to hit to wound, and where to hit to kill. I knew she had skill. I saw some of it in the hedge the other day when we investigated the Hollow. That was against a hedge beast though. No real finesse needed there. Hand to hand fighting though, that requires finesse. I had to work to keep that girl on her toes, and she sure as hell kept me on mine. And it was fun. I don\u2019t think I\u2019ve really had that much fun in a long time. Before Rook wanted to kill me, we had some good sparring matches. I know how he fights though, so fun though it might have been to spar with him, I knew the moves. With Calamity though, it\u2019s all new. I had no idea what she was going to do next, so I had to rely on practice and skill to see me through. In the end though it was a kind of feint that got me. I was going for a spot on her ribs. With a sharp blade it would have slid between two of them and made it hurt to breath. She took the hit. Before I could register what she was planning she stepped into my space and landed a touch on my chest. Left side, right on the brand. It was a thrust that she\u2019d turned the blade to hit me with the handle. She put some force behind it too. I had to concede defeat at that and started to hold up my hands. I almost dropped the knife in my left hand from the pain though. I had forgotten how much that damn brand could hurt. I think Calamity noticed something because she asked if I was okay. I thought I\u2019d hid my reaction well enough, but she\u2019s as good as I am with such things. I told her that I was fine, just that it ached now and again. She looked at the brand more closely, like she wanted to touch it like she had my scars. I told her that The Lady gave me that. That she put that mark on everything that was hers.<br /> <br /> I almost said more. I\u2019m not sure what I was going to tell her, but I stopped myself at the last moment. Instead I complemented her on a good fight and offered to bring the blades back to Gawain. We then split up, her to get a shower and me to return knives then shower. I walked into the garage and over to the big guy. He turned when he heard me. I handed back the knives and told him that the balance is good and headed to get my own shower. I think normally I might have stayed longer to go into detail, but I was too tired. Too sweaty. Too sore.<br /> <br /> I will admit that I was a bit surprised when Calamity hit me in the chest. Good target, but it hit the Lady\u2019s brand and it hurt. I have been doing my best to forget about that dam thing that I forgot how much it can hurt to mess with it. I tried to remove it once. Figured I\u2019d bleed a bit and have a new scar, but I\u2019d be free of her mark. Yeah, didn\u2019t work out that way. I tried to remove it one quick cut. All I remember is blinding white hot pain, then I woke up on the floor bleeding. I had managed to cut myself. I cut myself good, but the wound was to the side of the brand not on it. I know I positioned the knife correctly, it just wouldn\u2019t cut it. I can only guess that is left over from the bargain I made with the Lady so long ago. Or maybe it\u2019s a reminder that I\u2019m hers, forever and always. Yeah, cheerful thought that.<br /> <br /> So, now my arms and legs feel like jelly from the exertion and my chest hurts where Calamity didn\u2019t cut me. Doesn\u2019t sound right when I put the thought on paper, but it\u2019s accurate. I just need a long hot shower, and maybe a beer. Yeah, hot showers. Haven\u2019t gotten tired of those yet either.<br /> <br /> **** ****<br /> <br /> The show went off without a hitch tonight. Everyone did great, even Ace, who\u2019d been kinda scarce today. I think he was working on ideas or something. That guy takes brainstorming sessions to a new level. Anyway, I did my bit as bartender, making drinks and serving them. I did act the \u201cwaiter\u201d a couple of times though. Took drinks to a few people early on so it wouldn\u2019t look weird if I brought drinks to my sister and her friends later. I don\u2019t get to see her much, so I guess I\u2019ll take any opportunity. I just don\u2019t want to seem like a stalker. I want to make sure that she\u2019s safe. Plus part of me really wants to be able to pick up where we left off as brother and sister, hanging out and talking, watching movies or hiking. We used to love hiking in the mountains and discovering hidden places. That desire kind of got tempered by discovering the Lady\u2019s cave, but I still like hiking. Damn, going down depressing roads with all that. I miss her even though she\u2019s so close. I miss my parents. I was looking forward to my father teaching me how to drive, and my mother telling me the secret behind her grandmother\u2019s stew. I wanted to hear father\u2019s stories of when he was young and Russia was called the Soviet Union. I know he did things he was not proud of to keep himself and mother safe. I\u2019d see a scar on his side or the knife he kept tucked in his desk drawer, and this shadow would cross his face. I didn\u2019t understand when I was sixteen. I didn\u2019t know what that look meant. I do now. Father always said that he\u2019d tell me when I was older, and now an imposter wears my face and rejects my heritage. I can never have that conversation with him now and I mourn the lost chance.<br /> <br /> Yeah\u2026definitely moving into depressing territory there. Better dial that back down before I decide drinking might be a good idea. I know I should move on and let my family live their lives. I guess I\u2019m just jealous of the little shit that wears my face and lives my life and doesn\u2019t realize what he has.<br /> <br /> **** ****<br /> <br /> As last night was a show we all gathered in the kitchen around noon-ish to eat. Gawain walked in with far less energy in his step than usual and was in a bit of a grumpy mood. As this has been far from the norm for him we all expressed concern. He just said that he hadn\u2019t slept well, and moved on to preparing to make breakfast. I figured that I would do what I could to help and poured him a larger than usual coffee, made just how he takes it, and offered to make the toast. I told him I\u2019d need more practice before I cooked eggs, but I could brown bread. Calamity chopped up vegetables to put in the omelets. In pretty short order we had breakfast for all of us, including De la Roche. Apparently she stayed with Lorelei last night. Julia had stayed over with Insincere Marguerite, but left early so she didn\u2019t join us for food. I think our resident French woman has feelings for Julia. I don\u2019t think she wants something serious there, or won\u2019t let herself get too attached. What she had mentioned before about stealing Changelings from Keepers and keeping them for herself made me think that\u2019s why she doesn\u2019t want a committed relationship with anyone. Too close to what she had before, or too easy for it to become what she had before and I don\u2019t think she wants that.<br /> <br /> Anyhoo\u2026while we were talking over food De la Roche mentioned something about the Night Court doing something to spoil the Day Court\u2019s May Day celebration. Something about actual zombies acting out the sex scene from some big movie over and over. Sometimes I just don\u2019t understand people. Insincere Marguerite seemed to think it was amusing and I think made some comment about having wondered if they were going to go through with it. What is the phrase? Whatever makes your boat float?<br /> <br /> As Del la Roche was leaving there was mention of laser tag and Gawain instantly perked up. That seemed to get him at least a bit back to his normal mood. Apparently the Summer Court runs the business and makes money while using the place to train its courtiers. Sounded like fun. I like paint ball myself, though I don\u2019t think I\u2019ve actually played laser tag. It wasn\u2019t super big in Portland, or in St. Petersburg for that matter. Maybe we can plan something for the motley. Lorelei looked like she wanted to keep De La Roche to herself for any game that might get played though, so we may need to go a couple of times. I don\u2019t have a whole lot of experience with guns, especially not since I found that damn cave, but at least with the laser tag guns you just point and shoot, right?<br /> <br /> After the Summer courtier left Calamity brought up that Andromeda had wanted to go into the hedge to get Goblin fruit and figured now was as good a time as any to discuss our options. She told us that had been warned by a friend that the Summer and Winter Courts were keeping an eye on her because of her relationship with Andromeda. Apparently they are both getting restless because the girl hasn\u2019t tried anything yet. I\u2019m not sure if they know that we\u2019re planning a trip into the hedge with the suspected loyalist or not. They\u2019ll find out at some point, or someone will tell them. I wonder if this is something that I\u2019m supposed to mention to my king?<br /> <br /> So, we discussed when would be a good time to go to the hedge and what to bring. I believe we decided on Monday night about 8:00/8:30pm. It\u2019s a show night, but we decided that the motley doesn\u2019t need to be present for every show. Calamity called Andromeda and let her know what day we\u2019d picked, and to see if that worked for her. I believe the date and time were acceptable, so now we just need to wait and see what happens. As much as Calamity likes Andromeda I believe she is planning on being prepared for any eventuality, including betrayal. I know my motley-mate wants to believe the best of her lover, but I think I know her well enough to know that Calamity won\u2019t let herself do that. She is practical if nothing else. I suggested a couple of things to bring, mostly stuff I\u2019d bring on any hiking trip, to the Hedge or otherwise.<br /> <br /> Lorelei mentioned that she had plans to take a first aid class soon. I believe she is learning the healing contracts of the Spring Court and from what I understand it is a good idea to have a working knowledge of first aid to perform the contracts better. Calamity mentioned that the Spring healing contract works really well, and implied that she\u2019d been on the receiving end of it in the past. I have too, and agree that it is nice. It\u2019s certainly very helpful. Sometimes it just isn\u2019t enough though. I couldn\u2019t help but thing of Felicity. Diane tried so hard to heal the girl. I could tell she was tired before she even tried to heal the girl, but she did her best. It just wasn\u2019t enough. I could see the moment when Diane realized that despite her best efforts Felicity wasn\u2019t going to make it. That sweet girl just smiled at Diane, she had always looked up to her, and closed her eyes one last time. That sweet shy girl that loved popsicles and after the first time wasn\u2019t afraid to ask me to make one for her. Dammit. Why do the innocent always suffer while those of us who deserve our fates keep going?<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t honestly know Andromeda well enough to gauge if she\u2019s being straight with us, or if she\u2019s serving her keeper. I want to give her the benefit of the doubt, but like Calamity I have a hard time trusting. So when we go into the hedge with the little alien-looking girl I will treat her like I would anyone, but keep an eye out for any tricks. I will prepare for a fight. I would rather do that and laugh at my paranoia later than be caught unaware. And if that girl betrays us, if she leads us to a trap. I will end her.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite's Whispers</b><br /> <br /> An uneventful day after the drama of the previous night, we spent a quiet afternoon before opening the Cabaret. Some of the talk and events last night made me a little homesick, so I decided to watch <i>Am\u00e9lie</i>, as it always reminds me of home. I told others they could watch with me. No one was interested; I thought perhaps Lorelei would watch with me, as she seemed without anything to do, but no, as it turned out she went out to see De La Rocha. It is okay. I am not sure Americans would really enjoy <i>Am\u00e9lie</i>. I hauled a small TV up to the catwalks and set up the puppets. They watched it with me. I became melancholic part of the time. When I cried a little, the puppets were there for me to help dab the few stray tears away.<br /> <br /> Still, no one can remain sad watching <i>Am\u00e9lie</i>.<br /> <br /> The show went well. Julia was there. It was nice to see her. Lorelei went on stage. It was a good show. Afterwards, I met Madame Spidertoes with Calamity. She did not say much to me, but she was not rude. She wore a veil over face and carried a fan. We went first to Calamity\u2019s room, where she used a contract to speak to what she called an echo. Turns out that the room Calamity was in has the more dangerous ghost. There was second ghost in the dressing room. It was the mischievous one, the one Lorelei saw. I should say she. Madame Spidertoes spoke to the echo there as well, and said she is sort of on our side. Sort of. But mischievous.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m mischievous.<br /> <br /> Afterwards, I found Julia, and retired. She loves me. It\u2019s scary. She wanted some form of Pledge, mostly just a short term romantic one. We will see. I am not sure what there is to Pledge, exactly, since I am not being chaste (and don\u2019t expect her to) and I don\u2019t think either of us plan to stop having sex. Support her maybe? I do already. We will see. I am nervous of what would happen if my Dearest showed up, but Julia fell in love with me in a much more \u2026organic, less terror filled sort of way. Does it matter if they both loved me in the end? Maybe. Maybe Julia is better for me. Maybe not. What if my Dearest returns, wanting be taken back into the dark. It\u2019s uncomfortable, and I just can\u2019t quite explain what was peculiar about my previous\u2026\u201drelationship\u201d. I don\u2019t know what to do. The idea of Julia being horrified and no longer wanting anything to do with me is\u2026deeply, deeply upsetting.<br /> <br /> She left early. I asked her if she wanted to join us for breakfast. Maybe she will later. I think that if our relationship is going to work at all she needs to be okay with the Motley. When she met them in the context of hanging around while Calamity was practicing all was well. I do not know why they scare her in other contexts. I should speak to her further. Yes.<br /> <br /> Breakfast went well. It is a new day. We discussed Andromeda\u2019s request. Monday night we go with Andromeda to the Hedge. We will see how it goes. I have some ideas to use the Caravan Palace song <i>Brotherswing</i> for something, but I am not sure what. I am glad I liberated my movies and CDs from my Fetch. I will brainstorm on stage a bit, see if a dance comes to me.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session VI</i><br /> <br /> Not much to comment on. My computer died and this is being written with an unfamiliar word processor, so I am mostly just trying to keep the usual formatting. I will be brief.<br /> <br /> Fatigue from lack of sleep from my various issues combined with Ace's player's very last minute cancellation meant I was a bit unprepared. Still, it was a good session overall, good RP. Hopefully should be a bit more action in the upcoming one.<br /> <br /> Comments and questions welcome as usual. I may be a bit slow till after Monday, but feel free to chime in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 06-22-2014, 05:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T17:55:44-07:00","id":189013,"title":"","content":"Journals are in! However, due to 4<sup>th</sup> of July related stuff going on (the group is American) we won\u2019t have journals from Lorelei or Jacob this time. Both players intend to have next journal cover this and next session, however (it looks like both will miss the coming session due to aforementioned hijinx) so you won\u2019t be without their perspectives for long. Fear not, though, Gawain, Calamity, and Insincere Marguerite have stories to tell, though a bit myopically. Nonetheless, let\u2019s hear them out.<br /> <br /> I should note, again, some journals (especially Calamity\u2019s) contains some adult content. Seems a theme with my WoD games.<br /> <br /> <i>Session VII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> May 5th<br /> <br /> Wow. Just, I mean, wow. These past 24 hours might have started out rough, but man. They sure as hell got better fast. I kinda didn\u2019t even wanna start breakfast, just stay there in Calamity\u2019s bed with her for as long as possible, but it\u2019s kinda like a tradition now, and besides, I don\u2019t need to go getting clingy or anything, you know?<br /> <br /> See, after breakfast yesterday, Calamity asked me to help her figure out the Contract of Stone. She wanted to be able to shoot her pistol-shotgun thing, the one she called Max, without hurting herself, and that takes some serious brute strength. I\u2019d even have a problem with it, without the Stone Contracts, apparently. The others were all up to their own thing. I think Ace got roped into shopping with Lori, God rest his soul. So we headed off to the forge, since that\u2019s kinda my space in the House, plus we didn\u2019t want to bother Insincere Marguerite and Julia.<br /> <br /> Once she\u2019d gotten it mostly down, she got kinda a set, focussed look on her face, a little like she\u2019d had the night before, after the show. Things had been weird, she said, and we needed to figure out what was going on with us. I kinda joked that I\u2019d hoped she knew, but it was actually mostly true - I didn\u2019t really have any idea what was going on. I was mostly just terrified I\u2019d screwed things up somehow, you know?<br /> <br /> I still think she\u2019s why I got back. The dream getting disrupted let me get out of the Dream-lord\u2019s domain, and into the Hedge, you know? But I had nothing pulling me back to the real world, no real memories left of family, or home, or loved ones to get me back, just the kid I ran into, who I needed to protect, who turned into a beautiful woman as we ran to whatever she needed.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t want to, not really, but I said we could go back, to the way it was before, where we were friends and I\u2019d try to stop asking for more. I wasn\u2019t going to be able to stop loving her though and I said so. I probably shouldn\u2019t have, it wasn\u2019t really fair, you know? She knew I thought she was beautiful and she knew it was more than that. But I don\u2019t think she expected me to pull out the \u2018l\u2019 word. She\u2019d made her objections - that she couldn\u2019t make me happy, that I was a fairy tale prince and she liked pain too much. And that she was a monster.<br /> <br /> She said it different then, or at least explained it more. She said it like it was a part of her, something that was under control. That her darker side is, well, darker than mine, and even closer to the surface, is something I can\u2019t really argue, it\u2019s a fair point. And if that\u2019s what she means when she says she\u2019s a monster, I can accept that, you know? Especially if she\u2019s my monster.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s the way she said it too, that she could be my monster. If this were one of the video blog diary things, I\u2019d have to figure out how to edit out about 2 minutes of me grinning like a doofus at the paper after I wrote that. It\u2019s even sillier since I\u2019m not one hundred percent sure I know exactly what that means. I think it means we\u2019re dating, but an open kinda dating thing? She needs an S&amp;M kinda thing, sometimes, and I don\u2019t think either of us could manage the S part with the other. And she keeps insisting I should see Monica again, to do sunshine things with. Apparently, she\u2019s been checking up on Monica, and she checked out, so that\u2019s good, I guess? She explained more later, that she mostly just didn\u2019t want me to be standoffish with girls or anything and that sex isn\u2019t just a relationship type thing, you know?<br /> <br /> I wasn\u2019t thinking too much about that then though, especially when she stepped forward to hug me. I went for a kiss, before I let go, and man, that was an awesome response. She threw her arms around my neck and I wound up lifting her up as she wrapped her legs around my waist. And that\u2019s when Jacob walked in.<br /> <br /> He left after just a little bit of smirking and when we finally came up for air and realized we still had to get ready for a show or something silly like that, Calamity found him to let him know I was free. I\u2019ll be giving him driving lessons, since he got taken when he still just had his learners. It makes good sense really, having as many people as possible *able* to drive, if push came to shove, you know?<br /> <br /> The show went well, I think. I was still a little on Cloud 9 and all, so I\u2019m maybe not the best judge, you know, but people seemed pleased. I lingered around after cleanup and everything and made some sort of lame offer about Calamity coming over to my apartment to play video games or hang out or... something, cause I\u2019m 12 apparently. But thankfully she saw through it, and after she ran her finger down my chest and I picked her up to kiss her properly again, it seemed like way too much trouble to go all the way back to my apartment. so we stayed at the House. The guest bed was probably more comfortable anyway. Not that being with her wouldn\u2019t have been awesome no matter where we were. Cause it totally would have been. And was. Man, life is awesome.<br /> <br /> (Later)<br /> <br /> Well that was exciting. We had our adventure in the Hedge, you know, with Andromeda and all. Most of the day was spent prepping, since we didn\u2019t want to do any serious work until after sundown, so our Darklings would be at a disadvantage or anything. I worked on my flammenschwert, giving it an edge that was unsustainable, but that my glamour made last for the day at least. Ace and Calamity had a secret consultation that I guess was prep? Jacob spent the afternoon gathering all sorts of stuff for a hiking trip, extra water bottles, first aid stuff, stuff we might need if we got stranded for a bit even. He\u2019s big on being prepared for everything. It did wind up being good luck for us he did.<br /> <br /> I also let folks know about my new Dream Contract clause, where I can pull things from their dreams. Lori wasn\u2019t really cool with it, you know, and Jacob wasn\u2019t at first, but when I promised I\u2019d always ask first, he was ok with it. They all (except Lori) gave me a pillowcase thread even. Apparently none of them actually wear clothes to bed. I know Calamity doesn\u2019t. Well, at least she didn\u2019t last night. She\u2019d worn a night shirt before, at my place, but she gave me a pillowcase thread anyway. Insincere Marguerite was very confused at even the idea of wearing clothes to bed. Julia and I tried to explain, but I don\u2019t think it took very well.<br /> <br /> Julia stayed most of the day, even coming down for breakfast, so she\u2019s getting less nervous around us, which is good. She almost didn\u2019t though, cause she walked into the kitchen to hear Ace exclaim \u201cCause, you know, fuck aligators!\u201d Insincere Marguerite convinced her to stay though. I don\u2019t really remember why he said that - maybe something to do with his flaming trapeze plans? I dunno if that\u2019s going to work though, cause Lori said emphatically no fire, and the only fire-like Changeling in town is the Day Court lady, and Insincere Marguerite disapproves.<br /> <br /> Lori was more ok with Captain Jack\u2019s plan though, which is awesome, by the way. Totally a Bugs Bunny kinda thing. See, he\u2019s gonna sneak in and pretend to be part of the girls dancing on stage, dressed up and everything. I\u2019m gonna act like I notice something weird but can\u2019t figure it out until his wig slips, or something like that. Then I start chasing him around the place, over the stage and through the dressing room where we change clothes and everything. Lori thought it\u2019d be cool, and so did Calamity and Ace, so we\u2019re going to start planning that for serious.<br /> <br /> But first, we had a promise to keep. Andromeda met us right on time, in a shiny silvery spaceman outfit thing. Calamity set up a quick oath, that we\u2019d watch each others\u2019 backs and have a bit of a boost to our Hedge survival skills. If nothing else, it would have let us know if any trouble we came across was her trying to lead us to an ambush, you know? We did have a fight in there, but it wasn\u2019t to do with her, just some hobgoblin things.<br /> <br /> Andromeda knew where we were going, and Calamity and I did our dream contract thing and didn\u2019t find anything to serious going on, so everything was fairly straightforward. I still took up the rear, while Calamity took point. Lori was still real nervous, so she stayed in the middle of everyone. We ran across a couple of interesting things. The first one was a big hole in the ground, full of goblin fruits: some red water that was really good at healing you, but then you\u2019d be out for a good 8 hours sleep and also some lichen that would make it so you weren\u2019t feeling tired, like super coffee. Jacob and Lori dumped out their water bottles to get some of the red water. Insincere Marguerite wasn\u2019t willing to pour out her Perrier, but still we got about 5 doses of the water and 4 of the lichen.<br /> <br /> Andromeda knew about that, though that wasn\u2019t the goblin fruit she wanted. The next thing she didn\u2019t expect - a campsite that Jacob said had been abandoned a few weeks ago. Apparently it hadn\u2019t been there the last time Andromeda had been by there a couple of weeks ago. In the backpack left behind was a map leading from Arcadia to there, so it was probably a loyalist, or just a really lucky Changeling. As best Jacob could tell, someone with bird feet had set up camp then left and not come back. In the meantime, a group of 4: 2 pairs of dress shoes, 1 pair of high heels and 1 pair of webbed feet had shown up, ransacked the place and followed the bird feet.<br /> <br /> We decided to follow ourselves and found where the five had had a fight. The bird-dude definitely lost, though there wasn\u2019t any blood, just frost damage, icycle marks and bullet casings. The non-bird feet wandered around a bit, after the fight, but when they got back to the path, they just vanished. So, that\u2019s weird. I think we\u2019re going to be looking into what went on there once we have a moment.<br /> <br /> Lori wasn\u2019t too pleased by the delay, by the way, especially with the whole bird feet thing. Insincere Marguerite stuck close to her the whole rest of the way there and back, except during the fight, even though Lori was mostly better after the fight. I guess cause she didn\u2019t get hurt and was helpful, fixing up our wounds afterwards, you know?<br /> <br /> The fight was a little crazy, though fun, in its way, you know? We got attacked by some flying things called Vile Shrikes that are some weird bird human mix. We had warning and everything, so we all got armored up that could. Calamity started us out by almost killing one of them in one shot, then Ace slammed another to the ground. Jacob finished that one off after Insincere Marguerite and I teamed up on the one that actually hurt Calamity - she whammied it, making it slower to react and I cut it in half. Calamity finished off hers with her second shot and Andromeda showed she was a pretty awesome shot too and took down the other one attacking Calamity. In the heat of battle that irritated me some, as I was set to receive its dive, but I really can\u2019t complain with anyone working to keep her safe. I hadn\u2019t committed to that one in any way either, so I was well prepared for the last one that dived down and Jacob and I finished it off.<br /> <br /> Calamity had drawn a lot of attention with her first shot, so she was pretty beat up. I dropped my armor as soon as the last one was down to make sure she was alright. Lori brushed me aside almost immediately and started healing her and between that and Andromeda\u2019s first aid and one of the goblin fruits, she was as good as new. In the meantime, I finished off the Shrikes so they wouldn\u2019t have to bleed out slowly and so I wouldn\u2019t just be sitting there fretting. Jacob helped with that. Once Calamity was all set, Lori and Andromeda got me all fixed up too and we were all good - Ace had a few bruises, but Jacob and Insincere Marguerite got out of it without getting divebombed.<br /> <br /> The trip back was pretty uneventful, so we got out safe with all our loot. It was a pretty good haul too - the red water and the lichen, and 10 of the salubrious fruits that we\u2019d come for originally. Plus, no ambush! Score one for trusting people, I guess? Andromeda does seem nice, and did some good doctoring. She\u2019s still a little bit of a mystery, if nothing else because everyone else is so focussed on her. Maybe Calamity will have some insights in the morning.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> <b><u><b><u>May 6<sup>th</sup></u></b></u></b> Days without Stabbing: 0<br /> <br /> Fuck, where do I even begin. Holy fucking hell I am a goddamn hot mess. I'm sitting here in the dark writing this, I'll add it to the diary later. Andromeda is passed out but thankfully seems to be sleeping peacefully. Fuck, I haven't slipped as far as I just did since Belleview. Oh yeah, this relationship thing is going to work out just fine... Alright, I need to start at the beginning here. I haven't felt as fucking good as often as the past couple of days in... well ever. And that's the problem really. <br /> <br /> So, Sunday. Feels like more than just a day and half ago but I have been a busy little monster, oh yes indeed. I asked Gawain to teach me the contract of Stone and went to the garage, since that's his space in the house. We spent a couple of hours going over it while Lori took Ace shopping for nice clothes and Jacob headed over to the college. Insincere Marguerite was up in the catwalks with Julia. Mm... such a sweet little pet my Darkling sister's got herself there... I wonder if she's one to share her toys... <br /> <br /> Fuck. What in the everliving hell is wrong with me tonight? When did I steal the libido of a frat boy? Maybe it was when I swore to never drink like one again...<br /> <br /> But anyway, once Gawain had taught me how to boost my strength so I could use Max if I needed to it seemed like as good a time as any to have that talk with him. I knew exactly what I was going to say, what I was going to explain. I'd gone over the words in my head. I'd fortified my resolve. I was ready to settle this foolish crush and put him straight on the path to finding someone worthy of him. But the big man is stubborn. He just kept not listening to reason. Then... oh fuck he told me he loved me...<br /> <br /> He <i><i>loves</i></i> me.<br /> <br /> No one loves me. I don't even love me. <br /> <br /> It took the breath from me like a hammer to the gut. I was <i><i>not</i></i> ready to hear that. I mean, I knew he liked me. I knew he wanted more than just a quick (or even long and intense) fuck. But he said it and... oh dear Minerva he <i><i>meant</i></i> it. I know he did. He's a damn open book. It was written all of his face and I could see the look after it escaped. It wasn't that he'd chosen to say it to win me over, it had just happened because it was what was inside and he couldn't keep it in...<br /> <br /> I... I was weak. I was selfish. I <i><i>want</i></i> to be loved so badly. But I did at least manage to make it clear that I can't change. Not even for him. No matter if I wanted to. I told him I was still a monster, but he didn't care. And then I told him I could be <i><i>his</i></i> monster<i>. </i>Then Gawain picked me up and I wrapped my legs around his waist and clung to him and we <i><i>kissed</i></i> like something out of one of Katt's most romantic dreams.<br /> <br /> I'm not really sure exactly what it all means. I don't think either of us knows what we're doing but we are charging forward headlong into it. I just can't manage to think of myself as his girlfriend. It's just... wrong somehow. I don't fit in anything that normal. But I am his now and it is both amazing and terrifying.<br /> <br /> There was a show Sunday night of course, but I was somewhat on autopilot for most of it. I circulated the crowd as usual and made sure to speak to all of the changelings present. It occurs to me I need to look into some nicer clothes for that manager/hostess bit after seeing Dionisia in that off the shoulder slit up one side little black dress. I did sit and speak to her for a bit longer than the others. She's such a sweetheart; it really is no surprise everyone wants her. <br /> <br /> After the show, when things were winding down, Gawain approached me. I was nervous. I mean, I know how to fuck and after that kiss I think that was certainly on both our minds (I know it was on mine...) but I wasn't quite sure exactly how to say that to him you know? But as soon as he approached and started asking me if I wanted to come back to his apartment to hang out or play video games or whatever I could see he was having the same quandary. It was a bit adorable to see him like that but I could see he was feeling really unsure, like maybe he expected me to have changed my mind since the afternoon or he couldn't quite believe I'd really said that. So I smiled at him and ran my finger down that solid chest slowly as I purred out, \u201cIf that's what you <i><i>really</i></i> want to play with...\u201d<br /> <br /> Suffice to say, that took care of the uncertainty right quick. Next thing I knew, I was up in his arms and nuzzling into his chest as he carried me to the guest bedroom. I won't lie, I love how it feels when he picks me up like it's nothing and holds me in those strong metal arms. As I said, I know how to fuck and I've had my share of sex, but what happened wasn't either of those things. He made love to me. It was amazing and I ended up curled up in his arms feeling what I can only describe as blissfully. I was worried that it would wake memories when he gathered me close. He was so careful as he did it, clearly recalling what I had said about that and I don't know if it was that, or the way I trust him, or maybe just how so very solid he is but the ghosts of my past stayed in the past for once. I slept like that, clinging to him like a life raft at sea. <br /> <br /> We went down to breakfast more or less like any other day, though I do think there were a few more glances back and forth but for the most part it was the easy comfortably way it had been once more and I really liked that. Ace was looking quite striking in his new suit, having returned from his early morning meeting with Lucian Torrez (Thug, Lawyer, and morning person? What does the man do in his spare time, kick puppies and eat babies?) I have to say, Ace did look good in the formal ware and I told him so, but I like him better in his normal look. Apparently he's moved from piranha to flaming trapeze acts, or barring a flaming trapeze a flaming trapeze artist but so far the only fiery changeling we know of is the Day Courtier who came to opening night and she does not seem theatrically inclined. Insincere Marguerite's girl Julia joined us for breakfast. She's shy and demure. Insincere Marguerite was close, touching and even licking her pretty little pet and while Julia seemed a little embarrassed perhaps that they weren't alone she clearly didn't object to being claimed. I'm not sure the others noticed but I know that look, and oh fuck it did things to me. Still warm from the night before with a man that loves me and I couldn't help but wonder what kind of noises she'd make while I ran my razor-tipped fingers along her perfect skin. I couldn't keep from trying to imagine the look in her eyes as she waited for when, not if, I was going to cut her and give her Mistress a true taste of her... <br /> <br /> I was pulled away from my dark fantasies by Ace, who wanted to speak to me 'in his office'. Apparently his meeting with Lucian had (surprise surprise) concerned a certain little grey alien girl. He was being subtle so it took me a minute to realize that he was concerned that I might have a problem dealing with her seeing as we'd been intimate and all. I laughed and assured him that while we'd fucked I was not attached to Andromeda. If the girl proves to be a loyalist, then I will personally carve her heart out, simple as that. (And yeah, part of me really wouldn't mind having the excuse...) At any rate, it seems that the Summer Court did intercept a message she sent back to inform her Keeper when she first arrived but she hasn't had any further contact (that they can prove). So, they do have more than just Hailey's word but it's not exactly damnable proof. And that was what they wanted. It was suggested that she might not try anything with all of us being present so maybe only Ace and I should go into the Hedge with her. I countered that it might be suspicious to change things up at the last minute and that we should stick to the plan, which included being ready for anything. He agreed that that made sense but now I know there is at least some evidence against her. <br /> <br /> The afternoon was spent in preparation. I made sure everything was straight with the books and that the regular staff wasn't going to burn the place down without me or the others being there. We didn't leave until almost showtime, so everyone had time to make sure things were squared in their area before we packed into Gawain's van and drove to Glamour Springs. Andromeda met us as planned, wearing a rather stereotypical silver shiny space-girl outfit and a much less fanciful pistol on her hip. I had Sam and Max both and Ace was once again borrowing the Remington. Jacob had a pack with some basic supplies just in case we were gone more than just a couple of hours or something unexpected came up. Gawain had his two handed sword. I had taken a few minutes to draw Lorelei aside. I knew she was doing this out of loyalty to us more than any desire to be even halfway to Arcadia again. I made sure she knew that I expected her to keep her head down and stay out of trouble if things got dangerous. I pointed out that the rest of us were all good at taking things apart but only she had the means to put one of us back together and that was just as important. And as before, Insincere Marguerite stayed close to her.<br /> <br /> My heart picked up as we entered the Hedge. Gawain checked before and I after but neither of us sensed anything unexpected. We moved cautiously up a gradual incline through the forested terrain. Andromeda told us that at the top you could see the lights from Hollywood's Hedge. Along the way, we came across a cave that held some healing waters and stimulant lichen. It wasn't what Andromeda was seeking, but she waited while we send Insincere Marguerite down with the (now) empty water bottles and a pack to gather them. I kept a sharp eye on the treeline but nothing took that opportunity to attack us. <br /> <br /> Next we found a campsite. It was old but hadn't been there the last time Andromeda came through this area, so a couple of weeks. The tent and pack were Arcadian and had been ransacked already. The only thing left was a map from Arcadia to the Malibu area. Jacob was all over the tracks, and, in fact, proved to be quite a skillful outdoorsman. There were two sets, a single traveler with bird feet, the owner of the tent it seemed, and a foursome that came afterward. The four were two pairs of dress shoes, one set of high heels and one pair of webbed feet. They sacked the camp and then followed the first tracks. We debated a bit, but looking into what seemed to be a loyalist or bounty hunter seemed too important to ignore. Besides which, as old as the tracks were there was little chance we'd run across any of the people involved. And what we found was a fight scene. The second group had overtaken the bird man and attacked with powerful ice magic and at least one sidearm. There was no sign of blood or a body (or a shallow grave) so they took whatever was left with them and their tracks vanished shortly thereafter. Lori was a little uncomfortable during the investigation, no doubt due to the possibility that it might well have been her Empress' Hunting Hawk. Unfortunately, we don't know who exactly found the interloper or what they did with him. Or her, it might be some other random bird person with no connection to our own songbird. Sure, it's not likely but it could be the case. We won't know until we look deeper into what happened and who was involved and get some answers. But there wasn't anything more to be gained right then and there so we headed back to the task at hand.<br /> <br /> After that detour, we did reach the top of the hill and the promised view. It was quite spectacular. From there we got to the salubrious fruits Andromeda was after and collected quite a few of them. As we started back, the Vileshrikes attacked.<br /> <br /> We caught sight of them in the distance and had a moment to prepare. Insincere Marguerite disappeared into the shadows. Jacob and Gawain called up their respective elemental armors (I need to learn that fucking trick from Gawain sometime). Ace used his beast magic to thicken his own scales into armor while Lori did that trick where she becomes too beautiful to attack. (And let me just say, I really, <i>really</i> don't mind her being a non combatant when she uses that contract...) Despite my own new contract, I opted to draw and ready Sam. The sawed-off barely has more reach than my razorhand. I figured these bastards where going to circle and swoop in on us so I'd need the colt's range. Turns out I was right. The fuckers were part human, part bird and all ugly. They were filthy and mismatched, no two being quite the same mix of parts. I picked one at random and cracked off a shot while the others braced for their dives. I nailed it pretty squarely but failed to kill it outright. <br /> <br /> Ace hammered the first one that got near him, sending it sprawling. Jacob pounced on it and made sure it never got back up. I danced aside from the first swipe but my shot had drawn the bulk of the fucking harpies wrath down on my pretty little head. I managed to give all of the ones that got near a swipe with my off hand but I still took a couple of decent nicks. Ace took a hit as well but it didn't get through his extra scaly hide. Gawain was the only other one injured, taking a decent scratch as well. Jacob managed to stay mobile and Insincere Marguerite was unseen except when she emerged to lay the curse of darkness on one and set it up for Gawain to cut it in fucking half. I finished off the one I wounded with a second shot. Andromeda proved to be an effective shot as well. It was a good fight and we won it handily. I have no doubt Luna would have had something to say (okay, a<i><i> lot</i> </i>to say) about how much fire I drew standing in the open like that but sometimes a girl's just gotta go toe to toe with a flock of monstrous bird things, right? <br /> <br /> At any rate, Lori was quick to shoo Gawain away from me and lay the sweet Spring magic on my wounds. Then Andromeda took over and with one of the fruits to round out things I was good to go. They also took care of Gawain's wound but Ace was just bruised. While they were tending to me, Gawain and Jacob made sure the beasties were all properly dead, good lads that they are. The remainder of the trip back was uneventful and once we were at Glamour Springs again I brought up Andromeda's promise to show me her collection of toys sometime. She seemed quite agreeable and so I waved goodnight to the motley and left with her instead. <br /> <br /> So... Yet again the best laid plans of mice and Calamity fell completely fucking apart. I mean, yeah there wasn't any pretense about what we were going to be doing but I'd intended to keep it casual. Have our fun and keep her from getting suspicious, set things up for a smaller outing or something to see if she's going to try something, and maybe look about for any conspicuous Arcadian magical artifact tables. Well... I did get around to searching for this table that everyone's after and I did find where there had been a large table of unusual shape that was removed with difficulty a while ago. So I know it was here but has since been moved. That counts for something I guess. <br /> <br /> As to the rest... Well, I had the run of her house because by the time she passed out I had put the little joytoy through her paces and then some. Oh dear lord that girl suffers beautifully... I hadn't meant to take things that far but once we were alone and started to play I just couldn't control myself. I wasn't sure before we started if she even remembered some of the more intense moments from our previous night together and some of the things she'd said and done. Well, she sure as fuck did and having found that submissive streak and coaxed it out then meant she was ready, willing, and downright eager to slip back into it again. I think the poor thing is lonely and desperate for someone's attentions and for better or (I fear) worse what she's found in me is a big bad wolf.<br /> <br /> Well, once the fun and games began, I found that she has even more wonderful toys than she'd told me about at Beltane. She's built machines that fuck in ways no person could hope to keep up with and she can take them quite expertly but she clearly hasn't had very much experience with flesh and blood lovers. I was not in any way gentle as I changed this and for quite a good portion of the night it seemed that no matter how roughly I used her she was greedy for more. Gods know I was... Right up until I touched her with the sharp edges of my razored hands and sent her into hysterics. It was a light touch, almost feathery, just a tease really. There is a thrill that it brings to most, a hint of fear and excitement to feel a blade against their skin even if so few are prepared to actually bleed for me... I thought that maybe, as deeply submissive as she is, that she might just be one of them. And even if not the tease is a wicked little game. But it was no game for her. She jerked hard and began to thrash, nearly cutting herself on my hand in her panic. It was such a primal reaction that, for a moment, I could only drink it in. For a moment, I wanted nothing so much as to continue. To coax more of that pure terror from her. To shatter and ravage her. And I think, in that moment, she may have caught a glimpse of the monster I am inside. But I did not harm her. I banished the glass from my hands and lifted them for her to see before gathering her slowly and carefully and gently into my embrace. I stroked her hair softly and I rocked her as she trembled and slowly came back to herself. After a time, she grew calm enough and as she clung to me she spoke, softly and quietly. She told me about when she was taken, when she was changed. It was surgical. On the Mothership, she was kept on an operating table as she was cut and remade with sharp blades and heartless efficiency. I listened as I held her close and comforted her until she grew quiet and slipped into an exhausted sleep. <br /> <br /> She looks so tiny and fragile sleeping there now. I can see my mark upon her skin, right at the base of her neck where my toothy kiss bruised her smooth flesh before I made her scream in fear rather than pleasure. I brushed her hair away from it so I could see it clearly and as I reach to pet her I find my gaze drawn to it. It pulls at my fingers, the urge to brush them over it and feel the imprint my teeth made earlier. When I growled against that tender spot I'd made I called her mine. In the heat of the moment, I was hungry to claim her, to take everything she would give but what about when she wakes? If she was just some human I'd be gone already. But she's not. She's a changeling. She's a member of Lorelei's court. What I cannot believe is that she's a loyalist. Whatever she's involved in, she is a pawn, a lost lamb surrounded by wolves. I cannot help but look upon that promise written in her flesh and think that maybe what she needs <i>is</i> a big bad wolf after all. <br /> <br /> What is Gawain going to say when I tell him? How do I explain this desire to protect her without him wondering if I have feelings for her? And what about Ace? I know he's a man of honor at heart but what I am thinking would put us at odds with his court. And the others? Master Darke and Lucian Torrez are not to be trifled with. Defending this girl would make enemies of them. And what if there are actually Gentry behind this all? How can I bring so much risk upon them and for one girl? <br /> <br /> One girl who is alone and helpless, just like Katt was. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers </b><br /> <br /> My dark side is growing stronger. I would say I only am a dark side, being a Darkling, but this is not a humorous thing. Probably.<br /> <br /> After breakfast I called Julia to tell her about my past. Having told the Motley it seemed like I would be able to tell her as well. But she was so eager to see me. I hesitated on it. Instead I told her to bring a few personal items she could leave here when she stays over, instead of telling her to stay away. She was quickly over in person. I of course resolved to explain the truth while waiting for her to arrive, but I of course didn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> I lurked about her all day, kept her close. Kept her scent nearby. Her taste in tongue\u2019s reach. She sketched Lorelei, and I remained near to tease her and try to generally be her muse. Afterwards we retreated to the catwalks. She remained up there with I through the show. And spent the night. Which was nice, but did nothing to make her any less my possession.<br /> <br /> I sent her away Monday, but only after she spent most of the day close by. I\u2026was less myself. I told her she was mine several times. She seemed pleased by this, she did not understand, and I did not want her to. I tasted her skin a few times. She was less sanguine about having her face licked in front of people. Probably. I sent her away when we went into the Hedge, but not before. She remained about and nearby all day. She has given in as surely as I have.<br /> <br /> This is bad, as I am yielding to my baser self. The creeping, hungry little grub. The urge to collect and keep her is strong, and I am giving in. I may have to go out of communication or something. I am concerned about her, certainly, but also myself\u2026I do not want her to turn I into something bad. I must keep her away, where I cannot grab or touch or smell her. Maybe I should talk to someone in the Motley. I am unsure who. And who would I tell to keep my girlfriend away from I, someone I looked forward to resenting? Probably.<br /> <br /> Julia would make the perfect pet though. Beautiful, dark humored, artistically talented (Artists get me so hot), pliable without being too submissive. And she loves my accent. Yes, yes. She would make such a good\u2026no\u2026I will not do this. I will not keep her to touch and smell and pet. I must shove her from my mind, with all the dark corners and warm passages it holds. Things best left never to stir lurk there, my mind. Yes.<br /> <br /> Other things\u2026the time in the Hedge went well. Maybe. We gathered some fruit and peculiar water. I did not wish to pour out my water (with bubbles) to bring more. I like water, especially with bubbles. The others do not drink water with bubbles. They are fools. Probably. We fought Vileshrikes. We proved effective, though Calamity was injured. The glass is ever symbolic. Notable was Gawain fought like a berserker when she was hurt. I think he is half Ogre. That he could be goaded into such behavior by Calamity being injured a side of myself found illuminating. Possibly. But we made it, and Andromeda did not try to take us away to the Gentry. Probably.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve not gotten as much work done with the <i><i>Brotherswing</i></i> number as Julia has distracted me.<br /> <br /> Speaking of distractions, I\u2019ve been distracting myself flirting with Lori, trying to retreat from Julia a bit. I hope this does not lead to anything bad. Maybe. My intentions in keeping close to her in the Hedge to help her keep her nerve were honorable. Mostly. It\u2019s a fun distraction, regardless. Yes.<br /> <br /> But I still wonder what she tastes like.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>End Session VII</i><br /> <br /> Man these people are messed up<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite failed a Resolve + Composure roll and had to make a Clarity check (with an extra die) for brainwashing Julia further. She did pass the Clarity check. So far, she is the one having to do all the Morality checks, but she is one of the two PCs with 7 (Gawain is the other).<br /> <br /> Vileshrikes are in <b><b>Autumn Nightmares</b></b>. The various fruits and oddements were of a homespun variety.<br /> <br /> Calamity had changed from <b><b>Armory</b></b>\u2019s Spetsnaz Knife Fighting to the Light Weapons style in GMC. The Flurry ability was quite effective. Gawain was still using his two handler style from <b><b>Amory Reloaded</b></b> with the extra action ability removed. His player is rather enamored of the style. Ace switched to Street Fighting and did well enough. We got the tilt slightly wrong for knocking down a Vileshrike, but lesson learned. We also had Dodge wrong, but no one attacked Lorelei (who was the one dodging) so it did not come up.<br /> <br /> This session went better than last. A lot of good Rping with Gawain and Calamity. I was simultaneously running the meeting between Ace and Lucian so I missed some of it. It\u2019s also worth noting Insincere Marguerite\u2019s journal is a bit less sexual than it appears\u2026she was licking people during the session. She the character, not she the player. That would be weird.<br /> <br /> OK I think that covers it. Comments and Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T04:41:01-07:00","id":190136,"title":"","content":"When I started reading Gawain's part I had this image in my head of one of the people from the motley (Not sure who) seeing Gawain and Calamity starting to have their emotional talk, stopping to watch and then another motley mate seeing him/her watching. The second one then asks the first one if they should be watching. The first one says &quot;Probably not&quot; and then offers the second one popcorn. The second looks away, grabs the popcorn, and then starts watching as well. Things fade to and out from black as appropriate much to the watchers confusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T12:52:16-07:00","id":190636,"title":"","content":"LOL. Jacob would probably be one. Insincere Marguerite they would never see. Heh.<br /> <br /> <br /> Last night went well, despite being a foursome. Some light was shed on the Andromeda storyline, and the Darklings had a heart to heart about boys. Look forward to sharing those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T18:56:50-07:00","id":202539,"title":"","content":"OK, doing things slightly different this time. Lorelei and Jacob\u2019s journals cover both sessions 7 and 8, but their descriptions of events in session 8 just cover what they were up to during the session (both players had to miss) so don\u2019t cover any events as rolepayed in the session. So I am putting those first, so the journals can flow from session 7 to 8 sicne we basically had three session 7 journals last time these will cover the remainder (well, except Ace, whose player does not really journal). Then Gawain, Calamity, and Insincere Marguerite cover events of session 8 as played at the table. Alright? Alright!<br /> <br /> <i>Session VIII (with Session VII Overflow) </i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> We went into the Hedge last night. It was terrifying and exhilarating and magical and overwhelming and\u2026 well, all sorts of things. And I have to admit, as frightened as I was to go in there, I think it was good for me. I feel a lot better about this motley \u2013 and my role within it \u2013 now that I\u2019ve survived a battle without being knocked unconscious. And the nigh-magical experience that followed helped as well, of course.<br /> <br /> Ace came to me on Sunday afternoon and confessed that he had a problem\u2026 he was supposed to meet with some high muckety-muck of the Summer Court the next morning, and he needed something formal to wear. Ordinarily I think he\u2019d just wear his usual street clothes no matter how important his contact was, but this meeting was supposed to take place in an upscale office building in Malibu, and he didn\u2019t want to get thrown out by security before he even met the Grand Poobah.<br /> <br /> We hit a few nice shops and picked up a small array of outfits that looked good on him, and then headed home. I tried to be conscious of this era\u2019s incredibly odd sense of what constitutes a \u201cfashionable\u201d look, and let me tell you, it wasn\u2019t easy. Most of the suits we looked at were black or charcoal grey, with nary a warm earth-tone in sight. Stiff white shirts. Black shoes and belt. It was <u>boring</u>. The only splash of color men seem to be allowed in their formalwear is on their ties\u2026 we got a red one with little blue diamonds on it and a green one with sedate golden stripes. I tried to push for the paisley, but Ace balked for some reason.<br /> <br /> The show Sunday night went okay, though it was nothing spectacular. I repeated a couple of numbers I\u2019d done before, and added my own take on \u201cElusive Butterfly\u201d to the mix. I think it went pretty well, though I\u2019m not sure the tone of that song really suits our venue, so I might retire that number from the regular rotation.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t socialize much after the show. Oh, I made the rounds as usual, chatting with the mundanes and paying my respects to the local changelings, but I didn\u2019t linger too long after the final curtain. I guess the novelty of the club is starting to wear off, because there weren\u2019t as many Lost in attendance as usual (though we still played to a packed house overall). D wasn\u2019t there. I\u2019ve spent rather more time than I should have trying to convince myself that I just noticed that detail in passing, rather than looking for her specifically.<br /> <br /> Shortly after I got up the next morning, Ace returned from his meeting with the Summer Court so-and-so. They\u2019re utterly convinced that Andromeda is a loyalist, largely based on the word of Hailey, the other alien girl in the area. Calamity is just as convinced that there\u2019s no true malice in Andromeda, and the rest of us don\u2019t know what to believe. We decided not to change our plans for that evening, since doing so might have alerted Andromeda to our suspicions if she <u>was</u> a loyalist. For the same reason, we decided against setting a trap for her using ourselves as bait. Apparently the Summer Court had recommended against all of us accompanying Andromeda into the Hedge, as they thought such a large group might make her gun-shy about revealing her true colors.<br /> <br /> So we met Andromeda as planned, and she led us into the Hedge. Things went fairly well for a while. We found a pool of red-tinged water that had the power to heal the wounds of anyone who drank it, but would also put them to sleep for eight hours. We emptied a few liter bottles of water we\u2019d brought along and filled them up with the red stuff. You never know when something like that will come in handy, after all.<br /> <br /> We came across an old campsite shortly thereafter. Jacob spent some time studying the site, and came to a few conclusions about its occupants. I don\u2019t claim to understand \u2013 or even remember \u2013 everything he said about what went down there, in part because I began to get really terrified at that point. One of the camp\u2019s occupants had talon-tipped bird feet. I never saw Hunting Hawk\u2019s feet directly; he always had boots on when he attended Her Majesty. But I couldn\u2019t shake the feeling that he had been there, and that he had been looking for me.<br /> <br /> Apparently there were rather a <u>lot</u> of us bird-people in that part of the Hedge. As we followed a trail from the remains of the camp, we were attacked by a group of foul creatures called Vileshrikes. Like me, they were part bird and part human, but their parts were mixed in odd and unpleasant ways, and no two were alike. There were five of them, and they used their wings to their best advantage, striking at our group from above and darting away before we could retaliate.<br /> <br /> Yeah, they could actually fly. Lucky bastards. I can\u2019t help wondering if I would have turned into something like that if I\u2019d remained in Arcadia instead of making my escape.<br /> <br /> I won\u2019t go into the gory details of the fight, but suffice to say my friends made short work of those creatures. Even Andromeda did her part, firing her gun to good effect. I poured glamour into my appearance in an attempt to make myself more intimidating. I think it worked, as I was never attacked directly.<br /> <br /> My friends were not so lucky. Gawain and Calamity were both pretty badly hurt in the fracas. I took each of them aside in turn and invoked the Contract of Eternal Spring to heal their wounds. I couldn\u2019t quite erase <u>all</u> of the damage they\u2019d suffered, but it was clear enough afterward that they\u2019d both improved significantly.<br /> <br /> I can\u2019t tell you how good it feels to have been able to contribute to this little outing in a tangible and positive way. My friends know that I\u2019m no good at the fighting stuff, and in all honesty I don\u2019t really <u>want</u> to be. But they\u2019re all doing so much to keep me safe\u2026 it\u2019s just nice to know that there\u2019s something I can do in return when they really need me. I\u2019m definitely going to take some first aid classes to improve my caregiving techniques, too.<br /> <br /> Things went pretty well after that incident, actually. Andromeda was able to find a large cache of the goblin fruit she was looking for, and we loaded up all our packs and made our way quickly out of the Hedge. These fruits, incidentally, are also of the healing sort, but as far as we can tell they don\u2019t come with any strings attached\u2026 eating one just heals your wounds with no side effects. Useful stuff to have around.<br /> <br /> I was still kind of high on adrenaline when we got home, so after I grabbed a quick shower, I stayed up watching some crappy romantic comedy on TV. I was a little surprised when there was a soft knock at my door a couple of hours later, and even more surprised to find Jacob there when I answered the knock.<br /> <br /> \u201cI was wondering,\u201d he said in his slight accent, \u201cis there something you truly enjoy doing?\u201d<br /> <br /> I think I blinked four or five times at that sudden question, then asked for clarification. I mean, I love to sing, of course\u2026 that\u2019s the obvious answer. But I had the feeling that he was asking for something else\u2026 something I don\u2019t do for a living these days.<br /> <br /> \u201cI am just trying to get to know you all,\u201d he explained softly. \u201cI want to know what makes you happy\u2026 what makes you forget your troubles.\u201d<br /> <br /> I thought about it for another couple of minutes, but there was really only one possible answer. My mind kept drifting back to the first time I tried it\u2026 the lights, the colors, the sounds. I took to it almost immediately, and Mom said I was a natural. It\u2019s one of the only memories I have of her. Dad tried to take me a few times after she died \u2013 on my birthdays, mostly \u2013 but it seemed to remind him of her, and he always looked so sad. But when I was with my friends, particularly Missy and Jane\u2026<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s stupid,\u201d I said, not looking him in the eye. \u201cI don\u2019t even know if people still do it anymore. God knows that most of the things I used to enjoy have gone the way of the dodo\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cPlease,\u201d he said, \u201ctell me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSkating,\u201d I replied. \u201cRoller skating, I mean. In a real skating rink, with a waxed wooden floor, and colored lights, and music, and a mirror ball hanging from the ceiling.\u201d I turned away. \u201cGod, that makes me sound like such a <u>kid</u>\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay,\u201d he said, smiling kindly. \u201cMeet me in the garage at ten o\u2019clock tomorrow morning. I will see what I can do.\u201d And he walked back to his room.<br /> <br /> Intrigued, I set my alarm, stripped down, and went to bed. I didn\u2019t feel much like getting up the next morning when the alarm went off, but I somehow managed to yawn my way through a shower and get a mug of coffee in me before Jacob\u2019s deadline hit. Knowing something of what he had in mind, I put on a tight pair of jeans and a t-shirt and walked into the garage to find him standing next to my \u2018vette and grinning.<br /> <br /> \u201cI found a place,\u201d he said, waving a sheet of paper at me. \u201cI think it will do.\u201d<br /> <br /> The place he found was about fifteen miles inland in Northridge, almost all the way to Van Nuys. I don\u2019t know how he found it (when I asked him, he told me that he used a service called \u201cGoogly Maps,\u201d or something like that), but I\u2019m glad he did. Skateland is <u>exactly</u> the sort of roller rink I remember from my childhood\u2026 which is hardly surprising, as its sign proudly proclaims that it has \u201cbeen an icon of Northridge for over 50 years.\u201d<br /> <br /> They had a lot of diversions. A video arcade, something called a \u201claser maze,\u201d food, drinks, giant televisions\u2026 but Jacob and I went straight to the counter to rent our skates, and then out onto the floor. It took Jacob a few minutes to find his feet, but he has good instincts and good balance, and he was zipping around like a champion in no time.<br /> <br /> As for me\u2026 it was like I\u2019d never been away. My wings are actually a huge help in maintaining my balance, and I found that I could perform feats I\u2019d never have even attempted before I was taken. Jumps, spins, tight turns, speed-skating backwards\u2026 I tried it all, and fell a lot less often than I would have expected. Even on the one or two occasions when I <u>did</u> lose my balance, I popped up again laughing and grinning like a loon.<br /> <br /> And then it started. The house lights went down, the colored spots shone on the mirror balls, and the opening strains of \u201cNight Fever\u201d by the Bee Gees began to thrum. It\u2019s never been my favorite song\u2026 but it was familiar, and in those surroundings, it felt like I was <u>really</u> coming home for the first time. I started to dance as I skated.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t notice the spot on me until the song ended. There was actually some applause, which was gratifying. I thought about doing a little impromptu advertising for the Dream House then\u2026 but as the median age of the patrons seemed to be around twelve, I quickly reconsidered.<br /> <br /> We skated our way through a few more songs, and I even got Jacob to dance with me once or twice. He was a little awkward, but not bad for a beginner. We were skating and twirling and laughing and singing and\u2026 and the only thing that existed for me today was <u>fun</u>. I can\u2019t remember the last time I felt that. I don\u2019t know if I <u>ever</u> have.<br /> <br /> But it got late eventually, and we had to say our farewells to the Northridge Skateland. Believe it or not, it was actually getting dark when we left; we\u2019d been there for nearly eight hours. I know people say that time flies when you\u2019re having fun, but I could have sworn it hadn\u2019t been <u>that</u> long.<br /> <br /> I drove us back to the Dream House in comfortable silence, with the top down. As we walked back into the house, Jacob spoke.<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you for sharing this with me,\u201d he said quietly. \u201cIt was a lot of fun.\u201d<br /> <br /> I stopped, tried desperately to keep the tears out of my eyes, and pulled him into a hug. I kissed him once on the cheek, and gave him a fervent \u201cthank you.\u201d I hope he can tell how much today meant to me. For one whole day I wasn\u2019t thinking about everything that I\u2019ve lost, or everything that was done to me. And that\u2019s more valuable than I can possibly express.<br /> <br /> The others are downstairs, but I think I\u2019ll just relax in my room for a bit. Or maybe I\u2019ll call D. I wonder if she likes to skate\u2026<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Where to start? It has been a very eventful couple of days. Sunday I rode over to Santa Monica college to put up posters for the show and to look into first aid classes that are open to the community for Lorelei. She mentioned before that knowing more about first aid would help with the use of her healing contract. I figured I could look for classes for Lorelei and do a little advertising at the same time. I will admit that a part of me was hoping that I would run into Elena while I was there. It was not really likely, but I can hope right? Man\u2026that makes me sound like a stalker. It\u2019s a good thing no one here can read Cyrillic. Actually, sounding like a stalker would be the least of my troubles if my motley-mates could read Cyrillic. They probably wouldn\u2019t even get to this entry before lynching me for any or all of my previous admissions.<br /> <br /> Anyhoo\u2026Ace and Lorelei went shopping this morning for some nice clothes for our resident beast aspected. Apparently Ace had a meeting with Lucien Torres (Summer Court\u2019s Mr. Plausible Deniability), and he wanted to look good. They came back with some nice stuff and Ace went off to his meeting. I will admit to being really curious what they talked about. I have a feeling that at least part of it was about Andromeda and our upcoming trip to the hedge with her. I know that probably wasn\u2019t everything they talked about, but Ace did not tell us much when he returned. All this talk of possible Loyalists in our midst makes me hope that the Summer Court\u2019s \u201cbehind-the-scenes man\u201d doesn\u2019t have anything on me. Having to run would make me break at least two pledges and that would not be good. Not just because of the backlash either. I honestly don\u2019t want to hurt the others. They could get into trouble for harboring me or decide that my silence regarding my past is betrayal enough and come after me themselves\u2026or both.<br /> <br /> Yeah\u2026gotta stop thinking down such dark paths. On the more positive side of things Calamity asked Gawain to teach her Contracts of Stone, which he did. I think they also talked some things out and cleared up some of the tension between them. I had a favor that I wanted to ask Gawain, but I figured they\u2019d need some time so I waited. I walked in after a good while to find Gawain holding Calamity up in an embrace, and the diminutive Darkling had her legs wrapped around his waist. All I could think at that moment was, \u201cFinally!\u201d I made my apologies then backed out closing the door. Then I couldn\u2019t help myself and opened the door a moment later and took a picture of them with my phone. They were adorably flustered. Well, as outwardly flustered as that pair gets. It was still cute. I\u2019ll have to remember to send that picture to them later.<br /> <br /> After that I really did excuse myself and stepped out. A little later Calamity came out and found me and let me know that Gawain was free. I\u2019ll admit that I was a bit embarrassed by my favor, but figured Gawain wouldn\u2019t tease me too bad about it. I asked him if he could teach me how to drive. I had my learner\u2019s permit before I was taken but hadn\u2019t yet taken my driver\u2019s test. My parents were going to take Elena and I do take the test after we got home from the camping trip. Then I spent twenty some odd years in the Lady\u2019s realm, and I\u2019ve pretty much forgotten most of what I knew from before. I remember going to school, but I don\u2019t really remember what I learned. It\u2019s all fragments, bits and pieces floating around in my head like a thawing pond in Spring. That\u2019s true for pretty much everything I learned in school, not just the driving lessons. So now I just have my bike, but thought that it might be a good thing to know how to drive. Gawain was understanding, not that I really expected him to be otherwise, and he said he\u2019d be happy to teach me. Now I just have to make sure I don\u2019t dent his van while practicing.<br /> <br /> So\u2026Julia came by today and hung out with Insincere Marguerite. Things seemed to be progressing steadily in their relationship. They\u2019re spending a good bit of time together. I think something was said about Julia leaving some of her stuff in the bathroom too. I guess my only real concern is not so much that someone else will be staying at the house on occasion, but Insincere Marguerite\u2019s overly tactile reactions to Julia\u2019s presence. Our resident urban explorer did tell us that she had stolen and kept other Changelings while living in Arcadia. I wonder if she realizes how possessive her actions seem? I\u2019ll give her a bit. If she continues to be so \u201ctouchy-feely\u201d over the next few days I\u2019ll mention something. I know how hard it is not to fall back on old habits. I find myself assessing other Changelings when I meet them as to whether or not they\u2019d be a threat to me, and what tactics I\u2019d have to use to subdue them and get them back to The Lady\u2019s realm. Goddess knows I wouldn\u2019t do it, but sometimes I find my mind going in that direction. It just became so ingrained after so many years that it\u2019s hard to not think that way now. I guess that\u2019s why part of me hasn\u2019t thought that Andromeda would be all that much of a threat. Not by herself anyway. She\u2019s a little thing, and unless she\u2019s got some talent she keeps hidden I don\u2019t see her as a danger to me personally. That said, I never underestimate the power of forward thinking. Diane after all is not a threat by herself, but add in an Ogre and a couple other guys laying in wait and the odds definitely skew out of my favor.<br /> <br /> That whole line of thinking reminded me of Calamity\u2019s lessons with Gawain\u2019s. I am a little excited and scared about her learning the Contracts of Stone. On the one hand, woe be to our enemies. On the other hand, woe be to me if she decides my past activities are punishable by fist. Her fist. Or Gawain\u2019s fist. That hurts.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Okay, so the day of the \u201cgreat Goblin fruit adventure\u201d arrived. Most of us packed bags to take with us. Well, mainly me and Calamity. I packed an assortment of granola and snack bars, bottles of water and some containers to put Goblin fruit in. Everyone, well most everyone, else brought weapons, but only a handful of us brought anything else. I guess years of hiking and camping with my family taught me a few things. Well, that and those lessons were reinforced while working for The Lady. I always packed supplies when venturing into \u201cThe world.\u201d I mean, I stole plenty of stuff and picked pockets to pay for meals out, but I also brought a lot of my own supplies in case I had to avoid people. The irony is not lost on me. The last time I packed a bag like this was my last trip in The Lady\u2019s service to \u201cThe world\u201d to retrieve Diane. Now I\u2019m packing the same kinds of things for trips into the Hedge. I\u2019m just playing it off as a lot of camping trips with my family though. Best to just leave the rest unsaid for now. I guess this whole \u201cpossible Loyalist\u201d thing with Andromeda has been dredging up memories. Actually, I don\u2019t think that\u2019s true. Maybe that\u2019s the excuse I want to use. Those memories are just surfacing on their own. Best to keep busy. Put up flyers at the college. Look for classes for Lorelei. Inventory the bar. Activities with my motley-mates. Just keep busy.<br /> <br /> So\u2026the hedge was interesting. Before we went in Calamity suggested a contract to keep us a bit safer and help with our woodland skills. And since Calamity can also detect when someone has broken a vow, she would know if Andromeda was responsible for any misfortune that might befall us. Handy skill that. Anyway, we found a spring that had some healing water and some lichen that had stimulant qualities. I emptied out most of the water bottles I\u2019d brought to collect some of the red water. It pays off to be prepared for a variety of eventualities. Shortly after gathering that stuff we came across a clearing with a tent. I motioned for the others to stay back so I could check out the site and look for tracks. I found human sized bird tracks around the site. My guess is the camper last came to the site two or three weeks ago. Then I found two sets of dress shoe tracks, one high heeled set and one webbed set. This group came across the camper and followed him into the woods. I also found a backpack in the tent with a map leading from someplace in Arcadia to the gate we came through. I suggested that we follow the tracks and see if we could learn anything else. What I found interesting is that whatever else had been in the pack was taken out, whether by the owner or the group of four, I don\u2019t know. The fact that the map was left behind was kind of telling. It kind of implies that it wasn\u2019t going to be important anymore. Yeah, I didn\u2019t have high hopes for the guy (or gal) the group was tracking.<br /> <br /> We tracked the other party to a small clearing where we found evidence of a fight involving ice/frost powers and some bullet casings. It wasn\u2019t hard to guess that a winter-aspected changeling or changelings was involved. Probably someone(s) in the Winter court. I will have to keep an eye out once we get back to \u201cthe world\u201d to see who has shoes/feet to match the tracks that I found. The bird footed individual probably didn\u2019t survive the encounter, as his tracks did not lead away from the clearing, but the others did. The tracks unfortunately disappeared shortly after leaving the clearing making it apparent that someone in the group started to actively hide their tracks after that. I didn\u2019t see any blood on the ground, so if the bird-footed guy was killed they used bludgeoning attacks, or were good about not leaving an obvious sign. So, lucky or professional? I\u2019m gonna lean towards the later I think. There was not enough of a mess in the clearing for this to have been a novice attack. These guys knew what they were doing, and had practice doing it. And that thought is more than a little disturbing.<br /> <br /> As we were leaving the clearing to continue our search for the Goblin fruit that Andromeda wanted I spotted something flying our way. Five somethings. I let everyone else know and given the rapter-like appearance of the incoming creatures we all prepared for a fight. Elemental and beast armor was raised, weapons drawn and abilities used. Part of me wants to get in more fights just so I can see Lorelei use that appearance power, \u2018cause damn! Anyhoo\u2026we got attacked and things got interesting fast. Calamity did a good bit of damage with her opening attack and after that she was the primary target. The Vileshrikes, as I\u2019ve been told the beasties were called, pegged her as the dangerous one and acted accordingly. Gawain took offense to this and did his best to lay waste to any and everything that came close to his girl. I mainly focused my attacks on those who were already injured and tried to take them out before they could do any more damage. I think I got the killing strike in on a couple of them. As long as they went down and stopped moving I changed focus to another target and worried about the others later. Insincere Marguerite worked her magic on slowing one and Gawain pretty much cut the damn thing in half. Then Ace knocked one prone and I finished it off before it could regain its footing. Calamity continued to do some impressive damage, along with Gawain. Andromeda even helped protect Calamity by shooting one as it came in to attack her lover. All in all it wasn\u2019t that hard a fight. Fun though.<br /> <br /> Despite some of us being just as dangerous as Calamity in the fight the creatures continued to focus their attention on her. I tried to draw them away so she\u2019d get a bit of a respite, but it didn\u2019t work too well. Somebody said something about these things having poisonous attacks, and that just made getting hit by them more problematic. I mean, Calamity is the most dangerous among us from I\u2019ve seen. Gawain is a close second, but I don\u2019t want them being the ones that get hit all the time. Part of me keeps trying to tell myself that it\u2019s not good from a strategic standpoint if our heavy hitters get taken out too fast, but I think it\u2019s becoming more a case that I don\u2019t want to see them getting hurt. Insincere Marguerite can be invisible for all intents and purposes, and Lorelei does that thing where it\u2019s just not possible to look at her and think violent thoughts, so they\u2019re usual safe. Well, safer anyway. Yeah, Rook would tell me that I\u2019m going soft. He would likely have some things to say about my friends, and not all of them entirely complementary. He would look at combat ability first and deem some lacking. But as much as a part of me still looks at Rook like a brother, I know that he is not a good person. Plus a good part of me kind of hates him for torturing me too. Yeah, complicated. Anyhoo...Rook\u2019s likely commentary aside I like my motley-mates.<br /> <br /> When it was all over there were five Vileshrikes on the ground either dead or unconscious and three of our number with wounds of varying degrees of severity. Calamity was the worst off. She had several long gashes that looked fairly deep. She was rather calm about it. And if I hadn\u2019t known it before, that girl has a decent threshold for pain. Gawain seemed more agitated about the whole thing than she was. Then while Lorelei was working that Spring court magic on Calamity, Gawain and I checked the Vileshrikes and killed the ones that weren\u2019t dead yet. Gawain is practical that way, and I think it helped him work out any residual anger towards those things for hurting Calamity. I think most of the others were not really paying close attention to what we were up to, which is not necessarily a bad thing. I was so focused on making sure that the threats were dealt with that I didn\u2019t stop to think about how my familiarity with killing prone enemies could be taken by the rest of the group. Maybe it didn\u2019t stand out so bad. Gawain was doing the same thing I was and everyone knows that he\u2019s a nice guy. Me\u2026not so much, but apparently I can fake it okay. Well, that\u2019s not entirely accurate. I should have said that everyone knows that Gawain is a good guy. I can be a nice guy, but I don\u2019t know if I\u2019d necessarily be considered \u201cgood.\u201d<br /> <br /> Once everyone was healed up we continued on our way. We found the Goblin fruit that we originally came for and headed back to \u201cthe world.\u201d Going back was uneventful. Part of me was a little disappointed I\u2019ll admit. I was still kind of hyped up from the fight and still kinda felt like I wanted to hit something, or someone. I think I kind of reminded myself of Calamity and her \u201cDays between Stabbings\u201d sign on her office door. I don\u2019t necessarily think that I should keep track though.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> After we got back last night I briefly considered stopping by Insincere Marguerite\u2019s room to see if she wanted to fool around. Yeah, adrenaline. But then I wasn\u2019t sure if Julia was still here or not, or if Insincere Marguerite was up for anything. So, I just did some isometric exercises to work off some of that extra energy. I tried reading for a bit, but the only book I had wasn\u2019t really catching my interest. That led to me thinking about getting a library card and checking out some books, which then led to me wondering if anyone would like to go with me, which led to thoughts of doing stuff with the group. Yeah, probably didn\u2019t need all the explanation there, but I figured I better spell it out because I\u2019m not sure I\u2019d remember why my thoughts on library books would lead me to going roller skating with Lorelei.<br /> <br /> Okay\u2026so I stopped by Lorelei\u2019s room and saw that her light was still on so I knocked. I asked her if there was anything that she really liked to do and she kind of blinked at me. I was afraid that the way I said it might be been wrong, so I clarified and asked if there was anything she liked to do that was fun or made her forget her troubles. I could tell that she\u2019d thought of something a moment later but she seemed kind of embarrassed about it. I figured it couldn\u2019t be all that bad and asked her what she was thinking of. I even said please. She said that she really liked roller-skating. With lights and music and a disco ball. I smiled and asked her to meet me in the garage at 10:00am and I\u2019d see what I could do.<br /> <br /> I slept for a bit and woke up fairly early. I can\u2019t seem to stop doing that. Anyway, I booted up the machine in the office and did a Google search for roller rinks in the area. Got several hits, and found one called Northridge Skateland. The pictures on the webpage showed a disco ball, multi-colored lights and folks wearing old style skates. It looked just like what Lorelei described, so I printed out directions to get there, made a pot of coffee for the group and grabbed something quick to eat, then headed out to the garage to meet Lorelei. I couldn\u2019t help but smile when she walked up to me as I was leaning on her car.<br /> <br /> It didn\u2019t take long to find the rink and we went in and rented skates. I opted for the old style skates since that was what Lorelei was wearing, and the whole point was to do something that she wanted to do. So\u2026old style skates. It took me a few minutes to get used to the skates. I remember skating with my sister, but we always used in-line skates. Those feel different. Those are more like ice skates and give you a different range of motion than the old style skates so. So after stumbling for a bit I got the hang of it. I will admit it was fun. Lorelei took to the skating floor like a duck does to water. She was great. At one point some old disco song started playing and she just started dancing. It was really neat to watch. She glided around like a dancer and several of the other skaters just stopped and went to the side so they could just watch her go by. Then one of the attendants made a motion to the light guy and suddenly there was a spot light following her around the rink. It was neat.<br /> <br /> After the song ended she stopped and seemed to come back to herself and she smiled. It was a genuine, happy smile and it was wonderful to see. After her solo Lorelei pulled me into a dance. I tried to match her grace, but yeah, that wasn\u2019t happening. I wasn\u2019t horrible though, and the important part was that we had fun. We skated a little while longer, singing along with the songs we knew, which left a good bit of them that were too early for me or too late for her, but it was all good.<br /> <br /> When we finally stopped and sat down to take off our skates Lorelei had that same beautiful smile on her face. Not that I haven\u2019t seen Lorelei smile since I\u2019ve met her, but this was just different. In comparison, other times I\u2019ve seen her smile always seemed to have a hint of sadness to it. This didn\u2019t, and it made me happy to see it. Her face with lit up with joy and I had something to do that that. It made me really glad I started asking what kinds of things people like doing. It started off as a way for me to get to know people better. At least that was my original intention. But since I skated with Gawain and he had so much fun, it has become a way to help the others forget all the bullshit we deal with and just get lost in the moment and have fun. Calamity was beaming by the end of the fight, and the smile that Lorelei had on her face made my heart skip a beat. In my dreams I remember the way people looked at me when I was taking them to The Lady. Some were happy, some were sad, some were angry, but even the ones that were happy were tainted by something darker. Over the past few days I\u2019ve seen genuine happiness on the faces of those closest to me and it made me feel good to be able to do that for them. I know that these few kind deeds won\u2019t really do much to make up for the things I\u2019ve done, but I suppose it\u2019s a start. I know what kind of person I\u2019ve been and it wasn\u2019t good, or kind. And I know I don\u2019t deserve the nice things that they do for me. I just don\u2019t. But if I can help them heal, just a little bit, it\u2019ll be worth it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> May 6th<br /> <br /> I could so totally get used to this... dating? girlfriend? thing. Whatever it is, it\u2019s all official now too - there\u2019s a memo on the whiteboard even. And that was pretty intense just now. I mean, sure, if I\u2019m being really honest, you know, it\u2019s a maybe a little weird that it was hearing about a dude we\u2019re maybe about to piss off punching <u>through</u> another dude\u2019s head that got her pulling me to the bedroom, but I\u2019m sure as hell not going to complain. Not when I\u2019m sitting here worn out and happy, having been sent to my protective monster\u2019s bed after yawning one too many times trying to keep her company. I brought my sword up with me though, so I can be ready as soon as I hear anything going down.<br /> <br /> I probably should explain how we got here, you know, since remembering things is what this is for, you know?. See, we were having breakfast (waffles!) at one or so. Ace was muttering about dimensions for a piranha tank, since Lori and Jacob had headed off to go roller skating earlier. This was after he\u2019d walked in, grabbed a raw egg, a chunk of cheese and a glass of milk, wandered out, then wandered back in to grab a waffle for roughage. Apparently (heh), my waffles go well with raw egg, which is good, I guess? He was in the middle of trying to make his tongue as long and dexterous as Insincere Marguerite\u2019s when Calamity got dropped off.<br /> <br /> That started off a whole big thing, cause when Calamity said we had a problem, I got worried right off, you know? But then Ace started going on about fire going out in water and so Insincere Marguerite suggested napalm! I mean, I\u2019m all about some flaming trapeze shit and piranhas eating cows and everything, but napalm?! So I got a little distracted. Anyways, that wasn\u2019t what Calamity meant. She was talking about a table that Andromeda had at one point, that had gotten stolen. That didn\u2019t really help the rest of us, except Ace I guess, since she asked if he\u2019d not told us.<br /> <br /> He said it was a secret, so Insincere Marguerite covered her ears with her feet, but since Calamity was involved, I was, and I said so. After I said it, I was worried Calamity might think I was being clingy or bossy or something, but she didn\u2019t seem upset, at least until Ace said something about not knowing Calamity came with a hanger-on and that\u2019s when she decided to write a memo on the whiteboard: \u201cCalamity + Gawain\u201d That made me feel totally awesome, you know, and so did standing next to her with an arm around her waist, while Ace used the rest of the whiteboard to explain. Before that though, Calamity and I both had a little bit of a panic attack, cause Insincere Marguerite heard \u2018apparently\u2019 as \u2018a parent\u2019 and thought Calamity was going to have a kid! She had her feet over her ears, you know. Calamity and I did talk about it a little just now - neither of us really want kids, like, any time soon, so we\u2019re going to look into getting birth control stuff. She did mention maybe at some point, maybe, you know, wanting kids, which is kinda terrifying, but also kinda, well, awesome, cause she was thinking about <u>us</u> having kids particularly, so she\u2019s thinking about us being together for, you know, a long time and everything. Anyways, just then at breakfast, after I said no about a billion times and Calamity backed me up, Ace took over.<br /> <br /> He started off drawing an alien head with an A on it, that he made sure to tell us didn\u2019t stand for adultery. He didn\u2019t say what it did stand for, but I don\u2019t think it was important. That discussion kinda derailed the drawing bit though until he drew a dragon monkey later to explain why he and Calamity didn\u2019t go off with Andromeda by themselves. We\u2019d all known that people thought she was a loyalist, but I guess the Summer and Winter Courts really think so, and the Summer Courts had even intercepted a message from her to her Keeper. So that didn\u2019t look good, and it didn\u2019t help that they both thought she had some special table from Arcadia that Calamity had found out was stolen. But Calamity\u2019s convinced (and I\u2019m pretty sure too) that she\u2019s not a loyalist and Calamity really, really wants to protect her.<br /> <br /> Ace still wanted us to be subtle and everything, even though it wasn\u2019t really a secret anymore, so we didn\u2019t all go back to Andromeda\u2019s to visit, especially since it\u2019s probably bugged, you know? Plus, Calamity told her she should visit us. Insincere Marguerite checked out the House for bugs too and didn\u2019t find any, but we decided to talk with her in the Hedge House anyway, after the show.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, there was business and shit to get done. Well, Calamity and Insincere Marguerite had business to do. Ace and I prepped a list of stuff to turn the spare basement room into a gym kinda place. I just wanted some basic stuff, stuff I hadn\u2019t been able to get cause of living in an apartment, you know, an adjustable bench, an expanded set of kettlebells. A chin up bar definitely - Insincere Marguerite had to bring that up too, cause I kept being distracted by Ace\u2019s giant list of different kinds of punching bags. Apparently, if you punch a bag until your hand breaks, it won\u2019t hurt when you punch a dude and you\u2019ll win. So all the bags had to be as hard as rocks, but otherwise they were all over the place. He is a very strange man.<br /> <br /> Going over all that stuff though, the afternoon passed by really quick. It was a good show, of course. No big interruption or anything - that\u2019s still for Friday. Captain Jack did give me a call and tomorrow he\u2019s going to be obnoxious, apparently in a helicopter, at the pier, so he was thinking he\u2019d set up a breakaway \u201cNo Fishing\u201d sign and when I told him off for being obnoxious, he\u2019d \u2018knock me out\u2019 with it and throw me in the water. Then, since the \u201cNo\u201d would have broken off, he\u2019d start fishing. Also, on Friday, I\u2019d make sure to look wet when I chase him off. Calamity keeps teasing me about my \u2018dates\u2019 with Captain Jack, but it does sound fun. But they\u2019re totally not dates. Anyways, at least she likes him, you know?<br /> <br /> After the show, we went into the Hedge and heard Andromeda\u2019s side of the story. I\u2019m sure she was in an awesome state of mind, since the first thing she saw was the giant Hedge spider posed like it was about to pounce, and then Calamity and Ace started arguing about the best way to scare people off with a dead spider. Then Ace dove right into \u2018Where\u2019s the table?\u2019 It\u2019s not really a wonder we got it all disjointed, but I think this is the way it goes:<br /> <br /> Andromeda was taken by the Mothership and cut into pieces and sewed back together, partially so that she could use the special table thing. It could... fix people, I think medically and stuff (I think. She has weird ideas about fixing people.) but it can also turn people into alien Changelings. Andromeda did actually use it to turn Hailey into an alien, after the Mothership took her, but at least tried to make it not hurt, and didn\u2019t just cut and slice like the Keeper had done to her. Other than that bit though, she didn\u2019t seem to hate her Keepers or her home in Arcadia, kinda like Ace. I didn\u2019t say that to him, cause he seems fixated on not knowing if she\u2019s a loyalist or not and I don\u2019t wanna imply he\u2019s a loyalist or anything, you know?<br /> <br /> Anyways, after she changed Hailey, she kinda fell for her, hard. Hailey pretended to like her back, even told her that she loved her, just before she took advantage of the fact that Andromeda\u2019s room was less secure than hers to escape. Now, I know this next bit is like the pot calling the kettle black, or at best the campfire calling the furnace hot, but man Andromeda doesn\u2019t get people. She thought something was wrong with Hailey, to make her run, so she talked the Mothership into giving her the table so she could bring her back. Not against her will, she promised, but she thought she could talk her into it. Or... fix her into wanting to? That\u2019s kinda disturbing to think about. And she doesn\u2019t understand why Hailey avoids her, or why people don\u2019t like her sometimes. Or why people might be upset about, well, lots of the things she said, if they didn\u2019t know the whole story.<br /> <br /> I do think Andromeda really cares for Hailey, even if... yeah. I think she means well., really, and she\u2019s so tiny and sad, I see why Calamity wants to help her. Andromeda does want to stay, now, which is good. Of course, it means the Mothership might be back for her, or at least the table, and they can\u2019t have either. Unfortunately, someone stole the table like 3 days after she got here, which was a couple of months ago, so the trail is pretty cold. It is true that someone knew right off, which narrows the field to... nobody? Which is not particularly helpful. Hailey might have guessed, but she told Lucian and Lucian thought Andromeda still had it. So unless Hailey is lying to the Summer Court people and is maybe the loyalist Joan thinks she is, that seems unlikely. There <u>was</u> another alien from their keeper, Mr. Gray, who was here in the area for a little bit, in the Winter Court, so he might have told them that other aliens might have magic tables maybe? Even Lucian wasn\u2019t sure who might have grabbed it. He did give Ace a hand grenade, in case the Winter Court came after us. And he\u2019s getting him a bulletproof vest.<br /> <br /> So, plans. First off, I think we should convince the non-super creepy Changelings in town that Andromeda\u2019s alright, just kinda, well, alienish. She hasn\u2019t hurt anyone since she got out of Arcadia and since she got out of their control proper she hasn\u2019t even talked with the Keepers. I mean, <u>Joan</u>, is pretty sure Andromeda\u2019s not a loyalist and she thinks everyone is until she had a reason not to, it seems like. That\u2019s got to count for something, you know? But anyway, that way, her court and everybody could help protect her from the Gentry. Then we need to find the table. The Summer Court wants to destroy it, but it does seem useful, as long as people agree to be changed and everything, you know? Regardless, we can\u2019t let bad guys have it, and if we don\u2019t know who has it, bad guys might. So we gotta figure that out.<br /> <br /> For now though, Andromeda is staying here, in the basement room. At least for tonight. We\u2019ll have to see how tomorrow goes. She was really tired and quiet, after she cried herself out a little. Hopefully she\u2019ll feel better tomorrow. Maybe she\u2019ll want to come to the pier with me and just relax and have fun. Though, if I\u2019m leaving via getting tossed in the water, I don\u2019t want to abandon her or anything, so maybe not the best plan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 07-19-2014, 10:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T18:58:12-07:00","id":202540,"title":"","content":"<b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> <b><u><b><u>Tuesday May 6<sup>th</sup></u></b> </u></b> Days without Stabbing: 1<br /> <br /> Love. Katt used to read all sorts of fanciful poetry about it and listen enraptured to every love ballad there was, the more saccharine the better. She dreamed of love, yearned for it. Then Snow Globe taught me the danger of love, of any trust. Taught me to show nothing, to give nothing that might be used against me. I thought of how utterly foolish that naive little girl had been to crave something so maddening. It really is a drug, it warps your thoughts and your perceptions. It makes you do things you would never consider otherwise. It takes control and drags you along like some wayward carnival ride. And then, inevitably, it's over. Only it still doesn't let go. It clings to your soul and whispers in your ear like some twisted little devil on your shoulder. It makes you forgive the unforgivable. It makes you do the unthinkable.<br /> <br /> I know these things to be true. I have seen it this very night. It was love that allowed Haley to trick Andromeda. Love that drove Andromeda to forsake everything she knew and was comfortable with to pursue the object of her affections. Sure, she is now free of the Mothership, but that wasn't ever her goal. And, blasphemous as it might be to even think it, is she honestly better off here than she was? She's lost the place where she belonged and is in danger from both the servants of the Mothership and her fellow changelings. I sat there as she explained how she knew that Haley had betrayed her. As she explained that she understood how the other girl had used her to make her escape. And then cried and told us how much she still loves Haley. That she would still do anything for her.<br /> <br /> It was love that drove me to kill. Hearing it in their voices as they spoke of the sinister bitch that stole my life. I survived the hell of Snow Globe and they never even missed me. They loved that superficial whore more than they ever loved me. They knew she wasn't the same and THEY FUCKING LOVED HER MORE FOR IT. All I wanted was to go home... to be safe again... to be able to let my guard down... To be that stupid little trusting girl that believed in love again. But they betrayed me and they died for it.<br /> <br /> Fuck, I shouldn't have sent Gawain to bed and stayed up alone. I wish I was there instead of here. Curled up against him with that hard metal skin under my fingertips and those strong arms around me just laying close and talking about anything and everything... even the idea of children. Me? A mother? There is an absolutely terrifying idea. But for him... with him... He loves me so much. It's there in the way he looks at me and speaks to me and in his touch... I tried to warn him, but it was too little too late. Love had taken root and would not be dislodged. And oh holy fuck did it feel good to have him standing there at breakfast with his arm around my waist or to see the fury when he struck down the vile shrike that wounded me Monday night. He would never betray me the way Haley betrayed Andromeda... the way my parents betrayed me. He would never hurt me like that. I can trust him. I just wish I could say the same about myself.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite tells me that I just need to listen and he'll tell me what he wants and needs. That he is a boy and an honest and straightforward one at that. That I can protect that innocence from the truths of the world. But Gawain is not stupid or dumb. He knows... just somehow he is still able to be... bright. The way Katt used to be. I can remember waking up before daybreak almost every day just so I could see the dawn. I can remember how it made me feel. I can remember it, but I can't feel it anymore. The Whispers took that away from me. Cut it out with Their razors and disappointed voices. I remember how it hurt, how I had to learn to be cold and numb inside to survive it, to endure it. Gawain's Keeper made him kill. Murdering over and over, spilling a river of blood that haunts his dreams still. He stopped fighting because of the pain it brought him and it did not save anyone. But somehow, somehow he did not lose his soul. Gawain would not have killed that night in Belleview. He's murdered more than I have... more than I ever will most likely... yet he's not the monster I am. How can he love me? Hell, how can he even stand to look at me? I kept the truth of that night from him for much too long and yet his only reaction was to comfort me when I did admit the truth of it. Insincere Marguerite thinks I can protect him from the world, but what he needs protection from most is me.<br /> <br /> Damn I am fucking maudlin tonight and I haven't even gone near the bar. This is why I hate being goddamn idle. Too much time to think... to remember... And as much as I fucking need to stab the ever-living fuck out of something right now I do not believe the Winter Court is stupid enough to send assassins or kidnappers after Andromeda while she's here. Not when she's been alone in her home and most likely is going to be again soon. But I brought her here and someone should watch over her. I cannot allow her to be taken or killed on my watch. I must remain awake and alert just in case. I don't know what will happen tomorrow but for now, she is safe.<br /> <br /> Maybe I should look for Insincere Marguerite. I'm sure she's awake still and her girl isn't here. She was willing enough to try to answer my questions about being in a serious relationship and she did seem troubled. I don't recall her ever mentioning her dearest before but her feelings clearly run deep there. I have no idea what I could do to help, but maybe just talking about it would be of use... Or maybe I should mind my own business. It's hard to be sure if it's something she wants to talk about or not. And I'm sure she knows I'm awake and alone, so I guess if she wanted company she'd have sought me out.<br /> <br /> Fuck, I am not good at all of this. I don't know how to be her friend. I don't know if I'm doing any of this right. I like her. I like all of them. I want to help but fuck, unless it's something that needs to be gutted in the dark what in the ever loving hell am I going to do about it? What do I know about anything? Katt was too young and too sheltered. Snow Globe was hell. I have no idea how the real goddamn world works. I have no idea what normal people feel and do. Fuck, I drug Gawain to bed because hearing about how Lucian Torrez murdered a man got me hot and bothered. (To be fair, it <i>was</i> fucking epic. The man may be evil but I am jealous as fuck of his style right now.) I am not afraid to stand up to him or Master Darke or even the fucking Mothership to help Andromeda, but what good does that do when it's her broken heart that hurts her more than anything else? Haley tricked her, used her to escape and never looked back. If Andromeda wasn't here now, how would I feel about that? I'm not sure, but I doubt I'd find myself thinking of how to make sure that her ghost couldn't identify me as her killer. But I know it won't actually fix anything. It would hurt Andromeda even more and there isn't any proof Haley has done anything but fear that an agent of her Keeper had come to take her back.<br /> <br /> What I need to do is find the goddamn magical table. Andromeda managed to coax the Mothership into letting her bring it with her to fix Haley but it was promptly stolen. So, all of the ones that we know want it aren't suspect because if they had it they wouldn't be looking for it still. I think Ace is still annoyed that I told the others about it, but we're the damn Musketeers. One for all and all fucked over if one of us does something stupid (like deciding to harbor a suspected loyalist.) I know Queen Charlotte is interested and... well... I know when I talk to Andromeda about this I am going to be trying to convince her that the Autumn Court should have The Table. But first we have to find it. Andromeda told us it's not simple to use, that it would be beyond even Haley. But the ones after its power don't know that and I imagine that given time whoever claims it will be able to unlock The Table's power. The only person she knows of that would understand it is a Mr Grey, who was the Mothership's doctor before her. He was apparently a member of the Winter Court but has not been seen or heard from in some time. If they have him stashed somewhere, it could be why they want The Table. Or maybe he dropped out of the courts and joined up with some other group... loyalists or bounty hunters or something? Maybe they have the Table? Or maybe I am just spinning wild conjecture and have absolutely NO fucking idea where to start looking for the damnable thing.<br /> <br /> I hate this feeling of having no idea what to do. I hate being idle. I need to do something.. anything... I'm not a patient monster tonight. But there are no good leads and Andromeda already told us everything she knows. She said she needed to be alone, so I have left her be. There really is nothing to be done right now, but I can't just sit here any longer or my head is going to explode. There's room in the unused part of the basement to practice my walking and Annika will be here tomorrow. I'll still be close enough to watch Andromeda's room and a few hours of strutting should help clear my head.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> Today was a fairly relaxing day, but full of awkward conversations. Mostly.<br /> <br /> For example, at breakfast we had some discussion of Andromeda, who was rather the subject of the hour, as Calamity returned from, well, \u201cspending time\u201d with her, which did not seem to bother Gawain. Maybe. Calamity inadvertently revealed information from a secret conversation she had had with Ace about a Table and Andromeda. I covered my ears, but saw them write a Calamity and Gawain heart sort of thing on the whiteboard, and thought I heard something about Calamity becoming a parent but with my ears covered I don\u2019t hear as well and apparently it was something else but I thoroughly embarrassed both. Anyway, Andromeda is coming to the show tonight, probably, and we will interview her after. That was the plan, anyway. Mostly.<br /> <br /> I must remember Americans like guns, but don\u2019t like Napalm. It seems if you like one horrid violent weapon you should like another. Also, with people from three different countries and probably even more different eras, cultural references are a minefield. Also apparently my turns of phrase are amusing to the Motley. Ace in particular was more amused by the good-natured jibs about the British I made and took them in stride. Probably. It was how I intended them, anyway. I have nothing against the British, after all, even though they are terribly strange.<br /> <br /> I was working on ideas for my <i><i>Brotherswing</i></i> show when Calamity entered the stage area and wanted to ask me some questions. It seems I am being sought for romantic advice, due to I\u2019s clearly excellent relationship with Julia. Probably. Calamity is indeed dating Gawain, and does not want to hurt him. She does, however, like sleeping with Andromeda but was not in love with her. I was sort of surprised Calamity was not gay myself. Mostly. Of course I was also surprised Lorelei was queer, so I am clearly bad at this. Usually.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m\u2026not in a good place to give romantic advice. Mostly. I am, after all, trying to force myself to give Julia space and not give in to the urge to keep and abscond with her, despite her being regrettably okay with the concept. Still, I shared what advice I could. Gawain is a boy, and a straightforward one, so her path seems free of stones so long as Gawain does not bore her. Probably. Indeed, I helped not if she is worried about his innocence, she can protect him from many of the dark truths of the world by murdering them without his knowledge.<br /> <br /> Of course, Gawain is not really innocent. Indeed, he has killed far more people than I have, wrecked more lives than I have. Probably. Well human lives. Mostly. Maybe. I reserved my thefts for those in Arcadia, who were already compromised by their role as servants and playthings of the Gentry. I was not going to bring that up to Calamity of course. I suspect she would take it badly, and her hands make knives. I am soft despite being boney and would make a poor, if adorable, pincushion. Probably.<br /> <br /> Also Calamity was apparently stuck at thirteen for some time. Thirteen is a terrible age to be stuck at. No wonder she is angry all the time.<br /> <br /> I spoke some of my problem. It\u2019s hard to bring up without sounding egocentric, really. \u201cOh dear, this beautiful artists absolutely loves me, wants to be with me in clothing optional situations, and seems okay with almost anything I want, however kinky.\u201d That is the sort of problem one would get slapped for complaining about. Usually. And yet, I am worried about my soul, and I think, or hope, I conveyed that to Calamity. Some odd looks crossed her face when I started mumbling about my Dearest, so I think perhaps I did.<br /> <br /> The show went well, and we met Andromeda at the hedge house. I won\u2019t use the word innocent for Andromeda but she is terribly naive. It seems she came here following Hailey, another Wizened whom she had turned into her alien-looking self for the \u201cMothership.\u201d Hailey sensed her captor was smitten with her, and seduced her (or allowed herself to be seduced) and slept in Andromeda\u2019s lower security part of the \u201cship,\u201d escaping that night. Clever, I think. I have to say outwitting the minions of the Gentry is a fine pastime. Generally. Andromeda went after her, confused why she would want to escape (for some reason) and took an artifact called The Table with her\u2026a \u201ctool\u201d she used to reshape humans into Changelings. She brought it to \u201cfix\u201d Hailey when found, and made the mistake of sending her Keeper a message back to let it (she?) know she arrived in town. This letter was, apparently, intercepted by the Summer Court, who was watching Andromeda at Hailey\u2019s insistence. Wisely.<br /> <br /> It seems, however, a wrinkle appeared\u2026the Table the Summer Court was seeking had been stolen from Andromeda, very shortly after arriving. The Summer Court allegedly does not know its location, neither the Ogre Lucian Torrez nor Hailey. Calamity implied the Autumn Court may be interested in it, so apparently they don\u2019t have it, and the Winter Court also appears to be seeking it. It is an issue, probably. The odd thing is Andromeda claims it would be useless to them as she is one of the few who can use it\u2026apparently even Hailey can\u2019t. Andromeda\u2019s odd behavior, early comments about her Keeper and preoccupation with derrieres have not lead her to be well accepted even in her Court. Apparently.<br /> <br /> We decided to look at her for the moment. She will be sleeping downstairs. This does beg some questions; are we sheltering a Loyalist? She has not betrayed her Keeper. Does that make me a Loyalist? I came here on Mama Lion\u2019s orders. I do not wish Mama Lion harm. I would be some racist Parisian pseduointellectual without her intervention, after all, and probably fat. Probably. At the same time, I don\u2019t wish to work for her again either. Most would say we are not Loyalists. Probably. But the Lost are seldom even tempered about such things. Maybe.<br /> <br /> Ace met with Mr. Torrez, to let him know Andromeda did not have the Table. Apparently he witnessed Mr. Torrez killing a human, then they had coffee. Summer Courtiers are strange. Mostly. Ace did discover that Joan, of all people, wasn\u2019t suspicious of Andromeda\u2026she originally suspected Hailey, in fact, before Andromeda\u2019s presence made that seem unlikely. She still apparently dislikes and distrusts Hailey, but then she is as friendly as a hornet\u2019s nest covered with manure. I don\u2019t know why the Spring Court is so fixated on her.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s all rather confusing. This should help me keep it straight in my mind. Now I must prepare answers if Gawain comes seeking advice for romancing Calamity. I will give him good answers. Probably. I should also make plans in case it happens for me to steal the Table from someone.<br /> <br /> Hopefully.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session VIII (with Session VII Overflow) </i><br /> <br /> \u201cThe Table\u201d if you have not guessed is actually a Prop. Andromeda lacks the ability to turn people into Changelings or alter Changelings, but The Table can allow it\u2019s Operators to use it\u2019s power as a Kindly One to do so, as per the Contract with the Wyrd that created The Table.<br /> <br /> In terms of RP, Insincere Marguerite made a lot of random stereotypes of people in conversation (including her usual distain for French Canadians and, for some inexplicable reason, Albanians) so it came up she got up on \u201cthe racist side of the bed that morning.\u201d It came up OOC in the IC conversation with Calamity about boys how very differently the two Darklings see their pre-kidnap time. Calamity misses her old self, pines for it a bit, and sees her transformation as a terrible thing. Andromeda reminds her of Katt so she feels protective. Insincere Marguerite was a privileged teenage Front National supporter who, while it comes out in her attitude sometimes, loathes her old self deeply, and lashes out at people who remind her of her old self at all. It\u2019s an amusing and unplanned dichotomy.<br /> <br /> The scene with Torrez was they saw him walk out in front a car to stop it. Get hit, then jump through the windshield, pull the driver out, interrogate him, and punch through his head. Lucian is a Stonebones/Render (and, as noted, played by Brian Thompson) so really good at a) taking damage and b) breaking shit. It was also intended to send a strong \u201cfuck with this guy at your peril unless you do a lot of preparing\u201d message to the PCs. The message was received.<br /> <br /> At this writing we should have the whole crew this time (I totally wrote Krewe there the first time) so back to usual hijinx. See you for the next one, in the meantime Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T23:18:01-07:00","id":204698,"title":"","content":"I thought the near complete infertility of changlings was common knowledge. Is this no the case in your rendition?<br /> <br /> Also, reading your journals made me have an idea for a changling character. A servant type who was accepting of his lot without being broken first and was genuinely kind to his Keeper. This however confused Her and she let him go. He suspects that She let him go because She wouldn't get the fun of breaking in a new servant. Also there might be the possibility of him having infected his Keeper and Her being Banished. Not that he knows this of course. See what you did?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T01:53:56-07:00","id":208013,"title":"","content":"In my version Changelings are slightly less fertile than normal humans (especially with normal humans) but can and do reproduce...though not Changelings, as per the default rules. This is because children and the possibilities thereof add something to more highly social games (like I run) and in an era where contraception means a female PC can easily avoid pregnancy if her player does not wish to deal with it, it adds something and takes away little to have. The main exception is in Arcadia, for whatever reason, it never happens (to keep with part of the original reasoning for it).<br /> <br /> As for the latter, heh, well could work, certainly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T14:33:55-07:00","id":208692,"title":"","content":"As for the latter, a little too special snow flake?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T15:21:00-07:00","id":208757,"title":"","content":"Not necessarily. Depends on how they are played.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T23:03:47-07:00","id":217198,"title":"","content":"Back to the Lost of Malibu Dream House. Last session we were back to the full group, and got on the same page. Mostly a lot of PCs followed their own plans. Fortunately, we have several journals as per, so you get to get the full account. Back to the usual order.<br /> <br /> <i>Session IX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> May 7th<br /> <br /> The Summer Court shenanigans might have gotten Calamity in the mood, but they showed up in my nightmares. The usual ones, you know, back in the Dreamlands, killing the people I love, except this time I wasn\u2019t using my sword, just punching their heads off. That\u2019s how it worked too, not, like, I punched their head through and their face crumpled, like Lucian did, but I punched them in the face and their head just popped off as if I\u2019d cut it with my sword. Dreams are fucking weird, you know? Calamity wasn\u2019t there when I woke up, but I kinda figured she wouldn\u2019t be. She does that sometimes, just staying up, and since she was feeling all protective I kinda thought that\u2019d be the way it went. I was still kinda hoping though.<br /> <br /> I did find her downstairs, walking up and down the basement hallway like Annika had been teaching her. Her practice was today, and that started making things better. They were doing actual dance stuff this time. Calamity did great, of course. Apparently, next time Annika\u2019s going to teach her to crawl. Dancing practice days are awesome days, nightmares be damned. Anyways, I told her I was gonna make some breakfast, and we decided on omelettes.<br /> <br /> Jacob noticed I wasn\u2019t very with it, when I got to the kitchen, so after he gave me my coffee and I mentioned omelettes, he started getting everything out so all I had to do was stand there and put it together. He\u2019s pretty awesome. I missed his help the day before, not that waffles and fruit is too rough. Speaking of waffles, Ace repeated his performance from before, this time eating his raw egg with spaghetti noodles. Apparently, it would have been perfect with Fritos, but since we didn\u2019t have any, he just crumbled up the eggshell into it. At least what was left of the egg shell, since he\u2019d cracked it by biting it anyway.<br /> <br /> Over breakfast some, and then more once Andromeda went back home, we caught Lori and Jacob up on what they missed while they were rollerskating. I think they got most of it, flying piranha vampires with chainsaws notwithstanding. We did decide the whiteboard was the business whiteboard, and so there shouldn\u2019t be any murder/stabbing stuff on it, you know? We\u2019re going to get another whiteboard for that, and put it somewhere so it\u2019s not where everybody who comes in can see it.<br /> <br /> Then I took Jacob to a meeting with Master Dark. He\u2019s one creepy ass dude, and I was still a little twitchy from the dreams, so I made sure my sword was stowed in an easy-ish to get place. I mean, I can\u2019t really put it somewhere actually easy to get, not and not get pulled over for whatever it\u2019s called when you get pulled over for having a big ass sword, you know? But I did my best, and then waited right outside Master Creepypants creepy rehab hangout for Jacob to be done. On the way home he was little keyed up, but we still got some driving practice in for him.<br /> <br /> So we had more discussion time when we got home. Master Dark told Jacob about the table, actually a little more than we knew. I guess it can change peoples\u2019 kiths, and maybe seemings. And it may be sentient, which is really spooky to think about. Master Dark was really pushy about *not* wanting the table, just wanting to make sure Lucian didn\u2019t have the table. They\u2019ve got real hate-ons for each other, you know? I think we should give it to the Autumn Court, like Calamity said. I mean, not just cause Calamity said so, but it seems like it might be really hard to break (kill? I mean, if it\u2019s sentient, maybe). It\u2019d probably be best to, but we also probably don\u2019t want to keep a hold of it for long enough to do that. The Autumn Court can probably hide it better than us, and maybe can find a way to break it using their library. Insincere Marguerite said our library probably didn\u2019t have anything, since she\u2019d only found books about dancing, with notes about blowjobs.<br /> <br /> Lori really wanted to destroy it though, and also didn\u2019t like that I had a grenade in my glove box. I didn\u2019t really like it either, so much, you know? So I went and got it and now we have a grenade in our house, which is awesome? Or one cow short of an Ace act, one or the other. Or both, I guess. Anyway, we decided to put it off a bit, since we didn\u2019t have the table anyway, and also Lori\u2019s going to ask the Spring Princess what she might want done with it. Ace was all about asking other Courts too, but I don\u2019t think Insincere Marguerite was too excited about asking her Court\u2019s representative, and I\u2019m the only one from mine. Bringing that up did get Calamity to dub me as Sir Gawain, Marquis of Santa Monica and Malibu, which sounds super fancy. Better not let Lucian hear though, he might think we non-Seasonal Courts are getting uppity, you know?<br /> <br /> After that we just kinda chilled until it was time to go to the pier. Well, Lori went to see the Princess, and came back kinda bummed, but didn\u2019t want to talk about it much. And I was kinda distracted, cause it was practice time, you know? But everybody decided to go out to the pier, so it was kinda like a party, and I think Lori got to feeling better super quick, cause De la Roche was there and they pretty much immediately started making out.<br /> <br /> Joan was there, so Ace and I went to talk with her. She said she didn\u2019t trust Halley for two main reasons. First, cause her story didn\u2019t add up and kept changing - first a whole group of people were coming after her then no one was coming and people should leave her alone and then Andromeda was coming for her. Second, Joan thought she was trying to kidnap Monica. She said it wouldn\u2019t even be hard to change her, just \u201ca palette swap and some dental work\u201d. I guess cause of her eyes, you know? Also, when she talked with Andromeda she didn\u2019t feel like she was being deceptive at all, and Halley seemed really manipulative, to her.<br /> <br /> She also said the Spring Court people keep trying to date rape her, which is so not cool. I guess there\u2019s some sort of competition going on to sleep with her, you know? She is very pretty, but that\u2019s just making her paranoid and making her question if she ever really does like somebody. Or, I guess, to be fair, she might be being paranoid about the whole thing to start with. Either way, it\u2019s a bummer, you know? I should ask Lori about the competition thing. I think Joan\u2019s Keeper did very bad things to her though. Or made her do bad things to people. She\u2019s very sure that bad things will happen to people without constant vigilance, or that people will do bad things whenever they get a chance. She said we should put a GPS thing under Andromeda\u2019s skin, in case whoever has the table tries to kidnap her, cause they\u2019d probably strip her and so the GPS thing would get removed unless it was under her skin. That seems really creepy to me, you know? I guess we could *ask* Andromeda, but... I dunno. It seems weird.<br /> <br /> Calamity had gone to talk with Monica and Halley while we were talking to Joan. I guess they talked about the bounty thing, that Captain Jack told me about. There\u2019s a pack of these briar wolf things around, in the Hedge that\u2019s kinda a mirror of the state park, at the edge of Malibu. When Captain Jack told me about it, I thought it\u2019d be an awesome date with Calamity, you know, stabbing bad guys and everything, but then he said there was probably, like, 8 or 12 of them, so I figured we\u2019d probably need the whole motley. She still have fun hopefully though. I think we\u2019re going to tomorrow. Maybe it will distract her from wanting to stab Halley so much.<br /> <br /> I went and joined them after I got done talking with Joan, and we were talking about beating up the Vile Shrikes when Captain Jack showed up! He had his own helicopter and everything, he got lowered down to the pier wearing angel wings with \u201cSend me an Angel\u201d playing from loudspeakers. He was flirting with everybody, he even gave Jacob his number, then his wings. When he got over to the No Fishing sign, I started hassling him about making a nuisance and we had a killer fight. He was really good about telegraphing what he was about to do, and did most the work on making us both look good, but I did ok, I think. It ended just like we\u2019d planned, with the breakaway sign and everything. We certainly had everyone watching! I circled round and just headed for the car, since I didn\u2019t want to have to talk with the police for forever. The others showed up a little later, sans Lori, cause she drove separate and was going home with De la Roche.<br /> <br /> Calamity had brought a nice big towel for me, and had been keeping my stuff like my wallet and my keys and my phone so it wouldn\u2019t get wet. She told me my boyfriend had called, even though Captain Jack is *not* my boyfriend, but I guess he wanted to make sure I was ok after pretending to hit me on the head with a sign, which seems fair.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> My motley is involved in a political shit-storm which threatens to blow up right in our faces. None of us really knows whether one of our new allies is a Loyalist or a na\u00efve young girl. My friends are volunteering to lead the motley into the Hedge to hunt down a pack of vicious, cunning, killer hobgoblins. I may have blundered my way into upsetting one of the kindest, most beautiful, and most powerful women I know. And despite all of this, I\u2019m elated. I can\u2019t remember the last time I felt like this!<br /> <br /> Okay, first thing\u2019s first. Jacob and I apparently missed some important things while we were skating the other day. The motley has come to some conclusions regarding the situation with Andromeda. According to the little alien girl, this magic table everyone is looking for was stolen from her a few days after she arrived in the area, and my friends think she\u2019s too awkward and self-conscious to lie effectively about things like that. While I can\u2019t really fault their logic, I do think Calamity is taking this whole thing rather personally. She seems to have developed an unhealthy fixation on the idea of killing Hailey in horrible ways.<br /> <br /> Andromeda also claims that \u2013 while she was still working happily for the Gentry she calls \u201cThe Mothership\u201d \u2013 she fell in love with Hailey. The other alien girl used this attraction to get close to her\u2026 and then made her escape. As a loyal servant of the Mothership, she volunteered to hunt the escapee down, but once she made it back to the world, she realized how wrong she had been, and came back to the side of the angels. Hailey \u2013 quite understandably if you ask me \u2013 isn\u2019t convinced that the woman who transformed her has genuinely changed sides.<br /> <br /> There was also something about how Lucien Torrez killed a man he suspected of setting a trap for him. By punching him in the head. And then he gave Gawain a grenade. Remind me not to piss off Lucien Torrez.<br /> <br /> After breakfast, Jacob got a call from Master Darke, the King of Winter. Gawain drove him out there while the rest of us hung around the house. Which of course meant I was treated to another of Annika\u2019s <u>fabulous</u> dance lessons. I can\u2019t think of <u>anything</u> I\u2019d rather do than watch one of my best friends go to someone I <u>hate</u> instead of me when she wants to learn to dance. Sarcasm is a wonderful thing, isn\u2019t it?<br /> <br /> When Jacob got back, he told us what Master Darke had wanted to talk about. He claimed that the Winter Court didn\u2019t actually want the table\u2026 they just wanted to make sure that Lucien Torrez doesn\u2019t get his hands on it. And, well, I can kind of see their point, though I\u2019m not sure I buy Master Darke\u2019s disinterest completely. He might just be trying to throw us off the scent, and secretly plotting to take the table for himself.<br /> <br /> I decided that it would be best if I asked Princess Jolie about my own Court\u2019s feelings on this matter, so I announced that I was going to head over to Glamour Springs for a visit. Jacob pulled me aside and shared a few other choice tidbits Master Darke had let slip. There are some nasty rumors floating around about Princess Jolie. People say that she devours the souls of artistically inclined mortals to keep herself young and beautiful, and that she can\u2019t really control these appetites. Master Darke really didn\u2019t want her getting her hands on the table, and opined that Lucien Torrez works to keep Jolie in power because he feels that her secrets keep my Court from gaining any true political power in the area.<br /> <br /> Well, those little revelations certainly made for a happy visit to Glamour Springs, let me tell you. Becky and Dark Kimberly were there, as well as a darkling boy I hadn\u2019t met before named Davie. I was escorted into Princess Jolie\u2019s presence, and she received me warmly enough. I told her everything we\u2019ve learned about Andromeda, Hailey, and the table, and asked her if the Spring Court had any particular position of which I should be mindful. She told me that we didn\u2019t, although she\u2019d be happier if neither Torrez nor Darke got their hands on it.<br /> <br /> Then I mentioned the rumors Jacob told me about. I wish I hadn\u2019t brought those up, but I thought it was important for Princess Jolie to know what the other monarchs were saying about her. She got this incredibly sad look on her face, and refused to look me in the eye. It broke my heart.<br /> <br /> \u201cI came back from Arcadia with certain\u2026 appetites,\u201d she admitted in a hoarse voice unlike her usual lilting drawl. \u201cUsually I can keep them under control, but sometimes things slip past my guard. It only works with mortals\u2026 you have nothing to fear from me.\u201d<br /> <br /> I tried to reassure her that this information didn\u2019t affect my loyalty to the Court \u2013 or to her personally \u2013 but it was too late. She was already sinking into a very deep funk. After securing my promise that I wouldn\u2019t reveal her secret to anyone (she didn\u2019t make it a pledge, but I\u2019ll hold it as a binding promise anyway), she asked me to tell Dark Kimberly to cancel the rest of her appointments for the day. I bowed and left her to her thoughts.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe Princess doesn\u2019t want to be disturbed for the rest of the day,\u201d I told Kimberly in the waiting room.<br /> <br /> She raised an eyebrow. \u201cWhat did you <u>say</u> to her?\u201d she asked incredulously.<br /> <br /> My guilt must have been written all over my face. \u201cI told her something that\u2026 reminded her of something she\u2019d rather forget,\u201d I confessed.<br /> <br /> Kimberly rolled her eyes at me and made her exit. I was feeling lower than dogshit, and that must have been pretty apparent too, because Davie gave me a reassuring smile. \u201cDon\u2019t pay her any attention,\u201d he said soothingly. \u201cThe Princess will get past whatever\u2019s upsetting her, and things will be back to normal in no time.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks,\u201d I sniffed. \u201cI don\u2019t think we\u2019ve been introduced. I\u2019m Lorelei.\u201d<br /> <br /> He nodded. \u201cI know; you run the Dream House, right? I haven\u2019t been able to stop by yet myself, but I\u2019ve heard good things. I\u2019m Davie, the Spring Court\u2019s token darkling. I think every court has to have at least one, whether they want us or not\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I gave him a smile. \u201cI\u2019m sure that\u2019s not true,\u201d I said, \u201cI know a darkling in the Summer Court, and I know she wouldn\u2019t be there if she didn\u2019t belong. I\u2019m sure it\u2019s the same with you.\u201d<br /> <br /> I secured a promise that Davie would check out our show over the weekend, and said my goodbyes. I drove back to the Dream House considerably more subdued than I had left it. I think at least Insincere Marguerite picked up on that, because she was very affectionate and sympathetic. While I appreciated her efforts to cheer me up, even the fact that Annika had left before my return didn\u2019t really lift my spirits much.<br /> <br /> Gawain had been planning something with Captain Jack over the past week, some sort of street performance out at the pier to spread word of their \u201crivalry.\u201d I think some of the others wanted to question Joan about her take on the whole Andromeda/Hailey situation (which was reputedly pro-Andromeda), and she often hangs out at the pier as well. Since I didn\u2019t have anything else to do other than wallow in my own misery, I decided to call up D and see if she wanted to meet up at the pier and hang out.<br /> <br /> She did. She asked if she should drive, or if we\u2019d be leaving together. I told her that I\u2019d love to have her company tonight, but that if she was getting sick of me I wouldn\u2019t take it personally if she wanted an evening to herself. She paused for a moment, and then told me she\u2019d catch a ride to the pier with Monica, and just like that my evening got a whole lot better.<br /> <br /> I had no idea how <u>much</u> better it was going to get, though. Ace and Gawain spotted Joan almost as soon as we arrived (me in my \u2018vette, the rest of the motley in Gawain\u2019s van) and split off to talk with her. The rest of us soon found D, Monica, and Hailey hanging out near the boardwalk and approached them.<br /> <br /> As soon as she saw me, D ran up, threw her arms around me, and gave me an incredibly passionate kiss. There were wolf-whistles and cat-calls from some of the bystanders, but I don\u2019t think either of us gave a damn at that moment; we were too wrapped up in each other.<br /> <br /> \u201cI swear, Lori,\u201d she said breathlessly when we came up for air, \u201cyou must be trying to turn me into a full-time dyke.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled at her. \u201cI\u2019m not trying to turn you into anything, D,\u201d I said innocently, \u201cI like you just the way you are.\u201d She kissed me again. \u201cWhat was that for?\u201d I giggled after we disengaged.<br /> <br /> She gave me a look that was almost shy. \u201cMaybe\u2026 maybe I\u2019m just tired of pretending this thing between us is only casual,\u201d she admitted.<br /> <br /> So after that I kissed <u>her</u>. I pretty much got over my funk in that instant. And I think the two of us probably missed out on a lot of other conversations as we pretty much lost ourselves in each other\u2019s eyes. I know a few of my friends spoke with Joan about Andromeda and Hailey, and our resident stick-in-the-mud shared her opinions on that whole shebang. She essentially thinks that Hailey has changed her story once too often, and that Andromeda is so guileless that if she attempted to lie about her intentions most people would instantly see through her deceptions. Makes sense to me.<br /> <br /> There was also some talk about hunting down some creatures called briar wolves that had moved into the local Hedge. Apparently there\u2019s a bounty on them, and some of my more adventurous motley-mates have decided it would be good fun to tangle with a large pack of vicious and intelligent killer beasts. I\u2019m not looking forward to it, but I\u2019ll probably go along anyway. I\u2019d feel horrible if one of my friends got hurt and I wasn\u2019t there to help them. I just hope I don\u2019t get roped into the stereotypical role of \u201cbait.\u201d<br /> <br /> I did take notice when Captain Jack showed up. It was a well (if somewhat obviously) staged fight. Basically Captain Jack arrived at the pier and started acting like a jerk. He was actually airlifted in by a helicopter, riding on a dangling rope ladder with a pair of tacky angel wings strapped on to his back and some song I didn\u2019t recognize blaring out of the sound system. He set down lightly and played to the crowd, even going so far as to give Jacob his wings with a wink and a grin. Gawain confronted him about his attitude, and the two of them started to throw down. This staged fight ended with Captain Jack smashing a \u201cNo Fishing\u201d sign over Gawain\u2019s head and throwing him off the pier. This action took the \u201cNo\u201d off the sign, and Captain Jack planted the sign back on the pier and produced a collapsible fishing rod from his bag.<br /> <br /> Gawain was okay, of course, and he joined us again as we made our way back to the cars. And I must admit, most of the people on the pier will probably remember that \u201cfight\u201d for the rest of their lives, no matter how corny the trappings were. If Jack\u2019s looking for publicity, he\u2019s on the right track.<br /> <br /> The others piled into Gawain\u2019s van while D and I got in the \u2018vette. \u201cYou wanna come back to my place this time?\u201d she asked me. \u201cIt\u2019s not as fancy as the Dream House, but\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019d love to,\u201d I said with a grin. \u201cLay on, MacDuff.\u201d<br /> <br /> Ten minutes later we walked into a slightly cluttered, modestly appointed loft. The windows were covered by blackout curtains, but I\u2019d been expecting that (Darklings, man\u2026 no appreciation for the beauty of a sunset). Movie posters decorated the walls. I recognized a few of them (<i>Casablanca, Key Largo, My Little Chickadee</i>), but most of them were for films I\u2019d never heard of. There were also posters for bands. I noticed the Clash, the Cramps, and the Ramones, but the others were mostly unknown to me. The Dead Kennedys. Black Flag. Sonic Youth. Rancid. From the band names, I\u2019d guess that most of them are also punk bands, but I confess that I\u2019m not really sure.<br /> <br /> I noticed an electric guitar leaning up against an amp in one corner. \u201cYou play?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cNot well,\u201d she smirked in answer. \u201cI see that look in your eye, Lori, and no\u2026 you\u2019ll never get me up on that stage of yours.\u201d<br /> <br /> I laughed it off as though the thought hadn\u2019t even crossed my mind. \u201cOkay, fair enough. But I\u2019m gonna want to hear you play something one of these days.\u201d She nodded as she turned away.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou can put your stuff anywhere,\u201d she said as I looked around. \u201cI don\u2019t really spend a lot of time here, so don\u2019t worry about keeping it neat or anything.\u201d<br /> <br /> I hung my jacket in her closet, and found a few sets of freshly pressed scrubs in plastic garment bags. \u201cSo, are you a nurse, or just kinkier than you\u2019ve been letting on?\u201d I asked playfully.<br /> <br /> She rolled her eyes. \u201cI work some nights as a nurse\u2019s assistant at a radiology clinic,\u201d she said simply. \u201cI probably don\u2019t really need to wear that shit; it\u2019s just to keep up appearances.\u201d<br /> <br /> It sort of struck me at that point how little I really knew about my paramour. \u201cSo, D,\u201d I said as I plopped down on her bed and slung an arm around her shoulders, \u201ctell me all your darkest secrets.\u201d<br /> <br /> She stiffened and gave me a helpless look. \u201cI\u2026 I don\u2019t\u2026 I can\u2019t\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I smacked my own forehead. \u201cShit, I\u2019m sorry, D,\u201d I said, kissing her softly. \u201cI didn\u2019t mean we had to talk about\u2026 <u>that</u>. Or anything you don\u2019t want to talk about. I just want to get to know you better, that\u2019s all.\u201d<br /> <br /> She sighed in relief and leaned in to my embrace. \u201cWell\u2026 I\u2019m a third generation Mexican immigrant,\u201d she said after a minute. \u201c<i>Mi abuelo</i> \u2013 my grandfather \u2013 came over from Oaxaca a long time ago. He married a local girl, and the family was assimilated into the American culture pretty thoroughly, but he always made sure we knew the old lingo and were aware of our culture.\u201d<br /> <br /> I grinned. \u201cSo it\u2019s Spanish you shout out when you\u2026 I mean, when we\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> The color rose in her cheeks, ever so slightly. \u201cYeah,\u201d she admitted.<br /> <br /> \u201cI speak French and German,\u201d I told her, \u201cbut only a few words of Spanish. Maybe you should teach me. I\u2019d sure like to know what you\u2019re saying so emphatically in the heat of passion.\u201d<br /> <br /> Her blush deepened. \u201c<i>Madre de Dios,</i> Lori,\u201d she said, \u201chow do you <u>do</u> this shit to me? I\u2019m\u2026 I mean, I always thought of myself as mostly straight. I never even looked at another woman before Madame Spidertoes. But you\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I put a finger on her lips. \u201cI try not to think of myself as straight, gay, or bi,\u201d I admitted. \u201cI just\u2026 I know I like you, D. I mean, I <u>want</u> you; that should be obvious. You\u2019re <u>hot</u>. But you\u2019re also smart, and fun, and funny, and sweet\u2026 though you try to hide that last bit from most people.\u201d<br /> <br /> She didn\u2019t respond.<br /> <br /> \u201cI like sex,\u201d I continued after a minute had passed in silence. \u201cYou\u2019ve probably figured out by now that I like sex a <u>lot</u>. But for the past week or so\u2026 mostly I\u2019m thinking about you. Like when I was with Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne last week\u2026 okay, so I wasn\u2019t actually thinking about you while we were making out, because that would be tacky. But afterwards I couldn\u2019t stop thinking about you. I wanted to see you again.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019ve been on my mind a lot too, Lori,\u201d she replied softly. \u201cAnd I\u2019ve really enjoyed the time we\u2019ve spent together, and I want to keep seeing you\u2026 <u>and</u> to keep screwing you. I\u2019m just having a hard time figuring out what that might mean about me as a person.\u201d<br /> <br /> It was hard to say the next part. \u201cD\u2026 if you\u2019re not ready for this, you can take as much time as you want.\u201d<br /> <br /> She chewed on that for a minute, then gave me that cocky grin I\u2019m quickly growing to love. \u201cNah,\u201d she said, reverting to her usual cocksure manner, \u201cfuck it. I\u2019ll figure it out as we go.\u201d<br /> <br /> I squeezed her hand. \u201cWe\u2019ll figure it out together, D,\u201d I promised.<br /> <br /> The next few hours are a passionate blur in my memory. The next time I looked at a clock it was about 3:00am, and D and I were lying in each other\u2019s arms, naked, tangled in her sheets, and glistening with sweat. I think we were both drifting off to sleep, but I felt the need to say something.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019ve made me really happy tonight, D,\u201d I whispered, kissing her hair. \u201cI mean, the sex was great as always, but it\u2019s the other stuff that\u2026 Jesus, D, why do I only get tongue-tied around <u>you</u>?\u201d<br /> <br /> She stopped my stammering with a soft kiss, gazed into my eyes, and whispered \u201cMaria.\u201d<br /> <br /> I probably blinked at her a few times. I tend to do that when I\u2019m confused. \u201cWhat?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cMy name. It\u2019s Maria de la Rocha.\u201d Before that could really sink in, she continued. \u201cYou can\u2019t tell anybody. And you can\u2019t call me that when anyone else can hear you, okay? But I wanted you to know.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you,\u201d I replied. \u201cIt means so much to know that you trust me with this, Maria.\u201d The name felt odd on my lips the first time.<br /> <br /> \u201cEven my boss doesn\u2019t know,\u201d she explained. \u201cI work under an assumed name. Including you, I\u2019ve only told three people since\u2026 well, you know.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019d like to tell you something as well,\u201d I said, hoping to reciprocate her show of trust. \u201cIt\u2019s\u2026 not really on the same level as what you shared, but\u2026 Lorelei Grace is my real name now, but it isn\u2019t the name I was born with. I used to be Juliette Wells. My friends called me Jules.\u201d<br /> <br /> She smiled at me in the darkness. \u201cJuliette\u2026 it\u2019s a pretty name,\u201d she said.<br /> <br /> I smiled back. \u201cBut it\u2019s not really mine anymore. Juliette Wells is a fifty-four year old woman living with her husband in the Midwest. I\u2019m Lorelei Grace.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWouldn\u2019t have it any other way, babe,\u201d D said as she snuggled into my arms.<br /> <br /> \u201cMaria,\u201d I said, and it sounded less strange that time, \u201cI\u2019m not fishing for any particular answer here, but I\u2019d like to know how you see this relationship. Are we exclusive, or is it open?\u201d<br /> <br /> D stroked my stomach lightly as she thought about it. \u201cShit, I don\u2019t know, Lori. I\u2019m still trying to cope with the idea that there <u>is</u> an \u2018us.\u2019 I\u2019m usually all about free love and open relationships and all that modern shit, but\u2026\u201d Once again I saw the secret, shy, insecure side peek out, and she closed her eyes. \u201cI really don\u2019t want to fuck this up,\u201d she admitted.<br /> <br /> I stroked her hair, tracing the streak of purple, barely distinguishable from the sea of black hair surrounding it in the darkness. \u201cI feel the same way,\u201d I said. \u201cI\u2019m okay with open relationships, too, but\u2026 right now, I don\u2019t really <u>want</u> to be with anyone but you.\u201d I thought about that for a minute. \u201cHow about this: we\u2019ll treat it as exclusive for the time being, but if either one of us wants to spend time with someone else, it\u2019s an option as long as they discuss it with the other one first. Deal?\u201d<br /> <br /> D nodded. \u201cWorks for me. Just\u2026 promise me one thing, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cName it,\u201d I said.<br /> <br /> \u201cJust don\u2019t fuck Annika, okay? I don\u2019t think I could take that after the way Madame Spidertoes used to talk about her\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I almost laughed at the notion that I would ever sleep with that stuck-up posturing whore, but I could tell that D was really vulnerable at that moment, so I held it in. \u201cYou have <u>nothing</u> to worry about, Maria,\u201d I promised, and the name sounded right in my ears, \u201cshe\u2019s the last person in the world I\u2019d hop into bed with.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2019kay,\u201d she said with one more soft kiss. \u201cI\u2019m gonna get some shut-eye. Night, Lori. I\u2019m really glad you\u2019re here.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMe too, D,\u201d I said as I felt her warm breath blowing out against my neck. \u201cMe too.\u201d And then I fell asleep.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T23:07:46-07:00","id":217201,"title":"","content":"<b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> <b><u><b><u>Wednesday May 7<sup>th</sup></u></b> </u></b><br /> <br /> I must confess that I feel like a monster. Thanks Pandora... sometimes random coincidence fits just perfectly. Though tonight I am a tired monster. Skipping sleep does that. The night ended up passing without incident, but better safe than sorry and the strutting practice was oddly soothing. Gawain made me omelets for breakfast and I got to use my new mug, which was fun. Over breakfast we caught Lori and Jacob up on events with Andromeda. At one point, Ace suggested that I might need professional help. I think it was that comment about having a need to murder. Of course, I doubt it would do any good. Besides, where would something like me even begin to explain what's wrong to a therapist? Of course, as fucked up as we changelings tend to be, I'd imagine an ensorcelled shrink would clean up. Though I guess technically some of Darke's spook squad must be, given that they run a rehab clinic. Yeah, I think I'll take my chances with the madness thank you very much.<br /> <br /> Speaking of doctors, I need to call Austin in the morning. Dionisia suggested he'd be the one to talk to about picking up some birth control off the record, seeing as I lack a legal ID or a proper mundane name these days. I'm sure he'll help me out, after all I have no doubt he'll agree that the last thing anyone wants is for me to be pregnant. I need to go out and pick up my hunting outfit anyway, so hopefully I can take care of it at the same time.<br /> <br /> Yeah, so the hunting. We're going to be hunting briar-wolves. When he was calling to finalize their play-date at the pier, Captain Jack tipped Gawain off about it. Seems a pack of the bastards has taken to skulking around the outskirts of town and the Summer Court is offering a bounty on them. I must say, El Capit\u00e1n is alright in my book. The spectacle he and Gawain put on was epic. It was completely over the top and ridiculous but the pair of them pulled it off with style and flare. It seems a bit silly to be honest, but Gawain adores this whole feud thing they've got going. They're like a pair of oversized boys when they get to planning their next confrontation. I keep teasing Gawain about his 'boyfriend' but I really am glad he has someone bright like Jack in his life. He needs someone to get into shenanigans with. I lost that when I lost my Stasia. I swear, that girl could talk Katt into anything. She was the one that always got us into trouble and then I had to figure out how to get us out of it. <br /> <br /> But I got taken and the sinister bitch They left in my place hated her. She went out of her way to make Anastasia's life miserable. She delighted in hurting her. It churns my gut to read the vitriol she dripped onto these pages about Stasia. That's why I can't look for her. All she knows is that her best friend, her blood sister (boy was THAT one of her better ideas... seven stitches and a round of tetanus shots for us both...), just turned on her for no reason. The sinister bitch knew all of our secrets and used them to hurt her whenever she could. She ruined everything we'd shared, turned it rotten and vile and betrayed Anastasia's trust and confidence. When Lori asked me if I had ever been in love, it was my sweetling Stasia I thought of. I did love her like a sister and a friend and... well... we were only thirteen but I think we were well on our way to being even more than that. She was my first kiss. Sure, we were both tipsy off a contraband six pack of Zima (I wonder if they still make that stuff?) but it was soft and sweet and I can still remember what her lips tasted like. I remember the look in her eyes when she suggested with such well rehearsed casualness that we should try it just to see what everyone was making such a fuss about. I didn't know what it was at the time, but I do now. I can't bear the thought of seeing hate in those eyes instead, and what else could she feel for me? She doesn't know it wasn't her Kitty Katt that tormented her. No, I cannot face her. I shouldn't look for her. Whatever started that night withered and died. Just one more thing the Whispers and their abomination took from me. But some dark night, I will exact payment in blood from the sinister bitch for every tear she coaxed from my Stasia. And after that... I know the Whispering Voices can bleed. And what bleeds can be killed. I am not stupid though. I know I am not ready. Not by a long shot. But there will come a time when I am the monster that even They must fear. And some dark night, I will come for Them and make Them pay for what They did to Katt and all of those other innocent girls and boys. I will shatter Their precious Snow Globe. <br /> <br /> I do realize now why I feel such malice toward Haily. She reminds me of the girls who used to bully and tease Katt and Stasia, the kind of girl my fetch became. (Considering that she's a successful executive at a major marketing company, I imagine she's evolved from mean girl to bitch queen.) That's why I felt such a strong urge to stab the smug right off her face at the pier. But I did not and I will not. Not unless it turns out that she is guilty of something worse than being manipulative. I may not be able to ignore this hunger for pain but I can choose who I sate it on. I control the monster. The monster does not control me. <br /> <br /> That's why I'm looking forward to hunting the briar-wolves. They are cruel things that deserve to feel the kiss of my glass. I can let the monster run free and delight in their slaughter. Killing them is a service to the Freehold. Defeating them and collecting the bounty will boost Gawain's status. It will earn us some goodwill with the Summer Court. Hell, it might even impress Luna.<br /> <br /> Damn, it was good to hear her voice today. And, of course, she had solid advice on how best to deal with the hobgoblins. Keep the guns hidden until it's too late for them to escape and make sure those of us they can see appear weak. Hit them hard while they're toying with their prey. Not sure how good Gawain and some of the others are at hiding, but an ambush is certainly the best way to go. If they see our full numbers they might shy away. They're cowardly things that want victims they can play with rather than a fight. I'll bait the trap myself. If I cover up my armor and glass and the lads I'm small enough to seem weak. And if things don't go as planned, I can hold my own fighting or use my contracts to escape. Plus I am not going to put someone else at risk. Too bad we don't know the area well or have a map to plan with. I imagine there's something in the library or someone who might be familiar with the terrain but we are talking about doing this sooner rather than later. <br /> <br /> Of course, bounty hunting is also appealing because it's something I can do something about, unlike this business with Andromeda and The Table. Jacob was called in to speak with Master Darke. He claimed to be far more interested in making sure the table didn't fall into the wrong hands than anything else. Of course, while he doesn't want The Table, he is prepared to take it for safekeeping to be sure Lucien does not get a hold of it. He also warned Jacob that Lucien might try to kill him simply for being Winter Court and showed him what was left of the man he killed and then used to beat two others to death with. Damn that man is fucking hard core... I won't lie, hearing about that sent a shiver down my spine. Fuck, thinking about it <i>now</i> is making me squirmy. Jesus fucking Christ on the holy rascal I am screwed up. The man is ruthless... He's a soulless killing machine... He's a fucking <i>lawyer</i> for Hades\u2019 sake... But holy shit is he a magnificent bad-ass. I seriously hope we do not wind up fighting him any time soon. If the best efforts of Master Darke can't end that ogre I doubt we'd manage to pull it off. Unfortunately, I don't see any way to put The Table in Queen Charlotte's web without making an enemy of him. <br /> <br /> I think most of the motley is on board with the Autumn Court taking possession of The Table. We don't want Darke or Torrez to wind up with it and we really don't want the kind of heat we'd get from the other for making that happen. Princess Jolie has expressed no interest in it or who gets it. Andromeda cannot protect it from the forces that would come after it. We can't either to be honest and we have no idea how to destroy it. It's the logical choice. Of course, I have been promised favor if I make it happen, but if it wasn't (at least as far as I can tell) the right choice (okay, at least a good choice) I wouldn't be supporting it. Now if we just had some idea where the damnable thing was. Our best (only) lead still seems to be the elusive Mr Grey. According to Joan he used to be close (or as close as a super creepy alien that dissects you with his eyes gets) to a couple of his fellow Winter Courtiers, Dr Bright and Twitch. So, clearly talking to one of them about what happened seems like a logical move. But Bright is one of Darke's inner circle (hell, I've heard a rumor that they're the same person) so anything we say to him is going to Darke. Not that Darke wouldn't have thought to look for the The Table's previous operator but do we want to tip our hand that we're on that trail? I don't know anything about Twitch. He was at the opening night and I greeted him along with the other Winter Courtiers but that's the extent of my familiarity. If he was a friend of Grey's and Grey is on the out with his court he might help. Or he might try to protect him from us. Or maybe he's part of the mysterious rogue group that seems to have The Table along with Grey. Gah, I so prefer problems that can be solved with a good old fashioned face punching.<br /> <br /> So, on a more positive note, Annika seemed pleased with my progress earlier. She put me through some actual dance steps rather than just strutting practice and apparently next week we'll be working on crawling, and how it do so both dominantly and submissively. I do suspect Gawain will enjoy that, though I need to talk to him about this whole sweeping bit. It's not fooling anyone and if he's going to ogle me than I damn well expect his full attention. Insincere Marguerite's girl was there to do some sketching but I am not sure how much she got accomplished with her Mistress wrapped around her so possessively despite Jacob's efforts to maintain some decorum. She does seem sweet and she seems to be warming up to the rest of us, which is good as I think my Darkling sister has decided to keep her. I should, however, be a bit more mindful around her. I am pretty sure I unnerved her on the way home from the pier while I was venting my frustrations with Haily and all that face having and breathing she does. <br /> <br /> And on the subject of couples and happy things, I think De La Rocha and Lorelei are getting serious. They've been hanging out a lot recently and at the pier they were most certainly hanging on each other rather unabashedly while I was talking to Monica about the details of the briar-wolf bounty and fighting hobgoblins in general (and trying to ignore the way Haily was weaseling her way into the woman's attention. Why? Why does everyone always fall for those selfish self-centered bitches? I like Monica... she could do so much better than that little tramp.) After Gawain and Captain Jack had their extravaganza, Lori went home with De La Rocha. So yeah, it looks like I won't be helping Lori clean her wings again any time soon. But it's alright given how happy they seem together.<br /> <br /> Alright, tomorrow is going to be a long day and I am quite tired. But Gawain hasn't come to bed yet. I'm sure he wouldn't leave without saying goodnight so he's most likely at his forge. I should talk to him about moving his things from the apartment at some point. He's a member of the Last Dance and it seems pretty clear we've both developed a fondness for sharing a bed. Well, I know I have... Though I guess it's selfish of me to expect him to come to bed early tonight when I never came to bed last night. And I wasn't even here the night before that because I was with Andromeda. Yeah... I really need to work on this whole relationship thing don't I? Well, selfish monster that I am, I'm going to go find him and at least claim a goodnight kiss before I pass out. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Today has been an interesting day, and by that I mean something along the lines of the Chinese curse. Well, it wasn\u2019t a horrible day, but we found out a lot of stuff and things are going to get \u201cinteresting\u201d really soon around here. Remind me again why I moved here? Oh yeah, Elena. Funny that. Right now I have the feeling I would be keeping my sister safer if I had not arrived, but I know the blame does not fall entirely on my shoulders. All this shit would be going on in this town regardless of my presence. At least I got a promise out of Master Darke to keep my sister safe if things should become dangerous. I made that arrangement because of a general need to keep my sister safe. I didn\u2019t think that bargain might be coming up so soon though. Here\u2019s hoping it won\u2019t.<br /> <br /> So, to explain the whole \u201cinteresting\u201d times comment. Master Darke called me pretty early this morning. I was up, getting ready to make coffee, so I picked it right up. He said that he wanted to meet with me today at his office in the clinic at 1:00pm this afternoon. He said that he has some things he wanted to discuss with me, so I said \u201csure\u201d and agreed to meet him at the clinic. So, right off I was on edge. Not the best way to start the morning. Then other folks started coming in. Gawain made his way into the kitchen looking a little worse for wear. It looked like he had a rough night of it, so as he commented on what he was going to make for breakfast I started pulling out the eggs and veggies for the omelets. I also got out one of the larger mugs and made up a coffee for him the way he likes it. There\u2019s not much I could do at the moment to relieve the bad night he had, but I figured I could at least make the morning easier for him.<br /> <br /> Andromeda also wandered in as the coffee finished brewing and we all sat down to talk. Gawain and the others told us what happened while Lorelei and I were roller skating yesterday. Apparently we missed a good bit. So, the others had a talk with Andromeda about the rumors surrounding her and Hailey. Apparently Andromeda was a good little servant to the Mother Ship and used a device called \u201cThe Table\u201d to change people. She was the one to \u201cchange\u201d Hailey, but had a crush on her so tried to make the procedure as painless as possible. Hailey seemed to return her maker\u2019s affections, but was apparently pretending so she could be allowed more room to move. When the time was right she fled to \u201cthe world.\u201d Andromeda followed, bringing the Table with her, with the intention of \u201cfixing\u201d whatever was wrong with Hailey to make her run in the first place. Shortly after arriving the Table was stolen from her. Then she found Hailey and discovered that the other girl had told the local Changelings about her and what happened. Andromeda said that she realized that she didn\u2019t want to go back to the Mother Ship and that what happened there was wrong.<br /> <br /> Most of the others seemed to believe her story. Calamity I know is protective of the girl. I don\u2019t doubt that she would take action if Andromeda proved to be a traitor, but for the moment she seems keen on keeping the slight girl safe. For the most part the others seem to feel the same. Lorelei looked like she still had some reservations about the whole thing. The others even brought up the fact that Joan, Ms. Paranoia herself, was inclined to believe that Andromeda was telling the truth. I think she was suspicious of Hailey due to inconsistencies in the girl\u2019s story. Details changed when Andromeda showed up in town. I\u2019m not sure what I think. I would like to believe that Andromeda is as innocent as she appears and that Hailey is nothing more than a victim in this whole thing. I think that the truth is more complicated than that though. I am inclined to keep my doubts to myself for the moment and voice them if I see something that looks suspicious. I will keep my eyes open around both girls. I will say though, that if Andromeda betrays our trust she will wish that I was wasn\u2019t so well versed in the art of causing pain.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I could say that I\u2019m a hypocrite in some ways for that. I betrayed a lot of people in my time. I\u2019m not overly proud of that fact, but I won\u2019t hide that fact from myself. Granted most of the people that I betrayed were already in Arcadia at the time. There was only a few that I tricked into coming back to the Lady\u2019s realm while in \u201cthe world.\u201d Most of the time I just took them by force. Yeah, so all of that is going through my head while the others were talking about Andromeda and her little tale of woe. I\u2019m a trickster, well used to be more of one than I am now, so I know how this works. I know the bullshit that people pull. I will admit that Andromeda doesn\u2019t seem to be lying. In fact she doesn\u2019t seem like much of a liar at all, but that doesn\u2019t mean that she\u2019s not a pawn in a bigger game. I guess time will tell.<br /> <br /> Okay\u2026so about my meeting with Master Darke. Gawain offered to ride with me to the clinic as I drove, as a way to practice. I took him up on the offer. I will admit that it was fun. I was a bit nervous, but at least it was a more benign kind of nervous than I had been before when I was worrying about my meeting with Master Darke. Once we arrived the fear of hitting telephone poles was replaced by my original nervousness about talking to the winter monarch. \u2018Cause yeah, that man is scary and the meeting today did nothing to dissuade me of that notion. When I was escorted into his office it was pretty much completely dark except for a single light over the desk. This left Master Darke in shadow, sitting behind his desk. Yeah, creepy.<br /> <br /> So, turns out that Master Darke wanted to talk about the situation with Andromeda and the Table. Well, mostly the Table. He was very keen on the summer courtier, Lucien Torrez not getting it. Very keen. Like, holy shit scary keen. He went on to describe how dangerous Lucien is and then showed me some of the man\u2019s \u201chandiwork.\u201d It was some poor sod that Lucien had literally torn to pieces, then beat another man to death with the first guys corpse. He actually brought out what was left of the man and displayed it like proof to a court. I\u2019m just sayin\u2019, a photograph would have done just as well. Really. Though I suppose there is nothing quite as impactful as an actual body (or what\u2019s left of one) laying out in front of you.<br /> <br /> Okay, so he was really big on Torrez not getting the Table. He didn\u2019t want the Spring court to get it either. He was ambivalent about the Autumn court getting it, and said that the Winter court didn\u2019t have any particular desire for it either. I\u2019m not so sure about that myself, but I didn\u2019t say anything while there. I didn\u2019t figure that would be very politic of me. I agreed to let him know if we came across the Table or to destroy it if we could. He didn\u2019t seem convinced that it was possible to break the thing, but he seemed okay with that option if it came to it. Given that it is an Arcadian artifact I don\u2019t know if our Motley can make a dent in it. Maybe the Autumn court would have an idea on how to do it? I guess we can ask if we find the thing. Honestly I\u2019m not sure if I want to be the one to find it. I have a feeling there are going to be several conflicting parties interested in it. Darke may say that he doesn\u2019t want it, but I think he actually does. He is afraid of what Torrez would do with it, that much is abundantly clear.<br /> <br /> Master Darke has something personal against Torrez though, and apparently the other way around as well. From what Darke said, Torrez has been trying to put a stop to the Winter court\u2019s drug business and is hurting and/or killing people to do it. That\u2019s where the body-turned-weapon came from. Torrez attacked a group of dealers and pulled them apart. There are more subtle or at least less messy ways to put a stop to the drug running, but I don\u2019t get the impression that Torrez does \u201csubtle.\u201d I think Master Darke telling me this was also a kind of warning for me. I don\u2019t deal much, but I do deal so I guess I need to keep an eye open for Torrez or any of his guys that might decide they don\u2019t like my side business or me. Yeah, more things to keep an eye on, and that\u2019s not even the best of it.<br /> <br /> I was also informed that the Winter court had become aware of a Loyalist watching my Motley mates and me. Apparently there are drop points in the hedge that the Winter court has found and read the messages there. They put the missives back so the Loyalist or Gentry do not know that it has been compromised. The gist of the messages is that this Loyalist is watching us and has decided that while Ace and Calamity would not be good to approach, Insincere Marguerite and I would be. I really don\u2019t like the idea that a Gentry or their loyal servant is interested in me, or Marguerite for that matter. I asked if Master Darke knew which Gentry the Loyalist served, but he didn\u2019t know. I don\u2019t think he\u2019d keep it from me if he did know the name or title of the Gentry in question. Hopefully more information can be gleaned from future messages. What is the phrase? I have my fingers crossed.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t like the idea that people are watching me, and I really don\u2019t like the idea that I am considered approachable. Okay\u2026that\u2019s not exactly true. I know why I would be considered \u201capproachable,\u201d but I think it is worrying that someone else has the same idea. I had hoped that I had made myself look fairly innocent and uncertain, rather than sympathetic to the Gentry. So, it could be that someone knows of my past and figures that I might like to come back to serve the Lady, or one of her enemies since I did not leave her service on the best of terms. Or they are interested in me for other reasons like skill set or personality. I just don\u2019t know, and it makes me feel edgy. Part of me is afraid that it is the Lady looking for me. I don\u2019t know why she would be interested in Insincere Marguerite as well, but I guess I still have that fear in the back of my mind. I do not want to go back to her. I will admit to being afraid that she would torture me for my deceit and escape, then kill me if I\u2019m lucky. Yeah, that would be the better option. The worse option is that she would make good on her word to break me and remake me like she planned to do before. I can deal with pain. I have had plenty of practice with that. I just really don\u2019t want to lose who I am. The idea of being remade and going back to who and what I was scares the shit out of me. I can\u2019t let that happen. I won\u2019t let it happen.<br /> <br /> So\u2026.after that \u201coh so enlightening\u201d conversation with Darke I was escorted out and met Gawain at the van. We drove back to the Dream House and I told everyone what Master Darke had told me. Well, most of it anyway. I told them about Darke\u2019s supposed \u201cnot interest\u201d in the Table. His desire that Torrez not get it and his ambivalence about the Autumn court. There was some discussion about Torrez and Darke, and a bit about what we might do if we found the Table. <br /> <br /> I took Insincere Marguerite aside, up on the catwalk, and told her about the Loyalist watching the Motley, and in particular, us. She nodded and for the most part seemed unconcerned. She mostly looked annoyed. At the idea of working for a Gentry or the implication that she would, I\u2019m not sure. Other than that she didn\u2019t seemed overly worried. As I started to go back down she looked at me for a moment and said that she\u2019d keep me safe and gave me a hug. I was a bit surprised, but who am I to turn down a hug? I guess I must have let my mask slip for a bit if she picked up on my edginess. Either that or she\u2019s getting better at reading me.<br /> <br /> After I had talked to the group about what Master Darke had said and we\u2019d had our discussion, Lorelei said that she was going to talk to Princess Jolie. I asked if I could talk to her real quick before she left. I told her what Darke had said about liking to keep some amount of chaos among the monarchies of the different courts. I also mentioned what he\u2019d said about Jolie\u2019s past and the implications that she harmed artists. I thought she might want to know what had been said about her, and also figured she might want to know about her monarch\u2019s past activities just in case. Lorelei is an artist after all. I don\u2019t know how much of the stuff he told me about Jolie and Charlotte is true. Supposedly Jolie sucks the souls out of artists and Charlotte kills and eats people. Maybe they make a good pair in more than one way? Kinda scary if it\u2019s true. That said, it\u2019s not like Master Darke is any less scary. That man has creepy down to an art form, and I have no doubt in my mind that he is just as dangerous as Torrez, just more subtle. Just my luck.<br /> <br /> Then, on a more positive note, to wrap up the day we all went to the pier. Gawain and Captain Jack had something planned, but he wouldn\u2019t say what it was. Gawain and Calamity went over to talk to Joan. I walked with Insincere Marguerite and Julia for a bit before walking off on my own. Lorelei met up with De la Rocha. The other girl ran up to our Spring courtier and they kissed, and wrapped limbs around one another. It was awfully cute. Then De la Rocha said something to Lorelei that made her whole face light up. Two genuine smiles in as many days. I\u2019m glad I got to see it, not to mention a bit curious what they were talking about. I guess I\u2019ll find out later.<br /> <br /> Turns out the whole plan between Gawain and Captain Jack involved the other guy getting flown in on a helicopter. Not in it, but under it. Hanging from a rope ladder! He then jumped off and strode towards Gawain. He was wearing a pair of white costume wings, which he took off and handed to me as he walked past. He paused for a moment to give me the gift and flirt a bit. He asked me out for a drink later and I politely turned him down. He shrugged, smiled then headed on over to Gawain. There were words, there was some posturing, then Captain Jack grabbed the \u201cNo Fishing\u201d sign from the end of the pier and clocked Gawain with it, knocking him into the water. He then put the sign back and started fishing since the \u201cNo\u201d part of the sign had broken off. Convenient that. I might have been concerned if I hadn\u2019t seen Gawain handing off his phone and wallet to Calamity when we first arrived. He had said he didn\u2019t want to get them wet. I guess I know why.<br /> <br /> I checked to make sure that Gawain was getting to shore okay by himself before making my way over to De la Rocha and Lorelei. I greeted them and then gave the set of wings to the darker girl. I commented that they could be a matched set. I left before I could really gauge their reaction. I thought it was cute anyway.<br /> <br /> Oh\u2026I almost forgot. Gawain brought up something that he thought the motley might be interested in. He found out about a bounty that the Summer court had put out to hunt down and kill some Briar wolves that were causing some problems in the hedge. I think Jack told him about it. Anyway, it sounded like a good way to help the community, make a name for ourselves, and work out some tensions. Yeah, I got plenty of tension to work out. All the shit going on with the Table, Andromeda and Hailey, Loyalists watching me, and Lucien Torrez hunting down dealers. I think that constitutes tension. Maybe, if we don\u2019t go looking for those wolves soon, I can ask Calamity if she wants to spar again? I definitely want to do that again soon. <br /> <br /> And since I can\u2019t spar or kill wolves right now, I think I\u2019m going to have a drink or three and go to sleep. Alcohol is not the best answer, but it takes the edge off and dulls the dreams. Both of which are good things.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> Today was a fairly normal day, without much in the way of issues. Mostly.<br /> <br /> I woke this afternoon to find that Master Darke summoned Jacob for a meeting. I had fears, mostly revolving around Andromeda\u2019s role, but it turned out to be no big deal\u2026he just wanted to give his side of the story, complete, of course, with implicit threats. Naturally. Jacob did say he and I were determined most likely to be recruitable by loyalists, according to their intelligence. Allegedly. I am sort of put off by that. I work for no Gentry, and am disinterested in changing that. He was concerned however, and was kind enough to say it. I searched his eyes and saw nervousness, but not much I could do but give him a hug and promise to look out for him. Definitely.<br /> <br /> We spoke away from the puppets, for privacy.<br /> <br /> Julia came by, as did Annika. Annika was there teach Calamity, while Julia was there to sketch. She did get to sketch I, Calamity and Annika, but not Lorelei as she went to go speak to the Princess Jolie. Apparently. I distracted Julia, kissing her and wrapping around her. Her smell is intoxicating, and my hormones, well, far overpowered my dignity. Mostly. Jacob was there, and he seemed to try to keep me from being too possessive, which is good. In retrospect, it seems\u2026unkind to cuddle with my girlfriend right there at him, but at the same time he chose to sit with us and I did not wish to ask him to leave. I don\u2019t know. Artists are so\u2026well, talented. Deliciously.<br /> <br /> We sipped water together. With bubbles.<br /> <br /> I did manage to pull away a bit when Lorelei returned with a long face. She said she may have upset her Monarch, but seemed disinclined to go into detail. I searched her eyes as well. I do understand the Spring Court fairly well, but I could not fathom what she did and could not help, and did not wish to ask.<br /> <br /> Julia also distracted I. Significantly.<br /> <br /> I am concerned about Lorelei, Jacob and Calamity. Lorelei puts a lot, too much in fact, stock in what people think of her, and someone like her Monarch being upset with her must be a blow. I am not sure this little grub can make her feel better. Jacob I still don\u2019t feel like I really know what is going on. I search his eyes a lot, but while he is more affectionate he keeps me at arms length. Just perhaps with a slightly bent elbow compared to the rest of the Motley. I\u2019ve not slept with him again. I want the birth control to have time to, uh, control births, maybe? Calamity needs to realize she can be the monster her Keeper made, or actually stand up and be what she wants to be. She just needs to decide if she actually wants to have a spine or not. I should talk to her about it, but not put it in confrontational terms. She will never be a child of the light any more than I, but we can decide how we want to feel the shadow\u2019s love, and if she wants to be a bloodthirsty killer of those who escape their Keeper, as her Keeper would no doubt approve of, that is her prerogative. Or she could rebel in a way that is actually neither easy nor comfortable. Either or.<br /> <br /> After all, if her Keeper just told Katt to kill people she would have refused. No no, Calamity was, I believe, a blade carefully forged. Probably.<br /> <br /> Ace and Gawain seem okay. Oh it came up that Lucian had given Ace a hand grenade. Americans.<br /> <br /> I have never been the sort of person who rushes things, but we all discussed going to the pier and, well, not to put to fine a point on it, I was not going to make it. I took Julia up to my room and we had sex on the floor just inside the door. Of course she accidentally pulled my hair laying her leg on it and I accidentally kicked my door rather solidly, but it was fun if intense. I felt her nails dig in my leg, and a little blood running down from her intensity. She howled like an animal; Nightsinger you know. I am pretty sure had anyone been around they would have thought we were having a brawl. Then we had a shower, and then she helped I pick an outfit. I wore some of my new long socks, with little crescent moons on it with nightcaps, and some shorts and a black short sleeve button up shirt. The feet cut out of the socks of course. Naturally.<br /> <br /> A touch cooled down, we all rode together to the pier. Mostly. Lorelei anticipated picking up De La Rocha so she drove separately. Julia sat with us, and she seemed so very happy. Julia usually avoids people. She likes to sit by herself and sketch, so this is taking some real effort for her. But she did well. She even spoke up to the others without prompting. I am so proud. Mostly.<br /> <br /> She had my teethmarks on her leg. I was happy.<br /> <br /> On Pier, we split up and had fun. Jacob hung out with Julia and I for awhile, so I minded my manners while he was there. Calamity and Lorelei went to speak to De La Rocha, Monica, and Hailey. Lorelei and De La Rocha paired off quickly, and actually displayed a lot of affection more publicly than before. I mean, I had seen them kiss, but not quite so openly. Calamity chatted with Monica, and did not quite snub Hailey. Meanwhile Gawain and Ace spoke with Joan, in what was apparently a fairly good conversation.<br /> <br /> I think Madame Spidertoes may have been watching me. Definitely.<br /> <br /> Then Captain Jack showed up, was lowered from a helicopter, and had a brawl with Gawain. It really was something to see. Somewhere in there, Ace flagged Jacob down, and Julia and I seized the opportunity to what De La Rocha and Lorelei were doing. Happily.<br /> <br /> Once he had tossed Gawain over the side, done some fishing, and fled we withdrew. Lorelei went off with De La Rocha to I think her place, and the rest of us discussed findings. Calamity made Julia nervous with her talk of, well, killing Hailey.<br /> <br /> In truth, I don\u2019t understand why she hates Hailey so much. Mostly. Yes, Hailey seduced and abandoned Andromeda. But Andromeda warped Hailey into what she became, apparently with gusto. Hailey used her wits and wiles to trick her Keeper\u2019s loyal minion into leaving her where she could escape. When the loyal minion appeared looking for her, she rightly told the Freehold. Now it turns out Andromeda had a change of heart but still, everything I know for sure Hailey did was somewhere between practical and laudable. Mostly.<br /> <br /> Joan, not exactly known for practically, also dislikes Hailey. I suppose we will have to see what happens with that. Tomorrow, however, we hunt Briarwolves. Probably. I am not exactly looking forward to it, but eh, it\u2019s a chance for Gawain to get some recognition and Calamity to kill something. Both of those are good things. Maybe.<br /> <br /> Tonight, my lovely trembling artist and I retired to my room. Rather than the visceral driven hunger of earlier there was gentleness. We kissed. We whispered things to one another. Some romantic. Some frightening. Then we slept. Mostly.<br /> <br /> I hope today ends as well.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session IX</i><br /> <br /> Mostly role-playing, not as much to comment on.<br /> <br /> So we should have the session as per today, but I am not sure exactly when I will be getting it out to you. We will probably have no session for the next time; I am going to be at Gen Con that weekend, and the usual alternate day is part of the same weekend. Thus I will also be out when the day comes to put journals up. You will assuredly get them, but maybe late. If you are coming to Gen Con, I will be at the Onyx Path booth much of the time, and would love to meet some of those enjoying the APs. Sadly none of the players will be there. Still, feel free to come say hi.<br /> <br /> Okay, well that is it for now. Comments and Questions welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T16:09:18-07:00","id":235841,"title":"","content":"Hello folks. This is seriously delayed in terms of being put up, but last week I moved and also Gen Con happened. I\u2019m just now getting settled back in so I can start making much use of the forums, and hey, journals to put up. The good news is we had Changeling last night, so huzzah! No bad new really, beyond the delay. But here you go, enjoy.<br /> <br /> <i>Session X</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> May 8th<br /> <br /> So, I\u2019ve never been told I had to save someone with my penis before. It\u2019s, well, flattering, I guess? I mean, what De la Roche said Monica said about me certainly was. But it seems not fair, you know, to sleep with Monica again just to fuck up Hailey\u2019s day. Not that I wouldn't like to sleep with Monica again, just, you know, not for that reason. I think Calamity understood, even if she was a little disappointed. Hailey really likes Monica though, since she found her and promised to protect her, you know? Which seems fair, as long as Hailey\u2019s not a loyalist.<br /> <br /> We did get to see the two of them again and I met another maybe-loyalist. She was really nice though. See, De la Roche was over for breakfast again. Lori made a big deal about asking me if it was ok this time. I guess I was pretty snippy before. I shouldn\u2019t have been, I don\u2019t mind cooking for the motley or any of their friends. But that day, with the nightmares and her rubbing it in about having had company the night before... I guess I was just a little grumpy. I had nightmares last night too, but between waking up with Calamity in her bed and having a picture on my phone from Jacob of her and me kissing that first time in the forge, I wasn\u2019t very grumpy by the time I started making pancakes and bacon for breakfast.<br /> <br /> Anyways, De la Roche told us we ought to come check out the Rose and Thorn, the other big Changeling night life type place, run by Flores, a Spring Court friend of De la Roche\u2019s. She\u2019s really nice and pretty cute too - she smells amazing, like flowers, you know? So we decided to check it out, then go briar wolf hunting. This, of course, called for a shopping trip. Me, Jacob and Ace totally had all sorts of guy things to do, like sharpen swords and knives and set up the gym, so we left Lori and Calamity to that. Julia and Insincere Margeurite stuck around the House too, watching us working mostly. I also called Captain Jack, since he hangs out at the Rose and Thorn and I didn\u2019t want to surprise him in public, you know? We decided to just pretend like there was no feud, if anyone asked, just for tonight.<br /> <br /> It did also cheer me up this morning thinking about what Ace\u2019s breakfast would be. He didn\u2019t disappoint, that\u2019s for sure. He had a whole tomato, a few pickle spears and another raw egg. Since the others pointed it out, the whole snake/raw egg thing has made... more sense? But snakes don\u2019t eat tomatoes and pickles. I don\u2019t think they do, anyway. And I\u2019m even more sure they don't eat Cheerios in OJ. Not with OJ. In OJ. He is a strange, strange man.<br /> <br /> Anyways, we totally hit up the Rose and Thorn all punked out. Well, the girls did. Me and Jacob were just dressed normally and Ace, well, he really did look like he came out of Mad Max with leather straps and buckles and spikes. Calamity looked a-mazing. She even put on makeup for the first time I\u2019d seen. She was super hot. Not that she isn\u2019t always, but, you know. I guess Insincere Marguerite wasn\u2019t all punked out either, so it was really just Calamity and Lori and De la Roche. Insincere Marguerite was in an awesome corset shirt thing of Julia\u2019s, that she was, well, falling out of. She looked a little embarrassed about it even, which was new - I didn\u2019t think she could get embarrassed. It seemed mean to tease her about it though. Regardless, Julia certainly enjoyed it, which seems fair, considering Insincere Marguerite was petting Julia\u2019s hair with her feet while we were all together eating breakfast this morning. And really, I doubt Insincere Marguerite minds since I only have time to write this cause of how much Julia enjoyed it and wanted to express her enjoyment.<br /> <br /> The Rose and Thorn was awesome, tons of dancing space, a killer bar, and a giant aquarium room thing, right in the middle of the ceiling. I think it started giving Ace ideas, but first apparently he had to fix the fact that he was not drunk enough for his feet. Jacob went to the bar first too, but then he went and talked with the other Night Court lady in the catwalks. Lori got showed off by De la Roche and everyone was envious, especially once she started dancing. Calamity wandered off to talk with the other Autumn Court member there, Ginny, so I went to say hi to one of the Changelings there I hadn\u2019t seen before.<br /> <br /> She was very nice, and named Desiree. I tried to break the ice by asking about the area as a new guy in town, but it mostly got her talking about her Keeper, the Director that Joan had told us about. Apparently, all the other Changelings from her Keeper have been loyalists. Like, all all. The one she escaped with was one even, though that was weird - Desiree said the other one only started talking about recruiting after they got out. See, she ran away cause she was next in line for a \u201cstarring role\u201d and everybody else that got one were all weird after. The girl who escaped with her was second in line. She turned her friend in and everything, since she started talking about recruiting, you know? So Joan\u2019s not allowed to kill her, since there\u2019s no proof or anything. Joan does want to though, and has told her so. At least she\u2019s honest? I dunno. I did ask about the contest thing, since Desiree is Spring Court, you know, and she did confirm it. So she\u2019s not paranoid about that at least...<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not just Joan that\u2019s paranoid about Desiree though, cause everybody warned me about her. Well, both Monica and De la Roche did. De la Roche also warned us all about Madame Spidertoes. Thankfully, she doesn\u2019t like dudes, cause she seems kinda scary. Intense, you know? Plus, spiders watch while she\u2019s having sex with you and that\u2019s just... strange. She was mixed up a little with the burlesque place that was at the Dream House before us. The Golden Swan was the dude who ran it, and before he died there was a different Spring and Summer King. But the Summer King was was a douche who thought they should just let Golden Swan die cause he was gay, so Lucian hit the King with his own desk until he abdicated.<br /> <br /> The Spring King was Austin. He made a vow to save Golden Swan, but then the Summer douche forbade anyone from helping, so Austin had to go alone and was too late getting back. So that was the vow he broke, that Calamity figured out. That\u2019s also why he abdicated. Annike was torn up pretty badly too, she\u2019s been a shut in since then, until our opening night. She didn\u2019t even come out to eat, Madame Spidertoes arranged food to be delivered and everything.<br /> <br /> De la Roche\u2019s story did make me think a little better of Lucian. He sticks up for the local Latino community too. And I guess lots of girls think he\u2019s hot? Gunnar likes him too, even though they\u2019re not sleeping together (according to De la Roche). So he\u2019s got some redeeming qualities. And of course, like De la Roche and Joan said, a murderous psychopath\u2019s not the worst thing to have on your side when fighting against things like the Gentry, you know? So long as he is on our side and Madame Spidertoes isn\u2019t right about him being blackmailed out of being the Summer King after the douchebag abdicated. Cause I think I kinda agree with De la Roche, I\u2019m not sure what he would care about hiding, other than being a loyalist. But who would know he was a loyalist and do nothing except keep him from becoming King with that knowledge? I think, if Madame Spidertoes is kinda right and he did actually want to be King, maybe he\u2019s protecting someone.<br /> <br /> Anyways, now it\u2019s time to hunt briar wolves. De la Roche is coming with us and Calamity learned more about them, from her friend Luna - that they are cowardly bullies, and like ambushes and playing with their food, so we\u2019re going to turn it around on them. Me and Lori are going to be bait. I don\u2019t precisely look the most vulnerable or anything, but one, I\u2019m the worst at sneaking, two, I don\u2019t like the idea of leaving Lori alone, even as a trick and, three, I\u2019m going to pretend to be distracted, like me and Lori are out on a date, you know, like a horror movie setup or something. I won\u2019t even have my sword with me, which maybe makes me the most nervous, but Calamity will be holding on to it for me so when the ambush happens, it\u2019ll be there. Also, I sharpened up a knife that\u2019ll be in our picnic basket just in case. Anyways, we\u2019re gonna be able to send the wolves packing, no problemo, and Calamity will get to stab things.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> I woke up this morning about 10:00am in a very dark, unfamiliar room. The lean feminine form nuzzled up next to me, on the other hand, I recognized immediately. My head was tucked into the crook of her arm, my hand draped across her toned stomach. I slowly began stroking it back and forth, marveling at how tight her abs were without sacrificing an ounce of femininity.<br /> <br /> Of course, thinking about D\u2019s body soon got me all hot and bothered, and I slithered down to the foot of the bed to give her a wake-up call she wouldn\u2019t soon forget. I started out gently, slowly, lovingly\u2026 but her lack of reaction soon had me turning up the heat. A few minutes later, when she <u>still</u> displayed no sign of waking up, I glanced up at her face. Her eyes were closed, but she had the biggest shit-eating grin on her face.<br /> <br /> \u201cKeep it up, wise-ass,\u201d I said, licking my lips, \u201cand I\u2019ll stop.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t you dare,\u201d she admonished.<br /> <br /> Five minutes later, Maria was shouting something in Spanish. I have no idea what she said, but it sounded remarkably dirty. A few seconds after that, she reached down, grabbed my shoulders, flipped me onto the bed beside her (remarkably gently, considering the strength she put behind the maneuver), and returned the favor. My own reactions to her skilled ministrations were sadly confined to English.<br /> <br /> A few minutes later we were holding each other and sharing soft kisses. \u201cSo,\u201d I said as she was staring at me with those <u>amazing</u> grey-blue eyes of hers, \u201cyou want to head back to the Dream House with me for a late breakfast, or have you already had your fill?\u201d I giggled a little at the unintentional joke.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll never get enough,\u201d she said. \u201cNever, never, never.\u201d She punctuated each word with a kiss. \u201cBreakfast sounds great, if you think your friends won\u2019t mind. Just let me throw something on\u2026 or do you think we should head over like this?\u201d She smirked.<br /> <br /> I laughed. \u201cIt would give them a thrill. I\u2019m pretty sure every member of the motley likes looking at hot naked girls. But we might get stopped on the way, and I\u2019m not sure I want to explain that sort of thing to the cops at this point in my life.\u201d<br /> <br /> She stuck her tongue out at me. \u201cYou\u2019re no fun,\u201d she teased as she climbed out of bed and walked across the room to her dresser. For my part, I just relaxed and enjoyed the view for a while.<br /> <br /> We pulled up to the Dream House about 11:00am and walked into the kitchen to the smell of bacon and pancakes. After greetings had been exchanged, I walked up to Gawain in what I hope he took as a posture of gently teasing contrition. After my faux pas the other day, I wanted to make sure he understood that I wasn\u2019t taking him for granted any more.<br /> <br /> \u201cPlease, Mr. Gawain, sir,\u201d I said, \u201ccan my girlfriend stay over for breakfast?\u201d He allowed as how she could, and set about making a few more pancakes.<br /> <br /> As we devoured the tasty morsels, talk turned to our upcoming hunt for the local briar wolves. Our current plan is to have Gawain and myself draw the wolves out and lead them into an ambush while the others lie in wait. Calamity offered to act the part of bait in my place, and was really concerned about putting me in danger (that sweetie-pie), but I\u2019m no good at hiding, and I want to be close in case anyone needs healing. Looking helpless and drawing attention to myself are two things I\u2019m fairly good at, anyway.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou want me to come with?\u201d D asked. Her voice was nonchalant, but I caught a glimpse of something in her eyes. It wasn\u2019t fear\u2026 not even worry, really. I\u2019ll just call it concern and move on.<br /> <br /> The others were fine with it, though some of them had some questions. \u201cYou know how to fight?\u201d Calamity asked pointedly.<br /> <br /> \u201cI can take care of myself,\u201d D answered.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat style of fighting do you use?\u201d Jacob inquired.<br /> <br /> D grinned. \u201cFinger to the eye, jab to the throat, knee to the groin,\u201d she answered.<br /> <br /> Calamity shrugged. \u201cThe more the merrier,\u201d she commented.<br /> <br /> I turned to D and took her hands in my own. \u201cYou don\u2019t have to do this to impress me,\u201d I told her fervently. \u201cDon\u2019t get me wrong, I\u2019ll use any excuse to spend time with you, but this could be dangerous. I only want you to come along if you really want to.\u201d<br /> <br /> Her face turned serious for a minute. \u201cHey, I volunteered,\u201d she reminded me. \u201cBesides, if I didn\u2019t go with you, I\u2019d just sit around and worry until you got back. Not my style, babe.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, if you\u2019re sure,\u201d I replied, and kissed her lightly on the cheek.<br /> <br /> \u201cOnly thing is, I was gonna ask if you guys wanted to join me at the Rose and Thorn tonight,\u201d she admitted. \u201cA bunch of my friends hang out there most nights, and I thought I could introduce you around a bit before you all got tied up with the weekend shows.\u201d<br /> <br /> I looked at the others. Marguerite shrugged. \u201cWho is to say we cannot do both?\u201d she asked. \u201cThe night is long, no?\u201d<br /> <br /> The rest of the group agreed to this plan after a quick huddle, and I turned back to D. \u201cWhat\u2019s the dress code?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhatever you want,\u201d she replied. \u201cI usually go pretty punked out, but I guess that\u2019s hardly surprising.\u201d<br /> <br /> Calamity looked uncertain. \u201cI don\u2019t have many nice clothes,\u201d she said slowly, \u201cand I don\u2019t want to wear one of my Dream House outfits to the club.\u201d<br /> <br /> I could feel my own eyes light up at the prospect. \u201cShopping trip!\u201d I said brightly. What can I say? I lived my first eighteen years in a town of four hundred people, then spent God-knows-how-long naked in a birdcage. Now I live spitting distance from some of the nicest boutiques in America. So sue me if I choose to enjoy it.<br /> <br /> So D, Calamity and I hit the town while the boys opted to stay behind and start setting up a gym in the basement. Julia and Insincere Marguerite also stayed behind\u2026 mostly to watch the boys get all sweaty, I think (which is a perfectly valid choice, of course). Although, come to think of it, behind the Mask Ace is a reptile, Gawain is a suit of armor, and Jacob\u2019s skin is covered by a fine layer of frost. I wonder if any of them <u>do</u> sweat.<br /> <br /> While I did help Calamity out a bit in picking out her new outfit, I mostly let D take the lead when shopping for myself. She selected a pretty daring punk-style ensemble, with leather boots, fishnet stockings, and a black leather corset and bustier combination that showed my figure to its best advantage. In all honesty, it was fairly similar to one of the outfits I wore my first night on stage at the Dream House.<br /> <br /> So by the time we got back to the house, dressed, helped Calamity with her makeup, and did our own makeup, it was pretty much time to head out. Julia and Marguerite had also been playing dress-up while we were out, and the shy girl had managed to squeeze our French colleague into a corset which was frankly a bit frightening. It did\u2026 nice things to Marguerite\u2019s bust, I admit, but\u2026 <u>ouch</u>.<br /> <br /> The guys, of course, threw on T-shirts and jeans and called it a day. Sigh.<br /> <br /> We all piled into Gawain\u2019s van and drove across town to the club. The Rose and Thorn is a nice place, with multiple dance floors and several levels of balconies for spectators. One of the dance floors even had aquariums in the ceiling above it, which made for an interesting experience to say the least. In any case, though we jokingly told Flores that we were \u201cchecking out the competition,\u201d the club offers a very different sort of evening than the Dream House, so I don\u2019t think we\u2019re going to step on each other\u2019s toes too much.<br /> <br /> I noticed that amongst the patrons of the club were two distinct cliques. One seemed to be composed mostly of Hispanic people (both Changelings and mortals), while the other seemed to represent the area\u2019s Chinese population in a similar fashion. They didn\u2019t seem to be hostile to each other, though they didn\u2019t tend to mix much either. After we\u2019d greeted our hostess, D dragged me off toward the former group.<br /> <br /> \u201cHey, wait a minute,\u201d I said mock-angrily. \u201cDid you just drag me out here tonight to show me off to your friends? Am I just some glorified arm-candy?\u201d<br /> <br /> She must have caught something in my tone, because she grinned. \u201cYeah, that pretty much sums it up,\u201d she replied. \u201cIs that a problem, babe?\u201d<br /> <br /> Already she knows how much I love being the center of attention, and she\u2019s bending my psychological quirks to her own nefarious ends! I really like this girl.<br /> <br /> So D introduced me to a lot of terribly nice people, calling me her girlfriend and being very openly affectionate all the while. I think she might be overcompensating for the insecurity she showed me last night\u2026 but on the other hand, I\u2019m glad she\u2019s comfortable advertising our new relationship to the people she cares about.<br /> <br /> After hobnobbing for a while, I made my way out on to the dance floor. I started strutting my stuff almost immediately, but I didn\u2019t <u>really</u> hit my stride until about ten minutes later, when a song I didn\u2019t know started playing. Something about it resonated with me, and I began to lose myself in the rhythm of the song and the motions of the dance. I looked it up on my phone later; the song was called \u201cEverybody Wants You,\u201d and it was by a man named Billy Squier. I immediately purchased and downloaded it.<br /> <br /> So the club went kind of quiet for about twenty seconds after that song ended. I glanced around. Everyone was looking at me. Some folks were positively <u>leering</u>. I ate it up, of course; there\u2019s nothing better than being the object of everyone\u2019s desire in a crowded place like that. And I heard Calamity telling someone \u201cyeah, and she sings, too. She performs most nights at the Dream House just outside of Malibu\u2026\u201d So my sick and twisted little obsession with the spotlight might have drummed up a little business tonight as well.<br /> <br /> After my little show, I dragged D off to talk with some of <u>my</u> friends. Dark Kimberly and Davie stood to one side of the dance floor with a small knot of other Spring Courtiers. I admit I wanted to show my girlfriend off a little as well, but mostly I just wanted to talk to them about Princess Jolie. I\u2019d been worried about her ever since our little chat the previous day.<br /> <br /> They greeted me warmly enough, and the talk soon turned to our august monarch (or, since she\u2019s the Spring Princess, would that make her our \u201cApril\u201d monarch instead?). \u201cHow\u2019s the Princess doing?\u201d I asked with concern.<br /> <br /> Kimberly sighed. \u201cShe\u2019s still pretty depressed,\u201d she admitted, \u201cbut she\u2019ll get past it. She\u2019s strong.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI feel so bad for upsetting her,\u201d I confessed.<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t worry about it,\u201d Davie replied, \u201cnobody blames you.\u201d<br /> <br /> Kimberly nodded. \u201cShe just really likes you, Lori, and she thinks she\u2019s screwed up whatever\u2019s between the two of you.\u201d I felt D stiffen slightly beside me, and I gave her hand a reassuring squeeze. I also, I admit, felt a little flutter deep in my stomach at the news that the Princess was fond of me.<br /> <br /> \u201cShould I go to Glamour Springs and talk to her?\u201d I asked. \u201cOr do you think that would only make things worse?\u201d<br /> <br /> Davie considered that for a minute. \u201cThe Dream House is about to go into a run of special weekend shows, right?\u201d he asked. When I nodded, he continued. \u201cWhy don\u2019t you invite her to one of the shows? Then she gets to make the decision about whether or not she\u2019s ready to talk to you.\u201d<br /> <br /> I leaned forward and gave him a hug and a kiss on the forehead. \u201cDavie, you\u2019re a genius,\u201d I gushed. \u201cNow no more excuses. I\u2019m going to expect to see you in the audience for at least one of our shows this weekend, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> He held up two fingers, but in a good way. \u201cScout\u2019s honor,\u201d he promised with a smile.<br /> <br /> Kimberly latched on to this new topic with a squeal. \u201cYou <u>have</u> to let me dress you up for your night out, Davie! It\u2019ll be so much fun! I\u2019ll make you soooo <u>cute!</u>\u201d<br /> <br /> I started to object to this treatment, but D dragged me off before I could get involved. \u201cIt\u2019s for his own good,\u201d she promised me once we were out of earshot.<br /> <br /> \u201cHow could that humiliating display be for his own good?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> D grinned. \u201cBecause if Davie ever figures out how much trim he could have just for the asking, he would become insufferable, and he\u2019d lose all his friends,\u201d she explained. Still seems kind of mean to me, but I\u2019ll leave that problem for another day.<br /> <br /> More dancing followed. I kind of lost myself in the (mostly unfamiliar) music after that, but I know that most of my friends were hob-nobbing with the other Lost in the club. Gawain hung out with a young woman named Desiree. I\u2019d seen her before at Spring Court functions, but didn\u2019t know much about her. Apparently she escaped from the infamous \u201cDirector,\u201d and this has raised suspicions among the local Changeling population. She\u2019s the only person to escape from the Director who has not \u2013 thus far \u2013 turned out to be a Loyalist, and that has a lot of people twitchy. Joan has publicly expressed her desire to kill Desiree, but apparently the Summer Court is keeping her murderous urges in check because there\u2019s no proof that Desiree is a traitor to her kind.<br /> <br /> Gawain seems to like her. Now, I know that Gawain can be a bit na\u00efve from time to time, but my first impulse is to trust his judgment in this. Based on a very brief interaction with her, I don\u2019t think Desiree would willingly betray any of us to the Gentry. What worries me is the possibility that she might be a <u>Manchurian Candidate</u> style sleeper agent. The Director has employed such methods before. If that\u2019s the case, she might be a Loyalist and not even know it.<br /> <br /> Jacob sort of latched on to a woman I recognized from our opening night show. Her name was Willow Black, and she\u2019s a local representative of the Night Court. Could romance be blossoming there? I suppose it\u2019s possible, but I kind of doubt it at the moment. I think he just noticed that she was all alone in that crowd and wanted to reach out. That\u2019s something I\u2019ve noticed about Jacob: he doesn\u2019t really like crowds, but he doesn\u2019t like to be alone either. I\u2019m not sure he\u2019s entirely comfortable in the presence of other Changelings, but I think he feels like he needs us around to keep him grounded for some reason.<br /> <br /> In any case, more power to him. The Dream House is supposed to be a place where Lost of all descriptions can gather to rest, socialize, and soak up the glamour in peace, so the more friends we have in the area, the better.<br /> <br /> Calamity mostly hung out around Monica and Hailey, and I even saw her engaging Hailey in conversation in a mostly non-threatening way. I think she\u2019s growing as a person.<br /> <br /> Ace mostly confined his antics to the dance floor. I should mention his outfit\u2026 it was sort of uber-punk in a way that I can\u2019t really describe. It was leather, and more revealing than my own clothing\u2026 especially around the \u201cposterior\u201d area. I heard one of the patrons describe it as \u201croad warrior chic,\u201d though I\u2019m not really sure what he meant.<br /> <br /> So we danced and socialized for a few hours before saying our goodbyes and making our way back home. In the car on the way home, I put my head on D\u2019s shoulder as she told us a bit more about what happened to Golden Swan back in the day. It\u2019s even more depressing than the bits we had already heard, though it does shed some light on a few of the locals.<br /> <br /> When Swan got sick, the King of Summer at that time \u2013 who must have been a real dick \u2013 forbade anyone from going into the Hedge to help him. He claimed that he didn\u2019t want good Changelings to risk their lives \u201cjust to save some queer.\u201d The Spring King \u2013 none other than our good friend Austin \u2013 ignored the Summer King and went into the Hedge alone, swearing an oath that he would save Swan\u2019s life or die trying. Since he didn\u2019t have anyone to help him, the trip took longer than it should have, and Swan was already gone by the time Austin made it back. So I guess that solves the mystery of how Austin is an oathbreaker.<br /> <br /> One other wrinkle to this story involves the enigmatic Lucien Torrez, but it only serves to muddy the waters of opinion even further. Torrez apparently disapproved of the Summer King\u2019s decision not to help Swan\u2026 and when Torrez disapproves of something, it rarely goes well for the subject of said disapproval. The rumor is that Torrez lifted the Summer King\u2019s desk into the air and beat him with it until he agreed that it would be in the Freehold\u2019s best interests for him to abdicate the throne.<br /> <br /> Everyone thought for sure that Torrez would take over the position, and he had a lot of support. But at the last moment, he pulled out of the running without giving an explanation, and Viscount Augustine took the job. There are all sorts of rumors about why he might have refused the top job. Some people think he was blackmailed, but considering that he doesn\u2019t seem particularly concerned about his public image, it\u2019s hard to imagine what he could have done that someone could use as leverage against him. I can\u2019t think of anything short of being a Loyalist\u2026 and that\u2019s probably the one thing I just can\u2019t believe about him, considering how vehemently he opposes them.<br /> <br /> Talk turned to relationships after a while. Mostly D talked about Hailey and Monica. Monica was the one who rescued Hailey from the Hedge after she escaped from the Mothership, and Hailey sort of latched on to Monica romantically as a form of hero worship. D said that happens a lot, and Monica is usually fine with it, and will sometimes sleep with the men she rescues. The girls don\u2019t usually get very far with her, though; Monica is attracted to women but not comfortable with that part of herself. Hailey has managed to stick around longer than any of the other star-struck girls who have latched on to Monica so far. Even in the darkened van, I could see Calamity grinding her teeth through this entire conversation.<br /> <br /> Then D started talking about Madame Spidertoes. She got sort of wistful as she spoke about her former lover, but she was stroking my hair and holding my hand all the while. I think \u2013 I hope \u2013 she was purging something, getting it out of her system. Spidertoes sounds a little creepy to me, with real control issues, but it was obvious that D really cared for her at one time, and some of that lingers. It\u2019s hard for me to imagine my strong, rebellious girlfriend becoming submissive for <u>anyone</u>, but Spidertoes has this aura about her that seems to make people roll over for her.<br /> <br /> At one point, Insincere Marguerite asked if she reminded D of Madame Spidertoes\u2026 I\u2019m not sure why. D admitted that she did, both with her beauty and with her all-too-obvious possessive streak. I confess I stiffened a bit at that. I don\u2019t want D thinking about an old girlfriend every time she glances at Marguerite; especially one who had such an obvious hold over her. Spidertoes is beautiful and exotic and powerful and full of mystical knowledge. Insincere Marguerite is smoky and mysterious and gorgeous, and\u2026 and <u>French</u>. Stacked up next to that I\u2019m just some out-of-touch corn-fed hick from Iowa. It\u2019s enough to make anyone insecure.<br /> <br /> I guess D noticed my discomfort, because the hand that had been stroking my hair moved on to my cheek and gave me a very gentle caress. She winked at me in the darkness and gave me one of the warmest smiles I\u2019ve ever seen from her. I couldn\u2019t help but smile back.<br /> <br /> We got back to the Dream House, and Marguerite and Julia immediately disappeared upstairs. It was hardly a surprise; they hadn\u2019t been able to keep their hands off each other for the entire car ride home. D and I went to my bedroom to change into clothes more appropriate for briar wolf hunting, and we shared a few private moments as well, though ours were more tender than amorous\u2026 which was nice and sweet and thrilling in ways I can\u2019t really describe.<br /> <br /> Well, the noises from Marguerite\u2019s (or \u201cMags,\u201d as D has taken to calling her) room have died down, so I\u2019d better wrap this up and get ready to play the damsel in distress. I hope things go well, and I\u2019ll write more when we get back.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 08-20-2014, 07:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T16:11:00-07:00","id":235843,"title":"","content":"<b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> <b><u><b><u>Thursday May 8<sup>th</sup></u></b> </u></b><br /> <br /> Fuck. I really have to be more mindful about what I say to Gawain. I tried to pass it off as joking, but I think everyone knows I was at least partially serious about him seducing Monica to cock block Haily. He was so damn apologetic as he explained that it wasn't right. And last night he dropped everything to come to bed early because I was. Dammit the boy is well and truly twitterpated. I don't understand why. I'm selfish and troublesome and destructive. Hell, I'm not even that pretty. I shouldn't have caved in when he confessed his love to me. I should have pushed him away. If I honestly cared about him I'd have walked away. It would have hurt him, but in the end he'd have gotten over it and found someone better. Someone like Monica. Someone that deserves a man like him. But I didn't and I... I can't bring myself to push him away. Not now. It feels so good to wake up with him there, to have his arms around me at night. I like the fact that he dropped what he was doing to come to bed with me. I like that he thinks of me. I like how he looks at me. I don't deserve his devotion but I enjoy it and I don't want to give it up. I'm too selfish to turn him away so he can find someone he deserves, and I can't change what I am inside. But I can smile. I can play nice. I can control the monster. And, for him, I can hide it.<br /> <br /> But for now, I don't have to. We're gearing up to fight the briar wolves and I am so looking forward to it. The moment when we fall upon them, when they realize that they are the prey and not the predators. The sweet taste of fear as it dawns upon them. As the first one falls and the others waver. When they must choose to flee or fight. But it does not matter, we will kill them. They will bleed and they will die. It will be glorious. They are monsters and monsters deserve no mercy.<br /> <br /> But for the moment, we wait. I am eager but not restless. No, I learned patience in Snow Globe. Insincere Marguerite and her pet are fucking like the girl doesn't expect her to come back. Or maybe it's just that my sister was tormenting her relentlessly at the club earlier. Of course, I can't say that I entirely blame either of them. That corset julia put her in was fucking hot. They're rather adorable together, so very head over heels with each other. It really surprised me that Insincere Marguerite asked me to pick up some birth control for her as well earlier. I hadn't noticed her being particularly interested in men and as serious as she and julia seem... Is there something I don't know about that shy little artist? I mean, I know Luna was a man before being taken... If they can make us snakes and birds then who knows? Surely some Gentry out there has seen Hentai right? But I didn't ask and it's not really my business who she's sleeping with. Though now I'm really wishing she shared her toys...<br /> <br /> The Rose and Thorn was an enjoyable outing. I am glad De La Roche suggested it. If there was any doubt those two are an item it has been firmly banished. Lori showed up to breakfast with her and asked Gawain very sweetly if her girlfriend could join us. While we were eating, De La Roche suggested we check out the club (as it turned out so she could show Lori off to everyone. But then, if Lori was my girlfriend I'd sure as hell be doing the same.) She did also try to stick Insincere Marguerite with the nickname Mags, which she clearly detested and I voiced my own disapproval of. Maybe Marge or I guess IM but Mags? So not her. And if we let that one pass then Hera only knows what she might start calling me. Nope, much as I do find that I quite enjoy De La Roche's company, there are lines that should not be crossed. Now, in preparation for the clubbing, she and Lori and I went clothes shopping. I had been meaning to get Lori to help me look for something more suitable to playing hostess anyway and I didn't really have anything that seemed quite right for the Rose and Thorn (though having been there now, I think my biker look would fit well enough.) We all got punked up, which was fun. And Lori helped me with makeup (and by help, I mean did it for me). I... I looked pretty hot all told. I mean, I was in with a pack of beauties but I know Gawain liked it and that was nice. He and Jacob went fairly casual. Ace, of course, went full bore Mad Max ass-less chaps and spikes and all.<br /> <br /> Lori and her girl did the rounds and then danced, which put the entire club on hold to watch. Ace hit the bar and the dance floor. I chatted with Ginny (as a fellow Autumn) about the club a bit and then ended up with Monica and the ever present Haily. Gawain spent a bit of time chatting with Desiree, one of the infamous Director's escapees. Everyone seems quite suspicious due to all of his other escapee's turning out to be loyalists. Gawain seemed to think she was nice. Clearly, I have to keep a close eye on her and may well have to cut a bitch quietly and discreetly. Jacob vanished up into the catwalks and hung around the woman from the Night Court that came to our opening.<br /> <br /> On the way home, De La Roche got into some history. Apparently she had a fling with Madam Spidertoes (which is still just weird to think about. It's like hearing about someone fucking your grandmother.) that went sour because Spidertoes is very Domme and De La Roche didn't like how subbie she was getting. Also, Spidertoes and Annika apparently used to be an item (if she had Annika on a leash... well first off, that is something I'd kill to see but damn she must be intense to have tamed that one...) After they broke up, Spidertoes arraigned for food to be delivered to Annika's house and took care of her. So, all around a weird situation. Annika's withdrawal was caused by the death of Golden Swan.<br /> <br /> Golden Swan, previous burlesque theater mogul and apparently God's gift to men, women, and anything in between. Everyone wanted him and loved him, except the Summer King at the time. When Golden Swan got AIDS, the Summer King refused to authorize an expedition into the hedge to secure a cure. And in response, the Spring King gave him the royal fuck you and went anyway. Sadly, he failed to return in time to save the Golden Swan and thus broke his vow to do so. That failure also prompted him to abdicate his position and opened the way for Princess Jolie. That man is Austin. Damn, I knew he was a stand up guy but fuck. That is some epic shit there. I really really feel bad about breaking his rib now.<br /> <br /> And as for the asshole Summer king, Lucien beat him with his own desk until he decided it was in his best interests to abdicate. Then he did not take the throne that everyone expected him to. There are plenty who suspect some sort of blackmail but I have to wonder if he just prefers to be in a position to get shit done without having to deal with the political bullshit. I can't lie, the more I hear, the more I catch myself wondering what he might do to this little monster on his desk... And that, of course, leads to wondering what the everliving fuck is wrong with me that I'm day dreaming about that when I have Gawain. It's not that I want to be Torez's girl or anything. Fuck, I don't think I could stand to be around the asshole that much without wanting to stab him. I just want him to put me through my paces and send me on my way. Gawain is... different. I fuck a lot of people. He's the only one that I sleep with. It means something in my fucked up brain but I'm not sure how to explain it. It's not right. He deserves more but that's the kind of damaged goods I bring to the table.<br /> <br /> And while we're speaking about my damage, De La Roche also had some insight into Haily and Monica. Monica rescued Haily and promised to protect her. It is apparently not uncommon for those she rescues to develop a crush on her and she is not adverse to sleeping with them for awhile. Haily is female, which isn't usually her thing and thus why she hasn't slept with her. Also, Haily seems more than just passingly interested (hmm... that sounds a little familiar...) and Monica isn't looking to encourage her when her own interests aren't that deep.<br /> <br /> I hate to say it, but I think I am going to have to just take Haily aside and spend some time alone with her. I know my dislike is based on hearsay and my own misplaced issues. I have to get to know her. If I am going to hate her, it needs to be for her own merits. Otherwise I need to let it go. Easier said than done perhaps, but I cannot continue to let myself feel like this about her without some grounds. And fuck, maybe she really is just a scared girl reacting to the appearance of her Keeper's favorite pet. Maybe they're both victims of a fucked up realm and their individual trauma.<br /> <br /> Fuck all this moral grey area shit makes my head hurt. At least there is no question about the damn briar wolves. Maybe Luna has the right idea. If I didn't have promises to keep I swear, I'd be tempted to wash my razor-hands of all this hullabaloo and move to the woods myself. Or maybe lock myself in my house like Annika. But that is not going to happen. Gawain needs me. The others need me. I made a promise to Queen Charlotte and a promise to them. And I keep my promises. I'm a good monster that way.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Okay\u2026so today started like most days. We all got up. I made coffee. Gawain made breakfast. I continued my trend of getting out the ingredients that he would need, after I had made up cups of coffee for him and myself. He looked a little sleep deprived, but not as bad as I\u2019ve seen him in the past. I wonder if he\u2019s just an insomniac or if he has nightmares. Could be a combination of the two I suppose. I wouldn\u2019t be surprised if he had bad dreams. He did not have the best time of it in Arcadia. He was forced into it, but that doesn\u2019t help too much when it comes to the subconscious. I don\u2019t know if he\u2019d take me up on it, but maybe I should offer to be a sympathetic ear. I wasn\u2019t exactly forced into my actions, but I still have nightmares about them. I know what it\u2019s like to see the faces of the dead in my dreams. I can give general details I suppose. I did kill people before serving The Lady after all. That was more of a survival thing, and sometimes I\u2019m not sure if I feel so guilty about those or not. Some not at all. Those that attacked me deserved what they got. The others that I attacked, maybe not so much.<br /> <br /> Anyhoo\u2026I\u2019m sure Gawain talks to Calamity about that kind of stuff, but it might be good for him to talk to someone that is not as close as she is. I guess I just don\u2019t like to see him suffer. He\u2019s such a good person, he doesn\u2019t deserve the nightmares or the pain. It doesn\u2019t seem fair.<br /> <br /> Yeah\u2026depressing territory again. Anyhoo\u2026we had breakfast. De la Rocha joined us and was suitably impressed with Gawain\u2019s culinary skills. We were talking about what to do today and we brought up the idea of going after that bounty for the Summer court. The Briar Wolves. Then De la Rocha brought up the idea of going to the other big Changeling club in town. It\u2019s called the <i>Rose and Thorn. </i>After a bit more discussion we decided that we could do both. We\u2019d go to the club for a while, then head on out to take on the wolves. After much talk and consideration we decided to present two of our group as bait while the rest of us stayed hidden and attacked the wolves as they ambushed our \u201chelpless victims.\u201d It seems that Briar wolves are somewhat cowardly. They won\u2019t attack a large or strong looking group. They prefer easy prey, and to separate individuals from a group, chase them down and kill them at their leisure. They also don\u2019t like guns. I can understand both points. Separating your target from the larger group is definitely a sound way of achieving your goal. I think the phrase is \u201cpicking them off one by one.\u201d I\u2019ve used the tactic myself to get targets away from allies/bodyguards. Rook and I would work in tandem to retrieve our Lady\u2019s wayward subjects and kill any opposition that might stop us from returning to Arcadia. Hmm\u2026 makes me sound something like a coward doesn\u2019t it? It was effective though. It worked really well, especially when I worked with Rook. I was very good at my job. Not overly proud of those accomplishments at the moment, but I can look back and see the effectiveness of our team.<br /> <br /> Okay\u2026anyhoo\u2026earlier the ladies, well most of the ladies (except Insincere Marguerite and Julia) went shopping for appropriate party clothes. They looked at Gawain, Ace and I, and we all decided that we had better things to do. Like set up the gym downstairs. So, we stayed while then went out. Insincere Marguerite and Julia watched us as we set up the gym equipment. Not the most exciting thing to do, but it was better than clothes shopping. I\u2019d say shopping for weapons might be interesting, better than clothes shopping anyway, but that would only be true if the knives I found in stores around here weren\u2019t pieces of shit. Seriously, how do the makers of these knives expect anyone to use them for any length of time? The knives I keep on me were gifted to me by Rook when I was Knighted. Not a moment I\u2019m keen on commemorating, but the knives are good quality. Gawain\u2019s knives are good quality too. I have to give the man credit, he knows what he\u2019s doing at that forge. Speaking of which. For the most part it was Ace and I who set up the gym equipment and punching bags. Gawain was working at his forge making a new sword and a knife, and much to my surprise, another knife for me. It is a very fine blade. Well balanced, with a wicked edge. Simple in design, just a bit of a flourish on the handle, but beautiful all the same. I almost didn\u2019t know what to say. The last time anyone gave me anything of real value was Rook or the Lady. My paired knives, or the Lady\u2019s brand. The later lost its value since then, but it meant a lot at one point in time. Most of the time spent in Her realm everyone looked out for themselves. Charity and generosity were pretty much foreign concepts. I traded for things I needed, or killed to get those things I couldn\u2019t trade for. And here is a man that I\u2019ve known only for a couple of weeks and he made a good knife for me. Not as an afterthought, or originally for someone else but decided to give it to me. This was something that he made just for me. The surprised \u201cThanks\u201d I gave him was barely adequate, but I wasn\u2019t sure what else to say. I\u2019m not sure what I can do to repay him for the gift. I\u2019ll have to think on it.<br /> <br /> The <i>Rose and Thorn</i> was an interesting club. They played an interesting and eclectic variety of music. The decorating was just as unique. There was even one room that was pretty much wall to wall aquariums. Even the ceiling. Neat. Anyhoo\u2026we all split up when we got inside. De la Rocha was fairly obviously \u201cshowing off\u201d Lorelei as her girl. It was kind of cute, and almost \u201chigh school-ish.\u201d Almost. Insincere Marguerite was wearing one of Julia\u2019s corset tops, and doing her damnest to slide on out of it. Not that anyone was complaining mind you. Her figure got a nice little showcase with that top, and I got to see her actually appear a bit shy at the same time. She\u2019s adorable when she blushes.<br /> <br /> Not sure where everyone went. I did see Ace head to the bar and proceed to drink rather a lot of alcohol. I know that he can produce poison, so it only stands to reason that he\u2019d be immune or resistant to other poisons as well\u2026.including alcohol. Fortunately, or unfortunately depending on the point of view, I don\u2019t suffer from that particular quirk. Alcohol works on me just fine. But to back up just a bit. As I was looking around I noticed a changeling sitting up in the catwalk by herself, just watching. I\u2019d never met her and figured it might be nice to introduce myself and see if she wanted any company. I understand the need to get away from people, but it doesn\u2019t hurt to try to be social, and goddess knows I need all the practice I can get. So, I went to the bar to ask the bartender who she was and if he knew what drink she preferred. He told me that she didn\u2019t really drink anything hard, so I got a bottle of water for her and a beer for me then climbed up to the catwalk.<br /> <br /> I introduced myself and we chatted a bit. She said that her name was Willow Black, I told her who I am. I found out that she is a part of the Night court. We chatted for a bit and she told me of a prank that Insincere Marguerite (when I mentioned that I knew her) had played on someone, filling their house with bags and bags of insects. Someone from the Day court I think. I thought it sounded kinda gross, but funny. Willow seemed a nice person. She seems to be the sort to stay out of the way, when there is trouble and socially as well. She likes to watch things from a distance. I can appreciate that. I tend to be an up close and personal kind of creature. Well, mostly when it comes to fighting. She also mentioned that Lucien Torrez doesn\u2019t like her. I told her that I don\u2019t think Torrez likes anyone. I think I mentioned at that point that he doesn\u2019t like anyone in my court. Not sure if I specifically mentioned that I\u2019m Winter court or not. Don\u2019t know if it really matters. We had a pleasant conversation. Nothing serious, but enough that it wasn\u2019t forgettable. I wonder if I\u2019ll see her again?<br /> <br /> So on the way home, De la Rocha told us about her relationship with Madame Spidertoes, and how she had to get out while she could. I think the conversation started about relationships and ended up with De la Rocha telling us about her experiences. Apparently Madame Spidertoes was rather possessive and De la Rocha decided that she didn\u2019t want to be subservient to anyone. She also told us of Madame Spidertoes and Annika and their little stint together. I\u2019ll admit, I didn\u2019t pay attention for a good bit of that conversation. I probably should have, but I was distracted. Willow Black reminded me of someone I\u2019d met in the Lady\u2019s realm. She obviously wasn\u2019t that person. That other person is dead, but there was something about her eyes that reminded me of that girl.<br /> <br /> I thought I was doing right. The girl appeared to be pompous. Too good to be in The Lady\u2019s realm or to accept her help. I know now that she was just scared, terrified actually, and reacted the only way she knew, which was to push me away. I led her away to the promise of a warm place to sleep, only to leave her stranded in the middle of nowhere, surrounded by ice and snow in a dark, dark cave. Willow Black has the same eyes. Only hers are a warm brown, instead of an iced over hue that may have been hazel at one point. Dammit\u2026 I have to stop thinking about those days. Stop it. Stop it.<br /> <br /> So, it turns out that Austin used to be the Spring King. He swore an oath to go into the hedge and find a cure for Golden Swan. The Summer King (at the time) decided that it was too risky for so many folks to go into the hedge to look for a cure for a queer, so he forbade it. Austin said \u201cto hell with that,\u201d and went by himself. By the time that he got back with the cure, Golden Swan had already died. Guess that explains the broken oath. Apparently Torrez did not take kindly to this and beat the previous Summer King with his own desk. (Smack down by furniture) He did not kill him from what I understand, but convinced him to step down. Folks thought that Torrez would take over as Summer monarch, but he declined. Some are not sure if he stepped down because he wanted to, or if he was forced to. I personally think that he let someone else take the throne so he could be the power behind it. In most cases the person on the throne is not the real power. The actual power usually resides with those behind the scenes, so to speak. And Torrez doesn\u2019t seem like the type that wants the throne, he wants the power. And damn does he have it.<br /> Well, back to more pressing matters. As soon as Insincere Marguerite and Julia are done expressing their passion for one another we will leave for the hedge to hunt Briar wolves. I hope that love is really what they have. Insincere Marguerite seems rather possessive of Julia. I try to distract Marguerite when I can from being overly clingy in public. Not sure how successful I am. I just don\u2019t want my friend falling back on old or bad habits if I can help it. I just don\u2019t know how to really do it without flat out saying, \u201cHey, lay off the \u2018touchy, feely\u2019 in public.\u201d I know that she doesn\u2019t want to become like her keeper, but sometimes I worry. I know, pot, kettle and all that. Maybe I should just take her aside, alone, and express my concerns. Not that I don\u2019t think that she has a genuine interest in Julia, I\u2019m just afraid that she\u2019s becoming more possessive than is strictly normal in a relationship.<br /> <br /> And now I hear footsteps coming down the stairs. Time to go kill some wolves.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> Tonight we hunt Briarwolves. Probably. I am nervous about this; traveling and dealing with what crosses our path is not a big deal, but hunting things hunting us is a little more scary for this grub.<br /> <br /> Today has been good. Julia has been my pet today. Lorelei brought De la Rocha to breakfast. Jacob went out of his way to be nice to I there too. I like Jacob. Julia tolerated my possessive affections with good grace. Mostly. I should send her away, go cold turkey, stop having the urge to cover her with my smell. At least I have mostly stopped slobbering on her face in public. Mostly. I should send her away. But\u2026we have to go fight Briarwolves. Another time, then. Possibly.<br /> <br /> De La Rocha needs to stop calling I Mags. It is a terrible nickname. She tried to make it stick. How unpleasant.<br /> <br /> De La Rocha also suggested we go to Rose &amp; Thorn, Flores\u2019club, tonight. Lorelei was enthusiastic; especially given De La Rocha wanted to show off her lady. Julia was\u2026not unhappy to be seen in my company there, apparently (She met Flores there and they became friends when she was new and lonely. Flores apparently tried to set her up with people from time to time though, Badly.) Lorelei, who is addicted to shopping, took Calamity out to work on her wardrobe. Jacob and Gawain and Ace were to set up the Gym as a \u201cguy thing,\u201d which Julia was happy to watch them do. I was happy to do whatever she wished then. We did stop by her place, though, to get a top she could modify for me to wear in the evening. I suspect she made I, ahem, overflow a bit on purpose. Frankly, I am impressed my chest is not really a major asset for me but she made it impressive. And reaped the benefits thereof. There was a bit of role reversal as she was doting on I once there.<br /> <br /> Calamity needs some help veiling herself in the feminine mystique, as I think they say in America. Perhaps I can help. I like to think I manage to remain a lady even when crawling upside down in a pipe. She does not need to be a fading flower, but a true lady never is.<br /> <br /> Our time at the club was fun. Mostly. Julia and I spoke to Flores some, and it was good to see them getting along again. Flores was clearly apologetic for coming onto I. She is, however, still clearly intensely attracted to I. The feeling is not exactly unreciprocated, which means I should, perhaps, be careful going there by myself. Possibly. Especially given this time she took a submissive posture I believe Julia did not notice but was not uncalculated, I suspect. Probably.<br /> <br /> Several of the Latinos there also spoke to Julia, like Sandoval. Apparently Flores gave her an \u201cin\u201d with that clique. Captain Jack was there, but did not battle Gawain, who spoke to some ladies on the floor then Monica and Hailey, which Calamity also sought out while there after speaking to Ginny. Ace and Lorelei danced. I did not see where Jacob went, but I was distracted by Julia\u2019s attentions to my d\u00e9colletage and could have missed him easy. Probably.<br /> <br /> On the way home, De La Rocha gave us some history. She apparently had been involved with Madame Spidertoes, and their relationship was rocky at times and fun at times but she is glad it is over. Apparently. She had some affection for Spidertoes, but was clearly afraid of her. Spidertoes may have a variation on my possessiveness problem. I asked her if I reminded her of Spidertoes and she said yes. Definitely. I suppose that Spidertoes has not gone Gentry that is a good sign, right? Of course, she is far older than I, and I might be slipping faster. De La Rocha said Spidertoes goes all the way back to the mid-19<sup>th</sup> Century. I am skeptical a Lost could live that long, generally, but I won\u2019t assume she was wrong. Annika is also insane, to her mind. A recluse who Spidertoes never got over. She seems a difficult woman to just forget but then, she works hard to cultivate that aura. Probably.<br /> <br /> When we returned, Julia, having been reacquainted with my bosom via the top she altered for me, was eager to further reintroduce herself, but we had Briarwolves to kill, and frankly she was getting a little forward. I am the forward one, after all. Usually. I spent a bit of private time with her, but commanded her to stay and wait for me. The idea of her sitting and waiting like my Dearest had was, well, unfortunately very pleasing. Of course, she won\u2019t be sitting in my room but walking around the stage and getting good perspective points but, eh, can\u2019t have everything. Usually.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s good to see Lorelei so happy with De La Rocha. De La Rocha is not who I would expect her to have a serious relationship with, not just because she is a woman (though that is part of it; I still have trouble wrapping my brain around Lorelei being a lesbian. It feels strange, somehow) but because she is a Darkling and an aggressive summer courtier. Though straight women tend to like tough guys and bad boys, or so I remember from before I was taken, so apparently Lorelei sees those traits in De La Rocha.<br /> <br /> Ace is still insane. I have met insane Englishmen before, but none were crazy in the way he is. It seems benign, though. I am unsure of his obsession with cattle and piranhas, though. I always found barracuda more menacing. But if I say that Gawain will flip out again. I think a lamptotoxus would be scarier, but there are logistical problems there. Best not mention that around Gawain either though. Probably.<br /> <br /> I have decided what I must do with Calamity. Probably. I must lure her to the catwalks, plop her down where the puppets can join us with a nice cup of tea from the tea set while I sit with my own steaming cup and we talk about her aggression and nature. I\u2019d think getting laid would lower her aggression but it seems to not affect it. I worry she is letting the monster control her not controlling the monster. I worry she is what her Keeper wanted. I am in no position to throw stones, but she trusts I, and what sort of friend, what sort of comrade would I be if I did not whisper to her my fears?<br /> <br /> Gawain is basically the opposite of Jacob. You can read him like a book. It will eventually work to our detriment, of course, but when paranoia makes you suspicious of everyone, it can be a relief to have someone like him. Also he can be quite intimidating and a good fighter. All around good, I think. Yes, definitely.<br /> <br /> And Jacob, cute little Jacob. What is going on in your mind? He is helping me curb my most egregious excesses, but his cards are kept close and he disappears at times. Also, he is the other most likely to be targeted by loyalists. Perhaps he also left his Keeper on good terms? I don\u2019t know, but I hope I enjoy finding out. Probably.<br /> <br /> Bah time for wolves. Get it done and move on to something interesting. Maybe.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session X</i><br /> <br /> I was not sure if we would get to Briarwolves that session or not. Turns out no, we did not. Heavily social session.<br /> <br /> People were happy to learn some details from the Golden Swan story IC. We knew it was coming, and De La Rocha made for an interesting point of exposition.<br /> <br /> Well I am short on time, so no long winded wrap up. You can feel free to ask questions and make comments as always. Last night was mostly a combat session, so mixing it up a bit. Ace\u2019s player could not make it, but these things happen. I\u2019ll see you at the usual time for that game journals if not before.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/