oD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T12:09:12-07:00","id":241580,"title":"","content":"Neat. New NPC maybe? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T12:46:17-07:00","id":241618,"title":"","content":"I am not gonna shake things up too much just yet. I mean they are just now getting well settled in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T13:31:22-07:00","id":245636,"title":"","content":"Well we managed a changeling session despite Gen Con, and it were exciting! And as usual, more questions than answers. Did you expect anything less? Ace\u2019s player could not make, so he was (mostly) absent from journals.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> May 9th<br /> <br /> Note to self (which I guess this whole thing kinda is): hunting briar wolves is, in fact, an awesome date night for Calamity. She certainly appreciated it, even if I asked her not to kill Desiree or Ginny. I even got a dance, in public! I\u2019d been kicking myself for not asking her to dance at the club before we left, so when we wound up back there, I pretty much had to, you know? Plus, I think the mind-blowing sex when we got home left no room for nightmares. At least, I\u2019m gonna go with that, and not that enacting violence in real life did it. I like the sex one better, you know?<br /> <br /> The hunt went well too, even if everyone got hurt more than I\u2019d hoped. Our setup worked just like we wanted, except that the wolves were so fast that when we stopped for the ambush, they got to tear into Lori way more than I would have liked. She was in a bad way, but was super brave and stood it out, going all super-beautiful so they\u2019d stop attacking her so much and then healing everybody until she was just exhausted. Even with how hurt she\u2019d gotten, she didn\u2019t heal herself until the fight was over! De la Roche helped with that too, cause she does this thing where she can transfer damage between people a bit at a time, so she made sure that Lori was consistently getting a little bit put back together.<br /> <br /> Other than that though, it went just right. The others were pretty much invisible, and we managed to get a group of 6 all gathered together without tiring ourselves out too much. I didn\u2019t do a great job of pretending to be scared, but I kinda hoped our team act helped with that, and they maybe just thought I was stupid, or just being protective, or something, you know? They chased us anyway. We did decide to stop with just the six though, cause there were these weird-ass mannequin things chasing the next two that were supposed to force us into a further ambush, I think. They eventually showed up to fight near us, and then 2 other briar wolves got away, but they\u2019ll probably fuck off at this point, considering we killed 8 of their ten.<br /> <br /> We also killed 8 of the mannequin things. See, while we were being chased, I saw 4 of them chasing two wolves away from us, so we decided to let them handle themselves. Then, in the middle of our melee, 4 more of the mannequins chased Ginny and Desiree right towards us! I called them out, and even used some of my Contracts of Stone to awesome effect, and cut one right in half! It helped that it was super focused on Ginny and didn\u2019t even try to get out of the way. They paid more attention to me after that though. They had long blades for arms, and knew how to use them, for sure. We just got done finishing those off, and the 6 wolves we started with, when 2 more mannequins showed up, chasing 2 more wolves! They weren\u2019t too bad though, considering the wolves had been fighting back more, and so we just had to finish things off.<br /> <br /> After we\u2019d dealt with all the bad guys on the field, Calamity started turning towards Desiree. She didn\u2019t seem berserker-y or anything, but she was still very much in fight-mode, you know? Apparently, the mannequin things had been holding back when they attacked her. Desiree, I mean. I guess I could see it, when it was pointed out - she\u2019d certainly been cut, but nothing super deep or particularly crippling. Jacob said Desiree hadn\u2019t noticed that they were holding back, so she probably wasn\u2019t in league with them or anything, and me and him managed to talk Calamity down.<br /> <br /> Desiree did say the mannequins were from the Director, his extras. So maybe they recognized her and weren\u2019t allowed to kill the Director\u2019s people? Not like, Desiree is still working for him, but she used to and maybe they didn\u2019t know that anything\u2019s changed, you know? Or maybe they were planning on capturing her back, or something? There could be tons of reasons why they weren\u2019t trying to kill her, especially since she didn\u2019t know that they weren\u2019t.<br /> <br /> Then there was Ginny - I think Calamity is super suspicious of her too now. De la Roche sure was. She said she was supposed to meet somebody, on the main trod between Santa Monica and Malibu. She really didn\u2019t want to say who, and when people pressed her, she said it was Flores she was meeting. That\u2019s what got De la Roche suspicious right off, cause I guess Flores wouldn\u2019t have been having clandestine meetings in the Hedge? She also checked, and Flores didn\u2019t back that up. She did say that maybe Ginny was hooking up with a lady that\u2019s not out, and was just trying to protect that, you know? She was supposed to meet this mystery person right where she found Desiree hanging out, and then a bit later was when the mannequins showed up. Though, thinking about it, they probably weren\u2019t there to recapture Desiree, cause Ginny said they didn\u2019t even notice Desiree until she started freaking out and kicking them and stuff. Then they started attacking her too.<br /> <br /> After we\u2019d finished fighting though, Calamity did the thing where we can tell what\u2019s up around us in the Hedge to figure out that there were two more briar wolves, but they were running away, and that there were two more mannequin extras just kinda milling about. The sneaky folks went to go deal with them, which made good sense but did mean I had to stay back so I wouldn\u2019t ruin things. I\u2019m not super bad at sneaking like I am at searching for things, but I\u2019m not nearly as good as Jacob, Insincere Marguerite or Calamity, you know? De la Roche is good at sneaking too, but she wanted to stick back and stay near Lori, and also keep an eye on Ginny. Those three could deal with two mannequin extras that weren\u2019t paying attention to them no problem though.<br /> <br /> We escorted Ginny and Desiree out of the Hedge, and back to the Rose and Thorn so we could check on Flores, who was, well, occupied and probably not planning on meeting anyone in the Hedge. The ladies got rides home from the club that kept them out of the Hedge for a bit (and I got a dance with Calamity) before we headed out ourselves. Our non-Calamity ladies all went back home, while me and Jacob and Calamity went to go get magic-y bits from the briar wolves. Lori in particular was disturbed at the idea of skinning something that used to be human, which, to be fair, was not particularly cool, but that sort of thing comes in handy and they\u2019re not human anymore, you know? Jacob is really good at all the hunting/camping/surviving outside type stuff, and he was super great about explaining everything he was doing and having us help out with stuff. I promised to give him some pointers about working with the leather once we\u2019d cured it.<br /> <br /> I also promised to teach Calamity the Contract of Elements. Boy was I happy to do that. All throughout the fight, she kept overextending and leaving her guard completely down. To be fair, she usually killed whatever she was attacking, but when she didn\u2019t, she got hurt bad. She\u2019s all about a good offense is the best defense, which is cool and all, but I\u2019m happy to show her anything that gives her defense that she can\u2019t give up for more offense. Maybe I can work some of the wolves skin into some magic armor stuff. I dunno a lot about how that works, but I should be able to do something like that, you know?<br /> <br /> We left the stuff we gathered in the Hedge House, and found the ladies watching Am\u00e9lie in the far bedroom. They\u2019d teased me that they were going to have a big orgy while we were gone, but I guess they really were just teasing. It did mean we had a TV setup in that room now, which is the first steps to a totally killer video games room. I mean, I have a moral obligation - Lori has never seen video games other than Pong and Space Invaders! This cannot be allowed to stand, you know? So many awesome games to introduce her to...<br /> <br /> <br /> May 9th, later<br /> <br /> That probably could have gone better. Though, really, maybe not? Joan did agree not to kill anybody out of hand, so that\u2019s really the best thing there. And I couldn\u2019t just not say anything, cause she flat out asked and so it\u2019d be super dishonest and it\u2019s her job to know about things like the mannequin extra things, you know? Also, she would probably have found out about the mannequins and Desiree and Ginny being there anyway, and when she did I wouldn\u2019t necessarily have been there to convince her not to just kill them. So, maybe they went as good as was possible, considering.<br /> <br /> See, we had to turn in the bounty, and over an omelette breakfast (Julia was super adorable asking for an \u201comelette du fromage\u201d over and over again), we decided we all kinda wanted real identities. Like driver\u2019s licenses and things like that. So we headed on over to the Summer Court headquarters to turn in the stuff. That all went super well - a big goat-y looking dude named Old Billy negotiated some with Lori, but she had him around her little finger in no time and he was super cool with getting us some ID.<br /> <br /> There was also a big dude called Percival, which was kinda hilarious, even if he did keep saying I reminded him of green peas. I wonder if there\u2019s Galahad or a Bedivere wandering around town. Maybe we can make up a whole Table. Though, Percival is kinda a douche. I mean, he\u2019s probably really funny, when he\u2019s not just being mean. Like, if the person was ok with his teasing and sarcasm and stuff, you know? But Joan really wasn\u2019t, so it wasn\u2019t cool at all.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Joan asked me if I knew of any new threats in the Courts, so I told her about the mannequin extra things, and that we killed them. Which of course meant I also told her about Ginny and Desiree being there, cause she asked about details and stuff, cause she\u2019s good at her job, you know? She wanted to kill them right off, but I managed to talk her out of that, and offered to go get them to talk with them even, so that Lucian wouldn\u2019t send somebody to get them. I figured if Lucian arranged for them to be gotten, they might show up a bit worse for wear, which Joan confirmed was probably the case. In the end, Insincere Marguerite managed to talk her out of even sending for Ginny, since she came to the Dream House a lot and we could keep an eye on her - Old Billy liked that plan too. He seemed pretty cool. Joan said she\u2019d just watch Desiree too, for now, since I asked, so hopefully that will go alright.<br /> <br /> One other thing was good - De la Roche took Joan out for a sundae, a hot fudge sundae, since Joan was upset over things and Percival kept being a dick. So Joan does have other friends, who care about her too. I was a little worried, cause she seemed like she might be really lonely, but it\u2019s good to have people who will take you out for sundaes when you feel a little down. Also, Lori was really nice to Joan, and made sure to let her know she didn\u2019t want any part of the Spring Court jerkitude about her. So now I just hope Desiree and Ginny don\u2019t get in too much trouble over this. And that they\u2019re not, you know, bad guys.<br /> <br /> <br /> Lorelei\u2019s Diary<br /> <br /> So after Insincere Marguerite and Julia emerged from the boudoir, we piled into the van and headed out to one of the better known local entrances to the Hedge. It was one end of a \u201ctrod,\u201d a relatively stable pathway between two fixed points. The briar wolves had apparently been stalking this trod because it was heavily used by local changelings as a shortcut across town.<br /> <br /> Before we entered the hedge people started activating their defenses, with the Darklings slipping into the shadows and the others triggering their mystical armor. As my own defensive contracts mostly involve magically making myself too intimidating to attack, it seemed counter-productive to activate it too early. We were <u>trying</u> to get the briar wolves to attack us, after all.<br /> <br /> D gave me a quick kiss and an admonishment to be careful before she disappeared into hiding with the others. \u201cI\u2019ll be watching,\u201d she said softly, \u201cI won\u2019t let anything happen to you, Lori.\u201d And then, as far as I could tell, it was just Gawain and me walking slowly along the trod like a pair of young lovers out for a moonlight stroll. I got into the role, and it was even sort of fun for a while\u2026 until we spotted our quarry.<br /> <br /> Two of the briar wolves appeared on the path in front of us. We\u2019d rehearsed what to do in this situation, and my inherent professionalism overwhelmed my mortal terror. In other words, I fell into my role. Gawain and I screamed and ran, but we ran where <u>we</u> wanted to go rather than fleeing blindly further into the Hedge. It helped that the wolves seemed to be trying to herd us in that general direction anyway. Other wolves popped out of the greenery here and there to make sure we were running straight into their trap.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a good thing their rudimentary intelligence didn\u2019t allow them to realize that they were also running straight into <u>ours</u>.<br /> <br /> We also caught a glimpse of a few stranger denizens of the Hedge. They looked like mannequins with blank faces and long swords for arms, but at that time they didn\u2019t seem to have anything to do with either us or the briar wolves, so we ignored them.<br /> <br /> Eventually, Gawain and I found ourselves surrounded by six of the creatures, and decided that the time was ripe to spring our trap. Unfortunately, I think we waited a few seconds too long, because two of the briar wolves had enough time to decide that I was going to be their favorite chew-toy.<br /> <br /> They tore into me pretty badly. I\u2026 well, the pain was nothing compared to being on the Stranger\u2019s table, but still, it\u2019s not an experience I\u2019d care to repeat. I felt teeth and claws sink into me from several different directions before I could react. Shouts and the sounds of weapons being drawn surrounded me, but it was all I could do to summon up my glamour and put up an intimidating aura in the hope that the wolves would abandon me in favor of other targets.<br /> <br /> It seemed to work; I was left pretty much alone for the rest of the fight. I began to gather my healing energies in the hopes of repairing the damage I\u2019d been dealt\u2026 but then I glanced over at Gawain. He\u2019d been hurt just as badly as me, and the wolves were still attacking him. I let the energy I\u2019d been collecting flow into him, and he looked a lot better immediately.<br /> <br /> A few seconds after that, I felt gentle fingers on the back of my neck. \u201cJust concentrate on keeping the others fighting,\u201d D\u2019s voice whispered in my ear. \u201cLike I said, I won\u2019t let anything happen to you.\u201d And then I felt a rush of warmth flowing in to me\u2026 and my wounds started to close. Not completely; I was still pretty badly hurt, but it was obvious that D\u2019s touch had somehow healed me a little.<br /> <br /> She explained the effect to me later. Like many of her darkling kin, she can drain small amounts of life force out of others with her touch. She has a somewhat rarer gift, however: the ability to transfer that life force to another living being through a second touch. So D spent the rest of the fight pulling living energy out of the briar wolves and sending it into my body to heal my wounds.<br /> <br /> As the fight progressed, we were joined by a few unexpected guests. Two more briar wolves entered the fray, followed by four of those odd mannequin things, and the most unlikely pair of changelings imaginable\u2026 Ginny and Desiree. The mannequins were attacking our fellow lost, but they were also doing what they could to fend off the briar wolves. Reading between the lines, I think the wolves interrupted something and the mannequins had no choice but to defend their \u201cprize.\u201d<br /> <br /> I healed the group as much as I could, but in the end I simply ran out of juice. It\u2019s exhausting trying to keep the glamour flowing in exactly the right way; it takes a level of concentration I never really knew I had before. It seemed like I had to devote all of my being into each casting, and if I let my mind wander for even a second, it wouldn\u2019t work. But then I turned my magic on D, and it was\u2026 easy. Almost effortless. It was like her wounds <u>wanted</u> to be healed, and all I had to do was ask.<br /> <br /> In the end, my friends made short work of both the briar wolves and the mannequin things\u2026 and then Calamity turned toward Desiree with a look of manic glee. Gawain restrained her before she could attack the poor girl, and the rest of us looked at her like she was crazy. \u201cWhat everyone says about you is true,\u201d Calamity spat at Desiree. \u201cYou\u2019re a loyalist. Those things weren\u2019t really trying to hurt you; they were holding back!\u201d<br /> <br /> Well, you could have fooled me, but admittedly I had been devoting most of my attention during the fight to the twin concerns of healing my friends and not dying. Jacob confirmed Calamity\u2019s take on the encounter, though he wasn\u2019t as quick to label Desiree as a loyalist.<br /> <br /> Desiree confirmed that the mannequin things <u>were</u> servants of the Director (called \u201cExtras,\u201d appropriately enough), but claimed that she didn\u2019t know why they were after her or why they would particularly care about keeping her safe. Ginny confirmed that the Extras hadn\u2019t attacked Desiree at all until she became aggressive against them in Ginny\u2019s defense\u2026 which brought up a few additional questions, like what the two of them were doing in the Hedge at night in the first place.<br /> <br /> Desiree claimed that she had just been walking home, taking a shortcut through the Hedge, which is reasonable and common enough. She ran into Ginny accidentally as she was passing through. Ginny was cagier about her answer, and hemmed and hawed for a while before admitting that she was meeting someone there. We asked her who, and she said she didn\u2019t want to talk about it. I explained that we needed to know because her paramour might be in danger, or could have set her up, and she reluctantly told us that she was supposed to meet Flores that evening for a clandestine encounter.<br /> <br /> I was prepared to accept this explanation, but while the others were talking it out, D touched my shoulder, glanced at Ginny, and gave a very slight shake of her head. When she was relatively certain we wouldn\u2019t be overheard, she went on to explain that Ginny\u2019s story made no sense. If Flores and Ginny were an item, neither one of them would have any particular reason to hide that fact, so Ginny\u2019s secretive attitude about their meeting made no sense. What\u2019s more, Flores tends to \u201centertain\u201d guests at the Rose and Thorn, so why would she agree to meet a paramour in the Hedge?<br /> <br /> It\u2019s suspicious behavior, but not necessarily damning. It\u2019s fairly well known in the area that Ginny is a lesbian, and she could have been meeting someone else in the Hedge for a secretive romantic rendezvous\u2026 someone who is not openly \u201cout.\u201d In that case, Ginny could simply be protecting her lover\u2019s identity. But I have to admit, her behavior is suspicious, especially considering all the intrigue going on in the area of late.<br /> <br /> D, Gawain and I kept a close eye on <u>both</u> of our unexpected companions while the others ambushed the remaining Extras in the area. Once that little chore had been taken care of, we exited the Hedge and made our way to the Rose and Thorn. Flores was there, by the way, entertaining a guest in her upstairs rooms. So I guess D was right, and Ginny was lying.<br /> <br /> Ace was <u>also</u> there. Apparently we forgot to take him with us when we left the club earlier that evening, and he\u2019d consequently decided to drink the bar into submission. It looked like he was well on his way to accomplishing that goal by the time we caught back up with him.<br /> <br /> I needed glamour pretty badly by that point, so I decided to dance. Once again, I felt all eyes in the club turn to me, and again I became the focus of all that desire. It was <u>beautiful</u>, and I walked off that dance floor a few minutes later feeling refreshed. One of the patrons referred to me as the \u201cQueen of the Zombie Prom,\u201d at which point I realized I was still wearing the slashed and blood-stained sundress I\u2019d worn into battle earlier. I\u2019d been able to heal my own wounds after the fight, but there was no putting the dress right again. Oops.<br /> <br /> In any case, enough glamour flowed into me from the onlookers to completely replenish my supply. I was still physically and mentally exhausted, of course, but the magic was there, and that helped.<br /> <br /> We scooped Ace up and returned to Gawain\u2019s van. Jacob, Gawain, and Calamity decided to head back into the Hedge and \u2013 ugh \u2013 <u>skin</u> the briar wolves so that they would have some vaguely mystical materials with which to make clothing or armor. Mercifully, they decided to drop D, Marguerite, Ace, and me off at the Dream House first. I know that the briar wolves were monsters who were hurting and killing people, and that they had to be dealt with. But they used to be humans\u2026 humans who got lost in the Hedge and weren\u2019t \u201clucky\u201d enough to catch the attention of the Gentry. There but for the grace of God\u2026<br /> <br /> When we got back to the House, Insincere Marguerite was flirting pretty heavily with D and me. And this time it wasn\u2019t her usual playful flirts; she seemed really serious. I glanced at Julia, who looked nervous but excited at the prospect. The look on D\u2019s face worried me a little\u2026 she seemed eager for the chance to sleep with Marguerite. Maybe a little too eager.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt could be fun,\u201d she said noncommittally when I drew her aside. She must have caught something in my expression, because the gleam in her eye faded after a moment. \u201cIt\u2019s okay if you don\u2019t want to, Lori,\u201d she said, squeezing my shoulder, \u201cit\u2019s not going to be a deal-breaker, I swear.\u201d<br /> <br /> I took her hand in mine gratefully. \u201cI just\u2026\u201d I started, but found it hard to continue. \u201cI don\u2019t think I\u2019m ready. I\u2019m just\u2026 would it make me sound like a wimp or a flake if I said I was insecure?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> She smiled and kissed my forehead. \u201cNo,\u201d she said gently, \u201cnot at all.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m not saying no,\u201d I continued quickly. \u201cI\u2019m just saying\u2026 not right now.\u201d<br /> <br /> Marguerite was looking at us quizzically, but managed to conceal her disappointment admirably when we explained our decision. Instead of a night of raw unbridled passion, the four of us settled onto a couch in front of the TV and watched a French movie called <u>Amelie</u>. It was fun. Lighthearted, funny, and romantic. I don\u2019t think D enjoyed it as much as I did, but we both reveled in the closeness as I snuggled up against her.<br /> <br /> Later, as we were lying in bed together, I tried to apologize to D for my squeamishness. \u201cIt\u2019s not that I don\u2019t like Marguerite,\u201d I explained. \u201cShe\u2019s one of my best friends these days, and I\u2019d be lying if I said I hadn\u2019t imagined being with her and Julia on more than one occasion. It\u2019s just that\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> D put a finger over my lips. \u201cIt\u2019s just that I said she reminded me of an old girlfriend, and then the next day I was practically panting to hop into the sack with her,\u201d she finished for me. \u201cShit, I\u2019m sorry, Lori. I wasn\u2019t thinking about how that might make you feel.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s okay, D. I\u2019m really not a jealous person. I\u2019d just like to give us a little more time to figure out what it is we have here before we start pushing the boundaries. Is that okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cMore than okay,\u201d she said.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo,\u201d I said, bringing up something I\u2019d been thinking about for hours at last, \u201cwhen I healed you earlier, it was easier than it had been with the others. It was like I didn\u2019t need to put any glamour into the contract at all.\u201d<br /> <br /> D shrugged. \u201cMust have triggered the catch without knowing it,\u201d she said lightly. Most of the magical contracts changelings use have a \u201ccatch,\u201d a condition under which we can access their power without expending our own glamour. It\u2019s a useful loophole when you can get it to work.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, I know what the catch for that clause is,\u201d I replied, letting a little mischief into my voice.<br /> <br /> D looked at me sharply. \u201cNow you\u2019re making me nervous,\u201d she said. \u201cYou gonna tell me, or leave me in suspense?\u201d<br /> <br /> I grinned. \u201cThe catch is triggered if the person being healed has told me they loved me within the last day,\u201d I explained. \u201cSo I guess that explains what \u2018<i>te amo, Lori!\u2019</i> means, huh?\u201d I\u2019d heard her shout it out a few times as she reached her peak, and it had sounded vaguely familiar to me, like something I used to know but had forgotten.<br /> <br /> D\u2019s face turned red. \u201cThat was just\u2026 I mean\u2026\u201d she stammered. It was adorable.<br /> <br /> \u201cI know,\u201d I said, rescuing her with a quick kiss. \u201cThroes of passion, heat of the moment and all that. If it helps, I\u2019ve almost said the same a few times. I won\u2019t take it as a promise, D\u2026 but thanks for saying it anyway.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. She didn\u2019t meet my eyes, but I could see the corners of her mouth turn upward in a shy smile.<br /> <br /> Reassured, I got up and turned off the light. \u201cWe should probably get some sleep if we\u2019re going to turn in those bounties in the morning,\u201d I said.<br /> <br /> \u201cReady when you are,\u201d she said, recovering from her sudden bout of shyness quickly. \u201cOnly, could you\u2026?\u201d She trailed off.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat?\u201d I asked as I lay back down next to her.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, it\u2019s stupid,\u201d she mumbled in reply.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat?\u201d I asked again, more firmly, as I snuggled into the crook of her arm.<br /> <br /> \u201cI was going to ask if you could sing for me,\u201d she admitted. \u201cJust a little bit before we go to sleep.\u201d<br /> <br /> I thought about it. \u201cYou know I don\u2019t know much about modern music yet,\u201d I said apologetically, \u201cI\u2019ve been out of the loop for a while. I probably wouldn\u2019t know many songs you like.\u201d<br /> <br /> I could feel her shake her head. \u201cI\u2026\u201d she began, \u201cI sort of wanted to hear you sing something <u>you</u> like,\u201d she breathed.<br /> <br /> I considered for a moment, and then launched softly into an <i>a capella</i> version of Paul McCartney\u2019s \u201cBlackbird.\u201d It\u2019s a surprisingly deep and complicated song for such a simple-sounding ditty, with an evolving tempo and non-traditional scales, but I\u2019ve always liked it, and it\u2019s seemed particularly near to my heart in the wake of my transformation.<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026you were only waiting for this moment to arise,\u201d I finished softly.<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you,\u201d de la Rocha whispered, kissing the top of my head, \u201cthat was beautiful.\u201d<br /> <br /> When everyone was back at the house and awake late the next morning, D offered to introduce us to a few people at the church where the local Summer Court tends to congregate. I\u2019m glad she was there. The Summer Court plays host to some\u2026 \u201cintense\u201d personalities, and without D around things might have gotten out of hand.<br /> <br /> We turned the bounties in to a satyr-like beast named Old Billy, who seemed like a nice enough guy. He offered us several options for our rewards, including money, goblin fruits, and hedge-spun clothing. We\u2019d already discussed what we wanted to do as a group, though. Calamity gave me a gentle push toward Old Billy, and I began the negotiation process.<br /> <br /> I am Lorelei Grace. Everyone who knows me knows that. Most of my changeling friends, however, also know that Lorelei Grace doesn\u2019t really exist as far as the government is concerned. My other name, Juliette Wells, is currently claimed by a fifty-four year old woman in the Midwest, so that identity is useless to me. I have a few scraps of documentation, like a driver\u2019s license, but if a cop was to check my license number at the records office (or however they do that these days), he\u2019d find out that it was a fake pretty quickly. Most of my friends are in the same boat.<br /> <br /> So we decided to have the Summer Court bulk up our identities a bit. Old Billy was a little hesitant about providing so many backgrounds and documents, but I managed to talk him into it in the end. It\u2019ll take a few days, but soon enough my friends and I should have at least a rudimentary presence in the official records of this country. Hell, we might even be able to vote!<br /> <br /> There were a few other changelings there, including Joan and an ogre named Percival (which Gawain thought was hilarious for some reason) who might just be the rudest person I have ever met. He seemed to have a snide comment prepared for every occasion, and took particular delight in tormenting poor Joan. Old Billy later confided in us that Percival acts the way he does to create a ready supply of anger for the Summer Courtiers to snack on, which I <u>guess</u> makes sense, but it was still very off-putting. At one point he implied that it was a good thing I had nice boobs to make up for my lack of a personality. I calmly informed him that I happen to have a fucking <u>amazing</u> personality to back up my admittedly spectacular boobs, and left it at that.<br /> <br /> Joan overheard us talking to Old Billy about our adventure in the Hedge, and asked several pointed questions about both Ginny and Desiree\u2019s behavior. She seemed to think that their suspicious actions were proof positive of their Loyalist tendencies, and wanted to go hunt both of them down right then and there. Luckily we were able to talk her down, but Percival\u2019s barbed comments about her zealous nature did nothing to help the situation. In the end, Joan agreed to limit herself to watching Desiree closely for now, and allowing our motley to keep an eye on Ginny (since she spends so much time performing at the Dream House anyway), but I could tell she wasn\u2019t really happy about it. What\u2019s more, I could see that some of Percival\u2019s jibes were starting to get to her.<br /> <br /> \u201cJoan,\u201d I said seriously when the conversation ebbed, \u201cwe know that you\u2019re passionate about your work because you really care about keeping this freehold safe, and we appreciate it. We should probably tell you that more often. You don\u2019t deserve the abuse you take from some ungrateful assholes.\u201d I glanced pointedly at Percival when I said that, and then played my ace.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd you don\u2019t deserve what some members of my Court have done to you, either. I just want you to know that not all Spring Courtiers are like that. Some of us want nothing to do with that stupid bet.\u201d<br /> <br /> Joan looked at me for a few seconds. Her fa\u00e7ade didn\u2019t slip even a fraction of an inch, but I think I saw something flicker behind her eyes. \u201cThank you,\u201d she said softly, and gave me a nod.<br /> <br /> D put a hand on my shoulder. \u201cSorry, babe, but\u2026 would you mind if I bailed for a while? I promise I\u2019ll see you at the show tonight.\u201d<br /> <br /> I turned to look at my girlfriend and arched an eyebrow. \u201cWhat\u2019s up?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> D shook her head. \u201cNothing much. I just think somebody needs to go out for a sundae,\u201d she explained. I looked over at Joan. Joan turned away stoically.<br /> <br /> D leaned in closer. \u201cHot fudge sundae?\u201d she asked with a crooked grin.<br /> <br /> Joan turned back, and she was actually smiling. It was startling; it turned her rigid austere beauty into something soft and warm. She shook her head. \u201cOnly for you, de la Rocha,\u201d she said softly. My honey sure knows how to bring out the best in people!<br /> <br /> Joan turned to regard me formally. \u201cI hope you don\u2019t mind me stealing your date,\u201d she said, and I could tell that it was a serious question.<br /> <br /> \u201cNot at all,\u201d I said with what I hope she took as a friendly smile. \u201cYou two have fun.\u201d I gave D a quick kiss goodbye, and the two of them went off together.<br /> <br /> After that the rest of us drove back home. I\u2019ve been spending the afternoon lazing around my room, taking little catnaps and writing this diary entry in between. I\u2019ve got a couple of numbers in tonight\u2019s show, but there\u2019s no real need to rehearse; I could sing those songs in my sleep if I had to. It\u2019s left me a lot of time for reflection, which is both a good and a bad thing.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve been thinking a lot about my relationship with D, unsurprisingly. She\u2019s off having ice cream with a drop-dead gorgeous girl at the moment, and that doesn\u2019t bother me in the least. So why am I so worked up over this proposition from Marguerite? Is it really just because she reminds D of Madame Spidertoes, or is there more to it? There\u2019s a part of me that wants to just take the plunge and go through with the whole sordid affair. I know I\u2019d feel much better at the end of the night when D and I were back in each other\u2019s arms and no one else existed in the whole world.<br /> <br /> But then\u2026 what if I\u2019m wrong? I haven\u2019t known Marguerite long, but I know she can be something of a control freak where her relationships are concerned. What if she gets her claws into D and won\u2019t let go? What if D remembers how Madame Spidertoes made her feel, and decides that she needs someone like that in her life again?<br /> <br /> What if D chooses <u>her</u> instead of <u>me</u>? What if someone else takes that place in her heart? What if I\u2019m not the one she burns for, dreams of, and cries out \u201c<i>te amo\u201d</i> to in the middle of the night?<br /> <br /> What if I\u2019m no longer the prettiest bird in the cage?<br /> <br /> Dammit.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T13:32:11-07:00","id":245637,"title":"","content":"<br /> <b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> <b><u><b><u>Friday May 9<sup>th</sup></u></b> </u></b><br /> <br /> I am a happy little monster, yes I am. Last night was glorious fun. We set out to the state park and crossed into the Hedge as planned. Insincere Marguerite sprang up into the trees and vanished. Jacob slipped ahead of the group. De la Rocha and myself spread out to flank our faux picnickers. We walked along for a little while and then sure enough Yogi and Boo-Boo and a couple of their friends appeared. I am going to have to work with Gawain on his acting but Lori carried the scared witless off well enough for both of them. I imagine it helped that she was actually afraid for her life. But she wanted to play bait and she did point out that she'd have been no good trying to stay hidden. Still, I do wish we'd had our plan worked out a little tighter and kept her from getting hurt.<br /> <br /> We ran at first, the wolves chasing but letting their prey stay ahead. Pretty soon another pair of them appeared, blocking one of two paths and channeling Gawain and Lori down another path. So far so good we thought. But at the next intersection, we saw the next duo of wolves being chased by a pair of strange faceless things with swords for hands. I thought maybe Winter Court was involved but at any rate it was clear that we were done gathering briar-wolves and it was time to spring the trap. <br /> <br /> Gawain and Lori turned and we all started to rush in but holy mother of pearl those furry bastards are fast. They were on the pair before we could engage them and they tore into Lori and my man hard. Lorelei bore it well, making herself beautiful and starting to dispense the Spring healing magics. Fuck but that girl suffers beautifully...<br /> <br /> I handed Gawain's sword off to him as Jacob and De la Rocha started to hit the beasts. Insincere Marguerite dropped a couple of darkness curses from above and we started to turn things around rather quickly. The wolves were caught in close and couldn't focus on any one of us. They fought savagely with all the panic and desperation of cornered animals but we were too strong and Lori's healing kept us all up and fighting while they went down one by one under our blades. Oh goddess their fear was flowing almost as freely as their blood and I let myself fall upon them without hesitation. Damn but it felt so fucking good. <br /> <br /> Then we spotted four of those faceless things with the sword arms chasing Ginny and Desiree right toward us. Both girls were hurt, but I could see right away that the things were holding back on Desiree but not poor Ginny. There were still wolves up as they stumbled into the middle of the fray and after a moment's hesitation I opted to stay on them to be sure none escaped. The extras (as we learned later they were called) are fast and strong but not very intelligent or aware. They completely ignored us until Gawain cut one in half. <br /> <br /> And before we could sort all of that out, two more wolves showed up, hotly pursued by two more extras. They were busy fighting each other but once they fell into the swirl of our razors they took notice of us. Not that it really helped them, we weren't leaving monsters alive last night, whether they were hedge-spawn or minions of the Gentry. And when we'd put the last of them down, I turned toward Desiree. But both Gawain and Jacob interposed themselves. I pointed out that the extras had been pulling their punches and Jacob agreed but claimed that Desiree hadn't been aware of it. I'm not sure but I wasn't going to go through them over it. <br /> <br /> Desiree explained that the extras were minions of the Director. Ginny told us they'd ignored Desiree but she'd attacked them to try to drive them off from Ginny. I guess they simply weren't programed to harm one of their master's creations or maybe they were trying to take her alive. This was around the time Ginny lied to us about meeting someone (or at least that that someone was Flores). I get that she might have good reason not to say who was meeting her, but at the time we were concerned about the safety of anyone out there with briar-wolves and sword for hand mooks all over the damn place. <br /> <br /> I used path-finding and found two more extras and the last two briar-wolves fleeing hard and fast. Sadly, we opted to let the wolves go since we would have been hard pressed to catch them if we could have at all. But they're not likely to return and we broke the pack pretty hard so the area should be safe for the time being. As for the other two extras, Insincere Marguerite, Jacob, and myself put them down like stray dogs. Damn it felt good to get my hands so bloody.<br /> <br /> Once the Hedge was clear, we escorted the ladies back to the Rose and Thorn so they could get mundane transport home. It was pretty clear that Flores hadn't made plans to meet Ginny and that did sour my mood a little. I mean, I like her and I would hate for her to be a loyalist or something. As we were at the bar, I started to grab a drink (my first since Truth or Dare night) but Gawain interrupted and asked me to dance. I don't think he did it intentionally, he's not that subtle. It was just timing. And despite being bloody and ragged, I let him whisk me out onto the floor and spin me about a bit. Hell, I was still flying high enough from the fight that it felt good just to move and it made him happy which felt even better. After a bit we did pack it in to get clean clothes and such.<br /> <br /> Jacob wasn't happy about leaving the bodies of the wolves to rot and I had to agree it seemed wasteful. Gawain joined us and the three of us headed back to skin them and collect their useful bits. It was nice to spend some time with Jacob and see him being talkative and all. He knows a lot about survival and he was quite patient as he explained and showed us how to clean and skin the bodies and then to prepare the skins for leather. Gawain's going to be taking point on the working of that leather I think and I shall simply try not to mess anything up and learn a little. The rest of the girls stayed behind and apparently ended up watching some romantic French movie. They were paired off in one of the spare bedrooms when we returned, De la Rocha and Lori on a loveseat and Insincere Marguerite with her sweet little julia. We only peeked in for a couple of minutes before I informed Gawain that we needed a shower. He agreed and then once it clicked that I was suggesting one shower for the both us his expression lit up. I grinned and took him by the hand to spend the next few hours having my way with him since I was still keyed up from the fight. I was a rather enthusiastic little monster but I don't think he minded in the slightest.<br /> <br /> Sometime later (I think the sun was creeping up outside) I found myself curled up small and tight against his side as he drifted into a thankfully easy sleep. I lingered a little, savoring the sight of him so peaceful as I traced the seams and rivets of his skin. His time in Arcadia was terrible. Sealed into that armor and forced to be the executioner in his Keeper's horrible dream play. I imagine it hurt, to have those plates fastened around his flesh, to be trapped in them like that. But strangely, I'm glad that he is the way he is. I can curl in tight and not have to worry about cutting him accidentally. There is something in the solid feel of him that absolutely dispels any thoughts of the Whispering Voices. It's only been a week but I already can't imagine sleeping without his arm around me as I nestle in against him. I guess in that moment I realized that he is not the only one that's in love. It's not the way I used to imagine it but I can't deny that I care for him more than anything. I am indeed <i>his</i> monster.<br /> <br /> Afternoon followed a blissfully good sleep and came with that feeling of waking up right where I belonged, still curled in safe and protected in my knight's arms. We had omelets and I just sat and basked in the banter and sipped my coffee and felt... peaceful? Well, maybe not but certainly relaxed and at ease. We went to the Summer Court to deliver the proof of our deed and report our success. Lori negotiated with Old Billy (an aptly named beast that I had not met before but who seemed like a decent enough chap) and secured some further bolstering of our false identities. Nothing bulletproof but they should stand up to a casual background check now at least. <br /> <br /> Joan was also there as was an ogre named Percival that I'd not met previously either. And once he opened his fucking mouth, I could have lived without meeting Percival. Yeah, Joan isn't easy to deal with but for the love of whatever cosmic thunderer you bow to that ass-hat was downright caustic. And as we were trying to let her know that we'd run across a pack of minions belonging to a known and troublesome Gentry without starting a witch hunt against either Desiree or more importantly Ginny we did not need him verbally pissing on Joan's corn flakes. Thankfully, she ignored him for the most part. We talked her down to just watching Desiree and letting us investigate Ginny. Then De la Rocha took her out for hot fudge sundaes and the woman actually smiled a little. I have to say, I was glad to see them head off. As much as I find her paranoia difficult, Joan herself seems genuinely devoted to the welfare of the Freehold. And well, I can't say I know exactly what flavor of hell she went through but clearly it broke something inside her pretty badly. And I swear, if I hadn't been so sated from last night I might just have broken a few things inside that fucking ogre. I am going to have to steer clear of him in the future to avoid the temptation of getting myself into trouble by removing his foot from his mouth and shoving it up his ass. <br /> <br /> On the way home we stopped at the tobacconist\u2019s so I could pick up a pair of nice cigars for Annika and myself to share later. I think a caught Lori rolling her eyes a bit but she didn't say anything. I'm not sure exactly way she dislikes Annika so, but given my own penchant for phantom grudges I'm not going to throw any stones. Currently I am dressed in one of the outfits Lori helped me pick up for hostess duty. Honestly, I am not completely sure about the 'timeless' nature of this powder blue tux but it certainly is striking. Of course, wearing a dress shirt cut low enough to show off what her girl would call my 'belly jewel' doesn't hurt. I am still not entirely used to wearing things like this but I trust Lori's sense of fashion. I mean, normally I wouldn't give a rat's ass what anyone thought about what I was wearing (or not wearing or almost wearing) but when I'm representing the house like this it matters. Oh well, no time to change anyway at this point so I might as well head down and enjoy Gawain's reaction while I wait for Annika to arrive. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Well, we went into the hedge looking for a fight, and we were not disappointed. Lorelei and Gawain pretended to be a pair of inattentive picnickers while the rest of us spread out and hid in the underbrush, behind rocks or up trees. Marguerite can disappear when she puts her mind to it. It\u2019s damn impressive. Calamity wasn\u2019t too bad either. It didn\u2019t take long for the wolves to come across our \u201cbait\u201d and attack. Well, four of them ran at our people chasing them back down the path. Then two more jumped out and herded Lori and Gawain down the other fork, and then the fight began.<br /> <br /> We managed to take the briar wolves by surprise, which worked out nicely. The fight itself was a free for all melee. I had at least two wolves attacking me at any given time. They missed most of the time, but one of them managed to get a hit in. Those claws leave a pretty good mark too. More scars to add to the collection. Heh. The \u201cnot cool\u201d thing about the fight was the wolf going after Lorelei first thing. Maybe is saw her as the weakest target, but it tore into her the first chance it got. It hit her hard. <br /> <br /> We never should have used her as bait. Gawain is a fucking suit of armor. Lorelei is not. She is a non-combatant. She shouldn\u2019t have been put into the middle of all this shit. We should have used someone else to act as the bait. Hell, I would have made better bait. Not that Lorelei didn\u2019t convince the wolves that she was terrified, she was, but I can act scared. If I got hurt it wouldn\u2019t have been as bad as her getting cut like that. I\u2019m used to the pain. She doesn\u2019t deserve that. <br /> <br /> Other than that, the others handled themselves well. As soon as she could, Calamity handed off the long sword to Gawain, who proceeded to mow things down. It was damn impressive. I never want to be on the receiving end of his wrath\u2026\u2019cause damn! There was one wolf that got a decent hit in on Calamity, and moments later was cut in half by our dear Green Knight\u2019s sword. Calamity was her usual, efficient self in taking down the wolves. Though, I did notice this time that she was going all out on the attack and leaving herself open for retaliation. A few times the wolves obliged and hit her when her guard was down. I wonder if I need to talk to her about that. If it happened just the once I might have thought that it was a rare kind of thing and she just did it because she needed the energy for that attack, but she did it several times. It happened at least three or four times that I know of, which kind of has me concerned. She got hit. Several times, and not light scratches either. If she keeps this up something is going to hit her hard and kill her or hurt her in a way that she can\u2019t come all the way back from.<br /> <br /> I saw it happen in the Lady\u2019s realm. People who were either too cocky or had conscious or subconscious suicidal tendencies going all out in a fight against Rook, myself, or one of the many wild animals. A lot of them died, and some of them got maimed and ran off to tend their wounds. The next time I saw them, they had a permanent limp, were missing some body part, or had some kind of brain damage that affected their memory or reason. It never ended well for them. They were just that much easier to pick off by us, or by the animals. I don\u2019t want to see Calamity succumb to something that can be avoided.<br /> <br /> I also have to wonder if it\u2019s a conscious choice on her part to forgo defending or if she doesn\u2019t realize that she\u2019s doing it. If she\u2019s doing it intentionally then it might be easy enough to address. If she doesn\u2019t know that she\u2019s doing it, it might be harder to fix. I don\u2019t want her to get hurt, and I know that Gawain will fucking mow down anything that hurts his girl, but there might come a time when someone can\u2019t get to her in time. <br /> <br /> She calls herself a monster and I\u2019m pretty sure she honestly believes that. She may have darker impulses, and I know she enjoys fighting, but she is not a monster. She may be closer than any of the others, but she\u2019s still not that close. I just don\u2019t want her to lose herself in some sense of guilt or self-hatred that leads to her death. She is a good person. More so than she believes. I just don\u2019t have the heart to tell her what really makes a monster. The kind words, the promises of protection, the lies. All the fucking lies. The betrayal. Being a killer doesn\u2019t make someone a monster. It\u2019s the nice guys that promise safety and only bring death. And not for revenge. Not for justice. They bring death on a whim. On the orders of their Lady. Because they\u2019re bored. Fuck\u2026<br /> <br /> **** **** **** <br /> <br /> Okay\u2026that went to a dark place. I\u2019m back. Had something to drink. Vodka. Stereotypical as it is, I like it. There was an already open bottle at the bar, and it\u2019s bad luck to leave the bottle open like that and not finish its contents. So, I did. Wow, it\u2019s fucking early in the morning. As if it wasn\u2019t early enough when we got back from the hedge. Ha. Anyhoo\u2026 During the fight in the hedge we not only had the fun of fighting briar wolves, we fought some faceless mannequin things that appear to work for The Director. They were chasing Ginny and Desiree. We decided that they needed to die and attacked them. They ignored us almost entirely until we actively started hitting them. They were fixated on attacking the two newcomers up until that point. Funny thing is though, while they attacked Desiree they pulled their punches. She didn\u2019t realize that they were doing it though. I think she thought they were intending to kill her, like they were the rest of us. <br /> <br /> All told we killed eight briar wolves and six mannequins. Two of the wolves got away, but still not bad for a night\u2019s work. Everyone fought well. De la Rocha had a neat trick where she could steal the life force from an enemy and use it to heal a friend. She did that a few times to heal her sweetheart. Neat trick. Wonder if anyone can learn to do that? Might be neat for Lorelei to learn something like that. I mean, she is already a good healer with the Spring court abilities, but De la Rocha\u2019s little trick might be good if Lori got tired and it might be easier to use someone else\u2019s energy to heal folks than her own. It\u2019s gotta be draining to do that much healing. Maybe I\u2019ll ask her. <br /> <br /> Thankfully, Lorelei was able to heal herself and the others. I think she got everyone up to snuff before she got too tired to keep going. I know Gawain got hurt defending folks, especially Calamity. Calamity herself got herself into the thick of it time and again. Marguerite kept up the shadow attacks. I think she was slowing the enemy down here and there. I was not able to pay close attention to all she did, but I know she helped me with one of the mannequin things that was trying to go back to its master. Hell, even De la Rocha did her part. She drained the life force from the enemy and used it to heal her sweetie or herself. I did not expect her to be a front line combatant, and she\u2019s not, but she\u2019s more than proved herself useful in a fight.<br /> <br /> Of course at the end of the fight we had to persuade Calamity that Desiree was not conspiring with the \u201cextras.\u201d I stood between Calamity and the object of her suspicion and convinced her that Desiree was not aware of the \u201cextras\u201d pulling their attacks. As far as she was concerned, they were trying to kill her just like they planned for the rest of us. We wrapped up The Director\u2019s blank faced dolls, and most of the wolves. Two of the wolves got away, but there was no way that we were going to catch up with them. After that we made our way back to Santa Monica. We figured most folks could find a ride home from there, and we could confirm Ginny\u2019s story<br /> <br /> After the immediate threat was over we got a chance to talk. Ginny explained that she was in the hedge waiting to meet someone. That someone being Flora. Desiree said that she was cutting through the hedge as a shortcut from one place to another. They just happened to meet up when the Extras showed up. The girls, or maybe just one of them, the details are hazy now, freaked out and attacked the mannequin things. Then said mannequin things attacked the girls. They ran, and ended up leading the \u201cunfriendlies\u201d to us. It all worked out in the end. We laid waste to the servants of the The Director and the wolves we\u2019d originally went into the hedge to fight.<br /> <br /> Of course it was after Desiree and Ginny had left that the real conversation started. Calamity did not believe the story that Ginny spun about meeting Flora in the hedge. When we got back Flora was with someone and it seemed that she had no intention of leaving. This means that Ginny lied about who she was meeting in the hedge, or lied about her purpose altogether. At this point I\u2019m not sure what to think. I\u2019d like to give Ginny the benefit of the doubt. At least I\u2019m pretty sure that she doesn\u2019t have anything to do with The Director. Those Extras seemed rather keen on killing her outright and they weren\u2019t pulling their punches. They were trying to kill her. That doesn\u2019t mean that her plans in the hedge were benign. They could have just been interrupted. They could have been perfectly innocent, but if they were, then why lie? It doesn\u2019t make sense. She was hiding something by lying. I just don\u2019t know what yet.<br /> <br /> Desiree is another story. She honestly thought that the Extras were out to kill her, but in reality they were just taking token pot shots at her as she fled. It\u2019s entirely possible that they were conditioned or ordered not to attack The Director\u2019s toys. If Desiree is a pawn of her Keeper, she is not aware of it. At least not yet. It will be worthwhile to keep an eye on her for the foreseeable future. <br /> <br /> After the serious discussion and Gawain getting Calamity to dance with him, I announced my intention to go back into the hedge and salvage what I could from the briar wolf bodies. Gawain and Calamity seemed interested, so we headed back the way we had come just a short while ago. We found the bodies where we\u2019d left them, and I was about to start skinning the first one when I was asked if I could show them how to skin the kill and prepare the hide. I figured what the heck and started to explain what I was doing as I did it. I guess I didn\u2019t really think about all the steps that you must take to properly skin an animal and prepare the hide for use. I\u2019ve done it so often over the years that I didn\u2019t really think about the steps anymore, but Calamity asking questions in a genuinely interested tone made me slow down and think about what I was doing. So, in what definitely took twice as long as it would normally, I demonstrated cleaning the hide and separating the useful parts from the rest. Calamity and Gawain helped with the rest of the kills, and with only a couple of rough starts we had all of the briar wolves skinned and prepared.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think I\u2019ve talked so much since I got back from Her realm, not all in one go anyway. Gawain just listened, even when my voice got hoarse. Calamity on the other hand seemed interested in keeping me talking. I\u2019m not sure if it was just the fact that I\u2019d talked so much lately and she wanted to keep the trend up, or if they were actually interested in what I had to say. They did seem interested in my explanations, so I just kept going. They started to help after the first one, and with only a few beginner mistakes we managed to get everything that we could from the bodies. I will admit that it was kind of nice to have someone to work alongside while doing this kind of work. It\u2019s definitely not glamorous or exciting, but it is necessary if you want to survive in The Lady\u2019s realm, and plenty of other places here in \u201cthe world.\u201d I remember helping my father skin rabbits or deer when we lived in Russia. We lived in the country, and as much as I\u2019d like to say everywhere in the world is up to \u201cmodern\u201d standards, that would be a lie. So, we supplemented where we needed to when it came to food and clothes. Mostly we cured the skins and sold them and used the money to buy clothes. The meat we ate.<br /> <br /> I made the mistake of telling someone in my class at school when I first moved to the United States that I had hunted deer. They looked at me with revulsion and asked how I could be so much a monster as to kill a poor defenseless deer. I don\u2019t remember what I said to them, but looking back I can think of several things. Bucks have antlers and outweigh humans by a good bit. You piss one off, or injure it, they will fucking gut you. I decided not to mention the rabbits. Figured that would go even worse. Though I did get compliments on my winter gloves. I just laughed.<br /> <br /> So, after the second excursion into the hedge we headed back to the house with our haul. Most of the stuff we stored in the garage, the meat went in the big freezer. We then went our separate ways, showered and went to bed. Well, I have yet to sleep, but I\u2019m getting there. I just need to rewrap my wounds before I do. I hadn\u2019t even really thought about it until we were hauling stuff back to the house. I felt something in my side twinge and I was reminded of the wounds one of the wolves gave me. I suppose it\u2019s only fair that it would hurt as I was carrying their carcasses back to the house. I suppose I should go downstairs and get some of the actual medical supplies we have on hand. Store bought stuff will undoubtedly work better than strips of cloth and moss.<br /> <br /> Actually, that gave me an idea. Calamity and Gawain seemed interested in the survival skills I showed them earlier, with skinning the wolves. I wonder if they\u2019d be interested in other stuff along those same lines. There are several tricks I learned over the years to treat wounds and infections, or to find and collect water. Deer stomachs make excellent water-skins. Certain kinds of moss work really well to stop bleeding, as do spiderwebs. Little stuff like that might come in handy if we find ourselves in a situation where alternate means of healing, like Lorelei\u2019s skills, are unavailable. I wonder if all that would make me sound just a bit paranoid. Maybe I\u2019ll just start with teaching them how to start a fire without matches. <br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> Okay\u2026rewrapped the cuts. They bled a bit more than I thought they had. Guess that explains why the vodka hit me a bit harder than usual. Might not have been a good idea to drink so much then, huh. Oh well, not much I can do about it now. It\u2019s really late, or early depending on your perspective. We didn\u2019t get back until almost 4:00am, then we took the time to put everything away and wash up. Then I spent a good bit of time writing in this stupid notebook. I need sleep\u2026<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> Okay\u2026it\u2019s a new day. I\u2019m tired and wired all at once. I got up a bit before the others and made coffee. I drank a good bit of that first pot, so I made some more for the others. Blood loss has an interesting effect with caffeine too. Definitely got to remember that. Anyhoo\u2026I caffeinated the others while Gawain did his usual wonderful job making breakfast. We all tucked in and ate. Then we discussed what kind of boon we wanted to ask for as recompense for taking care of the briar wolf problem in the hedge. I think we all agreed that strengthening our official identities would be the best thing. We all have basic forged identities, but they won\u2019t hold up to any sort of official scrutiny. So, we decided it would be best to remedy that. So, we all piled in the van and headed over to collect our boon. It was straightforward enough. The guy we talked to, Billy, didn\u2019t seem keen on doing that many ID\u2019s, but we turned Lorelei loose on him and it was just a matter of time before the man caved. It\u2019s just not possible to stand up to that woman when she turns on the charm. Hot. Anyhoo\u2026that got worked out quickly enough.<br /> <br /> Then we noticed Joan and decided that we should talk to her about our concerns with Ginny and Desiree. Yeah, that was an interesting \u201cconversation.\u201d It was mostly her going on and on about how she was going to hunt down the pair of them and end the threat. Then this guy Percival kept making pointed comments about her and to her and it really didn\u2019t make things better. I was tempted to deck him just to get him to shut up. I think we managed to talk her out of killing the two outright and instead settled on us keeping an eye on Ginny, since she works for us, and Joan (or someone in the Summer court) watching Desiree. It was a rather stressful time all around. I think we managed to avoid any outright bloodshed for the moment. We\u2019ll see how long that lasts. Personally I think Joan will keep to her word. She seems the sort. I\u2019m not so sure of the other Summer Courtiers, but we\u2019ll see how it goes. Suspicious behavior does not necessarily mean that someone is a Loyalist. <br /> <br /> Hell, a good bit of my behavior has probably been considered to be suspicious and I am most definitely not a Loyalist. I was, but not anymore. Does that distinction mean as much as I hope it does? I hope so. I have no intention of serving The Lady or any of her compatriots. I have in point most definitely acted against them since I\u2019ve arrived here. I guess the only thing I can do is what I have been doing, and that is watching out for my friends and keeping them safe. Most of them are not na\u00efve by any stretch of the imagination, but I don\u2019t think they really understand the other side. That\u2019s not necessarily a bad thing. Some of them think that they are monsters in some regard. I can understand why they, she, thinks that. From a certain point of view that might be true, but it really isn\u2019t. I have seen what it means to be a monster. I have been that monster. Willingly. The only thing I can do now is try to make up for that. I\u2019m not sure if I can, but I have to try. I have to try to make right the sins that I committed. Fuck. I don\u2019t know if I can do that. I don\u2019t know if it\u2019s possible for me to even that out, or even come close to wiping out all the shit that I did. The thing is, I have to try. I know what it is to be the monster. I know what it is to be indifferent. I have to be something else. I have to try to make things better. Goddess let me do some good with this second chance that I have been given. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> The hunt for Briarwolves went fairly well. Mostly. Gawain, Lorelei and Calamity got beat up a bit, but Lorelei heals well and took care of it. Mostly. We ran into Desiree and Ginny Green in the Hedge though, being chased by some sort of strange Mannequins. The Mannequins were personally more dangerous that the Briarwolves, if much much more disorganized. The Director apparently sent them out. They hurt Desiree, but were not trying to kill her. Apparently. Jacob drew a lot of attention in the fight, of course, but seems okay.<br /> <br /> After killing all the enemies, we spoke to the two. People were keen to know why they were in the Hedge. Doubtlessly nefarious reasons, apparently unlike we, who were simply there to murder Briarwolves. If Calamity kills something, it is always murder. She is just the sort. It\u2019s not a matter of justification; it is a matter of resonance. Clearly. Desiree did not say why she was lingering, but could have stopped to rest on the path. Ginny said she was there to meet someone, eventually Flora, but De La Rocha says (and Julia later said) that makes no sense. She was hiding something, which seemed to annoy Calamity. Truthfully, I think Calamity wanted to cut them both down. Is the Autumn Court not the Court of Secrets?<br /> <br /> Remind me not to be found by Calamity in the Hedge. Especially on secret Night Court business I can\u2019t explain.<br /> <br /> Once we ascertained that Flores was okay and our foundlings wandered off, we split up. Calamity and the boys went to skin Briarwolves for Hedge-Spinning, and De La Rocha, Lorelei and I returned home. I did some playful flirting with them, and they were intrigued. Obviously. Julia joined us when we returned. De La Rocha and Lorelei decided to not have their entire view of sex turned on its head by me that night. Sadly. Julia was nervous but also interested. Naturally. I think she likes Lorelei. Which is fair, I do as well. De La Rocha clearly is intrigued by me though\u2026our eyes met a couple times. I smirked at her of course. They do not act on their desires, instead choosing to live life less fully. I do not understand that. I mean, I do, I was Catholic, but they should know better by now. Clearly. The Gentry could come at any time, best spend what time we can in a hidden, dark place coiled around someone pleasing, mingling your sweat with theirs. Yes.<br /> <br /> Since they felt unprepared for my sensuality, I decided we could watch a movie. It wound up being <i>Am\u00e9lie</i>. I had just seen it, but it was good to watch again. Happily. I don\u2019t think it was De La Rocha\u2019s sort of movie, but she liked it okay. Julia actually had seen it before. Strangely.<br /> <br /> The following morning as a bounty we decided to have the Summer Court put some resources toward tightening our identity, or rather our legal identity. It makes sense. Once there, while a Beast named Old Billy made the arrangements, the others talked to Joan and an odd Ogre named Percival. For some reason Gawain decided to tell Joan all about Ginny and Desiree, and seemed surprised when Joan wanted to reap them like bloody wheat. It\u2019s what she does. Surely he has been around Calamity enough by now to know some people are just like that. Americans especially. Before they could all decide to drag Ginny screaming into some underground room I spoke up and suggested maybe we should observe her a bit, since walking through the hedge, fighting the minions of the Gentry, and not wanting to say her precise business are not crimes. I did not say it that way or it would have been taken badly. I don\u2019t really know Desiree, so did not argue with the homicidal maniac about her.<br /> <br /> Percival called me Frye for reasons I cannot explain. First Mags now Frye. Americans are weird. Evidently.<br /> <br /> Show tonight, must get ready. Should be interesting. Hopefully.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XI</i><br /> <br /> De La Rocha had the Leechfinger merit from Swords at Dawn to transfer damage. As a Leechfinger/Witchtooth it made sense, in a witchy way.<br /> <br /> The Extras were from no specific book. They did more damage than Briarwolves, but due to \u201crole fixation\u201d did not defend against new changes to their environment until it had hurt them, which meant the \u201cbatches\u201d the PCs got free attacks on. Lorelei got hurt so bad because the Briarwolves rolled really well on Initiative, and the PCs rolled really mediocre, so the Briarwolves initially had two targets and Gawain defended much better. Combat was appropriately lethal, which is good for the tone of game. It is important to reinforce that fights must be approached carefully.<br /> <br /> Juliet said \u201comelet du fromage\u201d a lot as she had seen Dexter\u2019s Lab. And found it amusing to tease Insincere Marguerite.<br /> <br /> Okay I think that covers it. But if you have comments or questions lemme know. See you in two weeks.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/