nd I\u2019ve seen evidence of the spread of that franchise all over the world. Calamity and Gawain\u2019s faces lit up immediately, but D cut in before they could say anything. \u201cI\u2019ll field this one, guys,\u201d she said with a grin, \u201cwhen we have enough time to properly cover the subject.\u201d<br /> <br /> Gawain offered to bring his entertainment system over to the Dream House, which includes high-end speakers and at least two or three video game machines. Calamity stated that they had to see me play some game called \u201cRock Band.\u201d Well, I said that pressing buttons to simulate music didn\u2019t sound like much fun to me, but Gawain patiently explained to me that this game actually uses real microphones which can gauge the pitch and timbre of your voice to judge your performance. What\u2019s more, there are <u>lots</u> of these games out there, including one that focuses on Abba and another that contains exclusively Beatles music. So that might be fun.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not sure how we got on the subject of literature. I think someone quoted something famous, and I recognized it. Shakespeare or Dickens, most likely. Someone English, anyway. I mentioned that I was more into French Romantic literature, like Dumas and Hugo. At which point Jacob asked me if I had heard or seen the musical version of <u>Les Miserables</u>.<br /> <br /> I think I said something clever, like \u201cwhat?\u201d<br /> <br /> Gawain chimed in at that point. \u201cOr seen the movie, even? It\u2019s not bad.\u201d<br /> <br /> Someone else asked if he meant the movie version of the novel, or the movie version of the musical, and people all started talking at once, jabbering quickly about actors I\u2019d never heard of. It was too much to take.<br /> <br /> \u201cShut up,\u201d I said loudly. When everyone quieted down, I turned back to Jacob. \u201cNow\u2026 what?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> Jacob smiled. \u201cThere was a musical version of <u>Les Miserables</u>,\u201d he repeated softly. \u201cIn France first, I think, and then on Broadway.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWas it good?\u201d I asked, hardly daring to hope.<br /> <br /> He shrugged. \u201cI do not know,\u201d he said simply, \u201cbut I think it won many awards. My sister liked it.\u201d<br /> <br /> I turned to D. \u201cDo you think I\u2019ll be able to download the soundtrack when we get back to the Dream House?\u201d I asked her.<br /> <br /> She grinned. \u201cWe can probably find it,\u201d she allowed, in a tone that sounded suspiciously patronizing. \u201cAnd while we\u2019re at it, let\u2019s look up the musical version of <u>Phantom of the Opera</u>, too. I think you\u2019ll like it.\u201d<br /> <br /> (The soundtrack to <u>Les Mis</u> is playing now as I write this. On Marguerite\u2019s advice, I downloaded the international cast recording rather than the Broadway version; it contains the complete score.)<br /> <br /> After that, the conversation turned to more serious matters. Calamity started talking about the things she had liked as a girl, before she was taken, and that caused us to start speculating on how Arcadia had changed us. Calamity mentioned that she used to want to be a doctor, but had since let that dream fall by the wayside. This sent Marguerite into a tirade about how we shouldn\u2019t let what our Keepers did to us ruin our dreams.<br /> <br /> Gawain opined (and I agree) that just because Calamity\u2019s dreams had changed didn\u2019t mean that she\u2019d allowed her <u>Keeper</u> to change them. People grow out of their dreams all the time. Unfortunately, Calamity couldn\u2019t let the subject go at that. She started wondering (with Marguerite egging her on) if everything she experienced in the Snow Globe was intended to forge her into the exceptional killer she has become. I suppose it\u2019s possible that the \u201cwhispers\u201d put just enough pressure on her to create that steely resolve and hatred of conformity that we\u2019ve all come to know and love. It seems devious to the point of implausibility\u2026 but I suppose the Gentry are nothing if not implausible.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a sobering thought, and I could tell that it affected Calamity in a profound way. I wanted to say something to make it better\u2026 but I honestly wasn\u2019t sure what I could say. I think this is something she\u2019s going to have to work through on her own.<br /> <br /> So all in all, a little bit of heartbreak and a little bit of joy came out of the time we spent fixing up the Hedge House. I suppose learning to accept that things pass and new things come into being is part of moving on with your life. And now, I really need to put this diary away and start getting ready for the show. My first number is \u201cWalking on Sunshine,\u201d and it\u2019s our opening act.<br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei Grace</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-14T14:50:20-07:00","id":256843,"title":"","content":"<b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> <b><u>Saturday May 10<sup>th</sup></u></b><br /> <br /> Well, it was certainly been a delightful night. I'm writing this as I sit here in my bed with a pair of sweet little pretties curled up on either side of me. I suppose I should sleep as well but I don't want to risk rolling over and cutting one of them or worse yet waking up startled. Besides, I find this oddly relaxing, sitting here watching over them as they sleep. Petting their dark hair and soft pale skin. They rest easily, safe in my bed and my embrace. Oh the temptation was there, it's always there. Even now the hunger is restless, stirring in the darkness inside me. I'm an insatiable thing; I feasted on that violence in the Hedge and already I want more. But tonight my sweetlings are safe from all the monsters, even me. <br /> <br /> I shall have to thank Annika for the tips about Kimberly. I was pretty sure the girl was one that enjoyed a firmer hand but I would not have guessed just where she wanted that hand. Her friend Davey seemed surprised to discover her enjoyment of breath control as well. Then again, last night was quite full of surprises for the dear boy though I must confess I <i>was</i> hoping he'd prove a bit more pliable then he did. Ah well, he performed admirably and quite satisfyingly often. Neither Kimberly or myself was left wanting. And oh dear lady Kimberly was certainly a delightful and delicious plaything. <br /> <br /> It wasn't just the end of the night that went well. As we were preparing for the show, Ace declared that he was going to recreate the Thunderdome sequence (as a one man act.) Lori had never heard of Mad Max and while we didn't have time to fully bring her up to speed, I did sit her down for the two that really mattered. It was nice, I hadn't watched since getting back to the world and seeing her reactions was fun, especially when Tina Turner showed up in Thunderdome. Jacob needed to cure the hides and Gawain was tagged to help him. Insincere Marguerite declared that Australians were all too ugly and didn't join us either. Personally, I have to disagree with my Darkling sister on this one. A leather clad Mel Gibson figured quite prominently in many of young Katt's daydreams and I can't say I wouldn't still love to ride that supercharged V8. I wonder if he's aged well...<br /> <br /> Friday is one of the big nights and we had a good crowd. Several Changelings were present though no royals (well, Madam Spidertoes was there) and no contingent from the Winter Court at all. I guess maybe they've gotten tired of watching us? Or they've decided to properly spy on us rather than send a table of stony-faced creepers to the shows. Whichever, we'll deal with it if (more likely when I suspect) it becomes an issue. The show was amazing. Lori was even more spectacular than usual (which is kinda like saying that a nuclear blast is brighter than a solar flare). Annika had everyone eating out of the palm of her hand as she always does. Ace was insane but had the crowd in stitches. Insincere Marguerite introduced her Brotherswing and It's a Sin numbers (which were both quite excellent) in the most adorable outfit while putting her sexy accent to full use. It was one of our best shows start to finish. I still find it hard to imagine that Annika honestly believes that I'll ever be good enough to keep up with them but I know that she would not waste her time trying to teach me if she didn't. She's far too brutally honest for that, which is actually one of the things I like about her. <br /> <br /> After the show, we shared a cigar and some conversation. We talked about how we'd been and made a bit of small talk, which was pleasant. Then our conversation drifted to a bit less innocent topics, like Dark Kimberly. Annika assured me she was the sharing sort and that if I wanted Kimberly she'd simply pick another plaything for the evening. Yes, she really was that arrogant, but it's not vanity if you really are that good and I don't think I've ever met anyone as seductive and alluring as Annika can be when she wants someone. I did suggest that we could share Kimberly together but Annika brushed it off with a statement that there could only be one Mistress in that situation and it would be her. Even as alluring and darkly beautiful as she is, I don't surrender to anyone and I don't behave without a fight. I'm not sure if she's willing or able to be as physically aggressive as it would take to rule me but it <i>would</i> be one hell of a ride to find out. To the point though, I agree that that's not the kind of power struggle to have in front of a sub. Also, I'm pretty sure it would be a bad idea to fuck her while she's teaching me to dance but that still doesn't stop me from wondering just how good she really is with that whip. Damn, it has been too long since anyone put me through my paces. I really should see about fixing that.<br /> <br /> Not that I am complaining about how my night ended. Oh quite the opposite. After getting a few tips from Annika about what the girl liked, I moved to Dark Kimberly and Davey's table. I am not sure quite what came over me but I just spilled in and started to flirt and tease the pair of them as naturally as breathing. I was smooth and witty and the perfect words were always right there on the tip of my tongue. And once to ran my fingertips along Kimberly's neck and hinted not too subtly about stealing her breath away I knew she was mine. Davey didn't respond quite as readily to the Domme vibe I was throwing out but he certainly wasn't afraid of it either. As for myself, I was quite enjoying being the center of their attention.<br /> <br /> And as I was wrapping those two around my fingers, I could see that Lori and De la Rocha and julia and my Darkling sister were all getting rather friendly at a nearby table. Not for the first time (or last I'm sure) I did catch myself wondering about Insincere Marguerite's long dexterous fingers and her prehensile tongue and that boneless flexibility. But I only let my thoughts drift a moment before Lori reminded me that Davey was a friend of hers. I laughed and promised to be careful before I stepped over to Ace and his punchbowl to take a drink. Turns out he'd mixed it based on finding an alcohol of every color rather than any sort of proper flavor comparability. Surprisingly, it wasn't really that bad, more a burning sensation than a flavor but honestly but I've had worse. Ace offered me more but I declined with a wink and nod toward the pair of Gothic beauties and a comment about needing to be up for a night of mixed doubles. He looked to Gawain and my dear knight blushed delightfully (quite a feat for a suit of armor I suppose, but he manages to be quite expressive). But this night wasn't for love, I was on the prowl for something darker. As I was walking back over to collect my prizes and take them up to my room, I saw him heading from the bar to Chalcedony's table with a pair of drinks in hand. I don't know that much about that one, but she is an excellent dancer and thus athletic and flexible. I do hope my knight enjoyed her as much as I enjoyed my own conquests of the evening. <br /> <br /> Tomorrow I'll talk to him. I know he said he was alright with this and I believe he meant it when he said it. But claiming it was alright and seeing me flirting and teasing not just another woman but another man as well are two different things. I am his monster and he is my knight. I still can't understand why, but he loves me and I can't deny that I love him back. As delicious as tonight was, I need that and I will not hurt him. I'll find some other way to satisfy my darker appetites if I have to. But that's a matter for the daytime. For now, I think I've let my toys rest long enough, it's time to set this journal aside and indulge myself in pleasures of the dark a little more.<br /> <br /> <sup>*****</sup><br /> <br /> It's surprising what a few hours can do. What a few words can do. The day started off well enough. Gawain made a breakfast casserole and Jacob made perfect coffee. We woke Ace up from where he'd passed out with the punchbowl. Insincere Marguerite and I both showed off our trophies from the night before and none of said trophies seemed to mind. I gave Gawain a kiss and took a moment to make sure he was as alright with things in practice as well as theory and he honestly is. Pleasant conversation over our afternoon breakfast followed. We decided to work on the Hollow house. After Dark Kimberly and Davey left, I went to change. I swear, I only left that girl alone in my room a few minutes and she not only made the bed but she'd changed the sheets. And the bathroom was as spotless as my boots after she'd finished with them the night before. Such is our nature, she cannot stop being what she is anymore than Lori could simply decide not to have wings. We all fled Arcadia but we'll never truly escape it. We carry it in our hearts and wear it on our skins. <br /> <br /> I'm not quite sure how it started. We'd headed into the Hedge after breakfast to work on the Hollow House and put in a few hours making the place safer and more comfortable. We were winding down to head back and get ready for the show and talking. I forget exactly what prompted it, but our fetches came up and I mentioned that Katt had wanted to be a doctor. Insincere Marguerite got quite insistent that just because I'd been taken did not mean I couldn't still be whatever I wanted. That it was my choice to be what I wanted and not just to be what my Keeper made me. That to follow the path They wanted to was to let Them win. She told me she'd support me and help me pursue medicine or whatever I wanted to do. They all did. I tried to explain that I just wasn't that girl any more but they would not hear it. <br /> <br /> It went from there. Insincere Marguerite made some very piercing observations. I have always thought of myself as a survivor. As a victor in my own way. I beat Them by not breaking. I beat Them by enduring Their cruel tortures and finding the strength to keep resisting. I became the monster I am because that was the only way to survive. And I did survive. I did beat Them. It was the price I paid to achieve MY victory but it was worth it. <br /> <br /> But what if it wasn't a victory at all? What if this is exactly what They wanted? Did I survive through my own strength or was I worked like a piece of steel, honed to the edge and then brought back, over and over and over... folded and worked and made stronger and sharper with every blow. I was so sure of everything before and now I can't stop seeing the possibilities. <br /> <br /> I whisper like They do. I crave and savor pain, just as I know They savored my suffering. I punish the bad boys and girls just as They did. I come for them in the dark, feeding on their fear before I torture them for being criminals and bad people and taking things I want from their broken bodies. Or I seek the ones that desire the release of submission and surrender and pain... I give them as much as they can take and then I hold them close, watching over them after I've savored their pain. Holding them and petting them the way The Whispers held my own broken and torn flesh in the dark. I did not become the good girl They claimed They wanted. No, I became Them instead. I became the monster that was stronger then me. I became the monster that I was powerless against. I became the monster that tortured me. I was so focused on resisting Them that I was blind to it. Blind to everything except my need to fight back. <br /> <br /> I don't blame Insincere Marguerite for what she said. I didn't want to hear it but she's right. She said it because she cares about me. They all do. Gawain loves me, he was there, arm around me to support me. Jacob brought up my recklessness in the fight against the briar wolves. He told me he'd seen people in the Lady's Realm fight like that and wind up maimed and crippled. I think he can guess that I find that idea worse than dead. He also said he'd seen real monsters and that I am not one, no matter what I've done. I think he's worried that I was being reckless out of some self-destructive urge. I can't blame him. Hell, I'm not sure that he's entirely wrong. Lori pointed out that we've all done things. I told them all that I cannot forget (or forgive) what I did. They all talked about what matters is what I do now, how I move forward. Lorelei told me that she didn't understand me but that she loved me anyway. Yet she did make a point of mentioning that Davey was her friend last night. So she understands me well enough to know what I wanted to do to that boy. How can she know me that well and want to support me? How can she know me that well and promise to be there to heal me? <br /> <br /> I told them I was alright. That I just needed to think about what they'd told me. I lied to them. I was not alright. I was not even fucking close to alright. All I could think of was that I am not just a fucking monster, but that I am the fucking monster that I feared and hated with ever fiber of my being while it tortured me for nearly twenty years. Hell, the very suggestion of Them still sends me into a panic. I can't sleep with anyone but Gawain because I'm too afraid that I'll wake up thinking of Them and lash out. I can't bear to be touched gently and softly because it reminds me of Them. I crave pain because that was the only proof I had that my resistance meant anything to Them. If I'm not a monster than what in the ever living fuck am I? Hell, I don't think there are words for how messed up I am. <br /> <br /> I came back to my room in a daze, my mind spinning with those sick thoughts. I tried to push them down, to dismiss them or to promise to deal with them later. But I couldn't. I looked at myself in the bathroom mirror and I lost it. I broke down. I tried to pull the glass out but it's rooted in my very bones. All I managed to do was cut the shit out of my hands and cover myself in blood and tears as I clawed at my face and cried before I collapsed in a messy heap against the tub. And when I looked up and saw that wretched failure in the mirror misery turned to rage. I charged that reflection and I swung at it. I beat against it until both my knuckles and the glass cracked. <br /> <br /> And that's when I stopped. I saw myself reflected in the broken glass breathless and covered with blood and tears. A dozen slightly different faces were gazing back at me. Maybe the glass was trying to tell me something. Maybe I was just that close to the edge of sanity. But I saw Katt there and all of the rage and sorrow and loathing drained out of me. Mixed in with the wild-eyed monster was the lost little girl I've mourned for so long as being dead and gone. And that's when it hit me. I do crave violence. I did think about just how easily I could keep squeezing Kimberly's neck last night. I did see the terror in Andromeda when I brushed her skin with my razors and I did want to continue. But I did not. I did not harm them. I may not be that mousey girl who wanted to grow up and be a doctor and help people anymore but I am not just the monster that The Whispering Voices forged either. That's what Gawain sees in me. Somehow he can look at this jumbled broken mess and see the parts of Katt that are still part of me. I guess that's what they all see. I've been so focused on what the monster did that I've been blind to the fact that there is anything else inside me. Insincere Marguerite is right, I am very much the creature of The Whispering Voices. But I have refused to give into that side again since murdering my parents and I will be even more mindful of it now. They all keep telling me that what matters is where I go from here, not where I've been. I've spent all this time worrying about who I am or bemoaning who I'm not anymore but I haven't stopped and seriously considered who I <i>want</i> to be.<br /> <br /> But right now I need to clean up before anyone sees the mess I've made of myself or the bathroom. There is nothing to be done about the broken mirror but I can put off telling anyone about it till tomorrow at least. Thankfully I didn't razor up while I was ranting so my face isn't cut. A good shower should wash away the blood and the evidence of crying. I'll wear that off the shoulder black dress Lori helped me pick out. It has matching long opera gloves to hide my hands during the show. Afterward I need to go to the lighthouse and see what they know about Snow Globe and The Whispering Voices. I should also let Tommy know I want to talk to him. If there is anyone else here who escaped that place he's likely to know. I have never questioned why They did what They did. But if there is some method to Show Globe's madness I need to know about it. What if I am not the only monster They've created? What if they send Timmy or one of the others to try to hunt me down? I had let myself believe They would simply find another Jane and continue. I have been stupid and selfish and careless and it could endanger my friends. It could endanger my lover. I am not alone anymore. They believe in me. They fucking <i>trust</i> me. And I will not let them down. <i>That</i> is the kind of monster I choose to be. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Normally I try to keep up with the day to day activities of my motley mates and generally rant about things. I don\u2019t know if I can do that this time. Yesterday was a typical day. We had a show, people were great. Insincere Marguerite choreographed a number and introduced it. That was new. She was adorable in her striped socks and matching hat. Ace reenacted part of \u201cMad Max Beyond Thunderdome\u201d during the mid-show break. Again, his usual awesome. I want to be able to focus on those things right now, but I can\u2019t. I need to vent or explain or justify all the shit going through my head right now, because I\u2019m slipping. Goddess am I slipping.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite took me aside and asked if I was okay. I told her I was fine. She kind of looked at me and asked if I would lie to her. I replied that I try not to. She seemed satisfied for the moment (or maybe mollified), but I\u2019m not sure how long that will last. She didn\u2019t ask if I was injured or hurt, and so my answer of being \u201cfine\u201d was not a lie. Not really. Yeah, justification. My life is all about justification. But honestly, I am fine. I am still technically injured from the fight with the briar wolves, but it\u2019s not bad. It\u2019s just a scratch. The cuts are barely bleeding anymore. Not like it was before. I\u2019m fine. This is nothing compared to injures I\u2019ve had in the past. Besides, it\u2019s not like it\u2019s going to kill me.<br /> <br /> So, this morning we had breakfast like usual, and a lot of conversation. Things became interesting when Calamity mentioned that her fetch has a daughter. She says, and seems to be able to back up the fact, that this was a natural child and not an adoption. That is not good. That is so not good. The children of fetches don\u2019t really have souls. They, like their parent, are not real. They are a mockery of life, walking and talking and going about their business. Until that is, their business is to fuck with your life. I\u2019ve never seen the actual child of a fetch before, but I\u2019ve heard stories. I\u2019ve heard others talk of them. Some with awe and some with horror. Fetches at least can fake it for a while. They act out your life, and can do so for years. They can become aware though, and start fucking with your life if they know that you are nearby. It just makes me glad that my fetch is in Portland and I don\u2019t have to worry about running into him by accident. I think the others are as lucky as I am. I think pretty much everyone\u2019s fetch is towns, if not, states away. <br /> <br /> Damn fetches. Made up of whatever their creator, usually the Gentry, has lying around. I saw the Lady creating the fetch for Delight Diane. The Lady of the Winter Winds pulled together sticks from dead trees, charcoal from a dead fire, and bits and pieces of bone and hair from someone long dead in a cave. She combined all these pieces together to make a replacement for Diane, which I then escorted to her home. I was proud at the time to do my duty for the Lady, but looking back it makes me sick. The Lady took detritus, and the remains of someone I likely killed to create a duplicate of a young woman I kidnap\u2026.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> <br /> Okay\u2026felt sick. Was sick. New topic. I enlisted Gawain\u2019s yesterday to help to finish working with the wolf skins we got. It is important to clean the skins completely and to rub fat or lard into the leather to keep it supple. Otherwise it dries out and it\u2019s useless. I have a feeling that Gawain would have rather been watching the Mad Max movies with Lorelei, Ace and the others, but he had agreed to help me, so he did. Maybe I can make it up to him later. Maybe if he can teach me how to hedgespin, I can make something for him? Even if he doesn\u2019t, there are some things I know how to make out of leather that might come in useful for him. Hmmm\u2026maybe a sheath for his sword. It might be better to have a flexible sheath and strap it across his back. Would make drawing his greatsword easier. Plus it would be better than carrying bare steel around. We have enough leather. I should be able to make that for him and still have plenty to practice with and/or for Gawain to hedgespin with. Maybe he can make some more armor for Calamity. I know she has armor of a sort with her glass shards, but she seems to get caught up in the moment during fights and doesn\u2019t actively dodge attacks. I figured any actual armor she wore would just be that much better. Or maybe we should make something for Lorelei? She is a non-combatant, and doesn\u2019t have the training to avoid or take hits like she did. Maybe we can make something for her that would be functional and stylish at the same time. Definitely have to look into that.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Later we got into a conversation that was all around unpleasant. I\u2019m not sure what started it, but Insincere Marguerite said something to Calamity about how her Keeper shaped the kind of person she became. The glass, the violence and the whispers turned Kate into Calamity. Maybe not intentionally, but the idea has merit. Made me feel sick just thinking about it, but not because I didn\u2019t believe her. The idea has all too much merit if you ask me. We become what the Gentry make us. Killers, songbirds, executioners, docile pets, thieves, and betrayers. Lovely. Now I feel sick again.<br /> <br /> I watched the others as we talked. Well, most of the others. Ace had already walked off muttering something. Usually when that happens it\u2019s because he had some sort of creative idea. The remaining people seemed a bit uncomfortable with the idea that the Gentry shaped us, intentionally or not, but seemed to accept it as fact. Calamity seemed more than a little upset about the idea. That she, in her rebellion against the Whispers became closer to them than she had before. I can understand that. I didn\u2019t truly grasp how like the Lady I\u2019d become until after Rook brought me back to her. I\u2019m still not sure what opened my eyes, but when I saw the Lady again, I felt like I was seeing her for the first time, but this time, as she actually is. I saw myself as a reflection of her. It was not a happy realization. Up there with Diane being my minder in Claire Falls. I\u2019m still not sure to this day if she realized who I was. Part of me is convinced that she had to know. I mean, how could you forget the face of the man who ruined your life? She was never hostile towards me. She helped and was kind, and in the end let me go. I pray to the goddess that she doesn\u2019t know me. It would be better if she never had to think of me again. Forget that whole experience. Not sure how possible that is though. <br /> <br /> Man, a part of me really wants to get drunk right now and forget all of it for awhile. I can\u2019t though. We have a show to put on tonight, and I should be sober.<br /> <br /> During this whole conversation I tried telling Calamity that she\u2019s not a monster. That having killed doesn\u2019t mean that she is a monster, or enjoying fighting doesn\u2019t make her less. It\u2019s all about the circumstances. The reasons. She killed her parents in a fit of anger. It wasn\u2019t premeditated. It wasn\u2019t her intention. They\u2019re dead by her hands, but she\u2019s not a monster for having done it. I still don\u2019t think she sees that though. The others know that I\u2019ve killed. They saw the room with the bloody knives. I can only assume that they think I\u2019m projecting. That I\u2019m telling Calamity she\u2019s not a monster for having killed, because I don\u2019t want to be a monster for having done the same. I wish that were the case. If it were only that simple.<br /> <br /> I also mentioned my concern about her disregard for her safety during the fight with the wolves. How she went all out attacking, but left herself open for retaliation. Doing that then was partially because I wanted her to be aware of it if she wasn\u2019t. The other reason I did it was so that the others would know of it too. She may honestly get caught up in the moment while fighting, but it might also be something else. Leaving herself open for punishment without conscious thought. I don\u2019t know. I wish I knew what to do, what to say, to convince her that she\u2019s not a bad person. That she\u2019s not a monster.<br /> <br /> I know Arcadia changed us all. Left its mark. Insincere Marguerite desperately wants to possess things and people, but tries very hard not to. She says that her Keeper was grooming her to be just like her, but I think she failed. Marguerite decided not to be that person and left. She has been an asset to the rest of us. She helps us see what we need to see. Calamity loves to fight, and has no problems inflicting pain, but she is also fiercely protective of those she cares about. She says she\u2019s a monster. I see her as a protector. Lorelei, more than the rest of us (save me) hides behind a mask, I think. She acts happy, and seems happy, but sometimes when I look back her smiles seem forced. She mentioned leaving two friends behind in Arcadia when she left. That she\u2019d made a pledge with them that they\u2019d all leave or none would, and yet she is here alone. She won\u2019t say it, but I think that weighs heavily on her. That might be why she doesn\u2019t like to talk about Arcadia. But here, she is doing so much good. A lot of people are inspired by her talents, and not just because she\u2019s hot. Plus she\u2019s a healer. I\u2019m fairly certain that at least one of us would have been killed in the fight with the wolves if she hadn\u2019t been there. And Gawain is a good fighter and I\u2019d take him at my back any day, but that\u2019s not all he is. That\u2019s just a small part. He is a creator. I have watched him working at his forge for hours, making knives or a new sword. You don\u2019t normally think about how much time goes into making one knife, but he does it. He gives something back, literally. Plus every morning he makes us breakfast. We would all eat if he didn\u2019t cook, well, most of us would. Maybe not regularly, but we\u2019d eat.<br /> <br /> Actually thinking about it I probably wouldn\u2019t eat much if Gawain didn\u2019t cook for us so often. I didn\u2019t get much to eat in the Lady\u2019s realm, so I got used to doing without. Sometimes I wonder if I\u2019m becoming weak since I got back to \u201cthe world.\u201d I eat at least two meals every day. I sleep in a soft bed, with a blanket, and in a safe place. The weather here is so warm, almost too warm, and yet despite that, sometimes I just feel so cold. I don\u2019t know what I\u2019d do if I was brought back to Her. I don\u2019t know if I\u2019d still feel the cold like I did during the early years or if I could just turn it off like I did later. And food. I don\u2019t know how long I could make it without eating now. A week maybe? I\u2019ve gone longer before. I think the longest was 15 days. I had all the water I wanted, just no food. That was a rough time. Looking back, I think the Lady was just fucking with us. Letting less animals into the woods for us to hunt. Some people got really desperate and ate their dead. I\u2019ve never sunk that low. I may be a reprehensible person, but I never did that.<br /> <br /> Sometimes I dream that I\u2019m still in Her realm. That living in California and meeting up with the others is the dream. I\u2019m fairly certain that this is real. The Lady never knew of Elena, and yet I see her around town occasionally. I\u2019m still afraid that all this is going to end though. Like it\u2019s too good to be true and I\u2019m just waiting for it to get yanked away. I wonder if it will all collapse when (if) the others find out about me. About what I am was. Will they kill me? Will they bring me to the Summer court to be punished or executed? Or worse, the Winter court. I have no wish to meet Master Darke as an enemy. I have a feeling, that like the Lady, he would make me pray for death. Or would they accept me, tell me that I\u2019m not a monster, that everyone deserves a second chance? I almost hope they kill me, because the later option is so much worse.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> The show has gone well. My acts were done to my satisfaction. Mostly. I even went on stage, when Julia insisted my accent would draw interest. She was correct, as she often is. Mostly. I wore a floppy stripy hat to go with my stripy socks. I am not a fan of being looked at by so many people though. We will see what comes of it. Maybe.<br /> <br /> After the show. Lorelei and De La Rocha succumbed to the inevitable, and found themselves in my boudoir. I ravished them, and Julia, thoroughly. To touch, to taste, to smell, to learn them and make them smell like me, that is what I did. They will never be the same again. Mostly. I made them mine as utterly and completely as I could, and went to sleep with their taste on my lips and smell in my nose, and them all under I.<br /> <br /> As it should be.<br /> <br /> De La Rocha is, even more than Julia, submissive. She became passive quickly, and it was pleasant. Lorelei not so much, but she was a very pleasing partner. Julia was clearly fond of her. I enjoyed exploring what they enjoy and need, and will continue to enjoy doing so.<br /> <br /> The next day we worked in the Hedge House, getting it more presentable and in some cases better defended. I also made out with Julia some. Delightfully. The Hedge House is much much more livable now, and more secure. Though I would still sleep between the walls. Probably.<br /> <br /> Ace is still fixated on dead animals being mounted. Must be his British big game hunter issues.<br /> <br /> Jacob is still hurt. I cornered him and he said he was fine. Probably that Russian machismo. Putin has too much of it. Fascists. Anyway, I will need to keep an eye on him. He needs to be sneakier, so he does not get hurt. I will encourage him to make a Contract with Smoke. That will help. Probably.<br /> <br /> We talked before the show. I cornered Calamity with the idea that she was, in fact, what her Keeper made. Probably. Maybe not her Keeper\u2019s first choice, but a well-honed killer like her does not happen accidentally. She was disquieted, which is good. She should not want to be what her Keeper made. She is better than that. She is better than her Keeper. Absolutely. I told her so!<br /> <br /> Ah relations get complicated. How delicious Lorelei is. How I savored her delights! So pretty, so sweet, such a fine, fine voice. I could not ask for a better little bird! I am sure she will find her way into my boudoir again. They always do. Julia talked about sketching, even painting her more. This is good. She should be immortalized in that way. Jacob worries I. As I wait for my reproductive system to fall into line, I am holding him at arms length that way, but I touch him every day. I still don\u2019t know his secrets, though, and it makes me sad. I do worry about him, though.<br /> <br /> Gawain and Ace are somewhat typical of guys, in a good way. Mostly. Ace is very interesting despite being British. And Gawain is a sweetheart. Mostly. He gets a little half cocked when Calamity gets hurt. Usually. My Darkling sister still struggles with herself. I hope my words helped her. Mostly. I want her to be strong because she deserves to be strong and rise above. And we make a good team. Usually.<br /> <br /> De La Rocha and Julia are also part of the family, if not the Motley, now. I hope De La Rocha will introduce Julia to more people, I am sure she can use friends. At least she is talking to the Motley now. Walking around and hanging out with us even! Progress! Mostly.<br /> <br /> Hmmmmmmmmmm\u2026new show. Whatever shall I wear?<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>End Session XII</i><br /> <br /> Not much to comment on, roleplaying heavy session. Calamity\u2019s player was waiting for the chance to have that possibility dredged up to discuss, and it came up organically in conversation. This group is less adventurers more kinda exploring their lives, so that is cool.<br /> <br /> Okay well nothing else comes to mind, but if you have any comments or questions let me know<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-14T20:52:06-07:00","id":256973,"title":"","content":"Were there any clarity rolls made that session?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-14T22:44:58-07:00","id":257004,"title":"","content":"There was consideration of it for Calamity, and the player offered to, but we elected not to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T12:57:43-07:00","id":267617,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to return to the Dream House. A festive evening takes a dark turn.<br /> <br /> We don\u2019t get a journal from Calamity this time\u2026rather a dream sequence. Circumstances are defined below.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> Early May 11th, technically<br /> <br /> Well fuck. Shit shit g-damn fuck. That went from pretty damn awesome to pretty fucking terrible really fast. And I don\u2019t know any way to fix it! Calamity was already feeling kinda shitty, I think, with the kid thing and the being shaped to be a monster thing and this sure didn\u2019t help that. Lori\u2019s all worried about her Princess and this random girl she found naked. De la Roche and Julia are worried about their friends and Ace is off bar hopping and I don\u2019t think he has a cell phone. Shit.<br /> <br /> OK. I went to limber up a bit and it helped some, moving around, you know? Maybe if I write it all down, in order and everything, things might make more sense? Worth a shot I guess. It started after the show. I got a text from Captain Jack, saying there was a problem at the Rose and Thorn, and that I should bring Calamity. I dunno really what I was expecting at that point, but I did bring my knife. I wound up leaving it in the car though, cause there were tons of cops all around, cause Dark Kimberly had gotten shot. De la Roche knew a side door, and when I texted Captain Jack to let him know we were there, he met us at it, so we managed to avoid the cops for the most part.<br /> <br /> So, as it turns out, not only was Dark Kimberly shot, but we couldn\u2019t fix her up, cause of the police and regular human doctors, you know? She wasn\u2019t gonna to die or anything, even though it was from, like, three feet away, but it had to have hurt like a bitch. The whole three feet away thing opened up all sorts of questions like why shoot someone from three feet away and not kill them? Did the fucker not understand how guns work? Were they trying to drive people away from the club? To send a message to someone? Why Dark Kimberly? Just, the fuck, man? Seriously.<br /> <br /> The worst bit though? The worst bit is they did it in front of everyone and <u>everyone</u> saw somebody different. Dark Kimberly saw a Latina woman. Lucian saw a Chinese dude. Davie saw a white chick. None of them saw any kind of Changeling-y bits. No cameras got a good shot. It\u2019s enough to make a saint swear, and really wasn\u2019t helping Calamity\u2019s mood, you know? Or mine.<br /> <br /> Lucian was actually pretty awesome for all of it. He kept the police off people\u2019s backs and let us know what he knew. He didn\u2019t know anything about the bullshit shapeshifting powers or anything though. He\u2019d noticed Molly Nuit wasn\u2019t around after the shooting and had been before, but that was the furthest his feud with the Winter Court got into it, you know? Since we (and he) kinda figured the gunperson\u2019s mission had been to fuck with the club, or its reputation, you know, he did mention that another club had been burned down about a decade ago, after hours when no one should have been there, but the owner and five mystery people\u2019s bodies were found. That made me think it was maybe some other supernatural something or other that didn\u2019t like any kind of supernatural clubs in the area, since the burned down club wasn\u2019t associated with any Changelings. It doesn\u2019t look like it though, with our research.<br /> <br /> See, after we checked up on Dark Kimberly, when the police were done talking with her, we decided to hit up the Autumn Court library. Well, Calamity decided to and I offered to go along, to get the tall books, you know? And to keep her company, mostly, but it turned out my rusty library skills weren\u2019t so rusty. Jacob came with us and helped out too, while Lori got Dark Kimberly healed up, then went in search of Princess Jolie, and Ace went bar hopping to scope out the area around the Rose and Thorn.<br /> <br /> We did finally hit a break at the library, which is good, since Calamity promised Dark Kimberly we\u2019d find and kill the fucker who shot her. We found a goblin contract that would do exactly what people were describing. Its downside was that, after your mission was over/some length of time had passed, you forget who you are until you sleep and wake up again. You also won\u2019t remember anything that happened during the time you didn\u2019t know who you were. Calamity texted folks about that right off, so they\u2019d know something to look for and called Lucian.<br /> <br /> He suggested (and it made sense) that Jacob check up on his Court mates, since, you know, that probably wouldn\u2019t set off a war or anything. And he had the excuse of letting his monarch know what was up. So Jacob went off to the clinic they run. Calamity had some Court business to look up and talk about, plus probably didn\u2019t want me hovering anymore, so I brought her her bike and then headed back here, to the House.<br /> <br /> Alright. I guess things feel a little less hopeless, kinda. We know how they did it, which is important. We have a pattern of behavior to check for, which could be useful. We have a girl who\u2019s lost her clothes at Glamour Springs at the House, which is... less pertinent to the whole shooting thing. Hopefully. Lori found her while she was looking for Princess Jolie. Also, we did have an awesome show. And you know, I think I\u2019ll end with talking about that. It\u2019ll be a happy ending and everything, and then maybe Calamity will be home and I can sleep easier. Or maybe just make everyone breakfast at that point.<br /> <br /> So, like I said, the show was awesome, of course. I was super nervous about mine and Captain Jack\u2019s bit, but it was so much fun doing it, I pretty much forgot to be nervous. It started with that Rockette\u2019s song, with Captain Jack wearing a wig and everything, to \u2018blend in\u2019, you know? He still had on his sunglasses and the clothes didn\u2019t quite fit right (plus he\u2019s like seven feet tall) but I made a show of peering from the sides, trying to figure out what was wrong until his wig slipped. Then I \u2018scuse me pardon me\u2019d my way through the whole dancing line as he ran off. We got in three or four costume changes, including when we switched into outfits like the other had on to start. That was just after I had stomped on his skirt so that everyone could see the heart boxers he had on under it. If I saw it right, he huffed from a helium balloon right before, which kinda explains the following scream, along with Captain Jack\u2019s serious lung capacity. I think everybody else had fun too - there was lots of laughing and the dancer whose skirts Captain Jack \u2018hid\u2019 under for a bit until he sneezed winked at me when I set her back upright.<br /> <br /> The others were all awesome as usual too. Ace did a Flashdance act, complete with leg warmers and everything. After the show, he put one of the legwarmers on his arm and called it Mother Teresa, insisting \u2018she\u2019 got a drink before he did. Yeah, that actually happened. <u>Before</u> he had anything to drink. Lori sang Walking on Sunshine, which was super fun. Insincere Marguerite introduced her acts again. This time she was all dressed up in purple, with a suit, top hat and gloves and painted her face white, except for red around her eyes. It was totally striking. Calamity looked great too of course. She came down a little before the show and got all ready in the dressing room, so I guess Lori\u2019s giving her some pointers. She spent the night schmoozing, talking alot with Ginny, some with Desiree and tons with Madame Spidertoes. She was going to check with Ginny about whether what she was going when the extras showed up had something to do with Court business, so maybe she got some idea about that. Then again, Chalcedony was there, so maybe not.<br /> <br /> After my act thing, I headed to grab a seat with Julia, De la Roche, Hailey and Monica. I had more than a few beers too (its nice being kinda part owner of the bar) and it got to the point I was reenacting my favorite parts of the bit, you know, the coolest parts, even though Lori kept rolling her eyes and reminding me she had been there. I do feel a little bad, cause I think I distracted her from talking to the Spring Princess and now she\u2019s all worried about her.<br /> <br /> Well, not the brightest side to end things on, but that\u2019s about when I got that text from Captain Jack. Ah well. Things will be better in the morning, and hopefully Calamity will be home soon.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary </b><br /> <br /> I don\u2019t really know how to frame the events of the night. I\u2019m full of so many emotions right now that I don\u2019t know which should take the fore. Anger, sadness, fear, confusion, curiosity\u2026 how do you choose between so many options in a situation like this?<br /> <br /> For lack of a better idea, I guess I\u2019ll try to report things chronologically. First, the single shining ray of good news from this entire hellish evening: the show was gangbusters. My rendition of \u201cGoing to California\u201d went over fairly well, though maybe not as well as I would have liked. In contrast, my \u201cWalking on Sunshine\u201d number was <u>very</u> well-received, and had the crowd clapping and singing along with obvious joy\u2026 but the real show-stopper was Captain Jack\u2019s \u201cunscheduled\u201d interruption. His Benny Hill-style chase sequence with Gawain brought the house down.<br /> <br /> D and Julia were sharing a table, and I swung by after the show to say hello. Gawain joined us there eventually, and it was easy to see that he\u2019d been bitten by the showbiz bug. It was almost cute the way he kept going over his favorite parts of his debut routine. Unfortunately, I got so wrapped up in teasing him that I forgot I was supposed to talk to Princess Jolie about our conversation the other day, and by the time I remembered she had already taken her leave.<br /> <br /> So an hour or so later, the House had emptied out except for the motley and a few \u201cclose family\u201d associates like D and Julia. We were talking and joking around and generally having a fine old time when Gawain got a text from Captain Jack. It was very terse, but stated in no uncertain terms that he should go to the Rose and Thorn\u2026 and that he should bring Calamity with him. When Gawain inquired as to the nature of the excursion, the Captain allowed that he might want to bring the whole motley along, but that Calamity should definitely be present.<br /> <br /> It was with a palpable sense of dread that we piled into Gawain\u2019s van and made our way across town to the Rose and Thorn. I think most of us assumed that knife-work would be involved, as that\u2019s usually why people call in Calamity, but when we got there, an even nastier shock awaited us.<br /> <br /> Captain Jack met us at the club\u2019s side door and told us that Dark Kimberly had been shot! I was so stunned I couldn\u2019t even process the information for a minute. Who\u2019d want to shoot Kimberly? She\u2019s so sweet and helpful and accommodating\u2026 she\u2019s one of the least offensive people I know! The others started asking important questions like who had done it and how it had happened, but to my mind no one was asking the <u>most</u> important questions.<br /> <br /> \u201cIs she all right? Where is she?\u201d I asked, starting to push past Captain Jack and into the office.<br /> <br /> He put a hand gently but firmly on my shoulder. \u201cShe\u2019s going to be okay,\u201d he said softly to me, \u201cthe wound wasn\u2019t that bad. Some mortal cops and doctors are taking a look at her right now, and we can\u2019t use magic to heal her until they leave, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded, not happy with the situation, but willing to accept it.<br /> <br /> We spoke with a few other people, including Lucien Torrez. For once I was glad of his gung-ho attitude, as he seemed really keen on getting to the bottom of this crime and bringing those responsible to justice. Unfortunately, it\u2019s starting to look like that might be a bit of a tall order. You see, everyone who witnessed the attack saw the attacker as someone different. Some people saw a black man, some saw an Asian, and others saw a Hispanic. No two accounts of his appearance agree.<br /> <br /> When the police had cleared out, I called on the Contracts of Spring to heal Kimberly\u2019s wounds, and in no time she was good as new. She\u2019d been shot high in the chest. The bullet missed everything vital, but it must have really hurt. I tried to keep my emotions in check as much as possible so that Kimberly wouldn\u2019t see how upset I was. She needed confidence from me more than sympathy; she needed to know that she hadn\u2019t been hurt that badly and that she was going to be okay.<br /> <br /> Some of my friends are wondering if the attack wasn\u2019t meant to kill, but rather to drum up negative publicity for the Rose and Thorn, or maybe to send a message to the Spring Court. There are no changelings that we know of who have the power to make themselves look different to different people, and there are no common Contracts that grant that ability either, though it\u2019s possible that there might be Goblin Contracts or Hedge Fruit that can do so.<br /> <br /> Davie offered to take Kimberly home, and we all agreed that it would be best for her to get some rest. Calamity, Jacob, and Gawain decided to check out the Autumn Court\u2019s library to see if they could find any reference to an ability that would cause people to see or remember someone\u2019s features differently. Torrez had mentioned that Molly Nuit had been at the club earlier, but he couldn\u2019t find her in the aftermath of the shooting. I understand Jacob decided to check up on her after he left the Autumn Court\u2019s library (since she\u2019s also a member of the Winter Court). Ace \u2013 acting on a tip that there was another local club that burned down a few years back \u2013 decided to go club-hopping to see if he could find anything out along that angle.<br /> <br /> I called Princess Jolie, but got no answer. I decided to head by Glamour Springs to see if I could catch her in, as she needed to know that a member of her Court had been shot. D pulled me aside before we headed out.<br /> <br /> \u201cLori,\u201d she began seriously, \u201cFlores is really upset about this whole thing. I think she needs friends around. Julia and I are going to stay with her, if you don\u2019t mind.\u201d<br /> <br /> Honestly, a part of me sort of <u>did</u> mind. I wanted comfort myself, and I didn\u2019t want to face the night alone. But it would have been petty to play that card, and I don\u2019t want to be the stereotypical jealous girlfriend. I gave D a kiss and a smile and told her to go and be with her friend, and that I would see her tomorrow. She squeezed my hand gratefully and went off with Julia.<br /> <br /> Gawain dropped me off at the house, and I drove over to Glamour Springs and used my key to get inside. It was dark inside, and beaucoup creepy. I had almost decided that the place was empty and was about to give it up as a wash when I heard a quiet, nervous voice calling out my name tentatively\u2026 \u201cLori?\u201d<br /> <br /> I looked around but didn\u2019t see anyone. \u201cWho\u2019s there?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s me\u2026\u201d the voice replied, and I recognized it this time. Mary is a local beastlike Changeling with ovine features. We\u2019ve chatted a few times, but I don\u2019t know her that well.<br /> <br /> \u201cMary? Where are you? Come out where I can see you,\u201d I called out, more than a little freaked out by the events of the night.<br /> <br /> \u201cI, umm\u2026\u201d she stammered for a few seconds. \u201cI\u2026 don\u2019t have any clothes on,\u201d she finished in a rush. \u201cI don\u2019t know where they are.\u201d<br /> <br /> I grabbed a towel from one of the service stations. \u201cCome on out and wrap yourself in this, Mary,\u201d I called out. \u201cI\u2019m averting my eyes.\u201d Calamity or Jacob would probably scold me for closing my eyes in the presence of an unknown factor at a time like this, but honestly\u2026 what would I do even if I could see an attack coming? I\u2019m completely useless in a fight.<br /> <br /> A moment later Mary, blushing furiously, explained what she knew of her situation. \u201cI was relaxing in one of the hot tubs in the private area of the springs,\u201d she said, \u201cand I must have fallen asleep. Davie and Kimberly were there\u2026 I remember the two of them saying they were heading to the Dream House to catch tonight\u2019s show. When I woke up, nobody was around, the lights were out, and I couldn\u2019t find my clothes.\u201d<br /> <br /> I told her about the shooting at the Rose and Thorn, and she was just as upset as the rest of us. \u201cWhy would anyone want to hurt Kimberly?\u201d she asked plaintively. I could only express similar feelings of confusion and anger.<br /> <br /> Mary couldn\u2019t get into her apartment without her keys (which were in her missing clothes), so I offered to put her up in the Dream House\u2019s guest room for the night. I called Gawain to catch the others up on the situation, and he shared a bit of information with me as well. Apparently there is a Goblin Contract that can allow its user to appear as a different person to everyone they meet, though it\u2019s fairly rare magic\u2026 almost unknown around here. The downside is that once the magic wears off, the user tends to forget who they are for a few hours\u2026 at least until they go to sleep and wake up.<br /> <br /> I talked the situation over with Gawain, and both of us entertained the notion that Mary might have something to do with the shooting\u2026 but the facts don\u2019t really fit. If Mary was the shooter, she would have had to get all the way from the Rose and Thorn to Glamour Springs incredibly quickly and then force herself to take a catnap and wake up before I got there\u2026 all without remembering anything about who she was or why she was acting that way. I suppose she could have used a Goblin Fruit to fall asleep at will, but those things tend to knock you out for at least eight hours.<br /> <br /> One other thing doesn\u2019t really add up about her story, and it\u2019s been bothering me for a while now. She said that Davie and Dark Kimberly left Glamour Springs to head to the Dream House just before she passed out. But those two weren\u2019t at the Dream House tonight\u2026 they went to the Rose and Thorn instead. I suppose it\u2019s possible that Mary just misremembered what they said, or that they changed their mind after they left Glamour Springs\u2026 but those explanations seem too pat somehow.<br /> <br /> After I\u2019d already shown Mary to the guest room, I decided I wanted to ask her a few questions after all, so I knocked on her door. She answered in a borrowed dressing gown, and seemed eager to help me however she could. I asked her what day it was, wondering if maybe she had passed out the previous day (when Davie and Kimberly <u>did</u> come to the Dream House) and had been unconscious for more than 24 hours, but she knew it was Saturday.<br /> <br /> \u201cDid you want anything else?\u201d she asked brightly. \u201cDo you want to come in?\u201d<br /> <br /> I shook my head, thinking that I would just crawl off to bed and try to get past the events of the day. \u201cNo thanks, Mary,\u201d I replied.<br /> <br /> Her face fell. \u201cOf course not,\u201d she mumbled, \u201cstupid of me to ask. Sorry.\u201d And she closed the door before I could process what had just happened. Poor girl. She has very low self-esteem, and what she sees as my rejection will probably make her feel horrible about herself. I\u2019ll have to apologize to her in the morning\u2026 let her know that I wasn\u2019t saying \u201cno\u201d to her, I was just physically and emotionally exhausted.<br /> <br /> I turned to walk back to my bedroom, and Insincere Marguerite was there, grinning her catlike grin. \u201cIt has been a long night, <i> <i>non?</i> </i>\u201d she asked softly. \u201cPerhaps you would like to join me in my bed tonight?\u201d<br /> <br /> I sighed. \u201cNot really in the mood right now, Marguerite,\u201d I said softly.<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cI thought maybe\u2026 if not for pleasure, then at least you might like another heartbeat close by tonight.\u201d I love the way that word sounds in her sexy French accent: heartbeat. <i><i>Art-beat</i>. </i> It\u2019s like she\u2019s describing the rhythm of some beautiful song or the cadence of an intensely meaningful poem. In my case, the phonic coincidence is even more meaningful: music really <u>does</u> seem to flow through my body, nourishing my tired limbs, bringing attractive flushes to my skin, and keeping me going on nights like this, when the world seems determined to beat me down.<br /> <br /> In the end I agreed to join her in her boudoir. I\u2019ve been up for a while writing in this journal, but I think I\u2019m about ready to hit the sack now. It\u2019s been a hell of a night, and I can only pray that tomorrow is better.<br /> <br /> I miss D.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> The street is dark and wet. The air is still damp from the rain and my boots scatter the puddles of water it left behind. The wind is fitful and warm, it teases my hair around my shoulders, makes it brush and dance with the crystalline spikes rising from my shoulders.<br /> <br /> There is a light above the door. I shift the package to my left hand, feeling the present's weight and smiling as I lift my hand and knock upon the white door. My bloody knuckles leave a smear of crimson behind. I can hear footsteps beyond. A droplet of blood falls from the ribbon-wrapped box to patter against my booted toe.<br /> <br /> The door swings open and reveals Kimberly. She's perfect, as always, nothing out of place, not a curl or a stitch.<br /> <br /> I lift the present, smiling as I offer it up. The box is wet and soft so I make sure to support it with both hands. \u201cI brought you a gift,\u201d I tell her.<br /> <br /> She hesitates, eyes moving over the now red and white box with it's bright festive ribbon but her hands remain at her sides. \u201cWhat is it?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOpen it and see. It's for you.\u201d<br /> <br /> Her fingers shake ever so slightly as she reaches to tug at the end of the ribbon and pull it apart, letting it slip free and dangle in the listless air. She looks up at my eyes and I nod to her. \u201cGo on sweetling.\u201d<br /> <br /> She gingerly plucks the lid up and away, careful not to let the blood get on her hands or to drip on her. She looks in and her throat tightens. Her eye widen and she drops the lid as she backs up.<br /> <br /> \u201cI'm the only one that gets to hurt my pretty little doll,\u201d I whisper as I step forward and she backs away, shaking her head. I set the gristly box on a side table, blood staining on the lace doily rapidly as I smile and lift my jagged fingertips to stroke her cheeks with my razors. My hands slip to her neck, curling around it to squeeze as I lean in slowly and claim her lips, sinking my teeth into that perfect plump swell. Her fear and blood taste so sweet...<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> I wake up again and roll over. It's late. Or maybe it's early now. It's still dark at any rate. The moonlight filters in through my window. The light from the nightlight in the hallway cuts across the floor to meet it. I can't sleep. Maybe it's silly to be so excited about turning fourteen but I am. Mom and Dad reserved one of the big shelters at the park and there's going to be cake and ice cream and cookout food and more cake. Plus I know Stasia has been planning something big for \u201cEmpress Kitty Katt's Annual Tribute\u201d as she's taken to calling it. I am a little afraid to find out what madness my blood sister has gotten into her head this time but whatever it is, it will at least be interesting.<br /> <br /> I pull the covers tighter around me and shiver. It shouldn't be that cold in here. I blink and frown. When did it get so dark? Did the power go out? But why can't I see the moonlight? I squirm and look for my clock but I can't see it. It's got a battery, it should be lit. I start to reach out for it but something brushes my hand. Something soft and cold. I jerk back and pull the quilt tighter around me. I can't see anything. I'm trembling now. I'm not alone. I can hear them. Whispering in the dark, dozens of voices all jumbled together. I can't understand what they're saying because they're talking over each other. I'm not even sure if it's English. It sounds foreign...<br /> <br /> \u201cW-Who's there?\u201d My voice sounds so tiny. I'm shaking and terrified and it shows. \u201cW-What d-do you w-want?\u201d<br /> <br /> This time the mad chorus is unified for the most part, only breaking apart at the last word.<br /> <br /> \u201cSnowglobe is incomplete. It needs a new Jane/girl-child/player/daughter/pet/sister/toy/friend/plaything/voice.\u201d<br /> <br /> Then I fall... straight up. I cry out in surprise as I tumble through the air. The ceiling opens up and I fall up through it. As I spin through the air I can see my house and my neighborhood dwindling as I fall helplessly up into the night sky.<br /> <br /> I fall and fall and fall through the void for hours or days or years. It's timeless and cold and dark.<br /> <br /> Then I see something. A speck of light. I'm falling towards it. It grows larger. It's a city in a bubble of glass, like one of those holiday souvenirs. I'm hurtling towards it uncontrollably.<br /> <br /> It's farther away than I thought. It gets bigger and bigger as I fall closer and closer. It's not a model at all, it's a real full-sized town. It fills my vision. I close my eyes as the glass comes rushing toward me. I wrap my arms around myself and I scream. I've been falling for so long. There's no way I'll survive an impact at this speed. Then I just fall <i>through</i> it. I feel it washing over and around and <i>through</i> my body but there is no bone shattering impact. I'm still falling.<br /> <br /> I spin and tumble through the sky. It's night but there are stars painted on the inside of the glass and soon I can't tell it's not the sky I've lived under my whole life. I fall toward a house and once more I brace myself for a fatal crash. This time as I near it my decent slows. I'm drifting, sinking more than falling now. The roof ripples and flows like water to open up. I float down through the hole and it flows closed behind me. I sink into my bed and pull the comforter tightly around myself. The room is dark. I've never seen it before but I know it's my room.<br /> <br /> I'm home.<br /> <br /> I'm Jane.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Well, on the plus side the show tonight went really well. People were staring in wonder at Lorelei on the stage like they\u2019d seen an angel. Not hard to imagine with those wings. Insincere Marguerite announced her act again, still wearing those adorable socks, but with a different outfit. I can understand why she prefers the shadows. I do too, but she looks awfully good in the spotlight. Anyhoo\u2026Ace did his \u201cFlashdance\u201d act, which was just, well, interesting. He borrowed one of Insincere Marguerite\u2019s puppets for the act. I think it went rather well. It certainly entertained the crowd. During all of this, Calamity was working her way through the audience, talking to people here and there and generally getting a feel for how things were going. She stopped and talked to Ginny and Chalcedony at one point. I can guess what that conversation was about.<br /> <br /> Gawain and Captain Jack pulled off their little \u201cshow.\u201d Jack snuck up on stage, badly disguised while Gawain pretended to try and figure out what was wrong. It was all very slapstick and reminded me of Benny Hill. Still funny though. I will admit that a smile crossed my face once or twice during their antics. After their little act finished the show continued like normal.<br /> <br /> I will have to remember to tell Calamity that having her walk through the crowd all dressed up in that lovely dress certainly encouraged drink sales. Not beer though. I had more \u201cfancy\u201d drink orders tonight. I think some of the patrons where trying to look more sophisticated when they saw Calamity walking by in that sexy dress. Not that I\u2019m complaining, drink sales are a part of this place doing well. Maybe if we had one or two of the other girls walk around and chat up the customers it would have the same effect. Gives a more personal feel. Wow\u2026my mind goes to strange places when I drink\u2026<br /> <br /> And on to the reason I\u2019m drinking. Well, not really. It has been a really long day. I\u2019m tired, I\u2019m stressed out and my side hurts. Pain killers weren\u2019t cutting it, so I figured drinking could only help, right?<br /> <br /> Okay\u2026so after the show Gawain got a text from Jack asking him and Calamity to come to the Rose and Thorn right away. That something had happened. The fact that he requested Calamity made us think that he was expecting a fight, so with a minimum of discussion most of us decided to go. We got to the club to find it surrounded by police cars and an ambulance. We left our weapons (or concealed them) and headed for a side door. The door was opened by Jack and we all filed in. Within moments none other than Lucien Torrez came up and offered to explain what happened. He led us to a private office and told us what was going on. Apparently someone came into the club, walked up to Dark Kimberly and shot her, then disappeared. No one saw where the shooter went, but everyone saw the shooter do it. Only problem is, everyone saw someone different. The shooter\u2019s gender and ethnicity changed depending on who you asked. No one knew of a power or gift that could do that, or at least we didn\u2019t know of anyone that could do it.<br /> <br /> We also discussed whether or not the shooting was specifically against Kimberly, or if it was to make the club look bad. I think we pretty much agreed that it was likely to discredit the club. There are far more effective ways to terrorize someone than give them a non-fatal would. The shooter was close enough to have their pick of targets and yet they specifically shot her in the shoulder, away from major organs. They wanted to wound, not kill. It was brought up that several years ago there was another club in this area that had been targeted by an arsonist. No one was supposed to have been there, since it was closed but the police found several bodies in the remains of the building. Only one was identified I think. I\u2019m not sure if it\u2019s related or a coincidence, but I plan on keeping it in mind.<br /> <br /> After finishing our talk with Torrez, who was amazingly civil to me I might add, we split up to look for answers. Gawain, Calamity and I headed for the Autumn Court\u2019s archives and looked for any reference to a power that a Changeling might possess that could do what was witnessed tonight. I wasn\u2019t that much of a help, but did my best to hand books to people or put them back. It\u2019s been a really long time since I\u2019ve been in a library, so I don\u2019t feel like a complete failure, but I do need to get reacquainted with normal things, like libraries. After some time the others found a reference to a Goblin contract that Changelings can use that would do exactly as was seen. The downside to this power is that the person who uses it loses all memory of who they are and what they did after the act until they\u2019ve slept and woken back up. We figured this would make it a bit easier to find the culprit, if we could catch them sill awake.<br /> <br /> Torrez mentioned that Molly Nuit had been at the club, but was not seen there after the attack. The Summer courtier did not actually see her leave, but thought it could be significant. The rest of the motley thought that there might be something or someone targeting clubs, so Ace and Lorelei went out to see if anyone else had any strange events happen in their place. I know Lorelei went to Glamour Springs, I think to look for Princess Jolie, and Ace went to LowJack\u2019s among other places. At Glamour Springs Lorelei found Mary (I forgot her family name) in one of the pools. Apparently she\u2019d fallen asleep and someone had stolen her clothes, and with them her keys and phone. Lorelei didn\u2019t know of what we\u2019d found out at that point, but wanted to help Mary, so she found her a towel and took her back to the house.<br /> <br /> Calamity called Torrez and let him know what we\u2019d found out. He said he would let his court know of what was going on, but suggested to her that I might go to speak to Master Darke about this. To let him know what was going on, and to check up on Molly since she\u2019s in my court. I agreed that this would be a good idea and headed out. I went to the clinic and found that Doctor Bright was in residence. I went with him to his office and told him of what happened and what we had found out. He seemed interested and wanted to check on Molly himself. I suggested that I go with him to be on the safe side, in case something happened. I think he was amused, or possibly annoyed. Most likely the later. Anyhooo\u2026. He didn\u2019t show it, but said that he\u2019d be fine. I don\u2019t doubt that for a moment, but insisted that I should go. I said that I did not feel right staying behind, and wanted to make sure that Molly was okay. Privately I wanted to be there in case she was our culprit so the fact couldn\u2019t get swept under the rug. I would be a witness to anything that happened. That could have been a good thing or a bad thing if something had happened. I\u2019m not sure I\u2019d be writing in this journal right now if I\u2019d seen something Dr. Bright or Master Darke didn\u2019t want known. Anyhoo\u2026He finally relented and he drove us to her apartment, handing a pistol to me as he grabbed a shotgun for himself. That just reminded me that I need to ask Calamity for shooting lessons.<br /> <br /> When we arrived at Molly\u2019s apartment he called her phone and left a message threatening to take her door down if she didn\u2019t open it within 15 seconds. She didn\u2019t get the door open and he wasn\u2019t bluffing. He pulled his shotgun from under his coat and shot the doorknob off the door and pried open the door. We walked in. I was never so glad that I kept my hood up as I was in that moment. I really don\u2019t want to be identified by neighbors as breaking into Molly\u2019s place with possibly violent intent. Anyhoo\u2026after we walked in it only took a moment for Molly to come out of her room, bleary eyed and wearing her night clothes. It appeared that we had just woken her up. I told her what had happened at the club and that no one knew where she\u2019d gone and we were worried. She seemed a little amused at this and asked if I would be staying to keep her safe for the rest of the night/early morning. I declined as politely as I could citing that I needed to get back to my Motley to let them know that everything was okay.<br /> <br /> After we\u2019d established that Molly was fine Dr. Bright turned around and just marched right out of her apartment. I followed, but wished her a good night and tried to get the door to stay closed as I left. Dr. Bright drove back to the clinic and we went our separate ways. I headed back to the house and let everyone know what I\u2019d found out. It wasn\u2019t much I guess, but every little bit helps.<br /> <br /> This has been a very eventful day. Hard conversations, busy night at the club, and someone shooting one of ours. I guess I\u2019ve just gotten used to quieter days since I got back to \u201cthe world.\u201d I\u2019ve gone weeks without drawing a knife or getting involved in anything \u201cout of the ordinary.\u201d Well, out of the ordinary for a regular person. My \u201cordinary\u201d is different from other people\u2019s definition of the word. Pretty much all Changelings have a different definition of what an ordinary day is. I\u2019ve seen some that are actually able to lead lives pretty close to the one that they left behind. Sometimes I envy them. Sometimes. Sometimes I think that I am too much changed to go back to a normal life. I used to be able to relate to people, at least in that hormonal teenage drama kinda way. But I\u2019ve become so much more wary when it comes to others and their motivations. Maybe that\u2019s just because mine are not always so clear that I see it in others where it may or may not be. I just feel separated from the people around me. Less so with my motley-mates, but still to some extent. That\u2019s probably my fault though. I have a hard time letting people in. Trust issues, I know. I\u2019m still convinced that a therapist dedicated to Changelings would make a fortune, not to mention help a lot of people. The lot of us could be the poster children for mental health problems. But until that day comes I have my good friend Jack D.<br /> <br /> And I just bled through my shirt. Shit. Okay, gotta take care of that. I wonder if I should have stitched that cut closed? Maybe I can get some of those little butterfly Band-Aids to keep it closed until it heals. I suppose if all else fails I can find a sewing kit somewhere in this house. Maybe in the costume room. You\u2019d think that there would be seamstress stuff in there. Actually I\u2019ll go do that now. Most everyone should be asleep by now, that way I won\u2019t disturb anyone. Then sleep. I think the adrenaline from earlier is wearing off and the alcohol is taking over. Time to take care of things then sleep. Sleep would be good.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> Tonight was a fun night that took an unfortunate turn. Sadly. It was a good show. I took the stage again in my purple suit. Julia and De La Rocha were appreciative. Captain Jack was chased around by Gawain. Ace forgot it was not the 80s. All fun.<br /> <br /> Then we heard Dark Kimberly got shot. Not killed, and apparently as shooting victims go, not seriously hurt. America. Nonetheless the others, including Julia and De La Rocha, went to investigate. It happened at Rose &amp; Thorn, and both Julia and De La Rocha are friends with Flores, who was not shot but owns the club and was not answering her phone. Apparently.<br /> <br /> Calamity has not returned. Worryingly. Gawain came back and got her bike. Jacob returned eventually, as did Ace. Lorelei returned with Mary, who lost her clothes. Apparently. Women, and Men really, sometimes have that problem around Lorelei, but not usually like that. Lorelei wound up in my bed. It was no seduction\u2026Lorelei was in no mood, and I had no intention to change that. So she still found herself listening to a heartbeat tonight.<br /> <br /> Mary\u2019s odd behavior and the suspicious circumstances that found her in the altogether had Lorelei on edge, and for, I believe, good reason. Possibly.<br /> <br /> But she is safe here. Safe enough.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XIII</i><br /> <br /> Calamity had been awake for over 48 hours, and her Merit to help her stay awake was beginning to falter. Her player elected to have her fail the roll to stay awake, rather to fall asleep in the Autumn Court\u2019s library. Thus the unusual journal.<br /> <br /> Events were pretty well covered. Ace had a scene at Lowjack\u2019s. Calamity had an interesting discussion about Lorelei with Spidertoes. Lots of questions but not many answers. Not least of which was what was up with Ace and the whole Mother Theresa thing anyway?<br /> <br /> More in two weeks, comments and questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T15:06:55-07:00","id":279108,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to look in on the Malibu Dream House. The plot thickens as the PCs learn more about the secrets of the Fey surrounding them. Note Calamity\u2019s journal covers the past two sessions, not one, so is longer and covers more time.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XIV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> May 11<sup>th</sup><br /> <br /> Well, today has sure been a roller coaster ride. From terrified to sad to confused to sad to worried to... paranoid, I guess? At this point even I\u2019m beginning to be a little suspicious of Desiree, though Calamity made some good points that maybe that\u2019s a reason that it\u2019s not her. I mean, that everything\u2018s looking just a little too sure, you know? Of course, that led to the awful idea that maybe not all of the Director\u2019s Changelings have been loyalists like everyone says, but that any of them that weren\u2019t got framed by the Director. On one hand, that\u2019s super arrogant, to think we\u2019re the only ones that could see through it. On the other, us Changelings are a really paranoid group as a whole, and the Director is really good at telling stories, you know, so maybe it\u2019s not really very farfetched.<br /> <br /> Anyways, to start at the beginning, I got woken up by Lori making eggs and Jacob making coffee. I had fallen asleep in the office chair, so I was right there, you know? But Calamity wasn\u2019t. There, I mean, or up in her room. Her mirror was broken and she hadn\u2019t left a message, with me or any of the others. So I was maybe a little bit panicky. I grabbed Jacob, since he\u2019s good at tracking, you know, and left Ace checking his scrambled eggs for a pulse. I don\u2019t even know what that was about. That would have meant asking.<br /> <br /> I made good time to the lighthouse and a Fairest named Moon was pretty quick to answer my banging. Ze hadn\u2019t seen Calamity, which did nothing for my state of mind, so I followed hir closely when ze went to check. Thankfully, Tommy had found her, and left a note saying so. That calmed me down, and I apologized to Moon, and ze was really nice about it. Ze even came to the show tonight, with Dionysia. *That* was a table full of pretty people. Ze even had on this awesome silver suit thing, with a really intricate dragon embroidered on it, you know?<br /> <br /> Anyways, I got me and Jacob back home and there were even some eggs left. It was strange to not have made breakfast, but between everything else, it was kinda just a weird feeling, you know, like I was forgetting something. And that was nothing on the conversation we walked back in on. Apparently Ace wanted to have tarantulas in his act, and Lori said no, so he decided to do William Shatner\u2019s Rocket Man instead. He and Insincere Marguerite even worked out doing the three dude parts, one with him in the cloud dress at the piano, on in the stained glass outfit and one in a straitjacket hanging from the ceiling.<br /> <br /> Lori decided to do a song from Les Mis - she had even managed to get a Les Mis shirt in the day since she\u2019d heard about it, so I guess she liked it? It fit her super well, *you* know. She did an awesome job with the song too, having decided to go with the sad one, not the super sad one or the really, really sad one. We decided that after this we\u2019re going to do a new thing with the advertising, where we do some sort of symbol or decoration for each Court, and put them on flyers for shows where we know our acts will cater to a particular emotion.<br /> <br /> But before our show, we tried to help out the naked girl, Mary, that Lori had found at Glamour Springs last night. Well, she wasn\u2019t naked anymore, Lori had lent her some clothes, you know, since she couldn\u2019t get into her house yet. It turns out she\u2019d been drinking, which might explain her fuzzy memory, but when we found Davie he said they\u2019d put her in the resting room before they left, and put her clothes and stuff in there with her. I guess the rest of the motley got suspicious about something, cause they sent Insincere Marguerite to check out her house before she got there. It turns out someone had slept in her bed last night (when she was supposed to be at the House) and she had a pistol with armor piercing ammo. Not what shot Dark Kimberly, but a little out of keeping, you know? The bed thing was especially weird. She seems really smitten with Lori though. It was kinda super adorable.<br /> <br /> I missed most of that though, cause when we got to Glamour Springs, Desiree and Chalcedony were having a huge fight. Ace was sure it was over a hairbrush, and even tried to get me to bet on it with him. He wound up giving me $5 even though I didn\u2019t take the bet, because he eventually convinced himself that it wasn\u2019t about a hairbrush. It was actually about Chalcedony accusing Desiree of shooting Dark Kimberly, because, Chalcedony said, she saw Desiree not at home, and Desiree said she was at home. They both seemed to be telling the truth, you know, even Jacob said so. Chalcedony was acting really weird though.<br /> <br /> Lori broke it up, and convinced Chalcedony to drop it without proof, so she left. Jacob followed her and she told him specifically that she had followed Desiree after she left the House, and that Desiree had gone to the Rose and Thorn, but disappeared at the door. Calamity said later, when we all got back, that Desiree had said Chalcedony seemed familiar in a way she couldn\u2019t place, before all this even happened. Desiree also told us, at Glamour Springs, that some of the Director\u2019s people could do the shape changing thing like the shooter had. So that\u2019s all a giant mess. Desiree was not taking it well, at the Springs, so I sat with her a little while to give her a shoulder to cry on while the others helped Mary look for her stuff, until Desiree felt ok enough to go home, you know?<br /> <br /> We didn\u2019t find anything at the Springs though, so Insincere Marguerite just let her in to her house. I guess her landlord can get her another set of keys, hopefully quick. That would suck a lot, getting all your stuff stolen. Also, hopefully she\u2019s ok, cause it was maybe the person who stole her keys that slept there last night. Shit. Maybe we shouldn\u2019t have let her go home, but then we\u2019d have had to explain about the bed thing, and I\u2019m not sure that would be so good, with the giant crush Mary has on Lori. Maybe I\u2019ll give her a call, or have Lori do it...?<br /> <br /> Back to earlier. Calamity called while we were driving to Mary\u2019s, still really tired sounding. She looked super worn out too, when we met up at the House. We caught her up on everything, such as there was, then I pulled her aside. She said she was ok. When I asked about the mirror she looked at her hands, and I could see some extra cuts. After the conversation about being what her Keeper made her, and about her fetch\u2019s kid, she just had a bad time, she said, but she was better now. I did ask if we could sleep here tonight, and I think we\u2019ll get to. She needs a real full night\u2019s sleep, you know?<br /> <br /> But just then it was time for a show, just enough time left to get ready. Julia and De la Roche were there, and Joan came with Monica and Haley, to talk about the shooting, you know. I sat with them, after the doors closed. Joan kept bringing up the shooting, and Monica kept trying to change the subject, it was a little funny. I almost didn\u2019t notice when Chalcedony came in to get Ginny and didn\u2019t think anything of it, but Calamity noticed something odd was going on when they got up to leave, so she did her whisper thing to let me know she was following them.<br /> <br /> It was really good she did too, cause it turned out to not be Chalcedony at all, but an Extra thing that looked like her, out to kill Ginny. Calamity brought the shredded manikin back to the House, along with Ginny, once Ginny had checked in on the real Chalcedony, who was not happy at all about it. She figured it had to be Desiree, I guess. Jacob did his best to keep her from going after Desiree right off at least.<br /> <br /> By that time, it was just the motley, Julia, De la Roche, Monica, Haley and Joan. Calamity stepped aside to make a phone call almost right off, then pulled Joan aside right after. Whatever she said, Joan was much friendlier towards Ginny after, in her own particular idiom, so that was good. The rest of the conversation was kinda a disaster though. See, they came back talking about sparring, I think, but we just caught the last bit, where they were talking about me coming to, and how big my sword was, and how good I was at using it... I think Calamity was doing it on purpose, you know, but Joan was clueless. And I felt bad, cause, I mean, yeah, it would be hot, me and Calamity and her, but Joan needed a friend, not somebody who was always thinking of her like that, especially after her Durance and the Spring Court thing.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, that was awkward, I was bright red, and all of us had the giggles, so Joan decided it was a bad time for discussing things. I tried to make excuses, you know, cause it had been a long, frustrating 24 hours, which prompted a beautiful speech, about justice and light and goodness. I think we were all a little stunned. Like Lori said, it was pretty much poetry, you know? Ace even offered her a job performing, which set her hyperventilating as soon as we assured her she could just talk like that and everyone would love it, she wouldn\u2019t have to dance. She almost pulled Monica\u2019s arm off, running for the door.<br /> <br /> We still weren\u2019t done though. Since Chalcedony had said Desiree had gone to the Rose and Thorn, but disappeared at the door, we decided to check out the cameras outside, and talk with the doorman. We figured on looking around ourselves, as much as we could, so people didn\u2019t get even more bad ideas about Desiree before we knew anything concrete, you know? Julia and De la Roche said they thought Flores would be fine with that, so most of us headed that way, while Jacob went to intercept Chalcedony before she did anything to Desiree<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> I woke up this morning to the alarm\u2019s shrill beeping with Insincere Marguerite draped over me like a blanket\u2026 or a shroud, I suppose. I extricated myself from her embrace as gently as I could, shrugging off her sleepy kisses. There was a small part of me that wanted to stay there with her, but she was being awfully clingy, and I didn\u2019t want her to get the wrong idea. Besides, the Lord was calling, and time, tide, and church services wait for no woman.<br /> <br /> So I made myself up and headed out the door. Aside from the usual glasses and ponytail, I wore a white shirt with a modest collar and a prim grey skirt. No solos for me today, but the choir sang a few beautiful hymns, and dad\u2019s sermon on the parable of the mustard seed was a lovely little homily about personal growth and how great things can come from humble beginnings.<br /> <br /> People were still asleep when I got back from church, and I\u2019d been thinking a lot lately about how much Gawain does for us, so I figured I\u2019d give him the day off and make breakfast myself. I may not be a gourmet chef, but I did my fair share of cooking after Mom passed, and I can at least make scrambled eggs and toast when the need arises. Jacob was the first to join me, and he started making the coffee as the others filtered in.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite sashayed into the kitchen wearing a shirt that barely preserved her modesty\u2026 and nothing else. She was flirty and smoky, and obviously in the mood\u2026 but I wasn\u2019t. I don\u2019t know if it was the fact that I\u2019d just come home from church, my lingering dismay over Dark Kimberly\u2019s shooting, or just the fact that I don\u2019t want her to think I\u2019m going to come running whenever she crooks her finger at me, but something just wasn\u2019t right. I could tell that she was a little put off by my standoffishness, but she\u2019ll get over it.<br /> <br /> Gawain was almost frantic because Calamity never came home last night, and he found the shards of a broken mirror in her bathroom (and I <u>still</u> don\u2019t know what that\u2019s about). He grabbed Jacob, and the two of them headed over to the Lighthouse to look for her. They didn\u2019t find her immediately, but apparently her friend Tommy left a note for Gawain to let him know that Calamity was okay, and he passed the message on to the rest of us so that we wouldn\u2019t worry.<br /> <br /> When they got home, we started talking about the upcoming show, and I announced a late change in the line-up. I\u2019d thrown on a <u>Les Miserables</u> T-shirt after I got back from church (and let them all wonder how I\u2019d acquired it roughly eighteen hours after I learned of the musical\u2019s existence), and told them all that I\u2019d like to do a song from the show. The only problem, I said, was that I wasn\u2019t sure whether I wanted to sing \u201cThe Sad One\u201d (meaning \u201cOn My Own\u201d) or \u201cThe Really Sad One\u201d (meaning \u201cI Dreamed a Dream\u201d). Gawain got this goofy look on his face and suggested that I could sing the \u201cSuper Sad One.\u201d I gave him a blank stare and deadpanned that \u201cA Little Fall of Rain\u201d really doesn\u2019t make much sense when taken out of the context of the rest of the musical. Then I chuckled to let him know I was joking.<br /> <br /> I mentioned that Jacob should probably invite some of his fellow Winter Courtiers, as the sorrow would probably be flowing freely tonight. That got the motley talking about how we should start catering our shows to the individual courts, and <u>that</u> led to a truly great idea! We\u2019re going to set up a system of codes or symbols which we will implement in our advertising, letting fellow Changelings know which emotions we intend to stir up in our audience at any given show.<br /> <br /> Mary got over her shyness and joined us a little while later. Her obvious crush on me is still adorable, even if I feel a little bad about maaaaaybe ever so slightly leading her on. A little. We drove her over to Glamour Springs to look for her clothes, but they were nowhere to be found. Nor were her keys.<br /> <br /> Davie was there, though, and he was able to shed a bit more light on Mary\u2019s story\u2026 sort of. He corroborated the earlier parts of her tale: he and Kimberly were here with her yesterday, and she passed out after drinking quite a bit. They moved Mary and her clothes into one of the resting areas (she had been wearing a bathing suit at the time) and left her there when they went to the Rose and Thorn. We examined the resting room, but found no trace of Mary\u2019s clothes. There were signs that someone had slept there recently, and there was also evidence that someone had used the nearby restroom, so I suppose it\u2019s possible that Mary had woken up in a drunken stupor and removed her suit to go to the bathroom, but that still doesn\u2019t explain what happened to her clothes.<br /> <br /> We got a bit distracted at this point by a loud argument which looked to be on the verge of becoming violent. Desiree and Chalcedony were shouting at each other, ad Chalcedony looked ready to throw a punch when we intervened. She stopped just short of accusing Desiree of shooting Dark Kimberly, but she admitted that this was only because she couldn\u2019t prove it yet. For her part, Desiree seemed genuinely hurt and upset that anyone could believe she\u2019d do something like that.<br /> <br /> Gawain pulled the two of them apart, and I tried to talk Chalcedony down. I got her to calm down a little and promise to at least lay off the public shouting matches until she dug up some proof. Later, Chalcedony admitted to Jacob that she knew Desiree was lying about her activities last night. She said that she had seen Desiree walking alone late last night, and had followed her to the Rose and Thorn, but lost track of her when she went inside. For her part, Desiree remained firm in her assertion that she had stayed home last night, and didn\u2019t know anything about the attack.<br /> <br /> Who the hell are we supposed to believe? Chalcedony could be lying to throw suspicion off herself. Or she could be telling the truth, in which case someone needs to take a serious look at Desiree and her actions. Or, she could be telling the truth, and Desiree might have a perfectly innocent (or at least unrelated) reason for lying about her whereabouts. Or (as later events demonstrated) she could be telling the truth but mistaken about who or what she actually <u>saw</u> last night. Man, I hate this Nancy Drew shit.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, we all thought Mary\u2019s story had more holes in it than French lace, so we decided to do a little snooping. We told Mary that Insincere Marguerite could get into her apartment, but that she\u2019d have to run back by the Dream House first to pick up some tools. While we supposedly waited for her, Marguerite (who has never needed tools to effect a little B&amp;E) went straight to Mary\u2019s apartment and looked around for a bit. What she found was more than a little worrying.<br /> <br /> First, <u>someone</u> slept in Mary\u2019s bed last night, and I sincerely doubt that it was Goldilocks. Perhaps even more troublesome was the fact that Mary apparently keeps a loaded large-caliber pistol in her nightstand, loaded with armor-piercing ammunition. From Marguerite\u2019s description it doesn\u2019t sound like the gun that was used in Dark Kimberly\u2019s shooting, but it still doesn\u2019t add up with what little we know about Mary at all.<br /> <br /> Since we had nothing solid to confront her with, we ended up just letting Mary back into her apartment and heading back to the Dream House. I tried calling Princess Jolie again, but got no answer (which didn\u2019t really surprise me; Davie had told me that she was probably with Queen Charlotte and had likely turned off her phone).<br /> <br /> Calamity was at the Dream House when we got back, and though she looked really tired, she threw herself into preparing for the night\u2019s show along with the rest of us. I decided to go with \u201cI Dreamed a Dream\u201d for my big solo number tonight, and worked with Marguerite until we had the musical accompaniment just right before heading off to get into costume and makeup.<br /> <br /> The show went well, I think. It wasn\u2019t the best I\u2019ve ever performed, but I think my number was fairly well received. I even saw the glint of tears on more than a few cheeks as I poured my glamour into my performance. I glanced up at D as the spots went down, and she wasn\u2019t crying, but she gave me one of her real smiles and a nod of approval as I left the stage, and I knew that she\u2019d liked it.<br /> <br /> After the show (and the obligatory post-show mingling) I ambled over to D\u2019s table and planted myself firmly in her lap\u2026 making sure to keep my wings out of her face this time. Julia was there, of course, and Monica and Haley and Joan were sharing the table as well. Joan was obviously uncomfortable with all the females-only affection being thrown around, and kept trying to bring the conversation back to Dark Kimberly\u2019s predicament. I got so engrossed in the conversation (and the company) that I didn\u2019t even notice when Chalcedony and Ginny left together.<br /> <br /> Calamity noticed, and it turned out to be a good thing that she did. It\u2019s no secret that Ginny\u2019s had a crush on Chalcedony for a while, and that Chalcedony has been reluctant to return her affections. Since she seemed to have changed her mind, Ginny jumped at the opportunity to get closer to her would-be paramour. Only it <u>wasn\u2019t</u> Chalcedony\u2026 it was one of the Director\u2019s extras wearing her shape. Calamity spotted the deception before things got tragic, followed the two of them out of the House, and dealt with the extra as only Calamity can.<br /> <br /> Ginny was understandably upset by this development. She called to check on the real Chalcedony (who once again asserted her belief that Desiree must be behind this whole mess) and then accompanied Calamity back to the Dream House. Calamity made a few calls and then spoke to Joan in private for a few minutes. When the two of them returned to the table, Joan seemed convinced that Ginny was not a Loyalist. I don\u2019t know what Calamity said to her, but I\u2019m glad she said it.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m sort of ashamed to say it, but a lot of subtle (and not-so-subtle) teasing of Joan followed. Most of us were pretty high on life at that point, I think, and the endorphins were flowing either from combat, near-death-experiences, stage highs, or various other exciting goings-on, and the innuendo and double-entendres were flowing fast and thick. Joan, who kept trying to bring us back to the point, eventually decided that it was a bad time to pursue her investigation, and got up to leave.<br /> <br /> We all apologized and tried to get her to stay\u2026 and, you know, to maybe loosen up a little. She didn\u2019t really respond to our efforts at first, but then she got this <u>look</u> in her eye and started talking about justice and righteousness, and\u2026<br /> <br /> It was <u>amazing</u>. I\u2019ve never seen her like that. She went on for a few minutes, and had this passion in her voice. Her words weren\u2019t clipped or measured; they flowed out in an endless stream that seemed to come straight from her soul. I wish I could remember what she said, and exactly how she said it, because it was <u>beautiful</u>.<br /> <br /> \u201cJoan,\u201d I said quietly when she finished, \u201cthat was <u>poetry.</u>\u201d The others agreed with me.<br /> <br /> She got really flustered, mumbled a few excuses, and almost ran out the front door, pulling Monica with her (our verdant friend was her ride). I felt bad for her\u2026 but I\u2019m glad I got to hear her speak from the heart. I feel like I understand her a little better now.<br /> <br /> \u201cWill she be okay?\u201d I turned to ask D quietly.<br /> <br /> D grinned. \u201cShe\u2019ll be fine in a few hours. Hell, it might even be good for her,\u201d she opined.<br /> <br /> I wanted nothing more than to lead D up to my bedroom at that moment and spend the whole night luxuriating in her presence, but unfortunately some of the others had a pretty good idea about how to follow up on Dark Kimberly\u2019s shooting. We\u2019re going to head over to the Rose and Thorn and see if Flores will let us take a look at the security footage from last night. We\u2019re not really expecting to find out anything about the shooter himself (or herself)\u2026 the cops would have already picked up on anything that obvious. But we might be able to tell if Desiree was really at the club last night or not, which would at least answer a few questions on that front.<br /> <br /> So I\u2019ve been writing in this journal while the others get ready to go. D is sitting across the table from me, pretending that she\u2019s not trying to read what I\u2019m writing about her. Now she\u2019s sticking out her tongue at me. Now she\u2019s making an obscene gesture. Now she\u2019s...<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T15:08:00-07:00","id":279110,"title":"","content":"<b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> <u><b><b><u>Sunday May 11<sup>th</sup></u></b> </b></u><br /> <br /> Has it really only been a little over twenty-four hours since my last entry? So much shit has gone down despite the fact that I managed to sleep through way too gorram many of those hours. Damn it has been a long fucking weekend and it's not over yet. Doesn't matter how badly I need to curl up in Gawain's arms and let him hold me. We've got to go look over hours of security footage and we've got to do it right fucking now before somebody goes off the deep end and we have one (or more) dead Changelings on our hands.<br /> <br /> Fuck. This is all coming out in a jumble. I need to sort this crap out and write it down in some sort of order. That will hopefully get my damn head back in the game. I do not have time to play fucking weepy and needful right now. I passed out and slept for nearly twelve hours earlier, I can fucking get this shit sorted before I indulge in any more slumber-time lollygagging. Besides, I do not really have the sanity to spare to deal with dreaming of Snow Globe again right now.<br /> <br /> Okay. Saturday night. Roller-coaster was on the upswing after my fucking breakdown in the bathroom. I dressed up pretty in that gown and I went down to use the dressing room to do my hair and face. It has much better makeup and lighting and a not broken mirror and Lori, who is so much better at being a girl than I am. I swear, that woman is the only thing that keeps me from looking like a clown school dropout.<br /> <br /> So, I was looking all sexy and hit the crowd with smiles up to my eyes. I made sure to greet the regulars and swing by the Changelings in the crowd. Ginny was sitting with Chalcedony. I offered up an apology for interrogating her out in the Hedge and warned her that Joan was suspicious of her. She wasn't able to speak freely about what she had been up to and I left it with an assurance that I was always willing to help out a fellow Autumn Courtier.<br /> <br /> Desiree was there as well and wanted to tell me that Chalcedony seemed familiar to her but she couldn't place where she knew her from. That meant it was most likely from her time with the Director. A troublesome situation if she really did see her there and assuming she's not laying or being mislead. I won't say I'm flawless, but the more I speak to that one the harder I find it to believe she's acting. I mean, I know that is what she does and what she was made for but she's either amazing or she believes her own innocence. Of course, there is the possibility that she doesn't know she's a loyalist, that it's some sort of programming or mind fuckery. Of course, that leads to doubting everyone and everything. But hell, you're not paranoid if they really are out to get you, right?<br /> <br /> And from that fun little she-said she-said I wound up at Madam Spidertoes table. I stopped by to greet her and all and she asked me to sit. There was something different about her demeanor toward me, like I'd been moved up to being a real person. That sounds catty but it's fairly accurate. The woman is ancient and powerful, it's not so much a stuck up thing as she just doesn't relate to most people anymore. We are no doubt as odd to her as she is to us and she just doesn't make the effort to 'get' us whippersnappers and our strange ways. But I am Annika's apprentice and if Annika sees value in me then there must be value in me. The woman clearly does not let her relationships ever just slip away. And the topic of her questions quickly reinforced that. She wanted to know about Lorelei and her relationship with De la Rocha. I was taken aback slightly and I took a moment to consider my reply. I adore Lori but I was sure that if I just laid it on that Madam would see through it. Plus I honestly do have pretty much nothing but good things to say about my motley mate. So I answered truthfully, that Lori has been a true friend to me and that she's shown real courage facing her own fears and putting her well-being second to our own in dangerous situations. On the surface, she might seem a little superficial but she is loyal and trustworthy and caring. Once I got to speaking, I did wax a bit adoringly but the truth is I do look up to Lori in many ways. She's got her issues like all of us but she's hands down the most well adjusted person in the Dream House. Madam Spidertoes remained as inscrutable as ever but I think I managed to convince her that Lori was good for De la Rocha. I don't think she was jealous but that she simply continues to feel some instinct to look after her former lover.<br /> <br /> After I wound down and Madam Spidertoes finished asking her questions, we settled comfortably into a little small talk. For once, there was not the usual sense of dismissal but I did excuse myself to continue circulating after a bit. I know that this shift is entirely based on Annika. Now, I am sure that my teacher wouldn't be investing time in me if she didn't believe it was worthwhile so I suppose in that regard I could claim it's based on my own merits but that would be a lie. Still, whatever the reason, Madam Spidertoes is one of the most powerful beings in the area and being on her good side is a good thing. I should make damn sure to stay there if I can.<br /> <br /> The show, of course, was amazing. Gawain carried out his escapade with Captain Jack and it went off beautifully. The crowd loved it. Captain Jack is a consummate showman. Gawain may not have the training but he was so clearly having the time of his life up there. Even as fucked up as things went later and as much shit as we're wading through currently I can't help but smile thinking back on it.<br /> <br /> And yeah, it was after the show that the solid waste hit the rotational air circulation device. We were sitting around having a few drinks. Gawain was retelling his favorite parts of the show, which was pretty much all of it to be honest but I for one didn't care. I was sipping some coffee and enjoying listening to Gawain bask before heading to the Lighthouse to hit the library.<br /> <br /> And then Gawain got a text from Captain Jack. He'd gone to the Rose and Thorn after being 'thrown out' of the Dream House. He said Gawain needed to come at once and bring me with him. The rest of the motley would be good as well. It was a mood killer to be sure. We piled into the van and made sure we had some light weapons at hand. I mean, there aren't a whole lot of reasons to call for me and almost all of them involve my knack for stabbing things. I wish to fucking hell that it had been something that simple.<br /> <br /> We got there and the whole place was covered in cops and EMT s. My throat got tight and I felt sick. This was the aftermath of something bad. Gawain called the Captain and he directed us to a side door. I was on the fucking edge as he let us in and took us to an office. I didn't think that bombastic ogre could manage to look grim but he was. Then he told us that someone had shot Dark Kimberly.<br /> <br /> I had to lock down hard. I know my fists were clenched tight enough to reopen the cuts on my hands and I welcomed that trickle of pain. Lucian was there and doing cop deflection duty as well as spearheading the investigation. Dark Kimberly was alive and surprisingly well but we couldn't use any Contracts until we'd gotten her away from the mundane medicos. I focused on the details as Lucian shared them with us. He was all business which I greatly appreciated. Captain Jack did what he could to try to make sure I was alright but I wasn't and there was nothing to be done about it. I do have to say that having seen him in that light my opinion of him is even higher. He was calm and focused on what needed to be done. The kind of man you want in your corner in a crisis.<br /> <br /> The details did not make anything better. Someone just walked up to Dark Kimberly and drew a small caliber pistol and fired a single shot from approximately three feet away. Lucian saw a Glock, which fits the wound but given the confusion there is no certainty that what he saw was the real weapon. Because Lucian saw a Chinese man fire the shot. Dark Kimberly saw a Latina woman. That prompted some concern that the mask was an attempt to create racial tensions between those two groups in the club but Davey saw a Caucasian female. Apparently, nearly everyone saw the shooting but no one saw the same assailant. The only consistent trait in all descriptions was that it was a human with no seeming or obvious supernatural characteristics.<br /> <br /> Lucian and I both had reached the same conclusion about one thing. At that range even an inexperienced shooter should have been able to hit a more vital location or would have fired a second shot to finish the job. If they had wanted her dead, she would have been or at the least would have been far more seriously wounded. But why wound her? And why in such a public location? Clearly great effort had been made to protect the identity of the shooter rather than wait for a more intimate moment. So the objective was not to kill and it was meant to be seen by a full crowd of humans and Changelings. All of that points to Kimberly being a target of convince. The real target was the Rose and Thorn.<br /> <br /> Of course, that helps exactly fuck all not. The shooter knew where the cameras were and avoided them, so he, she, or it was familiar with the club's layout. There hadn't been any sort of violent activity of a similar nature in this area. Another club had been burned down about a decade prior after hours and claimed the owner and five unidentified bodies. Lucian didn't think it was related and we were inclined to agree. Though without much else resembling a lead it was as worth looking into as anything else. He did also mention that Molly Nuit was present before the shooting but not after, though he wasn't watching her closely and didn't know if she'd left just before or disappeared in the chaos.<br /> <br /> Around that time, Dark Kimberly was escorted back to see us at last. She confirmed what we knew and assured us she was fine. She made a show of being more upset about her dress than the wound. Everyone did their best to be comforting and supportive. Lori wasted no time healing her.<br /> <br /> I didn't say anything right away. It was easy enough to let the others speak first and to not crowd her. I just kept looking at her. She was hurting. She was scared. When I did step forward I reached and I took her hand. I swore that I would find the person that had done this and I would kill them. It wasn't what she needed or wanted to hear, not really. Not that she didn't desire vengeance but it was no comfort in that moment. But truth be told, it was as much for me as it was for her.<br /> <br /> I was furious inside. The glass was itching in my fingers. Some other monster had hunted my prey. No, I hadn't savored her pain the night before, but that had been by choice. It had been MINE to claim. I had chosen instead to protect her and to see her wounded so soon, to know that she could have been killed just as easily... I had failed. All that remained was to hunt this other monster down and to end them. To show all the others what happened to any who dared to bring harm to someone under my protection.<br /> <br /> I will keep my promise. I will see her assailant cold and stony dead. And if I have any say in it, it will be a very slow and excruciating death.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, this lead to a conflict. The only lead we had to follow up on was whatever power had allowed the assailant to be disguised. As the only member of the Autumn court available, I needed to go to the library and see if I could discover what it might be. But I needed to be sure Kimberly made it home and was protected. It was Captain Jack that solved my dilemma. He offered to see her safely home, going so far as to make a vow to me. I am indebted to him.<br /> <br /> Gawain and Jacob joined me in the library. I was still seething but I kept it inside, consumed that fury to keep me focused. We were able to find what we needed. There is a goblin contract that grants exactly the effect witnessed. It wasn't much but it felt good to have a fucking break. And the price of the contract was fairly steep. Once you have finished carrying out your task, you forget who you are completely and what you've done until you sleep. And then after waking, you cannot recall anything that happened during that period of forgetfulness. I promptly shared my find with the motley and Lucian but as it had been hours since the crime and it was the wee hours of the morning so it wasn't as helpful as it might have been to track down the contract user.<br /> <br /> Lucian suggested that Jacob should check on Molly Nuit since he is a member of the Winter Court and not in the midst of a feud with their leader and thus considerably less likely to end up with a razor blade in his urethra if he showed up at their clinic. I agreed and made the suggestion to Jacob. He decided it was sound and needed to be done sooner rather than later on the off chance that she did it and hadn't slept yet. As it turns out, she had simply picked a very fortunate (if inadvertently suspicious) time to leave. Bonus fact, Doctor Bright is apparently handy with a shotgun and a bit cavalier about using one as a skeleton key.<br /> <br /> Once Jacob set off, Gawain seemed ready to take me home. I should have let him. I was well past even my reserves and starting to feel a thickheadedness that not even the rage and guilt could burn through. But I just couldn't stop. I had nothing to pursue for finding Kimberly's shooter but I needed to do something, anything really. Stopping would have meant thinking and there was nothing I wanted to think about right about then. Gawain saw my hesitation and asked if I needed him to let me work alone for court business. I told him yes. I mean, technically any business in the library is Autumn Court business. Looking up Snow Globe or the Violet Empress or seeing what I could dig up on that brand of Jacob's fall under personal use and not really the sort of things that they'd be keen on having an outsider involved in. I also could see Gawain was in need of rest, though I should have known better than expect him to not try to wait up for me. I'm told he spent the whole fucking morning asleep in my office chair waiting for me to get home and when I didn't show up he freaked. Dammit, I knew better but I was being stubborn and selfish again.<br /> <br /> Once I'd sent Gawain home alone like a cold-hearted bitch, Dionysia approached me. She was the only other person in the library at that point (Hardly surprising as it was past 3 am) and she asked me if there was anything she could help me with. I asked her if she knew anything about Snow Globe. I was trying to distract myself and accomplishing something useful while I was at it seemed like a good idea. She admitted that she really only know that it was where I'd been and what (very) little I'd shared. She pointed out that it wasn't one of the durances that seemed to connect with this area, which isn't really a surprise I guess. I mean, we escaped the Hedge in Washington state and I was taken from the same vicinity. She then offered to help me investigate it, though not right then. I thanked her and she left.<br /> <br /> That's about the point where I finally just crashed and fell out. Shouldn't have come as a fucking surprise. I hadn't slept since Thursday night/Friday morning. When I came too again, I was in an unfamiliar room of the lighthouse and there was sunlight outside. The bed was looking rough as was my gown. It was never meant for sleeping in. I found a bag of biscuits and orange juice and a note from Tommy that he'd moved me. I also had a very worried voice-mail from Gawain. Fucking embarrassing all around. I called and learned that the fucking merry-go-fuck-round hadn't skipped a beat while I was tossing and turning and dreaming of things better left undreamed about and being totally AWOL. Thankfully, Gawain had brought my bike to the Lighthouse so I did have a way to get back to the Dream House.<br /> <br /> They were out helping Mary, a Spring Courtier that Lori apparently found wandering naked at the springs when she tried to go check on the Princess and make sure she was up to date on the whole kit and clusterfuck going on. I took the occasion to change out of that gown at last and get a good hot shower. I hope I haven't completely ruined it, I kinda like that dress. But around the time I was presentable again they returned.<br /> <br /> They caught me up on what I had missed, which apparently involved quite a bit of drama at Glamor Springs and raised a fresh crop of damned questions and not a single fucking answer. Apparently Mary's story (or more specifically her lack of a story) doesn't really make sense. She was hot tubing with Davey and Kimberly and drinking (which she apparently recalls and doesn't do often so there is an explanation for the lack of clear memory). Before they left, they moved her to the resting room, still in her bathing suit and they put her clothes on a shelf by the cot. So how exactly did she wind up naked and unable to locate her clothing? Davey was rightly suspicious and so Insincere Marguerite went ahead of them to Mary's apartment to slip inside and check the place out before they took her home. The bed was still warm from being slept in and there was a large handgun with what my sister believes to be armor piercing ammunition. All very peculiar. That is some serious shit, I'd love to know where she got her hands on anything that heavy in this state. That kind of firepower is not civilian legal in any way shape or form. But at the same time, it's definitely not the weapon that was used on Kimberly. So who stole her clothes (and presumably her keys) from Glamor Springs so they could break in and sleep in her bed? That's just... weird. And it's not some fucked up amnesia or schizo trip because she was here last night and with them at the Springs so she couldn't have been the one sleeping in her bed. I wonder if anyone thought to ask her about her fetch? Whatever is going on there, it doesn't seem related to Kimberly's shooting or the gorram missing Table or anything else we're trying to sort out.<br /> <br /> The other excitement came from Chalcedony and Desiree. They apparently got into it and where almost at blows when the motley found them. The gist of it was that Chalcedony claims to have seen Desiree at the Rose and Thorn last night and Desiree insists that she went home after leaving the Dream House. In the aftermath, Desiree shared her suspicious deja-vu feeling about Chalcedony with the others and Chalcedony confided in Jacob that she specifically followed Desiree because she doesn't trust her and saw her go into the Rose and Thorn but then vanish into the crowd. Neither of them seemed to be lying which means, yet again, either someone is really, really good at it or there is some gorram mind fuckery going on and they're both telling the truth as far as they know.<br /> <br /> I could see Gawain was worried and as soon as the updating was finished he pulled me aside. He'd found the broken mirror and he was understandably concerned. I looked down at my hands and he followed suit, seeing the fresh cuts there. I think mumbled something about having a disagreement with my reflection but that I was okay now. I told him it had been a long fucking weekend and that I was just really really weary. He wrapped me in those solid strong arms and held me close. I just melted into him with unabashed needfulness and rested my head against his metal chest. I'd already wallowed in self pity way too fucking much and there was no time for any more selfish indulgence but I just couldn't help myself. He asked me if we could sleep here tonight and I nodded and told him yes. I think he needs it and Zod knows I do.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite came over and leaned in as I was lingering in Gawain's embrace. She searched my eyes openly and asked me if I was alright as well. I feel guilty for making her worry as well but it's sweet that she does and as weak and selfish as it is, I needed it. I managed a tired smile and assured her I would be. I told her I was weary, that it had just been a rough couple of days. Without thinking about it, I reached out and stroked her hair and she just kinda leaned into and let me pet her for a few minutes. It was certainly a bit more intimate than normal for us but it was really nice to just have that physical connection.<br /> <br /> But there was still a show that had to go on and for that to happen we had to get ready for it. Getting properly dressed and making myself up was oddly calming. By the time I came out to greet the early arrivals I was much more focused and had my inner demons tucked securely back in their cages. De la Rocha and julia already had a table and soon Monica and Haley arrived with Joan and joined them. Once the doors closed, Gawain joined them. Joan had come to speak with us about the shooting and she kept bringing it up at the table. And Monica kept trying to change the subject and avoid watching any of the steadily growing number of women openly displaying affection around her.<br /> <br /> I spent a while being gracious and charming to all of them (even Haley) and then moved to meet and greet the rest of the guests. Jacob was working the floor as well and things were going smoothly. Ginny was there and seated alone, so I joined her for a bit. Able to speak freely, she apologized for not being able to tell me sooner and explained that she'd been in the Hedge on orders from Queen Charlotte, investigating the location of a dead drop and watching to see who showed up at it. Which is where she encountered Desiree before being attacked by the Extras. I offered to coach her a bit in delivering a more convincing cover story. Then the conversation drifted to Desiree. It seems that Ginny is quite smitten with Chalcedony, who has not yet been entirely reciprocal. So, having heard about the altercation at Glamor Springs and seeing how upset Chalcedony was she did begin to wax a bit about drowning Desiree. I smiled and assured her that I knew the feeling well. We spoke a bit about stabbing and drowning and our respective talent with and enjoyment of such things. But I did also point out that while I did believe that Chalcedony was telling the truth as far as she knew it we were dealing with deceptions and illusions and thus had to be careful not to act without being sure. I then assured her that if we did find proof against Desiree that I'd be right there with her for the kill and that seemed to calm her.<br /> <br /> The show itself was excellent, if I do say so myself. Lori sang a number from Les Meserables, apparently she's become quite a fan of it since learning of it's existence. And despite how little time she had to prepare, she nailed it like she'd been singing it for years. That woman's gift is simply amazing and despite what she might say, there is no way it's all because of what was done to her in Arcadia. And, perhaps to balance out the tragic, Ace did a Shatner-style performance of Rocket Man that involved the cloud dress and mirrors with prerecorded images that was spot on.<br /> <br /> I didn't catch most of the second act because Chalcedony arrived and made a beeline for Ginny. With hardly a word, Ginny was up and they were heading for the door. There was something about it all that was far too deliberate for my liking. I'll be honest, my first impulse was that Chalcedony had arrived to fetch Ginny and they were on their way to lynch a suspected loyalist without inviting me. I had to hurry across the room to intercept them before they left and the moment I did I knew something was seriously off. Chalcedony was acting very off kilter, flat and emotionless. And she was very intent on leaving with Ginny immediately while Ginny was just very intent on the object of her lust.<br /> <br /> I followed them outside discreetly as they headed to Ginny's car. I caught up in time to overhear Chalcedony tell Ginny they were going to her place and for the poor ogress to ask rather eagerly, \u201cWe're going to have sex, right?\u201d At this point, alarms were going off in my head. I may not know Chalcedony that well but she's never stuck me as the sort to use \u201cYou. Me. Fucking now.\u201d as a pickup line, especially not when just the night before she'd apparently been too busy playing detective to play footsie with Ginny. So I tailed them on my bike. They drove to what I'll charitably call a slum. No way in any of the nine hells someone as classy as Chalcedony lived in that rat infested shithole.<br /> <br /> They got out of the car and headed to the building. Ginny was oblivious to anything except the willowy blonde leading her into what could only be a trap. I started to follow. Then I saw Chalcedony's features melt away to reveal one of the Director's faceless extras drawing its saber arm back to impale an unsuspecting Ginny from behind. I broke into a run and let the glass slip through my skin. It was as blind to me as its victim was to it. I threw myself into the attack with a shriek and I tore into that faespawned abomination full bore. It was dead before it ever even knew what hit it. Without a doubt, that was the high point of this whole evening. No fucking ambiguity, just a threat that needed killing. And when Ginny turned and realized what had almost happened it was amazing. Not seeing her upset over how close she'd come to being assassinated of course, but knowing that I'd been in the right place at the right time to save her life. Tonight I was exactly the monster I wanted to be.<br /> <br /> I didn't have time to bask in my moment of triumph though. While the extra had seemed to be acting without any sort of backup I wanted to get Ginny out of there and back to safety as soon as possible just in case. She was freaked out, not only for herself but for the actual Chalcedony as well. She called her dancer while I called Gawain to give him a quick head's up. Then I grabbed the remains and ushered Ginny back to her car so we could get the hell out of there.<br /> <br /> The show had ended and the mundane crowd had departed by the time we returned to the Dream House, so we were free to speak freely. I handed Ginny over to the others and stepped aside to make a quick call. Thankfully, I was able to reach Queen Charlotte directly. I explained what had happened and then brought up that Joan was highly suspicious of Ginny after we'd found her in the Hedge. I told her Ginny had explained about it being court business to me privately and asked if it would be acceptable to share that much with Joan to dissuade her from hounding the poor woman. My monarch was reluctant to risk revealing Ginny as one of her agents but did agree that leaving Joan convinced that Ginny was a loyalist would be worse. She also enlightened me with more of the details. She had been rather surprised to learn that Desiree had been the one to show up. Apparently she had been expecting Chalcedony. I quickly pointed out that Ginny was anything but objective with regard to the blue girl. I also raised that point that the sheer volume of circumstantial evidence against Desiree is almost too solid. The Queen agreed that it did seem almost too pat.<br /> <br /> Well, with the royal go ahead to tell Joan and the Motley that Ginny was on court business I took her aside next and did pretty much exactly that. My word that Ginny had lied about why she was in the Hedge because she did not want to reveal that she'd been on an errand for the Autumn Court satisfied Joan. We then exchanged notes on our investigations into the shooting. I mentioned the possibility that Desiree was there and involved (which to Joan automatically meant that the Director was somehow involved.) Apparently she'd been looking at motives for attacking Dark Kimberly rather than the club. Which did get a little tense when she called the girl a strumpet. I shouldn't have reacted so strongly but after everything else it was all I could do to catch myself and keep my razors in check. Hell, I understand that she meant it as more of an observation than a judgment but that woman needs to learn some tact. She was clearly upset that she'd made me angry and we got past it and finished our discussion. Knowing what I do about her time in Arcadia I do understand why she's the way she is but that does not make it any easier to deal with her and I actually <i>like</i> the woman. I guess that's why I suggested that we should spar sometime. The poor thing desperately needs some friends and to learn to relax. And since I know Gawain likes her as well I brought up having him join us. I swear the first double entente wasn't intentional. But Joan's total deadpan and lack of grasp of innuendo ended up being too hard to resist. I shouldn't have continued, but fuck, I think we all needed some release and watching Gawain get steadily more and more embarrassed was just too damn adorable.<br /> <br /> Once we all had the giggles Joan decided it was time to leave. We tried to explain that it had just been tense and hectic but then suddenly Joan let loose with a truly inspiring speech. I think we were all a bit shocked at how eloquent she was. Lori and Ace started to compliment her and even suggest that she should consider speaking as part of a show. That proved to be a bit of bad idea. I have never witnessed stage phobia before but fright just does not do justice to the intensity of Joan's reaction. Jacob got her a paper bag to breathe into to keep her from hyperventilating and Monica took her home.<br /> <br /> At that point I think we were all beyond ready to be done. But Jacob shared some of what Chalcedony had said about going after Desiree for trying to kill Ginny. And it was brought up that we still had the security footage from the Rose and Thorn waiting to be examined and that delaying wasn't a good idea considering how volatile the whole situation was getting. No one looked pleased. Hell, Insincere Marguerite looked ready to throttle someone. Lady knows all I want to do is curl up with Gawain and try to forget that there's anything beyond the circle of his arms but it seems there's no rest for the wicked yet. Instead I am taking a few moments to write this all down and sort my head out before we head over to the Rose and Thorn.<br /> <br /> Of course, now that I think about it, Chalcedony certainly has been pressing to do something RIGHT FUCKING NOW about Desiree. I mean, Joan may have dropped in for a midnight chat about how she was going to kill the woman as soon as she has proof and she has no doubt whatsoever about her guilt but she's still waiting for something concrete. Damn, if Chalcedony turns out to be the actual loyalist it will tear poor Ginny apart. But if Chalcedony was the one that should have been at the drop and she got wind of the observation she might have set Desiree up and she'd know the perfect way to get rid of Ginny. I mean, who else would know she's infatuated enough with Chalcedony to follow one of those things without question if looks like her? Fucking fuckity fuck. I wish I had thought of this sooner. I was too worried that Chalcedony might do something reckless that I told Jacob to distract her by convincing her to look in on Ginny. I better make sure he knows to watch Chalcedony. Dammit, I fucking hate all of this fumbling around without a clue and jumping at shadows.<br /> <br /> Well, if Chalcedony is a loyalist she's been pretty careful about her cover. And if something were to happen to Ginny while she's there it would be mighty fucking suspect. So unless she's prepared to ditch subtlety she's going to wait for another opportunity and try to make sure to frame Desiree for it. Of course, she might also be innocent and Desiree might be the loyalist everyone thinks she is after all. Hell maybe they're BOTH fucking innocent and it's someone laughing their gorram ass off watching us chase our tails and turn on each other.<br /> <br /> I know it's way too much to hope for but maybe, just maybe, there will be something in the Rose and Thorn's security footage. Hell, even if we can't identify the shooter it should tell us if Desiree was there last night or not. Or... fucking hell... Even if we do <i>see</i> Desiree on the footage what will that really prove at this point? I am so fucking weary of chasing shadows but I made a promise to Dark Kimberly. I <i>will</i> find the miserable little fuck that shot her and I <i>will</i> end them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> And the days just keep getting interesting. Not really sure how to begin this one. So many ideas and theories have been going back and forth. I can see why Joan is so paranoid. I guess I\u2019ll start at the beginning. The day almost started like any other. I got to the kitchen and started making my usual pot of coffee, but Gawain didn\u2019t come in. Lorelei was already there and had apparently decided that since our usual chef wasn\u2019t available she\u2019d make breakfast for the lot of us instead. I think she said something about doing her part. I just did my usual and handed over eggs and any ingredients that she needed but hadn\u2019t already gotten out. She makes good eggs.<br /> <br /> Eventually Gawain did come in. Apparently he had fallen asleep in the office and the smell of coffee and cooking eggs woke him up. He stumbled in looking sore and a bit out of sorts. Looked like he slept through the night. No overly dark shadows under his eyes, he just looked \u201csleeping in a chair is not good for my back\u201d sore. He asked if either of us had seen Calamity yet this morning. I confessed that I had not, Lorelei also answered in the negative. Gawain got worried at that and asked if I could come with him to the archives to look for Calamity. It was possible that she was still there, but in case she had left Gawain said he wanted me there to track her if it came to it. I said sure and poured a travel mug of coffee for Gawain as he got his keys.<br /> <br /> We got to the archives with no problems and met a young changeling named Moon. Ze didn\u2019t know where Calamity was but let us follow hir to go look. Yeah, been awhile since I used gender neutral pronouns. Had a friend in high school that didn\u2019t conform to either gender. Got some flak for it, but ze was a good friend and the other kids were just assholes. That feels like such a long time ago. I wonder if the little shit (aka my fetch) kept up a friendship with Jo or not? For me it\u2019s been\u2026 20-something years? I\u2019m guessing. No calendars in the Lady\u2019s realm. But here it\u2019s only been 2 years. I may have to look hir up to see how ze\u2019s doing. Anyhoo\u2026Moon reminded me of Jo, hence the pronouns. So, ze led us further into the library and we found a note from Tommy, Calamity\u2019s friend, saying that she had fallen asleep and was resting in a guest room. Relieved, we left. I think Gawain sent a text to Calamity to let her know that we\u2019d been by. We thanked Moon for hir help and went on our way.<br /> <br /> Back at the house there was discussion about different acts. Ace wanted to do something with tarantulas dangling from the ceiling, or something like that. We talked him out of it. He decided to go with William Shatner\u2019s version of Rocket Man. I had not seen it, so looked it up on You Tube. Very strange. Insincere Marguerite helped him pre-record some of the extra parts to play during the actual performance. Lorelei talked about doing one of the sad songs from Les Miserables. But apparently not the <i>really</i> sad one. In the day or so since I told her about the musical she\u2019s already gotten the soundtrack and a t-shirt. I had to smile at that. We also talked about putting some kind of symbol on the flyers for each show letting the changeling community know which court\u2019s emotion, if any, we were going to focus on for that night. Tonight\u2019s show was obviously going to focus on sorrow.<br /> <br /> After that is when things got interesting. Mary, the girl that Lorelei found at Glamour Springs told us that she\u2019d been drinking and had fallen asleep. She didn\u2019t remember details but figured she\u2019d fallen asleep in the water since that\u2019s where we found her. Later we talked to Davie and he said that when she had passed out she was put into the resting room on one of the benches. We checked out the club, looking for clothes and keys and anything else we could find. The bench was still damp as was the restroom floor. This backed up the theory of her being laid on the bench and maybe going to the ladies room later. Her clothes and other stuff had been put in the room with her, but were not there now. So, either someone else stole her clothes and moved her to the pool, or she did something with her own clothes and got in the pool herself but conveniently forgot what she did. Like I said, interesting things going on. Lots of theories.<br /> <br /> Anyhoo\u2026before talking to Davie. The lot of us when to Glamour Springs with Lorelei. When we got there we discovered Chalcedony and Desiree arguing, and from the looks of it about to get into a fight. Lorelei intervened and tried to get the two ladies to stop fighting. Chalcedony insisted that she knew that Desiree was involved in what happened to Kimberly. Desiree pled innocent and said that she had gone home after having been at the Dream House. After that Chalcedony stormed out and I followed her. I figured the others could take care of Desiree, but someone should make sure that Chalcedony was alright. I guess I wasn\u2019t sure if she just needed help or if I might need to talk her down from doing something rash. I tried to let her know that I was on her side without flat out saying that. Don\u2019t want to make a liar out of myself now do I? Ha. Anyhoo\u2026Chalcedony was upset and insisted that she had actually followed Desiree to the club and saw the other girl disappear as soon as she entered the building. She had been suspicious the whole time, and this just confirmed it for her. I told her that I would help her, but that we needed proof if we were going to come forward with this accusation. She said that she needed some time alone to clear her head and look for clues, but that she\u2019d call me later if she found anything.<br /> <br /> I will note that when we arrived and found the two girls arguing it looked for all intents and purposes that each person was angry at the other, but if you really looked you could see that Chalcedony was saying angry words but the emotions, or lack thereof, going across her face told a different tale. It didn\u2019t last long, but it made me wonder. Was she being influenced? Was she acting and took a moment to \u2018get into character?\u2019 Was she something else entirely pretending to be her?<br /> <br /> After she left I went back into the club to see how the others were faring. Apparently Gawain had stayed with Desiree to make sure that she was okay. Soon after she left and the rest of us got to talk. I at least told Gawain what Chalcedony had told me about seeing Desiree going into the club. After all the drama was done we did our little investigation into Mary and her disappearing clothes. At this point she had no keys, no clothes and no phone. She was wearing borrowed clothes from Lorelei, but needed to be able to get back into her apartment. We offered her our services, but said that Marguerite would need to go home and get some tools first. Insincere Marguerite left before us and headed straight for Mary\u2019s apartment. She didn\u2019t actually need tools to let herself in, and did just that. She told us later that she found that Mary\u2019s bed had been slept in that night, and was actually still a bit warm. There was also a semi-auto pistol in the bedroom that looked to be loaded with armor piercing rounds. This was not the kind of bullet that Kimberly was shot with, but still suspicious.<br /> <br /> The rest of us arrived after Insincere Marguerite had let us know what she\u2019d found. Marguerite made a show of letting Mary into her apartment and we left her to get dressed in her own clothes and get cleaned up. We headed back to the Dream House by way of a \u201cJack in the Box\u201d for take-out. When we got home Calamity talked to Ginny about what\u2019s been going on and the many theories. Desiree could be involved in the shooting and just not remember it because of that goblin contract, or Chalcedony might have just seen someone that looked like Desiree but actually wasn\u2019t. Definite innocence of pretty much everyone involved was going right out the window after we\u2019d all talked.<br /> <br /> This whole situation is just getting messed up. After dinner we got ready for the show, which was great as always. Lorelei did a song from Les Miserables, which had the audience\u2019s rapt attention. Ace did his \u201cRocket Man\u201d number, which was interesting to say the least. And at some point during the night Chalcedony came in and talked to Ginny, then the pair of them left. Calamity, who was nearby, thought something was off about the way the former girl was acting so she followed them. Calamity texted Gawain to let him know what she was up to, then she followed the pair to a rundown apartment complex. On the way to a room Chalcedony, or the being that looked like her, changed shape mid-stride into an \u201cextra\u201d with a blade arm and aimed a killing blow at Ginny\u2019s undefended back. Calamity, who\u2019d been shadowing the pair, jumped out and took out the extra in one swing. After they calmed down, Calamity called Gawain to let him know what had happened and Ginny called the real Chalcedony to make sure that she was okay. She was. Chalcedony then texted me to let me know that Desiree had sent an \u201cextra\u201d after Ginny. I guess that answers the question as to whether or not I gave my phone number to the real Chalcedony or a fake one earlier.<br /> <br /> When Calamity got back to the Dream House, and most of the others had gone home the rest of us talked. Joan was there too. We figured she should be in on this conversation. So, we mentioned to her that Chalcedony had \u201cseen\u201d Desiree walking to the Rose and Thorn and then disappearing once she got inside. At first it seemed like this was proof that she had at least gone to the club, but after having witnessed an \u201cextra\u201d mimicking one of the freehold, it calls a great many things into question. The idea that the Director\u2019s \u201cextras\u201d had impersonated others in the area led to some disturbing thoughts. What if he had them wear someone else\u2019s form and do things that would bring doubts on their loyalties? What if the reason that just about all of the Changelings that escape from the Director seem to be loyalists is because those that are not loyal are being framed by their former keeper. Even Joan looked a little upset about that idea.<br /> <br /> After everything that\u2019s happened over the past couple of days I\u2019m just not sure what I believe any more. Both Chalcedony and Desiree have been acting suspicious in one way or another. Both suspect the other, and both have circumstantial evidence that the other is lying and is up to no good. One thing that did get cleared up though, was the reason that Ginny was in the hedge on court business when we found her there being chased by briar wolves. That, I\u2019ll admit, was a bit of a relief. Her excuse really didn\u2019t sound all that believable the other day, which makes sense now, since it had been a lie.<br /> <br /> Ah\u2026looks like Calamity and the others are ready to go. We\u2019re going to go back to the Rose and Thorn and take a look at the security footage and see if we can find any answers or if we just find more questions. I\u2019m assuming it\u2019ll just be a waste of time, or create more questions, more things to look into, but maybe, just maybe we\u2019ll get lucky.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> Bah. This has been a frustrating day. Mostly.<br /> <br /> It began well. I woke when Lorelei began moving under me, and got up to go visit the house of her god, or more correctly visit her father. I suggested she return after, and dozed anticipating having some one on one passions with her. Happily.<br /> <br /> This was not to be. She made breakfast, and set about getting busy for the day. It was a snub, no question. I dressed nice for her, for certain definitions of nice, but she wanted to prove her independence, basically. Fine. It will just make her eventual surrender that much more satisfying. Unfortunately, this meant I was in the mood all day, not languid, and that made me crabby. Julia, at least, cares enough about my needs to try to keep me happy. I had, I suppose, thought better of Lorelei, that she would prefer pleasure and happiness to games. I overestimated her. Apparently.<br /> <br /> I did not pursue Jacob, as sex with him is dangerous for a bit longer yet, and given my hormones today, I suspect today would have been a really, really bad day for a tumble with him. Definitely.<br /> <br /> <br /> That night Julia and De La Rocha came, together of course, and both paid me some of the attention I needed. I quickly saw that Julia would be happy to be bedded, and I indicated rather clearly that it would be happening. I think she was intrigued by my\u2026interest in carnality. Mostly. I usually prefer the sublime approach, but this was not the day for it. Apparently.<br /> <br /> I am not, however, writing this crisscrossing her sleeping form. Reality prods at our private lives, and there is sadly more to life than chasing skirts and planning shows.<br /> <br /> The original issue was Calamity was missing, in the morning, but that was thankfully resolved in a safe manner. She had fallen asleep it turned out and Tommy secured her sleeping form somewhere in the Lighthouse. No problems there. Hopefully.<br /> <br /> The next issue was Mary. Evidently. She had stayed over, and still lacked her personal effects. We went to Glamour Springs but her clothes did not turn up, though there was evidence she slept somewhere besides where she woke up. I offered to get her into her apartment, and Ace concocted the idea that we should send me to it earlier so I could search it. I suggested I needed lockpicks, then went and acquired a black Volvo and drove straight there.<br /> <br /> The search revealed her bed had been slept in, and she has a heavy pistol (not sure what kind, I am not American) as well as what I think were armor piercing bullets (not positive, again not American, who I believe get their first gun when they are six). Nothing else unusual. I went back out, and feigned breaking in when they arrived. We then left. Quickly.<br /> <br /> Maybe it is at five. Probably.<br /> <br /> While we would like to investigate further, other things came up. While at Glamour Springs helping Mary, we saw Desiree and Chalcedony on the cusp of a fight. Apparently Chalcedony followed, or claims she followed, Desiree from the Dream House to the Rose &amp; Thorn, and saw her vanish into the crowd. Apparently. She was enraged when Desiree denied it. I am not sure what she was expecting. We decided to check the outdoor footage at Rose and Thorn, which is where we are about to be on the way too and why Julia can still form whole sentences. Sadly.<br /> <br /> Then tonight one of the Director\u2019s Extras tried to murder Ginny Green. She came in appearing as an apparently unconvincing version of Chalcedony and lead Ginny to a slum to kill her. Fortunately, Calamity followed, and killed the Extra before it could strike. Fortunately.<br /> <br /> This leaves us with a number of troubling questions. Why was Ginny attacked? Was it over the meeting in the Hedge with ourselves in Desiree? How does this relate to the shooting of Dark Kimberly? Does it? Did Desiree shoot Kimberly? Why? What does any of this have to do with Mary? What was she doing? Is Chalcedony framing her? Framing Desiree? A Victim?<br /> <br /> Bah. I should be under covers giggling my heart out with Julia, but now I must go to Rose &amp; Thorn, which is not even open. I am not a happy grub. Not at all.<br /> <br /> I miss Paris.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XIV</i><br /> <br /> As I say, the plot thickens, who to trust? Not much extra to note, Insincere Marguerite did not need lockpicks as that is part of her birthright as a Lurker. The Extras are hedge beasts working for the Director. Not many other rules permutations. Lots of paranoia this session, as they were left wondering about a lot of people.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, if you enjoy such games of paranoia, I have begun a Demon: the Descent game, Night Train Detective Agency, which can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\">here</a>. Feel free to check it out. Along with this and Balance of Shadows, it makes for a trio of New WoD games taking place in roughly the same world, and same as my old Brand New Key Geist game or Beyond the Sea Changeling game. Session 1 just went up, so it is easy to start on the ground floor.<br /> <br /> Anyway, more excitement next time. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T14:08:02-07:00","id":293178,"title":"","content":"New session, things get less murky. Not much less, but less. Ace\u2019s player was unable to make the session.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> I better never, ever forget Calamity, and if we have, and me from the future is reading this - you find her. Find her, go to her, bring her back, whatever you have to do, wherever you have to go. If she\u2019s not there anymore, we\u2019re missing something, something important, and however difficult it may be, it\u2019s worth it. And be sure to save some of whoever stole her away for her to stab.<br /> <br /> But I\u2019m getting all ahead of things. Last night was exciting, for the ladies at least. They got to look over the video footage at the Rose and Thorn and then go save Mary from a burning building. Jacob hung out at the Dream House with Ginny and Chalcedony, keeping watch over them and making sure Chalcedony didn\u2019t do anything stupid, you know? I headed over to Desiree\u2019s, to do the same for her. I didn\u2019t like leaving Calamity - I didn\u2019t want to do anything but hold her close until we both were feeling better - but the Director kept dictating the moves in this game, and whether I ended up protecting her from an attack, keeping her from going after someone else, or just served as an alibi for her, it seemed like we needed to do something preemptive, you know? I did make sure to get Calamity to promise to give me a call as soon as they were done. I didn\u2019t want to miss out on spending the night with her.<br /> <br /> My bit of it was mostly just awkward small talk until I got that call. I did get to check out Desiree\u2019s apartment, which is a nice place, if you can ignore all the manikins everywhere. She caught me looking at them, like, a lot, and explained that it was cause she didn\u2019t like being alone, but didn\u2019t want to have a whole bunch of people just hanging around all the time, you know? That made sense, kinda, so I was feeling better until I was having a look around when she stepped away, and found the circle of manikins, surrounding and staring down at her bed. That... made things a little creepy again. She did have this really pretty picture of her in front of a kinda spooky house, standing near the mailbox. She was, well, naked, which, you know, helped with the pretty. I kinda wonder who did it? It was of her seeming, so it was probably another Changeling, maybe before everyone got all paranoid about her. Anyway, there weren\u2019t any attacks or anything, so I headed out to let her get some sleep.<br /> <br /> There weren\u2019t anymore attacks on Ginny or on Chalcedony, so Jacob had a pretty calm evening too. He did get to pass along that Chalcedony hadn\u2019t been following Desiree to the Rose and Thorn, she had been following Molly Nuit, all dressed up like Desiree, and probably using a contract to look like her, you know? I guess the Winter Court doesn\u2019t like Chalcedony for some reason, or at least that\u2019s what Becky told Calamity, so maybe Molly was trying to lead Chalcedony to some kind of trap or something. She had dropped her disguise when Gunnar started following \u2018Desiree\u2019 around too, so that\u2019s why she seemed to disappear to Chalcedony. They were able to figure out, from the security footage, that Molly had in fact left just before the shooting, like maybe two minutes before, so maybe she knew it was going to happen? But like Lori said, it seems like if she knew, she\u2019d have left earlier to make it not so suspicious, you know? Maybe the shooter was just waiting for her to leave, for some reason.<br /> <br /> That was all from the ladies looking over the footage at the Rose and Thorn. Insincere Marguerite stayed awhile to go over the whole night, but Calamity and Lori left after not too long, cause Mary called, saying there was an intruder in her house. They headed right over and by the time they got there, Mary\u2019s apartment was on fire! Calamity, Lori and De la Roche were able to rescue her, and everyone else in her building, so that was good. Turns out though, it was her fetch who set the fire. She is fucking crazypants and tried to kill Mary as soon as she got back home that first time, from Arcadia, you know. This time, the fetch had wedged a chair against her door and everything, and used gasoline to set her kitchen on fire. She also left that gun Insincere Marguerite had found in her desk, so that if Mary didn\u2019t die, she\u2019d totally have gotten arrested for arson and whatever badness that gun was connected to. Calamity got the gun though, and erased the security tape that had a girl who looked just like Mary carrying gasoline up to her apartment.<br /> <br /> So, Mary\u2019s staying with us for a bit. Becky offered to take her in and find a place for her that was safe, but I think Calamity is hoping to draw her fetch here, so she can stab it. It makes sense to me - this fetch really does seem as cruel as Mary is sweet and needs to be dealt with. I don\u2019t really like the idea of using anyone as bait again, so we might have to experiment some with disguises, you know, something to trick the fetch into thinking she\u2019s caught Mary again.<br /> <br /> However we manage to get our hands on her, hopefully we\u2019ll be able to do something to make Mary safe more permanently soon. It\u2019s not like she\u2019s a horrible houseguest or anything though. She keeps trying to be useful, and she blushes more than me, not that it helped with the teasing much today. Calamity and Jacob decided to spar, which I guess Lori decided was going to always and forever be about innuendo, at least until Calamity started talking about how sex and fighting were the same thing, sometimes, you know, and made Lori blush.<br /> <br /> Anyways, last night Calamity was super snuggly once we\u2019d all gathered back together, which I sure wasn\u2019t complaining about. Once we\u2019d all filled each other in, I swept her up and carried her upstairs. We were both too tired for anything crazy, but it felt good, you know, right, to fall asleep like that, with her nestled up against me. It was peaceful and warm, right up until I actually fell asleep and started dreaming.<br /> <br /> The nightmare started right off. It was a faceless man who had come into my glade, with Dark Kimberly slung over the back of his horse, a much larger wound then the one she actually got bleeding through her shirt. At first, it almost didn\u2019t seem like a nightmare - if anyone who\u2019d ever come into my glade deserved what he got there, whoever did that to Dark Kimberly probably deserves it most of all. But then his face started to change, first flickering between people I didn\u2019t know, like a random Latina woman and a Chinese man, before settling on a rotation through pretty much all my friends here - the motley, Captain Jack, Desiree, Chalcedony, Ginny, Monica, Joan, Andromeda, even Lucian and Master Darke showed up occasionally. And I couldn\u2019t seem to cut him down, no matter how many times my sword fell, no matter whether I was trying to stop it or not.<br /> <br /> Then Calamity showed up. She came in over the river, and as she did, the colors and sounds and smells of that place got kinda... muted, you know? Everything was less intense, less gripping. She came over and stood next to me, and for a second the lingering fear made me certain she would stab him and he\u2019d look up at me with the face of someone I cared about and there\u2019d be one more body, one more ghost. I looked at the horse with Dark Kimberly\u2019s body, certain that Calamity wouldn\u2019t be able to leave that unanswered and saw that it was gone. When I looked back down, the faceless man was gone too, and Calamity held out a hand to me. I took it, and we walked and talked and spent the rest of the night enjoying each other\u2019s company in the gentle green of the forest.<br /> <br /> I almost didn\u2019t want to wake up, which is usually not the way my dreams go, but I did and she was there, smiling down at me. I\u2019d woken her up, with my nightmare, and she\u2019d used the Contract of Dreams on me, scouring everything down, you know? Cause she\u2019s amazing, and wonderful, and all sorts of things like that. I was a little worried that she\u2019d not gotten any rest herself, but I guess dreaming with other people is as restful as dreaming for yourself. At least, she looked like she\u2019d gotten some sleep.<br /> <br /> She had a surprise for me too - she\u2019d snuck a few things in on the last food stocking order, like Angus steak and blue cheese. She suggested they\u2019d make for a good black and blue salad, which sounded awesome to me. I made some hard boiled eggs, as a topping and so Ace wouldn\u2019t go hungry. We had a nice vinaigrette dressing thing and I even managed to scrounge up some walnuts and honey to do it right. It was a little different from the usual breakfast, but like Calamity said, we were eating breakfast in the early afternoon, so it didn\u2019t always have to be breakfast-breakfast. It was pretty tasty too, if I do say so myself. Calamity did, and nobody else had any complaints at least.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s been a pretty lazy day so far. There was the sparring, like I said, and I spent a few hours working on a spare flammenschwert, since I can only improve my current one one more time before it shatters. It turned out nicely, very well balanced and easy to reset. I might have to keep this one, and be very selective about when I do any Smith work on it.<br /> <br /> We did have a visitor at some point. Davie came by, to check up on Mary and let us know that Princess Jolie was making it a rule that Desiree and Chalcedony shouldn\u2019t be in the same place at the same time, since they kept causing problems whenever they were around each other. They decided to have the Dream House be an exception, unless they caused problems here, and then it\u2019d go like the general rules said - whoever started something got banned.<br /> <br /> Davie was also worried about Dark Kimberly. She\u2019d gone to Annika\u2019s yesterday, and hadn\u2019t come out or responded much to his texts. Calamity figured she was just \u201ca little tied up\u201d, you know, but said she\u2019d go check. I dunno how she could tell I was blushing behind my forge, but she could and only teased me a little before promising she\u2019d be back in time for the show. She was back way before that, actually, reporting that Dark Kimberly was fine, just, you know, hiding out a bit, getting over the psychological stuff of being shot. Calamity was super amused too - I guess Annika\u2019s house was crazy messy, and Dark Kimberly\u2019s cleaning thing was winning. It was good to see Calamity so pleased with things, and to hear Dark Kimberly was doing alright.<br /> <br /> Jacob also dropped by the garage while I was forging. He wanted some pointers on working leather, like we got from the briar wolves, so I put some calls out to get us some more mundane leather to practice on. He\u2019s off at the library at the moment, though I think he\u2019s due back soon.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know quite how to characterize the eighteen hours or so since my last entry. We\u2019ve had some horrible revelations, some thrilling experiences, and we\u2019ve even thrown a little light on what\u2019s been going on in the Freehold\u2026 at least enough to eliminate some potential explanations. But most of my attention has been focused on the few glorious hours of sleep I grabbed this morning\u2026 and the admittedly not entirely unexpected revelation that followed.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m afraid I wasn\u2019t much help going over the security footage at the Rose and Thorn last night; I kept getting distracted by the patrons\u2019 outfits. But Calamity and D managed to figure out what was going on with Chalcedony and Desiree. It seems that Chalcedony wasn\u2019t really following Desiree at all the other night\u2026 she was following Molly Nuit, who had <u>disguised</u> herself as Desiree to\u2026 well, we don\u2019t really know why. Presumably she was just screwing with Chalcedony for some reason.<br /> <br /> We were also able to glean that, like Lucien Torres said, Molly Nuit left the Rose and Thorn just prior to the shooting. Like, <u>immediately</u> prior, which in and of itself is sort of suspicious. On the other hand, if she knew anything about the impending violence, why would she have waited until just before it happened to make herself scarce? That sort of thing is bound to draw attention to her, so one has to wonder if the shooting was timed to coincide with her departure specifically to make people suspicious of her.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve said it before and I\u2019ll say it again: this Nancy Drew shit is for the birds. Other birds. Not me.<br /> <br /> In any case, our analysis of the video evidence was cut short when I got a frantic call from Mary. She was whispering, and was obviously terrified of something. I eventually managed to get out of her that someone was in her apartment, moving around and doing something in her kitchen. She told me that she had already called Becky Wan, but that it was going to take her almost half an hour to come to Mary\u2019s aid. I did some math in my head and figured that we could be at her place in ten minutes if I drove my \u2018vette.<br /> <br /> Marguerite stayed at the Rose and Thorn while Calamity, D and I made tracks for Mary\u2019s apartment. When we were still about five minutes out, Mary called again to tell me that she could smell smoke. I told her to try to get out of a window, still frightened that whoever was in her apartment might hurt her if she went out the front door. We sort of lost the connection after that, and I laid on the gas a little harder.<br /> <br /> Smoke was pouring out of the building by the time we got there. People were starting to gather in the parking lot, but the crowd was still small enough that we managed to slip into the building unnoticed and make our way up the stairs to Mary\u2019s unit. We got the door open, and Calamity headed into the kitchen to see if she could do anything about the blaze (and, presumably, the motherfucker who started it). I told D to do what she could to wake up the building\u2019s other residents and then to get out into the parking lot. She nodded and gave me a quick but passionate kiss before departing.<br /> <br /> I ran down the hall to Mary\u2019s bedroom, and found a chair wedged under the doorknob, forcing the door shut. I pulled it away and opened the door, trying to keep low to avoid choking on the thick black smoke. Mary was lying in the corner, passed out. My eyes were watering, so I couldn\u2019t easily tell if she was still breathing, but I knew I had to get her into the fresh air as quickly as possible. I called out to Calamity that I was going out the window, forced it open, grabbed Mary, and leaped out into the cool night air.<br /> <br /> I spread my wings and glided down to the ground in lazy circles. Luckily Mary\u2019s window doesn\u2019t face the parking lot, and I found myself drifting downward into a broad but secluded alley. Mary coughed, moaned softly, and shifted in my arms, and I allowed myself to breathe a sigh of relief. \u201cIt\u2019s okay, sweetie,\u201d I said soothingly, \u201cyou\u2019re going to be okay now.\u201d<br /> <br /> Calamity and D both made it to the parking lot okay, and D let me know that the building was clear. We were able to resuscitate Mary, who was upset but not badly hurt by her experience. Calamity asked her if she had any enemies; anyone who would want to hurt her. She responded with the expected negative. Then Calamity played a hunch and asked about Mary\u2019s fetch. Mary got this hurt look in her eyes and hung her head, and replied \u201cokay, there is <u>one</u> person who wants to hurt me.\u201d<br /> <br /> Calamity nodded, and we had a quick huddle. It seems likely that Mary\u2019s fetch was the one who stole her clothes from Glamour Springs the other day. She must have come back to Mary\u2019s apartment and planted the illegal gun and ammo in her bedroom (and slept in her bed\u2026 creepy). Then she waited for Mary to return and came back with a can of gasoline and a few matches\u2026 Calamity says it was obvious that some sort of accelerant was used in the kitchen.<br /> <br /> This is sick. Mary\u2019s fetch isn\u2019t just trying to kill her; she\u2019s trying to <u>ruin</u> her. Even if the flames hadn\u2019t killed Mary, the subsequent police investigation would have turned up a lot of bad shit. The complex\u2019s security footage would have shown someone who looked just like Mary walking into the apartment with a can of gasoline just before the blaze started, and checking her apartment would have turned up an unlicensed firearm with God knows what crimes attached to it and a box of illegal ammunition. Luckily, Calamity had thought to grab the gun and ammo before leaving the burning apartment, and in all the confusion she had no trouble slipping into the security office and erasing the offending video footage.<br /> <br /> Becky arrived in the middle of this conversation, and the five of us had a powwow about how to proceed. Becky agreed that our interpretation of the facts was probably correct, and that it was unlikely Mary\u2019s fetch would let things go at this point. She offered to take Mary to a safe house, but in the end the motley agreed to put her up at the Dream House for the time being. With people like Calamity and Gawain around to protect her, she should be pretty safe, and I can heal any injuries she might sustain. Plus, I think Calamity is hoping to draw the fetch out of hiding so that she can\u2026 err\u2026 \u201ceffect a more permanent solution.\u201d<br /> <br /> We got Mary calmed down and brought her back to the Dream House (Becky drove Calamity in her car, as the \u2018vette was getting pretty crowded by this point). We also picked up Marguerite from the Rose &amp; Thorn, of course, and touched base with the others. Jacob had been keeping an eye on Chalcedony and Ginny \u2013 nothing new to report there \u2013 while Gawain made sure that Desiree was safe. Desiree apparently has some sort of weird fetish or something\u2026 according to Gawain, her apartment was full of clothing mannequins, including a semicircle of seven of them arranged around the foot of her bed, all looking inward. Creepy.<br /> <br /> It was getting pretty late by this point, and some of us had to work the next day, so we split up and headed off to bed. I got Mary settled in the guest room again, and then slipped back into my bedroom to find D waiting for me under the covers. Neither one of us was much in the mood for lovin\u2019, so I just slipped out of my clothes and snuggled up against her.<br /> <br /> \u201cMissed you, babe,\u201d she yawned.<br /> <br /> \u201cLikewise,\u201d I said, kissing the back of her neck.<br /> <br /> \u201cPretty good day for you, all told,\u201d she continued.<br /> <br /> \u201cHow\u2019s that?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> D rolled over to face me. \u201cSaved a life. Figured some shit out. Had an awesome show. Not bad.\u201d<br /> <br /> I grinned in the darkness. \u201cI guess you\u2019re right. Can\u2019t complain about the way it\u2019s ending, either. I have the most <u>amazing</u> girl in the world to cuddle.\u201d She gave a little purr of contentment, but didn\u2019t really answer. I put a hand under her chin and made her look into my eyes. \u201cI mean it, D. I love having sex with you, and making out with you, and all the rest. But even when we\u2019re just lying here together like this\u2026 you make me so <u>happy</u>.\u201d<br /> <br /> She kissed me gently on the mouth, and her eyes were shining in the darkness. I don\u2019t know if it was the sheen of tears, or if it\u2019s just a Darkling thing, and I don\u2019t really care. \u201cLikewise, Lori,\u201d she breathed into my ear. Then she put her head on my chest and we let ourselves drift off.<br /> <br /> We woke up in early afternoon to the most wonderful smells drifting up from the kitchen. Apparently we weren\u2019t the only ones who had a restful night\u2026 Gawain and Calamity were quite chipper, and Gawain was making the most <u>amazing</u> black-and-blue salad. I\u2019d never had one before, but it was delicious, and both of them looked as happy as I\u2019d ever seen them.<br /> <br /> Note to self: I need to remember that Mary is quite a bit more innocent than the rest of us. We were making the usual early-day small talk, and of course the conversation turned to sex (well, sex and violence, really, but that\u2019s neither here nor there). You should have seen how fast her face turned red! I apologized for making her uncomfortable before she could flee the scene, and we toned the conversation down for a bit.<br /> <br /> D had to eat and run, as she had to work today. We kissed each other goodbye, and she got into her scrubs and drove off a few minutes later. As I was walking back toward the kitchen, much to my surprise, Julia pulled me aside and asked if she could speak with me privately.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sorry to bother you, but it\u2019s about Insincere Marguerite,\u201d she explained.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat\u2019s up?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t know what happened between you two yesterday, but she thinks you snubbed her in some way, and it\u2019s got her very upset. I don\u2019t\u2026 I don\u2019t think she\u2019s <u>mad</u> at you, exactly, but she\u2019s stubborn enough that she\u2019s not going to bring it up, and I don\u2019t want to see something this foolish drive a wedge between you two.\u201d She frowned cutely. \u201cShe\u2019s being very childish about this whole thing, if you ask me.\u201d<br /> <br /> I sighed as I thought back to yesterday morning\u2026 and the evening that preceded it. I\u2019d been very upset about Dark Kimberly\u2019s shooting, and Marguerite had offered me a shoulder to cry on. We\u2019d slept in the same bed, but kept things PG. Then, the next morning, she\u2019d come on to me pretty hot and heavy. I hadn\u2019t been in the mood, and I guess I thought it was just Marguerite trying to \u201clay claim\u201d to me in some way, and the part of me that won\u2019t be caged rebelled against that notion.<br /> <br /> \u201cMarguerite has\u2026 issues with control,\u201d I said softly after a minute had passed, \u201cand I have issues with being controlled. But that\u2019s not all it was. I\u2019m sure you\u2019ve noticed that D and I have gotten very\u2026 \u2018close\u2019 lately, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> Julia looked at me as though I\u2019d just tried to explain to her how the Pacific Ocean was a bit damp. \u201cShe\u2019s madly in love with you,\u201d she replied drily.<br /> <br /> My heart exploded at that sentence. I tried to control my expression so that the happy eradication of all my insecurities and doubts didn\u2019t show, and all she could see was a shy, coy smile, but I was elated. \u201cI\u2026 feel the same way,\u201d I told her, and she nodded. \u201cIt\u2019s scary. I\u2019ve never really felt like this about anyone before, and I just don\u2019t want to do anything to mess that up, so I\u2019m being a little bit more careful about my relationships\u2026 my lovers. I didn\u2019t mean to hurt her feelings.\u201d<br /> <br /> She took my hand in hers. \u201cI get it. You don\u2019t have to explain, Lorelei. I just don\u2019t want you two to end up angry at each other over something like this. You both mean too much to me,\u201d she finished softly.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll talk to her,\u201d I promised.<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t tell her I talked to you, please,\u201d Julia said as I turned to leave.<br /> <br /> \u201cMy lips are sealed,\u201d I promised. \u201cAnd Julia\u2026 thanks.\u201d I gave her a quick kiss before I left. There was warmth and affection in that kiss; caring and regard and maybe the tiniest bit of passion. It wasn\u2019t what I feel when I kiss D, but it wasn\u2019t just a throwaway gesture, either.<br /> <br /> I had two jobs lined up for this afternoon. The first one didn\u2019t pay much, but if it goes well I should have some great shots to add to my portfolio. If it goes <u>very</u> well, it might put a real feather in my cap. I drove out to Santa Monica College and met my client at the Student Union. He was an art student focusing on photography, and he wanted to enter a contest sponsored by the Jack Daniel Distillery to create an ad for their signature line of whiskeys. The winner of the contest will have their ad featured in a number of magazines with national distribution.<br /> <br /> Ironically, he wanted me to pose in such a way that he could add a pair of angel wings to my back\u2026 umm\u2026 somehow. I think it has something to do with computers. So I dressed up in really skimpy lingerie and posed sitting at a breakfast table, looking bored and hoisting a bottle of Jack with a lit cigarette smoldering in an ashtray in front of me. I have no idea how it\u2019s going to look when the photographer is through with it, but I wish him the best of luck.<br /> <br /> (He was very professional during the shoot, by the way; I think he has the right demeanor to go far in this business. He did ask me if I wanted to get a cup of coffee or something after we were through, but I had another shoot to get to, so I had to take a rain check.)<br /> <br /> My next shoot was also in Santa Monica, albeit across town from the college. This one was for Gary, and I got my standard rate for wearing a variety of techno-Victorian \u201csteampunk\u201d costumes and doing my best to look sexy and alluring. Gary can be kind of a sleaze at times, but he pays well, and he\u2019s never actually <u>done</u> anything inappropriate beyond his flirting and the occasional salacious comment. And he knows how to sell his shots, too\u2026 I\u2019ve probably gotten more exposure from the sessions I\u2019ve done with him than from most of my other modeling work combined.<br /> <br /> I was posing with Madeline today, and she was chipper as usual. Gary put us in some pretty suggestive poses, but she took it with good grace, laughing and joking around like she was having the time of her life. I was distracted, so it took me a little while to realize that she was flirting with me. I threw a couple of light double-entendres back at her, but things didn\u2019t progress past the verbal phase today. I wonder if D would like her?<br /> <br /> We agreed to meet up for a drink \u201csometime,\u201d and I drove back to the Dream House. I apparently missed a few things, like Jacob and Calamity sparring in the yard, but as I\u2019m not quite the connoisseur of violence that most of my friends are, I count that as a minor loss at most.<br /> <br /> When I got back, I made a beeline for Insincere Marguerite. I asked her quietly if I could talk to her for a moment, and then took her gently by the arm and pulled her into a secluded spot away from the others.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d been rehearsing what to say in my head ever since my conversation with Julia. \u201cSaturday night,\u201d I began softly, \u201cI needed a friend. I needed someone to be there so that I wouldn\u2019t be alone in the wake of the shooting. You were there for me when I needed you, and I want you to know how much that means to me.\u201d<br /> <br /> She started to respond, but I begged her to let me finish. \u201cThe next morning you needed something from me, and I blew you off. I <u>wasn\u2019t</u> there for you. I thought it was something it wasn\u2019t, and I let my own issues get in the way. I just want you to know that I never meant to hurt your feelings, and I\u2019m so sorry that I did.\u201d And because I\u2019ve always been better at making myself understood through actions, I leaned in and gave her a slow, emotional kiss. \u201cI hope you can forgive me,\u201d I said as we parted. I might have been a little misty-eyed by that point.<br /> <br /> She flashed me one of those dazzling grins of hers. \u201cNot to worry, <i>mon cheri</i>,\u201d she whispered, \u201cit is already forgotten.\u201d<br /> <br /> I think we\u2019re going to be okay now.<br /> <br /> So anyway, Davie had also stopped by while I was gone to pass along the Princess\u2019 latest decree. Jolie has decided that until they get their problems worked out, Chalcedony and Desiree are not to be in the same place at the same time. This will hopefully help us avoid scenes like the one at Glamour Springs yesterday. The only exception to this rule is the Dream House itself; both girls are welcome here until and unless one of them makes trouble\u2026 which is nice, as one of them is a regular performer at the Dream House, and the other could easily become one.<br /> <br /> Davie also expressed a private concern to Calamity: Dark Kimberly has been staying with Annika since the shooting, and she has been uncommunicative, and he\u2019s understandably worried. Calamity agreed to check on her, and drove over to Annika\u2019s place, which is apparently a creepy old Addams Family mansion on the edge of town. Color me shocked.<br /> <br /> Kimberly\u2019s doing fine, according to Calamity; she\u2019s still upset and frightened about the shooting, and just needs some time to decompress before she\u2019s ready to face the world again. She\u2019s kept herself busy by cleaning up parts of Annika\u2019s house (much to her host\u2019s distress), but seems none the worse for wear.<br /> <br /> I suppose I shouldn\u2019t be so hard on Annika, even in my private journal. She\u2019s been a good friend to Calamity, and she obviously cares for Kimberly in her own way and wants the best for her. I guess my negative feelings towards her are mostly about her attitude and personality rather than her actual character. And, if I\u2019m being completely honest, I suppose I\u2019m jealous of her too. She\u2019s so beautiful and alluring and talented\u2026 she\u2019s everything I want to be. I guess it\u2019s easy to see why nobody seems to pay the slightest attention to me when she\u2019s around.<br /> <br /> I want D. I want <u>Maria</u>. She never bats an eye at Annika; she feels just as insecure around her as I do.<br /> <br /> She promised she\u2019d be at the show tonight, and that we could be together afterward. It\u2019s not a big show, just a Monday night, so it won\u2019t be too crowded. Maybe we can make an early night of it, or go out somewhere\u2026 just the two of us. Maybe we can find some little romantic place that\u2019s open late and have a real date.<br /> <br /> Maybe we can each find the courage to say the words we both know are true.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T14:08:53-07:00","id":293181,"title":"","content":"<b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> <b><u><b><u>Monday May 12<sup>th </sup></u></b></u></b><br /> <br /> I am... happy. Not simply contented or sated but genuinely happy. I've felt good all day and while we're no closer to finding Andromeda's missing Table or identifying the bastard that shot Dark Kimberly I cannot help be feel optimistic that we will. Maybe it's just false hope after last night but it's worlds better than the emotional morass I was sinking into. Yesterday, I was a good monster. And not in the I managed to behave like a civilized human being and not stab anyone sense. I helped people. I made things better.<br /> <br /> I saved Ginny's life yesterday. That Extra had the drop on her. I was there and I was able to stop it. I was fast enough and skilled enough to end it before it could harm her. If not for the glass and for the training that it prompted me to seek I would never have been able to kill that thing so easily. And after those years in Snow Globe, it was so clear to me that something wasn't right about the way it was acting while it was impersonating Chalcedony. I took what the Whispers made me into and I used it the way I wanted to. I saved her because I was the better monster.<br /> <br /> While us girls were going over the security footage at the Rose and Thorn Jacob called Ginny and Chalcedony over to the Dream House both to keep a watch on Ginny after her scare and to make sure that Chalcedony neither went after Desiree or tried again. For pretty much the same reasons, Gawain went to check up on Desiree. We found Chalcedony fairly easily, but it wasn't Desiree she was tailing. It was Molly Nuit. Seems the Winter Court was trying to lure Chalcedony into some sort of trap. But Gunnar also started to watch her (no doubt because she was disguised as Desiree) and so Molly slipped out of sight and changed out of the outfit she'd been wearing as Desiree and presumably dropped the magic as well since both Gunnar and Chalcedony lost interest in her at that point. That was about the time Lori got a call from Mary. Someone was in her apartment. So, Lori and De la Rocha and I rushed over to help, leaving Insincere Marguerite to finish looking over the footage. As we were on the way, she called again and told us she smelled smoke. When we arrived, the apartment was on fire. We rushed in and split up. Lori went to help Mary get out and I headed to the kitchen to see if I could put the fire out.<br /> <br /> Lori found the door blocked with a chair and once inside the bedroom an unconscious Mary. Thinking quickly, she finished prying open the window Mary had been struggling with and flew them both to safety. Meanwhile, I found that the kitchen had been doused quite liberally with gasoline and set on fire. No effort at all to hide the arson. It was also obviously beyond the simple extinguisher to put out by that point. So instead I took a moment to try to find any clues before the fire destroyed them. It was clear the arsonist had used a key to get in (most likely the one stolen from Mary at the springs). At that point, seeing that there wasn't anything to be gained trying to fight the fire and that everyone else was safe, I decided to get out myself. But at the last moment I recalled the gun and decided to grab it and the box of armor piercing ammo. I could tell immediately it was too heavy for Mary to use effectively and it had not had its serial number filed off. On the way back to the parking lot, I noticed there was a security camera with a clear view of the stairs leading up to Mary's apartment.<br /> <br /> As Lori and De la Rocha tended to Mary, I slipped over to the security office. In the chaos, it was empty and so I was able to help myself to the footage. It showed a woman that looked like Mary with no seeming wearing the missing clothing and carrying a gas can up to the apartment. To avoid awkward questions from the authorities, I erased the file and rejoined the others.<br /> <br /> Becky had arrived and it did not take long to put it all together. The culprit was Mary's fetch. Guess I should have voiced that gut feeling I had about it after all. Turns out her fetch had stabbed her back in Kansas when she'd first tried to return home. She'd fled and apparently the motherless thing has been tracking her since. It passed up an easy kill to torment her and set her up for a much worse demise, framing her for the arson and planting a gun that is almost assuredly tied to something heinous in her apartment. (Note to self, I need to see if Lucien can and will check that serial number out.) The poor little thing was terrified and confused and lost as things came to light. Becky put forth a couple of ideas for temporary hideouts for the girl until a proper safe house could be arraigned. I volunteered the Dream House. After all, she's never been there except when Lori brought her and so the fetch has no reason to look there for her. And if it does... well I can't say the idea of laying into that soulless abomination isn't appealing. Would save us all the effort of hunting the damned thing down.<br /> <br /> Becky seemed unsure about putting us out but I assured her it was fine. I also promised that we'd make sure to keep Mary safe. Lori asked about the Princess and Becky explained that she was recovering from her most recent visit to Queen Charlotte. She was not pleased in the least with the situation or with how her claws were tied in regards to the spider queen. I guess my discomfort at that did not go unnoticed and she apologized. I do understand and I told her so. I also said that as much as she might not like it as long as Jolie is aware and willing it's not really anyone's place to tell her what she can or can't do. Becky countered that the Princess' safety is her responsibility. It places her in a position I cannot envy. Of course, the idea of her being in conflict with Charlotte would place me in an even less comfortable position. But fortunately the conversation didn't linger there and before we'd separated into Lori and Becky's cars to carry everyone to the Dream House her hair was teasing one of my spikes and I couldn't help but let out a soft purr at the memories of that night we shared. Hades knows I was completely worn out to let the ride back alone with her pass with nothing more than a little flirting after that.<br /> <br /> We put Mary up in the guest suite and then we all exchanged notes. Ginny and Chalcedony had both behaved and learning that it hadn't been Desiree she'd followed had not dampened the blue girl's determination that she was a loyalist. However, Jacob did manage to get them both back to Chalcedony's place and insure a further delay in open hostilities. Desiree continued to be hapless and sweet according to Gawain. Though the woman does apparently have a thing for manikins, arraigning them about her home to keep her company as she hates being alone. I remain unsure if this is more sad or creepy. Insincere Marguerite confirmed that there wasn't anything else of note in the tapes from the Rose and Thorn. And then, we all retired quite gratefully to our beds.<br /> <br /> Gawain swept me up into his arms and I curled in close with a pleased smile. It felt so good to be close to him as he carried me up to our bed. I think even once we do get the murder ghost dealt with I'm going to stay with this room. The other is my room, but this one... this one is ours. Though at some point I really do need to talk to him about moving into it officially. We sank into the bed and I burrowed in close while he held me tight. Yeah, neither of us was up for anything wild or kinky or even vanilla but it was still perfect.<br /> <br /> Oh dear Lord and Lady above, if that last paragraph isn't proof that some part of the girl I used to be survived Snow Globe I don't know what is. But you know what, fuck it. Zod only knows why but Gawain loves me and that was what I needed last night. And while I was running somewhere less than zero emotionally, I wasn't that physically tired after sleeping in the library. Gawain slipped away pretty quick but I was still just laying there listening to his heartbeat and dozing when I felt him start to toss. It woke me up fully and I sat up, watching him fall into the grips of his nightmare. Sharing his apartment, I'd learned of the nightmares. I'd seen him afterward and when I asked, he'd opened up about them. I'd heard of dream weaving but it was a desire to find some way to do something more than just see him suffer that drove me to study it deeper. And last night I was finally able to do something.<br /> <br /> I moved to cradle his head in my lap and stroked his temples as I activated the Contract of Dreams and soon enough I fell into his dream. For the first time, I saw the forest glade that had been his hell for so long and continued to haunt him. I could feel the fear and anger filling the air and I concentrated on dampening everything, scouring away the dream the way I'd been taught to make way for replacing it with another. But I didn't weave anything. I just entered and walked up to him. As I reached the clearing I reached for his hand. He took it and I drew him out of the past. Away from the ghosts of what he'd been forced into night after night. I saved him, at least for one night. There are no words for how good it felt to be able to do that.<br /> <br /> And this morning, I awoke with him and a rush of joy surged to see him smiling up at me, rested and happy. It made me feel energized and more at peace than I have in a long time. I mentioned to him what I'd added to the last order and suggested black and blue salads. He seemed to like the idea of not always doing breakfast, and I don't think it was just because he's crazy about me.<br /> <br /> I decided to hit the gym he and Ace and Jacob set up downstairs while he cooked as I was feeling so full of energy. Everyone seemed pleased with the change in pace, though I am sure it helped that my handsome is such an amazing chief. I guess I don't think about how unusual our usual breakfast conversations are. I was still stoked and already dressed for it so I told Jacob we should spar, since we'd both said we wanted to again. And that got to talking about sex and fighting and I made some comments about them being similar if done right and that got Lori a little flustered, which was a beautiful sight as always. Only when she tried to steer things toward less violence and more sex it made poor Mary go bright red. She tried to tell us not to change our topics because of her while also asking how she could help out and not be a burden on us while she's there. She really is such an adorable little thing.<br /> <br /> She and most of the others ended up tagging along to watch Jacob and I this time. Lori had a photo shoot and Gawain was working on a new sword since his current one won't hold up to the stress of being enhanced again without breaking. As it turns out, Jacob isn't used to sparring with dulled weapons either. So we went at it live steel to glass. It was a really good workout for us both and well worth the nicks and cuts I picked up. It was a little different than last time, less about testing each other and more about working to practice and improve. It really is a delight to spar with someone that fights like I do and is so evenly matched to my skills. As we danced, he did ask me about some of the techniques I'd learned from Luna and I did my best to explain some of the basics. It felt a little strange to be the one teaching rather than learning for a change but I liked it and I'm looking forward to showing him more. Also, I think he enjoys being able to lose himself in the heat of battle as much as I do. He doesn't show it quite as gleefully, but I definitely caught a few stray unguarded smiles and smirks on his face. I'm not sure any of the others completely understand the joy and freedom fighting brings me but I believe my fellow monster does. Unfortunately, I also noticed something less pleasing than his mutual enjoyment of the fighting. It wasn't too obvious, but he was favoring his right side a bit more than he had before and he was definitely protecting his left. I am convinced that his decision to wear a shirt this time wasn't just modesty. I'm trying to think back over the past few days but it was only the proximity of the sparring that tipped me off so I can't be sure how long he's been hiding an injury. I hate to think it's from the briar wolves but unless he's kept more than just a wound from us I can't think of when else it might have happened. I didn't call attention to it and I don't think anyone else picked up on it but at some point when I can speak to him privately I am going to have to confront him about keeping it from us.<br /> <br /> As Lorelei was working, Davie texted me about dealing with a bit of Spring Court business. I had him come around back and when he arrived both Jacob and I were starting to get a bit winded so we broke for the day. First off, Princess Jolie had ruled that Chalcedony and Desiree were to avoid each other and that lead to the issue of the Dream House. I pointed out that they had both been present without issue recently and that as long as they weren't seated closely or both performing there was a fair amount of separation. He agreed and so I ended up basically stating that our standing policy would remain in effect, they were both still welcome so long as they did not cause trouble. And if they did, their Dream House privileges would be revoked and they'd have to deal with me. As far as performing, Desiree hasn't actually done a show with us, though I wouldn't be opposed to having her. He also brought the Princess' official thanks for looking after Mary and asked if there was anything the Court could do to help out. I assured him she wasn't a bother and had actually been quite eager to help out. I also assured him that I would let him know if there was something we needed.<br /> <br /> The final matter was personal. Dark Kimberly had gone to Annika's after being shot and she'd not been seen since. She was answering her texts, though even there she was apparently being far less the social creature she normally is. While it did make sense that she'd be a bit withdrawn after what she'd been through, he was still a bit worried about her. Given that I am one of a fairly short list of people that are close to Annika I promised him I would go and check on her, but that I was sure that she was fine. He seemed quite relieved. I then sent him on his way with a hug and light kiss.<br /> <br /> I wasn't lying to Davie about being confident that Dark Kimberly was fine (just perhaps tied up more than just figuratively) but at the same time, Annika is powerful and as much I am fond of her, the woman is not playing with a full duck. So, in the interest of being safe rather than sorry, I dropped by the forge (another note to self, I really should see about getting handsome a more proper set up. Maybe something in the hollow? Have to look into that...) I filled Gawain in on the situation and told him I was going to Annika's and that I would be back before the show.<br /> <br /> Annika's house is full on Addams Family. Seriously, I would not have been surprised if Lurch himself had answered the door. But it was Annika that did. She seemed a little surprised to see me but was cordial and invited me in. The interior of her home was... well to be generous I shall say neglected. It wasn't completely surprising based on what I know about her but that did not make the vast collection of empty bottles scattered about less sad. There were also quite a number of pictures. A couple were portraits of Madam Spidertoes but most were old photographs of the same attractive woman. In most she was dressed as a dancer and in at least one she was standing with a younger Annika. I can't help but wonder who she is, but it did not seem the best time to ask. Annika invited me to the kitchen and shared brandy and a cigar. We spoke about Dark Kimberly and Annika confirmed that she'd been there and steadily reclaiming the house from it's derelict state. I mentioned Davie's concern and asked about her. Annika told me the girl was resting and seemed a bit confused about the concern since she was aware that Kimberly had been answering her phone. I did explain that Kimberly was usually rather social and that her friends were just worried about her. So she escorted me to the sitting room and went to bring Kimberly down so I could speak to her. What followed was actually quite amusing. Kimberly had been awake and cleaning, as is her nature. I explained to Kimberly what we'd found and made sure she knew that we were certain that she hadn't been targeted specifically and so was most likely not in danger of a second attempt. It was clear that she was scared and shaken from her ordeal. It was also quite clear that she was in no way being kept from leaving. I think she feels safe in Annika's home (Which she is. The woman is not simply dominant but quite powerful.) Also, she can throw herself into cleaning it which keeps her busy and distracted. Dark Kimberly did decide that it would be good to make at least a brief appearance though Annika assured her was welcome to remain as long as she wished. Kimberly explained she couldn't leave until she'd reclaimed Annika's music room and more importantly the piano at which point Annika firmly explained that she was not allowed to harm any spiders in the house. I had to smile as I listened to them. They make quite the couple and I have no doubt they're going to take good care of each other. I bid them a good day and took my leave.<br /> <br /> I am still smiling as I take a break to write this before getting myself ready for tonight's show. The big things are still unresolved, investigating the shooting and finding the Table and hunting down Mary's fetch. I need to talk to Jacob. I still need to take Dionysia up on looking into Snow Globe and spend a bit of my own time in the library looking into Lori's Empress and Jacob's tattoo. I am waiting to hear back from Tommy and Madam Spidertoes so I can speak to them about that goblin contract the shooter used and perhaps see what they might know about The Whispering Voices. I've got a play date with Joan to do some sparring, possibly with Gawain. I need to speak to Lucien about the tapes and about my new gun. I need to look into a forge for Gawain (and the rest of us) to use for hedge crafting. Hmm... Andromeda is quite knowledgeable about tools and workshops. Maybe enlist Joan as well, she's familiar with the specifics of the arms and armor. And those two could certainly both use a friend. Perhaps working together on my little project would be a good way to get them talking to each other. And, of course, there is practicing my dancing.<br /> <br /> I am quite the busy little monster, oh yes indeed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> I almost feel compelled to ask myself what the hell I\u2019ve gotten myself involved in. This is not the \u201claying low\u201d that I had planned on. This is the opposite of that. Okay, so I volunteered to keep Chalcedony and Ginny company and make sure they were alright, and to keep Chalcedony from going out and killing Desiree. For my side of things it was a pretty dull evening. For the others however it was much more exciting. Apparently Lorelei got a call from Mary in a panic saying that she heard someone in her house. Lorelei told her she\u2019d be there as soon as she could, maybe ten minutes. A little after the first call, Mary called back to say that she smelled smoke. The lot of them (Lorelei, Calamity, and De la Rocha) stepped on it and got to the parking lot in time to see smoke pouring out of Mary\u2019s place. Lorelei and Calamity got into the apartment. Lori looked for Mary, while Calamity checked out the kitchen, where Mary had heard the intruder. Lorelei found a chair wedged under the door handle to the bedroom and quickly moved it before going in. She found Mary unconscious on the floor. I think she got her to come around a bit before grabbing hold and gliding out the back window with her.<br /> <br /> Calamity found gasoline and fire in the kitchen. The fire was too big for the extinguisher to really do anything so she did a quick once over to see what she could find before running to the bedroom and grabbing the gun and ammunition out of the nightstand drawer. No sense leaving it there to be found by the authorities. After they got Mary to safety and the gun stowed, Calamity went to the management office and took a look at the security footage. It confirmed a theory that had been brought up. It showed what looked like Mary, wearing the clothes that had been stolen, walking into the apartment carrying a gasoline can. That in and of itself would have been damning for Mary if the police saw it. The gun would just add another layer to that. The serial number is still on the weapon so it would be easily traced, and there\u2019s no telling what it\u2019s been used for. At least not yet. So, Calamity erased the footage of Mary\u2019s fetch and rejoined the others. Mary had also called Becky for help and she arrived after they\u2019d gotten the frightened girl out. They split between her car and Lori\u2019s \u2018Vette to come back to the house.<br /> <br /> Before all that the motley, minus me and Gawain, had gone to the Rose and Thorn to check out the security footage for the night of the shooting. They saw Molly Nuit walking up to the front of the club wearing the same clothes that Chalcedony had seen Desiree wearing. Apparently Molly disguised herself as Desiree to mess around with Chalcedony. I\u2019m not sure if this is a Court approved thing or if Molly just felt like messing with her. Calamity called me to give me the news and I reassured Chalcedony that she had actually seen Molly in disguise and not Desiree. Not that this news was going to completely cool Chalcedony\u2019s ire towards the other girl, but it did temper it somewhat. Other than that the evening with the two ladies was uneventful. Ginny spent most of the evening flirting with Chalcedony and serenading her (for lack of a better word). It was kind of sweet. I\u2019m not sure that Chalcedony knew what to do about it. She seemed a bit uncertain, maybe uncomfortable with all the attention. Later though, when we talked about Ginny staying with Chalcedony to keep her safe, she seemed okay with it. Maybe she just needed to get used to Ginny and her flirtations.<br /> <br /> One thing to take note of\u2026.the security footage at the club had no images of the shooter that came into the club and shot Kimberly. None at all. That in and of itself says a lot. It says that the shooter was familiar enough with the placement of the security cameras to completely avoid being captured on film. So they either work for the club, or have been there enough times to map out where the cameras are and what areas each of them cover. I\u2019m inclined to think that it is someone that has at least gotten a look at the security footage to map out the area that each camera covers. Without knowing what will show up on each camera it is too much of a gamble to just look at them and guess where their coverage stops. I will have to bring this up to the others and see if they think the idea has any merit, or if I\u2019m imagining things.<br /> <br /> The camera footage also showed Molly leaving the club right before the shooting took place. The timing would make it pretty much an impossibility that she turned around and came back in to shoot Kimberly. So, I think we can take her off the suspect list. I\u2019m not 100% positive of course. I\u2019ll still keep an eye on her, but I think we should focus our attention on other suspects. We\u2019ll see how it goes.<br /> <br /> Later we all got together to compare notes on our evenings activities. Gawain had spent his evening with Desiree making sure that she was okay, much like I had spent time with Chalcedony and Ginny. So, we caught each other up on what happened and tried to figure out what we were going to do next. We bounced ideas off each other trying to figure out how to draw out Mary\u2019s fetch and take care of her. Some people suggested having someone act as a decoy, dressing up as Mary, or using a disguise of some sort. The only problem is if we use one of the motely we are all too distinct as ourselves and could not reliably pass as Mary, probably not even from a distance. I think we decided that we would use Mary as bait, but have people hidden in an area that we had staked out before. We talked about drawing the fetch out by making it look like Mary was running. Have her pack up and start to load up her car, or something like that. If we do that, we would have to move fast. If we wait too long it will look like something we had planned. If people are going to do something in a panic then it will happen right away. Scared people who intend to run do not hole up and plan things carefully.<br /> <br /> I remember well enough people that I toyed with in the Lady\u2019s realm, or those that I brought back for her. Some got away, but a good number of them did not. The ones that could keep their cool were the harder ones to catch. The others that spooked and acted on impulse were so much easier to catch. Those were the ones that would respond to the scare tactics that Rook and I used. They walked right into our trap, and we brought them back to the Lady. Sometimes it was too easy. Other times not so much. Goddess I remember their faces. I remember them begging me to let them go, to not return them to Her. We did anyway. I did anyway. Some of them even survived Her wrath. Most of those that did wished they hadn\u2019t. Goddess, I\u2019m so screwed if when she finds me or when I am brought back.<br /> <br /> Okay\u2026have to get out of that frame of mind. Got to focus on something else. Anything else. Okay\u2026so all that happened last night. This morning I made coffee like usual, and Gawain made food, but this time changed things up a bit. He made what he called a \u201cblack and bleu\u201d salad. I thought at first he was saying \u201cblue\u201d as in the color, but he was saying \u201cbleu\u201d as in the cheese. It is apparently a salad with strips of steak and blue cheese on top with a kind of vinaigrette dressing. It was good. A nice change from the American breakfast food that we\u2019ve been having lately. Not that there is anything wrong with Gawain\u2019s breakfasts.<br /> <br /> After food we split up to do individual things, for the most part. Lorelei had some modelling work to do and Gawain went to the garage to work on his sword, or to make a new one. He said something about only being able to improve a weapon so many times before it broke. I\u2019ll have to take his word on that. I have had some pretty nice knives in my time, but nothing special or enchanted. At least until Gawain that nice blade for me. I think De la Rocha went to her own job as well. Before we all split up though Calamity, who had just come from the gym downstairs, looked at me and said that we should spar. I agreed and decided to be a bit daring and asked if she wanted to spar with dulled knives or live steel. Somehow I wasn\u2019t surprised when she said live steel. I knew that she was good with a blade, but wasn\u2019t sure if she had practiced with another person with sharp blades before or not. Turns out she was as used to practicing with dull knives as I was, which meant not really at all. So, she jumped at the chance to take the stabilizers off the bike so to speak. I went upstairs to change into work-out clothes that I did not mind getting holes or blood on. I left a t-shirt on this time. I think I kept telling myself that it was because I didn\u2019t want to draw attention to my scars and the Lady\u2019s mark with so many watching, and that may have been part of it, but I think a small part of me didn\u2019t want to draw attention to the bandage on my side. It\u2019s stopped bleeding through, so it\u2019s almost gone, but I just didn\u2019t want people to make a fuss over nothing. I guess I can understand not wanting to leave friends with a lingering hurt, but it really wasn\u2019t all that bad. Not compared to some injuries I\u2019ve had, plus I\u2019m afraid of letting myself get soft. I\u2019ve already gotten too used to eating regularly, not to mention sleeping in a bed. Intellectually I know that I\u2019m safe here, but I just can\u2019t let myself slack off. I can\u2019t let myself become too comfortable. It never ends well.<br /> <br /> Anyhoo\u2026Calamity and I sparred with live steel and it was exhilarating. I almost felt like I had to hold back less than I did with a dulled knife. I know how much pressure to put to inflict a scratch and how much harder to press to make it more than that. It seems Calamity felt the same way. This time though we weren\u2019t so much feeling each other out as far as ability went. We\u2019d already established that. This time we just let go and fought. I commented on Calamity\u2019s fighting style as we practiced. I know lots of moves and how to put them together here and there, and how to fight with a certain amount of creativity, but she knows a distinct style. It is beautiful to watch, and I couldn\u2019t help but comment on it. In return for my interest, she started showing me a few of the moves as we practiced. We didn\u2019t even really stop what we were doing. She just made suggestions or corrections to my stance or moves as we went through them. It was a lot of fun. I definitely want to do that again.<br /> <br /> Calamity is a really good fighter and I know that I don\u2019t have to hold back when sparring with her. I don\u2019t have to be careful, at least not overly so. I know that she will dodge or block the truly dangerous strikes while dishing out some of her own. I think with any other member of the motley I would have to slow things down to give them time to react. Not that they aren\u2019t good in their own right, they just aren\u2019t as practiced in the up close and personal kind of fighting that Calamity and I are proficient in. Calamity says that she is a monster because she likes to fight. I don\u2019t agree. Loving to fight doesn\u2019t make you a monster. Being good at fighting does not make you a monster. I don\u2019t even think that hurting other people in a fight makes you a monster. Hunting down and capturing or killing innocent people, that is wrong. That makes you a monster, if you believe you\u2019re doing right. But fighting someone that is trying to hurt you or yours, stopping them from doing harm. That does not make you a monster.<br /> <br /> I think Calamity got to step outside of her self-imposed role as \u201cmonster\u201d by helping Chalcedony the other night. She was definitely more upbeat today and I know that she had fun going all out in a fight with someone that didn\u2019t end up with someone dead. I know I had fun. There is a certain freedom in going all out while sparring. I suppose it would be like losing yourself to the music while dancing, or blocking out the rest of the world as you painted, just becoming engrossed in the colors and patterns of your art. I didn\u2019t have to keep a part of my mind focused on holding back or slowing down. Not with Calamity. With her, I can let the fetters go and just be free.<br /> <br /> So, after the sparring match Davie came to visit to tell us what had been discussed about Desiree and Chalcedony by the Courts. Apparently they have decided that those two are not allowed to be in the same place together to avoid any trouble. He wanted to talk to us about that since our establishment is public. I think we all agreed that it was fine if they were in the club at the same time but someone would keep an eye on the pair of them to make sure they don\u2019t start anything. I guess we\u2019ll see how that goes. I think after that Calamity went over to see Annika and talk to Dark Kimberly.<br /> <br /> We are also going to be hosting Mary for a while. The house seemed to be the logical place for her to hide out since her fetch has not been here, and there are several combat capable people here that would take offense at Mary\u2019s fetch trying anything. Part of me kind of hopes that thing does try something here. I\u2019m fairly certain we\u2019d be able to deal with the problem, and we have an entrance to the hedge on hand to chuck the detritus through.<br /> <br /> And now I\u2019m going to get back to the book I got from the library. I decided to get a library card today. It seemed a normal thing to do. Plus I wanted to learn more about leather working and Gawain is not much more practiced at it than I am. And given that this is probably not the most commonly found skill set, I figured it would be prudent to do some research. Gawain even suggested that we get some scrap leather to practice on before we try to make anything with the Briar Wolf pelts. Seemed like a good idea to me. I\u2019ll be honest that the book I got created a bit of a problem that I hadn\u2019t thought of. Since I\u2019ve been in the Lady\u2019s realm I spoke English and a good bit of Russian, but I didn\u2019t really do much in the way of reading. Any notes I was able to write to myself were in Cyrillic. Hell, every word I\u2019ve written in this book is in Cyrillic. But, the book I got from the library today is not. It\u2019s in English. I\u2019ve had some practice lately with the names of different alcohols, street signs and such. It will just take some practice to make out all the words. Guess it\u2019s good that I can keep the book for two weeks.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> Last night got better. Remarkably, things got clearer. Mostly.<br /> <br /> We visited Rose &amp; Thorn and looked at the cameras. Turns out Molly Nuit was trying to lure Chalcedony somewhere, only to have Ghoul Friday begin stalking her, so she dropped the disguise, thus \u201cdisappearing.\u201d Molly goals remain opaque, but the Winter Court is always up to something. Usually.<br /> <br /> The reason Mary\u2019s story and behavior seemed so odd and out of left field was it was her Fetch who was causing trouble. Her Fetch had tried to kill her in Kansas, and has now tracked her to Santa Monica. She stole the clothes getting past the mortal stuff as she looks like Mary. Turns out in addition to robbing and gaslighting Mary, she was also setting up to trap her in her room and set her apartment on fire. Fortunately she called Lorelei, and she and Calamity got her to safety. Thankfully.<br /> <br /> Calamity\u2019s name is becoming increasing ironic. That is two lives she helped save last night. I suppose it is a Calamity for someone. Certainly.<br /> <br /> We wound up taking Mary back here. Nothing horrid happened with Ginny, Desiree or Chalcedony, and I wound up spending time on the roof with Julia. I like the roof. Generally.<br /> <br /> Today has been pretty quiet. Julia and I argued a little this morning about Lorelei so I tried to be nice to her. It generally went well. Julia is a little sweet on Lorelei, which is to be expected I suppose. We watched Calamity and Jacob spar in the back yard, until Davie came by to make sure we knew about the Desiree and Chalcedony stuff. He also wanted Calamity to check on Dark Kimberly, who has been staying at a Annika\u2019s estate in the hills, but nothing horrid was going on there. Fortunately.<br /> <br /> I did tell Jacob I was not ignoring him but worried about the Birth Control. It was awkward. Needed to be done but I am glad it is over.<br /> <br /> Lorelei came up and apologized to I for snubbing me. I was really taken aback by it, but perhaps I should not have been. I accepted her apology, and we kissed. It was not the kiss of a one true love, but it was the kiss of a woman with feelings for her partner. And that was the kiss Lorelei received in return. Blissfully.<br /> <br /> I do understand how people fall so hard for Lorelei. She is a lovely and intriguing woman. She has a bit of an aggressively independent streak, but one could say the same of me, I suppose. Correctly. But we seem to get along well enough she and I. Usually.<br /> <br /> Now, lets see what we can get done before something terrible happens to bring everything down.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XV</i><br /> <br /> Not a lot of very specific stuff to go over from behind the curtain this time. We played out Calamity preventing one of Gawain\u2019s Nightmares, which meant exploring the dream system a bit. Calamity and Gawain are, in theory, the ones better at such.<br /> <br /> Not much else to add this time, but comments and questions are welcome.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T01:58:00-08:00","id":307273,"title":"","content":"Settle in folks, top off your drinks. This is going to be a long one.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XVI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> May 13th<br /> <br /> It feels kinda weird to write that it\u2019s Tuesday when I haven\u2019t either gone to sleep or watched the sunrise at least, but technically it is and I\u2019m not sure regular sleep is going to be for awhile, you know? Or sunrise watching. I feel like I should be more freaked out than this, but I just feel kinda numb, I guess. Calamity is here with me, standing vigil over the soundly sleeping Mary. That helps.<br /> <br /> She told me she loved me, after the show. That was, well, amazing, you know? I\u2019d told her before, and I told her again, but that first time was kinda by accident, even though I meant it. She did it on purpose, with intention and all that. It\u2019s nice to think about. It makes me feel. I don\u2019t want to be empty again, even if there is another sadistic coward that deserves executing. And thinking about her is better than being angry.<br /> <br /> She even offered to stop having sex with other people. I told her that was ok. And it is. I can\u2019t give her everything she needs. Definitely not the <s>cowardice</s> fear that thrills her. And I couldn\u2019t hurt her - she doesn\u2019t deserve it, no matter how much of a monster she needs to be, and I would never forgive myself if I misjudged my own strength. But she loves me, and that\u2019s way more important, you know?<br /> <br /> It was talking with Madame Spidertoes that started all that. I\u2019d been sitting at her table cause Moon was there, and I wanted to apologize again at how impatient I\u2019d been at the library. Ze understood. I stuck around to chat, especially since Moon was feeling nervous. It was hir first time being Madame Spidertoes' escort, you know, ze and Dionysia. Calamity was making the rounds and stopped off at our table after checking up on everybody.<br /> <br /> She wanted to ask Madame Spidertoes two things. First was about the shooting, since Madame Spidertoes knows a lot about what powers people have, you know? She thought Tommy was the only one who probably had that Goblin Contract, but also pointed out it might be some other kinda supernatural thing. She told Calamity how to get in contact with some vampires. Calamity said I could come to, but that\u2019s probably on hold until we figure out how to deal with the dishonorable mockery of life that...<br /> <br /> <br /> Calamity also asked if Madame Spidertoes knew anything about Snow Globe. She had known two changelings from there. One was a mannikin who hadn\u2019t stayed long, about twenty years ago. The other was another darkling, back in the 1930s. Snow Globe was a little different then, obviously, but was the same idea, you know? Just different outfits. She\u2019d snapped and started strangling people when they tried to get her to follow Court rules and stuff. It was when Madame Spidetoes talked about how she\u2019d killed her Snow Globe family to get out that Calamity really started looking upset.<br /> <br /> She pulled me aside after the show to tell me I was the only reason she didn\u2019t go out like that. She was the only reason I got out of the Hedge, so it seemed fair to me, you know? I tried to joke around a little. I got a couple of smiles. But something felt like it wasn\u2019t working. So, when she started talking about being a monster that enjoyed killing, I got serious.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t talk that much about Arcadia, here or out loud. Lots of details are missing and all of them are blurred. But I killed thousands of people, and remember every face, and every transgression. There is no sensation I know more thoroughly than the shock that travels up your arm when your blade bites into someone\u2019s spine. I killed old men, young men, and everywhere in between. No children, but a number of teenagers that may as well have been. And some of them deserved it. Cowards and liars and people who just didn\u2019t want to die. I rode them down, tormenting them, one small cut for every day they acted in bad faith. And I enjoyed it. They deserved it.<br /> <br /> Fuck me, no they didn\u2019t. They were dreaming, running for their lives and terrified. But it\u2019s so easy it say it. To believe it. To justify it. So easy to be angry at them for failing, the worthless cowards...<br /> <br /> <br /> So I know what it is to be a monster, a machine created for killing. But I can\u2019t dwell on that. I don't need to dwell on that. I shouldn\u2019t be dwelling on it right now. I should go over to Calamity and pull her on my lap and bury my head in her shoulder and remember that I\u2019m the innocent one. I\u2019m the one that believes there is hope. I should remember the one dreamer, the one whose neck I couldn\u2019t cut because he was a good man, because there is good in this world. But instead I see Mary and think of her fetch, who makes me remember every backstabbing coward, every craven who offered me others in his place, who hid behind non-combatants. I think of the child it beheaded, so that Mary would be the one forced to run. I will be its executioner. We will be its executioners Even Lori agrees that it should die.<br /> <br /> The look on Mary\u2019s face is so peaceful now. Insincere Marguerite's chloroform did the trick. It is in sharp contrast to the look on her face when I got back from getting my stuff, the one that had me dropping it all in a small pile inside the door before I even got to the stairs to take it to Calamity\u2019s room. Our room. She\u2019s right. It should be ours, some place to be safe. Together. And there\u2019s no point in me keeping that hole in the wall. Hopefully it\u2019s not in anyone\u2019s way. But I would have needed my hands free if there\u2019d been an intruder, instead of just the display of honorless bullying it had left. She was at the door while I looked around. I don\u2019t think she saw the skull fragments. I hope she didn\u2019t. The overt threats left on her bed were bad enough as it was.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve stood guard over her since then. When Insincere Marguerite discovered that the police were after her, she took the two of us into the Hedge through Lori\u2019s mirror, and broke it on the other side. I guess that\u2019s how the spineless wretch got in, through a mirror that had reflected Mary. It\u2019s been a quiet vigil, once Insincere Marguerite helped Mary to sleep. The only interruptions were when Julia showed up, to assure me that Calamity was alright and to curl up at Insincere Marguerite's feet, and then later when Calamity herself came over.<br /> <br /> She\u2019d driven Mary\u2019s car over a cliff, and was bruised, with a few chips in her glass shards from diving out of the car into the Hedge. It had gotten the police out of the picture for awhile at least. She left Jacob and De la Roche looking after Lori. It would be just like the sadistic craven bastard to try and kill off one of Mary\u2019s protectors, and Lori is the <s>weakest</s> most vulnerable of us. Those two should be able to keep her safe though. Insincere Marguerite and Julia went off to sleep here in the Hedge, so it\u2019s just me and Calamity now in Lori's Hedge room, both writing. I wanted to hold her, and check and make sure she's alright, but I can't now, while I'm running between rage and emptiness. I needed to get this down, but I don't think it helped. I hope her thoughts are easier than mine to put down on paper.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> I am so angry and frightened and devastated and sad and confused right now that I don\u2019t know how I\u2019m containing it all. I have experienced all sorts of desires since returning from the Empress\u2019 realm, some healthy and some obsessive, some venal and some pure, some open and some illicit\u2026 but until today, I can honestly say that I\u2019ve never had the unambivalent desire to <u>kill</u> someone before. Not the Stranger, not the Empress\u2026 not even Hunting Hawk.<br /> <br /> The evening started out well enough. I prepared for the show, my heart and mind full of D and thoughts of how I could tell her about my feelings for her in a thousand romantic ways. I spoke with Ace and Marguerite about changing my third set number, thinking I might be able to start getting the message across that way. Marguerite grumbled a bit about the last minute substitution, but she was able to make it happen in the end.<br /> <br /> Ginny stopped by before the show to speak with Calamity and Jacob. Apparently she and Chalcedony hooked up last night, and Chalcedony is sort of freaking out about it, and it\u2019s got Ginny worried. She\u2019s doing the classic love-struck thing where she\u2019s second guessing herself because of her partner\u2019s uncertainty. Based on Jacob\u2019s later phone conversation with Chalcedony, I\u2019d guess Ginny doesn\u2019t really have anything to worry about; her paramour is probably just freaking out a little over her first experience with another woman and trying to fit that new information into her existing self-image. I could hear some of what was said from backstage, and it is positively <u>cute</u> how Ginny\u2019s reacting to the whole situation.<br /> <br /> Calamity popped her head into the dressing room area just before the show started to let me know that Princess Jolie was in attendance. I got a few butterflies in my stomach at that, but mostly I was just glad that she felt well enough to show up\u2026 and that she felt good enough about our relationship to have the conversation she must have known was going to come.<br /> <br /> The show itself went well. My first number was \u201cHaunted,\u201d a dark and eerie tune from around the turn of the century by a band called Evanescence. An hour or so later, Gladys \u2013 one of the more talented mortal vocal artists we employ \u2013 sang harmony with me on \u201c