But there\u2019s another reason.\u201d<br /> <br /> She paused once more, and seemed to be gathering her courage. \u201cI don\u2019t think Doctor Twitch recognizes me. I don\u2019t think he\u2019s ever made the connection between the terrifying <u>thing</u> that chased him from Arcadia and the little darkling girl that showed up around the same time. I hear that he still has nightmares about it, and wakes up screaming in the middle of the night. I\u2019ve even heard people whisper that he\u2019s afraid that Maria is still coming for him. He\u2019d do anything to feel safe again, Lori, and he\u2019ll never feel safe as long as I\u2019m alive. So when I told you my first name, I was trusting you with my life in a very literal sense.\u201d<br /> <br /> I pulled her into a tight embrace. \u201cI don\u2019t care,\u201d I told her fervently. \u201cMy durance wasn\u2019t as terrible as yours, but I know what it\u2019s like to lose pieces of yourself until there\u2019s almost nothing left. So I don\u2019t care who you were in Arcadia, or what you did while you were that person. I love you, Maria de la Rocha, and nothing is going to change that. Now come on, let\u2019s go to bed. I\u2019m tired, but I don\u2019t think I can sleep without some serious cuddles first.\u201d<br /> <br /> We went back into my room, took off our clothes, and got into bed. We made love slowly, softly, and tenderly, and drifted off while holding each other and sharing sleepy kisses. And I cannot tell you how much I wish I could just stop writing now and say that\u2019s how the evening ended. I wish I could just wipe away the horror of the next few hours and move on with my life as though none of it had ever happened.<br /> <br /> No. That\u2019s not true. I sincerely wish it had never happened, but since it has, I never want to forget it. I never want to forget how that monster made me feel.<br /> <br /> D and I woke up a short time later to a series of piercing shrieks coming from down the hall. I jumped up, pulled on an oversized T-shirt and ran toward the noises with D close behind me. Mary was curled up in a ball outside of the guest room gibbering incoherently. She was obviously terrified of something, and kept pointing at the door to her room.<br /> <br /> Most of the others were out enjoying the night, but Gawain had come by to move some of his stuff into the Dream House (apparently he\u2019s given up his apartment and decided to move in with Calamity full-time, and I say good for him). He thundered up the stairs a moment later and asked if everyone was okay. Once he was satisfied that Mary wasn\u2019t actually hurt, he pushed open the door and we looked inside.<br /> <br /> Mary\u2019s clothes were there, on the bed. It was the set of clothes that was stolen from Glamour Springs the other day. Each article of clothing was pinned to the bed with a long knife. Her fetch had obviously been in the Dream House\u2026 and none of us had known. She\u2019d even left a note: \u201cyou are not safe here.\u201d<br /> <br /> Gawain went into the guest room to look around, maybe try to figure out how the fetch got in and out. He opened the closet door, and jumped out of the way as a bucket came swinging down at his chest. It was filled with blood, which splattered everywhere around the room. Gawain managed to avoid the splash, but the rest of the room looked like a slaughterhouse.<br /> <br /> I called Becky Wan to let her know what was going on, and Gawain called Calamity and told the others that they should come back as soon as possible (luckily they were all together, hanging out on a rooftop somewhere). I didn\u2019t want to contaminate the scene any further\u2026 okay, I admit it, I didn\u2019t want to go in the room at all. I was grossed out and more than a little scared myself. So I took Mary by the shoulders and led her gently down the hall, back toward my bedroom. I pulled on a pair of sweatpants and sat with her until she calmed down a bit.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sorry, Mary,\u201d I said when she\u2019d recovered some of her composure. \u201cWe weren\u2019t prepared for her to strike this quickly. We\u2019ll do a better job of protecting you from now on, I promise.\u201d Mary shook her head and made a token effort to reassure me that she didn\u2019t blame the motley for the night\u2019s events, but I could tell her heart wasn\u2019t really in it.<br /> <br /> Calamity and the others made it back in record time, and we set about deciding what to do about the situation. Marguerite started checking online with her phone to see if there had been any violent crimes in the area. After a few minutes, she turned very pale and showed us a police sketch of a woman who looked remarkably like Mary.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe police are looking for this woman,\u201d she told us softly. \u201cEarlier tonight, she killed and decapitated a child in front of her parents.\u201d I felt sick. The breath literally rushed out of me, and I had to sit down. I can\u2019t even begin to frame how that revelation made me feel.<br /> <br /> The next few minutes are sort of a blur to me. I know that Calamity called Lucien Torrez, who advised us to get Mary out of the house and somewhere safe as quickly as possible. He figured the police were probably watching the highway near the Dream House. Calamity checked, and Mary\u2019s car was parked in our lot, even though we\u2019d left it at her apartment the day before. She started talking with him about ways to get rid of it, but I could barely hear her over the rushing sound in my ears.<br /> <br /> I came back to myself as Marguerite was running her hand over the guest room mirror. \u201cSomeone entered the room through this mirror,\u201d she said with a frown, \u201cand left the same way. It is similar to a power I possess, but I can only step through mirrors in which I have been reflected.\u201d<br /> <br /> Calamity thought about that. \u201cMaybe Mary\u2019s fetch can step through mirrors that have reflected <u>Mary</u>,\u201d she guessed. That brought us up short; Mary\u2019s been pretty much everywhere in this house.<br /> <br /> Marguerite thought for a moment. \u201cI can take Mary and one other through to the Hollow with my power,\u201d she said. \u201cShe has never been there before. We can then break the mirror we step through and cover the other mirrors in the Hollow before Mary sees them. She should be safe there.\u201d<br /> <br /> Gawain offered to go with them, and the rest of us began the unenviable task of cleaning up the guest room. So that was how I found myself in a ratty T-shirt and sweatpants, on my knees, scrubbing blood off the floor at three o\u2019clock in the morning. I tried to hide how all of this made me feel, but I couldn\u2019t stop the tears from running down my cheeks every time I came across a tiny fragment of bone or a strand of hair stuck to the floor. More than once I felt like I was going to vomit, but I managed to keep my roiling stomach under control through sheer force of will.<br /> <br /> Jacob was taking care of the rest of the room, getting rid of the sheets and the area rug and anything else that couldn\u2019t be easily cleaned. I also saw him surreptitiously trying to get rid of some of the larger bone fragments\u2026 presumably so that I wouldn\u2019t have to. It was a sweet gesture, and I love him for it\u2026 but there was only so much he could do.<br /> <br /> When the room was once again vaguely presentable I stumbled downstairs to wait for Becky and Mr. Torrez. Calamity was looking out of the front windows. \u201cWe need to get rid of that car,\u201d she said slowly. \u201cLucien said it would be best if we could drive it off a cliff into the ocean, and I think I might have a way to make that work.\u201d She turned to look at me. \u201cAlso, there appears to be a letter crawling up our driveway toward the front door.\u201d It\u2019s a measure of how shell-shocked I was that this remarkable pronouncement didn\u2019t faze me in the slightest.<br /> <br /> When the letter got to us we opened the door, and I discovered much to my surprise that it was addressed to me. Calamity picked it up, and a number of tiny spiders scuttled away from us. It therefore came as no surprise that the letter was from Madame Spidertoes. \u201cMs. Grace,\u201d it read in a thin, elegant hand, \u201cthank you for speaking with me earlier this evening. I apologize for my rudeness.\u201d I had to smile at that, even in the midst of everything that had happened. The fact that she felt the need to apologize for a conversation I initiated was oddly charming.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m going to take Mary\u2019s car,\u201d Calamity said. \u201cDon\u2019t worry, I have a plan. I\u2019ll be back in two shakes.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCalamity,\u201d I said, gripping her wrist and struggling to keep the fear and sorrow out of my voice, \u201cbe careful.\u201d<br /> <br /> But I had to say more. I know that of all my friends, I\u2019m the one who\u2019s least prepared to deal with violent bullshit like this. I know that Mary\u2019s fetch is the most dangerous, most monstrous thing we\u2019ve faced so far. And I know that Calamity, Gawain, Jacob and the rest will need to focus all of their attention on dealing with this threat. They can\u2019t afford to coddle or protect me; a distraction like that could cost them their lives.<br /> <br /> I let the depression drain out of me and replaced it with the only other emotion I could summon at that point: cold, pitiless rage. I put as much of it as I could into my next five words. \u201cThis bitch needs to die,\u201d I said.<br /> <br /> Calamity pulled back from me a little at that, but then leaned in and kissed my forehead. She patted my hand gently. \u201cIt will, Lori,\u201d she said softly, \u201cI promise.\u201d Then she strode out the front door, bold as you please, and walked to Mary\u2019s car.<br /> <br /> D and Julia stayed pretty close to me after she left. Mr. Torrez and Becky showed up not long after that. Not together, of course\u2026 while Mr. Torrez was very pleasant to Becky, I get the feeling that my fellow Spring Courtier doesn\u2019t like him very much. Both were very supportive and offered helpful suggestions for getting through this crisis, and Becky offered once more to take Mary under her own protection, but Jacob and I told her that we could handle this situation.<br /> <br /> Jacob made drinks to order for everyone (well, everyone except Mr. Torrez, who asked for something called \u201cCrystal Pepsi,\u201d which we didn\u2019t have). I was almost finished with my vodka and tonic when Calamity returned, looking a little scraped up but exceptionally pleased with herself.<br /> <br /> \u201cI drove her car off the cliff on the Pacific Highway,\u201d she said, flushed, \u201cand I slipped into the Hedge right before it went through the railing. What a rush!\u201d I gave her a careful hug to let her know how glad I was that she was okay. \u201cJesus, Lori, you look terrible,\u201d she said softly as we parted. \u201cGo on upstairs, get some sleep. I\u2019ll make sure everything is squared away here.\u201d<br /> <br /> I looked over at Mr. Torrez, who nodded. \u201cYou shouldn\u2019t have any trouble with the police tonight, and if you do, I\u2019ll send them packing\u2026 oh, that reminds me. Do you agree that in this matter I am acting as your attorney, Ms. Grace?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAbsolutely,\u201d I responded instantly.<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you,\u201d he replied. \u201cNow, Calamity is right, you should go and try to get some rest. We\u2019ll take care of everything else.\u201d<br /> <br /> I looked over at D and Julia, who were hanging out together at the bar. \u201cWhat do you say,\u201d I asked D, \u201cyou willing to put up with me for a few more hours?\u201d<br /> <br /> D threw me a cocky grin. \u201cWas there ever any doubt?\u201d<br /> <br /> I turned to include Julia in the conversation. \u201cYou want to stay with us too, hon?\u201d I asked softly. \u201cI know I wouldn\u2019t want to be alone tonight\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Julia shook her head. \u201cI don\u2019t\u2026 but I should head to the Hollow and check on Marguerite. I\u2019ll see you tomorrow,\u201d she said. After promising that she would be careful, she took her leave.<br /> <br /> D supported me all the way up the stairs, and I just let myself sort of sag against her. All the energy just drained out of me as we made the climb, and she almost had to carry me down the short hallway that leads to my bedroom. Once there, we collapsed into bed without even taking off our clothes, and I just started sobbing.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know how long we stayed like that. If anyone else had been there, it would have been super embarrassing. I was bawling like a baby, and there didn\u2019t seem to be any way for me to stop. I couldn\u2019t help thinking about that poor little girl, and what that <u>creature</u> had done to her. It doesn\u2019t seem fair that a monster like that could be allowed to exist in this world. It doesn\u2019t seem right.<br /> <br /> I thought I had hated people before. I was wrong. Before last night, I never really knew what it was to truly hate someone with all your heart. If I\u2019d had Mary\u2019s fetch at my mercy, I would have killed her in a heartbeat, without hesitation or remorse. I still want her dead, and I still want to have a hand in it. And I hate her for showing me this side of myself. It seems a little clich\u00e9 to put it this way, but I hate her for taking away my innocence.<br /> <br /> D understood. I wasn\u2019t embarrassed to show her that side of myself, and she wasn\u2019t embarrassed to see it. She held me close against her chest as my tears soaked her shirt, stroking my hair and my wings and whispering sweet nothings to me for the hour or so it took me to cry myself out. \u201cLet it go, babe,\u201d she said, over and over again, \u201clet it all out. I\u2019m here.\u201d My tough, sassy Chicana girl was <u>so</u> <u>sweet</u> last night, and it was just what I needed.<br /> <br /> She must have stayed up for a while after I passed out. She\u2019s still there, lying on my bed snoring softly, as I write this. We had planned to spend the evening together tonight. I was going to take the night off from the cabaret, and we were going to meet this afternoon to do something <u>she</u> enjoys. We might still do that. But there are a few things I need to take care of first.<br /> <br /> I need to check on the rest of the motley, to make sure they\u2019re okay and that Mary is still safe.<br /> <br /> I need to visit the church. It might be dangerous if the fetch is still watching us, but\u2026 I need to make sure dad is okay. I need to see him and talk to him again.<br /> <br /> I need to talk to Mr. Torrez about getting a gun, and ask Calamity to show me how to use it.<br /> <br /> And I need to see what I can do about finding a way to cure Princess Jolie of her addiction to human creativity. That may be the most difficult thing on my plate, actually. I mean, we\u2019re talking about a trait that\u2019s essentially a part of her being; finding a way around that would be like trying to find a way to fundamentally alter the basic facts of her existence\u2026<br /> <br /> Oh my God. The table! I have to talk to the others right now!<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T02:01:17-08:00","id":307274,"title":"","content":"<b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> <b><u>Tuesday May 13<sup>th </sup></u></b><br /> <br /> When jumping into the Hedge from a speeding car as it goes off the rails of the Pacific Highway to escape from a high speed chase with police is the <i>second</i> most heart pounding thing to happen you know it has been one hell of a night.<br /> <br /> But I should start at the beginning. Tonight was apparently Calamity has important conversations and rides the emotional roller coaster night. It started simply enough, I caught up with Jacob before opening and drew him aside to talk. I told him directly that I'd noticed his injury and asked if it was from the briar wolves. He said it was and dismissed it as just a scratch. He's used to dealing with things on his own. I get that. I don't know a lot about his Durance but it seems it was a lonely and hardscrabble sort of place. And while I may not have ever lacked for basic necessities in Snow Globe, I was surrounded by enemies and on my own. So trust isn't a thing I believe either of us is familiar or comfortable with. But we're not alone anymore, either of us. That was what I was trying to get across and I think I did so without seeming to scold or accuse him. He did not seem upset, though as tough as he can be to read I can't be sure. But I believe it went the way I wanted it to. And we are intending to continue to spar, so perhaps he'll open up more to me at some point. I know first hand how badly it eats away at one to keep it all inside. Still not proud of how it happened, but I am glad I managed to confess to what I did that night in Bellevue. I don't know what he's guilty of but he needs to talk to someone about it. Maybe if we have less of an audience next time we spar I can at least make it clear I'm here and willing to listen.<br /> <br /> I was still musing on how to thaw out the Russian winter when the doors opened and people started to arrive. It was a very solid crowd for a Monday and we had a fair number of the Lost in attendance including Princess Jolie. I slipped backstage to make sure Lori knew since she has been quite anxious to speak to her monarch. Then I hit the crowd all smiles and charm and gracious hostess.<br /> <br /> Flores was there with julia and De La Rocha since the Rose and Thorn hasn't reopened yet. I did make it by briefly but didn't really stop to speak to her. Madame Spidertoes was in attendance with Moon and Dionisia. Also, I spotted Ginny and Davie both sitting alone and looking troubled.<br /> <br /> I started with the river ogress because she was actively waving me over. Apparently my advice to make a move earlier had been the right answer. She informed me that she and Chalcedony had engaged in amazing sex. I couldn't resist smiling at the look on her face, she is so head over heels. It is fucking adorable. Apparently she'd tried to call twice (exactly four hours and one minute apart, so as not to seem too desperate) and not heard back from the object of her obsession. She'd driven by Chalcedony's place and seen her car and lights on. She was concerned and flustered. I could see that she was honestly worried and I did my best to clam her down and assure her that it was most likely just that Chalcedony needed a little time to get used to the idea of being in a relationship with another woman. I pointed out that she, like far too many others, is still a bit hung up on proper gender pairings and all that crap. I did also assure her that I'd have Jacob give Chalcedony a call and be sure that she was alright. By the time I left her table, I had talked her out of drinking herself sloppy and thinking she'd been dumped or screwed things up. Sweet Aphrodite\u2019s tits I hope for Ginny's sake my take on things is right. Because, damn, I think she's got it worse than Andromeda and that's saying something.<br /> <br /> Next stop on the heartache express was Davie's table. Sadly, Dr Calamity wasn't able to fix this problem. Apparently, during her appearance in court, Dark Kimberly had announced that she was moving in with Annika. This crushed Davie's hopes and dreams of them becoming a couple, which I guess I had furthered by taking them both to my bed the other night. But honestly, while I am fond of the boy, he is not the master Dark Kimberly desires. I took his hands and offered my condolences and did explain that from what I had seen Annika and Dark Kimberly truly did seem to fill a need in each other and they looked very happy together. He clearly cares about her as a friend as well so it helped a little, but I think the poor thing is going to be heartbroken for a while.<br /> <br /> Well, having spoken to the others I approached the table where Madame Spidertoes was holding court. I waited because I expected the conversation to take a bit. Okay, that and I was nervous that she would actually know something about Snow Globe... which she did. But I started with the shooting and what I'd found and asked for her advice. She did point out that we could not be completely sure it was the Goblin Contract, though it did seem to match up rather well. The one person she could think of that would know that contract was Tommy, but thankfully she did not seem to think he might be responsible. (Admittedly, mainly because she was sure he'd have gone about it differently if he was targeting either Kimberly or Flores or the club.) And no court would have reason to damage the club, so it seems likely to be a loyalist or agent of the Gentry trying to destabilize things. She then brought up the vampires. Seems the LA courts have a thing for hunting vampires. (I did NOT let myself look interested in that.) So it is possible, though unlikely, that they had something to do with this. But she told me of a vampire by the name of Dexter that she apparently has known for a long time. It seems he's running a metal club called the 'Mailed Fist' these days and apparently keeping up with the passage of time better than she is. She gave me the password to use to get a meeting with him and some advice on how to behave (including a statement of her trust that I would NOT do anything to damage relations with the vampires.) She doubts they had anything to do with it, but feels it would be useful to reach out and make sure as well as let them know we're not gearing up to do anything rash. I can tell that Gawain is not about to let me go play diplomat alone and I have a hunch that the rest of the motley isn't going to want to pass up a chance to meet a real live... er, undead... vampire.<br /> <br /> That settled, I drew a deep breath and dove into the next order of business. I asked her about Snow Globe. She mentioned briefly a manikin from there who had passed through the area a couple of decades back, and spoke at more length of an older changeling. A darkling that had been in Snow Globe when it was a pure turn of the century world untainted by the roaring 20's. This darkling, I didn't get a name, had strangled her fake family and arraigned the bodies to provoke the Whispering Voices as part of her escape. Apparently it did not upset Them but she still managed to escape. Unfortunately, she proved unwilling... no, unable to abide by the ruler-ship of the courts. Seems she took to strangling people and told the powers that were that she would rather die than be made to heel. And the Summer King at the time was willing to oblige. I cannot lie, the more she told me the more it made my gut clench. I made sure to point out that I was more in control, as much for myself as her. She said she would see if she had any journals or belongings since the girl was a darkling. I thanked her for that and took my leave.<br /> <br /> Gawain followed and without a word he wrapped me into a desperately needed hug. I sank into him gratefully and looked up and told him that he was the reason I was sane. He responded by telling me I was the reason he made it out of the hedge. I lingered there in his arms and let my own cling to his waist as we talked. He is truly the anchor that keeps me grounded and I love him so much it frightens me.<br /> <br /> And I <i>told</i> him so. Oh lords and ladies above and below I said the words. Out loud. I told Gawain that I love him. And he said it back to me. I... Oh fuck it just happened. We were talking and I was telling him that I could stop fucking around, that I would stop for him. And I told him it wasn't the same with anyone else. He said he understood but he seemed like he was trying to explain it and couldn't find the words to and... and I just...<br /> <br /> I pushed up onto my toes and looked him in the helmet and I told him it was different because I loved him. That I trusted him. I felt my heart racing and I knew that I'd crossed a line and I couldn't unsay it. But it doesn't matter, I meant it. I do love him. And he knows it. I said it out loud. I didn't think those words could come out of me but suddenly they just rolled off my tongue and now I wouldn't take that moment back if I could.<br /> <br /> And I told him how I don't understand why or how he can love a monster like me the way he does. He looked down at me and he got serious. Perhaps more serious than I've ever seen him. He told me how he remembers the killing and how there were times he savored it, enjoyed it. I knew he'd killed so many, but it is so easy not to think of when I look at him. I had not heard him speak of it like that before. I felt embarrassed and relieved both. He's not going to suddenly realize what kind of monster I am because he already knows and understands and he loves me anyway. Honestly, it was exactly what I needed to hear right then, even if it did make me feel ashamed for doubting him.<br /> <br /> Well, after that I talked to him about the bedroom. Told him how it mattered that it was ours rather than mine. I joked about getting him into this place and how he should move his stuff out of that hole in the wall apartment and truly make it ours. He agreed and decided to go and move his remaining things while I was off with Insincere Marguerite and julia enjoying the bell tower of St. Monica's Cathedral.<br /> <br /> It was a lovely night. The moon was nearly full and bright. Jacob joined us and my sister and her pet were so sweet together. Insincere Marguerite curled about and atop her girl while she was sketching and julia kept fretting about her falling off and asking her to be careful. I am pretty sure I was floating high enough that I could have stepped off there and never made it to the ground. I know it showed because Jacob snapped a couple of pictures with his phone. He told me he was going to send them to Gawain and I was just about to start actually posing for more when my own phone rang.<br /> <br /> It was Gawain and I answered it happily. What he told me brought the happy go lucky mood to a screeching halt. Mary's fetch had dared to trespass at the Dream House. Everyone was alright so I told him we would be back. I gathered the others and drove us back as swiftly as I could manage. We arrived to find the guest room covered in blood with Mary's clothes spread on the bed and pinned down with knives. There was a note informing her she was not safe here. The blood and skull bits had been in a bucket set atop her closet. Insincere Marguerite informed us first that the police were hunting a murderer that had decapitated a child in front of its parents and that the damned thing had used the mirror to enter the room.<br /> <br /> She then went and took Gawain and Mary to the Hollow. I called Becky to let her know what was happening and then as he was the only one I could think of with experience dealing with the police I called Lucien. He agreed to come and be ready in case they showed up. He also was able to trace the serial number on the gun and confirmed it had been used in a shooting back in Kansas. We also spotted Mary's car parked in the lot below and I told him I would take care of it.<br /> <br /> In the midst of this, a letter crawled up the drive. Well, it was carried up the drive by a gathering of spiders. I do not know exactly what passed between Madame Spidertoes and Lori earlier, but she'd sent an apology. I was quite intrigued, but it was not the time to ask. Instead I took to the car (not surprisingly covered in more blood and the rest of the missing head) and I started it up. I was about to pull away when Becky arrived and I just flashed her a mad grin and told her I was off to drive off the cliff and I'd be back shortly. Yeah, despite everything I was riding the adrenaline pretty hard at that point. I mean, sure the situation was fucking horrible but how often do you get to pull off that kind of Summer Blockbuster action movie shit in real life? Even this crazy life? Not often enough, that's for damn sure.<br /> <br /> I thickened the darkness to make sure they couldn't get a good look at me and I tore out of there like a bat of hell. Right away I had a trio of cop cars on my ass and despite how well I was channeling James Bond there was no way I was going to outpace them for long. But I didn't have to. I got a ways down the road and then zigged when the road zagged. As the car tore through the safety rail, I opened the driver's door and leaped out. But I enchanted the doorway so I landed in the Hedge rather than the real world. In a flash, I left the car and the cops behind. I hit the ground fairly well and rolled. I still got some scrapes and bruises and I chipped a couple of my spikes rather noticeably but I managed to walk away from it so it must have been a good landing. It was a fairly short walk back to the house and I used the portal there to return.<br /> <br /> Lori was looking mighty damn ragged. And once I'd assured her I was alright, she looked me dead on and told me she wanted this thing dead. Her eyes told me she wanted to be there, maybe even be the one that put it down. It took most of the wind out of my sails to see her like that. I took her hands and promised her I'd see it done. Her lover took her up to bed and I watched them go, feeling a little sick. Lori's eyes aren't meant to have that kind of hate in them. It's my fault. I failed her. I'm supposed to keep this motley safe. I'm supposed to keep this house safe. I brought this upon us by bringing Mary here and I underestimated her fetch.<br /> <br /> But both Lucien and Becky were there so I turned my attention to them. Lucien was calmly handling things and busied himself with his laptop and tablet. So after offering him hospitality, I moved to the kitchen where Becky was avoiding him. I apologized for calling him without letting her know but she was alright with that. We talked a little, and I assured her that we were still alright guarding Mary. Maybe it was a bit of stubbornness but I will be damned if I'm going to throw in the towel and give up just because the fucking bitch got one over on me. That thing is going to die and I am going to be the one that ends it. I am going to win this game. We talked a little about fetches, and how McDonald's Farm seems to always mean either a seriously fucked up Changeling or Fetch. Becky warned me that the fetch would likely also be able to pull blades out of mirrors since she could move through them. I didn't keep my eyes from lighting up as I licked my lips. So it'll be a proper fight, all the better but in the end I am still going to dance on its fucking soulless corpse after I rip that fucking monster back into whatever collection of stray trash it was made from.<br /> <br /> Becky departed before too long. And Lucien reported that the police were focused on the car and not likely to bother us for a few days if at all. He mentioned working on finding a burned female body that could be used to fake Mary's death and headed out as well. At that point, I asked Jacob to look after Lori and told him I was off to the Hollow. I know De La Rocha is with her, but she's not part of the motley. Also, I wanted Jacob to be prepared just in case but I didn't want to seem like I was questioning his abilities.<br /> <br /> I got to Lori's bedroom in the Hollow and Mary is out soundly and thankfully peacefully. I guess my sister's chloroform did the trick for her. She was waiting up with julia curled up at her feet like a good pet and Gawain was standing guard with his sword. He looked a bit worried (apparently julia told him I was fine and prompted him to wonder why I might not be.) I assured him I was whole, nothing worse than a few chips. Insincere Marguerite and her left for their room shortly afterwords. I'd grabbed this journal and with everything a swirl in my head I wanted to go ahead and get it written down. I'm not sure exactly how I feel right now. I can't stop seeing that look in Lori's eyes. I am angry at myself. I was fucking careless. I brought this mess into our home and I fucked up. This is my fucking fault. At the same time, I am excited. I am going to kill this soulless bitch and I am going to fucking love every second of it and no one is going to question it.<br /> <br /> I'm restless now. I want to be hunting but I don't know where my prey is hiding. It won't be foolish enough to use the same trick again, even if it sees the opportunity so setting a trap for it isn't likely to work. I cannot let this thing keep the upper hand. I have to find some way to take this fight to her, to be proactive rather than reactive. I... Fuck, I am spinning my wheels. And Gawain is here, pretending to still be writing and waiting for me to finish this. He keeps looking over like he wants to say something but then looking away. This twisted mess is getting to him. Dammit, this is not at all how this night was supposed to end. I should be curled up with him in OUR room... in OUR bed... But everything had to go all pear-shaped. Hell, I'd suggest he try to sleep but there is no way he'd get any rest from the look of it and I can't do anything to banish his nightmares while I'm awake. Fuck, right now I would love to pounce on him and fuck this whole gods-forsaken shitstorm out of both our minds but I can't risk dropping my guard like that right now. But I can go to him. He needs me right now.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Okay, today has continued to be another of those \u201cwhat the hell is going on\u201d days. Well, it\u2019s technically \u201ctomorrow\u201d now since it is just before dawn. I figured what I wrote before would be the last thing I wrote for today/yesterday. How wrong I was. Right before the show Calamity came up to me while I was stocking the bar for the evening. She didn\u2019t really beat around the bush either. She expressed her concern that I was hiding an injury and that if I hadn\u2019t been up to something she didn\u2019t know about it was probably from the fight with the briar wolves. I admitted that I had been hurt, but that it was just a scratch and nothing to worry about. That wasn\u2019t the end of it though. She kept on about how there were people here that I could go to for help or healing and that I didn\u2019t need to suffer in silence. She also brought up the practical concern that if someone was injured and wasn\u2019t seen to it might become a liability should anything come up. I was quiet for a bit after she finished. I think I tried to reassure her again that it was just a scratch and nothing to worry about.<br /> <br /> The idea though that it concerned her enough that she took the time to get me alone made me think. I know that we\u2019re a motley and that we are supposed to look after one another. I guess I just had it in my head that I would be the one doing the \u201clooking after.\u201d Pretty much all of my experience with being wounded is that if you\u2019re not bleeding out then you\u2019re okay. I said that to Calamity, though in retrospect it might not have been as reassuring as I hoped. I think I wanted to convey that I was used to dealing with worse, but I\u2019m not sure that\u2019s how she understood it.<br /> <br /> I mean, Rook patched me up many times over the years, and I him. One or two of those times I\u2019m pretty sure I\u2019d be dead if he hadn\u2019t been there. He built a litter and brought me back to the Lady. Most of the time though if I could stand, walk and swing a blade I was good to go. I guess I was still in that mindset after the fight with the briar wolves. The gash I got wasn\u2019t pretty but it did stop bleeding and it didn\u2019t impair my ability to stand, walk or swing a blade. I guess it just surprised me that they noticed. Insincere Marguerite said something the other day, and Calamity tonight. I assured Calamity that in the future if I was injured, even if it was just a scratch, that I\u2019d seek help or healing. I will have to remind myself to do it though. Calamity admitted that she too was used to taking care of herself, but was adamant that neither of us had to do that now.<br /> <br /> In a way Calamity reminded me of Diane. She is more blunt than the young spring courtier, but she insisted on addressing the wound like Diane did before. I still don\u2019t think I deserve the kindness that Diane showed me, or the second chance that she offered, but I am greedy and so I took it. She offered me a way out, not knowing if I\u2019d go back to the Lady or not, but she let me go. I had thought before that Diane had just tended to my injuries out of sense of guilt since it was her motley mates that gave them to me. But now Calamity shows the same concern and she had nothing to do with the injury I sustained. I\u2019ll admit that it made my chest ache just a bit after she left to get dressed for the show.<br /> <br /> Later, early in the show, Ginny came up and talked to Calamity. She expressed concern for Chalcedony, who in her opinion was acting a bit \u201coff.\u201d Calamity assured the ogre that Chalcedony was probably just getting used to the idea of being attracted to a woman. She asked me if I could contact Chalcedony and make sure she was okay. So I sent her a text asking if she was alright. She replied that she was fine. I asked if she was planning on coming to the show tonight. She replied that she was not. That she had some things to work out first. I bid her a good night and let Calamity know that all was well.<br /> <br /> After the show Lorelei left with Princess Jolie. To talk I guess. I know she was worried about the Spring monarch. About that same time Calamity was talking to Gawain. After all of that some of us, Calamity, Insincere Marguerite, Julia and I went to the St. Monica cathedral and climbed to the top to sit on the roof of the bell tower. Julia wanted to sketch, Insincere Marguerite wanted to watch her sketch. The rest of us mainly enjoyed the view. Calamity had a goofy kind of grin on her face when she didn\u2019t think anyone was looking. Or she didn\u2019t realize that it was there. I guess the little talk she had with Gawain earlier went well. I snapped a couple of pictures with my phone and said I\u2019d send them to Gawain. She smiled and asked if I could send them to her too. She also said that while we were climbing cathedrals that Gawain was moving his stuff out of his old apartment and into the Dream House. He\u2019s been pretty much living here anyway, so it seemed like the next logical step.<br /> <br /> It also shows the amount of trust that Calamity has in our resident Knight. She is like me in several ways. She is used to looking after herself and not trusting those around you because in her experience there is no such thing as a genuine friend. I get that. For her in Snow Globe all the other \u201cplayers\u201d were essentially spies. Everyone spied on everyone else and sold them out for a prize. In the Lady\u2019s realm, before I entered her service, it was every person for themselves. I remember early on I tried to help those that I came across. The first time I helped a girl, no older than myself. We built a shelter together and tried to stay warm. When I woke up in the morning I found that she had stolen my flashlight, pocket knife and a couple small things from my pack that didn\u2019t really matter. Losing the knife had hurt though. I had lost the one tool I could use for food or defense. I took to carrying a walking stick with me and using it to fend off animals or people. Eventually, after much trial and error, I became proficient with knapping stone blades. They worked well enough to use for skinning animals I managed to trap.<br /> <br /> Despite that girl stealing my stuff I still looked for people. I had thought I suppose that since we were all in the same situation that they would help. I was so wrong. I\u2019ll never forget the day that those guys found me. I remember thinking that it was going to be my lucky day. Then I got hit from behind and it all descended into pain. They beat me down and stole my jacket, my gloves, my pack, everything. In payment, or mockery, one of the guys dropped his old worn out coat behind as they left me in the snow. I\u2019m being charitable when I call it a \u201ccoat.\u201d After that I didn\u2019t trust anyone. I think Calamity learned the same lesson. And it says a lot that she wants Gawain to move into the Dream House and share a room with her. I don\u2019t know if I can do that. Hell, I still sleep with a knife under my pillow.<br /> <br /> But all good things have to come to an end, right? While we were up on the roof Calamity got a call from Gawain. Apparently Mary\u2019s fetch had gotten into the house and left a little \u201csurprise\u201d for our newest addition. We got down from the roof of the tower and drove to the Dream House as fast as we could. We rushed upstairs to meet Gawain and others. He had gotten Mary out of the bedroom, but she was still upset. Lorelei was doing her best to calm her down and the rest of us looked at the scene. On the bed a set of Mary\u2019s clothes were lain out with knives at the wrists and a melon placed where the head would be, also impaled by a blade. Accompanying all this was a note that said \u201cYou are not safe here.\u201d And as if the note and clothes weren\u2019t \u201csurprise\u201d enough\u2026 when Gawain was investigating the room he accidentally tripped what normally might be a prank, but this time definitely wasn\u2019t. There was a bucket rigged to the closet door and when he opened it to take a look inside it fell, spilling its contents. In this case the contents were a good bit of blood, hair and skull fragments. Talk about fucked up.<br /> <br /> While we were taking a look around, we found out that the police were looking into the killing of a little girl in front of her parents. Actually decapitated the child in front of them. Messed up. At this point we talked to Torrez. Well Calamity talked to Torrez. It was suggested that he might be a good person to call since he has connections in the police department. He told us that the suspect they were looking for was Mary. Or at least the police sketch was a dead ringer for her. So it appears that Mary\u2019s fetch killed a little girl and set up this \u201cprank\u201d to psychologically torture the real Mary, with the added bonus of ruining her life as if that wasn\u2019t enough. It also turns out that the gun Calamity found in Mary\u2019s room was used in the shooting of several people a couple weeks ago. Anyhoo\u2026after the phone call Calamity, Gawain and I looked for clues. Didn\u2019t find much else except the fact that the door was not opened or unlocked from the outside. Insincere Marguerite is the one who discovered the most important thing, which backed up what we\u2019d found. Apparently she can look into a mirror and see what it \u201csaw\u201d so to speak. In doing so she saw the fetch climb through the mirror itself and set up the clothes and the bucket.<br /> <br /> Torrez did say that the police knew that Mary was at the Dream House and would likely be heading our way. We said we\u2019d get Mary someplace safe and clean up the room. He said he would head over to talk to the police when they arrived. After that we all got to work. Insincere Marguerite used her own mirror abilities to grab Mary and Gawain and head for the Hollow. Julia and Lorelei started cleaning up the blood on the floor, door, wherever it was. I grabbed a trash bag and started gathering up anything that could not just be wiped down. So, the bedding, clothes, bucket (and it\u2019s less liquid contents), even the area rug. I made a few trips in and out of the room and each time I came and went I looked over at the two girls cleaning up. They couldn\u2019t have been more different than night and day. Julia was calm and collected, actually rather stoic. It didn\u2019t look like it was fazing her all that much, but it could have been a mask. Lorelei on the other hand was an absolute mess. She kept cleaning, but she had tears streaming down her face in silent rivers.<br /> <br /> As if killing a little girl and terrorizing another wasn\u2019t enough to make me want to kill the fetch, bringing Lorelei to that state would have done it. She was absolutely wrecked. In some ways she had managed to maintain a kind of innocence about her. Not anymore. Nobody should have had to see that, not to mention clean it up. I started to reach out to give her shoulder a squeeze a couple of times but stopped myself before I did. I didn\u2019t want to disturb her and I have a feeling that trying to lend support at that particular time wouldn\u2019t have ideal.<br /> <br /> Calamity also called Becky Wan to let her know what was going on. Becky said she\u2019d be here as soon as she could. The rest of us continued cleaning and/or hiding things. I brought a trash bag and the area rug to the Hollow to store for the time being. Putting them in the trash is obviously not an option and just chucking it through the hedge gate probably wasn\u2019t a good idea. Who knows what could have found the stuff. Weird things happen in the Hedge.<br /> <br /> Just before Torrez arrived we discovered that Mary\u2019s car was pulled up in front of the Dream House. Now, I know it was left at Mary\u2019s apartment so it seems that the fetch decided to plant one more bit of evidence against Mary for the police to find. Calamity looked over the car and found the front seat had a good deal of blood in it and the rest of the young girl\u2019s head. Have I mentioned yet how much I want to take that damned fetch apart bit by bit? She It has gone to great lengths to ruin Mary\u2019s life. As if stabbing her when they first met wasn\u2019t bad enough. It then burned down Mary\u2019s apartment while leaving a gun \u2013 which is connected to a violent crime \u2013 in her nightstand. Tonight she kills a little girl and not only brings evidence here to frame Mary, she keeps going with the psychological shit. She It pulled that in our house. Now, either It\u2019s so focused on messing with Mary that It isn\u2019t paying attention to anything else, or it wants us to get involved. And unless it has friends or is more powerful than I\u2019m thinking It is, it wants to get massacred. Just saying. As soon as Gawain saw the scene he went quiet. He was being protective and a bit guarded by the time we arrived. Calamity was set on spilling the fetch\u2019s blood as soon as she found out what had happened. Well before she saw the room. The look on her face changed. The happy smile left and it was replaced by rage. Her eyes held more than a glint of bloodlust too. I will admit that I too have felt a desire for violence. I channeled my anger into cleaning up and making sure nothing could be traced to the killing within our home. Hell, even Lorelei expressed a keen desire that the fetch should die when we were talking downstairs. The look in her eyes mirrored the one in Calamity\u2019s to some extent, which was not something I ever thought I\u2019d see. It\u2019s not something I wanted to see either. She has ever been the voice of reason, of humanity in the group. I know I don\u2019t feel things the way she does. Honestly I don\u2019t know if I can. The same goes for Calamity. She feels things very strongly, whether it\u2019s anger or love. For me, everything is muted. There are the moments of sharp anger or affection, but it doesn\u2019t seem to last. People used to say I was cold, and I know they were not trying to make a pun. I was efficient and unemotional when I executed my duties for the Lady. I didn\u2019t really blink when I killed someone, unless I got blood in my eye. I just didn\u2019t think about it. I performed by duty, and I did it well. I try to make myself believe that I am better than that now. In some ways I think I am just a bit. The death of the little girl wouldn\u2019t have made an impact on me before, but now I am mad. I felt sorry for the girl whose life was cut short, and for the parents that will grieve, but mostly I just feel a desire to kill something. Is that progress? I don\u2019t want to kill in cold blood, now it\u2019s fueled by a desire for retribution.<br /> <br /> To be honest I didn\u2019t want to see the desire for violence in Gawain\u2019s eyes either. He comes across as such a sweet and somewhat innocent guy. I know that he\u2019s not without blood on his hands. I don\u2019t know how many times he had to play out the Green Knight story, but it was enough. He doesn\u2019t usually let that side show, but I could tell that he was angry and might possibly wish to inflict violence on the walking scrap pile. I do have to give him credit though. He was clearly angry and wanted to do something about it, but he stayed with Mary and Insincere Marguerite to keep them safe. Being a body guard is sometimes not the most exciting job, but it is very important and Gawain takes the safety of everyone in the House seriously. I admire him for that.<br /> <br /> Once we discovered the car in the driveway we knew that we had to do something about it. Torrez told us that there were three squad cars parked nearby, ready to move in if need be. One of which was a K-9 unit. That made me think that I\u2019d have to go back over the floor in Mary\u2019s room with a strong cleaner. It might make it obvious that something was cleaned up, but the smell of blood would be worse. Maybe we can repaint a couple of rooms upstairs and use paint and turpentine to cover the smell? Would also be a good excuse for pulling out old rugs and bringing new ones in.<br /> <br /> Anyhoo\u2026the car. We quickly thought up and shot down a few ideas on what to do with the car. In the end it was decided that Calamity would drive off as fast as she could and plow the little sedan through the barrier on the Pacific Highway sending the car and its supposed passenger to a watery doom. She planned to open the door right before she went over and create a portal to the Hedge using the open doorway as a frame. I wasn\u2019t keen on the idea, but Calamity insisted that she could do it. She also made the shadows a bit heavier in the car so it would be really difficult for the police to identify who was driving. I knew that Calamity could do it, and it did go off without a hitch, but I was still unsure that it was a wise idea. I didn\u2019t voice that opinion though. We didn\u2019t really have a better idea and I didn\u2019t want to sow any doubt in Calamity\u2019s mind.<br /> <br /> Calamity returned soon enough through the gate in the actual hedge and let us know how everything went. She stayed for a while after Torrez arrived. He mainly checked his tablet and phone while we chatted amongst ourselves. I tried to be hospitable and offer to make drinks for everyone. Torrez turned down alcohol, Calamity did not. \u2018Course, neither did I. I didn\u2019t let myself have more than one drink though. I knew that Calamity was going to go to the Hedge to be with Gawain and make sure that Mary was safe as soon as she was able to. By that point De la Rocha had already taken Lorelei upstairs to get some rest. De la Rocha is good for Lori. The way they look at each other is sweet, and they are so devoted to one another. It\u2019s good to have connections like that, someone that can understand you and fill a space that you cannot. Hopefully she will be able to comfort Lorelei and help her deal with the anger and horror I saw earlier. I wish I could let her un-see what was in that room. I would take that memory from her in a heartbeat if I could. Hell, I\u2019d take it from the lot of them if I could. Calamity would not thank me for it if I did though. Not sure that Gawain would be happy either.<br /> <br /> After a while it appeared that the police would not be making a visit to the Dream House. They thought that Mary went into the ocean with her car and were in the process of looking for a body. Torrez said something about finding a burned female body to use as a decoy for Mary. Something tells me that I don\u2019t want to think too hard on where he would or could obtain such a thing. Too late. Thought about it. Still not going to ask though.<br /> <br /> After Torrez left, Becky who had come by earlier also made her own way home. We assured her that we would continue to look after Mary and that it was no problem. I assured Calamity that I would keep an eye on Lorelei and De la Rocha so she could go to the Hollow. She nodded in thanks and took off. And so that\u2019s why I find myself sitting on a folding chair in the upstairs hallway. I don\u2019t think that the fetch would try for a second time today, but I wasn\u2019t about to take any chances. I have a good vantage point here and can see Lori\u2019s door and hear any noises from downstairs. When the others return I may see about trading out with someone so I can get some rest, but we\u2019ll see about that when the time comes. I am prepared to stay up if the need should arise. I\u2019ve done it before. I will make sure nothing gets by me while I\u2019m on watch. Anything that tries will meet my blades, and I\u2019m not in a very charitable mood right now.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> Looking back, I noted everything was probably going to go to hell, and I was right. Though it was not as bad as it could have been. Thankfully.<br /> <br /> So the show went well. Madame Spidertoes was in the audience, with Moon and Dionisia, and I visited her briefly. She seemed pleased to see I. Flores was there with De La Rocha and Julia, as her club has not yet reopened. I visited them a time or two also. Lorelei got to speak to Princess Jolie, but still seemed glum about it. Calamity spoke to Spidertoes and seemed pleased about it. It was a good night overall. Generally.<br /> <br /> I had planned on going to sit on the bell tower of the St. Monica\u2019s Cathedral with Julia so she could sketch nearby buildings and late night pedestrians. Julia has some awesome little black and purple, um, mini binoculars? I am unsure the English name. I could ask Gawain but would probably confuse him. Anyway, Calamity went with us invited earlier, and on a lark I asked Jacob, who also likes sitting on the roof of tall buildings, to come as well. They both seemed happy to do so. Calamity especially was in an excellent mood.<br /> <br /> I was as well. I wrapped myself around Julia, sitting on her shoulders some when she sat up or laying atop her as she stretched out on her stomach. I smelled her hair, and smiled. I looked at some of the dark, evocative sketches she had been doing and smiled again. I looked at my dear friends all around I and was content. Then Calamity\u2019s phone rang, suddenly.<br /> <br /> We were called back to the Dream House. It seems Mary\u2019s Fetch had been there, and as before had undermined her sense of security by defiling her room. Calamity got back with great alacrity, and we found her clothes were impaled to her bed with knives, and a bucket of blood, and scalp of a skull, had been rigged to dump on her from her closet. Gawain had discovered, and thankfully mostly sidestepped, the booby trap. Her bloody clothes were there as well. I frowned and checked my phone, and found her Fetch had decapitated a child in view of it\u2019s parents and fled with the head. The police had a suspect they were not commenting on, and there was a sketch of her, sans her large nose, naturally.<br /> <br /> Lorelei was had mostly calmed her but Mary was getting mentally unstable. Her eyes showed her Fetches campaign of psychological warfare was working, and she was beginning to crack. I checked the mirror in her room, and found her Fetch had, in fact, used the Mirror to enter and leave the room. That her Fetch can mirror travel deeply concerns me. It is not proper to use my mirrors in my house to travel. Those mirrors and this house are mine! I should\u2026probably not say that out loud. Definitely.<br /> <br /> We decided to take Mary elsewhere. The police coming was a threat, and her Fetch could strike again. I took she and Gawain through the mirror in Lorelei\u2019s room to her room in the Hollow. Once there, I broke that mirror. Regrettably.<br /> <br /> I laid out Mary to sleep with the help of some chloroform for her own good, and have been sitting, writing, and chatting with Gawain, who has been standing a vigil. A few minutes ago Julia returned, noting Calamity was okay and talking to Lucian Torrez, and that Lorelei had gone to sleep.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Calamity just got here. Apparently she drove Mary\u2019s car off the cliff on the Pacific Coast Highway while being chased by police and slid through the door into the Hedge. Lucian had determined the police were not coming and gone home. Becky Wan had come and gone. If we keep her from the mirrors Mary should be safe here. As for I, I am taking Julia to seem my room in the Hollow and leaving Mary to Gawain and Calamity. She is sleeping peacefully so it should be fine.<br /> <br /> Hopefully.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XVI</i><br /> <br /> Okay that was a long read, eh?<br /> <br /> Not a great deal to add. Mary\u2019s Clarity is plummeting, she has lost several points since this began. The PCs are more or less aware of this.<br /> <br /> A certain amount of mirror vs. mirror hijinx has ensued, with Insincere Marguerite and Calamity\u2019s powers being interesting foils for the fetch.<br /> <br /> Well there is a up there, so I am going to leave the ending discussion short, but Comments and Questions are absolutely welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T00:55:13-08:00","id":307972,"title":"","content":"Now I have read and own the core changeling book, but only one of the supplemental books. My question is are the rule robust enough to play a fetch as regular character? Could they keep up with changeling characters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T12:52:22-08:00","id":308464,"title":"","content":"Fetches are detailed more in Autumn Nightmares, and are playable. I'd definitely say the rules are robust enough. They would be nowhere near the power level of a Changeling, though, not having access to Contracts, Oniromancy, Talecrafting, Hedge-Spinning, or anything like that, as well as no Seeming, Kith, or Court abilities. They would have Echoes, but only a handful. Definitely a lower flexibility than a Changeling. But playable yea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-29T16:47:41-08:00","id":325644,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the delay, it has been a busy week with Holidays and stuff going on. <span style=\"font-size:10px\">Also, Dragon Age: Inquisition</span>. But here are the journals from the last Changeling game. Enjoy!<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Session XVII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> I guess it was about 11 when Lori rushed in. She was babbling, excited about something. She needed Calamity. I said I\u2019d watch over the still sleeping Mary, so the two of them left me by myself to guard. I asked Calamity to bring me back a whetstone. I kinda thought she\u2019d be back sooner than she was, but there were more important things going on, I suppose. I managed to stay busy, stretches and stuff, and to stay awake. Lori helped me with that, before she left, with a Spring Court trick.<br /> <br /> It turns out Lori, in addition to wanting gun lessons, wanted Andromeda and her Table to help her Monarch. Lori told us, in confidence, that the Spring Princess had a compulsion to feed on the creative essence of mortals and was both too weak to stop herself and too much of a coward to actually follow through on killing herself, despite feeling bad about it. Apparently, Andromeda thought the Table might be able to remove the compulsion.<br /> <br /> In more important news, Calamity had heard from Lucien that he was following a lead on the Fetch\u2019s whereabouts. He also had a warning for her, that sometimes damage inflicted on a Fetch was also inflicted on the Changeling it replaced. He had tortured his own to death despite this, with the help of a Spring Courtier. So Lori has remained behind as the rest of them, except Ace, go to follow the lead. Ace is guarding the two of them, Lori and Mary, now, and besides, he somehow doesn\u2019t believe that its current transgressions have earned it a death sentence. I am staying behind because Calamity can\u2019t stomach seeing me kill in anger. If this lead Gunnar found doesn\u2019t pan out, she\u2019s staying behind next time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> (later)<br /> <br /> It\u2019s over. Calamity was hurt, and Jacob and Insincere Marguerite. The Fetch is dead. Mary was hurt by that, but Lori stopped the death blow from being repeated on her. Flores and Andromeda came to help with the healing. I made waffles. To celebrate, even if I\u2019m not sure what. Flores and Calamity talked about business things. We\u2019re closed, tonight. No one wanted to perform, in front of outsiders.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s over.<br /> <br /> May 14th<br /> <br /> God, I\u2019ve been a dick in here for a bit. I think I managed to keep it in, mostly. I just hope I didn\u2019t make things worse for the rest of the motley. I am feeling kinda more, well, human now, you know? Still haven\u2019t slept. Maybe I\u2019ll just stop doing that. It\u2019s more trouble than it\u2019s worth, sometimes, you know? And cuddling with Calamity in our room, once I finally got all my stuff up there, watching an awesome TV show called Firefly and then the sequel movie, all at once, was a much, much better use of my time. Kaylee is super adorable, even if Calamity teased me a little bit about having a crush on her. I got to tease her about her crush on Jayne, or at least his guns, anyway, so turnabout was fair play, you know? I guess she couldn\u2019t sleep either. Anyways, after all that, even if I\u2019m maybe not all put back together, I\u2019m getting there at least.<br /> <br /> I need to make something epic for breakfast, I think. There\u2019s a Firefly cookbook on the Internet, maybe I\u2019ll find something from there I can put together with the stuff we have. Then we can put our heads together to find that Table for Jolie. It\u2019ll be nice to just help somebody, you know?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Okay, so I know at the end of my last journal entry I was super depressed, but excited because I thought I\u2019d finally managed to push a decent idea through my thick skull. Well, the last sixteen hours or so have seen both our fortunes and my mood improve dramatically\u2026 though I admit the motley has suffered a few lumps today as well.<br /> <br /> I gently shook D awake just after my epiphany. She blinked and gave me a sleepy smile. \u201cWhat\u2019s up, babe?\u201d she asked through a yawn.<br /> <br /> \u201cI have to go to the Hollow,\u201d I said quickly. She probably saw something in my eyes, because she put one of her hands in mine.<br /> <br /> \u201cEverything okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cEverything\u2019s fine,\u201d I said in what I hoped was a reassuring tone. \u201cI just had an idea, is all\u2026 something that might help Princess Jolie with her current problems. I need to talk to Calamity.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s great news, hon,\u201d she said with a sparkle in her eye. \u201cYou want me to come with?\u201d<br /> <br /> I kissed her forehead. \u201cI know you stayed up last night to make sure I slept well,\u201d I said softly. \u201cGo back to sleep, D. I\u2019ll be fine.\u201d On a whim, I leaned forward and gave her a real kiss. \u201cI love you, D.\u201d<br /> <br /> She blinked, but didn\u2019t balk at saying the words this time. \u201cI love you too, Lori,\u201d she replied.<br /> <br /> I smiled. \u201cGood, that\u2019s taken care of then.\u201d I almost giggled at her confused expression. \u201cI mean it, D, and I can\u2019t tell you how good it makes me feel to hear you say that, but there are practical considerations too. There\u2019s a monster out there who wants to hurt Mary\u2019s friends and protectors\u2026 and you saying that is the catch for my healing contract.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded in understanding. \u201cGuess I\u2019d better make sure I say it to you every day, huh?\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded and said \u201cit would make me feel better\u2026 for more than one reason.\u201d<br /> <br /> I took my leave after that, with D already snuggling down under my blankets, and made my way quickly into the Hollow. Gawain and Calamity were awake, though Gawain looked pretty ragged. I used the Contracts of Spring to siphon off some of his exhaustion and pep him up a bit before drawing Calamity aside. \u201cI need to talk to Andromeda as soon as possible. Can you contact her, or give me her number or something?\u201d<br /> <br /> She pulled out her phone and looked up the alien girl\u2019s contact information. \u201cAnything else I can do for you, Lori?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah,\u201d I said. \u201cYou once offered to teach me to shoot a gun. I want to take you up on that. Do you think Mr. Torrez would be able to get me a gun?\u201d<br /> <br /> She got a sour look on her face. \u201cI\u2019ll talk to him, see if I can get you something you can handle,\u201d she said after a minute. \u201cLook, Lori\u2026 I\u2019ll teach you to shoot if you really want me to. I think it\u2019s a good idea for you to learn how to protect yourself when I\u2026 when the rest of the motley isn\u2019t around. But this thing with the fetch\u2026 let us handle it, please.\u201d<br /> <br /> I gave her a look. \u201cI\u2019m going to do whatever I can to make sure she doesn\u2019t hurt anyone else,\u201d I said defiantly.<br /> <br /> \u201cI know,\u201d Calamity said in response, \u201cbut killing someone\u2026 even something like this fetch\u2026 that\u2019s something you can never take back. Once you close that door, it won\u2019t ever open again. I\u2019d like to spare you that, if I can. Let me handle it.\u201d<br /> <br /> I took one of her hands in both of mine. \u201cCalamity,\u201d I said softly, \u201cyou can\u2019t protect me from <u>everything</u>. It\u2019s sweet that you want to try, and I love you for it, but I\u2019m not a child. If it makes you feel any better, I promise that I\u2019m not going to go looking for the fetch\u2026 certainly not by myself.\u201d<br /> <br /> Calamity smiled, but it was a sad smile. Then she said something long and complicated that I think was the name of a kind of gun. \u201cOne of those would be perfect for you,\u201d she elaborated. \u201cGood stopping power, but not much kick, and small enough to fit in even one of your freakishly tiny stylish purses.\u201d<br /> <br /> The two of us made our way back to the Dream House after that, and I gave Andromeda a call. She was surprised to hear from me, but agreed good-naturedly to come over and speak with me when I asked. Forty-five minutes later she arrived, and I pulled her hastily into an empty room to talk. I explained the nature of Jolie\u2019s dilemma without using proper names or giving real details, and Andromeda listened carefully. The long and the short of our conversation is this: if we can find the Table and get it back into Andromeda\u2019s hands, she can use it to cure Princess Jolie. And she\u2019s willing to do so.<br /> <br /> It will <u>work!</u><br /> <br /> Most of the motley was back in the Dream House by this point, with Gawain keeping an eye on Mary in the Hollow. I told everyone that I needed to go to Glamour Springs, and they immediately started talking about who would come with me. \u201cWhoah,\u201d I said sharply, \u201cSpring Court business. No chaperones allowed, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> D took that as written as soon as I said it, and I felt my love for her blossom like a rose in my chest at how much she trusts me. The others were not so quick to do so. It took a good ten minutes of arguing before I got them to agree that I could drive to Glamour Springs and back by myself\u2026 a drive I\u2019ve made dozens of times before, I might add. It\u2019s like five minutes away!<br /> <br /> Anyway, I made the drive all by my lonesome, and Dark Kimberly waved me into Princess Jolie\u2019s office, telling me that I was expected. Jolie greeted me with a smile and asked me to sit. I guess she could tell that I was excited about something\u2026 though I wonder now if she might have had the wrong idea about what that was. \u201cSo, what\u2019s up, Lori?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s going to take some work,\u201d I admitted, \u201cbut I might have found a way to help you with your problem.\u201d She quirked an eyebrow in surprise. \u201cYou remember last week when I asked you about the Court\u2019s views on Andromeda\u2019s Table? Well, I spoke with her this morning. Without using any specifics, I gave her an idea of your situation, and she thinks that if we can recover the Table, she might be able to cure you.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jolie\u2019s eyes widened, and her face split into a cautious grin. \u201cThat\u2019s\u2026 Lori that\u2019s incredible!\u201d she said after a moment. \u201cI\u2019m not quite sure about\u2026 is there anyone else who might be able to use the Table, aside from Andromeda?\u201d<br /> <br /> I thought for a moment. \u201cMaybe Doctor Grey from the Winter Court,\u201d I suggested.<br /> <br /> She wrinkled her nose cutely. \u201cI think I\u2019d rather take my chances with Andromeda,\u201d she admitted. \u201cLook, I can\u2019t thank you enough for this, Lori. I know it\u2019s only a first step, but it\u2019s more hope than I\u2019ve had for myself in a long time. Thanks for justifying my faith in you.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled at her. \u201cLike you said, Princess, this is only a first step. I\u2019ll do whatever I can to locate the Table, but I\u2019ll probably need my motley\u2019s help. I know I promised not to tell anyone your secret, but\u2026 well, it might help speed things up if I can let them know what\u2019s at stake.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cIf you trust them, then you have my permission to share my secret. But please don\u2019t let it go any further than that.\u201d<br /> <br /> I dropped my gaze. \u201cThere\u2019s something else,\u201d I admitted. \u201cI need to talk to you about your offer. I\u2026 I\u2019m sorry, but I can\u2019t be your mistress.\u201d<br /> <br /> She looked disappointed, but not surprised. \u201cYour girlfriend, right?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cD would be okay with us having sex, if that\u2019s all you want\u2026 but she doesn\u2019t want it to go any further than that. She said she doesn\u2019t want to see me hanging on your arm at public events. It would hurt her, and that\u2019s the one thing I just can\u2019t do.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jolie took my hand. \u201cI understand. A relationship like that would almost have to go beyond the purely physical. I can\u2019t blame her for not wanting to risk what you two have.\u201d She sighed and turned away. \u201cLori, again, I can\u2019t thank you enough for what you\u2019re doing for me. But that being the case\u2026 maybe you\u2019d better go now.\u201d<br /> <br /> I kissed her hand and took my leave. I could <u>feel</u> her watching me as I walked out, and it was all I could do to suppress a little erotic shiver until the door closed behind me. Dark Kimberly gave me a wink on my way out, and we chatted for a few minutes. She seems sublimely happy with her new relationship with Annika. I told her I was happy for her, and I meant it\u2026 as far as it goes.<br /> <br /> I got back to the Dream House remarkably un-killed, much to the others\u2019 relief. Calamity said she had talked to Mr. Torrez about getting me both a gun and a license to carry, and he said it shouldn\u2019t be a problem, which is a load off my mind. It\u2019s going to take at least a few days, but it turns out that\u2019s okay.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d been pretty much convinced that my date with D was going to be called off due to homicidal monster attack, but much to my surprise, Calamity pretty much insisted that we make an evening of it. She did give D a look that clearly stated \u201cyou\u2019re-her-babysitter-for-tonight-now-don\u2019t-fuck-it-up,\u201d though.<br /> <br /> Mr. Torrez had also told Calamity that his people had found the apartment where Mary\u2019s fetch had been holing up, but she\u2019d left the premises. Calamity, Jacob, and Marguerite drove out there to check it out with Gunnar Friday. Though I was still in a funk about the fetch\u2019s actions, my progress with Princess Jolie\u2019s problem and the thought of spending a whole evening with D had perked me up somewhat.<br /> <br /> I got a call from Calamity about an hour later. Marguerite had looked into the few remaining mirrors at the fetch\u2019s apartment and it was clear that the creature had been going mad for several days. She described it having violent arguments with the meet in its refrigerator. She\u2019d later destroyed half of the apartment with some sort of explosive device (which was how the Summer Court found it in the first place).<br /> <br /> Gunnar had some sort of method he thought he could use to track the fetch; Calamity didn\u2019t share the details with me so I assume it involved some sort of icky occult mumbo-jumbo. In any case, he and my friends were going to track the fetch down, and asked that I stay close to Mary until the whole situation had been resolved. Apparently Mr. Torrez had a theory that there was some sort of sympathetic link between Mary and the fetch, so that whatever damage one of them suffered would also be visited upon the other. This made killing the fetch a worrying prospect, so they wanted to make sure I was on hand to use my healing contracts in case of an emergency. It turned out to be a worthwhile precaution.<br /> <br /> So a short time later, D, Julia and I were sitting in the kitchen of the Hollow House with Mary when she suddenly started screaming. Her skin began to redden and blister all over, and she fell over onto the floor writhing in agony. I rushed to her side and invoked my healing contract, which seemed to sooth her a bit. The damage kept coming, though, and a moment later she passed out. I invoked the contract one more time to ease her suffering a bit\u2026 but at that point she seemed to be out of immediate danger. Using the contract multiple times is really draining, and since it looked like Mary would pull through, I decided to save my energy in case my motley mates needed it.<br /> <br /> They needed it.<br /> <br /> Calamity got back first, carrying Insincere Marguerite in her arms. Both of them were really badly burned. Julia started screaming when she saw her lover in that state, and I sort of desperately snapped at D to get her out of the room so that I could work my magic. A few minutes later Marguerite was sleeping peacefully; still unconscious but no longer in any real danger.<br /> <br /> \u201cSit down, and I\u2019ll take care of your wounds too,\u201d I told Calamity.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s okay, Lori, I\u2019m\u2026\u201d she began.<br /> <br /> \u201c<u>Sit</u>,\u201d I said forcefully, pushing her into a chair as gently but firmly as I could.<br /> <br /> Once I\u2019d healed what I could, she got up and started for the door. \u201cJacob and Friday are still out there,\u201d she said with some agitation.<br /> <br /> I nodded, told D where I was headed, and the two of us made our way back into the world. On the way, Calamity explained what had happened. Apparently, the fetch had decided to destroy Mary and all of her protectors in one fell swoop, and take herself out in the process. She had created some sort of large chemical bomb and was in the process of setting it up near the Dream House when my friends found her. Jacob ran forward and tried to stop her from setting the bomb off, but the volatile chemicals caught fire and pretty much everyone was very badly burned. Marguerite ran into the flames to pull Jacob out, and succumbed to her injuries and passed out. Calamity and Gunnar were \u201cotherwise occupied.\u201d No, they won\u2019t tell me what they were doing or why they couldn\u2019t join the fight, but I assume it was important.<br /> <br /> Mary\u2019s fetch is dead. Mary herself would probably be dead if I hadn\u2019t healed the worst of her injuries as quickly as I did. I guess that\u2019s something to be proud of: I got to contribute to this important battle, but instead of committing violence, I saved an innocent life.<br /> <br /> When we got to the edge of the Dream House property, we could see smoke rising from the woods, but there was also a huge, dense storm cloud over the area, and it was starting to hail. I\u2019m guessing Gunnar had something to do with that, though I suppose it could have been Jacob; he has a real affinity for ice, snow, and other wintry weather. In any case, whoever summoned up the storm, it did an admirable job of putting out the fire before it could spread.<br /> <br /> Honestly, that fetch was willing to set a fire to a bone-dry section of Southern California woodlands with summer right around the corner! Doesn\u2019t she watch the news?<br /> <br /> Jacob wandered out of the woods as we were looking at the sky, looking about three inches from death but smiling and reveling in the unseasonable weather. One look at him was enough to let me know that I wouldn\u2019t be able to heal him properly without recharging my internal reserves\u2026 and some of the others were still in pretty rough shape too. So I pulled out my phone and called Glamour Springs. Dark Kimberly answered, and when I let her know the situation, she said she\u2019d send a few people over to help out.<br /> <br /> I waited for our guests on the front steps, and it wasn\u2019t long before Flores and Andromeda showed up. I escorted them into the Hollow, and they set about making sure everyone was ship-shape again. Julia, eyes red, held Marguerite\u2019s hand until she woke up, muttering darkly to herself in French. I caught a few words, something about a \u201cfucking stupid suicidal thing to do.\u201d After she\u2019d recovered, she, Julia, and Flores disappeared into one of the back rooms for a while, and I can\u2019t blame them.<br /> <br /> Mary\u2019s going to be leaving us now. We told her she was welcome to stay as long as she liked, but honestly\u2026 it\u2019s probably for the best that she\u2019s leaving. The Spring Court has people who can help her through the trauma she\u2019s endured. Sometimes the death of a fetch can have unpredictable effects on their changeling, I\u2019m told, and the Court wants to keep an eye on Mary to make sure she\u2019s coping okay.<br /> <br /> As things were winding down, I yawned and stretched theatrically. \u201cWell, I\u2019d better get back to the real world and grab a shower,\u201d I said in an offhand way. \u201cI have a date tonight.\u201d D looked stricken for a moment, and I couldn\u2019t stop myself from laughing. \u201cWith <u>you</u>, dummy,\u201d I reminded her.<br /> <br /> \u201cRight,\u201d she said, looking oddly sheepish. \u201cSo, want me to meet you over there in an hour or so?\u201d<br /> <br /> I gave her a meaningful look. \u201cYou can come with me if you want, sweetie,\u201d I said warmly. Turns out she <u>did</u> want. The shower was fun, but it took longer than usual.<br /> <br /> D still hadn\u2019t told me where we were going or what we were doing. This was supposed to be a night for us to do something she enjoyed, so I let her direct me when I was picking out an outfit. It wasn\u2019t a huge surprise when she told me to get punked out\u2026 but it did eliminate a night of Laser Tag as an option.<br /> <br /> We ended up club-hopping for most of the evening, traveling between various Santa Monica establishments, drinking a bit, and taking in a wide variety of musical acts. I can\u2019t even remember all the bands we saw last night: Love H\u00e4ndel, PFT, The Scraping Fangs, Zanzibar, King of Loud\u2026 mostly punk, but with a little variety thrown in here and there just for fun (The Scraping Fangs were unsurprisingly a fairly hard metal act, while Zanzibar seemed to be an unlikely fusion of rockabilly and zydeco).<br /> <br /> I had a blast, of course. I can usually enjoy music of just about any sort, and the fact that D obviously loves music too makes me unspeakably happy. Her hand stayed on my ass like it was glued there for most of the night, and we made no secret of our relationship as we moved from club to club. There was dancing (both with each other and with various temporary partners of both genders), there was beer, there was making out\u2026 all in all, a fantastic evening!<br /> <br /> We were closer to D\u2019s place when we decided to wrap things up, so we decided to crash there, and slept through most of the morning. I\u2019ve been up and writing in this journal for about an hour now. D\u2019s still asleep, with a tangled diaphanous white sheet pulled up over her, leaving one leg and one breast bare, like a priestess of Aphrodite. Look at me, getting all classical and shit!<br /> <br /> I love her. Yesterday I proved that in the face of Herculean temptation. She loves me; enough to drop her \u00fcber-cool tough-girl fa\u00e7ade and show me her jealous, vulnerable side. The fetch is gone, and Mary is safe. I have good, powerful friends who care about me and want to protect me from the monsters that lurk in the shadows. I\u2019m partial owner of a business in which I am allowed to sing as much as I want, and make people want me.<br /> <br /> Treasure these moments, Lori. Today, life is good.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-29T16:51:54-08:00","id":325646,"title":"","content":"<b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> <b><u><b><u>Wednesday May 14<sup>th </sup></u></b></u></b><br /> <br /> The gorram fetch is dead. Mary is not. Gawain is putting together a Firefly themed lunch from the internet and smiling again. That's enough that I don't even mind that the sun is riding high in a sky of shameless perfect blue. I am so glad that the damn business is settled.<br /> <br /> Standing guard over Mary last night was fucking terrible. Mind you, I can deal with tedium, but having to watch Gawain stewing like that and not being able to find a way to reach out and bring him back from that mood hurt. Give me a problem with a face that I can crave off and I'm great but for this I was fucking useless. And, of course, there wasn't a fight or anything to break the tension.<br /> <br /> So it was a fucking relief when Lori burst in. She looked better than she had the night before, which was good. She needed to talk to Andromeda for some reason. She had also decided she needed a gun and training to use it. Gawain agreed to stay with Mary while I went to put out some calls, since I am not prepared to risk dialing out from the hedge. Well, I told her I would teach her of course, because I do agree the girl should be better able to protect herself. But I did try to talk to her about being too eager to kill. I think she got what I was trying to say but she was firm that she was not going to let this thing continue. She was still angry but also calm enough to be rational. I'm glad she didn't end up having to be part of the actual kill this time, especially given how we hunted the damn thing down but once Lucien gets her the gun I am certainly going to show her how to use it properly.<br /> <br /> Jacob was still awake and watching the house so he caught some of our discussion. As Lori was talking to the little grey sweetling he and I spoke about him being part of the shooting lessons as well. I think the Glock we recovered from Mary's apartment will suit him. Especially since I spent the time between calls removing the serial number from it.<br /> <br /> Andromeda came to the Dream House and spoke to Lori privately. After that she left and Lori announced that she needed to go to Glamour Springs. That was fine but as soon as I started trying to figure out who was going to go with her to insure her safety she got indignant and pointed out it was court business. We argued. I mean it's not like we didn't know where she was going so having one of us ride with her wasn't a breech of court security. She refused to let anyone accompany her and in the end I had to let her go off alone despite the risk. It did not help my mood one bit to have her decide to be reckless and childish but I am not the boss of her and I think once she got it into her head that I was trying to tell her what to do she was dead set on not doing it. I sincerely hope I am not that fucking annoying when I'm being stubborn but I'm sure I am. Actually, considering that she didn't curse or threaten me, I would imagine I'm worse.<br /> <br /> She got back safe and sound (thankfully) and promptly called a motley meeting. Once we were gathered in the Other Dream House she finally explained what the hell the deal was. And oh what a deal it is. So, it seems the Spring Princess stays fresh and perky by sucking the talent out of mortals. And her infatuation with Queen Charlotte is based on some weird fucked up self destructive urge over what she's forced to do. And apparently Lori's got it into her head that the Table could remove this need from her and Andromeda thinks it can as well. Apparently Jolie is prepared to risk exploratory magical surgery for a chance to be freed of her appetites. I guess I can grok that shit. I mean, if my own rage and pain could just be cut out like a tumor I might give the magical Table a ride myself. Hell... I may have to chat with my little space girl about the possibilities when I get a chance. Of course, this is all well and good but without the actual fragging thing in our possession it's about as useful as a promise from Loki. And the subject of our lack of leads closed that meeting on a sober note.<br /> <br /> So, while that was going on, I was also playing a bit of phone tag with Lucien Torrez. Started with the call to him about securing a gun for Lori. He agreed with me that the North American Arms Black Widow would suit her well. Range is a bit short and it could have more power but it's small and easy to use and conceal which is important if Lori is going to keep it hidden in one of her tiny purses (or tucked in a garter belt... fuck that would be hot. Maybe I can talk her into that..) If it looks like she's going to use a handgun with more frequency, we'll see about something a bit larger for situations where we're more interested in being loaded for bear than subtlety. Maybe a Colt Ladysmith. It's a nice little .38.<br /> <br /> He seemed concerned that her being armed might be more of a risk in some cases and he's right. Most folk are less inclined to shoot a pretty girl that's unarmed than one with a gun, but I think she needs to be ready to protect herself in a pinch (like oh maybe when she decides that while being stalked by a crazy fetch is the time for jackass teenage rebellion flashbacks...) He said he would look into it, but obviously the fetch was the priority.<br /> <br /> And on that front, his people had a lead. It turned out a bit later that they were right but that the fetch had abandoned the apartment and left it booby trapped with explosives. While Gunnar was going over the wreckage, he asked if we wanted to see what we could turn up. I suggested that Insincere Marguerite go since she could use the mirrors. Jacob went along to help keep her safe.<br /> <br /> When Insincere Marguerite called from the apartment, she told a pretty grim tale. The fetch was out where the buses don't run. Like rocking herself back and forth while muttering and getting into fights with the meat products crazy. She was also nowhere to be found and had not left any leads in her wake.<br /> <br /> Just after we spoke to her, Gunnar called me and I spoke to him discreetly. He'd gotten authorization to use the 'black card' which meant any means was on the table to stop the bitch. And apparently any means involved ripping the soul of the child she'd murdered back from the Underworld and using it to hunt her. He needed a bit of the body to do it. I told him I could provide that. I told Lori to stay close to Mary, telling her we had something to try and implying that it might get dicey if we found the fetch. I spoke to Gawain and I told him I needed him to stay behind. I don't think he would have batted an eye at how we were going to track the fetch right then and I couldn't watch that. Plus I did not want him to have to carry that fucking baggage later. No, this was a monster only party. And so, a few minutes later (he'd left after Jacob and Insincere Marguerite but got to the Dream House ahead of them) I met Gunnar with the skull fragments and some restraints (yes they were meant for sex but I can vouch that they do work. I haven't had a worm wriggle free of them yet and I have certainly given a couple of my toys motive to try.) Before we could leave, Jacob and Insincere Marguerite pulled up. I tried briefly to get them to stay as well but they weren't going to have it. And while I really would have preferred to be the only one privy to the fucking soul abuse I think they can handle it. I hope so at least. I do not believe Gunnar was joking about the whole 'I'd tell you but then I'd have to kill you' routine.<br /> <br /> And it wasn't just that we were ripping a soul back from beyond rather than working with a ghost that had remained. That was some seriously messed up shit Gunnar was working. Way above what I know occult wise but I caught just enough to know that was some fucking Lovecraftian grade shit man was not meant to know. I don't think either of the others grasped just how not okay the ritual was (you know, as if dragging a dead child back from beyond screaming wasn't bad enough) It was a seething mass of hate and pain and fury once it appeared and it made the hair along my neck stand up watching it as Gunnar wrestled it into a binding.<br /> <br /> Well, once he'd firmly convinced it that it did not get to ride the Calamity express to vengeance town, it took off and we followed. It made a beeline back the way we'd come and before long we were getting way closer to the Dream House than I liked. Sure enough, when we found the crazy bitch, she was clutching a pair of chemical jugs that she was clearly planning to use to blow up the whole fucking Dream House to try to get to Mary.<br /> <br /> Jacob dove in first, trying to wrestle one of the jugs away from her. Unfortunately, it spilled as they both lost control of it and the contents burst into fire as soon as they were exposed to the air. Before any of us could act, the fucking bitch slammed the other container into the pool from the first and caused an explosion.<br /> <br /> Even before I could see or was sure if I was still able to I heard Insincere Marguerite screaming. It was a horrible sound. Dammit, I'm the one that\u2019s supposed to deal with stuff like this. I know how to take the pain. Worse yet, the first thought that crossed my mind was that if she was able to scream she was still alive. And as long as she was alive, Lori could heal her. I hoped that Lori had been able to keep Mary alive through the burning and explosion but right then I had more serious things to deal with. I blinked my eyes open and saw Jacob was still on his feet somehow. (Elementals are tough like that) I almost went for him, but the fire was still surrounding him and I was barely holding it together. Nothing good to be gained from having us both wind up burning to death. Plus I spotted the headless ghost pulling up a rather substantial rock and howling at Gunnar, who was looking as ragged as the rest of us. (Yeah, don't ask me how a thing with no head howls. It's fucking ghost shit) I recalled the exorcism ritual we'd been shown for the house ghost and I started chanting. That got her attention and we were locked into a battle of wills. Man, I could feel the fury in that little thing. While I was locked in spirit combat, Insincere Marguerite decided to rush into the fire to try to pull Jacob free. I couldn't divert enough attention to even call out for her to stop. The burns proved too much for her, but she did pull him mostly free and he managed to stop, drop, and roll the flames out. As the poor child faded (I really need to catch up with Gunnar and confirm that she went back where she belongs. If she's still out in the woods, that will need to be dealt with) Gunnar was calling upon the Autumn and called for us to take cover I think, but I was focused on my Darkling sister. I rushed to her and could see that she was badly hurt but breathing. I scooped her into my arms and took off for the Dream House at a run as it began to hail.<br /> <br /> I barreled through the gate to the Other Dream House and rushed in screaming for Lori. She was looking pale before she saw us, no doubt keeping Mary alive had taken a lot from her. Poor julia started to lose it as soon as we entered. Lori asked De La Rocha to take her out of the room and promptly set to mending Insincere Marguerite. Once the touch of Spring had the worst of her injuries cleared away I relaxed a little. Lori turned on me and started to push me into a seat but I tried to wave her off. She was having none of it until I managed to get out that Jacob was worse off than I was and that he'd been right behind me but wasn't here.<br /> <br /> I was feeling it for sure at that point. The immediacy of combat and the surge of panic at seeing Insincere Marguerite so badly hurt had passed and the pain of my own burns and lacerations was kicking in. I could feel the familiar grinding of a fractured bone in my left leg but I just gritted my teeth as I followed after her and headed back toward where the fight had happened. I'd walked to school with worse back in Snow Globe. We found Jacob walking back slowly, more to savor the freak cold hailstorm than from diminished ability to move I think. Lori muttered something about him actually being worse off than I was and went to him and laid on hands.<br /> <br /> For my part, I allowed myself to start to drift a little at that point. Everyone was safe so I found my way to a seat in the Other kitchen and leaned into the wall of Gawain that materialized at my side. Flores and Andromeda arrived a little later, called by Lori I believe. Once it was safe to move me without anything falling off Gawain had me up and in his lap. I curled up like a kitten. There was a bit of banter and some explaining what happened. Flores started to cozy up to Insincere Marguerite and julia while Andromeda ducked out as things started to get friendly. Lori went up to shower and get ready for her date night with her lady. They were both looking delicious when they returned later before leaving. They never came home, so I guess they ended up at De La Rocha's apartment.<br /> <br /> Driving a car off a cliff and getting blown up in the same twenty-four hour span was enough excitement for even me and I told Gawain as much. I got him to take me up to our room and I broke out the boxed set of Firefly and the Serenity movie that followed it. I picked it up a bit back after looking into what I had missed while I was gone. The internet assured me this was the best thing to ever grace a television screen. I am not sure about that, but it is a damn entertaining show and it was exactly what Gawain and I needed last night I think. I remember being in the sort of dark place he was and the best thing he did for me was to just be there and let me come back as and when I was ready to. Still, it's fucking hard to be on the other side of that but I did. I curled up with him and we watched. And before too long we were joking a bit and I teased him about having a crush on Kaylee, which prompted him to suggest I had an eye for Jayne. To which I say that he can have that name and I do not have a crush on him. Vera maybe...<br /> <br /> And by the time we'd finished watching, it was getting toward the usual brunch firstmeal whatever. Gawain is closer to his usual self which makes me happy to see. He is a little frustrated that he didn't play more of a role in saving Mary and he's interested in doing something to help her recover from the whole ordeal to make up for it. He's a good man that way.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Well today was basically a continuation of yesterday. And considering I didn\u2019t sleep it just feels like one really long day. One really long, really shitty day. Don\u2019t get me wrong, there were some nice aspects to the day. The Fetch is no longer an issue, which is nice, and I got to feel hail on my face again. I always seem to remember the bad things about the Lady\u2019s realm. The bone numbing cold, the pain\u2026everything else. Maybe it was just because I\u2019ve been living in this entirely too warm state for too long, but the hail and rain felt really good on my face. It might also have been due to the fact that I had second and probably third degree burns over a good bit of my body. That was not fun, but the rain felt nice. I\u2019m getting ahead of myself though, aren\u2019t I?<br /> <br /> So, in the beginning, of the day anyway, Lorelei rushes out of her room and out the door to talk to Calamity like her ass is on fire. Okay\u2026maybe not the most accurate way to describe it, but I\u2019ve got fire on the brain right now. Anyhoo\u2026she goes to talk to Calamity who then calls, or gives her Andromeda\u2019s number \u2018cause the little alien girl was here when I got out of the shower. Lorelei seemed excited about whatever she had talked to Andromeda about and told the rest of us that she needed to go to Glamour Springs. Calamity insisted that someone go with her since we didn\u2019t know if the Fetch would target us individually or not. Lori insisted that it was court business and she would be fine on her own. The argument went on a bit, but she stayed firm. Figuring that she wasn\u2019t going to relent, I talked to Insincere Marguerite off to the side and asked if she could follow Lorelei to make sure she was safe. Insincere Marguerite agreed that it was a good idea and slipped out to hide in Lori\u2019s car. As Lorelei was leaving I offered her an apple for the trip, hinting that the ability she has to make you feel rested would be appreciated. It was. I think she did the same for some of the others. Those of us that didn\u2019t sleep anyway.<br /> <br /> Before Lorelei left for Glamour Springs, she asked Calamity if the Darkling could teach her how to shoot, and possibly get her a gun. Calamity said that she would talk to Torrez about the gun and said that she\u2019d be happy to give Lori shooting lessons. A bit later Calamity also asked if I knew how to shoot. I admitted that I had fired a rifle a few times, but had no experience with handguns. She asked if I would be interested in learning how to shoot as well. I said yes. How can I not? She also offered me the Glock that she found in Mary\u2019s apartment as a weapon for me to use. I\u2019m pretty sure that the recoil on that thing won\u2019t be too bad. Probably wouldn\u2019t work for Lori. Her wrists are more delicate and I\u2019m not sure if the kick-back wouldn\u2019t be too much for her to fire comfortably. She could probably shoot it without hurting herself, but it wouldn\u2019t be easy. So, I said I\u2019d be happy to take the Glock. I guess once things calm down Calamity will show us how to safely use the damn things.<br /> <br /> While Calamity was on the phone with Torrez however he did mention that he had a possible lead on the Fetch. He also said he\u2019d do what he could to find Lorelei a gun, but that it might have to take second place to finding the thing that was threatening the Freehold. Lori was fine with that. What none of us were too keen about was his next tidbit of information. Apparently in a lot of cases whatever damage is inflicted on the Fetch will also appear on the Changeling. Not sure if it works the other way around. If so, that little brat in Portland just had one hell of a bad day! Ha! Nope, sorry\u2026can\u2019t feel bad about that. Anyway, this changed our plans on how we were going to deal with the Fetch once we found it. Our original plan of slicing and dicing until there wasn\u2019t much left wasn\u2019t really feasible if the same thing would happen to Mary. None of us wanted to hurt her.<br /> <br /> This connection is not always there, but seems to be a good bit of the time. Torrez himself tortured his fetch to death and had a Spring Courtier nearby to heal him when necessary. I\u2019m not sure what the fetch did to deserve such a fate, but Lucien doesn\u2019t seem to be the type to suffer from guilt. All this made me wonder what I would do if my fetch came after me. The quick and easy answer is that I\u2019d kill it. The downside to that is, annoying though he is, Elena still thinks that he is her brother. It would hurt her to lose him, and I don\u2019t want to hurt my sister. But as has been evidenced by the experience of others, one\u2019s fetch is not always crazy, murderous, or hell bent on destroying the original. Here\u2019s hoping the mopey emo kid in Portland stays there.<br /> <br /> Lorelei came back within a short time and said that we needed to have a \u201cMotley meeting\u201d in the Hollow, and that she had something important to tell us. She stressed that this information could not be repeated, to anyone. We all agreed. Then she told us that Princess Jolie feels compelled to feed on the creativity of mortals. Something like a Rusalka, but not quite. More like an Irish Bean Sidhe, or is it Leanne Sidhe? Anyhoo\u2026Lorelei went to talk to the Princess this morning because she had the sudden inspiration that the Table that Andromeda\u2019s keeper lost might be able to cure the Princess of this compulsion. It seems that the compulsion has been taking its toll on Jolie lately, and that she has been less careful with her health and wellbeing that she would normally. Apparently she came close to dying after an evening with Queen Charlotte. All consensual I\u2019ve been assured, but it still left her near dead. She told Lorelei that she doesn\u2019t want to die, but that she is tired. I don\u2019t have a compulsion like she does, but I can understand how something can just drag on you until don\u2019t think you can handle it anymore. After those assholes stole my stuff, beat me and left me for dead I reached that desperate point where I didn\u2019t really want to die, but living was getting so much harder to do. So I get it. And if the Table that so many people have been looking for can cure her of the compulsion that is making her so miserable, it\u2019s got to be a good thing, right? So, it sounded good to the rest of us. We decided that once we got the Fetch business straightened out then we would renew our search for the Table.<br /> <br /> After that little revelation we all went back to the House and went our separate ways until we got some word on the whereabouts of the Fetch. Gawain seemed really angry and headed straight for the forge. I decided to follow him. I don\u2019t think I\u2019ve ever seen him so pissed off in the entire time I\u2019ve known him. Granted that isn\u2019t all that long, but still. He is usually so laid back and friendly. Seeing him like that was a bit disturbing to say the least. I resolved myself to trying to help calm him down, or failing that, distracting him. So, as he worked at his forge I asked what he was working on. The one word response was \u201cknives.\u201d I started asking questions I\u2019d always wondered but have never asked, like how to you make the weapon take shape, why do you alternate between heat and cold, how you get a stronger or sharper edge, etc\u2026 Unfortunately my plan didn\u2019t work all that well. He answered my questions but the answers were short and terse, and his level of tension didn\u2019t really change. I tried to express to him that if he needed something or someone to talk to I was there. That\u2019s what friends are for.<br /> <br /> And it struck me in that moment that I do consider him a friend. I\u2019m not sure when that distinction switched over in my head, but it has. I\u2019ve only known these people for two and a half weeks (give or take a day or two)? And in that time I\u2019ve played Truth or Dare, hunted Briar wolves and tracked a deranged fetch into the woods with the intention of murdering it and suffering third degree burns for the effort. And the last one was all for a girl (Mary) that I barely know, and for the pain it caused my Motley mates. I mean, the thing was a menace, it had to be taken down. I suppose I would have hunted the thing to keep the freehold safe, but this felt more personal. To see Lorelei\u2019s innocence pouring out with her tears, and Gawain\u2019s anger and frustration pounded into the metal he forged made something shift inside my chest. I got angry that it hurt my friends. They\u2019ve suffered enough, and I didn\u2019t want to see them suffer any more. They don\u2019t deserve that. None of them. Calamity and Insincere Marguerite are not innocent, I know that, but I still didn\u2019t want to see the anger on their faces. The rage in Calamity\u2019s eyes. The pain written on Marguerite\u2019s face when she got burned.<br /> <br /> I guess I just associate the word \u201cfriend\u201d with trust, and I think that I have come to trust this colorful band of misfits. At least in some ways. In a fight I trust them not to stab me in the back. I know, that doesn\u2019t sound good just written out like that, but that really is a compliment. I learned from hard experience to only ever rely on myself because regardless of shared hardships, or perceived friendship, everyone will betray you. Everyone has a price. Something changed in me though. I have fought back to back with Calamity and didn\u2019t really worry about her \u201cslipping.\u201d Hell, I\u2019ve sparred with her using live steel, and there was no apprehension. It was just fun. I\u2019ve even slept with a girl that can pretty much be invisible. Insincere Marguerite could backstab me with ease if she so desired, but I don\u2019t think she will. And after today, I\u2019m pretty damn sure that she wouldn\u2019t do that.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s levels of trust though. I trust my motley to not physically attack me, and not just because of the Motley Pledge. I don\u2019t think they would have someone else do it. Probably. I will admit to being worried about their reactions if when they find out about my past loyalties. I mean, right now I\u2019m lying to them about who I am. Mostly. I should probably feel bad about that, but I really can\u2019t. For the moment I have friends. I trust them in a fight, and I trust them enough to leave my bedroom door unlocked at night. That\u2019s a lot coming from me. A damn lot. But if they find out about the real me? Whatever happens I can\u2019t blame them for it. Based on past actions I am a danger to the community. I am a liability. I know that, and I know what will likely happen if my past comes out. I guess I just want to push that unhappy day back as far as I can.<br /> <br /> Damn I\u2019m maudlin today\u2026..<br /> <br /> On to the \u201cmain event,\u201d so to speak. Okay\u2026so Torrez called Calamity back and said that he had a possible lead on the Fetch. He (or his people) had found its apartment. The Fetch had already left, but had rigged the front door to an explosive on her way out. Gunnar (Ghoul Friday) got caught in the blast, but seemed to be fine. Not sure how he did it, but hey, whatever works. Insincere Marguerite and I went to check it out to see if any mirrors survived that she might look into to see what it \u201csaw.\u201d I basically went along to keep Marguerite safe. The only surviving mirror in the kitchen told us that the Fetch is well and truly nuts. Insincere Marguerite saw it arguing with cold cuts in the kitchen! Yeah, just a couple screws loose there. We explained what we\u2019d found out to Gunnar and he said he\u2019d let the others know.<br /> <br /> When we got back to the Dream House Gunnar was already there and talking to Calamity. I\u2019m not sure how he got to the House so quick. Maybe magic? I\u2019m generally not one to rule that out. So, he\u2019d been talking to her, presumably about a way to track the Fetch. I caught up with Calamity as she started to head out to take care of things. I asked if she was going after the Fetch. She said \u201cyes,\u201d and I said \u201cOkay, I\u2019m coming with you.\u201d She seemed a bit unsure at first, which confused me, but made sense later. Insincere Marguerite also noticed us and asked if she could come along. She pointed out that her abilities would make her ideal to sneak up on it if needs be. So, we went with Gunnar to an alleyway, far from prying eyes. You see, the way he had to track the Fetch was to summon the ghost of the little girl that it killed and have the angry spirit lead us to the Fetch. The focus for this ritual was something from the person they were trying to summon. In this case pieces of bone that were left at the Dream House. Needless to say I can see why Calamity did not want to involve any of the others and was hesitant at first about anyone else coming along at all. The method of tracking the thing was not strictly benign. There was some dark magic going on during the ritual. I\u2019m fairly certain those of us that did not come along would have freaked out.<br /> <br /> After the ghost was summoned and brought under Gunnar\u2019s control she started leading us to the Fetch. The thing about this that stood out to me wasn\u2019t the pissed off ghost leading us, it was Insincere Marguerite walking kind of hunched with her head and shoulders rolled forward a bit. It made her look like she was walking in a heavy rain instead of a sunny afternoon. Then it hit me. The sunny part anyway. Insincere Marguerite is a Darkling, and they tend not to like the sun overly much. I guess I\u2019d never really thought of it before since all the shows are at night, and most of our \u201cadventures\u201d are too. Anyhoo\u2026we followed the ghost until we got to the woods near the Dream House, and along a path until we found the psycho herself. She was standing on a path holding two jars of liquid and a manic smile. She was so far gone it wasn\u2019t funny. So, it was me, Calamity, Insincere Marguerite and Gunnar facing off against a deranged pyromaniac. Yeah, that was destined to end well. She looked like she was going to forgo the burning down of our house since we\u2019d caught up to her, and instead burn up the lot of us in one go. I figured if I could disrupt her plans and take one of the components out of the picture that would be a good thing. Yeah, didn\u2019t go like I hoped. I managed to knock one of the jars out of her hand. Problem was the liquid inside splashed all over me and the Fetch and ignited as soon as it was exposed to air. I figured that the two mixed together would make a pretty good explosive, but hadn\u2019t considered that just exposure to air would cause combustion. Next time, I am not bodily knocking explosives away from bad guys. \u2018Cause, yeah\u2026.that sucked.<br /> <br /> Let me tell you, burning is now at the top of my list of shitty things that have happened to me. I had to find out later what happened after the ill-conceived disarming attempt because I\u2019ll be honest, I had other things on my mind at the time. Part of it was just pain. All-encompassing pain. And there was also the strange comparison going on in my head between freezing to death and burning to death. With freezing to death you shiver until it hurts, you get drowsy, and eventually you go numb. Your mind slows and you just kind of turn off. Your extremities hurt like hell until they go numb, but it\u2019s a different kind of pain. With burning, it\u2019s like all of your nerves are working at 1000% capacity. They are all on, and all screaming. I had the brief thought in the beginning that I could drop and roll and get the fire out before it did much damage, but I had not been taking into account that there was an accelerant involved, and it was sticking to my clothes and my skin. Once the fire burned that off it started on me. Some of the fabric burned right off, other parts, I\u2019m guessing more man-made materials, melted or otherwise stuck to my skin. Of course I didn\u2019t really notice those details until later. At the time I was just screaming in my head and trying my best to not scream out loud. The old mantra kept going through my head, \u201cKeep quiet or the others will come.\u201d I guess I must have flashed back to times in the past when I couldn\u2019t take the chance that one of the less than helpful denizens of the Lady\u2019s realm would find me hurt and/or weak and take advantage. Then what felt like eons later there was a concussive explosion and the pain increased tenfold. I hadn\u2019t thought that was possible. Later I learned that this was when the Fetch added the second liquid to the first and caused an explosion with me at the center. I guess the first liquid didn\u2019t need to be contained to react with the second. Duly noted.<br /> <br /> So, just as I seemed to regain control of my brain I saw Insincere Marguerite running towards me. She looked worried, really worried. I tried to tell her to stay back, to keep away, but nothing came out. I just ended up coughing as I choked on smoke and wisps of flame. She actually ran into the fire and pulled me out! We tumbled out of the flame and staggered away. A moment later her eyes rolled back in her head and she started to fall. I caught her as well as I could. It was more like I slowed her decent. Then as fast as I could, I rolled around and beat out the flames on myself and on Marguerite. I don\u2019t know how long I laid there just staring at the sky and the treetops. A good part of me hurt so bad I wanted to cry, but found that I actually couldn\u2019t. I don\u2019t know if it was because my tear ducts were burned or my body was too dry. I don\u2019t want to know. I could see and I focused on that. The disturbing part was when I realized that my right hand and part of my arm didn\u2019t hurt too much anymore. I knew that meant nothing good. Probably meant that the nerves in that hand were charred and dead. I didn\u2019t want to think about that at the time so I looked around to see what was going on.<br /> <br /> The Fetch was lying on the ground several feet away, still burning. It was not moving. Calamity was fighting, in a way, the spirit of the dead girl. It looked like she won. At least the ghost faded and went away. Calamity then cried out in alarm and rushed over to Insincere Marguerite and gathered her fellow darkling up in her arms. She was terrified and angry and determined all at the same time. Just seeing that look in her eyes was like a knife sliding between my ribs. I got to my feet slowly, using my right hand to steady myself, which probably wasn\u2019t the smartest thing for me to do, though it seemed logical at the time since I couldn\u2019t feel anything with it anyway. Once I was up, I watched as Calamity ran towards the Dream House with Marguerite.<br /> <br /> As I was starting to walk towards the House myself, Gunnar raised his hands and it started raining. And hailing. It was blessedly cold and I stood there for a moment just enjoying the feel of ice on my face again. The remaining fire from the explosives was still burning and the rain helped put it out before it could spread. Not something that I would have come up with so quickly, but then I\u2019m not used to having to deal with too much fire. The problems I had in the past were more along the lines of trying to keep the fire alive. So\u2026I enjoyed the rain for a moment before I forced myself to start walking toward the Dream House. I wasn\u2019t confident in my ability to stay conscious for too much longer and knew that Lorelei could at least take the edge off the pain if not more. Unless she was spent, then I would be among friends when I passed out, which is preferable to alone or among enemies. Yeah, that definitely says something about my motley mates. That I\u2019d trust them enough to be unconscious in their presence. The last person that I trusted that much was Rook. And while we were allies I really could trust him to watch my back. He was a good friend. Sometimes I miss him and his dry humor.<br /> <br /> Before long Lorelei actually found me. I guess she found out that I was still outside and came to find me. She healed some of the burns, but was completely exhausted and could not heal them all. She seemed upset that she could not do more, but it really was more than enough. I felt significantly better after her ministrations. While she was there, she made sure that Gunnar was okay. I also thanked him for the hail. I think he understood that it wasn\u2019t just for putting out the fire. After that Gunnar went on his own way, after assuring us that he was fine, and we made our way back to the Dream House. Lori called someone in the Spring Court and they sent over Andromeda and Flores to help heal the lot of us.<br /> <br /> Waiting for that pair to show up didn\u2019t take long, but it was long enough. My burns weren\u2019t blistered as bad as they had been and some were healed outright thanks to Lori, but that wasn\u2019t what was bothering me. Calamity was still hurt and definitely favoring one side over the other. Insincere Marguerite was still out cold, and everyone looked worried and/or stressed. Especially Julia. And I was the cause of at least some of it. I was wholly responsible for Marguerite. Watching her lie there with her clothes burned and her newly healed skin all pink made me feel like that knife was still twisting in my heart. I don\u2019t understand why she did what she did! Why would she run into a fucking fire? For me? I don\u2019t get it. I mean, I know she worries about me sometimes, but this went above and beyond that! She ran into a fucking fire! For me! I can\u2019t let her do anything like that again. Her safety is too important to do such dangerous things. She could have been killed!<br /> <br /> Later, when everyone was awake and healed, Insincere Marguerite asked if we could talk. I said sure, and we went somewhere private. She asked if I was okay and I assured her that I was. I think she wanted to reassure herself, and to make sure I wasn\u2019t hiding anything this time. I can understand checking on whether or not I am wounded if it\u2019s serious, but if it\u2019s just a scratch I don\u2019t understand all the attention. Both Calamity and Insincere Marguerite seem keen on me not bleeding. At all. So, I promised that I\u2019d get any injuries looked at. And I did this time. I was actually hurt this time, so I guess I had the motivation. So, I assured Marguerite that I was fine. I did make her promise not to do anything like that again. I appreciated her concern, and her help, but I don\u2019t want her to get hurt. I realized that I don\u2019t want to lose her. Somehow she got under my guard and found her way into my heart. Sounds cheesy, but it\u2019s still true. I care about Marguerite. And in Insincere though she claims to be, she seemed to genuinely care about me. I don\u2019t deserve friends like her. I really don\u2019t.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> I almost died today. I can hide from almost anyone, but I cannot hide from explosives. I cannot hide from fire. It is a sobering thing. I suppose on some level I always thought I could escape from anything I really wanted to, until today.<br /> <br /> Of course, today I escaped death by explosive, so maybe I am not so wrong. Maybe.<br /> <br /> Right now I am pressed between and under Julia and Flores. A human shell or room, giving I a small chamber. Okay maybe not <i>right now</i>, but I was and will be again. Anyway. I need to be close to people, or I would be in the ventilation. Well, that and Julia won\u2019t leave me alone longer than it takes to go to the bathroom. I want to find a deep dark hole to crawl in and hide, and be forgotten.<br /> <br /> I would, of course, run out of Cognac and cheese. Intolerable.<br /> <br /> In Arcadia, I was menaced by physical harm before, but it never hurt so badly. And Jacob almost died too\u2026it was intolerable. Calamity was badly hurt, but if she goes into anything without being nearly eviscerated I suspect she would be disappointed somehow. She is very different from I. I am fragile. I am not a grub that has any business being on fire.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t want Jacob and Calamity to keep getting hurt. They both seem to relish it. What is wrong with them, anyway? Jacob is an Elemental, so has a certain bond with the inanimate, but Calamity is a Darkling like I. Does she feel a need to prove how tough she is? Is it because she is a girl so has to be tough like a guy? Is it seeking penance? I half think Jacob is just showing the damn Russian machismo that keeps Russia from interacting with the rest of the world as anything but an angry barbarian, but Calamity I don\u2019t understand.<br /> <br /> Those two need to start showing some self-preservation. Perhaps I will scold them. When we have had time to decompress.<br /> <br /> The Motley also has this huge hang up about monsters. Seriously. I am a monster. So what? So is Elmo from Sesame Street. It\u2019s not a big deal. They really need to get over it. Maybe the Fetch was a monster. Based on my understanding of the term that seems a little off, but English is their native language so I assume they know what they are talking about. But monster is just a word. As I said, Elmo is a monster, and all he does is sing about his goldfish in a voice that makes I want to choke him till the light goes out of his eyes. Monster does not MEAN anything, except someone or something unusual, ugly, or frightening in some way. And not even all those\u2026I am absolutely beautiful, and Elmo can\u2019t frighten anyone, except maybe they worry their child will be like that or date someone like that. But while I am nothing less than feminine perfection, I do like living in dark holes and stealing cheese. That makes me a monster. Or a mouse. But mice are ugly and I am not. The metaphor appears to have escaped I.<br /> <br /> The point is there have been far, far too many arguments about whether Calamity, Jacob, or the Fetch are on a moral level with Elmo, and I think it is strange.<br /> <br /> I should probably review things outside this, may calm me down.<br /> <br /> Lorelei went to Court, to talk to Jolie about a private matter. She wished to go alone, without even taking De La Rocha. Jacob suggested, wisely, I might want to follow her, so I hid under her passenger seat, which took some doing but worked out for me. The trip, however, turned out uneventful. Thankfully.<br /> <br /> Lorelei later explained that Jolie apparently has a need to consume the creative essence of artists. This has made her self-destructive of late, and the meeting was about the fact that Lorelei got the idea of using The Table to repair the problem. I am slightly ashamed to admit that while Jolie was always attractive to me in a physical sense, I had never considered her that intriguing until Lorelei mentioned her consuming creativity. I am unsure what this says about me as a person. Bah, I\u2019m over here acting like Calamity now.<br /> <br /> After the meeting we got word that Lucian had found the fetch\u2019s base, but something had gone awry. Jacob and I went, and found a bomb had gone off which Ghoul Friday had somehow avoided despite his clothes being less lucky. I suspect a Goblin Contract. I was able to check the mirrors, and watch the fetch go insane over a process of days. Despite myself I felt pity. The creature was mad and quite literally lashing out, especially at meat products. While I had not had a special desire to kill the fetch before, unlike the others, I did now, if as an act of mercy.<br /> <br /> We returned to find Ghoul Friday had somehow beaten us back. He had made a deal with Calamity to use occult means to find the Fetch. Specifically, by summoning the dead child\u2019s ghost as a hound. While manipulation of the dead by a Darkling seemed perfectly sensible at first, his methodology seemed very disturbing. I need to ask Calamity or Jacob about it. Or enquire at the Autumn Court. It is a shame I can\u2019t be a part of two Courts. I don\u2019t think.<br /> <br /> We pursued the bastard to the woods near the dream house, where she was bringing chemicals to probably blow it up, maybe out of frustration she could not find Mary. Jacob knocked one chemical out of her hand, which set both of them and the immediate area on fire. She slammed the second chemical into the fire and it exploded. I pulled Jacob out of the fire despite being hurt the pain was too much, I blacked out. Painfully.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve been scolded somewhat for pulling Jacob out. Was that not the Pledge we made as Motley to look out for each other? Standing and watching people burn to death seemed in violation of the spirit if not wording of the Pledge. I don\u2019t see how I really had other options.<br /> <br /> Well, that is an easy out anyway. The \u201creal\u201d answer is I am not sure why I almost died for Jacob. Despite being wonderful overall I am rather selfish, and my attraction to men tends to be light and fleeting, if perhaps healthier (if I am being cruelly honest) than my attraction to women. The draw is less intense, however, and I feel less control in the sex, and feel that what control I have is a polite fiction. I don\u2019t like this feeling. I feel very safe and in control with women, though. A therapist would have a field day with me. Probably.<br /> <br /> This leaves I wondering what to do about Jacob. I don\u2019t need to do anything, I suppose. I am friendly and flirty and affectionate. I never promised anything more. But I still ran into a damn fire for him. What does that say? Why would any given implication bother me? My brain is complicated it seems and full of cobwebs. Perhaps almost dying has made I introspective? I do not know.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll continue to be nice to Jacob and not worry about it. I believe it is the path both of us would prefer. Yes.<br /> <br /> I also worried about never seeing, never smelling Yvette again. It is not a pleasant thought. I should not look for her. That way lies madness. Probably.<br /> <br /> Besides, I have Julia, who is not afraid of me. Mostly. Flores has also been here, and she is the best smelling person I have come across. She is so minty! And decidedly more\u2026flowerlike\u2026than one might expect. She is also headstrong in her way, though not as pushy as resilient. Still, taking her as a regular lover would go over like a lead balloon with Julia. I suspect the reason this indulgence was allowed was she was just happy I was okay. She is good friends with Flores, but it has not been the same since Beltane. I hope this repairs their friendship somewhat, though the shooting has also brought them together somewhat. This pleases me; Julia needs friends. She is painfully shy sometimes. Usually.<br /> <br /> Ah Julia. What would I do without you? I\u2019ve turned your life upside down in so short a time. Sweet devoted Julia. Someone should really rescue her from me. Possibly.<br /> <br /> I am, after all a monster. Like Elmo.<br /> <br /> Americans.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I was discussing the aftermath. Calamity, I am told, carried me in, rather than Jacob, but Jacob was more hurt. Calamity is devoted in her own way. Lorelei healed me, then Andromeda and Flores arrived to bring everyone back to health, assuming Calamity and Jacob were not pretending to be less injured. Which they probably were, honestly. There was hail coming down outside the window, from Friday. Apparently. He is very strange.<br /> <br /> No show tonight, so we went our separate ways. Broody Gawain and less broody Calamity vanished, and Lorelei and De La Rocha went out. I am unsure what become of broody Jacob or less broody more coked out of his mind than broody Ace. Flores made some bad excuses for giving me some \u201cround the clock care\u201d and we ended up in my room. Julia\u2019s interest in her is much less than I, romantically speaking, but she did not have a bad evening.<br /> <br /> I should return. Julia is awake and looking at me. Hi Julia.<br /> <br /> Yes. I should return. Immediately.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XVII</i><br /> <br /> Of course, it is never that simple.<br /> <br /> So the Fetch was pretty clearly out of Clarity. Mary\u2019s return, and the problems that often manifest in Changelings and Fetches from Old McDonald, had taken away the last of her sanity. Her goal, since she was unable to locate Mary, was to destroy the Dream House (which she assumed Mary was in) and destroy herself as well (since she could no longer get to Mary and was suicidal anyway) Her Echo to have damage also hit the Changeling made things extra complicated\u2026that is an especially nasty Echo.<br /> <br /> Gunnar\u2019s magic will remain mysterious for now, but it was not Changeling, and nothing to do with the Wyrd. It was the sort of Magic that forces a Morality check from use with a die penalty\u2026nothing wholesome at all. Jacob remained standing in the fight due to his Elemental Blessing\u2026he would have been down otherwise. Insincere Marguerite took enough fire damage to lose consciousness\u2026the explosion did 6 lethal levels to all present (except the ghost) and the Fetch and Jacob had taken some besides.<br /> <br /> Calamity had an exorcism/banishment battle using a version of the rules in the WoD book.<br /> <br /> Several people (Lorelei, Jacob, Insincere Marguerite) hit Wyrd 4 after that session, so new excitement coming the groups way.<br /> <br /> One small other note that amused me\u2026it was pointed out most of the group could translate rather easily to <b>Changeling: The Dreaming. </b> Gawain would make a good Troll, Lorelei Sidhe (House Fiona most likely) Ace Pooka, Calamity Redcap, and Insincere Marguerite Sluagh. Jacob is the tough one, but Eshu could work for him. Alternately, Lorelei could be an Aonid (playing up her artsy side), Jacob an Aithu (playing up his shady/charming side) or Ace an Eshu (playing up his showmanship). I dunno what do you think?<br /> <br /> Apologies for the delay, comments and questions welcome. Ideally next journals will be on time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T00:57:10-08:00","id":332857,"title":"","content":"The near death stuff brought &quot;Glory to Brave&quot; to mind. Interesting to see Insincere being introspective in this way. Also, was the use of &quot;me&quot; at one point in her whispers accidental or inentional?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T02:20:12-08:00","id":332872,"title":"","content":"Probably accidental, though she sometimes remembers to use the right word. I and me are a problem for her as she has to recall to use &quot;me&quot; when writing, tho it is not usually a speaking issue.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s time to look in on the Motley. These journals do not cover the whole session (well, except Gawain\u2019s, that does), as we spent about an hour of play at the party but did not get through it so it was hard to record it in retrospect. Still, much of it is covered. Enjoy.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XVIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> (later)<br /> Breakfast did turn out pretty epic. Everybody, Flores, De la Roche, Julia and the motley, seemed to enjoy it, especially the strawberries and cream. Insincere Marguerite tried to steal some using her long tongue as Calamity offered them to Lori and De la Roche when they showed up, but Calamity caught it. She let Insincere Marguerite\u2019s tongue go right away - I guess she just wanted to see if she could, you know? But Insincere Marguerite didn\u2019t steal anymore using her tongue after that.<br /> <br /> People were still feeling pretty celebratory. Jacob even made fancy coffee. I was feeling much better, you know, more human, but I still didn\u2019t feel too... I dunno, accomplished? I just sat around being pissy, \u2018guarding\u2019 the House while everyone else saved Mary. I had an idea for something I could do to actually help, you know, and earn some part of the party the Spring Court was throwing the motley for being heroes. But now I\u2019m too late for that even. There is still something I can do at least, that could still maybe help. Hopefully, right?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m rambling though. See, Lori got a message saying the Spring Princess wanted to meet with us, so we headed out right away. It turns out, she wanted to throw us a party, tomorrow. She was trying to figure out where we wanted it to be and when and everything. I tried to stand back and just shrug. It\u2019s really for them anyway, you know? They wound up deciding on the Rose and Thorn, which does sound like fun.<br /> <br /> She also recommended me and Insincere Marguerite make powerful allies in the regular Courts, since we were becoming \u2018prominent\u2019 and everything, you know? I kinda figured on doing that a little with the Summer Court - I\u2019d gotten along well with the Summer folks in the travelling motley we met, I like Joan, and Lucien has been awesome in the last two crises, even if my first impression, with the Winter Court stuff, was a bit on the scary side. I dunno though. Maybe I\u2019ll make like Captain Jack and just have everybody like me.<br /> <br /> Lastly, she warned us that Mary was being kept isolated, cause Austen thought she was \u2018taking it well in a troubling way\u2019. I called him once we got home, and he let me know she\u2019d actually attacked Dark Kimberly and tried to eat her, all out of the blue. So she was being kept sedated and everything, you know? So I couldn\u2019t go talk with her and sit with her to give her a restful, mind-healing kinda dream. But I can still make her a dream vessel. I was hoping to get to talk with her to make the dream more personal. I knew Davie was her friend, since he was hanging out with her and made sure she was ok that time she got drunk right before the attack. I guess she had a crush on him or something, cause she hadn\u2019t talked much around him. I felt a little bad about calling and waking him up for that.<br /> <br /> My last hope is Dark Kimberly, but I think I\u2019ll go visit her in person, in case talking about it upsets her, so I can tell easier and make sure she\u2019s ok, you know? Lori was going to go with me, once Annika gets here, but I think Insincere Marguerite has lured her away with back rubs.<br /> <br /> <br /> May 15th<br /> <br /> Alright, I can do this. Gotta take a break though, now and then. It takes a lot of focus to make this whole dream vessel thing work. I think it\u2019s going well though. Dark Kimberly was super helpful. And doing well too. She seemed really happy and not even bothered by getting attacked again. She said she didn\u2019t even realize she was in danger really until she was safe. I guess she likes that kinda thing, you know, being bitten and everything.<br /> <br /> She was doing awesome things to Annika\u2019s big old rundown house. I could catch glimpses of the rooms whose floors were covered in bottles and the bags and bags of more bottles, but the hallway and the sitting room were really clean, and the shutters looked new and everything. She was a little bothered, cause she didn\u2019t want to be a maid again, like she was in Arcadia, you know? But it was different, cleaning for you and someone you care about. Also an awesome place like that. She and Annika seem to be really good for each other. Dark Kimberly also mentioned maybe going on a double date sometime, which would be super cool.<br /> <br /> Like I said, she was really helpful with the dream thing. I mentioned what I was trying to do and she said, right off, that Mary\u2019s sister needed to be there. It was her big sister, who was tall, blonde and hot, and protected Mary when she was a kid and got bullied, you know? She\u2019d joined the military and Mary had gotten taken the day her sister left for boot camp. So, with her, Lori and Davie and Mary\u2019s love of taking care of farm animals, I hope I can give her some reasons to keep in control and help her feel safe and cared for.<br /> <br /> I got back from talking with Dark Kimberly and picking up a stuffed bear in a military uniform to put the dream in just before stuff was about to start. I was a little distracted, planning things out, you know, but everything went smoothly anyway. I let Calamity know I was gonna be dream crafting a while, and the wicked look in her eyes when I asked if she needed anything before I got down to it might\u2019ve made me blush, a little. She gave me a hug and a kiss and set me to it though.<br /> <br /> I took another quick break when it was time for breakfast again. Lori perked me up, which was good. I dunno how Calamity does the whole being awake for multiple days in a row thing. That and needing to focus weren\u2019t playing well together for me, you know? Mostly we talked about clothes. First it was cause Calamity had gotten a new fancy dude\u2019s watch, which somehow that led to talking about making Calamity some new dresses and Lori some suits that would fit with their Changeling features. I wasn\u2019t really paying close attention until De la Roche started trying to get me in a dress. Then Jacob joined in! Calamity backed me up at least. For now though, they\u2019ve given up, cause I think we\u2019re all going in our Hedgespun clothes to the party.<br /> <br /> Alright, I oughta go back to work, if I wanna have this ready to go by partytime.<br /> <br /> <br /> May 16<sup>th</sup><br /> <br /> So I did wind up getting it finished, just in time too. I had just enough time to shower and hop into the Hedgespun tux before it was time to gather up downstairs. Everyone was looking super hot. Jacob used actual ice to frost his hair and make it spiky, which was really cool. Julia even found a black cloth rose to complement Calamity\u2019s super awesome dress. It gave me an idea - I bet I could work a metal rose and blacken it, maybe even in a pattern to match the embroidery on the dress. I\u2019ll have to find just the right metal for it, you know, so it isn\u2019t too heavy.<br /> <br /> So many people were there: all the Spring Court, most of the Autumn Court, Joan, Monica, Lucien and Haley from the Summer Court, and Lojack, Molly and Tamara from the Winter Court. Ginny was there with Chalcedony, which was awesome, though Chalcedony did look a little uncomfortable, you know? Calamity\u2019s mentor, Luna, was there too. We all went to go say hi to her first. She was standing all by herself, by glaring at everyone who got close, but she was really nice to all of us. She got nervous with everyone standing around, you know, so Lori went off to talk with Jolie and I went to say hi to Captain Jack.<br /> <br /> I dubbed him Captain Tightpants for the night though, cause he was dressed in aviator goggles, tight leather pants, a harness covered in Christmas lights, that blinked his name sometimes on the front and \u2018Other Side\u2019 on the back. He also had on a cape. He\u2019d thrown a spotlight on me, once we\u2019d all come in, so I waved. Her had a present for me - a bright green robe, actually big enough to for me to wear with a giant sword along the back that had \u2018Gawain\u2019 in sparkly green letters. There was even a button to make them light up. He also offered an ear, if I ever needed to talk. I guess I didn\u2019t look as happy as I\u2019m supposed to be. Or just tired. He\u2019s a good guy, Captain Jack, you know?<br /> <br /> I checked in with Calamity and Luna again after that, and Joan came by, to congratulate them and everything. It came up she wasn\u2019t supposed to talk with the police. She had some interesting ideas about how they were supposed to protect and serve us too. It\u2019s nice in theory, but not really fair, I think. I mean, if we ensorcelled them they\u2019d at least be able to see thing properly, but they\u2019d still be at a serious disadvantage. It might be interesting, maybe at a smaller town or something, to see if we could actually have Changelings and humans knowingly integrated and everything, you know? But here in the city would just be crazy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> By necessity, this will be a shorter than average entry; I only have a little time before we need to go.<br /> <br /> So D woke up a few minutes after I finished my last entry, and I slipped back into bed for a few late morning cuddles. We actually thought about just staying in bed all day\u2026 we really truly did discuss it. But in the end, the thought that we might be able to make it back to the Dream House in time to partake of one of Gawain\u2019s yummy breakfasts got us up and moving.<br /> <br /> Breakfast was odd but still delicious. Apparently Gawain and Calamity stayed up all night watching episodes of some cancelled TV show, and Gawain had prepared an eclectic set of dishes based on that. There was even a bowl of strawberries and cream for a treat. Marguerite amused herself by whipping her long tongue out to grab strawberries from the bowl, and at one point Calamity grabbed it, quick as a striking snake. She looked pleased with herself after that, but Marguerite threw her some very dark looks.<br /> <br /> I got a call from Dark Kimberly as we were finishing up breakfast. She told me that Princess Jolie wanted to see us \u2013 the whole motley this time \u2013 as soon as possible. I conveyed the message to the others and told her that we\u2019d be at Glamour Springs in half an hour.<br /> <br /> Turns out the Freehold wants to thank us for our part in taking down Mary\u2019s fetch, and as the reigning monarch, it fell to Princess Jolie to plan the festivities. She asked us if we had any ideas or preferences along those lines. I hesitantly suggested a changeling-only party at the Rose &amp; Thorn, and the others were quick to agree. Jolie mentioned that the club had not yet reopened following Kimberly\u2019s shooting last weekend, but that she was sure Flores wouldn\u2019t mind hosting the party anyway.<br /> <br /> She also expressed her opinion that it was time for Gawain and Marguerite to begin associating with one of the Seasonal Courts. She\u2019s not trying to recruit them or lure them away from their chosen organizations, of course\u2026 she just pointed out the harsh reality that the Dawn and Night Courts have no real power in the Malibu/Santa Monica area, and that it would be prudent for my friends to ally themselves with one of the freehold\u2019s political powerhouses. Of course I put in a few words in support of the Spring Court.<br /> <br /> Finally, the Princess told us that Mary has taken a turn for the worse. Whether due to the trauma she\u2019s recently experienced or because some magic was triggered when her fetch was killed, this whole situation has taken a toll on her mind. She had attacked Dark Kimberly earlier that morning, and is being held in isolation until the Court can either find some way to help her\u2026 or decide what to do with her.<br /> <br /> So we were a bit gloomier as we drove back to the Dream House, but still pretty high on our own accomplishments. Gawain seemed confident that he could do something to help Mary; something to do with giving her a therapeutic dream to help ground her. I don\u2019t really claim to understand it all that well, but he was sure it would work, and as soon as we got back he called Austin (who is currently looking after Mary).<br /> <br /> When he mentioned Austin, it got me thinking about my latest pet project. See, I want to set up a special outdoor show for the evening of the Solstice, a sort of Shakespeare-in-the-park number. <u><u>A Midsummer Night\u2019s Dream</u></u> seems to be the obvious choice, and I thought it would be interesting if we cast Changelings in all the human roles and mortals in all the faerie parts. And Austin would be <u>perfect</u> as Nick Bottom.<br /> <br /> So I was really excited about this idea, and I was sort of bouncing around Gawain as he was talking with Austin, waiting for him to finish his conversation and probably annoying the fuck out of him in the process. But then I started catching fragments of what they were talking about, and the enthusiasm drained right out of me. Mary didn\u2019t just attack Kimberly this morning\u2026 she bit her, and seemed intent on <u>eating</u> her. The cannibal curse of Keeper MacDonald strikes again, and a shy, sweet, innocent girl is paying the price.<br /> <br /> So that took the wind right out of my sails, and when Gawain handed me the phone I sort of glumly related my play idea to Austin. He was a real sport about it, and agreed on the spot to play whatever part we needed. \u201cDon\u2019t worry, Lori,\u201d he said soothingly, \u201cMary will get through this with the help of her friends. And the play sounds like a great idea. I\u2019m sure it\u2019ll be a big hit.\u201d<br /> <br /> We said our goodbyes and I set about preparing for the evening\u2019s show. Gawain said he had \u201cresearch\u201d to do and went off to talk to some of the people who know Mary best (Davie and Kimberly). I spent most of the afternoon just hanging out with D, Julia, and Marguerite. Between bouts of passion and tenderness, I spent a lot of time thinking about what I wanted to perform.<br /> <br /> In the end, I decided to take the plunge and sing \u201cPiece of My Heart\u201d for my first number. I\u2019m always a little wary of singing that one in front of people, since I know I\u2019ll never be able to do it as well as Janis did back in the day. Still, I think it went relatively well. I translated it into my own style, but I think I managed to preserve most of the pain and soul inherent in the lyrics in place.<br /> <br /> My second and final number of the evening was Gary Wright\u2019s \u201cDream Weaver,\u201d which I decided to sing as a sort of tribute to Gawain. It seemed appropriate, since he spent most of his day literally attempting to create a soothing dream that will guide our friend back to health. And it doesn\u2019t hurt that it\u2019s a song full of hope and optimism, which is his preferred flavor of glamour.<br /> <br /> As I made my way backstage after that number, I heard some of the girls talking. They were having an old-fashioned bitch session, griping half-seriously about the show, the theater, and their paychecks. I could tell that no one was really seriously upset about anything, so I was just going to let it pass, when I heard one of the girls make an offhand comment about \u201cthe Lioness.\u201d It took me another few seconds of listening to realize that she was talking about Marguerite.<br /> <br /> I asked the girls about this nickname, and they told me that it had just sort of evolved over the past few days, mostly in reference to the way Marguerite watches over them all from on high, like a big cat checking on her cubs. I laughed it off, but felt a chill running up my spine, as Marguerite had told me that her Keeper was called \u201cMama Lion.\u201d <br /> <br /> I decided that she should hear about the nickname from me so that it wouldn\u2019t come as a surprise when she heard it from the girls later. I pulled her aside after the show and told her what the girls had said as gently as I could. She covered it up quickly and well\u2026 but I don\u2019t think I\u2019ve ever seen that look on her face before. There was fear in her eyes, and sorrow, and trepidation\u2026 and maybe, underneath the rest, a flicker of pride.<br /> <br /> The four of us went back to bed after the show. Honestly, I would have been happy if it had just been D and me\u2026 but I think Marguerite needed us tonight. And not just for the sex. She needed Julia and D to remind herself that she was in control\u2026 and in a weird way, I think she needed me there to remind her that she doesn\u2019t always <u>have</u> to be in control. So we were doing good by joining Marguerite and Julia in their bed last night. And hey, the orgasms were nice too.<br /> <br /> Today has been all about getting ready for tonight\u2019s party. We agreed pretty early on that we should all wear our hedge-spun attire (even though it irks me that the whole Freehold is going to see me again in the same dress I wore to opening night). Spirits were high as we chatted over breakfast. Gawain seems to have come out of his funk; he\u2019s pretty sure he\u2019ll be able to help Mary by sending her a healing dream. Marguerite once more seemed secure in her identity. Hell, even Jacob cracked a smile and started flirting with my girlfriend over coffee.<br /> <br /> \u201cHey now,\u201d I teased, \u201cjust keep in mind that where D goes, I go. We\u2019re a package deal.\u201d<br /> <br /> D kissed me on the cheek and slid an arm around my waist. \u201cDamn right,\u201d she agreed passionately.<br /> <br /> Jacob looked intrigued by the possibilities (which, I must admit, <u>are</u> intriguing) but at the moment I was too busy melting in D\u2019s embrace to pay much attention to the poor guy. Her arms were warm, her smile was bright and toothy, and mischief gleamed in her dark eyes. I never wanted to be anywhere else. I was home.<br /> <br /> I spent the next three hours getting ready for the party. The entire freehold, gathered to honor me and my friends? Of course I had to look my best! I tossed and teased my hair into golden waves, shaved my legs, and spent entirely too much time deliberating over my makeup. I\u2019d like to be able to say that by the time I was through not a feather was out of place\u2026 but I haven\u2019t really been able to say that since I got back from Arcadia. Those damned thorns really did a number on my wings, and they\u2019ve looked pretty ragged ever since. I\u2019m starting to wonder if they\u2019ll ever regain their former sleek perfection.<br /> <br /> In any case, we\u2019re about to head over to the Rose &amp; Thorn, so I only have a few more minutes to write. I\u2019ve been feeling a little introspective lately, and I thought it might be a good idea to set some of my thoughts about my situation down. Anyone who knows me will tell you that I\u2019m as happy now as I\u2019ve been since I was Taken, and any idiot would be able to tell you why. D has me feeling more normal, more <u>human</u> than I thought was possible. It\u2019s like she\u2019s given me back a piece of myself that I hadn\u2019t realized was missing.<br /> <br /> At the same time, I\u2019ve started feeling\u2026 strange. I\u2019m not sure how to explain it. I\u2019ve gotten stronger lately. Glamour flows through me much more easily than it used to, and it seems to be all around me. I feel more confident in myself. And ever since the night the fetch visited the Dream House, I\u2019ve felt like I\u2019m more in control of my emotions. I guess that makes sense; after living through something like that, the trials and tribulations of a normal life don\u2019t seem so arduous anymore.<br /> <br /> But it\u2019s more than that. I feel like I\u2019m on the edge of something; like the other shoe is about to drop. I don\u2019t know if it\u2019s a premonition of bad things coming, or if my new connection to the magical energy of the area is picking up on something my conscious mind hasn\u2019t noticed yet\u2026 or if I\u2019ve been repressing something I\u2019m only now becoming capable of facing.<br /> <br /> I guess it doesn\u2019t really matter. I\u2019ll face it when and if I have to, whatever it is. But tonight, we party!<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T02:20:58-08:00","id":332873,"title":"","content":"<b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> <u><b><b><u>Thursday May 15<sup>th </sup></u></b></b></u><br /> <br /> Tonight we party like big damn heroes. Seems people are taking note of everything we've done recently. Specifically, this is being hosted by the Spring Court for stopping Mary's fetch. Luna's even coming out for it. I really did not expect her to when I called to let her know about it. I just wanted to let her know I wasn't wasting the skills she'd shared with me. Okay, I <i>did</i> hope that she'd be pleased with me but to actually make a public appearance to make a point showing it... I am still shocked about it. But if she really does come out that will give me a chance to introduce the rest of the motley to her. Jacob in particular. I want her to meet him. At some point, I'd like her to see him fight so she can see that he's a worthy student.<br /> <br /> I also want to see what she thinks about Gawain. I know he's interested in meeting her since I've spoken about her to him fairly glowingly and he's seen how ragged I came back from some of my stays with her during my lessons. But I also kinda want her to meet him since he and I are close. It's weird but I guess I want her to approve of him. I mean, it's my life and I will bed down with whomever I damn well please but still... It would be nice for the important people in my life to get along.<br /> <br /> Lori seems a bit less down than she was earlier, which is good. It turns out Mary is not doing as well as we'd hoped. She attacked Dark Kimberly this morning, tried to eat her when they were alone and her back was turned. Austin is keeping her sedated and isolated until they can either help her learn to control the urge or have to put her down. It's a shame to be sure and it hit Lori hard that even after what we did it might not have been enough to save Mary. I did try to remind her that without us and specifically her Mary would be dead or worse right now. That she was the reason Mary had a chance at all and that the girl is in the best hands she could hope for right now. I think it helped a little. Maybe not as much as being pulled off to spend all of yesterday afternoon and last night in an orgy with Insincere Marguerite, julia, and De la Rocha but they're better at that sort of comfort than I am.<br /> <br /> And yeah, that is certainly becoming a foursome rather than a pair of couples there. Her brush with death seems to have Insincere Marguerite rather hungry for intimacy, but interestingly not with Jacob. Maybe she's not comfortable with discovering just how much she cares about him? I do hope it's not him pushing her away. (Why yes kettle, I am calling you black...) I mean, I totally know how that goes. The idea that Gawain would do something that reckless and stupidly brave for me scares the fuck out of me. But I should speak to Jacob about it at some point. Of course, I haven't had a lot of success in getting him to warm up to me yet, but the fact that he hasn't shut me out completely is a good sign. I have to at least make the effort and make sure he knows I'm willing to listen and talk. We monsters need to stick together after all.<br /> <br /> So, all things considered, it's been a quiet couple of days. Gawain's been working on crafting a dream vessel for Mary. Austin isn't keen on letting people close to her right now but it lets him try to soothe her mind without having to be there. He went to speak with Dark Kimberly since she was the closest person to Mary and thus most likely to have some useful information about what sort of imagery would be best to help her regain her clarity. Apparently she has an older sister who joined the military that used to protect her. So he picked up a saccharine sweet little teddy bear in a military uniform to anchor the dream to. I am sure that Katt would have absolutely loved it. Now it just makes my teeth hurt to look at. He's been working so hard on it, I hope she's not too far gone for it to help.<br /> <br /> When I first heard of dream vessels, I was excited that it might be a way to help Gawain with his own nightmares, but I've learned that in cases like his the psyche will twist any strong dream even one crafted to be restful or curative. And I can't really trust my own subconscious. I don't really want him to see what passes for a good dream in my mind these nights. At least I can scourge the nightmares when we're together. And I guess if I crafted a vessel and used it myself while he was riding my dreams I could dream a happy dream for him. I wonder if I could pull up a memory of Katt watching the sunrise for him? Hmm... That might wind up being a bit bittersweet after the fact. I'll have to think on it a bit, maybe something a little less personal would be safer. The whole point here is to make Gawain happy, not start a pity party for me over what I've lost.<br /> <br /> The Firefly theme went over well yesterday morning. Of course no one else had seen the show so they were a bit confused by the quotes and all. I think we convinced the others to give it a whirl, though Insincere Marguerite is apparently quite against anything set in space due to the fact that Patrick Stewart had the audacity to play a Frenchman when he isn't actually French in Star Trek. But we assured her that there were no faux French in Firefly and she seemed to begrudgingly decide it might be worth watching. Maybe she was grumpy because I caught her tongue when she went to snatch a strawberry. I mean, it doesn't bother me when she does it or anything but I just... I don't know I wanted to see if I could. I guess after spending the night watching with Gawain I was feeling playful.<br /> <br /> The rest of the morning was spent at Glamour Springs being congratulated by Princess Jolie and planning our victory party. She also told us the bad news about Mary and warned Gawain and Insincere Marguerite that they might want to foster some goodwill with one of the seasonal courts now that they're making a name for themselves. I think Gawain may be leaning toward the Summer Court. He knows people there and they do respect strength. I'd be happy to do what I could to make connections in the Autumn Court for him, but he really doesn't mesh well with them. Insincere Marguerite, on the other hand, would fit in pretty well. I should see if she is interested in me making some introductions for her.<br /> <br /> Once we'd finished up there, the other girls all took off to Insincere Marguerite's room and only reappeared long enough for the night's show before returning. I spent the afternoon with Annika and she seemed pleased enough with my progress. She did cut things a bit shorter than usual since she wanted to get back to Dark Kimberly. It's a bit surprising how quickly those two have fallen into each other but I really feel they're good together so it's not a bad thing. I had a bit of paperwork to catch up for the house anyway.<br /> <br /> The show went well and Lori made a point of singing Dreamweaver for Gawain. He seemed to appreciate it. He let me know he was going to be working all night on the dream and I told him it was fine. As the only girl not invited to the decadence upstairs, I slipped into my street clothes and hit the road for a while.<br /> <br /> I haven't done any night-stalking since the Dream House opened and my bank account is feeling it. I mean, most of my expenses are covered under room and board but not everything. Plus I miss the hunt you know. Cruising along the streets of Santa Monica on my bike, drifting in and out of the dive bars. I drove by the Mailed Fist but since I'd promised Gawain I wouldn't go alone I didn't stop in.<br /> <br /> In the end I found me a nice fat tourist with a nice fat wallet that was hassling all the ladies. I decided to do them a favor and let him buy me a few drinks and touch my thigh before I suggested we go somewhere more private. I don't know if he was stupid enough to think I was in his league or drunk or maybe just assumed I was a professional. But he slapped down his tab with a tip stingy enough to make the bartender stop watching me suspiciously and bounced toward the door like his last shot had been gummy berry juice.<br /> <br /> I took him a block or so down before I caught him by the collar and shoved him into the alley. Stupid piece of shit didn't have enough of a clue to resist, just let me drag him away from the illusion of safety the street lamps offered before I pushed him back against the wall and flashed him a nice little show of knife blades. Once I\u2019d brought them to rest at his neck and his crotch he got right damn agreeable. I cleaned him out and once he'd offered up the PINs for his cards I applied a knee to his swollen balls and left him weeping and cursing. Filthy pig is lucky I didn't take anything that was attached but the cops pay a lot more attention to aggravated assault and murder than they do to armed robbery. Of course, that assumes he even reports it, after all he did get mugged by a woman. Always nice when the fucking patriarchy works in a girl's favor for a change.<br /> <br /> A few ATM stops later and a visit to a pawn shop run by a guy who's chronically forgetful about proof of ownership and my own accounts were much happier. I ended up hanging onto his watch, damn thing's an actual Rolex. I was admiring it at brunch this morning which prompted a whole discussion about clothes and styles and who was or wasn't 'butchy'. De La Rocha in particular seemed to dislike the term and so we had to tease her with it. Then julia offered to make something for me but pointed out that she'd need my measurements. Which seems pretty obvious so I wonder if it was some sort of flirt... either way I agreed. I mean, she's an amazing seamstress and quite the tasty morsel so whatever she's got in mind should be a win for me. The conversation took a turn before I could do more than agree, with plans to put Gawain in a dress. Jacob even volunteered to cross dress as well just to see it. While I won't say I didn't find the whole thing amusing, Gawain did not and so I put my foot down and told them I wore the dress in our relationship. I then suggested we go with our hedgespun outfits for the victory party and everyone seemed to like it. Lori definitely liked the idea of wearing the wine dress and Insincere Marguerite started considering what to wear under her spiderweb dress. Gawain's virtue was saved and I headed to get into the evil queen dress. I am still not quite used to something quite this low cut (I mean, if I had Lori's cleavage to show off it would be different, but I don't.) Once I'd come down in it, julia decided that what I needed was a black rose for my hair (which, of course, she happened to have) and so she and the girls fixed my hair up with it while Gawain stroked his chin. When I asked, he told me he was considering making one out of metal and I told him straight up that if he did I would wear it on stage when I perform.<br /> <br /> Well, I think at this point everyone is ready so it is time to pile into Gawain\u2019s van and go bask in the glory of my triumph.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Well the day from Hell is over. Mostly. Didn\u2019t get much in the way of real sleep last night, but I did get some. The adrenaline had me on edge all night and into the early morning. I kept expecting someone unfriendly to pay a visit. And it wasn\u2019t really the fetch that had me on edge, not entirely anyway. I had not realized how far I\u2019d really relaxed my guard since coming to this town. Even travelling between Portland and here I was more wary. Dangers were all around in the Lady\u2019s realm and I learned really quickly in order to survive that I had to be clever, selfish, and above all else, quiet. Sometimes I can\u2019t help but notice how loud the others can be. Even without meaning to, they make quite a bit of noise. During the fight with the Fetch there was so much noise, just people moving, talking, and later screaming. <br /> <br /> I can\u2019t help but feel bad about the screaming. It was my fault that the others got hurt in the first place. If I hadn\u2019t been messing with explosives things wouldn\u2019t have gone the way they did. Okay\u2026I understand that people were likely to get burned regardless of what I did. That crazy bitch was intent on torching the lot of us. I just shouldn\u2019t have tried to \u201cdisarm\u201d the bomb before we had a better understanding of what the components were and what they did. Not sure if we would have gotten that chance, but I still feel bad. I was honestly a little surprised that the others did not seem angry with me about the whole thing or give me a hard time for setting myself on fire. They just went about the day as if nothing had happened. I don\u2019t get it. The image of a scared Insincere Marguerite running towards me, towards the fire will live with me until the end of my days. Seeing her on fire. Seeing her skin turn red and blister. Hearing her cries of pain before mercifully falling unconscious. I don\u2019t know how she can stand me after going through that. <br /> <br /> I know that Marguerite is not a paragon of innocence, but I do wish I could have saved her from that little bit of reality. Hell, I wish I could have saved them all that little bit of reality. Not something I\u2019m keen on visiting again either. I know Calamity is used to the pain. There is a reason she channels her anger the way she does. She falls back on what became routine for her. Violence was a regular part of her life. I get the impression that most of it was done to her, but later, when she got back to \u201cthe world\u201d she learned to fight from Luna. Then it became an outlet for her to use. And use it she does.<br /> <br /> I remember Diane used to channel her anger or stress through art. She was always a gentle soul. I don\u2019t know how she survived in the Lady\u2019s realm. Maybe she had a protector? One can hope. But when I was a \u201cguest\u201d of her motley I\u2019d watch her sketch, and when she stepped out of the room I\u2019d peek through her sketchbook. She somehow managed to draw the beauty of the Lady\u2019s realm, as well as the darkness. She even had a few sketches of me in there. She had several of Felicity, the young fawn girl that was her charge. Felicity wasn\u2019t much more than ten when she was taken. She was such a sweet, shy girl. She didn\u2019t deserve what happened to her.<br /> <br /> Dammit, why are those memories coming back so clearly? I was more than happy with the fuzzy memories of that \u201cvisit\u201d to Claire Falls, mostly due to head trauma, but still, fuzzy. Now they\u2019re clear as day. I used to have nightmares about that damn Ogre, until the Lady\u2019s \u201cattention\u201d pushed it out of my head. Now I can see that man\u2019s scarred face clear as day, and I\u2019d really rather not. After he beat me near to death they didn\u2019t allow him so close again. I heard him though, through the door. That last day he was arguing for my execution. Saying that Felicity\u2019s death was my fault. That I\u2019d brought Rook to their town. In a way I suppose that I did. I did not summon him, but he did come to retrieve me, so in that way her death was my fault. She wasn\u2019t a target, but she got caught in the crossfire. Rook was never overly concerned with innocent casualties. Of course to be fair, neither was I. I think Felicity\u2019s death opened my eyes to just how ruthless I\u2019d been. I felt bad and I didn\u2019t even really know her. I think she would have been thirteen next week. I think I\u2019ll make popsicles for the Motley. Felicity always seemed to like them.<br /> <br /> Okay\u2026so we were invited to Glamour Springs by Princess Jolie. She wanted to talk to the whole lot of us, so we went. Apparently, she said, since we\u2019d defeated a powerful Fetch that was threatening the Freehold there was going to be a party thrown in our honor. We talked, and agreed that the Rose and Thorn would be the best place for that. She also hinted to Insincere Marguerite and Gawain that they might want to cultivate stronger ties to one of the Seasonal Courts to strengthen their positon. There have been no threats or anything, but the Night and Dawn Courts are not all that powerful in town, so it might be good to have allies in one of the stronger Courts. I hate political bullshit. There was enough of it in the Lady\u2019s realm, though I didn\u2019t have to deal with it too much. I just followed my Lady\u2019s orders, whatever they might be.<br /> <br /> Oh\u2026apparently Mary has also been isolated from the rest of the Freehold. She has shown some violent tendencies towards others since the Fetch died, and people are worried that she might turn to cannibalism. They are trying to prevent that. Seems a shame that we free the girl from the persecution of her Fetch only to be driven to madness once she\u2019s free. Gawain said something about wanting to talk to her if possible and the Princess directed him to talk to Austin. I guess he\u2019s taking care of Mary. Hopefully she can be helped.<br /> <br /> While Gawain was talking to Austin, and the others did their thing, I went to the College campus to check on my sister. I don\u2019t know why I got it in my head that I needed to make sure she was okay, but I did, so I went. I wandered around a bit until I saw her coming out of the Humanities building, laughing with her friends. Some of the tightness in my chest eased at the sight. It also answered a question I\u2019d had, If the injuries I took affected my fetch or not. Apparently not, since Elena seemed completely unconcerned, and she wouldn\u2019t be if I her brother had been hurt. I guess the little shit is just lucky that way. Also, while I was there I saw a \u201cmissing persons\u201d poster that caught my attention. I don\u2019t know why, it just looked familiar.<br /> <br /> Later that day I caught a bit of conversation between Lori and Marguerite. Apparently some of the mundane dancers have taken to calling Insincere Marguerite, \u201cThe Lioness\u201d because of the \u201cfeline\u201d way she makes her way around on the walkways above them and kind of stalks the girls. This was, I think an uncomfortable association with her keeper, and the conversation made Marguerite a bit troubled. She asked Lori if she thought that Julia was being too dependent on her. I will admit that I see her becoming more and more possessive of Julia and keep thinking I should call her on it. To make sure she realizes what she\u2019s doing. Part of me wants to stay far away to keep her safe from me, but that same part of me wants to stay close to make sure she\u2019s okay. Hell, I stayed in this entirely too warm town just to keep an eye on my sister. I\u2019ll stay to keep Marguerite safe. Maybe even from herself.<br /> <br /> **** **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Today started like any other for the most part. Gawain made breakfast and I made coffee, though I decided to try a flavored coffee to change things up. I made French vanilla. I\u2019ll have to see if Insincere Marguerite liked it. I just figured a change would be nice, and it would also help blend the extra bit of espresso I put in the coffee. I needed it. Had bad dreams about that damn ogre. I mean, the beating itself hurt and was scary, but the thing that I remember most clearly was the anger in his expression. I have rarely seen such raw hatred. That\u2019s why those dreams are so bad, and why I needed slightly stronger coffee this morning. Lots of coffee.<br /> <br /> Again this morning the others didn\u2019t say word one about my \u201coh so spectacular\u201d fuck up, and just focused on what the lot of us were going to wear to the party. I think we were all going to wear our Hedge Spun outfits. We also talked briefly with each other about who we might want to invite personally. I know Calamity wanted to see if Luna could or would come to the party. I called Lowjack to see if he\u2019d like to come. I thought he might have fun, and I\u2019ve wanted to talk to him again and figured this would be a good chance to do so. <br /> <br /> After the discussion of clothes, but before phone calls, Marguerite asked me if I had any projects going on. I replied that I did not, but still wanted to go urban exploring with her. I have been able to do activities with almost everyone else so far. I think I still need to do something with Ace. Hell, I\u2019ve sparred twice with Calamity now. Maybe I should see if Lorelei wants to go roller skating again? She can bring De la Rocha. I\u2019ve been informed that they are a package deal. De la Rocha was flirting with me earlier and Lorelei had to interject that they go as a pair. I won\u2019t say that I wasn\u2019t intrigued and a little bit interested, but I\u2019ve never done a twosome. Hell, I still feel kind of inexperienced with just one woman. I said something like \u201cI\u2019ll keep that in mind\u201d with a smile, and I certainly will. First though, I want to spend an evening with Marguerite again. She explained a little while ago that she\u2019d been holding off on doing anything with me until the birth control kicked in. I get that. Don\u2019t want any surprises down the line. Hopefully it\u2019ll be soon. She does this thing with her tongue\u2026<br /> <br /> **** **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Okay\u2026.gotta focus on getting ready for the party. I\u2019m wearing that leather Highwayman outfit, which I must admit doesn\u2019t look too bad on me. Wasn\u2019t too far off from what I wore when I worked with the Lady. My old clothes were lighter and had frost patterns (and some actual frost) woven in. Maybe thinking about that is what prompted me to spike my hair using ice? I used to wear it kind of spiked with ice in the past. Now it is usually kind of spikey on its own, but thought that doing it with ice would be a little fancier. Here\u2019s hoping the reaction from the others is favorable. <br /> I just\u2026looked in the mirror. To check my outfit. I saw my reflection and saw Rime. And then I remembered the face of a boy. It was the face of the boy on the missing person poster. I just remembered who he is, or maybe was. His name was Brandon. Mills I think. He said he was from Santa Monica! He lived here, but I didn\u2019t meet him here. He and his friends where hiking on Mount Pinos. They had left him behind and he looked sad and a little betrayed. I remember seeing this as I watched him from behind an evergreen. An early snow had fallen and I was taking the opportunity to \u201cplay.\u201d I remember thinking when I saw Brandon that the Lady would like this boy. He had a nice face and calm demeanor. So, I played one of my usual \u201ctricks.\u201d I moved ahead of him on the trail and made it look like I\u2019d been coming down the path. I muttered under my breath about inconsiderate jocks. Just loud enough for the boy to hear me, and he did. That started a conversation, which led to sympathizing, then amicable conversation. I remember thinking that it was all too easy. I led him to a seldom used path that led to a beautiful cave. I had him, hook, line and sinker. And he came willingly into the cave. Into the Lady\u2019s realm. The look on his face when we reached Her lands and he saw me for what I am was hilarious. I laughed. He was not amused. I soothed his ruffled feathers and spun a tale of loneliness and searching for a friend. I think I was better at that stuff back then. I could spin a tale and tell it convincingly. One of the many things I lost when I left the Lady. <br /> <br /> I convinced Mills to follow me further into the forest, towards the Lady\u2019s castle. We met up with Rook on the way and the pair of us continued to escort Brandon to the Lady of the Winter Winds. We almost got him there too, but he spooked and ran. Rook could be intimidating just standing there, so I suppose it wasn\u2019t a surprise. He wasn\u2019t the first runner either. He was one of the few that we didn\u2019t catch within a day or two though. Not that we didn\u2019t look, we did. But there are so many things in those woods that will kill you, we figured he\u2019d freeze to death, get killed by one of the roving bands, or get himself killed by a wolf.<br /> <br /> I spotted him one more time before I left to retrieve Delight. He was starting to change. His hair was thicker than it had been, and he was a bit broader in the chest. He seemed well though and I made a note to myself to start again the search for him when I got back. Yeah, that didn\u2019t happen. <br /> <br /> Goddess I just read what I wrote and I sounded so dispassionate relating those events. I know I was not a good person, still not in some ways, but I guess I hadn\u2019t been so close to that person while writing in this journal before. Sometimes I think I\u2019m closer than I\u2019d like to be. I wonder how far I\u2019ve come from being Rime. I don\u2019t have a problem stealing things. I don\u2019t really have a problem when fighting, and didn\u2019t really blink when we had to cover up blood and bone bits from Mary\u2019s bedroom. I\u2019m not sure where that puts me. Maybe I\u2019m not that far at all\u2026.it\u2019s just now, I see it. Sometimes I wish I was blind.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> My power is waxing. Of course, I am going slightly mad.<br /> <br /> Last night, surrounded by my pretties, I tossed and turned in my sleep. I remembered sneaking into an orchid in Arcadia, with only the prettiest apple-cheeked tree girls. I startled them as I took apples from the trees, unseen. I recalled scanning them from the shadows, and decided to hedge my bets of getting one of my own by stealing two. Mama Lion would not take two. I remember sweet-talking them one at a time into my sack\u2026the second was harder since my sack was meeping. But I took two and slipped out. My bag was heavy. Obviously.<br /> <br /> Mama Lion did indeed let I keep one. But she seemed\u2026cross\u2026that I had taken two just in case. It seemed like weeks before I had more capering, and I know others were called in the meantime. Sure, at first I did not care, I had an apple lady for my garden. But I grew resentful. Eventually I was told to go meet to discuss a caper, and I recall everyone looking at I when I entered the room. Curiously.<br /> <br /> Were my girls, kept deep in my lair, getting paler, their eyes larger? The vivid flashes of memory suggested so, as I often remembered taking them and they seemed\u2026more normal. For changelings. I opened my eyes and saw Julia\u2019s pale leg in the darkness. Was she always so pale? Of course she was, I could not change anyone\u2019s nature. Not yet.<br /> <br /> In the morning Flores was in a terribly good mood. Giddy even. She was more like De La Rocha, less Lorelei. Also, very smitten. I promised I would spend more time with her in the future. Julia\u2019s behavior was returning to normal, but she was still not over the previous day\u2019s shock. Clearly.<br /> <br /> Calamity decided I was having too good of a morning. I was stealing a strawberry when she grabbed my tongue. I was not okay with that. Less because it is my tongue, more because she grabbed a limb suddenly. While I got fairly angry, I realize she did not mean anything by it. She is American, after all, and probably does not know better. I decided not to try to scold her about it. Maybe she was trying to protect Lori from having a strawberry stolen. I don\u2019t really know. I just know I was not happy about it. If she continues doing it however I will be most cross with her. I am not Gawain, I am not a person she can touch or grope at her leisure. I touch people when I speak to them, but not like that.<br /> <br /> We got word the Spring Princess wanted to see us. De La Rocha decided to take the still jittery Julia out to shop, the Fresh Market if nothing else. Even beyond being lovers, those two are striking up a friendship. It\u2019s good; Julia needs friends. Definitely.<br /> <br /> So, they are going to have a party for us, it seems. That\u2019s nice. Jolie also wants Gawain and I to associate ourselves with a Seasonal Court, though she stopped well short of making anything even resembling a demand, or suggesting we join those Courts. I am torn between Spring and Autumn. I will have to consider. I lean toward Autumn.<br /> <br /> Most of the rest of the day was spent in bed with Lorelei, De La Rocha, and Julia. Honestly, after yesterday, I needed it. A lot of contact and softness. The smell of hair and hair products. A lot of kisses. I like kisses.<br /> <br /> There was a break where Lorelei and I had to work. I was returning to bed, as De La Rocha and Julia did not bother leaving my room, when Lorelei stopped me to tell me that some of the girls had taken to calling I \u201cThe Lioness\u201d justified by my blonde hair and tendency to watch them from above. I remember so many emotions passing before me when my little bird spoke those words. Pride, anger, fear, lust\u2026part of I is terrified of becoming like Mama Lion. Part of I thinks it is my birthright. Part of I envies her power she had. Part of I feels superior that I am not gentry. I don\u2019t know how I feel. I collected my emotions, swept them away under the rugs of my eyelids, and thanked Lorelei.<br /> <br /> It came full circle. My power is waxing. I returned to my girls. The night was one of passion but\u2026possessive passion. Lorelei tried to not let herself be claimed, as she always does. Julia made it clear she belonged to I, as she always does. De La Rocha allowed herself to be controlled, as she always does. Still a good night. Certainly.<br /> <br /> I dreamed of stealing curtains. Were they people? Diamonds. Everything. I crept through a library and stole many curious books. I remember I was going to build my own library. Have I become so decadent I only steal to sleep with people? I mean, I steal for practicality, but once as much as I loved my big-eyed girls in the dark, I also was proud of all the things I had taken and possessed not all of which were fey. Have I fallen to being a hormone-driven strumpet, using my talents to only sate my physical needs? I\u2019ve spent an inordinate amount of time in bed with Julia. Worryingly.<br /> <br /> Yet her work is improving, and she is creating more. She is quite afire from my musing her. She is, perhaps, becoming more valuable? That is a terrible way to think of it. Julia says my influence has been excellent upon her. Is she right? Hopefully.<br /> <br /> Today has been getting ready. Julia lay on my bed while I perused her outfits and found a little black dress for her to wear. Julia has such classy clothes; frankly I am envious. Sometimes looking at her skirts and lace I wonder if I should dress more like a girl. She is tall enough her clothes won\u2019t fit I\u2026she is a good almost eighteen centimeters taller than I. This did not stop I from flitting about the room in some of her lacy finery, much to her amusement. She seems to take pleasure in my choosing her clothing. If she did not have the aggravating tendency to suggest I am somehow a man in regards to our relationship she would be perfect. Then again, if I stopped being aggravated she would probably stop doing it. Americans.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll be wearing the spiderweb dress. It appeals for my need of femininity, and Julia enjoys it effects on my bosom, which delayed I coming downstairs for a bit. I am wearing some grey knee socks with spiders dangling from the knees. They are Julia\u2019s, so they go pretty high on my legs, since Julia seems to possess legs as an endless resource. Wonderfully.<br /> <br /> Now she sits with a black rose in her hair to match Calamity\u2019s and wearing adorable fingerless gloves. I should go smell her hair again.<br /> <br /> Yes.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XVIII</i><br /> <br /> Not a lot of extra details that need to be covered.<br /> <br /> A lot of folks spoke of changes as they increased their Wyrd. As each went from Wyrd 3-4, they sort of rose a threshold and began to recall more of their time in Arcadia, and became more aware of the ebb and flow of glamour.<br /> <br /> It may be worth noting that Calamity succeeded on a roll of one die to grab Insincere Marguerite\u2019s tongue as she was grabbing strawberrys. It was funny.<br /> <br /> That about covers the session. Comments and Questions welcome<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T14:28:26-08:00","id":346996,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to look in on the crew at the Dream House. They had a big party to go to, and discussions to be had. Here we go.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XIX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> Joan also wanted our opinion on security type things. Even she noticed something was at least pretty awkward between Chalcedony and Ginny, but Calamity\u2019s pretty sure it could just be that Chalcedony\u2019s not used to being with another woman. That got us talking about romance, and Joan let it slip she had fallen for somebody before, but was worried about hurting them. Like, I think, during sex? She was worried about losing control at least. Then, when she was asking if we thought Becky was doing a good enough job, it became really clear that she\u2019d fallen for Andromeda. She\u2019s worried about her and thinks Becky\u2019s not doing enough, but is afraid if she started protecting Andromeda, that she might wind up taking advantage, you know? We did say we were after her Table (we might have some problems if we wind up wanting to give the Table over to the Autumn Court once Princess Jolie is cured, unless Andromeda is really ok with that), but once Calamity mentioned that Andromeda was sturdier than she looked, Joan started stammering and left pretty abruptly.<br /> <br /> Joan had left her drink behind, so I went and got her a refill and waited for her to come back out to the party. I tried to encourage her, about the hurting people thing. She still kept protesting, about how she can\u2019t provide an emotional connection and doesn\u2019t know anything about gay culture and wouldn\u2019t understand the stuff Andromeda would talk about. I pointed out that that\u2019s how you get to know people better, is teaching them about things, and that even if it might be bad to, you know, be all protector-y and stuff and then try to sleep with her, you\u2019re supposed to protect your girlfriend/boyfriend, so that\u2019d work out perfect! She was getting all panic-y though, so I started talking about swords and stuff to let her calm down, you know?<br /> <br /> I guess it didn\u2019t calm her down enough though, cause after a bit, I told her I was gonna put on a romantic slow dance song and she should ask Andromeda to dance and it left her stammering again. I got the DJs to put on Bryan Adams and stood between Calamity and the dance floor and waited for her to notice. She looked kinda amusedly exasperated, you know, but she came and danced with me anyway. I think she even enjoyed herself too.<br /> <br /> We spent awhile just dancing, enjoying being close like that, but Everything I Do is a really long song, you know? We wound up talking about stuff for the last bit. She told me Luna wanted to go see her fetch perform at a comedy club after the party and had invited us. She wasn\u2019t specifically planning on murder or anything, but of course, you know, it wasn\u2019t off the table or anything. I told her about my plan for Joan, since she was still kinda sputtering where I left her. It worked out perfectly. After the song was over, Calamity went to ask Andromeda to dance and I went back over to Joan. She was kinda sad when she told me she just couldn\u2019t do it. So I asked her to dance and at just the right moment, I spun her and Calamity spun Andromeda and they wound up dancing together.<br /> <br /> After, Andromeda dragged Joan into a corner and me and Calamity high-fived. We danced to another song or three, but eventually the DJ ran out of romantic ballad type songs, you know, and we both got tired from the faster dancing. Calamity started doing the mingling thing, and I grabbed a table and chilled, wearing the awesome robe that Captain Jack gave me. There was lots more dancing - Jacob danced with Luna, Julia pulled Insincere Marguerite out to dance for the Addams Family song, and then Calamity and Captain Jack did the Mamushka! You know, with the knife-throwing and catching. With Calamity\u2019s teeth. That looked super fun. I might even be convinced to let Captain Jack \u2018sneak\u2019 in to perform it at the Dream House sometime. Lori performed too, singing \u201cAnything Goes\u201d, which was great as always.<br /> <br /> Sometime in the middle of all that, Flores told me there was a lady who wanted to talk with me in the back rooms. Actually talk, you know, not do the usual back room stuff. Her name was Felicity and she\u2019s really pretty. She\u2019s in the Day Court and wanted to kinda ally up with us. I think it\u2019s both for the politics kinda stuff, you know, and also cause she\u2019d had her house broken into and the Courts weren\u2019t being super helpful about it. She\u2019d been kinda allied with the Spring Court for awhile - Captain Jack said she and Princess Jolie had been a couple before she was a Princess - but that didn't end great, I guess.<br /> <br /> She came to me cause she was worried about just showing up, with Insincere Marguerite there and everything. Plus, people said I was chivalrous! I gave her my number in case things got bad and she gave me hers in case the motley was cool to help. I hope so. Something seemed a little... weird, I guess? I kinda wondered if somebody was breaking into her place to look for the Table, but I dunno why she\u2019d get suspected, you know? I guess maybe Joan is rubbing off on me. I do still wanna help her though, cause everybody needs friends and support. I did ask Captain Jack about her. He\u2019s pretty chivalrous too, so I didn\u2019t know why they weren\u2019t allies, you know? I guess he doesn\u2019t have the political clout of a whole mixed Court motley though. She struck him as ambitious, I think. And as hiding something, but not like hiding that she\u2019s a loyalist or anything.<br /> <br /> Stuff eventually started winding down. I made sure to get Austin the dream vessel. I just hope it helps. Captain Jack left by jumping out the skylight, which was awesome. Luna invited Jacob to come to the show so it made for a foursome of us heading out to the comedy club.<br /> <br /> Calamity had used masculine pronouns for Luna\u2019s fetch, but I hadn\u2019t really caught on. He was definitely a dude though. A hilarious dude. It was a super fun time, though I was getting a bit nervous at how much Nathan, the fetch, was looking at Luna. Sometimes fetches can see what we really look like, you know? That wasn\u2019t the case this time - he just thought she looked really familiar. He invited us backstage after, because of that, you know? Me and Jacob had to run interference for a bit when Luna mentioned she knew him from a long time ago and then got flustered cause she didn\u2019t have a story to back it up, you know? Calamity helped her sort it out though.<br /> <br /> Luna decided to stay the night, so we headed back to the Dream House after. I was trying to think of something to do to not sleep, again, and I guess Calamity noticed. She\u2019d had an idea, and hopefully it works out. See, if I\u2019m riding along, you know, in someone else\u2019s dream, it won\u2019t necessarily turn into a nightmare. Hopefully. And if I do it properly, you now, not cheating with a Contract, then I actually get a night\u2019s sleep. We made a pledge, so I could do it properly. So, here\u2019s hoping...<br /> <br /> <br /> May 17<sup>th</sup><br /> <br /> It worked! It took some time, you know, to get centered and stuff. I oughta work on that, probably. But Calamity drifted off to sleep at around the same time and I was able to hop right in and forge a dream. I was kinda aiming to help her out some too, since she had to expend some will to make the pact and everything. I think it worked pretty well.<br /> <br /> I asked Calamity what Luna\u2019s favorite food was. Apparently, it\u2019s \u2018meat\u2019. So I made steak and eggs, which seemed to go over well. Luna was in a super good mood at least, but she was when she came downstairs, so maybe it wasn\u2019t my steak and eggs. Insincere Marguerite and Julia had gone off with Dionisia, but came back in time for breakfast.<br /> <br /> After, it was time for sparring! I I joined in, using a knife this time. It\u2019s easier to spar knife on knife with live steel, than knife on langschwert. Lori decided to watch as soon as she heard Jacob was taking his shirt off, and when I jokingly asked if I should too, De la Roche insisted. Insincere Marguerite and Julia joined them, so we had something of an audience, though between Insincere Marguerite sitting on Julia\u2019s shoulders, and gossip about last night, they were a bit distracted. All to the best I think, cause Lori kept wincing whenever she looked straight at us. Luna won, of course, but it was a damn good showing all around.<br /> <br /> I took advantage of a break to let folks know about Felicity. Insincere Marguerite was not super thrilled, you know, with her being Day Court, but we agreed to talk with her at least (and have her come here, after Insincere Marguerite made a bunch of comments about how big her house was). She\u2019s coming by tomorrow afternoon. Joan stopped by about that time to let us know she was \u2018protecting\u2019 Andromeda. Andromeda\u2019s even moving in with her and has some ideas for decorating. Not that it\u2019s a gigantic shock or anything, but she found Joan\u2019s place a little spartan, you know?<br /> <br /> Calamity managed to talk her into staying awhile and sparring some. I swapped over to sword and board with her, so it was the knife trio against the shield wall. Now, that was tons of fun. I hadn't been in a shield wall since before I was taken. Joan\u2019s technical precision and control are amazing. And Luna\u2019s tactics are exhausting to guard against. It was certainly a workout.<br /> <br /> Tonight was one of our big shows, so we eventually had to call a stop to get ready. Luna decided to stick around to see the show, and Joan came back with Andromeda in tow. Andromeda was totally hanging all over Joan, you know, and Joan was feeding her cheese fries. They were adorable. Luna looked like she was having tons of fun hanging out with Jacob at the bar. I checked in on our other regulars too. You know, Moon and Dionisia, Monica and Haley. They were all doing good. Monica was a little nervous about Andromeda being with Joan, but was still happy for Joan, you know? Ginny wasn\u2019t so happy. Chalcedony had disappeared again, after giving her the slip during the party. I think Lori and D are... cheering her up, I guess.<br /> <br /> Desiree was there too, and I wound up talking to her for awhile. We\u2019d been kinda flirting, you know, for a little bit when Calamity joined us, and then we were all really flirting. I was a little uncertain about having someone over, since the guest room was occupied for the night, and her place... well, there\u2019s the mannikins, and, you know. But Calamity was definitely up for it, so that was all good. She wound up staying with us, which was pretty damn awesome.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Okay, so the last time I wrote in this diary, I was waxing rhapsodic about the changes my character has gone through recently, and preparing for the big fete the Spring Court was throwing in our honor.<br /> <br /> Ah, the party! The party was something else. Pretty much everyone who\u2019s anyone in Changeling society was there, and they were there to honor us and our efforts on behalf of the freehold. We got a huge round of applause as we entered, and they threw a spotlight on us and everything. I\u2019m used to the attention, of course, but some of the others looked a little less comfortable at being in the public eye.<br /> <br /> Before we dispersed to make the rounds and play the social game, Calamity introduced us to her friend/mentor, Luna. She\u2019s a startlingly attractive dark-haired beauty with moth wings. While she was friendly enough, I could tell after a few minutes of conversation that she was not comfortable with all the attention, so I said my farewells to give her a little bit of breathing room and started making the rounds.<br /> <br /> Aside from the guests of honor \u2013 <i>tee-hee</i> \u2013 most of the crowd\u2019s attention was focused on Captain Jack, whose outfit looked like a cross between Elton John\u2019s armoire and Glitter Gulch in Las Vegas. Seriously, his name was spelled out on his chest in blinking Christmas lights. What\u2019s more, he gave Gawain a similar \u2013 if slightly less garish \u2013 robe as a \u201cwell done bro\u201d gift. At least it was green.<br /> <br /> Joan was there, which sort of surprised me a little. I know that she approves of how we took care of the fetch, but this sort of social gathering really doesn\u2019t seem like her scene. The others told me why she was there later\u2026 she has an enormous crush on Andromeda! I suppose I should have seen it earlier; she\u2019s always been the little alien girl\u2019s staunchest supporter. Though I was\u2026 otherwise occupied while all this was going on, it seems that my friends proved more than equal to the role of matchmakers.<br /> <br /> Gawain arranged it all, getting the DJ to play some slow romantic song from the 80s and pulling Joan out on to the dance floor. Calamity picked up on the cues, and likewise started dancing with Andromeda. The two of them deftly maneuvered the other two into close quarters and then spun into each other\u2019s arms, leaving Joan and Andromeda dancing together! I wish I could have seen it; it sounds like it was very well plotted.<br /> <br /> Where was I during all this? Why, hanging out with royalty, of course!<br /> <br /> We\u2019d only been at the party for about twenty minutes when Jolie approached me, looking ravishing as always in a low-cut green dress. She slid up next to me and gave D a warm smile. \u201cExcuse me, my dear,\u201d she purred, \u201cI hope you won\u2019t mind if I steal your paramour away for a little while?\u201d<br /> <br /> D shook her head. \u201cOf course not, Princess,\u201d she said, but her smile didn\u2019t quite reach her eyes. She gave me a quick kiss on the cheek. \u201cHave fun,\u201d she whispered, giving my arm a squeeze.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t want you to think that I just ignored her feelings. I\u2019m not that heartless; I am in love with that girl, for Pete\u2019s sake. But I\u2019d wanted Jolie for so long that I knew I\u2019d always wonder what it would have been like if I let this chance slip by. And\u2026 in a way, I thought it might be good for my relationship with D. If she can watch me \u201cstray\u201d and then see me come back to her more in love than ever, maybe it\u2019ll build her confidence in what we have.<br /> <br /> She needs to know that I\u2019ll <u>always</u> come back to her.<br /> <br /> So I spent the next hour or so schmoozing with Jolie. We danced, we talked, she bought me drinks (rather a lot of drinks, actually). When I tried to return the favor, the bartender wouldn\u2019t take my money. \u201cThis is your night, sweetie,\u201d Jolie said, laughing at my consternation, \u201cenjoy it!\u201d<br /> <br /> She also all but insisted that I perform at least one song on stage. I wonder if she would have been so persistent about it if she hadn\u2019t known how much I enjoy being the center of attention. In any case, I spoke to the DJ, grabbed a live mic, and slinked up onto the stage to perform the Cole Porter classic \u201cAnything Goes.\u201d Since there were no mortals present, I couldn\u2019t gather any glamour from the performance, but I still had a blast.<br /> <br /> The Princess liked it. As I stepped down from the stage, she gave me a come-hither look that I sincerely hope was a spontaneous expression of her desire for me\u2026 but more realistically was probably calculated to set my lady parts aquiver. In any case, I went-thither like a shot. She pulled me into one of Flores\u2019 back rooms, locked and bolted the door, and pinned me to the wall with her body.<br /> <br /> Oh my God, her <u>body</u>. Her skin tastes sweet, like strawberries and spring water, and her hair is so soft and smooth that it was like running my hands over the finest silk. Her laughter was like the ringing of bells, and every gasp and moan and grunt came together in an almost symphonic way.<br /> <br /> Our dresses came off before we even made it to the bed, and there she was. It was what I\u2019d wanted to see ever since I\u2019d come to Malibu five months ago. She was everything I\u2019d hoped for and more. She was holy; a priestess\u2026 a goddess. So I did the only thing I could think of: I knelt and worshipped her.<br /> <br /> I was lost in her embrace for\u2026 I\u2019m not really sure how long. It was divine. I can\u2019t put it any other way. I\u2019ve never known another woman who could affect me that way. Well, maybe <u>one</u>\u2026 but with the Empress, it was more about adoration than desire. I couldn\u2019t be in the same room with her and <u>not</u> obsess over her though, and in that way things were pretty much the same with Jolie.<br /> <br /> It would be crude to go into the details of what happened here, but let me just say that Jolie is as skilled as she is beautiful. She\u2019s a caring, giving lover, though neither of us ever completely lost sight of the fact that she is a monarch and I am her subject. Her commands were subtler, gentler than Insincere Marguerite\u2019s, and maybe that\u2019s why I didn\u2019t mind submitting to them. Or maybe it\u2019s just because I\u2019ve sworn my loyalty to the Spring Court anyway. Whatever.<br /> <br /> Minutes or hours later it was over, and we were basking in the afterglow. \u201cSo,\u201d she said with a catlike stretch that did interesting things to her breasts, \u201care you reconsidering my offer?\u201d<br /> <br /> I looked into her eyes, and I saw warmth there, and genuine affection, and the heat of desire simmering just below the surface. But there was something missing. Something I never knew I\u2019d want before a few weeks ago. It\u2019s not just chemicals, like I\u2019d always suspected. It\u2019s not just psychology responding to pleasure, reassurance, and sympathy. There\u2019s something more, and it wasn\u2019t there when I looked at Jolie.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sorry,\u201d I said softly, stroking her cheek. \u201cI really am. What we just shared was\u2026 <u>amazing</u>, but I\u2019m spoken for.\u201d<br /> <br /> She smiled sadly and kissed me one more time. \u201cI understand,\u201d she said kindly. \u201cI won\u2019t pretend I\u2019m happy about it, but I respect your decision. Now, we should get back out there, or people will start to talk.\u201d<br /> <br /> I snorted out a very unladylike laugh. \u201cYeah, that\u2019d be just <u>awful</u>,\u201d I said with a giggle. \u201cWe both <u>hate</u> to be the center of attention, after all.\u201d<br /> <br /> She laughed with me, and seemed to come out of her funk just a little bit. We got dressed quickly, and each of us made sure not a hair was out of place before heading for the door. Just before she opened it, though, I stopped her and pulled one of the straps of my dress off my shoulder. If anyone <u>was</u> paying attention, at least I gave them something to talk about!<br /> <br /> (Although it occurs to me now that Jolie might have been so keen to get into my panties in such a public place as part of a plot to make Queen Charlotte jealous. I really hope that\u2019s not the case, as I do not need any enemies as powerful and scary as that lady).<br /> <br /> By the time I rejoined the rest of the motley, things were starting to break up. Jacob, Calamity, and Gawain were going to accompany Luna to a local comedy club to see some local comedian perform (I\u2019m still not sure what that was all about). Insincere Marguerite and Julia had hooked up with Dionysia at some point, and the three of them left together. I\u2019m not sure what happened to Ace; I hadn\u2019t really seen him since we got to the Rose &amp; Thorn, but I think he might have been propping up the bar.<br /> <br /> I walked toward D and called out a greeting, and she responded with a subdued \u201chey.\u201d I felt my stomach drop at that; usually she\u2019s much more expressive.<br /> <br /> A slow song started. \u201cWanna dance?\u201d I asked her quietly. She muttered something that sounded like \u201csure\u201d and allowed me to lead her out onto the dance floor.<br /> <br /> I held her close and we swayed back and forth to the music. As the song was winding down, I leaned in and whispered, unsure if she could even hear me over the noise of the club. \u201cPlease,\u201d I said, choking back tears, \u201cplease tell me that I haven\u2019t just fucked up the best thing that\u2019s happened to me since I escaped Arcadia.\u201d<br /> <br /> She turned to look at me, and I saw genuine surprise surface in her eyes. \u201cYou haven\u2019t,\u201d she said, giving me a squeeze.<br /> <br /> \u201cGood,\u201d I said. \u201cBecause, you know, I\u2019ve <u>maybe</u> wanted to get Jolie in the sack ever since I first came to Malibu, but\u2026\u201d I felt my bottom lip start to quiver, and I hated myself for it. I knew the tears weren\u2019t far behind.<br /> <br /> Luckily D spared me the indignity. She grabbed my head in both hands and pulled me into a passionate kiss. \u201cI know,\u201d she said when we parted.<br /> <br /> I looked around, and noticed that the club was starting to empty. It was only about midnight, but I guess when half the motley left to go watch some stand-up, people decided that the party was over. \u201cYou want to get out of here?\u201d I asked. \u201cWe can go somewhere fun. Just the two of us.\u201d D nodded, and we walked toward the exit together.<br /> <br /> We had no idea what we were going to do. Several ideas were pitched, including a late-night breakfast at a diner somewhere, an attempt to find a club with a decent band, and people-watching at the pier. Hell, I even suggested night surfing, since surfing is something I\u2019ve always wanted to try (and I know D can surf). As we were driving around, though, the answer dropped into our laps.<br /> <br /> \u201cHoly shit!\u201d I exclaimed as we drove past a stately old theater. \u201cPeople are still doing that?\u201d<br /> <br /> D looked where I was pointing and laughed. \u201cHell, yeah,\u201d she said. \u201cIt\u2019s a classic now.\u201d She glanced at her watch. \u201cThe next show starts in twenty minutes. You\u2019re maybe a little overdressed, but do you wanna\u2026?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019d love to,\u201d I said, and promptly pulled into the parking lot.<br /> <br /> The pageantry and rituals of <u>The Rocky Horror Picture Show</u> have evolved a lot over the years, but at its core it\u2019s still the same risqu\u00e9, raunchy romp it always was. I had a blast, from shouting out <u>ASSHOLE!</u> every time someone said Brad\u2019s name to getting pulled up on to the little stage in front of the screen to do the Time Warp with a few other audience members. I couldn\u2019t be pulled into the \u201cvirgin\u201d ritual hazing, because I saw the show last year when Missy, Jane and I visited Jane\u2019s sister up in Des Moines\u2026<br /> <br /> Shit. I mean back in \u201977. Whatever. Anyway, Dad would have been pissed if he\u2019d found out.<br /> <br /> Somehow, through fits of giggles, I managed to drive us back to D\u2019s apartment after the show. We fell into bed together, still laughing, and talked for an hour or so before drifting off to sleep in each other\u2019s arms. I think \u2013 I <u>hope</u> \u2013 that things are okay between us now. I mean, we didn\u2019t really <u>talk</u> about Jolie or anything, but things felt like they were back to normal.<br /> <br /> We woke up around noon, cuddled, talked some more, and inevitably drifted back to the Dream House for an early afternoon breakfast a la Gawain. Luna was there, and she seemed more relaxed than she had on the previous evening. Apparently things went well at the comedy club\u2026 the group of them even got to meet the comedian in person. Also, Luna seemed oddly solicitous of Jacob, which makes me wonder if the two of them\u2026<br /> <br /> Anyway, Calamity, Luna, Jacob and Gawain were sparring in the yard, so the rest of us sat under one of the big shade trees and watched\u2026 which had absolutely <u>nothing</u> to do with the fact that Jacob took his shirt off, despite any pointed comments Julia might have made along those lines. I <u>did</u> make some comment about how they should spar in teams, shirts versus skins, at which point Julia asked if I would be participating.<br /> <br /> \u201cSweetie,\u201d I said in a smoky voice, \u201cif you want a peep, all you have to do is ask.\u201d I pulled up my shirt and briefly flashed her my breasts. She got this sort of dazed happy look on her face, and I heard D stifling laughter behind me.<br /> <br /> After that I leaned back against the trunk of the tree to enjoy the show. D snuggled up on my right, and Julia leaned up against me on the left, and after a few minutes, Marguerite stretched out across all three of our laps, purring like a big contented cat as we gently stroked her sides. It was a pleasant way to spend the afternoon.<br /> <br /> Gawain also told us that he had met with another Changeling at the party the previous evening; a representative of the Day Court named Felicity. She came to him to ask for our help, since her house has been robbed recently and she didn\u2019t feel comfortable going to the seasonal courts directly for assistance in this matter. We discussed it between ourselves, and decided \u2013 over Marguerite\u2019s inexplicable objections \u2013 that we\u2019d offer to do what we could. We\u2019re supposed to meet with her later today.<br /> <br /> Joan stopped by this afternoon as well, and she was as happy as I\u2019ve ever seen her. I mean, she still had that stoic exterior, but it was like there was a light behind her eyes if you knew how to look for it. I know that D noticed it too, and it seemed to make her happy. She joined in the sparring, too\u2026 she and Gawain used swords and shields while the others attacked with knives. If either team \u201cwon\u201d the mock combat, it was a mystery to me.<br /> <br /> But time, tide, and curtain calls wait for no woman, so eventually we had to go back in and get ready for the evening. For my first number, I performed \u201cThose Shoes\u201d by the Eagles\u2026 kinda-sorta as a reminder to myself that even the smallest actions can have consequences. I don\u2019t regret spending time with Princess Jolie the other day, but I <u>do</u> still remember how scared I was when I thought I had really screwed things up with D in the aftermath.<br /> <br /> My second solo was \u201cSmoke Gets In Your Eyes.\u201d I\u2019m mostly familiar with the version recorded by The Platters, but I know it\u2019s a much older song that\u2019s seen many releases over the years, and it makes a hell of a torch song if performed with a certain twist. I tried to instill both sorrow and desire into my performance, so that it would slake the thirst of our guests from both the Spring and Winter Courts.<br /> <br /> After the show I started hobnobbing as per usual. D seemed to be in a frisky mood, so I started looking around to see if anyone might be interested in sharing our bed for the evening. My gaze fell upon two of our heartbroken friends: Davey and Ginny. Davey was still moping about Dark Kimberly\u2019s recently revealed relationship with Annika, while Ginny was still fretting over Chalcedony\u2019s less-than-effervescent attitude regarding their recent fling.<br /> <br /> I considered going after Davey. He\u2019s cute and sweet as hell, and I thought he might be grateful for the chance to forget about his troubles for a while. Plus, it\u2019s been a few weeks since I\u2019ve been with a guy, and I thought it would be nice to remind myself that I\u2019m <u>bi</u>sexual. But D always gets sort of weird when I mention bringing a guy into the bed we share, and\u2026 well, Davey\u2019s a friend and he\u2019s hurting right now, and I don\u2019t want to risk doing anything that might make his situation worse.<br /> <br /> So the two of us made our way to the bar and started talking with Ginny, who by this point was quite drunk and eager to be consoled. Predictably, one thing led to another, and the three of us ended up heading upstairs to my room together after a few minutes. I won\u2019t go into details on the evening that followed, but I will say that I enjoyed myself immensely\u2026 and repeatedly. Though D and I have gotten a lot of practice lately, Ginny still has more experience with lesbian sex than either of us, and she was eager to share her expertise.<br /> <br /> Plus\u2026 a lesbian who can hold her breath for half an hour has certain natural advantages over the rest of us. \u2018Nuff said.<br /> <br /> The two of them are curled up together on my bed right now, and it\u2019s <u>soooo</u> cute. D\u2019s never been a morning person, and Ginny was <u>really</u> wasted last night, so it\u2019s no surprise that I was the first to wake up. I can\u2019t help it; I\u2019m restless this morning\u2026 I want to go out and do something. D will grumble if I wake her up, but I flatter myself by thinking that she\u2019ll be happy to spend time with me anyway.<br /> <br /> And now, after thinking about it for a minute, and looking at my love as she lies with the sheets wrapped around her waist, I know what I want to do today. It\u2019s been in the back of my mind for a while now, but I finally have the time to do it right. It\u2019s time to put all those lessons Dad put me through as a kid to good use. I think I\u2019m going to go out and buy a piano. Show the Dream House\u2019s patrons that I\u2019m not just a one-trick pony (or a two-trick pony, I suppose, since I\u2019m already singing and dancing on stage).<br /> <br /> Plus\u2026 looking at D, I think I might be ready to start writing my own songs.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> <u><b><b><u>Saturday May 17<sup>th </sup></u></b></b> </u><br /> <br /> The moon is waning but still too close to full for prowling. But as I gaze up at it I feel so restless. I think I used to feel this way in Snow Globe on nights like this. Too bright to skulk about safely and yet, like tonight, I'd be out instead of in bed like I should be. The daystar isn't far away at this point. I can feel it lurking below the horizon, crawling along to set the sky aflame. I should bed down before it casts it's baleful and unblinking eye over me. Only... Desiree is in my bed. I can't curl up with my knight with her there. I'll have to find somewhere else to sleep... or maybe I'll just stay up. Might be better... Can't dream while I'm awake and I don't think Gawain needs to see what's dancing about my sick mind right now...<br /> <br /> Desiree is such a pretty little thing... so soft... that delightful skin... perfect for marking with my razors...those bright and expressive eyes... Oh how they would show her fear and pain... But I was a good little monster, I played nice with our toy. She was clearly a bit uncertain about coming to bed with another woman earlier, so I was very attentive to her. Oh yes, I coaxed that pretty sweetling quite thoroughly... I took such good care of her... her and Gawain both. I made sure they enjoyed themselves. And now they're both asleep, worn out and peaceful and vulnerable. I watched them for a while after I slipped from the bed but I had to slip away.<br /> <br /> Luna's not in the guest room. I guess things went well with her and Jacob last night. I must admit, I had hoped she'd approve of him as a student but I had not considered that she'd take a fancy to him. I do hope this isn't going to cause issues with whatever he and Insincere Marguerite have going. Of course, she's got sweet little julia and has been fucking Lori and her girl so it shouldn't. But one never knows, we all get strange when we think with our hearts rather than our brains.<br /> <br /> The house is so quiet. I have the run of the place it seems. Everyone is curled up safe and sleeping and warm. I think I'll take a cigar with my old friend Jack on the front balcony while it's still tolerably dark out.<br /> <br /> ~ ~ ~<br /> <br /> That's better, got a nice pleasant burn in my belly and my lungs both now. My new watch is loose. I should see about getting the band taken in if I'm going to actually wear it regularly. I'm not normally one for trophies but I find myself rather taken with it. As I twist my wrist and watch the moonlight play and reflect off it I keep seeing his eyes... Oh how wide his eyes were and that perfect little quiver in his lip as he begged me to take it to take whatever I wanted... His fear was so delicious... just like poor little Timmy back in Snow Globe. The replacement of course. Oh I imagine he was so relieved to find a new Jane waiting to be walked to school after I escaped. He'd been there a couple of days before he finally asked me if he seemed different. I smiled at the boy and nodded. I explained that sometimes people faded away or vanished and were replaced. I told him we all knew but the others were too afraid of the Whispering Voices to act different. He asked me if I knew what happened to the old Timmy... I just smiled wider and turned to face him. I knew that I was in trouble already so I didn't hold back, I pushed him against the wall and leaned in so close. His eyes were so wide and confused. He was bigger then me but he was too stunned to do anything to stop me. I lifted myself up on my tip toes and whispered into his ear. I told him I'd killed the old Timmy. I described how I lured him to the well and pushed him in and waited. How I'd listened to him crying and wailing and begging me to help him as he bled out in dark. Then I kissed him with my lips and my teeth until I could taste his blood and skipped away. Oh the Whispers were displeased with me that night but it was worth it to see that fear in his eyes every morning when he came to walk me to school and when we played. Watching and wondering if I was going to play nice or if I was going to do something bad... Better to succeed at disobedience than to fail at behaving. Better to be punished on my terms than for falling short of the perfection They demanded of us all. Better a wolf than a sheep. and the wolf never loses sleep over the opinions of sheep.<br /> <br /> It's strange, I'd forgotten about that until the other night. Not until I had that filthy pig pushed up against the wall and cowering. It suddenly came back to me. I know I should feel bad about it but Timmy was weak... soft... prey... And a wolf never loses sleep over the opinion of sheep. Other things are coming back as well since then, snippets and fragments. I wonder what else I have forgotten about that thrice-damned place. Hopefully these other bits will fall into place and not just continue to tease me like cheap whores.<br /> <br /> At least the last couple of days have been good. The party was quite fun. I think I may have squealed to see Luna there when we arrived, which thankfully went unnoticed as Captain Jack hit Gawain with a spotlight as we entered. I introduced Luna to the motley, which was a bit of a crowd for her and so everyone disbursed rather quickly except for Jacob. He is interested in the fighting techniques she taught me and I think the both of them were pleased to find someone to talk wilderness survival with.<br /> <br /> I spent the early part of the evening close to Luna catching up and just enjoying her presence. Gawain keep checking on us, attentive and thoughtful as always. Captain Jack in addition to his own outlandish outfit (tight pants and a harness of lights... only someone with his sheer over the top showmanship could pull that off.) had brought a custom robe for Gawain. Green with an embroidered sword and Gawain's name spelled out in lights down the back. I swear, that man is truly, truly, truly, truly outrageous. But he manages to pull it off well, much like Ace.<br /> <br /> Joan approached me and started to ask me about Becky, which seemed odd. She started to ask my opinion of Becky's abilities as protector and clearly was fishing for me to agree that my favorite draconian succubus was lacking at her job. I kept my feathers smooth, mainly because I was more interested in why Joan was asking than in a fight at my own victory celebration. (Something I am sure Lori would never have forgiven me for) So I managed to give a fairly non-committal answer and it quickly because apparent that Joan's focus was Andromeda and the stolen table. From there, it quickly because clear that she was quite infatuated with the wee gray sweetling. But she was wound up with concerns about propriety and harming the girl. I couldn't resist dropping some forward comments about Andromeda's endurance. I really was hoping it would break the tension a little and open the way to trying to talk her up to approaching her crush but Joan turned quite red and fled to the ladies room.<br /> <br /> Thankfully, Gawain caught enough to take up where I had left off. And because he is a far better person than I am, he caught Joan when she came out of the restroom and had a much more productive conversation with her. Then he went and requested a string of slow dance numbers leading off with Everything I do, I do For You. Yeah... even got the long album version. And as it started, he just stood there at the edge of the dance floor waiting for me. Big silly lug... It's ironic, he is everything Katt dreamed of but if she'd never been taken I'd never have met him.<br /> <br /> His stunt drew some attention, I mean... Bryan Adams? Really? And I think it brought a few more eyebrows when I marched up to him and let him sweep me onto the dance floor. Yeah, I guess it was more than a little out of character as far as they know but what the fuck ever. I let my man lead me around the dance floor and hold me close like some sort of high school romance. And as we danced, the matter of another romance came up, and a plan was hatched. A plan cheesy and high school enough to match the moment perfectly.<br /> <br /> Gawain went and asked Joan to dance. I went and asked Andromeda (Yes, I did actually ask rather than order). Then, midway through the song, we both did a spin and turned and suddenly he and I were dancing and Joan and Andromeda were in each others arms. I'll confess, I had not expected it to work anywhere near that smoothly but it was some kind flawless prestidigitation that shouldn't be possible outside of a romantic musical. Handsome and I shared a well earned celebratory high five and then I let him hold me all close and tight and sway me about the floor till the DJ got tired of slow songs. (which was just a couple of songs later to be honest) Now that I am actually learning to dance, I may have to see about learning the big guy something a bit showy for the next time. I mean, if he is going to insist on dancing we ought to do something impressive. Maybe a tango? It's a classic standby for showing off and being sexy...<br /> <br /> Anyway, after Gawain's dance revolution was over, I drifted back to Luna and that's went she mentioned that she had her eye on Jacob. She had also invited him to come to see her fetch perform at a local comedy club. She was a bit nervous about that, as she'd not approached her fetch and inviting Jacob was potentially awkward as her fetch is male. Yeah, not a story I've ever gotten out of her in any detail. All I know is her Keeper took a man and made the lovely femme fatal that is my mentor from him. It was a little weird to see her uncertain about anything, but people really aren't her element at all. And I'm glad I went with her to the club.<br /> <br /> But as she was actually enjoying talking to Jacob, I pointed out that I should circulate as I was one of the guests of honor. She agreed and I did spend the latter half of the party making the rounds. I noticed that Andromeda had taken the opportunity to drag Joan into a corner and initiate a make out session. And julia had requested the theme song to the Addams Family to dance with Insincere Margrethe, which apparently got Captain Jack in the mood to dance the Mamushka...<br /> <br /> That ogre 's spirit is infectious and what can I say, this monster likes anything involving knives. I am not sure everyone in attendance was ready for us to storm the floor and start throwing knives about and I haven't watched that movie since I returned so I was making it up as I went along as much as anything. But no one ended up missing any body parts and I had a blast. I suppose Captain jack did manage to get me high that night. It also give me some ideas for my own act eventually. I mean, I'm never going to be able to deliver the sheer sensuality that Annika does or sing like Lori. And even if I could, I need something my own, something that suits Calamity. Which means, really, something with knives. Sword dancing or knife throwing or perhaps some combination... At any rate, it is a direction to investigate. And in the mean time Gawain suggested letting Jack sneak in so he and I can do that again on stage some time... That would be fun.<br /> <br /> After that, Jack made a suitably cinematic exit by leaping up to the catwalks and out the skylight (conveniently opened for him by Flores) and things started to wind down. So Luna, Gawain, Jacob, and myself went to see her fetch perform. He was amusing though it was hard to imagine the beautiful and deadly mothwoman at my side had come from such a decidedly effeminate stock. Though, I suppose this could be a case of her fetch being as outgoing as she was introverted perhaps. At any rate, I'm pretty sure Jacob caught on to why we were there fairly quickly. For as different as they were there were clues for the observant. Clearly it did not dissuade him from, as Luna would put it, a good rutting. I won't lie, I certainly have thought about what it would be like but Luna does not particularly care for females. So she does have at least that in common with her fetch.<br /> <br /> As the show ended, we received word that he was interested in seeing us backstage. Well, Luna but we all tagged along. He didn't seem to be able to see her truly but he did have a strong feeling of familiarity. He started asking about where he might know her from and where she'd grown up and gone to school. Innocent enough but Luna had not come expecting to talk to him and was, quite frankly, flat footed. I could see her tensing and growing flustered and so a caught her arm and pulled her aside, leaving Gawain and Jacob to distract the comedian while I took a moment to calm my friend and help her get a story straight. She'd already told him she'd gone to the same high school so I suggested she just stick with that and tell him she remembered him from there.<br /> <br /> We returned and, now prepared, she gave him her cover and they exchanged a few common memories and everything seemed to be smoothed over. Then just as we were making our excuses to take our leave he got that look and started to really stare at Luna like he'd started to notice something. I don't know if he was starting to see through her mask or if he was realizing that she looked familiar because she looked like him but we cut the goodbyes short and pretty much fled at that point. Luna said she had quite gotten the urge to see her fetch out of her system and then pointed out that she'd gotten a ride in and asked about staying over for the night. I agreed, of course, as we have plenty of space and I was happy to have a chance to cross blades with her before she returned.<br /> <br /> And I did get to do just that. After a breakfast of steak and eggs (since Gawain asked after Luna's favorite foods and I informed him that she is a fairly devoted carnivore) we ended up heading out to the back for a workout. Gawain joined us, taking up knives rather than his sword and Jacob got a chance to test himself against Luna. Lori suggested shirts verses skins (perhaps only to convince Jacob and Gawain to take off their shirts) but in the end it was more free for all (though both the boys did go shirtless).<br /> <br /> It was glorious. Luna was the clear master but we made her work for it. It feels so good to be able to keep up with her and give her an actual challenge. I have come such a long way from the wild slasher that stalked out into the woods to challenge her to train me. And having Gawain join in was nice. Even with a smaller blade he's a power fighter and it's a good change to keep me from falling into bad habits or getting too used to fighting other quick types. Everyone was in excellent form and I knew I didn't need to hold back and was able to just let myself go. It was just fucking amazing.<br /> <br /> And when we did take a break and join the girls who were watching from the shade and grab some drinks it felt like every fiber in my body was still humming and overstrung. It feels so good to just let everything melt away. But Then Gawain started talking about Felicity. She's a Day Courtier that quietly met with him at the party to ask after a meeting with us. Apparently she's dealing with the issues Jolie warned Gawain and Insincere Margrethe about. She's got no strong ties to a seasonal court and so no one is inclined to help her with her troubles, which apparently include Lucien Torrez (as she's not Latino) and some breaks ins. According to Captain Jack she's a serious man eater and his gut tells him she's not trustworthy though she's apparently dealt straight with him but it may very well be only because she can't wrap him around her finger. The Day court and Night court are, as I understand it, sworn enemies and Insincere Margrethe certainly was not keen on having this woman in our house or entertaining any notions of being 'good neighbors' with her. For my own part, I feel like she's trouble. Gawain is a fellow non-seasonal courtier and so her approaching him alone and first is not unreasonable, but if Captain jack's gut is right (and I would never question a gut so majestic) it could very well be that Gawain is known to be trusting and susceptible to her feminine whiles. Of course, Gawain likes to look for the good in people. The rest of the Motley seemed inclined to hear her out at least and I agree that we should see what she wants from us. I'm not going to speak directly against Gawain on this one but neither he nor any of the others seemed to appreciate my Darkling sister's position. It may be that she and I need to deal with this bitch quietly. I'll make sure that she knows that her enemies are my enemies and that I am ready, willing, and able to do what needs to be done even if the others can't know about it.<br /> <br /> We'd decided to go ahead and meet her the next afternoon when Joan showed up. She had come to inform us that she'd taken Andromeda under her protection (and, I believe, to squee with someone over being in a relationship with her but without admitting it). The woman is still wound up tighter than a hummingbird's ass but I think she and Andromeda will be good for each other. I mean, they are both kinda fucked up but they also both really needed someone and while they're certainly a strange couple they were most certainly a couple. Also, I know Joan will protect that little pretty alien (which the sweet little lamb needs desperately).<br /> <br /> While she was there, I asked her if she'd be interested in joining the sparring. I've been curious to see just how good she is since I met her. I wasn't sure she'd be game but perhaps it was a productive enough form of recreation or maybe she was just flying high on new relationship energy. Gawain was eager to fight at her side, happy to have a shield partner and so the rest of us went knives against them. It was a very different fight from the chaotic melee. Joan's defense was amazing and I was almost jealous of how well she and Gawain worked together. Though to be fair, Jacob was almost as flawlessly part of Luna's offense as I was. It is such a joy to dance with skilled partners. By the time the others called a halt I was sore in all the right places and perfectly spent. I could have kept going but I was honestly content and satisfied. And it was time to prepare for the show by then anyway.<br /> <br /> I was still feeling quite pleased as I circulated the incoming patrons. Luna had quite readily agreed to stay another night rather than trouble anyone for a ride with the show (though given that she spent the show at the bar paying Jacob more attention than the performance it was clear she had an ulterior motive) Davey was there and still clearly forlorn over Dark Kimberly's whirlwind relationship with Annika. And Ginny was there and down that Chalcedony had slipped away from the party and gone silent on her again. On the flip side, Desiree was looking cheerful for the reprieve from Chalcedony's hostility.<br /> <br /> Gawain ended up gravitating to Desiree's table as the show wound down and as I drifted by to check up on them there was some mild but unmistakable flirting going back and forth. But Gawain tossed me an uncertain look and glanced over at the bar where Luna was still seated when I came by and I recalled he'd mentioned the mannequins around Desiree's apartment. I figured he wasn't sure if it was cool and we haven't really talked about either of us bringing someone else into our bed. Honestly, the thought didn't sit entirely well with me since that is our space now but it also wasn't the time or place to sort it out either. But Desiree is a delicious little morsel and we had mused on that before so I inserted myself into Gawain\u2019s lap and the conversation and made it clear I was going to be part any further inserting. Gawain was fine with the idea and while Desiree seemed less excited by another woman's involvement she wasn't completely turned off either. And by the end of the evening I'd managed to peak her interest enough to join Gawain and I.<br /> <br /> Now I'm sitting here alone writing in this diary. Jack ran out on me a couple of pages ago and Katt's been gone a long time. The moon's set and the edge of the sky's turning. I'm going to lock this little book up safely and find a nice dark corner to curl up in. Maybe I'll see if I can't wake handsome and our toy up so I can play with her a bit more... On second thought, I should leave them be. I'd have to be gentle and I've had my fill of that for one night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T14:30:22-08:00","id":347002,"title":"","content":"<b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Well, that was an interesting party. It was nice to not be the one serving drinks. Kinda strange, but nice. I talked to Lowjack and Tamara for a bit and danced to something peppy with Tamara. She\u2019s not a bad dancer. She, Lowjack and Molly were the only Winter court folks to show up. Not that I\u2019m surprised, but I thought there might be an off chance others might show. I\u2019m pretty sure no Winter court people would have shown if I hadn\u2019t invited Lowjack to come. I figured a friendly face would be nice. <br /> <br /> They played some slow 80\u2019s song, I think someone said it was Bryan Adams. Anyhoo\u2026Gawain and Calamity danced to that. They make such a cute couple. I had been considering asking Insincere Marguerite to dance when another slow song played, but the look on her face convinced me otherwise. Not a big fan of 80\u2019s slow rock, I guess? When something faster started playing I asked if she wanted to dance. She did. It was nice. Definitely want to do that again at some point.<br /> <br /> Later Calamity introduced us to Luna, her mentor. I\u2019ll admit that I had been curious to meet the woman that taught Calamity how to fight. She stood by herself wearing a long blue dress, which looked nice on her, but she seemed a bit uncomfortable in. She doesn\u2019t do these social gatherings very often, so I can understand the feeling. The fact that she came to this thing for Calamity says a lot. To me anyway. Oh\u2026she also has large, purple moth wings. They were beautiful. Slightly different shades of purple throughout. I wonder if she can fly or glide?<br /> <br /> Anyway\u2026after the initial uncomfortableness on all sides we introduced ourselves and made a bit of small talk. Most of the others politely stepped away, leaving me and Calamity alone with her mentor. I asked what I\u2019d been wondering for a while, and found that Calamity had actually been brought to Luna for training. I didn\u2019t follow up on that. After a bit more awkward conversation Luna admitted that she was used to spending time alone, and that this was the most she usually spoke in a whole year. I couldn\u2019t help but smile, and agreed that quiet time was definitely under-rated as far as I was concerned. I think she said something about Darklings preferring to spend time alone. I understand that, and told her as much. Since I escaped I\u2019ve become friends with a couple of Darklings, and in the Lady\u2019s service, my best friend was a Darkling. Though I didn\u2019t mention that last part. I just said that I\u2019ve been friends with several Darklings.<br /> <br /> After a little while I got up the courage to ask Luna if I could spar with her sometime. She grinned just a bit, and that was a predatory smile on her face if I\u2019ve ever seen one. Calamity was keen on joining in, so we planned it for tomorrow morning/early afternoon. I\u2019m looking forward to that, let me tell you. I\u2019ve had a lot of fun sparring with Calamity and I\u2019ve learned a bit of her style already. It\u2019s pretty easy to incorporate into my own semi-style of fighting. Her style has a couple of special moves designed to help you take advantage of someone\u2019s weak points, and some that put you at a bit more risk, but it definitely increases your chance of landing a palpable hit. I figured if it was that much fun to spar with the student, then I wanted to take on the Master. I figured pretty much from the time I asked that I\u2019d be getting my ass handed to me, but that\u2019s how you learn. That\u2019s how I learned anyway. Rook never held back when teaching me to fight. He always said that the enemy would not hesitate to hurt me, and that in order to keep me among the living he wasn\u2019t going to teach me to \u201cplay fight\u201d first. He was just going to teach me to fight, and he did. I got the impression from Luna\u2019s face, and from Calamity\u2019s reaction that her mentor has a similar philosophy. <br /> <br /> I\u2019ll admit that I was hoping to get at least a little bit of respect from Calamity\u2019s teacher. Yeah, it was a bit of an ego thing. I am not a novice fighter. I know I\u2019m good. My career has spoken to that most assuredly. But, to be regarded by a Master as something worth paying attention to is something that all fighters look for. I think I earned at least a bit when I asked her to spar. For the temerity if nothing else. I will admit that I was a bit hesitant to ask since it would mean fighting someone that I\u2019ve never met with live steel. I\u2019d be doing this with the full knowledge that she is better than me. That was some blind faith on my part, that\u2019s for sure. Calamity trusts her implicitly and speaks very highly of her. I was working on the idea that if Calamity trusts her then I can too, at least enough for this. So, I told that little voice in my head (that sounds an awful lot like Rook) to shut up and asked if Luna wanted to fight. In the end Calamity was going to join us, and Gawain too. Though we were going to make him fight with paired daggers instead of just his sword.<br /> <br /> After a bit Luna and Calamity wanted to talk privately so I mingled and refreshed my drink. When they came back, Luna asked me if I\u2019d like to go to a comedy club with her and Calamity after the show. She seemed a little nervous to ask, like she was rethinking her decision even as the words were coming out of her mouth, but she asked anyway. I said that it sounded like fun. I\u2019ve never been to a comedy club, so it\u2019s a new experience for me. I will admit that it did strike me as a little odd that the quiet recluse wanted to go to a crowded comedy club after having been to a big party. I figured there was something more to it, but she didn\u2019t say anything else about it, and I wasn\u2019t going to pry. Forcing the issue would only put her on the defensive and that is not how I wanted this evening to end.<br /> <br /> Towards the end of the party Calamity and Captain Jack did the Mamushka dance from the Addams Family movie. I always thought that the name of that knife dance was a bit odd, but then it was written by people who do not speak Russian. I suppose it was at least appropriate that there was a woman involved in the dance. Anyhoo\u2026.they threw knives, caught them, and had a blast. After that Jack made a spectacular exit by jumping up on something then out the open skylight.<br /> <br /> Once the dance was over, Calamity, Luna, Gawain ad I went to the comedy club that Luna had mentioned earlier in the evening. The headliner for the night was pretty good. I thought he was funny. Luna appeared to be more studying the man instead of just watching him as an audience member might, so I took to watching her, watching him. Then it hit me. He was her fetch! Something just clicked. I don\u2019t know if it was some feature that was similar, some gesture they both used, or maybe it was just the eyes. You really can tell a lot about a person by looking at their eyes. So, Luna seemed to be studying the man to see if he recognized her or not. It didn\u2019t appear that he did. That was until later when he sent someone to invite Luna and the rest of us backstage to talk. I will admit, I was prepared to do serious damage if needs be, but it turned out to be unnecessary. I surreptitiously slipped my knife back up my sleeve and we all talked. <br /> <br /> Turns out that the fetch just wanted to talk to Luna because she seemed very familiar to him. Luna got flustered and when he asked if they knew each other she said something about High School. Then to save her mentor Calamity took Luna off to the side and left me and Gawain to entertain the comedian. We both tried to assure him that Luna was fine, just nervous. When the ladies returned, Luna said that they had gone to High School together and that she hadn\u2019t seen him since. After a bit he seemed to perhaps <i>see</i> more than he had before and Luna grabbed my arm, said some quick good-byes and we fled. The others made their excuses and left as well. Luna asked if she could spend the night at the Dream House since it was late, and we agreed. We have a guest room after all.<br /> <br /> Late last night, or early this morning (as the case may be) Luna came by my room. She knocked on the door and when I opened it up, she was standing there naked as a jay. She was less than subtle in her advances, and I\u2019ll admit she turned me on. I didn\u2019t try all that hard to resist, or at all really. I invited her in, locked the door and let events unfold as they would. She was definitely more aggressive in her actions than pretty much anyone else I\u2019ve been with, but that wasn\u2019t a bad thing. With Marguerite, she was very gentle, so I was gentle in kind. Luna was not gentle, so I allowed myself to be a bit rougher than I would be with Marguerite. I always made sure that Luna was okay with whatever I was doing though. That is a line that I will <b><i>never</i> </b>again cross.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m watching her sleep at the moment, as I write. She\u2019s sleeping on her stomach, her wings twitching occasionally as she dreams. She looks peaceful right now, but even in sleep there is a hint of the predator inside. I think that\u2019s what drew her to me in the first place. And now I have moth and flame metaphors going through my head, so I\u2019m going to stop writing and lie back down.<br /> <br /> **** **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Today was awesome. Just got to get that in writing. Holy shit, today was awesome. Okay\u2026first off, Luna asked me if I would like having another night like that in the future. I had to say yes. Things with Marguerite are open, and I have to admit that I\u2019m attracted to both ladies for different reasons. So, I said yes, I would like to do that again. She then asked if I minded if the others knew about us. I told her that I have no problems with that, and explained the open bit about me and Marguerite. Then we took a quick shower, and let me say, that girl can take a quick shower. She must be used to smaller water supplies, or cold water. I can relate. We showered together, and though she tried to hop out after a quick wash, I touched her shoulder and told her that she still had a bit of soap in her hair. She did, I wasn\u2019t kidding, but I may have taken a bit more time than was strictly necessary to rinse it out and rub her scalp. I don\u2019t think she minded.<br /> <br /> After we got dressed and headed downstairs, we had a wonderful breakfast of steak and eggs made by Gawain. He made them with peppers and onions. Fancy. Really good too. I made coffee and added Luna\u2019s preferences for coffee to the list in my head. There was conversation about the knife throwing at the party last night and the explanation of the Addams Family movie. Lori\u2019s face lit up at that. She remembered the TV show. We\u2019ll have to show her the movie. I remember it being a lot of fun.<br /> <br /> Well, after breakfast is when the fun started. Calamity, Luna, Gawain and I all changed into something more work-out appropriate and went to the backyard with our weapons of choice, except for Gawain, who sportingly agreed to twin knives. Gawain and I took off our shirts, mainly so they\u2019d survive, and the fun began. All I can say is that was an awesome fucking fight! Okay, that\u2019s not all I can say. Luna is damn fast! I mean fast. Possibly faster than Rook. Not sure on that one. Not sure I want to find out either. Luna moved like water, she flowed from one place to the next and meted out lashes as she went. It was beautiful. Part of me wishes I could have just watched it from the sidelines so I could see it all properly, but I\u2019m not sad to have asked her to spar. I had to keep all my attention on what I was doing, especially with so many people to keep track of. I saw the same moves that Calamity uses, but Luna\u2019s were just a bit more polished. A little bit more muscle memory than conscious thought. Calamity is good, don\u2019t get me wrong, but sometimes I can tell she\u2019s thinking about what to do next and there is a slight pause or the move is just slightly off. Granted, I would never have known that anything Calamity did was in any way off if I hadn\u2019t seen Luna doing the same moves today.<br /> <br /> Lorelei, De la Rocha, Insincere Marguerite and Julia sat under a tree and watched us spar. From what I could see from brief glances, Marguerite was lying across all of their laps and Lori was hiding her face in her hands. I wondered if she was just afraid of someone getting hurt, or if it somehow brought back bad memories of Mary\u2019s fetch or something like that. I know Lori worries about the rest of us getting injured, but the little scratches we get while sparring are nothing. I take note of acquiring the injury then just push it to the back of my mind. I get the impression that Calamity and Luna do the same thing.<br /> <br /> So, paired knives were definitely not Gawain\u2019s preferred weapons, but it didn\u2019t really make much of a difference. He wielded those blades like they were an extension of his arms and damn was he fast! And good. I will admit that I felt just a bit jealous. I doubt I\u2019d be so good if I tried to use one of his long swords. Hell, I\u2019m not confident I could pick one up in any way that resembles threatening. It might not be a bad idea to learn how to use bigger blades, maybe just not that big. Anyhoo\u2026the fight was awesome! Luna won. Can\u2019t say I\u2019m too surprised about that, but the rest of us made a good show of it. In a real fight she could have skewered me on a couple of occasions. Just before we stopped I felt a whisper of metal along my ribs. After the fight I looked down at my right side and saw a slight scratch just between my third and fourth ribs. The scratch mirrored a scar that I had on the other side in the same place. That old injury had hurt. A man, or what had been a man but actually was closer to a wolf by that point, dug his claws into my side years ago. Two just scraped ribs, the third got through and punctured my lung. I can remember in vivid detail what it feels like to drown on dry land. I have no desire to repeat that. <br /> <br /> I noticed that recently. My memory, which has always been pretty good, has gotten even better lately. Memories of Arcadia are clearer than ever, and some from before I was taken are starting to come back. Earlier this morning I had a brief flash of memory watching Gawain cook. I remembered my father cooking dinner on an open fire. The family was camping (this was back in Russia) and dad was cooking while Elena and I set up the tents. Mom gathered more firewood. After Elena and I were done, we sat near the fire and watched Dad turn the spit. It was a simple thing to do, but he seemed so content. He had a slight smile on his face and hummed an old folk song as he cooked. Gawain had that same kind of look on his face this morning and I couldn\u2019t help but smile. Cooking in a way is an act of creation and he always looks happy to do it. That\u2019s part of the reason I\u2019ve never pushed for anyone else to be the \u201cofficial\u201d cook. I help so it\u2019s not so much of a burden, but I can tell that Gawain really loves to cook. It\u2019s a way to separate himself from his past. I do the same when I tend bar. I guess my job is a little more mindless, but I find a way make my good balance and memory work for me. I try to remember people\u2019s preferences so they feel more welcome, and my dexterity helps when bringing multiple drinks at a time to tables. <br /> <br /> I hadn\u2019t thought too much about remembering drinks being anything special until someone thanked me for it. He told me that it made him happy to know that remembered who they were, and not just in the general \u201cI know that face\u201d kind of way. I remembered his name and greeted him by it, and brought him his martini just the way he liked it. He said that he liked the idea that after he was gone that someone would remember him and it got me thinking. I got taken when I was sixteen. Granted a fetch was left in my place, but the fetch isn\u2019t me. Our parents raised Elena and me to be proud of our heritage and of our family, and we are. I am. But now this little shit wearing my face has turned his back on everything I held dear, and it seems that no one remembered me as I really was and just accepted that this facsimile was really me. I don\u2019t know. I suppose it was fair in some messed up way. I didn\u2019t even remember the old me after I entered the Lady\u2019s service. That life was gone. I only remembered my time in Arcadia, in the woods, and then she came. The beautiful Shining Lady that saved me from my frozen hell. I wonder if that is the world balancing things out? I forget my life entirely and some fake comes in and starts living it. People forget the outgoing bookworm and now only see the moody, quiet brat when they look at Jacob Mikalev.<br /> <br /> Okay\u2026so, after the fight Gawain gathered up the Motley and let us know that he had talked to a Day courtier at the party last night. She wanted to meet with him, and maybe all of us, since she was having problems with people breaking into her house and she was partially convinced that it was Changeling business. She heard that our resident Knight was a stand-up kind of guy and took a chance on talking to him. I gathered all of that information later after I thought back over the conversation, because after I heard the girl\u2019s name all conscious thoughts turned to Claire Falls. Her name was Felicity. As soon as he said the name I felt like I\u2019d been sucker punched. I could only think of the little fawn girl with the fuzzy antler buds. So earnest and yet so shy. I forced my thoughts back to the situation at hand about the time the rest of the motley agreed to meet with her on Saturday afternoon about 2:00pm.<br /> <br /> After that Joan came by to talk. I think she wanted to see if we liked the party, and to let Gawain know that she was now protecting Andromeda. It sounds like the little alien girl was going to be moving into Joan\u2019s place soon. I think Gawain and Calamity had some hand in setting them up last night at the party. However it happened, it was good to see a genuine smile on Joan\u2019s face. While we were talking over coffee, Calamity suggested sparring with Joan and asked if she\u2019d like to join us. I think it was Gawain that said something about \u201cSword and Board\u201d against knives. I left my shirt on for that fight. Figured enough folks had seen the Lady\u2019s brand that I didn\u2019t need to add to that list. Especially with someone so keen our rooting out Loyalists.<br /> <br /> That second sparring match was pretty darn cool too. Both sides were doing what they did best and it showed. Gawain is good with sword and shield, and Joan\u2019s defense is solid. Very solid. I may have managed to nick her once when Luna was commanding her attention. She certainly landed a few hits on me. My arms and ribs have the bruises to prove it. One time she aimed a blow right about neck height. Luna was to my side, so I couldn\u2019t side-step the attack. I also didn\u2019t want to mess with her concentration. So I just dropped. Literally just let my legs go loose and dropped. Almost to the ground I rolled to my right and Joan\u2019s left and came up with a quick strike aimed at her ribs. Right between three and four. Almost had her too, but Gawain reached over at that moment and blocked my attack with his shield. I turned my crouch into a back roll and got out of his reach. Together they made a very effective team. Of course Calamity, Luna and I made a pretty good team ourselves. Things might have been a little different if those of us with knives broke out the dirty fighting, but we kept it clean for the purposes of a friendly sparring match. <br /> <br /> There\u2019s still a part of me that rails against sparring with folks so freely here. It\u2019s telling me that the more I do it, the more they will learn about my fighting style and more specifically about my weaknesses. My motley won\u2019t hurt me, at least for the moment, but Joan is under no such obligation to \u201cdo no harm\u201d to me. I don\u2019t want anything she gleans to get used against me later, but that paranoid part of me reminds me that I also found out a good deal about her fighting style as well. Fair trade? Plus, I just wanted to have fun, and that fight was fun. Both fights were fun, and I really enjoyed them both. Given the expression on Calamity\u2019s face during (and after) both fights, she enjoyed it just as much, if not more than I did. I\u2019m trying to put that paranoid part of me to rest, but I don\u2019t know if it will ever fully go away. I\u2019ve lived like that for so long, I think it\u2019s just going to be a part of me no matter how much time passes.<br /> <br /> So much of what happens to us sticks around for so long. Sometimes for the rest of our lives. I was thinking about the Lady\u2019s brand and my scars earlier and it got me to thinking. There are some injuries I know left scars, but I can\u2019t see them anymore. If I run my fingers along the right spot I can sometimes still feel them though. It\u2019s like they\u2019re hiding, or they\u2019ve become so much a part of us that they don\u2019t stand out as separate anymore. I wondered if they ever truly go away or just camouflage themselves really well. And if someone really looked would they be able to find them? The wounds I inflicted on others can\u2019t be seen on my skin, but those they did to me can. What can you tell from my scars I wonder? Can you map out how the fight went? Who won, who lost? I suppose if you\u2019re good enough you probably could. If television has taught me anything, it\u2019s that forensics can uncover just about anything. Not sure how much of the stuff in TV shows is verifiable, but I\u2019m sure enough of it is, at least in part. And what would happen if they never faded? Would the pain, anger or hurt stay fresh too? Would the loss? Or the guilt?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m sure that if forensics can look at the scars on a person and tell the tale, then those that were trained to give and take those kinds of wounds could do it too. I\u2019ve been walking around shirtless like an idiot in front of Calamity and Luna. What did they find out about me? What did they see? What did they guess? What does Luna read with her finger tips as she runs her hands up my sides? And will I let her read more tonight?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> A fair amount of time today has been spent considering an alliance with a Court. The Warlock of Night had never seemed to have much preference, beyond seeing the Seasonal Courts as too slow to change and thus easier to infiltrate or harm for the Gentry. While I have been considering returning to LA to consult her and ensure that such behavior will not been as anything more than making contacts, I feel myself bristle at thinking such is necessary. This isn\u2019t LA, and I left for a reason. Still, irking the Warlock of Night is low on my to do list. Obviously.<br /> <br /> The party last night went well, and I used the opportunity to talk to some Autumn Courtiers. Madam Spidertoes was polite and receptive, and interested in the possibility of allying with the Autumn Court. Indeed, she was interested in possibly something more formal between the Courts than simply myself involved, but I am not diplomat. I am just a passing grub. Still, she complimented me and told I to consider something along those lines. She did imply it need not be discussed outside the Courts in question.<br /> <br /> De La Rocha was rather disquieted by the discussion. She felt Spidertoes was flirting with I. She had no problem with Spidertoes flirting with someone per se, or so she said, but felt upset at the notion of I getting involved. She did not seek to tell I not to, for it was not her place, but expressed disquiet at how Spidertoes acted toward I. That and Lorelei\u2019s having a fling with the Monarch left her rather twitchy for the evening, I think. Julia, for her part, did not perceive Spidertoes as flirting, though she was up front about the fact that while they had shared several pleasant cups of tea, she knew little of Spidertoes beyond a polite mentor to the local Darklings who was held in esteem and a little dread, as is only proper for a revered Darkling. Definitely. She was not crazy about such a woman being involved with I, but she knows full well she will never be parted from I.<br /> <br /> Honestly De La Rocha\u2019s jealousy and disquiet were pleasing to me. I am not really proud of the fact, but not ashamed of course. I simply found it interesting to observe.<br /> <br /> I also spoke to Moon and Dionisia. Dionisia fielded many of the questions about the Court that I felt too trivial for a woman of Spidertoes\u2019 station. Dionisia was full of good answers. Terrorizing people is not how I prefer to spend time enjoying myself, but it is as close to a weapon as I wield. I am not the warlord Gawain is nor the assassin Calamity is. I am simply a grub who gets herself in trouble, and if faced with conflict I cannot escape, fear seems a viable weapon. The Autumn Court is a darker Court, which pleases me, and are a court of magic and secrets. If I must choose a seasonal Court to collaborate with, they seem to work. Also, Julia is in the Court.<br /> <br /> Spring is not completely off the list, but they are a court of light and frivolity\u2026I don\u2019t really know how Davie can stand it. My desires are, if anything, the biggest enemy I have. I cannot reach my full potential or achieve true greatness if they distract I. I don\u2019t know that the Spring Court would be the best fit for I, in the long term.<br /> <br /> I was planning to speak to Queen Charlotte, but she seemed in a rather dark mood, that was not helped by Lorelei running off with Princess Jolie. I elected to restrict my interviews to Madam Spidertoes and Dionisia.<br /> <br /> Still, it was a party and I had fun. I danced with Julia several times, Jacob a couple times, and De La Rocha once. I hung out with and flirted with Flores and Dionisia as well as the usual suspects. When Calamity, Jacob, and Gawain left with Calamity\u2019s mentor Luna, Dionisia apparently decided to make her move. Boldly.<br /> <br /> I had returned to the table with her when I found Moon curiously missing, and when I sat I swiftly found her hands to have taken up exploring. She was rather direct, and Julia and I wound up at her home. I had been warned she fixates on Faerie Tale logic at times, so I was careful to not make <i>too</i> good an impression, though I nonetheless found her rather impressive. Definitely.<br /> <br /> Her bedroom, with a lot of pink and a rather fantasy oriented motif, was insufficiently Goth for Julia. Julia is a bit strange. Dionisia also showed I considerable favor, which might have put her off. But she mentioned the Goth thing several times. I will endeavor to not be insufficiently Goth, though I cannot imagine she found my bedroom terribly Gothic, at least compared her rather\u2026extensive use of black in her private chambers.<br /> <br /> Much like Flores, Dionisia made absolutely clear she wanted to continue to have a fling. This worries I slightly. Again because I have concerns she will see I as her true love or something. I realize I may be casting aspirations but she is a member of a kith prone to such.<br /> <br /> At least she is terribly attractive.<br /> <br /> I returned and De La Rocha, again, warned I Spidertoes had displayed interest last night. I looked deep in her eyes, and I believe I saw fear. Perhaps she think I might simply take up with Spidertoes and abandon her. Or perhaps she has some other reason she is deeply worried we will get together. I need to talk to her about it when I can do so in private. I don\u2019t want to upset her, and I don\u2019t want to upset Lorelei, or make her think De La Rocha is not devoted.<br /> <br /> The afternoon was spent watching Jacob, Gawain, Calamity, and Luna spar. Eventually Joan came by and joined them. I don\u2019t follow fighting in sunlight on purpose. I found a spot under the shady tree to lay across Julia, De La Rocha, and Lorelei\u2019s laps. Joan seemed to be doing better, but she is still clearly insane. I saw she buttonholed some of the group at the party, I am glad I was not there for that. She seems to have gotten together with Andromeda, which is good. That bundle of nerves seriously needed to get laid. Maybe she be more stable. Hopefully.<br /> <br /> Luna clearly favored Jacob, which is interesting. Because he is a knife fighter perhaps? She does not seem the sort that would care that he is pretty. Which he is. She was not really flirting exactly (she does not seem to be the swooning type) but there was decided interest. Clearly I need to find out more about this girl.<br /> <br /> Gawain brought up that he had been approached by Felicity, a Day Courtier in the area. However, rather than discussing how to take all of her stuff and sell it on the black market, for some strange reason Gawain seemed inclined to make a deal with her. Deal with the Day Court? Seriously? What next, the Gentry? Julia looked at I as soon as they mentioned she was Day Court, she at least grasped the gravity of the situation. De La Rocha less so, perhaps she was distracted by something.<br /> <br /> We can\u2019t actually align ourselves with the Day Court, can we? I mean we must have standards, right? Surely they are the enemy of anyone sensible.<br /> <br /> Dionisia was back and on the prowl tonight. She put some moves on but I managed to beg off for the evening. If nothing else, Julia is exhausted and has been looking forward to just sleeping for once. She is not as athletic as I, though to be fair I am not as artistic as she. Still, her plan seemed sound.<br /> <br /> Sleep for the little grub in the big house.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XIX</i><br /> <br /> Not much to add about session 19, though comments and questions are welcome, as always.<br /> <br /> We decided after the game to have some downtime. We wound up jumping ahead from Friday the 16<sup>th</sup> into the 17<sup>th</sup> to Monday, June 9<sup>th</sup>, or a bit over 3 weeks. This was done as we were at a decent stopping point, and the character relationships had evolved due to real world time passing perhaps faster than they should have. So some downtime will help that. Also, it gave us a chance to spend some of the XP the Motley had been accruing for the Dream House and for the Hollow.<br /> <br /> We decided to put off the Felicity meeting. Apparently she suddenly had to go out of town. It did not occur the next session as we wanted Gawain there for that and his player is pretty reliable.<br /> <br /> The next session was somewhat abbreviated due to being on a different night (where the players all had to work) and missing both Ace and Gawain. The usual night would have missed Ace Gawain and Calamity, which would have been too many, but we could move it to a night where at least Calamity\u2019s player could show.<br /> <br /> Abbreviated or no, there will be journals for it, and we will have some downtime discussion. I\u2019ll see you then, comments and questions welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T21:03:02-08:00","id":348777,"title":"","content":"When Calamity hunts, she hunts for the fear of her prey. When/were Jacob to hunt, what would you say he takes from the hunt? The despair of his prey's defeat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","user":"omenseer","date":". 12-24-2014, 01:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T12:29:45-08:00","id":349220,"title":"","content":"Hard to say.<br /> <br /> Jacob does not generally seek to engender Sorrow the way, say, Calamity seeks Fear, Insincere Marguerite seeks Disgust, or Lorelei seeks Desire. I suspect his would be more purely thrill of the hunt. Of course, he can still reap the benefits of Fear, just without the bonus point an Autumn Courtier like Calamity would get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T19:36:07-08:00","id":349465,"title":"","content":"That is interesting to know. The story so far has inspired a kind of foil or rival character idea to Jacob and Calamity. A changeling who hunts predators and monsters, but not for the kill, fear, or pain. When he gets to the point where one would strike the kill he either cuts them just to draw blood or takes a piece of cloth or some personal effect. I had the idea that he starts to hunt Jacob and Calamity as short or medium goals with the eventual goal of hunting the likes of Luna, Rook, or Annika. He calls himself Coup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T07:27:00-08:00","id":349812,"title":"","content":"Annika seems an odd choice. While Calamity regards her as a hunter of sorts due to her predator/prey mindset, Annika is really a dancer and singer, not a hunter or warrior like Luna or Rook. She is a domme, but not really any sort of huntress.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T10:46:19-08:00","id":349952,"title":"","content":"Annika was a flub on my part. I meant generally the ones above the PCs who are hunters or predators.<br /> <br /> Merry Christmas!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T13:49:02-08:00","id":350035,"title":"","content":"You as well!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T14:26:34-08:00","id":351975,"title":"","content":"How do you think they would react to such a character?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T02:34:03-08:00","id":352502,"title":"","content":"Hard to say really. I mean I assume with Calamity involved violence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T01:17:06-08:00","id":353558,"title":"","content":"That is an interesting idea there. Calamity would respond to being hunted by either drawing her hunter into a trap or otherwise trying to turn the tables on them. She'd likely assume that hunting her was an attempt to remove one of the motley's defenders. Also, self defense is a beautiful excuse to commit violence so she would fight back viciously.<br /> <br /> Now, if she were aware enough of this hunter to know that they did not intend harm to her or the other members of the motley, she would still strive to turn things around on them but would actually quite enjoy the challenge and sport of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T18:12:11-08:00","id":354211,"title":"","content":"Hey Baron, I've noticed that all of your characters have some level of the Dual Kith merit. I've been meaning to start a Changeling game at my LGS (if I can find players), and poking around on the internet it looks like a significant number of PCs have Dual Kith.<br /> <br /> Is it standard operating procedure to offer this merit for free, or is it just so good that everyone takes it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://paizo.com/campaigns/RageAcrossIreland/gameplay\" target=\"_blank\">My W20 Play-by-Post Game</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2760-formosus","name":"Formosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T02:59:22-08:00","id":354634,"title":"","content":"Hey there.<br /> <br /> I do not offer Dual Kith for free. I use the system where you buying a second Kith of the same Seeming is 2 points, different Seeming is 3 points. Everyone in <i>Malibu Dream House</i> does indeed have Dual Kith. My previous Changeling game <i>Beyond the Sea</i> had 5/7 PCs with Dual Kith, we had a Mirrorskin and a Mannikin who only had their single Kith.<br /> <br /> I use a HR that if you do not buy Dual Kith at creation, you can buy it ingame if your Wyrd hits 5+. Of course, if you already had it, you can't buy it again. This never came up in play, however, those without it never chose to pick it up even at 5+ Wyrd, which they both eventually hit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T09:01:06-08:00","id":354779,"title":"","content":"Thanks Baron. Sorry to derail your thread a bit. Can't wait for the next journals!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://paizo.com/campaigns/RageAcrossIreland/gameplay\" target=\"_blank\">My W20 Play-by-Post Game</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2760-formosus","name":"Formosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T02:36:09-08:00","id":367169,"title":"","content":"Apologies for the late arrival, some journals were delayed. It\u2019s time to cover our big downtime session. This session was a shorter run, as Gawain and Ace\u2019s players could not make due to holiday plans. We only had Calamity as we moved the game (Gawain and Ace would have missed regardless). Still, we had some things happen, and a lot discussed.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Wow, I have really let the journaling slide lately, haven\u2019t I? Checking the last entry, it looks like it\u2019s been close to three weeks since I last wrote anything in this diary. And I don\u2019t even have the excuse that nothing much has been happening. Okay, we haven\u2019t had any more deadly explosive firefights with insane fetches \u2013 I haven\u2019t even had to use my healing powers at all \u2013 but that doesn\u2019t mean things haven\u2019t been eventful nonetheless.<br /> <br /> In the wake of our brief dalliance, Princess Jolie seems to be playing the field. Okay, I don\u2019t know that she\u2019s been sleeping around, exactly, but she\u2019s definitely stepped up her dating schedule. She\u2019s been out with any number of the Freehold\u2019s eligible singles, both male and female. In fact, Insincere Marguerite approached me the other day to ask if it would be okay with me if <u>she</u> went out with the Princess. I know that I don\u2019t have any room to complain about Jolie\u2019s dating habits considering that I turned her down when she flat-out <u>asked</u> me to be her girlfriend a few weeks ago, but I confess that our fling feels less special now that she\u2019s going out with so many other people.<br /> <br /> Of course I told Marguerite to go for it. Who am I to stand in the way of true lust?<br /> <br /> Speaking of the L-word (well, sorta), things are still going just swimmingly with D. We had one of those important talks the other day, ushering in a new phase in our relationship. I took her out to dinner and brought her back to the Dream House as per usual, but as we were sitting on my bed \u2013 <u>our</u> bed \u2013 before things got too intense, I handed her a small box tied up with a red ribbon. <br /> <br /> She got this sort of deer-in-headlights look on her face and I had to laugh. \u201cJesus, D,\u201d I said with a grin, \u201cI love you, girl, but it\u2019s only been about a month. It\u2019s not a ring, so you can stop looking so terrified.\u201d<br /> <br /> She chuckled and unwrapped the box. Inside was a small key ring with four keys on it. \u201cI talked it over with the others,\u201d I said softly, taking her hand in mine, \u201cand they agreed that it would be okay for you to have your own set of keys. That\u2019s the front door, that\u2019s the back door, and that\u2019s the garage,\u201d I said pointing to each one in turn.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd what\u2019s this one,\u201d she asked, holding up the fourth.<br /> <br /> I sighed and decided to take the plunge. \u201cThat\u2019s a key to my \u2018vette,\u201d I said after a moment\u2019s hesitation.<br /> <br /> She just kind of stared for a minute.<br /> <br /> \u201cI hope you know what this means to me,\u201d I said, \u201cand how much I trust you. <u>Nobody</u> else has a key to my car\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShut up,\u201d she said breathlessly, and then she leaned in and kissed me and\u2026 things progressed from there. A few days later she gave me a key to her apartment. I\u2019ve broached the subject of her moving in here officially a few times since then, but she\u2019s determined to keep her own place despite the obvious advantages of cohabitation. She can be as stubborn as a mule sometimes.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m <u>really</u> in love with this girl, and sometimes I even forget to be scared by that fact. I\u2019ve attempted to subtly clue my father in on my newfound bisexuality, but the good reverend is determined not to take my hints, and thus remains blissfully ignorant of his young parishioner\u2019s romantic proclivities. Sigh. I\u2019m going to have to come right out and say it at some point. I hope he can deal with it.<br /> <br /> And speaking of things that are nominally good for me but probably wouldn\u2019t make my father particularly happy, my star seems to be on the rise! A package was delivered to me the other day (I had to sign for it and everything). When I opened it, I found to my surprise that it contained ten copies of next month\u2019s issue of <u>Playboy</u>. There was a Post-it note stuck to the top copy: \u201cCheck out page 34, Jimmy.\u201d Curious, I flipped past pages of reader mail, editorials, and breasts, and found the page in question.<br /> <br /> I ran into the kitchen, but only Calamity was there. I slammed one of the magazines down on the table. \u201cYou have to see this,\u201d I said breathlessly.<br /> <br /> Calamity picked up the magazine and flipped to the table of contents. \u201cCheerleaders of the Atlantic Coast Conference?\u201d she asked flippantly.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s not what you think,\u201d I said in a rush, \u201cI\u2019m in this one!\u201d She gave me a look, and I realized how that must have sounded. \u201cNo\u2026 I\u2019m not naked or anything\u2026 well, actually, okay, I <u>am</u> naked, but it\u2019s\u2026 it\u2019s not what you think!\u201d I said again.<br /> <br /> She arched an eyebrow. I sighed. \u201cLook, just turn to page 34, okay?\u201d She did.<br /> <br /> Jimmy Liles is a very promising young man studying photography in Santa Monica. He photographed me a few weeks ago, ran the results through some filters and computer doohickies, plopped some text on the finished product, and submitted it to the advertising department of the Jack Daniels Brewing Company as part of a nation-wide contest. He won.<br /> <br /> His ad is going to be in several magazines with national distribution. <u>My</u> picture is going to be in several magazines with <u>national</u> distribution!<br /> <br /> The picture itself is a side-on shot of me seated at a table, mostly naked but with all of my bits covered by the angle of the shot (it\u2019s what they call a \u201ctasteful nude\u201d). I\u2019m looking sultrily at the camera with a bottle of Jack raised halfway to my parted lips, and a lit cigarette smoldering in an ashtray in front of me. Ironically, Jimmy used the computer to give me wings\u2026 white angelic wings rather than the colorful ones he couldn\u2019t see.<br /> <br /> For some reason, looking at that picture made me think of one of the other birds \u2013 one of the other <u>girls</u>, I mean \u2013 who briefly shared our cage in Arcadia. What was her name? Annabeth? Annabelle? Something like that. She was lovely, but she didn\u2019t last long. None of the girls lasted long, aside from Missy, Jane, and me. Weird that I should think about her now, after all this time, though. She was no angel, as I remember her, and her hair and wings were both bright red, so I don\u2019t know why a picture of li\u2019l old me wearing angel wings would bring her to mind.<br /> <br /> So anyway, Calamity said she\u2019d use the Dream House\u2019s contacts in L.A. to get me meetings with a few agents. <u>Real</u> agents, not lowlife scum like Gary. With any luck, I should be doing some much bigger shoots in the not too distant future. And once they hear me sing and see me act\u2026 who knows?<br /> <br /> In other news, it looks like my production of \u201cA Midsummer Night\u2019s Dream\u201d is coming together nicely. I\u2019ve stuck to my guns, and I\u2019m casting changelings only as mortals and mortals only in faerie roles. I\u2019m playing Hermia myself, which is maybe a little bit on the nose, but it seemed like the best choice. I think we\u2019re on target for our \u201cone night only\u201d show at the Solstice, and we should give the Freehold \u2013 and the local mortals \u2013 a night to remember.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve been practicing on the piano for the past few weeks, and things are really starting to come back to me\u2026 I think I might actually be able to perform in front of an audience soon. It\u2019ll be an interesting change letting one of the other performers take center stage while I provide musical backup, and I doubt I\u2019ll do it very often, but as they say, variety is the spice of life.<br /> <br /> Oh, Jacob took me out roller skating again, and we brought the rest of the motley with us this time. I had a blast! I bought my own skates on a whim a few weeks ago, and they fit perfectly. It was so much fun hanging out with my friends and watching them enjoy each other\u2019s company in that strangely familiar setting; I hope we can do it again soon, and maybe even make it a regular thing.<br /> <br /> One last bit of fluff before I move on to more serious matters\u2026 by and large, movie night has been a rollicking success. We\u2019ve been cycling through the motley members based on Courts \u2013 Dawn, Spring, Summer, Autumn, Winter, Night \u2013 and my place in the rotation has come up twice now.<br /> <br /> So the first week, Gawain picked a film called <u>Ladyhawke;</u> a fantasy drama about a pair of lovers who were cursed so that they turn into animals at different times of day\u2026 they could only see each other in human form for a few fleeting moments at dawn and dusk. It was silly but romantic in its way, and I ended up really enjoying it.<br /> <br /> For my part, I had been told that I needed to see a movie called <u>Indiana Jones and the Temple of Doom.</u> I sort of apologized as I suggested it, since the title sounded so silly, but most of the others were more than happy to watch it with me. Calamity suggested starting with another film called <u>Raiders of the Lost Ark</u>, since it was technically the first film in the series, and I agreed readily enough. It was\u2026 much better than I was expecting! A great period action film, with a bit of romance and supernatural horror thrown in. Plus monkeys. And Nazis. Monkeys and Nazis are guaranteed to make any film better, I\u2019m told.<br /> <br /> For the next week, Ace inflicted a zombie film called <u>Dead Alive</u> on us. It wasn\u2019t really to my taste, but it was fun cuddling up to D during the scary or revolting parts. I did a little research, and apparently the film was originally named <u>Braindead,</u> and the director went on to create some pretty popular adaptations of the <u>Lord of the Rings</u> books. As that was one of the few fantasy novels of which Dad actually approved when I was growing up, I read it more than once. Maybe I should check those films out\u2026 though if they came from this Peter Jackson fellow, I\u2019m not sure how good they can possibly be.<br /> <br /> Calamity\u2019s selection was more to my taste\u2026 a little fantasy romantic comedy called <u>The Princess Bride</u>. It was written by William Goldman, the same guy who wrote <u>Butch Cassidy and the Sundance Kid</u>. It was <u>amazing</u>. Exciting, romantic, funny, moving\u2026 it seemed to have everything, all wrapped up in the touching framework of Columbo reading a story to his sick grandson. It might be my favorite film that I\u2019ve seen since I escaped Arcadia. And when I mentioned at the end of the evening that it was time to go to bed, the way D said \u201cas you wish\u201d sent shivers down my spine\u2026<br /> <br /> The next week was\u2026 well, the films were <u>good</u>, but\u2026 I dunno. <u>Donnie Darko</u> was \u2013 as its name might imply \u2013 quite dark, and sort of mind-bending\u2026 I never quite knew where it was going, sort of like Marguerite herself (who suggested the film). Jacob\u2019s selection was a heart-breaking three-hour portrayal of the Holocaust called <u>Schindler\u2019s List</u>. I\u2026 don\u2019t think I can talk about that film yet in any meaningful way. It was emotionally devastating, and the way the director used occasional flashes of color in the otherwise black-and-white film was a thing of terrible beauty. I almost couldn\u2019t believe it when Jacob told me that it was directed by the same man who gave us <u>Raiders of the Lost Ark</u>.<br /> <br /> So when it came \u2018round to the next movie night, both Gawain and Ace were unavailable, so the selection fell to me and Calamity. I\u2019d been looking into <u>The Princess Bride</u> online, and found a persistent rumor that it was tangentially connected to a film called <u>This Is Spinal Tap</u>, a \u201cmockumentary\u201d about a fake heavy metal band. It seemed interesting, so I suggested it, and the others went along with it. It was fun, and really funny, though not as good as <u>The Princess Bride</u>. It went all the way to eleven, to quote what I am informed is a highly overused line from the film.<br /> <br /> Calamity brought a French film called <u>Le Pacte des Loups</u>, or <u>The Brotherhood of the Wolf</u>. It was an exciting period piece set in 1700s France, supposedly based on the true story of a monstrous wolf that terrorized the countryside for months. I\u2019m not sure how much of the story is actually true \u2013 I never knew Canadian Indians knew such powerful kung fu, for example \u2013 but it was certainly action-packed, and an enjoyable way to spend an evening.<br /> <br /> Okay, so I\u2019ve dicked around enough with this entry, talking about how hunky-dory life is and how happy I\u2019ve been. Now it\u2019s time to get down to business. A few important things have happened lately, and it looks like life is about to get interesting again.<br /> <br /> First, Jacob approached us the other day with word from Master Darke, who has had people looking into the attack on Dark Kimberly at the Rose &amp; Thorn. According to his sources, a group called the Phantom Tong is probably involved. From what I\u2019ve been told, they\u2019re an organization of changelings who try to spread chaos through the world for reasons which frankly escape me. The very inexplicable nature of the crime <u>does</u> seem to point to one of their terrorist acts, but it doesn\u2019t quite fit in my opinion. The Tong always leaves some sort of calling card at the scene of their mayhem; they <u>want</u> people to know that they\u2019re behind these senseless acts. Nothing like that has been uncovered in Kimberly\u2019s case as of yet.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s also the fact that Darke seems to be working really hard to tie the attack to Lucien Torrez, who has had some circumstantial connections to Tong members in the past. Now, I don\u2019t like to point fingers at powerful members of the community or anything, but it\u2019s well known that Darke and Torrez hate each other, and it seems to me that Darke is just using this as a way to sling a bit of mud in Torrez\u2019s direction.<br /> <br /> (Oh, that reminds me\u2026 Mr. Torrez got me my gun! It\u2019s a cute little pistol by American Arms called a Black Widow. Calamity\u2019s been teaching me how to shoot along with lots of gun safety rules so that I can avoid, you know, killing myself and shit.)<br /> <br /> The other recent development is possibly even more disturbing, and certainly calls for more immediate action. Andromeda dropped by the other day and asked to speak with Calamity about a matter of some delicacy. It turns out that things have gotten quite steamy between her and Joan lately, and they\u2019ve been \u2018experimenting\u2019 with some of Andromeda\u2019s more\u2026 exotic inventions. During the course of their exploration, Joan officially \u2013 <u>physically</u> \u2013 lost her virginity.<br /> <br /> Here\u2019s where it gets interesting. Joan is apparently suffering the effects of a curse; something she\u2019s lived with since her durance. She becomes completely and utterly subservient to whoever takes her cherry. It\u2019s kind of scary, actually\u2026 to hear Andromeda talk, you wouldn\u2019t even recognize her as the same feisty, grumpy warrior we all know and love these days. She\u2019s like a puppy, eager to please its mistress.<br /> <br /> Andromeda is understandably upset about this. Aside from the fact that Joan is no longer the girl she fell for, there are practical considerations in place as well. For example, her reputation in the Freehold really can\u2019t take another hit right now, and if people were to start gossiping that she caused these changes in Joan\u2019s personality <u>intentionally</u>, it could spell the end for her in Malibu and Santa Monica. So she\u2019s asked us for our help.<br /> <br /> Calamity went by the Autumn Court\u2019s library to look into ways to reverse the curse. Unfortunately, Gentry magic is pretty unique, and there are no catch-all ways to remove such a powerful enchantment. However, most sources seem to agree that if we can somehow restore Joan\u2019s virginity then the detrimental effects will pass, and as long as she and Andromeda are more careful in the future there should be nothing to worry about.<br /> <br /> We came up with two options. First, Joan could restore both her physical and spiritual virginity by completing some sort of mystical quest in the Hedge. Seems like a no-brainer, right? I mean, Joan is almost as much of a knight in shining armor as Gawain is. You\u2019d think this sort of thing would be right up her alley. And ordinarily, you\u2019d be right. But such a quest requires clarity of purpose and steely determination, and Joan is running short of both of those at the moment. She\u2019d probably do the quest if Andromeda asked her to, but her heart wouldn\u2019t really be in it, and that could be dangerous for her\u2026 maybe even deadly.<br /> <br /> So we looked into option two. There is a kind of goblin fruit that can restore someone\u2019s virginity. It\u2019s known to grow in the Hedge not too far away, and we thought there was at least a decent chance that we would be able to find some in the Freehold. Alas, such was not to be. I spoke with Flores about it, but she didn\u2019t have any on hand. Of course, I didn\u2019t bring Joan\u2019s name into it\u2026 I\u2019m actually rather proud of my subtle misdirection. I told her that I was looking for the fruit for \u201ca friend,\u201d which of course made her think that I wanted it for myself (or maybe for D).<br /> <br /> I won\u2019t deny that the thought has crossed my mind. There\u2019s a part of me that sort of wishes I could give that part of myself to someone that I really love, and D would certainly fit the bill. I guess there\u2019s a part of me that wishes I hadn\u2019t lost my cherry to Tommy Salinger when I was\u2026 I\u2019ll just leave it at \u2018far too young,\u2019 shall I? I mean, I really only did it because I knew it would infuriate Dad if he ever found out. It hurt, and Tommy was a real jerk about it later. I\u2019ve always wondered if it would have been different if I\u2019d been with someone who really cared about me that first time\u2026<br /> <br /> No. I\u2019ve made my choices, and some of them were mistakes, but I\u2019m going to live with them regardless. D knows that I\u2019m damaged\u2026 hell, I\u2019m a changeling, right? It sort of goes with the territory. Anyway, she loves me all the same. It doesn\u2019t pay to start second-guessing myself at this point.<br /> <br /> So the others didn\u2019t have any more luck with their own courts. This goblin fruit is either really rare or not worth the trouble in most cases, because no one seems to keep it handy around here. So we\u2019re going to head into the Hedge in the next few days to try to track it down. We have to hurry, because sooner or later someone is going to notice the changes in Joan\u2019s personality, and that\u2019ll be the end of that. The good news is that we know approximately where the fruit is located in the Hedge, and have a pretty good idea of how to get there. The bad news is that it\u2019s located in a swamp. Sigh. Why don\u2019t we ever get a quest that leads us to beautiful tropical beaches?<br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei Grace</b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T02:36:39-08:00","id":367170,"title":"","content":"<b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> <b><u>Monday June 9<sup>th</sup></u></b><br /> <br /> I haven't been writing. There is no point in writing if I can't be honest and I don't want some of the things in my head to be here where Gawain could find them. Not that I think he reads this... Not that I think any of them do... But they could. Someone else could. I could. I... I remember things. Things I had forgotten. It started with that filthy fucking pig in the alleyway. The one with Timmy's eyes. The one who had my watch.<br /> <br /> The memories have been coming back in my dreams. Things I saw in Snow Globe... Things I did...<br /> <br /> I know they are real. I can feel it. I just didn't want to remember. I really am naughty. I am bad girl. Not just because I defied Them. Oh that wasn't bad... Well... Maybe when I did it by hurting someone. But I was small and weak in Snow Globe. I wasn't dangerous there. Not like I am now. Not like I am with my glass. I can feel it, even now, inside my hands and fingers... just waiting. It itches... I haven't feed it properly in a while now and I need to.<br /> <br /> Fuck. That's why I stopped writing. My thoughts start trailing when I write and I sound like some kind of fucking psychopath. Okay, spoiler alert, maybe I AM a fucking psychopath... But when I let my thoughts run I drift into crazy things and I don't like it. I have kept myself very busy this past few weeks for a reason. I have to keep it together. I cannot afford to be crazy. It makes me reckless and reckless gets you killed in a fight. I cannot die. I must not die. I have promises to keep... Gawain needs me... If I die he will read this...<br /> <br /> You will read this after I die won't you love. All I can say is that I am so sorry... I want so much to be the kind of girl you deserve. I really do. I just can't... not anymore. If I could be whole again... If I could be good... If I could be fixed... I would do that for you love. But we both know better. It doesn't work that way, not for us. I love you Gawain, with all the love my dark and twisted heart can manage. And I hope you do read this after I'm gone. You might not be the only light in my life, but you are most certainly the brightest. <br /> <br /> Holy fucking shit I am maudlin and sappy tonight. Maybe it was seeing that hint of loss still clinging to Queen Charlotte earlier... Maybe it's just that I'm writing this while I watch over Gawain now that he's finally getting some decent sleep. It's not serious or life threatening, just food poisoning. Not sure what it was exactly but it does appear to be just my poor Gawain that got hit with it. But fuck did it hit him like a runaway train. He's been well and truly wretched, to the point of being unable to even get any real rest. But he seems to have turned, he's not looking feverish and he's so soundly under I've actually caught myself staring just to be sure he's still breathing. Hopefully it means he'll be feeling himself again when he wakes up. Because we've got a trip to the Hedge that can't wait and wild horses won't be able to keep him from coming along to make sure I'm alright.<br /> <br /> Guess I should try to catch this thing up to date while I\u2019m writing. All in all, the past weeks have been good. The Dream House is doing well. The motley is safe and happy. I've managed to be a good girlfriend to Gawain. So far it seems to work that he can take refuge in my dreams from his nightmares when he needs to, scouring my own terrors and crimes away and crafting something better for us both. A fair amount of thrilling heroics with plenty of fighting and sex because well... that is the sort of thing we both like. But sometimes it's something as simple as exploring some mundane place he's made together. And it's nice, maybe because he made it just for me or because he's there with me, but we just walk along quietly while I look for every little detail or surprise he's put there and he just trails along and watches me and we talk or maybe make love in a strategically placed spot that just so happens to be perfect for it. It's more peaceful than I ever manage to be in the real world. I still can't help but worry that my darker fantasies and desires will creep in one of these nights but my love is a craftsman and never leaves any loose dream threads or stray wisps before he starts crafting. I I know he's well aware of what's creeping around down in my psyche just as my own forays into his dreams show me things, glimpses of his nightmares before they finish fading. I do wish I could make dreams as vivid and breathtaking as as the ones he crafts for me but his nightmares weave a subtle warp to everything that corrupts and takes over any dream that becomes too intense. But even subtle and subdued, there is nothing so intimate as sharing dreams.<br /> <br /> And that's the problem. I wouldn't let him into my dreams if I did not trust him implicitly. I know that nothing he sees will change how he feels about me because he knew before he entered what kind of monster I am. But I still don't want him to SEE those things. And with these returning memories, I don't want him to see the way I used to skulk around Snow Globe at night. At first I just looked for a way out while no one was watching. But I wasn't the only one that sought to move unseen. To act without being witnessed and reported and punished for being wrong and imperfect and bad. In time, I realized that there was no break in the glass, no way to escape. But by that time I'd become good at hiding and creeping. I was small and it made it easier for me to avoid the others. And in the night, in the dark, that was when people hoped to avoid the watchful eyes of their neighbors. That was when people did things.<br /> <br /> That was when Hans would prey on the wives and older daughters. He was the milkman and his pale gray eyes were sharp, sharper than even my own. He saw everything. He never missed anything. But he didn't tell, not at first. No, he would come to them and he would tell them what he'd seen and he would give them the chance to buy his silence. Oh the things he made them do... And I would watch hidden from them both. He never came for me. I was only a child and as foul a creature as Hans was, he had no interest in children. I think he knew that I was like him, a fellow predator. Sometimes, as he was delivering to our house on a morning after I'd followed him and watched his games he would tip his pristine white cap and wink at me with one of those cold gray eyes. But we never spoke. I could have stopped him, I could have told on him. The Whispering Voices would have punished him for his wickedness. But I never did. The older girls were mean to me, prettier and stronger and always watching. Always looking down on me and turning away. Always too good for weak little pain in the neck Janey Painy. Oh how I hated them and loved to tell on them whenever I could. But when the Whispers came for someone, it was all ink dark and cotton ears. Nothing to see. Nothing to hear. Just a pass to the candy store brought in a striped envelop with the morning mail. But Hans had no magic, just his keen hard eyes and his soft light step. You could see and hear everything when he came calling on one of them. A word to the shadows and I could have ended it but I never did.<br /> <br /> While Hans relished his cruel games of blackmail and power, I liked the candy. Oh it was so sweet. I'd like to say that if I'd known then what I do now it would have been different but I refuse to lie in these pages. The candy... pure burning nerve searing pleasure. Hell, I knew where it came from back then. The old man told me as he gave it to me and I took it gladly. Bittersour tears of pain... moans of agony and pleasure spun out wispy like cotton candy... brittle of broken dreams... Oh Fuck... Just thinking about it makes me ache...<br /> <br /> * * *<br /> <br /> That's a little better. By Lucifer's sweaty balls I am screwed up. Yeah... I knew what it was and I didn't care. Hell, I hated them all, I would have done it even without a reward. Of course, there was no way to trick the Whispering Voices. They always knew everything but They couldn't punish you unless someone told. And good girls don't lie. I had the taste of blood in my mouth for days before my tongue healed from that lesson. So I had to watch and catch the others being bad to get my candy. Of course, we were all wicked and naughty so it wasn't that hard when I was so much better at sneaking than the rest of them.<br /> <br /> And the old man in the Sweet Shoppe was always waiting. Ready to serve up a malt or a root beer before he brought out the candy. Always smiling. Always friendly. He was nice to me, not just pretend nice like everyone else but actually nice. Kindly and patient as he waited for me to pick my candy. Always knew what I needed most but still waited for me to look at all of them and decide. Of course, looking back I know that he had to be more than he seemed. The fact that he was always so gentle and proud of me wasn't a good thing. He was shaping me as much as the Whispering Voices but I was blind to it at the time. And knowing he wasn't just another lost soul doesn't change the fact that I still miss him and his damned candy.<br /> <br /> But my life here is good. I have Gawain. I am his monster. I have the motley. I have Luna and Tommy and Becky. I have Annika and Kimberly and Andromeda. They trust me. They depend on me. They like me... some even love me. Gawain and I have actually started dating. I mean, we've been pretty close since we ran into each other in the Hedge but it's been different lately. We still hang out and play video games and stuff but we've also gone out together. And we've gone out on a couple of double dates with Annika and Kimberly. And while it has also been nice to spend time with them, Annika is very much the dominant partner and acts the role of the man. I mean, I happen to enjoy sipping brandy and smoking a cigar (and I do not believe either is really Gawain's thing) but I do have to chuckle when Kimberly starts up with girly talk to him while my dance trainer and I carry on like some sort of old boys club robber barons. Our other date was with Insincere Marguerite and Julia. The four of us went to see \u201cMaleficent.\u201d It was an interesting retelling of the story and I enjoyed it. Being out with good company was also nice. Julia and I have spent some time getting to know each other better lately. Plus I think Gawain appreciated getting to be the man for a change.<br /> <br /> There was also the skate rink trip. The whole motley and our assorted hangers on and camp followers all piled into Gawain\u2019s van and rolled out to the skate rink Jacob and Lori had gone to previously. It really was straight out of the 70's. I hadn't worn a roller skate since my 11<sup>th</sup> birthday and I spent so much of that night running into people and falling down that Anastasia was still asking me if I was done with my roller derby phase months later. Thankfully for all involved, my sense of balance has come a long way since then. A few laps to get the hang of it and I was zipping around hand in hand with Gawain and smiling. I may even have laughed when no one was looking. To my great surprise, Insincere Marguerite put a pair of rental skates on her feet and joined us. While I was trying to set some sort of amateur speed record she and Jacob were happy playing hide and seek with the random spotlights sweeping the floor. At some point, they started up couples skate, which involved a slower and more romantic selection of music and dimmed main lights so the disco ball's rainbow color spots were more visible while they used a big spot to highlight couples that were particularly impressive. Of course, Lori and D got spotlit early and often while Jacob and my darkling sister went to some adorable and comical lengths to avoid it the whole time. Gawain and I also got caught in it rather unexpectedly (We weren't going anything more fancy than holding each other close without falling down honestly...) and on a lark I decided to put some of what Annika's been teaching me to use. I guess it went well, we did keep the light a fair bit before they moved on and I did keep getting looks for the rest of the evening, which prompted me to just curl into Gawain's side while we did lazy circles around the rink for a while before folks were ready to pack it in.<br /> <br /> We've also started up a movie night. Every Monday we all pile into the TV room and watch a couple of movies together. The idea is get folks caught up on pop culture they've missed but it's also a nice bit of fun group time. (even if there are some pretty well defined knots and cuddle piles.) We've gone through a pretty wide range of movies. Gawain picked one that Kat had seen and loved, \u201cLadyhawke\u201d It was odd to watch it again and realize just how different it felt to me now. And it reminded me of Kat's hands down favorite, \u201cPrincess Bride\u201d It was one I knew Gawain and Lori would love and that I also knew Lori had not seen. I was a little nervous to watch it again but while the romance didn't move me anywhere near the way it used to it was still fun and full of contagious lines. It's like the damn sunrise... I can remember how it made me feel but I can't feel that way anymore. Still, everyone seemed to really enjoy it and Gawain decided to sweep me off to bed after it was over in the most outrageously silly and overblown manner (I fear Captain Jack is rubbing off on him). I don't know how that man also knows just when I need him to pull something like that but it was the distraction I needed to pull my mind back from my Stasia. I can remember how much she and I loved that movie. I think we hit the theater every weekend (at least once) while it was playing. And thinking of her led to wondering where she is and how she's doing, which I shouldn't do. I have to stay away from her. Nothing good would come from tracking her down. She doesn't know the sinister bitch isn't me and even if I could explain that would drag her into this fucked up insanity that I live in. No. She must hate me after what happened and I don't want to see that. I just have to content myself with remembering her the way we were and accept that I there is no way I'll ever have my Stasia back. The girl I loved is lost to me just like the sunrise. <br /> <br /> And I am not going to let myself fall down that gorram rabbit hole tonight. The past is fucking gone and I've got shit worth fighting for in the fucking here and now. Like Lori. She wanted to watch 'Indianan Jones and the Temple of Doom\u201d but we talked her into 'Raiders of the Lost Ark\u201d instead since it was the first one and she hadn't seen it yet. That was another fun watch with everyone laughing and commenting, no memories getting dredged up as a bonus. Ace rolled out a zombie movie which I quite enjoyed. Putting Jacob and Insincere Marguerite on the same night is going to prove interesting. Jacob decided to pick \u201cSchindler's List\u201d which I had not heard of before. That... was a hell of a movie. A serious departure from fun entertainment and into serious drama about the horrors of the Holocaust. It was very well done in every way I can think of but I don't think I can watch it again. The scenes of brutality were abrupt and stark and... and I am not comfortable with how they made me feel. And my darkling sister's choice of \u201cDonnie Darko\u201d followed it. That movie is just weird and reeling from the other I was pretty soundly lost more often than not. I think I do want to watch it again at some point when I can focus. That and Frank is the most epic fucking creepy rabbit ever. I wonder where I could get a copy of that mask? If nothing else, I bet Julia would be all over making one or at least helping Gawain do it. Not sure he'd be down with it hanging in the bedroom though, might should promise to put it up in the office when I bring the idea up.<br /> <br /> And my surprise for Gawain went over perfectly. It wasn't hard for the others to keep him distracted while I got it done. I still asked Andromeda and Joan to help, even though I had originally intended to use it as a way to get them together. It was rather enjoyable to watch them together. They are so fucking head over heels for each other and still in the whole it's all new part of things. Hey, I may be a Darkling but those two are adorable together and Zod knows they both needed someone. And they were a great help getting the basics of the workshop set up. And it was so worth it. I mean, we will all benefit from it but Gawain loves to work. I know he was into it before and I think having some link to his past feels good for him. And seeing him working, creating something beautiful rather than destroying something. I know that look. It's like when I fight. His mind is narrowed down to what he's working and it blocks out all the shit and guilt and doubt. I can watch him work for hours. And once I showed it to him, Jacob and he and I set to fixing things up a bit more, adding a few things for the leather-working (Gawain is still determined to make me some armor to keep me from getting hurt. And I won't lie, I wouldn't exactly mind rocking some sexy bad-ass briar-wolf leathers) We also spent some time rounding out the tools and all. I think we've got it set up pretty well now. And just in time to see about getting me some knives and swords for my upcoming act. <br /> <br /> My lessons with Annika have been going well. I am still far (very far) from perfect but I am getting better. She liked my ideas of bringing sword dancing or knife throwing to my stage act and we've been working on how to incorporate those sort of moves into it. I've been focused on the more Slavic style with its flashy and quick weapon moves but mating it with the sensuous body movement of the more middle eastern inspired dancers. It's complex and blending the two is quite demanding. I'm not ready for a performance yet but it feels good when I pull it all together. I'm still kinda amazed by the notion that I'll ever be good enough to share a stage with her and Lori without embarrassing them.<br /> <br /> Practicing knife throwing has gone really well. I think I may actually be ready to build an act around my skills very soon. Jacob was quick to join in when I started working on it after the party and my impromptu performance with Captain Jack. We've both got plenty of raw coordination and so it's come quite easily and quickly to us. I'm a little better than he is at it, but then everything involving knives comes naturally to me. <br /> <br /> And we've continued our regular sparring as well. I've also been trading blows with anyone that I can coax into the backyard. Gawain's danced with us several times and I even managed to convince Lori's girl to play with me by promising to keep it purely to fists and feet. That was a good workout. It was unfamiliar and different and she didn't hold back once we got going. I've never spent much time learning to fight without a blade but I always figured that with the glass being a part of me it wouldn't be that difficult. I was wrong. I am thinking of asking if Ace would be willing to show me how to box. It would be good to be prepared for a situation where I need to use fists, like taking down Mary's fetch without killing it. I'm sure Ace misses having someone to spar with and boxing is an actual sport... I might actually be able to find a gym and be able cut loose when I'm feeling the need without the complications of picking a knife fight with some drunken asshole in a random bar.<br /> <br /> I've also been showing Jacob and Lori how to shoot. Jacob's doing well with the Glock and Lori is quite taken with her Black Widow. I made sure to emphasize safety heavily from the start. You know, don't point a gun at anyone you're not planning to kill and all that. A poorly trained shooter is more of a threat to themselves after all. That and I really, really do not want to get shot by either of them by accident. (If I'm going to get shot by one of my own, it had better fucking be intentional and fatal.) So far they're both coming along well.<br /> <br /> Now while it has been nice to catch my breath, I am a bit frustrated about a couple of issues. I mean, the lack of new fires to put out has given time to focus on the existing ones but I really wish we'd had more luck with those. We are no closer to the Table or Kimberly's shooter. Our only real lead in the former remains Mr Grey, who is simply nowhere to be found. And while Twitch isn't as scarce, he's only come to the club once (opening night) and none of us are exactly close enough to discreetly chat him up about Grey. And hell, the way folks talked, it's not that they were friends, but more he was the only one that put up with Mr Grey's alien behavior. I mean, at least Andromeda is cute and has a tight little rack and ass to make up for her weirdness. And Hailey wasn't made to be an operator and thus seems to lack the habit of dissecting you with her eyes. (Or the bitch is just better at hiding it, her sort usually are...) My only concern with getting Joan and Andromeda together is the Table. Joan seems keen on her girl having it back, which isn't going to happen. She's made it clear she thinks of it as belonging to Andromeda. Hopefully, I can press upon them both the risks of trying to keep the damned thing safe and the need for it to be under the watchful eyes of the Autumn Court or better yet for them to destroy it. I mean, not even Jacob trusts Master Darke with the thrice-damned thing, Jolie doesn't want to deal with it, and as much as I'd like to believe Lucien's claims of wanting to destroy the thing I do not trust him to give up a potential weapon of that magnitude. Not that destroying it is the top of Charlotte's agenda, but she's been honest about her intentions and I do believe that she will if it's the most damage it can inflict on the Gentry or the only way to keep it from falling back into their hands. Yes, I'm a little biased and yes, I am interested in whatever \u201cspecial tutoring\u201d she promised if I managed to see that it landed in her web. Still, it really does seem like the best solution we have and the others seem to agree. Of course, we still have to find the blasted thing before we can do anything with it.<br /> <br /> At least we have a real lead to chase in that one. The trail of Dark Kimberly's shooter has been cold stony dead. The goblin contract (or power that produced the same results) isn't common or easy to find but there isn't a way to know who has it. And the one flaw to it that might have given them away wasn't found soon enough to be useful. So really my efforts in the library have been no fucking help in tracking down the bastard. We don't know why or who or really what did it. We don't know if Kimberly was specifically targeted and if so if it was personal or aimed at Changelings in general or Flores or maybe inhuman nightclubs. I haven't gone to see this Dexter vampire yet but Madam Spidertoes didn't believe he or his kind were involved. Still, I did say I would go and play diplomat and it is an excuse to make the acquaintance of the undead. His club is pretty decent, I've checked it out a few times but I promised I wouldn't meet him alone so I didn't drop the code phrase. I am pretty sure the others are going to want to check this out as well. I'm just not sure how he'll feel about a half dozen of us dropping in on him when part of the reason I need to go is to make sure he knows the local Fae haven't taken up vampire hunting as a hobby like they do in Hollywood. Of course, Lori is far better at sweet talking and even if he doesn't have a pulse if anyone can raise the dead she can. And hell, our venues may be totally different but maybe we can talk shop. And who knows, he might actually know something useful.<br /> <br /> The only other news in that case comes to us from Master Darke. He summoned Jacob this morning and outlined a theory that the shooting was the work of the Phantom Tong. He wasn't forthcoming on what evidence had come to light but he was quick to finger Lucien Torrez as being an ally or a member or maybe even the leader of the Phantom Tong. He did back that up with a pattern of behavior favorable to the Tong but if this group is everything they're alleged to be they could be manipulating Lucien. Also, even if it was the Phantom Tong, we're no clearer on why or who exactly was being targeted. And the Phantom Tong isn't big on unclear messages. They always make sure everyone knows their handiwork since it helps to spread their reputation for being able to get to anyone anywhere. There are theories about why there wasn't a claim (Kimberly was the target and knew why she'd shot or it wasn't sanctioned, which does conveniently explain why Lucien Torrez is actively investigating if he's involved). It feels thin to me and consciously or not Darke wants Lucien to be responsible for something. Hell, he might just be tossing the accusation out to try to weaken his enemy. But thin is more than nothing. The Tong is slightly more open in LA since the Night Court is less hostile to their stated purpose of keeping Freeholds from getting complacent or their actual purpose of being a Fairy crime syndicate. Apparently, Insincere Marguerite knows a guy who knows a guy or something along those lines. Not a solid contact but someone connected enough to at least pass along an inquiry. Of course, there's no reason for them to give us a straight answer (if they give us an answer at all) and no way for us to really know if we can believe anything they might tell us. Lori is right, this Nancy Drew bullshit blows fucking moon rocks through a straw. I am so much more of a Mike Hammer kind of girl. <br /> <br /> At least news on the home front is better. I need to go through the talent agents we've been working with and see if I can't make some magic happen. Seems one of Lori's recent gigs has gotten her some decent exposure (it's a tasteful nude you see...) She's been featured in a Jack Daniels ad that's getting some distribution in the latest Playboy among others. And while she's got some traction she needs to leverage it into landing an agent that can use all these buzzwords and lingo to land her some big time work. The kind of big time work that means she gets to evolve from model to <i>super</i> model, or maybe branch out to model/actress, or bring her powerhouse combination of talent and beauty within radar range of a music producer with two brain cells to rub together. And the higher Lori's star rises the more fame and fortune she brings back to the Dream House as our headliner.<br /> <br /> And I've also made some headway into thawing the Russian winter. While we were sparing last week Jacob just spaced out on me. Not just missed a beat but full on fucking Kung Fu flashback shit. I had to jerk hard to try to pull my thrust short and I still ended up carving his collarbone hard enough to draw blood. That snapped him out his grasshopper moment right quick with a surprised yelp. And I had to slam down the mental breaks even harder. He tried to just shake it off and keep going but I called a stop and pulled my glass in. Fuck... There is absolutely no way to describe just how visceral it feels to drag your razor along a bone. I knew I hadn't hit anything vital and it wasn't that deep but he was bleeding freely and the visions dancing in my head were not sugar plums. So I shook my head and called a halt. I fetched the first aid kit and washed my hands without giving into the urge to taste his essence. Once I made it clear I wasn't going to do more than just clean and dress his cut he relaxed a little. I do get it, most of the others do tend to react strongly to light wounds and he's used to not having the luxury of having enough bandages to bother with something that minor. Of course, the fact that he and I do know pain and hardship more intimately than the others is exactly why I couldn't hold my tongue about what had happened.<br /> <br /> Once I'd gotten the cut cleaned and taped a couple a gauze pads over it to keep it that way till it healed I kept a hand on his shoulder and fixed him a hard look and told him firmly that we don't get to be distracted because it falls upon us to protect the others. We've already paid the terrible price to learn how to bleed and kill. I don't know what he's done and I don't have to to know what he's going through trying to keep that monster caged. I tried to keep the truth about my parent's murder inside and we know how that ended. I told him it would could out sooner or later. That he didn't get to choose if it happened. What he did get to decide was how it would happen. I told him he had to pick someone and talk to them about it. I suggested Insincere Marguerite because I know she's dark enough to understand and I believe she cares enough about him to accept whatever he's done. And while I don't personally trust his court, I know they actually have people specifically trained for this kind of shit and he is one of them. I know his relationship with Luna pretty much begins and ends with fucking but her pragmatism and brutal honesty was surprisingly helpful with some of my own issues. I also told him I was there and ready to listen whenever he needed or wanted to talk and I promised that no matter what he's done I will hear him out. From his reaction, I am pretty sure he's no closer to pulling up a couch at the clinic than I am. He did seem to be honestly thinking over what I'd said and so once I'd given him my promise I paused to wait for his response. It wasn't easy to just let the yard fall quiet as I packed the kit back up but I'd made my case and he was thinking about it, deciding if he could trust me with his terrible secret.<br /> <br /> I finished and set the kit aside in silence. He looked at me and wet his lips. I gave him a nod and reached out to touch his arm lightly and rest my fingertips on the back of his hand. The moment drew out into several very long seconds before he shook his head and pulled back slightly. His voice was tight and quiet as he told me he couldn't. Not yet. I nodded as grabbed one of the bottles of water we'd brought and offered it to him before getting one for myself.<br /> <br /> We both took a couple of sips and then he started to talk quietly. He told me that he thought he was suffering from post traumatic stress. I've seen his scars and I know enough to know they're not all battle scars. He has flashbacks sometimes but he assured me that today was the first time they've had any serious effect on him. I gave him a somewhat skeptical look at that but didn't say anything. I can't say I have seen any evidence to the contrary after all. It seems to be a result of his exceptional memory. I hadn't thought of it, but in addition to recalling names and faces and favorite drinks almost flawlessly it means he recalls his time in Arcadia quite vividly. He didn't go into any detail but he admitted that he'd done things he wished he could forget and experienced things that he still had nightmares about. Then he fell quiet, so I took his hand and squeezed it. \u201cVictims have graves.\u201cI told him, \u201cSurvivors have scars. And the worst of them are rarely the ones we wear on our skin. You are alive and you are not alone.\u201d He gave that a moment's consideration and then told me that he did feel that talking about it would help but that he wasn't ready to. I smiled and promised again that I was available any time he needed to talk and that no matter what it was, I would hear him out completely. Then I rolled away from him and back to my feet while calling forth my glass so we could finish sparring.<br /> <br /> Damn, I've been at this all afternoon. But I'm pretty much caught up and Gawain's had a good rest. It's almost time for tonight's culture night. Since Gawain's sick and Ace is otherwise occupied this evening we've skipped them in the rotation. Which makes tonight Lori and myself. I've tracked down a copy of \u201cBrotherhood of the Wolf,\u201d or \u201cLe Pacte des Loups\u201d since I got it in the original French with English subtitles. The Internet promises that it's a solidly entertaining action movie and it will give me a chance to test the French Insincere Marguerite's been teaching me. Lori's pick is \u201cThis is Spinal Tap\u201d which I've never seen but is apparently the movie that started the whole goes to eleven meme.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T02:38:38-08:00","id":367171,"title":"","content":"<b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> I guess I\u2019ve been kind of slack in writing in this thing over the past week or so. Early on in the week I made everyone Fuzzy Navel popsicles. I think they were popular. Gawain\u2019s mention of the woman Felicity made me think of the little fawn girl I knew. So, I made popsicles, like I did for her, but these were of the more adult variety. Maybe I should see if anyone at the shows would be interested in frozen margaritas or something? <br /> <br /> Yeah, so the nightmares that night were not fun. I kept seeing them bring in that little girl and lay her down on the bed. I stood at the back of the room and watched Diane work as hard as she could to save the little girl, but there was too much damage. Felicity gave one last sigh and closed her eyes. Flecks of blood dotted her lips and chin. Her stomach was a mess. There was blood everywhere, dark and sticky. I could only guess as to what caused the injury. No one told me any details. No one really paid much attention to me at all actually. I probably could have walked right out the door while they worked to save her, but I couldn\u2019t move. I was rooted to the spot, and could only look on as that shy little girl fought to live. She did. She was so brave, but it wasn\u2019t enough. In that moment I think I truly hated my brother in arms.<br /> <br /> Goddess I need a drink. I need a few drinks. I am going to do my utmost to be nothing close to sober tonight.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Goddess, I\u2019m slipping. Over the past few weeks I\u2019ve been sparring with Calamity and practicing my knife throwing. I\u2019ve never been great at it, and she hadn\u2019t really tried, so we figured \u2018Let\u2019s learn a new skill!\u2019 The knife throwing has been going great. Both of us are getting better with each passing day. The sparring has been going well too, except for a bit of a hiccup today. I\u2019m not sure what it was that did it. Maybe Calamity came in from a different angle than usual, maybe it was the expression on her face, or in her eyes, but suddenly I wasn\u2019t in the backyard of the Dream House anymore. I was outside of Claire Falls. I had just told Rook that I wasn\u2019t going to help him bring back Diane or let him hurt the others. Not that the residents of Claire Falls would believe my sincerity. Anyway, I defied Rook and he attacked. It wasn\u2019t like the sparring where he held back, and the look in his eyes wasn\u2019t the teasing glare it usually was. It was cold and hard. I remember that strike hurting a lot. It wasn\u2019t a mortal wound, he wasn\u2019t going for the kill. He aimed to incapacitate. Then I felt a sharp burn across my collarbone and snapped back to reality. Calamity had cut me. <br /> The look on her face instantly told me that she hadn\u2019t meant to actually draw blood, but had no choice but to change the angle of her attack as much as she could to avoid actually slitting my throat. I stepped back and fingered the hole in my shirt. I\u2019ll admit that I was still a little fuzzy from the flashback and took a second or two to get my bearings. Calamity looked at me with those knowing eyes and a flicker of something else, hunger is the only word that really describes it. I insisted that I was fine and got back into a ready stance. I was ready to keep going, but Calamity stayed relaxed and even sheathed her knife. I asked her what was up, and she insisted on bandaging my cut. Even though we share similar views on what constitutes an injury that needs attention, she insisted that we see to it. I will admit that I was a little relived to not get a lecture on men trying to act macho in the face of injury. I wonder if that\u2019s how the others see me when I insist that I\u2019m okay when I just get minor wounds. If they think that I\u2019m just trying to show off how much it doesn\u2019t bother me? I\u2019ll admit that the cut hurt a bit, it was right across the bone and starting over my shoulder, but it wasn\u2019t life threatening. It wasn\u2019t even that serious. The only things it was doing was stinging and bleeding. I could still stand, I could still fight, and none of my limbs were incapacitated. The others don\u2019t go all \u201cmother-hen\u201d over a paper cut, and this wasn\u2019t that much worse. Just a little bigger. I guess it\u2019s just a matter of perspective.<br /> <br /> When she came back with the kit Calamity scolded me for being distracted and reminded me that we are the ones that have to stay vigilant, and that the others rely on us. Then she reminded me why I sometimes think of her as a predator with keen senses. She looked right at me and said, &quot;I don't know what it is, but I know there's something and it will not stay inside. It's going to come out. You can choose when or you can wait till it escapes but it will come out.&quot; I went cold inside at that. She then told me that I needed to talk to someone. It could be Marguerite, Luna, someone in my court or her, but that I needed to find someone to open up to. She promised that she would listen and hear me out no matter what I had to say, no matter how bad I thought it was. I had to stifle a manic laugh. I could never talk to the folks in my court. The only one that wouldn\u2019t kill me outright is LowJack, but I\u2019m not 100 % confident in his reaction. I\u2019m sure Insincere Marguerite would take it all in stride and be understanding and anything I needed her to be. She really is very sweet and attentive, but the thing is I don\u2019t want her to see that part of me. I don\u2019t want to be a monster to her. She met me as a quiet, kind of sad bartender that protects his friends and makes a good fuzzy navel. I want to be that good guy in her eyes. I don\u2019t want to be the monster that I know I am deep down. Maybe I\u2019m being selfish, but I want her to see the good in me without the taint of the truth.<br /> <br /> I was so tempted to open up right there and then and let things fall as they would. I was prepared to die by her blade if she saw fit to end me. I couldn\u2019t do it though. My throat closed up ad nothing would come out. As soon as I could breathe I admitted, albeit in a softer voice than I intended, that I think I suffer from post-traumatic stress and that I have flashbacks on occasion. They usually have no effect on my life, saying that today was an exception. I\u2019m not sure she really believed that last little white lie. I told her that I have a nearly photographic memory and admitted that there are things I\u2019ve done that I\u2019m not proud of, and things that happened to me that I still have nightmares about, and I can recall them all in vivid detail. Sometimes it catches me by surprise. She reiterated that she\u2019d listen if I needed an ear, but I declined. She looked so certain that she could handle whatever I told her. Maybe she could. I don\u2019t know. I don\u2019t know if I wanted to find out at that moment. I think a part of me did though, so I told her that I think she was right about talking being helpful, but that I wasn\u2019t ready yet. She just nodded and said that she\u2019d be there when I was. Then like a switch the conversation was over and we got back into a ready stance for the dance to resume.<br /> <br /> A part of me wishes that I could just talk to her and tell her what a bad guy Rook is and how I want to see him dead for what he did. It might add credence to my switching sides story, but it wouldn\u2019t be true. I don\u2019t really want to see him dead. I don\u2019t even want to see him hurt. Despite everything he did to others and to me, he was always there for me. We were like brothers. He looked out for me when I started out. He trained me and kept me going. He even helped bandage my wounds after he brought me back to our Lady. He carried out his orders. He did what he was good at, and used his skills to break me. You don\u2019t deny the Lady and get away unscathed. He did little things between \u201csessions,\u201d to help. He brought food every couple of days. I\u2019d gone longer without, but he made sure I had food and water. He would also bandage my wounds and reset bones if needs be. There were a few times that he made a cut that just an inch or two in any other direction would have been more serious or more painful, but he did what he could. Don\u2019t get me wrong, he did the Lady\u2019s bidding. He did it well. Between the two of them I was praying for death. <br /> <br /> There was one time the Lady had Rook make cuts across my back, clear from one side to the other. They crossed one another, some up, some down, some diagonal. I thought perhaps they made a shape that pleased her? (Later I found out that the scars make the shape of her brand). Then she used her own ice blades to make the cuts wider and eventually cut strips of skin off the length of the cuts. I don\u2019t know how long it took for her to be satisfied with the work. Every time I passed out, she woke me back up. When it became harder to keep me conscious she used some sort of drug to keep me awake. It must have been a powerful stimulant. On a normal day it likely would have made me hyper I\u2019m sure, but given my state it just kept me in the land of the waking. I discovered then that after a certain amount of pain the body shuts down for a reason. It does it to keep you sane. I\u2019m fairly certain that if I\u2019d been in the Lady\u2019s care much longer I would have lost all grasp on reality, at least moreso than I already have. As it was she got bored and left me hanging by my wrists from the ceiling. Hours later she sent Rook in to cut me down. That was the last time before the end that we were alone. He looked honestly worried when he saw my back. It was there. I know I saw it. It didn\u2019t show long, but I saw concern.<br /> <br /> Rook cut me down and tended to my back as best he could. He even gave me some goblin fruit to help speed the healing. I\u2019m pretty sure that I was dying at that point. I don\u2019t know if that was the Lady\u2019s intention or if she even realized how far she\u2019d gone. So, Rook helped heal me and I was finally allowed to pass out. I was left alone for days after that. Then the last day came. The Lady came to my cell and used her powers to immobilize me in a relatively thin layer of ice. Then she slowly, so very slowly made spikes of ice grow out in every direction. They had gotten to maybe four inches long when she stopped and looked up. A look crossed her face, kind of half way between angry and worried. She melted all the ice instantly and left me gasping and coughing up blood on the floor. She healed the wounds that were lethal and called for another to take over. Then Rook was sent in to finish what the Lady had started and he opened the session by running his blade across my throat. I will admit that I was a little concerned what the rest of the session would entail if that\u2019s how it started, but there was that part of me that didn\u2019t care. I didn\u2019t mind if I bled out then and there. But then he was called away as well by a servant, and I was left lying on the floor, unrestrained. Then the door was left open just a crack, and I took my chance to escape.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know if it was an accident that the door was unlocked, or if it was intentional. I\u2019ll never know unless I ask Rook himself, or find the messenger that came for him, and I\u2019m not sure I\u2019m ready for that confrontation just yet. Part of me even worries that he might have gotten in trouble for my escape. I can\u2019t help it. Despite all that has happened between us, Rook was like a brother for over a decade. That kind of bond is hard to break. That kind of bond is what might make it hard for the others to believe that I renounced the Lady. If Rook comes looking for me I know that I will likely not allow the others to kill him. Whether by force or persuasion, I will do what I can to keep him alive. For better or worse he is my brother, in arms, in deed, in everything but blood.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> <br /> Today, well technically yesterday since it is 2am, I asked Lorelei if she\u2019d like to go roller skating again. She seemed keen on it and we decided to invite the others as well. They were all interested, so after Lori grabbed her own skates, we all headed over to the roller rink. Ace was his usual exuberant self. Insincere Marguerite agreed to come when I asked her. She hesitated a moment, like she was considering the pros and cons, but eventually said \u2018yes.\u2019 I was happy she agreed to come. We skated a couple of slow dances, and the rest of the time just tried to stay out of the lights. We made a game of it, trying to stay out of the spot lights. We skated this way and that, zigging and zagging. It was fun. <br /> <br /> Overall I think Marguerite was happy that it was an indoor rink. Sunlight would not have been her friend. But we were inside and the rink was fairly dark. There were colored lights and a disco ball that made colors dance across the floor, and across her pale skin. The pair of us, pale as you can get, with a rainbow dancing around us. I probably looked silly, but Marguerite did not. She was lovely. She is only moreso in moonlight.<br /> <br /> Gawain is far more graceful on skates than you\u2019d think seeing him. Well, seeing him as we do, not as the humans do. Calamity of course is grace on wheels, and together they are just cute. And whatever I do, I cannot let Calamity hear me say that out loud. They roller skated/danced together a couple times during slow songs. The lights were dimmed and the disco ball was reflecting a myriad of colors across the floor. The cute couple even had a spot light on them for part of one dance. I just had to take a picture.<br /> <br /> Lori was great as usual. Beauty and grace combined. She was better than Calamity, but only because she\u2019s had more recent practice. She flowed across the rink like silk. The mortals of course just saw a pretty blonde dancing across the floor, but the rest of us saw her as she is, wings and all. I bet those things are great for balance. <br /> <br /> After we got back to the Dream House I took a few more pictures of the cute couple, \u2018cause, yeah, they\u2019re adorable together. Overall it was a pretty good day.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> So, we decided as a motley that enough of us were behind the times, so to speak, so we came up with the idea of Culture Night. We figured the best way to do this was through movies. We decided to do this on Monday nights, and to pair up. The pairs we came up with are Ace and Calamity, Gawain and Lorelei, and then Insincere Marguerite and me. The first night we did this was Gawain and Lorelei. Gawain suggested \u201cLadyhawke\u201d, while Lori suggested \u201cIndiana Jones and the Temple of Doom,\u201d but we ended up watching \u201cRaiders of the Lost Ark\u201d. I hadn\u2019t seen \u201cLadyhawke\u201d before. I thought it was pretty good. The effects were a little cheesy, but the story was good. I can see why Gawain would suggest it. Then we saw Raiders. I don\u2019t think there isn\u2019t a time or place where that movie isn\u2019t popular. I saw it in St. Petersburg before we moved to Portland.<br /> <br /> The next week was Ace and Calamity\u2019s turn. Ace suggested \u201cDead Alive.\u201d Another movie I had not seen before. Not bad for a horror/zombie movie. Then Calamity showed us \u201cThe Princess Bride.\u201d That was a fun movie. Fun fights, witty dialogue, and the \u201ctorture\u201d scene made me laugh. I couldn\u2019t help it, it was too funny. If only.<br /> <br /> After that was Insincere Marguerite and my turn. I suggested \u201cSchindler\u2019s List.\u201d I figured the others suggested action movies that were fun to watch, but not all that serious. So I suggested a really good movie that I had to watch in school years ago. It was as good, and depressing, as the last time I saw it. The others enjoyed it I think, but there were more than one comment made about Winter court and sorrow. It was good though. The others may not have all really enjoyed the movie, but they all admitted that it was a good film. After that Marguerite showed \u201cDonnie Darko.\u201d I had never seen that one either. I\u2019ll say one thing for it. It\u2019s definitely a step or two away from my movie suggestion.<br /> <br /> And the last movie night was a slight change up. Calamity suggested \u201cBrotherhood of the Wolf,\u201d while Lori suggested \u201cThis is Spinal Tap.\u201d The fights in \u201cBrotherhood\u2026\u201d were fun, the plot was not hard to figure out\u2026hell, it played out like a 7<sup>th</sup> Sea game. Spinal Tap was interesting. I think I would have enjoyed it more when I was a kid. Hell, my fetch might like it. He\u2019s a \u201cmusician.\u201d I guess I just need to think of what the next movie I want to show on Movie Night will be. Maybe I\u2019ll suggest \u201cButch Cassidy and the Sundance Kid.\u201d The last time I saw it was dubbed into Russian. Might be interesting to see it in English.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Today was informative and kind of scary all at the same time. I met with Master Darke earlier today. He wanted to talk to me about the attack on Dark Kimberly and new information that he found recently. As usual we met at the clinic in Master Darke\u2019s office. It was dark and foreboding as always. It would be nice to meet somewhere brighter, less full of shadows, but I suppose that would defeat the purpose behind the threatening aura presented in that place. He likes to intimidate, no question about it. Anyway, he said that he had an idea of who was behind the attack on Kimberly. He believes that the culprits are a group called the Phantom Tong, and that Lucien Torrez is a member of this group. It has never been definitively proven that Torrez is a member of the Phantom Tong, but apparently he has been seen to support them, aid them, or approve of them in some way. It sounded circumstantial to me, but who am I to argue with my court\u2019s leader? He also has suspicions that Gunnar is a member of the Tong. Gunnar seemed like a capable fellow during the whole \u201cfetch mess,\u201d though I will admit that he has an impressive understanding and practice with dark magics. I didn\u2019t want to ask Gunnar questions then, and honestly am not sure I want to know the answers now. I can see Gunnar being effective in a group that caters to chaos, but he seemed to only use those dark magics under the order of Torrez.<br /> <br /> Apparently the Tong always leave a \u201ccalling card\u201d to claim responsibility to whatever action occurs, but that was not the case this time. Darke is still convinced that it is the Phantom Tong\u2019s fault, but if they did not leave a card, and they have for every other thing that they\u2019ve done, it calls that assumption into question. I\u2019ll admit that it is a valid hypothesis, but for the moment that\u2019s all it is. There is no definitive proof that this was the work of the Tong or that Torrez was connected. Frankly, Torrez was rather interested in finding out who the culprit was and helped us gain access to security footage to look for clues. Unless he was 100% sure that nothing would show up on film, it sheds some doubt on his involvement. Don\u2019t get me wrong, I\u2019m not especially trusting of the man. He is dangerous, and not just to the gentry. Darke is too, but Torrez is more rash. More apt to react in anger, violently. Darke is calm, collected, and almost always has a plan. I\u2019m not sure who is more dangerous to be honest. For me personally I\u2019d have to say it\u2019s Torrez. He actively hates the Winter court, and especially those of us that deal in narcotics.<br /> <br /> Speaking of narcotics, that reminds me of something else that Master Darke said. He had the idea that the hit might have been originally targeted against the Winter court because the Tong disapprove of our involvement in the drug trade in town. They want a monopoly and we\u2019re interfering in that. He thought that Molly Nuit might have been the original target, but they changed at the last minute because Molly left so soon. He also suggested that it might have possible that I was their original target, because of my \u201cside job,\u201d but was not ultimately targeted because the security at the club is too tight. Anyone that got into the club with the intention of doing me, or anyone else, harm could get in. They might even hurt me, but getting back out in any other way besides a body bag is not likely. If Gawain didn\u2019t cleave the fucker in half, Calamity would slice and dice the guy until they wished for something as sweet as pain.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not sure if I was actually a target, or if Master Darke just wanted to put me on edge. I suppose I\u2019m always something of a target for the Summer court, but I\u2019ve yet to see any evidence that I might be a target for the Phantom Tong. I suppose I could try and draw any possible attackers out by making a tempting target of myself, but I\u2019m not entirely sure I\u2019m that much of a masochist. I wasn\u2019t confident enough in what Master Darke might have in mind if I suggested the \u201cbait\u201d idea to even suggest it while I was in his office. If someone in the motley had been telling me all of that stuff then I might have offered to be a lure, but I trust their intentions towards me right now far more than I trust Master Darke\u2019s. Or at least, I trust their intentions not to change as quickly as Darke\u2019s might. I seem to be somewhat in his confidence at the moment considering the information he has shared with me. Even if he hadn\u2019t flat out said that he was trusting me with this information, I would have understood the subtext there. It\u2019s actually a bit unnerving when someone specifically points out that they are trusting you with something. Like they felt they had to be implicit rather than just assume your trustworthiness. <br /> <br /> So, aside from the semi-informative and kind of creepy meeting with Master Darke, the other thing that happened today was Andromeda coming by with concerns about Joan. Apparently they have been intimate over the past couple of weeks, but just recently was the first time that they used one of Andromeda\u2019s \u201ctoys.\u201d To put it politely, Joan had been a virgin, but no longer. This flipped some kind of switch in Joan however. Now, the normally strong, take charge woman, is acting completely subservient to Andromeda. This is more than a little disturbing if you ask me. Granted, I\u2019ve only known Joan for a relatively short time but submissive is a word I would have never associated with the woman. Her becoming so docile and meek is exactly what she had been fighting so hard against during her time in Arcadia, and once she returned to The World. <br /> <br /> Andromeda was very concerned about this and came to us to see if we might be able to help. After the explanation was done there was much discussion about what to do. Calamity went to the Autumn court archives to research the issue. She wanted to, and I agree with her, keep Joan\u2019s problem quiet for now. It might be seen as suspicious if Joan suddenly changes her personality so drastically due to something Andromeda did, benign or not. The rest of the freehold may not see it as such. So she came back with some options. Joan can either complete a quest in the hedge on her own, or we can look for a special kind goblin fruit that restores her maidenhead. <br /> <br /> We discussed the quest and figured in her current state, Joan would be in more danger if she went alone into the hedge. We all agreed that it might not be a great idea. We figured the goblin fruit would be the better option, which led to phone calls to a couple of folks in the freehold that deal with goblin fruit. Turns out that no one in town has any of this fruit, but one person did know where it could be found. I think we all agreed that going into the hedge to retrieve some of this fruit for Joan, though dangerous, was the better option. It would have the advantage of more of us being present to watch each other\u2019s backs. Now we just need to make sure we know where we\u2019re going, and pack accordingly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> I\u2019ve been such a bad grub and not updated this book. It\u2019s been weeks! Um, okay. I don\u2019t have time to write everything down. I am a busy grub. So, summarize.<br /> <br /> English: English is improving. Maybe. Rereading old journals, I don\u2019t seem to use \u201cme\u201d enough when writing. Possibly.<br /> <br /> Work: Going well. The catwalks are well set up just how I want them. The people who work the nights I don\u2019t now understand that they will not touch or move things they are not supposed to touch or move, unless they have no fear whatsoever of heights. I am not in the habit of repeating myself, especially when dangling one over the side does just as well. The Puppets watch them as well. Carefully.<br /> <br /> I have worked on an adaptation of \u201cQueens\u201d by Caravan Palace, but not gotten it where it is\u2026exciting enough. It is easy to sultry it up a little and hand it to Ginny or Lorelei, but it needs to be\u2026burlesqued up a bit. Now \u201cClash\u201d may do well for that. I am working on some general stuff for that. Outside there, I may perhaps do something with \u201cIsrealism\u201d by Army of Lovers. And I bet Austin could do well with \u201cKing Midas.\u201d<br /> <br /> Love: Julia has pretty much moved in with me, despite us only having dated for about two months. Her stuff is split between my room and a room in the basement, and a lot of her furniture is in the hall that has my and Lorelei\u2019s rooms. Julia is very much mine. My possession of her could not be more complete without my being her Keeper. And I am not.<br /> <br /> Probably.<br /> <br /> Julia had an art show, and essentially came out by having I there as her partner. They made I wear shoes. It was awful. Julia let me sit behind the desk and remove my shoes, so I stayed behind it the entire time, except when I had to be on Julia\u2019s arm. Since Lorelei modeled, she had Lorelei in a gown she was about to fall out of there, because given her druthers Julia will have cleavage everywhere. \u201cMostly Straight.\u201d Clearly.<br /> <br /> Lorelei is doing well, if quite stubborn. She is very focused on herself and De La Rocha. She has accepted that the lines between the couples are blurred, and we share a bed sometimes. She has now been in playboy. Technically. I don\u2019t see the draw of playboy\u2026I rarely find women attractive I cannot smell. I must protect my small grub nose. Of course, for whatever reason, I lack this issue with men, on the rare occasions I actually find one attractive. Anyway.<br /> <br /> Lorelei smells pretty good.<br /> <br /> De La Rocha is not giving herself as wholeheartedly to the whole moving in together thing. She almost always stays with Lorelei, but it seems a point of pride that she maintains her own space. To her credit, Lorelei appears to be taking this the right way. Though if she moves in here, I hope she puts that vinyl collection where I can easily access it. Hopefully.<br /> <br /> Flores is still my plaything also, though she only comes here for fun. She really smells amazing. I honestly envy her a bit on that. I\u2019ve not really fooled around with Dionisia again but we flirt. A lot. Jacob I have seen privately a few times, which is nice. Of course he is, I believe, seeing Luna as well. I will be going on a \u201cdate\u201d with Jolie, who is \u201cdating\u201d a number of area fey as her relationship with the Autumn Queen is in tatters. I suspect she is\u2026investigating certain rumors. She will find the truth. Definitely.<br /> <br /> I am trying to not claim more people, beyond Julia and my Dearest of course. That would be bad. Flores tests me, however. Frequently.<br /> <br /> Oh, Julia and I went with Calamity and Gawain to see <i>Maleficent</i>. It was neat. My first double date. Julia wanted it more than I, but I can be accommodating. They don\u2019t like shoeless people in the theater. Plebes.<br /> <br /> Motley: We have begun doing \u201cCulture Night\u201d on Monday nights. The first one was Gawain and Lorelei. Gawain picked <i>Ladyhawke</i>, which I had not seen. Lorelei chose <i>Indiana Jones and the Temple of Doom</i>, but we watched <i>Raiders of the Lost Arc</i> instead. Then Ace and Calamity, where Ace showed <i>Dead Alive</i> and Calamity showed <i>Princess Bride</i>, which was not what I expected. Cary Elwes is, however, an excellent actor and attractive, so I was fine with it. As for <i>Dead Alive</i>, it was much better than I expected for a zombie movie, which don\u2019t tend to be to my taste. My night was with Jacob, I originally considered the <i>Broken</i> video, but decided it was too grim. So of course Jacob showed <i>Schindler\u2019s List</i>, which I wound up following with <i>Donnie Darko</i>. This past evening was <i>Brotherhood of the Wolf</i> (which I had not seen, as I do not, in fact, view every film originating in France) and <i>This is Spinal Tap</i> from Calamity and Lorelei. Calamity does continue to surprise. Generally.<br /> <br /> Jacob took us all roller-skating, it was interesting. I had not been since I was a young girl. Once I found my balance, however, it did not escape me. I did a couple dances with Jacob and had fun zipping around and avoiding the lights. Naturally.<br /> <br /> Calamity and Gawain seem to be doing well, and Ace is always hard at work on his\u2026projects. Lorelei has this Midsummer Night\u2019s Dream thing going on. A bit on the nose I think. Probably.<br /> <br /> Calamity is deranged. Jacob is moody. Lorelei is self-absorbed. Ace is unhinged. Gawain is na\u00efve. They are my Motley and I love them. Usually.<br /> <br /> Stuff: Recently it came up that Joan\u2019s relationship with Andromeda came with side effects, and we need to go to a swamp to get a fruit to make her a virgin again. I do not like swamps. I would prefer to swipe the fruit. Obviously.<br /> <br /> Also, Master Darke is claiming the Phantom Tong are responsible for Dark Kimberly\u2019s shooting and that Lucian is a member. Honestly, he probably is. I dealt lightly with the Tong in Los Angeles, and plan to root around there and see if I can dig anything up about the Tong in North LA. Maybe I can go instead if wallowing in the bog. Not likely.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XX</i><br /> <br /> The stuff with Master Darke, Joan, and the last \u201cmovie night\u201d happened in game. Everything else was covered as downtime.<br /> <br /> A lot of the \u201cgroup XP\u201d was spent. They upped Security, Doors, Amenities, and Workshop.<br /> <br /> Not much else, sorry for the (significant) delay in posting. Hopefully next will be sooner. I already have Gawain and Insincere Marguerite. Comments and Questions welcome<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span>