s=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://paizo.com/campaigns/RageAcrossIreland/gameplay\" target=\"_blank\">My W20 Play-by-Post Game</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2760-formosus","name":"Formosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T19:30:14-08:00","id":368174,"title":"","content":"It's absolutely a more long term thing. Your AP has, by the way, resulted in me fleshing out my local history more, some of which will come up when they meet with Felicity.<br /> <br /> So thanks for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T19:50:12-08:00","id":368191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play?p=368174#post368174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's absolutely a more long term thing. Your AP has, by the way, resulted in me fleshing out my local history more, some of which will come up when they meet with Felicity.<br /> <br /> So thanks for that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My pleasure <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I didn't mean to be flippant, by the way, I just meant it will be interesting to see if the Phantom Tong is really behind the attacks, who their targets really were, if Master Darke is making the whole thing up (or even just making part of it up in order to gain advantage over the Summer Court), etc. It's a cool mystery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://paizo.com/campaigns/RageAcrossIreland/gameplay\" target=\"_blank\">My W20 Play-by-Post Game</a>","edited":{"userid":2760,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2760-formosus","user":"Formosus","date":". 01-12-2015, 10:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2760-formosus","name":"Formosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T01:11:56-08:00","id":368406,"title":"","content":"That's the hope. ^_^. There is a lot going on behind the scenes, and stuff the PCs are just unaware of. The stuff with Felicity will hopefully let them know of some of the stuff going on in the background of the greater area.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T02:41:17-08:00","id":382833,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to check on the group at the Dream House. A trip into the Hedge to find fruit to help their friend Joan. Let\u2019s see how things go.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> Session 21<br /> <br /> June 9<sup>th</sup><br /> <br /> Man, I haven\u2019t written here in awhile. It\u2019s not that nothing has happened, really, just nothing... crazy, I guess? Things have been great and human and real, you know? Dates and movies and roller skating and shows and food poisoning. Hopefully whatever that last one was is out of my system now - it did make me miss movie night. Tonight was supposed to be me and Ace, but Ace was somewhere doing Ace-ly things, and I was mostly puking my guts up. So Calamity chose Le Pacte des Loups, which she says we\u2019ll have to rewatch sometime for me. It does sound great. Lori picked This is Spinal Tap, which is always fun. I think they enjoyed it. It\u2019s been great tradition so far. Everyone liked Ladyhawke, which was my first choice, and we\u2019ve gotten to see Princess Bride, and Schindler\u2019s List and Raiders of the Lost Ark. Lori had suggested Temple of Doom, but we talked her into starting with Raiders. I hadn\u2019t ever seen Dead Alive or Donnie Darko before, but they were fun too. Well, Donnie Darko was mostly bizarre, but in a fun way, you know.<br /> <br /> Me and Calamity are doing great. We\u2019ve gone on a bunch of dates, just her and me, and lots of double/group dates too. Me and her and Insincere Marguerite and Julia went to see Maleficent which was great. It\u2019s like Sleeping Beauty, but live action and Maleficent is the good guy and man was she hot. We also went out for dinner with Annika and Dark Kimberly. That was a little weird. Annika has interesting ideas about gender roles, you know? It was still fun though. I don\u2019t mind talking with Annika about stuff she likes or Calamity and Annika checking people out. And no one suggested I put on a dress, so that was a plus. We went roller skating too. It was kinda like a date, but mostly a motley thing. I did get Calamity out on the floor for a couple of the slow songs though. Insincere Marguerite and Jacob played a game of trying to avoid the spotlights. It was pretty adorable.<br /> <br /> Also! Calamity is just the best. I mean, I knew that and all, but it always deserves repeating. She got me a surprise present a couple of weeks ago. Andromeda and Joan helped her set up a whole metalworking shop in the Hedge House! It\u2019s amazing. We\u2019ve worked a little more on it together, set up some tanning and leatherworking tools and stuff like that. Me and Jacob have done some more work on that kind of thing. I think we\u2019re still hoping to put that briar wolf skin to good use, you know, and now we have a lot of the stuff to do it. I also managed to find enough time to make another flammenschwert, since I have the one that I can Smith up once more, and my nice one, that I managed to balance perfectly.<br /> <br /> Now, to the problem, the thing that reminded me that memory is fragile and the Gentry are dicks. Andromeda came by to talk with everyone, during one of my vomiting fits. The others filled me in though. I guess she and Joan were, well, using one of her special toys and it, you know, broke her hymen. And now she\u2019s all weird, acting really subservient and shit. It bothers Andromeda a lot, not to mention the rest of us. Calamity managed to figure out it was some kind of Gentry curse, and the best way to fix it, at least temporarily, would be to restore her virginity and there are goblin fruits to do that. She even figured out where to get them, letting everyone think she wanted them for herself. We can\u2019t let anyone know what happened, you know? For either of their sakes. Andromeda is on kinda thin ice already, and people like Percival and some of the Spring Court don\u2019t need any ammunition against Joan.<br /> <br /> The area of the Hedge with that goblin fruit wasn\u2019t too far. Jacob led us right to the swampy area. Lori was not happy with the idea of hanging around in a swamp. She kept her wings tight around her, and winced every time she pulled her boots out of the sucking mud. Insincere Marguerite had a better time - she can walk on water apparently. It seems like a handy trick, though I\u2019d feel super weird trying it. I was actually sinking in a little bit more than everyone, so I felt a lot less tall than usual. I was very careful not to pull my feet up too quickly, I didn\u2019t feel like having the ladies pissed at me, you know.<br /> <br /> The cherries we were looking for and a couple of other thing Flores asked us to keep an eye out for all grew under water, which was fine except said water was full of bog lurkers. I thought they were just logs, but Calamity and Insincere Marguerite noticed eyes moving on them. There was also tons of little caiman looking alligators. We brought back one of those for Ace. It\u2019s the sole inhabitant of the pirahnaquarium for now. There was also a big tree, about six people widths around, that Calamity kept saying was watching us.<br /> <br /> We were getting all set up to \u201cannounce ourselves\u201d by having Calamity shoot one of the lurkers when Lori kinda trumped it. She whispered to De la Roche, who moved off a bit, and then went all scary hot. Like beautiful and terrible and radiant and, just, wow. All the lurkers ran off plus six muck women we hadn\u2019t noticed. Me and Jacob gathered up some of the magic beans Flores wanted, that let whoever ate them control their blood flow by concentrating. There were no cherries, so we moved on to the next pool, which a lurker and four of the muck women ran off. We found more beans, the cherry we needed and a kelp-like thing, that made you see in infrared (and only infrared) for a few hours. Kinda like Predator vision, you know.<br /> <br /> So, there was a lot less stabbing than anticipated. Oleander, the Autumn Court goblin fruit person, didn\u2019t get her lurker blood, but I don\u2019t think it was an emergency need or anything. But we did get out a lot faster than we expected and in a good mood. Calamity was feeling really playful, even without stabbing anything, and threw some swamp muck at Lori, to have something to clean out of her hair, you know. She mimed tossing some at De la Roche too, but I scooped her up and put her on my shoulder. De la Roche wouldn\u2019t take my offer of my other shoulder, cause invisible Insincere Marguerite couldn\u2019t molest her up there but Lori did. So that was pretty awesome.<br /> <br /> We ran into Desiree on the way out. She asked for an escort right off, cause Ginny had been stalking her all night. We got her out safe though, and Calamity promised to talk to Ginny about it. I hope it\u2019s not to try and make Chalcedony like her again or maybe more? I did take the opportunity to remind Calamity that I didn\u2019t find \u201churting people I dislike\u201d particularly romantic, you know? Necessary, sometimes, when they\u2019re, you know, bad guys, but not really romantic. And not like torturing them, ever.<br /> <br /> But in general, things are pretty good, you know? We got the fruit to help Joan, Mary\u2019s doing better - she still craves flesh but not enough to kill for it, and tomorrow we meet with Felicity. She had to go out of town kinda suddenly a few weeks ago when we were going to before, so I was a little worried, but I think she\u2019s ok. We\u2019ll see tomorrow I guess. Also, I haven\u2019t had any nightmares in a while. Most nights me and Calamity stay at the Hedge House so I can sleep in her dreams. It\u2019s taxing in a different kind of way, you know, but glamour\u2019s not really scarce at the Dream House.<br /> <br /> Oh, I almost forgot. Master Darke told Jacob he think the Phantom Tong are behind the attack on Dark Kimberly. They usually leave a calling card, you now, some kind of signature, and Master Darke figures Lucien is part of the Tong, so I dunno how much is reasonable and how much the idea is just a way to discredit Lucien. Still, it\u2019s something tangible to look into, I guess.<br /> <br /> June 10th<br /> <br /> Right after breakfast, Calamity called Ginny and Lori called Andromeda. Andromeda was super excited, you know, and sped the whole way here with Joan. She was really really worried about her. GInny, on the other hand, was not really worried, She promised Calamity she didn\u2019t intend to physically harm Desiree, just scare her, but thought there was nothing wrong with that cause no one in the Spring Court would listen to Desiree, or care that someone was harassing her. That\u2019s just not cool. I mean, scaring people is the Autumn Court\u2019s thing, I get that, but especially saying it like that, this is just Ginny being a bully, maybe cause some girl is running hot and cold on her. I like Ginny. I don\u2019t like thinking of her as a bully.<br /> <br /> Anyway, on happier topics, the cherry worked! Joan was really freaked out when she came back to herself (and really freaky before that. In multiple ways, actually...) Andromeda was so terrified that Joan would be mad at her, and so glad that she was herself again. She sure falls in love fast and hard. I do think Joan reciprocates in kind and intensity, so hopefully it will work out better for the little alien girl this time. I hope they\u2019ll be ok. We do need to find a way so that can\u2019t happen again. Fucking Gentry douchebags.<br /> <br /> We had some time before Felicity was coming by, so we stopped by Flores\u2019 to give her the beans. We told her a little bit about our trip, and she was really worried about the muck women, who are technically called murk wives. So I was close. They weren\u2019t supposed to be though, that close, I mean, to the freehold. They\u2019re pretty dangerous I guess, and try to make more of themselves by drowning people. So we might get Oleander that lurker blood anyway. At least, I gonna try and get the others to go with me to deal with them. Flores also mentioned there was a sarcastic talking owl that had showed up in the nearby Hedge recently. I think me and Calamity had the same idea at the same time. I said we needed to go find it and she said we should ask how many licks to the center of a Tootsie Pop. Somehow that led to De la Roche licking Lori, and when I told Calamity that Insincere Marguerite\u2019s licking habit seemed to be contagious, she licked me! I have a very strange motley.<br /> <br /> We met with Oleander too, at the Lighthouse. We warned her about the murk wives, and gave her the kelp thing we found. The Autumn Court uses it for night work, you know. So it is kinda useful. Oleander let us take handfuls of some squealberries she\u2019d gotten a whole bucketful of. They make your eyes and tongue bulge out, like a Looney Tunes thing, and made you, you know, squeal. We\u2019re all going to eat them next time Ace shows up for breakfast. I can\u2019t wait to see the look on his face.<br /> <br /> Felicity should be here soon. Hopefully things have been ok for her. She hasn\u2019t called or anything, so probably?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> This is probably going to be a pretty short entry. Not because things are busy, or a show is about to start, or I have somewhere else to be or anything like that\u2026 it\u2019s because I\u2019m pissed off. And I\u2019m pissed off at one of the motley. And I hate feeling like this, and I don\u2019t want to dwell on it.<br /> <br /> And why am I so angry? Calamity threw mud in my hair. I know, it sounds so stupid and petty when I just say it like that, but bear with me; there\u2019s context.<br /> <br /> So we were all gung-ho to head into the Hedge to find the goblin fruit which could mystically restore Joan\u2019s virginity (and hopefully turn her back to normal). I\u2019d run down to a local boutique for a few minutes and picked out an outfit which was both sexy and functional\u2026 tight rubber pants which would hose off well if things got messy, topped with a black shirt and leather jacket altered to accommodate my wings. I strapped my Black Widow into a holster across my hips. Some of the others wanted to see me tuck it down my cleavage, and the gun is small enough that I can do that, but it\u2019s pretty uncomfortable. I got a few appreciative ogles as I joined the others in the parlour, and D even smacked my ass once. I gave her a withering look, but I know she meant it in the nicest possible way.<br /> <br /> We entered the Hedge through the local gate and made our way toward the swampy area where the goblin cherries were known to flourish. It wasn\u2019t long before we found the place we were looking for. It was a collection of large murky pools surrounded by trees that looked like cypress and willows and mangroves. Some suspicious looking logs were floating in the ponds, and small alligator-like creatures swam about and climbed onto the muddy banks, mostly ignoring us.<br /> <br /> The others said that the \u201clogs\u201d were actually Bog Lurkers, a kind of Hedge beast I\u2019d never encountered before\u2026 and Calamity swore blind that one of the trees was watching us warily from across the nearest pond. So people started putting up their defenses and getting ready for a big fight. I\u2019ve been thinking of ways I can contribute to combat more, and though I\u2019m not very good with my gun yet, I had come up with another possibility that seemed useful.<br /> <br /> \u201cHang on a sec,\u201d I said to the others, \u201cI want to try something.\u201d Everybody quieted down for a minute as I wrapped the glamour around me. I knew what I was about to do wouldn\u2019t affect my motley-mates\u2026 they\u2019re too intimately connected to me. But D isn\u2019t bound to me by a pledge. \u201cSorry, sweetie,\u201d I said as I gathered my power, \u201cbut could you scootch over thataway about fifty feet? This could get messy.\u201d<br /> <br /> She rolled her eyes, but moved away without complaint. The others looked at me curiously as I steeled myself for the confrontation to come. \u201cI think I\u2019ve got this,\u201d I said warily, \u201cbut, y\u2019know\u2026 be ready to back me up, please.\u201d<br /> <br /> Then I stepped out onto the shore and let my glamour sort of\u2026 explode out of me. I turned my attention to the Bog Lurkers in the pond and let the magic flare up around me. \u201cLeave this place,\u201d I said in what I hoped was an intimidating snarl.<br /> <br /> They did.<br /> <br /> In less time than it takes to describe, the Bog Lurkers fled the pond, quickly followed by half a dozen vaguely female forms which had been submerged beneath the oily surface. The latter creatures seemed to be made mostly of mud and decaying plant matter. We learned later that they were creatures called Murkwives\u2026 or maybe Mirkwives? It\u2019s hard to tell; that swamp was both murky and mirky.<br /> <br /> In any case, we were free to explore the pond in the absence of Hedge-beast threats. A few minutes later, we\u2019d scavenged a handful of goblin fruits, but had not found the mystical cherry-regenerator for which we\u2019d come. We did find a few of the magic beans Flores had been looking for\u2026 beans which would allow one to control the flow of blood in their own body temporarily. There was some discussion of how this might provide an interesting high\u2026 but in the end it seemed sort of futile, as slowing the flow of blood to one\u2019s brain isn\u2019t exactly conducive to the sort of concentration you\u2019d need to employ to use the bean in the first place.<br /> <br /> We moved on to the next pond and repeated the experiment. Once again a handful of Bog Lurkers and Murkwives scampered out of the area at my approach, and we began searching the pond for magical reinhymenators. This time we had more luck; Insincere Marguerite found the fruit we were looking for almost immediately, along with some sort of magical seaweed that lets you see into the infrared spectrum. And wouldn\u2019t you know it, the goblin fruit that gives you back your cherry actually looks like a cherry!<br /> <br /> Oh, did I mention that Marguerite can apparently walk on water now? Well she can, and was looking pretty smug about it as the rest of us slogged through the thigh-deep muck.<br /> <br /> And speaking of muck\u2026 well, here\u2019s the part of the story that I\u2019m not looking forward to reliving. You see, I had let the glamour fade enough for D to rejoin the group, and the two of us were talking about what had happened while the others tried to catch one of the little caiman-critters as a souvenir for Ace. D was saying something about how what I had done was pretty amazing, and I was feeling pretty good about myself, when\u2026 SPLAT!<br /> <br /> A big gob of slimy muck hit me right on the side of the head. It was disgusting. I turned to glare at the rest of the motley, and Calamity had this smirk on her face like she\u2019d done something clever. My good mood deflated like a popped balloon, and I saw red. \u201cWhat the <u>hell</u>?\u201d I shouted at her.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou said you\u2019d let me help you clean the mud out of your hair and wings,\u201d she said lightly, \u201cbut there was no fight, so you stayed pretty clean. I was\u2026 disappointed.\u201d<br /> <br /> I ran my fingers through the slimy tangles of my hair. I wanted to spit with rage. Either that or cry. You know, whatever.<br /> <br /> In any case, I let her know in no uncertain terms that she would not be enjoying my company on that particular evening. I maintained a fairly frosty silence between the two of us all the way home, even when Gawain picked us both up and put us on his shoulders. I was still mad at Calamity, but I wasn\u2019t going to turn down the chance to get my feet out of that disgusting sucking mud, was I? D had declined when Gawain offered her the same courtesy\u2026 mostly so that an invisible Marguerite could continue to subtly molest her, I think. It\u2019s a good thing I\u2019m so secure in our relationship these days. Whatever gets her motor running, I know my girl loves only me.<br /> <br /> We ran into Desiree \u2013 again \u2013 as we neared the exit. She had been hiding out in the Hedge because she was convinced that Ginny was stalking her, hoping to frighten her or worse. We offered to escort her out and see what the deal was. Incidentally, it turns out that she was <u>right</u>; Ginny is terrorizing the poor girl in the hopes that this will impress Chalcedony, for whom she\u2019s still carrying a bit of a torch. The ways of desire are strange and complicated, but I hope things work out for those two in the end.<br /> <br /> What was a little more disturbing was the fact that Ginny honestly seemed to think no one would <u>care</u> that she was threatening Desiree. She said that since everyone was convinced Desiree was a loyalist, no one was going to stop her from doing whatever she wanted to the poor girl. I don\u2019t think that\u2019s true, and I fully intend to speak to the Princess about this at the next opportunity.<br /> <br /> So we got Desiree safely out of the Hedge, dropped off the struggling caiman in Ace\u2019s unused piranha tank, and immediately got cleaned up and called Andromeda. She and Joan showed up much more quickly than the law allows, and we gave Joan the goblin fruit. The results were immediate and startling. Joan is back to her old self now. She doesn\u2019t remember much of what happened while she was all submissive and shit, but she remembers enough to be embarrassed. She\u2019s really grateful that we did what we could to help her\u2026 but I think in a way she\u2019s even <u>more</u> grateful for our discretion, which is kind of odd. Her priorities might be a little off. In any case, she doesn\u2019t blame Andromeda for what happened, and the two of them are still an adorable couple.<br /> <br /> We took the magic beans to Flores, who thought they might be useful for medical emergencies in the Freehold. I briefly considered asking her for a cow or two in trade, but decided against it (even if we did secure a cow of our very own, it would just encourage Ace to start planning his crazy piranha act again). In the end we just donated the beans to the Freehold, hoping to earn a bit of goodwill for the motley.<br /> <br /> Flores was the one who told us what the Mirk-or-murkwives were. She seemed a little disturbed that they had ventured so close to the Freehold, and mentioned in an offhand way that someone would need to run them off or destroy them (I could practically see the excitement on the faces of most of my motley at this pronouncement). She also told us that other people had noticed the sentient tree in the area, but that it was usually content to just watch those who visit its home and let them go about their business unless they disturb it in some way.<br /> <br /> She also mentioned a sarcastic talking owl who has taken up residence in the Hedge nearby. Calamity and Gawain immediately started talking about finding it and asking it how many licks it takes to get to the tootsie-roll center of a tootsie-pop. Of all the things from my childhood that people might still remember, I never expected that commercial to come up! It seems like most people these days have only seen an abbreviated version, though\u2026 Mr. Cow and Mr. Fox are largely forgotten\u2026 and even Mr. Turtle has been cut out of the shorter versions.<br /> <br /> So as not to leave anyone out, we took the infrared seaweed stuff to Oleander. She insisted on offering us a reward from among her stock of\u2026 \u201cinteresting\u201d goblin fruits. In the end we took a bunch of fun little fruits called squealberries. Apparently they\u2019re one-off fruits that cause the ingester\u2019s eyes to pop out of their head temporarily, and make one emit a high-pitched squeak for a second or two. They\u2019re harmless, and pretty much useless except as a practical joke. I think we\u2019re all going to use them the next time Ace shows up for breakfast, just to see what his reaction will be.<br /> <br /> Okay, so I guess I have to talk about why I\u2019m still pissed at Calamity now. I hate feeling like this, especially about someone I usually like so much. Ah, hell, who am I kidding? I still like her\u2026 even love her, though not in a romantic way. That\u2019s not going to change over something as petty as mud in my hair.<br /> <br /> So here\u2019s the skinny: it hurt because it served to minimize and belittle what had happened just before it. For the first time since I had escaped the Hedge\u2026 hell, maybe for the first time in my <u>life</u>, I had done something spectacular that wasn\u2019t based on my looks or my performing talents. For the first time in my life, people were impressed with me not because I was pretty, but because I was <u>strong</u>. It\u2019s not a feeling I\u2019d ever had before, and I just wanted to enjoy it for a little longer. That handful of flung muck served to <u>humiliate</u> me right when I was riding the wave of that success, and that probably made it hurt worse than it should have.<br /> <br /> Will I forgive Calamity? Of course I will. She didn\u2019t mean to spoil my moment; she just thought she was doing something cute and playful. I know she would never intentionally hurt me like that. But it <u>did</u> hurt, and I want her to understand that before things go back to normal between us. Does this make me petty? Maybe. Honestly I don\u2019t really care.<br /> <br /> I think D believes I\u2019m being unreasonable about this. She hasn\u2019t said it outright, but I can tell. And that\u2019s okay, too. It\u2019s nice to know that she can disapprove of the way I act from time to time, but it won\u2019t affect the way she feels about me. Or, hell, maybe I\u2019m just projecting my own feelings on to her, who knows?<br /> <br /> And speaking of D, I can\u2019t wait for Saturday! I think I\u2019ve finally convinced her to come to the masque with me, though she\u2019s putting up a hell of a fight (probably mostly for my benefit; she likes to keep her tough-girl image intact whenever possible). It\u2019s going to be so much fun. I just hope I can find what I need in time\u2026<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> <b><b><u>Tuesday June 10<sup>th</sup></u></b></b><br /> <br /> I am not jealous. I mean, yeah, I have just finished fixing my hair and putting on a bit of subdued makeup but I always girl up for playing hostess during the show. No reason to not go ahead and do so a little early. Certainly not because we're meeting with a beautiful man-eating Day courtier who's already singled my Gawain out to be the one to talk to about getting a meeting with us. I get it, he's not a seasonal courtier and all. And he does have a reputation for being a decent and fair sort (also known as a soft touch) so it makes sense. If I was her I would certainly have picked Gawain as the way into our confidence. And maybe I am being overly suspicious of her motives and intentions. All I honestly know is that her court and Insincere Marguerite's are hostile to each other and what Captain Jack said about her. But I trust Captain Jack and as I told my Darkling sister, her enemies are my enemies. So I am going into this meeting wary. I swear to Zod, if this Felicity bitch tries to sink her claws into my Gawain, I will sink my own into her... several times...<br /> <br /> Damn, I guess I am wound up a little tight still after last night's trip into the hedge. After movie night I checked on Gawain and he was feeling much better. So we all girded our loins and loaded up on containers for holding goblin fruits. I just grabbed some older jeans I didn't mind getting muddy and my bike leathers (which are meant to get dirty after all) and strapped on Sam and Max. Lori had actually gone out to get rubber pants for the occasion. Lori in skin tight rubber pants. Yeah... I offered to to help clean any mud out of her wings and hair after we got back, and she actually didn't brush me off. So I was feeling right pleased at the nights prospects.<br /> <br /> Anyway, we headed out to the swampy area both Oleander and Flores had described as a likely spot to find the rehymenating goblin fruit with which to cure Joan of her unfortunate curse. There was, as expected, a lot of mud. What I hadn't expected was just how fucking adverse to it my motley was going to be. I mean, I don't think people in Snow Globe were as afraid of getting dirty and back there it was punishable by a wire brush scrubbing for openers. Gawain just trudged resolutely but unhappily through despite how much his heavy tread sank in. And Jacob was clearly upset by how noisy we all were (okay, all but Insincere Marguerite, who used a contract to walk over the mud and water like some sort of fucking Tolkien elf, yet was still all aghast at just being near it) And Lori was disgusted by the whole affair but then she's not fond of the Hedge or of getting messy so the two combined had her doubly unhappy.<br /> <br /> We reached our destination without incident and paused to survey the terrain. There was a clump of Will O Wisps off to one side that we unanimously decided to avoid and a massive gnarly tree (I think if we'd all joined hands we could have made a circle around it but just barely) that I swear was watching us. The others seemed skeptical but seriously we were in the fucking Hedge, a ginormious creepy-ass tree with voyeuristic tendencies is par for the mother-loving course. There were also a bunch of little caiman things scurrying about and some Bog Lurkers lying in wait (they have the same pretend to be a log thing that gators do)<br /> <br /> Well, everyone started to summon up magical protections. I called up the glass to wrap and dance across my skin and pulled Max out. I glanced at the others and called for a ready check. And Lori sent De La Rocha back to the edge of the swamp and stepped forward. She had a pleased look and said she had it. Then the next thing I know she's gone all beautiful and terrible and she's ordering the critters to begone and fuck if they are not tripping over themselves to do exactly that. Hell, there were even a bunch of mud women that we hadn't seen fleeing with the rest. I just gaped a bit and shivered... I mean seriously... Lori is fucking sexy no matter what but seeing her like that... I mean, I knew it was still the same Lori I knew but part of my brain was all Holy Fucking Shit that Bad-Ass Angel could Kick My Ass and Holy FUCK would I enjoy it.<br /> <br /> I was so distracted that I hardly noticed and certainly didn't mind that we were gathering the fruits without a fight until Jacob asked me who I was and what I had done with Calamity. I just pointed to Lori and he chuckled. It took us a couple of pools to find the cherry (of course it looks like a cherry) that would make Joan back into the woman she'd been. And once we had what we'd come for, we decided to pack it in. No one wanted to push our luck with those mud women or the tree.<br /> <br /> Well, I guess I was just antsy and more than a little heated and it was sinking in that I wasn't going to have a chance to release any of that in a fight. But I was also just feeling playful you know. So once we'd drawn back and started to regroup to head back I scooped up a little mud and tossed it at Lori. When she shrieked, I grinned and reminded her that she'd told me I could help her clean her hair and wings but that there hadn't been anything to clean out of them so I fixed that. She was sputtering mad and most of the others seemed to think it wasn't funny either. De la Rocha informed me pretty firmly that if I tried that with her there would be a punch and I just grinned and reached down slowly.<br /> <br /> Well, Gawain didn't wait to see if I was serious or not. He picked me up and set me on his shoulder to keep me out of mischief. I may have flashed a bit of a pout for show but I like it too much when he does things like that to be upset. Besides, I was just playing around anyway. He offered to carry D as well but she declined in favor of being within reach of Insincere Marguerite's invisible hands. Lori did accept, but she remained miffed at me on the way back.<br /> <br /> And on the way back we ran across Desiree. She was hiding from Ginny, who had apparently been chasing her and threatening to drown her. She asked us if we'd escort her out of the hedge and we agreed. And once we had, I offered to call Ginny and talk to her about her behavior the next morning.<br /> <br /> Once we'd gotten back, Lori continued to give me the cold shoulder and made it clear I wasn't getting anywhere near her wings or hair or any other part of her. I didn't mean to make her that angry. Sheesh. It was just a little mud. But Gawain interrupted and pointed out that he had a bit of mud on his back he could use help with and I laughed as I marched him up to our shower to clean him head to toe like a good little monster.<br /> <br /> This morning after breakfast I called Ginny while Lori called Andromeda. Ginny not only freely admitted to chasing Desiree, she was downright pleased with herself. I tried to convince her that it wasn't a good idea but honestly the more she talked about chasing a stuck up bitch like Desiree and how she shrieked and panicked and ran... well let us just say when she suggested that I join her I really had to stop myself from agreeing. She did say she'd come to the Dream house tonight, hopefully I can convince her of the risks involved. Now is not the best time to stir up trouble between the Spring and Autumn court. Unfortunately, she's convinced that since everyone thinks Desiree is a loyalist anyway no one will believe her or care. If that were true, it wouldn't be the issue it is, but while Desiree's court may not trust her they're not going to ignore an Autumn courtier terrorizing one of their own. And Lori certainly isn't going to let it slide. We'll see how tonight goes but I may have to bring this to Queen Charlotte and now is not a good time to have to bother her with anything if one can help it.<br /> <br /> Thankfully, our other business went much more smoothly. Andromeda and Joan arrived far quicker than I'd expect the wee gray girl to muster. And from the very brief exposure to Joan under the curse we saw before Andromeda gave her the fruit I can see why. It was... frightening to see how completely submissive Joan had become. But the cherry did its magic quite promptly. Andromeda was so relieved and Joan was clearly disoriented. They stepped aside and Joan was quite shaken to learn what had befallen her. I and the others all assured her that Andromeda had taken great care to keep her condition discreet and that we'd likewise handled it quietly. Joan seemed very relieved by that and while she was pretty obviously still shaken (which given how stoic she usually is says a lot) she thanked us and they both departed fairly quickly. It felt damn good to be able to actually fix something neatly and tidily without any loose ends. I mean, Joan is still under her curse but she knows about it now and when (not if, but fucking when) we find the thrice-damned Table Andromeda will be able to cure her of that permanently.<br /> <br /> And so, feeling rather pleased with ourselves we set out to deliver the goblin fruits to Flores and Oleander. We ended up donating all of the other fruits we'd recovered. None of them were incredibly rare or precious so it seemed like a good way to build up a bit of goodwill and reputation with the Freehold. We also told them both about the mud women we'd encountered and they told us they were called Murk-wives and seemed concerned that they were this close to the freehold. Seems the murk-wives add to their number by drowning people but if they are here they've been drawn or driven or something. Both indicated it was something the Summer court needed to know about and De La Rocha promised to pass the word to her court for us. Flores also told us about a strange sarcastic talking owl that had been seen in the hedge recently and that some suspected might be a spy for the gentry. Gawain and I both decided pretty much in unison that we should find it and ask it how many licks to the center of a tootsie roll pop. And that prompted D to lick her girl. And then Gawain said something about Insincere Marguerite's licking being contagious and I could not resist leaning in and licking him before telling him I had no idea what he was talking about. Yeah, I guess I am just in a mood today.<br /> <br /> But now we're back and getting ready for Felicity's visit. After that we've got a show to do. I'm going to check my makeup in the mirror one last time and head down. I am not jealous. I am not because I trust Gawain. But I also know he doesn't like to see the bad in anyone. That's where I come in. If this she viper is beguiling him I'll just have to carve her up. Holy fuck, my glass is itching for a good excuse to lay someone open but I'm going to hear her out.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Why do I feel like I\u2019m living in a faerie tale? Yesterday we went into the hedge to find the Goblin fruit that would restore Joan to her previous self and found several other things as well. Everyone dressed for the occasion, denim, leather jackets and rubber boots. We all armed ourselves and packed empty water bottles and Tupperware to collect the Goblin fruit in. It was kind of funny to see just about everyone come downstairs with backpacks. Just a few weeks ago they didn\u2019t think to do that, but now they do. Maybe I have been a good influence?<br /> <br /> So, we gear up, prepared for a fight if it comes to that and head on out. The swamp was not pleasant. I mean, there was a certain novelty in trudging through something that wasn\u2019t snow, but the novelty ended there. The mud sucked at almost everyone\u2019s shoes, Gawain worst of all. Insincere Marguerite on the other hand, walked deftly on top of the mud and ooze. I must say, that would be a really helpful skill to have. I\u2019ll have to ask her if it\u2019s possible for me to learn that.<br /> <br /> We arrived at the place that we were directed to in short order and began searching to see if we could find the fruit we were looking for without disturbing the water until we absolutely had to. There were bog lurkers waiting just below the surface of the murky water, watching us. They looked like logs, but they definitely weren\u2019t. I was preparing to fight off the bog lurkers while someone else looked for and gathered the Goblin fruit, but then Lori whispered something to De la Rocha, who stepped back. Lori told the group that she had an idea. She then proceeded to turn on the charm\u2026or something. She does this thing sometimes that makes her even hotter than she normally is. This time she was sexy as all get out, but terrifying at the same time. Holy shit. Yeah, that pretty much covers it. Those of us in the motley were unaffected, but we still stared. \u2018Cause, yeah. Gonna stare at that.<br /> <br /> Not to compare Lorelei to my Queen keeper, but the Lady had a similar ability. She could be absolutely gorgeous, but terrifying to the same degree all at the same time. She would shine like the sun does on freshly fallen snow. Her hair glistening and her skin shining. It was made all the more beautiful because the sun never rose fully in her realm. It was always twilight, so she stood out that much more as a beautiful beacon of light against the dark sky. Lorelei shone like that, but perhaps more beautiful and less terrifying than the Lady. I think the biggest difference is Lori\u2019s smile. It is just as radiant as she is. The Lady\u2019s, not so much.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the bog lurkers and other critters in the immediate area, including the previously hidden \u201cbog women,\u201d all fled as fast as they could. This created the perfect opportunity for Insincere Marguerite to walk on top of the water and look for the Goblin fruit we were looking for. All told we found 12 magic beans, one bit of kelp, and the one thing we were looking for, the cherry. Yeah, the Goblin fruit we were searching for was actually a cherry. Irony aside, we were just happy to have found it for Joan. We had ended up searching a couple of pools to find all of this, but with Lori\u2019s \u201cterrifying presence\u201d up, we had no problems with would be attackers. On the way out we even snagged a caiman for Ace. We saw several of them while looking for the fruit and decided that since we wouldn\u2019t let Ace get the piranha he got a tank for, he could have a caiman. Insincere Margurite turned invisible and grabbed one quick.<br /> <br /> While there some folks, mainly Calamity and Lori, were joking about cleaning mud or anything else out of hair and/or wings when we got back. Calling back to previous banter and practices. Now, Lori never actually got any mud or anything in her hair, so Calamity decided that if she was going to help Lorelei in the shower that she\u2019d have to add the mud herself. So she did. She threw a small handful of mud into Lori\u2019s hair. To say Lori was not pleased is an understatement. Not sure Calamity is going to help her wash her hair either. There was some more good-natured teasing and/or threatening about throwing mud, so Gawain scooped Calamity up onto her shoulder and started walking. After a moment I offered to take his backpack, which had the caiman in it, so he could also carry Lori on his other shoulder. It was kind of cute to watch, though I didn\u2019t get to do too much watching. Most of my attention was spent keeping the caiman in the bag and the bag on my shoulder.<br /> <br /> On the way back, when we got close to the gate, we came across Desiree. She was hiding in the Hedge, trying to keep away from Ginny. Desiree said that she thought Ginny was trying to kill her. Apparently Desiree takes a short cut through the hedge to get between cities and Ginny followed her. The slight girl is convinced that Ginny will kill her just to make Chalcedony happy. There is no love lost between them, and the others were skeptical at first whether or not Ginny would actually kill the girl. I wasn\u2019t sure, but like I said, there\u2019s no love lost, and they have been at each other in the past. I wouldn\u2019t put it past the Autumn courtier to do damage to Desiree. So, being the good Samaritans that we are, we escorted Desiree back to The World.<br /> <br /> When we got back to the house I deposited the caiman in the empty tank and put a lid on it. I added a couple of rocks and some water so it would feel more at home. I\u2019ll let Ace take care of the rest. Wouldn\u2019t want to step on his toes. Here\u2019s hoping he likes the new pet.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> So, the day started out like normal. I made coffee, Gawain made breakfast. There was some discussion about iced coffee, but I told them I\u2019d only do that on request. Coffee should be hot. Anyway, while we were preparing the food Gawain and I discussed the next movie night since we were up. We agreed on a pair of movies that should go well together. Robin Hood: Prince of Thieves and Robin Hood: Men in Tights. Ha. This should be good.<br /> So, that was the fun stuff. After that Lorelei called Andromeda to let her know that we had found the fruit and that she could bring Joan by any time. She was very keen on doing just that, so the conversation was short and the little grey girl set out as quickly as she could with the former warrior woman.<br /> <br /> Calamity called Ginny, while Lori was on the phone, so she could get the other girl\u2019s take on what happened with Desiree. Ginny flat out admitted that she had been intimidating Desiree and said that she did it because she \u201cliked to terrorize stuck up bitches and that no one would care if she got hurt or killed because she was a loyalist.\u201d I went just a bit cold when I heard that. It\u2019s true that most people have a very low opinion of loyalists in this area, especially the Summer and Winter courts. I\u2019m just not sure how they feel about former loyalists. Would they come after me with the same fervor that Ginny goes after Desiree? Would Calamity and Gawain be deterrent enough to keep would be assassins out? Would it even be as covert as all that? I wonder if the courts would just drag me before them and publically execute me? Don\u2019t know if it\u2019d get that far. Master Darke or Lucien Torrez probably already have plans in place for when they come into contact with Loyalists. Those two are more alike than they like to admit. It\u2019s kind of scary actually. I\u2019ll never say it out loud though. Hell no. I just hope that I have time to try and make up for some of my past transgressions before I\u2019m killed.<br /> <br /> Okay\u2026so very shortly after Lori talked to Andromeda, the pair showed up at our door. We got everyone comfortable in the sitting room and gave the cherry to Andromeda to give to Joan. The once stoic woman seemed willing to eat anything the slighter girl gave her. Just a little disconcerting. So, she ate the cherry and a minute later she was shaking her head and asking what was going on. Andromeda all but cheered. Joan didn\u2019t seem to remember what happened over the past couple of days, so Andromeda took her aside to explain. Joan definitely wasn\u2019t happy after learning what had happened, but she seems to understand that it wasn\u2019t Andromeda\u2019s fault. It seems to be some sort of curse that was put on her by her keeper. Shitty curse if you ask me. Have sex, lose your mind. Not a good trade.<br /> <br /> After the couple rejoined the group we assured Joan that the whole matter was kept very discreet and that the only people that knew what had happened were the motley, De la Rocha and Andromeda. I could tell she was extremely relieved to hear that last bit of information. Truth be told I would be too if I were in her shoes. She seems to be okay though, aside from a bit of confusion and I\u2019m guessing some embarrassment. I figured we\u2019d just leave them to talk and figure out what they were going to do next.<br /> <br /> After all that was over the motley talked about what to do with the other hedge fruits that we found. We figured that we didn\u2019t actually need it, so we agreed to call Flores and give the lot of it to her if she should need it. We all went over to meet with her at her place. We told her about what we had found and what we had come across, creature-wise, while we were in the swamp. She said that the \u201cmud women\u201d (as we called them) are actually called \u201cMurk Wives,\u201d and are not usually so close to the freehold. That they are is distressing and she suggested that we contact the Summer court and let them know what we had seen. Apparently these Murk Wives kill those that they come across in order to add to their numbers. Gender doesn\u2019t matter in their game. They just need the bodies, and the muck makes up the rest. Not a pleasant thought. Anyway, we gave the twelve beans that we\u2019d found to Flores and stayed to chat for a bit longer.<br /> <br /> After we left Flores\u2019 place we all headed over to see Oleander to see if she wanted the kelp we found. We told her the same thing about the \u201cMurk Wives,\u201d and she too was surprised that they were so close. She echoed the same concerns that Flores did about their proximity and their proclivity for killing folks to add to their numbers. Still not thrilled about that. Neither it seems was Calamity. I think my Darkling cohort is planning on going back to the swamp to clean out some of those \u201cMurk Wives,\u201d or at least persuade them that coming so close to the Freehold was a bad idea. I think I\u2019ll go with her. Not that I don\u2019t appreciate Lorelei\u2019s excellent use of Terrifying Beauty to scare off the local threats, but it did deny those of us spoiling for a fight, well, our fight. If the others aren\u2019t keen on going maybe Calamity, perhaps Gawain and I can eliminate some threats.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m sure the others would argue that we should just leave the job to the Summer court. It does seem the thing to do but then again\u2026 Sparring with Calamity brought to mind times where I was the victim. I think I\u2019d like to remind myself what it is to be on the other side of that equation. Yeah, that\u2019s perhaps not the healthiest attitude right now, but I\u2019m sick of being the victim. Even in my memories, or at least in my flashbacks. Having a flashback in front of Calamity was a bit unnerving to say the least. She was so understanding while still being firm. I know I can\u2019t afford to show that kind of weakness again, but I can\u2019t help it. I don\u2019t control the flashbacks. I can\u2019t even bring myself out of them. They have to just end on their own, or something from the outside (say, like a knife blade) has to bring me out of it. If I have a flashback when there is a real threat to the motley my inattention could get them hurt, or killed. Damn, I have to find some way to compartmentalize all that shit again.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> Swamps, I\u2019ve decided, are not my thing. They are too dirty, too smelly, too dangerous for I. I am a creature of urban life. Peering out the window, creeping down the stair, that sort of thing. Naturally.<br /> <br /> That said, it was a successful mission. Lorelei used her Fairest powers to ensure it was fairly non-violent\u2026she scared off what monsters were there to menace us. One type, a type of Hob called Mirkwives or Murkwives, have apparently moved into the area and, according to Flores and Oleander, need to be driven out. Oleander, being Autumn, favored a longer term solution including seeing who or what attracted them here in the first place. I think that is wise. Definitly.<br /> <br /> But yes, overall the trip was smooth as it could have been. I suspect Calamity is a bit disappointed she did not get to murder some hobs, but eh. She may get to kill the mud-women later, with or without some scouting or divination first. Wisely.<br /> <br /> The past month or so I have learned a good deal about what Julia is turned on or pleased by. Sex on rooftops. Erotic moments in graveyards\u2026I think the reality of the hardness of markers on ones back meant she now prefers \u201cvery heavy petting\u201d in graveyards. Lilies and nudity, or at least female nudity, for some reason. Nooses. Buildings on a slant so there is not a flat floor. But I also found what she does not like, and that is old-fashioned mushy romance. She dislikes it like I dislike Andy I Over and the Dutch.<br /> <br /> So\u2026while she was, as always, polite, aloof, and most of all very tall, she was less than impressed by reactions to fixing Joan. Make no mistake, she was happy to see Joan herself again, just most of the group was rather moved by it, and I think Julia was a bit annoyed by that. Maybe a bit of the stereotypical eye rolling Goth Girl. Maybe because I find her as an aloof Goth Girl incredibly hot. She also really smells good. Pleasently.<br /> <br /> But Joan was fixed. She would be, I think, horrified by her behavior before being fixed, and I wonder if fighting that is why she is so\u2026picky\u2026about women\u2019s behavior; she throws around words like \u201cstrumpet\u201d or \u201ctrollop\u201d and others I did not know people below the age of sixty used faster than she should, and thought she was just a frigid bitch but maybe there is more to it. Regardless, she was cured and she and Andromeda were quite goo-goo eyed, as they say, with each other, and she even carried Andromeda out. I thought it was sweet. I won\u2019t tell Julia that though. Probably.<br /> <br /> It is odd because De La Rocha is the one you would expect to reject feminine things because they are feminine. I\u2019ve never seen her in a skirt, or not wearing at least one leather item when fully dressed. I\u2019ve only once seen Julia not in a skirt (for practical reasons then) and never without wearing silk while fully dressed. Julia and Lorelei have to be all delicate and ladylike, De La Rocha has to be all tough. Usually.<br /> <br /> And here is Insincere Marguerite, just being herself. And Insincere Marguerite thought Joan was adorable with Andromeda.<br /> <br /> With everything sorted out about the goblin fruits, we are moving on to dealing with this Day Courtier. May as well, I suppose, get it done.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXI</i><br /> <br /> The fruit looking like a cherry was what the group wanted so I ran with it.<br /> <br /> Mainly hedge encounters. No real combat due to Lorelei\u2019s use of Vainglory, but that is okay. I don\u2019t, as a rule, worry too much about how the PCs are \u201csupposed\u201d to deal with an obstacle, so it was all good.<br /> <br /> Dealing with Felicity got further pushed back, but that is okay. They finally met with her this past Sunday\u2019s session.<br /> <br /> Next session we get some more background and move toward the masquerade. See you then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 01-27-2015, 05:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T14:26:53-08:00","id":388922,"title":"","content":"With their hedge tromping done, our heroes settle in to get ready for the big masquerade ball. And meet their neighbor Felicity. Let\u2019s see how it all went.<br /> <i><br /> Session XXII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> While we were waiting on Felicity, Calamity made up with Lori. Kinda. I think. Well, she\u2019s still mad cause Calamity took her moment when she felt strong and impressive and then made her look silly, but she did accept Calamity\u2019s apology and decided to not take her up on the offer to hit her. Or to have De la Roche hit her. Though while it\u2019s fair that De la Roche would probably hit harder, even I know that wasn\u2019t really the time to bring that up, you know? But Lori\u2019s been a little more like her usual self for the last little bit though, so I think that\u2019s ok.<br /> <br /> Oh, and Ace brought the caiman up to the kitchen. Lori wound up running away to get dressed up for the meeting after spending a few minutes perched like an angel on the edge of her chair. Ace thought it was breakfast, so he was there to get Jim (that\u2019s what he named the caiman) an egg. Of course. He wound up pouring a raw egg down its throat and then letting it peruse the fridge. I hope caimans don\u2019t throw up. If Jim does, Ace gets to clean it up. After Felicity left, me and Jacob made a leash/harness thing for it. So he could walk it, you know, and let it have its \u2018three seconds free\u2019 without terrorizing Lori.<br /> <br /> Eventually, Felicity showed up, looking beautiful. Insincere Marguerite had dressed up to match and Calamity too. That was a little weird, cause she spent the entire time curled up in my lap. Insincere Marguerite spent the entire time flirting with Felicity, so that made more sense. I was glad, cause I thought she\u2019d be angry. I mean, she\u2019s planning on trying to recruit her away from the Day Court, so that could be exciting, but she wasn\u2019t mean or anything. She did do the kinda creepy shadow petting thing. She said after that Felicity had a thing for Lori. I guess - I mean, like Calamity said, she has a pulse and her sight, but I dunno what Insincere Marguerite was going on particularly. She did smile at her a lot, but who wouldn\u2019t, you know?<br /> <br /> Anyways, Felicity told us a lot about the history and politics of the Changeling stuff nearby and kinda why they don\u2019t like the non-Seasonal Courts here. It\u2019s mostly about the Day/Night thing, not Dawn/Dusk so much, but I guess we kinda get all lumped together? See, originally there was the Lady by the Sea freehold which was just Malibu. The rest of nearby - Santa Monica, Venice Beach, LA and Hollywood - was all part of the Court of Fallen Stars. Then the Grand Maw showed up and caused all kinds of havoc but was defeated (and possibly captured, which is just a bad plan, you know?) by the Court of Fallen Stars. Then a dragon Gentry came looking for the Grand Maw and killed even more Changelings in LA and Hollywood. So now, the Court of Fallen Stars is crazy and in control of Hollywood. The Court of Fallen Angels, which is Day/Night, took over in LA. And Santa Monica and Venice Beach, since they were mostly ok and therefore still mostly Seasonal, kinda went along with the Lady by the Sea. The problem is that the Court of Fallen Angels still claims Santa Monica and Venice Beach, since they were part of what they took over, back in the day. So the Seasonal Courts here don\u2019t want there to be enough Day/Night Court folks about to, you know, legitimize the claim or anything.<br /> <br /> We also talked about the break ins she mentioned before. She said her alarms had been tripped and her lock scratched up where someone had picked it. Insincere Marguerite was quick to point out that it was obviously not her, cause she wouldn\u2019t be so clumsy. So either whoever did it was bad at subtlety, or they wanted her to know, like say, Lucian wanted her to be intimidated enough to leave. She did point out the house had belonged to a group of loyalists before Joli arranged that she got it as thanks for rooting them out. So just because they didn\u2019t take any of Felicity\u2019s stuff doesn\u2019t mean they weren\u2019t after something in the house.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Princess Joli... maybe what helped Calamity out is that she, Ace and me all kinda pissed Lori off and she couldn\u2019t handle being that mad and it all kinda shut down. See, Felicity mentioned again that, you know, they\u2019d dated in the past and when the masquerade ball and Joli being available came up, she was quick to point out that she had dumped Joli, not the other way around. When she kept talking about crossing a line, and not having changed, I figured it was the soul eating thing. So I kinda, you know, asked her if it was. It was, so I didn\u2019t really fuck up, and I was pretty sure so... But Lori was not particularly pleased anyway.<br /> <br /> As far as helping her, barring any random break ins, our next opportunity to do anything will probably come up Saturday, at the masquerade. Felicity got an invitation, which was weird, cause she doesn\u2019t usually get included in general freehold events. But it was anonymous, which isn\u2019t really Princess Joli\u2019s style, according to her. So maybe it\u2019s someone who wants to make a statement by attacking or denouncing her in public. Or someone who just wanted to make sure she was out of the house for awhile. Or, more happily, someone is trying to play matchmaker for her and Princess Joli. I\u2019ll be working security at the ball, so I\u2019ll be sure to keep an eye out for her. I do think she\u2019ll be safer there than at her house. And if someone breaks in, Insincere Marguerite could use her mirror thing to figure out who it is!<br /> <br /> We still had some time to kill before the show after she left, so I got Insincere Marguerite and Calamity their masks. I\u2019d just gotten done with the finishing touches, well the metalwork finishing touches, before I got sick and they are pretty awesome, if I do say so myself. That did lead to Calamity asking if I wanted to put my stuff in her hair so everyone would know she was mine. I think I blushed hot enough that my faceplate could have just been in the forge. The conversation kinda flowed on before I could figure out how words worked again. I mentioned it later to Joan and Andromeda (who are super adorable and are going to do the Greening too) and that made me realize she did say she was ok with it, even if she did go and phrase it that way. So I made sure to track her down after the show and say yes. I think she was pleased.<br /> <br /> June 11th<br /> <br /> The squealberries trick worked pretty well, though I\u2019m not sure whether Ace was reacting more to us or to the agitated caiman he suddenly had on his hands. Willow Black even joined in - she had picked Insincere Marguerite up last night, so she stayed for breakfast. She really liked the crepes, but said she wasn\u2019t going to be Insincere Marguerite's sex slave for them. When Insincere Marguerite said that they all said that at first, I made my first mistake by trying to play along, saying that wasn\u2019t really fair, since, you know, it was my cooking. Good lord, then they all ganged up on me. Willow kept trying to get me to sleep with Ace, and Calamity suggested Lori and I have sex while she had her dance lessons. Insincere Marguerite just kept Sultan clapping and demanding I sleep with people. I wound up \u201csneaking\u201d away at Jacob\u2019s suggestion. That probably works better for him. I think they all saw me.<br /> <br /> De la Roche came to get me after Willow left and to make sure I was ok. She understood the Ace thing, but wanted to make sure something wasn\u2019t wrong since I was also running away from the super hot girl throwing herself at me with my girlfriend\u2019s approval. I said something about how it was more like my girlfriend was throwing her at me (which is better than some things she throws, you know?) but I guess there was the comment that I shouldn\u2019t sleep with her cause Insincere Marguerite said so, but because Lori did, so... I guess she kinda was? Then there was yesterday, when conversation about Felicity led to Insincere Marguerite explaining that some people don\u2019t like sex, like if they were really gay but only had sex with the ladies, or really straight but only had sex with... whatever. Apparently, she got bored with her own metaphor. Anyway, that somehow led to Lori mentioning she had nothing against boy parts, and hadn\u2019t had anything against boy parts in a while and apparently that was her trying to pick someone up?<br /> <br /> I really don\u2019t understand people sometimes. But, you know, maybe I should go see what Lori is up to this afternoon.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> So Calamity and I hugged it out, and I think things are going to be okay between us now. I don\u2019t know if she really understands why I got so upset at her, but she at least allows that her joke was in poor taste, and was particularly badly timed. She apologized, and even offered to let me hit her in retaliation. I just sort of rolled my eyes at that, as it always seemed like a particularly pointless exercise in revenge to me. Calamity misinterpreted my reaction though, and offered to let D hit her instead. D\u2019s eyes sort of lit up at that, but I declined once again.<br /> <br /> Then Ace walked into the kitchen with his new pet caiman in tow. I attempted to explain to him that the breakfast table was not an appropriate venue for a vicious reptile like \u201cJim,\u201d but Ace was adamant that the little beast had to learn how to behave. It was struggling in his arms as he attempted to force a raw egg down its throat. I discretely shrieked and pulled my legs up into my chair, and settled into a perching position that felt disturbingly natural.<br /> <br /> Once Jim had been safely stowed, we got ready to meet with Felicity. She seemed nice enough, and even Marguerite warmed up to her after a while (I\u2019ll never understand these Court rivalries\u2026 just because someone has a different philosophy from you, it doesn\u2019t make them a bad person). <br /> <br /> After we\u2019d all been introduced, Felicity gave us a lot of political background on the area so that we\u2019d have context for her problems. I don\u2019t claim to understand a lot of what she told us, but apparently our local Freehold \u2013 officially called the Lady by the Sea \u2013 used to just include Malibu, while the Court of Fallen Stars controlled LA, Santa Monica, Venice Beach, and Hollywood. Then a Gentry called the Grand Maw showed up, and all hell broke loose. The Court of Fallen Stars took care of it, but at a tremendous cost. There\u2019s some speculation that the Court didn\u2019t kill the Grand Maw, but rather captured it so that they could learn about the Gentry by studying it.<br /> <br /> Ick.<br /> <br /> In any case, another Gentry (or maybe just a powerful hobgoblin) in the shape of a dragon showed up a few years later looking for the Grand Maw. It tore through the Court of Fallen Stars, and decimated those changelings before they were able to take it down. There were only enough of them to hold Hollywood, so the Court of Fallen Angels (mostly composed of Day and Night courtiers) took over LA. More seasonal courtiers survived in the Lady by the Sea Freehold, so they moved into Santa Monica and Venice Beach from their base in Malibu.<br /> <br /> So Felicity told us that someone had tried to break into her house on more than one occasion recently. There are any number of reasons this might have happened, but here are the most likely ones. First, it could be a Court rivalry thing. Marguerite turned up her nose at the idea that the Night Court was responsible\u2026 she claimed that they would have asked her to break into Felicity\u2019s house if they wanted something from it, and she would not have left any signs of her passage at all. <br /> <br /> It\u2019s possible that someone from the seasonal courts might be trying to spook her. Felicity used to date Princess Jolie \u2013 I\u2019m not jealous, by the way \u2013 and some people saw that as an attempt by the diurnal courts to move into the territory of the Lady by the Sea, which has always been dominated by the seasonal courts. A lot of locals are paranoid that one of the other Freeholds will move in on our territory if given half a chance, and these break-ins could be some sort of obscure scare tactics warning the Day Court to keep the hell out.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s also possible that Felicity isn\u2019t the point of these burglaries at all. Her house was a gift in repayment of some help she gave a few years ago in taking down a group of Loyalists. In large part due to her relationship with Jolie, she was allowed to move into their base of operations after they were defeated. So Felicity thinks that whoever is breaking in to her place might be looking for something the Loyalists left behind. If so, they haven\u2019t found it yet.<br /> <br /> She was invited to the masquerade this weekend, which is\u2026 a little odd, since it\u2019s usually more of a seasonal court thing. She doesn\u2019t know who sent the invitation, though it doesn\u2019t seem likely that Jolie would send the invitation anonymously. Felicity was quick to tell us that she was the one who broke up with Jolie, not the other way around, due to certain aspects of Jolie\u2019s character with which she couldn\u2019t deal.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou mean like how she sucks out people\u2019s souls to extend her own life?\u201d Gawain blurted out.<br /> <br /> I couldn\u2019t believe it. I was livid. That secret was a sacred trust, and I was quick to let him know how I felt about his carelessness. Luckily, that was what Felicity was talking about, so we didn\u2019t actually reveal the secret to anyone who didn\u2019t already know about it.<br /> <br /> In any case, it seems like maybe someone sent the invitation to Felicity so that they would know that she would be away from home at a certain time\u2026 presumably so that they could attempt to break in again. So we\u2019re going to be keeping an eye on her house during the masquerade\u2026 which I hope won\u2019t detract too much from our enjoyment of the masquerade itself. Does that make me shallow?<br /> <br /> Felicity took her leave after that, thanking us for our willingness to help her out with this situation. Oh, and before she left, I asked her two things. First, I wanted to know if she knew anything about the elusive Mr. Grey. She confirmed a lot of what we\u2019ve already heard about him \u2013 that he works for Master Darke, is hard to track down, and had some pretty serious mental issues \u2013 but didn\u2019t have anything truly useful to tell us. I also asked if she knew any good or well-connected agents. What? She lives in a really ritzy neighborhood, and it never hurts to have connections. She gave me a smile and said that she\u2019d be happy to look into it.<br /> <br /> That seemed to irritate Marguerite for some reason. I know she has her eye on Felicity, and for some reason she\u2019s convinced that Felicity has the hots for me (though I didn\u2019t notice anything of the sort). Well, I don\u2019t have any designs on Felicity, so I don\u2019t suppose it\u2019s anything to worry about in any case.<br /> <br /> People started talking about their masks after Felicity left (I picked up a pretty and ornate angel mask the other day, and I\u2019m quite looking forward to wearing it), and that got us talking about the Greening ceremony, which is a sort of public declaration of love and devotion within the Freehold. Calamity and Gawain are doing it\u2026 though I will refrain from mentioning the uncouth way Calamity chose to announce this to the rest of us. We found out later that Joan and Andromeda are also planning to perform the Greening, which is not really a surprise.<br /> <br /> D elbowed me as this talk was going on. \u201cWhat do you say, babe?\u201d she asked with a grin.<br /> <br /> I returned her smile with interest. \u201cIf you\u2019re okay with it, I\u2019d like nothing more,\u201d I said.<br /> <br /> She leaned in for a kiss. \u201cI\u2019m okay with it,\u201d she assured me. \u201cI\u2019m more than okay with it.\u201d So that\u2019s settled.<br /> <br /> The show was a rousing success. Ace convinced me and Ginny to back him up in a comic performance of \u201cManuh Manuh\u201d from The Muppet Show, which was hilarious. For my solo number, I put my own spin on U2\u2019s \u201cI Still Haven\u2019t Found What I\u2019m Looking For.\u201d And I\u2019m still vaguely ticked off that nobody mentioned that band when I asked about popular and influential musicians of the last thirty years a few weeks ago.<br /> <br /> So we tried the squealberries at breakfast this morning, and it worked like a charm. Ace was pretty surprised, but took it in typical Ace fashion. Even Willow Black \u2013 who had spent the evening in Marguerite\u2019s company \u2013 joined in the festivities, which was nice of her. She complimented Gawain\u2019s cooking, and I made the comment that D and I always come back to the Dream House for breakfast even if we spend the evening somewhere else. Willow wrinkled her nose at that. \u201cThey\u2019re good crepes,\u201d she said, \u201cbut I don\u2019t want to be Marguerite\u2019s sex slave for them.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHey, that\u2019s not fair,\u201d said Gawain. \u201cThey\u2019re my crepes!\u201d<br /> <br /> Oh, the poor boy. He should have known better than to open that particular door. It was a free-for-all after that, with the sex talk flying fast and thick. I once again mentioned my willingness to canoodle with our resident uber-hot suit of armor, and he blushed (which is something to see). Somehow, it came around to Willow trying to get Gawain and Ace to sleep together, which didn\u2019t seem to be to their taste. Marguerite kept doing this little two-clap thing and demanding that Gawain have sex with different people (including me), but he didn\u2019t bite. Then she started talking about how some people don\u2019t like sex, and I commented that I just can\u2019t understand that point of view, because orgasms are the best thing ever.<br /> <br /> Marguerite attempted to explain. \u201cSome people are just repressed,\u201d she said archly. \u201cIf a man is gay, but only has sex with women, then he can\u2019t be expected to enjoy it. And if a man is straight, but only has sex with\u2026\u201d she noticed that the metaphor had drifted, and gave it up for a loss. \u201c\u2026whatever.\u201d<br /> <br /> D gave me a look. \u201cWhat about you, babe?\u201d she asked. \u201cYou don\u2019t seem all that interested in boy-parts lately\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I chuckled. \u201cI have nothing against boy-parts,\u201d I said, and then continued wistfully \u201cin fact, I haven\u2019t had anything against any boy-parts in the last few weeks.\u201d Everyone in the room sort of blinked and then started laughing. I gazed longingly at Gawain for a moment before turning away.<br /> <br /> Gawain fled after that, and in our mercy we let him go. Jacob went with him; I think they were planning to make a harness for Ace\u2019s caiman or something. D went out to check on Gawain a few minutes later, but I\u2019m sure he\u2019s alright. He\u2019s easy to pick on, but he\u2019s pretty resilient once you scratch the surface. And who knows, maybe she\u2019ll smack some sense into him!<br /> <br /> Three days \u2018til the big party! I can\u2019t wait!<br /> <b><br /> Lorelei Grace</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <b><u><br /> Wednesday June 11th</u></b><br /> <br /> It's all fun and games till somebody gets stabbed in the heart. Fuck, I should be focusing. I'm supposed to be getting ready for my dance lesson. And after that I've got a meeting with Queen Charlotte about the clandestine negotiations at the masquerade ball and Ginny. I do not have time for this gorram self indulgent insecure bullshit. Somehow I doubt taking the time to write this down is going to help but who the fuck knows. It can't hurt. <br /> <br /> Alright, so yesterday before Felicity showed up I took a moment to approach Lorelei. She'd been keeping me at length all day while we were meeting with Flores and Oleander. So I asked her what was wrong. She informed me that she was still upset about my mudslinging in the Hedge Monday night. I was shocked and I had to try to wrap my brain around that. Unfortunately, my damn mouth just rattled right on. I think I actually stammered something about there not being a rock in there or anything like I was some sort of fucking simple minded child. And Lori pointed out that there were other ways to hurt someone and explained that she'd felt strong for the first time since escaping or maybe ever. I hadn't thought of that, I mean Lori's not a fighter but she's amazing in so many other ways. I did manage to get something more coherent out there. I told her that it would take a hell of a lot more than a little mud to make her any less impressive. I don't think it helped. I fell back on an apology from there but it felt pretty lame and she didn't seem moved by it. Though she did tell me she'd accept it and that she'd be fine but she needed some time.<br /> <br /> Well, suffice it to say that when Felicity did appear in all her fucking glamorous beauty I was not feeling stellar. It's most likely for the best that I'd already gotten girly or Zeus only knows what I might have decided to wear to that meeting. Not that I think I could have outdone Insincere Marguerite. When she said she was thinking of trying to seduce the woman away from the Day court she was not kidding. She was fucking dressed to the nines. (Or perhaps I should say undressed to the nines... fuck that was an outfit...) For my part, I introduced myself to our guest and then proceeded to plant myself in Gawain's lap. Hell, I don't think I could have more fucking blatant about it unless I'd planted a flag or pee'd on him. Way to show your confidence and trust in the man you love there Calamity. <br /> <br /> The actual meeting went fairly well I think. Felicity did have some interesting history about the area that none of us were familiar with. So, back in the day, Hollywood's Court of Fallen Stars controlled all of LA and Santa Monica. But after the Grand Maw and the Dragon both swept through (the former to devour as many Changelings as she could to regain her strength to return and resume devouring gentry and the former to draw her out and defeat her in battle) their strength was vastly reduced. In addition, the rumor is that the Grand Maw wasn't killed but was instead captured. (Tommy has told me as much and he's generally a reliable source) To curtail some disappearances among their numbers (rumored to be Changelings taken to feed the captive Grand maw) Chinatown broke free and set up a directional court. LA's diurnal courts stepped up then and allied themselves with Chinatown to form the Court of Fallen Angels. The catch is that the Santa Monica area had seasonal courtiers from the former Hollywood court who rather than answering to the new court switched to the seasonal courts in Malibu. So, our courts claim on half of their territory is basically squatter's rights which is why the Summer court is so hostile to any non seasonal courtiers. It was certainly an interesting bit of information to be sure.<br /> <br /> And she also hinted that Insincere Marguerite's downfall in LA might not have been quite as simple as she thought. She is apparently not the first rapidly rising star to have a sudden and abrupt downfall. That was news to my fellow Darkling.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, she elaborated on the issue she's been having with her home. Seems she did inherit the mansion as something of a gift from Jolie (who she was in a relationship with previously) and Austin (during his reign as Spring Prince) after she helped to ferret out a cell of loyalists who were using it as a headquarters. Recently, there have been break ins, clumsy enough to leave visible damage on the locks and set off burglar alarms. Nothing has been taken. It seems likely that it is either the Summer court (or Lucien Torrez) trying to drive her away or someone seeking something left behind (or thought to be left) from when the home was a base for Loyalists. Hmm... I know she's done some searching for anything magical but I wonder if she's checked for gateways or anything in the local hedge? Wish I had thought of that at the time, shall have to ask about it at some point.<br /> <br /> The last item was an anonymous invitation to the masquerade ball. She's been pretty much out of the social loop since she broke up with Jolie (over her need to devour souls). She doesn't believe it came from Jolie since she would have told her she was inviting her. So the question is is it someone trying to get her away from the house? An attempt to draw her into a high profile social situation to make some sort of political or social move against her? Someone trying to get her and Jolie back together? Someone trying to throw Jolie off her game at the ball by having her ex that dumped her over her curse (that she's borderline suicidal over) present while she's trying to move past breaking up with Charlotte?<br /> <br /> Lots of questions, few answers. If nothing else, for bringing us up to speed on the history we agreed to ask a few questions. We can look into things with our courts that she can't after all. I'm going to contact Gunnar and see if he can confirm if it's Lucien or not. He might also know a bit more about the loyalists that were driven out, maybe a hint about what they might have left that someone's after if it's not his boss doing it.<br /> <br /> Once Felicity was on her way (and I suppose lower on the list of people I need to stab, at least for now.) Gawain brought out the masks he'd forged for Insincere Marguerite and myself. I had been thinking about a copy of Frank's rabbit mask anyway and so when the ball came up it just seemed like a natural choice. Insincere Marguerite had him make her a lion half mask. Interesting, considering what I know about her past but I didn't say anything to her about it. I was a bit distracted with something else.<br /> <br /> There has been some talk about the Greening happening at the ball. It's a tradition where couples mark each other by putting ivy in their partner's hair to show their love and commitment (and off the marketness since this party is often a free pass to fool around without consequence). The kind of thing Katt would have ab-so-fucking-lutely adored. And I had no doubt that whether or not he was going to ask, Gawain would want to do it. So I took the occasion to let him know he could put his stuff in my hair in front of everyone so they'd know I was his if he wanted to. I do believe it took him about five minutes to remember how to form words... He is so adorable when he's like that. I'm not sure everyone else appreciated my wry wit though.<br /> <br /> After that, I at least managed to get through the show without chewing on any more shoe leather (which is good since those damn tiny little heels cost more than pair of decent boots. And even if Lori did buy them for me I wouldn't want to have to replace them.) TJ, one of the Summer courts top goons, was there but he was well mannered enough and told me he'd just come to check out the boobs. I'm pretty sure he found them to his liking so we may be seeing more of him. Joan and Andromeda were there, being completely lovey dovey. Monica and her hanger on were there. (Yeah, I know... I said I was going to deal with my issues with Hailey. I'll get around to it... eventually.) Ginny was there and I spoke to her about Desiree. She did at least seem to grasp that tormenting Desiree might lead to trouble but rather than a reason to stop she explained how she intended to conceal her identity in the future. As much as I hate to dampen such adorable blood lust (and despite how fucking contagious her eager mood is) I tried to dissuade her from hunting but I didn't really make any headway. You know, things would be SO much fucking simpler if I'd just gutted that woman like a trout in the hedge when we the Extras were holding back. But the right thing is always the fucking inconvenient thing it seems.<br /> <br /> On a more cloak and dagger note, Willow Black of the Night Court was there and asked to speak with me in private. Once we were alone, she explained that the Warlock of Night was going to be at the Masquerade but wasn't going to announce it until the last minute so as to keep the Day Court's king from having a chance to attend. And while she's there she and Queen Charlotte are intending to have a secret meeting to seal an agreement to cooperate in mutual defense and aid in dealing with common enemies. It seems like a good arrangement for my court and it seems that Insincere Marguerite and myself will be among the small group hammering it out. I mentioned my intention to work security and how this would likely be helpful in getting this meeting pulled off discreetly. Once I get them all together, I shall let Charlotte and Spidertoes do the talking. Negotiation isn't my strong suit after all. Willow spoke a little about her court and I have to say, the more of them I meet the more I find I do like them. Not going to jump ship on my own court but there is a certain appeal to their philosophy. Also, when I do stray into LA to hunt my fetch down it won't hurt to have some local allies.<br /> <br /> Moon and Dionisia where also present for the show and bantering playfully. After the show I spoke to Dionisia and set up my meeting with Queen Charlotte. She suggested that a good time would be in a few months but I insisted that I needed to speak to her sooner so she told me that if I came in the evening she'd get me in to see the monarch. You know, as much as everyone is focused on helping Jolie with her problem and her search for a new consort, no one seems to fucking care that Charlotte's destructive appetites aren't something she wants either or that she just lost the woman she loved as well. Don't get me wrong, I do feel for Jolie but the woman does not have a fucking monopoly on emotional pain. Of course, I'm not sure what the fuck I can do for my Queen. I mean, I won't lie and say I don't think about how it would feel to have Charlotte throw me up against a wall and pin me while she feasted but the reality is I like being alive too much to not fight back. And as much as the thought of being in Charlotte's web gets me squirmy I cannot be hers and truthfully I don't want to be. I'm Gawain's monster and I'd make a pretty fucking lousy consort. I'll just have to see how she looks when I have my audience, but I am worried that she's hurting way more than she's trying to let on and I hope it doesn't interfere with the meeting Saturday. I wonder if a chat with Tommy might be in order...<br /> <br /> After I'd set up the meeting Gawain approached me and broke me right out of my troubled thoughts. He was all tongue tied and nervous. And he pointed out that while it was certainly not in a couth manner I had kinda said we could do the Greening and if I was really serious about it he would like that and.. and that was pretty much as far as I let him go since I could see just how unsure he was feeling and I couldn't bear to let him keep on like that. I silenced him with a kiss and told him that yes, I had meant it and yes I would like nothing more than to show everyone that I'm his. Then he swept me up and carried me off to our bed.<br /> <br /> He loves me so much. I don't understand why or how someone as bright as him can love something as twisted and dark as me but I cannot deny that he does. He shows it so often in so many ways. He's amazing and he deserves so much better than me. I try to give him what I know he needs and it makes me so glad to see him happy... But underneath... I still want things... dark hungers that he can't satisfy. I do love him. It feels so good to be with him. I am so fucking lucky to be loved by someone like him... so why can't I just be fucking happy?<br /> <br /> Willow Black joined us at breakfast. Apparently she'd stayed last night with Insincere Marguerite. She was quite delightfully brazen and at one point made a comment about Gawain\u2019s cooking being good though not good enough to become Insincere Marguerite's sex slave over. Well, Gawain made some noise about it being his crepes and oh did that start things. Pairings were promptly declared and thrown about. Gawain tried to keep up but gave up to just start blushing brighter and brighter as things spiraled. And especially when Lori started to flirt with him. I pointed out that I had my dancing lesson and Lori needed to be distracted from the presence of her nemesis. And as things continued, he and Jacob tried to slip away but we called a few final chuckles after him.<br /> <br /> He came back in after it had died down a bit and I did take a minute to make sure I hadn't missed him being anything but a bit flustered. Once I was sure he was okay, I left to get ready. And now I am, but I'm almost afraid to go down and wait for Annika to arrive. I know I told him to take Lori up on her flirting but he always watches my lessons. It's fucking stupid but I want him to pick me instead of her. Right... Who would ever choose my ragged glass-ridden ass if they had a shot at Lori's perfect body? Hell, I wouldn't fucking pick me over her why should I expect him to, especially when I fucking told him to go for it? But I do want him to. Because I love him and love makes you fucking stupid. <br /> <br /> <b><br /> Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Well, today was not a very eventful day, which is not to say it was bad. Uneventful days are good too. I will admit that I like a little bit of excitement every now and again. Exploring the local hedge, following tracks in said hedge, looking for rare goblin fruit. I don\u2019t like it if/when the others get hurt, but I do enjoy the adventure. It must come from working for the Lady for so long. I had a great deal of adventure while doing tasks for her. Lots of tracking and retrieving, and inevitably fights. <br /> <br /> I guess it was some kind of adrenaline rush to always be on the go, moving between the Lady\u2019s realm and the world. Being an envoy to other Gentry on the Lady\u2019s behalf. Okay, mostly it was Desire that was the envoy for the Lady. I was Desire\u2019s bodyguard. Damn that woman could talk a hungry dog out of his bone. Like Lorelei, she could do that \u201choly shit beautiful\u201d thing, but Desire always had a bit of \u201csinister\u201d thrown in to that look too. Porcelain skin, hair the color of ebony, cherry red lips\u2026she was gorgeous. Though I suppose I should say that she is gorgeous. As far as I know she is alive and well, and still works for the Lady.<br /> <br /> So, yeah I\u2019m used to a bit of adventure. I\u2019m about as ready for a fight as the next person, which is Calamity, and we all know her proclivity for fights. I just don\u2019t like my friends getting hurt. If we could take that part out it\u2019d be all good.<br /> <br /> So, today was interesting but not exciting. To start off the day Gawain and I were working in the workroom. He was forging a mask and I was making one out of leather. Not the Briar wolf pelts. Still hanging onto those. I used some of the nicer practice leather we got to make a mask for myself for the masquerade ball that\u2019s coming up. I think it came out pretty good. It\u2019s black with some subtle designs on it. It covers about half of my face. I was thinking of asking Gawain if I could borrow the tux (minus the top hat) and wear that to the ball. I figured the mask I made would go good with that outfit. I could even slick my hair back. People will probably still know it\u2019s me, non-spikey hair or not, but that\u2019s not really the point.<br /> <br /> After we were done with that we got cleaned up and went to meet up with everyone else. Felicity was coming over to talk. Insincere Marguerite and Calamity dressed up really nice for the meeting. Calamity seemed to want to show off, and to make sure that it was known that Gawain was hers and she was his. Big time. She sat in his lap for pretty much the whole conversation. <br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite on the other hand was turning the charm way up and coming onto Felicity in a big way. Even her shadow was interested. The conversation continued despite all the hormones. Felicity shared some information with us on the history of the area. Apparently this whole area used to be under the control of the Court of the Fallen Stars. Or Malibu was under the Lady by the Sea, and the rest under the Court of the Fallen Stars. Not sure which. Anyway, at some point they came under the attack of a banished Gentry called the Grand Maw (maybe Grandma)? She sounded like Baba Yaga to me. Anyway, this Gentry shows up and literally starts eating Changelings. Apparently she used to eat other Gentry to gain power when she lived in Arcadia. They didn\u2019t like that so they kicked her out. Then she turned her sights on California.<br /> <br /> The Court of Fallen Stars killed, or possibly captured the Grand Maw. She wasn\u2019t seen after that in any case. Then, a short while later, another Gentry that resembled a dragon came to town looking for Grand Maw. There was mass destruction and a lot of lives lost. A good bit of the seasonal courtiers were killed off. This explains why the Day/Night courts hold so much sway in Los Angeles. I think technically we fall under their purview, but the seasonal courts are definitely in power here, so the Day and Night courts don\u2019t have nearly as much power as they do elsewhere. <br /> <br /> I\u2019ll admit to being a bit curious and more than a bit worried if the Court of Fallen Stars has the Grand Maw held as a prisoner. There are so many ways that can go badly. The afore-mentioned mass killing is just one thing. The Gentry have so many powers that we couldn\u2019t hope to have. Granted, they\u2019re not as strong here as they are in Arcadia, but it\u2019s still a bad idea. I would love to be the idealist and say that the Gentry is dead and that the courts would not do something so dangerous as to keep a pet Keeper, but I\u2019m not. I\u2019m so not an idealist. I\u2019m a realist, and I know that people in power can be stupid. Most of them in fact. And, that is another thing I will not say out loud anywhere near Darke or Torrez. Yeah, that\u2019d be a good way to die.<br /> <br /> So\u2026after the history lesson Felicity told us that she has had several break-ins at her house. Now, she has a really nice house, in a really nice neighborhood. Gated and everything. Thing is, nothing has ever been stolen. It\u2019s just been entered in such a way that you know that someone had been there. Now, either someone is trying to scare her, or they are looking for something and haven\u2019t found it yet. Apparently the house itself used to be the residence of a group of Loyalists that were active in the area. Felicity was instrumental in helping kill them all and was given the house as a kind of \u201cThank you\u201d from Princess Jolie. This may have been when they were dating.<br /> <br /> The gist of all this is that Felicity is asking if there was something she could do for us if we can help her figure out who is breaking in and why. Ideally stopping it. She does not have a lot of people that she can call on for help. Apparently she split up with Jolie because of the monarch\u2019s cravings, and they are not on the best of terms still. So, the Spring court is kind of out for her. Then there\u2019s the fact that she\u2019s in the Day court, which puts the rest of the Seasonal courts out as well. She reached out to Gawain because of his reputation as a decent and helpful guy. I think she was hoping he would help, and maybe that we would go along with him.<br /> <br /> Now, I\u2019m not a fan of terrorizing people. Not anymore anyway. So, I figured I\u2019d at least go along with Gawain if he wanted to help her. The others seemed willing to lend a hand as well, so we were pretty well agreed on that. To add to the whole situation, Felicity received an invitation to go to the Masquerade ball. It was sent anonymously and Felicity wasn\u2019t sure who would have sent it or why. The idea that it was Jolie was there, but Felicity figured the monarch would just sign her name. The Day courtier doesn\u2019t have a lot of friends in town either. The idea was then bounced around that someone may be trying to get her out of the house. Or get her somewhere definite if they had other plans. The first option is plausible. The previous break-in\u2019s both back up the idea that someone wants to get in the house, but also refutes it since they\u2019ve obviously not set something like this up before to get in.<br /> <br /> While she was here we also asked her about Mr. Grey. She said that last she heard he was working out of Santa Monica. He was, and probably still is, one of Master Darke\u2019s men. Apparently he is a very quiet and meticulous man bordering on OCD. This makes me think that we may not find him if he doesn\u2019t want to be found. That kind of person, if properly motivated, could probably disappear quite easily with some planning and forethought.<br /> <br /> After Felicity left Gawain and I went to the workshop to make a leash for the caiman. Ace has decided to name it \u201cJim,\u201d and bring it with him to the breakfast table. Lorelei was less than pleased and ended up perching on her chair. Then we watched as Ace tried to feed it a raw egg and let it look in the fridge for further dining options. Very strange group I\u2019ve fallen in with. Just saying. Anyway, Gawain and I agreed that a harness would be the best option for Jim, so he couldn\u2019t wiggle out of it and run free through the house. Sometimes I wonder at the sanity of the rest of us for even thinking about grabbing a caiman as a pet for Ace, not to mention a caiman as a pet at all. I guess we are all a bit closer to barmy than the average people, so we have our eccentric moments.<br /> <br /> I think that something was going on at the show tonight. Willow Black came into talk to Calamity, privately. Then Insincere Marguerite was gone, meeting with someone is my guess. Not that both of those lovely ladies don\u2019t disappear from time to time, but Calamity is usually good about always keeping an eye out during the shows, and Marguerite left Julia behind rather than take her with her. So, I think something was going on. I\u2019ll admit to curiosity, but won\u2019t poke my head in if it\u2019s not wanted. Maybe some hint will get dropped. Willow Black did stay after the show tonight, to spend some time with Insincere Marguerite.<br /> <br /> <br /> **** **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Okay\u2026I had to escape the kitchen. It was cute, but it kept going. We started off the breakfast with the Squealberry trick. Worked like a charm, and Ace took it with his regular aplomb. Then there was some comment made that got taken the wrong way and after that it was all about sex and who should sleep with who. I\u2019ll admit that I wasn\u2019t the most comfortable with the subject. Compared to the rest of the motley I have been the least sexually active of the bunch. Not that I don\u2019t like sex mind you, but I guess I\u2019m just not as constantly horny as the rest. Sometimes I feel like a prude. Ha. Anyway, Gawain was turning a darker shade of red the longer the conversation went on, so I leaned over and offered to help him escape the kitchen and go outside. He agreed and we made our way out. I made it out undetected. Gawain did not. He then stopped trying to sneak and just met me outside. A little while later, when he figured it had died down he went back in. I decided that some time alone was not a bad thing, hence writing in this book. I guess we\u2019ll see what else today holds.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> Well that was\u2026bracing.<br /> <br /> There are, I suppose, worse things than finding oneself pressed against the wall by an intriguing woman. I do prefer to be treated a bit more like a lady, however.<br /> <br /> Ace was giddy to find his Caiman. Being British he had of course not seen the like. He named it Jim as British people are terrible at names. At least he did not name him Lord Chestycoat Dunwoffle Pendragon the III or Dr. Sir Lord Hugh Cuthburt Smithers the Less Floppy. I doubt I could have taken that. Obviously.<br /> <br /> The meeting with Felicity went well. She is an attractive woman, a trait the Day Court highly values. She certainly came in with a well-rehearsed script. I was familiar with some of what she said, but that the Courts in LA claim Santa Monica and Venice Beach [strike]I me[/strike] I was actually unaware of. She seemed to want our help. Evidently.<br /> <br /> Felicity is living in a house taken from Loyalists. Someone, either Loyalists to find something or Summer Court to harass her, has been breaking in. I lean toward Summer Court. She stopped short of accusing the Night Court. I can\u2019t imagine them sending someone this far up to break into her house. And if they wanted something there, they know how to find I.<br /> <br /> She did suggest someone in the Night Court could have set me up. She is just trying to make [strike]I[/strike] me doubt.<br /> <br /> Felicity is a Treasured, and reminds me a little of my Dearest. Had she been spotted in Arcadia I would have put her in my sack and kept her. I want her badly. She can leverage that against me if I am not careful. I found myself wanting to give her what she wants, and while I doubt she was using any magic I have no doubt she was deliberately trying to ingratiate herself to me. She also looked at Lori. I felt jealousy. Sadly.<br /> <br /> I suspect Julia sensed some of that. She is usually\u2026sanguine\u2026about me talking about women, even if I suspect she preferred I didn\u2019t, but she does not like Felicity. She did not even meet Felicity, but made noises about something happening to her\u2026for I of course. I\u2019ll have to decide what to do. I will not give Felicity power over [strike]I[/strike] me.<br /> <br /> I will master her.<br /> <br /> That night Willow Black, the Owl Lady, came by to meet with Calamity and I. The Warlock of Night is coming to the Masque, and wants to meet with Queen Charlotte about an Alliance. Calamity and I will be involved in it. Calamity, Charlotte, and Spidertoes will meet with Willow, The Warlock and I. I would feel left out about not having a W name, but my name is perfect. Does the Warlock have a name, I wonder?<br /> <br /> When Calamity left, I found myself pressed against the wall by Willow, who kissed me. She said something about owls eating grubs, and told me she heard very intriguing things about me and wanted to see if they were true. I assured her they were, but only happened to people who treated me like a lady. I also wrapped my tongue around her neck, so she backed off a little. Wisely.<br /> <br /> We did end up going to bed. I will have to thank Lorelei; I had a pretty good idea of how to handle wings with Willow, even if they were more of the under-arm variety than Lorelei\u2019s. Willow was nonetheless rather impressed. By the end of the night I had regained control of the situation. Julia actually rather liked her. I suspect she is into women with feathers. And large breasts. Definitely.<br /> <br /> That reminds me, I need so speak to De La Rocha. She seems to be handling being involved with women somewhat poorly emotionally. I am worried about Lorelei here primarily, I am not sure how much it played into DLR\u2019s breakup with Spidertoes, but her discomfort is apparent. That said, that she is strongly attracted to women is not in question, just her being able to emotionally handle that. De La Rocha has been handling it in her usual tough manner, and seems to be trying to be defiant about it, much as she is with the sun. And to be fair, her riot grrl demeanor is part of why I enjoy spending time with her without clothes on. But I think on some level she may not be handling this well, especially as, well, her relationships are only getting more intense.<br /> <br /> Breakfast went okay. Willow was all but strutting around. She is odd. I have a mask now for the ball. I just need to decide what to wear. Gawain is not sneaky, and I need to work on I\u2019s sultan clap. Apparently.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXII</i><br /> <br /> Felicity gave us some background on the political situation in the area. A lot of that was in the handout that I posted, but she did clarify some of the more political elements that I had not earlier gone into.<br /> <br /> Past that heavy roleplaying, not a lot of plot. The \u201cgreening question\u201d was a big one for the couples, with 2/3 going for it. Tonight\u2019s session will likely be similar as we build up to the masquerade.<br /> <br /> Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T02:05:24-08:00","id":407510,"title":"","content":"Our heroes are preparing for the ball, when a problem presents itself. The end result may not be what they hoped for.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> Well, that wasn\u2019t really how I pictured the afternoon going. I mean, parts of it were. It turns out Lori was at least a little serious about having sex, you know, with me. That was as amazing as I pictured it, if not even more. I was a little worried about hurting her wings at first, but that wasn\u2019t a worry at all after too long - they mostly just kinda balanced things differently. Not that Lori isn\u2019t super graceful regardless. It\u2019s an awesome thing about having sex with dancers.<br /> <br /> But then... she was good-naturedly complaining about not being able to smoke inside and I was running my hand across her feathers and watching how the light hit them differently when Insincere Marguerite and Jacob knocked once and came in, looking super concerned. Turns out Desiree was there and was upset, you know, cause she lost time, which is really bad. I started pulling on my shirt as soon as they said Desiree was in trouble and took the stairs down two at a time to get to the side room they\u2019d got her a seat in.<br /> <br /> She burst into tears as soon as I got there and all but curled into a ball under my arm when I sat down beside her. In between sobs, she told me again what Insincere Marguerite and Jacob had filled me in on quickly. She\u2019d been about to send an email this morning to her agent but when she started typing, she didn\u2019t remember what about and when she tried, she realized she didn\u2019t remember anything since dinner last night.<br /> <br /> I asked Insincere Marguerite to go check her mirrors (after I asked Desiree if it was ok) but she didn\u2019t find anything weird, apparently. Julia and Lori both called their Courts as soon as they heard. The Autumn Court didn\u2019t know of anything weird that happened. The Spring Court didn\u2019t know of anything weird, but when Lori asked Dark Kimberly if she knew where Desiree had been last night, she said Desiree had been on a date with Princess Jolie! I asked Desiree about that, and she said she\u2019d turned her down, cause people had implied it\u2019d be bad for her, what with the loyalist suspicions, you know?<br /> <br /> Lori left to go talk with the Princess and came back with Becky. I was... not happy. There was no need to keep her in custody, or take her there chained either. I did manage to avoid going for my sword (which wasn\u2019t on my back anyway) at least long enough to hear her out. Becky promised the binds would come off once they arrived and that no harm would come to her, unless she tried to hurt someone else. She wasn\u2019t going to be held indefinitely either, just until some people \u2018checked her out\u2019 and she got a tracking device put beneath her skin. I still don\u2019t like it but Calamity and Lori both took up Becky\u2019s side and Desiree\u2026 well, she didn\u2019t object. I offered to go with her, and stay until she felt safe or even got to go, but she shook her head. I think she kinda, you know, gave up. She looked so hopeless - she\u2019d come to someone she trusted and I\u2019d gotten her basically arrested for something she\u2019s not even sure she\u2019s innocent of. When I called Becky later, she hadn\u2019t gotten any better. Becky said Desiree\u2019d be on suicide watch if it wasn\u2019t for how afraid she was of getting hurt.<br /> <br /> Anyways, poor Flores came over right after Becky left and we were all kinda down. She\u2019s one of the planners for the masquerade and was helping out us new folks by offering a crash course in dancing. She also made a Pledge with us to help out with the whole socializing thing. It was a fun time, dancing and flirting with Flores - she is very pretty and smells just like the flowers she\u2019s named after. I was a little distracted though, trying to figure out some way to help Desiree. I did hit upon the idea of oneiromancy - I can maybe tell if mind/emotion altering powers were used on her - and that made me feel a little better. Becky said she\u2019d let the Princess know this evening, and they\u2019d decide.<br /> <br /> Calamity went off to visit Queen Charlotte after her dance lessons with Annika. She was a little upset when she got home. She said it was cause Gunnar and Tommy were paranoid, but wouldn\u2019t say what about. She did get Queen Charlotte to keep Ginny busy so she\u2019d leave Desiree alone and figured out it wasn\u2019t the Summer Court who were breaking into Felicity\u2019s place. It made sense once somebody said it - the Seasonal Courts liked the status quo where Felicity (who used to be the consort of the Lord of the Day in LA) stayed at home and chilled. These break-ins mean she\u2019s making contacts and stuff, which is not what they want at all. Which means coming to the masquerade might be dangerous, cause, especially with the Princess Jolie dating thing, that\u2019s, you know, making contacts in a big way.<br /> <br /> She had some other secrety devious thing to talk about with Insincere Marguerite and she warned us about a pair of Night courtiers in town after they consulted. Insincere Marguerite wasn\u2019t sure about their intentions and then, when Insincere Marguerite and Lori went off for \u2018dancing lessons\u2019 with Flores. Calamity started muttering about wanting to read minds. So I told her about my new Contract, where I can tell what motivates people - you know, so I can inspire them better. She stood up on her tiptoes and kissed me, hard. I told her about the rest of the Clauses, but I\u2019m not sure she was even listening after the second, just pulling me upstairs. Apparently, my timing is awesome, even if it\u2019s not nearly as awesome as my girlfriend.<br /> <br /> <br /> June 12th<br /> <br /> Sex breakfast. That\u2019s what it is now. Sex breakfast. Flores is adorable, but if anyone else comes over looking for crepes with a side order of orgy, we might have words. I mean, not that an orgy with the particular breakfast table would be a hardship or something. But it didn\u2019t help that she mostly wanted to see me and Jacob make out.<br /> <br /> We did manage to have a conversation that wasn\u2019t just me being ordered/told to have sex with people. For instance, we talked about Courtly crepes. Crepes made with love (but not that kind), crepes of wrath (they punch you in the mouth and then kick your ass), crepe fear (made with ghosts?), crepes of good hope (made by me!)... I don\u2019t think we came up with a good crepe pun for sorrow. Or disgust either.<br /> <br /> We also talked about the Princess Jolie matchmaking thing going on at the masquerade ball. I think we generally agreed that maybe getting her and Queen Charlotte back together would be good, with the whole suicidal thing being kinda worked out? Calamity said Queen Charlotte was definitely still in love. We did get a little side tracked, cause Julia really doesn\u2019t like Felicity. Like, full on hate. I guess cause of the way Insincere Marguerite treats her? That\u2019s the kinda thing my new Contract would tell me, I think. I should remember that.<br /> <br /> Anyways, De la Roche distracted Julia a little and then we really got sidetracked by Captain Jack stopping by, asking if he\u2019d missed sex breakfast. He announced himself with a text: \u201cINSUFFICIENT MISCHIEF - WE MUST MEET ANON. Captain Jack\u201d He wanted to work together to plan some kind of shenanigans for the masquerade. We pretty much settled on him obviously fakely stuffing Calamity into a closet and coming out dressed like her, complete with fake glass shards. One of them would bend or something while we danced (cause clearly I\u2019d notice nothing different until then) and I\u2019d flick one off into Lori\u2019s cleavage. It should be tons of fun.<br /> <br /> Calamity did do the \u2018my stuff in her hair\u2019 things again when I asked about timing to do with the Greening, which had Captain Jack stage whispering to me that she was one to hold onto. I sure hope to. It\u2019s not just my amnesia that makes it hard to imagine life without her. I love her, and I would even if she did decide to go naked to the ball so that Captain Jack would have to wear a rubber lady suit. All that talk had gotten the girls, especially Julia, all in a tizzy about getting new dresses for the occasion though, so I think she\u2019ll be in a gown.<br /> <br /> I checked into some things and I think I can get a decent dress tunic for myself. Not really a toga, to properly match my mask, but it\u2019s not a costume thing anyway. But court dress is way more comfortable than modern formal wear and works with the mask I think. I\u2019m holding off until I know what color Calamity\u2019s getting for her dress though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Okay, so a couple of hours after I wrote my last entry, things took a turn for the interesting\u2026 and shortly thereafter, another turn for the terrible. Annika was over for her weekly dance lesson with Calamity, so I was making myself scarce in my room (which is easier than pretending I like her). I was a little surprised when Gawain knocked on my door, and I confess that at first I thought some new crisis had come up.<br /> <br /> Imagine my surprise when he started shyly pursuing our flirtation from breakfast! It was sweet and adorable, and I found myself accepting his invitation and pulling him into my bedroom. What followed was a very pleasant hour or two before everything turned to shit. Gawain started out as a very gentle lover. I guess he\u2019s used to being careful with girls due to his unusual physique; he\u2019s so chivalrous that the thought he might hurt his lovers with his sheer weight and size must be a constant concern. I soon convinced him that I\u2019m stronger and more durable than I look, though, and things got a bit more \u201cvigorous\u201d after that.<br /> <br /> So I was basking in the afterglow, sweating and stretching and purring and bitching just a little bit about how we can\u2019t smoke in the house (since it\u2019s a public building in which we serve food in the state of California) when there was another knock at the door. I jumped up and answered it while Gawain covered himself with a sheet (I lost my modesty about such things a long time ago). It was Insincere Marguerite and Jacob, and of course this time it <u>was</u> something dire.<br /> <br /> It turns out that Desiree showed up while Gawain and I were frolicking, and she was looking for Gawain. She was distraught, and with good reason. She says she was at her computer sending a computer-mail to her agent this morning when she suddenly realized that she couldn\u2019t remember what the mail was supposed to be about. Thinking about it some more, she realized that she couldn\u2019t remember <u>anything</u> that had happened to her since the previous evening\u2026 a gap of about fourteen hours.<br /> <br /> Obviously, considering the speculation about her \u201cManchurian Candidate\u201d status, this worried us a lot. I called Dark Kimberly up pretty much immediately and asked her if anything weird had happened last night, and she responded in the negative. I took a deep breath and then asked if she knew where Desiree was last night (Kimberly\u2019s close to the Princess, and tends to know a lot about the activities of Spring Courtiers). She seemed puzzled, but told me that of course she knew where Desiree had been\u2026 she went out with Jolie last night!<br /> <br /> I felt like I had no choice but to head over to Glamour Springs to meet with Princess Jolie. She <u>had</u> to know what was going on with Desiree, and I thought maybe it would give me a chance to check and see if anything had been, y\u2019know, <u>done</u> to her last night (in a bad way).<br /> <br /> I drove over to Glamour Springs and walked right up to the desk. I intended to ask Dark Kimberly if I could speak with Jolie immediately, but before I could even approach, Becky Wan strode up to me with a very unfriendly look on her face. \u201cDark Kimberly tells me that you\u2019ve been asking\u2026 interesting questions,\u201d she said in a stern voice.<br /> <br /> \u201cI need to speak with the Princess,\u201d I said.<br /> <br /> Her eyes narrowed.<br /> <br /> I sighed. \u201cLook, you can come in with me if you want. In fact, you probably <u>should</u>. You need to hear this too. But I need to talk to Jolie <u>now</u>.\u201d<br /> <br /> Becky looked me up and down and then nodded curtly. The two of us knocked on Jolie\u2019s office door and entered at her invitation. She smiled brightly at us and gestured toward a couple of comfy chairs. \u201cWhat can I do for you ladies?\u201d she asked. She looked happier than I\u2019ve seen her in weeks.<br /> <br /> I closed my eyes for a moment before starting. \u201cI hear you went out with Desiree last night,\u201d I said hesitantly.<br /> <br /> The Princess blinked. \u201cYes,\u201d she said after a moment. \u201cIt\u2019s\u2026 not exactly a secret, but I didn\u2019t think people were talking already.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHow did things go?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> That shy, secret smile tugged at the corners of her mouth again. \u201cIt went pretty well,\u201d she admitted. After a moment, with a twinkle in her eye, she continued. \u201cIt went <u>very</u> well, actually. She\u2026 came back to my place after dinner. And despite what the other Courts say about me, that really doesn\u2019t happen very often.\u201d<br /> <br /> She must have seen something in my expression then, because her smile started to slip. \u201cWhat\u2019s wrong?\u201d she asked. \u201cDid something happen to Desiree? Is she okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019s\u2026 not hurt,\u201d I began. \u201cShe came to the Dream House a little while ago. She was upset because\u2026\u201d I took a deep breath, weighing my motley\u2019s friendship with Desiree against the Princess\u2019 safety and the security of the Freehold, but in the end I knew I had to do what was right. \u201c\u2026because she\u2019s missing time from last night. She doesn\u2019t remember anything between about six o\u2019clock yesterday evening and about eight o\u2019clock this morning.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jolie\u2019s good mood evaporated like water on a hot griddle. \u201cShe\u2026 doesn\u2019t remember last night?\u201d she asked in a hopeless, helpless voice. \u201cBut\u2026 she called me up and asked me if I wanted to join her for dinner later last night. She\u2019d turned me down last week because she didn\u2019t want to give her detractors anything else to bitch about, but she said she changed her mind\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I hated the dead tone that crept into her voice, and I wanted to comfort her. I reached out to touch her shoulder\u2026 only to find that Becky\u2019s hand was already there. When she caught me looking, she carefully composed her expression once again, but for a split-second, I could see how much it hurt her to see the Princess in that state. Girl\u2019s got it bad. And, well, who am I to judge? I think all of us in the Spring Court love Jolie at least a little bit.<br /> <br /> We had to discuss what to do next. Jolie was adamant that Desiree not be harmed, and I came down on her side of things as far as that went. But Becky raised several good points\u2026 namely that we can\u2019t be sure Desiree isn\u2019t being manipulated by the Director in an attempt to destabilize the Freehold\u2026 and harming or compromising Jolie would be an excellent way to do that. We have to keep her under watch until we know more.<br /> <br /> I agreed to take Becky back to the Dream House to collect Desiree, though it burned me up inside to do so. Desiree had demonstrated a ridiculous amount of trust in the motley \u2013 in Gawain in particular \u2013 and I didn\u2019t want to repay that trust with betrayal. But Becky assured me that Desiree would not be harmed, and as long as she came along voluntarily she\u2019d be treated well. The Court just wants to watch her and see if they can figure out what exactly is going on with her. I believe \u2013 I <u>really</u> want to believe \u2013 that they\u2019re going to try their best to <u>help</u> her.<br /> <br /> When I got back to the Dream House, I could tell I was going to be in the doghouse with at least some of the motley for a while. Gawain wasn\u2019t happy that I had brought Becky into the situation. How can an empty suit of armor manage to look so betrayed? After the wonderful time we\u2019d had together earlier, that hurt look left me feeling lower than dog shit.<br /> <br /> Desiree herself was fine with the precautions. She wasn\u2019t particularly happy about having her hands bound, but Becky assured us that it was a temporary measure to keep her still while Becky was driving and less able to defend herself, and that the ties would come off as soon as they reached a safe place. They\u2019re going to keep Desiree under observation for a few days to try to figure out what\u2019s going on with her memory loss, and if they can\u2019t determine what caused it, they\u2019re going to put a tracking device under her skin.<br /> <br /> Oh, yeah, I feel like such a <u>hero</u> right now. Desiree trusted us, and now she\u2019s being treated like a dangerous animal. I\u2026 deep down, I still think I did the right thing. I can\u2019t let anything hurt Jolie. Just because I\u2019m not in love with her doesn\u2019t mean I don\u2019t care about her welfare. She\u2019s my Princess, and my friend. And I really do hope that Desiree will come out of this experience in an improved position. If we can figure out what\u2019s really going on with her and put a stop to it, it\u2019ll put those nasty rumors about her to rest once and for all.<br /> <br /> Flores came over after Becky and Desiree left to offer lessons in formal dancing to the motley\u2026 you know, in preparation for the masquerade. I think she was a little nonplussed to find us all so glum, but most of the others decided to take her up on her offer. Calamity had to finish her lesson with Annika before she could join the group, and I decided I didn\u2019t need the lessons, so I went up to my room to cry for a while and mope about what a terrible friend I am. I wanted D more than anything (she always makes things seem better), but she was still at work.<br /> <br /> I came back downstairs a few hours later to find that Flores was still about, but the dancing lessons were pretty much over. Calamity had left after her lesson to speak with Queen Charlotte. She didn\u2019t share much of what was discussed at that meeting, but did tell us that a pair of Night Courtiers were in town, and that they should be treated with caution. Insincere Marguerite seemed to know who she was talking about, and promptly seconded the suggestion.<br /> <br /> The show went well despite my less than enthusiastic attitude. I sang Aretha Franklin\u2019s \u201cRespect,\u201d and I think I managed to get enough sass and pizazz into it to win the audience over. That was my only solo last night, though I danced in a few ensemble numbers. Then I allowed myself to be led upstairs by D, and promptly collapsed into her arms and sobbed about what a terrible traitorous bitch I\u2019ve become. I told her about Desiree, and she soothed me and offered up a remarkably insightful opinion.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not really upset about turning Desiree over to Becky. Logically, it was the right call. I\u2019m upset because this betrayal of her trust reminds me of the friends I left behind in Arcadia. This is more about Missy, Jane, and the Empress than it is about current events. God, I still remember the look in their eyes when the Empress opened the door of the cage for me. Jane was silently pleading for me to get the hell out of there while I still could, but Missy\u2026 she was looking at the door with something like terror. It was like she had to struggle even to <u>want</u> to be free anymore.<br /> <br /> That dead look in Desiree\u2019s eyes\u2026 like all the drive and energy had just drained out of her. It made me think of Annabelle. Yeah, I\u2019m pretty sure that was her name. \u201cI hurt myself today,\u201d she sang in a voice that could tear your soul to shreds, \u201cto see if I still feel.\u201d Whenever I try to remember what she looked like, the details seem to swim away from my mind. Sometimes when I think about her she\u2019s a blonde like me, with dazzling pure white wings. Sometimes she\u2019s a redhead with dark red wings. Sometimes she\u2019s pale and thin almost to the point of emaciation, and sometimes she\u2019s plump and ruddy\u2026 but her voice never changes. It was the most beautiful, sorrowful voice I\u2019ve ever heard.<br /> <br /> Anyway, D held me until I fell asleep, and I woke up this morning in her arms, and things seemed to be a little better.<br /> <br /> We went down to breakfast \u2013 or \u201csexfast,\u201d as some of the motley are now dubbing it, thanks to the randy talk we always engage in \u2013 to find that Flores had stayed the night. It wasn\u2019t really a surprise; she\u2019s been spending a fair amount of time with Julia and Insincere Marguerite lately. She gently teased D about coming out of the closet, which upset my honey to a degree I wasn\u2019t really expecting. Most of the motley didn\u2019t seem to notice on account of how Julia was practically hissing and spitting about Felicity. She <u>really</u> doesn\u2019t like that girl. And I mean that in the strongest possible way. My own dislike of Annika is probably less intense than Julia\u2019s antipathy for the Day Courtier.<br /> <br /> D quietly made her excuses and started for the door. I said I\u2019d walk her out, and pulled her into a side-room out of earshot of the others. \u201cWhat\u2019s wrong?\u201d I asked, more than a little worried about her.<br /> <br /> She smiled unconvincingly. \u201cIt\u2019s nothing, babe,\u201d she said with a swagger.<br /> <br /> \u201cD,\u201d I said seriously, \u201cgive me a little credit. If something\u2019s bothering you, I want to know about it. I want to help.\u201d<br /> <br /> She sighed. \u201cIt\u2019s stupid,\u201d she began, \u201cbut what Flores said about me really bothered me. I\u2019ve always been the tough girl, you know? And that had people making certain assumptions about me wherever I went. \u2018Oh, de la Rocha lifts weights, likes punk music, and has an attitude\u2026 she must be a lesbian.\u2019 I wasn\u2019t insulted by the assumption, but the stereotypes bothered me. And now that I\u2019m with you\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I raised an eyebrow. \u201cYes?\u201d I asked archly.<br /> <br /> She pulled me close and kissed me. \u201cI love you, Lori. I\u2019m not going to let my issues come between us, I promise. But when Flores joked about me \u2018finally coming out of the closet,\u2019 it just felt like I was validating all of those stereotypes. Like all those assholes were right about me all along, and I was just too stupid to see it.\u201d<br /> <br /> I hugged her tightly. \u201cLook, D,\u201d I began, \u201cI don\u2019t know if this\u2019ll help or not, but\u2026 I don\u2019t really think of myself as gay, or straight, or even bi. I just\u2026 like sex.\u201d<br /> <br /> She grinned, even though her eyes still had sort of a misty sheen. \u201cI\u2019d noticed,\u201d she said.<br /> <br /> I rolled my eyes. \u201cMy point is that when I started to notice my feelings for you, I didn\u2019t get hung up on what that meant about my sexuality. I just wanted to be with you. So don\u2019t get hung up on whether you\u2019re gay or bisexual or whatever.\u201d I leaned in to whisper in her ear. \u201cYou\u2019re Maria de la Rocha, the same person you were before I met you, and you\u2019re the woman I love.\u201d<br /> <br /> She kissed me, and it lasted longer than either of us expected. When we\u2019d separated, she was a little flushed. \u201cI really need to get to work,\u201d she said breathlessly. \u201cThanks, Lori. I\u2019ll think about what you said. I can\u2019t promise I\u2019ll get over this immediately, but I <u>swear</u> I won\u2019t let it come between us, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded and smiled.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, but I did want to tell you that you were wrong about one thing,\u201d she said, and for a second I could have sworn I heard a tremble in her voice. \u201cI\u2019m <u>not</u> the same person I was before I met you. I\u2026 I gotta go. See you tonight.\u201d And then she was gone.<br /> <br /> I wandered back into the kitchen just in time to witness Captain Jack\u2019s arrival. And yes, his entrances are always \u201cwitnessed\u201d for some reason\u2026 they\u2019re too big and bombastic to merely be observed, noted, or marked. Jack wants to do something with Gawain at the Masquerade this weekend\u2026 nothing too disruptive, but something memorable and exciting. They started tossing around ideas, and came up with something that should fit the bill. I\u2019ll have a minor part to play in it, if all goes according to plan, but I\u2019ll leave the details for a later entry.<br /> <br /> I will note that the Captain \u2013 huh\u2026 does that make Gawain Tennille? \u2013 was very careful about setting up the timing of his little prank. He doesn\u2019t want to disrupt any important proceedings, and doesn\u2019t want to spring his joke in the middle of anyone\u2019s Greening or anything like that. Sometimes I forget how considerate he is underneath all of that bluster.<br /> <br /> We also talked over a few possible acts for the Dream House in the coming weeks. My earlier thoughts about The Captain and Tennille almost led me to suggest that the two of them perform \u201cLove Will Keep Us Together,\u201d but in the end I thought better of it. Gawain\u2019s had enough teasing along those lines lately, and who knows if Captain Jack even knows how to play a keyboard?<br /> <br /> My suggestion was to have Captain Jack interrupt a \u201cserious\u201d number with a female singer at some point. He would be dressed in full mustache-twirling villain regalia, and would \u201ckidnap\u201d the performer right there on the stage. This would prompt Gawain to quick-change into a Dudley Do-Right Mountie uniform to thwart his evil plan. This would soon turn into a rendition of The Coasters song \u201cAlong Came Jones.\u201d Captain Jack seemed to like the idea, so I\u2019m confident we\u2019ll end up going with it at some point. Ideally, I\u2019d like to have Calamity in the role of ing\u00e9nue, but I\u2019m not sure if she\u2019s ready for the spotlight yet. It\u2019ll be up to her.<br /> <br /> Julia dragged Calamity, Marguerite and me off shopping while the boys were fine-tuning their ideas. We decided that we all needed new dresses for the masquerade. Hedge-spun garments are all well and good, but even a magical dress gets old if you wear it to <u>every</u> formal occasion. My friends all picked out suitably slinky, sexy gowns. I purchased a virginal white dress with a plunging neckline and no back (naturally) that should go well with my angel mask.<br /> <br /> Then Julia bought lingerie for all of us (including D, after getting some measurements from me). It\u2019s lovely and sexy and comfortable, but\u2026 sometimes I wonder about that girl. Still, I think it was kindly meant, so I thanked her and accepted her generous gift with good grace.<br /> <br /> Now, I should really go and practice on the piano a bit before the cast shows up for play rehearsal. Midsummer is right around the corner!<br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei Grace</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 02-16-2015, 05:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T02:06:35-08:00","id":407513,"title":"","content":"<b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> <b><u><b><u>Thursday June 12<sup>th</sup></u></b></u></b><br /> <br /> Why can't anything ever be as fucking straightforward as it seems? What I wouldn't give for a fucking problem with a damn face I can punch it in until it doesn't have one anymore. Fuck, I am wound up tighter than a hummingbird's ass right now. I have got to find some way to let some of this out before Saturday. Gods below, I can't remember the last time I had a proper knock down drag out fight. Maybe I should go looking for trouble after tonight's show, find me some knuckle-dragging doushe-waffle that deserves to get carved up like a Thanksgiving turkey. Oh fuck that sounds so tempting. But I have no doubt there is going to be something more pressing. And it'd be my luck that I'd wind up having to deal with the fucking cops and I do not need that shit on my spinning plate right now.<br /> <br /> I want a gorram drink but if I start I might not fucking stop and I don't have time for that shit right now. Fuck. Why the fucking hell is it my job to keep this shit together? Okay, that's not fair. Tommy and Gunnar are both in the same damn boat and they're both as stressed about the shit going on as I am. But if they don't know what the fuck is going on how the ever living hell am I supposed to?<br /> <br /> Tommy's right, this shit will drive you fucking crazy until you start murdering random people in the street. At least Charlotte promised she'd have me put down quickly when... no, IF. If it comes to that. It'd make it a little easier on Gawain. Personally, since I only get to die once I'd prefer it to be so fucking epic even Michel Bay shakes his head and says it's overkill. But if (IF not when) I lose my shit that badly it'll be hard enough on Gawain without a blockbuster-worthy death scene. Heh, at least Lori will be there to comfort him...<br /> <br /> Okay, that was fucking uncalled for. Dammit why is THAT bothering me so much? Sheesh, I fucked her first and I'd do it again in a gorram heartbeat if she offered. I know how fucking amazing she is and I should be happy he got to enjoy that. Hell, I fucking told him to go for it. And the way she and De La Rocha carry on it's not like she's looking for anything more than a little fun. I know he loves me. I don't understand why but I know he does. Fuck. Fuck. Fuck. Between this and the way I was acting around Felicity... What the fucking hell is wrong with me? I love him but I still want to fuck the ever-living shit out of Scarlet and Natalia. (Oh Zod I want to do <i>such</i> bad things to those two pretty little morsels it hurts.) So why am I being so... so fucking jealous? Hell knows I have no right to be. I want him to be happy and fucking sure as hell makes a body happy. Dammit, I do not have time for this fucking naval gazing bullshit. There are real problems to deal with. I need to woman the hell up and focus.<br /> <br /> Like the fact the Desiree lost time. She showed up yesterday looking for Gawain while I was having dance time with Annika. And it just so happened that during the missing time she called Princess Jolie back and changed her mind about not going out with her and then proceeded to seduce the Spring Princess and twitterpate her completely. By the time I came into the situation, Jacob had escorted Insincere Marguerite over and discovered that apparently Desiree had stopped in the middle of making dinner and just left everything out and half finished. But it was apparently her and not some duplicate on the date. Becky came and took her to Glamour Springs to keep her safe until the situation can be sorted out. Gawain has volunteered to go and see if he can help via Oneiromancy. (At least <i>that</i> hasn't triggered any irrational jealousy in his monster.)<br /> <br /> So I got brought up to speed on that whole train wreck when Becky showed up to take the girl away and right on her heels Flores showed up offering dance lessons. Seems she's part of the planning for the first time and she's nervous about everything going just right. Poor poor thing. At this point I couldn't bow out if I wanted to. But Becky is in charge of security so I suppose I shall try not to be too much of a bitch to anyone. (Summer's not that far away, surely <i>they</i> have parties where light stabbing is okay...) And Annika did give me some pointers on waltzing so I should be able to make handsome look good on the dance floor.<br /> <br /> I left Flores to work with Gawain and Jacob (they need it most) and headed to my appointment with Queen Charlotte. Moon was clearly not overly pleased with the role of Royal Secretary and I guess I shouldn't blame hir. But still, I didn't completely mask my scowl at hir tone when zee told me Charlotte was at least not so moody that she was causing thunderstorms around the lighthouse. I get that it's got to wear on everyone close to her while she's like this but for fuck's sake the woman is in fucking pain. I mean, if I lost Gawain I am pretty damn sure there would be a fucking ocean of blood spilled.<br /> <br /> Once I got in to see her... Damn, it just hurts to see her like that. But she's strong and she's soldering through. I don't obey her because she wears the crown, I follow the crown because she wears it and I told her as much. We both spoke a bit more freely than usual. She is heartbroken but she is still the Autumn Queen and the crown doesn't let up just because she's in pain. She asked me for my thoughts on the alliance with the Night Court and shared her advisors' thoughts. Dionisia isn't in favor of it because it would make it easy to cast us as villains using tale crafting. (I really do need to learn more about how that shit works, and not just because it would involve being in close proximity to Dionisia...) Tommy had to consider it but seems to feel (as I do) that the pros outweigh the cons as long as we're careful about just what we commit to. And Spidertoes... this is the part that bothers me a bit. Madam Spidertoes proposed this alliance without asking or telling Queen Charlotte of her intentions to. As much of a stickler for protocol and propriety as she is, that is very peculiar. And she's apparently threatened Gunnar (more than usual) that if she will kill him quite painfully if he does anything to derail this alliance. It does not sit entirely well with me. And taken with the Warlock's handmaidens it does make me more leery of this arrangement than I was before.<br /> <br /> Tommy did enter into the discussions and brought his brutal honesty with him. I know he means well, but as Charlotte said, that didn't mean she wanted to hear it right then. But she remained calm (mostly) despite his tactless and direct manner, which is honestly good to see since she's going to be negotiating with the Warlock of Night in two days. Justified or not, if her head isn't in the game she needs to step down at least temporarily (something she freely admitted and told me she'd spoken to her council about). The whole subject of Desiree was clearly tough on her since she's still in love with Jolie, but we were all in agreement that it seemed much too clumsy. The Director is far more well organized. Tommy is sure (so sure he bet MY pinky finger on it) that it's a setup and someone wants to get rid of Desiree. That's not exactly a short list of suspects unfortunately.<br /> And that led to talking about Ginny. I felt like I was ratting her out, but she's made no real effort to keep this a secret. Honestly, if she keeps this up (especially now) and something happens... The Spring Court isn't exactly keen on some of the aspects of Charlotte and Jolie's relationship (no matter how consensual it was) and while they might not be fond of Desiree, she is still one of their own. I suggested that perhaps keeping my favorite river hag busy with some court business so she doesn't have the free time to stalk Desiree might be the best solution. I hadn't realized before that Queen Charlotte is more than a little fond of the ogress herself. The way Tommy laughed when Charlotte considered tasking her with security at the masquerade made me want to throw something at him but Charlotte had that covered.<br /> <br /> So, needless to say, I was not in the highest of spirits as I left. I was on my way out and reaching for my phone to call Gunnar and check on whether or not any of what was going on with Felicity was he and Lucien when I got waylaid. (though not quite as laid as I'd have liked...) Scarlet and Natalia are the handmaidens of the Warlock of Night. They are delightfully shameless and sexy as fucking hell. They wanted to ask me a few innocent questions (there is NOTHING innocent about this pair. Nothing.) In the spirit of cooperation I decided to sit and chat with them for a while. (Also because I was curious to see just how blatantly sexual their shadows were going to get with my own. Fuck, I have never been jealous of my own gorram shadow before but DAMN...) They did not honestly ask anything beyond completely general questions about how things went in the area and what to expect at the ball but fuck if they weren't pouring on the seduction and charm. And they are such amazingly delicious little sweetlings... Perfect little succubi that did everything (and promised to do so much more) in such seamless unison. Fuck, I would almost expect the other to bleed if I cut one of them. (And there IS only one way to find out for sure...) Yeah, they just sat and talked but their shadows... Scarlet's was massaging mine's neck while Natalia's was rubbing my shadow's feet and sucking on its toes... Fuck it was hard to concentrate and make sure I wasn't saying anything I shouldn't like how much I would love to see the perfect bruises that their perfect skin would bloom into or hear their sweet sweet cries... Or how perfectly sweet their blood would taste on my razors... Or, you know, any court secrets. Fuck, just writing about them has me squirmy and wet again. Now I need a cold shower to go with that drink...<br /> <br /> Once they left (shadows linked arm around each others waist of course) I resumed my plans to call Gunnar. He was NOT a happy camper. He does not trust the Night Court in the least and he does not think this alliance is a good idea. He does not like the twins skulking about sweet-talking everyone. He told me straight up to avoid them and that if he could it would be an order (silly man, like that would stop me...) I assured him I hadn't spilled any secrets and pointed out that the game had certainly been fun to play. He was not amused. He was less amused when I pointed out that fucking wasn't what I'd be doing if I lost control anyway. Enough so that he asked me quite earnestly not to start a diplomatic incident by killing them because then he'd have to deal with me and he did not want to have to kill me. It was sweet, I didn't know he was so fond of me.<br /> <br /> As far as Felicity, he thanked me for checking to make sure we weren't interfering. But he assured me they hadn't been doing this. Seems Jolie isn't Felicity's first monarch and so despite her exile, they can't touch her without starting an incident (dammit, who CAN a girl stab in this fucking city?) and were actually quite content for her to be over there minding her own damn business. So the last thing they want is someone hassling her and making her seek allies and get involved. And then there is this mystery invitation that throws her back into the middle of everything. He's deeply suspicious of her and warned me about getting involved with her. And when he warned me to be wary of her 'letting' Insincere Marguerite seduce her so as to get her claws in her I had to admit that it was pretty much exactly what my darkling sister had been doing.<br /> <br /> So when I got home, I was horny as fuck and full of doubts about the Night Court that I hadn't had before and unable to stop seeing Charlotte's broken-heartedness and feeling for the stress both Tommy and Gunnar were under. Gawain and Insincere Marguerite cornered me. Gawain set to working my tense neck with those strong hands while Insincere Marguerite got in close to question me. I told them a bit and then gave my fellow darkling the whisper that I'd met Scarlet and Natalia. She drug me aside promptly and we spoke. She found the fact that Spidertoes had set this into motion a bit suspect as well and she seemed concerned about the twins. She suggested that they were a distraction, acting so blatantly like spies to distract from whomever was actually ferreting out secrets. She also warned me to be careful of them but admitted that they were every bit as spectacular in bed as they advertised.<br /> <br /> When we returned to the others, she told them to be wary of her fellow courtiers as well. I leaned into Gawain and bemoaned the lack of mind reading. I mean, so many maybe's and what if's and unclear motives. What if the handmaidens are just having some fun getting to know (and fuck vigorously) their new allies? (Hey, I can dream dammit!) And that's when Gawain started to tell me about the Contract he'd learned through his court. Holy fucking shit, it is EXACTLY what we fucking need to help untangle this shit web of intrigue. It was only about half an hour till the doors opened so I didn't bother with full sentences, I just kissed him hard and took him upstairs and had my way with him. It didn't really douse the inferno in my loins but it did take the edge off and Gawain certainly seemed to enjoy my attentions.<br /> <br /> The show went well. It wasn't one of our big nights and there seemed to be a slightly off vibe running through the whole motley but everything went smoothly and the crowd seemed happy. I think the events of the day had taken a toll on everyone because we all retried pretty directly afterward. Thankfully the Spring Court wasn't ready for Gawain to do his dream work so I was able to pick things back up where I'd left off before. Maybe I was feeling a little insecure about him being with Lori or a little guilty about how hungry I was for those handmaidens but I threw myself into showing him how good I could be for him with gusto. He didn't stop me but once I'd worn us both out he just... he gathered me close and he held me. No one else can do that without making me remember the Whispering Voices. After every punishment They would gather me broken and bloody into Their arms. Their touch was cool and soft and light but Their strength was there. They would pet my hurts and brush away my tears and stroke my hair. They would whisper how much They didn't like having to hurt me... how much They wished I could be good... how no one would ever love such a naughty girl....<br /> <br /> But They were wrong. Gawain does love me. I am a monster, a vile, twisted, horrible little thing that delights in hurting people and breaking things and he knows it. He knows and he loves me anyway. I cannot understand how or why but he does. And I fucking need that so much it scares me.<br /> Gawain held me and I slept in his arms. I've told him I won't... can't do that with anyone else and I think it makes him happy to know he can give me that. I wonder if he thinks he can fix me? It is a nice little fantasy, isn't it? We made our way downstairs and Gawain started working on breakfast. He likes taking care of everyone. I really hope he does manage to help Desiree with the dream waking. It would mean a lot to him.<br /> <br /> Flores was there, not too surprisingly she'd stayed to spend the night with Insincere Marguerite and Julia. The banter was, as always, fast and heavily changed. I swear, there is more heat at our breakfast table than an old fashioned Hollywood roast. And this morning's victim was De La Rocha. She's hung up on being in love with another woman and Flores made some comments that bothered her. Of course, Flores didn't notice. It wasn't malign, she's an elemental and they just don't get it sometimes. And Lori followed her out when she left for work. I have no doubt she managed to say what the girl needed to hear. She's sympathetic and kind-hearted like that. Maybe that's why I keep being worried about her being with Gawain. They're both such bright souls.<br /> <br /> And on the subject of Gawain's relationships, Captain Jack decided to crash our 'sex breakfast' as there had been insufficient mischief between he and Gawain. In particular, he was looking at what they were going to pull at the Masquerade Ball. That ogre is truly an overgrown boy in all the good ways but underneath it all he's all heart. He and Gawain are so much alike in that. They got to talking about plans which involved Jack replacing me and Gawain not noticing until after they'd danced a while. It sounds like a delightfully silly and very distracting event. I immediately found myself considering how it might serve as a perfect cover for Queen Charlotte and the Warlock of Night to slip away for their meeting.<br /> <br /> Of course, if Jack is going to impersonate me (badly) he does need to know my dress would look like. I have to admit, I hadn't really thought about what I was going to wear with my mask. I joked that since it was a Spring Court party I'd considered not wearing anything but the mask and apparently folks thought I was being serious about going naked. More than that, apparently it wouldn't be completely amiss if one owned it with the right mix of boldness and poise which was worded in the sort of polite tones that told me no one thought I had the social graces (and perfect body) to pull it off well. Julia picked that moment to start insisting (rather adorably) that we should all go shopping for gowns. She and Lori were downright giddy. Insincere Marguerite was as aloof as always (I believe her French citizenship might be revoked if she were to appear in public and not be) but she was enjoying herself. I think it surprised Julia just how much I actually like all of that girly stuff. Even if I am getting far better at it than I used to be thanks to Lori I don't indulge in dress up that often. While I did let them talk me out of going au natural I didn't go with anything as proper as what we found for all of them. I decided that since I was already wearing a rabbit mask I'd go with the classic playboy bunny outfit. It will require some work on my part to pull off without insulting the Spring Court but it'll give me a chance to show off what I've been learning from Annika. Julia seemed a bit disappointed that it wasn't a properly fancy gown and in the end she bought me a rather lovely sleeveless lace number that I had my eye on.<br /> <br /> Once we had dresses it was, of course, time to shop for equally fancy lingerie. It was fun though I can't lie, the fact that I was the only one of the four of us not fairly routinely fucking the others made me fell like a bit of an extra wheel once they started to tease and flirt. When Julia bought outfits for all of them and De La Rocha with a provision that they would be showing them off for each other later I did end up making a snarky comment. I regretted it rather immediately since Julia was obviously upset by it. She was quiet on the way back and so once we were home I drew her aside to talk about it. I told her I didn't mean it as anything more than a playful jab. I like Julia and have grown to consider a friend. Apparently she feels the same and was feeling a little worried that she'd offended me by being sexually interested in every woman in the Dream House that wasn't me. I assured her that wasn't the case. I mean, I wouldn't mind putting her through her paces but I'm not going to put on my nice girl fedora and whine about being friend-zoned because she doesn't want to fuck me.<br /> <br /> I've decided to wear my new dress and unmentionables for tonight's show and taken a bit of extra time properly girling myself up since this dress certainly deserves it. I think Julia will appreciate my efforts (it in a completely platonic way of course). I did try on my mask and bunny outfit first and took a few pictures to send Captain Jack (yet again for completely platonic reasons). And for once, ranting about everything has actually calmed me down a bit. Which is good because I have things I need to do. I need to speak to Annika about Spidertoes. She knows her better than anyone and might be able to help puzzle out what her angle is. Don't really have time before the show and I doubt she'll be here. If not, I'll call her after. I also need to speak to Andromeda privately. We don't know that finding Grey will bring us closer to finding the Table but it might and before I do that I need to make sure we're on the same page about it's ultimate fate. And having learned Relentless Pursuit, I can't help but think of who else this power could lead me to. I mean, as long as she's under the same sky I could find Stasia. No having to try to track down where she went after high school or anything... just a little glamour and I'd know how far away she is. I could find her. But this is not the time for that. Hell, never is the time for that trip. I need to stay the fuck away from her. There is nothing good going to come from seeing her. Either she's moved on and doesn't want or need to be reminded of me or she's been carrying the scars for twenty years. I don't need to see her eyes full of hate and betrayal. I don't need to hurt her. I already tried to go home. I'm not going to repeat that terrible mistake by looking for her. I'm not that kind of monster.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Okay\u2026things kind of snowballed today. Desiree came over to the house, agitated and asking for Gawain. Insincere Marguerite and I talked to her for a bit and tried to see what the problem was. Marguerite had looked for Gawain first thing, but found that he had actually taken Lori up on her offer from before, so he was unavailable for awhile. We managed to get Desiree to tell us what the problem was after getting her settled and more comfortable. Yeah, she\u2019s having a bad time of it.<br /> <br /> Apparently she is missing time since yesterday about dinner time. She said that she sat down at her computer this morning to write an email to her agent, but couldn\u2019t remember what she was going to type. A moment later she realized the problem was bigger than that, when she couldn\u2019t recall what she had done at all since making dinner last night! I tried to comfort her as best I could, which definitely wasn\u2019t as much as she needed.<br /> <br /> Enough time had passed and we figured that we\u2019d go get Gawain whether they were done or not. Luckily for us, they were. Insincere Marguerite and I knocked on Lori\u2019s door and let ourselves in. We found them in her bed, sort of covered by sheets. About like I expected. We told them that we had something important come up and we needed at least Gawain to come downstairs. He threw on some clothes and followed us out. Lori met us downstairs. The whole situation got relayed one more time and this time Desiree got the comfort she needed. Gawain is good at that stuff.<br /> <br /> So, what happened after that all kind of blurs together. It all breaks down to Lori calling the Spring court to see if anything strange had happened last night. The answer was no. Lori then asks if anyone had seen Desiree last night. Turns out that Desiree had been on a date with Princess Jolie last night, and it went rather well according to the Princess. Of course people started getting suspicious about why Lori was asking all these questions, so she drove over to see Princess Jolie and ended up explaining the whole situation to Jolie and Becky. That\u2019s when things went further than I think anyone wanted them to.<br /> <br /> Becky suggested that Desiree be put under House arrest and brought back to the Spring Court to be checked out. When Lorelei and Becky showed up with this suggestion you could see Desiree just wilt. She gave up and just sat down. The only thing she said after that was that she didn\u2019t want to die. Gawain argued for going with her to make sure she was okay. Becky assured everyone that Desiree would be put in handcuffs for the ride over, but would be released as soon as they arrived. She would then get checked out and let go once she was cleared. They were even going to put her to sleep before they let her go to put a tracking device under her skin!<br /> <br /> I think I felt a bit sick after that. I can understand Becky wanting to keep an eye on Desiree, but she could have just had Gawain sit in the backseat with her and they\u2019d be fine. Someone would be watching Desiree while Becky drove. It would be easy to have someone stay with Desiree after that to make sure she was okay and just overall keep an eye on her. I don\u2019t think a tracking device was strictly necessary!<br /> <br /> Desiree looked devastated. She wasn\u2019t going to fight anything that Becky wanted her to do, and said she\u2019d come along peacefully. I wanted to reach out and stop her. To get her to fight back and insist on staying with us, or at least having Gawain stay with her. I don\u2019t know why I didn\u2019t. Maybe I was scared for myself. I could so easily end up in her situation. Hopefully not the losing time part, but the ending up in handcuffs part. Maybe I thought that even if I did step in she wouldn\u2019t try to stand up for herself. She looked so defeated. I\u2019ve seen that look on people\u2019s faces many times. I know what it looks like when all the hope leaves them and the light goes out of their eyes. I had hoped to never see that look on someone\u2019s face again. Goddess I\u2019m such an idiot. I should have stopped them. I should have insisted that we could watch Desiree just fine.<br /> <br /> I think this is how I know that I\u2019m still not that good a person. At the time I should have acted, I didn\u2019t. I kept my mouth shut and only thought about myself. I didn\u2019t want to get in the middle of a Spring court situation and just shine that \u201cspotlight\u201d on me. So, I stayed quiet and didn\u2019t draw any attention. I\u2019m good at that.<br /> <br /> By this point Calamity had taken a break from her dance lesson with Annika to come over and discuss things with the rest of us. It was suggested that Insincere Marguerite go to Desiree\u2019s apartment and see if the mirrors saw anything that might help us piece together what happened last night. I volunteered to go with her. I figured two sets of eyes would see more and I could be looking for mundane clues while she used more magical means to do the same. Unfortunately we didn\u2019t find anything that helped. Last night Desiree was cooking dinner, ramen noodles, and stopped to make a phone call. A moment later she turns off the stove, leaving the noodles in the pan, and heads out of the house. The next thing the mirrors saw was her coming back this morning, taking a shower then sitting down at her computer. There wasn\u2019t much else to see, so Insincere Marguerite called the others and let them know what we didn\u2019t find anything out of the ordinary. No body swapping, no one forcing their way in. She just made a phone call, possibly to Dark Kimberly about going on a date with Jolie, and left.<br /> <br /> Perhaps someone, one of the Motely, should check Desiree\u2019s phone and see if any other phone calls were made or received by her phone during the time she blacked out. I am curious to see if perhaps she received a phone call to activate some kind of \u201cprograming.\u201d Whether that is the Director\u2019s programing or someone else\u2019s is still up for debate. It was discussed that the Director is too clever to leave such an obvious gap in her memory. He would have filled it in with false memories so there were no questions or worries when it was over. It is likely that someone in the Freehold or close to it, is manipulating Desiree to get her in trouble, or is using her because of who her Keeper was. It has been said many times that everyone that escapes from the Director is a Loyalist. What if some of them aren\u2019t and they were all set up for some reason?<br /> Probably someone that really doesn\u2019t like the director, wants to sow fear, or is just being an asshole? Don\u2019t know yet. There are too many possibilities.<br /> <br /> By the time that Insincere Marguerite and I got back to the Dream House Desiree and Becky were gone. Headed back to Glamor Springs I\u2019m assuming. Funny thing is that I don\u2019t even know Desiree all that well, and at least part of the time I have known her I\u2019ve been on the fence as to whether or not she is a Loyalist. You wouldn\u2019t think that this whole situation would bother me so much. Guilty conscience? Maybe. I have enough shit to feel guilty about. Yeah, no shortage of red in my ledger. I guess it\u2019s all just a bit too close for comfort. Difference is I know what I did, and I did it willingly. I\u2019d like to think that I\u2019m doing something to even things out, but I have to be honest with myself. I haven\u2019t even made a dent yet.<br /> <br /> How do I make up for all the things I did? Most of my actions so far have been selfish to some extent. Clearing the hedge of the giant spider-thing was mostly selfish since we were just clearing it out to get to the Hollow. I guess the incident with the Briar wolves could be considered altruistic. We cleared them out so they wouldn\u2019t be a threat to anyone traversing that part of the Hedge. It wasn\u2019t so much of an immediate threat though, so I don\u2019t know if it really counts. Goddess, what can I possibly do to make up for all the shit that I have done? Maybe I should let them catch me? At least I know that I would deserve to be in those handcuffs. Just from observing her, I doubt that Desiree is a willing Loyalist, if a Loyalist at all. It\u2019s really hard to fake such deep emotions so well, and I\u2019m not convinced that she\u2019s that good of an actress.<br /> <br /> Anyhoo\u2026while we were all discussing things, Gawain came up with the idea of going into Desiree\u2019s dreams to see if anything had been messed with, memories, dreams, etc\u2026 If he does this he might be able to see if anyone planted any suggestions in Desiree\u2019s head or messed with her in some other way. The Spring Court seemed okay with Gawain doing this since he is both skilled and trusted by the person whose dreams he\u2019d be entering. Trust is really big when it comes to dream crafting, and I\u2019m pretty sure that Gawain has Desiree\u2019s trust. Especially considering that he is the first person that she wanted to talk to and the only one that she really responded to.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think that I could willingly let Gawain into my dreams. It\u2019s not just a matter of all the things that I have to hide either. It\u2019s more a matter of those things that give me nightmares. Gawain has enough bad dreams of his own. I certainly don\u2019t need to be adding to that load of his with my own baggage. There are also the things that I don\u2019t want him to know. I\u2019m not sure if I can hide those in my dreams or not, but figured for both of our sakes that it would be best to leave all that in my head. I can deal with my usual nightmares and Gawain can stick with the horrors that he already has to deal with. He doesn\u2019t need mine adding to his burden.<br /> <br /> Okay\u2026so back to normal stuff. After Desiree was escorted out and Insincere Marguerite and I were back, Flores came by to see if anyone needed or wanted lessons in dancing before the big Masquerade. I will admit that though I served a Queen, courtly manners and etiquette were not stressed during my training. So, I took Flores up on her offer of dance lessons. Gawain did too. I will give her credit. She knows what she\u2019s doing when it comes to dancing. Here\u2019s hoping I can avoid stepping on too many toes.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Okay, so had to add some more to this entry. Calamity came back from talking to some of her Court\u2019s higher ups and she passed along what information she could. Turns out that Felicity had connections to the Warlock of Night, and that they would not have good things to say if some harm should befall Felicity. Calamity also reported that the break-ins at Felicity\u2019s house were not done by the Summer court. She talked to Gunnar and he assured her that drawing attention to Felicity was the last thing that the court wanted to do. They were perfectly happy with her not being involved in any Seasonal court business. I think that they are afraid that if she becomes involved too much in the Seasonal court business that it might bring down scrutiny from the Day court, or others. And since Felicity used to be the consort of the Lord of Day, if anything bad should happen to her in our town then payback would be rained down on our heads. Pleasant thoughts, yeah?<br /> <br /> After that whole conversation happened, Insincere Marguerite asked to talk to Calamity in private. A few minutes later they both came back. Insincere Marguerite told us of two young ladies that were affiliated with the Night court could be dangerous and that we should avoid them. Their names are Scarlet and Natalia. I have not yet met them so I don\u2019t have anything really detailed or specific to say about them. I only know that Insincere Marguerite was warning the rest of us about those two young ladies. She also mentioned that she does not know what they want, so their motives are as of yet, unclear. I will admit to being curious as to their goals, but am not all that eager to meet the two young ladies that have caused quite the stir. Maybe I can just avoid them altogether?<br /> <br /> It would be nice if things were clear, but they are not. Nothing in life is ever clear it seems. Somebody is manipulating a prominent, if reclusive, Day Courtier. Not sure why yet either. Whoever is manipulating things around her is good. What is the Night court up to? Do they have something to do with the break-ins? They could be trying to draw attention to one of their own so they have an excuse to be involved in what\u2019s going on here. Then there is also the person(s) who is messing with Desiree. It seems like they are trying to make her look like a Loyalist, but to what end? Do they just want her discredited, or do they want her dead? And who is doing the manipulation?<br /> <br /> All of this is enough to give anyone a headache. As if my thoughts aren\u2019t full enough lately, I need to add this to the pile. I would love to chalk it up to a pile of political bullshit and be done with it, but I know that it\u2019s not as simple as all that. If I want to keep my head above water, so to speak, then I better start paying attention to all this political BS and figuring out what is going on. Question is how to do that, keep my motley safe from threats local and not so local, and try and make up for at least a little of what I\u2019ve done. Good question, huh?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> It\u2019s been busy, and I have been unable to focus on my dancing. Julia and I did sneak down to the stage when the others were asleep, put on some Nightmare Before Christmas and waltzed around a bit one night, but that is all. Sadly.<br /> <br /> Calamity was practicing today during the day, and besides, Desiree came by. Julia and I were going to practice some more (as much as she decries romance, she <i>loves</i> it when we dance especially old-fashioned. She gets a dreamy, distant look and long smile) Desiree was looking for Gawain, who was apparently seeking to regain some lost masculinity by having sex with Lori. Silly Gawain, it has nothing to do with that. Simply.<br /> <br /> Not that I blame Gawain for sleeping with Lorelei, but pursuing her right away like that does nothing for his dignity nor respectability, both of which he seems to desire to cultivate. Apparently.<br /> <br /> Desiree has a big problem. She does not remember the previous evening or morning, time that she apparently spent in intimate company with Jolie. And here I wanted to be the only one that happened with. She was terribly upset (I would be too) and concerned she really was a Manchurian Candidate for her Keeper. Gawain, Lorelei and Jacob decided to promptly sell her out. They were nice about it, but she is under lock and key awaiting a chip in her head. Note to self: If I think I may be being controlled by a Gentry do not, under any circumstances, tell Gawain, Lorelei or Jacob. Absolutely.<br /> <br /> Jacob and I checked her house, and found only that she had gone out after dinnertime as the daylight people reckon it and returned in the late morning.<br /> <br /> Once Desiree had been cuffed and carted off for telling the wrong people, Calamity headed off to talk to Queen Charlotte, about other things. Flores had arrived, and despite her ill timing sought to help us prepare for the ball. Jacob and Gawain took her up on it, so Julia, sensing there would be no midnight practicing, snatched me off to practice on the roof. Waltzing on a roof is interesting, and a dance floor will probably seem easier. Definitely.<br /> <br /> Once Calamity returned (and probably assumed Julia and I were a bit out of breath for the wrong reasons) she reported Tommy Rawhead and Charlotte suspected Desiree was being set up. That does make sense, though I am unsure that it is the case. I am not prepared to say for sure. It just seems unlikely someone mind controlled her into bedding Jolie and then forgetting it. To what purpose? I mean, it\u2019s not common Director behavior, as I understand it. No, I suspect we don\u2019t know what is going on, and I am not positive Desiree is not lying due to suspicion cast on her as a result of her bedding the Princess. Possibly.<br /> <br /> I also discovered something slightly troubling: Scarlet and Natalia are in town. The Warlock of Night\u2019s \u201cHandmaidens,\u201d I spent time with them just before the incident with the Lord of Day\u2019s house. They are <i>excellent</i> lovers; I learned my techniques involving underarms, inside of the knee, and behind the ears from them, techniques that my lovers most appreciate. I shudder to think about my time with them, but I shudder more that hearing they were in town, I wanted to throw myself at them. I will not be out of control. Absolutely.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know why they are here. Calamity said they were sashaying around the Lighthouse asking questions. Surely anything relevant the Warlock can simply ask. She is not afraid to. I wonder at their intentions. I\u2019d suspect they are here to individually seduce each single monarch, but I have never even seen them go to the bathroom separately, much less have sex. It does make me concerned about just what they are planning.<br /> <br /> I am also worried their hot passions were part of what spurred I toward my assault on the home and dignity of the Lord of Day. I wanted to please them, and\u2026I don\u2019t think I should discuss it further. I don\u2019t think they set me up, but I do recall Felicity\u2019s words. Clearly.<br /> <br /> Calamity also noted Spidertoes intense interest in having the Night Court alliance. She threatened Gunnar over it, though I am not sure she actually likes Gunnar so I am less worried than Calamity is. Still, something to watch, doubly if Scarlet and Natalia are slinking around. Definitely.<br /> <br /> Having been around Jacob, I am fairly sure Natalia does not have a genuine Russian accent. I wonder if hers is from elsewhere or if she is faking it. Maybe he will know if he hears her speak.<br /> <br /> The evening went fine. Flores remained, as Julia expected, and we spent a fine night. I did my best to shut out my fancies of Scarlet and Natalia\u2019s whispered promises in my ears.<br /> <br /> I did warn Julia. She can do as she chooses, though I suspect that will mean allowing herself to be bedded by them if it comes up. Probably.<br /> <br /> Breakfast was, as always, interesting. Flores flirted heavily; she seems incapable of not doing so. She put De La Rocha off when she left, and Julia attempted to be supportive, which, well, seemed to start building an erotic charge between the two. It happens very easily with Julia. Frequently.<br /> <br /> Julia was also quick to defend Chalcedony, not that she knows her, but her disappearances. One would not know now that she has warmed up to us, but Julia is terribly introverted.<br /> <br /> Speaking of such things, Julia has made clear her hate for Felicity, and implied to I she intends to do her harm. She does not seem to know her, but it smacks of jealousy. I am pledgebound to not abandon her as much as she is pledgebound to belong to me, she is not getting cut out of the picture, and would not even if there was no pledge. I would simply collect Felicity. I have not exerted control of her to not harm Felicity, but I will if I have to. Sadly.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Felicity, I got a warning from Calamity she may be manipulating I. This had occurred to I me and I was not upset she said it, though she clearly chose her words carefully to be respectful.<br /> <br /> But back to breakfast, De La Rocha headed to work, trailed by a slightly worried Lorelei. Captain Jack showed up to plan hijinx with Gawain. It was fun. Discussing what Calamity may wear (because Captain Jack may disguise as Calamity) lead to Julia and Lorelei deciding a shopping trip was in order. Calamity and I were drug along.<br /> <br /> Still, it was not all bad. I stood under Julia\u2019s parasol, and helped her pick out black, lacy, feminine dresses that made I me smile. We picked something in gold for me for the ball to match my mask. Then we shopped for Lingerie. Julia bought myself, Lorelei, and the absent De La Rocha something and declared we must wear them for each other tonight. I look forward it. Perhaps I will even forget what Scarlet and Natalia promised about our next meeting\u2026<br /> <br /> Yes, I will. These girls deserve no less. Definitely.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXIV</i><br /> <br /> Not much to add. The players seemed very conflicted over how to handle Desiree. It was a powerful scene. I enjoyed seeing them working at it.<br /> <br /> Also making sure they have plenty of small subplots for the ball to take an interest in. What are these femmes fatale up to? Who invited Felicity? What is the Warlock of Night and Madame Spidertoes true intentions? Is Desiree going to be up to something? And my goodness did we just arrange for Captain Jack to be in a dress again?<br /> <br /> So many questions. Some may be answered next time. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 02-16-2015, 05:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T23:58:48-08:00","id":411147,"title":"","content":"Why is Lorelei so keen to sell the angel image? Also, was the sex with Gawain not as off handed or doing it to humor him as it came off as?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","user":"omenseer","date":". 02-19-2015, 03:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T12:01:11-08:00","id":411848,"title":"","content":"1) My guess would be she digs the wings, they are a big part of her, but the &quot;angel&quot; not &quot;bird&quot; is more distant from her durance. Also being a fairest, not beast, it may feel more right to her. All speculation here, it has not come up in conversation. She seems to dislike anything referring to her as a &quot;bird&quot; either as slag for woman or referring to her as a bird animal somehow.<br /> <br /> 2) Eh, off handed, sure. To humor him probably not. Lorelei likes sex, and she likes having sex with people she is fond of. It is not a big deal for her, she just likes doing it. Even the other sexually active members of the Motley (everyone but Ace) has less than she does...though they are also not as attractive as she is, and Insincere Marguerite prefers sleeping in small, tight spaces rather than, say, beds, and Jacob has issues.<br /> <br /> Of course she has more sexual drama than the others, though Calamity, Gawain, and Insincere Marguerite tempt fate that way sometimes.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T13:53:04-08:00","id":412038,"title":"","content":"I've just spent the last week working my way through these posts. It's definately a campaign that I wish I was involved in.<br /> <br /> I'm wondering if you've imagined the possibility of the PCs reading each other's journals in-game, either due to plot events (detective work to find a missing motley member, trying to assess Clarity breaking points, etc) or just due to plain nosiness or paranoia. Maybe the players have an unspoken agreement that the journals will have no &quot;MacGuffin&quot; status; I certainly don't expect these players to metagame using character secrets. Even the idea of one or more of the journals being stolen by an NPC seems possible, unless you view them as entirely a means of recording session events and establishing character psychology.<br /> <br /> Can't wait to see what happens next!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4722-birnam","name":"Birnam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T16:30:10-08:00","id":412200,"title":"","content":"It's not impossible; essentially it could happen with permission. I am not going to &quot;punish&quot; a player for doing journals though if they are interested it could absolutely happen. Several of us have played Castle Falkesntein where journals are, by default, an in game artifact, but we elected to go for &quot;journals are only an artifact if you want them to be.&quot;<br /> <br /> I believe Calamity and Gawain's are known to each other and they (in theory) know where the others is. Insincere Marguerite's one would need to use powers to get to, as it is inaccessible outside the use of powers to shrink or become intangible. I don't think anyone can read Jacob's if they found it.<br /> <br /> My other games are different, <b>Demon</b> is almost all internal monologues and conversations, though Kilroy has reports he sends. Perfect memory means no need for journals. In <b>Geist</b>, the tweets Natalie sends Doc and Sara easily can, and sometimes have, read since they are &quot;preferred&quot; and have special access, while the few &quot;journals&quot; are on her laptop. Jasmine's are in Chinese, and Alice's are internal monologues, Sara's are mailed. It might be possible to find Doc's though.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T04:44:52-08:00","id":413984,"title":"","content":"Thank you Birnam. I always love knowing that someone enjoyed my writing. <br /> <br /> Calamity's journal is physically in the same rather well used diary she started as a young teen and that her fetch wrote in during high school. And while she has in character made it clear she expects someone (at least Gawain) will end up reading it after her inevitable violent demise I don't think she's considered the other characters reading it while she's alive too seriously. She doesn't guard it that closely and she doesn't make a secret of it's existence. She generally keeps it with that collection of photo albums and other highly incriminating evidence she took from her parent's house after she murdered them.<br /> <br /> Calamity is perhaps a bit careless in this regard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T14:39:16-08:00","id":414450,"title":"","content":"Hi, Lorelei's player here.<br /> <br /> Omenseer, the good Baron pretty much has the right of it as far as Lori's attraction to the angel image goes. Angels, at least in popular culture and literature, are strong, powerful, morally forthright beings. Lori's durance had her singing in a cage for her Keeper, which is about as powerless as one can get, so she's more keen on inviting the comparison to an angel. She's also trying to reconnect with her estranged father, a Methodist minister, so there may be some subconscious impetus from that direction as well.<br /> <br /> It may sound callous to say so, but sex isn't really a big deal for Lorelei. She certainly enjoys it, and indulges as frequently as possible, but she doesn't equate it with romance. Honestly, until recently it never really occurred to her that she was looking for a romantic relationship with anyone. Since de la Rocha is almost equally cavalier about physical relationships, Lori doesn't feel like she's cheating when her attention occasionally wanders. Of course the time she spent with Gawain was special to her because he's a dear friend, but she doesn't see why the fact that they had sex should change their relationship.<br /> <br /> Of course, if she had even the slightest clue that Calamity had been hurt by the fling, she'd be wracked with guilt.<br /> <br /> As far as the journal question goes, Birnam, I've always assumed that Lori's journal is a physical object that exists in the game setting. The Baron is welcome to use it in any way he chooses.<br /> <br /> Thanks for reading, everyone. It's nice to see that people are interested in the game. Keep the feedback coming, folks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T15:02:42-08:00","id":414471,"title":"","content":"Thanks for replying to my questions, all of you.<br /> <br /> Baron, I totally understand all of your points. I'm curious about Insincire Marguirite's journal, now. I'd sometimes assumed that it was her whispering to her puppets. Is it just a journal hidden somewhere, then?<br /> <br /> Amberghylles, I did get the impression that, if anyone would earn the right to read Calamity's journal, it would be Gawain. I don't really think it would affect their relationship, though: he seems to be the understanding and forgiving heart of the motley. I also understand why Calamity would keep all that evidence together; it kind of fits in with her guilt/monster complex.<br /> <br /> Penitent Tom, I think you have the right attitude in mind with Lori's approach to sex. It's suitably Spring Court and, from having several poly friends, the separation between romantic faithfulness and being sexually open is absolutely consistent. It can get tricky, sure, but that's just how emotions roll. It certainly must keep the RP interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4722-birnam","name":"Birnam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T15:36:47-08:00","id":414503,"title":"","content":"Insincere Marguerite's journal is hidden in the ventilation shafts in the house she crawls through and sometimes sleeps in. One would have to slip through an opening not much wider than a head to get to it. Eternal Autumn 4, Separation 5, or the Tunnelgrub ability can do that, but no one in the house, save Marguerite, has it (even Julia's Contracts are more Fleeting and Spellbound than Eternal Autumn). Insincere Marguerite and Lorelei do have Contracts of Separation 1, but neither has higher. Her journal is in English though (it's practice since her English is a step behind everyone else) hence the grammar errors with me and I among other things (when speaking she rarely mixes up me and I, its more a writing problem).<br /> <br /> Gawain is certainly the conscience of the group. Most people just have an area they struggle with. Some, like Calamity, Jacob and Insincere Marguerite, wear that on their sleeve, for others it is more subtle.<br /> <br /> And yea, it came up in my <b>Geist</b> thread that that game could be a TV supernatural drama with all the drama and such in the game. It applies here too, I think. I like mixing action and mystery and romance, and I think my players do an excellent job of making characters accordingly. The <b>Changeling</b> group is a fairly poly bunch, certainly.<br /> <br /> Also, thanks for the feedback. Discussion like this helps shed more light on the game, which helps give a new dimension to the journals. And I know my players and I enjoy reading what people are thinking as they enjoy the journals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T23:42:18-08:00","id":414954,"title":"","content":"I am fairly sure Calamity would let Gawain read her journal if he asked, though she would not write in it as freely if she knew he (or anyone else) was doing so. Gawain is rather the exception to many things where Calamity is concerned. And yeah, he is the heart, one of the reasons she needs him since she considers Gawain the anchor that keeps her from going too crazy. <br /> <br /> As a point, I know why she's bothered by Lori and Gawain being together, though it has not really clicked into place for her yet. She hasn't completely let go of the idea that Gawain deserves someone better than her and she does consider Lori to be a better person, more the sort of bright soul that Gawain should be loved by. Too many years in a place where she was told she wasn't worthy of being loved and that her parents hadn't loved her and had wanted a good girl instead. I do look forward to her moving past the guilt and self-loathing and I see it happening with the motley and her friends in the local freehold, but I feel it's deeply ingrained in her and not something she'll shed quickly. <br /> <br /> I do appreciate the feedback and, in case it's not obvious, I do rather like to talk about Calamity and the game so please do feel free to ask any other questions that occur. I hope you continue to enjoy reading the journals, I enjoy writing Calamity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T02:00:39-08:00","id":414991,"title":"","content":"I am sure I speak for the Motley when I say we look forward to Calamity moving to a better, healthier headspace (where she is less likely to stab us). ^_^ But it is about the journey and all that.<br /> <br /> Also, one of the PCs is a good girl? What?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T02:38:19-08:00","id":415003,"title":"","content":"Calamity made a promise not to stab anyone in the motley and Calamity keeps her magically binding promises.<br /> <br /> And yes, Calamity considers Lorelei to be a good girl.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T08:43:06-08:00","id":415183,"title":"","content":"I forget. Does Calamity have a particular grudge against Oath breakers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T12:16:30-08:00","id":415528,"title":"","content":"Calamity began the game with Oath and Punishment and currently has it at rank 4. She is distrustful and so puts stock in the power of Oaths to compel people to keep their word. And while she does not specifically have a grudge against Oath breakers, she does like to justify the acts of violence she craves by finding victims that deserve it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T13:33:19-08:00","id":415603,"title":"","content":"Well, okay, I suppose Lori is a &quot;good girl&quot; in that she doesn't wish anyone any specific harm... not even Annika, when you scratch the surface of her dislike. The darkest she's gotten has been when she wanted to see Mary's fetch punished for its atrocities, and I don't think many people are going to judge her too harshly for that. There is, however, a little more to her durance than has been revealed so far, and as her Wyrd score increases I've been trying to drop a few hints that not everything in the Empress' realm was as peaceful and boring as Lori has let on...<br /> <br /> Still, it's fairly telling that Lorelei, who was the archetypal &quot;wild child&quot; back in the 70s when she was Juliette Wells, and is still known for debauched promiscuity, is the group's token goody two-shoes.<br /> <br /> And allow me to second Amberghylles' sentiments; I love talking about my characters and will be happy to field any questions the readers might have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T14:31:02-08:00","id":415718,"title":"","content":"She is the one non-Darkling gal, even when de la Rocha and Julia are around, which is amusing. I suppose with Calamity and Insincere Marguerite there she is the good girl.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T14:59:17-08:00","id":415736,"title":"","content":"Well, she is literally a choir-girl. :-P<br /> <br /> Baron's observations made me realise that I've yet to run (or even play) a game with strong player romance. In the Changeling campaign I ran, the motley members were almost all deliberately asexual. I included NPCs with romantic ties, which the players loved, but chose to ignore potential romance thrown in their direction.<br /> <br /> You know that you have a good campaign going when you can at least ship a few of the characters with each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4722-birnam","name":"Birnam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T15:17:34-08:00","id":415751,"title":"","content":"Heh. Well romance is something you have to have a group ready for. Some people just don't like it in games. That's fine. As I have noted I find it really interesting, and thus have a fair amount of it. It's always optional, of course, and good to know people's comfort level first. I've also found that it is something that it really helps to have pictures for, as pictures help with the X-factor of little things about someone's appearance that can get chemistry. One thing I do have as a sort of boilerplate when I add new Players to my groups is to say that we don't permit IC stuff to be used to show OOC interest. You can have OOC interest and an IC relationship with another player, but telegraphing that via character is a no-no. I've never run a game where it happened, but I was in one once, it was awkward (I was not involved as either party).<br /> <br /> But once that is out of the way people sometimes feel more comfortable with it. And when people know no one is going to laugh at them or anything. My groups tend to be mixes of sexes (and orientations) and that helps too, I think.<br /> <br /> But it is all about comfort level and interest. Some find romance dull, some exciting. And yea, the shipping can be fun too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T15:45:05-08:00","id":415794,"title":"","content":"Wow. Yeah, people acting out unrequited feelings for another player IC sounds like it would break a game. Even the OOC couple I've played with in multiple games avoided IC relationships beyond friendship.<br /> <br /> Playing with mixed gender/orientation group can be the best. The other thing I like is your inclusion of a third gender/non-binary member of the freehold. Transgender themes via durance seem to be a popular choice in C:tL games, too.<br /> <br /> The nearest I got to romance in my campaign: Spring Court Flowering Fairest NPC crushing on emotionally distant Woodblood Elemental PC. Matchmaking hilarity ensues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4722-birnam","name":"Birnam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T15:47:06-08:00","id":415797,"title":"","content":"To Birnam:<br /> <br /> Yeah, well, I guess I walked right into that choir-girl comment, didn't I? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The fact that Lori is a church-goer grew from two factors, one IC, one OOC. In character, she attends church regularly in a mostly successful attempt to reconnect with her father... it was actually the reason she moved to the West Coast in the first place. Out of character, I wanted to depict a character who was a progressive, tolerant, but still devout Christian rather than the stereotypical bible-thumping hate-monger. Though I admit, Lori's adherence to the Ten Commandments has been... less than perfect since the start of the campaign.<br /> <br /> The Baron's campaigns have a healthy amount of PC/NPC romance in them, though MDH has more than most campaigns in which I've been involved (as a more socially-oriented game, it makes a certain amount of sense). Of all of us, I think only Ace has proven stubbornly asexual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T17:29:38-08:00","id":415908,"title":"","content":"I always pegged Gawain as the groups goodie two-shoes.<br /> <br /> The reason I ask about the oath breaker was because while I was trying to think of other images besides birds or angels that would fit Lorelei to see what fits and succubi and erinyes came to mind. Then I was thinking succubus fits Insincere Marguerite better while erinyes would fit calamity better. At least if you gave them the appropriate wings of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T00:36:08-08:00","id":416255,"title":"","content":"Hey now, Insincere Marguerite has had the fewest partners of any of the ladies in the game.<br /> <br /> Since the game started anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 02-23-2015, 03:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T00:59:54-08:00","id":416271,"title":"","content":"Its not about how much, but how she uses it and why (Cocks eyebrow, but then realizes I look silly).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T02:48:56-08:00","id":416319,"title":"","content":"Fair. She is a dirty temptress I suppose. When one's durance was stealing people, it was part of being a thief.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T08:37:05-08:00","id":416513,"title":"","content":"How is Insincere Maggy in terms of Clarity, anyway? I remember you saying she was still at seven, which surprised me at the time. Everyone else seems to be taking hits, from what I can tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4722-birnam","name":"Birnam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T11:46:17-08:00","id":416709,"title":"","content":"Calamity is the only one who has actually lost Clarity, which she lost for assaulting someone for thrills, glamour and cash. Insincere Marguerite has made four rolls, but made the rolls (all of them were for stealing, so level 7 checks, not the hardest to pass). She usually steals credit cards which she can more easily justify as &quot;victimless&quot; so I gave her a die on those, though she had a penalty when she stole a car.<br /> <br /> I believe currently Insincere Marguerite and Gawain are 7, though I may be misremembering who the other 7 is. Jacob and Calamity are currently 5, everyone else is 6. I am not too harsh on Clarity checks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T13:32:16-08:00","id":416842,"title":"","content":"I would point out that Calamity's ideas about who is 'good' are firmly based on her own interpretations. She absolutely ignores the notion of sexuality being bad. Also, as far as she is concerned, Lori is much better at being human than anyone else in the motley, something she admires in the girl. Really, Calamity views Gawain, Lori, and Ace as the good or bright or perhaps (as she is geeky from before being taken) even Seelie. While she, Insincere Marguerite, and Jacob are the darker souls of the motley. Now, Ace is simply insane, but both Lori and Gawain she feels should be shielded from the necessary evils that she can do since she's already sinful and tainted and dark. <br /> <br /> Omenseer, I do have to agree that Calamity could make a fair erinyes with some wings.<br /> <br /> This is not the first game I have played where romance was an element, but it is a much more significant one than most of my others. Love and relationships are the core of a huge amount of human motives, so I like that we explore them freely in this game. Also I fell in love with CtL rather quickly because it is so conducive to flawed yet fascinating characters and their inner struggles. From a writing standpoint, I have found that the broken toys are usually the most fun to play with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T22:47:55-08:00","id":417265,"title":"","content":"Could Lorelei's singing revive an ailing emperor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T08:32:20-08:00","id":417570,"title":"","content":"Insomnia, a melancholy mood and rediscovering my old CDs made me realise that a suitable song for evoking Calamity and Gawain is 'Bubble Gum Years' by Gomez.<br /> <br /> Just an observation while I wait in the world's longest airport security line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4722-birnam","name":"Birnam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T18:52:32-08:00","id":418188,"title":"","content":"Omenseer,<br /> <br /> Lori might come up with the succubus idea, but as far as erinyes go... keep in mind that she was Taken from a time in which D&amp;D was in its infancy. If she was familiar with the term &quot;erinyes&quot; at all, it probably conjures up images of half-human crones from Greek mythology, relentlessly pursuing disrespectful oathbreakers and whipping them with brass scorpion scourges. Seeing as how she's still consumed with guilt over breaking her <u>own</u> oath to her two friends back in Arcadia, she's not particularly keen on that idea.<br /> <br /> As far as Lori's singing reviving an ailing emperor... well, with a combination of talecrafting and her Spring contracts, I'd say the odds of his recovery are good. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T19:34:22-08:00","id":418243,"title":"","content":"Oh, and in response to the Baron's post... Lori's Clarity is currently 7. She started with a Clarity of 6, but I bought it up after the encounter with Mary's fetch, based on the fact that Lori was so profoundly affected by the atrocities the fetch committed. Rather than driving her a little crazier, I feel that the shock of witnessing the results of those acts actually brought her more in line with her human sympathies and emotions; her grief over those deaths gave her another connection to the real world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T22:14:29-08:00","id":418421,"title":"","content":"Don't worry Mr. Tom erinyes is solely reserved for Calamity. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Does Lori know of Hans Christian Andersen works then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T02:25:54-08:00","id":418527,"title":"","content":"I was not familiar with that song before just now Birnam. But having found and listened to it I can see where it wouldt bring them to mind. I have a playlist of Calamity music that I put together to listen to while writing her and she has her own Pandora station that I seeded with it. It is more music that makes me think of Calamity than music Calamity would listen to, though I do have a fairly good idea of her tastes. And I also have a small but growing collection of songs Calamity might perform when she reaches a sufficient level of skill to do so as part of the show.. <br /> <br /> You know, Omenseer, Gawain could make a brass scorpion scourge for her easily enough. Really it's just who.. er where she'd acquire the wings from...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T11:11:16-08:00","id":418988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amberghylles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play?p=418527#post418527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, Omenseer, Gawain could make a brass scorpion scourge for her easily enough. Really it's just who.. er where she'd acquire the wings from...</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunting trip?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T16:33:17-08:00","id":419527,"title":"","content":"If I didn't know in my heart of hearts that Calamity would never hurt Lori, I might take offense to this line of thought...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T16:43:59-08:00","id":419538,"title":"","content":"I wasn't talking about hunting Lori for the wings I meant hunting a hedge beast or some such. I figure if Calamity wanted wings, functional or symbolic, she would want a fight behind their acquisition. Sorry about that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T18:20:44-08:00","id":419658,"title":"","content":"No offense taken; my response was intended to be tongue-in-cheek. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T19:14:02-08:00","id":419735,"title":"","content":"I figured <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Although that could make for an amusing moment misunderstanding in game.<br /> <br /> Also, I want to call Lori Nightingale now... What would her reaction to that be?<br /> <br /> Lori = Nightingale<br /> Calamity = Erinyes<br /> Insincere Margarete = Succubus<br /> Ace = Madman<br /> Jacob = ?<br /> Gawain = Gawain<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T20:00:47-08:00","id":419765,"title":"","content":"Dragon Age: Inquisition has shifted my view of the name &quot;Nightingale&quot; beyond repair.<br /> <br /> ETA: Insincere Marguerite says Insincere Marguerite is perfectly fine, no need to call her anything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 02-25-2015, 11:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T03:07:37-08:00","id":423934,"title":"","content":"Preparing for the ball. Lorelei is Gawain is worried, Lorelei is down, Calamity is stressed, Jacob is melancholy. Just another typical day at the Dream House.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXIV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> June 13<sup>th</sup><br /> <br /> Well, yesterday kinda took a turn. I think the girls had fun at the shopping trip, but by the time the show came around, everybody was down. To be fair, really it was Lori that was down, but then she sang [a really sad song]. I mean, that\u2019s a pretty sad song, but she made it, you know, really really sad. I don\u2019t think anybody wasn\u2019t crying, at least a little. Calamity started drinking at the bar instead of doing her usual smoozing thing. She was playing with the scar she got from her blood sister thing with Anastasia. I was really worried she had figured out something bad had happened to Stasia, but she was just missing her. I mean, that\u2019s still not good, but it\u2019s not, like, final or anything.<br /> <br /> I kept her company for a bit, but then Lori went right upstairs after her set, and Calamity pointed out that De la Roche wasn\u2019t here, and she\u2019s -always- here. We checked up on her, and she was dressed in pajamas, which was kinda weird. She said De la Roche had to work through things, I guess before the Greening and all. It seemed to come out of nowhere, but Calamity seemed like she understood, and Lori said they hadn\u2019t broken up or anything, so I think it\u2019ll be ok? She said once the whole show was over and folks were gone, she\u2019d come down and have ice cream and bourbon and watch a movie with people, which seemed like a good plan. She certainly had the hangover to go with that today.<br /> <br /> I had to duck out to go to the Spring Court. I felt bad leaving Lori upset like that, and Calamity not ok either, but I wasn\u2019t gonna be the best at helping out anyway, and helping Desiree was important too. She trusted me, and I needed to do something to make it better. That went pretty well - I think me and Desiree might have had the best nights of anyone. I didn\u2019t find what I needed yet, but it was right there. Tonight I\u2019ll get it, I\u2019m sure. She\u2019s a strong dreamer too - I didn\u2019t have any problems slipping in, but I didn\u2019t run any risk of overwhelming her \u2018scape.<br /> <br /> Her dream was affected a little by the event of the evening for her part - she and Princess Joli had been making out when I got there. She was in much better spirits, even if Becky was, you know, not happy. Not happy at all. I can\u2019t really blame her... if I didn\u2019t trust Desiree, and was in charge of the Princess\u2019s safety, I\u2019d probably be just as pissy. But it was good to see Desiree less... hopeless. And her dream was upbeat, her in a theatre with a large appreciative audience - I think I saw Joli in there, out of the corner of my eye. The people other than Desiree flickered between being kinda vague and faceless and being regular people though. I didn\u2019t really see anything I\u2019d have pinpointed as control though, like strings, or cue cards or something that fit the scene. I didn\u2019t have a full insight though, so we\u2019ll have to just see, you know?<br /> <br /> Anyway, I got back to the Dream House in time to make breakfast. Lori was super hung over, like I mentioned, so she just had aspirin and OJ. I suggested she have something with salt, to help with the water retention, you know, so she put salt in her OJ, which was disgusting, of course. And probably didn\u2019t mix well with the taste of dead skunk plus ashtray she said she already had when she woke up. Jacob made coffee, and looked a little foggy. When I noticed the coffee pot had been used a lot last night, I asked him if everything had gone ok. Then he started telling me about Chalcedony having stayed the night because Becky needed help and so Calamity couldn\u2019t watch over Chalcedony and it was kinda a mess.<br /> <br /> That was about the time Calamity showed up from Becky\u2019s, and Chalcedony came up from the guest room in the basement. Once Becky had come to pick Chalcedony up, I asked for clarification and Calamity told me the whole story in order. So, Flores had called Julia and asked her to keep an eye out for Chalcedony if she came back, cause she seemed unwell. When she didn\u2019t come by, Calamity decided to go check up on her. She found Chalcedony agitated and pacing and smoking. See, she\u2019d gotten a weird phone call, with no one talking at the other end, just tones, and since then she felt foggy, wasn\u2019t thinking straight and couldn\u2019t concentrate. She didn\u2019t lose time or anything, but it was probably still the same thing, since Desiree had also gotten a phone call from a Private number just before she called Princess Joli to set up the date.<br /> <br /> So Calamity was going to stay the night and make sure nothing kicked in when she went to sleep, but first she called Becky to let her know what was going on, and Becky was really, really not happy. I guess after I went in with Desiree, Becky and Joli had an argument about Desiree coming to the Masquerade (Joli insists) and the two of them spending time together and everything. Princess Joli got mad enough that she told Becky to leave her be and not watch over her while she was at home, and Becky wasn\u2019t taking it well. I think Becky\u2019s in love with her too. Calamity likes Becky, so she went to go make sure Becky was alright, and took Chalcedony to the Dream House so Jacob could watch over her.<br /> <br /> So that was all exciting. Things seemed a little calmer after breakfast - Lori went to sleep it off some more, Jacob took a nap too, and me and Calamity headed off to tour the house the Masquerade was going to be in with the rest of the security team. That was Becky, of course, and Davey and Sandeval from the Spring Court. It was a little surprising to see Davey there, but he\u2019s a Mirrorskin, which does sound super useful for security stuff. TJ and a pair of dudes called Louis Guo and Ji Wen Ja were there from the Summer Court. Louis Guo and Ji Wen Ja seemed really cool. They introduced themselves to us later. Well, Louis did, cause Ji Wen Ja doesn\u2019t speak English. He can understand it, just not speak it. He\u2019s got a cool thing where he can make it so that no one can fight around him and he can calm situations, which is pretty handy. Louis was very careful to point out that they looked to the Viscount, specifically. And that TJ looked to Lucien. Politics stuff, but good to know, you know? I like the Summer Court in general, and I like Joan, but Lucien makes me... concerned, sometimes. So it\u2019s good to know there\u2019s another faction, I guess?<br /> <br /> The site itself was big. There were three dance rooms - a big ball room and a pair of smaller rooms set up, one for rave type stuff and one for other more modern dances - plus about 30 side rooms for liasons. The hallway between the dance rooms had a surveillance station that we had a key to. We had a key to all the rooms actually, though of course we\u2019re not to barge into a side room without an emergency. But if one of the silent alarms went off that were handed out to folks who wanted, that counted, and of course anything obvious.<br /> <br /> Becky also went over specific situations to watch out for, like Desiree and Chalcedony and Mary and whoever shot Dark Kimberly. Sandeval mentioned that the Warlock of Night had just today accepted the traditional invitation. That threw Becky for a loop and I almost felt bad bringing up Felicity, but it seemed important and pertinent with the Night Court having a bigger presence. Apparently she has a particular bad relationship with the Warlock\u2019s Handmaidens. They threatened to eat her, and not only in a good way. So we\u2019re just going to try and keep them apart, as best we can, you know? I gave her a call to warn her about that, and also let her know that it probably wasn\u2019t the Summer Court breaking in. I\u2019m still kinda hoping that her being away at the Masquerade will get whoever it is to make a move, and we can catch them out, either using Insincere Marguerite\u2019s mirror powers, or just regular security.<br /> <br /> After the tour, Calamity went off visit Annika. She had called Queen Charlotte to talk about some Court business, and the Queen had pointed out that maybe it wasn\u2019t the Director at all, but someone was targetting people of the Dancer kith. Since Annika is the only other one of those, Calamity offered to go warn her. On the way home though, so she could get her bike, she asked me if I really wanted to do the Greening. The way she said it at first I almost wasn\u2019t sure if she was trying to say she wasn\u2019t sure about it anymore, so I pulled over so I could actually talk. That\u2019s not what she was trying to say, I'm pretty sure now, but she started talking about there being other prettier, nicer, more dangerous girls and that she didn\u2019t want to force me into belonging to her, so I was glad I pulled over anyway. I held as close as I could there in the van, and told her of course I did, cause of course I did. I think all the craziness of not being able to figure something out and *do* something about it is getting to her again. I hope it\u2019s just that and not something I\u2019ve done that makes her think I might want someone else more.<br /> <br /> It makes me feel really bad that I\u2019ll be away again tonight, but I was so close... I think she understands. I hope she does. Jacob pulled her aside to spar after the show as I was leaving, which is really good of him, you know? I think that\u2019ll help even her out. The show did good too. Lori was less depressed - she sang a blues song, but it was Weird Al\u2019s \u2018Generic Blues\u2019, so it was as fun as anything else. She started out dressed in a long trenchcoat and wide brimmed hat, before throwing it off to reveal a sparkly dress. Captain Jack came by to make more plans, dressed in a long trench coat and wide brimmed hat too, so he could be incognito. He didn\u2019t have a sparkly dress underneath though. Since they were dressed so close to the same they decided to do an impromptu Stand by Your Man performance, which was awesome. Captain Jack is a great singer.<br /> <br /> He\u2019s also good at acquiring things - he managed to get a Playboy bunny outfit to fit him, through intimidation I guess. Oh right, I almost forgot to mention. Calamity decided a blue Playboy bunny outfit would be the best match for her Frank mask. I\u2019m not going to argue with that, for sure, though Captain Jack in that is going to be... special. We decided to do the whole scene about nine - late enough that folks would all be there, but not going to interfere with things like the Greening or anything.<br /> <br /> We talked some about the Warlock\u2019s Handmaidens too - he called them Thing 2 and Thing 1. They seem to be on good terms actually, though apparently it took a lot to get there. They were displeased that they couldn't seduce him, then failed at pranking them, but then they all three got rip roaring drunk together and now they\u2019re friends. According to their driver\u2019s licenses, they are married to each other, and according to Captain Jack, they are very ticklish. It was a very different conversation about them than I\u2019d had with anyone else, so it was good we talked with him. Also good so I don\u2019t misjudge any teasing that goes on between them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> June 14th<br /> <br /> Yes! I figured it out! Well, kinda. It was touch and go a bit, especially at first when I almost shattered her dreamspace hitching a ride. But I managed to keep it together and something kept pulling me backstage. Like, the whole dream was a stage, and I was in among the rigging and the machinery and curtain stuff. One of the control systems had holes around it, like someone strong was flailing around in the dark, and knew there was a switch but not quite where. It was in the off position when I found it, and when I flipped it, the scene completely changed on stage, to what looked like a dinner date, and a mannikin that looked kinda like Joli was on stage with Desiree, who was acting wooden all of the sudden. No, more like clockwork. Anyways, definitely different, you know?<br /> <br /> So it wasn\u2019t some kind of mind control directly, but an implanted thing. A piece of her psyche that was waiting to be switched. So, Manchurian candidate was the right idea, I guess. But whoever switched it didn\u2019t know what they were doing, which was why it was so clumsy. Like, they got her to go on a date with Joli but they couldn\u2019t cover it up well, so there was the lost time and the obvious threat. It clearly wasn\u2019t her Keeper, or whoever implanted the switch, who did it, just someone who figured it out.<br /> <br /> I even figured out I could get rid of the switch, though it\u2019d probably take a while. One of those Oneirophysics I\u2019d heard about might be able to fix it faster, but there weren\u2019t any of them around, that I knew of. But that means we could get rid of Chalcedony\u2019s switch, if it was the same thing, and anyone else who comes from the Director too, now that we know where to look, which is awesome!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> I am getting sick of starting these journal entries with sentences or paragraphs about how terrible I\u2019ve been feeling. This one really takes the cake, though. Tomorrow is the masquerade; I should be over the moon with excitement. It\u2019s one of the biggest events of the Spring, and since my Court really knows how to party, I imagine it\u2019s going to be spectacular.<br /> <br /> So my life started to go to shit yesterday about an hour before the show. I\u2019d been planning to do an upbeat number; something to really get the crowd clapping their hands and stomping their feet. Then D dropped by and asked to speak with me privately. I said sure and we walked into a currently unoccupied room and closed the door.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m not going to stay here tonight,\u201d she said glumly.<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay,\u201d I said, a little disappointed.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m going to get some vodka, a pack of sexy dude playing cards, and\u2026 probably something even stronger than the vodka,\u201d she continued. \u201cI\u2019m going to have a long conversation with myself. More of an argument, really. Then, myself and I are going to find my self-image, and my insecurities, and we\u2019re going to hash this whole thing out. I\u2019m probably going to yell, and I might cry. And if I have to, I\u2019m going to beat the shit out of that bitch until she sees the light. It won\u2019t be pretty. I don\u2019t know if I\u2019ll be back tomorrow or not, but I\u2019ll be here on Saturday, and I promise I\u2019ll have this whole thing worked out by then, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> I\u2019d been expecting her to have some sort of crisis/epiphany over her sexuality or her self-image for a few days, so it didn\u2019t really come as much of a surprise (though her wording of the situation threw me for a minute). \u201cD,\u201d I said softly, \u201cI know you need to do this, and I know you need to work through it on your own. But is there anything I can do to help you? Anything at all?\u201d<br /> <br /> She shook her head and thought about it for a moment. \u201cI might call you up and ask you to come over to my place tomorrow,\u201d she said eventually, \u201cand it\u2019s cool if you want to. But\u2026 don\u2019t have sex with me there, okay? Not even if I ask you to. If I show up here, it\u2019s fine\u2026 that means I\u2019ve worked things out already.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded in understanding. I know that Insincere Marguerite or Calamity\u2019s friend Tommy could be listening in on any conversation we had in the Dream House, so I leaned in, kissed her on the cheek, and whispered in her ear. \u201cI love you, Maria, and I will be waiting for you when you come back, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded, kissed me back, and turned to leave. \u201cI\u2019ll\u2026 I\u2019ll see you Saturday, if not sooner, okay Lori?\u201d she said without turning around. I acknowledged her statement briefly and then she was gone.<br /> <br /> I couldn\u2019t let myself fall apart; it was time for makeup and costumes. I talked with some of the girls and managed to arrange substitutions for all of the numbers except my solo near the end of the first set. I really wasn\u2019t in the mood to sing \u201cCopacabana\u201d or anything like that, so I spoke with Marguerite about a substitution. She raised an eyebrow at my selection and asked me if everything was alright, and I assured her that I would be fine, and then made my way backstage again.<br /> <br /> When my number came up, I walked out in a sedate blue evening gown. It was pretty enough, but not nearly as sexy as most of my outfits. I had my hair brushed out straight over one shoulder, and kept my eyes mostly lidded through the number to hide the sheen that I knew would show there. As the opening chords of Eric Clapton\u2019s guitar drifted softly from the house speakers, I began to sing.<br /> <br /> \u201cTears In Heaven\u201d came out years after I was taken, but I came across it when researching songs to generate sorrow as a favor for our friends in the Winter Court. It is beautiful, devastatingly sad, and the lyrics have almost nothing to do with my current situation, so it\u2019s not giving away anything personal. It seemed like a perfect choice. I put my all into that number, and infused it with a little glamour to ensure that everyone could feel the sorrow as keenly as I did. I admit it was a little spiteful of me, and I\u2019m kind of ashamed of it now, but they do say that misery loves company.<br /> <br /> After my number I retreated upstairs to my bedroom. I dug out a pair of warm, comfy flannel pajamas. They were a gift from D; kind of a gag gift since she of all people knows I almost never wear anything to bed. They were tailored by a Changeling I haven\u2019t met in Santa Monica who specializes in making clothing for those of us with \u201cinteresting\u201d physiques, so they have large slits cut in the back to accommodate my wings. They aren\u2019t simple tears in the fabric, either\u2026 the edges are doubled up and sewn so that the garment will stand up to use.<br /> <br /> They\u2019re a little baggy on me, and they\u2019re this ugly red tartan pattern. D claims that she gave them to me to prove that I would look sexy no matter what I was wearing. I love them.<br /> <br /> Calamity and Gawain knocked on my door a little while later. I was a bit surprised, because the show was still going on. Calamity explained that they were worried because it\u2019s not like me to leave the parlor before the end of a show, and Julia had told her that D was acting weird earlier. I told them that I was fine, but of course they didn\u2019t leave it at that. I wouldn\u2019t have left it at that if one of them was acting like I had been acting.<br /> <br /> I sniffled and wiped at my eyes. \u201cD is working through a few things. It\u2019s\u2026 not easy for her, and there\u2019s nothing I can do to help her through it, and I hate feeling helpless.\u201d<br /> <br /> They commiserated, but there wasn\u2019t really a lot they could do to help. I announced my intention to head downstairs after the crowds had dispersed and lay claim to a half-gallon of chocolate ice cream and a bottle of bourbon. Calamity and Gawain both told me that they\u2019d be happy to join me in a movie marathon while I drown my sorrows. I gave them a weak smile and told them that it sounded like a good plan to me.<br /> <br /> Didn\u2019t work out that way, unfortunately. Gawain got the call from Glamour Springs that he was welcome to try his oneiromancy on Desiree tonight, and Calamity got word that Chalcedony had been acting strangely at the Rose &amp; Thorn earlier in the evening, and went to check on her. When I came downstairs, only Jacob, Insincere Marguerite, and Julia were anywhere to be found (I have no idea where Ace went). Calamity actually called me to apologize for bailing, but I told her I knew that she had more important things to do.<br /> <br /> It was almost funny how quickly she got indignant at that statement, but I was in no mood to appreciate the humor. \u201cOkay, if not more important, then at least more immediate,\u201d I corrected myself. \u201cI understand, Calamity. Don\u2019t worry. You\u2019re off the hook, I promise.\u201d I think she might have been worried that I was still mad over the mudslinging incident. I hope I reassured her on that count.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t remember much of last night. I know Jacob started me off with a mudslide, which was very tasty, but did not deter me from dipping (deep) into the bourbon next. Julia was concerned about me and D, and I did my best to reassure her (and myself) that things would be fine. Insincere Marguerite seemed largely unconcerned, and spent most of her time being fed small slices of banana by Julia.<br /> <br /> Julia actually brought me a little pot when I idly asked if anyone had any. Just enough for one joint\u2026 just enough to get me a little mellow. What can I say? I just didn\u2019t want to think seriously about anything last night.<br /> <br /> I was completely shit-faced by the time Calamity showed up a couple of hours later with Chalcedony in tow. I don\u2019t really remember much of the encounter, but the others have since filled me in on the details. Apparently Chalcedony received a telephone call earlier that day, and heard a series of tones with no associated words. She said she hadn\u2019t felt quite right since; like her thoughts were fuzzy and unfocused, and she didn\u2019t trust her own judgment. It had been Calamity\u2019s intention to stay with Chalcedony at her place, just to ensure that she would be safe and wouldn\u2019t do anything unfortunate. But then Becky had some sort of crisis and needed a friend, so Calamity decided to drop Chalcedony off at the Dream House and go check on her pal.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m told I had a somewhat embarrassing conversation with Chalcedony, but I really don\u2019t remember it. She apparently asked if I was alright, and I blurted out all of my insecurities about how the girl I loved was off wrestling with her sexuality and I was afraid that she was going to dump me because I \u201cdon\u2019t have a dick,\u201d and how that would utterly destroy me. Wow\u2026 I didn\u2019t even know all that was in me. Understandably, Chalcedony chose to just retire to a guest room after that.<br /> <br /> Jacob made sure I got to bed okay, and made sure a big glass of cold water was on my nightstand to help with the next morning\u2019s inevitable hangover. I\u2019m pretty sure I didn\u2019t proposition him (or anyone else) last night; I was not in the mood for lovin\u2019 at all. I wanted D, but mostly I just wanted her to be there and to be okay.<br /> <br /> I woke up this morning (or early afternoon) with a splitting headache and a terrible taste in my mouth (I later described it as tasting \u201clike a skunk had dropped its ashtray in my mouth before it died\u201d). I staggered down to the kitchen, my hair a mess and drool drying on my chin. Jacob smiled sympathetically when I stumbled in and offered me a glass of orange juice with aspirin ground up in it. He also suggested that I should try to get some salt back in my system, so I shrugged, upended a shaker over the orange juice, and downed the whole glass. It was <u>vile</u>.<br /> <br /> I went back to bed for an hour or two. After the headache subsided, I spent the rest of the afternoon researching blues music, trying to come up with an act for the show that would suit my mood and still be club-appropriate. I came across a number of songs which seemed suitable, but I also came across something else which surprised me.<br /> <br /> I figured the best place to start looking was with the grand-daddy of all blues musicians, Mr. B. B. King himself. I came across an article online in which he listed what were, in his opinion, the ten best blues songs ever performed. I recognized some of them, and others were completely new to me. The biggest surprise came in the form of a song called \u201cGeneric Blues,\u201d by an artist with the unlikely name of Weird Al Yankovic.<br /> <br /> Hey, jazz and blues musicians have always had colorful nicknames. I didn\u2019t think anything of it at the time. But it turns out that Mr. Yankovic is a fairly famous parodist, and his \u201cGeneric Blues\u201d song was incredibly funny. I think it must have flipped a switch inside me or something, because I couldn\u2019t stop laughing for about five minutes. And that got me thinking\u2026 I\u2019d been obsessing over D\u2019s absence for a day, even though I know she\u2019s doing this for us, so that she can devote herself to our relationship wholeheartedly.<br /> <br /> I guess I really am as self-absorbed as people say. You have to laugh, right? It sure beats the hell out of being depressed for no good reason. I still miss her, and I know I will continue to miss her until we\u2019re back together for good. But I\u2019m not going to let it take over my whole life any more.<br /> <br /> D actually called a little while before the show. She sounded a little choked up. She said that she wouldn\u2019t be at the show tonight, and she wouldn\u2019t be staying here with me tonight either\u2026 but she also promised that she would come by the Dream House tomorrow before the masquerade, and that she would be whatever I needed her to be. I tried to be strong for her as I told her again that I\u2019d wait as long as she needed. I\u2026 hope she finds what she\u2019s looking for soon, though.<br /> <br /> I decided not to share my plans for the show with the rest of the motley, so I just gave Insincere Marguerite a thumb drive with instructions to play the file it contained when my solo came up, and just to throw a single spot on me when the music started. She was willing. I walked out on stage in a long coat (with my wings tucked in under it) and a broad-brimmed hat. Much to my surprise, Captain Jack was in the audience talking to Gawain\u2026 and he was wearing a nearly identical outfit. He gave me a mock-exasperated look, then a grin and a thumbs-up. When the music started, I threw off the jacket and the hat, revealing one of my usual spangly revealing dresses and launched into \u201cGeneric Blues\u201d with gusto.<br /> <br /> After the song was over, I walked down into the crowd and joined Gawain, Calamity, and Captain Jack at their table. \u201cWelcome back, Lori,\u201d Gawain said with a smile, and I felt like things were close to all right again. The Captain asked me if I\u2019d like to do a duet with him, so I put the coat and hat back on and had a quick word with Marguerite. A few minutes later we were belting out the Tammy Wynette classic \u201cStand By Your Man.\u201d It was a lot of fun, and seemed to be a comedic hit with the guests.<br /> <br /> So we talked a bit about what\u2019s been going on in the Freehold. Gawain is making progress with Desiree; he thinks another night or two will help him figure out what\u2019s going on with her (and maybe with Chalcedony as well). Becky\u2019s problem is mostly with Jolie\u2026 the Princess is so smitten with Desiree that she\u2019s ignoring Becky\u2019s (quite reasonable) safety precautions in regards to her new paramour, and that has Becky in a lather, both thinking that she\u2019s unappreciated and worried that the Princess is going to get hurt. Calamity and Gawain met with the security team for the masquerade earlier today, and have assured me that the location will be well protected. And Captain Jack has managed to find a Captain Jack-sized duplicate of Calamity\u2019s outfit, so the \u201centertainment\u201d we\u2019ve planned is still a go. We\u2019ve decided to spring the surprise around nine o\u2019clock\u2026 late enough that everyone should be there, but early enough not to interfere with the Greening or any of the other important business of the masquerade.<br /> <br /> After the show was over, I decided to make it an early night. I didn\u2019t get much restful sleep last night, and no matter what happens, tomorrow is going to be a long day. So I said my goodnights, came upstairs, and put those flannel pajamas back on. I\u2019ve been writing in this diary ever since. I think I\u2019m about done with it for now, and I find that I\u2019m more than ready to lie down and get some rest, no matter how lonely that big bed looks to me. I\u2019m confident that the next time I write in this diary, it\u2019ll be about how deliriously happy I am to be back with D, with the Greening proclaiming us a couple officially in the eyes of the Freehold.<br /> <br /> Oh please, God, let things go well.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T03:09:24-08:00","id":423936,"title":"","content":"<b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> <u><b><b><u>Friday June 13<sup>th</sup></u></b></b></u><br /> <br /> It's Friday the thirteenth but so far my luck is holding out. Let's just hope it continues to do so tomorrow. Thanks to Jacob I am well and truly worn out and no amount of worried thoughts are going to keep me from getting a good sleep so I should be bright eyed and bushy tailed at least. Well, fluffy tailed to be more accurate. Hey, if I am wearing a playboy bunny suit I am wearing the whole damn thing, detached cuffs and collar and cotton ball tail included. There is no half assing this shit, I walk in and own the ever-living fuck out of this or die trying. (okay, maybe not quite life and death, I'm not Ace.) And besides, if shit does go sideways pear-shaped I should be able to fight in it without ruining it or at least without it getting in my way like a long fru-fru skirt would. You know, like the red and black lace number Julia bought me yesterday. Though I certainly did look damn fine in that.<br /> <br /> Of course last night did not pan out in the way I think any of us expected it to. I still had thoughts of Anastasia on my mind and so when Lori came out and dropped 'Tears In Heaven\u201d on the room with the full force of her glamour backing it up it hit me hard. The whole room was transfixed and I just let my feet carry me to the bar and waved Jacob over to give me a drink. Gawain found me there before it was over, sipping and brushing the scar on my left palm from our blood bonding misadventure. He was, of course, concerned that I'd gotten some bad news or something but I assured him that it was just that the song had me thinking about her. Fuck. I miss her so much. I won't lie, there were times in Snow Globe that I slipped. I thought about giving up and being what They wanted if only to make the pain stop. I got so impossibly weary in body and soul. But I couldn't do it because I knew I'd forget her if I did and I could not let that happen. I was prepared to die for her memory. Now I know that the whole time she was being betrayed and tormented by the thing They replaced me with. They took so fucking much from me but Stasia is what I hate Them most for. It is why the Sinister Bitch has to die. I cannot, will not ever forgive what They and their thing did to my Stasia.<br /> <br /> Yeah. That's a deep fucking well of angst and bitterness there isn't it? And I keep brushing the scar, like suddenly it's new and unfamiliar. It's all I have left of her. I am not going to seek her. I'll avenge her but I won't find her. I mustn't. All I would do is reopen old wounds... hers and mine both. I need to let her go. Of course... I'm selfish and bad at that. I should have let Gawain go when he confessed his love for me. I should have turned him away. Should have lied and told him I didn't feel that way about him. It would have hurt him... but it would have set him free to find someone else. Someone better. Someone that deserves his kindness and his protection and his heart. But I was selfish. I was needful. I was greedy.<br /> <br /> And I'm doing the same fucking thing with Becky. I am not fucking blind. She is in fucking love with the gorram princess of the Spring Court. She's strong and she'd actually be good for Jolie. But the princess is completely hung up on Desiree after their date and night of sex. (I mean, hell's fucking bells the woman isn't THAT good...) I am starting to find myself with a bitter taste in my mouth when I think of Princess Jolie. Lori cares about her and not just because she's her monarch, but dammit, I fucking care about Charlotte and Becky.<br /> <br /> And when in the nine hells did it become my business who the Spring Princess is fucking? Jesus Christ on a fucking crutch, if the woman cannot decide who should be hammering her keys in the night by herself how in the ever loving hell can she be running the freehold and making life or fucking death decisions? She's not a gorram child. Now if only she'd woman the hell up and stop acting like one.<br /> <br /> Maybe I am not being fair to Jolie here but it's not my fucking job to be. If I'm what passes for a level headed voice of reason in this freehold then we are in serious fucking trouble. You know, Master Darke may be evil, but at least his personal life isn't a fucking national crisis. But that's why it's my fucking problem. Because someone has to steer this fucking train wreck and if I don't get involved then I'm at the mercy of whoever does and that means someone like Darke or Lucien or fuck maybe even Spidertoes is going to steer us right into crazytown while we're all distracted by this fucking high school bullshit instead of paying attention to things that matter. And here I thought the one good thing to come out of Snow Globe was that I got to skip high school... Silly monster. And fuck, it's not like I'm not right there playing the relationship game myself.<br /> <br /> Maybe it would be better if there wasn't just so damn much relationship chap going on. But after Lori's one soul devastating number, she was off to her room. Didn't wait for the end of the show and certainly skipped the usual post show socializing. Well, between that and the fact that her girl wasn't there set me and Gawain both to full ahead concerned. We headed up to her room and when she answered the door she was wearing a pair of red flannels. We asked her pretty directly what was wrong. She did open with a claim that she was fine but our skepticism kept her from really trying to just leave it at that. She explained that De La Rocha had not come because she was home dealing with her issues over being in love with another woman. I guess Snow Globe helped me out in that regard. I'm wicked and sinful and wanton and I don't care what anyone thinks about who or what I decide to fuck. (okay, I do care what Gawain thinks, but that's different. And... okay, maybe I also care a little what Becky thinks...) At any rate, DLR had assured her that she would have it sorted out before the Ball and that their Greening would still happen. I can understand, even though I care fuck all what the Freehold thinks about me and Gawain the fact that we're doing it matters because it matters to him. (And yes, it does mean something to me that he's going to announce his commitment and love to me in front of everyone and their fucking uncle.) So for her, I get that she needs to resolve her issues before doing that. And if she does, then it will mean things are better for her and Lori. I really, really, really hope she can manage to put her demons to rest. Because Lori is so fucking in love with that girl that it would kill her otherwise. And there is absolutely nothing I can do about it except hope that De La Rocha's love is stronger than her hangups. She did call tonight and promise that she would be there and that she'd be Lori's girl, which made Lori cheerier. Gods above and below, I hope she actually is.<br /> <br /> Needless to say, Lori was in no mood to come down before the crowd was clear and the house was ours. But she did say she was coming down to lay claim to booze and ice cream, which seemed fair enough as long as she was willing to let the rest of us at least try to cheer her up (and keep an eye on her). In the end, that fell on Jacob and Julia and Insincere Marguerite. Gawain got the word that things were ready for him to perform Oneiromancy for the Spring Court so he was off to sleep with Desiree. That was pretty much expected. But Julia had gotten a call from Flores to keep an eye out for Chalcedony. Apparently she'd been at the Rose and Thorn and acting kinda off. She'd left to go home but Flores wasn't sure and was worried. She didn't put in an appearance, but I decided to go check up on her since shit has been weird lately and all.<br /> <br /> I showed up at her house and made a quick circuit of the grounds. Finding no signs of another, I then went to knock on her door. Gawain had mentioned that her place was very blue but he really did not do justice to just how completely blue it was. (Suffice it to say, I had to catch myself from humming that damned Abba de abba da song out loud.) Chalcedony herself was clearly a bit out of it. She let me in after I explained what had prompted me to come by. Once I pointed out that her condition seemed suspicious on the heels of Desiree's incident she did get concerned. She'd gotten a call that consisted only of tones that had set her off. No words and no response to her attempts to speak to them. And after that, she was hazy and off. She'd gone to the Rose and Thorn looking for Ginny to talk to her about the Masquerade. And I took that opening to ask her about Ginny. Maybe it wasn't proper to do so while she wasn't thinking clearly but I was not going to let the chance slip away without trying to figure out her intentions. Apparently it boils down to Chalcedony enjoys having sex with Ginny despite not usually being inclined but she's not anywhere near as deeply into Ginny as the other woman is of her and she does care enough to not want to lead her on but also doesn't really want to hurt her by ending things. It was a relief to find out where she stood. She was looking to crash out and hopefully sleep off the last of the weird feeling and to go and speak to Becky at Glamour Springs in the morning. I suggested she might want someone close to keep an eye on her in case of odd behavior or a follow up from whomever had tried to whammy her. She agreed, mainly because I suggested it I think. I told her I would make a couple of quick calls and got her permission to call Becky about it.<br /> <br /> My plan was to let my motley know I was staying and to give Becky a head's up. But Becky was clearly upset. She'd been arguing with Jolie and the princess had ended up telling her to stay the fuck away from her that night and left in a huff. Seriously... it would have served her right if someone had attacked her that night.... But Becky was on edge and headed home to get drunk so I was already double booked on more pressing business than doing something regretable. So I offered to come over and keep Becky company. After she declined I informed her I was coming over to keep her company anyway. Then I called the house and spoke to Lori, apologizing for bailing on her. She wasn't so far gone that she didn't understand and when I explained the situation she made a reference to saving throws... At some point (perhaps when there are only one or two disasters looming) I am going to have to inquire further about her about her knowledge of D&amp;D. At any rate, she had the folk better suited to taking care of her there anyway. I made sure Jacob was making sure she didn't try to leave or do anything dangerous while intoxicated. I also made sure he would be okay watching Chalcedony and he agreed to given the situation. I dropped her off and with all settled I headed for Becky's house.<br /> <br /> I pulled up and parked my bike in her drive. I sprang up the walk and knocked on her door and in the few moments before she answered it finally hit me that I had no fucking clue what exactly I was going to do to help. She opened the door and told me again that I really didn't need to do this. But I did need to and I told her as much so she let me in. She was frustrated but it was manifesting as depression rather than anger for the most part. Jolie was being unreasonable and irresponsible with her own safety. And clearly it was bothering Becky not just as a matter of her duty but because she's in fucking love with that damn woman. She did a lot of venting and ranting while I did a lot of listening. It honestly did seem to help her just to get some of it out of her system and that made me happy. I mean, I hated seeing her upset but I was able to be there and help. I am glad I was there, she really did not need to be alone. Not that I think she would have done anything stupid, but she was able to get some of it out and have the support of a friend. She kept apologizing for being poor company but I waved it off. I told her I was her friend. I told her I was glad to be there.<br /> <br /> And toward the end of the evening, I even told her something I shouldn't have. She'd been asking the mostly rhetorical why would Jolie do something that reckless and I'd just offered the one thing I know to be absolutely true when it comes to relationships. I told her that love makes people stupid. And then, not five fucking minutes later as she was apologizing yet again for her mood and being so not fun I said it. I told her it was okay. I told her I was there for her because I cared and that when you cared for someone you did things that weren't fun because they needed you to. Then... Then I told her I would do stupid things for her.<br /> <br /> Fuck me. I fucking told her I would do stupid things for her. And as I did I realized what the fuck I was saying but not before the words where free of my lips and out there. And I meant it. I knew I meant it as soon as I said it. Damn but I hate when my mouth gets ahead of my brain. I mean, I've had feelings for her since that night we spent together but I hadn't admitted it was like that yet. And there it was, dropped on her right in the middle of all the shit she was already trying to sort out. She just smiled at me and didn't say anything about it. But she's not dumb. I know she did not miss it. And it's not that I am not okay with her knowing I have feelings for her, but it was the shittiest timing to hit her with something like that. Or... maybe it wasn't. Maybe it was a comfort to know I cared more than just as a friend. But it was most certainly not the time to bring it up. The silence was there, a pause as it sank into us both but then, ever smoothly, she picked the conversation up and deftly let it slip quietly behind us. She told me she was tired and invited me to stay but made it subtly though firmly clear she wasn't up for any sort of sex.<br /> <br /> I assured her I wasn't there for that but that I would very much like to stay with her. We changed for bed and I gathered her up. I kissed her on the forehead, lightly and softly and drew her to lay her ear to my chest and the sound of my heartbeat. She fell into a deep sleep pretty quickly, the sort that comes from being emotionally and physically drained. I stayed awake. I rested and stroked her wonderful hair. It stirred and stroked back. That is such a strange sensation but I really like it. And once again I did find myself wondering about her past. She did not become the gloriously sensuous creature she is by chance. We don't often speak of our Keepers and our time in Arcadia. It's the most deeply personal part of us. I've told people that I am from Snow Globe but only a few have any idea just what I endured there. (And much of that came while I was smashingly drunk and speaking way too freely) I want to know if only to know how to avoid her scars. More than that... I want her to trust me enough to share that part of herself with me.<br /> <br /> Fuck, this is so not good. I am on the eve of what amounts to announcing my engagement to Gawain and I'm having these feelings. Someone I care about is lonely and hurting and I want so badly to be there for her... but not as a friend. I want her. I want this glorious dragon lady succubus to be mine. Zod, I am such a greedy monster. I need to stop this. I need to avoid her tomorrow. I need to stop thinking of what I would do to her in one of those private rooms. Of slipping my fingers into that amazing hair and curling a fistful of it as I shove her hard against a wall and hiss into her ear. The way that silken steel would grip back around my hand and wrist as I tell her exactly what filthy and perverse things I am going to do to her and slide my other hand down her body to feel exactly how eagerly she responds to each and every dark promise that drips from my lips.<br /> <br /> No. Tomorrow is about Gawain. It is about making sure the meeting between Charlotte and the Warlock of Night goes undetected. It is about keeping the Handmaidens and Felicity separate so nothing interrupts the Ball. It is about watching for any sort of action by whomever shot Dark Kimberly trying to disrupt the event. It is about watching Desiree and Chalcedony and making sure they're safe and themselves. It is about making sure that Mary does not decide to nibble on anyone or get hassled for what happened to her. It is about being there to witness De La Rocha and Lori's Greening. It is not about my selfish desires.<br /> <br /> The morning came too soon. I would have been content to lay there with my pale goddess slumbering in my arms all day. But Becky was awake early and off to make sure Jolie was alright. It might have caused a flicker of jealousy in my twisted dark heart to see her worry and know it was more than duty that spurred her on but I made sure not to let anything show. I was smiles all the way up to my deceitful eyes. She did look better for the night's rest and I didn't hide my pride in having been part of the reason for that. Becky said she'd be by to pick Chalcedony up from the Dream House once she'd checked on the princess.<br /> <br /> I rode home, wrapped in my own thoughts. My meeting with Becky and the rest of the security to go over the site was coming up and the final arrangements for the negotiations between Charlotte and the Warlock would follow that. I got back to find Lori as hung over as I've ever seen her. Poor dear went pretty damn hard last night. But the others had kept an eye on her. Jacob was looking a bit rough from watching her and Chalcedony and he was trying to explain things to Gawain when I got there. I picked up that task as Chalcedony came up from the secure guest room and before Becky had come to collect her everyone was up to speed on developments. Gawain's dream seeking had gone well and he was sure that he'd have it with another night.<br /> <br /> Lori and Jacob both decided to grab some more well needed rest as Gawain and I left to meet the other security folk and get the run down of the site. The place is big, a nice rental mansion affair. One huge main ballroom and a pair of smaller but still impressive rooms take up most of the main floor. The upper floors have thirty rooms that are being prepared and stocked for private use. According to Becky they only expect to need about twenty of them but better to be prepared than to run short on sex rooms. There are cameras in the ballrooms and hallways but not the restrooms or private rooms. The main station is somewhat central on the first floor and we'll all have access to it.<br /> <br /> And we is Becky, Gawain and myself of course. From the Spring we've also got Davey (who is a mirror-skin as it turns out, rather useful to know and apparently not common knowledge as folk tend to be distrustful of someone that can be other people for some reason) and Sandeval (who seemed fairly level headed and experienced with the work). And we have a trio from the Summer Court. My new friend TJ (who was every bit as genteel and charming as ever but if the excrement hits the rotary air circulation device he'll be good to have ready) and a pair of Asian Changelings who introduced themselves as Louis Guo and Ji Wen Ja. They certainly seem to be a pretty solid team. Ji Wen Ja is something of a monk and can among other things drain the hostility from a crowd which seems like a tremendously useful ability for this event. Louis is a talker and seemed alert and ready. They made a point of mentioning that they answer to the Viscount while TJ is Lucien's man-pig. I filed that tidbit away for later use. <br /> <br /> Once we'd gotten the layout, Becky started to go over details of import. There will be silent alarms issued to whomever wishes one and security is more or less supposed to stay out of the private rooms unless one goes off. Apparently, it has been known for people to use them to try to arrange a hook up with one of the security members but we should discourage this behavior (though perhaps a bit more gently than the pummeling TJ seemed to favor).<br /> <br /> She went over some of the more specific concerns and that was when things got uncomfortable. The Warlock's last minute acceptance came to light and the presence of her Handmaidens. And I could not speak about why they were there so concern about their intentions was running high. And apparently Becky had not been made aware of Felicity's invitation so it was a double whammy of Day and Night courtiers. Becky was seriously stressing over the last minute guests and I felt almost sick watching her and keeping quiet. But there was nothing to be done and when she asked about speaking to Insincere Marguerite about the members of her court I agreed to set things up. It did at least seem to amuse her more than further concern her when I gave her the head's up about Captain Jack and Gawain\u2019s planned hijinks. It would not do for someone to mistake the good Captain's intentions when he snatches up a member of the security team after all.<br /> <br /> I took some time to look for the best options for a discreet meeting. There is no avoiding the cameras but disabling any of them even for a brief time would be too risky. I took a minute to call and update my Queen and she told me Willow Black was going to be by the Dream House that night to handle the last details.<br /> <br /> Speaking to the Queen did give me a good excuse to visit Annika. She pointed out that both Chalcedony and Desiree were dancers and that Annika was the only other one in the freehold. It seems unlikely to me that it's dancers being targeted but it was worth giving a warning and it gave me a good reason to see her.<br /> <br /> As we were heading back so I could grab my bike I told Gawain I needed to talk to him about the Greening. He pulled over before he answered and turned to give me a close look. He was clearly concerned and I quickly explained that I wasn't unsure about committing myself to him but I wanted to be sure he really wanted to declare himself mine in front of everyone. I mean, this is a major event and it is pretty seriously focused on cutting loose and getting sexed up down and sideways. There will be a lot of women there, women prettier than me and nicer than me and hell even more dangerous than me if that's what he wants. And I don't want him to give up the chance to enjoy time with them for me. He shook his head and he hugged me and kissed me as he told me I was the one he wanted. I relaxed a bit, but I could see that he was still a bit worried. I thought I'd explained clearly that I wasn't getting cold feet or anything. Fuck, I hope he doesn't think I'm doubting him? Shit... I still don't know how to do this relationship thing properly and I'm thinking of complicating it by pursuing Becky? I really am fucking insane. Being bisexual means I get to have a boyfriend OR a girlfriend, not one of each.<br /> <br /> Well, after that I rode over to speak to Annika. She was pleased to see me and invited me in for brandy and cigars. I took her up on both quite gladly. The house shows even more of Kimberly's influence, not a stray bottle in sight even in the side rooms. I settled in and relaxed a moment in small talk with Annika. Then I brought up the recent attacks on both Desiree and Chalcedony. I explained that we were not completely sure of the connection and that one possibility was that they were both dancers, like Annika. She asked what she should do as far as precautions and when I mentioned the phone calls she remarked about having a phone. A landline of course, with an old rotary dial on it. But even that could carry the signal to her and so I warned her to hang up immediately on any call that consisted of tones just in case. I did mention that I doubted that dancers was the pattern but felt better warning her just in case. Then I moved on to the other reason for my visit. I did open by explaining that I didn't want to be suspicious of Madam Spidertoes but I was suspicious by nature. She did agree that she was certainly the most knowledgeable about her former lover. She was also already aware of the pending alliance between us and the Night Court. When I mentioned what I had heard concerning Spidertoes very adamant support of that agreement, she did seem to find it odd. She wasn't aware of any history between Spidertoes and the Night Court (or if she was she choose not to share it with me) and agreed that obviously Spidertoes was up to something but that she had no ideas what. She then pointed out that concerning myself in politics was a road to paranoia and frustration and trouble. I can't say that in that moment I didn't envy her total lack of concern. But I fear I don't have it in me to ignore what's going on around me. We concluded with a happier topic, the Masquerade. She hasn't attended one in years but will be there tomorrow with her dear Kimberly. She asked me if she could help me with any of this business I'm caught up in but I initially said no. I didn't want to try to drag her into any of it really. But before I left I did make a request of her. I told her I'd love to see her enjoy herself at the Ball. She chuckled and assured me she had every intention of doing so. It was a nice note to end our chat on and I rode back feeling a little better.<br /> <br /> Back at the dream house I had a bit of time to get ready for the show and let Insincere Marguerite know what was going on with the meeting. I also let her know Becky was coming so she would be prepared. She seemed confident (of course, if she didn't I would be seriously worried.) And when Becky arrived just before the show she managed to quite promptly put her off guard before they retired to speak in private. Becky left not much later looking flustered and I swallowed a pang of guilt (and certainly not jealousy). I did take a moment to speak to my darkling sister and point out that I was rather fond of Becky. I don't think she entirely got why it was bothering me. She pointed out that while what we were doing was certainly clandestine it wasn't actually wrong on any level. And she's right. Still, lying (even if it's just by omission) to Becky isn't something I like doing. And I expressed just how firmly I wanted to make sure things went seamlessly tomorrow. That part Insincere Marguerite was completely on board with at least.<br /> <br /> Captain Jack put in an appearance at the show. But it's okay, he was wearing a fedora and long coat so no one knew who it was. He'd come to let us know he had his costume and to make sure we ironed out the final details for tomorrow. It was refreshingly light hearted. And apparently he knows Scarlet and Natalia. They got frustrated at being unable to seduce him and there was apparently pranks and drinking that resulted in everyone parting on more or less good terms. He did have some useful tidbits to share. They are legally married. They are very ticklish. And they do not like the nicknames Thing One and Thing Two. All filed away for later use.<br /> <br /> As we were speaking, Lori came out for her number in... a long trench coat and fedora. There was a moment. But then she launched into her song, which was Weird Al's 'Generic Blues' and had the room laughing and grinning. Afterward, she came down and joined the conversation for a bit before she and El Capitan decided to sing a duet of \u201cStand By Your Man\u201d that upped the mood even further. It was a really nice break and it was damn good to see Lori in a more positive mood again.<br /> <br /> Things continued to go well from there. Willow Black made her appearance. I slipped out to meet with her and Insincere Marguerite. She wanted to keep things quick, apparently she'd left Scarlet and Natalia alone and was afraid that if she didn't get back to them soon they'd get into trouble. She was not particularly fond of them apparently and generally spoke of them like they were unruly children. The meeting will be late enough that no one finds it suspicious that folks are slipping away but not so late that everyone has thinned out too much. I shared my recommendations for the most inconspicuous rooms. Apparently Thing One and Thing Two will be the distraction as they behave the way everyone expects Night Courtiers to and keep attention away from the meeting between Charlotte and the Warlock.<br /> <br /> After the show, Lori again headed to bed early but seemed alright. Missing her love to be sure but not as worried and upset as last night. Handsome was off to Glamor Springs to continue the Oneiromancy. He seemed a little reluctant to leave me but we both knew that he needed to continue or risk losing the headway he'd made. And helping Desiree is something that means a lot to him. I certainly get that. And as I was assuring him I'd be fine and wishing him a good night's work Jacob came over to ask me about sparring. Oh was that music to my little monster ears and I quite happily accepted. Gawain finished his goodbyes and I headed up to change and meet Jacob out back.<br /> <br /> We've never sparred at night before, we almost always hit it in the early afternoon when we're both well-rested and before it's time to get ready for the nightly show. But I think he'd picked up on the fact that I was slightly more tense than Ulysses' bowstring. In hindsight, I was tired before we even started, having pushed myself without any actual sleep the night before. But the opportunity to lose myself in a good fight was too tempting.<br /> <br /> We worked into it like always. I don't think many would call it a slow build, at least not until they'd seen us when we really get going. The more familiar we get with each other the faster and harder our fights get. It was a glorious dance. Once we were at it my mind went to that place where there was nothing beyond right fucking now and my body was singing from the exertion. No worries, no guilt, no second guessing. We traded a few light touches as always.<br /> <br /> But pretty soon, way too damn soon for my liking, I started to feel myself lagging. I had been running on willpower and coffee more than anything before we even started. The burn and hum in my muscles started easing into aching and it took more and more effort to keep myself moving full tilt. But I didn't want to stop and I thought I had a bit more in me, a few more passes at least. Jacob asked me as we were circling between clashes if I'd gotten any sleep at all last night. I admitted I had not and he just nodded and kept going. I should have stopped or at least slowed the pace down.<br /> <br /> But I wanted to keep going and I wanted it enough that I convinced myself I was still good to keep going even though I knew better. We kept at it a bit longer until I was seriously feeling the strain. And that's when I fumbled. He was coming in fast and low and I started to spin and sidestep. His eyes followed my movement, flicking to my razorhands, one low and one higher. He shifted his weight, preparing to pivot and turn the thrust into a slash as he passed, a move that would force me to step back far enough to avoid it that I wouldn't be in reach to cut him while he was off balance from the lunge. Only my body was two steps behind rather than ahead. Jacob's eyes flickered with surprise as it suddenly became clear that I was actually still going to be there when his knife reached me. He shifted abruptly, twisting his arm and knife away from us both and crashed into me shoulder first.<br /> <br /> I was off kilter to begin with and so was he at that point. So down we went in a graceless tumble. I landed hard enough to snap one of my shards off almost at the skin (fuck did that hurt like a bitch... it's still throbbing as I write this.) Jacob came down on top of me and for a moment we just laid there before we started to untangle ourselves and help each other up. As we started to check each other for injuries I managed to break the quiet with a quip about how I generally preferred to be the one on top.<br /> <br /> As it turned out, I ended up with a fairly good nick from his knife despite his best efforts and a lovely bruise from his shoulder. But Jacob still got the worse of it with a couple of long though thankfully shallow cuts from my glass. Thankfully, nothing needed stitches (or rousting Lori for her healing magic). So the first aid kit was brought out and we took turns cleaning and bandaging each other.<br /> <br /> I was rapidly moving into sore and a little shaky, clear proof that I'd pushed myself past a reasonable point. Jacob didn't say anything, but I know he noticed. I admitted that I'd pushed too hard and apologized to him for not calling a stop sooner as I worked on his shoulder. I also thanked him for the workout. Even with things flowing back in I'm feeling clearer than I was and I know that once I finish this and stretch out I am going to be dead to the world. Once we were both patched up and sipping some water, I asked him how he was doing, more to remind him that I was available than to try to get him to open up any. I believe he will talk to me at some point, but not until he's ready. And I like to think it helps for him to know I'm willing when that time comes.<br /> <br /> But tonight was not the night. He said he was fine and I moved to thanking him again for watching things while I was busy seeing to Becky last night. Then we slipped into a comfortable silence and cleaned up before biding each other goodnight.<br /> <br /> Tomorrow is going to be a long night. I have more irons in the fire than I'd like but so far everything looks like it might just go off without a hitch. But if I hope to keep it that way I am going to have to bring my S+ game. And that means I have to stop putting off crawling into this empty bed alone. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Tonight was odd all around. Lorelei seemed a bit down before she went on stage, and then proceeded to sing an utterly depressing song. \u201cTears of Heaven\u201d I think it was called. Not a dry eye in the house after that number. Great for us Winter courtiers, but not so much for the others. I will admit that I did take advantage of all the sorrow in the room and re-centered myself. I felt a bit more invigorated after that song. The customers not so much. Though it did good things for the drink sales.<br /> <br /> During Lori\u2019s sad song Calamity came to the bar to get a drink. Apparently she was not unaffected by the song or the little bit of power that Lori put into it. We talked for a bit, and Gawain came over to join us. After the song was over, Lori walked off stage and headed straight upstairs. It\u2019s not like her to just blow off the rest of her numbers, so we figured that something was wrong. As if the downer of a song wasn\u2019t hint enough. So, I offered to keep an eye on the crowd while Calamity and Gawain checked in on our resident songstress. <br /> <br /> Turns out that De la Rocha is taking a day or so to work out her issues, presumably about being involved with a woman. I know that De la Rocha has had these issues since she first started dating Lorelei. I thought that she had made peace with herself about the whole same sex lover thing already, but apparently not. I understand that she needs to figure things out, but she probably could have done it in a better way. Lori looked like a wreck when she was going upstairs. Calamity and Gawain said she wasn\u2019t looking too good either. Apparently her plans for after the show included chocolate ice cream and bourbon. I decided then that I would do my part to help Lori feel better, even if she wouldn\u2019t thank me in the morning. <br /> <br /> So, after the show and all the customers left, Lorelei came downstairs and started to raid the freezer for ice cream. I convinced her that I had a better option for her, so I went about getting the ingredients for a frozen mudslide. Not strictly by the book, but I think it tastes better if you make it with chocolate ice cream. I frosted the glass first then went about making the drink. I think Lori liked it. At least the way she was licking her lips after she drank it said as much. I tried to keep her interested in mixed drinks so I could control how much alcohol she drank, but she went back to the bottle of bourbon. She didn\u2019t even get a glass. I knew that wasn\u2019t going to end well, but there wasn\u2019t much I could do to stop her unless I took the bottle from her. I think she took the rest of the ice cream with her too.<br /> <br /> But before I get too ahead of myself. Calamity called me tonight, before Lori absconded with the liquor, to say that she needed to drop Chalcedony off at the dream house so she could take care of Becky. Long story short, Julia approached Calamity to let her know that Chalcedony had been acting odd. Calamity went to Chalcedony\u2019s house to make sure that everything was okay. Turns out that it wasn\u2019t. Chalcedony told Calamity that she had received a strange phone call. No voice, just strange sounds/tones. Then after that she said that her head felt fuzzy and it was really hard to concentrate. Kind of sounded like what happened to Desiree, but didn\u2019t work entirely. <br /> <br /> Calamity wanted to keep an eye on Chalcedony, but while she was at the fuzzy headed girl\u2019s apartment she called Becky to check on Desiree. She apparently got an earful of Becky ranting about the Princess and Desiree, and was really upset and feeling marginalized. Calamity then had two young ladies who both needed attention. So, she called me and said that she was going to bring Chalcedony by the Dream House and asked if I could keep an eye on her over night to make sure that she didn\u2019t try to do anything strange, or that nothing happened to her. I said that was fine, and that she should see to her friend.<br /> <br /> My sparring partner dropped off Chalcedony, who I invited to join Lori and the rest of us for drinks. She said that she was just tired and wanted to go to sleep. That was fine. I showed her to the basement guestroom. I figured that if she tried to leave, or if she sleep walked or anything she\u2019d have to go past me to do it. So, after Lori finally went upstairs to pass out, I stayed downstairs and read or flipped through TV channels. <br /> <br /> I will admit that I felt bad for both Desiree and Chalcedony. Something is definitely going on with them and it\u2019s taking away their self-control. That is kind of scary in and of itself, but being made to do stuff that you don\u2019t remember later. That\u2019s not good. Whatever is going on likely has something to do with their Keeper, but I don\u2019t know if the Keeper is the one messing with them now. You\u2019d think that such a canny guy would cover his tracks better. It\u2019s obvious that something is going on with those girls. If I had been the one to make them do stuff for me you better believe I\u2019d be a lot more subtle about it. At least the Lady never messed with my head in that way. Not to say that she didn\u2019t mess with my head. She did, but it was more psychological. She used fear, pain, hunger, all that stuff to get the desired result out of me. It wasn\u2019t exactly subtle. I don\u2019t know if the Lady \u201cdoes\u201d subtle. It was effective though. Can\u2019t say that it wasn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know what it is that changed in me when I met Delight Diane and others in her freehold, but something did. I guess the best way to describe it, is that something in me thawed. I felt things again, well, at least stronger than I had in a very long time. Sometimes I miss that numbness that surrounded me when I was in the Lady\u2019s service. I didn\u2019t really think about the consequences of my actions, I just knew that I was doing right and making Her happy. Now\u2026.now I can\u2019t stop seeing the faces of those that I wronged or killed over the years. I see them when I close my eyes. I see them in the faces of people in the crowd at the club, or in strangers walking down the street. I feel a pain deep inside me that won\u2019t go away. Sometimes it lessens a bit. Sometimes I can put it out of my mind if I\u2019m focusing on something else, but it never really goes away. Sometimes it is so tempting to go back to her realm, and beg forgiveness so I can get that blessed numbness back. Sometimes.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> So, today was a pretty good day. It started with Lorelei coming downstairs hungover. I had left water and aspirin on her nightstand last night (or early this morning) figuring that she\u2019d need it. I think she did drink it, but brought the aspirin downstairs with her. We got her some juice and she put the pills in it. Then Gawain said something about salt being good for hangovers so she added that too. Not the most appetizing thing, but she drank it down. Hopefully it helped her in some way. I myself have found that equilibrium that lets me get mostly drunk, at least pleasantly buzzed, and not get a hangover in the morning. It works most of the time. Though, I do admit that sometimes I say \u2018fuck the equilibrium\u2019 and get trashed out of my head. Sometimes I need it I think. Not the healthiest way to deal with my issues, but it\u2019s working for now.<br /> <br /> Gawain guessed that I\u2019d been up all night since it was obvious from the coffee grounds in the trash that the morning pot was not the first one I\u2019d made today. It\u2019s those early morning, getting close to dawn hours that are the hardest for me. Maybe it just makes me realize just how long I\u2019ve been up and my body reminds me that it\u2019s tired. So, coffee was my friend. I admitted that I\u2019d been up all night and explained why. I may not have been the clearest in my explanation of things. It certainly felt complete at the time I was saying it, but looking back I can see the gaps. When she got back, I think Calamity filled in her beau about the details of what happened a little later.<br /> <br /> It wasn\u2019t that long before Becky showed up to collect Gawain and Calamity to go over security measures for the Masquerade ball. I was tempted to volunteer for security detail, but decided not to at the last minute. Not sure why now that I think about it. Dances can be fun and all that, but I don\u2019t do a whole lot of dancing. I do like people watching though. It\u2019s interesting to see interactions with folks and how it differs from person to person and group to group. I suppose if I\u2019m not busy paying attention to safety issues then I\u2019ll have more time to just watch people. I do want to dance a little bit. Maybe Insincere Marguerite would like to dance?<br /> <br /> Early this afternoon I took the opportunity to get a bit of sleep. I figured if I was going to be able to stay awake for the show tonight and mix drinks without dropping bottles, I would need some shut eye. When I got up I did something that has been on my mind for a while now, but I haven\u2019t had the guts to do. I looked for any trace of Brandon Mills. I looked online and in the phone book. He actually has a listing in the book. I found it in L.A. Not somewhere that I can ride my bike to unfortunately. I\u2019ll need to get a car for that trip. I had thought about asking Gawain to borrow his van, but I didn\u2019t really want to take him with me. I need to get my license and my own car. Then I can make the trip myself and not have to explain things to the others. I\u2019ve been saving up some money from my side job, and hopefully will have enough to buy a used car out of the paper. Maybe a jeep. I\u2019ve always wanted a jeep.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t honestly know what I\u2019m going to do when/if I find Brandon. As long has he hasn\u2019t strengthened his mask I should be able to tell by looking if he is a Changeling or the fetch. Of course that is not substantial evidence. If I find a fetch, then I know one of two things, that Brandon is still in Arcadia, or that he\u2019s out and has taken a new name. Still leaves me not knowing where he is. I\u2019m not sure that I could just go around asking local Changeling\u2019s if they\u2019ve seen anyone that sort of looks like Brandon used to, but fuzzier. The last time I saw Mills he looked to be on his way to becoming an ogre or beast. Big, hairy and strong. He could still be in the area, or he could have moved far away. If he\u2019s nearby though, and I start asking after him it might draw a bit more attention my way than I\u2019d like. If someone tells him that a skinny guy with white hair and frost on his face was looking for him, I\u2019m not sure what he\u2019d do. He was a big kind of guy when I met him the first time. It was one of the reasons I chose him. Skinny little me tricking the big, strong jock into the Lady\u2019s realm where the tides could turn. He\u2019d be the weak one and I\u2019d be strong. Yeah, kind of messed up there.<br /> <br /> Okay\u2026back to track, so to speak. Tonight at the show everything went pretty much like normal, except one number where Lorelei walked out wearing a floppy hat and a trenchcoat. The look was not the most attractive on her and I wondered what she was up to. Then she threw off the outer wear and was wearing a spangly low cut dress underneath I thought it was a nice change up from what she normally did on stage and the audience appreciated the reveal. Yeah, they definitely appreciated the reveal. The thing that kind of tied the whole evening together in a funny kind of way was when Captain Jack showed up at the club wearing a disguise of a floppy hat and a trenchcoat. He was actually here to talk to Gawain about their plans for the ball, but it turned into more than that. Both he and Lori got on stage and did a number together, and to pull it together they both wore their long trenchcoats and floppy hats. For their number they decided to do \u201cStand by Your Man.\u201d It was good. They make a good duet, but at the same time it was funny. I couldn\u2019t help it. I laughed a bit at the bar while watching them on stage.<br /> So after the show I asked Calamity if she wanted to spar. She\u2019s been acting kind of stressed out all day and I could tell that she was just itching for a way to release all that pent up frustration. Unfortunately Gawain wasn\u2019t going to be able help with this. Calamity needed to be able to enact physical violence on something or someone. I decided to be that someone. I know, I\u2019m such a good friend to let her beat the snot out of me. Well, to try anyway. Each of us gives as good as we get.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T03:10:13-08:00","id":423937,"title":"","content":"The match went much like most of our matches. We did a brief warm up period where we attacked and defended but it was all really sedate. It was obviously just to get in the \u201cgroove\u201d, so to speak. Then the sparring started in earnest. Despite the long day and long night Calamity was just as spry as usual. To start with anyway. The fight started off fast and furious. I got a nick in here and she got a nick in there. It was gradual, but I noticed that Calamity was slowing down. I asked in between strikes if she\u2019d managed to get a bit of shut eye since yesterday. She said no. I replied with an \u201cokay,\u201d and kept going. I kept an eye on her after that to be on the safe side. Well, I thought I kept a good enough eye on things. I will admit that I got caught up in the moment and fought on the same level that we usually did. Then things kinda went south. I lunged for Calamity\u2019s ribs. That magic spot that will incapacitate but not necessarily kill, when it happened. She fumbled. Calamity actually stumbled as she went to evade my attack and it was all I could do to not hit her. I twisted my body as far as I could to keep the knife away from her, but could not stop the momentum. I ended up slamming into her shoulder with mine and we both went tumbling. I tried to keep the knife aimed away from her, and would have just dropped it if I could, but that would lead to her definitely getting hit. As it was, I think I just scratched her as we fell into a heap.<br /> <br /> During this whole mess I discovered just how sharp those glass shards of hers are. Pretty sharp by the way. I got a couple of good cuts out of that little fall. I think we were both shocked for a second that we\u2019d ended up on the ground, and then a second later we both snapped out of it and helped each other up. I checked to see if I\u2019d cut her or hurt her when I hit. She had a small nick from my blade and will likely have a bruise from me slamming into her shoulder, but other than that she\u2019s okay. Hopefully Gawain won\u2019t be upset with me. Though I\u2019m sure he understands that accidents are going to happen when you spar with live steel.<br /> <br /> So, we got the first aid box and I helped Calamity clean and bandage her cut, and she helped bandage the ones on my shoulder that I couldn\u2019t reach. She apologized for the error on her part as she taped the gauze down, and seemed a bit embarrassed, but no more than any other time she\u2019s made a mistake. She was definitely more at ease after our practice, so I think my idea worked to help her work out that pent up frustration that she had and channel her need for violence in a way that didn\u2019t hurt any innocents.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll admit that sparring with Calamity can be a bit of a gamble. Not that I think that she\u2019d intentionally harm me or anything. Not without good reason anyway. It\u2019s more that I\u2019m afraid of having one of those little flashbacks of mine and screwing up at exactly the wrong time. Though I suppose I\u2019m living every day taking that chance, so sparring shouldn\u2019t be that different. Well, except for the whole having a knife in my hand bit. I can still count the number of flashbacks I\u2019ve had while living here on one hand, and I\u2019ve been here for several weeks now. Okay\u2026I know, that almost makes it once a week that I\u2019ve had one of those things, but I\u2019ve been okay so far. Nothing has interfered with my life and no one has noticed anything. Well, Calamity noticed that one time that it happened while we were sparring, but it hasn\u2019t really happened since, so maybe I\u2019m getting over them? I know, wishful thinking, but I can delude myself if I want to. Probably shouldn\u2019t though. Calamity was right last time. I have to stay on top of things. I\u2019m one of the people keeping this motley safe, and I can\u2019t afford to lose focus. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> Tonight has been uneventful. De La Rocha has been dealing with the fact that, horror of horrors, she likes women and sleeps with three extraordinarily attractive ones on a regular basis. She dislikes the fact she is fairly stereotypical, but she is. Stereotypes exist for a reason. Sure, occasionally the reason is because the people of other countries are jealous of the culture and sophistication of the peoples of a given country, but often it is because people of a certain feather act a certain way. I was not shocked De La Rocha likes girls, I will put it that way. Definitely.<br /> <br /> I only thought Julia was moody about it, until I saw Lorelei. Julia was always more into Lorelei and I than De La Rocha, but they have become good friends (something Julia needs more of) and romantic ties have increased somewhat. Which may be good, De La Rocha always had a serious thing for Julia apparently going a ways back.<br /> <br /> Lorelei was sad and wanted us all to know it, then wanted to leave so people would go after her, which they did. It worked out pretty well for her. Obviously.<br /> <br /> Julia got a call from Chalcedony that her mind was fuzzy, that she passed to Calamity and Gawain, who called the count. Well at least they are equal opportunity in selling people out. Clearly.<br /> <br /> After a bit, Julia and I went downstairs and she sketched and fed me banana while Lorelei got drunk and ate ice cream. Jacob hung out with us, which was nice, though he went to keep an eye on Chalcedony after a point. It was a nice, peaceful, relaxing night. I need more of those. Definitely. We made sure Lorelei did not hurt herself and made it to bed.<br /> <br /> Now I shall sleep myself.<br /> <br /> ~<br /> <br /> It\u2019s been a quiet day, which is nice I need to rest a day before my busy evening tomorrow. Julia got me some very short shorts I wore, and it was pretty relaxing. Nicely.<br /> <br /> Becky came by to collect Chalcedony, but I did not get the impression they were going to hold her for safekeeping. Shortly thereafter, Calamity and Gawain went to meet Becky and the other security. Wisely.<br /> <br /> Flores came by. Julia dragged me into being taught to Charleston by her, but she spent more time with others whose Lady had not dragged them into dances earlier. Obviously.<br /> <br /> The evening was fairly uneventful. Willow came by to speak to Calamity and I about meeting arrangements; Calamity is looking a little high strung. Willow is not a huge fan of Scarlet and Natalia, but as she is (somewhat) responsible for their behavior I can see why not. Lorelei was more herself, and even got into a duet with Captain Jack that was\u2026very\u2026American.<br /> <br /> As the show wound down I recalled from the dancing practice and various activities over the day I had been exposed to several flashes of Julia\u2019s legs. They are very long, and taste very good when my tongue is run over them. I looked down at her and she smiled up at me. Warmly. I knew how I would be spending the night. Happily.<br /> <br /> And I did.<br /> <br /> Hopefully the day tomorrow is as restful and relaxing for me as these past couple were. It promises to be a busy night. Of course, with Julia dolling I up it may be a busy day as well. <i><i>C\u2019est la vie</i>, </i> as they say so often in America.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXIV</i><br /> <br /> Mostly a social session. Not much particular to add.<br /> <br /> Next session we begin the ball! I know you are looking forward to it. Comments and Questions are welcome!<br /> <br /> I have enjoyed all the discussion in this thread. Feel free to continue. I know it has my players pleased, and that is always a good thing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T14:05:11-08:00","id":424481,"title":"","content":"Omenseer:<br /> <br /> Sorry it's taken me a few days to respond; had to think about this one for a while. Lori's knee-jerk reaction to the nickname &quot;Nightingale&quot; would be negative, because she's generally opposed to being compared to a songbird in any wise due to the nature of her Durance. Upon reflection, she'd probably realize that the term is most likely intended as a compliment, and would just accept the nickname as inevitable after a few days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T16:40:18-08:00","id":424651,"title":"","content":"Now to some extent every changeling carries their cage with them, but who would you say bears theirs more?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"