ast one picture, but not looking to drop 50-odd pictures on this thread makes it harder on you. I can put up specific NPC pics if you are curious about specific people<br /> <br /> Long List, includes people met for the first time at the ball. This informaiton is correct as far as the players know...there could be info left out or misinformation, but it should work for your purposes.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <b>Spring</b><br /> <br /> Princess Jolie Fairest Muse/Waterborn<br /> Austin Beast Steepscrambler/Runnerswift<br /> Becky Wan Fairest Succubus/Draconic<br /> White Maria Fairest Treasured<br /> Flores Elemental Woodblood/Flowering<br /> Dark Kimberly Wizened Chatelaine/Drudge<br /> Mary Beast Steepscrambler/Truefriend<br /> Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne Fairest Minstrel/Larcenist<br /> Andromeda Wizened Chirurgen/Inventor<br /> Sandoval Elemental Sandharrowed/Airtouched<br /> Chalcedony Fairest Dancer/Shadowsoul<br /> Davey Darkling Mirrorskin<br /> Desiree Fairest Dancer/Romancer<br /> <br /> <b>Summer</b><br /> <br /> Viscount Augustine Ogre Gargantuan/Render<br /> Joan Fairest Bright One/Soldier<br /> Monica Ogre Gristlegrinder Bishopric of Blackbirds<br /> TJ Beast Roteater/Broadback<br /> Lucian Torrez Ogre Stonebones/Render<br /> De La Rocha Darkling Leechfinger/Witchtooth<br /> Old Billy Beast Steepscrambler/Riddlekith<br /> Percival Ogre Troll/Farwalker<br /> Hailey Wizened Inventor/Gremlin<br /> Juan-Carlos Hypnos Fairest Playmate/Telluric Family of Silent Nights<br /> Ji Wen Ja Elemental Di-Cang/Earthbones<br /> Louis Guo Elemental Airtouched/Levinquick<br /> <br /> <b>Autumn</b><br /> <br /> Queen Charlotte Beast Skitterskulk/Venombite<br /> Tommy Rawhead Darkling Tunnelgrub/Leechfinger Scarecrow Ministry<br /> Madame Spidertoes Darkling Antiquarian/ Gravewight Office of the Vizieral Council<br /> Annika Darkling Palewraith/Dancer<br /> Gunnar \u201cGhoul\u201d FridayDarkling Gravewight/Illes<br /> Dionisia Wizened Fatemaker/Author Twilight Gleaners<br /> Julia Oldacre Darkling Nightsinger/Artist<br /> Ginny Green Ogre Water-Dweller/Nix<br /> Luna Beast Skitterskulk/Windwing<br /> Moon Darkling Moonborn<br /> Oleander Elemental Woodblood/Woodwalker Barony of the Lesser Ones<br /> Shi Beast Riddleseeker/Coyote<br /> <br /> <b>Winter</b><br /> <br /> Master Darke Elemental Manikin/ Blightbent<br /> Doctor Bright Elemental Manikin/ Blightbent<br /> Vic Twilight Elemental Manikin<br /> Tamara Chance Wizened Oracle Knighthood of the Utmost Silence<br /> John Lowjack Wizened Brewer Magistrate of the Wax Mask<br /> Molly Nuit Elemental Manikin<br /> Twitch Wizened Chirurgen<br /> Mr. Grey Wizened Chirurgen?<br /> <br /> <b>Dusk</b><br /> <br /> \u201cCaptain\u201d Jack Martinez Ogre Gargantuan Sacred Band of the Golden Standard<br /> <br /> <b>Day</b><br /> <br /> Olivia Gold Fairest Bright One/Flamesiren<br /> Felicity Fairest Treasured/ Bright One<br /> Leonidas, Lord of Day Beast Hunterheart<br /> <br /> <b>Night</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Willow Black Beast Windwing/ Hunterheart<br /> The Warlock of Night Darkling Leechfinger/Nightsinger<br /> Scarlet Noir Darkling Leechfinger/ Whisperwisp<br /> Natalia Darkling Leechfinger/ Moonborn<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Tell me if you need a reminder of who anyone is, or have a specific character you want a pic up of.<br /> <br /> ETA: Formatting isn't super but assume no one has their seeming as part of their name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T13:12:37-08:00","id":425599,"title":"","content":"Hey, thanks. This helps as is. It gives context to some of the NPCs that pop up more infrequently. I can follow who most of the major ones, but some of the extraneous ones I couldn't remember what court they were in and thus sort of how they fit into the picture.<br /> <br /> I would be kind of curious to see the pictures you use for the some of the main NPCs. Julia, De Flores, Becky, Jolie, Queen Charlotte, Lucien and Master Darke.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","name":"Gravitas Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T17:14:01-08:00","id":425819,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> Okay<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://s169.photobucket.com/user/LeRoienJeune/media/Julia%20Oldacre_zpsh9kc8asv.jpg.html\" target=\"_blank\">Julia</a> Oldacre was one who sort of surprised me how different her planned role to her in game her role was.It's easy to forget Julia is a high Mantle Autumn Courtier, whose original introduction was her watching/stalking Lori. Then Insincere Marguerite seduced her. Julia was intrigued by the mysterious woman, and was never the same again. Insincere Marguerite's personality makes people underestimate Julia, but she is fine with that. She murdered her fetch, and her attraction to Lori stems in part to how much Lori resembles the beautiful women who often meet dark or tragic fates in her work. Indeed, one possibility was for Julia originally was to be the unlikely murderer if her desire to create one of her dark Gorey-esque tableaux in real life overcome her, which means Flores and Lori are no longer in danger. Maybe.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i169.photobucket.com/albums/u223/LeRoienJeune/de%20la%20rocha_zpsbta7so7m.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Maria De La Rocha</a> is a good place to note how I handle NPCs and romance regardless. Most NPCs are potentially bisexual to PCs, but may well not be to NPCs. DLR left to herself would have never gotten into a lesbian relationship despite (or, partially because of) her romance with Madame Spidertoes. Females have a harder time seducing her, but Lori can seduce anything. Of course, being in a romance with a woman means making her confront her sexuality, which means more baggage for a female PC, but she is more open to commitment with a woman than man, so there is that.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i169.photobucket.com/albums/u223/LeRoienJeune/Flores_zpsmjskq32y.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Flores</a> is a sweetheart. She does not get why people are so hung up on sex, but she really wants to make people happy. Total flower child. Probably won't be murdered in an artistic fever by Julia now, which means I need to find something to do with her. People seem to like and want to protect Flores which is cool, she is an innocent and may be one of the most legitimately good people in the freehold. She has no dark side to speak of, unless people consider being a sexual tyrannosaurs a dark side.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i169.photobucket.com/albums/u223/LeRoienJeune/Becky_zpsatfwvm6d.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Becky Wan</a> the overworked Clavager looks pretty sinister, and is a potent and dangerous fighter. She's not really evil though, just crafted by the gentry that way. Not up to anything untoward the PCs know of, but you know, she really, really does NOT like Desiree...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i169.photobucket.com/albums/u223/LeRoienJeune/Jolie_zps6usyqucy.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Princess Jolie</a>'s picture was actually put forth by Lorelei's player. She is absolutely the sweetest soul eater you will ever meet. She is smart, charismatic, the Spring Court adores her, will kill for her, and will ignore heinous crimes she commits. Even the PCs were disinclined to take her down.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i169.photobucket.com/albums/u223/LeRoienJeune/Queen%20Charlotte_zpsvuj4etsa.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Queen Charlotte</a> is beautiful, cunning, and dangerous. Not as powerful as, say, Tommy or Spidertoes, she is a people person, being a predator, and is cunning and wise enough to lead and pretty enough to fight for. If anything is working against her, it is her powerful, capricious, and frankly mad patrons within the Court.<br /> <br /> For <a href=\"http://i169.photobucket.com/albums/u223/LeRoienJeune/Lucian%20Torrez2_zpsbodtxgb6.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Lucian Torrez</a> I picked Brian Thompson to play the heavy. Lucian is friendly and charismatic, and willing to kill out of hand for frighteningly little provocation. He is what I call an agenda'd NPC; not a direct villain, because the PCs are not on a collision course with him, but certainly someone they could find themselves in a position where they must ally with him or become his enemy. The PCs have worked to keep themselves out from his way for now. They are wise.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i169.photobucket.com/albums/u223/LeRoienJeune/Mister%20Darke3_zpskwwxjhx1.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Master Darke</a> keeps secrets like beehives keep bees, and his are ten times and dangerous. Ruthless, amoral, cruel, callous, and the biggest thing keeping the Gentry out of Malibu/Santa Monica/Venice Beach.<br /> <br /> Hope that is helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 03-03-2015, 01:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T21:37:02-08:00","id":426152,"title":"","content":"I must admit I forget that Julia is something other than Insincere Marguerite's toy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T01:41:51-08:00","id":426283,"title":"","content":"It is not hard to underestimate Julia..There is a reason Calamity didn't capitalize her name for a while there.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T18:43:11-08:00","id":427220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play?p=424964#post424964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably Calamity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yeah. Literally. It's embedded in her skin. :-P<br /> <br /> Like your NPC analysis, too. My favourite activity in running Changeling is creating members of the Freehold and working out their roles, both in the society and in the story itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4722-birnam","name":"Birnam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T21:38:34-08:00","id":427405,"title":"","content":"It is fun to have different Court arrangements My first game <i>Beyond the Sea</i> for <b>Changeling: The Lost</b> featured a situation where the Winter and Autumn Kings were incapacitated by a loyalist agent, and the Summer Queen was soon after it started. The primary defenders of the area were high Wyrd, low Clarity Changelings and the whole city was surrounded on three sides by swamp and one side by ocean...the two ways out were a single road (which required crossing a bridge to connect to land) or by sea, playing up the isolation, and a group of (mostly) humans all but controlled the area though political dominance...the leader was a powerful Thaumaturge with a Spirit Patron. There were lots of ghosts and a somewhat lovecraftian storyline going on as well. The end result was isolation, dangerous marches around the city, and mad and unreliable leaders. There were no Sun or Moon Courtiers, but there were a small contignent of Directional Courtiers in one part of town who did not mingle with the Seasonals. By the end, a PC was Autumn Queen.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, only one player reliably did journals, and his journals were a colloquy of different personalities that represented different people he as a mirrorskin imitated. He was not MPD, more a consensus. This meant that his journals were arcane if you were not present for the game. One player did a single journal (which did not actually record any of what happened in the game so much as his reflections on being a Changeling) and while we had one player in game for six months or so who did journal more coherently, the nature of the PDFs the player produced were not such that I could copy and paste it...which means I have sadly little in the way of records of that game.<br /> <br /> <i>Malibu Dream House</i> is a whole different set up. There are many more Changelings and the Courts are relatively stable. Much of the threats are beneath the surface, and there is less crossover with other WoD games (probably because I am now running <b>Geist </b>and <b>Demon</b> both of which feature more crossover). There is still a major, threatening figure who is not quite an antagonist but the PCs must dance to his tune if they seek to avoid that (in <i>Beyond the Sea </i>played by Wilfred Brimly, in <i>Malibu Dream House</i> by Brian Thompson, very different characters,)<br /> <br /> Totally as an aside, despite having only two common players (Ace and Insincere Marguerite) the Seeming layout was kind of similar between them. <i>Beyond the Sea</i> had 4 Darklings, 1 Elemental, 1 Fairest, while <i>Malibu Dream House</i> has 1 Beast, 2 Darklings, 2 Elementals, 1 Fairest. (Courts were different, 2 Spring, 1 Summer, 2 Autumn, 1 Winter vs. 1 each Spring, Summer, Autumn, Winter, Dawn, Moon. Maybe they were not that dissimilar)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 03-04-2015, 12:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T01:59:51-08:00","id":427536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Birnam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play?p=427220#post427220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, yeah. Literally. It's embedded in her skin. :-P<br /> <br /> Like your NPC analysis, too. My favourite activity in running Changeling is creating members of the Freehold and working out their roles, both in the society and in the story itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was, perhaps, not the wisest course of action to steal a fragment of her Durance/keeper and take it to heart but at the time she really didn't know better.<br /> <br /> And as far as the NPCs, I had heard of Changeling but not read or played it before this game started. since then I have determined that I am going to have to run a campaign at some point as it's the only way I can ever use all the character ideas I've got now (several of which really shouldn't be player characters anyway...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T05:53:26-08:00","id":427643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amberghylles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play?p=427536#post427536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And as far as the NPCs, I had heard of Changeling but not read or played it before this game started. since then I have determined that I am going to have to run a campaign at some point as it's the only way I can ever use all the character ideas I've got now (several of which really shouldn't be player characters anyway...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, that's the universal problem. I have no idea when I'll next get to run a game. Yet I'm writing down the NPCs for a London Freehold in the meantime. It's addictive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4722-birnam","name":"Birnam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T20:39:53-07:00","id":435211,"title":"","content":"The NPC I've been most curious about? Tommy. I'd like to see his inspiration pic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4722-birnam","name":"Birnam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T12:23:53-07:00","id":436045,"title":"","content":"Heh. I am afraid I can't provide a Tommy picture. I have one, but no one in game has ever seen him. Honestly IIRC only Calamity and Insincere Marguerite have spoken to him, unless I am forgetting something. Tommy talks through vents and grates, or occasionally huddles in dark corners too shadowed to make out anything but long arms. So I am saving that for...a surprise when/if people do see him. As he put it, he is not hiding in the dark because he wins beauty pageants.<br /> <br /> I can talk a moment about him. Tommy's cadence and verbal tics are inspired by <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wfT7Bj0Zk7w\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Gorgeous&quot; Gary Golden, Nosferatu Primogen in Vampire: The Masquerade: Bloodlines</a> though he has been much more polite with Calamity and Insincere Marguerite since they are sort of his people; he took Calamity under his wing, and given he intruded in Insincere Marguerite's turf he did not wish to make an enemy, especially one who is...similarly able to access hidden places he thrives in.<br /> <br /> Everyone says Tommy is old, and he is...even Madame Spidertoes is somewhat deferential, and she is over a century old. The man has many secrets, and knows a great deal. He dislikes politics, and prefers to revel in fear. He does not seem to act very human at all, in fact. But maybe he just does it to scare you. Or maybe you should be scared...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T07:04:44-07:00","id":439842,"title":"","content":"Tommy is a consummate gentleman and Calamity will have words with anyone who says otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T02:41:20-07:00","id":443956,"title":"","content":"The Masquerade has begun! We don\u2019t get all the way though, but we can get the story so far from our Motley. Calamity\u2019s player has elected to hold off and do the whole Masquerade in one go, so they can set the emotional tone of it when they have the whole story. Fear not, you will hear from the stabby redhead soon enough. But for now, it\u2019s time for the Masquerade!<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> June 15th<br /> <br /> So, the first half of the ball was super awesome. A little bit frustrating, cause I just couldn\u2019t get my Contract of potential to work, you know? I did manage to figure out that Chalcedony has known Desiree for long enough that they had to have been in Arcadia together, but that\u2019s it. I guess I was distracted. There was plenty to be distracted by and I was kinda fidgety, you know, waiting for the shenanigans. And the Greening.<br /> <br /> The Greening was just perfect. De la Roche and Lori went first - they showed up together, so I guess De la Roche worked out her stuff. We left early, cause we were security, you know, so Lori was still glued to her phone and fretting when we left. Me and Calamity both felt better, I think, when they walked in together. They danced together a lot too, though Lori\u2019s dance card was crazy full - I dunno if she got to just chill, ever, everyone wanted to dance with her.<br /> <br /> Joan and Andromeda went second. They even Pledged themselves to each other, with Joan promising to kill anyone who harassed Andromeda. So, she\u2019s not any less super intense. Not that I expected her to be, you know. Really though, they were super adorable all night, being completely twitterpated over each other.<br /> <br /> Then and last, it was me and Calamity. We each Greened each other, cause that seemed the most right. I had to go down on one knee so she could reach my head, so I took that moment to say the kinda tweaked fealty oath I\u2019d prepped. It wasn\u2019t a capital-O oath, or anything, but it seemed the most \u2018me\u2019 thing to say, you know? Calamity told me again that she was my monster, there in front of everyone and then we kissed. I kinda forgot everything else cause of that kiss until the mask slipped down and bopped me on the head. I had had to take her mask off to put the ivy on, which was good - I may have made it, but I really didn\u2019t want to kiss the creepy rabbit mask.<br /> <br /> It was amazing, just the best. That by itself made the night and along with the shenanigans with Captain Jack and the good news about Desiree, I was pretty sure I couldn\u2019t be happier. Desiree wasn\u2019t quite as happy as I thought she\u2019d be - not that she was ungrateful or anything, you know, she was happy and super glad it could be fixed, but it also occurred to her that her friend that escaped with her, that she turned in for starting to be loyalist-y, probably just had the switch flipped. That is a bit of a bummer, but hopefully one that won\u2019t have to happen again, you know? For now, Sandeval\u2019s going to see if the Court can\u2019t track down an Oneirophysic and I\u2019m gonna work with her in the meantime. With that and Captain Jack\u2019s help with the phones, I\u2019m sure we\u2019ll get everything figured out.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Captain Jack... shenanigans were fucking had. They went off perfectly too. He played some \u2018villain music\u2019 just after 9 and pounced on Calamity, dragging her off to the closet. When he came out in a Captain Jack sized version of Calamity's bunny costume, me and \u2018Calamity\u2019 danced again. I almost ruined it when Calamity came out in a Calamity -sized version of his costume. She told me she would, but then when I saw shirtless Captain Jack in tight pants, a luchador mask and a giant back tattoo of a dragonfly with a chihuahua in its mouth, I didn\u2019t put two and two together until shirtless Calamity came out in tight pants, a luchador mask and a giant back tattoo of a dragonfly with a chihuahua in its mouth. It was, well, distracting, you know? She stayed in it til Captain Jack came back in his old costume, so I got plenty of time to stare after shenanigans.<br /> <br /> But I managed to tear my eyes away at the time, and after a bit a shard of \u2018Calamity\u2019s\u2019 glass flew off into Lori\u2019s boobs. I got fake angry and then he kissed me on the cheek and ran with me running after him. When we got to the ballroom, he managed to surreptitiously punch one of his fake boobs out and it went bouncing everywhere, so he started chasing after that. Once we\u2019d made a circuit, a rope was hanging from the skylight and he got pulled up and away with his bouncy boob while I shook my fist at him.<br /> <br /> He came back after a bit, of course. He kinda just slipped back in, you know, but then nothing could compare with his first entrance. Eight shirtless dudes singing O Fortuna while carrying him on a palanquin. Then he got introduced as \u2018Captain Jack Martinez of the Dusk Court, Just Some Guy, You Might Have Seen Him\u2019.<br /> <br /> The titles were cool. Us in the motley kinda had a theme. Lori was Siren of the Malibu Dream House. I was Sentinel of the MDH. Insincere Marguerite was Watchful Eyes of the MDH. Jacob was Master of Spirits of the MDH. Calamity was Flashing Blades of the MDH. And Ace, of course, was Minder of the Egg of the MDH. Ace was his usual crazy self. He kept trying to talk without a British accent - I guess so that no one could tell who he was behind the mask? At least he didn\u2019t bring the caiman...<br /> <br /> Other people had cool titles too, and it was interesting to note some of the patterns. Most people were Lord or Lady, except Captain Jack was Captain Jack and Moon was Mystery Moon. The Hispanic folks were Don and Dona, again, except for Captain Jack. Julia had the title \u2018Creator of Wicked Eerie Tableaus\u2019. Felicity was \u2018Solar Mirage\u2019 and Joan was the \u2018Blazing Summer Sentinel\u2019. The Handmaidens had matching titles, of course - Scarlet was \u2018Some of Them Want to Use You\u2019 and Natalia\u2019s was \u2018Some of Them Want to Abuse You\u2019.<br /> <br /> The Handmaidens kept making me feel uncomfortable. Probably it was the way they kept circling around my motley mates like sharks. Just the ladies though, they left us dudes alone. Ace did dance with the Warlock, but I think he started that, you know? She seemed pretty cool, dancing by herself and having fun. He danced with her a couple of times actually, and everyone else seemed kinda standoffish. The Handmaidens though seemed like trouble and I couldn\u2019t get a read on them. Calamity could tell I was bothered and promised she wasn\u2019t going to leave me for them or kill them, which wasn\u2019t really what I was worried about really, but good to hear, I guess? They did seem more human? at least when they were interacting with Captain Jack, even if that did mean him spinning Scarlet above his head. It would just be nice to know what they were after though.<br /> <br /> Jacob did some dancing too, even if the Handmaidens didn\u2019t go after him, with Insincere Marguerite and Molly Nuit. He didn\u2019t get a chance to dance with Luna before the Greening, cause she showed up right then, but he brought her a drink right off and he and her and Calamity talked some. I think Calamity was helping her figure out the heels, cause Luna looked super uncomfortable and unsteady walking in them. She seemed more steady after talking for a bit, and hanging on to Jacob of course.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Okay, so for once I get to start this diary on a high note. I have a lot to write about, but for the most part it\u2019s happy stuff. For the most part.<br /> <br /> Saturday afternoon was nerve-wracking as the motley got ready for the Masquerade. After breakfast I took a shower, did my hair, applied makeup, and got dressed, all the while keeping my phone within arm\u2019s reach and checking for messages from D every five minutes. I\u2019m sure it must have amused and/or annoyed the hell out of the rest of the motley, but Julia (the big sweetheart) seemed really concerned about me, and spent most of her time trying to calm me down and reassure me that everything would be all right. I really need to thank her for her concern.<br /> <br /> When D finally did call, I answered immediately. It\u2019s hard to sound nonchalant and aloof when you answer a call within two seconds, but I think I made an admirable effort. \u201cHey, babe,\u201d I said as I answered. \u201cHow are you doing?\u201d<br /> <br /> There was a pause, and I could almost hear her grin slightly. \u201cI\u2019m fine, Lori,\u201d she said. \u201cI\u2019m okay now, I promise. What time do you want to get to the Masquerade tonight?\u201d<br /> <br /> I looked at the clock. I\u2019d actually been hoping to arrive fashionably late, but my desire to see D as soon as possible made me change my mind in less than a heartbeat. \u201cSeven,\u201d I said, \u201cI\u2019d like to get there around seven.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGreat,\u201d she replied sedately, \u201cI\u2019ll be at your place by six-thirty, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay,\u201d I said. I was trying to play it cool, but I just couldn\u2019t keep it in any longer. \u201cI can\u2019t wait, D. I\u2019ve missed you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know,\u201d she said. \u201cI missed you too, Lori. Thanks for giving me the time I needed. I\u2019m ready now. I love you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLove you too, D,\u201d I said, and we disconnected.<br /> <br /> I turned around, and Julia was there. She smiled at me, reached up and brushed a tear from my cheek. \u201cTold you so,\u201d she said softly, and I kissed her in gratitude.<br /> <br /> When D actually arrived, I was speechless for a moment. She was <u>gorgeous</u>. I mean, I\u2019ve always thought D was beautiful, but she really stepped things up for last night; she was like fashion model beautiful. She hadn\u2019t really changed her hair; it was still that lustrous black with the shocking purple streak in it. She was wearing a long purple dress that accentuated her figure and complimented her coloration nicely, and she had makeup on\u2026 honest-to-god makeup!<br /> <br /> Purple lipstick. Purple hair. Purple dress. For an instant, an image of the Empress flashed through my mind, and I felt something swelling inside me. I don\u2019t know if it was fear, revulsion, or love, but whatever it was, I fought it down before it could show on my face. What I have with D is real, and I\u2019m not going to let the Empress ruin it. Not now that I\u2019ve finally escaped her.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m back,\u201d D said simply.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou look <u>amazing</u>, sweetie,\u201d I said. \u201cWelcome back.\u201d And then we kissed. And after that, we both had to touch up our makeup.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo\u2026 are you sure you\u2019re okay, D?\u201d I asked a few minutes later as we made our way to the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> She sighed. \u201cI\u2019m dealing with some pretty heavy shit, Lori,\u201d she said so softly that I almost couldn\u2019t hear her over the \u2018vette\u2019s engine, \u201cit\u2019s not going to completely work itself out in two days. But yeah, for now I\u2019m okay. I\u2019m right where I want to be.\u201d And she put her hand on top of mine on the gear-shift, and we continued like that until we reached our destination.<br /> <br /> The Masquerade was held in a stately old manor house just outside of Santa Monica. There must have been thirty rooms in that place, but the biggest three had been converted into dance floors. One was for traditional ballroom dancing, one was for more modern music, and the third was for electronic and rave music. Over the course of the evening we spent time in all three of those rooms, though I think we spent most of our time in the second.<br /> <br /> A majordomo announced us as we entered. \u201cThe Lady Lorelei Grace of the Spring Court, Siren of the Malibu Dream House\u201d (gosh!). \u201cOn her arm, Do\u00f1a de la Rocha of the Summer Court.\u201d<br /> <br /> Everybody got titles like that. Jacob was the \u201cMaster of Spirits,\u201d Calamity was the \u201cFlashing Blades,\u201d Ace was the \u201cKeeper of the Egg,\u201d and so on. Some of the changelings outside of our motley had even more fanciful titles\u2026 the Warlock of Night\u2019s handmaidens were \u201cSome of Them Want to Use You\u201d and \u201cSome of Them Want to Abuse You\u201d respectively. I didn\u2019t get it personally, but a lot of folks seemed amused by that.<br /> <br /> The ball itself was marvelous, like something out of a fairy tale (but in a good way). I had a very full dance card\u2026 but no more so than some of my friends, really. Ace tried to play the wallflower for a while, driving people away with an <u>atrocious</u> put-on American accent, but by midnight he was dancing like a loon with the Warlock of Night herself, who seemed both amused and pleased by his company. Could romance be in the air for those two? Would that be a good or bad thing?<br /> <br /> Calamity and Gawain were working security, but they both took time to dance and let their hair down every once in a while. I know Calamity danced with Becky Wan at least once, and I saw her spending time with the Warlock\u2019s handmaidens too. Gawain\u2019s meanderings were a bit more subdued, but I think I caught a glimpse of him out on the floor with Felicity at one point, and I\u2019m pretty sure he at least spoke with Joan and Andromeda.<br /> <br /> Marguerite and Julia spent most of their time with each other, of course. As much as Julia claims to hate romance and all of its trappings, she does love to dance, and I think she was enjoying herself more than she\u2019d care to admit. I danced with each of them once or twice over the course of the evening; it was fun.<br /> <br /> And speaking of Marguerite (who was wearing a beautiful gold dress and a somewhat disturbing lion mask), I saw her take a turn or two across the floor with Jacob. I know the two of them are \u201cclose,\u201d so to speak, and it\u2019s nice to see her drawing our friendly neighborhood Russian out of his icy shell. In fact, once she got him going, he seemed to find his inner party animal. I saw him dancing with Molly Nuit later that evening, and as midnight drew near he seemed to latch on to Calamity\u2019s friend Luna. I wonder if something interesting is happening between those two\u2026 I\u2019ll have to keep my eyes open around them.<br /> <br /> As for me, well, as I said, I had a lot of dance partners, but I never let myself forget that that night was supposed to be about me and D, and I never left her side for more than a few minutes. We must have danced dozens of times, across all three ballrooms, and I never got tired of it. And I could see in her eyes that she was enjoying herself every bit as much as I was.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t turn anyone else away, though. Fairly early on, the Handmaidens approached me and asked for a dance (together). I\u2019m not sure why everyone seems to judge them so harshly; they seemed perfectly nice to me. They were very complimentary of both my appearance and my dancing skills, and promised to come by the Dream House soon to watch me perform. Their manner was lightly flirtatious, but not overtly sexual or overbearing. I did my best to return every entendre which was served to me while still keeping the conversation light.<br /> <br /> I danced with Flores for a bit, too. She was as sweet and caring as always\u2026 but also just as direct. She questioned me about my relationship with D, stating frankly that she had always hoped that D would come to her if she discovered she had a passion for other women. I didn\u2019t really know how to respond to that, but Flores went on to tell me that she was happy the two of us had found each other, and that she hoped our relationship would make us both happy for years to come.<br /> <br /> Next on my dance card was Oleander, Flores\u2019 counterpart from the Autumn Court. I haven\u2019t really spent much time around her other than bargaining with her over the goblin fruit we brought back from the Hedge last week, but she seems nice enough. She and Flores are both plant-based Elementals, but they\u2019re very different from each other. Whereas Flores is all about perfume and blossoms, Oleander had a more solid, earthy feel to her. Hearing her talk was like listening to the wind moving through the leaves of trees, and there was a subtle smell of freshly cut grass around her. It reminded me of Iowa in the late summer\u2026 and for the first time in a while I thought of that place as \u201chome.\u201d We didn\u2019t talk much; and afterward she just thanked me for the dance and congratulated me on the upcoming Greening.<br /> <br /> I was also asked to dance by a striking woman I\u2019d never met before who introduced herself as Olivia Gold, Ambassador of the Day Court. She was nice enough, and seemed genuinely interested in how the Dream House was doing, but she also \u2013 like almost everyone else \u2013 wanted to warn me to be careful around the Handmaidens. She said that they have killed people before, and that they\u2019re very good at putting their intended victims off their guard. I\u2019d say that her attitude was just prejudice based on the rivalry between their two Courts\u2026 but Marguerite said something similar about the Handmaidens the other day, and I\u2019ve learned to trust her judgment on such matters.<br /> <br /> Somewhere in the middle of all this, Captain Jack made his entrance\u2026 and what an entrance it was! He was borne into the mansion on a palanquin carried by six attractive \u201cslave boys,\u201d all of whom were singing \u201cO Fortuna\u201d from <u>Carmina Burana</u>. He was wearing a type of mask I\u2019m told was popularized by Mexican professional wrestlers, and skin-tight pants. He wasn\u2019t wearing a shirt, but his back was covered by a huge tattoo of a dragonfly with a Chihuahua in its mouth. What can I say? The man knows how to show up for a party.<br /> <br /> When nine o\u2019clock rolled around, I made sure I was in place for the Captain\u2019s big stunt. Everything went just as planned. He slipped up behind Gawain \u201cunnoticed,\u201d snatched Calamity, and dragged her into a conveniently located closet. Moments later, he emerged wearing an exact duplicate of her costume and began dancing with Gawain. Neither of them seemed to notice the laughter that surrounded them as the rest of the room\u2019s occupants caught on to what was going down. A bit later, Calamity burst out of the closet, now wearing a replica of Jack\u2019s outfit (including the lack of shirt and the gaudy-but-beautiful tattoo) and approached the couple angrily. Gawain, apparently confused, reached out to the person he believed to be his beloved Calamity and touched her shoulder, causing one of her shards to snap off, flip through the air, and land squarely between my boobs. It was actually a prop made of rubber, so my assets survived intact.<br /> <br /> What followed was a chase scene worthy of a Benny Hill run-off, complete with a full orchestral rendition of \u201cYakety Sax.\u201d The Captain made his escape by distracting Gawain and the real Calamity by tossing one of his fake breasts back at them (it bounced around like a superball), grabbing a rope which was conveniently dangling through one of the skylights, and getting pulled up and out of the house by helicopter. How does that man have 24-7 access to helicopters, I\u2019d like to know\u2026<br /> <br /> He slipped back in quietly a little while later, and no one seemed to care. I guess they figured the show was over.<br /> <br /> At midnight, Austin called for a halt to the music and got up on a little raised stage to announce the Greening ceremony. His speech was light and funny, but despite that managed to convey how serious and meaningful the Greening itself is. There were three couples performing the ceremony that night: me and D, Calamity and Gawain, and Joan and Andromeda. Austin called us to the stage.<br /> <br /> D and I went first. I put the ivy garland in her hair and looked deep into her eyes. \u201cI don\u2019t have a big speech planned,\u201d I told her softly, \u201cnothing as important as this moment deserves. I just know that I love you, de la Rocha, like I\u2019ve never loved anyone before. If the last few days have taught me anything, it\u2019s that I never want to be without you again.\u201d<br /> <br /> Her eyes shone as she leaned in close. \u201cYou never will be,\u201d she said softly, and we kissed. There was applause, I remember that. Some scattered wolf-whistles, too. And a polite cough from Austin, who seemed eager to remind us that two other couples were waiting for the stage. But mostly I remember the feel of her in my arms, her lips on mine, her body pulled close, and her fingers lightly stroking my feathers.<br /> <br /> A thousand years later we yielded the stage to Joan and Andromeda. Joan made a bigger speech than I had, but mostly the gist of it seemed to be \u201cI will kill anyone who annoys you, Andromeda.\u201d It was\u2026 sweet, I guess, but a little violent for my taste. I\u2019m glad my D is a little more laid back about her violence. Summer Courtiers, man\u2026<br /> <br /> Gawain\u2019s speech, on the other hand, was <u>beautiful</u>. I think he must have adapted it from some sort of medieval poem or play or something, because it was very formal and courtly. Calamity\u2019s response was rawer, but just as meaningful to anyone who really knows her. Underneath her words, what she said was essentially \u201cI know I\u2019m not worthy of you, but I\u2019m yours for as long as you want me.\u201d It nearly brought a tear to my eye. I just wish she\u2019d stop referring to herself as a monster.<br /> <br /> As the music started up again, I pulled D into one of the corridors where we could have some privacy. I think she might have assumed I was making for one of the bedrooms, but I really just wanted to talk to her. \u201cD,\u201d I said once I was satisfied that we were nominally alone, \u201cI was wondering\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes?\u201d she said, raising an eyebrow.<br /> <br /> I composed myself. \u201cYou look amazing tonight,\u201d I began, \u201cand I love discovering new sides of you. You\u2019re everything I could ask for in a partner.\u201d<br /> <br /> Her eyes twinkled, and I felt my hopes rise a bit. \u201cBut\u2026?\u201d she prompted, a little teasing note entering her voice.<br /> <br /> \u201cBut,\u201d I continued pointedly, \u201cI hope I haven\u2019t seen the last of my badass in-your-face butt-kicking punk-rock girlfriend. I\u2019m going to miss her if she\u2019s gone for good.\u201d<br /> <br /> She smiled and winked. \u201cShe\u2019s not gone for good, Lori,\u201d she assured me, \u201cand she hasn\u2019t gone far. I just had to work some things out, and I guess I wanted to be, y\u2019know, <u>feminine</u> for a little while. To prove I\u2019m not a stereotype. Sorry if it rattled you.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled back. \u201cYou be whatever you need to be, D,\u201d I said. I almost called her Maria, but I figured the chance of us being overheard was too great.<br /> <br /> After that we kissed and went back to the dance floor. That was about the time that...<br /> <br /> Hang on, someone\u2019s at the door. I\u2019ll finish this later.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Well, the day started like most others, with a wonderful brunch courtesy of Gawain, but did not end like a typical day. Most of us had crepes and coffee for brunch, all except Calamity that is. She didn\u2019t wake up until later, after having been up for so long. Gawain, being the gentleman that he is, saved some food for his sweetie and heated it up for her when she got up. I must say that Calamity looked a lot better after a good night\u2019s sleep. She was looking kind of rough early this morning and had been up for over a full day. I think the sparring and sleep did her some good.<br /> <br /> Most of the motley spend a good part of the afternoon getting themselves ready for the masquerade ball. Mostly the ladies really, not to say us guys didn\u2019t take time to look nice. We did, but it doesn\u2019t take us quite as long to get dressed and spiffed up. I kind of spiked my hair with ice again after showering and dressing in the hedge spun tux. The mask I made was a fairly simple half mask. I dyed most of it black and put a bit of design on the edges. I\u2019m still not a master at that, so I figured simple was better than trying too much and messing up. As for the others, Lorelei wore a low cut white dress with a white domino mask. With the wings she looked rather angelic. Gawain was wearing a Roman style outfit. Pretorian Guard I think. He looked suitably impressive. Calamity wore a Playboy bunny outfit, complete with tail, but had a different spin on the mask. She had a rabbit themed mask that Gawain made for her that was patterned after the mask from Donnie Darko. Just a bit disturbing. I think it fit Calamity though. She is beautiful, but a bit scary at times too. Insincere Marguerite wore a long form-fitting gold dress that showed off her curves in all the right places. She of course did not wear shoes, but you could not tell since the dress covered her feet. Her mask was a gold leonine half mask that looked great on her, even if it was just a bit disturbing. Kind of an acknowledgement of her Keeper I suppose? Maybe an acknowledgement of how she is like her Keeper, perhaps? Ace, he was practically nondescript compared to the others, but still looked good in his suit. He kept walking around practicing an American accent. It was actually kind of funny.<br /> <br /> Everyone was introduced as Lord or Lady, or in the case of the Hispanic changelings, Don or Dona. Well, Moon was introduced as Mystery Moon, which was pretty cool. Anyway, we all had fancy titles, which was more than a little reminiscent of the Lady\u2019s realm. She had Lords and Ladies in her court. I was never a Lord though. I was her loyal Knight. As was Rook. There were a few other Knights in her employ, but we were her favorites. Together, Rook and I were the most efficient and dangerous Knights in the Lady\u2019s service. But tonight I wasn\u2019t a Knight. Tonight I was a Lord, which was still kind of weird. <br /> <br /> Anyway\u2026so we all had titles. I was Lord Jacob Stojanovic, of the Winter Court, Master of Spirits at the Malibu Dream House. Lorelei was Lady Lorelei Grace, of the Spring Court, Siren of the MDH. Gawain was Lord Gawan Vert, of the Dawn Court, Sentinel of the MDH. Ace was Lord Aaron Constantine Evermore, of the Summer Court, Minder of the Egg of the MDH. Insincere Marguerite was Lady Insincere Marguerite of the Night Court, Watchful Eyes of the MDH, and Calamity was Lady Calamity of the Autumn Court, Flashing Blades of the MDH. All very apt and descriptive titles if you ask me. Ace\u2019s may not have made much sense to a lot of the people present, but it definitely meant something to us, which I suppose is the point. Mine kind of had a double meaning, though I\u2019m not much involved in the ghost side of things at the Dream House. I kind of picked it because of the reference though. The ladies that were killed in that house didn\u2019t ask to die, and I figured that some homage to them would be appropriate since they are very much a part of the Dream House.<br /> <br /> Captain Jack had a suitably extravagant entrance, being carried in on a palanquin by good looking guys. He was just introduced as \u201cCaptain.\u201d I guess when you get to his status you can pick whatever you want to be your title. There were some others than had personalized titles. The two handmaidens of the Night Court were called Lady Scarlet of the Night Court, Some want to use you, while her wife/companion was called Lady Natalia of the Night Court, Some want to abuse you. I think it was a reference to an 80\u2019s song. Sounded like something my mother would sing while she was cleaning. At least when I translate what she sang into English, those are the lyrics. I wonder if she still does that? Sings American 80\u2019s songs while cleaning the house? Or has she moved onto a new decade of music yet? Makes me wish I could go back home and find out, but I really can\u2019t do that. My fetch is wearing my face and I can\u2019t take his place since I look so much older than he does.<br /> <br /> Sometimes I wonder what my parents would think of me now. I wonder if they\u2019d be ashamed to call me their son after all the things that I\u2019ve done. I know my father did some things during the Cold War that he was not proud of, but he didn\u2019t really have a choice. He was forced to do them. I wasn\u2019t. I didn\u2019t need coercion to do what I did for the Lady. I defended her, I killed for her, and I ruined lives for her. All of my own free will. Which may just answer my question for me. I used to be so proud of my heritage and my family. I made sure to speak Russian at home so I wouldn\u2019t forget it. I kept my name, instead of Americanizing it like some people do. I read the old stories and listened to my father retell the family\u2019s history. Now, I think, I have shamed my family and myself. It\u2019s probably for the best I was forced to change my name when I got back, so I don\u2019t bring shame to the Mikalev name.<br /> <br /> Sometimes I feel jealous of Lori. She goes to church every Sunday and gets to see her father. He doesn\u2019t know who she is, but she still gets to start a new relationship with him. And even if he did find out who she was, and didn\u2019t freak out, she doesn\u2019t really have anything to be ashamed of. She was a victim, pure and simple, and did what she had to do to survive and escape. There\u2019s not really a way for me to do anything like she\u2019s done to reconnect with my family. The closest that might ever come up is if I meet up with Elena while our parents are visiting her, but that\u2019s not likely to happen. And even then, how do I introduce myself. \u201cHi, I met your daughter while working at a restaurant. Now I work as a bartender at a Burlesque House, and still see your little girl on occasion.\u201d Yeah, not really a good introduction. Makes me wonder if she has ever mentioned me to her our parents since she\u2019s been going to school. I think we have a pretty good friendship going on, even if I don\u2019t get to see her as often as I did when working at the restaurant. <br /> <br /> Anyhoo\u2026back to the party. Almost as soon as we\u2019d arrived I did the polite thing and sought out Master Darke and made my presence known. On a whim I asked Molly Nuit to dance. It does no harm to dance with a pretty girl, even if I do need to watch what I say. It was nice. We went to the Modern music room and danced. She is pretty good, I\u2019ll give her that. While we danced she asked me about the Warlock of Night and what I know of her intentions in coming to the dance. I told her that I only knew that it was odd that she replied in the positive. I figured that she was up to something and said as much to Molly. Something like that is going to be automatically assumed anyway. In a moment of generosity I also let Molly know that I had been warned about the Warlock\u2019s handmaidens and to keep an eye out for them. They are considered dangerous, and I didn\u2019t mind sharing that information with Master Darke. <br /> <br /> And as if the fates read my mind I saw the two handmaidens circling Calamity as she stood off to the side. The display was nothing short of predatory if you ask me. They kept walking around her, smiling and occasionally touching her arms, shoulders and back. I\u2019m sure up close they were being coy and sexy as hell, but from a distance it didn\u2019t look sexy to me. I know Calamity can handle herself so I was not overly worried about her. The handmaidens cornered Lorelei after that and danced and flirted with our songstress. They didn\u2019t circle her the way they did Calamity though, so I figured Lori would be okay.<br /> <br /> After a while Molly and I went our separate ways. I asked Insincere Marguerite to dance, keenly seeking out less inquisitive company. It was nice to dance with Marguerite. She is a good dancer, and I do not feel quite as tense dancing with her. Not that I\u2019m overly tense when with Insincere Marguerite in particular, I\u2019m just usually kind of tense with any people. Anyhoo\u2026.while I was dancing with Marguerite I could not help but notice that her gaze frequently rested upon the expensive (and stealable) knick-knacks and items around the room. I also noticed that she deliberately tore her eyes from these items, as if to get them out of her mind. It seemed an ingrained habit to look for things of value that she could steal. Something perhaps left over from her time in Arcadia. I know that she used to steal things, sometimes people, for her Keeper. So, I didn\u2019t bring any attention to the fact that I noticed her doing this and just kept dancing. <br /> <br /> I\u2019d be a hypocrite if I said that my time in Arcadia didn\u2019t color the way I saw things or evaluated people. Without conscious thought I will look at people and immediately start to gauge their worth based on my Lady\u2019s criteria. The first time I saw Flores all I could think was that the Lady would think her wonderful prize and keep her as one of her \u201cpretties.\u201d Flores is so sweet and innocent. The Lady likes that in her collection of pretty things. That\u2019s what she liked most about Delight Diane. Then there\u2019s Joan. The first time I saw Joan all those weeks ago was that my Lady would revel in breaking her. Joan is such a strong, independent woman. The Lady does not like those that defy her. She likes to take those that are strong and break them, then mold them into her own image. I will admit that I am a little afraid of what Joan would become under the Lady\u2019s \u201ctutelage.\u201d <br /> <br /> The same kinds of thoughts went through my head when I first met the other members of the Motley. Ace, she would make into a pet. Not sure how a snake would survive in her realm, but he would be her pet. Lorelei would be another prize. A pretty thing to be shown off when she had company. Insincere Marguerite would have been given tasks right up her alley, so to speak. She would have been asked to obtain \u201cpretty things\u201d for the Lady\u2019s pleasure. She might have even worked alongside me and Rook when we went out to \u201cthe world.\u201d Calamity, given the proper \u201ctraining\u201d would be one of the Lady\u2019s Knights. Or at the very least someone that retrieves what is lost. Gawain would be one of the Lady\u2019s bodyguards. He is strong, loyal and protects what he loves. Given enough time with the Lady, he would love her and protect her with his life.<br /> <br /> Without really wanting to, those are the thoughts that popped into my head the first week or two that I knew the other members of the Motley. I couldn\u2019t help it. I had worked for so many years doing my Lady\u2019s bidding that my mind fell into familiar paths. I would of course never want the Lady to get her hands on my friends. I would not subject them to her \u201ceducation,\u201d nor would I want to see them become her tools to use as she pleased. I feel ashamed that I evaluated them when I first met them. I tell myself that it was habit, that I could not prevent my mind from going to familiar thoughts. Lately I have been better about having such thoughts about people that I meet, but not always. After I got past the shock of Felicity\u2019s name, I started thinking about which of her traits the Lady might like best. I think that the Lady would use Felicity as someone to calm people\u2019s nerves and to gain their trust. She is a friendly person that engages well with those that she talks to. The Lady would probably use her to calm her prospective servants and get them to trust her. <br /> <br /> By the Goddess I am in a mood tonight. Anyway, while Insincere Marguerite and I were dancing Captain Jack pulled his requisite prank. He pretended to kidnap Calamity and stuff her in a closet. Moments later he emerged wearing a larger copy of Calamity\u2019s Playgirl outfit, complete with fake glass shards on \u201cher\u201d shoulders. Calamtiy came out a moment later wearing a smaller version of Jack\u2019s costume. Here\u2019s the catch though: Jack was wearing a Mexican wrestler outfit with spandex pants, fake tattoo on his back and no shirt. So, that\u2019s what Calamity was wearing. I\u2019m not sorry. I took a couple pictures on my phone. I just couldn\u2019t pass up that photo op. I took pictures of Jack in the Playgirl outfit too. I\u2019ll send copies of the Calamity pics to Gawain. I figure that he\u2019ll appreciate them.<br /> <br /> Gawain played his part and pretended to not notice the switch. He danced with Jack until it was \u201crevealed\u201d that his date was an imposter. I think one of the fake glass shards came off and bounced away. Jack then made his escape through a convenient skylight. It was all very silly, but the other guests laughed and had fun watching it. I will admit that I enjoy seeing what those two come up with. It\u2019s usually interesting, and always funny. Jack is by nature an exhibitionist who loves to be the center of attention, and I can tell that Gawain is thoroughly enjoying himself too.<br /> <br /> At midnight the Greening took place, and those that wanted to proclaim their love for someone before the freehold did so. Those that participated were Lorelei and De La Rocha, Gawain and Calamity, and Joan and Andromeda. Lori put the wreath in her girlfriend\u2019s hair. Then there was Joan and Andromeda. Joan put the wreath in the other girl\u2019s hair, and made a vow before the free hold that pretty much said, \u201cmess with my girl and I\u2019ll kill you all.\u201d Very protective, as opposed to Lori who was just beaming at De la Rocha. The last couple was Calamity and Gawain. They put a wreath in each other\u2019s hair. Gawain took off Calamity\u2019s rabbit mask to claim her, and then got down on one knee so she could claim him. He then recited what sounded like an old fashioned wedding vow, promising to be hers forever. Calamity kissed him and in turn promised that she was his monster.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m happy that they found each other, all of them. They all looked so happy and were practically beaming afterwards. Joan smiled as much as she ever does, Andromeda was ecstatic, and the others were all happy and touchy-feely. I think each of them found something that they needed. Andromeda found a protector, Joan found love and (presumably) trust. Lorelei and De La Rocha found stability and tenderness. Calamity found unconditional love and trust, which is important to her. And Gawain found his own unconditional love. They have both done things that they aren\u2019t proud of, but they each found someone that cares for them as they really are. All the couples found that I think. The cynic in me keeps saying that none of them have known the other long enough for the level of dedication and trust that they are claiming and displaying. I have to ruthlessly tell that part of me to shut up. If Calamity found someone that loves her for the \u201cmonster\u201d that she is, it can only be a good thing. They all found something that they needed, and they are happy, so I have to tell the pessimistic side of me to shut it.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I\u2019m all over the place here aren\u2019t I? Anyway, shortly before the Greening a newcomer arrived. It was Luna. I was at the bar when I heard her introduced, so I ordered her favorite drink and went over to meet her. She wore a long slim dress in blue and black with light blue highlights, and a low cut back to accommodate her wings. She looked really pretty in her dress, but was kind of uncomfortable in the high heels. I think I made some comment to the effect that guys don\u2019t have to worry about those things. She started briefly at that and it took me a second to remember that before she was taken she\u2019d been a guy. Her Keeper had changed her gender. I never did ask why, and I had completely forgotten that when I made the comment about high heeled shoes. She seemed okay after that and I didn\u2019t really detect any unease, so I think she was comforted by my casual reference. No stress on it, no judgments. I will admit that I was afraid for a moment that I\u2019d put my boot in my mouth, but all was well. I really had forgotten. It doesn\u2019t even register to me, though I know intellectually. Luna is Luna. Girl or guy on the outside, it doesn\u2019t really matter to me. I like Luna for who she is. We share a cynical sense of humor and I enjoy her wit. She may not be the most socially adept, but neither am I. We have a lot in common, and I\u2019m hoping to get to know her better. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> Preparing for the ball was interesting. It had been a long time since I dressed up for a major social occasion\u2026months at least, perhaps a year. And I have far more clothes now. Happily. Julia was running around helping, it was fun. She even went to help Lorelei; though I suspect she was more being sure Lorelei was okay without De La Rocha around.<br /> <br /> We did talk about Lorelei. Julia wanted to be sure I know she was very in love with I and wanted me to be her partner despite her interest in Lorelei, though she admitted her attraction to Lorelei was not purely physical. That was obvious. It was enough to upset her when Lorelei ignored her because she was hung up on De La Rocha. But she wanted me to know where I stood and that I was the center of her life. While I knew this, it was nonetheless pleasing to hear. Definitely.<br /> <br /> Still, we discussed we were both pleased by our\u2026arrangement with De La Rocha and Lorelei. They are cute, and I rather like how submissive De La Rocha is. I have never been with anyone, woman or man, who was such an excellent sub. Lorelei is fun to and her stubbornness is\u2026interesting\u2026to try to break down a little at a time.<br /> <br /> We also talked about Calamity. Julia is worried she is under too much stress. I admitted I had not noticed, but when I peeked out at her she did seem a little stressed. Less so than Lorelei. We talked about her as well. Julia had apparently worried Gawain was preventing her from exploring her inner darkness, but feels now Gawain is good for her\u2026as long as she does not turn her back fully on the darkness. I reminded her we Darklings cannot do this. Fortunately. She did at least like that Gawain was keeping Calamity happy. I can\u2019t imagine what she would be like right now without him. Also, and this cannot be stressed enough, he makes good cr\u00eapes.<br /> <br /> We also discussed Felicity. I stated I would be seducing her and attempting to bring her under my control. I salivate at such a valuable prize. Julia was, and is, afraid I will lose interest in her over Felicity. She is foolish. Felicity is not my partner, someone to scheme with. Julia needs have no fear. We agreed, however, if Julia truly felt Felicity was excreting undue influence and I had fallen under her spell, Julia could murder her. But she would have to herself. If she gave evidence I was being unduly influenced and killed her personally, I would not seek to get revenge. Casting Julia out is not an option anyway, of course; we have a Pledge. I am unsure why she is worried.<br /> <br /> I have no doubt Julia <i><i>could</i></i> murder her. She murdered her fetch and got away with it. Of course, Julia\u2019s fetch was never missed, since Julia stepped back into her life with \u201chead injury related memory loss\u201d after hurling her into that well. But she would at least need to take more time than just asking Calamity to do it, thus would have to think through it.<br /> <br /> We arrived at the Masquerade looking glorious. I noticed Felicity watched Lorelei enter, so I swooped in quickly to talk to her. Felicity was indeed interested in talking to me\u2026privately. We had a dance and then spoke in a corner to ourselves.<br /> <br /> She noted we were the most powerful, most respected Night and Day Courtiers outside downtown LA, possibly in the state, and it would behoove us to work together. As she told us before, she has no desire to unseat the Seasonal Courts. She does wish to leverage our influence a bit, though, though allies of our Courts, including the Motley. I asked her if she sought to be Day Queen of some sort and she sort of smiled and shrugged, but reiterated that she does not want to see the Seasonal Courts removed from Santa Monica, noting if they were, we would go back to being smaller fish in the area. I told her I liked her cunning and kissed her. Aggressively.<br /> <br /> As most do in my experience, after going limp a few seconds in surprise she returned the kiss. She seemed more amenable to my advances afterwards. I reminded her she was going to be seduced. I also told her her life might depend on not upsetting Julia, that Julia was my partner, and would be involved in any scheme we were. There was some discussion of Julia, and I informed her I needed to go find her, but that I would come back before long. Truthfully.<br /> <br /> Felicity is, however, a remarkably good kisser. I mean, not as good as I, but then who is?<br /> <br /> I danced with Julia, and then after she asked I told her again it was perfectly fine for her to dance with Lorelei. I plan to myself. I myself asked one more time if she wanted to do the Greening, and she responded the same as before that she wanted no part of anything so twee. Apparently.<br /> <br /> Jacob wanted to dance next. I am very fond of Jacob. He seems relaxed somewhat, though I did not search his eyes. He is shy, poor lad, and I was considering trying to introduce him around, but Luna\u2019s arrival suggested such may be unnecessary or even dangerous if she gets jealous. I don\u2019t want to accidentally seem to be trying to break them up. Definitely.<br /> <br /> I also danced with Willow briefly. I had just finished when Scarlet and Natalia showed up. They greeted me warmly (and made a point of also greeting my tongue, which was annoying as it is just part of me) and expressed interest in continuing our\u2026rapport\u2026where it left off. They paced around me, hungrily, like sharks. I was polite, but I did not encourage their advances. Calamity is a clever girl, and she is correct; they are indeed up to something. Perhaps they see me as a way to increase our Courts power in Santa Monica without Felicities rather political concerns about her own power, since they are themselves very influential. Perhaps I really am just that amazing, as Julia suggests. Probably that one. Probably.<br /> <br /> Somewhere in all this I danced again with Felicity. Afterwards Captain Jack, Gawain, and Calamity carried out their tour-de-force, which involved at times Captain Jack dressed as a playboy bunny and Calamity running around bare chested dressed as a luchador. Julia thought it was terrific fun and even I thought it was amusing. People will certainly be talking about Captain Jack, Gawain, and Calamity after this.<br /> <br /> During the time before the Greening I danced with Julia again and kissed her on the floor. Publicly. I saw Luna had arrived and made for Jacob. At first I thought she was drunk but no, she was unsteady on heels. Poor thing. I don\u2019t even wear shoes most of the time. Heels? I cannot even imagine! I have not worn them since I returned to Earth. I certainly did not return to wear heels!<br /> <br /> After a bit, they Greening occurred. Mostly Motley members, Lorelei and De La Rocha went first, then Joan and Andromeda, then Calamity and Gawain. I thought it was sweet, even if Julia acted like she was watching people play Andy-I-Over. Strangely.<br /> <br /> With that, it was ninety minutes until the meeting, and I had more dancing to do. Good thing I did not wear shoes! Definitely.<br /> <br /> (TBC)<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXV</i><br /> <br /> So for introductions, I had a sort of Lord/Lady [Name] of the [Court] and those in especially good Court standing (3+ Mantle) could add a title\u2026those with 5 could add a particularly unusual title (like the Handmaidens). Because they are trying to keep the Latino Changelings from splitting off or otherwise making their own Court (after all, they don\u2019t have any rulers who are Latin in the Freehold, and really never have), they decided to give them a nod and added Don/Do\u00f1a as an optional substitute for Lord/Lady and Moon, being agendered, elected to go with \u201cMystery\u201d in place of either. Zee is the only really agendered Changeling in the freehold (Luna identifies as female, though I would still call her genderqueer) so zee had hir choice pretty much. In other news, I did not realize both genderqueer NPCs in Changeling have lunar name themes (though that is not the case in other games).<br /> <br /> It\u2019s possible for folks to gain some Mantle or Court Affinity from the ball, or lose it, though I am waiting to hand that out after. De La Rocha lost a point of Clarity having to sort the major life change out, but is dealing with it okay.<br /> <br /> Things seem to be going well, just have to see how it all ends up. Tonight\u2019s session was fun and wound up the Masquerade, so next time we will be having the end of it then moving on to other things. See you then. Comments and Questions welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T07:40:33-07:00","id":444179,"title":"","content":"Man, I love Captain Jack. It's official.<br /> <br /> I had a thought when reading Lori's interaction with the Handmaidens: Night and Spring Courts probably get along okay, since it takes a little more effort (on average) to disgust a Spring courtier. &quot;Your mother sucks cock in Hell!&quot; &quot;Well, if that's her kink, then good on her.&quot; Or maybe that infuriates Night to no end.<br /> <br /> Sounds like it was a great session!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4722-birnam","name":"Birnam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T12:58:59-07:00","id":444806,"title":"","content":"Well since Changelings can't get Glamour off each other, the Night Court has little reason to go out of their way to bug Spring...unless that is just their thing. ^_^ Being big on &quot;let your freak flag fly&quot; they generally can potentially get along with Spring, though some in the Courts embrace of ugliness may cause some issue (though they have less issue with pretty people than the Day Court has with ugly people).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T19:59:41-07:00","id":445259,"title":"","content":"What title would someone who has standing in all four courts and acts on all's behalf be called? Or rather could they add a title as well?<br /> <br /> Side note: I had an idea for a &quot;Keeper of Keys&quot; power. Basically for any group or place the keeper has the trust of they can produce a ring of keys with a key for every lock lock associated with said group or place. Should they break that trust they lose the key ring and suffer an appropriate wyrd/glamour backed punishment. How would you rate or work that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T16:50:21-07:00","id":446702,"title":"","content":"Birnam,<br /> <br /> The Good Baron should feel free to correct me if I'm wrong, but my impression of the Handmaidens was that they modified their approach to suit those they were addressing. When they spoke with Lorelei, they were flattering and friendly. When they approached Calamity they were dangerous and subtly predatory. Jacob's encounter with them hasn't been chronicled here yet, so I won't go into detail about it, but in my opinion it continued that trend.<br /> <br /> And Captain Jack is a favorite with the players as well. I can't wait to see how he tops this performance. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T02:42:02-07:00","id":447435,"title":"","content":"Penitent Tom is absolutely on the money, and when they interacted with Insincere Marguerite they attempted to flatter her ego and draw attention to the assets they know she was vain about. So yes, their approach varies.<br /> <br /> Omenseer: You mean in general, or at the party? In general there is no title. At the party they would have gone with whatever they had Mantle in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T01:41:16-07:00","id":463208,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to finish the Masquerade! Let\u2019s look in on the Motley and see how they did. Note Calamity\u2019s journal covers both this and last session.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXVI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> I also got to dance some with Felicity and Desiree and not just hover protectively. Felicity was a bit nervous - between her Court\u2019s ambassador giving her the cold shoulder, Insincere Marguerite coming on pretty strong, the Handmaidens threatening her, Queen Charlotte giving her dirty looks and Julia catching her eye before drawing her thumb across her throat, I can\u2019t really blame her, you know? I had a good idea about Insincere Marguerite and Julia\u2019s motivations, and I tried to check out the others using the Contract of Potential, but the only one I got a read on was Olivia, the Dawn Ambassador. She didn\u2019t like Felicity, but it was a vague kinda dislike, like she thought Felicity was lazy about promoting their Court, and she was jealous of how pretty she was, you know? Not really \u2018lure you to your downfall\u2019 kinda passions. I think<br /> <br /> Desiree on the other hand was just a little overwhelmed by Princess Joli\u2019s attentions. It did seem to be moving really fast. I thought about checking the Princess out with the Contract, but it can\u2019t really reveal the origin of the feelings, you know, like whether it was a natural infatuation or if mind-zapped Desiree had used some kind of power to force it along. Desiree was trying to be good and get to know Princess Joli a little better, slow things down, you know, to make sure it\u2019s not just infatuation. Still, she was a little jealous of the Princess paying attention to Felicity. I tried to reassure her on that front. Felicity didn\u2019t need another woman to be jealous and threatening towards her.<br /> <br /> The rest of the motley certainly seemed to enjoy themselves as the night went on. Lori actually left first, which was a little surprising, but not too much, what with the way she and De la Roche were looking at each other. Also I guess Flores pissed De la Roche off really bad by fussing at the darkling about getting in a big bar fight last night. Julia said De la Roche almost hit Flores, which would have put her out for sure. The Elemental was pretty bummed, you know, so I helped Julia cheer her up some. Julia, Flores and Insincere Marguerite headed off after a bit. That was a little surprising too, cause I kinda expected Insincere Marguerite to take home Felicity, or get taken home by her and come back with all her stuff, but Felicity took advantage of her disappearing for a bit to head home by herself. She let me know when she was safe at home, so that was a worry dealt with, for now.<br /> <br /> At one point while I was dancing with Flores, the Warlock came in, removed \u2018Utility Backpack Scarlet\u2019 from Ace\u2019s back (I think Captain Jack put her there? I stopped keeping quite as close a track on them after Captain Jack kinda started corralling them. They seemed inclined to play along with him, and his hijinx aren\u2019t nearly as malicious as theirs.). Then she put a leash on him and walked out with him in tow. He seemed fine with it, so I didn\u2019t make a fuss or anything, though it seemed... weird to leash somebody like that. And I didn\u2019t think he liked sex. I mean, I guess they could be doing non-sex things but... it seems unlikely.<br /> <br /> Jacob left with Luna. That was no surprise - he even blew off the Handmaidens, twice, in favor of dancing or just sitting and talking with Luna. At some point she lost her heels, which was probably for the best, you know? She looked adorable, but really unsteady and more importantly, super uncomfortable in them. She seemed way more collected once she was going around barefoot, except when the Handmaidens were standing in Jacob\u2019s personal space.<br /> <br /> Calamity and I wound up bringing Becky home. Calamity thought it would make Becky feel better after a shitty week of people she\u2019s supposed to be protecting not letting her protect them, and I thought she was hot and trusted Calamity\u2019s judgment about making her feel better. Her week did sound pretty shitty. I felt maybe a little guilty, but she is the one who asked, so I guess I shouldn\u2019t, you know? Anyways, it was super awesome. Like I said, Becky is super hot, and her hair moves all on its own and... yeah. Plus, Calamity was really happy. It was good to see her so content with things. Her week hadn\u2019t been too great itself and she seems much more relaxed and chill now.<br /> <br /> June 16th<br /> <br /> Becky, Luna, De la Roche and Flores were all here for breakfast. The rest of the motley was too, even Ace, though he wandered in from outside (instead of downstairs) and only just long enough to grab his egg before taking Vesuvius the caiman for a walk and leaving him in the fountain. I made crepes again, cause Becky had heard about them and wanted me to impress her. I made sure there was plenty of syrups, boiled fruits and sugared cinnamon, as befits a house of note. It did occur to me over breakfast that it had been some time since I had had venison, and I ought being preparing a proper dinner on occasion. Fish would be easier to get, but there\u2019s no need to make do with fasting food, you know. Luckily, both Becky and Luna knew where I could get some.<br /> <br /> Flores and De la Roche worked their stuff out, I think. It got tense there for a bit, you know, especially when Becky got worried about De la Roche punching Flores. But it turned out alright, partially cause Flores is so damn cute, even if it was a little awkward. Speaking of awkward though, Lori apparently told her dad the priest about De la Roche being her girlfriend. She said he took it well, which is good. Definitely didn\u2019t kick her out of the choir or something stupid like that.<br /> <br /> For the sake of completeness, I will note that Captain Jack has the fine muscle control to mustard up a hotdog with both his pecs and his ass. The pecs bit came up at the Masquerade, as he was serving hot dogs as the night waned. The ass bit came up in the tasteful? nudes he sent Becky and Calamity. I don\u2019t think that hotdog got served to anyone...<br /> <br /> But the best part of breakfast, I have saved for last. Calamity, to Lori\u2019s great chagrin, pointed out that if Ace dreamed of fire-breathing piranhas, I could pull them out of his head! Unfortunately, I\u2019m not quite good enough at that to have them stay permanently. Yet. But one day, our Hedge House will be protected by a moat full of fire breathing piranhas. For now though, our day\u2019s plans involve some general fixing up and moat digging, Hedge-side.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> So that was Ace at the door. He wanted to share some hare-brained idea he\u2019d had about\u2026 y\u2019know, I guess it doesn\u2019t really matter in the long run.<br /> <br /> The first person to ask me to dance after the Greening \u2013 other than D, of course \u2013 was Mary. As usual, she was a bundle of nerves and insecurities, but I guess that\u2019s understandable. She was careful to thank me many times for the help the motley gave her during the troubles with her fetch. She\u2019s obviously still at least a little smitten with me. I tried to put her at ease, but I\u2019m not sure if it worked. In the end, I kissed her lightly on the forehead and invited her to come by the Dream House in a few days to hang out. We\u2019ll see how things go from there. I like Mary; she\u2019s adorable, and I wouldn\u2019t mind frolicking with her a bit if she\u2019s willing\u2026 but I need to make sure she understands that anything that develops between us would be purely physical. I don\u2019t want to end up hurting her.<br /> <br /> She was very inquisitive, and seemed particularly interested in catching up on the internal politics of the Spring Court. She asked about Princess Jolie and Desiree, and she wanted to know who Felicity was and why Jolie seemed so interested in her. She asked about the Warlock\u2019s Handmaidens, too, but I guess that\u2019s only natural. Maybe some of my more suspicious motley-mates are rubbing off on me, but I started to wonder if she had some hidden reason for asking so many questions.<br /> <br /> Oleander found me again next, muttering something about how she had danced with me more than Flores, so she was \u201cwinning.\u201d I\u2019m not one hundred percent sure, but I think she was mostly joking about that. I get the impression that the two of them don\u2019t really dislike each other; they might even have a strained sort of friendship beneath the surface, but there\u2019s a friendly rivalry there, too. Since they\u2019re both plant-type elementals, I think Oleander might be a little threatened by the more feminine, flowery presence that is Flores.<br /> <br /> I noticed that the Handmaidens tried to dance with Jacob at some point, but he brushed them off (politely, of course) in favor of spending more time with Luna. Ace ended up clinging to one of the chandeliers along with the Warlock of Night, who seemed quite impressed with his willingness to do bizarre things to keep up with her (if she only knew, right?). Calamity disappeared for a while about an hour after the Greening, and Gawain danced with Felicity during her absence (she slipped off a little while later, presumably to avoid falling to Marguerite\u2019s seductive charms).<br /> <br /> D found me after Oleander left, and I could tell she was upset. \u201cEverything okay, sweetie?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah,\u201d she muttered unconvincingly, \u201cI just need to tell you something and you\u2019re not going to like it.\u201d<br /> <br /> I pulled her into a deserted hallway. \u201cWhat\u2019s wrong, D?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s nothing too bad,\u201d she assured me, \u201cI just did some things yesterday that I\u2019m not proud of, and I got a little roughed up, and I went to Flores for healing this morning. She promised she wouldn\u2019t tell anyone, but she says she\u2019s worried about me, and I think she\u2019s about to blab it to you.\u201d<br /> <br /> I took her by the shoulders, trying to look compassionate and supportive. \u201cWhat did you do, D? Are you okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m fine, Lori,\u201d she said quickly. \u201cI just needed to work out some frustration, so I went to this biker bar in Los Angeles. I found the prettiest girl in the place \u2013 you know, the one all the guys were trying to impress \u2013 and I bashed her head against the bar. I think I might have broken her nose. I\u2026 don\u2019t really remember many details after that, but I know I felt a lot better when it was all over.\u201d<br /> <br /> I was quiet for a minute, but I\u2019m sure my disapproval showed on my face. \u201cI have two questions for you, D,\u201d I said softly. \u201cFirst, are you sure you\u2019re okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cI got a little scraped up, but Flores was able to heal it all. And you know I can heal myself by draining a little life from other people.\u201d<br /> <br /> I hugged her. \u201cI\u2019m truly glad,\u201d I said. \u201cNow what about the poor girl in the bar?\u201d<br /> <br /> She grinned at me. \u201cShe\u2019ll be fine, Lori. I promise I didn\u2019t hurt anyone too badly.\u201d<br /> <br /> I rolled my eyes. \u201cWhy did I have to fall in love with a Summer Courtier?\u201d I asked with mock exasperation.<br /> <br /> We went back into one of the ballrooms after that for a bit more mingling. Things went well for a while. At one point Captain Jack slipped up behind the Handmaidens, grabbed them both about the waist, and carried them out of the room, loudly proclaiming: \u201cno time to explain!\u201d He later strode into another room wearing one of the Handmaidens like a backpack. Monica followed him \u2013 a bemused look on her face \u2013 wearing the other one. The Captain referred to the Handmaidens as his \u201cutility backpacks.\u201d No, I don\u2019t get it either.<br /> <br /> Things got a little dodgy after that. D sort of stalked up to me looking angry, and when I asked her what was wrong, she just sort of shook her head in Flores\u2019 direction. Flores was walking towards us with a nervous, upset look on her face, and D muttered something about how she was going to have to hurt the poor flower girl. I put my hand on her shoulder in what I hoped was a reassuring manner.<br /> <br /> \u201cLori\u2026 I need to talk to you for a minute,\u201d Flores said softly.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou don\u2019t need to say anything to her,\u201d D snapped.<br /> <br /> I tightened my grip on her shoulder slightly. \u201cIt\u2019s okay, sweetie,\u201d I said softly. She nodded after a minute, but her look didn\u2019t soften. Flores, for her part, looked miserable as she led me out of the ballroom.<br /> <br /> She took a deep breath once she was certain we were alone. \u201cDe la Rocha came to me this morning, and she\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I put up a hand to stop her. \u201cI know,\u201d I said softly, \u201cshe already told me. She\u2019s working through some tough issues right now, and she lashed out.\u201d<br /> <br /> Her face fell. \u201cShe\u2019s going to hate me for telling you,\u201d she said.<br /> <br /> I tried to smile reassuringly. \u201cMaybe for a day or two,\u201d I said, \u201cbut she\u2019ll come around. Deep down she knows that you\u2019re telling me because you care about her. She just needs a little time, and a little space, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay,\u201d she sniffed.<br /> <br /> D was still glowering at nobody in particular when I made my way back to her, but she did her best to hide it. I pulled her into a hug and asked her \u201cyou wanna get out of here?\u201d<br /> <br /> Her fake smile slowly transformed into a real one. \u201cYeah,\u201d she said softly, \u201cI\u2019d like that.\u201d<br /> <br /> We made our way around the various dance floors saying goodbye to everyone. Princess Jolie barely acknowledged us; she was too wrapped up in Desiree and Felicity to pay anyone else much mind. I let the motley know that we were leaving so that nobody would worry, but they all seemed to be in good hands. Jacob and Luna were hanging out together, and I later heard that Jacob had turned down the Handmaidens\u2019 offer to dance <u>twice</u>. Gawain and Calamity were still working security, so they couldn\u2019t leave yet. Marguerite was pouting because Felicity had slipped her grasp, so I pulled Julia aside as D gave our French beauty a little pep talk.<br /> <br /> \u201cFeeling better?\u201d she said with a little smirk.<br /> <br /> \u201cMuch,\u201d I admitted. \u201cLook, Julia\u2026 I know I\u2019ve been sort of wrapped up in myself and my own problems for the last few days. It was a hard time for me, and you\u2019ve been really great. All of my friends have been there for me, but you went above and beyond. You looked after me, you helped me through it, and\u2026 you <u>cared</u> when I really needed that from someone. It might have seemed like I didn\u2019t notice or appreciate it\u2026 but that\u2019s not true.\u201d I leaned in and gave her a long, lingering kiss. \u201cThank you, honey,\u201d I said when we separated.<br /> <br /> She smiled at me. \u201cThat\u2019s what friends are for, right?\u201d she said.<br /> <br /> It got me thinking. I\u2019m truly madly deeply in love with D. I\u2019ve never felt this way about anyone else. What I feel for Julia and Marguerite isn\u2019t the same\u2026 but it\u2019s more than just friendship. I do love them, even if it\u2019s not quite the deep emotional and <u>spiritual</u> connection I feel with D. I didn\u2019t mention any of these thoughts to her at the time; I wanted to sort out my own feelings before I brought it up to her.<br /> <br /> D and I headed out after that. The drive back to the Dream House was quiet and comfortable. At one point D raised an eyebrow and said \u201cdo I need to ask if I\u2019m staying over tonight?\u201d<br /> <br /> I chuckled. \u201cIf I had my way you\u2019d never leave,\u201d I quipped. \u201cI do need to head to church in the morning, though.\u201d<br /> <br /> She pouted. \u201cNo sex tonight?\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled. \u201cI didn\u2019t say that, though I\u2019d be happy just cuddling. I just want to know you\u2019re close, D. But if you spend a little time convincing me\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> She stretched, which made it challenging for me to keep my eyes on the road. \u201cWell, sex or not, I\u2019m getting out of this damn dress as soon as we get to your room.\u201d<br /> <br /> She was as good as her word\u2026 and she had another surprise for me, too. As she removed her lavender panties, I saw that she had tried her hardest to convince me that her hair was <u>naturally</u> purple.<br /> <br /> I hadn\u2019t been kidding before; I wasn\u2019t really in the mood for physical love (I know, shocking, right?). But D was hot to trot, and I just couldn\u2019t resist her. Purple hair. Purple eye shadow. Purple lipstick. Purple\u2026 I just fell into it. Something welled up within me, and I was tired of fighting it. Whatever the Empress put inside me was triggered. The adoration, the worship, and the lust rose up, and my last coherent thought was that at least I was channeling the feelings toward someone I <u>really</u> loved.<br /> <br /> I came back to myself a few orgasms later. I didn\u2019t feel good about losing control, but I <u>did</u> feel good about finding D nestled into my arms and giving me that cocky grin I love so much. \u201cFeel better?\u201d she asked when I\u2019d caught my breath.<br /> <br /> I started to cry. I couldn\u2019t help it; my emotions were so up and down it felt like I was riding a roller coaster. She scooted up and pulled my head up against her chest and let me let it all out. \u201cIt wasn\u2019t me,\u201d I bawled. \u201cIt was her. She\u2019s still inside me. I thought I\u2019d gotten away from her, but she\u2019s still there. I\u2019ll never be free.\u201d<br /> <br /> When I\u2019d calmed down a little, D whispered in my ear, stroking my hair. \u201cYou let go,\u201d she said gently. \u201cYou let it out. You must really trust me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMore than anything,\u201d I said. \u201cBut D\u2026 it wasn\u2019t <u>me</u> just now\u2026 it was what she <u>made</u> me. Don\u2019t you get it? The purple\u2026 it triggers something in me. I was conditioned to respond to it. And I don\u2019t want you to think\u2026 I don\u2019t want you to <u>ever</u> think that\u2019s all this is to me.\u201d<br /> <br /> She shushed me gently. \u201cNever thought it for a second, babe,\u201d she said. \u201cSo what if it\u2019s because of something they did to you in Arcadia? Use it, make it work for you, like you do with your wings. If the color of my hair makes you all hot and bothered, well, there are worse things, right? Do you regret making love to me?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo,\u201d I said.<br /> <br /> \u201cWould that have happened if you\u2019d been with some other chick with purple hair?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cProbably not,\u201d I admitted.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo why are you upset? Why are you fighting it so hard? Forgive yourself, Lori, and let\u2019s get some sleep, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> I figured she was right, so I set the alarm (for about two hours later) and curled up in her arms. The cruel facts of my anatomy dictate that I\u2019m almost always the \u201coutside spoon\u201d when we cuddle up together, but this time we slept facing each other, and D gathered me into her arms and held me against her chest. I felt safe, and warm, and loved, and fell asleep almost immediately.<br /> <br /> The alarm hit me like a sledgehammer what felt like seconds later, and I think D was groping blindly for something to throw at it while I got up and turned it off. The room didn\u2019t want to settle into focus for some reason, and my eyelids refused to stay open without help, so I gathered up my glamour and used a contract to give myself a little more energy. \u201cI\u2019m heading to church,\u201d I said brightly as I made my way toward the bathroom. \u201cYou want to come with me?\u201d<br /> <br /> Her response was something like \u201c<i>murffle</i>,\u201d which I interpreted as a no. She was lying on her back scratching herself idly under her right breast and snoring loudly when I returned to the bedroom and started getting dressed. \u201cI\u2019ll be back in a few hours,\u201d I assured her, \u201cmaybe a teensy bit later than usual today. Love you, babe.\u201d<br /> <br /> She smacked her lips once, smiled, and muttered something that sounded like \u201cluvlori.\u201d It was adorable, and I brushed her hair out of her face and kissed her gently on the cheek before I headed out.<br /> <br /> The service was beautiful as usual. I sang in the choir and listened to Dad preach about courage. I think that was when I made up my mind to do what I\u2019ve known I had to do for a couple of weeks now. So after the benediction, as the congregation filed out, I asked the Reverend Wells if I could speak to him privately about a personal matter. As usual, he smiled, took my hand, and told me that he was always at my disposal.<br /> <br /> Fifteen minutes later we were seated in his office. \u201cHow can I help you today, Lorelei?\u201d he asked indulgently.<br /> <br /> I lowered my eyes. \u201cI need to tell you something, Reverend,\u201d I began. \u201cI\u2019m seeing someone new. It\u2019s not a traditional relationship. I\u2019m\u2026 I\u2019m dating another woman.\u201d<br /> <br /> His eyes widened a little, but that was all the reaction I could see from him. \u201cI see,\u201d he said after a moment. \u201cWell, it\u2019s a complicated issue, of course, and I\u2019m certain you\u2019re grappling with it on a personal level as well. It\u2019s not the first time this has come up within this congregation\u2026 though of course I\u2019m not at liberty to reveal the names of the others.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course,\u201d I said, hardly daring to believe what I was hearing.<br /> <br /> \u201cI am an old man, Lorelei, and I\u2019m not certain how I feel personally about this issue, if that\u2019s what you\u2019re asking me,\u201d he said slowly. \u201cBut if you\u2019re worried that this church will no longer accept you, then I can put your mind at ease on that count. I will not turn you away. You will always be welcome here, my dear\u2026 and your paramour as well, if you\u2019d like to bring her along some day.\u201d<br /> <br /> It was more than I had hoped for, considering how Dad had railed against homosexuality back in Iowa. I guess the last thirty-plus years have mellowed him even more than I\u2019d thought. \u201cMy\u2026 my girlfriend isn\u2019t a very religious person, but I\u2019ll ask her if she wants to come to church with me sometime,\u201d I said. \u201cAnd Reverend\u2026 thank you. My faith means a lot to me, and I want you to know how grateful I am for your understanding.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThis girl,\u201d he said after a moment, \u201cdo you love her, Lorelei?\u201d There was something in his face that I couldn\u2019t quite place\u2026 or maybe I was projecting some of my own feelings onto him. I can\u2019t be sure.<br /> <br /> \u201cI do,\u201d I said, \u201cI\u2019ve never been in a relationship like this before.\u201d<br /> <br /> He thought about it for a minute before responding. \u201cLove is tricky, if it\u2019s real. It can be misguided, or infuriating, or dangerous. It is also <u>rare</u>. In my time on this Earth, I\u2019ve been privileged to love very deeply, and I can honestly say that nothing in my life has hurt me as much as that love. But love itself is never evil, Lorelei. If you have found someone to love, then\u2026 quibbling over the object of that love feels petty and ungrateful to me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you,\u201d I said, \u201cthank you so much, Reverend.\u201d I didn\u2019t trust myself to say more, so we said our goodbyes and I made my way back to the Dream House, not sure whether I wanted to laugh or cry or sing.<br /> <br /> Sex Breakfast was well underway when I got there, but Gawain had saved me a crepe. We had more than our usual contingent in attendance, though. I wasn\u2019t particularly surprised to see Luna there, considering how much time she spent with Jacob at the Masquerade. Flores was present as well, after having spent the night with Julia and Marguerite (that really only surprised me as I had thought she might want to keep her distance from D for a while). The real shocker was that Becky Wan was there, having spent a presumably enjoyable evening with both Calamity <u>and</u> Gawain\u2026 on the night of their Greening, no less! I\u2019m incredibly jealous of one of those three\u2026 I just wish I could decide which one.<br /> <br /> Julia apparently likes my church clothes. She kept staring at me while I ate, and when I announced that I was going to get D up, she followed me out into the hall, pushed me up against the wall, and kissed me passionately until we were both gasping. \u201cSorry,\u201d she muttered as she pulled away.<br /> <br /> I stopped her, pulled her back, and kissed her more tenderly. \u201cI\u2019m not,\u201d I said, putting a little heat into it.<br /> <br /> \u201cThings are okay with you and de la Rocha now?\u201d she asked. \u201cAll greened up and ready to get back to normal?\u201d The question was layered with sarcasm, but I could see the genuine concern behind it.<br /> <br /> \u201cYep,\u201d I said brightly. \u201cCouldn\u2019t be better.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGood,\u201d she said sultrily, \u201cbecause Insincere Marguerite and I intend to claim some quality time with both of you this evening. And\u2026 you can wear these clothes to start with, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> I couldn\u2019t help but laugh. \u201cWouldn\u2019t miss it,\u201d I promised.<br /> <br /> I wandered upstairs and poked my naked, disheveled, wonderful girlfriend until she agreed to get out of bed (what eventually got her moving was the information that Julia and Marguerite had claimed us for the evening, actually). She immediately went to one of her drawers in my bureau and pulled out one of her usual punk outfits and started putting it on. When she was done, she turned around and winked at me.<br /> <br /> \u201cThere\u2019s my girl,\u201d I breathed, and the two of us went downstairs together.<br /> <br /> Once there, D sighed and pulled Flores out of the room, and the two of them went upstairs and began talking loudly in Spanish. I don\u2019t know what they said, but both of them looked a bit happier when they returned, and D told me later that they\u2019d made up. Apparently Flores offered to let D hit her, but she declined (which is a good thing, as D could probably put a fist right through Flores if she wanted to).<br /> <br /> When D got back, I sort of casually sidled up next to her, and she put an arm around me comfortably. \u201cSo\u2026 I told my dad about us after church today,\u201d I said casually. I admit, it was funny to see her stiffen and tense up.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat did he say?\u201d she asked with feigned nonchalance.<br /> <br /> I smiled. \u201cHe was cool about it. I\u2019m still a member of the church in good standing, and he even asked if I wanted to bring you by sometime.\u201d She relaxed a bit, and I pressed my advantage. \u201cI don\u2019t want to push you into anything, D,\u201d I said, \u201cbut if you don\u2019t mind, I want you to meet him sometime. You know, when you\u2019re ready.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cI\u2019ll have to work up to it,\u201d she admitted, \u201cbut I know it\u2019s important to you. I\u2019ll do it.\u201d I can\u2019t wait to introduce my girlfriend to my Dad!<br /> <br /> Ace drifted in even later than I did, spinning some pretty disturbing tales about the evening he spent with the Warlock of Night. And here I\u2019d always thought he was pretty much asexual\u2026 I guess he\u2019s just reserved. He went downstairs and got his pet caiman \u2013 called \u201cVesuvius\u201d today \u2013 and took it outside so that it could swim in the fountain. I protested weakly, but Ace was insistent.<br /> <br /> While the others discussed some cockamamie plan to pull fire-breathing piranhas out of Ace\u2019s dreams, I found myself thinking about the bond between Ace and Vesuvius. He can talk to the little \u2018gator, and even get it to follow simple commands, thanks to the affinity he feels for reptiles. It occurred to me that logically I should have a similar connection to birds, and I began to wonder if I could develop the same sorts of powers. Probably best to wait until I\u2019m alone to try it out, though. I <u>really</u> don\u2019t want to have to explain to the others why I\u2019m trying to talk to the pigeons at the fountain.<br /> <br /> We\u2019re heading to the Hedge House in a few minutes to try to spruce the place up a bit. The others are talking about adding a moat, but I don\u2019t know if they\u2019re serious or not, as they also keep talking about filling it with the aforementioned fire-breathing piranhas. Sometimes I wonder about this group.<br /> <br /> Still, I can\u2019t complain. I have a motley of wonderful crazy friends who care about me and want to keep me safe. I have an even closer friend who likes it when I dress up as a sexy choirgirl. I have a <u>wonderful</u> girlfriend who loves me for my faults, and a father who accepts me for who and what I am, even if he doesn\u2019t really know it yet. As far as blessings go\u2026 I must admit that I\u2019ve lost count.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T01:42:25-07:00","id":463209,"title":"","content":"<b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> <b><u><b><u>Sunday June 15<sup>th</sup></u></b></u></b><br /> <br /> I am a happy little monster today. Oh yes indeed I am. You know, I'm not going to say Snow Globe was worth it, but right now I am almost fucking blissdrunk enough to. Yeah, life is that fucking good right now. If you're reading this Gawain, I hope you know just how happy you made me this weekend. You are my light and we Darklings need that more than any of us want to admit.<br /> <br /> I am supposed to be changing to dig a moat and as I'm sitting here half dressed I can't help but turn to keep trying to get a good look at the body art those friends of Captain Jack painted on my back. I had decided that if Jack was going to be dressed as me, I had to either stay in the closet and miss everything or change outfits. And the logical choice was to dress as Jack. Only hitch was that he was dressed full on luchador. The boots and tights and mask were simple enough, but he was shirtless and had a temporary tattoo painted on his back that looked like something from an 80's metal album cover. I wavered a second and I considered pasties or something but then I just shook that off and said fuck it. If I was going to do it, I was going to do it fucking right. He didn't seem terribly surprised with my decision and he directed me to the sisters, but only after I promised to pay them even if they said I didn't need to. Well, I couldn't not ask why and Jack was happy enough to share the story. Apparently, some years back, the Captain had caught wind of a border smuggling operation that was selling the illegals into slavery at brothels and the like. He intercepted the crew and made his displeasure known by punching their truck and then the scum driving it and setting the cargo free. When I first heard of the Sacred Band of the Golden Standard all I could think of was Gaston with the bragging and the false heroics and while Captain Jack is certainly larger than life and not afraid to boast, underneath the theatrics that ogre is a real hero. I am glad he sought out Gawain and I am fortunate to call him a friend.<br /> <br /> Once the sisters had painted my back, I returned and got ready. It wasn't an overly lengthy process, the Playboy Bunny suit isn't that complex and with the full coverage of the mask Gawain had made for me there was no need for makeup or doing more than tucking my hair up. Lori was on pins and needles, checking her phone and her makeup and her outfit in a fairly non-stop rotation. I tried a bit to cheer her and a test of her cleavage's suitability as a target did break the tension for a bit. As security, Gawain and I had to be there early and so we left before De la Rocha arrived. I'll admit, I was a bit worried. But De la Rocha did show up as planned and when she and Lori made their entrance together it was heart-warming to see them together. DLR had departed quite a bit from her usual look. She was decked out in a gown of purple and had makeup with shades of it as well, all of it matched that familiar streak in her hair. She was quite lovely like that and the way she and Lori were looking at each other as they arrived was adorable.<br /> <br /> Each arrival was formally announced. The motley had a common theme centered around our roles at the dream house. Lori was the Siren, Insincere Marguerite the Watchful Eyes, Jacob the Master of Spirits, and Ace was the Keeper of the Egg. When the majordomo announced \u201cLord Gawain Vert of the Dawn Court, Sentinel of the Malibu Dream House and on his arm, Lady Calamity of the Autumn Court, Flashing Blade of the Malibu Dream House\u201d I couldn't help but beam. The reality of The Fae and the horrors they inflict isn't often pretty but every now and then you have a moment that is every bit the kind of fairy tale magic that Katt dreamed of. That was one of them and I just drifted along and basked in it while it lasted.<br /> <br /> The Latino changelings were Don or Dona as appropriate. And Moon was Mystery Moon of the Autumn Court, which was fitting. Most of us had elaborate titles with all of our Entitlements and court positions and such while some simply had witty or clever titles added. Joan was aptly introduced as the Blazing Summer Sentinel. Julia was the Creator of Wicked Eerie Tableaus. Felicity was the Solar Mirage.<br /> <br /> The Handmaidens were Some of them want to use you and some of them want to abuse you, which certainly suited them or at least the image they work so diligently to show. The most amusing in my opinion was 'Captain Jack Martinez of the Dusk Court, Just Some Guy, You Might Have Seen Him\u2019. Of course, he was carried in on a litter by eight absolutely delicious muscleboys all oiled up and singing O' Fortuna. Let me just state for the record, that ogre has mighty fine taste in beefcake.<br /> <br /> As security, I steered clear of the bars while I was circulating through the dance floors. And while I did spend more time watching than dancing, I didn't wallflower it up the whole time. I certainly didn't hold a candle to Lori's dance card (I think she spent the whole night on the dance floor) but I was perfectly content to sway with Handsome and Becky a few times. And, of course, there was the business of mischief with Gawain and Captain Jack. As we came to the appointed hour, Jack peeked out of the closet we'd planted our costumes in to let me know he was ready. I drifted close and let him grab me. I gave a suitably indignant squeak and kicked my heels in the air pointlessly as he plucked me off my feet as effortlessly as Gawain does. (And yeah, I did kinda like it. I guess manhandling just trips my trigger in general.) He placed me in the closet and I gave him a thumbs up as he closed the door. I changed outfits as quickly as I could and when I emerged Gawain and Jack where dancing to the vast amusement of everyone in the area. Gawain missed a step when he saw me and Jack had to nudge him to keep him from breaking the routine too soon. I had a flash of nerves as a few heads turned to see what had distracted him and join those near the closet who'd glanced over at my return. But it was far too late to rethink my decision to go topless. I gave a smirk and threw my shoulders back purposefully and strode into the crowd as nonchalantly as I could. Gawain and Jack where the center of attention, but I garnered a good share as I moved in to watch the reveal. I am not sure I want to do anything quite that brazen again any time soon but it was a hell of a rush. As I reached them, Gawain 'accidentally' knocked one of Jack's spikes off and sent it sailing to land square in Lori's cleavage. And that was the cue for the DJ to play an exaggerated record scratch and start up Yakety Sax as Gawain and I started to chase Jack around the room and on a winding route through the other two dance rooms. The ballroom's orchestra were kind enough to humor us by also switching to the famous chase music as we passed through that room (and judging from the looks we got when we made the arrangements before the ball I think some of them had been waiting years to do something like that.) As we moved into the rave room, we got a suitably techno remixed version and Jack took that moment to loose one of his fake breasts and send it around the room like an oversized superball. As we made our way back into the modern dance room a rope ladder dropped from the now open skylight and Captain Jack caught hold of it and was lifted up and away by a waiting helicopter as Gawain shook his fist up at his nemesis amidst a sea of laughter. By this point I was well past my bout of modesty and so as we circulated I was basking rather shamelessly in the attention, especially from Handsome. I swear, you'd think he'd never seen them before or something the way he keep looking (not that I'm complaining, mind you. I loved every second of it.) But before too long Captain Jack slipped back in quietly in his previous attire and so I returned to the closet to change back as well and the night proceeded onward. <br /> <br /> The Handmaidens made the rounds. They introduced themselves to Lori and made a good impression from what she's said. Seems they were quite friendly and complimentary as they danced with her. When they found me, it was a much different approach. They slipped up and flanked me, easing in close and running their fingers along my upper arms as they began to speak. Their touch is cool, almost cold. I guess it's the Leechfinger though I've never noticed De la Rocha's touch to be so unusually chilled. They began to circle like sharks, neither of them breaking contact with my skin as they spoke back and forth, completing each others sentences or sometimes speaking in unison. I'd been expecting them and even looking forward to another round of flirting after our previous run in. But this wasn't the same and their behavior conjured up memories of the Whispering Voices. The featherlight touch of Their cold soft fingers on my torn and tattered flesh as that insane chorus whispered in my ears. Then one of the Handmaidens, Scarlet I think, brushed a shard of my glass experimentally and it sent a jolt through me. I couldn't keep the shiver from my body and I didn't try to. I focused on that sliver of hunger in my glass and I let their little game stoke it. I smiled wickedly at each of them as they took their turn drifting in front of me. I leaned into the teasing brush of fingers and I let my breath come in low growls. And I set myself to giving as good as I got. We flirted with equal parts sex and violence, innuendo laced with hints of murder and hunting. Perhaps they are simply perfect temptresses but I think they were enjoying the verbal dance as much as I was (and I was enjoying it quite muchly indeed). By the time they peeled themselves away to move on, they promised that we'd speak again soon and that they would come see me at the Dream House.<br /> <br /> The chill hadn't left my skin before Gawain was there, hand on my shoulder with practiced caution and a note of concern in his voice. I turned to him and melted into his arms as he swept me out onto the dance floor. My glass was still humming and my blood was rushing from the flirting so as Handsome led me across the floor I called on everything Annika had showed me to make it clear that I was Gawain's and make everyone wish they could be in his place. And while I am certainly not as good as her or Lori, I know I had quite a few eyes on us. As we danced, I did assure him I had no intention of leaving him for the Handmaidens or of murdering them. It was meant to be at lest a little joking to lighten things but he remained worried. He explained that his contract hadn't been able to get a read on either of them and he was just worried about their intentions. I have to agree, I do not trust those two at all and it would be good to have an idea of just what they were up to. Personally, I think part of it is simply that they enjoy the aura of mystery and menace they cultivate but I would be a fool to think they weren't ready, willing and able to make good on that promise of danger. I know they are every bit as deadly as the sharks they were acting like. The problem, of course, is that only makes me want to play with them more.<br /> <br /> Despite the concerns, they did not end up causing security any trouble. Of course, Captain Jack had a hand in that. I do not believe their involvement in his hijinks over the evening was random. I think he was intentionally keeping them out of and from causing trouble.<br /> <br /> And speaking of trouble, their mistress is certainly an interesting woman. The Warlock of Night settled into a corner of the modern dance room shortly after arriving and stayed there most of the night. At a glance, she seemed to be flailing more than dancing, but there was an undeniable grace to the chaos of motion. The other guests gave her a wide berth and she seemed perfectly content to dance alone. But after a while, Ace approached her and did his best to match her gyrations. She adapted her dancing to his presence and seemed pleased well enough that he wasn't too intimidated to approach her. He returned a few times over the night but no one else worked up the verve to dance with her.<br /> <br /> Jacob danced with Insincere Marguerite and Molly Nuit early in the evening but spent most of his time enjoying the drinks that someone else was mixing and watching the festivities. At least until Luna showed up. It was just before midnight and folks had begun to drift toward the main ballroom when I heard the announcement. I was waiting with Gawain and I excused myself to go greet her. I had not expected to see her at the Ball. Even swaying on those heels and fighting to straighten her dress she was beautiful. Jacob had also come and the moment she laid eyes on him it was clear that he was why she was there. She proceeded to say as much as we started to speak. I knew she had paid him a few discreet visits in the night since they met at the victory party but I hadn't realized it was anything more than just a bit of, as she would say, rutting. We only had time to speak briefly before the Greening started and when I explained that Gawain and I were doing it she was pleased and wish us well. I smiled and left her in Jacob's capable hands, where she remained for the rest of the night. The next time I spotted them the heels had been abandoned and they were dancing quite happily and talking. Apparently the Handmaidens did approach him not once but twice seeking a dance but he declined, though he did dance with Willow Black later in the evening. I believe the Night Court diplomat had the courtesy to ask Luna first. After watching them, I was not surprised that they left together.<br /> <br /> Austin lead the Greening ceremony. He introduced it with just a dash of humor but made sure the significance of it clear to everyone present. Lorelei and De la Rocha went first. Lori put the ivy wreath in her girl's hair and looked into her eyes. Her words were unpracticed but honest and obviously heartfelt. Then they leaned in and kissed. There were cheers and calls. It was such a perfectly storybook moment. <br /> <br /> I felt a fresh wave of nervousness as I stood there watching with my hand in Gawain's gauntlet. It was all so fucking perfect... Lori was so fucking perfect. I glanced over, sure Gawain would be watching that lingering kiss as wistfully as everyone else seemed to be. But he was smiling brightly like he was the king of the world with the belle of the ball on his arm instead of some mad woman in a horror mask and bunny suit. Seeing that look made me relax and straighten. I truly cannot fathom what he sees in me but I was clearly the one he wanted.<br /> <br /> Once Lori and her sweetheart yielded the stage it was Joan and Andromeda's turn. As Joan placed the ivy in the little sweetling's hair Andromeda was positively glowing. I know there are some that are concerned that Joan's devotion to her lover has distracted her too much from watching over the freehold's security but seeing them together and especially up there I refuse to think that helping to bring them together was a mistake. Joan's speech was eloquent if more a warning to all present that she was prepared to defend her love's well-being and honor to the death than anything else. But then, protectiveness is how she expresses her feelings for the girl and it's what the little grey lamb needs.<br /> <br /> Gawain and I took the stage last. We had chosen to both lay claim to each other. Gawain lifted my twisted mask up to expose my hair so he could set the wreath in my hair properly before taking one knee before me so I could place my own ivy around his helmet without having to reach up awkwardly. As I settled it in place he spoke solemnly and earnestly. He'd taken the time to find and adapt an oath of fealty. It was so perfectly Gawain. He'd made those words his own and he meant every single one of them. I was left blinking away tears as I tried to think of how to answer him. I hadn't prepared anything and even if I had I don't think I would have said it after that. It was beautiful and so terribly honest. I brushed the side of his helmet and I told him once more that I was his monster. It's not poetic or pretty but it is the truth and it's what I have to offer. Once I'd finished, he just rose and showed me it was enough as he claimed me with a kiss so deep and tender. I slipped my arms around him and kissed him back for all I was worth. I don't understand how he can love a monster like me the way he does but I don't have to understand it to know it's true.<br /> <br /> He swept me up and carried me off the stage and I curled into him. And as the music resumed he set me down and we shared the next dance together and for a few perfect minutes there was nothing beyond the two of us. Maybe that sounds cheesy as hell but fuck it, I am allowed to be as sappy and saccharine sweet as I damn well please when I want to be and that's how Gawain makes me feel.<br /> <br /> I danced with Handsome for a few songs since despite us both being security we had the earpieces to let us know if anything happened. And as we were doing so, Captain Jack made a show of sneaking up behind the Handmaidens and then with a shout of 'No time to explain!\u201d he grabbed one of them under each arm and ran off with them. We trailed after them, just in case, and as we caught up with them Natalia was clinging to his back with a bemused expression as he lifted Scarlet and moved around behind a confused Monica, explaining the need for utility backpacks as he placed Scarlet on her back and the night courtier obligingly held on as the ogress then followed Jack as he lead them off. All three women seemed to have no clue what Jack was doing but everyone involved was willing to go along with The Captain's game so there was no reason to break it up or anything.<br /> <br /> While that was going on, the Warlock apparently decided she'd had enough dancing. She Darkling crawled up the wall and settled atop one of the chandeliers to watch the dancing. But I am pretty sure it was Ace she was watching to see how he handled her challenge. Well, being Ace, he was undaunted. He scratched his chin a moment and then shrugged. Moving to the wall, he proceeded to slither up it and across the ceiling to the nearest adjacent chandelier to the one she was on. It wasn't as graceful and his perch creaked ominously with his weight but the Warlock seemed amused and they remained aloft chatting until the hour of the meeting. Her dismount was to roll off and pretty much just bounce harmlessly off the floor to her feet and dust herself off. Ace lowered himself from the hanging light and then dropped to his feet heavily but without injury or stumbling.<br /> <br /> I told Gawain I was going to be off the floor for a bit and slipped away myself. Julia passed me as I stepped away, apparently moving in to keep Handsome occupied while Insincere Marguerite and I both headed back the meeting room.<br /> <br /> Everyone arrived without incident and we got down to the business at hand. Insincere Marguerite and I stood with our respective courts quietly while Queen Charlotte and Willow Black went back and forth over the details of the arrangement. Everyone was in agreement that a pact of mutual aid to our people in each others territory and defense if either court came under direct attack was the goal but the Night Court seemed to find our insistence on details such as exactly what kind of aid and what circumstances would be binding to be overly exacting and tiresome. As the two of them worked on that, the Warlock was amusing herself by toying with a stiletto while Madame Spidertoes fanned herself. It all seemed to be going as expected until the Warlock threw her dagger up into the ceiling and interrupted. She stated that the real purpose of this meeting was the Hollywood Court's imprisoned gentry. She claimed to know without doubt that the Grand Maw's continued existence was more than rumor but she declined to elaborate without first our agreement to aid them in dealing with the situation. Charlotte clearly wasn't expecting this turn of events and there was a moment as we all tried to react to the sudden shift. I did voice the fact that something had to be done while I whispered to my Queen that we couldn't risk the Night Court taking sole possession of the Grand Maw. That was the moment she'd needed to collect her response and while I did move a little closer I went back to holding my tongue for the most part. Charlotte pointed out that this was the sort of undertaking that might require more than simply our two courts and it was certainly a threat to all of both Malibu and LA. The Warlock countered that the Day court's honor and glory approach would be suicide and that the only reason she'd approached the Autumn Court was that we could keep a secret. She was concerned (not unreasonably) that there was a high risk of someone warning their counterparts in the Hollywood seasonal courts of an impending attack if too many were brought into this. It made good sense, but Charlotte's concern at our two courts facing all of Hollywood alone was equally valid. There was also the matter that she was not willing to commit her followers to something this dangerous without their consent. Things seemed stalled for a moment but I stepped forward and pointed out that we all agreed that something had to be done but before action could be taken more information had to be gained. I then proposed that our Courts agree to share information and to work in concert to gather more for now. Once we had a better idea of what we were facing we would be better able to judge if it was within our Courts' capabilities or if others, and specifically which others, would need to be involved. Much to my relief, everyone present agreed that my suggestion was reasonable. The Warlock retrieved her stiletto and waved to Willow to iron out the details as she went back to idly playing with the dagger. I stepped back as Charlotte and Willow worked out the details of the agreement. As I was looking to the Warlock and Spidertoes, I realized something that sent a knot to the pit of my stomach. Spidertoes was watching the Warlock's weapon intently, but she didn't have the tension of someone expecting an attack. And the movements of her fan were likewise of great import to the Warlock once I started looking for something suspicious. The longer I watched, the more certain I became that they were passing messages back and forth. Though I believe that the Warlock's gestures were mixed in with random fidgeting that forced Spidertoes to scowl and squint ever so slightly as she tried to decipher what was signal and what was noise. I only paid half an ear to the details but it all seemed fairly cut and dry at that point. Once we'd come to agreement, a few parting words were exchanged. I did step over and nod to the Warlock of Night, telling her that I did feel personally that this matter was one of great import and that I looked forward to working alongside her court in the coming nights. She mentioned that she'd heard of me and seemed to find my statement interesting (well she was at least not dismissive of it) but she said she had other matters and could not linger.<br /> <br /> As we returned, that business became clear. She went to the modern dance room and made her way directly to Ace. Apparently at some point during the meeting he'd ended up the one wearing Scarlet as a backpack and had begun looking to find who's backpack her wife was. The Warlock walked up and without batting an eye removed Scarlet and produced a collar and leash. That didn't particularly surprise me but the fact that Ace let her slip it around his neck and lead him away certainly did. I frowned a bit but while the Warlock's behavior is erratic, I am sure she is too shrewd to use a Contract or other magic to drag someone oath-bound to both Insincere Marguerite and myself off against their better judgment. I decided it was most likely just that he had peaked her interest by being the only one that had not been put off by her behavior and apparently he'd not found himself a bird of the right feather before.<br /> <br /> For my own part, I had asked Queen Charlotte if she would do me the honor of a dance while we were walking back and she'd agreed. It was a pleasure to dance with her and I do wish I could have simply enjoyed it. As befits a monarch, she is a skilled dancer and blessed with spidery grace. She did, of course, lead with confidence and a firm hand. She is so very much a predator and part of me could not help but imagine being with her. But sadly I know I would make for poor prey. I believe we both do. And I had an ulterior motive for asking her to dance. I leaned in and whispered to her quietly of my discovery that Madame Spidertoes and the Warlock had been exchanging messages. She was concerned. Spidertoes was the one that made this meeting happen after all. She asked if I thought Spidertoes was working to dangerous purposes. I honestly said I wasn't sure. Clearly she was prepared to break proper convention and that was not something she would do lightly. It might be that she is simply convinced that the necessity of getting the Grand Maw away from the Hollywood courts is that important. But it could be that she has darker motives to want the gentry. I pointed out that it would be suspicious to cut her out of things, so perhaps the best solution would be to simply continue as before but be wary of Madam Spidertoes' advice. I hate casting suspicions on her without more to go on but it wasn't something I could keep from Charlotte. And as we finished our dance I reminded her that I followed the Autumn Crown because she wore it rather than the other way around. Of course, as much as I respect her and do genuinely like her, part of what makes her a good leader is that she will do whatever is in the Court's best interests. I have no doubt that if the Court's well-being required it she would harm me, but at least she wouldn't be happy about it.<br /> <br /> By this point, the Masquerade began to thin out. Lori and De la Rocha actually left fairly early. Unfortunately, it wasn't just that they'd been apart the past two days and wanted to be alone together. (Though I am pretty sure that was part of it.) In the course of coming to grips with her love for another woman, De la Rocha had opted for some high impact therapy. She had apparently walked into a biker bar in LA and found the prettiest girl there and walked up to grab a fistful of her hair and slam her face into the bar hard enough to break her nose. This triggered the ire of all the men who'd been hitting on her or thinking of hitting on her or just enjoying the view. And while being a leechfinger does give one a certain edge in a brawl, she did not walk away unscathed. Not wanting to show up tonight looking like she'd gone ten rounds with an angry mob she went to Flores to heal her wounds. Unfortunately, Flores had decided that getting into bar fights was unhealthy behavior and asking a friend to heal it up quietly to keep it from one's girlfriend was doubly bad. So she decided she was going to tell Lori. De la Rocha told her first, but only so she'd hear it from her. Apparently the whole mess included De la Rocha nearly punching Flores in the middle of the modern dance room before she and Lori left.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Insincere Marguerite and Julia had collected Flores and were soothing her. Since Felicity had foiled my Darkling sister's plans of seducing her and despoiling her virtue by leaving during the meeting the pair of them ended up taking Flores home with them.<br /> <br /> As the mansion continued to empty out, I caught up to Handsome and pulled him out to the dance floor. As we danced, I asked him how he felt about Becky. He didn't express any dislike and so I went on to mention how rough Becky's week had been. He agreed. So I told him that I was pretty sure she and I shared favorite stress reduction methods and pointed out that fighting wasn't looking likely. I am pretty sure he had figured out where I was going with things and I told him I liked Becky and I wanted to take care of her. But I also made it clear that tonight I was his and if he wanted it his alone. But my Gawain is a good man and the prospect of making me happy by letting me make Becky happy and thus being in bed with two happy women appealed to both the good and the man.<br /> <br /> So we made our way to find her and did so as she was sitting and watching Captain Jack demonstrate his amazing pectoral muscle control by using them to squeeze condiments onto hot dogs. He was making the rounds offering them to all the ladies. I strolled up and sat on one side of her while Gawain sat on the other. I couldn't resist getting a wiener from Captain Jack when he made his way by and as I nibbled away Gawain and I flirted with her and I pointed out that tradition frowned on sleeping with one member of a Greened couple but was rather nonspecific about sleeping with both of them. And that was when Becky thumbed her radio and informed the remaining security personnel that she would be leaving as she had something, nay two somethings to do and reached to take each of us by the hand and lead us out. I had not expected her to be quite that enthusiastic and I did ask about three of the remaining security leaving but she quickly made sure everything was covered for the few remaining guests and we were off to the Dream House.<br /> <br /> The ride back to the Dream House was entirely too long for this needful little monster. My night had been well filled with flirtation and the fact that everything had gone the way I wanted it to had my head spinning. No one got punched or eaten or shot or mind controlled. Secret meeting was secret and I managed to come off looking pretty competent and reliable to not only my own monarch but to the Warlock of Night which will be good since we're going to be working together. And fuck it, apparently I even was going to get to have my cake and eat it too. (And oh yes was there much having and eating indeed.)<br /> <br /> I dozed but never slipped fully into sleep. I was content to lay there nestled against one of Gawain's sides with his arm curled around my back (carefully low enough to avoid the glass) while Becky was draped over the other side of him. Her face was inches away, eyes closed and expression relaxed and peaceful as her hair teased my cheek and lips lazily. And the soft even sound of Gawain's heart beat in my ear and the soft brush of his breath across my hair and neck only made the time perfect. Once the sun started to warm to late morning I teased those silken strands until Becky's slow sleepy squirming gave way to waking with a heavy lidded look of arousal and I convinced her to join me in giving Gawain a proper wakeup. It was a while after that before we made it to the kitchen for breakfast.<br /> <br /> Gawain asked Becky what she wanted and she mentioned that she'd heard how good his crepes were. And so she sat cuddling with me at the table while he made them. Not that we were the only ones. Luna had stayed and she was quite happily planted in Jacob's lap. And Insincere Marguerite was happily lounging with Julia and Flores. It was lazily flirty and shamelessly decedent and just about perfect.<br /> <br /> Lori returned from church and drew no shortage of attention in her church clothes. Julia in particular found the look to her liking. Gawain left Becky and I to fix the remaining crepes while Lori went up to change and wake De la Rocha. When they came down things did get a little tense. But she and Flores stepped upstairs and while there were some raised voices there was no yelling or violence. When they came back down they had talked things out.<br /> <br /> Lori explained that while she was at church, she had spoken to her father and come out to him. From what she said it went well. She is still welcome and is apparently not the only non-heterosexual in her congregation. And apparently he is interested in meeting De la Rocha. He may not realize who Lori is and so I doubt he understands how much this means to her but I do and I was glad to see it.<br /> <br /> And on the heels of that Ace came strolling in. Seems he had quite a time with the Warlock of Night. He headed down to bring up Vesuvius and carry him out to let him swim in the fountain. And as the conversation drifted to fire-breathing piranha I made a comment that Lori might never forgive me for. But the way both Gawain and Ace's faces lit up was worth it. Gawain has enough contract of Dreams to bring things out of a dream. And it's hard but sometimes if you do it well enough they don't fade away. So all Ace has to do is dream of fire-breathing piranha and then let Gawain pull them out of his dreams. Gawain isn't sure he's good enough to make something as complex as a living fantastic creature real and lasting yet, but once he's a little better who knows?<br /> <br /> And that is how I wound up recruited to dig a moot in the Hedge this afternoon. It was kinda my idea since we would need a place to keep these fire breathing piranha. They had no luck convincing anyone else to help with the moot but fixing up the Hollow itself had the rest of the motley's interest. I don't care. I am still fucking floating after last night. And it's the Hedge. Why the hell shouldn't we have a moot filled with fire-breathing piranha guarding our magical fairy castle?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> And tonight was the perfect night to get to know her a bit better. We stood by the sidelines for a bit and talked and sipped at our drinks. It was good to catch up with her. While we were talking the two Handmaidens made their way over to us and started talking to me. More accurately, they were flirting with me. They seemingly ignored Luna and focused on me. Lucky me. Scarlet just seemed interested in getting me to dance with them. Natalia on the other had actually asked me in accented Russian if I was originally from Russia. I answered her in kind that I was, but had moved here a few years ago. After that little opening the two ladies started up again, but both in Russian this time.<br /> <br /> During this whole thing I could tell that Luna was uncomfortable, which was probably the intention of the Handmaidens. Truth be told, I wasn\u2019t the most comfortable either. Natalia seemed genuinely interested in the topic of Russia, and if she had come up to talk by herself and not started the hard and heavy flirting I might have talked to her for a bit. It\u2019s nice to be able to talk in my native language with someone. Natalia seemed to feel the same way, though Scarlet does speak pretty good Russian. After a couple minutes I could tell that Natalia was not herself Russian. Bulgarian I think, if I heard her accent right. That made me pause and wonder if her interest was actually genuine or if there was an ulterior motive. Bulgarians don\u2019t like Russians. I mean, really don\u2019t like Russians\u2026so her interest suddenly seemed suspect. I could be misreading the whole situation with Natalia, but I didn\u2019t stay alive this long by trusting blindly.<br /> <br /> The ladies eventually asked me to dance, and I politely turned them down letting them know that I was otherwise engaged. The Handmaidens seemed disappointed but went on their way. Luna seemed to breathe a sigh of relief after they left. She asked if flirting in Russian would work on me and I replied \u201cNot from them.\u201d I\u2019ll admit that it was nice to speak in Russian again, but I don\u2019t trust the Handmaidens. Not to mention they were rude. Not to me of course\u2026me they were trying to seduce. They were rude to Luna. They ignored her presence even though I was obviously just talking to her. I may not be the best with people, but I at least still have manners.<br /> <br /> I reassured Luna that I had no interest in the Handmaidens and asked instead if she\u2019d like to dance. She readily agreed, but seemed a bit unsteady on her feet. High heels never did look very practical to me, and they seemed to definitely make Luna uncomfortable. So, I suggested that she just take them off and leave them by the side. Her dress was long enough to hide the fact she was barefoot, and I wanted her to feel comfortable. So, she kicked off her heels and we danced. I discovered that Luna is just as graceful on the dance floor as she is while fighting. Makes sense I suppose, but it was still nice.<br /> <br /> While the Handmaidens were talking to me, Ace was dancing with their mistress. Well, dancing is being generous I suppose. Gyrating is more like it. She seemed interested in his advances, such as they were though. Eventually she stopped dancing and suddenly climbed up the wall and down onto one of the chandeliers hanging from the ceiling. Not to be outdone, Ace slithered up the wall, it\u2019s really the only way to describe it, and settled himself on a nearby chandelier. The Warlock of Night seemed pleased with Ace\u2019s actions. Luna and I moved out from under the chandeliers that they were resting on, just in case.<br /> <br /> During a break, while Luna and I were talking and watching the other people dance, Willow Black came up and basically asked Luna\u2019s permission to dance with me. I think Luna was a bit surprised, and maybe a bit amused, but agreed. So, I danced with Willow Black. Willow was a pretty good dancer too. Not as innately graceful as Luna, but pretty good nonetheless. <br /> <br /> Not long after that Captain Jack came back into the ballroom and \u201csnuck\u201d up to the Handmaidens. He called out loudly \u201cNo time to explain!\u201d and grabbed one under each arm and rushed out of the room. Not sure what that was all about, but the ladies did not seem overly concerned. I remember someone mentioning that Jack has a seemingly honest friendship with them, so they are probably used to his antics. Later Jack came back into the ballroom with Scarlet on his back. Monica followed with Natalia on her back. Monica seemed a bit bemused. The Handmaidens seemed resigned. Jack made some comment about the utility packs being set up. It was all very silly.<br /> <br /> Shortly before Jack\u2019s further silliness the Warlock of Night jumped down from the chandelier and sort of belly flopped and bounced to her feet. Ace followed her down, but he landed more carefully so as to not break his legs. The Warlock seemed impressed. About this time Jack came over and transferred Scarlet from his own back to Ace\u2019s. Ace of course took it all in stride. The Warlock disappeared for a bit after that and Ace continued as he had been, practicing his American accent and carrying Scarlet around. Some point a bit later the Warlock came back up to Ace, removed Scarlet from his back and put a leash around his neck. Ace kind of shrugged and she led him outside. Not hard to figure out what those two were up to. It was a bit unique in that it was Ace going off with someone. As far as I know he hasn\u2019t had any partners since moving into the Dream House. The leash was also a bit odd, but Ace didn\u2019t mind, and that\u2019s all that really matters.<br /> <br /> Later in the evening, after they were done being used as utility belts, the Handmaidens came back over to me and asked one more time to dance. I turned them down for a second time that night and they left seemingly disappointed. I\u2019m not sure if they\u2019re used to being turned down. I supposed I might have danced with them once if Luna hadn\u2019t come, but she did, so it\u2019s kind of a moot point. I mean, the Handmaidens are attractive. I can\u2019t deny that, but they just set off warning bells in my head. They appear to people in whatever manner that person would find attractive. For Calamity it was predatory and sexy. For Lorelei it was sweet and flirty. For me, they played on my homesickness and tried to establish a common thread between us. They are so many different people depending on who they meet, I wonder what they are really like under all the masks? Do they even remember?<br /> <br /> Someone that wears that many faces is hard to trust. You never know if you\u2019re talking to the real person or a persona that they\u2019ve adopted because they think you\u2019ll like it better. One face may be a consummate liar and another unbelievably honest. But which one is real. Who are you really talking to? I may not like their ability to be everything to everyone, but I do understand it. I have used tactics like that in the past. I\u2019m not as good as they are, but I\u2019ve worn my share of masks. I\u2019ve put on faces designed to coax, or console, or to scare. I guess I see myself to some extent in them, and I don\u2019t trust it because I do understand it. Who better to spot a liar, than another liar?<br /> <br /> I really do need to get my head out of that dark place. I can\u2019t seem to help it sometimes though. A thought will pop into my head and my mind runs with it. And they\u2019re not always pleasant thoughts. I suppose that\u2019s why I write in this journal. I exorcise those thoughts from my head and put them down on paper. Realistically I know that talking about all this shit would be the healthy way to deal with it. I would probably help a good bit. Trouble is I have a hard time trusting people, and I\u2019m selfish. I have friends I can trust for the most part. I do trust them. I just don\u2019t trust them with everything. If I did, I would lose them, and I\u2019m selfish and I don\u2019t want to lose them yet.<br /> Okay\u2026back to the dance and what followed\u2026.<br /> <br /> After the Handmaidens left the second time Luna commented that it was getting late. Some guests, including Lorelei and De la Rocha had already left. I asked Luna if she\u2019d like to come back to the Dream House for drinks and she agreed. We retrieved her shoes from the edge of the room and headed out ourselves. Once back at the Dream House I made sure that Luna liked chocolate and proceeded to make chocolate ice cream mudslides. I think they were a hit. I can do frozen drinks in my sleep and they aren\u2019t the most exciting to me, but sometimes I have to remind myself that not everyone lived in a frozen realm and ice cream is a treat. Me, I like hot coffee. The way it burns its way to your stomach. Kind of the way that alcohol does. Ice cream does it to some extent, and it is nice to have something cool I suppose when it is so hot out. I\u2019ve been assured that it will only get warmer as summer approaches and I find that I\u2019m not really looking forward to that. Maybe I can bring some spring snow down from the mountains. I wonder if I can do that yet?<br /> <br /> So, Luna likes chocolate and frozen chocolate mudslides. The drinks were a prelude I suppose, but they were also a good way to go from a very public event to something more intimate. After drinks we went up to my room and got more comfortable. Luna looked nervous and for a minute I wasn\u2019t sure what was going through her head. She\u2019s never been nervous with me in the past. Then she took a breath and asked \u201cat the risk of sounding high school\u201d if we could be boyfriend and girlfriend. I couldn\u2019t help it, I smiled. The question was so innocent and I could see the apprehension written all over her face. The question as to whether or not I wanted to commit myself to someone flashed through my brain in an instant. The expected panic wasn\u2019t really there, and I realized that I really liked spending time with her and planned on doing more of it in the future. So, I looked at her and said that I would like that. And so, I made a little promise in my head that I would do right by Luna and do my best to make her happy.<br /> <br /> **** **** **** ****<br /> <br /> New day, more crepes. Apparently Flores (I think) had heard how wonderful Gawain\u2019s crepes were so he made them special for her, and for the rest of us. There were several of us at brunch, including Flores, De la Rocha, and Becky. I think Becky stayed with Gawain and Calamity, De la Rocha was with Lori of course, and Flores had been with Insincere Marguerite and Julia. I guess the thing that made this afternoon different, besides the sheer number of guests, was the fact that Luna sat down on my lap and stayed there during the whole meal. I wasn\u2019t sure if she was going to want to make our relationship public or not, but that display pretty much put any doubts to rest. I thought I saw a flicker of disappointment from Insincere Marguerite, but I\u2019m not positive on that. I know that she\u2019s happy with Julia and the two of them have been thick as thieves for weeks now. I had thought that perhaps I had been just a passing fancy, but maybe not. I guess time will tell.<br /> <br /> Speaking of relationships, though more familial in nature, Lorelei had some news for the motley this afternoon. Apparently after the church service Lori went to talk to her dad in private. She came out to him and told him that she was dating another girl. According to her he seemed to take it well and even invited De la Rocha to join them at a service sometime. I\u2019ll admit that I felt that same mix of jealousy and happiness for her that I\u2019ve felt in the past. I only expressed the latter to her though. I really am happy that her father took the news well. He may not know that Lori is his little girl, but she does and his acceptance means a lot to her. I hope things continue to go well on that front.<br /> <br /> During brunch interesting conversation usually comes up and this morning was no exception. I\u2019m not exactly sure whose idea it was, but we started talking about the possibility of digging a moat around the Hollow and filling it with water stocked with fire breathing piranha. Yes, Ace was one of the primary people involved, and funnily enough so was Gawain. He was the one that suggested that if Ace dreamed about fire breathing piranha he could pull them out of his dreams and into reality. For a short time at least. We all got involved in the conversation, even Lorelei who wholeheartedly disagreed with the whole plan. I tried to be a voice of reason, but it didn\u2019t go well. The idea had taken hold and I have a bad feeling that I\u2019m going to be one of the poor souls roped into digging that damn moat.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T01:43:15-07:00","id":463210,"title":"","content":"<b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> After the Greening, things quieted down. Mostly. De La Rocha and Flores almost got in a fight, apparently because Flores was badgering De La Rocha about getting in fights to work out her self-loathing. Julia was taking this hard\u2026they are both our lovers, and she is a sentimental girl who still credits Flores with helping us get together. She even bodily stood between the two at one point; gambling De La Rocha would be unable to bear hitting her. To be sure, Julia weakened De La Rocha\u2019s resolve. The situation was not resolved, but the conflict was suspended, at least. Lorelei and De La Rocha left not long after.<br /> <br /> The Clandestine meeting was interesting. I separated from Julia with a kiss and headed there, while she separated off to distract Gawain. Successfully. The meeting was primarily negotiated between Willow Black and Queen Charlotte. The Warlock\u2019s laissez-faire attitude did not seem to be an insult or a sign of distrust or disrespect so much as\u2026 she is more a rallying point than politician. She is always like that. She mostly played with a stiletto (presumably turning on Calamity in the process) while Spidertoes fanned herself. Detachedly. After a point the Warlock threw her stiletto up so it embedded in the ceiling and demanded the Autumn Court help with the theft of the Grandmaw, the Gentry that the Hollywood Courts are apparently not just allegedly holding onto. She wants to steal the Gentry from them, though she seemed less concerned over what happened to it, apparently going along with Calamity\u2019s suggestion to kill it. However, her lack of comment may indicate some plan. Regardless, after a series of outbursts which even took Willow off guard, she returned to quiescence, playing with her stiletto and allowing the Beasts to negotiate.<br /> <br /> I suppose in retrospect such a clandestine political meeting with 6 Darklings, 2 Beasts and no Fairests is sort of amusing.<br /> <br /> Eventually some general self protection and access agreements were handed out, and I returned. Unfortunately, Felicity took advantage of my absence to slip out, citing defense of her Virtue. I was saddened, but Julia was, unsurprisingly, amused. We elected to take home Flores, who was mopey that her friend was upset with her. We left while Captain Jack was doing something bizarre with the Handmaidens.<br /> <br /> Flores felt bad about what she had done, and she and Julia decided perhaps a little edgeplay would let the negative feelings bleed out. Long story short there are now bloodstains on my bed, and Julia has been informed she never gets to come near I with a paring knife. But Flores seemed to feel better and Julia is correct, the blood of such a bright soul does taste rather good to Darkling lips. I still don\u2019t think bloodletting is in any way, shape or form good for I, nor do I really see the draw. Unquestionably.<br /> <br /> As the night wore on, I told Flores she belonged to me now. She agreed. I have quite a pretty flower. A second claim and verbal acknowledgment of possession, it was sweet like eating too much candy is sweet, but as Flores slumbered after healing herself, I felt a distant sense of disquiet. I looked at Flores, her face peaceful in the dark, and I looked at Julia, large eyes looking lovingly at me despite the lack of light. And I wondered how awful a thing am I? Both girls had happily called me master, and Julia also calls me partner, and sometimes in the heat of passion\u2026other things which I am definitely not yet, but\u2026am I hurting them? Is this bad? I am not sure.<br /> <br /> I did not sleep on either of them that night.<br /> <br /> In the morning, Flores sweetly, but firmly, said the knifeplay would not be mentioned again and hopefully would not happen again. I halfheartedly told her the part where she said she was mine still applied and she said, simply, \u201cI know.\u201d Julia did not seem bothered by Flores statement, but she seemed more\u2026languid. I wonder if the edgeplay was better for Flores or her. She certainly seems less tightly wound. But then, the sex was very good.<br /> <br /> Breakfast was bright. Lori was all done up in conservative churchwear, which is a look Julia likes. So the flirting was quickly hot and heavy. It turned out Lori came out to her father, who of course does not know he is her father, and it apparently went well. I was happy for her; she should live her life without shame.<br /> <br /> The good spirits lasted at breakfast until De La Rocha came down. While Flores initially attempted to simply avoid her, De La Rocha wanted to talk. They went upstairs and hashed them things out. Hopefully things will improve with those two. They are friends, and friends of Julia, so having things be harmonious is good.<br /> <br /> Apparently Flores asked De La Rocha to punch her. I thought she was over her pain issues. Julia says it was more for De La Rocha to let out her anger. Flores is strange. Definitely.<br /> <br /> Gawain and Ace were babbling about pulling fire breathing piranhas out of Ace\u2019s dreams. Lori made an 80s song reference (a bad one, in fact) then backpedaled when they seemed serious. De La Rocha had no interest in ditch digging, which shows good things about her, I suppose. Gawain and Ace are odd, wanting to bring a Fire Hazard into my house.<br /> <br /> Last but not least, Jacob was sitting very familiarly with Luna at breakfast. While she was not exhibiting claiming behavior, it was clear things had progressed. I confess a mite bit of jealousy, but I had not planted the proverbial flag on Jacob, and I could hardly blame him. Maybe she will make him happy. I hope so. I shall simply try to not be annoyed by it.<br /> <br /> I wonder if Julia has any ideas how she wants to kill the afternoon before the show. I bet she does.<br /> <br /> Definitely.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXVI</i><br /> <br /> Poor Gawain\u2019s player kept rolling crap on Contracts of Potential.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite\u2019s self-reflection was a result of her getting an Exceptional Success on her Clarity check for \u201cclaiming\u201d Flores.<br /> <br /> Flores and De La Rocha\u2019s issue partially come from the fact that while Flores is sweet, outgoing, and very likable, she misses social cues a lot and is sometimes puzzled by the behavior of non-Elementals. She also has some fairly open-minded ideas about love and sex and is genuinely puzzled by less open minded ones. She is by no means dumb; she is actually fairly intelligent. She just has behavior comprehension issues. She was of course concerned about De La Rocha (and still is) and finds the Summer Courtier\u2019s anger mystifying\u2026she loves herself, is at peace with her sexuality, and rarely gets angry about anything. Her insistence that De La Rocha be open with her partner in order to get help with her issues (that she as her friend feels helpless to help her with) lead to their fighting. As for Flores and Oleander, there is some rivalry, but not really an unfriendly one. Flores thinks Oleander is adorable. Oleander has\u2026some issues with Flores, both being Woodbloods, but Flores being a Flowering and Oleander being a Woodwalker. Also, Flores is younger than Oleander and came along later. There is no active dislike either way, Flores just annoys Oleander sometimes.<br /> <br /> Well, I think that covers things, but if you have comments or questions let me know.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T18:01:22-07:00","id":465420,"title":"","content":"I know the Dream House does theme show tailored to a specific court at times. While listening to some Sabaton, the idea of a &quot;Summer Metal Special&quot; came to mind.<br /> <br /> Also, I imagine Lori would ultimately be jealous of Gawain. Just from what I read of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T20:15:51-07:00","id":465544,"title":"","content":"Well, Ace has the mohawk and is at least 30% Metal, though not metal. Gawain is more metal. Course Calamity has spikes, which is pretty damn metal too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T00:09:52-07:00","id":465750,"title":"","content":"I would point out that it has been agreed upon that In This Moment's 'Bloody Creature Poster Girl' is Calamity's theme song. So she fully supports this idea. <br /> <br /> Also, Lori need not be jealous of any of the three, she just needs to be the fourth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T17:35:35-07:00","id":471880,"title":"","content":"The jealousy comment was intended to be tongue-in-cheek, of course. Lori has enjoyed the amorous company of both Calamity and Gawain in the past, and though she's not had the pleasure of Becky's charms, she's not greedy. And while she'd love to be part of the filling in that sandwich... that particular evening was all about spending time with de la Rocha.<br /> <br /> Now, the next time Becky sleeps over, Lori will be gravely offended if she's not invited to partake... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T00:40:53-07:00","id":473951,"title":"","content":"I suspect if Calamity keeps inviting people to sleep with becky she may have words with her. (They might not be bad words mind you...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T11:40:37-07:00","id":480520,"title":"","content":"Sometimes, the answer to a question is not the answer you want. Two questions were asked and answered, and I suspect the results pleased no one.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXVII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite does make us think, sometimes. And like Lori says, it is a good thing to practice. While we were digging the moat, and fixing up the Hedge House, she asked if any of us thought being taken was a good thing. Like, if we were better off, you know? See, she had a picture of her from before, and she was wearing a youth fascist uniform. So she was thinking, if she hadn\u2019t been taken, she\u2019d have grown up to be a fascist and a racist and just pretty horrible, you know? But she worried that people would think she as a loyalist, thinking like that.<br /> <br /> We reassured her it didn\u2019t sound like loyalism to us. I mean, she wasn\u2019t talking about tracking down other fascists/racists and dragging them to Arcadia to have the Gentry reforge them into something else. We all kinda disagreed with her personally though. Lori was closest, since she figured she\u2019d have wound up dead on the way to California, and she's better off here with us. But the way she said it, adversity making you stronger doesn\u2019t make adversity good, you know?<br /> <br /> Jacob and De la Roche both said no, period, De la Roche cause she killed people, in Arcadia, and Jacob didn\u2019t elaborate. Julia wouldn\u2019t say anything other than that she and Insincere Marguerite wouldn\u2019t have met. So maybe she did think she was better off. I was super proud of Calamity - she figured she\u2019d have become Dr. Katheryn Moss and married Anastasia and have been making the world a better place. But she said she could and would still make the world a better place, which is, you know, progress.<br /> <br /> As far as ends justifying and all, I wasn\u2019t sure for me. I don\u2019t remember who I was enough to know if I\u2019m a better dude for having killed thousands of people. I think I was kinda a jerk, from stories I heard. The others pointed out those stories were either my fetch or me as a teenager, so they didn\u2019t count. So I dunno. I think I\u2019m with Lori though, in any case.<br /> <br /> But now, we\u2019re driving to Venice Beach, cause that\u2019s where Mr. Grey is at. Calamity learned a Contract that lets her know what direction he\u2019s in, so she\u2019s driving. Hopefully we\u2019ll know where the table is soon!<br /> <br /> <br /> Early morning, June 17th<br /> <br /> What does it gain us, if in defending ourselves against the hosts of Evil, we become one of them? Would we revile the Fae less if they restricted their hunting to our criminals, our outcasts, our mentally ill? Fuck no! If someone has transgressed, let them be killed, quickly and cleanly, or suffer the lash or excommunication, as the transgression demands. There is no sin that allows a just law to give a sentence of remaking, that allows the judge to take away the very memory of who the sinner is and replace it with something more pleasing to the judge alone, or to reforge a living being into something else. There is no redemption there, no justice. So if mortal laws will avail me not, then I will declare judgment against him myself, and carry out the sentence with my own hand. Darke will die.<br /> <br /> My motley\u2019s overlords\u2019 hands are tied in this, and so therefore theirs are as well, so long as the blackguard remains King. The alliances such as they have are necessary for a strong Court, even if the current ruler of Winter is poorly chosen, being not a man but rather a pale imitation of a fucking Fae. However, the delay is unbearable. Every moment that passes brings him closer to learning what we have uncovered and taking measures to remove the Table from our reach. Still, the movements have begun and the Queens are united in this.<br /> <br /> Autumn was certain that Summer would follow suit. The three would then be tasked with convincing the Wyrd, while we turned a quiet man into a would-be King. Lojack\u2019s advisor saw the necessity clearly, once I stopped her prattling on about Lady Joan and her lady. I still fear we did more to accomplish the monarchs\u2019 task than our own, as Lady Chance did believe she could increase the number of Winter courtiers in support of Lojack, should he agree, however, her hopes were dim in that regard. We will see the strength of his conviction tomorrow.<br /> <br /> My lady left me for a time to secure Lord Stojanovic\u2019s sister. She is unaware of his true nature, but Darke is aware of hers, so she is in danger that simply bringing her to our House is not an acceptable solution to, for now. So Lady Marguerite has seen herself in each mirror of her residence, and Lady Calamity and Lady Luna will stand guard as they can. This night, however, Lady Stojanovic was judged safe, and my lady returned to me after a short vigil. Her yielding embrace soothed away the last of my fevered anger. I think she is pleased as well, that I am merely brooding and no longer in a rage.<br /> <br /> She has received Lady Grace\u2019s blessing of restedness, and is watching over me closely, for signs that I have been overcome with sleep. But I have stood longer vigils that this. I will see the sun, and soon, by God\u2019s grace, Darke\u2019s blood.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> It\u2019s almost funny what a difference a few hours can make, isn\u2019t it? After I got home from church, I was riding high in the afterglow of the Greening and my father\u2019s acceptance of my relationship with D, and it felt like everything was coming up Lorelei. <br /> <br /> We were all in the Hedge House, cleaning a bit and sprucing things up while Gawain and Ace worked on that ridiculous moat. As we were going through the main hall, we came across a large dining table\u2026 I could have sworn it was never there before, but things like that are always happening in the Hedge House. A few of us moved it into the middle of the room. It was heavier than it looked, and we were all sweaty and tired by the time the job was done\u2026 and there in the middle of the table was a big pitcher of ice-cold orange juice. Refreshing!<br /> <br /> Anyway, things turned introspective when we got back to the Dream House. Marguerite showed us a picture of herself from before she was Taken, and it looked like she had been involved in some sort of fascist youth group. She told us that she had been a terrible person before she was Taken, and had been wondering if maybe her abduction had been a <u>good</u> thing.<br /> <br /> I was speechless for a moment. I mean, I can certainly see why she was thinking along those lines, and I guess from a purely metaphysical or philosophical point of view it was a valid question, but still\u2026 being Taken by the Gentry, a good thing? I took one of her hands and softly but fervently expressed my opinion that the Durance could never be good in and of itself\u2026 but that didn\u2019t mean that nothing good could happen as a result. I pointed out our relationships with D and Julia, respectively.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, neither of them wholeheartedly supported my decision. Julia was absolutely of the opinion that her time in Arcadia was a good thing, since it led to her meeting Marguerite. D, on the other hand, seemed to think that fate would have brought the two of us together with or without the Fae, and that we would have had some sort of May-December romance.<br /> <br /> (I don\u2019t know about that. It\u2019s hard for me to picture myself as an old woman seducing the young and vibrant chicana punk that is currently my wonderful lover. But who knows? Maybe she\u2019s right about that. Maybe some things are just meant to be. I just wish she\u2019d stop chuckling and calling me a \u201ccougar\u201d\u2026 whatever that means.)<br /> <br /> I also mentioned that I\u2019d been planning to run away from home when I was Taken. I\u2019d hoped to make it to California to become a famous singer or actress (ironic, no?), but realistically I probably would have made it as far as Omaha before ending up dead in a dumpster with a needle in my arm. So while I agree that good things may have happened as a result of my Durance, I still can\u2019t bear to think of the Durance itself as \u201cgood.\u201d<br /> <br /> So Calamity and I both mentioned around that point that we\u2019d been working on some new contracts. I was going to lead gently into the whole \u201cI can talk to birds\u201d thing, but Calamity went first, talking about how she could now track down just about anyone she wanted to no matter where they were, and how we could use that to find Mr. Grey and maybe finally make some progress on getting Andromeda\u2019s table back\u2026 and I decided I didn\u2019t want to follow that number.<br /> <br /> She concentrated for a few minutes. I could tell it wasn\u2019t easy for her; she was obviously putting a bit of glamour into the effort. She finally sighed, opened her eyes, and told us that Mr. Grey was hiding out in a house in Venice Beach. We were so excited about turning up this lead after weeks with no progress that we decided to pile into Gawain\u2019s van and head out that way right away.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not going to dwell on the events of the afternoon too much here, since recent developments still make me faintly nauseous. I just can\u2019t believe that changelings would do that sort of thing to other changelings. It\u2019s like we learned nothing from our time in Arcadia\u2026 or rather, like we learned all the <u>wrong</u> things.<br /> <br /> There was some discussion as Calamity drove us to Venice Beach as to whether we were going in guns a-blazin\u2019 or trying to talk things out with the elusive Mr. Grey. In the end we decided on a prudent course: we were going to knock on the door and try to talk to him first, while letting Insincere Marguerite sneak in through a window to scout the premises. Like the Romans said, strive for peace but prepare for war.<br /> <br /> It turns out our precautions weren\u2019t necessary. Mr. Grey answered the door \u2013 albeit reluctantly \u2013 when we told him we represented the Freehold, and was perfectly willing to answer our questions. Yes, he knew where Andromeda\u2019s table was. Yes, he would tell us if we really wanted to know, but he warned us that the information would be dangerous. No, he didn\u2019t much care why we wanted it, or how we knew he might have news of it.<br /> <br /> Master Darke has the table. The King of Winter stole it from Andromeda, and has been concealing its whereabouts from the rest of the Freehold. And what\u2019s worse, he\u2019s been using it. He\u2019s had Mr. Grey use it to reprogram Loyalists, changing them in fundamental ways to make them useful members of society. Apparently Molly Nuit and Vic Twilight are two such former Loyalists, though nobody knows it because they\u2019re completely unrecognizable as their former selves. He told us that Molly Nuit used to be a Beast\u2026<br /> <br /> I withdrew from the conversation around this point. I don\u2019t understand how any of the Lost could do that to another\u2026 even a Loyalist. Execution would be preferable! No matter what our differences are, all changelings have one thing in common: we were taken against our will by the Gentry and <u>changed</u> so that we better fit their needs. The fundamental attributes that defined us were stripped away and reshaped for the whims and convenience of the Fae. We fled from that, and against all odds managed to escape to the world of our birth, and thought we had found a refuge at last. Oh, sure, most of us are still angry and afraid that the Gentry will take us again, but we never stopped to consider that one of our own might be doing the same thing right under our noses.<br /> <br /> The mortal world is supposed to be safe from that sort of thing!<br /> <br /> I thanked Mr. Grey for his willingness to talk to us as we were preparing to depart. It\u2019s obvious that using the table has taken its toll on him, both magically and psychologically. I never met him before today, but he seemed very dull and uninterested, as though his emotions had been stripped away. He told us that he was answering our questions because he couldn\u2019t be bothered to care about keeping Darke\u2019s plans secret any longer. He also told us that if Master Darke inquired, he would reveal that we had been asking uncomfortable questions.<br /> <br /> We took our leave and drove back to Santa Monica. We talked it over and decided to go to Queen Charlotte with the information. We had to take it to one of the monarchs, but Augustine might let his court\u2019s rivalry with Darke cloud his judgment, and everyone (myself included) agreed that Princess Jolie hasn\u2019t had the clearest head lately. Gawain drove this time, while Calamity called ahead and let her monarch know that we needed to speak with her.<br /> <br /> Queen Charlotte agreed that Darke had to be stopped, and offered two options as to how that might happen. First, she could rally the other monarchs against him and attempt to remove him as the King of Winter. This would apparently involve making a case to the Wyrd itself that Master Darke is unsuited to the role. You can\u2019t just vote a monarch out of office; you have to convince the world that he isn\u2019t worthy. This will take time, and might give Darke the opportunity to set contingency plans in motion.<br /> <br /> The second option is to hit Darke\u2019s stronghold hard and fast, and try to take the table by force. The other monarchs could not officially sanction such an action, and would be bound by pledges to come to Darke\u2019s aid if he should ask them. None of us were particularly fond of this idea, so we opted to let Queen Charlotte speak to the other monarchs on our behalf.<br /> <br /> Having decided upon a course of action, we discussed it a little bit further. If we\u2019re going to depose the King of Winter, we need to have a successor in place. Charlotte suggested John Lowjack, who held the office once before, but warned us that Lowjack would be a hard sell. We agreed to try, in the hopes that we could make him see the need to temporarily step back into the role.<br /> <br /> The drive home was not fun. Most of the conversation was about how we could prepare for Darke\u2019s inevitable retribution, since he\u2019s bound to find out we\u2019re behind his troubles sooner or later. Though what he\u2019s doing is horrific, it\u2019s not actually against Freehold law, so it\u2019s unlikely he\u2019ll be punished in any permanent way. And though he probably won\u2019t strike against us openly, he has access to any number of loyal thieves and assassins.<br /> <br /> I rolled down a window as Gawain drove us home in silence. Alone among my friends, he seemed as deeply affected as me. But whereas he seemed to withdraw inside himself in a silent rage, I felt physically ill. The idea that one of us could do that sort of thing fills me with revulsion. Master Darke is a perfect little Gentry-In-Training, and he deserves whatever he gets for the horrors he\u2019s visiting upon the Freehold. But the idea that we might have to kill him after the coup, just to protect ourselves and the ones we love revolts me almost as much. I couldn\u2019t help it; I had to get some air or risk throwing up in the back of the van. And <u>nobody</u> thinks you\u2019re sexy once they\u2019ve seen you throw up in the back of someone\u2019s van.<br /> <br /> D, Julia, and Marguerite were sympathetic, and did their best to comfort me. It was sweet, and though I was acutely embarrassed by the situation, it was also nice to be the center of attention in that group for a while. It was nice to know how much they care.<br /> <br /> Professionalism took over when we got back to the Dream House, and I hurried off to get in costume and makeup. Jacob called Lowjack\u2019s bar and invited Tamara Chance (Lowjack\u2019s aide-de-camp) to attend the show, hinting that we had something to discuss with her. Queen Charlotte had intimated that we might have more luck convincing Lowjack to take up the mantle of Winter King if we got her on our side first. I hope she enjoyed the show, though she seemed to spend a lot of it doing tarot spreads at the bar.<br /> <br /> It was kind of a light night for me; I only had one solo, one duet, and a couple of numbers singing backup or dancing. Ace and I opened the show with a duet called \u201cTubthumping,\u201d a rollicking British punk pub anthem from the 90s. For my solo number, I chose \u201cSo What,\u201d an in-your-face empowerment ballad by an artist with the unlikely name of P!nk. What is this vogue with bizarrely spelled names among musicians? No caps, all caps, punctuation marks, unpronounceable symbols\u2026<br /> <br /> For the first song, I stood sedately to one side in an elegant evening gown while Ace flounced around the stage like a maniac. For the second I broke out the leather and fishnets again, and took the opportunity to really strut my stuff. I guess I was hoping the bright, powerful lyrics would help me get over the funk I was in, but it didn\u2019t really work.<br /> <br /> Our conversation with Tamara Chance after the show was brief, and not entirely encouraging. She did not seem optimistic that we\u2019d be able to convince Lowjack to take up the mantle of Winter King\u2026 but after hearing us out, she agreed that we had to try. She even offered us a few tips about how we might try to convince him, and said she\u2019d help us if she could.<br /> <br /> After she\u2019d left, I was prepared to head up to bed with Marguerite (D and Julia had already retreated to the boudoir together after the show). The events of the day had sort of put a damper on my amorous enthusiasm, but I knew how much Julia had been looking forward to spending a little quality time with me, and I thought the sex might provide a welcome distraction from our situation\u2026 and maybe improve my overall mood.<br /> <br /> Before we could take our leave, Jacob said something that brought us up short. He mentioned that Master Darke would eventually learn of our involvement in this plot, and that he was not the sort of man to take betrayal lightly. He is also subtle and devious, and might try to strike at us through those we hold dear. I glanced over at D as he said that, but she just gave me a cocky grin, and I was reassured. Hell, I\u2019d be a much easier target than her any day of the week, right? <br /> <br /> But Jacob\u2019s trepidation was about his sister Elena. Darke knows about her, and she\u2019s not aware of the supernatural world or the dangers it poses. Almost immediately, Luna and Calamity both offered to head over to Elena\u2019s apartment and make sure she was safe (and not being watched). Marguerite gave me a longing look before turning back to the rest of the group and offering to go along so that she could look into the mirrors in Elena\u2019s apartment. With her contracts, that should allow us to check on her safety at any time in the future.<br /> <br /> I admit it. I love her a little bit for the need I saw in her eyes when she looked at me, but I love her a little bit <u>more</u> for the fact that she put Elena\u2019s safety and Jacob\u2019s peace of mind first.<br /> <br /> So Calamity and Marguerite headed over to Elena\u2019s place while Luna stayed with Jacob. I went upstairs to join D and Julia when the group dispersed, and the two of them set about making me feel better. And, for the night at least, it really did seem to be all about comforting and pleasing me. We were just starting to drift off when Marguerite returned, and the whole cycle started up again.<br /> <br /> We finally collapsed into an exhausted heap in the wee hours of the morning, and I started to fall asleep. D was snuggled up against my back (a complicated but not impossible proposition with my wings) while Julia contentedly nuzzled my breasts. Both of them were snoring softly. Marguerite, quiet as a shadow and light as a feather, crawled up on top of us all and stroked my hair. I know it\u2019s a dominance thing with her, but it seemed a simple enough concession to let her sleep on top, and it obviously made her happy, so I kissed her sleepily and allowed myself to drift off.<br /> <br /> I woke up about an hour ago, and have been writing in my diary and watching the girls sleep ever since. My three little darkling lovers are definitely not morning people. I hope that this whole business with Master Darke will be over soon so that I can get back to just enjoying the good things about my life, but I\u2019m worried that it won\u2019t be as simple as all that. Even if we didn\u2019t have to worry about his retaliation, there\u2019s still the little matter of getting him removed from office in the first place. I mean, at this point, it\u2019s really just our word against his.<br /> <br /> Except of course that we have Mr. Grey as a witness. Even if Darke catches wind of our plans and moves the table, Mr. Grey will almost certainly back up our story. I mean, he obviously doesn\u2019t care about keeping secrets, and can\u2019t be bothered to lie, right? So all we have to do is present him to the monarchs, and we should be golden! Maybe I\u2019ve been too negative about this whole situation after all.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T11:41:11-07:00","id":480521,"title":"","content":"<b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> <b><u><b><u>Monday June 16<sup>th</sup></u></b></u></b><br /> <br /> The saying goes that he who hunts monsters should be careful lest he become one. That's why it's better to leave it to those of us who are already monsters. We know what we're doing. Yeah, life took a turn for the dark since that last entry. I sound like the stupid little girl I used to be. Katt would be fucking useless right now. But Calamity... oh Calamity is exactly the monster my family needed last night.<br /> <br /> They are family to me and I will kill for them. Hell, when the day comes I will most likely die for them. Until that happens, I will do whatever it takes to protect them from the other monsters. I will do what must be done in darkness to keep the light from turning away from them. I am damned beyond redemption already, so what is one more sin or even a hundred more? I murdered a man tonight. I set out to end his life and I did so. There was no mercy, no remorse. I did not fight him. I stole his life while he slept. I ended him in a shower of fire and glass. Mr Grey will never tell Darke that we know about his misdeeds. That we know he has used the Mothership's Table to remake loyalists into minions and slaves. Mr Grey was a threat to my family and so he had to die.<br /> <br /> I am not ashamed of my deed. I do not regret murdering him. I acted to protect those I am sworn to from Grey's master. I did it without telling them of my intent to spare them the guilt. My blackened soul can bear the weight of it alone. I did not kill him because I wanted to, but because I am a monster, I did take pleasure in it.<br /> <br /> Somehow, I knew that seeking him would be the turning point. That is why I did not speak of my contract before the Masquerade, before I was able to speak to Andromeda about the Table. And now we know that it was being used in the worst possible way. Knowledge is a dangerous thing sometimes. Only a day ago we were ignorant of the magnitude of Darke's evil. We were laughing and joking about digging a moat for fire-breathing piranha for the hollow. I was stupidly daydreaming of Gawain and Becky and some foolish notion that I might somehow get to live happily ever after with both the knight and the dragon.<br /> <br /> We were all in high spirits except Insincere Marguerite. She was more thoughtful at breakfast than usual I think but I was distracted. But yesterday afternoon as we were resting after working she poised a question. Could it ever be that being taken might be a good thing? The mood shifted quite abruptly. Arcadia is never an easy topic for any of us. It seems she had found an old picture of herself from before being taken, and in that life she was a member of a fascist youth order dreaming of nothing more than furthering the racial purity of France. Between that and what I know of her Keeper, I can certainly see where she is coming from. But she was worried that putting forth any sort of positive feelings would make her seem like a loyalist.<br /> <br /> Julia was firm that she would not have met Insincere Marguerite otherwise and so it was a good thing for that reason. It's odd, but I have said much the same to Gawain, that if not for Snow Globe I would never have met him and his answer was unhesitatingly that he would rather have never met me than for me to have suffered the torments the Whispering Voices put me through. De la Rocha said it was a bad thing because she had killed and she seemed convinced that somehow she and Lori would have found each other regardless. Lori seemed less optimistic, explaining that just before being taken she had been planning to run away from home to become a singer. She seemed fairly sure that she'd have wound up dead in a dumpster with a needle in her arm long before ever reaching the West Coast. I told her I didn't agree, that she was underestimating herself. The strength that allowed her to survive Arcadia had been inside her before even if she hadn't known it.<br /> <br /> Jacob was quieter than usual and stated only that it was bad and refused to elaborate. His expression was unreadable but I know he wrestles with whatever he did in Arcadia and I'm sure he was dwelling on that guilt. I wish I could convince him to trust me or someone enough to speak of it. I know that pressing him will only make him withdraw more, but I worry about him keeping that all inside. Yeah, sounds like pots and kettles coming from me but it isn't entirely selfless. If he can trust me with those things then I can trust him with own darkness. Us monsters need to stick together.<br /> <br /> Gawain doesn't really remember much, when each night was a dream year it makes his mortal life a very faint memory. But his fetch is kind of a jerk and he's fairly sure the stories of that go back to before he was taken so he'd most likely be the same privileged asshole. And he's not sure if the people he killed in the dreams died or not. In the end, Lori found the best way to sum it up, that just because the adversity made some of us better or stronger does not change that it was a bad thing.<br /> <br /> For myself, I told them that I was pretty sure that had I not been taken I'd have become Dr Katheryn Moss and married Anastasia. I mean, if I had it in me to not give up in Snow Globe then I am sure I could have taken on medical school. Insincere Marguerite took the moment to tell me again that I still could be a doctor. It made me smile. I told her I knew that, but that I wasn't the girl who wanted that anymore. I am the monster They made me. But that I was still making the world better, just not the same way. Damn, that was rather prophetic given what happened later that night.<br /> <br /> Things started to get quiet, she'd stirred up some deep wells and gotten us all thinking hard. I don't think Insincere Marguerite really had things sorted out and something was clearly still bothering her but I didn't know that it was something she'd open up about with all of us. So I took the opportunity to tell them about my contract of Relentless Pursuit intending to draw her aside privately to ask her about it later. I had no idea just how big a fucking dam was about to burst.<br /> <br /> They were excited, of course, and everyone was pretty keen that I should go ahead and try to find him, if only to get an idea of how far. And once I did, I found he wasn't far at all, seeing a glimpse of him alone in a plain little house across town. It was long enough before the show so we piled into Gawain's van and I took off, following the pull as best I could while staying on the roads (more or less).<br /> <br /> Once we got to the house, there was some discussion. While I was itching for a fight enough that the kick the door in like a SWAT raid plan was sorely tempting even I agreed that at least trying to talk to him was the best opening gambit. Well, that and having Insincere Marguerite slip in to look for the Table while we had his attention on us.<br /> <br /> Tension and excitement were running high as we knocked on his door. Lori did most of the talking, coaxing him into letting us in and explaining what had prompted us to seek him out. From the first, I felt an uncomfortable lack coming from him. Not the mask that Jacob or myself wears, but rather the opposite. There was nothing to hide, nothing at all. He told us that he knew where the table was and would tell us but that if he did it would most likely get us killed. And when we assured him we wanted to know anyway he told us about Darke. The Table is at his clinic and he has been directing Grey to use it to remake loyalists. To destroy them utterly and reshape them into new changelings loyal to himself.<br /> <br /> To have something so utterly vile explained in such flat and soulless tones only made it that much more surreal. Molly Nuit and Vic Twilight are two of his victims. Molly apparently was a beast when he started on her. And there was nothing as he admitted to his own role in this violation. I haven't encountered anyone that hollow since Snow Globe. I know that she's promised to use it to help Joan and Jolie but seeing Grey made me concerned for Andromeda and glad that I'd convinced her not to keep the damned thing close at hand if Grey is any indication of what using the Table does to someone. As we left, Grey told us that he would tell Darke if the man asked, that he didn't care enough not to, just as he couldn't be bothered to try to keep the truth from us.<br /> <br /> That statement wouldn't leave me as we left and drove, after some discussion, to the Autumn Court to speak to Queen Charlotte. Moving against Darke directly, and against the stronghold of the Winter Court to boot was a task beyond our abilities. So we opted to see what my monarch thought we should do. She made sure we understood that if we acted against Darke while he remained Winter King that by pledge he could call upon the other courts for aid and they would be required to answer. So the answer is for the other monarchs to petition the Wyrd to strip him of his crown. The problem is that it requires convincing the other monarchs (something Queen Charlotte felt was very likely though would take some time to do quietly) and most importantly presenting a suitable candidate to take his place.<br /> <br /> The best choice for that is John Lowjack, who was the Winter King before Darke. Lowjack did not want the position and convincing him to take it up again might prove difficult. We agreed to approach him while Queen Charlotte started to get the other monarchs in agreement. At her suggestion, we decided to contact Tamera Chance first. She is close to Lowjack and he's likely to listen if we can convince her to speak on our behalf.<br /> <br /> The ride back from the lighthouse was not happy. Jacob called Tamera and she agreed to come by the Dream House. Gawain was tight-lipped and angry. Lori looked like she about to be sick and rolled down a window for air. I tried to offer some support, but soon Insincere Marguerite and Julia and De la Rocha had gathered and I moved to give them room. They're better at comfort than I am. I called Becky to let her know that Charlotte was going to be paying Jolie a visit and that it really was court business. It seems that Jolie was in the midst of catching up with her former lover, Felicity, when I called. Becky seemed rather happy to talk and given the way the afternoon had turned it was good to just chatter with her a bit.<br /> <br /> Once we got home it was time to get things in gear for the show. The routine was a nice distraction, especially for Lori. I don't think it really drove everything away from her mind but she was focused on the show. She did a nice punk number with Ace and then another as her solo act. I am going to look both of those up next time I'm working on paperwork. Tamera did come out and I guess she picked up on the tension because she was quietly reading her tarot cards rather than watching the show. Gawain continued to be terse, staying by the door after the show started rather than circulating. He claimed to be fine (which he clearly wasn't) but I wasn't going to press him. I worked the room like I usually do and I don't think it was too obvious that I was distracted. TJ had come out again and I made a point of chatting with him a bit. White Maria was there and clearly unhappy. I did ask and she said it was relationship issues that she didn't want to talk about so I just made some generally supportive comments and didn't pry. Moon and Dionisia were also there and when I stopped by Moon was relentlessly trying to convince Dionisia to divulge who she'd ended up with at the Masquerade. Moon kept guessing while Dionisia just grinned and said she wasn't telling. Clearly it had been going a while since as I approached Moon even asked if it had been me. Despite everything, I had to chuckle at the pair of them.<br /> <br /> Once the show ended we gathered to talk and started to Tamera. Talking about the Table got her sidetracked talking about Andromeda and the way she was distracting Joan from protecting the freehold. I bristled a little. I mean, before they got together everyone was going on about how Joan was wound up way too tight and paranoid and now it seems like all anyone has to say about the fact the woman has found someone she loves that she's neglecting her duty to guard the freehold. Before anyone could steer things back to the topic at hand Gawain snapped at Tamera loud enough to make the woman cringe. Thankfully we were able to smooth things back down and once we did and explained what was going on she saw why we'd asked her to come out.<br /> <br /> Tamera went over the situation a bit more. It seems that when Lowjack stepped down it upset a fair number of winter courtiers who preferred him to Darke. And a good number of them had been unhappy enough with Darke as Winter King that they left the area, meaning that the support for Lowjack among the Winter Court wasn't as strong as we might like. She did say that she could and would try to coax some of them back but she wasn't sure if any would. She was also quite sure that Lowjack very much did not want the crown. It wasn't just personal. He is a part of an Entitlement that helps to shelter those that need to be hidden, especially those being actively hunted by the Gentry. Being king puts him far too much in the spotlight to do that work effectively. While she was not encouraging, she did promise to arrange for us to meet with Lowjack before the bar opened.<br /> <br /> Once she had left, Gawain was about to head to the hollow to work at the forge. De la Rocha and Julia had already gone upstairs and Lori and Insincere Marguerite were poised to join them when Jacob brought up his sister. Darke knows about her. As she is unaware of who Jacob is or anything supernatural bringing her to the Dream House wasn't an option. Both Luna and I offered to guard her. The Insincere Marguerite sighed and suggested that if she went she could look into the mirrors and thus be able to watch through them and travel there instantly if need be to retrieve Elena. I promised that I'd see that Jacob's sister was safe and watch over Insincere Marguerite.<br /> <br /> We rode on my bike. It wasn't hard for the pair of us to enter quietly and unseen. I stayed near the window we used, looking around just a little to get an idea of the layout just in case. Insincere Marguerite crept in further, peering into all of the mirrors before returning. And as everything was peaceful, we then made our way back to the Dream House.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite headed up to join her lovers eagerly. I had a final errand to see to myself and after quickly retrieving the grenade I'd been keeping with my guns I headed back out. Jacob was still up and asked me if I needed any backup. I'm sure from his tone that he had guessed I was up to something but I told him it was something I needed to do alone and he nodded and let me go without any questions.<br /> <br /> Of them all, I think he'd have agreed with me that Grey needed to be dealt with but as a member of the Winter Court, I wasn't going to put him in the position of knowing that harm was coming to another courtier. I don't think my darkling sister would have opposed the idea but I imagine she'd prefer a less violent solution. And none of the others would have agreed to it. They'd rather risk Darke finding out and taking steps to move the table or silence us rather than harm an innocent.<br /> <br /> If Grey was truly innocent it would have been harder to justify what I was doing. And yes, maybe Darke threatened him or even tortured him, but ultimately he made the choice to carry out his master's will. He made a choice to use the Table to steal the free will... the very identity from others. And he and Darke claim these were loyalists but how can we know for sure? How many newly escaped Changelings are confused or hostile when they encounter other lost? Even those who exit the Hedge to carry out their Keeper's will can choose to break away once they are separated from the madness of Arcadia. No, that soulless husk may well have been as much a victim as an accomplice but he did make his choice. There was no guard on his home. He was not being kept against his will and forced to commit atrocities. And would it have really been kinder to spare him and heal his ruined soul? Had he regained any semblance of humanity wouldn't he have been plunged into guilt over the horrific deeds he'd willingly carried out? I have no answers to those questions. What I can say is that I was not willing to risk harm coming to those I had sworn to defend for some chance of salvaging some part of that ruined shell of a man.<br /> <br /> And so I rode back to that comfortable little house and parked a couple of blocks away. I crept up to that picture perfect lawn. I called upon the Contract of Darkness to scale the wall and found his bedroom. Another call and his slumber was sealed against any interruption. Then I threw the grenade in through his window and saw it land on his pillow before I rolled away and lept away. The shock-wave from the explosion washed over my back and sent me further from the house before I hit the ground and rolled. I never looked back, there was no need to. I was clear of the yard before the lights came on in the neighboring homes. By the time I could hear sirens I was back to my bike and riding away casually.<br /> <br /> I got clear and back to the Dream House without incident. It was quiet so I took a moment to call Andromeda. The biggest risk in killing Grey was that Darke would try to seize Andromeda to work the Table for him. Joan answered unsurprisingly. I told her that I couldn't explain and that I shouldn't be telling her as much as I was but that Andromeda was at risk and I cared about her. That was all it took to lock Joan's attention. I told her that the people who had the Table had lost their operator and thus it was possible they would try to kidnap Andromeda. I could tell she wanted to know more but she didn't ask. I told her I'd explain when it was over and I could. I then just told to keep Andromeda safe until then.<br /> <br /> And once that had been taken care of I headed to up to mine and Gawain's room. There wasn't any noticeable evidence of my activities but I peeled out of my riding leathers and hit the shower. Once I was clean I debated but then decided to get perfumed and pretty before going to the hollow. I fixed my hair and dabbed a little makeup and slipped into a nice midnight blue lace number that both Gawain and I are fond of. I added a pair of indoor/outdoor slippers and lifted the pretty matched robe that had come with it. I've never worn it before and even as carefully as I eased it on I could hear the glass catch and pick and the soft tearing. But when I checked myself in the mirror I decided it was worth it.<br /> <br /> And even before I got to the workshop in the hollow I could hear the furious pounding. It wasn't the steady, almost soothing rhythm I'm used to. It was fast and hard and a little erratic in tempo. I hesitated. Gawain is strong and with no more than a thought his contracts can make him inhuman. I wasn't worried about that, but he is always so very careful when he touches me, as if he's afraid of breaking me. And I've seen him do the same with Desiree and Becky. I could tell he was still enraged and I considered turning back and changing into something less blatantly sexual. But the robe wasn't going to survive coming off at that point anyway so I just walked to the doorway and paused till he looked up.<br /> <br /> He noticed me immediately and looked up. And then he <i>noticed</i> me. His gaze was raw and swept over me with an intensity I'm not used to from him. And then he was across the room and pressing me against the door-frame and kissing me hard enough to steal my breath. When he released my lips he swept me up and for the first time I can recall told me we were going to the bedroom. I don't object to aggressive and demanding as long as they're willing to earn it. I am just not the sort to yield and surrender myself to anyone. Even if I am in the mood to be the prey you have to prove that you're stronger and willing to prove it. At least, that's how I have always been in the past. But when he scooped me up and growled I just relaxed and whispered something I have never said before. \u201cYour monster... to do with as you will.\u201d And he did.<br /> <br /> I'd expected that once the anger drained away he'd sleep and I was prepared to stay up and see that it was a dreamless rest. But once he was done he rose. He's still clearly tense but at least that furious edge is gone now. I am stretched out in our bed and feeling deliciously well-used and just a touch sore in all the right places. It's nice and I am going to just lay here and bask in it while I can. Tomorrow will be here all too soon and I can worry about everything then.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> I\u2019m not sure how to describe today. It was not a good day, that\u2019s for sure, but nothing really bad happened to any of us. I guess it\u2019s just that knowing the truth is not necessarily a comforting thing. It all started early this afternoon over our usual brunch. Insincere Marguerite asked a question that got most of us talking, and all of us thinking. She asked it was necessarily a bad thing that we were taken. She admitted that before she was taken she was not a good person. She had been part of a fascist group and apparently was happy being racist with other like-minded individuals. I agree that her old self was not ideal, and that her current self is a more understanding and tolerant person, but I don\u2019t know if that still means that being taken was a good thing. She was worried that having thoughts like that would make her sound like a loyalist.<br /> <br /> She asked the rest of us our opinion on the matter. Was being taken a good thing? Lori admitted that before she was taken she was planning on running away and probably would have ended up dead before she made it to California. Julia thought it was good because it brought the two of them together. De La Rocha said that it was not, because she killed people while she was there. Gawain agreed that it was bad for pretty much the same reasons. I just said that it was bad. I didn\u2019t really know how to elaborate on that. Being taken was bad, but not because of bad things that my Lady did to me. It was bad because I discovered what kind of person I really was when push came to shove. None of us could claim to be lily white. We all did things that we weren\u2019t proud of, but I took that a few steps further. Gods, the things I did in that woman\u2019s service. The people I hurt. The lives I ruined. So no, it was not a good thing.<br /> <br /> I felt bad later. Insincere Marguerite was looking for validation that having thoughts like that did not make her a bad person and I did nothing to dissuade her of that idea with my silence. I just couldn\u2019t speak. My throat felt like it was closed off and I felt lucky just to breathe. I\u2019m sure the others just saw my usual unflappable facade. Or maybe they saw me shut down just the tiniest bit. I\u2019m not sure which. I\u2019m good at not showing emotion when I don\u2019t want to, and today was definitely not a day for me to show my actual emotions.<br /> <br /> And guess what\u2026that wasn\u2019t even the best part of the day. Calamity, in an effort to move onto less depressing subjects, brought up the fact that she had recently learned a contract that would allow her to track whoever she wanted to by direction and estimated distance. So, we used this ability to find Mr. Grey. Calamity drove the van and we all rode in the back as she zigzagged her way across town to Venice Beach. We arrived at a slightly run down house and knocked on the door. Insincere Marguerite went pretty much invisible and was sneaking into the house as the rest of us took a more direct approach. Mr. Grey answered and eventually let us in when we told him that we wanted to talk to him about something important. Lorelei did most of the convincing.<br /> <br /> So, we told him what we were looking for and he told us that he knew where it was but it would be dangerous for us to try and retrieve it. He implied that it would lead to us getting killed. After a bit more persuading, though it honestly didn\u2019t take that much at all, he admitted that Master Darke has had the table all along, hidden at the clinic. He then told us, after some prodding, what Master Darke had been using the table for. Apparently he\u2019s been capturing loyalists and then using the table to change them into new people. He completely rewrites who they are and even what they are. Mr. Grey said that Molly Nuit and Vic Twilight used to be loyalists until Master Darke had him use the table to make them loyal to him. He also admitted that Molly Nuit originally wasn\u2019t even an elementally based changeling. She used to be a beast oriented person. To make things just that much more disturbing was Mr. Grey\u2019s attitude during this whole conversation. He didn\u2019t care. He didn\u2019t care what he\u2019d done or what would happen to us if Master Darke found out about our search for the table leading to him. And I\u2019m not talking sociopath kind of \u201cdidn\u2019t care.\u201d This guy seemed empty. Like he\u2019d been hollowed out, but not filled back up with anything new. I have to wonder if just operating the table did that to him, and if so, how many times he\u2019s used it in recent years. How many people has he changed?<br /> <br /> Before we left we asked Mr. Grey if he was going to tell Master Darke what he had told us. He said that he would tell the Winter King if he asked, but wasn\u2019t going to seek him out to tell him. That in itself was a relief. I didn\u2019t relish the idea of having to kill Mr. Grey in front of my motley mates to keep him quiet. I didn\u2019t particularly want them to see that side of me, but I also didn\u2019t want Darke to find out what we knew.<br /> <br /> Master Darke is a powerful man and he does not suffer fools lightly. And I am a fool.<br /> <br /> So, we headed back to the Dream House after that enlightening yet disturbing conversation. On the trip back Lori looked physically ill. I was half expecting her to be sick before we got back, but she managed to keep herself together. De la Rocha provided a lot of support, as did Marguerite and Julia. I was too numb to really be of much help, so I sat where I was and tried to keep myself together. I felt sick myself. The very idea that Master Darke has used that device to completely remake people just because he didn\u2019t like who they were is terrifying. And the thing that makes it that much worse is that he didn\u2019t even break any laws of the freehold. It is not against the rules to punish or kill loyalists. Pretty much anything goes when it comes to those serving the Gentry.<br /> <br /> The others asked me specifically how I felt about all this. I wasn\u2019t really surprised. I\u2019m the Winter courtier of the group and Master Darke is my monarch. He\u2019s also kind of my boss in some things. The others still don\u2019t know what I deal under the table, so to speak, when I work at the bar. Master Darke implied, though I don\u2019t think it was part of our contract, that my activities on his behalf should remain secret. But when it comes to the table I was able to answer honestly. I told the others that I was not comfortable with how the table was being used. Lori said that they were glad to hear me say that. I was a little surprised at first. Just for a moment though. I asked myself how they could possibly think that I\u2019d be okay with how Master Darke was using the table, but then I had to remind myself that I don\u2019t really share a lot about myself with anyone. I am good at wearing masks, and while they have seen a more real version of me than most people have, they still have not met the real me. I\u2019ll be honest. I\u2019m not exactly sure who the real me is anymore. I\u2019m not who I was before I was taken, and I\u2019m not who I was when I first met the freehold at Claire Falls. Something must have shown on my face because she clarified that she mentioned it because they were asking me to go against my monarch. I nodded my understanding. I have to stop jumping to conclusions, though it is true that I hide more of myself than I share.<br /> <br /> After we left Mr. Grey we discussed what to do next. We came to the conclusion that we needed help and that Queen Charlotte might be able to provide that. She is not affiliated with either the Winter court or their enemies so she could be seen as a neutral party. When we arrived we were escorted in and were allowed to talk to her alone. Probably alone. She most likely had someone keeping an eye on things, it would only be prudent to do so. So, we explained to her what we had found out and she agreed that it was not a good thing. She suggested taking the matter to the other monarchs and bringing charges against Master Darke and having him removed from power. To do this we would need to have a replacement lined up to be Winter King and Charlotte would have to meet with the other monarchs as soon as possible.<br /> <br /> The only problem with trying to solve this the political way is that it could take a while, and time is something that we do not have a lot of. If Master Darke finds out about our inquiries then he can easily move the table and make sure no one knows where it is, or he can kill us and take care of the problem that way. I was more concerned that he would use other means to persuade us to stop looking into the table and trying to get it back. If he targeted those that we hold dear he might be able to convince us to stand down. He is not above hurting innocents in the course of getting what he wants, and he knows about my sister.<br /> <br /> The alternative to going about this in a political way was to raid the Clinic ourselves and steal the table back. A couple of problems lie with that idea. The first is that Master Darke and those loyal to him are not pushovers. We could all very well be killed in the attempt. Also, if we raid his place then it is within his right to call on the other monarchs for aid, and they would be pledge-bound to help him, and we would be in serious trouble\u2026 if we weren\u2019t already dead. So, we decided to put the political plan into motion tonight. Queen Charlotte would talk to the other monarchs as soon as possible and we would talk to Lowjack and see if we can convince him to become Winter King. He has done it in the past and wasn\u2019t happy about it then. I know he doesn\u2019t really want the crown, but I think he would make a good ruler. We just need to convince him of that. To that end we have invited Tamara, Lowjack\u2019s right-hand woman, to the club tonight to see the show. I also hinted that I might like to talk to her after the performance if she\u2019d be amenable. Tamara was a bit surprised by the request, but she agreed to come. I\u2019m hoping curiosity and not suspicion was her motivating impulse when she agreed.<br /> <br /> While I was on the phone with her, Tamara asked me about the Warlock of Night\u2019s handmaidens. She said that they had flirted heavily with her at the masquerade, and that she had felt a bit dizzy during their \u201cvisit.\u201d They helped her sit down when she started feeling ill. They kept up the flirting though, and Tamara wasn\u2019t sure what they were up to. I warned Tamara that the handmaidens are leechfingers, and that she should be careful around them. She did not seem to think that the ladies had done anything to her, dizziness aside, but I wasn\u2019t so sure. They could have helped Tamara\u2019s social anxiety along.<br /> <br /> I think the show went well tonight, even if we were all a bit distracted. You wouldn\u2019t know it from Lorelei\u2019s performance that she was trying not to be sick in Gawain\u2019s van mere hours before. Gawain himself was a bit more pensive. He got a drink and set up a chair near the entrance after the doors had been shut. He assured anyone who asked that he was fine, but I think he was anything but fine. I didn\u2019t try and push him though. I know he\u2019s got his own demons to work through and I wanted to give him some time to do that. So, he was our sentinel for the evening.<br /> <br /> After Tamara arrived and the show had started I brought her a drink, something I remember her ordering at Lowjack\u2019s place, and mentioned that I was looking forward to talking to her a bit after the show. She asked me if everything was okay. I just motioned that it was so-so and smiled as I went back to the bar. A little while later I thought I saw her laying some cards out on the table in front of her. It didn\u2019t look like a standard solitaire spread, and the show was anything but boring, so I assumed she was doing something else. The cards were big too. Maybe tarot cards? Not sure. Anyway, after the show was over and the customers were gone, we all sat down with Tamara and laid out what we had discovered and had been discussing about the table, Master Darke, all of it. She reiterated that she did not think that Lowjack would want to be Winter King again, but back when he filled in the current monarch had not been doing the sort of things that Master Darke has been up to. She also mentioned that he is part of an entitlement called the Knighthood of Utmost Silence, and that being king might interfere with his ability to carry out any responsibilities for that. Apparently this entitlement helps people that need to be hidden for their safety disappear. That sounds like something I can get behind. I wonder if I offered to help if that might make Lowjack more amenable to being King? If he didn\u2019t have to worry that those that needed his help would not be able to get it\u2026 I\u2019ll bring it up when we meet with him. Speaking of which Tamara also told us that she would let him know that some people would be by tomorrow to talk to him, but would leave the details out. We thanked her for her time and saw her out.<br /> <br /> We talked for a bit longer about our options and what Master Darke\u2019s reactions might be. I mentioned that he might go through people we are close to in order to get to us or hurt us. I brought up the fact that Master Darke knows about my sister Elena and I was worried for her safety. That statement prompted an overwhelming reaction. Both Luna and Calamity offered to go to Elena\u2019s apartment and make sure that she was safe and that no one was watching her. Insincere Marguerite even offered to go to her apartment and look in all of Elena\u2019s mirrors so she could see through them herself if need be. She would even be able to travel through them if it came to that. In the end it was decided that Calamity would check the place out and Insincere Marguerite would peek in all the mirrors. Luna stayed at the Dream House with me. I\u2019ll admit that it was comforting to have her there with me, and for so many people to speak up and offer to help me like that. I have some good friends here and I am lucky to have them. No matter what the future brings, they will have my support.<br /> <br /> After most everyone had headed up to bed, or to the Hollow in Gawain\u2019s case, I noticed that Calamity had not done so and looked to be heading out. I asked her if she needed any help. She doesn\u2019t normally just head out this late for a random walk. She had a plan, though she didn\u2019t tell me what it was. She just said that she was fine and would be back soon to meet Gawain in the Hollow. I just looked at her for a moment and said \u201cokay.\u201d I told her to be safe and I\u2019d see her later. I don\u2019t know if she just needed to work out some frustrations or think or if she had a specific plan in mind. I\u2019m fairly certain that she\u2019s up to something though. Not much I can do about it right now though. I trust her to take care of herself. I\u2019ll just make sure to talk to her in the morning/afternoon.<br /> <br /> Call me depressing, but even after all the planning and starting to put said plans in action, my mind kept going back to Darke and the table and what had happened with Molly and Vik. I guess the thing that bothers me the most is that they weren\u2019t even given a choice. They didn\u2019t decide to become different people. They didn\u2019t decide on their own to turn away from their masters. They were forced. They were violated. It is possible to change and to leave their service. I\u2019ve done it. I was given a chance. I don\u2019t know why, but Diane and her motley gave me that chance. They didn\u2019t kill me when they could have. Diane just talked to me like a normal person. She was kind to me. Even though I was her enemy, even though I had been the one to hurt her, she gave me a chance. She tended to my wounds as I healed. She brought me food and snuck in books. She brought warmth back into my life. Warmth that I didn\u2019t even know had been gone until she came. She made me think of Elena, and until that instant I had forgotten I had a sister. I remembered the bond that we shared, and knew that I had to find some way to get back to her. Diane helped me remember who I was. I\u2019m fairly certain that if it wasn\u2019t for her I would have remained loyal to my Lady. I would have remained Rime.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> Today was a whirlwind of emotion.<br /> <br /> After my considerations last night, I decided to discuss with my Motley my question: Was being taken ultimately bad? I found a picture on the Internet of myself a decade ago in my organization\u2019s youth uniform\u2026a snappy black uniform with an armband. The picture worried me. My face was rounder, and the look in my eyes\u2026cold. I recall when it was taken. I was sternly sure of my superior breeding, my genes, my eugenic soundness\u2026I was different, then.<br /> <br /> More like the Day Court. Yes.<br /> <br /> Lorelei, Jacob and Gawain were certain that being taken was strictly bad, as was De La Rocha. Calamity was more ambivalent. Julia was sure it was a good thing, as it is how we met. She was almost chillingly firm. Their reactions told me much. They (aside from Julia) fear the possibility is it not a bad thing. Should I not consider this? Once, I believed I knew everything. Now I know I knew nothing. Can I afford to be so sure of what I know now?<br /> <br /> Maybe.<br /> <br /> Regardless, Calamity changed the subject. She had found a way to locate Mr. Grey, the Wizened Operator of the table. Specifically, one of the Ogre contracts she has taken to. We decided to set off to do so in the van. It was almost a letdown how easy it was to find the house. I slipped inside while the other talked. Unfortunately, the Table was not there. Fortunately, the others discovered it\u2019s whereabouts. Unfortunately, its whereabouts were in the Rehab clinic of the Winter Court. Indeed, Vic Twilight and Molly Nuit were once Loyalists who were transformed by Mr. Grey upon the Table on Master Darke\u2019s orders. Mr. Grey, it seems did leave the experience unscathed\u2026the others said he was a shadow of a man. He freely gave us the information, but freely said he would tell Darke if asked. Unfortunately.<br /> <br /> We decided to go to the Autumn Court and talk to Queen Charlotte. Calamity filled her in. She claimed that we had essentially two ways of dealing with it. Jolie, Charlotte and Augustine would meet and appoint a new Winter King. If John Lowjack were Winter King, he could demand the Table. This would, however, take time, as according to the Old Oaths they would essentially need to petition the Wyrd to change the King. This will take time. Also, it is unlikely that Master Darke would be\u2026dealt with\u2026in a permanent way, as he has not technically broken Freehold law. We would make enemies.<br /> <br /> Option B was a rush on the headquarters. The other Seasonal Monarchs would be obligated to intervene in they were asked by Darke, so it would have to be fast and brutal. And extremely risky. I don\u2019t think anyone seriously considered that one.<br /> <br /> The third unmentioned option is I could steal it. This would be terribly risky to me. I could do it, of course\u2026only problem would be lifting it. I am unsure if I could. Otherwise would be a matter of sneaking in and finding a mirror to get out.<br /> <br /> We decided on option 1. Jacob called Tamara Chance, John Lowjack\u2019s right hand woman. She agreed to attend the show tonight. I don\u2019t know her or Lowjack very well, but from what Queen Charlotte said convincing her would be important. Definitely.<br /> <br /> We returned. I checked on Lorelei, who was unwell in the car on the way back. She said she was fine. She seemed\u2026not fine, but able to go on. I took my place with the puppets. Happily.<br /> <br /> The show went well. Luna was there talking to Jacob. Julia and De La Rocha were all over each other in the audience. Someone could have stripped onstage they would not have noticed for their trying to swallow each other. I suspect many of us did not have the show foremost on our minds, but one would never know from watching. Lori and Ace are masters of show. Unquestionably.<br /> <br /> Afterwards we talked to Tamara Chance. Tamara agreed with us but said it would be difficult to convince Lowjack to become King Lowjack again. Tamara felt this was unlikely, but agreed to help us. Lowjack is a member of an Entitlement that helps hide and protect people, and would be less able to do that as King. Also, it did not suit his temperament. Unfortunately. Still, we will speak to him tomorrow.<br /> <br /> When Tamara left, Jacob mentioned concerns about his sister, Elena. Elena is someone Darke knows of who may be used against him. Calamity and Luna both volunteered to check on her. I was eager to go upstairs and kiss my lovelies, but the fact is if she came into peril, having I having been reflected in Elena\u2019s mirrors seems like the best thing for her, since I can quickly get there that way. Ultimately, Loyalty defeated Libido, and I went with Calamity. Lorelei went upstairs to join the other lovelies.<br /> <br /> The trip was simple. They had few defenses\u2026getting in and out was surprisingly easy. I recognized Elena as the human girl who had spoken to Jacob in the dream house. She is pretty, but I pushed the dark thoughts away. Having been reflected in each mirror, I returned to the window I entered through where Calamity was waiting. We withdrew from a secure house.<br /> <br /> Calamity had other business I heard her dissuading Jacob from helping with, so figuring she did not need me I went up to the lovelies. How pretty each of them are! Lorelei\u2019s eyes are orbs of such darkness, yet can be so expressive. I don\u2019t see the aggressive defiance as much as I used to, though they don\u2019t seem submissive either; I think I detect a growing affection, though I could be wrong. De La Rocha\u2019s eyes are brown, but seem less dark than Lorelei\u2019s\u2026I love the far off submissive look they get. Julia\u2019s baby blues reflect my own, as her light hair does mine. So many gorgeous pairs of eyes to lose myself in! So much pale pink skin to touch. I ravished them all, and heard my name said quite loudly, as it should be. Definitely. In the end, we clustered. Julia somehow managed to sleep hogging almost all of Lorelei\u2019s bosom, as she often does, so I slept on top of them, smelling Lorelei\u2019s hair. Lovely as these woman are, I love their smells almost as much, their tastes close behind. Such wonderful creatures.<br /> <br /> I wonder, when I search people\u2019s eyes, what they see when they look back at me. What do they see when they look at Insincere Marguerite? A lover? A fool? A monster? A slut? A dandy? Even the women who sleep under me; do they see a better person than was in the photograph? Do they care?<br /> <br /> As I look down at my contented doodler though, I worry; Julia stated we will not be safe until Mr. Grey, Master Darke, and Doctor Bright are dead. Julia is not a violent person, but she will do nearly anything to protect those she loves. Should I be worried?<br /> <br /> It is all most unsettling. Definitely.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXVII</i><br /> <br /> Did you miss it? Calamity\u2019s journal discussed an event the others did not.<br /> <br /> Tamara\u2019s card play was primarily tied to her Oracle Kith and Contracts, trying to get a read on her situation. After all, the PCs were being somewhat oblique about their intentions, and while she did not suspect a trap, exactly, her Oracle nature could not let it alone.<br /> <br /> Mr. Grey\u2019s behavior was a good indicator of the Clarity loss that would await Andromeda should they get the Table for her to use.<br /> As a none on mechanics, I allowed Calamity\u2019s player to purchase a merit which, like \u201cPrehensile Tongue\u201d for Insincere Marguerite was made more or less for the character, something I am mostly just doing for Changeling. Anyway<br /> <br /> <b>Hedgehog\u2019s Dilemma (level 2)</b><br /> <br /> If an opponent attacks Calamity with their bare hands, their player rolls a die. If even, it lands with no ill effects. If odd, the attacker takes half their Strength (rounded up) as damage from Calamity\u2019s glass spikes. This in no mitigates the damage Calamity takes, and non-barehanded attackers take no damage. An attacker can carefully attack Calamity to avoid any glass, but she adds her Wyrd to her defense.<br /> <br /> If Calamity does damage in a grapple, she does Lethal damage on her attack instead of Bashing unless she takes a penalty equal to her own Wyrd. If she is grappled her attacker takes damage equal to half their own Strength (rounded up) due to her glass spikes. This damage cannot be avoided. Armor applies normally.<br /> <br /> Drawback: Accidental contact can be dangerous with Calamity. An ally or innocent can take damage, which makes her dangerous. Sex or roughhousing requires a Dexterity + Athletics for her to avoiding harming her partner, and if she actually sleeps next to someone she damages them on an odd number on a single die roll.<br /> <br /> Well they have an interesting situation. What to do? We will see what they decide. Comments and Questions are welcome.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 04-14-2015, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T00:46:39-07:00","id":481195,"title":"","content":"Killing Grey may not have been the most prudent of courses. Completely understandable though.<br /> <br /> Angry Gawain is disconcerting. He reverts when inspired to genuine wrath it seems.<br /> <br /> What experience level average wyrd level would you say the group is at right now?<br /> <br /> It's interesting that this thing with Dark pops up now. If you recall, I had mentioned a valet character this game had inspired in my breezy noggin. I've recently had an image of a group of goons attacking the dream house and the valet introducing himself to them, cutting away to the others fighting, and then back to the valet tidying up after &quot;Taking out the trash&quot; and making a comment about the amount of laundry he has to do in a week.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","user":"omenseer","date":". 04-15-2015, 04:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T01:58:09-07:00","id":481229,"title":"","content":"Calamity does not apologize for art!<br /> <br /> If I am not mistaken, the average Wyrd is currently 4. And I like that valet idea you have there Omenseer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T02:02:35-07:00","id":481232,"title":"","content":"I was not actually expecting Grey to be murdered, but you know players keep you on your toes. And yea, angry Gawain is disconcerting.<br /> <br /> I THINK everyone is currently Wyrd 4. I am not sure about Ace, whose player's circumstances have made his presence spotty. But I am pretty sure everyone else is Wyrd 4. I have Insincere Marguerite's current stats, but not access to anyone else's right off. As putting them up is simple copypasta I will.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <b>Insincere Marguerite</b><br /> <br /> Changeling<br /> Concept: Mysterious Stranger<br /> Aspirations: Find and Reclaim Yvette (long term), Seduce Felicity (short term), Get Good Standing in the Autumn Court (short term)<br /> Virtue: Loyalty<br /> Vice: Possessiveness, Pride<br /> Seeming: Darkling<br /> Kiths: Tunnelgrub/Lurker<br /> Court: Night, the Court of Disgust<br /> Entitlements: None<br /> Titles: None<br /> Place of Birth: Paris, France<br /> <br /> Intelligence 2<br /> Wits 3<br /> Resolve 3<br /> <br /> Strength 2<br /> Dexterity 4<br /> Stamina 2<br /> <br /> Presence 2<br /> Manipulation 3<br /> Composure 4<br /> <br /> Academics 1<br /> Computer 1<br /> Crafts 1<br /> Investigation 2 (In the dark)<br /> Medicine: 0<br /> Occult 1<br /> Politics 0<br /> Science 0<br /> <br /> Athletics 3 (Tight Places)<br /> Brawl 1<br /> Drive 0<br /> Firearms 0<br /> Larceny 3 (B&amp;E) [Asset]<br /> Stealth 4 (Shadows)<br /> Survival 0<br /> Weaponry 0<br /> <br /> Animal Ken 0<br /> Empathy 3 (Intense Eye Contact)<br /> Expression 2<br /> Intimidation 1<br /> Persuasion 3<br /> Socialize 2<br /> Streetwise 1 [Asset]<br /> Subterfuge 2<br /> <br /> Darkness 5<br /> Fang and Talon: Feline 2<br /> Reflections 4<br /> Separation 1<br /> Shade and Spirit 0<br /> Smoke 5<br /> <br /> Wyrd 4<br /> Clarity 7<br /> Willpower 7<br /> Health 7<br /> Glamour 13<br /> Size 5<br /> Defense: 6<br /> Initiative: 8<br /> Speed: 11<br /> <br /> Contacts 2 (Criminal)<br /> Court Goodwill: Autumn 3<br /> Court Goodwill: Spring 1<br /> Double-Jointed 2<br /> Duel Kith 2<br /> Gentrified Bearing 4<br /> Language: English 2<br /> Language: French 3<br /> Mantle: Night 5<br /> Parkour 2<br /> Professional: Criminal 2<br /> Prehensile Tongue 2<br /> Resources 1<br /> Striking Looks 2<br /> Taste 1<br /> Vice-Ridden 2<br /> Quote: <i>\u201cHello! Ah, I see you have noticed me watching you\u2026\u201d</i><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T14:57:47-07:00","id":492932,"title":"","content":"Things are moving fast. Something like the murder of Mr. Grey won\u2019t stay secret for long, and our PCs find themselves engaged in argument.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXVIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> Afternoon, June 17th<br /> <br /> The hope present in the midst of a long vigil often becomes laughable in the face of the cruel Lady Fate. Yet, for all that it rankles, I must acknowledge that the man has a point. Two, as it happens. Not only is the safety of the Freehold entire paramount, but Lowjack is in a position to make demands. If he removes the Table as promised, and secures the motley\u2019s safety with a strong web of pledges, I must be satisfied. At least until such a time as the Freehold is determined to be safe without Darke\u2019s presence.<br /> <br /> I do wonder if such an affront to justice would sit as easily were I not benumbed by rage at my own lady. On whether or not the man Gray deserved to die I will concede that he may very well have not been innocent. If he willingly carried out a dishonorable order given by a dishonorable liege, or even did so to save his own skin, he certainly was not, and deserved the same fate as our villain. The truth of the matter is, if not lost, inconsequential at this point.<br /> <br /> More pressing is the reckless abandon she showed in this. Her first inclination is thoughtless amoral violence. Fine. I do not fault her on that, no matter what she believes. But that is why you have a priest, and a wisewoman, and a Master of the Guard and a spymaster. Because one\u2019s first inclination is not the only option. Perhaps we would have chosen that course. But <i>we</i> did not consider any others.<br /> <br /> She says that she wished to protect us. Does she think that the sins of one would never rest on the others? Does she truly believe any of us feel the better for not having been consulted? That if she were to be brought before a judge for her crime that I would allow them to touch her without destroying me first? Does she take me for a child, all unknowing of what makes up the world? Gah. At least there is no doubt she does not take me for a partner.<br /> <br /> <br /> Early morning June 18th<br /> <br /> Fuck. Fuck fuck fuck fuckity fuck fuck. Jesus, where the hell have I been for the past day and a half? Who have I been? That one\u2019s easier. Lord Bertilak is who. Recently I keep getting flashes, memories of day-to-day life as him. It\u2019s starting to seem more real than before, that life where I was the lord of a castle, with a wife and a witch and a duty and a story. Way more real than being a kid, and having a family, listening to music and watching movies. As for where, unfortunately, I\u2019m pretty sure where I\u2019ve been is right here. For once, I wish I\u2019d been dreaming. I wish this was all a nightmare.<br /> <br /> I hurt Calamity. I... it wasn\u2019t malicious. But I knew what I was saying when I sat where she couldn\u2019t even be nearby for movie night. And sure, she hurt me, but that\u2019s not the way it works, you know? Not the way it should work. I guess it\u2019s justice but... fuck. She drank almost as much as that night with the truth and dare. The way she sighed and leaned against me when I picked her up and took her to her room was heartbreaking. She fell asleep quickly. I could stay calm and comforting until then at least.<br /> <br /> I love her. I can\u2019t stay really mad at her for long. But Lord Bertilak was right about one thing. Nothing about what happened is the way you treat a partner, someone you respect and trust, you know? I can accept that she considers herself a monster, that that is a path she\u2019s decided to walk. I can accept that, if we\u2019d had that discussion, that she would have been arguing to kill someone we didn\u2019t know for certain was guilty, because of what he might do in the future. I could even respect where she was coming from. But eventually, she will have to accept that I am a man, not a fucking kid to be kept away from the scary things. That I get to make decisions about the path I walk, and she doesn\u2019t get to make them for me, you know?<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t choose the Dawn out of naivet\u00e9, dammit. I choose it consciously and with intent. She can\u2019t take that away from me, any more than I can take the monster away from her. I just wish she\u2019d stop trying, you know?<br /> <br /> <br /> Afternoon, June 18th<br /> <br /> I think things are better? I don\u2019t know how well I communicated things to Calamity when she woke up. She seemed appreciative of breakfast though, and didn\u2019t object when I followed her up for a shower. So I guess things are mostly back to normal at least. I\u2019m kinda foggy though cause I didn\u2019t sleep. And didn\u2019t really feel like asking Lori for a wakeup zolt again, you know? I might need to before tonight though. See, the meeting to dethrone Darke is tonight, at 8. So we need to be ready for problems there, either from Darke himself, or the Wyrd being a jerk, or maybe even from little grey aliens.<br /> <br /> I guess I Lord Bertilak didn\u2019t explain very well. Lowjack was pretty sure this whole thing was orchestrated by the Mothership - sending the Table down as bait to get Darke eliminated, and Andromeda to distract Joan. Not as a loyalist - Joan\u2019s got a keener sense than that. But if Lowjack is right, Andromeda is more useful to the Mothership by not being loyal. And those two, Darke and Joan (and Percival, but he\u2019s a jackass), are the first line of defense of the Freehold, the one that stops things *before* people get hurt. So his condition for agreeing to become the Winter Monarch was that Darke would be required to stick around and help with the defense, until we could build up better ones. Not... ideal, but I trust his judgement. Perhaps Darke will even see what he\u2019s done wrong for what it is, and not just some \u2018difficult\u2019 and \u2018well-intentioned\u2019 decision justifiable in the name of the Freehold. Perhaps.<br /> <br /> But anyway, that means we need to be prepared for the Mothership to capitalize on what chaos there turns out to be. Unless that happens though, Lowjack would prefer we stay out of it. So we\u2019re just kinda kicking around, you know? Well, Lori and Jacob went off to check on Tamara, cause she went home with the Handmaidens and then called in sick, so that\u2019s terrifying, but they haven\u2019t called for backup yet. Hopefully she\u2019s ok.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> What separates us from other people and makes us different? What is it about human beings that can cause us to see the same set of circumstances in such completely dissimilar ways? How can two people who both essentially want the same thing choose to go about achieving it using completely antithetical methods? What is it that separates me from someone like D? Or Calamity? Or Annabelle?<br /> <br /> I had crawled back into bed to cuddle with the Darklings for a while, and had started to drift off again when Marguerite stirred. She got dressed and made for the door, clearly intending to head downstairs for breakfast. Then, as she was reaching for the doorknob, she turned to look at the three of us. \u201cI want you to know, I love you all,\u201d she said sharply. Then she turned and fled the room.<br /> <br /> D and I looked blankly at each other for a minute while Julia stretched like a cat. Then we both sort of shrugged and started to get dressed.<br /> <br /> We didn\u2019t mention anything about it at breakfast, and D had to go to work right after she finished eating. After she left, breakfast-table conversation soon turned to Mr. Grey. Both Gawain and I had come to the conclusion that it would be best if we took him into our protection, both to keep him from telling Master Darke about our involvement in this situation, and so that we could produce him as a witness if the other monarchs had any questions about the Table and how it was used.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know why she didn\u2019t tell us then. I don\u2019t know why she let us drive all the way out to Venice Beach without telling us what we would find. The police lines were a shock, and the sight of the shattered second-story window was another. I started to freak out, assuming that Master Darke had already heard about what Mr. Grey had told us, and had begun his retaliation.<br /> <br /> Calamity told Gawain to pull into an alley a few blocks away. When we got there, she started talking. I think a part of me already knew what she was going to say. She killed Mr. Grey. She told us that it was to protect the motley; that she did it to keep him from telling Master Darke about our investigation. I wish I could believe that; I really do. And I think that in part <u>she</u> honestly believes it, but the truth runs deeper. It wasn\u2019t her reason, it was her <u>excuse</u>.<br /> <br /> Gawain drove us back to Santa Monica for our meeting with Lowjack. There was a lot of discussion back and forth on the subject of Mr. Grey\u2019s murder. Some of the motley thought it was the right move; a sort of pre-emptive strike to prevent trouble down the line. Others thought that the matter should have been discussed among the motley before action was taken. Jacob mostly kept silent on the subject, which I respect\u2026 Mr. Grey was a member of his Court, after all.<br /> <br /> After a while I couldn\u2019t take it anymore, and I confess I sort of quietly exploded. A man is <u>dead</u>. Does it matter if he was a friend or an enemy? How can we calmly sit around and discuss the facts of his murder as though the loss of one of our own means nothing? How can it ever be right to dole out the ultimate punishment for a crime someone hasn\u2019t even committed yet, and might <u>never</u> commit?<br /> <br /> Needless to say, it was a quiet, tense trip to Lowjack\u2019s, and we didn\u2019t present the most united front when we spoke to the once-and-future-king. What he told us when we explained the situation to him didn\u2019t make us any happier, either.<br /> <br /> What Tamara told us after the show Sunday night was true: Lowjack never wanted the monarchy, and he still doesn\u2019t want it. He agreed that Darke has gone too far, and that something needs to be done to prevent the continued misuse of the Table\u2026 but he put a new spin on it that I don\u2019t think any of us had considered. He described the roles of the Summer and Winter Courts in the Freehold, using a complex metaphor about antibodies and white blood cells. Essentially, the Winter Court\u2019s role is to quietly protect the Freehold from Gentry incursions during times of peace, while the Summer Court takes up the sword to beat back more obvious invasions.<br /> <br /> Every Court has their spies, but Master Darke is the spymaster for the entire Freehold. And he\u2019s <u>very</u> good at it. Lowjack believes that the Mothership might have allowed the Table to fall into Darke\u2019s possession, knowing that the rest of the Freehold would eventually find out about his misuse of its powers, and would not stand for it. Regardless of our personal feelings about the man\u2019s actions, Darke\u2019s removal will weaken the Freehold\u2019s defenses significantly. Add to that the fact that this is coming when Joan is distracted from her duties, and you get a perfect time for the Gentry to strike.<br /> <br /> The long and the short of it is that Lowjack is willing to take over as the King of Winter\u2026 but only on the condition that Master Darke be allowed to remain in place as spymaster. He won\u2019t be punished beyond removing him from the throne, and possible banishment somewhere down the line, when a suitable replacement can be found. Nobody much liked that solution, but after a brief discussion, we all agreed that it was the only way.<br /> <br /> We told Lowjack that we would agree to his terms, and asked him to contact Queen Charlotte to let her know. He also said something rather strange: he told us not to judge Darke too harshly, because his durance was something like living in Sin City.<br /> <br /> \u201cLas Vegas?\u201d I asked, confused.<br /> <br /> The others explained to me that <u>Sin City</u> in this case was a pop culture reference, probably to a movie based on a comic book which was a sort of concentrated look at the noir genre. We stopped at a video store on the way home and picked up a copy. What can I say? It was right next to the liquor store, and I felt the need for a fifth of bourbon in the worst way.<br /> <br /> So while the monarchs met to discuss deposing Master Darke and the Monday night show proceeded downstairs, we of the motley drank ourselves stupid and held an extended movie night. Things started out tense, but by the time the second flick was over we were starting to relax again (I blame the alcohol). Gawain sat by himself for the entire movie marathon, but he carried her off to the room they share at the end of the night when he saw how miserable his isolation was making Calamity.<br /> <br /> I was pretty stony toward Calamity at first as well, I admit. She refuses to apologize, or even to admit that she might have been wrong to take out Mr. Grey without even consulting the rest of us. But she looked so lost and alone sitting there by herself drinking alone\u2026 I couldn\u2019t let it stand. I called her aside after the first movie and spoke to her softly.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m still mad,\u201d I said to her seriously. \u201cIn fact, I\u2019m bordering on furious right now, and that\u2019s not likely to change any time soon.\u201d She nodded and lowered her eyes, and I leaned in and carefully kissed her forehead. \u201cBut I still like you, I still love you, and I still respect you, Calamity. I don\u2019t want there to be any mistake about that, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> I think I saw a little of her old spark return to her eyes at that. \u201cThanks, Lori,\u201d she said simply, and then we went back to start the second film.<br /> <br /> It was an eclectic night of movie-watching to say the least. We started out with the two films which had been scheduled, and then moved on to <u>Sin City </u>and another film Marguerite recommended.<br /> <br /> The first film was called <u>Robin Hood: Prince of Thieves</u>. It was fun; nothing to write home about, but a fairly good mindless action flick. It had its share of problems, sure\u2026 some of the acting was pretty wooden, and the leading man seemed to lose his British accent about fifteen minutes in (which was probably a good choice all in all\u2026 it wasn\u2019t very convincing to begin with). The villains were good, though\u2026 the Sheriff of Nottingham was delightfully wicked and crazy, and the man playing Guy of Gisborne had this sexy gravelly voice that set my loins a-quiver, if you know what I mean.<br /> <br /> Everyone gave me one of those Oh-Lorelei-You\u2019re-So-Out-Of-Touch looks when I asked why the filmmakers had felt it necessary to include the guy that played Dracula in that <u>Electric Company</u> show Brad and Cindy Mullendorf used to watch when I was sitting for them as a condemned Arab, though.<br /> <br /> D got back from work near the end of that first film, and that made everything a little bit better (well, I admit the bourbon helped too). She took in the fact that we were all drinking and watching movies earlier than usual, and noted the seating arrangement, and raised an eyebrow at me in question. I pulled her into my room and explained about Calamity, Mr. Grey, Lowjack, and Master Darke. She was suitably sympathetic, though I think on some level she might have agreed with Calamity about the dangers posed by Mr. Grey. I didn\u2019t pursue the subject.<br /> <br /> Before we rejoined the motley, I brought up the other thing that had been on my mind. \u201cHey, D,\u201d I began, \u201cabout what Marguerite said this morning\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> She grinned. \u201cI know, crazy right?\u201d she asked. \u201cI never would have expected her to just come out and say it so baldly\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ve been thinking a lot about our relationship with those two lately,\u201d I admitted, \u201cand\u2026 I mean\u2026 they\u2019re obviously more than just friends to us. I was thinking about\u2026 reciprocating.\u201d<br /> <br /> D cocked an eyebrow, still grinning.<br /> <br /> I sighed and pulled her close. \u201cYou\u2019ll always be first in my heart, D,\u201d I said earnestly. \u201cDon\u2019t ever doubt that. But I can\u2019t deny that I feel something for Marguerite and Julia, too. They\u2019re more than friends\u2026 more than just casual lovers, even.\u201d<br /> <br /> D laughed softly in my ear, and it was musical. \u201cYou don\u2019t have to explain, Lori,\u201d she assured me. \u201cThere\u2019s more than one way to love someone. And just because you and I have fallen in love, that doesn\u2019t mean we can\u2019t feel something for other people, too.\u201d She held me tightly and whispered into my ear. \u201cHell, I feel the same way\u2026 though I\u2019m much too macho to ever admit it.\u201d<br /> <br /> Then came the kissing.<br /> <br /> A few minutes later, we rejoined the group. I sprawled out on one of the sofas with my head in D\u2019s lap as she not-so-subtly groped me, played idly with my hair, and fed me the occasional spoonful of melty ice cream. The second movie was actually a parody of the first, made by the incomparable comic mind of Mel Brooks. <u>Robin Hood: Men In Tights</u> did not approach the hilarious majesty of <u>Young Frankenstein</u> (my personal favorite of his films), but it had more than a few laugh-worthy sequences, and watching it immediately after <u>Prince of Thieves</u> made it a little more topical.<br /> <br /> Plus it had Cary Elwes (Wesley from <u>The Princess Bride</u>) as Robin Hood, and that can\u2019t be bad.<br /> <br /> Next up was <u>Sin City</u>. It was a mostly black-and-white flick with splashes of color here and there to call attention to important plot or thematic elements, sort of like <u>Schindler\u2019s List</u>. But unlike that holocaust drama, in <u>Sin City </u>there were no shades of grey. The shadows were pitch black, and the lights were white as snow. It\u2019s almost ironic, as the characters and stories were all about moral ambiguities. Marv is an ugly man in almost every imaginable way, but there is something redeeming and pure in his quest to avenge the only person who ever saw the good in him. Dwight is a handsome rogue with a checkered past who is willing to do the most unthinkable things to protect the people he loves (even as he betrays them in little ways). And Hartigan \u2013 maybe the only <u>truly</u> good person in all of Sin City] \u2013 is forced to betray his principles and resort to acts of unspeakable barbarism to save his beloved Nancy.<br /> <br /> It was a shocking film, beautiful in its brutality. Parts of it were painful to watch. Decapitation, cannibalism, sado-masochism\u2026 the list of atrocities goes on and on. When I was growing up, the idea that a popular film would include not one but <u>two</u> on-screen castration scenes was unthinkable. If that\u2019s what Master Darke\u2019s durance was like, then maybe his choices regarding the Table are a little more understandable. Not forgivable, mind you\u2026 but understandable.<br /> <br /> The final film of the evening (well\u2026 it carried us well into the wee hours of the morning, actually) was called <u>Reservoir Dogs</u>, and Marguerite insisted that we watch it for some reason. It\u2019s a gritty crime film; the story of a heist gone wrong\u2026 although the heist itself is not shown. The audience only sees the aftermath of that disastrous escapade as the criminals turn on each other in savage ways. I think Marguerite was trying to tell us something in her own way. I confess I wasn\u2019t in the mood for moral lessons about solidarity in the wake of Calamity\u2019s earlier display of \u201cinitiative.\u201d<br /> <br /> I was, however, in the mood for debauched bedroom shenanigans once the movie marathon was over. D and I allowed ourselves to be led to Marguerite\u2019s room, and I once again found myself surrounded by my three lovers; the token Fairest in the middle of a writhing mass of Darkling flesh. Before things became too prurient, however, I pulled Marguerite up so that we were face to face.<br /> <br /> \u201cD and I were talking about what you said this morning, <i>ma cheri</i>,\u201d I said softly. I\u2019m not sure, but I think she actually lowered her eyes a bit when I said that, as if she didn\u2019t want to hear what I had to say. I caressed her face. \u201cI want you to know that I feel the same way,\u201d I said with as much warmth as I could muster, \u201cI love you both, and I\u2019m so glad we\u2019ve all found each other.\u201d I stroked Julia\u2019s hair; for once she didn\u2019t seem to have anything to say to that.<br /> <br /> A minute later, to prevent things from getting too mushy, I added \u201cD feels the same way, but she\u2019s much too macho to ever admit it.\u201d My soulmate chuckled, cuffed me a good one in the shoulder, and then decided to shut me up in a more pleasant way.<br /> <br /> The rest of the evening is kind of a blur, I admit.<br /> <br /> Lowjack called us bright and early the next day\u2026 well, bright and early for us, at least. Noonish. He let us know that the monarchs had all agreed to our plan, and they will be taking steps to replace Master Darke today. He also asked for a personal favor\u2026 he wanted me to check on Tamara Chance for him, as she left the bar early last night in the company of the Warlock\u2019s Handmaidens, and had called in sick this morning. Of course I agreed to look in on her, and Jacob and I dropped by her apartment less than an hour later.<br /> <br /> She seemed to be all right, if a bit tired and\u2026 \u201cdrained,\u201d I suppose, though that adjective seems a bit on the nose. I used my Contracts to restore a little of her vitality, and she felt much better immediately. We tried to warn her against dallying with the Handmaidens again, but I don\u2019t think she took us seriously. I don\u2019t judge\u2026 I know the thrill of loving a Leechfinger myself (though I know D would never drain me in the heat of passion), but I think we\u2019d better keep an eye on Tamara to make sure she doesn\u2019t end up getting hurt.<br /> <br /> <br /> So I\u2019ve had a few things to distract me and keep me from thinking about what Calamity did the other day. Every time I think about her treating Mr. Grey\u2019s life so casually it makes me so <u>angry</u>\u2026 it\u2019s hard to wrap my brain around the fact that she killed a man \u2013 snuffed out his life like a candle \u2013 just because he <u>might</u> turn out to be a threat at some point in the future.<br /> <br /> Why would she do such a thing?<br /> <br /> And why does it remind me of Annabelle, of all people?<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 04-26-2015, 06:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T14:58:21-07:00","id":492936,"title":"","content":"<b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> <b><b><u>Tuesday June 17<sup>th</sup></u></b></b><br /> <br /> I have told my motley many times that I am a monster, so why is that when I act like one they're all so fucking surprised? Maybe I shouldn't have told them, but I just couldn't lie to them directly yesterday. I knew it was going to go badly the moment everyone decided that we should take Grey with us to see Lowjack. Fuck it, maybe it would have been better to leave him alive but then none of the bastards would have gotten their just desserts.<br /> <br /> Oh yeah, the icing on this cake is that Darke is off limits. No one liked that, not even Lori. I do believe that the oaths Lowjack intends to bind him with will be ironclad but I don't trust any oath to keep Darke from finding a way to get back at us. I guess it is fucking fair play since as far as I'm concerned this deal is just a gorram delay on putting that motherfucking sonofabitch down like the Gentry he's trying to become. So yeah, we'll all play nice till the crisis is past and this city doesn't need Darke's toxic ass anymore. But in the end, not a one of us will be well and truly safe while that sick bastard's breathing. And I'll be damned (again) before I take that shit laying down. Lowjack and his damned logical thinking can go fuck themselves if he expects anything different.<br /> <br /> Fuck I'll be glad when Jacob gets back so we can spar. I'm not dumb enough to think that it's not an opportunity for him to speak to me discreetly but fuck it I need a fight and if he was going to yell at me he might as well have joined in when everyone else was. And by everyone I mean Lori and Gawain. Insincere Marguerite did try to kinda back me up. I mean, she didn't say I was right (and given how painfully clear Gawain and Lori had both made their positions I can't say I blame her.) But she did argue that I did what I thought was right and that I deserved at least a little mercy for that. And Lori did make a point of telling me that she still cared about me, which was part of why she was so mad at me for doing it.<br /> <br /> The worst was Gawain. He was furious. He shouted and then just drove in silence with a death-grip on the wheel. The rest of the day I could feel the anger coming off of him in waves and every time he had to look at me he was still enraged. Fuck, it would have hurt less if he'd just hauled off and laid into me. I'm good at dealing with that kind of fucking pain. And the fact that I fucking deserved it didn't fucking help. I fucking knew they'd never agree to killing Grey and I knew when I did it they'd be fucking pissed. Still, doesn't matter if you're the one that stabbed yourself or not, it still hurts just as much.<br /> <br /> So yeah, the mood when we showed up at Lowjack's was absolutely delightful. And then he went and laid out the Mothership's plan and how we'd all been played like a damned fiddle. Seems so obvious once he explained it all. Andromeda was perfect Joan bait and while I have had it with folks whining about it I can't deny that the woman is sorely distracted from keeping an eye out for loyalists. And Darke couldn't fucking resist having the Mothership's Thrice-damned Table right there. You know, even if murdering Darke is exactly what the Mothership wants, for once I don't give a rainbow colored crap about it. Which is why this plan is so absolutely fucktasticly perfect.<br /> <br /> Like I said, no one liked it. Not one little bit. But we had fuck all for choices. I mean, once Lowjack pointed out we were dancing to the Mothership's tune what were we going to do, tell him to go fuck himself? (Okay, I am almost surprised Gawain didn't but also kinda glad because I sure as fuck wasn't in any position to talk him down yesterday.)<br /> <br /> Well, once we'd finished that round of emotional pummeling we decided to stop on the way home. Lori knew a perfect little strip mall. (I am going to have to ask her about that when she's talking to me again.) One of the last surviving movie rental places in the fucking state anchoring a liquor store, a Ben and Jerry's, a pawn shop with guns and ammo and a c-store that had way too many baby food signs up. The look Insincere Marguerite threw me when I came back out of that store would have been hilarious any other day but I just waved my cigar. Zod that thing was cheap and nasty, might have just as well grabbed a handful of leaves from out back but it suited the rest of the day perfectly.<br /> <br /> Anyway, armed with double movie night and booze and ice cream, we headed up and told the understudies and assistants not to bother us even if the fucking place WAS on fire.<br /> <br /> And that was when the magic happened. We were filing into the den and folks were getting settled in. I looked over at the loveseat Gawain and I always share and hesitated. Gawain had been pretty solidly pissed at me all day so it didn't seem like time to just try to slip into his lap like usual, but I wasn't in the mood to fight either. As I was trying to guess as to proper seating, Gawain walked in with his sword (since, you know, fucking Gentry attack or Darke attack were both in the gorram forecast) and made things clear as fucking crystal. He didn't say anything or even look at me, he just walked past our usual seat and settled into one of the chairs by the wall.<br /> <br /> Well, at that point I was sorely fucking tempted to just leave. I mean, everyone was ticked off and I did not really want to sit by myself watching movies with them when nobody really wanted me there. Plus there was Lori and Insincere Marguerite and Julia all cuddlepiled onto the couch waiting for De La Rocha to join them. Hell, even Jacob and Luna were snuggled up. But I knew that if I tried to duck out I'd get drug back in and the last thing I wanted was to fuck up everyone's night. So since no one else wanted to be anywhere near me I snatched up a bottle with each hand and ended up sharing the loveseat with Captain Morgan and Jack Daniels.<br /> <br /> The timing was pure shit. Seems Gawain and Jacob had worked out this plan to watch 'Prince of Thieves' back to back with Mel Brook's sendoff of it, 'Men in Tights'. Yeah. Just what I needed, a reminder of what a fucking stupid little twit I used to be. Gods above and below that movie is shit. Maybe if I had not been sitting on the fucking loveseat alone getting hammered and feeling like shit it would have been better but I was as completely far from in the right mood for that as I could possibly have been. And I wasn't much better for the comedy. It was good, but I was just not in the mood. And drinking was not putting me any closer to it.<br /> <br /> After that we rolled 'Reservoir Dogs'. I need to watch that one again when I'm sober. I couldn't really keep the plot straight (and I know it wasn't really that deep). But there was that one scene with 'Stuck in the Middle with You' playing that got me out of moody and sullen for a few minutes. Yeah Mr Blonde, it was as good for me as it was for you. Then he got shot before he could light the guy up and I went back to being disappointed and quiet. Somehow I did manage to successfully download the song and set it as my ringtone. I think I'll keep it and I fucking dare anyone to say a gorram word about it.<br /> <br /> And the last one was 'Sin City' which I also need to watch again when I'm sober. It had been added because apparently Darke's durance in Arcadia was that same kind of hard choices noir hellhole. Guess it proves things could always be worse. At least my Keeper wasn't Frank Miller (Though I guess I'd have come out a hell of a lot sexier that way...) By that point, I really wasn't in any condition to be doing much of anything besides wallowing in my self pity. As it finished up, I realized that I was way past staying awake and that I don't exactly have my own bed these days. The thought of crawling down to the murder ghost bedroom crossed my mind but I wasn't really up to moving and I didn't figure getting strung up would be productive. So I just kinda sank down further on the loveseat and decided to pass out where I was.<br /> <br /> Only then I realized that Gawain was standing over me. I think I might have fucking cringed when he reached for me. I mean, I was so shitfaced at that point that I couldn't handle being yelled at any more. But he very gently took the bottles away from me and took care of them. Then he knelt down and just gathered me up and holy fuck did I curl up into him. It was all I could do not to fucking cry like a baby as he tucked me against his chest and carried me to our bed. He laid me down and sat there next to me and I latched onto him like a drowning woman. Fuck I wish I'd had some fucking iota of self control or something. But I was way too drunk to be anything but a fucking open book and getting cold shouldered like that fucking hurt. If he said anything, I don't remember it. I think he realized how fucking wasted I was and decided to wait till I had a decent chance of remembering it. Or maybe he did and I just forgot.<br /> <br /> I was still attached tighter than a tick when I woke up. And from the way Gawain was sitting, I could tell he had sat up watching me all night. He asked me how I felt and I muttered something about feeling like I'd had too much to drink last night. Then he said his piece. I think he'd been rehearsing it in his head overnight. The anger was gone but it had been replaced by sad and disappointed which was worse. I bit down on my lip and just listened as he told me I wasn't the one that had to carry the motley's sins. Fucking hell, how can he still think I'm anywhere close to as worthwhile as the rest of them? And he told me he was a murderer as well and that it wasn't my job to protect any of them from guilt.<br /> <br /> Then he finally told me what I'd been needing to hear for the past twenty-four hours. He told me he still loved me and he got up to go make breakfast. When I came down, Gawain kissed me on the cheek and he was attentive during breakfast. Jacob had a hangover remedy for me and Gawain made pretty much the perfect breakfast for someone hung over. Lori even started to get up when the office phone rang before I waved her off. Despite how they feel about what I did they still care about me. And dammit, I care about them. That's why I did it.<br /> <br /> After we got word that the official meeting of monarchs was happening tonight we decided to check in with Lowjack and make sure our part in this whole ugly clusterfuck was done for now. There wasn't anything on that front but apparently the Handmaidens had descended upon Tamera last night and she'd called in sick (something she never does.) So Jacob and Lori went to check on her and it seems the Handmaidens drained her a damn sight more than just halfway to death last night. What the bloody fucking hell are those bitches up to? Is this some sort of dig to find out about Lowjack through his aide de camp or is it just that she's such fucking sweet prey?<br /> <br /> Well, since I had to wait for Jacob to get back I went up to shower and change out of yesterday's clothes. Gawain followed me up and decided to join me in the shower. I didn't repeat any of last night's pathetic mewling but I certainly didn't turn him away. I think he and I both want everything to be back to normal so fucking desperately but... but it wasn't. It's not. I don't think we're done or any shit like that but the whole fucking mess is still lingering there between us.<br /> <br /> I realize that I fucked up. I have to apologize to Gawain for that. Really I owe them all one. Not for trying to protect them. I won't apologize for that. But this is making me realize I am not a fucking island. Even if they didn't know what I was doing they're caught up in hurricane Calamity now. I made a decision that affected them and I made it without their consent. I thought it was the right thing to do based on what we knew at the time but the bottom fucking line is it wasn't my decision to make. And now I can't help but wonder in hindsight if it was even as clearly logical as I convinced myself it was or if I fucking talked myself into believing it was because I wanted it to be the right answer so I could murder Grey. Fuck, that's exactly the kind of shit I swore I wouldn't do again after Belleview. At any rate, by not telling them I also showed a lack of trust. I didn't think of it that way but listening to Gawain this morning made me realize it. I didn't trust him. I didn't trust any of them. I knew they wouldn't agree and I fucking decided that I was right and they were all wrong. Jeez that was pretty fucking arrogant of me doesn't it?<br /> <br /> And I know Gawain's not innocent. I've been in his nightmares. I've seen what haunts him. I didn't set out to treat him like a child. I just didn't want him to have to do that again. More than anyone, I need to talk to him. I need to explain. I need to apologize. And I fucking need him to forgive me. Because unless he can and will then it doesn't matter how much he still loves me it'll keep lingering there between us. And that means we're fucked up for good and it's my own damn fault and there is not a damned thing I can do to make it right again.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Well, there\u2019s no question about it. Calamity was in fact up to something last night. We (the Motley and Luna) decided at breakfast that we would drive out to Mr. Grey\u2019s house and bring him back for protection (for him and us). We arrived at his house to find it surrounded by Police and Fire trucks. We kept going and stopped around the corner for Insincere Marguerite to get out and sneak onto the crime scene and find out what happened. She came back with a Police report that said that an explosive device went off in Grey\u2019s bedroom, killing him and setting fire to part of the house. Calamity seemed almost sheepish when this was revealed and she admitted that she had thrown a grenade into the man\u2019s bedroom. Her rationale was to keep us safe from him and Master Darke should he decide to talk to the Winter Monarch.<br /> <br /> To say that folks were not pleased with this turn of events is putting it mildly. Lori was horrified at the whole thing. Despite Calamity\u2019s reasons, misplaced though they be in regards to some of us, I can understand. She apparently wanted to keep the rest of us from becoming murderers by doing this herself. It\u2019s too late for some of us, as Gawain pointed out, but I can understand the sentiment. I would not want Lorelei, Insincere Marguerite, or Ace to have to experience that. I understand that Lori feels upset about the whole thing, but that\u2019s not the same as having another person\u2019s blood on your hands. Marguerite has enough stuff on her mind right now, I wouldn\u2019t want to add that to it. Though she is probably better able to handle the situation than say Lori is.<br /> <br /> Gawain was really upset that the rest of us had not been consulted about the whole thing and that no other options were explored before Calamity went for the permanent one. I don\u2019t know if I\u2019ve ever seen the normally unflappable Knight so livid as he was then. The argument went on for a bit longer on how the situation could have been handled when Lori broke in. She was upset that we were arguing over technicalities when a man had died. I will admit that the reality of Mr. Grey\u2019s death was not the first thought in my head when the situation presented itself. My first thoughts were of the technicalities and I told her that right now we don\u2019t have the luxury of mourning for the man, we have to work out the details before it comes back to bite us in the ass. I don\u2019t think she was all that happy with me or my comments, but I can\u2019t let myself worry overly much about it. We really don\u2019t have the luxury of putting the details off until later. We have to deal with it before the fallout hits. To do otherwise would make us vulnerable.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite agreed with Calamity that the rest of us didn\u2019t need to be involved, though I think she thought that we could have discussed our options rather than someone acting alone. The whole situation was later related to the movie \u201cReservoir Dogs\u201d which is basically about a heist that goes wrong and ends badly for all involved. I can see the similarity to some extent. I just hope that things don\u2019t end for us like they did for the guys in that movie.<br /> <br /> Once we\u2019d finished arguing, or at least run out of things to say, we went on with our original plan to meet Lowjack today. We were originally going to bring Mr. Grey with us, but that wasn\u2019t exactly an option, so we went without. When we arrived we were met by John himself who offered us a drink before we talked. I think everyone accepted. We then went to his office to have our chat. It went better than I was expecting it to.<br /> Lowjack asked us what we needed to talk to him about so I started off by explaining what we\u2019d found out about Master Darke, the Table, Mr. Grey, all of it. I didn\u2019t see much point in hiding details from him. We wanted him to do something for us, so I figured being honest from the start was for the best. I left off the bit about Mr. Grey being dead though. We could discuss that later. After we were done explaining what Master Darke had been up to we told him about the plans to remove him from power. John was a step ahead of us and asked us if we intended for him to take Master Darke\u2019s place as Winter monarch. We said yes.<br /> <br /> John explained that if he were to be the Winter King that he could not banish or execute Master Darke for his actions. I\u2019ll admit that he gave us some pretty convincing reasons why. Not that I wanted the man dead, but I\u2019m not sure about some of the others. John told us to think of the Winter court as the white blood cells of the freehold. We seek out intruders that intend harm. We identify those individuals and remove the threats quietly. Then the Summer court acts as the antibodies for the freehold and works to eliminate the bigger threats. Essentially the Winter court is the first line of defense against the Gentry and their loyalists. Master Darke and his crew are a very effective deterrent. They do their jobs well, and the freehold has been largely kept safe. If we removed Darke from the city (one way or the other) then we are leaving ourselves open to attack. It is no secret that agents of at least two Genry have their eyes set on our city.<br /> The idea that the Mothership could have created this whole situation intentionally was brought up as well. It just so happens that an object that Master Darke would covet is introduced to the city. Darke then goes too far in the use of said device. We find out about his actions and work to remove him from power, and if not done properly, remove him from his position as protector. At the same time Andromeda is introduced to the freehold and Joan, another front line defender, is smitten. All of her attention is now on the little alien girl instead of watching the borders like she used to. Not that Lowjack thought that Andromeda was a loyalist or intentionally drawing Joan\u2019s attention away from her job, but she sure is a convenient distraction.<br /> <br /> We asked to speak amongst ourselves for a moment and Lowjack showed us to an empty room. We discussed our options and agreed that while some of us were not keen on John\u2019s conditions concerning Master Darke, they were reasonable. Someone also brought up the idea that that there might be a whisper campaign against the Winter court, or at least those that are on the front line (so to speak). It seems that all of the front line people in the Winter court are looked at with suspicion or at least wariness. Master Darke and those close to him are set apart from the rest of the freehold. Granted they are not the most sociable group and they are dangerous, but they\u2019ve never shown themselves to be anything but loyal to the freehold itself. I won\u2019t deny the enmity between Darke and Torrez but that\u2019s mutual. Torrez is as much to blame for the hostility as Darke is. Thing is, Torrez doesn\u2019t have the same reputation that Darke does. At least people don\u2019t treat him the way they do Master Darke, and he\u2019s just as dangerous as the Winter king.<br /> <br /> After we talked we rejoined Lowjack and let him know that we agreed to his terms. He said that he\u2019d talk to Queen Charlotte and get things rolling. That settled, we said our good-byes and headed out. On the way home there was an effort to move onto brighter topics so we discussed which movies we were going to watch for Movie Night. The two Robin Hood movies were mentioned (Prince of Thieves and Men in Tights). It had been said while we were talking to John that Master Darke\u2019s durance was much like \u201cSin City[\u201d if that would help us to understand his motivations. Lori was not familiar with the movie, which led to conversation about movies appropriate to the situation. \u201cSin City\u201d of course was listed, as well as \u201cReservoir Dogs.\u201d Lori hadn\u2019t seen that one either, which led to us renting more movies than we intended. We also stopped to pick up alcohol and ice cream for the making of drinks later. It was promising to be a very lazy rest of the day.<br /> <br /> So, we watched the two Robin Hood movies in the afternoon, then took a break and watched the other two movies at night. Things were still kind of tense despite the movies. Gawain elected to sit by himself in a single seat and had his sword leaning against it near his leg. It was rather clear that he was still upset with Calamity about what had happened, which seemed a bit out of character for him. He doesn\u2019t usually get as upset as he did today or if he does, he doesn\u2019t hold onto that anger for that long. To be fair though, all of us were still upset or shaken by the day\u2019s events and had been drinking pretty steadily. I don\u2019t think I\u2019ve seen Calamity drink so much since the night we played Truth or Dare. She was not in a good way at the end of the night. Gawain had been drinking pretty heavily too, though at the end of the evening he seemed to really notice what shape Calamity was in and scooped her up and carried her to their room. Perhaps he finally forgave her? Or the bulk of his anger passed and he went back to his normal self?<br /> <br /> As for myself, I drank probably a bit more than I intended to. Actually no, I think I did intend to drink that much. It was a long, stressful and confusing day and I didn\u2019t want to be sober at the end of it. So, I got good and maudlin. After the movies Luna and I went upstairs and just snuggled. It says something about me that I allowed myself to be so vulnerable with someone that could likely kick my ass six ways from Sunday. I trusted her to keep me safe and just let myself go. I haven\u2019t done that in a long time. And if anyone can appreciate that trust I think it\u2019s Luna. She holds herself apart from others, much the way I do. I have only ever seen her relax and be comfortable in Calamity or my presence, which makes me feel a bit warm inside at the thought.<br /> <br /> And now, in the wee hours of the morning I write in this stupid book and think about my fucked up day. Thankfully I\u2019ve moved out of being maudlin and into a more introspective mood. So much has happened in such a short time. I\u2019m not sure if the others really understand how much is going to change. It\u2019s more than Darke being replaced as Winter king. Some people may resent our place in his removal. Others may suddenly be more friendly. And I\u2019m not even sure how this is going to affect my relationship with him. I still work for him on the side. Hell, it was part of our agreement when I first accepted the job in the Dream House. He wanted someone inside to represent the Winter Court\u2019s interests, and to help sow sorrow at the same time. His side of the bargain was to keep Elena safe from threats. I have been fulfilling my side of the deal, as has he. My job doesn\u2019t stop when/if he steps down. My bargain is with him, not the title.<br /> <br /> I know the others are afraid of Master Darke, and with good reason. The man is dangerous, but he hasn\u2019t done wrong by me. Hell, there are a lot of dangerous people in the freehold, but for some reason Darke seems to be singled out. Maybe people are not comfortable with his somewhat amoral attitude. It\u2019s true that he\u2019s not very expressive, and can be damn intimidating, but some of that can be attributed to what happened to him in Arcadia. He does what needs to be done. I can understand that, and it doesn\u2019t really bother me all that much. I think the whole thing with the Table went a bit too far, but other than that he has worked in the best interests of the freehold.<br /> <br /> All of that may say something about me though. I know that there is something intrinsically wrong with me. I don\u2019t seem to react to things in the same way that others do. Well, most others. If Lorelei is our moral compass, then I\u2019m way off. She was very upset over the death of Mr. Grey. I was not happy with it, but at least some of that stemmed from the fact that wasn\u2019t tactically good for him to die right now. And I know that\u2019s not what should be going through my head. I should be upset over the loss of life. I think a part of me is. I didn\u2019t really know the man, and my first (and only) impression of him was rather flat. Not sure if that\u2019s the right word for it, but he was very hollow and I couldn\u2019t help but get the impression that whoever he was in the past was long gone. I should have been more upset by what happened, but I wasn\u2019t. I mean, I\u2019m not as cold as I used to be. There are things that bother me now and I know they didn\u2019t used to. I\u2019ve always taken offense at close friends and family (not that I remembered I had family in Arcadia) being hurt. Then that thing with Mary\u2019s fetch came up and I found myself getting angry on behalf of someone that was not a close friend. Maybe it was because we as a motley had agreed to keep an eye out for her? Mr. Grey on the other hand was a complete stranger to me, and I find that I\u2019m not overly affected by his death. That would seem to follow with my old self, but I am more than a bit intimidated by Master Darke, but I\u2019m fairly certain that I would be upset if he was killed. I guess that means that I\u2019m getting better, but I\u2019m just not quite whole yet.<br /> <br /> **** **** **** ****<br /> <br /> This morning\u2019s breakfast was a bit subdued. Not because of mood, but because most of us were in some way or fashion hung over. When Calamity came down, after she got her morning kiss from Gawain, I offered to make her a prairie oyster. To my surprise, she accepted. So, I made the infamous drink that is supposed to cure hangovers. No one else took me up on the offer, so I just made the one. All that aside, Gawain seemed to be back to his normal self this morning. He was sweet and attentive to Calamity and was definitely more open to public displays of affection. Last night I could not say the same, so they must have talked (unlikely) or he worked through what was specifically making him mad and got over it enough to be affectionate with his girlfriend.<br /> <br /> Shortly after breakfast we got a call from Moon, who let us know that there would be a meeting of the Monarchs tonight to go over everything. We made sure that our presence was not necessary and hung up. I then called Lowjack to let him know that we\u2019d been informed of the upcoming meeting and to see if he needed us to do anything beforehand. He said that there was nothing that we needed to do for the meeting, but did have a favor to ask. Apparently Tamara called in sick today, which is out of the ordinary for her. To top it all off she was seduced away from the bar last night by the Handmaidens. That is also out of the ordinary for her. Not just to be seduced by them, but to be seduced away from her job at all. Then to top it all off, she called in sick this morning, claiming that she felt unwell.<br /> <br /> So, John asked us if Lorelei knew any of the Spring Court healing contracts. I answered that she did, and he asked if we could check on Tamara to make sure that she was okay. I got Tamara\u2019s address from John, and Lori and I headed straight there. She answered the door when we knocked, but it was readily apparent that she was not feeling well. Lori did her thing and healed Tamara. She said that the Winter courtier had been weakened significantly. We asked her what happened and she said that she remembered being seduced by the Handmaidens and they all came back to her place. They laid on the charm and one thing led to another. She was not too clear on details, but she did remember them asking her if she wanted to die. She said that she did not. They asked her if she was certain and she said that she was. They left sometime after Tamara passed out.<br /> <br /> My theory is that they used their leechfinger abilities on her and drained away some of her life energy. If she had answered that she did want to die I\u2019m pretty sure that I would not have been able to have a conversation with the shy woman this afternoon. I suppose it is a good thing that they asked if she wanted to die instead of just trying to kill her, but the fact that they did anything at all is a little disturbing. They could have killed her. I suppose the fact that they left her alive speaks to their not so malicious intentions, but they did leave her in a severely weakened state. She also said that she remembered them asking her general questions about herself and about Lowjack. I can\u2019t help but wonder if they knew what was going to happen with Darke, or if they were just curious about those that have influence in the freehold and figured the best way to get Tamara to talk was to weaken her from the get go. They were also fairly obvious in what they were doing. They had to know that their actions against Tamara would not go unnoticed. Question is was that intentional on their part or were they just being sloppy?<br /> <br /> So, before Lori and I left to check on Tamara I had asked Calamity if she would like to spar after I got back. I figured we could both use the practice, and the exercise would help sweat out the hangover. She agreed readily enough, so I\u2019m assuming she had similar thoughts. To be fair though, Calamity has yet to turn down an offer of sparring. I will admit that I kind of had an ulterior motive in asking her to fight. I wanted to let her know that I don\u2019t blame her for what she did. I don\u2019t necessarily agree with the course of action that she chose, but I don\u2019t blame her for it. To blame her would mean that I did not have similar thoughts to hers, but I did. I had considered briefly that it might be necessary to kill Grey to keep the others safe. He did not see inclined to talk so I put that plan on a back burner. I was not dismissing it out of hand, I just thought we had time to investigate other alternatives. But Calamity is a child of the moment and acted in what she thought was the best interests of the motley. I cannot fault her for wanting to keep the rest of us safe in her own way.<br /> <br /> In some ways I think a lot of us didn\u2019t get much of a chance to grow up when we\u2019re in Arcadia. Calamity was taken as a child and spent much of her durance as one. When she got back she had suddenly aged several years and was expected to just pick up as if she had lived all the in-between years. Lorelei is still a confused teenager looking for approval. Not that we ever really grow out of that I suppose, but for her not much time passed at all in her Keeper\u2019s realm. For Ace, time was not important. Insincere Marguerite is the same way in some regards. Time was not important for her, just the moment. For Gawain and myself, too much time passed and I think we did a bit too much growing up. My fetch is just eighteen, but I lived in the Lady\u2019s realm for more years than he\u2019s been \u201calive.\u201d Gawain lived for hundreds if not thousands of years in Arcadia. I think the two of us have lost more than we\u2019d like to admit.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> My mental state is improving somewhat. Happily.<br /> <br /> Before we left to see Lowjack, Calamity came to speak to me. She saw my distraction and was looking for a time to discuss it.<br /> <br /> I vented a bit\u2026how unsure I was about many things. How worried I was by the dogmatic \u201cWhat the Gentry do is bad because the Gentry do it\u201d lines I have been hearing. Indeed, it seemed as much horror was from the emulation of Gentry behavior by Mr. Grey and Master Darke as by the nature of the act itself. At the same time, I don\u2019t want to be on a slippery slope of becoming too much like Mama Lion, so I was torn. Calamity was very understanding. She tried to encourage me. I thanked her for listening, and not trying to stab me, which she regrettably but understandably misconstrued and I had to explain. I did not mean to call her violent. Naturally.<br /> <br /> Nonetheless, it was good she was trying to understand. Everyone else was reticent. Well, Julia was dogmatically on my side, but not in a way that helped. Sadly.<br /> <br /> When I left the bed with Lorelei, De La Rocha and Julia, I told them I loved them. Which is true. I did not plan to, but it sat in my throat and had to be said. It was far from the first time Julia had heard it but they were possibly the second and third person I had uttered the words to outside a familial sense. The words were surprisingly hard to say despite insisting to be said. I felt vulnerable. I don\u2019t like feeling vulnerable. Certainly.<br /> <br /> Tonight, Lorelei approached me as we went, as a group, to bed. She wanted me to know she felt the same way. De La Rocha essentially confirmed it without saying it. Julia made it clear that she had feelings for them.<br /> <br /> I am happy.<br /> <br /> Of course, it\u2019s not all equal; Lorelei and De La Rocha have a special bond, as do Julia and I. But we are all close. Having these lovers feels right. I do want to talk to them about my thoughts on my own evolution and considerations of my role in the world, and how that intersects with my relationship with Faerie but\u2026not now.<br /> <br /> Even outside I\u2019s emotional tumult, much is going on.<br /> <br /> Lowjack has agreed to be Winter King. But he had requirements; particularly that Darke and his team serve the city, at least in short term until we can get things solidified. He noted that removal of that group would leave us quite vulnerable, and that, in fact, this was probably the plan of the Mothership all along; to remove the lookouts for incoming loyalists and threats so the Summer Court cannot respond until they are already in the city. While the Summer Court would likely win the Mothership\u2019s forces, if well coordinated, could steal a number of people. Lowjack is cunning enough to be on the lookout for it.<br /> <br /> I would have to note this sat poorly with Gawain. Poor Gawain, like many Elementals, including my dear Flores, he does not understand people. He does not understand realpolitik. He is intelligent enough to understand the only way to get this done is to take Lowjack\u2019s deal, but he seems to deeply resent it. Silly Gawain, if people got what they deserved most of your friends would be dead. It all works out. Usually.<br /> <br /> Mr. Grey is dead, killed by Calamity to protect us. An understandable move, and she was unwilling to directly lie to us about it. She had the decency to cover it up and not use her usual modus operandi. This sat poorly with Gawain too. I don\u2019t think it was an ideal move, but I know why she did it. The Motley certainly did yell a lot though. Well, Lorelei and Gawain anyway. Jacob and I not so much. Definitely.<br /> <br /> In happier news, had movie night. Double movie night. First were <i>Prince of Thieves</i> and <i>Men In Tights, </i>Gawain and Jacob\u2019s picks. I had little use for the former, but Cary Elwes was in the latter therefore it was acceptable. Lorelei actually knew who Mel Brooks was. Actually Alan Rickman was pretty handsome in <i>Prince of Thieves</i>, but that did not make the movie acceptable. Unfortunately.<br /> <br /> The second pair were <i>Reservoir Dogs</i> and <i><i>Sin City</i></i>. The former was my choice. I felt it was important to demonstrate what can go wrong in a heist if the team cannot rely on one another. Especially in light of current events. I hope the group got the right message and understands how important trust and teamwork is. Calamity, for her part, was rather distracted by Mr. Blonde\u2019s torture scene. Not upset, quite the opposite, actually. I blame her being American. <i><i>Sin City</i></i> was to show something similar to Master Darke\u2019s Durance. My goodness but Miho was tasty. I might have preferred it have been shown on a different night so as not to blunt <i>Reservoir Dogs</i> impact. Possibly.<br /> <br /> Tonight is the second night in a row my lovelies and I have spent together. I feel this bodes well for the future. Definitely.<br /> <br /> o o o o<br /> <br /> Things are going well, but ominously Tamara was seduced by the Handmaidens and left greatly weakened. She is far from the first to have experienced that\u2026they clearly saw her as prey. I am not sure what they were after, but I suspect it was access to Lowjack. Do they suspect he will soon by Monarch or are they up to something else. I must investigate.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXVIII</i><br /> <br /> This was mostly a drama session. Not much needs elaboration.<br /> <br /> Lowjack\u2019s office had a lot of character. He had pictures of himself with several individuals including Robert Kennedy and Jimmy Hoffa. It had a number of bowling trophies and awards from everything from the Teamsters Union to Toastmasters.<br /> <br /> Most movies viewed had been preplanned for some time Sin City was an unplanned addition. The Drama made the Robin Hood movies go down differently than they likely otherwise would have, given Gawain picked Pimp of Thieves knowing Calamity adored it before she was taken.<br /> <br /> For those who enjoy my Actual Plays, I have started a Crossover one set between 1920 and 1949 called <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465832-world-of-darkness-the-golden-eagle-actual-play\">The Golden Eagle</a>. It should be taking place across Europe and the Levant, as a group of Supernaturals drawn togather by a strange artifact and mysterious patron work to survive in the post Great War era as Fascism and other dark forces rise. There are three Changelings among the PCs: Dearbh\u00e1il MacGowan of Ireland; Fairest Minstrel/Windwing of the Spring Court, Dacian Umbr\u0103 of Romania; Darkling Lurker/Larcenist of the Spring Court, and Lizette \u00c9toile of France; Wizened Inventor/Gremlin of the Autumn Court. The plots won't be Changeling heavy but expect some Changeling elements. I expect most games will have their critters show eventually. There will be some pulp and noir elements worked in, so if you enjoy that sort of thing check it out. And don\u2019t forget to check out my Geist game (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\">Balance of Shadows)</a> and Demon (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\">Night Train Detective Agency</a>) as well.<br /> <br /> But it was an interesting session wasn\u2019t it? Comments and Questions are welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T12:51:43-07:00","id":511057,"title":"","content":"The aliens are coming. Little grey men and women creep through the hedge toward Malibu and Santa Monica. Actions set in motion begin show results. The arrival begins.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXIX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> Evening, June 18th<br /> <br /> It is time. Our enemies are upon us and our forces here have girded themselves as<br /> <br /> No. Dammit, no. I am NOT Lord Bertilak, prepping to fight with my vassals on behalf of our king. I am Gawain and me and my motley and some others the Monarchs sent over are getting ready to defend ourselves from people who have been hurt and brainwashed and molded to the very will of a [strike]tyr[/strike] fucking jackass. Maybe if I tell things in order, you know, I\u2019ll be able to keep that straight at least.<br /> <br /> So, once Jacob and Lori got back and said Tamara was now recovering/mostly recovered from the Handmaiden\u2019s leechfingery attentions, I spent the rest of the afternoon at the forge. I worked on blades for all of us, you know, that use them - a pair of knives for Jacob, my sword and a pair of throwing knives for Calamity. I figured she would be using her guns for this, but I didn\u2019t want to leave her out again, you know? Besides, I was in the zone and it was a good way to just tune out, you know, how tired I was and all the lingering badness.<br /> <br /> The others kept themselves busy until the show. Calamity and Jacob sparred for a bit. Willow Black showed up at some point, and was talking with Jacob when I brought Calamity her knives. Lori was off modeling, which made me a little nervous, but things weren\u2019t really gonna start til 8 anyways, at least, you know, we figured. Insincere Marguerite kept Luna company while Jacob sparred and Calamity caught up on paperwork and stuff.<br /> <br /> Door guard duty at the show was more exciting than usual. White Maria showed up with a concealed SMG. She seemed really, you know, nervous, but I checked using my Dawn contract and she\u2019d brought it for self-defense, so I figured she knew about the potential Mothership threat. I made sure Calamity knew about it anyways. TJ was armed as well, with a mace, but his intentions were clearer and his status as a guardian was, you know, less surprising, I guess? Louie showed up too, and was gracious enough to show me the proper courtesy to let me know he was armed, with an assault rifle. He even offered to stash it with Jacob behind the bar. I took him up on that. I felt a little bad, you know, taking his weapon and not TJ\u2019s, but an assault rifle would have caused more of a panic among the non-Changelings than a mace. That was all there was to it - I trust both of them. Especially after that, I probably trust Louie at least a little more, you know?<br /> <br /> Since we had a few Changelings here by themselves, I decided to go around and offer escorts to people, so they wouldn\u2019t be out along tonight. I went to Haley first, which was really, really good. She was talking super nasally and, well, alien-like, saying she felt strange. I pulled her to the bar, scaring away a few folks so we, you know, had a corner to ourselves.<br /> <br /> I asked Calamity to call Joan and make sure Andromeda was ok. She had warned them off after killing Mr. Grey, since Darke might have come for Andromeda, if he figured things out before stuff got moving. Turns out that was for the best, cause they were far enough away that Andromeda wasn\u2019t affected the way Haley was.<br /> <br /> I got to the point Haley was rocking in place with her hands over her ears pretty quickly. I hated to leave her, but I figured that reaction was proof the Mothership was going to move tonight, so it was even more important to make sure no one left alone. I worded it poorly with Chalcedony, but after, you know, getting my foot out of my mouth and convincing her I <i>wasn\u2019t</i> trying to hold her here, she said maybe she\u2019d stick with White Maria. Flores was hoping to stay the night with Insincere Marguerite and Oleander with Lori, I think. Or, you know, Flores was just teasing her. They were gonna be safe here though. I didn\u2019t figure Madame Spidertoes or Dionisia as her escort needed protection, but she was gracious about my offer anyway, you know. She even told me to have a drink on her, once my duties were over and everything.<br /> <br /> I had just gotten back to the bar to hear Haley say she could almost make out the message, something about Joan. She kept trying really hard and managed to figure out that 20 people had been sent to Joan\u2019s house! Calamity whispered to let me know Joan was on her way back so I stepped aside to where Haley couldn\u2019t hear to call her and warn her off. She decided to come to the Dream House instead.<br /> <br /> Monica arrived just as Calamity led Haley off, and they all three went down to the basement. Haley was worried about the signal, you know, l forcing her to so something she didn't want to, so Calamity restrained her. She kept trying hard to hear the signal though, and told us that the Mothership was still moving people into position and trying to figure out if the Winter Court had been eliminated.<br /> <br /> Calamity had some things she needed to do, and I was all prepped, so I took over Haley guarding duty, with Monica. She told me to call Captain Jack if Haley said anything about the Monarchs being in danger, and gave a number for Tommy for anything else. Haley didn\u2019t wind up getting any new messages from the signal, but Andromeda did call to tell me what she knew about how they fought, you know? Stun/weakening guns and electrified fields that were obvious if used, but would shock anyone who hit them. She said contact with a large amount of metal would draw the current away though, so I worked out the next clause of my Contract with metal and tore a door of my van so I\u2019d have plenty to work with, if I needed to.<br /> <br /> Me and Monica got relieved a little later, by Julia. Lori had figured out that she and Flores could use their wake-up jolt to remove the weakening effect of their guns, so the oranges I brought them from the kitchen on my way up were just the first in a line of food offering for the pair of them. Jacob had just gotten word from Tamara that in about 15 minutes, the word was going to go out that the Winter Court had been detained, you know, for the most part, when really, Dr. Bright, Molly Nuit, Vic Twilight and Twitch were being armed and sent out to reinforce places more secretly. Tamara figured the Mothership would make its move once that news got out widely.<br /> <br /> It did. We\u2019d just gotten the mortals out, citing broken plumbing and health codes to prevent a panic, when we got word that people had moved on Joan, Oleander and Captain Jack\u2019s houses. Dr. Bright called Jacob to let him know that around 10 people were approaching us via the Hedge, but the Winter courtiers had, you know, laid a trap for them, so they might be less by the time they got here.<br /> <br /> Joan got there shortly after we got that word, which made me feel much better. Louie warned that she might want to stay out of sight - the counterattack at Joan\u2019s had killed 10 or so of the [strike]aliens[/strike] Mothership\u2019s people, but they kept searching, while the attackers at Oleander\u2019s and Captain Jack\u2019s ran as soon as they were struck at. Louie figured that if they saw Joan, they\u2019d bring everything to bear on the Dream House.<br /> <br /> That gave me an idea. The House is not precisely the fortress town of Montargis, but we do have considerable strength here. If we did show Joan, we should be able to hold out until the bulk of their force arrived, then, with some coordination, the Monarch\u2019s forces could counterattack, crushing our enemies between us. A truly resounding victory such as that would buy us more breathing room than just driving them off here and there.<br /> <br /> If I am going to follow in the Bastard\u2019s footsteps, we must have communication with the Monarchs outside the siege lines. Joan agreed to take over that duty from Louie so he could focus on fighting, since she needed to not fight unless my plan was put into place. I wonder if there\u2019s any pressure we could put on the Hedge gate to split their forces... We don\u2019t really have sluice gates. Anyways, maybe I should stop drawing comparisons to a town that was lost less than a year after its salvation...<br /> <br /> On happier thoughts, Calamity actually apologized. Not for killing Mr Grey, cause she still believes it was the best choice, and I understand that. She didn\u2019t want to argue that point, since it\u2019s moot, really, and I agree with that. She did apologize for not including us, for not behaving like we are the team that we must be, that we are, and I appreciate that. It was hard to respond appropriately, in the middle of preparing for war, but I smiled as wide as I could at the time and banished my elemental armor long enough to hold her close for a moment.<br /> <br /> Now we just have to get through tonight safely, and everything will be ok.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> So here I sit, on the edge of what will almost certainly be a battlefield within the next hour. I\u2019m scared shitless, but ready to stand and fight at the side of my fellow changelings when the moment arrives.<br /> <br /> As you can probably tell, a lot of big, important things happened today\u2026 and I was present for exactly none of them (so far). I was still pretty steamed at Calamity when I got back from Tamara\u2019s place, and I didn\u2019t feel like hanging around the house all day, so I decided to make use of the Dream House\u2019s performer contact list and make the rounds of LA\u2019s talent agencies.<br /> <br /> I met with a lot of people today, and got a few nibbles, but didn\u2019t sign anything. Some of those agencies could probably help my career take off, but I want to make sure I go through all of the contracts before I decide on one (and maybe have someone a little more familiar with modern contract law than I am go over them too). <br /> <br /> I made it back to the House with plenty of time to get ready for the show, and started getting dressed and putting on my make-up. Calamity came back to speak with me as I was getting ready for my first number \u2013 this would have been right after the show started \u2013 and warned me that bad things were afoot. <br /> <br /> Hailey was in the audience, and she was acting and speaking strangely. She had asked Monica to stay home tonight, and seemed worried about Andromeda and Joan. It didn\u2019t take my friends long to deduce that she was receiving some sort of mental commands from the Mothership. The strange alien Gentry has stepped up its plans in the wake of our discoveries, and it\u2019s attacking the Freehold tonight.<br /> <br /> Hailey was afraid of what she might do; the signal was getting stronger as the Mothership neared. Calamity and the others considered knocking her out, but decided in the end that the intelligence she could provide on the Gentry\u2019s plans was too valuable, so they settled for tying her up in the basement (with Hailey\u2019s permission, of course). Jacob called Monica, who came running to make sure Hailey was alright. <br /> <br /> Calamity called Joan and Andromeda, who have been vacationing in San Francisco. Okay, well, I say \u201cvacationing,\u201d but in actuality the two of them fled there after we discovered the location of the Table\u2026 apparently Calamity warned Joan that Master Darke might be looking for a new operator in the wake of Mr. Grey\u2019s \u201caccident.\u201d In any case, \u2018Frisco is apparently far enough away that Andromeda was not affected by the Mothership\u2019s signal. Joan started back for the Freehold as soon as she heard what was happening, but Andromeda is staying away for now.<br /> <br /> So it was a little difficult to concentrate on being sexy and alluring as I belted out \u201cHey Big Spender,\u201d but the show must go on, right? So while the monarchs met and argued over Darke\u2019s fate and the Mothership moved in on the Freehold from all directions, I worked my way through two sets, performing here and there and keeping the girls pepped up despite the fact that they could obviously tell something strange was going down.<br /> <br /> About two-thirds of the way through the night\u2019s planned acts, Calamity came up and whispered something in Ace\u2019s ear. After the current number was done, he took the stage and announced that there was a problem with the local water main, and that city ordinances dictated that we had to close the club for the evening. There was some grumbling, but Ace promised the patrons that if they saved their ticket stubs, they would get a discount the next time they stopped by the Dream House, and a few minutes later the House was empty of everyone except changelings.<br /> <br /> We got periodic updates from Hailey and from various contacts within the Freehold. The Mothership seemed to be targeting specific changelings\u2026 most notably Joan, but they also sent people after Oleander and Captain Jack. Jack was providing impartial security for the meeting of the monarchs, so he was relatively safe, while Oleander luckily enough picked tonight to stop by the Dream House\u2026 possibly in the hopes of hooking up with yours truly, though that might have just been Flores teasing her. A part of me hopes not; Oleander is nice, and I\u2019d love to dally with her at some point.<br /> <br /> Joan decided to head straight for the Dream House rather than stopping by her own place first, since Hailey told us that about twenty of the Mothership\u2019s soldiers were converging on her house. We later heard that most of these soldiers had been taken out by a well-timed explosive blast. This blast unfortunately took out Joan\u2019s house as well, but if anyone understands the necessity of sacrifice in wartime, it\u2019s Joan. Since the Mothership seems to have such a hard-on for her, we\u2019re going to allow her to be seen at the Dream House, which will hopefully draw most of the alien forces here\u2026 just in time for us to spring our trap.<br /> <br /> You see, with all the unrest in the Freehold, the monarchs thought it would be best to keep most of the Winter Courtiers under lock and key for the time being, which vastly reduces the number of people available to defend the area. It\u2019s a sensible precaution. It\u2019s also a lie. The Winter Courtiers are free and clear, and ready to fight off the invasion at a moment\u2019s notice. So the forces of the Mothership will find us more than prepared to take them out when they arrive.<br /> <br /> One saving grace is that the Mothership doesn\u2019t seem to like to use lethal force. Like many Gentry, its agents prefer to capture their prey rather than kill them, so they use these little ray-guns that sap their targets\u2019 energy rather than causing actual wounds. It occurred to me that we have an ace in the hole in that regard\u2026 Flores and I both know the Contracts of Eternal Spring, one clause of which allows us to restore energy to those who are flagging. As it\u2019s fairly well-known that the catch in that clause is that the target has given the invoker food of some sort within the past day, each of us was soon approached by a long line of changelings bearing peanuts, cocktail weenies, and other common club fare.<br /> <br /> Neither of us actually ate much of it. The contract doesn\u2019t require that the food be <u>eaten</u>, and I found that I didn\u2019t have much of an appetite by that point.<br /> <br /> I admit it: I\u2019m scared. I mean, I\u2019m <u><u>really</u></u> scared. The forces of the Gentry are coming here, with the express intent of claiming changelings and taking us back to Arcadia. I can\u2019t think of anything worse. It\u2019s not even for myself that I\u2019m worried (mostly, at least). Everyone I care about is here, too. When I think about what the Mothership might do if they captured D\u2026<br /> <br /> Maybe what scares me most is that Calamity came up to me as people were preparing for the fight and actually apologized for the situation with Mr. Grey. I mean, she didn\u2019t apologize for <u><u>killing</u></u> him, but she apologized for not consulting me and the rest of the motley about it first. I know she wouldn\u2019t have done that unless she was at least a little worried that she wouldn\u2019t get another chance to do so.<br /> <br /> I reiterated to her that I\u2019m still mad about the whole situation, but that I still like her and consider her a close friend. I just can\u2019t forgive her quite yet. I don\u2019t know why; maybe it\u2019s the fact that she really doesn\u2019t seem to comprehend the magnitude of what she\u2019s done. Mr. Grey is <u><u>dead</u></u>, for no reason other than that he might have been an inconvenience to us in the future. If that ever starts to seem like a viable way of doing things, then nobody is safe.<br /> <br /> So she was standing there trying to apologize and make nice on the eve of battle, with her knives at her belt and her shards of glass sharpened and poking through her clothes and her dark red hair almost exactly the same shade as Annabelle\u2019s, and I just couldn\u2019t bring myself to force the anger down. I accepted her apology somewhat coldly and told her that I had to prepare for the fight to come. She looked a little hurt, but she covered it quickly and left me to it.<br /> <br /> Now all I want is for this to be over. I want to lie down with D and Julia and Marguerite and maybe a few other people and forget about the troubles our actions have caused the Freehold, and forget about the trouble that might be coming due to Master Darke\u2019s impeachment. I want to lose myself in beauty and sensation for a while, and not think about everything that\u2019s gone wrong in my life, and what I\u2019ve become. Sometimes forgetting is the only way to cope.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> <u><b><b><u>Tuesday June 17<sup>th</sup></u></b></b></u><br /> <br /> They're coming for us but we're ready for them. I don't have a lot of time but just in case this all goes pear-shaped I'm updating. I'm geared up for war and damn but do I look good. No matter how much Lori may and the others may have worked to help me improve my ability to girl the denim and leather hugging my skin just feels more natural, more me. Sam and Max are a comforting weight on my hips. Gawain made me another pair of throwing knives, they're beautifully functional and perfect. I'm wearing them on my right thigh with the pair he made me previously on my left. I'm looking over at the mirror and I recognize the tough as nails bitch looking back at me. That's Calamity and those sorry little bastards are going to get a first hand lesson in what it means to fuck with my people and my shit tonight.<br /> <br /> Might as well get my moment of glory in while I can. The word from the court via Tommy is that Darke is playing the someone murdered a winter courtier and he won't step down without the other monarchs promising to carry out justice. Fucking justice... I can't believe the bastard believes in that particular fairy tail any more than I do. But I told Tommy that I was prepared to stand tall for killing Grey and I do. I'm not going to fucking run from it. I had my reasons and I won't apologize for killing that sad sack. I know it's made this more difficult but it was the right call at the time. Even if it wasn't, it's done and I can't take it back. The blood only flows one way. And whatever they decide I'm prepared. I am a gorram murderer and I deserve it anyway.<br /> <br /> I can't help but think about that other girl from Snow Globe, the one Spidertoes told me about. I wish I knew her name. I wish I could somehow speak to her. She sounds familiar. She sounds like me. She choose to die rather than follow the courts. But she was alone and I'm not. I told Gawain at the time that the fact that he was waiting for me was what pulled me back from the brink that night in Belleview. I have my motley. I am not alone. Not anymore. I should have trusted them. I should have listened to them. I should have trusted Charlotte and the courts to remove Darke and keep him from acting against us. But I am so much better at killing than trusting. And tonight that is what they need from me. Tonight I will be the Calamity that befalls the Mothership's minions.<br /> <br /> Trust. I keep telling Jacob that he needs to trust us. That he's not alone. He is a killer like me. He's done things. Today when we sparred he told me that he'd considered killing Grey. But he didn't. He thought it through and saw that it would make things harder. He wanted to try to find a better solution. He's good at killing and he's not afraid to do what needs to be done. However, unlike me he doesn't like it. He didn't let his bloodlust cloud his reason.<br /> <br /> I swore I would control the monster and wouldn't let it control me. I have kept my anger in check. I have been good. I felt proud of that. But I underestimated it. I didn't think it would whisper softly rather than roar. I let it seduce me. I let my desire taint my judgment.<br /> <br /> This shit has been weighing my mind down. Not even the sparing drove it out. Between that and the hangover I was not on my game earlier and Jacob gave me a nice little cut for it. But the workout was still good and the talking was important. In addition to what he told about how he felt about what I did, he opened up a little. He talked about a little fawn girl that liked popsicles. I've seen how much he enjoys using his powers to frost a glass or the like for someone but when he spoke of that changeling girl he really smiled. But it wasn't a truly happy smile. It was bittersweet and when I asked he admitted that it didn't end well. There was a fight and the girl was hurt. He spoke of a spring courtier who'd struggled to heal the child and failed. Of watching the moment unfold powerless to do anything. I took his hand and offered what comfort I could. He didn't elaborate too much on things.<br /> <br /> We talked about the Table and Darke as well. We both agreed that we could see where Darke was coming from. Maybe that's why it bothers us both so? That we can see how a person like Darke (or us) can lose sight of the lines that shouldn't be crossed. I told him I felt that even those loyalists deserved better than to be changed against their will like that. He agreed that they should have been given a chance to change willingly. He hesitated a moment after he said that and I thought about what he'd said about the girl and the Spring Courtier. I don't know anything for certain but I have some suspicions about why Jacob doesn't speak of his time in Arcadia. Even if I'm right, that was there. Gawain was a murderer in Arcadia. Insincere Marguerite was a thief, stealing Changelings for her Keeper. I may have fought my own Keeper tooth and nail but the things I did to the other Changelings in Snow Globe was horrid. If we were held accountable for what we did while in Arcadia there would be very few Lost indeed. The past is done. We can't change it. We can only move forward.<br /> <br /> Maybe I did let my need color my decision to kill Grey. Did I keep my intentions from the others to protect them or because I knew they'd stop me? Fuck if I know for sure but I cannot allow myself to ignore the possibility. I swore I'd protect them and that includes from myself. If I can't trust myself, how can they? I like the woman I see in the mirror right now. I like being her. But she's fucking dangerous and I cannot abide a threat to my motley. I cannot allow her to be a threat to them. I won't allow her to be a threat to them.<br /> <br /> But for tonight things are simple. I have a problem with a face to punch. I will get my fill of blood and fear and pain. It will be glorious. Yeah, part of me couldn't help but consider that dying in battle would solve the issues with Darke and make life simpler. But the Mothership's army carries stun weapons and that would be the easy way out. I am not a fucking coward. I'll take my punishment head on. I never shied away from the Whispering Voices and I'll be damned if I'm going to cower now. I will stand before the Courts with head high and I'll take whatever the fuck they care to dish out.<br /> <br /> That's not going to be easy for the others. I will have to make them promise not too interfere when they come for me. I know Gawain won't like it but Queen Charlotte has gone to bat for me and I'm not going to repay that by disgracing her with a display of cowardice. I'd rather die on my own fucking feet with my head up than live on my knees.<br /> <br /> But that's not for tonight. Tonight we have a battle. Tonight I kill and bleed for the ones I love.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> So, Calamity and I got our chance to spar and to talk today. After I got back from checking on Tamara we got changed and went out back. Calamity wore her usual workout clothes, a tank top and sweats. I just wore sweats. June in California I\u2019ve discovered is hot. Too hot if you ask me. I figured that Calamity has seen all my scars before, there was no point in trying to hide them. Hell, I think the whole motley has seen them by now. After the incident with Mary\u2019s fetch and the fire, and the truth or dare game there\u2019s not much on my upper body that they haven\u2019t seen before.<br /> <br /> As for the fighting, we were both hungover so we were not at our best, but it showed just a bit more with Calamity. Not to say that she wasn\u2019t damn good, she was just a little slower than usual. I had the advantage early on before she evened things out. But it wasn\u2019t long before I started besting her and we called it after she made a mistake that would have gotten her killed, or at the very least, maimed. As it was I gave her a small scratch as a reminder to work on blocking her left side better in the future.<br /> <br /> As we were cooling down and tending to the scratches here and there we talked. It\u2019s become something of a habit, or maybe tradition. After sparring we talk about things that are bothering us, or in my case I avoid talking about those things that are bothering me. I admit that I can be cagey when it comes to conversation. This time though I wanted to let her know that I did not blame her for Mr. Grey, nor was I angry with her. I admitted that I\u2019d had similar thoughts in my head, so I can\u2019t fault her for her logic. I told her that I\u2019d kept the permanent option in the back of my mind and was going to look for alternatives before resorting to that plan. I don\u2019t know if everything came out as clearly as it was in my head, but I think she understood what I meant.<br /> <br /> Talk of Grey led us to other equally sensitive topics, but I really wanted Calamity to understand that I know where she\u2019s coming from. I am not a good person. Who I am now is as good a person as I\u2019ve been in a long time, and I told her that. I don\u2019t know if she fully grasped what that means, considering my current moral flexibility, but I think she does. I told her that I can understand where she\u2019s coming from, because I\u2019m in that same place. I can understand the need for practicality over moral certainty. I needed her to know that she\u2019s not alone. I think a part of me needed to know that I wasn\u2019t alone either. <br /> <br /> Calamity admitted that she\u2019s not used to being able to rely on others to listen or help, so when she had a plan of action she followed through with it. I told her that I understand that as well. I was alone for a good while in the Lady\u2019s realm. I learned the hard way that I could only rely on myself. So, later, when I worked with others it was a learning curve for me. I had to relearn how to trust someone else when I\u2019d been dependent only on myself for so long. <br /> <br /> When I was paired up with Rook I didn\u2019t trust him at first. After my training was done we\u2019d go on missions and I\u2019d make things harder on myself by not waiting for Rook, or deviating from the plan because I could not trust him to back me up. After some time, and a smack or two to the head, he convinced me that he was not going to let me down. After that we were a perfect match. Sometimes I miss that. I miss his dark sense of humor. That might be part of the reason I feel a connection with Calamity? Her sense of humor is dry and dark and I can\u2019t help but think of Rook when she gets that wry smile on her face. And I only mean that as a compliment. Rook was like a brother to me.<br /> <br /> Today really was a day for revelations, I guess. I admitted to Calamity that when I first got back I found a freehold that took me in for awhile. I didn\u2019t go into details, just that they had taken me in and that there was someone there that helped me open my eyes. She gave me a chance, a second chance to do things over. I told Calamity things I didn\u2019t intend to. I told her about the woman and the little girl that helped me. I told her in vague terms about the attack on the freehold by a loyalist. That Felicity had gotten caught up in the fighting and was very badly wounded. Diane tried so hard, and it took so much out of her, but it just wasn\u2019t enough. I don\u2019t think there was a way to save Felicity that day. I\u2019m pretty sure Diane blamed herself though. She loved that little girl. I admit that I was quite taken with her as well. She was so sweet and innocent. I had not remembered that such a thing could exist, and there she was. She was utterly delighted when I made her that first popsicle. I just wanted to see her smile like that again, so when she came back the next day I offered to freeze her juice again. She smiled and pulled a spoon out of her pocket. So I used my dwindling stores of glamor to make her another popsicle. I couldn\u2019t deny her that. I was sorry to not have enough glamor later when I fought with Rook, but I never regretted using it to make that little girl smile.<br /> <br /> I haven\u2019t talked to anyone about that day. I still didn\u2019t use names with Calamity, but I told her about Diane and Felicity. I don\u2019t know why, other than it just seemed right. The words started to come out and I kept going with it. I was a bit sad remembering Felicity, but it felt good to tell someone about her and Diane. I\u2019m glad I did.<br /> <br /> Conversation also went to Darke and the Table. I admitted that I could see where Master Darke was coming from with some of what he did, and thought that he worked in the best interests of the Freehold, but did not agree with how far he\u2019d gone with the Table. I agreed with Calamity that what he did was too close to what the Gentry do to be comfortable with. Calamity said that Vik and Molly should not have been changed without their consent. I agreed and said that they should have been given a chance. I froze for a moment after I said that. It pretty much mirrored what I had said about myself. I\u2019m not sure if Calamity picked up on that or not, but as soon as the words left my mouth I got just a bit nervous. I realize that I have to tell the others about my past at some point, but with everything going on right now I really didn\u2019t want them to doubt what side I\u2019m on.<br /> <br /> We ended the sparing on the usual, \u201cIf you need to talk to someone, you can come to me\u201d bit. I made the offer to Calamity first this time and she reciprocated. I told her that I would take her up on that but I\u2019m still working out some stuff. Which is not entirely a lie. I am working it out in my head. Trying to figure out when\u2019s a good time to tell my motley that I used to be the one to capture people and bring them back to Arcadia. Yeah, and after Insincere Marguerite brought up her question about whether or not it was bad, that would go over well. So, I\u2019m waiting for now. Taking the coward\u2019s way out, as Rook would say, but I haven\u2019t had friends like this in a long time and I don\u2019t want to fuck it up.<br /> <br /> After I went inside and showered I spotted Luna and Marguerite talking in the sitting room. I walked in, trying not to interrupt, but I did anyway. Insincere Marguerite apologized and was about to leave when I stopped her. I told her that I wanted to say I was sorry for the other day. The day she brought up the question about whether being taken was bad, I only said yes, that it was. I didn\u2019t elaborate and I know that she was looking for validation that she wasn\u2019t a bad person for having those thoughts. So, I made sure to explain myself this time. I told her that while I do not think that being taken in and of itself was a good thing, I did think that good things can happen as a result of it. I agreed that she is a better person now than she was before she was taken. I admitted that I\u2019m not better than I was before, but that\u2019s me. She changed for the better and I like who she is now, and I told her as much. I wanted her to know that I did not think that her thoughts made her a loyalist or anything close. She said that she did not feel any loyalty towards any of the Gentry. I knew this, but it was good to hear it out loud.<br /> <br /> After Insincere Marguerite left I talked to Luna for a bit. She said that she\u2019d had a perfectly pleasant conversation with Marguerite, but that at some point the other woman\u2019s shadow became very agitated and imposing. Luna wondered if this meant that Marguerite was upset with her, and admitted that she\u2019d been preparing for a fight if it came to that. Thankfully it never did. The shadow thing started after Insincere Marguerite asked Luna if she wanted me all to herself. Luna answered yes, that she preferred that. After that the conversation continued to be friendly, but the shadows got weird. I assured Luna that Insincere Marguerite\u2019s shadow sometimes has a mind of its own and does things like that. I did not think that Marguerite was actually upset with her, disappointed perhaps, but not too upset. <br /> <br /> After all of that I decided to look online and in the paper for a used car. I have been thinking that if I want to be able to look for Brandon Mills then having my own car would be a good thing. So, I enlisted Luna\u2019s help in my car search. During said search Willow Black stopped by to talk to me. She wanted to apologize for the behavior of the Handmaidens the other night with Tamara. She was in charge of watching them while the Warlock of Night was looking for a sunken ship, or something along those lines. The pair got away from her and paid Tamara a visit. So, Willow has been apologizing on their behalf today. Apparently she\u2019s been to see Tamara, me and Lowjack. I didn\u2019t see any reason to not accept her apology. She is not wholly responsible for the behavior of the Handmaidens.<br /> <br /> Luna and I continued to look for used cars after that and just spent time together. It was nice. We each pointed out vehicles that might be good, which I took down the info for, and some that were just wrong or silly. It made a nice change to do something so mundane. And it probably wouldn\u2019t have been as much fun if I\u2019d been alone. So, I was happy to have Luna there to help.<br /> <br /> Throughout the early part of the day Gawain would come out at irregular times to give me and Calamity knives that he had been forging. He made a pair of nicely balanced fighting knives for me and a pair of throwing knives for Calamity. He may have also been working on something for himself. I\u2019m not sure. Later, I thanked him for the fine blades and expressed my compliments on the workmanship. He had dropped mine off while I was sparring so I couldn\u2019t look at them as he delivered them. I believe Calamity\u2019s came later.<br /> <br /> All in all it has been a fairly good morning. Sparring went well, and we talked out a few things, which I\u2019ll agree with Calamity is a good thing. The exercise was also good for the pair of us. I know I felt a lot better afterwards. I got to look for a car, and spend time with my girl. I also got to talk to Insincere Marguerite about what had been bothering her. She was doubting herself, and I just wanted to make sure that I told her that there was nothing wrong with her thoughts or reasoning. Not everyone has a durance that is all that bad. Some of us do, but it\u2019s not fair to expect everyone\u2019s feelings about being taken to be the same. Marguerite came out the better for it, and I\u2019m happy for her. I just don\u2019t want her to doubt that she\u2019s a good person.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> This is going to be quick, but I wanted to get something down on paper before the shit hit the fan. Things started to get tense at the beginning of the show. At least three people came in armed. Three Changelings I should clarify. TJ brought a mace and carried it openly. Most people probably just thought it was a prop. Louis Guo also came armed. He was carrying a sub machine gun. He talked to Gawain first thing and let him know what he had on him, and offered to leave it at the bar with me until it was needed. If it was needed. It\u2019s going to be needed. So, I had my own weapons on me. Let\u2019s face it, when am I not armed? I had the normal shotgun behind the bar and Louis\u2019s SMG. Tonight would be a bad time for the police to come by. Just saying. There is a third person that has a weapon. I think Gawain went to talk to them. I don\u2019t know who it is, but apparently it\u2019s not a threat to us nor is it related to the trouble that people thought might pop up tonight. I can ask later.<br /> <br /> Yeah, so we thought that there might be trouble tonight since today is the day that all the monarchs are meeting and Darke is stepping down. Or that\u2019s the plan anyway. Tonight is also the night where our defenses could be at their weakest, so everyone is planning for trouble. Gawain being the gentleman that he is started going around to the single ladies, those that were at the Dream House alone, and was offering to escort them home if they wanted. I think Calamity might have talked to one of them. White Maria I think? Anyway, Gawain extended his offer to Haley who he discovered right off wasn\u2019t acting right. In fact she was behaving downright odd. Her actions were strange as was her voice. Gawain brought her over to the bar so she\u2019d be away from most of the customers and she could sit down. She kept saying that she felt strange. She also kept saying that she was concerned for Monica\u2019s safety so she had asked the other woman to stay away from the club tonight. She was also curious whether or not Andromeda was feeling strange.<br /> <br /> Gawain called Calamity over and filled her in on what was going on. She promptly called Joan, who was out of town keeping Andromeda safe. Apparently Andromeda was feeling just fine, and Calamity suggested that they keep the young alien girl far away from Santa Monica. I\u2019m not sure where they are, but apparently it is far enough away that whatever is affecting Haley is out of range for Andromeda.<br /> <br /> Haley\u2019s behavior just got stranger. She started rocking every once and awhile and holding her hands over her ears. She then told us that she was getting a message from the Mothership. It was coming from the Hedge. They wanted Joan and were going to send about twenty people to her house to retrieve her. They did not want to kill her, just capture. Haley said that she had not been given instructions yet, but if she was, she did not want to follow them. <br /> <br /> Earlier, when Haley first started exhibiting odd behavior, I called Monica to see if she could come and maybe comfort Haley. She arrived in short order and Calamity escorted her and Haley to a spare room. The idea was to keep her out of the way in case she started doing anything and Calamity would be there to stop her if needs be. I saw Calamity leave and come back with handcuffs. I assumed that Haley was being restrained for her own good.<br /> <br /> Calamity told the rest of us what was going on and what she\u2019d learned from Haley. The Mothership is launching an invasion and their people were currently moving into position. Andromeda also called and gave us a quick rundown on what she knew about the Motherships tactics. Apparently they are big into stunning their targets and dragging them back to the Mothership. They aim to incapacitate rather than kill. This is good and bad for different reasons. Good that they\u2019re not aiming to kill. Things could get really messy really fast if that was the case. The fact that they likely plan on taking prisoners is more than a little scary. No one is real keen on going back to Arcadia, especially to a place that is known to mess with the minds of those they take. Sometimes I wish that I could forget my past, or at least forget my sins, but then I wouldn\u2019t be me. I don\u2019t know who I would be and that kind of scares me. That and I don\u2019t really want to go back to what I had been before. Sometimes I miss Rook. Sometimes I miss the quiet beauty that can be found in the Lady\u2019s realm, but not enough to want to go back to Her or to any one of the Gentry for that matter. <br /> <br /> Tamara called and let me know that there was going to be word going out that all of the Winter courtiers save myself, Tamara and Lowjack were going to be taken into custody pending the outcome of the big meeting. This is a ruse. They will use this opportunity to place some of the more combat oriented courtiers to shore up where the Summer court has gaps. I told the rest of the motley what was up. Calamity did not look surprised, so I can only assume that she got word from someone else. I gave details to those that were alone, and left it vague for those that were near those not in the motley. For all, I mentioned that trouble may start in about fifteen minutes.<br /> <br /> In order to keep the mortals safe we invented a lie about the plumbing not working properly, and due to strict laws we were required to have all patrons exit the building until it could be repaired. We offered everyone there to give them a 25% discount on their next visit. After the mortals left I returned Louie\u2019s weapon to him.<br /> <br /> We got further news that there were a number of enemies descending on Joan\u2019s house, some going after Captain Jack and some even going after Oleander\u2019s place. The initial attack on Joan\u2019s house showed just how keen they were on getting the Summer courtier. Even the explosive trap that was laid for them didn\u2019t do much to deter them. <br /> Dr. Bright called not long ago to let us know that about ten people were heading towards the Dream House though the hedge and would likely come out through the gate in the front. I passed the message along to the rest of those people present. Gawain then suggested the idea that we let it be known that Joan is at the Dream house. This will lure the bulk of the Mothership\u2019s people to us and we can take them out all at once. We would need to coordinate with the Monarchs to get reinforcements to catch the enemies from behind. <br /> <br /> Dr. Bright called again. Five minutes or less until the attack. Louie gave his Bluetooth to Joan so she could be the contact with the Monarchs. He had been our line of communication, but we needed him as a combatant and for Joan to stay out of sight for the time being.<br /> <br /> The others prepared for the attack. Everyone got weapons and those able, put up armor, elemental or otherwise. Calamity even apologized for her actions with Grey. She said she was sorry that she hadn\u2019t inform us before she acted and that she would make sure to do so in the future. It was like she wanted to say it in case she didn\u2019t get a chance to later.<br /> <br /> Part of me is scared of those that are coming for us, precisely because they don\u2019t aim to kill. Then there is another part of me that is looking forward to the fight. I am good at fighting. I want to fight, and right now I want to kill. They think that they can systematically take down our freehold? This is my second chance and they\u2019re not going to take it away from me. So, we are going to fight. Goddess keep my motley safe.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> Today has escalated quickly.<br /> <br /> The initial poor form of the Handmaidens was followed up on by Willow Black having to be an apologist for them. Which, given the dictates of our Court, must have been galling. Still, she apologized to Jacob and apparently has to Lowjack and Tamara.<br /> <br /> I had a nice chat with Luna while Jacob and Calamity sparred. We established that, regrettably if understandably, she wants Jacob solely for herself. I wonder if she has discussed this with him? Questionably.<br /> <br /> Jacob wanted to discuss with I my question about our abduction by the Gentry. He still believed that being taken was bad, but expressed he could follow the logic that the results were ultimately good. He did not feel it was for him, but agreed it at least seemed to be good for me. Mostly, though, he wanted to apologize for not articulating himself despite having given it a good deal of consideration. His, and Calamity\u2019s, comments are heartening. It means perhaps at least they were giving things more thought than I was giving them credit for. Fortunately.<br /> <br /> This evening began somewhat guarded but, as I say, escalated quickly. Hailey arrived, speaking in a decidedly unusual voice, making unnatural head motions, and covering her ears. Apparently she is picking up broadcasts from the Mothership, and she was preparing for a strike. While Hailey had difficulty understanding at first, she was with it enough to realize Joan was a major target (and Oleander and Captain Jack lesser but still specific targets) for abduction. By a stroke of luck, none of the three were home; Joan had been tipped off by Calamity and was elsewhere, Captain Jack was at the meeting of the Monarchs and Oleander was here. Fortunately.<br /> <br /> The Monarchs are deciding how to deal with the passing of the crown from Master Darke to John Lowjack.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Oleander, the reason for this first visit to the Dream House was\u2026complex. Flores had talked her into coming, allegedly to get her hooked up with Lorelei, whom Oleander is sweet on. However, Flores took me aside and spoke of more things. For one, she had been pining for I. For another, she wanted to make love to De La Rocha and Lorelei, and was hoping this might help. De La Rocha specifically she felt like she \u201cowed\u201d and hoped to bring some pleasure to. She asked if she should offer to let De La Rocha drain her some as part of it, but I advised against; De La Rocha is sensitive about Leechfinger stuff. I doubt she would be thrilled about the \u201cowed\u201d thing either.<br /> <br /> The most disturbing part was, of course, Oleander was partially a present for I. Flores believed once we had been together Oleander would see I as she did. I felt a chill. Flores is kind and selfless, and dedicated to her friends. This was no betrayal to her; she was doing Oleander a favor. I had to step away. Quickly.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile Gawain and Calamity had moved Hailey downstairs. Monica had arrived and was worried. Two other Summer Courtiers, Louis and TJ had arrived armed, and apparently White Maria had a weapon for no related reason. Such a pretty Treasured, White Maria\u2026<br /> <br /> Madame Spidertoes was among the others as well, which gave us serious mystic options. Andromeda called and laid out what she knew of their weapons, while Calamity coordinated with Tommy. Then she lead Julia down to the basement and came back alone. I confronted her. Swiftly.<br /> <br /> It was innocent, she wanted Julia to keep an eye on Hailey so the more warrior types like she, Gawain, and Monica could be there to stop the Mothership\u2019s forces. I am not distrustful of Calamity, but I still had to check, but I did acquiesce.<br /> <br /> Julia, for her part, is facing this with all the bravery only someone who can turn invisible and knows her love can turn invisible can.<br /> <br /> I went back and talked to Flores and Oleander. Poor Flores has no idea what a drubbing she gives Oleander\u2019s self esteem. Oleander is clearly intelligent, if a bit awkward, and covers for it with snark a bit too much. Flores is not dumb but\u2026she is naive. Not too naive to run a club, however. Certainly.<br /> <br /> Eventually Jacob that the enemies were coming, and we began to prepare. Gawain and Lorelei were obvious in their powering up.<br /> <br /> As for I, I too am ready. Ready to get this over with.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXIX</i><br /> <br /> Lazy morning followed up by a tense evening. Lots of planning and preparation from the PCs. The superhumanly intelligent Gentry was squaring off against the equally intelligent Lowjack, so a certain amount of strategizing was going on outside the PCs.<br /> <br /> Part of my goal was building tension this time. The PCs had people they needed to keep safe, but really could only go by what was being reported by Louis Guo and reports from Tommy, Tamara, and Dr. Bright.<br /> <br /> This is not really a Heel-Face turn for Master Darke\u2019s minions; Darke has always been an evil person who held defense of the Freehold highest, hence his targeting by the Mothership who is something of a planner. His plans did not evaporate and Lowjack was able to hide behind a more visible monarch to work behind the scenes, hence her lack of preparation for Lowjack. Others targeted included the freehold-famous heroes like Joan or Captain Jack and Oleander who wandered the local hedge enough to be known by the hobs.<br /> <br /> Of course, like many Gentry the Mothership does not fully understand how the Freehold works. This has worked to their advantage, especially given she does not quite understand Darke\u2019s role.<br /> <br /> Of course, in the Monarch meeting room, it has been declared that the death of Mr. Gray must be answered for, and in the Winter Court headquarters, a deadly loyalist has gotten free, leaving a trail of dead grays behind him. But for now, they work toward making it through the night.<br /> <br /> Join us next time, when the tension breaks and things come fully to a head. The Mothership landed, ironically, on Mother\u2019s Day. Comments and Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T19:23:07-07:00","id":511418,"title":"","content":"There will be blood *smiles*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T00:46:25-07:00","id":512705,"title":"","content":"I don't want toi say too much before the journals get finished and posted but there was an acceptable amount of blood in Calamity's opinion..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T16:43:40-07:00","id":513462,"title":"","content":"...and too much for Lori's taste. Though that shouldn't surprise anyone who's been paying attention. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T02:22:07-07:00","id":526473,"title":"","content":"The Mothership has landed, and the battle over Santa Monica is over. The causalities are not obvious at a glance, but if you look around, they are there.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> Early morning June 19th<br /> <br /> The fight is won and now I\u2019m standing vigil again. I never really figured that I\u2019d, you know, avoid the nightmare problem by just not sleeping but with Lori\u2019s pick-me-up power, the physical exhaustion is less of an issue. And tonight at least, I feel more mentally and emotionally refreshed than in a while. I have served my purpose and stood sentinel for my motley and our friends.<br /> <br /> Our initial plan was simple. Calamity, Jacob, Louis and I were the front line. Calamity, Jacob and Louis were concealed, Calamity and Jacob surrounding the Hedge Gate and Louis on the high ground afforded by the walkway to the guest house. Lori and Insincere Marguerite were on a balcony, safely behind us but, you know, still where she could see us all clearly. And fall back to help the others in the worse case scenario. I stood in the courtyard facing the Gate, to draw their fire and hopefully the bulk of their attention<br /> <br /> That worked for the first three, whose volley was really draining. But Lori got me, you know, fixed up, right off. Calamity fired her shotgun into the group of three, killing one and leaving the others in a sad state. Jacob finished those two off. Calamity had revealed herself though, so the next volley took her down.<br /> <br /> I... well, I don\u2019t remember the rest of the fight clearly. I killed one of the aliens and both of their cow-skeleton-alien-robot creatures. There was a lot of gunfire and in the end, eight dead aliens. We moved quickly, tossing the bodies into the Hedge, you know, for now. We\u2019ll give them a proper burial later. The rain Flores summoned up washed most of the blood away. We still didn\u2019t really wanna get caught up by the police, especially after Joan updated us. Flores dealt with them well, while we were gone, apparently - she answered the door wearing mostly nothing and acted confused<br /> <br /> So, Joan\u2019s news was that the pincer maneuver on the House wasn\u2019t going to be possible/needed, as the Mothership had turned its attention on the Table. In a move both fortunate and unfortunate, the aliens had let out a loyalist on their way, and the loyalist killed 12 of them before disappearing. So the aliens didn\u2019t have the Table but a loyalist, one that had eyes on Jacob, got out.<br /> <br /> The eyes on thing was only apparent when we got to the Rehab Center that was the Winter Court Headquarters. It was super obvious there - a knife embedded itself into the van just in front of Jacob\u2019s face as he stepped out. Jacob promises that if this Rook wanted him dead, he wouldn\u2019t have missed, so apparently he likes playing games. He\u2019s also slippery, slippery enough that Calamity\u2019s power to find people gave really weird results. So Jacob is staying with Luna tonight and Calamity and I are guarding the two access points to the ladies while they... well, sleep at this point. I guess that\u2019s what the lack of moaning and yelling in Spanish means, you know?<br /> <br /> Anyway, we figure he\u2019ll wanna go back and report to his Keeper, since he\u2019s been held up here, but for now the Hedge is on fire. So was the Rehab Center, kinda. At least the bushes and stuff. There was also, you know, laser marks, like the Mothership shot through the Hedge Gate there. It was mostly cleanup when we got there though. Twitch had made the table like three times the size it usually is, so the aliens couldn\u2019t move it through a door into the Hedge. He was also so hopped up on adrenaline I thought he might explode.<br /> <br /> He had these weird guns that shot needles into people. The needles were full of formaldehyde, tonight. He and Gunnar and Captain Jack were in charge of cleaning the place out and were almost done - all the aliens were either dead or run off, and there was just a herd of the cow-skeleton-alien -robot things, including one that looked like it was made up of four or five of the others, you know? Me and Captain Jack took care of that one, while the others dealt with the rest. Lori even finished one off.<br /> <br /> She didn\u2019t deal with that too well though, and Calamity\u2019s score-keeping of kills didn\u2019t help. She had still been giving Calamity the cold shoulder, but they talked some, when we got back home. Lori had some kind of breakdown while they were talking, so De la Roche took her off to bed. I hope she\u2019s doing ok - De la Roche\u2019s taking good care of her at least.<br /> <br /> Early afternoon June 19th<br /> <br /> Asking me to stand down if someone comes to arrest her is a tall fucking order. But it is her choice, and I will stand aside for it. She better get a damn good lawyer cause I will bring their house down around their heads if they try to hurt a hair on hers.<br /> <br /> Jacob survived the night. Lori will tell us what was eating her when she\u2019s ready. Moon is escorting Oleander to make sure her house is safe.<br /> <br /> Fuck.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> I don\u2019t\u2026<br /> <br /> I can\u2019t\u2026<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know\u2026<br /> <br /> Okay, first thing\u2019s first. Our plans to defend the Freehold against the Mothership went well. No one was killed, and very few people were even hurt. We set ourselves up in defensive positions outside the Dream House and watched the gate intently. I was up on the front balcony, mostly shielded from sight but still very much a part of the battle. Marguerite was up there with me, invisible but present, ready to come to my defense should it prove necessary.<br /> <br /> Close combat fighters like Calamity and Jacob hid in the underbrush near the gate, while ranged combatants took up positions which allowed them a clear line of sight. Gawain didn\u2019t bother to conceal himself; he just stood back from the gate and readied that gigantic sword of his. His job was to draw the attackers out of the gate. He did his job well, and it wasn\u2019t long before they walked right into our trap.<br /> <br /> Two of the little grey alien things managed to hit Gawain with their ray guns early on, and he looked like he was really flagging. I managed to pep him up with my Eternal Spring contracts, and then quickly ducked behind the balcony\u2019s railing again. Calamity fired off that little shotgun of hers and did a lot of damage, and as soon as three of the creatures cleared the gate, Louis Guo opened up with his automatic weapon and took out a few more.<br /> <br /> Things might have ended there, but one of the alien attackers threw a couple of little silver balls on the ground. I thought they might have been grenades, and was about to shriek out an alarm when these\u2026 <u><u>things</u></u> erupted out of the spheres. They looked like armored alien cow skeletons\u2026 but the armor was biological, like the chitinous exoskeleton of an insect or crustacean. With these things serving as a distraction for Gawain, a few of the aliens managed to get some good hits in at Calamity, and she went down.<br /> <br /> I got her up again a few seconds later, of course. Just as Andromeda had told us, the aliens\u2019 weapons weren\u2019t lethal. Jacob leaped out of hiding and helped Gawain mop up the remaining aliens and the cow-things, and the night was ours. I heard my friends talking about how a few of the aliens had retreated from within the gateway rather than pressing the attack, but I think our forces probably defeated seventy or eighty percent of the attackers. I know Jacob was hit by at least one or two of those laser blasts, but they didn\u2019t seem to affect him. Well, after the fight he sort of sagged a bit, but at the time he seemed fine.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s weird to think that we were essentially fighting other changelings like ourselves. I mean, they were \u2013 if you\u2019ll forgive the expression \u2013 so <u><u>alien</u></u>. But it\u2019s sad to think that we were essentially killing hapless mortals who were spirited off into Arcadia at some point. The only difference between them and us is that we were lucky enough to find our way out again. Nobody seemed to want to talk about it much, but I think we were all profoundly affected by the experience, each in our own way.<br /> <br /> The others started tossing the bodies into the Hedge to hide them from any local authorities who might show up to investigate all the gunfire. Gawain insisted that we would give the aliens a proper burial later, so I went along with it for the sake of expedience. Flores had called up a light Spring rain to wash away the blood, so there was no evidence of violence on the premises.<br /> <br /> Joan called at that point to update us on the situation in the rest of the Freehold. The forces of the Mothership had been beaten back pretty handily in most of Malibu and Santa Monica, but there was still some fighting at the rehab clinic which serves as the headquarters of the Winter Court. That worried us, because that\u2019s where the Table is currently stored. There were scattered reports that the aliens had \u201copened a door they should have left shut,\u201d and something had escaped which had killed a baker\u2019s dozen of them.<br /> <br /> We checked on the others in the Dream House, and found that they were mostly okay. I say \u201cmostly\u201d because it looks like poor Hailey finally succumbed to the Mothership\u2019s signal and tried to escape the basement. Julia did everything she could to keep Hailey restrained, but in the end she had to attack her to keep her docile. She made sure her attack did not cause a lethal wound, and Flores healed the damage as soon as the danger had passed.<br /> <br /> We hopped into Gawain\u2019s van (which he had torn apart and reassembled over the course of the afternoon) and drove across town to see if we could help. The grounds of the clinic were on fire, but the building itself looked mostly intact. As we stepped out of the van, a knife flew out of nowhere and lodged in the door about three inches in front of Jacob\u2019s face. He got this look of surprise and fear on his face like I\u2019ve never seen. He and Gawain tried to locate the source of the thrown blade, but whoever it was had fled quickly after making that single attack.<br /> <br /> If it <u>was</u> an attack. Jacob seems to think that he knows what the Mothership set loose tonight. He says it was a Loyalist, and that it was trying to send him a message. But we didn\u2019t have time to follow up on those developments since the Table was still in danger. I didn\u2019t learn more about the mysterious prisoner until the next day.<br /> <br /> When we got into the clinic itself, we found Captain Jack, Gunnar Friday, and Twitch contemplating plans of attack. Twitch had done something to the Table which increased its size, making it impossible for the aliens to transport it until whatever contract or ability he\u2019d used wore off. The aliens themselves had withdrawn, leaving some of the cow-things to keep an eye on the Table for them while they considered their options.<br /> <br /> We moved in to secure the artifact. Once again, Louis and Calamity peppered the room with shotgun and automatic gunfire, wounding many of the beasts inside. The rest of us backed them up as best we could, mopping up what was left. Captain Jack and Gawain tag-teamed a giant monstrosity that seemed to be composed of about five of the cow-things stitched together, which was a relief\u2026 I really didn\u2019t want to have to fight that thing. Twitch used a pair of guns which fired syringes full of formaldehyde from bandoliers wound about his torso.<br /> <br /> I moved around the corner with my little pistol drawn, planning to cover my friends and back them up with healing magic when necessary. One of the wounded cow-beasts lurched toward Calamity, and I\u2026 I just reacted. For the first time since I got it, I fired my gun at another living creature. And as tiny as that gun is, it did its job well\u2026 the monster\u2019s head imploded, and it crumpled to the floor. It didn\u2019t even twitch.<br /> <br /> I kept staring at the body for a few seconds; I couldn\u2019t help it. I kept my gun pointed at it, even though it was clearly dead. I think my eyes might have started to water, but I wasn\u2019t crying out of fear or regret; I just wasn\u2019t blinking. Calamity gently put a hand on my forearm and forced me to lower the weapon.<br /> <br /> \u201cNice shot,\u201d she said softly. I nodded, but didn\u2019t say anything.<br /> <br /> The Table was almost comically large, and there was no way that anyone was going to be able to get it out of the room until the magic wore off. Calling various contacts in other parts of the Freehold told us that the forces of the Mothership were in full retreat. The Mothership itself had appeared in the Hedge, but had withdrawn when its forces were clearly bested. Still, it had done a lot of damage, and large portions of the local Hedge were burning.<br /> <br /> As we drove back to the Dream House, things got tense between me and Calamity again. \u201cFour. Not a bad score,\u201d she said with a grin when we were about halfway home.<br /> <br /> I should have let it pass, but I just couldn\u2019t. The enormity of what I had done was still to fresh and raw in my mind. \u201cWe\u2019re keeping score now?\u201d I asked in acid tones.<br /> <br /> Calamity looked sheepish and turned away. \u201cI\u2026 I didn\u2019t mean\u2026\u201d she began.<br /> <br /> \u201cForget it,\u201d I said, and went back to staring out of the window. I think that it started to build up inside me at that point. Something was growing in my heart and trying to claw its way out. I didn\u2019t feel sick, exactly\u2026 it was more like I was trying to hold in a sneeze, or a hiccup, or an orgasm. Some outbursts won\u2019t be denied.<br /> <br /> We got back to the Dream House, and everyone seemed to be doing all right. D asked if I was okay, and I sort of bitterly informed her (where Calamity could hear me) that I\u2019d only \u201cracked up a score of one.\u201d D looked concerned at that, but let it pass.<br /> <br /> Flores embarrassed Oleander again by suggesting she proposition me, and Oleander prepared to leave, but we suggested that she might want to stay the night with us until we could be sure that her house was safe (she was one of the Mothership\u2019s intended targets, after all). She seemed really flustered when we made the offer, so I pulled her quietly aside and took both of her hands in mine.<br /> <br /> \u201cFlores means well,\u201d I said gently, \u201cbut she doesn\u2019t really understand subtlety. I\u2019ve had a long day, so I\u2019m going to follow her example and be blunt. I\u2019d like to sleep with you, Oleander, but tonight is not ideal with everything that\u2019s going on. Do you think I could get a rain check?\u201d<br /> <br /> Oleander smiled slightly. \u201cI\u2019d like that,\u201d she said after a moment.<br /> <br /> Calamity showed Oleander to the guest room. I really wanted to talk things out with her, so I waited for her to get back before preparing for bed. I asked if we could talk privately, and she agreed, and the two of us walked into an adjacent office to hash things out.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cLook, Lori,\u201d she said quickly as I shut the door, \u201cI\u2019m sorry about what I said about keeping score. It was insensitive, and I wasn\u2019t thinking about what you were going through\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI get it,\u201d I said. \u201cAnd for what it\u2019s worth, I think we did the right thing tonight. I <u>hate</u> that we had to do it, but we were fighting to protect everything we care about. I just\u2026 I don\u2019t think it should ever be our go-to option. I think killing should always be a measure of last resort.\u201d<br /> <br /> Calamity\u2019s mouth tightened a little. \u201cI know,\u201d she said, \u201cand in a perfect world it would be. But sometimes we have to make hard choices. I meant what I said earlier, about Mr. Grey. I\u2019m sorry I didn\u2019t consult the rest of you before I acted. That was wrong. And I\u2019m going to pay for that rash decision, too\u2026 there are going to be political consequences\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> There was a rushing in my ears, and a red haze settled over my vision. \u201cI don\u2019t give a damn about the consequences, Calamity,\u201d I said sharply. She looked surprised to hear me say that. \u201cIt\u2019s not about the consequences. It\u2019s about what\u2019s right.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know it\u2019s not a<u> <u>nice</u></u> option\u2026\u201d she began.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo!\u201d I said loudly. The rushing became a roaring. The haze got thicker and darker. There was a coppery taste in my mouth, and I felt little jolts running up my arms and legs. \u201cYou don\u2019t get it. You just don\u2019t<u> <u>see</u></u> it. It\u2019s not about being nice or good or moral. It\u2019s about the finality of it. It\u2019s something you can never take back. It shouldn\u2019t be decided on a whim.\u201d<br /> <br /> I advanced on her, and I think she actually took a step back, which is kind of funny considering that she could probably kill me with one hand if she decided to try. \u201cYou can\u2019t just get <u><u>mad</u></u> at someone and decide they need to <u><u>die</u>!\u201d </u> I said, my voice rising. \u201cIf that\u2019s how we deal with our problems then no one is safe! You could just get mad at someone and lose control and the next thing you know your hands are around her throat and then she\u2019s lying there on the floor and she\u2019s not breathing and there\u2019s blood in her hair and\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know how long I was away. The memories came flooding back then, bursting in my chest and spreading like poison through my body.<br /> <br /> Annabelle. Annabelle Rigdon. Beautiful, sweet, sad Annabelle. She came to us what felt like a few months after Jane, Missy and I entered the Empress\u2019 service, though it must have been years in the outside world. She appeared to be about our age. She was slim and had a fair complexion, with ash blonde hair that almost looked silver. Her wings were pure white; they seemed to shine in the dim light of our cage. She told us she was from Seattle, and did her best to be friendly to us, even though we could all hear her crying every night.<br /> <br /> She was never a part of our little group; Missy and Jane and I were too close to let anyone else in. But sometimes, when the two of them were too wrapped up in each other to pay much attention to me, Annabelle and I would sit and talk about our homes and our dreams and our hopes for the future. I remember one of the few times I saw her smile: she said she thought she was becoming a clich\u00e9, because she was from Seattle and she worked part time as a barista and she liked grunge music. I didn\u2019t get it at the time.<br /> <br /> When she heard about the Empress\u2019 contest, she started bouncing ideas off of me. She sang a song I later learned was called \u201cHurt,\u201d by nine inch nails. It was one of the saddest things I had ever heard. Something inside me snapped, and I saw her differently.<br /> <br /> She was beautiful. She was pure. She had the voice of an angel. And she knew songs that could wring tears out of a stone. She was going to win. She was going to <u><u>win</u>. </u><br /> <br /> I waited until she was asleep, and then I softly woke Missy and Jane. I told them about how that <u><u>bitch</u> </u>was trying to take away our chances of winning our freedom. We all turned to look at her; six dark eyes reflecting the madness and jealousy in our souls. And then we fell on her as she slept.<br /> <br /> By the time we were through there was very little left of her. Her slender face had been beaten until it was puffy and bruised; her fair white skin looked ruddy and rough. Her pale hair and white wings were stained a dark crimson with her own blood. Oh God, her <u>blood</u>\u2026 it was <u>everywhere</u>.<br /> <br /> I wailed as I came back to myself. I couldn\u2019t help it. I\u2019ve known for some time that the Empress was trying to turn me into an animal. I had forgotten that she\u2019d succeeded.<br /> <br /> I threw my arms around Calamity. She spun away from me, and for a second I thought she had seen my guilt on my face and was rejecting me\u2026 but then I realized that she was trying to keep me from cutting myself on her shards. Her own arms wrapped around my shoulders and she held me as I sobbed.<br /> <br /> D and the others rushed in a few seconds later. D ran up to me, and I fell into her arms as Calamity released her grip. My love was glaring at her fellow darkling like she intended to do some serious violence. \u201cYou okay, babe?\u201d she asked me softly.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo,\u201d I said miserably, \u201cno I\u2019m not. But Calamity didn\u2019t do anything wrong, D. I just\u2026 I just remembered something. Something I should never have forgotten.\u201d<br /> <br /> D nodded sympathetically. \u201cIt happens to all of us sometimes,\u201d she said softly.<br /> <br /> I lowered my head and took her hand. \u201cI think I\u2019d like to go upstairs now, if you don\u2019t mind,\u201d I said.<br /> <br /> She nodded again. \u201cOf course, Lori. Whatever you want.\u201d<br /> <br /> Marguerite gave me a brief hug before we left. \u201cI love you, Lori,\u201d she said quietly.<br /> <br /> It was the first time she\u2019s said it in front of\u2026 well, everyone. \u201cI love you too, Marguerite,\u201d I replied through my misery. \u201cYou <u>know</u> I do.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe will be right down the hall if you need us,\u201d she said.<br /> <br /> I couldn\u2019t let that pass. \u201cI <u><u>do</u></u> need you,\u201d I said. \u201cMaybe not right this second, but\u2026 I <u>do</u> need you, Marguerite. And you too, Julia. Always.\u201d Marguerite looked pleased to hear that.<br /> <br /> D led me upstairs and sat me on the bed. \u201cSomething you want to tell me, Lori?\u201d she asked gently.<br /> <br /> I shook my head no.<br /> <br /> She sighed, then leaned in and kissed me. \u201cSomething you<u> <u>need</u></u> to tell me, love?\u201d she asked this time. \u201cIf you really want to keep it to yourself, I won\u2019t push it\u2026 but it\u2019s usually better to get these things out of the way. You\u2019ll feel better later.\u201d<br /> <br /> I sighed, nodded, and started talking. I told her pretty much everything I could remember about Annabelle, and what we did to her. I\u2019m not sure how coherent the story was, since I was sobbing through a lot of it, but I think D got the general idea: I\u2019m a murderer. And what\u2019s worse, I\u2019m someone who will kill for petty, selfish, conceited reasons.<br /> <br /> And Calamity says <u><u>she\u2019s</u></u> a monster\u2026<br /> <br /> D held me until I had worked through the worst of the crying. Then she kissed me until I stopped vocalizing my self-loathing. \u201cCut that shit out right now,\u201d she said sternly when I started on another downward spiral. \u201cArcadia did horrible things to us all\u2026 remember what I told you about <u>my</u> durance. Doesn\u2019t make you a monster. Doesn\u2019t even make you a bad person. You freak out about killing Hedge beasts, for Christ\u2019s sake, Lori! You want to feel bad about what you did to this Annabelle chick? Fine, feel bad about it. Regret it all you want. But don\u2019t let it take you over. Don\u2019t let it undo all the progress you\u2019ve made in getting away from your Keeper.\u201d<br /> <br /> She leaned in and looked seriously into my eyes. \u201cDon\u2019t let it take away the girl I love, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> I could tell she wasn\u2019t really worried about losing me. She was just trying to make me feel better about my life, and the direction it\u2019s taken. It worked. \u201cI\u2019m not going anywhere, Maria,\u201d I said softly with a sniffle, \u201cyou\u2019re stuck with me for good.\u201d<br /> <br /> We kissed and cuddled for a while after that, and it was good, but there was still that nagging, buzzing, wheedling voice in the back of my head that wouldn\u2019t let me forget what I had let myself become. I hated myself for it a little bit, but I knew that there was only one way to shut that voice up.<br /> <br /> \u201cMake love to me?\u201d I asked D softly.<br /> <br /> She quirked an eyebrow. \u201cYou sure?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cI need you,\u201d I said hungrily. I put a lot of lust into those three words. I didn\u2019t use any glamour or contracts \u2013 I would <u><u>never</u></u> do that to D \u2013 but I did everything else I could to let her see how much I wanted her. I saw the fire kindle in her eyes, and she started to kiss my neck and slide the straps of my dress from my shoulders.<br /> <br /> We started off slowly, sensually\u2026 but things escalated quickly. As our passion mounted, things got almost rough\u2026 I\u2019m sure Calamity would have called the sex tame, but it was very raw and unrestrained for me and D. As things moved toward their crescendo, I took her face in my hands and forced her to look into my eyes.<br /> <br /> \u201cTell me I\u2019m pretty,\u201d I said. It wasn\u2019t a request.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re the most beautiful woman I\u2019ve ever met,\u201d D panted.<br /> <br /> \u201cTell me you love me,\u201d I demanded next.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou know I love you more than life,\u201d D agreed, her eyes rolling back in her head.<br /> <br /> We were almost there. I just needed one more thing. \u201cTell me I\u2019m the <u>best</u>,\u201d I hissed, my hands tightening around the back of her neck as I pulled her closer, losing myself in the purple streaks in her black hair.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re the best, Lori! You\u2019re<u> <u>everything</u>!\u201d </u> she wailed, and we both peaked.<br /> <br /> A few moments later I was kissing her all over her face and neck, little kitten-kisses to thank her for everything she had done. \u201cI\u2019m sorry,\u201d I said over and over again. \u201cI\u2019m sorry, Maria. I needed it. I needed to hear it. I needed you to say it. I\u2019m sorry.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s okay, Juliette,\u201d she said, using my old name to address me for the first time. \u201cIt was\u2026 good. And I meant every word.\u201d<br /> <br /> And my God, even after the terrible events and revelations of that day\u2026 in Maria\u2019s arms I was able to sleep.<br /> <br /> We woke up the following morning to find that Calamity and Gawain had stood watch over us all night\u2026 Calamity on the balcony and Gawain in the hall outside. Flores had stayed with Marguerite and Julia, and Oleander slept in one of the guest rooms. Jacob decided to stay at Luna\u2019s place.<br /> <br /> Jacob knows about the Loyalist the Mothership\u2019s forces set free last night. He says it\u2019s a servant of his Keeper; a man named Rook. He thinks this Rook is incredibly dangerous, and I can believe it after what he did to the aliens yesterday. Jacob says that Rook would probably report back to his Keeper as soon as possible\u2026 but with the local Hedge burning he\u2019d probably be stuck in the Freehold for the night. Hence the extra security and Jacob\u2019s absence from the Dream House last night.<br /> <br /> Everyone was really nice to me at breakfast this morning. They were obviously curious about my little breakdown yesterday, but with Jacob facing such a serious problem it didn\u2019t seem the time to burden anyone with my own baggage. \u201cI\u2019ll tell you all about it soon,\u201d I said hesitantly when asked, \u201cbut I need a little time to come to grips with it first.\u201d<br /> <br /> I did make a point of apologizing to Calamity. I\u2019d been walking around feeling so superior for the past few days, when all this time I\u2019ve been guilty of the exact same crimes. \u201cI still don\u2019t agree with what you did to Mr. Grey,\u201d I told her, \u201cbut I\u2019m sorry I\u2019ve been such a bitch about it ever since. I wasn\u2019t really mad at you, I was mad at myself.\u201d<br /> <br /> Calamity accepted my apology with good grace. \u201cWhen you\u2019re ready to talk about it, I\u2019m here,\u201d she said. Then, she sort of lowered her eyes and said something I never would have expected to hear from her. \u201cI\u2026 I love you, Lori.\u201d She\u2019s usually so guarded with her emotions; it must have taken a lot for her to say that.<br /> <br /> I smiled at her. \u201cI love you too,\u201d I said softly. Then I looked at the rest of those assembled\u2026 D and Marguerite and Julia and Ace and Gawain and Jacob, and \u2013 what the hell \u2013 even Flores and Luna and Oleander. \u201cI love you all,\u201d I said with a bit more conviction.<br /> <br /> Before things could get too mushy, Calamity told us that she had something important to share as well. She had informed Queen Charlotte that she was the one who killed Mr. Grey. This is all well and good, but it has become politically inconvenient, as Darke is now demanding that Mr. Grey\u2019s killer be brought to justice as one of the conditions of his \u201cretirement.\u201d So that could be a problem.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhen and if they come to take me into custody, I want you all to stand down and let it happen,\u201d Calamity said earnestly.<br /> <br /> \u201cLike hell,\u201d Gawain said with passion.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe\u2019re not going to let anything happen to you,\u201d I agreed quietly.<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t want you guys fighting the Freehold over me,\u201d she explained. \u201cI did this. I\u2019m willing to accept the consequences.\u201d<br /> <br /> Gawain grumbled for a bit, but in the end he had to accept Calamity\u2019s wishes. So did the rest of us, but none of us are willing to take this lying down. We\u2019re not going to fight the forces of the Freehold, but we\u2019re not just going to let Calamity fall victim to Darke\u2019s last act of spite, either. We\u2019ll find some way to get her out of this. Some non-violent way, within the mandates of Freehold law.<br /> <br /> So now I have a homicidal Loyalist targeting one of my friends and a second friend about to take on a political shit-storm over an act of which she is admittedly guilty. It would seem like that would be enough to keep me nice and distracted, wouldn\u2019t it? Sadly, even though I might not be the brightest bulb in the pack, my brain is more than big enough to stress and obsess over three things at once.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m sorry, Annabelle. From what I remember, you were a genuinely good person. You didn\u2019t deserve what we\u2026 what <u>I</u> did to you. And I will never forgive the one who taught me that I had that much hate inside me. The Empress showed me that I have the capacity to murder someone. If I ever get the chance, I will prove to her that I learned that lesson well.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 05-24-2015, 05:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T02:25:17-07:00","id":526477,"title":"","content":"<b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> <u><b><b><u>Wednesday June 18<sup>th</sup></u></b></b> </u><br /> <br /> We threw back the Mothership last night. The Winter Court's rehab clinic took heavy damage and Joan's house got blown up. The hedge was left burning. I haven't heard of any losses on our side and I'm not sure if Jack's place or Oleander\u2019s were damaged in the fighting. So I can't say for sure if it was a total win for the Freehold but it was fucking glorious.<br /> <br /> After I'd girded my loins and all, I caught up with the motley as everyone was starting to prepare for the inbound hostiles. I told them that I still thought killing Grey was the right decision but that it wasn't my decision to make. I think it was well received by most. Gawain dropped his metal armor so he could hug me. Lori was still cool but she told me again that despite being upset with me she did still care. That look in her eyes did hurt a bit but what the fuck ever, I swore to protect her and I will do whatever the fuck it takes to, even if she hates me for it afterward. And while I didn't find out till later, part of it was due to the fact that she's dealing with some demons of her own right now.<br /> <br /> Louis took tactical lead on the defense and the lot of us put together a solid ambush. Gawain took a stand out in the open in front of the Dream House, sword at the ready. Lori and Insincere Marguerite were on the balcony above the main doors, ready to use contracts to support us and to withdraw to warn and rally the reinforcements if the front line went down. Jacob and myself both took up concealed positions in the landscaping near the Hedge Gate. Louis was on the walkway above it. At his suggestion, we had Flores call down a good steady rain before the fight to wash away the blood evidence since there was a good chance the police would get called in once the gunfire started.<br /> <br /> Louis agreed to let me have the opening shot. Spidertoes had given us both a blessing with her contracts and so we settled in to wait. The grays popped out and promptly started to fire upon Gawain, who took a couple of jolts but Lori was able to banish the effects. Once a nice clump of them had emerged I let loose with both barrels of Max. Even with the contract of Stone the kick was delightfully brutal, my shoulder is still a little sore from it. The one that caught the brunt of the blast never knew what hit him as his chest pretty much evaporated under the double aught buckshot. The other two took it hard and squealed as they staggered back. One of them spun right into Jacob's reach and he gave it a quick scissor cut with his knives that added a perfect arterial spray to the last lazy turns it made before going down in a heap.<br /> <br /> The scrawny little bastards kept pouring out. The next pair targeted me and laid into me with those thrice damned shock guns. Andromeda may have been right about the gray's stun guns being harmless. But they do pack a fucking wallop and that was a whole new flavor of pain. Worse yet, there was no toughing it out. I was only on the ground jerking and spasming for a few seconds before Lori's Spring magic revived me but it was awful. Aware but helpless is not a state Calamity likes. Just thinking about it makes my skin crawl.<br /> <br /> Louis opened up on them at that point, cutting the ones that had zapped me down while Jacob finished off the other one I'd wounded with Max. Then one of the damn buggers tossed down a pair of fucking alien pokeballs. I expected some sort of grenade but instead of exploding they opened up and a pair of hobgoblins rolled out and just kinda unfolded and unfurled. They were like HR Geiger\u2019s version of cows, all bone gaunt and spiked out.<br /> <br /> Gawain charged in at that point with his sword low and braced like a spear. He impaled one of the nightmare cows and ran it through before lifting his weapon to pick the damned thing up and over like a bale of hay. It landed in pieces. Holy shit but at that point I was a little weak in the knees and not from the aftereffects of the rayguns. I think Insincere Marguerite cursed the other one, because it started to bellow and flail wildly.<br /> <br /> Since we were all in close, Louis started to lay down cover fire at the gate, keeping the remaining grays from joining the fight and preventing the last of them from escaping. The remaining hellcow blundered into Gawain, lunging at him clumsily. He countered and spun to cut the thing down before following through with a fatal strike on the little fucker that had tossed them down. Jacob had cleaned up the other grays while Gawain was charging the bulls.<br /> <br /> With the Dream House's ground clear, we looked and spotted the remaining grays fleeing on the other side of the gate. Jacob and I both fired. I dropped mine with a clean round to the back of his oversized gray head that exploded it like a ripe melon. Jacob caught his in the back but it managed to keep stumble-staggering away. I took a step forward to cross over and finish it off but a chorus of protests started up and I stopped myself. Much as I hated to let that one escape, there was no telling what they had waiting to cover their retreat and the world does not need a little gray Calamity. No way I could pull that look off half as well as Andromeda.<br /> <br /> With nothing left to kill, we set to tossing the dead through the gate before it closed and policing the grounds so the cops wouldn't find anything incriminating. Joan let us know that the grays had hit the rehab clinic to try to recover the table and had, as Dr Bright put it, opened the wrong cage. Also Hailey had succumbed to orders from the Mothership and used her wizened contracts to get loose from her restraints and the basement room. Julia had stabbed her in self defense, but had tried to do so as non lethally as possible. Flores was confident she could heal the girl so we left her to it and piled into Gawain's van to reinforce the Winter Court's clinic.<br /> <br /> We caught our breath on the ride and reloaded. Gawain multitasked, driving and managing to deliver a pretty solid St Crispin's Day speech. We rolled up and found a damned warzone. The grounds were on fire and there were some long deep ruts carved across the landscape from the Mothership's lasers. We could hear gunfire from inside and so we hit the ground running.<br /> <br /> Only as soon as Jacob exited the van he had a knife plant itself beside his head. He plucked it free and frowned. There was no sign of where it had come from and while he was as stoic as ever I could tell he was shaken. I whispered to him to remind him that we had his back and whatever it was he wasn't facing it alone. He gave me a tight nod and we all rushed inside.<br /> <br /> Captain Jack, Gunnar, and Twitch were the first response team apparently. We found them surrounded by a pile of dead grays. Gunnar was, well, Gunnar. But seeing Captain Jack without his usual act was odd. He seemed a bit less than happy with Twitch and the Winter Court in general. Of course it didn't help that Twitch was jacked up on adrenaline and living up to his name. He had medical scrubs on with a fucking bandoleer of hypodermic needles and a pair of guns that shot them. He smelled of blood and formaldehyde and was going on about how he'd made them himself. He was also talking about using them to dose his allies with adrenaline. I was tempted to ask him more about that but everyone else seemed rather displeased with the whole idea.<br /> <br /> Apparently Twitch had used his contracts to make the Table too big to fit through a doorway and thus prevented the grays from recovering it. He seemed well and rightly pleased with himself over this. The chamber with the table was held by the Mothership's forces so Insincere Marguerite and Jacob and myself all decided to creep closer for some recon. There were no grays, only more of those fucking monster cow things, including one massive one that seemed to have been Voltroned together from several of the regular ones. <br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite slipped back to report to the others while I crept closer and ran my fingers along Max eagerly. Jacob stayed close and ready. The others showed up soon and Louis told me he was going to open up on the hellcows and that I should wait to open up on them when they charged our position. I whispered my agreement to him and we set that plan into motion.<br /> <br /> He caught several in his initial spraying. They rallied and charged the door we were using and I caught the first wave of them with Max. Then Jack and Gawain charged in to attack the massive cow amalgam. Jack broke a desk over it's head (must be an ogre thing...) and then Gawain sliced that monster in fucking twain. Damn my man is a sight to see when he doesn't hold back.<br /> <br /> The rest of us were dealing with the regular sized cow things. Max was empty after that initial double barrel volley so I fell back on my razorhands rather than drawing Sam since it was in close and personal. Well, that and I wanted to run my fingers through at least one of the abominations. I cut one as it closed in to skewer me with a spur of bone. The spike skittered off my glass and leathers harmlessly and I thrust in to rake it's underbelly and send it staggering back before it collapsed. I'd locked my eyes on another, this one wavering from being caught in the edge of the buckshot and getting a cut from Jacob but still up and attacking.<br /> <br /> Before it could close with me, a shot rang out, pitched differently from the other guns in use and the thing went down nice and clean as you please. I looked back and saw Lori standing there with her Black Widow drawn and ready. She was in stance and holding it steady just like I taught her as a little wisp of gunsmoke rose from the barrel. It was a beautiful sight and I felt a surge of pride.<br /> <br /> Only after that first glimpse, I realized that her wings were quivering and she was holding her entire body much too tense and rigid. Her eyes grew wider as she just stared at the sight of her target laying lifeless and limp and continued to keep her weapon trained on it. I moved over and gently lowered her arm and complimented her on the shot. That seemed to get through the shock and she blinked and relaxed a little.<br /> <br /> Twitch told us the Table wouldn't be back to normal before morning and reports were coming in that the Mothership was withdrawing, though it was leaving the Hedge in flames behind it. Everyone seemed to feel that our work was done and that it was time to get back to the Dream House. I didn't argue. I did exchange a few words with Twitch before we left.<br /> <br /> Gawain and Jacob took a minute to examine the area where the knife had been thrown from but they found nothing. Insincere Marguerite had Lori in the van and was trying to soothe her. Once they were sure there wasn't any trace of the attacker, we loaded up the van and rolled out. I smiled and let the whole night wash over me again as I rode back. They came and we kicked their worthless asses back to Arcadia. Surely such a decisive victory would make the Mothership or any of the other Gentry think twice about fucking with us. And hell, it felt good to be able to cut loose like that without having to feel guilty about it. I guess I was too wrapped up in my own bliss to notice how upset Lori still was until I muttered something to myself about my personal score for the night.<br /> <br /> That set Lori off. She snapped at me about keeping score with some serious venom in her voice. I was caught off-guard and it kinda kicked me back into the present. I fumbled and tried to apologize for upsetting her but she wanted none of it. She just turned away from me and went to looking out the window. Insincere Marguerite continued trying to calm her down and I just sat and watched them. I really wanted to say something but it was pretty fucking clear that there wasn't shit she wanted to hear from me at that point. I gave up and curled up quietly with my thoughts while we drove in silence.<br /> <br /> The police had showed up while we were gone but Flores had cleverly used her cluelessly shameless manner to answer the door mostly naked and claim she'd been too distracted to notice anything and told them to look around if they wanted but not to interrupt her again unless it was important. Since they hadn't and weren't still there when we rolled in I am guessing they let it slide. I imagine with all the hot spots in the attack they've got their hands full trying to make heads or tails of it all.<br /> <br /> Flores rather promptly embarrassed Oleander talking about her staying the night with Lori and the rest of them. She was not comfortable and Flores was confused by it. Lori and Insincere Marguerite soothed things over. I caught her before she left and suggested that she might want to stay since her house was one of the ones targeted. I pointed out that we have guest rooms and she agreed at that point. While I was talking to her, I couldn't help but overhear Lori telling De la Rocha that she'd only racked up a score of one and when I looked over De la Rocha gave me a dark look. I rolled my eyes and turned back to Oleander and left the room to show her to the guest room. Once we were there and I'd made sure she was settled for the night, she put a hand carefully on my arm and told me rather earnestly that she appreciated me fighting to keep her and the freehold safe. Then she leaned in rather gingerly and kissed my cheek. I'll be honest, it surprised the shit out of me and I just told her it was my pleasure. Because it was.<br /> <br /> That thought was bouncing around as I walked back. I wasn't fighting to protect the Freehold. I wasn't even fighting to protect my motley. I was fighting because I could. Because it was an excuse to indulge my need for blood and pain and violence. And that noisy and unwelcome thought was buzzing around when I got back and Lori told me she needed to talk to me.<br /> <br /> I wasn't exactly pleased with the idea but I stepped aside with her into one of the side rooms. As she closed the door behind us I braced myself. I haven't been her favorite person of late and she was clearly irate with my behavior after the fighting. And I had let myself get carried away and caught up in the rush of it all. She's not a monster like me, she was upset at what she'd done. I tried to apologize again for being insensitive. She waved that off and told me that while she hated it she did agree that it had been necessary. But the way she said it, speaking of killing as a last resort and all made me grit my teeth. I really, really, really did not want to have another fucking argument about killing that sad sack Grey. And yeah, my own doubts about my actions flared and in reaction I dug my heels in harder. I reiterated my position. I informed her that I knew there were going to be consequences and that I was ready to face them.<br /> <br /> That just made her even more angry. I can't say that I have ever seen Lori so furious. She advanced on me, raising her voice as she shouted down my attempt to admit that I knew it wasn't a good option. I shifted unconsciously to brace myself as she stepped closer and got in my face. I forced my arms to stay down at my sides and clinched my hands until my nails dug into my palms just in case she actually struck me. But what followed was even more unexpected.<br /> <br /> Her rant started to wander. It was clearly not about what I had done recently but about something from her own past. And then she wailed and threw herself at me. Thankfully I was quick enough to shift and keep her from getting cut on any of my shards. As she sobbed I just wrapped my arms around her and stroked her hair softly. I murmured quietly to her as the others came rushing in.<br /> <br /> I think it was truly good that I managed to keep her from cutting herself when I saw the look in De la Rocha's eyes as she burst into the room. I quickly released Lori to let her gather her up instead and she pulled her girl close. Lori told her she was not alright but that it wasn't my fault. I did not miss the way her lover said she knew or the hard look she still had toward me. She'd come through that door fully prepared to fight me if she needed to. Honestly, I can't say I blame her.<br /> <br /> I trailed quietly as they guided Lori out and everyone gathered to show their concern. Insincere Marguerite even went so far as to admit in front of all of us that she loved Lori. Everyone was worried about her and wanted to help her. I just watched it unfolding quietly. I had no place there. I don't soothe or heal or fix things.<br /> <br /> It wasn't too long before De la Rocha took Lori upstairs and Insincere Marguerite went up with Julia and Flores. I looked to Jacob and asked him directly if we were in danger. He nodded and told us we were. He then told us more about Rook, who he is sure is the loyalist that the grays set free. He's deeply concerned, even afraid of this man. And I know Jacob isn't given to exaggeration so when he says this Rook is deadly I believe him. The idea of fighting another razorhand and one so skilled excited me more than it should have and I couldn't hide my reaction. Jacob and Luna both disapproved.<br /> <br /> As we talked about what we should do and what Rook was likely going to do I pointed out that I could try to locate him with my contract of Oath and Punishment. Jacob told me that Rook was vary good at being undetected when he wanted to but it seemed worth trying at least. The power flowed through me quite readily but it wasn't enough. For a moment I was struck with a powerful sense that there was no such person. I frowned at Jacob before I managed to think it through and realize that the power doesn't work that way. Clearly he's shielded from scrying by a powerful magic.<br /> <br /> With no clear idea of where he might be or what his intentions at the moment would be, Luna suggested taking Jacob to her cabin since it was unknown where the Dream House is common knowledge. We all agreed it made sense and they departed.<br /> <br /> And that left just handsome and myself. I knew before I turned to look at him that we weren't going to falling into bed together like everyone else had. He reached for me and lifted me up to give me a deep and longing kiss before he pulled me back. We just looked into each other a long moment and he just asked me if I wanted the balcony or the hallway inside.<br /> <br /> So I ended up on the deck outside Lori's room waiting. I resisted the temptation to ease-drop on her but she and her lady were not exactly quiet. At the time I contented myself with the idea that I might get to tangle with this exceptional Rook but the only enemy that arrived was the Sun. I spent the latter part of my watch sitting near the house in the shade scowling until Lori woke up and stretched all naked and glorious in the late morning sunlight. I bid her a good morning as I headed inside and she returned it without much more than a touch of surprise to find me out there. Of course, if I was that fucking perfectly beautiful I wouldn't mind being seen either.<br /> <br /> Jacob and Luna were back for breakfast, and reported that things were as quiet there as here. Then he filled the rest of them in about Rook. Lori seemed a little subdued but better than I'd feared after seeing how upset she was the night before. She told us that she'd remembered some things and assured us that she'd explain once she'd had a chance to sort it out. Then she made a point of apologizing to me for the way she'd been treating me. I told her it was alright and that I understood. Then I made sure she knew that I was there whenever she was ready to talk about it. I also told her I love her, maybe not the way De la Rocha and Insincere Marguerite do but I do care about her. I care about them all.<br /> <br /> I rose after a few moments and got their attention. I explained that one of Darke's conditions for stepping down peacefully was the oath of the other monarchs to seek justice for Grey's murderer. I then told them that I had already told Queen Charlotte that I was the one who'd killed him and that I intended to surrender myself to the agents of the Courts when, not if, they came for me. They started to murmur and I shook my head and cut them off. Gawain in particular was not pleased. I could see that he was ready to fight, to face down the entire Freehold for me. The fact that he agrees that I am guilty of murder, that he was so upset that I'd killed Grey doesn't matter. The others weren't as militant but they were all ready to do something. I told them I knew it was hard but that I needed them to stand down. I need to do this. They did all agree, though Gawain was clearly loathe to. The rest of the meal was somber.<br /> <br /> And I do need to do this. As I look back over my actions with Grey and last night I can see that I have been deceiving myself with claims of being able to control myself. I murdered Grey because I wanted to kill. Because it was easy. I killed the Mothership's grays gleefully. More than once I nearly let my bloodlust get the better of my judgment last night. I really am becoming more of a liability to the motley than an asset. How long will it be before I do something reckless and get them hurt? Or worse yet, how long before I lose control and end up hurting one of them myself? And seeing them this morning, ready to protect and defend me from the consequences of my own actions. I'm out of control and I'm getting worse. I'm broken and I have no idea how to fix it. Hell, I don't know there is a way to fix what's wrong with me. Maybe it's because I'm carrying a piece of fucking Snow Globe inside me, poisoning my heart and my soul.<br /> <br /> I don't want to die, but I'm not afraid of it. Not as afraid as I am of dragging them all down with me. I was wrong. I can't be Gawain's monster. I'll end up destroying us both and I can't... I won't be the cause of that. I won't be the cause of harm for any of them. I don't want to end up like Mary's fetch but I don't know how to stop it. I like hurting people. I like killing. I am sick and broken and wrong. And I am starting to forget that. Last night I felt glorious. I was so busy reveling in the carnage and violence that I completely forgot the fact that those grays were Changelings like me. <br /> <br /> One way or the other, when I go before the Monarchs I'm going to seek an answer. I... I don't deserve mercy but I am going to ask for it anyway. I know I can't fix what's wrong with me and I won't wait until it drags everyone I love down with me. Maybe there is some way. Maybe there is someone who can help me. Hell, I'd go under the fucking Table if it was the only way at this point. I am willing... I just don't know how. And if they can't or won't help me then hopefully Charlotte will keep her promise of a clean death.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Shit, shit, shit, he found me. It wasn\u2019t on purpose. He wasn\u2019t specifically looking for me, but he found me. Apparently he\u2019d been held captive by Master Darke and some of his people and was inadvertently set free by attackers from the Mothership. They of course did not survive the encounter. But now he is free and I\u2019m not sure what he\u2019s going to do. I don\u2019t know what Darke and his people did to Rook, if they did anything. I don\u2019t know if they used that damn Table on him or not. I can at least tell that he\u2019s still upset with me but doesn\u2019t want me dead. He threw a knife which hit a hairs breadth from my face. He\u2019s very upset with me. I don\u2019t blame him, but I am a little concerned with what his next move is going to be. Okay, more than a little concerned. Shit. I\u2019m so screwed.<br /> <br /> Okay, to put things in context\u2026 the fight from the Mothership was fast and violent. They sent in several guys, to the Dream House, who attempted to stun the lot of us. They succeeded in taking Calamity down, but only after a few of them ganged up on her. They tried to take Gawain out, but Lori kept throwing that Spring court magic at him to renew his flagging strength. Me, I shrugged it off during the fight. I paid for it later when the damage made itself known, but I was able to hold off the effects until the end of the fight. Neat little contract that is. I hadn\u2019t tried it before but it works well. I wonder how well it works on knife wounds?<br /> <br /> Anyway, Calamity, Gawain and I took out the greys. They were not exactly built or trained for up close and personal fighting and it showed. Gawain took the greys and their summoned beasts down like they were made of tissue paper. Seriously, it was a sight to behold. Very unlike the usual calm, collected Gawain. Calamity, once she was revived by Lori, and I had to work a little bit harder than he did, but it wasn\u2019t too much trouble. I suppose it was somewhat satisfying. I had been hoping for a bit more of a fight, but I also didn\u2019t want the others to get hurt, so it all worked out in the end. One grey made it back through the hedge gate and we mopped up what was left. It looked for a second like Calamity was going to follow the last guy into the hedge, but thought better of it at the last moment.<br /> <br /> During this whole fight Flores had the rain coming down to wash away any blood that got spilled, theirs or ours. It also served to wash out any tracks left behind harder to read. Though, I\u2019m not confident that the police officers of Santa Monica could read a track if it was two feet across and right in front of their faces, but the thought had at least occurred to me. We also threw the bodies of the greys into the hedge to keep them from prying eyes. We\u2019ll deal with them later. Gawain suggested giving them a proper burial. Makes sense to me.<br /> <br /> After the greys that attacked the Dream House were dealt with, Joan let us know that the Winter court headquarters had been under attack and that another wave of enemies might come back. She also mentioned that Dr. Bright said that greys had opened the wrong door and \u201cgot what they deserved.\u201d She had been told that it was a captive loyalist that had been let out and decimated the alien\u2019s troops in short order. They had been killed by a knife. <br /> <br /> So, we hightailed it over to the clinic to help defend the Table from the greys. We had just arrived at the clinic, and I got out of Gawain\u2019s van when I was given an up close and personal reminder of my brother in arms\u2019 skill with a blade. I took the blade and pocketed it. I will admit that I had been a bit wary when I heard that a loyalist that attacked with knives had been set free. I wasn\u2019t\u2019 sure it was Rook until the knife was thrown and barely missed my head. That encounter was all I needed to know who it was and what kind of mood he was in. Lucky me.<br /> <br /> When we got inside we were greeted by Gunnar, Captain Jack, Twitch and a whole lot of dead greys. It certainly looked like Rook\u2019s work to me. Gunnar pointed to the room that had the Table in it and said that they had not been back in there yet, but they had made the Table too big to fit through a door, so it wasn\u2019t going anywhere for the moment. Calamity, Insincere Marguerite and I snuck up to look through the doorway and see what was waiting for us on the other side. There were a whole bunch of those cow things, including a really big one that may have been three or four of the regular ones put together. I\u2019m assuming Marguerite went back and told the others what we saw, because Louis showed up with his SMG and asked us to step back a moment while he opened up. After he got their attention and took out one and wounded two more, Calamity and I opened up with our respective guns and took out the others. After the moment of surprise was over we waded in and took out the rest. Again, still not much of a challenge, but enjoyable. Most of us had gone for the \u201cnormal\u201d sized cow things. Jack and Gawain went for the big one. Jack got a decent hit in then Gawain took out any anger he might have been holding onto by taking out that big thing in one final hit. It was impressive to say the least.<br /> <br /> After the fight, Twitch was living up to his name. He had a gun that fired hypodermics full of formaldehyde at the enemy. He used it to good effect on some of those cow things. He was also kind of twitchy due to adrenaline. He said he was high on it, but didn\u2019t elaborate so it might be a natural high, or he might have dosed himself with it. Not sure which, and I\u2019m not going to ask.<br /> <br /> Lorelei also did well in the fight. She brought out the small pistol that Calamity got for her and she took out one of the cow things. After the fight however she started to freak out. It could be the fighting in general that was getting to her. She asked before the fight at the Dream House if it might be possible to ask the greys if they\u2019d like to talk peace. It\u2019s more likely though that she was freaking out because she killed something. My guess was that she had never killed anything or anyone before. Not that that is a bad thing mind you. It\u2019s just not in my experience. Even when I was still a kid and new (relatively) to the Lady\u2019s realm, I had to learn to put my feelings aside and do what had to be done to survive. I had shed enough of my morals and memories by the time that the Lady made her offer that I had no qualms about saying \u201cyes.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sometimes it slips my mind that the others are not quite as morally flexible as I am. I need to keep these things in mind. I really didn\u2019t have any problems killing the greys or the cow/beast things. That\u2019s probably not a good thing, right? Am I supposed to feel bad about that? I think I am. I think it\u2019s supposed to bother me more than it does. Before the fight I\u2019ll admit that I was a bit antsy about the possibility of killing other Changelings. They are essentially just like me, but are still serving their Gentry. But after the fight was done something just clicked in my head and I realized that whatever they happened to be, they were trying to hurt my friends and they deserved what they got.<br /> <br /> Anyhoo, after we mopped up the cows Gawain and I tried to see if we could find any tracks in the vicinity of where I thought I saw the knife come from. We found nothing at all. This did not surprise me at all. If Rook doesn\u2019t want to be found then we won\u2019t find him. Hiding one\u2019s tracks is not hard if you know the right skill to do it. I can change my tracks to whatever I want them to be, and am very close to making them disappear altogether. I guess I\u2019m still following in my teacher\u2019s footsteps to some extent. No pun intended.<br /> <br /> We all piled back into Gawain\u2019s van and headed home. En route Calamity said something along the lines of having a score of four. Lorelei became angry at that and asked if we were suddenly keeping score on such things. Calamity tried to backpedal but Lori wasn\u2019t really cutting her any slack. She was really angry about the comment. I hadn\u2019t thought much about it. I can see where Lori is coming from. Those were four people that won\u2019t get back up and continue on with their daily lives. Any potential actions from them will not happen. I tried to feel bad about it, but found that I really couldn\u2019t. Just like at the Dream House that something clicked in my head and all I could see was the people that they had hurt, or would hurt in the future. I know better than most what kind of person it takes to do that kind of work, and I know that they were not good people. I suppose if I didn\u2019t want to be a hypocrite then I should have suggested that they be given a second chance to do what was right, but in this case I couldn\u2019t. <br /> <br /> I saw what Rook had done to the dozen or so greys that had been in the clinic when they let him out. And I found myself agreeing with Master Darke, that they had opened the wrong door and got what they deserved. I don\u2019t know what happened to change how I saw this situation. Before I could understand some things that Master Darke did, but I did not agree with them. Today, technically yesterday, I found myself agreeing with him and actually found it darkly humorous. It\u2019s probably because things are so personal with this. Those greys were going to take my friends back to their Master. They were going to be hurt or changed against their will. I\u2019m having a hard time feeling bad for them. There is also the fact that Rook is back and so much of this is familiar in a way that I haven\u2019t felt in a long time. It\u2019s a bit different this time, in that I\u2019m on the opposite side from my brother. I\u2019m not happy about that. <br /> <br /> After we got back to the Dream House we talked to Flores who said that the police had been by, but she answered the door after a minute or two barely dressed and acted confused about the noises they were talking about. She said she\u2019d heard a car backfire, but she\u2019d been busy with other things and wasn\u2019t really paying attention. She then offered to let the officers search the grounds and asked them to knock if they had any other questions. They did not come back so I\u2019m assuming their search of the property did not reveal anything incriminating. <br /> <br /> After a bit of planning on who was sleeping where, just in case, Lori and Calamity went to the next room to talk some things out. I\u2019ll admit that I was curious what they were talking about, but figured that they deserved their privacy so I wouldn\u2019t ask. Only a couple minutes later we all heard a shriek and we ran for the door. De la Rocha was the first one there and threw the doors open. Lorelei was crying and clutching Calamity like she was a lifeline. De la Rocha comforted Lori who calmed down enough to say that she had remembered something and didn\u2019t want to talk about it. I can understand that. I\u2019ve had some memories come back and leave me feeing rather raw. I can only guess as to what she suddenly remembered, but whatever it was, it was not a happy memory<br /> <br /> After Lori and De la Rocha went upstairs Calamity looked at me and asked if we were going to be in danger. I said yes. There was no point in sugar coating things. Rook is dangerous. I did say that it was unlikely that he would kill me, but I was unsure what he would do to the others if he had a chance. They are not his target after all and therefore are expendable. Unless he can use one of them as leverage to get to me. It is an old tactic, and in this case would likely work. I do not want to see my friends harmed, and I know what kinds of things he might do to them if he felt like being creative. It might be nice to think that perhaps captivity had mellowed my old mentor, but I already know that is pretty unlikely. Not that he would be out of control. He never is when he\u2019s hunting, and I have no reason to believe that he\u2019s not hunting me right now.<br /> <br /> Calamity offered to use her ability to find people to see where Rook was, or at least how far away. I agreed that it would be a good idea and told her what his name is. She concentrated for a moment before looking confused for a moment. She looked at me and for a brief second I thought she was going to question me. Instead she looked thoughtful and said that she couldn\u2019t find him. In fact the power that she used came back saying that he didn\u2019t exist. I was about to defend myself when she continued. She said that if the power could not find a person it would just fail. It wouldn\u2019t come back with something like a specific message saying that he wasn\u2019t real. So, this meant that he was somehow spoofing her tracking powers. Or anyone else\u2019s for that matter. I did admit that Rook is very good at not being found if he doesn\u2019t want to be.<br /> <br /> We discussed briefly what he might do. I admitted that he would likely need to go back to the Lady and report in. Luna however pointed out that the Hedge is still on fire after the fight with the Mothership, so that option is out for the time being. This means that he has to hide until he makes his move. Either to come after me or to return to the Lady.<br /> <br /> Luna seemed rather upset by this turn of events. She did not seem happy at all to find out that I was being hunted. To be fair I would not be happy if she was the one being hunted either. It seems that in a short time I have found a kindred spirit. We are alike in many ways, but different in others. There\u2019s just some things that I don\u2019t have to explain. I know that I will have to come clean with her about my past if we\u2019re going to continue this relationship. I should probably tell her before Rook has a chance to say anything. I know that I\u2019ll wish I\u2019d already explained but won\u2019t have time in that instance. I just hope that the truth doesn\u2019t push her away.<br /> <br /> There was some fear for my safety, mostly on Luna\u2019s part, and she suggested that I go back to her cabin to stay for the night to keep me safe. I reiterated that I did not think that Rook would actually harm me. I said just that, and left off the bit about him not hurting me too badly. After all, he needs me alive if he is going to return me to the Lady. That is of course, if that is his plan. He may not be under orders to retrieve me this time. All these thoughts were going through my head rather fast, so I agreed that going back to Luna\u2019s cabin would be a good idea. The night passed quietly. Both Luna and myself stayed awake through the night, watching. Just in case Rook managed to track us there. I\u2019ll admit that it was interesting to be the one that was being kept safe. Normally I\u2019m the one doing the protecting. In the freehold, or at least the Dream House I\u2019m one of those that protects the others. I keep Lori and Insincere Marguerite and the other safe from threats. I\u2019m not usually the one on the other side of that.<br /> <br /> In the Lady\u2019s service I protected the Lady herself and her treasures. I also protected the realm itself from outside incursions. Not that we had many of those while I was her Knight, but we did have a couple of scouts from other Gentry try and sneak in and gather information on the Lady and her realm. Rook and I discouraged them. Some thought that they were being clever, others just had an overinflated view of their own skills or importance. I do remember having fun proving them wrong or just taking them down a peg or two. Some we sent back to their Masters with messages. Some we sent back as messages. It all seems rather ruthless now, but I remember enjoying it then. <br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> We talked for a bit this morning about the situation as it stands. Apparently Darke is willing to step down, but only if the person that killed Grey is brought to justice. Calamity said that she had told Queen Charlotte what she\u2019d done and was prepared to pay the price, whatever price. The Queen, from what I can tell, has not yet told the other monarchs what she knows. I\u2019m not sure how this is going to play out. Gawain was very upset by the whole thing. He did not want to allow Calamity to turn herself over to be punished. Calamity herself did not want us fighting the freehold over her, or getting ourselves in trouble over this. There was nothing saying that we couldn\u2019t use the law to defend her though, so maybe we\u2019ll go that route if it comes to it. I certainly hope that something can be worked out that does not involve losing my motley mate. <br /> <br /> A lot of things are uncertain right now. Rook being here brings up all sorts of conflicting thoughts. I think of him as a brother and a friend, yet he did the Lady\u2019s bidding and tortured me after I defected and he brought me back. I\u2019m not sure how to feel right now. I miss my friend, but I don\u2019t miss what that friend represents, or what he might do to me or mine. I know that my new friends will fight him to defend me, but I really don\u2019t want to see them get hurt or worse. Just like I really don\u2019t want Rook to die either. I don\u2019t think I could kill him even if I had the chance. Despite all he\u2019s done, and what he is, he is still my brother and I don\u2019t want him dead.<br /> <br /> Dammit, I don\u2019t want to lose the friends I have. I don\u2019t want to lose my place here, but Rook threatens all that. Or at least he could threaten all that. I don\u2019t actually know what he\u2019s going to do. Do I tell the others about my past, or at least some of them the truth, or do I stay silent and hope that it doesn\u2019t come up? Or do I try and convince my brother that the Lady is wrong and he should leave her? Would he even do it? Could he be convinced? And if he could, would the others give him the chance? Goddess give me strength. I don\u2019t know what to do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> The Business with the Mothership is completed. Finally.<br /> <br /> We all survived due to planning, both our own and that of the Monarchs. It was the first major Gentry incursion in Santa Monica, and I am pleased it went as smoothly as it did. Absolutely.<br /> <br /> Nonetheless, killing means you have erred, that something has gone wrong, that your control has slipped. Every time I have killed things have gone awry, and I possess no eagerness to do so again, even of things of the Hedge, though their quasi-reality makes the act less troubling the motions and apparent effects are the same. <br /> <br /> I\u2019ve killed people before. They were not good people. I am nonetheless not happy I did. If I were more cunning, more canny, more careful it would not have happened. It would not be needed. These people marched under orders, not necessarily even understanding what they were doing. All of us, to some degree, were loyal to our keepers once.<br /> .<br /> All of us, it seems, have secrets.<br /> <br /> While I was unsurprised by the fact that Calamity feels the need to kill so much, given her tendency to give in and be what her Keeper wanted, I was surprised by Gawain\u2019s personal bloodthirstiness. Rather than use gunfire to keep the invaders back, he was eager to surge forward and kill them himself, as he had so often in dreams. As before, those he judged wanting he dealt summery justice to. While he had previously seemed inclined to draw back and do violence only when needed, his grasp of humanity was apparently shaken somewhat by recent events with the Table as, rather than defending those inside, he was eager to go out and spill blood, including the blood of those still in the thrall of their Keeper. <br /> <br /> Perhaps he and Calamity make a better couple than I anticipated. Though this means he functions less effectively as a conscience for her than anticipated. Of course, given her ability and willingness to go behind his back and do what she wants anyway, I suppose that part is of little concern. Theoretically.<br /> <br /> Jacob, too, went out there, but his self-destructive urges are self-evident at this point. Obviously. I care for him, but whatever ghosts his past hold will, I think, drive him to the grave by his own hand. Not suicide, but reckless behavior. It is saddening. I am fairly sure Gawain was not driven by self-destructiveness, however. Not while Calamity is alive.<br /> <br /> Julia injured but did not kill Hailey, which I frankly regard as a good thing. I am still uncomfortable with her eagerness to kill Felicity. I want her to remain someone I feel safe sleeping on. Blissfully.<br /> <br /> Similarly, for all her bravado, De La Rocha stayed in to defend. Which is good, given her general preference for fighting with her fists. She is not Calamity after all; even with being a Leechfinger her hands are less dangerous than Calamity\u2019s knife hands.<br /> <br /> Flores remained a rather helpful force, keeping an eye on things and healing Hailey when needed. While a bit clueless it is important to remember, I suppose, that she is not the creampuff. Fortunately.<br /> <br /> Lorelei seemed a bit disturbed by everything. My little bird did not remain inside but went out to help. And I must admit, she was quite useful, getting Calamity back on her feet. I stayed behind her as I was worried for her safety. When she actually participated in the rehab clinic and shot one of their creatures, however, it seemed to have hurt her inside, and my own reassurance had distressingly little impact on her. Sadly.<br /> <br /> I confess I felt helpless. Nothing I did seemed to reassure her much, or have any helpful effect on her psyche. I did not expect her to shake off killing someone, even a hedge creature made of smoke and dream, but I did not expect the level of trauma. Is she more fragile than I gave her credit for? I should have insisted she remain behind at the rehab clinic. I don\u2019t want her bloodlust to become like Calamity or Gawain, though she keeps it deeper. Of course Lorelei is a lover, not fighter, and it probably won\u2019t, but still. I do earnestly hope De La Rocha was of more assistance to her than I was. Hopefully.<br /> <br /> I need perhaps to study the Contracts of the Moon that I might monitor the stability of my Motley. Partially to help them, partially to head off and deal with threats to myself and loved ones before they catch me by surprise.<br /> <br /> Flores thoroughly embarrassed Oleander, and when Julia and I went upstairs, was quite upset. She was deeply worried about alienating De La Rocha and Oleander with her attempts to help them, and perhaps sensed and misinterpreted Lorelei\u2019s being upset as being upset with her. Possibly. While she was hoping to dally with Lorelei and De La Rocha, whom she had not dallied with, she was less disappointed that had not happened than worried she was ruining her friendships. I worked at my mirror as we sat up and talked awhile. Julia recommend before \u201chelping\u201d someone she should talk to them and, if they seemed to be resistant to help and either Julia, De La Rocha, or Sandoval was not involved she speak to them, privately, and ensure that she was not, well, missing something. She seemed more upbeat after that conversation. Fortunately.<br /> <br /> We made love afterwards; she missed my unique style, as they all do sooner or later. It is a burden, I suppose, being such a bendy lover. When she passed out, Julia and I made love vigorously, as much so as we had in weeks. The worry, frustration, and fear we released in what was frankly one of the more aggressive sessions I have had, and slept quite blissfully afterwards. Soundly.<br /> <br /> This morning most folks seemed better. Lorelei was still upset and disinclined to talk about it, which upset I, but she did talk to De La Rocha, which is good at least. Possibly Calamity, though I am less certain of what was said there. She said she would speak to the rest of us eventually. I hope she is okay. Lorelei means a great deal to I and our lovers, after all. <br /> <br /> The other issue is someone from Jacob\u2019s past has returned to menace him, someone called Rook. Jacob seems quite concerned, so I do as well. Of course, Rook has been in the \u201ccare\u201d of the Winter Court for some time, so I doubt he is feeling terribly well\u2026likely he has some recovery to do. But he will be back, we are sure. I doubt it will be right away, but we must be prepared for when he is. With any luck, though, he will want to kill some Winter Courtier who experimented on him first. Maybe, hopefully, that will give us time to react and prepare\u2026not that we should assume such. Foolishly.<br /> <br /> And Calamity may be arrested for killing Mr. Gray. I don\u2019t want to encourage her to go murdering, but I don\u2019t care to see her be banished or killed for this either. She has, unfortunately, set the precedent she is willing to kill because she thinks it is a good idea heedless of the consequences, rather than it being a crime of passion or a case where her back was against the wall. I can\u2019t imagine the rulers being okay with that, if they are than they are idiots. I may should talk to her about seeking asylum in L.A. with the Night Court. They have use for psychopaths. Apparently.<br /> <br /> With any luck, Gawain won\u2019t do anything to provoke them also. Hopefully.<br /> <br /> The Mothership is gone, but I wish we could get this lingering issues dealt with. Quickly.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXX</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T02:25:48-07:00","id":526478,"title":"","content":"Lots of perspectives on the events of the night.<br /> <br /> Okay, so, each PC had at least one Clarity check this session. After the fight, rolls were made, and Gawain, Lorelei, Jacob, and Insincere Marguerite got an extra two dice due to following their Virtues, All five got a die because they were defending their home, and Lorelei and Insincere Marguerite got an additional die since they did not hurt or kill anyone. Lorelei and Insincere Marguerite passed. Jacob and Gawain lost a Clarity level, and Calamity lost a Clarity level and gained a second Derangement. That leaves her and Jacob at 4, though Jacob started at 5 while she started at 6. Gawain is at 6 now, so still able to use Kenning (Calamity lost it a bit ago, Jacob never had it). The Motley currently stands at Clarity 7-Lorelei, Insincere Marguerite 6-Gawain, Ace, 4-Calamity, Jacob.<br /> <br /> The Greys weapons caused rapidly increasing die penalties which I allowed Gift of Warm Breath from Fleeting Spring to counter, so Lorelei used a good deal of that. Insincere Marguerite used Murkblur of Smoke while invisible (also from Smoke.) I let Jacob use Sorrow-Frozen Heart\u2019s A Mere Vessel for Loss to ignore the penalties as if they were wounds.<br /> <br /> Rooks situation is\u2026complicated. The Winter Court had not broken him, but have left him damaged and having difficulty knowing what is true in his past and what they have brainwashed in him. He is not an immediate threat but foreshadows a plot which will be more of a thing a short ways down the line. The damage could be to Jacob\u2019s advantage, depending on how things go. Of course, it may not.<br /> <br /> Need more details, just ask in thread. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 05-24-2015, 05:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T16:30:54-07:00","id":527148,"title":"","content":"What was Ace up to during all of this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T23:07:37-07:00","id":527368,"title":"","content":"Ace's player has not been able to make the past several sessions dealing with an illness in the family. We hope to have him back before long, but we do not know precisely when.<br /> <br /> In game he was inside protecting people in the Dream House.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 05-25-2015, 02:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T16:20:46-07:00","id":549483,"title":"","content":"Sorry about the delay. Calamity\u2019s player had their journal explode, so no Calamity this time. Longer next time, hopefully. Still four accounts.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s time again to look in on the motley. Several face intensely personal demons, within and without, as the fallout from the invasion continues. Also, the wheel of seasons turns as the Summer Court takes power. Let\u2019s look in on them.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXXI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> Late night June 19th<br /> <br /> OK, so today went better than it started. I mean, kinda better. Not so... ah, I dunno. I guess it\u2019s mostly just me being selfish cause it\u2019s gone kinda shitty for Jacob, and just better for Calamity and me. It did go better for Jacob than he expected, I think, cause we\u2019re all behind him, you know?<br /> <br /> But, in order, the way this is supposed to go - Calamity let me calm down a bit, then talked to me about the arrest thing. She promised she wasn\u2019t just giving up, like Desiree did, but she needed help. And she didn\u2019t want me getting hurt. But the important thing is that she *wants* help, she knows she\u2019s not in great control and she was actually a little repentant. I think - I hope - that\u2019ll be, you know, points in her favor, and the folks here will help her find help. If not, well, I\u2019ll take her away and we\u2019ll find someone who will. I can\u2019t, or don\u2019t know how, or... anyways, there\u2019s gotta be someone who can and will give her a second chance.<br /> <br /> Then while we were talking, Twitch showed up to speak with Jacob. Twitch had just left and I was trying to cheer Calamity up by offering that I could maybe manage to scare Annika away if she wanted to take a break when Jacob walked calmly by and started punching a door. We all kinda converged, you know, and Jacob explained he had wanted to hit Twitch but resisted and hit the door instead.<br /> <br /> Then he asked Julia to leave so it was just the motley and Luna. He explained that Rook, aka \u2018Subject 61\u2019, the loyalist the Winter Court had been torturing lately, had been his partner, back when Jacob was a loyalist. Lori was quick to confirm the past tense there. He told us a little of the story - he\u2019d been given a second chance, by one of the people he had lured into Arcadia no less, and had grabbed it tight. There were details missing that he must have told Calamity cause she seemed to understand better. Still, the meat of the story was there, and this Rook was the villain. But everyone deserves that second chance and Jacob wants to extend his former brother-in-arms his.<br /> <br /> And so we\u2019re looking for him. To see if we can\u2019t talk him around before he reports back to his lady, and even more importantly, before the, you know, Winter Court find him. Twitch had been by to warn Jacob that Rook was free and had been after him, before the brainwashing. Apparently they left him uncertain as to which of 6 or so Keepers was his, an extreme aversion to hurting Jacob specifically, a fear of buildings and an adverse reaction to sunlight. Jacob left out the details telling us, but I don\u2019t think Twitch had. Jacob was as close to seething as I had ever seen our ice Elemental.<br /> <br /> Calamity did her finding thing again was the same weird results. With the whole building-phobia thing, we figured he\u2019d hole up in some wooded place, you know? So Luna is checking out her neck of the woods, and we hit up some nearby Hedge. Nothing so far, but we\u2019re not giving up!<br /> <br /> <br /> Early morning June 20th<br /> <br /> Still nothing. Jacob keeps muttering unkind things about Twitch, in Russian and sometimes English. Apparently he does a lot of drugs and hallucinates that someone named Maria from his Durance is chasing him? I might be able to help if it was dreams/nightmares, but I don\u2019t think I can help with hallucinations.<br /> <br /> <br /> Early morning June 21st<br /> <br /> Well, that went better than I expected. Again, for Calamity and me, not Jacob - there\u2019s still no sign of Rook. At this point, the drugs are wearing off and he\u2019s probably far away. At least the Winter Court didn\u2019t get him either - surely they would have let Jacob know he was safe after all, you know?<br /> <br /> But the Courts came for Calamity and it was nothing like I expected. No restraints, no being marched off, just an Oath to not run off and a scheduling for the trial. Apparently, Darke \u2018believes in second chances\u2019 (if he says that to my face it will be very very difficult not to punch him in his) and so isn\u2019t calling for the death penalty. Neither is Queen Charlotte, of course, or Boss Lojack. So that\u2019s not on the table - it\u2019s banishment, or oaths and reparation. The trial is set for Monday.<br /> <br /> Friday said something about Moon using the Lunar Contract, to test how stable Calamity is. She\u2019s really worried about what zie\u2019ll find. She keeps saying she\u2019s not going to end up like Mary\u2019s Fetch and she\u2019s not - I\u2019ll see to it, you know? Jacob mentioned that the Winter Court keeps some non-Changeling counselors on the payroll for things like this. The irony didn\u2019t escape me, that the second chance and help I mentioned in my last entry would come from Darke and the Winter Court. But... if it will help, you know?<br /> <br /> Captain Jack thinks it will. Calamity finally called him and he agreed to represent her. Took it as kinda like a given, since she was his friend and that\u2019s not a thing he takes back lightly, you know? Especially since her intentions were good and she recognizes that she needs help. He\u2019s a great guy, Captain Jack is. He was really hopeful about it, and that helped a lot.<br /> <br /> He did warn us that he and Lojack had been in a relationship once, and it had ended kinda, you know, badly. They\u2019d made up since then, and Lojack wasn\u2019t the type to get biased over it, but he thought it was only fair to let us know. Lojack\u2019s not out though, so it\u2019s just between us.<br /> <br /> Captain Jack also helped bring the mood up cause he had plans (of course) for the Summer Coronation. After the optional Christian-y ceremony and the official coronation bit, he is going to show up dressed as Spiderman with a thing rigged so it would look like he was shooting webbing and using it to \u2018steal\u2019 bras. I of course would have to put an end to such dastardly shenanigans and there would be an epic church rooftop chase, complete with a yell of \u201cSanctuary\u201d at some point.<br /> <br /> He also pointed out that the celebration was very Ren Faire-y, so if I wanted to set up a tent to sell my smith work, it would be cool. So he\u2019s lending me a tent and Jacob and I will be doing that, you know, when I\u2019m not chasing off superpowered bar thieves. More importantly though, this revealed that De la Roche and Lori have never been to a Ren Faire and Lori didn\u2019t even know what one was! So we\u2019re going to have to visit one sometimes. There\u2019s the Belmont Pier thing, that\u2019s usually the end of June. I always loved the Big Bear Ren Faire, though that\u2019s a few hours away. Or maybe we\u2019ll just have to wait til next spring and so see the original, RPFS.<br /> <br /> The other thing, which I think is a good thing too, was that Lori told us about the thing that bothered her, that she remembered Tuesday night. There was the whole contest thing, in her Durance, and when a girl named Annabelle who was prettier and a better singer than Lori (she said) showed up, Lori and her friends killed her so she wouldn\u2019t win.<br /> <br /> So she was projecting a little, when she got upset at Calamity for killing Grey for what he might do. I mean, I still agree with a lot of what she said then, not that I\u2019m gonna rub that in, you know, ever, but Lori was worried about how jealous a person she was, which seemed weird, looking at her 3 girlfriends and thinking about Flores and Oleander and Felicity, you know? But then she mentioned Annika, which made more sense. And like Insincere Marguerite said, it spoke well for her being better than she was in Arcadia, since she hadn\u2019t done anything to Annika, not even talked behind her back or tried to turn us against her, even if we could all tell she didn\u2019t like the Dancer.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t really know what to say, but the others seemed to. Hopefully they cheered her up and she knows I wasn\u2019t, like, judging or something. She did seem more cheerful at least, especially after talking about clothes for later today.<br /> <br /> <br /> Late night June 21st<br /> <br /> That was just awesome. A nice, relaxing day, just talking about swords and smithing, chasing grown men dressed as Spiderman and meeting someone who might sponsor me into the Family of Silent Nights. Not to even mention all the beautiful girls in corsets. It was great!<br /> <br /> Calamity was a little quiet though - even Andromeda noticed and I wasn\u2019t sure she knew anyone but Joan existed sometimes. Calamity was worried about the trial, I think. It did mean she stayed in the tent with me almost the whole time, which I certainly didn\u2019t mind, you know, not in that awesome outfit, and she wasn\u2019t upset, I don\u2019t think, just thoughtful.<br /> <br /> Andromeda was looking super good herself. She used the Table on Joan, you know, and fixed her curse, which is great, but she felt a little... empty afterwards. Not nearly as bad as Grey, but it was reminiscent enough that I talked with her about it. She was trying to hide it from Joan, probably so as not to worry her, and she says she\u2019s not gonna use the Table again, except to fix Princess Joli. Not that she said that specifically, but she said she promised someone and I know from Lori that she promised her, so I assumed.<br /> <br /> She and Joan stayed at the booth awhile. It\u2019s fun to talk metalwork with Joan, you know? We had a couple of other visitors too - I even sold a couple of pieces, which is not bad for a booth with no rental fee. One guy that stopped by drew quite a crowd - my whole motley + girlfriends, Captain Jack - I mean Spiderman, cause my nemesis totally wouldn\u2019t show up like that - and a few others were all but drooling at Juan Carlos Hypnos, a Family of Silent Nights who had heard about me asking around after them. He\u2019s gonna come by the Dream House to talk more Tuesday. Lori mimed stabbing me when I even paused in confirming the Dream House was a good meeting place and again when I didn\u2019t make introductions all around fast enough. He was handsome, I guess. Spiderman even tried giving him a \u2018Get out of gay free\u2019 card, so having sex with him wouldn\u2019t be gay, you see. Juan was far more interested in the ladies though. Poor Captain Jack.<br /> <br /> Speaking of the crazy awesome dude, shenanigans went off perfectly. I managed a pretty sweet jump, right to the top of the roof after I \u2018noticed\u2019 he wasn\u2019t really Spiderman after he \u2018stole\u2019 Lori\u2019s bra and he ran off. He somehow got the old Spiderman cartoon theme song to start playing as we ran along the roof. No helicopter this time, I just chased him off after being momentarily foiled by his crying \u2018Sanctuary\u2019 from the steeple. He did come back, sans costume, to enjoy the rest of the celebration.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Okay, it\u2019s been a few days since my last entry, and things are starting to settle down. It looks like Rook has left the area for the time being, we have a strategy to deal with Calamity\u2019s political situation, and I\u2019ve been drowning my other troubles in sex, alcohol, and music.<br /> <br /> I still see Annabelle\u2019s face every time I close my eyes, but I think I\u2019m starting to get a handle on it. Mostly thanks to D and the others.<br /> <br /> Twitch came by the Dream House on Wednesday afternoon and asked to speak to Jacob. I didn\u2019t hear everything that was said, but I know he officially told Jacob that Rook had escaped, and that there was a chance that he would come after Jacob. I know he detailed some of the atrocious brainwashing techniques Darke\u2019s people used on Rook. And I know that Jacob was <u>furious</u> after Twitch left.<br /> <br /> Jacob told us all about his history with Rook after that. It was\u2026 hard to hear, in a way. The two of them were Loyalists together for a long time. They were partners. Their Keeper sent them out into the world to retrieve Changelings who had escaped, and they were very good at their job.<br /> <br /> Jacob looked miserable during this entire conversation, like he was steeling himself to pack up his things and walk away from us forever. I asked him the one question that I thought really mattered. \u201cBut this was all in the past, right? You don\u2019t do those things anymore?\u201d<br /> <br /> He shook his head.<br /> <br /> I breathed a sigh of relief. \u201cOkay, then.\u201d<br /> <br /> Calamity stepped up. \u201cWhat do you want to do about this, Jacob?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> He considered for a moment. \u201cRook is very dangerous,\u201d he admitted, \u201cbut he is also a friend. A brother. I used to be like he is now, but I got better. I came back from it. Maybe I can help him to come back from it too.\u201d<br /> <br /> I think most of us have our private doubts about whether or not that is possible, but we owe it to Jacob to try. So we agreed to start searching for Rook, and to try to bring him back alive if possible, in the hopes that we can make him see how his Keeper is using him and bring him into the Freehold.<br /> <br /> I won\u2019t go into the details of the intense three-day search that followed\u2026 mostly because I wasn\u2019t able to contribute in any meaningful way, but had to be there anyway in case any of my friends required on-the-spot healing. The long and the short of it is that we didn\u2019t find him, and by now he\u2019s probably miles away and in the wind.<br /> <br /> One thing that really disturbs me about this whole situation is that Twitch referred to Rook as Subject 61. I\u2019ve spent the past few days telling myself that the numbers might be assigned randomly; that there aren\u2019t necessarily sixty other people out there who have been subjected to the same crap that Rook went through. According to Jacob, his friend isn\u2019t sure which of six different Keepers is really his, he has an aversion to architecture, the sun causes him physical pain\u2026 I\u2019m terrified of this man, but I also can\u2019t help but feel sorry for him.<br /> <br /> He\u2019s Jacob\u2019s friend. We have to at least <u>try</u> to help him.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, Jacob mentioned that Twitch said he\u2019s still haunted by hallucinations of \u201cMaria,\u201d a monster who plagued him during his Durance and followed him when he made his escape. I very pointedly did <u>not</u> glance at D during this conversation, but I squeezed her hand under the table in what I hope was a comforting way. She seemed to appreciate it.<br /> <br /> So we had to briefly interrupt our search on Friday afternoon to receive Gunnar Friday and Ji Wen Ja, who were serving as representatives of the Freehold. They had come to take Calamity into custody\u2026 sort of. Those of us who have survived the Durance don\u2019t look kindly on the practice of locking people up in cells, so they settled for an oath that she wouldn\u2019t try to leave the area until the Freehold had held a trial.<br /> <br /> The death penalty is officially off the table. Apparently Master Darke wants to stress to the Freehold that he believes in second chances. I think we all breathed a big sigh of relief at that, though Gawain fumed at the phrasing, and who can blame him?<br /> <br /> As she had promised she would, Calamity agreed to all of the Freehold\u2019s terms, and that was that. She plans to show contrition, and she hopes that she can get help for what she now recognizes as a problem in the way that she looks at violence. \u201cThere\u2019s something wrong with me,\u201d she said miserably when Gunnar and Ji Wen Ja had left. \u201cI told myself that I was protecting the motley, but that wasn\u2019t it. I <u>wanted</u> to do it. I wanted to hurt him because I <u>could</u>.\u201d<br /> <br /> I heard the echoes of the things I had said to her in anger a few days before, and it broke my heart. \u201cLook, Calamity, I know I said a lot of things like that to you\u2026\u201d I began.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt was all true,\u201d she said quickly.<br /> <br /> \u201cBut I didn\u2019t say them because they were true,\u201d I admitted, \u201cI said them because I was being a bitch. I was angry about something else\u2026 something I wouldn\u2019t let myself see, and I was taking it out on you. And I\u2019m so sorry.\u201d<br /> <br /> I turned to the rest of them. \u201cI\u2019m not trying to steal focus here,\u201d I said as levelly as I could. \u201cI know what\u2019s happening to Calamity and Jacob is much more important than what I\u2019m about to say. I just\u2026 I think I owe Calamity an explanation, and I don\u2019t want to have to say this more than once.\u201d<br /> <br /> They were all looking at me, which gave me inappropriate tingles. I fought them down. D nodded encouragingly, and I took a deep breath. <br /> <br /> It took a surprisingly short time to tell the people I care about most the worst thing I\u2019ve ever done. And in the end, just like D, they all accepted it and said and did things they thought would make me feel better. No one actually tried to tell me that it was <u>okay</u> that I\u2019d killed Annabelle, but the other platitudes were all present and accounted for. We all did horrible things in Arcadia. Don\u2019t let what your Keeper did to you ruin the rest of your life. You\u2019re a better person now than you were then.<br /> <br /> I tried to explain it to them, but they all seemed determined not to get it. I told them all that I\u2019m a very jealous person, even though that doesn\u2019t really cover the problem by a long shot. They pooh-poohed the notion, pointing out that I\u2019m willing to share my lovers as evidence that I\u2019ve gotten over that. I brought up my hatred of Annika \u2013 which I admitted is completely irrational \u2013 as evidence that I\u2019m <u>not</u> better. Nobody seemed to think it was a problem. After all, I haven\u2019t tried to kill Annika, or even turn my friends against her.<br /> <br /> It is a problem. I killed someone. She was a friend. She could have become a lover, given time. She was a good person. I liked her. And I killed her because she was better than me. She was prettier, she was smarter, and she was more talented. And I just couldn\u2019t stand it. And that\u2019s what I feel every time I look at Annika. Every time I see her dance, and I know that I can\u2019t do what she does. I\u2019ll probably <u>never</u> be able to do what she does. I haven\u2019t tried to kill her\u2026 yet. I probably couldn\u2019t take her on even if I <u>did</u> try. But God, sometimes I look at her and I <u>want</u> to. I didn\u2019t recognize the feeling for what it was until recently, but it\u2019s there.<br /> <br /> It <u>is</u> a problem. But it\u2019s my problem, and I\u2019ll deal with it the only way that I can\u2026 one day at a time.<br /> <br /> In any case, Calamity called Captain Jack up and asked him to represent her at the trial on Monday. She actually tried to apologize for not asking me to do it instead, but I assured her that it wasn\u2019t necessary. I don\u2019t want that responsibility. Of course, I would have done my best if she had chosen me to speak for her\u2026 but I don\u2019t know the first thing about the legal realities of this situation.<br /> <br /> Luckily Captain Jack does, and he was perfectly willing to speak for Calamity. He\u2019s a neutral party as far as the seasonal courts are concerned, and he\u2019s well-regarded in the area despite his antics\u2026 or maybe because of them. In any case, he\u2019s a good choice as an advocate for a lot of reasons. He thinks the best defense strategy would be to show contrition and a willingness to make amends for her transgressions. He wants her to stress at the trial that she wants to get help; to ensure that whatever problems she\u2019s working through don\u2019t cause any more deaths. The Winter Court keeps a number of enchanted mortal psychiatrists on staff, and they\u2019re quite adept at helping Changelings deal with this sort of situation.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a good idea. There are probably any number of contracts which would tear apart any cover story we might come up with if we tried to convince the courts that she was innocent.<br /> <br /> So when the Captain arrived, he was so certain that he could help Calamity\u2019s case that he put us all at ease within a matter of minutes, and talk turned to the next day\u2019s coronation event. With all the recent drama, I had almost forgotten that the reins of power were about to pass from Princess Jolie to Viscount Augustine and the Summer Court. D asked me on behalf of her Court if I would sing at the event like a week ago, and I had completely forgotten.<br /> <br /> I did my normal thing and started obsessing over what to wear. Hey, it beats moping about the motley\u2019s myriad <u>real</u> problems, right? Captain Jack told us that there was no real dress code, but that the Summer Court tended to run their events like a \u201cRen Fair.\u201d I expressed some puzzlement over the term, and Gawain launched into a lengthy explanation about the cultural phenomenon known as the Renaissance Festival.<br /> <br /> Apparently there\u2019s sort of a tradition where a bunch of people get together in vaguely period costumes and pretend it\u2019s medieval times\u2026 sort of. It\u2019s been going on for a while, and there are a few venerable annual festivals that were even around back in my day, though I never really heard anything about them growing up in Iowa. There\u2019s music and jousting and whatnot at the larger ones. It sounds like it could be a lot of fun\u2026 though I still don\u2019t claim to understand how the turkey legs fit into the whole thing.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo, I should, what?\u201d I asked as Gawain went on about the festival. \u201cPut together some sort of an outfit with a long skirt, a peasant top and a leather corset? Where am I supposed to get something like that in my measurements before tomorrow night?\u201d<br /> <br /> Julia got this kind of glazed look in her eyes, muttered \u201cI\u2019m on it,\u201d and ran out of the room.<br /> <br /> D chuckled, and I turned and grinned at her. \u201cSo, sweetie,\u201d I asked mischievously, \u201cyou gonna get dolled up as Ye Olde Tavern Wench too?\u201d<br /> <br /> She shook her head and held her hands up defensively. \u201cNot my scene, babe,\u201d she commented lightly. \u201cCan\u2019t wait to see <u>you</u> in it, though.\u201d<br /> <br /> We launched into coronation preparations after that. Julia came through in a big way with the medieval threads, and though lacing up that corset was not my idea of a fun Saturday night (and was made all the more difficult by my wings), I have to admit that it looked <u>good</u> once we got it on. Jacob decided to wear the Hedge-spun \u201chighwayman\u201d outfit we found in the Hedge House, whereas D got dolled up in biker leathers as per usual (her good leathers, though, not her everyday leathers). Calamity also decided to sport a corset, although in her case the look is less \u201cbawdy serving girl\u201d and more \u201cbad-ass dominatrix.\u201d I\u2019m not sure how she got roped into this, but Julia agreed to let D pick her outfit for the coronation, so she was also tricked out in biker leathers (which was an unusual but viciously hot look for her). <br /> <br /> Gawain had managed to obtain permission to sell some of his metalwork at a specially dedicated booth at the coronation, and Jacob asked if he could display some of the leather pieces he\u2019s been working on out there as well. Their booth turned out to be quite popular, so the two of them were kept pretty busy throughout most of the party\u2026 except for the requisite shenanigans between Gawain and Captain Jack.<br /> <br /> Oh, yes, there were shenanigans.<br /> <br /> D and I showed up a little early, as Viscount Augustine had arranged for a brief religious ceremony before the coronation proper. I wanted to show my solidarity to the Freehold\u2019s other Christian members, and D wanted to show her support for me. The service was lovely.<br /> <br /> The rest of the evening was essentially a big party; a chance for the Freehold to get together and celebrate the turning of the seasons. Princess Jolie stepped down graciously\u2026 and I can\u2019t have been the only one who detected a hint of relief in her voice as she passed the mantle of leadership over to Viscount Augustine.<br /> <br /> I spent a lot of the party up on the little makeshift stage they\u2019d set up outside the church, singing old favorites and requests, but I got a few chances to join the crowd and mingle. Just about everyone was there, so I was able to catch up with people I hadn\u2019t seen in a while.<br /> <br /> Andromeda approached me at one point, during one of the rare moments she was away from Joan. She was happy, but seemed tired and more than a little disturbed. She\u2019d used the table to remove Joan\u2019s curse, and though it seemed to have worked well, the effort obviously took a lot out of her. She told me that she would honor her promise to fix my friend, but that she\u2019d like a little time to recover first, and that she didn\u2019t think she\u2019d be using the table more than was absolutely necessary.<br /> <br /> I remembered the look on Mr. Grey\u2019s face as he dully told us about the atrocities he\u2019d committed in Darke\u2019s name, and I saw the shadow of that fading in Andromeda\u2019s eyes. I told her that I understood. I would have told her to forget about using the table to help my friend, if Jolie\u2019s situation hadn\u2019t been so dire.<br /> <br /> I sought out the Princess next. She was talking with Queen Charlotte, but agreed to speak privately with me when I asked. I explained about Andromeda\u2019s situation and the table, and Jolie agreed to wait a week or so before undergoing the procedure. I promised that I would be there with her when it happened, to make sure everything went according to plan. I feel a little bad about putting Andromeda through this, but I don\u2019t know of any other way to honor my promise to help Jolie with her problem.<br /> <br /> We talked for a while about other things, as well. It\u2019s nice that Jolie is willing to confide in me, but it\u2019s a little strange that someone for whom I\u2019ve long had such a strong sexual attraction is becoming such a close friend. She shared her recent travails regarding the Malibu dating scene, including Queen Charlotte\u2019s continued interest in rekindling their relationship. \u201cI know she really cares for me,\u201d Jolie confided, \u201cbut that relationship wasn\u2019t good for me. For either of us, really.\u201d<br /> <br /> I commiserated for a while, but there wasn\u2019t much I could say to cheer her up beyond reminding her that by next weekend at least one of her problems will be properly over and done with. It helped, but I wish I could have done more. I love D, and I would never do anything to hurt her in a million years, but sometimes I wish I could have taken the Princess up on her offer last month, just to see if I could be the kind of lover that would make her position a little easier to bear. It\u2019s hard for me to see her in pain.<br /> <br /> My next number came up, and I wandered toward the stage once more. Marguerite met me as I was stepping down and gave me a big kiss. I\u2019m not sure if she thought she was laying some claim to me, or just announcing our relationship to the Freehold. If it\u2019s the former, well, I hope she knows that she doesn\u2019t own me, and I\u2019m still going to keep doing exactly as I please as far as my romantic life is concerned. If it\u2019s the latter, then that\u2019s okay; I don\u2019t mind people knowing about us.<br /> <br /> A few minutes later we joined D and Julia in one corner of the grounds. We were just discussing how to spend the rest of our evening (Julia had some <u>very</u> interesting ideas on that topic) when I glanced over at Gawain and Jacob and felt the rest of the world slip away for a minute. I swear, it was almost like the festival went into soft focus or something as I developed a severe case of tunnel vision.<br /> <br /> An absolutely <u>gorgeous</u> man was talking to Gawain. He was clearly of Latin descent, with flowing black hair and olive skin. He was wearing a tie, but no shirt, and it was obvious that he took care of his body.<br /> <br /> \u201cWho is <u>that?</u>\u201d I asked faintly, nodding in his direction.<br /> <br /> The others turned to look. \u201cI think we should find out,\u201d D murmured. <br /> <br /> Marguerite nodded, but Julia didn\u2019t seem impressed. \u201cHe\u2019s cute, but not really my type,\u201d she commented nonchalantly.<br /> <br /> Marguerite turned a piercing stare at her paramour. \u201cYou are <u>not</u> \u2018mostly straight,\u2019 Ma Cherie,\u201d she commented wryly.<br /> <br /> I couldn\u2019t seem to tear my eyes away from him. \u201cI know I just learned to talk to birds and all, but for some reason all I can think right now is <u>woof</u>!\u201d I commented.<br /> <br /> We made our way over to the booth and stood patiently aside for a moment or two while the attractive stranger talked to Gawain. I eventually resorted to the clich\u00e9 of clearing my throat loudly several times before the big lug thought to introduce us.<br /> <br /> Juan-Carlos Hypnos certainly is a charmer. He had most of us eating out of his hand in seconds. He asked Calamity if she was a performer at the Dream House, and expressed his disbelief that someone so lovely had not yet taken the stage.<br /> <br /> He kissed my hand as we were introduced. \u201cMs. Grace,\u201d he said with just a hint of an accent, \u201cI had heard rumors of your loveliness, but they do not do you justice. I must speak with Mr. Vert on Tuesday evening. I think perhaps it is time I attended a show at the Dream House.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll do my best to live up to your expectations, Mr. Hypnos,\u201d I said with a smile.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd you,\u201d he said, turning to D, \u201care you also a performer?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI am now,\u201d she breathed, her cheeks reddening adorably.<br /> <br /> I chuckled and smirked. \u201cYou little minx!\u201d I said with mock exasperation, playfully swatting at her arm as Juan-Carlos turned to address Marguerite. \u201cYou told me I\u2019d never get you up on that stage when I asked you last month. I believe your exact words were \u2018no way in hell, Lori!\u2019\u201d<br /> <br /> She grinned sheepishly. \u201cA girl can change her mind, right?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s when Spider-Man showed up. He also seemed enamored of Mr. Hypnos, even going so far as to offer him a \u201cGet Out of Gay Free\u201d card, so that having sex with him once wouldn\u2019t mean he was homosexual (honestly, the labels people will hang on themselves these days! Why can\u2019t people just fuck whoever they want and stop worrying about what that means about them as a person?). Of course it was Captain Jack beneath the costume. Who else?<br /> <br /> Then came the aforementioned shenanigans. Spider-Man\u2019s arrival made quite a commotion, though everyone seemed to know it was the good Captain, and most of the Freehold seemed to have been expecting something outrageous from him. \u201cSpider-Man\u201d began acting in a most un-heroic way, using his web-shooters to steal bras from the ladies of the Freehold, ripping them right out from under their outfits!<br /> <br /> (Yes, of course it was sleight-of-hand. I was the nefarious wall-crawler\u2019s first victim, and anyone who had been paying the least bit of attention \u2013 and I\u2019m willing to bet that included more than a few people \u2013 was well aware that I wasn\u2019t wearing a bra to begin with\u2026 the straps would have shown.)<br /> <br /> Gawain quickly noticed that something was amiss, and chased the notorious ne\u2019er-do-well off the grounds, all the while loudly berating him for impugning the good name of a true hero. There was a daring chase across the gothic rooftops of the church complex, including Jack bellowing \u201cSanctuary!\u201d when he reached the bell tower, and culminating in the requisite \u201cand don\u2019t come back!\u201d The crowd ate it up, and even the stuffier members of the Summer Court seemed amused by it.<br /> <br /> I was watching Juan-Carlos walk away and contemplating the enticing possibility of breaking in that particular stallion on Tuesday night when I felt a tentative tap on my shoulder. It was Julia, and she looked really upset. \u201cDance with me?\u201d she asked quietly. \u201cPlease?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course, honey,\u201d I said, putting an arm around her and pulling her out on to the dance floor. \u201cWhat\u2019s wrong?\u201d I asked after a moment.<br /> <br /> \u201cNothing,\u201d she said quickly, resting her head on my shoulder.<br /> <br /> \u201cJulia\u2026\u201d I said.<br /> <br /> \u201cI just\u2026 all three of you were drooling over that guy, and I just wanted you to pay a little attention to me for a while,\u201d she whispered.<br /> <br /> I pulled her close. \u201cSweetie,\u201d I said softly, \u201cI love you, okay? You know I\u2019m a free spirit as far as sex is concerned, and I won\u2019t deny that I\u2019ve been thinking about taking that guy for a ride\u2026 if he\u2019s willing. But you <u>know</u> I\u2019ll come back to you three, right? You have nothing to worry about.\u201d<br /> <br /> She looked almost on the verge of tears. \u201cI know, I just\u2026 before, when you guys were teasing me about my orientation\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I leaned in and kissed her. It lasted a while. When we separated, I explained my philosophy succinctly. \u201cStraight, gay, bi\u2026 I don\u2019t care, Julia. I love you, okay? And D loves you. And Marguerite <u>really</u> loves you. I\u2019m sorry if we upset you.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded, smiled through her tears, and let her gaze linger on my corset-enhanced cleavage. I think she\u2019s going to be all right.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T16:21:35-07:00","id":549485,"title":"","content":"<b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Well, I\u2019m not dead or locked up and I\u2019m not exactly sure why not. I told the Motley and Luna today about my past with Rook, and they haven\u2019t done anything but be supportive. I\u2019m not sure I know how to handle that. I was expecting more negative reactions ending with me being shipped off to the Winter Court for questioning. Questioning may still come from the Winter court, but not as of yet. But no, my Motley didn\u2019t really react all that much all things considered. Luna didn\u2019t either. I was expecting a more negative reaction from Lorelei at least, considering she was lured to Arcadia in the first place by a Loyalist. Figured my past would be too close to home, but nope, she was just as understanding as the rest of them.<br /> <br /> So, how did this come to pass you ask? Easy, Twitch paid me a visit and then after he left I punched a door repeatedly. Yeah so, Twitch came by to talk to me. I invited him in so we could have a private chat. He was there to bring me a warning about Subject 61 (ie Rook). Apparently they caught Rook some time back and discovered that he was here to kill me or bring me back to the Lady. Darke and his people focused on the \u201cplanning to kill Jacob\u201d bit and decided to change Rook\u2019s mind. Not in a nice way, or through debate. No, they tortured the fuck out of him and filled him so full of drugs it will be a wonder if he\u2019s sane. They basically used torture and drugs to break him down and try and confuse him as to what Gentry he actually served. They gave him a possible six. They used electrical shocks, strong ones, to kind of program him to be afraid of hurting me, and made it so he is afraid of buildings and the city in general. They also did something to make him afraid of the sun. Too long in the sun and his mind could break even further!<br /> <br /> To say I was unhappy about all this was an understatement. Twitch just kept blithely telling me about all of this and his part in it while I stood there and somehow didn\u2019t hit him. Granted he didn\u2019t know what Rook means to me, but even if I hated the man I would be sick at what was done to him. Yet, Twitch didn\u2019t seem to find anything wrong with what he\u2019d done. He did seem to realize what would happen to him if Subject 61 ever found his way back to town and to a certain jittery Winter courtier though, so there\u2019s that. He saw what Rook did to those twelve greys when they invaded the clinic and let him go. Considering what kind of shape he had to be in at that point twelve is a damn impressive number. At some point training just kind of kicks in and you go on muscle memory. I think Twitch realizes just how much time he has left, and it\u2019s not in years.<br /> <br /> So the problem is, they were planning on building Rook back up to be a respectable member of society, or at least one on the side of the freehold (and likely in Darke\u2019s employ). But they didn\u2019t get that far. The greys attacked and let Rook free before Darke and Twitch could \u201crecreate\u201d him. So, I don\u2019t know where this is going to leave Rook. I don\u2019t know what state of mind he\u2019s going to be in once all the drugs wear off. I don\u2019t know if he\u2019s still going to want to kill me, or take me back or just keep running. He could be anywhere right now and that makes me anxious. Not really because he might still want to hurt me, but because he\u2019s alone and hurt and has no support. I know, I know I should be hating his guts for what he did to me. For bringing me back to the Lady the first time and participating in my torture. I wish I could say that at that time I wouldn\u2019t have done the same thing. But if I hadn\u2019t changed, if I hadn\u2019t seen what I used to be and been given a chance to come back to that, I probably would have done the same thing to him. The Lady\u2019s wish was my command and I made her wishes come true.<br /> <br /> So, I guess a part of me really can\u2019t completely blame Rook for what he did, and so when I heard Twitch talking and talking about all the shit they did to him I got mad. Really mad. After Twitch left to go hide I walked over to one of the interior doors and punched it until the wood cracked and my knuckles bled. I wanted to hit it some more, but the noise drew the Motley and Luna to find out what was going on. When they were all standing there looking at me I realized that I needed to come up with some excuse for destroying the door. I was about to lie and give them some other excuse for my actions. Being bothered by the blithe description of torture would probably have been it, but I stopped myself before I could even really start. I realized in that instant that they deserved the truth, not some bullshit. So, I told them the truth. I told them what Darke and Twitch and the others had done to Rook, and what condition he was in now. I told them that Rook and I used to be partners and we were both Loyalists. We served the Lady and I saw him as a teacher and a friend.<br /> <br /> I was expecting to be admonished for keeping this secret, or to see looks of distrust or anger in their eyes, but there was none of that. I don\u2019t understand. Why don\u2019t they hate me? Why did they accept what I was and what I did so easily? I don\u2019t understand. Why? I can\u2019t look in the mirror without seeing Rime look back. Especially lately. I see the Loyalist. I see his crimes. I see the blood on my hands and the looks in the eyes of my victims. I hear the desperate prayers on their lips as I brought them back, or abandoned them to die. They should be disgusted with me. Don\u2019t they understand what they have in their midst?<br /> <br /> Calamity thinks herself a monster because she likes to fight and to hurt people. I guess from some people\u2019s perspectives that description might fit, but not for me. She needs help and she knows it. She has admitted that she needs to talk to someone about her urges and get help to stop them. That in and of itself proves that she is not irredeemable. I know that what she did to her parents and probably some others was wrong, but I don\u2019t think her acts were monstrous. I know what it is to be a monster and she\u2019s not it. The monster is the one that commits heinous acts but doesn\u2019t know that they\u2019re wrong. They do them for one reason or another and will keep doing them because they enjoy it or because it really doesn\u2019t bother them to do so. In my case it was both. The Lady asked me to do jobs for her and I was more than happy to do them. The tasks themselves did not bother me the way that they should. I led people to their deaths or to the Lady, which might be considered worse. I did it all knowingly and willingly. I am the monster\u2026I just don\u2019t know why they don\u2019t see it.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll be honest. I wasn\u2019t sure if I would find acceptance or denial from Calamity because she does have an inkling of what I was. She chose to accept me though, and I still don\u2019t understand why. What I did was so much worse than anything she or the rest of them have done. So much\u2026 Why don\u2019t they hate me? Why? I just don\u2019t understand. A punch in face, a knife in the ribs\u2026something. I would have deserved it, but nope. I got none of that. I don\u2019t understand. Fuck I need a drink.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> So, yesterday we started looking for Rook. We figured he might still be close by hiding in the Hedge or nearby woods, so we started looking. I had expressed to the group that I wanted to try and help Rook and give him a second chance like I was given. They agreed and we planned out who would look where and when. Luna said that she would search the woods where her cabin was. The rest of us started our search in the Hedge. Nothing came of it so far. Not even Calamity\u2019s \u201cFind \u2018Em\u201d power worked\u2026again. During the search I told the others a little bit more about what Twitch said, including something about a \u201cMaria\u201d that he was terrified of and running from. Apparently he\u2019s convinced that she followed him out of the Hedge and will kill him if she finds him. I\u2019m almost tempted to lead her to him. I\u2019m not even sure if I\u2019d feel bad about that or not. Yeah, probably not a healthy line of thought.<br /> <br /> Anyhoo\u2026I also mentioned another thing that Twich told me. He said that they had overheard Rook talking to a hallucination, speaking in a familiar tone and asking why they changed their name to Jacob. So, yeah\u2026he hallucinated a conversation with me as if we were out on a job. Twitch said that he wasn\u2019t sure what that was about, but did say that at that point Rook was quite full of various drugs. In light of that I may need to have a conversation with Lowjack in the near future. No one has come to arrest me, so they don\u2019t have any solid proof about me having been a loyalist, they just have the word of a drugged out torture victim. I may want to nip that whole thing in the bud before imaginations get the better of people.<br /> <br /> So, we had stopped the search for the day when Gunnar Friday and Ji Wen Ja came to the Dream House to talk to Calamity about the death of Mr. Grey. They said that there will be a trial and that she can get someone to represent her from the freehold. They said that Master Darke was interested in giving the guilty party a second chance and wanted execution taken off the table, and the Autumn Monarch was all for a non-lethal outcome as well. If execution was off the board the possible options for punishment left were banishment or a strict oath to work for someone in the Winter or Autumn court. They will also determine if Calamity was unstable at the time of the crime or not.<br /> <br /> As a Motley we discussed who we could ask to represent Calamity at the trial on Monday. We decided on Captain Jack. He has been a friend to the Motley and is pretty influential in his own right, so figured he might make a good advocate. Calamity gave him a call and he came over to talk. She explained what was going on and asked if he\u2019d be willing to speak on her behalf. He agreed. In the interest of fairness he did mention that in the past he\u2019d been in a relationship with Lowjack. It had not ended well, but they were friends again now. He said that it should not affect the trial in anyway, but thought it was only fair to mention it. We agreed it was fine, and Calamity made sure that he was still okay defending her.<br /> <br /> We talked for awhile after that about the coronation of the Summer King and all that entailed. Jack said that this started off with a Christian service at the church (where the Summer court is based), and after that there would be a Ren-faire type set-up with tables and vendors and food. Gawain asked about setting up a table at the faire and what was entailed. We arranged to have a table for our good Knight to display the weapons he\u2019s made and for me to show off some of the stuff I\u2019ve done with leather. I will admit that I was eager and a little bit nervous to be showing off my leatherworking, but I wanted to also lend my support to Gawain so we got it all arranged.<br /> <br /> And speaking of arranging things. Jack mentioned his plans for after the Summer coronation. It involves him dressing in a Spider-Man outfit and \u201cstealing\u201d bras from \u201cunsuspecting\u201d ladies throughout the faire with his web-shooters. De la Rocha has already offered herself as a volunteer, as did Lorelei. As far as plans go, I think this one will go about as well as the rest of them have, with flying colors.<br /> <br /> More importantly than plans for stealing underwear, we all planned when Calamity would go to the Winter court\u2019s therapists for help. I mentioned earlier that my court has mortal counselors on staff to help Changelings through any difficulties that they may have. Our plan was that regardless of what was going on, I would escort Calamity to the clinic to seek help. If it looked like others, such as the Monarchs, knew about Calamity\u2019s role in killing Grey then it would be Jack and me that went with her to the clinic. We wanted to make sure that she sought help for her problems before the trial started, but not make a big deal out of it. Calamity doesn\u2019t need the extra scrutiny.<br /> <br /> After Jack left we had another serious conversation. It started somehow by Lorelei apologizing to Calamity for being hard on her the other day for killing Grey. Calamity tried to assure her that it wasn\u2019t necessary, but Lori wouldn\u2019t let her. She explained that she had recently remembered something that reminded her of the whole situation and took it out on Calamity. Apparently while in Arcadia Lori\u2019s Keeper had a contest of sorts going on between the girls. The winner could ask a boon of her. Lori won her freedom this way. Though before that happened other girls were introduced periodically over the years. One girl was named Annabelle. She was very pretty and smart and nice, which made Lori nervous and a bit jealous. Overcome by that jealousy Lorelei and two others snuck up on Annabelle while the new girl slept, and killed her.<br /> <br /> The lot of us then tried to reassure her that she was still a good person and we didn\u2019t blame her. I don\u2019t think any of us said that there was nothing wrong with what she did, but we still don\u2019t think that she is bad. I\u2019m not sure if she believed us or not, but we tried. I can\u2019t say that I haven\u2019t killed out of jealousy, so I\u2019m not one to throw stones. I was usually more jealous of the things that someone had rather than skills they possessed, but it\u2019s a similar enough idea. I think I felt bad the first time I killed someone for that reason, but the feeling wore off. The rest were easy. Granted, I was killing for survival so I pushed a lot of things to the back of my mind while I was doing that, mostly my conscience. It could be argued that Lori was killing for her survival too. Though I\u2019m not the best one to judge her actions against. I just don\u2019t think it was all that bad. I mean, she feels bad about it and obviously wouldn\u2019t do it again. If you ask me I\u2019d say that there were extenuating circumstances. I mean, we\u2019re not even sure what happened to those girls that did not live up to their Keeper\u2019s expectations. It very well could have been a contest where those that failed, died.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Today is the solstice, which means that it is officially summer. As if it wasn\u2019t hot enough here as it was. Earlier today we did a bit more searching for Rook, but even I have to admit that he\u2019s just not here anymore. He\u2019s gone far away by now, and the drugs have probably started to wear off. I hope he is okay. I mean, I know that if he comes back to his senses then I very well may be in trouble, but I just can\u2019t find it in me to worry about that. I worry more that the others might get caught up in the crossfire between us if it comes to that.<br /> <br /> Today is also the day that the reins of power will be transferred from Princess Jolie to Viscount Augustine. So there was the Christian service, which Lorelei and De la Rocha went to. While they were doing that, Gawain and I were setting up our table for the fair. I didn\u2019t realize just how many blades Gawain has made in the past few weeks. The man keeps busy. He had a good selection of swords and knives. I have to give him credit. He is talented. I myself had just a few things to show off. I had made a couple of scabbards for Gawain\u2019s longswords and a couple different styles for knives. Some are meant to be worn on the arm, others the ankle, and still more to be worn at your side. I have not yet made some of the sneakier sheaths, like the one you can keep at the small of your back, or the one to go inside your boot. Those are harder to make and would not likely be well received.<br /> <br /> So, we all dressed up for the Solstice party. I wore the highwayman hedgespun outfit, Gawain wore a tunic and plain pants, and the ladies wore corsets. Oh yeah, there were other articles of clothing to go with them, but there were a lot of corsets. And they did what any good corset does. Luna on the other hand also wore leather, but of the more practical variety. I will admit that though I\u2019m sure she may look good in a corset I\u2019m glad she didn\u2019t wear one. They are not comfortable and I don\u2019t like seeing her feeling so out of her element and looking so miserable. At the Spring court party she looked so unhappy to be wearing those heels, but she did for me. I don\u2019t like it when people are uncomfortable or in pain because of me. So, she wore her leathers, looked good and seemed to feel a lot more comfortable and that\u2019s what really mattered.<br /> <br /> Also at the faire Julia had a table set up and she was selling her art. Some were just sketches of people that she\u2019d seen, but others were sketches of the Dream House and its entertainers. They were really quite good. She is a good artist, no matter the medium. I found myself hoping that she does well selling her art. I know she\u2019d be happy to make a bit of money on the side, but having people appreciate your work is the far better reward.<br /> <br /> When it came time for the actual transfer of power it looked like Jolie was a little bit relieved to be done with the job. Augustine took up the mantle with good grace and humility. He made a speech about the freehold coming together to protect itself and fight off the incursion from the Mothership. I think he wanted to continue to foster that feeling of camaraderie. It seemed to go over well with the rest of the people present though. So, good feelings all around, right?<br /> <br /> Lemme see\u2026what else happened. Oh yes, Juan-Carlos came by the table at one point and wanted to talk to Gawain. Apparently our resident blacksmith is interested in joining an entitlement called the Family of Silent Nights. I didn\u2019t catch a lot of what they said. I think Juan-Carlos said he would come by the Dream House some time this week so he and Gawain can talk more in private about it. I hope that it works out for Gawain. He looked quite interested when Juan-Carlos introduced himself and what he was there to talk about. I mean, Lorelei and most of the ladies seemed quite eager to just ogle the man, but Gawain just wanted to talk to him.<br /> <br /> I had my own conversation about entitlements today as well. I talked to Lowjack about the entitlement that he is a part of. His is called the Knighthood of Utmost Silence. They help people that need to get away from someone or something disappear. I will admit that the idea has a great deal of appeal to me. Not just because I\u2019d like to be able to hide myself, but the idea of keeping folks safe from people like me or Rook has a great deal of appeal. Some people may just need a second chance to start fresh. Others may need to find safety. I can understand both desires all too well. So, if I can help people feel safe, and actually be safe then I think I\u2019d like to be a part of that. I\u2019ve been responsible for hurting so many people, for ruining their lives. I can\u2019t change that. Goddess knows that I wish I could, but I can\u2019t. This may give me the opportunity to help even out the scales just a bit. I know it won\u2019t be enough, it\u2019ll never be enough, but maybe I can make a dent.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> It\u2019s been several days since I have written. Much of the time has been spent trying to find Rook. Unsuccessfully.<br /> <br /> Also, dealing with the Courts coming for Calamity, in the form of Gunnar Friday and Ji Wen Ja. Her death is not being sought by Darke or Lowjack, fortunately. I would not prefer to see her exiled, however.<br /> <br /> Lorelei also revealed her murder of her rival, Annabelle. I knew, of course, but did not say so. Naturally. She blames her Keeper. She is mistaken. She chose to do it. She is not yet ready to accept it. Unfortunately.<br /> <br /> Creepily, the more visceral aspects of Julia\u2019s attraction to her were heightened by this. She was quite eager to get her hands on, and in, Lorelei after her announcement. She did not let it show too much, but I know her well. I have no idea of Lorelei picked up on it.<br /> <br /> Jacob also revealed that he had worked with Rook as partner loyalists, after Twitch visited him. The Winter Court were aware, it seems. Of course, he cased doing so, but still. He still sees Rook as a \u201cpartner\u201d and \u201cbrother.\u201d I wonder if Luna knew.<br /> <br /> Today has been spent preparing for the changing of the leadership to the Summer Court. The Spring Court has had scandals but lead during at least one major Gentry intervention, and that is good I think. Princess Jolie is a lovely woman and an excellent lover. I hope she remains in power. Her fondness for me not being least among the reasons, but still.<br /> <br /> Lorelei went and performed on stage, while De La Rocha stood by looking butch. After one especially hot number, I pointedly went over and kissed her where people could see. I am not ashamed to be involved with Lorelei, after all. While I did not flaunt my relationship with De La Rocha as much, this has a lot to do with her relative discomfort about things, and I took no pains to hide the connection. Naturally.<br /> <br /> As if De La Rocha\u2019s issues were not odd enough, Julia seemed to get bent out of shape by our suggestion she is not \u201cmostly straight.\u201d For one thing, she is sleeping off and on with four women. For a second, her general lust for breasts exceeds any woman I know and is the equal of most men. Then she was apparently insufficiently attracted to a Fairest named Juan-Carlos Hypnos. Juan-Carlos is handsome enough to even get my attention, though I had heard of him from Flores. He wears a tie well. Julia was little attracted. Which is fine with me, but not her apparently.<br /> <br /> Julia has never dated a man. Kissed a boy once as a tween. She went to bed with me the first night she met me, and all but moved in in less than a week, then did move in after about a month or so. She eagerly availed herself of Lorelei and De La Rocha when I seduced them, and changed from \u201cShe is my good friend and it would be weird\u201d to \u201cfull on lesbian\u201d when Flores took her top off. Then Julia was not at all turned on my Juan-Carlos. Julia is not, has not ever been, and never will be \u201cmostly straight.\u201d So what, pardon my American, is her damn problem? She was not raised religious, her parents are (apparently) queer friendly enough she does not anticipate a problem with me meeting them if I ever decide I must go to Anaheim, but she was in tears because we don\u2019t believe she is \u201cmostly straight.\u201d<br /> <br /> I do not understand. Unfortunately.<br /> <br /> I got sidetracked. Okay so Julia was selling paintings and doing sketches while keeping me nearby stealing kisses. We sold a few of some of the girls, including Lorelei, to locals, and had fun chatting. Definitely.<br /> <br /> Gawain set up shop with Calamity hanging around nearby chatting with Joan and Andromeda, Captain Jack (who he did a Spiderman thing with involving running around on rooftops), Juan-Carlos, and others. Everyone seemed to have a good time.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXXI</i><br /> <br /> The conversation between Jacob and Twitch was pretty interesting in game. Twitch was immediately rather popular for his awkward, matter of fact way of talking about terrifying things. Also his use of \u201cHigh as balls.\u201d Of course, in game only Jacob dealt with him and he was not happy, but there was a couple \u201cJacob is not laughing at this\u201d or \u201cI am not there right? Tell me I can\u2019t hear this.\u201d<br /> <br /> The logistics of Rook\u2019s flight meant that the PCs were not likely to be able to find him, so we just sort of handwaved some time passing to deal with it. This brought us to the Solstice faster than anticipated, but that was okay.<br /> <br /> Comments and Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T23:33:02-07:00","id":568876,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time for the Courts to decide Calamity\u2019s fate. Also drama out of nowhere. That is best* drama.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXXII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> June 22nd<br /> <br /> So today has been about the longest day ever. It\u2019s been the longest weekend ever, for that matter, you know? Saturday at least had the coronation for a distraction. There was a little bit of a distraction at the show today, but it wasn\u2019t anything nearly as positive, and has made Calamity even more mopey.<br /> <br /> The sparring was good, at least. Jacob and Calamity sparred. I did a solo work out alongside them, but I didn\u2019t really feel like going up against either of them. I mean, my temper\u2019s been under control these last few days and everything, but I dunno. I just wasn\u2019t feeling it. We did make a good distraction for Lori's rehearsal, anyway, for her Midsummer's Night Dream thing, you know, but she kept them on task, mostly.<br /> <br /> Then there was the show. It went well, as a show, you know, and a lot of our regulars were there. Monica brought a new arrival by, named Dominica. She\u2019s really pretty. We all stopped by to say hi, and you know, talk up our Courts. Not me, really, cause I figured Lucian and his bunch wouldn't take it too kindly, and besides, she was looking super overwhelmed anyway. Insincere Marguerite was being really flirty, which made Monica uncomfortable, but like I told Monica when she asked me to ask my motley-mate to stop, that would probably just make it worse. I don\u2019t think she wound up picking her up or anything.<br /> <br /> Calamity left that conversation at some point to do her rounds, but then came back almost right away and pulled me aside. See, White Maria and Dark Kimberly had come in together and now were fighting kinda intensely (in Chinese). Even better, White Maria was armed again. Calamity was wondering if my Contract of Potential could help figure out, you know, what was up, since they were being all tight-lipped about it.<br /> <br /> I started off trying to figure out White Maria\u2019s motivations in the argument, but came up blank. I really need to get better at that Contract. Dark Kimberly at least was easier to read - she wanted White Maria to back off on her accusation, which was that Dark Kimberly had let someone die. Not, like, killed someone, but maybe coulda stopped it, if she tried? It was kinda fuzzy. I tried White Maria again, this time about the gun, and that was super clear. She was afraid that someone (not Dark Kimberly) was out to kill her. Also, it occurred to her that if Annika blew up about her accusing Dark Kimberly, maybe the gun would get the dancer to back off.<br /> <br /> There was far too many someone/things in what we figured out, so Calamity decided she would talk with Dark Kimberly if they split up at some point, and I could talk with White Maria. My talk didn\u2019t go so great. White Maria did agree to leave her gun at the bar, so, you know, not a wash, but she wouldn\u2019t tell me anything about who was after her except that no one had ever hassled her here, that she was sticking to public, well lit spaces at night and that it had been a rough couple of weeks.<br /> <br /> Calamity\u2019s went worse, cause Dark Kimberly just took off from the bathroom out the door. Calamity was following her, and White Maria got up to follow too, and I followed her. I mostly just wanted to make sure neither of them snapped and went for the other, but when I saw the shadows deepen, you know, like when the Contract of Darkness is used, I moved in close. White Maria fussed at me for it, until I mentioned about the Contract, and then she panicked. I managed to catch her before she ran blindly into the road, or off a cliff or something and carried her inside and up to the TV room.<br /> <br /> I got one of the kitchen crew to grab Jacob for me, and he went to look for tracks, once I filled him on what I saw. We eventually got White Maria to tell us some more of what was up. After the initial panicky bit, she definitely got her dignity back on and didn\u2019t really wanna talk about it. But once we got her to start, she told us pretty much the whole story, I think.<br /> <br /> A Changeling named Sundown, a mutual friend of White Maria and Dark Kimberly, was killed in a gang hit a few years ago. White Maria hired an investigator to look into in and found out that Dark Kimberly had supposedly known about the upcoming hit and not warned her. Since White Maria had figured this out (and from before she confronted Dark Kimberly about it), she\u2019d been attacked a couple of times, well, three times now, always hearing a whistle just before. She said she heard it tonight, but we didn\u2019t. She gotten a glimpse of her attacker at some point and figured it was either a darkling or a humanish looking hobgoblin. It had attacked her out of her bathroom mirror, and from a car driving next to her, with long reaching arms.<br /> <br /> By the time we\u2019d gotten all that, Jacob had gotten a good look around, so it seemed as safe as it could be for her to head out. We still escorted her to her car anyway. There can\u2019t be too many people with that set of skills. Hopefully Calamity\u2019s inquiries will turn something up.<br /> <br /> She did come out of the whole mess worse for wear though. She said Dark Kimberly had been acting really scared of her when she was just trying to see what was up, and you know, if she could help. I tried to convince her it was just guilt, if White Maria was right, or nervousness cause of the accusations, even if she wasn\u2019t. Dark Kimberly had apparently had a bad couple of week too, so she was probably just stressed and scared in general. Why else would Dark Kimberly have to be scared of Calamity?<br /> <br /> June 23rd<br /> <br /> The trial is over and went well, I guess? I didn\u2019t punch Darke, it wasn\u2019t long and drawn out or anything, and everybody was really supportive. The sentence wasn\u2019t just a slap on the wrist, but it wasn\u2019t, you know, onerous or anything. She had to take a Pledge to not kill any Changeling in good standing with the freehold, not even in self-defense. She could still fight in self-defense, but since she\u2019s so awesome with knives, they figured should should be able to non-lethally. She also has to give a glamour a month to the Winter Monarch and was drafted to work with a handler (a new to town Winter courtier named Dahlia) to defend the freehold along with Darke.<br /> <br /> The trial itself was pretty open and shut, like I said. We did learn that Captain Jack\u2019s proper full name is Joaquin Martinez. He was a bit put off by the fact that darklings, and darklings only, have an advocate in Madame Spidertoes, who has to approve any trial and sentencing of darklings, so that they are treated fairly. It was kinda weird, but apparently she always approves.<br /> <br /> There were lots of speeches during the character witness part of things. Lori\u2019s was really, super beautiful and Insincere Marguerite, Jacob and Julia were all really eloquent too. I kinda stumbled over my words, but I\u2019m not so good with words anyway. And it all worked out - I at least didn\u2019t screw anything up by, you know, punching the fuck out of the creepy bastard Darke when he started talking about second chances. Jacob did have a restraining hand on my shoulder, but I was able to content myself with staring daggers at him.<br /> <br /> So now that\u2019s all behind us, and we\u2019re about to settle in for bourbon, ice cream and movies. Insincere Marguerite picked both this time: Eraserhead and Barton Fink. I\u2019ve never seen either, so this should be interesting, since she has very eclectic tastes, you know?<br /> <br /> Later<br /> <br /> what the ever loving fuck just what that was i mean jesus not enough bourbon oh god why<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> So after the events of my last entry, the Summer King\u2019s coronation wound down and people started to head home. Our evening didn\u2019t end there, however, as my three darklings spent rather longer than was necessary removing my outfit when we got home. In fact, Julia offered to put the corset back on me after everything else had been taken off, but I declined her offer in favor of breathing freely for the rest of the evening.<br /> <br /> Well\u2026 relatively freely, anyway.<br /> <br /> Suffice to say, I didn\u2019t get much rest Saturday night, and Sunday morning services rolled around right on schedule, so I used the Contracts of Eternal Spring to give myself a little more energy. As always, it was a beautiful sermon filled with light and love and music, and I felt better about my life just for having sat through it.<br /> <br /> That afternoon we had a rehearsal scheduled for \u201cA Midsummer Night\u2019s Dream,\u201d so I didn\u2019t get much of a chance to relax. The production is coming along nicely, I think. It\u2019s nowhere near ready yet, but we still have about four weeks before the performance, so I\u2019m hopeful that we\u2019ll be able to get everyone in line with time to spare.<br /> <br /> We rehearse outside, of course, and there were plenty of distractions. Jacob and Calamity decided to spar for a bit, and Gawain was out there practicing with that gigantic sword of his as well. I had to keep reminding the cast that we were on the clock just to keep them from staring. I love my motley, but I have to remind myself that not everyone is used to seeing people practicing sword and knife fighting in their backyards on a Sunday afternoon.<br /> <br /> In no time at all it was time to hit the showers and prepare for the show. Since many of my cast members are also regular performers at the dream house, available bathrooms were running a little scarce. I offered to share my shower with Genevieve (one of our regular backup singers), but she just blushed and muttered something about waiting for the next one. Oh well\u2026 her loss. I could tell how much she wanted me anyway, and that was enough for the moment.<br /> <br /> As I had promised, I performed John Lennon\u2019s \u201cJulia\u201d for one of my numbers tonight, as a tribute to one of my girlfriends. She rolled her eyes at the sentimentality of it, and I know it\u2019s not really her kind of music, but I think she appreciated the gesture anyway.<br /> <br /> After my last song, I mingled with the audience as per usual. Most of our regulars were there, and I stopped by to say hello to many of them. Dark Kimberly and White Maria seemed to be having some sort of argument (in Chinese, so I have no idea what it was about), but I think Calamity and Gawain sorted it out before things went too far.<br /> <br /> Monica had brought someone new to the Dream House tonight, a recent arrival named Dominica. She was a very pretty black girl \u2013 I think she was a Fairest \u2013 and seemed nice enough, aside from the fact that she was obviously a little overwhelmed by the complexities of Freehold society. Each of the motley dropped by to say hello and to talk up the virtues of our courts. I think each of us hoped to recruit her to our respective courts, though of course we were all quick to point out that it\u2019s much more important for her to find the court that\u2019s <u>right</u> for her.<br /> <br /> Marguerite was flirting with Dominica pretty shamelessly. She explained later that this was mostly because the Summer Court had tried to stop her from doing so. I\u2019m not sure why\u2026 maybe they were worried that she\u2019d recruit Dominica for the Night Court in L.A. or something. In any case, my French lover was laying on the charm pretty thick when I dropped by, and while Dominica was responsive, it was obvious that it was all a bit much for her to deal with at the moment. So after I\u2019d said my hellos and made her feel as welcome as I could, I meandered away to give her some space.<br /> <br /> I really did try to explain to her why I chose to join the Spring Court. I tried to tell her how we use desire to better understand people so that we can help them, but I\u2019m not sure it really got across. I hope I didn\u2019t come off sounding like too much of a vapid nymphomaniac.<br /> <br /> I made the rounds, chatted with a few of the (mortal) regulars, posed for a couple of photos, and to no one\u2019s great surprise ended up at a table with D, Julia, Flores, and Oleander. After giving my sweetie a kiss, I darted significant glances at Oleander and Flores, and D nodded slightly in understanding. She whispered something to Julia, and the two of them began running interference with Flores while I planted myself in a seat next to Oleander.<br /> <br /> She was certainly in high spirits. I almost didn\u2019t recognize her as the same person; she was light and happy and carefree, fun and flirtatious. I found myself talking and laughing without really thinking about what was going on around me. She\u2019d had her hand on my knee for about three minutes when I realized that I was being seduced\u2026 and that she was doing a very good job, too. I guess she just needed a little time free of Flores\u2019 interference to come out of her shell.<br /> <br /> Once Marguerite had finished chatting up the new girl, she, D, Julia, and Flores went upstairs together. The house had pretty much emptied out by that point, so I turned toward Oleander, leaned in, and kissed her hard on the mouth. \u201cYou want to get out of here?\u201d I whispered once we had separated.<br /> <br /> She nodded and licked her lips nervously. \u201cWould you like to see my place?\u201d she asked. <br /> <br /> I indicated that I would love to, and about two minutes later she was driving me up the Pacific Coast Highway at speeds that bordered on reckless. My skirt was hiked up, her hand was <u>really</u> high up on my thigh, and the only reason I wasn\u2019t all over her was because of my very real fear that we would plummet into the Pacific Ocean if I distracted her any more.<br /> <br /> Once back at her place, we didn\u2019t waste a lot of time on preliminaries. After her first orgasm, she told me it was amazing. After her second, she told me I was incredible. After her third, it was that she\u2019d never met anyone like me. Every last compliment was like a shot of fine whiskey to me. I got drunk on her\u2026 and on her admiration for me. We fell asleep spent, exhausted, sweaty, and tangled in her bed sheets.<br /> <br /> I woke up alone the next morning, but I knew Oleander hadn\u2019t gone far. For one thing, the big softie had put the covers over me when she got up., and they were still relatively cool. For another, I could smell frying bacon wafting in from the kitchen. So I sat up, stretched, spread my wings, and walked naked in that direction.<br /> <br /> Oleander stood in front of the stove with her back to me. She was wearing a T-shirt and an apron. Two frying pans sat on the burners; one held scrambled eggs, the other sizzling bacon. A plate next to the stove was piled high with toast. I cleared my throat softly to let her know I was there, and she turned her head and smiled shyly. I walked up behind her and put my arms around her, pressing myself up against her back.<br /> <br /> \u201cMorning, gorgeous,\u201d she said, turning her head to give me a lingering kiss.<br /> <br /> \u201cMorning yourself,\u201d I breathed. \u201cYou know you didn\u2019t have to make me breakfast.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know,\u201d she said, darting in for another quick kiss, \u201cI wanted to. Last night was\u2026 special.\u201d I saw it in her eyes then\u2026 that gleam. That warmth. That <u>light</u>. I knew I should say something. I knew I should caution her\u2026 warn her against becoming too attached. But in the end, God help me, I just couldn\u2019t. I need to see that light in people\u2019s eyes when they look at me. I <u>need</u> it.<br /> <br /> I slid my hand down the front of her body, past the hem of her shirt. She gasped, and giggled a little bit. \u201cStop, unless you want me to burn the eggs,\u201d she said without much conviction.<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay,\u201d I pouted, backing off a bit, \u201cwe\u2019ll save something for next time.\u201d Her eyes lit up again at that. The eggs didn\u2019t burn, and they were delicious.<br /> <br /> Oleander gave me a ride back to the Dream House after breakfast, and left me with a kiss on the doorstep. I changed into some comfortable clothes and set about preparing for Calamity\u2019s trial. Mostly that involved organizing the performers to make sure the show would be okay without us\u2026 but as it was a Monday night anyway, our regular singers and dancers were used to going it alone.<br /> <br /> The trial itself was relatively short and simple. I dressed in one of my nice church ensembles \u2013 a sober button-up shirt and skirt combination \u2013 but didn\u2019t bother with the ponytail or glasses. I wanted to look nice without going for a sexy or seductive look, and I hope I managed to pull it off.<br /> <br /> We met with Captain Jack \u2013 or should I say \u201cJoaquin Martinez,\u201d which is apparently his real name \u2013 before the trial proper, and he explained how things would go. The charges would be read by the monarchs in front of interested parties from the Freehold. Then Madame Spidertoes would give her consent to the trial, which is a little weird. Apparently the Freehold officially defers to her in legal matters involving Darklings as a courtesy, but she never dissents.<br /> <br /> Anyway, after that Captain Jack would speak on Calamity\u2019s behalf, and she\u2019d be allowed to plead her own case. Then, character witnesses would be brought forward to speak for her. The monarchs would deliberate, and a verdict and sentence would be announced. Of course, in this case Calamity wasn\u2019t contesting the charges, so only the sentencing was in question.<br /> <br /> And that\u2019s pretty much how it went. Jack and Calamity spoke about how she did what she did based on a desire to protect her motley, and that she understood she took it too far. They brought up that she was already seeking help for her problem\u2026 she had gone by the Winter Court\u2019s clinic that morning and set up a series of appointments with an enchanted mortal psychiatrist.<br /> <br /> Darke wasn\u2019t afraid to throw his two cents in\u2026 though the slimeball found a way to support Calamity\u2019s position while still defending his own by stating that he \u201chas always believed in second chances.\u201d I thought Gawain was going to sock him one for a few minutes there, but the big lug managed to keep his emotions under control.<br /> <br /> Pretty much everyone in the motley spoke up on Calamity\u2019s behalf, which I guess surprised no one\u2026 that\u2019s what motleys are supposed to do, right? Some of us were clever, citing precedent and enumerating reasons, while others spoke plainly but passionately about how important Calamity was to us and to the Freehold. When my turn to testify came up, I Atticus Finched the hell out of that testimony. Don\u2019t get me wrong, I wasn\u2019t thinking of it as a performance per se\u2026 channeling all of the best courtroom dramas I\u2019d ever seen just sort of put me in the right frame of mind. I hope it helped.<br /> <br /> Close friends of the motley like Julia and Luna spoke up too. D didn\u2019t say anything. That surprised me at first\u2026 I <u>know</u> she was worried about Calamity, and I <u>know</u> she wanted to help. But then I saw her dart her eyes nervously at Twitch, and I understood. She was afraid that he would recognize her voice. She was afraid that he would know that she\u2019s the \u201cMaria\u201d that still haunts his memory. So I took her hand and gave it a squeeze to let her know that I understood.<br /> <br /> In the end, the sentence wasn\u2019t nearly as bad as it could have been. In light of Calamity\u2019s sincere desire to get help, the monarchs have instated a pledge with three conditions. First, Calamity must defend the Freehold when called upon to do so. No worries there; she\u2019d have done that anyway. Second, she must not kill any member of the Freehold in good standing, not even in self-defense. She <u>can</u> defend herself, but she\u2019s not allowed to use lethal force in those instances. Again, I don\u2019t really see a problem here, as she\u2019s a good enough fighter to incapacitate her enemies without killing them if necessary, and the imposed restraint will probably do her good. Finally, she must donate a small portion of her glamour to the Winter Court each month as a token punitive penalty.<br /> <br /> It was better than we could have hoped for, and I know Calamity was pleased. Lowjack escorted her and Jacob into a back room and introduced them to Dahlia, who will be her \u201chandler,\u201d or the person who will be handing out her assignments in the defense of the Freehold. I take it that she\u2019s one of Lowjack\u2019s supporters from out of town, as I\u2019ve never seen her before. Calamity seems to get along well with her, though.<br /> <br /> So the trial was over so quickly that we still had time for our traditional Monday movie night. I suggested on the way home that we stop for ice cream (and bourbon), and the rest of the group agreed. Insincere Marguerite picked the films this time. I might have known that her choices would be\u2026 unconventional. <u>Eraserhead</u> and <u>Barton Fink</u>. I\u2019d never heard of either film, and I\u2019m not sure what to make of them.<br /> <br /> <u>Eraserhead</u> was so surreal and incomprehensible that I\u2019m afraid I spent most of my time concentrating on the ice cream (and bourbon). <u>Barton Fink</u> seemed to be a bit more coherent, but I confess that by that point I\u2019d consumed a bit more ice cream (and bourbon) than was strictly good for me, and I found myself \u201cdistracted\u201d by D, Julia, and Marguerite.<br /> <br /> Much of the rest of the night is a blur to me after we put away the ice cream (but not the bourbon). I do remember two little tidbits of conversation before things degenerated into pure debauchery, though. First, D seems pretty happy that she finally gave in to the inevitable and slept with Flores. \u201cThe next time you get a chance with her, you should take it,\u201d she said fervently. I didn\u2019t ask for details. I admit that the teeniest tiniest part of me was a little jealous to hear her talk that way about someone else, but I know how hypocritical that is, and I know in my heart that D loves me more than anyone else, so I ignored it.<br /> <br /> Second, I announced my intentions for the following night. \u201cJuan-Carlos Hypnos is coming to the next show to speak with Gawain,\u201d I told my girlfriends in a smoky voice. \u201cI intend to seduce him after they\u2019ve had their talk. If he\u2019s into it, would any of you be interested in joining us?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> D turned to face the other two. \u201cSorry girls, looks like I\u2019m going to have plans tomorrow night,\u201d she said with a grin. It\u2019s weird... in the past she\u2019s been pretty firmly against the idea of the two of us sharing a guy, but she jumped on this opportunity. Then again, Juan-Carlos is ridiculously hot. Maybe it\u2019s nothing more than that. In any case, I fully intend to enjoy this experience.<br /> <br /> You know, assuming Juan-Carlos <u>wants</u> to have sex with us, of course. I guess there\u2019s only one way to find out.<br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei Grace</b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T23:33:33-07:00","id":568877,"title":"","content":"<b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> <b><u>Monday June 23<sup>th</sup></u></b><br /> <br /> It's done and since I'm writing this I guess it's clear that I survived my night in court. Honestly, it could have gone much worse for me. See the whole still alive part there. Everyone came with me to show their support, which meant a lot to me. I know that no one fully agreed with what I did (and some where decidedly against it) but they stood by me anyway. Captain Jack met us when we arrived and laid out what we should expect. Given that the issue of my guilt wasn't in question, it was all pretty straightforward. None of the monarchs had it out for me. Not even Augustine with his reputation for being uncompromising in matters of justice was hostile.<br /> <br /> The trial began with the monarchs asking for Madam Spidertoes permission to try one of her people. This is apparently something unique to Darklings, as Jack pointed out more than once. He also added that she has never declined and he's pretty sure no one knows what would happen if she did. I guess it's just a courtesy they extend to her on account to her age and power. Both Darke and Twitch were present on Grey's behalf and both confirmed that they did not seek my death. Darke took the opportunity to rub in his smarmy claims of second chances and look smug. For a moment I thought Jacob might have to try to physically restrain Gawain from hitting the bastard but Handsome kept his rage in check. Twitch seemed nervous as usual and from his reaction to the question I have little doubt that his private thoughts on my fate are less charitable than his public stance. But it's too damn late now and if he doesn't have the balls to call me out and speak up for his friend then fuck him. As the testimony began, we learned that Captain Jack's real name is apparently Joaquin Martinez. As my representative, He spoke first. He explained that he believed that I am genuine in my acceptance of my problem and my desire to seek help in gaining more control over my darker impulses. And he brought up my visit to the clinic and as evidence of both. Then they opened the floor to anyone else who wished to speak on my behalf. Julia told them that I was the reason she slept safely. Then the whole motley each took their turns. What some of them lacked in polish, they made up for with heartfelt sentiment. It was touching and a little hard to listen to Gawain speak. I could feel how badly he wanted to say the right things and his frustration at not finding the right words to do his feelings justice. Even if it didn't sway the monarchs, it certainly stuck me. I don't know why or how someone like him can love someone as unworthy as me but he does and if he's not going to give up on me then I am just going to have to find a way to become the kind of woman he deserves. Lori spoke last and when she did she held the room captive. She was eloquent and genuine and fuck, even I was ready to forgive me when she finished.<br /> <br /> With all the testimony heard, the monarchs (and Spidertoes, who again had to give her consent to my punishment) retired to decide my fate. Honestly, they weren't at it all that long but when you're waiting for your sentence every second is a fucking eternity. <br /> <br /> When they did return, they made it abundantly clear that they couldn't let me off too easy and I get that. You can't control people if they don't fear the repercussions of breaking the rules. The sentence was far from onerous. I swore to not kill any member of the Freehold for any reason, not even in defense of myself or another. I must tithe a glamour to the Winter monarch each month. I must take part in defending the Freehold. Given that I don't fully trust my self control the ban is a good idea and they're right that I am good enough to disable someone without killing them even if I don't fucking want to. The glamour is punitive but honestly no more than a minor inconvenience. And I have made my willingness and desire to use my abilities to protect the others clear. If Lowjack (That's BOSS Lowjack now) wasn't such a decent sort it might be a problem but when he spoke to me about the details of it he was unfailingly reasonable. Hell, I've only just met my new handler Dahlia and I like her already. She's no nonsense and pragmatic and thinks Darke is a creepy fucker. <br /> <br /> So why am I feeling so damn pissy? I dodged a fucking bullet and got what I wanted. I have no right to feel anything but fucktons of relief (Metric fucktons even, they're bigger than Imperial ones after all...) So where is this fucking sense of discontent coming from? Hell's bells I wasn't this petulant when I was an actual child. And the last thing I need to be doing right now is acting ungrateful in the face of the monarchs' gesture of leniency. But despite how reasonable it all is, the sheer fact that I'm on a leash now is chapping my ass like an overdue diaper. I knew it was going to be irritating but I didn't expect it to bother me this much. Fuck, the worst part is I FUCKING know it's the best deal I could have expected and it's a gorram good one. Hell, they literally let me get away with fucking murder with pretty much nothing more than: \u201cNow now... Don't do that again.\u201d If I was someone that knew and liked Grey I'd be pissed at how much of a slap on the wrist it really is. And I didn't miss Twitch's comment in court. I can't say I blame him for talking about me behind my back. Maybe I should remind him that I can't kill him and ask him how he really feels sometime. Of course, the fun part would be pointing out just what I can do without killing him after he's said his piece. Pity that I can't feed on another Changeling's fear sometimes.<br /> <br /> Fuck, I guess I've got something to talk to the doctor about tomorrow already. Yeah, I am conflicted about that shit. On the one hand, I fucking need help getting my shit the fuck together. On the other... holy fucking shit I am fucked the hell up and I'm supposed to tell some total stranger all about that? I can't even have a conversation with Gawain about some of this shit and he's been inside my gorram head and seen it firsthand. I get that a fellow Changeling isn't really equipped to help me regain my grasp of what is real and what is lingering Arcadian fever dream but what human can even begin to grok the magnitude of being in a place like Snow Globe or the Lady's Realm or the Empress' cages? Of being at the mercy of something that can literally twist your flesh and soul like clay? How can this doctor even begin to understand what the glass is or what it means to me? I'm not his first Changeling (Jeez, I sure hope I'm not his first) but we're all unique special fucking snowflakes aren't we? And even if he (or she... all I've got is a name after all) knows something about Arcadia, there hasn't been a survivor from Snow Globe here in a human lifespan. Fuck. I just don't know what the hell to expect and that pisses me off and worries me. I don't know what I'm fucking doing. What if I fuck this shit up? What sane person is going to listen to the fucking nightmare fuel in my head and willingly be trapped alone in a soundproof room with me?<br /> <br /> Maybe it's just that I am completely fucking tapped on glamour that's making me so cranky. Last week was pretty fucking shitastic all around and I didn't really have a chance to grab more than a pinch here and there.<br /> <br /> Because when it rains it fucking pours you know. After the Mothership's attack, Twitch came by to talk to Jacob. I was talking to Gawain at the time, trying to explain how while I was not fighting the courts I wasn't surrendering either. Damn, the man loves me. Even at my worst. Even when we both know I'm wrong. It scares the fuck out of me how willingly he'd follow me into the very mouth of Hell. But that's why I have to get better. I have to become the sort of woman who deserves his love and devotion.<br /> <br /> Things had started to lighten up when Jacob walked past us and started laying into one of the doors without a word. Even in his rage the man's quiet and stoic. Needless to say, none of us were going to let this go without some questions. I've known for a while that Jacob's carrying guilt over things he did before. Well, that all came to something of a head. It seems he used to be a loyalist in the worst way. Not simply obedient to his Keeper within her realm but one of the agents who brought her new victims or tracked and returned escaped Lost. I can't blame him for being afraid to open up to us about that but I know him. I trust him. That person, that Rime, is as dead and gone as Jane. But the loyalist that escaped during the attack was Rook, his former partner. He admitted that he still feels strongly for the man, thinks of him like a brother. A brother that he feels deserves an actual second chance. We all agreed.<br /> <br /> The problem is that Twitch had detailed some of the horrific tortures they'd employed on 'Subject 61' and the lingering drug and psychological effects. He wanted to find Rook before they could and try to give him a real opportunity to be free of their Keeper. The motley readily agreed to look. I think Jacob was concerned what we'd think about him having compassion for a loyalist but in his own words this man was like a brother to him for years. You can't just turn that shit off because you've left that world behind. I used my contracts. Luna scoured the woods. We all spent hours combing the areas he'd have been likely drawn to hide in but to no avail. At this point, it is clear that Rook is no longer in the area. At least he avoided the Winter Court's people as well. I am sure we've not seen the last of him. For Jacob's sake, I honestly hope Rook can be freed from the Lady's grasp. If not, at least I can see the man receives a clean death.<br /> <br /> So as our fruitless and frustrating third day of that was underway the Dream House was visited by Gunnar Friday and Ji Wen Ja. They had come for me but as I'd made my intentions clear already so it was a rather civil affair. They informed me that the Courts would convene Monday and made me pledge not to flee the city. They also let me know that as no one, not even Darke (who claims to believe in second chances...) was pressing for my death so that wasn't on the table. Then they departed and left us to our preparations.<br /> <br /> I told them all that I intended to seek help, that I understood that the damage the Voices had done ran deeper than I realized and that I didn't know how to fix it. It wasn't easy to admit it to them all and I didn't really try to hide how pathetic it made me feel. Lori looked guilty and tried to be encouraging. She tried to apologize for some of the things she'd said but I waved her off. But she continued, explaining that it was the emerging memory that was fueling her words and then she explained more about the outburst she'd had the night of the Mothership's attack.<br /> <br /> Her Keeper had a contest, one that she and her friends had pledged to win and use the boon to ask for their freedom. That much she'd told us before, but apparently there had been other songbirds. One in particular had been (in her mind at least) prettier and more talented. Annabelle had been her name, a platinum blonde with pure white wings, as angelic in temperament as appearance. I can't help but wonder if the guilt has smoothed over the flaws but I do imagine the girl was an innocent. That seems to be the Empress' preference in victims after all. And one night, consumed with jealousy, Lori spurred her friends and the three of them fell upon poor Annabelle and murdered her quite brutally. It was clearly hard for her to tell and even once we all started to assure her we didn't hold what she'd done in Arcadia against her she protested. She said she was petty and jealous and pointed out her dislike of Annika as proof. We all tried to convince her that we didn't think of her as a bad person but I don't think she believed it. I think I had the same look that night when I told the motley about my parents. Nothing we said was going to sway her opinion of herself. Maybe I should try to talk to her about it one on one at some point. Zod knows there are plenty of folks better at that than me but I do grok what it's like having something dark inside and maybe it will help.<br /> <br /> From there, things drifted back to my impending fate. The issue of a representative had been brought up before and it came up again. The whole motley made it clear they wanted to be there to support me and it was comforting to hear. I did consider asking Lori to speak for me but, as I explained to her, I didn't think the Monarchs would weigh her words as heavily given that she is my motley-mate. She readily agreed that she was far from impartial and when I announced that it was my intention to ask Captain Jack she and the others thought it was a good idea. He's well respected and has a solid reputation and is as neutral in court politics as you can get. Of course, that meant calling him and asking him.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I started and stopped dialing that number a few times. Jack is a good man, one of the best I know. He's one of the few people who I actually give a fuck about his opinion of me. He agreed to come to the house indicating that he had intended to to anyway to discuss plans for the upcoming Summer Coronation.<br /> <br /> Once he arrived, I laid out my situation and waited. Jack informed me that he was a friend and he didn't revoke that lightly, even if he didn't agree with what I'd done. Then he set to going over what he knew about these things and what we should do. He also informed me that he and John Lowjack had been lovers and it had ended badly. Not that it was still bad and he didn't think it would effect things but it was fair disclosure. I told him I still wanted him there. Jack agreed that the fact that I had already planned to seek counseling was good (and not just for the sake of my case I'm sure.) He suggested that I should go ahead and get that underway beforehand so it would show my intention rather than just saying I was going to. Since it was late on Friday, we decided to go Monday morning. There was some discussion of who, if anyone, should go with me. Since it wasn't yet common knowledge I picked just Jacob, since the Clinic is his court's headquarters. Jack said that he was willing and that it it did leak he'd be there as well, but otherwise we agreed that keeping it low profile might be better.<br /> <br /> From there, Jack managed to lighten the mood without downplaying the seriousness of my situation. I'm realizing that his antics are often not as random as they seem. I mean, he did spend quite a bit of the Masquerade Ball insuring that the handmaidens were too occupied to cause trouble. Saturday was the solstice and thus the passing of the crown from Princess Jolie to Viscount Augustine. Jack had plans (of course) and he wanted Gawain to be part of them. And between that and the abrupt realization that there was a major social function that would require new dresses and such the mood was fairly high for the remainder of the day.<br /> <br /> The coronation proper was preceded by a religious service (Augustine is a rather Godly sort after all). Lori chose to attend and her girl went with her. I opted to help Gawain set up the tent he'd borrowed from Captain Jack to showcase and sell some of his metalwork. Jacob brought out his leather-work as well. The latter portion of the event was something of an open air almost Ren Faire sort of thing. The others seemed to enjoy it but I stayed mostly in the tent with the boys. I tried not to be too glum but I just wasn't feeling much like being social. I did speak to Andromeda a bit, who was both quite pleased and a bit drained from using the Table to remove Joan's curse. I expressed some concerns about the Table and how it had affected Grey but she'd already decided that she didn't want to use the thing any more than absolutely necessary. I know that means helping Jolie and she and Lori spoke privately to arrange that.<br /> <br /> We had another interesting visitor, a Spring Courtier by the name of Juan-Carlos Hypnos. He is certainly a handsome man and rocked the whole tie and shirtless look quite well even if he was a pair of disembodied cuffs short of the full Chippendale. In addition to flirting quite skillfully with with all of the ladies (myself included) he was there to speak to Gawain about the Family of Silent Nights. He is interested in sponsoring Gawain and arraigned to come to the Dream House Tuesday night to speak to him at greater length about it. Lori has since made it quite clear that she intends to seduce the man (or die trying, might be spending too much time with Ace) and De la Rocha is planning to be there with them. I can't say I blame them but I'm not going to even think of competing and besides, it would be weird when he's evaluating Gawain for his Entitlement.<br /> <br /> And speaking of my Knight, he's been amazing through all of this. I really hope his meeting goes well. I know this is something that means a lot to him. He spent so long in Arcadia destroying, it's important to him to create. Whether it's through his forge or Oneiromancy and even more, being able to help people with it. I think I'm going to ask him if I can help when he goes back to work on Desiree's trigger. I do know my way around a dream and it's a way I can do something good. It would be good to share something like that with him.<br /> <br /> Yesterday was interesting. Lori went to church and afterward at breakfast Jacob asked me if I wanted to spar. I guess my agitation was showing. At any rate, I was more than happy for the chance to unwind and thanked him immediately for the suggestion. Gawain joined us, though he was working solo with his sword.<br /> <br /> I wasted no time and threw myself into it full tilt from the get go. Jacob wasted no time in matching my pace. I think we both had some serious tension and frustration to work out and we danced hard and fast. I think we might have distracted Lori's rehearsal a bit with our display but at the time it just felt so fucking glorious to let go of everything for a while. We've both gotten better, learning more of the others style and incorporating parts of it into our own. We went back and forth a good while before I managed to lure him in with a feint. I confess, it felt good to see him commit. To know that I'd pulled it off against someone so skilled. I slipped in and banished my glass to use just my fingers to brush the vital artery on the inside of his thigh lightly. I guess it might have seemed a little flirtatious especially with the wink I gave him. And maybe it was just a bit. There is a very real intimacy to intense sparring and sparring with someone like Jacob or Luna who fights the same way I do is always intense. It's a shame that Gawain and I fight so differently. While we have some good workouts together, it's just not as well matched when we spar. I felt much more relaxed as we were cooling down and Jacob seemed to as well. It was one of our best sessions and I'm glad for the timing. I know he has to be worried that despite what everyone said that we're seeing him differently now. But actions speak louder than words so hopefully he could see that my trust in him isn't any less than before.<br /> <br /> Sadly, the night wasn't as positive. The show went well but White Maria showed up armed (again) and with Dark Kimberly. But the usual friendly vibe was missing completely. They say at a back table and argued. I can't speak Chinese but I didn't have to understand the words to pick up on the tension and hostile tones. I tried to approach them and ask if things where alright but they both just shut down and mumbled that they were fine and waited for me to go away so they could resume.<br /> <br /> I called upon Gawain and his contract. I used a bit of Autumn magic as well. He determined that Maria's intent for being armed was to protect herself from her stalker and possibly from Annika and not to harm Kimberly. When Kimberly got up to use the restroom, I followed her and Gawain moved to have a word with Maria and ask her to leave her gun with Jacob. Clearly, there needs to be some sort of official policy about weapons in the Dream House.<br /> <br /> My attempts to speak to Kimberly alone didn't really go any better. She was panicky and afraid. I tried to assure her I was trying to help, that I was her friend. But she just panicked more and jerked away from me to flee. She made a beeline for the door and Maria took off in pursuit. Both Gawain and I followed them out to the parking lot. Kimberly had gone to her car and Maria was following, clearly determined that their conversation was anything but over. But as she was crossing the lot, the shadows suddenly got heavy and thick. Maria screamed and fled while Kimberly started her car and drove away. Gawain and I gave chase and Gawain ended up having to physically grab hold of Maria as she was completely terrified beyond reason. We brought her inside through the side door and took her upstairs.<br /> <br /> She started to settle a bit once she was inside in the light and all. She was still pretty shaken and she explained that someone had been hunting her for a while. Someone with impossibly long arms and the ability to climb through mirrors. They'd come through her bathroom mirror and then later attacked her on the highway while she was driving. She was convinced they were trying to kill her but I don't believe that. She would be dead if they wanted her to be. This is a campaign of terror. I tried to explain this but she remained skeptical. At any rate, once she'd calmed down she got much less talkative and just wanted to leave. Jacob swept the parking lot and found no trace of the assailant. He returned her gun and Gawain walked her to her car.<br /> <br /> It seems that it's all centered around Sundown Kwon, a former member of the clique along with Becky. She was murdered a few years back and it's been an unresolved case. Well, seems Maria hired a PI to look into it and is now convinced that Kimberly knew it was going to happen and failed to warn their mutual friend.<br /> <br /> I called Tommy to see if he could shed any light on things. Once he'd finished making it clear that it wasn't his handiwork and that White Maria was a bitch he told me he didn't know who was doing it. His only guess was Gunnar. Since Ghoul Friday has the right contracts and the skills to use them. Also, he works for Lucien and the gang members that shot Sundown Kwon were Latino so there might be a connection.<br /> <br /> When it was all said and done, I was left feeling right sour. I don't know what's going on but clearly Dark Kimberly is in trouble and it may well be nothing I can do anything to help with. Hell, based on how she acted, she may not fucking want me to help. I have no idea what is going on but my gut says it's a royal fucking mess and this shitball is only going to get bigger and nastier as it rolls on. I like Gunnar and Kimberly, I don't want them to end up being the bad guys here. Maybe I should just walk the fuck away from the whole fucking situation. It's not like it's my damn problem or my job to deal with it. I really should just take a cue from Sargent Schultz and know nothing.<br /> <br /> And so yet again I was about as much fun as a wet blanket full of drowned puppies when Gawain took me to bed. And he was, yet again, far more understanding and gentle and loving than I fucking deserve. And between watching Eraserhead as part of movie night (seriously what the fucking fuck was that shit?) and how fucking wound up I am about starting therapy tomorrow all I want is to curl into those solid arms and have him tell me that everything is going to be fine.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> So, the trial is tomorrow and everyone is tense, especially Calamity. For the most part everyone was trying to keep busy to make the time go by faster. Lorelei was out back with her performers rehearsing for their upcoming \u201cMidsummer Night\u2019s Dream\u201d production. The only thing I really had in my mind to do was to continue my search for a car. I mentioned that I\u2019d settled on looking for a jeep. Insincere Marguerite looked up and asked what color jeep I\u2019d like. I almost took her up on that offer. It was really tempting, but since establishing my identity so carefully I\u2019d like everything to be on the up and up, officially anyway. So, that means buying a car with my own money. Smaller items are much harder to trace and I may take her up on future offers of larceny, but big dollar items I\u2019ll try to acquire legitimately. <br /> <br /> I was flipping through the newspaper when I noticed Calamity. She was trying not to seem restless, but I could tell. So, I folded the paper and asked her if she\u2019d like to spar. We had a go at it just a couple days ago, but she seemed to really need a distraction, so I offered one. We gathered up our knives and went out back. Gawain came with us saying that he\u2019d like to get some work in with his longsword. I had almost forgotten that the troupe was practicing. We opted to work out on the grass so the others could use the stage. <br /> <br /> Calamity and I paired off and started. Calamity started off fast with very little warning. She got a little closer than I usually like, but I was able to avoid her strike. After the initial fast start, Calamity relaxed into her usual fighting style and I slipped into mine. I\u2019ve learned a bit more of the fighting style that Luna and Calamity use and it shows in our practices, but I still retain a good bit of what Rook taught me. So, I was able to keep Calamity off balance for a bit and on her toes. Of course she was doing the same to me. She started off with such force that it seemed a shame to not reciprocate, so I did. We kept the level of intensity up pretty high throughout the fight. Calamity was working out her anxieties over the upcoming trial and I was dealing with my own Rime related demons. Talking may have worked as well, but neither of us is the type to be overly forthcoming about what\u2019s going on in our heads. Maybe therapy will help Calamity work out her emotions in a less violent manner. Though I would miss it if we stopped sparring altogether. <br /> <br /> All good things have to come to an end though, at least for today. Calamity feinted and like an idiot I fell for it. I stepped in for a lunge, I had a good angle on her ribs, when she suddenly sidestepped. I stepped forward before I could stop myself and she gently ran her fingers over the inside of my thigh. I froze for a second, but then realized she had banished the knives and it was just her fingers. She smiled, at my surprised expression no doubt, and winked before stepping away. It was a very effective move, I have to give her that. Not much harder, and with her knives, and I\u2019d be bleeding out. I\u2019m glad she\u2019s on my side.<br /> <br /> And like that it hit me, she <i>is</i> on my side. The whole time we were sparring was just like any other time. There was no extra tension, no undue caution, nothing out of the ordinary. I honestly don\u2019t know what I was expecting. I will admit that I was a little afraid that something might change with our relationship since I told everyone about my past, but Calamity hasn\u2019t changed how she acts around me at all. I figured of all the motley she would best understand my past, but I still had worries that what I\u2019d been might be too much for her. I feel like we are kindred spirits, and I\u2019ll admit that I didn\u2019t want to lose that. The others seem to just put my past in the category of \u201cHappened in Arcadia,\u201d and move on from there. I don\u2019t see it that way. For me, I accepted a job from a Gentry and regularly came \u201cto the world\u201d to do that job. I don\u2019t know how much of what I did was influenced by the Lady and how much of it was just me. It certainly felt like I was in control of my actions the whole time. And there really wasn\u2019t much of a gap between me working for the Lady and living here in California. Time-wise in the Lady\u2019s realm it was several months at least. I honestly don\u2019t know how long I was there before I managed to get away. Here in \u201cthe world\u201d it was only a couple of weeks. So, it doesn\u2019t feel like I can really separate who I was from who I am now. Not the way that the others seem to be doing. I wish it was as easy as that.<br /> <br /> Anyway\u2026the show went off without a hitch. I caught bits of it in between customers. I usually tune it out while I\u2019m mixing or serving drinks. It doesn\u2019t do well to split my attention in that situation. I did notice Monica coming in with someone I\u2019ve never met. I got the impression from the \u201cmeet and greet\u201d that was going on that the new girl was just that, a new arrival from the Hedge. I went over during a lull and introduced myself. Dominica, the new girl, said that she was trying to find out information on the different courts and asked which one I was in. I told her, and answered her questions about the Winter court. She also wanted to know what I thought the Winter court\u2019s contribution was to the freehold, why sorrow was important. I answered that if you don\u2019t know what sorrow is, how do you know when you\u2019re happy? You need to understand both sides of things like that otherwise your \u201cunderstanding\u201d is an illusion. After answering all that I asked if she\u2019d like a drink. She said yes. I asked if she liked chocolate. I got a hesitant yes in response. So, I made her a frozen chocolate mudslide as a treat.<br /> <br /> I think all of the motley introduced themselves to Dominica. Insincere Marguerite flirted heavily with her, if the body language was any indication, but it didn\u2019t look like she was actually trying to pick her up. Lori, Gawain and Calamity all went over to the new girl and I\u2019m assuming answered questions much like I was asked. She did have a bit of an overwhelmed look in her eyes so I kept my distance after the initial meeting. Calamity had also talked to Monica about the new girl and warned the rest of us that she had not been vetted yet and Monica was unsure of her. I\u2019ll also admit to a certain amount of wariness on my part. Dominica has been back for one day and is asking a lot of questions about the courts and their benefits. It could be that she was seeking to learn more in a desire to find a good fit for herself, but it seems awfully fast. I\u2019m not a good example, but most people I\u2019m given to understand take a few days to get used to the idea of being out of the Hedge before they start even thinking about the different courts and who they might like to join. I don\u2019t know\u2026maybe I\u2019m reading more into it than there is? I\u2019ll keep an eye on her for now.<br /> <br /> And speaking of interesting behavior. At one point during the night Gawain escorted White Maria to the bar. Apparently she was carrying a gun, and Gawain and Calamity sought to ensure the peace by making sure no one was armed with guns in the club. So, she turned over her gun to me with the understanding that I would hold onto it until she wanted to leave. I was fine with that. I\u2019ve held onto people\u2019s weapons before and likely will again. From what I understand White Maria and Dark Kimberly had an argument. Calamity went to talk to Dark Kimberly, while Gawain spoke to White Maria. Not sure what was said but it led to White Maria turning over her gun and Dark Kimberly stalking out of the club, getting in her car and driving off. White Maria followed her to the parking lot, but that\u2019s where things got weird. She said that she heard this whistling sound. Gawain, who had followed her out, said that it also looked like someone had used contracts of darkness on the area, making it harder to see. It made for less visibility and a really creepy atmosphere. Gawain escorted White Maria upstairs and met up with Calamity, who called me up. <br /> <br /> Apparently starting a couple days ago someone has started stalking White Maria. They haven\u2019t hurt her, but they\u2019ve been employing scare tactics and they\u2019ve been working. They are working so well that White Maria has taken to carrying a gun wherever she goes. She believes that this whole thing has to do with the argument that she\u2019s been having with Dark Kimberly. So, basically here\u2019s what\u2019s going on as I understand it. Awhile back a mutual friend of both ladies, Sundown Kwon, died in some gang related conflict. A short while ago White Maria, still upset by this, hires a private detective to look into it for her. He comes back with information that makes it look like Dark Kimberly knew about the danger to Sundown but intentionally did not tell him, which led to her death. White Maria is upset and confronted Dark Kimberly with this. Kimberly isn\u2019t saying much and Maria is getting frustrated. Shortly after that was when the harassment started towards White Maria. She\u2019s not sure if Dark Kimberly has anything to do with it, or if those responsible for Sundown\u2019s death are trying to keep things quiet by scaring Maria away from the case.<br /> <br /> Once Maria was calmed down I offered to check the parking lot for any sign of the perpetrator. I gave it my all, but there\u2019s only so much you can do to track someone\u2019s trail on asphalt. I didn\u2019t find anything. No sign. So, I let everyone know that I could not find a trace of whoever had used the contracts of darkness in the parking lot, so it should be safe. White Maria was keen on going home, so we escorted her to her car, I gave her gun back and she left for home. I think Calamity was going to call or talk to Tommy about whoever is doing this and see if he has any ideas. It\u2019s definitely a changeling, given the powers used tonight and in the past. Maybe Tommy will have an idea of who might be doing this. <br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> It\u2019s finally Monday. I took Calamity to see the psychologists at the clinic this morning. She went ahead and set up two appointments a week to start with and I guess she\u2019ll see how it goes from there. I\u2019m happy that I can help Calamity in this. It\u2019s not much, but having someone that supports you is important. I figured that she\u2019s got enough on her plate that she doesn\u2019t need to be worrying about going to the clinic by herself. Not that the place is intimidating. It\u2019s actually rather welcoming. It\u2019s just Darke\u2019s office that\u2019s kinda creepy. <br /> <br /> There was a bit of time before the trial. Everyone got dressed up in nice clothes. Lori wore her church clothes. The rest of us dressed in something sedate yet semi-formal. I wore a sports jacket and matching slacks that I got some time back. The others also dressed appropriately. Jack met us there and explained how the trial would go. First they read off what Calamity was accused of and what she admitted to. Madame Spidertoes was asked if the trial could continue forward, apparently a Darkling thing. Captain Jack, aka Joaquin Martinez, says that he will be representing the accused. Master Darke spoke up and said that he wished for Calamity to be given a second chance to serve the freehold. Gawain leaned forward and I put my hand on his shoulder to keep him where he was. He was angry at what my former monarch said, and I can understand that. I can also understand the sentiment behind wanting a second chance.<br /> <br /> Everyone who wanted to, got a chance to speak on Calamity\u2019s behalf. The whole motley plus Julia expressed our feelings on how Calamity was a benefit to the community, how good a person she was and how much she had to give to the freehold. Everyone spoke from the heart, and I think said some pretty good things. Lori made the rest of us look like children though. She was eloquent and just damn impressive. After that the monarchs plus Madame Spidertoes went back to consider Calamity\u2019s case. When they came back they determined that Calamity was not allowed to kill any member of the freehold who is in good standing (i.e. not exiled etc.) even in self-defense. She must be part of the defense force for the freehold should it be needed, and she will need to give the Winter King one glamor once a month. Overall not too bad. Calamity would have defended the freehold regardless, and the monarchs determined that Calamity is skilled enough with her knives to be able to not do lethal damage to anyone who might attack her. I can attest to her skill at not inflicting lethal damage. When we spar we use live steel and I never walk away with more than a minor cut or two as reminders to work on my defense.<br /> <br /> Boss Lowjack, as he\u2019s being called now, asked to speak to Calamity about her responsibilities and she asked me to accompany her. So, we went back to a private room and went over the particulars. Calamity will be reporting to a woman named Dahlia. Dahlia seems to be a good person. She is a straightforward kind of person. I think she and Calamity will get along just fine. Just from our brief interaction I thought she seemed like a decent sort and would be easy to work with, as long as you don\u2019t pull any bullshit with her. She is apparently also Darke\u2019s handler, and finds the man about as creepy and off putting as the rest of us.<br /> <br /> So, Calamity\u2019s specific task from Dahlia was to keep an eye on the patrons of the Dream House, look for loyalists or their supporters and keep the clientele safe. She may have more tasks for Calamity later, and may or may not be able to give much information about the whys and whats. It seems that Boss Lowjack, or maybe it\u2019s just Dahlia, is the type to compartmentalize the information. It is given to individuals only on a need to know basis, so if that person should be compromised they don\u2019t have all the details to give. It is a sound way to do things. The Lady did something like that with us, Rook and I. Depending on what she asked us to do, she would give us all the information or just some of it. Usually when we were sent as envoys to another Gentry we were given only some details. It wasn\u2019t often that things went badly with the other gentry, but it was good to be prepared. <br /> <br /> During one mission the Gentry we were sent to see decided that he wanted to betray our Lady. Rook and I were held as \u201cguests\u201d in his realm. He tried to get us to talk, to tell him about our Lady\u2019s strengths and weaknesses. Some of the information he wanted we just didn\u2019t have, not that we told him anything anyway. He was not the most imaginative questioner and his methods lacked that spark that really terrifies people into talking. That and he wasn\u2019t counting on Rook picking the locks and the pair of us escaping. We left a mess in our wake. It was satisfying. <br /> <br /> Anyhoo\u2026Calamity was given her task and she readily accepted it. I didn\u2019t think she\u2019d decline. It\u2019s good to have all of that behind us now though. We can concentrate on other things, such as movie night with ice cream and bourbon. We rented a couple of movies, Barton Fink and Eraserhead. I\u2019m given to understand that Eraserhead is rather surreal, but both should be seen. So, I\u2019m going to end this here and eat ice cream, drink bourbon and watch movies with my friends.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> Tonight has been a peaceful night.<br /> <br /> They brought in a new girl, Dominka, to the freehold. However, the Summer Court wanted I to keep away from her. Curiously. I discovered this as Calamity told me. So I spent a certain amount of Sunday night flirting with her. I did not actually try to pick her up, but she seemed to find me amusing.<br /> <br /> There was some hubbub with White Maria and Dark Kimberly but the others seemed to deal with it. It may have weighed on Calamity a bit, but she was also likely stressed about tomorrow.<br /> <br /> De La Rocha, Julia, Flores and I retired, while Oleander and Lorelei went off together. De La Rocha aggressively dominated Flores, which was surprising. Flores telegraphed she wanted that, and our Latina complied. I\u2019ve never seen her so; she is extremely submissive to me, and somewhat submissive to Julia. But Flores never had a chance. Watching them was delightful. Certainly.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, both Flores\u2019 friends De La Rocha and Julia enjoy pushing her and hurting her. Does this mean something? Possibly.<br /> <br /> But De La Rocha won\u2019t put her hand around MY throat twice. Perhaps I should make sure she knows that before she tries it once\u2026.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Calamity\u2019s trial has happened, and could have gone so much worse.<br /> <br /> The short version is, she is Pledged to defend the Freehold, give a monthly tithe of Glamour to the Winter King Boss Lowjack, and not kill any member of the Freehold in good standing. I hope she does not seek ways to weasel out of it, but she apparently wants to improve, so she probably won\u2019t. Hopefully.<br /> <br /> Gawain looked rather violent when Darke said he was not pushing death because he \u201cbelieves in second chances.\u201d He should know how good people are at lying to themselves by now. Twitch was sort of hilarious also. He comes by his name honestly. Certainly.<br /> <br /> I am not sure why Joaquin Martinez would want to be known as Captain Jack. Joaquin is a more attractive name than Jack, and helps him stand out. Capitan Joaquin sounds impressive. I\u2019d probably have sex with Capitan Joaquin. Captain Jack not so much. I did not start calling myself Margaret just because I came to the USA. And I never will. Someone calls me Margaret they get a tongue in their eyeball. If they are lucky.<br /> <br /> Note Bene, Madame Spidertoes apparently carries a special role in the Freehold when it comes to our kin; The Court formally asked permission to try Calamity, and got her approval for the sentence. Captain Jack did not know why this is in place, beyond the fact that she is over a century old and all Darklings hold her in esteem. He was honestly unsure what would happen if she refused. He also bemoaned other Seemings not having someone so looking out for them; he seemed to be only half joking. Probably.<br /> <br /> Tonight we celebrated with ice cream and movies. I had three movies to show, but put off Mulholland Dr. in favor of Eraserhead and Barton Fink. Eraserhead is a movie everyone should see once, and Barton Fink is useful for examining perspectives as well as surprise fascists. After a point though, Lorelei just wanted to make out.<br /> <br /> And who am I to refuse a lady?<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXXII</i><br /> <br /> C\u2019mon Gawain <u>Barton Fink</u> is an awesome movie. It may be my favorite John Goodman role, and John Goodman has had some awesome roles.<br /> <br /> If you usually skip Calamity, she has some information on the White Maria/Dark Kimberly/Sundown Kwon affair otherwise not mentioned.<br /> <br /> Also, yes, there is a reason for Madam Spidertoes\u2019 privilege. Perhaps it will even come out.<br /> <br /> Lotta people showing at the Dream House Tuesday night. Some folks may wind up joining Entitlements! Catch us then. Comments and Questions Welcome<br /> <br /> *worst","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T01:33:01-07:00","id":584391,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to return to Malibu. Getting back to the show and life. Also, looking into joining Entitlements for some.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXXIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> June 24th<br /> <br /> Well. After last night\u2019s movies, and the drinking, it was a little disconcerting to groggily woke up to find Calamity rummaging through our closet. Once I figured out she was fretting (a little) about what to wear for therapy. I tried to calm her down and convince her that normal, everyday clothes would be fine. I mean, therapy is all about letting someone know who you are, so they can help you get to who you want to be, and clothes, you know, tell you things about a person. I think. I mean, they don\u2019t usually tell me anything, but that\u2019s not really saying much, you know?<br /> <br /> I got another bit of sleep after she left, and then got up and made breakfast. I was just starting to worry a little when she got back, having grabbed lunch and some glamor at a bar on the way home. She said therapy went well, or at least not as bad as she was afraid it would. Which is great. Also, I think she got glamor without scaring the shit out of anyone, and still had fun, so that's awesome. I was a little sad I didn't get to make her breakfast, but it was good to see her less mopey and more her usual self.<br /> <br /> On another note, I may have provoked something crazy. See, Oleander sent Lori this super awesome bouquet of roses, that changed colors slowly over time. Calamity asked if Oleander knew Lori had a girlfriend and she responded that she had three and gave a wicked grin at the suggestion of a fourth. So I opened my big mouth and said we\u2019d need another wing just for girlfriends. Lori, with her clever web of words, turned that into a wing of closets and then decided, you know, she\u2019d rather have a Hedge wardrobe that was forever providing new clothes (though Julia still wanted the wing of closets I think). To be fair, we have a table forever providing us with more food, and a moat full of fire breathing piranhas, or at least, you know, we will, so a magic wardrobe is not too crazy...<br /> <br /> I did get to talk with Calamity some finally before the performance. It\u2019d been a rough week or so, and I hadn\u2019t been able to help out Desiree some more. Things seemed to be quieting down a little, so I wanted to give her a call, but first I wanted to, you know, give my girlfriend a heads up that I\u2019d be spending the night with someone else? Turns out though, that she\u2019d been wanting to ask if she could help out, provided Desiree was cool with it, She was, and is free tomorrow. It\u2019s complicated now though, with the Juan Carlos thing, but we\u2019ll work something out I\u2019m sure.<br /> <br /> She also wanted to formalize a weapons policy, which makes sense, even if it is just \u2018leave your weapons at the bar\u2019. But with the White Maria thing, and Dahlia asking after it, it seemed best to have it be official. It came into play right away too, though Louie was cool like before and Dahlia had gotten word from Calamity yesterday. Dahlia had a nicely made matched pair of daggers and Louie had his gun like before. Sadly, Louie and Ji Wen Ja were not around to enjoy themselves any this time, but were investigating the thing with White Maria.<br /> <br /> I let them know the details of what happened here, and Calamity told them about the argument, since she knew a little more about it. She knew even a little more than she told them and, you know, to be fair, learned more after, talking to Becky and Dark Kimberly on the phone.<br /> <br /> So, to get all of it down in one place - Sundown Kwan, White Maria, Dark Kimberly and Becky were a tight clique a few years ago. There is and had been tension or at least distance between the Asian Changelings and the Latin Changelings. So when Sundown was killed by two non-Changeling Latin gang members, while talking to a third at his house, the first suspects were Lucien, cause he has ties to Latin gangs, Oleander, cause she is creepy, apparently? and De la Roche, cause she and Sundown didn\u2019t get along. Lucien got off cause no one could find a motive, Oleander cause even if she is \u2018creepy\u2019 it didn\u2019t really match her style, and De la Roche cause she would have punched her lights out herself, not gotten gangers to do it.<br /> <br /> So it\u2019s an unsolved cold case, and something made White Maria hire a private investigator to look into it. Maybe cause she suspected the Latin Changelings had a hand in Dark Kimberly\u2019s shooting. The investigator found - and Becky apparently interviewed them extensively, so it\u2019s not just White Maria\u2019s interpretation - that Dark Kimberly knew about the murder before hand and didn\u2019t do anything to prevent it. Dark Kimberly said she just wasn\u2019t in time, but Becky was pretty damn convinced she had no intention of telling ever.<br /> <br /> Dark Kimberly had been being evasive, and Calamity called her and talked her into going to interview with Louie and Ji Wen Ja. They might at least be kinder than Becky\u2019s feeling at the moment, you know? As far as the terrorizing, Calamity was convinced Dark Kimberly was not behind that, especially as she seemed pretty terrified herself. My thinking is maybe Dark Kimberly had been threatened in order to make her not tell before, so now that it\u2019s coming to light, those threats might come true too. Or maybe she just feels guilty over what she\u2019s done...<br /> <br /> Anyways, Calamity was bummed cause no matter how it worked out, someone she cares about will probably be hurt. She seemed in a little better mood after the show, even though Captain Jack was awkward some more around Lojack, and Dahlia shut down any and all flirting cause relationships would be distracting, I guess? It was a little reminiscent of Joan, and those two did seem to hit it off some, which is good, both for the freehold\u2019s defense and cause Joan needs more friends. And maybe Joan can convince her that having a relationship can be a good thing. Calamity did get to introduce them and flirt with Andromeda, so maybe that\u2019s why she\u2019s feeling better.<br /> <br /> Julia and Insincere Marguerite were a little down too, Insincere Marguerite cause of Dahlia also, I think, and Julia cause of how everyone, especially, you know, Lori, was fawning over Juan Carlos. So I distracted them by trying to get them to help me come up with crazy ways to get Captain Jack and Boss Lojack together again. It worked a little, I think, at least to, you know, cheer them up. We didn\u2019t actually get together a solid plan for the matchmaking shenanigans yet.<br /> <br /> The Entitlement meetings went well, I think. Jacob seemed satisfied with his, at least, and mine certainly did. Juan Carlos told me about the Family of Silent Nights, and what they do. I had heard about them as dream warriors, and that is kinda what they do, both by fighting in dreams - we talked a lot about how that works - and by trapping nightmares, which sounds really cool. They have tricks to do that, and deal with dream poison and things like that, and can even use nightmares as weapons, which is less appealing for me. I think I\u2019d have problems, you know, using something so personal a bane against other people, even people that are my enemies. But it is a tool nonetheless, I suppose, and being able to trap them is still awesome.<br /> <br /> Juan Carlos is willing to sponsor me, but wants to see my work with dream stuff first. Conveniently, I have some dream stuff scheduled for tomorrow. The thing with Desiree is more of an Oneirophysicy kind of thing more than a Family thing per se, but it well let him get a sense of how I work and move in dreams. Provided, you know, Desiree is ok with it of course. In that case, Calamity may or may not be helping me. Apparently, she\u2019s interested in the Family too, so we\u2019re gonna see if Juan Carlos is ok with sponsoring her too, and if we could do the observation thing jointly then. We do work really well as a team, and Calamity is very good at Oneiromancy.<br /> <br /> So it was a good night, all in all. Lori moved in on Juan Carlos as soon as it was apparent that our business was done, and she and De la Roche and he are off to their room. Insincere Marguerite and Julia went off together, and Jacob and Luna. I think it\u2019s time I found me a Calamity.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Thbbbbbbt.<br /> <br /> Okay, I think that about covers my groggy state this morning following a night of fantastic sex. Well, I mean, let\u2019s face it, my life right now is pretty great, and I\u2019m groggy most mornings following a night of fantastic sex, but this one still stands out. But I digress.<br /> <br /> So, right, yesterday. The big deal yesterday morning was that it was Calamity\u2019s first therapy session. She was fretting about what to wear, which was oddly cute. I wanted to swoop in and save the day \u2013 it\u2019s so rare that she has a problem I can actually <u>help</u> with \u2013 but Gawain was on point, and mentioned that she should probably just wear her normal clothes, since it will help her therapist get a feel for her character.<br /> <br /> We were all eager to hear how it went when she got back, but nobody wanted to pry. She actually didn\u2019t get back to the Dream House until shortly after lunch, having gone to a local bar to blow off some steam and collect a little glamour. I\u2019m reliably informed that no one was killed, or even hurt, so I guess that\u2019s okay.<br /> <br /> Oh, I had another nice surprise yesterday morning, too! There was a knock at the door while Calamity was gone, Gawain answered it, and called up that it was for me. A local changeling courier I didn\u2019t know asked me to sign for a delivery, and then presented me with a beautiful bouquet of roses, courtesy of that sweetie Oleander! What\u2019s more, she\u2019d somehow enchanted the blossoms so that they all gradually changed color in concert (or maybe they were some sort of Goblin Fruit roses; I don\u2019t know). I put them in water and set them by the sliding glass doors in my room where they\u2019ll get a lot of sunlight.<br /> <br /> Either she\u2019s just incredibly considerate and sweet-natured, or the time we spent together Sunday night was very special to her. Sigh. Looks like I\u2019m going to have to have The Talk \u2122 with her soon. I hope she doesn\u2019t take it too hard; I really do like her a lot and I\u2019d like to keep seeing her if possible. I admit that her feelings for me are something of a turn-on, but I shouldn\u2019t think like that. I don\u2019t want her to get hurt.<br /> <br /> So time marched on toward the show \u2013 aka Seduction Zero Hour \u2013 and our respective duties took us away from each other. Juan-Carlos Hypnos showed up well before the show actually began \u2013 wearing a shirt this time \u2013 and I saw him chatting with Gawain when I peeked out at the audience before the show. That was good\u2026 I didn\u2019t want to interrupt their serious discussion with my not-so-subtle attempt to get laid.<br /> <br /> They seemed to have concluded their talk by the time the curtain rose. My first solo number was near the end of the first set. I decided to start out at a simmer and bring things to a boil later in the evening, so I began with \u201cWe\u2019re All Alone\u201d (emulating the Rita Coolidge version, naturally\u2026 never been a fan of the Boz Scaggs version). It\u2019s quiet, smoky, and sensual, and I went through the whole song sitting on a stool in a single spotlight, with my eyes locked on Juan-Carlos. He held my gaze easily, the hint of a smile playing around the corners of his mouth.<br /> <br /> Things heated up in the second set, and I decided to stop being subtle. Many of the musicians of the past thirty-odd years are something of a mystery to me on a personal level, and I don\u2019t claim to understand the antics of the vocalist who calls herself \u201cLady Gaga,\u201d but I do like a lot of her music (I should thank Marguerite for introducing me to her work). \u201cBad Romance\u201d had just the right combination of sexy and playful, and I had a ball strutting around the stage in my corset and fishnets while belting it out.<br /> <br /> During the second chorus I stepped down into the audience and got flirty with a few of the regulars. This fraternization came to a crescendo when I planted myself in Juan-Carlos\u2019 lap. I fell back on a classic cabaret move as I slowly lifted one leg until it was vertical, and then swiveled in his lap and brought it down on the other side of his torso so that I was straddling him. I don\u2019t mean to be crude, but, well\u2026 it was pretty obvious to me at that point that my seduction attempt was working.<br /> <br /> I made the rounds after the show ended, but never left Juan-Carlos alone for too long. Calamity was still fretting over whatever is going on between Dark Kimberly and White Maria. I still don\u2019t know anything about whatever contention has arisen between the two of them, but I know that it has several of my friends very upset, and that bothers <u>me</u>.<br /> <br /> Calamity\u2019s new handler, Dahlia, also turned up at the show tonight. She\u2019s cute, though she has this aloof, angry demeanor that is a little off-putting. Unfortunately, she\u2019s taken some sort of macho vow of chastity. She says that if she has romantic feelings about someone, it creates a sort of blind spot for her, which could seriously hamper her ability to protect the Freehold from Loyalist infiltrators.<br /> <br /> I guess I understand that, even if it sounds like a very lonely and \u2013 let\u2019s face it \u2013 shit-poor way to live. I voiced this opinion to Calamity, who seemed to agree with me. Still, it\u2019s not my way to force my attentions on those who genuinely don\u2019t want them, so I agreed to be a good girl and not press my feminine wiles on Dahlia. I confess that there\u2019s a part of me that is more intrigued by her now than I was before. I think maybe Marguerite is a bad influence on me.<br /> <br /> I said my good nights to the motley and associates (giving Julia a kiss and a heartfelt \u201csee you tomorrow, sweetie\u201d in the process) and made my way back to Juan-Carlos\u2019 table.<br /> <br /> \u201cI was beginning to think you had forgotten about me,\u201d he said with a smile.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re not easy to forget,\u201d I batted back at him.<br /> <br /> We passed a few minutes in flirtatious banter, then I waved D over to the table. \u201cJuan-Carlos, you remember my ridiculously hot girlfriend de la Rocha, right?\u201d I asked with a mock-innocent air.<br /> <br /> \u201cBut of course,\u201d he said, leaning forward to kiss her hand.<br /> <br /> \u201cI <u>like</u> this one,\u201d D commented with a wry grin.<br /> <br /> I put on a theatrical pout. \u201cLook, Juan-Carlos, I know you were hoping to spend the evening with me, but I can\u2019t leave D alone all night. Would you mind if she joined us for our fun?\u201d I made sure to bat my eyes at him in an exaggerated fashion, which made D snort with laughter.<br /> <br /> Juan-Carlos sketched a bow as he rose. \u201cWho could say no to two such beautiful companions?\u201d he asked as he took our hands. We led him upstairs and\u2026 frivolity ensued.<br /> <br /> As usual, going into details on the events of last night would be tasteless. Suffice it to say that Juan-Carlos Hypnos is a very capable and conscientious lover. And though D has always resisted letting me bring a man into our bed, she took to it well. I think sharing Juan-Carlos has brought the two of us even closer. I feel like I understand her a little better now.<br /> <br /> I woke up sore in all the right places this morning. It\u2019s a feeling I got quite often right after I moved to Malibu, but it\u2019s been a lot less common since I started my relationships with D, Marguerite, and Julia, and I never felt it before I was Taken. Oh, I was no angel back in Defiance (ha!), but High School boys don\u2019t fuck like that.<br /> <br /> Juan-Carlos got up just after I did, sliding gracefully out from under D\u2019s arm. I started to greet him, but he pressed his finger to his lips to silence me. After he\u2019d put his pants on, he leaned in to whisper his goodbyes.<br /> <br /> \u201c<i>Adios, mi Sirenita,</i>\u201d he breathed in my ear. \u201cThank you for a wonderful evening. I hope we can do it again sometime. When <i>Dulzura</i> wakes up, pass along my thanks to her as well, please.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou can\u2019t stay?\u201d I asked softly. \u201cI could wake up D\u2026 I\u2019m sure she\u2019d love\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> He raised his finger again and put it against my lips this time. \u201cWith regrets, I must decline, <i>Sirenita</i>,\u201d he said. \u201cI have business in the Freehold which cannot wait. And let her sleep; she\u2019s earned it.\u201d<br /> <br /> I threw on a robe, more out of consideration for the rest of the motley and any guests they might have over than out of any sense of prudish modesty. \u201cI\u2019ll walk you out,\u201d I said softly, opening the door.<br /> <br /> He kissed me softly on the front doorstep. \u201cNext time,\u201d I said a little breathlessly, \u201cmake sure you have time to stay for breakfast. Gawain makes a mean crepe.\u201d<br /> <br /> He laughed heartily at that. \u201cNo further enticements are necessary, I assure you,\u201d he said. \u201cNow I really must go, or I will be late for my first appointment. But I am certain we will see each other again, when I have more leisure time.\u201d<br /> <br /> And he was gone. I walked back up the stairs and into my room, threw off my robe, and climbed back under the covers with D, who murmured happily as I spooned against her. I buried my face in her black and purple mane and my lips found her neck.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo,\u201d I whispered more to myself than to her, \u201cthinking of going back to boys full-time now, Maria? Or do you still love me?\u201d<br /> <br /> I had thought she was asleep, and maybe she was\u2026 mostly. But I heard a muzzy voice answer me in Spanish. <i>\u201cSi, Lori,\u201d </i>she sighed. <i>\u201cTe amo. Siempre.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> Most of that I understood. I looked up the last word on my phone after we got up. It means \u201calways.\u201d<br /> <br /> Always.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> Days Without Stabbing: 7<br /> <br /> They say that admitting you have a problem is the hardest part. Well, obviously whoever 'they' are they don't actually know jack shit about having problems. I mean yeah, you can't get better until you admit you need to, but the hard parts are what get skipped over with a catchy montage of 80's pop music. So where is my fucking montage? Probably off making out with my damn flying car somewhere...<br /> <br /> Okay, so I just started this whole thing today and despite what Mr Miyagi (lying old bastard...) told me and every other child of the 80's this kind of shit takes time. But fuck it, I am allowed to be whiny and impatient here at least. And for the love of Zod did this whole mess with Dark Kimberly and Becky and White Maria have to happen right the hell now? I mean, it's not like Sundown Kwan will be any less dead next week or sometime after I have at least figured out how to start fixing my crazy.<br /> <br /> And, on that front, today I met Dr Carole Emmett. I was trying to be quiet about it but I woke Gawain up going through the closet trying to decide what to wear. I haven't exactly done this before you know. Handsome was comforting and suggested that I should dress normally since the whole point is for the doctor to get to know me. I avoided making any comments about scaring her off and decided to take his advice and just go with the basic jeans, boots, and vest over an a-shirt. It didn't exactly fit the relaxed business casual atmosphere of the clinic but the receptionist didn't seem overly surprised. I guess we junkies tend to dress down. Or maybe I'm flagged as special since I'm a Changeling. At any rate, I didn't get to spend more than a few moments in the waiting room with him before I was ushered back to Dr Emmett's office.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what I was expecting. I know Darke's replacement wasn't long enough ago to have really trickled down to the mundane functions of the Clinic so I guess he didn't personally oversee this side of things. The room was modern, light colored walls and carpet, chrome framed furnishings with glass or black leather. There was a fairly large window dominating the exterior wall but as soon as I arrived Dr Emmett made a point of drawing the curtains while the receptionist withdrew and closed the sturdy door behind him.<br /> <br /> We faced each other for a moment then she stepped closer and extended her hand and introduced herself. She gestured to the couch (a normal one, not a reclining cot like you see on TV and movies). I settled onto it and shifted a little. She didn't miss the discomfort. She launched into her opening speech, making sure I knew that I was not her first or only Changeling client but also making it clear that she would not say more about that, just as whatever I told her would be in strict confidence. If called upon to, she would speak in general terms and give her honest evaluation of my progress and stability. I didn't miss the way her eyes flicked to my shards as she said that last part and I couldn't help but tense up a little. I know I need this but I hate anyone having power of me.<br /> <br /> I have to give her credit, she picked up on that right away. She explained that she felt it was important to make sure I understood exactly what to expect before we began. Then she leaned back and asked me why I was there. I started to mumble a bit and made some vague comments about self control. She shook her head and cut me off. She explained that there was one rule. Once the door closed and we began there would be nothing but truth. She told me that if I was only there to convince the courts' that I didn't need to be put down like a rabid dog for murdering Mr Grey that she'd do what she could short of lying to make that happen. Then she tilted her head and continued. She said she didn't think that was the case. Then she asked me again why I was there.<br /> <br /> I didn't answer right away. Not that I was holding back, but I seriously took a minute to try and put it into words. What exactly it was that I wanted... needed... her help to do. Then I had to push those words out. Once I started, I kept going. I told her I was afraid that I was a danger to my motley. That recent events had made me realize that I did not have my impulses under control the way I had fooled myself into believing.<br /> <br /> She listened intently, absorbing every word. She told me that as long as I continued to be honest that she would do what she could to help me. I asked her (only half jokingly) if she really believed that she could fix me. Her answer was immediate.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo. No one can fix you. You're not a toaster. You're a person. You're the person that you become to survive in the situation you were trapped in. And now that you are free of that situation, that isn't the person you need or want to be anymore. What I can, and will, do is help you become the person you want to be instead. But you're the one that has to make the changes. It will not be easy. It will be a difficult and painful process. You're going to have to work for it.\u201d She paused then and gave me a knowing smile. \u201cBut it's worth it.\u201d<br /> <br /> She let me chew on that for a moment before shifting the focus of the session to working on my clarity. I have to shore up my perceptions before I can really tackle the deeper issues. Also, working through that will give the two of us a chance to get a bit more familiar and comfortable with each other which is key to working together to make the changes I want. It's early yet but I think this might just work. Time will tell though.<br /> <br /> After that I was hungry so I went out for lunch. I could have gotten back in time for Gawain's breakfast but I wasn't ready to face anyone I knew just yet. Also, I was in dire need of some glamour. I drifted a bit aimlessly along the way back and somehow I wound up at an honest to ghost pub. Okay, so it was assuredly all very Americanized but still it had a charm to it and decent bar to go with the pub food. It also had a couple of dartboards and as I washed down my fish and chips with a Guinness I noticed that the locals were taking it pretty seriously. After a couple more drinks I made my way over and asked about giving it a try. The condescension stopped just short of trying to pat me on the head and the older guy with the Andy Capp hat all but laughed when I suggested a wager. I goaded him into it, my tab against his and he agreed. I think he felt it was a low enough stake that he wouldn't be taking too much advantage. Fucking smug bastard. The look on his face when I smoked his ass was pretty damn sweet. Threw a couple more rounds just for fun after that, mostly just to show off for the crowd. It felt pretty damn good to be honest and the glamour was much needed.<br /> <br /> So I was in much higher spirits when I got back to the Dream House. Everyone was interested in how things went. I didn't go into the details; I just told them it hadn't been bad. It really is too soon to be sure but I do think Doctor Emmett and I are going to be able to get some of my shit sorted. Still, I don't want to count any unhatched chickens or anything. Lori also showed me the roses Oleander had sent her. They had a slow color changing effect to them and came with a love note. The woman is clearly rather smitten. I just hope she's not taking things too seriously. I like her but she IS the Autumn Court's poisoner and we all know that old saw about Hell and scorned women.<br /> <br /> There was a real air of anticipation during preparation. Gawain has a meeting with Juan Carlos and Lori and her girl have their own plans for him. Jacob's got a meeting with Boss Lowjack about his entitlement as well. And Dahlia was coming by to talk to me and check the place out. I don't know, maybe it was seeing Lori and De La Rocha all giddy and anticipating their hijinks. Maybe it was just that I was feeling relieved after my initial session didn't end up being terrible. Maybe it was the glamour high. Most likely a bit of all three but I decided that I was going to fucking act on that spark that meeting Dahlia gave me last night. I pulled out the hedge-spun evil queen dress and eased into it. I took the time to use all the tips and tricks I've learned from Lori and Julia to get good and girly. By the time the doors opened, I was looking pretty damn fine. Sure, I'll never be Lori gorgeous but I do clean up pretty damn well and I certainly would have done me. Satisfied with my reflection, I went down to mingle and wait for Dahlia to arrive so I could find out if she agreed with my assessment of my current degree of fuckability.<br /> <br /> Gawain's look when I caught up with him made his thoughts on that subject clear, which felt really nice. He'd wanted to speak to me about spending some time working with Desiree. Things got hectic last week so he hadn't had a chance to try to start helping her deprogram her trigger but he wanted to make sure I was okay with him being busy with that instead of sleeping with me. It was sweet and thoughtful because that is the kind of man Gawain is. I told I was fine with it and then I brought up something I had been thinking about. I asked him how he felt about the idea of me assisting him. Obviously only if Desiree is agreeable to it but I do know some Oneiromancy and we have spent a fair bit of time in each others dreams recently so we work well together. Gawain was more than happy with the idea. Of course, now it looks like we may have to postpone it since Juan Carlos is going to be observing him tomorrow night when he works with her. But so long as it doesn't interfere with the Family of Silent Nights I plan to assist him in his dream work as long as he's willing to let me. It's important to him and something I am good at that doesn't involve murder. Well... there are nightmares and incubi and dream poisoning Gentry to fight but that's all the sort of things that need killing so it's okay. Sanctioned murder is best murder.<br /> <br /> Sadly, my efforts in getting dolled up were in vain. Insincere Marguerite was all over Dahlia when I arrived and the woman was clearly interested. My Darkling sister slipped away to let us talk and I couldn't help but notice that her eyes followed Insincere Marguerite and didn't even register me. We talked about her role in the Freehold and her intentions for how to make use of my talents. She did guess rather correctly that I would be both well suited and more than happy with the role of hatchet-woman. She spoke about how dangerous my motley could be, pointing out how everyone desires Lori and mentioning how she'd go about leveraging her if she were a loyalist. It was disheartening on more than one front, both because she was uncomfortably accurate about what would be the best way to tempt my friend and her own admissions of interest. And she also seemed concerned about my Darkling sister, apparently there are some whispers about her twisting the minds of those she seduces and her lack of viability would make her able to work quietly to corrupt and spy on people. She asked me about speaking to both of them about not trying to seduce her. I should have just agreed but I couldn't resist muttering a not really joking comment about I guess that meant I shouldn't either.<br /> <br /> That was a fucking mistake. She looked completely surprised by the idea. Yeah, she did immediately ask me confusedly about Gawain but still, I'm apparently the only woman in the motley she isn't interested in. She said that was out of the question since it would interfere with her ability to send me into a dangerous situation. And that got us to her issues with relationships in general. She doubts her ability to be objective and do her job if she allows herself to have feelings for anyone. She joked that her sexual frustration fuels her relentless dedication to hunting loyalists. Personally, I think it makes her more vulnerable not less. It's a hell of a lot easier to turn down temptation if you know that you can go home and screw the shit of someone that isn't going to use or murder you instead of being as horny as a virgin at prom. It does give your enemies a different point of leverage admittedly, but at least it's one you can anticipate.<br /> <br /> I did, as she asked, speak to my motley mates for her. Lori did not have any designs on her (not that she actually has to try to make everyone want her...) She agreed with me that Dahlia's eschewing of any relationships was pointlessly lonely but she does respect people's choices about such things (even when they're wrong). Insincere Marguerite was a bit less willing to dismiss her own interest. The fact that Dahlia was clearly attracted made her disinclined to relinquish the chase. She did assure me that it wasn't any sort of power or dominance thing that she was trying to seduce my new boss and she seemed quite concerned that I might see it that way. I knew it wasn't anything like that and I told her so. I admitted my own interest and then asked her to back off as a favor to me. She locked eyes with me like she does when she's serious and agreed before she resumed her usual demeanor. She did seem a bit put off the rest of the night and at some point I do need to make sure she knows that I really do appreciate her giving up the hunt for me.<br /> <br /> Lori's hunt did at least go quite well, not that I think Juan Carlos was in the least bit inclined to resist. She was, as always, fucking amazing on stage. And while doing Lady Ga Ga's 'Bad Romance' she ended up straddling his lap. Thankfully (and she was quite clear on making sure of it) he had finished speaking to Gawain about the Family of Silent Nights early on in the show. The gist of that is that everything seems to be a go but Juan Carlos wants to watch Gawain work so he'll be observing his work on Desiree tomorrow night. It does mean I won't be helping but I am proud of Handsome and quite happy to see that his efforts to help people with their dream problems have been noticed. After the show, she and De la Rocha descended upon Juan Carlos' table and before too much later the three of them slipped away together. I think the whole thing had Julia bummed out. She and Insincere Marguerite were both kinda quiet as the night wound down but Gawain did his best to cheer them up and they did end up retiring together so I believe they're both fine.<br /> <br /> Jacob was naturally tight lipped about his own meeting with Lowjack but I believe it went well. I think he is on his way to being a member of the Knights of Utmost Silence. Sadly, Captain Jack's meeting with Lowjack was straight out of what popular media assures me High School is like. For one thing, Jack just happened to pick tonight to drop in and catch the show while Lowjack was there. And the conversation between them was awkward. Damn it was almost painful to see Joaquin so ill at ease. I really wish I knew how to do something about that situation but despite what romantic comedies promise matchmaking and meddling (much like violating airport security) do not always end well. I should maybe call him and see if we can meet quietly and talk about things without the whole wrestling persona. The man stood by me when I needed him, he's a friend. The least I can do is offer him a shoulder... well maybe just a friendly ear would be safer.<br /> <br /> But before the interpersonal relationship disappointment train could run me down I had a different situation to deal with. Ji Wen Ja and Louis came in early to ask about the attack on White Maria. Gawain and I sat down with them and went over the details of what happened. Much of what they filled in about the situation I already knew from Tommy but they did add a bit and give me a different take on it. The actual shooting happened at the hands of two Latino gang members who arrived while she was at the home of a third gang member for unknown reasons. That guy's mind had apparently been tampered with. Some suspicion fell on Oleander because she's Latino and creepy. But apparently even those that considered her noticed that there was no motive and the method was completely out of character for her. Lucien was a more likely suspect since he does have gang ties and is more inclined to violence. But ultimately there was no evidence linking him to it and no real motive. So the investigation stalled out and went cold. Until White Maria started to stir things up by hiring a private detective. And the intimidation tactics make it clear someone has something to hide. Louis seemed a little frustrated since White Maria had apparently been uncooperative and Dark Kimberly was avoiding them. Ji Wen Ja was simply stoic and imposing, as always.<br /> <br /> After speaking to them, I called Dark Kimberly and Becky. Dark Kimberly was still panicking over the whole situation. She claims that Sundown was acting crazy right before her death and admitted that she didn't act in time. But she was adamant that she wasn't involved in the actual murder. I believe her on that front but she's too guilty and too afraid. There is more going on than she told me. It is disappointing that she doesn't trust me to help her. She did listen to my advice that her avoidance of Louis and Ji Wen Ja was making her look guilty of more. I pointed out that their focus was really on the terror campaign against White Maria and advised her to meet with them and just admit to what she had done wrong and explain the recent rift between her and White Maria. She did agree to do so and hopefully that will at least get those two to look elsewhere for the one hunting White Maria.<br /> <br /> It doesn't help her with Becky though. That was a difficult call. I could hear the anger in her voice from the moment we started to speak. Fuck but that woman does things to me and hearing that silky undercurrent of impending violence was damn distracting. Sundown Kwan was her friend and she was going to taste blood from anyone involved. White Maria is also her friend. That Dark Kimberly knew something and didn't act is a betrayal. She told me she'd spoken to the PI White Maria hired and apparently someone else had also gotten information out of him or her. She was quite certain that Dark Kimberly's failure to warn Sundown Kwan was deliberate. I was honest with her as we talked about the situation. I told her that I really felt that Dark Kimberly wasn't behind the attacks on White Maria. She was at least willing to listen to me and assured me that so long as that proved true that she wasn't going to kill or maim Dark Kimberly. The way she said it sent some very inappropriate tingles down my spine (and certain other places) I mean, fuck Dark Kimberly is such a fucking sweet little morsel. Bloody hell just thinking about her writhing and whimpering and Becky licking her blood from her claws... Oh by Zeus' electrified balls part of me wants to be there to watch that... to lick that sweet, sweet blood from her claws and let her taste our prey on my own... It was all I could do to hold it together while I was talking to her. Shit, getting shut down completely after that had me all revved up was just salt in the wounds (and not in any sort of fun way...)<br /> <br /> Fuck, just writing about it has me squirming now. Okay, the thinking about it is what has me squirming and... and I like Dark Kimberly... I should NOT be thinking about doing such things to her. I really should not be this fucking turned on at the thought. Fuck. She's Annika's girl and I like them both. But fuck, I really like Becky and as much as I hate it she's got just cause. Dammit it is fucking hard to pick sides when I like everyone involved.<br /> <br /> Fuck it. I am frustrated and horny and tired of thinking about all of this shit. I am going to go find Gawain. At least he thinks I'm pretty.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> I guess I\u2019d have to call today a productive day all around. It started with Lorelei getting color changing roses from Oleander, which is sweet, but may cause problems later. Lori isn\u2019t the type to pick just one person to be intimate with and even if she did, it would be with De la Rocha. So, I hope Oleander doesn\u2019t get her hopes up too high there.<br /> <br /> My own day started with me going to check out some of the jeeps I found in the paper. I think I\u2019ve pretty much settled on a jeep. They are good for street driving and off-roading and can fit passengers. As much as I like Calamity\u2019s bike, it\u2019s not very practical for carrying passengers or stuff. I\u2019ll see how all this pans out though. I checked out a forest green jeep that had a decent number of miles on it, but the owner assured me that it was in great working order. I was more concerned by the couple spots of rust I saw in the wheel wells though. It\u2019s not like the streets around here have ever seen salt for slippery weather, but still, I don\u2019t want the car rotting out from under me. Huh\u2026I think I just \u201ctalked\u201d myself out of the green one. Okay\u2026so I also looked at two blue ones. One was dark and the other light. They are both in good shape and have a reasonable number of miles on them. The only real difference, besides a couple dollars in the price, is the dark one has a soft top that you can take off, while the light one has a hard top. I guess I just need to decide if I want the hard or soft top.<br /> <br /> Today was also Calamity\u2019s first therapy session. She started off worrying about what to wear. I thought it was a bit funny at first, but after thinking about it I can understand. How you dress influences how people see you, and she wanted to make a good impression on the psychologist. Gawain recommended just wearing regular clothes, like jeans and a t-shirt. I agreed with him. So, in the end Calamity chose just that and headed out. She got back some time later, after lunch, in a better mood than when she left. Some of that might have been the beer she had at lunch, or the glamor she got while at the bar. I\u2019m leaning towards a combination of the two. I don\u2019t even think she scared the snot out of anyone to get the glamor either. Probably a good start all around.<br /> <br /> The show went off with no problems. Overall it was a quiet night. At one point Ji Wen Ja came in with Louie. I think they wanted to talk to Calamity and Gawain about what happened the other night with Dark Kimberly and White Maria, or maybe just about White Maria being targeted. Louie checked his weapon at the bar and I directed them to where Calamity was. I was there for the whole conversation with her, but figured those two could handle any questions that came up. I would just be saying more of the same. I\u2019ll have to ask them how it went, and if they learned anything interesting in turn.<br /> <br /> Later in the evening Juan-Carlos came over to Gawain to talk to him about joining his entitlement, the Family of Silent Nights. It sounded interesting. Something to do with helping people through dreams. Seems to be right up his alley. Gawain has already started helping Desiree with her \u201cswitch\u201d problem. Hopefully he\u2019ll be able to cure her entirely. Who knows, maybe Juan-Carlos and his folks can help if needs be.<br /> <br /> I also met with Lowjack to talk about the Knighthood of the Utmost Silence. He explained what it was all about and said that he\u2019d talk to Tamara about bringing me into the Knighthood. He said that he\u2019d put in a good word for me. So, from what I found out, it seems that the main job of the Knighthood is to help people start new lives somewhere else, for whatever reason. So, whether they\u2019re being hunted by a True Fae, having problems in with authorities, etc\u2026 the Knighthood helps them set up a new identity somewhere new where they cannot be traced. Lowjack stressed that the Knight who helps someone relocate cannot talk about where s/he has moved that person to. Not even to other Knights. I think he wanted to stress that bit and make sure I understood that even if forced I cannot give up that information. I wanted to smile at that. It took some work to keep it from showing. Granted it probably wasn\u2019t going to be a happy smile\u2026more of a dark painful smile. I\u2019ve had experience with \u201cbeing pressured.\u201d I assured him that I could keep a secret and was interested in helping people start new lives and get a second chance.<br /> <br /> Lowjack also said that sometimes the Knighthood is looked on with suspicion because they do everything behind the scenes and in the shadows, and never talk about what they\u2019ve done. That makes sense. Unless you\u2019re completely transparent about what you\u2019re doing people are going to look at you with some amount of suspicion. This entitlement is such that you cannot do that. You can\u2019t talk about what you\u2019ve done or who you\u2019ve helped because to do so would possibly leak the information of that person\u2019s whereabouts to unfriendly parties. To keep them safe, you must remain silent. I get that.<br /> <br /> One of the skills that he said they need their members to have is skill using a knife. I assured Lowjack that I was proficient with a blade. I\u2019m not sure if Lowjack saw me fight during the Mothership\u2019s invasion or if he\u2019s head by word of mouth about my abilities. I forgot to ask about that. If he\u2019ll take my word on it, or if they\u2019ll need a demonstration. He talked about other skills that are useful but not required, such as computer skills etc\u2026to create the new identities. I don\u2019t have much in the way of advanced computer knowledge though. I\u2019m not even sure how one goes about creating a new identity. I guess the main skills that I could bring to this entitlement are discretion, stealth and skill with a blade. I can also make a mean mojito, but don\u2019t think that will be quite as useful. I just hope that the skills I do have are some that they need.<br /> <br /> After conversation was over Captain Jack joined us at the table. He wanted to say \u201cHi\u201d to me and Gawain and it just so happened to correspond when Lowjack was there too. To say that Jack was a flustered is an understatement. I\u2019ve never seen Jack so awkward and hesitant when talking to someone than I did tonight when he was talking to Lowjack. I mean, it was High School levels of awkward! For my part I offered to get everyone a drink, on the house and left for the bar. My plan was to make something I thought each of them would like, but nothing too hard. I don\u2019t want them getting plastered, just more relaxed. We\u2019ll see how it goes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> Not much today of note. It was Tuesday night, most anticipated as several of my Motley mates looked to join Entitlements. And Lori to score with Juan-Carlos. Naturally.<br /> <br /> Calamity went for therapy in the day, and Lorelei got nice flowers from Oleander. I am sure she was happy. De La Rocha loves her no less, but is not a flowers sort of women. I have gotten a rose a couple times from Julia. Romantically.<br /> <br /> Not that she would admit it. Oh no no no.<br /> <br /> There was some checking up on us from Louis Guo and Ji Wen Ja on the events of last night. Calamity and Gawain handled it. Calamity seemed worried, and I spoke to her. She is\u2026ill at ease for good reasons. Not much she can do but watch and wait though. Unfortunately.<br /> <br /> The evening took an interesting turn when Dahlia arrived. She was wearing striking black, and her eyes fell on me as I moved around the room. I am not Lorelei, but I can tell when people are checking I out, so I went to go flirt. Cheerfully.<br /> <br /> The chemistry was really going, and Dahlia was excited. I could see it in her eyes, and when my foot brushed her leg I thought she might explode. Unfortunately, she was very guarded. She insisted women who I took to my boudoir came back different (sort of true, yes Julia and Flores, not really so much Willow or Dionisia). I played coy and suggested she come and see the truth for herself, but she insisted in imply I had dark intentions. We were working on that impasse when Calamity came along. She is Calamity\u2019s handler so I left to let them talk. Regrettably.<br /> <br /> That may have been a mistake. Calamity afterwards asked I not to seduce Dahlia. I suggested that, like with Julia, it was less a seduction than she and I simply getting what we both wanted, but Calamity insisted. Dahlia feared I would compromise her ability to objectively observe, well, I, and perhaps others in the dream house. It was a foolish idea. She could not objectively observe me even now. But Calamity is my friend, my Motley mate and, as she is fond of saying, my \u201cDarkling Sister.\u201d The eyes I gazed into were earnest. They feared angering me, not fear of my wrath but loss of friendliness, affection. The really strongly wanted, even needed me to do this. I did not, do not need Dahlia. I agreed. Reluctantly.<br /> <br /> I was, nonetheless, a bit mopey. As I say, there was chemistry. Julia was bugged by Lorelei throwing herself at Juan-Carlos. I think Lorelei\u2019s sleeping with he and Oleander may be bugging her. There was some time Lorelei only really spent time with she, De La Rocha, and myself, and she was perhaps a bit used to Lorelei being ours. It would be overstating it to say Lorelei is a bird and must be free, much as it would be to note I am a cat and Lorelei is delicious. Okay I have lost the plot.<br /> <br /> Julia could not do much to help. She seems to be disconcerted. Gawain was a good guy and told us stories that helped, though, and Jacob brought some alcoholic milkshakes. They are nice. I will have to steal something nice for them. We must have looked miserable. Apparently.<br /> <br /> Gawain was also, somewhat non-seriously yet sort of seriously, looking for ideas to help Lowjack and Captain Jack hook up. I must consider this. Mischief is fun, and I am not against mischief that harms no one. So perhaps.<br /> <br /> I walked Julia upstairs and cuddled with her, while jazz was on so she could not hear them, and we danced some. I\u2019d always assumed any naked dancing I did would be a sexual thing but no, this was just a display of affection. Julia finally laughed, which was good, and we eventually settled back in. Happily.<br /> <br /> Julia and I should go out, I think, maybe with Lorelei and De la Rocha, maybe with Gawain and Calamity, maybe just us. I will talk to her. Later. Yes.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXXIII</i><br /> <br /> The session ended early, so we started a bit early, but the overall session was still shorter.<br /> <br /> Not really much to add to or clarify. The therapy system I am using is the one in Rites of Spring.<br /> <br /> Back to normal next time. Comments and Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 07-09-2015, 04:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T14:06:33-07:00","id":595955,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to return to Malibu and see what the latest drama is. This time Calamity discovers a new link to her past in an unexpected place, and Lorelei provokes a barfight.<br /> <br /> There is a rooftop picnic, also.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXXIV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> June 25th<br /> <br /> Today\u2019s gone well, so far, I think. At least, you know, for me. My day was pretty low key though. Calamity\u2019s was more exciting, but I think it\u2019ll turn out good for her too. Knowing more about her past, being able to confirm shaky details... even if it\u2019s bad, it\u2019s good to know, you know? If I met someone from my Durance, well, I\u2019d probably go out and buy a lottery ticket, or else be really happy that the Gawains lived. We didn\u2019t change out actors or anything, so there\u2019s not really many possibilities of people to meet. I guess the Dream-lord could have had other stories, other repeating dreamscapes and that\u2019d kinda be like being from my Durance.<br /> <br /> Anyways, I\u2019m getting all out of order. Breakfast was the standard subjects, no extra dudes. I guess Juan Carlos snuck out early. Insincere Marguerite was in fine form - I ducked out for a second to grab something from the pantry and when I got back, her sputtering was in full blast and at its highest pitch. Apparently about the eighties, with its legwarmers, coke and SMGs and/or death metal, with its \u2018cookie monster\u2019 vocals.<br /> <br /> We scattered as usual for Calamity\u2019s dance lesson, Lori off to the city to do modeling (and talk with Oleander, I think). In sincere Marguerite and Julia off to primp and me cleaning the floor in front of the stage. Jacob tried to convince me that I didn\u2019t have to sweep, I could just watch, you know, but there are rules to these things. Lori knows. He eventually gave up on trying to ineffectually take the broom from me and headed out with Luna to buy a Jeep he\u2019d had his eye on.<br /> <br /> After the dance lesson, Calamity and Insincere Marguerite had an invitation to tea with Madame Spidertoes. Dahlia was there too, part of Madame Spidertoes\u2019 clever plan , you know, to reveal the secret that Dahlia was from Snow Globe. Insincere Marguerite kinda ragged on Madame Spidertoes a lot, about how she was gloating and creepy and everything. It kinda upset De la Roche, I think. Calamity felt bad pushing Dahlia in front of other people, but she did figure out that she had escaped through the well, that was full of zombies. This bothered Calamity a lot, since. you know, she had pushed Timmy down a well and so either he turned into a zombie or he got out and might be upset at her.<br /> <br /> She seemed really shaken by all of it, so I made sure she was alright for real. The thing with Desiree and Juan Carlos tonight is important, but not as important as her being ok, you know? She promised she was though, and that the therapy was going great. It seemed true too, which is awesome. She goes again tomorrow. Hopefully it keep going great.<br /> <br /> June 26th (morning)<br /> <br /> Not quite time for breakfast yet, but I figured I\u2019d get out of there and give Desiree some privacy. The dream therapy thing went well, I think. I\u2019m working with what she knows about staging and I know about building things and what being in a dream lets us all know to do a maintenance overhaul of her mind stage, going from the damage the interloper caused and removing everything connected to the switch. It\u2019s slow going cause I\u2019m trying to replace/repair things as I go, cause I don\u2019t wanna just leave a ruined stage behind. But we made some good progress.<br /> <br /> The show went well too. Joan, Haley and Monica came as a group. Monica was trying to get Haley and Joan to be more friendly. I went over to help once I\u2019d made sure that Juan Carlos observing was ok with Desiree. I was pretty damn charming, if I do say so myself. They even talked to each other directly a few times, politely, by the end of it, you know?<br /> <br /> June 26th (later)<br /> <br /> Calamity got back in time for breakfast this time and in good spirits. Juan Carlos and Desiree both stuck around for crepes, so it was a regular party, you know? Captain Jack even showed up after a bit, but not before Lori had me suspecting she was a pod person cause she said she\u2019d enjoyed causing a bar fight and Juan Carlos thinking she was cause she called him \u2018JC\u2019. Insincere Marguerite licked her to check though, and apparently she still tasted like Lori at least.<br /> <br /> Captain Jack was here, of course, to discuss shenanigans. His newest scheme involved a dance off, interrupted by a Dirty Dancing interlude, culminating in simultaneous Hammer dancing. You know, so we could both win, as the Hammer dance is clearly the winner\u2019s finale. In Captain Jack\u2019s words, it is the cherry on the \u2018I won\u2019 pie. It might even involve me and Calamity break dancing in fedoras to It\u2019s Tricky.<br /> <br /> Because he\u2019s Captain Jack, and Juan Carlos was around, he explained his plan with a banana, that always moved to point, you know, straight up whenever Juan Carlos talked. Lori eventually stole it and ate it in a way that had all us dudes wincing. I think she even winked at Captain Jack.<br /> <br /> Also! We\u2019re totally gonna do a burlesque, gender swapped version of Cannibal the Musical. Of course, I think that means I get to be the Chief\u2019s (played by Insincere Marguerite, of course) son, but still, it\u2019s gonna be awesome!<br /> <br /> On a more serious note, Captain Jack had found out that the phones that called Desiree and Chalcedony had been burner phones, so that was a dead end. We figured whoever was poking at the switch had gotten distracted by the invasion, whether they were Winter Court, loyalists of a rival Keeper, or the Tong. As much as I despise Darke and his crew. I doubt it was them. If they\u2019d had an inkling of the switch and wanted to test it, I imagine she\u2019d have been in one of their cages. Whoever is was, we need to get this fixed before they, you know, try again, so Desiree\u2019ll be back tonight.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> I almost hate to admit it, but I had fun last night. I got to see a side of D that she usually keeps hidden (from me, anyway).<br /> <br /> But I\u2019m getting ahead of myself. A few hours after I crawled back into bed, D and I yawned, stretched, and kissed each other awake, threw on a couple of robes, and headed downstairs to breakfast.<br /> <br /> Talk soon turned to the differences between decades. I spoke for the seventies, while Calamity reluctantly took up the case of the eighties. Even she admitted that fashion trends went sort of seriously weird for a few years, with big hair, shoulder pads, and leg warmers coming into vogue. Leg warmers? As a fashion statement? Those things are <u>hideous!</u><br /> <br /> We also spoke briefly about music, and somehow talk turned to \u201cTake On Me\u201d by A-ha. I heard that song a few weeks ago when I was researching the musical trends I\u2019d missed while I was away, and I quite liked it. I wanted to show my erudition, so I mentioned a bit of trivia I\u2019d picked up at the time: that \u201cTake On Me\u201d is the only song by a Norwegian band ever to hit number one in the United States.<br /> <br /> Marguerite sort of snootily commented that it was no surprise, as Norway is not known for its cultural contributions. I racked my brain for other examples of Norwegian music, but all I could come up with was the fact that the Scandinavian countries supposedly produce a lot of heavy metal bands. Marguerite scoffed, and even I had to admit that a lot of the metal from that part of the world seems to incorporate what I call \u201ccookie monster vocals,\u201d which is not a style I particularly enjoy. This just served to muddy the subject further. I gave up trying to explain it a few minutes later.<br /> <br /> More differences between the decades came up. Apparently the abuse of cocaine became a major problem in the 80s. It was mostly a high-end club drug when I was Taken; something you heard about happening mostly in swinging disco halls in the big cities on the coasts. When asked, I admitted that I\u2019d never tried cocaine\u2026 but also admitted that I probably <u>would</u> have if the opportunity had presented itself. It would have <u>destroyed</u> Dad if he ever found out, after all.<br /> <br /> And then it was time for Annika to arrive for Calamity\u2019s weekly dance lessons, so I made myself scarce. What can I say? I don\u2019t see the point in aggravating myself over her. And it\u2019s not like I was making excuses; I actually did have things to do in the city today.<br /> <br /> I visited a couple of the talent agencies I\u2019d contacted in LA, which took up most of the afternoon. No bites yet, but several of them definitely seem interested. It\u2019s not easy to break into the entertainment industry, no matter how many rags-to-riches stories you hear. It has as much to do with making the right contacts as it does with natural talent and hard work. So I\u2019m laying the groundwork. I hope my efforts will start to bear fruit before too long.<br /> <br /> On my way back to Malibu I stopped in Santa Monica and met Oleander for a late lunch. It was pleasant, and the two of us talked and laughed about a lot of things which aren\u2019t really important. I\u2019d sort of been dreading that meeting, actually, which just goes to show that my mind can make mountains out of molehills with the best of them.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo, I wanted to talk to you about something serious,\u201d I said after a while.<br /> <br /> Her face clouded.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s nothing bad,\u201d I hastened to add, \u201cor at least, I don\u2019t think so. I just wanted to talk about this relationship and what it means.\u201d<br /> <br /> Something fell around the corners of her eyes, and I sighed.<br /> <br /> \u201cLook Oleander,\u201d I began, \u201cI like you. I like you a lot. I enjoy spending time with you, and I like sleeping with you, and I want to keep doing both. I\u2026 I\u2019d like to see if something <u>more</u> could develop between us over time.\u201d I took her hands in mine and felt her squeeze them gently. A smile played at the corners of her mouth.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019d like that too,\u201d she said simply.<br /> <br /> \u201cBut I need you to understand my situation,\u201d I continued. \u201cI\u2019m in committed relationships with three other people right now. One of those people is D, and we just went through the Greening together. They\u2019re <u>all</u> very special to me, and they\u2019re not going away.\u201d<br /> <br /> She closed her eyes and nodded, but didn\u2019t say anything.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m not saying this to hurt you, Oleander,\u201d I said softly, \u201cthat\u2019s the last thing I want to do. In fact, I\u2019m hoping to spare you some future pain by putting this out in the open at the beginning. I want to see where this thing between us goes\u2026 but I need you to understand that any relationship between us won\u2019t be exclusive. If you can handle that, then we\u2019ll be okay. If not\u2026 well, like I said, I don\u2019t want anyone to end up getting hurt.\u201d<br /> <br /> She seemed to think about it for a while, and then she smiled. It was sort of a melancholy smile, but it was genuine for all that. \u201cI\u2026 think I can manage,\u201d she said softly. \u201cI admit that it\u2019s not the ideal relationship I\u2019d thought about between the two of us, but I\u2019m not so na\u00efve that I expect everything about my life to be exactly the way I want it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou sure?\u201d I asked seriously.<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cI\u2019m just thrilled you want to be with me, Lori,\u201d she said. I looked into her eyes, and I didn\u2019t see anything hidden there; she seemed genuinely at peace with the situation.<br /> <br /> I smiled, and leaned in for a kiss. She stopped me before I got too close. \u201cToo public?\u201d I asked, raising an eyebrow.<br /> <br /> She shook her head. \u201cIt\u2019s not that,\u201d she said quickly. \u201cGod, I\u2019d kiss you on the pitcher\u2019s mound at Dodger Stadium during a home game if you wanted me to. But I had to go into the Hedge the other day. It\u2019s where I got those flowers. I turned on my body\u2019s natural defenses, and\u2026\u201d she blushed and didn\u2019t meet my eyes, \u201c\u2026I\u2019m still a little toxic. I don\u2019t want to make you sick.\u201d<br /> <br /> I took her chin in my hand and gave her a quick peck on the cheek. \u201cI think we can risk that much affection, don\u2019t you?\u201d I asked with a wink.<br /> <br /> She nodded and smiled; a guileless open smile this time. \u201cThat should be safe,\u201d she agreed. \u201cThe toxins will have worked their way out of my bloodstream by tomorrow morning,\u201d she said after a minute. \u201cWhen can I see you again?\u201d<br /> <br /> I thought about it. \u201cWhy don\u2019t you come by the Dream House tomorrow night, and we can get together after the show,\u201d I said. She agreed.<br /> <br /> As we were paying the bill I got a call from Calamity, who wanted to talk to the motley. I told her I\u2019d be back to the Dream House in twenty minutes, bade my new paramour a hasty goodbye, and hit the highway.<br /> <br /> So apparently Madame Spidertoes invited Calamity and Marguerite to an afternoon tea today. It proved an interesting time for all. She had also invited Dahlia, Calamity\u2019s new \u201chandler\u201d for the Winter Court. At some point during the gathering, Madame Spidertoes \u201caccidentally\u201d let slip that Dahlia had also spent her Durance in Snow Globe, like Calamity.<br /> <br /> Dahlia didn\u2019t much want to talk about her captivity (which is totally understandable), but Calamity was able to get her to spill the beans about her escape: she got out through the town\u2019s well. The well was filled with people who had been thrown down there. They didn\u2019t die\u2026 but they weren\u2019t precisely <u>alive</u> anymore, either. It sounded something like a Romero movie to me. Calamity was upset because\u2026 well, while she was a captive in Snow Globe, she <u>put</u> someone down that well. If this \u201cTimmy\u201d died down there, then he might be one of these zombies. If he survived, he could have made his way back to Earth, and probably isn\u2019t very happy with Calamity. Though it sounds harsh to say so, I\u2019m not sure which to hope for. D\u2019s situation with Twitch is a similar reminder of how the terrible things we did in Arcadia can come back to haunt us.<br /> <br /> Marguerite opined that Madame Spidertoes put Calamity and Dahlia in that situation on purpose, hoping to stir up some interesting trouble for her own inscrutable purposes. Privately, I think she might be right\u2026 but her accusations <u>really</u> upset D. She insisted that Spidertoes isn\u2019t a bad person; she just doesn\u2019t understand social niceties anymore. I know the two of them used to be together, and that sort of history can have a powerful effect on your perceptions, so I tried to be as supportive as I could. Marguerite was unwilling to concede the point, however, and D walked out in a huff.<br /> <br /> I caught up to her before the show and drew her aside for a private conversation. She was <u>really</u> pissed off. \u201cI know Mags means well,\u201d she said through clenched teeth, \u201cshe\u2019s just worried about Calamity. But she\u2026 she shouldn\u2019t talk about Madame Spidertoes like that. It\u2019s not right.\u201d<br /> <br /> I took her in my arms and kissed her gently. \u201cWe don\u2019t know her as well as you do,\u201d I said softly, \u201cand she\u2019s so much older and more powerful than we are. It\u2019s hard for us to tell what she\u2019s thinking, and that\u2019s a little scary. But you know Marguerite would never do anything to upset you, right sweetie?\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cI know. I guess I just need to let off a little steam.\u201d<br /> <br /> I thought about it. \u201cHow about after the show tonight we go out together and do something just for you\u2026 like maybe hit one of those biker bars you\u2019re always talking about and start a few fights?\u201d<br /> <br /> She actually grinned at that. \u201cYou sure?\u201d she asked. \u201cBecause that sounds awesome, but I don\u2019t want to pressure you into anything.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s a date,\u201d I promised, \u201cbut for now I need to get into costume.\u201d<br /> <br /> We kissed goodbye and I went to join the bustle of the performers preparing for the show. I had two solo numbers last night as well as a couple of backup and ensemble dance acts. During the first set I put on my glasses, pulled my hair back, and threw on a sedate sweater/skirt combo to achieve a look I like to call \u201cfrumptious.\u201d Marguerite threw a spot on me while I was just lounging on a chair in the middle of an otherwise bare stage, and I softly launched into a 90s song called \u201cStay (I Missed You)\u201d by Lisa Loeb. It\u2019s a catchy if somewhat rambling number about the inevitable dissolution of what sounds like a rather one-sided relationship. It seemed to go over pretty well.<br /> <br /> For my last number of the evening, I turned things up a notch (though it was still pretty sedate by the Dream House\u2019s standards). I got into a low-cut, tight T-shirt, a leather jacket, and a tight leather miniskirt (knowing that I was headed out to a bar with D later) and performed my own take on Aerosmith\u2019s \u201cDream On.\u201d What can I say? The fact that Gawain and Juan-Carlos were going to be entering Desiree\u2019s dreams later that night inspired me.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t do the usual hob-nobbing after the show; I just met up with D, and the two of us hopped on her bike and headed off down the Pacific Coast Highway. We ended up at a bar called Larry\u2019s or Harry\u2019s or something like that\u2026 not very memorable. It was a pretty stereotypical biker dive. It was quite crowded considering that it was past two in the morning when we got there. I wiggled through the door with D\u2019s hand glued to my ass, and the fun started almost immediately.<br /> <br /> I turned on the charm. Most of the inhabitants of Larry\u2019s or Harry\u2019s probably wouldn\u2019t recognize charm if it showed them its passport, but it had the desired effect nonetheless. Most heads turned to look at us as we walked up to the bar. There were a lot of big hairy muscly men with full beards and beer bellies there, but there were a few younger guys and some pretty hot ladies there too.<br /> <br /> I tried my hand at the subtle art of flirting without flirting. I tried to use my body language and little facial cues to entice as many people as possible, but I didn\u2019t say or do anything directly to lead them on. It was enough. Suffice to say that D\u2019s wasn\u2019t the only hand that found my ass last night, and it wasn\u2019t long before the first punch was thrown.<br /> <br /> D really seemed to enjoy herself during the ensuing chaos. A lot of people ended up unconscious, but nobody was seriously hurt. I think the worst injury was a broken nose; most people got away with a few bruises or cuts. There were no broken bottles, but a couple of pool cues were smashed over a few heads. The fighting never touched me, though\u2026 not even when some of the other girls in the bar started scratching and pulling hair. I mostly spent my time tossing darts, with the occasional wink thrown in to keep things interesting.<br /> <br /> Thanks to her Leechfinger powers, D was easily the last person standing in the bar (myself excluded, of course). All the anger floating around had topped off her glamour and left her more than a little randy, and the lust I\u2019d generated in the crowd had the same effect on me. We <u>did</u> manage to make it back to the Dream House before we started shedding clothes, but it was a near thing.<br /> <br /> I can\u2019t believe I\u2019m about to say this, but\u2026 I had <u>fun</u> last night. Seeing D in her element like that, doing something that\u2019s so much a part of who she is\u2026 it was nice. I mean, I\u2019m still not very comfortable with the violent aspects, but at least the two of us found a way that we could share that part of ourselves\u2026 desire and anger flowing freely from so many mortals, feeding us both as we spent time together\u2026 it was a whole new type of intimacy between us.<br /> <br /> We woke up late this morning and found most of the denizens of the house already at breakfast, along with Desiree and Juan-Carlos (Gawain had been helping Desiree in her dreams while Juan-Carlos observed). The scene became complete when Captain Jack showed up to discuss his next escapade with Gawain. Apparently the Captain wants to stage some sort of dance-off between the two of them, ending with something called a \u201chammer dance,\u201d which involves jiggling ones legs rapidly, moving back and forth laterally, and wearing billowy oversized pants.<br /> <br /> Calamity can say what she will\u2026 the 80s made no sense whatsoever. But of course I still promised to help coach Gawain with his dancing.<br /> <br /> Calamity also used this opportunity to pitch an idea for a \u201cvery special evening\u201d of Dream House entertainment. She wants us to stage a gender-swapped version of something called \u201cCannibal: The Musical.\u201d I looked it up on my smart phone as the others were talking about it, and apparently its sort of a cult classic loosely based on the true story of Alferd Packer, the only man ever convicted of cannibalism in the United States (most cannibals take the murder rap instead). The few clips I\u2019ve seen of it are amateurish but genuinely amusing, so I think it just might work. As creative director of the Dream House, I\u2019ve insisted that I see the whole film before I agree to this plan, though.<br /> <br /> So that\u2019s the last day or so in a nutshell. I have my fingers crossed that one of those agents will give me a call in the next day or two with some work. I have my date with Oleander to look forward to tonight. I have the exciting tingle of a new project on the horizon with this silly cannibal show. And I have D. Always. <i>Siempre</i>.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T14:07:23-07:00","id":595958,"title":"","content":"<b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> <u><b><b><u>Thursday June 26<sup>th</sup></u></b></b></u><br /> <br /> Days Without Stabbing: 9<br /> <br /> Clarity is strange. I mean, I had noticed that I was slipping, that things were all a bit less distinct and it was harder to focus on what was really there. I was aware but working with Dr Emmett to focus on and dismiss those little flickers of Wyrd rather than just trying to ignore them made me realize just how frequent and persistent they've been getting. Ignoring them is accepting them and that leads to getting used to them and the slide into simply forgetting that this isn't Arcadia. I've heard stories of what can happen when a Changeling loses track completely of reality. I can't let that happen to me. I won't let that happen to me.<br /> <br /> According to the doctor, it is not all that different from Schizophrenia and anti-psychotic medication can actually help. But given the time involved and the side effects, she doesn't think I'm so far gone that we need to go that route. Yay for small victories? Go me for realizing I was crazy before I was too crazy to notice? At any rate, the flickers are still there but I'm much more conscious of them and working on actively discounting them rather than ignoring them and Dr Emmett assures me that's the right solution. She is a real doctor and she's done this before so I have reason to doubt her. Besides, facing a problem head on always satisfying.<br /> <br /> She also knew right away that something significant had happened since Tuesday and asked me straight out what it was. Given how little I actually got from Dahlia so far, it's not something I really wanted to talk about, at least not yet, and I know she doesn't want it to be common knowledge. I tried to dismiss the question. Note to self, Dr Emmett is a highly trained observer of human nature and thus very good at seeing through bullshit. Corollary, Dr Emmett is not afraid to call me out on said bullshit. I imagine she's modified her style a bit to suit me, because I'm not sure most people would be comfortable with such brutal directness. But then being comfortable isn't really how you get better is it? No pain no gain? At any rate, I hadn't gotten all of the word nothing out before she literally called bullshit on me and reminded me that the first and second rule of therapy club is that I'm honest with her. When I told her it involved someone else's secrets and I couldn't go into detail she nodded and accepted it. I told her I'd met someone else from Snow Globe, but had not had the chance to talk to them. I did not miss the interest that came to her eyes as she listened and asked me why it was so important to me. I explained that there were things about Snow Globe I was unsure about, that I wasn't sure if there had been deeper motives to what was going on than I'd believed. She did point out that in her admittedly limited experience, things were rarely what they seemed in Arcadia. From the way she said it, I get the idea that she finds all of this quite fascinating. I do hope she never lets that curiosity lead her to doing something stupid or dangerous. The price tag for all this cool magical power is way too damn high and even the Hedge is awfully dangerous for a normal human.<br /> <br /> So yeah, we agreed to table that topic for now at least. She's not the one I want to talk to about Snow Globe anyway. I guess I do know more about why Dahlia pinged so hard on the Calamity meter when we first met (besides, you know, being such a hard ass both literally and figuratively and wearing violence like a slinky nightgown). But she's also from Snow Globe. I can fucking talk to her about things without having to explain them. I don't have to sound like I'm laying out the plates at my pity party for her grok how fucked up shit was. I can compare notes with her. I can answer these questions or at least get some clues. Madam Spidertoes outed her at tea so I didn't find out too much. Fuck I shouldn't have pressed her for as much as I did but when she admitted it I lost all sense.<br /> <br /> She really did not want me to know, that much is clear. From the bits she did admit, she was apparently such a tattle-tail that the others came lynch-mob style and threw her down the well. She seemed really ashamed of how much she'd wanted the candy, which makes sense. I'm not sure anyone who hasn't eaten the damn stuff would really understand the things we did to get more of it. Fuck, I'm kinda terrified at the notion of what I'd do for more it right now to be honest. I do know that she escaped very shortly after I arrived but we never really met there. Seems that when they threw her down the well it was full of dead things that tried to drown her, but she fought them off and swam and swam through the darkness until she was suddenly out. She showed me (well all three of us really) something, when she pressed on her face water seeped from her eyes and nose and ears and mouth. She said none of us got out without a scar. She did agree to speak to me more about it later, in private. I shall at least try not to descend upon her like the Spanish Inquisition but the prospect of answers and comparing notes is strong. I hope her reluctance was based on Insincere Marguerite and Madam Spidertoes being present and maybe some concern that I would look down on her for who she was there.<br /> <br /> I have to admit, hearing what she had to say about the well was troublesome on a personal level. I pushed Timmy into that well. At the very least, he died a far more horrific death than I realized. But if there is a way out through there, could he get out? Is he one of those things now? Is that where the ones that disappear end up? Many questions, few answers. Talking to Dahlia might not answer all of them, but it will give me more to go on. What she has told me does suggest some disturbing trends. I know of three of us now. All of us are female. All of us are murderous. She and I were both quite good at spying, even as much as I rebelled against the proper facade I was damn good at spying and did it well and often. Even without learning more, I can no longer deny that I am indeed the sort of monster They wanted me to be. But why? What was the purpose? How can I avoid doing what They made me to do unless I know what that is? I cannot help but think of that other girl. Did she choose to die rather than follow the rule of the courts or was it to escape being the creature The Whispering Voices wanted her to be? Because FUCK THAT NOISE. I won't be Their girl but damn if I am going to kill myself to avoid it.<br /> <br /> And maybe that's what They really want...<br /> <br /> Conditioned to hate rules and obeying. Kept weak and helpless until there is nothing but seething rage inside. Sent into the world to wreak havoc and chaos and destruction upon my fellow Lost.<br /> <br /> Fuck. That makes a hell of a lot of sense. Way too much fucking sense. Shit. It seems crazy to spend that much time crafting a weapon to cast it out at random. If They went to that much effort there must be more to the plan than set the crazy murdergirl loose and see how many Changelings she kills before they put her down. Psychological warfare? Making the Freehold less likely to trust Lost? Seems thin. Better to make a good little infiltrator and have them betray the Freehold. Good intel and paranoia. I'm too obvious for that. Maybe I'm not as good as They intended? No, both Dahlia and that strangler (I need to learn what her name was) didn't fit in any less noticeably than I do. No, I am intentional and there must be a reason for it. They make us into weapons, that is clear. But who was I meant for? Fuck, the answers just lead to more questions. I have to talk to Dahlia. Have to see what she knows, compare notes. Are there more of us out there? Okay, now I am starting to just spin my wheels. I am not going to get anywhere until I learn more.<br /> <br /> And as many questions as it raises (and as much as I might not like what they are) the prospect of fucking answers makes me a happy monster. Impatient, but happy. The doctor is helping. Gawain's oneiromancy went well both in terms of helping Desiree and as an audition for the Family of Silent Nights. I still wish I'd been able to help out with that. Not that Handsome needs it mind you, but I want to be part of something that's so important to him. And I need to find ways to heal rather than harm. There was a time when that was so fucking important to me. And despite what Insincere Marguerite says, the road to medical school is way too long now to be reasonable. But I can fucking do this with him. I've got a knack for it and with time I could be really damn good at it. As talented at it as he is, together we could be fucking amazing. We WILL be fucking amazing.<br /> <br /> So, since pretending to sweep the bedroom while he was working wasn't really an option, I was a bit at a loss last night with what to do with myself. Jacob left with Tamera, most likely for his own entitlement or maybe some Winter Court business. And Lori went out with De la Rocha. Apparently her Summer Court lover is rubbing off on her in more than just sexy bedtime ways. They went out cruising bars doing the ol' bait and switch, Lori flirted until De la Rocha had an excuse to start a fight with whichever poor soul had fallen into the honeytrap. Mmm... always fun times. You know, Gawain and I haven't played that game in way too long... Anyway, that had the both of them occupied as well. But by fortunate coincidence, Insincere Marguerite and Julia had decided to take the quiet evening to have a picnic on the roof and they invited me to join them. I was a touch hesitant just because I didn't want to intrude on what would have otherwise been a private moment. But they assured me it was fine and I did want to watch the two of them together. At the end of tea, Madam Spidertoes and Insincere Marguerite had a somewhat unsettling exchange. Spidertoes asked my darkling sister if De la Rocha was hers and she told our matriarch that she was. There was a moment and then Madam Spidertoes seemed to acknowledge the answer and we went about our way. Given De la Rocha and Spidertoes history and how overwhelming Spidertoes can be it was most certainly the right answer to give. But I also know Insincere Marguerite was a thief in Arcadia and she certainly has a way of considering pretty much everything to be hers. I know that Julia is very much hers but having spoken to her I know she is aware of it and beyond having some conflicting feelings about enjoying the idea being that she's a Changeling and all she is quite consenting. Still, Dahlia spoke of Insincere Marguerite's conquests not being entirely the same afterward as one of the reasons she was not inclined to be among them. And I have been awfully intent on my own navel lately so I'm making sure to keep an eye on her and the ladies that share her bed just to be sure it's all good. After all, those Arcadian mannerisms do sneak up on us. But once we got home, seeing how De la Rocha got almost confrontational over some of Insincere Marguerite's comments about Madam Spidertoes underscored that laying claim to keep Madam Spidertoes from considering trying to reclaim the girl was a good thing.<br /> <br /> So, I wasn't too worried and the picnic was free of any red flags. It was actually quite nice to just watch and enjoy seeing Julia and Insincere Marguerite being affectionate but I never felt like I was a third wheel or anything. It was relaxing. I really don't ever just stop and bask in the moonlight and enjoy the view and the quiet company of my family often enough. And at some point, I think sparked by the pair of them discussing Poland's entry in Eurovision, the idea of having the Dream House do a burlesque version of Cannibal the Musical came up. I rather promptly called dibs on the role of French the trapper. And afterward, the Internet was quite helpful in getting me up to speed on the initial topic. I will just say that after watching that churning I have some thoughts on just what to spread that butter on...<br /> <br /> The motley as a whole seemed fairly receptive to doing a gender-swapped Cannibal production, though Lori insisted that she as the creative director she was not going to okay the idea before she'd seen it. Fair enough honestly, but I imagine she'll be on board. Also, I was so busy laying claim to the trapper that I totally didn't even think about the fact that I have firmly placed myself on stage as part of the show. I mean, it's a secondary role but holy frankenfuck I didn't even think about the whole on stage part when I was talking to them about it. I am worlds better than I was just a month ago but am I really ready to share a stage with Lori and the other performers? And as the Dream House's business manager, I guess it also falls on me to make sure we don't get sued for doing this. Hadn't thought about that one till just now.<br /> <br /> Gawain made his famous crepes since Juan Carlos and Desiree where both there. He didn't go on about it too much but he did say that while he hadn't repaired all of the damage he had made a solid start on it and Juan-Carlos was suitably impressed with his skills and prepared to act as his sponsor. There was some well deserved pride in his voice and I was quite pleased that things had gone well. And we also had a visit from Captain Jack to speak to Gawain about some ideas for their next 'confrontation'. He was thinking a dance off would be entertaining and that it needed to be arraigned to end with them both throwing down a hammer-dance as the finale. That sounds silly and fun and I'm most likely going to end up as part of it, rolling in to provide fedoras to myself and Gawain and a spot of break-dancing to it's tricky. I guess given it's Gawain and myself that makes me Penn, which I am alright with. Lori seemed quite happy to coach Gawain on dancing. I did also take the opportunity to speak to Jack about his knife juggling skills. At some point, I'm going to throw knives at him and he will, naturally, catch and juggle them. Key is to make sure I run out of knives before he runs out of juggling skills. Then I shall most likely stomp my foot in a dramatic and overly girly fashion and go fetch Gawain. Not sure the framework for it honestly, but we are going to start practicing with three knives and see how things go from there.<br /> <br /> Also, at some point, I really think I need to call him and have a quiet and calm conversation over a meal with him as Joaquin rather than Captain Jack. I know some folks have been thinking of trying to play matchmaker with him and John Lowjack, especially after seeing them together here Tuesday night. And while there is most certainly something between them still this is old wounds and stirring up the past rather than just abruptly putting two ladies that are obviously head over heels for each other unexpectedly into each others arms while dancing.<br /> <br /> Annika spoke to me while she was here to do my lesson yesterday. Seems Kimberly did take my advice and speak to Louis and Ji Wen Ja, which is good. Annika doesn't think the girl is innocent but frankly doesn't care and wants them to leave her alone. Which shouldn't get ugly since they are focused on the harassment of White Maria which is related but not Kimberly's handiwork. What worries me more is that Becky does care about Kimberly's part in Sundown Kwan's death. Annika does not like it, I can tell, but she knows just how dangerous getting between Becky and her prey is and doesn't seem to have an inflated sense of her own prowess. Still, love makes people stupid and sometimes that means you stand your ground no matter how much of an ass kicking you're signing up for.<br /> <br /> Fuck, now I'm ending this on a down note. I could investigate this more directly, but I don't really believe that the truth will defuse things between Dark Kimberly and Becky. And Kimberly has avoided opening up and trusting me already. I'm guessing she either fears that I won't help her or can't help her in the face of whatever exactly she's afraid of. She's probably right. The smart move would be to just leave this whole mess be. But fuck it, I am feeling ornery. Why just watch a train wreck when you can jump in and be part of it right?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Well, today started off light-hearted and moved into more serious territory the later it got. There was much silly conversation over breakfast about the pros and cons of ice in drinks. Basically the European vs American views on drinks. Insincere Marguerite was of the opinion that Americans put too much ice in their drinks. Lorelei argued that cold drinks taste better. I agreed with both of them, so didn\u2019t really interject my opinion. I appreciate having cold or cool drinks, even after my stay with the Lady, since growing up as a child our sodas tended to be warm or cool from the fridge. I do agree that sometimes there is too much ice in drinks here, but I do like it. <br /> <br /> After that we moved on to deciding who represented which decade. Lori is the 70\u2019s, Calamity is the 80\u2019s. We didn\u2019t assign one to me, which is fine. I feel disconnected from my childhood anyway, since so much more time passed in the Lady\u2019s realm than it did here. So, we talked about fashions from those two decades. Big hair, shoulder pads, leg warmers, etc\u2026 We even briefly talked about drugs. Cocaine was big in the 80\u2019s, Lori admitted that if she hadn\u2019t been taken she likely would have tried it, if for no other reason than to annoy her father. Like I said, light-hearted conversation. Mostly.<br /> <br /> So, after that conversation we all split up to do our separate things. Lorelei went to talk to an agent to see about modeling jobs. She left shortly before Annika arrived to have her dance lesson with Calamity. During said lesson Gawain swept the audience area and surreptitiously watched his girlfriend strut on stage. I tried telling him that he could just sit down and watch since it was his girl up there. He kept going on about how there where rules about these things and wouldn\u2019t let me take his broom away. I wasn\u2019t going to force the issue, so I left him to his \u201ccovert\u201d watching.<br /> <br /> Last night, and after further thought this morning, I decided which jeep I liked best. The dark blue one. It\u2019s got a thousand more miles on it than the other one, but it\u2019s in really good shape and actually cheaper than the light blue one. I also like the idea of being able to take the roof and doors off if I wanted. So, Luna and I went to go get the dark blue jeep. It was a pretty straightforward deal. I got a cashier\u2019s check for the amount and we had a notary at the bank sign the title over to me. Done and done. After that Luna and I decided to go for a little picnic in the new jeep. We had just started driving out when Insincere Marguerite called and asked us to come back to the Dream House. She said that Calamity had something to tell us, as in the motley, and wanted to do it only once. I got the impression that it was something personal. And I was right.<br /> <br /> Calamity and Insincere Marguerite had been to have tea with Madame Spidertoes, and ended up learning something interesting while they were there. Apparently they weren\u2019t the only guests. Dahlia was also there, and it was information concerning her that had Calamity preoccupied. Apparently Dahlia is also from Snow Globe. Madame Spidertoes revealed this, much to Dahlia\u2019s chagrin and Calamity\u2019s interest. I can only assume that Spidertoes just came out with this information without consulting Dahlia first because she has lost touch with social niceties. Madame Spidertoes is old, very old, and not very good with people. There is perhaps a bit too much distance there, but I\u2019m not sure if it\u2019s something that can be fixed, or if she wants to fix it.<br /> <br /> Dahlia was less than inclined to talk about Snow Globe, but she did give some details. She mentioned that the well was a way out of that place, but not everyone got out. Some people that went into the well didn\u2019t die, but they didn\u2019t really live either. Zombies? Maybe? This upset Calamity more than a little bit because way back when she was there she dropped Timmy down the well. It is uncertain what happened to him after that. Ideas were bounced around that he might have escaped. And if he did, would he be upset with Calamity or not? He could also be a zombie, but we didn\u2019t dwell overmuch on that possibility. <br /> <br /> Calamity said that she didn\u2019t press Dahlia for any more details about her durance this morning, but did say that she might talk to her handler more about it later, and in private. Calamity also said that Dahlia\u2019s reaction to the whole topic of Snow Globe made her think that perhaps Dahlia had done things that she wasn\u2019t proud of while in that realm, hence not wanting to talk about it. She looked at me when she said that. And that is something I can understand more than most. Nobody\u2019s durance is a happy time, but some escape with less \u201cdamage\u201d than others. Most people are the victims during their time in Arcadia. They had things done to them that they wish hadn\u2019t happened. Some people were made to do things, bad things that they regret later. Then there are those of us that freely did those bad things. I don\u2019t know where Dahlia falls in that spectrum, or if she should even be placed in it to begin with. <br /> <br /> Whatever happened to her in Arcadia shaped who she is now. She has a severe dislike of loyalists and is paranoid about who might be one. So either she was hurt by a loyalist in the past and has a healthy mistrust of them, was betrayed by someone that turned out to be a loyalist, or she was one and knows just how tricky we they can be. I can understand that. I\u2019m well familiar with how they operate, at least for the most part, and have a healthy respect for their abilities. They are all different though. I encountered emissaries of other Keepers when I was in the Lady\u2019s service and found that some of them were much bolder and more straightforward than Rook and I were. Others were as sneaky, if not more so than us. I guess it all depends on who they served and what their purpose was. Some Keepers changed their subject\u2019s minds forcefully, while others inspired genuine feelings from their followers. I can say that while I served the Lady I did it out of love. Or at least what I thought was love at the time. I was devoted to her and her cause and it was freely given. It wasn\u2019t until my last trip to \u201cthe world,\u201d to Claire Falls that I started to doubt my Lady and my purpose. <br /> <br /> I honestly don\u2019t know what changed, but something did. It felt like something thawed inside me, no pun intended. Maybe it was because Diane was genuinely worried for my health and worked to heal me when she didn\u2019t have to. She was warm and caring and used all of her mundane medical skills to treat my injuries. She was told not to use her Spring court abilities to heal me and I can understand why. They didn\u2019t want a dangerous loyalist being mobile and getting away. I think they also wanted time to \u201cwork on me.\u201d To convince me to leave the Lady. Liam, the motley\u2019s leader, seemed genuinely interested in my wellbeing and in giving me a second chance. He talked to me about leaving the Lady\u2019s service and becoming a productive member of society. Their man Travers wanted nothing more than to continue to beat me into a bloody smear. I\u2019m glad they made sure he stayed away. He could have easily killed me. Even at full strength I don\u2019t think I could take him in single combat. He just hits too hard and too fast. Granted, he wasn\u2019t alone the last time I fought him, but he was still hard to hurt and his punches cracked ribs with very little effort on his part.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m still debating whether or not to tell Boss Lowjack about my past. Darke and his folks found out more than I\u2019d like them to know, but it might be something that they can use against me later if I\u2019m not careful. If I\u2019m up front with Lowjack now it could help mitigate future unpleasantness. Or it could cause problems in the immediate future. Maybe I should ask my motley mates about it and see what they think I should do. I do realize this kind of makes me a hypocrite. Sort of. I\u2019ve shared the secret of my past with these people, when I was at my very worst, but I haven\u2019t told them about my little side business selling drugs at the bar. Maybe because I\u2019m still doing it, and don\u2019t have any immediate plans to stop. I should probably feel bad about selling this stuff to people and making their lives harder, but I don\u2019t. I used to feel a twinge every once and a while, but after the fight with the Mothership\u2019s minions it just doesn\u2019t seem all that bad. These people know what they\u2019re getting into when they buy this shit from me. No one is forcing them. That came out kind of cold, didn\u2019t it?<br /> <br /> Wow\u2026talk about tangents. Anyhoo\u2026after the whole conversation about tea with Madame Spidertoes Gawain took Calamity aside to make sure that his girl was okay. A lot of stuff must have been dredged up just thinking about Snow Globe. I know Calamity has questions about the place and how things were. I think she wants to talk to Dahlia about her experiences and see if they match up with hers. So, Gawain and Calamity had their little chat. It was kind of cute. At the end Gawain picked up Calamity and spun her around. They were both wearing big grins and it was just too cute. I took a picture or three and sent the best one to the happy couple.<br /> <br /> As has become usual, before the show White Maria checked her gun at the bar. Sometimes I wonder where she got an SMG from. Let\u2019s see\u2026what happened after that. I saw Gawain talking to Desiree. I\u2019m assuming it has to do with the dream healing that Gawain was going to do for her. If Gawain needs Juan-Carlos to observe him at work he might have asked Desiree if she minded the extra company. That\u2019s my guess anyway.<br /> During the show Tamara joined me at the bar. She asked if after the show I wouldn\u2019t mind going back to talk to Lowjack. I said sure. I figured it had to do with the Knighthood of the Utmost Silence and whether or not I\u2019m in. I\u2019ll admit I had been nervous about that. It was like waiting to get your grade back on a test and see if you passed. Sort of. I don\u2019t actually have a lot of comparisons. I was just chosen by the Lady to be her Knight, there was no waiting to see if I got in or not. Like I said, I don\u2019t have the best comparisons.<br /> <br /> Tamara had a few drinks and started to get chatty. They all do. She asked me if people were sure that Desiree was not a loyalist. Her question was asked rather suggestively so I gently informed her that yes it seems that she is not a loyalist, but that she is kind of involved with someone right now. That little bit of news was not taken all that well. It wasn\u2019t all that bad, but she was disappointed. Seems that Tamara is lonely and wanted Desiree\u2019s company. She also admitted to missing the Handmaidens. I reminded her that those two are not healthy for her. She admitted that was true, but still really missed them. I couldn\u2019t think of anyone that might make a good match for her, so I kept silent on that part. Gawain and Calamity seem to be the matchmakers. Maybe I should talk to them about who might make a good, and healthy, companion for Tamara.<br /> <br /> After the show I drove Tamara back to Lowjack\u2019s bar. She wasn\u2019t drunk, but she\u2019d had a few drinks and there was no reason to get into unnecessary trouble for driving while under the influence. So we got to the bar and made our way to Lowjack\u2019s private office. And there, with very little pomp and/or circumstance, I was inducted into the Knighthood of the Utmost Silence. This will make the second time that I have been made a Knight for someone/thing, but this time I can be proud of it. Lowjack also explained that he was what is called the Quiet Marshall for this area. The Quiet Marshall is kind of the person in charge of an area\u2019s Knights and hands out jobs and such. But, because he is also the Winter monarch, he put Tamara in place as acting Quiet Marshall. So, I guess that Lowjack is my monarch and my boss. Yeah, not a big difference from how things were before. Anyhoo\u2026he said that there are no active jobs right now so things were quiet, no pun intended. He\u2019ll let me know if anything comes up that needs attention though. <br /> <br /> **** **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Breakfast as usual was delicious. We had crepes. Juan Carlos was here for breakfast as well, so I\u2019m assuming he and Gawain did their thing to try and help Desiree. I hope they can help her get rid of that \u201ctrigger.\u201d I would be terrified if I knew that at literally the flick of a switch someone could control my actions, and I would have no defense against it. No way to stop. I know what kind of damage I can do when I am in control of my actions, I don\u2019t want to know what would happen if someone could direct me like a puppet to do their bidding. Not a pleasant thought. So, I hope that Gawain and Juan Carlos can help Desiree. Gawain told the rest of us that things went well last night, but that they weren\u2019t done yet. They at least made a good start though.<br /> <br /> Calamity went to her second therapy session this morning, before most of us even got up. She came back in a really good mood, so I\u2019m assuming things went pretty well with the therapist. I was glad to see it. Calamity has been on edge an awful lot lately, granted it\u2019s been with good reason, but it was still good to see her so relaxed and happy. She almost didn\u2019t even bat an eye when Lorelei announced that she had fun instigating a bar fight last night. A few of us stopped and looked at her. Insincere Marguerite even licked her to make sure that she was really our Lori. She is. Apparently Lori and De la Rocha went out to a bar last night and Lorelei used her wiles to get folks to flirt with her, then De la Rocha got \u201cangry\u201d and there was a fight. Good for stress relief and collecting glamor. They both had fun and neither of them got hurt, so that\u2019s good.<br /> <br /> Then of course what day is complete without Captain Jack coming by? The good Captain showed up and started conspiring with Gawain on their next \u201cencounter.\u201d I didn\u2019t listen to all of the planning, but apparently there is going to be some sort of dance off. Something involving Break dancing and Hammerpants. I\u2019ll admit, I had to look that one up. And since we were on the topic of acts, Calamity asked Jack how many knives he can juggle at one time. I think she was planning for their knife throwing and juggling act that they\u2019ve been wanting to do. She assured him that she didn\u2019t want to throw more knives into the mix than he could safely handle. They agreed to practice with three and see how it goes. I\u2019ll admit, I\u2019m looking forward to that. There was also something about putting on a gender-swapping production of \u201cCannibal the Musical.\u201d I had to look that one up too. Looks seriously silly. I\u2019m looking forward to that too.<br /> <br /> Then on a more serious note, Gawain asked Captain Jack about the phone numbers that we had him trace from the night Desiree\u2019s \u201cswitch was flipped.\u201d As it turns out the phones were burners so there is no real way to trace who they belong to. I know the others were as frustrated at the news as I was. It makes sense though. If you\u2019re going to do something like that over a phone you don\u2019t want to use you own. Of course the mere fact that the phones were burners points to a non-Gentry culprit. It may still be a loyalist, but it would have to be someone that spends enough time in \u2018the world\u2019 to understand how all that stuff works. Calamity suggested that it might be someone in the Winter court, but I pointed out that Darke and his people wouldn\u2019t have triggered Desiree and let her go. If they were going to do anything it would be to capture her and reprogram her. Or she would have just disappeared. Whatever else Darke may be, he does have the best interests of the Freehold in mind. Gawain agreed with me on that, well the first part anyway. He didn\u2019t comment so much on the later bit.<br /> <br /> The other reasoning behind it not being a Gentry that triggered her, is that it was done sloppily. If it was the Gentry that actually set up the switch in the first place they would know how to activate it properly. Other ideas were bounced around. Perhaps another changeling? Perhaps someone from the Phantom Tong? It doesn\u2019t really matter which person/group is behind it, we need to get the trigger removed soon. We can figure out the \u201cwho\u201d later. Gawain also pointed out that now that the business with the Mothership is done, there are less distractions and they might make another move. This is certainly a possibility, and one that we will need to be mindful of. On the flipside, they might not try anything else since we\u2019re aware of what\u2019s going on. They may call it a loss and leave off. I know that once my cons were known to someone I would not try it again in the same area in case they told friends about what had happened. Makes sense. If your opponent knows what you\u2019re going to do, or what your usual tactics are, then they can plan for it. Which means that we need to try and plan based on the past actions of those that used Desiree. Plan for the worst, hope for the best.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> A pleasant evening, a pleasant picnic on the roof, a pleasant breakfast. It has been a good day all around. Mostly.<br /> <br /> At breakfast yesterday the Motley would up drifting into American trends by decade, or as the Motley seemed to believe trends by decade. While some have holes in their knowledge that seem odd, Lorelei has odd knowledge in the holes of time she was gone. She mentioned the song \u201cTake On Me\u201d by A-Ha, noting it to be the only Norwegian song to hit number one in the USA. I asked if she had ever heard Norwegian music? I was sure it was terrible. Norwegians are good for some things, of course, like surviving the cold but music not so much. She spoke of death metal and \u201cCookie Monster Vocals\u201d but nothing that sounded remotely appealing. Certainly.<br /> <br /> I have not listened to Muppets sing on purpose since I was much smaller.<br /> <br /> That afternoon, Calamity and I had tea with Madam Spidertoes and Dahlia. It passed rather pleasantly. Well, mostly. Apparently Calamity and Dahlia shared a Durance, which she revealed as was intimated by Spidertoes. It was certainly not her idea. Calamity was (naturally) curious but Dahlia quieted quickly after the revelation. I was sure Madam Spidertoes presence affected that. Clearly.<br /> <br /> As I felt Spidertoes asked me if De La Rocha was mine. She noted she knew of the relationship but asked the question very specifically. I confirmed she was. For one thing, she is. For another\u2026I know she managed to escape Spidertoes web once but I would not want to risk Spidertoes trying to catch her again. Not that I am saying that is Spidertoes intention, but it certainly well crossed my mind.<br /> <br /> We returned and explained to the others what had occurred. De La Rocha was\u2026edgy\u2026about my comments about Spidertoes. She argued angrily with I, as is her way, but seeing how she reacted only made me more sure I did the right thing saying she belonged to I. Definitely.<br /> <br /> Madame Spidertoes is powerful, and keeps the Darklings in line through fear and respect. I think we all feel a bit\u2026overpowered\u2026by her. She does, however, brew excellent tea, has adorable flatware and cups, and throws a good tea party. Obviously.<br /> <br /> Having the party in an abandoned building also reminded I that I still need to go urban exploring with Jacob. Eventually.<br /> <br /> The show was fairly smooth. Desiree arrived with Princess Jolie. I spoke them (Jolie especially) briefly. She was well, relieved to not have the responsibilities of leadership, but concerned about some of the Spring Court rifts. Chalcedony was there too. Maybe or maybe not to torment Desiree. Her showing up lead Ginny Green to show. Creepy.<br /> <br /> Afterwards, Gawain went with Juan-Carlos and Desiree to work on repairing her mind. Lorelei and De La Rocha went to get in a barfight. Summer Courtiers. Julia suggested having a late dinner on the roof. Calamity seemed a bit forlorn so we decided to invite her. She seemed pleased to attend. Julia ran out for Sandwiches and we had a very nice on roof picnic. Romantically.<br /> <br /> It was nice, I think. Sitting under the moon, watching the Pacific Coast Highway and Ocean in the distance. It was not full, but it was close. Julia was so beautiful in the pale light. Calamity actually smiled genuinely for the first time I have seen in awhile, the stress briefly gone from her eyes. Our little Darkling family celebrated under the moon. Happily.<br /> <br /> We discussed a few things\u2026Julia was keep to discuss De La Rocha\u2019s behavior. She liked to tease a torch may be being carried (did I write that right in English?) We also discussed doing a the show of <i>Cannibal: The Musical</i> with an entirely gender reversed cast.<br /> <br /> Julia wears full skirts to the roof. I wonder what she would do without Contracts of Darkness to shimmy up and down. She dresses like a girl even compared to Lorelei. This pleases I. Absolutely.<br /> <br /> Juan-Carlos and Desiree were at breakfast, and Captain Jack joined us. We discussed the idea of doing <i>Cannibal</i>, and everyone seemed to like the idea, though Lorelei had not seen it. It was suggested I should play the chief, since I am \u201cthe most racist.\u201d Where do they even get such an idea about I? I am not racist. Anymore.<br /> <br /> That said, a white person pretending to be Japanese \u201cpretending\u201d to be an Indian might not go over as well as just a Japanese person doing it.<br /> <br /> Also, there was talk of a \u201cDance Off\u201d with Gawain and Captain Jack. Which sounded fun, though perhaps outside of Gawain\u2019s talents. Maybe Captain Jack is secretly trying to turn Gawain into a performer. I confess he had a few good ideas. Also, Julia does not like the <i>Dirty Dancing</i>. The rest of the Motley just does not like I comparing the <i>Dirty Dancing</i> Patrick Swayze to himself in <i>Donnie Darko</i>.<br /> <br /> At least I was not the one to bring up <i>Ghost</i>. Ugh. I agree with Julia on that one. Obviously.<br /> <br /> Regardless, spirits were high. Calamity\u2019s therapy seemed to go well, and while we are concerned about a lot of things, it seems a lot of smiles are in the Dream House. Just the way I like it. Definitely.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXXIV</i><br /> <br /> Okay lets see.<br /> <br /> The game was slightly heavier than usual on IC because I had a mild toothache from a hard part of my sandwich that night. I\u2019m doing better now. It was aggravating and distracting, though. Of course, my games are IC anyway.<br /> <br /> Touching on discussions, pop culture discussion ran hot and heavy as it often does in this game, as people who have lost time in very different eras compare notes. Thus you get everything from Cannibal: The Musical to A-Ha. One thing that may be less familiar to American readers is the discussion between Calamity, Insincere Marguerite and Julia referenced Poland\u2019s entry into the 2014 Eurovision song contest. It\u2019s\u2026<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q8J3GAg5zaI\" target=\"_blank\">racy</a> to say the least, and NSFW.<br /> <br /> As a note on clothes and NPCs, since it was brought up a time or two, De La Rocha tends to wear a combination of leather, fishnet and denim much of the time\u2026more riot grrl less Cher, though. Julia wears gowns and very conservative dresses, and has been seen once outside an ankle-length skirt. Luna dresses in what most people would call comfortable or casual. The Ball was the only time she or De La Rocha were seen in anything feminine. Captain Jack\u2019s wardrobe varies wildly but is always colorful and ostentatious.<br /> <br /> The tea party (patterned off Sluagh tea parties from Dreaming, Spidertoes could be a Sluagh with little translation issue) actually was RP\u2019d earlier, since it was a planned event only Calamity and Insincere Marguerite would see. It took place after the previous night\u2019s session of Night Train Detective Agency, my Demon: The Descent campaign.<br /> <br /> I think that covers everything, but if you have any questions comments and questions are welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T05:34:45-07:00","id":599241,"title":"","content":"First, I have to say I absolutely love how dynamic your campaign feels. So many deep NPCs, so many mysteries, secrets and plots, so much interaction... I dream of breathing so much life in my stories.<br /> <br /> Second, I'm curious about a few things:<br /> Does Calamity's therapy have some mechanical effect or is it only RP?<br /> Do some members of the freehold such as Madam Spidertoes and Master Darke belong to High Wyrd Entitlements?<br /> How big are Lorelei's social dice pools?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T15:42:19-07:00","id":599875,"title":"","content":"Hey there Anteros, and thanks for the kind words. My WoD games tend to be heavy sandbox, and as noted, tend to be just lousy with plots and NPCs...I like to run very social games. As with anyone else feel free to use and tinker with ideas here...it is part of why I have the threads here! <br /> <br /> 1) Calamity's Therapy uses the therapy rules in <i>Rites of Spring</i>, namely when her therapist gets enough success, she can raise her Clarity at x2 rather than x3 cost for that one dot as long as she does so in the next month. It also gives an excuse to raise one's Clarity. So she is getting a game benefit from it.<br /> <br /> 2) Some Freehold members do belong to various entitlements, others don't. Madame Spidertoes is a member of the Office of the Vizieral Counsel from<i> Equinox Road</i>. It's how a woman well over 150 years old looks as fresh as a (monochromatic) daisy. Tommy is a member of two, because of a House Rule I have allowing high Wyrd Changelings to be a member of two so long as they do not conflict in any way...the Scarecrow Ministry from the rulebook and the Lost Pantheon from <i>Lords of Summer</i>, though he has sort of an immortal monster variation. Boss John Lowjack and Tamara are of course with the Knighthood of Utmost Silence (also from <i>Lords of Summer</i>) and Captain Jack is with the Sacred Band of the Golden Standard from the rulebook. Oleander is with the Barony of the Lesser Ones also from LoS and of course Lucian Torrez is rumored to be with the Phantom Tong from <i>Winter Masques</i>. For his part, Master Darke is not actually with an Entitlement. None of the Monarchs were till Boss Lowjack's rise.<br /> <br /> 3) I don't have access to Lori's stat's offhand, I will poke her player. I am sure they will be happy to post.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the feedback and the questions. If you have any more let me know. I do appreciate your kind words and your interest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T16:49:49-07:00","id":599986,"title":"","content":"I just knew Captain Jack was a Gilded Aspirant. He totally rocks that Entitlement!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T03:01:44-07:00","id":600301,"title":"","content":"It is indeed a really deep sandbox Anteros and I very much enjoy playing in the style. <br /> <br /> As far as Calamity's therapy, beyond the cost break and justification forbuying clarity it's also going to be the basis for some shifts to her IC behaviour. One of which is her starting to make use of the meditation rules to gain bonuses on resisting future clarity loss. <br /> <br /> And yes, Captain Jack does indeed rock that entitlement. When I first read about it I had a strong Gaston from Beauty and the Beast image. And while that still fits, I like seeing how Jack spins the idea. <br /> <br /> Oh, and Lori just rolls ALL of the dice I think. ^_^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T14:50:34-07:00","id":603215,"title":"","content":"Hi, Anteros, Lorelei's player here. Welcome to the discussion; we're glad to have you!<br /> <br /> Determining social die pools for Lori is always an adventure, and her selection of Attributes and Skills runs the gamut and presents a wide range of potential dice pools.<br /> <br /> The lowest social pool that's likely to come up for her would probably be Manipulation/Streetwise. If unmodified by any other abilities or mitigating circumstances, that pool would be a measly three dice. Lori is a surprisingly genuine and earnest person for a Fairest Spring Courtier, and she's not used to the &quot;mean streets&quot; of the Malibu/Santa Monica Freehold. Her instinct when such skills are needed is to leave it to someone like de la Rocha or Calamity. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Her <i>highest</i> possible social die pool is a little more difficult to determine. Her Presence and Expression are both five at the moment, and she has several Specialties which apply to her most common rolls, such as Singing, Dancing, etc. Her pledge with her motley gives her an additional +1 to Expression rolls. If her target is attracted to her, she adds two dice due to the four-dot version of the Striking Looks Merit. She can effectively double this bonus by invoking the &quot;Splendor of the Envoy's Protection&quot; clause of the Contracts of Vainglory, adding another two dice. As a Fairest, she can spend Glamour to increase her die pool on Presence rolls at a one-for-one basis (up to a maximum determined by her Wyrd; currently 4 assuming that SotEP was already in effect).<br /> <br /> So that's 20 dice so far on a Presence/Expression (Singing) roll, if she's going all-out. There are other factors that might affect the roll, too. If her audience is entirely composed of Spring Courtiers, she could conceivably add her Mantle of 5, since this roll makes use of supernatural powers but is not &quot;predicated upon&quot; them, as stated in the Changeling rule book (I'd defer judgment on this point to the Baron if it ever came up, of course). So that takes the potential total dice pool up to 25. If she chose to hold back one point on the &quot;Glamour for Presence&quot; trade, she could then use her Enchanting Performance Merit (from <i>Rites of Spring</i>) to make this a 24 die rote action.<br /> <br /> This is, of course, an extreme example. Lorelei has never rolled so many dice on anything, and it's unlikely that all of these powers and situational modifiers would ever come into play on a single roll. Most of her Expression rolls come up to around 14-16 dice if I remember correctly, and other social pools cap a bit lower than that. While her Expression and Persuasion are maxed out, most of her other Social Skills are at more moderate levels. She is definitely the motley's social juggernaut, but this has come at a cost. She's only managed to kill one thing since the campaign began more than a year ago, and that was essentially kill-stealing by attacking something that was already on its last legs. Her entire contribution to the first fight of the campaign was to get knocked out in the surprise round and sleep through it. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> As a Spring Court burlesque performer with such advantages, however, Lorelei rarely wants for Glamour.<br /> <br /> Hope that sates your curiosity on this subject. Let me know if you have any other questions; I rarely tire of talking about my characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2591,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","user":"PenitentTom","date":".  Edited to insert a mysteriously dropped word. 07-26-2015, 12:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T14:56:17-07:00","id":603221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If her audience is entirely composed of Spring Courtiers, she could conceivably add her Mantle of 5, since this roll makes use of supernatural powers but is not &quot;predicated upon&quot; them, as stated in the Changeling rule book (I'd defer judgment on this point to the Baron if it ever came up, of course). </div> </div> </div>Seems legit to me. I might also have her make a general roll for the audience and roll extra dice for the Spring Courtiers to see how much better it was for them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> She's only managed to kill one thing since the campaign began more than a year ago, and that was essentially kill-stealing by attacking something that was already on its legs. </div> </div> </div>She has till killed more people since the game started than Insincere Marguerite or (I think) Ace. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a