started.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T15:08:06-07:00","id":603232,"title":"","content":"Well if we count before the game started I suspect she has killed the least.<br /> <br /> And of course, hedge beast, not person. Whatever makes her feel better. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T15:08:34-07:00","id":603234,"title":"","content":"Thank you for answering!<br /> I feels like I understand your character and her impact better now. No wonder everybody wants her! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Did she start the game with Striking Looks or Enchanting Performance?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T15:19:45-07:00","id":603242,"title":"","content":"No problem, Anteros. I'm glad someone is expressing an interest.<br /> <br /> Yes, Lori started the game with both the Striking Looks and Enchanting Performance Merits, which took most of her merit points (even considering that the Baron is fairly generous about handing out extra points at the start of a campaign). Most of the other powers and abilities mentioned came along later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T15:28:52-07:00","id":603248,"title":"","content":"Ok, thanks.<br /> Do Lorelei and Insincere Marguerite intend to train their combat abilites, or will they continue to specialize in their given domains?<br /> Also, were the romances between PCs something you discussed beforehand or something that happened spontaneously during play?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T15:50:53-07:00","id":603256,"title":"","content":"Well, I can't speak for Marguerite, naturally, but Lori doesn't really intend to increase her combat abilities, beyond <i>maybe</i> a little self-defense instruction if this &quot;combat&quot; thing becomes a bit more of a regular occurrence. One possibility we've kicked around is that Lori will eventually join the Pilgrims of the Endless Road entitlement (from <i>Swords at Dawn</i>), at which point she'll need to improve both her physical and mental stats to show willing. It's more likely that she'll increase her base physical stats and Athletics, though, than working on combat skills in particular. I just can't see Lorelei taking the time and effort to teach herself how to hurt people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T15:57:31-07:00","id":603261,"title":"","content":"Insincere Marguerite is above such behavior.<br /> <br /> Well, that's what she would say. She uses Touch of Paralyzing Shudder, Murkblur, and pushing people off of high places.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T16:10:23-07:00","id":603266,"title":"","content":"On a more serious note, speaking as GM I do try to have some options for people who enjoy action and combat in the game, but I don't really run combat games. It has even been done to have games of all non fighty PCs who get NPCs to fight for them, though with Gawain, Calamity, Jacob and Ace it is not really necessary here. But while being able to destroy your opponents is helpful and can keep people safe, with or without combat (Calamity and Gawain have had people back down because of their prowess and/or gigantic sword) a character like Lorelei or Insincere Marguerite has no trouble participating since combat is rare enough a lack of combat skills is no issue, and both have ways of dealing with threats (Lorelei can be super seductive, or pitiful, or intimidating, and Insincere Marguerite can simply cast a disdainful look, roll her eyes and vanish) . Calamity and Gawain are dangerous enough for two PCs each and Jacob and Ace can hold their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":".  grammar 07-25-2015, 07:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T16:27:33-07:00","id":603280,"title":"","content":"The Pilgrims are one of my favorite entitlements since the time wanted to play a Changeling based on a Drac (a French shapeshifting faerie dragon who lives in underwater palaces, plays tricks and kidnap people to take care of its offsprings in its stead). I needed 3 kiths (Draconic, Mirrorskin and Waterborn).<br /> <br /> I as a bit surprised at Marguerite's relative aversion to violence after reading her intro.<br /> <br /> Will you update the campaign to 2E when it comes out?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T16:49:08-07:00","id":603285,"title":"","content":"Insincere Marguerite is a blazing hypocrite. But generally dislikes violence. She also could not just vanish at the time that story was set, she maxed Smoke later.<br /> <br /> On 2e I will have to see the finished product to know for sure. Apart from not using beats, MDH is fully played in 2e systems already, though, except where there is only a 1e system. Compared to other WoD games, though CtL 2e is a very different game from what I have read though, again, I will judge the finished product not piecemeal.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I will probably Frankenstein in aspects of the systems I like and drop those I don't. As I understand it, every MDH PC would be impossible to make in 2e and would have to lose a Kith and all their Seeming abilities, though I could be wrong. That means we get cases like Lori can't have her super harvesting AND wings, both are which see a lot of use, Calamity has to lose her innate knives or whisperwisping abilties that are key to her evolution into the whispering voices, etc. I could be off on this, of course.<br /> <br /> OTOH, some of the Kith updates are really good, and I will probably use them ( I really like new Palewraith and Windwing, for instance). I suspect I will use the new Clarity rules, though I will need to read them first. I may use the new Seeming Clarity loss/gain rules even if I keep the old nuts and bolts as well, as a more fluid Clarity would benefit from them. I am inclined to think as Contracts will be (IIRC) very different, I will keep the old system for MDH and possibly use the new system in the next game, though if I misread and they are fairly compatible I may just update them...<br /> <br /> In general I have adopted new game systems whole cloth (<b>Requiem, Forsaken</b>, and most of the 2e GMC update save beats, which are unpopular with my group more than my own issue) so it is not impossible but, as I say, 2e is very different than 1e. We will see. I won't decide till I have the book, and I won't decide alone anyway but have us decide as a troupe.<br /> <br /> ETA:<br /> <br /> I missed the Romances question.<br /> <br /> No Romances were planned before the game. Lorelei and Insincere Marguerite were a surprise to no one but not <i>planned</i>. Gawain and Calamity are more or less the exception, as while the players did not pre-decide to have their PCs get together, they started play with a romantic spark.<br /> <br /> While no potential love interests were specifically planned for anyone, Julia Oldacre was originally designed as a dangerous liaison for Lorelei, not a hookup for Insincere Marguerite. Captain Jack was considered as a potential LI for Gawain or Jacob. Most single NPCs were potential love interests, though few were assigned per se.<br /> <br /> Romances tend to play heavily in my campaigns, though...relationship drama you can leave at the table is better than soul crushing real life angst. I think everyone expected some, especially centering on a burlesque house.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 07-25-2015, 07:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T17:30:59-07:00","id":603320,"title":"","content":"As for the romance thing, I had no specific plans for Lorelei to become deeply romantically involved with anyone prior to the start of the campaign. Oh, she'd have intimate liaisons with lots of people, but romance wasn't really in her bailiwick in the beginning. She was supposed to be a love magnet in the beginning... people would fall in love with her, but not vice versa. De la Rocha changed that initial idea pretty quickly once things got started. I love it when characters take on a life of their own and do things I didn't expect.<br /> <br /> Over the course of the campaign, Lori's love for D has only grown, and she's developed true feelings for Marguerite and Julia as well... and maybe Oleander too (see her next journal entry for more on this). She's just thankful she's found so many paramours who don't mind her continuing to sleep with other people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T18:31:53-07:00","id":603352,"title":"","content":"The various romances and assorted drama are tremendously fun to read, so it's awesome to know they're spontaneous. I wonder if Ace feels a bit left out given that he's seemingly not involved with anyone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T22:32:07-07:00","id":603509,"title":"","content":"I like to think they are a strong point of my storytelling. Generally keeps things interesting.<br /> <br /> Ace\u2019s player has not been able to make for awhile due to personal issues and work issues that have come up. We hope he will be able to rejoin us, but remains to be seen. He was not interested in Captain Jack, but had some rapport with the Warlock of Night. Sadly his absence began just after that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T00:01:22-07:00","id":613063,"title":"","content":"Things start to come to a head with the White Maria story. Our Motley takes action and deals with the problem. Or do they?<br /> <br /> Due to stuff going on IRL no Calamity journal this time. Her player has promised a double journal next time dealing with both sessions.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXXV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> June 26th, morning<br /> <br /> Well, that all accelerated quickly. It was a lazy afternoon, full of relaxing and working out and a little bit of business, then Becky showed up and things kinda exploded. Well, not right off, kinda a delayed fuse, you know, but anyway, the afternoon was not a good tell for the evening. At least it all ended well.<br /> <br /> The reason it all exploded when Becky showed up was that she had a favor to ask Calamity. She\u2019d figured out that whoever was terrorizing White Maria was going to again tonight. Well, really, oracular sources just said something bad was going to happen to her, and we didn\u2019t want to assume that was just her, you know, tripping on something or something.<br /> <br /> White Maria was going to the pier to see a local band perform, so Becky wanted Calamity to, you know, shadow her, keep her and anyone in the range of her SMG safe and hopefully catch the terrorizer. Calamity enlisted Insincere Marguerite and Jacob to help with the shadowing part, and me and Lori to be nearby, for a quick getaway, and in case muscle or healing was needed. Of course, that meant catching the others up to speed.<br /> <br /> Lori was not happy to just now learn about it. To be honest, I hadn\u2019t even thought about it - I guess I figured Calamity would tell her? I was also a little distracted. Calamity, though, hadn\u2019t told on purpose, hoping we wouldn\u2019t, you know, \u2018Scooby Gang\u2019 into it. I guess we kinda did anyway though...<br /> <br /> Anyways, the basic plan was pretty simple. Insincere Marguerite would steal the clip from White Maria\u2019s gun, so she wouldn\u2019t, you know, freak out about not having it, but still wouldn\u2019t be able to panic and fire wildly at whoever spooked her and also what was behind them. We couldn\u2019t just tell her she was safe, cause then she might act different and scare the terrorizer off and Becky really wanted to catch them. Insincere Marguerite would stick close even after that, while Calamity and Jacob were prowling around. Lori and I stashed ourselves further down the Promenade, closer to the parking lot, at a little coffee shop place. Note to future self: do not let Lori drink 5 espressos in a matter of hours. Definitely should have cut her off. She might have started vibrating.<br /> <br /> With all that, I think things worked? We definitely got more info, you know? We didn\u2019t see much action until the concert was about over, when Jacob texted to warn us that White Maria was leaving and almost immediately after Insincere Marguerite warned us that there was an unconscious dude in the back of the van. I gave Lori the key, since she\u2019s better at driving that me, and we wanted to unobtrusively follow White Maria home.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite popped into the back by herself a little bit down the road. Apparently, she\u2019d dropped Calamity off to follow a different lead and she explained about the dude. He was one of a bunch of ganger dudes that were eyeing White Maria, waiting for something. She\u2019d chloroformed the one and they\u2019d dispersed without doing anything but that.<br /> <br /> Lori poofed him awake, in between grinning manically and announcing what a tense high speed chase this was, as she checked her blind spot and used her blinker to change lanes, all, you know, a mile or two above the speed limit. I got a good growl going, holding him by the shirt collar. Of course, he didn\u2019t speak English. De la Roche was called over, and between the two of us, we had him terrified. He said they were supposed to observe White Maria, and, if they got a signal, kidnap her to a particular warehouse. We got his boss\u2019 name, an office for him and the address of the warehouse, but that\u2019s it.<br /> <br /> We shared all that with Calamity when she joined us outside White Maria's house. She recognized the boss\u2019 name as the big guy in a decent sized, localish gang, based in LA. It was a kinda moot point though, since her lead had confirmed it was Lucien and filled in the details on the Sundown Kwan story. According to them, she\u2019d been the girlfriend of the head of the Tong gang \u2013 you know, the mortal one, not the Phantom Tong. She\u2019d had a lot of control of the gang through him, and with her powers they\u2019d thrived. Especially when she\u2019d allied with Darke. After she didn\u2019t back down based on some unspecified \u2018warnings\u2019, she\u2019d been killed as an example, specifically to Dark Kimberly, who was something of a rival for the gang boss\u2019 affections. She did know about the hit beforehand, and didn\u2019t say anything, probably either for fear of her own life, or to win that rivalry.<br /> <br /> So Calamity wanted to warn White Maria off, hoping to do that better than the terror campaign, since the presence of the gang dudes was probably a sign that Lucien was tired of waiting for that tack to work. Lori and Jacob went with, Lori to hopefully convince White Maria to drop it without bringing Lucien\u2019s name into it, and Jacob to offer to hide her, if needed. Insincere Marguerite, me and the girlfriends went on home, since we didn\u2019t wanna swamp White Maria or anything, you know? Plus, I was pretty sure I couldn\u2019t help there and it was close to the time to meet Desiree.<br /> <br /> Calamity and the others did get back before we\u2019d started the session. Just before though so I didn\u2019t get to ask what all happened. Calamity looked bummed enough, and was muttering darkly about dragon slaying, that I doubt it was good, you know? Also, she apologized for not being able to help with the dream stuff, but Becky showed up about the same time Calamity did and they clearly needed to talk.<br /> <br /> We wished each other luck and she continued on to the bar while I went upstairs. I only hope she had as much luck as I did. Everything went smooth and as good as I could have hoped. Desiree is a really light dreamer - I had to focus hard, again, to not shatter everything when I stepped in. It did make it easier to shape things back into the theatre, with our half-finished construction work backstage. It was fun, almost like a game, with paint fights and spurts of tension releasing destruction in between the always awesome work of building a strong foundation and the familiar task of helping a performer make some art with stage scenery.<br /> <br /> Going over things carefully near the end of the night, I was happily surprised to find no traces of the switch. Once we\u2019d torn up the wire leading to it, and rebuilt the stage to Desiree\u2019s specifications, it had vanished. And not just moved either, I\u2019m sure of it. Dream Desiree didn\u2019t really know what we were doing, but my happiness was infectious, and the dream dissipated with her kissing me. It was a nice way to wake up.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s early yet, maybe I can go find Calamity and give her a similar awakening.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Okay, so things have accelerated, and a situation I barely knew existed has come to a head. I won\u2019t say things are perfect, and we\u2019re going to have to play things carefully for a while, but I <u>hope</u> we\u2019ve stabilized things in the Freehold for the time being.<br /> <br /> We\u2019d been discussing the redecoration of the Dream House before everything went down. The House is going to officially buy some of the posters Julia\u2019s been creating of our headlining performers (including a few of yours truly) and put them up in the entrance hall and stage area. It gives the house a very bijou feel, and I think it will greatly enhance the ambience of our little theater.<br /> <br /> So Becky Wan came by this afternoon before the show to speak with Calamity. After she\u2019d left, Calamity gathered the motley to ask for help. There\u2019s been bad blood between White Maria and Dark Kimberly lately. White Maria has been looking into the death of one of her friends a few years ago, and she blames Dark Kimberly for the incident. Kimberly has gone into seclusion at Annika\u2019s place, but someone has been terrorizing White Maria for the past week or so.<br /> <br /> Calamity has known about this for a few days. So has Gawain. <u>And</u> Jacob, apparently. I\u2019m not sure why they chose not to let me in on the \u201cfun.\u201d But things came to a crisis point tonight. Becky got word somehow that something bad was going to happen to White Maria tonight. She knew that her friend was going out to Santa Monica pier to listen to a local band, and she assumed that whatever was going down would happen there. She wanted Calamity and maybe some of the rest of us to keep an eye on her, make sure she was safe, stop her from hurting anyone else (she\u2019s taken to carrying a gun wherever she goes as a precaution), and if possible, draw out whoever has been tormenting her.<br /> <br /> Of course, we agreed to do what we could. White Maria\u2019s not exactly a friend (rumor has it that she\u2019s something of a bitch), but I don\u2019t want to see anyone get hurt. And besides, this sort of nonsense is bad for the Freehold. So I called in one of our contracted mortal performers to take over my acts for the night, and we headed out for the pier.<br /> <br /> I also called Oleander before we left. She answered on the second ring. \u201cHey, Lori,\u201d she said, and I could hear the eagerness in her voice. \u201cWhat\u2019s up?\u201d<br /> <br /> I sighed. \u201cSorry, honey,\u201d I said, \u201csomething\u2019s come up. I won\u2019t be performing at the Dream House tonight, and I might have to take a rain check on our date.\u201d<br /> <br /> I could <u>hear</u> her face fall over the phone; it was sort of amazing. \u201cOh,\u201d she said simply.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m really sorry,\u201d I hastened to add, \u201cand I wouldn\u2019t do this if it wasn\u2019t important. It\u2019s Freehold business\u2026 kind of.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, it\u2019s okay Lori. I understand,\u201d she said quickly.<br /> <br /> I reached for something to say. \u201cLook, maybe the motley\u2019s chore won\u2019t take very long,\u201d I said. \u201cIf we finish early, I\u2019ll give you a call, and we can still get together, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay,\u201d she said, sounding a bit mollified. \u201cOnly\u2026 give me a call when you\u2019re done anyway, please,\u201d she continued, \u201cjust so I\u2019ll know you\u2019re okay.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI promise,\u201d I said. I\u2019m glad I did. \u201cOh, and by the way, I had something I wanted to ask you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat\u2019s that?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> I paused before continuing, pondering the best way to bring it up. \u201cD wanted me to ask if you would be open to her joining the two of us some time. You know\u2026 intimately.\u201d<br /> <br /> There was silence on the other end of the line.<br /> <br /> \u201cIf you\u2019re not comfortable with that, we\u2019ll both understand,\u201d I said quickly, \u201cand there will be no hard feelings from either of us, I promise. I just wanted to let you know that it was an option.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay,\u201d she said. \u201cI\u2019ll need to think about it. I know you\u2019re trying to include me, to make me a bigger part of your life, and I appreciate that, but\u2026 I\u2019ll just need to think about it for a while, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSure thing, honey,\u201d I said warmly. \u201cDon\u2019t obsess over it, okay? Whatever you decide is fine with me. Now I should go; I need to get ready to head out. I\u2019ll call you tonight.\u201d We said our goodbyes and I left to dress for the pier.<br /> <br /> Our plan was for Calamity and Jacob to position themselves stealthily on the pier while Marguerite tailed White Maria invisibly. If possible, Marguerite was going to remove the clip from White Maria\u2019s weapon without her realizing it. D \u2013 who hangs out on the pier all the time, and thus would not arouse suspicion \u2013 was going to be nearby in case the others needed backup, while Gawain, Julia and I \u2013 who are not known for our stealth abilities \u2013 would be a few blocks away ready to come in if called. We didn\u2019t want to be too close, because if White Maria spotted any of us she would probably realize that something was up, and it might blow our chance to nab whoever had been terrorizing her.<br /> <br /> So most of my evening was actually pretty tame, y\u2019know, comparatively speaking. I spent an hour or so sipping espressos with Gawain and Julia, and then we got a call from Marguerite informing us that White Maria was on the move and that there was an unconscious Chicano gang member in the back of Gawain\u2019s van. While Gawain made sure the ganger was properly subdued, I drove his van, following White Maria at a safe distance. And hey! I don\u2019t think she spotted us even once!<br /> <br /> So we parked ourselves down the block from White Maria\u2019s place and I channeled a bit of energy into the ne\u2019er-do-well until he was awake. Then we had to wait twenty minutes for D to join us, since our guest didn\u2019t speak English and none of us spoke Spanish. When she arrived, D gave me a quick kiss and then got to work. A few minutes later she stepped out of the back of the van, dusting off her hands theatrically, and informed us that he and his friends were supposed to kidnap White Maria and deliver her to a warehouse near the docks. Someone named Alessandro Pi\u00f1a had told them to do this.<br /> <br /> I gave her a critical glance. \u201cYou enjoyed that, didn\u2019t you?\u201d I asked, quirking an eyebrow.<br /> <br /> She grinned. \u201cI don\u2019t know what you\u2019re talking about,\u201d she said nonchalantly.<br /> <br /> \u201c<i>Tu madre y tu padre?</i>\u201d I asked. \u201cWas it really necessary to threaten his parents?\u201d<br /> <br /> She shrugged. \u201cIt was effective,\u201d she returned. I couldn\u2019t really argue against that point, so I let it pass. For now.<br /> <br /> Marguerite showed up a few minutes later, and Calamity not long after that. They had a strange tale to tell. The one who\u2019s been terrorizing White Maria is Gunnar Friday. Well, okay, to be perfectly honest, Gunnar\u2019s name never actually came up directly, but considering who else was involved, by the end of the night even I didn\u2019t need a textbook to calculate that particular logarithm. Marguerite was able to chloroform him tonight before he got too close to White Maria, and teleported him back to the Dream House through a pair of handy mirrors. Calamity had been interrogating him there while we kept watch on White Maria\u2019s house.<br /> <br /> Gunnar was reluctant to tell her anything, but she eventually managed to wrangle the whole story out of him. Years ago, a young changeling named Sundown Kwon became the girlfriend of the head of the local tong (a sort of Chinese analog to the mafia, if I understand the term correctly). Rumor had it that she had a lot of influence over the tong leader, and could pretty much do as she pleased. Her biggest rival for his affections was none other than Dark Kimberly, who was about seventeen years old at that time.<br /> <br /> Now the tong had been getting more and more entrenched in Santa Monica \u2013 thanks in part to Sundown Kwon\u2019s surreptitious use of her changeling powers to help them out here and there \u2013 and a lot of people thought that Kwon was using the tong to influence Freehold business too. It was widely believed that Kwon had officially allied the tong with Master Darke. A lot of powerful people didn\u2019t like that, and <u>someone</u> issued a warning that Kwon and Kimberly should back off\u2026 if they knew what was good for them. Kimberly listened to the warning\u2026 but didn\u2019t pass it on to Kwon. Kwon died as a result.<br /> <br /> Fast forward to a few weeks ago. White Maria began looking into Sundown Kwon\u2019s murder again, possibly in response to Kimberly\u2019s shooting at the Rose &amp; Thorn. <u>Someone</u> was afraid of what she would find, and began trying to scare her into giving it up. But Kwon was her friend, and she didn\u2019t give up the chase easily. She thought Kimberly might have had something to do with it, as her investigations had revealed that Kimberly knew about the threat to Kwon\u2019s life and didn\u2019t say anything. But the truth is not so simple.<br /> <br /> According to Gunnar, Lucien Torrez killed Sundown Kwon (or at least ordered her death) all those years ago, because the tong was infringing upon the territories controlled by his contacts in the area\u2019s Hispanic gangs. Torrez didn\u2019t want White Maria\u2019s new investigation to reveal his complicity in Sundown\u2019s death. Gunnar claimed that he was actually trying to save White Maria\u2019s life by terrorizing her; if she gave up her investigation, Torrez would have no reason to \u201csilence\u201d her by other means.<br /> <br /> Based on the cadre of Hispanic gangers on the pier tonight, we\u2019re guessing that Torrez is just about out of patience.<br /> <br /> Calamity, Jacob and I went to talk to White Maria, hoping that we could convince her to drop her investigation before things turned deadly. The others left to drop the gang member off somewhere private and secluded. White Maria was surprised to see us, but she was willing to let us in so that we could discuss her current situation. I had suggested that we try to leave Torrez\u2019s name out of this, but Calamity was having none of it. She told Maria exactly what was happening with no holds barred.<br /> <br /> I tried to salvage the situation by leveraging Lucien\u2019s reputation. White Maria agreed that Torrez is too powerful for her to take down, and that he could almost certainly dispose of all of us put together without too much trouble if he put his mind to it. She agreed to halt her investigation into Sundown Kwon\u2019s death. <br /> <br /> Unfortunately, she wasn\u2019t willing to call off her grudge against Dark Kimberly. I get that Kwon was a friend of hers, and I guess I can understand why she\u2019d be mad at Kimberly for standing aside while her friend was in danger\u2026 but holding on to that much hate for so long can\u2019t be healthy. I tried my best to get her to let it go, but in the end she would only agree to <u>consider</u> dropping her grudge if Dark Kimberly was willing to make some sort of atonement. I agreed to ask her, but I\u2019m putting off that chore for another day.<br /> <br /> Once everyone was back at the Dream House, Calamity called up Becky and invited her over to explain things. I don\u2019t know everything that she said (I wasn\u2019t privy to the conversation), but I hope she was able to calm Becky down enough to keep her from doing something stupid. If Becky goes after Lucien Torrez, she\u2019ll just get killed. And if he traces her information back to us, then we\u2019re <u>all</u> in big trouble.<br /> <br /> As promised, I gave Oleander a call. It was close to midnight by that point, and I was tired and more than a little fed up with all the unchecked hatred and revenge talk flying around. I admit I wasn\u2019t in the most social of moods, and I kind of wanted to just be alone to unwind for a bit, but a promise is a promise.<br /> <br /> \u201cHi, Lori,\u201d she said as soon as she picked up. \u201cIs everything okay? Are you\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled despite myself. \u201cI\u2019m fine, Oleander. I think things have pretty much wrapped up over here. If it\u2019s not too late, I can be at your place in about half an hour.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay,\u201d she said, and then, a little shyly, \u201conly\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat is it?\u201d I asked, curious.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell,\u201d she continued, \u201cI was hoping we\u2019d have a little more time, to talk, and, y\u2019know\u2026\u201d I almost couldn\u2019t hear the last word, \u201c\u2026cuddle.\u201d<br /> <br /> So sweet. So earnest. I didn\u2019t hear an ounce of hate, or lust, or jealousy, or recrimination in her voice. And I realized that maybe I didn\u2019t want to be alone that night after all. I realized that maybe Oleander was just what I needed.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat sounds <u>perfect</u>,\u201d I said. \u201cHalf an hour, sweetie, okay? See you then.\u201d<br /> <br /> I had the radio blaring and the top down on the way to Oleander\u2019s place. I didn\u2019t want to think about anything serious, so I had it tuned to some ridiculous fluffy pop station. I didn\u2019t think about what was playing \u2013 some lighthearted ditty by Ariana Grande or some such modern idol \u2013 but it was catchy. It got inside my head without me even realizing it.<br /> <br /> I had a wonderful evening with Oleander. We talked, we had a little to drink, we laughed about silly things, we cuddled together, and yes, we did end up making love\u2026 slowly, quietly, and comfortably. As we lay in each other\u2019s arms afterward, I found myself humming quietly without thinking about it\u2026 something that often happens when I let my mind wander happily.<br /> <br /> Oleander stirred sleepily against me. \u201cIs that popular?\u201d she asked. Or at least, I thought that was what she asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t know if it\u2019s popular or not,\u201d I said. \u201cI heard it on radio on the way over here, and it sort of got stuck in my head.\u201d<br /> <br /> She chuckled. \u201cNo, I mean the melody. It sounds like the song \u2018Popular,\u2019 from <u>Wicked</u>.\u201d<br /> <br /> I shrugged. I\u2019d heard about the musical, which was essentially a re-telling of <u>The Wizard of Oz</u> from the witch\u2019s point of view, but I\u2019d never seen it, and I told her so.<br /> <br /> \u201cHang on,\u201d she said, and she reached for her smart phone, tapped the screen a few times, and played the song for me. She was right; the melody of the pop song I\u2019d heard was clearly based on the song from the musical, but the remake paled in comparison to the original.<br /> <br /> The song was funny, and the two of us laughed about it together as it wound down. Oleander\u2019s not a huge musical theater fan, but she saw <u>Wicked</u> a little while ago, and something about it struck a chord with her. That led to a conversation about movies and music that she likes, and before I knew it we\u2019d been chatting away for more than an hour.<br /> <br /> Then we started kissing again. I\u2019m pretty sure we were still kissing when we both fell asleep some time later. That\u2019s never happened to me before. I woke up a few hours later with Oleander curled up in my arms, her head snuggled into the crook of my neck.<br /> <br /> I think I might really like this girl.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T00:02:00-07:00","id":613064,"title":"","content":"<b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> As if the day hadn\u2019t started out on an interesting note, it had to continue on one. Some things were normal. Calamity talking to Julia about buying some of her pictures of the dancers to hang up in the club was normal. Nice and ordinary. A little past due maybe. We try and change out the art that\u2019s hanging on the walls to keep the decorations fresh, and Julia is a really good artist.<br /> <br /> After the art discussion was done Becky came by to talk to Calamity about something important. Shortly after Becky left Calamity called a motley meeting to go over what she had learned. At said meeting the whole situation surrounding White Maria and Dark Kimberly came out. Most of us knew at least a little bit of what was going on, but apparently Lorelei had no idea what had been happening. I hadn\u2019t thought of the fact that while most of this stuff happened Lori was on the stage and wouldn\u2019t have known about it. So after a bit of scolding we talked about what brought Becky to the house.<br /> <br /> Apparently some diviners in the Autumn court saw that something bad was going to happen to White Maria tonight. Becky said that White Maria was planning on going to the pier to listen to a band that she likes. It was assumed that whatever was going to happen would happen there. So, we all planned to see what we could do about it. Becky had asked Calamity if she would keep an eye on White Maria, but had no objections if others in the motley helped out. She just didn\u2019t want anything to be obvious or for Maria to know what was going on. If she did know she would react differently than she would normally.<br /> <br /> So, our plan was for Insincere Marguerite to sneak through the crowd and surreptitiously remove the magazine from White Maria\u2019s gun. Calamity and I had Marguerite practice on our guns for a while until she got comfortable thumbing the magazine release without looking. We figured that stealing the gun itself would be too obvious, but we still wanted to render it inoperable just in case she got spooked and started shooting. Calamity and I stayed in the shadows and watched the crowd for anything or anyone suspicious. De La Rocha was walking around openly since she frequently hangs out on the pier. Lori and Gawain were hanging back at a nearby caf\u00e9. They would be too obvious in a crowd, but we wanted them close by in case we needed any help.<br /> <br /> Early on in the evening I saw Calamity go over to a shadowy corner. It looked like one of those little areas where fisherman could kind of camp out and fish for long periods. I\u2019m assuming she was meeting with someone since it looked like she was talking. After a bit I think I saw Insincere Marguerite. Not sure what they were discussing, but Marguerite left and Calamity stayed behind. She seemed content to watch the crowd from her new vantage point. It wasn\u2019t that long before I saw the Handmaidens make their way over to Calamity. From the circling and sly smiles on their faces I\u2019m assuming that they were flirting with Calamity. And from her reaction I\u2019d say that Calamity was flirting right back. I found myself hoping that the duo did not succeed in distracting Calamity from her purpose. It certainly looked like it might work, but then Insincere Marguerite came over and looked rather stern as she talked to the Handmaidens. Shortly after that the duo left, looking a little disappointed.<br /> <br /> I noticed that there was a group of less than savory looking young Latino men watching White Maria. They were watching, but it didn\u2019t look like they were about to do anything. At least not yet. It seemed like they were waiting for a signal or for something to happen. I didn\u2019t like this, so I texted the rest of the group about what was going on. It seemed that as time went on they got more and more agitated, like whatever was supposed to have happened didn\u2019t. A moment later I saw one of the group walk near the restrooms and suddenly get pulled in and the door shut behind him. Just after that we got a text from Insincere Marguerite saying that she\u2019d \u201cgot one.\u201d The whole gang seemed to be derailed from their main purpose by the loss of one of their own. At least that meant that they were not so keen on following Maria anymore. Then a moment later I saw White Maria start to leave, so I let the others know. I followed her to the parking lot and go into my jeep to follow her. I saw Lori and Gawain get into the van to do the same.<br /> <br /> We followed White Maria back to her place and parked a discreet distance away. We all met up in the van to share notes. I will admit I was surprised to find the young Latino man that Insincere Marguerite snagged in the back of the van. There was also a mirror in the back, so there was no question as to how he came to be in Gawain\u2019s van. Gawain started off as intimidating as he could, which is pretty damn good if you ask me, to interrogate the man as to what he was up to. Turned out that the guy didn\u2019t seem to speak any English, or at least not enough to have a conversation in. So, Lori called De La Rocha, who showed up in record time to actually talk to the guy. She was just as intimidating as Gawain, in my opinion. We found out from our \u201cguest\u201d that they had been hired to take Maria hostage if they got a certain signal. Apparently that signal was never sent, hence their uncertainty. They work for someone named Alessandra Pina, and are supposed to report on what happened, and have taken White Maria to a warehouse. We let the poor guy go after he\u2019d answered all of our questions, with the understanding that he wouldn\u2019t speak about us to anyone else. I think he\u2019ll keep to his word just to have to avoid telling anyone that he was intimidated and beat up by a girl. De La Rocha plays \u201cbad cop\u201d well, I\u2019ll just say that.<br /> <br /> Calamity arrived shortly after and told us what was going on. Turns out that Dark Kimberly and White Maria were both involved with the Tong, the actual Chinese mafia, along with Sundown Kwon. Apparently Kwon was dating the leader of the Tong and was lending her aid in the way of Changeling powers. Not that the Tong knew that, but she was still ensuring their success that way. Then Sundown Kwon apparently made some sort of deal with Darke to help the Tong. Lucien, who had problems with them before this, didn\u2019t like this and sent a less than friendly message for her and the others (Dark Kimberly included) to back down and leave well enough alone. They did not back down. Dark Kimberly then got word somehow that Lucien was going to move against Kwon. She, being seventeen at the time, freaked out and hid instead of warning Kwon about what was coming. Kwon was killed and this is what White Maria has been investigating and finding out details about. Hence the scare tactics, we\u2019re pretty sure made by Lucien\u2019s people, to get her to back down.<br /> <br /> After that Calamity, Lori and I went to go talk to White Maria. We figured that if we explained what was going on, without naming names then maybe we could get her to stop looking into something that was likely to get her killed. So, we knocked on her door and she answered, a little surprised to see us, wearing a white bathrobe. I will not mention out loud how pretty she looked. Anyhoo\u2026she let us in and we talked. First off we explained how we got the magazine out of her gun and why. Then we returned it. We started in on our explanation pretty well, without mentioning names, but then I guess things were moving too slowly for Calamity and she flat out said that if White Maria didn\u2019t stop looking into the whole thing then Lucien Torrez was going to kill her. This, I think, shocked her into agreeing to stop investigating the whole Sundown Kwon incident. It did not abate her anger at Dark Kimberly though. She was still really pissed at the other girl for betraying the group. Lorelei asked if Maria might consider the matter closed if Kimberly did something to atone for what she had done. White Maria at least seemed a bit interested in that idea, so maybe it will work. Maybe if Dark Kimberly can do something to make up for her past mistake then the rift between friends can begin to heal.<br /> <br /> <br /> The other person that we, or at least Calamity, needed to talk to tonight was Becky. We wanted to let her know what was going on and see if she might consider backing down as well. So, Calamity called Becky and arranged to meet her at the Dream House. We all went back home and arrived at about the same time as our guest. Calamity and Becky went to another room to talk privately. The conversation with Becky didn\u2019t take all that long, and after it was done she left and Calamity came out to talk to the rest of us. She explained that Becky was also really mad at Dark Kimberly and the person that had been terrorizing White Maria. She said that if it was true that the person, no names were given but we\u2019re pretty sure it was Gunnar, was just trying to save Maria\u2019s life then she would just physically hurt them, not kill them. I think we either need to work on calming her down, or warning the person in question about Becky\u2019s intentions. She was also still rather pissed at Dark Kimberly and no amount of explaining would get her to back down on that. She sees Kimberly\u2019s actions as a flat out betrayal of the others in the group and will not forgive her, or even let her make up for her mistake.<br /> <br /> I can understand being upset at someone that has betrayed you. I can also understand why Kimberly may have done what she did. In my life I have been the betrayed and the betrayer. There were several people in the Lady\u2019s realm that I trusted early on. I was so na\u00efve in the beginning. But, I did, I trusted them. On more than one occasion I trusted someone, only to have them betray me. I trusted that girl when I first arrived. I helped her make a windbreak and we camped for the night. I woke the next morning to find that the girl was gone and so was my flashlight. A while later, after you\u2019d think I\u2019d have learned my lesson, I met up with a guy, Derek, that seemed to be having a hard time of it. I wasn\u2019t much better off, but I offered to help him. I showed him how to set a snare and we waited to catch some dinner. We traveled together for several days before the inevitable happened. I had my back turned for just a moment and suddenly I felt a knife at my throat. He said he was taking my canteen and cooking kit and if I didn\u2019t chase him he would leave me alive. Being the idiot I was, I agreed and he took my stuff and left. I counted myself lucky. Not quite the same as the situation between Dark Kimberly and the others, but I can understand. She was seventeen and scared. What if warning Kwon got her killed too? She may not have had time to think it through after the terror wore off and warn her friend.<br /> <br /> As for the part of betrayer, I\u2019ve done that too. In some people\u2019s minds it probably doesn\u2019t count because those that I betrayed were a Gentry and her loyal Knight. It does count for me though. I served the Lady loyally for many years and watched Rook\u2019s back. Then after Claire Falls I turned my back on them and refused to take Delight Diane back. I don\u2019t know why, but I just couldn\u2019t bring her back to the Lady. I could see the hurt in Rook\u2019s eyes when I told him \u201cno.\u201d That hurt was quickly replaced by anger, and he showed no restraint when the inevitable fight happened, but it had been there. I know the Lady was upset at my betrayal when Rook brought me back to her. She expressed her displeasure clearly enough. I have the scars to remind me. I can understand her anger though. I was a trusted Knight and I turned my back on her for a \u201cpretty thing\u201d that the Lady wanted back. So I denied the Lady a treasure and a Knight all in one blow.<br /> <br /> So, I can understand Dark Kimberly\u2019s side of things as well as White Maria and Becky\u2019s. They are hurt by what their friend did, but there are probably reasons why Kimberly did what she did. Based on what Calamity has said the girl certainly is upset by what happened and what she did. She did not decide to betray her friends out of malice, she was scared and didn\u2019t act. Her lack of action led to bad consequences, but it was not something that she did intentionally. I\u2019m not sure if Becky can be helped to see or understand that. She is too angry and is not thinking clearly. It will take more time than I think Dark Kimberly has for Becky to see things objectively. Becky seems to be a creature of the moment, and I don\u2019t have high hopes for Kimberly getting out of this unscathed.<br /> <br /> After the explanation of what\u2019s going on, Calamity seemed really upset by everything. She is friends with both Becky and Dark Kimberly and doesn\u2019t want to see either of them get hurt. She feels caught in between and can\u2019t really do anything to help one friend without hurting the other. She\u2019s stuck in between a rock and a hard place and feels horrible about the whole thing. Insincere Marguerite chose that moment to be frank with her emotions and tell Calamity that\u2019s why she\u2019s not a monster. Marguerite doesn\u2019t share her feelings so openly often, and it was endearing to see it tonight. I\u2019m not sure if Calamity believed her, but I\u2019m hoping that something of the message got through to her heart if not her head.<br /> <br /> Once the heartwarming moment was passed we moved onto more practical matters, like what to do about the Dark Kimberly and White Maria situation. We talked about offering to move Dark Kimberly to a new town using my new contacts in the Knights of the Utmost Silence. The only problem with that option is Annika. Annika will not allow her sweet to be moved away from her. Which led to discussion of offering a new place away from here for both Annika and Dark Kimberly. Not sure that would work either. It would necessitate that Annika, and Kimberly for that matter, wanted to move and start over. Annika is very well established in this freehold. I can\u2019t see her moving away from her life here. Our other option was to somehow get White Maria, Dark Kimberly and Becky all in a room together, with no one hurting/killing anyone else, and talking things out until an agreement is reached. I don\u2019t have the highest hopes for that one either, but we don\u2019t have a lot of options at this moment. We\u2019re still working on coming up with others. I guess the only thing left for us to do right now is talk to Dark Kimberly, preferably away from Annika, and see what her take on this whole mess is.<br /> <br /> After our discussion people split up to do their own things. Gawain was going to try and do some more work on removing the trigger from Desiree. Most of the ladies had other plans. No need to think too hard on what they\u2019ll be up to. The one person who didn\u2019t leave to go do something else was Calamity. I asked her if she was going to go to sleep. She shook her head, so I said \u201cokay\u201d and sat down on the couch with her. She mumbled something about just going straight to Torrez and talking to him about this whole mess, but I suggested that plan might not be a good one. I could tell that she knew that already, but she\u2019s so frustrated and she just wants to do something productive. I can understand that. She admitted to me that she was worried that she\u2019s letting Becky down by trying to talk her out of taking vengeance on Dark Kimberly. And she\u2019s afraid that the same thought might be going through Becky\u2019s head. She then said in a quiet voice that she wished Gawain hadn\u2019t made plans to finish the oneiromancy with Desiree tonight. I found myself wishing the same thing. If there is anyone that needs a friend right now, it\u2019s Calamity. So, since Gawain is absent for the moment I decided that I was going to be that friend.<br /> <br /> I told Calamity that I\u2019d stay up with her. She looked at me and said that she wasn\u2019t planning on doing anything stupid. I believed her and let her know that, but admitted that staying up and letting the demons run wild in your head is not fun. Calamity decided then and there that we shouldn\u2019t mope. I agreed. I asked her to wait right there and ran upstairs to get my deck of cards. I came back and suggested that we play a game and gave her the choice of Gin, Rummy, or Poker. Perhaps unsurprisingly she chose poker. She asked what the wager was going to be, so I made another trip. This time to the bar and got a bowl of straight pretzels and came back. I told her that after buying the jeep I was poor so suggested we play for food. She smiled and revealed that this reminded her of playing for jelly beans with Stasia. Calamity rarely goes into details about her once best friend and I could tell it was a sensitive subject, so I didn\u2019t pry. I confided that in the Lady\u2019s realm I used to play poker with sticks. Food was too valuable to play a game for. The few times I found someone that didn\u2019t outright attack or run away from me we\u2019d trade news and sometimes played a game or two. Betting for sticks was neutral. No need to fight over anything if the game should go against one of us. I trust Calamity so I don\u2019t have a problem playing for food with her.<br /> <br /> While we were playing I asked Calamity if she thought that I should tell Lowjack about my past. She said that I should. Since Rook is still out there and may come back, it\u2019s best to tell my side of it before misunderstandings can come up. She also mentioned Dahlia and suggested that she may be a good person to tell as well since she seems to be the one in charge of hunting down Loyalists. She would be especially useful if we managed to find Rook, but wanted to try and reform him instead of just straight out killing him. I fully realize that it may be necessary to kill Rook. There may not be another way, especially if he is a danger to the freehold. I can\u2019t condone killing him if he is only a danger to myself though. I deserve his wrath. I will try my best not to get killed by him, but I will understand if he continues to come after me in the future. If he actually tries to kill me for real I will defend myself, lethally if I have to. I just don\u2019t want him to be killed because he might be a threat to me.<br /> <br /> Calamity mentioned during our conversation that Dahlia was from Snow Globe as well. I wasn\u2019t sure if she brought that up to say that she might be more understanding of my past, despite her current duties, or if she had another reason for mentioning it. I asked her if she was okay with finding this out and with the situation in general. She admitted that she was a little nervous. She has questions that she wants answered, but she\u2019s anxious what those answers are going to be. She would rather know, good or bad, than remain in the dark. I can understand that. I admitted that I didn\u2019t want to bring up any bad memories for her. Calamity replied that bad memories are the only ones that Snow Globe makes. I knew that she didn\u2019t have much in the way of good memories from that place, which is why I made sure she was okay bringing it up. I don\u2019t want to cause a friend pain because my mouth gets away from me.<br /> <br /> I expressed my hope that Dahlia\u2019s reaction to things will be similar to Calamity\u2019s, and she agreed that it is likely. The idea of telling Lowjack and Dahlia at the same time was brought up, but Calamity assured me that I only needed to tell who I wanted to tell, who I trusted to tell. She suggested that it might be a good idea to tell them at the same time. She said that we are like family and she trusts me. She also offered to go with me when I tell them, and I told her that I would like that. It might be good to have someone there that can assure my fellow Winter courtiers that I am being honest. Calamity also joked that if the worst should happen she would get to find out just how good a knife fighter Dahlia is. I figure that I will tell them both about my past so there are no misunderstandings. Once I can gauge their reaction to that I may or may not tell them about Rook and my plans to try and rehabilitate him. I don\u2019t know if it will be possible to do so, but I want to at least try.<br /> <br /> I will freely admit in these pages that I am more than a little nervous about telling Lowjack and Dahlia about my past loyalties. If they decide that I am an enemy, I will not fight them. I\u2019m not saying that I won\u2019t run like hell, but I really don\u2019t want to fight them. Truth is I don\u2019t know where I\u2019d run to. I came here in the first place because of my sister. I don\u2019t want to leave her if I don\u2019t have to. I might be able to go back to Claire Falls, though I\u2019m fairly certain that Travers would try and turn me into that bloody smear that he threatened the last time I was there. I can\u2019t go back to my hometown since that place is known. I don\u2019t even know if it would be feasible to run. If Calamity can use her abilities to find anyone she wants as long as she knows a name, then others in the freehold would be able to do the same. Huh, I think I just talked myself into taking any possible punishment like a good little boy. The only place I could really hide would be the Hedge, or Her realm and I\u2019m not going back to the Lady. I don\u2019t want to know what the Lady could turn me into if she had the time to do so. Just thinking about it makes me feel sick.<br /> <br /> During our conversation I had a million thoughts flying through my head and then Calamity mentioned that Lowjack does not know that Dahlia is from Snow Globe, and she doesn\u2019t want it to be known either. Apparently the only other person to come out of Snow Globe was years ago, and she did not adjust well to being in \u2018the world.\u2019 She reacted rather badly in fact and became something of a local killer. She would not bow to the Courts and so faced their justice. In the end, they killed her. So, it seems that I\u2019m not the only one keeping secrets. I\u2019m not sure if Dahlia\u2019s really compares to mine, but it\u2019s something anyway. Maybe she will understand?<br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> Tonight I have been a successful Grub. I have helped one of my dearest friends, seriously impressed my girlfriend, and shown I can steal one of the most cunning spymasters of the Freehold. Triumphantly.<br /> <br /> After breakfast, things were slow and fairly innocent. Julia and Calamity negotiated having more of her paintings up to advertise the show. There was discussion of which to rotate, which to use with advertisements, etc. Our resident Toulouse Lautrec (only much, much taller) was proud to have her paintings used here. Rightfully.<br /> <br /> Of course, she has not given up her macabre work. She is still making that, and working on her \u201cBethany Barlowe and the Creaky Tower\u201d book. She calls it a children\u2019s book, but I think it isn\u2019t so much. She wants to do more on Bethany Barlowe (and her Owl) books. I think it will happen. Hopefully.<br /> <br /> But then Becky Wan came in and had a conversation with Calamity. This worried I, as Calamity has been stressing out over issues with that Motley for a while. And now it was coming to a head. Calamity gathered us to say that Becky expected White Maria to be attacked tonight at the Santa Monica Pier. Calamity timidly asked for our help to stop this, knowing her own limits. I, of course, agreed immediately, as did the Motley. Luna, De La Rocha, and Julia were also willing to help. Obviously.<br /> <br /> There was a lot of discussion but we made a plan:<br /> <br /> -Calamity, Jacob, Luna and I would infiltrate the Pier and shadow White Maria, who would be unaware of our presence. I would also remove her magazine from her gun.<br /> <br /> -De La Rocha, who hangs on the Pier sometimes anyway, would be there tonight as immediate backup.<br /> <br /> -Lorelei, Gawain, and Julia would be close by with a van as less immediate back up but still back up.<br /> <br /> -The van would have a mirror in it, so I could bring any of us directly to the van from a bathroom mirror.<br /> <br /> I did tell Calamity if I saw Gunnar I would strike preemptively. I am glad I told her this.<br /> <br /> We arrived and split up. Luna remained at a bit of a distance being very distinct beyond our ability to disguise, but Jacob Calamity and I were closer. I did manage to acquire the magazine, and a few other items from passersby. Easily.<br /> <br /> I called upon Smoke to help conceal me, the senses of the cat to help me find my target, and spot him I did. Gunnar was skulking along also concealed by Smoke, but not well enough. I got my sleeping cloth and crept up and pulled him into one of the \u201chuts\u201d for fishers. He struggled a moment but I had him in a very bad position and used Darkness to weaken his struggles, and in a short time he succumbed, the music being played drowning any sounds of distress.<br /> <br /> I was about to signal everyone, but it occurred to me it might be a kindness to just message Calamity. I did so, she came quickly, and I left her to decide what to do with Gunnar. Jacob had spotted some Latino toughs following her, so I said to keep watching her and watched for a straggler to stray from the pack. I saw a shorter one mostly out of sight and pulled him into a restroom with the sleeping cloth, and deposited him in the van via the mirror, returning to find Calamity. Jacob reported they seemed confused by their lack of member and anxious about what was happening as White Maria was leaving, so I decided to check back on Calamity. Quickly.<br /> <br /> It was a good thing I did so.<br /> <br /> She had been cornered by Scarlet and Natalia Noir, and they were, well, sinking their claws into her heart and psyche, as is their way. She twisted like a fish on a hook as they ran their hands over her, whispering and of course, trying to see whom she had behind her. Like so many others she was ready to do anything they asked.<br /> <br /> Based on their expressions, my look must have been\u2026displeased. Despite themselves, the Handmaidens stepped back and let me pass, and I moved between they and Calamity and informed them we would be leaving. Calamity fumbled an apology but I sent them on their way with a bug in their ear. I swallowed my irritation with Calamity\u2026she does not need more stress right now, she does not need to be scolded (though a bit slipped out) but she certainly did not need those strumpets to make her their lunch and chew toy. Calamity is a killing machine, but once you are inside her heart she will do anything for you, and they don\u2019t need that kind of toy.<br /> <br /> Calamity views herself a monster. A child can lash out and stab a man. Even toddlers can murder. It is a far more dangerous sort of beast that twists one to their will and make them crave servitude. I hope Calamity remains forever na\u00efve to that fact. Her presumptions are usually endearing, in a dark way, much like Gawain\u2019s naivet\u00e9 is. When she brushes against a true predator though it becomes dangerous for her. Unfortunately.<br /> <br /> We moved Gunnar to a bathroom and tumbled through the mirror into Calamity\u2019s room. I left them there and moved into the mirror in the van. Unfortunately, my role in the drama was ending, and Gawain and Lorelei\u2019s was beginning. They interrogated the poor twit with some help from De La Rocha, who spoke Spanish, the only language he did\u2026ironically Calamity and Ace are our Spanish speakers, and the two not present. De La Rocha rather enjoyed the interrogation, showing her darker side. In the end, we figured out they were there to capture White Maria if given a signal, observe her if not. They were hired by a gangster who was likely a proxy of Torrez. A small fish who knew nothing was all he was.<br /> <br /> Calamity finished dealing with Gunnar and met us once we turned the waste of flesh lose. I spoke privately to her, and she had released Gunnar. I hope I do not regret her decision, as there was no oath against revenge for humiliating him. We compared notes and determined clearly Lucian was going to kill White Maria if she kept investigating Sundown Kwan\u2019s death. Sundown Kwan was affiliated with the Tong, and she and Dark Kimberly, then 17, were rivals for the leader\u2019s affection. She decided to not warn Kwan when she discovered a plot against her. She allowed Kwan to die. They, with White Maria and Becky Wan (who does not understand naming conventions apparently) were a Motley, but apparently one without a Pledge. While they remained friends after, White Maria discovered Dark Kimberly\u2019s actions, and her stalking was due to her digging. Calamity (who felt it was her responsibility) Lorelei (who was our best talker) and Jacob (with his connections to the Knighthood of Utmost Silence if that was needed) were sent in, while the rest of us returned. Tiredly.<br /> <br /> Julia was looking through the booty bag and found some tampons I had acquired and announced she would not need to buy tampons for awhile when Lorelei and Jacob were walking in as well as Gawain peeking back to see if Calamity was home, which got some second looks. It was funny.<br /> <br /> Calamity had a meeting with Becky, and based on Becky\u2019s storming out and Calamity\u2019s dark look I could see it did not go well. Lorelei had gone off to have fun with Oleander, so De La Rocha and Julia were well interested in some upstairs time. It\u2019s been a few nights now since I made love, so I told them I would be along, I felt the need to try and comfort Calamity. Gently.<br /> <br /> I am a master thief. I am an excellent technician. I am a beautiful, well-bred woman. I am a smooth seductress. Good at comforting people I am not. I entered with Jacob, took Calamity\u2019s hand, and looked her in the eye as she spoke. Her friends were upset, and people she cared about, like Dark Kimberly and Becky, were on opposing sides, and Gunnar whom she deeply respected she had been forced to hostily confront. She was deeply unhappy. As she spoke of her guilt, I placed a hand beneath her chin, looked her in the eye and told her this is why she is not a monster. Plainly speaking from the heart is difficult, even painful for me, and I left rapidly after. I am not cut out for it. I am not Sincere Marguerite. It was like when I told the girls I loved them.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s very difficult. Painfully.<br /> <br /> I only hope I helped, and that Calamity did not misinterpret my rapid exit. I am glad Jacob was there\u2026after opening up that much I needed to get away.<br /> <br /> My worry for Calamity and residual disquiet at having been so open with her aside, it has been a good night. I acquired many valuables and impressed Julia, even if she was more interested in the marijuana and tampons than phones. I had stolen a powerful spymaster, though I will have to meet him to ensure there is no further hostility. But I proved I could steal him even from a crowded place, and without his knowing what was happening.<br /> <br /> I am truly magnificent.<br /> <br /> My time with De La Rocha and Julia was pleasing. De La Rocha is slightly concerned about Oleander, I think, but less from a \u201cLori will lose interest in me\u201d and more \u201cI don\u2019t want Oleander as my enemy.\u201d I relieved her tensions partially by returning her to her fully submissive mind. I think she can go even deeper without Lorelei there and no fear of not being butch enough for her. Regardless, she was pleased by it, and Julia and I spent some very quality time together too. The night was fun, and a good opportunity to blow off some steam and relieve some tension.<br /> <br /> And surrounded by such pretties, I remembered how magnificent Insincere Marguerite truly is.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXXV</i><br /> <br /> If New WoD has rules for Chloroform I could not find them. I had the subject make a penalized Stamina + Resolve where the penalty grew if they could not struggle out. Insincere Marguerite tended to invoke Touch of Paralyzing Shudder and strike more quickly than her subject could get a breath, which lead to Gunnar and average joe guy being knocked out quickly. The thug actually went down almost immediately. Insincere Marguerite used her full Professional Merit along with Shadowpatch to get a rote action for Stealth and got 15 successes. Gunnar\u2019s eight successes to spot trouble did not match, and she (barely) saw him. Calamity rolled just shy of spotting Gunnar but got a lot of other info. So a lot of the drama for Calamity, Insincere Marguerite and Jacob came down to Stealth and Investigation rolls, the latter of which Calamity and Jacob were addled on due to low Clarity.<br /> <br /> Lorelei also rocked some Shadowing rolls keeping an eye on White Maria.<br /> <br /> Because of events going on in the news at this writing, I wanted to discuss my use of a Latino gang in this session. Yes, I had Latino criminals as an element. This was due to connection to Lucian Torrez who, honestly, is one of the most dangerous and sinister people in the city, and yes he is Hispanic. But (at least I feel) my portrayal of Latinos in the game has been fair and not intended to make them seem like criminals. De La Rocha, Captain Jack Martinez, Flores and Oleander are good friends and allies of the group, and less closely allied but still positive characters like Sandoval and Juan-Carlos Hypnos are out there as well. So while I had Latino thugs, and not for the last time, I want to be crystal clear at my intentions, which is a balanced view of a major part of California\u2019s population, and avoiding stereotypes as much as possible. We do have a crimelord, but also a punk chick, a wrestler/wrestling manager, nightclub owner, botanist, mancandy and professional dream warrior. Hopefully this is a good spread.<br /> <br /> Similar with Asian characters, there are 6 living at current (Becky Wan, White Maria, Dark Kimberly, Shi, Moon, and Davey) none of whom are currently involved in crime, and Dark Kimberly (and honestly, the late Sundown Kwon) merely dabbled where they shouldn\u2019t have.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t have enough Black characters, currently just Dominika. I do need to do something about that. Dominkia is not, at least, any stereotype beyond \u201cNoob\u201d really.<br /> <br /> Anyway, that is it for this session. Next session is mostly an RP session with fun on the beach\u2026or what passes for such with a group with a bunch of Darklings. See you then, comments and questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T13:07:16-07:00","id":613890,"title":"","content":"So, some of the players were talking, and we wondered if people had theories about who was playing which characters in the various WoD games I have up. So I figured we would offer a chance at discussion of it. In order to protect identities of players, I have not been in a habit of confirming links between players between games. But if you are curious and follow more than one game you can ask. Anything else you ask about will be up to the players if they want to answer. But I will confirm or deny common links between characters if you ask.<br /> <br /> Some facts<br /> <br /> In the four New WoD and one Classic WoD games there are 13 different players. 2 are/were in all five games. 1 is in four games, 4 are in three games, and 6 are only in one game each, at least of WoD games.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d rather you be nice\u2026I don\u2019t want to hear \u201cI think player A plays X and Y because they suck\u201d or anything, I am proud of my players. A number of them will be peering in to enjoy this too.<br /> <br /> Anyway, if you have any theories I would enjoy hearing them!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T08:37:26-07:00","id":615153,"title":"","content":"It's incredible how Insincere Marguerite's outrageous arrogance and casual creepiness can actually be endearing. That's some good characterization!<br /> <br /> Would you like some forumites to propose black/african-american NPCs to add to your game?<br /> <br /> I've just started reading your Geist and Demon AP. I'll see if I can identify someone. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar