:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> The first set are all different people. Lorelei and Dearbh\u00e1il are actually almost identical builds, but their players are not in the opposite games. Neither is also Clytemnestra (actually neither player is in <i>Night Train</i>.)<br /> <br /> You have two of three correct with the second line. Tatiana and Speed Demon have the same player. I see you are putting the butches together <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The player of those two is cool because all their journals are done in very different styles.<br /> <br /> Third and Fourth have no matches.<br /> <br /> Lizette and Insincere Marguerite have the same player. One cannot accuse her of playing her French characters as the same. Kilroy is in that game but has a different player.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'd be curious the logic there if you get time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The comments (and guesses) are appreciated!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 08-04-2015, 07:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T17:29:58-07:00","id":615792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play?p=615709#post615709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd be curious the logic there if you get time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The comments (and guesses) are appreciated!</div> </div> </div> </div>I mostly tried to fit the characters into strereotypes, then regroup the characters depending on those stereotypes. I also tried to look for quirks and partcularities in the writing patterns, but it's not easy in English.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T17:50:23-07:00","id":615832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play?p=615709#post615709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hey Anteros,<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite is a pretty deep character, moreso than she lets on. It's always nice when she can be endearing. I love how deep and complex the PCs I guess are. Few are easy to pin good or bad people.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>When Insincere Maguerite commented on real predators, I seriously wondered if she realized the description applied to her and if she did, what she thought about it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T22:40:47-07:00","id":616013,"title":"","content":"Re: Insincere Marguerite and Predators: Part of her pitch was IM has a different reason to fear her Keeper, not that she would be taken again by her, but that she would become her. it has not come up yet, but Mama Lion was, in the setting history, a master thief who disappeared when she went to steal a major prize from the Gentry and never returned. People assumed she was caught, but they were wrong. I added the Handmaidens as a different potential dark side for Insincere Marguerite to see herself in; she does, and that is why she hates them...they could be her. So yes, she is aware.<br /> <br /> Also, going further on a comment earlier, in four Changeling games and three Crossover games with unique Changeling characters, the only three(!) Fairest we ever got all had Wings. One was a Draconic/Incubus, the other two of course the Minstrel/Windwings.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Many players deliberately have quirks specific to their characters in their writing. Insincere Marguerite makes a lot of grammar errors as she is practicing writing English. Jacob and Lizette do not, as they are writing in their native languages, ditto Dacian. You can see the extremes in difference with Tatiana and Speed Demon...good on you picking those out anyway.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Since you made the comment on English I am curious of your native. If you don't want to answer here feel free to PM me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T04:20:58-07:00","id":616253,"title":"","content":"I like how your players handle their characters' darker sides: Gawain basically has an evil personality he reverts to when pissed off (and holy bells, it's terrifying to read! love it!); Jacob is painted in so many different shades of gray, he should find a dungeon, a brain dead girlfriend, and wait for the dollars to roll in; Calamity is basically a Sith Lord trying to find her way back to the light; Lorelei struggles with how far she's able to go to satisfy her need to be loved and admired above anybody else, and Marguerite walks a on the edge, straying in danerous territory while trying to become as talented as her Keeper, without becoming her Keeper.<br /> I haven't read enough about Ace to figure out what demons he might be fighting if any; he might be bothered with how he misses his rock?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T11:38:33-07:00","id":616724,"title":"","content":"When we started making characters I did not have anything specific on dark sides as part of the pitch....it was to be about a group of Changelings running a Burlesque House. That just evolved naturally from the players I think. As we got moving some players may have tried to make theirs a little deeper by the time we got to the &quot;Truth or Dare&quot; session. Ace was pitched as the MC, and I am not sure he really worked that extra facet in. It looks like the player may be back in the next maybe month as his job situation changes, we will see. Hopefully. You will see more Ace then, though I would still not expect journals really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T22:52:40-07:00","id":630723,"title":"","content":"Last session was a stressful attempt to save Dark Kimberly, which they did, though it left several with feelings of disquiet. Only one way to deal with that! TO THE BEACH!<br /> <br /> Note Calamity covers this and last session.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXXVI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> Jun 27th, morning<br /> <br /> Lori has the best ideas. Just, the best. A beach trip was an awesome celebration/distraction for/from everything I think even Julia enjoyed it, in her way. Lori suggested it at breakfast. It maybe started as trying to, you know, distract us from the fact that her wings get all fluttery when she has enough coffee, you know? But it kinda snowballed once we got a couple of the darkling majority to agree. De la Roche, of course, can\u2019t let the sun win, Insincere Marguerite agreed so long as she got a nice big kerchief and Julia just got a promise she wouldn\u2019t have to leave her umbrella shade. Calamity agreed when I looked pleadingly at her, so it was a date. We even got Ace out, though he spent the whole time sunning on a rock.<br /> <br /> And it was great! Bikinis and surfing and volleyball and a picnic and sandcastles. I hadn\u2019t been surfing since I got back, but I picked it up quick enough, even with a rented board. I was able to give Calamity some pointers too. She and Lori and Insincere Marguerite all caught on quick. Insincere Marguerite was even balancing on her tongue.<br /> <br /> We split up into the Lovers (De la Roche, Lori, Oleander and Insincere Marguerite) and the Fighters (me, Calamity, Luna and Jacob) to play volleyball. We Fighters lost. Just barely though, even with De la Roche\u2019s flashing shenanigans. Not that I minded - a fun game and boobs is even better than a fun game and winning, you know?<br /> <br /> After our picnic and sunscreen break, it was sand castles time. Calamity got a bit impatient with one of the walls of the structure (that was admittedly starting to look unfortunately like my Bertilak\u2019s manor) and it collapsed. I stuck my tongue out at her and started a new one, though I didn\u2019t get too far, you know, what with the laughing at her second project - a shark\u2019s fin cutting a wake through our ruins. I had told her she wasn\u2019t allowed to fake a shark\u2019s fin in the water, before when she mentioned glamour harvesting, so she kept looking furtively at me and making faces.<br /> <br /> It was an awesome time and led into a great show. Calamity dressed up really nice and did her thing. It was an Annika night and she was great, like usual. She seemed, you know, a bit grumpy though, even with Calamity. I hope she\u2019s OK and Madame Spidertoes got to talk to her like she wanted. I got to hang out with her and Moon some, which was cool.<br /> <br /> After the show... well, that wasn\u2019t so fun. Gunnar had told Calamity that someone was selling drugs from the Dream House. Turns out it was Jacob. I wouldn\u2019t really mind, though heroin is a hell of a drug, but he was doing it for Darke. Maybe it\u2019s bad that, you know, that\u2019s what bugs me but... it\u2019s people\u2019s choices to do drugs. And legally, the Dream House is not really directly implicated in it. I just don\u2019t like the idea of supporting Darke in any way.<br /> <br /> Anyways, with that shared around, we got out the ice cream, booze and movies. We were just chatting at first, some about our fetches, cause Julia had looked into Insincere Marguerite's, cause she wanted to know her last name. It\u2019s DeLisle, though Julia thought it was Blessent, cause that\u2019s her married name. Calamity and Lori had talked about their fetches some before, but I think I confused them all by saying mine was a Duke. And De la Roche mentioned she didn't have one. I knew that happened sometimes - Peter, the Dawn Court guy I met on the way down to Santa Monica, didn\u2019t have one. De la Roche was able to pick her old life back up though.<br /> <br /> We also talked about escaping. Lori had heard a song, Lorelei by Styx, while she was singing Amazing Grace. Thus, her name. De la Roche ran into Monica and got punched out. Julia used to be able to paint paths in the Hedge, so that\u2019s how she got out. Jacob knew his way out, what with the stuff and all. Calamity told our story, though she tried to say I led her out. I might have broken a way through, you know, but she knew the way home. It was good to have happy storytelling time though.<br /> <br /> Once we got the liquor out, we decided to watch Cannibal, so Lori could approve it for a performance. We agreed yellowface for Insincere Marguerite crossed a line, so we\u2019re just gonna have her be obviously French (it\u2019ll be hard, you know?) and pretending to be an Indian. It gets the same joke across anyway. We wound up having to explain Smurfs to Lori part of the way through. See, she wondered if shpadoinkle was a real word, and Calamity explained it wasn\u2019t by saying it was like the word smurf, just, you know, a stand in for whatever. So we went through that whole thing, which is really kinda disturbing and racist, thinking about it.<br /> <br /> The Cyclops got Insincere Marguerite talking about why she avoided rural America. Apparently it was him, and \u2018The Field of the Dreams\u2019. I shouldn\u2019t make fun of her for that quirk, cause she does speak English really well, and that\u2019s an easy translation mistake to make, coming from a romance language, you know? I mostly just mention it cause I did correct it at the time so Lori could look it up easier (and since Insincere Marguerite\u2019s description was the movie about \u2018the baseball field full of dead people\u2019 I thought maybe she should?). When Insincere Marguerite got defensive, and Lori responded by saying her own French was impeccable, Insincere Marguerite almost had an aneurysm. She'll forgive Lori eventually, I\u2019m sure.<br /> <br /> So, it was a great day and a great night after. It felt like forever since I got to spend the night with just Calamity, even if it had only been a couple. She\u2019d been much more... calm? centered? something about all the mess of the night before than I\u2019d expected. I doubt her conversation with Becky went better than expected, you know, since she\u2019d stayed up all night playing poker with Jacob. Maybe her therapist was onto something with the whole meditation thing. Anyway, it was nice seeing her be ok, and falling asleep with her and waking up next to her. Hopefully day is that good too.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> I feel good. Even in the middle of the shit-storm surrounding White Maria and Dark Kimberly, I feel really good. I think every once in a while we need a day like yesterday to unwind and take a break from the stresses and concerns of our daily lives.<br /> <br /> So as I was saying, I woke up yesterday morning with Oleander snuggled in my arms. I must have shifted or something, because she opened her eyes and blinked sleepily a few times. I saw something settle in behind her eyes before the smile touched her lips. \u201cGood morning, beautiful,\u201d she said as she stretched.<br /> <br /> \u201cRight back at you,\u201d I said, kissing her forehead.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo, you want to hang out here for a while,\u201d she asked, \u201cor do you want to head back to the Dream House for the infamous \u2018Sex Breakfast?\u2019\u201d The curiosity was written clearly across her face.<br /> <br /> I chuckled. \u201cSex Breakfast sounds wonderful,\u201d I said, \u201cbut only if you\u2019ll come with me this time.\u201d<br /> <br /> She agreed, and twenty minutes later we were both en route to the Dream House (in separate cars). Gawain was just getting started when we got back \u2013 omelets! \u2013 and was happy to set another place at the table. He was in a great mood, as he\u2019d managed to remove the trigger from Desiree\u2019s subconscious during the previous night.<br /> <br /> Desiree had already left, but the rest of the usual suspects were all present and accounted for. D was fiddling with some sort of hand-held video game that Marguerite had stolen from someone at the pier the previous night. I pursed my lips disapprovingly, but decided to let it pass. For now. Things were going about like usual, with the innuendo flying around the table hot and heavy. Oleander didn\u2019t really contribute much to that, but she took it with good grace.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not sure what got me thinking along these lines, but something suddenly occurred to me. \u201cHey,\u201d I said quietly. It must have been something about the way I said it, because everyone stopped talking and looked at me. \u201cWell,\u201d I said, \u201cI just thought\u2026 we\u2019ve lived here together in Malibu for almost two months, right\u2026 so why haven\u2019t we ever taken a day and gone to the beach together?\u201d<br /> <br /> Gawain was all for it, and Oleander smiled warmly. \u201cSounds like fun,\u201d she said with a sparkle of mischief in her eyes, \u201cbut how are you going to convince the pack of darklings?\u201d<br /> <br /> I thought about it. \u201cWell, D\u2019s no problem,\u201d I commented easily. \u201cShe thinks that if she hides from the sun, the sun will somehow <u>win</u>, and she\u2019s vowed never to give it the satisfaction. Right, sweetie?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDamn right,\u201d she commented, walking to a window and miming that she was watching her nemesis carefully.<br /> <br /> Marguerite opined that she would be fine as long as she had a large kerchief to keep the sun off her face, and Calamity \u2013 like D \u2013 decided to face the sun without flinching, but Julia was a tougher nut to crack. \u201cCan\u2019t we just go for a stroll along the beach after sunset?\u201d she asked plaintively. \u201cYou know, moonlit walks on the shore? It\u2019s romantic, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> I sighed, and might have rolled my eyes a little. \u201cThat would be missing the <u>point</u> of the beach, honey,\u201d I said gently. \u201cPlus, we\u2019ve got a show tonight, and it\u2019s a Friday. We can\u2019t just skip out two nights in a row.\u201d She eventually relented, on the condition that she be allowed to bring a large umbrella to keep out the hated sunlight.<br /> <br /> Honestly! Darklings!<br /> <br /> Oleander ran back to her place to get a suit, and the rest of us got changed and packed up. I wore a nice dappled blue and green bikini that goes well with my wings (and, I\u2019m told, with the way my eyes appear to look through the Mask). D put on a somewhat more sedate bikini \u2013 purple, natch \u2013 and grabbed a couple of surfboards that have been sitting in our garage for a while.<br /> <br /> Most of the others wore attractive if not remarkable suits (Oleander showed up in a sedate one-piece with oval windows along the sides), but Marguerite decided to go all out in a barely-there bikini that left her ass almost completely exposed. It\u2019s a nice ass, so I didn\u2019t think we\u2019d get any complaints.<br /> <br /> We all piled into Gawain\u2019s van (parking is murder at the beach) and headed down to the shore. Some of the others rented surfboards from a little hut off the beach, and we made our way down to the waterside. Julia immediately set up her umbrella and hid herself away beneath it, but the others were really getting into the spirit of the thing. Oh, except Ace, who just found a nice warm rock in the sun and curled up.<br /> <br /> First, D taught me how to surf. It\u2019s not that hard once you get the hang of it (though I suppose my wings give me a slight advantage where matters of balance are concerned). I felt a little bad, though, because D was spending so much of her time and attention on helping me that she didn\u2019t get to really cut loose and show what she could do. Gawain was pretty impressive out there, and I saw D narrow her eyes at him, like he was challenging her or something.<br /> <br /> I tried to defuse the situation by suggesting a beach volleyball match, but that just stoked my honey\u2019s competitive fires even higher. Calamity suggested that we divide the teams into the \u201cLovers\u201d (me, D, Marguerite, and Oleander) and the \u201cFighters\u201d (Calamity, Gawain, Jacob, and Luna). D was so into the competition that she didn\u2019t even bat an eye at being lumped in with us \u201clovers.\u201d<br /> <br /> The game was pretty close in the end. I get the impression that there were some dirty tricks played on both sides \u2013 distractions and whatnot \u2013 but I didn\u2019t actually witness anything, so I kept my mouth shut. We\u2019d drawn a bit of a crowd by the time we were through\u2026 six smoking hot girls and two hunky guys in swimsuits jumping around on the beach tends to do that. We couldn\u2019t resist showing off a little. I saw Marguerite return a serve with her tongue at least once, and I used my wings a couple of times to get some extra \u201chang time.\u201d When the scores were tallied up, the Lovers had won the day, but only just barely.<br /> <br /> That seemed to satisfy D\u2019s competitive streak. She was able to relax a bit and enjoy the day after that. In fact, she took her board out and went surfing again, and was able to pull some much more impressive moves this time. I mostly waded in the water and cheered her on, before heading back to the beach, lying on my stomach, untying my bikini top, and wondering loudly if anyone would like to apply more suntan lotion to my back. There were a few volunteers.<br /> <br /> I had never really thought about it before, but it is going to be <u><u>really</u></u> difficult to maintain an even tan on my back. I know it\u2019s what they call a \u201cfirst world problem\u201d these days, but still\u2026 sigh.<br /> <br /> Calamity and Gawain busied themselves making sand castles while I preened and showed off for the crowds. I even managed to do a little bit of advertising, and I think some of those guys are quite likely to drop by the Dream House before too long.<br /> <br /> And speaking of, all good things must come to an end, and so it was with our lovely day at the beach. We made it back to the Dream House with minutes to spare, and performed to a packed house. I think the show went quite well, though everyone could tell that Annika was not in the best of moods (she was presumably upset over the situation with Dark Kimberly), and it might have affected her performance adversely. I feel <u><u>really</u> <u>really</u></u> bad about the tiny shivers of glee that sets off in me whenever I think about it.<br /> <br /> For my first number, I dressed up in a slinky evening gown and sat on a swing inside a gilded birdcage. I sang a song called \u201cLearning to Fly\u201d by Tom Petty and the Heartbreakers. Taken on its own, the song is cheerful; even uplifting. But I infused it with a sense of loss and longing so profound \u2013 based upon my own few memories of the freedom true flight grants \u2013 that it became a very sad song. I hope Jacob and the few other Winter Courtiers in the crowd enjoyed it.<br /> <br /> I <u><u>miss</u></u> flying. Freud said that when you dream about flying, it\u2019s supposed to represent sex. Sometimes I wonder if that works in reverse, too, and I\u2019m so addicted to sex because when it\u2019s good it reminds me of flying\u2026<br /> <br /> I lightened things up a bit in the second set. I actually made a last-minute substitution, got back into my bikini, and wallowed in self-parody as I belted out \u201cCause I\u2019m a Blonde\u201d by Julie Brown. I\u2019ve noticed that, of all things, dumb blonde jokes have persevered through all the years that I was gone. People will tell the same jokes that I heard when I was a kid, convinced that they\u2019re fresh and witty. Those of us who happen to have light-colored hair will never escape from the stereotypes, so it seems like the best thing we can do is own it.<br /> <br /> Plus, that song is fucking hilarious.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately things began to get a little tense after the show. I\u2019d been wandering around schmoozing and paying my respects to the local bigwigs (still in my bikini, but with a kimono tied loosely over it) when I heard someone hissing quietly at me from behind a pillar. Wandering over that way, I found Julia looking a little worried.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat are you going to do about this?\u201d she asked softly.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat?\u201d I asked, confused.<br /> <br /> She gestured her head to where D was sitting with Monica at one end of the room. Then she shook her head in the other direction, to where Oleander was sipping a drink quietly. Once she\u2019d pointed it out to me, the tension between the two of them was obvious. Neither one of them looked like they wanted a confrontation, but there was a palpable stress on the room\u2019s social dynamic.<br /> <br /> \u201cShit,\u201d I swore softly.<br /> <br /> \u201cIf it was me,\u201d Julia advised soberly, \u201cI\u2019d slip out the back door and not stop running until morning. But you\u2019re better at this stuff than me.\u201d<br /> <br /> I sighed, approached each of them, and asked if I could speak with them privately for a few moments. I led them both to a secluded table in the back corner of the theater, took their hands, and started to speak earnestly.<br /> <br /> \u201cLook,\u201d I said softly, \u201cI don\u2019t want things to be awful between you two, okay? I care about you both, and I want to keep spending time with both of you. So let\u2019s talk about the elephant in the room.\u201d<br /> <br /> Oleander looked at her own lap. \u201cDon\u2019t worry, Lori\u2026 I have nothing against de la Rocha, and I certainly don\u2019t want to fight her or anything. And I don\u2019t want to monopolize your time, either. It\u2019s just\u2026 a little awkward right now.\u201d<br /> <br /> D nodded her agreement. \u201cI don\u2019t want to fight either, babe,\u201d she said, giving my hand a squeeze, \u201cand I hope I\u2019ve proven that I\u2019m not the jealous type. But sometimes you just have to flex your muscles and show your teeth, you know?\u201d<br /> <br /> I couldn\u2019t quite suppress a sigh. Oleander squeezed my hand. \u201cLook, the point is that neither one of us wants to make this difficult for you, Lori.\u201d She looked away for a moment and seemed to reach a decision. \u201cYou spent last night at my place. I\u2019ll head on home and let you catch up with de la Rocha, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> D turned to her and said something interrogative in Spanish, and Oleander nodded.<br /> <br /> \u201cI <u><u>do</u></u> want to spend tonight with D, Oleander,\u201d I admitted. \u201cIf you\u2019re sure you don\u2019t mind\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> She smiled and nodded. \u201cI can catch up on my Netflix queue,\u201d she said lightly as she stood up.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll see you soon,\u201d I promised.<br /> <br /> \u201cCount on it,\u201d she said, and then she was gone.<br /> <br /> D looked sort of sheepish when I turned back to her. \u201cSorry about the Spanish,\u201d she said softly. \u201cIt\u2019s just that when I\u2019ve hung out with her in the past, we usually speak Spanish. I wasn\u2019t thinking, and it just slipped out.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo worries,\u201d I said with a smile. \u201cI should probably try to pick up some of the lingo myself, if I\u2019m going to keep making a pest of myself and hanging out with you. What did you say?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI just asked her if she was sure, that\u2019s all.\u201d<br /> <br /> D and I went upstairs to join a conversation already in progress with the rest of the motley. Several of them expressed sympathy for the situation from which I had just emerged, and Calamity light-heartedly suggested that the perfect solution would be a three-way orgy between Oleander, D, and myself. I glanced at my girlfriend and shrugged noncommittally, as if to suggest that it was worth a try.<br /> <br /> D sighed and rolled her eyes. \u201cLook, I\u2019ve come to grips with the fact that I like girls, okay? But that doesn\u2019t mean I\u2019m attracted to <u><u>every</u></u> girl I meet.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled and took her hand. \u201cJoking,\u201d I said, \u201cmostly. But look, D\u2026 I love that you\u2019re willing to let me have this thing with Oleander\u2026 but a part of me also loves that it bothers you just a little bit.\u201d I looked into her eyes for a minute, oblivious to the others. \u201cSweetie, you know that if you say the word\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> She kissed me before I could finish. \u201cWe\u2019re good,\u201d she said simply after a minute.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo,\u201d I said, turning back toward the others with a blush, \u201cwhat were we talking about?\u201d<br /> <br /> Jacob sighed. \u201cI have been selling heroin for Darke,\u201d he admitted with resignation. <br /> <br /> That kind of killed the lighthearted mood. Apparently Gunnar mentioned something to Calamity about someone selling drugs out of the Dream House, and when she raised the subject with the motley, Jacob admitted that he had been doing so ever since we opened. Though none of us were particularly happy about the situation, once we talked it through and realized that we could probably insulate the Dream House itself from his actions if things get legal, I think we came to terms with it. He\u2019s not forcing the drugs on anyone, and he\u2019s not selling them to kids or anything like that. Like it or not, people are making a conscious choice to buy his product.<br /> <br /> (I confess that I <u><u>did</u></u> ask if he had access to any other illicit substances. I have no interest in heroin, but I confess to being a little curious about this \u201cecstasy\u201d drug, and I wouldn\u2019t mind dropping acid again at some point. Unfortunately, he answered in the negative. Looks like I\u2019m stuck with whatever pot I can grow on my balcony or bum off Julia for the time being).<br /> <br /> Conversation turned to other things quickly. Julia mentioned that she had done some digging and discovered that Marguerite\u2019s real last name is Blessent. Marguerite was quick to correct her, informing us that this was the name of her Fetch\u2019s ex-husband. She seemed pretty steamed that Julia had gone looking into her past like that, but she didn\u2019t make a big deal out of it, and in fact told us a few minutes later that her mortal name had been Marguerite DeLisle, but as she doesn\u2019t like the person she used to be, she doesn\u2019t feel any real kinship with that name anymore.<br /> <br /> That got us talking about names. Calamity doesn\u2019t have a last name at the moment, but in this day and age that\u2019s not really much of a handicap. I told the story of how I came up with my current moniker, basing it on the two songs that helped me make it out of the Hedge.<br /> <br /> Talk then turned to our first same-gender sexual encounters. Julia talked fondly about waking up with Marguerite lying on top of her (something I\u2019ve experienced for myself), and that got me thinking about the first time I slept with Missy and Jane. It was in Arcadia, of course, so parts of it are still pretty hazy in my mind, but I know that I joined that party late\u2026 the two of them had been sleeping together for at least a few weeks before I finally joined in out of sheer loneliness. The two of them had each other, and I had been a third wheel, and I was tired of it. There were no men around aside from Hunting Hawk, and as they say: \u201cany port in a storm.\u201d I\u2019m glad I\u2019ve always been adventurous. I\u2019ve never looked back.<br /> <br /> D\u2019s story was a bit disturbing. She remembered waking up in an unfamiliar bed in an unfamiliar room. She slowly began to remember the events of the previous night, and gradually turned over\u2026 to see Madame Spidertoes perched on a chair and watching her in absolute silence.<br /> <br /> Yeesh! I\u2019m glad none of <u>my</u> darklings are quite so existentially creepy.<br /> <br /> To lighten things up a bit, we all went upstairs together and watched <u><u>Cannibal: The Musical</u></u> so I could decide whether it was right for the Dream House. After having viewed the movie, I can honestly say two things: it\u2019s <u><u>terrible</u></u>, and it\u2019s <u><u>hilarious</u></u>. I think it will actually be a good fit for us. Now we just have to figure out the logistics of a few things, like how to depict Liane (the horse character) and how to recreate the big production number \u201cHang the Bastard\u201d on our teeny stage.<br /> <br /> So we laughed ourselves silly for the next hour and a half. I had been planning to spend some quality time with Julia tonight (I feel like I\u2019ve been neglecting her recently), but when the time came to turn in, she and Marguerite disappeared pretty quickly. All night I\u2019d heard her muttering things that sounded suspiciously like \u201cOldacre-DeLisle,\u201d which was <u><u>adorable</u></u>. I kind of wanted to be alone with D in any case. The two of us headed back to our bedroom and got ready for bed together.<br /> <br /> \u201cFeel up to some lovin\u2019?\u201d D asked with a cocky grin.<br /> <br /> \u201cAlways,\u201d I said, leaning in to kiss her, \u201cbut I want <u>real</u> lovin\u2019, honey\u2026 not just sex. Hold me. Kiss me. Show me how you feel about me.\u201d<br /> <br /> She did. I have no complaints. I slept like a baby last night, but I should really start getting ready. I\u2019m supposed to go to Andromeda\u2019s place with Princess Jolie tonight to see what we can do about finally undoing her curse.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T22:53:28-07:00","id":630726,"title":"","content":"<b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> <b><u><u><b>Saturday June 28<sup>th</sup></b> </u></u></b><br /> <br /> Days Without Stabbing: 11<br /> <br /> I am a lucky [strike]monster[/strike] woman. That was actually hard to write but if my sister can set aside her own issues to say it then I owe it to her to listen. She and the others keep telling me that I am not a monster and I keep not believing them because I have done monstrous things and I have the desire to do so again. But I regret those actions. I try to resist those urges. I told myself I wouldn't let that anger and dark hunger control me again after my parents. I convinced myself that I could keep it buried inside or ride it out and decide who did or did not deserve to feel the caress of my glass. In short, I was a fool.<br /> <br /> I do regret what I did. If I could take it back... If I could trade my own life for theirs... If there was some way to make it right...<br /> <br /> But there is not. The past cannot be changed. All I can do is move forward. I can make the choice not to be that monster again. It's not easy but I owe it to them. I owe it to the people who love me, to Gawain and my Darkling sister and Lori and Jacob and Ace. I owe it to the people who believe in me, to Becky and Jack and Charlotte and Annika. Hell, I even owe it to myself.<br /> <br /> I don't expect or deserve forgiveness. The things I have done are not ones I can ever be forgiven for. I am a murderer. I will always be a murderer. Nothing will ever erase that. But I can be more than that. I AM more than that. When I look in the mirror, I see the monster that lured Timmy to the well and squirmed in delight at the sounds of his death. I see the monster that flew into a rage at her parents for loving the pale imitation left behind more than they loved her and killed them. I see the monster that murdered a helpless man in his sleep because it was easier than finding a way to save him from Darke.<br /> <br /> I don't see the woman that saved Ginny's life. I don't see the woman that drove off the Briar wolves that were hunting travelers along the Freehold's edges. I don't see the woman that lead a stranger she'd just met back to the real world. I don't see the woman that risked her life to drive back the Mothership's invasion. I don't see the woman that helped Joan regain her free will after her curse stole it away. I don't see the woman who hunted down Mary's fetch and carried her friend back to be treated. Yes, I am a monster, but I can also be a protector, a friend, a lover. I must never forget the evils I am capable of doing in my moments of weakness but I must also learn to see the good I can do when I rise above it. I can and I will be the kind of woman Gawain deserves and fuck anyone who says I can't do it... especially that lying bitch in the mirror.<br /> <br /> Damn, I wish I really felt as confident about that as I sound. But Dr Emmett says that the whole point of affirmations is that whatever you tell yourself enough is what you'll start to believe. Self doubt and self loathing will poison you and I sure as fuck have no shortage of those. She told me that if I wouldn't put up with some random fucktard off the street saying it to me then I shouldn't put up with my own damned self talking that shit to me. (Okay, she may have used more professional language but that's the gist of it.)<br /> <br /> So, I wasn't thinking too hard on that when I left Thursday. I was much more focused on being (at least somewhat) more focused on reality again than her comments on trying to start working on the touchy-feely home game before our session Tuesday. But then I was blissfully unaware of the roller-coaster ride I was already in line for.<br /> <br /> Much like a classic detective story, it started with a dame. And hells yeah Becky's legs go ALL the way to the floor and all that other fucking Dick Tracy bullshit. (Well, I can't actually say I've ever seen my favorite dragonlady smoke but I bet she'd look hella sexy with her lips wrapped delicately around the end of one of those insane femme fatale cigarette holders.) But to be serious, I could see right away she was wound up tight. Fuck, the woman was all but vibrating from all the rage and fury she was holding in check. And yeah, that set certain parts of me to their own quivering but that wasn't what she was looking for from me so I took a slow breath and behaved like the gorram adult everyone seems to think I am.<br /> <br /> Not surprisingly, she was there to talk to me about the mess with White Maria and Dark Kimberly. Before she started, she made a point of making very sure I was up to this with everything I'd been dealing with. It set my teeth on edge that she doubted me but she did make sure I knew it wasn't my willingness to help she was questioning but my well-being. I nodded and kicked that flash of irritation away by focusing instead on the fact that she was concerned about me even in the midst of this situation. I assured her I was up to the task and more than willing to help her. She smiled a little through the stress then and explained what was going on. She'd been in touch with Dionysia and gotten her to use some oracular powers. According to her readings something bad was going to happen to White Maria that night. As White Maria was planning to go to the pier to listen to a band she liked it seemed most likely that whatever it was would happen there. Becky wanted to try to catch the person who had been terrorizing her friend red handed. The catch was that White Maria couldn't know what was going on since it might change her behavior. I asked her if she'd mind if I brought the rest of the motley in on it and she said that if I felt they could help it was fine with her.<br /> <br /> So, I promised to let her know what happened and called a house meeting. My mind already had a sinking feeling that I knew who was most likely the culprit and I considered calling Gunnar to warn him but I couldn't betray Becky and she'd already expressed suspicions about Dionysia and threatened to do bodily harm to her if she let the plan slip. The only thing to do was go and apprehend him myself and hope I could somehow defuse this fucking mess myself. Plus there was always the (slim and unrealistic) chance it was someone else.<br /> <br /> Getting everyone up to speed was quick, though Lori was a little miffed that no one had told her about any of it. I tried to explain that I had been hoping that for once we could avoid playing Scooby Gang. And as fucked up as everything still ended up I must confess I am glad we got involved. We kept things from getting as ugly as they could have on the spot and with any luck I can talk Becky down from doing anything she'll regret about what we learned.<br /> <br /> We worked out a plan of action. Insincere Marguerite would stay close to White Maria and unload her gun. After all, spooking her in public and having her overreact with a firearm would certainly be one way to get her out of the way. And even if it wasn't her stalker's plan it was a real possibility considering how jumpy she'd been acting. My Darkling sister isn't particularly familiar with guns, so Jacob and I showed her how the release worked and let her practice dropping the clips from our guns by feel.<br /> <br /> Jacob and I were going to be nearby, skirting the crowd unseen. Insincere Marguerite's role was to get White Maria down and safe while Jacob and I dealt with the attacker. Gawain and Lori are too visible so they were at a nearby cafe, close enough to join in if things got too out of hand for additional fighting and healing. De la Rocha was also close at hand, wandering the pier openly since she does that fairly often anyway so it would not be suspicious for her to be about.<br /> <br /> We traveled to the pier and right off, I noticed that the Handmaidens were about. I don't want to be paranoid, but I can't help but wonder about their presence. They were over by an ice cream vendor, arm in arm licking each others soft serve like the foreplay part of a porn movie. (Which I would totally watch the ever-loving fuck of.)<br /> <br /> I was jolted from my fantasies by a text from Insincere Marguerite. It was sent just to me, which made me double time it over to where she was loitering at one of the fishing stalls. And soon as I got there, I saw she had put Gunnar down with her sleeping cloth. We pulled a hat down over his face and I parked myself there to watch over him while she moved back out into the crowd. I started trying to figure out what we were going to do when the handmaidens showed up.<br /> <br /> They wasted no time in asking about the unconscious but unknown figure behind me. I avoided answering them and decided to try to deflect their attention by flirting back with gusto. After all, they'd have only been more suspicious if I hadn't shown interest after our previous meetings. Well, as much as I'd like to believe my flirting was what set them off I am going to leave the hubris to the Greek heroes and be honest. Those two are so far out of my league I'm not even playing the same fucking game. They stepped things up from their usual hints to promising to making all my darkest fantasies come true. I should have sent them packing but damn... even if those two are the bullet train to Hell I still wanted to ride that ride as long and as hard as I could. But I was right in the fucking middle of things and I just couldn't drop it all to go play.<br /> <br /> I tried to explain that it was just the timing but they were having none of that. They backed me up against the stall and then leaned in until I could feel their soft bodies brushing against me as they ran those perfect fucking deadly fingers along my skin and my glass. I'm not sure if it's just them or if it's a leechfinger thing (Maybe I should ask De la Rocha to touch me sometime... you know, for science...) but their touch is cool, almost cold, and their fingers are so soft and they make sure it's impossible to watch both of them so one or the other is always out of sight. And the way they speak in unison or trade back and forth... Yeah, it's way to fucking close to The Whispering Voices and yet... Holy Mother of Pearl even just thinking about it makes me shiver in ways that remembering Them shouldn't. Then Natalia nicked her finger 'accidentally' on a shard and offered it to my lips. Zeus help me but I couldn't resist pulling that digit into my lips and tongue. Fuck but her blood tastes so damn sweet and I wanted all of it. And yeah, I did fucking mewl like a gorram kitten when she pulled it away and they told me they were leaving to go fuck and made it clear they wanted me to join them. My protests were pretty damn weak at that point and if it hadn't been so fucking important I would have been on that offer like white on fucking rice. <br /> <br /> And while I (barely) managed to not fold like a house of cards I have to be honest. If Insincere Marguerite hadn't showed up about that point and rescued me those two would have had me on my knees begging them to let me go with them (or to just do whatever the fuck they wanted to with me while I was on knees with a crowd watching... after all they are Night Court). And that is not okay. I do NOT play that game for anyone and certainly not for someone I actively distrust. I really, really should avoid those two. They've got a fucking backdoor to my gorram psyche and unless they're stupid (which is the one thing nobody thinks they are) they damn well know it. I need to avoid them like a mother-loving plague. But by my fucking glass and blood, I WANT them so bad it hurts.<br /> <br /> I am not sure I recall ever seeing Insincere Marguerite be that direct before to be honest. She pushed between us and all but shoved them away physically as she sent them on their way. And yeah, I was in the midst of hating to see them leave but loving to watch them walk away when she gave me a scornful look and told me what nice ring I made. I stiffened and scowled and muttered something half-hearted and all untrue about not being under their sway just because I was interested in fucking them. Thankfully, she choose to let my lapse of judgment drop and return to the task at hand. While I had been completely distracted, Jacob had caught wind of a group of Latino toughs trailing White Maria and Insincere Marguerite had put one of them to sleep as well and sent him to Gawain's van via the mirror in the bathroom. White Maria was leaving and the motley was gathering to follow. I glanced at Gunnar and she offered to take him and I to the Dream House before joining the others.<br /> <br /> By the time he came too in my room at the Dream Hose I'd gotten my pulse back down to normal and my game face on. I didn't bind him and I made a point of being as calm and reasonable as I could. Gunnar was suffering from a serious chloroform hangover and was obviously not in the least pleased that anyone had gotten the drop on him. Still, he was with it enough to make sure to butter me up like a southern biscuit by playing up how very helpless he was and how very dangerous I was. I made it clear I wasn't buying it and didn't underestimate the threat he still represented. I had left him free because I believed that we could discuss things like civilized adults rather than with threats and hostility. <br /> <br /> When I explained why we'd jumped him on the pier he got a bit offended that we'd been concerned he'd try to set White Maria off in public. It is true that drawing police attention to any Changeling is bad for all of us and I don't doubt that he's too pragmatic to want that. I'd like to believe that he also found the idea of causing panic, injuries, and potentially deaths as abhorrent as he claimed but I've got my doubts on that one.<br /> <br /> At any rate, without going too far into the sort of details that would require him to kill me for knowing he did clarify what was going on. Sundown Kwan and Dark Kimberly were both affiliated with the local tong. Kwan was the leader's girl and through him was secretly running things. Kimberly was jealous. Kwan (and I suppose Kimberly) were using their Changeling powers and influence to boost the tong's fortunes. This put them at odds with Lucien Torrez and his own primarily Latino criminal enterprise. Apparently warnings were sent and ignored and then an example was made of Sundown Kwan. Dark Kimberly distanced herself from the gang and their fortunes withered swiftly without fae support.<br /> <br /> All was well enough until White Maria hired a PI to look into Kwan's death after Kimberly\u2019s shooting. Gunnar confirmed that as far as he knows Lucien Torrez didn't have anything to do with that. And considering that he did task Gunnar with looking into it without telling him what not to find, it makes sense. Could the shooting have somehow been tied to the tong? Maybe, but all accounts are that they lack the supernatural means used. Someone trying to stir this whole mess up? Seems an awfully circuitous method with no guarantees of actually causing this particular fallout. No, I'm pretty sure it really was unrelated to this whole fucking clusterfuck.<br /> <br /> Gunnar explained that his efforts had ultimately been aimed at saving White Maria's life. Apparently Lucien Torrez's inclination had been to simply silence the woman. When I asked him about the Latino gang-bangers we'd spotted he truly seemed to know nothing about them. But given what he'd told me it was pretty clear that Torrez had run out of patience with the 'soft' touch.<br /> <br /> At this point, Gunnar was keen on leaving and nursing his headache. He also really wanted me to stop asking questions before we hit a point of no return. I think he is at least mildly fond of me, or at the very least doesn't actively dislike me. So I decided to bring the chat to a close and offered to give him a lift but he reminded me he could use a mirror. Before he left, he did ask to have his gun and cellphone battery back. I told him to come by Friday night at the show.<br /> <br /> I called and found out the others had followed White Maria home and were waiting. I took off on my bike to join them. While they were waiting, Gawain and De la Rocha had shaken the unfortunate ganger until answers fell out. He and his crew had been sent to trail White Maria and to grab her and deliver her to a warehouse in LA if they got a call. The whole thing was set up by a mid level boss named Alessandro Pi\u00f1a. Once he'd told them what he knew, he was suitably threatened and sent on his way.<br /> <br /> I arrived and we exchanged information. I didn't name Gunnar specifically but I don't think there was any question who I'd been speaking to. I wasn't in the mood to play around and suggested we just go to White Maria with the facts and lay the cards out for her. There was a bit of discussion but the motley agreed that the only way to end things without escalation was if White Maria let the matter drop. Lori and Jacob decided to go with me. Jacob to present the option of disappearing Maria (in the good way his entitlement does rather than the way Lucien would) and Lori to try to smooth things over since I was pretty clearly fed up with all this bullshit.<br /> <br /> White Maria was surprised to see us and even more so to see her missing clip. She invited us in and Lori started to explain things. I should have held my damn tongue and let Lori keep at her but the woman just wasn't taking the whole situation seriously. I lost my temper and just told her straight up that if she didn't drop it Lucien was going to have her fucking killed. That got her attention. She confirmed that we weren't there on Torrez's behalf and Lori pointed out that we weren't and pointedly added that it meant that if she did keep at it we would be at risk for telling her what we knew. She clearly hated it but she admitted that Torrez was out of her reach and that nothing good could come from further investigation of Sundown Kwan's death.<br /> <br /> She was not willing to forgive Dark Kimberly for her complacency in it but she did not seem inclined to seek retribution. There's no hate like the hate that blooms in the scorched heart and she feels (admittedly with justification) that Kimberly betrayed their friend and her by staying silent all these years. Lori wasn't satisfied to leave it at that. She seems determined to push for some sort of reconciliation. I guess, given her own history, she needs to believe in forgiveness. It's a pretty thought but I know all too well that some crimes can never be forgiven. In the end, the most White Maria would give was to say that if Dark Kimberly somehow atoned properly and deeply enough she would at least consider forgiving her.<br /> <br /> We left her and headed for home. At the time I think we were all feeling pretty fucking glum. Dark Kimberly was just a frightened girl in way the fuck over her head. And once it was over she was terrified that her friends would hate her for her weakness (which is exactly what fucking happened). So everyone involved is miserable and bitter and the one ultimately responsible is fucking untouchable.<br /> <br /> On the way back to the Dream House I called Becky and told her I needed to tell her about what had happened in person. Her voice was tense and I knew that the worst of the night was yet to come. Lori offered to tell her with me and I should have taken her up on it. No fucking way she couldn't have done a better job of it than I did but I felt some fucking misplaced sense of responsibility to do it my damn self and she'd already pushed her date with Oleander back but there was still time to salvage at least some of it. Gawain had previously made plans with Desiree to work on her subconscious trigger. I took his hands and told him I was sorry that I could help him with that after all. I wasn't sure how long the talk with Becky would be and I was pretty sure I wasn't going to be in any sort of headspace to do Oneiromancy. I do not doubt that if I had asked, he'd have canceled but as much as I wanted and maybe even needed the grounding he gives me I didn't want him to. See, I can be a fucking adult.<br /> <br /> When Becky arrived, I snagged a pair of glasses and a bottle of whiskey. She looked me dead in the eye and asked me if we were about to fight. I told her no, at least I was wasn't going to fight her and she frowned. We took a quiet seat and I set the drinks out, mainly to stall for a moment while I steeled myself for what was clearly going to be a difficult conversation.<br /> <br /> Compared to Becky, White Maria had taken the whole thing like a zen master. I was rather surprised that her glass didn't shatter when I refused to actually name Gunnar or Lucien directly. Becky's no fool, she'd already put the numbers together and guessed who was behind the campaign of terror and why. She already knew of Lucien's role in Sundown Kwan's death and she told me with utter certainty that some day he would die for it. As for Gunnar, she was out for blood but she wasn't prepared to kill him without confirmation. Unfortunately, all I was offering her were excuses she didn't want to hear. I pointed out that he'd honestly been trying to save White Maria's life and she conceded that rather than killing him she could perhaps settle for only maiming him. I added that he hadn't exactly told me what was going on without some duress. As much as I hated doing it, I intentionally left the statement vague enough for her to assume that I'd tortured it out of him and it seemed to placate her a little. As far as Dark Kimberly was concerned, she was unrelenting. I brought up the fact that she was only a teenager at the time and that she was clearly distraught over it and that there was no way to go after her without going through Annika but I really don't think anything made a dent in her rage. She thanked me and told me she needed to go and check on White Maria. It was terrible to see her so furious and hurt and frustrated. I tried to apologize but she just told me it wasn't my fault and left. I should have done something for her but I had no idea how to make any of it better. I still don't honestly. All I could do was watch her stalk away and feel miserable.<br /> <br /> The others came in and I muttered about how much I hated the whole fucking mess. There were people I cared about on both sides and I hadn't helped any of them and I felt like I'd let Becky down and more importantly I was afraid she felt like my attempts to smooth things over were some sort of betrayal.<br /> <br /> I was in the midst of this pitiful rambling when Insincere Marguerite did something completely unexpected. She leaned in and took me by the chin to lift my face and fix my eyes with her own. Then she just told me that this is why I am not a monster. For her, it was raw and direct and clearly painfully honest. I was too shocked to respond before she let me go and turned away. Then she left the room without another word, not exactly running but clearly not comfortable with drawing out the moment any longer than it had already lasted. As much as I call her my Darkling sister (and do love her like one) she sure as fuck isn't Sincere Marguerite. That whole brutal honestly and direct confrontations shit is my thing. Yet between that and the handmaidens she did both in one day, for me.<br /> <br /> Alone now, Jacob filled the silence by pointing out that had we not gotten involved tonight White Maria would likely have been taken by the toughs and quite possibly killed. He was right. I drained the rest of glass and signed. Maybe I hadn't fixed things but we had prevented a number of much more horrible outcomes. That is something worthwhile, though at the time all I could focus on was how disappointed Becky had seemed when she left. I refilled the glass and caught him watching me. I capped the bottle and slumped. I told him I was bummed but I was alright and wasn't going to do anything stupid. I just didn't want to sleep alone and Gawain was with Desiree so I was going to stay up rather than deal with my subconscious.<br /> <br /> He told he believed me but that a friend didn't leave another alone with their demons. On the heels of Insincere Marguerite's gesture and the concern the rest had shown not even my finely honed self loathing could muster a dismissal. So instead I gave him a weak smile and swirled my drink without actually sipping it. I told him that I could certainly use the company but if he was going to stay up we were not going to spend the whole night moping.<br /> <br /> He seemed pleased with my answer and got up, telling me he'd be right back. I sipped my drink and shook my head. I truly don't deserve the family I've found in my motley, but they just won't fucking give up. They may not always agree with who I am and what I do, but they accept me and even love me despite my best efforts. When Jacob returned he had a deck of cards. As he broke them out he asked me if I preferred Gin, Rummy, or Poker. I picked Poker but jokingly asked him what we were going to play for. He grabbed a pair of bowls of pretzel sticks from the bar.<br /> <br /> I smiled for real at that and mentioned that it reminded me of playing for jellybeans with Stasia. He told me that back in the Lady's realm sometimes he'd play for sticks since food was too scare and valuable, but here was different. I don't often talk to anyone about Stasia and Jacob is still pretty tight-lipped about his time in the lady's realm so the fact that we said as much as we did was an indication of how close we've grown. But neither of us was quite ready to go much further than that casual mention and there was no pressure to.<br /> <br /> We let those topics go and slipped back to comfortable quiet or small talk for a bit as we traded salty winnings back and forth. It was surprisingly soothing actually, the game was distracting enough that my mind wasn't dwelling on the events of the night.<br /> <br /> After a bit, Jacob brought up talking to Lowjack about his past as Rime. He seemed nervous about it and I can't blame him for that. But I told him he should. Better to get ahead of that rather than have it come to light. I told him as much, that being honest would serve him much better than trying to convince Lowjack and especially Dahlia in response to it coming to light from some other source. I then pointed out that Dahlia was from Snow Globe like me, and thus distrustful and paranoid.<br /> <br /> Jacob asked me if I was okay with talking about Snow Globe and having someone else from there about. I admitted that as much as I want answers I am also a little worried what those answers will be. But I assured him that I'd rather know it's as bad or worse than I fear than continue to not know. He told me he didn't want to bring up bad memories and I had to chuckle. I explained that Snow Globe was nothing but bad memories but I was alright talking about it. I did also mention that Dahlia didn't really want people to know about her being from Snow Globe so he shouldn't bring it up, especially not in front of Lowjack.<br /> <br /> I also pointed out that if we told Lowjack and Dahlia about his past that we could explain the situation with Rook and maybe get them on board with trying to bring him around or at least not assuming that we're loyalists for trying to do so ourselves. He seemed a bit skeptical but I know he cares about his former partner and I am sure that he is going to try to help the man when (I'm pretty damn sure it's when not if) he returns to the area no matter what the powers that be decide.<br /> <br /> I asked him if he wanted me to accompany him to talk to them about his past and he accepted the offer gladly. He's been there for me and we're family. I do know more about how to approach Dahlia and as I told him (mostly) jokingly, worst case I'll get a chance to see what my fellow escapee can do in a fight. And hopefully my being there to vouch for him will count for something with them.<br /> <br /> We played past sunrise and through the morning until Gawain came wandering in looking for me. It was a bit early and he seemed relieved to find me in something resembling a good mood. He joined us for a few hands and told us that he'd managed to succeed in finishing the removal of Desiree's trigger programming. He was quite pleased both at his accomplishment and at having helped her. I told him I was proud of him and happy it had gone so well. He really is a good man and I love him so much. Yeah, that makes the prospect of failing him or dragging him down so much worse but it's also all the more reason not to let myself be that monster.<br /> <br /> Once Gawain headed to make breakfast, I also excused myself. I hadn't really planned to start the whole meditation thing yesterday but seeing him had rekindled my desire to become the woman he deserves. I was already feeling a lot more focused. I'd had time for the motley's support to sink in past my knee jerk inclination to try to brush it off. I'd also had time to realize that as unsatisfying as things felt they had gone well. White Maria was safe from terrorizing and being murdered. Becky wasn't happy but she'd gone to check up on her friend not hunt down and murder anyone. Dark Kimberly was at least safe from physical harm and as far as the social fallout, it was coming at her own actions. I hate it and I wish I could spare her that but she made that choice and even if she was just a stupid girl at the time it's at least partially her own fault for being too weak to stand up for her friend or to be honest about it. I'm not sure exactly where the whole thing leaves me with either her or Becky right now, and I'm not okay with that. I just hope Becky doesn't feel like I've betrayed her.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I went and settled in and followed the guidelines Dr Emmett had given me. It wasn't that hard to relax my body. I think it helps that I'm not prone to fidgeting and have actually practiced remaining perfectly still for long periods of time. Getting my head clear was more of a challenge. Thankfully, I was already in a fairly decent place mentally by that point. At first it really just felt kinda silly and pointless. But I kept at it and at some point things just faded back. I mean, I was still completely aware of everything that had happened but I stopped second guessing what I'd done and just let it go. The actions of my motley, my friends, was even clearer in my mind as I thought about them. I had a weird moment of clarity there, thinking about how I'd feel if it was someone else that I was so distrustful of while they were so clearly prepared to support them. And I know that Captain Jack wouldn't have stood before the monarchs and told them he believed in my ability to master my urges and impulses if he hadn't believed it.<br /> <br /> By the time I headed to breakfast that sense of calm stayed with me. I was looking forward, thinking of how best to deal with the results of my actions rather than dwelling on what I could have done differently. I was thinking about the things I needed to speak to Joaquin about. I should thank him for believing in me and I should speak to him about John Lowjack. But these are things best down out of character as it were and in private. I ended up asking De la Rocha if she could recommend a good restaurant with decent Mexican food and a nice atmosphere while we were waiting for the rest of the motley. She looked up from her dual screen (newly acquired during our outing at the pier I believe) and seemed a bit curious so I explained that I wanted to treat Captain Jack to a nice dinner and thank him for his help with my trail and all. At that she gave me a couple of suggestions of places she knows he likes.<br /> <br /> From there, the hijinks started (as they tend to do at the infamous sex breakfast). Lori showed up with Oleander and Handsome served them both up some of his amazing omelets (more like ZOMG-lets really). As we were all enjoying the good food and good company Lori put forth that we'd been living together in Malibu and hadn't gone to the beach once. Well, it was rather quickly pointed out that there were rather a lot of Darklings in the room. Of course, DLR is Summer Court and goes out of her way to prove herself by spending as much time in the sunlight as possible. I am not quite so dedicated to it as that as I do prefer to go out at night but I don't back down from the Daystar's fiery gaze when necessary. Insincere Marguerite was fine so long as she had a kerchief for her hair (which ended up being pretty much all of her that was covered, not that I minded) Julia was the only real holdout. She countered that the beach was better at night, even going so far as to resort to trying to appeal to Lori's romantic sensibilities. But in the end, she agreed so long as she was allowed to bring and remain under her [strike]umbrella[/strike] tent.<br /> <br /> We broke to change, with Oleander heading back to her place and Jacob calling and inviting Luna. I am glad to see the two of them getting close. They are well matched and they do seem to make each other happy. I mean, who else would my mentor wear a bathing suit for? Once we were changed we loaded up Handsome's van since parking is rough at the beach. De la Rocha tossed her boards on the roof rack and so as we were heading from parking lot to water we stopped at one of the ubiquitous huts to rent some more boards.<br /> <br /> She took charge of teaching Lori (who put her wings to good use to aid her balance, which was quite a breathtaking sight for those that could see it) and Insincere Marguerite (who took it upon herself to show off her contracts of separation and her tongue). Gawain hadn't gone surfing since before being taken but he clearly still had his moves. Jacob and I proved to be quick studies, which doesn't surprise me given our fighting prowess. All in all it was a lot of fun. I think I'd like to do it again sometime.<br /> <br /> Once we were all back in from the waves it was time for the beach volleyball. There was some debate about how to divide up but in the end it was Lori, De la Rocha, Insincere Marguerite, and Oleander (the Lovers) against Gawain, Jacob, Luna, and myself (the Fighters). We started to draw a crowd even before the game even started but the mood was high and not even the less exhibitionistic among us seemed self conscious about having an audience. Lori was soaking it up and showing off, using her wings to hang in the air that extra second as often as possible. I think the sensation of surfing had rekindled some memories of flying in her. Insincere Marguerite put that tongue to good use, lashing it out to give her the extra reach to make a couple of returns she'd have missed otherwise. De la Rocha was ferocious in keeping the whole team on point. There was no question that she was playing to win not just have fun but she never took things too far (not even when she flashed Gawain to try to distract him.) My side of the net had more quiet determination. But we were all having fun. Luna smiled despite all the noise and people. I am really glad that none of the baggage of their pasts seems to come between them. I mean, it doesn't faze me but I know some folks would be weird about that fact that he used to be a loyalist and she used to be a man. But Arcadia changes us all. Hell, I used to be nice and well-mannered.<br /> <br /> We all played hard and I think that while it was certainly the sexy that drew attention it was the sheer physicality that held it. At one point, De la Rocha did decide to flash Gawain to throw him off a return and I did return the favor by whisperwisping a few comments in her ear. I have to say, it was a bit of a thrill to see how hard she blushed. Ultimately, none of the 'underhanded' tactics really affected things which is for the best. The Lovers edged out the Fighters and won the day. De la Rocha's machismo started up immediately but it was good natured. I had to make a few suggestive jabs for the sake of appearances of course but the mood was high and it was all in fun.<br /> <br /> After the game we all settled a bit. Well, DLR took her board back out and without any beginners to watch over she was in the zone and really showed off her stuff. Lori and Insincere Marguerite both stretched out for some sunbathing while Jacob and Luna settled in together. Gawain and I set to working on a sand castle. Damn thing was looking really nice before I got impatient and tried to build it up too high without packing it down enough. All that effort evaporated in seconds and left me sitting there with a half crumbled ruin. Gawain, of course, was cool. I mean, he wasn't happy that I'd done it but he just gave me a look and moved a few feet away to start over. I stayed where I was, scowling at the treasonous pile of sand that had betrayed me and running my fingers back and forth in the loose pile. And then something from earlier hit me and I started to sculpt the sand that had spilled. See, on the way to the beech I had commented that I was a bit low on glamor and Gawain had interrupted to state firmly that there would be no shark fins. So... I glanced over at where he was working and started making a fin out of sand. Gawain glanced over (because even if he was working alone he was still keeping an eye on me to make sure I was okay because he loves me like that). I shielded it from him with my body at first but then once it was clear what it was I sat on the other side and was rewarded with a shake of his head and a smile.<br /> <br /> So yeah, it was that kind of day, relaxed and silly and just... happy. Gods and goddesses above and below did I need that. I think we all did but I felt so much better as we started to gather our things so we could be back in time for the show. I stepped over and took Lori by the hand. Once she'd stopped and looked over I leaned in (careful with my glass of course) and just wrapped my arms around her tight and thanked her. She seemed a little surprised but smiled really brightly as I stepped back.<br /> <br /> Then it was time to return the boards and pile into the van and return to the Dream House. It was Friday, so it was Annika's night to perform. I could tell from the moment I saw her that she was not in a good mood. When I greeted her and asked if she was well she was very curt though not quite rude. I could see that she wasn't truly feeling her performances though I think it was only that I know her so well. The guests certainly didn't seem displeased. At the end of the show, I tried again, thinking that with the need to focus on her act behind her she might be more inclined to talk. But she wasn't. Again, she wasn't rude, just very firm about not wanting to talk. Then she informed me that she was going to go disappoint Spidertoes and go home. As a friend, and I do consider myself her friend, it's hard to just give someone space and do nothing when they are clearly hurting or upset but it was the only thing I could do at that point.<br /> <br /> As Is said, her acts were as flawless as ever and the rest of the show went really well. Lori sang Tom Petty's 'Learning to Fly' in the first act and turned it into such a wistful and mournful thing. It's not something she talks about but I know she misses the power of flight and she channeled all of it into that song. But after the intermission she flipped the switch completely in the other direction. She hit the stage in her bikini and sang an insanely over the top number named 'Because I'm a Blonde'. It lifted spirits and had folks laughing to end the night on a much higher note.<br /> <br /> As things were wrapping up, I drew Insincere Marguerite, Gawain, and Jacob off to talk to them. I explained that Gunnar had told me he had heard that someone was dealing drugs out of the Dream House. I asked if anyone knew anything about it. Insincere Marguerite and Gawain started to muse on who it might be and exactly what they were selling while Jacob seemed more thoughtful than usual. I wasn't sure and I didn't want to call him out even if I was right so I used my powers to whisper to him and ask if there was something he needed to tell us.<br /> <br /> Well, I think he was already considering telling us or maybe my prompting did it but he quietly informed them that it was heroin and he was the one selling it. There was a dead silence and then Insincere Marguerite started trying to change the subject. I think she wanted to diffuse the whole mess and keep us from grilling Jacob. Gawain seemed a little put back by the fact that it was heroin and not something softer. I swore to protect Jacob as part of my motley. I did also swear to protect the Autumn Court's investment in the Dream House. So I was caught trying to sort out the potential legal ramifications. Gawain chipped in as I was considering and put that concern to rest. So long as the money was entirely going to Jacob and his supplier then there was nothing to prove the Dream House was an accessory or accomplice. Even if the police did comb over the books, there was nothing to find and no way to shut us down or charge us. Since the house was safe, I relaxed. I'm not sure any of us expected it and I don't think anyone really approves but he's one of us and he doesn't sell to children or anything that sleazy. Gawain was not cool with learning that he was and still is dealing for Darke and I can't blame him. At some point, Lori joined us and her reactions matched up pretty evenly with ours. She did ask him about some less hardcore drugs but Jacob isn't a multi-stocked retailer. For my part, I made sure he was alright with things given the whole shift in power and offered to do anything I could to help if he did decide to stop and had any trouble severing his ties. He thanked me but said he was fine with the situation at the moment.<br /> <br /> I think we were all rather looking to drop that line of conversation but the mood was serious and no one wanted to just start up about the weather or that local sports team you know. The lull passed though and Julia brought up that Insincere Marguerite's last name was Blessent. My Darkling sister was not pleased. For one thing, that was her fetch's married name which she'd kept after her divorce so it was not and never had been HER name. Her name had been DeLisle but she wasn't that person anymore. I think she was bothered that Julia had gone digging and I know she's a bit ashamed of who she was before. But that got the topic of fetches started and a few stories of where and what are imposters were came up. Lori's is old and living back in Iowa. Insincere Marguerite's is apparently divorced and fat. Jacob's is young and whiny and in a band, which I am pretty sure is an excuse to be unemployed and high. Gawain's is a Duke (which gave everyone a moment of confusion before he explained that it was an SCA thing.). De la Rocha didn't have one, so she was able to slip back into her life when she returned. Julia's had an 'accident' involving a well. I told them about the Sinister Bitch myself.<br /> <br /> The topic of names prompted Lori to explaining how she got her new one. It was an interesting story, she was lost in the hedge and to keep from losing herself she latched onto a memory for her father teaching her to sing Amazing Grace. And as she sang it, she heard an answering song. Lorelei by Styx. She followed it and found herself out of the hedge to where it was playing on a radio. I did always think her chosen name fit her perfectly but knowing the story behind it makes it even more appropriate. That got the rest of us to talking about how we escaped. Julia was able to paint a path out (something she can't do anymore sadly). Jacob found his way back to the cave he'd stumbled through to get into the Lady's Realm. I told them how I literally ran into Gawain while fleeing and we helped each other make our way out. He tried to claim it was all me of course, saying he'd never have known which way to go without me. But I would never have been able to make a path through without him clearing the heaviest of the thorns away first. De la Rocha just fought everything in her path until she ran across Monica and got knocked out and woke up back in the world.<br /> <br /> We drifted up to the den and pulled out the now standard ice cream and booze to accompany the movie. It wasn't Monday but we decided that Lori needed to see Cannibal so she could give it the thumbs up or down. It was a spedonkle night from there. That move was as awesomely awful as I remember from when Stasia and I watched it. Of course, this time I was curled up in Gawain's lap and nibbling ice cream while he held me close. The beach and the meditation and all was nice but nothing was as restorative as laying my head against his solid chest while he ran his fingers through my hair and circled me with his arms. As the movie wrapped up, Lori agreed it was something we had to do but then she launched into the technical concerns we'd need to address. I made a few comments but mainly was too busy feeling content to really get into things. I did drop Captain Jack a text to let him know we wanted him for a part in a show, he'd be perfect for the cyclops. It's a small part but it needs someone like him to just take it over the top.<br /> <br /> When Gawain gathered me up and rose from the loveseat I think I might have actually purred. He is so strong yet so careful and gentle with me. And that's a thing that would set me off in all the wrong ways with anyone else but with him... I just relax. I curl into him and feel safe and protected and happy. Maybe Doc Emmett can sort out the why of it but I don't rightly care about how it works as much as that it does. We made love and it was as magical and tender and sweet as anything I'd imagined before I was taken. I fell asleep in those strong arms and I sleep deeply.<br /> <br /> I was back to feeling much more Calamity than Katt when I woke though I was certainly a very pleased little monster indeed to wake in my Handsome's arms. I always sleep long and hard after I stay up but rather than leave me to it, Gawain was laying there just watching me sleep half atop him and stroking my hair when my eyes fluttered open. I told him I loved him and then I decided to offer up a practical demonstration of the ardor and intensity of my feelings before letting him go fix breakfast while I basked in the lingering scent and warmth of him in our bed and wrote. I imagine he's about done by now and the bed's gone cool anyway. Also, as nice as yesterday was, there are things that need doing today. Time for this little monster to get busy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T22:54:01-07:00","id":630727,"title":"","content":"<b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> It\u2019s been too long since I slept last. I stayed up all night with Calamity, keeping her company and trying to raise her spirits. I think it worked to some extent. I caught her smirking more than once when we were playing poker. Of course she really brightened up when Gawain got up and came downstairs. He joined us for a few hands of cards before leaving to make breakfast. After he joined us her smiles were a little more genuine and she laughed easier. He is so good for her. When Gawain went off to cook breakfast Calamity went up to her room to meditate. Apparently it\u2019s something that her therapist has been having her do. I hadn\u2019t really thought about it, but it seems to be having positive effects already. Wonder if it would do anything for me? Might help me cram those pesky bad memories back in their boxes. Though I\u2019m fairly certain that a therapist would not advocate my particular idea for meditation.<br /> <br /> While Gawain was in the kitchen Lori and Oleander came back to the Dream House. I guess they spent the night at her place. There was conversation and Lorelei brought up the idea of going to the beach. She said that we\u2019d been living together for months now and have yet to go to the beach for a day of fun in the sun. Well, the Darklings in the group had something to say about that, but not all of them were opposed to going to the beach. De la Rocha seemed up for it right off. Insincere Marguerite was all for the idea as long as she had a large kerchief to put over her head. Julia was patently opposed to going at all, but was eventually talked into it. She finally relented and said she\u2019d go if she could bring her sun umbrella with her. The others agreed. I thought the idea of going to the beach sounded like fun, so I called Luna and asked if she\u2019d be interested in going with me. She was a little hesitant at first, I think because she wasn\u2019t so sure about a bathing suit, but she eventually said \u201cyes.\u201d<br /> <br /> We all rode in Gawain\u2019s van to make parking easier. It was kind of cozy in the back with all of us in there, but we made it work. De la Rocha brought her surf board, which kind of prompted some of us to rent boards once we got there. She gave us all a crash course in surfing and sent us on our way. Our instructor was helping Lorelei, which was interesting to watch. Having those wings must help her balance. Gawain did really well for a first time. Insincere Marguerite was certainly having fun as well. At one point she was balancing on her tongue. I\u2019m not sure what the humans saw when she was doing that. Must have been interesting though. I think I did okay for my first time. Balance is a strong suit of mine so I didn\u2019t have any problems staying on the board. It took some getting used to, to steer it the way I wanted it to go though. But like the skateboarding, I picked it up pretty quick and had a good time.<br /> <br /> After that we played a volleyball game. We divided up, Lorelei, Oleander, De la Rocha and Insincere Marguerite vs. me, Gawain, Calamity and Luna. Someone dubbed it the Lovers vs. the Fighters. Cute. I will admit that it\u2019s been awhile since I\u2019ve played any kind of team sport. There wasn\u2019t a lot of sports in the Lady\u2019s realm and any other physical activity was usually sparring, hiking or strength training, which are not exactly team activities. I think the last time I played an actual sport was in high school, and that for me was a very long time ago. The game went well though. De la Rocha was extremely competitive which led to a bit of friendly attempted sabotage on both sides. De la Rocha flashed her breasts at Gawain trying to distract him. In retaliation Calamity whispered something in the Latinas ear. Not sure what was said, but De la Rocha went a little red, and it wasn\u2019t from exertion. In the end, though it was a really close game, the Lover\u2019s won the day.<br /> <br /> Once the crowd that had gathered dispersed we split up and did our own thing. Gawain started making a sand castle with Calamity\u2019s help, but she ended up living up to her name and the castle came tumbling down. Gawain then started over, but wouldn\u2019t let Calamity help. Calamity decided that the best use of her time was to sculpt a shark fin swimming through the ruins of the first sand castle. I thought it was funny and I think Gawain did too. I took some pictures. Most of us went swimming or wading too. Julia stayed underneath her black umbrella and essentially hid from the sun. She seemed to be enjoying watching the rest of us, so I think she had a good time. <br /> <br /> I will admit that I have not been swimming at the beach in a very long time. Again the last time I went was sometime in high school. Though the beaches in Oregon don\u2019t really compare to the ones here in California. But the swimming was fun. Luna joined me in the water and I tried to make sure that she was having a good time. I think after a little while she forgot about being self-conscious and just let herself have fun. Lorelei waded in the water. Calamity I think was trying to throw sand at someone, at least she had gathered some up in her hand, but Gawain thwarted her. He picked her up and carried her into the water and dumped her in. It was kind of funny. Later when we were about to leave the beach Calamity went up to Lori and gave her a hug, and thanked her for the idea of coming to the beach.<br /> <br /> We have all been under varying amounts of stress lately but I think Calamity has been under a good deal more than some of the others. She eventually hit bottom and asked for help, which is a good thing, but I think that coming to the beach was better for her than therapy as far as relieving tension.<br /> <br /> For the most part it was pretty relaxing for me too. I had fun playing volleyball and surfing, but while some of the others were making sandcastles I just watched. I started to make one of my own, but got distracted by a couple of kids nearby burying each other in the sand. I started to dig my own feet into the sand until I was buried to my calves, but things got a bit hazy after that. The sensation of being buried was all too familiar and suddenly I was in the Lady\u2019s cell again. She had me strung up by my wrists to the ceiling and started forming ice around my feet. She moved the ice up my legs slowly, encasing me in it until she reached my neck. It wasn\u2019t the cold that got to me, it was the feeling of utter helplessness at being completely immobile. Then she started making spikes of ice, small at first, grow out of the ice that encased me and angled it inward. It of course had only one place to go, through me. At first it was just pin pricks. Then the spikes grew in length and diameter, very slowly. I don\u2019t know how long the spikes got to in the end. I only knew pain as the ice turned pink, and then red. I jerked my feet free of the sand as I came back to myself. I think I startled Luna, but assured her that I was fine. I\u2019m not sure if she fully believed me or not, but she didn\u2019t bring it up again. <br /> <br /> After having fun in the water for a bit we dried off and headed back to the Dream House. We needed to get back in time to get ready for the show. We got back in good time. Everyone was able to wash the sand off and get dressed up. I talked to Calamity after she was done dressing up to make sure she would be available to go with me to talk to Lowjack tomorrow afternoon. She said that she would be happy to come and reassured me that everything would be fine. I know that she\u2019s probably right, but I still can\u2019t help but be nervous. If things don\u2019t go well with Lowjack tomorrow then I will probably be in trouble. It should be fine though. I haven\u2019t been loyal to the Lady since well before I came to this freehold, and I consciously left her service. That has to count for something, right?<br /> <br /> Anyhoo\u2026 near the beginning of the show I saw Calamity go over to talk to Gunnar. A short while later he came up to the bar to collect a package that our resident Razorhand have left for him. I\u2019ll admit, I peeked. It was a cell phone battery and a gun. I don\u2019t know if that confirms that Gunnar was the one harassing White Maria or not. Not sure why else Calamity would have his weapon. He doesn\u2019t seem the type to let go of it willingly either. I bet there is an interesting story there. I\u2019ll have to ask Calamity how she got that stuff. <br /> <br /> When Gunnar had left and business slowed down for a bit I pushed down any apprehension I was feeling and called Lowjack to set up that meeting for tomorrow afternoon. We agreed on 1:30pm. That should give us enough time to eat and get over to his place. He also mentioned that he had someplace to show me that was associated with the Knights of the Utmost Silence. Sounded like a safe house or something like that. I guess I\u2019ll find out tomorrow if I still get to see it. I know, I\u2019m probably worrying over nothing. Still not sure how to tell him about being Rime. How do you open that conversation? I started talking about Rook to the motley which led into me telling them about Rime, but I didn\u2019t want to start off that way with Lowjack. I was going to bring up Rook after I told him about myself.<br /> <br /> Yeah, so as it turned out worrying about how to tell my King that I was a loyalist was not my only concern for today. After the show was over Calamity called Insincere Marguerite, Gawain and me over to talk. She brought up that she\u2019d been talking to Gunnar and he mentioned that someone was selling drugs out of the club. Her concern was that one of the dancers or kitchen staff was dealing. I guess I wasn\u2019t up to form tonight because she did that whisper thing in my ear and asked if I had something to share with the group. About that same time Insincere Marguerite made a comment about cocaine gas stations or something along those lines. Not sure what she was on about, but figured if Calamity saw something on my face I better fess up. I also didn\u2019t want some poor sod who works in our kitchen to get canned because I\u2019m dealing on the side. So, I said that it wasn\u2019t cocaine, it was heroin, and that kind of killed the conversation for a few seconds. There were a few questions, mostly along the lines of making sure I don\u2019t sell to kids and stuff like that.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite, bless her, tried to make things a little less awkward and take the heat off of me by talking about smoking too much pot and her getting too relaxed and just becoming a pile of limbs. About that time Lorelei and De la Rocha came over and the whole thing was brought up again for her information. She seemed to have the same questions, no dealing to kids, that kind of thing. For the most part people seemed to take the news well. At least no one told me to pack up my stuff and leave over it. Things got a little tenser when I mentioned that I was selling for Darke. Gawain in particular was not happy about that. He does not like that man in the least and was not happy that I was dealing for him. Gawain might also have a problem with the drugs, but he didn\u2019t say anything to me about it. He did comment that heroin is one of the bad ones. <br /> <br /> Lori asked if I sold anything besides heroin and I said no. I think she\u2019s looking to try other recreational drugs but didn\u2019t want to go too hard core, so to speak. I can understand that. Heroin is rather addictive and it\u2019s hard to get off of. That\u2019s my guess as to why Darke sells it in the first place. He runs the rehab clinic so he can guarantee a supply of glamour off of the poor sods trying to get clean of it. <br /> <br /> Because I mentioned Darke I think some of the others may be under the impression that I didn\u2019t have a choice about selling drugs. Calamity offered to help me if/when I decided to get out of the drug business. I may take her up on it someday, but am not planning on doing that in the near future. The others act like they\u2019re okay with things, but I suspect that they aren\u2019t quite as cool with it as they say. I don\u2019t see a problem with things as they are. The club is not profiting from the drug sales so they are not connected to my side activities in any way. If I get caught they won\u2019t get in trouble. I know I should probably feel bad about selling heroin to people. It really isn\u2019t a good drug to take, and is highly addictive. Hence my repeat customers, but it really isn\u2019t good for people. I don\u2019t sell to kids. I try not to sell to any college students in general, but some of them probably do go to the University. If I know that someone has been trying to clean up I will sometimes act like I\u2019m all out so they don\u2019t get any more. I do little things, but I should probably still feel worse about this than I do. I think something is wrong with me.<br /> <br /> Somehow the conversation moved onto fetches. I think Julia mentioned looking up Insincere Marguerite\u2019s old last name and it spawned from that. Everyone mentioned what their fetch was doing. Calamity\u2019s apparently is a fairly successful Ad Executive, Insincere Marguerite\u2019s is in the Fascist Party in France (and is fat), Lori\u2019s is in Iowa and being married. De la Rocha said that she didn\u2019t have a fetch, so she was able to step back into her old life. Lucky her. I mentioned the goth/Emo wannabe in Portland that wears my face. Nobody went into a lot of detail. Just a quick little bit about what their fetch was up to. By comparison it was a light hearted conversation.<br /> <br /> Of course sex had to come up at some point. The main topic of this conversation turned into who was each person\u2019s first same-sex partner. I heard at first who was everyone\u2019s first partner which brought up all kinds of bad memories for me. You\u2019d think that a guy\u2019s first time would be nice if a bit awkward. My first time was in Arcadia. One of the Lady\u2019s treasures, Desire, wanted to see if she could \u201cthaw me out a bit\u201d as she put it. I was young, she was beautiful. At the time I thought that I was the lucky target of her affections. I did not realize at the time that she slept with pretty much everyone. She lived up to her name I\u2019ll give her that. <br /> <br /> The conversation was about first same sex partners and I\u2019ve not had sex with another man before, so I just kind of stayed out of that conversation. At least, I don\u2019t know if Luna views herself more as a woman or as a man so I didn\u2019t want to bring that up. I\u2019m cool with either way she goes. Though I have felt kind of awkward just flat out asking her if I should adjust which pronoun I use. I don\u2019t want to make her self-conscious. Luna is a beautiful person. She is caring, for those close to her, quiet, and dangerous. You\u2019d think that the last bit would turn me off, but I know that I am dangerous too, so we\u2019re a good match.<br /> <br /> After that, maybe to change topic, maybe because Insincere Marguerites old name had been brought up, I don\u2019t know, Lorelei asked us if we knew how she picked her name. I don\u2019t think most of us knew so she told us. Apparently when she was trying to get out of the Hedge she was singing hymns as a way to remember herself and to keep herself focused. She was humming \u201cAmazing Grace.\u201d Then as she was walking she heard music answer her back. It was \u201cLorelei\u201d by Styx. So after she got back she chose the name Lorelei Grace. I thought that was rather poetic. I\u2019m glad her name has meaning for her. That\u2019s how it should be. It should not just be something that you pick off a list of names. It should be something that means something to you. <br /> <br /> I chose my name because I wanted to take back the name Jacob, and I chose Stojanovic to honor my mother\u2019s father. From her stories of him he was a dour man who rarely smiled, but he loved his family dearly and worked very hard to provide for them. The only photograph we had of him was standing next to my grandmother looking grim. I think it was the fact that he spent so much time outside that he face became weathered. Unfortunately I never got to meet him. He died when I was an infant. Sometimes I wish I could have met him and talked to him. I am afraid of what he\u2019d think of me, but I am still curious what his views on things were. <br /> <br /> When Lori told her story of getting out of the hedge it prompted others to briefly tell how they got out. Calamity ran until she found Gawain, and together they made their way out to the \u2018world.\u2019 De la Rocha fought her way out. She didn\u2019t give a lot of details, and that was fine. Julia painted paths out of the hedge and followed them home. Gawain said that he followed Calamity and likely wouldn\u2019t have made it out without her. I just told the others, since we were in a larger group, that I managed to find the path that I took to get into the Hedge and followed it back out. That is not a complete lie. I did know several paths to get back to \u2018the world,\u2019 but as I was running from the Lady I managed somehow to find the same cave and passage that I followed to get to Her realm in the first place.<br /> <br /> Rather unexpectedly, but not unwanted, conversation turned to movies, and we decided to do a movie night. The film that was chosen was \u201cCannibal the Musical.\u201d Yeah, that is a strange, bad, and hilarious movie. I think it was made better by Lori\u2019s staple of bourbon and ice cream for movie nights. The others want to do a production of this film for the Dream House and I applaud them for it. I am curious to see what they come up with. I may have fallen asleep through some of it, but then I have been up for two days straight. Speaking of which I need sleep. I will write more if all goes well tomorrow. If nothing is written in this journal after this entry then I will bid you a fond farewell.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> Today has been a good day. I\u2019ve come down from a nice late night snack on the roof with Julia. I expressed how I felt about my privacy intrusion, she discussed her frustration that I was withholding my family name, and we got back in a good place with each other. Fortunately.<br /> <br /> I had not really considered how my withholding a name might affect her. Admittedly, she did no say it bothered her, but even semi-even relationships are new to me. The implications of her interest have also not been missed.<br /> <br /> Today started as it often does. De La Rocha was playing the portable game system I acquired when Lorelei and Oleander arrived for breakfast. I felt (without even touching her) De La Rocha tense but she kept playing. Lorelei played it some but feigned ignorance of video games. This despite having played more modern ones with us. Video games are not her favored sort of games. Lorelei was super keen, however, on going to the beach. The beach is\u2026not my first choice, but several wanted to go, so I decided not to be a killjoy. I put on my kerchief (the French Flag one) and a bathing suit and stepped out. Julia wore a long one-piece bathing suit that was conservative, and a long tee shirt with some Goth girl character having coffee. Lorelei and De La Rocha wore bikinis, of course. Oleander had to go home for a suit and Jacob called Luna so there was some time for them to arrive. Luna for her part wore a one-piece but forest green and not quite as covering as Julia\u2019s black one.<br /> <br /> There was surfing, in which Gawain did a rather remarkable job especially for a man his size. Others of us tried with less spectacular results. I hear Malibu is a major surfing location, and can see why. It was easy to pick up extra boards\u2026only De La Rocha owned any, and she used hers. She does like purple. Obviously.<br /> <br /> Surfing was fun. The water is, however, a touch cold. Then there was the volleyball, the \u201clovers\u201d (Lorelei, De La Rocha, Oleander and I) against the \u201cfighters\u201d (Calamity, Gawain, Luna, Jacob). How De La Rocha got in a team called the \u201clovers\u201d over a team called the \u201cfighters\u201d remains mysterious. I did use my tongue and flexibility to show off a bit, then we waded in the water some, at which point De La Rocha did some very impressive surfing, I suppose the waves cooperated more with her then. Then it was all sunbathing and sandcastles. Happily.<br /> <br /> Julia, for her part, put up a black pavilion umbrella and sat on a beach chair and watched us through her sunglasses, quite happy to not be in the sunlight. I thought I was photophobic. <br /> <br /> Eventually we went in, all of good cheer. The show went all right, I am given to understand Annika was not in a good mood. Spidertoes was in the audience and we spoke briefly. Gunnar arrived to get his gun and battery for his phone. I manifested myself, and we sat awhile and talked. Gunnar conceded we were, in fact, a serious threat to each other. He could seek revenge for being trussed up and kidnapped, as was his inclination, but depending on how complete it was, I might come after him again and leave him in a situation he was less likely to walk out of. He sought an end to hostilities, so we made a cease-fire pact, that we would not act against the other\u2026without a courtesy note ending the protection a reasonable amount of time before the first strike. This seemed fair (I was not after him anyway) so we agreed to it and he was on his way.<br /> <br /> Lorelei found herself in a tense moment as the show ended, as Oleander and De La Rocha were\u2026well not staring down but sort of watching like great cats in the same cage. There was tension, and it was growing. Lorelei managed to defuse the situation for now, with Oleander headed home and De La Rocha staying with her. I hope it does not become a serious problem. Neither Oleander with her poisons nor De La Rocha with her aggression and aptitude for curses are people I would want as my enemy.<br /> <br /> While that went on the rest of us had one of the most meandering conversations we have ever had. Calamity had discovered someone was dealing, and it turned out that someone was Jacob, dealing Heroin. I felt this was a poor choice. Heroin is a drug cops notice. They may be slow to move against weed (especially in LA) but Heroin is a problem. Still, it was his deal and I was unprepared to move against him. The conversation obviously had him uncomfortable, so I made reference to Julia and weed, and after mentioning a distaste for her dealer Gawain recommended his old landlord in Santa Monica to get weed from while Calamity recommended Austin. Lorelei sauntered over and noted she was growing now, using her Spring magic. Spring magic is interesting.<br /> <br /> I wonder why Gawain did not join the Summer Court. He is good a being angry. Maybe he needs weed.<br /> <br /> Names had come up, and my last name came up when De La Rocha asked, and Julia said my last name was Blessent. This is untrue, I was confused a moment then I realized\u2026she used the old picture of I to find my Fetch, using the reverse Google search. I found this disquieting. Julia had tracked down my fat replacement and could have found my family. I quickly told her my name was not Blessent, the name of my Fetch\u2019s ex-husband I never married, but DeLisle.<br /> <br /> I never told them that because Marguerite DeLisle was the person I was before being taken. Insincere Marguerite is how I returned. Marguerite DeLisle was a fascist with the Front National. I am Insincere Marguerite, not Marguerite DeLisle. Still, it has caused Julia some joy to learn the name. I am surprised by how she has taken to it, whispering it to herself or writing it, given her lack of interest in romance. But she has a romantic soul and a poetic heart; she just hides it. She is, perhaps, one of the most passionate people I know. If only she would allow herself to see herself that way. Romantically.<br /> <br /> I digress, from there we moved into the awkwardness of our first same sex encounter. Lorelei\u2019s and I\u2019s was in Arcadia, but Julia talked about waking up and mistaking my hair for hers before realizing I was laying on her (I am rather light), and De La Rocha spoke of waking up, lying it bed a few minutes, and looking over to see Madame Spidertoes silently watching her in a chair eating a sandwich. That one won for being surreal. Calamity for her part noted she has never <i><i>slept</i></i> with a member of the same sex. Just Gawain. Because of his armor. Naturally.<br /> Sadly the boys did not have one. Shame, I have no idea how two men would handle wake up or that sort of thing. Same as anyone else I guess? Maybe I can ask Jack.<br /> <br /> We decided to watch some movies, to cap off a good night,. I suggested <i><i>Mulholland Drive</i></i> but we just watched <i><i>Cannibal the Musical</i></i>. We will watch <i><i>Mulholland Drive</i></i> Monday, I suppose. We discussed options for our burlesque interpretation, and I made some notes while Julia scribbled \u201cDeLisle\u201d all fancy over and over. There was a sidetrack about the Smurfs, which Lorelei somehow had not heard of despite them going back to the 60s, and Lorelei for reasons that could only have been her own asserted her French was flawless after Gawain corrected my English, leaving I unsure how to deal with such a blatant falsehood without saying something ugly, so I just said nothing, I don\u2019t think. I was too addled to recall clearly, honestly.<br /> <br /> Afterwards, the couples retired. I ascertained that Jacob was okay then went for a rooftop picnic with Julia to cap off the night. Romantically. Julia said hearing me say that name made it more real for her. Perhaps I will reclaim it, but I will always be Insincere Marguerite.<br /> <br /> We held hands and slipped back down into the house. It was a good day.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXXVI</i><br /> <br /> Total minor mechanic note, Insincere Marguerite had to use Contracts of Separation to balance on her tongue. When she has weight she cannot support herself with the appendage without spending 1WP per turn. Also on the subject of our expat, she speaks imperfect English as MDH has been using the old language rules. Everyone got a 3 point and 2 point language, and while most had English primary, she had French primary English Secondary, similar to Jacob with Russian and English.<br /> <br /> On Vollyball, we used teamwork. Lorelei got extra dice for her wings, Insincere Marguerite got extra dice for tongue and activating her tunnelgrub flexibility. DLR made a roll to cost Gawain dice by flashing him, and Calamity used her Whisperwisp ability to distract DLR and cost HER dice too. Lorelei\u2019s player rolled for the lovers and Jacob\u2019s player for the fighters. Obviously the lovers had\u2026certain advantages.<br /> <br /> Calamity also took a WP to convert her failure helping Gawain make a sandcastle to a Dramatic Failure and made the whole thing collapse. It was funny.<br /> <br /> Well most of the rolling was at the beach, beyond Lorelei rolling for performances. The RP was awesome.<br /> <br /> If you read this and other game journals, note the comments above about guessing about common players. We are curious what you think. Though comments and questions of other sorts are welcome as well.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T01:19:28-07:00","id":633268,"title":"","content":"Beach episode! Looks like it was a fun session!<br /> The relationships between characters, PC and NPCs, continue to be fascinating, from the reactions to Jacob's dealing heroin, to the tension between Oleander and De la Rocha.<br /> I wonder how far Jacob intends to pursue his relationship with Luna. He obviously likes her a lot, but he's so guarded and secret, it's hard to imagine him opening up to her completely.<br /> It's also interesting to see the closeness between Calamity and Insincere Marguerite, as they seem not to spend that much time together.<br /> Does Calamity merely think of Becky as a friend with occasional benefits or something more? I wonder if Lorelei thinking of <u>her</u> darklings is significant?<br /> Also, the thing about Marguerite's name made me wonder: are any of the characters interested in meeting their fetches?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T12:49:39-07:00","id":633717,"title":"","content":"It was a fun session. The dynamic of the discussion was interesting...everyone was surprisingly okay with the Heroin thing...Insincere Marguerite even tried her best to keep the subject away from it. So that is good for him. Was wondering how that would shake out when it came up...I wonder if it being after Darke was deposed affects things. As for De La Rocha and Oleander...we will see how that develops. Neither wants to hate the other, but both are deeply in love with Lori and see each other as rivals. The butch/femme dynamic and attraction vectors play in, and the fact that despite her cynical exterior Oleander is something of a romantic.<br /> <br /> It will be interesting to see how Jacob/Luna goes. Both are terribly fond of each other, inexperienced, and not given to opening up. Jacob is more secretive with more skeletons in the closet than Luna is though; I suppose depending on how you feel about certain things her skeleton is a big one tho.<br /> <br /> Not spending too much time with Insincere Marguerite makes her more likable. ^_^ More seriously, that's true, but they very much see each other as kin, and look out for each other a great deal. They are also both more obviously struggling with their natures than the others, as well as both being Darklings and being 2/3 of the women in the Motley.<br /> <br /> I am positive Calamity's player will chime in but she sees Becky as more than a friend. Becky being a succubus it's hard to say how she feels. Offhand, my observation is Lorelei's possessive thoughts are not a huge issue. Her sort of moral Achilles's heel is a need for attention, where possessiveness is more Insincere Marguerite's bag.<br /> <br /> Calamity struggles with seeking out her fetch for a bloody reckoning over her middle school best friend. I think she is the only one who does, aside from Insincere Marguerite cyberstalking hers (possessive!).<br /> <br /> Thanks for the comments! =-)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T13:08:23-07:00","id":633730,"title":"","content":"Anteros, As far as Jacob and Luna go, he is interested in furthering that relationship. He has gained acceptance for his past by the Motley and his monarch and plans to tell Luna in the near future. He does not want to start their relationship on a lie or covering up something so important. Luna is important to him and he doesn't want to mess it up. We'll see how it goes. ;-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7378-nanae07","name":"Nanae07","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T13:20:44-07:00","id":633738,"title":"","content":"It was a fun session Anteros.<br /> <br /> Well, Calamity and Insincere Marguerite interact during the group scenes and they do often have a quiet exchange or two during the game. While Calamity is fond of everyone in her motley, she feels a certain kinship with IM and Jacob. She considers them the other 'unseelie' members of the group. (Yes, her past as a geeky girl does show through a little sometimes) Some of it also comes from the chatting that happens outside of the game between the players about the characters which fills in those more mundane times.<br /> <br /> As far as Becky... Well, that's a complicated can of emotions. Calamity likes her a lot but she is in love with Gawain. Calamity also has self esteem issues and feels unworthy of being loved. Plus there is the fact that she can't (won't) actually sleep with her since she might accidentally harm her as she has glass shards growing out of her. (Gawain is immune to accidental harm as a metalflesh) There is also the fact that Becky likes the rough to the point of violent sex that Calamity enjoys. Though that is also tainted by the knowledge that as a succubus Becky likes whatever the person she's with likes. *chuckles* It's actually something she's wrestling with in the current journal due to some follow up on the whole Dark Kimberly situation that happened in Sunday's session. I guess the best answer is that Calamity feels that she and Becky are friends but knows that her own feelings run deeper and she's really not sure what (if anything) to do about that.<br /> <br /> And so far as her fetch goes, Calamity swore that she would find and kill the Sinister Bitch for stealing her parents' love and tormenting her best friend/first crush through high school. Less a meeting and more an assassination planned there.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the question. I really do like discussion the game and Calamity. I like getting into her head to figure out how and why she does the things she does and I never mind sharing what's going on in there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T13:59:43-07:00","id":633769,"title":"","content":"Thanks for all your answers! it' really nice of you to take the time to satisfy my curiosity. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Speaking of which <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> : how different from their fetches do the PCs actually look like? And does every PC have a fake ID? I kind of wondered about Insincere Marguerite status.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T16:14:26-07:00","id":633922,"title":"","content":"Contrary to what Insincere Marguerite says, her fetch looks like her but maybe slightly overweight but well within normal range. Insincere Marguerite (who if human would be severely underweight, as a Tunnelgrub she is merely underweight) is just persnickety. Amberghylles actually hooked me up with a picture of Calamity's fetch, the only one who has a picture. She is also probably the only one who might show up, the rest are mostly a ways away and out of mind. If the group actually does visit Paris Insincere Marguerite's may come up, but I suspect not.<br /> <br /> The PCs did a bounty early-ish on on Briarwolves for the Summer Court, and their pay was false identification provided for all of them. I gave them essentially a dot's worth for free at the start (as I did not want having that merit to essentially be a character tax since they were working in the Burlesque House) and they all upped it as their reward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T06:54:33-07:00","id":635728,"title":"","content":"Hey, Anteros, thanks for reading and commenting!<br /> <br /> When I write dialog for Lorelei's Diary, I tend to hear it playing out in my head. When she wrote &quot;I'm glad none of <u>my</u> Darklings are...&quot;, I underlined the &quot;my&quot; because the little Lori in my head emphasized the word when she said it, not to indicate that she was feeling particularly possessive. Her years as a caged pet gave her a healthy aversion to the very idea of possessing another human (or Changeling). I'm not going to claim that she has no possessive feelings toward anyone - she's still inclined to a bit of jealousy where de la Rocha is concerned, for example - but I don't see her ever taking that to Insincere Marguerite levels.<br /> <br /> As for the Lorelei/de la Rocha/Oleander situation, well... we'll have to see how it shakes out. The fact that D and Oleander aren't getting along is really upsetting Lori, though personally I think it's a miracle that something like this hasn't come up before now. As indicated in the last journal, if forced to choose between them, her decision at the moment would be clear-cut. As things progress, however, who knows? Lori loves D... but no relationship is without its problems, as the next journal will begin to show.<br /> <br /> I have not defined what Lori's fetch looks like, though if anyone has an image that looks like Emily Bett Rickards as a 54-year-old woman, I'd be happy to consider it. I don't really see her coming up in the story much, but I'm not the Storyteller... :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T12:42:32-07:00","id":636192,"title":"","content":"De La Rocha and Oleander get along fairly well given the circumstances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 08-22-2015, 04:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T00:08:22-07:00","id":636773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenitentTom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play?p=635728#post635728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As for the Lorelei/de la Rocha/Oleander situation, well... we'll have to see how it shakes out. The fact that D and Oleander aren't getting along is really upsetting Lori, though personally I think it's a miracle that something like this hasn't come up before now. As indicated in the last journal, if forced to choose between them, her decision at the moment would be clear-cut. As things progress, however, who knows? Lori loves D... but no relationship is without its problems, as the next journal will begin to show.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play?p=636192#post636192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">De La Rocha and Oleander get along fairly well given the circumstances.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have the feeling none of the three ladies quite understood what they were signing up for when they began these relationships...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T01:37:01-07:00","id":636810,"title":"","content":"Oleander had a reasonable idea. DLR is not exactly the &quot;planning ahead&quot; type.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T01:54:58-07:00","id":647785,"title":"","content":"Hey folks, low key session this time. The PCs spent a lot of it split up on various tasks. There is a decent overall review though in most journals.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXXVII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> Jun 28th<br /> <br /> Man, today has been the day for coming up with hard decisions. I mean, it\u2019s gonna be hard enough finding something both in my idiom and symbolically appropriate to the capture of dreams, but I also have to come up with a movie that epitomizes the 90s. Such I hard life I lead, you know?<br /> <br /> The second bit there came up at breakfast today. Insincere Marguerite decided that for our next move in the war of the decades, we should all pick a movie that will serve as a champion for our identified decade. Lori is the 70s, Calamity the 80s, and Jacob represents for the 00s. Me and Insincere Marguerite are sharing the 90s. It\u2019s a serious responsibility, you know? I haven\u2019t gotten any good ideas yet, but I\u2019m sure one will come to me.<br /> <br /> We all were pretty busy the rest of the day. Insincere Marguerite and Julia were off to Anaheim to visit Julia\u2019s parents. Lori and De la Roche went off to Muscle Beach to work out, then Lori sat with Princess Jolie while Andromeda used the Table on her. Calamity and Jacob visited Boss Lojack to explain about Jacob\u2019s past, before it came up in a more damning light. Calamity was worried about me rattling around the House, you know, with only Ace for company, but Juan Carlos had told me I could look him up for some lessons on making dream prisons and dream combat, so I assured her I\u2019d be fine.<br /> <br /> Folks\u2019 things went well, from all accounts. Julia was afraid her parents like Insincere Marguerite better than her, mostly cause they told embarrassing stories about when she was a kid and drew boobs or lip synced heavy metal songs. But that\u2019s what parents do, you know? I guess... Jacob and Calamity were fairly tight lipped, but no one was hurt and Boss Lojack was still cool with him being in his Entitlement, so I guess it went well? The Table worked (Lori thinks) but Andromeda was really drained. Still, we all knew that was a possibility, so Joan came and picked her up and is, you know, taking care of her.<br /> <br /> Juan Carlos and me were at it for a few hours, over at his townhouse. It was my first time and all, so it took me a bit to get the hang of it. See, he makes clay pots, to trap the dreams in, painted in a Grecian style to represent the kind of dream within. That\u2019s just his way though, they can be all kinds of things, so I oughta, you know, come up with my own thing. I mean, throwing pots was fun and all, but I was thinking something in metal. It will probably involve my jeweler\u2019s tools more than my heavy duty stuff. Especially for a \u2018stealth\u2019 version, for when I need to sneak something like that in somewhere. I did make one in a pot version, so he could give me pointers on the dreamy part of it. I think it turned out pretty good, myself. We\u2019ll see if it\u2019s strong enough to catch one of my dreams.<br /> <br /> Calamity was schooling noobs on Gears of War when I got back, so I joined her for a few maps until, you know, it was time for the show. We even got an audience for a bit. The turn around on Lori\u2019s part from \u2018why are you being so mean to these kids?\u2019 to \u2018shoot them again Calamity!\u2019 was almost worth listening to the little twerps talking to Calamity that way. Almost.<br /> <br /> The show was awesome. Calamity came out of getting ready looking like a priest who raided a velvet factory (Becky was coming by) and so Insincere Marguerite mentioned she\u2019d put in It\u2019s a Sin to the line up. And Calamity decided to dance to it! It was super great. She managed to even put a distinct air of spooky into the incredibly sexy dance Insincere Marguerite has choreographed and it was just, you know, awesome. Lori did some good songs too.<br /> <br /> Calamity made a beeline for Becky and I\u2019d gotten the impression she wanted to, you know, blow off some steam, so I hung out with De la Roche and the girls. Something killed the conversation at some point, I don\u2019t remember what, so I asked folks for ideas about dream containers. That didn\u2019t do much to help cause it made Lori think of birdcages, but then Insincere Marguerite theatrically complained again about De la Roche calling her gringo, even though she called all of us gringos really, and it\u2019s true anyway. That did cheer things up better, and soon we were talking about girl piles with Insincere Marguerite cherries. You know, the usual things. We were talking about them being in the Hedge House, which is not so usual, but I guess Lori just wants to get more comfy with being on that side of things.<br /> <br /> We also decided what to have for breakfast tomorrow, and by \u2018we decided\u2019, I mean that Insincere Marguerite indicated she wanted crepes and looked at me with big eyes until I said OK. That got De la Roche talking about her family some, which she hasn\u2019t really done much apparently. She wasn\u2019t real close, you know, cause they have kinda strict ideas about gender roles and stuff, and she doesn\u2019t really fit into their ideas of right. It seemed like maybe she missed some of the foods her mom makes and I can maybe help with that, you know? I mean, I\u2019m sure mine won't be as good as her mom\u2019s, cause that\u2019s the way these things work, but I could at least make that kinda food.<br /> <br /> Thinking back over all this and getting it down, we did talk a lot about families and parents and things today (De la Roche is gonna get dragged to church one of these Sundays). Poor Calamity was getting a little depressed and drink-y about it. Hopefully Becky\u2019s treating her good. Tomorrow\u2019s bound to cheer her up some too, since she\u2019s taking Lori and Jacob to the shooting range for practice. It didn\u2019t throw her off her game with the dancing either, so I\u2019m sure she\u2019s alright.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Something has changed within me. Something is not the same.<br /> <br /> Okay, I admit it: I downloaded the soundtrack to <u><u>Wicked</u></u> after Oleander recommended it to me the other day, and I might have listened to it a time or twelve since then. But that doesn\u2019t make the opening strains of \u201cDefying Gravity\u201d any less appropriate.<br /> <br /> Maybe I\u2019m getting stronger. Maybe now that some of my other responsibilities have been fulfilled, things look clearer to me. Maybe I just finally realized that I\u2019ve messed around for long enough, and it\u2019s time to get serious. Whatever the reason is, I know that I can\u2019t put off rescuing Missy and Jane any longer.<br /> <br /> D and I got up yesterday morning and prepared to head down to Muscle Beach for a workout, as agreed. I put on a snug sports bra and a pair of bike pants, figuring I could soak up a little glamour while we exercised. My outfit got a few appreciative ogles at breakfast, and Calamity made some salacious comments about our plans for the workout.<br /> <br /> D grinned at her in a mock-exasperated way. \u201cLori may be a nympho, but we <u>are</u> capable of focusing on other things,\u201d she explained as we walked away.<br /> <br /> Is that how my friends see me? Okay, I know I like sex\u2026 I might even technically <u><u>be</u></u> a nymphomaniac; I\u2019m not sure how you diagnose or classify something like that. But is that really my defining feature? Is that as deep as my character goes? I know D didn\u2019t mean to hurt my feelings with that statement\u2026 ordinarily I wear my libido as a badge of honor, but at that time it felt like a slight even if it wasn\u2019t intended as one.<br /> <br /> So maybe I was a little more focused during our workout than usual. I got advice from D and Monica (and Juan-Carlos, who was also there) about how to target specific muscle groups to start building up strength and stamina. And while I know I still have a long way to go, I think I got in a good workout before it was time to shower and head out.<br /> <br /> I accomplished something else while we were there, too. I asked Monica about her duties for the Bishopric of Blackbirds. She seemed almost eager to talk about it, and when I asked hesitantly if they had any sort of \u201cride-along\u201d program, she quickly informed me that there was nothing formal in place, but that she\u2019d be glad to have me along if I wanted to go with her someday.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhen are you heading in next?\u201d I asked nonchalantly.<br /> <br /> \u201cI thought I\u2019d do a small patrol on Monday,\u201d she returned.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat would be perfect,\u201d I said eagerly, \u201cI don\u2019t perform on Monday nights, so I wouldn\u2019t have to be back early or anything.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt probably won\u2019t be very exciting,\u201d she warned me, \u201cthings in the local Hedge have been pretty quiet since we beat back the Mothership.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded, and refrained from mentioning that I <u><u>like</u></u> it when the Hedge is quiet. \u201cBut you\u2019ll be able to teach me a few things about navigating in there, right? Like how to find trods and spot dangers and such?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSure!\u201d she said with a grin. \u201cI\u2019d be glad to.\u201d<br /> <br /> D shot me a couple of inquisitive looks during this conversation, but she refrained from asking about it. I think deep down she knows what I have in mind, and isn\u2019t really surprised that I\u2019m finally working myself up to it. I dropped her off at her apartment with a promise that I\u2019d see her at the show that night, went back to the Dream House to change, and then headed across Santa Monica to\u2026 brrrr\u2026 the Children\u2019s Library.<br /> <br /> Okay, so writing it out like that doesn\u2019t really cover just how creepy that place really was. In my own defense, I\u2019ll just note that Madame Spidertoes calls it home, and it suits her. Andromeda, Princess Jolie, Becky Wan and I were ushered into a secret room at the back of the library, down a set of stairs, and into a chamber containing the infamous Table. I thanked Andromeda and Madame Spidertoes for allowing us to do what had to be done, and the little alien girl went to work.<br /> <br /> It took a few tense hours of work. Andromeda strapped Jolie down and began manipulating the Table, and eventually reaching <u>into</u> Jolie\u2019s body to make the alterations. Jolie didn\u2019t seem to mind it most of the time\u2026 her moans and screams didn\u2019t really sound like <u>pain</u> if you know what I mean. But Becky was as tense as a guitar string through the whole process. And sometimes Jolie\u2019s familiar beautiful visage seemed to fade, and a pale grey alien face took its place, and Becky <u>really</u> didn\u2019t like that.<br /> <br /> I did my best to calm her down. I took her hand in my own. \u201cAndromeda knows what she\u2019s doing,\u201d I assured her. \u201cThis is a <u><u>good</u></u> thing, Becky. Jolie wants it, and she\u2019ll be better off afterward.\u201d Becky nodded and squeezed my hand, but she kept her lips pursed tightly the whole time.<br /> <br /> When it was over, both Jolie and Andromeda looked exhausted. Jolie yawned and stretched and said that she wanted to go home and get some sleep. Andromeda nodded that this was a good idea, and stated that she thought the operation had been a success. Jolie gave me a hug and thanked me for my part in helping to cure her condition, and then allowed Becky to quickly usher her out of the creepy secret basement room.<br /> <br /> I turned to Madame Spidertoes and solemnly thanked her for her hospitality (she gave me a regal nod in response) before turning my attention back to Andromeda. \u201cYou okay, sweetie?\u201d I asked, concerned.<br /> <br /> \u201cI am fine,\u201d she replied in a dead monotone.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sorry you had to do that, Andromeda,\u201d I said desperately, \u201cI wouldn\u2019t have asked if it hadn\u2019t been so important\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt is fine,\u201d she replied in the same empty voice. \u201cI will require rest now.\u201d<br /> <br /> I called up Joan, truly concerned. Joan swung by the library a few minutes later and picked Andromeda up. I tried to apologize for putting her girlfriend in such a situation, and Joan waved it off. \u201cYou and your motley have been true friends to us; she was happy to help you in return. And don\u2019t worry, she was like this after she helped me as well. I am confident she will recover.\u201d<br /> <br /> I remembered how thin and stretched Mr. Grey had seemed before his untimely demise. \u201cJoan,\u201d I said softly, \u201cdon\u2019t let her use it again. Not for anything, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> Joan nodded, and for a second I saw how worried she really was, but then it was gone. She ushered Andromeda gently into the passenger seat of her car \u2013 I\u2019d never seen her be that careful with anything before \u2013 and said her goodbyes. I watched them drive off before heading for my own car. I really hope they\u2019ll be all right.<br /> <br /> I got back to the Dream House an hour or two before the doors opened to the public to find Gawain and Calamity playing some video game online. It was pretty violent, and Calamity seemed to get off on spouting profanity at the people they were playing against. I was frankly shocked at some of the language I heard from her, but the guys on the other end seemed to give (almost) as good as they got, so I assumed it was all in good fun.<br /> <br /> Marguerite and Julia had gone up to Anaheim for the day to meet Julia\u2019s parents, and they returned about half an hour after I got back. Apparently things went well. Marguerite certainly looked pleased with herself, and told us that Julia\u2019s parents had shared all sorts of embarrassing stories about her as a child. Julia was mortified, but I think in an odd way she was pleased with the day\u2019s events as well.<br /> <br /> We had a little time to talk before the show, and one of the things that came up was Marguerite\u2019s idea that each of us should pick a movie to represent our signature decade, and then the whole motley should watch these films. Calamity will represent the 80s, Marguerite and Gawain will choose for the 90s, and Jacob will pick for the 2000s. Naturally, yours truly will be choosing a film to represent the 70s. It\u2019s not as easy as it sounds. Most of the best films of that decade seem to be set in <u><u>other</u></u> decades, so they\u2019re not really representative. \u201cThe Godfather,\u201d \u201cM*A*S*H*,\u201d \u201cGrease,\u201d \u201cCabaret,\u201d \u201cAmerican Graffiti\u2026\u201d There\u2019s also \u201cStar Wars,\u201d of course, but that doesn\u2019t really say much about the world of the 1970s.<br /> <br /> I think I\u2019ve narrowed it down to four films. The obvious choice for a film to demonstrate culture in the late 1970s is \u201cSaturday Night Fever,\u201d but that seems a little on the nose. There was more to the 70s than Disco culture, after all. \u201cThe French Connection\u201d reinvented the crime drama, bringing a gritty, real-world feel to a genre which had previously been filled with idealized black-and-white cops n\u2019 robbers stories and sneering noir anti-heroes. \u201cAnnie Hall\u201d was a revelation in its day, and I\u2019m told it sort of set the stage for the future of the romantic comedy genre. And according to the internet, \u201cJaws\u201d is almost single-handedly responsible for the development of the summer blockbuster.<br /> <br /> In any case, as showtime approached I had to bid adieu to this lively discussion and go off to ruin a cheap dress. I\u2019d found a cheap frumpy white dress at a local Goodwill and purchased it for about $2 a couple of days previous, and I spent about ten minutes carefully cutting a dashed line down its back. With considerable effort I managed to squeeze into it without ripping the fabric further\u2026 which was made more difficult by the fact that I had tucked my wings in tight against my back and pulled the dress on over them.<br /> <br /> My first number came up early in the show, which was good, because while I was wearing that dress I had to be extremely careful whenever I moved. As the opening strains of Halestorm\u2019s \u201cMs. Hyde\u201d played over the club\u2019s speakers, I strutted out onto the stage in my virginal white dress and a pair of prop glasses (thick black frames with no lenses), with my hair pulled back into a tight bun. Then when the first chorus started up, I spread my wings energetically, tearing the dress away and revealing the lacy black lingerie underneath to the audience. The glasses came off next, and then I shook my hair out of the bun.<br /> <br /> Okay, so it was a little more stripper-y than I usually go, but the crowd seemed to enjoy it, and I didn\u2019t let the disrobing go any further than that.<br /> <br /> I only had one other solo tonight, and I toned it down a bit with a sultry version of the Classics IV song \u201cSpooky.\u201d I suppose I could have flipped the genders like Dusty Springfield did in her cover version, but at the last minute I decided to leave \u2018em as they were originally written. I like girls. I\u2019m sure this brave new world can deal with it.<br /> <br /> Oh, I should mention that Calamity also made her stage debut last night, and she was fucking <u><u>amazing</u>!</u> She strutted and danced around the stage to one of the songs Marguerite choreographed (\u201cIt\u2019s a Sin\u201d by the Pet Shop Boys) in a black velvet number that had pulses racing all over the club. I don\u2019t much like Annika, but I have to admit that she must be a good teacher; Calamity looked great up there. While she was on the stage, she <u><u>owned</u></u> that audience, and I couldn\u2019t be happier for her. Becky \u2013 who had stopped by to see the show after escorting Princess Jolie safely home \u2013 looked pleased at the performance too.<br /> <br /> In the wake of Calamity\u2019s command performance, Insincere Marguerite suggested that she might want to try her hand at singing for an audience in the not-too-distant future. She mentioned a French song called \u201cNon, Je Ne Regrette Rien.\u201d I told her that it sounded like a wonderful idea to me, though I\u2019ll want to hear her sing it before I give my final okay to her proposal. Privately I\u2019m sure she\u2019ll be fine, and Calamity was similarly enthusiastic in her support. It\u2019s nice to see so many of my darkling friends coming out of their shells.<br /> <br /> Calamity and Becky made themselves scarce pretty much as soon as the show was over, and as usual I found myself seated at a table with Jacob, Gawain, and my darkling lovers. Talk ranged all over the place. Gawain was looking for inspiration and advice on constructing a \u201cdream container,\u201d something he can use to trap nightmares and other dreams. He said that Juan-Carlos uses pottery vessels, but that he wanted to do something a little more personal (which we all understood meant something metal). I sort of half-heartedly suggested a miniature cage, but that got me thinking about birdcages, which sort of killed my enthusiasm for the conversation.<br /> <br /> Jesus, I must be the only person in the world who routinely gets depressed thinking about birdcages. But with all due respect to the recently departed Maya Angelou, I also know why the caged bird sings\u2026 because her owner will fucking murder her if she gets bored enough.<br /> <br /> Talk turned to Julia\u2019s parents again. They\u2019re apparently hippies (they still have hippies these days!). This led to D mentioning something about never taking me to meet her family, as she didn\u2019t feel like suffering the same embarrassment Julia had just gone through.<br /> <br /> I took her hand gently. \u201cThat might be the first time I\u2019ve ever heard you mention your family, D,\u201d I said softly.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, there\u2019s a reason for that,\u201d she said, not meeting my gaze. \u201cThey\u2019re very traditional. They have very definite opinions about gender roles and how proper young women should behave. I don\u2019t see them much.\u201d<br /> <br /> That might have been the saddest thing I\u2019ve ever heard her say. She made it back from Arcadia, had no Fetch, and was able to reconnect with her family\u2026 only to become estranged from them for perfectly mundane, <u>human</u> reasons. I squeezed her hand. \u201cWell,\u201d I said, \u201cyou can probably look forward to hearing my dad embarrass me horribly someday, even if he doesn\u2019t realize he\u2019s doing it. I think it\u2019s like a universal law that parents have to do that. That is if you ever get around to joining me for a church service\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> She tensed again, and I sighed. \u201cWhen you\u2019re ready, sweetie.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI will,\u201d she promised again. \u201cI just have to work up to it.\u201d<br /> <br /> After that, I asked Jacob if he wanted to go out camping or hiking some time. I figured I ought to at least try to pick up the basics of wilderness survival if I\u2019m going to venture back into the Hedge, and he knows more about that stuff than anyone else I\u2019ve ever met. I may never be Aragorn, but I\u2019m hoping he can at least teach me to recognize the difference between a pothole and a footprint, or show me how to set up a shelter that won\u2019t collapse on me while I sleep. He seemed willing to try, though he gave me a look that indicated he was questioning my motives.<br /> <br /> I also asked the girls if they would mind sleeping in the Hollow last night. <u><u>That</u></u> got a lot of raised eyebrows, let me tell you. I haven\u2019t exactly made a secret of the fact that I don\u2019t like going into the Hedge\u2026 even into the relatively safe area around the Hollow. This, of course, is pretty much why I wanted to try to spend more time there, to acclimate myself and get used to the way things work there.<br /> <br /> So we did sleep there. It was nice to spend the night with Marguerite and Julia again. Julia in particular has been very supportive lately, and sometimes I feel like she doesn\u2019t get enough of my attention. I tried to reassure her last night that she is never far from my thoughts, and I think I succeeded. <br /> <br /> Once again I got up much earlier than any of the others, headed back to the Dream House (alone!) and got ready for church. The others were awake and munching on crepes when I got back, and I had time to scarf down a few before I had to change and head out again. I\u2019d asked Calamity to take me down to the firing range for another lesson in marksmanship, and Jacob decided to come with us as well.<br /> <br /> I asked D if she wanted to come along, and she got kind of sheepish. \u201cGun ranges around here tend to be sort of\u2026 unofficially segregated,\u201d she explained. \u201cI doubt your NRA buddies would appreciate a Latina chica hanging out in their little clubhouse.\u201d<br /> <br /> I was disappointed, but prepared to leave it at that. I should have known that my honey wouldn\u2019t let something like that lie for long, though. After a few minutes of talking the situation out with herself, she decided that she wasn\u2019t going to take that sort of attitude lying down, and insisted that she come with us just to spite these theoretical racists.<br /> <br /> Ordinarily I find my love\u2019s in-your-face attitude endearing, but I think she took it too far today. She was taunting the guys in the lanes next to me as I was shooting, trying to throw off their aim and rile them up. I know she\u2019s Summer Court, but honestly, those boys were just minding their own business and not bothering anyone else in the least. I think I even caught her hexing one of them to spoil some of his shots. When the two of us retrieved our targets, she started ridiculing him about how he couldn\u2019t even outshoot a girl.<br /> <br /> I was seething all the way home, and I sort of retreated into my room and started writing this diary entry as soon as we got back. I think D is hanging out with Marguerite and Julia\u2026 she must have taken the hint that I wanted to be alone.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t get it, I really don\u2019t. She was so determined to see a problem where there wasn\u2019t one that she ended up <u><u>being</u></u> the problem in the end. I know her Court gains glamour from anger, but I was trying to improve my skills, and she was causing a distraction I couldn\u2019t ignore. And dammit, it\u2019s <u><u>important</u></u> for me to learn to defend myself if I\u2019m going to mount this rescue mission.<br /> <br /> So I\u2019ve been stewing alone in here for about an hour, wondering what I should do next. A part of me wants to just let D chew on things for a while, and maybe spend the night with Oleander, but I know I can\u2019t do that. Both D and Oleander have been very accommodating in letting me have my cake and eat it too, and the minute I start using them as weapons against each other is the minute this whole open relationship stops being okay.<br /> <br /> I love D. Being mad at her doesn\u2019t change that. <u><u>Nothing</u></u> will change that. I just need to make her understand that my priorities have shifted, and that I have to stop fooling around and focus on getting ready for the trials to come.<br /> <br /> Survival. Jacob can teach me that, which will help me cope with the dangers of the Hedge itself. Monica and Oleander can help me acclimate to the unique challenges the magical borderlands present. Insincere Marguerite can probably help me with the basics of stealth, which will have to be my go-to option for encounters in the Hedge. If I <u><u>have</u></u> to fight, I\u2019ll fall back on my Contracts of Vainglory to scare the enemies off, and in an absolute last resort I\u2019ll have my pistol. I\u2019ll continue working out with Monica and D to build up my strength and stamina in case I have to run for it.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll also need to work on improving my healing abilities. The Contracts of Eternal Spring offer miraculous curative abilities, but my mastery of them is still limited by my lack of knowledge of the human body and how it actually <u><u>works</u></u>. I need to learn medicine, and I need to learn it <u><u>quickly</u></u>. There\u2019s only so much that online classes and CPR lessons at the Y can do for me, but I don\u2019t have time to go back to school for real. And let\u2019s face it, I\u2019ve never been the smartest girl on the block. Maybe if I\u2019d spent more time in High School studying and less time partying and trying to get laid\u2026<br /> <br /> No, this isn\u2019t about me. It\u2019s about the girls I left behind in the Empress\u2019 Realm. For them, I\u2019ll find a way.<br /> <br /> No, I haven\u2019t told the rest of the motley what I\u2019m planning, but I haven\u2019t been exactly subtle about it either. Hell, I even asked Calamity this morning if she could get me access to the Autumn Court\u2019s library so I could see if they have any intelligence on the Empress. The motley knows about Missy and Jane. I told them that I\u2019ll have to go back one of these days, and they even offered to help me rescue them at the time.<br /> <br /> I can\u2019t ask them to do that. This is my responsibility, and I\u2019m not going to risk my friends\u2019 lives or freedom to correct my mistakes. Now don\u2019t get me wrong; I\u2019m not going to sneak off alone in the middle of the night and try to do this myself. If the others insist on helping me, I won\u2019t be so ungrateful as to demand they stay behind. But I won\u2019t <u><u>ask</u></u>. Accepting help that\u2019s offered is one thing. Roping someone into a mission like this unwilling is another thing entirely.<br /> <br /> D will want to come with me, and my God in heaven that terrifies me. I can\u2019t ask her to stay behind, but I <u><u>will</u> <u>not</u></u> let the Empress have her. I\u2019d rather see us both dead than risk that.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> We started off the day with light conversation about who should represent which decade and what movies best represent that decade. I was appointed the 2000\u2019s. Lorelei is the 1970\u2019s, Calamity the 1980\u2019s, and Insincere Marguerite and Gawain are the 1990\u2019s. Depending on what criteria folks are looking for, I was thinking of the \u201cDark Knight\u201d as a movie that kind of represents the 2000\u2019s. It\u2019s a fun action movie, but has darker elements to it than previous decades generally went for. It\u2019s also a remake of the Batman series, which seems to be a thing for the 2000\u2019s. Remakes have been popular lately. Now, if we\u2019re going for a movie that changed how films were made in the 2000\u2019s I\u2019d have to say \u201cLord of the Rings.\u201d It kind of kick started the whole filming multiple movies at the same time, or at least signing the same actors for multiple films at a time thing. It was a huge undertaking and something of a risk, but it worked out and other producers have followed suit. It\u2019s hard to pick just one movie to represent the decade.<br /> <br /> The others were bouncing movie ideas off one another. Some of them I\u2019d heard of. Most of them I haven\u2019t seen. Saturday Night Fever was mentioned for Lori. Breakfast Club came up for Calamity. Not sure what Insincere Marguerite and Gawain are going to come up with. Should be interesting to see. If we end up watching these movies I will get to see a bunch that I\u2019ve never seen before I\u2019m sure. Of course a lot of the movies we end up watching for Movie Nights are films that I\u2019ve not seen before, so it\u2019ll be par for the course.<br /> <br /> After all that, Lori asked Calamity if the razorhand would go with her to the shooting range tomorrow to practice with her pistol. Calamity agreed readily enough. I asked if they would mind me joining them and they said that would be fine. I get to practice on a pretty regular basis with my knives, but not so much with my gun, so figured that it might be a good skill to work on. I guess Lorelei feels the same. She has only been to the range a couple of times, and if you\u2019re going to own a gun, making sure that you are familiar with it is a good thing. Of course there might be more to her interest. It seems like almost overnight Lorelei has an expressed an interest in joining De la Rocha in working out at Muscle Beach, going into the Hedge with Monica, and learning to track from me. It hasn\u2019t literally been overnight, but it does seem to be kind of sudden. I can understand wanting to better yourself. To be stronger and more knowledgeable is a good thing, but I\u2019m still not sure of her reasons as of yet. I have an idea, but I\u2019m not sure if I\u2019m right or not. I will have to ask our pretty songstress what brought on the self-improvement kick. <br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite and Julia had plans to go visit Julia\u2019s parents in Anaheim. Apparently things went well. Julia\u2019s parents broke out the embarrassing childhood pictures and stories and regaled Insincere Marguerite with tales and photos. They seemed to like Marguerite and were not surprised in the least that their daughter brought home a girlfriend. It seems that Julia liked to draw girls with breasts from an early age. Almost makes me wish that I could take Luna home to meet my parents, but I know that is impossible. Even if I didn\u2019t have a fetch wearing my childhood face, I am a good deal older than their \u201cson,\u201d and it would look strange for me to show up at their door anyway. As much as I\u2019d like to take my old life back, I can\u2019t. I\u2019m not even sure how I\u2019d do that even if I didn\u2019t have a fetch and looked eighteen. I\u2019ve changed so much during my time in Arcadia, that I\u2019m not sure how I\u2019d just pick up my old life and start again. I\u2019m not the na\u00efve bookworm I was before. I have scars that run deeper than my skin, and I just don\u2019t see things the same way anymore. I don\u2019t know if it is even possible for me to get to what I was before. And even if it was, would I want to?<br /> <br /> Sooner than I guess I would have liked it was time for me and Calamity to go talk to Lowjack. Or should it now be Boss Lowjack? So, I waited until Calamity was off the phone with Becky. It think she was checking to make sure that the other woman was okay after their conversation the other night. Then we took my jeep over to Boss Lowjack\u2019s bar and were escorted back to his office. I was reminded again by the pictures on his wall just how old he is. There is a picture of him shaking Robert Kennedy\u2019s hand behind his desk. It made me think that he\u2019s got to be pretty canny to have come so far, and be where he is. He didn\u2019t want to be the Winter King, but of everyone in the court, he was the natural choice for the job. He has power, visible or not. He is not someone to be toyed with. All that was going through my head before I was about to tell him about my less than stellar past. Not the most comforting of thoughts.<br /> <br /> So, I opened by saying that we\u2019ve all done things that we\u2019re not proud of and that is true for me as well. I went on to explain about working for the Lady, returning those that had run, and taking those the Lady had chosen. I explained that I had my eyes opened and decided to turn from Her and leave for \u2018the world.\u2019 Calamity backed me up and told Lowjack that I been acting in the best interests of the Freehold since I joined the motley and that she trusted me with her life and the lives of the others. Lowjack for his part seemed to believe me. He did have a couple of requests for me though. He wanted me to write up anything I could remember about the Lady\u2019s realm, her strengths and weaknesses, those that work for her, anything. He also wanted a separate write up of anything that I\u2019ve done that might come back and bite me in the ass. Well, he said back, but in my experience the bad things aim lower.<br /> <br /> Boss Lowjack specifically wanted everything written as technical and distant as possible, so there would be no way for it to be traced back to me. The first write up he will likely share with the other Monarchs or those in the Autumn court library that record the Freehold\u2019s information on Keepers and their realms. The second write up he said would stay with him alone and would be encrypted six ways from Sunday. I asked if writing it in Cyrillic would help, but he doesn\u2019t read Russian. That led to a small tangent about getting me to teach Lowjack Russian. I agreed to the write ups and to the language lessons.<br /> <br /> I also agreed to take an oath with Lowjack that everything I tell him about my past will be the truth and to let him know if there is something that may be left out and why. I get the impression that he wasn\u2019t going to take advantage of me in that regard. If there is something that I\u2019m not ready to talk about I\u2019m sure he\u2019ll let me stay silent, as long as I don\u2019t lie about it. Or if there is something that I don\u2019t fully explain I can tell him why I don\u2019t detail it further. As a counter to me being honest with him, Lowjack said that he will not tell anyone else about my past or where any of the information came from. He will back me up if anyone comes to him with concerns about me or my past activities. I will admit that was a comforting thought. It\u2019s good to have someone in a position of power that will have my back should I need it.<br /> <br /> I will admit that I felt a little awkward telling Boss Lowjack all of this but admitting that I never told Darke. Though to be fair, Lowjack did agree with me that if I had told Darke about my past the man would have blackmailed me with it. I can see him doing that clear as day. And since Twitch and Darke questioned Rook under duress it\u2019s possible that they have figured some of it out and are holding onto it for a \u201crainy day.\u201d All of this just puts me in a precarious position with the former Winter King. He may hold a grudge against me for being a part of the motley that got him dethroned, but on the flipside I still sell his drugs and make him some decent money. I\u2019m not sure what to do about that. Maybe I should stop selling the heroin and break ties with the man altogether? It might be safer to stay where I am for the moment. I\u2019m still doing a service for him and am therefore useful. Once I stop being useful things might go badly for me.<br /> <br /> Another thing that I thought was interesting, though I suppose it should have been expected, was Lowjack offering to help me disappear if I so desired. Either short or long term. I guess this was in response to me telling him about Rook and him escaping from Darke, then throwing a knife at me. I did explain that I wasn\u2019t sure what Rook\u2019s intentions were. He normally does not miss a target, but he could have been less accurate due to what had been done to him, or he only want to give me a warning. Twitch did say that they had \u201cprogramed\u201d Rook to not want to hurt me, so that may be why he missed, rather than a genuine desire not to. Not completely sure on that point, and won\u2019t be until I get a chance to talk to him about it. I also told Lowjack that I would like to try and give Rook the chance to change and leave the Lady of his own free will. I don\u2019t know how successful that will be, but I have to give him the chance. I will do what I can to try and help save my former brother in arms.<br /> <br /> Overall I thought Lowjack was very understanding about the whole thing. His requests of me were very straightforward and logical. I will admit that I was kind of glad to be able to tell someone in the freehold tactical information about the Lady and her servants. It wasn\u2019t often that I, or anyone else in her employ, came this far south to look for people that the Lady might like for her collection, but information on her practices would be still good for the Freehold to have. The Lady tended to have us hunt in colder climes. I did stray further south on occasion, for variety if nothing else. I guess that\u2019s why I came so far to get Brandon. I mean, I wasn\u2019t after him specifically, but he was hiking in the mountains near here and he just seemed like a good choice at the time. A target of opportunity if you will.<br /> <br /> So later I did a write up on the Lady\u2019s tactics, how she works and who works for her. I also detailed in a separate document the things that might come back and cause problems, including Brandon and Claire Falls. I also mentioned my fetch, though that is not likely to come up if the little shit continues to stay at home. I mentioned my sister as well. Not as something that might cause problems, but as something that might be used against me if the connection between us was found out. <br /> <br /> After the talk with Lowjack I dropped Calamity back off at the Dream House and came back for the second part of my meeting. When I got back to Lowjack\u2019s bar I met up with John again and we got into his car to go check out the safehouse for the Knights of the Utmost Silence. I will say that the safehouse appears to be just that, safe. It is well hidden and well stocked. The rest I will not put in writing. If anyone ever reads my journal it is true that I will have damned myself, but I will not damn others too.<br /> <br /> Once I got home from checking out the safehouse I asked Calamity if she minded if I used the office computer. She was upstairs playing Halo with Gawain and Lori watching. Lori seemed to be scandalized at first by what Calamity was saying into the microphone. Then Gawain unplugged the headphones so we could all hear the guys on the other end and Lori started shouting right back at them. It was kind of funny.<br /> <br /> When everyone was together Lorelei updated us all on Jolie\u2019s status. I\u2019ll admit that I had forgotten that Andromeda would be working on \u201cfixing\u201d Jolie today. I had so much other stuff on my mind. Apparently everything went well though. The compulsion that was there before has been removed. Andromeda was a little worse for the wear though. She was, according to Lori, acting rather a lot like Grey had been. I guess this was to be expected after using the Table. She should go back to normal after a little while and lots of rest. <br /> <br /> After all of that we still had a show to put on. Overall it went rather well. Lori pulled off a cool act to \u201cMs. Hyde\u201d by Halestorm. And to make things more interesting, I suppose, Calamity also did a number. It was her first time on stage and I thought she did really well. She got all dressed up and kind of last minute did a song. I think she was showing off for Becky. I know that she dressed up to impress the other woman, so it stands to reason that she put on that act to impress her as well. After the show was over she went to Becky\u2019s table to talk, and it looked like a good bit of flirting was going on as well. I know that Calamity is sweet on Becky and really didn\u2019t like antagonizing the other woman over the whole Dark Kimberly/White Maria deal. For what it\u2019s worth though, I think they got some of their differences worked out.<br /> <br /> While Calamity was flirting with Becky the rest of us gathered at a table and just sat down to talk. This was obviously after the show was over and the customers had left. This was when Lori brought up the idea of sleeping in the Hollow tonight. She wanted to know if anyone was up to joining her. I think De la Rocha, Insincere Marguerite and Julia all agreed to spend the night with her. Lori admitted that she wanted to do this in order to try and get over her phobia of the Hedge. She wants to get more comfortable there, and while she did not list a reason I have an idea. She had mentioned in the past that she wanted to go back to her Keeper\u2019s realm and retrieve her friends. She had made a promise with them that all of them would escape or none of them would, and then she goes and wins that contest. So, now she feels guilty and wants to make things right. I can understand that. I already told her that I would help her retrieve her friends from Arcadia. I will admit that I am not really looking forward to going back there, but I will if I have to. That place just gets in your head and makes you forget who you are. It remakes you according to the Keeper\u2019s wishes, and I don\u2019t want to be that person again. I don\u2019t want to become Rime. Nor do I want the others to ever meet him. He was not a good person.<br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> After another wonderful breakfast courtesy of Gawain, we started talking about who would be going to the range today. Luna said that she would like to come along, but lamented the fact that she had left her rifle at her place. Calamity, Lori and I were obviously going, and Lorelei invited De la Rocha to come along. De la Rocha went on for a while about places like that being discriminatory towards Latinos, even though Calamity tried to reassure her that this place was not like that. De la Rocha seemed intent on proving that she was not intimidated and said that she would definitely go and woe be to anyone that tried to give her any trouble. I\u2019m fairly certain that she was preparing for a fight to happen. I suppose if she had pressed the right buttons she could have easily started something, but instead she spent her time cursing the nearby guys who looked like they were doing any better than her sweetheart. Overall Calamity did really well, I was not too bad and Lorelei did well herself. And true to the Latina\u2019s word the guys nearby did not do as well as they might have if left to their own devices. Isn\u2019t love sweet. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> Today has gone well. Not the zany fun of yesterday but fun.<br /> <br /> Breakfast was short, but I tossed out Julia\u2019s idea to all pick decades and show the most epitomizing American film for it and decide which was superior. Lori got 70s, Calamity 80s, Gawain and I 90s, and Jacob 00s. I am not sure what movie I should pick\u2026I am considering <i><i>The Craft</i>, </i> which is terribly 90s, and <i><i>Trainspotting</i>, </i> which may be too British. I think <i><i>The Matrix</i></i> may be a bit late.<br /> <br /> The Motley went to take care of various errands, so I went to Anaheim with Julia. We met her parents. They are nice people but very\u2026they are hippies. I mean, they really look like stereotypical hippies. Her mom\u2019s hair was a rainbow, which was pretty. Julia\u2019s comparatively conservative dress and skirt sort of stood out.<br /> <br /> We got along well. They decided to embarrass Julia as much as possible, from discussing her tendency to draw breasts on her sketches of women in an obvious manner as a child (which I suspect they exaggerated to make her turn an even deeper beet red) to her disdain and apathy toward love scenes between men and women even into her teens. We got along very well, though, and I was told I was pretty and had a great voice several times. I was pleased. They also mentioned Julia singing. I still have not heard her sing.<br /> <br /> We returned, and everyone was playing video games. Jolie was cured which damaged Andromeda further, and Jacob is okay with Boss Lowjack. Gawain made a dream prison. De La Rocha ran in and tackled I, which I was not prepared for. Apparently she was in a good mood.<br /> <br /> I told Calamity and Lorelei my intention to sing \u201cNon, Je Ne Regrette Rien\u201d while sensually coiling around the stage. Julia suggested a Dietrich-esque suit and tophat, but Annika does that better than I, and I am somewhat known for my striped tophat and socks on stage, so I will do something with that. Maybe a striped jacket. I will work on choreographing something tomorrow. Oh, and recording it and replaying it very slowly at recessional. That should be something everyone gets, and the Changelings find especially amusing. I like that song anyway. I just need to do something that limits my dancing needs, I can\u2019t dance like the girls can.<br /> <br /> Tonight went well on stage. Lorelei was lovely, though I did not know her song. Calamity, seeking to impress Becky Wan, got all dressed up in pseudoreligious cloth, and I hooked her up with my choreography/system for \u201cIt\u2019s a Sin,\u201d which was popular in the past. She was quite impressive. She cuddled with Becky the rest of the night which was a little awkward as I planned to flirt with White Maria but did not want to draw Becky\u2019s eye\u2026since the Dahlia incident I am trying to be careful. It seemed to go okay.<br /> <br /> I had fun with my lovers and Gawain there hanging out and talking. Gawain agreed to make crepes tomorrow. He makes very good crepes. I pay him compliments because he deserves them.<br /> <br /> Lori wanted to sleep in the Hedge House, so afterwards she, De La Rocha, Julia and I all went out there for our usual display of affections. It had been a few nights since I had sampled Lorelei, and was pleased to indulge. Expressions of affection even love mixed with our passions, and the night passed beautifully. Now, sleep and breakfast.<br /> <br /> o o o o<br /> <br /> Breakfast was smooth, Becky joined us despite Calamity going home with her. Just like Oleander did with Lorelei a few days ago. Apparently bringing the person you went home with back to sex breakfast is a thing. Not that I am complaining. There was talk of \u201cMormon Hunting\u201d combining the weird American fixations on Firearms and Religion.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Firearms, the others went to the range, so Julia (after seeing to my needy toes) went with I to work on \u201cNon, Je Ne Regrette Rien.\u201d I put on a stripy hat, socks, and coat, and practiced it with a single chair I could wrap around and strut in front of. I am still working out the kinks, and this lead to making out (again) with Julia, I am not sure how I wound up laying on her kissing her on stage, but as the song says, je ne regrette rien.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXXVII</i><br /> <br /> I am sure Lorelei is too good a person to make the others watch Annie Hall. That is a Clarity check right?<br /> <br /> I am sure we all can\u2019t wait to see what is picked.<br /> <br /> Onto other subjects: Lowjack. Ah, Boss Lowjack. I took the curtain aside to discuss Lowjack after Jacob\u2019s scene. On some level, John Lowjack is what he seems to be: A well-connected bartender, good listener, busy guy who will give you the shirt off his back. But Lowjack is also a well-connected man who often leads from the shadows and gives nudges where they are needed. He is also older than most think\u2026he is around the same age as Annika, and while his Contracts are nothing to write home about, he is sporting a 6 in his Intelligence, Presence, and Manipulation, as well as a few skills like Politics and Empathy. Lowjack\u2019s plans are long term, and like Darke, Torrez or Spidertoes he is a character with an agenda\u2026but one that, honestly, I don\u2019t see the PCs disagreeing with too much.<br /> <br /> But yes, Jacob went to his King who simply said essentially \u201cGive me the data and I will forgive and protect you.\u201d This was partially because John Lowjack is a nice guy, sure. But Jacob is an asset. A skilled asset and an asset connected to some very important people in town, a motley with their fingers in all the Courts and some\u2026particular sets of skills. Jacob also, to Lowjack\u2019s eye, seemed both somewhat guilt ridden an unlikely to betray him. A low risk investment, considering the payoff.<br /> <br /> Also, accessing the hideaway he has for his own purposes and for the Knighthood of Utmost Silence involves reciting the last four lines of \u201cStopping By the Woods on a Snowy Evening\u201d by Robert Frost (The woods are lovely, dark and deep/But I have promises to keep/And miles to go before I sleep/And miles to go before I sleep.) It seemed appropriate.<br /> <br /> Not much else specific. Andromeda further damaged, issue with Jolie fixed. Relationship stuff. The usual. Good times.<br /> <br /> That about covers it. As always, Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T16:11:12-07:00","id":648443,"title":"","content":"Has Gawain been formally accepted in his chosen entitlement yet?<br /> Are Calamity and Becky girlfriends now?<br /> Is Lorelei's sudden decision to train to go free her friends due to Clarity gain/loss?<br /> Did Insincere Margueriite sleep on top of the girl pile in the Hollow?<br /> The public must know!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T22:13:39-07:00","id":648579,"title":"","content":"1) Yes, Gawain is part of the Family of Silent Nights, and Jacob is part of the Knighthood of Utmost Silence<br /> 2) No, Commitment and Becky Wan don't talk much. That will take some specific work.<br /> 3) No, everyone's Wyrd is about to go up, this is Lorelei's growing Wyrd. Her Clarity has stayed pretty much the same.<br /> 4) Probably. She tends to do that. I think it is part of her cat behaviors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T01:11:28-07:00","id":648651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play?p=648443#post648443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Calamity and Becky girlfriends now?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am sad that time got away from me and I didn't get Calamity's journal finished for the session. She does, in fact, muse on just that question for a good bit of it. At this point, I am planning to cover everything in another double journal next time. <br /> <br /> Basically she has feelings for Becky but she isn't sure exactly what to do about it. She knows she should speak to Gawain and Becky both but isn't sure exactly how to broach the topic with either and is a bit worried that it might not go well in either case. So for now she and Becky remain friends with excellent benefits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T02:33:00-07:00","id":665481,"title":"","content":"Another drama session, less eventful, moving towards a short time jump to Highsummer. But this session covered some more immediate stuff. Note Calamity\u2019s journal covers two sessions, so kinda long.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXXVII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> Jun 30th, early morning<br /> <br /> Is it bad I\u2019m waiting for the other shoe to drop, me in the future? I guess you\u2019d know, since the other shoe has probably either dropped or not dropped for you. Anyways, I think it\u2019s bad. After a day of smithy work and friendly conversation and a night with my lady, I should just, you know, be basking in the awesome. I mean, sure, part of the friendly conversation was distracting Joan from being upset and Desiree is worried about Chalcedony again and Lori managed to seduce Flores before me and Calamity could, but... basking.<br /> <br /> The others had far busier days than me. Lori, Jacob, Calamity and De la Roche went to the shooting range right after breakfast. Then they traded Jacob and De la Roche for Julia and went on up to the Autumn Court library. I guess that went well? Lori didn\u2019t so much say, you know, what she was after.<br /> <br /> I was just finishing up my metal work when they got home. I\u2019d settled on a spiraling metal vine, with the thorns, leaves and flowers being the imagery that signified, you know, the type of dream to be caught. I had some trouble getting the design down, my first two weren\u2019t so great. My third I designed to hold a nightmare, and it turned out excellent, in design and function. It figures that I\u2019d be better at nightmares, though Calamity did point out that maybe it was just having a focus, you know? She thought the third one was pretty awesome too.<br /> <br /> Calamity had a dinner date with Captain Jack, so she didn\u2019t take Flores up on her offer to have sex before the show. I walked in on them and De la Roche talking in Spanish. The offer was a little out of the blue, you know, from what I could tell, it had seemed kinda more serious and tense before then. Conversations with so many \u2018I\u2019m not angry\u2019s (I could interpret that much) in such angry tones rarely swerve so fast to quickies, but Flores was involved, so... She is super adorable. And hot.<br /> <br /> The show was pretty packed. Desiree was around so I talked with her some. She was doing good since last I\u2019d seen her, but like I said, was a little worried about Chalcedony. She\u2019d kinda hoped I\u2019d, you know, been talking with her, or that I knew something that\u2019d changed to make Chalcedony start following her and lurking around places she was. Not being threatening like Ginny had been, but worrisome anyways, you know?<br /> <br /> I talked with Joan too. Calamity had gotten there first and was able to, you know, give me a warning that Andromeda still wasn\u2019t feeling great and Joan was a little ragey. But she was supposed to be here and relax. So I got her to go back and forth with me about effects of military technology on the decline of feudalism. We\u2019d been over the ground a couple times before, so I was able to hop right in and distract her with familiarity before she had time to get grumpy and push me away. It was fun, and I think she did get some actual relaxing done.<br /> <br /> When Joan was in a better mood, and the show almost over, I found Calamity getting a backrub from Austen at the bar and Flores sitting in Lori\u2019s lap. Calamity had mentioned maybe seeing if Flores wanted to stay the night and, well, she certainly did. I jokingly told Calamity I was sorry for, you know, not out-seducing Lori, to which she mock-exasperatedly told me not to apologize. I think she said that a lot yesterday. It was good having her all to myself last night anyway. But I best get down to the kitchen, if we\u2019re gonna have steak dinner for sex breakfast.<br /> <br /> June 30th afternoon<br /> <br /> Well fuck. There\u2019s that other shoe. And breakfast was so nice, you know, with Flores and the rotating cast of sitter on Lori\u2019s lap as well as the newly discovered common thought of the two Spring courtiers of \u2018How do the plants feel about vegetarianism?\u2019. But then we started to split off - De la Roche to work, Julia to paint Flores, Flores to be painted.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite asked if we needed helped for out plans, and I mentioned needing to talk with Chalcedony. She volunteered to sneak around her place first, you know, just in case, and Calamity seemed pretty keen on it, so I let them, you know, feel secure about it before I made the call. All they found that was suspicious was some chloroform.<br /> <br /> So then I called her. There was a lot of \u2018things going on\u2019 and \u2018favors to be dealt with\u2019, busy schedule stuff, and so she wanted to put off dealing with the \u2018little irritation\u2019 of the trigger. It\u2019s her life, not mine, but something like that seems to be, you know, more than a little irritation. Something\u2019s going on, she said as much, and that she wasn\u2019t sure what she could say without breaking a pledge. She was still worried about Desiree being a loyalist and did promise to call me if things went bad, But, I dunno, it seemed off even to me. Calamity was even more sure that something was up.<br /> <br /> I hated myself a little for doing it, but I did ask Insincere Marguerite to follow her. Maybe we can help her, to stop her from hurting others, or maybe I\u2019ll just have started spying on people cause they don\u2019t trust me 100%. She\u2019s gonna start this afternoon and be back in time for movie night. You know, so long as things don\u2019t go bad. I don't even know what I want to be the case. No, that\u2019s not true. I want it to be the case that there\u2019s something I can help with and nobody gets hurt. That\u2019s worth feeling a little guilty.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Sometimes I really don\u2019t know what I\u2019m doing. Here I am rushing headlong into preparations for rescuing Missy and Jane, like it\u2019s something I\u2019m going to do within the next few days, when in reality I know that it could be months before I\u2019m ready to head back into Arcadia\u2026 hell, I may <u><u>never</u></u> be ready. But I guess it\u2019s better than sitting around pretending that it never happened\u2026 that I\u2019m not responsible.<br /> <br /> So anyway, after I finished sulking in my room yesterday, Calamity and Julia took me by the Autumn Court\u2019s library to see what we could find on the Violet Empress. There wasn\u2019t a lot there, and what we found was\u2026 inconclusive. The Freehold doesn\u2019t know a whole lot about her. Apparently she\u2019s not very well-liked among the Gentry, and she doesn\u2019t have any close allies who will come to her aid if she\u2019s in trouble. She\u2019s set herself up as a social butterfly, and she gets invited to all the best parties\u2026 but that might just be because that\u2019s how she defines her role in their society.<br /> <br /> I should probably talk to Queen Charlotte or Madame Spidertoes about her at some point; I might be able to add to the Freehold\u2019s knowledge. I remember one time, for example, Her Majesty brought us out to show us off to a few puissant guests. She wanted to make a big entrance, of course, and when she arrived, the herald announced her with a list of titles as long as my arm. Among those titles, I caught \u201cDarkest and Most Terrible of the Seven Sovereigns of the Broken Light.\u201d So maybe she does have a clique, and the Freehold just doesn\u2019t know about it. Or maybe she made up the title to make her sound impressive in front of her guests. Who knows?<br /> <br /> As far as I can tell, none of the Empress\u2019 other playthings have ever come to Malibu. There are no other escapees on record, and she doesn\u2019t tend to employ Loyalists. Oh, she uses Changelings like Hunting Hawk as bounty hunters, but the Freehold has never found an infiltrator from her realm.<br /> <br /> Calamity and Julia ganged up on me before we left the library for a little of the old \u201cOkay-Lori-What-Exactly-Are-You-Planning\u201d routine. They both pretty much knew what was going on in my head, so I didn\u2019t see the point in prevarication. I explained that yes, I am planning to head back to the Empress\u2019 realm to rescue Missy and Jane, and that yes, I am stepping up my timetable. I also told them that I wasn\u2019t going to ask for any help from the motley on this mission\u2026 but that I wasn\u2019t just going to sneak off like a thief in the night, either.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou can\u2019t do this alone, Lori,\u201d Calamity said seriously.<br /> <br /> \u201cI know,\u201d I said in return, \u201cbut I can\u2019t ask anyone to come with me. I can\u2019t have that on my conscience if things go wrong.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou don\u2019t have to ask, you know,\u201d she shot back.<br /> <br /> I think I might have smiled and cried a little at the same time. \u201cI know,\u201d I said again, \u201cand I won\u2019t be so ungrateful as to tell you guys that you can\u2019t come with me. For one thing, it would destroy D if I left her behind. Hell, she\u2019s probably already figured out what I\u2019m up to\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe has,\u201d Julia said quietly. \u201cShe\u2019s really worried about you, Lori.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShit,\u201d I replied. \u201cGuess I need to talk to her about this, huh?\u201d<br /> <br /> Julia nodded. \u201cLori\u2026 you know I\u2019m with you on this too, right? I mean, I don\u2019t know how much use I\u2019ll be in Arcadia, but if you go, de la Rocha and Marguerite will go with you, and the thought of staying behind on my own is\u2026 I just couldn\u2019t.\u201d She looked me straight in the face and said seriously \u201cI\u2019d die first.\u201d<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know what to think about that. I\u2019m flattered that she\u2019d want to help with this, but I really don\u2019t need another loved one risking their life for my sake. Julia\u2019s not built for quests like this. Come to that, neither am I, but I don\u2019t have any choice in this matter.<br /> <br /> Julia also had another bit of advice to impart: she thinks we ought to talk to Madame Spidertoes about this before setting out. She has a point; of everyone in the Freehold, Madame Spidertoes has spent more time in Arcadia than anyone else, and her knowledge could prove invaluable. But she\u2019s pretty damn intimidating, and she\u2019s not known for being particularly forthcoming with her secret knowledge.<br /> <br /> \u201cThere\u2019s one person she\u2019d talk to,\u201d Julia said hesitantly.<br /> <br /> I sighed. She\u2019s right, though. Spidertoes would probably tell D everything she wanted to know. I just wasn\u2019t relishing asking my honey for a favor, considering how things had gone between us earlier that day.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Julia and I made our way back to the Dream House (Calamity had dinner with Captain Jack, but she eventually made it back as well). We spent a little while enjoying each other\u2019s company, and then I had to get ready for the show. It was not my best work; I just rehashed a few of my old numbers, but it seemed to go pretty well nonetheless.<br /> <br /> Joan was there, sitting at a table by herself. I tried to stop by and ask how Andromeda was doing, but Calamity intercepted me before I got there. She\u2019d spoken with Joan during the show, and warned me that she was\u2026 angry. Angrier than usual, I mean. Andromeda is not getting better, and Joan blames herself. Calamity says that she\u2019s blaming herself because if she doesn\u2019t, she\u2019ll end up blaming\u2026 other people.<br /> <br /> Like, you know\u2026 me. Because it\u2019s my fault. Because I made Andromeda use the Table to fix Jolie. I wanted to apologize, to offer to do whatever I can to help, but Calamity\u2019s right\u2026 in her current mood, that would only have made Joan angrier.<br /> <br /> So I avoided her gaze and went to my usual table, where D, Flores, Marguerite and Julia were waiting. I pulled D away from the table and asked to speak to her privately for a moment, and she agreed with a curt nod, followed me up to our room, and closed the door behind us.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo you\u2019re talking to me again?\u201d she asked quietly.<br /> <br /> I pulled her into a hug. \u201cSorry,\u201d I whispered into her ear, \u201cI was just so angry. You seemed intent on starting a fight at the range for no reason\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> She pulled back for a moment and looked into my eyes, and there was so much pain in her expression that I didn\u2019t know how to process it. \u201cI hope,\u201d she said softly, \u201cthat you never know what it feels like to have a room full of people looking at you and judging you and thinking of you as a lesser being just because of who you are,\u201d she said with a quiver in her voice. \u201cAnd it\u2019s not your fault, Lori\u2026 you always make me feel like a queen when we\u2019re together. But I hope you never get to the point where that sort of judgment is something you can see in their eyes\u2026 even if they don\u2019t actually say or do anything about it.\u201d<br /> <br /> It was like she\u2019d slapped me. I\u2019d never thought about it in those terms before. I mean, I\u2019ve always thought that racism was a particularly stupid way of looking at the world, but I guess I\u2019ve never really gotten inside the head-space of a minority and thought about what it would be like to be on the receiving end of that kind of ignorance and prejudice. I felt like a stupid, entitled white girl, and it made me sick.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, sweetie,\u201d I whispered, pulling her in close, \u201cI\u2019m so sorry. I love you. You know that, right? Even when I was so mad earlier, all I could think about was how much I love you. I\u2019m sorry you had to go through that, and I\u2019m sorry if anything I said or did made your day worse.\u201d<br /> <br /> She smiled at me and kissed my forehead. \u201cHey, it\u2019s okay,\u201d she said soothingly. \u201cI know you\u2019ve had some heavy shit on your mind lately\u2026 which you\u2019re hopefully going to share with me at some point,\u201d she added pointedly.<br /> <br /> I sighed. \u201cYou already know what I\u2019m going to say,\u201d I said flatly.<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cI think so, yeah,\u201d she said in a serious tone.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m going back for them,\u201d I stated. \u201cMissy and Jane. I\u2019ve put it off too long, and I\u2019m going back for them. I just need to learn how to find them, and how to stay alive long enough to get them out of Arcadia.\u201d Simple as that, right?<br /> <br /> D nodded again. \u201cWhen do we leave?\u201d she asked. When I sputtered, she put a finger across my lips. \u201cYou are <u><u>not</u></u> going without me, Lori, and that\u2019s final, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> I took her hand. \u201cOf course not,\u201d I acquiesced. \u201cI would never have just snuck off on my own; I respect you too much for that. And I know you\u2019d never let me go alone. But\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re afraid,\u201d D supplied gently.<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cOf course I\u2019m afraid,\u201d I said. \u201cWho wouldn\u2019t be? How would you feel if you were going back to the Hospital? But that\u2019s not the main thing. The real problem is Her.\u201d <br /> <br /> I leveled my gaze at my wonderful girlfriend and put as much steel in my voice as I could. \u201cYou\u2019re mine,\u201d I said after a moment. It was the first time I\u2019d said it so baldly; the first time I\u2019ve done anything even remotely like claiming her. I\u2026 don\u2019t like framing relationships in terms of possession. I imagine that point of view is common among people who have spent time as slaves.<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course I am,\u201d she replied immediately.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe can\u2019t have you,\u201d I said firmly. D looked a little confused. \u201cShe can\u2019t have you,\u201d I said again, and I heard a quiver starting up in my voice. \u201cYou\u2019re mine and I won\u2019t let Her take you from me and She\u2019ll try if I bring you along because you\u2019re mine and she can\u2019t stand for anything to exist in Her realm that isn\u2019t Hers.\u201d Oh, yeah, the tears were really starting to flow by this point. \u201cI\u2019d rather\u2026 I\u2019d rather leave Missy and Jane behind in Her realm than let Her have you\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> My eyes widened as I realized what I\u2019d just said. I turned away from her and started to sob. A second later her arms settled comfortably around my waist. \u201cLori,\u201d she whispered softly in my ear, \u201cI love you. Nobody is going to take me away from you. Do you understand? Not the Empress. Not Marguerite. <u><u>Nobody</u>.</u>\u201d<br /> <br /> My love is the best girlfriend in the world.<br /> <br /> I got myself under control after a few minutes of kisses. \u201cYou up for joining the company again?\u201d D asked once I\u2019d fixed my makeup. \u201cOr would you rather just stay up here for tonight? Or do you have\u2026 other plans?\u201d<br /> <br /> The hitch in her voice was only there if you know her well. She was asking about Oleander without using her name. She\u2019s <u><u>really</u></u> good at keeping the bitterness out of her voice. She doesn\u2019t want me to know that it still bothers her. She doesn\u2019t want to shame or manipulate me into doing anything. Sigh. I\u2019m probably going to have to address that issue soon, one way or another. And deep down, I think I know what I have to do.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t feel like dealing with it last night, however. \u201cWe should get back,\u201d I said brightly, \u201cbefore people start to talk.\u201d D laughed at that, which was exactly what I wanted.<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay, cool,\u201d she said as she took my hand and led me to the door. \u201cI can introduce you to Flores.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI already know Flores,\u201d I said, confused.<br /> <br /> \u201cNot well enough,\u201d D smirked.<br /> <br /> So we went back downstairs and joined the others. I started flirting pretty shamelessly with Flores, and D backed me up. Before long she ended up sitting in my lap, and as the drinks flowed, she eventually turned around so that she was straddling me, and we started making out. It wasn\u2019t long before the group of us made our way upstairs.<br /> <br /> Flores is an enthusiastic lover, to say the least. She enjoys sex at least as much as I do, and tends to devote herself whole-heartedly to her partner\u2019s pleasure. And she\u2019s\u2026 hmm\u2026 how to put this delicately? Ah, the hell with it. That sweet floral smell that surrounds her extends to pretty much <u><u>every</u></u> part of her, and she tastes as sweet as she smells.<br /> <br /> It was a very pleasant night, and I ended up snuggled up against D for a while as the others continued to frolic. Of course, we woke up as part of the usual contented tangle of limbs, and Flores opted to join the rest of us for sex breakfast.<br /> <br /> Topics of conversation this morning included White Maria and Chalcedony. White Maria apparently decided to give Dark Kimberly the chance to atone for her past misdeeds\u2026 by sending her an ornate ceremonial dagger. This was her not-so-subtle way of informing Dark Kimberly that she could make up for her mistakes by taking her own life honorably. Dark Kimberly returned the knife without using it, and I say good for her. As I said aloud during breakfast, I hadn\u2019t realized that we had opened a burlesque house in fucking sixteenth century China.<br /> <br /> Chalcedony\u2019s situation is if anything even more worrying. Gawain called her up to see what he could do about removing the trigger inside her brain, like he did for Desiree. Chalcedony apparently isn\u2019t interested. Oh, she\u2019s not against the idea, exactly\u2026 but she doesn\u2019t seem to think it\u2019s very important at the moment, and claims to have other things to do right now. She\u2019s still got her eye on Desiree, too\u2026 she says that just because the other girl isn\u2019t being controlled by the Gentry, that doesn\u2019t mean that she can be trusted.<br /> <br /> Marguerite and Calamity actually went out to check out Chalcedony\u2019s place to see if she was up to anything untoward, and their findings were not encouraging. In addition to the freakish prevalence of the color blue in the d\u00e9cor (which we already knew about), Marguerite also found chloroform. How many legitimate reasons are there for someone to keep chloroform in their apartment?<br /> <br /> So through the early part of breakfast, Flores was sitting in my lap with her hands around my neck. It was fun, and light, and I think we were both enjoying ourselves as we laughed and talked about sex. At some point, she got up, and Julia took her place. When the two of them went off to work on sketches, Marguerite plopped down into my lap. It seemed that we were starting to develop a theme.<br /> <br /> When Marguerite vacated my lap, I glanced at Gawain with a wink and beckoned him over as a joke. He took me up on the offer, but rather than sitting in my lap, he picked me up as if I weighed nothing at all, sat down in my place, and then put me in <u>his</u> lap. I gave him a mock-pout, and then turned my attention to Jacob and invited him to join us. Much to my surprise, our stoic Russian comrade gave me a little smile and settled himself gently into my lap. Who knew he even had it in him?<br /> <br /> Hmm\u2026 a Gawain-Lorelei-Jacob sandwich. The idea has merit.<br /> <br /> D went off to work after that, and most of the others seem to have things to do, so I\u2019ve been writing in this journal to kill time before I go to meet Monica for our little excursion into the Hedge. I\u2019m not sure how I feel about this, exactly\u2026 I\u2019m scared, because I\u2019m always scared when I have to go into the Hedge, but I\u2019m also excited. It\u2019s sort of like a new chapter of my life is about to begin, and, scary or not, that\u2019s kind of thrilling.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T02:33:35-07:00","id":665483,"title":"","content":"<b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> <u><b><b><u>Sunday June 29<sup>th </sup></u></b></b></u><br /> <br /> Days Without Stabbing: 12<br /> <br /> Technically, that count should be reset after last night, but really the only thing that couldn't be fixed with a little Spring Court magic was my outfit. Mmm... It's a shame velvet is so expensive. This little monster quite enjoyed the effect it had on Becky. And after seeing what dressing up for her does I can only imagine the kind of defiling and ravaging I'd get to experience if I lured my favorite succubus into one of the local cathedrals.<br /> <br /> It was so good to see how much less stressed out Becky was this morning. Yesterday when I called her I could tell she'd moved from hot wrath to cold anger toward Dark Kimberly. On one hand, I was glad that she didn't seem to be on the verge of doing anything reckless but it was clearly still weighing heavily on her. And she had to escort Jolie to her meeting with Andromeda and The Table. I almost asked if there was anyone else who could go, but I knew there was no one else Jolie would trust with her secret and no one else Becky would trust with her queen's safety. And yeah, it goes beyond Jolie's position and Becky's duty to her monarch. Which, of course, made the prospect of having to be there but not be able to do anything that much harder for her. She did promise to come to the Dream House for the show.<br /> <br /> I did wish I could have been there to try to comfort her during the procedure. But Jolie wasn't keen on having any more of an audience than necessary (and I can't honestly blame her there). Also, I'd promised to go with Jacob to confess to Boss Lowjack about his past and his desire to try to bring Rook around when he returns. Lori was there and she did her best to calm Becky. I imagine she was a more soothing presence than I could have been.<br /> <br /> John Lowjack was polite and took us into his office to speak when we arrived. He took the time to hear Jacob out carefully, nodding and asking a few questions. I didn't speak much, letting Jacob tell his own story. Though at one point I did confirm that I trusted him with my life and the lives of my motley mates. I think Lowjack took it as a point in Jacob's favor.<br /> <br /> In the end, he requested a pair of very carefully worded reports, one of the Lady's people and tactics and previous activities. The other on Jacob's own actions in her service. The former he intended to share. The latter he promised to keep very secure. Also, he promised that if anything came up or if anyone accused Jacob that he would have the proof that he knew of Jacob's past already. It was all very practical and reasonable. Once we were done, Jacob dropped me back at the Dream House and returned to deal with some entitlement business.<br /> <br /> I spent the afternoon unwinding with a nice spot of virtual murder. Before long everyone filtered in. Gawain joined me which was nice, since it meant at least one person on my side was competent. Lori seemed a bit taken aback by the taunting I was delivering, at least until Gawain unplugged the headphones and she heard the little shits. I do adore the way they sputter and fume when they get their fucking asses handed to them by a girl.<br /> <br /> Lori let us know the operation to remove Jolie's curse had been successful. But it had taken a heavy toll on Andromeda. According to her, the dear little sweetling was drained and emotionless when it was over. Joan came and collected her but Lori was worried about her. I couldn't help but recall how soulless and dead inside Grey had been. Of course, he'd used the thrice-damned thing often over a much longer time. But my little dear knew what she was risking when she agreed to do it. She recovered from using it to cure Joan, so hopefully she'll be back to her perky self soon. I do agree with Lori that she needs to be done with The Table after this. Of course, that's easy to say right now but as long as it exists there will be temptations to use it. Even without straying into the sort of soul rape Darke committed with it, there will be another like Jolie or Joan with some curse or affliction. And I know Andromeda. She's kind hearted and wants to help people... fix them. And even beyond the danger of that temptation, so long as we have it, the Mothership will seek to recover it. No, it must be destroyed.<br /> <br /> So as showtime approached I went to get ready. I took a gamble based on a few things I knew about Becky and hit the costume room for something with lots of velvet and religious symbolism before settling in to paint my face like I meant it. I have to say, I was pretty damn pleased with the results. And Gawain certainly looked approvingly over me when I caught up with him to talk to him about my intentions to spend the night focused on Becky. He was supportive because that's how he is. But in hindsight, I wonder if he feels like I take him for granted. I mean, I did go pretty fucking all out for Becky last night. And hell, I did make her part of our Greening night. I mean, yeah it was two hot women in his bed but on the other hand, maybe that particular night should have been just about the two of us. I guess it's on my mind because sitting here now I can't deny that I have some feelings where Becky is concerned and a desire for more than just occasional nights of amazing, mind-blowing sex. Not that I don't want as much of that as I can get, after all the woman is literally made for sex. But I do consider her a close friend and I... fuck I'm not sure just what I'm feeling and I sure as fuck am not sure what to do with it.<br /> <br /> But last night my mind was laser focused on Becky and trying to drive the past week out of her thoughts. The moment she laid eyes on me I knew the extra effort in preparation had been worth every second. I did my best demure but actually sexy walk across the room and smiled at her. We talked a bit and then I did make a circuit of the room like I'm supposed to. As I was, Insincere Marguerite asked me if I wanted her to substitute in 'It's a Sin.\u201d I thought it was a good idea and we to switch things around with Lori and the performers. I'm not sure exactly who's idea it was but by the time we'd finished the last minute schedule changes I was slated to lead it. Fuck if I wasn't nervous as hell. But I think in the end it was the best way for it to happen. I have no idea how long I would have ended up waiting for everything to be perfect otherwise. When Ace announced me, he made a point of letting Becky know the number was for her and I gave her the bedroom eyes as I danced for her. Insincere Marguerite's choreography was an ideal vehicle for my desires and I fucking nailed it. I mean, I'm still not close to Annika or Lori but I certainly didn't embarrass myself. And I felt... damn I felt so gorram amazing up there. Fuck but now I understand how people can get so fucking caught up and addicted to the rush of performing. Zod knows I'm fucking eager to take to the stage again after that.<br /> <br /> And after I was done, I zeroed in on Becky's table. She was giving me a look that let no doubts that she'd caught my intentions and was totally on board. I was a bad girl for the rest of the night, I slipped into the seat beside her and spent the rest of the show flirting and playing with that wonderful hair. I'm pretty sure nothing caught fire but I can't say for sure I would have noticed. Once the show was over, Becky swept me up and took me to her car and drove me to her house. Considering that neither of us was paying attention to the road, I am not sure quite how we made it without an accident. She opened the door and waited for me to enter. I stepped past her and then before I could turn she was behind me, catching a fistful of my hair and spinning us to use me to slam the door shut as she crashed into me hard enough to drive the air from my body and then she claimed my mouth in a long hard kiss. My lungs were burning and I had spots dancing at the corners of my vision by the time she relented and let me draw a breath.<br /> <br /> Her eyes were hungry and blazing. She pressed against me and caressed me with her fingers and her hair as we both caught our breath. I purred under those touches. Then I looked at her and asked her what she wanted.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou,\u201d was all she answered.<br /> <br /> \u201cSeriously Becky,\u201d I wriggled my arms free enough to return the light touches along her sides and hips, \u201cI want to make tonight about you. I want...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTo know what I like.\u201d she finished. Then she gathered me and drew me to the living room and down onto a loveseat with her. \u201cYou're not the first to ask Calamity. But the truth is, I want what whoever I'm with wants me to.\u201d<br /> <br /> I cocked my head a little but before I could speak her hand was on my lips. \u201cIt's how I was made,\u201d she explained as she let her fingers slide slowly over and caress my cheek, \u201cIt's not just that I want to please you. I honestly want what you want me to. I need what you need. And right now, you need...\u201d Suddenly her fingers curled, claws biting into the skin along my cheekbone sharply before she jerked her hand down and left a quartet of red lines down the side of my face. \u201cTo bleed or draw blood,\u201d she growled as she lifted her fingers with the stark crimson adorning their tips.<br /> <br /> I blinked to hear my own words on her lips and realized that I knew that hungry look in her eyes intimately. I shivered and watched her slowly bringing her hand to her lips. Then I reached, grabbing her wrist with my hands and leaning in to trap her fingertip in my mouth and clean it with a long low moan of pleasure. As I worshiped her claws with my lips and tongue her other hand stroked my hair, curling it around her fingers slowly. Then, once I'd reclaimed my essence quite completely she clenched that hand into a fist, pulling tight at my head and using it to turn and tilt my head so she could lean in and lick the wounds she'd left on my face. Then her lips were at my ear. They brushed it as she whispered, her breath soft and warm against my skin. \u201cDon't worry my pretty little sweetling,\u201d she whispered, \u201cI'll put you back together after I'm done...\u201d<br /> <br /> It was a long and glorious night. By turns I begged and coaxed and provoked my beautiful dragon until I'd milked every bit of frustration and anger and tension from her. I was broken and put back together and broken again. But at last, sometime near dawn she tiredly mended me with a long ragged yawn. I smiled and reached for her, pulling her closer and resting her head on my chest. Her hair lazily shifted as I stroked it, teasing me a little but we were both far too well and truly spent for anything else. She looked up at me sleepily and frowned a little.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou're not going to sleep are you?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo. But I promise I'm not going anywhere. I'll be right here when you wake up love-ly.\u201d<br /> <br /> If she caught the pause she didn't show it. She eased an arm under and one over me and held onto me tightly as I ran my fingers through her hair and brushed her back. \u201cYou should sleep,\u201d she murmured but I just kept petting her until her breathing went regular and she relaxed. I rested like that and when she woke I was right there smiling at her.<br /> <br /> As we were unhurriedly waking and dressing I took her hand and brought it to one of my shards. I explained why I can't let myself sleep with her or anyone else. She assured me that she does understand even if if it does make her a little sad. I assured her that as a Darkling, I am vampire enough to enjoy watching her sleep. She huffed and hit me with a pillow, which prompted a playful return swing but did not escalate from a pillow skirmish to a full blown fight.<br /> <br /> Since she had to drive me back to the Dream House anyway I invited her to the infamous sex breakfast and she accepted. It was the usual banter and playful hijinks and I think she enjoyed it. When she excused herself afterward she did seem much more relaxed which made me quite happy.<br /> <br /> After breakfast it was time to head to the gun range. Our beautiful songbird has really doubled down on the self improvement these past few days. Going with DLR to work out wasn't odd, I mean staying in top shape is important for a performer and a model. So wanting to spend time getting sweaty with her girl outside the bedroom wasn't unusual. But apparently she's going into the hedge with Monica on Monday and she spent last night in the Hollow House. I know how uncomfortable the Hedge makes her and she says she's trying to get over that. Again, not a terribly suspicious thing by itself. But while we were at the gun range she asked Jacob about showing her some survival basics and me about the Autumn Court's library.<br /> <br /> I have a pretty good guess as to what her end game is. She broke a promise to her friends when she left Arcadia and she told us she would go back for them some day. I think that day is coming sooner rather than later. Not sure what's prompted the shift but it does explain all of the things she's doing. The fact that she hasn't said anything concerns me. I mean, it could just be that I'm wrong about what's going on here. But I don't think so. I hope she's not thinking of running off to Arcadia by herself. I mean, I know it's something she needs to do but she doesn't need to do it alone. I'll watch her at the library. I should be able to get a clearer idea of her intentions and if my hunch is right it will be a good opportunity to bring it up with her discreetly.<br /> <br /> I am her friend and her motley sister and this is actually the sort of shit I'm fucking good at thanks to Snow Globe. Time to cut some assholes that truly do deserve it for a change.<br /> <br /> Besides which, slipping into a Gentry's realm to rescue a pair of changelings is firmly on the black side of the ledger. I mean, karma is nothing but fucking spiritual victim blaming and I'll be damned (literally and gladly) before I fucking do anything just because some cosmic voyeur is watching me and keeping score. Fuck all that shit. The only person I answer to is the one that looks back at me from the mirror and there's no point is trying to lie to her. She knows my sins and she knows exactly what I am. And what I am is fucking dangerous. But as long as there are monsters out there worse than me to take it out on, I can at least do good. And at the end of the night, that's fucking close enough to being good.<br /> <br /> <u><b><b><u>Monday, June 30<sup>th</sup></u></b></b></u><br /> <br /> Days without Stabbing: 13<br /> <br /> Well, that was fun-fucking-tastic. Malevolent. That's the word the archives kept using to describe Snow Globe. Even compared to the Gentry standard apparently that place rates the term. It's old, older than the whole fifties black and white. Apparently the other Gentry try to take over from time to time and the fighting always levels the current town and a new one is built. A new place of nostalgic it-was-better-back-then purer morals. But it's not the Voices. It's not even the old man. It's the entire fucking place. Snow Globe itself is the Keeper. The entire fucking place is aware and malevolent. It doesn't care about the other Gentry. It doesn't make loyalists. The whole candy and torture conditioning doesn't work well once someone is away from that fucking hell hole. The other survivors are all like me, fucked up and anti-social. Apparently we tend to be court-less wandering murder hobos. Makes sense. I do not do well with authority and bullshit after being in that place. I certainly don't take orders well. It's weird, nothing in there was really news to me. But somehow seeing it like that just made things I knew but didn't want to admit sink in. Malevolent.<br /> <br /> Lori and Julia could see that it was bothering me. When I muttered about never being able to destroy it Lori touched one of my shards and reminded me that maybe I couldn't kill it but I could hurt it. The glass inside me is Snow Globe. Snow Globe IS my Keeper, not the Whispering Voices. I carry a piece of It inside me now. It's coiled around my bones like a cancer and it grows out through my flesh. Malevolent. Snow Globe is aware and It's evil. Everything is designed to twist and torment and torture It's victims. Why? Because it ENJOYS the suffering and pain it causes. It craves the fear and pain. Snow Globe is a sadistic malevolent thing that feeds upon the misery and suffering It sows. And when I left that place, I brought a piece of It with me. I clutched it close and made It part of me. And now I am cruel. I enjoyed killing Grey. I... I enjoyed killing my parents. It felt amazing. Malevolent. I escaped, but I will never be free of Snow Globe. It is part of me now. It pierces my skin and itches inside my fingers, craving blood and tears and pain. As I write this, I can feel the weight of my stolen Rolex like a shackle. The memory of that night, of how it made he feel to make that man wet himself in fear and beg and grovel for his life is vivid. Calamity is well and truly Snow Globe's daughter.<br /> <br /> Despite having the weight of that settling in, I did not miss the relevance of Lori's search. The Violet Empress and her realm. She's going back for her friends. Rather than dwelling on the thoughts brewing in my own head, I focused on that and confronted her about it along with Julia. She didn't deny it. She hasn't been trying to hide it (which is good because she hasn't been subtle) but she simply cannot and will not ask us to be part of this. She knows she needs help and she wants us to be there, but she can't use the ties to us to guilt us into joining her. I made it clear that I am going with her. I'm sure we all are. Julia was also determined to go. She won't sit and wait for those she loves to return. She's going with us to make sure Insincere Marguerite and Lori and de la Rocha return. This isn't the sort of thing she does, but she's tougher than I think most of the others give her credit for. She knows how to use a knife. She did kill her fetch to reclaim her life. She's an artist but she is still a Darkling and there is steel under that silk and lace.<br /> <br /> So I was a bit sober when I met with Joaquin for dinner. Since I was asking him to step out of character it only seemed fair to do the same so I told him he could call me Katheryn. He asked about when it was alright to call me by it. Names have power after all. And among us they have magical power to be sure but it was more than that. Captain Jack is larger than life. Captain Jack is a hero. We didn't get into too many details, but he hinted at his own past and that he was not the man he is now when he first returned. He remade himself into the face he we all know him as. I told him I was trying to reclaim whatever might be left of the girl I was before. I also explained how much his belief in me at my trial meant to me. The role he played in the Court's leniency really isn't as important to me as the fact that I know he wouldn't have said what he did if he hadn't believed in my ability to actually salvage and rebuild myself. Oh, he would have done his best to help me no matter what. He is my friend. But if he hadn't thought I could do this on my own, he would have pushed for me to be helped like Mary was. I can see now just how dangerously close to the edge I was but he believed that I could bring myself back from it. Now I just have to prove him right.<br /> <br /> I also brought up John Lowjack. He wasn't keen on the topic but we talked about things. That there are feelings there is obvious. But Lowjack isn't open about his own feelings and Joaquin isn't subtle about his. Why must people get so fucking hung up about this shit? It nearly wrecked de la Rocha that she fell in love with a woman. Julia still seems to be trying to deny that she's not interested in men. Life is short and hard like body building elf as it is. Why in the hell make it more difficult and complicated with all this fucking bullshit? I'm with Flores on this one, sex is good period.<br /> <br /> But self inflicted repression aside, I do get why Joaquin is attracted to John Lowjack. The man's smart and reasonable and seems inclined to do the right thing as best as he can. Jacob and I's meeting with him yesterday was proof of that. I'm not naive, Jacob is valuable to the Freehold and the Winter Court and their Entitlement. Helping him is both the right move and the practical one. The man is prepared to do what's best for the Freehold. As much as I despise Darke and what he did, Lowjack was right about us needing him. I also have no doubt that the man can and does place a value on Jacob and doing the right thing by him. A value that will be weighed against sacrificing him. I do believe that if that scale tipped in the wrong direction he would try to find a way around it and he'd feel terrible about it. But ultimately, I think if push comes to shove John Low jack\u2019s pragmatism would outweigh his personal feelings toward anyone.<br /> <br /> All in all it was a good dinner. I like Joaquin and I think he enjoyed the gesture. I got back in time for the opening. I was already presentable so I just took to the floor and began making my usual rounds. And oh but there was more drama on the floor than the stage.<br /> <br /> Joan was there nearly vibrating with barely contained rage. When I approached her, she explained that Andromeda was not recovering nearly as well or as quickly from the most recent use of the table. She was there because she had been told to go and relax. Of course, she was anything but. I tried to speak to her but she didn't want company and she wasn't in the mood to be comforted or distracted by anything I managed to suggest. In the end I had to just leave her to seethe. I caught Lori as she was stepping that way and told her Joan was not up for seeing anyone remotely connected to the table being used. I also spoke to Gawain, mostly to have him help me keep her table clear but he decided to try speaking to her. They do have a better rapport and he was able to actually distract her by discussing medieval history and weapons. I breathed a sigh of relief when I saw that she wasn't going to shut him out like she had done with me.<br /> <br /> Of course, as it turned out that wasn't the end of my headaches. I moved to check on White Maria and see how she was doing in the wake of the whole mess. She was dour. She had apparently sent Dark Kimberly a rather ornate and expensive dagger so that she could cleanse her honor with suicide. Dark Kimberly returned the blade unused and White Maria was not pleased, though apparently she credited Kimberly with not keeping the blade like a thief. I can at least understand where White Maria is coming from and while I have no use for all this honor bullshit it was not the worst thing she could have done.<br /> <br /> I left her there alone with her honor and her indignant rage. I saw that Gawain was engaging Joan still and headed to the bar to ask Jacob for a stiff drink. Austin was there and by the time I'd set the shot glass back down he was behind me and slipping his hands down the sides of my neck to pinch the tense muscles at the base of my shoulders. I was a bit surprised but I sure as hell wasn't going to complain. I eased back into his magical hands as I relayed the frustrations with White Maria and Joan. He and Jacob listened and commented a bit but before long I was just purring and relaxing as the conversation shifted to light bantering. Damn that man has amazing hands.<br /> <br /> The show ended without incident and Austin had to take his wonderful hands with him. I thanked him quite sincerely for his efforts and wished him well. Gawain found me as things were wrapping up and I was quite happy to let him scoop me up and carry me off to our bed. After not sleeping the night before I was fading even before he got me to our bedroom and tucked me in. I curled into his arms and sighed contentedly as I nuzzled into him and told him not to keep me waiting in my dreams. He didn't.<br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> After we got back from the range Lori and Calamity went to the Autumn Court\u2019s library to do some research. They did not mention specifically what they were looking for, but I can make an educated guess. Well, I can guess for Lorelei anyway. I\u2019d say she was probably doing research on her Keeper and the Violet Empress\u2019 realm. She\u2019s been making more inquiries about the Hedge than usual and volunteering to spend time there. Heck, she\u2019s even set up a time to go into the Hedge with Monica on a patrol. Plus she wants me to help her learn how to track. Yeah, our pretty lady is up to something, and as I\u2019ve mentioned, I think I know what it is. I can\u2019t help but wonder if something prompted her interest in retrieving her friends or if it was a spur of the moment kind of thing? Did she remember something, or did something that someone said make her think of it? I need to talk to her about that and make sure that she\u2019s not planning on going after her friends by herself.<br /> <br /> So, I finished up my \u201chomework\u201d for Lowjack and brought it over to his bar. He said that he\u2019d take a look at it and let me know if he had any questions. It took me a while to put it all together. The information wasn\u2019t hard to arrange, but wording things in such a way that they don\u2019t implicate me was the hard part. I tried to write in as detached a manner as possible, and I went over it probably half a dozen times to make sure it sounded okay. I wrote it with the idea that whoever read it had absolutely no knowledge of the Lady\u2019s realm. Which will probably be true. I do not know if the Freehold has many people that are familiar with the Lady and her land. I guess I\u2019ll just wait for Boss Lowjack to read it and see if he has any suggestions or questions about what I\u2019ve written.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> During the show I had a couple of interesting conversations. The first was with Austin who came over to ask me if I would be available to work as the bartender during the High Summer event that will be held this year. Apparently Lowjack is their usual bartender, but since he will have monarch duties to attend to this time around they are in need of someone to mix and serve drinks. I told him that I\u2019d be happy to help out as long as it didn\u2019t conflict with a show at the Dream House. He assured me that it shouldn\u2019t clash with any show times. It will be interesting bartending for such a large group. There are several members of the freehold that do not frequent the Dream House, so I will have the opportunity to learn new drink preferences and mix up different things than I usually do. It has the potential to be fun.<br /> <br /> The second interesting conversation to come up was with Calamity. She came over after I\u2019d talked to Austin, but while the Spring courtier was still there. She went on about Joan being upset by Andromeda not being back to normal yet. Apparently the slight girl is still acting \u201coff\u201d and Joan is concerned. And Joan\u2019s way of showing concern, or at least channeling her worry, is to get angry. So, Calamity talked to her and tried to calm the other woman down. It didn\u2019t go so well. Joan was keen on holding onto that anger. Calamity even offered to spar with Joan, but our lady in white\u2019s concern about that was that she would do permanent injury to whoever she sparred with. I can understand that. After talking to Twitch about Rook, sparring with me would likely have been a bad idea. I was not in a \u201cgood place,\u201d so to speak, after that conversation and would have likely gone too far in fighting someone. I\u2019ve had some time to cool off since then, but right after the conversation I wanted to beat Twitch until he stopped moving and take out the rest of my anger on Darke. I suppose that despite what Rook had done to me I still didn\u2019t want anyone else hurting him.<br /> <br /> After the bit about Joan, Calamity told us about the situation with White Maria and Dark Kimberly. Apparently Maria sent Kimberly a very ornate dagger as a \u201cpresent.\u201d The implication being that the girl should kill herself in a bid to regain her lost honor. Well, Dark Kimberly didn\u2019t want to die, so she sent the dagger back to Maria. No note. Just the dagger back to the sender. The meaning was clear enough.<br /> <br /> I guess a part of me can understand why White Maria wants the other girl to die. Truth be told though, there are far worse things in this world than death. And making someone work towards making up for their sins and living with the guilt of them is certainly the harder task. I know what it is to live with guilt and to try my best to make up for past crimes. Death would be the easy way out. I don\u2019t think White Maria is thinking very clearly when she considers her old friend though. Her anger still runs hot and she just wants the other girl to die. I personally think that she\u2019d regret it if she was the cause of Kimberly\u2019s death. White Maria is not so cold as to kill someone, especially a friend, and walk away unscathed. Once the anger wears off or wanes a bit maybe she will display a little more restraint in her reactions towards her former friend.<br /> <br /> I could tell that Calamity was upset by all of this and so could Austin. And while I was trying to think of a way to lighten my friend\u2019s mood, Austin solved the problem himself. He decided to give Calamity an impromptu shoulder rub and within minutes had Calamity \u201cmelting into a puddle.\u201d I will admit that I was a little jealous at Austin\u2019s ease at helping a friend. I\u2019m just not good at coming up with comforting words in the moment. I think of things to say after the fact, but at the time I usually just draw a blank. Times like that make me hope that the others don\u2019t think that I\u2019m being too cold, or that I don\u2019t care. I do. I care for my motley rather more than I thought I would when I first met them. At the time I wondered what I\u2019d been thinking to make a pledge with a group of strangers. To promise to do no harm to them when I wasn\u2019t sure that they would not try to hurt me. Looking back, I\u2019m glad that I came to this place and got involved with this ragtag group. In a very short time they have accepted me for who I am and what I was, and I am grateful to have fallen in with such an understanding crowd.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> This morning seemed to come really fast. I got up and made my usual pot of coffee, while Gawain made breakfast. Though this morning he decided to do something different for our morning fare and made steak. This was perfectly okay in my book. I\u2019ll admit that having eggs so often took a bit of getting used to. I ate a lot of rabbit and venison in the Lady\u2019s realm, but not a lot of eggs, or chicken for that matter. So the steak was kind of familiar in a way.<br /> <br /> Our morning conversation was more serious than usual. Once Flores, who spent the night with Lori, made her \u201chellos,\u201d we talked about other issues that need attention. One in particular: Chalcedony. Gawain brought her up since he had removed the trigger in Desiree and wanted to see about helping out Chalcedony. She has been stalking Desiree lately, so there has been some concern as to what is driving this behavior. Insincere Marguerite offered to go and take a look around Chalcedony\u2019s place and see if anything suspicious came up, or if there was anything to give a clue to her current behavior.<br /> <br /> During this whole conversation it seemed that people were taking turns sitting in Lori\u2019s lap. It started out with the ladies. Gawain was invited, but he changed it up and plopped Lori down in his lap. Then she kind of winked at me and asked if I wanted to sit in her lap too. I\u2019m not sure why, but I said \u201csure.\u201d Lorelei was being playful and I decided in that moment to be playful back. It was a spur of the moment thing but makes me think when I look back on my actions. No one said anything, though Lori may have had a flash of surprise on her face as I stood up to walk over. I haven\u2019t really done much that could be described as \u201cplayful\u201d in a long time so this tiny little incident kind of stood out in my brain. I was more lighthearted in the Lady\u2019s service and liked to play little jokes. A lot of my jokes were kind of cruel, so I don\u2019t want to go back to that, but I wouldn\u2019t mind regaining something of my sense of humor. That may just be something that I have to wait for it to come back on its own.<br /> <br /> Anyhoo, Insincere Marguerite and Calamity went to go check out Chalcedony\u2019s apartment. Calamity waited outside on her bike just in case there was trouble while Marguerite snuck in. The whole place is very blue, but we knew that already. Doesn\u2019t make it not strange, but we were at least expecting that. What was unexpected was the presence of chloroform in the apartment. There wasn\u2019t a lot of it, but any quantity is cause for concern. Why would Chalcedony need to be able to knock someone out? I\u2019m not sure what else it can be used for, so it\u2019s not like there is likely to be a perfectly innocent reason for its presence. Other than that though, there was nothing suspicious in the place, or anything really that gave an insight into the other girl\u2019s behavior. Chalcedony was even there while Insincere Marguerite was sneaking around, which just goes to illustrate how good our little Darkling is at stealth, and acted completely normal.<br /> <br /> After the ladies got back from spying on Chalcedony, Gawain called the girl in question to check up on her. He explained that he had managed to dismantle the switch that was in Desiree and offered his services to get rid of the one in Chalcedony. The interesting thing is, she didn\u2019t readily jump at the opportunity to get rid of it. She, according to Gawain, was acting a bit cagey and seemed much more concerned with what Desiree was up to rather than getting help for herself. Gawain asked questions but Chalcedony said that there was only so much she could say without breaking a pledge. That in and of itself was kind of suspect. What kind of pledge did she take? What specifically can\u2019t she talk about? She tried to reassure Gawain that she was not in danger, but I\u2019m not sure our resident knight completely believed her. I\u2019m not sure that I completely believe her.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> I have spent most of the day working on my act. Julia eventually left with Lorelei and Calamity to do research, and did not turn up until nearly showtime. De La Rocha watched me work some in her place, I suppose; she was less distracting\u2026until Flores showed then they vanished for awhile. Turns out they went to dinner. Flores is apparently worried about De La Rocha and Oleander\u2019s friendship. So I worked on \u201cNon, Je Ne Regrette Rien\u201d alone for a bit.<br /> <br /> All returned in time for the show which went well. Joan was there and\u2026down\u2026 apparently Andromeda is having issues. I was going to speak to White Maria when Flores and De La Rocha started telling me that I needed to take care playing too fast and loose with seducing people regardless of race, as while mixing with whites or blacks was not unusual, the Asian and Latin Changelings rarely mixed with each other, and their lovers also tended to segregate somewhat. That is crazy. I thought I left such racist bullshit behind in France. For now I acquiesced (De La Rocha was what could be best called \u201cJittery\u201d and worst called \u201cIn the mood to punch someone in the face till the hurting stops\u201d) and simply enjoyed the time with the ladies. I was more intent on Flores time anyway, and Flores was eager for attention.<br /> <br /> When Lorelei joined us, she and Flores paired off quickly. I mean, they did not leave the table, but they barely noticed Gawain joining us. We teased him a little and had fun. I admit my opinion of Gawain has risen. He has been genuinely fun hanging out with us of late. It was odd how quickly Lori ended up with Flores in her lap. She had never shown an aversion to Flores per se, but her interest had been rather limited. Maybe De La Rocha said good things.<br /> <br /> To the surprise of no one, we five headed upstairs. The night was fun. With Lori there, De La Rocha did not try any \u201cbreath control\u201d with Flores, which frankly I was happy about. I am not comfortable with anyone\u2019s hands on anyone\u2019s throat. Julia had dallied with Lori earlier, and I made haste putting my scent back on her. In the end, the all smelled like me. My pretty, pretty ladies.<br /> <br /> I was, I am, happy.<br /> <br /> \u201cSex Breakfast\u201d was the usual flirting, and as always Flores added to it. She is both innocent and is neck and neck with Lorelei for most sexually minded woman I know. Dirty minded does not sound quite right. We had steak and potatoes for breakfast. No fruit. Americans are a strange lot.<br /> <br /> Afterwards De La Rocha went to work, while Julia went to work on her portrait of Flores, who went to pose. The rest of us discussed some concerns of Gawain and Calamity.<br /> <br /> The concern was about Chalcedony because of comments to Gawain while he was talking to Desiree. Chalcedony was watching Desiree, apparently, so we had concerns\u2026she also had the programming. Had it kicked in? Was she a loyalist who was observing Desiree for programming related issues? Gawain wanted to speak to her, but I advised having me search her house first, see what we were getting into. Both Gawain and Calamity knew where her house was, and Gawain agreed fairly easily. Calamity gave me a ride.<br /> <br /> The house, it was\u2026blue.<br /> <br /> I mean everything blue. The house, the walls, the furniture, even the light diffused though blue bowls that fit around the bulbs. It gave her home an unearthly feel on the inside, and her bluish skin, hair, and eyes looked eerie, and beautiful, bathed in the blue light. I wanted run my tongue along her smooth, blue legs, but I regained myself and searched. I found little incriminating, beyond a sleeping drug of the chloroform type. I mean she had mace and a taser, but that is not unusual for a beautiful single woman. I withdrew, she none the wiser.<br /> <br /> I reported to the others and expressed my concerns\u2026the house it was so blue I don\u2019t see it as being a good sign with her Clarity, and am wary of the sleeping cloth. I know why I have it so\u2026I am thus wary of the sleeping cloth.<br /> <br /> Gawain called her, and she said a lot of vague stuff about being busy and having to deal with favors. She wanted it removed, but not immediately. It was a little concerning, but not definite. We will have to decide what to do.<br /> <br /> Lori goes off with Monica soon, and we must prepare for movie night. We might be doing it over two nights, we shall see. I think we should buckle down for one but, eh, who knows. Or maybe they will need I to watch Chalcedony. We will see, won\u2019t we?<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXXVII</i><br /> <br /> Not much to add. There was research going on but Lori is\u2026well, the polite way would be to say she is not the research type, and got a lot of help from Julia.<br /> <br /> Most of the rest of the scenes were pure roleplaying. Some empathy rolls and such while talking to people during the show, and Insincere Marguerite easily owned the Stealth and Larceny rolls to investigate Chalcedony. She used Shadowpatch and Nevertread, since she pretty much always meets the catch for them, of course.<br /> <br /> About built up to the time jump, and folks are on the cusp of Wyrd 5. But still in normal time as we start next session. We will see you then. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T23:58:24-07:00","id":678597,"title":"","content":"The tangle of limbs in Lori's diary reminded me of a Rat King.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T13:00:11-07:00","id":679278,"title":"","content":"Ah, enjoying Shadowrun: Hong Kong omenseer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T19:40:42-07:00","id":679558,"title":"","content":"Very much so thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T00:44:09-07:00","id":680738,"title":"","content":"One more session before we jump ahead about two weeks, this had people rather busily dealing with new drama from Joan and movies by decade. Let\u2019s get caught up.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXXIX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> July 1st late morning<br /> <br /> Well, movies by the decade was super awesome. Super long, but super awesome. We wound up watching all 5 movies last night. And everyone had a good time. Well, you know, mostly. Nobody had a bad time, for sure.<br /> <br /> The rest of the day was kinda a bummer though. Insincere Marguerite shadowed Chalcedony like I, you know, asked her to. Calamity had set all kinds of rules like checking in and timing and stuff that I hadn\u2019t wanted to think about. It sounded like she didn\u2019t find much. Chalcedony went out to dinner with some mortal friends, spent a lot of time around the house and ended the day at the Rose and Thorn. Desiree was there too, but I guess nothing big happened there.<br /> <br /> Lori had been out in the Hedge with Monica and just before she came back, Joan showed up at the Dream House looking for her. Calamity said it well after, that Joan was angry like the sun was hot. Not at Lori, though Calamity was a little worried she was gonna take a swing. Anyways though, she apparently \u2018requested\u2019 a meeting with the Monarchs and by requested, she meant, you know, she threatened them. But she wanted Lori to speak on her behalf at the meeting. She\u2019s a really good impassioned speaker, but right now all her passion is, you know, focused on destroying anything and everything threatening her love. And since that\u2019s not really a viable target, she mostly just wants to destroy everything. The meeting is this afternoon. I\u2019m sure Lori will be able to convince them and promise not to ask Andromeda to use the Table again. You know, without threatening to destroy them if they do.<br /> <br /> But first there was movies. Lori picked Jaws for the 70s. De la Roche and Calamity got really into it, you know, encouraging everyone to punch the shark whenever it showed up. Calamity \u2018s pick for the 80s was Ferris Bueller\u2019s Day Off. Julia was very convinced that Ferris was, you know, a figment of Cameron\u2019s imagination. The Crow is what I picked for the 90s and Insincere Marguerite chose The Craft. I think the 90s won, definitely. The 00s was close too - Jacob picked The Dark Knight. Lori pegged it as Batman just by the name, but we did, you know, warn her it wasn\u2019t, like, Adam West Batman or anything.<br /> <br /> Julia got really really turned on by the last three, so she pulled the rest of her quartet aside right after. Luna was... a little confused? uncomfortable? I dunno, by that, but we chilled out and talked some, Calamity and me, and Jacob and Luna. Calamity was a little nostalgic, in a good way, she promised, cause of The Crow. I was super worried I\u2019d fucked up, cause she started rubbing her blood sister scar and looking all thoughtful. But she said it was good memories only - the last time she and Anastasia hung out was to go see The Crow at the mall. She had a strip of those photo booth pictures of the 2 of them. They looked pretty adorable.<br /> <br /> I did get a little bummed out, with the talking about how memories were all we really had, you know? Not super bummed though - it\u2019s hard to be sad when somebody as beautiful as Calamity loves you. It was 6 or so by the time movies were done. We haven\u2019t gotten a whole lot of sleeping done since, but Lori\u2019ll pick us up, I\u2019m sure.<br /> <br /> July 1st afternoon<br /> <br /> And all is, well, ok at least. I hate to see Joan hurting so much, but it did have an effect on the monarchs. Between that and Lori being amazing, there wasn\u2019t any talk of repercussions for Joan\u2019s threats. I\u2019d been pretty sure Queen Charlotte, at least, was gonna try, at the beginning.<br /> <br /> Captain Jack showed up at breakfast to coach Lori and brainstorm ideas. Lori was grateful enough to give him a big kiss, so Captain Jack had to break the bad news. Generally though, we had a good plan and a hopeful outlook. The plan was to emphasize the, you know, pain Joan and Andromeda were in and how dangerous a tool the table was.<br /> <br /> Joan was not so hopeful, mostly just still wound tight. She made Lori and even De la Roche a little nervous. I stuck close, trying to keep her spirits up as best I could. When Lori started talking about what Andromeda was going through, she broke down, bursting into tears. I put an arm around her and De la Roche took her hand. Everyone else was pretty shocked. Princess Jolie was particularly moved and insisted that the Pledge be to never use the Table, not just to not make Andromeda use it. She had to negotiate with the other, but pushed it through.<br /> <br /> So it\u2019s worked out and all for the best, I think. Joan went right back to Andromeda. She promised to let us know when she felt good enough for visitors. Now if we can just help Chalcedony out, maybe we\u2019ll have some time to relax.<br /> <br /> --------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Lord Bertilak shook with hearty laughter at the slight man\u2019s joke. He slapped Gawain on the back. \u201cWell said, man, well said.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s not what she thought.\u201d He winked at the lord.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhere did you learn these tales? You must be a well traveled man.\u201d Bertilak spared a moment\u2019s thought to his lady-wife. She would have a hard time drawing this one in.<br /> <br /> Gawain paused. He ran his fingers through his spiked hair. \u201cI... California? It\u2019s the strangest thing. It\u2019s like it\u2019s from a different life. I...\u201d He shook his head. \u201cI was called Greg, Greg Andrews. And lived in San Francisco, California, with my partner Alex.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCal - if - ornia? That is no where I have heard of. It certainly does sound strange. A dream, perhaps?\u201d Lord Bertilak gestured at Gawain with an eating knife.<br /> <br /> Gawain smiled. \u201cPerhaps.\u201d<br /> <br /> Lord Bertilak roared for the next course. He rather hoped this one would stay strong against temptation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Calamity shook Gawain\u2019s shoulders, then moved with a practiced quickness aside as he sat bolt upright. He stared forward, chest heaving. She laid a hand on his shoulder gingerly. \u201cYou ok, handsome?\u201d<br /> <br /> He turned to her, eyes wide, still breathing heavily. \u201cI... I remember. One of the Gawains, I remember. He was... California. Greg Andrews. He didn\u2019t kiss my wife, but he did miss me and called it a trade so I...\u201d Gawain looked a little sick.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt wasn\u2019t you, big guy, it\u2019s not your fault.\u201d Calamity put her arms around him and leaned up against his back.<br /> <br /> \u201cBut I remember him. His name, where he\u2019s from, what he looks like. A little like Jacob, actually, short hair, thin. A little shorter. And not quite so... Russian?\u201d He paused. \u201cAnd... I don't think it was too long ago. He talked about a black guy getting elected President, again.\u201d He turned around to look at Calamity. \u201cMaybe I could try to find him. See if...\u201d<br /> <br /> Calamity put a hand over his. \u201cAnd see that he\u2019s alright.\u201d<br /> <br /> A hopeful half smile crept up the big man\u2019s face.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> My theme for today\u2019s entry: matters of the heart are complicated, and can cause unforeseen problems even if you take the utmost care at every step along the way. Or, to use Calamity\u2019s phrasing, \u201cLove makes you stupid.\u201d<br /> <br /> So Marguerite continued to watch Chalcedony yesterday afternoon, while the rest of the motley split off into sparring groups and I headed out to meet Monica for our Hedge date. She greeted me with a smile when I arrived, and ushered me toward one of the better known local gates. Just before we entered the Hedge itself, she gently but firmly put her hands on my shoulders.<br /> <br /> \u201cI need to tell you something, Lori,\u201d she said softly, \u201cand I need you to listen, and I need you to promise that you\u2019ll take this seriously, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> I agreed, and she sort of sighed and turned away from me. \u201cI need you to promise that if I tell you to run at any point while we\u2019re in the Hedge, you\u2019ll do it. You\u2019ll head straight back here, and you won\u2019t stop until you\u2019re back in the world. And if you see me again before you get here, you\u2019ll keep running, no matter what I say. Agreed?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAgreed,\u201d I said seriously. I know from D that Monica used to have a problem with\u2026 well\u2026 eating people. Apparently those cravings haven\u2019t entirely dissipated. While this knowledge was alarming to say the least, I know that it\u2019s been a long time since she lost control. We all have to overcome the things Arcadia did to us. D trusts her, and that\u2019s good enough for me.<br /> <br /> The patrol itself was pretty routine, from what Monica tells me. We didn\u2019t come across any unusual creatures or strange tricks of the landscape, and Monica was able to teach me loads about how to navigate through the thorns, and what sorts of obstacles I might expect to encounter there. It was actually kind of fun, and the thorns are kind of beautiful in a stark, wild sort of way.<br /> <br /> It wasn\u2019t long before we were talking about our respective romantic difficulties. Monica is looking for a way to let Haley down easy; to disentangle herself from that relationship without hurting the fragile alien girl. She says that she enjoys hanging out with Haley, and that the sex is good, but she\u2019s not in love with her, and doesn\u2019t think she <u><u>can</u></u> be in love with another woman like that. Since Haley is obviously devoted to her, and sort of delicate emotionally, this poses a problem. I tried to offer the best advice I could, but in the end I had to content myself with providing a sympathetic ear and commiserating for the most part.<br /> <br /> Then talk turned to <u><u>my</u></u> romantic situation. Of course we had a bit to talk about, as Monica is one of D\u2019s closest friends and knows her as well as anyone in town. Monica is a teensy bit jealous of all the time D and I have been spending together, but she insists it\u2019s not a big deal. I confessed that I knew I\u2019d been monopolizing her time, but what can you do? When you love someone, you just want to spend all of your time with them. I suggested that the three of us should hang out more, like we did the other day at Muscle Beach. Monica seemed to like that idea.<br /> <br /> Then she started telling me how much D had changed since she met me. I knew that my honey had mellowed a bit, but to hear Monica talk she used to be like a completely different person. \u201cShe used to go out every Saturday night and pick fights in bars,\u201d she told me at one point.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, I know,\u201d I said, \u201cwe did it together last week. It was a little strange, but fun in a weird way,\u201d I admitted.<br /> <br /> Monica raised an eyebrow. \u201cHow many people did she send home with massive dental bills?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> I stopped. \u201cNone,\u201d I said in shock. \u201cSome cuts and bruises, and maybe one broken nose, but nothing like that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSee,\u201d Monica said with a huge smile, \u201cshe\u2019s calmed down a lot since she met you. I think you\u2019re really <u><u>good</u></u> for her, Lori.\u201d So <u><u>that</u></u> gave me some food for thought.<br /> <br /> The rest of the jaunt was pretty uneventful, but I think I picked up some useful tips about navigating the Hedge, and generally had a good time hanging out with Monica. She dropped me off back at the Dream House a few hours later with a friendly wave and a promise that she\u2019d be in touch about hanging out some more in the near future. So it was with high spirits that I glided into the parlor and called out that I was home.<br /> <br /> My good mood popped like a balloon when I saw what was waiting for me. Joan had dropped by, and she was so tense that I could almost feel her anger like waves of heat rising from her. Calamity caught me before I approached and told me that Joan was there to speak with me\u2026 in fact to ask me for a favor. I approached with caution and stammered out a greeting.<br /> <br /> \u201cLorelei,\u201d she said, rising and taking my hand. I could feel the tension through her fingers. \u201cI need a favor,\u201d she almost growled.<br /> <br /> \u201cName it,\u201d I said.<br /> <br /> \u201cI have called a meeting of the monarchs tomorrow,\u201d she continued. \u201cIn fact, I <u><u>demanded</u></u> the meeting. I told them that they would speak with me or they would\u2026 suffer the consequences. At this meeting, I intend to insist that Andromeda <u><u>never</u></u> be required to operate the Table again. If they do not agree to my terms, I will kill them all.\u201d She looked away for a moment. \u201cI had hoped\u2026 that is, I believe they might take this better coming from you, if you will speak for me.\u201d<br /> <br /> I took her hand in both of mine. \u201cOf course I will, Joan,\u201d I promised fervently. \u201cI know how much I owe the two of you\u2026 but even if that wasn\u2019t the case, you\u2019re friends. Of course I\u2019ll help however I can.\u201d<br /> <br /> Joan squeezed my hands, and I did my best not to wince. \u201cI thank you,\u201d she said tersely. \u201cThe meeting will be held tomorrow afternoon at the headquarters of the Summer Court. I trust you will convey the seriousness of my demands\u2026 and of the consequences if they are ignored.\u201d She turned to go.<br /> <br /> \u201cJoan,\u201d I said before she left. \u201cDon\u2019t worry about this. I promise I\u2019ll take care of it. Everything will be fine. Just concentrate on being there for Andromeda. She needs you now.\u201d<br /> <br /> Joan nodded, and to my shock I saw the shimmer of tears in her eyes. She left without another word.<br /> <br /> Then the panic hit. \u201cShit,\u201d I muttered, collapsing into a chair. \u201cWhat the hell am I going to do? What the hell am I going to <u><u>say</u></u>? Joan threatens death to four of the most powerful people in the Freehold, and she wants me to make it right and convince them to do what she wants? Shit!\u201d<br /> <br /> So the great movie night battle of the decades started out with a bit more stress than I\u2019d hoped. I tried to alleviate some of the stress with my old friend Jack Daniels, and it seemed to work for the most part. At least, I was able to lose myself in the films and forget my troubles for a while. I resolved to try to enjoy myself, stay up all night with my friends, and use my Contracts to pep myself up the next morning.<br /> <br /> Okay, so maybe <u><u>Jaws</u></u> wasn\u2019t the best choice to represent the 70s cultural experience, but I still thought it was pretty indicative of trends and the social mindset of the day. And I really didn\u2019t want to go with <u><u>Saturday Night Fever</u></u>. I\u2019ve noticed that people these days seem to think the entirety of the 1970s can be summed up with disco culture, but that\u2019s not the case at all; disco didn\u2019t really even gain that much popularity until the decade\u2019s fading years. <u><u>Jaws</u></u> had the decade\u2019s sense of building tension, as though we were on the verge of something big. It was the beginning of the \u201cevent\u201d movie; that genre in which the film itself was more important than the things it depicted. And it depicted a nation betrayed by its government (in that the town refused to close the beaches despite the danger to the tourists), which we all felt in the wake of Watergate.<br /> <br /> Plus, it\u2019s a hell of a lot of fun to watch. D got really into it, and I think most of the others enjoyed it too.<br /> <br /> Next up was the 80s. Calamity\u2019s pick for that decade was called <u><u>Ferris Bueller\u2019s Day Off</u>,</u> and it was about the adventures of three teens who decide to play hooky from school. Everything that can go wrong does, but they seem to have a good time regardless. For a film from the 1980s, however, most of its music seemed to be from the 1960s\u2026 which at least meant I knew what it was. Wayne Newton and the Beatles\u2026 what a spread!<br /> <br /> Julia got off on a tangent at some point, expounding upon her theory that the movie was meant to be symbolic. She apparently thinks that everything that happens on the screen is actually happening inside of the imagination of Cameron, one of the main characters. It\u2019s\u2026 an interesting theory, but Julia\u2019s tenacious defense of this interpretation was a little off-putting. She seemed unable to accept the idea that other theories were even possible.<br /> <br /> She also compared it to another film called <u><u>Fight Club</u></u>, but when I asked about it I was told that \u201cwe don\u2019t talk about <u><u>Fight Club</u></u>.\u201d Apparently it\u2019s a rule.<br /> <br /> Next up was <u><u>The Crow</u></u>, Gawain\u2019s pick to represent the early 90s. It was a fun if bleak tale about a murdered man who comes back from the other side to take revenge upon the people who killed him. The main character was played by Brandon Lee \u2013 son of the legendary Bruce Lee \u2013 and he was quite good in the role (despite being hindered by some overly melodramatic dialog). Unfortunately, I\u2019m told he died while making the film\u2026 someone fired a gun which had been loaded with improperly neutralized ammunition.<br /> <br /> The film also starred Michael Wincott as the villain\u2026 I remembered him from that <u><u>Robin Hood</u></u> film we watched. Who could forget that sexy growl of his?<br /> <br /> Marguerite\u2019s pick to represent the late 90s was called <u><u>The Craft</u></u>. Out of all the films we watched, that one probably impressed me the least. Marguerite herself explained that she chose it not for its quality but because it was very representative of filmmaking in the late 90s. The story involved a number of teenage girls who get into witchcraft, discover that they have real power, and let it go to their heads.<br /> <br /> Jacob\u2019s contribution to represent the 2000s was <u><u>The Dark Knight</u>.</u> When I perked up at this title and asked if it was a Batman film, people looked at me kind of strangely. Jacob nodded, but cautioned me that it was nothing like the old Adam West TV show. I was almost insulted at that\u2026 my favorite Batman stories were always the darker ones when I was growing up. I particularly liked the stories involving Ra\u2019s al-Ghul, who I understand appears in the film which preceded the one we watched last night.<br /> <br /> The film was amazing. It looks like the head honchos in Hollywood finally figured out that the dark knight should be\u2026 well, <u><u>dark</u></u>. The main villain in the film was the Joker, who was played to insane psychotic perfection by a man named Heath Ledger (who <u><u>also</u></u> died shortly after the completion of this film\u2026 what is this, a trend?). The highlight of the film for me was an elaborate deathtrap wherein the Joker took two barges full of people \u2013 one full of convicts and the other loaded with civilians \u2013 and gave each the power of life and death over the other. He was attempting to prove something about the basic bestial nature of humanity. I can\u2019t tell you how it felt to witness the resolution of that scene\u2026 where the worst elements of humanity demonstrate just how wrong the Joker is.<br /> <br /> Anyway, by the time this cinematic extravaganza was over, it was after six in the morning. The last 6-plus hours of moody gothic goodness had put Julia in the mood for love, and she was pretty insistent that Marguerite, D and I should join her in Marguerite\u2019s room. So I lost another couple of hours that I should have been using to prepare Joan\u2019s case for the monarchs\u2026 not that I\u2019m complaining.<br /> <br /> By the time we all staggered down to sex breakfast \u2013 a little earlier than usual \u2013 I was frantically going over everything I knew about the monarchs, Joan, Andromeda, and the Table in my head, desperately trying to figure out what I was going to say to fix this shit-storm and save my friends from the mess I\u2019d inadvertently landed them in. I guess the others could tell I was pretty tense, because aside from stopping by briefly to offer me small morsels of food, they pretty much left me alone.<br /> <br /> And then, sweet salvation! Captain Jack stopped by to offer his advice on how to present Joan\u2019s case. I was so stressed and grateful and overwhelmed that I just walked up to him, threw my arms around him, and kissed him on the mouth\u2026 possibly with tears in my eyes. He returned my embrace, grinned, winked, and said \u201csorry, sweetie, but I\u2019ve got some bad news for you\u2026\u201d which actually made me laugh.<br /> <br /> With the tension broken, we got to discussing strategy. Jack proposed (and I agreed) that it would be best to try to sell the monarchs on the point of Joan\u2019s emotional trauma and the damage the Table had done to Andromeda. These are personal, tangible consequences for most of the monarchs, and it shouldn\u2019t be too difficult to demonstrate that the gains will no longer be worth the cost of we persist in using the Table. Jack also suggested that we push early for a pledge that the Table never be used again for any reason\u2026 mostly so that we could fall back to the less hardline condition that <u><u>Andromeda</u></u> never be required to use the Table again if negotiations went against us.<br /> <br /> I felt a little better after discussing the issue with the rest of the Motley. Some of us had spoken with our respective monarchs following Joan\u2019s visit, and the news was largely good. I\u2019d talked to Jolie myself, of course, and while she was grateful for what Andromeda had done for her with the Table, she worried that the use of the Fae artifact might represent a slippery slope in the future. Jack was pretty sure that Boss Lowjack and Viscount Augustine would adopt similar positions, which left only Queen Charlotte. According to Calamity, Charlotte was <u><u>not</u></u> happy that Joan had threatened Princess Jolie, and was eager to see her pay for her audacity. So there was my biggest hurdle.<br /> <br /> By the end of breakfast, it was almost time for us to head to the meeting, and I had developed a game plan. I was nervous as hell, but all in all I felt pretty good about our chances. I got dolled up in a sober set of church clothes, but didn\u2019t go with the ponytail or reading glasses. Everyone in the Freehold knows me pretty well by sight, and to put on my librarian disguise might have come across as dishonest.<br /> <br /> Joan met us at the church as she had promised. She was obviously still very agitated, but was managing to hide it better. She soberly thanked me for helping her, and I put what I hoped was a comforting hand on her shoulder. \u201cJoan,\u201d I said quietly, \u201cI promise I\u2019ll do everything I can to help you. Try not to worry, okay? But some of the monarchs are angry with you, and in order to minimize the consequences, I might have to show them just how much Andromeda\u2019s situation has hurt you. I just want you to know that I\u2019m not trying to embarrass you. Everything I say or do is to help Andromeda. Okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded curtly, thanked me again, and took her seat. Most of the motley chose to sit next to her, to show support and solidarity. D looked at me and raised an eyebrow in question, and I did something selfish. \u201cI\u2019m sorry,\u201d I whispered to her with a little bit of panic in my voice, \u201cI know she\u2019s your friend and she\u2019s hurting and she probably needs you right now, but can you stay with me please? I don\u2019t want to do this alone.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cGive me a minute to explain it to her,\u201d she said. I saw her whispering something to Joan. Joan looked at me, nodded, and gave her a friendly pat on the shoulder. A few seconds later D was seated next to me, holding my hand, and things were a little better. Jack settled in on the other side of me, ready to help if I needed him.<br /> <br /> The meeting was called to order, the situation was reiterated for the sake of clarity, and I was called to speak on Joan\u2019s behalf. I allowed a trickle of glamour to flow through me, to enhance my natural talents and put me more at ease, but I swear I didn\u2019t activate any Contracts or do anything overtly magical. The situation was too serious for that. While Joan and Andromeda certainly deserved the best representation I could give them, to use magic would have been tantamount to admitting that their case could only be argued effectively through trickery.<br /> <br /> I started off by explaining why Joan had acted in the way she did. I put it in terms which I thought would particularly move Queen Charlotte\u2026 describing how afraid and angry one can feel when the person they love more than anyone else is threatened or hurt by circumstances. I then went on to describe exactly how Andromeda had been affected by the use of the Table\u2026 how she had lost part of herself, and how we couldn\u2019t know if she would ever truly be whole again. \u201cCan any of you say you wouldn\u2019t do the same to protect the one you love?\u201d I asked earnestly.<br /> <br /> Murmurs spread through those gathered. Joan was crying. No one had ever seen that before.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019s recovering,\u201d I reassured the monarchs, \u201cand we have every hope that she will come back to us fully in time. But only if she\u2019s never again required to operate that God-forsaken relic of Arcadia,\u201d I finished strongly. They were hooked. I saw it in their eyes. Viscount Augustine was even nodding in agreement. So I pushed my advantage.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd if it\u2019s that dangerous for Andromeda to use it,\u201d I said, \u201chow can we force <u><u>any</u></u> member of the Freehold to take on that same risk? Even if another operator could be found, how can we ask another changeling to put their hard-earned soul on the line, no matter what the potential gains might be? Master Darke and Mr. Grey thought they were using the Table for the good of the Freehold. No one is disputing that. And since the Table was recovered by the monarchs, we\u2019ve used it with the same justification! How can we claim moral superiority under those circumstances? No, the Table is too dangerous to use. Keep it if you must. Study it if you think you\u2019ll learn something valuable. But <u><u>don\u2019t</u></u> use it again\u2026 not even if it seems like the good it can do outweighs the negative consequences.\u201d<br /> <br /> The church got quiet, and I realized that everyone was still staring at me. For once, the attention didn\u2019t send inappropriate tingles through my body. \u201cThat\u2019s\u2026 all I have to say,\u201d I muttered quietly into the silence. \u201cThank you for your time, Your Majesties.\u201d<br /> <br /> I sat down primly, and then sort of collapsed into the uncomfortable pew. D threw an arm around my shoulder and whispered into my ear. \u201cMagnificent,\u201d she said, \u201cyou were fucking <u><u>amazing</u></u>, babe!\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled at her. \u201cI just hope it was enough,\u201d I said uncertainly.<br /> <br /> It was. The monarchs agreed almost immediately to make a Pledge never to use the Table again, for any reason. Madame Spidertoes and Austin agreed to craft the Pledge, and a few minutes later it was all over. Even Queen Charlotte conceded that Joan\u2019s hasty actions of the previous day were understandable in light of the situation, and no action against her is being contemplated.<br /> <br /> Joan approached me as we walked out of the church. \u201cLorelei,\u201d she said quietly, \u201cI have no words to express my appreciation. Thank you.\u201d She gave me a handshake that could easily have snapped several bones.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m happy I was able to help,\u201d I replied. \u201cIf you ever need me for something like this again, I hope you know that all you have to do is ask.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cAnd if you or your motley ever find yourself in need\u2026 my sword is ever at your disposal,\u201d she replied.<br /> <br /> I smiled. \u201cThank you. But right now, I think you\u2019re needed more elsewhere. Go home. Hang up your sword for the day, and make sure your love is all right. That\u2019s what all this was for, after all.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded gratefully, said her goodbyes to D and the rest, and strode purposefully toward her car.<br /> <br /> The rest of us went back to the Dream House after that, and here we all are. And as hard as it is for me to believe, life goes on. I\u2019ve been writing in this journal for long enough. We have a show in a couple of hours, and I have to prepare.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T00:44:41-07:00","id":680739,"title":"","content":"<b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> It happened while I was meditating. I was alone in the dark, still and silent. I was trying to center myself and clear my mind, envisioning the darkness washing over me and sweeping everything away like an ocean wave in time with my breaths. Yeah, it sounds a little granola crazy but hell, it fucking works and that's all that matters. It just sweeps all the crap away and leaves my mind empty the same way a good fight does, but once the fight is over and my blood's stopped boiling the stress just picks right back up where it left off. With this, it comes back slower and I can actually consider it rationally as it does. See the shit that's fucked up inside me as a to do list rather than a condemnation. At least, that's the plan. Scary thing is that it actually works that way some days. Not all the time yet, but more than when I started and even on the bad days I think it's a little better. I mean, my shit's still fucked the hell up but it's not like I can trade this life in for a new one. I'm like a classic car, no matter how damaged it is it's never totaled right?<br /> <br /> So there I was, floating away on the black when I heard laughter. A girl's laughter. Too young to be anyone that works here and it was too early for them to be in anyway. I thought it might be a radio or a TV but it was at the same time to faint and too clear for that. The ghost had never made noise and she was older. This was a girl. Young. It wasn't a good laugh. It was cruel. It was the laughter of someone savoring someone else's suffering. It was high pitched, manic. It was familiar. I tried to think of where I knew it from and that's when I realized it was me. It wasn't that I was laughing and not aware or anything, it was in my head. It was a memory. Something I'd forgotten. Something I'd left behind.<br /> <br /> I felt it then in the glass. Like a thrumming that ran along the shards and down into my bones. The glass remembers that laugh. That was the day I thought I was going to die. That was the day Dick... no Robert... his real name was Robert... That was the laugh I laughed when I thought Robert was going to kill me.<br /> <br /> It was after I'd taken to creeping out at night. After I'd started to spy on the others. Dick was going steady with Suzy. But at night, when he thought no one was watching he met with one of the other girls. Betty was bookish and quiet and helped out in the library. At night she would meet up with Robert. He called her Lindsey. They spoke of love and staying strong and escaping together. They fucked a lot. It was desperate, forbidden, and furtive. They met as often as they could manage. They risked everything to steal a touch, a kiss, a soft word. I watched them.<br /> <br /> Even remembering things clearly again, I don't really know why I did it. I think it was just a whim, a moment of petulance. I might have done it just because I could. Because it was the only power I had in Snow Globe. But one night I told. I whispered into the shadows where the Voices waited, They waited in every shadow for someone to tell Them what They already knew so They could act on it. But I was clever. I remember how wickedly I grinned as I told Them that I had seen Betty using her old name and sneaking out to fornicate. I told Them everything. But I made sure to never let Dick's name slip out. I only told on her, not him.<br /> <br /> The next morning my ticket was waiting, crisp and fresh. I went to breakfast smiling and set it on the table as I ate. Mom and Dad and Dick all narrowed their eyes but they didn't say anything. I could see that Dick was indeed fine. I asked him to take me to the candy shop. And he couldn't really say no. I skipped along beside him, holding his hand and clutching my prize in the other like a good and happy little girl.<br /> <br /> And as we neared the store I saw her. I could tell right away she'd been visited. The Whispering Voices had punished her harshly. She was moving stiffly, limping and holding her arms close to cradle herself as she shuffled along. I stopped and hid the ticket behind my back, waiting and watching for her to look up. When she did... shit the thrill that shot through me was sick. I watched her eyes. Shock at seeing Dick, her beloved Robert, whole and hale and standing outside the candy shop. Shock gave way to hurt and betrayal on its way to hate. That's when Robert looked up at last and saw her. His surprise didn't help. It took him seconds to grasp what he was seeing, and in that time she spun and fled, throwing her books aside and shoving her way through the others on the street. Dick started to go after her, took a step before my grip on his hand and the sound of my laughter bubbling up reminded him of my presence.<br /> <br /> As he looked back I held up my ticket and my giggle bloomed into a full and proper laugh. His eyes went wide as it all fell into place. I laughed harder as his gaze turned dark, rage-filled and furious. His hand jerked free from mine and he clenched it into a fist so tight his knuckles turned white. I just kept laughing.<br /> <br /> Then he drew back that arm and wound up just like when he pitched one of his unhittable fastballs. He launched that fist at me with his whole body and it caught me square in the face. My vision went blurry and I spun and fell to the ground. Only one of my eyes would open and focus as he grabbed the collar of my dress and jerked me back up to my feet. My face was wet. I could taste blood. I blinked and looked up at him with my one good eye as he lifted me and drew the pitching arm back again. His knuckles had a speck of blood on them, my blood. His eyes were blazing with hate and his teeth were clenched so hard I half expected to hear them cracking.<br /> <br /> \u201cI got you.\u201d My voice was raspy and I coughed to clear my throat. \u201cI got you.\u201d Louder and clearer this time, with a smile on my face and pleasure in my eye. Then the giggling and laughter flowed back up. I couldn't help it and I didn't want to.<br /> <br /> He shook me and he screamed. A crowd was gathering but no one moved to intervene. No one moved to stop him. I just kept laughing as he held me there like that. For a long few seconds I just dangled from his grip while everyone watched and waited. Then he screamed and swung. Once he started, he just kept hitting me, beating me until his knuckles were raw and bloody. I never tried to defend myself. I just kept laughing.<br /> <br /> When I fell and didn't get back up he switched over from fists to feet. I was choking and shuddering, his fists had driven the air out of my gut and I couldn't manage to replace it because I couldn't stop laughing. Though it wasn't really laughing any more, it was a raspy wheezing. Tears welled up and ran down my face to mix with the blood. It was wet and cold. Whenever he hesitated for a moment and I could suck in a breath my manic giggles would resume and he would snarl and kick me again.<br /> <br /> I knew he wasn't going to stop until I was dead but it didn't matter. He wouldn't change what I'd done. Nothing could. I'd broken something and not all the King's horses and all the King's men could fix it again. I was going to die but I just kept laughing, wet horrible laughter mixed with splatters of frothy blood as my weak little body gave way to his fury. I heard things break, felt the sharpness of tearing inside as his foot connected over and over. Then suddenly, the crowd moved in. I don't know why they did, but hey pulled him off before he could finish me. They took him away, took him home.<br /> <br /> No one helped me up as they took him away. No one spared me more than a brief glance to see if I was still moving, still wheezing and coughing up blood as I tried to laugh. They just left me there, broken and alone in the street. I closed my eye and let the darkness wash over me.<br /> <br /> The next thing I knew I was inside the shop. I guess the old man and gathered me up and carried me inside. He cleaned me up gently with a damp cloth. The pain was intense but I was alive. It hurt to breathe and my lips stayed wet and red no matter how many times I dried them. He went into the back and brought out a candy I'd never seen. It was deep red and heart shaped. It was soft, like chocolate and had a thick crimson filling when I bit into it. It was bitter and sharp but sent a surge through me that burned away the pain and left me tingling in it's wake. When I finished it I could breathe again, though my side was still sore and bruised.<br /> <br /> He smiled at me, warm and kindly. He took my hand and walked me to the curtain that I'd never been allowed to go through before. He took me into the part of the shop where he kept the special candies. Brittle of broken dreams. Bittersweet tears of sorrow and loss. Red hot rages. Softly spun moans of pleasure and pain, woven together like pink and blue cotton candy. He let me gorge myself on all of it. Then he walked me to the door and told me that I could have more next time. That from now on I would be allowed into the special room because I was such a good girl. Then he sent me on my way.<br /> <br /> I didn't tell on Dick. I was too tired and too blissfully high on the candy to do anything but drift home and crawl into my bed that night. The next morning he was fine. No one had told on him. His eyes were hard and cold at breakfast and I just smiled at him. I think he came close to attacking me again, but he didn't. I never did tell on him for what he did and I don't think he was ever punished for it. Everyone saw it but none of them turned him in for trying to murder me. He didn't attack me again but he certainly never forgave me. His eyes spoke volumes whenever he looked at me. I didn't blame him for it but I never felt guilty. Not even after what happened to Lindsey.<br /> <br /> We never saw her again. There was a new Betty at school that day, fresh and bright and confused. No one ever spoke openly about the replacements, it was forbidden after all. But there were rumors, whispered in secret and under cover of night. They say she went home and killed herself. I had no way of knowing if it was true, but I can remember hoping it was. I certainly chose to believe it. I was weak but not helpless. I was clever enough to trick her into believing her precious Robert had betrayed her. I was miserable, but not as miserable as she had been. As Robert continued to be without her. I wasn't strong enough or clever enough to fight the Whispering Voices, to hurt Them or break anything They kept, but I could hurt the others. And after that, I did. The special candy was so very sweet and that it came from hurting the others only made it better at the time.<br /> <br /> Now I see things more clearly. They turned us against each other, rewarded us for distrust and rewarded us for keeping our fellow victims isolated and hurting and miserable. Malevolent indeed. I think it would be less terrible if there was truly some grand purpose behind it all but I don't really believe that anymore. There is no higher purpose to Snow Globe. It is nothing more than cruelty for its own sake. And it runs through my veins and coils around my bones now. But I know it's there. I understand it. I know what it wants from me.<br /> <br /> Guess it's a good thing I don't much like doing as I'm fucking told ain't it?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Greg Andrews. That's the name of at least one of the dreamers that got sucked into the Dream Lord's twisted little morality play. Gawain remembered his name last night. And based on the other details he recalled it seems the man was from California and remembered Obama's re-election.<br /> <br /> So he's thinking about looking for him. And by thinking about, he's girding his mental loins for what he's afraid he might find. I made sure he knew I was prepared to help. What he's recalled is all my contract of Oath and Punishment needs and I've made sure he knows I am ready to seek this guy out with him. I don't blame him in the least for needing some time to be ready. This is a huge deal. I know he sees them in his nightmares sometimes. I know he worries about those deaths. It was a dream, but a dream in Arcadia. So who the fuck knows if follows the rules or not. And well, this might be the point where we find out.<br /> <br /> I mean, maybe it was nothing but a passing nightmare for those guys? That would take so much weight off Handsome's shoulders to know that none of them suffered anything worse than a rough night. Of course, I don't believe it's going to be that easy. This is fucking Arcadia after all. I know Gawain thinks of himself as a killer already. So it would suck royally if it turned out to be true, but he's not completely unprepared for that possibility. At least he'd know and he could start trying to put it to rest and move forward rather than never being sure. And yeah, I know I should listen to that bit of sage advice myself but fuck it, I am not ready to face Stasia hating me yet. I know that some day I'm going to break down and seek her out. I know nothing good is likely to come of it but the not knowing is too much of a bitch. But that's for later.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I understand why he's building up to it and I am not going to push. When he's ready I will help him track the guy down and no matter how bad it might be, I'll be there at his side. We'll face it together and we'll deal with whatever we learn because we're in love and that's what you do when you love someone.<br /> <br /> Hell, maybe we'll even get a happy ending. Surely one of these damned fairy tales has one, right?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> So after the little peek into Chalcedony\u2019s apartment it was agreed that Insincere Marguerite should continue to follow the other girl for the day and see what she gets up to. For safety\u2019s sake Calamity insisted that Marguerite call in every hour to let us know how she was doing and what was going on. The rest of us agreed that would be a prudent precaution to take. Shortly after Insincere Marguerite left to follow Chalcedony Lorelei left to go patrolling the Hedge with Monica. I would have liked to go with them, but did not want to intrude. I trusted Monica to see my friend safely through the Hedge and home again.<br /> <br /> While all that was going on Luna had an interesting suggestion. She wanted to spar, but while hanging upside down. She admitted that it was not likely to ever come up, but that it would help me be able to defend myself no matter what position I was in or what position my attacker was in. Made sense to me. We started with a demonstration. I was on the ground and Luna was upside down in a tree outside. I have to admit that she did really well, and used her wings to good effect. Like Lori roller skating, Luna\u2019s wings gave her an advantage with balance and stability. When we actually started sparring Luna said she wanted to start from an equal standpoint and did not use her wings at all. She had a rough start I think, but she was still good. Just not as polished as she is normally. It didn\u2019t take long for her to readjust herself and begin fighting with her usual finesse. In a real fight however she would use her wings. It is only prudent to use any and all weapons at your disposal to take the enemy down. And if Luna is anything, it is sensible.<br /> <br /> The first time that I tried sparring upside down made me feel like a rookie all over again. It is a totally different experience to be the one upside down and trying to gauge where the other person\u2019s blades are coming from and going to. Not to mention that all of your movements are different. There is no pushing off of the ground to switch position. There is no solid surface to stand on and keep yourself steady with. Every move you make changes your position and sets you to swinging in one direction or the other. You can\u2019t really stop swinging either. So, it was more a matter of timing which way I was moving at any given time and trying to use it to my advantage when blocking strikes or making attacks of my own. There was also the fact that my range of motion was limited. I couldn\u2019t jump back to avoid a strike. I had to dodge or twist away from the blade, and get creative on how I did so. There was a limited number of ways I could move and Luna took advantage of that. Of course when the roles were reversed I took advantage of it too.<br /> <br /> After we got back in from sparring Joan came by to see Lori. To say that she was angry was like describing the ocean as wet. She was pissed. Initially she wanted to talk to Lorelei alone, though I don\u2019t think any of us present were keen on that idea. After a little while Lori got back from her excursion with Monica, and Calamity went to go meet her. She wanted to warn her about the bundle of pissed off that was at the house waiting for her. When Lori and Calamity rejoined us Joan had decided that she would speak in front of the rest of us. Apparently what was pissing her off so much was that Andromeda is not recovering from the use of the Table as fast as she did the first time. She is getting better, but she is still not back to her normal self and this angers our lady in white. Apparently Joan threatened all of the Monarchs into meeting with her tomorrow. She wanted to make sure that no one would ever ask Andromeda to use the Table again, but she didn\u2019t go about it in a very diplomatic way. I\u2019m not sure if she flat out said or just implied that if anyone from the Courts asked Andromeda to use the Table again she would end them in a bloody swath. She seemed to realize this was the wrong way to go, which is why she came to talk to Lori. She wanted to get Lorelei to speak on her behalf to the Monarchs.<br /> <br /> Calamity, bless her, tried to recommend to Joan that she go to speak to someone at the clinic. I agree that it would be a good thing for Joan to do, but she wasn\u2019t quite ready to think about that let alone do it. Joan was not pleased with the idea and announced that she would slaughter everyone in the place if she went there. I\u2019m not sure if she is specifically mad at the Clinic, or my Court, or just in general. I wasn\u2019t about to ask though. I have more self-preservation than that. Lori advised Calamity to back down about the clinic for now. Not that she should drop the idea entirely, just that she should wait until Joan was calmer to bring it up again. Given how mad the other woman was, I didn\u2019t think that would be today.<br /> <br /> Lori of course agreed to speak on Joan\u2019s behalf and said that she would call Princess Jolie in an effort to start to smooth things over with the Monarchs. Joan told us when and where she \u201casked\u201d the Monarchs to meet her and said that she\u2019d meet us there. We agreed and Joan thanked us before leaving. Lorelei then called De la Rocha and told her about what was going on. De la Rocha said that she would to speak to Joan at home and try and calm her down.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite got back part way through the conversation with Joan, but as soon as the conversation was over Calamity asked to talk to her alone. Apparently Calamity was concerned for Insincere Marguerite since every time she called in to report on where she was and what she was doing she would also comment on Chalcedony\u2019s beauty. It is generally not in Marguerite\u2019s normal behavior to compliment someone so freely and openly. And repeatedly. Insincere Marguerite assured Calamity that she understood why the other woman was concerned and said that she didn\u2019t have an explanation for her actions. A couple of ideas were apparently bounced around, like pheromones or some latent power. Not sure what it is or how it works, but I do think that there was something at work there. Don\u2019t know if it would be pheromones unless Marguerite got really close to Chalcedony. Those you have to be able to sense and I\u2019m not sure how far a distance they travel. Could be something visually based. Of course it could be nothing and Insincere Marguerite was just commenting on the other woman\u2019s beauty because she wasn\u2019t really up to much of anything at all besides eating lunch with mortal friends and going to the Rose and Thorn.<br /> <br /> After her little conversation with Marguerite, Calamity called Queen Charlotte to discuss the whole \u201cJoan affair.\u201d Charlotte was apparently very angry about things, especially the implied threat to Jolie. Charlotte assured Calamity that she will remain even tempered tomorrow during the meeting despite being angry at Joan. Lori also called Jolie and tried to help smooth over the confrontation with Joan. She explained to the monarch that the whole thing was to do with Andromeda and the use of the Table and that is why Joan is so upset about everything.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Okay\u2026.we just watched a lot of movies in a row. Five to be exact. In order we watched \u201cJaws,\u201d \u201cFerris Bueller\u2019s Day off,\u201d \u201cThe Crow,\u201d \u201cThe Craft,\u201d and \u201cThe Dark Knight.\u201d I will admit that it was fun to watch \u201cJaws\u201d in English. I\u2019ve seen it before, but only in Russian. Still, big shark, suspenseful music, explosions at the end. Good stuff. That was Lori\u2019s pick. \u201cFerris Bueller\u2019s Day off\u201d was pretty good as well. Had a couple of things I wanted to call Bullshit on, but it was a fun movie overall. Julia was convinced and tried to persuade the rest of us that Ferris was a figment of Cameron\u2019s imagination urging him to break the rules. It doesn\u2019t really work if you think about it, but she was very adamant. It wasn\u2019t really worth arguing over. Then came \u201cThe Crow.\u201d That was Gawain\u2019s pick. It was a fun movie. I think I saw bits of that in Russian too. I remember Top Dollar saying something cool in my first language. Julia was definitely into that movie. She watched it intently and she seemed completely engrossed.<br /> <br /> The second to last movie was \u201cThe Craft,\u201d which was Insincere Marguerite\u2019s movie pick. I think I may have dozed through part of that movie because I don\u2019t think I\u2019m remembering all of it. It was pretty late by that point too. I remember the character Bonnie and the bad scars on her back. I don\u2019t think she was a good person, or at least her actions were definitely not good. I could kind of get behind her desire to get rid of her scars entirely though. I have plenty of my own that I wouldn\u2019t mind if they were gone. Thankfully the really bad injury to my back that I got from the Lady was healed by her after she\u2019d inflicted it. She cut her mark into my back, and it was deep. I\u2019m pretty sure if she hadn\u2019t healed me then that I would have died. That would have been too easy now wouldn\u2019t it? She couldn\u2019t have her plaything dying on her. If that happened she wouldn\u2019t be able to remake me into her perfect little Knight. Anyway..I know about scars.<br /> <br /> Then the movie that I suggested was \u201cThe Dark Knight.\u201d I really enjoyed it. Good plot, awesome characters, and a bit of moral dilemma thrown in for good measure. I think my favorite character was the Joker. He\u2019s a horrible person and completely psychotic, but an awesome character. You love to hate him. Ledger\u2019s take on the Joker was different than previous incarnations of the character. He still did the humor, but it was darker and more dry witted. Less practical jokes and joy buzzers.<br /> <br /> I think my movie was the last straw for Julia. After it was over she almost growled at the other ladies, minus Calamity and Luna, that she wanted them upstairs and quick. I think someone got all hot and bothered by the darker, more Goth leaning movies. Meanwhile Calamity was looking all nostalgic over a strip of photos like you get from a photo booth. She showed the rest of us the picture. It was of her and her best friend growing up, Stasia. Apparently they went to a photo booth after seeing \u201cThe Crow\u201d for the first time. Calamity was kind of quiet after that and Luna asked if she was okay. Calamity assured the rest of us that she was fine, and that the memories the movie and the pictures brought up were good ones. I will admit that I was happy to hear that. Calamity has enough things to deal with that are not so happy. I was glad that she has some positive memories from her past to think on. It\u2019s just not healthy to only dwell on the bad. Yup, pot \u2013 kettle. I\u2019m not a complete hypocrite though. I do have some good memories that I think about, and I\u2019m remembering more and more of my mortal past as time goes on. I just have a lot of bad memories that like to take center stage, so to speak.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Well, that was interesting, and good. Captain Jack just came by. He said that Becky asked Jack to lend his aid to Lori for the meeting with the Monarchs, or at least to prepare for it. His main bit of advice was to go for \u201cdamage control.\u201d He said to play up the relationship difficulties of Joan and Andromeda and to make Joan look more like a victim in this whole thing. Basically anything that will put Joan in a more sympathetic light. He also suggested, and we\u2019d had the same thought, that she should bring up the dangers of using the Table in the first place. It can do good things for people. We\u2019ve seen it do good things, but that is a slippery slope. There will always be justification for using the Table, as long as the end result justifies the use in the first place. We decided that nothing positive should be said about the Table at all. It doesn\u2019t matter if it can do good things. The danger that it presents to the operator and the Freehold in general is too great. It\u2019s just too much power for anyone to have. The power to remake people entirely is scary. It\u2019s what the Gentry do. It\u2019s what the Gentry did to us.<br /> <br /> Luna offered to stay at the Dream House while the rest of us accompanied Lorelei to the Church where the meeting will be. She will act as our go-between if it turns out that the main dancers will be missing the performance tonight. It shouldn\u2019t come to that, but we figured it would be good to have a contingency plan in place anyway. I am a fan of contingency plans.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Okay\u2026the meeting went well. Most everyone dressed up for the occasion, at least a little bit. Julia was completely \u201cgothed up,\u201d Calamity wore business casual, and Joan wore her silvery armor and had her sword strapped to her hip. She was still pissed off, but was holding her anger back. I\u2019m not sure how much good the past day or so has done for her mood. So, we went to the church. Jack\u2019s ride, a biker sitting on his bike was waiting out front. Spidertoes greeted us and warned us that the Monarch\u2019s each brought a bodyguard to this meeting just in case. We agreed that it was fair, but I did not expect it to be an issue anyway. Apparently Lowjack agreed with me, because he brought Tamara as his guard. She may be competent, but she is not good enough to take down Joan.<br /> <br /> Lori\u2019s speech was great. Just as Jack advised, she brought up the troubles that Joan and Andromeda have had since the slight alien girl last used the Table. The dissociation, and robot-like behavior. She actually went into a bit more detail than I thought she would, but it turned out to be a good thing. Just hearing about Andromeda\u2019s troubles from an outside point of view actually made Joan cry. The stoic woman that rarely displays any emotion besides anger and suspicion actually broke down in tears in front of all the Monarchs plus Austin and Madame Spidertoes. Gawain tried to comfort her by wrapping an arm around her shoulder. De la Rocha reached out and took one of Joan\u2019s hands, lending her own support. Her behavior surprised more than just the Motley. The Monarchs too were looking on with surprise and a touch of pity.<br /> <br /> In the end all of the Monarchs agreed to sign a Pledge stating that they will not ask Andromeda, or anyone else for that matter, to use the Table against their will. This is taking into account any future Mothership escapees that may have the ability to operate the damned thing. Austin and Madame Spidertoes where requested to draw up the Pledge that they will all agree to since they are technically neutral parties in this matter. I thought it was a good resolution to the problem, and I know that Joan was happy that no one would be asking her beloved to use the Table again. From what I can tell, Andromeda is slowly coming back to herself, but it\u2019s taking longer than it did the first time. This is what prompted this whole thing in the first place. Not that I think Joan was wrong to make her grievances known, she just might have gone about it in a different way. But, the past is in the past and everything worked out for the better.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> I think Lorelei\u2019s healthy kick has inspired me. I decided to take up jogging. It will be good exercise and help me build up my stamina. Not that I\u2019m in horrible shape now, mind you. I just figured that I should get in better shape. I used to exercise with a lot more regularity when I was in the Lady\u2019s service and could hike for hours with little effort. Since Claire Falls really I haven\u2019t had the opportunity or desire to do much of anything exercise-wise. But Lori has inspired me to get back to it and start working out again. So far I\u2019ve just been jogging on the streets near the Dream House. My plan is to start jogging through the Hedge once I\u2019ve mapped some good routes out in my head.<br /> <br /> See\u2026when I was in the Lady\u2019s employ I had far more talents than I do now. In leaving her I left some of those skills behind. The one I wanted to get back, and the one that Calamity and Gawain have, is the ability to get a sense of what is around you while in the Hedge. So, I figured that I would try and figure out how to do that again, and spending time in the Hedge will help me do that. I may have to ask Calamity about those meditation exercises that she does and try that. See if that helps me attune to the Hedge around me.<br /> <br /> I also started giving Lori lessons in tracking and some Hedge survival skills. Not just finding your way around and identifying things to eat. I showed her how to camp and remain hidden, how to look at a track and tell how fast or slow the person/hedgebeast was going. I also showed her how to make a quick improvised weapon if needs be. It was a lot to cover and I don\u2019t expect her to remember it all now. I plan on taking her out several more times and have her demonstrate what I\u2019ve been showing her. I think she did pretty well for a first day. Her lessons with Monica are definitely helping her become more accustomed to the Hedge. She did seem a bit distracted today though. I asked her what was up and she said that Hailey and Monica had a falling out of some sort. Nobody was talking about it, so she didn\u2019t know any details. Apparently the two are just not talking to each other and are studiously avoiding one another. It\u2019s probably just something that they need to work out on their own. They\u2019ll get over it, eventually.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Okay\u2026things are progressing. I\u2019ve noticed a difference in my endurance since I\u2019ve started jogging. I can run further before I need to slow down and I can spar for a longer time without getting winded. Definite improvement there. I have also made some headway with the whole meditating thing. I talked to Calamity and she walked me through a couple of relaxation techniques that she learned from her therapist or the web. It\u2019s amazing how much more I can hear when I let go of all the thoughts racing through my head and just concentrate on the sounds around me. In \u2018the world\u2019 I could hear birds chirping nearby, the omnipresent sound of cars, the wind rustling the leaves on the trees, the sound of insects buzzing, everything. It was amazing. I probably wore that stupid grin for at least an hour afterwards. Calamity smirked, but didn\u2019t say anything.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> I got it! I was meditating in the Hedge today and kind of went past what I was hearing. It was like a background sense just came forward and I suddenly knew things about the environment around me that I could not see or hear. I knew that down the trail a ways and to the right there was goblin fruit, and to my left a little ways off was a Hedge beast minding his own business. At least it wasn\u2019t heading my way and didn\u2019t come across as a threat. I\u2019ll admit that it was pretty cool to be that attuned to the land around me. In a way it reminded me of the family camping trips we used to take in the mountains. At night me and my sister would stay up past when our parents went to sleep and try and see how many different sounds we could hear. Sometimes we would go for short hikes at night. Our parents didn\u2019t know we did it, or at least I don\u2019t think they did. We subtly marked our trail as we made our way through the forest trying to see what was out there at night that wasn\u2019t during the day. Night sounds are so much different than day sounds. There were little to no bird sounds, but more rustling in the underbrush. The most interesting thing we saw when we were out walking was a cougar. We saw her eyes first glinting in the moonlight. We just stopped in our tracks and kept an eye on her. You don\u2019t want to run or break eye contact with a cougar. They might take it as a cue to start chasing you. So we watched her and slowly backed off, and after a moment she lost interest in us and headed back up the mountain. She was beautiful.<br /> <br /> So all of this sense stuff made me remember something from my time in the Lady\u2019s service that I\u2019d forgotten. Rook, attuned to the darkness as he was, insisted on teaching me to fight with little to no light around. He said that it would make me a better fighter, if I didn\u2019t have to rely on something that could easily be taken away. Hearing is harder to take away, but sight, that\u2019s simple. You just need to throw something, dirt, snow, sand, whatever is on hand, in someone\u2019s face and you\u2019ve rendered them temporarily blind. So, Rook was adamant about me practicing while blindfolded and sometimes during the new moon. We would go to \u2018the world\u2019 at night and find somewhere that we wouldn\u2019t be disturbed and spar. The Lady\u2019s realm is always dusk, so it was not an ideal location for Rook\u2019s lessons. I remember thinking, when I was young, that the lessons were a waste of time and that I\u2019d never need them. I resisted at first, but eventually gave in and learned what he was trying to teach me. And, boy am I glad I did.<br /> <br /> I remember one night I was travelling through the hedge and came across a small party of Changelings. They didn\u2019t buy my excuse for being out alone at night in the Hedge and decided that I was a threat. I gave two of them a shallow cut with one swipe of my knife and they both stumbled back. That\u2019s why it\u2019s not good to bunch together too much in a fight. The other guy ran at me, but I tripped him on his way past. I started to lean down to attack him but he threw a handful of dirt and leaves in my face. It rendered me blind for a moment, but that was all he needed to get up and attack me. I sidestepped his blow and followed up with one of my own. He did not expect me to be able to tell where he was and got cut deep for his presumption. He went down, holding his stomach and moaning in pain. The other two, having recovered, started towards me. I wasn\u2019t sure how good they were, but they each held their weapons with a practiced ease that made me wary. I decided that discretion was the better part of valor and tipped my head at them, said \u201cSee ya.\u201d And ran off. They started to follow, but couldn\u2019t keep up and turned back. Plus they had their wounded comrade to go back for. That guy needed a healer and soon.<br /> <br /> All of that made me think that I haven\u2019t practiced fighting blindfolded in a long time and ought to start again. First though, I needed to practice moving around a known environment blindfolded. So I chose the backyard. I managed to make it around with only stubbing my toes or bruising a knee a handful of times. I tried to listen for how sounds change when they bounce off of something, like the bushes or the stage, and move accordingly. I also tried walking around the Hollow and surrounding area in the Hedge while blindfolded. That was a different experience. Sound bounces off of things mostly like it does in \u2018the world,\u2019 but there are some differences and it\u2019s not always consistent. It\u2019s hard to describe. There\u2019s just something \u201coff\u201d about it. Luna agreed when I asked if she\u2019d like to come with me. I think she was mostly amused by my fumbling around, but I soon got her to join me and we were bumbling around together. She was hesitant at first when I put the bandana around her eyes, but she seemed to adjust to it quick enough. After the initial awkwardness it was fun.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Today we started actually sparring blindfolded with blunted knives. Gawain was gracious enough to make a pair of knives for Luna to use since all of her blades most definitely have an edge. We started our practice in the backyard, on the grass. I figured it would be too easy to fall off the stage, so we saved gravity the hassle of coming to get us and stayed on the ground. It was interesting to say the least. Given my performance this afternoon I would have been assuredly dead. Luna was in the same boat though. I could tell that she\u2019s had practice, with Calamity I think, and I\u2019ve had practice with Rook, so we were pretty evenly matched. We both got some pretty good shots in, and based on where the scratches were each of us would have been fairly well incapacitated. We had plenty of annoying \u201cwounds,\u201d but there were some that we wouldn\u2019t have gotten back up from, at least not too easily. I\u2019ll need to ask Calamity and see if she wants to join us. I\u2019m pretty sure the answer will be \u201cyes.\u201d<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> Alright\u2026the calm is over. Today there was an altercation at the court. Dark Kimberly and Becky got into some sort of argument, or something, and they were going at each other, at least verbally\u2026to start. Kimberly said something that had Becky lashing out and Flores, the sweetheart that she is tried to intercept and calm the situation down. She did intercept things but not perhaps the way she intended. From what I heard the two went at each other and Flores got between them and tried to force them apart. And for her trouble she got slashed. She went down bleeding and the altercation just stopped. Luckily Flores was in a place that had plenty of healers on hand, so they were able to mend her wounds before she lost too much blood. She was upset with how things played out but not enough to let other people go after either Dark Kimberly or Becky. She pretty much flat out told people to not go after the pair of them or she would be angry.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not sure what\u2019s going on with those two, but they better work it out. Whatever their issue is, it\u2019s causing problems throughout the courts. My guess is that it probably has to do with the whole \u201cbetrayal\u201d issue. I\u2019d honestly thought that they\u2019d gotten past the violence aspect of that whole disagreement, but apparently I was wrong. Not the first time that\u2019s happened, nor will it be the last. Only problem is now they are getting innocents caught in the middle of it. Maybe they just need to be able to yell at each other and have folks kind of referee them so they don\u2019t actually get into a physical fight. Not sure how many people know of the original problem though, so not sure that would work. We need to do something though. If they will hurt someone like Flores, who gets in the middle of things just trying to help, who\u2019s to say that they won\u2019t hurt anyone else. It doesn\u2019t matter if others may be better able to defend themselves or not. Neither Kimberly or Becky should have gotten angry enough to not pay attention to who they were stabbing, and who were they were hurting. Even I can stop myself from striking in anger if I know that the person is innocent. I don\u2019t know how practiced Dark Kimberly is, but Becky at least is a bodyguard to a monarch. She should have better self-control. They both should.<br /> <br /> Then to top things off apparently Chalcedony is still acting suspicious, according to Insincere Marguerite. She hasn\u2019t done anything overt, but she is interacting with different groups of mortals on different days. Not sure what that\u2019s all about or if there is anything really going on at all. Most of the people that she is interacting with are not Changelings. Not sure if that means anything or not. Basically there are two people that dislike each other and are spying on each other and have not stopped. And one of these people may or may not be responding to some preprogrammed plan from her Keeper. That\u2019s \u201cfun,\u201d that\u2019s what that is.<br /> <br /> Okay\u2026that\u2019s enough speculating for now. Now, it is time to sleep. Maybe have a drink or two, then sleep. Yeah, I\u2019m thinking the later. Goodnight.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> Things have been sort of stressful.<br /> <br /> I spent time observing Chalcedony, but without any indication she was up to anything. She had dinner with some human dancers and went to Rose &amp; Thorn, but nothing suspicious. The conversations were normal, shoptalk; some were our dancers but any questions about the dream house were general. However, on returning, Calamity said I kept commenting on how attractive she was, and I rarely do so with anyone, even Julia or Lori, in that manner, other than to them. Thinking back, she was, of course, correct, but I don\u2019t feel any more attracted to Chalcedony than usual, which is to say how I would feel about a beautiful dancer who I had spied on in her unmentionables in her house for several hours. She has great legs. Definitely.<br /> <br /> Of course, that conversation was not upon I\u2019s immediate return. Joan was there, and (of course) angry. She wished to press the Monarchs to agree never to compel Andromeda to use the table again. She had threatened them to get them to meet, and realizing she was compromised asked Lori to speak for her. She then stormed out, after apparently threatening to raze California. I don\u2019t think her request was unfair. I suspect her assault on the state would be brief. Certainly.<br /> <br /> However, this continued to an actually fun evening, where we watched movies. I discovered that American culture in the 1970s apparently focused heavily on shark attacks, as Lori chose <i><i>Jaws</i></i> to represent the decade. Calamity having had the 80s thrust on her chose <i><i>Ferris Beuller\u2019s Day Off</i></i>, which was well, a very American film. It used Beatles music instead of American music for some reason. If one is going to use English music it should be the Clash (they being the only band that matters) and really, for such a painfully American story it should be an American group. Probably.<br /> <br /> Julia became fixated on claiming Ferris and Sloane were entirely in Cameron\u2019s head hallucinations building to his psychotic breakdown. While funny at first, she kept insisting on this darker take that they were hallucinated by a lonely and mentally ill Cameron to justify his rebellious behavior. I mean, it is a cute theory but\u2026Julia was insistent. I will touch more on her recent behavior in a moment.<br /> <br /> The 90s were split between Gawain and I, who picked <i><i>The Crow</i></i> and <i><i>The Craft</i></i>, respectively. I smiled when I heard <i><i>The Crow</i></i> mentioned\u2026that movie always inflames Julia\u2019s passions, and once it was going she kept finding Lori\u2019s toes in her mouth. <i><i>The Crow</i></i> is a good film. Any Darkling not reminded too much of their Durance can appreciate it. There was less comment about <i><i>The Craft</i></i>, but Julia liked it too. Finally, Jacob picked <i><i>The Dark Knight</i></i>, the second movie I had not seen besides <i><i>Jaws</i></i>. That\u2019s good, I was afraid he would pick <i><i>Requiem for Dream</i></i>.<br /> <br /> It would be ironic given his side vocation. Certainly.<br /> <br /> So Julia continued to be aggressive. She took great initiative in getting the other three of us alone, and took control of the evening. I knew those films appealed to her aesthetic, the last three I mean, but she was unstoppable. She has been taking Lori and myself (maybe De La Rocha that I haven\u2019t seen) aside for ravishment the last few days, and her painting and sketching are getting almost manic. I sense a growing of power among us and she is clearly building as well. The way her creativity is expanding, as well as her libido, who knows where it might lead?<br /> <br /> Today we had the meeting. The Darklings crawled from the darkness of my room later than Lori emerged, but we all still needed her magic to get us going. Captain Jack was there to help, because of course he was. It\u2019s the sort of man he is. Absolutely.<br /> <br /> Lorelei performed impressively at the gathering, though. She stood up and defended Joan well, flanked by De La Rocha and Captain Jack. Her speech, and Joan\u2019s almost crystalline tears, sold the monarchs on our point of view. In the end, the agreed the table will not be used. Fortunately.<br /> <br /> I am pleased by this result, but hope we do not have cause to regret it.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXXIX</i><br /> <br /> Mostly RP. Some powerful moments though and the players got really involved. Lorelei rolled very well on her speech, and pulled out all the stops to maximize her attempt. It payed off.<br /> <br /> The whole Motley, well save Ace, are now Wyrd 5, hence some of the odd memories and changes.<br /> <br /> Some journals touch on some downtime notes I sent about a week before the session. Those notes will be popping up here in the \u201coff week\u201d between updates.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, however, comments and questions are welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" targe