custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T19:50:26-07:00","id":691908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play?p=690885#post690885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At least one of does. I taste kind of bitter.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But do you taste faintly of almonds? I have an allergic reaction to cyanide you see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T13:22:04-07:00","id":695285,"title":"","content":"Faintly? That's no allergy, that's simply survivalist aversion. You'll get over that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is just my bright, shiny two cents.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing. I try not to argue in forums. It's like pouring concrete in a river. It doesn't get you anywhere in the short term and it poisons the environment long term.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2668-asmenedas","name":"Asmenedas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2668_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T00:11:34-07:00","id":695834,"title":"","content":"As the kids are fond of saying these days You Only Live Once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T02:49:01-07:00","id":696899,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s been two weeks, and recent events have raised concern at the Dream House. Also, the return of Bastille Day brings a certain longing in a certain young woman passed over by the great pumpkin for her lack of sincerity. Come on in and enjoy investigation, crisis support and Tim Burton night.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XL</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> July 14th, late night<br /> <br /> No time for my usual afternoon check in today. It\u2019s Bastille Day - well, I guess it\u2019s pretty soon to be that yesterday was Bastille Day, but anyway, Insincere Marguerite got super homesick. Julia was crazy worried - I mean, you know, we all were. It was weird, seeing Insincere Marguerite so... emotional, so sad. I didn\u2019t figure I could say much to cheer her up, and she had Lori and Julia with her - she didn\u2019t say anything until De la Roche left for work, so she wasn\u2019t around until later.<br /> <br /> So anyway, I started making a proper French dinner. Maybe not, you know, a very Bastille Day dinner, if my quick research was to be believed, but my vague memories of Paris included at least one dinner of Banquette de veau, and it seemed like something I could handle. I threw in a more summery salad, with goat cheese and apples and walnuts, and finished it off with cream puffs and crepes for dessert. I think Insincere Marguerite liked it.<br /> <br /> Calamity and Julia helped me some too. That was when Jacob took Insincere Marguerite off urban exploring, so Julia wasn\u2019t hovering around her. She wanted to learn how to cook French cuisine, so I explained my steps, you know, more than usual. Cutting up the fruits and vegetables seemed to help Calamity some too. She\u2019d gone to talk with Annika and Dark Kimberly about the \u2018incident\u2019 as we\u2019ve taken to calling it. We spent most of sex breakfast arguing over whether it was worse cause Flores got hurt or worse that Becky would have succeeded at killing Dark Kimberly without Flores\u2019 interference.<br /> <br /> De la Roche went over what she had heard - while Becky and Dark Kimberly had been, you know, avoiding each other, they were both in court yesterday. Dark Kimberly said it was because Princess Joli came back to the Springs early to meet with Desiree. They argued and Flores had intervened and managed to deescalate the situation. Then, according to Davey, Becky lashed out for no reason and according to Sandeval, Dark Kimberly said something cutting about White Maria in Chinese and Becky attacked in response. Dark Kimberly said she had said something innocuous about White Maria, asking if Becky\u2019d seen her recently or something. Becky, when Calamity called, didn\u2019t say anything in particular about it, but that she was just really angry.<br /> <br /> This kinda backed up De la Roche\u2019s conspiracy theory that someone might have used Contracts to flare Becky\u2019s anger. Problem still was, no one there but Becky or maybe Sandeval had the connections to use the obvious Contract, Fleeting Summer. Louie and Gunnar had the Smoke to be there without anyone knowing, and the connections for Fleeting Summer. Haley and Juan Carlos had some Smoke, but probably not enough to be unnoticed. Then there\u2019s always some other weird powers, you know, like the one used by the person who shot Dark Kimberly at The Rose and Thorn...<br /> <br /> The idea enraged Flores, you know, that it could be the same person. The flowers in her aura even got big toothy maws. She was around for movie night (Sleepy Hollow and Edward Scissorhands - Lori\u2019d never seen the latter and it made for a theme. Plus it cheered Julia and Insincere Marguerite up) and also maybe to make sure De la Roche and Calamity weren\u2019t gonna go after Becky for the \u2018incident\u2019. She apparently encouraged Annika not to by sleeping with her and Dark Kimberly last night. Calamity was really turned on by \u2018Angry Flores\u2019 - enough that Luna got a little annoyed. Flores stayed with De la Roche and Lori tonight though.<br /> <br /> All in all, the day ended pretty well. Even with Julia and De la Roche almost coming to (fake) blows over the fact De la Roche\u2019d slept with Davey, and bitter interpretations of life lessons from Pinocchio and Edward Scissorhands, we were all having fun, together. Tomorrow there\u2019ll be mysteries to solve and tonight we\u2019re home and safe.<br /> <br /> July 15th, afternoon<br /> <br /> So that was a nice blend of investigation and fun, if I do say so myself. Well, maybe a little light on the investigation but Lori did call Davey and the two kinda different stories, you know, matched up. He was the only one there not directly involved who could speak Chinese. Davey only vaguely remembered Dark Kimberly saying anything cause it was so innocuous, something about whether Becky\u2019d seen White Maria, like Dark Kimberly said. It wasn\u2019t anything provoking, which is why he hadn\u2019t mentioned it. His back was turned, so he\u2019d heard screaming and assumed it was Flores. Others had told him it was Desiree, which Dark Kimberly had commented on multiple time. According to what Calamity had told us yesterday, Flores was in shock and didn\u2019t make any noise, while Desiree, right behind Dark Kimberly, screamed super loud. Davey explained that Desiree had been waiting around for Becky to be free to chaperone her conversation with Princess Joli.<br /> <br /> After that call though, we went out for a few games of Laser Tag! It was tons of fun, even if I was mostly just, you know, a bit of moving cover and a distraction for the others. Insincere Marguerite snuck around the place, capping all the special targets without the other team (all mortals that were around the arcade - we were all on a team together). De la Roche, Luna, Jacob and Lori were all on fire, dodging around the place and putting their practice at the range to fun use. Calamity was a terror, scaring the shit out of the poor dudes there. Even Julia got out there with us, after Insincere Marguerite pouted her into it. She did good, long flowing skirt and all. The other guys didn\u2019t stand a chance.<br /> <br /> And tonight, we get to see Andromeda! Joan wants to get her out and about amongst people, you know, before the super public High Summer, so we\u2019ve got it all set up so she can disappear into the den if she needs to. Joan says she\u2019s doing better, even if she\u2019s not back to like before. I\u2019m sure she\u2019ll get there though. Joan loves her too much for her not to.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Huh\u2026 it\u2019s been nearly three weeks since I wrote anything in this diary. I guess the time has sort of gotten away from me, what with Highsummer and the play coming up later this week and everything else I\u2019ve been concentrating on. I haven\u2019t had a lot of spare time.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve continued working out with D and Monica every couple of days, and I think it\u2019s paying off. I\u2019ve gained a little bit of muscle definition, and I\u2019ve noticed an increase in both strength and stamina. I doubt I\u2019ll ever sport a real six-pack \u2013 and let\u2019s be honest, that probably wouldn\u2019t be the best thing for my career in the burlesque industry anyway \u2013 but at least I feel like I\u2019m a little more prepared for the physical rigors of the journey to come.<br /> <br /> And speaking of my impending jaunt into the Hedge, I\u2019ve also been preparing in other ways. I\u2019ve slept in the Hedge House a few more times, and I\u2019ve gone in twice more with Monica and once with Oleander. I think I\u2019m starting to get used to the eerie, otherworldly feel of that place. It\u2019s really not so bad in there as long as you\u2019re careful. Some of the thorns can even be beautiful, in a wild, harsh way.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve also spent some more time at the range with Calamity (though D, after that first disastrous trip, has opted not to join us again). I doubt I\u2019ll ever be a real sharpshooter, but my aim isn\u2019t bad. And Jacob has taught me a bit about tracking and survival in the wilderness, which has been fun. Oh, and Marguerite has deigned to show me the basics of stealth as well. What with rehearsals and all, my afternoons have been pretty full for the past few weeks.<br /> <br /> As have my mornings. After my Darkling darlings drift off, I tend to extricate myself from their tangled sleeping forms and head downstairs to hit the books. I\u2019ve been reading a lot of medical textbooks and journals lately. Though I\u2019m not nearly smart enough to understand most of the articles, I think I\u2019m slowly gaining a greater understanding of human anatomy and the way the body is supposed to work. I\u2019m hoping that this will improve my healing abilities\u2026 if I know where to channel the glamour, maybe I can maximize its effect.<br /> <br /> I just wish I was <u><u>better</u></u> at that sort of thing. Oh, I\u2019m good at picking up on social cues and body language, and I have a good enough vocabulary to fake it in conversation, but I know I\u2019ve never been the brightest bulb in the pack. Picking up new skills, retaining difficult information, and the proper application of knowledge have always been difficult for me. I\u2019m pretty sure that\u2019s why things never worked out between me and Kyle. Sometimes I wonder how my life might have gone differently if I\u2019d been just a little smarter\u2026<br /> <br /> But anyway, that\u2019s not important right now. What <u>is</u> important is that I\u2019m giving this rescue preparation my all. It might still be a while before I\u2019m ready to go back for Missy and Jane, but I\u2019m slowly getting there. I\u2019ve even picked up the pace a bit lately by studying all night and morning and then using my Contracts to refresh myself. It\u2019s not like the glamour is hard to come by around here\u2026 I find that I really only need to sleep once every four or five days.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve even had time for a social life. D and I have gone out for dinner and a movie a couple of times, both by ourselves and with Marguerite and Julia. It\u2019s been nice doing regular date stuff with the three of them, instead of just our usual bedroom hijinks. And I can firmly state that I am as much in love with D as ever, and things between us are going great. I\u2019ve made a few more hints that I\u2019d like her to come to church with me soon, but she\u2019s determined not to understand them\u2026 so far.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve also been out with Oleander a few times, and have found myself spending the night at her place on more than one occasion. Since D is pretty much living out of our room at the Dream House these days, it doesn\u2019t seem fair to invite Oleander to stay over at my place. I can\u2019t ask D to go back to her apartment; it wouldn\u2019t feel right. And if she stayed in Marguerite and Julia\u2019s room, there would be too many chances for\u2026 awkwardness.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know if I\u2019m falling in love with Oleander or not yet. I definitely like her a lot. I really enjoy the time we spend together. She\u2019s smart, she\u2019s funny, and she\u2019s sweet in a way that\u2019s uniquely hers. She\u2019s very passionate about a great many things, but she doesn\u2019t let it control her. And while our lovemaking can be spontaneous and wild, it\u2019s more often the result of careful planning and preparation on her part. Last week, I arrived at her place to find the bedroom lit by candles, heady incense filling the air, champagne on ice, a tray of chocolate truffles, and soft music playing from hidden speakers.<br /> <br /> I love D; there\u2019s no question about that. But I can\u2019t really imagine her doing something like that; it\u2019s not her style. And it was a nice change.<br /> <br /> A few weeks ago, I was contemplating breaking things off with Oleander because of the tension between her and D. I\u2019m glad I didn\u2019t. I\u2019m discovering that our relationship has layers I never suspected, and I look forward to discovering more of them. But the tension is still there. D and Oleander don\u2019t really talk anymore. I mean, neither of them is making aggressive moves toward the other, but I think they\u2019re deliberately avoiding each other. I know that they were never particularly close before, but they used to get along fairly well.<br /> <br /> D\u2019s actually a little depressed about this, I think. She won\u2019t say it in so many words, but whenever she mentions something that came up in the past involving Oleander, she gets this sort of wistful look on her face, like she\u2019s talking about a friend who moved away. While the two of them are very different people, they actually have a lot in common as well, and I feel bad about being the one who\u2019s keeping them apart, however unintentionally.<br /> <br /> In the darkest hours of the night, sometimes I still fantasize about getting both of them in bed at the same time. The scary thing is that I could probably convince them if I really set my mind to it. But as wet as that thought might make me \u2013 having two beautiful girls who love me that much pleasing me at the same time \u2013 it would almost certainly do more harm than good in the long run.<br /> <br /> Bad Lori. These wonderful girls are willing to let you have the finest steak dinner <u><u>and</u></u> the most delicious mousse cake for dessert. It\u2019s petty to complain that you can\u2019t eat them both at the same time.<br /> <br /> In other romantic news, Halley and Monica have decided to call it quits. I feel a little responsible for this, considering that they split up pretty much immediately following my conversation with Monica in the Hedge, but in the end I think it was for the best. Halley is pretty broken up about it, and that\u2019s hard to watch, but it\u2019s better than continuing in a relationship built on false assumptions. The two of them aren\u2019t speaking to each other, and Monica doesn\u2019t seem to want to talk about it at the moment.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, those aren\u2019t the only tense situations that have intensified over the past few weeks. The ire between Dark Kimberly and the rest of the Freehold\u2019s Chinese population seems to have taken a turn for the worse. Dark Kimberly and Becky both turned up at Glamour Springs the other day, and things got tense. Flores tried to separate the two of them and calm things down, and it seemed to be working at first, but then Becky just\u2026 snapped. I <u><u>still</u></u> don\u2019t know exactly what happened, but Becky lashed out at Kimberly, and Flores got in the way. She was pretty badly hurt. It\u2019s lucky she was at a Spring Court function, and there were several capable healers close at hand.<br /> <br /> The details of the incident are unclear. Of course, my motley has taken it upon itself to investigate, and get to the bottom of it if we can. Becky says that she doesn\u2019t remember exactly what Kimberly said to set her off; the rage just came across her suddenly (as it sometimes does with us all, I guess). Kimberly says that she didn\u2019t say anything particularly inflammatory; she just asked how White Maria was doing. Since the two of them were speaking Chinese at the time, Flores doesn\u2019t know what was said on either side.<br /> <br /> There were a few other witnesses, but their stories just serve to muddy the waters even more. Davie was there, and he claims that Kimberly asked something completely innocuous\u2026 so much so that he can\u2019t remember exactly what it was. But then again, he\u2019s one of Kimberly\u2019s best friends, and he might be covering something up to help her. I don\u2019t want to believe that, but it\u2019s a possibility. Sandoval was there too, and he says that he distinctly heard Kimberly say something biting about White Maria\u2026 but he doesn\u2019t speak Chinese, so he might have just heard her name and made assumptions.<br /> <br /> There are more sinister possibilities as well. There are contracts tied to the Summer Court which can cause a person to instantly and irrationally act upon their greatest angry feelings. But someone would have to either be a member of the Summer Court or be in very good standing with them in order to learn those contracts, and no one meeting that description was there at the time. Of course, there are other contracts which can allow people to make themselves practically invisible (just look at Marguerite), and there <u><u>are</u></u> certain members of the Freehold who might have both of those powers.<br /> <br /> Gunnar Friday is Autumn Court, but he\u2019s very close to Lucien Torres, and we <u><u>know</u></u> that Lucien was tangentially involved with the whole Kimberly-Maria-Sundown debacle years ago. He certainly has the stealth chops to pull it off, too. I don\u2019t have a problem with Gunnar; I remember how helpful he was in dealing with our resident ghosts and Mary\u2019s fetch, but I don\u2019t know that much about him on a personal level, so for the moment he seems like the most likely suspect in my opinion.<br /> <br /> Louis Guo is known to possess high levels of the Contracts of Smoke, and he\u2019s a Summer Courtier in good standing. He used to have ties to the Tong as well from what I hear, back when he was a mortal. But he supposedly cut all ties to them when he found religion and became a Buddhist. And besides, he made it very clear to the entire motley that he was Viscount Augustine\u2019s man through and through, and not one of Lucien\u2019s toadies. Still, by the strength of his capabilities alone, he\u2019s probably number two on the suspect list.<br /> <br /> There are a few wilder theories out there too, and some facts \u2013 admittedly gleaned from unreliable witnesses \u2013 which hint at something stranger going on. Desiree was there, standing directly behind Kimberly, when Becky attacked. Kimberly says she remembers Desiree screaming in what sounded like fear when Flores went down. Flores herself apparently didn\u2019t make a sound. Could the attack have been intended for Desiree rather than Kimberly? Could Desiree be <u><u>behind</u></u> the attack? I know Gawain removed the trigger from her brain, but the conspiracy theorist in me can\u2019t help but wonder\u2026 what if she\u2019s <u><u>really</u></u> a Loyalist, and the trigger was only there to let her known when to drop her cover personality?<br /> <br /> And what about Flores, for that matter? Kimberly has been attacked twice in the last few months, and on both occasions Flores was present. While I don\u2019t think any of us think Flores could be behind the attacks, could she be their true target? The Rose &amp; Thorn had to shut down for several days after the shooting, after all. And Flores certainly got the worst of things in this encounter as well.<br /> <br /> Annika is not taking the attack on Dark Kimberly well\u2026 but then again, Annika isn\u2019t exactly the most stable block in the pyramid, is she? Reading between the lines of Calamity\u2019s report on the two of them, I think there\u2019s trouble in paradise. Annika is trying to be too controlling (surprise, surprise), and Kimberly is chaffing at the overprotective treatment. Kimberly <u><u>has</u></u> agreed to travel with a bodyguard for her own protection when she goes out, but it sounds like Annika would rather she never goes out at all.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">Controlling overprotective cradle-robbing psycho bitch.</span><br /> <br /> Ahem.<br /> <br /> If only that was the only drama slung in our faces yesterday. Alas, \u2018twas not so. You see, yesterday was Bastille Day, and that simple fact had Insincere Marguerite feeling more than a little homesick. I confess that I didn\u2019t pick up on this at first, and when she started in with her usual Classier-Than-Thou-Francophile spiel, I snapped at her. I think I said something like \u201cI am in no mood, Marguerite.\u201d It wasn\u2019t until later that I realized she hadn\u2019t corrected me for shortening her name, and she stayed pretty quiet throughout the rest of the discussion of Dark Kimberly\u2019s woes.<br /> <br /> When Calamity went off to visit Annika, D ran off to her job, and I retreated to my boudoir to catch up on my studies. Oh, interesting side note\u2026 I think I might actually be a little farsighted, as I\u2019ve found it easier to focus on the books if I wear my fake reading glasses. I dunno, maybe it\u2019s a psychological thing. Girls who wear glasses are smarter, right?<br /> <br /> Anyway, Julia knocked on my door about an hour later, and she was frantic with worry. Marguerite was crying in their room\u2026 actually crying! Julia didn\u2019t know what to do, and it was obviously tearing her apart that nothing she said seemed to have any effect on her beloved. She\u2019s a sweet, caring, wonderful girl, and I love her, but this was a situation to which she was not well-suited. She had been trying to reason with Marguerite; to make things better with logical suggestions. That wasn\u2019t what Marguerite needed today.<br /> <br /> I started off by speaking nothing but French to her throughout our conversation. Despite how I sometimes tease Marguerite, my French is <u><u>anything</u></u> but perfect, and I\u2019m sure I stumbled and fumbled and generally came out sounding like a backwoods hick to her, but she seemed to appreciate the gesture in any case. I told her that I was there for her, and that Julia was there for her, and that later that day D would be there for her as well. We all know what it\u2019s like to feel homesick, and no one was going to think any less of her for it. I told her to cry if she needed to cry, to let it out, and to purge it if she could.<br /> <br /> We also kinda-sorta make tentative plans to maybe visit Paris next year on Bastille Day. It was Julia\u2019s idea, and what can I say? I\u2019ve never been to Paris, and I\u2019ve always wanted to go. Marguerite pointed out that there might be a few problems with that plan, as she is not well-liked by the Courts there. In point of fact, she fled Paris to escape capture, and was tried and convicted of being a Loyalist in absentia. She said that one of the Changelings she had previously \u201cliberated\u201d from their Keeper (and kept for herself) had testified at the trial, which doesn\u2019t sound hopeful. So either we\u2019ll have to straighten that mess out, or she\u2019ll have to go incognito.<br /> <br /> (Marguerite also said that her \u201cDearest,\u201d her favorite of those she had stolen, had \u201ccome to love her in the end.\u201d I don\u2019t know quite how to respond to that. I suppose it\u2019s good that there\u2019s no bad blood between them, but\u2026 well, lots of Changelings come to love their Keepers in the end, and that\u2019s definitely not a good thing.)<br /> <br /> She lived in Montreal after that, but apparently that just made the homesickness worse. She said it was like living in an American town that was pretending to be French; the little things were all wrong and it drove home how much she missed the genuine article. I guess I can understand that.<br /> <br /> Once she had calmed down a bit, I left her to Julia\u2019s tender graces, and went back to my room to resume my studies until it was time for us all to gather for dinner. Gawain had outdone himself when he\u2019d heard about Marguerite\u2019s funk, and had prepared a meal of traditional French cuisine. Banquette de Veau, a light salad, appropriate wines, and a dessert of crepes and cream puffs. It was delightful.<br /> <br /> Jacob had also taken Marguerite \u201curban exploring\u201d while I was studying, which also seemed to cheer her up a bit. I don\u2019t know what the two of them got up to out there, but it was nice to see her excited about something again. I hope they didn\u2019t break too many of the important laws.<br /> <br /> And then there was movie night. Whatever we had originally planned was summarily preempted by Julia, however, who decreed that we would be watching two films by a director named Tim Burton, based on a conversation from earlier in the day. Both films starred an actor I didn\u2019t know by the name of Johnny Depp, and it was deemed imperative that this should be addressed.<br /> <br /> <u><u>Sleepy Hollow</u></u> was a fun little re-telling of the old Washington Irving story\u2026 with a lot of elaboration and a hefty dose of creative license. Depp was pretty good as Ichabod Crane, who was presented here as a sort of primitive forensic policeman rather than the nervous and impressionable schoolteacher of the story. His love Katrina was played by a very pretty young woman who could really fill out a peasant top. And there were a few older actors I recognized as well\u2026 Christopher Lee and Martin Landau were present in minor roles, and Christopher Walken played the Horseman (in a flashback to when he actually had a head, of course).<br /> <br /> <u><u>Edward Scissorhands</u></u> was far stranger, and I\u2019m told it\u2019s more representative of Burton\u2019s early work. Depp played an android in this film, a na\u00efve but kind-hearted young man whose \u201cfather\u201d died before he could properly finish his creation. This left the poor creature with a number of sharp blades on the ends of his arms rather than proper hands. Why the old inventor thought scissors would make suitable temporary hands is never explained. Nonetheless, young Edward is taken in by a kindly Avon lady and her family, and he slowly learns how he can fit into society. Though of course there are bumps along the way, many people learn to appreciate Edward for the things that make him different, and his haircuts, hedge trimmings and ice sculptures are big hits. But there are many very dark twists and turns, and the film doesn\u2019t exactly have a happy ending. The love and acceptance this outcast oddball craves simply aren\u2019t in the cards in the end.<br /> <br /> This was a better film overall, in my opinion, and it certainly had a message. On an artistic level, it was visually striking, and I could see why it appealed so much to Julia\u2019s dark Gothic sensibilities (though I still teased her about it a little). Maybe I should look into more of this fellow\u2019s films. Though I have to say, I would <u><u>not</u></u> want one of the haircuts Edward gave the neighborhood ladies in that film. Maybe it\u2019s because I skipped the 80s or something, but the styles just looked weird to me\u2026 almost as much as Edward\u2019s. His hair stuck out all over the place, and looked sort of like he\u2019d rinsed it with egg whites.<br /> <br /> Flores was there for movie night, and we used the opportunity to question her about the incident between Dark Kimberly and Becky. She mostly confirmed what we had heard from the others, but there\u2019s one thing I should probably mention at this point. When we mentioned the possible connection between this event and the shooting at the Rose &amp; Thorn, she got angry. Really angry. I\u2019ve never seen Flores angry before, and it\u2019s not something I\u2019d like to see again. Her mantle changed, and the little flowers that always seem to be surrounding her grew teeth. Luckily, D and I managed to calm her down.<br /> <br /> As Julia and Marguerite wanted some private time in the wake of the latter\u2019s breakdown, it fell to me and D to keep Flores entertained last night. It was a heavy burden to bear, but I think we managed to show her a good time. Several, in fact. And she eagerly returned the favor in spades.<br /> <br /> In the middle of the night, as I was reading an article on blood coagulation in the <u><u>American Journal of Medicine</u></u>, I heard soft strains of music coming from down the hall. I quietly got up, checked that D and Flores were still asleep, and then made my way quietly out into the hallway. The tune resolved into a singing voice, and it was obviously coming from Marguerite and Julia\u2019s room. It was <u><u>beautiful</u></u><u>.</u> The music seemed to get inside my head somehow, and my thoughts became fuzzy and dim.<br /> <br /> I met Jacob in the hall. He was the only other resident of the Dream House who had heard the song. We conferred for a few seconds, and then knocked on the door. The singing stopped, and our heads cleared a bit. Julia opened the door with an embarrassed look on her face. \u201cYes?\u201d she asked softly.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe heard singing,\u201d I whispered back. \u201cIs everything okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes,\u201d she said again. \u201cI was singing Insincere Marguerite to sleep. Sorry I disturbed you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo worries,\u201d I replied, \u201cI\u2019ve just never heard you sing before. We wanted to make sure you two were okay.\u201d<br /> <br /> Julia thanked us for our concern, said her goodnights, and went back to the slumbering Marguerite. But the singing didn\u2019t start up again.<br /> <br /> Sex Breakfast came a little earlier than usual this morning, but was doubly appropriate, as most of us were practically humming in the afterglow of something or other. Flores joined us for breakfast before hurrying off to see to the Rose &amp; Thorn. I called Davie up and gleaned some of the information I mentioned above, and promised him that we were looking into the situation and would do everything we could to ensure that it wouldn\u2019t happen again. He\u2019s not happy at the moment, but I think \u2013 I hope \u2013 he feels a little better knowing that we\u2019re on the case.<br /> <br /> Of course, he might not have been thrilled to learn how we spent the rest of the afternoon. Almost as soon as I hung up the phone, someone \u2013 I think it might have been Gawain \u2013 suggested that we resurrect the tabled idea of heading out for a few rounds of Laser Tag. The idea had initially been suggested by D as a kind of date for the two of us before she moved in, and the rest of the motley had gotten excited at the prospect. I admit that I had previously sort of manipulated conversations away from that notion, because at the time I was really anxious to spend more time <u><u>alone</u></u> with D, so that the two of us could get to know each other better. Now that we\u2019re pretty solidly involved, the idea of playing a few rounds of the game with all of our friends present sounded a lot more appealing.<br /> <br /> We got there, paid for a few games, and suited up. I bemoaned the fact that the glowing red target would be sitting squarely atop my boobs, but it was all in good fun (and while I\u2019m being honest, when have I ever really minded any accessory that calls attention to my assets?). The best part of the experience for me was the fact that we didn\u2019t split up into teams\u2026 no \u201cLovers vs. Fighters\u201d bullshit this time. The entire motley, Luna, D, and even Julia (who practically had to be dragged kicking and screaming into the arena) was on a single side, and we were arrayed against a group of mortals.<br /> <br /> Those poor schmucks never had a chance!<br /> <br /> Okay, so I\u2019ll never be the marksman that some of my motley-mates are. I\u2019m no Annie Oakley, that\u2019s for sure. But I think I gave at least as well as I got out there today. Better, in fact, because while I didn\u2019t rack up a huge amount of \u201ckill shots\u201d like Calamity, at least I was only hit a couple of times myself. I guess all that time I\u2019ve spent jogging and working out with D has paid off a little bit after all.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s see, about my companions. Gawain spent most of his time shielding the rest of us with his body, which was noble and very\u2026 \u201cGawain\u201d of him. Calamity and D were the queens of the battlefield, cackling like lunatics as they picked off the competition one by one, rarely even bothering to take cover, just dancing through the thick of the fray and dodging this way and that. Jacob was a shadow; his shots were precise, and he was careful about breaking cover. Luna was, if anything, even deadlier than her paramour. Marguerite scored incredibly well, practically disappearing from sight and making straight for the other team\u2019s base to rack up major points. Julia\u2026 has many fine qualities, and was a very good sport about being roped into this activity.<br /> <br /> We made it back to the Dream House in time for a quick rehearsal of \u201cA Midsummer Night\u2019s Dream.\u201d Highsummer is only a few nights away, and I\u2019m starting to get really nervous about my directorial debut\u2026 especially since I\u2019m also directing <u><u>myself</u></u> in the role of Hermia. I know the role fairly well, of course\u2026 I memorized the lines and the blocking weeks ago. And I know that my cast is up to snuff; most of them are professional actors, while the rest are Changelings with a flair for the dramatic. <br /> <br /> I hope the Courts will appreciate the artistic choice of having Changelings play the mortal roles while mortals play the fairies. It seemed like such a bold direction to take at first, but now I\u2019m starting to wonder if some of the more traditional members of the Freehold might think it\u2019s in poor taste. Well, it\u2019s too late to change things up now.<br /> <br /> And there\u2019s also the Summer Court\u2019s Highsummer Festival to look forward to. It\u2019s supposed to have the same sort of \u201cRenaissance Faire\u201d theme as the ceremony which transferred power from the Spring to the Summer Court. I considered wearing my \u201cbawdy serving wench\u201d costume again, but decided that repeating myself would be gauche. I went online and ordered a fancy-shmancy medieval-style noble lady\u2019s gown which should arrive in the next day or two. Julia helped me pick it out (and made sure the measurements were correct). I can\u2019t wait!<br /> <br /> So, to sum up: training, romantic joys, romantic woes, violence, more Nancy Drew bullshit, homesickness, Johnny Depp movies, laser tag, thespian endeavors, Highsummer. Think I\u2019ve got enough on my plate?<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T02:50:45-07:00","id":696900,"title":"","content":"<b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> July 15<sup>th</sup><br /> <br /> New book. New pages. It was Dr Emmett's idea. She thinks I'm better off looking forward rather than backward. Not going to forget (or forgive) the past. You can't learn from it that way. But you also have to accept that what's done can't be undone at some point.<br /> <br /> Yeah, not so subtle hint about my guilt with my parents there. Not sure how that woman expects me to let that shit go. I mean, she's right that I'd be happier if I wasn't haunted by it but I'd also be a fucking sociopath. Of course, right now, I've got bigger fish to fry, so there's no time for the introspective shit.<br /> <br /> Something's off with this whole fucking incident between Becky and Dark Kimberly. Sure, I may not be the most impartial person but my interest isn't one sided. Dark Kimberly may be Annika's but I have not forgotten what a wonderfully soft and sweet little morsel that girl is. And Becky... Oh fuck but my feelings there are a gorram mess. Gawain's assured me (more than a few times since I can't stop being insecure about this) that he's on board with me pursuing her. It's ironic. I would actually do the whole fucking devoted to him and him alone thing for him if he asked me to. But it's because he doesn't expect that kind of shit that I love him so much. Calamity is a fickle and complicated monster.<br /> <br /> I guess the stress of it was showing because Insincere Marguerite asked me straight up if I was okay after today's outing. At the time we were discussing her thoughts on recent events. It was good to see her much more her usual self after yesterday's bout of severe homesickness. Shit that was jarring to see, and I only caught a glimpse of it. Julia and Lori talked her through the worst of it. Jacob distracted her with their overdue urban exploring outing. Gawain cooked an actual gorram French feast for dinner. She's lucky to have them. That's how this motley works though, we're all in this for each other. Fuck knows I've needed it before and I have no doubts I will again.<br /> <br /> But like I told her. I'm good. I'm a fucking rock. Right now, I have to be. Too much shit going down for me to fall apart right now so I won't. Highsummer is the day after tomorrow. And even with Flores doing her best to defuse things, it's tense. But Insincere Marguerite is right. There is always going to be something. The world is always burning, you have to fiddle with one hand and firefight with the other. That's why the motley hit the Laser tag arena today. Damn, that shit was fun. We stuck together and squared off against a bunch of poor kids. I mean, it was dark and noisy and twisty in there, so slipping around behind them and suddenly being right fucking there and shooting them was too damn easy. Yeah, I may have had a bit too much fun toying with them, but it was harmless in the end and it did scratch the itch.<br /> <br /> And after she pointed that out I dug out the package that arrived and showed her the spiderweb patterned leather harness I'm wearing. I mean, I did go topless at the Masquerade but only for a little while and it was kinda in the spirit of the whole costume swap hijinks. As the saying goes, if you've got it flaunt it and if you don't fake it. And if anyone has a problem with me showing a bit of skin they can just suck it up. But yeah, I was pretty excited about it and then things were pear shaped and I just set the box aside when it showed up yesterday. Hell, I was half considering toning it down if things didn't get sorted out. But fuck that. It's Highsummer and I am going to strut.<br /> <br /> And Highsummer is when Joan and Andromeda will be making a proper appearance again. Apparently the darling is close enough to her former self to be comfortable being seen. The fact that she's even concerned about that at all is a good thing from what I heard about her condition right after the operation. And just to make sure it goes well, they'll be coming out to the Dream House tonight to dry run her being around a crowd of people. We've set aside one of the balcony tables for them. It's quieter up there and it's near the door to the house where she can withdraw to the den if she feels overwhelmed. We're all hoping it isn't a problem, but better safe than sorry and all that shit.<br /> <br /> Oh, and as an aside, holy mother of fuck is Flores sexy when she's angry. I didn't think she had it in her but when it was suggested that someone had orchestrated the whole thing she got dark. The mantel of flowers around her grew fangs and she insisted that I pledge to tell her what I found and that she be there when the culprit went down. It was intense and damn I have never been as hot for her as I was right there. I don't think the others liked seeing it and I am pretty sure there was some disapproval of my interest. I think they're worried I am going to encourage more of that sort of behavior. To be fair, they're right, I am.<br /> <br /> Gawain hasn't brought up Greg Andrews. I imagine with things going down he's thinking it's not critical. I'll ask him about it after the show, make sure to at least remind him that I'm ready and willing whenever he is. I really hope we find something good. Handsome deserves it. But good, bad, or ugly it'll be closure. And that's important.<br /> <br /> Putting the ghosts of the past to rest. Given the Dream House's spectral hangers on I've been learning a bit more about dealing with ghosts myself. At least, that's the story I've given. Full truth? It is possible that my parents aren't completely gone. Everything I've studied tells me it would be a bad thing for me to seek their ghosts out. The fact that I killed them violently is going to define whatever is left behind. And there is no way to know if they're actually lingering. But I have to know. I have to find out. I need the closure.<br /> <br /> And there is the matter of the Sinister Bitch. I can't let go of it, but I have also had to admit that I know almost nothing beyond her High School diary. There is a link between us. All Changelings have it with their fetch. I can find her dreams. I can watch and study. I can see what kind of woman she is now. She's dangerous prey, best to make sure I am ready before I hunt her down. I might not be Katt anymore but it's my fucking name and I will take it back. I will pry it out of her screaming bloody wreckage when I end her. And when all that's left of her is a pile of debris and lies, that's when I'll let the past go.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Today was an odd mix of conspiracy theory, raw emotions and adrenaline. It started off with us talking about the Becky and Dark Kimberly\u2019s situation over breakfast. The theories were coming fast and furious. De la Rocha pointed out that there is a Summer court ability that allows someone to make someone else\u2019s anger flare to life in an instant and have them act on that emotion. It\u2019s possible that this contract was used to get Becky to attack Dark Kimberly. Okay\u2026so what happened was the two ladies ended up in the same place at the same time. Not intentionally, but it happened. They had less than friendly words, but Flores managed to calm them down. They were speaking Chinese the whole time. Then Kimberly said something or asked something about White Maria and Becky just seemed to snap. She lashed out to attack Kimberly, but Flores got in the way and took the brunt of it. She actually got hurt pretty bad, but she is an elemental and was surrounded by Spring courtier healers. We figured out who had been there, and there were no Summer courtiers as far as we know. At least none visible. The only way that someone could have used that contract on Becky is if they were successfully hiding in the shadows and either were Summer court and good at hiding, or another court and had goodwill with the Summer court enough to use that contract.<br /> <br /> I have to agree with Calamity that Becky just attacking like that is out of character for the woman. Every time I\u2019ve seen her she\u2019s had good control over her emotions. Even when the Table was being used to heal Jolie, I was told she was not happy about it, but she kept herself in check. Plus there\u2019s the promise she made to Calamity a while ago when her anger was at its peak. Even then she promised not to harm Kimberly, and since then she\u2019s kept her word. Calamity also called Becky to make sure the other woman was okay after what happened. She seems to be okay. She admitted that she didn\u2019t really have a reason for attacking either. She just felt really angry and couldn\u2019t stop herself.<br /> <br /> Some possibilities that we\u2019ve discussed are that the attack was a follow-up to the prior attack on Dark Kimberly and that it\u2019s her that is the target and Becky was a convenient way to get to her. Another possibility is that it was Louie that made Becky attack Kimberly. We believe he has the ability to pull it off and has something of a motive too. He used to be involved in the Tong a while back. Of course since then he has become a Buddhist and apparently avoids violence. Not sure how true that is, but it seems to be. Which of course puts us back at square one, but it\u2019s an idea to keep in the back of our heads. Torrez of course was brought up, not by name, and after discussing things it didn\u2019t seem like him either. At least we don\u2019t think he\u2019s got the abilities we\u2019d discussed. It could be his man Gunnar. I believe that Gunnar has all the abilities that we were thinking would have been needed to pull off the contract and not be seen. Maybe he was acting on Torrez\u2019s orders? Basically, we\u2019re still not sure. There are too many things up in the air, and too many things that we don\u2019t know to make a reliable guess.<br /> <br /> After our little conspiracy theory conversation wrapped up Calamity decided to go and visit Annika and Dark Kimberly and get the young lady\u2019s take on what happened. See if any new details come up, or anything that might lead to a clue as to what really happened.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Insincere Marguerite was quietly losing her shit. Today is Bastille Day and she was feeling really homesick. She seemed to be okay until everyone left to do their own thing. Lori left to go study, Calamity left to talk to Annika and her girl. De la Rocha left for work. The room was emptying out and Marguerite got more and more upset. Julia took Insincere Marguerite aside and tried to cheer her up.<br /> <br /> Gawain and I, seeing what was going on, decided that we would make a traditional French meal for Marguerite for dinner. I had some good French wines, we\u2019d get bread and Gawain would work his magic in the kitchen to create a culinary delight. While we were planning the menu Lori, having been fetched by Julia, went to go talk to Insincere Marguerite.<br /> <br /> Calamity got back from her little talk. Apparently everyone is okay in Annika\u2019s house. Annika herself is really worried for Kimberly, and Dark Kimberly is frustrated and feels trapped in the house. She eventually agreed to take someone with her as a bodyguard whenever she leaves the house. She just needs to find some people that will do that for her. I believe Calamity offered to help if the need should arise.<br /> <br /> After we talked to Calamity Julia, Lori and Insincere Marguerite came in. Marguerite\u2019s face had tear tracks going down her cheeks and Calamity went up to her first thing to ask if she was okay. Marguerite said that she was but explained that she was homesick and since today was Bastille Day it all came back to her. I could understand that. So, in order to cheer her paramour up Julia promised Insincere Marguerite trips to Paris next year for Bastille Day. The whole motley could go. The only problem it appears is that Insincere Marguerite is wanted in Paris by the Changelings for being an alleged loyalist. They even tried her in absentia and found her guilty. Not cool. It sounded like they basically tried her based on things she\u2019d done in Arcadia, which is not right. We have all done things in our Keepers realm that are not good. We all tried to please our Keepers. Whether it is to gain approval, stave off disapproval or just plain survive, we have all done something. It isn\u2019t right that they tried her for things she did there. True loyalists serve their masters by infiltrating Changeling communities and stealing people for their Keepers, or taking escapees back.<br /> <br /> If Insincere Marguerite\u2019s \u201ctrial\u201d was considered valid then we\u2019d all be guilty. Calamity informed on other people she saw disobeying in order to gain approval and candy. I get the impression that the candy there is closer to a drug than just plain sugar. Then you have Lorelei who preened and sang and tried her best to impress her Keeper and gain her regard. She did some regrettable things to earn her Keeper\u2019s regard, but so did we all. Gawain did his duty and lived up the architype he was set and killed a lot of people. Insincere Marguerite tried to emulate her Keeper and kept some people as her own while in Arcadia. While she does have a \u201ccollection\u201d of lady friends in \u2018the world,\u2019 they all seem pretty willing to me. She is a bit possessive of her girlfriends, but she has not tried to hold anyone against their will. Me, no question there. I was a loyalist. I know what I did and it wasn\u2019t good. I brought people to my Lady and fetched people back. I killed on her behalf and played emissary when the need arose. I have since left her service. Dear Diane opened my eyes I think, and I am forever grateful to her. I can\u2019t tell her that though. I\u2019m not sure she\u2019d appreciate it, nor would it be safe for me if her motley mates found out where I was. Travers at least would do his best to make a paste out of me.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know what other evidence was brought forward in the trial held for Insincere Marguerite without her presence, and I really don\u2019t care. I know what kind of person she is now and that is what matters. So, if we are able to go to France, and maybe Paris, then Insincere Marguerite will be in disguise and I will do my best to keep her safe.<br /> <br /> So, all of this talk of home reminded me that I sometimes really miss Russia, or at least living with my family. I so rarely get to speak my native language anymore since no one here understands it. Lessons with Lowjack have been going pretty good, but I\u2019m not used to teaching so it\u2019s slow going. I have to remember all my grammar lessons from school so I can teach those to Boss Lowjack so he\u2019ll know why you use certain words one way and others another. Plus irregular words. Every language has those. Why didn\u2019t I pay more attention in school?<br /> <br /> So, I miss Russia a good bit too, and find that the best way for me to get past those homesick feelings is to distract myself with other tasks. Talking about it might also help, but I have yet to go with that option. There\u2019s a lot of things I should probably talk to someone about, but I haven\u2019t as of yet. Anyhoo\u2026 so I think Insincere Marguerite has been bottling those feelings up for a while and they just all came out at once when a catalyst came up. So, I came up with a plan. While Julia went into the kitchen to learn how to prepare the dishes Gawain was working on, I suggested to Insincere Marguerite that we go urban exploring. We\u2019d meant to do that weeks ago, but we haven\u2019t had the chance yet. I thought today was a good day for it seeing as we didn\u2019t have anything planned for the afternoon. I also thought that it would make a good distraction for Marguerite. I confided in Insincere Marguerite that I feel homesick too sometimes, and that I miss speaking my first language with other people and hearing it spoken around me. I especially miss my sister, who while she lives in the same town I do, she doesn\u2019t know who I am and so I can\u2019t talk to her the way I\u2019d like to. She nodded her understanding and then we spent the rest of the afternoon exploring abandoned buildings and generally sneaking into places we probably shouldn\u2019t have been. It was fun. And the best part is that I think I caught a smile or two on Marguerite\u2019s face. Mission accomplished.<br /> <br /> Another tactic, so to speak, that was brought up to help cheer up Marguerite was to watch a couple of movies. We eventually decided on Edward Scissorhands and Sleepy Hollow. So it was a Tim Burton themed afternoon. I will admit that the movies were fun. Not sure that they were good examples of cinema, but they were certainly fun to watch. I\u2019m not sure that Lori quite understood Edward Scissorhands, but that\u2019s okay. Burton can be kind of strange sometimes. I\u2019m not quite sure why the inventor thought that scissors would make good temporary hands, but I think that you\u2019re supposed to just look past that bit and pay attention to him trying to fit in with \u201cnormal\u201d society. The whole thing is kind of a tragic outsider\u2019s story. Sleepy Hollow was an interesting take on the original tale. Granted I haven\u2019t read the original since I was a kid but I\u2019m pretty sure that Crane was a school teacher. This was a more action oriented story, which was fun.<br /> <br /> Dinner was wonderful. I can\u2019t remember off the top of my head what the names of the dishes were but they were great. We had a salad, main course and dessert. I raided our wine stores for a couple bottles of wine to have with dinner. I think I made pretty good choices based on what Gawain was cooking up. I will admit that I cheated and looked online to see what kind of wine goes best with each kind of meat, etc\u2026 Then I just picked a couple that fit what we were having. I also got out a dessert wine that the internet said would be good with cr\u00e8me puffs and crepes.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, during the movies we continued our conversation from earlier. Flores joined us for movie night and we all ended up talking about what had happened. Someone brought up the insight that both attacks happened in Flores\u2019 place or with her present, and that it might be a way to try and make her look bad or discredit her in some way. After this was said Flores got mad. I have never seen the normally cheerful woman so upset. Even her mantle reflected her mood and the normally happy little flowers suddenly had maws with sharp pointy teeth that snapped at everyone. She even demanded that Calamity make a pledge with her that she will tell Flores who or what is behind the attacks so that she can be involved in the confrontation. After Calamity agreed, Flores forced herself to calm down. Her aura calmed down as well, going back to happy flowers. I\u2019ll just say that damn that girl can be scary when she\u2019s mad.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Well that was interesting. I just heard an eerie, haunting kind of sound coming from down the hall. It sounded like someone singing, but it was like nothing I\u2019d heard before. It was almost sad, so I went to go check it out. Turns out it was Julia singing Insincere Marguerite to sleep. Apparently Lori heard it too, and we met up in the hall and knocked on the door together. Both the occupants were fine, and that\u2019s what matters in the end. So, we wished Julia a good night and went on our way. After Julia closed the door, and as Lori and I were walking away I turned to our resident songstress and asked her what she was doing up so late. She admitted that she was up studying. I commented that she\u2019d been up studying late a lot in the past few weeks, and expressed my concern that there is such thing as too much studying. She told me that she was fine and that she could easily use her Spring court contracts to stay refreshed. I said that though she has an advantage over other students in that regard she should still try and get some sleep. She told me that other students have an advantage over her, and pointed to her head. I tried, unsuccessfully I think, to convince her that she\u2019s just as smart as the next person. I got the impression that she didn\u2019t believe me. Maybe I can find a way to convince her that she is intelligent? Or, maybe I just need to express my concerns to De la Rocha and watch the fun unfold. I don\u2019t want Lori to get mad at me, but she does need to get some actual sleep on occasion. Going for days without real rest, Spring contracts aside, doesn\u2019t cut it.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> I\u2019d say that today was a pretty good day overall. Joan called Lori this morning and said that she was planning on bringing Andromeda to the club for a show and wanted to make sure that her love wouldn\u2019t get too overwhelmed. We talked it over and planned to set aside a quiet room that Andromeda can go to if the crowd or music is too much for her. Hopefully this won\u2019t be necessary but it\u2019s always good to prepare for all possibilities.<br /> <br /> After that conversation we discussed what we wanted to do today and the idea of going to play laser tag came up. We also talked about wanting to talk to Davey to find out what he heard at the club when the little incident between Dark Kimberly and Becky happened. So, Lori called Davey before we did anything else and asked him what he saw and/or heard. He said that he didn\u2019t hear anything that would have instigated the attack. In fact whatever Kimberly said to Becky was so innocuous he doesn\u2019t even remember what it was. Can\u2019t have been too memorable. So, his account of things pretty much mirrors what others have been saying. He did mention that as Becky was attacking, Desiree, who was standing behind Kimberly, screamed. Throughout the whole thing, Flores didn\u2019t make a sound. Maybe it was the shock, but she was absolutely silent. Interesting that Desiree screamed. Maybe she thought that she was the target? If so, why? Maybe she was just reacting to the attack on Dark Kimberly? It just struck me as odd. Definitely going to keep an eye on that one.<br /> <br /> Then after all that business was taken care of we decided to have some fun. It had been suggested a while back that we play laser tag, but we never got around to doing it. Since we had a free afternoon today we decided to play. Now instead of breaking up our group into the \u201cLovers\u201d vs. the \u201cFighters\u201d again we decided that the motley plus significant others would be one team against whoever else was there. We were in luck and found another large party there when we arrived. We set it up so it was us vs. them. They had no clue what was coming their way. It was fun. All of us for the most part were better than average with the guns. Some of us had more practice than the others, but we all made a good showing of it. The other side of the game is where we really excelled. The hunting, staying hidden, and sneaking up on the other players. We were more than capable in that regard.<br /> <br /> Calamity was pretty much at a professional level with the gun and was downright scary intimidating the other players. She\u2019d sneak up on them and scare the wits out of them before shooting them. Lori was pretty good shooting, and even better at dodging. I don\u2019t know that she got hit very often. Gawain was average with the gun and didn\u2019t even try to hide. He acted as a human shield for the rest of us when he could. He was very good at protecting the rest of us. De La Rocha was as good as Lori with the gun and dodged like an expert. You\u2019d almost think that she knew where the other guys were going to fire before they did. Julia was not as good as the rest of us with the shooting aspect. I don\u2019t think she\u2019s really had much in the way of practice, but she gave it her all. She was okay at dodging as well. To be fair, she didn\u2019t even want to come along, but she did because her sweeties were coming. Insincere Marguerite was as good with the gun as I was, and the rest of the time might as well have been a ghost. I couldn\u2019t find her half the time. Then there was Luna. She was better at the offense today than she was at defense, but she was good all around. She definitely shot better than I did, but I think I utilized my surroundings and stayed under cover more effectively.<br /> <br /> I will say that playing Laser tag was fun but it did bring back some memories. Both good and bad. Well, good memories and those that were good at the time but I probably shouldn\u2019t feel good about them now. The first thing that came to mind was memories of Elena and I having water gun fights when we were kids. We\u2019d go in the backyard, which went right up to the woods, and we\u2019d hide behind trees and rocks and try and shoot the other one. The water faucet was neutral ground and we had a certain number of seconds to fill up and get back behind cover. It varied by day how much time we allotted for refills. Once summer our cousin Alexei came to visit and joined us for a game of water guns. He, even after the rules were explained to him, would not abide by the faucet being neutral ground, and kept soaking both of us when we went to fill up. Then in an unspoken agreement Elena and I ganged up on Alexei and got him good. We didn\u2019t even break the neutral ground rule either. We just used our surroundings and snuck up on him from behind and let him have it. It was fun.<br /> <br /> The other thing I remembered was an assignment with Rook. We were tasked with finding and killing the emissary of another Gentry that decided to play \u201cspy,\u201d and try and get the Lady\u2019s secrets. We tracked him easily though the Lady\u2019s realm. He may have been a good woodsman, but we knew the lay of the land. Eventually he decided that he wasn\u2019t going to get any more information than he\u2019d already obtained and he fled into the Hedge. Rook and I followed. He led us on a merry chase, but we kept gaining ground on him and harried his passage. We didn\u2019t just go in for the kill, we \u201cplayed\u201d with him first. We\u2019d let him think that he\u2019d eluded us and then just pop up right where he was headed. Eventually the game had to end, and it did, but not before we\u2019d truly terrorized the little thief.<br /> <br /> Yeah, so that last memory was not really a good one. It was fun for me at the time, and struck me as kind of funny now. But then I really let myself think about what we did and I\u2019m not so proud of those actions. I guess today just kind of reminded me of that time. I was doing the same thing, hunting down those kids who thought they were so smart and so clever, and proving them wrong. I guess it all depends on the context though. Today we used laser guns, no projectile guns, no knives, no real weapons, but the skillset was the same. And despite the quick flash down memory lane I really did have a good time. I know the others had fun too. It was good to get out of the house and just let loose for a while. Insincere Marguerite really needed the distraction and Lori just needed to be doing something other than studying. It was good for the rest of us as well, but those two really needed some time away from our everyday lives. Maybe we can do this again sometime?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> Bastille Day.<br /> <br /> I have not written for awhile, because my English is quite good and improving. But I need to use the diary as a diary today. Bastille Day has long been, for me, a day of homesickness. But always before I was in transition, not in a place of contentment. I was busy, and being busy let I ignore it. Usually.<br /> <br /> But today, I was in the Dream House, a place I hope to be in 20, 30, even 50 years. I have a family. I have lovers. I have a home. And that home is not Paris, just as it would never be Paris. When my eyes opened and I recalled the day it is, my heart sank, and I felt a despair settle in.<br /> <br /> At breakfast I tried, I think, too hard to act normal, and upset Lorelei. Sadly, I did not even care. I did not even correct her failure to say \u201cInsincere Marguerite\u201d rather than just my common name. She left, De La Rocha left, Calamity left, and I fell apart. I just started talking. Julia looked overwhelmed, poor girl. She did not know how to handle it. Somehow we got to our bedroom, and I finished falling apart. I don\u2019t remember what I said, just crying. Lori was there soon\u2026I think Julia went to fetch her; I could not contain my emotions. I was drawing in my sadness and despair. Julia began making logical, helpful suggestions that were not what I needed to hear then, and Lori jumped in with warm, sentimental caring words that were exactly what I needed. I feel a little sorry for Julia; I don\u2019t think she has ever been in that position and it clearly upset her. Sadly.<br /> <br /> She really did sort of badly. Unfortunately.<br /> <br /> Still, Lori and Julia managed to stabilize me with promises of trips, plural, to Paris in the future. And they told me Jacob and Gawain were preparing an authentic French dinner. Lori went on down (with my Cognac, which I had been gulping down like a woman dying of thirst) while Julia and I put myself back together into being presentable. When I came down Calamity was there, having met with Annika and Dark Kimberly about the \u201caccident\u201d yesterday. The meeting did not go poorly but also not well, from the impression I got. She rushed over to ensure I was okay, and I truthfully said I was\u2026now. I must have still looked terrible; she seemed very worried. We moved into the kitchen, where Julia was carefully watching Gawain to learn how to cook authentic French cuisine, and discussed movies. Julia wanted to show <i><i>Edward Scissorhands</i></i> (she owns a copy), which had come up earlier. While we considered <i><i>Fight Club</i></i> for a second movie night pick we went with <i><i>Sleepy Hollow</i></i>, watching it first. Julia was quite pleased. Obviously.<br /> <br /> Before then, before dinner, Jacob took me urban exploring. My exile after the events at the home of the Lord of Day had delayed my hobby, and so much had gone on here that I had not gotten around to it. Sadly enough time had passed my plan of seducing Jacob in an abandoned church was now\u2026well, I could have done it, but I would not wish to make an enemy of Luna. Even without sex, we had fun\u2026Jacob is an athletic man, and can keep up with me easily. We must do more in the future, he and I. It was fun. We did not talk about much but what we were actively doing, but that was what I needed.<br /> <br /> Dinner was good, and De La Rocha was there. Flores showed for the movie, though Julia told her she needed to be alone with me tonight. I am sure Lori and De La Rocha took good care of her. I am not sure Lori really \u201cgot<i>\u201d </i><i><i>Edward Scissorhands</i></i> but we still enjoyed them. A lot of us had not seen <i><i>Sleepy Hollow</i></i> as well. Flores had not seen either. Surprisingly.<br /> <br /> Julia took me to bed and we made love. Tenderly. Julia did everything she could to sooth me. And then, afterwards, she held me and sang I to sleep. It was the most beautiful, haunting thing I have ever heard. I shall never, ever forget it\u2026it will always be there in my mind, until I die. Certainly.<br /> <br /> I do love Julia. Completely.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <i><i>Sleepy Hollow</i></i> made me think. Perhaps we were looking at this the wrong way. What if we were being mislead, like Ichabod Crane? There are two possible Director Changelings, but what if they were the distraction? The true mastermind lay in the shadows. I spoke to Calamity about it. Davey and Gunnar I tossed out, or Juan-Carlos, but I suspect the mastermind is not a Fairest, and Calamity felt Gunnar was unlikely, not because he was a good person, but because he was in the employ of Lucian and Charlotte, two people he would have trouble hiding his allegiance from. Evidently.<br /> <br /> Then the two I suspected more strongly. One is Dark Kimberly. Both rather theatrical attacks targeted her, she was never too seriously hurt, and she is often at the center of a drama whirlwind. And even if revealed, Annika would protect her, and Madame Spidertoes would protect Annika. She is well placed to cause chaos, and we changelings rarely suspect the victim. Understandably.<br /> <br /> The other is Captain Jack. More theatrical than either confirmed director Changeling, everyone trusts Captain Jack, yet like me he has sworn allegiance to no seasonal ruler. He can betray the freehold without even bending an oath. He has affinity with every court, can come and go as he pleases, and is beyond suspicion and reproach. Even if revealed for certain many may refuse to raise a hand against him given the real good he has done time and time again. If the person behind the scenes is Captain Jack, the whole freehold may be doomed. Unfortunately.<br /> <br /> Calamity took I\u0336'\u0336s\u0336 my suspicions rather well. She dismissed Juan-Carols and Gunnar, but agreed the other people could be the manipulator. Hopefully she is fine as she said because as she also says, she has to be fine right now. I will not discuss this with the others yet\u2026maybe Jacob. Possibly.<br /> <br /> I hope I am wrong. Truly.<br /> <br /> Sex breakfast went well. Laser Tag had come up yesterday and to Julia\u2019s chagrin De La Rocha had failed to forget. Julia was eventually talked into going by my adorable pouty face. Once Flores left (it was Tuesday, so De La Rocha did not need to work) we made final plans. Soon enough we were suited up at the Laser Tag arena. I, of course, was a shadow, and overall people did well. It was a good excuse to get the blood pumping. Definitely. Once again Jacob and I got to be athletic. Gawain is fast for his size.<br /> <br /> Now that we have returned and Calamity has been informed of my suspicions, I return to preparing my own show. Naturally.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XL</i><br /> <br /> Mostly RP this time. Well, most times.<br /> <br /> Julia is a Nightsinger as well as an Artist, and this was the first time it came up. Lori and Jacob were the awake ones.<br /> <br /> For Laser Tag, everyone rolled Dexterity + Firearms, and one other pair of skills, usually Dexterity + Athletics, but everyone got to choose\u2026Calamity used Intimidation, for instance, while Insincere Marguerite used Stealth. I did a general pair of rolls for the other team, and everyone but Julia beat them badly.<br /> <br /> Lot of Conspiracies, Drama, and it\u2019s two days before Highsummer. Let\u2019s see what happens next. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T14:54:26-07:00","id":698993,"title":"","content":"The motley has some interesting ideas about the Dark Kimberly situation, it seems. I wonder how things will turn out.<br /> I like how the girls all seems to be evolving: Calamity with her therapy, Lori with her training, Insincere Marguerite letting herself be seen in a vulnerable moment. Funny to see hown Lori's animosity towards Annika doesn't change, though.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T23:03:47-07:00","id":699520,"title":"","content":"Yea all their personalities are evolving. Each has goals and ties to their past (the other girls, Calamity's Sinister Fetch, Paris) that they are dealing with as their glamour waxes. Jacob has some too just has not come out as much, and Gawain has another Gawain they will be looking for.<br /> <br /> We are doing some short spurts of time until we move on to the Autumn, where things will slow down a bit. I expect 1-2 more sessions (not counting yesterday) before we move on into August. That will also be short, then as I say an undetermined point in the reign of the Autumn Court.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T10:54:48-07:00","id":703657,"title":"","content":"I imagine they set some new high scores for laser tag.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T00:57:52-07:00","id":710129,"title":"","content":"Calamity did collect a nice bundle of fear glamour from terrorizing the other team.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T23:04:54-07:00","id":731363,"title":"","content":"Sometimes the best laid plans fall apart. A peaceful night becomes a whirlwind of drama.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XLI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> June 16th, morning<br /> <br /> I\u2019d say that didn\u2019t go as well as we\u2019d hoped, but I did get to spend the night with Monica, which was, you know, kinda unexpected too, but in an awesome way. She was looking smoking hot last night and Calamity all but pushed me at her after doing her usual rounds and stuff. but it wasn\u2019t til after Andromeda asked for Joan again, so the immediate stuff was kinda resolved, you know?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m getting ahead though. Like I said before, Joan and Andromeda came out last night! They weren\u2019t here very long though before Andromeda started yelling about having her right to choose taken away and then bolting. I moved to intercept her, but Calamity tried to grab her first and accidentally caught her with a bit of glass. Jacob had better luck, but then Andromeda got a little, you know, hysterical. I had to pick her up bodily to stop her flailing her way out and maybe running off and hurting herself.<br /> <br /> She really is too good for her own good. I think we maybe got through to her a little bit, that killing yourself wasn\u2019t as good a route for helping people that maybe it seemed, that sacrificing herself had more consequences than she realized. I mean, I think maybe it was just all her emotions coming back at once and everything - no way she\u2019d have accused Joan of not looking out for her normally. That was still a little, you know, across the line though. Maybe not slapping length across, though it did seem to help when Lori did slap her. At least, she calmed down a little bit.<br /> <br /> We let her have some alone time, after getting her a glass of water to, you know, help counteract the damage the shrieking did. Me and De la Roche kept Joan company, commiserating about how \u2018bitches be crazy\u2019 (De la Roche\u2019s fault) and assuring her that she didn\u2019t screw up or anything. Boss Lowjack showed up and talked with Julia and Jacob, I think. Calamity was making the rounds, talking with Ginny, Chalcedony and Mary Helene, who were there together to talk about working with us again sometime, then Madame Spidertoes then Monica. I think she got around to White Maria after she pushed me towards Monica, though I was, you know, a little distracted.<br /> <br /> So everything turned out alright, I guess. According to Insincere Marguerite, Andromeda and Joan left together, with Joan\u2019s arm around Andromeda, so they should be alright. And it\u2019s probably good it didn\u2019t happen at Highsummer. Plus, I got to have another fun night with Monica. Handily putting off, you know, things. I haven\u2019t had any more remembering dreams and Calamity hasn\u2019t asked me about it again. Still, I should do something, try and find him. Maybe I\u2019ll tell the others after this stuff with Becky and Dark Kimberly is sorted out...<br /> <br /> June 16th afternoon<br /> <br /> So apparently lots of stuff happened last night that I missed. When I came home, Lori was making pretty awesome green eggs and ham, and so everybody filled me in over breakfast. Madame Spidertoes had been there to let Calamity know that Annika wouldn\u2019t be around for dancing lessons today, cause she was trying to salvage relationship stuff. Also, Dahlia stopped by to consult with Calamity last night about the situation with Becky and Dark Kimberly. I don\u2019t think she had anything new to add, but I guess it\u2019s good to have kinda, you know, official backing on our investigations.<br /> <br /> Once Insincere Marguerite left to work on her routine, Julia told us about why Boss Lowjack had come by last night. She was, well, upset is putting it kinda lightly, but, she was upset, we\u2019ll say, about the charges of loyalism laid against Insincere Marguerite and wanted to clear her name. Lowjack had the connections to get contact info, but made it a condition that Julia involved all of us rather than her charging in along and threatening everyone involved with throat slashings, and generally sound like a brainwashed minion. Lori made it clear she wanted Insincere Marguerite involved too. Julia thought she\u2019d not want us going to the trouble, I guess, but they managed to convince her, so as soon as we get the contact info for the Autumn Monarch of the Court of Love, we\u2019re gonna see what we can do. Maybe even get Queen Charlotte to vouch for her.<br /> <br /> After that Calamity went off to do paperwork, so I asked Jacob if he wanted to spar, you know, to practice for the tournaments during Highsummer. I\u2019m gonna go for heavy weapons and Jacob\u2019s light weapons, of course, so it\u2019s, you know, a little awkward, but we traded off for a bit. It wasn\u2019t too long though before Captain Jack showed up, so we took a break for a bit.<br /> <br /> He was here for hijinx planning, of course. He would have been by earlier, but he was on damage control after the incident at the Springs. But still, it\u2019s gonna be awesome. Some dude called Wincelas is apparently a doppelganger kinda for Captain Jack, just white and with less of a beard. So Captain Jack\u2019s gonna do a take-on-all-comers kinda thing, and I\u2019ll go up and challenge him and start to win, so somebody masquerading as Captain Jack using Cobblethought hops in. Then Calamity wearing my face using Cobblethought hops in with me. Then Wincelas joins in, after folks are expecting Cobblethought shenanigans, and we\u2019ll have a real brawl going. I guess after that Captain Jack will make a suitably grand exit. It\u2019s gonna be awesome!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Andromeda\u2019s first night out following her extended recovery did not go as well as we had hoped. She\u2019s definitely coming out of her emotional fugue state, and we\u2019re hopeful that this is a sign that she will eventually recover completely\u2026 but if last night was any indication, she still has a long way to go.<br /> <br /> First thing\u2019s first, though. Julia pulled me aside before the show to talk to me. \u201cLook, Lori,\u201d she said nervously as she closed the door behind us, \u201cabout what you heard last night\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I started to say something, but she put a finger gently across my lips. \u201cLet me finish, okay? I don\u2019t sing very often because my voice tends to\u2026 affect people oddly. I\u2019m never sure whether\u2026 well, let\u2019s just say that I don\u2019t sing for anyone unless I\u2019m very secure about their feelings for me.\u201d She closed her eyes and turned slightly away from me. \u201cI\u2019ll\u2026 I\u2019ll sing for you sometime\u2026 if you want me to,\u201d she sighed quietly.<br /> <br /> I took her in my arms and kissed her passionately. \u201cI\u2019d love that,\u201d I said when we disengaged. She had tears in her eyes, but she looked happy. Come to that, my own vision was a little shimmery, which suggests that there might have been a bit of a sheen to my own admittedly freakish black orbs.<br /> <br /> Then it was time to get ready for the show. I wasn\u2019t out front when Joan and Andromeda arrived; I was backstage getting in costume and makeup, but Calamity met them at the door and showed them to their reserved seats. Gawain was working the door, and before curtain he let me know that a lot of people had turned up for the show, including Ginny, Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne, and Chalcedony, who wanted to talk with Calamity and me about coming back to perform on a semi-regular basis. White Maria was also there, and Madame Spidertoes turned up as well.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, things didn\u2019t go smoothly. I heard a fracas as I was putting the finishing touches on my ensemble, and I headed out to investigate while admonishing the rest of the girls to keep prepping. I found Jacob and Calamity restraining a hysterical Andromeda, who was screaming and crying and wriggling, trying to get out of Jacob\u2019s grasp. She had a fairly deep gash across her stomach, and Calamity looked stricken; apparently she\u2019d tried to gently stop Andromeda and had accidentally cut her with her shards.<br /> <br /> I took hold of Andromeda \u2013 with some difficulty \u2013 and healed the worst of the damage, leaving only a small bruise. We got her into one of the back rooms, but she was having none of it. She was furious about the pledge we\u2019d arranged between the monarchs. The idea that she will not be able to use the Table again to help other changelings is very much against her nature. She doesn\u2019t care that using the Table destroys her; in her mind that\u2019s not as important as the good she can do for people who have no other option. The fact that we made that decision for her had her spitting with rage.<br /> <br /> She wanted to leave, but none of us thought she should be on her own in that state. She wasn\u2019t wild about that, either, and I think most of us regretted the necessity of restraining another changeling against her will, but she would almost inevitably have harmed herself if we\u2019d let her go without supervision. This caused her to go ape-shit again, and she rapidly screamed herself hoarse with her imprecations.<br /> <br /> One thing she said broke through the tirade. She turned to face Joan with venom in her eyes and spat out \u201cyou were supposed to look out for me!\u201d Joan looked stricken. Tears sprang out in her eyes and she turned and fled the room.<br /> <br /> I saw red. In that moment, I almost understood how Becky could have gotten mad enough to lash out at White Maria and injure Flores. I spun back around, raised my hand, and slapped Andromeda hard across her cheek. Her screams were cut off short, and she staggered back to collapse on a sofa, her eyes wide and staring.<br /> <br /> \u201cI know you\u2019re angry,\u201d I said coldly. \u201cAnd I\u2019m sorry if we overstepped when we tried to protect you. But don\u2019t you <u><u>ever</u></u> insinuate that Joan doesn\u2019t care about you again. You didn\u2019t see her then. You don\u2019t know how much your condition hurt her. You don\u2019t know how far she went to protect you.\u201d<br /> <br /> She turned her head away from me, muttered \u201cyes ma\u2019am,\u201d and sat there quivering. The others looked at me with guarded expressions, but nobody seemed to think I\u2019d gone too far. I exhaled slowly. \u201cI need to get backstage,\u201d I murmured before walking out. I briefly checked to make sure D had Joan in hand, and then I rejoined the rest of the performers and re-did my makeup. Most of them took in my expression and opted not to ask me what was going on.<br /> <br /> Marguerite approached me before my first number, which was just as well, because I wasn\u2019t in the mood to perform a cheerful love song at that point. I asked her to change out my first song, and in turn she asked if I had really hit Andromeda.<br /> <br /> \u201cSlapped,\u201d I corrected without much enthusiasm. \u201cSorry. She just made me so <u><u>angry</u></u>.\u201d<br /> <br /> Marguerite looked nervous, and asked tentatively if I had felt the rage swell up beyond my ability to control. I thought back, but I hadn\u2019t detected any supernatural tampering with my emotions. \u201cNo,\u201d I said softly, \u201cit was just normal righteous anger.\u201d She seemed reassured.<br /> <br /> I only had one solo tonight, along with dancing and backup vocals and a few dance numbers. I thought through the Runaways catalog, but eventually decided to work out my anger with a number from after the girls broke up. It turns out that Joan Jett went on to have a pretty lucrative solo career, and her music carried on the style and traditions of the band admirably. So I belted out \u201cBad Reputation\u201d at the top of my lungs, and felt a little better afterward.<br /> <br /> I did hear later, by the way, that Joan and Andromeda left together. They both still seemed a little upset, but Joan had her arm around the smaller girl, and she was no longer struggling or screaming, so I\u2019ll call that progress. I asked Marguerite if Andromeda was mad at me for slapping her, and her answer was \u201cmore upset than angry.\u201d So hopefully we\u2019ll get past that eventually.<br /> <br /> Calamity and I spent a bit of time after my acts talking with our trio of visiting talent. I gave my immediate consent for any or all of them to perform whenever their schedules allowed, and dropped a few hints that I wouldn\u2019t mind pairing up with them for group acts at some point as well. I haven\u2019t forgotten how successful Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne and I were when we worked together before. And yes, I\u2019m talking about the act, not the sex (though that was good too).<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not sure what exactly Calamity had going last night, but I watched in a state of amused respect as she skillfully pointed Gawain at Monica and watched as hijinks ensued. It was masterful and subtle. I was absurdly proud of her, and decided to let it pass without comment. Gawain and Monica looked happy about the situation in any case.<br /> <br /> Calamity went on to speak with White Maria, presumably about the incident with Becky and Flores. She told us later that Maria didn\u2019t have much to add; most of what she said confirmed what we had already heard (and of course she wasn\u2019t actually present for the incident in question anyway). She did apparently cast aspersions upon D\u2019s character, insinuating that my honey might have sparked the incident due to her fairly well-known animosity with Sundown Kwon, but that makes no sense to me, as the attack was presumably against Dark Kimberly, who was also one of Kwon\u2019s rivals. And I <u><u>know</u></u> that D would never want Flores to get hurt.<br /> <br /> Speaking of D, my love had also spoken briefly with White Maria earlier, and was not pleased with the results. When I saw her looking slightly more disgruntled than usual, I cornered her and asked what was wrong, of course. She demurred for a few moments, but eventually she admitted that White Maria\u2019s typically bitchy attitude had put her out of sorts. She had also been worried about her former flame, Spidertoes (and didn\u2019t <u><u>that</u></u> set off my inner jealousy nicely?), who had been acting oddly\u2026 but apparently it\u2019s just something to do with a compulsion she has to wash bloody clothes. With that matter settled to her satisfaction I suggested that Maria wasn\u2019t worth her trouble, and she nodded and headed off to the bar.<br /> <br /> I joined her there later, and she was pretty sloshed. She winked at me as I approached, and directed my attention to Monica, who was once more carrying Gawain from the premises over her shoulder. \u201cRemember the last time that happened?\u201d she asked, her voice slightly slurred. \u201cRemember what we did just after?\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cI\u2019ll never forget it, sweetie,\u201d I promised.<br /> <br /> She arched an eyebrow. \u201cWanna do it again?\u201d she asked with a grin.<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cI\u2019d love to,\u201d I replied. The two of us linked arms and walked up the stairs together. Unlike the first time, we kept our clothes on until we made it to our room and closed the door behind us.<br /> <br /> The sex was vigorous to start out with, but settled down into more tender lovemaking as the evening wore on. I was fine with that, and I think it was what D needed too. She dropped off a little earlier than usual (she must have been worn out, and I guess the alcohol didn\u2019t hurt). I turned on a small night light, put on my glasses, and settled into reading and trying to make sense of another chapter of a medical textbook. I <u><u>think</u></u> I have a much better idea of how the liver and kidneys are supposed to function now.<br /> <br /> I wandered downstairs about nine this morning. No one else was up yet, and Gawain was still out at Monica\u2019s, so I decided that I would make Sex Breakfast for once. Now, as anyone who has ever tasted my cooking will attest, I am not the world\u2019s greatest chef\u2026 but I figured I could probably manage some nice simple omelets. I diced the ham, cheddar, and monterey jack cheese, cracked open a couple of eggs, and started to hum as I cooked.<br /> <br /> Jacob was downstairs first, and he let the unusual sight of me cooking pass with nothing but a simple \u201cthank you\u201d when I handed him the first of the omelets. Calamity filed in a little later, looked at me, quirked an eyebrow, shrugged, slipped up behind me, pressed up against my back, kissed my neck, and whispered \u201cgood morning, handsome,\u201d like she usually does with Gawain. I laughed it off and gave her the second omelet.<br /> <br /> My darklings filed in together a little later. Julia in particular was in a playful mood, and kept repeating the French phrase \u201cOmelet du fromage!\u201d in a chipper voice, much to Marguerite\u2019s consternation. She\u2019s done that before, and I didn\u2019t get it then either. I served her up next, asking in a dry voice if she would like a plate of \u201cscramble eggs folded over cheese,\u201d to which she nodded and said \u201coui!\u201d Gawain arrived last (I don\u2019t know where Ace was this morning), thanked me for doing the cooking, and set to his meal with gusto. I confess I put a little food coloring in his, to create a \u201cGreen Eggs and Ham\u201d omelet.<br /> <br /> D had to head off to work for a bit, and lamented the fact that she was going to have to dodge come-ons from doctors who couldn\u2019t take a hint. I tried to commiserate with her, but figured there wasn\u2019t much I could do to help. She got one of those almost shy looks on her face and sort of mumbled something I couldn\u2019t quite make out. I asked for elaboration, she took a deep breath and repeated \u201cif you want to, you could stop by the hospital around 2:30 and bring me my lunch.\u201d<br /> <br /> I told her I\u2019d love to do that, and she came back to herself, grinning cockily. \u201cCool. If enough people see me dry-humping you in the break room, maybe my co-workers will catch on.\u201d Then she headed out.<br /> <br /> Marguerite went out to the stage to work on her choreography a little later. As soon as she was out of the room, Julia asked to talk to the rest of us. She had met with Boss Lowjack last night and asked him to put her in contact with the courts in Paris. She\u2019s adamant about talking to them and clearing Marguerite\u2019s name. Lowjack promised to do what he could, but only on the condition that she bring the rest of us in on the plan. He is of the opinion \u2013 and I can\u2019t say I disagree \u2013 that the courts in Paris wouldn\u2019t put too much stock in the word of someone who is so obviously in love with the accused. And since one of the things Marguerite is accused of is essentially brainwashing those she kidnapped\u2026<br /> <br /> In any case, of course we all agreed to help in any way we could. The one thing upon which I insisted before I would agree was that we had to be open and honest with Marguerite about what we were doing. I promised that I would help her plead our case; help convince Marguerite that this was something we all needed to do, but I wasn\u2019t going to make such a huge decision about her life without her knowledge. Julia wasn\u2019t happy about the condition \u2013 I\u2019m not sure how she thought she was going to do all this without Marguerite\u2019s consent, but there you are \u2013 but eventually she agreed to it.<br /> <br /> So Julia and I interrupted Marguerite\u2019s stage planning for a serious discussion. Perhaps predictably, she wasn\u2019t immediately onboard with Julia\u2019s plan to clear her name. Honestly, she didn\u2019t take as much convincing as I had expected, though. I think her recent bout of homesickness might have helped convince her of the need to clear her name in Paris. We talked a little about strategies, and we\u2019re going to try to get some words of support from the local monarchs. Hopefully that will make pleading our case to the Parisian changelings a little easier.<br /> <br /> At one point, Julia viciously said that she would kill any of Marguerite\u2019s former victims who would dare to slander her name. Marguerite answered her quite sharply, insisting that she would do no such thing. It almost sounded like an order, and Julia seemed to take it as such. Maybe there\u2019s something to this brainwashing stuff after all\u2026<br /> <br /> Nah, that\u2019s just the kind of relationship they have. In any case, I should probably brush up on my French. Sigh\u2026 as if I didn\u2019t have enough studying to get on with.<br /> <br /> Julia also opened another conversation; one that we opted to put on hold until D could join us. She suggested that the four of us make a pledge officially proclaiming our mutual love. It\u2019s a beautiful idea, and I certainly have no doubts about my feelings for these three wonderful girls\u2026 but it\u2019s a big step. It\u2019s not quite tantamount to a marriage in the changeling community, but it\u2019s probably the next best thing. We\u2019ve only known each other for a couple of months, after all. I\u2019m not saying that I won\u2019t make the pledge if the others want to\u2026 but I need time to think about it first.<br /> <br /> In any case, Gawain very graciously whipped something together for D\u2019s lunch, and I took my leave and drove down to the hospital. I\u2019d dressed up in an ensemble that looked casual, but was in fact carefully selected to be flattering. I admit I wanted to impress the people D works with. I wore a loose green top with spaghetti straps and a pair of white pants; tight enough to show off my curves but loose enough to be comfortable. Not to toot my own horn, but I think I looked pretty damn good.<br /> <br /> I got directions to the break room from a nice security guard at the door. D spotted me as soon as I entered, and walked quickly up to me. I caught her checking surreptitiously to make sure all of her co-workers were watching before she threw her arms around my neck and kissed me passionately. I returned her kiss with equal ardor. \u201cHey gorgeous,\u201d she said when she came up for air, \u201ccouldn\u2019t wait until tonight to fuck me, huh?\u201d<br /> <br /> I rolled my eyes, but couldn\u2019t suppress the big goofy grin on my face. \u201cYou know it, hot stuff,\u201d I said, punctuating it with another quick kiss, \u201cbut I also brought your lunch.\u201d She introduced me to a couple of her friends and co-workers, who all seemed nice enough, and then we sat down to eat together. It was a most pleasant meal, but duty called, and all too soon I had to head back for the final dress rehearsal. I actually got back with a little time to spare, and I\u2019ve been using it to write this diary entry.<br /> <br /> So, to recap. I have one friend who is hysterically upset that we did what we could to protect her from a Gentry artifact. I have another friend who is devastated by this attitude. I have one lover who is pushing for us to get involved in what promises to be a very difficult legal matter. I have another lover who is at the center of that matter. I have my directorial debut coming up at one of the biggest events of the year tomorrow evening. And I have my increasingly intrusive studies to focus on. And none of this is even touching on my plans to head back into Arcadia to rescue Missy and Jane.<br /> <br /> And then there\u2019s Julia\u2019s idea about a pledge between herself, D, Marguerite and me. I love them all; I really do. But a part of me can\u2019t help but wonder\u2026 if I do enter into this pledge with the three of them, how is that going to make Oleander feel?<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Well, things could have gone better. Andromeda and Joan came to the club tonight for the show. Things were going well until Joan left to get drinks and Andromeda asked what had been decided about the Table. Not thinking to be anything but honest, we answered her. She did not take this well. To say she was upset was an understatement. She yelled about not being able to help people if she couldn\u2019t use the Table and ran down the stairs. Calamity tried to catch her, which did not go exactly as planned. Calamity of course has shards of glass coming out of her body and Andromeda was squirming like a woman possessed. Needless to say, she got cut. She brushed the injury off and kept running down the stairs. I managed to catch her after that. I tried to be as gentle as I could, but still not allow her to hurt herself or me. I started to walk back towards the stairs to bring her to the quiet room we\u2019d prepared earlier, when Lori came by to see what was going on. She saw that Andromeda was wounded and immediately healed her. I\u2019ll admit that I had not thought about healing or treating her wounds just yet. My only goal was to get her back to the room and get her calmed down. I figured others would do the calming, and once that was done we could address the bleeding. Lori, being the sweet natured person that she is, sees a hurt and has to fix it.<br /> <br /> Getting her back upstairs was not easy. She was fighting and yelling the entire time. I will admit that this was not the most comfortable thing for me to be doing. I think it reminded me too much of taking people back to the Lady. If someone was struggling too much I would just knock them out and carry them, but there were plenty that I just dragged back. Andromeda was fighting rather hard, but I was not going to knock her out. It would do nothing good for her and it would not look very good for me. So, I endured the screaming and the struggling and \u201cguided\u201d her back up the stairs. Even when we\u2019d gotten back in the room she was screaming that we had taken away her ability to help people, and that she needed to be able to do that. She also yelled that Joan had taken away her ability to choose and that the other woman was not looking out for her. Joan looked rather upset and left the room as Andromeda continued to scream. Then suddenly there was a hand slapping Andromeda across the face. It took me a second to realize that the person that had slapped the other girl was none other than Lorelei. Lori looked livid. She argued back that Joan had done nothing but look out for her for the past several weeks. She described just how far Joan had gone for her and what it had done to the woman in white to care for Andromeda as she slowly recovered. Andromeda quieted instantly and said \u201cYes ma\u2019am.\u201d She stopped screaming, but she was still crying. She then said that she wanted to be alone and for the most part we all agreed that was okay. We her alone in the room and asked Insincere Marguerite to watch the door. The slight darkling had not seen what had happened in the room, but understood that Andromeda was upset and agreed readily enough to keep an eye out.<br /> <br /> After all that De La Rocha went after Joan and started to explain to her that she had done nothing wrong, and that Andromeda was just surprised and upset. She kept talking as I headed back towards the bar. I saw Gawain headed towards the table with Joan and De La Rocha, so I figured the normally stoic woman was in good hands. When I got back to the bar one of our regular customers was there with a smile on his face and said that he wanted to try something new. He always wants to try something new, so I get to experiment and mix different drinks and see how well they turn out. His name is Richard. I know that he works as a vet at a local animal rescue. He comes in and tells me about the latest animal that was brought in. Sometimes they are happy stories, sometimes not so much. But he always talks for about ten minutes, has at most two drinks, never the same, and then goes to a table to enjoy the show. He is always polite, not usually maudlin, and seems impressed that I remember what drinks he\u2019s tried and which ones he hasn\u2019t. He came in tonight and had a Fuzzy Navel and a Nikolaschka. I substituted vodka for the cognac, since I know that is not his favorite alcoholic beverage, and he seemed to like it just fine. Insincere Marguerite would probably be offended by my substitution.<br /> <br /> After Richard went to watch the show Boss Lowjack came by and said that he needed to talk to me. I said sure and was about to grab my assistant when Julia came by. She seemed upset, and told Lowjack that she wanted to discuss something with him alone. He explained that as the Winter monarch he couldn\u2019t go off with anyone alone, so asked if she minded if I came along too. She obviously did mind, but said that it would be fine. So, we went to a private room and talked. Turns out that Julia was really upset about the Freehold in Paris labelling Insincere Marguerite as a loyalist and wanted to clear her name. Julia wanted the contact information for the French Freehold. She was rather adamant about this and said that she would slit the throat of anyone who talked down about her love. I really wanted to point out that her attitude would not help any, but Lowjack beat me to it. Though he phrased it much better than I\u2019m sure I could have. He explained to her that he would not provide any information for the Courts of Love unless she involved the rest of us in the Dream House. He even wanted her to take a Pledge to this effect. She agreed readily enough.<br /> <br /> We discussed things a bit further after that. Lowjack reiterated that threatening the other freehold would be counterproductive, and I suggested that a neutral party should be the one to talk to the Monarchs of the Parisian courts. It would look less biased and perhaps more objective and factual. Since Marguerite was basically accused of the coercion of several young ladies, it would perhaps not carry much weight to have a similar young lady be the spearhead to clear her lover\u2019s name. Julia agreed to the third party spokesperson idea. I figure that we\u2019ll come up with who that\u2019ll be when Julia brings this up with the other members of the household.<br /> <br /> After our little conversation I got Julia a drink at the bar and talked to Lowjack. It turns out that he just wanted to make sure that I was all set for the High Summer event. I told him about my little plan for trying out new drinks on some of our more adventurous customers. He thought it was a good idea.<br /> <br /> When the show was over Dahlia came by to talk to Calamity to find out what we have discovered about what has been going on recently and specifically what happened the night that Becky accidentally cut Flores. During the recapping of what happened they discovered that a lot of the same people were present for each of the attacks that happened recently. The attack on Dark Kimberly and the latest \u201cmisunderstanding\u201d at Flores\u2019 club. The people in common are Dark Kimberly, Flores, Becky, Sandoval, Davey and Desiree. Both incidents seemed to be attacks on Dark Kimberly. Both attacks either brought negative attention on Flores\u2019 club or hurt her physically. I don\u2019t think that she was supposed to get hurt the second time. I think it was intended that Kimberly take the brunt of that attack.<br /> <br /> I also can\u2019t help but notice that both attacks took place in a location where there were plenty of Spring Courtiers around to conveniently heal whoever got injured. If it was Dark Kimberly behind both attacks then she could have tried to throw the suspicion off of her by making herself the victim, but in both cases there was no real danger of the injuries doing any lasting harm. All that happened the first time was that Dark Kimberly was in pain for a short period of time. The second time it was Flores, but if she hadn\u2019t gotten in between the two rivals Dark Kimberly very well could have ended up on the floor temporarily bleeding. If someone really wanted to hurt Dark Kimberly they would have stabbed or shot her while she was alone and without means of communication. I can think of half a dozen different scenarios that would have been more effective than what actually happened. Whoever planned the attacks didn\u2019t want them to succeed in doing any real harm, or at least no lasting harm.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> New day, new conversations. This morning since Gawain was actually gone (I think he was at Monica\u2019s place), Lori decided to fill in and make omelets for breakfast. I made coffee as usual. Everyone streamed in to get food. Calamity took it all in stride and walked over to Lori, kissed the back of her neck and said \u201cGood morning handsome.\u201d The eggs were good. I think Lori was a little worried that her food wouldn\u2019t compare to Gawain\u2019s normal fare, but I don\u2019t think that she had any reason to worry. Her breakfast was really good. Still getting used to eggs so often, but I\u2019m not one to complain about food.<br /> <br /> So, after breakfast De La Rocha left for work and Insincere Marguerite went out to the stage to work on the choreography for a dance number she was perfecting. Once the slight darkling was gone Julia explained to the rest of us what her plans were in regards to her lover\u2019s reputation in France. She explained how she wanted to contact the Freehold in Paris and try and convince them that Insincere Marguerite was not a loyalist and to clear her name. She admitted that she was acting on Boss Lowjack\u2019s suggestion to include the rest of us in the planning of any actions involving the Courts of Love. It was pretty much unanimously decided that if we were going to do this for Insincere Marguerite then that self-same person should be involved in the planning and implementing of said plan. So Lori and Julia left to go get Marguerite.<br /> <br /> After Insincere Marguerite came in things were a little tense to start with, but mellowed out soon enough. Marguerite was not keen on approaching the Parisian courts as she was afraid that they would come after her. We reassured her that we would not let anyone do anything to her. The discussion soon turned to who we would ask to speak on her behalf. The idea of asking Queen Charlotte was brought up and I think we all decided that she would be the best person to ask. She is neutral and her voice carries some weight. Between Lorelei and Julia I think we convinced Insincere Marguerite to let us defend her to the Courts of Love.<br /> <br /> It wasn\u2019t too long before the conversation turned back to the upcoming High Summer events and what we were all doing. Lori of course has her play, which I\u2019ll admit that I\u2019m kind of looking forward to see. I like the irony of the humans playing the fairies and the changelings playing the humans. Gawain said that he was planning on participating in the heavy weapon events and some foot races. Calamity is interested in the light blade events, as am I, and also plans to put on a knife throwing demonstration. I for my part am planning on being a bartender for the most part, but also participating in the light blade events and have even agreed to be the \u201ctarget\u201d for Calamity\u2019s show. And I\u2019ll admit that it takes a lot for me to agree to stand against a board and let someone throw knives at me. It takes a damn lot. In a short period of time I have grown to trust these folks, which is odd for me. I learned the hard way that you can\u2019t trust anyone to do anything but what\u2019s right for them, but these people are different. I trust Calamity to have my back in a fight, and I trust her to not intentionally stab me with a throwing knife. I fully realize that there may be accidents, which is part of the reason I agreed to do it. I could not see any of the others up there. If something happens and a knife goes astray I know I can take it. It\u2019s not like it would be the first time I\u2019ve been hurt.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> Last night was difficult.<br /> <br /> Andromeda did indeed show with Joan, and it went about as badly as it could have. She found out she was barred from using the Table and threw a fit. Now, I don\u2019t blame Joan for most of it, but Calamity set her off without knowing Joan had never told her, and frankly that was weeks ago and Joan should have told us she was keeping something like that back. If she had she would not have had to see Gawain, Jacob, and Calamity restraining her girlfriend. Regretfully.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t feel any animosity though. Having been put through the wringer a couple weeks ago she went through it again hearing Andromeda screeching and screaming about making decisions for herself and being restrained\u2026in front of a ton of people, including her peers. Less than forty-eight hours before the big seasonal fete. Unfortunately.<br /> <br /> I would leave town for a couple weeks.<br /> <br /> She did not see Lori slap Andromeda, and I am glad of that. I would have been upset. I hope Lori is okay. She seemed to be last we spoke. She has gone to see De La Rocha. Naturally.<br /> <br /> Sill, a bit like the last time. With Becky.<br /> <br /> I helped, of course; I guarded the door. So it was I her haunted eyes fell on when she asked for her beloved to be brought to her. She didn\u2019t\u2026look as good as she did when she arrived. Emotionally. I worry about her. I mean, she was never one of my lovelies, and based on how she and Joan are I suspect she never will be, but when I look at her\u2026she could have been. Certainly.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I left the haunted eyed creature in Joan\u2019s care, and helped them slip out the back. I swallowed my worries and went on to deal with Julia, who seemed\u2026distracted.<br /> <br /> Julia has been driven by her passions of late. Whether it is her increased production of paintings, charcoal pictures and sketches, her increased movement of her hands, her practically swallowing my face when we kiss and the increase in sex drive. Julia is possessed of a muse. I would say a fiery muse but\u2026I am not fiery. Hopefully.<br /> <br /> She once said she would not sing for I unless we \u201cwere getting married or something.\u201d She sang just the night before last. I suspect she had not forgotten her words when she did. Strongly.<br /> <br /> Now, it turns out, she wants to clear my name in Paris. That\u2019s\u2026I don\u2019t think she realizes how much she sounds like she is under my control. To be fair, she is. But her speaking will not help. I doubt they will believe she invited me to her apartment, and that she did not resist my advances when Flores left. Blissfully.<br /> <br /> I am torn between wanting to get it done and not wanting to have to deal with seeing women who used to belong to me calling for my head. It is shattering. They used to be mine. They are there because I did not trap them for the Gentry to find. If my Dearest is among those calling for my head I\u2026<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t even want to think about it.<br /> <br /> Julia wants ourselves and Lori and De La Rocha to pledge out love before the Wyrd. I have no issue with that. I mean, Lori and De La Rocha have more commitment issues than I do. I suspect De La Rocha might flee when this comes up, actually.<br /> <br /> The White Maria stuff is continuing. Everyone hates her. I wish they wouldn\u2019t. She is cute. She is sassy. Her tongue is a bit sharp, yes, but that does not make her a bad person. Besides, she has always been very nice to I. Maybe they were doing something wrong. Probably.<br /> <br /> De La Rocha is the main sticking point though. She does not like I \u201cMacking On\u201d White Maria. I suspect she does not like her for having the same name. Probably.<br /> <br /> Worrying does not suit I. Maybe tomorrow will be better. Hopefully.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XLI</i><br /> <br /> Calamity is an excellent knife-fighter but not a great brawler. Her attempt to grab Andromeda resulted in a Dramatic Failure (Andromeda\u2019s Defense is pretty good), and she wound up cutting her instead.<br /> <br /> It was pointed out that Andromeda screaming about \u201cbeing able to choose\u201d and \u201ctaking that away\u201d that a lot of people may have thought she was arguing about having an abortion. Probably not the fae though, who know of events with her.<br /> <br /> In fact, the PCs did not handle it as well or as badly as they could have. There will be repercussions for her trauma, mostly on her, but it\u2019s still better than if she had escaped.<br /> <br /> Madam Spidertoes has a frailty about washing bloody clothes, which resulted in her acting bizarrely with Calamity.<br /> <br /> With the Monica carrying off Gawain and Lori seducing De La Rocha callbacks, I could not resist \u201cOmelet Du Fromage\u201d<br /> <br /> Okay, I think that covers everything. Next time they try to fix the damage to Andromeda, and more drama happens. Comments and Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 10-27-2015, 02:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T22:59:45-07:00","id":740969,"title":"","content":"Well, things just got real with Lori there.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Song Bird trails darkness behind her<br /> Depths filled with screams and laughter<br /> Fear not her flight<br /> Give in to the night<br /> And wake the morning after?&quot;<br /> <br /> ... Well that kind of came from nowhere, and has nothing to do with my first statement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","user":"omenseer","date":". 10-30-2015, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T00:05:26-07:00","id":743925,"title":"","content":"Some of the feedback I get on the forums are from PMs or discussions outside the forum threads where the games are discussed. A number of them can be applied pretty broadly to my games, so I paraphrased some and put some info down here to \u201cdraw back the curtain\u201d as it were as I thought some would be of interest to some readers. Add your own if you wish, as always.<br /> <br /> <b>You have a lot of female characters in your games. Like, most of them. Is this on purpose?</b><br /> <br /> Yes, yes I do. Some of it is deliberate. Media is all about men, and many TV shows, movies, books and, honestly, role-playing campaigns have few females that are often lovers, prizes, victims or relatives. I try to make women who fit every conceivable role, but have many male characters too.<br /> <br /> At the same time, I just come up with female characters more easily, and since I cull pictures from the internet which provide inspiration for PCs, the fact that I have way more female pictures means I get inspired for female characters more often. That is not deliberate, just the way it turns out.<br /> <br /> <b>How about LGBTQ characters? Same?</b><br /> <br /> Most NPCs are actually Herosexual. With a few exceptions such as Captain Jack, Luna, or Madam Spidertoes (Julia was not originally designed to be a lesbian, but just sort of evolved that way; she was always designed to be easier for females though) most NPCs orientation is such that they would be interested in PCs interested in them. Those with exceptions are NPCs whose concept defines their sexuality, and they are rare. Then sometimes as I see them in action NPCs seem to make good couples or drift together. I have no bias to create gay or straight couples this way. It just happens. However, see above that women outnumber men. I am proud, however, of the queer representation in my games.<br /> <br /> Of course, just because an NPC could fall for a PC of either sex does not mean they are equally easy to woo. Desiree could go either way but is easier for men, for example.<br /> <br /> <b>No gay male relationships with PCs, but there are several lesbians\u2026</b><br /> <br /> I don\u2019t tell my players what orientation to make their PCs. If a male character wants to have a relationship with a male NPC that\u2019s fine (it even happened in my <i>Masquerade</i> game) but it is what the players want.<br /> <br /> <b>You have less Trans characters than I expected.</b><br /> <br /> Yea, not so impressive regarding those numbers. Luna and Moon are trans, and I promise you the naming is a coincidence, they were conceived months apart, and Luna is named for a moth. Moon is explicitly genderqueer, and the only trans character for whom it is a major part of their concept. Luna is the only transwoman not a POC.<br /> <br /> <b>You have a lot of, um, sex in your game. Is everyone okay with it?</b><br /> <br /> Yes, yes I do. I will speak plainly. Sex for me is way more interesting than violence. I\u2019d be more interested in seeing a PC having a torrid affair than a gunfight. This does not mean my games are without action; <i>The Golden Eagle</i> has a setting conceit allowing for more danger and daring-do since the conceit prevents a PC revolving door. There is more action there than other games. <i>Night Train Detective Agency</i> has more action than <i>Balance of Shadows</i> or <i>Malibu Dream House</i>, because it is spy-noir, while <i>The Golden Eagle</i> is part noir, part mystery, part pulp. But yes, relationships are a huge thing.<br /> <br /> My players know this, and new players are told before they join. No player has to play romantic relationships, straight or queer.<br /> <br /> For the record, we almost always fade to black unless there is a good reason not to, and sex is only rolled if something besides having a good time is going on, such as getting a foe vulnerable, staying awake so the PC can rummage through their partners stuff, staying awake so their partner can\u2019t rummage through theirs, impressing a countess, etc.<br /> <br /> <b>So everyone has pictures, can I see a picture of [NPC]?</b><br /> <br /> Probably. If it is a picture culled from the internet and you want to see an NPC, I will show it unless I am using the picture with particular permission of the photographer or model, in which case no because they have not given me permission for that.<br /> <br /> <b>How many of your players are women/lesbian/bisexual/giraffes/etc</b><br /> <br /> I am not going to give out too much information on my players. I will say every game linked in my sig has a mix of male and female and straight and LGBTQ players. Most games hover somewhere close to 50/50 male female, or one more of one or the other. <i>The Golden Eagle</i> is the exception, with many more women than men. I will tell you, if you have read about a female PC having relationships with female NPCs in these games and assumed they are being played by a guy you will be wrong much more often than not.<br /> <br /> <b>Do Players plan their PCs relationships before the game starts?</b><br /> <br /> Not usually. Sometimes they have an idea getting together is likely. Calamity and Gawain had a connection and romantic tension from design, for example.<br /> <br /> <b>What genre would you call your games</b><br /> <br /> Mystery/Supernatural Drama. <i>Balance of Shadows</i> has ghost story elements. <i>Night Train Detective Agency</i> has noir and spy elements, and <i>The Golden Eagle</i> has noir, pulp, and mystery. <i>Malibu Dream House</i> is more pure mystery-drama.<br /> <br /> <b>Can I play in your game?</b><br /> <br /> Probably not. If you live in North Carolina we can discuss it, but even then probably not. My games are almost all full.<br /> <br /> Normal Journals next week, wherein our heroes seek to help repair Andromeda's fractured mind, and Insincere Marguerite seduces someone she probably shouldn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 10-31-2015, 03:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T01:42:55-07:00","id":743974,"title":"","content":"As her player, I can add a bit to some of these as far as Calamity is concerned. <br /> <br /> Calamity's sexuality isn't terribly physical/gender based. She is drawn to a more predator/prey relationship. Mechanically, she has a derangement that requires a self control roll to resist harming someone when she has the opportunity. In short, she is a sadist, and violence has a sexual connection for her. This is one of the things that she's striving to learn to control in herself. The result is that she's attracted to victims and feels a desire to both abuse/hurt them and protect them. In general, the more she wants to do terrible things to someone, the more she feels they need to be protected from those who share her particular hungers but not her self-control. <br /> <br /> Also, stemming from the way the Whispering Voices expressed physical and verbal tenderness and concern after punishing her and that this was the only affection she revived in Snow Globe she has some odd reactions to pain and being hurt. Basically, she's drawn to predators stronger than herself. She is not submissive but she is turned on by acts of physical dominance and pain. <br /> <br /> Thus she's attracted to those who are are predatory and strong enough to overpower her (Charlotte, Becky, and Lucien for instance) and she's attracted to victims (such as Dark Kimberly and Andromeda) But she isn't strongly attracted to Juan Carlos or Jolie because while they are beautiful and sexy they don't trip either of those buttons. So for her gender isn't terribly relevant to her sexual attraction. As she has stated, &quot;If you're not prepared to bleed or draw blood then you're wasting my time.&quot;<br /> <br /> She's attracted to Gawain because he genuinely loves her and after spending twenty years in a place where the closest thing to that was an abusive unseen Keeper she has a need and desire for that so strong that she finds it absolutely terrifying. Also, twenty years of being told she is unworthy of love is hard to shake off which is why she continues to find it so hard to believe and keeps expecting Gawain to come to his senses and leave her.<br /> <br /> Now, as far as her encounters and her journals, there was a fade to black at the game session as mentioned. After, I generally get some general details and perhaps a couple of details (such as how Becky reacted to her not sleeping or how she answered the attempt to ask her what she likes for instance) from either Baroness Narek or the other player and then made sure to run the final by them to verification. Usually there are minor edits (though her second time with Andromeda was initially written without knowing how strong a trigger knives are to the poor girl... that was a bit of rewriting.) In general, we all do that with anything involving another PC or NPC that wasn't 'on screen' at the session. <br /> <br /> For me it's a lot about getting into Calamity's mind and puzzling out how her history would have shaped her and how she'd deal with and react to things.The story is interesting despite and often because of her failures.It also means that for the most part, I try not to let my own interests influence Calamity's attractions too much. <br /> <br /> And if that's not already more than you wanted to know, feel free to ask. I rather like talking about Calamity. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T01:52:14-07:00","id":743985,"title":"","content":"I thought she just liked hugs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T02:03:22-07:00","id":743999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroness Nerak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play?p=743985#post743985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought she just liked hugs.</div> </div> </div> </div>She likes hugs from Gawain because he's strong and made of metal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T08:54:52-07:00","id":744557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amberghylles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play?p=743974#post743974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And if that's not already more than you wanted to know, feel free to ask. I rather like talking about Calamity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would she poke, in a bad, anyone who calls her Jane?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T00:16:38-07:00","id":746021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play?p=744557#post744557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would she poke, in a bad, anyone who calls her Jane?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe. She would most likely ask them firmly not to at least the first time. You see, in Snow Globe, people were brought to fill roles. So while she was there, she was Jane, younger sister to Richard (aka Dick). The connection is actually where she got Calamity since after escaping she was asked her name and still being very fuzzy headed from Arcadia her mind went from &quot;Not Jane&quot; to &quot;Calamitiy&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T09:09:33-08:00","id":746721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amberghylles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play?p=746021#post746021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe. She would most likely ask them firmly not to at least the first time. You see, in Snow Globe, people were brought to fill roles. So while she was there, she was Jane, younger sister to Richard (aka Dick). The connection is actually where she got Calamity since after escaping she was asked her name and still being very fuzzy headed from Arcadia her mind went from &quot;Not Jane&quot; to &quot;Calamitiy&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooh, OK. I gets it now. What's her opinion on the use of whips though <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T01:14:14-08:00","id":756008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play?p=746721#post746721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oooh, OK. I gets it now. What's her opinion on the use of whips though <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Calamity is in favor of whips as recreational tools. Given that her stage acts for the Dream House have a very Dominatrix flair and she's quite adept with weaponry, she may well use one in her act.<br /> <br /> As far as actual fighting, she's loyal to her knives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T17:37:20-08:00","id":757557,"title":"","content":"One of the reasons I like Baroness Nerak's APs so much is how predominant character interaction is.<br /> The relationships, the drama, the simple fun, even when there is no action. It's so different from the packs of sociopathic murder hobos I'm used to see rampaging through various settings. The NPCs are deep and complex, the PCs have meaningful relationships with them and ech of these relationships can lead to an adventure. That's awesome.<br /> <br /> Does Calamity's focus on Predator/prey dynamics make her less sensitive to Lori's charms? There seemed to be some attraction at the start, but it seems to have mostly faded now.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T01:07:08-08:00","id":758176,"title":"","content":"Thanks that really means a lot.<br /> <br /> Lots of games and GMs have their strengths. I have had GMs that run incredibly compelling narratives. Stories good enough to be a book. I've played under GM's who could run a fight scene with the best pacing and <i>juuuuust </i>the right amount of tension. I've had a GM who could run an awesome dungeon crawl you looked forward to planning, and a GM who put you though the wringer and you did not care because it was so awesome. My strength is scenarios, characters, relationships. My stories are not terrible, but nothing to write home about. What makes them work, I think, are the NPCs, their complexity, their and both where they are unpredictable and predictable. I love it when players start putting together stuff about an NPC's past, or what their behavior may mean. Honestly, if I could get togather with someone who does plot well, I could do a lot with characters or relationships and we could get a hell of a book out.<br /> <br /> Of course, it is not just me. My players are great. They play all sorts of characters. They communicate what they want. They react to a complex tapestry of NPCs and relationships by giving their characters those themselves. No matter how good a GM I was my stories would not be so good without them. My players are <i>awesome</i>.<br /> <br /> And when I get people reading the APs and saying they are inspired to run games like this I feel good. I every bit want all sorts of games in our hobby, from dungeon crawls to mysteries to epic journeys. I am happy to say my peace for urban fantasies with a bit of soap opera and a bit of mystery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 11-06-2015, 04:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T02:24:30-08:00","id":758310,"title":"","content":"Fair question Anteros. Calamity has not stopped being fond of Lori and she stills thinks of the wee songbird as a rather delicious morsel. She does still flirt with Lori but given the foursome that she, Insincere Marguerite, DLR, and Julia have formed Calamity hasn't pushed it too strongly. And despite the occasional (almost completely joking) comment about being the only female in the Dream House not invited to the fun, she's happy for them. That said, if Lori ever seemed interested in a repeat of their prior encounter Calamity would be quite willing and interested. But, as with Dark Kimberly and Andromeda, she's happy to see Lori in a stable relationship with someone that isn't considering what sort of noises she'd make when cut or just what her blood tastes like.<br /> <br /> Honestly, Calamity tends to try to find 'better' lovers for the people she's attracted to because, well, she's got self-loathing issues and figures that if she really likes them then she should make sure they're with someone more worthy/less dangerous than herself. She still does this with Gawain to a certain extent, though she also has the very contradictory intensely jealous/clingy feelings for him.<br /> <br /> Also, I do enjoy playing someone who is kinda a classic murder hobo in a game that's not hack and slash. And while Calamity is far from the first violent/murderous character I've played, she is the first that is honestly concerned and troubled by that aspect of herself. Which is because I haven't ever played a game truly suited to that depth of character introspection before.getting into the group with Baroness Nerak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T13:01:07-08:00","id":760874,"title":"","content":"Andromeda\u2019s return to Changeling Society was not what she or her beloved hoped. Now, traumatized and withdrawn into her mind, she waits, her favorite music playing as her beloved Joan tries to draw her out. Maybe the Last Dance Motley can set things right.<br /> <br /> Note Calamity\u2019s journal covers two sessions.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XLII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> June 17th, morning<br /> <br /> The Spring Court\u2019s wake up power is the best, really. It\u2019s time for Highsummer festivities and despite not sleeping any last night, I\u2019m still, you know, raring to go. It helps that I think we really did some good last night. I mean, even just holding vigil with Joan would have been doing good, but I think we really helped.<br /> <br /> See, De la Roche caught us all before the show yesterday, to tell us that Andromeda had, you know, withdrawn again. Except that it wasn\u2019t really again, cause it wasn\u2019t like it was before, she was super emotional, just not, you know, interacting with people. Unless Joan started crying, then Andromeda would get upset.<br /> <br /> Moon checked her out and said it was trauma from what happened the night before at the Dream House. Spring courtiers were keeping an eye on her to make sure her desire to run away to her Keeper (the last place where no one betrayed her) didn\u2019t, you know, overwhelm her. Joan was standing vigil to make sure she didn\u2019t make a break for it or try to hurt herself and Monica sat up with her. Calamity went to check on her during the first part of the show too. Apparently Andromeda wanted to talk to her, but not more than she wanted to stay hidden in her own mind, same as she did with Joan. So Calamity decided to try and craft a dream for her, with my help.<br /> <br /> We, me and Calamity and Jacob for moral support, went back after the show. She wasn\u2019t asleep yet, but I came prepared with a deck of cards. I managed to cajole Joan into playing by overruling Mary Helene\u2019s suggestion of strip poker. I hope it helped her relax some, a t least a little. She certainly wasn\u2019t gonna get actual, you know, rest.<br /> <br /> The dream weaving went awesomely. We were going for subtle, you know, taking the already existing elements and making them more here than Mothershippy, and making Joan more like she was than what she seemed to be to Andromeda at the moment. She didn\u2019t kick us out which we were afraid of - she did Moon and Chalcedony. But Calamity was point and apparently was welcome enough.<br /> <br /> And it worked! When she woke, Joan was right there and Andromeda actually talked to her! Mary Helene scanned her and found she really did, you know, seem to be better, and Calamity got to talk with her some and everything. Joan said they repledged their love and support for each other and might even show up at Highsummer! I really hope they do.<br /> <br /> All that, and I even managed to do some investigating. I almost forgot to - I was just talking to Desiree to make sure she was doing alright and she mentioned Becky not liking her, so I got reminded. She\u2019d wanted to talk with Princess Joli that day cause she was feeling insecure and upset, with Felicity being kinda a rival now, and Queen Charlotte being jealous of her and all, you know? I told her that maybe those two problems canceled each other out a little - if Queen Charlotte is only jealous of Desiree and not Felicity, maybe she knows Felicity isn\u2019t really a rival, right? I also promised to ask Calamity to talk to Queen Charlotte about it. I dunno if it helped, but I think trying to help out with the investigation did, at least as a distraction.<br /> <br /> And she helped a lot. She gave us a whole new lead, that we talked about over our oatmeal and fruit sex breakfast, after White Maria left. That was a whole bundle of exciting there - even I could, you know, feel the tension between White Maria and De la Roche. Anyway, Desiree mentioned that Bedlam could have been what was used on Becky, instead of some Summer Court Contract. It would make Becky act out her strongest instincts and especially since Desiree was certain the attack was timed or when she was closest to Dark Kimberly and was predicated with eye contact between them, there was a lot of rage in Becky at that moment. Becky even said earlier, according to Desiree, that she\u2019d kill Desiree if she gave her any excuse to do so, you know, legally. She\u2019s got a serious thing for Princess Joli, I guess.<br /> <br /> But anyway, with the Bedlam, it could have been used even like an hour beforehand. So that kinda opened the field then closed it again, since, you know, you have to be really powerful to do that. The Warlock, Madame Spidertoes, Annika, Tommy and maybe Sidhe and Darke were the only ones we could think of. Chalcedony might, and might be hiding it, since all her blue might be a Wyrd frailty. Or maybe just an eccentricity, you know? But it did get into her contract with the Dream House even. And if it was a pre setup thing, it could have been easier to know that Becky was gonna be near Desiree than Dark Kimberly. So Chalcedony\u2019s dislike of Desiree might be the motive...<br /> <br /> But that\u2019s to look into later. Now it\u2019s time for Highsummer and it\u2019s going to be awesome! I promised I\u2019d hang out with Desiree some, since she was bummed that Felicity would be Princess Joli\u2019s official date. And Joan and Andromeda might show up. And my \u201cofficial date\u201d is rocking just enough leather and a whole lot of Calamity. It\u2019s gonna be a good day, I know it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> This is necessarily going to be one of my shorter entries; I only have about half an hour before we have to head out to the Highsummer Festival. I\u2019m already laced into my tight corset \u2013 thanks for that, Julia \u2013 and ready to head out, but some of the others are still getting prepared.<br /> <br /> Okay, so a few things have happened since I last wrote in this journal. First, when D got back from work yesterday, my honey informed us all that Andromeda\u2019s fragile mental state had not improved. In fact, she seemed to have dropped into a sort of fugue state, and refused to communicate with anyone except Joan. The Spring Court had people watching her and checking her desires every half hour or so to make sure that she wasn\u2019t about to bolt back into the Hedge to rejoin the Mothership. And yes, according to Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne and Chalcedony, that was a real danger. She felt betrayed and rejected by the Changelings of the Freehold, and subconsciously longed for the security and clarity of purpose she felt with her Keeper, and only her love of Joan was so far keeping her from bolting.<br /> <br /> Apparently restraining her, cutting her, and slapping her the other day only added to the sense of betrayal she was already feeling. Yeah, I already feel like shit about that, so no need to dwell on it now.<br /> <br /> Calamity and Gawain offered to head over to Joan\u2019s place to see if they could help, and Jacob and Marguerite went with them for moral support. Gawain wanted to try a little dream therapy, and Calamity felt that the bond she shares with Andromeda might help the poor girl to open up a bit. According to their reports the next morning, there are hopeful signs. Calamity has almost convinced Joan to let the Winter Court\u2019s therapists speak with Andromeda\u2026 and considering how well they seemed to have worked their magic on Calamity herself, I can only see that as a good thing. Gawain crafted a dream for Andromeda that should help her to see things a little more clearly. He didn\u2019t go into details about the dream itself, but I think he cast Joan as a protector rather than a restrictive element.<br /> <br /> God, I hope she feels better soon. If nothing else, I feel horrible about that little slap the other night. I lost control for a second, and made things worse for the poor girl. I\u2019d really like to apologize to her, when she\u2019s ready to hear it. That\u2019s the main reason I didn\u2019t offer to go with Calamity and Gawain last night, of course\u2026 I was afraid that the sight of me would just make things worse after my outburst.<br /> <br /> Of course, we didn\u2019t exactly have a quiet night here at the Dream House, either. The show went well enough, though it wasn\u2019t one of our better nights. Many of our regulars were taking it easy due to tonight\u2019s big production, and I felt that my attention would be better served working on the play than planning and rehearsing new numbers for the Dream House. The gate was still pretty good, we sold a fair number of drinks, and people seemed to enjoy themselves\u2026 which I suppose is the only yardstick that matters when measuring our club\u2019s success.<br /> <br /> White Maria showed up to watch the show. She\u2019s been coming around a lot more lately \u2013 not that she\u2019s ever been a stranger to our club \u2013 and I can only assume that it has something to do with Insincere Marguerite\u2019s continued attempts to seduce her. Well, those attempts bore fruit tonight after Marguerite got back from Joan\u2019s place. D was\u2026 not pleased, to say the least, and while we were socializing with Moon and Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne (who was not on Andromeda Watch at the time), she turned her back pointedly on our French friend and tried her best to pretend that she couldn\u2019t see what was happening across the room.<br /> <br /> I tried to take her mind off our paramour with idle conversation and copious booze, but in the end I just took her hand and led her up to our boudoir for a little lovin\u2019. Before we got to anything physical, however, she turned very serious and said she wanted to talk to me. I admit to a little trepidation, but asked what was on her mind.<br /> <br /> \u201cLori,\u201d she began softly, \u201cI\u2019ve seen what\u2019s going on around the Freehold. Relationships are breaking down all over the place. Joan and Andromeda are having trouble, Annika and Kimberly are fighting, Monica and Haley split. It\u2019s like a goddamn epidemic.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled in what I hoped was a reassuring way. \u201cNothing like that is going to happen to us, sweetie,\u201d I said softly.<br /> <br /> She smiled weakly. \u201cI know. I\u2019m not really worried about it. Hell, it\u2019s probably just the turn of the seasons. Everyone hooks up in Spring, when Desire is heavy in the air. And then Summer comes, and Anger takes its place\u2026 it\u2019s the natural cycle. But\u2026 you mean so much to me, Lori. I don\u2019t want to risk anything like that happening to us. So this is it. I\u2019m giving you carte blanche. I know my previous relationship with Spidertoes has been a\u2026 touchy subject, but I want you to know that you can ask me anything, and I\u2019ll answer it as truthfully as I can.\u201d<br /> <br /> I was blown away. D is usually such a private person. I know she\u2019s opened up to me more than she does to pretty much anyone else, but this was on a whole new level. I confess that for a few minutes my mind was blank. I couldn\u2019t think of anything I wanted to know. I\u2019ve always accepted that her relationship with Madame Spidertoes was a huge part of D\u2019s past. It was very intense. And anything that means that much to you is bound to leave its mark.<br /> <br /> \u201cJust answer me one thing,\u201d I said softly. \u201cDid she ever hurt you?\u201d<br /> <br /> D smiled, reached out, and stroked my hair gently. \u201cNot intentionally,\u201d she said, and I was shocked to see a sheen of moisture in her eyes. \u201cNot like you mean, anyway. I think we hurt each other plenty without meaning to, though.\u201d<br /> <br /> I waved that off, and told her I was satisfied; that I trust her. She nodded gratefully and took my hand as she went on. \u201cIt\u2019s just\u2026 I want you to understand why I react the way I do when people talk about her.\u201d She took a deep breath, and then took the plunge. \u201cShe\u2019s <u><u>old</u></u>, Lori. I mean, everybody knows that, but most people don\u2019t seem to <u><u>get</u></u> it. I know you understand what it feels like to be left behind by the world, but she suffered through her Durance before cars were invented. You\u2019ve seen how hard it can be for older people to adapt new technology like cell phones, right? Well she had to go through that with light bulbs. She\u2019s incredibly intelligent, and wise, and powerful, and she puts everything she has into this Freehold, and all she asks in return is that we put up with a few quirks and go to the occasional tea party\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026and people talk about her like she\u2019s some sort of freak,\u201d I finished for her softly. \u201cI\u2019m sorry, D. I never really thought about it like that before.\u201d We were both quiet for a minute or two. I cracked first. \u201cWhen you and I\u2026 when we first got involved, she asked to speak with me,\u201d I said hesitantly.<br /> <br /> D nodded. \u201cI remember,\u201d she said.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt was a little scary,\u201d I admitted. \u201cShe\u2019s so powerful, and she still cares for you so <u><u>fiercely</u></u>. I think she wanted to make sure that I would treat you well. But she also offered me some advice on how to make you happy. That was very important to her. And then, later that evening, she sent me a letter to apologize for confronting me like that. It was delivered by\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSpiders,\u201d D finished, the hint of a grin touching the corners of her mouth. \u201cIt\u2019s kind of her thing.\u201d<br /> <br /> We both chuckled at that, and things were okay for a while. We\u2026 actually, we mostly just slept last night. It was nice; and I think it made us both feel comfortable and loved. At least I hope so.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, whatever sitcom gods watch over my life applied their sense of awkward comic timing acutely the next morning. D and I were just about to head down to sex breakfast when she stopped dead in the doorway in front of me. I leaned around her and spied the reason immediately: White Maria was emerging from Marguerite\u2019s bedroom, looking disheveled and decidedly uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat the <u><u>fuck?</u> </u>\u201d D growled dangerously.<br /> <br /> Marguerite peered out of her bedroom looking very pleased with herself indeed. \u201cIs there a problem?\u201d she asked innocently.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo,\u201d I said, edging my way around D and into the hall.<br /> <br /> \u201cYes,\u201d D said at almost the exact same instant. Anger and disbelief slipped across her face, and I thought I caught a glimpse of genuine hurt there as well. \u201cI <u><u>told</u></u> you not to fuck her, Insincere Marguerite.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t want to cause trouble between you,\u201d White Maria said softly, \u201cI\u2019ll just go.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo,\u201d I said firmly, placing a hand on D\u2019s shoulder. \u201cYou\u2019re a guest in our house, White Maria, and you\u2019re welcome here.\u201d I turned back to face D. \u201cSweetie, Marguerite is a grown woman; she can make her own decisions. We don\u2019t have any right to tell her who she can sleep with.\u201d D gritted her teeth, and I could tell that she planned to argue with me, so I headed her off. \u201cRemember what you were talking about last night, hon? About how so many relationships seem to be breaking down for no good reason lately? We don\u2019t want that to happen here, do we?\u201d<br /> <br /> She still looked inclined to argue, but I saw something click into place behind her eyes. She nodded slightly, and turned to face White Maria. \u201cI\u2019ve been rude,\u201d she said grudgingly, \u201cyou can stay for breakfast if you want to.\u201d<br /> <br /> White Maria sighed. \u201cI\u2026 I don\u2019t want to cause problems for you,\u201d she said to the hall at large. I\u2019ll just go.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cStay for breakfast,\u201d Marguerite said imperiously.<br /> <br /> I decided to take a more diplomatic tack. \u201cPlease, White Maria,\u201d I said, \u201cwe\u2019re going to have to get past this at some point. Stick around; Gawain is an incredible cook.\u201d<br /> <br /> She looked uncertain, but nodded. \u201cWell, if you\u2019re sure,\u201d she said after a moment.<br /> <br /> So breakfast was tense, and D and White Maria spent most of it not looking at each other, but things could have been worse. No blood was spilt, no insults were hurled\u2026 all in all it was chilly but civil. I\u2019ll take it.<br /> <br /> After White Maria left, Gawain, Calamity, and Jacob filled us in on how things had gone with Andromeda. Gawain also mentioned a brief conversation he\u2019d had with Desiree about Becky\u2019s attack on Flores the other day. Desiree mentioned that she knew Becky had strong feelings of dislike for her, and she had thought at the time that Becky\u2019s target hadn\u2019t been Dark Kimberly, but herself. It\u2019s no secret that Becky is jealous of the time Jolie has spent with Desiree, but she\u2019s always been pretty good about keeping a lid on those feelings before.<br /> <br /> Desiree apparently said that Becky could have been suffering the effects of \u2018Bedlam.\u2019 Something clicked from one of the textbooks I\u2019ve been studying lately, and I blinked at Gawain. \u201cBethlehem Hospital in London?\u201d I asked plaintively. \u201cThe old madhouse?\u201d<br /> <br /> The others looked at each other briefly, and I was again reminded of how little I still know about the strange world of the Lost. \u201cIt is something particularly old and powerful changelings can do,\u201d Marguerite supplied. \u201cThey can take very strong emotions and force you to act upon them, regardless of the consequences.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut no one at the scene was powerful enough to be able to do that, as far as we know,\u201d Gawain said.<br /> <br /> \u201cThey would not have to be present,\u201d Marguerite added. \u201cIf they saw Becky, and they knew where she was going, and they knew that Dark Kimberly or Desiree would be there, they might have simply used Bedlam to intensify her anger. It might not have shown until she saw something to be angry <u><u>about</u></u>, non?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo\u2026 who in the area is powerful enough to use this \u2018Bedlam,\u2019\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s quite a list. Madame Spidertoes. Tommy. Annika. Darke. Old Billy. Boss Lowjack. Captain Jack. The Warlock of Night. A few others <u><u>might</u></u> have the potential, but it\u2019s hard to know for certain. Flores is probably on the cusp of gaining that power, but out of everyone there, she had the least to gain from using it. In fact, she got hurt by trying to <u><u>stop</u></u> the chaos from spreading.<br /> <br /> One further theory was mentioned: Chalcedony. She doesn\u2019t <u><u>seem</u></u> to be that powerful, but she might be acting weaker than she really is. There\u2019s her thing about wearing blue clothes, for instance. Everything she wears is blue. I\u2019ve seen her in the dressing room, and I do mean <u><u>everything</u></u>. Calamity informed us that there\u2019s even a rider in her contract with the Dream House stipulating that she not be required to wear anything that isn\u2019t some shade of blue. It could be what\u2019s called a \u2018frailty;\u2019 a little personality quirk that plagues older Changelings, like Madame Spidertoes\u2019 thing about washing blood out of clothes. If that\u2019s the case, then there\u2019s clearly more to our azure acquaintance than meets the eye.<br /> <br /> It was at this point that someone reminded me what time it was. \u201cMaybe we can figure something out by watching how she acts at the Highsummer Festival,\u201d someone said, and\u2026<br /> <br /> \u201cShit!\u201d I shouted. \u201cI have to get ready!\u201d Clich\u00e9, I know, but if I\u2019m going to be the Dream House\u2019s social butterfly, then I might as well take my role seriously, right?<br /> <br /> I ran upstairs and started getting ready. I decided against wearing the Hedgespun dress this time. I mean, I\u2019ve worn it for several important occasions already, and I don\u2019t want to get the reputation of being a one-outfit girl. Plus, its deep red color contrasts with my wings and gives me a decidedly \u2018Christmasy\u2019 look\u2026 <u><u>not</u></u> what I want to go for at Highsummer. So I stripped down and started getting dolled up in my newest medieval finery. Unlike the peasant dress I wore last time, this was a real noblewoman\u2019s gown, shimmery green and soft and altogether like something out of a fairy tale (if you\u2019ll forgive the expression).<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, it wasn\u2019t the easiest outfit in the world to assemble. At some point I leaned out of my door and bellowed downstairs \u201ccan I get someone up here to help me lace up my corset, please?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThought you\u2019d never ask,\u201d Julia whispered in my ear after an indecently short interval. There was a lot of inhaling, some small sadistic noises from Julia, and a few moments later I was firmly entrenched within my outfit (not sure yet how I\u2019m going to get out of it, but I\u2019m sure someone will volunteer to help when the time comes). I put a few finishing touches on my hair and makeup, and was ready to go.<br /> <br /> I can\u2019t wait. The Highsummer Festival sounds like a lot of fun, even if I\u2019m not participating in any of the martial events like some of the others. D is escorting me, in a purple leather highwayman\u2019s outfit (she\u2019s doing the purple thing on purpose now, I just know it). And the two of us are going to meet Oleander there. That\u2019s right, the three of us are going to spend the whole day together. I am both nervous and exhilarated at the thought.<br /> <br /> And then there\u2019s the play tonight. My directorial debut! I couldn\u2019t be more excited! I\u2019ll write more later to record how it all turns out.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T13:01:43-08:00","id":760875,"title":"","content":"<b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> July 15<sup>th</sup><br /> <br /> It hurts like a bitch when I break a shard of my glass. It's not like a damn fingernail, it's more like a tooth. But I know, no matter how many times it happens it will come back. It's fucking part of me. The glass rooted in my fucking bones... in my fucking soul.<br /> <br /> I cut Andromeda tonight. Sliced her smooth soft skin open like fucking cream. Splattered us both with her blood. It wasn't my intent to hurt her. She was lost somewhere between rage and panic. How was I supposed to know Joan hadn't told her what fucking happened while she was recovering? How was I supposed to know she was going to fly off the handle because the monarchs agreed the Table was a piece of Mother Fucking Dangerous Gentry shit that needed to be destroyed?<br /> <br /> I should have seen it coming. The way she asked me about it should have warned me to be careful with my answer. I should have been cagey and deceitful until I could judge her sanity and her mood better. But no, Calamity had to go and drop the truth on her without a second fucking thought. I assumed her lady love had been straight with her. I assumed that because she seemed to be her old self that she was going to react like a gorram adult. In short, I was more fucking wrong than a Peanuts and Family Circus slash fanfic.<br /> <br /> Right off Andromeda flew off her hinges and I knew that telling her the straight truth had been a huge mistake and that there was jack all shit I could do about it. She started screaming like a child at a supermarket and rushed for the door. Joan was stunned and I was pretty sure from how completely batshit she'd gone that she wasn't in any condition to be loose and alone. I tried to grab her but fuck... I am MADE of fucking sharp edges and knives. I skipped Grecro Roman foreplay class. And damn that girl was nothing but a ball of thrashing and screaming fury. Hell, the gash didn't even slow her down. I'm not sure she even noticed as worked up as she was.<br /> <br /> But I sure as hell did. It stopped me dead in my tracks just staring at the red blood on my hand and arm. Jacob managed to catch her without doing more damage and Gawain just picked her up like a kid having a meltdown and carried her off to the den. Lori hit her with that healing Spring magic while he was manhandling her. I didn't follow them to the den.<br /> <br /> I stood there watching them haul a woman I care about away screaming and fighting like a madwoman while her lover and protector stood helpless to do anything. I am not sure which hurt more to see. But at that point, there wasn't anything I could do for either of them that wasn't being done by someone better at it than me. So I just ducked into the kitchen to wash the blood away and took a slow breath to fix my smile.<br /> <br /> The Changelings there for the show had some idea already. But the mortal patrons not so much. I started to make the rounds soothing things over and dismissing questions and concerns. Joan came down with de la Rocha and the others trickled down after. Insincere Marguerite stayed with her. The show went on. Eventually, she called for Joan and they left together out the side door to avoid any more attention.<br /> <br /> I made the rounds and talked to people. Smiled with my eyes as well as my mouth and all that shit. At one point I felt a presence and I turned to find Madam Spidertoes right behind me with a wild look in her eyes and reaching out making grasping motions like Bella Lugosi. It was certainly unexpected and I took a step back, only to have her follow and reach, gesturing a bit more pointedly and insistently at my shirt. I followed her gaze and realized that while I had washed the blood off my skin I still had some on my clothing. I walked with her into the house proper and down to the costume room, were I peeled off the shirt and offered it up to her. She set to washing it determinedly. I have to say, she took the blood out of it like it's never been there. And once she'd done so she was pretty clearly uncomfortable with me witnessing that whole business. Seems she'd come by to let me know Annika wouldn't be there for my lesson as she was trying to straighten things out with Dark Kimberly. I thanked her for the message and told her I understood. Then I slipped on a fresh shirt to let that one dry and returned to the manager thing.<br /> <br /> Monica was there and looking quite on the prowl. I talked with her a bit about her breakup with Hailey. I'm glad I got past my irrational hate on for the other gray before they split. I do actually hope things work out for Hailey and she finds some real happiness. At any rate, I pointed out Monica's presence to Gawain and how fine she was looking. It was all the nudge he needed to head over and the pair of them fell to flirting promptly. I think I caught Lori giving me a look as I watched them with a pleased nod but she didn't say anything about it. And at the end of the night Monica once again carried Gawain off over her shoulder.<br /> <br /> Yeah, maybe it is weird that I'm pleased but if I'm going to raid the Sinister Bitch's dreams I need to be alone. And Monica's decent people. I know as closely tied as our dreams are that I can't keep this from Gawain but tonight is not the night for that talk. Tonight is watching and waiting. Studying my prey. Learning more about the imposter wearing my face and using my name. Let's be honest. It really doesn't matter what I see. I won't forgive what she did to my beautiful Anastasia. I can't. I am going to murder her.<br /> <br /> But before I could lay myself down to dream Dahlia stepped out of the shadows. I'll confess, when she addressed me as her little spy it set my teeth on edge. It doesn't matter how lightly it's held, a mother-fucking leash is still a mother-fucking leash. But it's also my own damn baggage. I think she and Lowjack both are keenly aware of how I feel and try their best not to aggravate the situation. She wanted to know if I'd learned anything about the altercation at Glamor Springs. She did agree that my conclusions so far seemed reasonable and matched what she'd found.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, I did speak to her a little about Snow Globe. She was less defensive as we were alone and she wasn't being blindsided by the whole topic. I asked her about Richard, but she didn't know anything of note. She was apparently the reason for Snow Globe needing a new Jane and she did seem a little cautious when she told me. But I don't blame her. She didn't choose to replace Jane and she didn't pick me. It would be like the next songbird blaming Lori for leaving the Empress with a cage to fill. When she spoke of Snow Globe, I could see a glimmer in her dark eyes. She was most certainly a predator like Hans.<br /> <br /> And speaking of predators, it's time for this little monster to slip into the filthy dreams of a hollow woman and find the strings to pull and unravel her.<br /> <br /> <br /> July 16<sup>th</sup><br /> <br /> Once she'd left, I settled in to meditate and cast myself into the dreaming. It was the first time I'd tried to find and follow the intrinsic link that connects me to my fetch. Once I'd calmed and focused myself it proved to be as easy as I'd been told. The hard part was staying that way. I nearly broke the dream as I entered it but I somehow managed to keep myself steady.<br /> <br /> It was only one night, but I learned a great deal about the Sinister Bitch. I think the diary helped. I can see that she still has a need to be in control. Of herself, of her surroundings, of everything. It was tempting to step in and spin the dream world away from her, so tempting. I know that she will learn to recognize my presence in her dreams sooner or later but I can only imagine that it will make it that much worse for her when she's helpless to stop me from stealing control of her dreams from her. But not yet. I will be patient. I will know her completely before I destroy her. And I WILL destroy her.<br /> <br /> With Gawain at Monica's, Lori had taken up the stove and was making omelets. Well, not to pass up the opportunity, I smirked and walked right up behind her like it was any other morning. I slipped my arms around her waist and pressed up against her back as I kissed the back of her neck and murmured a good morning Handsome into her ear. It was perhaps a bit harder to resist the temptation to let my hands ride up than usual but I was a good little monster. She seemed amused but took it in stride so I relinquished my hold and turned to take my coffee from Jacob. Gawain arrived shortly after and seemed pleasantly surprised to receive a green dyed omelet and ham.<br /> <br /> Once de la Rocha had headed to work and Insincere Marguerite had stepped away to the stage to work on her number Julia addressed us. Apparently she's gotten it into her head that she is going to clear my Darkling sister's name back in Paris if she has to murder everyone in the Court of Love to do it. While I have to admire her spirit, even this monster knows that's not exactly a workable plan. And apparently Boss Lowjack was only willing to help her with contact information if she pledged to ask for the entire motley's help. Pragmatic as always. We did readily agree to the idea but only so long as Insincere Marguerite was on board with it. Lori and Julia went to the main room to talk to her and while she was initially hesitant they managed to convince her that it was possible. I certainly hope it is. I would hate to get Insincere Marguerite's hopes up about it and have things end badly. Time will tell.<br /> <br /> For my part, I settled into the office to catch up on all the mundane paperwork and bookkeeping and such that falls to the business manager. I'll confess, I ended up spending as much time cyberstalking one K Elizabeth Blacklaw as I did working. There is just no way I can just let it drop and no way for me to really move forward without settling it. Until I end this, it's going to haunt me and hold me back. In the end, there can be only one and I damn sure intend for it to be me.<br /> <br /> <br /> July 17<sup>th</sup><br /> <br /> So yesterday evening went sour. I was still pretending to work and Gawain and Jacob had just come back in from sparring in preparation for the martial competitions at Highsummer. We were all about to start getting ready for the show when DLR came home and called us together to share some news.<br /> <br /> Andromeda had lapsed into an unresponsive state after Tuesday night's carnival of errors. Members of the Spring court had come to check on her and found her desires were all over the place but that she was seriously thinking of retreating back to the last time and place when she'd felt completely safe, which was when she'd been on the Mothership. Well, I think we all took that like a mule kick to the groin. I get it, but I didn't fucking like it. More to the point, I didn't fucking like that I'd been party to the monumental clusterfuck that had resulted in her having notions that fleeing back to Arcadia might be better than staying.<br /> <br /> She'd been unresponsive. But I wanted to try to see if maybe I could get through. I mean, she and I were quite intimate before she got together with Joan. Gawain and Jacob and Insincere Marguerite came along as well. Chalcedony was there on desire watch. Joan was looking strained to say the least. We offered what comfort we could, which was pretty fucking little.<br /> <br /> And once I'd taken a few minutes to do that I girded my loins and stepped into the side room where Andromeda was sitting with the lights dimmed while something neoceltic played. It was soothing I guess. She shifted slightly and glanced up when I entered, but only briefly and then went back to just... sitting there. I tried to talk to her a little but it was clear enough that she wasn't going to respond so I slipped back out.<br /> <br /> Seems I was the only one beside Joan that she'd reacted even that much to. And she'd wanted to speak, but it hadn't been strong enough to rise through the weight of her withdrawal. Gawain mentioned Dream therapy, if not directly then perhaps a crafted dream. Moon had tried but Andromeda had pushed hir out. Joan wasn't sure if it would help but honestly wasn't going to reject anything that might help. She even took my suggestion that one of the therapists from the Winter Court's clinic might be able to help. Not right away, but I told her directly that they'd done me some real good and reminded her that all of them and the whole program had been put into place by Lowjack before Darke took power. That did seem to alleviate the worst of her misgivings. It was also brought up that in this case, they might well be able to work out something not at the actual clinic.<br /> <br /> In the end, we decided that Gawain and I would return later to at least attempt dream healing. Since she'd responded to me it seemed I had the best change of being allowed into her dreams without resistance. Well, me or Joan but Oneiromancy isn't something she's particularly adept at.<br /> <br /> I won't lie, I was kinda on autopilot for the show. It was the night before Highsummer and I was worried about Andromeda. But things seemed to go smoothly enough. Desiree was there and Gawain talked to her about the mess from Sunday. Her take wasn't new but did bring up an interesting point. Becky had made it clear she did not like her and would quite happily kill her if she gave her a reason to. So when Becky drew back, Desiree screamed because she was quite sure Becky was looking at her directly and coming for her. She also suggested that rather than Summer magic, it might have been Bedlam. Something that she herself has apparently experienced. That opens up a whole host of new angles on the means. And gives us some new suspects, but as it can only be done by those with a truly strong connection to the Wyrd, all of these new possibilities are powerful and important.<br /> <br /> Tommy. Spidertoes. Annika. Darke. Old Billy. Captain Jack. The Warlock of Night. Lowjack.<br /> <br /> Yeah, not a name on that list that wouldn't be a major nightmare to deal with. Also no real clear motives to do so there. At least none that we know of. The other name that came up was good ol Chalcedony with her weirdling thing for the color blue. Could be that she is more powerful than she's let on. The cost of that level of connection to the power of fate and fairytale is frailty. Everything in her house is blue. Hell, she even insisted on a clause in her contract that her costumes would be blue.<br /> <br /> A problem with a face I can stab... Is it really too much to fucking ask for?<br /> <br /> At least the dream healing worked. We went back after the show with Jacob along to provide Joan some emotional support. Monica was there for her friend and Marie-Helen was there to keep an eye on Andromeda's desires. The setup was the same. Jacob had a deck of cards and we settled in to play some poker while we waited for the wee sweetling to fall asleep. Marie-Helen suggested strip poker (and I am not entirely sure she was joking about it) but it wasn't the time or place for that. Still, the mood was lighter than it could have been otherwise. I won't say Joan relaxed, but she was perhaps a ratchet or two less.<br /> <br /> When the little morsel did drift away I nodded and left the table as did Gawain. I made sure to look calm and confident but unholy hell was I anything but. As we stepped into the other room I was fucking terrified. I looked at her as I cast the darkness charm to keep her from waking and for a long moment I was just fucking paralyzed looking at her face, softer even with sleep and framed by that silk hair. For a moment, I seriously considered asking Gawain to take the lead. I kill. I murder. I'm a knife.<br /> <br /> But then Gawain took my hand and looked over, waiting for me. There was no doubt there. I glanced back and saw Joan watching from the other room. And fuck, there it was, that glimmer of hope in her eyes. I nodded to her and took a slow breath. Then I gave Gawain a tight smile and squeezed his hand. I was the one Andromeda had tried to reach out to earlier. I was the one that had to do this. And my Handsome fairy prince was right there at my side.<br /> <br /> It was a long night but together we slowly reshaped and guided the dreaming woman back to herself and her love. It felt good to work so closely with Gawain. And watching as our efforts took hold was... fuck I don't have words for it honestly. But morning came and we woke and I looked over at Gawain and then down at the woman we'd helped. And even before she woke I knew we'd moved her forward. When she opened her eyes and spoke it was fucking amazing.<br /> <br /> We stepped out and let her and Joan have some time together. I was weary but flying high all at once. And after a few minutes Joan came out and thanked us all. I said a brief goodbye to Andromeda and while she was better I could see she wasn't fully back to her old self. But she was on the road to it. And it occurred to me that a scalpel is a knife. Insincere Marguerite keeps telling me not to give up on my childhood dreams. I don't know, but maybe... Maybe it isn't impossible.<br /> <br /> Anyway, back at the Dream House. Lori was kind enough to refresh Gawain and I with her Spring magic. And everyone was quite happy to hear Andromeda was on the mend. But before too long, it was time for us all to get ready for Highsummer. I'd put together and ordered an outfit before everything went sideways. Pulling it out felt more than a little weird. I mean, so much shit is going on and here I am playing dress up. And beejebus I am suddenly wondering just what I was thinking when I ordered this getup. I had to grab some of the adhesive from the dressing room to keep this top decent.<br /> <br /> But the looks Gawain gave me while he was helping to lace me into these pants (are they still pants if there is more lacing than anything else?) was worth it. And fuck it, there is always a fucking fire to put out. Might as well look good while I fight it. And you know what, I look DAMN fine right now. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Well today definitely got more interesting. De la Rocha came over before the show and said that she needed to talk to the lot of us. So all of us gathered and De la Rocha launched into her story. She said that Andromeda was not doing well at all after the incident the other night at the club. She apparently retreated within her own mind so much so that she\u2019s not responding to anyone save Joan, and that\u2019s only when the other woman is upset. Those in her court had someone reading her emotions to make sure that she\u2019s not thinking of hurting herself or anyone else for that matter. They have managed to find out that she feels rather betrayed by those around her. Also because of her feelings of betrayal she is considered a flight risk. They are afraid that if she should run and make it to the Hedge she\u2019d be gone for good. The fear is that the only one she may not feel betrayed by is her Keeper, and we don\u2019t want her to run back there.<br /> <br /> I suggested what I thought was the obvious idea of having her talk to one of the counselors from the Clinic. The idea seemed to be well received and Calamity thought it would be good for her to suggest the idea to Joan. She also wanted to try and talk to Andromeda since she didn\u2019t really have anything to do with the incident the other night. I offered to come along as a neutral party. I haven\u2019t really been involved in the whole affair, aside from stopping her from running, and figured it might be good for someone that has an outside perspective to be there. Calamity also suggested that Insincere Marguerite come along since she also was not involved in the excitement.<br /> <br /> So, we all went to visit with Joan and Andromeda. Chalcedony and Monica were there as well. I think Monica was acting as support for Joan, while Chalcedony was there in order to periodically check on Andromeda\u2019s emotional state, just in case. Calamity brought up the idea to Joan of Andromeda talking to one of the Clinic\u2019s counselors. Joan\u2019s expression immediately soured when she heard the idea. Not that it hasn\u2019t been brought up to her before, but she was obviously not a fan of that particular plan, and I wondered why. I wasn\u2019t sure if the whole deal with Darke upset her so much that any place that is associated with the man has a negative image in her mind. Calamity did her best to talk about the good qualities of the Clinic. She cited her own positive experience as proof that they can help. She also reminded Joan that all of the counselors that are on staff there now were actually hired by Lowjack. He\u2019s the one that set the place up. <br /> <br /> Joan never did seem keen on the idea of the counselors but admitted that it could help, and that Andromeda\u2019s happiness comes first. I thought then that a lot of people say those words but don\u2019t really mean them, but not in this case. Joan is obviously deeply in love with Andromeda and will do anything to keep her safe and to make her happy. She will give up untold things to ensure this. In some ways it was a little unnerving to see that much devotion radiating from one person. The last time that I saw that level of loyalty was when I was in the service of the Lady. Rook and I both were completely devoted to the Lady. We did everything she asked and we were happy to do it. Granted she was the one that held the power in that relationship. With Andromeda and Joan they are both devoted to one another. <br /> <br /> To ease Joan\u2019s worries I suggested that they have one of the counselors come to where Andromeda is and talk to her here, or wherever they want to meet. That way the talks will have a more comfortable feel and it will be more discreet. I think Joan preferred that idea over actually going to the Clinic and talking to someone there. And as I was making my suggestion to Joan, Calamity went in to see if Andromeda would talk to her. She never did talk, but she did react to Calamity\u2019s presence, which is a positive thing. She is reacting to those she is close to, which is good. I figured since there seemed to be a positive reaction from Andromeda that it wouldn\u2019t be necessary for me to step in and see if she would talk to me. Not that I minded. I would have done so if it seemed like it would help, but the whole reason I came along was to support Calamity. She offered her support when I had my conversation with Lowjack about my past, I thought it only fair that I do something to help her. Even if my role was have a minor part in the overall conversation. I could tell how much the whole situation bothered my friend and didn\u2019t want her to have to go alone. Not that there weren\u2019t other people around, but I know just how possible it is to feel utterly alone in a room full of people.<br /> <br /> Calamity left the den door open when she went in to talk to Andromeda. I saw her express how much she missed her friend and how hard it was to see her like this. She kissed the alien girl on the forehead and left. She then came back out to talk to Joan. She suggested that dream therapy might help and offered her and Gawain\u2019s assistance with that after the show tonight. Joan agreed that it was worth a shot. Moon had tried doing dream therapy once before, but Andromeda rejected the attempt. Anyway, the plan was to have our two dream travelers come back after the show, or during if Joan called to say that Andromeda had fallen asleep before the show was done.<br /> <br /> The show went on like usual. Nothing out of the ordinary. Richard came by again. I figured he\u2019d had a rough day at the shelter considering he doesn\u2019t usually come in so soon after his last visit. I was proven right when I went over to talk to him and he had grim look on his face. So, I did the stereotypical bartender thing and asked him what was bothering him. He said that he\u2019d had a bad day at work. Given his line of work I had an idea of what had happened. I assured him that I could take it and offered him an ear to listen. So, he told me about Buster a Pitbull mix that had been at the shelter for a long time. He was rescued from a dog fighting ring and had been at the shelter ever since, but because Buster had some Pit in him no one wanted to adopt him. Richard had pulled every string he could to keep Buster around. The higher ups finally pulled rank and told him that because of the dog\u2019s history and the fact that he\u2019d not been adopted yet he\u2019d have to be put down. I know he would have taken the dog in if he could of, but his daughter\u2019s allergies make that an impossibility. So, he had to put the poor dog to sleep. I offered my condolences and told him that he had made Buster\u2019s life happy up to the end and sometimes that\u2019s the best thing you can do.<br /> <br /> So, I made at least one drink specifically because of the name, Hanky Panky (it was the goofiest drink I could think of beside the Fluffy Critter, and figured the latter would be in poor taste), and another called a Lorraine. He thanked me for the drinks and the conversation and headed off to watch the show after he\u2019d had the first cocktail. He brought the second with him to sip while he watched. He still was not in the greatest of moods, but he seemed a little less morose after telling his story. With an eight year old daughter, it\u2019s not something he can really share at home without utterly depressing his kid. So, he talks to me, gets it off his chest and enjoys the show. He stayed until close tonight and then went home to his understanding wife.<br /> <br /> After Richard went off to watch the show I talked to Calamity for a bit. I asked her if she knew how long Joan had been staying awake. Turns out that she hasn\u2019t slept since the incident so that makes it what, two days? I understand that she\u2019s been taking advantage of Spring court contracts to stay awake and refreshed, but that only really helps with physical exhaustion. It does nothing to combat stress. Sleep is a very good way to let go of stress, at least for a little bit. But Joan hasn\u2019t taken advantage of any opportunities to rest though. She\u2019s been staying awake non-stop in case her lover needs her. And there is that kind of scary devotion again. I asked if she thought Joan would mind if I came back to keep them company while she and Gawain do their Dream therapy thing. Calamity didn\u2019t seem to think that Joan would object, so I said I\u2019d come along after the show. I doubted that I could convince Joan to actually sleep, so I decided to go prepared to distract her instead. Playing cards works well for that.<br /> <br /> Once the show was over I met up with Calamity, Marie-Helen and Gawain and we all went to Joan\u2019s place. Monica was already there keeping Joan company. I offered to keep watch with Joan while Calamity and Gawain did their thing. While we were waiting for Andromeda to fall asleep I brought out the cards and we decided to play poker. Marie-Helen wanted to play strip poker, but Gawain managed to talk her out of that idea. I\u2019ll admit that I had fun playing poker. I\u2019m hard for people to read on a good day and I don\u2019t have much in the way of \u201ctells\u201d so I had an advantage when it came to bluffing. I could see Joan being really good too, but she was a bit distracted. Gawain seemed to enjoy himself, and Calamity was her usual inscrutable self. Marie-Helen was flirting with Monica and they both seemed to be having fun. No surprise with what happened later. <br /> <br /> As soon as Andromeda fell asleep Calamity used a contract to make sure that the slight girl would not accidentally be woken by anything. Then she and Gawain went into their dream trance and started crafting a dream for the poor girl. Meanwhile I kept things going with the poker, even when Monica and Marie-Helen stepped out. It was pretty obvious to me what they were up to, but Joan seemed to be concerned by it. I reassured her that it had nothing to do with Andromeda. They eventually came back, carefully staggered 20 minutes apart. It didn\u2019t seem long after that when Gawain and Calamity came back to the main room saying that Andromeda was waking up. Joan immediately got up and went to the den where her lover was laying on the couch. When Joan came back out she said that she and Andromeda had spoken, yup she finally opened up, and they agreed that they had a lot more to speak about. Though they may make it to the High Summer event after they have that chat. We\u2019ll see how that goes.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Okay, yeah, so breakfast was just a bit on the tense side. Apparently White Maria, who most of the motley thinks is a royal bitch, stayed the night with Insincere Marguerite and Julia. To say that De la Rocha was upset is like saying that the sun is hot. She was really not pleased to find White Maria walking down the hall this morning when she got up and left Lori\u2019s room. I think that Lori had a chat with De la Rocha and Marguerite with Maria. Not sure about the last one. But they agreed to a sort of truce where they didn\u2019t snipe at each other and tried their best to just ignore the other. It worked for the most part. They faced away from each other and didn\u2019t speak, and we all ate in relative peace.<br /> <br /> During breakfast Gawain mentioned his conversation with Desiree yesterday. He had talked to her about her side of things in regards to the attack the other day. She said that she was sure that Becky was aiming for her, which is why she screamed. Apparently sometime earlier Becky had expressed her intent and/or desire to kill Desiree and so when she saw Becky look her right in the eye and lunge forward she automatically assumed that she was the target. The fact that Dark Kimberly was in front of her didn\u2019t seem to register in that instant.<br /> <br /> Gawain also shared with Desiree, whether this is good or not is yet to be seen, our theory about someone using a Summer Court power to spike Becky\u2019s anger and cause the attack. Desiree said it sounded like someone had used a power called Bedlam on Becky. Apparently this power can be activated in advance and stays active for about an hour. It feeds on the existing emotions of the target and enhances them causing the target to possibly lose control. This could have been used on her any time before she actually arrived at the club. And it just needs for the caster to be able to see the target. It would only have taken the knowledge of Jolie\u2019s itinerary to be able to be in the right place at the right time to use Bedlam on Becky. To narrow things down a bit, it seems that Bedlam can only be used by people with a higher connection to the Wyrd. So people like Lowjack, Madame Spidertoes, Tommy, etc. would be able to cast it. While we were puzzling this out it came up that most folks with higher Wyrd have a weakness of some sort. Something that they have to do, or avoid, etc\u2026 It was also brought up that Chalcedony has serious affinity to the color blue. Everything in her apartment is blue, her clothes are always blue and it\u2019s in her contract that any costume she wears has to be blue. Could be a weakness. We\u2019ll need to look into that further.<br /> <br /> What made things more interesting was how Desiree knew about the use of the power Bedlam in the first place. She\u2019s not old enough to use it so she doesn\u2019t k now about it that way. No, she\u2019s had the power used on her in the past. Makes me wonder who used it and why? And what did it force Desiree to do? She\u2019d only been in \u201cthe world\u201d for a little under a year when it happened. Raises more questions if you ask me, and Desiree didn\u2019t seem keen on staying on the topic.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll admit that during part of this whole conversation my mind was somewhere else. I\u2019m not even sure of the context for this, but at some point Julia was talking about Insincere Marguerite and described her as \u201cmy Lady.\u201d Common enough phrase I know when speaking of someone you see as a higher rank than you, though kind of antiquated. Thing is it immediately made me think of the Lady of the Winter Winds and the first time I met her. I was taking shelter in a cave. Only days before I\u2019d been in a fight and killed a couple of guys with an improvised dagger. Apparently she was impressed enough with my determination to survive, because at that point it certainly wasn\u2019t because of my skill, and she invited me to enter her service. She was so beautiful. A little scary maybe, but beautiful. Her voice sounded like falling snow. I thought about it for a brief moment before nodded my assent. I knew who she was of course. There were stories of the White Lady and of her power. She was not one to cross. And the fact that she asked me, this scared, desperate kid, if I wanted to work for her. It was a no brainer. Of course I did.<br /> <br /> The first time the White Lady told me to just call her my Lady was such a thrill. Everyone except her favorites had to use her full title. The Lady of the Winter Winds. She had other titles, other nicknames, but that was the one that she expected to be called by her subjects. The fact that I just called her my Lady set me apart, and it made me feel powerful. She had plenty of servants, but Rook and I were her favorites. We spoke to other Courts on her behalf, we kept order on her behalf, and we killed on her behalf. I\u2019ll admit that some part of me misses the position I had, the power. I was given a great deal of autonomy in my job, and I enjoyed it. Not that I don\u2019t have the freedom to do as I choose here. It\u2019s just that here I am a bartender and occasional open ear. In her service I was so much more. But I know that I can\u2019t go back to that. I won\u2019t go back to that. I\u2019m trying to be a better person than I used to be. I think somehow that I\u2019ve backslid. It happened a little while back, but lately I\u2019ve thought of the good times in the Lady\u2019s service more than the bad times at the end.<br /> <br /> Dammit! I will not do that to myself. I have a life here. I have friends. I have responsibilities. I may not wield the power that I used to, but that\u2019s okay. It\u2019s good to be underestimated. I know that I can be a force for good. I have proven that in my time here. I will do better. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> There has been a lot going on.<br /> <br /> Last night was not the peaceful night we wanted. De La Rocha came home and informed us Andromeda had withdrawn from, well, everyone. It turns out carrying her against her will through the Dream House, slapping her, and slashing her caused her great strain in her fragile mental state. Not a shock to I. Monica was watching over she and Joan, and while Joan was not taking it well she was not taking it as badly as she could have. Neither did Lorelei. Fortunately.<br /> <br /> Calamity volunteered to talk to her, as they had been close. Jacob went as well. I volunteered in case we needed someone who had not slapped, slashed, or grappled her. Joan\u2019s house had far too many weapons. They were not guns, which is unusual in America. The room with Andromeda had the Irish singer Enya playing, which I would not have expected for the alien girl, but was apparently her music. Surprisingly, Chalcedony was there, apparently to check Andromeda\u2019s desires. She seemed sympathetic. I still don\u2019t trust her, but she had lost none of her succulence. Calamity had some luck but could not break Andromeda out of her shell. She got permission from Joan to return. Hopefully.<br /> <br /> We returned to the Dream House. I saw White Maria was there, and struck up a conversation. She asked if I was going to seduce her, and I admitted such was my intention. I enquired if we need go through the motions, or should just plan for her slipping into my arms, then bed. She agreed that it would be most sensible to move on to the actual fun part. I\u2019s foot having slipped into her skirt may have affected her decision. Possibly.<br /> <br /> She asked if I was going to collect her. I told her I was. She told me I shouldn\u2019t. I told her I would ask her in the morning how she felt about it, and kissed her. I took her breath away, and she joined her tongue to mine with great eagerness. Intensely.<br /> <br /> Julia joined us, and we had quite an intense evening. White Maria had been under a great deal of stress, and the orgasms I delivered seemed to do much for helping her by sending her screaming over the edge. I took her as aggressively has I had anyone in some time. My own lust clouded my mind. I told her she belonged to me now. She said nothing.<br /> <br /> By the morning, a good deal of tension was out of her muscles; as I noticed as I was giving her a morning backrub. She still had some knots but I think I did a lot for the poor thing. She put on her clothes and stepped out to go to the bathroom and, of course, accidentally met De La Rocha out in the private hall Lorelei and I share. It didn\u2019t go well. De la Rocha opened up with a growl in her voice; my Latin lover really hates her. Julia threw herself before the Latina\u2019s wrath as White Maria retreated into my room. De La Rocha followed us despite Julia\u2019s protests. She stood in our doorway as White Maria sat quietly on the bed. Julia stayed protectively between us, but imploring, rather than challenging, De La Rocha. Wisely.<br /> <br /> It is not White Maria\u2019s intent to cause strife, and I believe she could; correctly, see arguing or sniping at De La Rocha would only turn us potentially against her so said nothing. When De La Rocha did not let up she got up and said she was leaving. As soon as she was out De La Rocha reiterated her intense displeasure that we had slept together. Julia and I went after White Maria while Lori talked to De La Rocha. We got her to stay for breakfast, under the agreement De La Rocha would not abuse her further. Firmly.<br /> <br /> To her credit, De La Rocha was well behaved. They did not speak, but she was well behaved. Definitely.<br /> <br /> Quite frankly I am mystified by their reactions to White Maria. The common reason for disliking her is the nebulous \u201cShe is a bitch\u201d which generally means, \u201cShe is a female and I don\u2019t care to actually justify disliking her.\u201d De La Rocha and Calamity both dislike her, and Lorelei does not care much for her at all but is less intense in her feelings. Julia thinks she is a \u201cbitch\u201d but perhaps predictably, does not see that as a problem. She is terribly fond of me, after all. Certainly.<br /> <br /> I need to confront De La Rocha about why she hates White Maria so much. As convenient as it would be if she just had a repressed thing for her, I am fairly certain that is not the case. Sadly.<br /> <br /> Calamity and Gawain returned with a good report\u2026Andromeda was, as a result of their dream work, actually improving. She practically demanded time with Joan. That\u2019s really good. Happily.<br /> <br /> After White Maria left, under better circumstances than I had feared, Gawain mentioned Desiree talking the night before about how the attack could have been caused by a Changeling inflicting Bedlam. This made sense, and a number of changelings could do it, including Madam Spidertoes, Annika, Tommy, Shi, Darke or Old Billy, at least. None were conveniently present, however; the most likely to be that potent was Flores, who probably isn\u2019t and would not be inclined to make things worse. However, Bedlam could have been used before arrival, when she was already in a bad mood, and not noticed till she lashed out. We need to find out who saw Jolie and herself before she returned to have Jolie see Desiree. Potentially.<br /> <br /> Desiree also, at least at the time, felt like the target of the attack, which is why she, rather than Flores, screamed. She was not positive, but said she thought when she struck Becky and she made eye contact. Briefly.<br /> <br /> With that in the mix, Chalcedony\u2019s name came up too. Her fixation on blue could be a frailty, as her house is blue, her clothes are blue, even her underwear is blue. Her contract stipulate she not be asked to not wear blue. Julia was quick to dismiss this, noting she wears black, including underwear, all the time. She mentioned her paintings, and reports of Desiree\u2019s\u2026odd house. Finally, she noted having frailties did not imply guilt. Correctly.<br /> <br /> The Warlock also came up, but I really do not think it is her doing. Though it is difficult to say for sure with the Day Court\u2019s involvement with Jolie. I suspect, however, it is more connected to the previous attack than the current political situation. Probably.<br /> <br /> Of course this talk of clothes with Julia and Chalcedony and what not reminded us that it was time to change for Highsummer, and so we have. Be back. Shortly.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XLII</i><br /> <br /> So had you picked up on the seasons and themes in the story? Good thing Winter is very weak in Southern California.<br /> <br /> First off, we actually started Highsummer. For Journaling purposes the last bit of the session will be covered next time. Nothing major happened but some stuff was set up.<br /> <br /> Couple pretty big rolls happened here. Calamity and Gawain worked as a team to use Dream Therapy on Andromeda. Gawain assisted Calamity; since Andromeda has resisted Moon in hir attempt, they thought Calamity might not be resisted, or resisted less. They were correct; Andromeda did not \u201cfight back.\u201d Gawain got 5 successes, and Calamity killed it with 7 of her own with Gawain\u2019s extra dice.<br /> <br /> I will note as an aside, probably not important but it went unmentioned, when Gawain, Calamity, and Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne arrived (Moon stayed behind since different dream weavers were coming) Chalcedony was still there checking emotions on the top and bottom of the hour, till Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne relieved her.<br /> <br /> Other big roll was poor White Maria had one door left when Insincere Marguerite made another play, and Insincere Marguerite also got 7 successes to open that last door. White Maria was pretty much in the palm of her hand after that.<br /> <br /> Discussion of powerful Fey. First, not mentioned in Lori\u2019s journal, according to De La Rocha Madam Spidertoes is \u201caround 180 years old.\u201d She stays fresh as a petrified daisy because both her Wyrd and her membership in the Office of the Vizieral Council. Second, there was a lot of guessing about Wyrd ratings for the local fey. No one doubts Tommy or Spidertoes is that powerful. The others? Largely speculation. Finally, the hour timetable was our best way to describe a scene duration in character. This is not so much a house rule changing it as a general reflection of my rule of thumb that when outside dramatic time a turn is roughly a minute, scene is roughly an hour, chapter is roughly a day, or story roughly a week. We actually usually use the dramatic time, but it can be useful when we doing want to have a character discussing being cursed for the next chapter.<br /> <br /> I kept naming off songs playing at Joan and Andromeda\u2019s house. Mostly Enya, leaning heavily toward her \u201cThe Celts\u201d album. These little clues pop up.<br /> <br /> Again, Richard is a character unique to Jacob\u2019s player\u2019s writing. They do not actually appear in game, but is considered part of the world at this point (need a pic).<br /> <br /> During the off week next weekend, I will be putting up a short vignette written by Gawain\u2019s player of the dream Gawain and Calamity constructed. In it you will learn Joan and Andromeda\u2019s mortal names (as they call each other that in private) for the first time. Then the week after back to the hijinx, this time at Highsummer (finally there!) Comments and Questions welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T12:44:37-08:00","id":766471,"title":"","content":"It's between updates.<br /> <br /> This is an account of the dream that Gawain gave Andromeda. It was a Dream Therapy roll they did very well on, which lead to her being in better shape for Highsummer than expected. Enjoy!<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> The slight alien woman turns down another tight hallway with a dead end. The white, sterile plastic walls are featureless and her heavy shoes make no sound, even on the smooth metallic floor. A diffuse white light shines from the flat low ceiling, glinting off the metallic fabric of her clothes.<br /> <br /> Another 90 degree turn leads to a dead end. She looks listlessly from side to side at the dead end before she turns back and follows a different path. She keeps to the right side, lifting her left hand to run her fingers along the wall. Her fingertips catch on the mortar between the smooth white stones.<br /> <br /> A female figure appears at the next turn. She looks coldly at the shorter woman, her short white blond hair tucked behind her ear. The alien woman\u2019s eyes widen and she moves towards her. The taller woman turns aside and around the corner.<br /> <br /> Following the newcomer, the alien woman grabs onto the rough hewn white stones at the corner. The other woman is gone, but she continues down this new path, the large cobblestones scuffing her soft shoes.<br /> <br /> She glances up into the vaulted arches above her. Looking forward again, she catches sight of the tall woman veering into another branch of the hallway, her cape fluttering behind her. The alien woman takes a quick step forward, sinking back into herself when the other woman is out of sight again. She looks briefly down the narrowing hallway she had been on, and takes the offshoot.<br /> <br /> The other woman is some distance down the path and glances back at the alien woman. A small smile crosses her face as she opens a small door and steps through it, her armor clinking as she moves. The door is still open when the shorter woman gets there, and the other woman is still in sight through it.<br /> <br /> She moves quickly to catch up, but the taller woman stays the same far distance away, her back to the alien. She stops, resting her hand on the top of the waist high wall surrounding the path. Her flowing white dress brushes the mossy ground as she sways forward. She raises a hand to her throat, and finding her voice, calls out. \u201cLindsay!\u201d<br /> <br /> The figure in white armor stops and turns. She takes a step towards the alien woman, who takes a step of her own, off the walled path into a small clearing. The alien woman takes a shuddering breath, not reaching out to the woman an arm\u2019s length away. \u201cProtect me...\u201d<br /> <br /> The warrior draws her sword, and the alien tenses. Then the taller woman kneels, plunging her sword into the ground, and looking up at the shorter woman with love. She says nothing, but the sound of her voice pledging to protect, cherish and honor the other woman, as well as destroy anyone who harms her, fills the clearing.<br /> <br /> An ivy leaf escapes from her crown to brush the alien woman\u2019s cheek as she reaches for her beloved. She raises her up and they walk hand in hand through the woods. As the light fails, and their surroundings fade, the taller woman stops and takes the alien woman\u2019s other hand as well. \u201cCome back to me, please, Rebecca. I\u2019ll be waiting for you.\u201d She squeezes her love\u2019s hands, then drops them to walk into the darkness, turning just before she is out of view to look into her love\u2019s eyes once more.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Isn't that sweet. And now you know their mortal names!<br /> <br /> Back to usual next week. We cover Highsummer...well, a lot of it. We actually started Highsummer session before last, Highsummer was all last session, and still not done. I know we are getting at the very least Gawain and Insincere Marguerite journals...I have them in my metaphorical right hand. Others are usually the week before, so we will see how the players want to handle it. It is always harder to do an event like Highsummer in process. Regardless, I will at least have something, hopefully a lot of something, for you in a week. See you then, comments and questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T14:14:22-08:00","id":771710,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s Highsummer. The festival has started and all sorts of things are going on. And of course the Last Dance Motley find themselves in the midst of it.<br /> <br /> The Highsummer event started the last 30 min or so session before last, and covered all of last session. It is not over. Thus some journals are laid out a little strangely, since no one knows exactly how it will end yet. Calamity\u2019s account will come once it is all over.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XLIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> June 17th, late<br /> <br /> Whew. Alright. OK. Man, today was something. Fun and awesome, sure. But I am gonna have to get this all down in order, you know, before I forget something in all the craziness.<br /> <br /> So, Highsummer. Tons of things going on, tons of people, all dressed super snazzy. Dark Kimberly had on a suit with a velvety looking shirt. White Maria and Becky both had dresses with dragons moving around on them. Beck\u2019s had a tiger too, and they chased each other around her, which was super cool. Oleander had a dress made of what looked like living roots and Princess Joli and Felicity had matching dresses of sunlight! Poor Desiree was bummed cause she didn't have anything near so, you know, magnificent, even though she was still looking super hot. I was glad I had promised to keep her company. And even more glad later when - in order. I gotta keep it in order.<br /> <br /> When we got there we kinda scattered. Jacob went to tend the bar. I went to keep Desiree company and Calamity peeled off to check in with Dark Kimberly. She was feeling kinda nervous and antsy, apparently, but Calamity promised to keep an eye out, cause she\u2019s awesome. The others split into two groups, Lori with Oleander and De la Roche, and Insincere Marguerite with Julia and White Maria.<br /> <br /> We were all being sociable and wandering, so I wasn\u2019t, you know, keeping close tabs on anyone, but I think everything important got shared around eventually. I did see some of the first drama that happened, cause I was keeping an eye on Calamity and it got set off when she went to go talk with Princess Joli, Felicity and Becky. After a minute or two, there was a little arguing between everybody, enough to catch Lori\u2019s group\u2019s attention and they joined in. Becky wound up storming off, towards the bathrooms, apparently? Girls are weird. Then Calamity went to talk with Insincere Marguerite\u2019s group, and almost right away, White Maria went rushing after Becky. They kept talking kinda seriously though.<br /> <br /> I got a little distracted then by Austin coming up asking for support for a chestnut party a la Pope Alexander. Around Christmas time, of course. I guess it was a tradition when he was Spring King and he wanted to bring it back? He did assure me it was a more gender progressive chestnut party - ladies and dudes could both be either givers or receivers. I wished him good luck, but that\u2019s, you know, not really for me. Poor Desiree, she told us the first time she went to a Spring orgy thing, she was so surprised she ran away and threw up. She did bring it up to cheer Calamity up though, so it wasn\u2019t to traumatic or anything I guess. But, dammit, I\u2019m out of order again.<br /> <br /> See, Calamity was sitting on a bench all sad when I caught sight of her again, so I snuck up behind her and picked her up and me and Desiree tickled her. It was good to hear her laugh, you know? And to have her all curled up in my arms. But I couldn\u2019t think of anything distracting to talk about. Desiree could though, and asked about the chestnut party, since Austin had said Calamity supported it, and also told her story.<br /> <br /> That cheered Calamity up a little, and then when Louie and Wen Ja stopped up and offered us the position of honor guard for Joan and Andromeda, that cheered her up even more. The two weren\u2019t here yet, so we sat and talked some. Lori, De la Roche and Oleander even joined us and De la Roche and Oleander were getting on great, which was, you know, awesome to see.<br /> <br /> They were there with us when Louie came by to let us know Joan and Andromeda were here, which was good cause Louie also let Desiree know Felicity wanted to talk with her. Desiree was super worried, so Lori offered to come along. It turns out that someone had dissolved something into Felicity\u2019s water bottles, about an hour before, and had been wearing Desiree\u2019s face at the time! Dark Kimberly had used her Contracts of Animation to ask the water bottle who it had been. Felicity accepted that Desiree had been with me all day and didn\u2019t push it, so that was really good.<br /> <br /> What that, Lori took Desiree around to let everybody know what was up. Jacob\u2019s bar was a busy place, you know, with Luna and Dominika and Monica keeping him company, but Lori pulled him and Luna aside to fill them in. She gave a bottle of the spiked water to Oleander when she got her ladies up to speed, cause she has stuff to analyze it with back home. She chatted with Joan and Andromeda some before filling us in, and then Calamity asked her to check on Dark Kimberly, since she wasn\u2019t in sight anymore, and there was the whole feeling nervous thing before.<br /> <br /> Joan and Andromeda, by the way, were entirely adorable. They were both dressed in pure white with gold accents, you know, mostly in the form of Joan\u2019s heraldry. It was awesome to see them so happy together. Tons of people stopped by to say hi - the motley, Desiree, of course, Monica, Dominika, Princess Joli, Mary Helene, for just a few - and all of them, you know, respected their space, so we mostly just had to look pretty.<br /> <br /> So, Lori went looking for Dark Kimberly. She found her back behind the tents where Lori\u2019d seen her last, a little faint-y. Dark Kimberly said it was because of the heat and being tired, but did move to sit in the shade where Calamity could see her, you know?<br /> <br /> Then Lori decided to go look for White Maria and Becky. She left Desiree with Jacob and went around towards the bathrooms. She found Chalcedony, which was kinda weird, you know, cause we hadn\u2019t seen her anywhere around before that, and then she started acting even weirder, kinda stilted and moving oddly. We\u2019d already thought about Extras, since they can look like any of the Director\u2019s Changelings, so Lori got a little freaked out. But she kept an eye on Chalcedony, unlike Molly - but that was later.<br /> <br /> Lori found White Maria and Becky just fine, arguing in Chinese. She told Becky about the water tampering thing, since she was, you know, Claviger and all. Becky decided right off to get somebody else to use Contracts of Animation on the bottles, since she didn\u2019t trust Dark Kimberly. She didn\u2019t get upset at Desiree though, which I was sure worried about. People seem to be giving her a break a little, thankfully.<br /> <br /> When they were leaving, they found Molly with a knife, staring north (this was also the first time she\u2019d been seen today). She said Chalcedony had been there being all robot-ish and when Molly turned her back to her, Chalcedony had attacked her! Molly said she had still come out ahead and stabbed her, but there was no blood. Luna and Jacob showed up about then, since Lori had taken long enough to be worrisome, and we decided to stop sending people off one by one. So they managed to track... something? northwards. The trail they found stopped at Vic Twilight, who had supposedly been sent to join them by Molly, so that got awkward. It wasn\u2019t good ground for tracking, and things like Contracts of Smoke exists, so...<br /> <br /> Anyways, nothing else crazy happened before the competitions. Light blades was first. Lojack relieved Jacob, complete with Burger King crown, and Louie relieved Calamity. It was awesome sitting and watching the event with Louie and Joan. It was awesome watching period, really - they were all pretty great. Sandeval is super fast and wields a sword very well and you know it\u2019s always fun seeing Calamity, Jacob and Luna spar. TJ competed too, with a long sword, but it clearly wasn't his area of expertise. Shi rounded out the competition, pitting his two sai against Jacob\u2019s daggers. Luna came out on top overall, with Jacob and Calamity tieing for second.<br /> <br /> Then came heavy blades. It was me, TJ with a rough sort of polearm, Percival with a maul, Moon with a scythe, Shi with a hedge crafted quarter staff that had lanterns on each end, and Viscount Augustine, with a two handed sword himself. Moon held hir own - it was definitely interesting watching hir fight. I haven\u2019t had much opportunity to, you know, see a scythe in action. Ze lost to Percival though. Shi was pretty mesmerizing too - it looked like fireballs at the end of his staff when he swung it. Viscount Augustine won handily though. Shi was cool though, he was mostly standing in for Joan, to make the numbers work. I beat TJ to progress, though Percival got me in the second round. That was a hell of a fight though - a <u><u>hell</u></u> of a fight. He wasn\u2019t a dick about things either, so that was a win. Viscount Augustine won in the end, in another awesome match.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Well, the Highsummer Festival has begun, and I suppose I should have known things wouldn\u2019t be boring. Plots and intrigues abound, and I\u2019m pretty sure I have personally been in significant danger already this afternoon\u2026 but I can\u2019t help feeling happy, as on other fronts things are going quite well. I\u2019m currently watching the weapons competitions, which affords me a little time to write \u2013 I\u2019m really glad I thought to put my diary in my purse before we left this morning, because there\u2019s a lot to get down \u2013 though of course I\u2019ll have to pause every now and then to cheer on my motley-mates as they compete. Maybe I should have worn a cheerleader outfit\u2026 God knows the Dream House\u2019s wardrobe contains enough of them.<br /> <br /> The Festival started out well enough, with the motley breaking into small groups to hobnob and mingle, and me personally eying the styles sported by the Freehold\u2019s elite. Becky and White Maria each wore hedge-spun kimonos featuring moving dragons (Becky\u2019s also had a tiger on it). Princess Jolie and Felicity were <u><u>literally</u></u> radiant, wearing dresses which seemed to be made of sunlight itself. Jolie\u2019s was a bright golden color, while Felicity\u2019s was a deeper red shade. And Oleander\u2019s dress seemed to be composed of living roots and branches which twined sinuously around her slender form. She looked great!<br /> <br /> Sigh. I need to expand my wardrobe. I\u2019m sure I looked pretty drab in my \u201cregular-fabric\u201d dress, but I honestly don\u2019t want to wear the one hedge-spun outfit I have too often, or it\u2019ll become old-hat. If I\u2019m going to continue to be a social butterfly in this area, I\u2019ll have to find some way to keep it fresh.<br /> <br /> Not that my lovely companions seemed to mind. That\u2019s right, for the first time in\u2026 well, <u><u>forever</u></u>, I\u2019ve gotten to spend time with both D and Oleander. And they seem to be getting along really well, too! It started off with a snarky comment from Oleander about White Maria, which immediately put her on D\u2019s good side, and they seem to have let that move them back into the easy camaraderie they used to enjoy. I\u2019ve even detected some light flirting between the two of them, though I\u2019m pretty sure they were mostly teasing each other. Still, it set my imagination working\u2026<br /> <br /> No, I\u2019m not going to try to seduce the two of them into a threesome. As much as the idea appeals to me on a visceral level, I care about both of them way too much to risk our respective relationships by forcing them into a sexual situation neither one really wants. Maybe as time goes by, things will change, but for right now I\u2019m resigned to enjoying my <u><u>separate</u></u> trysts with each of them.<br /> <br /> In any case, the motley spread out as soon as we hit the Festival. I was showing off my two scoops of arm candy (yay for mixed metaphors!), naturally, and Marguerite was doing pretty much the same with Julia and White Maria. The two of us didn\u2019t interact much today\u2026 oh, there was no bad blood between us or anything like that, each of us was intent on being the center of our respective groups; the star about which everyone else orbits. Lorelei Grace cannot be part of a binary system!<br /> <br /> Marguerite\u2019s group had a bit of drama early on. It seems that Becky Wan is more than a little upset that White Maria has allowed herself to be drawn in to Marguerite\u2019s web of lovers, and spent a few minutes venting her spleen about it to Calamity. Honestly! As far as I know, Becky and White Maria have never been anything more than friends, so where does she get off trying to dictate the details of the other girl\u2019s romantic life? In any case, Becky sort of retreated to the ladies\u2019 room after Calamity made it clear that she would hear no threats against our motley-sister. Calamity went to discuss the matter with Marguerite and White Maria, and a few minutes later, White Maria hurried off to explain things to Becky. More on that situation later.<br /> <br /> On other fronts, Jacob spent most of his morning tending bar so that Boss Lowjack could attend to his kingly duties. I saw Calamity hanging out with a variety of people, but Gawain spent most of the morning speaking with Desiree, who was depressed about the fact that Princess Jolie was attending the Festival on Felicity\u2019s arm. Ace seemed to disappear into the crowd almost immediately, and I have no idea what he\u2019s gotten up to.<br /> <br /> So there was a lot of hobnobbing from the outset. Flores was in fine form once again, with not a trace of ill-will about her recent experience on display. She was handing out flowers to any and all who approached her. The blossoms were lovely, but I noticed that those of us who have become particularly close to her recently received distinctly more colorful blooms. Even Oleander couldn\u2019t maintain a grumpy demeanor for long. \u201cIt\u2019s impossible to hate her,\u201d she grumbled under her breath with the hint of a grin at the corners of her mouth, \u201cI\u2019ve been trying for years.\u201d<br /> <br /> Austin was wandering around trying to gather support for something he called a \u201cchestnut party\u201d around Christmas. I happened to be near Princess Jolie when he pitched this idea, and she got a very sour look on her face and told him that what he wanted to do on his own was his business, but that the Spring Court would not officially sponsor any such thing. Austin retorted that the chestnut party had been a Christmas tradition when he was the monarch, and that people had come to expect it. Jolie remained firm in her stance.<br /> <br /> I confess that I was confused by this exchange, and like the perfect patsy, I walked right into the trap. I think Oleander might have tried to stop me from saying anything, but it was too late by the time I noticed. \u201cWhat\u2019s a chestnut party?\u201d I asked innocently.<br /> <br /> Austin adopted a mildly manic grin and launched into an explanation of the custom. The tradition was apparently started by one of the cardinals of the Catholic church back in medieval times\u2026 which actually lends a bit of credence to the things dad used to say about \u201cCatholic idolaters\u201d back in his fire-and-brimstone days. Apparently, at such an event chestnuts are strewn around the floor of a large room. Traditionally, nude women bend over to pick up the chestnuts, while men engage them in various sexual acts while they are \u201cvulnerable\u201d until all of the nuts have been recovered. Prizes are supposed to be given to the men who are able to complete the sexual act with the most different women.<br /> <br /> I gave Austin a sort of blank look as he explained this. \u201cOf course, my parties are a little more egalitarian,\u201d he said loftily. \u201cChangelings of either gender are allowed to participate in whichever role they like. So, can I count on your support?\u201d<br /> <br /> I blinked a few times, and looked at my companions for help. D looked just as shocked as I was, but Oleander threw me a grin and a wink. \u201cThose parties are actually a lot of fun, honey,\u201d she said softly. \u201cOf course, the one time I attended, I was pitching\u2026 and high as balls.\u201d<br /> <br /> I took a moment to digest that before telling Austin that I would consider his invitation. I told him that I would certainly support his right to host such an event, but I didn\u2019t promise to attend or anything like that. I mean, it\u2019s definitely an intriguing notion. Anyone who knows me knows how much I enjoy carnal acts of all sorts. But despite my reputation, I\u2019ve never experienced a true orgy\u2026 not with a whole room full of people just trading off partners this way and that, anyway. It might be fun. And it sounds like booze and drugs are readily available at these things, too, which could do a lot to enhance the experience. On the other hand, when I\u2019m engaged in the sexual act, I can\u2019t deny that I like to be the center of attention. Becoming an anonymous vagina in the crowd lacks something in the way of appeal for me. I\u2019ll have to think about it carefully before December rolls around.<br /> <br /> Joan and Andromeda showed up around this point. Louis Guo and Ji Wen Ja were supposed to act as honor guards for them, but the two Chinese changelings approached Gawain and Calamity just prior to the couple\u2019s arrival and offered that honor to my motley-mates. Louis said that if anyone had earned the post, it was those two, and I privately agree. So Gawain bustled off to attend to his new duties, and I stayed behind to keep Desiree company (the poor girl was very depressed). I\u2019m glad I did.<br /> <br /> Oh, I spoke with Joan and Andromeda when they arrived, of course. It was good to see the two of them looking so happy. Andromeda was obviously doing <u><u>much</u></u> better today than she has been, though she\u2019s still not quite at one hundred percent. She spoke quite pleasantly to me, hanging on to Joan\u2019s arm the whole time, and smiling. She was actually <u><u>smiling</u></u>! I can\u2019t remember the last time my heart felt so light.<br /> <br /> The only time a shadow seemed to pass over her face was when I attempted to apologize for my outburst the other night. For a moment, I was worried that bringing it up had been a horrible mistake, but she seemed to shake off the bad memories after a moment. \u201cIt\u2019s okay, Lori,\u201d she said softly, squeezing my hand gently, \u201cI understand why you did what you did, and I don\u2019t blame you.\u201d<br /> <br /> I gave her a smile. \u201cThank you,\u201d I replied. \u201cI\u2019ve been feeling horrible about it ever since. It\u2019ll never happen again, I promise. Anything you need, just ask, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> She gave me a genuine smile and turned to look at her paramour. \u201cThanks\u2026 but I already have everything I need,\u201d she said softly.<br /> <br /> I let them go at that. Ain\u2019t love grand?<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, elsewhere matters of the heart were getting complicated. You see, when he stopped by to deliver the good news about Joan and Andromeda\u2019s honor guard, Louis had also mentioned to Desiree that Felicity wanted to speak with her. As the two of them are rivals for Jolie\u2019s affection and none too friendly with each other, Desiree was understandably nervous about meeting with the Day Courtier without some backup. Seeing as how this was a social situation, and Gawain was otherwise engaged, I offered my services to help keep things civil.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m glad I did. The mood between those two is not quite hostile, but still simmering, and if a neutral party hadn\u2019t been there, someone almost certainly would have said or done something they\u2019d later regret. Desiree and I wandered off to an area behind one of the large tents, where we encountered Felicity standing by a cooler full of water bottles. The area was full of such coolers; it was a hot day and a lot of people had opted to bring their own refreshments. But Felicity was <u><u>seething</u></u> as we approached.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat did you do to my water?\u201d she asked Desiree as we walked up to her.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat?\u201d Desiree answered, obviously confused by the question.<br /> <br /> \u201cSomeone has tampered with my water bottles,\u201d Felicity shot back, holding one up and waving it at us, \u201clook, the seal has been broken. I know it was you. What are you trying to pull?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2026 I didn\u2019t\u2026\u201d Desiree began, but Felicity was having none of it.<br /> <br /> \u201cI <u><u>know</u></u> it was you, Desiree. Kimberly spoke to the bottles and <u><u>saw</u></u> you do it!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFelicity,\u201d I said softly, \u201cDesiree has been with either Gawain or me all morning. She hasn\u2019t been anywhere near your water.\u201d<br /> <br /> She turned to glare at me for a moment, and I could see the calculations behind her eyes. I\u2019d been with Jolie before as well, and at the time I made no secret of the torch I carried for her. Felicity was weighing the possibility that I was in league with Desiree in some attempt to separate her from Jolie (if only temporarily). I will confess to occasional pangs of jealousy at seeing the Princess with other women, but I don\u2019t want to <u><u>hurt</u></u> anyone over it. I\u2019m past that part of my life now; happy with the girls I have.<br /> <br /> Plus, I occasionally console myself by remembering that Jolie asked <u>me</u> to be her consort before she approached either Desiree <u><u>or</u></u> Felicity. Now, admittedly she was going <u><u>back</u></u> to Felicity after having dated her before, but that\u2019s neither here nor there.<br /> <br /> In any case, Felicity\u2019s face lost its steely determination after a moment and her brow wrinkled in thought. \u201cYou\u2026 you\u2019re sure?\u201d she asked me plaintively.<br /> <br /> I nodded firmly. \u201cUnless she can be in two places at once, Desiree is not your girl,\u201d I said with some assurance.<br /> <br /> Felicity nodded and turned solemnly to Desiree. \u201cIf I\u2019ve accused you unjustly, I\u2019m truly sorry, Desiree. I don\u2019t bear you any ill will. It\u2019s just\u2026 she was so sure\u2026 why would Dark Kimberly lie?\u201d<br /> <br /> I closed my eyes in thought for a moment. \u201cI don\u2019t think she did lie,\u201d I said slowly. \u201cUnless I\u2019m very mistaken, Dark Kimberly saw exactly what she said she saw. We have an imposter. Someone is trying to turn the Freehold against itself.\u201d Privately a host of thoughts occurred to me\u2026 a dream image made real, a Mirrorskin impersonating Desiree, or even one of the Director\u2019s dreaded \u201cextras.\u201d<br /> <br /> Felicity looked momentarily lost, and Desiree looked frightened. \u201cWhat should we do?\u201d Great, just what I need: more people turning to me in a time of crisis. As if I know how to handle these things any better than they do! I\u2019m a singer, I\u2019m a dancer, I\u2019m a model. I\u2019m <u><u>not</u></u> one of Charlie\u2019s Angels.<br /> <br /> Still, I did my best under the circumstances. \u201cFirst,\u201d I said, \u201cgive me one of those water bottles. Oleander is here with me; if anyone will be able to tell what\u2019s been done to it, she will. Felicity, I want you to get back to the Princess and let her know what\u2019s going on. We want the monarchs to be informed of this, but we don\u2019t want to start a panic or have people second-guessing each other\u2019s identities. Desiree, stay with me for the time being. I want a member of my motley to have eyes on you at all times, so that we\u2019ll know you\u2019re really <u><u>you</u></u>. Finally, I need to find Becky. The Claviger needs to hear about this from someone who isn\u2019t directly involved.\u201d I let that sink in for a moment. \u201cNo offense, but it <u><u>certainly</u></u> shouldn\u2019t be one of you two.\u201d<br /> <br /> Desiree looked pale, and maybe a little ill, but I thought I saw a smile quirk at the corners of Felicity\u2019s mouth. As I have noted before, Felicity is a strikingly beautiful woman in her own right. I wonder if she and Jolie would ever consider\u2026 no. Focus, Lori.<br /> <br /> At that point, Dark Kimberly emerged quietly from around the side of the tent where she\u2019d been hiding and watching the confrontation with interest. I took the opportunity to question her about what exactly she had seen related to the water bottles. She went on the defensive, but I think I managed to convince her that we weren\u2019t accusing her of anything. When I told her my suspicions that someone was playing the entire Freehold for chumps, she agreed that her power was not infallible, and that she could only see things witnessed by the objects in question (which could in turn be fooled by magic).<br /> <br /> She was dressed very fetchingly today, by the way, in a pseudo-Victorian ensemble which seemed to be made mostly of dark velvet. I complimented the outfit, and she thanked me graciously\u2026 and more than a little lasciviously. She was obviously on the prowl today, so I guess the rumors about the trouble between her and Annika must be true. I\u2019m ashamed to admit that the first thought that crossed my mind following her suggestive wink was that I could strike a blow against Annika by seducing her sometime girlfriend\u2026 but I forced that thought down almost immediately. Sex should never be a weapon; it should never be used with the express purpose of hurting someone. It\u2019s one of the most beautiful things two people can share, and it should only be done to bring a little more pleasure and joy into the world.<br /> <br /> I want to note one other thing before I move on. It may be nothing, but it could end up being of vital importance. Damn, I wish I knew more about this whole Changeling thing! I noticed that Dark Kimberly couldn\u2019t seem to stop herself from cleaning up the grounds whenever I saw her walking around today. She\u2019d stop to pick up rubbish on the ground, and place it carefully in the designated receptacles around the field. I remember Annika saying something about how Kimberly sort of compulsively cleaned her house, too. Is this just a Wizened thing, or could it be another example of these \u201cfrailties\u201d the others were talking about this morning? Or is it just a regular facet of her psyche? Who knows?<br /> <br /> In any case, I dragged Desiree around with me as I wandered the grounds looking for my motley mates and various other concerned personages (like Becky). I found D and Oleander first, still chatting amiably like old pals. They both drew up short when they saw my face, though. I quickly explained the situation to them, and Oleander took the water bottle from me. She examined it closely, and smelled it, but didn\u2019t dare taste it. \u201cWithout my lab, I can\u2019t tell exactly what\u2019s been done to it,\u201d she admitted a few minutes later.<br /> <br /> I looked everywhere for Becky, but she didn\u2019t seem to be available. I asked around a bit and eventually discovered that the Claviger was still closeted in the ladies\u2019 room, presumably still engaged in an intense discussion with her friend White Maria. Sighing and rolling my eyes at the unnecessary drama in the midst of a real crisis, I left Desiree with Jacob and wandered off toward the restrooms, hoping that I could speak to Becky without upsetting her further.<br /> <br /> As I approached the ladies\u2019 room in question, I noticed that I wasn\u2019t the only person with an interest in it. Chalcedony stood just outside of the door, staring at it. I\u2019m not sure if she was trying to listen in on the conversation inside (which was fairly hushed by this point, and in Chinese in any case), or if she was waiting for a vacancy, or if she was waiting for either Becky or White Maria, but she turned to face me as I approached. She greeted me kind of tonelessly, which set off alarm bells in my head.<br /> <br /> \u201cHi, Chalcedony,\u201d I said, \u201cwhat are you doing back here?\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded toward the bathroom. \u201cBecky and White Maria have been in there for a very long time,\u201d she said.<br /> <br /> \u201cThey\u2019re still there? Good, I need to talk to Becky,\u201d I said, making for the door. Chalcedony turned as I walked past her, always keeping an eye on me. I admit that I was pretty spooked by this point, so I returned the favor, and made sure I never turned my back to her until I was in the bathroom myself.<br /> <br /> Becky and White Maria were both in there, and they both stopped talking and turned to look at me as I entered. \u201cThis is private,\u201d Becky muttered before I could say anything.<br /> <br /> \u201cI know,\u201d I said, \u201cand I\u2019m sorry to interrupt, but I need to talk to you as soon as possible.\u201d<br /> <br /> White Maria\u2019s eyes lit up. \u201cDid Insincere Marguerite send you to get me?\u201d she asked hopefully. Becky\u2019s face registered disgust at the question. <br /> <br /> I confess I bristled a bit at the implications of her words, and my response was a little sharper than I intended. \u201cI\u2019m not Marguerite\u2019s errand girl,\u201d I snapped, \u201cshe doesn\u2019t <u><u>send</u></u> me anywhere.\u201d White Maria\u2019s face fell and she muttered an apology, but I thought I detected a hint of approval in Becky\u2019s slight nod.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sorry,\u201d Becky said after a moment, \u201cit\u2019s been a trying morning. What\u2019s wrong, Lorelei?\u201d<br /> <br /> The real reason I\u2019d sought her out came back to me then. \u201cI need to speak to you in your role as Claviger, and I need you to listen to everything I have to say before you act or make assumptions, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> Becky nodded, and she was all business at that point. \u201cSomeone might have tried to poison Felicity earlier today. She noticed that her water bottles had been tampered with, and she asked Dark Kimberly to look into it with her magic. Dark Kimberly did so, and reported that Desiree had been messing around with the water bottles about an hour earlier.\u201d <br /> <br /> I saw the look of triumph pass across her features as I reported the apparent misdeeds of her rival. \u201c<u><u>But</u></u>,\u201d I continued, \u201cwe know that isn\u2019t true, because Desiree has been with either me or Gawain all morning, and did no such thing.\u201d <br /> <br /> \u201cSo Dark Kimberly lied,\u201d Becky spat out, \u201cthat\u2019s nothing new.\u201d<br /> <br /> I shook my head. \u201cI don\u2019t think so. Why would she lie about this? I personally think whoever has been trying to destabilize the Freehold is behind this. I think someone is trying to turn us against each other, put us at each other\u2019s throats so that they can sweep in and take us out.\u201d<br /> <br /> Becky nodded. \u201cAnd you have a theory?\u201d she asked impassively.<br /> <br /> \u201cI have no proof of this,\u201d I replied, \u201cbut I immediately thought of the Director\u2019s extras. They can take on the form of any changeling who used to be his, right? And, well\u2026 Chalcedony was standing right outside of this bathroom as I approached, and she was acting sort of weird.\u201d Okay, so I probably should have led with that information, but to be fair, Chalcedony <u><u>always</u></u> acts sort of weird, and I didn\u2019t want to fall prey to paranoia\u2026 especially if some unknown force is actively trying to spread it, as I suspect.<br /> <br /> Becky spun toward the door in alarm. I followed her out, only to find that Chalcedony was gone. We weren\u2019t alone, though\u2026 Molly Nuit was there, holding a knife and looking off into the distance. When I asked if she had seen Chalcedony, she nodded. \u201cShe was here, acting very strangely\u2026 sort of detached. When I turned my back on her, she attacked me. It stunned me, but I managed to draw my knife and stab her. She ran off to the north.\u201d She indicated the direction she\u2019d been staring with a wave.<br /> <br /> I looked down at the ground, figuring the girl would be easy to follow if Molly had stabbed her. Jacob has taught me that a wounded quarry is much easier to track; they tend to run headlong in a straight line, heedless of any marks they might be leaving behind, and blood shows up well against most backgrounds. But there was no blood that I could see (nor was there any blood on the blade of Molly\u2019s knife, which is just the teensiest bit suspicious), and the ground was hard-packed and dry, and didn\u2019t take prints well. \u201cJacob might be able to pick up a trail here, but I can\u2019t,\u201d I said apologetically.<br /> <br /> As luck would have it, Jacob and Luna actually turned up around this point, as I had been gone for some time and they were getting worried about me (Desiree had been safely transferred back into Gawain\u2019s company). They agreed to attempt to track Chalcedony \u2013 or whoever it was \u2013 and set about it immediately. I didn\u2019t stick around for the conclusion because I\u2019m hopeless in a fight, but I heard later that they followed a very faint trail into the fields north of the Festival grounds, where they came across Vic Twilight. It was a false alarm, though\u2026 Vic was only there because Molly had called him and asked him to go after Chalcedony for her.<br /> <br /> Or at least that\u2019s his story. When you\u2019re dealing with inter-court rivalries and magical beings who can change their shape, who\u2019s really qualified to judge the truth of a situation like this?<br /> <br /> (Incidentally, Luna let slip that she had been a Boy Scout during the whole tracking debacle. I can only assume that she said that by accident, because she\u2019s usually very private about that aspect of her life. Of course, we of the motley know about the unusual circumstances of her Durance\u2026 though I can\u2019t remember right off hand if I\u2019ve ever actually written about it in this diary. In any case, she got a few weird looks from those who were not in the know, but nobody commented, and I\u2019m guessing her unguarded words won\u2019t go any further).<br /> <br /> But as I was saying, there was very little I could do to help at this point, so I rejoined my paramours and we settled in to watch the melee competitions. What? I\u2019d done everything I could, and alerted the proper authorities, and made sure that everyone knew where I would be if I was needed. I didn\u2019t want to just sit around stewing about the situation, or worse yet get in the way of more qualified investigators, so I decided to keep myself busy with the distractions of the Festival.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve been sitting here for close to an hour writing in this journal and sort of halfway watching the Light and Heavy Blades competitions while at the same time basking in the warm feeling I get whenever I glance over and see D and Oleander talking and laughing together like the old friends they are. <br /> <br /> Now, this may shock you, but I\u2019m not much of a fighter, so I\u2019m going to refrain from giving a blow-by-blow account of the competitions. I will simply note that in the Light Blades tournament, Luna came out on top, while Calamity and Jacob tied for second place. A lot of that action was actually too fast for me to follow, but there was a beautiful, balletic quality to the matches that really appealed to me. And no, you shouldn\u2019t read too much into that statement\u2026 I have no intention of learning to fight with knives. If I have to defend myself, my gun will have to be enough.<br /> <br /> The Heavy Blades competition was interesting as well. Gawain was the only participant I knew well, with that huge sword of his, and he did fairly well, but in the end he was defeated by that blowhard Percival. Huh, I never really thought about it before, but that pair is a shocking reversal of the way the characters are portrayed in <u><u>Le Morte d\u2019Arthur</u></u>, in which Gawain is full of bluster and aggression, and Percival is possessed of an almost otherworldly purity and serenity. <br /> <br /> Okay, okay, I admit it\u2026 I never actually read the original Mallory (not even when I was <u><u>supposed</u></u> to be reading excerpts from it for French class). I\u2019m basing this assessment on T. H. White\u2019s <u><u>The Once and Future King</u></u>. But I have to do my best to at least <u><u>seem</u></u> smart, and believe me it\u2019s an uphill battle. If I can appear to be erudite and well-read, then people might start to see me as a sexually-liberated intellectual instead of just some dumb slut. That\u2019s where things started to go wrong between me and Kyle, after all\u2026 sometimes I still wonder about the things that might have been.<br /> <br /> In any case, Percival lost the final round of the Heavy Blades tournament to none other than Viscount Augustine himself. Some of the other matches were quite spectacular. Who would have thought that Moon would be such a deft hand with a scythe? And the reclusive Autumn Courtier known as Shi fought with a flaming staff, which at least made for quite the spectacle.<br /> <br /> But the competition is over now, and I suppose I should stop writing and get back to the Festival. I\u2019m anxious about what\u2019s happening with Chalcedony and Desiree, of course\u2026 but I confess that I intend to focus most of my attention on my fair ladies for the time being. They\u2019re actually getting along! I need to ride this wave while it lasts\u2026<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T14:15:06-08:00","id":771713,"title":"","content":"<b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Well, things definitely got interesting at the High Summer event. Everyone dressed up for the day. Several of us were dressed Highwayman/woman style, including Luna. I wore my own Highwayman outfit, which seemed appropriate for the Ren Faire feel of the day. I smiled when I saw Luna\u2019s clothes. They are so practical and utilitarian. And she seemed so much more at ease in them than most things I\u2019ve seen her wear for events. It was good to see her more relaxed. I wanted her to have a good time today, and I like to think that I helped in some small way. Adventures chasing mysterious people and all out melees with knives definitely helped, but I\u2019m getting ahead of myself.<br /> <br /> In the beginning Luna asked if I was okay. She had been concerned that some of my texts seemed \u201coff\u201d and wanted to know if I was alright. I guess it speaks to how much I open up to her that she could tell that something had been off at all. I explained to her that there had been some excitement involving Joan and Andromeda lately and that had likely been the cause. I also explained that I was worried about Insincere Marguerite and Julia, in particular Julia\u2019s interactions with Marguerite. Julia displays that scary level of devoted that I was talking about with Joan and Andromeda, but this is a step above that even. Julia has on more than one occasion threatened to kill anyone that spoke badly or even just against her \u201clady.\u201d Then there\u2019s the whole \u201clady\u201d thing, but that\u2019s my problem more than anyone else\u2019s I think.<br /> <br /> Luna also asked, in a roundabout kind of way, if I\u2019d slept with Insincere Marguerite. I didn\u2019t see the point in lying so I said that I had. I did not want to hurt Luna\u2019s feelings or make her think that I still thought of Insincere Marguerite in that way. I\u2019m not so sure that I succeeded at that. I\u2019m much better at boxing up things like emotions rather than deal with them, so sometimes my responses to situations are not quite right. Those of us that are elementally aligned, whether natural or created like Molly, tend to have that problem. So, Luna asked what I saw in her, or what drew me to her in the first place. I admitted that Insincere Marguerite has an understanding of the darker side of things, of life, and that we kind of had a mutual understanding. In retrospect I should have told her that I think our connection, along similar lines, is stronger. I only let Marguerite see me without my mask up once, and that was mostly an accident. I think I\u2019m more open with Luna, and try to be sensitive to her needs. I don\u2019t know how well I\u2019m succeeding. I just hope I\u2019m not messing things up too badly. Emotions are hard.<br /> <br /> Apparently I was the person to talk to today. While I was talking to Luna, Monica came up and asked if she could speak to me for a minute. She made a point of asking Luna\u2019s permission as well. I can\u2019t help but notice that pretty much everyone does that, or at least the women do. I guess they have a healthy respect for her abilities\u2026.and well they should. Her blades are not for show. Anyhoo\u2026Monica came over to talk about what happened with Marie-Helen. Monica feels bad because she thinks she has betrayed Joan by going off with the other woman for part of the evening. She wanted to know if I would be mad at Marie-Helen or not. I told her that it was a moment\u2019s indiscretion and that there was no betrayal there. She had not been the only one keeping company with Joan, so she wasn\u2019t leaving her friend alone by stepping out. I admitted that I would probably be annoyed by Marie-Helen seducing me at an inappropriate time, but I wouldn\u2019t be mad. I\u2019m not sure if I was best able to give her advice, but I was the only other person there that Monica could talk to about it. After a bit she went back out on her own. I hope I helped in some way. Again\u2026not so good with the emotional side of things, so I\u2019m not sure if I helped or hindered there.<br /> <br /> Emotional turmoil abounded today. Apparently, and I\u2019m retelling this second hand, Becky saw White Maria walking arm in arm with Insincere Marguerite and got really upset. Apparently she thinks that Marguerite is beneath Maria and that the slight Frenchwoman has a bad influence over other women as well. I think she was afraid that Insincere Marguerite would try to \u201ccollect\u201d Maria. I don\u2019t know all the details. I just know that Lori and Calamity were involved and trying to talk Becky down. Becky ended up stalking off and when White Maria was told what was going on, she went after her. They ended up in the Ladies\u2019 room. I\u2019ll get back to that though.<br /> <br /> Calamity even went to talk to Insincere Marguerite about the whole \u201ccollecting women\u201d thing. She expressed her concern about what some others in the freehold are saying. I think Felicity was worried because it seemed that any women that slept with Marguerite were not the same after, and she seems to have several of them as regular lovers. Felicity herself was almost \u201ccollected\u201d one night, but Insincere Marguerite left off and disappeared for a bit. Anyhoo\u2026I think it was brought up by someone that Insincere Marguerite is just a good lover and people appreciate what she can do. I know I did. Just sayin\u2019. Anyway\u2026Julia got pissed when all this was brought up and Calamity had her work cut out for her trying to calm the willowy artist back down again. I would not envy her that task. I think she succeeded though. Mostly.<br /> <br /> Also involving Calamity, and this time Gawain, Ji Wen Ja and Louie came over to talk to them. I later found out that the pair had told my motley mates that they had been assigned as Joan\u2019s honor guard for the event and were wondering if Calamity and Gawain would like to do it. Apparently they felt that the pair deserved it since they had done so much to get the pair together and helping to heal Andromeda. I think someone said that the idea was also approved by Viscount Augustine. I thought it was a nice gesture for my friends. I know that they have a vested interest in seeing Joan and Andromeda happy, and if they can do some small thing to help ensure that, they\u2019re gonna do it. They kept a little distance away from the two lovers so they wouldn\u2019t crowd them, but stayed close enough that they would be there if there was any trouble. And there wasn\u2019t really any trouble that I saw early on.<br /> <br /> Around this time Austin was going around talking to different folks trying to drum up interest in a \u201cChestnut Party.\u201d After I looked up what that kind of party entails, and what he had meant by \u201cpitching\u201d and \u201ccatching\u201d I told him that it wasn\u2019t my kind of thing. I think he did get Calamity\u2019s approval though. Not sure who else backed him on the party idea, but it\u2019s likely that he got some of the Spring courtiers.<br /> <br /> Later Luna and I saw Monica talking to Marie-Helen, and the other woman was flirting pretty heavily with Monica. I could tell that Monica was feeling a bit overwhelmed and felt bad for her. Eventually Marie-Helen headed off on her own, leaving Monica alone and a bit dazed it seemed. So, I motioned for Monica to come over to the bar. She did so, and I asked if she was okay. She said that she was, but admitted that she was afraid of becoming someone\u2019s (I\u2019m thinking Marie-Helen here) plaything. Luna reassured Monica that she\u2019s not a plaything, she is Marie-Helen\u2019s sexual partner and trying to have an enjoyable time. Around this time Dominika came over to talk to Monica. I think Monica was just a bit flustered by the extra ears hearing about her liaisons, but she tried to hide it. Dominika also commented that she did not see any other black changelings in the freehold, which I\u2019ll admit is odd. I mean, there\u2019s Vic, but I can\u2019t think of any others off the top of my head. Given later events it is strange that she never noticed Vic since she was specifically looking for other dark skinned folks. I, for my part, made small talk with Dominika and offered her a drink. I believe she said that she likes rum, so I made her a cocktail. I think she liked it. Monica, after a little while, seemed to get herself back together.<br /> <br /> So, about that time Louis went to go get Calamity and Gawain so they can escort Joan and Andromeda. The pair looked good. Andromeda looked much happier than the last time I saw her, and was wearing a white dress to match Joan\u2019s. She even wore Joan\u2019s symbol on her outfit. I guess they made up, or are in the process of it. That seemed like a pretty solid way to say that she is Joan\u2019s girl. They are so cute together. They, with Calamity and Gawain as escorts, walked around watching things and checking out different booths.<br /> <br /> Louis also told Desiree that Felicity wanted to talk to her. Being nervous about this, due to the whole who was sleeping with Jolie thing, Lori offered to go with Desiree. From what I heard once they were back behind the tents Felicity accused Desiree of tampering with her water bottles. She said that she noticed that the bottles had been opened and had Dark Kimberly \u201cask\u201d the water bottles what happened. They clearly saw Desiree opening them up and pouring something inside. Now here\u2019s the problem with that whole thing. Desiree has been with Gawain and/or Lori all day. The bottles might have \u201cseen\u201d someone that looked like Desiree tampering with the water, but it wasn\u2019t the real Desiree. So, unless someone thinks that Lorelei was lying, which I highly doubt, then we had an imposter pretending to be Desiree. This could likely be one of three things\u2026a mirrorskin, someone using Cobblethought, or one of the Director\u2019s Extras impersonating Desiree. They can take the form of anyone who has been in his keeping, which includes Desiree. Lori suggested that someone was trying to cause unrest within the freehold. This could just be to cause suspicion, but if Felicity hadn\u2019t noticed that the water was tampered with it might have ended up with her getting hurt. I think Lori gave one of the bottles to Oleander to analyze and see what was added.<br /> <br /> The other thing to consider about this whole thing is that some people were not happy with Felicity and Jolie being together and may have taken it upon themselves to \u201cpunish\u201d Felicity for having the nerve to show up with the Spring Princess. They even wore matching gowns of sunlight. Jolie\u2019s is as bright as a spring day, while Felicity\u2019s is more of a sunset color. I\u2019m sure folks got the whole symbolism of wearing matching outfits. They weren\u2019t exactly being subtle. So, the question remains. Who messed with the water? Was it the Director, a mirrorskin, or some other changeling that doesn\u2019t like Felicity?<br /> <br /> Anyway\u2026after the initial confrontation occurred Lori came over to the bar to talk to me and Luna. Lori filled us in about everything that had happened and said that she was going to go talk to Calamity. Desiree went with, but stayed a little to the side as Lori filled in Calamity and Gawain on the goings on. Calamity then brought up the question of where Dark Kimberly was. So, Lori and Desiree went looking. They found her behind the tents, sitting down. She apparently looked tired, shaky and was acting a little \u201coff.\u201d<br /> <br /> Lori then went to go looking for Becky, who at last sight was heading towards the Ladies room. So, Lori dropped off Desiree at the bar so that a member of the motley would have eyes on her at all times. Made sense to me. Keep the girl\u2019s alibi airtight in case it\u2019s needed later.<br /> <br /> So, Lorelei headed to the ladies room and outside the doors ran into who of all people, but Chalcedony. The other woman was acting a bit more \u201coff\u201d than usual and said something about doing some work back there. Her gaze followed Lori\u2019s progress and our songstress made sure to keep the other woman in her sights at all times. Probably a good call in retrospect. So, Lori made her way into the restroom and filled Becky, who had been arguing in Chinese with White Maria, in on what was going on and about Chalcedony hanging out outside the ladies room. The three women left the room and found that the strangely-acting changeling was gone and in her place was another semi-strangely acting changeling, Molly Nuit. Molly said that Chalcedony had attacked her and that she had defended herself with her knife. She said that she had wounded the other woman, but there was no blood on her blade, nor was there any blood on the ground. One would think that any wound left by that blade would leave a mark and possibly a trail. After Molly hit the other woman, Chalcedony headed off North. Strange that no one had seen Molly before that moment or Vic for that matter. Where did they come from? What were they doing?<br /> <br /> Calamity got worried when Lori didn\u2019t come straight back so she came over to the bar to enlist Luna\u2019s help in finding our wayward motley-mate. Luna insisted on someone going with her, so we sent Desiree over to Calamity and we both made our way to the restrooms. We found the ladies standing around and we got filled in on what had happened. Lori said that she was grateful that we\u2019d come because they needed help tracking Chalcedony and wished out loud that someone had been a boy scout. Luna admitted that she had been a scout before taking to the sky to look for Chalcedony. I followed what faint trail I could find on the ground. I will admit that I just watched Luna fly for a moment before picking up the trail. I had never seen her fly before and it was beautiful. I was also a bit worried about her slip with the Boy Scout reference. No one made any comment and I\u2019m not sure if anyone picked up on it. Anyhoo\u2026we eventually ended up meeting in the same place. The tracks led to an area near the woods and to Vic Twilight. Unfortunately for him Luna found him first and had her knife against his throat before he could do more than squeak. Molly took that moment to call Vic to see where he was at. I took the phone from him and talked to Molly. Based on her descriptions I was able, at least as far as I could tell, determine that Vic was in fact himself. The whole idea is a little scary if you ask me. There is someone out there that can take on the face of someone else. The Extras can take on the faces of those that fled the director, but we have also run into changelings that can change their appearance at will. We know that Molly can do it. She took on Desiree\u2019s face a while back, and we never did figure out why. I wonder if she did it again?<br /> <br /> I will admit that it was a little suspicious to run into Vic right where the tracks ended. It might have been a little less damning if he\u2019d been a few feet away, but he was right at the end of the trail. I wanted to give Molly and Vic the benefit of the doubt, and I told Molly that I took her word for what happened when she explained things, and when Luna got confrontational. In reality I don\u2019t know what to believe. I don\u2019t know if those two were or are up to something or not, but figured if they didn\u2019t think that I was on to them then it might be easier to keep an eye on them later. I honestly don\u2019t know if they are up to something. Things are just awfully iffy right now. I will mention my suspicions to the rest of the motley when I get a chance. I will definitely include Luna in that conversation. I want her to understand that I was not trying to say that I didn\u2019t think that she had a valid point for being suspicious of those two. As it stands right now Vic and Molly don\u2019t have a reason to think that I suspect them of anything. I am in their court after all.<br /> <br /> After all that had been \u201cwrapped up\u201d we heard Juan-Carlos announce that the melee competitions would be taking place in the next few minutes. So we left to go to the tourney area. I believe it was mentioned that the Monarchs know what\u2019s going on with the whole duplicate thing, so I didn\u2019t feel so bad stepping away from the problem for a bit. So, Louis takes Calamity\u2019s place and she made her way over to where the rest of us were. It looked like the light blade competitors would be myself, Calamity, Luna, Sandoval, Shi and TJ. The fights started off between Calamity and her knives against Sandoval and his sword. They were both really good. I could see where Sandoval had a bit of an advantage with his longer reach, but Calamity is fast and she used her speed to her advantage. In the end they called it a draw. After that it was me vs. Shi with his paired sai. We were also pretty evenly matched. His fighting style is different than Luna and Calamity\u2019s so it was kind of fun to just kind of feel him out for a few minutes before getting down to real fighting. Once I\u2019d figured out where he left himself open it wasn\u2019t too hard to get a final strike in on him. I could tell that he realized what was happening, but by that point it was too late. I was too fast and he couldn\u2019t react in time to get away. He was a good opponent, I\u2019ll give him that. Things might have gone differently if Joan had actually been up to fighting, then I would have faced off against her. Now she\u2019s good.<br /> <br /> Next up was Luna and her paired butterfly knives vs. TJ and his sword. TJ was good I can say that, but Luna was just better. Watching her fight was beautiful. She really is exceptionally good with those knives and it is a joy to watch her. Her economy of movement, her speed, and the way she seems to just be able to read what her opponent is going to do next and react accordingly, it\u2019s just amazing. I\u2019ve been on the receiving end of her blades, so I know how TJ was feeling and it probably was a little overwhelmed. After that it was me vs. Sandoval and his sword. Sandoval was still good, but not good enough. I changed up my style to something closer to what Rook taught me. I didn\u2019t want him to be able to use what he saw Calamity doing against me. We both studied under the same teacher after all, so our styles are pretty close. If I put my mind to it though I can use moves almost exclusive to my old fighting style. Apparently it worked so I pretty handily won that fight.<br /> <br /> Then it was Luna vs. Calamity and damn that was a fight worth watching. If you knew what to look for you could tell that Calamity was the student and Luna the teacher, but it didn\u2019t really make a difference in the end. They both fought extremely well, and it ended in a draw. Their final strikes would have been lethal if they\u2019d been intended that way. Calamity aimed high and Luna low. In an actual fight they would have dropped simultaneously. After that I got to fight Calamity. And maybe it was just that she\u2019d fought off Luna, but she wasn\u2019t quite up to her top form. Now I say that because I won with a pretty good margin, but it\u2019s in no way like Calamity wasn\u2019t good. She was easily still better than anyone else I\u2019ve seen fight in this freehold. Her moves were flawless and here agility amazing. I just happened to get the drop on her a few times that she couldn\u2019t block. I used a combination of Rook\u2019s and Luna\u2019s style. She knows both of my styles, but I wasn\u2019t sure how\u2019d she\u2019d take it when I mixed the two together. Apparently it worked though, so I\u2019m not complaining. Of course next time we spar I think I\u2019m going to be in for it.<br /> <br /> The final fight in the light blades competition was me vs. Luna. I think I did well, at least I know there were some pretty lethal moves that she pulled that I was able to deflect or just plain dodge that I\u2019ve had trouble doing in practice, but she was better. She was just amazing. At first I\u2019ll admit that I was a bit self-conscious getting \u201cschooled\u201d by my teacher in front of the Freehold, but after a couple minutes the rest of them all just fell away and it was just me and Luna up there. In the end she won with a move that I don\u2019t remember her having used before. I\u2019ll remember it though, now that I\u2019ve seen it. It was pretty impressive, as was she. It was ruled that Luna took first place, while Calamity and I tied for second. I can live with that.<br /> <br /> After the light blade competition the heavy blades took the stage. I\u2019ll admit that I was not quite as invested in these fights as I was the light blades. Gawain was the only fighter that I knew personally and the only one who I really wanted to see. Granted the others were good, and most had impressive weapons and forms. Shi even stepped in on behalf of Joan and wielded a quarter staff with a lantern on each end. Moon had a scythe, Percival had a maul, Gawain had his two hander as did Augustine. The fight between Gawain and Percival was damn amazing. I\u2019d never have thought that someone could move that fast with a two-handed sword or a maul, but both men up there acted like they were swinging nothing bigger than a fly swatter. It was amazing to watch them dodge and weave. The strikes were so different than what you see in knife fighting. There is more dodging and less actual strikes. They kind of have to do it that way. It\u2019s not possible to strike as many times with a heavy weapon and the strikes have to be planned then implemented. Not that it looked choreographed or anything, but I could tell a couple times that Gawain was waiting for certain opportunities to land different hits. The same was true for Percival. In the end Percival won, but not by much. Gawain wasn\u2019t happy to lose to Percival, but he was gracious in his defeat.<br /> <br /> In the end Augustine ended up winning the melee with Gawain and Percival tying for second place, much like Calamity and I did. I\u2019m sorry to say that I missed most of Augustine\u2019s fights. I was going over events in my head and taking some notes. I originally brought along my little notebook to take notes on drink preferences and to make a list of anything that we were running low on, but it did come in handy for other purposes as well. Anyway\u2026back to the events of today\u2026<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> <u>Highsummer \u201914 Observations</u><br /> <br /> -The Summer Court has attempted to scare or harm Felicity. They had previously told Felicity should she appear in a public Court function something bad would happen. While the Spring Court\u2019s last gathering was not dangerous for her, she took them by surprise; this time they knew she would be on Jolie\u2019s arm and had time to prepare. The others are chasing ghosts and stories of Extras, but the facts are self-evident here. This is what passes for subtle among the Court of Wrath. Apparently.<br /> <br /> The method was to frame Desiree for altering Felicity\u2019s water. As it turns out, we always knew where Desiree was. While they may not have been able to predict that would be the case, it would work if we were not fooled (because they would be the obvious choice but with plausible deniability) or if we were (because Desiree is, outside the Winter Court, the most hated Seasonal Changeling by Summer since Joan\u2019s relationship with Andromeda seems to have caused an about face on her.).<br /> <br /> In other words, it\u2019s obvious. Completely.<br /> <br /> -Becky is more unstable than I expected. My seduction of White Maria was sure to upset De La Rocha and would possibly upset Dark Kimberly. As Dark Kimberly looks up to Julia, I assumed she would handle Dark Kimberly if it came to it. As it turned out, Dark Kimberly was not upset, and De La Rocha, while angry, ultimately proved herself and adult about it. Fortunately.<br /> <br /> Becky, I am told, lost her shit. This was completely unexpected; White Maria is her best friend, but there was never anything romantic between them (broadly speaking, White Maria is not very into women, except me, because I am better than most women) and little sign of jealousy. And jealousy was not the issue here; she felt I was making her my slave. Which is fair. She does smell like me now. But I am not dictating she do anything, I am not making her stay with me, I am not telling her what to wear or who to screw. For someone being kept as a slave, she sure has a lot of options.<br /> <br /> That said, she is I\u2019s now. She has not admitted it, but she will. Absolutely.<br /> <br /> According to Calamity, Becky and Dahlia both mentioned my seductions and collecting people. No one comes to me without the desire, and I do not keep any Changeling against their will. They talk of Flores, but the fact is Flores no longer needs others to satisfy her lusts. She still enjoys lovemaking and cuddling to bond, but when she craves satisfaction\u2026well\u2026she knows where to come. Of course she changed after sharing my bed; that is a watershed moment for anyone, man or woman. Still, Calamity is right, and I must have someone deal with these rumors. Not Julia. Maybe Lorelei. Maybe.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, Calamity named those names in front of Julia, so now I have to tighten my grip on her to ensure she does not murder either of them. The one exception to my rule of not controlling them after claiming them is Julia, and her\u2026fanatical love makes me forced to tighten her leash. If I did not believe she was tightly under my control, she would scare me. Definitely.<br /> <br /> -Jolie and Felicity wore the most unappealing sun gowns. Ugh. Who wants sunlight wrapped around them? Oddly.<br /> <br /> -Lorelei is having more luck with her girls keeping peace than I have been with mine. De La Rocha and Oleander have been chatting away like (I am told) they used to before Lori entered the picture. I hope this helps to repair their friendship. In all the anger and turmoil of late, seeing that repaired is nice, and I am very fond of De La Rocha and I like Oleander, so if they are not fighting such is excellent. Certainly.<br /> <br /> -Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne and Monica seem to be getting along very well. And so soon after the break-up with Hailey. Interesting. It is sad Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne and I have not spoken more. Even if she is Belgian we are the Western Europeans in the Freehold, and while she may be Belgian, and least her French is correct. Silly Canadians.<br /> <br /> -Andromeda and Joan came by, and have been there longer than the brief visit expected. Louis and Wen Ja actually gave their honor guard positions to Calamity and Gawain, and they could not be happier. Andromeda smiled so much. I too smiled, despite myself. Her love for Joan was infectious, and I did not expect her to be doing so well. I may have held Julia\u2019s hand a little tighter while there. Lovingly.<br /> <br /> -Dark Kimberly was looking ridiculously attractive. No further comment, but she was clearly on the prowl. Were it not for concerns about Calamity\u2019s happiness, I would be looking to helping to\u2026repair\u2026her relationship with White Maria. Perhaps\u2026with Flores\u2019 help. Possibly.<br /> <br /> Seriously. Yum.<br /> <br /> -Austin wants to get support for a \u201cChestnut Party\u201d around Christmas. I had heard the men in my family discussing such things, pursuits with \u201cfallen women\u201d gathering chestnuts nude from the floor and men\u2026taking advantage of the situation. Austin\u2019s was less sexist, allowing for \u201cpitchers\u201d and \u201ccatchers\u201d (I hate those terms. Sex is more complicated than that. Americans.) each of either sex, though I can\u2019t imagine it was that exciting for the female \u201cpitchers,\u201d but I could be wrong.<br /> <br /> I am not sure if I would go, but I would not be gathering, as I would be dressed. Not because I have issue with being seen nude\u2026showing my body nude can only draw more pretty things to me. Hopefully.<br /> opefully<br /> <br /> <br /> -So the more masculine diversions happened not too long after Joan and Andromeda arrived. Joan was still joined at the hip with Andromeda, and so her position in both light and heavy weapons was taken by Shi, a Kitsune of the Autumn Court (and the Freehold\u2019s only Japanese Changeling other than Moon I think.) I have only seen him a couple times. For light weapons Calamity, Jacob, and Luna represented our group, all fighting with knives, while Shi (Sai) Sandoval (Sword) and TJ (Sword) participated. Calamity, Jacob, and Luna were the finalists, with the master defeating her students. Heavy weapons were more varied. Gawain with his Heavy Sword faced off against Viscount Augustine (Heavy Sword) Shi (Flaming Staff) TJ (Giant Razorblade) Moon (Scythe) and Percival (Maul). Viscount Augustine was the victor, with Gawain and Percival as the other finalists. My Motley represented well.<br /> <br /> Scythe, Giant Razorblade, Magic Fire Staff. Seriously.<br /> <br /> People watching was fun and the outfits elaborate. I must consider what I need to exchange to get some hedgespun clothes made. As the day wore on, however, more occurred\u2026<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XLIII</i><br /> <br /> The best thing about Insincere Marguerite is her humility.<br /> <br /> I will note Dark Kimberly's trashing picking was mentioned several times.<br /> <br /> Each match, including NPC vs. NPC was rolled out as a single contested roll. For light it was Dexterity + Weaponry, for Heavy it was Strength or Dexterity + Weaponry given no damage rolls were involved.<br /> <br /> Heh, Chestnut parties. That was funny.<br /> <br /> Anyway, excitement and intrigue! We finish this next session, and move ahead the timeline to Calamity\u2019s Birthday. Once that is done, we move into Autumn. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T01:47:16-08:00","id":782147,"title":"","content":"Here we finish up Highsummer, then jump to Calamity\u2019s Birthday before jumping ahead to October, so this is the rest of the summer of 2014. Enjoy. <br /> <br /> <i>Session XLIV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> Archery was the last of the three big competitions . Percival, Haley, Ji Wen Ja, Shi and Felicity all made a good showing, but only Percival and Felicity made their shots at maximum range. They went on to moving targets, just those two. Felicity and her bow made of sunlight blew Percival and his Robin Hood costume out of the water. I was pretty happy about it until I noticed that Desiree was bummed about it, considering how Felicity, you know, strutted over to Princess Joli after.<br /> <br /> Once the competitions were done, it was time for the showing off. Captain Jack showed up on the back of a circus elephant, about that time, plodding into the fairgrounds with his usual flair. Calamity and Jacob threw knives at each other and various fruits they carried, and they did it damn well. It was just awesome to watch, you know?<br /> <br /> Mine and Captain Jack\u2019s shenanigans went perfectly. Wenceslas handled Jenny\u2019s Cobblethought mask, so she could be the third Captain Jack. Wrestling is not my strong suit, and it took a couple of tries to get my face to stick on Calamity, so I wasn\u2019t, you know, the most super awesome, but Calamity and Captain Jack were both just great and made all five of us look good. And wrestling in the mud was tons of fun.<br /> <br /> Speaking of tons of fun - the Midsummer\u2019s Night Dream play was definitely that. Lori\u2019s idea to have Changelings playing the mortals and humans playing the fairies went over awesomely. Austin as Bottom was fucking hilarious, and Lori was just radiant, of course. Maybe we should do more stuff like that, not that she isn\u2019t awesome whatever she does.<br /> <br /> Chalcedony was there, playing her part. She moved a little stiffly, like she\u2019d been hurt. I went to go talk to her after the play, since Joan and Andromeda left right after, but Insincere Marguerite beat me there. She was acting kinda weird too, less, you know, aloof than usual. Chalcedony wouldn\u2019t say what had happened, said she was too embarrassed and that she had healed herself already. Lori came up after a bit and specifically asked about the bit outside the bathroom, but Chalcedony was noncommittal.<br /> <br /> That was the end of the investigating we did though. Not the end of the evening - bonfires were lit, a couple of musical acts started performing and we all hung out for a bit. The Handmaidens showed up, which, you know, I wasn\u2019t thrilled about, but Calamity rescued Tamara and then got out herself. I owe Becky a drink for that, I think. They went after Lori next, but De la Roche stared them off and wound up dragging Lori into one of the tents.<br /> <br /> I stuck at the bar with Jacob. Boss Lowjack, Tamara and Dominica were hanging out with us until Dark Kimberly came up and lured Dominica away. That had me a little worried, cause I didn\u2019t want Dominica having problems with Annika. But it wasn\u2019t really my place, so... Dominica is a real sweetheart though. When I mentioned some things were, you know, stressful, she really wanted to help. I couldn\u2019t really think of anything then, but I promised I\u2019d keep her in mind.<br /> <br /> Moon and Shi came by after a while. They wanted to warn us that the Handmaidens were about and then Shi Cobblethoughted Lori\u2019s face from my dreams and wandered off to embarrass them. It startled me a little, but since he apparently flipped them both over at the same time, it couldn\u2019t, you know, look bad on Lori.<br /> <br /> Shi came on to me a little, when he\u2019d come back and we were chatting. He\u2019s a very pretty dude, but, you know, not really my type, and I was hoping to distract Desiree a little. She was amenable, so I\u2019ve had a pretty good night. Calamity went home with Becky so she\u2019s probably had a good night too.<br /> <br /> <br /> August 13th<br /> <br /> Well, I finally figured it was as good a time as any to go looking for Greg Andrews. And it figures that Oath and Punishment would say that he\u2019s not under the same sky. At least it does mean he\u2019s not dead. So I\u2019ve started trying to track him down more, you know, mundanely. Or at least, see if he can be, where he lived before, how he disappeared, or whatever happened. I haven\u2019t gotten anywhere so far, but it\u2019s a step. The others know about it now too.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s see, other stuff - Felicity\u2019s car got stolen the other day. They found it smashed into a canyon wall. Princess Joli bought her another one apparently. Their relationship has gotten even closer, which has Becky and Desiree, you know, a little bummed. Calamity and me have tried to keep them cheered up, but it\u2019s only gone so far.<br /> <br /> Things that haven\u2019t been going on is working with Chalcedony. She\u2019s never said \u2018no\u2019 but things keep coming up. I\u2019ve tried not to be pushy, you know, cause it\u2019s her choice and everything. It\u2019s a big deal, to let somebody in your head like that. Insincere Marguerite\u2019s gotten fussy about it anyway. I don\u2019t like the whole thing.<br /> <br /> On the good news front, De la Roche and Julia are in the motley now, all official, you know? We offered to include Luna but she likes her independence. Also, plans for Calamity\u2019s birthday are proceeding apace. I can\u2019t wait. I don\u2019t think she knows about it yet - the others all promised to keep it secret. It\u2019s gonna be awesome!<br /> <br /> August 19th<br /> <br /> That went perfect! Just like I imagined and even better. Calamity loved it and she told me it kept her from doing something self destructive, so... bonus? Thinking about being taking was bothering her, obviously, but she did a good job focusing on the positive.<br /> <br /> We went to Guardians of the Galaxy after sex breakfast, to give Becky and Captain Jack time to set things up. And cause it sounded awesome, you know? It totally was just super amazing. Not at all like Flash Gordon or Space Jam, really. Definitely not like both, despite Insincere Marguerite\u2019s insistence that Flash Gordon was Space Jam for football. Anyways, Guardians of the Galaxy was amazing.<br /> <br /> When we got home, Joan, Andromeda, Dahlia, Flores and Oleander all jumped out to yell Happy Birthday. Then we had cake, and Captain Jack jumped from the large one, wearing a slave Leia costume to sing Happy Birthday a la Marilyn Monroe. Calamity ate it up.<br /> <br /> Tommy and Queen Charlotte showed up too, a little bit later. It was a hell of an evening, with cake and flirting and presents. Insincere Marguerite even worked out some of her problems with Becky and Dahlia, and Queen Charlotte agreed to speak with the Courts of Love for her. That was another good thing for Calamity to hang onto, you know?<br /> <br /> Things kinda trickled off, with people heading home or grouping up to head to rooms. Flores, De la Roche and Oleander all joined the ladies, Luna and Jacob went off together, and then me and Calamity, and Becky found ourselves alone. We wound up deciding against the lawn darts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> It\u2019s the morning after, and there have been a few developments, but unfortunately we\u2019re no nearer to truly solving whatever mystery Chalcedony is wrapped up in. Still, by and large the Highsummer Festival was a rollicking success, and the play\u2026<br /> <br /> But I\u2019m getting ahead of myself. The last time I wrote in this diary I was watching the weapons competitions. It was a little disappointing that none of the motley actually won their respective events, but I think we made a pretty good showing nonetheless. None of us were participating in the archery event, so I confess I didn\u2019t pay as much attention to that one. I did note that Felicity won that particular competition, wielding a bow that seemed to be made of sunlight. She dedicated her victory to Princess Jolie, which raised some eyebrows (and some hackles, unless I\u2019m very much mistaken).<br /> <br /> Of somewhat more interest to me was the knife-throwing demonstration, which involved Calamity and Jacob taking turns as performer and target. I confess to being a bit of a girly-girl for a while there, and gasping and hiding my eyes every time one of Calamity\u2019s knives got close to hitting Jacob\u2019s pale flesh. I trust Calamity\u2026 I really do, but even a master can make the occasional mistake. She never even nicked him, though, and that\u2019s impressive considering all of the fancy throws she tried. And he gave as good as he got, too\u2026 Jacob is also quite the impressive knife thrower, as it turns out.<br /> <br /> The last noteworthy event of the Festival was the requisite horseplay between Gawain and Captain Jack. Ever the impresario, Jack showed up for the festivities riding a full-grown elephant. Man, I wish I had his connections! In any case, it wasn\u2019t long before he and Gawain started their little staged tiff, and a few others (cleverly disguised in a variety of ways, both magical and mundane) joined the fray, so that eventually there appeared to be three Captain Jacks and two Gawains wrestling in the mud (there was some splash damage, but I made sure to keep well clear of the fracas). Though there were no definitive winners or losers, the Jacks had the Gawains outnumbered, so I suppose the outcome was a foregone conclusion.<br /> <br /> The Festival itself wound down after that, and I had to hurry back to the Dream House to make sure that everything was ready for the play. I tell you, directing the evening\u2019s entertainment was a harrying, maddening, <u><u>wonderful</u></u> experience. There are ten thousand things that the director and producer have to keep an eye on which the actors never even think about, and the fact that I was also acting in one of the lead roles meant that I had even less time to devote to them, so I tried to make sure that everything was as ready as it could be<u> <u>before</u></u> the curtain rose.<br /> <br /> We performed <u><u>A Midsummer Night\u2019s Dream</u></u> on our outdoor stage, and I couldn\u2019t be prouder of the way things went off. My cast \u2013 both mortals and changelings \u2013 performed the familiar lines almost perfectly, and the sets and costumes were well worth the extra time and resources we put into them. I had been a little nervous about how the Freehold would react to my creative casting, but the fact that mortals were cast in all the faerie roles and changelings played all the mortals was regarded as clever\u2026 maybe even avant-garde.<br /> <br /> Plus\u2026 no one can fault the casting of Austin as Nick Bottom. He\u2019s a natural comedic genius.<br /> <br /> My own performance as Helena went fairly well, too\u2026 okay, if I drop the false modesty, I\u2019d say I nailed it. It was one of the better performances of my career to date, and I don\u2019t see any harm in being proud of that fact. But in all honesty, I know that one good performance does not make a good show, and that the success of last night\u2019s staging was the result of a <u><u>lot</u></u> of hard work from a <u><u>lot</u></u> of talented people. As I said before, I couldn\u2019t be prouder of my cast, stagehands, and technical staff, and I made sure that they all knew how much I appreciated their efforts.<br /> <br /> The party continued at the Dream House for a couple of hours after the final curtain, and the cast got the chance to mingle with the crowd. I think some of the mortals were a little awe-struck by the Lost they met, and I wouldn\u2019t be surprised if some of them went home with members of the Freehold. In fact, it\u2019s entirely possible that a few of them might be enchanted the next time I see them, so I suppose I should be prepared to explain a few things.<br /> <br /> I schmoozed and hobnobbed as best I could, trying to make at least a few minutes for everyone present. Dominica was there (oh, I forgot to mention that I had spoken with her earlier at the Festival and invited her to attend), and I was glad to see her out and about. She wasn\u2019t there for <u><u>long</u></u>, though, as Dark Kimberly swept in and turned on the charm, leading her arm-in-arm from the grounds. I almost feel like I should have tried to stop that seduction, but they\u2019re both adults. I just hope Annika can see past her petty jealousy when it comes to coping with the new girl.<br /> <br /> Madame Spidertoes stopped by as well. I saw her across the crowd, talking with D. My honey looked a little stricken, so I decided to come to her rescue. Spidertoes turned her attention away from my paramour as I approached, and it looked like D let out a breath that she had been holding for a few seconds. \u201cLorelei my dear,\u201d Spidertoes said with a smile, \u201cwhat an enchanting performance. It was most enjoyable, and you were radiant, of course.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled and dropped into a shallow curtsy. \u201cThank you so much for coming, Madame,\u201d I said in my most courteous tones, \u201cno Freehold function would be complete without your presence. I\u2019m glad you enjoyed our little show.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded imperiously. \u201cIndeed. But I am afraid I must be going. The evening wears on, and there is much to do.\u201d And with that she took her leave.<br /> <br /> I turned to look at D, who was still breathing a little funnily, and had her eyes closed. \u201cYou okay, babe?\u201d I asked, touching her arm.<br /> <br /> Her eyes snapped open, and she gave me a quavery little smile. \u201cYeah,\u201d she said softly. She took my hand in her own, and that seemed to steady her. \u201cYeah, I\u2019m fine, Lori. She just\u2026 Spidertoes just\u2026 I think she was flirting with me,\u201d she said softly.<br /> <br /> I tried not to let the ice water in my veins reach my face. \u201cWho could blame her?\u201d I asked lightly.<br /> <br /> Her face stayed serious. \u201cNo, it\u2019s just\u2026 she still has so much power over me, Lori. She talks to me like that, and it gets my motor running, and\u2026\u201d The pain in her eyes was heartbreaking. \u201c\u2026and that\u2019s <u><u>not</u></u> okay. I\u2019m with you now.\u201d<br /> <br /> I squeezed her hand, as much to reassure myself as her. \u201cIt <u><u>is</u></u> okay,\u201d I said softly. \u201cI won\u2019t pretend that it doesn\u2019t bother me at all, honey, but\u2026 she was a huge part of your life, and it\u2019s natural that there are still some residual feelings there. And even if I don\u2019t like it very much, I do understand it.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded, and a genuine smile peeked through. \u201cThere\u2019s Oleander,\u201d she said, nodding over my shoulder, \u201clet\u2019s go say hi, and the two of us can hang on your arms while you play the social butterfly for a while, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> That sounded like a peachy-keen idea to me, so the next hour or so is a very pleasant warm blur in my memory. I think we talked to just about everyone before one of my lovers was hijacked by someone who has been trying to get into her panties for even longer than I have. Flores dropped by to say hi, and to compliment me on the production, and to attempt once more to seduce Oleander. My lover was a little tipsy by this point, and I could tell that her resolve was weakening. She looked at me and mouthed \u201cwhat should I do?\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled at her. \u201cSweetie,\u201d I said softly, \u201cyou\u2019re the only person who can answer that question. If you want to go off with Flores for the night, I won\u2019t stop you. I won\u2019t blame you, and I promise I\u2019ll still be here for you tomorrow. She\u2019s a talented, passionate, caring lover, and I wouldn\u2019t stop you from sharing that experience for the world, if it\u2019s something you want.\u201d<br /> <br /> D threw in her two cents as well. \u201cShe\u2026 really knows what she\u2019s doing,\u201d she said softly, \u201cand Lori\u2019s really not the jealous type. I\u2019d go for it if I was you.\u201d<br /> <br /> Oleander still looked uncertain, but she nodded, and allowed herself to be led off toward the parking lot. D and I were both overcome by a fit of giggles (and yes, D <u><u>does</u></u> giggle, no matter what she says, and it\u2019s <u>adorable</u>). \u201cI wondered how long it was going to take her,\u201d D said breathlessly a moment later. \u201cFlores always gets her girl in the end.\u201d<br /> <br /> D left me alone for a few minutes after that so that she could talk to a few of her friends (in Spanish, which is never much fun for me anyway). I caught sight of Chalcedony standing by herself across the yard, and decided to see if I could get anything else out of her. I\u2019d noticed during the performance that she looked a little stiff, like she was sore or otherwise hurt in some way.<br /> <br /> \u201cHey, Chalcedony!\u201d I called out as I approached. \u201cOr should I say Hermia? Great performance tonight. You really did the Dream House proud.\u201d<br /> <br /> She smiled a little nervously. \u201cThanks,\u201d she said softly, \u201cit was fun.\u201d<br /> <br /> I gave her my best concerned friend look. \u201cAre you okay, Chalcedony? You seemed almost like you were in pain a few times tonight. Not enough to affect your performance or anything, but\u2026 well, I was just wondering if anything was wrong.\u201d<br /> <br /> She shook her head. \u201cNo, I just\u2026 I think I might have sprained something the other day. It\u2019s kind of you to ask, but don\u2019t worry.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, okay,\u201d I said, before pressing my advantage. \u201cI confess, I was a little worried about you earlier. You\u2019d been waiting for the bathroom when I went in to find Becky, and then you were gone when we came out. I thought something might have happened to you.\u201d<br /> <br /> Something that looked like panic showed briefly in her eyes. \u201cI\u2026 no. I just\u2026 I got tired of waiting and went somewhere else.\u201d She smiled wanly at me, and then looked around. \u201cI\u2026 I should go. I have\u2026 things to do.\u201d And she scampered off. Curiouser and curiouser, as Alice might say.<br /> <br /> I mentioned this encounter to the rest of the motley, but there was nothing much we could do about it at the time. Marguerite looked stricken over the fact that Chalcedony had been upset by our encounter, which in and of itself is a little strange. I wonder what sort of mysterious hold Little Girl Blue has over our Gallic nymph?<br /> <br /> In any case, as I wandered around waiting for D to rejoin me, the Handmaidens of Night approached me. They played their usual games, keeping on opposite sides of me like predators probing for a weak spot, but they never actually adopted a threatening air. In fact, whichever of them was behind me at any given time was usually giving me a <u><u>heavenly</u></u> shoulder rub around my wings while I attempted to stay lucid enough to talk to the other one.<br /> <br /> They were very complimentary, as usual, though they didn\u2019t arrive in time to see the play (I threw them a pout upon learning that little tidbit). I knew what they were up to with the flattery and the coy glances, of course, but at the moment I didn\u2019t really care. The thought of spending part of my evening with one or both of them was particularly appealing, and I still wouldn\u2019t mind giving them a try at some point.<br /> <br /> It wasn\u2019t to be, alas. D charged in as bold as brass to rescue my virtue (ha!). \u201cWhat the fuck do you think you\u2019re doing?\u201d she asked the Handmaidens angrily.<br /> <br /> \u201cD,\u201d I hissed, \u201cyou\u2019re being rude!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot rude enough,\u201d she growled as the Handmaidens smiled at her.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe were just talking to Lori,\u201d they said innocently.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell you can cut that shit out right now,\u201d D retorted, \u201cyou can get your kicks elsewhere. She\u2019s mine tonight.\u201d<br /> <br /> The Handmaidens looked at each other and sort of shrugged, then apparently decided that discretion was the better part of valor. \u201cVery well,\u201d one of them said. The other completed the thought with \u201cwe\u2019ll continue this at some later time.\u201d And they wandered off.<br /> <br /> \u201cNot fucking likely,\u201d D muttered to herself as they left.<br /> <br /> \u201cD,\u201d I said sternly, \u201cthis is our house, and they are guests. What\u2019s gotten into you?\u201d<br /> <br /> She muttered something I couldn\u2019t quite hear.<br /> <br /> \u201cSorry,\u201d I said, \u201cI didn\u2019t quite catch that.\u201d<br /> <br /> She sighed. \u201cI know the look of a Leechfinger looking for a meal,\u201d she said reluctantly. \u201cHow are you? Do you feel weak?\u201d<br /> <br /> Well, of course, I <u><u>hadn\u2019t</u></u> felt weak until she asked me that. After the question was out there, however, I couldn\u2019t tell if they\u2019d drained any life from me or not. I sort of shrugged and waved the question off as unimportant. \u201cSo what you\u2019re trying to tell me,\u201d I said with \u2013 I admit \u2013 a bit of malicious glee, \u201cis that you weren\u2019t claiming me as your territory back there, you were swooping in to rescue your helpless and pathetic girlfriend?\u201d<br /> <br /> I saw the panic rising behind D\u2019s eyes. \u201cLori, I\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I couldn\u2019t hold in the laughs any longer. \u201cI swear sweetie, sometimes you are just too <u><u>easy</u></u>,\u201d I sighed. \u201cI know you had my best interests at heart. You\u2019re my guardian angel\u2026 my knight in shining armor.\u201d<br /> <br /> She grinned sheepishly at the characterization. \u201cWell\u2026 I admit I was sort of staking a claim as well,\u201d she said. \u201cAfter what happened earlier with Spidertoes\u2026 well, maybe I feel like I need to reassert myself a little bit. Remind myself how much better things are with you.\u201d She looked away for a moment. \u201cI need to be with you tonight, Lori,\u201d she muttered. \u201cI couldn\u2019t let them get in the way.\u201d When she turned back to face me, the raw need and lust in her eyes lit a fire between my legs.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou want to head up to our room?\u201d I asked breathlessly. My goodness, but the night had gotten hot all of a sudden.<br /> <br /> She put her hands on my shoulders. \u201cFuck that,\u201d she whispered. \u201cThere are tents all around us. I want the whole Freehold to hear you <u><u>scream</u></u> out how happy I make you.\u201d<br /> <br /> The thought was\u2026 intriguing. I felt the capillaries open in my cheeks, but I wasn\u2019t blushing out of embarrassment. I opened my mouth to say something, but for a moment the only sound that came out was a quiet little moan. I looked around. Nobody was really paying any attention to the two of us, but a lot of people were still around. Privacy was not going to be possible. \u201cLet\u2019s do it,\u201d I husked. \u201cLet\u2019s do it <u><u>now</u></u>.\u201d<br /> <br /> D pulled me into an unoccupied tent and fumbled with the zipper for a few moments before turning to ravish me. I\u2019d like to be able to say that we tore each other\u2019s clothes off in a fit of passion\u2026 but, well, I was still wearing my costume from the play, and that\u2019s Dream House property, so in reality things were a little more controlled. D spent the next half hour or so dedicated to pleasing me, and well\u2026 a few months of practice have done wonders for her technique. She knows my body better than any of my other lovers, and she knows lots of ways to drive me crazy, and she used them all. I\u2019d be surprised if anyone at the party didn\u2019t hear us.<br /> <br /> Now I was a little out of it by the time we emerged (I carefully timed the opening of the tent flaps so that I hadn\u2019t <u><u>quite</u></u> finished putting my dress back on), but I thought I heard a vague rumor that someone had run the Handmaidens off by deftly pushing both of them into the mud at the same time. And that someone was\u2026 me, apparently. Nobody <u><u>really</u></u> believed that I would (or could?) do such a thing, and the prevailing theory was that the incorrigible trickster Shi had adopted my appearance in order to make a little mischief.<br /> <br /> But I digress. D and I continued to make the rounds for a while, until the crowd started to thin out. As the evening wore on, most of the motley disappeared with their more-or-less significant others. Calamity had left with Becky while D and I were otherwise engaged, and I think Gawain ended up going home with Desiree. Marguerite and Julia left the party soon after (I think White Maria might have been with them, but with D purring contentedly in my arms I didn\u2019t want to spoil the mood by inquiring). Jacob and Luna were among the last to retire.<br /> <br /> The two of us made our way up to bed after saying goodnight to the last partygoers. I closed the door behind us and the two of us undressed for bed. As I pulled the covers over us and snuggled up against D\u2019s back, I leaned in to kiss her neck and whisper in her ear. \u201cI love you, Maria.\u201d<br /> <br /> She turned gently in my arms and kissed me softly. \u201cI love you, Juliette,\u201d she replied, and a few minutes later we were both fast asleep.<br /> <br /> Even with all the crazy shit that went down at the Festival yesterday\u2026 I can\u2019t help but think about how good life has been to me.<br /> <br /> \u00d8 \u00d8 \u00d8 \u00d8 \u00d8<br /> <br /> Ooga-chaka-ooga-ooga!<br /> <br /> Happy birthday to Calamity! Well, yesterday was, anyway. Honestly, it\u2019s been so long since I wrote anything in this diary that I should probably do a brief recap of recent events before I even try to cover what happened yesterday.<br /> <br /> Relationship-wise, things continue apace and romances rise and fall. Dark Kimberly and Annika say they\u2019re taking an extended \u201cbreak\u201d from each other, though it seems to me like that story has reached its end. Andromeda continues to improve, and she and Joan seem to be more in love than ever. Desiree is forlorn because Jolie and Felicity seem to be closer than ever. (A lot of people aren\u2019t happy about that, by the way. Someone stole Felicity\u2019s car and drove it off a cliff last week. This did not faze Jolie, however: she just bought her lover another one.) And Julia is still pushing for the four of us to make our love both public and official with some sort of binding pledge.<br /> <br /> There hasn\u2019t been much movement on the Chalcedony front; things seem to have calmed down there for the moment. She still won\u2019t let Gawain into her dreams to disarm her trigger; he says she keeps making excuses and putting it off. We\u2019re probably going to have to force some sort of intervention there if this continues. In possibly related news, Oleander was able to analyze the chemical in Felicity\u2019s water bottles. She says that it wouldn\u2019t have killed Felicity (not in the quantities present, at any rate), but would have had a particularly embarrassing effect on... well, let\u2019s just say \u201cher stomach\u201d and leave it at that.<br /> <br /> The biggest news in my opinion is that the Last Dance motley now has two new members! By common agreement, D and Julia were invited to join us officially, and both of them were happy to accept. D has even been grumbling recently about giving up her apartment, since these days she really only drops by there about once a week or so to make sure nothing has been stolen anyway. We also asked Luna to join, but she declined (politely), saying that she prefers to be more of a lone wolf (err\u2026 moth). I also mentioned the idea to Oleander, but she\u2019s already in a motley of her own, and she quite understandably didn\u2019t want to insult them by leaving it.<br /> <br /> Things are going really well between me and Oleander, by the way. She\u2019s sweet and funny and romantic and the two of us get along famously. I think she and D have worked through the awkwardness now as well, and they seem to be comfortable in each other\u2019s company again. I\u2026 have more to say on that front, but I\u2019ll get to it a little while later. For now, let\u2019s just say I\u2019m more than content with the state of my various relationships.<br /> <br /> So\u2026 birthday. Right. Gawain had told us all that Calamity\u2019s birthday was August 18<sup>th</sup>, and that we were under no circumstances to let her know that we were planning a surprise party for her. We gave it our best shot \u2013 our collective nonchalance could probably have leveled a city block from a mile away \u2013 but I\u2019m sure the sheer lack of interest in the date probably clued her in that we were planning something. Luckily, we had an ace in the hole.<br /> <br /> Most of us had seen the trailers and commercials for the new <u><u>Guardians of the Galaxy</u></u> movie, and people were moderately excited about it. I\u2019ve now seen most of the Marvel Studios \u201cCinematic Universe\u201d films, and I\u2019ve been consistently impressed by the quality of the films\u2026 although, let\u2019s face it; I was always more of a DC girl back in my comic-reading phase. What can I say? I dig the Batman.<br /> <br /> In any case, the fact that the trailers for the film actually contained music I <u><u>know</u></u> got me interested. I\u2019m glad I decided to give it a chance, because the film was phenomenal. It had this sort of action-comedy-sci-fi vibe that I can\u2019t really describe, and the soundtrack was entirely comprised of songs from the good old 70s, thanks to a mix tape made by the main character\u2019s mother before he was abducted by aliens. Blue Swede, the Jackson 5, David Bowie, the Runaways\u2026 the hits just keep on coming!<br /> <br /> Julia was quick to claim \u201cdibs\u201d on the green-skinned alien assassin Gamora, which of course led to \u201chot-and-not\u201d discussions. Marguerite and I both opined that Chris Pratt\u2019s Star-Lord was quite tasty\u2026 though I don\u2019t think either of us would have kicked Gamora out of our beds either. As the other major characters in the film include a tree, a raccoon, and a very large scarred muscle-bound wrestler type, the discussions mostly centered around those two.<br /> <br /> In any case, we were all in high spirits as we walked back into the Dream House only to have all of our friends jump out from hiding and shout \u201csurprise\u201d at Calamity. She took it well, possibly because she was obviously expecting something of the sort to happen. I\u2019m not sure if she was expecting Captain Jack to jump out of the cake wearing speedos, though. I certainly wasn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> Since this was Calamity\u2019s shindig, Becky and Dahlia were naturally in attendance\u2026 though it quickly became clear that the two of them had other motives for being there as well. I think Marguerite must have spoken to the two of them at some point about their suspicions regarding her hypnotizing women into becoming her slaves, because the two of them approached me quietly at one point and began asking me very pointed questions about my French lover.<br /> <br /> \u201cLook,\u201d I said after a few minutes of pointless back-and-forth. \u201cInsincere Marguerite is a very powerful, commanding personality. People react to that sort of thing differently. Someone like me pushes back against it, while someone like Julia\u2026 well, we get our kicks in different ways.\u201d<br /> <br /> Becky nodded as I said this. \u201cYou can see why we\u2019re concerned\u2026\u201d she began.<br /> <br /> \u201cNot really,\u201d I countered. \u201cInsincere Marguerite and Julia have sort of a domme and sub relationship, but that\u2019s not really that unusual these days, is it? Do I act like I\u2019m under her power? Does de la Rocha?\u201d<br /> <br /> Dahlia considered the question. \u201cNo,\u201d she admitted, \u201cI suppose you don\u2019t.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cIf Julia is under Insincere Marguerite\u2019s power, it\u2019s because that\u2019s where she <u><u>wants</u></u> to be,\u201d I continued. \u201cThose two are very much in love. You only have to look at them to understand that. D and I are lucky enough to share in that love, and sometimes things get a little kinky. D takes to it better than I do, but I\u2019ve never seen <u><u>anything</u></u> that would make me believe that Insincere Marguerite is doing anything mystical or unethical to influence her partners. Okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> Though neither of them looked entirely convinced, they both acknowledged my opinion. \u201cThanks for talking with us about this, Lori,\u201d Becky said, and I think she really meant it. \u201cWe\u2019re just trying to look out for the people of this Freehold. You understand, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course,\u201d I said simply. \u201cLet me know if you want to know anything else.\u201d Neither of them approached me about Marguerite again last night, but I saw them talking to her, and the conversation seemed to end well. I hope they\u2019ve come to some sort of understanding.<br /> <br /> Queen Charlotte was there to wish Calamity a happy birthday as well (Captain Jack unabashedly gave her a big hug despite the fact that he was still mostly naked and covered in frosting at the time). A few of us approached the Autumn monarch to ask for her support when it comes time to plead Marguerite\u2019s case to the Courts of Love in Paris, and she cautiously agreed to reach out to them so that we can take the first steps along that path. I assure anyone reading this diary that my giddy excitement at this prospect has everything to do with clearing Marguerite\u2019s name and nothing to do with fulfilling my life-long dream of visiting Paris. So there. And shame on you, by the way! What the hell are you doing reading my private diary in the first place?<br /> <br /> One more thing I should mention before I get to the main event. Marguerite herself approached me as the evening wore on and drew me into a secluded alcove. \u201cBecky and Dahlia, they told me what you have said about me, ma ch\u00e9rie,\u201d she began. \u201cAnd Queen Charlotte as well. I wished to offer you my thanks.\u201d<br /> <br /> I gave her a quick but affectionate kiss. \u201cYou know I\u2019ll always do whatever I can to help you, Insincere Marguerite,\u201d I said. I specifically added the adjective to her name because I could see that she was feeling vulnerable and uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> \u201cOui,\u201d she said with a small smile, \u201cand I am grateful. But it is more than that, Lorelei. You are\u2026 I do not quite know how to say it. You are so special to me. Of all of my lovers, you are the one I cannot control. You push back against me whenever I try. And yet you stay with me. It means a lot. It means everything.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled back and kissed her again. \u201cYou don\u2019t have to take from me,\u201d I whispered to her, \u201cI\u2019m willing to share.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes,\u201d she agreed, \u201cbut sometimes I feel that I <u><u>need</u></u> someone to push back against me. Sometimes I pursue things which are not good for me. I could become what Becky and Dahlia fear, if I am not careful. I need to know that you will be there to stop that from happening. I need to know that you will save me from myself.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAlways,\u201d I promised seriously. I thought about saying more, about telling her how much I need her to do the same for me. I thought about telling her my deepest fears, that my need to be loved will end up driving away everyone I truly care about. I thought about telling her that every time I spend the night with Oleander, I worry that more and more of D is slipping away from me\u2026 but I also worry about the same thing happening in the other direction. But in the end I didn\u2019t say any of that.<br /> <br /> We sat in a comfortable silence for a few minutes. \u201cYou know,\u201d Marguerite began after a while, \u201cJulia is becoming more insistent that the four of us should make a pledge sealing our love. She wants something binding to exist between us.\u201d<br /> <br /> I sighed. \u201cI know,\u201d I said glumly, \u201cand I don\u2019t want to upset her. But\u2026 I was taken in the Spring of 1978, Marguerite. And for all that thirty-six years passed while I was in Arcadia, it sure as hell didn\u2019t <u><u>feel</u></u> like it while I was there. I talk a big game, but\u2026\u201d I hope she could see the trepidation and vulnerability in my eyes as I continued. \u201cI\u2019m really only nineteen, maybe twenty years old. I just\u2026 I need to think about it some more.\u201d<br /> <br /> Marguerite nodded, leaned in to embrace me, and kissed me passionately on the lips. \u201cI understand,\u201d she said softly. \u201cWhen you are ready, I would be happy to make such a pledge\u2026 with the three of you, or just with you. Whatever you would like.\u201d<br /> <br /> So that gave me a lot to think about.<br /> <br /> Luckily, I didn\u2019t have to think about it right then and there. I decided that I\u2019d been neglecting my other girlfriends for far too long, and set off in search of D and Oleander. Okay, it wasn\u2019t <u><u>that</u></u> big of a party, so I found them pretty quickly, chatting amiably off to one side. Each of them leaned in for a kiss as I approached, and the three of us started discussing music from the film, and everything was right with the world.<br /> <br /> And then Flores arrived. In typical Flores fashion, she blurted out that she was glad to see the two of them getting along so well, and then asked if we had all slept together yet. Oleander turned pink almost immediately, and even D colored slightly at the remark. I tried to salvage the situation by explaining that we didn\u2019t have that sort of a relationship, and Flores simply asked \u201cwhy not?\u201d<br /> <br /> Maybe it was the copiously flowing alcohol. Maybe it was the fact that the two of them had been getting along so well lately. Maybe it was the teasing, flirty atmosphere that seems to permeate the Dream House most of the time. Maybe it was just Flores. But whatever was responsible, I saw a flicker of interest in both D and Oleander\u2019s eyes.<br /> <br /> The two of them looked away from each other quickly. Flores looked confused, and maybe a little upset at this reaction. I took their hands in my own. \u201cLook,\u201d I began gently, \u201cI love you both. I don\u2019t want either of you to do anything that upsets you or makes you uncomfortable. But if this is something you both <u><u>want</u></u> to experience, I would love to share it with you.\u201d<br /> <br /> It was a fairly big moment for several reasons. I\u2019d told Oleander that I loved her once or twice before, but never in front of other people. To her credit, D didn\u2019t even bat an eye. I guess she knows me well enough by now that it didn\u2019t really come as much of a surprise to her.<br /> <br /> D and Oleander held a quick muttered conversation in Spanish, and then turned back to me. Their smiles were nervous, but genuine.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe, umm,\u201d D began softly, \u201cwe don\u2019t really want to\u2026 to do anything with each other. But we\u2019ve agreed that we can\u2026 be in the same bed while we do things with you two.\u201d<br /> <br /> Flores was obviously radiantly happy. As for me\u2026 well, I\u2019m not ashamed to admit that I might have cried a little bit as we headed upstairs. And then I was lying in bed surrounded by the flesh of my lovers, and their hands and lips were all over me and I was sighing and crying and moaning and screaming and at some point Marguerite and Julia were there as well and everything descended into a hot pink haze\u2026<br /> <br /> And I woke up this morning with D snuggled naked up against my right side and Oleander curled up against my left, both of them in my arms and breathing softly against my neck. And I remembered flashes of the two of them kissing briefly and holding each other for short moments in the heat of passion. And I grinned the biggest, happiest, most satisfied grin that I could. Because maybe, just maybe it\u2019s possible for this crazy relationship to work out after all.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T01:52:04-08:00","id":782150,"title":"","content":"<b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> \u2026 So, the knife throwing demonstration was next. Calamity went first and demonstrated her trick throwing by narrowly missing me and/or hitting a piece of fruit that I was holding. Then we switched it up and I threw knives at her. We both did well I think. Calamity was able to get her knives slightly closer to me without actually hitting me, which made her demonstration a little more interesting, but I held my own pretty well. Which is something considering I have not been throwing knives regularly since I got back from Her realm. I didn\u2019t tend to do a lot of knife throwing in Arcadia, but I have been practicing for a couple months here and I managed to sharpen, pun intended, my rusty skills a bit.<br /> <br /> After our demonstration there was an archery contest. I believe it was Percival, Ji Wen Ja, Haley, Shi and Felicity that entered. It came down to Felicity vs. Percival. They were both really good, but in the end Felicity won the day by splitting Percival\u2019s arrow down the center of the shaft with her shot. It was straight out of a movie. Remind me never to get on her bad side if she\u2019s got a bow handy. That was some damn impressive shooting. She then curtsied to Princess Jolie and said \u201cMy Lady.\u201d The downside to her winning was some people\u2019s reactions. Desiree was not happy with the whole \u201cMy Lady\u201d bit. TJ, Louis, Billy and Percival all kind of muttered and looked in Felicity\u2019s direction. Apparently they were not happy with either her winning, or her esteem in the Princess\u2019s eyes. It could have been a combination of the two. Trouble might start with Jolie being so openly \u201cwith\u201d Felicity. Her paramour is not of the seasonal courts and apparently the Freehold takes issue with those folks. Mostly.<br /> <br /> The tension didn\u2019t last long though. Around that time Jack arrived, spectacularly as usual. He rode in on an elephant being led by a couple of handlers. Jack then hopped down and thus began the latest \u201cshenanigans.\u201d The whole idea was that Jack and Gawain would wrestle and eventually be joined by doppelgangers of each of the participants. In the end there were two Gawain\u2019s and three Jack\u2019s. All of this was achieved using Cobblethought and one person that just looks an awful lot like Jack to begin with. It was fun. From what I heard the wrestling eventually moved out of the authorized area and into the mud. It was messy and eventually involved some of those standing on the sidelines. It sounded like a lot of fun. I\u2019m sorry to have missed it.<br /> <br /> And the fun and intrigue continued apace. The play went spectacularly well. Truly amazing. It was so easy to forget that it was just a production and to get sucked into the story. That had some interesting connotations considering it was a story involving the Fae and we\u2019re changelings, but other than that random thought that passed my mind, it was awesome. What happened after the play was interesting as well. It seems several people were concerned over Chalcedony\u2019s health. She performed in the play and did really well, but if you were observant you could tell that she was moving stiffly. Not stiffly in the way that would indicate that she was a puppet or anything, more that she was favoring one side over another due to pain. Insincere Marguerite, Gawain and Lorelei all went to talk to the girl at different times and came back with the same response. Chalcedony insisted that she was fine and was just stiff from an earlier injury. The injury itself was healed already, it was just sore. She didn\u2019t want to talk about it because it was embarrassing. I don\u2019t know about the others, but her answers were not really good enough for me. There was too much going on with her, or an imposter of her, earlier for this to not be suspicious. Lori I will admit was clever. She said that she was worried over Chalcedony since she hadn\u2019t seen her since the time outside the restrooms. Chalcedony for her part did not deny that had been her, but nor did she confirm it. More and more questions.<br /> <br /> For a little while it seemed that the bar was the place to be. Lowjack came by to chat. He mentioned that he had asked Vik and Molly to stay in plain sight for the rest of the evening. If for nothing else than to ease any possible suspicions as to their whereabouts. After a bit Tamara came by looking a bit flustered. Apparently the Handmaidens had cornered her again, but Calamity had \u201crescued\u201d her by telling her that Lowjack was looking for her. She gratefully left the twin terrors and came to the bar. The Handmaidens then flirted with Calamity for a while, from what I gathered, before moving on to Lori and De la Rocha. Lori seemed okay with the attention, but De la Rocha just wanted to hit them. I can understand the sentiment. But she held her temper and her tongue, and no violence was done upon the two predators.<br /> <br /> Shi and Moon came by not long after to talk and socialize. Shi wondered aloud if he should go stop the Handmaidens from doing more mischief. He seemed to answer his own question, pulled an image of Lori out of Gawain\u2019s head using Cobblethought and used it to disguise himself as our dear songstress. He then went in search of the two troublemakers to have some fun. He returned a little while later with a \u201ccat ate the canary\u201d grin and said that the Handmaidens wouldn\u2019t be bothering anyone else tonight and were currently going home to change. I\u2019m not sure what happened, but I think mud was involved. Couldn\u2019t have happened to a nicer pair.<br /> <br /> So, anyway\u2026Gawain and Desiree had come over to talk earlier and had stayed through all of that. Nothing important, just small talk, but it was good to see them. Dominika was also there, for a little while anyway. Dark Kimberly came by and was flirting with the dark skinned young lady and the two seemed to hit it off. They eventually went off together. No need to guess what they were up to. I guess Kimberly has broken things off with Annika. I suppose I can\u2019t blame her. Annika does seem the type to be rather controlling and I\u2019m not a fan of people trying to influence me like that.<br /> <br /> Oh\u2026before I forget. Apparently Oleander got back to Lori about what was in the water. It was nothing deadly but it would have caused some serious GI upset. Given the quantities in the bottles it would have kept Felicity laid up for a couple of days at least with a really embarrassing and miserable sickness. It was determined that the additive was a Goblin fruit that is fairly easily acquired in the Hedge, or at a Goblin Market. So that doesn\u2019t get us any closer to a culprit.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Okay\u2026so we\u2019d been setting this up for weeks and it mostly went as planned. Well, the party did go as planned. Calamity was wise to what was going on the whole time I think, but Gawain didn\u2019t realize how badly he was telegraphing that he was trying to keep a secret. He is a sweet guy, but deceit is not his forte. Which is all to the good. So, Calamity knew that we were planning her surprise birthday party, but it was fun anyway. While Jack, Becky and a few others got things set up we all went out to the movies to see \u201cGuardians of the Galaxy.\u201d It was the whole motley, including our recent editions of De la Rocha and Julia. We did ask Luna if she would like to become a part of the motley, but she said that she preferred to opt out. I can understand that. I think a part of me was a bit disappointed, but I can understand why she\u2019d want to remain unattached. Being a part of a group gives them some amount of power over you and that can be scary, and sometimes a bit confining. I worked alone or with just Rook for a long time so sometimes I will admit that I find myself a bit overwhelmed by my motley mates. I think Luna would be a bit overwhelmed too if she stayed in close proximity to the rest of us all the time. Anyhoo\u2026I had fun and can say with some confidence that the others had fun too. The opening of the movie was a bit of a downer, but the rest was just fun. It had action, explosions and talking raccoons. What more does a movie need? Anyway\u2026so we got back from the movie and Joan, Andromeda, who is doing much better now, Becky, Flores and Oleander all jumped out and yelled \u201cSurprise!\u201d Well, Calamity didn\u2019t really look surprised but she did look happy and that is what really matters the most.<br /> <br /> A little after the party started we had an unexpected guest arrive to wish good wishes to the birthday girl. Queen Charlotte came by. I think Calamity was really taken by that. They chatted for a bit and Charlotte agreed to stay for cake, which was soon enough rolled out. And of course after a rousing rendition of the \u201cHappy Birthday,\u201d Jack jumped out of the obviously fake cake much to everyone\u2019s amusement. Okay\u2026there were aspects of the cake that were real. I mean Jack was covered in bits of frosting for a while after that, but it was obviously hollow. The funny part, at least for those of us that were not her, was when Jack came up and hugged Queen Charlotte frosting and all.<br /> <br /> The party it seemed was a bit bittersweet for Calamity. She looked like she was having fun and went through all the correct motions, but I could tell that my friend was upset about something. She was enjoying herself at the party. She liked the company, but there was sorrow behind her smile. So as the party started to wind down I waited until Calamity was alone and asked if she was okay. She said that she was having a great time that the party was fun. I told her that \u201cI can see that but\u2026\u201d I left the sentence hanging there waiting for her to tell me what was going on. After a moment Calamity admitted that she was upset because she had been taken by the Gentry on her birthday. Her 14<sup>th</sup> birthday to be exact. Yeah, so that sucks. I told her that I was sorry this day brought up bad memories for her. I told her that I understood what she was feeling and admitted that I had been taken on my birthday as well. For me it was my 16<sup>th</sup> birthday. What is it with birthdays and life changing events?<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll admit that when she said she\u2019d been taken on her birthday it felt a bit like a sucker punch to the gut. I wasn\u2019t taken per se, but ended up getting lost and drawn into Arcadia on by birthday. Well, I suppose one could count the walls closing in on me and Elena as a hostile attempt to keep us. I thank the goddess that she made it out of that cave. I don\u2019t know what I would have done if Elena had been taken too. Would she have become like me, cold and dangerous? Would she have helped me keep my humanity? Would she be dead? What would she have become? All questions that I have thought of a million times and never want answered.<br /> <br /> So, yeah I understood where Calamity was coming from on that front. I\u2019m not particularly looking forward to my birthday in December either. Calamity asked what I was planning on doing and I told her that I was likely going to get spectacularly drunk. Probably not the healthiest way to go about dealing with things, but then when have I consistently done the \u201chealthy\u201d thing when it comes to me? Granted this will be my first birthday since coming back to \u2018the world.\u2019 I\u2019m not sure how I\u2019m really going to feel on that day. I\u2019m guessing it won\u2019t be great, but I don\u2019t know. In Her realm we didn\u2019t really celebrate birthdays. There wasn\u2019t really a way to track the passage of time, so the years all kind of blended together. The Lady celebrated my entering her service that day in the cave as a kind of \u2018coming of age\u2019 thing. There was also a ceremony when I was made a Knight of my the Lady\u2019s realm. So, I guess accomplishments were celebrated but not birthdays. I\u2019m not even really sure how old I am. In actual time I was only gone two years, but in Her realm it was so much longer than that. My guess is closer to fifteen or twenty. Long enough to make a name for myself in Her service and to grow close to my mentor. So, yeah, I\u2019m not sure how things will go on my birthday. I\u2019m still leaning towards getting spectacularly drunk.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not sure if I succeeded in cheering Calamity up. That was my initial intention, but I wasn\u2019t sure how to actually go about doing that. I don\u2019t know what would cheer me up, so I think I settled with commiserating with her and trying to lighten the mood just a bit. In the past I might have tried some silly prank on one of the others or some funny anecdote, but I haven\u2019t been that carefree since coming back to \u2018the world.\u2019 Ironic that I was more of a joker when I was so cold, no pun intended. Of course, most of my pranks ended up in someone getting hurt or me adding to the Lady\u2019s collection of treasures. I think the Lady liked my taste when it came to Treasures. She trusted me with the task on several occasions and I delivered. She certainly liked my taste when it came to Delight. She was so innocent and pure. She was gorgeous anyway, but I think those two qualities were what made my the Lady like Delight so much T\u0336o\u0336o\u0336 \u0336b\u0336a\u0336d\u0336 \u0336s\u0336h\u0336e\u0336 \u0336g\u0336o\u0336t\u0336 \u0336a\u0336w\u0336a\u0336y\u0336 \u0336. But then she got away. The Lady was not pleased to lose that particular Treasure. I was not happy at the time that she escaped and was more than willing to go get her back. How strange it is that the Lady\u2019s favorite Treasure is the one that cost the Lady of the Winter Winds one of her favorite Knights?<br /> <br /> And now I want to get drunk. Fuck.<br /> <br /> All that reminiscing over a single comment at a party. I think I might need help.<br /> <br /> Anyhoo\u2026 after the party wrapped up Lori, Insincere Marguerite, De la Rocha, Oleander and Flores all went upstairs together. No need to guess about their planned activities. The rest of us stayed downstairs and talked for a bit. Becky then told the rest of us about some other conversations that were going on tonight, specifically about Insincere Marguerite. Earlier that evening Insincere Marguerite gathered up Becky and Dahlia (yeah, she was at the party too) and started up a conversation. Things were going for a while and then they invited Lori to join them. Apparently they just flat out asked Lori if she thought that she was being controlled by Marguerite. Lorelei answered \u201cNo.\u201d Then De la Rocha was called over and she got a bit defensive about the questions, which may or may not have been a boon in Marguerite\u2019s favor or not. Both women said that they did not feel like they were being controlled in any way and essentially resented the inference. I think Insincere Marguerite finally got fed up with indirect accusations from both woman and just wanted to confront them and get the issue out in the open. I don\u2019t blame her. I would get fed up with people talking behind my back. Granted, I can understand to a certain degree the ladies\u2019 concerns about Marguerite. When you look at Julia you see a woman possessed and you wonder if it\u2019s just her personality or if it was something inspired by Marguerite in the first place.<br /> <br /> Earlier this evening I also noticed Julia and Insincere Marguerite talking to Charlotte. They were essentially asking the monarch if she\u2019d be willing to speak on Insincere Marguerite\u2019s behalf to the Courts of Love in Paris. Charlotte said yes and just asked that they have Lowjack send her the contact information that she would need to get in touch with them and start the process. I think it sounds like a worthwhile endeavor to me. Insincere Marguerite\u2019s habits with women may seem \u201coff\u201d to other people, but I don\u2019t think that she actually has any bad intentions towards them. The level of devotion from Julia is the one scary part of Marguerite\u2019s relationships with anyone. It\u2019s probably just the other girl\u2019s personality, but it does become a little intimidating sometimes if anything negative about her paramour comes up. At all. In any way. If Julia could tone down the level of fanatical love for Marguerite then it might be easier to make a case to the Courts of Love. Or anyone else for that matter.<br /> <br /> Hopefully some progress will be made for Marguerite so that she can return home without fear of reprisal. Insincere Marguerite is certainly not an ordinary girl, but she is a good one. I trust her with my secrets and with my life, and that is not something I can say of most people. I only hope that Charlotte is able to make some headway with the Parisian Courts and convince them to reconsider their opinion of Marguerite. I don\u2019t know what good I can do, but I will support my motley mate as best I can.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Halloween. The word just brings to mind images of goblins and ghosts and monsters. And candy. I myself am looking forward to helping the Autumn court with their Haunted Trail this year. I have never done anything like it and am keen on seeing what I can do to scare the locals. Sounds bad I suppose, but it\u2019s all in good fun. The kids have fun and they get candy at the end. I always used to enjoy this American tradition when I moved here. I am looking forward to it again\u2026<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> <u><u>Highsummer \u201914 Observations</u></u> con\u2019t<br /> <br /> -Remaining martial events included a Knife throwing demonstration (Calamity and Jacob threw knives at each other) and an Archery Contest. None of us were in the Archery Contest. Percival, Hailey, Shi, Ji Wen Ja, and Felicity participated. Percival and Felicity easily made it to the end. Felicity, with her bow of sunlight, easily beat Percival for the big win, and clearly enraged the Summer Court. Proudly.<br /> <br /> I cannot wait to corrupt her into the Night Court. For she is so high, her fall will be so hard, but what crawls out of the hole will be worth keeping. Deliciously.<br /> <br /> -Finally, Captain Jack and Gawain\u2019s jest. With help from Calamity, Ginny Green, and Wenceslas, the fight turned into a battle royale of Gawain\u2019s and Captain Jacks, eventually becoming a muddy fight.<br /> <br /> Also Captain Jack arrived on an elephant. It did not poop while there. Fortunately.<br /> <br /> -Lori\u2019s Midsummer Night\u2019s Dream play went well. She was pleased. I kissed her first, for luck. Not that she needed it. Naturally. Chalcedony was part of the play, but seemed hurt. Was she really stabbed by Molly? She waved me off but still seemed stiff. I hope she okay. Definitely.<br /> <br /> -The Handmaidens showed up, and pestered people. Someone should do something about them.<br /> <br /> -Eventually, White Maria, Julia, and I retired. Blissfully.<br /> <br /> <br /> o o o o o o o o o o o<br /> <br /> I have not written a journal in some time, but today was important. It was Calamity\u2019s Birthday, which is important as my Darkling Sister is very valuable to me. Certainly.<br /> <br /> The day began simply enough with a trip to the American movie Guardians of the Galaxy. It was a bit like Flash Gordon, the Space Jam of Football. I\u2019m sorry Calamity, but that is just the way it is. Definitely.<br /> <br /> We got back, and various people leapt out to cheer on Calamity, including Joan and Andromeda, but also Becky and Dahlia. Just the women I wanted to speak to. I confronted them quickly about socially backstabbing me. I insisted if they wished to accuse me of something they should do so, and not tip-toe around it. Harshly.<br /> <br /> Dahlia said little, beyond that she understood why I felt that way. Becky was, surprisingly, more open to listening. I offered to have Lori and De La Rocha talk to them. They did so. I just went ahead and conceded that Julia would not make me look good. In the end, Dahlia\u2026acquiesced, and Becky promised to stop talking about me in that manner, though she said it was \u201cnot her place\u201d to correct anyone else. Unfortunately.<br /> <br /> Julia approached Charlotte about talking to the Courts of Love. For me. Too much was going on I felt addled, emotional. I pulled Lori to the side. I told her I loved her, words that come far easier when speaking to her or Julia. I told her just as I had with Julia, I would be fine to make a private vow of affection and loyalty, or do it with the group\u2026or wait, years if necessary. I don\u2019t foresee our relationship coming to a close. At least, I dearly hope not. I love Lori. Deeply.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m\u2026struggling a bit. No matter how many women look adoringly at me, sometimes I think I will wake up and my father will tell me he has picked out who I should marry. He said he probably wouldn\u2019t but\u2026even surrounded, sometimes I am weak Marguerite DeLisle. Some Changelings fear discovering they are still in Arcadia. I fear discovering I was never taken at all.<br /> <br /> So on a more pleasant note American cartoons occasionally postulate that if the characters don\u2019t know how physics or some other aspect of reality works, it won\u2019t impede them and their lack of understanding can essentially be a weapon. While this of course explains American politics and environmental policy, sometimes I wonder if Flores cannot harness that and make it actually work for her.<br /> <br /> Flores, with aplomb, marched up and out of hand, talked both Oleander and De La Rocha into a bed. Our bed. With all of us. Lori had been trying to keep them (socially) satisfied, and somehow she just walked up and talked them into it. With a bright smile. I wish I could do that. Regularly.<br /> <br /> I should get her to do something with Felicity and Julia. Quickly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>End Session XLIV</i><br /> <br /> De la Rocha wants you to know she does not giggle. Chortles, at absolute worst.<br /> <br /> Lori had a smaller die pool for her expression roll for the play, but of course, she killed it.<br /> <br /> The \u201cIs Flash Gordon the Space Jam of Football\u201d conversation totally happened. It was surreal, if partially my fault.<br /> <br /> So next week, on our \u201coff week\u201d will be downtime journals and info. Right now I have a short story for Insincere Marguerite and a short thing I wrote for Lori\u2019s player about how stuff is going with her girlfriends. May see more, may not.<br /> <br /> Regardless, Comments and Questions are welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 12-08-2015, 04:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T02:26:42-08:00","id":784612,"title":"","content":"We have a couple months of downtime, so I wanted to provide two things here on the \u201coff week\u201d for folks who want a glimpse into what the Motley has been up to. One is a short story from Insincere Marguerite, which gives more insights into her character. The other is a short list I gave Lori\u2019s player of what has been up with her ladies that I will give folks a glimpse of. Enjoy<br /> <br /> <i>Downtime</i><br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> <b>\u2018Tis Autumn</b><br /> <br /> From her perch on top of the house, Marguerite Madeleine DeLisle could see the ocean.<br /> <br /> The trees were turning red and gold, and the wind was a little cooler. As a little girl, Marguerite had loved the colors of autumn, and hated the cold. She loved having bare feet; to squish the mud between her toes, to pick up sticks with her foot, to splash them in the water and not get her socks wet, it felt like freedom. Sure, her parents scolded her, but sometimes she would put on her skirt and slip her shoes off when her parents could not see her feet, then she would laugh if caught with little bare feet away from the house.<br /> <br /> Of course, when autumn came in Paris it would get cold, and with the cold came the time it was too cold to have bare feet. That time rarely seemed to come in California. She did very much like this about her new home, she decided. So much better than Montreal, which was worse than Paris. She flexed her toes, as her feet dangled off the roof.<br /> <br /> The moon cast a silvery light down on her as her mindscape changed. Marguerite Madeleine DeLisle remembered how the night had scared her as a child. Fear monsters would bite her feet. She was taught the day was the time good people were out. Good people like her family. Pure people. Strong people. Honorable people. Wealthy, blessed by God people. Marguerite Madeleine DeLisle never doubted.<br /> <br /> Then she was taken. Marguerite looked at the moon as she remembered, then cast her vision down to the Pacific Coast Highway, below and away. When she returned she discovered her family\u2019s purity, righteousness, and blessing from God was a lie. No! Worse, it was <i>true</i>. Marguerite discovered her family\u2019s vaunted purity was no virtue. They used it to prove they were better than others. Even as she had mingled her flesh with other \u201cpure\u201d white women, so too she had done so with women whose blood was mixed with blood of the native peoples, women like De La Rocha or Flores. Purity was bad. Her family\u2019s honor let them lie and cheat minorities and claim things from poorer people. Businesses, and people, were crushed to protect their honor. Honor was bad. They were the most high, shining in the sunlight. Marguerite Madeleine DeLisle had been one of them, but Marguerite Madeleine DeLisle was no more.<br /> <br /> What emerged from the Hedge was something else entirely. In time, she would align herself with the Night Court. While all the noble things her family held high were despicable goodness, the twisted Night Court, reveling in the disgust of others, cast aside aspirations of beauty, honor or purity. This was the Court of Insincere Marguerite. It was here she learned proper dress, proper respect, proper manner, all the things her family had vaunted, were bad. Here, she could be the monster she always held deep inside.<br /> <br /> Here, she did not need to wear shoes.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite looked down at her feet and flexed her toes again.<br /> <br /> Once it was all so easy. The family, honor, purity, the church good. Ugliness, lesser races, the poor, non-French, bad. Then she reversed it, with all the hideousness, depravity, and insincerity as her bread and butter. Sure, she was a refined monster, but a monster none the less.<br /> <br /> She was less sure where she stood now. Dark things like the Handmaidens crept across the night, and the costs of her peccadilloes were sometimes surprisingly high. On some level, that scared little girl afraid something would grab her pretty feet in the darkness stirred behind Insincere Marguerite\u2019s eyes. She was in control. She <i>had to</i> be in control. When control was left to others, they manipulated her to do good, which she discovered to be far worse than evil. She was in control. This was her house. These were her friends and her women. Just as in Arcadia she could take what she wanted. She would never give up control. But was she using it correctly?<br /> <br /> \u201cBon-Bon?\u201d<br /> <br /> It was Julia, looking up out of the window. \u201cMay I join you?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCertainly,\u201d said the grub, and one pale hand then the other found their way to the rooftop as Julia pulled herself up. Her Darkling gifts allowed it even in her skirt and petticoats, Insincere Marguerite noticed. In the moonlight, Julia Oldacre\u2019s skin was almost translucent, almost luminous in its pallor. Pale is ugly, the color of death, and Insincere Marguerite loved it.<br /> <br /> Julia sat down next to Insincere Marguerite. \u201cCentime for your thoughts, lover?\u201d she offered.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite smiled. \u201cI was just considering my past. So much before we met seems so distant now.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLess important?\u201d Julia volunteered, hopefully. \u201cHow do you mean?\u201d her lover asked.<br /> <br /> Julia took a deep breath, \u201cBon-Bon, you are a haunted woman. Haunted by the person you once were, and will never be again. But you\u2019re the opposite of Calamity, you are better, happier now. Don\u2019t let that former you hold you back.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd reclaim my name, I suspect you are hoping.\u201d Insincere Marguerite smiled impishly.<br /> <br /> \u201cOui,\u201d Julia smiled. \u201cUm, Bon-Bon, while it is all okay with me either way\u2026you are my Bon-Bon to me, I\u2026do you want to keep being called Insincere Marguerite? I mean, it does give people the wrong idea, and I don\u2019t think you need to rebel against that long dead girl anymore\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite slowly turned to look at Julia, then slowly looked back out over the ocean. There were several seconds of silence before she spoke. To Julia, it felt like an eternity.<br /> <br /> \u201cYes, yes I do Julia.\u201d<br /> <br /> Julia waited, but there was no explanation coming. \u201cO-Okay Bon-Bon, I will honor whatever you-\u201c<br /> <br /> \u201cJulia, do you want to be freed from your Pledge? Free to do whatever you wish with your life?\u201d Insincere Marguerite asked suddenly. Emotionlessly. Sharply.<br /> <br /> \u201cNO!\u201d Julia stood and shouted. Insincere Marguerite regarded her passively. \u201cAre you breaking up with me?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo,\u201d Insincere Marguerite said simply.\u201d I was not asking if you wanted to end our relationship. I presume the answer is no. I was asking if you wanted to no longer belong to me, for me to cease to be your Keeper now.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou are NOT my Keeper, Bon-Bon. That\u2019s a Gentry thing. You are my committed girlfriend, my soulmate, and my life partner, but not my Keeper.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAs you say,\u201d Insincere Marguerite turned and looked back at the ocean. \u2018Why did you ask me about my name?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2026your\u2026you are changing, Bon-Bon. Ever since Calamity\u2019s party. You are a kinder person now.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s why I asked my question, my dear, but why did you ask yours?\u201d Insincere Marguerite threw Julia a sidelong glance.<br /> <br /> \u201cI didn\u2019t know how much you were reinventing yourself,\u201d Julia started carefully.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd you were afraid,\u201d her lover finished, \u201cOf a question like I asked you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBon-Bon\u2026\u201d Julia\u2019s voice cracked a little.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite turned her whole body to face her, pulling her feet up from the side of the roof. \u201cYou know you are part of why that is, don\u2019t you? In my life, not just now, you are wholly unique. No one else has been my partner. I am\u2026unused to partners, and one oathed to obey me is not\u2026\u201d the Darkling shook her head, \u201cWhatever makes you happy, Julia.<br /> <br /> \u201cI am happy, my love.\u201d Julia smiled brightly.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite pulled Julia closer and smiled, \u201cBon. Then in keeping with my end of the Pledge, I will do by best to keep you that way.\u201d<br /> <br /> Julia breathed a sigh of relief and sat down. \u201cBon!\u201d she said, and smiled. Looking out at the trees, she smiled again, holding her love\u2019s hand.<br /> <br /> \u201cI love autumn. Obvious for an Autumn Courtier, I suppose,\u201d She said with a giggle.<br /> <br /> \u201cI as well,\u201d agreed her lady. \u201cEspecially now that it is not so bad for my feet.\u201d<br /> <br /> Julia nodded, then paused. \u201cWait\u2026what?\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Notes for Lori\u2019s Player<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>De La Rocha</b>: So over the months, Maria has been at war with herself. She wants to move in with Lorelei. She only goes to her apartment around once a week to be sure nothing is stolen, and to throw out now spoiled food that she never ate being never there. She feels very secure in the dream house and in her romance with Lori.<br /> <br /> But, the apartment is the symbol of freedom from Spidertoes. Getting it, buying furniture, decorating it herself, even if a lot was old punk venue posters and stuff she calls &quot;hilariously ethnic&quot; meant she was her own person. This is\u2026damaging that feeling of independence, at a time when Spidertoes is flirting with her again. Her mind reels...did she...ever escape Spidertoes?<br /> <br /> But now she is firm. It is time to move on. She pushes the dark thoughts away, even as she wonders if seeing Spidertoes flirt with her sped up her desire to leave her apartment behind. But she is moving in with Lori, and the immediate thing is her &quot;OMG COMMITMENT&quot; problem then the fact she might be backing into a web. Due to the aforementioned problem, she is forestalling responding to Julia's request (but only forestalling, if nothing else she does not want to anger Julia, nor close that door forever.<br /> <br /> And oh god going to church. That will seal it, won't it. OMGOMGOMG<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Insincere Marguerite:</b> You know most of this. Insincere Marguerite's rejecting of the trappings and outward behaviors of good for evil while believing herself good are fraying just a little, even as her sense of being in control slips. She watches Felicity with unabashed hunger. But she clings to Lori. Lori is not the only thing keeping her together, Insincere Marguerite is a willful creature. But she helps. She has indirectly referenced that her &quot;acquiring&quot; Felicity would be bad in a moment of weakness alone with Lori, even as she usually claims she will have Felicity in the Night Court as her personal mistress by June. Lori has some idea her need for control stems from her own feelings of helplessness, fighting being a future housewife and baby factory with her being a dominant lesbian. And Lori knows sometimes she wonders if even that is what she really is.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite has also worked on teaching Lori French.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Julia</b>: Julia is mildly annoyed her girlfriends are not jumping on the group oathbinding. She is less worried about Insincere Marguerite, who is pledged to take care of her, and her insecurities about if Lori and Maria really love her are strong. She is less worried about Flores or White Maria. Otherwise she is quite okay and rather cheerful. Though she sees the hunger in Insincere Marguerite's eyes as she looks at Felicity, and fondles the carving knife in her bag.<br /> <br /> Julia is willing to go to church with Lori, though she would not push it or anything.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Oleander</b>: Oleander is also doing well. Imelda Gonzales (as she was named when born, and has no desire to be called) is quite happy with her relationship with Lori. She has continued to get along with De La Rocha right up until the announcement DLR would be moving into the Dream House, at which point she vanished (non-suspiciously) for about a week, and has been distant with DLR since. She and Julia had begun flirting, but this made her less comfortable flirting with DLR's other girlfriends so she has largely stopped. Otherwise she seems fine.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Flores</b>: Flores is okay are you okay? Need a hot coca? It is getting cooler. Sex maybe? A backrub?<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <i>End Downtime</i><br /> <br /> Journals return next week. It is October 30th, and all is not well. Join us then. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T14:49:49-08:00","id":789932,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s been a couple months, and Autumn has arrived. The leaves turn gold, and the anger in the air gives way to fear. The warm, breezy Lady by the Sea welcomes her new ruler, and everyone gets ready for the Masquerade. Everyone but Madam Spidertoes, who has found something that troubles her.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XLV</i><br /> <b><br /> Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> October 30th, evening<br /> <br /> To start off with the usual, these days: still no sign of Greg Andrews. Chalcedony still doesn\u2019t have time to deal with the trigger. Things with Felicity and Princess Joli are heating up, but no more, you know, overt moves against Felicity have been made. Things have started to get \u2018interesting\u2019 again though. I\u2019d like to say I wasn\u2019t looking forward to it - that I could live contentedly as a craftsman for the rest of my days. But the idea of defeating a Hedgebeast that is guarding a threat to my freehold has a feeling of rightness to it that I can\u2019t shake. But I\u2019m getting ahead of myself.<br /> <br /> We spent most of the day moving De la Roche in. She\u2019d been planning on getting a moving van, but after we all showed up with vehicles, we figured we could, you know, make do. She was a little antsy about it but it did make the most sense, especially if, like she said, she only ever came back to it to throw away expired milk. It was a fun time anyway.<br /> <br /> The show was awesome. Calamity did her bit, you know, the Stuck in the Middle with You thing and it went great. The poor audience member was terrified. Something after that started setting the girls off though. I think I figured out why De la Roche stormed off to the basement - she felt left out when Madame Spidertoes wanted to talk with all the darklings but her. That got cleared up when Calamity pointed out that \u201call the darklings but her\u201d was the same group as \u201call the Autumn and honorary Autumn Courtiers\u201d. I still dunno why Julia started shoving Insincere Marguerite though.<br /> <br /> In addition to pointing out about the Autumn Courtiers thing, Calamity filled us in on what Madame Spidertoes told them. It turns out Tommy had figured out that the Hollywood Courts had a base full of human spies and a Hedgebeast in an old shut down strip club called Foxy Boxes in a sketchy part of town. Madame Spidertoes wanted us to take care of it and recover their computer, all while being super secret about it. Insincere Marguerite and Calamity had different ideas about \u2018taking care of it\u2019 since Insincere Marguerite was all about the sleepy cloth and Calamity was all about taking no prisoners and sending a message. It got a little, you know, tense. I can\u2019t say I approve of Calamity\u2019s plans myself either, honestly. But I didn\u2019t say much then - she was getting plenty of heat from Lori and Insincere Marguerite. And we\u2019re gonna take this slow, so there\u2019ll be plenty of time for a plan that doesn\u2019t involve, you know, a slaughter. Tomorrow is Halloween, and the Masquerade Ball, so I think the plan is for some recon the day after. But for now, it\u2019s tabled, except for Calamity talking with Dahlia now. Her pledge says she has to, so she is, but with as few details as possible. Dahlia seems, you know, reasonable, so hopefully that will fly.<br /> <br /> October 31st, afternoon<br /> <br /> Well, we\u2019re just about to head out for the Masquerade Ball and things have gotten even more interesting already. Jacob and Insincere Marguerite got summoned by Boss Lowjack during breakfast. They came back fairly quickly - it was a short conversations apparently. Just, you know, kinda disturbing.<br /> <br /> So, the Handmaidens visited Tamara again last night, and very nearly killed her. Two Spring Courtiers were keeping her stabilized. So Boss Lowjack made a promise, that if any Winter Courtiers were killed, a Night Courier would die. Starting with Willow, but the implication was strongly made that Insincere Marguerite was next in line. I can't fault his depth of feeling, even if I don\u2019t like Insincere Marguerite being threatened. I mostly wish the Handmaidens weren\u2019t immune to the consequences of their actions. Politics suck sometimes, you know?<br /> <br /> Boss Lowjack did also warn Insincere Marguerite that since Willow and Olivia had come here to set up Courts they would rule, the fact that should the Day and Night Courts get setup, Felicity and Insincere Marguerite would, you know, be the Monarchs meant that they had motives for foul play. He didn\u2019t think Willow would move against Insincere Marguerite herself, but thought Insincere Marguerite should know. And it struck enough of a nerve that Willow raised a hand against Boss Lowjack. That got her a gun to the head, courtesy of Molly Nuit. So... excitement.<br /> <br /> On a more fun exciting note, the Masquerade Ball got way more intriguing as of this afternoon. De la Roche let us know that Joan and Andromeda would both be there, heavily disguised, to have, you know, a last fling kinda thing. De la Roche told me and Lori what Joan\u2019s disguise would be, after I gave her a backrub and Lori gave her sexy promises. She\u2019s gonna be dressed up in a silver space-y outfit, with a big boxy helmet and a hologram of a different woman\u2019s face on it.<br /> <br /> Joan is very smart, passionate, pretty and awesome with a sword - I gotta at least, you know, take a shot. Calamity\u2019s definitely all about it. She\u2019d been wanting to scratch that S&amp;M itch and was worried I\u2019d be lonely, you know? I\u2019m at least gonna give it a try - can\u2019t hurt, right?<br /> <br /> Everybody looks awesome. A few of us are wearing the raiment I\u2019ve made these past few months - Jacob with his ice armor, Insincere Marguerite with her savannah shadowed lion dress and my shadow dappled armor. The others are more of a, you know, Halloween-y kinda dressed up. Calamity is dressed up as a droog from Clockwork Orange and her outfit looks, you know, perfect. Luna is dressed up like Lara Croft, which looks awesome on her. Lori is going as Death from the Sandman comics. She even dyed her hair black! Julie\u2019s noble outfit and mismatched eyes, and De la Roche\u2019s (non sexy) nun\u2019s habit round out our group.<br /> <br /> Time to go have fun.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Time marches on, and Summer fades to Autumn, and yet for some reason I\u2019m still pissed at the state of the world\u2026 although I suppose if I\u2019m being entirely honest with myself, I\u2019m mostly angry because I\u2019m afraid. So I guess that makes sense in a way.<br /> <br /> Until very recently, things in the Freehold had been pretty quiet. D started making vague noises a couple of weeks ago about getting rid of her apartment. She was still clinging to it as a sign of her independence, though even she had to admit that she really only stopped by there once or twice a week to make sure that nothing had been stolen and to throw out the expired milk. It made no sense for her to keep paying rent on a place she hardly ever used.<br /> <br /> Of course I told her that she would be welcome to move in with me full time at the Dream House. She\u2019s a member of the motley now, after all, and it only seems right that she should cohabitate with the rest of us (officially, I mean). She was kind of weird about it for a while, but that\u2019s understandable. That apartment was <u>her</u> place\u2026 the first place of her own she had after her break-up with Madame Spidertoes. It was a symbol of her self-reliance, a symbol that she was out from under the heel of her ex. And now she\u2019s giving it up to move in with another girlfriend, and there\u2019s a part of her spirit that rails against that sort of thing, even as most of her is (I think) quite happy with the idea.<br /> <br /> Aside from D\u2019s nerves, the only real downside to this situation is that it\u2019s upset Oleander, and she and D are no longer getting along as well as they had been. Things were awkward but cool in the wake of our shared experience following Calamity\u2019s birthday party, but the tension has been building again since D announced that she was moving in. Dammit! I wish there was some way I could make each of them happy without upsetting the other.<br /> <br /> Oh, I almost forgot! Oleander told me her real name the other day! Well, the name she was born with in any case. It\u2019s Imelda Gonzalez, which I think is beautiful. She really doesn\u2019t like the name, though, so she\u2019ll still be my Oleander in the pages of this diary.<br /> <br /> In any case, D had intended to rent a truck to move her stuff over to the Dream House, but between us all we had more than enough vehicles to make that unnecessary. Well, okay\u2026 I didn\u2019t actually offer up the \u2018vette as a transport. Let\u2019s face it; my car has trunk space roughly equivalent to the interior of a fashionable handbag. But between the others\u2019 cars and Gawain\u2019s van, we managed to get everything packed up and moved in a single trip. D hung out in the apartment for a few minutes after everyone else left. I stayed with her, but I waited outside so that she could say goodbye to her place in private.<br /> <br /> This was all on the day before Halloween, by the way\u2026 yesterday as I write this. We had a show that night, but had cancelled the following evening\u2019s entertainment so that we could all attend the Autumn Court\u2019s Halloween Masquerade. From my point of view, things started to go south during the show, though I suppose the seeds of the snafu had been in place for some time already before I noticed their effects.<br /> <br /> I strutted out onto the stage to perform, and noted with only a slight pang of jealousy that D was seated at a table near the back having a conversation with Madame Spidertoes. I tried my best to put it out of my mind as I husked my way through Cole Porter\u2019s \u201cEv\u2019ry Time We Say Goodbye\u201d (taking my cues from the inimitable Ella Fitzgerald\u2019s version), but when I glanced back after taking my bows, both Spidertoes and D were gone. I felt a trickle of ice water run down my spine as I hurried off the stage to look for my love, yielding the floor to Calamity\u2019s Tarantino-inspired \u201cStuck In the Middle With You\u201d dance routine.<br /> <br /> I trust D. I do. That\u2019s why I checked the basement first, rather than heading for the bedrooms upstairs or the parking lot. I could tell as I rushed down the stairs that my first guess had been correct\u2026 I could hear the unmistakable sounds of D taking out her frustrations on a punching bag. Though of course I was worried about her, I confess I allowed myself a small sigh of relief before I approached her.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat\u2019s wrong, honey?\u201d I asked quietly after a moment or two.<br /> <br /> She didn\u2019t look at me. \u201cNothing,\u201d she said in a surly voice as she threw a vicious punch at the poor bag.<br /> <br /> \u201cD,\u201d I said gently, placing a hand on her shoulder, \u201cplease give me a little more credit than that. Something\u2019s obviously bothering you. Let me help.\u201d<br /> <br /> She turned to face me then, and her eyes were shimmering. \u201cSpidertoes,\u201d she rasped softly, \u201cshe\u2019s meeting with Insincere Marguerite, and Julia, and Calamity. She actually sent me to <u>fetch</u> them. But she didn\u2019t want to talk to me at all. I\u2019m the only darkling in the Dream House she didn\u2019t want to talk to. I\u2019m not good enough for her anymore.\u201d<br /> <br /> My throat tightened to the point that it was actually a little hard for me to breathe. \u201cI\u2019m sure that\u2019s not it, sweetie,\u201d I said softly, pulling her toward me. To my alarm, she jerked out of my grasp.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ve put on weight lately,\u201d she said with an almost manic gleam in her eye.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou have not!\u201d I protested, considering myself the current foremost authority on D\u2019s body.<br /> <br /> \u201cI have,\u201d she shot back angrily. \u201cI\u2019m eight pounds heavier than I was. My muscle tone and definition haven\u2019t changed. I\u2019m fat and disgusting and\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> There were tears in her eyes. That was the last straw as far as I was concerned. She\u2019s the strongest person I know. I\u2019ve seen her vulnerable before, when she\u2019s opened up to me about her Durance and about her family\u2026 but those tears were for <u>me</u>. Spidertoes has no right to make my love feel that way. She gave up her claim long ago, and I\u2019ll be damned if I\u2019m going to give it back for anything.<br /> <br /> I threw a punch of my own that set the bag swinging. I\u2019ve rarely been that angry, and D had to catch the bag before it swung back and hit me. \u201cCut that shit out right now,\u201d I said sharply. \u201cShe\u2019s fucking with you, D. She knows that she has this power over you, and she\u2019s exercising it, making you dance to her tune. You don\u2019t have to put up with it. You\u2019re Maria de la Rocha, dammit! You are beautiful, and strong, and you don\u2019t give a damn what anyone else thinks. She\u2019s just checking to see if she can still control you now that you have me.\u201d<br /> <br /> A single tear spilled from each of her beautiful eyes, but she sniffed and nodded. \u201cI don\u2019t <u>want</u> things to be this way, Lori,\u201d she said quietly. \u201cYou know I love you\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know,\u201d I said, pulling her toward me, \u201cand I hate myself a little for what I\u2019m about to say. I don\u2019t usually think like this, and it makes me kind of sick to my stomach, so I\u2019m only going to say this once.\u201d<br /> <br /> I leaned in and hissed into her ear. \u201cYou\u2019re <u>mine</u> now, Maria. Nobody else can have you\u2026 least of all her.\u201d<br /> <br /> And there it was. Everything I hated about Arcadia\u2026 about the Empress, boiled down into a single moment of fear and jealousy. I swore that I would never treat <u>anyone</u> as property, that I would never make that sort of a claim, that I would never subject anyone to the same sort of Hell I had been through. And there I was, so damned scared of losing her that I was doing it to the person I love most in the world.<br /> <br /> She nodded at me and pulled me into a fierce embrace\u2026 probably so that I wouldn\u2019t see the brief flash of fear in her eyes. Tough, in-your-face, kick-ass D, afraid of <u>me</u>. Yeah, I\u2019ve got a lot to be proud of, don\u2019t I?<br /> <br /> I tried to salvage the situation. \u201cAnd I\u2019m <u>yours</u>, D. Never forget that.\u201d Yeah, it was a pretty weak save, I admit, but it was the best I could do at the time.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sorry,\u201d she said after a while. \u201cI don\u2019t mean to make you feel bad, Lori. You\u2019re my world, you know that. It\u2019s just\u2026 I spent so long trying to earn her approval. It\u2019s hard to get past that. I feel so rejected.\u201d<br /> <br /> I clung to my love like a life preserver. \u201cYou realize it\u2019s probably nothing, right? Julia and Calamity are both Autumn Court, just like Spidertoes. And Marguerite is in pretty tight with them, too. It\u2019s probably court business or something.\u201d<br /> <br /> Her eyes lit up at the suggestion, and a vicious little part of me hated that. \u201cYou really think that\u2019s it?\u201d she asked eagerly.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sure it is,\u201d I reassured her as best I could, given my own inner turmoil. \u201cNow come on, let\u2019s get back upstairs. Maybe we can get one of the others to tell us what\u2019s going on.\u201d<br /> <br /> D agreed, and we made it back upstairs just as things were wrapping up for the evening. We did a little of the mingling thing, though both of us were obviously a little red-faced and upset, and I\u2019m sure a lot of the regulars picked up on that. We managed to catch up with the darklings as they were saying their goodbyes to Madame Spidertoes.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, Lorelei my dear,\u201d she said as we approached, \u201cyou were as lovely and enchanting as always this evening.\u201d When I know for a fact that she couldn\u2019t have seen more than a few seconds of my act! Can you believe it? \u201cI wonder if I might impose upon you to allow your charming companion to escort me to my vehicle?\u201d<br /> <br /> The look of hope in D\u2019s eyes almost broke my heart. Still, after everything, she was fawning after Spidertoes, trying to win her approval. I thought nothing could compare to the place I had in her heart, but I don\u2019t have that sort of power over her. I don\u2019t <u>want</u> it, of course, but it\u2019s not nice to realize that the person you love more than anything in the world has stronger feelings for someone else.<br /> <br /> Oh my God\u2026 is this how D and Oleander feel sometimes? But no\u2026 D has always known I\u2019m polyamorous, and Oleander and I talked about the situation before we even started dating. I\u2019m sure there\u2019s no real comparison.<br /> <br /> In any case, with all of those thoughts rushing through my head, I confess that I was out of sorts and not in the mood to deal with Spidertoes\u2019 mind games. \u201cD can make her own decisions,\u201d I said waspishly.<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course,\u201d Spidertoes replied silkily. Was that a knowing look in her eye? Was she enjoying my discomfort? I\u2019m pretty sure she was. \u201cHowever, it would be unaccountably rude of me to deprive you of your paramour without first asking for your leave. You do not object?\u201d<br /> <br /> I tried to keep my gaze level as I responded. \u201cI trust D,\u201d I said evenly.<br /> <br /> D tried to salvage the conversation. \u201cMaybe, to avoid any\u2026 uhh\u2026 impropriety, Julia should come along with us as a chaperone?\u201d she said, throwing Julia a pleading glance. Julia readily agreed to these terms, and the three of them made their way to the exit together.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat the hell is going on?\u201d I asked the others angrily. Marguerite gave me a disdainful look, but didn\u2019t respond. I chalked her attitude up to ill humor over Julia\u2019s earlier behavior. When the other girl found her staring moon-eyed at Chalcedony \u2013 <u>again</u> \u2013 she decided that she wasn\u2019t going to take it anymore, and pushed Marguerite over. Marguerite still claims that there\u2019s nothing between her and Chalcedony, but really\u2026 when was the last time <u>anyone</u> was able to sneak up on her? She says that she recognized the sound of Julia\u2019s footsteps and didn\u2019t react because she trusts the other girl, but, well\u2026 I\u2019ve seen Marguerite fixated on girls before, but I\u2019ve <u>never</u> seen her act like she does around Chalcedony.<br /> <br /> Marguerite and Calamity opted to keep tight-lipped about their little secret club meeting until everyone was gathered so they wouldn\u2019t have to go over everything twice. Once D and Julia came back \u2013 both looking somewhat happier than necessary, in my opinion \u2013 Calamity spilled the beans. Spidertoes thinks she\u2019s uncovered a secret base for the Hollywood Courts. They\u2019ve been spying on the Freehold, and she doesn\u2019t think that should continue. Okay, in all fairness, she\u2019s probably <u>right</u> about that. Rather than bring this matter up with the monarchs, however, she\u2019s opted to let our motley know, and has offered a few helpful suggestions as to how we might want to deal with the situation.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t like it. Yes, part of the reason that I don\u2019t like it is that the information is coming from Spidertoes, who is not my favorite person in the world right now, but that\u2019s not all of it. She says they have a lot of enchanted human servants working in this closed-down old strip club (\u201cFoxy Boxes?\u201d Really?), and at least one Hedge beast seems to lair up there as well. She wants the Hedge beast destroyed, but is leaving the fate of the human spies to our discretion. Oh, and she wants us to retrieve the club\u2019s computer so that we can see how much the Hollywood Courts know.<br /> <br /> Calamity was very gung-ho. She wants to head in there guns a-blazin\u2019 and kill them all, \u201cto send a message,\u201d as she puts it. I hope it goes without saying that I was against this plan, and most of the motley came down on my side. Marguerite was all for using chloroform, her \u201csleeping cloth,\u201d to take down the human servants non-lethally. Since Spidertoes wants this done stealthily, I figured I\u2019d be useless during the actual infiltration. I pretty much left the \u201cways and means\u201d discussion to the others, but promised to be nearby should any of my friends need healing.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou okay, Lori?\u201d D asked softly as the debate raged on. She put a hand on my shoulder and I sort of shrugged it off.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo,\u201d I admitted, \u201cI don\u2019t like anything about this mission. This sort of thing isn\u2019t what I signed up for when I joined the Spring Court, and it\u2019s not what I agreed to when I joined this motley. I\u2019ll help however I can, I promise\u2026 but I don\u2019t have to like it.\u201d D looked a little stricken to hear me say that.<br /> <br /> I stood up and stretched. \u201cI\u2019m going upstairs to change,\u201d I announced to the motley, \u201cand then I think I\u2019ll head down to the basement to work out for a while. I feel like punching the bag for an hour or two.\u201d<br /> <br /> As I walked away, I heard D smack her own forehead and mutter \u201cI am such a fucking idiot.\u201d<br /> <br /> So yeah, I got upstairs, somehow managed to get my dress off without ripping it, and put on a pair of bike pants and a sports bra. As I was taping up my knuckles (I have picked up a <u>few</u> things from working out with D and Monica so often over the summer), I noticed that my palms were bleeding. I\u2019d been clenching my fists so hard during my conversation with Spidertoes that I\u2019d driven my nails into my own flesh. I hadn\u2019t even noticed.<br /> <br /> I punched the bag until sometime between three and four in the morning. D joined me down there at some point, but mostly braced the bag for me. We didn\u2019t talk much, except when she gently corrected my stance a few times, or gave suggestions on how to improve my power and aim. When I finally admitted that I was tired and started staggering toward my bathroom for a shower, D stopped me and pulled me into an embrace.<br /> <br /> \u201cStop,\u201d I said softly, without really meaning it, \u201cI\u2019m all sweaty.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ve seen you sweatier,\u201d she reminded me with a grin. Then she turned serious. \u201cAre we good, Lori?\u201d<br /> <br /> I returned her embrace. \u201cOf course we are,\u201d I said.<br /> <br /> \u201cGood,\u201d she replied. \u201cYou\u2019re my world, babe, and I\u2019m sorry if anything I said or did earlier made you feel like you weren\u2019t.\u201d She sniffed at me delicately, and wrinkled her nose in mock disgust. \u201cGet cleaned up, and let\u2019s hit the sack. We can talk about this more tomorrow if you want.\u201d<br /> <br /> So I woke up this morning \u2013 or, more accurately, this early afternoon \u2013 to the smell of coffee and breakfast, and the sounds of muted conversation from the kitchen. D was already down there, so I threw on some clothes and made my way down as well.<br /> <br /> \u201cCoffee,\u201d I slurred as I shambled into the room. Then I saw the looks on everyone\u2019s faces. \u201cWho died?\u201d I asked, a little dread tugging at my brain.<br /> <br /> \u201cNobody,\u201d Jacob said seriously, \u201cbut it was a very close thing. The Handmaidens of Night visited Tamara again last night. She barely survived this time.\u201d<br /> <br /> That woke me up. \u201cIs she okay? Does she need me to come by and help?\u201d I asked once I had found my voice.<br /> <br /> Jacob shook his head. \u201cShe has two members of your Court watching her. She is no longer in any real danger.\u201d<br /> <br /> I blinked, confused. \u201cSo why the long faces? I mean, I know it\u2019s horrible that she was hurt, and the Handmaidens will have to answer for it, but if she\u2019s going to be okay, why is everyone looking so serious?\u201d<br /> <br /> Marguerite fielded that answer. \u201cThe Handmaidens are important to the Warlock of Night,\u201d she explained. \u201cPunishing them directly would be politically\u2026 difficult. So Boss Lowjack has taken it upon himself to threaten two people who had nothing to do with this incident\u2026 Willow Black and myself.\u201d The bitterness in her voice was sobering.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh my God,\u201d I said, rushing to her. \u201cAre you okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOui,\u201d she said, and favored me with a little smile, \u201che only threatened. He says that if any members of his Court are killed by the Handmaidens, he will retaliate against the Night Court. He implied that Willow would be the first person targeted, and that I would be the second. He implied\u2026 other things as well.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> Marguerite shook her head, and Jacob took up the tale again. \u201cHe said that the Day and Night Courts have been trying to gain power in the Freehold. He said that they were trying to create crowns. Olivia Gold and Willow Black have been attempting this for some time. He also implied that if these crowns were to come into being\u2026 they would not go to those two, but to Felicity and Insincere Marguerite.\u201d<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t claim to understand how the whole Court and Royalty thing works, but I waved it aside as unimportant for the time being. \u201cSo you think he was just trying to pit you and Willow against each other?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cC\u2019est vrai,\u201d Marguerite nodded. \u201cHe spun some tale about Willow and Olivia being in league and seeking to eliminate Felicity and myself. I do not know quite what to think, but it seems likely that he was merely sowing the dissent.\u201d<br /> <br /> I moved closer to Marguerite and drew her into an embrace. \u201cI know it doesn\u2019t need to be said, but we won\u2019t let anything happen to you.\u201d She nodded happily and we left it at that.<br /> <br /> After that we kind of dispersed to get ready for the Masquerade. I\u2019d considered a lot of possibilities when building my costume for the evening. Gawain has been hard at work crafting new Hedge-spun outfits for many of us, and the feathered gown he made me is absolutely <u>gorgeous</u>. It\u2019s so pretty, in fact, that I decided I wanted to show it off at a function where the whole point <u>wasn\u2019t</u> in concealing one\u2019s true identity.<br /> <br /> (He also made me a leather doctor\u2019s bag, by the way. He says that he imbued Mothers\u2019 Kisses into the fabric of the bag, and that keeping my medical gear in it will give a boost to my admittedly meager first aid skills, so I\u2019ve taken to carrying it with me when I go out, just in case. I thanked him with a chaste kiss on the cheek when he gave it to me, of course, and solemnly avowed before the motley that I was through simply <u>playing</u> doctor. The stricken looks most of them gave me made me pause and take stock of what I had just said, and then I had to leave the room before the laughter started).<br /> <br /> In any case, my costume. So, after we performed <u>A Midsummer Night\u2019s Dream</u> at Highsummer, Julia approached me with a pile of books. \u201cYou like Shakespeare and comic books, right?\u201d she asked when I enquired about them. \u201cYou need to read these. I think you\u2019ll like them. One of the issues is about William Shakespeare performing that play for the first time in front of an audience of real fairies. That issue was the only comic book that ever won the World Fantasy Award.\u201d<br /> <br /> The series was called <u>The Sandman</u>, and Julia was right, I did like them. I liked them quite a lot, though they bore very little resemblance to the comics I remembered from my youth (apparently at some point in the mid-80s DC decided that the Comics Code was for pussies). The series was very dark, and each of the paperback collections bore the label \u201cfor mature audiences only\u201d on the cover for a very good reason. The main character is an anthropomorphic personification of the concept of fiction (or \u201cDream,\u201d as he calls himself), and I found his journey fascinating.<br /> <br /> His sister \u2013 I\u2019m given to believe one of the more popular characters of the series \u2013 is Death. She\u2019s usually portrayed as a pale hip young woman who prefers a Gothic style but is almost universally cheerful and upbeat. I thought it would be neat to dress as her for Halloween, and Julia concurred. \u201cBut you can\u2019t just wear black jeans and a tank-top,\u201d she complained when I explained my intentions. \u201cIt\u2019s a <u>ball</u>. We\u2019ll dress you up more formally.\u201d<br /> <br /> So we put together an ensemble that resembled the character when she\u2019s dressing for company, with a frilly, lacy black dress in a Neo-Victorian style, mesh stockings and fingerless gloves, and the ever-present ankh necklace. I layered on the white makeup, too. I\u2019m pretty pale for a California girl anyway, but I\u2019m nowhere near the lily-white majesty of that character\u2019s natural skin tone.<br /> <br /> Oh, and I let Julia dye my hair black. She assures me that it will wash out. It had better.<br /> <br /> Since this function is a masquerade ball, I capped the costume off with a small black domino mask, with Death\u2019s trademark curly-cue eye makeup mimicked on the mask in white. I\u2019m not actually trying to hide my identity tonight, so I\u2019m sure anyone who pays attention is going to know who I am almost instantly, but that\u2019s not really the point.<br /> <br /> I was chatting with Gawain about an hour before it was time to go when D hurried in, looking like the cat that ate the canary. I couldn\u2019t help myself; I had to ask her what was up.<br /> <br /> \u201cI just found out that Joan and Andromeda are coming to the Masquerade tonight, and they\u2019re looking to experiment a little,\u201d she said gleefully. \u201cThey\u2019re testing the boundaries a bit, and both of them are considering hooking up with other partners for the evening, just to see what it\u2019s like. And,\u201d here she grinned gleefully, \u201cI just spent an hour helping Joan get into her costume, so I know what she\u2019ll be wearing.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat?\u201d Gawain and I asked nearly simultaneously.<br /> <br /> \u201cUh-uh,\u201d she replied, still grinning. \u201cThat information is too good to go handing out for free. It\u2019ll cost you. What\u2019s it worth to you?\u201d<br /> <br /> Gawain thought for a minute. \u201cI could give you a backrub,\u201d he said with a smile.<br /> <br /> D quirked an eyebrow. \u201cThat had better be one hell of a backrub,\u201d she said. He demonstrated for a few minutes, and she sighed, her eyes rolling back into her head. \u201cOkay,\u201d she said eventually, \u201cthat\u2019s pretty damn good. But what am I bid from the lovely lady?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> I leaned forward and whispered softly in her ear. I won\u2019t repeat what I suggested even in the privacy of this diary. Let\u2019s just say that it was filthy, and it\u2019s something we haven\u2019t done before. D blushed, though she\u2019ll never admit it. \u201cThat\u2019s\u2026 quite an opening bid,\u201d she admitted. \u201cAre you bidding for exclusive rights, or do you care if I tell anyone else?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> I laughed. \u201cYou don\u2019t have to tell me anything, D, I\u2019d do that with you if you just asked,\u201d I admitted. \u201cGo ahead and tell us both, and may the best lover win!\u201d<br /> <br /> D nodded. \u201cJoan will be wearing a silver bodysuit, like something out of a sci-fi movie. Her mask will be a box like a TV, with a female face on the screen. The face won\u2019t be hers, of course, because that would sort of miss the point. It\u2019s pretty cool looking, actually.\u201d<br /> <br /> Gawain and I shook hands, a mock challenge in each of our eyes. I don\u2019t know if either of us will end up with Joan tonight, but it should be fun to try.<br /> <br /> If I decide to try, that is. \u201cCan I talk to you for a minute in private, sweetie?\u201d I asked softly as we left the theater.<br /> <br /> \u201cSure,\u201d she said, \u201cI need to start getting into my costume anyway, so why don\u2019t you join me in our bedroom.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo what\u2019s bothering you?\u201d she asked as she disrobed and pulled out the nun\u2019s habit she intended to wear to the ball.<br /> <br /> \u201cSorry about last night,\u201d I said softly, watching her as she dressed. \u201cYou know I\u2019m not a jealous person, Maria, but something about Spidertoes just <u>bothers</u> me where you\u2019re concerned.\u201d<br /> <br /> She gave me a look. \u201cI know the rule, Lori,\u201d she said. Mostly her tone was even and reassuring, but there was a hint of bitterness there as well. I had asked her a few weeks ago not to sleep with Spidertoes. I\u2019ve never asked her to restrain herself like that with anyone else, and I think the request sort of surprised her. D chafes when rules are in place, and if I\u2019d been thinking back then I never would have made the request.<br /> <br /> But then again, the first day we started dating she asked me not to sleep with Annika. And when Jolie asked me to be her consort, D sort of put her foot down against that, too. So I don\u2019t think she has the right to complain about my one little request, either.<br /> <br /> \u201cI know,\u201d I said, hoping she could see the love in my eyes. \u201cI love you, Maria, and I trust you. But I don\u2019t trust <u>her</u>.\u201d<br /> <br /> Maria turned away to straighten her wimple. \u201cShe hasn\u2019t asked me to sleep with her, Jules,\u201d she said. Maybe she was hoping that the affectionate nickname would soften her tone a little, I don\u2019t know. She started calling me that in private a week or so ago. No one has called me that since Missy and Jane, but it sounds right coming from her. \u201cShe hasn\u2019t made any sort of move on me.\u201d<br /> <br /> I sighed. \u201cShe loved you, D. At least a part of her still does. I\u2019m not saying anything against her. But I don\u2019t trust her, because\u2026\u201d I closed my eyes and turned away. \u201c\u2026because I know how far I would go to get you back if I ever lost you.\u201d<br /> <br /> D\u2019s arms circled my waist, and I felt her leaning up against my back. \u201cYou\u2019re not going to lose me, Jules,\u201d she whispered in my ear. \u201cI would never do anything to hurt you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI can\u2019t kiss you; it would ruin my makeup,\u201d I said with regret.<br /> <br /> She squeezed me tight, and then changed the subject. \u201cSo, are you going to go for Joan tonight?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t know,\u201d I said.<br /> <br /> She quirked an eyebrow. \u201cWhy not? I\u2019ve seen the way you look at her, Lori\u2026 ever since you first met her that night at the pier. And I\u2019ve seen the way she looks at you, though she\u2019s better at hiding it than you are. She\u2019s putting herself out there tonight, for the first time ever\u2026 you might not get another chance. Why not go for it?\u201d<br /> <br /> I shrugged. \u201cI\u2026 don\u2019t know if I\u2019m in the mood or not yet,\u201d I said lamely. \u201cLook, I\u2019m Spring Court. I\u2019m all about free love and shared experiences. I\u2019ve been looking forward to this night for months. But now that it\u2019s here, I find\u2026 well\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat is it?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFor the last twelve hours or so, I\u2019ve only really wanted to be with you, Maria,\u201d I said softly.<br /> <br /> She gave me one of those shy smiles that she saves just for me, and I felt everything rush away for a few minutes. \u201cThat\u2019s sweet,\u201d she said softly, \u201cand you know I\u2019m here for you if you need me, babe. But don\u2019t make up your mind until you see what the playing field looks like, okay? If you see someone you want tonight, go for it. That\u2019s what these functions are all about, right? I\u2019ll still be here in the morning.\u201d<br /> <br /> And she pinned a lily on my dress. That\u2019s part of the code of the function: wearing a flower indicates your interest in a certain type of romantic liaison. I\u2019m wearing a lily to show that I\u2019m comfortable having trysts with either sex. Strict heterosexuals will be wearing roses, gay men a green carnation, and lesbians a violet. It certainly seems like it will streamline the selection process, I must admit.<br /> <br /> I can\u2019t wait to see what the ball itself will be like. The costumes alone are likely to be amazing. From our group, Calamity probably put the most work into her costume. She\u2019s going as a \u201cdroog\u201d from <u>A Clockwork Orange</u> (yet another pop culture reference I actually get!). Gawain, Marguerite, and Jacob are all wearing their new Hedge-spun outfits. Gawain\u2019s outfit makes him look like he\u2019s standing in a sunlit wood, with green leaf-shadows moving constantly on his head and shoulders. Marguerite\u2019s dress is patterned like a lion stalking its prey on the African savannah (I was a little anxious at first that she\u2019s still emulating the leonine aspect of her Keeper, but, well\u2026 the dress really <u>is</u> beautiful). Jacob\u2019s armor looks like it\u2019s made from real arctic ice, and has this cool white-blue sheen on it. Julia is wearing a Victorian noble lady\u2019s dress, but she\u2019s using colored contact lenses to make one of her eyes red and the other a milky white (creepy). And Luna is dressing up as some video game and movie character named Lara Croft. I don\u2019t really know anything about the character\u2026 but Luna definitely looks hot tonight.<br /> <br /> So now we\u2019re off, to throw ourselves into the complex, deceptive, and often torrid social scene of the Freehold. I can hardly wait to see what happens!<br /> <b><br /> Lorelei Grace</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T14:50:25-08:00","id":789933,"title":"","content":"<b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> It\u2019s the day before Halloween and things had to go and get \u201cinteresting\u201d again. The day started out normal enough. The lot of us helped De la Rocha move out of her apartment and into the Dream House. It was kind of a bittersweet event for De la Rocha. She apparently moved into that apartment after she broke things off with Spidertoes in a bid to show her independence. Now she was giving that up to share a room with her lover and a house with several other people. She wasn\u2019t living in the apartment anymore. She just went back to make sure nothing had been stolen and to throw out any food that had gone bad. It wasn\u2019t practical to keep it, but I can understand why it would be hard to give up. It must feel like losing something of her independence. But we\u2019re not ones to make others feel like they\u2019re penned in, so I think that De la Rocha will come to believe that she actually hasn\u2019t lost that freedom she craves.<br /> <br /> Later, after Calamity\u2019s act Madame Spidertoes came by and gathered up Insincere Marguerite, Calamity and Julia. I would say that she was getting all the Darklings together, but De la Rocha was not included. Maybe it was an Autumn Court thing? Though Marguerite is in the Night Court. She does do a lot for the Autumn Court though\u2026she could be an honorary member by now. Anyhoo\u2026they eventually came back out. As Spidertoes was leaving she asked Lorelei if she minded if De la Rocha escorted her out to her car. Lori said it was up to De la Rocha, but seemed really tense about the whole thing. In the end De la Rocha and Julia, who looked delighted to go, escorted the elder Changeling outside. I don\u2019t know the whole story, but from what I\u2019ve gathered Madame Spidertoes has been flirting with De la Rocha, and since the older woman had a previous relationship with the Latin beauty Lori feels threatened. I think she might be afraid that Spidertoes is trying to woo De la Rocha back to her. For my part, I\u2019m not sure. Spidertoes does seem to keep those feelings of fondness alive for those that she\u2019s been involved with, and continues to take care of them in various ways. I can see why Lori might feel threatened. I just don\u2019t know what advice to give, so I have stayed silent on the matter.<br /> <br /> After the Autumn Court meeting Insincere Marguerite stopped to watch Chalcedony dance on the stage. I didn\u2019t think much about it until Julia came up behind her and just about pushed her over. How focused was Marguerite that she let herself be pushed? Makes me wonder if there is something to Insincere Marguerite\u2019s fascination with Chalcedony. Anyway\u2026after all that was over Calamity gathered up the motley and said that she needed to talk to us. She said that Madame Spidertoes had gathered up the Autumn Courtiers to discuss a threat that Tommy had discovered. She brought it to those she trusted first since she was afraid of the information getting out to the wrong people. Apparently they discovered that some people from the Hollywood Courts are sending mortals in to our area and are setting up a base of sorts in an old strip club called Foxy Boxes. The fear is that they are being sent to our neck of the woods to spy on our freehold. They also have a Hedge beast in the club for protection. So they are worried that they will need said protection, which doesn\u2019t sound like a clean conscience to me. It does sound likely that they are up to something.<br /> <br /> Madame Spidertoes wants to keep the number of people that know about this to the absolute minimum. She hasn\u2019t even told the Monarchs. She told select people from her Court, namely our motley mates, and gave them permission to tell the rest of us. She says that she doesn\u2019t know if there are any Changelings in the freehold that are actually spies for the Hollywood Courts, but didn\u2019t want to take the chance. So, we discussed the mortal spies and what to do about them. Calamity seemed to be leaning along the lines of killing everyone there, dealing with the Hedge beast and leaving. Insincere Marguerite was keen on the idea of just using her \u201csleeping cloth\u201d on them. She was quite adamant that anyone she knocked out with the chloroform not be killed while they are incapacitated. She repeated herself several times. I got the strong impression that she was trying very hard to influence Calamity away from killing them all. Lori was also very much against killing the mortals, saying that knocking them out and taking their computer and/or other information would be good enough. I am not sure where I fall on the whole matter. I generally try to draw as little attention to myself as possible, and killing the mortals would definitely draw unwanted attention. The police would get involved and could very well trace the crime back to us. I don\u2019t know if we are all good enough to not leave some sort of evidence behind. <br /> <br /> That covers the practical aspect of the matter. There is also the moral aspect, and I\u2019m not sure that I would actually mind all that much if some of the mortals died. I guess it depends on their reaction to us. If they just give up or run I\u2019d be tempted to just let them go. If they try to hurt or kill us then all bets are off though. That is one thing I do not tolerate. But is it right to kill them? I suppose I could just incapacitate them and leave them behind to crawl back to the Hollywood Court. My worry is what information they might already have on our Freehold. We can\u2019t exactly pull a \u201cHarry Potter\u201d and remove the memories of what they\u2019ve learned about us. Practically it\u2019s not wise to let them live. They are a security risk and could leak information that we can\u2019t afford to let out. On the other hand I\u2019m not sure it would be right to kill them if they aren\u2019t actively trying to do the same to us. I don\u2019t know what to do. Part of me agrees with Calamity\u2019s practical approach, but there\u2019s that small little voice of doubt in my head. Killing should be wrong, shouldn\u2019t it? So why am I unsure?<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> It\u2019s Halloween, Samhain\u2026and today definitely had a more \u201cinteresting\u201d start than usual. After I\u2019d finished making and handing out coffee for the group Lowjack called and said that he needed to talk to Insincere Marguerite as soon as possible. Okay\u2026it was implied that he wanted to talk to her right away. So, I told Marguerite about the meeting and she got ready to go. I offered to stay with her if that was allowed and she said that she would appreciate that. I can understand that. I figured something was up, but didn\u2019t know what for sure. I initially thought it had to do with the Loyalist that Darke said was looking at me and Insincere Marguerite a while back. Not sure if that Loyalist was Rook or someone else though. If it was Rook I am curious why the Lady would have him look into Marguerite. If it\u2019s someone else that was interested in us then we still don\u2019t know who they are, and that makes me nervous.<br /> <br /> So, we arrived at Lowjacks bar and were immediately ushered into the backroom. We were met by Lowjack, Vik, Molly and Willow Black. Boss Lowjack motioned for me to stay but close the door, which I did. He then opened with the information that Tamara had been attacked and nearly killed by the Handmaidens last night. He was pissed. I have never seen Lowjack so angry in all the time I\u2019ve been here. Granted that\u2019s not all that long, but still. Lowjack is usually composed and calm, but this afternoon he was furious. He said that he had made arrangements that if any other members of the Winter Court should be attacked or killed then one of the Night Courtiers would be killed in retribution! He said that plans were already in place. So even if it was him that was killed the plan would still be executed\u2026so to speak. It was kind of implied that Willow would be the first target. It wasn\u2019t said straight out, but the implication was there. Willow did not take things well and started to take a step forward. She got about half a step before Molly pulled a gun and aimed it right at Willow\u2019s head. The Night Courtier stopped.<br /> <br /> Willow objected to Lowjack\u2019s ultimatum and looked to Marguerite for help. Boss Lowjack then implied that there are others in the Night Court that are jealous of Insincere Marguerite\u2019s position within the Court and may be looking for a way to get her out of the way. He inferred that Marguerite and Felicity stood in the way of Willow Black and Olivia Gold respectively. Apparently there have been talks or whispers about the Night and Day Courts getting a monarch within the freehold, and my motley mate and Jolie\u2019s lover stand in the way of the crowns going to certain people in their respective Courts if/when created. I\u2019m not sure if he has facts to back up those accusations or if it is just speculation, but it was clear what he was doing in any case. Divide and conquer has been a tried and true method for centuries.<br /> <br /> I can understand the desire to protect one\u2019s own, which is why I was a little conflicted today. I understood Lowjack\u2019s desire for retribution should one of the Winter Court be killed, but it was also implied that Marguerite might be one of the targets and that is not acceptable. She is my motley mate and my friend and I will not allow her to be hurt. I hope that I am not forced to choose between my Court and my friend. I respect Lowjack, he seems to be a good person and genuinely wants to help people, otherwise he would not be in the entitlement that he is. I really don\u2019t want to side against him, but I really don\u2019t want Insincere Marguerite to be a target. I know I should have said something at the time, but I\u2019ll be honest. I was more than a little bit shocked by the ultimatum. Not that Lowjack made it, because I can understand why he did, but because I was being put on the spot in a way.<br /> <br /> I talked to Lowjack after Willow and Insincere Marguerite stepped out. I enquired how Tamara was doing and asked if I should get Lori to come by. Boss Lowjack said that two Spring Courtiers were already seeing to Tamara and that she was going to be okay. I offered to talk to Lorelei about coming over to help. He said that wasn\u2019t necessary. I nodded my understanding but left it as an open offer in case additional help was needed. I did not think that Lori would mind assisting Tamara should the need arise. <br /> <br /> After all that was over Insincere Marguerite and I went back to the Dream House to talk to the rest of our Motley. We explained what happened and the discussion began. The others were shocked at what had happened to Tamara and at Lowjack\u2019s response. Some were also not sure if John had proof that Insincere Marguerite and Felicity were in actual danger, or if he was just trying to sow dissent. It could have just been pure speculation on his part as well. I don\u2019t know for sure. I didn\u2019t want to ask him flat out if he had proof in front of Willow or Marguerite. I figured he wouldn\u2019t tell me while there was an audience anyway. I\u2019ll have to ask him later. Perhaps once he has calmed down a bit.<br /> <br /> Throughout all of this there is still one question that has gone unanswered. Why Tamara? Why did the Handmaidens decide to target her and nearly kill her? And was she supposed to have died and got lucky, or was she left on the brink of death as a warning of some kind? I\u2019m not sure exactly how a Leechfinger\u2019s powers work, so I don\u2019t know how much control they have over whether or not their victim survives. They clearly have been targeting Tamara for months now, but this is the first time they have gone so far. They drained her once before that I know of to the point she needed healing, but it wasn\u2019t life threatening then. This time it was. So why? That\u2019s what I want to know. I also wanted to know why we weren\u2019t threatening the Handmaidens if they were the ones that hurt Tamara in the first place. I asked Lowjack this and he said that it was politically bad for us to target the Handmaidens. Any harm that befell them would make the Warlock of Night upset and we apparently can\u2019t afford to make her mad. So because the real culprits cannot be targeted, Lowjack has moved on to the next most prominent members of the Court to use as scapegoats. Not sure how many members there are, but Lowjack implied that there were more than the two in the room with us. <br /> <br /> I can understand not wanting to make the L.A. Night Court monarch upset, but surely she has to realize that her people need to be disciplined for what they do wrong. Willow Black is supposed to be their minder while they are in town, but apparently she has not done a very good job of it so far. They have slipped their \u201cleash\u201d a few times now, and this time someone was badly hurt. I don\u2019t find it acceptable at all. Part of me really wants to teach them a lesson despite Lowjack\u2019s wishes. They are protected by the Warlock and can basically get away with anything they so desire. They should be held accountable for their actions just like the rest of us. If any of us from the Lady by the Sea freehold should pull anything similar in L.A there would be hell to pay, so why do these two get away with almost killing someone?<br /> <br /> **** **** **** <br /> <br /> Okay, some time has passed since this morning and I have calmed down somewhat. It is time to get ready for the masquerade. Several of us are dressed in our new Hedge spun clothes, courtesy of Gawain\u2019s awesome skills. Gawain\u2019s new armor makes it look like he\u2019s got forest shadows moving across his chest and back. Insincere Marguerite has a tawny leonine dress, which looks really nice. Kind of creepy that she\u2019s still kind of following in her Keeper\u2019s footsteps fashion-wise, but it was still pretty. Lorelei dressed as Neil Gaiman\u2019s Death, in Victorian/Goth finery. Very cute. I always liked that character. Let\u2019s see, Calamity is dressed as a droog from \u201cA Clockwork Orange,\u201d I am wearing my new ice armor\u2026it\u2019s actually made of ice. I thought about wearing the new sheath that Gawain also made for me that produces an ice blade when I need one, but figured it wouldn\u2019t be polite to go armed. I think Gawain did a great job on it if you ask me. And last but certainly not least is Luna. She decided to dress as Lara Croft. Totally hot! I think a new Tomb Raider game came out while I was gone, but I remember playing the older ones and liking Lara\u2019s character. <br /> <br /> There was something going on about Joan and Andromeda. I think the gist was that they were going to be dressed in costumes that the other didn\u2019t know about and that would hide their identity. They\u2019re going to go separately and see if they hook up with each other and maybe have a dalliance with someone new. Some of the others, Lori and Gawain included wanted to find out what Joan was dressing as so they could try their hand at seducing her. I guess we\u2019ll see how that works out. Me, I plan on dancing with anyone that wants to, but am not looking for any \u201chook-ups.\u201d I have Luna and she is more than enough for me. <br /> <br /> <b><br /> Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> Why is everyone but me completely irrational? It is as if my lovers and Motley lost their minds.<br /> <br /> The 30th was the day De La Rocha moved into the Dream House in full. It should have been a happy day. But she was deeply moody. Sure, there is some sadness leaving a place, but she had not lived there in months. She worried about Spidertoes, and Lorelei really, really worried about Spidertoes. They need to talk to Spidertoes. But no they do not, well, mostly not. Sadly.<br /> <br /> Opportunity knocked when Spidertoes arrived that evening. De La Rocha had gone to greet her, and she arranged a meeting with Calamity, Julia, and I. Spidertoes is unaccustomed to explaining herself, which to be fair to De La Rocha is annoying, but she took things in the absolute worst possible way: Utter Rejection. I discovered post meeting that she took her frustrations out on a punching bag, and upset Lori, who took out her frustrations on a punching bag. Weirdly.<br /> <br /> When we got out of the meeting, I paused to admire Chalcedony\u2019s dancing (which was very good) and Julia pushed me and Calamity flipped out about Chalcedony controlling me. I heard Julia walk up, she has a familiar tread. I just did not expect to be pushed. Calamity warned me of Chalcedony \u201chaving a hold of me\u201d but that hardly seems true. We always speak briefly when she comes to dance but it is a polite exchange. I almost as often have one with Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne. We haven\u2019t kissed, she has shown no interest in me, and has not even asked me to fetch a glass of water. And Calamity thinks I am controlled and seems to have convinced Julia of this. This is a non-academic problem, as Calamity is on a crazy uptick and wants to go murdering people while Julia can be violent in her defense of me. Unfortunately.<br /> <br /> So when Spidertoes was headed out, and perhaps sensing Lori had concerns (by perhaps sensing, I mean noticing the obvious tension on her face) Spidertoes politely asked Lori if she minded if De La Rocha escorted her out. Lori answered this consideration of her feelings by snapping that De La Rocha could make up her own mind. De La Rocha elected to do so, but with Julia there for Lori\u2019s sake. For her part Julia just seemed happy to bask in Spidertoes gothic mysteriousness. However, Lori did not address the elephant in the room about her feelings (despite Spidertoes giving her an opening) and De La Rocha did not use the relative privacy to discuss it. I fail to understand this, though perhaps she would wind up being like Calamity\u2019s amateur Kremlinology.<br /> <br /> The matter was simple. Agents of the Court of Fallen Stars had expended into our turf, into a former stop club called Foxy Boxes. De La Rocha explained it is a vagina reference. There were, well, boxes moved in, some agents at work, a hedge beast, and a computer system. We were tasks with killing the beast, dealing with the humans, and acquiring the data. Simple, no? While Calamity and I could probably do it ourselves, getting the Motley involved made sense and quite frankly raised the chances of an easy job. Fortunately.<br /> <br /> But Calamity insisted on a Bloodbath. Gawain clearly disapproved, Lorelei disapproved, and I made it clear we had a non-lethal means of dealing with humans. I would point out Julia disapproved, but I did and it goes to follow. Anyway dead humans are a waste. One nearly never needs to kill. Certainly not now. Dead humans also bring attention. They bring cops. Cops that could analyze a bloodstain if Calamity is hit by the beast or bullet, Cops that find a nearby camera that shows some of us enter, cops who won\u2019t accept \u201cfreehold business\u201d as a reason. Hedge Beasts, with their ultimate genesis from the Gentry, are one thing, but dead humans bring cops, and Calamity does not need cops right now. Especially given her blood fetish. Almost as importantly, Calamity is in therapy to not be a murder happy monster, but an actual contributor to society. But when she sees an opportunity to murder humans, she is eager to do so, despite the fact it has been <u>clearly shown</u> doing so makes her crazier. Like a child who experiences pain from stabbing a fork in a light socket and does so again, Calamity fails to learn. This makes me sad, as I like Calamity, but I consider having to use the sleeping cloth on her for her own good. Reluctantly.<br /> <br /> Also this person, who apparently thinks going crazy from killing people and having cops looking for you is a good idea, feels I am not exercising good judgment on Chalcedony. At this point if she told I my approach to Chalcedony was wholly rational I would rethink it. Obviously.<br /> <br /> Calamity, Lori, and De La Rocha are not the only ones who have lost their damn mind. I was summoned in the morning by Lowjack, who brought Willow and I into a room with Jacob and a pair of thugs and threatened our lives if anything happened to Tamara due to the Warlock of Night\u2019s Handmaidens. Has Lowjack lost his mind? Making matters worse he revealed how much Olivia and Willow would benefit from my and Felicity\u2019s deaths, saying we are just a few Day and Night Courtiers from having crowns, in front of Willow. I lack strong feelings about Willow, but I cannot believe she would be plotting against I me. Of course, I won\u2019t indulge blind trust. I will be wary. I am not happy with Lowjack, however, in part due to Molly putting a Gun to Willow\u2019s head, which almost got her blinded. Dangerously.<br /> <br /> Something must be up with Tamara. I do not like the Handmaidens at all but the Handmaidens do not choose victims randomly. Could she be a spy or suspected spy for the Court of Fallen Stars? Perhaps she makes people \u201cdisappear\u201d into the Grandmaw. I am not going to accuse her, but a with Willow, while I do not think it the case I will remain wary. I would not mention this to Lowjack, he would probably order Molly to shoot I. Unwisely.<br /> <br /> Now we have the Masque soon, I have my lovely outfit, and people need to get their shit together. Perhaps I will speak to Jacob and Gawain, who do not seem crazy, about this. Or maybe I will discover they have some bizarre problem of their own. Gods I hope not. I need some sanity right now. Certainly.<br /> <br /> Oh, Joan will be there under cover. She is not known to be but De La Rocha spilled the beans. Lori, Gawain, and Julia bribed her for information. I myself did not. If I sleep with her and she ever buys me a drink someone in the Court will decide I took a break from being Chalcedony\u2019s love slave to enrapture her with my vaginamancy. Clearly.<br /> <br /> Well, let\u2019s see if I can actually enjoy myself tonight. Hopefully.<br /> <br /> <i>End Cession XLV</i><br /> <br /> Tension rise!<br /> <br /> We actually covered the beginning of the Masquerade, but all decided it would be easier to cover in one go, so covering that next time.<br /> <br /> They really cover things this time. One point of clarification would be the crowns. According to John Lowjack, Willow and Olivia have been sneaking Day/Night Courtiers into the periphery of town, just like Insincere Marguerite squatted the Dream House. They want enough power for the Day/Night crowns to appear, but have discovered that Felicity and Insincere Marguerite, who resonate intensely with their court, would receive the crowns, rather then themselves. Thus, the two are \u201cin the way.\u201d Is it true? Well\u2026<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite\u2019s costume is not just the lion dress, but a leonine Venetian mask. DLR does not have a mask, but given her habit cover all of her head but the face itself, her distinctive hair is out of sight so she does not need one.<br /> <br /> I think that covers everything, but if I missed something let me know. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T11:46:52-08:00","id":797899,"title":"","content":"Now that I am caught up I can comment that the Foxy Boxes reference made me laugh audibly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T12:37:41-08:00","id":797920,"title":"","content":"Foxy Boxes is there as I often reference locations from Vampire: The Masquerade Bloodlines in Santa Monica. It's not the first, but it is one of the ones that made it into journal. Trip's Pawn Shop, (Gawain initially lived in the apartments above it) Surfside Diner, Megahurtz Computing have all shown up off the top of my head. Well and the Pier but it is a real place. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Sadly only Malibu place from that game is the monastery, which has not come up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 01-01-2016, 03:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T15:31:10-08:00","id":798000,"title":"","content":"I can dig it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Give it time. Maybe someone DLR knows has some issues that lead back to the monastery? Just a thought..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T15:02:26-08:00","id":799818,"title":"","content":"Big recap this time! We cover both the Masquerade and Foxy Boxes raid. We can do this as the Masquerade was the last ~1/3-1/4 of the previous session, so we already got a lot of play in, so longer journals. Lori focus\u2019s more on the Masquerade, Jacob on the raid, Gawain on the aftermath of the raid, Insincere Marguerite\u2026on particular elements of both, let\u2019s say. <br /> <br /> Let\u2019s dig in<br /> <br /> <i>Session XLVI<br /> </i><br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> November 1st, afternoon<br /> <br /> Well, and fun was definitely had. Even if my shot at Joan didn\u2019t get me anywhere (not that I can blame her, Lori was looking hot and really laying on the charm), I certainly wasn\u2019t disappointed and everyone had a great time, and that\u2019s what matters, you know?<br /> <br /> I did get to dance with Joan a few times. It was fun - she did a good job pretending to be Koozebanian, you know, from the Muppet Show. I mean, not in looks, but that\u2019s where she said she was from. I spent pretty much the whole time dancing, in fact, with De la Roche, and Flores (who was dressed as the Baroness from GI Joe) and even Princess Joli. She was dressed as Strawberry Shortcake and even smelled like strawberries, all over. She totally spent the night with me and... wow. It was an amazing night.<br /> <br /> Everybody else had fun too, I think. Calamity came in to \u2018Singing in the Rain\u2019 cause, you know, Clockwork Orange. She got in her share of dancing, with a 5\u20192\u201d Darth Vader (who turned out to be Dark Kimberly) and Flores (who she spent the night with). I thought she seemed, you know, a little worried at one point, but she was definitely alright when she came back into the ballroom, so I dunno.<br /> <br /> The costumes were fun - Shi was a coyote, Queen Charlotte was Batgirl. There was a Tinman, the Red Death and a female Link. Captain Jack showed up, in true Captain Jack style, to the Invader Zim theme and was dressed as Gir in his dog suit. Oleander was there as the Question, De la Roche was pretty sure, and Julia confirmed it as breakfast.<br /> <br /> It was a pretty busy breakfast. Joan didn\u2019t come back with Lori, but Princess Joli, Flores and Dark Kimberly stuck around. We spent most of the time guessing who was and who slept with who. Well, mostly it was trying to guess who \u2018the Koozebanian\u2019 was, since Lori wouldn\u2019t say. She did let it slip that Andromeda had been there (she was the Red Death, not Darth Vader like we all kinda thought).<br /> <br /> Once they all left, we started planning for the evening. We figure the Foxy Boxes thing should be dealt with sooner before later, you know? And our Darklings work better at night, of course, so our current plan is to wait until nightfall, have Insincere Marguerite, Jacob and Calamity sneak in and see what\u2019s up, maybe sleepy cloth any human guards there were. If feasible, Insincere Marguerite\u2019s gonna grab up the computer, then we\u2019ll deal with the Hedgebeast. We\u2019ll see how long it survives enemy contact.<br /> <br /> <br /> Nov 1st evening<br /> <br /> We will not be Darke. Desiree will not be another Molly or Victor. I refuse. Whatever we have to do, whatever rules we have to bend, I will make sure she returns to her very self. And, if necessary, I will personally deal with the consequences.<br /> <br /> The raid went fine. Insincere Marguerite, Calamity and Jacob dealt with the four guards handily. They were just some guys though, a local security firm that thought the Hedge-dragons were komodo dragons. One of the dragons was roughly hippo shaped and it had two mastiff-sized partners. Calamity dealt with one of the small ones quickly, then went after the larger one. They almost had it down by the time I knocked down the door and charged in. I managed to sink my sword into its heart and finished it off. Not before Calamity get hurt, and Jacob got hurt by the second little one before he managed to put it down as well, but Lori and De la Roche got them healed up.<br /> <br /> We decided to try and skin the dragons, so we left via the Hedge. Once we got home, Jacob and I help Calamity log onto the computer, then got to the dragons. We made pretty short work of it, until Calamity came and gathered everybody to let us know what it was that she had found.<br /> <br /> First off, they wanted the Table, and knew that the Autumn Court knew where it was. They didn\u2019t realize they needed Andromeda for it, or had their own Mothership escapee, so they weren\u2019t planning on abducting her. That last bit was the extent of the good news. Well, also that they were terrified of Madame Spidertoes, but that just shows they can follow some forms of realistic logic.<br /> <br /> They had lots of files on their spy. She had been a successful agent of the Director in Hollywood, the most successful yet. They have figured out that the Director\u2019s people are implanted with scripts - if a \u2018scene\u2019 begins, they automatically follow their role, even if they weren\u2019t really a Loyalist. The Courts in Hollywood managed to brainwash this successful agent (who had, in fact, been a Loyalist), forcing her to believe she was not a Loyalist, and that she had never been to Hollywood. Also, they managed to somehow alter her scripts, so she would get in close to the Monarchs here, and report back to Hollywood.<br /> <br /> Up until this point in the description, I had been willing myself to believe it was Chalcedony it was talking about, that it explained the recent oddness and her reluctance to have the conditioning removed. But then Calamity said they had figured out that someone here had been messing with the scripts, and that then, a different someone had removed them. They were worried, she said, because she kept building dioramas, dioramas that echoed the brainwashing sessions the Courts had put her under, sessions that very likely involved her being in the middle of a circle of other people, being looked down upon from their position of authority, watching. Controlling. If she continued with this, if she remembered, they feared, she might go back to being a Loyalist.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, we must tell her. Maybe, since I have removed the scripts, since we have been kind to her, since she has gotten a taste of what freedom is, maybe she won\u2019t wish to work for the Director anymore. And if she does, if she hurts someone... No. If she does, we will stop her before she hurts someone, and we will deal with her appropriately, not by molding her and reforming her into whatever shape we like best.<br /> <br /> Calamity agreed not to tell Madame Spidertoes, in case she gives orders to do something other than the right thing, but she did call to tell her that the Table was the target. I have called Desiree and she is coming here. I\u2019m going to tell her in dreams, as maybe there I\u2019ll be able to tell if she is still a Loyalist. The files warn that she is very good at lying, so I have the much better chance in dreams.<br /> <br /> Lord with us, I hope this works.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> So it\u2019s been about a day and a half since I last wrote anything in here, and things have\u2026 progressed. The Autumn Court\u2019s Masquerade Ball was a lot of fun, and I have no complaints about its immediate aftermath either. The events of the following evening were\u2026 less enjoyable, but I can\u2019t argue the point that we\u2019ve made progress in rooting out the enemies of the Freehold.<br /> <br /> So the last time I wrote we were getting ready to head over to the Ball. I was still feeling pissy about Spidertoes, but I had resolved to locate and seduce Joan (with D\u2019s blessing and assistance), so I was also feeling moderately more positive about the direction the day was taking. I was all gothed out in my Death threads, with dyed-black hair and an ankh necklace so big that it bordered on tacky. There, the stage is set.<br /> <br /> The Ball was a lot of fun. As with the Gala last spring when D and I performed the Greening, this event was separated into several themed rooms. One room was obviously set up for formal dancing, another for jazz dancing, and a third for more traditional Halloween party games (like bobbing for apples). Most of us made our way to the formal dance room and began to mingle.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t claim to know everything that everyone did that night. I know that most of us danced with multiple partners, and I\u2019m sure there was some intrigue-y stuff going on too, but I wasn\u2019t privy to most of it. Therefore I\u2019m going to contain my descriptions to the people I danced with and the conversations we had\u2026 with one notable exception.<br /> <br /> The first people who greeted us as we arrived were Queen Charlotte (dressed as Batgirl) and a woman dressed in a suit, a fedora, and a faceless mask. I later learned that she was a comic book character called the Question. A male version of the character was around back in my day, but didn\u2019t become incredibly well known until some years later. The later, female version of the character (Renee Montoya) was moderately notorious as one of DC\u2019s first \u201cout\u201d lesbians. D explained this to me quickly, and then grinned and stated that she would never forgive herself if she didn\u2019t get at least one dance with her (though neither of us knew who was behind the blank mask at that point).<br /> <br /> I kept one eye on D and the Question as I began mingling. D seemed to be enjoying herself, but the Question was oddly stiff and formal... it was like she was suddenly very uncomfortable about something. I began to formulate a theory about her identity, but I\u2019m getting a little ahead of myself.<br /> <br /> I danced with a few people early on. The first one to ask me to dance was a changeling of indeterminate gender dressed as the Red Death. He/she was a good dancer, and a charming conversationalist, but left after a single dance. I was also approached by a fairly short person dressed as Darth Vader, which was fun to say the least, but again, she left me to dance with someone else after a single number.<br /> <br /> I made my way toward the Question after that, eager to test my theory. I asked if she would like to dance, and she agreed readily. When the next song started, I leaned in close, put my arms around her neck, kissed her cheek, and whispered \u201cHello, sweetie. It\u2019s nice to see a familiar face.\u201d<br /> <br /> My partner stiffened for a moment, and then relaxed. A familiar if somewhat muffled voice chuckled softly. \u201cWas I that obvious? I thought I\u2019d been pretty clever.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled. \u201cI bet no one else here recognizes you, Oleander,\u201d I said softly, \u201cbut I\u2019d know you anywhere. Besides, I can\u2019t think of anyone else who would look <u>that</u> uncomfortable dancing with D.\u201d<br /> <br /> She laughed again. \u201cGuilty as charged,\u201d she admitted sheepishly. \u201cDo you think she knew it was me?\u201d<br /> <br /> I shrugged noncommittally. If D picked up on how uncomfortable her partner was, then I figure she probably had a pretty good idea of her identity, but I didn\u2019t want to say anything to embarrass Oleander. \u201cLook, sweetie,\u201d I said softly when the music carried us away from prying ears, \u201cI know the last few days have been hard on you, and I\u2019m sorry for that. Hurting you was never my intention. You know I love you, right? Just because you\u2019re not part of the Dream House Circle of Darklings doesn\u2019t mean I care any less for you\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> She sniffed slightly. \u201cI know. And I don\u2019t mean to give you a hard time about de la Rocha moving in with you. It should be a happy occasion\u2026 for both of you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat do you say we set aside some time for each other in a couple of days?\u201d I asked brightly. \u201cJust you and me. I\u2019ll come over to your place. I\u2019ll bring some massage oil, some scented candles, a bottle of wine\u2026 maybe even some bubble bath\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> She leaned in close, and there was a faint kissing sound from behind the faceless mask. \u201cSounds perfect. It\u2019s a date,\u201d she said after a moment. \u201cBut for tonight, go on and have fun. Hook up with someone who isn\u2019t already in love with you\u2026 if you can find anyone like that,\u201d she quipped lightly as the song ended.<br /> <br /> I gave her the best smile I could muster. \u201cOkay, but take your own advice. Have a fling, just for fun. I promise I\u2019ll still be there for you when it\u2019s over.\u201d<br /> <br /> She promised to make the most of her evening, and I moved off in search of my true prey. I saw her a few moments later, looking exactly as D had described her earlier that day\u2026 a silvery bodysuit topped by a big square monitor displaying a female head. I moved toward her through the crowd and made my presence known.<br /> <br /> \u201cHello there,\u201d I said sweetly as I approached.<br /> <br /> \u201cGreetings, Earth female,\u201d the otherworldly beauty replied.<br /> <br /> I had to grin at the stilted alien-speak. \u201cWhat brings you to our planet, honored visitor?\u201d I asked her with a smile.<br /> <br /> The video image on the screen blinked placidly. \u201cI have come from the planet Koozebane to observe human social interactions,\u201d she informed me in a matter-of-fact tone. Something about the name of the planet sparked my memory. At first I thought it sounded like the name of a barbarian warrior from a <u>really</u> bad porno flick, actually.<br /> <br /> I smiled and batted my eyes. \u201cI am considered something of an authority on human social interactions,\u201d I said modestly, \u201cand I would be happy to assist such a lovely ambassador in any way I can. Would you care to dance?\u201d<br /> <br /> The video image remained stoic, but the monitor itself bobbed up and down. \u201cThat would be most agreeable, Earth female,\u201d she said with animation. \u201cI would like to see how Earth gyrations differ from traditional Koozebanian dances.\u201d<br /> <br /> Wait a second\u2026 Koozebane! That was the planet they were always talking about on <u>The Muppet Show</u>. I <u>knew</u> I\u2019d heard that name somewhere before. I even remembered being highly amused by the hidden sexual humor in the original skit about Koozebanian mating rituals. I had found my ace.<br /> <br /> Luckily, a slow song had just started, and the two of us glided around the dance floor in sultry circles. My partner was a little taller than me, so I leaned in close and put my head on her shoulder, allowing her to lead. After a few minutes, the song ended, and I reluctantly separated myself from her toned form. \u201cWould you like to do that again, space girl?\u201d I asked breathily, batting my heavily mascaraed lashes at her.<br /> <br /> She stiffened. \u201cI\u2026 uh\u2026\u201d she stammered.<br /> <br /> There was a noise of someone clearing their throat. I turned around and Gawain was standing there, looking splendid (if a little nervous). \u201cExcuse me, ladies\u2026 mind if I cut in?\u201d<br /> <br /> The alien girl started to move away (the image on the screen grinning happily now), but I put a stop to that. \u201cNot at all, Sir Knight,\u201d I said as I dropped into a curtsy. I turned back to the alien girl. \u201cIt\u2019s what we Earthlings call a \u2018raincheck,\u2019 my sweet. Save me a dance later, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded and moved fluidly into a stately waltz with Gawain. D swooped in to dance with me in full nun regalia. \u201cYou gonna stand idly by while Gawain snipes your lady?\u201d she asked with a wink. \u201cI\u2019ve got money on this, you know.\u201d I think she was joking, but I\u2019m not entirely sure.<br /> <br /> I shook my head. \u201cI\u2019m playing a long game,\u201d I informed her confidently. \u201cShe\u2019ll be back for more before the night is over.\u201d<br /> <br /> D grinned devilishly. \u201cI know,\u201d she said. \u201cNo one can resist you, babe.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLook who\u2019s talking,\u201d I said, eyeing her up and down. \u201cYou trolling for Becky tonight, or do you have your eye on someone else?\u201d Becky Won\u2019s fondness for ecclesiastical regalia is fairly well known in the Freehold, though I really doubted D would specifically target her for an evening of passion.<br /> <br /> Her eyes twinkled. \u201cI have a few prospects,\u201d she admitted. Then her face fell. \u201cDon\u2019t worry, I\u2019ll be good,\u201d she said a little bitterly.<br /> <br /> I leaned in and kissed her. \u201cThat\u2019s not what I meant,\u201d I said earnestly. \u201cLook, I\u2019m sorry about the way I acted last night, okay? I\u2019ll make things right when I can. But for tonight, I just want you to concentrate on having fun while I claim a sweet piece of Koozebanian ass.\u201d<br /> <br /> D had to laugh at that. \u201cOkay, Lori, deal. You have fun too. Love you.\u201d And we went our separate ways for the evening.<br /> <br /> Calamity made her entrance sometime around then, fashionably late as always. She had somehow arranged to have the band begin playing \u201cSingin\u2019 In the Rain\u201d as she strolled in, decked out in her droog gear. I had to chuckle at that. She mingled for a bit, and we said hi to each other in passing, but she seemed pretty intent on crossing the dance floor to talk to Madame Spidertoes, so I didn\u2019t detain her for long. The two of them left the room together shortly after that.<br /> <br /> My next dance partner was Flores, who was not hiding her identity. She was dressed in a tight black latex bodysuit which sported a stylized cobra\u2019s head in red on her impressive chest. She was also wearing glasses. Someone told me later that she was supposed to be the Baroness, but they didn\u2019t bother to elaborate about which one. Dancing with Flores was fun, and she was as bubbly and effusive as ever.<br /> <br /> Calamity eventually made it back into the ballroom and spoke briefly with Marguerite, who then hurried off (presumably also to talk to Madame Spidertoes\u2026 what is it with her and Darklings, anyway?). I danced with a few other people, male and female, over the next hour or so. Highlights include Queen Charlotte (as Batgirl) and Princess Jolie, who was dressed as a cartoon character called Strawberry Shortcake (apparently I missed that one by a few years, and as fetching as Jolie was in that costume, I can\u2019t help but think that I might have dodged a bullet there).<br /> <br /> Marguerite returned to the ballroom a little while later accompanied by Madame Spidertoes, who looked thoughtful but unruffled. The two parted a few minutes later (Marguerite made a bee-line toward Felicity), and I seized my chance. I approached Madame Spidertoes and asked if she would like to dance. She favored me with a smile and accepted graciously.<br /> <br /> \u201cI thought I should speak with you about my behavior last night, Madame,\u201d I said softly as we glided through the crowd.<br /> <br /> She cocked her head to the side and looked ever so slightly uncomfortable. \u201cIndeed?\u201d she said quizzically. Sometimes I forget how detached she is from modern social norms.<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cI wanted to apologize. You were an honored guest in my house, and I was rude to you. My love was upset, and it put me out of sorts. I\u2019m sorry if I offended you in any way.\u201d<br /> <br /> She looked a little distressed, but not angry. \u201cIt was not my intention to upset either of you,\u201d she said after a moment.<br /> <br /> \u201cI know that now,\u201d I assured her. \u201cShe\u2019s very sensitive when it comes to you. She still cares about you so much, and sometimes\u2026\u201d I tried not to get choked up as I admitted my own insecurities, \u201csometimes I feel a little threatened by that fact.\u201d<br /> <br /> She leveled an intense gaze at me, and I found myself struggling not to flinch away. \u201cBut no,\u201d she said softly, \u201cyou make de la Rocha very happy, Lorelei. I do not wish to be the cause of trouble between the two of you. I have no romantic designs on her, and will not attempt to seduce her away from you.\u201d She paused for a moment as though considering what she was saying carefully. \u201cI will swear to it, if you wish.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled at that. \u201cThank you, Madame, but it\u2019s not necessary. Your word is more than enough for me.\u201d The song ended, and we curtsied to each other in courtly fashion. \u201cAnd once again, I\u2019d like to apologize for my rudeness last night. You are always welcome at the Dream House, and I promise I won\u2019t let my emotions get the better of me again.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThink no further on it, my dear,\u201d she said with a nod. \u201cThere are those who say that Spring and Autumn are opposed, but they speak without reflection. For who among us does not have something they desire so much that they fear it\u2019s loss?\u201d<br /> <br /> So that was the end of one of the stranger conversations I had that night. I started to mingle again, and paused to laugh with everyone else when Captain Jack arrived in some sort of cartoon stuffed animal dog suit. I have a hard time understanding his antics at the best of times, and I don\u2019t claim that this made a lick of sense to me. As I was scanning the crowd for my Koozebanian quarry, I felt a light plucking at my sleeve.<br /> <br /> It was Marguerite. Behind her lion mask, she looked wild-eyed and distressed. \u201cI must speak with you, Lorelei,\u201d she said insistently.<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course,\u201d I said as she led me toward a less populated area of the room. \u201cWhat\u2019s on your mind?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFelicity,\u201d she hissed when we were alone. \u201cShe is here and she is willing and I must have her.\u201d<br /> <br /> This didn\u2019t sound like much of a problem to me at first, but then I remembered our conversation at Calamity\u2019s birthday party, in which I promised to help her rein in her more possessive, self-destructive impulses. I took both of her hands gently in my own. \u201cAre you going to be all right?\u201d I asked softly.<br /> <br /> \u201cYes. No. I do not know,\u201d she said. Her face seemed to flicker back and forth between manic possessiveness and a sort of lost terror. I\u2019d never seen her like that before. \u201cThe urge to take her, to make her mine forever, it is so strong,\u201d she said quietly, pleading with her eyes. \u201cShe is waiting for I to return. I must go to her. I must claim\u2026 no. No, it is wrong.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat do you want me to do, Insincere Marguerite?\u201d I asked her softly. \u201cI can stay with you until this passes, if you like. You won\u2019t have to work through this alone.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll help too.\u201d Calamity had just walked up and quickly assessed the situation. \u201cMy therapist has taught me some pretty effective methods to get past the dark impulses. I think they might help you.\u201d<br /> <br /> Marguerite nodded. \u201cI will try. We should leave the room, so that I cannot see her. Lorelei, you must make my apologies, and\u2026 remove her from my grasp. Ensure that she is safe from I, please.\u201d<br /> <br /> I promised to do my best as she and Calamity left the ballroom. <br /> <br /> I made my way across the floor to a bemused looking Felicity, who was decked out in a classic Catwoman costume. \u201cSo who are you supposed to be?\u201d I quipped as I approached. \u201cJulie Newmar, Lee Meriwether, or Eartha Kitt?\u201d<br /> <br /> She favored me with one of her dazzling smiles. \u201cWhat, not going to bring up Michelle Pfeiffer, Halle Berry, or Anne Hathaway?\u201d She turned serious a moment later. \u201cIs Insincere Marguerite okay? We were talking and dancing, and I thought things were going really well, and then she just bolted\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled and nodded. \u201cShe\u2019s\u2026 dealing with a few things right now. The sort of things that we all have to deal with from time to time,\u201d I said pointedly, and Felicity nodded in understanding. \u201cI\u2019m sorry, but tonight\u2019s probably not going to be a good time for the two of you to get together. Insincere Marguerite sent me to convey her apologies. I hope you understand.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cOf course. I was just confused, and\u2026 a little worried.\u201d<br /> <br /> Once I had assured her that Marguerite would be fine, I headed off toward the bar area, in search of my lost Koozebanian friend. I found her there easily enough, and it was obvious that she had been indulging in a few shots of liquid courage. I flatter myself in thinking that I had something to do with that\u2026 and try not to wonder how the hell she could drink anything in that get-up.<br /> <br /> \u201cGreetings, my lovely friend,\u201d I said as I sat down next to her.<br /> <br /> \u201cHello again, Earth female,\u201d she replied. It was hard to read any kind of emotion through that digital mask of hers, but I thought she sounded pleased to see me.<br /> <br /> \u201cHow are your studies of human social interaction going?\u201d I asked with genuine interest.<br /> <br /> \u201cThey are going well, thank you. Many Earthlings have danced with me. I believe the phrase is \u2018I am having fun.\u2019\u201d<br /> <br /> I laughed at this. \u201cI\u2019m glad to hear it,\u201d I said. \u201cWould you like to spend a bit more time studying <u>me</u>?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> She stiffened, but nodded. \u201cI believe that I would find that most agreeable,\u201d she said after a moment.<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay,\u201d I replied. \u201cWould you like to dance again, or would you rather go upstairs for a little\u2026\u201d I leaned in and whispered the nonsense phrase breathily \u201c<i>galley-oh-hoop-hoop?\u201d</i> I was leaning in so close to her body that I could actually feel the little shudder that ran through her a second later. The three minutes I\u2019d spent on my phone earlier searching the web for the details of the old Muppet Show skit were definitely worth it.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2026 that is\u2026 galley\u2026\u201d she stammered for a moment before taking a deep breath and replying in a firm, familiar voice. \u201cI would like that very much.\u201d<br /> <br /> So we made our way upstairs and found an unoccupied private room reserved for just such eventualities. I let her precede me into the room and locked the door behind us. She turned to face me and began working at the clasps that held her helmet on. Just before she removed it she spoke, and her voice was serious once more. \u201cLorelei,\u201d she said softly, \u201cwhen I take this mask off, you might be surprised. And disappointed,\u201d she added.<br /> <br /> I nodded for her to continue, still smiling. A moment later the monitor helmet came off. She pulled a few pins out of her hair and shook out her platinum blonde locks. Joan looked almost vulnerable in that moment as she gazed questioningly into my eyes.<br /> <br /> I walked up and took her face in my hands. \u201cA little surprised, sure,\u201d I said, \u201cbut not at all disappointed.\u201d I pulled her into a kiss, and things progressed from there. What followed was a very pleasant night. Joan is not the most skilled of lovers, but she is passionate and dedicated and fierce, and she did just fine by me (several times). I flatter myself by thinking that she enjoyed the experience as well, and a few hours later we both fell asleep with her cradling me against her chest in a tight embrace.<br /> <br /> I felt safe. Protected. I knew that nothing could harm me as long as I was in her arms. Andromeda is a very lucky woman.<br /> <br /> I woke up the next morning in almost the same position. Joan still had her arms around me, but now she was softly stroking and straightening my feathers. That always soothes me, as it reminds me of the times Missy, Jane and I would preen each other to prepare for our audiences with the Empress. D does it sometimes, and so does Oleander, but Joan had a look of awed fascination on her face that was humbling.<br /> <br /> \u201cGood morning, Joan,\u201d I said sleepily.<br /> <br /> I had thought that might break the spell, but she didn\u2019t even flinch, she just kept stroking my wings and smiling softly. \u201cGood morning, Lorelei,\u201d she replied.<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you for last night,\u201d I said softly. \u201cIt was amazing, and I\u2019ll always treasure the memory. I hope we can do it again some time.\u201d<br /> <br /> Joan frowned slightly, but didn\u2019t stop running her fingers through my feathers. \u201cThat would\u2026 it would have to be okay with Andromeda\u2026\u201d she stammered a little.<br /> <br /> I smiled and shifted so that I could run my hand lightly along her strong jaw. \u201cOf course it would,\u201d I agreed. \u201cI\u2019ve been attracted to you for a long time, Joan, but the only reason I let that happen last night is because I <u>knew</u> you\u2019d never do something like this if you thought it would hurt Andromeda. Just like I hope you know I\u2019d never do anything to hurt <u>either</u> of you.\u201d<br /> <br /> Joan nodded. \u201cOf course. Andromeda is more\u2026 adventurous than I am. She thought it would be good to\u2026 broaden my horizons a bit.\u201d<br /> <br /> I arched an eyebrow. \u201cAnd what do you think, now that they\u2019ve been broadened?\u201d I asked with a grin.<br /> <br /> She smiled again. It\u2019s not the way she smiles at Andromeda, but then again, it really shouldn\u2019t be the same. It\u2019s more like the smiles she gives to D sometimes. That made me very happy.<br /> <br /> \u201cI have no regrets,\u201d she said after a moment. \u201cIt was, as I have said, a most pleasant evening. I do not want you to think that I am ashamed of anything that happened last night, Lorelei. It is important to me that you know that. However, there are those in the Freehold who might see this as an \u2018indiscretion\u2019 and seek to use it against me. So I must ask that you do not speak of what we have shared with anyone.\u201d<br /> <br /> I thought about that for a moment. \u201cI\u2026 don\u2019t keep secrets from D,\u201d I told her seriously, \u201cbut I\u2019m sure she won\u2019t let it go any further if I tell her how important it is to you. Is that okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> Joan nodded. \u201cI trust de la Rocha,\u201d she said. It gave me an odd pang of vicarious guilt to hear her say that, knowing that D had sold me the secret of Joan\u2019s costume in exchange for the promise of a night of unbridled filth, but I let it pass. \u201cUnfortunately this means that I must give up the opportunity to experience the storied \u2018Sex Breakfast,\u2019\u201d Joan added with a grin.<br /> <br /> \u201cToo bad, Gawain makes a mean crepe,\u201d I told her.<br /> <br /> Oh, she did tell me that Andromeda had been behind the Red Death mask at the ball. And here I\u2019d thought she had been the tiny Vader (I later learned that Vader had in fact been Dark-Lord-of-the-Sith-Kimberly).<br /> <br /> There was a little more light banter as we got dressed (she stared unabashed at me as I stretched and bent to pick up my things, which gave me a nice tingly feeling), and we said our goodbyes with one last lingering kiss. I made my way back to the Dream House to find that most of the others were already there, and crepes were indeed in the offing. Unsurprisingly, I had worked up quite an appetite.<br /> <br /> There were paramours and trysts galore in evidence. Oleander apparently ended up in bed with Julia, which made me smile. Calamity finally got to spend an evening with Flores, which I know pleased them both. Jacob and Luna stuck with each other, of course. Marguerite, following the incident with Felicity, decided to set her sights on a different lady, and ended up seducing Dark Kimberly. And Gawain didn\u2019t seem to suffer much from his \u201cdefeat\u201d in our little contest\u2026 his consolation prize turned out to be none other than Princess Jolie herself! Lucky dog\u2026<br /> <br /> D was there as well, wearing a very satisfied glow. Now we\u2019ve been together long enough for me to recognize her \u201cjust-fucked\u201d expression, and she was downright smug about it then. I ambled up next to her as my curiosity got the better of me.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou have a good night?\u201d she asked with a smirk.<br /> <br /> \u201cAmazing,\u201d I said brightly. \u201cI\u2019ll tell you all about it later.\u201d The others had been trying to guess who I\u2019d slept with all morning, but I wasn\u2019t about to betray Joan\u2019s trust. \u201cSo who did you end up with? Don\u2019t give me that look, I can tell you got some last night.\u201d<br /> <br /> She got this sort of irritated, nervous look on her face. \u201cIt wasn\u2019t who you think,\u201d she snapped.<br /> <br /> I put a hand on her shoulder and led her from the room. Once we had a little privacy, I turned to face her. \u201cLook, again, I\u2019m sorry about the other night,\u201d I said as earnestly as I could. \u201cI was out of line, and I know that now. But you were hurting and I was scared and she was an easy target. I\u2019ve already apologized to her, and I think things are okay between us now.\u201d<br /> <br /> D breathed an audible sigh of relief. \u201cGood,\u201d she said simply. \u201cYou know you\u2019ve got nothing to worry about, right? I love you. I\u2019m not going to leave you. Not for her. Not for anyone.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDamn right,\u201d I said. \u201cSo\u2026 who did you sleep with last night?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cA lady never tells,\u201d she smirked.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s why I asked <u>you</u>, chica,\u201d I replied drily. \u201cAt least give me a hint.\u201d<br /> <br /> She thought for a moment. \u201cOkay, it was a guy,\u201d she said.<br /> <br /> \u201cJuan-Carlos?\u201d I asked. It was the first name I came up with, and I know those two have slept together before (having slept between them myself).<br /> <br /> \u201cNope.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDavey?\u201d I asked. Again, I know she has history with the other Darkling, though this time it\u2019s only because she\u2019s mentioned it in passing before.<br /> <br /> \u201cNope. Are you just going to name every male member of the Freehold until you hit on the answer by pure luck?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYep,\u201d I replied.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat could take a while, and I\u2019m going to get really pissed when you get around to guessing Percival,\u201d she growled.<br /> <br /> \u201cI was saving him for last,\u201d I admitted.<br /> <br /> \u201cGood, because I have some standards.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSandoval?\u201d<br /> <br /> She stopped dead, blinked once or twice, and smiled slyly.<br /> <br /> \u201cGood for you, D. He\u2019s hot,\u201d I said, pulling her into a hug.<br /> <br /> After the guests took their leave, we spent most of the rest of the day planning our assault on Hollywood\u2019s little espionage base. The plan we developed was pretty simple in the end. Marguerite would scope the place out in advance and then communicate the locations of the guards. Our other stealth operatives (Jacob and Calamity) would then infiltrate the base, and together the three of them would incapacitate as many of the human guards as possible without raising the alarm. When only the Hedge beast guardians remained, the rest of us would storm in through the front door and join the fight.<br /> <br /> Well, okay, I never had any real intention of joining the fight; I was going to be there in a strictly backup capacity. Still brought my pistol, though.<br /> <br /> In the end it went off almost exactly as we planned it. There were four mortal guards in the \u201cFoxy Boxes\u201d club, and my friends incapacitated three of them with a minimum of fuss. The fourth guard was actually in the presence of the Hedge Beasts, so he couldn\u2019t be taken down without alerting them to our presence.<br /> <br /> Oh yeah, there was more than one Hedge Beast in that place. And they were all dragons.<br /> <br /> Okay, only one of them was what I would call a proper dragon, about the size of a small elephant or rhinoceros. The other two were much smaller, about the size of a large dog like a mastiff. In any case, Marguerite used her \u201csleeping cloth\u201d to knock out the last guard just as the other two attacked the smaller dragons. Calamity took her target down almost immediately, but Jacob only managed to wound his.<br /> <br /> The rest of us rushed in as the fight began in earnest. Gawain and D joined the melee proper, while Julia and I held ourselves in reserve to provide support. <br /> <br /> Those big lizards never had a chance. In fact, we might have gotten away with hardly a scratch if Calamity hadn\u2019t gotten \u201ccareless\u201d again. She has a real tendency to go all-out when she attacks, leaving her vulnerable to her opponents. She took a pretty bad hit from the big dragon, but it wasn\u2019t enough to take her out of the fight, and a few seconds later it was all over.<br /> <br /> I did what I could to heal Calamity and Jacob; everyone else had pretty much escaped unscathed. D used her Leechfinger abilities to heal those wounds my Contracts missed, and within a few minutes we were all right as rain. Gawain and Jacob started talking about the things they could make from the dead dragons\u2019 hide (eww!), and D \u2013 no doubt sensing a chance to show off \u2013 picked up the huge beast and carried it into the Hedge. I accompanied her, of course\u2026 I just didn\u2019t stick too close to the disgusting bloody carcass as we made our way back.<br /> <br /> Calamity also thought it would be a good idea to bring one of the human guards back to the Dream House. The idea was to interrogate him in his dreams or something like that, just to see what he knew about the local Courts. There was a fair amount of discussion about this, as no changeling really likes confining another person against their will, but in the end we decided that it was a necessary evil. It proved useless, though\u2026 the mortals were all employed by a local security agency, and thought they had been hired to stand guard over a rare species of Komodo Dragon.<br /> <br /> Honestly! The things mortals will tell themselves to avoid seeing the truth!<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, the rest of the news was not so good. The computer we recovered from the club had a lot of information on the changing politics of the Lady by the Sea Freehold. Even worse, it contained information about the Table, which the nobles of the Hollywood Courts seem to lust after. I don\u2019t know what they want that unholy abomination for. We speculated that it was probably something to do with the \u201cGrand Maw,\u201d the Gentry they\u2019re supposed to be keeping as a captive, but to be honest I don\u2019t really care. They must not get it.<br /> <br /> Even more disturbing was the identity of their spy within the Freehold. It seems that the Hollywood Courts managed to capture one of the Director\u2019s spies and reprogram her to act as their instrument. She was incredibly cunning, though they were worried that some of her original memories were starting to show through, as she was starting to create dioramas which crudely resembled past events. She had been quite successful in her mission to insinuate herself into a position close to a powerful figure in the Freehold, but had been frustrated in that endeavor lately. And things had nearly come apart when her new directives had been overridden or side-stepped by members of the Freehold.<br /> <br /> So yeah, we\u2019re pretty sure they\u2019re talking about Desiree. Gawain is taking it hard; he knows her better than the rest of us, but none of us are happy with this revelation. For my part, I had been so sure that of the two of them Chalcedony was the one to watch. Desiree has always seemed so innocent and trusting\u2026 I wonder if this is a function of her cover personality, or if she\u2019s just <u>really</u> good at pretending?<br /> <br /> We\u2019re not sure what to do now. Gawain is insisting that we go to Desiree directly and give her the chance to make the right choice. Some of the others are not too sure about this plan. We were supposed to take this information straight to Madame Spidertoes, who after all sort of sponsored this whole endeavor. I can tell that Calamity and Jacob think this news is too big for us to sit on, and I can kind of see their point. I like to think the best of people, and I\u2019d really like to take Gawain\u2019s side on this debate, but\u2026 well, there\u2019s a lot at stake here, and we can\u2019t afford to make mistakes. Desiree has been a friend, and I truly hope that we can help her\u2026 but if her presence is going to threaten what the changelings of Malibu and Santa Monica have built, then I don\u2019t think we can afford to be <u>too</u> understanding.<br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei Grace</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T15:03:00-08:00","id":799819,"title":"","content":"<b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> The dance certainly was interesting. There were all sorts of costumes including an alien, with the projection of a woman\u2019s head on the face plate, Darth Vader, Strawberry Shortcake, which I\u2019m told is based on an old cartoon, Red Death, and The Question from DC comics. Charlotte even came dressed as Batgirl. Never thought I\u2019d see that. Makes a certain kind of sense though. Batman and his allies strike fear into the hearts of the villains and fear is what the Autumn Court is all about. Jolie as Strawberry Shortcake was almost too sweet. Not sure who the alien girl was or the Red Death for that matter. Don\u2019t really suppose it makes too much of a difference who was dressed as who. I knew what my friends were dressed as, what Luna was dressed as and could identify a lot of the people there. Ideally I would have liked to have been able to identify all of the party goers, but that I think is a holdover from my time with the Lady. She held balls, but you were not allowed to completely obscure your features. She had to be able to see who was who. She had a thing about that and made sure that her Knights walked through the crowd and spoke to those whose mask or costume might have been too elaborate for the Lady\u2019s tastes.<br /> <br /> So, it was like most balls that I\u2019ve been to. I am used to being on the sidelines and watching the people, which is what I did a lot of at this ball. I danced with Luna several times and other partners here and there. I even danced with Shi, who was dressed as Coyote. I couldn\u2019t resist. I liked the costume too much and it appealed to that side of me that enjoys tricks. For the most part though, I was a wallflower, and that suited me just fine. I don\u2019t think Luna minded all that much either. Besides, people-watching is fun.<br /> <br /> There is one thing that happened at the ball that concerned me. I didn\u2019t find out about it until a few minutes ago though. Insincere Marguerite just came to talk to me about something that happened last night/early this morning at the Masquerade. Apparently while at the ball Insincere Marguerite had a bit of a setback, or maybe it was something of a flashback? Anyway, she started talking to Felicity, and flirting with the other woman when she started feeling possessive of the sunlight lady. To be more specific, she started feeling much like herself when she was still in Arcadia, and this scared her. She want to go find Lorelei to talk to her and get help. Lori was understandably worried and after a bit she left to go talk to Felicity at Marguerite\u2019s request. Calamity then went over to her darkling sister\u2019s side and tried to help her calm down and come back to herself. I think it worked since I didn\u2019t notice too much of what happened at the ball, and likely would have if Insincere Marguerite had started acting too oddly. Apparently Calamity also mentioned the possibility that Bedlam may have been used on Marguerite. If that\u2019s the case does the person know what kind of reaction they\u2019re going to get or are they just taking a chance and trying to cause chaos? I wonder if the Handmaidens can cast Bedlam?<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite was understandably upset and more than a little shaken by what had happened. I don\u2019t blame her. I have found myself sliding more and more into my old mindset and it\u2019s more than a little disturbing how easy it is to do. I tend not to stay there too long, but it is something that I\u2019ve noticed. I tried to comfort Insincere Marguerite that she was not alone in this, and mentioned my own \u201cslipping\u201d on occasion. She in turn tried to be comforting to me, which is not exactly the response I was trying to elicit but I appreciated it nonetheless. I can only hope that knowing that she\u2019s not alone will help ease some of her anxiety.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Breakfast was more of the usual in most respects. Some of the guests were different however. Present for crepes and good company was Dark Kimberly, Flores, and Princess Jolie. Apparently Kimberly stayed with Insincere Marguerite, Flores was with Calamity, and the Princess was with Gawain. So everyone got to mix up the couples for the evening it seems. Even Lorelei slept with someone new, but would not tell us who it was. It seems that she promised not to say, and she kept her word. Some people started just listing off names trying to see if they got a reaction out of our pretty siren, but she was resolute in her silence. For me it doesn\u2019t really matter who Lori slept with last night. It won\u2019t change how we look at her and it might only embarrass or cause complications for her partner. There were other people guessing who other people\u2019s partners were as well, so it wasn\u2019t just Lori getting picked on. Again, unless someone is playing their partner false, it doesn\u2019t really matter to me who slept with who, but it was quite the discussion topic for \u201cSex Breakfast,\u201d as it had been dubbed some months ago. Anyhoo\u2026after a while the discussion wore down and Jolie offered to give Kimberly a ride home and the two of them left. That\u2019s when we started planning in earnest for the rest of the day\u2019s adventures.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Well, our little foray to the closed down strip club went better than expected. The plan that we\u2019d come up with was that Calamity, Insincere Marguerite and myself would sneak in and knock out the humans that were there with chloroform, then call in the rest of our folks with our newly acquired Bluetooth devices. Well, we decided that going in through the roof would be the best bet, and the three of us climbed the building. Insincere Marguerite made it look like it was nothing. Even Calamity made an easy task of it. I didn\u2019t have too much trouble, but then it\u2019s not my first time free climbing a building. So, we all made it to the top and snuck in the top floor. Insincere Marguerite handed out cloths with chloroform on them and we went to work. Marguerite made her way downstairs while Calamity and I took out the guys on the second floor. Just a moment with the cloth and they were out like a light. We then snuck downstairs and found that the main room had a fairly large dragon in it, of all things, and two smaller dragons. So, Calamity got her wish, to fight a dragon. Calamity and I went in and attacked the smaller dragons. We each took one. Calamity killed hers in one hit and I wounded mine.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite knocked out the last guard and let the others know that they could join in anytime. Gawain was unsurprisingly the first to come through those doors. Things got a bit confused at that point. I know that Marguerite did her magic to slow down the big dragon. I can\u2019t remember if that was before or after I tried to hit it since I couldn\u2019t see her at all. Mine was only a glancing blow. Then since I\u2019d turned my back on the little guy, he attacked me. His wasn\u2019t the strongest hit I\u2019ve taken, but it wasn\u2019t too bad either. It did burn though, in a way that knife wounds generally don\u2019t. So that was interesting. Anyhoo\u2026Gawain got a decent hit in on the big one after it hit his girl, and then Calamity finished it off. I then proceeded to help take the little guy that was on me out. I was a little concerned to see Calamity going all out in a fight like that again. She devoted her whole self to the attack and when it struck back she had no defense. That dragon left a pretty bad wound too. Lucky for us we had Lori on hand to heal us of our wounds. I wasn\u2019t quite feeling it yet besides the slight burning. I had used that Winter Court contract to push the effects of wounds off until the end of the fight, and they hadn\u2019t quite kicked in yet when Lorelei came by and patched me up. Still haven\u2019t taken that for granted. Having a healer on hand is pretty damn nice. Just sayin\u2019.<br /> <br /> I will admit that I did not feel all that effective in the combat. I did land the killing blow on the small dragon, but only after it had been hit multiple times by me and others. Even from stealth I could not kill it, and that has always been my specialty. Okay, that was more of Rook\u2019s specialty, but I was pretty decent at it myself. I can\u2019t help but feel like my skills are slipping. Maybe I need to spend some time in the hedge just hunting and honing my abilities? I\u2019ve gotten out of practice and it showed today. How can I adequately protect my motley if I am not effective in a fight?<br /> <br /> A part of me is upset by the fact that I\u2019m not as effective a killer, and another part of me doesn\u2019t mind in the least. The part that misses the killing has always been small, but it\u2019s become bigger lately. Over the past few months I\u2019ve noticed that my reactions to things are not as emotional as they used to be. I need to hold onto the part of me that doesn\u2019t mind losing the ability to kill so easily. I know that is the person that I\u2019ve been trying to be. That is the good Jacob. The man that cares for his family and friends, who remembers what real warmth is. That feeling that spreads out from your chest and makes you feel alive. I don\u2019t want to be that cold killer anymore, but sometimes, just sometimes it seems like it would be so easy to be Rime again.<br /> <br /> I honestly don\u2019t know what\u2019s come over me lately. I don\u2019t think the others have noticed me slipping, but that\u2019s mostly because I haven\u2019t shown much of the Rime side of me recently. In this fight at the strip club a good part of me, the Rime side, didn\u2019t really see what was wrong with killing the humans. I know, and he knows, that it would cause complications and I\u2019m afraid that might be the reason that I went along with the chloroform so easily. I don\u2019t know. Was my decision made because it was more convenient for us to not have the cops called in, or because killing innocent humans would be wrong? Goddess help me, I don\u2019t want to be Rime again. Not really.<br /> <br /> Okay\u2026so our other objective besides taking out the Hedge beast was to retrieve the computer, which we did. Insincere Marguerite grabbed it while the rest of us were finishing off the dragons. We took the machine back to the house, but made a trip through the hedge to bring the dragons back with us. We didn\u2019t want to leave the bodies behind, and Gawain and I agreed that we could probably make some pretty good stuff out of dragon hide. I think the idea appealed to our resident Green Knight. So, Gawain and De la Rocha picked up the dragons and we walked through the Hedge until we got to the Hollow. We also brought back one of the unconscious guards. Calamity was planning on delving into the man\u2019s dream to see what he knew about the whole situation. As it turns out the man was hired by a company called Carson Security Limited and he was there to guard some rare komodo dragons. He was not ensorcelled and had no idea what he was actually looking after. So, it turned out that trying to get information from the guard was a bust. He essentially knew nothing.<br /> <br /> The computer however yielded more interesting information. We found out from the machine that the Hollywood Courts had found out about the Table and that an alien girl had brought in out of the Hedge. They were very interested in acquiring it for themselves, though they made no mention of an operator in their files. So chances are that they know what the Table can do, but not that it requires a specific type of person to control it. There was no mention of Andromeda or acquiring her at any point, so it stands to reason that they don\u2019t have all the information that they would need to use the damned thing. They\u2019d probably figure it out though. They are not idiots. We just have to make sure that they don\u2019t get their hands on it. On the plus side they know that the Autumn Court has the Table or has access to it. Yeah, doesn\u2019t seem like a positive thing, but the problem for them is that they are terrified of Madame Spidertoes. From my limited experience with the woman I\u2019d say that they have good reason to be afraid of her. She is old and powerful and really doesn\u2019t like it when people mess with what she sees as hers.<br /> <br /> The other interesting thing that we found out from the computer is that the Hollywood Courts have a spy working for them. Not that she knows she\u2019s working for them, as far as we can tell. This spy is supposed to be one of the most successful and dangerous of the Director\u2019s loyalists; one who was sent to infiltrate the Hollywood Courts. She was caught and brainwashed into believing her original cover story and rewriting her \u201cscripts\u201d to be more along the lines of what they wanted her to do. It seems originally that the loyalist was supposed to get close to the monarchs of the Hollywood Court and gather intel on them. I\u2019m not sure what else she was supposed to do. But when she came to The Lady by the Sea freehold she started doing just that and tried to get close to the monarchs. She made some good progress with Jolie, but was thwarted by an old love returning. Yeah, I\u2019m talking about Desiree. The computer even makes note of their spy\u2019s scripts being erased. I\u2019m assuming that\u2019s when Gawain helped her remove the \u201cswitch\u201d that still remained in her mind. The files also mentioned that the spy is coming closer and closer to remembering who she actually is and what was done to her. I guess that explains the creepy manikins that she has surrounding her bed. She\u2019s making a diorama of sorts to show what happened, but so far it\u2019s all been on a subconscious level. I believe Gawain wants Desiree to come to the Dream House so we can talk to her, I think he wants to do it in dreams, and tell her who she actually is and what was done to her.<br /> <br /> I am personally not sure what he hopes to accomplish with this idea. Yeah, I can understand wanting her to be on the same page as we are when we talk, but if she is supposed to be the most clever and successful infiltrator that the Director has in his employ then we would be remiss in underestimating her. I personally think that flat out telling her is a bad idea. I will have to make sure that the \u201cdream talk\u201d happens in a secure room and that if anything happens to threaten Gawain or anyone else that she is put down. I understand that Gawain wants to rehabilitate Desiree and make her come over to our side voluntarily, but I\u2019m not so sure that it\u2019s going to go as smoothly as all that. Sure I changed sides and maybe he\u2019s thinking that my transformation was simple. Truth is, it wasn\u2019t. I had only defied the Lady on one thing, and that was to return Delight to Her. I hadn\u2019t really been planning on completely betraying her at that point. At least I don\u2019t think I was. It took the Lady showing me her displeasure to fully make me realize what kind of a monster that I\u2019d been serving. She nearly killed me on several occasions and hadn\u2019t even finished what she\u2019d started out to do. It took that for me to really turn away from Her. I was terrified of her, of what she would do to me. Does Gawain honestly believe that he\u2019s going to just talk Desiree out of serving her true master? If I found out that I\u2019d been sent to California by the Lady and had been tortured and brainwashed into being their puppet and found out about it, there is no way in hell that I would decide to switch sides. Yeah, Hollywood and Santa Monica are different cities but it\u2019s still \u2018the world.\u2019 Arcadia was who she served. Her Keeper is who she came here for. It\u2019s not going to matter that it was Hollywood and not Santa Monica that did the torturing and brainwashing. I\u2019m sure she\u2019ll act appropriately thankful to us for saving her from the Hollywood Court, but it won\u2019t be real. She is supposed to be one of the best, and I\u2019m sure that if we follow through with Gawain\u2019s plan we\u2019ll find out just how good she really is.<br /> <br /> As I write this Calamity is calling Spidertoes to tell her the edited version of what we found on the computer. It was decided that we would tell her about the Hollywood Courts wanting to find out more about the Table and how to acquire it. She\u2019s going to tell the elder Changeling that we are still going through the information and will let her know if we find anything else of note. I can understand in some way not wanting to tell Spidertoes about Desiree just yet. If we did, Desiree would be scooped up and detained before we could blink. I understand that Gawain and the others want to give her a chance to come to our side willingly before she is locked up. I\u2019m not a fan of being locked up anywhere, but it is much preferable to a lot of other fates, so I say we should let Desiree be taken. I don\u2019t know if we could contain Desiree if she decided to leave. She might just convince us all that she is still our friend, and I don\u2019t know how much of that will be truth.<br /> <br /> I know about the lies. I know about telling people what they wanted to hear so you could get the desired result. I did it, on many occasions. I was good at my job. I tricked several people into coming to the Lady\u2019s realm and while there I tricked even more people into following me somewhere I could leave them to freeze and die. I could do all of that with words. Who\u2019s to say that Desiree can\u2019t do the same?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> <u>The Masquerade: </u><br /> <br /> The Masquerade went well. Mostly.<br /> <br /> There were problems right off, when Calamity accidentally angered Madam Spidertoes over Lowjack threatening I. It was a reasonable mistake. She was hoping Spidertoes would intervene with the Handmaidens, which was good. Unfortunately, Spidertoes latched onto a Darkling being threatened, which was\u2026not ideal. I myself moved to intervene when warned. I talked her down, mostly honestly, and felt relived. I was in a good mood so looked for Felicity. Happily.<br /> <br /> Felicity. Sweet Felicity. Soft Felicity. She was nervous when I saw her. I kissed her, and scolded her for running out on I months ago. She reminded I she was a short walk from the Dream House this whole time, had I really wanted to see her. Apparently.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not sure why the urges came. The confusion, I mean. I needed her right then, and touched her, but she looked quizzically at I when I was touching her, then laughed a little and nervously asked \u201cwho are you supposed to be?\u201d I realized, then, there was a problem. Communicating became difficult. I was nervous, now. Women were usually either charmed or upset and this point, but Felicity was somewhere between amused and worried. I kissed her quickly and fled. Helplessly.<br /> <br /> I ran up to Lorelei and tried to explain I was having problems. Her smile faded and she started asking I if I was okay. I attempted to communicate I was having dark thoughts, like we had discussed, and I needed her to help keep I separated from Felicity. I am not sure what I actually said, or what she understood exactly, but she looked very worried and said she would talk to Felicity. Then Calamity was talking to I as Lori walked away and looking concerned. I remember asking if I was acting normal. I think I did this more than once. I know as I thought about Felicity I wanted to seek her out. Urgently.<br /> <br /> Calamity and I ended up in the bathroom. While I stroked the mirror and greedily talked about Felicity, she was telling I about needing to regain control. I think. I looked in the mirror and saw it. While Insincere Marguerite held her head high, alone in the dark, with her pretties, she was a grasping, hungry, base creature. I had left that in Arcadia, I thought but here it was, staring fish-eyed at I in the mirror! It was a shock! Calamity sized on I\u2019s look of fear, I think\u2026I don\u2019t clearly remember the discussion. I remember\u2026coming to? Being able to talk clearly? I remember Calamity looking a bit relieved. Fortunately.<br /> <br /> My body tried to feel shame. I refused. Still, it was troubling. This did not happen last time I saw Felicity, or when fooling around with White Maria. I don\u2019t know what happened, but I will find out. Definitely.<br /> <br /> I avoided Felicity from there on out, and did not see Lori until the next morning. Once I had I\u2019s composure, I wound up flirting with Dark Kimberly in a Darth Vader outfit. We returned to the Dream House via the mirror and spent the night. The grasping horror stayed at bay. Insincere Marguerite was her partner all night.<br /> <br /> Sex breakfast went well. Jolie spent the night with Gawain, so I know he had a good time. Lori never fessed up but she bedded Joan. I think they were both winners. Calamity spent the night with Flores so her time was also well spent, and De La Rocha apparently did with Sandoval, who is handsome. Jacob spent the night with Luna, and Julia apparently did with Oleander\u2026I missed the specifics but she apparently implied it. I never saw Oleander there. I do know Oleander was showing interest in Julia before tensions raised again, so not a shock. Dark Kimberly was, if anything, a bit smug about her partner. She and De La Rocha did not argue, but did not speak, either. It was still less tense than with White Maria. Fortunately.<br /> <br /> I am troubled, however, by I\u2019s reversion. I have been getting stronger, more potent. But I remember more. I remember the monster in the dark. I remember being\u2026ashamed\u2026of how I really was, and when I crawled from the darkness, where I could be seen, I held I\u2019s head high. Now, it comes back as I approach Arcadian power. Is that it? Or did something, someone, bring that base creature out?<br /> <br /> I am troubled.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>The Raid: </u><br /> <br /> The raid on \u201cFoxy Boxes\u201d was successful. Fortunately.<br /> <br /> It was a two level building (technically three, but the third was empty) with four human guards and a Dragon in the big central room with two very small Dragons. Jacob, Calamity and I infiltrated the building and set about knocking unconscious the guards with the sleeping cloth. I would like to note that I\u2019s Motley-mates did an excellent job; they were quiet enough, they took down the guards with care, and compromised nothing. Even Calamity, with her uptick of bloodlust, showed herself to be reliable and did no more than told. Within a few minutes of I\u2019s sweep, three fourths of the guards were down. Successfully.<br /> <br /> Stage two was dealing with the Dragons and the human guard in the room. I knocked out the last human guard and Calamity killed her small dragon while Jacob injured his. With the enraged bellow, Gawain destroyed the front door and we entered. I used I\u2019s Darkling powers to weaken the greater Dragon, and everyone attacked it. Gawain finished it off, with that oversized German sword of his through they all contributed. Calamity and Jacob were hurt, but Lorelei and De La Rocha (with the Dragon\u2019s stolen life) healed them. Skillfully.<br /> <br /> De La Rocha showed off her strength removing the dead Dragon, and they took a human while I took the files. Jacob skinned the Dragon, for materials for Gawain. Gawain, Calamity and I interrogated the guard to no real result\u2026he had no idea anything supernatural was going on. The computer told us more. Unfortunately.<br /> <br /> Spidertoes had wondered what the Court of Fallen Stars could want with our Freehold, and we found it: The Table. The Damn Table again. Of course, Spidertoes and the Warlock of Night believe the Court of Fallen Stars has a Gentry prisoner, so what they would use the table for is obvious. More disturbing, or perhaps disheartening, was the identity of their spy. Sadly.<br /> <br /> As it turned out Desiree was an unknowing spy for that Court. She had been a loyalist who told them a story much like she did us, but it was a lie, she had sold out her fellow spy for a better chance. She manipulated her way up but was caught, and they used advanced brainwashing to make her their agent. Also, they discovered a way to circumvent the Director\u2019s \u201cScripts\u201d used to ensure that his \u201cActors\u2019 play their parts regardless of their loyalty, and changed her to work for them. She half remembered this, making dioramas of her brainwashing. Frighteningly.<br /> <br /> We know from their records the script was removed, but also altered. We do not know who altered it. The list of suspects who could have is short: Darke. Twich, Spidertoes (I assume), and maybe Shi or Moon. Maybe.<br /> <br /> But the dioramas are getting more accurate, and she may be beginning to remember. If she does she will remember who she truly is, and her full personality will return. I assume. We assume. We do not know for certain. And as she is apparently highly skilled at lying, we may not know. It may have even already returned. Frighteningly.<br /> <br /> So Gawain wants to talk to her, maybe in a dream, and figure out what side she will be on after she discovers who she really is. This is hard on him. I do not envy Gawain, he is a good man. We will see how his code holds up under this. I suspect he will continue to be a good man. I have faith in him.<br /> <br /> My role in this complete, I return to the shadows. I\u2019s mind is still full. Completely.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XLVI</i><br /> <br /> Desiree\u2019s secret is out. Was the revelation surprising for you?<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite managed to Parkour all the way to the top of the club. Parkour is powerful with five Athletics. She also impeded the dragon with the final Darkness Contract Clause.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d like to say a word on her using chloroform, the \u201cSleeping Cloth.\u201d It\u2019s use has been more cinematic than realistic, but she has only so far used it on unsuspecting humans, really. I\u2019m not going to let it be used as an ultimate knockout ability or anything.<br /> <br /> Not much else mechanical going on. The Masquerade was fun. If you have any Comments or Questions, as always they are welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T00:11:29-08:00","id":800323,"title":"","content":"I'll admit I was alos betting on Chalcedony being the spy, given all the oddities everybody noticed about her.<br /> Lowjack threatening Marguerite also surprised me. he must know it would the motley and their now quite numerous allies against him, for little direct gain that I can see.<br /> Was Insincere Marguerite's freak out brouught up by a Clarity check?<br /> I noticed that most of the Motley's members don't seem to have many close relationships with mortals. Especially Insincere Marguerite. Is it a deliberate choice?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T00:44:29-08:00","id":800360,"title":"","content":"Well, Chalcedony also has secrets of her own.<br /> <br /> It's complicated. Part of it is because a woman he sees as essentially his daughter nearly died. The problem is not &quot;he made a dumb move&quot; so much as &quot;he made a move inconsistent with his history as a cunning and shrewd politician.&quot; His plan is likley to work, but was more antagonistic than needed, and somehow Insincere Marguerite was collateral damage. I wonder why? It seems unlikely to be random....<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite's issue was a clash of her greater Wyrd and close proximity to the stand-in for Yvette, a different yet somewhat similar looking proud Treasured Fairest. While she cultivates the air of a gentleman thief, at the same time she has a grasping, Gollum-like side...she is a Darkling, not a Fairest, after all. At the Ball, she was totally unprepared for it. When it came up in tonight's session, she was better able to keep it at bay. Like Calamity and Jacob's issues, it is totally player controlled.<br /> <br /> Some of that is my fault. The PCs are friends with a lot of dancers in the club. I have some pics for dancers. However, we seem to gloss over that a lot in game, beyond little things like brief conversations with Lori or stuff like how they call Insincere Marguerite &quot;The Lioness.&quot; So they are there, I just do kinda a poor job of representing that, compared to <b>Geist</b> or <b>Demon</b>.<br /> <br /> Thanks much for the feedback. If you have any further questions let me know. We are approaching session 50 and quite pleased about it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T13:16:29-08:00","id":800703,"title":"","content":"It's funny you mention the Gollum-like behavior. A while back I pictured Gollum as a darkling and the Ring as a his Keeper in artifact form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T13:56:41-08:00","id":810800,"title":"","content":"Desiree is a Loyalist. But she does not realize she is a Loyalist. She will know soon enough, but what then?<br /> <br /> <i>Session LXVII</i><br /> <b><br /> Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> Nov 2nd, afternoon<br /> <br /> Well, that went kinda better than expected, considering Desiree showed up covered in blood with a big gash on her face. The Hollywood Courts work fast, at least that\u2019s, you know, who we figure sent the mortal in a trenchcoat with a bullet and the message \u2018the game is up\u2019. She was really shaken up, but had managed to heal herself enough to not bleed out. Lori healed her up the rest of the way, and we got her all cleaned up before we sprung the news on her.<br /> <br /> We didn\u2019t wind up going into dreams. She was a little uncomfortable with it and I guess it is a little weird. Things just make more sense, you know, there in dreams. People make more sense. But I wasn\u2019t gonna push her, so Lori took over. Desiree managed to figure out where she was going before she got there. She had a little bit of a disconcerting smile behind her eyes before it all hit her, but her upsetedness seemed really, you know, genuine.<br /> <br /> She told us what she remembered. She\u2019d been a meek and quiet girl, before she was taken, and had come to LA to make it big. The city had treated her poorly, and she\u2019d turned to prostitution and drugs. The Director had helped her out, brought her up. Given her her big break. That was why she was so, you know, loyal, why she didn\u2019t want to betray him.<br /> <br /> It made sense, and to be fair, as far as carrying out her stated mission, we actually kinda didn\u2019t want her to. She was supposed to get the Grand Maw out of their control. By killing it, preferably, but anything to not let them have it. That\u2019s something we can all get behind - even those of us who didn\u2019t know anybody still trapped on the other side of the Hedge, the thought of what a creature like the Grand Maw would do after it ate all of Arcadia is kinda, you know, terrifying. Desiree was super scared about it. I even used my Contracts of Potential, and stopping the Hollywood Courts was her primary motivation. They already had black marks in my book with the whole brainwashing thing so I\u2019m with her on this.<br /> <br /> Everybody else was... well, not on her side, so much, but OK with helping her with this bit at least. Calamity even got Dahlia to sign off on promises that Desiree wouldn\u2019t be killed as long as she helped us against the Hollywood Courts. She got those promises before we talked to Desiree which annoyed me a little, but Lori pulled her aside, with a little bit of a, you know, annoyed look herself, so I assume she handled the fussing at.<br /> <br /> The others were, you know, a little distracted too. Insincere Marguerite was really withdrawn - Jacob said it was because she was feeling like she was regressing, you know, acting like she did in Arcadia? Specifically about Felicity. So Julia wanted to kill her and Lori was worried about all of them and De la Roche came in later but tried to help everybody stay calm. Lori wound up going to talk with Felicity, since she was getting worried with Insincere Marguerite not answering her texts. De la Roche stuck nearby, holding Insincere Marguerite close.<br /> <br /> Calamity took Jacob aside while they were off with that, so I took Desiree to the Hedge House. It seemed like the safest place, since they\u2019d at least started with human assassins. I may have been a little overly excited to show her my workshop, but she, you know, seemed interested. Eventually, everyone but Calamity and Jacob joined us. Well, even those two did for a short bit to get Desiree\u2019s keys so they could check out her apartment and take her car back, to put Hollywood off the trail. The rest of us played cards and told Desiree about the fight with the giant spider when we first found the House. Insincere Marguerite seemed to cheer up a little and kept playing up Lori\u2019s role in the fight, despite Lori\u2019s valiant attempts at self deprecation.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, Calamity and Jacob had an exciting time, apparently. They figured out it had been a really serious wound, enough to be fatal judging by the amount of blood, if she didn\u2019t, you know, have healing magic. The pair had hoped to try and arrange it so maybe the Hollywood Courts would think their first attempt succeeded. But the shotgun trap they\u2019d rigged on her bedroom door indicated they\u2019d already figured out it hadn\u2019t. Thankfully, Calamity is super awesome and caught on super quick, so she foiled their plans, at least as far as the shotgun was concerned. So now we have a new shotgun.<br /> <br /> Calamity and I stayed up all night, Desiree nestled against me. Desiree tried to stay up, but sleep caught her after not too long. Julia and Insincere Marguerite stayed in the Hedge House with us, but they went off to bed. Lori had gotten super drunk on Hedge wine, that apparently tasted like Johnny Walker. I don\u2019t think our provisions table had ever given us booze before, so that was interesting. Apparently Flores can make Hedge alcohol too, something that makes you have vivid dreams that she got the recipe for from Oleander. It sounds interesting, and can even get her drunk. Anyways, Lori and De la Roche went back to the Dream House, along with Jacob, to sleep it off. Well, I think Jacob stayed up, you know.<br /> <br /> Nothing happened overnight, and sex breakfast time came after not too long. I grilled some dragon steaks, with a spicy rub and some potato wedges to match. The meat had a kinda fishy feel to it, it was very interesting to work with. It turned out awesome, if I do say so myself, and the other did too, to be fair. I\u2019ll have to remember this recipe. And go dragon hunting more often.<br /> <br /> The afternoon has been fun, for the most part. We discussed how long it took/would take various people to get Julia out of her clothes. We talked a lot about GI Joe and Jem &amp; the Holograms. That got Desiree a little out of her shell, she got really into it. Even the crazy idea that the Misfits were better terrorists than Cobra. OK, so maybe Calamity had some good points, but still... Anyway, we managed to convince Insincere Marguerite to perform tomorrow too. That last took Flores\u2019 help. She also offered to come over and help with positioning for whenever we had our motley-wide orgy, cause, you know, that\u2019s a thing, I guess. I mean, I didn\u2019t have a problem with it. She couldn\u2019t talk Jacob or Julia into it though. We did learn too that even Flores has a line. It\u2019s Spanish speaking Kermit puppets. I\u2019m not sure I really wanna know where that came up or what it had to do with Spaghetti-Os.<br /> <br /> But Flores was over to cheer Desiree up. She\u2019s her other really good friend, you know, and Desiree really wanted to let her know what was up. She told Flores about everything but the loyalist thing. Flores took it well - her main takeaway was wondering if the mannikins would be gone now, cause they \u2018got weird\u2019. Yes, even when Desiree turned them to face the other way. She really did help bring some cheer to Desiree, that and the GI Joe talk.<br /> <br /> She was also right there with me when Sandoval showed up. He was there to tell Desiree, and those of us she was willing to have hear, that the Monarchs wanted her in custody. Protective custody, he clarified, cause she\u2019s clearly at risk, and too important an \u2018asset\u2019 to lose. When Desiree said she wanted a deposition and soon, so she wouldn\u2019t be a priority target, Sandoval suggested it would be better if she stays more valuable to the Monarchs. It sure sounded like a threat at first, but he seemed taken aback when Flores and I got upset, so I think he was sincerely trying to look out for her. Still, I certainly hope the Freehold won\u2019t withdraw their protection from her just cause she\u2019s <u>already</u> helped them out. She has my protection anyway. Desiree was certain regardless that she\u2019d rather have Hollywood off her back, at least the relatively sane ones. Some might still go after her, but there won\u2019t be any real reason to, and some definite potential drawbacks. Anyways, Desiree was very sure the Monarchs won\u2019t kill her, and she wanted what she knew to be available, no matter what happened to her.<br /> <br /> Well, I\u2019m gonna make sure nothing happens, nothing I can stop. She asked, last night, how many times we\u2019ve sheltered people. I guess it is kinda a thing we do, you know? She does wanna stay mobile for now, and be a moving target, after the deposition tonight, which makes sense. I haven\u2019t asked if she wants me there for the deposition. I... it\u2019s probably sad, that I don\u2019t trust the Monarchs as much as Desiree does. It\u2019s not really fair, I guess, but I don\u2019t really trust them to do the right thing. When Sandoval said what he did, it was easy to assume that the Monarchs sent him to imply that without leverage, they\u2019d want her dead. Maybe too easy. Anyways, I\u2019m not gonna crowd her, you know, but I hope she knows she doesn\u2019t have to do any of this alone.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Okay, so apparently confronting a relatively close friend about being a Loyalist and a sleeper spy for the Hollywood Courts can\u2019t be simple. I suppose I shouldn\u2019t be too surprised about that.<br /> <br /> Desiree showed up on our doorstep a short time after Gawain called her. She looked like Hell; there was blood all over her and what looked suspiciously like a gunshot wound on the side of her face. She told us in a voice somewhere between deadpan and frantic that as she\u2019d been leaving her apartment to answer Gawain\u2019s invitation, a man in a trench coat had approached her in the hallway, said something cornball like \u201cthe game is up,\u201d and shot her in the face.<br /> <br /> She used the last of her strength to push around him and ran to her car, using Contracts to heal the worst of the damage and leaving a trail of blood behind her. She was obviously just barely holding it together, and wasn\u2019t up to the task of healing herself further. I did what I could to help her, and we got her cleaned up before breaking the news to her.<br /> <br /> She took it\u2026 well. Surprisingly well. <u>Disturbingly</u> well, if I\u2019m being honest with myself. As we slowly explained what we had learned from the spies\u2019 computer, a strange calm settled over her. Her only real reaction was to say, at a lull in the conversation, \u201cI guess I really am the Loyalist everyone said I was after all.\u201d It was kind of chilling. After we had finished our tale, she looked each of us in the eye for a few seconds, and then asked what we intended to do with her.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat depends on you,\u201d Gawain said charitably. I glanced briefly at Calamity, and she nodded ever so slightly. Charity is all well and good, and I don\u2019t think any of us really wanted to hurt Desiree if we didn\u2019t have to\u2026 but it was nice to know that Calamity was watching her, ready to act if necessary.<br /> <br /> Desiree spun her tale well. She talked about how she had been very shy and unassuming when she had first come to the west coast hoping to make her fortune. The cruel realities of the big city had crushed her dreams quickly, and she had fallen in with a bad crowd. She\u2019d gotten hooked on drugs, and eventually had been forced to resort to prostitution to feed her habits.<br /> <br /> That was what she was like when the Director found her. He had been kind, supportive, and encouraging. He raised her up out of the muck and showed her how to reach her true potential. He made her into something beautiful and pure when she thought she had lost that part of herself forever. In short, she\u2019s a Loyalist because the Director <u>earned</u> her Loyalty.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a good story. It\u2019s perfectly reasonable and understandable. I wonder how much of it we can believe\u2026<br /> <br /> She claims that she was sent to Hollywood by the Director in order to remove the Grand Maw from the Court of Stars\u2019 control\u2026 ideally by killing it or otherwise destroying it. The Director believes that the Hollywood Courts intend to brainwash the Grand Maw in some way and then turn it loose in Arcadia. The presumed goal of such a plan would be the ultimate destruction of the Gentry, and maybe of Arcadia itself.<br /> <br /> Now, anyone who knows me can attest that I\u2019m no fan of the True Fae, but that plan\u2026 it\u2019s not just insane, it\u2019s<u> monstrous</u>. We have no way of knowing if there are benevolent Fae out there, for one thing\u2026 those members of the Gentry who simply mind their own business and don\u2019t hassle mortals at all. There\u2019s also the question of all the innocent Changelings who are still trapped in Arcadia, like Missy and Jane. What would happen to them if the Hollywood Courts have their way? And finally, if the Grand Maw is as powerful and voracious as everyone says\u2026 what would it do <u>after</u> it devoured Arcadia? Would it turn its eyes back on the world? And if so\u2026 how would we stop it?<br /> <br /> Suffice to say, we were all more than a little shocked to discover that our own interests and those of the nefarious Director might coincide. Calamity wandered off for a bit while we were all digesting this. I assumed at the time that she just wanted to be alone while she processed what Desiree was saying. After about ten minutes, however, she rejoined the rest of us and told us that she had been in contact with Dahlia about this situation, and that the Winter Court was prepared to offer Desiree guarantees of her safety in exchange for all the information she could give us on Hollywood.<br /> <br /> It sounded like a pretty sweet deal, and Desiree was quick to go for it. I had other concerns about the situation, however, and pointedly asked Calamity if I could speak with her privately. When the two of us were alone, I expressed my dismay.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou told Dahlia about her? And about what we discovered at the strip club?\u201d I asked in shock.<br /> <br /> Calamity nodded. \u201cI had to,\u201d she said simply.<br /> <br /> I shook my head. \u201cWe got that intel from Spidertoes,\u201d I reminded her, \u201cand we haven\u2019t even told <u>her</u> about Desiree yet. She\u2019s not going to like the fact that you went around her back on this.\u201d<br /> <br /> Calamity nodded. \u201cI know,\u201d she said quietly, \u201cand I\u2019ll take the blame for that. But I\u2019m pledge-bound to report any information that poses a clear threat to the Freehold to Dahlia immediately. I don\u2019t think anyone can argue that this qualifies.\u201d<br /> <br /> Okay, so I had to concede the point in that case. We headed back to meet the others and found that the social dynamic of the room had changed somewhat. Gawain was still trying to calm Desiree, but something odd was going on between Marguerite and Julia. The former seemed really tense\u2026 almost twitchy. Julia, on the other hand, was positively<u> fuming</u>.<br /> <br /> While we tried to figure out what to do with Desiree tonight, Marguerite sort of clung to me, like I was a life preserver or something. I think I started to figure out what was going on around that point, and after a few minutes I pulled her into a secluded corner and spoke softly to her.<br /> <br /> \u201cAre you okay, Insincere Marguerite?\u201d I asked with a concerned look. \u201cIs it Felicity again?\u201d<br /> <br /> She didn\u2019t say anything, but nodded, and showed me a text on her phone. It was from Felicity, all right, and it was pretty obviously suggesting that the two of them meet up for an evening of fun. I sighed. I thought I\u2019d made things pretty clear at the masquerade ball, but apparently this was a situation which required me to discard subtlety entirely and spell things out.<br /> <br /> Marguerite looked at me with something like desperation in her eyes. I took her by the shoulders and kissed her hard. When I pulled away, I stared directly into her eyes. \u201cStay here,\u201d I said as firmly as I could. \u201cStay with Julia. You need to be with her right now. I\u2019m going to go have a talk with Felicity, to explain the situation. We\u2019ll talk more when I get back.\u201d Marguerite nodded, but still didn\u2019t say anything.<br /> <br /> I spoke briefly with D and Julia before I left, telling them to watch Marguerite, and not to let her leave the house if they could help it. They both agreed. I pretty much had to physically hand Marguerite over to Julia, actually. D was not happy about me going to speak to Felicity alone, which I had to admit sort of made sense with everything else that was happening, but I (very reasonably) pointed out that I\u2019d probably be safer while I <u>wasn\u2019t</u> in the house with the Loyalist who\u2019d been targeted for murder by the Hollywood Courts.<br /> <br /> A few minutes later I rang the bell at Felicity\u2019s house. She answered the door in a very fetching (and very brief) robe, and smiled warmly when she recognized me. She invited me in and offered me wine, and for a minute there I had to stop, take stock, and remind myself of why I was there.<br /> <br /> \u201cThis is about Marguer- <u>Insincere</u> Marguerite, isn\u2019t it?\u201d she asked with a slight roll of her eyes. \u201cIs she okay? I\u2019ve been texting her, but she hasn\u2019t responded.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019s safe,\u201d I assured her, \u201cbut, well\u2026 I think we need to have a more frank discussion about her situation. I didn\u2019t want to say too much at the masquerade, because there were too many inquisitive people around.\u201d<br /> <br /> Felicity nodded, the two of us sat on her sofa, and she beckoned for me to continue.<br /> <br /> \u201cIn Arcadia,\u201d I began, wondering how much I should tell her, \u201cMarguerite was owned by a Gentry thief. They had a good relationship, and Marguerite was more like her apprentice than her prisoner. The Gentry taught her how to escape notice and how to make off with pretty baubles belonging to other people. Sometimes they stole changelings\u2026 never mortals from the world, you understand, but changelings who already belonged to other Gentry.\u201d<br /> <br /> Felicity grimaced. \u201cI think I see where this is going,\u201d she said dully.<br /> <br /> \u201cInsincere Marguerite developed a taste for a particular type of Changeling\u2026 specifically the Treasured kith of the Fairest seeming. In short, people like you, Felicity. She didn\u2019t just desire them\u2026 she felt an obsessive need to own and control them.\u201d<br /> <br /> Felicity sighed. \u201cI thought she\u2019d been acting a bit odd,\u201d she admitted. \u201cSo her desire for me isn\u2019t real?\u201d<br /> <br /> I shook my head. \u201cI didn\u2019t say that. It\u2019s just that at the moment your presence is bringing back the wrong sort of memories for her. You\u2019re bringing out parts of her that she\u2019d rather repress.\u201d I let that sit in the air for a while. \u201cI\u2019m sorry, Felicity, but I think it would be best if you kept your distance for a while. At least until this passes.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cI understand,\u201d she said sadly. \u201cIt\u2019s just that\u2026 well, keep this under your hat, but it\u2019s pretty likely that Jolie is going to ask me to be her Consort soon, and I was sort of hoping to see where things went with Insincere Marguerite before I gave her my answer. She swore a few months ago that she would convince me to join the Night Court within a year, and\u2026 I thought it might be fun to let her try.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled. \u201cCongratulations,\u201d I said, maybe a little less enthusiastically than I could have. Felicity arched an eyebrow, and I felt obliged to explain a little. \u201cSorry, I\u2019m happy for you. For both of you. It\u2019s just that\u2026 last Spring I was where you are now. Jolie asked me to be her Consort, and\u2026 I had to say no. I had just started seeing D, and I didn\u2019t want to screw things up with her. I don\u2019t regret my decision, exactly, but\u2026 well, sometimes I wonder about what might have been. Jolie\u2019s a wonderful woman.\u201d<br /> <br /> Felicity nodded. \u201cI only left her before because of her\u2026 little problem. Now that it\u2019s been taken care of, I\u2019m starting to remember why we got together in the first place.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, congratulations,\u201d I said again, with a little more feeling this time. \u201cI wish you both the best. And I\u2019m sorry my visit had to be such a downer. I\u2019d like to see more of you, Felicity, you seem like a cool person. We should get together some time and just hang out or something.\u201d<br /> <br /> She gave me a warm smile. \u201cI\u2019d like that,\u201d she said a little huskily. I had a brief mental image of myself lying back on a bed with Felicity on one side of me and Jolie on the other, and I felt the heat rise in my cheeks. That\u2019s a scenario which bears thinking about, though I\u2019ll have to wait a while before I make any moves in that direction. I wouldn\u2019t want Marguerite to feel like I\u2019d betrayed her trust or anything\u2026 no night of passion is worth that.<br /> <br /> We said our goodbyes and I made my way back to the Dream House, only to find that pretty much nobody but D was there. Gawain had taken Desiree into the Hollow for the evening, and Marguerite and Julia had gone with them. Jacob and Calamity had gone to investigate Desiree\u2019s apartment. (God only knows where Ace was). D and I left a note for Calamity and Jacob and went to join the others in the Hollow.<br /> <br /> There was a card game going on when we got there, though it was not one with which I was familiar. Instead of joining the fun, I went to the Hollow\u2019s magical table and asked it to produce some wine. I\u2026 well, in all honesty, I don\u2019t remember much of the rest of the evening. That Hedge wine is potent stuff!<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t remember when Jacob and Calamity got back, but I heard about it the next morning. The Hollywood Courts\u2019 agents had set a trap for Desiree, rigging up a shotgun to blast whoever opened the door of her apartment. Calamity bypassed it by clinging to the ceiling (somehow) and only opening the door slightly, and then cutting the wire with her glass. And hey, they even brought the shotgun back when they returned. Calamity has a new toy, which ought to keep her happy.<br /> <br /> I know that Marguerite seemed a lot happier when I got back, and Julia seemed to have put aside her murderous rage toward Felicity (for the moment) as well. In fact, the two of them seemed so happy that Marguerite hardly batted an eye when D called her \u201cMags.\u201d So I guess that crisis has been dealt with for the time being.<br /> <br /> The only thing I really recall about the later portions of last night is that the talk eventually turned to our first trip into the Hedge House. Gawain was talking about the spider-thing that we fought, and Marguerite kept trying to make it seem like my part in the fight wasn\u2019t quite so \u2013 well, let\u2019s face it \u2013 pathetic. She made it sound like I\u2019d bravely put myself out there to draw our foe out of hiding, rather than just being surprised and immediately getting knocked unconscious.<br /> <br /> I think my own side of the conversation mostly consisted of me saying witty things like \u201cbut I jus\u2019 pastout! I din\u2019n even see nuffin\u2019 uvvafite.\u201d Yeah, not my finest hour.<br /> <br /> D eventually managed to get me back to our bedroom in the Dream House, and the two of us fell asleep in each other\u2019s arms. Like, immediately. Like, before I thought to set the alarm.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I woke up around noon today and realized that I\u2019d slept through church. This realization, combined with a killer hangover, did not serve to put me in the best of moods. D was sanguine about it, and managed to get me into a t-shirt and a pair of sleep shorts before ushering me downstairs for coffee and sex breakfast.<br /> <br /> Flores was there by the time we descended. Talk turned to her costume from the masquerade ball, and from there the conversation progressed into areas for which I was woefully unprepared. Apparently the \u201cbaroness\u201d costume Flores had been wearing was from some sort of mid-80s revival of the old G. I. Joe dolls. The even made a cartoon to help sell the dolls. I didn\u2019t claim to understand it. And even worse, Calamity then started talking about some <u>other</u> 80s cartoon called \u201cJem\u201d (yes, spelled with a \u201cJ\u201d), about which I knew less than nothing. I tried half-heartedly to ask if the show had been about that Welsh singer I came across when I was researching modern music a few months ago, but everyone just gave me blank looks and moved on.<br /> <br /> Gawain had made steaks for sex breakfast\u2026 <u>dragon</u> steaks, in fact. The meat had a slightly greenish tinge to it, but other than that it just seemed like very tender meat. And I\u2019m not sure if it was just the way Gawain spiced and prepared it or if it was something endemic to the meat itself, but it was absolutely delicious.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it was sort of a relief when people started talking about other things, and I could contribute to the conversation again. Flores mentioned that Oleander had given her the recipe for a concoction that is supposed to give people very vivid dreams. It sounds interesting, though I\u2019d want to try it out under controlled circumstances first (preferably with Oleander present if possible). Then she asked when we were going to set up a big, motley-wide orgy. She offered to help us arrange things to minimize awkwardness. I was intrigued by the idea, and most of the rest of the motley seemed okay with it, but Julia and Jacob resisted. Since none of us really wants to do anything that would make them uncomfortable, we sort of tabled the notion for the time being. In the future, who knows?<br /> <br /> Flores also convinced Marguerite to finally perform that \u201cJe Non Regrette Rien\u201d act she\u2019s been working on. She resisted at first, saying that she wanted the act to be perfect before she took it in front of a live audience, but Calamity and I chimed in, telling her that no act was ever really \u201cperfect,\u201d but that you had to eventually decide that it was close enough. I think she\u2019s resolved now, and I can\u2019t wait to see how the audience takes it!<br /> <br /> Sandoval stopped by a little later with a message from the monarchs. He wanted to confirm the deal that Calamity had offered Desiree last night. He also offered the suggestion that Desiree might want to keep what she knows to herself for the time being, so that she can continue to be useful to the monarchs, and thus relatively safe. While this sounded pretty sensible to me, Gawain and Flores took umbrage at a perceived hidden threat in his words, and Desiree herself said that she wanted to get the deposition over with as soon as possible so that Hollywood would have no reason to send more assassins after her. I can see the sense in that point of view as well, I guess.<br /> <br /> Since things had gotten sort of tense, I escorted Sandoval out of the Dream House while the others talked with Desiree about her plans. As we reached the front door, I sort of flashed him a sly grin and said \u201cso I understand you\u2019ve been making time with my lady, Sandoval. What\u2019s that all about?\u201d<br /> <br /> He shrugged and smiled back. \u201cYou seemed to be occupied with the Koozbanian,\u201d he said simply. \u201cShe didn\u2019t think you\u2019d mind.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cD is free to sleep with whoever she wants,\u201d I said simply. \u201cAnd so am I,\u201d I added, a little more seductively. Then I pitched my voice really low, leaned in, and whispered in his ear. \u201cAnd so are both of us together.\u201d<br /> <br /> His eyes widened a little, and he nodded. \u201cI\u2019ll\u2026 keep that in mind,\u201d he said. \u201cGoodbye for now, Lorelei. Thank you for your hospitality.\u201d<br /> <br /> And he kissed my hand and made his exit, his eyes on me the whole time. So I\u2019ve probably got that to look forward to in the not-too-distant future. For now though, we should probably just concentrate on getting Desiree to the monarchs safely\u2026 and watching carefully to make sure she\u2019s on the level.<br /> <b><br /> Lorelei Grace</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T13:57:13-08:00","id":810801,"title":"","content":"<b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> And the adventure continues. After getting off of the phone with Spidertoes, Calamity called up Dahlia to let her know what was going on with Desiree and in general. Almost as soon as she hung up the phone the object of our conversation arrived, just not how we expected. Desiree showed up at our door covered in blood. Apparently as soon as she opened her door to come over here she was accosted by a gunman that said, \u201cThe game is up,\u201d and shot her in the face. Yeah, the face. Luckily for her she is Spring Court and managed to heal herself of most of the wounds. That left the blood, but a majority of the damage had been fixed. Lorelei went into \u201chealer mode\u201d and finished healing Desiree\u2019s wounds. Some of the others helped clean her up. I watched. I probably should have shown more concern towards a friend, but honestly she was fine. It was mainly just blood that needed cleaning up. Once all that was done though, came the conversation. Yeah, the big one.<br /> <br /> Gawain started off saying that he had something important to tell Desiree but that he wanted to do so in dreams. He tried to explain that it was important, but he was better at conversing in dreams and really preferred to do it that way. Desiree started to get nervous the longer the conversation went on. I can understand the reaction too. I wouldn\u2019t have been much better, but I think Gawain was starting to freak out Desiree with his talk of \u201cimportant topics\u201d and \u201cyou\u2019ll be safe.\u201d I mean, even Calamity told Desiree that she\u2019d be safe from her. Now isn\u2019t that a comforting thought? At that point Lori took over and started explaining things. She pretty much covered everything that we learned about the Hollywood courts, what had been done to her and who she really was. There was a brief moment when I think her original memories were sliding back into place. She seemed a bit surprised at first, her eyes went wide. Then she smiled just a bit before adopting a fearful expression. She\u2019s good.<br /> <br /> Desiree then explained a bit about her past. She said that she had come to California to make it big, but ended up in trouble instead. She didn\u2019t find stardom, but she did find a way to make money. Just not the way she\u2019d imagined. Unfortunately her life of prostitution led her to drugs and things just went downhill from there. She may or may not have hit rock bottom, but it was a near thing. Apparently that was when the Director found her, or someone that worked for him did. She was saved from her life of whoring and drugs by a Keeper. I suppose it was a good thing that she was brought out of that life, but at what cost? She served the Director for who knows how long and still feels loyal to him. Even as we spoke this evening she said that she didn\u2019t think it would be right to betray the being that saved her. So she\u2019s still loyal. Good to know.<br /> <br /> She then explained what she knew about the Hollywood courts and their plans. They are holding a Keeper hostage and it is called the Grand Maw\u2026or maybe Grandmaw. They seem to be priming this thing to be set loose on Arcadia where it can eat the Gentry to its heart\u2019s content. Who\u2019s to say that it will stop at the Gentry though? It could hurt innocent Changelings that are still trapped in Arcadia. And what happens when it gets its attention drawn back to \u2018the world?\u2019 I\u2019m not sure how many Gentry there are, but here there are a good number of Changelings. Not sure if it gets the same \u201cfix\u201d from eating our kind as opposed to the Keepers, but I\u2019m opposed to the whole thing. The Grand Maw should be put down. It is too dangerous to be left alive. There should be no question about that. And that is where Desiree and I agree. She is 100% behind the idea of taking out the Grand Maw and ending whatever plans the Hollywood Courts have for it. I can\u2019t believe I\u2019m agreeing with her, but that thing is too dangerous to be left alive. No question about that.<br /> <br /> That was when Calamity admitted that she\u2019d been in communication with Dahlia about this whole situation and let Desiree know that if she cooperated with us and gave us information about the Hollywood Courts then we would let her go on her way, unmolested, as long as she agreed to never return. I think Lorelei was less than pleased to hear about that and took Calamity aside to talk to her. Not sure what the whole conversation was about. It could have been about telling Desiree the truth, but Lori didn\u2019t seem all that opposed to doing it in the first place and seemed more than willing to enlighten our former friend when Gawain\u2019s explanations seemed to further confuse the situation. Maybe it was about talking to Spidertoes, or Dahlia? Lori looked a little concerned when Calamity mentioned talking to her handler, but I\u2019m not sure exactly what the concern was about. I mean, Calamity is oath bound to tell Dahlia about threats to the freehold, and Desiree being a true loyalist surely fits into that category. It might have been about something else, but given when she interrupted I\u2019m thinking it was something to do with Dahlia, maybe Spidertoes.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Lori, Insincere Marguerite was awfully quiet throughout the whole conversation with Desiree, and clung to Lori like her life depended on it. I\u2019m not sure what was going on there, but I know Marguerite had a rough time of it at the dance, so this might be fallout from that whole \u201cregressing\u201d thing. I should probably talk to her later and make sure that she\u2019s okay. Her being all clingy is kind of worrying. If she needs help then I\u2019ll do what I can to make things right for her.<br /> <br /> Anyway, then there was a second phone call to Dahlia about our lovely spy. Calamity then told me that Dahlia had suggested that I take Desiree to the safe house in order to do what the place implies, keep her safe. She said that it was not an order since she was not currently in contact with Lowjack, that it was just a suggestion and figured that I would have the authority to bring someone to the safe house if I thought that the situation warranted it. Calamity came to talk to me privately about all of this. I wasn\u2019t so sure that the safe house would be the right place for Desiree. I know that we are supposed to be letting Desiree go after all of this, but I still feel like that would be opening us up to future problems. Desiree is intimately familiar with our freehold. The relationships between people, the social and political structure, everything. She would be able to go back to the Director and give him all kinds of information that he might not already have. Given how many spies he\u2019s had in our freehold in the past, it\u2019s possible that he knows all of the same stuff that Desiree does, but it still feels like a security risk to just let her go. I don\u2019t know if the others see the threat that Desiree can be once she decides that working alongside us is no longer something she wants to do. I suggested that perhaps our Hollow would be a good place to stash her to keep her safe. The Knighthood\u2019s safe house is a secret location and one that the occupant can leave at any point. I did not feel good about letting Desiree know where it was located since she could leave any time she wanted and reveal that location to anyone she wanted.<br /> <br /> Also, in the interest of getting the Hollywood Courts off of Desiree\u2019s trail, at least for the moment, I suggested that we take her car back to her apartment and see if it would be possible to file a false police report about a murder at her place. I figured that if her would-be killers wanted to confirm that she was dead they would do a search for a police report, which is a public record. Calamity seemed to think that the idea had merit, so we made tentative plans and went in search of Desiree and her car keys. It turns out that while Calamity and I were talking the others went to the Hollow, so we went there to get Desiree\u2019s keys. We explained our plan and she seemed willing enough to go along with it and handed over her keys. We left the ladies in Gawain\u2019s capable hands and headed to Desiree\u2019s apartment building.<br /> <br /> Desiree\u2019s apartment was not what we expected. Not the location, but what we found. There was a lot of blood outside and we found the front door cracked open. There were no police or sirens coming so we decided to take a quick peak inside. I\u2019m glad we did. We saw a blood trail leading away from the apartment to the parking lot. Apparently she healed herself in the car. When we went inside we found that every door save one was open. And the one that was shut was her bedroom door. We figured this was a bit suspect so Calamity crawled along the ceiling and started to crack the door open a bit. She found a trip wire connected to a shotgun on the other side. She deftly disabled the trap and we packed up the shotgun to take with us. Looks like the Hollywood Courts already know that she\u2019s alive. No need to booby-trap a dead person\u2019s bedroom door after all. We then figured it would be best to leave and did so. We headed back to the Dream House and left Desiree\u2019s car at the apartment. No need to call attention to it. I made sure to wipe my prints off of every surface I could think of that I had touched. Don\u2019t need to add police interest where it\u2019s not wanted.<br /> <br /> So, we told the ladies what we found and they agreed that the Hollywood Courts would likely keep coming after Desiree until she had spoken to the Monarchs and divulged any and all secrets that she had about the Court of Fallen Starts. She did tell us that the Court Monarchs do not get along at all and are constantly planning against one another. They are all holding a Keeper hostage and apparently it is messing them up big time. Maybe it\u2019s just prolonged exposure to the Gentry or the fact that they have been holding another living being captive for so long. Not sure which one it is, but whatever the reason it gives us an advantage. Our Courts get along, and together we can plan something to keep the Court of Fallen Stars out of our business.<br /> <br /> At that point it was getting late so some folks, Lorelei and De la Rocha, went back to the Dream House. While others, Calamity, Gawain and Desiree, stayed at the Hollow. Calamity was planning on staying up through the night to keep a watch and make sure nothing happened to the occupants. I thought it was a good idea so I went back to the Dream House and decided to stay up all night there to keep an eye on things. It is possible that if the Hollywood Courts knew that Desiree was alive then they might have trailed her to our place and it would be prudent to keep a watch. Nothing happened, which was probably good, but I\u2019ll admit that a part of me wanted the Hollywood Courts to try something. I don\u2019t like waiting for an ambush. We don\u2019t know what the Court of Fallen Stars is going to do and I kind of want the waiting to be over.<br /> <br /> So\u2026morning came and no ambush. Gawain, who it turns out also stayed up all night, busied himself making dragon steaks for breakfast. We had already started the hides curing and had frozen, salted and otherwise stored all the meat we could. So, we had dragon steak for breakfast, which is pretty awesome to be able to say. They were also really good which is a bonus. Who knew that dragons tasted good? I sure didn\u2019t. My contribution was of course, coffee. I made an offering of coffee to Lori in exchange for a quick Spring Court \u201cpick me up.\u201d I think Gawain and Calamity did the same thing if the offerings of toast and other food stuffs was any indication. It was strange to see her on a Sunday lacking the ponytail and glasses, but I think she skipped church this time. I think I overheard something about hedge wine and overindulgence. Poor Lori. I think she needed that coffee.<br /> <br /> While Gawain was cooking Calamity texted Dahlia to go over options. Apparently Lowjack is going to talk to the other Monarchs this afternoon to discuss the whole \u201cDesiree problem,\u201d and until then we\u2019re going to be watching the aforementioned Desiree to make sure she stays safe. And stays put. Well, mainly to keep her safe. I still don\u2019t think it\u2019s a good idea to just let her go after all of this is over, but who am I to go against the Monarchs? Well, truth be told that deal was made by Dahlia. I\u2019m not sure how much weight her word will have if the Monarchs decide something different. I guess we\u2019ll find out this afternoon.<br /> <br /> After that we asked Desiree if there is anything that she wants or needs, and she said that she\u2019d really like to see Flores. Apparently she has become close friends with our resident flower. So, we called Flores who said that coming to the Dream House was fine with her. We had suggested that since the Dream House is a defensible location and if the Hollywood Courts try anything we\u2019ll be ready. We figured that they might try something before this afternoon. As I mentioned before, there\u2019s not much point in killing Desiree after she gives up her information so the prudent thing to do would be to kill her before she has that chance. So, we invited Flores back here. Hopefully if anything does happen we\u2019ll be able to keep everyone safe.<br /> <br /> While we waited for Flores to come over conversation devolved into talking about some old TV shows, at least one of which I\u2019d never heard of. Something Jem, or Jem and the Something. I don\u2019t remember what was said. I was only paying so much attention at that point. I do remember something being said about G.I Joe. I know there was a couple movies that came out a few years ago, but they were talking about some cartoon by the same name. Sounds like it might have come out around the same time as that Jem show. Again, I only paid so much attention.<br /> <br /> So, eventually Flores showed up and Desiree gave her a very edited version of what was going on. She said that she found out that she was a sleeper agent for the Hollywood Courts against her will, and how they were now trying to hurt her because she was going to give information to our Monarchs. Flores was all for giving it to the Hollywood Courts for trying to hurt her friend. It wasn\u2019t much later that Sandoval showed up wanting to talk to Desiree. After a moment\u2019s hesitation Desiree just told him that he could talk in front of the rest of us. I think she had a good idea of what he was there to talk about and figured there was no point in trying to hide it. Doing so would be pointless and go against the whole \u201copen policy\u201d that she\u2019s adopted with us since she remembered the truth.<br /> <br /> As I expected the Monarchs want Desiree in some sort of custody. Protective mainly, but with someone keeping an eye on her activities as well. It was implied that they considered her important right now because she had information that they needed, but they weren\u2019t sure if that would change afterwards. Gawain got really protective at that. I think he took what Sandoval said as a threat to Desiree and was not happy. There was some more discussion, but it came down to the fact that Desiree really wanted to get the information that she has down on paper somewhere so she will no longer be a target of the Hollywood Courts. She was also very keen on getting the Hollywood Courts away from the Grandmaw or the Grandmaw away from them. Whether that involved killing the Gentry or not she didn\u2019t seem to care, as long as they were away from its influence.<br /> <br /> As much as some small part of me regrets saving Desiree from Calamity\u2019s blades that time in the Hedge, I have to admit that the information she possesses is important and will do good things for us. Of course, that\u2019s if her information is true. We don\u2019t have a lot of intel on the Court of Fallen Stars. At least I don\u2019t. Maybe the Monarchs do and will be able to weed out the truth from the bullshit. It\u2019s true that she is valuable to us as long as she has information we need. She seems keen on telling us all that she knows, but then her usefulness might be at an end. Do we let her go after Sandoval takes her deposition or will she conveniently have more information that we might find interesting?<br /> <br /> I realize that I didn\u2019t have much of an opinion on Desiree until all of this came up, but it kind of hit close to home. Though I didn\u2019t remain loyal to my Keeper, I gave a similar kind of deposition to Lowjack about the Lady\u2019s strengths and weaknesses, friends and enemies. Am I still useful to John? Is he keeping me close because he trusts me or because he has something on me and can use it to his advantage? I certainly am in a mood, aren\u2019t I? I guess this whole thing just brings up my own trust issues. I guess we\u2019ll see what Desiree\u2019s next move is after Sandoval gets her statement and she meets with the Monarchs. I think the plan is that we\u2019ll keep an eye on her for now and then she said that she wants to spend the night somewhere different tonight. She said that she doesn\u2019t want to endanger us should the Court of Fallen Stars come after her. Her concern might be genuine or it might be faked. I\u2019m not sure. I\u2019m tempted to say that she\u2019s just playing us. She\u2019s supposed to be one of the best and is very skilled at playing the \u201clong game.\u201d My guess is that for the moment our goals are the same so she\u2019s cooperating. She seems to honestly want the Grandmaw out of the picture one way or another. Working alongside someone for a mutual goal engenders feelings of trust and she could be counting on that. Who knows, maybe she just wants to get out of here alive and get back to the Director. Maybe she has some other ulterior motive. I\u2019m going to continue to be the pessimist, or as my father would say, realist, and watch her carefully.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> The meeting with Desiree went as well as it could have, given circumstances. Yes, she was a loyalist. Yes, she remembered, yes, she was ambivalent about the whole thing, yes she played on our caring about her. Now, that does not mean she was not earnest, but it is what she did.<br /> <br /> She agreed to give information freely about the Court of Fallen Stars. She said she would not bolt and flee the area. Calamity promised safety, it went as well as it could, her having been shot in the face aside.<br /> <br /> While waiting, I got a text from Felicity, suggesting I come over and have a late meal. Soft Felicity. Warm Felicity. Sweet Felicity. I felt the desires come; the thing in the dark began to rise behind my eyes. But I pushed her out, I gathered Iself and went over and hugged Lori as hard as I could, pressing my nose to her neck, smelling her scent, holding on and hoping she would keep I safe from Iself, like she promised. I felt bad about not going to Julia, but Julia knows she cannot stop I from doing what I desire, and that Lori can.<br /> <br /> I had trouble expressing Iself, again, but instead of sibilating and speaking oddly I did not speak, but clung to Lori like my life was at stake. Julia found my phone and discovered what the problem was. And, unfortunately, became enraged. She had been commanded not to kill or harm Felicity, and she pulled against my command. She could not break my chains, but not for lack of trying. She communicated to Lorelei what was going on, and Lorelei went, just as she had before, to fix my problem I was too lost to gibbering to deal with. I was handed off to De La Rocha, who handled I until Lorelei returned. I hopefully did not speak.<br /> <br /> It is so difficult to describe, the feelings. Expressing yourself becomes hard. I repeat Iself a lot, and become frustrated by speaking and not taking. I am told I even grasp at whom I am talking to. It is really bad. Also, I fear I have thoroughly ruined my mystique.<br /> <br /> Lori returned and told I that had spoken to Felicity and told her I was having trouble. She noted Felicity wanted to see I, but also that she wanted to be there when it happened, and it should wait a few days. That is fine. Lori was also quick to refer I to Julia, who did her best to deal with I\u2019s raging emotions. After a short talk, we wanted to find the others. We visited Gawain and Desiree with Lori and De La Rocha in the Hollow, and watched them play Euchre. It beats Andy-I-Over. I tried to make Lori sound more heroic to the girls, and Julia and I wound up getting roped in, and I distracted her by playing with I\u2019s cards in I\u2019s toes.<br /> <br /> Eventually, Calamity and Jacob returned. I got the feeling that they had dealt with their situation at Desiree\u2019s house as well as could be expected. The Motley, and Desiree, had a warm time in the Hollow. Lori drank a lot of the odd wine down there. I did not laugh as much as others, but was talking now. Eventually, Lori and De La Rocha went to their room at the house, followed by Jacob to keep an eye on things in the real world. Julia and I went upstairs, while Calamity and Gawain watched over Desiree.<br /> <br /> I would like to say there in the Hollow Julia and I made all sorts of crazy love, but actually, I just had enough and I cried. For the first time in\u2026.a couple moths, I suppose, I cried. I wept. I bawled, I pushed the desires, the emotions, the feelings out. Julia at first struggled to help, but soon saw I was doing needed purging of my emotions, and simply held I, gingerly at first, then close. Hours later, I was spent. Julia slept. She seemed so scared when I let myself go, she is so used to I being in control. She truly did not know what to do, much like Bastille Day. I will have to try to help her. I am the strong one. She depends on I.<br /> <br /> I feel, empty, but better. I am empty of that which is old and open to possibilities. I feel better. But I must get things under control with Felicity. This is, frankly, undignified, and just\u2026it\u2019s not Insincere Marguerite. It is the weak girl I was.<br /> <br /> I am her no longer. I will not be controlled by desires. I am not of the Spring. I am Insincere Marguerite. I am of the Night. I am the greatest thief on Earth!<br /> <br /> o o o o o o o o o o o o<br /> <br /> <br /> The morning, well, afternoon I suppose, has been good. Julia and I woke feeling rather refreshed. She was in a good mood, as was I, as we got up to face the day. We had stopped at the hall of the main house for a shower, and I was helping dry Julia\u2019s hair when Lori and De La Rocha came out. Julia has such long hair, and I do adore it so. It smells like her. I like the way she smells. I am unsure Lori and De La Rocha knew what to do about our giggling and playing in the hallway. Poor Lori seemed hung over. I hope I can cheer her up.<br /> <br /> The emotions at breakfast were mixed. I felt cheerful, even giddy. I surrounded my face with Julia\u2019s freshly washed hair, and stroked it with my hand while my feet held my toast. As delicious as my toast was (and probably paired with my mood, it seemed the best toast I had ever had) it was to be outdone as we were having dragon steaks. Gawain was excited to show off cooking them. Desiree joined us, and soon summoned Flores.<br /> <br /> Lori was recovering when Flores arrived, and Flores was in her full wonder. They had been talking about American army toys (Americans are obsessed with the Military) when she came in, and she wasted little time talking I me into doing \u201cNon, Je Ne Regrette Rien\u201d tomorrow night. I am still planning a version that is as much strut and attitude as song. But I can sing well enough I think, and Julia has for me a hat, suit coat and shirt but black shorts so I show bare legs. I look quite fetching in it. Maybe after these several months I should just do it. I kept tinkering with it, and Calamity is right, it will never be perfect.<br /> <br /> I am told after I set out to work on it, that Flores ran out of luck trying to arrange a Motley-wide orgy. Julia and Jacob protested. Gawain, to his credit, legitimately seemed to be trying to see if there was a way to do it and have them be comfortable, according to Julia, and did not seem weird or untoward. Still, it is perhaps comforting that Flores has some limit on her power. Not that I would sleep with the Motley anyway after Lori and Gawain did humorous versions of my tittering back at me.<br /> <br /> It was nice that she is still getting along with Oleander, given Oleander and De La Rocha are not back to full friendship.<br /> <br /> Oh, and Sandoval arrived. Julia and De La Rocha both said he was polite, but spoke for the Monarchs to lay down terms. Desiree was quick to defend herself, laid down her terms, and negotiated only barely giving us a word in. Calamity noted it is possible her usual demeanor is her real and negotiating was her game face, but the reverse could be true. Julia suspected the latter. Sandoval upset Flores and Gawain, but Calamity said it was misunderstandings between elementals. Regardless, Desiree will be staying elsewhere tonight.<br /> <br /> While we chatted on the catwalks with the puppets, Calamity discussed her intent to kill her Fetch (again). It could be necessary, but I noted too she was seeking to avenge someone she had not spoken to and had no idea how she felt, and she had killed the Fetch\u2019s parents. Perhaps, I suggested, she should talk to this Anastasia first. I promised to look into it and see if her speaking to Anastasia would be good or bad.<br /> <br /> I neglected to mention I had already tracked Anastasia down, sent her a lovely mirror \u201cby mistake\u201d with no return address, and had in fact been through her house in Bellevue a time or two. I am sure I will come up with a story when I have more information.<br /> <br /> Regardless, as Calamity retuned to find Desiree and Gawain, I felt good, helping my Darkling Sister. I\u2019ve felt good all day, from when my eyes opened and saw my sleeping Julia beneath me. Maybe this means good things. I hope so. There is business that must be sorted out. My Motley cares for me, my Darkling Sister is depending on me, my lovelies love me. I can ask for no more.<br /> <br /> There is a show to do, and Insincere Marguerite will not be kept from it!<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXVII</i><br /> <br /> Lori had a few inaccuracies this time.<br /> <br /> When Desiree was shot, she dropped. She got up when her assailant quickly left (he had fired on a hallway with many apartments on it). She didn\u2019t push past him.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite and Julia went downstairs after Lorelei and De La Rocha did; Lori met Julia on her return, sent her to take care of Insincere Marguerite telling her her girlfriend needed her right now, and went downstairs with De La Rocha. Insincere Marguerite started talking after that, but she did not cheer up much; the whole \u201cMags\u201d thing happened the next morning, not that night.<br /> <br /> The Welsh singer Lori\u2019s player mentions <i>every</i> time Jem and the Holograms come up like clockwork. This wasn\u2019t the first or fifth time, and it won\u2019t be the last.<br /> <br /> Other stuff\u2026there was an implication the Grand Maw had been tainted or altered by something. Made more twisted than it originally was, not quite a \u201cnormal\u201d Gentry, but Desiree was unsure of specifics.<br /> <br /> So what now? Desiree is clearly a loyalist, she does not wish to betray her Keeper. But then, neither does Insincere Marguerite. Desiree seems to want to continue her friendship. Is it a trick? A lure? Or can people on two sides care about each other? Would you put down your friend? What if you had shared a bed? What if you had risked yourself to protect her and she wasn\u2019t lying at the time, and has not lied at all. What would you do?<br /> <br /> Comments and Questions welcome, see you next time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T04:10:26-08:00","id":813273,"title":"","content":"This is the first of yours APs I've read; started a little under a week ago, powered through it all. Great storytelling going on here, with a wonderful cast of players and NPCs. My compliments to all.<br /> <br /> I admit, until the bit with the Warlock, I had been thinking that maybe the whole &quot;Ace&quot; nickname was actually a subtle play on Ace being asexual...<br /> <br /> With how out of character Lowjack was acting... I won't be surprised if we find out someone put the Bedlam whammy on him. Honestly, if you hadn't admitted the grub's crisis at the Masquerade was entirely the player's doing, I might suspect Bedlam there, too.<br /> <br /> Did Calamity join her entitlement over the course of the recent timeskip?<br /> <br /> Have you considered allowing the Advanced and Epic traits from Beast to be taken by your players, considering David Hill has mentioned on the forums he originally intended their inclusion in GMC for mortals and supernaturals alike? (Lori seems like a shoe-in for Advanced Striking Looks.)<br /> <br /> Which kiths has Lorelei's player considered for her 'third kith' if she takes up Pilgrim of the Endless Road?<br /> <br /> I confess I'm a little sad that the timeline isn't advanced enough that Lorelei could have heard Lin-Manuel Miranda's Broadway musical &quot;Hamilton&quot;.<br /> <br /> I know you've mentioned Captain Jack is both Latino and bearded, but without an image, I can't help but imagine him as looking like Captain Jack Harkness of Doctor Who and Torchwood. (Though maybe a character image would help with that. Wink wink nudge nudge. I confess, I'm also curious about Spidertoes, the Handmaidens, and exactly how alien Andromeda and Hailey look.)<br /> <br /> When Tommy showed up at Calamity's b-day party, did the players finally get a look at him, or was he lurking about in the vents again? If they glimpsed him, I'd be curious to see what he looks like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2286-indarkestknight","name":"indarkestknight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T12:05:36-08:00","id":813535,"title":"","content":"It's good to have you, indarkestnight. I am glad you have enjoyed it, and I hope you continue to. I am very proud of all my games I have posted here.<br /> <br /> You are not the first to say that about Ace, though I suspect that would be lost on the player.<br /> <br /> Well Bedlam is an interesting tool. Lowjack's behavior is odd, but may or may not be Bedlam. Changeling is an interesting game. You can change someone's desires with a level 2 contract. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Between the Seasonal Contracts and Bedlam I have a lot of leeway. Insincere Marguerite's behavior is tied to the growing Wyrd, much like a lot of the other oddness with PCs. Most PCs have internal dragons to slay. Which is cool; they manufacture their own internal character drama well.<br /> <br /> Yes, Calamity joined hers during the timeskip.<br /> <br /> It's hard to say about Epic Traits. My knee jerk is not to to futz with the game too much almost 50 sessions in. That said, <i>Balance of Shadows</i> was not far from 100 when I did the GMC changes and it went smoothly. As always, it is something we as a group need to decide. I might consider allowing it for Wyrd 6+ Characters.<br /> <br /> Last I spoke to them Lori's player had not settled on any yet. It has not come up in a while.<br /> <br /> These time jumps are to try and keep the game from getting &quot;historical.&quot; It started in the future, now is over a year in the past. We will see. I would like to keep it close to Modern Day for a lot of reasons.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately Captain Jack (and Flores) are two of the very few pictures I am using with permission of the person in the picture and don't have permission to repost them as the character. I am very sorry. Especially because Flores is gorgeous. Sometimes I have to wheel and deal to get good pics to use. I will get the post out and put up the other pictures probably tomorrow (<i>Golden Eagle</i> tonight, was moved to avoid the snowstorm). The response of almost everyone to Andromeda is &quot;wow she is...awfully cute!&quot; so I am curious what that will be here. If you think of any more let me know I will grab them as I gather pics. Tommy still has not been seen by anyone.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the feedback. It's good to have you along! I am glad you are enjoying our journals. Lemme know if you start any others....<i>Golden Eagle</i> has 3 Changelings since you like Changelings, and <i>Night Train Detective Agency</i> has the single best Character journal (Speed Demon's) I have seen yet. Feel free to share any further comments or questions here too. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://foru