et.com/albums/u223/LeRoienJeune/hw%2025_zpsids80eym.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Desiree of the Spring Court</a> As a bonus<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T12:29:07-08:00","id":817059,"title":"","content":"Screw you, Baroness. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Kidding, of course. Seriously, though, the reason I mention the singer Jem whenever the cartoon is brought up is because the opposite phenomenon is so prevalent. I consider Jem to be one of the finest female vocalists of the last fifteen years or so, but every time I try to recommend her to anyone, regardless of the context, all I get in return is &quot;you mean like that crappy 80s cartoon hurr hurr hurr!&quot; It gets ridiculously irritating when one is trying to have a serious conversation about a favorite artist. Turn about is fair play, right?<br /> <br /> Sorry about the inaccuracies in the journal. This week's might not be much better, honestly. Stress and long hours at work leave precious little time for writing, and less for copy-editing. I'll try to do better.<br /> <br /> Welcome to the circus, indarkestknight! To address your question, I've considered several kiths as Lori's third over the last few months, but haven't settled on any yet. As the Pilgrims haven't even shown up in game yet, I figure I have a little time at this point. I've considered shoring up her combat abilities somehow, possibly by giving her talons... but we already have a Razorhands in the group, so I kind of want to do something a little different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T12:52:40-08:00","id":817071,"title":"","content":"Penitent Tom and I are now scheming on Lori Kiths ^_^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T21:35:42-08:00","id":820143,"title":"","content":"I can understand if you want to keep the details under wraps if you're planning on using it in the future, but out of curiosity, what's the local Goblin Market like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2286-indarkestknight","name":"indarkestknight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T00:40:47-08:00","id":820211,"title":"","content":"Totally honest answer: There is one, that comes and goes with some regularity, but I have not done much work on it as it has not really come up as something of real interest. I am sure I will flesh it out sooner or later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T00:04:52-08:00","id":820793,"title":"","content":"No Gawain this week. His player was sick. But we have a Calamity!<br /> <br /> What do you do when your good friend is a loyalist and never knew it? Their answer was protect her. But when things come up when the other Changeling voted most likely to be a Loyalist 2014 comes for help well\u2026things get weird.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LXVIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> I don\u2019t have a whole lot of time right now (don\u2019t want to waste a minute of potential snugglage with Oleander), so I\u2019m going to make this entry pretty brief.<br /> <br /> First, the matter with Desiree. Before we went with her to meet the monarchs and discuss her fate, we had another unexpected visitor. Chalcedony showed up, escorted by everyone\u2019s favorite kitsune, Shi. Apparently someone attacked Little Girl Blue last night, in a situation that sounded shockingly similar to what happened to Desiree. In fact, if what Desiree says is true, then the man Chalcedony described as her attacker was almost certainly the same shooter that tried to take her out. More thoughts on this later.<br /> <br /> Chalcedony was (understandably) shaken up about the whole thing, and asked if she could stay with us for her protection. Now, none of us were particularly wild about those two staying under our roof at the same time considering the historical animosity between them, but we just couldn\u2019t turn Chalcedony away in cold blood, so the two of them ended up sitting awkwardly across from each other at our kitchen table.<br /> <br /> While Chalcedony was nervous and quiet, Desiree seemed almost gleeful in subtly tormenting the other girl, playing on her insecurities and fears and making her more tense by the minute. Finally it became too much for me, and I asked to speak to Desiree alone. She shrugged and joined me in Calamity\u2019s office a few moments later.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re not helping matters,\u201d I growled at her.<br /> <br /> She grinned sheepishly. \u201cSorry. We\u2019ve been sniping at each other for so long that I guess it\u2019s just second nature now.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019s scared for her life,\u201d I pointed out, \u201cand you\u2019re riffing on that for a few giggles.\u201d<br /> <br /> She looked suitably abashed after a moment. \u201cYou\u2019re right. Sorry. I\u2019ll tone it down from now on.\u201d<br /> <br /> She made to head back into the kitchen, and I stopped her. \u201cThere\u2019s more,\u201d I said resolutely. \u201cLook, Desiree, I know you\u2019re in a difficult position right now, and I\u2019m trying to be sympathetic. You\u2019re a friend, and I hope that still holds true even after everything that\u2019s happened over the past day. For what it\u2019s worth, I think you\u2019re on the level, and I\u2019ll do what I can to help you. But I\u2019m also good enough at manipulating emotions to know when someone is playing on my sympathies. Now maybe you have a good reason for doing so, but I want to make sure you know that if your actions hurt any of my motley, I will let Calamity have you.\u201d<br /> <br /> She looked\u2026 hurt. Disappointed. It made me ashamed. She\u2019s <u>good.</u><br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t want to hurt you, Lori,\u201d she said softly. \u201cI don\u2019t want to hurt <u>any</u> of you. I promise. I just\u2026 don\u2019t want to betray the one who saved me, either. Okay? I\u2019ll make a pledge not to hurt you or abscond with you\u2026 or with anyone in your motley, if you want me to.\u201d<br /> <br /> A little disgusted with myself, I allowed as how that wouldn\u2019t be necessary and agreed to leave it at that for the time being, and we went back into the kitchen together, where Desiree made a good show of being nice to Chalcedony until it was time to take her to meet the monarchs.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Calamity and Shi headed out to Chalcedony\u2019s place to check it out. Considering what the Hollywood Courts had done to Desiree\u2019s apartment, it seemed like the prudent thing to do. Instead of shotgun-rigged deathtraps, however, they only found more questions in <i>Casa Azul</i> For starters, it seems like our dancer friend has quite a few cell phones. Like, maybe four. All of which seemed to be registered under different names.<br /> <br /> They also found a Hedge-crafted blade\u2026 to hear Calamity describe the weapon, it was some sort of blue crystal machete or something like that. I didn\u2019t give it much thought; lots of people have Hedge-crafted stuff in this Freehold. Hell, I have a few outfits and a doctor\u2019s bag myself.<br /> <br /> Of course the cell phones raised some red flags, and when Shi and Calamity got back we asked Chalcedony about them. She was initially a little cagey, but eventually told us that the phones had been gifts\u2026 from Marguerite.<br /> <br /> We went to ask Marguerite about this, unfortunately interrupting her rehearsals. She\u2019s been rehearsing her number pretty much non-stop all day\u2026 though I\u2019d never put it this way in her presence, her nerves are oddly endearing and her determination to do well in her stage debut is positively <u>cute</u>. In any case, though my French lover was a bit defensive about the whole thing, she did admit to having given Chalcedony some of her ill-gotten gains. So that was one mystery solved.<br /> <br /> The meeting with the monarchs itself was fairly uneventful, but I feel like I should mention a few minor points that came up tangentially. First, the Night Court had sent a representative to observe the proceedings, a charming if somewhat odd fellow by the name of Salk. We of the motley introduced ourselves out of politeness, and he seemed like a decent sort to me, but I don\u2019t think the monarchs were particularly happy with his presence there, by and large.<br /> <br /> Second, notable by her absence was Madame Spidertoes. I would have thought she\u2019d want to be present for such an important event, and I can\u2019t help but wonder if something even more important was occupying her time.<br /> <br /> Desiree proceeded to spill her guts about the Hollywood Courts. I\u2019ve already hit most of the major bullet points previously, so I won\u2019t rehash them here. She went into great detail on the shifting political landscape of Hollywood\u2026 who was sleeping with whom, which monarchs had actively tried to assassinate which others, et cetera. From what I could tell, nobody in Hollywood trusts anyone else, and the whole Freehold is on the brink of collapse because of it. In fact, according to her, the Night Court is gaining new members faster than any of the Seasonal Courts in Hollywood.<br /> <br /> Desiree also shared her opinions on strategy to some degree, including her thoughts on the best way to seduce or eliminate each of the Hollywood monarchs. As I\u2019m not the most strategically-minded of songbirds, I\u2019ll leave the judgment of her plots to those who are better suited to it.<br /> <br /> I noticed during the deposition that Princess Jolie was irritable and, well, downright snippy. She offered to let Desiree stay with her until this whole thing blows over, but none of us thought that was a particularly good idea. Even if Desiree is on the level, it\u2019s not a very savvy move for the Princess politically. We offered to take her in at the Dream House \u2013 the quintessential neutral territory in the Freehold \u2013 and a few minutes later it was a done deal.<br /> <br /> As things were winding down, I pulled her aside and asked if I could speak to her privately. She agreed, and the two of us left the room.<br /> <br /> \u201cAre you alright, Princess?\u201d I asked simply when we were alone.<br /> <br /> She sighed. \u201cI sure can pick \u2018em, huh Lori?\u201d she asked after a moment. \u201cI start getting close to Desiree, and it turns out she\u2019s a hypnotized Loyalist spy. I think things are going well with Felicity, and she starts acting squirrelly and getting distant.\u201d She turned back to look at me and smiled wryly. \u201cSorry, sweetie, I guess I\u2019m just in a mood.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo one could blame you,\u201d I said in my best supportive friend voice. \u201cLook, this thing with Felicity will blow over soon. I talked to her last night; she\u2019s just exploring her options before she decides to commit to you. She\u2019s crazy about you. I recognize the signs.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jolie gave me a shrewd look. \u201cI never said that if Felicity became my consort she\u2019d have to swear off other lovers,\u201d she said levelly. \u201cShe\u2019d still be free to sleep with Insincere Marguerite if she wanted to.\u201d<br /> <br /> I took her hand in mine. \u201cI\u2019m not sure Insincere Marguerite would be as accommodating, honestly. But don\u2019t worry about it, just give her time. Felicity\u2019s a smart girl; she won\u2019t let this chance slip away from her.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLike you did?\u201d Jolie asked with a raised eyebrow.<br /> <br /> I dropped my gaze, but kept holding her hand. \u201cI never claimed to be smart,\u201d I muttered softly. \u201cI don\u2019t regret my decision; I love D. But sometimes I wonder\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> She brushed my hair out of my eyes and forced me to look at her. \u201cSorry, Lori\u2026 I\u2019m just teasing you. Mostly. Though it <u>has</u> been too long since the two of us got together\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAgreed,\u201d I said breathily. What is it about her that brings out the beast in me so powerfully?<br /> <br /> \u201cAnyway,\u201d she said lightly, breaking the spell, \u201cwhat\u2019s your take on this whole Desiree thing? Can we trust her?\u201d<br /> <br /> I thought about it for a minute. \u201cI\u2026 don\u2019t know,\u201d I admitted. \u201cI\u2019m sorry, I\u2019ve been thinking about this all morning, but I just don\u2019t know. She\u2019s obviously a master at manipulating the crowd onto her side, and she\u2019s playing with the Freehold\u2019s emotions with every word she says. But then again, she might do that even if she\u2019s on the level, knowing how most Changelings react to Loyalists. I confronted her about that this afternoon, and she didn\u2019t try to hide that she was doing it, which earned her points in my book\u2026 but even then it occurred to me that she was saying and doing exactly the right things to get me on her side. I\u2019m sorry, but like I said\u2026 I just don\u2019t know.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jolie nodded sympathetically. \u201cIt\u2019s a difficult situation. What does your gut say?\u201d<br /> <br /> I thought about it. \u201cFor what it\u2019s worth, I think we can trust her\u2026 for now.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks,\u201d Jolie said, then leaned in and kissed my forehead softly. \u201cDon\u2019t sell yourself short, Lori. There\u2019s more in here than you give yourself credit for. I want you to know that I value your opinions, okay?\u201d And then she was gone, leaving me grinning stupidly in the hallway and occasionally reaching up to touch the spot where she\u2019d kissed me.<br /> <br /> I got a call a minute or two later, and felt absurdly guilty when I glanced at the caller ID and saw that it was D. She\u2019d stayed behind at the Dream House to make sure that Chalcedony was safe, and wanted to let me know that she had spotted Shi skulking around the grounds peering through windows and being generally creepy. I told her that he had been the one who\u2019d escorted Chalcedony to us, and that he was probably just making sure she was okay.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m no longer convinced that this is strictly the case, but now I\u2019m getting ahead of myself.<br /> <br /> So we made our way back to the Dream House and started prepping for the show. I had a pretty light night, with only one solo (\u201cFever,\u201d a la Peggy Lee). I spent most of my time backing up the other performers and running things from backstage. I\u2019m finding \u2013 much to my own surprise \u2013 that I sort of enjoy the role of behind-the-scenes manager.<br /> <br /> In any case, the show went pretty well, with only one minor hiccup early on. When Luna showed up just before curtain, she had an interesting story to tell. Apparently she met Shi in the park earlier today, who had given her a letter to deliver to Chalcedony at the Dream House tonight. Based on her account of the encounter, it must have happened just prior to his arrival at Chalcedony\u2019s house... which was just before he and Chalcedony came to the Dream House.<br /> <br /> All of this begs the question\u2026 why would Shi give Luna a letter to deliver to Chalcedony if he was heading to her house himself?<br /> <br /> We opened the letter. Can you blame us? It contained only two words: \u201cI know.\u201d So what creepy game is Shi playing? What does he know about Chalcedony (if anything)? Why was he hanging around the Dream House all day keeping an eye on her? And perhaps most importantly\u2026 was <u>he</u> the one who attacked her last night?<br /> <br /> Maybe I\u2019m being paranoid here, but I also wanted to take note of something in case it turns out to be important later. When Shi brought Chalcedony to the Dream House earlier today, he seemed to have developed a nervous tic. He was tapping his staff as he walked around and talked to us. It\u2019s probably nothing\u2026 but I\u2019ve never seen him do that before. Was it an affectation designed to annoy or unsettle the people around him? Something targeted specifically at Chalcedony, maybe? Or could it be indicative of something stranger\u2026 is someone impersonating Shi for a change?<br /> <br /> So maybe I was a little bit distracted by weighty questions of Freehold security as I belted out my torch song tonight. Whatever the reason, I was fully prepared to let Oleander sweep me off my feet for our date tonight. She was wonderful this evening. The two of us left together as soon as the final curtain fell (I had an overnight bag packed) and headed back to her place.<br /> <br /> Wine and chocolates first.<br /> <br /> A bubble bath together in her garden tub followed.<br /> <br /> Then a massage while soft classical music played. Giving me back massages has been a difficult proposition since I returned from Arcadia, but Oleander proved more than equal to the challenge. It felt <u>heavenly</u>.<br /> <br /> She\u2019s sleeping now. Occasionally I glance across the room to watch her breasts rise and fall with her soft breathing. With everything that\u2019s going on and everything I still have to do, I just can\u2019t sleep. I\u2019ve been alternating my time between writing in this journal and studying a medical textbook I checked out of the library. I know I\u2019ll need to use my Contracts to pep myself up in the morning, but I think it\u2019s worth it. As I\u2019ve said before, gaining a greater understanding of how the human body is supposed to function and fit together seems to give my healing powers a little more oomph.<br /> <br /> Still, I might head back to bed in a few minutes. Even if I can\u2019t sleep, I can cuddle my dozing sweetie. And that\u2019s a pretty appealing thought right now.<br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei Grace</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> Nine years, seven months, twenty-one days<br /> <br /> Haven't written in here in a while. I guess with Dr Emmett it just hasn't felt as pressing. But I don't see her till Tuesday and right now it's early AM Monday and I'm sitting here perched on the roof in the shadows watching the back approach to the Dream House and the deck my bedroom opens onto. Gawain is standing vigil inside while Desiree sleeps in our bed. Jacob and Luna are standing guard outside of the basement guest room while Chalcedony sleeps in there. Lori is off spending the night with Oleander. Insincere Marguerite is nestled between de la Rocha and Julia. Becky is passed out drunk by now... alone. Fuck, I wish I was there or she was here. Maybe I should have accepted her offer to help guard these two. At least she wouldn't have spent the night alone. Fuck, maybe that was the reason she offered?<br /> <br /> I need to get a grip. She's strong. She can deal with this without me. It hurts though, seeing that pain there. I swear, every time I see it, soothe it in her dreams, it makes me hate Jolie just a little. I know I shouldn't. She is caring and kind-hearted. That's why Becky loves her. That's why Charlotte loves her. That's why everyone fucking loves her. And fuck knows that just because you care about someone doesn't mean they have to love you back. This isn't a fucking video game. You don't buy love with gifts. You don't earn love with gestures. It happens or it doesn't. And fuck if you get to pick who it happens to. But dammit don't tell me how wonderful love is when I'm holding a woman I love while she cries because the one she loves doesn't love her back. Love is crueler fucking monster than I'll ever be.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Wheels are spinning, I can feel it and I can see it all around the Freehold. Everyone seems off-kilter. Something is wrong but I don't know what exactly. I don't know how to get ahead of it. I don't know how to stop it before people I care about get hurt. Hell, I'm not even sure if I can stop it.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Desiree is a traitor. That much I do know. She was sent to stop Hollywood from unleashing the Grandmaw and to destroy it if at all possible. Only they caught her and tortured her until they could rewire her scripts and send her to spy on us. It all unraveled and now she's determined to help us against Hollywood. She's also said she won't turn on her 'former' master. If her story is true, and I honestly believe it is, she was another pretty girl come to Hollywood and lost to the meatgrinder. The Director plucked her out of a spiral of selling herself for the drugs she needed so she could forget what she was doing to survive. Saved and given the spotlight she'd come searching for, of course she's loyal to him. Preying on the weak and lost is just the thing a Gentry would do. Hell, at this point I believe what she's selling. I do. She wants to strike at Hollywood for what they did to her and because it's what she was sent to do. And hell, because they are fucking insane and feeding a mad Gentry that might well destroy everything. So yeah, everything she told the monarchs is as accurate as she can be.<br /> <br /> It's the what comes next I'm worried about. After the Grandmaw is dealt with. After Hollywood is no longer a threat. When the Director comes to reclaim her. When he calls her home. When he sends someone to remind her of what he's done for her. How much he could do for us. I don't think she's his girl now but I cannot help thinking how easily she could be again.<br /> <br /> And then our other guest... Desiree knows her. She is one of the Director's and that means she is programed and scripted. Desiree says she is a cruel and mean-spirited soul. And why would she lie about this? We are way past any point where throwing suspicion on her takes it off Desiree. But are we past rivalries between two of his performers? Maybe Shi will tell me why he's targeting Chalcedony tomorrow. (Yeah, I can dream...) I don't like her but I cannot let that color my actions here. I don't like the way Insincere Marguerite is smitten with her. It's... weird. It's not that her being into someone so pretty is unusual, but the way she's acting about it is so out of character. I mean, seriously, she's been giving her gifts and watching her. She keeps insisting that nothing is amiss because Chalcedony hasn't asked her for so much as a glass of water but the whole thing is just wrong. This is the woman that stated that she was going to have Felicity sucking her toes in public and suddenly she's shyly crushing on someone from afar? Insincere Marguerite does not fawn and crush on someone. She claims them. Yes, she's working on getting that aspect under control, but I cannot believe the same woman who was fighting down the impulse to drag her newest pretty off into the darkness Friday night can turn around and be all innocent schoolgirl crush today without there being something more going on. I just don't know what it is.<br /> <br /> And why was Marie-Helen guarding her after the shooting attempt? Where was Ginny? For that matter, I can't say I've seen her recently and she never contacted me about working at the show. Hmm. I mean, it might just be a coincidence that she was spying on Chalcedony for Queen Charlotte when she fell head over heels for her and then as soon as Insincere Marguerite started she also became smitten. Yeah, and maybe Lucien Torrez is just an honest businessman. Shit, I am going to have to see if I can't get a word with Charlotte while I am at court tomorrow.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Fuck, I wonder if it's too late to change my mind and tell Insincere Marguerite not to look for Anastasia. She hasn't had time to really do much yet. What was I thinking? I need to let go... It's over. Done. In the past. I need to stay away from her. Let her just live her life. Unless... Unless it still haunts her. Fuck, that sounds arrogant doesn't it? That she's still hung up on me after twenty years... It's not like I vanished. The sinister bitch tormented her. For all she knows I turned on her and hurt her. Her best friend... Her first love... Shit... I just don't know what the right answer is. Maybe this is the best way. Insincere Marguerite can find out how she's doing. Find out if she's laid that past to rest or not. I will do what's best. I'll stay away if that's what she needs. I won't seek her out unless I know she's still carrying those wounds. Not unless I can help her. I won't hurt her by dredging up the dead past if it's behind her. I won't. And if I know. If I know she's happy and well and whole somewhere that would be enough. Then I could stop worrying about her. Then I could let her go. I just need to be sure it's what she really needs.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Well that was fun. So apparently letting one of the dancers that doesn't live here sleep here brings out the murdering ghost. I heard something from the fountain. Jacob was scouting about because Chalcedony was awakened by a feeling of terrible dread. When we opened the door everything was.. off. And then we saw her rise up out of the fountain briefly before disappearing. I activated Shade and Spirit but she wasn't there anymore. Heading down to the basement, Chalcedony was quite rattled and I could see that the other ghost was there. Jacob and Luna took our guest out of the room while I stayed and approached the ghost. She warned me not to let any of the dancers sleep in the dream house because she wouldn't always be there to frighten them and keep them from falling under the other's sway. She told me her name when I introduced myself but withdrew before we could speak more.<br /> <br /> I checked the house over but there was no sign of either of them. The atmosphere in the murder bedroom was thick and oppressive but the ghost itself wasn't active. I spoke to Jacob and Luna about it and then returned. Clearly between the ghosts and the less than defensible layout we are just going to have to take people to the hollow house to guard in the future. It is not haunted and with all the work we've done it's both highly secure and pretty damn swanky.<br /> <br /> So is it completely wrong that I can't help but wonder if life wouldn't have gotten simpler if Monica (that's ghost Monica not green giant Monica) hadn't stopped our murdering spirit from having her way with little girl blue earlier...<br /> <br /> NO. I will NOT go there. We're doing this the right way, even if it's not the easy way and so far it sure as fuck has not been. And it's not going to be. And we are going to keep fucking doing the gorram right thing no matter how fucking hard it gets or how much I might want to hand Desiree to Becky and lick the blood off her claws when she's done with her before we move on to finding out what color blood Chalcedony bleeds. That is not how we are going to play this shit. I am not going to do things Darke's way. I am not going to be that monster.<br /> <br /> Not again.<br /> <br /> Never again.<br /> <br /> Ok, this damn business with the ghosts has stirred my shit up. I'm not there yet but my abilities are growing. I saw her and talked to her. Soon I'll be able to do more. I'll be able to confront the other. Lay it to rest and make the Dream House safe. And once I know how... once I know I can do it... that's when I go back to Belleview. That's when I deal with the unfinished business I left behind.<br /> <br /> Fuck. I need to focus. There is shit to get done today and I do not have time for all of this whining and mental floss. From the hint of light I'm guessing I've got an hour or so before daybreak. Should be enough time to work through my forms.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Alright. Well, my body's relaxed and my head's back to the here and now. Got a few hours before breakfast yet, think I'll make sure all the actual managerial tasks are up to snuff and then I need to work on a number for this week. Sun's coming up so I'm done here. Dawn is for honor duels and pitched battles which is totally Gawain's department to deal with.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> It\u2019s like d\u00e9j\u00e0 vu. Same story, different day. Chalcedony, accompanied by Shi, came to the Dream House today. She was concerned about what had happened or almost happened. Apparently yesterday she was shot at by a man in a trenchcoat as she was about to go into her apartment. She had just gotten back from the Rose and Thorn and spotted the guy with the gun. She managed to jump into her house and avoid the shot. After that the gunman left. Her description of the shooter is very similar to the one that shot at Desiree, and it was only about an hour later. He may have decided to try and take out both girls in one trip. She came to our place because she had heard that Desiree had been shot at as well and she was worried. I don\u2019t blame her, though I might have sought help yesterday if I were her. Personally I would have gone after the gunman, but that\u2019s just me. Well, maybe Calamity. Actually, definitely Calamity.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Calamity, she went to go investigate Chalcedony\u2019s apartment with Shi to see if any surprises had been left there. They didn\u2019t find much of interest save a hedge crafted, blue of course, machete and four cell phones, all different models. Calamity gave me the names of the phone\u2019s original owners and I did a google search on them. Didn\u2019t really come back with anything that stood out. On a couple of the guys there was no information that I could find. The phones themselves were a little suspect, but I figured that we needed to get more information before we came to any conclusions on our own. Meanwhile, Desiree was being perfectly sociable and seemed to be thoroughly enjoying unsettling and confusing Chalcedony the entire time.<br /> <br /> After Calamity and Shi returned they showed Chalcedony the phones and asked what the deal was with them. She said that they were a present from Insincere Marguerite, who backed up the story when asked. Insincere Marguerite for her part kept out of all the socializing that was going on in the house. That in and of itself stood out as a little odd since Marguerite is generally one to flirt with our friends and acquaintances. She also seems to have a thing for Chalcedony lately. She\u2019s been watching the dancer on stage and sometimes during shows. The others think that there is something untoward going on with those two. Specifically that Chalcedony is using some sort of power on Insincere Marguerite to fascinate her. I honestly don\u2019t know what\u2019s going on with those two, but it was a little glaring in its absence today. Marguerite did eventually come over to the group after Lori asked her about the phones. This was after Lori\u2019s private conversation with Desiree. Apparently Insincere Marguerite had been practicing her act for the show tomorrow night. If that\u2019s where she\u2019s been all day she must be nervous about her act. I think she\u2019ll do fine though.<br /> <br /> As expected Sandoval came by to collect Desiree for her \u201cinterview\u201d by the Monarchs. He said that the rest of us in the motley were all invited to be present for the questioning if we so desired. After a moment\u2019s discussion it was decided that Marguerite, Julia and De la Rocha would stay behind to keep an eye on Chalcedony while the rest of us went with Desiree to meet the Monarchs. All of the monarchs were there, as well as a man named Salk who represented the Night Court on behalf of the Warlock of Night. I thought it was interesting and a bit odd that he was present, a virtual stranger, while Madame Spidertoes was absent. I would have expected the elder member of this freehold to be there.<br /> <br /> Desiree for her part offered to just give the information that she had gathered and then answer any questions that she had not already addressed. The monarchs seemed to think that this was a good idea and Desiree started talking. She was very thorough and gave a good bit of detail in her deposition. She gave us information on the Monarchs of the Hollywood Courts, where they lived, their strengths and weaknesses, and who in the freehold got along with who. She even provided information about their military strength, numbers, human allies and their capabilities. The only thing that she did not know was the exact location of the Grandmaw. She did know that they were feeding Changelings to it in a bid to keep it sated enough so that it would not try and actively escape to seek food. Desiree did say that the Hollywood Courts\u2019 defenses are strong and that it would be hard to get into their freehold without at least their human allies seeing us.<br /> <br /> Another interesting bit of information that Desiree shared was something about the Night Court. She said that of all the Courts in Hollywood that was the one that seemed to be slowly growing in size faster than the other Courts. She also said that they were becoming more subtle and cunning in their actions. Salk did not offer any insights on this little tidbit. Not that I remembered anyway.<br /> <br /> And as we knew already, the Hollywood Courts are keen on retrieving and using the Table. They seem to have an idea of what it can do and might want it so they can change the Grandmaw into something else, something more docile or loyal. They don\u2019t seem to know that the Table requires an operator to make the thing work. They just know that they want it and have an idea that the Autumn Court has it. On the plus side, they are terrified of Madame Spidertoes. Apparently they have sent human agents into the Children\u2019s Library only to have them never come out again. I don\u2019t blame them for being afraid of her. She is old, though she doesn\u2019t look it, and she is very powerful. She seems to always work in the best interests of this Freehold and of her Darklings. I would very much not want to be on the wrong side of that woman.<br /> <br /> Anyway\u2026back to the Grandmaw. The Hollywood Courts have not yet figured out what the key weakness of the Gentry is yet. They have explosives that they can use to definitely weaken it, but they do not yet know what will kill it permanently. And that is exactly what Desiree suggested that we do. Her opinion is that sending in a small team to sneak in and kill the Grandmaw permanently would be the ideal plan. I can see where she\u2019s coming from on that. A quick in and out job would be ideal, but we don\u2019t know what will kill the Grandmaw once and for all, and we don\u2019t know how strong it is. What if we found ourselves at a disadvantage? It\u2019s not like we could just call in some back up. And would the locals hinder us or help? I\u2019m leaning towards the former. If they have plans for the Grandmaw, then us killing it might put a damper on that.<br /> <br /> After Desiree was done giving her information no one had any additional questions. I\u2019m not surprised, she was rather thorough with her information. Then we had to decide what to do with Desiree, at least in the short run. Jolie really wanted Desiree to stay with her so she\u2019d be safe, and someone could keep an eye on her as well. That person of course being Jolie. Jolie was keen on Desiree coming to no harm. Augustine may or may not agree with Jolie on that point, but he didn\u2019t say anything specific either way. Charlotte questioned the whole idea of keeping Desiree within the freehold, safe and unrestrained. Lowjack suggested that the idea of keeping her under protective watch is fine for the short term, but we will need to come up with something that works for the long term. So essentially they agreed that Desiree should stay in the Freehold, unrestrained, but watched for her protection (and ours). At this, Calamity offered the Dream House as a safe place for Desiree to stay for the time being. Jolie was upset that everyone seemed to be against Desiree staying with her and she stalked out of the room. Lori left shortly after to talk to the Spring monarch.<br /> <br /> During this whole thing I couldn\u2019t help but be reminded of myself and the things that I\u2019ve done. When Desiree described how she acquired her information, and what kind of information she was after it all sounded very familiar. I also brought back to my Lady the freehold\u2019s strengths, weaknesses, information about the monarchs, pretty much everything that Desiree did. I didn\u2019t have the benefits of a script in my head to fall back on to be a new person, I just had to wing that part, but everything else was rather similar. I infiltrated communities, sometimes making myself known, sometimes doing my best to blend into the background. When I went to Claire Falls I made myself known. I was a newly escaped Changeling as far as they knew. They took me in and offered me a place. I made a couple of friends here and there, but nothing too strong. I hadn\u2019t even picked a Court before I left. I gathered much the same intel that Desiree did and made semi regular reports back to my Lady. The Lady is the one that said she desired a treasure, and so I made friends with Diane. She was absolutely gorgeous. Blonde hair, blue eyes, kind to a fault, in short, she was perfect. So, I brought her back to the Lady. There\u2019s a good reason why a good number of the people living in Claire Falls do not like me. They took me in, trusted me, and I literally went on a walk with one of theirs one day and we never returned. Well, not until D\u0336e\u0336l\u0336i\u0336g\u0336h\u0336t\u0336 Diane escaped and I came to get her back. Yeah, Travers never liked me from the start. Now he has a definite reason to hate me.<br /> <br /> Even the deposition was similar. I wrote out all the information that I could think of about the Lady and her strengths and weaknesses, who the Lady\u2019s loyalists were, how we operated, everything. I of course wrote it in as general a manner as possible so anyone that might read it would not connect it with me, but Lowjack of course knows. Thankfully I did not have to do an interview in front of all the monarchs and friends. I do not want to think about how my friends would view me if they heard in detail about the things that I\u2019ve done. Sure they heard about what Desiree did, but hopefully they will keep that associated with her and not make the jump to me. As it is they have been more understanding than I deserve.<br /> <br /> So after all of that happened we had an additional discussion amongst ourselves to figure out whether or not Chalcedony will stay at the Dream House as well as Desiree. Calamity definitely wanted her to stay. The others seemed amenable and even Desiree said that she would not antagonize Chalcedony, so it was pretty much decided. The two antagonists would both reap the benefits of our hospitality.<br /> <br /> After that I called Luna and invited her over. I explained some of what was going on over the phone and the rest after she arrived. There are some things I didn\u2019t want to talk about over a phone line. As I was explaining what was going on, with the girls getting shot or shot at, loyalists and depositions etc. Luna mentioned that while she had been in the park Shi came up to her and handed her a note to give to Chalcedony. It simply read \u201cI know.\u201d He gave this note to Luna about an hour before he met up with Chalcedony leaving to come here. Kind of creepy, right? Apparently he was also creeping around the Dream House while we were listening to Desiree\u2019s deposition. Someone\u2019s suggestion is that he\u2019s just trying to freak Chalcedony out. In my opinion he was acting suspicious the whole time. Awfully convenient timing with Chalcedony leaving her apartment, him sneaking around the house, offering to protect her and yet leave her a note that says in very vague terms that he knows something about her. Of course Chalcedony has been suspect pretty much since her arrival in the freehold, so what he knows or wants to imply he knows could just be something that has already been suspected, or something else entirely.<br /> <br /> The motley decided that both Chalcedony and Desiree could stay at the Dream House. We planned on putting Chalcedony in the guest room in the basement and have Desiree take Gawain and Calamity\u2019s room. Luna and I would stand guard outside of Chalcedony\u2019s room just in case Hollywood sent any other would be assassins, and Calamity and Gawain were going to guard Desiree. So, we headed back to the house and got everything ready for our guests and then for the show. The show itself went on as usual. I watched a little less of it tonight than usual. Turns out the bar was the place to be tonight. First Becky came over to the bar to talk to Calamity and vent about not being able to kill the known loyalist. She really does not like Desiree at all. She also said something about having an idea of who has been messing with Chalcedony and Desiree\u2019s scripts, but didn\u2019t want to tell anyone yet. She said that she would look into it a little further before letting Calamity know if it is who she think it is.<br /> <br /> Later De la Rocha and Lorelei came by the bar after they had a conversation with Madame Spidertoes. I made sure that Spidertoes was okay with how everything turned out with the whole Desiree thing. Since we found out about all of this stuff thanks to her little mission to the strip club, but she was not the first to hear what we\u2019d found. She seemed mostly okay with it though, so that was good. De La Rocha said that she put in a good word for Calamity to help smooth things over. It seemed to work, somewhat. Sometime after this Calamity went to go talk to Spidertoes and discussed what happened. Apparently Madame Spidertoes complimented Calamity\u2019s actions but seemed just a little put out by the whole not telling her first thing. I suppose it could have gone a lot worse than that.<br /> <br /> Calamity, Luna and I also discussed our plans for tonight should things go pear shaped. The arrangements we came up with are to put the ladies in the rooms I mentioned earlier, and to make sure that there is a mirror in both rooms. We all made sure that we all had Insincere Marguerite\u2019s phone number so if something bad should happen she can pop through the mirror and bring the ladies to the attic. It was the most defensible room that we could think of. Once there we could easily open a gate to the Hedge and go to the Hollow to hide out. We also had a discussion about the two ladies in question. It seems pretty unanimous that none of us particularly trust Desiree or Chalcedony for that matter. So we\u2019ll all keep an eye on them for as long as needs be.<br /> <br /> After the conversation with Spidertoes Becky came back over to the bar with Calamity. She wanted to talk to our resident razorhand, myself and Luna. She offered us her services in keeping an eye on our two guests. I think she was keen on being here in case Desiree tried something. Then she\u2019d get her chance to do violence upon the young loyalist. Calamity assured her that we had everything well in hand but we\u2019d call her if we needed the help. She said that was fine, but I\u2019m not sure how \u201cfine\u201d that really was for her. We did have everything covered though. While the extra body being there wouldn\u2019t have been too much trouble, we had plenty of people keeping an eye on each one of our guests.<br /> <br /> So, it\u2019d be nice to say that the night/early morning passed without incident, but that wouldn\u2019t be true. We had a bit of excitement pop up, just not in the way that we expected. Probably around 4 AM Chalcedony popped her head out of the room she was in and said that she had a really bad feeling. She seemed to be honestly afraid of something, so I asked Chalcedony to go back in the room and Luna to stay and keep an eye out. I went upstairs to look around and see if we had any uninvited guests. I met Calamity in the foyer, who said that she heard a loud splashing sound come from the front of the house. I told her what Chalcedony said, and we both went out the front door to where the fountain was. It was the biggest pool of water nearby, so we figured that the splash might have come from there. We were right. Though as we walked outside the sky looked strange and the moonlight didn\u2019t seem right. I\u2019m not really sure how to explain it. It just felt wrong. Then the fountain started running on its own. Or it looked like it started on its own. A moment later we saw the figure of a woman with a broken neck standing in the fountain. It was the malevolent ghost that we\u2019d been warned about. She stood there watching us when suddenly my phone rang. I answered it to hear Luna\u2019s voice on the other end saying that Chalcedony was seriously freaking out downstairs. I told Calamity what was going on and when we looked back to the broken necked ghost she was gone. Calamity quickly activated a power that would let her see and hear ghosts that are not materialized and then we both hurried downstairs to Chalcedony\u2019s room. I couldn\u2019t see what was going on but Calamity said that there was the ghost of a woman in the room with our blue-loving guest, so I walked in and steered her out of the room. Calamity said after a moment that it was the ghost of a woman named Monica. She had been a dancer at the House years ago and was one of the young woman that hanged herself here. She didn\u2019t seem to mean any harm. She said that she was trying to get Chalcedony awake and worked up so the malevolent ghost couldn\u2019t get her. She also warned us about allowing dancers to sleep overnight at the house. Apparently it\u2019s not safe for them to do so if they don\u2019t already call the place \u201chome.\u201d<br /> <br /> Home\u2026when it comes down to it, this place really does feel like home. Now we just need to find a way to make sure that it stays in one piece\u2026<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> The Chalcedony thing is getting out of hand. Quickly.<br /> <br /> I spied on her, and came to feel some sympathy for her. Everyone seems to assume the worst. I don\u2019t trust her, but I found I have some feeling for her. She seems disinterested, so I have attempted to simply be nice and offer her an occasional token. I did elect to keep such quiet from my Motley, as they are suspicious, but this was also due to the fact that nothing was going on. Chalcedony had not even asked for a glass of water from me. Unfortunately.<br /> <br /> Strange events seem to surround her, though, and today was no exception. She was brought in by Shi, the Kitsune, saying she was attacked last night, same MO as Desiree\u2019s without any comment, and she was missed. Shi, for whatever reason, brought her in today. Desiree was needless antagonistic to her of course, but we took her in and are protecting her. Unreservedly<br /> <br /> While most of the Motley were at the dispensation, I got into an argument with De La Rocha about Chalcedony. Julia is prone to jealousy, but when De La Rocha is also getting on I. something must be done. Calamity has also been troubled, but she is suspicious of everything. I am a Darkling I still think she is too suspicious. So when Lorelei came back I came clean. Yes, I had some feelings for Chalcedony. I had not really admitted it to myself but I did. No, I was not in love with Chalcedony. I made clear I was, instead, in love with Julia, Lorelei, and De La Rocha, but not Chalcedony. Which is just as well dalliances with Ginny aside she has not shown a serious interest in women. Generally.<br /> <br /> I hope I have satisfied them. Now I need to talk to Chalcedony. She has always been nice and I am sure it will go all right. Yes, I am interested in her. No, I will not weep if she is not interested. Yes, I wish to be on friendly terms with her. If she asks if I think she is a loyalist I shall have to simply say I hope she is not. Carefully.<br /> <br /> Semi-related, Desiree\u2019s intense dislike of Chalcedony may be atrophying our groups good opinion of her. She was catty to her today. I had never seen Desiree be catty to anyone, even people who hated her. Still, she otherwise kept her eyes open and mouth shut, except when giving a large amount of information about the Court of Fallen Stars. If the old Desiree is in there, I believe we can get her to defect without making her betray her Keeper. After all, I never betrayed my Keeper and do not intend to, unless she messed with the Freehold, which I doubt. Time will tell. Eventually.<br /> <br /> I did not see or hear from Felicity today. I am both disappointed and relieved. Conflictedly.<br /> <br /> At least my girls are stable, for the most part. Julia has her rather violent hatred of Felicity and intense dislike of Chalcedony, but when she sees nothing between Chalcedony and I that will improve. I am still working on how to warm her up to Felicity when I inevitably seduce her. Maybe I can dominate them together. That sort of bonding was useful in Arcadia, but I have been reluctant to try it here. I should think before even now I do anything Arcadian, even if consent has been secured. And Arcadian thoughts have too often intruded on my mind. Chillingly.<br /> <br /> These days have stressed how my own Wyrd is growing. I am more powerful than I have been since returning to the World, and my capabilities run toward my Arcadian ones. Sadly, the darker side of my Psyche that ran rampant there is strong too. She was\u2026partially tamed anyway, my own personality here is closest to my demeanor in Arcadia, but I should spare no energy in not regressing even as I return to my true power. Thus my reluctance to indulge shared domination; however it drives people closer. Inexorably.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Julia is fine other than her anger at Chalcedony and Felicity, and I have steps to mitigate it. Fortunately.<br /> <br /> My only real worry about Lorelei is how stressed she has been. While a bit obstinate Oleander and De La Rocha have not really made her life too difficult. She is worried about her friend Desiree and probably Jolie\u2019s love life. I hope her personal life remains smooth sailing. I do not plan to bring drama into it. Hopefully.<br /> <br /> De La Rocha is struggling with settling into a long term stable relationship. Much less several. I suspect Spidertoes wishes to share a bed with her again, though I would be shocked if there was more. I am told Spidertoes was quite curious about the open nature of she and Lorelei\u2019s relationship. She also watched De La Rocha some. I know about watching. We will see what happens. Presently.<br /> <br /> It occurs to me I am boy yet feminine enough to fall into what she likes. I tend to be, as Julia reminds me with a gleam in her eyes, a gamine. I should be careful. I mean, I am sure she is attracted to I; I am I, after all. Absolutely.<br /> <br /> I do like that description, being called gamine.<br /> <br /> Sleeping between De La Rocha and Julia has been bliss. They smell like me. It is their natural way now to smell like me. But I wish Lori were here too. Still, I don\u2019t begrudge her time with Oleander, though. Certainly.<br /> <br /> And I need to get this show ready. It\u2019s hard. It\u2019s stressful. I am afraid. But soon, every man, and every woman in the audience who sees I will want I They will need I. With a swing of my hips I will make them mine. Definitely.<br /> <br /> Come, Malibu. Come, Santa Monica. Meet Insincere Marguerite. I think you will like her. I think you will like her a great deal. Helplessly.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXVIII</i><br /> <br /> What the hell was Shi up to anyway? Will Calamity get a straight answer from a Kitsune? All for next time, apparently.<br /> <br /> A note on the two Monica\u2019s: I do that on purpose. I notice a lot of games make sure no two NPCs have the same name but\u2026that is not like life. In the past decade or so I have hung out with two Kerry/Kerri\u2019s, three Brian\u2019s, two David\u2019s PLUS two other players whose name is David but they go by something else. It happens. The only thing I try to not do is duplicate a PLAYER name with a PC or NPC, because that gets complicated. Thus Brians or Davids tend to be rare in my games. My name change did complicate matters in Geist, but fortunately it was an NPC.<br /> <br /> Drama keeps running high next time. Insincere Marguerite triumphantly takes the stage, but finds herself overwhelmed by ghosts from her past. Answers from Shi are no answers at all, and Lori tries to help everyone with their drama. Comments and Questions Welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T16:08:01-08:00","id":821277,"title":"","content":"If I recall correctly you have said that you run the freehold like the gay or transsexual communities. Obviously, in real life they wouldn't have codified rules, but I don't suppose you could give some guidelines on how you run them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","user":"omenseer","date":". 02-01-2016, 09:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T01:03:09-08:00","id":821485,"title":"","content":"It's more that there is a sort of society moving in the city hidden from most of the inhabitants, with it's own folkways and morays, it's own power struggles, a society you can look at a person and never know if they are with, which has it's own struggles and woes. I'm overstating, but that sort of society-within-a-society has been compared to Queer Culture since the first Changeling, and it applies here too. It less is me making parallels and more just a theme I guess. I probably am being unclear. Possibly because it is 4 am. Lemme know if I can better explain.<br /> <br /> <br /> ETA: Discussing Christmas songs the PCs could do in an act, Calamity doing &quot;Mistress for Christmas&quot; while Lorelei and Insincere Marguerite could do &quot;Baby It's Cold Outside&quot; just to play up their...odd dynamic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 02-02-2016, 05:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T08:51:50-08:00","id":821653,"title":"","content":"I think I get it. No worries.Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T16:31:50-08:00","id":821962,"title":"","content":"Regarding the Baroness' comment upon our plans for the inevitable Christmas show, I hope it also goes without saying that Lorelei will dress up in a red teddy, fishnets, and a stocking cap for a rollicking rendition of Eartha Kitt's &quot;Santa Baby.&quot;<br /> <br /> Okay, back to work on the next entry of Lori's Diary. It was a fun session, and I'm looking forward to recounting it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T21:18:05-08:00","id":822108,"title":"","content":"There were certainty some highs and lows...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T02:18:59-08:00","id":822209,"title":"","content":"Felt good to get a Calamity journal out again. Work looks like it will be less hectic so I should be back on track with the writing again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T01:31:19-08:00","id":830096,"title":"","content":"Insincere Marguerite\u2019s name is dragged into a monarch\u2019s lover\u2019s spat, Calamity has a strawberry milkshake, and Lori licks whipped cream off Sandoval. Then things get complicated.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XLIX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> Monday, November 3rd, evening<br /> <br /> Well, after yesterday\u2019s deposition, and shootings, and ghost scares, today was a nice, relaxing break. You know, for the most part. It started out on a light note, with Calamity belting out \u2018Love Stinks\u2019 while I made breakfast and the girls argued about Kevin Costner\u2019s butt double in Prince of Thieves. Calamity joined the argument a little before Lori and Oleander showed up and even managed to weave a clever web of words to trap Insincere Marguerite into complimenting a Canadian butt.<br /> <br /> To be fair, the butt conversation started because everyone (except Julia who thinks all dude butts look the same?) preferred it to talking about murder ghosts. We did fill Lori in on the ghost thing, which, you know, didn\u2019t really make her happy. Calamity went to the lighthouse and the children\u2019s library to talk to her Court\u2019s people about it. And to talk to Shi, about the note and the weirdness with Chalcedony.<br /> <br /> Chalcedony actually left first, since with everything out in the open, she was probably safe, you know? She promised she\u2019d be careful and let us know what kind of arrangements she made. I think Lori mentioned she\u2019d staying with Flores tonight and working some things out with friends for the next bit. Hopefully that\u2019ll be good and not get ruined by - I\u2019ll get to that later. Anyways, after she left, we discussed the weirdness a bit. Desiree really doesn\u2019t like her, and was not even sure Chalcedony had actually been shot at. All the details of the dude doing the shooting, such as they were, were the same though, so it seemed likely.<br /> <br /> I was worried that maybe that meant that Chalcedony was working with Hollywood, you know, and they told her the right things, but Desiree said that she\u2019d been an experiment and she was pretty sure they\u2019d wanted to see how it worked before messing with another of the Director\u2019s agents, so that probably wasn\u2019t a thing. Shi got thrown out there, since he, you know, can look like anybody, including a generic mook dude, but there\u2019s was still the details problem, as in how he\u2019d know. Calamity did point out that it was him who found the crystal machete, which hadn\u2019t been there when Insincere Marguerite searched the place. Oleander pointed out that Chalcedony and Ginny had broken up since the searching, so maybe she got it for protection after her protector wasn\u2019t around so much. I don\u2019t think she meant that Ginny was a threat - she\u2019s torn up about it, but still in love, you know?<br /> <br /> Anyways, we split up after a bit. Lori and Julia went off to have sex, Calamity to the lighthouse, Insincere Marguerite to practice and Jacob to talk with Boss Lowjack. Flores came by not too long later, bothered and upset. Apparently, Princess Jolie and Felicity had gotten into a big fight over Insincere Marguerite and Desiree. A fight that ended with them breaking up. Flores wanted to make sure those two knew about it, since they were involved, you know? She didn\u2019t stay long, leaving us with a hug and a kiss to go handle club business. She came back to see Insincere Marguerite perform though.<br /> <br /> Lori went right off to go see Princess Jolie. I managed to convince Insincere Marguerite to give us a preview, a \u2018dress rehearsal\u2019 for her act, and it was awesome! It was awesome during the show too, just great. She didn\u2019t, you know, dance-dance, but the strutting across the stage thing she did went perfect with the song. Everybody really liked it. Lori started mentioned working on another new act, and gave me an eye - I hope she doesn\u2019t think I\u2019m next to be on stage.<br /> <br /> Everybody got back a little before the show. Calamity pulled me aside pretty much right away. I guess she and somebody she talked to, Becky or Queen Charlotte probably, decided that Chalcedony was out of time to agree to let me try and help with the scripts and that she was going to get it done or die. She does have a good point - it\u2019s not actually another case of, you know, punishing someone preemptively. If she\u2019s on the up and up, then the scripts are overwriting her free will and we\u2019re helping her. If she\u2019s not, then we are legitimately defending ourselves. And giving her the option to choose, to actually choose. I really, really don\u2019t like the idea of messing around in someone\u2019s head without their consent, but if it\u2019s going to happen, it might as well be me. I do have the most experience, and I know my own intentions at least.<br /> <br /> The rest of the evening was more, you know, fun. I had to explain to Insincere Marguerite how \u2018American Thanksgiving\u2019 is about white people. It was something to do with an argument between Julia and De la Roche, I think. I\u2019m not sure I got anything through, but maybe a little more than \u201cit\u2019s about God or something\u201d. But she had to go get prepared, so our history lesson was cut short.<br /> <br /> We had a nice crowd. Lots of VIPs too - Queen Charlotte, Princess Jolie, Madame Spidertoes, the Handmaidens with Salk - as well as a lot of our regulars plus some. I spent most of the time chilling out with Dark Kimberly and White Maria. They were getting along pretty well, which was good. It was fun hanging out with Dark Kimberly, since we hadn\u2019t gotten to much, with her break up, you know?<br /> <br /> It did look like there was some kind of drama going on though. Queen Charlotte seemed happy, which is good. Princess Jolie was not so much, especially after she talked with Insincere Marguerite. Those two and Lori bounced between each other a lot, when Insincere Marguerite wasn\u2019t talking to Queen Charlotte. The Night Court trio stuck around for a long while, until Julia saw them off. Desiree had some kind of encounter with Scarlet that stirred things up a little. Calamity got me to check out their relationship, but given how weak the thread was, they probably hadn\u2019t met before tonight. Desiree certainly didn\u2019t, you know, think much of the Handmaiden, but I couldn\u2019t see anything that raised any red flags. Calamity didn\u2019t seem upset after talking with her either, so hopefully that\u2019s all fine.<br /> <br /> Madame Spidertoes is wandering around checking out ghost stuff. It seems a little weird that the ghost would be upset at dancers staying her but not living here, but I don\u2019t know how ghosts work. Calamity is working really hard on being able to deal with ghosts, so I\u2019m sure we\u2019ll have this dealt with soon. I should go see what she\u2019s up to...<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> So once again I find myself scrambling to get my thoughts down during a few scant moments of peace between big events. And this has been a day for big events, let me tell you.<br /> <br /> Okay, that paragraph makes it sound worse than it is. Nobody has been killed, there has not been an invasion from Arcadia, and as far as I know nobody has had any crushing personal realizations. But things are still moving behind the scenes in the Freehold\u2019s social structures, and these things might have far-reaching implications in the days to come.<br /> <br /> The day didn\u2019t start out quite so fraught, of course. I woke up late this morning in Oleander\u2019s arms, feeling warm and secure and loved. We talked a little as we got up and showered, and I mentioned my frustration at my own suspicions about Desiree. I used to be such a trusting person, and I\u2019ve considered Desiree a friend for some time now, but I just can\u2019t bring myself to buy into her act completely. Oleander calmed me down with soothing words, telling me that nobody who has trained themselves to be that good at lying has any right to expect people to trust them out of hand. She always knows just what to say to make me feel better about myself.<br /> <br /> We made our way over to the Dream House just in time for sex breakfast, where we joined a spirited discussion already in progress over the ethics of using a stunt-butt. Yes, I\u2019m serious. I\u2019m not sure how the conversation came up, but Marguerite was adamant that Kevin Costner had somehow \u201csold out\u201d by consenting to use a stand-in for his (somewhat tame) nude scene in that Robin Hood movie we watched a few months ago. I don\u2019t really claim to understand her position on this volatile subject; lots of actors use body-doubles for all sorts of reasons. Maybe Mr. Costner was insecure about his backside. Never having seen his ass in person, I can\u2019t say whether he has cause to be.<br /> <br /> Things got a little more serious as morning became afternoon. Apparently the long-dormant spirits who haunt the Dream House began to wake up last night. Calamity spoke with Monica \u2013 the more benevolent of the two ghosts, not our jade-hued friend \u2013 who warned her that the <u>other</u> spirit had stirred due to Chalcedony\u2019s presence. Apparently she\u2019s got a thing for dancers, and it\u2019s not safe for such people to spend the night in our house. I confess I got a little huffy at that point, as the ghost never saw fit to attack me\u2026 but the others seem to think that I\u2019m exempt from this curse due to the fact that I call the Dream House home.<br /> <br /> After Chalcedony left (promising that she would find somewhere else safe to stay tonight) talk turned to her close encounter with the Hollywood Courts. Desiree in particular seemed to think she was making the whole thing up, though Desiree\u2019s opinion of Chalcedony has never been high, so we should probably take her suggestions with a grain of salt. Then again, she did say that to the best of her knowledge Chalcedony was not a spy for the Hollywood Courts, so one has to wonder what they would have to gain by trying to kill her.<br /> <br /> I brought up a notion that has been bugging me: the unlikely but possible idea that Shi himself could have been the mysterious shooter, engaging in one of his pranks. Think about it; he can look like anyone, he delights in teaching people \u201clessons,\u201d and the attack did no real harm. The others didn\u2019t seem to think this was likely, so I let it lie after initially mentioning it.<br /> <br /> Calamity decided to visit the Lighthouse to ask her compatriots in the Autumn Court to look into the ghost problem, and to maybe ask around a bit about Shi and Chalcedony. She actually met the precocious kitsune while she was there, and the two of them spoke with Queen Charlotte together\u2026 apparently while enjoying milk shakes (Calamity\u2019s was strawberry). While I don\u2019t think Calamity learned anything concrete about whatever game Shi is playing, she did manage to secure Madame Spidertoes\u2019 assistance with our ghost problem and make Queen Charlotte aware of Chalcedony\u2019s reluctance to submit to Gawain\u2019s dream therapy.<br /> <br /> As a side note, Calamity also mentioned that Salk was there at the lighthouse, and it looks like he and Moon might be hooking up. Good for him! And her. Or hir. I really need to drag my pronouns kicking and screaming into the twenty-first century.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, back at the ranch, almost all of my honeys decided to leave me at the same time. Oleander and D both left for their respective jobs, each giving me a quick kiss on their way out the door. Marguerite decided to give her number a full dress rehearsal, and disappeared into the theater area to practice. I turned to Julia plaintively and asked if she was going to leave me too.<br /> <br /> Her eyes smoldered. \u201cYou want to go have sex?\u201d she asked breathily. She\u2019d been making eyes at me all through breakfast, so I wasn\u2019t particularly surprised.<br /> <br /> So there went the next hour or so of my day. And then I had to shower again.<br /> <br /> When the two of us rejoined the others in the theater area, we found that Flores had arrived, and she was very upset. She told us that Princess Jolie and Felicity had been fighting, and had sort of officially broken up. Their respective fascinations with Desiree and Insincere Marguerite seemed to be at the root of their problems, and Flores helpfully dropped by to let those two know what was going on before they ended up in the middle of that mess.<br /> <br /> Being both Jolie\u2019s friend and something of a nosy busybody, I decided to head over to Glamour Springs to see what I could do to help. I made it there in record time, only to find myself stuck in the waiting room while the Princess was cloistered with Becky. Things weren\u2019t too boring, however\u2026 White Maria and Chalcedony were engaged in a spirited game of darts. Their targets? Balloons filled with whipped cream, which dripped onto Sandoval, who was loosely bound to a chair. If one of them hit a balloon, they then got to \u201cclean\u201d him.<br /> <br /> Okay, so I took a couple of throws while I was waiting. Can you blame me?<br /> <br /> Dark Kimberly was also there, though she wasn\u2019t participating in the festivities. Things seemed at least cordial between her and White Maria, if still a little tense. The same can\u2019t be said for Becky\u2026 when she emerged from Jolie\u2019s inner sanctum, she rudely and obviously bumped into Dark Kimberly, but things didn\u2019t escalate beyond that point.<br /> <br /> Jolie was feeling awful, obviously, and there was very little I could do to help. I made myself available as a friend, of course, and let her (figuratively) cry on my shoulder for a while, but in the end I guess this is just something she\u2019s going to have to work out for herself. She did say that she would be at the Dream House later that night, and that she hoped to speak to Marguerite about this situation in the hopes that they could work something out. Even then I thought it was a long shot\u2026 but I\u2019m getting ahead of myself.<br /> <br /> I managed to make it out of Glamour Springs after only getting roped into a couple more rounds of darts, and made my way back to the Dream House to start preparing for the show. I only barely had time to register the fact that Calamity had returned, and that she was trying to talk to Gawain about the necessity of making Chalcedony submit to dream therapy to remove her scripts and triggers. As much as I sympathize with the big guy\u2019s ideals about personal freedom, I think Calamity has the right of it this time. If what we suspect about the Director is true, then she\u2019s being forced by her programming to deny him access to her dreams, and we\u2019ll actually be working in favor of her freedom by forcing her to act against her will. It\u2019s complicated, but I think it\u2019s true nonetheless.<br /> <br /> The show went well. I did one of my regular numbers, and I think I really hit it out of the park, but the stand-out performance was definitely Marguerite\u2019s debut. She was <u>amazing</u> tonight. All of her hard work really paid off, and I couldn\u2019t be happier for her. I know how difficult it can sometimes be for my Darklings to step out of their comfortable shadows and stand in the spotlight, and while I know Marguerite likes the attention, it still made me proud to see her strutting and fretting her hour upon the stage.<br /> <br /> Julia approached me as things were winding down, and sort of nervously asked if I would like to join her at her parents\u2019 house for Thanksgiving. I could tell that she was really tense about it, and I tried my best to calm her down as I told her that I\u2019d love to meet her family. She sort of sighed and thanked me, and then started working up her courage to ask D. She\u2019d already broached the subject with Marguerite, who had agreed to go.<br /> <br /> I should have known that it wouldn\u2019t be as simple with D, but I guess I wasn\u2019t thinking. She\u2019s very politically minded, and she identifies so closely with the Latino culture that I suppose I should have known that she\u2019s not a big supporter of the American holiday of Thanksgiving. A lot of people these days seem to associate it with a lie; the idea that the white Anglo-Saxon majority is trying to sugar-coat the rape of the New World and its people with a fairy tale about how the Native Americans welcomed the European settlers with open arms\u2026 and I suppose there\u2019s some truth to that. To me \u2013 possibly because of my father\u2019s influence \u2013 the holiday always represented the idea of the early colonists\u2019 gratitude to God for saving them from disease and starvation\u2026 the trouble that cropped up later between them and the natives was never really connected to the celebration itself.<br /> <br /> That wasn\u2019t what D needed to hear at that point, however. I tried to take a different tack, telling her that in this case it really wasn\u2019t about the holiday itself, but about doing something nice in support of Julia. I think I\u2019ve managed to convince her to come along, and I might have scored another bonus in the process\u2026 D confessed that it didn\u2019t feel right for her to meet Julia\u2019s family before she meets mine.<br /> <br /> \u201cThree more weeks before Thanksgiving, babe,\u201d I said pointedly, and she sort of blushed and muttered something noncommittal\u2026 but she also nodded, and said she\u2019d think about it.<br /> <br /> Lots of dignitaries were in the audience tonight, including Queen Charlotte, Princess Jolie, Madame Spidertoes, the handmaidens, and Salk. I made sure to speak with everyone as I worked the crowd, of course.<br /> <br /> Queen Charlotte seemed almost giddy over Jolie and Felicity\u2019s break-up, and I suppose I can\u2019t judge her too harshly for that. Who among us hasn\u2019t felt that thrill of schadenfreude when someone for whom we have feelings suddenly becomes romantically available? As she was feeling particularly well-disposed toward Marguerite at the moment, she asked me to convey to my French lover that she is moving forward with her plans to speak to the Paris Courts on her behalf. I promised to do so.<br /> <br /> I stopped at the Night Court\u2019s table after that. The Handmaidens were up to their usual games, flattering and flirting up a storm while making no secret of their desire to get into my panties. I admit that they\u2019re good at what they do, and they really are quite lovely\u2026 but when I think about what they did to poor Tamara it sort of puts things in perspective. Even if they have no such designs on me \u2013 which I\u2019m in no way willing to concede \u2013 I don\u2019t think I could fully relax around them know what they\u2019ve done. They asked me if I could arrange a tour of the premises for them (not-so-subtly implying that they\u2019d like to see the bedrooms), and I told them that I\u2019d check with the rest of the motley. Salk stayed out of the conversation for the most part, and seemed to be amused by their antics.<br /> <br /> I spoke ever-so-briefly with Jolie, and told her that I would let Marguerite know that she wanted a word. I did so a few minutes later, and tried to keep at least one eye on the two of them as they conversed. Things did not go well, and Jolie left in a huff shortly thereafter, obviously angry and very nearly in tears. I caught up to her in the parking lot and pulled her into a hug until she stopped trying to storm out and talked to me.<br /> <br /> She was very emotional, and I won\u2019t pretend that I remember every last thing that she said. The long and the short of it is that she asked Marguerite to either back off from Felicity or make some sort of claim so that everyone would know where they stand. Marguerite refused to do so without first speaking with Felicity about things. According to Jolie, Marguerite didn\u2019t seem to think it was important to take a firm stance on the subject, and either couldn\u2019t see or didn\u2019t care how much it was hurting her to be in limbo like this.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd I can\u2019t help but wonder,\u201d she said fiercely as she looked straight into my eyes, \u201chow she would feel if someone was toying with <u>you</u>, and taking you away from <u>her</u>.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sorry, Jolie,\u201d I said, kissing her forehead. \u201cI\u2019m <u>really</u> sorry. I\u2019ll talk to her. I can\u2019t promise anything; she\u2019s her own person and she\u2019s got a stubborn streak a mile wide, but I\u2019ll try to help if I can.\u201d I sighed. \u201cFelicity isn\u2019t good for her, and I think she knows that deep down. I know how I want this to end, and I think it would work out best for everyone\u2026 but she\u2019s got to come to that realization on her own.\u201d<br /> <br /> The Princess gave me a lingering kiss and a heartbreaking thank-you, and then drove off into the night for some solitude. I composed myself on the doorstep for a few minutes before returning the House.<br /> <br /> Madame Spidertoes is staying here tonight to help us deal with our ghost problem. I spoke with her briefly to thank her, and of course she told me to think nothing of it. She made a few cryptic remarks about the necessity of her staying with us tonight, and I think she might have made some very subtle veiled reference to sharing a bed with someone after her night\u2019s work was done\u2026 but I can\u2019t be sure.<br /> <br /> D made sure to tell me later that she\u2019d behave while Madame Spidertoes is around\u2026 but the bitter acid that creeps into her voice whenever that subject comes up hurts me. I mean, it <u>physically</u> hurts me, like an ache in my chest. I put my hands on her shoulders and forced her to look in my eyes. \u201cIt\u2019s okay, D,\u201d I said softly. \u201cReally. I\u2019m not going to go off on you again like I did the other day. I\u2019m past it.\u201d That\u2019s probably not entirely true, but I\u2019m getting there.<br /> <br /> D looked relieved, apologized for her vitriol, and gave me a soft kiss\u2026 a <u>real</u> kiss, the kind she saves just for me. Nobody else loves me like she does\u2026 probably not even Oleander.<br /> <br /> Then she asked me if she was going to have to beat the crap out of the Handmaidens\u2026 but she never got the chance. They spoke briefly with Desiree while I was otherwise engaged, and something she said spooked Scarlett badly. Natalia was busy trying to comfort her wife as I approached. I made my apologies for not giving them the tour they had requested before they left, but I could tell that their hearts weren\u2019t really in it anymore in any case. I have to wonder what Desiree knows about Scarlett that scares her that much\u2026 what can she know that\u2019s worse than what everyone else already suspects?<br /> <br /> So after that I spoke with Marguerite. I confess that I was a little angry with my girlfriend because she had so obviously hurt Jolie\u2019s feelings, but she was sanguine about the whole thing. She told me that she couldn\u2019t make any promises about her intentions toward Felicity because she didn\u2019t know what those intentions were herself yet. I get that, I truly do, but she was so callous about how her attitude was hurting the Princess that I confess my thoughts weren\u2019t particularly charitable at that point.<br /> <br /> \u201cFelicity\u2026 she has sent me several messages tonight. She wants to meet,\u201d Marguerite informed me.<br /> <br /> I sighed. \u201cI suppose we can\u2019t really put it off any longer,\u201d I admitted. \u201cIs tomorrow night okay? Do you want me with you?\u201d<br /> <br /> She smiled and said \u201calways,\u201d but there was a hunger behind her eyes that had nothing to do with me.<br /> <br /> I hope we\u2019re doing the right thing.<br /> <br /> Well, Madame Spidertoes is ready for her inspection now, and she wants the motley front and center, so I\u2019d better bring this entry to a close.<br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei Grace</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Today started off with a combination of silly and serious. The \u201csilly\u201d was a conversation about Kevin Costner and his \u201cbutt double\u201d in the movie \u201cPrince of Thieves.\u201d Not really sure how that conversation got started but there was quite the debate going on about that when Lori and Oleander got to the Dream House this morning. Since Lorelei had stayed at her girlfriend\u2019s house last night I took it upon myself to change the subject and mention the incident that happened last night with the ghosts and Chalcedony. That was the \u201cserious.\u201d While that kind of soured the mood in the room I thought it was important for Lori to know. We cannot have any of our non-resident dancers stay overnight at the House. It is dangerous to them, and possibly to us.<br /> <br /> In response to this Chalcedony said that she would find another place to stay tonight. Somewhere that someone can look out for her, just in case. She left shortly after that. Pretty much as soon as she stepped out the door Desiree asked the room if we thought that Chalcedony had actually been shot at. She seemed to disbelieve the other woman entirely. It was pointed out that Chalcedony\u2019s description of the shooter was remarkably similar to the person who shot at Desiree. Though I suppose it is possible that Chalcedony herself was the shooter and she just described her disguise when people asked. I do not know if there are any witnesses to the incident at her house. I did not think of this idea at the time, but should probably bring it up with the Motley at least. Question\u2026can Chalcedony change her appearance magically or otherwise?<br /> <br /> The question as to whether or not Chalcedony worked for the Hollywood Courts was also brought up and shot down. Desiree said that when she was infiltrating their Courts and subsequently being reprogramed she did not see Chalcedony. She might have worked for the Hollywood Courts before or after that point however. It all depends on how such activities might fit into her timeline. How long ago she arrived here and where she was found would play into determining the validity of that idea. If I remember correctly she arrived around the time most of us did, so it doesn\u2019t seem likely.<br /> <br /> Lori brought up the idea that Shi could have been the one to do the shooting as a prank. He can make himself look like anyone he wants to. The only problem with that idea is that his pranks are not usually lethal, and the person that shot Desiree did some serious damage. I can see shooting someone with a paintball gun or water gun as a prank, but anything with metal projectiles would cease to be amusing to me.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite also brought up the fact that the blue machete was not in Chalcedony\u2019s closet the last time she went through the place. So, it\u2019s been purchased since then. I think in that meantime there was more of a falling out between Chalcedony and Desiree. I mean, those two have never liked one another, but this was apparently noticeable even for them. Did Chalcedony feel the need to protect herself or did she get that weapon with the intent to harm to someone, namely Desiree? She might have felt the need to get a weapon since she broke things off with Ginny who has been her protector and supporter to date. Every time we find out something new it just seems to raise more questions. I would really like to see the end game for this whole thing.<br /> <br /> In an effort to get some answers Calamity decided to go to the Autumn Court and talk to some folks specifically about Chalcedony and Shi. She also went to talk to Becky about Chalcedony\u2019s refusal to let Gawain remove the triggers/scripts in her head. It is possible that we may need to go against Chalcedony\u2019s wishes in this matter if it means keeping the Freehold safe. Becky offered to put a word in with Princess Jolie about this and to get her \u201cgo ahead.\u201d She may also be able to summon Chalcedony in and give her the option to submit or be forced in the matter.<br /> <br /> After that Calamity went to the Lighthouse to talk to Shi about Chalcedony. Ginny was also there, which made things more interesting. Something negative was said about Chalcedony and Ginny slammed Shi against the wall and held him there. She eventually let him down and excused herself from the conversation. Once she was gone Calamity expressed her concerns about Insincere Marguerite and her fascination with Chalcedony. It was also suggested that Ginny might have had the same thing going on. She has been rather smitten with the blue woman lately and when they broke it off Ginny took it rather hard. It sounds like she\u2019s still taking it rather hard.<br /> <br /> Then last but not least the pair of them went to talk to Queen Charlotte with the same concerns about our lady in blue. They mentioned that some people will be talking to Jolie about getting permission to help Chalcedony and remove the scripts that the Director put in her head. Charlotte says that she will lend her support even if Jolie doesn\u2019t want to do anything. She also said that she will go over Jolie\u2019s head if it becomes necessary. Hopefully that will not be needed, but it is good to know that one of the monarchs will go to greater lengths should it become necessary. Honestly I\u2019m not sure that there would be much of a question about the outcome of that particular conversation if it was any other Monarch. The rest seem sensible enough and I don\u2019t doubt that they would want to do what was in the best interest of the Freehold. Jolie on the other hand frequently seems to be ruled by her desires, which is not always a good thing.<br /> <br /> It was these same desires that led to Felicity and Jolie having a big fight about Insincere Marguerite and Desiree. Flores came to the Dream House to specifically talk to the latter two ladies about what had happened. Flores said that the fight was not violent and that it was something to do with Jolie wanting to keep Desiree nearby and the Spring Queen throwing the whole thing with Insincere Marguerite in Felicity\u2019s face. I can understand that Jolie has feelings for Desiree and wants to keep her safe, but she needs to worry about her own safety as well. I don\u2019t think Desiree would try anything against Jolie right now since there is so much attention on her at the moment, but she is an admitted Loyalist. She just went through all the information she gathered on the Hollywood Courts, specifically about the Monarchs, strengths, weaknesses, alliances, etc\u2026 She could very well be gathering the same information on our Freehold. It\u2019s probably a bit late to be worried about that considering how long Desiree has been here, but I think it\u2019s still something to think about. Jolie seems to be blind to those concerns though.<br /> <br /> Ever the busy one, Calamity also went to talk to Madame Spidertoes to discuss our little ghost problem in the House. She told us that Spidertoes said that she\u2019d look into making this issue a priority. Which is a good thing in my book. The elder Autumn Courtier also said that she would come for the show and be staying at the Dream House tonight, specifically in the \u201cMurder Ghost\u201d room. I\u2019m sure that Calamity will be helping Spidertoes with the ghost. She has abilities that allow her to see unmaterialized spirits, which is a distinct advantage if you ask me. I\u2019ll have to ask her if that ability also lets her hit unmaterialized ghosts or not.<br /> <br /> While all this was going on, before Calamity got back, Gawain asked Insincere Marguerite if she wanted to do a dress rehearsal of her act and she said sure. I forgot the name of the song that she danced/strutted to, but her act was really good. I don\u2019t think that our Marguerite has anything to worry about when it comes to the performance tonight. If she does anything close to what she did for us then she\u2019ll be just fine. Also while all of this was going on Lorelei decided to go and talk to Jolie. I think she was going to try and find out what was going on with the fight between Felicity and Jolie. Those two seemed so inseparable lately and now this happens. Not sure what\u2019s going on with them. I\u2019m not as close to the Spring Monarch as Lori is, so I figure I\u2019ll let her handle what\u2019s going on with that.<br /> <br /> I went on a self-appointed errand this afternoon as well. I went to go talk to Lowjack and see if needed me to do anything in light of the whole Desiree thing. He admitted that there\u2019s not much for me to do at the moment besides keeping an eye on her and let him know if she does anything suspicious. He admitted that Jolie and Charlotte are the two holdouts when it comes to a Pledge with Desiree to make sure that she\u2019s not a threat to the Freehold. I\u2019m not sure why they are waiting. Do they not think a Pledge is a good idea or are they trying to make sure the phrasing is just right? I also voiced my concerns about Chalcedony and her avoidance of getting her scripts removed. Lowjack\u2019s suggestion to that was to talk to Charlotte. Seemed like a good idea to me, so I made a note to do that.<br /> <br /> After that I brought up the subject that I\u2019ve been a bit hesitant about bringing up. I asked Lowjack if there was any further information about the Loyalist that thought recruiting either me or Insincere Marguerite would be a good idea. He said that there was nothing new on that, and that he was not worried about it. I asked if it might have been Rook and he said it was someone different. They\u2019re not sure who it was since they only found the correspondence and did not see who left the note. I will admit that it is comforting to know that my Monarch has enough faith in me to not worry about me becoming a Loyalist again. It always seems that the former addict is the first or most vocal in speaking out against drugs. I wonder if it works the same way with loyalties. Are those that served the Gentry and left more likely to turn against offers to return? I know that I at least have no desire to return. There are some aspects of my life with the Lady that I do miss, but not enough to go back to her service. I miss the comradery that I had with Rook. I miss the autonomy I had when it came to fulfilling my orders and I sometimes miss the power that I wielded. I had more power over snow and ice when I worked for the Lady, but I lost that when I left. I suppose I could say that I gave it up when I fled. Or perhaps she took it back? It was a gift from the Lady and I had turned my back on her.<br /> <br /> I think I heard when I got back from talking to Lowjack that Calamity had talked to Gawain about Chalcedony and the importance of removing the scripts. I know Gawain would not be okay with forcing someone to do something so I\u2019m sure Calamity was careful how she phrased things. We need to have Gawain on board with this whole thing as he\u2019s the best equipped to help her out.<br /> <br /> When she was free I took Calamity aside to talk to her about the Chalcedony issue and Lowjack\u2019s idea that we talk to Queen Charlotte about it. This was all before I knew that she\u2019d already done just that. She assured me that things had been taken care of already. I also brought up that I would feel more comfortable if Desiree would take an Oath with the Monarchs to do no harm to the Freehold. I suggested that if Desiree was the one that brought up the idea of an Oath to Jolie and Charlotte, they may be more positively disposed towards the idea. Desiree herself has said that she will take an Oath, so I don\u2019t think she\u2019d have any problems bringing up the idea to the Monarchs.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> I think the show overall went well. Insincere Marguerite\u2019s number was really well done and the crowd certainly enjoyed it. Lorelei was her usual amazing self on stage, as was everyone else. I\u2019ll admit that I didn\u2019t pay attention to all of the acts. I always try and watch those acts put on by my motley mates though. We also had some notable guests tonight. Madame Spidertoes and Queen Charlotte were both here, as was Salk and the Handmaidens. Dark Kimberly and White Maria were here, and markedly not at each other\u2019s throats. I think there has been a mellowing of the feelings of pure hate between those two lately. Hopefully that is a good thing. Normally I would assume that lessening of hostility to be a good thing, but if it\u2019s just the calm before a storm I want to have time to take shelter.<br /> <br /> Our social butterflies made their way around the room tonight. Calamity went to go to talk to Charlotte and the Queen brought up that she wanted to speak to Insincere Marguerite about talking to the Paris Courts on her behalf. Apparently Charlotte is in a very good mood about the whole fight with Jolie and Felicity and feels inclined to be charitable towards my Darkling friend. Lori talked to the Handmaidens briefly. From what Lori said, they requested a tour of the house. Lorelei said that she\u2019d ask the rest of us about it before leaving. After that she talked to Chalcedony and Flores about where the blue aspected singer was going to stay tonight. Apparently she will be staying with a couple of people and should be safe. I\u2019ll admit though that I wasn\u2019t all that worried about her safety. If anyone has the possibility of getting shanked it\u2019s the admitted Loyalist, not the suspected one. After that the two of them, Calamity and Lori, both went to go talk to Spidertoes. They discussed the plans for Spidertoes to stay the night in the \u201cMurder Ghost\u201d room and see what she can do about the dangerous spectre.<br /> <br /> There was a little bit of excitement at the end of the show\u2026so to speak. Insincere Marguerite went over to talk to Jolie, presumably about the fight that happened earlier between Jolie and Felicity. I don\u2019t know what was said, but whatever it was made Marguerite mad. After that Insincere Marguerite went to talk to Lori. I don\u2019t know what was said there either, but it didn\u2019t calm things down any. If anything it might have made Marguerite more upset. She stormed out of the room after the talk was over. Maybe I\u2019ll wait a bit until she\u2019s calmed down to see if she\u2019s okay.<br /> <br /> I have to admit that I found myself endeared to Desiree tonight. I saw that earlier she went over to talk to the Handmaidens, Scarlett in particular, and when she left there was a look of honest fear on the Handmaiden\u2019s face. I don\u2019t know what was said, but I will admit to being curious. I am still not happy with the Handmaidens after they nearly killed Tamara. I saw that Calamity talked to Desiree after that. Not sure if she found out what made Scarlett so scared or not. I will need to see if Calamity knows anything, and/or if she can tell it if she does. I know that Desiree did express an interest to Calamity that she would like to stay in the Freehold if possible. If she\u2019s allowed to that is. If she is not allowed to stay she says that she will travel the world and explore. That\u2019s what she says anyway. I\u2019m not sure if she\u2019d go back to her Keeper or not. She did not leave on bad terms, nor did she have an unpleasant experience while in his service. Granted I didn\u2019t have a disagreeable time working for the Lady either. It was only after I went against her wishes that things turned sour in our relationship. And she is unfortunately one to hold a grudge.<br /> <br /> I remember once the Lady entertained a minor Gentry as a guest. He brought a small entourage with him and they all enjoyed the Lady\u2019s hospitality. The other Gentry, The Duke of Dormant Winter was as his name implies was also a winter aspected ruler. He rather enjoyed being on good terms with the Lady of Winter Winds and relished staying for short visits over the years. He tried to court the Lady once, but she was not interested. He on the other hand was interested in her, but he was also interested in her Treasures. He rather admired Desire, who lived up to her name in any way you can imagine. He admired her so much that during one of his visits he tried to steal her away from the Lady. That was his last mistake.<br /> <br /> Rook and I overheard him talking to his servants one evening, or what passed for evening in that realm. We did our duty and reported what we\u2019d heard to the Lady. When the Lady of the Winter Winds found out about his treachery she reacted swiftly. By her reasoning we had heard enough for him to be deemed guilty. Granted we had actually heard him and his people planning on how they were going to sneak Desire out of the realm. It was a clever idea I\u2019ll give him that, but he was not counting on us hearing him. The Lady almost stormed into his quarters to confront him herself, but then thought better of it. We had brought the news to the Lady and she decided that it would be our treat to kill the would-be thief. So, we armed ourselves and went to confront the Duke. He did not take kindly to our accusations and called us liars. The Lady, who had come with us to watch, smiled her terrible smile and told him that her Knights are loyal to her and that we did not lie. With a wave of her hand the Duke\u2019s servants had been encased in ice, leaving just the minor Gentry for us to take care of.<br /> <br /> It was a long fight I remember that. He was not as powerful in the Lady\u2019s realm as he would have been in his own, but he was still the strongest opponent that we ever faced. His attacks, when they hit, were crippling, but thanks to the Lady\u2019s grace we felt no pain as we fought. He fought with a short sword and his ice powers. We fought with our knives and our own wintry gifts. In the end we managed, despite both being badly wounded, to whittle him down and eventually kill him. It was a practiced dual strike by both of us that brought him down. After he fell we presented ourselves to the Lady and dedicated the death to her. She smiled at us in her terrifyingly beautiful way and bade us sit with her. She then laid her hands on Rook\u2019s shoulders and frost started to cover his wounds. And when the frost flaked off he was healed. While she saw to my brother I started to fade. I\u2019m fairly certain that I was dying, and the last thing I saw before I passed out was her hand reaching out to cup my face. I woke later in my room, alive and whole. I found on my desk two new knives made of the bluest ice. They were weapons made for princes, and here I was receiving them from my Lady. I\u2019d never been so proud to be her servant.<br /> <br /> The Lady never did trust that Gentry again. Her anger towards him remained fresh in her mind and he was never invited back, once he recovered from us killing him of course. It wasn\u2019t until later that I found myself on the receiving end of her anger and rage. In her mind I was stealing her Treasure away from her. I was stealing Delight. I didn\u2019t let Rook take her back and to this day the Lady is denied her prize. I don\u2019t know if Diane ever really realized what she did for me when I was a guest of her Freehold. I wonder sometimes if she still thinks of me as a monster, or if she saw the changes her kindness had wrought. A part of me would like to think that she could see the good starting to come through, though I know it isn\u2019t likely that anyone from her Freehold saw me fighting Rook to protect Diane. In their eyes I\u2019m still the monster that took her in the first place and came to bring her back. Sometimes I don\u2019t know how my motley mates look at me and not see the same thing. I suppose I should be happy for the blinders of friendship.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> <u><b>No, I Regret Nothing</b></u><br /> <br /> \u201cBon-Bon?\u201d<br /> <br /> Julia entered dining room. Insincere Marguerite sat in a chair facing the wall, a complete lack of expression on her face.<br /> <br /> \u201cMay I talk to you, Bon-Bon?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat do you want, Julia?\u201d Irritated.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2026just\u2026well your birthday is coming up, I wanted to ask what you wanted to do for it. I mean, we could all go out, we could find an abandoned hospital to creep into\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite looked up and stared at Julia with disbelief.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell we hadn\u2019t talked about it,\u201d The willowy girl said quickly with a forced shrug.<br /> <br /> The Lurker sighed. \u201cJulia I don\u2019t feel like discussing this right now. I am sorry.\u201d<br /> <br /> Julia looked at her, her expression hardening. \u201cI don\u2019t either. Insincere Marguerite, I am worried about you. Listen I don\u2019t\u2026do\u2026a lot of social stuff well. Translate this from Aspie to English, if you would, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite raised an eyebrow \u201cI\u2026what?\u201d<br /> <br /> Julia walked up and took Insincere Marguerite\u2019s hands in her own. \u201cI love you. I need you. I always want to be with you. Lorelei loves you. Maria loves you. Hell, Flores loves you\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite opened her mouth, but Julia put her hand on her knee. \u201cOne more moment, my love.\u201d Insincere Marguerite nodded.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe belong to each other. I belong to you. We are Oathed, Pledged. If this is your problem, it is mine too. And I will get through it with you, or fail with you. Your fate is also my own.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut\u2026Julia my crimes are not yours. And\u2026My Dearest does not know you!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe will\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd you will try to kill her!\u201d Insincere Marguerite sat up sharply.<br /> <br /> Julia had an eerie calm settle over her face. \u201cOnly if she is not your friend. I don\u2019t hate Felicity because you like her so much. Okay, maybe a little, but not enough to hurt her. I want to hurt her because I do not believe she has your best interests in mind. Indeed, I think she is using you.\u201d<br /> <br /> The Tunnelgrub looked skeptical.<br /> <br /> Julia continued, \u201cWhite Maria is not my favorite person, though she is, I confess, extremely pretty and talented. But still she is not using you whether she is a jerk or not. You are getting the same thing from each other. What you don\u2019t get, and I can\u2019t seem to communicate, is Felicity is not your friend, as far as I can tell. And I don\u2019t really think Chalcedony is either, though I don\u2019t know for sure. \u201c<br /> <br /> \u201cYou think she could use me?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t know why she and Lord Leonidas broke up, but what better way to win him back than bring the most infamous thief the Night Court has ever had to heel? The one who humiliated him? And she is so aristocratic!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou think she threw her relationship with Princess Jolie away for another shot at being Lord Leonidas\u2019 girl?\u201d<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know,\u201d the Artist replied with a sigh, \u201cBut I don\u2019t trust her, and I think she at least originally saw you as a distraction and a challenge.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLike I saw her as, hein? \u201c Insincere Marguerite looked away.<br /> <br /> Julia moved so Insincere Marguerite faced her again. \u201cI don\u2019t care. I don\u2019t care how good or evil you are. It does not matter. My lot is with you, now. I\u2019m yours,\u201d She leans forward.<br /> <br /> \u201cDeal with it.\u201d<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite looked down, then up.<br /> <br /> \u201cVery well, Julia. I will deal with it. \u201c<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat is our plan then, Bon-Bon? With Felicity? With Yvette?\u201d Julia cocked her head.<br /> <br /> \u201cI must speak with Felicity,\u201d The Lurker sat up. \u201cI can decide nothing until I do so. You, Jolie\u2026everyone wants answers. I can give none until I speak to her. I can only wait, and hope I retain myself.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd Yvette?\u201d<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite gave her lover a long look.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe wait. When we find her, we decide how to add her to our family.\u201d<br /> <br /> Julia exhaled. This would be harder than she thought.<br /> <br /> \u201cOur family, Julia.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOur Family.\u201d<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XLIX</i><br /> <br /> It\u2019s hir, Lori.<br /> <br /> What isn\u2019t that how people usually play darts? I assume that\u2019s why I was not allowed to play darts as a kid.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite\u2019s song was \u201c<i>Non, Je Ne Regrette Rien</i>\u201d (aka that song from <i>Inception</i>) sung slow and sensual. She does not have near Lori\u2019s pool, though Lori bolstered her with Verdant Spring level one. She got five successes, good enough. Calamity did similarly on her roll with \u201c<i>Love Stinks</i>\u201d<br /> <br /> Next session is Session 50, on Valentine\u2019s Day! We had brownies! We will have journals, too, in two weeks. Comments and Questions Welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This