ser_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T19:18:02-08:00","id":838362,"title":"","content":"Becky into dark Kimberly.<br /> <br /> Also, safe travel's tomorrow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T20:43:43-08:00","id":838423,"title":"","content":"Ah right. <br /> <br /> Fair cop. And thanks","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T19:01:25-08:00","id":839611,"title":"","content":"Changeling back from Vacation edition. I am sort of swamped, so getting these up without much commentary. That\u2019s okay, role playing heavy anyway so not much to comment on. Oh, except it is Session 50! Huzzah!<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite\u2019s journal is unfinished, but better a partial journal than none at all. It does stop abruptly. Presumably she was interrupted. We get a Calamity though.<br /> <br /> <i>Session L</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> Evening, Nov 4th<br /> <br /> So, having Madame Spidertoes over for sex breakfast was mostly less, you know, awkward than I kinda expected. I mean, it was a little - De la Roche was pretty awkwardly attentive - but Lori seemed mostly not upset and it went alright. The breakfast burritos were a hit anyway.<br /> <br /> Madame Spidertoes had stayed the night to make sure her wards held up, or cause she got tired from making them, I\u2019m not sure. She taught Calamity how to do it herself too, since she stayed back to, you know, protect Madame Spidertoes in case the ghost got angry. So now we can keep her out until we\u2019re ready to deal with her.<br /> <br /> Julia and Lori went off to get baked while Madame Spidertoes did all that and Insincere Marguerite crawled off into the vents. She was still real upset from whatever happened with Princess Joli I think. So me and Jacob and Desiree hung out at the bar. I asked Desiree about the deal with Scarlet. According to her, Scarlet was an example of the horrible types of people that left Arcadia, of the horrible things they did to do so. She\u2019d thought maybe it was just stories, but with the way Scarlet reacted, you know...<br /> <br /> What Desiree was told was that, in order to make sure her Keeper was unprepared to stop her escape, she killed every other Changeling under their control. Over 20 of them. It was in Arcadia. We... we do things in Arcadia, especially to escape. That is an awful lot of people but... it\u2019s a hard question. Then again, she also supposedly killed a bunch of rivals for Natalya\u2019s affection, here on Earth, including a Queen of Night in Ukraine. I guess it mostly just reinforces that she\u2019s dangerous. Desiree was pretty sure they\u2019re trying to kill Lori - that they can even make it so she\u2019d consent, in the end, like she was pretty sure they got Tamara to.<br /> <br /> She was worried about Becky too. I mean, she\u2019s in love with Princess Joli and all and that doesn\u2019t just, you know, stop cause you\u2019re not their type. It might very well be easier on Becky if Sandoval was Claviger. Plus, apparently Latinos are off limits for Monarchs to date, so it won\u2019t even potentially become a thing? I don\u2019t really follow the political logic - they\u2019re becoming a more powerful demographic, so no committed sex? - but people are weird. I do understand that people are afraid of change, I guess that\u2019s it mostly.<br /> <br /> After a bit, I gathered Calamity up from her glass work and we headed off to bed. I think I saw Jacob leaving an offering of cognac and cheese near the vent at the bar. There was plenty of giggling coming from Lori\u2019s room. I heard them going on about Mexican food (munchies, you know?), so I went with burritos for breakfast.<br /> <br /> After Madame Spidertoes left, we got to planning movie night. We got sidetracked onto who would survive a horror movie. Calamity decided it was her, with the reasoning that she was either super plucky or the monster and, you know, they always \u2018survive\u2019. We wound up deciding on \u201cBut I\u2019m a Cheerleader\u201d and \u201cGoonies\u201d for movie night. De la Roche was really excited for \u201cBut I\u2019m a Cheerleader\u201d and \u201cGoonies\u201d was a last minute replacement for \u201cThe NeverEnding Story\u201d, since Lori hadn\u2019t seen it.<br /> <br /> That decided, we had a few hours of waiting for Felicity to come over. Insincere Marguerite was super nervous about it. She even asked Lori for rules to go by which Lori really didn\u2019t wanna give. Julia\u2019s still certain that Felicity is manipulating Insincere Marguerite. She definitely wants to kill the Day Courtier. She\u2019s keeping it under control and all, but it could get, you know, exciting.<br /> <br /> The meeting itself went well, I think. I boosted Insincere Marguerite\u2019s self control, and when Felicity showed up, I checked her motivation, which was to be seduced by Insincere Marguerite. I texted that to Lori, who was chaperoning them, which is just weird to say. She told us later that both of them were really, you know, conflicted about things - Felicity wanted closure, revenge for what Insincere Marguerite had done to her ex, the Day King, and the illicit thrill of being seduced by an enemy; Insincere Marguerite wanted to get closure in some way as well, but also to capture and control her. Still, like I said, it went well and they\u2019re going to go on a date in a couple of days.<br /> <br /> While that was going on, Salk showed up. I didn\u2019t really follow what he was after at first. He kept saying he wanted assurances that Scarlet would be safe at the Dream House, that \u2018his lambs\u2019 were very distraught, still. I guess I was mostly worried that he wanted some kind of weregild thing for whatever suffering Desiree\u2019s comments had caused, so I used the Contract of Potential to figure out what he really wanted, which was to see if he could weasel out some leverage on Scarlet. That made me really glad I hadn\u2019t, you know, called Desiree in, just taken him to Calamity in the office.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s where we all met up to share, and since Insincere Marguerite had wandered off to get herself together, we did some more planning for her surprise birthday party tomorrow. Mostly about the cake. We decided against Jacob jumping out of a cake cause we\u2019d just done that. We decided against ever mentioning the idea of someone jumping into a cake ever again, cause Ace would do it. We decided against a \u2018buttcake\u2019, stunt or not, cause Lori wouldn\u2019t say it without, you know, giggling madly for at least a few minutes. We did decide I was going to cook something delicious with the imported cheese Julia had gotten, a baked Camembert, probably and, I dunno, something to go along with it.<br /> <br /> After a bit we all split up again. Calamity was dreamcrafting something for Becky. I dunno what the others were up to, but Jacob checked up on Insincere Marguerite and then we sparred a bit before movie time. De la Roche recommended we do Goonies first, so the \u2018hormones\u2019 But I\u2019m a Cheerleader evoked wouldn\u2019t interfere with that. Goonies was a great time - Julia and Lori got a bit hung up on One Eyed Willie\u2019s name and there was the usual confusion about the oh so scary octopus, but it was all fun. But I\u2019m a Cheerleader was awesome too. I can see why De la Roche liked it.<br /> <br /> Before we headed off to bed, De la Roche cajoled us into informally agreeing that none of us would, you know, go off alone with the Handmaidens or let them go off alone with anyone at the Dream House. She was really bothered by the way they looked at Lori and Jacob. Plus, she know how the hunger for life force feels for a Leechfinger. Apparently she usually feeds it when she gets in fistfights, which seems fair enough. She\u2019s already punching them, you know?<br /> <br /> We did all agree - it made good sense - and headed off to bed, which is where I need to get myself. We still haven\u2019t heard from Princess Joli, Queen Charlotte or Chalcedony about the dream therapy thing and I haven\u2019t had a chance to talk with Calamity about the Claviger thing. But it was nice to have that break and just relax. All that stuff will be here tomorrow.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Well, that could have gone better\u2026 but on the bright side I suppose it could have gone a lot worse, too.<br /> <br /> So after her chat with Princess Jolie last night, Marguerite got very depressed and said she needed to be alone. I think she knew that she needed to come to some sort of resolution in the matter of Felicity, but she didn\u2019t know what to do about it. In any case, she crawled up into the vents and didn\u2019t emerge for the rest of the evening.<br /> <br /> After the crowds had cleared, Madame Spidertoes announced her intention to investigate the ghostly activity in the house, and Calamity offered to assist her (hoping to learn how it\u2019s done, so that we can better prepare for such incidences in the future, I think). D also offered her assistance, but she kept sort of nervously glancing in my direction, like she wasn\u2019t sure she was doing the right thing. Finally, she walked over to me and asked me point blank if I was okay with it.<br /> <br /> I smiled at her, trying my best to hide any lingering nervousness about her feelings for her ex. \u201cYou don\u2019t need my permission, D\u2026 you know that.\u201d<br /> <br /> She shook her head and gave me a nervous grin. \u201cIt\u2019s not about permission,\u201d she said softly, \u201cI just want to know if you\u2019re okay with it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI trust you, D,\u201d I told her, punctuating the sentiment with a brief kiss, \u201cand I know that no matter what happens, you\u2019ll come back to me.\u201d<br /> <br /> She gave me a real smile then, and a firmer kiss. \u201cI won\u2019t be too late,\u201d she promised, and then she was gone.<br /> <br /> I was left standing by the stairs with Julia, who kept darting plaintive glances at the vents. After a moment, she sighed. \u201cI need to get baked,\u201d she said, her frustration plain in her voice. \u201cCare to join me?\u201d<br /> <br /> I thought about it for a few seconds, but getting high seemed like a pretty good way to stave off my own agitation. The two of us made our way up to my room and then out on to the balcony, where my girlfriend produced some truly <u>quality</u> weed, and we proceeded to get blitzed out of our minds. I won\u2019t claim to remember much of what we actually said to each other last night, but I know that it was fucking hilarious.<br /> <br /> I know at some point we headed down to the kitchen for nachos. Madame Spidertoes was still doing her creepy occult stuff in the basement at that point, and we were still level-headed enough that we didn\u2019t want to screw up whatever she was trying to accomplish, so we just sort of grabbed a bag of chips and some salsa and brought it all up to the balcony. We\u2019d made it through about half of the bag when I noticed some movement out of the corner of my eye. D had come back to our room, and she was getting undressed for bed. At the time I couldn\u2019t figure out why she hadn\u2019t let me know she was back, but in retrospect I guess she was trying to work through the intense emotions that Spidertoes\u2019 presence always evokes in her. Considering how she usually works through her intense emotions, I can understand why she wouldn\u2019t want me around for that.<br /> <br /> Not that I think D would <u>ever</u> hurt me. Not in a million years.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I decided that I\u2019d had enough weed and chips for one night, and slipped into my room, where D was unconvincingly pretending to be asleep. I shed my clothes as quickly and quietly as I could, slipped under the covers, and snuggled up against her back. I drifted off to sleep almost immediately, but I think D stayed awake for most of the night.<br /> <br /> When I woke up, I was sandwiched between D and Julia, both of whom were snoring softly. Julia had her head pillowed on my right breast (of course\u2026 sometimes I\u2019m honestly surprised that she hasn\u2019t tried to write her name on my boobs in indelible marker) and D\u2019s breath was warm and comforting on my neck, while her hand rested possessively on my belly. I thought about how lucky I am for a few minutes, and realized that I would be perfectly happy to just stay like that all day.<br /> <br /> Then I caught the scent of breakfast burritos wafting up from the kitchen, and my stomach growled in a most unladylike fashion, which made me laugh. That woke up both of my partners, and after a brief yet intense debate, we agreed that food was a marginally more immediate necessity than sex. We threw on some clothes (I just grabbed a silk kimono-style robe out of my closet, actually), and made our way downstairs.<br /> <br /> The gang was all assembled, including Madame Spidertoes (who seemed highly amused to be included in the now-infamous \u201cSex Breakfast\u201d tradition) and Marguerite, who had finally emerged from her self-imposed exile in the ventilation system and rejoined the camaraderie of the motley. The darkling matriarch said her goodbyes a short while later, after we had given her our most sincere thanks for her help in ensuring the security of our home.<br /> <br /> After sex breakfast came the most difficult part of my day\u2026 though I\u2019m sure it was even more trying for Marguerite, in a way. Felicity came over to the Dream House so that she and Marguerite could talk things out and decide how to proceed. Marguerite asked me to \u201cchaperone\u201d the meeting to make sure that she didn\u2019t regress as she had in Felicity\u2019s presence in the past. Of course I agreed to do so. I didn\u2019t have high hopes for the meeting, though I recognized it as a necessity.<br /> <br /> Things actually went pretty well, all things considered. I\u2019d be lying if I said I was entirely pleased by the outcome, but as I said before, it could have been much worse. As the two of them spoke, I took a peek at their hidden desires to see if I could glean anything about their respective intentions. Each of them has a dark side they\u2019re suppressing\u2026 but honestly, the same thing could be said of just about anyone. In Marguerite\u2019s case, there\u2019s a part of her that wants to possess Felicity, to keep her hoarded away from anyone else who might desire her\u2026 like she did with Yvette in Arcadia. In Felicity\u2019s case, she\u2019d like a little payback against the girl who humiliated her ex-boyfriend, the Day King\u2026 but she also gets a naughty little thrill from the idea of humiliating him further by being with Marguerite.<br /> <br /> Stronger than any of these repressed desires, however, was a genuine interest and attraction. I know, it surprised the hell out of me too. Things were remarkably polite throughout the exchange, and I began to wonder whether I really needed to be there at all\u2026 but I\u2019m glad I was. I tried to gently steer the conversation along appropriate paths, and I think I must have succeeded on some level. Whenever either one of them seemed to be on the verge of giving in to their darker urges, I did what I could to bring out their more positive aspects, and both of them seemed a little more at ease by the time they parted.<br /> <br /> I confess that I also tried to subtly discourage the two of them from getting together in any serious way. It didn\u2019t make much of a difference in the end, but I had to try, and I\u2019m not sorry I did it. I know that as a member of the Spring Court it\u2019s sort of inimical to my nature to dampen the flames of passion\u2026 but I still don\u2019t think this relationship will be good for Marguerite, and I hated to see that look of despair on Princess Jolie\u2019s face last night.<br /> <br /> The two of them have decided to attempt a romantic relationship, to see if they\u2019re compatible. They\u2019re going to take things slowly at first, with an actual date rather than an erotic rendezvous, and I think that\u2019s a hopeful sign. I didn\u2019t see any indications that Marguerite is playing a long game here, hoping to \u201ccollect\u201d Felicity and claim her as a possession. But I have a wary eye on her, and I don\u2019t intend to relax my scrutiny any time soon.<br /> <br /> Just before she said her goodbyes to Felicity, I pulled Marguerite aside for a little talk. I told her that I thought the meeting went well (she smiled and agreed almost shyly), but that I was still worried about her.<br /> <br /> She sighed but nodded. \u201cYou will keep the watch on me, non?\u201d she asked seriously.<br /> <br /> I nodded in turn. \u201cCount on it,\u201d I said. She gave me a hurt expression, and I felt the need to explain myself. \u201cIt\u2019s not that I don\u2019t trust you, Marguerite,\u201d I said, pulling her into an embrace. \u201cI\u2019m worried about you. We all are. I love you, and I don\u2019t want to lose you.\u201d<br /> <br /> She returned my hug. \u201cYou will never lose me, cheri,\u201d she avowed firmly.<br /> <br /> I shook my head. \u201cI hope not. But\u2026\u201d and then it came pouring out, everything that\u2019s really been bothering me about this whole situation. \u201cMarguerite, I\u2019ve been on the other side of this obsession before. I\u2019ve been the most treasured possession; the prettiest pet in the cage. I\u2019ve been someone\u2019s property. I know what it\u2019s like to lose my sense of self, to find everything that I am subsumed by what my Mistress wanted me to be. I can\u2019t let that happen to anybody else.\u201d I paused for a breath, and whispered the last thing I needed to say. \u201cAnd I can\u2019t be with anyone who would do that to another person.\u201d<br /> <br /> Her grip on me tightened, and I almost didn\u2019t hear the quaver in her voice. \u201cYou will keep the watch on me, and I will be very careful, and together we shall see that it does not come to that. Agreed?\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cAgreed.\u201d<br /> <br /> I rejoined the rest of the motley as Marguerite said a private goodbye to Felicity. In our few moments of (almost) assured privacy from her, we hastily discussed a few plans for her birthday tomorrow (and Julia\u2019s is next week\u2026 jeez!). Unfortunately, nothing seemed to stick. We already did the whole \u201csomebody unlikely jumps out of her cake\u201d thing on Calamity\u2019s birthday, and we didn\u2019t want to repeat ourselves and make things boring. Some mention was made of buying an erotic cake shaped like Kevin Costner\u2019s stunt butt \u2013 since at least that was topical \u2013 but the others overruled me on that one. I confess that I was not the most effective advocate of that plan, as I couldn\u2019t seem to stop myself from dissolving into giggles every time anyone (myself included) uttered the words \u201cbutt cake.\u201d<br /> <br /> Buttcake! Pause for laughter.<br /> <br /> Buttcake. Buttcake buttcake buttcake. It sort of loses all meaning after a while, but it\u2019s still frickin\u2019 hilarious.<br /> <br /> We decided to go with something a little more sedate and dignified in the end. I think Gawain is going to cook up something Frenchified with some fancy imported cheese Julia picked up. Nary a buttcake shall be on display.<br /> <br /> Heh\u2026 buttcake.<br /> <br /> Anyway, since we somehow missed out on our regular movie night last night\u2026 and nobody seems entirely sure how that happened, by the way, we all just spontaneously forgot or something. But since we didn\u2019t get our usual night off from the hurly-burly of burlesque house management, we decided to take it easy tonight instead and watch a couple of flicks.<br /> <br /> At first we were going to watch a fantasy film called <u>The Neverending Story</u>, which is apparently based on a fairly popular children\u2019s book I missed by a couple of years. In the end, however, this was vetoed by Calamity when she found out that I\u2019d never seen another film called <u>The Goonies</u>. It was a cute film about a bunch of kids who get chased into a series of caves by crazy gangsters and end up working their way through a bunch of booby traps to eventually find the lost treasure trove of a pirate captain. It was pretty enjoyable, though I can\u2019t help but wonder about the name of the pirate in question\u2026 One-Eyed Willy? Seriously?<br /> <br /> The other film was a mildly subversive comedy called <u>But I\u2019m a Cheerleader</u>. It was about a girl whose parents send her to some sort of ultra-conservative re-education camp to \u201ccure\u201d her of lesbianism. Ironically, she ends up with a much clearer view of her own true sexuality due to her experiences at the camp. The film was surprisingly deep, calling into question not just the mainstream view of sex and sexuality, but some much more ingrained ideas about traditional gender roles as well.<br /> <br /> The film was obviously pretty meaningful to D. She played it cool, but anyone who knows her really well could see that she was affected by the story as it unfolded on the screen.<br /> <br /> As I lay draped across three of my lovers watching the film, I started thinking about my own sexuality. Okay\u2026 maybe \u201csexuality\u201d isn\u2019t really the right word for it. I\u2019ve known ever since Arcadia that I\u2019m bisexual\u2026 I enjoy the physical act of sex tremendously, regardless of the gender of my partner(s). But what about my feelings on an emotional level? I only seem to fall head over heels in love with other women. I haven\u2019t really felt a serious romantic connection to any male since Kyle back in High School. Does that make me a lesbian? I don\u2019t think you\u2019re allowed to be a lesbian if you like having sex with men, though. And even speaking on a strictly emotional level I\u2019m not sure I want to label myself like that. I mean, what if I meet a man tomorrow, or next week, or twenty years from now, and we just sort of click? Do I want to throw away that possibility because I\u2019m misinterpreting the romantic circumstances of my current life?<br /> <br /> I think in the end it\u2019s easier for me to just go with the flow. I\u2019m going to continue to defy any label anyone wants to hang on me, and be my own person without limiting myself needlessly. After all, as soon as you use a word to describe what something is, you\u2019re by omission also describing all the things it isn\u2019t. And who needs that?<br /> <br /> In any case, after the films D asked to speak to the motley briefly. She wanted us all to promise that none of us would allow ourselves to be alone with the Handmaidens. A few people seemed a little irritated at the request (Calamity, I\u2019m looking at you), but D made a good case: as a Leechfinger herself, she knows the cravings that those two feel\u2026 the urge to drain the life out of their partners completely. To hear her tell it, they\u2019re so adept at giving pleasure that their victims often <u>consent</u> in the end, and give up their own lives voluntarily. D wanted to make sure that none of us put ourselves in that position.<br /> <br /> I shrugged it off. \u201cD, I\u2019ll admit that the idea of spending time with them is intriguing,\u201d I said, \u201cbut I remember what happened to Tamara. I\u2019m horny, but I\u2019m not stupid. Well\u2026 I\u2019m not <u>that</u> stupid, anyway,\u201d I finished with a grin.<br /> <br /> She shook her head like she always does when I get all self-deprecating, but she seemed to accept my statement at face value. \u201cI can\u2019t lose you,\u201d she said seriously after pulling me a short distance away from the others. \u201cI know what those two do to people, and I can\u2019t lose you, Lori.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHave you ever\u2026 you know?\u201d I asked after a moment.<br /> <br /> D nodded. \u201cNot for a long time, though,\u201d she added quickly, \u201cand I\u2019ll never let myself do it again.\u201d<br /> <br /> I thought about it for a minute. \u201cYou could, you know,\u201d I said softly. \u201cWith me, I mean. I\u2019d let you. I trust you completely.\u201d<br /> <br /> She shook her head adamantly. \u201cNever,\u201d she said in a voice that brooked no argument. \u201cYou\u2019re too important. I\u2019ll never look at you as food. I swear.\u201d<br /> <br /> I took in the look in her eyes. \u201cOkay,\u201d I said, and the two of us rejoined the others for the usual post-movie shenanigans.<br /> <br /> Now, my presence is requested by a gaggle of giggling girlfriends, and I\u2019ve never been very good at saying no to them. After the rest of them drop off, I\u2019m going to hit the books for a while and try to think up something truly special to do for Marguerite\u2019s birthday.<br /> <br /> Until next time\u2026 buttcakes!<br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei Grace</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T19:02:01-08:00","id":839612,"title":"","content":"<b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> November 4th<br /> Nine years, seven months, and nineteen days<br /> Days without stabbing: 3<br /> <br /> Fucking hell. I should just stop watching movies I used to love before I was taken. It just reminds me of how fucking nave I used to be and makes me remember stupid little things like how much Mom used to love fucking movie butter and salt on her popcorn and how much Dad hated it. They would go at it for a whole movie, back and forth about how she'd ruined the popcorn and drowned any trace of it's actual taste and she'd counter how popcorn had no flavor. But despite how much vitriol the words themselves had the they were both smiling the whole time and it was clear they were just enjoying the verbal sparring. I don't know if either of them really cared about the damn popcorn at all, I think they just enjoyed the game and it was something that was absolutely trivial. Zeus knows he never complained about all that damn oil and salt being on her lips when he kissed her.<br /> <br /> And it wasn't fair to D's pick that I was so off kilter. I mean, it was good but I was just not feeling it at that point. Then again maybe if I hadn't already been sitting on fucking maudlin when we started it would have gone better. At least I didn't distract anyone from Insincere Marguerite. She was looking better but she still needed the others more than I did. Something can actually be done about the shit she's facing after all and since it doesn't happen to involve murder (despite what Julia wants) then yours truly is about as useful as a porcupine in a condom factory.<br /> <br /> Damn it, it's not just a thing I say when I call her my Darkling sister. I love that woman. I fucking love all of them. That's why I've been working so fucking hard. Not just putting in time with Dr Emmett but actually opening up the festering abscess I call a soul and letting her see just what a sick murdering thing I am at my core. Reading all the damn articles and books she's suggested. Even the fucking meditation. Every day I work at it. And what's the mother fucking point...<br /> <br /> She's right to worry. She knows. Fuck, they all should but except for Jacob I doubt they'd admit it. I've pledged to protect her and never let her come to harm. I call her sister. I would lay down my life for her. But she knows and this morning she was too weary from everything else to lie and pretend she didn't.<br /> <br /> No, I was the one lying when I said I'd never stab her. Because we both know that I loved my parents and look how much fucking good it did them. That's what I do. That's what I am. I'm a murderess. I'm a killer. I can dress it up with pretty excuses. I can pretend to be something else. But who am I fooling?<br /> <br /> Hell maybe that's why I hesitated when D called that little pow wow after the movies about the Handmaidens. She's a leechfinger. She does understand their hunger and those two are most certainly quite deadly. And Tamera hasn't leveled any accusations because at the time they were killing her she didn't want them to stop. So yeah, I so agree with D that we shouldn't let them be alone with anyone at the Dream House. And yet... Fuck if it wouldn't be so damn easy to just let them sweep me away with those cool fingers... soft and cold like silk... just for once be a good little girl and not fight back...<br /> <br /> Shit I shouldn't even think things like that. Fuck, why do I write this damned thing in pen? I need to avoid those two. They remind me of Them too much. Of the way They would gather me close afterward and soothe my broken body. The way They would brush the tears away from my useless eyes and stroke my hair and talk to me. The way Their many voices whispered in my ears all at once but so clearly. They told me They loved me there in the dark. They promised how much better it would all be if only I could be good. All the pain and misery and suffering was my own fault. If I would just stop fighting it would end. All I had to do was be a good little girl. But laying there bloody and broken in Their arms was the only time I wasn't alone. They didn't come for good girls.<br /> <br /> I keep saying how much better things would be if They'd never taken me but what if I hadn't fought Them? What if I had just let Katt go and become Jane until I forgot that I'd ever been anyone else? Timmy wouldn't have died in the well. Lindsey wouldn't have taken her life and she and Robert would still have each other. Maybe they'd have found a way out together. My parents would still be alive...<br /> <br /> Choices have consequences. I chose to fight. That required me to became the monster I am. And that monster has killed people. Innocent people that did nothing to provoke or deserve what happened to them. And it took pleasure in the deed. The memories of my darkest deeds do not conjure up the shame or revulsion that it should. Oh, I feel these things when I think about what I did and why. But recalling the events themselves brings only a warm pleasure. I like pain. I enjoy it. I am happiest when I am bleeding or drawing blood.<br /> <br /> Okay, being with Gawain also makes me pretty fucking happy and doesn't involve spilling blood. But then Handsome is the exception to most of my rules. And speaking of Gawain, he's waiting for me to join him in bed and right now getting fucked senseless or being gathered up into his loving arms (or both... yeah both would be double plus good) beats the shit out of sitting here feeling sorry for myself.<br /> <br /> November 5th<br /> Nine years, seven months, eighteen days<br /> Days without stabbing: 4<br /> <br /> Remember remember and all that. Today is Insincere Marguerite's birthday. There is much to do and thankfully my demons are back in their cage where they belong after spending the night with my love and doing my morning forms. I'm quite pleased with how the Tai Chi is working out. Focused movement suits me better than stillness. Just the way I'm tuned, I run great at full bore but I do not idle well.<br /> <br /> Yesterday was not one of my better days. Frayed to unraveling there by the end, but I did keep it together. I got around to making that necklace dream vessel for Becky I've been thinking of and it turned out quite well. Both the glass-work and the dream it holds. Making the individual beads into segments of the dragon worked as I'd hoped to give it a bit of life as it moves with the wearer and doing the whole dragon as one piece would have made it much to breakable for someone as active as Becky. And having that revitalizing dream handy will be good for when I'm not there to help with her stress. Hopefully it won't strain the tacit 'don't ask don't tell' dynamic between us. I doubt it will. She's much too smart to not see just how deep my feeling for her run so this shouldn't trip her commitment issues by making her realize it now and it's not really outside of the friends with benefits thing.<br /> <br /> And while it is true that Insincere Marguerite knows I'm dangerous. She also loves me in spite of it. Like Gawain does. Like they all do. She made that clear yesterday but my own self loathing kept me from seeing it. And it is a good thing that they know. That they understand. They can recognize it when I slide. They know to be wary. They know that despite how much I do love them it isn't impossible and that makes them safer. I won't stop working. I won't stop striving to improve my control. But it's there and it's part of who I am and it isn't ever going to go away. I will always have this darkness inside. But I will chose when and who I harm. I refused to be the good little girl They wanted in Show Globe and I will fight rather be the monster They want me to be here.<br /> <br /> It seems so simple stated like that doesn't it? But sometimes I am too afraid or tired or just plain weak. Yesterday was one of those days. I can't change it but I can strive to be better. I don't have time to wallow in fucking self pity bullshit. There is too much that needs to be done. Too many people that depend on me to falter like that. I owe it to them to be stronger. To be better. I won't let them down.<br /> <br /> I managed to make Gawain see the logic in doing the Oneiromancy on Chalcedony. It's going to happen and if he takes lead he can know it won't turn into any sort of re-purposing. He's got experience with the Director's scripts. He's a very strong dream weaver and this will raise his esteem in the eyes of the monarchs if not the whole freehold. And if he's in charge then I will be far less tempted to give into any of my darker impulses. Nothing else for me to do on this point but wait to hear back from the powers that be.<br /> <br /> If Lori and Gawain have read her correctly (and I trust their abilities here) then Felicity is not knowingly attempting to bring harm or ruin to Insincere Marguerite. However, just because her intentions aren't actively malevolent doesn't mean they aren't dangerous. She wants to see the woman that humiliated her former lover suffer for it. She's Day Court and that makes them enemies. Oh the other hand, she's thrilled by the prospect of being defiled by her enemy. Sadly, Insincere Marguerite and her have decided to engage in 'taking it slow' and having a low key date later this week. Even if she wasn't drawing the enmity of the Spring Monarch this relationship is bringing out far too much of her old self that she's trying to move past. Yes, she needs to face down those demons rather than running from them but pushing your limits is not the same as being reckless. And while Felicity may not have an ulterior motive she knows this relationship is a bad idea for both herself and my sister. And is self destructive really a better motive when she clearly doesn't care if she takes Insincere Marguerite down with her? Sadly, at this point, neither of them seem able or willing to head this train wreck off before it ends in tears and quite possibly blood.<br /> <br /> And Julia's hatred for Felicity is so strong. I've spoken to her and I think I've managed to calm her down a little. But ultimately, pursuing a relationship that your lover is so vehemently against seems wrong. Does it really matter if Julia's right about Felicity's intentions? She hates that woman. If your love can't stand rap music then even if you like it isn't it inconsiderate to blast it in her face on a regular basis? I need to speak to Insincere Marguerite about what she's doing to Julia. She is Julia's Master and she has a responsibility to take care of her girl. This relationship with Felicity is putting her girl through hell. As a friend, I can't not confront her about this. Lords above and below know she's called me out when I needed it and I owe it to her to do the same. I just hate the thought of doing it on her birthday.<br /> <br /> Also I need to decide what I want to do with this whole revelation about Scarlet. She's a murderess like me but she's clearly worried far more about being caught than any sort of guilt over her actions. I mean, she and Natalia both are pretty cold blooded which really, really ought to be more of a problem for me than it is. Is it that I feel some kinship because of my own hunger? Is it just that I want what they're selling bad enough that I'm willing to turn a blind eye to their behavior and risk my life? Okay pot, Imma let you finish this excuse train but first hold up and read that bit up there where you call the kettle black.<br /> <br /> I really need to stay the hell clear of those two. Nothing good will come from fucking them. Even if they are as amazing as I have heard I am certainly not good, so all that cumming doesn't count.<br /> <br /> Focus. Sex with the Handmaidens is a huge mistake and I'm most likely going to make it if I get the chance. But right now the issue is what do I do with what I know. Some leverage with them might be useful for Dahlia and if Lowjack had some way to reign them in he might stop fucking making death threats on members of my motley. But you know what, he made FUCKING death threats against a member of my motley so FUCK THAT ASSHOLE. Hell, right now I kinda want to murder Tamera myself just because it would piss on his hush puppies. But I am not going to do anything stupid. She is a member of the Freehold in good standing. Also, she isn't the one who threatened Insincere Marguerite and she's never given me any reason to want to hurt her. And of course I would never even think about murdering or harming one of the Monarchs of this Freehold. Nope. Certainly not this girl. But no, I don't really trust Lowjack with this and Dahlia's loyal so unless it becomes a matter of Freehold security (which it shouldn't be so long as those two are here as part of backroom deal with the Night Court) I think I'm going to keep what I know to myself.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Letting certain members of my own court know might prove useful if things do ever go pear shaped with our smokey back room allies. I don't think Charlotte or Tommy would misuse the information. I'll have to think about it.<br /> <br /> And beyond that, what about Salk's little fishing expedition yesterday? Given Willow's frustrations in trying to herd those pussycats I can get why he might want some authority over them. But reasonable or not, leashing anyone rubs me the wrong way. And someone who looks for that kind of leverage doesn't sit right with me. So, I am not going to tell his creepazoid ass anything. But should I let them know he was here looking? Maybe I should tell Scarlet. But if her wife doesn't know the whole deal (and given how she was reacting I'm fairly sure she doesn't know) I'll need to do so discreetly. Which isn't a problem. But should I be getting in the middle of this at all? Why do I care? Okay, I care because I want to fuck her, and I need to stop trying to pretend otherwise. Or is it that I don't trust anyone that wants control over another? (But I trust Insincere Marguerite and she certainly has the same inclinations...)<br /> <br /> Fuck it. I'm over thinking this shit. Salk trips my creepydar and I like Scarlet. End of discussion. I give her a head's up that he's been sniffing around. There, issue resolved and I can stop wasting time thinking about it.<br /> <br /> The warding Madam Spidertoes placed is holding the ghosts back for now. And I've seen how to do so myself, so if nothing else I can maintain security on that front. My talents with Shade and Spirit will allow me to speak to either of them and with a little work I could make either ghost manifest. I think the next step is to have a tea party in the attic with Monica and see if we can hash out some ground rules for cohabitation and learn more about the other ghost from her. As deeply appealing as making the murder ghost solid and punching her in the face with my knife is, it won't actually end her. I have to play this smarter. If Monica can't (or won't) help then deeper ability with Shade and Spirit may be able to give me the insight I need. Also, I need to spend some more time in the Library to figure out exactly how to lay a ghost to rest. And once I've worked it all out here, then I'll be ready to go back to Belleview and try to make things right.<br /> <br /> Alright, time to go enjoy Handsome's cooking and then make damn sure everything is perfect for my Darkling Sister's birthday party. Thankfully, no one was actually serious about the whole butt-cake thing so I'm not going to have to deal with that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> After the show Spidertoes came over to talk to the motley about the ghost. She said that she had a way that would make it harder for the \u201cMurder Ghost\u201d to materialize. This would also affect the good ghosts in the house to prevent them from making an appearance. I think we all figured it would be worth it and that the good ghosts would not mind overly much, so we said she could go ahead and do her magic. Madame Spidertoes did request the presence of someone dangerous while she performed the ritual to keep her safe if the malignant ghost decided to surface. Calamity, who has an interest in ghosts and who is dangerous, volunteered her service to the Autumn Courtier and they went upstairs to the \u201cmurder room.\u201d<br /> <br /> While Calamity was protecting our guest and learning more about ghost magic some of the rest of us had a talk with Desiree. Gawain asked about the conversation that she had with Scarlett that upset her so much. Desiree admitted that she\u2019d heard about what Scarlett had done to escape Arcadia and wanted to confirm if it was true. It was also apparently her way to keep the rest of us safe. She has information that Scarlett does not want known, and has people that she doesn\u2019t want hurt by the Handmaidens, namely us.<br /> <br /> We have heard that the Director tells tales about all the bad things that Changelings do to those around them as an object lesson why we\u2019re bad and staying in Arcadia is good. Well, the events that surround Scarlett\u2019s escape are one of those object lessons. Apparently Scarlett in her bid to escape wanted to create as large a diversion as possible to keep the Gentry occupied. So, she killed about 20 other changelings that were in the realm and fled while her Keeper investigated the crimes. I can see why Scarlett would not want this information to become public knowledge. Despite having happened in Arcadia it would color the way people look at her and by extension the Night Court. A lot of us do things that we\u2019re not proud of in our bid to escape and it\u2019s understandable to be reticent to talk about it. I\u2019m not sure what to think about the revelation about Scarlett\u2019s escape though. She hurt innocents in her effort to leave. I don\u2019t know what her durance was like, but I would think that it would be possible to come up with some other means to grab her Keeper\u2019s attention besides mass killing. Granted until I came back to myself, after Diane, I did not have problems killing people in or out of Arcadia. I left more than one body in my wake while traveling in the Hedge or through my the Lady\u2019s realm.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, leaving Arcadia did not curb Scarlett\u2019s violence. Apparently she has killed several people in her efforts to win over Natalia and to keep her paramour safe. She is very much in love with Natalia. Almost obsessively so. I don\u2019t know the context for what happened in \u2018the world,\u2019 but it does seem clear that violence is not just a sometimes reaction for her. Scarlett is definitely one to keep an eye on.<br /> <br /> On a side note, it turns out that Scarlett is Czech. I knew that Natalia was from the Ukraine. She has a faint accent, but I was not sure about Scarlett. She has worked hard to cover it up and speak with a neutral accent. Makes me wonder why. What is wrong with being Czech? Despite being wary of the pair I did enjoy talking to Natalia in Russian some time back at the ball. It was a nice change from thinking everything in Russian and having to translate to English before it comes out of my mouth. One more mystery to add to the pile it seems.<br /> <br /> Conversation turned to Becky, which brought up the fact that Desiree is all too aware that there are those in the Freehold that want to see her harmed or dead. The first one that came to her mind was Becky. The Claviger has openly threatened Desiree\u2019s life and remains at the top of the list of those that want to do bodily injury to our guest. In an effort to gain some modicum of protection Desiree seems to be making herself as useful to us as she can so we will keep her safe. Not that I blame her for that. I would probably be doing the same thing if I were in her shoes.<br /> <br /> Another thing that came up that I thought was interesting was that Desiree also suggested that perhaps Becky being Claviger was not good for her emotionally. Her position is causing her stress due to the fact that she has a serious crush on Jolie and the monarch does not return the feelings. Becky sees each day that the woman of her desires has chosen someone else. I\u2019m not sure if this interest in Becky\u2019s emotional well-being is genuine or if she has some ulterior motive behind it. And I would have wondered that even if we didn\u2019t confirm that she\u2019s a loyalist. Removing Becky as Claviger would make Jolie vulnerable, at least until they hired a new bodyguard.<br /> <br /> Shortly after that little talk everyone broke up to go their separate ways. I think Julia and Lori went off to get stoned, Calamity was working on forming glass beads around a silver chain. And since Insincere Marguerite had vanished into the ducts earlier I left a present of cognac and cheese outside one of the vents and knocked on it to draw her attention. I know that she was upset earlier by her conversations with Jolie and Lori. Not sure what those talks were about, but I\u2019m assuming it has something to do with Felicity. I could not directly console my friend, so I went for the indirect approach.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Today started off a little more subdued than usual. Insincere Marguerite was particularly quiet over breakfast burritos. Apparently Gawain overhead Julia and Lori going on about what they had been craving when they were high and decided to plan breakfast accordingly. So, we had breakfast burritos. I thought it was a nice change from omelets or waffles. Not that I mind omelets or waffles. The novelty of hot food has still not worn off yet. I\u2019m getting better about stashing food though. I used to always have a granola bar or something non-perishable stashed in my room or my \u201cgo bag,\u201d but lately I haven\u2019t been as diligent in that regard. I didn\u2019t even stash some of the jerky that we made from the dragon meat, and I know I definitely would have done that a couple months ago.<br /> <br /> Somehow during breakfast we started talking about American horror movie tropes, like someone going off alone, people that go off to have sex getting killed, saying \u201cAt least it can\u2019t get any worse,\u201d \u201cI\u2019ll be right back.\u201d etc\u2026 I guess all of these things came up after Lorelei had been taken because most of the conversation was explaining this stuff to her. It was kind of fun.<br /> <br /> Things then moved on to a more serious topic, Felicity. Insincere Marguerite asked Lori her opinion on whether or not she should meet with the Day Courtier. She was unsure whether she should sleep with the other woman or not. The rest of us pretty much all agreed that whatever happens Felicity is probably not good for Insincere Marguerite. Marguerite then went off to make a phone call and came back with the news that Felicity would be coming to the Dream House in two hours. She also asked us to stop her from hurting Felicity if it comes to that. Julia was very upset by this whole turn of events. She has not liked Felicity or any of her interactions with her paramour at all. She went so far as to threaten violence on the Day Courtier if she does anything at all to harm Marguerite. Desiree brought up the idea that this whole thing might be a plot by Felicity to get Insincere Marguerite in trouble or something along those lines. I\u2019m not sure of that. Granted I don\u2019t know much about what\u2019s going on between those two, but I know it doesn\u2019t seem healthy. Felicity has been told several times, by a couple different people, that Marguerite has a bad reaction to her presence, and yet she continues to try and court my motley-mate. What about \u201cstay away\u201d does she not understand? When Insincere Marguerite gets close to or thinks about Felicity she starts to backslide more than a little bit to the person she was before she escaped Arcadia. I think it\u2019s the fact that Felicity used to be a Treasure that brings that side of Marguerite out. So, the logical thing would be to keep Felicity away at all costs. But what is happening now? Marguerite invited the person that triggers her dark side over for a chat. At least Lori stayed with Marguerite when Felicity finally came over. Felicity\u2019s and Marguerites mantles fought the whole time I saw them standing next to one another. Presumably this kept up during their conversation. This isn\u2019t going to end well.<br /> <br /> While Insincere Marguerite, Lori and Felicity were having their chat Salk came over to have a chat of his own. He said that he was concerned with the safety of the Handmaidens and wanted to talk with us about it. Gawain, Calamity and I talked to him in the office. Salk said that he was concerned with what was said to upset Scarlett so much and that he wanted assurances that the Handmaidens would come to no harm while under our roof. We all assured him that they would be safe and that we did not know what the conversation between Desiree and Scarlett was about. I\u2019m not sure if he believed that or not, but we did not give anything away. After Salk had left Gawain said that he\u2019d \u201clooked\u201d at Salk\u2019s intentions and the man wanted to get information that he could use against Scarlett. Makes me wonder why he wants to have leverage over the Handmaidens, or at least the one. Is it to ensure that he can keep them in line or does he have another purpose in mind? Soon after that we sent him on his way. Always more questions.<br /> <br /> When the ladies came back from their chat Marguerite\u2019s and Felicity\u2019s mantles were still fighting. Apparently they are going to see each other, but they are going to take it slow. I\u2019m really not confident that this is going to end well for either of them, but in particular, Marguerite. Right now Felicity is not high in my books. She has been pursuing Marguerite, which is kind of like constantly plying an alcoholic with a drink. Eventually the alcoholic\u2019s resolve is going to break down and they\u2019re going to give in. I don\u2019t want Marguerite to give in to those older, darker desires that have been resurfacing lately.<br /> <br /> After Felicity left Julia and Insincere Marguerite went off to talk for a bit. A little while later Julia came back alone and said that she wanted to discuss plans for Marguerite\u2019s birthday tomorrow. We all agreed that having anyone jump out of a cake would be copying what we did for Calamity\u2019s party and we wouldn\u2019t want to duplicate what we did before. So, we discussed just getting an interesting cake, and pretty soon the idea of a \u201cbutt cake,\u201d to commemorate that whole conversation about Kevin Costner\u2019s \u201cstunt butt\u201d came up. That idea was thankfully shot down.<br /> <br /> When we finished up our discussions of \u201cbutt cakes,\u201d (our motley is so strange) I went to go find Insincere Marguerite and make sure that she was okay. I expressed my concern that being in a relationship with Felicity might not be the best for her and she appreciated my concern but reiterated that they were going to take things slowly and try and avoid things that will trigger any darker impulses. She also assured me that she would break things off with Felicity if the worst should happen. I am hoping that if she starts going down that dark path she\u2019ll notice and stop herself before it goes too far. I don\u2019t know if Marguerite will be able to fully come back from that state if she were to fall back into it. I can\u2019t help but worry about my friend. No matter how much she tries to reassure me that she\u2019ll be fine, I still have a bad feeling.<br /> <br /> So we went our separate ways and I met up with Gawain. He had asked if I wanted to spar and I said sure. It\u2019s been awhile since I\u2019ve sparred with anyone really and figured practice would not go amiss. Which reminds me that I should get together with Calamity to set up a time to spar with her. Maybe with Luna too. Anyhoo\u2026sparring with Gawain was fun. His style is all about hitting hard and making each strike do as much damage as possible. My style is all about hitting as often as possible and whittling the opponent down that way. Overall I think things went well. Gawain was certainly on his game and I had to work at not getting hit. Didn\u2019t always work, as the bruises will attest, but the same could be said for him. He didn\u2019t always avoid my blows either. It is interesting sparring with Gawain though. More so than other people. He is a suit of armor. He doesn\u2019t bleed. So, when I spar with him I make attacks on places that would hurt or incapacitate an ordinary fighter. I still leave scratches sometimes, but he doesn\u2019t really bruise. So it\u2019s more remembering where I\u2019ve already hit him than being able to see where I\u2019ve landed previous hits. He\u2019s not invulnerable, despite appearances, so I have to make sure that I don\u2019t actually do any real damage though I rarely leave a mark. It\u2019s a good thing I have a photographic memory. Sometimes.<br /> <br /> Since we skipped Movie Night yesterday we decided to have it tonight. The movies that were decided upon were \u201cGoonies\u201d and \u201cBut I\u2019m a Cheerleader.\u201d I remember Goonies. It was a cute movie that I\u2019d seen before on cable years ago. There were of course many jokes made about the Pirate\u2019s name\u2026.One Eyed Willy. Yeah, in a Burlesque house you can imagine the first place everyone\u2019s brain went. The second movie I remember far less of. I think I started to doze through it. Something to do with a girl whose parents suspected her of being a lesbian so they send her to a camp to \u201cfix\u201d her. Yeah, that goes about as well as you\u2019d expect. I think she ends up finding love with a fellow camper near the end. I do remember that at the end the girl\u2019s parents end up going to their own little meeting to get over the fact that their daughter is gay. Turnabout is fair play.<br /> <br /> After the movies, De la Rocha brought up the Handmaidens. Apparently they have a special interest in Lorelei and me. Not sure why, but their attention is on us for some reason. We all agreed that being alone with them is a bad idea. They are too dangerous and if they get you going they can get you to consent to killing or nearly killing you. Not too keen on that myself. As a motley we decided that none of us will be left alone with one or both of the Handmaidens at any point. It\u2019s just too dangerous. I\u2019ve seen them double team Calamity before, and they certainly expressed an interest in Lori at the club last night. They did not approach me, but that may be because I was at the bar the whole night. I did not go out and mingle with anyone while the show was on. They have come up to talk to me in the past, but didn\u2019t really start in on me from what I remember. They may have gotten the hint that I was with Luna. She might be the reason they did not try and sweet talk me last night. Or it could be that I was busy. Either way lucky me. They may be hot, but I\u2019m not keen on seeing how close to death I can get. Been there, done that and it wasn\u2019t fun.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> It\u2019s been a rough couple of days.<br /> <br /> Today, at least, I managed to get some headway on my issues with Felicity. After having Jolie, Lori, and Julia come down on I for it, I finally got to meet with Felicity today.<br /> <br /> Last night, it seems, was Monday, and with all the drama we had forgotten about movie night. There was discussion, and De La Rocha started pushing <i>\u201cBut I\u2019m a Cheerleader</i>\u201d fairly hard. The movie apparently held some emotional significance for her though having seen it I am mystified as to what that significance was. I mean, it was certainly gratifying for the queer viewer, but I am no less queer than she and it lacked any\u2026personal impact.<br /> <br /> I get ahead of myself. We also argued between <i>Never Ending Story</i> and <i>Goonies</i>, with the decision going to <i>Goonies</i> after a short time, despite initially choosing <i>Never Ending story</i>. I saw both when I was young and neither seemed extremely\u2026necessary I guess. But with the arguing about Canadian butts I did not want to cause any more turmoil.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session L</i><br /> <br /> Buttcake!<br /> <br /> Not much to add, a lot of talk and working through what to do. Felicity beat Insincere Marguerite at pure social combat, as despite Insincere Marguerite being good at social stuff she is no Fairest.<br /> <br /> Last game actually happened! Though I was running on about 2 hours sleep at the time. Tune in two weeks for Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Birthday, Strip Twister, and Lori having the best week ever.<br /> <br /> Comments and Questions Welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T13:40:57-08:00","id":842706,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s an off week, but as other games which missed sessions are getting character stats up, I am doing the same here. So enjoy about half of the Last Dance Motley of the Malibu Dream House, and see what Changelings can look like after about 50 sessions<br /> <br /> <b>Gawain Vert, Dawn Elemental Metalflesh/Smith</b><br /> <br /> Name: Gawain Vert<br /> Seeming: Elemental<br /> Kith: Metalflesh, Smith<br /> Virtue/Vice: Protective/Nosey<br /> <br /> Attributes:<br /> Mental:<br /> Intelligence 3<br /> Wits 3<br /> Resolve 4<br /> <br /> Physical:<br /> Strength 5<br /> Dex 2<br /> Stamina 3<br /> <br /> Social:<br /> Presence 2<br /> Manipulation 1<br /> Composure 3<br /> <br /> Skills:<br /> Mental:<br /> Academics 1<br /> Computer 1<br /> Crafts 4 (Blacksmithing, Cooking)<br /> Investigation 1<br /> Medicine 2<br /> Occult 2<br /> Politics 1<br /> Science 0<br /> <br /> Physical:<br /> Athletics 4 (Sprinting)<br /> Brawl 2<br /> Drive 1<br /> Firearms 0<br /> Larceny 0<br /> Stealth 1<br /> Survival 2<br /> Weaponry 4 (Sword)<br /> <br /> Social:<br /> Animal Ken 0<br /> Empathy 5 (Dreams) (+1 Pledge)<br /> Expression 1<br /> Intimidation 1 (+1 Pledge)<br /> Persuasion 1<br /> Socialize 1 (When Drunk)<br /> Streetwise 0<br /> Subterfuge 0<br /> <br /> Clarity 6<br /> <br /> Wyrd 5<br /> <br /> Merits:<br /> 2nd Kith<br /> Fighting Style: Langschwert 4<br /> Resources 1<br /> Court Goodwill (Spring) 1<br /> Court Goodwill (Summer) 2<br /> Mantle (Dawn) 4<br /> Languages (English, French)<br /> <br /> Derived Stats:<br /> Willpower (Res + Comp): 7<br /> Initiative (Dex + Comp): 5<br /> Health (Stamina + Size): 8<br /> Defense (min(Dex,Wits) + Athletics): 6<br /> Speed (Str + Dex + 5): 12<br /> <br /> Contracts:<br /> Stone 4<br /> Elements (Metal) 3<br /> Dreams 4<br /> Potential 3<br /> Blades 1<br /> <br /> Entitlements:<br /> Family of Silent Nights<br /> <br /> <br /> Tokens:<br /> Hedgecrafting Tools<br /> Sleepy sculpture<br /> Armor Embellsihments<br /> <br /> <br /> Pledges:<br /> Motley Pledge<br /> Dreaming Pledge (Desiree)<br /> ?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Calamity, Autumn Darkling Razorhand/Whisperwisp</b><br /> <br /> <u>Calamity</u><br /> <br /> Aspirations: 3<br /> (long) Confront and Lay to rest the ghosts of her Parents<br /> (short) Deal with the Murder ghost at the Dream House<br /> (short) Help Gawain find Greg Andrews<br /> <br /> Strength 3<br /> Dexterity 5<br /> Stamina 3<br /> <br /> Presence 3<br /> Manipulation 1<br /> Composure 3<br /> <br /> Intelligence 3<br /> Wits 3<br /> Resolve 3<br /> <br /> +Academics 1<br /> Computer: 1<br /> Crafts: 1<br /> Investigation 2<br /> Medicine: 1<br /> Occult: 1<br /> Politics: 0<br /> Science: 0<br /> <br /> Athletics: 5<br /> Brawl: 1<br /> Drive: 1 (Motorcycle)<br /> Firearms: 2 (Pistol)<br /> Larceny: 0<br /> Stealth: 3 (In Darkness)<br /> Survival: 2<br /> +Weaponry 5 (Knife)<br /> <br /> Animal Ken: 0<br /> Empathy: 3 (Dreams)<br /> Expression: 3<br /> Intimidation 2<br /> Persuasion: 2<br /> Socialize: 2<br /> Streetwise: 1<br /> Subterfuge: 2 (Hiding Emotion)<br /> <br /> Dreams 3<br /> Darkness 4<br /> Oath &amp; Punishment 4<br /> Stone 1<br /> Elements (Glass) 3<br /> Fleeting Autumn 3<br /> Shade &amp; Spirit 3<br /> Spellbound Autumn 2<br /> Smoke 3<br /> Eternal Autumn 1<br /> <br /> Wyrd 5<br /> Clarity 5<br /> Willpower 6<br /> Health 8<br /> Size 5<br /> Defense: 8<br /> Initiative: 8<br /> Speed: 13<br /> Virtue: Rebellious, Honest<br /> Vice: Violent<br /> <br /> Hedgehog's Dilemma<br /> Virtuous<br /> Striking Looks 1<br /> Duel Kith 2<br /> Language: English 3<br /> Language: Spanish 2<br /> Language: French 2<br /> Mantle: Autumn 5<br /> Goodwill: Night 1<br /> Goodwill: Spring 1<br /> Resources 2<br /> Iron Stamina 3<br /> Perfect Stillness<br /> Rigid Mask<br /> Lethal Mien<br /> Fighting Finesse: Blades<br /> Fighting Style: Knife Fighting 4<br /> Area of Expertise: Knife<br /> Interdisciplinary Specialty: Knife<br /> Fighting Style: Dream 1<br /> <br /> Note: June 23rd 2014 is the date of her oath to not kill<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite, Night (Moon) Darkling Tunnelgrub/Lurker</b><br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite DeLisle<br /> Changeling<br /> Concept: Cat Among the Pigeons<br /> Aspirations: Find and Reclaim Yvette (long term), Seduce Felicity (short term), Impress Chalcedony (short term)<br /> Virtue: Loyalty<br /> Vice: Possessiveness, Pride<br /> Seeming: Darkling<br /> Kiths: Tunnelgrub/Lurker<br /> Court: Night, the Court of Disgust<br /> Entitlements: None<br /> Titles: Dread Esquire<br /> Place of Birth: Paris, France<br /> <br /> Intelligence 3<br /> Wits 3<br /> Resolve 3<br /> <br /> Strength 2<br /> Dexterity 5<br /> Stamina 2<br /> <br /> Presence 2<br /> Manipulation 4<br /> Composure 4<br /> <br /> Academics 1<br /> Computer 1<br /> Crafts 1<br /> Investigation 2 (In the dark)<br /> Medicine: 1<br /> Occult 1<br /> Politics 0<br /> Science 0<br /> <br /> Athletics 5 (Tight Places)<br /> Brawl 1<br /> Drive 0<br /> Firearms 0<br /> Larceny 3 (B&amp;E) (Pickpocketing) [Asset]<br /> Stealth 5 (Shadows) [Asset]<br /> Survival 0<br /> Weaponry 0<br /> <br /> Animal Ken 0<br /> Empathy 3 (Intense Eye Contact)<br /> Expression 2<br /> Intimidation 1<br /> Persuasion 3<br /> Socialize 2<br /> Streetwise 1 (Escape Routes) [Asset]<br /> Subterfuge 2<br /> <br /> Darkness 5<br /> Fang and Talon: Feline 2<br /> Moon 1<br /> Mirrors 3<br /> Reflections 4<br /> Separation 1<br /> Smoke 5<br /> <br /> Wyrd 5<br /> Clarity 7<br /> Willpower 7<br /> Health 7<br /> Glamour 14<br /> Size 5<br /> Defense: 8<br /> Initiative: 9<br /> Speed: 12<br /> <br /> Contacts 2 (Criminal)<br /> Court Goodwill: Autumn 3<br /> Court Goodwill: Spring 1<br /> Double-Jointed 2<br /> Duel Kith 2<br /> Gentrified Bearing 4<br /> Language: English 2<br /> Language: French 3<br /> Mantle: Night 5<br /> Parkour 5<br /> Professional: Criminal 5<br /> Prehensile Tongue 2<br /> Pusher 1<br /> Resources 2<br /> Slight of Hand 2<br /> Striking Looks 2<br /> Taste 1<br /> Vice-Ridden 2<br /> <br /> Quote: <i>\u201cHello! Ah, I see you have noticed me watching you\u2026\u201d</i><br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Quite the group eh?<br /> <br /> So Hedgehog\u2019s Dilemma and Prehensile Tongue are not vanilla merits, but merits to accommodate those characters. Prehensile Tongue is actually inspired by the Sluagh merit from Kithbook: Sluagh but lacks the paralyzing slap. Insincere Marguerite is basically a Sluagh. A naughty one.<br /> <br /> <b>Hedgehog\u2019s Dilemma (Level 2)</b><br /> <br /> If an opponent attacks Calamity with their bare hands, their player rolls a die. If even, it lands with no ill effects. If odd, the attacker takes half their Strength (rounded up) as lethal damage from Calamity\u2019s glass spikes. This in no way mitigates the damage Calamity takes, and non-barehanded attackers take no damage. An attacker can carefully attack Calamity to avoid any glass, but she adds her Wyrd to her defense.<br /> <br /> If Calamity does damage in a grapple, she does Lethal damage on her attack instead of Bashing unless she takes a penalty equal to her own Wyrd. If she is grappled her attacker takes damage equal to half their own Strength (rounded up) due to her glass spikes. This damage cannot be avoided. Armor applies normally.<br /> <br /> Drawback: Accidental contact can be dangerous with Calamity. An ally or innocent can take damage, which makes her dangerous. Sex or roughhousing requires a Dexterity + Athletics for her to avoiding harming her partner, and if she actually sleeps next to someone she damages them on an odd number on a single die roll.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Prehensile Tongue (Level 2)</b><br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite\u2019s tongue is a slightly disgusting limb of it\u2019s own. It is two feet long and incredibly flexible. It can provide up to two die bonus on rolls where having a third limb can help, usually Athletics, but can include Persuasion (if \u201cI have a two foot prehensile tongue\u201d is an enticement in that situation) Larceny (Lockpicking), or Brawl (Grappling).<br /> <br /> The tongue has only half of Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Strength rounded up for lifting purposes, and is too soft to do damage as a punch (though it could poke an eye or slap).<br /> <br /> Okay, next Sunday is Insincere Marguerite\u2019s birthday party! What is \u201cStrip Twister\u201d anyway? See you then.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T15:21:13-07:00","id":846741,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s Insincere Marguerite\u2019s birthday! Surely nothing decedent and regrettable will happen today, right? Also, apparently, the Best Week Ever, I am told.<br /> <br /> Note the post above this one has stats for Gawain, Calamity, and Insincere Marguerite as of the end of this session.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> Nov 6th, evening<br /> <br /> Well, I think Insincere Marguerite had an awesome birthday yesterday, if I can say so myself. Not just saying so cause the rest of us had a great day too - she was all but, you know, giddy this morning. There was that one, kinda, hiccup, but everything else was a great distraction.<br /> <br /> The day started a little later than usual, at least all together, cause Lori wanted to do breakfast in bed with her ladies. We did decide, once they were all down, that Lori, as well as Raul Julia\u2019s ghost, had permission to strangle people if they want. Mostly cause Lori, you know, wouldn\u2019t want to and Raul Julia\u2019s ghost is unlikely to show up. I don\u2019t even remember how we got there - I think it was from talking about what acts Desiree could do, cause she wanted to contribute, and then someone brought up Chalcedony and Desiree doing the Mamushka.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Sandoval showed up after to talk about, well, Chalcedony actually. The monarchs have decided that she is going to get the scripts dismantled if she had to be strapped down the whole time. And they knew, cause of their, you know, seer type people, that it would in fact come to that. Better than killing her right off, it\u2019s true, and I at least know that all we\u2019d be doing is removing the scripts and allowing her the true choice of paths.<br /> <br /> But Queen Charlotte wanted to ambush her here at the Dream House, if we were OK with that. Which we were decidedly not - the Dream House is supposed to be, you know, a safe place. For anyone without intent to hurt those inside. Unfortunately, the other place she would be at regularly is her home, and if they listen to us, they won\u2019t do that. We\u2019re already strong arming her into getting the scripts removed. It might be best if her first decision on loyalty once she could truly decide wasn\u2019t the Director (who might very well have rescued her from some place bad, like Desiree) and the people who just invaded her home to kidnap and brain wipe her. Sandoval is gonna take our advice to have Queen Charlotte ask her to report to court. Hopefully they\u2019ll do that, or something like it.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite didn\u2019t take it great. I didn\u2019t like it either, discussing those things, but it really did need to be done, you know? And I can\u2019t run away from it. Insincere Marguerite understands, I think. She couldn\u2019t stay there, but she understands. There didn\u2019t seem to be any hard feelings or resentment anyway, last night.<br /> <br /> Then again, there was plenty of distractions. Tongue spankings, discussion of T&amp;A versus musical numbers by majestic women, French cuisine, strip Twister and, you know, orgies. I\u2019m a little worried Julia got kinda the short end of the stick with all of it (except on the food, I think she liked it as much as the rest). She did make us promise no strip Twister or strip mumbletypeg for her upcoming birthday.<br /> <br /> We did get everyone involved in strip Twister, which was kinda surprising. Luna and Jacob didn\u2019t go past underwear/shorts respectively, but they still played. Calamity didn\u2019t get on the mat - the glass made that a little, you know, dangerous - but she volunteered to be the caller. She got creative too. I\u2019m pretty sure there\u2019s no \u2018tongue on red\u2019, \u2018left wing green\u2019 or \u2018right boob blue\u2019 on the spinner. Even without the helpful calls, Insincere Marguerite blew us out of the water, of course.<br /> <br /> Things progressed kinda, you know, naturally onto the orgy part of the evening, after Luna and Jacob jumped out the window. Julia looked kinda awkward herself, but didn\u2019t seem really put off by me specifically, which I was a little worried about. It was, you know, one of the sticking points when Flores mentioned it before, and she is Insincere Marguerite\u2019s special girlfriend, and it was Insincere Marguerite\u2019s birthday orgy. But it was ok apparently, so that was super awesome.<br /> <br /> Julia did kinda scurry out this morning before anyone else was really up and she\u2019s been hiding out all day. Her girls have been taking care of her though, and I\u2019m pretty sure me trying to help would just make things worse. De la Roche also seemed a little, you know, edgy about it. I think that\u2019s what the Willy Wonka thing was about. She beat a bag for a bit though and seemed mostly ok.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve been mostly relaxing myself. Like I said, I don\u2019t think I\u2019d be much help with De la Roche or Julia. I did check on Desiree - Insincere Marguerite had been coming on pretty strong all day, even before the orgy stuff, and that was kinda intense all on its own. I couldn\u2019t tell on my own whether Desiree was alright with the attention, but she was mostly. She did promise she wasn\u2019t in love with Insincere Marguerite, just crushing a little. Not that there would be a problem if she was. I was mostly just worried that she was uncomfortable, you know?<br /> <br /> Things got a little weird later though. Calamity came over to talk to me about Becky coming over. She needed a night off, without any overdrinking, and Calamity had the glass dragon necklace to give her. Calamity wasn\u2019t sure if it is going to be a night for just the two of them, or all three of us, which is fine by me. I\u2019m nowhere near about to turn down a night with them, but I\u2019m not as insatiable as some folks - if I have a night of wasting some noobs and then sleeping on my own right after orgy night, I\u2019ll live somehow.<br /> <br /> Desiree poked her head back in after a bit though. After warning us about the perils of asking De la Roche about GG Allin concerts, and assuring me she wasn\u2019t worried about self defense kinda things, she asked Calamity after Princess Joli. Calamity was able to tell her Princess Joli was at a water park eating her weight in cotton candy, but it wasn\u2019t too long before Desiree managed to prod Calamity into showing her frustration with the way Princess Joli seems to leave lovelorn ladies in her wake, what with Becky and Queen Charlotte and all. Desiree\u2019s demeanor really shifted after that, going full on into soothing mode like a switch flipping. It was a, you know, drastic enough thing that I tried to get a handle on her motives, but my Contract didn\u2019t get me anything.<br /> <br /> Lori came up after that looking for De la Roche, kinda breaking the kinda weird mood. She\u2019s gonna be off tomorrow, so Desiree and Calamity are gonna cover her acts. Once she wandered back off, the others split off too, to get ready, you know. I went to help Jacob with the bar prep. Anything to not think about seeing Chalcedony all night, knowing what\u2019s gonna happen tomorrow. I\u2019m, well, not very good at lying. Maybe if I hang out with Desiree all night, Chalcedony will avoid us. Here\u2019s hoping...<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Sometimes I really enjoy my life. The last two days have been amazing, with only a few unpleasant hiccups to interrupt the flow.<br /> <br /> I stayed up all night after we finished the movies two days ago. I spent most of my time studying, of course, but when dawn rolled around I slipped out of our bedroom and headed down to the kitchen. While I\u2019m nowhere near Gawain\u2019s level of skill, I flatter myself that I\u2019m not a bad cook when the situation calls for it. I spent a little while mixing, kneading, and rolling dough, and a short while later I had two trays of bread: one of croissants and one of baguettes. I applied a little honey-butter glaze, chopped up some fruit, and diced a bit of cheese, and I was nearly ready.<br /> <br /> A few minutes later, I had D and Julia escort Marguerite into our bedroom for breakfast in bed. Why didn\u2019t I just bring it to her myself? Why, because I used my own body as the table, of course! So that was fun, but I needed a shower afterward.<br /> <br /> We joined the rest of the motley for a more traditional sex breakfast after the shower, though none of us ate much. Talk turned to how Desiree could help out around the house to pay us back for our hospitality. At the time I pooh-poohed the idea, since we\u2019re not doing it for gain, but she insisted. We decided in the end that she could both perform (on nights when Chalcedony is not performing) and help out behind the scenes. Her only stipulation was that she not be required to perform immediately after one of my acts. Her flattery made me blush.<br /> <br /> I have also been granted the dubious distinction of being the only member of the motley who is allowed to strangle people at the Dream House. I can only assume that this is because I\u2019m the member of the motley who is least likely to <u><u>want</u></u> to strangle anyone at the Dream House (though D quirked an eyebrow at me curiously and whispered \u201cas long as you\u2019re careful about it\u201d).<br /> <br /> Sandoval arrived later to discuss Queen Charlotte\u2019s decision regarding Chalcedony. The reigning monarch has decided that it\u2019s time to do away with Chalcedony\u2019s scripts once and for all, and she\u2019s going to force the issue in the very near future. The Autumn Court\u2019s oracles have informed her that Chalcedony will almost certainly resist, which means she\u2019ll need to be restrained, and the scripts will have to be removed by force. Sandoval wanted to ask us if Charlotte\u2019s agents could approach her here, at the Dream House.<br /> <br /> That sparked a bit of a debate. The Dream House is supposed to be a safe haven for all Changelings of the Freehold, and if we allowed one of our performers to be ambushed and restrained here, our reputation would certainly suffer. On the other hand, the only other place Chalcedony can reliably be expected to be found is her home, and kidnapping someone from their home so that you can invade their mind is not a great way to convince them that you have their best interests at heart.<br /> <br /> So in the end we decided to refuse the Monarch\u2019s request. I felt bad about it, but we really need to maintain the image of our club as a place of safety for all Changelings. If we let that slide once \u2013 even for a good cause \u2013 then who\u2019s going to trust us in the future?<br /> <br /> Marguerite left the room while this discussion was going on, looking upset. I followed her into the hall and we talked things out. She doesn\u2019t like the idea of restraining Chalcedony and forcing her to have her scripts removed, even as she recognizes the necessity of it. I told her that I didn\u2019t much care for the situation either, honestly. She promised me that she wouldn\u2019t do anything rash like warn Chalcedony or spirit her away or anything like that, and I believe her. The two of us joined the others in the kitchen after the conversation about Chalcedony had been concluded.<br /> <br /> D and I opted to show Sandoval out. There was the usual flirtatious banter \u2013 which in D\u2019s case amounted to \u201cyou haven\u2019t fucked me in a while, what\u2019s up with that?\u201d \u2013 and the three of us made plans to share a tryst the following evening. I confess that I\u2019ve been looking forward to it for a while now\u2026 Sandoval is a good looking guy, and a real straight arrow, though he hasn\u2019t let his impeccable honor dampen his sense of humor at all. At least, he gave me a dazzling grin when I offered him whipped cream in the kitchen.<br /> <br /> So the whole motley took the evening off again last night so that we could celebrate Insincere Marguerite\u2019s birthday in style. Things started out quite classy, with Gawain preparing a dinner fit for a French dignitary. Marguerit