g make up D/s sex between her and Becky would most likely not actually work.<br /> <br /> Shit. Becky knows what I want. Does the fact that she brought up me checking out the scene mean I've been itching for it around her more than I realize. I wonder... I mean, she wants what the person she's with wants. So, if I was really, really needing to put some pretty little chew-toy through the ringer that's what she'd want. Hell, maybe just letting go of everything would be good for her. I mean, being relieved of the pressure of being responsible for anything including yourself is awfully freeing. But... does she actually trust me that much? Hell, do I fucking trust me that much? This is fucking Becky I'm talking about here. And would it make things weird between us? I mean, we've had nights where things went way past anything that would be safe or sane for people without healing magic on tap. And while she's quite aware that while I won't give my power up, she also knows damn well that when the mood strikes I sure as fuck can enjoy having it ripped violently away from me. But still, being the one doing the breaking and being the one getting worked over are worlds apart. <br /> <br /> Whatever, tonight isn't the right time to get into this shit. Tonight I am going to give her my gift and then we'll go back to her place and do body shots until our tongues meander to more interesting spots and the night turns into a blur of good old fashioned vanilla debauchery. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> So, the day started out with Lori coming down to the kitchen and gathering up bread, cheese and fruit to bring up to her ladies so they could have breakfast in bed for Insincere Marguerite\u2019s birthday. I think Lori said something about being the table. So, that pushed back the regular start to the day but the four of them seemed to be in a good mood so I suppose it was all worth it. While the rest of us had our breakfast Desiree asked if there was some way that she could be useful to the Dream House. Whether that was greeting guests at the door or performing on stage, she wanted to do something to pay us back for our hospitality. She admitted that if she were to become too closely associated with our motley, such as joining it, it would be bad for our reputation. But as it is we have a fairly neutral reputation, and are fairly well respected by the Courts. We didn\u2019t make any firm plans on what Desiree could do, but it opened the door for further discussion.<br /> <br /> After breakfast Sandoval showed up to talk. Apparently the monarchs have been talking and Queen Charlotte has decided that Chalcedony will have the scripts in her head removed, willingly or not. The original idea was to detain her when she came to the Dream House for the show tomorrow. For his part Sandoval is pretty certain that Chalcedony will fight whoever tries to restrain her. He also said that it would not happen during a show, so there would be no disruption of our usual evening\u2019s activities. People reacted differently to this news. Insincere Marguerite left the room entirely. She was upset I think about the idea that someone would physically force Chalcedony to submit to having her scripts removed. We all know that it is important that the scripts not be an issue, but I think Marguerite was having more of a problem with the manner in which they planned to do it. No one was keen on this happening at the Dream House, or at her own home. Places that she goes to frequently should not have a negative connotation to them if at all possible. Taking her at her home would make that place feel unsafe for her. Taking her at the Dream House would make our place feel unsafe. It would also go against our stated neutrality in most issues. So the revised plan is to summon Chalcedony to court and have some of us waiting for her. We would then restrain her and have Gawain remove the scripts. I think he\u2019s going to have his work cut out for him. Desiree was willing and it all went pretty smooth. Chalcedony I think will not be cooperative and will fight him as he works.<br /> <br /> The only alternative to forcing Chalcedony to submit is to kill her outright, and Sandoval was very much against the idea of just slitting the azure lady\u2019s throat. I think we were all fairly dead set against the idea of Chalcedony getting killed. No one was particularly keen on forcing her to do something against her will either, but we all understood what is at stake. We don\u2019t know what her scripts are telling her to do, and what she may have done already. She could be a danger to the freehold in general, or to individuals. We don\u2019t know. And that is what we need to find out and put a stop to.<br /> <br /> After Sandoval left we all split up to do separate things. Julia left to paint, Gawain went to make sure that he\u2019s got what he needs to make Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Birthday dinner. I\u2019m not sure what the others were planning on doing. Luna and I left to go to the park so I missed what everyone else was planning to do. It was nice, walking in the park. I haven\u2019t been in a long time and it was relaxing and normal. I guess we\u2019ve just had so much stuff going on lately that it felt good to just get out and do something not at all weird or stressful or dangerous. Plus it was nice to just get outside. The trees created a nice shady path and it was reminiscent of hikes me and my sister used to take at home. Even though it\u2019s much too warm here I prefer being outside than in. I just like the way the trees sound when the wind blows through the leaves, or the branches creaking as they move. The earthy smell of leaves on the forest floor. Even the smell of grass is preferable to recycled and cooled air.<br /> <br /> So, we arrived back to the Dream House to the aroma of Gawain\u2019s cooking. It smelled really good. He cooked a sumptuous French meal with cr\u00e8me brule for dessert. It was really good. I think Insincere Marguerite really liked it too, which was the whole point, it being her Birthday dinner and all. Lucky us that we have such a good chef in the house. I\u2019m glad that Gawain decided to move in earlier this year instead of keeping his own apartment, and not just because he cooks really well. I think Gawain is a good influence on the rest of us, but especially on me and Calamity.<br /> <br /> After the meal was over we sat around trying to decide what to do and Luna just started throwing a knife up in the air and catching it again. Anyone else might have been showing off, but Luna was just passing the time. In the beginning anyway. When it became apparent that I was watching and Lori couldn\u2019t concentrate on anything else Luna started adding little tricks and switching hands. She really is very talented with those blades of hers. Lori and some of the others lightly teased Luna for trying to seduce them with her knife throwing abilities. I think she knew that it was all in good fun.<br /> <br /> Once the teasing was done we somehow came to the idea of playing Twister. I agreed since I couldn\u2019t remember the last time I actually played that game and I kind of wanted to see how the others would do. Luna included. So, we played Twister. Calamity called out the positions since it might get dangerous if she played. I think we all did rather well. Marguerite won the first round, though I wasn\u2019t far behind her. I\u2019m still not sure how I got my left hand on red, but I made it work. Lori was a little off her game at first. I think her wings were throwing her off for a bit. She made up for it in the second game. For the second round we decided to play \u201cstrip Twister.\u201d Twister with less clothes. I agreed, but I wasn\u2019t going to go past my shorts. Luna also did not want to go past her underwear. Insincere Marguerite of course won the second game, but this time no one came close to her score. She is amazingly bendy. Lori also did much better the second round. I think she finally got the hang of what to do with her wings.<br /> <br /> After the game was over things devolved just a bit. Someone came up with the idea of a motley-wide orgy. Yeah, I wasn\u2019t actually so keen on that. I like one partner at a time. Luna was also not interested in participating so we both excused ourselves and went back to my room. Okay..it was more like Luna jumped out a window and glided to the ground. I gathered up our clothes and met up with her outside. We then adjourned to my room for our own night of fun. Luna is sleeping as I write this. She looks so peaceful in sleep. Her wings even flutter just a bit now and again. She\u2019s gorgeous. <br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> This morning was kind of awkward between some of the other members of the motley. Mostly De la Rocha and Julia. De la Rocha went downstairs to the work out room and went at the punching bag for a good bit. Julia on the other hand went upstairs and painted. A lot. I was told that her current works were a little on the macabre side. Not that this is a surprise for Julia, she goes into some dark places in her art. I just wasn\u2019t expecting it after last night. I guess an orgy might have been a bit too much for the slight artist. De la Rocha tends to be a more private person with her affections, so I can see why she might feel a little awkward in front of everyone else after last night. I think that Lori went to check on both her girls before she went for a jog.<br /> <br /> While the others were jogging, painting or meditating I talked with Luna. She has noticed that there is a lot of drama going on in the Dream House. Julia painting suicides, Calamity being upset with the monarchs, everybody\u2019s stressed over Chalcedony and having to act normal around the other girl tonight at the club. Luna actually suggested writing a Roman a clef based on the denizens of the Dream House. After asking her what that was, I thought it sounded like a fun idea. I haven\u2019t done anything just for the sheer silliness of it for a while and this sounded like it could prove to be a silly endeavor. Now to come up with names for everyone\u2026<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> My birthday was much better than the previous few days had been.<br /> <br /> I got breakfast in bed from Lori, who provided the table (with her body, as is appropriate), and the girls and I had a good time. That really was an excellent start. I hope it happens again. Breakfast with the rest of the Motley went well afterwards, and Julia was pointedly submissive, which pleased I. It was, all in all, an excellent start. Definitely.<br /> <br /> Then Sandoval came by. He wanted to discuss, basically, ambushing and de-brainwashing Chalcedony. While for her own good, it would almost certainly involve overpowering her and forcing the change on her. Eventually I left the room. The thought of her being so manhandled was awful, and I was upset. I did not leave in protest, however, and made that clear to Lorelei when she came to see I. I think they decided to give Chalcedony her second abduction elsewhere. Fortunately.<br /> <br /> I find it all so unsettling, though while I can see why somewhat, I cannot help but wonder at the degree to which I am upset. I did not have the experiences others did. Is it loyalty to my friend, perhaps? I am quite a loyal person. Absolutely.<br /> <br /> So while everything was going on birthday spankings came up, and Julia presented herself for one to me, so I used my tongue. This got the usual reactions though Desiree was rather intrigued, and remained so. When we broke up to go separate ways, I confronted her, and wound up kissing her against the wall. I pulled her into a nearby mirror and we wound up in my room, where I showed her just how much my talents can do. It was honestly intense, in the way it is with Lori\u2026she was determined to push back and not submit, and like Lori I wore her down in time. I was perhaps more aggressive than I am with Lori. Still, it was a lot of fun, and Desiree is quite talented and graceful. I had never been with one of the Dancer Kith, and I suppose her Romancer Kith helped as well. Certainly.<br /> <br /> She was glorious, as was the push and pull of will. The temptation to steal her from the Director is strong. The Director, I have decided, does not deserve Desiree. Probably.<br /> <br /> But I must be good.<br /> <br /> While she recovered, I went downstairs and found the others, my spirits raised. They did not disappoint me. Gawain\u2019s meal was positively excellent. I do not exaggerate when I say he can make a worthy meal for any son or daughter of France. Soon enough the evening was full of Strip Twister (with Calamity calling given her lethal body) and the inevitable result of Strip Twister. Gloriously.<br /> <br /> I, of course, won at both.<br /> <br /> Jacob and Luna opted out of the sex party, while Desiree remained along with the rest of the Motley. Julia and Gawain seemed to politely avoid each other, and it worked out,. Beautifully.<br /> <br /> But now I am simply exhausted, and must sleep. Immediately.<br /> <br /> -o- -o- -o- -o- -o- -o- -o- -o-<br /> <br /> An interesting beginning to the day.<br /> <br /> Julia has been in her studio all day. She was out before I woke, she is there now as we get ready for the show, painting suicides. I think she has to deal with what happened last night. She says she will be okay. I have to remember she lead a sheltered life before. I was her first\u2026everything. Kiss, partner, everything. This may have been a bit much. Probably.<br /> <br /> We each spent time with her, Lori, De La Rocha, and I. I do think she is all right, but I doubt she will want to repeat the experience. Possibly.<br /> <br /> De La Rocha had some awkwardness with a few of us, like Calamity and Gawain who she had very different feelings about than her lovers, but she seemed mostly okay. De La Rocha is tough. I like that about her. Intriguingly.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve never had the \u201cwoke up the next day and things were weird\u201d experience, but that is more De La Rocha\u2019s issue. Apparently. She still looked quite impressive in her spikey leathers. Deliciously.<br /> <br /> Lori has plans apparently for the next two nights. De La Rocha is involved in tonight\u2019s at least. Just as well, Julia needs a little TLC. I think Calamity and Gawain are seeing Becky. Never a dull moment here. Naturally.<br /> <br /> I may see what is up with Desiree if Calamity and Gawain both spend the night with Becky. Julia could get to know her better. However, if Calamity and Becky\u2019s time is private, I suspect Gawain would appreciate Desiree\u2019s company. The two are, after all, quite close, moreso than she is to anyone else in the Motley. Certainly.<br /> <br /> But now we all get ready for tonight, where we look Chalcedony in the eye and pretend she is not going to be grabbed, abducted, held against her will, and have her mind altered. Horrifically.<br /> <br /> I am not looking forward to it. At all.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LI</i><br /> <br /> This is what happens when your GM is running on 2.5 hours sleep, but the orgy was not my idea, nor was Strip Twister. Random references to Raul Julia or GG Allin were may fault. But seriously, when was the last time you saw those two names in the same sentence, anyway.<br /> <br /> I think Insincere Marguerite got 18 successes or something crazy like that to win Strip Twister. She used her rote action and everything.<br /> <br /> So Lori\u2019s love life is exciting eh? We will have to see how she handles all the attention.<br /> <br /> Okay, well Comments and Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T01:43:42-07:00","id":847581,"title":"","content":"Hey Baroness, I have to say that I love reading through your APs. It sounds like you're doing an amazing job and your NPCs do an amazing job of bringing out the PCs. I can't say how awesome it's been to read the interactions and hear your remarks as GM afterwards. <br /> <br /> Some questions; how do you find the pictures for all of your npcs? Trolling the internet through deviantart/pinterest/other sources? <br /> <br /> How has the Entitlements changed the PCs from your perspective? Do you think they are an aspect of the characters that have joined them, or have they just not come up in game that much? Also, mostly curious about Jacob, but mein wise, how has Jacob's face changed? Or are you guys hand waving the Mein changes, as I don't believe it's ever been mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11332-freresebastian","name":"FrereSebastian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T11:42:10-07:00","id":847778,"title":"","content":"The Baroness gave me the choice of having Jacob's mein change or leaving it as it was. I elected to leave it as it was. The other Knights mein's have not changed either, so I figured that fit. :-)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7378-nanae07","name":"Nanae07","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T13:04:50-07:00","id":847809,"title":"","content":"Hey FrereSabastian!<br /> <br /> I'm glad you are enjoying yourself! My NPCs are really my biggest strength, and I am glad they work out well We get a lot of chatter and speculation on them. And I am glad the remarks help. I don't need as many this game with the large number of journals done.<br /> <br /> I keep a very large and growing archive of pictures. it means I have a lot to call on, and when a campaign ends, a lot of comparatively minor NPCs pics become &quot;available&quot; for elsewhere, though more prominent do not (I don't know if Julia or De La Rocha will ever be anyone but those people, for example, unless the group has pretty much no one in common with MDH) But I look at image threads and collect cool pictures, see them on twitter or facebook or news articles, some of my group sometimes sends me some, or I just take a mood to GIS a broad subject to collect pics (Goths is at least every 6-8 months). When I need one I don't have a good match for I may actively GIS or look through DeviantArt, or ask a member of my groups. (&quot;Does anyone have a gothic or vampiric looking woman with bone spikes coming out of her back and elbows?&quot; &quot;If we did would we not have sent it to you?&quot; &quot;Oh, right.&quot;)<br /> <br /> I tend to take any Mien changes for Seeming, Kith, or Entitlement as a suggestion. So PCs or NPCs may or may not display them. I think the PCs here generally do not.<br /> <br /> If you are enjoying Changeling journals, Golden Eagle has maybe half as many sessions and three Changelings among the PCs, as well as a Changeling subplot going on. Just more that could give you ideas.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the feedback! Always welcome!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T01:48:02-07:00","id":853941,"title":"","content":"A newcomer arrives in the Dream House, seeking sanctuary. But it is a second sanctuary seeker whose arrival tears a gorge into the Motley\u2019s trust and unity, and those pillars begin to fall. Note the short fiction for Insincere Marguerite did not happen in game but is part of the storyline.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> Nov 7th, afternoon<br /> <br /> Well, so far things have gone well. Mostly. I haven\u2019t had time to dwell on what\u2019s going to happen tonight, at least. I mean, it wasn\u2019t all, you know, thrilling, but it was fun and nice and all. It was good to be able to help someone without all this \u2018for her own good despite her own will\u2019 thing, you know?<br /> <br /> To explain, there was the show, last night, and it went well. I\u2019d been worried about talking with Chalcedony, you know, and not being able to keep a lid on it, so I stuck with Desiree, like I mentioned was my plan. It worked. Also it meant that when she saw someone she recognized from Hollywood, we both went over to talk with her.<br /> <br /> Gloria was pretty cute. I could see why Desiree was into her. I could also see why Gloria might have cause to be a little leery, at that point. See, they\u2019d been, you know, best friends when Desiree showed up in Hollywood. Like, platonic sleeping in the same bed, vouching for you to the Monarchs, best friends. Then it came out that Desiree was a loyalist, and had a file on her and everything.<br /> <br /> It was rough, separating things that happened for real from the, you know, propaganda and stuff that the Court of Fallen Stars put out there. Like the horror stories they spread around about the Night Court and Madame Spidertoes. Those last ones got her thrown against the wall, since she repeated them in De la Roche\u2019s earshot. I did my best to explain about who Madame Spidertoes really is, as best as you can, you know? Insincere Marguerite talked with her about the Night Court stuff, pointing out in made a nice scapegoat for all those disappearing Changelings. De la Roche and Gloria seem to have made up though, so that\u2019s good. De la Roche did calm down pretty quickly for that matter. I did have to yell at her though. I guess I was a little tense.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Gloria had come here cause she heard the Dream House in particular was a safe place, and she knew the freehold in general was not a place the Hollywood Courts would be interested in pursuing someone unless it was really really important, you know? Her Motley mates had all gone missing - an Elemental about a month ago, a pair of Darklings who\u2019d more recently found... something that worried them and then disappeared, and shortly before she\u2019d left, an Ogre who went to the Courts to demand their motley mates return and only just managed to get a message back urging her to get out of town. So she was a little, you know, freaked out.<br /> <br /> At a whisper from Calamity, I used Potential to get her motivations. She seemed on the level with what she said, though she\u2019d had the plan that since she knew Desiree was a loyalist and entangled in the Courts, she\u2019d come and kill her, revealing what she knew to ingratiate herself with us. That was kinda foiled by Desiree just walking up and saying hi, and I guess by me, you know, not really responding by her calling Desiree a loyalist.<br /> <br /> I got up with Joan to get Gloria an audience with Viscount Augustine. We maybe, you know, got a little sidetracked talking about her new acquisition - it\u2019s just off the shelf, so she was hoping I could mod it a bit, fix the balance the way she likes it, build up the guard a little. It should be a fun project. But anyways, she worked out a meeting for this afternoon, which is where Gloria is now.<br /> <br /> Everybody was feeling better by the time the show was over. Flores got Julia to come down. Calamity and Becky went off to Becky\u2019s place - I bowed out to look after our new charge, you know? Lori and De la Roche had their date with Sandoval, and Desiree and I were getting Gloria set up in the spare bedroom. Things went a little off the rails there, since Gloria was not all about having a private conversation with the woman who was a loyalist with a file on her, as of the last thing Gloria knew about her.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m still a little worried I screwed up the conversation after. Well, after that and after Desiree got invited up to bed with Flores, Insincere Marguerite and Julia. I think she was seeing if I wanted to be with her instead, and, you know, I did, but I needed to stay alert, in case Gloria hadn\u2019t gotten off as scot free as she\u2019d thought. And I didn\u2019t quite get that that\u2019s what it was until later, when I was venting to Jacob a little bit. He was a good friend last night - I don\u2019t even remember what all I, you know, babbled about, but things did seem clearer after.<br /> <br /> Sex breakfast went well. Gloria drowned her embarrassment in Irish coffee. Thinking about it, I guess we do have that kinda atmosphere, especially at breakfast, you know - she asked if we were a vernal motley. Calamity\u2019s jokes about it kinda drove Julia off again, but not, you know, angry or something. It started cause De la Roche was flirting with Gloria by pointing out who was her girlfriend, which was kinda weird? But I guess it worked - De la Roche took her off for a tour and there was lots of giggling. Plus De la Roche came and asked Desiree\u2019s permission to seduce Gloria, so... I guess so.<br /> <br /> That did kinda ruin all the cheering up I\u2019d been doing. Desiree kept going back and forth between seeming like she was blaming herself, getting upset at Gloria or feeling like nothing was done wrong, really. Gloria is obviously important to her and I really don\u2019t think she would have done anything to hurt her. Like Desiree said, the point was to neutralize the Grand Maw, not drag people back. The file, I guess, was just, you know, standard operating procedure, probably.<br /> <br /> I still did a little better with it this afternoon than last night though, even with De la Roche\u2019s help, I think. Right now she\u2019s working with Calamity on choreography. I guess they started when I introduced Gloria to Joan, you know, so she could take our new charge to meet Viscount Augustine. That was fun - Joan blushed a bright red as soon as she saw Lori, so it wasn\u2019t hard for even me to make a guess as to who Lori\u2019s secret date was with. Especially with the \u2018see you soon\u2019. I tried to help her get her cool back by talking about her new blade which worked mostly, I think.<br /> <br /> Just a few more hours until we get the call. Hopefully the rehearsal and show will keep me from fretting too much.<br /> <br /> <br /> Evening, November 7th<br /> <br /> It is begun. The blue Dancer has been restrained and Lady Oleander is utilizing her impressive skills with poisons to maintain bodily control of her until she is deposited in the Lighthouse, as that is where they have planned to secure her. This is not as we intended, not as any of us intended - we had no desire to break the sanctuary that is our very livelihood, even should there have been no other considerations - but the Director and his scripts have forced our hand, leaving us with no choice if we intend for her to regain her own free will.<br /> <br /> As best as we have been able to ascertain, a script was triggered this afternoon, prompting the Dancer to contact Lady DeLisle, claiming that she had caught the spy Lady Nuit lurking about her apartment. Now, Lord Stojanovic has informed us that while Lady Nuit was in fact lurking about at the behest of her liege, she was never seen. Rather she made another phone call, one of the many she had made this past day, hanging up without leaving a message, and contacted our leonine Darkling for help.<br /> <br /> And help she was willing to give. To the extent that she forsook her date with Lady Felicity and vowed to protect Lady Chalcedony in this her time of need. Her behavior was more than passing strange. Even if, as she told my lady in a raised voice, the sudden change of arrangements could be explained solely by the danger her friend claimed to be in, it doesn\u2019t explain any of the details surrounding the compromising position we found them in. Or the odd, yielding nature of their interactions of late.<br /> <br /> It also does not excuse the state our Darkling thief left my lady in. True, I suppose if her behavior is merely an extension of the mind controlling effects of the Director, I will extend her the same grace Lady Chalcedony will be offered. However, if she continues to vent her disorganized discomfort with the situation at my Lady Calamity in my absence, I will not be pleased. This is difficult for all of us, and if she cannot see past her addled lust to communicate with anything beyond doe eyes for Lady Chalcedony and vitriol for the Lady Calamity, then I have no time to waste on her right now.<br /> <br /> In addition to causing my wife pain, Lady DeLisle\u2019s lashing out has cost me my right hand. Our work will begin, make no mistake, but without Lady Calamity\u2019s aid, it will proceed at a much slower pace. But my love is in no position to enter the world of dreams at this time. Lord Stojanovic watches over her for now, and Lady De la Roche does the same for Lady Gloria. Those two, I have hope, will maintain order in my house until I have restored Lady Chalcedony to her actual self, whoever that may be, whether she know who that is or not. Until then, I have my duty.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Well, okay\u2026 I admit that could have gone better. Recent events have us all questioning the nobility of our own actions\u2026 and have turned members of the motley against each other. I can only hope that things will blow over given time.<br /> <br /> During the show last night, most of my motley-mates were studiously avoiding Chalcedony, presumably to avoid giving away anything about her upcoming deprogramming. I figured that if anything this standoffish attitude would be more likely to put her on her guard, so I tried to act normally around her. I hope it worked.<br /> <br /> Gawain was hanging out with Desiree (again, presumably because that\u2019s the most sure-fire way to avoid Chalcedony) while Calamity made her rounds and Jacob tended bar as usual. We had a pretty good crowd last night, with a lot of familiar faces and a few new ones making an appearance.<br /> <br /> So I only had one solo last night: my rendition of \u201cAngel of the Morning.\u201d I knew it mostly from the original Merilee Rush version and the Olivia Newton John cover, but the song has been remade more times than I can count over the years. I\u2019m told that a pop-country singer with the unlikely name of Juice Newton recorded a very well-received version a few years after I was Taken, though I haven\u2019t taken the time to seek it out. Sure, the lyrics are a little on the nose for someone like me, but what can I say? I\u2019m a sucker for that sort of smoky melancholy.<br /> <br /> So I get to the end of my song, right, and the spots go down and the house lights come up for an intermission, and as usual I scan the crowd for D. And what do I see but my honey with some poor blonde pinned up against the wall by her throat. Gawain was on it, of course, and it looked like he was having a few not entirely cheerful words with D. Most of the crowd hadn\u2019t noticed anything yet, and D let the poor girl go before they did. She sort of stalked off into the courtyard after that. I took my bows, hurried off the stage, and bustled over to the table where Gawain, Desiree, and the new girl were sitting.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat happened?\u201d I asked Gawain quietly as I approached.<br /> <br /> \u201cThis is Gloria,\u201d he answered just as discretely. \u201cShe\u2019s a refugee from Hollywood. She was telling us about some of the rumors they\u2019re spreading about the Lady By the Sea, and\u2026 Madame Spidertoes\u2019 name came up,\u201d he trailed off delicately.<br /> <br /> \u201cShit,\u201d I muttered to myself. I turned to face the pretty blonde. \u201cI\u2019m sorry about that, Miss. D has a temper. I\u2019ll go talk to her.\u201d<br /> <br /> The woman named Gloria assured me that she would be okay, but she was still rubbing her throat as I walked away. I hurried out into the night and found D sitting by the fountain. Her mantle was flaring, and the air around her seemed to shimmer with a midsummer heat haze. The water in the fountain was steaming subtly.<br /> <br /> \u201cHey,\u201d I said quietly as I approached.<br /> <br /> \u201cHey,\u201d she replied glumly.<br /> <br /> \u201cWant to tell me what that was all about?\u201d I asked, careful to keep any blame or judgment out of my voice.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe was spreading lies about Madame Spidertoes,\u201d she said sullenly.<br /> <br /> I sat down next to her and put an arm around her waist. \u201cShe was repeating the propaganda she\u2019d heard from the Hollywood Courts,\u201d I said soothingly. \u201cShe didn\u2019t know any better.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThen she should learn to keep her bitch mouth shut,\u201d D spat venomously.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019s a guest in our house, D,\u201d I reminded her. \u201cThis is supposed to be a safe haven for all changelings.\u201d<br /> <br /> D refused to meet my eyes. \u201cWell, she\u2019ll know better next time,\u201d she muttered. \u201cAnd if not, I\u2019ll be happy to repeat the lesson.\u201d<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t have an answer for that, so we just sat there in silence together for a while. After a few minutes, I gently extricated myself from her arm and stood. \u201cI should get back inside for the rest of the show,\u201d I said. \u201cYou gonna be okay out here?\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cI just need some time to cool off,\u201d she admitted. \u201cI\u2019ll see you after the show, babe.\u201d<br /> <br /> I started to walk away, but she caught my wrist in one of her hands. \u201cLori,\u201d she said quietly, \u201cI just want you to know. The things she said about Spidertoes\u2026 if she\u2019d said them about <u><u>you</u></u>, I would have <u><u>killed</u></u> her.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled sadly and leaned in to kiss her. \u201cThanks, sweetie,\u201d I whispered, \u201cbut, y\u2019know\u2026 sticks and stones, right? I can deal with a little rumor-mongering if I have to.\u201d<br /> <br /> I headed back inside and made my way to Gawain\u2019s table again. \u201cSorry about that,\u201d I said to Gloria again once I\u2019d taken a seat. \u201cD\u2019s a good person, really, but she has a hair trigger when it comes to Madame Spidertoes. Please don\u2019t judge her too harshly.\u201d<br /> <br /> Gloria nodded. \u201cIt\u2019s okay,\u201d she said. \u201cI shouldn\u2019t have bad-mouthed such an important member of your Freehold. Would it help if I apologized, and told her that I was just repeating what the Courts tell us in Hollywood to scare us away from this place?\u201d<br /> <br /> I shook my head. \u201cIt might be best just to drop it, honestly. And there\u2019s no need for you to apologize, Gloria\u2026 you didn\u2019t do anything wrong.\u201d<br /> <br /> We chatted for a while after that, and Gawain filled me in on Gloria\u2019s story. She\u2019d fled Hollywood following the disappearance of pretty much her entire motley. One of them vanished without a trace a couple of months ago, and the rest seemed to drop off the face of the Earth more recently as they investigated his disappearance. Finally a day or two ago, one of the last remaining members texted her and warned her to get out of town as quickly as possible. She hasn\u2019t been able to contact any of them since.<br /> <br /> I glanced at Gawain and Desiree as she was imparting this information, and I could tell that we were all thinking the same thing. If Gloria\u2019s motley was poking around and asking uncomfortable questions of the Hollywood monarchs, then it seems all too likely that they have been given to the Grand Maw. It\u2019s a horrible thought, and I don\u2019t want to believe that changelings could do that to each other\u2026 but I\u2019m not as na\u00efve as I used to be.<br /> <br /> None of us mentioned these thoughts out loud, as we didn\u2019t want to upset Gloria. Once the show wrapped up and the place started to empty, we gathered the motley and began to discuss what we should do about the situation. D joined us and murmured a hasty apology to Gloria. Gawain called Joan, who offered to set up a meeting with Viscount Augustine (Gloria is Summer Court). We also offered to put her up for the night in one of our guest rooms. Gloria gratefully accepted both offers.<br /> <br /> I was a little on edge after the tense first encounter between D and Gloria, and I was watching them both to make sure there was no bad blood between them. It is therefore a little odd that it took me a while to notice an odd, subtle flirtation between those two. I don\u2019t know what triggered it\u2026 maybe Gloria is into strong, forceful women or something like that. D obviously felt bad about overreacting to Gloria\u2019s offhand comments earlier, and was maybe overcompensating a bit in her embarrassment. But hey\u2026 Gloria\u2019s a beautiful girl, and who am I to tell anyone not to act upon their desires? In any case, it didn\u2019t take me long to insinuate myself into this situation.<br /> <br /> Desiree had also noticed this flirtation, and it seemed to make her equal parts sad and angry. I can\u2019t really blame her for that, I guess\u2026 she and Gloria used to be very close friends back in Hollywood, and it\u2019s obvious to anyone who\u2019s paying attention that Desiree is still carrying something of a torch for Gloria. From what I understand, the two of them were never actually intimate, and any possibility along those lines was firmly shut down when it came out that Desiree was a Loyalist. I\u2026 can\u2019t really blame Gloria for that, either, though from Desiree\u2019s