ld be adapted for the following evening.<br /> <br /> The three of us got up late the next morning for Sex Breakfast, and decided to save time by sharing a shower. Of course, as you might imagine, the shower ended up taking twice as long as it would have if we\u2019d just gone separately, but who cares?<br /> <br /> Sex Breakfast proceeded as usual, with Sandoval, Flores, Becky, Desiree, and Gloria all in attendance (as well as the usual suspects, of course). The quips were firing back and forth pretty regularly, and I think we might have embarrassed Gloria a bit. D took pity on her and offered to give her a tour of the house and the grounds, and she latched on to that offer like a drowning woman. After the initial unpleasantness, those two seem to have really hit it off. Good for them. Of course, if she hurts D, or tries to steal her away from me, I will kill her. That should go without saying.<br /> <br /> Ahem. The two of them turned up some time later with D carrying Gloria around one-handed. She can\u2019t resist showing off sometimes, and Gloria seemed to really dig my honey\u2019s incredible strength. We said goodbye to Sandoval and Flores, and Calamity showed Becky out after securing a promise that the Claviger would be here tonight for Calamity\u2019s performance.<br /> <br /> Since I had made plans with Joan and Andromeda tonight, I asked Jacob to serve as chaperone over Marguerite and Felicity\u2019s date in my stead, and he agreed. As I know he doesn\u2019t trust Felicity, he seemed like the ideal choice to make sure she wasn\u2019t up to anything untoward. Plus, Calamity was going to be performing, Julia would have stabbed Felicity without adequate provocation, and subtlety is not D\u2019s forte. <br /> <br /> While we were discussing this in the foyer, Joan showed up at the door to escort Gloria to her meeting with Viscount Augustine. Gawain brought Gloria to the front door and we commended her to Joan\u2019s keeping.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re in good hands, Gloria,\u201d I assured her as she gave me a nervous glance. \u201cWhile Joan\u2019s protecting you, you\u2019re safe from pretty much anything.\u201d<br /> <br /> Joan nodded. \u201cDo not fear, miss. I will convey you safely to the monarch. You have my vow.\u201d Then she turned to the rest of us. \u201cIt is good to see you again, friends. I hope all is well with you. And Lorelei, I shall see you\u2026 soon,\u201d she finished awkwardly. She was blushing beet red, which was somewhat startling with her usually pale complexion, white clothes, and platinum blonde hair.<br /> <br /> I beamed at her. \u201cLooking forward to it, Joan,\u201d I said softly.<br /> <br /> Gawain and Jacob gave me knowing looks as the door closed behind them. \u201cOkay, you figured it out,\u201d I grumbled as we walked back toward the kitchen, \u201cbut please don\u2019t say anything to anyone else, okay? She made me promise I wouldn\u2019t tell anyone. She\u2019s very self-conscious, and I don\u2019t want to do or say anything which would upset or embarrass her.\u201d<br /> <br /> They both promised to keep mum about my plans for the evening, and we rejoined the others in the kitchen, and everything was okay for a while. <br /> <br /> Then Marguerite\u2019s phone rang. That\u2019s when everything started to go wrong with today.<br /> <br /> The call was from Chalcedony. Little Girl Blue was in a lather because she thought she had spotted Molly Nuit skulking around her apartment before she could activate her invisibility. Marguerite and Calamity went to check on her, and Jacob excused himself to make a discrete phone call. He came back a few minutes later, reporting that Boss Lowjack had told him that Molly <u><u>was</u></u> watching Chalcedony (which is perfectly reasonable in light of her recent behavior), but that he could not reach her at the moment. A later call from the monarch informed us that he had connected with Molly, and that she had been watching Chalcedony but had remained invisible the whole time and had never been spotted. Chalcedony had made several phone calls that morning, but had spoken to no one and left no messages, after which she had called Marguerite and asked for protection and sanctuary. Curious.<br /> <br /> In any case, Marguerite and Calamity returned through a mirror a few minutes later with Chalcedony in tow. Marguerite had adopted her typical fawning attitude in regards to the dancer, and Calamity was almost visibly fuming about that. While Marguerite worked to calm Chalcedony, Calamity told the rest of us that she had personally witnessed the blue girl staring deep into Marguerite\u2019s eyes as she asked the darkling to stay with her until she felt safe. Marguerite\u2019s response sounded like a textbook case of hypnosis to me. She even said she would break off her date with Felicity tonight\u2026 which is something none of us thought she\u2019d do for anything.<br /> <br /> Without actively discussing it, we all agreed that it would be a bad idea to leave Marguerite and Chalcedony alone together, so I found myself relegated to the unfamiliar role of third wheel. Marguerite and I escorted her down into the basement while the others tried to contact the Autumn Court to step up the timetable on Chalcedony\u2019s detainment and deprogramming. We all hated the fact that she had to be taken from the Dream House, which is supposed to be a place of safety and refuge, but none of us \u2013 not even Marguerite \u2013 could see any way around it.<br /> <br /> So the three of us sat there in the basement waiting for something to happen. Ten minutes passed, then fifteen, then twenty. I began to wonder what the others were doing. Chalcedony chatted nervously with the two of us, and her banter began to become lightly flirtatious. I began to grow intrigued by the possibilities \u2013 Chalcedony is a beautiful woman, after all \u2013 but that very fact set off alarm bells in my subconscious, and I resisted the temptation to return her innuendo. I mean, why the sudden interest? She\u2019s always asserted her heterosexuality pretty vigorously in the past, right? <br /> <br /> Marguerite was not so reticent, and it wasn\u2019t long before the two of them were making out hot and heavy. There was a part of me that was still tempted to join in, and I can\u2019t help but wonder if Chalcedony was working some sort of magic or influence on me. I have no proof of that, of course\u2026 and let\u2019s face it, even without supernatural modification my libido has long since gone through healthy and come out on the other side. But I was steadfast in my refusal to give in to temptation.<br /> <br /> I thought about trying to break them up\u2026 it really wasn\u2019t the time for that sort of display, after all. If Chalcedony was really as frightened as she wanted us to think she was, I can\u2019t see her letting her guard down like that for a few minutes of lesbian curiosity. And while Marguerite is certainly a creature of passion, the way she just gave in to her urges in the midst of a crisis\u2026 it rang false to me. I cleared my throat a few times, and tried to strike up a conversation once, but didn\u2019t quite dare to physically separate them.<br /> <br /> I gasped with relief when the rest of the motley knocked on the door. Jacob, Gawain, and Calamity came in after I answered their knock. Calamity said that she needed to speak with Marguerite, and my French lover reluctantly allowed herself to be led from the room. Once they were away, Jacob and Gawain struck. They had prepared a cloth with chloroform, and a few moments later it was all over.<br /> <br /> Marguerite was livid. She hated the fact that Calamity had tricked her into breaking her word (as she had promised that she wouldn\u2019t leave Chalcedony\u2019s side today), and was irate that we apparently believed she could be so easily manipulated by a pretty face. She hauled off and slapped Calamity\u2026 but only succeeded in cutting herself on one of Calamity\u2019s shards.<br /> <br /> I chased after her and caught up with her upstairs. I begged her to stop, and used a healing contract to repair the damage she had done to herself. We had a tense conversation, and I tried to convince her to see Calamity\u2019s side of things, but she was in no mood to be magnanimous. She feels betrayed, and it\u2019s hard to fault that feeling even though I think she\u2019s wrong about it. She refuses to even entertain the possibility that she\u2019s being manipulated, and takes any suggestion to that effect as an insult to her willpower.<br /> <br /> \u201cI am in no state to see Felicity now,\u201d she admitted after a moment. \u201cI shall call her and reschedule our rendezvous.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sorry,\u201d I said, meaning it. \u201cI know how much you were looking forward to it.\u201d I paused for a moment, considering my next words. \u201cI\u2019m here for as long as you need me, Insincere Marguerite,\u201d I said, pulling her into an embrace. \u201cJust let me know what you want, and I\u2019m at your disposal.\u201d<br /> <br /> She smiled then. It was a sad smile, but it was something. \u201cNo,\u201d she breathed into my ear. \u201cYou have an evening planned, my love, and any fool can see how much you are looking forward to it. Go. Enjoy yourself. I will remain here with Julia and de la Rocha. I will be fine.\u201d<br /> <br /> I asked several times if she was sure about that, but she pooh-poohed my concern and practically insisted I proceed with my plans. I\u2019m still not sure if that\u2019s the right thing to do, honestly, but, well\u2026<br /> <br /> Anyway, once I had transferred Marguerite into Julia\u2019s keeping, I headed downstairs to check on Calamity. She was\u2026 not doing well. After Marguerite slapped her, she seemed to sort of retreat into herself. I found her sitting in the basement hallway, looking miserable. Jacob was watching over her from a discrete distance.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019s going to hate me now,\u201d Calamity said dully as I sat down beside her.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019s not,\u201d I reassured her. \u201cLook, she\u2019s very angry right now, but she\u2019ll get over it. Deep down she knows that you did what you did to protect her.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI betrayed her trust,\u201d Calamity sighed.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou did what you had to do to protect her,\u201d I corrected her. I carefully put my arms around her and pulled her close. \u201cYou did the right thing, Calamity,\u201d I said fervently.<br /> <br /> She thanked me, but it was more of a dull acknowledgement that I was trying to help than an actual expression of gratitude for the sentiment. She\u2019s going to have to get through this one on her own for a while. She has to forgive herself before she\u2019ll allow anyone else to help her.<br /> <br /> Shi and Oleander showed up a few minutes later to take Chalcedony into custody. My love had a few chemicals with her which they hoped would keep their charge docile while they transported her. Oleander expressed some concern over the use of chloroform on Chalcedony, as she didn\u2019t want her drugs to interact with the chemicals already in her system, but in the end everything seemed to work out okay. They gave Chalcedony something that made her compliant, and the blue girl seemed to sleepwalk out to their car, where they sedated her more traditionally.<br /> <br /> I pulled Oleander aside briefly before they left. \u201cBe careful sweetie, okay?\u201d I said as we embraced.<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t worry, Lori,\u201d Oleander said seriously, \u201cI know what I\u2019m doing. She\u2019ll be out like a light for the whole trip. We\u2019ll be perfectly safe.\u201d She kissed me tenderly and asked if I was free that night.<br /> <br /> \u201cSorry,\u201d I said with genuine regret, \u201cI\u2019m booked tonight. Give me a day or two?\u201d<br /> <br /> She sighed with mock exasperation. \u201cSometimes I think the worst thing about dating a poly girl is that I have to wait so long between opportunities to see you,\u201d she commented.<br /> <br /> I smiled at her. \u201cI\u2019ll make it worth the wait, I swear. I love you, honey.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLove you too, angel,\u201d she almost sighed. I\u2019m not sure when she started calling me that, but I like it. None of my other girls call me that. It\u2019s just for her.<br /> <br /> A minute later she was gone. Gawain went with them so that he could set up the dream therapy thing to deprogram Chalcedony. Calamity was supposed to go with him, but she was in no state to assist him at that point. I think Jacob\u2019s keeping an eye on her until Gawain gets back.<br /> <br /> So what am I doing in the midst of all this horrible chaos? Predictably, I\u2019m only thinking about myself. I\u2019m not comforting Marguerite; she\u2019s got Julia and D for that. I think I heard Julia singing to her earlier; I\u2019m hoping that\u2019ll have a calming influence on her. I\u2019m not trying to help Calamity out, either. She\u2019s made it clear that she\u2019d like to be alone with her misery; even Gawain acknowledges that there\u2019s very little any of us can do for her right now. So I\u2019m getting ready for my evening with Andromeda and Joan.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m putting on makeup and squeezing into a slinky dress and fixing my hair and oh God I can\u2019t believe what a horrible needy slut I\u2019ve become. The motley is in turmoil and we betrayed the trust of a friend and everything is horrible\u2026 and I just can\u2019t bring myself to break a date with two hot friends who want to spend the evening showering me with love and adoration. I can\u2019t face the strife within my new family, so I\u2019ve opted to ignore it in favor of vanity and sexual gratification.<br /> <br /> And for God\u2019s sake, even though I recognize that what I\u2019m doing is selfish and probably self-destructive, I know I\u2019m going to do it anyway. I am one sick chick.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T01:48:39-07:00","id":853942,"title":"","content":"<b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> Friday, November 7<sup>th</sup><br /> Nine years, seven months, sixteen days<br /> Days without stabbing: 7<br /> <br /> I don't know who Lori's mystery date tonight is with but I have to admit that this has been a pretty damn fine week. Becky came out for last night's show and damn if my breath didn't catch when I laid eyes on her. I am not sure how that woman manages to get sexier every time I see her but she does. Now, I'd put the time in myself getting ready and it was totally worth it to watch her eyes travel over me as I strode up to meet her. We greeted with a kiss that may have lingered a little more than proper before I escorted her to a table to chat and flirt while watching the show.<br /> <br /> Once the door closed, Gawain sat with Desiree since he didn't really want to talk to Chalcedony knowing that the wheels were in motion to have her taken into custody. I think most of the motley was feeling uncomfortable about having to face her knowing what was planned. For my part, I honestly wasn't thinking about her (or much else for that matter) with my beautiful dragon there.<br /> <br /> But I wasn't too distracted to miss that Desiree and Gawain had moved to talk to an unfamiliar Fairest. I was tempted to leave it to them, but I got up and went over to see who she was. Gloria is pretty and I could see she was on edge. Turns out she'd heard The Dream House was a sanctuary and she was looking for asylum from The Court of Fallen Stars. She's the last one standing out of her motley. There was an Elemental who went missing a while back and then a pair of Darklings who were looking into it who vanished recently and an Ogre who went to the court to demand their release who called her and told her to run for her life. She kept trying to call them to no avail. I have no illusions on that front but I tried not to crash her hopes too hard. And hell, I could be wrong. Maybe they haven't taken a trip over the river and through the woods.<br /> <br /> It was also apparent that she had no idea what her Courts were really up to. Seems the story around Hollywood is that Spidertoes is an insane Gentry who runs everything here in the Lady by the Sea. While she was sharing this with us de la Rocha interrupted to helpfully correct her spinal alignment. Gawain was quick to call her down but even if he hadn't I'm pretty she would have stopped short of actually harming the girl despite how hotly her mantle was seething. While she stepped outside to calm down, we explained who Madam Spidertoes really was and that de la Rocha had history with her. Insincere Marguerite joined us and that prompted her to share what she'd been told about the Night Court setting up inside Hollywood and heating up the war with the Day Court and how it was dangerous to be out at night because of it. We pointed out that this was also a fabrication but did not go so far as to tell her why her own monarchs were covering up the disappearances of local Changelings.<br /> <br /> In the end, we offered her the guest room and contacted Joan to secure her an audience with Viscount Augustine since she's Summer court. There was some awkwardness with her and Desiree which seems to be pretty much centered on the fact that they were really close friends before she discovered Desiree was a loyalist and thus she felt deeply betrayed. And as much as I find it hard to trust Desiree, I don't think she's faking her feelings at having her best friend treat her with distrust and suspicion.<br /> <br /> So, with the possibility that Hollywood might send someone after our guest Gawain bowed out of the evening with Becky and I. And since he wasn't joining us we headed out rather than upstairs. Instead of slipping onto my own bike I joined Becky and saddled up against her back while sliding my hands around her in an entirely improper manner before starting to whisper all sorts of wicked promises into her ear. Of course, unlike most, she wasn't completely unable to respond. I do love what that woman can do with her hair...<br /> <br /> Somehow we reached her place without either being pulled over or wrecking. Once we'd stopped and her hands were free she reached for me, but I laughed and danced away. Of course, as I had to wait for her to open the door I could only go so far. She just unhurriedly dismounted and sauntered over to pin me against the wall and kiss me long and hard and deep enough that I wasn't sure we were even going to bother going inside.<br /> <br /> But decency prevailed (eventually) or maybe it was just that the booze was inside and she hadn't forgotten about my promise to trade body shots with her. I decided to bring out the necklace before the drinking. I'd meant to give it to her sooner but... well I was nervous. It's the first glass-work I've made as a gift and all. As soon as she saw it though, my worry faded. She seemed surprised that I'd made it, which is fair since I've kept my practice kinda quiet. But she seemed quite genuinely excited and pleased with it. And that was before I explained that it was a dream vessel. From there the night unfolded pretty much exactly the way porn tells you two women licking alcohol off each others naked skin should.<br /> <br /> The best part of being an oneiromancer is that the fun doesn't have to stop just because the flesh is tired (and sore) and maybe it was the alcohol but last night once she'd drifted off and I was holding her and enjoying how even when she's asleep her hair stirs under my fingers I decided to try a little dream riding. I mean, I've been working with her for months now in her dreams and we have fooled around but just a little but we'd never really experimented with it the way Gawain and I do sometimes. Suffice to say, I make a most frumptious shy Catholic schoolgirl and I am pretty sure that won't be the last time we play dream games.<br /> <br /> So, needless to say, I was in a right fine mood for sex breakfast and Handsome was on point with the crepes. Since he had to man the stove I snuggled up with Becky while the usual conversation and laughter flowed around. I did break to speak to Julia quietly when she got up. She assured me that we were fine but she just wasn't quite done processing what happened yet. I think I managed to hit the right balance of still caring without crowding her. So, yeah, all's well there.<br /> <br /> I mentioned that I was doing a number tonight and Becky said she'd try to make it out before she left. Sadly, even if she does I'm not going to be able to enjoy her company afterward tonight. And on that note, I called the Lighthouse to confirm that Gawain and I will be doing the dream healing but apparently Queen Charlotte's in a meeting with Salk and is going to have to get back to me. DLR is giving Gloria a tour of the place while she's waiting for Joan to pick her up. Despite the rocky introduction they're getting on rather well. Desiree is in the stage area waiting for me by now. We're going to go over the numbers for tonight and make sure she's ready. Looks like it's going to be a nice quiet afternoon.<br /> <br /> <br /> Julia is singing.<br /> It's not for me. I shouldn't be listening.<br /> But I can't help it.<br /> It's beautiful.<br /> Just like Insincere Marguerite's blood.<br /> <br /> I didn't want it to happen the way it did.<br /> I didn't want to hurt her.<br /> I am so tired of hurting people I love.<br /> I thought I was better.<br /> I've been working so hard but it doesn't matter.<br /> I did the right thing.<br /> Jacob and Gawain and Lori said so.<br /> I wasn't bad.<br /> I wasn't wrong.<br /> Not this time.<br /> But it didn't make a difference.<br /> <br /> I couldn't trust her to be in that room.<br /> I don't know if it's magic or not.<br /> But I saw it.<br /> She loves Chalcedony.<br /> And love makes people stupid.<br /> It makes them unreliable.<br /> I didn't want to take her away.<br /> I didn't want to betray her like that.<br /> I love her.<br /> But I couldn't trust her.<br /> If she had tried to stop us<br /> If she'd tried to help Chalcedony escape<br /> I had to protect her.<br /> I had to protect the motley.<br /> I had to protect Chalcedony.<br /> <br /> I was right.<br /> It doesn't matter.<br /> <br /> She hates me now.<br /> <br /> Choices have consequences.<br /> I choose to take her away rather than risk her trying to stop us.<br /> Now I have to live with that.<br /> Now I know what her blood tastes like.<br /> <br /> Jacob is here.<br /> He's watching me.<br /> He's worried.<br /> They're all worried.<br /> Gawain wouldn't let me go with him.<br /> I can't blame them.<br /> I broke down.<br /> I was weak.<br /> Again.<br /> <br /> I was never this weak before.<br /> I never cried in Show Globe.<br /> Not like this.<br /> The Whispering Voices broke me<br /> tore me<br /> beat me<br /> tortured me<br /> But They never hurt me like this.<br /> They could not touch me inside.<br /> <br /> I am tired of hurting.<br /> <br /> This pain is the cost of being better<br /> I am tired of being better.<br /> <br /> I am tired of working so hard to be something I'm not.<br /> I was made to hurt people.<br /> <br /> I am not a good girl.<br /> I am Calamity.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> So, the plans for the Roman a clef have been put to the side for now. Had some interesting stuff happen today during the show. I\u2019m not sure about the exact sequence of events. At some point a newcomer to Malibu walked in and Desiree recognized her from Hollywood. Apparently they used to be good friends. So, Desiree walks over to the table that Gloria was at with Gawain in tow and they all start talking. Eventually they moved the conversation over to the bar and I found out what was going on.<br /> <br /> Apparently Gloria, a polychromatic Fairest, just arrived in Malibu, having fled from Hollywood. Over the past month or so her motley mates have gone missing. The first was about a month ago, then two more. The last was within the last day or two. He had gone to confront the Court about releasing their motely mates and he didn\u2019t come back. The only thing that Gloria got was a text several hours later from Jimmy to get out of Hollywood. He didn\u2019t tell her where to go, she just picked here because she heard it was a safe place. And by here I mean the Dream House. I guess our reputation precedes us. So, she came to us to find sanctuary. Later Gawain said that he\u2019d \u201cread\u201d her motivation and it seemed to be genuine. She wanted to get out of Hollywood to be safe. Her second motivation was to inform us about a known loyalist, Desiree, and get in good with the courts that way. Things didn\u2019t exactly work out the way she\u2019d planned since Desiree was the one to greet her. She rolled with it though. She asked if she could stay with us for the night and talk to the Summer monarch in the morning. We agreed. It didn\u2019t feel right just chucking her out on the street, and presumably she\u2019ll just be here the one night. Gawain texted Joan and arranged for the meeting with Augustine for tomorrow. So, that\u2019s all set.<br /> <br /> Oh\u2026before that whole conversation happened something else transpired. I guess Gloria said something to Desiree about Madam Spidertoes that was less than complimentary and De la Rocha, who was nearby, got upset. And by upset, I mean that De la Rocha grabbed Gloria by the shirt and threw her against a wall. Gloria had only repeated what she\u2019d been told about the older Darkling, which was that she is almost Gentry-like and rules everything in our freehold with an iron fist. Well, she does wield some power, in that any matters involving Darklings go to her first, but she does not have the kind of power that Hollywood seems to think that she does. Once the altercation was over De la Rocha removed herself from the club temporarily to cool down. I think Lori went outside to see if her paramour was okay.<br /> <br /> The rest of the rumor mill in Hollywood is saying that there are more and more Night Courtiers moving into the area and tensions are rising between them and the Day court. This has supposedly made things more dangerous, especially at night. Knowing something about what is actually going on in Hollywood makes this sound like a cover to explain the increase in missing Changelings. Those that are being fed to the Grandmaw. Well, Gloria didn\u2019t know anything about the Grandmaw and we didn\u2019t enlighten her. It was a near thing with Gawain, but he caught himself before he actually said anything that he couldn\u2019t take back.<br /> <br /> At some point Flores even coaxed Julia downstairs to meet our new guest from Hollywood. Meanwhile Gloria tried a couple of times while we were talking to call her motley mates. I suggested that if it was believed that an unfriendly party had a hold of her friends then she shouldn\u2019t keep calling with her own cell phone. They may be able to trace it back to here, or at least her. She admitted that this was probably a good idea and stopped trying to call her friends. I\u2019ll admit that I would have a hard time not calling my friends if they suddenly went missing. I am also enough of a pragmatist to know when to stop so those involved don\u2019t find me. I am proficient at tracking people through the woods or the Hedge, and now I\u2019m learning how to track people using computers. All skills that will come in handy, I\u2019m sure.<br /> <br /> After the show everyone split up. Gawain escorted Gloria and Desiree up to the guest room on the second floor. The one that is just down the hall from mine. Desiree then split off to go with Insincere Marguerite and the other ladies. Calamity went off with Becky. Sandoval stayed and went off with Lori and De la Rocha. I decided that I was going to stay up tonight to keep an eye on things just in case someone from the Hollywood Court found Gloria and decided to pay a visit. Gawain had the same idea. He came back downstairs after showing our guest to her room and vented to me about everything that was going on. He told me that Desiree and Gloria had continued talking as he walked them upstairs and that he felt ill prepared to help. He told me that Gloria and Desiree had been very close friends before it was discovered that Desiree was a Loyalist and had been keeping a file on Gloria. Gloria felt betrayed and I don\u2019t blame her. Apparently her whole motley had also been upset on her behalf. I don\u2019t think that Desiree ever gave the files to her Keeper, but it\u2019s the idea that she had created it in the first place that really bothered the Fairest. Gawain wasn\u2019t sure if what he said to try and help actually did, or if it made things worse. He wasn\u2019t sure what he should have said, and neither was I. So, we talked for a while about that. I tried to be reassuring. That he\u2019d done his best and that\u2019s all anyone can really do when it comes down to it.<br /> <br /> The whole conversation made me think of my own activities as a Loyalist. I kept files too, but I kept them all in my head. It was too risky to have anything written down where it might accidentally be found by someone, so I memorized details about people and places and reported what I remembered to the Lady. It was a system that worked pretty well. Rook kept actual notes, but he wrote them in his own code so they could not be easily read by outsiders. I figured out his code, but then we were partners for quite a while. For all intents and purposes his notebook looked like it just had poetry in it, so even if it was found it wouldn\u2019t be all that interesting to anyone else. My notes of course could not be touched. Not everyone has an eidetic memory though, so I had an advantage over my compatriots.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> At breakfast this morning we had several guests besides Gloria. We had Flores, Becky, Desiree, and Sandoval besides our usual contingent. I\u2019m not sure who Flores stayed with. Probably Insincere Marguerite and Julia. Maybe. Not sure. Don\u2019t really want to know. Anyway\u2026Gawain made his famous crepes and I made coffee for everyone to their tastes. I even \u201cIrished\u201d up a cup of coffee for Gloria, who was a bit nervous with the idea of \u201csex breakfast.\u201d Joan also contacted Gawain to let him know that the meeting between Gloria and Augustine would take place at 2pm, and that she\u2019d be coming by to pick her up. Then after we all had eaten Sandoval offered to give Flores a ride home, which she accepted. Then De la Rocha, who seemed to have gotten over her anger towards our guest, offered to give Gloria a tour of the Dream House. Gloria seemed a bit flustered but accepted the offer regardless. I got the impression that Desiree was not as sanguine about the whole thing.<br /> <br /> So, after De la Rocha came back from the tour carrying Gloria she and Lori approached me with a favor. Apparently Lori was supposed to act as a chaperone tonight for Insincere Marguerite and Felicity, but had accepted an invitation for a night out with someone already. She felt really strongly about someone else being there in case anything should happen and since most everyone else had plans already she asked me. I was not a fan of Insincere Marguerite going out with Felicity in the first place, which is why Lori said that she asked me in particular. I couldn\u2019t think of a reason to say no so I agreed to be a chaperone. Just as that conversation was wrapping up there was a knock on the door and Gawain came to answer it. Lori and I were talking in the foyer so we were right there when Joan came in to pick up Gloria. Joan greeted us all, but when she was talking to Lori she was particularly flustered. After that it wasn\u2019t hard to figure out who Lori\u2019s date was with tonight. I think Gawain picked up on the hints too. He kept his silence, as did I. Joan was embarrassed enough about the whole thing, and I didn\u2019t see any reason to make things more awkward. So, Joan picked up Gloria and they went to go talk to Viscount Augustine.<br /> <br /> And that\u2019s when things just took a downward spiral. Insincere Marguerite got a call from Chalcedony. Apparently someone broke into the blue girl\u2019s apartment and Chalcedony believed that they were still in the place. Marguerite asked if Calamity would go with her to the other girl\u2019s apartment so they could ascertain what was going on. So, Calamity and Insincere Marguerite left for Chalcedony\u2019s place through a mirror. Calamity texted after a little while to say that Chalcedony had gotten home to find Molly Nuit in her apartment, but that she\u2019d only seen the other woman for a very short time before she turned invisible. She also said that they were going to bring Chalcedony back through to the Dream House just in case Molly was still there. Now, figuring that if Molly was there, she had a good reason, I called Lowjack and talked to him. I confirmed with him that Molly has been keeping an eye on Chalcedony lately because her behavior has been changing so much over the past 24 hours. She has been making phone calls to several people but not leaving any messages among other things. He had not heard back from Molly nor could he get in contact with her at the moment. He figured if she was hidden then she\u2019d be unable to reply back.<br /> <br /> Before our guests came back through the mirror I explained to Gawain what was going on with Molly and why she was there. Then after the three ladies came back Calamity stalked off, angry. I followed her and explained to her as well what was going on. I think she\u2019d been upset that someone was spying on Chalcedony, but was understanding when I explained why. She was also upset by the fact that Chalcedony asked Insincere Marguerite to stay with her for the night and Marguerite dropped her date with Felicity like a hot potato. She wouldn\u2019t cancel the date because any of us thought that it was a bad idea, and potentially dangerous for Marguerite, but she will drop it for a pretty blue girl.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile Insincere Marguerite and Lori escorted Chalcedony down to the basement guest room to stay while things are worked out. Apparently Chalcedony then started turning the charm all the way up and tried to seduce Lori only to fail, and successfully seduced Insincere Marguerite. They just started going at it in front of Lori who was standing back watching things unfold. While all that was going on I got a phone call from Lowjack. According to him Molly called John as soon as she was able. Turns out Chalcedony never saw her, and that she\u2019d never been visible. Chalcedony just walked into her apartment, stopped and made the phone call to Insincere Maguerite. She was playing us from the get go. I suppose it shouldn\u2019t be surprising, something has been off about that girl for a while now, and it\u2019s only getting worse. I hung up with Lowjack and tried to call Charlotte since she was in charge of when things go down with regards to Chalcedony. She was busy so I waited. Gawain then told me what the plan was. He had already been in contact with the monarch and it was decided that we would subdue Chalcedony and Oleander and Shi would come over and pick her up to bring her back to the Lighthouse. The plan was to then have Gawain head over and work on removing the scripts.<br /> <br /> Our plan was to get Marguerite\u2019s \u201csleeping cloth\u201d and knock out Chalcedony. I helped Gawain figure out the dosage and then we enlisted Calamity\u2019s help to get Insincere Marguerite out of the room while Gawain subdued Chalcedony. We agreed that Marguerite was not acting like herself entirely and that she might try and stop us from doing what we had to do. So, Calamity escorted her fellow darkling out of the room and Gawain closed the door and grabbed a hold of Chalcedony and used the cloth on her. He laid her on the bed and we called the Lighthouse to let them know that we had knocked out our blue dancer. Shi and Oleander headed to the Dream House right away. While arrangement were being made by Gawain I got to hear an earful of Insincere Marguerite yelling at Calamity for what her darkling sister did. Marguerite for her part was very upset that Calamity had made her go against her word when she said that she would stay with Chalcedony. Calamity tried arguing that we thought that Marguerite might be compromised because of her behavior tonight. Dropping her date with Felicity because Chalcedony asked when none of us could persuade her not to go on this date with the Day Courtier. Marguerite replied that she dropped her date because a friend asked for help. And maybe that\u2019s true, but her behavior still seemed off to me.<br /> <br /> During this whole thing Marguerite got so upset that she slapped Calamity in the face. That ended just about like you\u2019d expect it to. Insincere Marguerite got cut and Calamity got hurt. It wasn\u2019t so much the slap that hurt Calamity, it was the attack in general that hurt her. I could see Calamity\u2019s face fall as the blow landed and from when Marguerite had yelled. I tried telling Marguerite that we had only done what we thought we had to, but it didn\u2019t seem to carry much weight. She dismissed me as easily as she dismissed the rest of us. During this whole thing Insincere Marguerite stalked off, still angry. Lori followed her, presumably to try and help calm her down. Meanwhile I talked to Calamity and tried to reassure her that what we had done was the right choice. That we had acted in the best interest of all those involved. I don\u2019t know if she believed me or not. She seemed to just kind of shut down and collapse in on herself. She sat down after Marguerite left and didn\u2019t really acknowledge the rest of us. I tried to be as reassuring as I could, but I don\u2019t know how much of it actually made it through to her or not.<br /> <br /> After about fifteen or twenty minutes Oleander and Shi arrived to collect Chalcedony. I directed them down to the basement room where Oleander used some sort of plant mixture and injected it into Chalcedony. The blue loving woman then kind of sleep walked and followed the directions given to her and walked upstairs and to the car. They let her sit down in the backseat and fall over, still asleep. They said that they would only have to use that mixture one more time to direct her to the Lighthouse and then she would be secured.<br /> <br /> Just a couple minutes ago Calamity and I moved upstairs so we could sit down and be more comfortable. As we sat down we both heard a haunting kind of song coming from upstairs. It sounded like Julia was using that voice of hers to calm down Insincere Marguerite. It worked on calming the rest of us too. Calamity is calm at the moment but does not really look any happier. She is writing away in her own journal. Hopefully she is exorcising some of the demons that are bothering her right now. As it is she was in no condition to help Gawain, so he left by himself to go and do the dream-crafting with Chalcedony. He likely won\u2019t be able to remove all of the scripts today without help, but hopefully he will be able to make a dent. Perhaps if Calamity comes back to herself before too much time passes she can go help her paramour with his task, but I\u2019m not sure she will be ready in time. I\u2019m not completely certain that she will be ready for the show tonight. Perhaps I can help out. I can greet people at the door and act as bouncer for the evening while Gawain is away. I have assistants that can help out at the bar.<br /> <br /> Practicalities aside, it was more than a little disturbing to see Calamity shut down like that. If anyone else had laid into her like that she would have defended herself, but she didn\u2019t with Marguerite. She tried to explain, but did not really try to defend anything. I can understand Insincere Marguerite\u2019s side, to some extent. She gave her word and then she was forced to break it. It\u2019s not like she did it willingly though. Circumstances didn\u2019t work out the way that they were supposed to and we were forced to move up the timetable with Chalcedony. She was already acting erratic, we didn\u2019t have a choice. We had to act. And I know that Insincere Marguerite denies it, but she has been acting odd when she is with Chalcedony. I did not expect her to drop everything and begin making out with the dancer quite so vigorously when there was someone else in the room. Granted the other person was one of her lovers, but you\u2019d think that Insincere Marguerite would at least wait until she was alone with Chalcedony before going at it like that. Then there is Chalcedony\u2019s actions. She was actively flirting and started to make out with Marguerite, after trying to seduce Lori first. Chalcedony is supposedly straight. She has said that she\u2019s uncomfortable dating women, which is why she dumped Ginny in the first place, and now she tries to seduce two women at the same time. Someone tell me that\u2019s not odd. And now because of that woman two of my friends are seriously upset with one another. If she\u2019s trying to sow dissent she\u2019s succeeding.<br /> <br /> What Insincere Marguerite said cannot be unsaid, not that I think she\u2019d want to at the moment, but I wish it was possible. Calamity is a mess right now. She\u2019s writing in her journal, but her emotions are written across her face. She does not normally let her mask down, but with this whole situation she has. I don\u2019t think she\u2019s realized that yet though, and so I can see the pain written on my friend\u2019s face. Thanks to Julia\u2019s singing she is calm, but that just means that Calamity is calmly hating herself right now. Things are just so messed up right now, and the day\u2019s not over yet.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> <b><u><b>Lovesong</b></u></b><br /> <br /> \u201cSo, you and Debbie Gibson eh?\u201d<br /> <br /> Maria De La Rocha had been trying to ignore Robert Smith for a while, and not think about what was going on downstairs. She hoped when <i><i>Pornography</i></i>was done she would move into something else, but after a whirr the CD player started \u201cPlainsong\u201d and she realized she had not escaped The Cure just yet. She was trying to place this next song\u2019s title when her girlfriend\u2019s question seemed to come out from nowhere.<br /> <br /> \u201cWho?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou know,\u201d Julia Oldacre grinned slightly. \u201cThe new girl. Cyndi Lauper or whatever.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh\u2026\u201d The punk could not help but grin a moment. \u201cSo I get pissed cuz she was absolutely slandering Spidertoes, and I literally throw her, and next thing I know she is flirting with me. And this afternoon she was eager for a tour alone. I should throw cute girls more often.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhy was Blondie slandering Spidertoes?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cPastime in Hollywood apparently. She knows better now. Anyway, I carried her around the house a bit.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI find this a little hard to believe.\u201d Julia looked up from her sketch of one of the newer dancers, eyebrow raised. \u201cYou throw her and she decides you are awesome?\u201d<br /> <br /> The Leechfinger flexed her bicep, \u201cWell, I am strong, and stalwart I guess, and willing to put myself out there to defend someone I care about. I am as confused as you are how that happened. Gawain must have bitten me sometime,\u201d she said and grinned. She looked at her phone and a look of concern crossed her face, then she looked back up at Julia.<br /> <br /> \u201cJust be careful,\u201d Julia said without looking up. \u201cI don\u2019t want Tiffany over there to cause trouble. We don\u2019t know who she is really.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGawain vetted her\u201d<br /> <br /> Julia mouth thinned, \u201cGawain also seems to like Desiree and Chalcedony. He is not quite totally reliable when it comes to pretty girls, and our Madonna seems good at getting people wrapped around her finger\u2026\u201d She trailed off as she heard Insincere Marguerite coming up, her steps much heavier than usual.<br /> <br /> Maria had picked up the case to <i><i>Disintegration</i></i><i>,</i> \u201cThis music is coming from 1989 babe. I don\u2019t think you can throw\u2026oh shit\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite stormed into the attic. Her entire demeanor was different. She was angry, but not the usual mock offended at \u201cAmerican barbarity\u201d angry or someone reminded her of the Day Court angry. She had an aura of fury and hurt. Julia was, somehow, on her feet before Maria. Both called out to her.<br /> <br /> \u201cCalamity has\u2026she has\u2026she\u2026grrrrrrrr\u201d the Tunnelgrub physically shook as her much taller lover threw her arms around her neck. \u201cSweetheart\u2026you are\u2026it\u2019s me\u2026please\u2026\u201d Julia\u2019s demeanor shifted fast from calm to affection to near panic. Maria crossed her arms and picked up her phone, replying to Gawain.<br /> <br /> \u201cCalamity lured me out, tricking me into breaking my word to Chalcedony. I do not break my word. It is\u2026\u201d Insincere Marguerite seemed to search for the words, as usual the frustration impaired her English \u201cImportant. Not me to do so.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhy did she do that,\u201d Julia looked bewildered. \u201cCalamity values keeping her word.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u2018She thought Chalcedony was controlling me. That I was her slave. I was worried, yes. Willing to break my appointment with Felicity. But to Calamity, being willing to break my appointment to help a friend who begged from my assistance is apparently suspicious to her when I would not do so just because people felt I was not strong enough to resist Felicity.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell Bon-Bon you have a valid point but we have concerns about\u2026\u201d Julia started.<br /> <br /> De La Rocha looked up. \u201cNot the Time.\u201d Julia nodded and closed her mouth.<br /> <br /> \u201cSorry, I am not good at social stuff\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> The Lurker looked at her girlfriend. \u201cIt\u2026is okay. I am not angry with you. I just\u2026I don\u2019t\u2026I don\u2019t understand why Calamity, who values her word, does not\u2026there is a thing called trust.\u201d<br /> <br /> Julia did not let go, \u201cSo what is she doing to try to deal with it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFeeling sorry for herself and not helping Chalcedony like she said she would, mostly.\u201d Insincere Marguerite shrugged. \u201cIt\u2019s how she deals with breaching trust. She sits around and feels sorry for herself. Or chafes at the repercussions for her actions. You notice she is the only one who does this\u2026breaking trust and then moping about it\u2026and I expect she will just throw herself at my mercy like she did when she murdered Mister Grey or her parents. It\u2019s what she will do next time she hurts or kills someone because she decides she knows what is best for everyone.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s a little unfair\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHow many times has large, powerful Gawain hurt or killed people, or violated trust, then sat down and felt sorry for himself? Lorelei? Jacob?\u201d Insincere Marguerite drummed her fingers. \u201cCause a problem, then sit and weep crocodile tears until everyone forgives or forgets\u2026then do it again.\u201d<br /> <br /> De La Rocha looked at Julia, then down at her phone. The artist carefully spoke, \u201cInsincere Marguerite\u2026Bon-Bon\u2026I won\u2019t make you stop talking, but you are only making yourself angrier. You need to relax. Please. I will always love you. I can get you some weed, if you want. But stop before you say or do something you can\u2019t take back.\u201d<br /> <br /> Her lover looked at her, but only shrugged, tears forming. \u201cI\u2026I do not know what to do or how to deal with this rage.\u201d<br /> <br /> Julia got a far off look in her eyes, and shut off the stereo, ending \u201cLullaby\u201d prematurely. She closed her eyes, holding her beloved, her \u201cBon-Bon.\u201d Tilting her head back, she began to sing a song of the night, in a voice not quite human. Insincere Marguerite\u2019s own eyes fluttered open as she heard the song, and while there was a moment of fear in them, she allowed the Nightsinger\u2019s power to take hold.<br /> <br /> Julia\u2019s lovers felt themselves almost melting into the night. Memories of chasing fireflies, of seeing the dark woods behind a childhood home or vacation spot. The howl of a dog, with its combination of fear and the promise of adventure, the song of crickets and frogs, the dancing lights in the distance, the sound of the ocean in the darkness, the rising of mist across wet grass. A sense of peace fell over the room, tensions meting away, and Maria leaned on her paramour as she and her girlfriend blissfully lost themselves in the song of the night, as it began to spread into the house.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LII</i><br /> <br /> What is there to add?<br /> <br /> Gloria has a kind of 80s look to her, hence Julia\u2019s stream of nicknames.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite and Lorelei did not actually have any magical effect on them, though some thought they did IC. Gawain vouched for Gloria with Contracts of Potential, and of course Insincere Marguerite used Contracts of Reflection to mirror travel. Insincere Marguerite took damage due to Hedgehog's Dilemma (see Calamity's stats a couple posts above).<br /> <br /> Lorelei\u2019s player claims the \u201cAngel of the Morning\u201d choice has nothing to do with Deadpool. I am awash with skepticism.<br /> <br /> The Chalcedony encounter went almost as badly as it could have save Chalcedony dying. The reputation of the Dream House has been compromised. Insincere Marguerite lost Clarity for breaking her word. Thus her rage at Calamity was due in part to Calamity tricking her into losing Clarity. Chalcedony was jumped by Gawain, who she previously trusted, which will make Dream Healing very, very difficult for him since he has gone from a trusted friend to a dire enemy.<br /> <br /> But now two members of the Last Dance seriously consider leaving the Motley. One member is emotionally broken, while a third throws herself into the arms of other lovers. The reputation of the Dream House has been lessened. Surely there is nowhere to go but up? Find out next time. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 03-27-2016, 04:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T12:01:18-07:00","id":855163,"title":"","content":"Seriously, &quot;Angel of the Morning&quot; is one of a number of angel/avian themed songs I've had earmarked for Lori to perform almost since the start of the campaign (other examples include &quot;Wind Beneath My Wings,&quot; &quot;Learning to Fly,&quot; and of course &quot;Freebird&quot;). I had completely forgotten that the song was used as the opening credits theme in the recent <i>Deadpool</i> film until just before I sent the journal entry out to the rest of the players.<br /> <br /> Now, if you'll excuse me, Lori has to go work on her &quot;Careless Whisper&quot; and &quot;Calendar Girl&quot; numbers now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T12:38:50-07:00","id":855187,"title":"","content":"<i>Awash</i>, I tell you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T15:40:12-07:00","id":857319,"title":"","content":"Couldn't it be argued that, rather that the sanctity of the Dream House being tarnished, it was being upheld for fear of what danger Chalcedony was posing to everyone within? She's clearly got some influence over Insincere Margeurite, or attempting to have some over others, and no matter how you look at it her reluctance to remove the scripts in her head shows some danger. The Dream House may be a safe spot, but they have to consider their own safety as well.<br /> <br /> I do appreciate why the characters would feel the reputation is tarnished though, since they have let in an outside force to take away someone who came to them for help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T18:43:26-07:00","id":857385,"title":"","content":"Hello, Taidragon, welcome to the discussion!<br /> <br /> Lorelei's player here. I've actually made that argument both in and out of character. Lorelei absolutely believes that we had no choice but to act as we did regarding Chalcedony. Oh, the specifics of the confrontation could certainly have been handled better... she's not disputing that. But you're right... with the information we had at the time, Chalcedony was a threat that needed to be dealt with, and we did the best we could in an impossible situation.<br /> <br /> Of course, the real problem is with public perception. The Dream House serves a population of beings who have all been abducted and abused on some level, and each of our patrons has - to some degree - a deep-seated fear that this could happen to them again some day. The Dream House has been touted as a safe haven... we're the ones people come to when they need help, because we're not aligned with a specific court or other political entity, and we've made a reputation for ourselves as do-gooders. Hell, Gloria came all the way from Hollywood to seek a safe haven with us for that very reason.<br /> <br /> Now, the Last Dance motley is actively complicit in the subdual and kidnapping of someone who specifically came to us for help. Though the details of this situation can certainly be seen as mitigating circumstances, it's going to be hard for people to get over that simple fact.<br /> <br /> Thanks for reading, and thanks for commenting. I know I speak for all of us when I say that we love knowing that people are following these journals!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T20:11:02-07:00","id":857425,"title":"","content":"Thanks Penitent, glad to be a part of it. :-)<br /> <br /> Indeed, the public perception is the real devil of these details. Even if one could convince the public of why the motley did as they did, that would most likely require throwing poor Chalcedony under the bus, and she's not exactly with a firm standing as is. As noted, Changelings have a deep seated (and somewhat deserved) paranoia within their ranks, and what with Desire coming out as a Loyalist, Chalcedony would probably be given the same suspicion even if she was entirely innocent in that regard. The only real circumstances that I could see fixing that damage to any real extent would be if these actions ended up publically revealing/repelling a danger to the freehold...which would, again, throw Chalcedony under a negative light.<br /> <br /> I've been following for a bit now, since I caught the Changeling bug from 2e's playtest chunks coming out and I caught up with the Baroness' Geist game. It's a bit ironic in that regard since Changeling was the first WoD game that I was introduced to, but before I could even make a character our GM had a change of interest from Fairy Tales to Ghost Stories, so we went to Geist instead. Now I've read Geist and gone to Changeling. :-p<br /> <br /> I've really loved how everyone covers the events of the games thus far, from the differences of memory to covering events others weren't aware of, to the differences of opinions within. Even the mistakes certain journals have towards specific events is interesting to me, as it suggests the characters themselves are mistaken in their recollections. The short stories are really cool too, helping give some voice to characters who aren't given as much of a voice due to being repeated through another characters' writings. It's all fascinating stuff. The tone of the game and the character from the journals actually helped me create a couple of prospective Changelings of mine in the 2e mold, a Beast and a Fairest. It's inspired me to try and make an in-character journal in an upcoming game. Here's hoping it goes well.<br /> <br /> Of course, now that I'm all caught up I can't wait to see more. Keep up the great work everyone. :-)<br /> <br /> Edit: Whoop, an Elemental got thrown in there too when I started thinking over the Fairest. Princess Jolie was her inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 04-02-2016, 01:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T00:54:34-07:00","id":857562,"title":"","content":"Taidragon: You raise some excellent points. The reputation of the Last Dance Motley is tarnished, but far from destroyed. The big thing weakening the \u201cbut she is a Loyalist\u201d argument is the group is currently sheltering an admitted Loyalist, Desiree. Of course, Desiree is not (currently) a threat to the freehold, so there is that. It is a dagger the groups enemies or those looking to cause unrest (like, say, the Phantom Tong) can use, but it is a damaging or tarnishing of that reputation, not breaking it.<br /> <br /> Geist and Changeling are definitely my two favorite games. If you ever decide to combine them, Golden Eagle has 3 Changelings and a Sin-Eater for 4/7 of the group (one Changeling, a Wizened, gives regular journals and another, a Darkling, does now and again).<br /> <br /> I am quite flattered you would work on a character based on NPCs in the game. Thanks for sharing that. ^_^<br /> <br /> Next session is major drama. I have read several journals and it was some very intense roleplaying. I\u2019ll have it out in a bit over a week.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T00:56:45-07:00","id":857564,"title":"","content":"Glad to have you following our adventures Taidragon. Calamity's player here.<br /> <br /> As far as the Dream House's reputation goes, Calamity will point out to people that we did subdue Chalcedony without harming her and the monarchs were looking at removing her scripts by force or killing her. She does feel that it happening at the Dream House was unfortunate, but that we did our best to protect her from the Director's programming and from less gentle methods Also, part of her goal was to have Gawain involved in the healing to try to prevent any malfeasance like Hollywood did with Desiree.<br /> <br /> So yeah, all intentions were good but the situation went pear shaped and mistakes were made in trying to handle it. Of course, Calamity is presently being very hard on herself because that is what the Calamity does. But she'll defend the Dream House (or at least take all the blame if she can) should anyone speak ill within her earshot. Of course, being that she is known for murdering Mr Grey and being the Monarch's hatchetwoman, they may not say anything to her directly and give her the chance to offer her side of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T17:06:13-07:00","id":858015,"title":"","content":"The Last Dance motley is certainly giving the Middle Shadows a run for their intraparty emotional conflict money recently. I'm more concerned with Calamity's relapse into &quot;I'm a monster&quot; territory combined with Gawain slipping into Lord Bertilack mode than the reputation personally. <br /> <br /> With more 2ed materials out, are you thinking about updating more? It's be interesting to see if anyone would change Seemings. Personally, I think that Calamity and Ace would probably stay the same, while Gawain could become a Fairest, Jacob could be a Darkling, and Lori could also potentially become a Darkling. Insincere Marguerite I'm not sure about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T17:22:38-07:00","id":858020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>andreamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play?p=858015#post858015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Last Dance motley is certainly giving the Middle Shadows a run for their intraparty emotional conflict money recently. I'm more concerned with Calamity's relapse into &quot;I'm a monster&quot; territory combined with Gawain slipping into Lord Bertilack mode than the reputation personally.<br /> <br /> With more 2ed materials out, are you thinking about updating more? It's be interesting to see if anyone would change Seemings. Personally, I think that Calamity and Ace would probably stay the same, while Gawain could become a Fairest, Jacob could be a Darkling, and Lori could also potentially become a Darkling. Insincere Marguerite I'm not sure about.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the primary issue with that is consistency. For example, if only the kiths were updated, suddenly everyone's a lot more capable than they were before (seriously, 1e kiths are nothing compared to 2e). Why would the characters suddenly become more capable with their powers? Likewise, Seemings are near completely different in how the blessings and curses work - 2e Fairest don't get the same glamor to presence dice bonus, as an example, and unlike kiths they aren't close to finalized.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T20:24:22-07:00","id":858104,"title":"","content":"Yea as I say This is a drama filled time. Middle Shadows is (maybe) calming back down a bit, The Last Dance will take longer to deal.<br /> <br /> I am happy to cannibalize any elements of 2e I like into my game, but Changeling is unlikely to change very much. I may incorporate 2e Kiths (since they are cooler/more updated versions) but probably not Seemings (though I could, I guess, keep the Clarity loss/gains if I use the new Clarity rules) I am nonetheless keeping the old Seemings. I am absolutely not adding huntsman. For this game I am almost certainly keeping old Contracts. Next game I run I might let people see if they like old or new better. As in all things, I keep what I like between the editions. I won't be running pure first or second (though my Vampire and Werewolf characters in GE are almost pure 2e).<br /> <br /> No one is gaining or losing Kiths, outside of joining the pilgrims or hitting Wyrd 9, or changing Seemings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T20:05:48-07:00","id":858702,"title":"","content":"Kind of like when the Barbarian named Mirth starts laughing, it always presses my &quot;We Need to Run NOW&quot; button when Gawain goes into Bertilac mode.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T16:30:39-07:00","id":862261,"title":"","content":"When Calamity's clarity was at it's low ebb, the idea of her personality fragmenting was discussed. This lead to the realization that there would be Gawain and Katt, the most adorable couple ever, and Lord Bertilac and his Lady Calamity which would be terrifying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T21:20:36-07:00","id":862406,"title":"","content":"The bond of trust within the Last Dance Motley has cracked. Can it be repaired? Many members try to escape the tension within the motley with their own pursuits, but some try to mend the wounds before they cannot be healed.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> November 8th, afternoon<br /> <br /> The sanctity of my home is broken. My motley is in shambles, with one member too uncomfortable around another to leave her room. The only so-called gain of last night was that a Changeling, a friend, lies in chains, her mind still not her own but now seething with hatred towards me. And it is all because the Monarchs are too afraid of losing some sliver of their power to see to the safety of their charges.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s not really fair, I guess, and sounds like Lord Bertilak besides. I... I can\u2019t let myself do that right now - Calamity needs me to be me, to be her Gawain, not her liege lord. Still, if the thing that was so distracting to Charlotte yesterday was this business of the Day and Night Courts getting crowns...<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know that it was, and I don\u2019t know what was said over the phone yesterday afternoon. We certainly seemed to have few options, and less time. All that I do know is that mistakes were made, and plenty to go around. I <u><u>think</u></u> we managed to not compound them last night. And now... now we need to find a way to repair what we can.<br /> <br /> As much as we can.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Okay, so with a few shining bright spots as exceptions, the last two days have turned my life to absolute shit. And the real hell of it is that I know that some other members of my motley \u2013 <u><u>most</u></u> of them, in fact \u2013 are suffering far worse than I am, and there seems to be fuck-all that I can do about it. It\u2019s hard to believe that just two days ago I was shouting out at the top of my lungs that this was the \u201cbest week ever.\u201d<br /> <br /> So I had just finished showering and was about to get started on my makeup when the doorbell rang. Figuring everyone else was either busy or elsewhere, I ran downstairs and answered the door. It was Joan and Gloria, who seemed pleased with how her meeting with Viscount Augustine went. She\u2019s going to continue staying with us at the Dream House for a couple of days while she finds her feet, and then try to find more permanent accommodations.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhile I would be pleased to introduce you to the other denizens of the Freehold,\u201d Joan was saying formally as I arrived on the scene, \u201cit may be truly said that there are many others more suited to this task than I. Lorelei and her motley, for example, or Monica.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cWe\u2019d be happy to show you around once things settle down a little,\u201d I said, \u201cbut Monica is a real sweetheart, and she knows everybody in the area. I\u2019ll introduce you to her soon\u2026 or maybe I\u2019ll let D handle that; those two are really close friends.\u201d Gloria blushed at that, but did a pretty good job of hiding it, so I let it pass.<br /> <br /> Joan, on the other hand, looked concerned. \u201cIs everything all right, Lorelei?\u201d she asked seriously.<br /> <br /> I shook my head. \u201cNo,\u201d I answered her quietly, \u201cit\u2019s really not.\u201d<br /> <br /> Joan turned to look at Gloria. \u201cI apologize, but could you give us a moment, please?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s okay,\u201d Gloria said, \u201cI\u2019ll just go see if anyone\u2019s in the kitchen.\u201d<br /> <br /> Joan took my hand. \u201cWhat is wrong, Lorelei?\u201d she asked, her eyes full of concern.<br /> <br /> I sighed. \u201cChalcedony came by here today. I don\u2019t know how much you know about that situation, but\u2026 things didn\u2019t go smoothly. Calamity and Insincere Marguerite had an argument about how to handle it, and they\u2019re pretty mad at each other right now.\u201d I turned away. \u201cI hate it when my friends fight.\u201d<br /> <br /> She squeezed my hand. \u201cIf you are needed here\u2026 Andromeda and I will understand,\u201d she said kindly.<br /> <br /> I turned back to look at her. \u201cNo,\u201d I said quietly, \u201cthey\u2019ll work it out. I\u2019ll do what I can to help them, of course, but eventually it\u2019s going to have to come down to the two of them, and I don\u2019t think either one of them is ready for that just yet. Unless you hear differently from me, I\u2019ll see you both at seven, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> Joan smiled then, and it was radiant. \u201cWe look forward to it. Best of luck in your efforts, my friend. My fianc\u00e9 and I shall see you tonight.\u201d She turned to go.<br /> <br /> I put out an arm to stop her, my eyes wide. \u201cWhoa, wait a minute. What was that word you just used?\u201d<br /> <br /> She just smiled, but said no more.<br /> <br /> After she made her exit, I joined Gloria in the kitchen, and the two of us went upstairs in search of D. We found her at the base of the retractable attic stairs, looking grim.<br /> <br /> \u201cMarguerite is with Julia?\u201d I asked softly as we approached.<br /> <br /> She nodded, and leaned in close. \u201cShe\u2019s making it worse,\u201d she whispered tensely.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll talk to them,\u201d I said, giving her a quick hug.<br /> <br /> \u201cBe careful,\u201d D admonished, \u201cI\u2019ve never seen Julia this angry. She\u2019s got her crazy going full blast.\u201d<br /> <br /> It was dark in the attic, but I could see Julia and Marguerite sort of huddled together a short distance away. \u201cHello,\u201d I said softly as I approached.<br /> <br /> Julia looked up. \u201cHello, Lori,\u201d she said carefully. Marguerite didn\u2019t say anything at all.<br /> <br /> \u201cHow is she?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cHow do you think?\u201d Julia spat.<br /> <br /> I sighed. \u201cLook, Julia, I\u2019m trying to help here. I don\u2019t want to take sides between the two of them\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSounds like you\u2019ve already taken a side,\u201d Julia snapped. \u201cSounds to me like everyone has.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s not fair,\u201d I gently rebuked her. \u201cYou know I love her. I\u2019ve proven that to you hundreds of times. I\u2019m upset about what happened too. So are the others. I\u2019m just trying to find a way to get past this with our motley and our friendships intact.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat ship has sailed, Lori!\u201d Julia was livid, and her eyes held a manic gleam I wasn\u2019t used to seeing there. \u201cCalamity <u><u>hurt</u></u> Insincere Marguerite. She hurt her <u><u>badly</u></u>. When she forced Insincere Marguerite to break her word, Bon-Bon lost Clarity. And Calamity is going to get away with it, because Calamity <u><u>always</u></u> gets away with it.\u201d<br /> <br /> I gasped as I took that in. I\u2019ve heard some of the older and more experienced changelings talk about Clarity-With-A-Capital-C before. It\u2019s a sort of unofficial gauge of how connected we are to reality. The more Clarity you have, the better you are at interacting with mortals and the mundane world. Lower Clarity allows greater connection to the Wyrd, but you risk losing yourself and becoming a creature of the Hedge and Arcadia. Lose too much Clarity, and you risk becoming a monster.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh my God,\u201d I whispered, my eyes widening. I leaned in to hug Julia; she was stiff but she allowed it, and even returned the embrace after a moment. \u201cI\u2019m so sorry, Julia, I had no idea.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019s been <u><u>hurt</u></u>,\u201d Julia said simply in my ear. \u201cSomething has to be <u><u>done</u></u>.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSomething will be,\u201d I assured her. \u201cI don\u2019t think the others know how serious this is, Julia. I don\u2019t think any of us knew how badly Insincere Marguerite had been hurt by this. We\u2019ll figure something out. Calamity will have to pay for what she\u2019s done, don\u2019t worry about that. But please promise me one thing, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat?\u201d Julia asked, leaning away with a guarded expression.<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t make any snap decisions tonight. Don\u2019t do anything you can\u2019t take back.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhy not?\u201d she asked. \u201cWhy should we wait to exact our\u2026 justice?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBecause you\u2019re angry right now,\u201d I explained. \u201cDon\u2019t get me wrong\u2026 you have every right to be angry. I\u2019m angry too, and so is D. But we shouldn\u2019t make such a major decision based purely on that anger. What if we act rashly, and then have to live with the regret for the rest of our lives?\u201d<br /> <br /> Julia chewed on that for a minute, but I could tell she wasn\u2019t happy. \u201cOkay,\u201d she said after a few moments. \u201cI promise I won\u2019t say or do anything about Calamity tonight, Lori. I can\u2019t leave her alone like this anyway.\u201d<br /> <br /> I turned to regard Insincere Marguerite, who was curled up into a tight little ball, staring at nothing and making no sound. I walked over to her. \u201cInsincere Marguerite?\u201d I asked hesitantly. She didn\u2019t respond.<br /> <br /> I leaned in and kissed the top of her head. \u201cI love you, Insincere Marguerite,\u201d I said softly, \u201cand I\u2019ll do whatever I can to help you get through this. Just let me know how to help.\u201d<br /> <br /> She looked up at me with such pain and loss in her eyes that I almost couldn\u2019t bear it, and she nodded. It wasn\u2019t much, but it was the most she\u2019d responded to anything since I entered the attic. I made my exit.<br /> <br /> D waited anxiously at the foot of the stairs. \u201cWhat\u2019s up?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cI think I talked Julia down for now,\u201d I informed her, \u201cbut she\u2019s unpredictable. Help me keep an eye on her\u2026 on both of them, please.\u201d<br /> <br /> D nodded. \u201cYou still going out tonight, then?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> I shook my head. \u201cI won\u2019t deny that I\u2019d like to get away from this mess for a little while, but I\u2019m not going out if you need me to stay,\u201d I answered.<br /> <br /> D thought about it. \u201cGo on,\u201d she said with a cocky grin, \u201cI\u2019ll look after things here. I\u2019ll call you if we really need you for anything, I promise. Besides, Joan would never forgive me if I screwed this up for her.\u201d<br /> <br /> I embraced her. \u201cOkay, if you\u2019re sure,\u201d I said.<br /> <br /> Gloria stood to one side of us looking uncomfortable. \u201cI\u2026 I\u2019m not sure what\u2019s going on, but\u2026 you\u2019ve all been so kind to me\u2026 is there anything I can do to help?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s sweet of you to offer,\u201d I said, \u201cbut I think the motley just has to work through this on our own.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cI\u2019ll stay with de la Rocha,\u201d she said after a minute, \u201cand lend a hand where I can.\u201d<br /> <br /> I grinned at her. \u201cYou two have fun,\u201d I said with a wink.<br /> <br /> She colored. \u201cThat\u2019s\u2026 not what I meant,\u201d she stammered out.<br /> <br /> I chuckled. \u201cIt\u2019s okay, Gloria,\u201d I said, \u201cnobody\u2019s going to rope you into anything you don\u2019t want to do. But don\u2019t rule anything out, okay? You don\u2019t know what you might be missing.\u201d I glanced fondly at my honey and made my way downstairs to look for Calamity.<br /> <br /> Before I found her, I was struck by an idea. I ducked into an unused room and looked up Becky\u2019s number on my phone. She seemed surprised to hear from me, and asked if everything was okay.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, not really,\u201d I said simply. \u201cI don\u2019t know how much you know about the situation with Chalcedony, but she came over here this morning, and we were forced to step up the timetable. We had to subdue her and hand her over to the Autumn Court. There was a difference of opinion about this in the motley, and Calamity and Marguerite had a bit of a falling out. Calamity\u2019s taking it hard. I think\u2026 if you\u2019re free tonight, Becky, I think she could really use a friend.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI was going to come to the show tonight anyway,\u201d Becky said, \u201cI\u2019ll be happy to do whatever I can to help.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks, Becky,\u201d I said. \u201cHonestly, I think Calamity and Marguerite need a little time apart. If you want to take her out somewhere, that might be for the best. It\u2019ll give Marguerite a little time to cool off and start thinking more clearly.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay,\u201d she replied. \u201cThanks for letting me know, Lori. I\u2019ll do what I can for her.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know you will. Thanks for being such a good friend.\u201d <br /> <br /> We disconnected, and I went in search of Calamity. I found her a few minutes later, looking falsely chipper and going about her usual pre-show routines. \u201cWhat are you doing?\u201d I asked, frankly flabbergasted.<br /> <br /> \u201cI have two numbers tonight,\u201d she replied in an awful bright voice. \u201cCan\u2019t let the crowds down, right? The show must go on. And with our star singer out for the evening, we can\u2019t make too many more substitutions\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cRidiculous,\u201d I said impatiently. \u201cYou\u2019re in no state, Calamity.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m fine,\u201d she said in that Everything-Is-Okay-So-What-Are-You-Worrying-About voice. I\u2019ll admit it, she\u2019s pretty good at hiding her emotions. If I hadn\u2019t known what she was going through, I might have bought her act.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re not,\u201d I retorted. \u201cBridget and Giselle will take your numbers tonight; their acts have been ready for a week at least. Becky\u2019s on her way over, and the two of you are going out tonight.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI can\u2019t,\u201d Calamity said, and her sunny look turned brittle, \u201cI have to perform.\u201d<br /> <br /> I sighed. \u201cNo you don\u2019t,\u201d I said finally. I carefully put a hand on her shoulder and pulled her closer to me to soften my next words. \u201cTake the night off, Calamity. Go with Becky. Get out of the house for a while. Let everything cool down, and take some time to process what\u2019s going on.\u201d She looked inclined to argue, so I leaned in closer. \u201cI\u2019ll pull rank if I have to. I\u2019m the Creative Director of the Dream House, and I\u2019m telling you that you are <u><u>not</u></u> performing here tonight. We\u2019ll reassess the situation in a few days, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> She sort of sagged in front of me. I don\u2019t think I\u2019ve ever seen her look so defeated. \u201cOkay,\u201d she said. After a moment she put her hand on top of mine and added \u201cthanks, Lori.\u201d<br /> <br /> I squeezed her shoulder. \u201cWe\u2019ll get through this,\u201d I promised her. \u201cSomehow, we\u2019ll get through this. Everyone just needs a little time to put things in perspective.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded, and I went upstairs to get ready for my dinner date. I put on a slinky black dress (low neckline, high hemline, nothing underneath) and a pair of high heel shoes, touched up my makeup, packed up a few necessities in one of my smallest purses, and bid the troubles of the Dream House farewell for the evening.<br /> <br /> Okay, well, in all honesty I made one more stop before I headed to the garage and revved up the \u2018vette. I sat down by the fountain when I was sure that nobody was watching and I called to all the friends I\u2019ve made among the area\u2019s songbird population. A lot of them came fluttering up after a minute or two\u2026 Conrad, Vivian, Binky, Momo, Sassy Miss K. Hell, even Olga and Chicago Joe showed up eventually, though they had a pretty bad attitude throughout the conversation that followed (pigeons, man\u2026 what are you going to do?).<br /> <br /> In any case, I asked the birds to watch over the Dream House for me that night\u2026 particularly the members of the motley. They\u2019re birds, so they didn\u2019t have a really clear idea of what I was asking them at first\u2026 but eventually I managed to get through to them that I wanted to be informed if any violent situations arose. They agreed to help me cheerfully (except for the pigeons, who groused), and fluttered off to station themselves at various windows.<br /> <br /> As I was stretching and standing up, I noticed that I had an audience\u2026 Gawain had returned to the house via our local Hedge gate. I tried to think of a story which might explain what he had just seen, but in the end I opted to ignore it and act as though nothing had happened.<br /> <br /> Gawain had adopted the oddly formal, almost cold persona he gets sometimes when he\u2019s particularly upset. He informed me that he had been turned away at the Lighthouse, on the grounds that Chalcedony no longer trusted him. Apparently if he tried to enter her dreams in the wake of his \u201cattack\u201d on her, it could cause her real lasting trauma, and none of us wanted that, so he reluctantly agreed to withdraw and allow others to attempt to deal with her triggers. I could tell he was very unhappy with the situation, and I tried my best to soothe him, but I don\u2019t know if it helped.<br /> <br /> Half an hour later (damn traffic) I was ringing the bell at Joan and Andromeda\u2019s place. Joan opened the door and favored me with a smile that lit up her whole face. \u201cPlease, come in,\u201d she said simply.<br /> <br /> I walked into the apartment and I think I said something clever like \u201cthank you for having me over, you have a beautiful oh my God what is that wonderful smell?\u201d <br /> <br /> Andromeda leaned out of the kitchen, favored me with a grin, and said \u201cLasagna. I hope you like Italian.\u201d<br /> <br /> I do like Italian. When the Italian is prepared by someone with Andromeda\u2019s skills, I <u><u>love</u></u> Italian. Dinner was fantastic, and the conversation was quite pleasant. I think Joan and I might have run out of things to talk about quickly if Andromeda hadn\u2019t been there, but she kept things light and flirty, and kept the ball rolling whenever we hit one of those awkward pauses. I\u2019m no doctor (sigh\u2026 maybe someday), but I\u2019m ready to pronounce her completely recovered from her ordeal with the Table.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a true testament to her hostess skills that Andromeda kept my mind off of the troubles back at the Dream House for pretty much the entire time that I was there. Oh, I\u2019d occasionally glance at the windows to see if any of my little birds had turned up with news for me, but other than that I felt genuinely comfortable and at peace throughout the meal and the evening that followed.<br /> <br /> We were enjoying a little wine in the sitting room after dinner when Joan turned all shy and nervous again. \u201cSo,\u201d she began softly, \u201cI am embarrassed to admit this, but our VCR is broken.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh,\u201d I said with a mock pout, \u201cand I was so looking forward to that feature film you mentioned.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI am very sorry,\u201d she said with a small smile.<br /> <br /> \u201cI suppose we\u2019ll have to find some other way to amuse ourselves,\u201d I said, \u201cI\u2019m not ready to go home just yet.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou are of course welcome to stay for as long as you like, Lorelei,\u201d Joan said breathlessly.<br /> <br /> \u201cI suppose we could listen to music,\u201d I suggested with a twinkle, \u201cor play a party game.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOr we could have sex,\u201d Andromeda piped up at that point.<br /> <br /> I looked from her to Joan. \u201cI\u2019m up for it if you are,\u201d I said. I hope she could hear the warmth in my voice.<br /> <br /> Joan smiled shyly. \u201cI would like that very much,\u201d she whispered, and the two of them took my hands and led me to the bedroom.<br /> <br /> I did my best to make this evening about their relationship, about how much they mean to each other and how happy I was that they were letting me share in that. I tried to make sure that they were always in each other\u2019s line of sight, and that when I was the center of attention, they were working together to bring me pleasure. I think it worked, and I detected no hint of jealousy or bad feelings from anyone concerned.<br /> <br /> Though I don\u2019t want to let this diary descend into the realms of poor taste, I would be remiss if I didn\u2019t mention Andromeda\u2019s\u2026 \u201ccollection.\u201d We\u2019ve known for some time that she\u2019s an inventor and a tinkerer, and Calamity has let slip once or twice that she has turned those inclinations toward pushing the limits of erotic technology. I was fortunate enough to be able to sample some of her finished products, and\u2026 well\u2026 gosh\u2026 they\u2019re terrific. The best. The absolute bee\u2019s knees. The cat\u2019s unforsaken roar.<br /> <br /> (It is worth mentioning that I must have made quite an impression on Andromeda last night, as I returned home with a large unmarked brown cardboard box containing a few gifts from her collection. I pointed out a few toys that I had particularly enjoyed, but she made the final selections after\u2026 well\u2026 taking a few measurements. I can\u2019t wait to show my new toys to D).<br /> <br /> When we woke up the next morning in a tangle of limbs and blonde hair, none of us particularly wanted to get up. Joan was once more straightening and preening my feathers with a fascinated look on her face. Andromeda didn\u2019t seem to mind, and told the two of us to have fun while she whipped something up for breakfast. \u201cI can scramble a mean egg, but then,\u201d she favored me with a remarkably dirty smirk, \u201cyou already know that.\u201d<br /> <br /> I think Joan might be forming a minor emotional attachment to me, but it\u2019s hard to tell with her. She\u2019s so guileless and earnest that pretty much anything she feels is magnified on her face and in her body language. I don\u2019t think I\u2019m a threat to her relationship with Andromeda, and if that ever changes, I swear I will break things off at once. If, however, I can have another night like that <u><u>without</u></u> endangering the cause of true love, I will jump on that chance like a flea on an Airedale.<br /> <br /> After breakfast I sighed with resignation and said my goodbyes, giving each of my lovely hostesses a lingering kiss on my way out. I didn\u2019t hurry back to the Dream House; I confess that I wasn\u2019t particularly eager to get back into that mess. I parked the \u2018vette and made it all the way upstairs and to my bedroom before I encountered anyone else at all, however.<br /> <br /> D stirred sleepily as I entered. \u201cMorning, Jules,\u201d she said with a smile as she turned to look at me. \u201cHow was your night?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAmazing,\u201d I replied softly, placing my box of new toys on the bureau, \u201cand I brought back souvenirs. I can\u2019t wait to show you some of these\u2026\u201d I trailed off as I saw her expression sag. \u201cWhat is it, D? What\u2019s wrong?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNothing bad happened last night,\u201d she assured me, \u201cbut things haven\u2019t improved with those two, either. Last night, when I finally talked them down from the attic, they started\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cThey were looking at apartments in Portland and the Bay Area,\u201d she said miserably.<br /> <br /> I felt like someone had punched me in the stomach. I turned on my heel and walked out into the hall with D right behind me. Though I knew I had to do it, it took nearly all of my courage to knock on that door.<br /> <br /> Julia opened the door a minute later. She looked tense, but not nearly as tightly wound as she had the previous evening. \u201cHi, girls,\u201d she said as she took in the sight of us. \u201cShe\u2019s doing a little better now. You can come in if you want to.\u201d<br /> <br /> Marguerite greeted us morosely from her perch on the bed, but responded in kind when we offered her hugs and kisses. \u201cFeeling any better, <i>ma cheri</i>?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> She shrugged. \u201cYes and no,\u201d she responded. But hey, at least she was talking. \u201cJulia brought me breakfast earlier, and I feel a bit stronger. But there are still certain things which do not feel right.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCan I talk to you about what\u2019s going on?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> She nodded.<br /> <br /> \u201cD says that the two of you were looking at apartments. That you were thinking of moving away.\u201d I couldn\u2019t bear to say any more. I almost couldn\u2019t get that out.<br /> <br /> Marguerite shrugged. \u201cIt is\u2026 not certain. We shall try to see if we can work something out. But I can no longer trust Calamity. She tricked me. She hurt me. She might do so again, if she feels the cause is worthy. Every time I look at her I will see that, for the rest of my life. I do not know if I can remain in this motley while she is here. It may be necessary for Julia and I to leave this place.\u201d<br /> <br /> I shook my head. \u201cI don\u2019t want you to go,\u201d I said simply. I was crying by that point; I couldn\u2019t help it. I sound like such a stupid kid sometimes. <br /> <br /> Marguerite took my hand. \u201cI do not wish to lose what we have found either,\u201d she said to me. \u201cYou and de la Rocha would of course be welcome to join us\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t want you to go,\u201d I said again, leaning in to her. \u201cI can\u2019t go with you. I\u2019m pledge-bound to the Dream House.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded in understanding. \u201cIt may not come to that. We shall try to work things out, no? But if I cannot be comfortable in this place any longer, then Julia and I may <u><u>have</u></u> to go.\u201d<br /> <br /> And like leviathan rising from a black ocean, an image surfaced in my mind. Mom, stick-thin but smiling, hair falling out, breath coming in ragged gasps, bedsores evident all over her body. I was eight years old, and they were trying to spare me the awful truth. \u201cI might need to go away for a long time, Juliette\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t want to misrepresent the situation. My tears were for Marguerite and Julia, not for my mother. I cried all I could for her long ago. But somewhere deep inside of me, \u201cgoing away\u201d is synonymous with \u201cnot coming back,\u201d and I couldn\u2019t bear the thought of it.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2026 you have to do what\u2019s right for you,\u201d I grudgingly admitted. \u201cI will always love you both, no matter what you decide.\u201d<br /> <br /> I fled the room after that. D found me curled up on our bed a few minutes later, crying like a baby. She put her arms around me and kissed my hair and stroked my wings and whispered that it would be okay until I got myself under control again. Once I could speak coherently, I only wanted to say one thing.<br /> <br /> \u201cPromise you won\u2019t leave me,\u201d I said, looking into her eyes.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat?\u201d she asked, clearly floored by the question.<br /> <br /> \u201cPromise you won\u2019t leave me, Maria,\u201d I repeated. \u201cMarguerite and Julia might be going away. I know you love them both. I have to stay here, though. I\u2019m bound to the Dream House for at least another six months by a pledge, and my dad is here, and pretty much everyone I <u><u>know</u></u> since I left Arcadia is here\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI will <u><u>never</u></u> leave you, Juliette,\u201d D said. \u201cNot for anything.\u201d<br /> <br /> I sighed with relief. \u201cI know,\u201d I said in a small voice, \u201cI just needed to hear it. As long as you\u2019re with me, I can survive anything else.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot for anything,\u201d she repeated. \u201cI\u2019ll hate every second of it if we lose Julia and Insincere Marguerite to this mess, but I\u2019ll deal with it. I\u2019m not leaving you. Not \u2018til my dying day.\u201d<br /> <br /> So after we\u2019d made that perfectly clear, we went down to sex breakfast. I didn\u2019t feel much like eating, but I thought we should check in with the others. Calamity was still out with Becky at that point, but Jacob and Gawain showed up. It was as grim and silent as I\u2019ve ever seen a breakfast in the Dream House, and it did nothing to improve my mood.<br /> <br /> The boys went out to spar after breakfast. I guess they wanted to blow off some steam or something, and I can hardly fault them for that after the evening I spent with Joan and Andromeda. D and I came out to watch for a while, and eventually Marguerite and Julia joined us as well. Gawain and Jacob stopped their sparring and walked over to speak with the four of us.<br /> <br /> It quickly became apparent \u2013 even through his oddly formal demeanor \u2013 that Gawain had no idea how deeply Marguerite had been hurt by Calamity\u2019s betrayal. Marguerite told him how Calamity\u2019s actions had forced her to break her word, and how this in turn had damaged her Clarity. He didn\u2019t react emotionally, but quickly asked her if it was possible for reparations to be made. Marguerite said that she would think about it, but didn\u2019t know if there was any way to repair the breach between the two of them.<br /> <br /> Judging from his face during this conversation, Jacob either already knew about Marguerite\u2019s loss, or had guessed as much from her actions.<br /> <br /> Calamity arrived around this point, though we didn\u2019t know it. Marguerite, Julia, D and I had retreated back to the kitchen to talk a bit more privately (I confess, I was hoping to convince the two of them to reconsider their plans to move away from Malibu). Calamity and Becky pulled up to the front of the house, but they heard the sounds of Gawain and Jacob sparring in the back and didn\u2019t come in.<br /> <br /> In fact, we didn\u2019t see anybody for a while, but eventually we heard a slight commotion from the front of the house, and I went to investigate. What I found was a somewhat bemused looking Calamity, Gawain, and Jacob on one side of the courtyard, with the Handmaidens on the other, and the Warlock of Night\u2026 climbing the spire in the center of our fountain.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat\u2019s she doing?\u201d I asked Gawain out of the side of my mouth, hoping to avoid giving offense.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe wants to speak with Insincere Marguerite,\u201d he answered me, his eyes never leaving our guests. \u201cShe\u2019s being quite insistent. Do you think an audience would be possible?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll\u2026 I\u2019ll go and check,\u201d I stammered out, and then hurried back into the house.<br /> <br /> I returned to the kitchen. \u201cWhat\u2019s going on out there?\u201d D asked curiously.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s the Warlock of Night,\u201d I began.<br /> <br /> \u201cShit,\u201d D said, and a slightly panicked look crossed her face. \u201cWith everything else that\u2019s going on, I forgot\u2026 she stopped by last night during the show, and wanted to speak with Insincere Marguerite. I told her that she wasn\u2019t feeling up to visitors, and she went away.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you for looking out for me,\u201d Marguerite said softly from across the room. \u201cI will see her now, as long as she does not mind if my friends remain present for the meeting.\u201d<br /> <br /> I went back outside and conveyed the message. The Warlock splashed out of the fountain and dripped her way across the courtyard. She agreed to Marguerite\u2019s terms, and all of us made our way toward the kitchen. I noticed Calamity following the rest of us at a distance, but she made sure to remain in the hall, within earshot but well out of Marguerite\u2019s line of sight.<br /> <br /> The Handmaidens came in too, but they didn\u2019t make any overt attempts at seduction today. As usual when they\u2019re in the presence of their monarch, they were demure and deferential.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not going to try to report the exact exchange that followed; parts of it were too surreal for me to capture with words. The gist of it is that the Warlock of Night had heard the rumors that the Day and Night Courts will be gaining crowns in the Freehold in the near future, and that she believes Marguerite will soon be her co-monarch (and that Felicity will be the Day Court\u2019s monarch\u2026 and didn\u2019t <u><u>that</u></u> raise a red flag in my mind). She claims that she wants to make certain that the relationship between the Night Court rulers of Santa Monica and Los Angeles will be benevolent, but I would be very surprised if she didn\u2019t have some sort of ulterior motive underneath all of that honey.<br /> <br /> Marguerite thanked the Warlock for her concern, and promised to consider her words carefully. The Warlock withdrew, glancing down at herself in apparent annoyance and asking the Handmaidens \u201cwhy am I wet? Was it the fountain?\u201d<br /> <br /> I walked our guests out, putting what I hope was a comforting hand on Calamity\u2019s arm as I passed her. She sought out Gawain after that, and I breathed a sigh of relief. The two of them need each other today, even more than usual. Calamity needs Gawain\u2019s strength, and Gawain needs Calamity to lead him back from wherever he\u2019s retreated to. Now that they\u2019re together, I think they\u2019ll both be all right. I hope so.<br /> <br /> When I got back to the kitchen, Marguerite and Julia were having another discussion about moving away. I don\u2019t want to read too much into this, but my take on it is that Marguerite is currently reconsidering that option, and even seemed to get a little annoyed at Julia when she wouldn\u2019t drop the subject. So while I\u2019m not ready to jump for joy just yet, that may be the beginning of a hopeful sign.<br /> <br /> I found D in the entrance hall, arranged at one corner of a tense triangle with Gloria and Desiree. They weren\u2019t exactly glaring at each other, but you could tell none of them were particularly happy, either. Gloria\u2019s still uncomfortable around Desiree in the wake of her betrayal, and Desiree resents how quickly Gloria and D have become close. For her part, I don\u2019t think D has a problem with either of the other two\u2026 but she doesn\u2019t like being glared at. Upon my arrival on the scene, Desiree sort of tersely announced that she would be spending the day with Flores, and made her exit.<br /> <br /> So now D and I are sitting around glumly, trying not to bring Gloria down with our own problems and hoping that there\u2019s something we can do to try to repair the danger to our broken family. And on top of all of this shit, I\u2019m nervous as hell about introducing D to my dad tomorrow morning. She still thinks I should tell him the truth about who I am, but I don\u2019t know if this is the time. But in the spirit of full disclosure, she\u2019s told me that I\u2019m allowed to introduce her to dad as \u201cMaria.\u201d<br /> <br /> I love her. She loves me. We\u2019re going to stay together. These are absolutes, no matter what else in the world might change. As long as that remains true, I guess I can be brave through just about anything else.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T21:21:17-07:00","id":862407,"title":"","content":"<b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> Saturday, November 8<sup>th</sup><br /> Nine years, seven months, fifteen days<br /> Days without stabbing: 0<br /> <br /> It's all my fault. Everything is fucking broken. How could I have been so fucking blind yesterday? Nothing went right. I fucked everything up.<br /> <br /> I knew better. I fucking knew better. She gave her word. I should have found another way. Maybe we could have delayed. Or Jacob could have been ready to hold her if she was so deeply controlled she tried to stop us.<br /> <br /> No. Gawain. Gawain should have while Jacob drugged Chalcedony. Jacob isn't the one Chalcedony trusted. He's not the one that was going to be going into her dreams to try to help her.<br /> <br /> Fuck. None of us should have been fucking doing it. This place is supposed to be a fucking safe haven. How many gorram times have I said that... how many times have I fucking LIED to people? We brought her in and we fucking betrayed her.<br /> <br /> I betrayed her.<br /> <br /> I betrayed my best friend.<br /> <br /> I betrayed the Dream House.<br /> <br /> I am fucking traitor and a royal idiot. How in the nine fucking circles of Hell did I manage to go so far wrong? Better yet, how I am going to even begin to fucking repair the damage?<br /> <br /> By not breaking down for one. I already spent too much time mewling like a lost kitten yesterday. I could see it as soon as she slapped me. As soon as she started yelling. I have never seen her so angry. I knew. I knew I'd gone too far. I saw it but I just stood there trying to explain like somehow making her understand why would help. But it didn't. It doesn't matter why. All that mattered was that I had harmed her. I tried to explain and then... instead of trying to fix the mess I'd made I just became part of it. <br /> <br /> I couldn't help Gawain. Even if our actions had poisoned Chalcedony against him, I should have been there with him. I should have been at his side. I should have helped him remember who he was. I shouldn't have let him slip away like that.<br /> <br /> But I was too broken. Too weak. Too busy crying and feeling sorry for myself and writing fucking teenage emo poetry in my diary.<br /> <br /> I was in no condition to help him or anyone else. Fuck, I couldn't even help my own damn self last night. Thankfully Lori put her foot down and called Becky to collect me and take me away.<br /> <br /> I tried to argue. But Becky wasn't having it. She took my arm and told me we should go out. She knew this little Vietnamese place that had opened and wanted to take me there. She was calm and patient and gentle but unwavering. She didn't stop me from rambling but managed to steer things back to something light every time I started. She patiently let me burn out my stubbornness and then she quietly took my hand and led me to her house.<br /> <br /> We talked. There was ethereal Oriental string and flute music played softly. She held me close. She touched me, soothing me and holding me in her arms while I cried until I was out of tears. She told me I was staying and I just nodded.<br /> <br /> I feel asleep in her arms. It was the first time I've ever done that. I was too weary to think about it. But sleep wasn't escape. The dreams were vivid, harsh.<br /> <br /> There was blood. There's always blood. It filled my senses. I could smell it, taste it, feel it on my hands and skin, I was covered in it. I was bathed in it, running my hands over my skin to spread the warmth of it into every pore. It was sweet... and familiar...<br /> <br /> It was Insincere Marguerite's. She was laying there face down in the pool I was gathering to coat myself with. Her back was ripped open from stem to stern.<br /> <br /> I awoke screaming and thrashing. Once I was coherent I could see that I'd cut Becky. But when I tried to apologize but she shook her head and covered my lips with a finger and just healed herself. I tried to get up but she drew me back down firmly (though gently) and told me I wasn't going anywhere. Gawain is the only one who's ever seen me like that. The only one I've ever let my guard down so far for and allowed to take care of me. I hesitated but she ordered me to relax and I was too worn out to fight it. I just curled into her like a child and closed my eyes. I laid like that the rest of the night, dozing in and out but never sinking all the way to dreaming again.<br /> <br /> We stayed like that until sometime after the sun had come up and the birds started to sing. She used her Spring contracts on us both and we rose for breakfast and coffee and quiet talking. She was concerned but didn't doubt me when I told her I was feeling better. While I was thanking her for being there, for helping me when I needed it so badly she told it wasn't charity. She told me she cared. It's as close to telling me she loves me as she's ever gotten.<br /> <br /> She didn't want to let me come back to the Dream House alone. She's worried about me and I can't blame her. If I am being honest here, I am not really okay. I am way ahead of where I was but I'm hurting. I still feel more than a little lost. In the end she brought me back and she stayed. We heard the clash of sparring and she immediately started steering me around the house to find Gawain.<br /> <br /> He was sparring with Jacob. They came over when I arrived. I saw from the way he was carrying himself and speaking that he'd regressed. The guilt kicked me. I was laying weak and helpless and basking greedily in Becky's strength while he was losing himself in the ghost of who he'd been.<br /> <br /> But before I could try to start coaxing him back, there was an arrival. The Warlock of Night and her handmaidens had come to speak to Insincere Marguerite. Gawain and I told them she wasn't well and made them wait while Lori went in to see if she was up to talking.<br /> <br /> She decided she was, though not alone. We entered and I waited in the hall, resting against the wall beside the archway to the kitchen. I could hear the conversation but was not where Insincere Marguerite could see me. She sounded weary as the Warlock explained that it seemed likely she and Felicity would soon have the Day and Night crowns for this city. She claimed she wanted to make sure Insincere Marguerite was prepared and that relations were good with them. I'm not sure how much I believe. Though she mentioned that if Insincere Marguerite rejected the crown it was likely going to Salk. I can't say that sounds like the best thing, though I really don't know him terribly well. I just don't trust him.<br /> <br /> They left before too long and Insincere Marguerite and Julia withdrew to their room. I protested that they shouldn't have to hide when I was the one who'd hurt her but Lori pointed out she needed to rest.<br /> <br /> Lori looked rough. She's been crying. Apparently Insincere Marguerite and Julia are considering leaving the motley and the city. I know the idea of being apart from her lovers is horrible and seeing them so hurt is tearing her up. DLR is caught in the middle of it all, trying to fix the mess I've made and being strong. Jacob is in the same position.<br /> <br /> Once the Warlock had gone and most of the others went up to settle Insincere Marguerite and Julia in, I moved to speak to Gawain. I hugged him tightly and told him I needed him. I do need him. I need his strength and Becky's both right now. I've made such a mess of things. Everyone is hurting and it's my fault.<br /> <br /> But Chalcedony is alive and unharmed. She's in the Lighthouse and they're trying to get Juan Carlos to come in and heal her. He's at least familiar with the Director's programming and I think he can be trusted not to do anything to harm her. Gawain seemed to came back to himself without too much difficulty. He said we should spar, push thinking aside for a while. I don't think it was just for my benefit but I needed it. This whole business has me riding on the razor's edge and as much as everyone is reeling I cannot afford to let myself break down like I did yesterday. Yes, I am hurting but I am the one that did this so I am the one that has to woman up and fix it. And I will. I don't know how yet, but there has to be a way and I will find it. I'll make things right somehow.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> So, today just kept going. I wish I could say that things got better as the day progressed, but that would be lying. The day didn\u2019t really improve much. I felt a bit bad for Gloria who was brought back to the Dream House by Joan. She ended up in the middle of our motley business and it was not all good. Calamity has, since earlier today, regained her \u201cmask\u201d and is walking around insisting that she\u2019s fine. She even acts like she\u2019s okay. If I didn\u2019t know what she\u2019d just been through I might have even believed her. As it was I knew that she was hurting but was doing her best to push on and focus on the show. So I humored her for a while and offered to watch the door and call in a back-up bartender to take care of drinks. In the end I finally convinced her that I had just the guy to watch the bar and that I was fine keeping an eye on the door. I think she was even planning on going on with her acts tonight. Not sure how they would have come out considering how much of a damper she\u2019s got on her emotions right now. Thankfully, Lori also noticed what was going on with Calamity and she talked to her backstage. I wasn\u2019t sure what was said, but figured out some of it when Becky showed up to take Calamity out for the night. I assured Calamity that I had the club covered and that she should go on and take some time for herself. I think she felt bad about leaving, but was starting to acknowledge that she needed the time to work through what happened.<br /> <br /> Before the show De la Rocha also came up to Lori with concerns that Julia was not being helpful with Insincere Marguerite and that she was making things worse. Not that she was doing anything to hurt the woman that she loves, just that her attitude was not conducive to helping matters resolve. So, Lori, being the sweet person that she is, went upstairs to talk to Insincere Marguerite and Julia about what happened. I don\u2019t know what was said. I just know that Lori came back from that conversation in tears. I will have to look more into that and find out what made her so upset.<br /> <br /> So, notable at the club tonight were the Warlock of Night and her handmaidens. There was also a new Day Courtier present. Calamity was worried by all of them, but I insisted that I had the club in hand and would find out what I could about the Handmaidens\u2019 agenda and the new Day Courtier. So after the show had started, but between two of the numbers I made my way over to the new guest and introduced myself. I made small talk and found out that her name is Rowan. She said that she is a Selkie. She is apparently visiting from Venice Beach and is new to the area. She decided to come to the Dream House based on our reputation. I can\u2019t say that I learned much more that is interesting other than that. She did not seem to be related to the business that the Warlock of Night was here for. Unrelated to our new guest I noticed that a number of birds seemed to be perched on the window sills, watching. It might not have struck me as so odd, but a number of the birds are diurnal and would not be up so late at night. It made me curious. I shall have to see if anyone else noticed this or if it was just me.<br /> <br /> After leaving Rowan I noticed that De la Rocha was talking to the Warlock of Night. I moved closer so I could be of assistance if needed, but it seemed at first that my presence would not be required. Then the conversation they were having turned into a more heated argument. Then De la Rocha argued that Insincere Marguerite was not helped when she needed it in Los Angeles and that the same was happening here. I decided that it was time for me to intervene and I went over and asked if I might borrow De la Rocha. This worked to immediately fizzle whatever was starting up between them. The Warlock and her Handmaidens went back to their table. The Handmaidens ran their hands along my arm as they left but didn\u2019t do anything else. After that I talked to De la Rocha and found out that the Warlock of Night was interested in meeting with Insincere Marguerite and that she wanted to see her tonight. De la Rocha insisted that Marguerite was not up to guests tonight and the Warlock had simply asked what time tomorrow was good for an audience. I don\u2019t know if a definite time was given or not. I think the Warlock just assumed that tomorrow was okay and left it at that.<br /> <br /> Once we were done discussing the Warlock and her intentions I asked De la Rocha how Insincere Marguerite was doing since I had not seen her for a while. De la Rocha said that she was still getting over what happened and needed time before she came downstairs. I asked if I was missing something. I know that Marguerite got angry about Calamity getting her out of the room before Gawain subdued Chalcedony, but nothing beyond that. The reaction on both parts seemed a little over the top. Then I found out what had really happened. De la Rocha said that Marguerite had made a vow to Chalcedony that she would not leave her side. Then when Calamity came in and got Insincere Marguerite out of the room it violated her vow. I supposed I should be writing Vow with a capital \u201cV.\u201d I don\u2019t think any glamor was spent on it, but Marguerite had been good about not going against her word since she got back from Arcadia. She always follows through on her promises, but this time she couldn\u2019t. She was prevented from fulfilling her vow by a friend. Something broke inside her when that happened and she lost something of herself. That\u2019s why she was so upset and why she reacted the way she did to Calamity. That is why Calamity is so upset. She knows what happened. They both do. Marguerite slipped just a little closer to what she had been before she left Arcadia. Before she came back to herself.<br /> <br /> I found that in that moment I knew exactly what Marguerite was going through. A while ago when we fought the grey aliens that came with the Mothership I felt something break inside me. I don\u2019t know exactly what it was that did it. Maybe it was the fact that I was essentially killing other Changelings like myself, but whatever it was it broke something inside me. I felt fractured for a little while after that, but then I became comfortable with the new me. Maybe it was because the \u201cnew\u201d me was so similar to what I had been for so long that I didn\u2019t mind the change. Like putting on an old coat. Sometimes I think about what I lost and I think that I may be broken in more ways that I realize. I feel like I\u2019m detached from what is going on around me. I try to be a part of the lives of my friends, but I feel so separate. So alone. I operated alone or with just Rook for so long that it feels weird to be part of such a large group. I think in the beginning I tried harder to be a part of their lives, but now I don\u2019t. I don\u2019t know when that changed. Have I always been so standoffish or is this something new? Am I going back to being that cold, emotionless person that I was for so many years? I thought I had become a better person, but sometimes I wonder. And why did it take a friend\u2019s loss for me to see that? Maybe her pain reminded me of what I should be feeling but am not?<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Breakfast was a slightly smaller affair that usual. Julia came down earlier and brought food up to Insincere Marguerite so those two did not join us. Neither did Calamity for that matter. It was just the rest of the motley plus Gloria and Desiree. The food was good, as usual, but the mood was subdued. Gawain mentioned that he was not able to help with the dream healing for Chalcedony last night after all. It was considered unsafe for him to help since he was instrumental in subduing her and she might see anything he did as an attack rather than as an effort to help. I believe he said that they were going to call in Juan Carlos to do the dream healing since he was not involved in any of what went down. I could tell that Gawain was disappointed, but he also seemed to be a bit detached this morning. I\u2019ve noticed that he gets that way sometimes. It\u2019s mostly when something important needs to be done and the \u201call business\u201d side of him comes to the fore. Hopefully he will come back to his regular self soon. <br /> <br /> We of course talked about what we could do to help with the whole Insincere Marguerite/ Calamity situation. It didn\u2019t amount to much. De la Rocha wanted to make sure that we didn\u2019t do anything that might mess things up. So we\u2019re all walking on eggshells, so to speak. This discussion got Lori to go upstairs and talk to Julia and Marguerite and see what she could do. Again, not sure what was said but it at least had some positive results later on.<br /> <br /> While that was going on Gloria asked me and Gawain what we did during the day when we had free time. Gawain mentioned sparring, and Gloria asked if she could watch us spar. Gawain and I looked at each other, shrugged and said \u201csure.\u201d So we went out back and began to practice. Gawain\u2019s style was the same as it always is, but his demeanor was different. Normally he smiles here and there while we spar, and makes comments on occasion. Today he was very serious and focused on the fight. I also noticed that he didn\u2019t pull his hits quite as much as he usually does. I probably walked away with a few more bruises than usual. I\u2019m not complaining mind you, I just have some physical reminders of where I need to work on my form. Overall it wasn\u2019t that big a difference from his usual manner but it was noticeable to me.<br /> <br /> While we were sparring we had some unexpected guests come out side to watch. It was Julia and Marguerite. Apparently Lorelei convinced them to come downstairs and socialize just a bit. It was likely done with the promise that Calamity was not here. So, Gawain and I paused our sparring match to go over and talk to our motley mates. I offered to make the both of them coffee, but only Julia took me up on the offer. So, I went to the kitchen and made up a cup just the way she likes it and brought it back out to Julia. We all talked and there was an explanation of what happened and why Insincere Marguerite is so upset. Lori was watching Gawain and I and I think she figured out that Gawain had no idea about how Marguerite was hurt. I had heard it from De la Rocha last night, so I was not as surprised. Gawain then asked if there was any way Calamity could make reparations for her actions. Marguerite said that she\u2019d think about it and admitted that she and Julia were looking into moving away and were currently searching for apartments. She also said that in the past she had never let herself get too close to other people so they couldn\u2019t hurt her, but with us she made an exception. She allowed herself to get close, to care about us. That was why she said Calamity\u2019s betrayal hurt that much more. Not long after that Insincere Marguerite and Julia went inside, to the kitchen I think. <br /> <br /> Gawain and I went back to sparring after they left. Soon after we started back up again Calamity must have gotten back to the house. She said that she heard the fighting and came around back to see what was up. We stopped what we were doing again and went over to talk to Calamity. Gawain then explained to his sweetheart about Marguerite\u2019s loss of clarity, for lack of a better term. Not long after that we heard car doors shutting at the front of the house. As we started walking around the front with the others I mentioned that it might be the Warlock of Night. I had forgotten until that moment that she had said something about coming back today to talk to Insincere Marguerite. So, Lori went inside to warn Marguerite what was up and the rest of us went around to the front of the house. Sure enough it was the Warlock and her Handmaidens. <br /> <br /> When we got around to the front of the house the Warlock was there. When we told her she would need to wait for a moment she just stepped into the fountain and had started to climb it. She was dressed rather interestingly too. She wore some sort of harness and had a bear\u2019s arm as a sleeve for one of her own arms. The combination was notable. After we arrived she stopped climbing and declared that she would like to speak to Insincere Marguerite. Lori came out at that point and said that Marguerite was waiting inside for her, so we all went in the house and met in the kitchen, the Warlock dripping on the tile. Calamity stayed just outside the door, out of line of sight with Marguerite. The Warlock admitted that she wanted to make sure that she and Marguerite were on good terms. She said that she believes that they will soon be crowning someone in our freehold to be the monarch of the Night Court, and that someone was likely to be Insincere Marguerite! There is also the possibility that it will be Salk, but the Warlock believes that they are leaning towards Marguerite. She also said that Felicity was likely to get the nod for Day Queen. She suggested talking with Felicity to make sure they were on the same page. I\u2019m assuming to make sure that the Day and Night courts are not actively fighting one another. Not long after that the Warlock of Night left mumbling about not knowing how she got wet.<br /> <br /> Soon after that Insincere Marguerite was told that Calamity was back and she immediately said that she was going upstairs. Julia protested but Marguerite went anyway. So we were shy two people when we started talking about the Warlock\u2019s odd behavior with the Fountain, then her not knowing how she got wet later. The confusion seemed genuine so I don\u2019t think she was putting on an act to appear crazy. I\u2019m not sure why she\u2019d want to appear crazy either. May be part of her image, it may be she has a legitimate disconnect from reality on occasion. Not sure which it is.<br /> <br /> After that Calamity went to the bar to get herself a drink. Normally not something I make a note of, but I did this time because Calamity doesn\u2019t usually drink so early. She also gripped the glass a little too hard and shattered it. Glass went flying and some ended up stuck in her hand. I think she started to clean up the glass by herself until Becky came over and helped. Becky also helped get the glass out of Calamity\u2019s hand, then got the first aid kit and bandaged her lover\u2019s injury. Those two are good for each other. They seem to ground one another. Gawain is also a good stabilizing influence in Calamity\u2019s life. He accepts her as she is and that is something really important. She needs that. Especially since she is getting help and trying to become a better person. It makes me wonder if I should ask for help too. I don\u2019t know if they can help though. Calamity has I\u2019d guess an excess of emotions, or at least emotions pointed to unhealthy activities. I\u2019m kind of the opposite. I\u2019m becoming disconnected and cold. I wonder if the folks at the Counseling Center can help me or not?<br /> <br /> There was a lot of talking today. All of it important though. Calamity and Gawain went off to talk privately. I don\u2019t know what they talked about, but I can make an educated guess. I\u2019d say that they were discussing what happened with Insincere Marguerite and the fallout from that. Funny how that one act affected so many people. From a completely dispassionate point of view it is interesting to watch the social dynamics change and adjust to take in the new mood in the house. While I was musing about ripples in the Dream House, Lori and De la Rocha went upstairs to talk to Insincere Marguerite and Julia. I hope they are trying to convince the pair of them to stay. I would miss them if they decided to leave. Marguerite more than Julia, but still, I\u2019d miss them both.<br /> <br /> I admitted to Becky, as everyone else had gone off to talk, that I did not know how to support both of my friends without making it look like I was taking sides. Everything is so tense right now. I\u2019m afraid that I\u2019m going to do something that messes everything up. I\u2019m not great with people on a regular day, and lately I just haven\u2019t been very social anyway. I don\u2019t know what to do. Right now I guess my plan is to act normally towards both of them and hope for the best. I\u2019m not going to act like nothing happened, that would belittle the injury to Insincere Marguerite. I can try and just keep on being my usual calm self and hope that it helps keep things the same way. Anyway\u2026Calamity and Gawain have just now gone outside to spar. Maybe I\u2019ll poke my head out in a minute and see if they want company or not. If all else fails I can just bring them water and watch them relieve some tension.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> I lost my best friend yesterday. Sadly.<br /> <br /> While I was trying to find a way to sweet talk Chalcedony into seeing the Monarchs, Calamity stepped in and asked I to speak with her. We walked over and someone shut the door, separating I from Chalcedony, and I realized Calamity had taken advantage of my trust to fool I into breaking my promise to Chalcedony to stay with her and look out for her. Getting her help is looking out for her, regardless. But I broke my word, because I trusted Calamity, and the cracks appeared. I don\u2019t remember everything that happened then. I remembered rage. I remember hurting myself slapping her. I remember Lori healing I. I remember Julia singing. Such beautiful singing. Certainly.<br /> <br /> Last night was a nightmare. I talked to Lori again. I cried a great deal. Julia said we should move to Portland, or San Francisco. De La Rocha begged us not to. She said she wanted to spend the rest of her life with us, but could not, would not leave Lori. Not that we asked her to. I\u2019ve never heard De La Rocha be quite that blunt about her commitment to our relationship. I don\u2019t think it registered at the time, but now it is slightly dizzying. Pleasantly.<br /> <br /> Still, when she left we began looking at places in those cities. Oakland was looking a bit better, or San Jose, than San Francisco so we widened our search a bit to the Bay Area. Well, really Julia searched and showed I pictures. My mind was not there. My best friend betrayed I. I would be losing two women who were true lovers, either of whom could have been life partners. Hell, both of whom are, frankly, life partners. When Julia swears she will go where I go, I confess I think a little more about stealing her ring and using it to propose to her instead. If this works out so we stay, I will think about her request to all four oathbond a little harder. Absolutely.<br /> <br /> Eventually we went to bed, and Julia stoked my hair and sang until I slept. She slept too, she was asleep when I woke. When she woke, she got us breakfast. It was not too long after sex breakfast Lori and De La Rocha came in. I was more myself but still a little addled\u2026I told Lori we were considering moving, and she cried. But she and De La Rocha wanted to help, and as much as I was angry with Calamity I wanted to be helped. Deeply.<br /> <br /> Angry my not be the right word. It is more a nameless sort of fear or pressure, maybe a stress bearing down on I when I need to be near her. Thinking of it tightens my throat and races my heart. I feel a sickened disquiet. It is hard to find the English. It is uncomfortable, and I dread it. Utterly.<br /> <br /> We went outside and joined Jacob and Gawain. Gawain was in his somewhat usual, what is the word, \u201call business\u201d demeanor I had seen before, while Jacob was his usual self. It quickly became apparent to I, and Julia had to admit, that Gawain was utterly unaware of my vow or damage, and that Jacob only knew recently. Calamity had kept to herself that she was damaging my integrity; they had no idea. While this hardened I to Calamity, I admit it softened I to them. We spoke a bit, and Julia and my moving came up again, and Lori teared up again, and I teared up again, so I went inside. Quickly.<br /> <br /> So, while we were eating and hanging out when I was told The Warlock of Night was there. She arrived, soaking wet, with her Handmaidens, who acted, well, like they usually do around her, which is to say, very passive. The Warlock claimed I was likely to receive the Crown of Darkness, as the power of the Day and Night Courtiers was increasing in the Freehold. She wanted to tell I so I could prepare before the Courts talked to I. Her message delivered, she saluted politely and left. De La Rocha seemed to dislike her presence. Strongly. Or perhaps that was the Handmaidens. Possibly.<br /> <br /> Calamity returned, and we went upstairs. Lori is trying to convince us to stay. I am beginning to think I should. But only if this matter with Calamity is settled. I will not tiptoe around her. I am Insincere Marguerite. I am better than that. Absolutely.<br /> <br /> But the crown it disturbs I. The Monarchs cannot be pleased; every non Seasonal Changeling (except Gawain, I suppose) has learned to be wary of the Summer Court. This is what they occasionally bullied or fought people to prevent. I am going to have enemies. Also, whoever set this in motion, be it the Warlock, Willow, Salk or someone else, did not do it to benefit I. I will be in the way. No, this is not a good thing for I. Frighteningly.<br /> <br /> I need to talk to the others but I do not want to deal with Calamity. I don\u2019t want to see her, hear her, smell her or taste her. I will need to go on tonight. Lori asked I, and I declared I would be doing my show. <br /> <br /> After all, I regret nothing.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LIII</i><br /> <br /> It should be noted first and foremost that OOC there is no problems between any players. It is intense IC, but will almost certainly not come down to either Insincere Marguerite or Calamity leaving.<br /> <br /> Far be it from me to cast aspirations on the diagnosis of Dr. Grace, but Andromeda is not completely recovered. Still, mostly recovered is a good description, and as I noted they actually did a lot for her, and her recovery, while she is not quite who she was, she is pretty close, and still getting better. She was happy enough for a wild night with Lori and Joan, certainly.<br /> <br /> It was a rough session, emotionally draining. But ended on a hopeful note. And the world is not stopping for those who are dealing with their issues. Next time we continue to advance the timeline as Insincere Marguerite face their demons. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T12:56:22-07:00","id":863278,"title":"","content":"Right, as always, everything you see in Lori's journal entries should be regarded as her take on current events and not as gospel truth (so to speak). In fact, one of the direct quotes from this session that didn't make it into the journals involved Lori admitting to D that &quot;I know dick about psychology,&quot; so her assessment of Andromeda's current mental state should be taken with a grain of salt.<br /> <br /> On a side note, I want to make it clear that Lori's avian friends were not role-played in session, so all credit (or, more likely, <u>blame</u>) for their names should rest squarely on my shoulders. Bonus points if you recognize the pop culture references therein.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T23:31:54-07:00","id":867390,"title":"","content":"It's the off-week, but I wanted to put up a fiction done by Jacob's player discussing Jacob's past, fleshing out part of the background. Enjoy<br /> <br /> <b>The Beginning of the End</b><br /> <br /> Light shone in through the room\u2019s small single window, illuminating the walls with a soft yellow glow. The lone occupant lay on the twin bed against the adjacent wall under light covers. His white hair stood up in an unkempt fashion, poking out from around a bandage wrapped around his head. Frost seemed to wind its way down the side of his face and over his forehead, which peeked from beneath white gauze. The young man\u2019s eyes flickered open and closed a couple of times before remaining open. He peered around the room with his light blue eyes taking note of where everything was. The walls were a cream color with a delicate floral border at the top near the ceiling. The floor was a dark hardwood with a pale purple area rug next to the bed. The color matched the flowers in the border on the wall. The window graced the outer wall, with lavender curtains and small ceramic unicorns arranged in a line on the sill. There was a chest of drawers and cubbies filled neatly with toys against the wall opposite the window and a small desk with a floral border under the window itself. A low table sat next to the bed with a straight-backed wooden chair sitting next to it. The chair looked like it belonged with the desk. The pale man started to raise himself up on his elbows but his actions were cut short by a sharp stabbing pain across his left side. His arms gave way and he fell back to the mattress with a stifled groan. A moment later a young woman with equally pale skin, white hair and light eyes walked into the room carrying a tray.<br /> <br /> \u201cTried to sit up, didn\u2019t you?\u201d A gentle smile graced her lips. She set the tray down on a table near the bed. \u201cYou hungry?\u201d<br /> <br /> The young man stared at her incredulously, arms wrapped around his ribs. \u201cWhat?\u201d He asked fingering the bandage around his middle.<br /> <br /> \u201cAre you hungry? Or maybe thirsty? You have been unconscious for a while now and I thought that you might like something to eat.\u201d She gestured towards a cup of juice and some toast.<br /> <br /> \u201cHow long have I been here?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cA couple days now. You were out for most of it. We weren\u2019t sure if you were going to wake up any time soon. I was happy to see you stir this morning.\u201d She sat down in the chair.<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t understand. Why am I alive?\u201d He asked, confusion playing across his features.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt was a little iffy in the beginning, but we did our best to heal you.\u201d<br /> <br /> The pale man shook his head. \u201cNo, why am I alive now? Why didn\u2019t you kill me?\u201d<br /> <br /> They young woman smiled sadly and gently pushed on the other man\u2019s shoulder until he was lying flat.<br /> <br /> \u201cLet me check those ribs to make sure they didn\u2019t shift again.\u201d She deftly but gently lifted his shirt and softly prodded his ribs. He hissed in pain as her fingers found a particularly painful spot.<br /> <br /> \u201cSorry.\u201d She said but her fingers continued their exploration. \u201cNothing feels too out of place. Your ribs should heal okay.\u201d The pale woman sat back<br /> <br /> The young man let out the breath he\u2019d been holding. \u201cYou didn\u2019t answer me before. Why am I still alive?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLiam honestly just wanted to talk to you and maybe get some information. Travers wasn\u2019t supposed to go as far as he did.\u201d She shook her head in apology.<br /> <br /> The young man looked at the ceiling, his brow furrowed in confusion. \u201cI don\u2019t get it.\u201d He mumbled quietly as the young woman reached over to get the juice. She looked back at him with sad eyes. \u201cHas no one ever shown you kindness?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cPeople don\u2019t do things without a reason. This\u2026 \u201cHe said gesturing to the room, \u201c\u2026is foolishness.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWould you rather be dead?\u201d<br /> <br /> The young man paused. \u201cNo. It just doesn\u2019t make sense to heal your enemy.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe don\u2019t have to be enemies. You don\u2019t have to go back if you don\u2019t want to.\u201d The pale woman reasoned.<br /> <br /> \u201cYour people wouldn\u2019t allow that. I came to bring you back to our Lady. They won\u2019t forgive that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThey might\u2026maybe if you made a Pledge not to go back.\u201d She smiled gently.<br /> <br /> \u201cThere\u2019s no gain for you if I were to do that.\u201d The young man reasoned. \u201cYou would still have someone in your midst that you didn\u2019t like and didn\u2019t trust.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhy does there have to be gain?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBecause that\u2019s how things work. People only do things that benefit themselves or their allies.\u201d <br /> <br /> The young woman paused in bringing the glass closer to her guest. \u201cIf that were the case, then why am I here checking your wounds and bringing you food?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t know!\u201d The young man started to raise himself up but hissed in pain and lay back down. \u201cI don\u2019t understand.\u201d His voice was quiet, barely a whisper.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sorry.\u201d She breathed quietly and leaned forward and kissed the young man on the cheek.<br /> <br /> He raised his hand to his face, his fingers tracing where her lips had touched him. His cheek still felt warm. \u201cSorry for what?\u201d Suspicion tinged his voice.<br /> <br /> \u201cFor what you\u2019ve been through.\u201d She pulled the small table closer to the bed and put the glass of juice back on it. \u201cI will leave the food here for you. I\u2019m going to see if I can find anything to help with the pain.\u201d She stood up and put the chair back where it had been before heading for the door. \u201cI\u2019m Diane by the way. If you need anything just ask for me, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> The young man nodded though his brow was still furrowed. \u201cI\u2019m Rime.\u201d He answered quietly.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, it\u2019s nice to meet you properly Rime.\u201d Diane smiled. \u201cI\u2019ll be back a little later.\u201d She slipped out the door and closed it behind her.<br /> <br /> Rime shook his head and looked around the room once more. His eyes settled on the food and drink on the table. He propped himself up carefully and took the cup of juice. He took a sip of the amber liquid and smiled slightly. \u201cApples,\u201d he mused to himself. \u201cI had forgotten what apples tasted like.\u201d He managed to eat half of the toast and all of the juice before exhaustion took over and he sank back down to the mattress. The sound of muffled voices carried through the door and Rime looked that way trying to keep his eyes open. His eyes finally closed and he slipped into an uneasy sleep.<br /> <br /> <br /> The next time Rime opened his eyes it was dark out. He looked around and noticed that there was another plate of food and some juice on the small table near the bed. He sat up carefully and ate what he could. The apple juice was slightly warm, but he drank it eagerly anyway. He tipped the glass back trying to get the last drops. Once he was done he carefully swung his legs over the side of the bed and pushed up to a standing position using the bed and table to lean on. He smiled in spite of the pain and started to take a step forward. His knee buckled and he caught himself painfully on the table, jarring his healing ribs. After another minute or two he tried walking again this time shuffling his feet and taking small steps. He made it most of the way to the door when he heard voices again.<br /> <br /> \u201cDrew the short straw huh Travers?\u201d Came a muffled voice through the wood.<br /> <br /> \u201cNah, I volunteered.\u201d The reply was gruff and low.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhy?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSomeone\u2019s got to watch this bastard. Make sure he doesn\u2019t do anything.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s two o\u2019clock in the morning. He\u2019s probably asleep.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCan\u2019t take that chance. Besides late night is the best time to try to escape. Everyone\u2019s asleep.\u201d Travers replied.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019d be surprised if he could walk, man. I saw him after they finally pulled you off of him. He had pink bubbles coming out of his mouth when he tried to breathe. You busted his ribs and punctured his lung. He was dying. If Diane hadn\u2019t healed him as much as she did he\u2019d be dead.\u201d The softer voice argued.<br /> <br /> \u201cBe better if he was.\u201d<br /> <br /> Rime started to feel his knees shake and slowly made his way back to the bed. He remembered the ogre Travers beating him. The man hit hard, and he was fast, very fast for a man his size. A shudder ran down his spine as he managed to sit on the edge of the bed, his ribs screaming in protest. His arms started to shake as he leaned on them and sweat ran down his face. He wiped his forehead with the back of his hand and went back to leaning on his arms.<br /> <br /> \u201cI know you don\u2019t mean that, man. You\u2019re not a killer.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cPhil, don\u2019t be an idiot. He\u2019s a loyalist. They all deserve to die. He was trying to take Diane back to that frozen hell.\u201d His deep voice cracked. \u201cHe was going to take her