boy with brown eyes that made her laugh. Not all of her memories from her durance have come back either.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDid you make her do all this?\u201d Rime motioned to his bandages.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, she volunteered to help you. She is a very generous person and cares for everyone she meets. She could no more leave you injured than one could stop a beaver from making a dam.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t understand.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know. That\u2019s why we\u2019re talking now.\u201d Liam replied. He took a sip from his glass and smiled at Rime\u2019s questioning glance. \u201cWhat do you want to know Rime?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhy you kept me alive. What you\u2019re going to do with me if I answer your questions.\u201d Rime replied.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe kept you alive because it was the right thing to do. We are not monsters. We don\u2019t kill people who disagree with us because it\u2019s more convenient that way.\u201d He gestured to the room. \u201cWe brought you here to recuperate and once you were able, to answer some questions.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut I am not here because I disagreed with you. I am here because I was sent to retrieve someone for the Lady. You are within your rights to kill me and yet you keep me alive. I do not understand.\u201d Rime gestured at the other man. \u201cYou are not a fool I think, but you are acting foolish.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s what Diane told me you\u2019d say.\u201d Liam smiled. \u201cRight now you are our guest. We are not encouraging you to leave this room however. Not until we get an oath from you that you will do no harm to this Freehold or its inhabitants. That includes taking or returning anyone to your Lady\u2019s realm.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIf I make this oath with you, you will let me go?\u201d Rime\u2019s eyebrow raised in question.<br /> <br /> \u201cThis is not something to take lightly Rime. The others may insist that the consequence for breaking 