2019t make more than a soft grunt in answer to the man\u2019s accusations.<br /> <br /> \u201cTravers!\u201d a female voice cried. \u201cLet him go. Now!\u201d<br /> <br /> Rime\u2019s vision faded further and his struggles were weakening. He knew that he was going to pass out soon and could do nothing to stop it. The ogre\u2019s grip was too strong. He tried reaching up with his other hand but his efforts were easily pushed aside by Travers free hand. The larger man looked over his shoulder to see who had come in and saw Diane.<br /> <br /> \u201cHe\u2019s a loyalist Diane. He can\u2019t be trusted.\u201d His grip did not lessen. If anything it got tighter.<br /> <br /> \u201cHe\u2019s our guest, loyalist or not. Now let him go before you kill him!\u201d The pale woman argued angrily.<br /> <br /> Travers pulled Rime forward and slammed him back into the wall, his head making a solid thud. \u201cI don\u2019t know why you\u2019re defending him. He tried to take you back to that frozen hell. He\u2019s probably still working on a way to get you back there. You know that you can\u2019t trust him. He could hurt you, Diane.\u201d The ogre pleaded.<br /> <br /> Rime\u2019s struggles weakened considerably and he barely held onto the ogre\u2019s wrist. The woman\u2019s voice sounded familiar but he couldn\u2019t hear what the two were saying over the rushing sound in his ears. The ache in his chest didn\u2019t even seem that painful now. He wondered briefly who the woman was before blacking out entirely. It almost sounded like Delight, but she had escaped hadn\u2019t she?<br /> <br /> Travers felt Rime\u2019s body go limp. He held on for a moment longer before finally letting go. Rime slid down until his body was almost flat on the bed and his neck was at an angle as his head still leaned against the wall. Diane walked forward, going around Travers and arranged the young man so he was lying flat. His breaths were raspy but regular. She gently checked his neck and ribs for damage and shook her head. \u201cI know that you are just trying to keep me safe Travers, but he really can\u2019t do anything to me here. His injuries were bad enough before that I don\u2019t think he could make it out of the house let alone kidnap me and bring be all the way to the Lady\u2019s realm.\u201d<br /> <br /> The ogre looked down for a moment before looking Diane in the face. \u201cI just don\u2019t think we should underestimate him. He could be faking it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHe\u2019s not faking it Travers. Remember, I\u2019m the healer. I\u2019m also an ER nurse. I know injuries, and he is hurt. Badly. You almost killed him this time. You re-broke his ribs. \u201d She said as she put her hands on the young man\u2019s bruised side and started sending healing energy into the injuries.<br /> <br /> \u201cI won\u2019t apologize for my actions.\u201d The ogre grumbled.<br /> <br /> \u201cI know. I just want you to go easy on him. Liam is trying to get information out of him so we\u2019ll know if anyone else is at risk from the Lady. He may even get him to make an Oath that he won\u2019t hurt anyone in the Freehold.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDo you think he\u2019d actually make that Oath?\u201d Travers said nodding in Rime\u2019s direction.<br /> <br /> \u201cI think so. Liam can be persuasive. Plus it\u2019s not Rime that I\u2019m worried about right now.\u201c<br /> <br /> \u201cIf not him then who?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cRime has a partner named Rook. He\u2019s good at traveling in shadows. I\u2019m just afraid he\u2019s going to come looking for his friend.\u201d<br /> <br /> The ogre made a fist. \u201cI\u2019ll be ready for \u2018im.\u201d <br /> <br /> Diane smiled. \u201cI know you will. That\u2019s why I can sleep peacefully at night.\u201d<br /> <br /> A faint blush tinged the ogre\u2019s cheeks and he looked down at his fists. A moment later the door opened and Liam walked in. He took in the scene and admonished the ogre. \u201cYou were only 