ether they laid Rime back down and covered him with blankets. Rime did not wake for three days.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Rime opened his eyes and blinked slowly. His vision was still somewhat hazy and his head felt like it was full of cotton. He turned his head to look around. He could not remember where he was but he knew there was something important that he needed to remember. As he turned a woman\u2019s voice interrupted his thoughts.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou need to lie still Rime. Your injuries are still healing.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMy \u2018ead feels funny. Like \u2018m floating.\u201d Rime slurred.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s the pain medicine you\u2019re on right now. I managed to get some of the good stuff so you wouldn\u2019t wake up in pain.\u201d She gently brushed the hair out of his eyes. \u201cI\u2019m so sorry that Travers hurt you again. He\u2019s not allowed to get near you as long as you are our guest here.\u201d<br /> <br /> The name Travers brought back an image of an angry man standing over him and Rime started to try and move away.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, Rime you need to lie still. Your ribs are still healing. There\u2019s no one here but us. It\u2019s okay.\u201d<br /> <br /> Rime stopped moving and looked at the woman that was trying her best to calm him down.<br /> <br /> \u201cThas good\u2026\u201d He slurred and closed his eyes. He was asleep in moments.<br /> <br /> <br /> The next few days were more of the same. Rime would wake up for a few moments, remember where he was and have a mild panic attack before calming down again. The pain medicine that Diane had obtained did its job well and the young man did not feel much in the way of pain when he did wake. <br /> <br /> The sound of quiet voices brought Rime around and he peered through lidded eyes to see who was in the room. He spotted Diane and a young girl, no more than eleven or twelve talking near the toy bins against the wall. The girl looked like a yearling deer. She had soft looking ears the poked through her chestnut hair and her legs ended in dainty hooves. Her all brown eyes flitted from one bin to the next.<br /> <br /> \u201cCome on, pick a toy or two then we can get something for lunch.\u201d Diane whispered to her young friend.<br /> <br /> \u201cI just need to find my Barbie\u2019s red dress. I know it\u2019s in here.\u201d The young doe girl replied.<br /> <br /> Rime looked at the pair and something twinged in his chest. The girl was taken young if she was a Changeling at her age. He shook his head as if trying to clear the thoughts from his head. Diane noticed the movement and started. \u201cOh\u2026I wasn\u2019t expecting you to be awake. Do you need anything?\u201d<br /> <br /> Rime\u2019s forehead furrowed for a moment. \u201cWater, if you dn\u2019t mind.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course.\u201d She turned back to the young girl. \u201cFelicity, find the red dress then join me in the kitchen.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c \u2018kay.\u201d The young girl replied. She looked shyly at Rime then continued her search in the toy bin.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhy\u2019re you here?\u201d Rime asked, curious.<br /> <br /> \u201cThis is my room.\u201d Felicity answered back quietly. \u201cI get to sleep in my sleeping bag in Auntie Diane\u2019s room while you use my room.\u201d She smiled shyly. \u201cAuntie Diane says that you need your rest.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019s pr\u2019bly r\u2019ght.\u201d The pale man slurred. The twinge in his chest came back and he pushed the feeling aside. He was not sure how he was feeling anything right now with the drugs that were coursing through his veins. His head still felt like it was full of cotton, though perhaps not as much as it had before.<br /> <br /> Diane came back with a pitcher and a glass. She smiled at Rime then filled the glass. She gently helped him sit up enough to drink his fill before letting him back down on the pillows. Rime looked at the young girl. \u201cTh\u2019nk you fer letting me st\u2019y in yer room.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re welcome.\u201d Felicity smiled shyly. \u201cI hope you feel better soon Mr. Rime.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDun underst\u2019nd.\u201d Rime mumbled before drifting off to sleep.<br /> <br /> The next time Rime woke it was to Diane sitting in the chair next to the bed, drawing in a sketchbook.<br /> <br /> \u201cAh, you\u2019re awake.\u201d She smiled. \u201cHow are you feeling today?\u201d<br /> <br /> Rime moved experimentally and found that while he could feel more of the aches in his body, they weren\u2019t so bad. His arm snaked around his ribs and held his side unconsciously. \u201cBetter, thank you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m glad. I was happy that I managed to get some morphine this time for your pain. I\u2019ve been scaling it back the past couple of days so you won\u2019t feel so woozy.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThas good,\u201d mumbled Rime.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou know, I remember you from the Lady\u2019s palace. You are one of her Knights.\u201d Diane paused. \u201cI remember you protecting us, the Lady\u2019s Treasures, when those thieves got into the palace. They tried to take us, but you and Rook stopped them.\u201d<br /> <br /> Rime looked at Diane carefully, suddenly more awake. \u201cWhat else do you remember?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot a lot. Some things here and there while I was in the Lady\u2019s palace. Then one day I saw something that reminded me of the symbol on the side of an ambulance. You know, the caduceus?\u201d<br /> <br /> Rime shook his head.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnyway, it reminded me of that and I suddenly remembered where I came from and managed to find a way out. I think there was a gate in the woods near here.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd you got out.\u201d Rime finished for her.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, and I was lucky enough to meet Travers and Liam soon after that. They helped me make a new life for myself.\u201d She indicated all around her. \u201cHere I was only gone for a month or so. In the Lady\u2019s realm it felt so much longer. When I got back I was able to create a new identity and slip into it. I chose to be an ER nurse this time around instead of an RN for a private practice.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou were lucky.\u201d Rime looked contemplative.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, no question there. What about you? What do you remember from your life before the Lady?<br /> <br /> <br /> Rime\u2019s brow furrowed in thought. \u201cI don\u2019t remember a life before the Lady.\u201d He said eventually. \u201cI remember the cold, but that ended when I entered the Lady\u2019s service.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sorry.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFor what?\u201d Rime questioned.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat you don\u2019t remember. Though I suppose if you did you wouldn\u2019t have tried to bring me back to the Lady\u2019s palace.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know. You were doing as you were asked. I don\u2019t blame you.\u201d Diane smiled. \u201cNow, you should probably get some more rest. It\u2019s getting late.\u201d<br /> <br /> Rime nodded and closed his eyes. Within moments he was asleep.<br /> <br /> <br /> Rime\u2019s life seemed to happen in moments since he woke up after Travers\u2019 beating. He woke to the sound of someone putting a tray on the table next to him and he stirred awake.<br /> <br /> \u201cGood afternoon.\u201d Diane smiled. \u201cYou hungry?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSure.\u201d Rime replied and propped himself up on the pillows. His ribs still ached but not nearly as sharp as they had mere days ago. At least he thought it was days. It might have been longer for all he knew. He wasn\u2019t sure how much time had passed while he was on the morphine. As he was getting himself more comfortable he noticed Felicity slip into the room behind Diane.<br /> <br /> \u201cGood afternoon.\u201d He said to the young girl.<br /> <br /> Felicity stood by the door fanning herself with a paper fan and holding a glass of red juice. \u201cIt\u2019s hot outside,\u201d moaned the young doe girl. She took a sip of her juice.<br /> <br /> \u201cMaybe I can help.\u201d Rime offered. <br /> <br /> \u201cHow?\u201d Felicity asked.<br /> <br /> Rime motioned towards the silverware on the try near him. \u201cPut the spoon in your juice.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhy?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cJust do it.\u201d<br /> <br /> Felicity looked to Diane who nodded. Encouraged, Felicity put the spoon in her drink. <br /> <br /> \u201cNow, come a little closer.\u201d Rime asked.<br /> <br /> Diane nodded again and Felicity moved to stand near the bed. <br /> <br /> Rime reached out with a slightly shaking hand and touched the glass. He focused for a moment and frost started to form on the outside of the glass. Felicity started in surprise but held on to the cup. Soon the juice inside froze and Rime let his hand drop back down to the bed.<br /> <br /> \u201cThere, now pull on the spoon.\u201d He suggested.<br /> <br /> Felicity pulled on the spoon and was delighted to see that she now had a cherry popsicle. \u201cThat\u2019s wicked!\u201d Felicity exclaimed. \u201cHow\u2019d you do that?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI can manipulate ice.\u201d He responded.<br /> <br /> Felicity happily started licking her popsicle. \u201cThank you Mr. Rime.\u201d Her smile was radiant.<br /> <br /> Rime felt that tightness in his chest again but brushed it aside assuming it was something to do with his broken ribs. He didn\u2019t even realize that his lips quirked up in a small smile of his own.<br /> <br /> Felicity practically skipped out of the room and Rime could hear her exclaiming to the first person she saw that she had a popsicle. Rime heard Travers grunt but not say anything else. Diane smiled at Rime. <br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cThank you for that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt was nothing.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot to her it wasn\u2019t. Did you see the smile on her face? I haven\u2019t seen her so happy in a long time.\u201d Diane paused as she fussed with the sheet covering Rime. \u201cWhen Felicity came back she found that a Fetch had been sent in her place and she lost her family. We took her in, but she still misses her parents and her little brother. She\u2019s usually so sad. She\u2019s only been back a couple of months now. Not long enough to get over the loss just yet. So, to see her smile like that is encouraging.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sorry for her.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou didn\u2019t do anything wrong, in fact you did something right. So, thank you.\u201d<br /> <br /> Rime nodded.<br /> <br /> <br /> The next couple of weeks passed quickly. Once Rime was able to stay awake for longer periods of time Diane brought in some books for him to read. Sometimes he pretended to sleep while Diane sketched in her book. Felicity would come to visit occasionally as well, and Rime made her several more popsicles of different flavors. Liam also came to talk, and true to his word, Travers did not come back or even show his face in the room. The antlered man did not try and ask questions that Rime had been reluctant to answer in the past. Instead he stuck to safe topics or asked general questions about what it was like to live in the Lady\u2019s realm. Rime answered in broad terms, but did answer. He found much to his surprise that he liked the Spring Courtier and enjoyed his conversations with him.<br /> <br /> One day Liam was talking to Rime. \u201cSo, the option of that Oath is still on the table if you\u2019re interested, Rime.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat exactly would it entail?\u201d the younger man asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt would be a simple promise not to harm anyone in the freehold, including taking anyone to the Lady\u2019s realm.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou make it sound so simple.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt is. If you agree then you can go where you please as soon as you\u2019re able.\u201d Liam smiled.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat happens if I were to break the oath? What is the consequence?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe freehold would only agree on death. If we were to let you go free then we need a guarantee that you\u2019ll keep your word.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll need to think about this. If you don\u2019t mind.\u201d Rime said softly.<br /> \u201cThat\u2019s fine\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> The door opened and a young man rushed in. His wooden joints creaked as he stopped in front on Liam. \u201cWe have a situation. The mo\u2026You\u2019re needed.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay\u2026I\u2019ll go talk to the others.\u201d He said to the young manikin. He then looked at Rime. \u201cI\u2019ll have to take my leave of you for now. Jesse here will be outside your door should you need anything.\u201d He walked quickly out of the room leaving Jesse behind. <br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll be right outside.\u201d The manikin said with a tense smile.<br /> <br /> Rime nodded, his brow furrowed in confusion. As Jesse stepped out and closed the door the young elemental could hear the lock click in place and wondered what was going on. He was left alone for a short time until Jesse came in with a sandwich and glass of tea for dinner. He stayed just long enough to put the food on the table. Rime paced around the room or read one of the books that Diane had left for him. He\u2019d been reading for an hour or so when the door suddenly burst open. An unknown man came rushing in and pulled Rime to his feet.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe need the bed, quick. Step to the side.\u201d There was an edge of worry in the older man\u2019s face. Rime did as he was asked and stepped back to the corner of the room near the door.<br /> <br /> A moment later Jesse came running in carrying a small bundle covered in blood. It took a moment for Rime to realize that the small bundle was Felicity. He stood in shock and stared as Diane ran in and knelt on the floor next to the bed. She quickly assessed where the worst of the damage was and put her hands on the child\u2019s abdomen. She frowned in concentration as she poured healing energy into the small body. She worked for several minutes. Sweat started to pour off her forehead and the pale young lady just blinked through it. After what seemed like forever Diane knelt back with a sob and wrapped her arms around herself. She cried as she knelt on the floor. Jesse offered to get Liam, but Diane said that it was too late. <br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019s gone. I couldn\u2019t fix the damage fast enough.\u201d Diane cried. Jesse knelt beside the upset woman and put his arms around her shoulders. Rime stood forgotten at the back of the room and stared at the little girl lying on the bed, her eyes looking at the ceiling unseeing. The young loyalist felt a sharp twinge in his chest and he rubbed his sternum to make the feeling go away, but it did not. If anything it got worse. A moment later Liam came in and made his way over to Diane. <br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sorry I wasn\u2019t here to help.\u201d He said quietly.<br /> <br /> \u201cThere was just too much damage. She was so small.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liam nodded and pulled the sheet up over the young fawn girl after closing her eyes. <br /> <br /> \u201cHow are the others?\u201d Diane asked after a moment.<br /> <br /> \u201cThey\u2019ll be fine. Roger was the worst off, but he\u2019ll be fine in a couple of days.\u201d<br /> <br /> Rime stepped forward and cleared his throat. \u201cWhat happened?\u201d He asked quietly.<br /> <br /> Diane wiped her eyes and stood up to face the young man. \u201cIt was Rook. He came looking for both of us.\u201d<br /> \u201cWe eventually had enough people out that he figured discretion was better and he left.\u201d Liam added.<br /> <br /> Jesse looked between his two friends and Rime before clearing his own throat. \u201cI\u2019ll take care of Felicity. We\u2019ll get Sharon to handle things discreetly at the funeral parlor.\u201d He leaned over and picked up the small bundle that was the little girl and headed out the door.<br /> <br /> Liam followed the manikin with his eyes before looking back to Rime. \u201cYou better stay here for the moment. I\u2019m going to go check on things.\u201d<br /> <br /> Rime nodded and watched the Spring Courtier leave the room.<br /> <br /> Diane stayed behind and fussed with the remaining sheets, balled them up and put them in the corner of the room. The blood went through to the mattress and Diane let out a little sob. She wiped her eyes and said, \u201cI better get those sheets soaking in cold water.\u201d<br /> <br /> Rime nodded and watched her leave. He sat on the straight backed chair and looked around the room. The same room that he\u2019d gotten so used to over the past couple of weeks seemed like a foreign place now. He crossed his arms and studiously avoided looking at the blood stained mattress next to him. A few minutes later Diane came back into the room, agitated. <br /> <br /> \u201cYou need to get out of here.\u201d She said with a hint of panic in her voice.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhy? What\u2019s going on? I thought Liam wanted me to take that Oath before I left?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDamn the Oath. They\u2019re voting right now on whether or not to kill you! They say it\u2019s too risky to keep you here, alive.\u201d<br /> <br /> Rime\u2019s reply was interrupted by the sound of voices in the hallway.<br /> <br /> \u201cThey\u2019re voting now. I\u2019m confident they\u2019ll see reason and we can get rid of the damned loyalist.\u201d Travers voice sounded almost smug.<br /> <br /> \u201cI thought they were going to get him to promise not to hurt anyone?\u201d Jesse replied.<br /> <br /> \u201cAn Oath doesn\u2019t keep his shadowy buddy from showing up now does it?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI suppose not. But will killing him really stop things?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes. They\u2019ll have nothing to come back here for. Diane is too well protected and their little buddy will be dead and gone. We also won\u2019t have to worry about the little bastard doing something while he\u2019s here. It\u2019s his fault Felicity is dead. That guy only came because the loyalist was here.\u201d The ogre growled.<br /> <br /> \u201cStill doesn\u2019t feel right to me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re still young. Trust me, this way is for the best.\u201d<br /> <br /> Diane looked worriedly at Rime who had stood up and wrapped his arms around his middle. The voices outside the door quieted as the two speakers moved further down the hall.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s okay. I\u2019ve been expecting this.\u201d Rime looked at Diane.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s not fair. It\u2019s not your fault. Any of it.\u201d Diane\u2019s gaze hardened. \u201cI\u2019m not going to let them kill you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s\u2026\u201d Rime started.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo.\u201d Diane held up a hand. \u201cI\u2019m going to go talk to Travers and try and make him see reason. We may be gone for a few minutes.\u201d Diane walked up to Rime and kissed him on the cheek. \u201cYou take care of yourself, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> Rime touched his cheek surprised at the sudden warmth and nodded. Diane quickly left the room and the young man could hear her haranguing Travers about his inflexible attitude. The voices got quieter as the pair moved further still down the hall way. A moment later Rime heard Jesse mutter something about a bathroom and his footsteps sounded down the hall. The young loyalist opened the door just a crack and looked out. There was no one in the hallway, though he heard muffled voices coming from two rooms down the hall to his left. He hesitated only a moment before slipping out. He took a second to orient himself, then headed down the hall to his right towards the front door. He found a grey hoodie hanging on a coat rack and pulled it on over his shirt and pulled up the hood. He peered out the window on the front door and saw that it was getting dark out and no one was on the street. After a moment he slowly opened the front door and slipped outside. The summer night air was still humid and made Rime uncomfortably hot in the borrowed clothes, but he wanted something that would hide his face. He casually walked down the street until he got closer to the park at which point he hopped the low fence and strode purposefully toward the walking trail at the back of the park. It led further into the woods and to a Hedge gate that Rime knew about. He made half way to the gate when he heard a familiar voice call out.<br /> <br /> \u201cRime! I\u2019ve been looking for you. What happened?\u201d Rooks low voice sounded from further up the trail.<br /> <br /> Rime stopped for a second before continuing forward. They both stopped when they got closer.<br /> <br /> \u201cAre you alright?\u201d The dark figure asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m okay.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThen what kept you? You\u2019ve been gone for so long the Lady was becoming concerned that you lost your way.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI did not lose my way. I ran into trouble while trying to return Diane, er Delight. There was an ogre who beat be badly. I was just now able to get away.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIs this something that we need to take care of?\u201d Rooks voice took on a serious tone.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, they are ready for you since your earlier visit.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThey may be ready for me, but they\u2019re not ready for both of us.\u201d Rook\u2019s smile widened. \u201cCome brother, let\u2019s teach the people of this town why we are feared in Arcadia.\u201d<br /> <br /> Rime hesitated. \u201cI don\u2019t think this is a good idea.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhy not, brother? We don\u2019t have to take revenge if you don\u2019t want. Just let me know where we can find Delight and we\u2019ll take care of our original mission and leave.\u201d Rook frowned.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat do you mean, no?\u201d Rook demanded.<br /> <br /> \u201cI mean, we\u2019re not taking Delight back.\u201d Rime clenched his shaking hands.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat\u2019s gotten into your head Rime? The Lady has ordered us to return her Treasure, and that\u2019s exactly what we\u2019ll do.\u201d <br /> <br /> \u201cNo.\u201d Rime repeated.<br /> <br /> \u201cAre you betraying the Lady?\u201d Rook asked incredulously.<br /> <br /> \u201cIn that I\u2019m not going to let you take back Diane or hurt these people, then yes.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cPerhaps you were hit a bit too hard in the head by that ogre, Rime. We have a job to do.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo. I\u2019m not going to let you take Diane back.\u201d The pale man swayed slightly on his feet.<br /> <br /> \u201cRime, you\u2019re in no condition to fight me. I\u2019ll win.\u201d Rook pointed out.<br /> <br /> \u201cMaybe, but I\u2019m still not going to let you touch them.\u201d Rime said determinedly and formed a dagger of ice out of the moisture in the air with some difficulty.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou would draw a blade on me, brother?\u201d Rook drew a dagger from the sheath at his waist. \u201cYou\u2019ll have to stop me then.\u201d<br /> <br /> Rime nodded and launched himself forward holding his dagger against his arm, edge out. He feinted to the left and made an attack with his right hand. Rook blocked left and felt his brother\u2019s dagger cut him along the side. He jumped back and spun in the direction the attack had come from and launched one of his own. His twin blades flashed and Rime parried and dodged each one. His arms shook with the effort it took. He tried to hide the involuntary movement by moving his left arm into an offensive position and twirling his ice blade in the other hand.<br /> <br /> Rook took the initiative and made another attack on his friend. He attacked with each hand, Rime defending each time but missed the quick kick that lashed out and collided with his knee. Rook threw his weight behind the last attack and swept Rime\u2019s legs out from under him. Rime landed hard and tried to suppress a gasp of pain as his healing ribs were jostled. <br /> <br /> \u201cGive up now Rime. I don\u2019t really want to hurt you, but if you continue to do this I will have no choice.\u201d<br /> <br /> Rime coughed painfully and levered himself to his feet. \u201cThen do what you must, because I\u2019m not letting you take her back.\u201d<br /> <br /> Rook smiled ruefully. \u201cWhat happened to you Rime? How did they get you to turn against the Lady?\u201d<br /> <br /> Rime shook his head. \u201cYou killed a little girl Rook. She was only twelve. How could she have possibly been a threat?\u201d <br /> <br /> \u201cCollateral damage.\u201d Rook replied. \u201cYou know how it goes. Sometimes people get caught in the crossfire. They don\u2019t matter though. Only the mission matters.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut she did matter Rook. She was just a little girl.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe was one of \u2018them\u2019 Rime. One of those that betrayed their masters and ran away. She shouldn\u2019t have been here anyway.\u201d<br /> <br /> The pale knight swayed on his feet but stood blocking the path to town. \u201cThen you\u2019ll have to come through me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo be it.\u201d Rook\u2019s expression hardened and he attacked twice in quick succession. Rime realized that the attacks before were almost gentle compared to this. He dodged the first strike but the second got through. He gripped his side where Rook\u2019s blade had cut deep. He lashed out with an attack of his own and tried to drive his one-time brother back toward the trees. Rook stepped back and Rime pressed the attack again. The younger man thought he\u2019d gotten close enough but when his knife flashed out it hit nothing but air. Rook danced to the side and kicked up leaves and twigs from the side of the path. Rime\u2019s hand immediately went to block the detritus and suddenly realized his mistake. He tried to step back but was too slow. Rook stepped forward and grabbed Rime\u2019s shoulder with one hand and plunged a dagger into the younger man\u2019s gut with the other. Rime gasped in shock.<br /> <br /> \u201cNow, do you yield brother?\u201d Rook asked the younger man as he withdrew his knife.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo.\u201d Rime coughed. <br /> <br /> \u201cVery well.\u201d Rook rasped and his blades flashed two more times. Rime felt the first strike hit up and under his ribs while the second took him in the shoulder.<br /> <br /> Rime staggered and his knees started to buckle. His own blade fell from nerveless fingers and hit the forest floor. Rook sheathed his knives in one swift movement and stepped forward to catch Rime as he started to fall. He pulled Rime\u2019s uninjured shoulder over his own and put his other arm around Rime\u2019s waist.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2026can\u2019t\u2026have\u2026her\u2026\u201d Rime rasped, blood flecked on his lips.<br /> <br /> \u201cFor now brother. Right now I need to bring you to the Lady. She will want to know of your betrayal.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou could \u2026just\u2026 leave\u2026 me here.\u201d Rime said quietly.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, I can\u2019t.\u201d Rook replied and started walking toward the gate. Rime stumbled as his feet staggered forward. He couldn\u2019t seem to get his legs to work properly. Three more steps and he tripped over a root, slipped out of Rook\u2019s grasp and fell hard to his knees. He caught himself on his good arm and wrapped the other around his middle.<br /> <br /> \u201cCan\u2019t\u2026walk\u2026\u201d Rime choked out.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019ve suffered worse. You can walk.\u201d Rook reached down and grabbed his brother\u2019s shoulder.<br /> <br /> Rime smiled sadly and his teeth were bloody. \u201cNot\u2026this time\u2026Rook.\u201d He coughed hard and grabbed the shadowed hand. His breathes came in short gasps as he struggled to take his next breath.<br /> <br /> \u201cShit.\u201d Rook swore and leaned down to pick up his friend in a fireman\u2019s carry. He walked with quick purpose to the gate and strode through to get to his Lady\u2019s palace.<br /> <br /> In the world a sudden thunderstorm sprung up and washed the ground clean of blood or any sign of a fight. And a loan dagger made of ice slowly melted as the warm rain came down.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Next week we return to the drama with Lorelei, Calamity and Insincere Marguerite. I hope you enjoyed the story and I will see you then. Comments and Questions welcome.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.t