ssic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T10:29:07-07:00","id":869412,"title":"","content":"Welcome aboard, Master Aquatosic! Glad to have you.<br /> <br /> Lorelei's player here. Feel free to ask questions, make comments, or rail against the decisions made in-character as you like. I think I speak for the whole group when I say that we love knowing people are reading these journals, and your enthusiasm for the material is most appreciated!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T11:24:55-07:00","id":869458,"title":"","content":"Greetings and welcome to the Malibu Dream House. It is always a pleasure to know folks are reading and enjoying the journals. As Lori's player has said, we love comments and questions so feel free.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T13:12:02-07:00","id":869589,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the kind greetings. Mostly just loving this, but I did have one question. Why does Ace not get so many POV journals? We know about his jovial energy, his charisma and his Durance, but I would love to have a better look inside his crazy, scaly head. He's much less ...angry than the stereotypical Summer Courtier, at least on the outside. <br /> <br /> Is his player just missing a lot of games? Or is he actually an NPC?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T10:57:03-07:00","id":870351,"title":"","content":"From my understanding, Ace's player just doesn't really do them; not every player in the Baroness' games make journals from their characters' perspective, though there is an incentive to do so. For one, it gives a better amount of memory to the games, and for another there's a small XP reward for doing them (I think). However, given how busy people are, or how creativeness has its roadblocks, even that sometimes isn't enough to really do them.<br /> <br /> Sadly, Ace's player seems to be having a difficulty getting free time for the games, hence why he's not appearing in the others' journals for swaths at a time. It's a shame, really. De La Rocha has since temporarily semi-filled his spot in the motley as a Summer courtier, but as far as I know Ace as a character is still present in the motley and the Dreamhouse at large. He's just assumed as being Ace and doing things that aren't documented.<br /> <br /> Bear in mind, I'm an outsider in all this so my word is very far from official on the matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T11:48:02-07:00","id":870406,"title":"","content":"that makes sense. Maybe I'll make some fan journals. His inner monologue could be fascinating. What emotions drove him to join the Summer court, when his persona is just so Spring Court? Anger at being treated like an animal for so long? A desire to find and protect the girl who helped him escape? Attraction to their over-the-top do-or-die attitude?<br /> <br /> His backstory journal took a very interesting tone that left me fascinated with what was going on inside the darker parts of his scaly head","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T12:07:46-07:00","id":870434,"title":"","content":"Master Aquatosic:<br /> <br /> the short version of my post is &quot;Taidragon is right about everything.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ace's Player: When Ace's player joined, they regularly played on that night, but some difficulties with job situation and their recently being a parent made it so they missed sessions frequently. This meant he made about as often as he missed. When his job situation shifted, Sunday became the only day he could really spend with his family. So for now he is not in any Sunday games, which MDH is. If things change again he could show again, but I am not holding my breath. He is currently playing in <i>Night Train Detective Agency</i> for <b>Demon</b> which is a very late game since he does not have to work on Sunday, but that is his only game at the moment. We are all in our 30s or 40s so this is just a reality of play. <i>Malibu Dream House</i> is actually not in my own game room but two players' house as they have a child and this lets both them play rather than one staying home and missing.<br /> <br /> Journals: I give 1XP for doing journals. if the whole group does them (who attended the session) an extra 1XP goes to the group fund. Groups normally gain 1 Group XP for the fund they can spend per session, on stuff like Hollow (and all the sub-areas) Bastian (and all the sub-areas) Harvest, Resources (for the house) etc, but nothing for a personal PC. <i>Malibu Dream House</i> is the only game I run which regularly has journals from everyone. I mentioned <i>Night Train</i> above, with normally around 2 journals per session of 5 regularly making players (though one of those journals, Speed Demon's, is written as a noir detective fiction covering all the events from the game with or without Speed, and my god it is good). <i>Golden Eagle</i> has 3-4 journals of 7 players. This is largely due to, as Taidragon noted, busyness or creative roadblocks. A lot of us have kids. Some have jobs where working on journals at work is just fine, others have jobs where that is impossible, dangerous, or could get them in real trouble. Some just see them as homework. Some of us are in several games and have to pick and choose which ones to journal for (There are nine games being run in our extended group right now, I am running four, one person is running three. I am not even running all the CoD games, there is another Changeling game out there).<br /> <br /> I prefer 3 journals to a game. That tends to cover everything going on. <i>Night Train</i> I am less worried about (as noted, Speed covers everything and her journals are frequently around 20 typed pages by themselves.) but outside that 3 tends to work. More is unusual, but I have been very fortunate with <i>Malibu Dream House</i>, and 4 is not unusual for <i>Golden Eagle</i>.<br /> <br /> Does that answer everything? Your questions and comments are of course appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T12:34:21-07:00","id":870465,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answer","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T15:21:00-07:00","id":870694,"title":"","content":"Man, who would have thought a forum story could educate me about the philosophies behind open relationships. I'm not sure I fully understand it yet, since I don't have a proper definition of Love (who does?), but the way Calamity/Gawain and Lori/D talk about it is teaching me a lot. I mean, it really makes sense in the first case. Instead of forcing Gawain to do something he'll never be comfortable with, Calamity can have a few flings on the side to satisfy that portion of her. it's a very elegant solution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T01:27:06-07:00","id":871049,"title":"","content":"So...<br /> <br /> There is a lot of things I hoped to expose my players to and possibly by extension, readers, in my various games. Glimpses into LGBT culture, how we are and how society sometimes treats us or dealing with a friend who is doing drugs. BDSM in a realistic context. Things like that. With female heavy casts, large numbers of LGBTs among the PCs and NPCs and in <i>Golden Eagle'</i>s case, viewing eras like the 1920s through a queer or female-focused lens.<br /> <br /> Polyamory was never really something I planned to have as a focus, but it is in damn near all my CoD games. So that's interesting. I have polyamorous friends, but no firsthand knowledge of polyamorous relationships, but it has been interesting especially here to see how those have matured and people adapted. As in all things it comes down to communication and trying to balance everyone's needs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T02:27:04-07:00","id":871068,"title":"","content":"As Calamity's player, thank you for the compliment on Calamity and Gawain's relationship.<br /> <br /> In a nut shell, Calamity simply does not view sexual interest/attraction and love as being intrinsically connected. She loves people that she doesn't lust after (such as Insincere Marguerite) and there are certainly people she's lusted after that she does not love or even like (I am looking at you Lucien Torrez) I'll admit, it's something that she has because it's a trait I have and it fits her disinclination to follow rules or traditions or social conventions. There is also a bit of her self esteem worked in that she feels Gawain deserves someone 'better' then her, but that's another issue. <br /> <br /> Of course, because she loves Gawain, she would be faithful if he wanted her to be. After all, people do things for love they wouldn't do otherwise. (Or as Calamity is fond of putting it, Love makes you stupid.)<br /> <br /> Calamity's interest in women is similarly fueled in part by her rebellious nature but also somewhat by being in a relationship with Gawain. She's less inclined toward other men because she's serous with him. And now that things have deepened with Becky, she's been a bit less actively looking on that front as well. Since, on a deep level, she still wants that romantic happy ever after she dreamed about before being taken. (even if she won't admit to wanting something so very normal)<br /> <br /> So, given her issues, it is a remarkably healthy relationship (I think in large part to Gawain being such a decent guy) Sadly, recent events may be sending her into a bit a backspin on her personal issues, as harming a loved one is pretty much the root of her guilt and self-loathing. <br /> <br /> But we shall see what unfolds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T11:48:36-07:00","id":871554,"title":"","content":"As far as Lori goes; well, she was originally intended to be a character who shied away from serious relationships and was more into instant gratification. Like all of my most memorable characters, she soon rebelled against my intentions and took on a life of her own. From pretty much the instant she met de la Rocha, her &quot;free agent&quot; status was out the window. Her relationship with Marguerite and Julia developed a little more slowly; they evolved from friends to lovers to lovers she genuinely cared about gradually over time. Oleander was another unexpected bolt of lightning, frankly, and blindsided me as much as Lorelei.<br /> <br /> By and large Lori is very happy in her multiple relationships, though she still thinks of D as her first love, and has intimated on several occasions that if her lifestyle ever becomes not okay with D, she'll take the plunge and sever romantic ties with the others. As her next journal will show, however, now that someone else has caught de la Rocha's eye in a serious way, Lori is finding that there are some aspects of polyamory that she might not be so cool with after all.<br /> <br /> Thanks again for reading and commenting!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T12:40:56-07:00","id":871615,"title":"","content":"Oleander certainly blindsided me. But let's be honest here, I suspect Oleander was blindsided the most.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T13:32:17-07:00","id":873252,"title":"","content":"All is not well in the Dream House. The Darklings still are not on speaking terms and jealousy is beginning to rear it\u2019s head elsewhere. While the Motley focuses inward, things continue to broil from without.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LIV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> November 9th, evening<br /> <br /> Man. If anyone took a look at my hands, they\u2019d think I was a very clumsy... paper shuffler? I dunno, that metaphor got away from me, but I am getting a collection of paper cut looking wounds. The Contract of Potential, you know, the Martyr\u2019s Will clause, has come in handy these past bit. Not, like, essential, but I like to think it\u2019s helped keep spirits going strong and all. Even so, I don\u2019t have to shed blood, it\u2019s not like I\u2019m Glamour starved, but it makes it feel more real, you know?<br /> <br /> But I\u2019m going all over the place, as usual. The show last night went well, for the most part. The stage part definitely. Lori was just, you know, amazing. I think she was showing off for Annika. Insincere Marguerite\u2019s debut of \u2018Je ne regrette rein\u2019 was awesome too. I think we all gave her a little boost, but I'm sure she'd have hit it out of the park anyway. Calamity didn\u2019t get to see it and was a little bummed, but she was worried about stressing Insincere Marguerite out, you know? She and Annika stepped out for cigars.<br /> <br /> I guess I\u2019ve mentioned it a few times now, but Annika was there, obviously, which was a little weird, since she\u2019s usually only by when she is performing or teaching Calamity. But she\u2019d heard the night before that, you know, Calamity wasn\u2019t doing so well, so she came by to try and keep her spirits up. Becky stuck around too and even stayed the night.<br /> <br /> It was nice having backup since Calamity really wasn\u2019t doing super still. Especially not after Moon came by with the news. I was happy to see hir - well, at first I was nervous to, since we hadn\u2019t precisely left on, you know, the best terms last time. Ze seemed a little nervous for hir part too, but we were cool when ze left. Anyway, hir news was that Gunnar - who\u2019d been out of contact for a month apparently - showed up at the Lighthouse and insisted that he should be there for Chalcedony\u2019s Dreamhealing. He kept insisting even after being told no in no uncertain terms and then Molly popped out from being invisible with a gun to his head.<br /> <br /> So Gunnar shrank to about 2 feet tall and Molly shot, cause that counts of moving I guess, and then they had a whole big fight. Eventually they both turned invisible and left. Well, they probably left since Queen Charlotte came out a little later and demanded they show themselves and they, you know, didn\u2019t. They\u2019d been looking into it, the Autumn Court folks - Boss Lowjack just said Molly was doing her part of the Winter Court\u2019s duties, and Lucien claimed Gunnar hadn\u2019t been out of contact, but working for him and wouldn\u2019t say how. So, that was great.<br /> <br /> Well, mostly it was a mess, but no one seemed to have gotten hurt, you know, yet. Still, Calamity did not take kindly to hearing that Molly had started a fight with an Autumn Courtier at the Lighthouse, or that Boss Lowjack was being cagey about it. But she fixed the glass she broke, and we managed to talk her down, the three of us. I do think it left Calamity feeling kinda, you know, fragile. She let Jacob make the rounds anyway.<br /> <br /> The next day, after the night of drinking Calamity\u2019d had, and to celebrate Insincere Marguerite\u2019s awesome performance, sex breakfast was blueberry pancakes and heavily loaded scrambled eggs with gouda, one of Insincere Marguerite\u2019s favorites. It went over well, I think. All and all, everyone seemed at least a little on, you know, an evener keel. Insincere Marguerite even joined us, with Calamity there. She didn\u2019t really, you know, engage with Calamity at all, of her own will, but she was there. De la Roche had gone with Lori to church and that seemed to have gone well also. De la Roche\u2019s outfit certainly did. I\u2019m not sure any of the ladies weren\u2019t drooling over her suit and purple tie combo.<br /> <br /> We did talk some about the Day/Night crowns. Julia attempted to give an explanation for why the Monarchs feared such a thing so greatly. And they do have a great fear, that this freehold should go the way of LA, where the Seasons lost their power to the Diurnal cycle. And so the Monarchs here, in an effort to maintain their power where LA\u2019s Seasons failed, speak of driving off or killing the Day and Night Courtiers that make this their home. It is as if they have no confidence that their subjects would follow the dogma presented to them by the Seasons, given their own truly free choice. It would seem to me that if the only way to maintain their power is to slaughter those who disagree, then perhaps they do not deserve to have any power...<br /> <br /> But. But. Focus. Julia had spoken with Queen Charlotte, who, to her credit, was interested very much in protecting Insincere Marguerite as the Dread Esquire. Which, you know, is not the biggest thing in, like, an overall view of morality, to only protect people you\u2019re, you know, fond of, but given that it is Insincere Marguerite were talking about, I\u2019m not gonna fuss. She\u2019s been pushing the other Monarchs to agree to not go with the whole killing Diurnal Courtiers. Princess Joli feels kinda similar to Queen Charlotte, I guess, just mirrored, since she wants to protect Felicity and distrusts Insincere Marguerite. Boss Lowjack does wanna drive out the Diurnal folks, but with incentives, rather than violence, so, I guess that\u2019s better? And Viscount Augustine is \u2018listening to the will of his people\u2019, so I dunno what that might mean.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it hasn\u2019t happened yet, so I guess we\u2019ll see. Other, more immediate things got a little, you know, tense at the end of breakfast, when Calamity pushed Insincere Marguerite a little hard about fixing things. Julia was just about to explode. I can\u2019t really blame her, really any of the hers involved, I guess, but hopefully Calamity can be a little patient, until Insincere Marguerite gets the distance she needs.<br /> <br /> Desiree tried to help with that, suggesting a trip for ice cream for those of us left behind when Insincere Marguerite and Julia went up to the roof and Lori went to help De la Roche get her shirt off. Gloria stayed behind at the House though, probably to hang out with De la Roche. And to avoid Desiree. Jacob and Calamity had a talk first, long enough that Becky and Desiree started making up one of those fanfics Calamity talks about sometimes, about the two of them. It was really, you know, weird? But it was kinda nice, right, to see Becky forget she didn\u2019t like Desiree.<br /> <br /> Ice cream was great - the place Desiree suggested had Rocky Road, my favorite. The news we got there was not so great - Jacob got a call from Boss Lowjack just as a story came on the TV, that a weapons cache downtown had exploded, which was perhaps related to a car explosion outside a bar called Lowjack\u2019s. Boss Lowjack told Jacob that things had, you know, escalated after the things with Molly and Gunnar. So, that was exciting. It\u2019s not our problem though, not right now.<br /> <br /> What was more our problem was what Lori told us when we got back. Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne had backed out of performing for a time, until she could feel comfortable in our domain again. I can scarcely blame the lady, given her continued lack of knowledge as to what was happening and why, seeing as the raw details of the matter were truly damning. I do not understand Lady Grace\u2019s reluctance to reveal the truth to one we know to be a close friend of Chalcedony\u2019s. I do understand that the prejudice against the Director\u2019s Changelings would make it inadvisable to connect the two in the public eye. However, that detail is not necessary to resolve Lady Beaumont\u2019s confusion, or the confusion of others. The rest however - I do not care what the Monarchs wish hidden...<br /> <br /> Still. I thought, you know, since we keep having problems with communication among, you know, us, that we should hash it out. We agreed that explaining that she had a magical effect lingering on her from her Keeper, to anyone who already knew where things stood from, you know, an outside perspective, was OK with everyone. It really does explain the actions taken, without letting on the anything that might imply anything along the lines of loyalist like the words \u2018the Director\u2019 do.<br /> <br /> I went to the forge after that, to try and work out the... tension, which doesn\u2019t seem to have, you know, worked so great. Poor Calamity came looking for me after a while, frustrated that Insincere Marguerite wasn\u2019t letting Julia yell at or hit her. Bottling up emotions usually isn\u2019t, you know, the best idea, but I gotta trust that Insincere Marguerite and Julia know what\u2019s best for them. I hope I was able to convince Calamity.<br /> <br /> We got interrupted before we could relax with a nice shower, me, Calamity and Becky, by De la Roche, who\u2019d found out Gloria had been programmed by Hollywood. De la Roche had found some notes on us, and confirmed with Desiree - I guess even her, you know, handwriting changed when acting under the compulsion kinda thing. I used one of Calamity\u2019s shards to spill a few drops of blood to focus our wills and we got down to it.<br /> <br /> As unfortunate as it was, it did kinda feel nice to have a problem we could do something productive about. I let Calamity take the lead, since she, you know, really needed the chance to do something good, and we rocked it. The brainwashing wasn\u2019t as extensive as it was for Desiree - they didn\u2019t have the Director\u2019s scripts to crib from. She was just supposed to gather what she could, then leave it in a dead drop. We managed to convince her to \u2018cut the strings\u2019 and free herself. Now we\u2019re just waiting for her to wake and probably to do some more explaining.<br /> <br /> Here\u2019s hoping that things keep looking up.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> I don\u2019t really know how to characterize the last few days; it\u2019s been an emotional roller-coaster ride, with every heartbreak followed by a triumph, every gain sliding into a terrible loss. While I\u2019m more hopeful that our motley will survive the current storm, it\u2019s beginning to look like the debacle with Chalcedony is going to have far-reaching consequences, and the situation with Gloria has become more\u2026 \u201ccomplicated\u201d as well.<br /> <br /> So in any case we spent the rest of yesterday afternoon getting ready for the show, which was a welcome distraction from the fact that the next morning I was planning to introduce my father/preacher to the love of my life, who happens to be a punk Chicana girl with anger management issues. Add to that the fact that Calamity seemed intent on pushing Marguerite into a conversation before she was ready, and I think I was holding up remarkably well under the circumstances.<br /> <br /> So I got dolled up and headed backstage to make sure the rest of the performers were ready to bring their A-game (Saturday night is one of our biggest shows, after all). After I was reasonably certain that our talent was in-line, I wandered out to mingle a little among the crowd, as usual. I saw D standing off to one side, glancing again and again at a table where Gloria and Halley were sitting, and trying not to be obvious about it.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat\u2019s up?\u201d I asked her as I approached.<br /> <br /> \u201cI wonder what\u2019s going on between those two,\u201d she explained with a hint of concern in her voice. \u201cI didn\u2019t think they even knew each other, but they\u2019re chatting like old friends.\u201d<br /> <br /> I could feel the evil smirk hit my face, but there was nothing I could do about it. \u201cWhy, D?\u201d I asked sweetly, \u201cAre you <u><u>jealous</u>?\u201d </u><br /> <br /> \u201cOf course not,\u201d she snapped, not meeting my eyes.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou<u> <u>are!</u> </u>\u201d I taunted her quietly, \u201cD, that\u2019s so <u><u>cute!</u> </u>\u201d<br /> <br /> She sighed and gave me a weary look. \u201cWhy are you doing this to me?\u201d she asked plaintively, blushing.<br /> <br /> I leaned in and kissed her nose. \u201cBecause I like watching you turn all those pretty colors, babe,\u201d I said with a laugh.<br /> <br /> She glared at me, but it was a glare of love. I can tell.<br /> <br /> In any case, the two of us made our way to their table, and discovered after a few moments of conversation that Halley was there on Monica\u2019s behalf. Our green gal-pal had been planning to introduce Gloria around to a few people this evening, but had begged off at the last minute for \u201cpersonal reasons,\u201d and had asked Halley to make her apologies and do what she could for Gloria. Halley either didn\u2019t know or didn\u2019t want to say what was going on with Monica. I hope everything is okay. Maybe D and I should make some time to hang out with her in the next few days. I\u2019ve missed our workouts, anyway.<br /> <br /> I had to cut the conversation short as curtain approached, and I made my way backstage. I performed a few of my old standbys last night, and tried out one new number as well: a smoky torch-style rendition of the Elvis Presley classic \u201cI Can\u2019t Help Falling In Love.\u201d There wasn\u2019t much staging; just me in a slinky evening gown lounging on a chair, but it seemed to go over well regardless. I\u2019ll have to think about adding it in to the regular rotation.<br /> <br /> I admit that I put a lot of effort into my number tonight, and I\u2019m not too proud to own up to the fact that part of that was because Annika was there checking up on Calamity. I don\u2019t know why I feel the need to assert myself in her presence. Of course I find her superior attitude off-putting, and it\u2019s no secret that I\u2019m jealous of her skills as a dancer, but, well\u2026 she\u2019s honestly never been anything but civil to me. She certainly hasn\u2019t done anything to deserve the sort of hostility I can\u2019t help feeling around her. I should probably work on that before it leads me to do something I\u2019ll regret.<br /> <br /> And speaking of regret, Marguerite still regrets nothing, and her number went just as well last night as it had at her debut. I did what I could to help her out using contracts\u2026 mostly because I thought her funk over the situation with Calamity might adversely affect her performance. I think Gawain might have done something similar. I\u2019m not sure if our magic helped her performance or if what we saw was just her natural talent shining through, but either way her act was spectacular.<br /> <br /> Things wound down pretty quickly after the show; most of the motley wasn\u2019t really in an entertaining mood, and I think the crowd picked up on that. Oh, we weren\u2019t rude; we didn\u2019t chivvy people out the door as soon as the bows were taken or anything like that. It just seemed to me that our patrons didn\u2019t hang around as much as they usually do, and cleanup didn\u2019t take very long either. In light of what happened the next day, I\u2019m starting to wonder if there was a reason the place cleared out quickly.<br /> <br /> We were hanging out at the bar, waiting for the last of the mortal patrons to slip away when Gawain walked up with some disturbing news. Moon had told him that there had been trouble at the Lighthouse earlier. Gunnar Friday showed up and demanded to know what they were doing with Chalcedony. When they wouldn\u2019t allow him access to her, he became very agitated, and claimed that it was vital that he know what had been done to Chalcedony, and what the Autumn Court was doing about it. Eventually Molly Nuit materialized behind him holding a gun to his head. He reacted badly to this (understandably, in my opinion), and used a power to sort of reflexively shrink to about three feet tall. Molly fired over his head, and after a few shots were exchanged in both directions, they each disappeared into thin air. The Autumn Court is pretty sure they both fled the area after that, as Queen Charlotte issued a direct command for them to show themselves, and neither one did.<br /> <br /> So things are heating up in the Freehold over the Chalcedony thing. I really hope the Autumn Court can do something to help her, and that things can get back to normal soon. As the events of the next day proved, though, this is far from over. Lucien Torrez won\u2019t just take an attack on one of his people lying down, and Boss Lowjack is unlikely to budge from his position either.<br /> <br /> D and I checked in on Marguerite and Julia, who had retired to their bedroom as soon as Marguerite\u2019s lighting duties were complete. They seemed a bit better, but both were obviously still shaken by what happened on Friday. They even shared an anecdote that would have been amusing if it hadn\u2019t been so sad. Apparently Calamity approached Julia earlier in an effort to apologize for the harm she had done to Marguerite. In an effort to prevent further scenes, Marguerite had ordered Julia not to speak to Calamity at all. As she was unwilling to go against this directive, Julia was forced to respond to Calamity\u2019s contrition via pantomime.<br /> <br /> Sometimes I worry about the amount of control Marguerite has over Julia.<br /> <br /> In any case, Marguerite wasn\u2019t quite up to our usual bedroom shenanigans, so D and I made our way back to our room, stripped down, and climbed into bed. I snuggled against my honey\u2019s back, feeling her heartbeat and the warmth of her skin. That\u2019s usually enough to put me in a place of deep contentment, so I rarely have trouble sleeping (once we\u2019ve both settled down for the evening, of course). Last night, however, I just couldn\u2019t seem to settle my mind. I was too nervous about bringing D to church the next morning.<br /> <br /> What\u2019s more, the agitated quivering of my wings kept D awake as well. Eventually, she sort of sighed, turned around, and kissed my neck. \u201cHey, Lori,\u201d she whispered softly, \u201cit\u2019s going to be okay. You\u2019ll see. I promise I\u2019ll behave, and you already know your dad is okay with our relationship. Nothing to worry about, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled weakly. \u201cRight,\u201d I said simply. \u201cOnly\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat is it?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ve been thinking about what you said\u2026 about telling my dad who I really am. I think you\u2019re right. I have to do it. I have to tell him the truth while we still have this time together.\u201d<br /> <br /> She leaned in to give me a tender kiss. \u201cGood,\u201d she said once we\u2019d separated. \u201cI\u2019m glad you\u2019ve come to see it that way. But there\u2019s nothing saying you have to do all this at once, you know. Let\u2019s take it one step at a time and see what happens.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cBut\u2026 you\u2019ll come back to the church with me when I tell him, right?\u201d I asked. \u201cI\u2019m going to need your support.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cSi, Juliette, I promise I\u2019ll be there whenever you need me.\u201d Then she rolled over and sniffed, and said in a mock-huffy tone \u201cnow let\u2019s get some sleep for Chrissakes. We\u2019ve got church tomorrow.\u201d<br /> <br /> I chuckled and dutifully tried to get some sleep, but it was no use, and I was still awake when the alarm went off a few hours later. D grumbled and wheedled and threw a pillow at me, but eventually I managed to use my contracts to pep her up a bit, and the two of us got dressed for church. I wore one of my usual sober long dresses, tied my hair back, and put on my glasses, while D opted for a black suit with a white shirt and a purple tie. <br /> <br /> She looked good. I mean, <u><u>really</u></u> good. I bit my lip and muttered that we had better get going before my libido got the better of me.<br /> <br /> Of course, as a choirgirl, I don\u2019t actually sit with the rest of the congregation in the sanctuary, so D had to fend for herself through the sermon. She quickly located a small group of Hispanic parishioners and joined them in their little corner while I went to put my robes on.<br /> <br /> Of course, my honey\u2019s arrival hadn\u2019t gone unnoticed. \u201cDid you see the girl with the purple hair sitting with the Corazon family?\u201d Sandra asked as soon as she arrived. \u201cI mean, she\u2019s pretty enough, but she\u2019s wearing a <u><u>suit</u></u>! A <u><u>man\u2019s</u></u> suit,\u201d she added in a hushed voice. \u201cI wonder if she\u2019s a neighbor of theirs, or a relative or something.\u201d<br /> <br /> I sighed, resigned, and spoke up. \u201cShe\u2019s my girlfriend,\u201d I said quietly. Conversations stopped on a dime all around the room.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh,\u201d Sandra said, obviously stunned. \u201cWell, like I said\u2026 she\u2019s lovely,\u201d she sort of stammered out.<br /> <br /> Things sort of went back to normal after that. A few people who are usually quite friendly with me seemed to be avoiding me, but I\u2019m honestly not sure if that\u2019s real or just my imagination\u2026 and even if it is real, I\u2019m clear-headed enough to know that there\u2019s a difference between being uncomfortable with something and disapproving of it. I\u2019ll just let things settle down for a bit and see how I stand within the church.<br /> <br /> Glenda came up to me in a quiet corner as people were preparing to head into the loft. \u201cSo, when you say that she\u2019s your \u2018girlfriend,\u2019\u201d she began hesitantly, \u201cdo you mean like \u2018we hang out a lot and had a spa day last winter,\u2019 or, like\u2026\u201d she stammered for a minute before making up her mind. \u201cAre you gay, Lorelei?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> I shrugged. \u201cBisexual, I think,\u201d I answered. \u201cI\u2019m in love with her, anyway, if that\u2019s what you\u2019re asking.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGood for you,\u201d she grinned shyly. \u201cI snuck a peek after Sandra\u2019s little gossip session. She\u2019s gorgeous!\u201d Then she squeezed my shoulder and the two of us joined the line to enter the loft.<br /> <br /> So that was nice.<br /> <br /> After the sermon, I found D in the sanctuary and the two of us joined the crowd of people around my dad. When the throng had thinned out a bit, I took her by the hand and led her up to speak with him.<br /> <br /> \u201cReverend Wells?\u201d I asked tentatively.<br /> <br /> As usual, his craggy face split into a guileless grin when he saw me. \u201cLorelei, my dear!\u201d he greeted me cheerfully. \u201cAnd who is your lovely companion?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThis is Maria de la Rocha, sir,\u201d I said softly, \u201cshe\u2019s my girlfriend.\u201d<br /> <br /> He took her hand warmly and gave it a firm shake. \u201cI am very pleased to meet you at last, Miss de la Rocha,\u201d he said earnestly. \u201cLorelei speaks very highly of you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you, sir,\u201d D replied with a nervous smile. \u201cShe\u2019s a very special girl, and it means a lot to her \u2013 to both of us \u2013 that you\u2019ve been so accepting of our circumstances.\u201d<br /> <br /> Dad shook his head. \u201cNot at all, my dear. Even an old fool like me can see that you\u2019ve made our Lorelei very happy. She is one of the most talented members of our congregation, and as such her happiness is important to me.\u201d<br /> <br /> D\u2019s grin turned effortless, and she chucked him lightly on the shoulder. \u201cYou\u2019re all right, padre,\u201d she said affably. \u201cI like you. If more of the priests had been like you when I was growing up, well\u2026 my life might have turned out differently.\u201d<br /> <br /> Dad quirked an eyebrow at that. \u201cRegrets, Miss de la Rocha?\u201d he asked.<br /> <br /> She looked at me and smiled with a shimmer in her eyes. \u201cNo sir,\u201d she replied slowly, \u201cnone at all.\u201d<br /> <br /> I arranged to meet with dad privately next Sunday after church. I\u2019m hoping I can work up my courage to tell him the truth by then. With D by my side, I <u><u>think</u></u> I can do this. I just hope I don\u2019t royally fuck up what I\u2019ve found here in Malibu.<br /> <br /> So I finally allowed myself to breathe a sigh of relief as we drove back to the Dream House. \u201cI think that went well,\u201d I said when we were about halfway home.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah,\u201d D nodded soberly. \u201cIt was touch and go for a little while there. I swear I had the strangest urge to blurt out something like \u2018did you know I was going down on your daughter a few hours ago, sir?\u2019 but I managed to rein myself in.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThus ensuring that you will have further opportunities to go down on his daughter in the future,\u201d I commented wryly, without looking at the shit-eating grin I knew would be splitting her face in half.<br /> <br /> When we got back to the Dream House, sex breakfast was in full blast, and a serious discussion of the situation with the Diurnal crowns was just beginning. Julia \u2013 when she could stop herself from staring at D in her suit \u2013 was attempting to explain why this scenario was so frightening to the local monarchs. It seems that something similar happened in L.A. a few years back, and the seasonal courts ended up losing most of their power to the Day and Night monarchs, which led to nothing but trouble. Everyone is a little worried that a similar situation might crop up here.<br /> <br /> On the plus side, it looks like most of the monarchs are taking a sensible view on this. Charlotte and Jolie are both in favor of fostering good working relationships with the rising Day and Night monarchs rather than attempting to stop the crowns from manifesting. Admittedly, this mostly seems to be because each of them is known to be fond of one of the emerging monarchs\u2026 Charlotte and Marguerite have a good relationship, and Jolie and Felicity have obviously been close. Boss Lowjack wants to try to lure Day and Night courtiers out of the area with incentives and deals rather than violence, and I guess that could work with someone as intelligent and crafty as him making the arrangements. Viscount Augustine is reputedly \u201clistening to the will of his people,\u201d which is a little ominous to say the least.<br /> <br /> After breakfast, things got a little tense between Marguerite and Calamity again, and Desiree suggested that she, Calamity, Jacob, and Gawain go out for ice cream together. It sounded like fun, but D and I were still in our church clothes, and I had a different sort of treat in mind. Julia and Marguerite went up to the roof to relax for a bit as D and I helped each other change, and I made good on the insinuations I had made during the drive back (I couldn\u2019t help it, okay? She\u2019s just so damned sexy in a suit!).<br /> <br /> When we made it back downstairs, we found Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne speaking softly with Gloria. In fact, she had the poor blonde nearly pinned to a wall and was presumably making some pretty forward suggestions, if the blush on Gloria\u2019s cheeks was any indication. D moved in snarling to separate the two of them (my, she\u2019s gotten possessive about the new girl, hasn\u2019t she?), and Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne backed away with a good natured shrug.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo what can we do for you, Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne?\u201d I asked to break the tension.<br /> <br /> It didn\u2019t work. Her face sort of fell, and she looked like she was about to perform a distasteful duty. \u201cSorry about this, Lori,\u201d she said after a moment, \u201cbut I don\u2019t think I\u2019m comfortable performing here right now.\u201d<br /> <br /> It wasn\u2019t entirely unexpected. Once word of Chalcedony\u2019s situation had spread, I knew we were likely to see some backlash. \u201cI understand,\u201d I said as calmly as I could. \u201cI won\u2019t pretend to be happy about it, but I respect your decision. I\u2026 can\u2019t really go into details about what happened here on Friday, but I want you to know that we did everything we could to prevent it, and none of us were happy about the way it went down.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded in acknowledgement. \u201cI get that,\u201d she said after a moment, \u201cbut Chalcedony is my friend, and from what I hear she was pretty much knocked out, restrained, and dragged away on the monarch\u2019s orders. That\u2019s not okay. It went down here, and\u2026 I just don\u2019t feel comfortable here anymore.\u201d<br /> <br /> I wanted to rail at her. I wanted to scream that we were trying to <u><u>help</u></u> Chalcedony to overcome the Director\u2019s programming; that when the Autumn Court was done with her she\u2019d be more herself than ever before. I wanted to tell her that the violent aspects of her capture and transfer were a horrible mistake, that we all felt terrible about it, and that it was even now ripping our motley apart. I wanted to cry, because I felt like I\u2019d lost something really important\u2026 the trust of the Freehold.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t do any of those things, of course. Chalcedony hasn\u2019t made it public that her Keeper was the Director. Queen Charlotte has kept what she\u2019s doing under wraps, so she obviously feels that secrecy is important. And the tension between Calamity and Marguerite is nobody else\u2019s damned business. Those are not my secrets to tell, and I wasn\u2019t about to blurt them out just to save one of our headliners.<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cI\u2019m not getting rid of your contract, though,\u201d I said as evenly as I could. \u201cWe\u2019ll call it a leave of absence for now, okay? I hope, once more of the circumstances have come to light and you\u2019ve had a little time to think about it, you\u2019ll change your mind and come back to us.\u201d<br /> <br /> Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne nodded glumly. \u201cI hope so too,\u201d she said, and she took her leave. At the door, she took my hand and squeezed it briefly. \u201cSorry about this, Lori,\u201d she said softly. \u201cIt\u2019s not about you, it\u2019s about what happened to my friend.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cDon\u2019t worry about it. When you know more, I hope you\u2019ll see that we were trying to help her\u2026 but until then, I understand your concerns. We\u2019ll still be here when you\u2019re ready to come back.\u201d <br /> <br /> And then she was gone. I counted to fifty, and then spent about thirty seconds shouting obscenities at nobody in particular. Just because I expected a little negative publicity around the Freehold doesn\u2019t mean I have to be happy about it. Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne is one of our most talented musicians, and her loss is going to be a blow to our regulars.<br /> <br /> D and Gloria found me fuming in the entrance hall. D tried to be comforting, but I was just in too foul a mood to let it sink in. She was also being very solicitous around Gloria, and I knew that if I stuck around the two of them while I was that angry I\u2019d eventually say or do something I\u2019d regret, so I pulled D aside briefly.<br /> <br /> \u201cI think I\u2019m going to head up to the roof to join Marguerite and Julia and cool off for a little while,\u201d I said softly.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou want me to come with?\u201d D asked, clearly hoping for a negative answer.<br /> <br /> I gave her a smile and glanced at Gloria. \u201cNah, I\u2019ll be fine. You have fun with the new girl.\u201d<br /> <br /> She kissed me gratefully, and the two of them headed off together. Gloria\u2019s encounter with Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne had clearly left her hot to trot, and D was not about to let that opportunity slip through her fingers (so to speak). Once they were out of sight, I morosely stomped up the stairs and made my way to the roof.<br /> <br /> I actually did feel a bit better once I was up there. I vented for a minute or two about the lost act to Marguerite and Julia, but after that we just sort of sat quietly and enjoyed the sunlight (well, Julia hid from the sun as usual, but still). <br /> <br /> About twenty minutes later, the rest of the motley pulled up, and I decided that it had been too long since I had stretched my wings. I glided down to the parking lot in lazy circles (enjoying the fact that everyone\u2019s eyes were on me, naturally) and alit about ten feet from the gaggle of them.<br /> <br /> We traded our respective tales of woe. Theirs was woe-ier, I have to admit. While Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne\u2019s departure from the Dream House was a sore blow, the others had learned that the action between Lucien Torrez and Boss Lowjack had heated up significantly. Lowjack had detonated one of Torrez\u2019s hidden ammo caches as a warning, while Torrez had apparently set off a car bomb in front of Lowjack\u2019s bar, blowing out the front window in the process. No one was hurt at either incident, but that won\u2019t last if those two keep this up.<br /> <br /> My friends knew about this because Lowjack had called Jacob to give him an update. He doesn\u2019t think that Lucien will target Jacob, since the Last Dance motley is sort of a neutral party in these matters, but as a Winter Courtier, he could still be at risk if things escalate. With that in mind, I ambled off toward the guest room, figuring that I should let D know what was going on. Listening at the door for a moment convinced me that I shouldn\u2019t interrupt the two of them. Gloria sounded like she was having a very good time.<br /> <br /> So I grumbled my way backstage and started making sure everything was in order for tonight\u2019s show. I tried to keep busy and not think about what was going on for the next half hour or so. Then D came backstage. She was obviously looking for me, and appeared to be really upset about something. She had a sheaf of papers clutched in her hand.<br /> <br /> \u201cEverything okay, sweetie?\u201d I asked as she approached.<br /> <br /> \u201cI need to talk to you,\u201d she whispered.<br /> <br /> We made our way to a more private part of the house, and she showed me what she had found. \u201cGloria fell asleep after we\u2026 well, you know,\u201d she said. \u201cI got bored and started looking around her room. I found this. She\u2019s been keeping notes on us. She\u2019s reporting on us to someone.\u201d My love looked so forlorn and dejected at this that I had to draw her into my arms.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt might not be her,\u201d I said, trying to comfort D. \u201cShe might have subliminal directives, like Desiree\u2026 we know Hollywood has been working on adapting those techniques. Hell, this could even be a plant to turn us against her. Don\u2019t jump to any conclusions just yet.\u201d I hate that there\u2019s a tiny, mean-spirited part of me that sort of hoped Gloria <u><u>was</u></u> a spy.<br /> <br /> We gathered the rest of the motley and Desiree to try to decide what to do. Desiree confirmed that the handwriting on those notes wasn\u2019t really Gloria\u2019s, but a sort of generic script that <u><u>exactly</u></u> matched Desiree\u2019s own handwriting from when she had been acting under Hollywood\u2019s orders. As Gloria was still sleeping at the moment, we decided to take action immediately.<br /> <br /> Calamity and Gawain entered her dream as subtly as they could, found the triggers that Hollywood had left there, and removed them. They were tight-lipped about Gloria\u2019s dream itself (which I suppose is understandable; it\u2019s a very private matter), but they did make sure to assure us all that the commands to report on us were the only evidence of mental tampering they found. So the person that Gloria seems to be is genuine. And her feelings for D are unfeigned. Joy.<br /> <br /> She\u2019s still sleeping now, and D is waiting for her to wake up so that she can break the news gently. I\u2019ve never really seen her acting like this around anyone else before. Well, that\u2019s not entirely true\u2026 it reminds me a little of the way D acted around <u><u>me</u></u> when we first started dating. And that\u2019s killing me.<br /> <br /> What the hell is wrong with me? Seriously, Lori, get a fucking grip and grow the hell up. You have four girlfriends, and D is fine with that. It\u2019s true that Marguerite and Julia are D\u2019s girlfriends, too\u2026 but Oleander isn\u2019t. You\u2019re in love with Oleander, and D knows that, and she hasn\u2019t said boo about it. Are you such an insecure hypocritical bitch that you can\u2019t offer her the same courtesy?<br /> <br /> Is this still about the Empress\u2019 stupid game? Do I still have to \u201cwin\u201d by making myself everyone\u2019s one-and-only, with no room in their hearts for anyone else? No! Fuck that! D loves me; she\u2019s proved that more times than I can count. She\u2019s offered to leave everything else in her life behind if it means that she and I can stay together. I feel the same way about her. That should be enough for<u> <u>anyone</u></u>. If she can find a little more happiness with Gloria in her life, then I should welcome that development. It\u2019s not like it\u2019s taking anything from me. Not really.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m probably making too much of this too soon. They had sex once; it doesn\u2019t mean they\u2019re getting married or going steady or whatever. I\u2019m pretty sure Gloria still thinks of herself as straight (the evidence of the last few hours notwithstanding). Maybe this whole situation will go away before it even becomes an issue.<br /> <br /> But should I hope for that? D\u2019s obviously already invested in whatever they\u2019ve found together, though she puts on a brave face. And I don\u2019t think it\u2019s just the sex, either\u2026 she seems to have an emotional attachment to Gloria as well. She seems to really <u><u>care</u></u> about this girl. It would hurt her if things ended between them, and it\u2019s selfish of me to think of that potential ending in a positive light.<br /> <br /> Sometimes I\u2019m not even sure what\u2019s really upsetting me about this situation. Oh, the fact that D\u2019s attention is wandering bugs the hell out of me, sure. But if I\u2019m being brutally honest with myself, there\u2019s also a part of me that\u2019s a little jealous of D, too. Gloria\u2019s barely looked twice at me since she arrived here; her attention has been devoted to my honey night and day. I know that Desiree said Gloria had a type\u2026 that she mostly found herself attracted to more aggressive and traditionally \u201cmasculine\u201d women, but still, I\u2019m not used to being shut out of the dynamic like that. And the fact that this bothers me even a little bit says some very nasty things about my character. \u201cEverybody falls in love with you, Lori,\u201d D said to me just three days ago, and there wasn\u2019t a trace of bitterness in her voice when she said it. So now, for the first time, someone comes along that\u2019s more interested in her than in me, and I can\u2019t deal with that? What the fuck?<br /> <br /> I can\u2019t take this introspection any more. I\u2019ve got a goddamned show to do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T13:32:53-07:00","id":873253,"title":"","content":"<b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> Sunday, November 9<sup>th</sup><br /> Nine years, seven months, fourteen days<br /> Days without stabbing: 1<br /> <br /> Fucking Hollywood bastards. Someone needs to bleed for what they did to that poor girl. Hell, right now I am not feeling picky, I'm sure if I cut enough of them I'll find the ones responsible. They want a gorram war I will give them one. Murder is the one thing I am fucking good at. They've poked us enough, it's high time they drew back a bloody stump. They're clearly not going to stop otherwise. They're obviously worried about us but they need to learn to be fucking afraid of screwing with us. I'm sure once enough of them wake up dead they'll get the hint and back the fuck off. Better yet, I'm sure if I carve up enough of their damned monarchs they'll tell me where the hole they're keeping their pet Gentry in is and we can kill the thrice damned thing and bury all of them together.<br /> <br /> Of course, that's not what we're going to do. We're just going to sit here with our thumbs up our collective asses while they continue to murder and mindrape their own people. No, we're too busy fretting about the fucking day and night crowns that might or might not appear and blowing each others toys up and generally acting like a bunch of fucking squabbling children. Hell, right now I don't blame Desiree for thinking about going back to the damn Director. I mean seriously, HE was fucking on board the this shit doesn't fly train months ago. The longer we wait, the less accurate the information Desiree gave us gets. We need to get our fucking act together and fucking do something about this shit.<br /> <br /> Fuck, maybe I am just frustrated because I can't actually do anything to fix this shit with Insincere Marguerite and Julia. For once, I fucking did the right thing and it blew up in my face anyway. It doesn't matter what the hell I do, I'm fucking made of nothing but fucking jagged edges. Everyone that gets too close ends up bleeding. Malevolent. That's what the damn book said and it was fucking right. I've got a piece of the damned place buried in my heart. Everyone that cares about me ends up hurt. They'd all be fucking better off if I'd never escaped or if the townsfolk hadn't stopped Richard from killing me that day.<br /> <br /> Fuck, I need to just leave it alone. I can't figure out how to fix it because it can't be fixed. She hates me now, just like Stasia. At least she's still alive to. Maybe she'll talk to me again eventually but it's never going to be the same. Julia's certainly never going to forgive me. Two more notches to add to my collection of victims. Anastasia, Timmy, Lindsey, Robert, my parents... How many more lives am I going to ruin?<br /> <br /> Two more at the very least. Gawain and Becky have helped me through the past couple of days. They've made it clear they love me. I wonder how long it will be before I lose them too? Will I kill them or just betray them and have to live with their hatred as well? And what about the others? When are Jacob and Lori going to wind up among the casualties? And what about Annika? She actually left her house to come see me last night, to try to cheer me up and support me. That might not seem like much, but it means the world where she's concerned. She's closed off from everyone already, is my inevitable betrayal going to be the last straw?<br /> <br /> Fuck, I don't want to hurt any of them but what I want doesn't matter. I'm Calamity. I'm misfortune and pain and chaos. I'm sharp edges and blood and tears. The worst part is I can't stop. I should push them away while I still can but I won't. I'm too fucking selfish and weak and greedy. I want them so much. I fucking need them right now. I need all of them.<br /> <br /> But this shit has to stop. I have to do something. I have to be strong enough to do what's right for them and not just my own needful desires. I have to do it sooner rather than later. I have to let them go. I have to push them away now, before it's too late. Before they end up like the others. Before I hurt them too.<br /> <br /> Fuck, I don't know if I can.<br /> <br /> Maybe there's another way... Maybe the answer is to leave. If I'm gone I can't hurt any of them. It wouldn't be enough to just leave the Dream House. I'd need to find another freehold. Only... they'd come looking for me. Maybe I should go back to Snow Globe. If I'm good this will all fade. I would forget all the pain and misery and suffering Calamity has caused. I'd forget Kat and all the things I've lost and can't ever get back. I could just fade away and forget everything. Fuck that sounds tempting right now.<br /> <br /> But they would just come after me. They'd follow me to Snow Globe and try to rescue me. They'd end up getting hurt or killed and it would be my gorram fault.<br /> <br /> Fuck. I just don't know what to do about any of this shit. I need to get ready for the show. Maybe I can manage not to fuck that up.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> When it rains it pours as my mother used to say. Today started out pretty good. Insincere Marguerite got herself psyched up for the show. Others in the motley also used some of their own powers to enhance her ability to perform for tonight\u2019s show. It definitely paid off if you ask me. I thought her number was really good, and it was definitely well received by the audience. The only unfortunate bit about Marguerite\u2019s show is that Calamity went backstage so she would not upset her Darkling sister with her presence. I know Calamity was looking forward to watching Insincere Marguerite perform. Not long after the performance was done Calamity came over to the bar. She tried to insist to me that she was fine. That was a lie and we both knew it. So, I assured her that I had brought in a backup bartender for the night and when Calamity needed a break I would be available to walk the crowd. It was about that time that Annika arrived and joined us at the bar. It was not her night to perform, but she came so she could support Calamity. I thought that was rather thoughtful of her. Despite her somewhat cold fa\u00e7ade she does care about her friends.<br /> <br /> After that things got interesting. Moon had come by a little earlier and talked to Gawain about an incident that happened at the Lighthouse. Apparently Gunnar, who\u2019s been missing/unseen for the past month, showed up at the Lighthouse with the intention of watching the Dream healing for Chalcedony. The Autumn Courtiers there kept telling him that he was not allowed to stay, but he kept insisting. Eventually Molly, who\u2019d been watching things unfold invisibly, came out of hiding and put a gun to Gunnar\u2019s head and told him in no uncertain terms that he was not allowed to stay. She told him not to move, but he did, and she fired. Luckily for Gunnar he shrank himself down to be two feet tall and effectively dodged the shot. After that it was a free for all which eventually ended in both parties turning invisible and taking off. Queen Charlotte ordered them to show themselves, and they didn\u2019t. This makes others think that Molly and Gunnar had already left the Lighthouse.<br /> <br /> When questioned, Lucien said that Gunnar had been away doing an errand for him. He did not give any details about said errand, just that Gunnar\u2019s whereabouts were not unknown during that month. Lowjack was then questioned about what Molly was doing at the Lighthouse. His answers apparently were also somewhat cagey. It is presumed that Molly was there to continue her job of keeping an eye on Chalcedony. Same as she was doing before. When Calamity heard about everything that happened she got really mad. She was especially mad at Lowjack. She got so upset that she broke the glass that she was holding. Thankfully Becky was there to heal the damage. I guess Calamity blamed Lowjack for Molly pulling the gun on Gunnar. It doesn\u2019t really surprise me that Molly did that. Those two have had a long standing rivalry going on and do not like each other in the least. Plus Gunnar had been asked several times by Autumn Courtiers to leave and he kept refusing to go. Molly got fed up and threatened him, and things escalated from there. Lori came over while Calamity was wiping up the alcohol that she had spilled and asked what was going on. So the whole story got repeated for her benefit. Thankfully no more glasses were broken. And to be fair, Calamity did repair the glass that she broke.<br /> <br /> Once Calamity calmed down somewhat Annika invited her out back for cigars. Calamity took her up on the offer and they went outside to smoke. I think Becky joined them as well for support. I don\u2019t know what they talked about but when they came back in later Calamity was much more relaxed. So much so that after the show was over she allowed Gawain to pick her up and carry her upstairs. Becky went with them. For support, I\u2019m sure. While Calamity was relaxing I walked through the crowd. I made small talk with some of the regulars and stopped to talk to Rowan one more time. She apparently decided to come back for another show, so I thought that I\u2019d make her feel welcome. Closing tonight was much like last night, quiet and incident free.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Today started off calmly enough. Gawain made us all blueberry pancakes and scrambled eggs loaded with cheese and other ingredients. As usual, it was all very good. Lorelei and De la Rocha both came in all dressed up for church. Apparently this morning was the day that Lori was going to introduce her girlfriend to her dad. Not that he knows that he\u2019s Lori\u2019s father, but it was still important to Lori that he approve of her paramour. Also while we were eating breakfast, Insincere Marguerite and Julia came downstairs to join us for \u201cSex Breakfast\u201d despite the presence of Calamity. They both kind of acted like Calamity wasn\u2019t there, but they didn\u2019t outright turn their backs on their fellow Darkling. It was really tense, but still better than I had been expecting. Then, since Marguerite had missed the news last night, we went over the happenings at the Lighthouse for Insincere Marguerite and Julia\u2019s sakes. Insincere Marguerite confirmed that Molly and Gunnar have never gotten along.<br /> <br /> This led into a conversation about the possible introduction of the Diurnal Courts Monarchs and how the Seasonal Monarchs feel about it. Julia brought it up that in L.A the Seasonal Monarchs lost their power to the Diurnal Courts and that our own Monarchs were afraid of something similar happening here. Lowjack seems to be okay with there being a Day and Night Monarch, just as long as there is not an increase in population for either group. He would rather there be peace, and incentives for folks to stay out of town or to move out if they want to. Charlotte is definitely pushing the other Monarchs to not kill Diurnal Court members, and I believe Jolie is advocating the same thing. Augustine seems to be \u201clistening to the will of his people.\u201d Not exactly sure that that entails, but he\u2019s likely talking to folks and see what they prefer. Overall it seems that they favor the idea of violence to fix the \u201cproblem.\u201d There was also some talk about what Salk was doing here, and the idea that he\u2019d come specifically because of the possibility of there being a Day and Night crown showing up in the near future. The Courts seem a bit concerned about him getting a crown. They are less opposed to Insincere Marguerite or Felicity getting the crowns as they have strong ties to the Seasonal Courts.<br /> <br /> After that Calamity directly asked if Insincere Marguerite will be okay with her being present for the movie night. Marguerite said that she doesn\u2019t want Calamity to leave the house because of her. Calamity kind of tried to explain what happened that night. Not to excuse her actions, but to at least explain them. I think she pushed Insincere Marguerite just a bit too soon, who said that she was going to go up to the roof and relax. Julia joined her paramour on the roof while Lori and De la Rocha went upstairs to get dressed.<br /> <br /> Desiree suggested that the rest of us go out for soft serve ice cream. It sound like a good idea to me, so I agreed. Calamity was up for it too. I did want to talk to Calamity about the counselors at the Clinic before we left so I took her aside to ask. I don\u2019t think that was the question that she was expecting, but she didn\u2019t turn me away. She said that they do a good job and that she trusts them. She mentioned that there are pledges in place to keep secrets just that, secret. I admitted to Calamity that recently I think I\u2019ve been sliding a bit closer to what I was before. Closer to being Rime. I did not want to continue down that path, but wasn\u2019t sure where to go for help. I wanted to make sure that the counselors would keep things to themselves too. I have some pretty damning secrets that I don\u2019t want getting out or being used against me. Calamity seemed pretty convinced of their trustworthiness and I trust her. She asked if I wanted to go with her to her next appointment and I can set something up for myself while I\u2019m there. I agreed. I will probably ask for the specifics of the pledge that they have to make sure that things will stay secret. I should also find out who they have the pledge with. I wonder if it\u2019s Darke? I also assured Calamity, because dammit I was going to support my friend, that I didn\u2019t fault her for what happened with the whole Chalcedony affair. I believe that she had good intentions and that\u2019s what matters.<br /> <br /> Sometimes the intention is the only thing we really have. So many times I did things because I thought I was doing the right thing. There was one young woman named Jenny that stumbled into the Lady\u2019s realm. She was an innocent free spirit, and that drew the wrong kind of attention. There was one man that decided he would take Jenny \u201cunder his wing,\u201d and keep her safe. He just didn\u2019t mention to her up front what the \u201cprice\u201d for his protection would be. Needless to say she didn\u2019t want to pay it. I caught him trying to have his way with her. I interrupted and assured him that if that\u2019s what he really wanted then I could take him to someone that could give it to him just as good and was already broken in. He was skeptical at first but he eventually followed my lead. Jenny was disgusted with me and spat in my face. I just smiled at her and led the sex crazed asshole deep into the woods. I led him on a winding path that brought him deeper and deeper until we found a cave. I told him that what he sought was inside. Wanting to get out of the driving wind, he went into the cave to find his prize. I don\u2019t know what happened to him after that. I know that there are bones in that cave, human bones, and I have an idea that they are the remains of those dumb enough to seek shelter in that particular cave. I led I him there to die, and I\u2019m assuming he did. Granted Jenny would never thank me for what I did. In her mind I betrayed her, but in mine I was doing the right thing. I was keeping her safe. Sometimes I wonder what happened to Jenny.<br /> <br /> Anyway\u2026moving onto more current, and less morose things. The lot of us went out for ice cream. It was good. And while we were out getting our frozen treat I got a call from Boss Lowjack. He wanted to warn me that there might be a slight increase in hostilities between the Summer and Winter Courts. He explained that there had been demonstrations of power from each side that may have riled things up. Around that time we heard on the news that there had been a series of explosions downtown, suspiciously close to Torrez\u2019s place. We were told that it was one of his ammo storage facilities. There was also a car that exploded outside of Lowjack\u2019s bar that took out the front window. Nobody was hurt in either of these incidents but there was property damage galore. I told the others what was going on which made the news on the radio a little more real than it had been before. Lowjack didn\u2019t seem to think that I\u2019d be specifically targeted since I\u2019m not so closely tied to the political goings on in town, but he felt it was better to err on the side of caution.<br /> <br /> After we finished our ice cream we went back to the Dream House. When we got there we could tell right off that Lori was very upset. Apparently Marie-Helene went to try and talk to Chalcedony and was turned away. She somehow found out that she had been taken while in our house and was uncomfortable with that. She said that she didn\u2019t want to continue to perform for us until she had gotten a chance to talk to Chalcedony. All of this upset Lori a great deal. She was worried that other performers might follow Marie-Helene\u2019s example and decide that they didn\u2019t need to continue to work for our club.<br /> <br /> That led to us talking about what we were going to tell people if they asked about Chalcedony being taken from the Dream House. There was some back and forth about how truthful we were going to be. I agreed that we should not mention anything about the Director or any possible programing of his. It would be instantly assumed that she is a Loyalist, which may or may not be true, but we don\u2019t want that assumption going around. In the end we agreed that we would tell people that there was a lingering magical effect placed on her by her Keeper and that she was gathered up to get rid of that effect. No mentioning of the Director or scripts or programing.<br /> <br /> A short while later, after Calamity talked to Insincere Marguerite about being in the audience while she performed, De la Rocha came back with some disturbing news. Apparently she and Gloria decided to take their flirtations to the next level and excused themselves to a private room. After they\u2019d had sex Gloria fell asleep and De la Rocha decided to take a look around her lover\u2019s room. She found notes. Notes on the activities of all of us in the Dream House. Our guess is that she had been caught by the Hollywood Courts and reprogrammed to work for them. They wanted an inside person and they had the perfect subject. The thing that really gave things away was the fact that Desiree recognized the format and handwriting of the notes. They were in the same format that she used to take notes in when she was under the control of the Hollywood Courts.<br /> <br /> Gawain and Calamity took advantage of the fact that Gloria was asleep to go into her dream and remove the programming that was there. They found out that she was supposed to take notes on the Dream House and the Freehold in general and then drop off her notes at a dead drop nearby. This was much simpler than the programming that they had performed on Desiree. With her, they had used existing cues from the Director and built off of that. With Gloria they had to start from scratch and create a way to make her do what they wanted her to do. I\u2019m not sure how they managed to \u201cprogram\u201d Gloria, but it can\u2019t have been pleasant. The question remains, how did they do it? Did they use mystical means? Did they use mundane means? Or was it combination of the two? It would be good to know how they did it if we want to be able to stop them. Of course what Gawain and Calamity did seemed to do the trick just fine. They managed to make her dream-self see that she had marionette strings attached to her limbs, controlling her. Then they handed her a pair of scissors and she started to take care of the programming herself.<br /> <br /> This whole thing has me concerned. This is not the first time that the Hollywood Courts have made in-roads into our Freehold. They are intensely curious about us and how and why we do what we do. The question is, why? Why are they so curious about us? What is it that draws their attention our way? I\u2019ve only been a part of this Freehold for a few months so I don\u2019t know everything there is to know, but I do know something about my new home. I know that for the most part the people here are good. I know that they may have selfish motives sometimes, but they will usually do the right thing. Torrez might be a bastard to Winter Courtiers, but when we were hunting Mary\u2019s fetch he was a great help in getting things cleared up and warning us when the cops took an interest in our house. Darke might be somewhat detached from reality, but he did try and do some good with the clinic. Granted, he was using it to help people to get clean just so he could get them addicted to smack again, but some of what he did was good. He may not be a great example. Anyway\u2026we have some good and some not so good people living here, but I\u2019m not sure that it warrants the amount of attention that the Hollywood Courts are paying to us. What\u2019s so special about us and our House that they program innocent Changelings so they\u2019ll spy on us and report our activities? Why do they want to know, and what are they going to do when they\u2019ve gotten all the intel that they want?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> I am getting ready to go on. I feel more settled than last time.<br /> <br /> Last night was my first show. I only came down long enough to do \u201cNon, Je Ne Regrette Rien\u201d but it went very well. Julia, Lorelei and Gawain all used magic to help me shake off my malaise. I got quite a response. I saw Flores and White Maria came to watch, but I did not have the strength to deal with them. Lorelei came up briefly, then returned briefly with De La Rocha to see I in my room, but I was not up to much. I slept as Julia held I. Blissfully.<br /> <br /> Julia loves me. Utterly. And I think we all made our feelings clear to each other. They are intense. It makes me think about our future. Deeply.<br /> <br /> I made it to sex breakfast this morning. Gawain made delicious eggs with Gouda cheese. Becky Wan, Desiree, and Gloria were there. Tensions were lower, as I hoped, compared to yesterday overall. The rulers are worried about I getting the crown\u2026Queen Charlotte backs me, but things are otherwise tricky. I mostly avoided speaking to Calamity so I was all right. Calamity did force the issue, though I do not clearly recall our conversation. It was\u2026upsetting. Terribly.<br /> <br /> Julia and I went to the roof for a while. We heard Lorelei and De La Rocha rutting in their room; De La Rocha showed up to breakfast in a suit having gone to church with Lori, and it was fetching. Quite fetching. I confess I felt some envy; Despite my stress and desire to push everyone away, I wanted to let go and rut as well. To feel Julia\u2019s warm wetness around I, to be lost in the sound of breathing, grunting and heartbeats. Shivering and writhing. Surrounded by lovers and their hissing breaths. I would\u2026ah, anyway\u2026<br /> <br /> While this went on the rest of the Motley, Becky and Desiree went out. Quietly.<br /> <br /> The lovebirds stopped eventually, and Lori joined us soon after on the roof. I had been relaxing watching the cars from the roof while Julia sat in her beach chair under the umbrella. Lori sunbathed when she joined us, saying Desiree and company had gone for soft serve. When they returned, she glided down to talk to them and we went inside. Beautifully.<br /> <br /> There was a good deal of discussion. Lowjack and Lucian\u2019s conflict, well, the conflict Lowjack had inherited from Master Darke, was heating up. A gunfight between Molly and Gunnar had happened at the Lighthouse over Chalcedony, and they had set off explosions on each other\u2019s turfs, though without any deaths. Tensions were high. Lori is also upset the Belgian Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne does not wish to perform for us at the moment; angry her dear from Chalcedony was jumped. Understandably.<br /> <br /> I cannot imagine.<br /> <br /> I worked on preparing for the show when Calamity came to talk again. I had more my wits about me this time. Perhaps hanging upside down helped. Possibly. She wanted to ensure I could go on with her there. I promised I could. She seemed satisfied, and I think went to go speak to Julia. Julia is not permitted to speak to her, for her own good, so I doubt she got much of interest. Unfortunately.<br /> <br /> I was psyching myself up, having gotten a boost from Lori and Gawain again, when word came up there was an emergency with Gloria. She had succumbed to the irresistible force of De La Rocha\u2019s lips (that is two carnal connections in, what, three hours? Four? I thought twice in a day was decadent. Lori must be rubbing off on De La Rocha. So to speak.) and De la Rocha, being a Darkling, had poked curiously about her things and found she was spying for Hollywood in much the same way Desiree had been. I missed much of the commotion preparing lights and effects. By the time I heard Gawain and Calamity were already down there, and from what I heard fixed Gloria\u2019s being under control, which was a minor effect compared to Desiree but still dangerous. I watched with Lori, and found myself succumbing a little as well to her charms. I pressed my lips to hers, and our tongues were\u2026<br /> <br /> Apparently I do need to make love more than I thought I did. Maybe tonight. Hopefully.<br /> <br /> Right now I have a show to prepare for, and Insincere Marguerite shall not disappoint!<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LIV</i><br /> <br /> So we had a Dreamhealing scene with Calamity and Gawain helping Gloria. She was fairly easy to heal, Hollywood is not at the point where The Director is, and they did not have his template to go on. Look for a short story from Calamity's Player covering the Dreamhealing in the offweek.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite got boosted by Vernal Spring (the die adder) Potential (the Willpower spending boost) and Fleeting Spring (stopping fear). It worked out for her. She got like 7 successes\u2026nowhere near Lori\u2019s 12, but it\u2019s Lori\u2019s thing.<br /> <br /> The scene with Lori\u2019s dad was played out, but her player elaborated in journal (which is cool).<br /> <br /> Julia angrily pantomiming responses to Calamity was fun.<br /> <br /> I think that covers everything. Comments and Questions welcome. See you next week for the short story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 04-24-2016, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T23:18:37-07:00","id":873554,"title":"","content":"sooooooo many emotions. also, while he is probably having the least amount of issues of all of them, someone really needs to help Gawain. Lord Bertilak is making much more frequent appearances and he is a really scary evil Day-Courty mofo. Perhaps he should tell his motley about that. Calamity needs to know that she is helping to keep away his darker urges just as much as he is helping her. <br /> <br /> Also, i am now certain I am going to do fan journals for Ace if i can, but I wanted to know if you guys could ask his player if he minded me doing that. And possibly posting it on a fanfiction site or something. Don't expect no Shakespeare. I pride myself on being a decent essay writer for my college courses, but it's been years since I've written fiction and i have never before written fanfiction","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T23:20:29-07:00","id":873556,"title":"","content":"Also, on the subject of the Dark Lord Bertilak, how is Gawain's Clarity doing? Are Lord Bertilak's appearances entirely a player decision like Insincere Marguerite's thirst for Felicity at the Masquerade, or are they connected to his new Clarity Level of 6?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T01:37:05-07:00","id":873600,"title":"","content":"So... I don't recall clearly, but Lord Bertilak either came out for the first time when Gawain's Wyrd went up, or when his Clarity went down. I actually think both happened at near to the same time. So, a combination of losing his connection to the real world, and having clearer memories of his time in Arcadia than he has of his previous existence, Since, he's tended to come out in times of stress. He will likely come out more as his Wyrd grows/Clarity falls.<br /> <br /> I don't really see Lord Bertilak as evil. He does often manifest as Gawain's temper, and I suppose he is Sith-like in his belief in absolutes, but one of the things that triggers him is Gawain's sense of honor being broken in a way he feels he can't control/stop. He's an asshole, commanding and super assertive, but supremely protective of his people and strictly adhering to an honor code. That in and of itself is possibly problematic, because it's the honor code of a chivalric romance, but...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1471-levinserra","name":"LevinSerra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1471_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T01:42:43-07:00","id":873603,"title":"","content":"Calamity is aware of Lord Bertilak (and maybe just a bit more okay with him than she should be) though I don't think just how much of a role she plays in keeping that side of him in check has truly occurred to her. In her mind, Gawain is pretty much as good and perfect as she is terrible and flawed and so she doesn't think of him needing her like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T01:53:10-07:00","id":873608,"title":"","content":"I've contacted the relevant people. Two already posted. I will send a message to you when I hear from Ace's player.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T05:39:59-07:00","id":873687,"title":"","content":"So much drama since I last read the AP! Love, betrayal, tragic mistakes, and madness lurking at the door. So fricking awesome.<br /> <br /> It's interesting to note the differences between each character's take on the last events. The girls' feelings feel very intense and chaotic, while Gawain reacted by going into protective mode over Calamity, then went back to being the motley's strong, gentle caregiver though it feels like he's struggling with this role now, and Jacob seem to feel things more remotely, as if from a distance, not that he appear unconcerned, but more able to put things in perspective and less passionately reactive than the others.<br /> <br /> I seriously wish I could have been there to see those last sessions.<br /> <br /> I'm really curious about the Handmaidens and their interest in some of the Last Dance's changelings, especially Jacob. I can't recall if they've shown sustained interest in another male.<br /> I also wonder if Becky really loves Calamity romantically or if the later is merely reading too much into the former's attempts to help a dear friend.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T10:33:42-07:00","id":873862,"title":"","content":"Thanks for contacting Ace's player. I've been reading over his two journals to get a feel for his character. I'm starting to see why he chose Summer Court I think. He's almost like a Dusk Courtier in his attitude, though less certain of his inevitable recapture.<br /> <br /> And I get that Lord Bertilak isn't evil per-say. But as I said, I think of him as having the philosophy of a fanatical Day Courtier, all extremes and such. And my momma always told me that the most dangerous people in the world were those who are absolutely certain that they are doing what is right.<br /> <br /> And it's not just the full-on Lord Bertilak outburst that scare me. It's the little moments where his medieval vocabulary creeps into Gawain's otherwise normal sentences. Those little moments that make it seem like Lord Bertilak is starting to influence Gawain. And I'm especially worried that no one is telling him that he should be seeing someone about what is basically MPD.<br /> <br /> I mean, it totally fits. He was in a stressful situation and created (with a lot of help from his Keeper) a new personality to take the abuse and the guilt that he could not. And since he does not remember his old life at all, who knows how old he was when he was taken? He could have been a young teenager.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 04-25-2016, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T11:43:24-07:00","id":873909,"title":"","content":"Anteros: Thanks for the Comments. It's been an intense time in the game, but a lot of fun. Things are starting cool down a bit from the madness, and last night a character made a decision that will change their life and the lives of at least a few others.<br /> <br /> The Handmaidens don't really swing one way or the other. Part of the issue really is the large number of NPCs that are female, and that they have a few types. They are not going after Gawain because of various reasons, a lot of which is he being a suit of armor is really not their type, but Jacob is cute. They have shown interest in Sandoval. Really, though, it is the large number of women thing.<br /> <br /> With Becky it is complicated. Her dislike for formalized relationships and commitment is something of an issue. As a succubus, she does not have a strong demarcation between &quot;friend&quot; and &quot;lover&quot; beyond if they are sleeping together or not. Love in general is an emotion she tries not to explore. She does seem pretty attached to Calamity though.<br /> <br /> MA: I'll leave Levin to discuss advanced Gawain. I am not sure Insincere Marguerite would approve of the Day Court comparison, but she is biased.The way Bertilak's language creeps into Gawain's speech is cool though. Gawain's player really writes well.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the feedback!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T16:18:08-07:00","id":874089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amberghylles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play?p=873603#post873603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Calamity is aware of Lord Bertilak (and maybe just a bit more okay with him than she should be) though I don't think just how much of a role she plays in keeping that side of him in check has truly occurred to her. In her mind, Gawain is pretty much as good and perfect as she is terrible and flawed and so she doesn't think of him needing her like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something that scares me a bit is that while Calamity is Gawain's love, she is also Lord Bertilak's dragon; put her into a situation where Gawain's focused on fighting, and I doubt that anyone coud stop her from joining him. That, honestly, sounds terrifying. I also like to think that if they ever go true fae, it'd be as a pair, and a rather devestating pair at that.<br /> <br /> Also, probably really indulgent of me, but did anyone else get the thought that Mary and Gunnar fighting each other would have looked a bit like when Homura and Mami went full on combat mode against one another? Two expert assassins, both capable of going invisible, sneaking around, firing gunshots at one another and with powers besides they could pull out? It sounds awesome really.<br /> <br /> Also, love the idea of Julia phantomiming angrily to Calamity - if anything it sounds like it could be a comedy act the Dreamhouse could perform (someone talking with Julia, who phantomimes angrily to them). Mind, that would mean making Julia the clown...although that said, it could prove to be a bonus to those who use sign language...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T16:27:08-07:00","id":874093,"title":"","content":"Sith and Jedi with their absolutes...<br /> <br /> Jacob brings up a good point. What is Hollywood's focus on the Malibu freehold?<br /> <br /> I forget if this was mentioned, but I assume Calamity lost clarity in the debacle with Ms. Insincere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T22:32:09-07:00","id":874275,"title":"","content":"Taidragon: I do not get the assassins reference, sorry. Julia is...unlikely to go up on stage. We discussing having her violin while Calamity and Insincere Marguerite dueted <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QxJrjV4PNXAhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QxJrjV4PNXA\" target=\"_blank\">When You're Evil by Voltaire</a>. At this point it seems unlikely. Even that was a case where the focus would be off her.<br /> <br /> Omenseer: The the former, unsure, though they are spying mostly at this point. To the latter no, Calamity lost no Clarity. Only Insincere Marguerite lost Clarity. And she did not gain a derangement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a hre