what I envisioned in the battle between Molly and Gunnar, from what little was described. Apologies for the confusion there (and seriously, what's wrong with me today getting names mixed up).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T00:24:01-07:00","id":874322,"title":"","content":"Sounds awesome, but more likely to be found in Exalted than Changeling.<br /> <br /> Baroness, do you use any of the stuff from the Changeling 2e playtest?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":1405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","user":"Anteros","date":". 04-26-2016, 03:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T00:47:54-07:00","id":874327,"title":"","content":"At this time, no. Once released, I will examine the 2e rules and decide what I will use and not use like any other game. 2e Kiths will get a hard look and likely an option to use the new or keep the old on a case by case basis. I will not be using Huntsmen. I will keep old Seemings. I may add the new Seeming mechanics on top of old if I adopt new Clarity. If I do not I likly won't. I don't expect I will use new Contracts, but I will look at them before rejecting them. Most games I adopt almost all of, but C:tL feels very different 2e from 1e. We will see. I will neither use or reject anything simply because it is new.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T00:32:30-07:00","id":879353,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s the off week this week, but we had a story written by Calamity\u2019s player about the Dream Healing they did to help Gloria last session, much like the took my outline and wrote when they helped Andromeda. I figured I would put it up now for you. Enjoy.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> The living room was typical middle class Americana as was the aging woman who stood beside the darkened television, arms crossed as she surveyed the younger woman before her with a skeptical expression. The girl was naked, her breasts hidden by the hands of her lover who stood behind her, nuzzling and caressing her.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo Mom,\u201d Gloria protested as she turned to try to sweep her hair to the side to conceal de la Rocha's playful nipping at her neck, \u201cIt's not like that at all. I'm not really a lesbian. It was just...\u201d she stopped to bite down on her lower lip and stifle a gasp as the Latino woman's teasing fingers found a particularly sensitive spot.<br /> <br /> The older woman nodded. \u201cUh huh. Just what?\u201d<br /> <br /> Gloria drew in a breath to answer but then her brow furrowed. She glanced to one side and then the other at the sense of others entering, though there was no sign of another.<br /> <br /> Then de la Rocha's hands started to move, sliding down Gloria's sides. Fingers brushed along her hips and thighs and calves. \u201cYou really don't have to explain yourself to her.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI should.\u201d<br /> <br /> Light fingers stroked around the contours of Gloria's ankles and then down the tops of her feet until they encountered the strings extending up from the woman's feet into the darkness that arched above instead of a roof or ceiling.<br /> <br /> Gloria frowned and blinked at the strings. \u201cWhere did those come from?\u201d she murmured softly.<br /> <br /> De la Rocha chuckled from behind her, rising to her feet and kneading the slender woman's shoulders. \u201cThey weren't always there?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo. They weren't.\u201d<br /> <br /> Strong hands moved down Gloria's arms to take and lift her hands, thumbs rubbing circles around the matching strings rising from the backs of them as well. \u201cThen these shouldn't be here either I guess...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat? No. What is going on?\u201d<br /> <br /> The older woman scowled as a lone strand of iron gray hair escaped her severe bun. She lifted the wooden control bar in her hand and turned it, pulling Gloria's hands away from the woman behind hers grasp. \u201cThere will be no more of that young lady. You will do as you are told.\u201d <br /> <br /> Gloria tugged at the strings, fighting the pull. \u201cNo. I don't want to...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThen don't.\u201d The husky voice in her ear whispered. \u201cSet yourself free of them.\u201d<br /> <br /> The elder clenched her jaw hard enough for the muscles to twitch under her pinched and leathery skin. Burning eyes narrowed. \u201cI will brook no more of this disobedience.\u201d She lifted the control and twisted it sharply.<br /> <br /> Gloria lurched forward awkwardly and then turned to push de la Rocha away. \u201cWait! No! That's not what I want to do.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThen stop.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHow? I can't...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCut the strings Gloria.\u201d Gloria looked from the woman down to her hands. \u201cCut the strings. You don't have to obey them. You don't have to be their puppet.\u201d In her hand was a pair of sewing shears.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou put those down right now young lady!\u201d<br /> <br /> Gloria brought the shears up and over, opening them and setting the string on her left hand into the V.<br /> <br /> \u201cDon't you DARE!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo strings Gloria. No strings on you.\u201d<br /> <br /> The shears were oddly loud as they severed the string. Then another snip and another until all of the strings had been severed. Gloria turned toward the withered crone and watched as she pointlessly tried to twist and shake the now useless crossbar in her claw-like hand. She fixed Gloria with a baleful expression and curled her thin lips back from her impossibly wide jaw to reveal the crooked and jagged teeth that filled her maw. But then the strings upon her went taut and suddenly she was pulled up and out of sight.<br /> <br /> A hand touched Gloria's shoulder and turned her back to face the other woman again.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt's alright now Gloria. You're free of them. You're still safe here. You're still with friends. Everything is going to be alright.\u201d<br /> <br /> Gloria nodded and agreed softly.<br /> <br /> \u201cCome along now. Everything is okay.\u201d<br /> <br /> De la Rocha took her hand and smiled, drawing her away from the fading room and the dream and back toward waking.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Not quite as sweet as the last one, but still. Helpful.<br /> <br /> Next session covers a longer amount of time, about two days. See how Insincere Marguerite\u2019s healing is going, and Lorelei working things out with Gloria! Find out Insincere Marguerite\u2019s plan for Julia birthday! Find out how the Motley feels about <i>The</i> Matrix and <i>Bound.</i> All this in one week. See you then, comments and questions welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T17:36:43-07:00","id":880603,"title":"","content":"I liked it. That's totally the kind of disturbing situation that always happens in dreams and whose peculiarity only becomes appearent when waking up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T20:26:19-07:00","id":880704,"title":"","content":"Yea we all have those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T00:30:59-07:00","id":880789,"title":"","content":"Thank you Anteros. I was rather pleased with how it turned out myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T13:52:51-07:00","id":885662,"title":"","content":"And the Motley slowly begins to recover from the Drama. Now with movie reviews for <i>The Matrix</i> and <i>Bound!</i>.<br /> <br /> Note there was an extra post with the dream from last time check it out!<br /> <br /> <i>Session LV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> Nov 10th, evening<br /> <br /> Maybe I spoke a little too soon. I mean, we did help Gloria, that worked out alright - she\u2019s ok, a little freaked out, but ok. Calamity\u2019s not though. I mean, she says she is, but... Thankfully, Becky\u2019s been a rock, and god, it\u2019s been, you know, helpful. Even just her presence while I helped Calamity get dressed, after she\u2019d shredded the first jacket she tried to get on, was stabilizing. The thing with Boss Lowjack did seem to, I dunno, perk her up but I\u2019m still really worried.<br /> <br /> The show did go well. White Maria and Dark Kimberly were there again, sitting at different tables, but still, you know, close by, and talking. Dionysia, Shi and Moon were there, and Andromeda and Joan. I meant to getting around to seeing everyone, but I started with Andromeda and Joan, and we got to talking, me and Joan, about medieval history and how it can be helpful, even these days, you know? There are so many lessons to draw from what\u2019s happened before... anyway, it was a nice diversion. Andromeda was pretty quiet, but she was all smiles for Lori when she stopped by, and Joan didn\u2019t seem worried, so she was probably just tuning out all the shop talk.<br /> <br /> Boss Lowjack stopped by after the show. He had a proposal to run by us, you know, non-Seasonal guys. He\u2019d already run it by Captain Jack, presumably with a positive response? He figured on heading off this whole Crown thing by having non-Seasonal courtiers swear allegiance Pledges to a Monarch of their choice. Nothing that would conflict with Court allegiance or anything, but enough to remove the political impetus for the new Crowns to show up.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not a bad plan, I guess. At least so long as no one gets pressured into it. His comments toed the line on that, but I do think he had good intentions at least. I\u2019m not swearing allegiance to any of them, but my Crown is not about to show up, and even then, they don\u2019t need everyone to swear, just enough. He did ask Insincere Marguerite to drag her feet, you know, in case they couldn\u2019t get enough, but I think he\u2019s gonna go ahead and get it pushed through.<br /> <br /> We did tell him about Gloria and worked out a plan I\u2019m much more comfortable with - we\u2019ll use her dead drop to spread some misinformation, first off. Boss Lowjack has some ways to spread information to the general populace of Hollywood, so once we cut off communication through the dead drop, we\u2019ll let the regular folks know about how to get ID mental programming in dreams. So if the Courts there are putting a low level command into a widespread group, it might get noticed and there might be, you know, a revolution.<br /> <br /> That got Boss Lowjack ranting about Viscount Augustine. Apparently, the Viscount believes that you don\u2019t not fight a knight because his master is corrupt. Which is true, if the knight presses the attack. However, given the opportunity to convince the knight of his master\u2019s perfidy, the honorable thing is to try, you know, to give the knight a chance to make his own choices.<br /> <br /> I felt bad for the guy. I do think he\u2019s got the best in mind, you know, for the Freehold, but, like Insincere Marguerite said, he\u2019s either a good man or a great liar. And I dunno which - he\u2019s too slippery for me to get a hold on with the Contracts of Potential, generally. Still, after our talk, even Calamity seemed more positively aligned towards him than she had since Boss Lowjack threatened Insincere Marguerite. She was also more cheerful in general, enough to pull Becky away from her, Desiree and Gloria\u2019s \u2018friendfic\u2019ing and drag the two of us upstairs to bed.<br /> <br /> <br /> Nov 11th, afternoon<br /> <br /> Well, yesterday certainly kept me busy. Not, like, work busy, to be fair, but enough that I didn\u2019t write in here. Partially it was my fault - after a sex breakfast discussion about, you know, dyke boots or omni/pan/bi clogs, I thought a trip to the outdoor ice skating rink would be fun. I managed to talk everyone around, and I only tackled Lori a little. Well, everyone except De la Roche, who had to work, and Gloria, who had a thing with Monica, and Desiree, who was feeling crappy.<br /> <br /> It was a great time - Jacob and Calamity did awesome, but they had both done it before. Insincere Marguerite was pretty good herself, especially since it was her first time. Lori and Becky were both better than me, but I did manage to stay on my feet. You know, most of the time. It was a blast anyway. Julia even had fun, and she just watched from a shaded table on the edge of the rink.<br /> <br /> Gloria texted me to let me know Juan Carlos was around as we were driving to dinner, so we decided to get on back and just order in. Juan Carlos was his usual charming self, with Lori fawning over him and Gloria blushing fiercely at his, you know, lack of shirt. We talked for awhile, going over what I knew and what happened that night at the Dream House. I\u2019m sure he\u2019ll do a good job. He promised to keep me updated too, so that made me feel a little better. At least it\u2019s not just all unknown, you know?<br /> <br /> When he left, Insincere Marguerite let me know Desiree wasn\u2019t doing so good. She got herself super drunk, not to, you know, do herself in or something, but still, she wasn\u2019t practiced at it, so she kinda went overboard a little. Lori rehydrated her and Jacob made sure she wasn\u2019t in danger of alcohol poisoning. I went up there as soon as I heard, and sat with her - she\u2019s really torn up about Gloria, the whole betrayal thing and her feelings for her, including jealousy re: De la Roche. I tried to get her spirits up, exerting my Mantle a little. I think it helped. She was feeling well enough to join us at movie night anyway.<br /> <br /> It was De la Roche\u2019s picks, The Matrix and Bound. Lori ordered pizza and with that and all of it, it was almost like, you know, old times. The movies were awesome, even if Lori\u2019s new science-powers ruined her suspension of disbelief during The Matrix. Bound was... hot. And fun. Calamity got all bitter at the end, but I tickled her into better spirits. Ish. Becky headed home, taking the opportunity to get some rest in her own bed.<br /> <br /> Today has been pretty awesome so far. It\u2019s Julia\u2019s birthday and we started off by having Julia eat omelettes, you know, off Lori\u2019s stomach. Then she and Desiree started making out. Well, first the quartet went to get Lori in a corset - gotta look nice for those afternoon graveyard walks, you know? Once that happened though, Julia decided Desiree hadn\u2019t had enough attention paid to her and... make outs.<br /> <br /> I called Annika, since Calamity didn\u2019t wanna risk ruining Julia\u2019s birthday, so she bowed out of the walk, and Becky wasn\u2019t back around yet. Becky did get there before we left though, so between her and Annika and Jacob, I figured Calamity was in good hands<br /> <br /> Desiree and Luna went with the quartet and I to the graveyard. It was a nice walk, though I kept being distracted by how excitedly nervous Insincere Marguerite was and how, you know, smirky Lori was. Whatever they were up to, it hasn\u2019t happened yet - Lori was too busy proclaiming herself Commander of the Legions of Air. It was good to see Insincere Marguerite so lively and excited though. I think everything\u2019s going to be ok.<br /> <br /> Now I just have to convince Calamity.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> It\u2019s been about two days since my last entry, and I think I\u2019ve calmed down a bit since then. At least I have my anxieties about D and Gloria a little more under control now that I\u2019ve spoken with both of them about it. Things seem to be moving forward on all fronts, and I\u2019m choosing to see that as a good thing.<br /> <br /> So Sunday night I was still a mass of jealousy and complexes when I went on stage, and the fact that D and Gloria were sitting together in the audience did nothing to improve my mood. I\u2019m sure my performance suffered a bit because of my distraction, but the audience still seemed to enjoy the show, so I\u2019m not going to stress over it now. Dark Kimberly and White Maria were both there, sitting relatively close to each other and chatting civilly, if not exactly amiably. I bonded with Kimberly briefly about the trials of dating one of Madame Spidertoes\u2019 exes, but then I moved on. Moon, Dionysia, and Shi shared another table, though I didn\u2019t get the chance to speak with them extensively. <br /> <br /> Oh, and Joan and Andromeda made an appearance as well. I would have liked to spend a little more time with them, but Joan was busy discussing medieval siege weapons with Gawain, and every time she looked at me she started to blush and stammer, so I made myself scarce after a while. Andromeda was quiet, but seemed happy (if not exactly as exuberant as she had been on Friday night). Joan mentioned that it had been a hard day for her paramour, and that she hoped coming out to the Dream House for some fun might help. I hope it did.<br /> <br /> Boss Lowjack had contacted Jacob earlier in the day and asked if he could speak with the motley after the show tonight. I admit that the hostility between the Summer and Winter Courts (combined with my own personal drama) has me a bit on edge, and I sort of snippily asked Jacob if we needed to check the parking lot for car bombs, but in the end there was no cause for concern.<br /> <br /> It turned out that Lowjack mostly wanted to talk to Marguerite and Gawain about his new plan for staving off the rise of the Diurnal crowns. Lowjack believes that if enough of the non-seasonal courtiers in the area swear allegiance to one of the monarchs \u2013 <u><u>not</u></u> that monarch\u2019s Court, but the monarch him-or-herself \u2013 the crowns won\u2019t appear at all. He says that he wants to craft a pledge to ensure that the monarchs in question will never ask those who swear to them to do anything which goes against their true court\u2019s philosophy, and that they won\u2019t try to trick or manipulate their allies into joining the Seasonal courts either.<br /> <br /> I confess that I don\u2019t know enough about Changeling politics to hazard a guess as to whether this is a good plan or not. Marguerite seemed willing to go along with it (she\u2019s never wanted the Crown of Night anyway), and Gawain was cautiously optimistic, though he made it clear that participation in this program should be entirely voluntary, and that he didn\u2019t intend to swear allegiance to any of the current sitting monarchs. Lowjack agreed that this wouldn\u2019t hurt his plan, as the Dawn Court crown isn\u2019t one of the ones that\u2019s supposed to be emerging in the near future.<br /> <br /> Boss Lowjack also asked Marguerite to drag her feet on actually swearing a pledge to one of the monarchs. It\u2019s part of a contingency plan\u2026 if the crowns materialize despite his best efforts, he would rather Marguerite inherit the position than Salk, who is apparently the runner-up. Lowjack doesn\u2019t trust Salk, and I can only assume that he has cause to feel that way.<br /> <br /> Before he left, we shared a little of our own information. Questioning glances were fired back and forth between members of the motley as to whether we should tell him about Gloria\u2026 but in the end there didn\u2019t seem to be any other choice. He is the Freehold\u2019s spymaster, and unwilling agents of Hollywood are something he needs to know about. I also mentioned a theory we had kicked around earlier: since Gloria\u2019s directives were so basic and simplistic, it\u2019s possible that she wasn\u2019t even a targeted spy. The Hollywood Courts might have put that sort of basic programming in <u><u>everyone</u></u> over there, to cast a wide net.<br /> <br /> Lowjack considered our information, and thanked us for sharing it, and then took his leave. I think he planned to meet with Felicity next, though Marguerite warned him that his plan would be a hard-sell with her, as our Day Court neighbor wants that crown for herself. Lowjack said that he thought he could get enough people to support his plan to make it effective even without Felicity\u2019s cooperation, but he wanted to make the offer first as a courtesy.<br /> <br /> The crowds had pretty much cleared out by the time our meeting with Boss Lowjack was concluded, and we found Becky, Desiree, and Gloria gathered around one of the tables speculating about who had hooked up with whom behind closed doors. Seriously, they even had a diagram (in which yours truly sat in the center of a vast web of connections, naturally). They called it \u201cfriend-fic,\u201d though I don\u2019t claim to understand the term.<br /> <br /> Marguerite had been acting more like herself lately, and I\u2019d heard Julia comment earlier that she seemed to be regaining her libido. She proved the truth of this statement to us that night, after almost dragging me and D (willingly, of course) into her bedroom to ravish us. It was good to see her back to her old self again. I\u2019m starting to think that this whole mess might turn out okay in the end after all.<br /> <br /> We managed to drag ourselves out of bed in time for Sex Breakfast on Monday morning, and found the usual suspects all assembled. Banter was flying fast and furious as usual, until D kissed me goodbye and regretfully made ready to go to work. Gloria gave the two of us a nervous glance, and then asked if she could speak with D privately for a moment. My honey agreed amicably, and the two of them walked out of the kitchen together.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t remember much of what was discussed after that; I was too busy staring a hole in the door through which they\u2019d left. A few minutes later, D walked back in looking just as chipper as ever, and reiterated the fact that she had to get changed and head to work. I offered to walk her out, and she agreed.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo, you want the full run-down, or are you just curious about where our hands were the whole time?\u201d she asked with a twinkle in her eye.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s not what this is about,\u201d I said softly as I closed the door to our room behind me so that she could change. \u201cI mean, it kind of is, but not in the way you think. What did she say to you? If you don\u2019t mind my asking\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> D shrugged. \u201cThe usual. She\u2019s working through a lot of stuff, and she needs time to figure out where all this is going.\u201d Her look softened, and she drew me into a hug. \u201cIs this bothering you, babe?\u201d she asked softly. \u201cBecause you know you only have to say the word\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know,\u201d I almost spat back. \u201cThat\u2019s part of the problem\u2026 but it\u2019s <u><u>my</u></u> problem. You don\u2019t need to worry about it. I\u2019ll get over it.\u201d<br /> <br /> D sighed. \u201cIf it\u2019s going to cause trouble between us, Jules, it\u2019s not worth it. You know how I feel about you. I won\u2019t let anything get in the way of that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI <u><u>know</u></u>,\u201d I said again, a little louder, \u201cbut that\u2019s not fair. It\u2019s not right, Maria. You have feelings for this girl, even if you don\u2019t know quite what they are yet. You\u2019ve been so good about my relationship with Oleander\u2026 I know it bothers you sometimes, but you haven\u2019t made a big deal of it at all. You\u2019re willing to share me. And now someone comes along who could maybe become that for you, and all I can think of is how threatened I am. If I can\u2019t get over this, then it means I\u2019m just being a hypocritical bitch, and you\u2019ll see\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll see that I\u2019m in love with someone who can be a hypocritical bitch from time to time,\u201d D interrupted me smoothly, \u201cand I\u2019ll deal with it, and we\u2019ll go on just like before. Nobody\u2019s perfect, Jules, but you are my life. Whatever you need out of this relationship, I\u2019m prepared to give it.\u201d<br /> <br /> I threw my arms around her, which made it difficult for her to continue putting on her scrubs. \u201cGod, I love you,\u201d I whispered through my tears. \u201cYou\u2019re the best girlfriend anyone could ask for, and I swear I\u2019ll work through this so that I can show you the same consideration.\u201d I thought about telling her that I would drop everyone else if she asked me to. I\u2019ve said it to her before, and it\u2019s still true. I\u2019m convinced that D is my soulmate, and I will sacrifice anything to keep what we\u2019ve found together. <br /> <br /> But the thought of having to look into Oleander\u2019s big soulful eyes as I explain that to her is almost more than I can bear. I can\u2019t help it. I love her too, and I will do everything in my power to avoid hurting her unless I have no other option. I would die for either of those ladies. The same goes for Marguerite and Julia. And that\u2019s a little scary. Before I was Taken, I never knew I could feel this intensely about anything.<br /> <br /> The two of us walked downstairs together so that I could give her a kiss goodbye, and then she was off to work. As I was heading back upstairs to talk this whole thing through with Gloria, Gawain practically tackled me and informed me that the motley was going ice skating. I sort of blinked once or twice at the rapid change of subject, then cautiously agreed to his plan as long as he promised to put me down first so that I could speak with Gloria before we left. He did so with a good-natured (if somewhat condescending) pat on the head.<br /> <br /> What happened next was really difficult for me, if only because my own emotions about the situation were so tangled and confused. Insecurity, jealousy, more different jealousy, lust, love, and\u2026 dammit all, I actually <u><u>like</u></u> Gloria. I mean, I have no romantic designs on her, but I think she\u2019s a pretty nice person, and all things being equal, I\u2019d rather have her as a friend.<br /> <br /> So I knocked on her door, and she opened it a moment later. She gave me a quavery smile. \u201cHi, Lori,\u201d she said softly, \u201ccome on in.\u201d<br /> <br /> I took a seat in one of the guest room chairs. \u201cI\u2026 thought we should talk, Gloria,\u201d I said with what I hope she took as a friendly smile. \u201cI know you\u2019re going through a tough time right now, and I don\u2019t want to make things any more awkward for you. That\u2019s not what this is about, but\u2026 I thought we should speak with each other\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026about de la Rocha?\u201d she asked, one corner of her mouth twitching up into a wry grin.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah,\u201d I said, resolved, \u201cbut probably not how you think. I\u2019m not here to bare my fangs and stake out my territory, Gloria. I just want you to understand how things are between us, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe loves you,\u201d Gloria said in response, as if that began and ended the conversation. \u201cShe\u2019s told me that much. She said that anything that developed between us would have to allow her to stay with you. She called it a \u2018deal breaker.\u2019\u201d<br /> <br /> My smiled widened, and I felt my cheeks color. \u201cAnd I love her, with all my heart. Nothing is going to change that. But that doesn\u2019t mean that there\u2019s no room in our lives for other relationships\u2026 other loves. You\u2019ve seen us with Marguerite and Julia. Okay, admittedly the last few days haven\u2019t been typical for us, but you\u2019ve still seen enough to know that there\u2019s love there as well. And\u2026\u201d I paused for a moment. \u201cGloria, has D told you about Oleander?\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded hesitantly. \u201cShe\u2019s your other girlfriend, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded in turn. \u201cThe one that D and I don\u2019t share. D has been\u2026 well, she\u2019s been supremely understanding on that score. I can\u2019t do less for her.\u201d<br /> <br /> Gloria looked away. \u201cLori, the last thing I want to do is cause trouble for you guys. You\u2019ve all been so kind to me, letting me live here, rooting out what\u2026 what they <u><u>did</u></u> to me\u2026 I\u2019ll back off if that\u2019s what you want.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks,\u201d I said, meaning it, \u201cbut that\u2019s not what I want. I\u2019m\u2026 well, I\u2019m a very competitive person by nature. I try to blame that on something my Keeper did to me, but to be honest I think She just accentuated something that was already in me. So I might be just a little bit tense around you if you decide to see where this thing with D is going. I just want you to know that it\u2019s my problem, not yours, and that I\u2019m going to do my best to work on it, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> Her eyes widened. \u201cI\u2019m not sure if I can be involved with another woman like that,\u201d she said softly, \u201cbut if so\u2026 are you saying that you\u2019d be okay with me dating de la Rocha?\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cAnd a bit of advice\u2026 if you find out that you do have the capacity to love another woman, you\u2019d be hard-pressed to find one as strong, beautiful, and special as my D.\u201d My vision shimmered briefly, but I think I kept the tears from flowing.<br /> <br /> There were a few minutes of awkward silence, then Gloria spoke again. \u201cSo\u2026 your other girlfriend, Oleander. She and de la Rocha are friends, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah,\u201d I answered. \u201cThere have been a few tense moments here and there, but I think they get along really well all things considered.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGood,\u201d Gloria said, and she flashed me a genuine smile, \u201cbecause I think you\u2019re a good friend, Lori, and I don\u2019t want this situation with de la Rocha to mess that up either.\u201d<br /> <br /> She pulled me into a hug, and that was pretty much that. I won\u2019t claim that my emotions about this situation are now all wrapped up in a neat little package, but I think I have a better handle on the situation than I did before. Gloria doesn\u2019t want her feelings for D to damage what the two of us already have, and D gave me the awesome safety net of telling me that she would drop everyone else if necessary to keep me. I <u><u>think</u></u> I can deal with the two of them becoming close if anything develops.<br /> <br /> So, ice skating. I had thought that perhaps my skill at roller skating would serve me well on the ice, but alas! \u2018Twas not to be. Oh, I handled myself well enough as long as I didn\u2019t try anything fancy, but I was nowhere near the level of some of my friends, like Calamity and Jacob (though his command over ice probably gave him an edge, now that I think about it). Still, it was fun, and even falling down is a laugh when you\u2019re with good friends. Plus, the idea of roller skating while playing laser tag came up, and that sounds like a hell of a lot of fun.<br /> <br /> We skated for most of the afternoon. We\u2019d intended to go out to a nice Italian place for dinner, but Gawain got a text from Gloria as we were on our way out saying that someone had arrived at the Dream House looking for him, so we changed our plans and headed for home, while I called in an order to Ginelli\u2019s for a couple of pizzas.<br /> <br /> When we got back, Gloria met us at the door, having recently returned from her tour of the Freehold with Monica and Halley. Her face was about four different shades of red and purple, and she was sort of shifting uncomfortably as we approached.<br /> <br /> \u201cGloria, sweetie, is everything okay?\u201d I asked with genuine concern.<br /> <br /> \u201cTh\u2026 that man that\u2019s here to see your motley. He\u2019s in the kitchen,\u201d she stammered. Then, apparently feeling that more of an explanation was called for, she elaborated. \u201cHe\u2019s not wearing a shirt.\u201d<br /> <br /> Suddenly her flustered state made sense. \u201cJuan Carlos!\u201d I called out with dignity and grace (okay it might have come out as more of an excited squeal), making for the kitchen. He appeared a moment later, looking like the cover of some trashy romance novel. I ran up to him, threw my arms around him, and planted a big ol\u2019 kiss right on his lips. He didn\u2019t complain.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s wonderful to see you!\u201d I said with enthusiasm.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe feeling is mutual, <i><i>mi sirena</i></i>,\u201d he replied. \u201cI have come to speak with Gawain today, regarding Miss Chalcedony\u2019s dreams. I thought it would be best if I had as much information as possible before beginning.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course,\u201d I said, all business once more. \u201cYou two have important work to do. You don\u2019t need any distractions. But\u2026 look me up before you leave town, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt is a promise,\u201d he said solemnly, and he kissed my hand before turning back to speak to Gawain. Gosh!<br /> <br /> I found Gloria in the entrance hall, and she seemed to be breathing normally again. \u201cSorry,\u201d I said with a wink, \u201che seems to have that effect on people when they first meet him. I seem to recall that all I could say was \u2018woof\u2019 the first time I saw him.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cUnderstandable,\u201d Gloria muttered.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo how was your tour of the Freehold?\u201d I asked when she\u2019d calmed down a bit more.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt was fun,\u201d she replied. \u201cI got to see the Lighthouse, and Glamour Springs, and the Clinic, and a few other important landmarks. I met lots of friendly people.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd Monica was available this time?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, yeah,\u201d Gloria said, \u201cshe and Halley and Dominika showed me around.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDid she seem okay?\u201d I asked, concern creeping into my voice.<br /> <br /> Gloria thought about it. \u201cWell, I don\u2019t really know her that well, but now that you mention it, she did seem a bit distracted,\u201d she said after a moment.<br /> <br /> I sighed. \u201cI\u2019d better call her and see what\u2019s up,\u201d I said.<br /> <br /> Turns out that Monica has recently been through a break-up. She\u2019d been dating a mortal guy, and things were getting pretty serious between them\u2026 to the point that she was about to reveal her true nature to him! Unfortunately, just as she was about to take the plunge, he broke things off. She\u2019s been understandably depressed by this turn of events, and has thrown herself into a series of one-night stands with various other members of the Freehold, including Halley and Dominika. I tried to offer my support as a friend, but sometimes people in these situations just need a little time to reflect.<br /> <br /> The doorbell rang as I hung up with her. Figuring I\u2019d give the delivery boy a thrill, I undid the top button of my shirt and adopted a sexy pose as I answered the door.<br /> <br /> \u201cOnly one button for the poor pizza delivery boy?\u201d D smirked as she gave me a friendly kiss hello. \u201cAnd after he drove all the way out here\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHow did you know we ordered pizza?\u201d I asked. \u201cAnd since when do you ring the bell? You live here!\u201d<br /> <br /> She chuckled and pointed at the delivery car across the lot. \u201cGive him a thrill, why don\u2019t you?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> I sighed and rolled my eyes\u2026 but I also unbuttoned the rest of my shirt. Who am I to say no to free glamour?<br /> <br /> Marguerite came to get me as I was taking the pizzas into the kitchen, looking worried sick about something. She asked me to come with her, and after pausing to think about it for a moment, asked Jacob if he would come as well. She led us to the room Desiree has been using, and ushered us inside. Desiree was lying sprawled on the bed, almost passed-out drunk and dead to the world, surrounded by a number of mostly-empty bottles. We assume that she was drinking due to a combination of depression about Gloria and guilt over what she sees as her betrayal of the Director.<br /> <br /> I took a look at her while Jacob examined the bottles. He did some quick calculations and told us that someone of Desiree\u2019s body weight shouldn\u2019t be in serious medical trouble considering the amount of alcohol she had apparently consumed. I checked her pulse, breathing, and pupils myself. She was responsive, but pretty out of it. Marguerite had known enough to turn her on her side, which ameliorated my most pressing concerns.<br /> <br /> \u201cTomorrow\u2019s not going to be much fun for you, sweetie,\u201d I whispered to her, \u201cbut maybe I can help a little bit.\u201d I did what I could using Spring contracts to rehydrate her, which I hope will help her deal with the inevitable hangover.<br /> <br /> After we were sure that Desiree was going to be okay, the rest of us gathered upstairs with the pizzas for movie night (after she was feeling better, Desiree did eventually join us). D had picked tonight\u2019s double-feature, and seemed inordinately pleased with herself for reasons which did not become apparent until somewhat later.<br /> <br /> The first film was called <u><u>The Matrix</u></u>, and was a mind-blowing sci-fi epic about a world in which machines hold humans prisoners within their own minds. People are confined to small mechanical pods, and sensory input is fed directly into their brains, making them think that they\u2019re living normal lives. The theory is that this makes people placid; if they don\u2019t know they\u2019re prisoners, they won\u2019t try to resist or escape. And why were the machines doing this? To harvest the bioelectrical energy generated by the human body, of course!<br /> <br /> The film was fun. There was a lot of good kung-fu action which had been enhanced by computers\u2026 somehow. The scenes where they slowed down the action so that you could see bullets tearing trails through the air in their wake were particularly memorable. I confess that I was sort of taken out of the moment by the machines\u2019 motivation, though\u2026 seems like those pods and the computers running them would consume a lot more energy than they could harvest from a human body. And, I mean, even if clouds of smog obscured the sun, making solar power impractical (as was implied), there\u2019s still hydroelectric power, wind power, nuclear power, geothermal power, and probably a dozen more options I could name if I was smarter\u2026 none of which would require the expenditure of the resources necessary to keep six billion human beings alive and functioning. But everyone just gave me blank looks when I brought this up, so I let it drop.<br /> <br /> Or maybe I was just nit-picking because of the awful thought that occurred to me about halfway through the film\u2026 what if everything I\u2019ve experienced over the last year is just a dream the Empress is giving me? What if I\u2019m still a slave, and all of this is just some elaborate trap designed to sate my desire for freedom? What if the times that I dream I\u2019m back in Her palace are real, and <u><u>this</u></u> is the dream?<br /> <br /> The second film was called <u><u>Bound</u></u>, and while it shared directors (and one actor) with the first movie, they couldn\u2019t have been more different. It was the story of two women: a tough, self-reliant ex-con and a Mafioso\u2019s trophy wife. The two of them hook up and decided to steal a couple of million dollars from the mob. Things go horribly wrong along the way, of course, and they have to use all their wiles and cunning to survive the experience.<br /> <br /> <u><u>Bound</u></u> was at its core a heist movie, but there was a strong undercurrent of lesbian romance to it as well. Corky and Violet are fairly obviously attracted to each other from the very first, and the sex scenes involving the two of them are incredibly hot. I found myself glancing fondly at D whenever Corky did something brave or belligerent, and caught her smirking back at me whenever Violet used her innate charm to get what she wanted. I didn\u2019t take offense; while Violet\u2019s strength is very different from Corky\u2019s, she\u2019s still an exceptionally strong character in her own way.<br /> <br /> Well that certainly set the stage for the rest of the evening. D obviously found the film very moving on a personal level (which is why she suggested it), but none of us could deny the fact that it was an arousing picture, and she, Marguerite, Julia and I retired to share a bed in pretty short order after the credits rolled. Poor Gloria\u2026 that can\u2019t have been an easy film for someone in her position to watch.<br /> <br /> So, fade to sex, and when the lights came up again this morning it was Julia\u2019s birthday! I confess I hadn\u2019t planned anything like I did with Marguerite\u2019s birthday last week\u2026 with everything that\u2019s happened over the past few days, I was more worried about whether Julia and Marguerite were still going to be living with us than thinking about how to celebrate a happy occasion. Still, fair is fair, and when Julia pouted about how she didn\u2019t get a \u201cbreakfast treat\u201d like Marguerite had gotten, I shrugged out of my robe, climbed onto the table, and allowed her to eat her breakfast off of me\u2026 which was perhaps just a <u><u>bit</u></u> exhibitionist of me, considering that we were in the middle of Sex Breakfast with the others at the time.<br /> <br /> Cheese omelets fresh from the frying pan are <u><u>really</u></u> hot, by the way. Just, y\u2019know, in case you were wondering. But Julia smiled \u2013 I mean <u><u>really</u></u> smiled, from her soul \u2013 so I figure I can take a little mild scalding if that\u2019s the result.<br /> <br /> Marguerite has given Julia the reins of power in their relationship for the day, and Julia is milking it for all it\u2019s worth. I haven\u2019t seen her quite work up to using Marguerite\u2019s patented \u201csultan clap\u201d against her yet, but I\u2019m sure it\u2019s coming. She even tried to levy her authority against <u><u>me</u></u> at one point. I let it slide because it\u2019s her birthday, but if it continues we might have to have a discussion at some point.<br /> <br /> The incident in question came when Desiree and Gloria joined us a bit later. Apparently neither one of them was quite prepared to find Julia eating her breakfast off of my naked body while I sprawled across the table. Gloria muttered something about believing that the term \u201csex breakfast\u201d wasn\u2019t supposed to be literal, and turned an alarming shade of purple. D whispered that it was Julia\u2019s birthday, and that things like this don\u2019t happen every day. Gloria squeezed D\u2019s hand in response, and Desiree turned away with a dark look on her face.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo,\u201d Julia said imperiously after she had licked the last of the cheese off of me, \u201cyou can\u2019t be gloomy on my birthday, Desiree. Lori, go make out with her and help her feel better.\u201d<br /> <br /> I shot her a look, but got up and walked over to Desiree. \u201cOkay,\u201d I said grudgingly, \u201cbut I\u2019m doing this because I want to, because Desiree is <u><u>hot</u></u>, and <u><u>not</u></u> because you told me to.\u201d<br /> <br /> Julia shrugged. \u201cOkay,\u201d she said with a grin. I\u2019m not sure if she accepted my chastisement or if she was just humoring me. If I find out it was the latter, then we will have words later. I left my status as a slave behind in Arcadia, and I will <u><u>not</u></u> take up those chains again for anyone.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I\u2019m probably just being touchy about this. When Marguerite asked her what she wanted to do today, she got a sort of shy-nervous look on her face and hesitantly suggested \u201cgraveyard walk?\u201d Most of us agreed to accompany her on such an excursion, though Calamity and a few of the others opted to stay behind. I asked her if she wanted to go right then, or wait until it was dark. She thought about it for a minute or two, and then quietly asked if we could do <u><u>both</u></u>: a daylight walk for the motley, and then a nighttime stroll for just the four of us.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd Lori,\u201d she said, all sweetness and insecurity, \u201cwould you mind\u2026 I mean, would it be too much trouble\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat do you want, sweetie?\u201d I asked, curious.<br /> <br /> \u201cCould you\u2026 put on one of the Gothic dresses I picked out for you before we go?\u201d she asked, blushing and looking at her own feet. \u201cPlease?\u201d she added at a prod from Marguerite.<br /> <br /> I smiled and leaned in for a kiss. \u201cI\u2019d be happy to,\u201d I said, \u201cbut I\u2019ll need some help lacing up the corset.\u201d<br /> <br /> As you can probably imagine, I did not lack for volunteers. Marguerite and D eventually got me trussed up in that Victorian torture device, while Julia manically whispered directions to them (most of which seemed to be \u201ctighter\u201d). It would be an exaggeration to say that my boobs were pushed up into my face by the time they were finished with me\u2026 but not by much.<br /> <br /> Before we left, Marguerite asked to speak with me privately. I followed her into an empty room, and the two of us sort of looked at each other a moment before either one spoke.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo,\u201d we both said at exactly the same moment. I laughed, and indicated that she should go first.<br /> <br /> She pulled the ring Julia had bought for her out of her pocket. I whooped quietly. \u201cI knew it!\u201d I said. \u201cThat\u2019s <u><u>exactly</u></u> what my \u2018so\u2019 was going to be about! Are you going to propose today?\u201d<br /> <br /> Marguerite nodded. \u201cI think that I am. Julia is\u2026 well, the last few days have proven how much we mean to each other. I would like to make that official. But I wished to ask for your advice about a few things first.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShoot,\u201d I said, elated.<br /> <br /> She wrinkled her nose. \u201c\u2019Shoot,\u2019\u201d she muttered, \u201chow very American. In any case, first I wanted to make certain that this \u2013 this new connection between Julia and I \u2013 would not damage the love that the four of us share.\u201d<br /> <br /> I shook my head. \u201cI love you both,\u201d I said, \u201cand nothing is going to change that. And I know that you both feel the same way about me. But we\u2019ve always known that within this big crazy love fest, there\u2019s you and Julia, and there\u2019s me and D. I know she feels the same way, so don\u2019t worry about it.\u201d<br /> <br /> Marguerite nodded. \u201c<i><i>C\u2019est vrai</i></i><i>,</i>\u201d she said softly, \u201cbut I had to make certain, no? And now, I also wished to ask you for advice on the proper way to propose. Do you think it should be in the graveyard as we walk, or should I do it on stage tonight? I thought perhaps declaring my love before so many people would make her happy\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I thought about it. \u201cShe\u2019s going to love it no matter how you do it,\u201d I said after a moment, \u201cbut I\u2019d probably go for the graveyard if it was me. And I\u2019d wait until tonight, when it\u2019s just the four of us. All of the most important people in her life will be there, and it\u2019ll show that you worked hard to propose in a place that would resonate with her character.\u201d<br /> <br /> Marguerite smiled, but it was a nervous, shaky smile. \u201cYou are correct, of course,\u201d she said, pulling me into an embrace. \u201cI shall proceed with my plans. And\u2026 if my courage should falter\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I grinned back. \u201cI\u2019ll keep you on mission,\u201d I promised.<br /> <br /> Marguerite gave me a grateful nod, then looked away. \u201cI\u2026 I would also like to revisit the idea of oath-binding the four of us together,\u201d she said quietly, \u201cwhen you are ready.\u201d I didn\u2019t know quite what to say to that, so I just agreed to think about it for now.<br /> <br /> We were about to head out when I got a call. A quick glance at the ID on my phone showed that it was Monica calling. Once I answered, it was clear to me that she wasn\u2019t thinking rationally; she was clearly randy and quite possibly drunk. She asked me in a low growl if I wanted to come over to her place for a few hours, and made it clear that she intended to ravish me if I agreed.<br /> <br /> I put her on hold for a minute and asked D for her advice. \u201cI doubt you\u2019ll hurt her if you sleep with her,\u201d she told me, \u201cbut it probably won\u2019t help much either. She does this when something has upset her romantically. She just has to work through it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t want to do anything that\u2019s going to damage our friendship,\u201d I said a little helplessly.<br /> <br /> \u201cThen don\u2019t do it,\u201d D advised.<br /> <br /> I sighed and reconnected with Monica. \u201cSweetie,\u201d I said softly, \u201cI don\u2019t think this is a good idea right now.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know it\u2019s not,\u201d Monica said breathily, \u201cbut I want it anyway.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMonica,\u201d I said evenly, \u201clisten to me for a minute, please. You\u2019re a close friend, and I wouldn\u2019t risk that for anything. You\u2019re upset and hurt right now, and you\u2019re not thinking rationally. Give it a few days, okay? If you still want this when you\u2019re feeling more like yourself, I promise I won\u2019t say no. But right now, I just don\u2019t think I can do this.\u201d<br /> <br /> There was silence on her end of the line for a few seconds. \u201cOkay,\u201d she said at last. \u201cI understand. Thanks, Lori. You\u2019re a good friend.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m trying to be,\u201d I said. \u201cFeel better, Monica. I\u2019ll see you soon.\u201d And she hung up. I hope I handled that well; the last thing I want is to hurt her when she\u2019s already feeling so low.<br /> <br /> I joined the others and we drove out to a local cemetery and began to walk around. It was actually quite beautiful; it\u2019s still warm and sunny in mid-November in Southern California, and the tranquil atmosphere made for a very pleasant afternoon. I confess that at one point I succumbed to the urge to play Snow White, and I twirled about in my pretty dress, singing and calling a few songbirds to flutter around me and land on my arms. When Gawain made a wry comment, I turned on him and went from Snow White to Wicked Queen in seconds flat. \u201cFear me!\u201d I bellowed, \u201cfor I command the legions of the air!\u201d The legions of the air twittered cutely, but made no move to attack.<br /> <br /> Julia was waxing rhapsodic about the joy of making love in a graveyard. D commented that she\u2019d never made love in a graveyard, and I couldn\u2019t resist chiming in that I had. D raised an eyebrow at me.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat?\u201d I said innocently. \u201cI was the bad-girl preacher\u2019s daughter in a small town. My house was graveyard-adjacent.\u201d<br /> <br /> That started D bragging about her sexual escapades on a roller coaster again. I swear, the two of us will have to go to an amusement park together sometime just so that she won\u2019t have that to hold over me anymore!<br /> <br /> Anyway, it was a very pleasant afternoon, but I should stop writing in this diary and get ready for the show\u2026 and after the show, the proposal!<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T13:53:24-07:00","id":885663,"title":"","content":"<b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> Tuesday, November 11<sup>th</sup><br /> Nine years, seven months, twelve days<br /> Days without stabbing: 4<br /> <br /> Today is Julia's birthday. The motley's taking her out for a cemetery walk currently. I elected not to join in. Things remain strained between myself and Insincere Marguerite and by extension Julia. I did wish her a happy birthday and that I hoped she enjoyed the walk. She thanked me. Insincere Marguerite started to scold her but apparently she's allowed to do as she wishes today, even speak to me. As I write this, I'm looking at her present. I'd forgotten about it with everything going on but it was delivered at some point over the past couple of days and someone stuck it here in the office. I'm not sure what to do with it honestly. Maybe Gawain can give it to her. I am pretty sure the only thing she wants from me right now is the pound of flesh closest to my heart.<br /> <br /> She's hurt and angry. They both are. And it's my fault. But dammit, Insincere Marguerite is alive and safe. We all are, even Chalcedony. It's easy to look back and say I should have done better but time was short and I didn't know what was going to happen and I was afraid for my Darkling sister. I made the best decision I could and I can't change it now. I can only move forward. I can only try to make them both understand why I did it and that I never intended to harm Insincere Marguerite.<br /> <br /> I have been such a mess these past few days. Dr Emmett asked about my meditation this morning and I told her that I just hadn't had the time or focus with all the turmoil. She gave me that look, the one that she does when I'm being stubborn or evasive or just stupid and she pointed out to me that such times are exactly when I needed it the most. She's right of course, but I was so far down the rabbit hole of my own navel that I wasn't thinking about much of anything clearly. Hell, I almost didn't even go see her this morning. But Jacob came to me over the weekend and told me he felt like he was slipping back into the person he'd been before, cold and heartless. He asked me about the therapy and if I thought it helped and if it would help him. I managed to pull my shit together long enough to talk to him about it. After a bit, he decided to give it a try and I suggested he go with me today. And I'm glad, both because it really does help to talk about it and because I needed the nudge to make sure I went today. I did not realize just how much needed it.<br /> <br /> Not that I haven't had people looking after me. Gawain and Becky have barely left my side. Annika's come out twice in the past couple of days. Lori and Jacob have both made sure to offer their support. They all care so deeply about me, and it's good, because these past few days, I certainly haven't. Damn, I really need to speak to Becky and apologize. I know what's been in my heart and why she's been so watchful. I hope she didn't tell Gawain about some of the things that crossed my mind. Not that he needs her or any contract to tell him honestly. He's been in my dreams. He's been with me since the Hedge. He knows my twisted heart and yet he just won't give up on me, no matter how hard I try to. I think he tries to love me enough for both of us because he knows how much I don't.<br /> <br /> I don't love myself, hell most of the time I hate myself. Sometimes more than others. Sometimes it's so small I can ignore it, pretend it's not there. Sometimes I can almost forget. But then something happens and it's back, as large and strong and vivid as ever. Ignoring it won't make it go away, it only makes it wait. I let it overwhelm me. Friday was not a good day for the Last Dance. We should have come together to deal with it but I was too lost in my past, in my own self loathing, to do anything.<br /> <br /> Of course, blaming myself now for being too busy hating myself doesn't fix the motley. Neither does running away to Snow Globe or dying. That's a coward's way out and I won't do that to everyone I care about. Honestly, I'm not sure what the answer is but I do know that I am sick and tired of slinking around like a dog that's been beaten. And I'm pretty sure everyone else has had more than enough of putting up with my pity party. I am Calamity, I am stronger than this bullshit. Why? Because I say so. Because I'm the one that decides what kind of monster I am.<br /> <br /> Dr Emmett has been telling me for months that I have to forgive myself or I will never be able to move forward. Then Jacob said the same thing to me after therapy as we drove home. They're right, I know they are, but it's so much easier to say than it is to actually do. Today though... today when the doctor was going into it I snapped and asked her how I was supposed to forgive myself for these things I've done. (There may have been a few choice colorful metaphors sprinkled in as well.) She didn't flinch, but she did pause and then asked me what if it was someone else. Would I feel this same unrelenting hatred for someone else?<br /> <br /> I started to say of course I would, but I stopped myself. I sat back and I actually thought about it. I mean, I can be a judgmental bitch to be sure but I have always maintained that what happens in Arcadia stays in Arcadia. And as I thought about it, I thought about Monica. About how she murdered Tussaud while she was lost and disoriented in the Hedge. Not exactly the same, but close and I don't hate her for it. I don't blame her for it. Of course, now I find myself wondering if it haunts her. I've never seen it, but how many people really know what's lurking beneath the blood-splattered veneer of cocky murderous bitch I try to project? We didn't get into it, but Dr Emmett could tell I was thinking about it and she told me to consider it and we'd return to it Thursday.<br /> <br /> And sitting here with my head as clear as it gets after going through my forms, I am trying to look at it objectively. I had barely been back a day. I didn't know what a fetch was so I was unprepared to discover that they hadn't missed me. I didn't know what I could do. I didn't know what the glass was or that it was inside me. I had been so small. So weak. And suddenly I wasn't. I was dangerous. I was strong. I had power and they were afraid of me. All those years of pent up helpless anger I'd damned up came flooding out and it felt good. So very, very good.<br /> <br /> What I did was wrong... evil... horrible. And the worst part was how even as I came to my senses I couldn't shake how much I enjoyed that thrill and rush of power. I'd like to say it's just the glass in my heart but I don't believe that. It's the spark, but without those years of abuse, of being helpless and weak to feed the flames it wouldn't consume me the way it did that night. The way it still does if I let down my guard. I like hurting people. I enjoy it.<br /> <br /> But that's not what happened. I DID control it Friday. I didn't give into the urge to sink my blades into Chalcedony\u2019s skin and taste her fear and pain while her blood washed over my fingers. I didn't set out to harm to my Darkling Sister. Everything else may have spiraled out of control, but I kept my need in check. I did end up hurting her, more than I meant to, more than I realized I was going to, but not because I wanted to. That has to mean something. Even if it doesn't to her. Even if she can never forgive me. Even if it doesn't keep it from hurting every time she looks at me right now...<br /> <br /> NO. I have to pull myself together. This motley isn't whole yet but the world isn't going to wait for us to be before it throws another punch. There is no more time for me to be weepy and maudlin and useless. There are people that wish my family harm. It's time for me to be the monster they need. Time for me to be fucking dangerous. Time to remind everyone that if you cross the Last Dance you cross Calamity. And maybe Lori's god will have mercy on you, but I sure as hell won't.<br /> <br /> It seems like everyone has an angle on these thrice damned Day and Night crowns. The monarchs feel threatened and powerful people are worried about the status quo. And with Insincere Marguerite being likely to receive the Night Crown that makes her a target for those that fear the crowns or want to control them. And given that Salk has designs on it her own court cannot even be trusted to protect her. Not that they've ever really done so. But she has us now. We will protect her. I will protect her or die trying.<br /> <br /> And then there's Hollywood. Do they have their eye on the Dream House in particular or are they just sending people wherever they can into the freehold? I guess it depends on how targeted Gloria's programming was and that's something we have no way to know. So I have to assume they've taken an interest in us. We're strong and we've shown that we're prepared to act to defend the Freehold. More than that, we're also not tied as a motley to any single court, so we can act as a unifying element in this Freehold. Whether they want to destroy us or just steal The Table the best way to begin is by dividing us and turning us against each other. So I have to assume they'll try something else once they figure out that we've unmasked their unwilling spy. Will they try again or will they move to something more direct? Have to be ready for either.<br /> <br /> But right now Annika is here and I should speak to her about a number. If we work today and tomorrow both, I should be able to get something new together for the weekend. 'Love Stinks' is just... now is really not the time for that number so I need something else. Something I can throw some real trademark Calamity aggression into. Maybe a couple of Rob Zombie numbers? I haven't done anything with him. If I focus Annika and I can hammer out one today for tonight's show and another tomorrow and then have them as a set for the weekend shows.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> So, the dream healing seemed to go well for Gloria. She was a little freaked out, at least according to De la Rocha who talked to her, but otherwise okay. The programming, which apparently was rather simplistic, was removed and she is back to herself. Not that she wasn\u2019t acting like herself before. Just now she\u2019s not keeping notes on us anymore. All of which are good things in my book. The commands that were given to Gloria were rather simple. Keep notes on the Motley and drop them at a dead drop. Whoever did this did not put a lot of thought into it, so the idea that she might be part of a larger group of people brainwashed all at the same time came up. Kinda scary if you ask me. I do not like the idea that the Hollywood Courts could be programming large groups of people all at once. Are they just throwing a bunch of expendable people at the problem and hope they get some returns? And is it just our freehold that they are investigating?<br /> <br /> After all that, Lowjack called and asked if he could run an idea past Gawain and Insincere Marguerite later tonight after the show. He said that he did not mind if the rest of us were there. He implied he\u2019d appreciate our input on something as well. I said that sounded fine to me and would let the others know to expect him. I will admit that my curiosity was piqued at that. I wondered what he had to talk about and whether or not certain members of my motley would be civil towards my king or not. I know that Calamity has been upset with him since he indirectly threatened Insincere Marguerite after Tamara was attacked.<br /> <br /> During the show I noticed that Dark Kimberly and White Maria, while not sitting at the same table, were sitting close enough to talk. And they were doing just that. Perhaps some healing is going on between those two? I would be good if it was. They have been on the outs for a while now. Maybe that old phrase is right, time heals all wounds. Tonight was also the first night that Calamity was back to walking the crowd and talking to people. She\u2019s so much better at it than I am. I could see Becky and Gawain keeping an eye on her, so I stayed at the bar and took care of customers. Just another sign that things are starting to go back to \u201cnormal\u201d around here. I do not think that things will go back to the way that they were before the events surrounding Chalcedony\u2019s departure, but they will probably get close. Marguerite and Julia haven\u2019t moved out yet and Insincere Marguerite will at least remain in the room with Calamity and acknowledge her presence. And now Calamity is back to work. I know that she\u2019s been beating herself up about what happened. She is getting to the point where she can be functional again, in a real way. Not that fake \u201cI\u2019m fine\u201d kind of way. There is also something else fueling her self-hate kick. I have some ideas, but I don\u2019t know for sure. I\u2019ll talk to her about it at some point.<br /> <br /> Okay\u2026so Lowjack came to the Dream House after the show was over. He let himself in the back door that I left open for him, so no one would see him come in. He wanted to keep things quiet for now, and after hearing him out I can see why. He wanted to talk to Insincere Marguerite and Gawain specifically about having all non-seasonal courtiers pledge allegiance to a seasonal monarch, not the court, just that individual monarch. He is hoping that by doing this it will forestall the appearance of the Day and Night Court crowns. Other freeholds have been torn apart by having a seasonal monarch in charge at the same time as a diurnal monarch. The people ended up following either the seasonal or diurnal but not everyone followed the same one. It got chaotic. Lowjack is hoping that he can forestall the Day/Night crowns from appearing and creating a mess like that in our freehold.<br /> <br /> On the flip side to that he did say that he wanted Insincere Margueirte to drag her feet on doing that. Just in case the Day/Night crowns do show up he wanted her to be in the running to get it. He\u2019s hoping that if those crowns do appear then something can be worked out with all the monarchs involved on who the people follow when. But he really doesn\u2019t want Salk to get the crown, hence Marguerite taking her time about who she might pledge herself to. Gawain was not keen on pledging himself to any of the monarchs and Lowjack said that was fine. He just wanted a majority of the non-seasonal Courtiers in the city to do it.<br /> <br /> After that the conversation turned to Hollywood. Significant looks went around the motely and we all agreed to tell Lowjack about Gloria and what had been done to her. He agreed that it is possible that the brainwashing was done on a larger scale than just individuals. We discussed the idea of planting misinformation in the dead drop location or maybe spreading the word to the Hollywood freehold itself that those in charge are brainwashing members of the freehold. Lowjack did say that he didn\u2019t want to mention any of this to the other monarchs yet since he\u2019s not sure which way they\u2019ll fall on the matter. Apparently he\u2019s been having problems negotiating with Augustine about Hollywood. The Viscount is all for war with Hollywood, and Lowjack understands that but would rather just fight the few that are actually causing the problems rather than every citizen just trying to protect their homes.<br /> <br /> I saw the sense in Lowjack\u2019s idea and I think the others did too. At least they all agreed to keep quiet on things until Lowjack can get something in place as far as the dead drop goes. If we can sow the seeds of truth among the Hollywood Courtiers then it might make our job a lot easier when we do finally do something about Hollywood. I know that Calamity at least has been keen on dealing with the problem that is the Hollywood Courts. I don\u2019t blame her. They\u2019ve been sending spies into our midst for a while now. And if their network is bigger than just one or two individuals it\u2019s likely that some information has made it back to them. We don\u2019t know what they know and what they are planning. It would be prudent on our parts to remove the threat before they have a chance to act.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Well, today started out good. Gawain made steak and eggs for breakfast and I made the usual coffee. And on the plus side Insincere Marguerite seemed a lot more cheerful this morning than she has in the past couple of days. I count this as a step in the right direction on her road to recovery. I think the others were just as encouraged as I was to see Marguerite so much closer to her usual self.<br /> <br /> Also on the note of things progressing, Gloria said that she would be picked up by Haley and will be meeting up with her and Monica for a tour around town. She has been in town for a little while now and has not yet gotten a full tour. Granted it was probably a good thing that her tour was delayed since she\u2019d been under the influence of a compulsion before. Not sure if she was just to get information on us or the whole freehold. Either way, she\u2019s free of it and can now look around town with impunity.<br /> <br /> After that brief update Gawain decided that the motley was going to go ice skating. We didn\u2019t discuss options, he just kind of said that we should all go. I agreed. It\u2019s been awhile since I\u2019ve been ice skating. I used to skate at home, well in both of my homes. Russia and Oregon. I also skated in the Lady\u2019s realm. There was not a lot of free time to do frivolous things while in her service and I certainly did not skate before she found me. I thought only of survival until that fateful day. Once in her service though I would occasionally have some free time and I would skate. Rook sometimes joined me. He was proficient at skating but didn\u2019t enjoy it as much as I did. But I also skated before I was taken, so today was a nice reminder of happier childhood days. Calamity and I were by far the better skaters. Most of the others had never been to a rink before, but I thought they all did a really good job for their first time. Julia stayed on the sidelines and sketched us as we skated. I got to see a glimpse of her drawing later. It was really good.<br /> <br /> We laughed and joked around, but one thing that stuck in my head was our conversation about lying. It started out with someone telling Gawain that he had a three headed monkey behind him. From there it moved on to lying in more general terms. Insincere Marguerite\u2019s advice was no not tell the same lie more than once. Gawain said that little lies were okay as long as no one got hurt. I didn\u2019t say this out loud, but I disagreed with Marguerite. It\u2019s okay to tell the same lie more than once, as long as you are consistent and stick to it. Either that or make sure that the people that you lie to cannot collaborate and catch you in said lie. I told a lot of lies to a lot of different people over the years, and I was good at it. I have a good poker face, so I could straight up lie to someone\u2019s face and have them believe whatever I told them. I even made friends with some of my targets. At the time I was able to lie to them just as easily as I was able to lie to strangers. Now would be different though. The only lies that I have told to the motley have been lies of omission. When Rook came back I told the others about my past loyalties. When the drug thing came up, I admitted what I\u2019d been up to. I didn\u2019t want some poor shmuck getting fired because of my activities. So, I guess I agree with Gawain. As long as no one gets hurt. It can be a slippery slope though. If lying comes too easily it can become a habit. So, my personal practice is to just be truthful, if somewhat secretive. It\u2019s a little hard after having been Rime for so long, but if I want to truly make a break from the man I used to be, then I have to change how I do things.<br /> <br /> It was after the ice skating that things got interesting. Gawain got a text from Gloria saying that Juan Carlos was at the Dream House, so we all headed back to the house. Apparently she was more than a little flustered because of Juan Carlos\u2019s habit of not wearing a shirt. We arrived at the house within short order and Gawain rescued Gloria from further embarrassment by taking Juan Carlos off to talk to him about the dream healing for Chalcedony. While he was doing that Insincere Marguerite came up to me and Lori. She was worried about Desiree. Desiree had not joined us skating claiming that she wasn\u2019t up to it. We found out just how low her mood had been when we went down to see her. She had pulled out several bottles of alcohol from behind the bar and had a good bit to drink. Insincere Marguerite found her quite drunk and semi-asleep. I estimated how much she had to drink based on how much was gone from each bottle. It helps having a photographic memory. I knew how much was in each bottle to start with. I guessed that with the amount she drank and given her body weight that she was not in immediate danger of alcohol poisoning, but she was in for one whopper of a hangover. Lori worked her Spring Court magic to help Desiree on that front. After a little while Desiree was up and about and Gawain had a chat with her. I think he did something to boost her mood and generally gave her some advice. I think the whole reason she\u2019d been feeling so down was due to the strained relationship between her and Gloria. Desiree really cares for the other girl, but Gloria is being a bit standoffish.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile Lori talked to Gloria about what she \u2018d been up to today. Gloria told her about being shown around the freehold by Haley and Monica. Apparently there was some concern about Monica so Lori gave her a call later. I think they worked some things out, but I got the impression from Lori\u2019s mood later that she had not been able to help the other woman as much as she\u2019d have liked to. I can understand that. There\u2019s just sometimes no matter how much you want to help someone it doesn\u2019t work the way you want it to. It\u2019s up to that other person to work things out in their own head before they can accept help from someone else. I feel the same way about Calamity. I have been trying to be supportive, but I don\u2019t think it\u2019s working the way I\u2019d like it to. There\u2019s just some things that she\u2019s going to have to come to terms with on her own before she can even begin to accept too much help from outside parties. She reacts well to Becky and Gawain\u2019s ministrations, and for that I\u2019m grateful. She is at least able to accept some help, but there\u2019s something she\u2019s still holding onto that she needs to let go of. I can tell. She may have as good a poker face as I do, but sometimes that just makes it easier to read her. And sometimes, like now, she\u2019s not doing as good a job as usual at keeping that \u201cmask\u201d up. I\u2019m sure it fools the customers, but it doesn\u2019t fool her friends.<br /> <br /> A little bit later in the afternoon Luna came by and I caught her up on everything that has been going on with Gloria, Hollywood, and Insincere Marguerite and Calamity. She said that I could have called her at any point over the past couple of days if I\u2019d needed to talk, and I apologized for not having done that. I guess it sometimes doesn\u2019t register through my thick skull that I have someone I can rely on again. I have someone that will be there for me regardless. I know I have my motley, but I usually don\u2019t go to them either when I should be talking to someone about things. I tend to keep my troubles to myself, and I know that\u2019s not healthy, but it\u2019s how I\u2019ve done things for a long time. Even Rook would chastise me for not coming to him when I needed help. I had just gotten so used to looking after myself that I needed the reminders. I guess I still need those reminders even now.<br /> <br /> So, for movie night we watched two films. One was The Matrix and the other was Bound. The Matrix I had seen before, so I remembered the plot about humans being used as batteries for the machines. Lori had something to say about how the human brain doesn\u2019t put out the amount of energy that would be required to do the things that they\u2019re doing in the movie. She also went on about solar and wind power being better producers of energy. We tried to get Lori to just roll with it, but I think it was still bothering her in the back of her mind. I guess that\u2019s what you get when you spend many sleepless days in a row studying anatomy and human health. So anyway, the movie was just like I remembered it. Crazy action scenes, burgeoning love between two of the characters, betrayal by a friend. It actually kind of reminded me of life as one of the Lost. We all used to be part of something else, something bigger than us, but we didn\u2019t know what was really going on. Then we escape that fake world and come back to the real one. Only sometimes there are people that never stopped serving the Gentry/Machines and they report back about the rest of us. They remained loyal. Like me. Like Desiree. Granted, I eventually turned away from the Lady, but only after I\u2019d done a good deal of harm. Hopefully my fate, or that of Desiree, won\u2019t end up like the spy in the movie. When did I start caring about Desiree? I\u2019ll still keep an eye on her, but it\u2019s possible that she\u2019s not just playing a long game on us.<br /> <br /> The second movie, Bound, was also good. It was more of a heist gone sideways kind of story, with a bit of romance (and lust) thrown in for good measure. The two characters, Violet and Corky are trying to steal money from Violet\u2019s boyfriend\u2019s mob connections while making it look like he took it. It all goes pear shaped of course, but it was fun to watch. The love scenes between those two were hot, and got most of the girls aroused, especially Julia. I think that\u2019s why we watched that movie second. \u2018Cause as soon as that movie was over Julia practically dragged Insincere Marguerite and the others upstairs. Of course we watched the unrated version, which shows a lot of more of the sex scenes than the rated version I\u2019m sure. Also, it seems that the person that did the betraying in The Matrix was the one who essentially got betrayed in Bound. Granted, he wasn\u2019t a good person in either movie, and definitely treated Violet bad in Bound. I think he got what was coming to him in both movies. In any case, it was a good movie. They both were.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Today is Julia\u2019s birthday, so breakfast was done just a bit differently than normal. Gawain made her favorite, cheese omelets, and Lorelei jokingly offered to be the table and let Julia eat off of her body. Julia took her up on the offer, much to Lori\u2019s surprise. I guess that is what she did with Insincere Marguerite, so she stripped down and climbed up on the table and let Julia eat omelets off of her. Lori was a good sport about the whole thing, but did comment on the heat of some of the omelets. Gloria came down for breakfast and almost turned right back around to go upstairs when she saw Lori lying naked on the table with food on her body. We assured her that this was not the norm and was only for Julia\u2019s birthday. She seemed to accept that and stayed downstairs, though she looked more than a little embarrassed about the whole thing. She focused on her food and didn\u2019t look much at what else was going on in the kitchen. Poor girl.<br /> <br /> After breakfast, and Lori\u2019s subsequent shower, Julia suggested going on a graveyard walk. She loves graveyards and thought it would be fun and romantic to go for a stroll. Calamity excused herself from the walk on the grounds that she didn\u2019t want to spoil Julia\u2019s day. While Insincere Marguerite is coping better with things and interacts with Calamity on a mostly normal basis, Julia is not. She is holding onto that anger a bit longer than her paramour is. Becky, Gloria and Desiree stayed behind. I talked to Luna and let her know that I was planning on staying at the house to keep an eye on Calamity. I know she\u2019s got plenty of minders, but after our conversation this morning I felt like I should show some kind of support. Luna decided that she did want to go, and that was fine.<br /> <br /> And what weighed more heavily on my mind is earlier this morning, before breakfast, Calamity and I went to the Clinic. Calamity had her usual appointment and I was going so I could set up an appointment for myself. I filled out all the required paperwork and picked a therapist from the list. The understanding is that if we don\u2019t get along I can choose someone different. I did meet the guy I picked briefly and I think we\u2019ll get along okay. We then worked out details for the contract. Changelings are big on contracts and promises and I\u2019m no different. I had to make sure that if I slipped up and mentioned my past loyalties then I wouldn\u2019t end up locked up or worse. I\u2019m not a big fan of confined spaces, especially those that I can\u2019t get out of.<br /> <br /> On the way home Calamity and I talked some more about what happened the other day with Chalcedony. It boiled down to me reassuring Calamity that I didn\u2019t see another way that we could have gone about our plan to keep our motley mate safe and detain Chalcedony. I still don\u2019t see an alternative. Even if I had been aware of Marguerite\u2019s promise to Chalcedony I would have proposed the same plan. I may have swapped places with Calamity, but at the time we were all honestly worried about Chalcedony\u2019s influence over Insincere Marguerite. I think we all had valid concerns. So, I tried to reassure my friend that we had done the only thing that we could have done at the time. She then admitted that she was afraid that she was destined to hurt everyone that she cared about, and then it hit me. Her parents, Stasia, they were people that she loved and ended up hurting. She didn\u2019t directly hurt Stasia as far as I know. It was the fetch that did that, but I know Calamity still feels bad that her best friend was hurt in some way because of her. Then there are Calamity\u2019s parents. She did hurt them. I can understand what led to such an act too. She had been replaced and her parents not only didn\u2019t notice, but they liked the replacement better. Or at least showed more approval for the fetch. Calamity snapped and in that instant did something that she can\u2019t take back. And now she feels like she does nothing but bring harm to those people that she cares about. It\u2019s not true, but I can see where Calamity is coming from. I tried to assure her that she was still a good person and that we still trusted her. That I still trust her. We all make mistakes and sometimes friends get hurt, but it\u2019s the intention that is the real key. Did Calamity set out to do harm to Insincere Marguerite? No, she did not. That was an unexpected side effect of Calamity\u2019s actions. It is not something that can be taken back, but Calamity can move forward. Thing is, I think that she needs to let go of some of the other baggage first. She\u2019s carrying a lot of guilt around for things that she was directly or tangentially related to.<br /> <br /> I told her that none of us are perfect. We\u2019ve all made mistakes. Some that small and some are not so small, but we do have to find a way to live with them. I admitted that I have betrayed a good number of people that I cared about. I didn\u2019t name names, but I did say that there were a few people that would have been better off if they had never met me. I betrayed a number of people in Arcadia, including Rook and the Lady. I betrayed people that I\u2019d become friendly with when I led them into the wilds to die or just brought them back to the Lady\u2019s realm. I can\u2019t take those actions back, but I do live with them. I\u2019m not dealing particularly well with all of it, but that is why I\u2019m going to get counseling. I did tell Calamity that I have no intention of ever betraying the motley. I felt that it was important to say out loud. I think Calamity already knew that, but I think I needed to hear me say it for my own good. Betrayal was my livelihood for a long time. I got good at it. I got good at the lying and didn\u2019t mind so much when people got hurt. I have felt myself growing distant somewhat and it is more than a little disturbing to me. I do not want to go back to what I had been before. I do not want to become Rime again. I just want to be Jacob. Bartender. Friend.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> November 11<sup>th</sup>, 2014 \u2013 Julia\u2019s Birthday<br /> <br /> I write to clear my head, to organize my thoughts. And to try to get my English grammar correct. Julia says I am overusing \u201cI\u201d again.<br /> <br /> This is a diary, so I will put recent events. My second show went well, just from me using my own talents. The audience was impressed. White Maria and Dark Kimberly came out again. Julia was not there as she went on a trip with Flores scheduled much earlier for her birthday. It was fine, and she was back by the end. F\u0336o\u0336r\u0336t\u0336u\u0336n\u0336a\u0336t\u0336e\u0336l\u0336y\u0336.\u0336<br /> <br /> Boss Lowjack (what an American title) put forth to us his idea to have the non-seasonal courts swear an oath to a Seasonal Monarch and gain their full protection. I have no desire to be Queen of Night and less desire to see Salk get it instead, so I agreed. Gawain seemed to like it in theory but made clear he would bow to no monarch. Lowjack is a magnificent manipulator, and either a good man or a great liar, as I believe I quipped aloud. C\u0336u\u0336n\u0336n\u0336i\u0336n\u0336g\u0336l\u0336y\u0336.\u0336<br /> <br /> The four of us made love for the first time in about a week. Julia\u2019s disquiet after the \u201cparty\u201d on my birthday and then my own betrayal at the hands of Calamity quelled our libido for some time. Well, Julia\u2019s and I\u2019s; Lorelei and De La Rocha seem unstoppable. F\u0336r\u0336i\u0336g\u0336h\u0336t\u0336e\u0336n\u0336i\u0336n\u0336g\u0336l\u0336y\u0336.\u0336<br /> <br /> Monday Gawain suggested ice-skating. I was wary, but in fact I had fun. My landings were a touch rough. Laser tag and roller-skating came up. For another time, perhaps. But ice-skating I can do. It is much easier than it was as an awkward child. C\u0336e\u0336r\u0336t\u0336a\u0336i\u0336n\u0336l\u0336y\u0336.\u0336<br /> <br /> We came back and had pizza. Gawain met with Juan Carlos. I went to check on Desiree. Desiree has had a rough time of it. Her former best friend, who she had something of a crush on, now hates her, and has been throwing herself at a certain Latina. Well Desiree got massively drunk. She had a pulse and was breathing, but was not terribly responsive. I turned her on her side and got Lori (who is studying medicine) and Jacob (who knows his alcohol). We found she was not in serious danger, it was clearly not a suicide attempt, just poor coping. Lori used Spring magic to rehydrate her, and we let her rest. She did join us for movie night, and looked a lot better. T\u0336h\u0336a\u0336n\u0336k\u0336f\u0336u\u0336l\u0336l\u0336y\u0336.\u0336<br /> <br /> Movie night was the <i>Matrix</i> and <i>Bound</i>. I had seen the former. The whole Motley was there, plus Becky, Luna, Desiree and Gloria. Desiree and Calamity sat on either side of Gawain, with Becky to Calamity\u2019s other side, while Jacob and Luna sat together, Gloria sat alone, and the rest of us in a pile on the floor. I did greatly enjoy <i>Bound</i>. The sex was good, chemistry good, and the heist was not bad. Not how I would have done it, but neither of the girls were master thieves. It got Julia pretty hot though, and the four of us had a second excellent evening. I did make sure Desiree was okay when she went to bed. C\u0336a\u0336u\u0336t\u0336i\u0336o\u0336u\u0336s\u0336l\u0336y\u0336.\u0336<br /> <br /> Today we had breakfast and went walking in graveyards. Julia was so happy. I let her be in charge for the day and she has reveled in it. I just hope she does not push Lori too far. The walk in the graveyards was good, and Julia was radiant, as happy as I have truly ever seen her. J\u0336o\u0336y\u0336o\u0336u\u0336s\u0336l\u0336y\u0336.\u0336<br /> <br /> She may become happier.<br /> <br /> I lifted the ring she bought me. Since my fingers are extremely flexible, Julia, thinking ahead, bought it in her size in case I got any ideas. After my experience with Calamity, I have ideas. Julia stuck with me. She defended me with every ounce of ferocity she had, she stood by me, even willing to leave Lori and De La Rocha and her old friend Flores. I knew it would hurt. While I wept or twitched, she stayed in the room with me. She sang me to sleep, but did not sleep herself. She did not want to be asleep if I needed her. L\u0336o\u0336v\u0336i\u0336n\u0336g\u0336l\u0336y\u0336 \u0336<br /> <br /> I could not ask for such loyalty from anyone else.<br /> <br /> The ring is sitting next to this paper. I just touched it with my hand. I am going to give it to her tonight. No! Offer it to her tonight. We return to the cemetery for a private party, the four of us, and I intend to propose. I am not sure how to adequately get across how nervous I am right now. A\u0336d\u0336e\u0336q\u0336u\u0336a\u0336t\u0336e\u0336l\u0336y\u0336<br /> <br /> Normally our relationship is such that it would be odd for me to just \u201cask\u201d but today she makes the decisions, so I am going to let her make a major one. I just hope I can give her the attention she deserves. H\u0336o\u0336p\u0336e\u0336f\u0336u\u0336l\u0336l\u0336y\u0336.\u0336<br /> <br /> Yvette haunts I. It is she more than anything else that stays my hand. How does she feel about me now? Does she love me, as she did in the dark? Does she hate I, as Hailey does Andromeda? Am I destroying my chance to be with her? Might this help as Julia may be less paranoid if she carries I\u2019s name? Might this make her more willing to accept her? What of Lori and Maria? Will this drive a wedge between us. I do, so, want to all be a family. C\u0336e\u0336r\u0336t\u0336a\u0336i\u0336n\u0336l\u0336y\u0336.\u0336<br /> <br /> I should not let the fear stop me. I am Insincere Marguerite. I am the greatest thief in the world. I am rightly proud. Julia should feel fortunate that such a woman as I wants to give her this ring! A\u0336b\u0336s\u0336o\u0336l\u0336u\u0336t\u0336e\u0336l\u0336y\u0336.\u0336<br /> <br /> Except that I am a pale, ugly grub. S\u0336a\u0336d\u0336l\u0336y\u0336.\u0336<br /> <br /> But no, I am going to do this. I am going to do this. I need to show Julia how I really feel, however scary that is to me. T\u0336e\u0336r\u0336r\u0336i\u0336b\u0336l\u0336y\u0336.\u0336<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Note to self, Julia is right. I do put words on the ends of paragraphs, don\u2019t I?<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>End Session LV</i><br /> <br /> Let\u2019s see\u2026<br /> <br /> Andromeda was played as fairly spacey this time, reflecting a bit the damage she still has.<br /> <br /> The \u201cSo\u201d was actually said by Lori and Insincere Marguerite IC at the same time, which was a really cool moment. It honestly happened out loud at the table just as Lori described.<br /> <br /> So funny movie story with this time, everyone had seen <i>The Matrix</i>, but only half us of had seen <i>Bound</i>. One player (who loved it anyway) actually bought it so everyone could see it, though two only saw it after the session (but before the journals were written) while the other saw it before. I was, perhaps unsurprisingly, one of the ones pushing to see it.<br /> <br /> I had everyone roll for ice skating. Dexterity + Athletics, with a penalty if the PC had not done it ever for very little (-2/-1) which it was up to the players to apply to their PCs. Calamity and Jacob rocked on it, while Insincere Marguerite did fairly well and Gawain and Lori passed.<br /> <br /> It was observed in the discussion that Lowjack when he came by was rather styling in his leather jacket and motorcycle gear and helmet, but then he had just been to dinner with Captain Jack to discuss his proposal, so maybe the Wizened\u2019s styling wasn\u2019t coincidental\u2026<br /> <br /> I think that covers everything. Let me know if I missed something. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T18:23:23-07:00","id":885851,"title":"","content":"Props to all for defying the idea that a story becomes less interesting once you put the characters in therapy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T23:09:12-07:00","id":885974,"title":"","content":"LOL. Indeed!<br /> <br /> Game went well tonight. Quieter session Gawain's player had to miss. Look for info on the Proposal and some hijinx next time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T01:16:28-07:00","id":895980,"title":"","content":"A marriage proposal, a potential clash between lovers, a rift between friends, exploration between lovers. Let\u2019s go.<br /> <br /> No Gawain this time as player had to miss.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LVI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Okay, so the last couple of days have been fairly eventful\u2026 not in an Earth-shaking, Freehold-threatening kind of way, but as far as the personal lives of the motley go at least. Things are looking up for most of my friends, as damaged relationships slowly heal, and existing bonds are strengthened. And there\u2019s something else, too\u2026 something that\u2019s hard to quantify. Something has changed within each of us, in a way that\u2019s almost impossible to describe\u2026 but I\u2019m getting ahead of myself.<br /> <br /> Yesterday\u2019s show went well, I think, with only a few hiccups caused by the absence of Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne and our subsequent last-minute substitutions. I decided to perform a heartfelt rendition of Elton John\u2019s \u201cYour Song\u201d as my one solo. What can I say? The lyrics are innocent, fumbling, and yet incredibly earnest, and the evening\u2019s impending proposal had me more in the mood for romance than seduction. It might not have been my most successful performance in terms of glamour-harvesting, but it was well-received, and left me with a warm feeling in my chest.<br /> <br /> Of course, part of that might have been due to Marguerite, who decided that during my performance was the perfect time to prank me. I had made some offhand comment earlier in the evening about professionalism on the stage, and how I tended to focus on my performance to the exclusion of all else; to the point that it\u2019s very difficult to distract me from it. Apparently Marguerite took this simple assertion as something of a challenge.<br /> <br /> I was about halfway through the song when I felt the familiar touch of my French lover\u2019s tongue creeping up my thigh. It was distracting and disorienting, leaving me in a state not well-suited to analytical thought\u2026 but I eventually realized that she had turned herself invisible, crept down on to the stage, and quietly began teasing me. She was merciless in her attentions, but I think I managed to cover it up pretty well. Sure, D and Julia noticed that something was up, but nobody else in the audience seemed to bat an eye.<br /> <br /> Her wandering lingus had me flustered and hot by the time I left the stage, and I briefly considered devouring one of the backup singers as soon as I was out of sight of the crowd\u2026 but I pushed that thought away with some difficulty. After all, I\u2019m technically their employer, and the last thing the Dream House needs at this point is some stupid sexual harassment suit. Instead, I waited until Marguerite revealed herself and made my feelings on the matter clear: I pushed her up against a wall and kissed her savagely for a few minutes before warning her never to do anything like that again. I love her mischievous side\u2026 but the show is paramount. Always.<br /> <br /> I made the rounds of the audience while the second set played out. Moon and Halley were there\u2026 and it turned out that they were there <u>together</u>! Halley noted that Moon hadn\u2019t been out on a \u201creal\u201d date in quite some time, and offered to take hir out for an evening of fun. While Moon looked as nervous as I\u2019ve ever seen hir, Halley seemed to be enjoying herself immensely, and took every opportunity to tease Moon. When I asked if I could get them anything, she winked at me and asked if I had any condoms handy.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m glad she made it clear that she was joking. I didn\u2019t have any handy at the moment, as most of my recent attention has been devoted to my female lovers.<br /> <br /> Marguerite, Julia, D and I made our excuses and ducked out a little early so that we could take Julia on her \u201cMidnight Birthday Graveyard Walk.\u201d I knew what was coming, and I confess that I had a hard time keeping my excitement from the others. D kept looking at me strangely. She knew something was up, but couldn\u2019t quite figure out why my feathers had gone all quivery.<br /> <br /> When we got to the graveyard, I grasped D\u2019s hand firmly in my own and held her back a little so that Marguerite and Julia pulled ahead of us by about ten feet. \u201cWhat\u2019s up?\u201d D asked me with some trepidation.<br /> <br /> \u201cJust wait,\u201d I whispered, unable to keep the grin off my face. \u201cGive them a little space.\u201d<br /> <br /> D\u2019s eyes widened. \u201cOh no,\u201d she said, a tremble in her voice, \u201cshe\u2019s not gonna\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Marguerite was down on one knee ahead of us, and Julia looked as happy as I\u2019d ever seen her. She took the ring she herself had bought from Marguerite\u2019s hand, put it on, and said \u201cyes.\u201d<br /> <br /> I might have squealed just a little bit. D looked faintly nauseous next to me, but she hurried forward with me to congratulate the two of them in any case. There were lots of congratulations, lots of exclamations over the ring, and lots of promises that Marguerite and Julia\u2019s impending nuptials wouldn\u2019t change the way the four of us felt about each other in the slightest.<br /> <br /> I confess that most of the rest of the evening is a big happy blur in my mind. When we got back to the house, I asked Julia if she wanted to be alone with Marguerite for the rest of the evening, or if she wanted me and D to join her. She was more than happy to include us in the fun, and the usual hijinks ensued. It was probably four in the morning before the three of them dropped off in an exhausted pile of Darkling flesh.<br /> <br /> I extricated myself as gently as I could, used a contract to bolster my flagging strength, and settled down with a medical textbook for the rest of the morning. I would have liked to drift off to sleep with the others, honestly, but I\u2019ve let my studies go a bit lately, and I don\u2019t want to get into the habit of putting them off. What if something I read last night ends up helping me save a life today?<br /> <br /> When the others woke up again about six hours later, the four of us went down to sex breakfast together. Of course Julia wanted to show off her ring to everyone, and of course it caused a big stir. Most of the motley was pleased as punch at the news, though Calamity seemed broody and upset by this development. I can only assume that she thinks Marguerite and Julia are still mad at her about last Friday. And while I\u2019m sure that there are lingering feelings of hurt and betrayal, I honestly think that our motley is on the mend, and that Calamity\u2019s harshest critic at this point is\u2026 Calamity.<br /> <br /> So yeah, Julia was doing the blushing bride thing all morning, looking at dresses and venues and cakes on the computer and talking a mile-a-minute about invitations and such. I\u2019ve been formally invited to be her Maid of Honor, and of course I said yes. D is going to be Marguerite\u2019s Maid of Honor. I sort of half-joked that she could wear her suit again and be the Best Man (citing the old stereotype that the Maid of Honor and the Best Man are supposed to hook up at the reception), but Marguerite insisted that she wanted a Maid of Honor too, and as it <u>is</u> her wedding, we decided to honor her wishes.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s almost cute to see how uncomfortable Maria is with this whole wedding shebang. She keeps giving me this \u201cdeer in headlights\u201d look whenever she thinks I\u2019m not paying attention, like she thinks I\u2019m going to get ideas from all the wedding talk. Now don\u2019t get me wrong, I\u2019m convinced that D is my soulmate and that the two of us will be together for the rest of our lives\u2026 but I feel no need to cement that with a gold ring. I\u2019ve made my promises of love and fidelity to D in front of all our friends and neighbors \u2013 and in front of God \u2013 and I don\u2019t really think we need to do it again in a church any time soon. A few years down the road\u2026 who knows?<br /> <br /> But it\u2019s fun to tease her sometimes.<br /> <br /> I talked with D and Gloria about their plans for tonight, and it was easy to see that the two of them were hoping to spend a little time together. I immediately pushed down the surge of jealousy I initially felt at that thought by reminding myself that I haven\u2019t even seen Oleander since last Friday. I called her up and asked if she was free for the evening.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2026 can be,\u201d she said after a moment. It always makes me feel a little bad when she says stuff like that, because when I spring something on her like this at the last moment, I feel like I\u2019m intruding upon plans she\u2019d already made. I started to apologize, and she chuckled into the phone. \u201cIt\u2019s nothing like that, angel,\u201d she promised me, \u201cit\u2019s just that I\u2019m a little toxic right now. I can whip up an antidote for you no problem, though.\u201d<br /> <br /> I could feel my brow wrinkling with concern. \u201cIs everything okay? Have you been dealing with Chalcedony?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo,\u201d Oleander replied, \u201cshe\u2019s still docile. I know what I\u2019m doing with this pharmaceutical stuff, Lori, there\u2019s no need for you to worry about that. I just took a jaunt into the Hedge yesterday is all.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, okay,\u201d I said, a little relieved. \u201cWhy don\u2019t you stop by the show tonight, and I\u2019ll cut out early. We can get a late dinner before we head back to your place.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSounds perfect,\u201d she said with a smile I could hear. \u201cI\u2019ll see you tonight.\u201d<br /> <br /> I had noticed that Desiree and Gloria seemed to have reached some sort of an understanding\u2026 they weren\u2019t exactly being friendly with each other, but they were at least civil, sitting at the same table and chatting relatively amiably. When I got her alone a little while later, I asked Gloria about this development.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s going to take time,\u201d she sighed when I brought it up, \u201cbut I think we\u2019re making progress. I\u2026 I just can\u2019t trust her again yet, but\u2026 well, we spent some time together last night with Jacob and Luna, and it was almost like it used to be. For a little while.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled. \u201cGood,\u201d I said. \u201cI\u2019m glad you two are starting to work things out. What did the four of you do?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> She shrugged. \u201cWe watched a musical on DVD. It was pretty good.\u201d<br /> <br /> I was intrigued. \u201cI love musical theater,\u201d I said (possibly unnecessarily), \u201cbut I missed a lot of it while I was in Arcadia. I was taken in 1978, and I still have a lot of catching up to do. What did you watch?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt was a show from the 80s called <u>Into the Woods</u>. Sort of a mish-mash of a bunch of famous fairy tales all twisted together. And then the second act was about the consequences of getting your wish\u2026 sort of an exploration of what happens <u>after</u> happily ever after. Like I said, it was good. Bernadette Peters played the witch.\u201d<br /> <br /> I raised an eyebrow. \u201cBernadette Peters? From <u>Silent Movie</u>?\u201d<br /> <br /> Gloria shrugged. \u201cAnyway, it was maybe a little on the nose for a bunch of changelings, but it was still a good show. The DVD was Desiree\u2019s; I\u2019m sure she\u2019d let you borrow it if you asked.\u201d<br /> <br /> Later that day, I did ask, and Desiree was more than happy to lend me the film (she also told me that she\u2019d played Little Red Riding Hood in a local production of the play years ago). I haven\u2019t had the chance to watch it yet, though.<br /> <br /> The afternoon passed without too much stress. Julia asked Jacob if he would be willing to create some ice sculptures for the wedding reception, and though he looked surprised by the request, he indicated that he would be happy to perform that service (but admitted that his artistic skills might need a little practice). Calamity was rehearsing a new number on the stage, and asked me to ask Marguerite if she would mind if she performed it tonight.<br /> <br /> Something snapped in me at that point. \u201cNo,\u201d I said flatly.<br /> <br /> Calamity blinked. \u201cNo?\u201d she asked incredulously.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo,\u201d I repeated. \u201cI\u2019m not going to play this game anymore. I\u2019m not Mr. McFeely, so don\u2019t expect speedy message deliveries. If you want Marguerite\u2019s blessing to share the stage with her tonight, you can damn well ask her yourself.\u201d And then I took her by the arm \u2013 carefully \u2013 and dragged her off to where Julia and Marguerite were talking about wedding stuff. What followed was an awkward yet civil conversation wherein the two of them agreed that it would be possible for both to perform tonight without undue stress or conflict. So that\u2019s nice.<br /> <br /> The show itself was fun. I didn\u2019t perform anything new or exciting, but I still found ways to amuse myself. In fact, I had been thinking in the back of my mind that it might be nice to pay Marguerite back for her little prank the previous evening.<br /> <br /> Now, my stealth skills are nearly nonexistent, so there was no way I could repay her teasing in kind. But there\u2019s an area just behind the curtain which is completely blocked from the view of the audience, but immediately obvious to anyone who is actually on stage. I made sure that I was in this wing area while Marguerite was performing. I was dressed in one of my tight, short, sexy dresses, and I might have just \u201cforgotten\u201d to put on underwear before leaving the dressing room today. So it was a relatively simple matter for me to flash Marguerite unexpectedly as her choreography suddenly turned her in my direction.<br /> <br /> There was maybe the teensiest microsecond of shock, but she covered it up like a pro. I mean, her performance was amazing, and I seriously doubt anyone noticed that anything was amiss (except, again, for maybe Julia and D, who were probably looking for it by that point). She wasn\u2019t happy with me when she left the stage \u2013 possibly due to the fact that both Queen Charlotte and the Warlock of Night were in the crowd \u2013 but I gave her a little kiss and massaged her ego a bit (\u201cYou were magnificent. How could you be anything less than magnificent? You are Insincere Marguerite!\u201d), and I think she\u2019s over it now. Teasing every once in a while can be fun, and little pranks like that are practically a tradition among theater types. But I don\u2019t want it to get out of hand and affect the smooth operation of the Dream House.<br /> <br /> I made my way up into the audience after that little scene, and found myself drifting toward Oleander. I joined her at her table, and she quickly handed me a small capsule. \u201cSwallow that,\u201d she said simply. \u201cBy itself if you can, with water if you have to. Give it fifteen minutes to take effect, and then it should be safe for us to touch.\u201d<br /> <br /> I did as she said, then dropped into a chair and made small talk. I confess that my conversation turned a bit maudlin after a while, as I shared my concerns about the situation with D and Gloria. Oleander paid close attention to everything I said\u2026 not like she was looking for signs of weakness in my relationship with D, but more like she genuinely wanted to understand the situation so that she could help me deal with it. I pointed Gloria out to Oleander, and she nodded thoughtfully.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou know,\u201d she said after a moment, \u201cin my experience, de la Rocha doesn\u2019t really go for long-term relationships. She\u2019s more of a whirlwind romance sort of girl.\u201d She seemed to realize what she\u2019d said a moment later. \u201cPresent company excluded, of course,\u201d she added hastily.<br /> <br /> I smiled at her. \u201cThanks, sweetie,\u201d I said, \u201cbut I don\u2019t want to get my hopes up. It\u2019s not <u>fair</u> for me to think that way. I can\u2019t monopolize her in good conscience, when both of you have been so great about this whole open relationship thing.\u201d<br /> <br /> I also spoke with Dark Kimberly briefly last night. She seemed a little depressed over the whole situation between her and Annika, and though I\u2019ve made no secret of my dislike for her sometime paramour, I tried my best to comfort her. The two of us commiserated for a while about the trials of dating one of Madame Spidertoes\u2019 ex-girlfriends. Kimberly got a really distressed look on her face when I mentioned that I knew what that was like, and asked if everything was okay between me and D. I assured her that, despite appearances to the contrary, everything is still hunky-dory with us.<br /> <br /> Roughly twenty minutes after I sat down, my watch alarm went off, and I planted myself in Oleander\u2019s lap and gave her a big, deep, sloppy kiss. She didn\u2019t seem to have any complaints.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou ready to get out of here?\u201d I asked when we both came up for air.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhenever you are,\u201d she said easily.<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay. Just let me say goodbye to the others, and\u2026\u201d I stopped short, and must have gotten a pretty distressed look on my face as a realization hit me.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat\u2019s wrong, angel?\u201d Oleander asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cI was going to give D a kiss goodnight,\u201d I admitted a little sheepishly. \u201cCan I do that? I mean, would I poison her, or make her sick, since we\u2019ve been making out?\u201d<br /> <br /> Oleander thought about it for a minute. \u201cIt <u>should</u> be okay, as long as you don\u2019t French her,\u201d she said after a moment. \u201cAt worst, you\u2019d make her a little sick to her stomach for the rest of the evening. If you want to be really sure, though, you can rinse your mouth out with mouthwash, or just kiss her cheek or something like that.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded, then glumly walked over to the table where D, Julia, Desiree and Gloria were sitting.<br /> <br /> \u201cHeading out?\u201d she asked with a grin.<br /> <br /> I nodded.<br /> <br /> She stood up and put her arms out. I held back. \u201cWhat\u2019s wrong?\u201d she asked, concern showing in her eyes.<br /> <br /> \u201cOleander\u2019s a little toxic right now,\u201d I admitted. \u201cI\u2019m immune, thanks to the medicine she gave me, but if I kiss you\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> D smiled. \u201cI gotcha. Pretty clever move on her part\u2026\u201d she chuckled after a moment to show that she didn\u2019t mean it, and leaned in to kiss me on the top of my head. \u201cYou two have fun. I\u2019ll see you back here tomorrow for sex breakfast, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> I kissed the top of her head in turn and nodded. \u201cYou too. If the two of you can come up with anything I wouldn\u2019t do\u2026 don\u2019t do it.\u201d<br /> <br /> And then the two of us headed out. Oleander knew a nice little all-night bistro in Santa Monica, and we had a light meal together before we headed back to her place. We didn\u2019t just fall into each other\u2019s arms though, we stayed up talking and listening to music. It was nice. Romantic. When we did make it to the bedroom, things were soft and sensual and warm\u2026 everything I needed from her. I\u2019m so lucky to have her.<br /> <br /> I woke up early (for me) this morning and spent a good deal of time looking myself over in the mirror in Oleander\u2019s bathroom. Okay, you can stop laughing now; it wasn\u2019t narcissism that had me self-gazing. Like I said way back at the beginning of this entry, something about me has changed over the last few days. I\u2019ve been feeling it for a while now, but I hadn\u2019t been able to put my finger on exactly what was different until this morning.<br /> <br /> I think my connection to the Wyrd has strengthened. Those things that define me as a Fairest changeling have become somehow more intense. There\u2019s something a little unearthly about my appearance now (even discounting the wings and the all-black eyes). My features have become just a little alien, a little elfin. The change is attractive; I don\u2019t think anyone is going to argue that point. The Empress wanted all of her pets to be pretty, and I don\u2019t think there\u2019s anything I could do to escape that doom even if I wanted to. There are little changes here and there that are difficult to quantify\u2026 a slight tilt to my eye-line, a delicate taper to my chin, a pixie-ish quality to my nose. My hair seems to have gained the ability to look artfully tousled when I first get out of bed, rather than like a disorganized rat\u2019s nest.<br /> <br /> But the biggest change is to my wings. For the better part of a year, they\u2019ve been poor, ragged things. Ever since I tore them up while rushing through the Hedge, they\u2019ve been largely decorative. Oh, I can use them to glide when I have to, but true flight has been beyond me ever since I returned to the world.<br /> <br /> For the first time, I have reason to hope that this might change some day. I looked in the mirror, and there they were, green and blue and red and gold. For the first time since I left Arcadia, I saw new feathers growing in to replace those I\u2019ve lost. And God help me, but it makes me happy.<br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei Grace</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> Thursday, November 13th<br /> Nine years, seven months, nine days<br /> Days without stabbing: 0<br /> <br /> Somehow there hasn't been a crisis since my last entry. At least, not that anyone's told me about. Of course, as fucked up as I have been most of this week I wouldn't be surprised if they left me out of the loop on something. The quartet has been pretty busy going into full bore wedding mode since Marguerite proposed to Julia on her birthday.<br /> <br /> Yeah, seems that happened during the cemetery walk. I heard about it at breakfast yesterday. Then I heard the four of them going on about bridesmaids and dresses and colors and all of that shit. And all I could do was sit there and listen because I'm sure as fuck not welcome to be part of it. I tried not to let anything show but I was not prepared for something this big. Hell, I'm still trying to deal with being cut out of the little things. Thankfully, Becky pulled me aside for a walk and tried to talk to me about it. It helped, mostly just being reminded that she still cares about me. Sure, sooner or later the hostility will fade but the problem is that I don't think things will ever be right between us again.<br /> <br /> I don't think anyone gets that. Lori is trying so hard to patch things up but this is not just some tiff between friends. This is deeper than that. I've lost my Darkling Sister just like I lost Stasia. I hate it and I wish it wasn't the case but it is and I just have to find a way to deal with it.<br /> <br /> And it's my own damnable fault. And I cannot fix it. Dr Emmett said I was being fatalistic and overreacting but she doesn't know Marguerite the way I do. It's so clear in hindsight. I betrayed her trust. And no one does that to a Darkling twice. Our friendship is as dead as my parents.<br /> <br /> Fuck, that's morose even if it is true. And Dr Emmett is right that I can't dwell on the past. I have to move forward. I have to accept the consequences of my actions and find a way to deal with them. I wasted enough time wallowing in self loathing already. I have at least managed to pull my head out of ass and get back to work. Thanks to Becky and Annika's help the past couple of days, my new number came together well enough to debut last night. Could use a little work still but it was solid enough to perform last night and I should have it down pat for the weekend crowds with a little more practice.<br /> <br /> Fuck did it feel good to leather up and push everything else out of my head long enough to get up there last night. I was still riding that when I hit the crowds to circulate again. I really needed to just leave the gorram weepy trainwreck behind for a while and at least pretend I really was as confident and in control as I act up there. Becky was there, sitting alone waiting for me and as soon as I laid eyes on her I wanted to make that beautiful dragon mine.<br /> <br /> I've never had that urge with her before. She's so strong, so dominant that she just doesn't ping my predatory side that way. Normally, no matter which of us is on top the other isn't letting it happen. It's a fight for dominance (which we BOTH win...) but neither of us is submissive. Except... well... I know how she works. I know how she's made. I know that she's like that because it's what I want. She's in the mood to be exactly as rough or as gentle as I am every time because it's what she was made to be. And last night, what I wanted her to be was... mine.<br /> <br /> Maybe it wasn't just that I was riding high on being Mistress Calamity. Maybe I was reacting to losing Marguerite. You know, rebounding emotionally or some shit. I don't know and I certainly wasn't asking questions last night. I grabbed us a fresh pair of drinks and put all of that walking practice to good use strutting over to the table. She was watching and I could tell she was enjoying the show. I think she was expecting me to have swung into aggressive mode and I'm pretty sure she was more than ready to play. She leaned in readily enough once I'd sat down and reached over. I slipped my fingers into that silken hair and curled them, taking hold firmly and holding her while I laid claim to those sweet lips and that perfect mouth. I didn't hold back, growling my desire to make her mine into the kiss. And she absolutely melted into it going soft and pliant and surrendering to my hungry kiss because that's how she's made.<br /> <br /> It was hard to pull back and stop but I did. I sat back and I forced myself to look closely and give her a moment to process. She was a little breathless and she didn't respond right away so I asked her if she was okay, if we were good. I am not sure what I would have done if she hadn't nodded and told me to keep going. Well, I know I would have been a frustrated little monster, because I don't think we could have spent the night together without it happening at that point and I was not going to push that on her without making sure she was okay with it. I mean, that's seriously emotional territory for anyone and for us changelings, so much more gets tied into it.<br /> <br /> But she trusts me. Which hell, maybe that's why I needed that as badly as I did. I don't know. But once I was sure she was really okay with it and not just reacting the way I wanted her to my heart started to race. I haven't indulged that particular urge in a long while. Technically, we stayed through the end of the show so I could keep an eye on things and be sure that Marguerite's meetings with Queen Charlotte and the Warlock of Night went smoothly. But honestly, I was enjoying holding my beautiful dragon close while teasing her and whispering some downright filthy promises into her ear. And, of course, the dirtier the suggestion the more she squirmed and reacted.<br /> <br /> Once it was clear there weren't going to be any (very unwelcome) disruptions to my evening's plans I gave Becky some rather specific (and delightfully naughty) instructions and sent her home. I grabbed my toy bag (I swear it had dust on it...) and an overnight bag (because yeah, as much as I am over at her place and vice versa it would make sense to have a few things but well... that would kinda require admitting we're in some sort of relationship). I also took a few moments to make sure to let Gawain know what I was up to. But well, elemental he may be but blind he is not. I hadn't been exactly subtle in my teasing and after seeing the way we were carrying on he had pretty much guessed where the evening was going.<br /> <br /> It was hard to ride calmly over to her place but I managed it. And upon arriving I found my Beautiful waiting for me exactly the way I'd told her to be. I hesitated, torn between my lust and a little flash of nerves and second guessing until she looked up and begged. I'm not sure if she was just that deep in the desires or if she knew I was unsure but it blew that flicker of doubt out of my head completely.<br /> <br /> There is something exhilarating about knowing that you really can do literally anything to someone and they'll crave it. It was a long and glorious night and I did not hold back once things got going. Between keeping the both us going full tilt without needing to rest and seeing to the results of my jagged caresses Becky's spring court contracts got a bit of a workout. It was a little sad to see everything swept away in the dawn's light but I did get to hold my ravished pretty and trace the marks I'd put in her skin while she lay worn out in my lap for a while first. And honestly, as much as I needed and wanted that, it's not the way I want things to be all the time or even most of it.<br /> <br /> I was a little worried that I'd feel differently having seen her that way or that she'd feel off about letting me dominate her like that. But as we shared breakfast things were normal. She was herself. She told me she'd quite enjoyed last night and I made sure that she was okay with me making her want that. It was a bit odd trying to put it into words but I think I managed to get across that I wanted to be sure I hadn't taken advantage of her programing. And she made it clear that she'd enjoyed it and if it was what made me happy than she was fine with it. Though she did hint that she might just remember a few of the more extreme moments the next time I'm the one being put through my paces. Which, of course, I informed her was not my thing. She just smirked and remarked about how if that was true then the room must have suddenly gotten colder.<br /> <br /> So yeah, that's a whole other can of shoggoths right there all right. It's not just my trust issues. There is this whole fucked up set of feels about the Whispering Voices tied up in with being helpless to another and my reactions to it. But I certainly do react to that sort of thing. I like it when Gawain picks me up like it's nothing. I like it (too much for his comfort) when Lord Bertilak creeps in. I like it when my dragon reminds me just how much stronger than me she is. So yeah, I guess I do like it when I'm not in control but only when it's taken by force. Which is more than a little screwed up but then what isn't where I'm concerned. I should probably talk to Dr Emmett about it and see if we can unravel that mess but where do I even begin to breech that topic...<br /> <br /> At any rate, from there the conversation turned to less charged topics. I brought up that I had to get going so I could get back to the Dream House before my therapy. Sex breakfast came up, and I assured Becky that she was, as always welcome but that I really felt like I'd kept her away from her duties to her court long enough. She agreed that she should get back but made it very clear that if I needed her, she would be there and that I could and should call her if I needed anything. I promised I would and assured her that I was better. Not perfect but better.<br /> <br /> Jacob was already ready when I got back and clearly a bit nervous. It says a lot when you can see something like that in him. I tried to be reassuring and I think it helped a little. Mostly I think just having someone there helped. We ended up running a touch early just in case but the clinic's staff know their stuff and everything went smoothly. And they were kind enough to help wrangle things to keep our appointments together going forward so we can keep riding together. Once we were done, I could see Jacob was much more relaxed even before he told me it had gone well. Seems he and Dr Sullivan are a good fit, which is good. We chatted on the way back, nothing too detailed but it was good to be able to talk to someone about it. I'm usually a bit uncomfortable with the subject. I mean, it helps and I need it and I know Gawain and the others want that but it feels like talking about what's in the sausage you know.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it was good to talk to him about things. It's not something either of us are great at and it helps that we're alike enough to understand. It's good to know that he's there if I need to talk or if I just need a good bit of sparring to clear my head. And I made sure he knew I was also there for him. You know, I think for us the sparring really is like meditation. It clears the mind and helps us focus and come back to our thoughts fresh. I'm going to meet him out back in a few minutes to do exactly that actually. I could see this becoming a fairly regular post therapy thing. I know I wouldn't mind.<br /> <br /> It occurs to me that this might stem from my tenancy to deal with stress by throwing myself into staying busy. I mean, I just don't idle well and I know it. But between the dance practice and my training with White Maria you'd think I wouldn't find the idea of regularly working out with Jacob so appealing. But I do. Maybe it's just that after the emotional ebb I was in being closer to my normal self feels like more but I think it's more than that. I can't really describe it, but I just feel like my limits have shifted and I need to push until I rediscover them. I'll worry about it later, right now it's time to dance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 05-22-2016, 04:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T01:18:15-07:00","id":895981,"title":"","content":"<b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> We didn\u2019t do much else after Luna and the others got back from the graveyard walk. I hung out with Luna and we played cards. I taught her how to play a card game called cribbage. My dad and I used to play it all the time and I missed playing it with someone else. Luna caught on pretty quick and we had fun. I\u2019m glad that she was amenable to learning a new game.<br /> <br /> I think while we were playing cards Calamity was up on stage working on a new dance routine for tonight. I don\u2019t think she was originally planning on doing it tonight, but she\u2019s gotten in a bit of practice in over the past few days with Annika and I think that she felt she was ready to perform it. From the brief glance I saw I guessed that she was going to do just fine tonight at the show. And I was right.<br /> <br /> At the show Luna hung out at the bar with me while I mixed drinks and made small talk with the patrons. Had a few regulars come in, but also had a lot of new faces. Things were going pretty well. I even saw Haley and Moon together on a date. I wasn\u2019t expecting that. They made a cute couple. Moon came up to the bar to get drinks and I made sure that they had any refills they wanted as the night went on. I brought out the first round of refills to them since they looked like they were having a good time.<br /> <br /> After the show Gloria and Desiree came up to me and Luna and asked us if we\u2019d like to watch \u201cInto the Woods\u201d with them tonight. They had a DVD of the stage production. Luna seemed interested so I said \u201csure.\u201d I got the impression that the two ladies really wanted to watch it together, but things were still tense enough that they weren\u2019t going to do it without someone else there. I can understand. Gloria needs to learn to trust Desiree again, and Desiree needs to earn back that trust. What she did was not irredeemable. She was being controlled at that point, but she still took notes on her friend for Hollywood, and so she needs to gain back that lost trust. So, we said yes and watched \u201cInto the Woods\u201d with them. It was enjoyable, I\u2019ll give it that. I found that I liked the witch. She was right about the other characters. They weren\u2019t good, they weren\u2019t bad, they were just nice. Well, I do think they were good for the most part, but I liked that the witch brought up the distinction between good and nice. As Rime I could be perfectly nice to anyone I chose. I was friendly and amicable and apparently trustworthy, but I was not good. I was pretty much the opposite of that. In the play, the witch wasn\u2019t nice, but she was right and could be good. Handing Jack over to the giantess was probably not the good thing to do, but she was looking out for the best interests of everyone there. Some would argue that she was just looking out for herself, but she did stay to argue with the others about how to stop the giantess rather than just running for it. So, yeah. I liked the play even if it did remind me of Rime to some extent. On the plus side Gloria and Desiree sat on opposite sides of the room, but they were together, so that\u2019s progress.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> So at breakfast this morning Gloria and Desiree sat at the same table for breakfast. They did leave a chair between them, but it was at the same table so I count that as a little bit more progress on that front. And speaking of good things, this morning Julia announced to the rest of us that Insincere Marguerite proposed to her last night in the graveyard. Not the most romantic of places for most people, but then those two are not most people. So, obviously Julia said yes and was deliriously happy all morning. She even started planning out aspects of the wedding, like who would play what role and what the dresses would look like. That kind of thing. Unfortunately Calamity didn\u2019t do well with the news. Not that I think she\u2019s unhappy about those two getting married, I think it\u2019s more a reminder of what she lost. She lost the trust of her best friend and is afraid that she\u2019s never going to get it back again. I think that Insincere Marguerite is starting to get over everything that happened. Things will not be the same between Calamity and Marguerite, I don\u2019t think that will happen, but it could get close. I just think that Calamity isn\u2019t ready to forgive herself yet so she can\u2019t see that Insincere Marguerite would ever forgive her either. So, Becky asked if Calamity would like to take a walk and they took off on their own.<br /> <br /> So after breakfast I decided that I wanted to spend some quality time with my girlfriend. So, I asked if she\u2019d like to go ice skating. Luna said yes, so we went back to the skating rink that Gawain had brought us to last time. I think she had fun today. I know I did. Luna also did really well at skating. I can\u2019t remember if she\u2019d ever been before, but you\u2019d think she\u2019d been skating for years as good as she did today. Afterwards we just sat and talked for a while. It was nice. We did talk about some serious stuff, like our relationship. I think she wanted to make sure that I was happy with things, and I assured her that I was. I also made sure that she was happy. I will admit that I got worried when she brought it up. I haven\u2019t been as attentive as I think I should have been, not for a while now. I know that Luna understands that I\u2019m just not very good with people, but I need her to know that I\u2019m happy with us as a couple and want to make sure that she is too. I felt bad that I hadn\u2019t invited her to the original ice skating outing. Gawain kind of swept us all up in his enthusiasm and I just didn\u2019t think. I should have stopped and invited Luna to come with us. I need to work on things like that. Luna is one of the best things in my life right now. I don\u2019t want to lose her.<br /> <br /> Right before we started to head back to the Dream House I got a text from Julia asking if I knew how to sculpt ice. I had to smile at that and replied back that I could. She asked me when we got back to the house if I could sculpt her and Insincere Marguerite looking lovingly into each other\u2019s eyes out of ice. I figured this was all for the wedding, though she didn\u2019t flat out say that. I think she was having some fun with all the planning stuff she had going through her head. She is definitely a creative person, so I wasn\u2019t surprised to see her taking on the creative details herself. But I assured her that I could sculpt ice and she seemed happy. I\u2019ll admit that it\u2019s been awhile since I have had the opportunity to do anything with ice and am looking forward to practicing. I want to make sure to do a good job for Marguerite and Julia, plus I miss my favored element.<br /> <br /> The show was somewhat interesting tonight. Luna stayed at the bar with me while I made drinks. Then Molly showed up and checked several weapons at the bar with me. She had a sniper rifle in a case, two pistols and a dagger. I asked what she was up to since she doesn\u2019t normally hang out at the bar, or as far as I know carry that much firepower. She said that she was tasked by Lowjack to keep an eye on the Warlock of Night and her Handmaidens. She is to tail them visibly, but to follow at a discrete distance. So far apparently the Warlock and the Handmaidens have had an interesting day. The Warlock had the Handmaidens groom each other like cats to start. This seemed to surprise the pair, so Molly was guessing that the Warlock knew she was being watched and wanted to put on a show. It obviously wasn\u2019t something they normally did for the Warlock. Then they went out for pizza and later stole a bunch of stuff from a convenience store.<br /> <br /> Yeah, so an interesting day. Then while we were talking Charlotte came over and wanted to talk to Molly privately. Since I couldn\u2019t leave the bar for long Luna showed them to a side room where they could talk. I told Molly that I\u2019d keep an eye on the Warlock while she was away. The only thing of note that I saw was Insincere Marguerite went over to talk to the Warlock. Their conversation seemed amicable enough. It probably had something to do with the possibility of Night and Day crowns coming to the Freehold. I have no actual idea of course, but it\u2019s not a bad guess. After that conversation it looked like Calamity and Lori went over to talk to Insincere Marguerite about something. Soon after that Calamity came up to the bar and ordered two drinks, whatever Becky had been drinking she said. So, I mixed up a couple of Hurricane\u2019s and gave those to her. She then went over to her sometimes lover and kissed her passionately and somewhat aggressively. Not that Becky minded. She sure seemed to be enjoying it.<br /> <br /> Anyhoo\u2026Molly came back after a few more minutes. We talked for a little bit longer and she admitted that Lowjack gave her the sniper rifle and the dagger as something of an afterthought. I said that I supposed it was good to be prepared, though I wasn\u2019t exactly sure what Lowjack was preparing Molly for. Though I get the distinct impression that he does not trust the Warlock in the least. Nor her Handmaidens. He even keeps a cyanide laced dagger in his desk drawer. Not that I blame him at all. Those two lackeys almost killed Tamara and I doubt that Lowjack has let go of his resentment over that. It would be politically bad for him to do anything directly to the Handmaidens because of their close connection to the Warlock, and he can\u2019t touch the Warlock for those selfsame political reasons. Ain\u2019t politics a bitch?<br /> <br /> After the show Calamity left with Becky. No need to guess what those two were going to be up to. Though Calamity\u2019s mood was a little forced I think. Not the attraction to Becky. That\u2019s real. It\u2019s just Calamity seemed to be forcing herself to be as far from mopey as she could get. I can only hope that she will let down her guard with Becky and just let herself be honest with her emotions. Molly also asked before she left if I would mind asking anyone who was in the Spring Court in my motley if they could give her a \u201cpick me up.\u201d So I asked Lori and she popped over to work that Spring Court magic on Molly so she could continue to follow and keep an eye on the Warlock and the Handmaidens. I do not envy her the task.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Well, this morning I went to my first therapy session with Dr. Sullivan. It was a lot easier than I thought it was going to be. He just asked me what things I wanted to work on and I admitted that I am afraid of going back to the kind of person I was in Arcadia. I admitted that I was not a very good person there and did not want to go back to that. He seemed to understand and said that a lot of us, those of us who escaped, did things to survive that they were not proud of while in our Keeper\u2019s realms. I did not bother to correct him just yet. I figured I wanted to get to know him a bit better before I drop any real secrets on him. I can be honest about some things without going into a lot of details. I can also tell him about before I entered the Lady\u2019s service. I was not a good person at the point either. I just didn\u2019t get any better after that time. Mostly what we covered today were introductory/getting to know you kinds of things. He asked when I got back from Arcadia, how long I\u2019d been gone, how much time passed over \u201cthere\u201d, If I\u2019d ever felt depressed. He even asked if I\u2019d ever had any kind of flashbacks. I wonder if all of the doctors here start with the questions to rule out or confirm PTSD? I guess he confirmed it for me given my answers to his questions. I guess I\u2019m not really surprised. I just hadn\u2019t put that label on it before. Not in any real way.<br /> <br /> I think there are some things that are going to take a bit longer to \u201cfix\u201d as far as my problems go. He asked if I\u2019d ever harmed myself in any way. I said that I had not done that intentionally. He seemed to think there was more to that and asked what had happened. I explained the situation when I got injured by the wolves in the Hedge, and didn\u2019t let Lori know right away. Dr. Sullivan agreed with the others that I should have sought medical attention, though he seemed to understand when I explained why I had not gone to Lori right away. It wasn\u2019t life threatening so I just dealt with it on my own, like I\u2019d always done. I guess even now I\u2019m learning that there are different rules in \u201cthe world\u201d than there are in Arcadia. Overall though I think it went well. The hour seemed to fly by and before I knew it, it was time to leave. Calamity and I set up our appointments for the same days and times so we could carpool to our sessions. I\u2019m glad they were able to work out that kind of schedule for us.<br /> <br /> On a different note, I think something changed in me recently. Nothing that I can really put my finger on, at least not all of it, but I feel different. I feel closer to what I used to be, but not in the negative detached way that I\u2019ve noticed already. This is more of a confidence in who I am, what I am. I feel closer to my element, which I suppose in California is just going to be uncomfortable. It\u2019s too warm here. I also noticed that the frost on my skin reaches past my shoulders now and goes down a bit of my upper arms. I used to think that the frost on my skin was a sign of my connection to the Lady, but lately I\u2019ve been thinking that it\u2019s just a representation of my element, of my connection to it. If I\u2019ve become stronger in snow and ice it would make sense that it is represented in some way, I suppose. In any case, it did not alarm me the way it might have in the past. After all, change is a good thing, right?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> A great deal has gone on this past day and a half or so.<br /> <br /> I am now formally engaged to Julia Oldacre. We got engaged in the nighttime graveyard walk on her birthday. I honestly don\u2019t remember it all clearly; I was too excited and too nervous. But it worked. I do recall her squealing with joy, which was interesting. But she is very happy, and I am very happy. I am glad the proposing is over. Given how obvious her intentions were (she bought the ring, after all) I had little need to be nervous, but I was very much so.<br /> <br /> We have discussed marriage arrangements a little. I have largely let her plan the ceremony, which she was, well, already planning. I believe she and I will both be in gowns, hers black mine white. My attempts to talk her into blue white and red did not work for me. There is some discussion of bridesmaids: We both want them. Just because I am marrying a woman does not mean I do not get to be a bride! Both having a maid of honor will be interesting, I would say Lorelei and Maria, but I am not sure Maria is willing to dress appropriately for Julia (I am unconcerned. A maid of honor need not wear a gown). We announced it (to Calamity\u2019s annoyance) this morning.<br /> <br /> I sort of want her to keep her old name, which surprised her. I am not going to take it, but I have little desire to force DeLisle on her. That said, the latter would be upsetting to my family if they ever found out, so it might even be worth it.<br /> <br /> Of course, there is some issue within my \u201csquad\u201d as Lorelei rather directly boasted I would not be able to disrupt her performing, so I snuck over invisibly and, sadly, she was right. However, despite my never making such boasts, she took it upon herself to distract I performing in front of both my Monarch the Warlock of Night and Queen Charlotte. This despite my being less then completely skilled at what I am doing yet, and only third time out there ever. Unfortunately.<br /> <br /> I am deeply displeased by this. Me messing with her doing something she does well on an off night and I doing everything I can to impress the Monarchs at something I am less skilled at only to be sabotaged by a loved one is deeply upsetting.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s two members of this Motley who have sabotaged me in less than a week. A gal could get rather paranoid.<br /> <br /> It seems, perhaps, she has forgotten that it was I who filled the Lord of Day\u2019s manor house with roaches and sewage. That the Night Court is known for it\u2019s dastardly tricks and frightening pranks. While I considered corrupting, say, Dark Kimberly into causing a wardrobe malfunction as they say in America, I am not sure that would be best. After all, she caused me to misstep at doing something important to me that I have less skill at in front of my Monarchs. I am sure I can find something she is less good at to cause her to foul up in a very, very public way. Yes, I do have a few ideas already. While some say she is self-absorbed, she cannot possibly be so self-absorbed as to have no idea that sabotaging me in my most important performance would not anger me so.<br /> <br /> My dreams were especially vivid last night. Vivid and intense. And now I feel stronger than ever before. Perhaps it is a reaction to my recent trials. I shall have to see if I can stretch my Wyrd and power a bit to see what happens.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s see\u2026I had an encounter with Desiree yesterday. It was fun. We spent a little time together a while back but everything fell apart soon after. It was good to do that again. She is a sweet girl. She asked me if I was trying to steal her from the director. Silly girl, that would be something happening in the future, not the past.<br /> <br /> But I have a wedding to plan and hi-jinx to scheme. So little more time for writing. I think I am improving though. Perhaps I will add more thoughts later.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LVI</i><br /> <br /> Everyone is now Wyrd 6! Gawain is compelled to offer protection to strangers, Lorelei must sing if commanded, Calamity is injured by innocent blood, Jacob cannot harm children, Insincere Marguerite cannot walk on bare earth without removing her shoes.<br /> <br /> Calamity performed <i>Tainted Love</i> as performed by Marilyn Manson, I note it as no journal stated the song.<br /> <br /> So, the pranking. There was a conversation (not recorded anywhere) where De La Rocha was insisting the protagonist of <u>Georgy Girl</u> (the movie, not The Seekers' song from the movie) was clearly gay (to explain her focus on kids over men) and Julia was telling her she was crazy and Insincere Marguerite was trying to not be dragged into it. Lorelei came in and dismissed the whole thing and wound up boasting she could not be distracted while on stage.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite tried to call her on it, using Light-Shy and her skills. However, she cannot apply any penalties to performance to a member of the Minstrel Kith, and so a reaction was the most she could get, with Lori staving it off. Lori distracted her, and Insincere Marguerite was penalized on her Manipulation + Expression roll to perform based on Lori beating her resistance roll.<br /> <br /> Not much more to cover, but comments and questions are welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T11:30:25-07:00","id":901199,"title":"","content":"I finally saw Kung Fury. Pretty crazy, and fun, but not the craziest thing I've ever seen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T17:22:18-07:00","id":903867,"title":"","content":"Looks like Marguerite is going to cause trouble. It feels weird to see her getting so vindictive towards one of her lovers, especially for something she initiated.<br /> It's kind of cool to see how much Jacob care bout Luna and how smooth their relationship is. It contrasts sharply with the other members of the motley.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T23:51:46-07:00","id":903994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play?p=903867#post903867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looks like Marguerite is going to cause trouble. It feels weird to see her getting so vindictive towards one of her lovers, especially for something she initiated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Problem is that Insincere Marguerite sees <i>Lorelei</i> as having initiated it by making the boast, and she's not appreciating that a) Lorelei has as much pride in all her performances as Insincere Marguerite had in the performance Lorelei pranked, and b) that Lorelei didn't know of the people Insincere Marguerite was trying to impress. Thus, Lorelei, in Insincere Marguerite's eyes, was vindictive, and kind must be repaid in kind.<br /> <br /> Which I have to say, is pretty cool of the players to do. Really shows their roleplaying chops. Can't wait to see how it turns out, and how long it goes until the girls hash out their perspectives on the matter. Hope that Insincere Marguerite doesn't go too far with the retribution before they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T00:35:29-07:00","id":904011,"title":"","content":"Some spoilers for next session, for those curious, to be ignored if not. If you comment on the spoiler please spoiler it.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> This will be, to a large degree, nipped in the bud rather aggressively by Julia, That does not mean there is no repercussion, but Julia will be forcing the two in a room to hash it out before it escalates because, goddamnit, she DOES NOT need this drama right now. It was a decision made after OOC discussion with the players that I was inclined to make for Julia anyway. The adult answer can be dull, but in the end, Julia is deeply in love with both parties and privy to Insincere Marguerite's venting.<br /> <br /> I am mentioning this rather then leaving it for next journals because it was starting to build up, but that was because of where we ended. I hate to let people down on it, and it was not a drama free conversation, but I don't want to gear people up for a Lorelei/Insincere Marguerite war that does not happen.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That said, spoiler free, you two have a good grasp of it. Insincere Marguerite feels wronged because of it, and Lorelei feels it was a fun tit for a tat. This is an issue in their relationships, that none are really good at this. De La Rocha is, by her own admission, terrible at relationships, Julia has never had one till this one, Lorelei is unused to anything serious, and Insincere Marguerite is very Insincere Marguerite. And of course Calamity is a (fun) trainweck. Their dysfunction keeps things interesting, to a degree. And Jacob/Luna is a fun contrast to that.<br /> <br /> ETA: It is also worth noting, as is the case with some excessively proud people, aspects of Insincere Marguerite's pride are fragile. She HAS TO be awesome, desired, the best, or she is just the scared little rich girl no one ever really liked and had no real friends, who became the awkward queer teenager who had no friends. There are reasons she regards being taken as good. The gawky slightly disfigured girl because a sleek confident feline beauty","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 06-01-2016, 04:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T09:04:32-07:00","id":904991,"title":"","content":"I will state - spoiler free - that if Lori knew how badly IM had taken her little prank, she'd be <i>horrified</i>. I try to play her as generally without malice; even people she actively dislikes (like Annika) are rarely the subject of plots or vindictive thoughts on her part. The only exception I can really think of to this rule was Mary's fetch, who finally broke through the walls of her good nature... that was the only time she actively <i>wanted</i> anyone or anything hurt. If anything, her (relatively) recent revelation regarding her actions against Annabelle back in Arcadia have strengthened her current resolve to &quot;do no harm.&quot; The idea that someone she loves might perceive her prank as intentionally hurtful is horrific to her, and the thought that she might have screwed up what she sees as one of the best things in her life with a single careless act is both sobering and terrifying.<br /> <br /> So - again spoiler free - I can see this situation playing out one of two ways. First, IM and Lori talk about this situation, and IM explains her perspective. Lori is devastated by this revelation, and immediately apologizes profusely, maybe even breaking down into tears at the thought of how she inadvertently hurt one of the people she's closest to. IM either accepts the apology or doesn't, but I imagine it doesn't go any further than that (though to some extent that's up to Marguerite's player, of course). The other possibility is that IM retaliates before the two have the chance to talk. Lori is in turn hurt by IM's actions, but has no context for the act, and sees it as needless cruelty from a direction she never anticipated. If this is how things go down... well, it's going to take a long time for anyone to get over the fallout of this action... if they can get over it at all. It might be a rift beyond repair, and I'd guess that Julia and de la Rocha would be caught up in the ensuing shit-storm as well.<br /> <br /> Keep reading, and keep commenting, please! The fact that people are actually interested in our scribblings keeps our resolve to continue writing strong in the face of hectic schedules and real-life concerns. Your comments and thoughts on the game are always appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T00:03:27-07:00","id":907006,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the insights Baroness, PenitentTom; it's cool getting them from both sides of the fence, as it were. Seriously can't wait to see how this all plays out.<br /> <br /> And PenitentTom, I love reading all the journals, pieces of fiction and, well, general posts the roleplayers make for these games. It helps build the world from multiple angles, and gives insights to the characters in turn, and their eccentricities. Shine on you crazy diamonds. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T00:29:42-07:00","id":907015,"title":"","content":"And we love your feedback. It is really fun to have feedback and discussion, and we check the forums for updates. I am very proud of how all our games are going. And our players for such great journals.<br /> <br /> But your feedback (general you, Taidragon totally included of course) is really awesome, and we appreciate it. We were just discussing it at the rescheduled Changeling game tonight. Thanks","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T00:42:14-07:00","id":907020,"title":"","content":"Yes indeed. I love seeing the feedback and knowing folks are enjoying the journals and following along. Calamity promises not to stab any of you (much). *grins*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T01:40:07-07:00","id":907031,"title":"","content":"Ah, that reminds me Baroness; I may have inadvertently drawn inspiration from Amdromeda as well as Princess Jolie for a certain Changeling I have in the wings. Her name is Andrea, she was a literal star in her keeper's domain (though not the only one) and she is an Ifrit/Gristlegrinder Elemental. Tempted to make her a new ruler in a freehold I am also making, but I am worried that may be a bit on the nose. Whether it is or not, thanks again for inspiring me to make Andrea. :-)<br /> <br /> Also, is it bad that I have made a Changeling who is an Elemental, amnesiac, has a self-made name, is combat based and whose mien is basically a walking suit of armor (if one from Kamen Rider Blade)...and yet didn't realize until later he may be a little similar to Gawain (and that I get the feeling I've asked this before)? He was definitely made after I started reading these Actual Plays, so Gawain serving as an inspiration is likely...actually in hindsight a lot of my Changelings can be linked back to here (pretty sure there's more than a bit of Lorelei in Ella Acap, my Metalflesh/Ministrel Wizened - also, cookie if you get the joke there).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 06-04-2016, 04:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T17:52:23-07:00","id":907345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenitentTom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play?p=904991#post904991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will state - spoiler free - that if Lori knew how badly IM had taken her little prank, she'd be <i>horrified</i>. I try to play her as generally without malice; even people she actively dislikes (like Annika) are rarely the subject of plots or vindictive thoughts on her part. The only exception I can really think of to this rule was Mary's fetch, who finally broke through the walls of her good nature... that was the only time she actively <i>wanted</i> anyone or anything hurt. If anything, her (relatively) recent revelation regarding her actions against Annabelle back in Arcadia have strengthened her current resolve to &quot;do no harm.&quot; The idea that someone she loves might perceive her prank as intentionally hurtful is horrific to her, and the thought that she might have screwed up what she sees as one of the best things in her life with a single careless act is both sobering and terrifying.<br /> <br /> So - again spoiler free - I can see this situation playing out one of two ways. First, IM and Lori talk about this situation, and IM explains her perspective. Lori is devastated by this revelation, and immediately apologizes profusely, maybe even breaking down into tears at the thought of how she inadvertently hurt one of the people she's closest to. IM either accepts the apology or doesn't, but I imagine it doesn't go any further than that (though to some extent that's up to Marguerite's player, of course). The other possibility is that IM retaliates before the two have the chance to talk. Lori is in turn hurt by IM's actions, but has no context for the act, and sees it as needless cruelty from a direction she never anticipated. If this is how things go down... well, it's going to take a long time for anyone to get over the fallout of this action... if they can get over it at all. It might be a rift beyond repair, and I'd guess that Julia and de la Rocha would be caught up in the ensuing shit-storm as well.<br /> <br /> Keep reading, and keep commenting, please! The fact that people are actually interested in our scribblings keeps our resolve to continue writing strong in the face of hectic schedules and real-life concerns. Your comments and thoughts on the game are always appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the things I like with Lorelei is how she chooses to be nice. Not just good, but nice.<br /> <br /> I'm alway impatient to read the next session. Thanks for writing!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T19:55:36-07:00","id":907394,"title":"","content":"Taidragon: Glad we give you ideas! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T20:35:10-07:00","id":907411,"title":"","content":"Mysteries continue when a new face appears in town. Is she trustworthy?<br /> <br /> Also, someone is threatened with \u201can assfull of Pontiac\u201d and not by De La Rocha.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LVII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> Nov 13, late afternoon<br /> <br /> Alright. This time, I think things really are back on track. After a couple more days of brooding and eggshells and pranks, things are a little easier around the Dream House. Not to where they were before or anything, but we\u2019ll get there.<br /> <br /> Calamity did skip sex breakfast, probably cause she expected more wedding talk, you know? There wasn\u2019t actually - we talked a lot more about the Dream Bastion and what all it\u2019s for. Lori doesn\u2019t like the idea of having to worry about being attacked in dreams but... my Keeper was the Dream-Lord, so I feel better being more safe than sorry.<br /> <br /> There was some kind of private conversation between Lori and Insincere Marguerite and Julia after breakfast, that Insincere Marguerite didn\u2019t really want to have and Lori came out of really sad, but that didn\u2019t seem to linger long. Maybe she was sad about being toxic or something, but that wore off at four, so they\u2019re probably OK.<br /> <br /> The big distraction that was Leanne Sheen probably helped too. She was another Changeling from Hollywood who was a high mucky muck but defected and was offering info. The Monarchs wanted her checked for programming first though. It seemed, you know, reasonable, and she was amenable, so we\u2019re gonna get that done tonight. It\u2019s important to keep her safe - I\u2019m sure Hailey's doing a good job until they return though.<br /> <br /> She\u2019s really hot, with really pretty eyes and long red hair. Between that, and the fact that she\u2019s a Leechfinger/Muse from Princess Joli\u2019s durance, and her name... well, it\u2019s not hard to guess why Princess Joli might be nervous of her. She did recommend to Lori to keep mortals away from Leanne specifically, too.<br /> <br /> Lori also talked to Princess Joli about us growing stronger. Apparently we\u2019re super good at it, what with all the Glamour we live in and the way our Wyrd\u2019s build off each other. Lori\u2019s wings are re-feathering, Jacob\u2019s got frost covering parts of him and Calamity\u2019s a little sharper. I didn\u2019t even notice my changes, but Calamity pointed out I\u2019ve got a little silver gilt tracing around some designs on my armor that are more intricate than they used to be. Insincere Marguerite said she felt more powerful and it may just be observer bias, but I think she is even more double jointed and boneless than she used to be. Apparently we need to be on the lookout for, you know, frailties too. Insincere Marguerite figures her is to do with being barefoot, and Julia that hers is to not destroy paintings. I have no idea what mine is, but I guess it is good to keep in mind, in case we get weird impulses and all.<br /> <br /> Anyway, after all the serious talk Calamity surprised me by asking me out to the amusement park on the beach! It was awesome - as she put it, we rode rides, ate tons of junk food and lost at rigged games. Well, expect I totally won one. I smoked the \u2018knock over the bottle\u2019 game and got Calamity a big green teddy bear that\u2019s as big as she is. <u><u>Everyone</u></u> thought it was adorable - I thought we were gonna have to pry it way from Julia. Somehow, the story of how I got it had Insincere Marguerite using \u2018milk bottles\u2019 as a metaphor for boobs and calling it a delicate one. Sometimes she\u2019s really weird. Of course, then she became kitten sized and rode around in Julia\u2019s cleavage, so maybe I\u2019m burying the lede.<br /> <br /> Nov 14, early afternoon<br /> <br /> OK, so that was a weird night. It started off alright - it was a good crowd, Ginny showed up, Leanne didn\u2019t disappear in the intervening hours. Hailey was there too, and vented loudly to Lori - I couldn\u2019t hear her, cause I was still at the door, but she looked pretty upset. Still, venting seemed to help and D kept her company after Lori had to go prep.<br /> <br /> The show was going well, and Calamity was just about to go on to give a super awesome performance of \u2018Love Stinks\u2019 when Monica stormed in and started arguing with Hailey. When they took it outside, I took my leave from Desiree and Gloria and followed them. Monica tried to shoo me off, but Hailey asked me to stay and besides, violence was, you know, in the air.<br /> <br /> So... I think -between what they said and Lori\u2019s Cliffnotes explanation between sets - Monica is dating Dominica and Hailey is worried that it\u2019s a rebound/fling thing and that Dominica will get hurt and so she warned her? At least, Monica called Hailey a stupid jealous two-faced whore for trying to get her girlfriend to break up with her and Lori said her girlfriend was Dominica and... just, man. Anyway, Monica threatened to give her an ass full of Pontiac, and I said I couldn\u2019t let her do that, so she stormed off and Hailey ran inside crying.<br /> <br /> De la Roche went after Monica and Lori went to help Hailey, so I went to ask Jacob if any of it made any sense to him. It didn\u2019t. Calamity did say, later, that there\u2019s anything I coulda done to make it better even if I did understand, so I felt a little better after that though. De la Roche did find Monica and threw her through a wall. After Monica tried to hit her with a car. You know, normally I\u2019d say I\u2019m glad De la Roche\u2019s my friend, but so is Monica. Hailey did decide to stay the night at the Dream House, so she crashed in my and Calamity\u2019s room while we did the dream thing in the Hedge House.<br /> <br /> We slipped into Leanne\u2019s dream easy and found ourselves in a Scottish castle where her second grade English teacher/mom figure was yelling at her and a goldfish in a fishbowl watched her from every room she went into. We could tell pretty quickly she had the programming, a simple thing like Gloria\u2019s. I had this idea to release the fish as the symbolic gesture to break her out. But it resisted and when I looked carefully, I could tell it was some kind of Incubus.<br /> <br /> That was the first time I\u2019d ever seen an Incubus. We figured it was probably up to no good, and it didn\u2019t seem responsive, so we jumped it and Calamity took it out right away. That kinda blew up the gentle manipulation thing, so we just talked with Leanne. I found a journal with her orders in it in a desk and handed it over. I guess it was kinda a test, but she moved right away to destroy it, tossing it into the spontaneously lit hearth. I promised to make a dream prison for her, in case it came back. I just hope it won\u2019t... recorporate, or whatever it does, and immediately go tell Hollywood.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Calamity and I got to spend a few hours in our Bastion before she had to go train with White Maria. It wasn\u2019t very big yet, but it was already shaping up as a great moss covered mound, with a carved stone door and hewn hallways. It was comfier than I remember the Green Chapel being, with a few more rooms, but it was a nice, peaceful place. I went back to it after she left, cause her training was pre-non-sex breakfast, which is way too early for, like, anything.<br /> <br /> Sex breakfast was, well, kinda bizarre, even for us. I mean, we went from Julia\u2019s mom\u2019s paintings of nude young ripped Elvis with a huge cock, to paintings of a nude Virgin Mary, to having sex in churches. De la Roche did promise to sign us up for hedge beast fighting training, which came up somewhere in there, and Lori stated emphatically that she did not want to defile any churches. Not even ones with padded kneeling benches.<br /> <br /> And now the day gets busy. Lori and I are going to check on Monica - De la Roche needed Spring Court contracts last night and Monica might too. Joan is dropping Andromeda off so she doesn\u2019t have to be alone while Joan deals with Court business that De la Roche hopes is not beating up Day Courtiers. At some point I need to work on that dream prison - who knows how long before the Incubus comes back, you know? First is Monica though, since she might have the same business Joan does. I just hope we\u2019re back in time, cause I need to make sure Joan\u2019s not involved in any diurnal bullying...<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> The last couple of days have been\u2026 enlightening, I suppose. They\u2019ve had their ups and downs, but overall I think we\u2019ve come out ahead.<br /> <br /> Oleander woke up about an hour after I finished my last entry to find me staring at myself in her bathroom mirror. I\u2019m not sure if she really got what was going on, but once I pointed out the new feathers to her, she figured out why I was so interested in my own reflection pretty quickly. She must have seen how concerned I was, because she pulled me back to her bed, and the two of us cuddled for about half an hour more before we decided to head over to the Dream House for sex breakfast.<br /> <br /> The gang was all there by the time we arrived. Well, mostly anyway\u2026 Calamity was conspicuously absent from breakfast. She claimed that she needed to practice her new act, but I can\u2019t help but wonder if she\u2019s still avoiding Marguerite for some reason. Gawain tried to draw attention away from her absence by boasting about what a good liar he is\u2026 which was admittedly a funny enough assertion on his part to be mildly diverting. <br /> <br /> Gloria and D were sitting together and both looking pleased as punch about whatever they got up to last night. It\u2026 didn\u2019t make me as jealous as it had in the past, and I think that\u2019s a good thing. I think I\u2019m getting used to the idea of the two of them being together, now that I\u2019ve been reassured that D\u2019s feelings for me haven\u2019t diminished. Gloria was also sitting relatively close to Desiree. They had an empty chair between them, but it was progress, and I can only see that as a hopeful sign.<br /> <br /> Sex breakfast proceeded with the requisite amount of banter and teasing, and everyone seemed to be enjoying themselves. Gawain brought up the idea of creating a Bastion, which is apparently a sort of permanent fortified dreamspace which the motley could share. It would always be there, on the edge of our dreams\u2026 a sort of fall-back position in case we ever get attacked in our dreams.<br /> <br /> In a somewhat tremulous voice, I mentioned the fact that I\u2019d never even <u><u>thought</u></u> about getting attacked in my dreams before. I never knew that it was something I needed to worry about. Gawain told me that it can happen\u2026 there are plenty of things that can slip into your dreams and do you harm, in fact. But he assured me that the Bastion would be a safe place, where I could hold my own until help came or I woke up. Oh, yeah, and we\u2019ll also be able to slip into each other\u2019s dreams using the Bastion as a bridge.<br /> <br /> I looked around the circle at all of my friends and flatly asked them to \u201cknock first.\u201d I have some dreams which I don\u2019t intend to share! Well, maybe with D\u2026<br /> <br /> In any case, as things were winding down, Julia took me and Marguerite by our arms and led us insistently out of the room, claiming that the three of us needed to talk urgently. I allowed it, as I figured it was going to be wedding talk, but Marguerite struggled a bit, claiming that she wasn\u2019t \u201cready\u201d to have this conversation.<br /> <br /> Once we had a little privacy, I turned to look at Marguerite, who didn\u2019t meet my eyes. I really started to worry at that point, as she\u2019s usually so bold and forceful. \u201cWhat is it, sweetie?\u201d I asked as kindly as I could.<br /> <br /> She started talking softly. She mentioned that she still lacks confidence on the stage. She brought up the fact that both Queen Charlotte and the Warlock of Night were in our audience last night. She said that, when she performs, she\u2019s always afraid that something will distract her at an inopportune moment, and that she\u2019ll mess up as a consequence. Then she looked me in the eye and told me how much it upset her when I distracted her during the show last night.<br /> <br /> \u201cI know that I did the same thing to you,\u201d she said before I could respond, \u201cbut you are a professional performer, and you are at home on the stage. I am not. And after Calamity\u2019s betrayal last week, I could not help but feel betrayed by you as well.\u201d<br /> <br /> I was floored. \u201cOh, Marguerite,\u201d I said, and for once I hope she could see the tears welling up in my eyes. \u201cOh my love, I\u2019m so sorry. I never meant\u2026 I didn\u2019t even think\u2026\u201d I couldn\u2019t come up with the words for a few minutes. \u201cIt was supposed to be a prank,\u201d I said at last. \u201cIt was just supposed to be mischievous and light-hearted\u2026 like what you did to me. I didn\u2019t stop to think about how it would make you feel. Please believe me, baby\u2026 I\u2019m not cruel, I\u2019m just stupid. I\u2019d never do anything to hurt you.\u201d <br /> <br /> I was almost sobbing by that point, and Marguerite looked a little teary-eyed too. \u201cYou are sorry?\u201d she asked plaintively after a moment had passed.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m <u><u>so</u></u> sorry,\u201d I said immediately. \u201cI will <u><u>never</u></u> do anything like that to you again, Marguerite. Just\u2026 just say you\u2019ll forgive me, please. I don\u2019t want to lose you over some stupid prank\u2026 some stupid mistake.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded after a moment, and then embraced me. I think we\u2019re going to be okay now, but that was too close for comfort. God, I\u2019m such a stupid, thoughtless bitch sometimes! How could I hurt someone I care about so much that badly\u2026 and not even realize I\u2019m doing it? I guess I was just too wrapped up in my own shit to pay attention. I was too consumed by my issues with D and Gloria, and too excited about my upcoming date with Oleander, and I just didn\u2019t think about how that sort of behavior would affect Marguerite. And now of all times\u2026<br /> <br /> So needless to say, I was more than a little subdued when the three of us returned to the kitchen. D cottoned to the fact that something was wrong at once and hurried toward me, holding her arms out. I remembered just in time why that would be a bad idea. \u201cPoisonous!\u201d I squeaked as I scurried away from her.<br /> <br /> D sighed, and turned toward Oleander. \u201cWhen will it be safe for me to kiss her again?\u201d she asked irritably.<br /> <br /> Oleander did some quick calculations on her fingers. \u201cShe should be free of the toxins by four o\u2019clock at the latest,\u201d she said after a moment. \u201cAnything before that is living dangerously.\u201d She looked away from D with downcast eyes. \u201cLook, de la Rocha\u2026 I\u2019m sorry about this. I didn\u2019t plan it this way. I try to schedule my excursions into the Hedge for times when I know Lori\u2019s spending time with you, so that we don\u2019t have to take these measures\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> After a moment, D smiled again. \u201cIt\u2019s cool,\u201d she said softly, and then turned to me. \u201cAre you okay?\u201d she asked, with a hard, pointed glance at Julia and Marguerite.<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cI\u2019ll be okay,\u201d I assured her. \u201cWe\u2019ll talk about it later.\u201d<br /> <br /> A few minutes later, there was a knock at the door. Gawain and I both opted to answer it, and I\u2019m kind of glad we did. Halley was there with a very attractive redhead neither of us recognized. She introduced the newcomer as Leanne Sheets, yet another recent refugee from Hollywood. She was apparently a part of the monarchs\u2019 inner circle, and is offering substantial intelligence on their plans and movements in exchange for her safety. Considering what we\u2019d learned about Gloria\u2019s conditioning, the higher-ups decided that it would be a good idea to send her to us for a thorough screening before taking any further action.<br /> <br /> Of course we agreed to help however we could. We asked a few simple questions (Gawain used his contracts to read her motivations, and I think Calamity might have done something similar), and agreed to look into her dreams that night to see about removing any directives Hollywood might have placed there.<br /> <br /> I got an odd feeling when I stood close to Leanne. I mean, she was beautiful, but this was more of a physical reaction; a certain chill in the air on the edge of perception. I might not have recognized the signs if I hadn\u2019t spent so much time around D, but since I <u><u>have</u></u>, it really stood out. Whatever else might be true about our new visitor from Hollywood, Leanne is a Leechfinger. One glance at her face is enough to tell anyone with eyes that she\u2019s also a Fairest.<br /> <br /> Over the course of the conversation, I discovered that Leanne and Jolie shared a Durance, so I thought it might be prudent to get the Princess\u2019 take on her before we made any further moves. I pulled out my phone, moved into a vacant room, and hit the speed dial for Jolie\u2019s personal cell.<br /> <br /> The long and the short of it is that Jolie doesn\u2019t trust Leanne. The two of them <u><u>did</u></u> know each other back in Arcadia, and apparently the memories are not happy for the Princess. She is inclined against trusting Leanne, and strongly advised me to keep her away from our performers (or really any mortals) at the show this evening\u2026 though she admitted that her own bias might be coloring her view of the situation.<br /> <br /> As we were about to say goodbye, something occurred to me. \u201cPrincess?\u201d I asked a little hesitantly.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat is it, honey?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell\u2026 I noticed this morning\u2026\u201d I began, then took a deep breath. \u201cI\u2019ve been out of Arcadia for about ten months now. I know you\u2019ve heard my story before\u2026 how I tore up my wings on the thorns as I passed through the Hedge. Ever since then, my wings have been pretty ragged, and there\u2019s been nothing I could do about that. This morning I noticed that new feathers are starting to grow in.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell that\u2019s a good thing, isn\u2019t it?\u201d she asked after a moment.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah,\u201d I answered hesitantly, \u201cbut I\u2019m just wondering what it means. Is it a sign of my growing connection to the Wyrd? If so, why is it growing so <u><u>quickly</u></u>? Is this something I should be worried about? I don\u2019t want to lose myself\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHold on there, sweetie,\u201d she said with a chuckle. \u201cDon\u2019t make a big deal out of it just yet. You and the rest of your motley are in sort of a unique situation. Your respective wyrds complement each other really well, and to an extent they also feed off of each other, so you\u2019re developing powers a little quicker than most. It probably doesn\u2019t hurt that you guys are living smack dab in the middle of a glut of regular glamour, too. You might want to talk with your motley about it; see if any of them are experiencing similar effects, but I wouldn\u2019t worry too much about it just yet.\u201d<br /> <br /> I breathed a soft sigh of relief. \u201cThanks for the advice. Anything else I need to know?\u201d<br /> <br /> She thought for a few seconds. \u201cWell\u2026 if your connection with the Wyrd has developed far enough, you might start to notice little behavioral quirks\u2026 we call them \u2018frailties.\u2019 It shouldn\u2019t be anything too serious just yet, though.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll pass it on to the others. Look, thanks for talking with me about this stuff, Princess. Sometimes I still feel like a kid when it comes to the facts of changeling life\u2026 there\u2019s so much I don\u2019t know\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe\u2019ve all been there, Lori,\u201d she replied easily, \u201cit\u2019s nothing to be ashamed of. Give me a call if there\u2019s anything else you need to talk about, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWill do. And I\u2019ll pass along your thoughts on Leanne, too.\u201d<br /> <br /> We said goodbye after that, and I made my way back into the kitchen, where the group was avidly discussing what to do about Leanne Sheets. I added my two cents, incorporating both Jolie\u2019s opinions of the newcomer and my own suspicions regarding her appetites, considering her shared durance with Jolie and her status as a Leechfinger. A few of my friends gave each other knowing looks at that; apparently there\u2019s something about her name that already had them suspicious, though I don\u2019t claim to understand the reference myself.<br /> <br /> Once that topic had run its course, I asked if I could speak with the motley privately, throwing an apologetic look at Oleander, Gloria, and Desiree. The three accepted the request gracefully enough. Oleander gave me a quick peck on the cheek (so as not to re-poison me) and bade us farewell, while Gloria and Desiree decided to go out for soft serve together. It looks like Gloria\u2019s really trying to patch things up between the two of them. Here\u2019s hoping it works out.<br /> <br /> So I sort of laid things out for the group as Jolie had explained it to me. Turns out that the others had noticed subtle changes in themselves as well. Marguerite has gotten more flexible (more thoughts on that later). D is ever so slightly paler. Gawain has developed this little silver filigree against the green of his armor. Calamity has gotten a bit \u201csharper.\u201d Frost is now running down Jacob\u2019s arms. I didn\u2019t notice any overt physical changes in Julia, but she assures us that she\u2019s felt the increase in her connection to the Wyrd too. I have no idea where the hell Ace was for this conversation.<br /> <br /> Only Marguerite and Julia had noticed anything like the \u201cfrailties\u201d that Jolie mentioned. Julia finds herself unable to deface or destroy painted art, while Marguerite has become even more opposed to wearing shoes for some reason. I hope whatever frailties I develop aren\u2019t shoe-related; I don\u2019t know if I could bear it.<br /> <br /> Yes, yes\u2026 I\u2019m a stereotypical girl, obsessed with fashion and shoes. Sue me.<br /> <br /> So as we were talking about frailties, Gawain mentioned Madame Spidertoes, and made a sort of pantomime motion with his hands, pretending to wash clothes. Of course this set D off like nothing else, and she lashed out at him about making fun of her ex. I put a hand on her shoulder and admonished her as gently as I could, telling her that Gawain didn\u2019t mean to make fun or show disrespect. I think she knew that deep down, because she seemed more embarrassed than pissed after that.<br /> <br /> So the two of us went up to our bedroom and spent the next few hours just enjoying each other\u2019s company. We eventually joined Julia and Marguerite in the attic, where Julia was painting. At four o\u2019clock on the dot, several alarms went off around the house (apparently my lovers were eager for my touch\u2026 they\u2019re all such sweeties!), and wanton carnality ensued. Julia held herself aloof at first; she spent most of her time painting the three of us as we took our pleasure.<br /> <br /> So the show tonight. Well, as always, the show itself was a lot of fun, though things were developing in the audience which made me sad. First of all, I noticed that Halley was there, looking even more depressed than she had the last time I spoke with her. Of course I made a bee-line for her, plopped myself down in the chair next to her, and asked her what was wrong.<br /> <br /> \u201cMonica and Dominika are going out,\u201d she admitted after a moment. \u201cIt\u2019s a terrible idea. Monica is making bad decisions in response to getting dumped again, and Dominika is going to end up getting hurt because of it. Believe me, I know\u2026\u201d she said, looking so miserable that I had to reach out and take her hand.<br /> <br /> \u201cI know you want to do what\u2019s right, honey,\u201d I said, \u201cand I know you\u2019re still carrying a torch for Monica, and I imagine it must hurt like hell. But there\u2019s only so much you can do to help them out. If you\u2019ve told them how you feel about it, I don\u2019t know what else you can do. They\u2019ve got to make their own mistakes.\u201d<br /> <br /> Halley sniffed and nodded. \u201cI guess you\u2019re right,\u201d she said after a moment.<br /> <br /> I left her to her own devices after that, as I was needed backstage to prepare for the show. I confess to taking a small amount of malicious glee in selecting my number for this evening: a deep cut from one of Billy Joel\u2019s earlier albums called \u201cSay Goodbye to Hollywood.\u201d I picked it because I thought the title was apt, what with Leanne\u2019s sudden arrival and Gloria\u2019s situation and all. Gawain later pointed out to me that some of the lyrics could be misconstrued as a warning <u><u>from</u></u> Hollywood to those who might desert. I guess I\u2019ll have to pay closer attention to my selections in the future.<br /> <br /> There was a disturbance late in the show, after my solo had already passed. Monica showed up, spitting mad about how Halley was trying to \u201csabotage\u201d her new relationship because she was a jealous two-faced bitch (her words, not mine). She and Halley went out into the parking lot to talk things out, and Gawain followed them to make sure things remained civil. It\u2019s a good thing he did. She was <u><u>really</u></u> mad. In the end, he had to remind her that the Dream House is a place of safety for all changelings, but she wasn\u2019t in the mood to listen. She wanted to settle the score, and her rage kept building. I believe Monica mentioned something about hitting Halley over the head with a Pontiac at one point. Halley was obviously reluctant to let her do so, and we weren\u2019t about to let her get hurt.<br /> <br /> Monica eventually stormed off, but Halley was inconsolable by that point. I felt so bad for her. I\u2019ve seen a lot of relationships go bad over the years (okay, if I\u2019m being perfectly honest, I\u2019ve <u><u>caused</u></u> a few of those relationships to go bad, though I\u2019m not proud of it), and it\u2019s always hard to watch. Halley was an emotional wreck, and terrified that Monica would exact some sort of painful revenge on her if she left the premises, so we offered to put her up for the night.<br /> <br /> This posed a bit of a quandary, as both of our guest rooms are currently occupied by Desiree and Gloria respectively. Marguerite made the not-so-subtle suggestion that those two could share while Halley took the room that became open, but nobody much went for that option. In the end, Calamity and Gawain agreed that Halley could stay in their room, as they were going to be doing the dream healing thing with Leanne in the Hollow that night anyway.<br /> <br /> I sat up with Halley for a while, while D went off to look for Monica. She called an hour or two later, having found her. It sounds like the two of them had a real knock-down, drag-out fight in the middle of a parking lot somewhere. D claims that she put Monica through a wall, and I believe her. When she got back to the house, my honey was battered and bruised and cut up all over\u2026 but she also looked very happy. She claimed that she\u2019d managed to knock some sense into Monica at last, and that she didn\u2019t think Monica would cause any more trouble for Halley or the Dream House.<br /> <br /> I <u><u>insisted</u></u> that she let me drag her off to our bedroom so that I could kiss her wounds all better, and she didn\u2019t put up much of a fight. Once she was feeling better (and I\u2019d had her all to myself for a little while), the two of us joined Marguerite and Julia in their room for a romp. Marguerite demonstrated her newly-enhanced flexibility, and\u2026 wow. I think each of us was a little desperate to make sure that things were okay between us again in the wake of that morning\u2019s conversation, because things got a little intense between us last night. But it was a <u><u>good</u></u> kind of intense.<br /> <br /> So that brings us to this morning. Gawain and Calamity reported that they had no problems removing the programming from Leanne\u2019s dreaming mind\u2026 but there was a small complication. Everywhere they went in her dream, they found a small fishbowl housing a little goldfish. The goldfish was always looking at them. Apparently they eventually recognized it as an \u201cincubus,\u201d a sort of psychic parasite which can insinuate itself into people\u2019s dreams. They were able to oust the incubus without too many problems, but that still leaves the question of what it was doing in her dreams in the first place.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s possible that it was just a coincidence, but that rings false to most of us. There\u2019s much easier prey out there for incubi than us changelings; after all; we have defense mechanisms in our dreams that the vast majority of the mortal population is simply lacking. It seems more likely that the incubus was conscripted by someone \u2013 possibly Hollywood \u2013 to keep an eye on Leanne\u2019s dreams, and report back on what it observed. Though I confess we have no direct proof of this theory, it seems like a good bet that Hollywood will shortly know that we\u2019re aware of their brainwashing\u2026 and that we\u2019re taking steps to counter it.<br /> <br /> There were a few other events of note during breakfast. First of all, D got a text indicating that Dominika now wants to fight her in retaliation for what she did to Monica last night. D looked particularly pleased with herself at that point. I\u2019m not <u><u>really</u></u> worried about this; I know that D won\u2019t do anything to seriously hurt the other girl, and I know that she can hold her own in most fights. I\u2019m just a little concerned that Dominika is taking this more seriously than anyone else involved. I don\u2019t want there to be any lasting bad feelings between the two of them. Maybe I should talk to Dominika or something.<br /> <br /> Marguerite was acting a little strangely this morning as well. As we were sitting down to breakfast, she actually crawled into my lap and curled up there like a cat. It was cute, to be honest\u2026 but a little weird as well. I wonder if I\u2019m getting more bird-like now that my feathers are growing back in. Julia eventually came to my rescue, picking her fianc\u00e9 up and transplanting her to her own lap. It was an oddly possessive gesture on Julia\u2019s part\u2026 but maybe I\u2019m reading too much into it.<br /> <br /> Halley will not be staying with us another night. She\u2019s reasonably confident that Monica has calmed down now, and feels safe returning to her own home once again. She also commented that if that changed, she had a few other options for where to stay, and she didn\u2019t want to put us out any further, since we were already playing host to several other refugees. We tried to let her know that she\u2019s always welcome at the Dream House, but she was firm in her intentions.<br /> <br /> I got a call as breakfast was winding down. Glancing at the ID, I noticed that it was from Joan. \u201cHey, honey,\u201d I said brightly as I answered the call.<br /> <br /> There was a pause, and I could almost hear her blush before she began talking. I know I shouldn\u2019t tease her, but it\u2019s just so damned <u><u>cute</u></u>. Despite the stern face she shows to most of the Freehold, she\u2019s such a gentle, kind, and caring person\u2026 and the fact that she displays such insecurity around me means that I\u2019m getting to see a side of her that she doesn\u2019t share with many people, which is flattering.<br /> <br /> \u201cHello, Lorelei,\u201d she answered after a few seconds. \u201cI hope I am not interrupting anything important\u2026\u201d she let that hang in the air for a moment.<br /> <br /> \u201cNot at all,\u201d I answered. \u201cTo what do I owe the pleasure?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI have\u2026 Court business to attend,\u201d she said after another brief pause. \u201cIt will likely take up most of my day, and keep me away from home. Andromeda is\u2026 a bit down today, and I do not wish to leave her by herself. If it would not be an imposition, I was wondering if you would mind\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019d be happy to keep her company,\u201d I said when she faltered. \u201cWould you like me to come over to your place, or do you want to bring her by here?\u201d<br /> <br /> Joan considered the question. \u201cI will drop her off in an hour, if that is convenient to your motley. I do not anticipate any trouble; she is not despondent or suicidal. I just do not want her to be alone all day.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s a date,\u201d I said. \u201cYou know I\u2019m happy to do whatever I can. Just promise me that you\u2019ll be careful while you\u2019re out on this \u2018Court business\u2019 of yours, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI so vow,\u201d she replied formally. \u201cI will see you soon.\u201d<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, it looks like that\u2019s not actually going to happen. In the wake of the text message about Dominika\u2019s grudge, we started discussing D\u2019s fight with Monica, and it occurred to a few of us that Monica might be in need of healing. D assures us that she didn\u2019t do anything permanent to our big green friend, and I know she\u2019s serious about that\u2026 but temporary injuries can still hurt like hell, and I don\u2019t want Monica to think that I\u2019m holding a grudge about last night or anything.<br /> <br /> I confess that in part I kept going back to this topic of conversation because the others started talking about having sex in a church. Okay, so that\u2019s not really surprising at sex breakfast, but still. It made me very uncomfortable. Yes, okay, I <u><u>have</u></u> had sex in a church before\u2026 back before I was Taken. It\u2019s one of those things that I only did because I knew it would destroy my father if he ever found out about it. For pretty much the same reason, I have no desire to repeat the experience, even though most of my lovers seemed eager to give it a whirl. So for once I was the prudish one, and I vetoed the idea out of hand. Or at least, I told them in no uncertain terms that <u>I</u> wouldn\u2019t participate in such a venture. I know better by now than to forbid Marguerite to do anything.<br /> <br /> So I texted Joan my regrets, to let her know that my talents were needed elsewhere this morning, but that I would be back to the Dream House shortly. She responded with her understanding, and told me not to worry about it. Gawain and I are about to head over to Monica\u2019s now to see how she\u2019s doing (since she has such a good relationship with Gawain, we thought his presence might make things go a little more smoothly). I hope everything is going to be all right.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T20:35:41-07:00","id":907413,"title":"","content":"<b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> Friday, November 14<sup>th</sup><br /> Nine years, seven months, eight days<br /> Days without stabbing: 0<br /> <br /> What the hell is it with me and leechfingers? I mean, I have absolutely no doubt in my mind that Leanne Sheen's claims of having fled Hollywood after discovering about the Grand Maw is a lie. She was in the inner circle and party to feeding their pet Gentry with hapless Changelings. She fled because she was afraid of ending up on the menu because they're running out of victims to feed to that thing. Hell, even if I'm wrong (and I'm not) she's from Jolie's durance. She's a monster. A very, very pretty monster. And she knows I know. We shared a look at breakfast, despite the fact that I said the polite words rather than call her out she could see that I didn't mean it. That I know she's a predator like me. She's dangerous and untrustworthy and only looking out for herself. And I want her. Holy fuck do I want her. I want to close my eyes and feel that cold touch along my skin. Maybe it's the thought that there actually is something worthwhile to steal inside me... or... no, I mean that is part of it. But honestly it reminds me of Them. It always makes me think of the way They gathered me broken and bloody and held me. Stoked my hair and my wounds and numbed all the pain and soothed me in the blissful darkness. It scares me and it excites me and fuck if it doesn't make me ache something fierce just thinking about it. What the fuck is wrong with me? I am not meek and soft and yielding. I am Calamity. I'm jagged edges and blood.<br /> <br /> I should talk to Dr Emmett about this maybe. But I'm... fuck I guess I'm afraid of what we'll find if we look under that particular rock too deeply. And it's weird, I trust that woman with the terrible things I've done but admitting to how that makes me feel is just... I'm uncomfortable with it. But who can I fucking talk to about this? Gawain has put up with so much of my bullshit lately and as much as I love him and know he'd be supportive I don't think he'd really have insights into this. Do I really need insight? I mean, I already know how it makes me feel and I'm just not okay with that. But what do I need? The Whispering Voices made me helpless. They tortured me until I was too broken to resist and then They were gentle and affectionate. They claimed They cared when no one else did. And so help me, I did start to want that, hell I fucking needed it. I needed someone in that horrible place to care about me despite the price tag,<br /> <br /> But I don't fucking need that anymore. I have Gawain. I have Becky. I have Jacob. I have Lori and Luna. I have Charlotte and Jack. I have people who care, who actually fucking care about me despite what a monster I can be. I don't have to buy an illusion of tenderness and affection with my flesh and blood and pain. I have the real thing.<br /> <br /> So why does the thought of her touching me that way make me weak in the knees and wet? Why do I still feel this lingering regret that I didn't let the Handmaidens take me home from the pier that day and have their way with me? Fuck, I guess I'm just lucky de la Rocha likes the other end of the leash and is apparently the only leechfinger that doesn't like vampire fucking people.<br /> <br /> I am going to have to watch myself around her. I am going to have to keep a lid on these urges. Leanne is fucking dangerous and not to be trusted. And unlike Gloria, the programming was the least of our worries with her. She's looking out for herself and it would be the height of stupid to not think she wouldn't twist me around her magic fingers in a heartbeat if it was in her interests or if she was just hungry. And even knowing that full well I fucking want her to.<br /> <br /> At least Gawain and I were able to purge the programming from her dreams last night and it was identical to Gloria's, which may lend more credence to the idea that Fallen Stars has blanketed their people with it. Also, there was that incubus. Those things don't tend to mess with Changelings without a reason. Human dreams are way easier to deal with and they're pretty much helpless to notice or fight back. I don't think it's a coincidence. Hopefully Gawain's dream prison will allow us to catch it and get some answers. And Leanne is aware it was there and can try to be on the lookout for it. And man, it did look rather surprised when I sucker punched the ever-living fuck out of it last night. I just wish I knew how long that bought us.<br /> <br /> At any rate, the trip to the amusement park really was just what the doctor ordered for Gawain and I. He's been fretting over me and worrying and trying to take care of me. I really don't deserve him. But after the week I've put him through I wanted to do something cheesy and romantic and silly with him you know. I hate that sort of thing usually, but when he's there it's different. And it really did bring out that bright almost childish side in him. And when he's having fun like that it is just infectious. Dear lady but we were so fucking THAT couple and we just didn't fucking care. And when he powered through the crooked bottle throw and won me that ridiculously huge green bear it was such a rom com moment. And it was absolutely perfect. And then I actually managed to carry it home without catching it on my glass. I think we both really needed that. I know I did. I love him and I love the way he can make me feel like I used to. And for a couple of hours at least, I was just his girl Kat.<br /> <br /> I just wish I had the same magic bullet for Dark Kimberly and Annika. They love each other, I know they do. They know they do. But despite what songs and poetry may claim, that is not enough. It's actually just what makes the whole situation hurt so damn much. They both want to make it work somehow but they're different and they've got baggage and I don't know how to help them resolve that. I want them to be happy and I know that they do make each other happy. The problem is they also drive each other crazy.<br /> <br /> At least their fallout hasn't involved threats of vehicular anal assault. This whole business with Monica and Haley and Dominika is a proper train wreck. I hope Gawain and Lori can talk at least a bit of sense into her. Monica is much better when she's a jolly green giantess. I like her, I do, but she came into my house intent on doing harm (during MY solo...) and I cannot have that. I know she and D had a conversation with their fists (and a wall and a chuck of concrete and some other poor smuck's car I think...) so maybe she's calmer. Though apparently now Dominika is in a fighting mood. Good to see she's as level headed as the rest, it bodes well for her and Monica's future. Honestly, I suspect Haley\u2019s right about the situation but they're all grown women and it's not my fucking problem unless one of them decides to come into my house and try to give another an assful of Pontiac again.<br /> <br /> My training with White Maria is going well. It's weird just how different her style is from what I know. We'd talked about it some while doing Tai Chi and I knew going in that I was going from a very hard fighting style to a very soft one. But talking about it in abstract, about the philosophy behind the flow of energy and intent is so not the same as actually trying to do it. It's going to require me to change to the whole way I think about and approach fighting, which is a very useful thing in the long run. This will make me a better fighter and the disciple of mind and body is important. But right now, I am so at the Chumbawumba stage. She gave me that odd look when I joked about that this morning. I know that she used to practice with Sundown and apparently my occasional witty banter reminds her of her friend. She's not an easy woman to read, so I am not sure how she feels about that. Honestly, I am not sure if she knows how she feels about it. But I like her and I enjoy training and practicing with her. I'm not sure I'd call us friends exactly, but I think we could be. I think I'd like it if we were.<br /> <br /> And speaking of friends, Andromeda is going to be here soon to spend the afternoon. Joan's got some court business which she was apparently a bit guarded with Lori on the details of and didn't want her love to be alone. Apparently she's been a little subdued lately and Joan wants her to have some company to keep her from just going quiet and withdrawn. I wish the circumstances were a bit brighter but I am rather looking forward to spending some time with my favorite alien girl. I can't help Gawain with the dream prison (and I won't be able to help him fight the incubus once he catches it.) so I need something to keep me busy. Maybe we'll all do something properly girly once Lori is back from checking on Monica.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> But there is something to be said for routine. After Calamity and I got back from our therapy sessions we decided to spar for a bit before breakfast. We went out back after we\u2019d gathered up our knives and went at it. Calamity was a little less tense this morning. Her movements were not as stiff as they have been for the past few days during our matches. It was good to see her closer to her usual self. Not that I think Calamity is back to her old self, nor do I think Insincere Marguerite is, but they are both closer than they have been. So, Calamity tried a couple of moves that I think she picked up from me. They worked pretty well with her fighting style. Though, it was a bit disconcerting at first to see moves that Rook taught me get used against me, but then we\u2019ve been sparring together long enough to pick up each other\u2019s moves without formal teaching.<br /> <br /> After we were done sparring Calamity said that she was going to go the stage and practice for her number. I would have thought that she\u2019d have worked up enough of an appetite after the workout to want to eat, but she elected to practice more. I have noticed her doing that more than usual lately. I think it\u2019s her way of avoiding direct interactions with Insincere Marguerite, or at least limiting them to as short a time as possible. She may have also thought that wedding plans would be brought up and didn\u2019t want to disturb anything with that. I understand that she doesn\u2019t want to upset Marguerite any more than she has to, but if they really are going to get some semblance of normalcy back then they need to interact more, not less.<br /> <br /> On a slightly more serious note, Gawain brought up the idea of creating a Dream Bastion that we can all use should the need arise. I thought it sounded like a good idea, though some of our number were not aware that being attacked through dreams was even a concern. I\u2019ve heard about other Gentry that used dreams to influence their \u201ccharges\u201d to do something or not to do something, but the Lady wasn\u2019t one of them. She left those that entered her realm to themselves for the most part, both in dreams and in the physical world. The environment and human nature were generally enough to cull the numbers and to keep them in check. Some she cultivated for more important roles, like me and Rook. Others she left to their own devices. Still, I thought that creating our own Dream Bastion was a sound plan. Especially considering that Gawain\u2019s Keeper was big into dream manipulation. That might be an avenue that he/she/it uses to attack Gawain and/or us.<br /> <br /> Something of a surprise for me was at breakfast this morning Insincere Marguerite asked to speak to me. She and Julia had been talking about who would give them away at their wedding and she wanted me to be the one to give her away. Julia\u2019s father is giving her away, but Marguerite doesn\u2019t have that option. Her father still believes that the fetch is his daughter, so she needed someone to fill that role since he obviously won\u2019t. I was surprised and honored by the request. I said \u201cYes\u201d of course. I would be happy to be the one to give away one of my best friends.<br /> <br /> The other notable thing that happened this afternoon was Hailey coming by to visit with a newcomer to Malibu. Hailey brought a young lady who had fled from Hollywood, named Leanne Sheets. Apparently Leanne knows the Hollywood monarchs personally and is willing to give us information on them and their activities in exchange for sanctuary. The reason that Leanne was brought to the Dream House is so that Gawain and Calamity can work their dream magic and see if Leanne has any \u201cprogramming\u201d that might make her a spy for Hollywood or to do something we may not want her to do. Gawain agreed readily as did Calamity. Our resident Knight explained the process in general terms to Leanne and while nervous she was still willing to undergo a screening of sorts to look for any hidden directives. She admitted that she did not want to be controlled by anyone and was happy to make sure that was not the case.<br /> <br /> After Hailey and Leanne had left, and Lori had talked to Jolie we had a discussion about Leanne. It turns out that Leanne and Jolie had shared a durance, hence the phone call from Lori, and she did not trust Leanne as far as she could throw her. I don\u2019t think she used those exact words but it seemed pretty clear that she did not trust the newcomer to town. Calamity revealed that Leanne\u2019s biggest fear was of the Grandmaw, which is kind of what most of us had been thinking, but it was good to have it confirmed. Lori also revealed that Leanne is a leechfinger. She said that Leanne gives off an aura of cold that is unique to those type of Changelings. Jolie did not seem surprised about this, and given their durance it makes sense. Jolie had a bad habit of feeding off the creativity of mortals before Andromeda \u201cfixed\u201d her with the Table. Then there is Leanne\u2019s name. Leanne Sheets. Sounds an awful lot like Leanan Sidhe. The Leanan Sidhe are supposedly Irish Faeries that lure creative mortals away from their homes and feed on their inspiration and creativity. Sounds like she picked her name aptly.<br /> <br /> Lori also wanted to talk to just those of us in the motley, so the others stepped out of the room for a moment so we could talk. Lori said that she had noticed some changes in herself and had brought it up to Jolie while she was on the phone with her earlier. Jolie said that it sounded like Lori\u2019s connection to the Wyrd was growing stronger, and that ours might be as well. Apparently the lot of us pick up on each other\u2019s energy and we help strengthen ourselves and each other by such close proximity. Lori revealed that she had new feathers growing in and was excited by this since her wings have always been a little bit on the ragged side. Gawain at first said that he hadn\u2019t seen anything, but then noticed that he had some new silver filigree on his armor. Julia said that she has been more creative, and Calamity says that she feels like she has more potential and is sharper, literally. Insincere Marguerite said that she had noticed that she had become more flexible and I rolled up my sleeve to show everyone the new frost on my arms.<br /> <br /> It was also brought up that we may begin to exhibit personality quirks, or frailties as Jolie called them. This immediately brought to mind Chalcedony\u2019s fixation with the color blue and Madame Spidertoes thing about washing blood out of any clothing that she sees. Gawain pantomimed this last one and apparently De la Rocha took this as an insult to her ex and started yelling at Gawain. I was a little taken aback by the intensity of her reaction. Lori calmed down her girlfriend by assuring her that Gawain did not mean any harm by the pantomime and had not intended any insult. Eventually De la Rocha calmed down. I have seen her defend Spidertoes in the past, sometimes violently but this was the first time she raised her voice like that to a member of the motley. I don\u2019t know what it is, but Madam Spidertoes inspires loyalty in her paramours.<br /> <br /> After we talked about the Wyrd and our growing connection to it, we talked a bit more about Leanne. I think we agreed that we cannot trust her, not yet anyway. She may have come to us with an honest fear of the Grandmaw and possibly being its meal, but she may have ulterior motives that are just not as strong as the fear of the captive Keeper.<br /> <br /> Soon after that we all split up. Oleander had already left, as did Desiree and Gloria. The later pair went out for soft serve. Gawain and Calamity decided to go to an amusement park for the day, and Lori and De la Rocha went off together. I think they eventually ended up in the attic watching Julia paint. Meanwhile Luna and I stayed in and just hung out and watched Netflix on the big screen TV. I told Luna what we as a motley had talked about. I didn\u2019t think any of it was especially private, and thought it might be good to bring up just because Luna is around a lot and is going to notice the changes in people. Overall it was a fun, relaxing afternoon.<br /> <br /> Later at the show was when things got interesting. It started off normal enough. I had Ginny come by and ask how I was doing. I told her that I was doing just fine. I think she had just gotten back from talking to Calamity. I\u2019m not sure what they talked about but Ginny seemed to be in an okay mood when I talked to her so it couldn\u2019t have been anything too bad. After that Monica came in and was upset. She literally grabbed Hailey and headed outside. A moment later Gawain followed to make sure that everyone is okay. I assume. He is definitely the one that would do that. After a while he came back in and came over to talk to me about what was going on. Apparently what happened is that Hailey took it upon herself to talk to Dominika about her relationship with Monica. She was afraid that it was just a rebound kind of thing for Monica and that it would end up hurting one or both of them in the end. Well, what I can tell from right now is that it just hurt both Monica and Dominika. I can understand where Hailey was coming from. She wanted to stop something before it went too far, but in this case I think things had gone far enough that both parties were emotionally invested in what was happening. Her talking to Dominika just hurt people\u2019s feelings on both fronts. Needless to say, Monica was upset by this and was eventually talked out of throwing a Pontiac at Hailey\u2019s head.<br /> <br /> De la Rocha thought that she might be able to smooth things over and went to go talk to Monica. She came back bruised and bleeding but happy. Apparently she had found Monica still in a bad mood and they duked it out in a parking lot. From the sound of it they both gave as good as they got and had the added bonus of incidental property damage to go along with the whole experience. Monica seemed to be somewhat calmed down at the end of the whole thing, so maybe she just needed to let off some steam and hit something or in this case someone. I suppose it all worked out in the end. Monica got to beat up someone that wouldn\u2019t suffer lasting wounds and go to blow off some steam. De la Rocha got to engage in one of her favorite activities \u2013 fighting \u2013 and both parties left the situation on good or at least neutral terms. Lori immediately worked on healing all of De la Rocha\u2019s wounds and started asking where Monica was since she was still out there injured and might need or want medical attention.<br /> <br /> From my own perspective I wasn\u2019t sure if Monica would want to be healed or not. I guess it depends on how she viewed the fight with De la Rocha. If I had just fought someone that was a worthwhile opponent and I wanted to remember the fight I might have refused healing because I wanted some sort of mark or scar to remember the fight by. I have several scars that do not invoke a bad memory, rather the opposite actually. The time that Rook and I fought that lesser Keeper in our the Lady\u2019s realm was something that I definitely wanted to remember. At the time I was rather proud of myself for the accomplishment of beating him, even if it almost killed me to do it. I have the marks to prove that I survived. They are almost like a badge of honor. I wasn\u2019t sure if Lori would understand that sentiment so I let it go and figured that Monica would tell Lori if she wanted to be healed or not when the time came.<br /> <br /> To end the evening Calamity and Gawain took Leanne into the Hollow to help her with the Dream healing. I stayed and kept watch just to be on the safe side. I realized that our defenses at the Hollow are rather substantial but it was a rather vulnerable position to put oneself in regardless. So I stayed. They woke in the morning and explained to everyone over breakfast that there had been a simple command left in Leanne\u2019s head just like there had been in Gloria\u2019s, but that it had been easily dealt with. There was also something about a goldfish in a bowl that appeared in every room in her mind. Turns out that was an incubus, but they are not sure it was just there or if it had been employed to keep an eye on her or influence her in any way. Hailey was also there and said that she would be okay and that Monica is no longer after her. Apparently she had talked with De la Rocha about the whole matter.<br /> <br /> So, overall it was not the most eventful day, but it was definitely interesting. I am finding that I have to reorient myself sometimes to the new order of things. I have been living here for several months now and am still expecting something big and bad to happen. I guess I am still waiting on Rook to figure out what was done to him and come back and hunt me all over again. Or something from Hollywood could spark a larger conflict. Things have been tense on that front for a while now and I find myself expecting something to happen. It may just be that I am used to a more active lifestyle. I used to get into life and death fights as a matter of course and now I find myself in a life where the worst things that happen are that people\u2019s feelings get hurt. Not that there weren\u2019t some valid feelings of betrayal and loss going on. It just didn\u2019t affect me too much and I find that I am somewhat distant from my fellows where I was closer before. That is something that I plan on working on with my therapist about. I do not like feeling detached from the feelings and events of my friends. What happens to them should be more important to me no matter how big or small the event in question is.<br /> <br /> It seems like me and Calamity are going in opposite directions here. She is feeling perhaps more guilt and upset than she should about recent events while I am feeling less. It is a rather disconcerting feeling. I try to reassure her that she did nothing wrong. That there was no other way to resolve the issue that we had at that exact moment, but right now I\u2019m not sure if that is true of if it is just because I am feeling so detached from things or not. Logically I cannot think of another way that we could have handled the situation, but I\u2019m also trying to look at my motives and feelings objectively. Are my emotions or reactions to things compromised? Am I viewing things in a way that other people, normal people would not? I don\u2019t honestly know. That might also be something that I need to talk to my therapist about. I am so messed up.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> Julia has taken it upon herself to fix my and Lori\u2019s rift. I was very unhappy with how she did it, as I was unready to confront Lori, but I understand. We really want our relationship with Lori and Maria to work. She did just have the three of us to make it easier on I, but it only sort of worked. Still, Lori tearfully apologized, and then we four went upstairs to enjoy each other\u2019s company. That was not a euphemism until four on the clock, when Lori\u2019s toxin ran out, and she Maria and I gently mingled while Julia painted us.<br /> <br /> Oh, also after breakfast but before upstairs we discussed the waxing of our power. Our Wyrds are feeding each other, bathed in glamour night after night, and our power is growing. My flexibility is improving, the realism of Julia\u2019s painting is improving, Lorelei\u2019s wings grow lovelier and Gawain is becoming more stately. We may have weaknesses growing as well, as I am more reluctant to walk with shoes, and Julia to destroy paintings. Maria made a big deal about not being able to wear gold rings, but I know exactly what she was thinking. Definitely.<br /> <br /> Related, our marriage update is Julia\u2019s father is giving her away, and I am going to be given away by Jacob. I do not feel a strong need to be given away, I am independent, but Julia is almost obscenely ecstatic at the idea of Jacob giving me away so we are doing it. I suspect she is reading more into the gesture than is there; I stopped sleeping with him when Luna entered the picture.<br /> <br /> The show that night went well. A woman named Leanne of the Spring Court also defected from Hollywood and came to have any scripts removed. Gloria remembered her as part of the ruling clique but not a ruler herself. Calamity\u2019s powers and Gawain\u2019s powers seemed to bear out she was not a spy against us, but both suspected she was hardly being selfless. Which is fine, I am not so selfless myself.<br /> <br /> There is a huge row between Monica, Hailey, and Dominika, focusing on the fact that Monica, on the rebound, entered a relationship with Dominika, and Hailey was enraged, both because of jealousy and believing (probably correctly) that Dominika was going to be hurt by the emotional fallout. As it stood, there was a shouting match between Monica and Hailey, and Monica and Maria beat the crap out of each other. Maria enjoyed it, apparently\u2026a very good thing for Monica. Had Maria been badly hurt, Monica\u2019s life would not be worth living.<br /> <br /> No one harms my women. But in fairness I do have to account for Maria\u2019s enjoying fistfights. At least it does not involve guns.<br /> <br /> That tasty looking Day Courtier showed up again to the show. I did not devour her.<br /> <br /> Afterwards, I threw myself at Lori. The warm, gentle mingling of our bodies and wounded souls from earlier was turned to a boil, and the night was one of intense passion and exploration, as I pushed the very limits of my empowered form. This morning, I had to pop everything back into joint. Perhaps push a bit less hard next time.<br /> <br /> I spent breakfast in Lorelei\u2019s lap, as is right and proper. Though Julia apparently had enough and after a short while pulled I into her lap, to feed I\u0336 me cherries and cream as she had the previous morning. Monica and Hailey kept fighting, so Lori is going to go with Gawain to talk to her. Joan is bringing Andromeda here, and I will watch her if Andromeda gets here before they get back.<br /> <br /> There is concern the Summer Court may be mobilizing against our Courts. Charlotte wants to absorb the Night Courtiers en masse, which would be quite a power play. Salk wants her to not be permitted to this, while the Warlock wants to know what would be best for her Courtiers here. I am inclined to side with Charlotte\u2026both because I lack desire to rule, and because it would get me considerable influence within the Leaden Mirror. And if I am still one of the more respected of the Night, well, that has even more benefit. Felicity would be enraged though. But she won\u2019t be happy about my engagement to Julia either.<br /> <br /> She can be as angry as she wants. I know who the master in our relationship is. Maybe it is time she knelt. But I must be careful\u2026<br /> <br /> Regardless, things are getting better, not worse, and Julia has dress sketches for me. Later then.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LVII</i><br /> <br /> It came up that Julia has a frailty against destroying paintings. De La Rocha dodged the question.<br /> <br /> Lori sensing Leanne is a Leechfinger is just something I let her do. I figure she and Insincere Marguerite have spent enough time intimately close to one to have some chance of pinging the Kith.<br /> <br /> Also, White Maria likes Calamity in her own distant, stoic way.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s see, Incubi are discussed in <i>Dancers in the Dusk</i>, same place as Gawain\u2019s Entitlement. Bastions are discussed in <i>Swords at Dawn</i>.<br /> <br /> I was amused by what details did and did not appear. No one mentioned White Maria came to the door with Hailey and Leanne, though most mentioned Hailey. Only Calamity and Gawain mentioned the giant bear, and only Gawain mentioned Insincere Marguerite\u2019s cleavage riding (with help from Contract of Mirrors), and her cat like behavior (she meowed at Lori once, and curled up in Lori\u2019s lap) was mentioned just by Lori. People latch onto different things.<br /> <br /> Well I hope that covers it and people are not disappointed by lack of prank wars. A combination of IC Julia wanting to nip this in the bud and OOC player discussion lead to the consensus it would not be best for the game or really the direction we wanted Lorelei or Insincere Marguerite to go.<br /> <br /> Anyway, comments and questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 06-05-2016, 02:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T12:55:58-07:00","id":912392,"title":"","content":"Baroness, do you usually just find pictures of the Changelings' masks, or do you find pictures of their mien as well? I'm curious as to what the respective mien(s?) of both Maria and Captain Jack look like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T13:56:49-07:00","id":912417,"title":"","content":"I like your in story rationale for the increase in wyrd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T01:24:27-07:00","id":912690,"title":"","content":"Taidragon&gt;It's a mix. For the most part, it is Miens. There are cases when I use a Mask pic and point out something different about it but it is almost always the Mien.<br /> <br /> Maria (assuming you mean Maria De La Rocha, not White Maria) looks mostly human, except she is very pale and her skin is unusually cool to the touch (but not, say, beyond human range). I considered giving her a witch's nipple but she wound up getting naked with people before I decided so I decided not to. Her Mask has a skin color closer to typical for Hispanics (though she is still very white, her ability to &quot;pass&quot; has not gone unremarked on given how aggressive she is about treatment of Hispanics). <br /> <br /> The only unusual thing about Captain Jack is exaggerated musculature. And excessive awesomeness.<br /> <br /> Omenseer&gt; Thanks. ^_^. Totally after the fact rationale, but sounded good. ^_^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T01:53:40-07:00","id":912696,"title":"","content":"Yes, I did mean De La Rocha; apologies for the vagueness there, I had work to get going to and I couldn't remember the proper spelling for her name, so I settled with Maria. I had forgotten that White Maria was about.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the reply! I have been working on finding references for my Changelings, and with some of them it has been rather difficult to get a good mien, so I was curious about how you went about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T13:14:51-07:00","id":912965,"title":"","content":"Yeah, finding good mask and mien pictures that actually match can be tough. For Calamity, I lucked out. I had a mental image of how I wanted her mask to look and an idea that Melinda Clarke as Lady Heather from CSI would likely fit the mood/expression/look I wanted. And I had completely forgotten that she was a zombie in Return of the Living Dead 3 until I did an image search. Calamity's background was actually not completely ironed out at that point and so I actually took some inspiration from the pic to get what have become some of the key points of her backstory now.<br /> <br /> In looking for images,Finding a mein pic from a show or movie can be useful since you can then hunt down a pic of that actor out of makeup. Doing an image search on a photomanipulation can also pull up the original sometimes, I guess the main thing is that in my experience so far, finding a mein first and working back to the mask seems easier. Also, I have more than a few pics that I've saved off because they look lke they could be interesting changelings. It is sometimes easier to adjust the details to suit a great pic than to find one that perfectly matches. <br /> <br /> Just my random thoughts as someone who has gone picture hunting for changeling concepts. Hope it is useful to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T23:02:38-07:00","id":913254,"title":"","content":"Taidragon&gt; It's all good. And yes, Mien is the hardest part of finding good pictures for Changeling. Especially ~100 NPCs or so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T09:52:13-07:00","id":913468,"title":"","content":"Just to throw in my two cents here...<br /> <br /> I also found the mien pic for Lorelei first and worked backwards from that. A quick google search for &quot;bird girl&quot; provided the usual mixed bag of results, one of which was the image I eventually went with (a beautiful if somewhat unearthly blonde girl with ragged, multicolored wings). Like Amberghylles, I incorporated elements of that picture into Lorelei's backstory to better fit the image.<br /> <br /> When I went looking for mask pics, I also lucked out a bit. It seemed to me that a cabaret performer should be wearing skimpy leather and fishnets, and as a comic book geek from way back, I started searching for good pics of Black Canary. This led me to a host of images from the CW television show <i>Arrow</i>, which in turn led me to Emily Bett Rickards (who, of course, does <i>not</i> play Black Canary in that show... but whatever). Her naturally glamorous look coupled with the host of images in her more &quot;sedate&quot; role as Felicity Smoak fit the two sides of Lori's personality very well.<br /> <br /> The only other time I've played in a Changeling game, my character (Molly &quot;Mopsy&quot; Swift, Winter Court Beast/Runnerswift) only had a mien pic; I never found a mask image that I felt suited her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T16:33:39-07:00","id":913718,"title":"","content":"yea, Gawain has vividly different pictures for Mask and Mien. Ace has a strongly photoshopped picture for his Mask from the same character as his Mien. Jacob has a recolor, essentially. Insincere Marguerite looks nearly identical apart from being slightly paler and skinnier, and having a two foot tongue and extra digit on tapering fingers, so no real difference in pictures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T03:03:39-07:00","id":913976,"title":"","content":"Did the players choose their frailties?<br /> Did Julia truly felt threatened by Jacob sleeping with Insincere Marguerite?<br /> Did Calamity name the bear Gawain won for her?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T10:23:03-07:00","id":914185,"title":"","content":"1) Yes. I felt they knew their characters best. There was discussion I had input on, and end of the day i could veto.<br /> <br /> 2) Yes. People can be very rather twitchy about exes, especially if there was no formal break up. Added to the mix is Jacob is a man and they are in a lesbian relationship. I have personally seen crazy tension there. Though it is less true fear Insincere Marguerite will leave her more worry about measuring up.<br /> <br /> 3) Not that I know of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T12:11:20-07:00","id":914259,"title":"","content":"My two cents:<br /> <br /> 1) I will note that Lorelei's frailty - which has not yet come up in game; even she doesn't know what it is yet - was one of two that the Baroness suggested. I came up with a few myself, but I honestly thought that our kindly GM's suggestions were better suited to the character in the long run. What is this frailty? Well, I'll let the suspense build for a while longer...<br /> <br /> 2) As for Julia, she can be quite possessive given the right circumstances. There have even been some subtle signs of resentment towards Lorelei, as Marguerite has gotten a little clingy over the past few sessions. It hasn't been prominent, and I don't think it necessarily heralds trouble to come, but it's there. Lori is doing her best to reassure Julia that when push comes to shove, she is Marguerite's one-and-only. <i>(The contents of the preceding paragraph represent my opinion of the situation only, and not some insight into the Baroness' future plans)</i>.<br /> <br /> 3) What? We're not sharing the exalted moniker of The Lord Sebastian Vercingetorix Bearrington McGrowlypants III, Esquire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T18:32:14-07:00","id":914522,"title":"","content":"I feel that everyone did a very nice job in making their fralities; they reflect on the characters very well, and feel like a natural extension off them.<br /> <br /> Even from afar, Julia does seem like the kind of person who'd be a bit...defensive towards Jacob simply for having shared a bed with Insincere Marguerite, and the bits of instability she has showcased before doesn't help her case. Still, glad that Insincere Marguerite is on hand to keep her from doing too extreme things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenitentTom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play?p=914259#post914259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> 3) What? We're not sharing the exalted moniker of The Lord Sebastian Vercingetorix Bearrington McGrowlypants III, Esquire?</div> </div> </div> </div>I love that name. XD Thanks PenitentTom!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T21:16:58-07:00","id":914655,"title":"","content":"I believe that was the name Lori gave Hailey for the bear when she showed her to Gawain and Calamity's room. I am not sure Calamity knows it however, I expect she'll run with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T22:05:56-07:00","id":914673,"title":"","content":"My players are super, super awesome.<br /> <br /> As an aside, Julia knows she is prone to irrational behavior, and that is part of why she follows Insincere Marguerite's guidance. It's not purely D/s, but, okay, it is mostly D/s.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T11:31:30-07:00","id":914939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amberghylles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play?p=914655#post914655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe that was the name Lori gave Hailey for the bear when she showed her to Gawain and Calamity's room. I am not sure Calamity knows it however, I expect she'll run with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if that was it exactly, but it was something along those lines. I hate that I forgot to include all mention of the bear in Lori's journal on my initial pass, but when I went back and tried to shoehorn it in, it just seemed forced. Never fear; I'm sure we'll have cause to visit The Lord Sebastian Vercingetorix Bearrington McGrowlypants III, Esquire again soon enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T15:55:17-07:00","id":915151,"title":"","content":"I just hope he is not conspiring against us with the puppets. I don't trust that Hubert Cumberdale. He's got shifty eyes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T16:19:45-07:00","id":915169,"title":"","content":"Very wise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" 