libu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T03:22:26-07:00","id":915493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amberghylles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play?p=915151#post915151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just hope he is not conspiring against us with the puppets. I don't trust that Hubert Cumberdale. He's got shifty eyes.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I suspect Edith. She's got shifty eyes.&quot;<br /> &quot;Mary, Edith's the one who was murdered.&quot;<br /> &quot;Then I suspect Misses Beddely. She's got shifty eyes.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm sorry, I couldn't help but quote &quot;The Chimes of Midnight&quot; there. It's a bit of a spoiler if you haven't listened to the audio, but it really is an awesome story...actually wouldn't be a bad Changeling game now that I think on it...<br /> <br /> Also, I forgot to do this before (and I'm questioning myself for it), but thank you guys a ton for your input on finding/making pictures for mien and masks. It is very helpful advice, kindly given and has me thinking on what I could do for certain Changelings I have in mind but not in image. Still not entirely sure where to find a picture of a chubby anthropomorphic black cat, but a half-oxidized copper maiden should be much easier to procure now...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 06-16-2016, 06:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T10:43:57-07:00","id":916317,"title":"","content":"So long as the puppets aren't trying to steal the life force of the Sesame Street demographic we won't have to worry about the Greater Threat (tm).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T23:40:25-07:00","id":917825,"title":"","content":"The Last Dance Motley settles into a nice weekend, busy as always but also exciting. Lori has a moment of elation (and mild fear), Calamity takes on a task, Jacob helps an unlikely friend in need, and Insincere Marguerite struggles with her loss of confidence. Speaking of that Darkling, her story did not really take place on camera, as these stories tend to not, but takes place at the end of the session.<br /> <br /> Gawain\u2019s player had to miss, but this should not be a pattern. They should be back next time.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LVIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Okay, so my mood has vacillated wildly over the past day or so, due to circumstances mostly beyond my control. So if this entry seems a little chaotic or disjointed, that would be why. Fair warning.<br /> <br /> (Why do I consistently write these journal entries as though I expect someone to read them? I don\u2019t know. It would be a colossal embarrassment to find out that all of my deepest darkest secrets were known to someone else\u2026 so why do I persist in taking a conversational tone in what is essentially a private reflection? Maybe it\u2019s the drama queen in me, plotting my life out in a series of monologues and dialogues. Maybe as a Changeling, I find it easier to think of my life as a story to be told. Or maybe I\u2019m just internally lonely and a little weird. Who can say?)<br /> <br /> So the last time I wrote anything in here, Gawain and I were preparing to head over to Monica\u2019s house to see if she needed any healing (and to see if she was holding a grudge). Unfortunately, Gawain was called away unexpectedly at the last moment, and was unable to join me. I\u2019m not sure what came up; he didn\u2019t say. In any case, I was prepared to head over to Monica\u2019s place all by my lonesome when another idea struck me.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d noticed that Marguerite had been acting sort of down lately. It was almost like she\u2019d lost her confidence on some level (if you can believe that). I\u2019d thought about asking her about it, but I didn\u2019t want to call attention to it and embarrass her. Considering that my own actions earlier this week probably contributed to her funk, I thought it would be nice if I could do something to draw her out a bit.<br /> <br /> I asked her if she would mind accompanying me to Monica\u2019s house. \u201cGawain can\u2019t make it after all, and I\u2019d really feel better if I had someone I can trust along, just in case Monica\u2019s still holding a grudge,\u201d I said, injecting just a bit of nervous tension into my voice. I didn\u2019t really believe that Monica would do anything to hurt me, of course\u2026 but you can never tell when Changelings are concerned. Some of us have odd triggers in our subconscious.<br /> <br /> Marguerite happily agreed to accompany me, and the two of us sped across town in my \u2018vette. She was awfully touchy-feely on the way over there, and I think she appreciated both the opportunity to spend time with me and the minor vote of confidence I gave her. When we got to Monica\u2019s place, Dominika answered the door with a glare. \u201cYou\u2019ve got a lot of nerve, showing up here after what your girlfriend did to mine last night,\u201d she said with no small amount of venom.<br /> <br /> I sighed softly. \u201cI\u2019m not here to fight, Dominika,\u201d I assured her. \u201cI just wanted to see Monica, to make sure she\u2019s all right.\u201d<br /> <br /> Dominika\u2019s stony look didn\u2019t soften. \u201cShe\u2019s fine,\u201d she almost spat out. \u201cI took care of her.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled. \u201cI\u2019m glad,\u201d I said softly. \u201cLook, can I talk with the two of you for just a few minutes, please? I\u2019d like to make sure this doesn\u2019t go any further\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Dominika looked like she was prepared to reply with something suitably scathing, but Monica\u2019s voice called softly from deeper inside. \u201cJust let her in, Dominika. We need to talk this out anyway.\u201d<br /> <br /> Dominika grudgingly allowed the two of us to enter, and we found Monika in the living room. She offered us seats, and we sat down to discuss the previous evening\u2019s fisticuffs like civilized people.<br /> <br /> It <u>was</u> remarkably civil in the end, actually. Monica apologized for making a scene at the Dream House, and seemed really embarrassed by the whole situation. I told her (and Dominika) that I understood why she was upset by Halley\u2019s actions, but that we at the Dream House have to work to reestablish our status as a haven in the wake of the Chalcedony incident.<br /> <br /> The rest of the conversation mostly consisted of Monica reliving her fight with D with something like fondness. Dominika and I exchanged long-suffering glances while she went on about the destruction, and I think the Caribbean beauty started to calm down and relax a bit at that point. I made sure to mention that Monica had given as well as she got, and that I had spent a considerable amount of time tending to D\u2019s wounds the previous evening. I think Dominika was sympathetic, having gone through something similar herself.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt wasn\u2019t as even as all that,\u201d Monica admitted. \u201cDe la Rocha has gotten a lot stronger recently. She could never have put me through a wall before, no matter how good she was.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cWe\u2019ve all developed a few new tricks recently,\u201d I replied, \u201cI just hope D\u2019s abilities don\u2019t get her into trouble.\u201d<br /> <br /> Yeah. What a laugh <u>that</u> turned out to be!<br /> <br /> I\u2019m getting ahead of myself. After Marguerite and I said our goodbyes, we hurried back to the Dream House. I confess that I might have been speeding a little in the hope that I could make it home before Joan and Andromeda dropped by. I had promised Joan that I\u2019d keep Andromeda company while she was off on Summer Court business today, and then I\u2019d been called away to deal with the Monica situation, and I didn\u2019t want Joan to think that I\u2019d forgotten about my promise, or that I was avoiding her or anything like that.<br /> <br /> We got back to the house about five minutes before Joan and Andromeda arrived. I greeted them at the door, and Andromeda\u2019s face lit up when she saw me. She gave me a big hug and thanked me for agreeing to spend the day with her. After an almost painful moment of consideration, Joan stepped forward and offered me a chaste embrace as well. It was the first time she\u2019d been openly affectionate with me in front of others, and that didn\u2019t escape my notice.<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you, Lorelei,\u201d she said softly.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou know you only had to ask, sweetie,\u201d I said warmly. \u201cSpending time with Andromeda isn\u2019t a chore; it\u2019s a privilege.\u201d<br /> <br /> Joan gave me a genuine smile and a nod, then turned to go. \u201cI hope this business will not take long. At the very least, I shall see you tonight at the show.\u201d Then she took her leave.<br /> <br /> Andromeda, Marguerite and I made our way upstairs to where Julia was once more painting in the attic. Andromeda revealed to us that she and Joan are officially engaged now, but that they\u2019re keeping it a secret from the rest of the Freehold for several reasons. At first, it was because Joan had taken a lot of flak for having a \u201cblind spot\u201d in Andromeda, but now\u2026 well, Andromeda very sweetly said that she didn\u2019t want to make the announcement now because she didn\u2019t want to steal Marguerite and Julia\u2019s thunder. I think Julia was touched by this sentiment.<br /> <br /> There was also some mention of the curious momentum that seems to accompany engagements. It\u2019s been remarked that once a single engagement is announced within a circle of friends, it seems like others inevitably follow. Joan and Andromeda <u>also</u> don\u2019t want to seem like they\u2019re just getting on the marriage bandwagon. There was a fair amount of giggling among us as we resolved not to mention this strange phenomenon around D.<br /> <br /> One thing that\u2019s probably worth mentioning is that Andromeda kept calling Joan \u201cLindsay.\u201d I can only assume that this was her name before she was Taken. Since it\u2019s not widely known, I can <u>also</u> assume that Joan doesn\u2019t want people finding that out. I think the others understand this as well, but maybe I should talk with them just to be on the safe side.<br /> <br /> Andromeda was pretty upset that she had let it slip, and as an act of contrition she told us all that her own former name had been Rebecca. In the interest of full disclosure, I told her that my name had once been Juliette (and told her that she could share that with Joan if she wants to). She smiled and expressed the opinion that it was a beautiful name.<br /> <br /> Before I get to the other big news, I wanted to mention that there were a few times when Andromeda\u2019s melancholy showed through\u2026 mostly in regards to the Table. She seemed almost desperate to find a way to use it safely, so that she could help more people like she helped Joan and Jolie. My motley-mates and I tried to oppose this line of thought gently but firmly, as none of us want to risk Andromeda\u2019s well-being again, but she was adamant about researching the possibility. Though I\u2019m sure Joan is aware of her fianc\u00e9\u2019s feelings on this subject, maybe I should mention this conversation to her just the same.<br /> <br /> Okay, so shortly after Jacob joined us in the attic, Andromeda got a phone call. It was one of those infuriating situations where you know someone is talking about something very important, but you\u2019re only getting half of the conversation, and your brain tries to make up likely scenarios about what\u2019s really going on. Add to that the fact that Andromeda kept glancing over at me and saying things like \u201cyes, she\u2019s fine,\u201d and \u201cno, I don\u2019t think she\u2019s heard yet,\u201d and you can understand why I was a big tense ball of curiosity after a few short moments.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat\u2019s going on?\u201d I interrupted when Andromeda paused.<br /> <br /> She shrugged. \u201cJoan says that de la Rocha might be in some sort of trouble with the Summer Court,\u201d she said after a moment.<br /> <br /> My heart plummeted. \u201cIs she okay?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019s not hurt,\u201d Andromeda hastened to reassure me.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat happened?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> Andromeda looked sheepish. \u201cShe\u2026 she punched Viscount Augustine in the face,\u201d she admitted after a moment.<br /> <br /> I know I blinked a couple of times at that. \u201cShe\u2026 <u>what</u>?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd menaced him with a church pew,\u201d Andromeda added. I\u2019m not sure, but I think I spotted a glimmer of amusement in her dark eyes.<br /> <br /> I sputtered for a moment, then regained my composure. \u201cIs that Joan? Can I talk to her?\u201d I asked frantically.<br /> <br /> It <u>was</u> Joan, and I <u>could</u> talk to her, as it turned out. Andromeda handed me her phone, and I held it up to my ear with trembling hands. \u201cJoan, what\u2019s going on? Is she all right? Does she need my help?\u201d<br /> <br /> Joan\u2019s voice cut across my increasingly hysterical questions with quiet assurance. \u201cCalm down, Lorelei,\u201d she said softly, \u201cde la Rocha is fine. She stopped by the church during her lunch break so that she could join the discussion regarding our Court\u2019s stance on the Day and Night courtiers within the Freehold. The discussion became rather heated. As your motley includes a Night Courtier, De la Rocha felt it necessary to remind Viscount Augustine \u2013 with some vigor \u2013 that the Dream House is meant to be a place of sanctuary for <u>all</u> changelings. The Viscount implied\u2026 he said\u2026\u201d Her voice faltered for the first time, and I thought I detected a hint of anger there.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat is it, sweetie?\u201d I asked, trying to remain calm.<br /> <br /> Joan\u2019s voice was tight when she continued. \u201cHe said that the Last Dance motley advertises the Dream House as a sanctuary mostly so that you will continue to enjoy a wide selection of lovers,\u201d she finished after a moment. \u201cDe la Rocha took issue with this opinion, and struck the King of Summer in retaliation. She then proceeded to pick up a full-sized pew \u2013 which had previously been bolted to the floor \u2013 and threaten to \u2018beat the bitch out of him,\u2019 as I believe she put it.\u201d By the end of this sentence, the anger had been replaced by tacit approval.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh shit,\u201d I said in response.<br /> <br /> \u201cIndeed,\u201d Joan agreed.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat are they going to do to her?\u201d I asked once I\u2019d wiped the tears out of the corners of my eyes.<br /> <br /> Joan thought for a moment. \u201cI do not know. She is officially being detained at the church for now, though I doubt anyone would try to stop her if she decided to leave. There will have to be some punitive action, of course\u2026 she struck the monarch. But Augustine himself has already admitted that his insult was unwarranted, so I doubt her punishment will be too severe.\u201d<br /> <br /> I sniffed with relief. \u201cIs she able to talk? Can I speak with her?\u201d I asked (a bit redundantly).<br /> <br /> Joan agreed, and a few moments later, my honey\u2019s voice came to me over the phone line, sounding chipper and incredibly pleased with herself. \u201cHey, babe,\u201d she said brightly.<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t you \u2018hey babe\u2019 me, missy,\u201d I started in, my fear making me a bit sharp. \u201cWhat the hell was that all about?\u201d<br /> <br /> D\u2019s voice faltered. \u201cHe said\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know what he said,\u201d I interrupted. \u201cThey\u2019re just [u]words/[u], D. I can take it. I\u2019m a big girl. I don\u2019t want you getting in trouble with your Court because\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> This time she interrupted me. \u201cHe as good as called you a <u>whore</u>, Lori,\u201d she said defiantly. \u201c<u>Nobody</u> says that about you. <u>Nobody</u> disrespects you. Not where I can hear them.\u201d<br /> <br /> I let out a shuddering sigh. This wasn\u2019t how I\u2019d wanted the conversation to go. \u201cCan I start over?\u201d I asked with a quaver.<br /> <br /> \u201cSure,\u201d D said, sounding a little confused.<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you,\u201d I said fervently. \u201cThank you <u>so much</u> for looking out for me like that. You are the best girlfriend ever, and I am lucky to have a knight in shining armor like you to take care of me. I\u2019m sorry I snapped at you before. I just get so worried about you sometimes. You\u2026 you punched the King, D. The monarch of your <u>own</u> Court. I don\u2019t want you to get in trouble over a little insult. I\u2019m not worth that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou are to me,\u201d she said after a moment, \u201cand you always will be, and nothing anybody says is ever going to change that.\u201d<br /> <br /> I was crying by that point, and I didn\u2019t care that the rest of the motley and Andromeda were staring at me from across the room. \u201cMy God, I didn\u2019t think it was possible for me to be any more in love with you,\u201d I whispered into the phone.<br /> <br /> \u201cI feel the same way,\u201d she replied, \u201cbut, y\u2019know, I can\u2019t get too mushy or emotional right now. I\u2019m kinda under a microscope at the moment.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAre they going to keep you there?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cThey might try,\u201d she said with a grin I could hear.<br /> <br /> \u201cBe serious,\u201d I admonished.<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t think so,\u201d she replied. \u201cThe Viscount has already apologized for what he said, and admitted that he was out of line. They\u2019ll probably give me a slap on the wrist at worst. But my lunch hour is almost up, so they\u2019ll have to let me go soon.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019ll be back for the show tonight?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cWouldn\u2019t miss it,\u201d she promised.<br /> <br /> \u201cGood,\u201d I said. \u201cDon\u2019t make any plans for later on tonight. I intend to show you my gratitude in a variety of ways.\u201d I let that hang in the air for a few moments as I moved as far away from the others as I could, turned away, and covered my mouth. \u201cTe amo, Maria,\u201d I whispered into the phone.<br /> <br /> \u201cTe amo, Juliette,\u201d she replied, \u201csiempre.\u201d And then she was gone. Joan and I exchanged pleasantries for a few minutes, and then I handed the phone back to Andromeda and walked back to the motley in a daze.<br /> <br /> Of course I had to explain the situation to the rest of them. Though I was still worried about D and about whatever punishment the Summer Court might level against her (Summer Court punishments can be pretty severe\u2026 at least according to Ace), I couldn\u2019t suppress a little shudder of glee every time I thought about how D is willing to fight for me. She punched a king. Because he insulted me. It\u2019s\u2026 I don\u2019t think the word \u201cflattering\u201d really covers it.<br /> <br /> So I futzed around for the rest of the afternoon, pretending to get ready for the show but really just bouncing back and forth between anxiety and elation over D\u2019s assault on one of the most powerful people in the Freehold. Joan stopped by a little before we officially opened the doors for the show to check on Andromeda, and pulled me aside for a private chat.<br /> <br /> After a brief kiss hello, she put a hand on my shoulder. \u201cI wanted to let you know that the penalty levied against de la Rocha was not as bad as it could have been. She is prohibited from participating in Court functions for one month.\u201d<br /> <br /> I sighed with relief. \u201cThat really was just a slap on the wrist, wasn\u2019t it?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> Joan nodded. \u201cEven so, de la Rocha almost declined to accept it. She demanded that Viscount Augustine apologize to you personally for his slight upon your character.\u201d<br /> <br /> That gave me pause. I mean, it\u2019s nice that D\u2019s concerned about my honor or whatever, but, well\u2026 it seems like maybe this is a little much. On the few occasions where I\u2019ve met Viscount Augustine, I thought we\u2019d gotten along pretty well. I admit that it stung when I heard what he\u2019d said about me, but I don\u2019t want to embarrass him or anything like that. He\u2019s supposed to stop by some time this weekend. I hope I can think of some way to make it less\u2026 awkward before then.<br /> <br /> In any case, D strutted into the Dream House shortly before the show, still looking like the cat that ate the\u2026 you know what, I\u2019m gonna drop that metaphor before it gets too weird. I ran up to her \u2013 probably making a complete fool of myself in front of our patrons in the process \u2013 threw my arms around her and covered her face in kisses. \u201cMy hero,\u201d I whispered when I came up for air.<br /> <br /> \u201cDamn, babe,\u201d she said with a smirk, \u201cI should punch Augustine more often!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t joke,\u201d I admonished gently. \u201cD, what you did for me today was incredibly sweet, and I am thrilled beyond measure to know that you\u2019re looking out for me like that, but it wasn\u2019t very politically savvy. You have to be careful now.\u201d<br /> <br /> She shrugged. \u201cIt\u2019ll blow over. We\u2019re the Summer Court, remember? We\u2019re all about anger. You think this is the first time someone\u2019s lost their temper with the monarch?\u201d<br /> <br /> I shuddered as I remembered the stories we\u2019ve heard about Lucien Torrez and his \u201cdisagreement\u201d with the previous Summer King, but I let it pass. \u201cI\u2019ve got to head backstage to make sure everything is set for the show,\u201d I told her. \u201cI\u2019ll find you in the audience after my number. And like I said\u2026 don\u2019t make any other plans. You\u2019re <u>mine</u> tonight.\u201d<br /> <br /> For once she didn\u2019t wince at the possessive tone, she just tipped me a wink, kissed me quickly, and whispered \u201cknock \u2018em dead tonight, babe.\u201d<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve been wanting to do a sort of soulful blues-rock number for a while now, and had looked into performing Bob Seger\u2019s \u201cTurn the Page,\u201d but my backup singers kept dissolving into giggles whenever I sang the line about \u201call the same old clich\u00e9s, is that a woman or a man.\u201d I guess that line is pretty silly when applied to someone with my physique. In checking out Mr. Seger\u2019s subsequent career, however, I came across a rollicking number called \u201cOld Time Rock and Roll.\u201d It was actually released a couple of weeks before I was Taken, but I\u2019d never heard it. Since it\u2019s about nostalgia and good old-fashioned rock music (both near and dear to my heart), I decided to give it a whirl. The crowd really seemed to enjoy it, though I\u2019m sure the very short skirt and fishnets helped.<br /> <br /> I changed into something (slightly) more sedate after my number and worked the crowd for a while. Halley was there, looking miserable but safe. I tried my best to comfort her. She still thinks that Monica and Dominika are making a colossal mistake by dating each other, and I think she really believes that (it\u2019s not just jealousy on her part). I sympathized with her, but repeated my opinion that sometimes people have to make their own mistakes.<br /> <br /> Molly Nuit was also there, and much to my surprise she looked like she was getting totally wasted. I don\u2019t know how many of those Black Widow drinks she had last night, but I know it was a<u>lot</u>. I gave Jacob a questioning glance, and he assured me that he had cut her off when it became apparent that she was overindulging. He\u2019d also called a cab for her to make sure she made it home safely. He explained to the motley the next morning that Molly had been feeling a bit lonely lately, and that her unique situation (having been completely remade by Master Darke less than a year ago) left her unprepared to relate to other people. We all agreed to do what we could to help her, of course.<br /> <br /> After working the crowd for a while (making sure to speak with Joan and Andromeda and Flores), I made my way to D\u2019s table. I climbed into her lap and put my head on her shoulder. Throwing Gloria an apologetic look, I said \u201cI hope you don\u2019t mind if I monopolize her tonight.\u201d<br /> <br /> Gloria chuckled. \u201cShe\u2019s <u>your</u> girlfriend, Lori. You don\u2019t have to justify anything to me.\u201d<br /> <br /> I flashed her one of my best smiles in gratitude, and then proceeded to attempt to burrow into the crook of D\u2019s neck, leaving lipstick stains on her porcelain skin. One of her hands wandered down to my thigh, and it wasn\u2019t long before she discovered that I had \u201cforgotten\u201d to put on underwear when I changed out of my stage clothes. Of course, we couldn\u2019t very well stay down in the audience with me in that condition, so I suggested we retire to the boudoir for the rest of the evening. D gave me an almost predatory grin, then stood up and carried me upstairs as though I was no heavier than a child.<br /> <br /> I gave her everything I had last night. It was all about her, and showing her how much I appreciate everything she does for me. We made love for hours, until neither of us could move or catch our breath\u2026 and then I used Spring Court contracts to revive us, and we did it again. We did every filthy, decadent, lustful act I could think of\u2026 but we always ended up cuddling in each other\u2019s arms, whispering our love to each other.<br /> <br /> Maria is the best thing that\u2019s ever happened to me. She is the object of every fantasy I have. She is the best friend I\u2019ve ever known. She is my beating heart, the center of my universe. I would hate to lose what I have with Oleander, or Marguerite, or Julia, or Joan and Andromeda. I love them all, and I\u2019d never say anything to diminish that. But if our situation ever changes\u2026 well, as long as Maria is there, I think I can be content with my life. I think I can be <u>happy</u>.<br /> <br /> Enough of the mushy stuff for now. The two of us staggered down to sex breakfast late this morning. Most of the rest of the motley was already there, along with Desiree, Gloria, and Flores. Flores took one look at the two of us in our somewhat rumpled state, gave us a knowing grin, and pepped us up with her own Spring contracts. As neither of us had actually slept, we both appreciated the thought.<br /> <br /> We obviously weren\u2019t the only ones who enjoyed ourselves last night. I\u2019m not sure what \u2013 if anything \u2013 happened between Marguerite and Desiree, but there was a fairly obvious level of sexual tension between them at breakfast. Flores noticed this, of course, and took Marguerite aside to discuss it, but I have no idea what they talked about or if they resolved anything.<br /> <br /> And speaking of Desiree, she and Gloria went out shopping together after breakfast! I know, I know\u2026 it\u2019s not exactly the Treaty of Versailles, but at least Gloria is trying to get past her feelings of betrayal. It\u2019ll take time, but I\u2019m confident that the two of them can repair the rift that\u2019s grown between them. Hell, they\u2019re even in the early stages of discussing the possibility of becoming roommates again once they\u2019re both ready to move out of the Dream House.<br /> <br /> That reminds me, I still need to watch that musical Desiree lent me. Maybe I can make time this afternoon.<br /> <br /> I noticed that one of Calamity\u2019s shards was broken at breakfast this morning. Assuming she had gotten into a fight, I started making a fuss about it, asking if she needed healing. She calmly told me that she had broken it off herself. When I asked her if it hurt, she sort of grimly replied \u201cyes.\u201d<br /> <br /> Turns out that she\u2019s making\u2026 something as an act of atonement. I\u2019m not sure of the details, but it seems obvious that she\u2019s trying to apologize to Marguerite. She\u2019s using her talent with glass to craft something special for her. Jacob offered to get her some broken glasses from the bar to work with, but she insisted that it would be more meaningful if she used her own glass. I\u2026 well, I admire her intentions, but I hope she\u2019ll get past the need to hurt herself in penance for the way she hurt Marguerite soon. I\u2019d really be more comfortable if <u>none</u> of us were getting hurt.<br /> <br /> So I suppose I need to talk about the elephant in the room now. I have a meeting with Reverend Wells tomorrow after church. I intend to tell him who I am, and <u>what</u> I am. Or at least, I hope I can do it. I\u2019ve never been brave, and the more I think about how he might take the revelation, the less certain I am that I should move forward.<br /> <br /> The others picked up on the fact that I was nervous and irritable at sex breakfast, and quickly got the whole situation out of me. I turned to D, desperate for her support. \u201cYou\u2019ll come with me, sweetie, right?\u201d I begged.<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cI won\u2019t let you face this disaster alone,\u201d she said firmly.<br /> <br /> \u201cDisaster?\u201d I asked, taken aback. \u201cYou think it\u2019s going to be a disaster?\u201d<br /> <br /> She sighed. \u201cI don\u2019t know how it could be anything else, babe,\u201d she admitted. \u201cYou\u2019re going to tell him that his daughter isn\u2019t really his daughter; she\u2019s been an imposter for the last three and a half decades. And his real daughter is a nineteen-year-old half-bird bisexual cabaret singer. I\u2026 just don\u2019t see how he can possibly take it well.\u201d<br /> <br /> I won\u2019t lie, it hurt. I\u2019d been hoping for some show of support, some comforting words to bolster my courage in the face of the very difficult task ahead of me. \u201cHe hasn\u2019t spoken with my fetch in <u>decades</u>,\u201d I said slowly, \u201cshe\u2019s not a part of his life.\u201d<br /> <br /> D shrugged doubtfully.<br /> <br /> I couldn\u2019t hold it in anymore after that. I was hurt and maybe even a little angry. \u201cD, you\u2019re the one who told me I have to do this,\u201d I reminded her.<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cAnd I still think I was right. You <u>do</u> have to do it. But I didn\u2019t say that you had to tell him right now.\u201d<br /> <br /> I turned away. \u201cMy father is almost eighty years old,\u201d I reminded her. \u201cI can\u2019t keep putting this off. It\u2019s never going to be a good time, and eventually it\u2019s going to be too late.\u201d<br /> <br /> She took my hand, but I didn\u2019t face her. \u201cI\u2019ll be there with you, Lori,\u201d she promised me, \u201cand I\u2019ll give you whatever help I can. But I just want you to prepare yourself for the possibility that things won\u2019t go like you hope.\u201d<br /> <br /> I know she didn\u2019t mean to hurt me with her doubts. I know she knows that she <u>did</u> hurt me, and she\u2019s beating herself up over it. I know she\u2019s trying to look out for me, and to be there for me when I need her. I\u2019ve tried to make sure she knows that I\u2019m not upset with her about this\u2026 I love her for it. I\u2019m just going to be tense and nervous until I see how it plays out.<br /> <br /> Hell, you know what? Screw it. I have to do this, and there\u2019s no sense making myself sick worrying about it in the meantime. Either he\u2019ll accept me or he won\u2019t, but me giving myself an ulcer won\u2019t affect his decision. And like I said before, as long as I have Maria, I can take anything else the world cares to throw at me. It might hurt like hell for a while\u2026 but I\u2019ll survive.<br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei Grace</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> Saturday, November 15th<br /> Nine years, seven months, seven days<br /> Days without stabbing: 1<br /> <br /> I'm stalling. The vessel and the dream are finished. I've got a couple of hours before I need to start getting busy for the show. It's time to go find her and give it to her and talk to her. Hell, making it was stalling in a way, but maybe.. hopefully... if I offer more than just words she'll at least listen to what I'm saying this time.<br /> <br /> No. It was too soon. She'd just told me she needed space for the love of dog. She wasn't ignoring what I said, she just wasn't ready to hear anything I had to say yet. Fuck I hope that's true. I don't want this thing to be cold stony dead.<br /> <br /> Truth is I'm scared. Scared that it's too late already. Scared that it doesn't matter how much she means to me. Scared that I'm right that our friendship over and gone. And if it is, it's my fault.<br /> <br /> But that means it's on me to make the first move. I made this mess and I need to try to fix it. I want my Darkling sister back. It's not just the closeness we had. She's been quieter... smaller. I did that to her. I harmed her and I have to try to make it right. But I don't know how to fix this. I don't know it I can. Hell, I don't know if it can be fixed. I don't know if she'll ever be the same... No, She'll never be the same. She trusted me. She won't make that mistake again.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter that I was trying to help. It doesn't matter that I didn't realize how much I was about to hurt her.<br /> <br /> I don't want to do this. I don't want to look into her eyes. I'm afraid of what I'm going to see there. And I'm even more afraid of what I'm not going to see there. It would be easier to just not look; to just keep at arm's length and move forward. The motley doesn't want to deal with more of last weekend. Maybe I should leave well enough alone. Maybe I should let sleeping cats lie.<br /> <br /> But I can't. I have to talk to her about this. Even if she can't or won't forgive me I need her to know I'm sorry and that I'm prepared to do whatever I can to help her. I have to look her in the eyes and tell her I fucked up and I was wrong. She needs to hear that from me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 06-20-2016, 02:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T23:41:00-07:00","id":917826,"title":"","content":"<b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Well, Luna headed out to avoid that craziness that is the weekend shows. I don\u2019t blame her. It\u2019s a lot of people to be around for three days and she is used to being alone most of the time. When I served the Lady I spent a lot of time on my own or just in Rook\u2019s company. I got used to the silence. I\u2019ll admit it was something of a novelty when I got here to be constantly surrounded by so many people all the time. I don\u2019t know if that novelty has worn off, but sometimes I think the quiet would be nice again. Not that I don\u2019t want to be around my motley mates. They are good for me. They keep me connected to the world and to other people. My therapist agreed that staying close to other people is a good thing and may help me feel more of a connection to them after some time. So, I don\u2019t feel quite so distant. Maybe I should socialize more with our staff too? The assistant bartender, Don, is an interesting guy. I think his daughter just had a birthday. Gotta remember to pass along my birthday wishes to her.<br /> <br /> With the intention of socializing more I hung around after Joan came by to drop off Andromeda. Apparently she has Summer Court business to deal with but still wanted Andromeda to be with friends. She\u2019s been having a somewhat down day and Joan wanted to make sure she\u2019d be alright. Joan also asked Calamity if the therapists at the Clinic could help \u201cfix\u201d what is wrong with her lady love since she used the Table. Lori and Calamity said that they weren\u2019t sure, but that it was worth a shot. I agreed with my motely mates.<br /> <br /> After Joan left Andromeda wanted to talk to Julia and Insincere Marguerite about wedding plans. Apparently she and Joan are engaged, but are not getting married just yet. They don\u2019t want to show up Julia and Insincere Marguerite\u2019s big day. Andromeda specifically wanted to talk about whether or not Joan should wear a dress or a tux. Joan is afraid of looking weak or soft if she wore a dress. I think everyone agreed that Joan would look strong no matter what she wore and that she should not let it influence her decision. I stayed quiet through this conversation. I agreed that Joan would look just as strong wearing a dress, but the girls seemed to have forgotten I was there and I didn\u2019t want to jar them out of the good mood they were in.<br /> <br /> Then the excitement came. Andromeda got a call from Joan saying that De La Rocha had just punched Augustine for saying something off color about Lorelei, and threatened him with a church pew. It seems that they got into a bit of an argument at the Summer Courts meeting. They were meeting about the diurnal Courts coming into the Freehold and specifically all of them seemingly coming to the Dream House. I don\u2019t know exactly what triggered Augustine\u2019s comment about Lori. I think it was something about us having so many visitors from other Courts and Lori having a variety of lovers to choose from. This upset our resident Latina and she decked the offending party, who just happened to be the Summer Court monarch. Yeah, so De La Rocha got into a bit of trouble. Not too much if I heard right, but enough that\u2019s more than a slap on the wrist. Though not by much, luckily for De La Rocha. Most of the details came after Lori talked to De La Rocha on the phone herself. She assured herself that her lady love was going to be okay and De La Rocha went back to work after the Summer Court meeting.<br /> <br /> Later, at the show, things got interesting again, but for completely different reasons. Molly came over to sit at the bar and asked for a drink, a Black Widow. She said that her job was to follow Leanne Sheets but she was told in no uncertain terms to go away by Queen Charlotte, who was planning on spending the night with the new arrival. So, Molly was here drinking and telling me that she really didn\u2019t want to have to break into Charlotte\u2019s house in order to fulfill her job for Boss Lowjack. She really didn\u2019t want to watch other people having sex. I can understand that. Well, I thought I understood until she started to go into details. She had a second drink and by that point wasn\u2019t going to be breaking into anyone\u2019s house. She said that she didn\u2019t like watching other people having sex because it made her feel inadequate. She explained that she is essentially a year old. She has no memories whatsoever before that point and had to be retaught all the basics like dressing herself when she started over. She\u2019s never kissed anyone, let alone had sex with them. At least, not that she remembers. She said that she feels disconnected from the rest of the freehold because of that lack of common experience with other people. She\u2019s really good at following people and being stealthy, but she doesn\u2019t socialize a lot with anyone so doesn\u2019t have any real practice at it.<br /> <br /> Molly also asked what I thought of Lowjack. I was mostly honest with her. I said that I trusted him more than I did Darke, though I was careful not to say anything too negative about the former Winter monarch. Molly said that he was good about engendering loyalty, but that he was more likely than Darke to kill someone. She cited the fact that he has a poisoned dagger in his desk drawer in his office. I wasn\u2019t sure how to take that. I was not too surprised I guess to hear that he\u2019d be willing to kill someone if the need should arise. I know Darke killed people. He even showed me the grim evidence of once such victim of his. So, I know that Darke is willing to kill people or have them killed. I don\u2019t know if Lowjack would be more willing to kill someone than Darke was, but I suppose if he did kill someone it would be one of Lucien\u2019s men. Those two are bumping heads almost as well as Darke and Lucien went at it. I\u2019ll need to make sure to keep an eye on that whole thing.<br /> <br /> So, I cut Molly off when she started getting too drunk. She continued with her tale of woe and wondered what kind of person she should be. She doesn\u2019t remember anything about her former life so she isn\u2019t sure what kind of person she should be now. I told her that she was given a second chance and that she had the opportunity to decide for herself who she wanted to be. She then asked me how I decided who I wanted to be. I will admit that I went a bit cold at that. I didn\u2019t know if she knew anything about my prior loyalties or if she was just asking a question. I admitted that I chose who I wanted to be by deciding what I did not want to be first and going from there. I did not lie. I just happened to know who I had been previously and decided that I was not going to be Rime anymore. I was going to be Jacob and I made a conscious effort to not do things as I first thought to do them. Instead I would pause, think about what I was about to do and decide if I was making decisions based on my life as Rime or not and make changes to my behavior as necessary. It became habit after a while to act differently and I became Jacob all the time. Lately though I have found that to some extent I need to do that pause before I decide on what I am going to do. Maybe I\u2019m closer to Rime that I thought I was?<br /> <br /> We continued talking and Molly also admitted that she felt disconnected from the others in the freehold because she has no memories of having had a durance. It is a common experience that all Changelings have, but she and Vik do not. They are blank slates in more ways than one. They have no nightmares or trauma of past abuses and they do not have much in the way of life experiences to help them deal with social and other situations as they come up. She admitted that she missed spending time with Vik for that reason. He understood exactly what she was feeling and could commiserate with him about it. I told her to look on the bright side. She has no nightmares that keep her awake at night from a bad durance, and she gets to decide who she is going to be. She can be anyone that she wants to be. I assured her that I was a friend and that all she had to do was call or come by if she needed my help or just needed a sympathetic ear. I wanted her to know that she\u2019s not alone, even if she does feel that way right now. I called a cab to take her home and she thanked me for the drinks and left.<br /> <br /> I will admit to myself that I felt bad for Molly tonight. I will never admit that to her face because I don't want her to think that I pity her. I don\u2019t. She has come a long way in a very short period of time but still has a ways to go before I think she will feel completely at ease in this Freehold. There are certain experiences that I\u2019m not going to help her with, she will need to find another for that, but I did assure her that I am her friend and will be there for her if she needs a friendly face or a sympathetic ear. Maybe we can invite Molly over for movie night. Or both Vik and Molly could come over for movies? I don\u2019t know Vik as well as I know Molly, not that I know her all that well. I will say that I got more of an insight into who she is tonight than I have in all the time since I\u2019ve lived here. She seems to be a good person. She\u2019s just not entirely sure who she is or how she fits in. She just has a unique set of growing pains to go through.<br /> <br /> Later in the evening Lori came by to talk to Hailey and see if she was okay. Earlier the girl was overly worried about Monica and her current dalliance with Dominka. She thinks that it is a mistake for the two of them to date. She thinks that it will just end in one or both of them getting hurt. Maybe that\u2019s true, but interfering now will just hurt them both and cause resentment. Lori also came by to check on Molly. This is the first time that either of us have seen Molly getting anything close to drunk and she was concerned. I assured my motley mate that Molly was okay, and that I had called a taxi for her to get home.<br /> <br /> After Molly was safely on her way home I called Lowjack. I figured that if he had tasked Molly with tailing Leanne and she was currently home sleeping off alcohol that he should know about it. So, I called him and tried to take some of the blame on myself for her getting drunk. I explained that she was feeling depressed and a bit disconnected from the other changelings in the freehold. He sounded genuinely concerned and said that he would put Dahlia on the task of watching Leanne and give Molly a couple of days off. I said that sounded like a good idea and that I would try and help her feel a little more connected to other people by having her over to the Dream House. I think he approved of that idea. At least no one got in trouble that I know of for this evening\u2019s events.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Today kind of picked up where yesterday left off. Several of us noticed that Calamity was missing a piece of glass from her shoulder. She admitted that she had cut it off so she could make a peace offering. She did not specify who the offering was for, but I got the impression that it was for Insincere Marguerite. I told her that if she needed glass that we had plenty at the bar that got broken, or could be broken for the right reason. She insisted that it be her glass because it would mean more. Shortly after that Insincere Marguerite walked Flores out to her car. Not sure if she just wanted to get away from the situation or if she genuinely just wanted to walk a friend outside. As that was going on Gloria said that she wanted to go shopping with Desiree for a good bit of the afternoon. Desiree for her part did not seem too put out by the suggestion. I think there was even mention of the pair of them finding an apartment together once they are okay with leaving the Dream House. Talk about progress.<br /> <br /> When breakfast was wrapping up Julia asked me if I was going to call Molly and see if she was okay. The prompted several questions about Molly. I explained to the motley that Molly had been feeling lonely and a little disconnected to the freehold and I wanted to try and make her feel more welcome. I suggested having her over to the Dream House to socialize more with folks, and they seemed to think it was a good idea. I will notice however that several people went off to do their own thing after this was suggested. I guess they thought that since it was my idea that I would take care of it all, but I had intended this to be an idea for a larger party than just me. I didn\u2019t want to give Molly the wrong impression if it was just me hanging out with her. Maybe someone else will stick around. I guess we\u2019ll find out.<br /> <br /> The other kind of big thing that came up this morning was that Lori was apparently getting herself ready to tell her father who and what she really is. I thought that this would take a lot of guts to do and applauded Lori for having the courage to do it. She was obviously worried about the fallout from doing this, and I\u2019ll admit that I was not the most supportive of friends at that exact moment. I said that that my parents will never know who or what I am. They have their \u201cson\u201d living at home and apparently never thought anything of the changes. They are content with the simulacrum they have. Marguerite also mentioned that her parents will never know her for who she really is. The conversation might have continued past that point but one look at Calamity\u2019s face and we were all pretty good about changing the topic of conversation. In general most people supported Lori\u2019s plan to tell her father. De La Rocha said that she\u2019d go along with her love and help her should she need it.<br /> <br /> So, I called Molly and made sure that she was okay. She said that Lowjack had called her that morning and had given her the next couple of days off to rest. She also apologized for \u201cblubbering\u201d to me at the bar last night. I assured her that it was fine and asked if she\u2019d like to come hang out at the Dream House before the show tonight. I\u2019m not sure what we\u2019ll do, but I\u2019m sure we\u2019ll figure it out. Maybe if some of the others stick around we can all watch a movie and make popcorn or something.<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> <b>The Cat and the Christmas Tree</b><br /> <br /> The closet door opened, and a pair of long pale arms, topped by hands with dexterous fingers removed a box. It was on the top shelf, and the arms had to reach way up, above the head of the woman they were connected to, she being petite and on her tippy-toes. But long extra joined fingers touched the sides of the box, and it was removed, brought down to its feline owner.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite DeLisle opened the box and peered inside. It was full of bright Christmas lights and ornaments. The Darkling had always loved Christmas. As an often frightened child, Christmas songs made her feel safe, and the light covered tree in the living room was left on, meaning the room did not have the usual darkness from the lack of overhead lighting. There was no need to scurry to a lamp to turn on to drive off the darkness and make the room safe. One lamp was on each side of the sofa, and only together was the room completely safe to cross after dark. Except those times when the tree lit the room. The girl\u2019s favorite times.<br /> <br /> The slip of a girl lifted a blue ornament. It reflected her face, but it was distorted, like a funhouse mirror. She smiled, and her mouth seemed huge, like the smile went on forever. While she had grown from a disfigured rich girl with no real friends to an awkward closeted queer rich teenager with no real friends, since her return she had a great deal of luck with women, and respect when people weren\u2019t trying to kill her. That\u2019s who she was when she met the Motley. That was the Insincere Marguerite that wooed Julia Oldacre. That even Lorelei the beautiful and Maria who does not need anyone had fallen for. That Insincere Marguerite could do, and would do, anything for her friends. That Insincere Marguerite\u2019s best friend, outside her lovers, was her Darkling sister Calamity.<br /> <br /> She lifted a red ornament and frowned, her face distorted into seemingly the most overwhelming frown possible, like a parody. That was the girl who was betrayed by her best friend. Calamity had damaged her sanity and stolen her confidence. And when she was upset about it she tried to keep her internal strife private, while her Motley and even friends from outside had to come and comfort her abuser for her being troubled that she had damaged her friend\u2019s psyche. Long after it was business as usual with Insincere Marguerite, at least on the outside, her abuser was still being smothered in love and support, her crocodile tears dabbed away. That\u2019s the way this world works, after all.<br /> <br /> Then one of the women she loved most in the world hurt her. It wasn\u2019t the same, her confidence was already shaken, but it was a kick to the ribs while she was down. Lorelei, however, had not defended what she did, but pled Insincere Marguerite to forgive her, said she was wrong. In the end, Lori was in her heart; a second rift like that might have destroyed her. She forgave her love. But the other wound festered.<br /> <br /> She put the balls back, and placed her hand on the top of the box. She missed the girl in the blue ball, confident and cocksure. This new girl in the red ball was needy and diffident, unsure if she was good enough for Julia and continually needing Lorelei to show her affection so she could be sure she still loved this lesser creature in Insincere Marguerite\u2019s skin. This girl was a phony, wrapped in a falsely confident exterior, like the girl who was taken. She closed her eyes.<br /> <br /> It was her first Christmas after being hit by that awful ball. Her nose was still sore though the stitches were gone, and her teeth had not come back in. She remembered standing under the tree and being afraid a ball would fall down and hit her in the face, like that ball over the roof. Afraid as she was, she was still lulled in by the beautiful blinking lights, and the music she had heard only this time of year for all her life. She just couldn\u2019t fear this tree. She reached up, hitting a gold ball like a swatting cat and it fell, bouncing off her little forehead. There. That wasn\u2019t so bad.<br /> <br /> She smiled, even if it made her more ugly. The music from the sound system was playing.<br /> <br /> <i>Vive le vent, vive le vent<br /> Vive le vent d'hiver<br /> Qui s'en va sifflant, soufflant<br /> Dans les grands sapins verts, oh !</i><br /> <br /> The Darkling took out the blue ball again. Putting it near her eye, her eye seemed freakishly huge in it. She remembered her first Christmas here, in the Dream House. Alone. Still, she pulled down the tree (she felt so lucky to find!), and set it on the stage. One by one, she had put the balls and icicles she had found on it, and the star on top. She carefully strung Christmas Lights around it. There was no power, not at the time, but the tree was not right without the lights. In the big empty room she shone a pair of flashlights she has stolen on it, the beam passed through the lights, giving them some small illusion of illumination. She danced around the tree. There was no music, but her voice rose.<br /> <br /> <i>Vive le vent, vive le vent<br /> Vive le vent d'hiver<br /> Qui s'en va sifflant, soufflant<br /> Dans les grands sapins verts, oh !</i><br /> <br /> She put the blue ball back and looked at the red. An exhale from her small nose fogged the not so small nose reflected. Things had gotten better since then. That Christmas morning there were, after all, no presents under the tree. This year perhaps there would be. Of course, the woman who had hurt her so badly would be there, and probably give her something, because that is how she worked. What Insincere Marguerite wanted more than anything was her confidence back. To have the past week have never happened. She could propose again, after all.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite returned the box to the top shelf of the closet, pushing it back a bit. After all, it was not Christmas time yet, though she could have used it\u2019s comforting embrace right now. After all, even as a newly ugly little girl Marguerite could not bring herself to hate Christmas.<br /> <br /> But there was a second box, and this one was empty, and just the right size. She looked around. Her women were on the roof, but Insincere Marguerite needed time to herself in this secret place. She had too much of it when the house was hers, now she did not have enough. She rarely slept in the vents anymore, Julia always needed her warmth, and the others were often there, even if Lorelei would leave them and not return. The Darkling hated that, though she never said anything about it. Maybe she should.<br /> <br /> Placing her feet on the sides of the doorway, Insincere Marguerite pulled herself up and into the closet, squirming in in such a way that would break a normal human\u2019s spine, if not perhaps a flexible cat\u2019s. She curled up into the box; it seemed to just hold her. So there was the cat thing, and she was not sure about it, but it grew stronger as she did. She wondered about it, just as she wondered what this more powerful form would have been like if the old, confident Insincere Marguerite she had been were in it. Not this creature who did her best to ape her old way of herself. A pale arm emerged from the closet and just reached the door with the help of the long fingers, which she pulled to a crack. She yawned. She would, most assuredly, worry about that later. However, she had to work tonight, and she needed this nap first. To forget that any of this happened.<br /> <br /> The door was closed to a crack, and the Darkling closed her eyes. And just like that, she was fast asleep.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session VIII</i><br /> <br /> Not much extra behind the scenes commentary to give.<br /> <br /> Gawain abruptly having to miss lead to the change bringing Insincere Marguerite on the car ride. We assumed he was working on the dream prison.<br /> <br /> Flores confronted Insincere Marguerite about dominating Desiree the night before. Desiree is her friend, so she felt a need to ensure Insincere Marguerite would not hurt her.<br /> <br /> There was a hilarious moment OOC when everyone was talking about their parents IC, then turns to Calamity\u2019s player and suddenly Insincere Marguerite was changing the subject. It was funny.<br /> <br /> I think that covers it, but comments and questions are always welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T12:03:55-07:00","id":919241,"title":"","content":"I was reminded of a discussion that was held before on this thread on what our main heroes would be if they were in Changeling: The Dreaming, rather than The Lost. It got me thinking on what they would be second edition of The Lost, and it lead to me compiling the list below. The Kiths are pretty much accurate to how they are now, given that in second edition a Kith represents the role the Changeling led (effectively replacing Seeming there), but Seemings would probably be a bit different.<br /> <br /> From what I remember, there was a discussion based on this topic before, but I wanted to throw my two cents to the thread before moving on to something more pertinent.<br /> <br /> Gawain would be a Fairest, given that he took charge and risked himself to help save the dreamer Gawain as well as Calamity. He could also be a Grimm, given the emphasis he has on having played the role of Gawain and the Grimm's role-based nature, but Grimms kinda confuse me so don't quote me on that. :-p<br /> <br /> Lorelei would be a Wizened; though she had help from her friends, it was her skill with her voice and her choice of songs that allowed her to convince her Gentry to allow her to leave.<br /> <br /> Ace would be an Elemental or a Beast; it's hard to say which because him biting his Keeper could be taken as him giving in to his snake-like nature (an Elemental) or defying the rules in order to help someone (Beast).<br /> <br /> Calamity would be a Beast; while she did betray others in Snowglobe (a Darkling's method), it was her lashing out and breaking the rules that allowed her to escape. Betrayal was all but bred into those within Snowglobe.<br /> <br /> Jacob would be a Darkling; it isn't a typical Darkling escape, but Rime's decision to not do as his Lady wished, and the general reaction Rook had, shows a clear betrayal. He could also be am Ogre, given all the abuse he had to endure before he escaped, but Ogres are usually those who plan their escapes from what I've read.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite would be a Fairest, ironically; she was released into the world, but she wanted to expand her potential, to become strong like Mama Lion and be the greatest thief, which is pretty much Fairest 101 in second edition.<br /> <br /> Ironically, De La Rocha would likely still be a Darkling given how she pretty much chased Twitch out of the Hedge, following how Darklings need a betrayal to escape.<br /> <br /> Julia would probably be a Wizened; it's hard to say since aside from her painting her way through the Hedge, and thus using her skills to their fullest, I don't think we've read much about her escape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T14:28:43-07:00","id":919316,"title":"","content":"Yea those limitations on seeming is one of the reasons I am slower to adopt that than other 2es<br /> <br /> Eta: Julia escaped because she could not choose what to paint. She was otherwise happy...which is why IM never tried to direct her on what to paint","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 06-22-2016, 05:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T15:34:49-07:00","id":919350,"title":"","content":"I find that 2e is more open than 1e is; any Kith can go with any Seeming, and your Seeming is how you escaped. No contract is limited to a particular Seeming, and any bonuses a particular Seeming gets from a Contract can be gained simply by paying another experience for it. 1e felt a little too...well, rigid in how Kiths and Seemings were paired up. True, Dual Kith allowed a lot of interesting combinations, but you were still stuck within a certain strata, and I found the use of Seemings to define what you were in Arcadia to be rather vague. It's not perfect, and I can see why someone wouldn't like it since it changes how one escaped to a particular method, but I like it. At the very least, things can be metaphorical in how you go about them.<br /> <br /> Thanks for elaborating on how Julia escaped. It's nice seeing a Changeling escaping for a reason aside from doom, gloom and beatings-from-a-broom, and to be given another angle on how Insincere Marguerite and Julia interact with each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T23:06:57-07:00","id":919529,"title":"","content":"I am fine to discuss the edition differences elsewhere, but I would prefer to move that out from here. We can PM if you like.<br /> <br /> I tried to have a variety of different stories for why people escaped. And I like sometimes what it says of them. Julia was not opposed to painting Gashlycrumb-esque tableaux that sealed the fate of the poor subject...it was not being able to choose, but having to paint the fate she saw. Flores simply got lonley, uprooted herself, and walked out of the garden to find someone to sniff her, then began to remember once she was moving around. Rowan was forced out and back when her husband saw her shapechange. Oleander...well...that needs to come up in game.<br /> <br /> And you really don't want to know Spidertoes'. Or maybe it's not so bad...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T13:52:03-07:00","id":920544,"title":"","content":"That's a good idea; there are better places for this kind of thing. Apologies for the late reply, it's been a bit of a tough few days.<br /> <br /> I admit, for a while I was under the impression Changelings were universally under horrible durances and that they were victims. In a sense, they are still victims, but the idea of having a more positive durance that one still had a legitimate reason to leave is interesting, especially if it still gives you nightmares of your time in it; heck, the idea of having nightmares of having betrayed those nice, peaceful people is an interesting switch. You're struck a good balance here.<br /> <br /> Another nice switch is that Molly Nuit and Nik don't suffer from nightmares thanks to their altered condition - their past well and truly has been removed from them if they don't suffer from something that fundamental to a Changeling's existence. It makes me wonder how many Changelings would willingly give up everything they knew, including their durance and what lives they had before it, simply to be rid of those memories, especially if the table didn't have the clarity destroying effects that it does.<br /> <br /> Also, another curiosity has hit me - aside from the garments that the crew got in the Dream House in the Hedge, and Gawain's own Hedgespun clothing efforts, what kind of tokens has the crew picked up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T14:00:09-07:00","id":920549,"title":"","content":"I am sorry you have had a tough few days, and I hope your situation improves.<br /> <br /> Thanks on the Durances. I really tried for variety. My players were good with it too. When I have an NPC, I tend to think first &quot;What story would create such a person&quot; and then possibly &quot;why did they leave&quot; depending on the story. I don't shy away from dark backstories...Joan's is only not unremittingly dark because she won every fight by those who would claim her, for example. Some seem pleasant, like Flores', and some seem fucked up if you think about it but was not to the changeling at the time, like De La Rocha's. <br /> <br /> I like provoking deep questions like that. Golden Eagle has been a lot recently, this game also has it's moments. <br /> <br /> Not many tokens, I have been kinda slack on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T02:19:47-07:00","id":925277,"title":"","content":"A lot of heartfelt conversations. How well they went, and how everyone felt, depends on who you ask\u2026<br /> <br /> Also: Random Disney Attack<br /> <br /> <i>Session LIX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> Nov 15, early morning<br /> <br /> So, Molly, right? We need to help her. Darke wanted a pair of tools to carry out his will, not real people, so she doesn\u2019t have any memories, or anything from more than a year back. A little like me, kinda, but at least I get, you know, glimpses of a past. She doesn\u2019t even remember Arcadia. I mean, that might feel like a blessing, but it\u2019s kinda, you know, a touchstone, I guess.<br /> <br /> So Jacob and I, we tried to come up with what we could do to help. Calamity and Lori stopped by to help some too. Calamity figured a kinda montage, like 80s movie style, would be best - you know, we\u2019d take her around to all sorts of places and see what it turned out that she likes to do. Lori approved, with some mixed metaphors, something about wide nets and seeing what\u2019d stick.<br /> <br /> I spent most of the show last night talking with Molly - and Jacob of course. The first thing we\u2019re gonna do is Disneyland. She got really excited about the idea. She\u2019d found a pamphlet once and was nervous at first cause it sounded like what people said about Arcadia. But she\u2019d read a lot about it since then, and was just, you know, super thrilled.<br /> <br /> We also talked about other things and hobbies and stuff and we learned she\u2019d never read <u>anything</u> but the Encyclopedia Britannica - they were the only books, the only, you know, anything in her house. So I decided to get everybody to loan her their favorites. I haven\u2019t decided what mine\u2019ll be. I\u2019m thinking Redwall though.<br /> <br /> There were other folks at the show of course. Most of the usuals, plus TJ. I didn\u2019t like the way he was looking at Rowan, or, you know, the way he was so pointed about turning over his arsenal, so I checked out his motivations. He had orders to intimidate Rowan and find out what she was up to, with explicit instructions not to hurt her. That made me feel a little better, though I still didn\u2019t like it.<br /> <br /> Anyways, he didn\u2019t try anything I could call him on, and we figured out Lori hadn\u2019t seen pretty much any Disney movies. Plus, she was super nervous, you know, about talking to her dad today so... Disney marathon. We watched The Princess and the Frog, Beauty and the Beast, Little Mermaid, Mulan and The Lion King. Julia even took a break from Insincere Marguerite and Desiree to watch Beauty in the Beast with us.<br /> <br /> Lori\u2019s off to her dad\u2019s church now, with De la Rocha. We volunteered to go with. She had trouble saying no, but even I could see it on her face. Hopefully it all goes OK - but now it\u2019s time for a nap.<br /> <br /> <br /> Nov 16, evening<br /> <br /> Lori\u2019s coming out went well! It went long, but I was just starting to get worried when De la Rocha let us know things were good. To be fair, I was still a little worried, but Calamity pointed out they wouldn\u2019t be sticking around unless things were going good. Well, not with De la Rocha saying it\u2019s ok at least. It did mean that Lori wasn\u2019t around to, you know, \u2018poof\u2019 Insincere Marguerite, or Julia, or Desiree, who had a long night. Desiree was all tapped out of Glamour, but she was able to \u2018poof\u2019 Insincere Marguerite and Julia, after they gave her some food.<br /> <br /> I made sure to save Lori and De la Rocha some, and they eventually got back. Lori told us a little about what had happened, and that her dad was gonna come by for sex breakfast on Tuesday! Of course, we probably shouldn\u2019t call it that, while he\u2019s here. Insincere Marguerite was a little hurt by that kinda idea - Lori didn\u2019t want to spring the whole, you know, poly thing on him right after the Changeling thing and the daughter thing and the bi thing. I think Insincere Marguerite\u2019ll be ok though. She came back after just a little bit anyway.<br /> <br /> I got to talk to everybody about adding Desiree to the motley. They were all for it, which is great! Things have been going better for her all around - I think she\u2019s really making a place for herself here and not thinking about the Director so much. Insincere Marguerite says so too. I know she was worried about repercussions for us, political stuff, but I was thinking, if we had a, you know, united front about how we didn\u2019t care about politics and all, if it wasn\u2019t just me saying it, then we could offer her a family.<br /> <br /> That\u2019ll be for later though. For now, we have a show. Lori\u2019s taking a nap, since she hasn\u2019t slept in like three days, but the rest of it all goes on. After the show, we have a few more Disney movies to watch. Aladdin, Pirates of the Caribbean and Frozen. Oh, that reminds me, we got a big stack of books for Molly: I did decide on Redwall, Insincere Marguerite recommended Fingersmith, Jacob Good Omens, Julia a book of Romantic poetry, Lori Eyes of the Dragon and Calamity... Cocklords of Mars. With all that, I also tossed my Halo: the Fall of the Reach on the stack, to get some more variety, you know? De la Rocha didn\u2019t have anything, you know, fiction/fun reading kinda books in English, and I don\u2019t think Molly can speak Spanish. I should maybe ask. Anyways, hopefully Molly\u2019ll find something she likes. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> I feel like singing!<br /> <br /> Okay, maybe in my case that isn\u2019t the best indication of my mood. I sing when I\u2019m happy, I sing when I\u2019m sad, I sing when I\u2019m angry\u2026 let\u2019s face it, I do a lot of singing. The moods just sort of come and go in the background. So let me make this a little clearer: I\u2019m so happy that I can\u2019t seem to stop crying.<br /> <br /> So the last time I wrote in this journal I was obsessing over my coming meeting with my father, just knowing that I was going to be a nervous wreck until it was over. I was trying to take my mind off of it up on the roof with Marguerite and Julia, but it was sort of a lazy setting while Julia was engrossed in her painting, and I couldn\u2019t keep my mind from wandering back to my cares. I decided that I needed something else to focus on, and went down to the living room with Desiree\u2019s DVD.<br /> <br /> <u>Into the Woods</u> is a fine musical in the best tradition of Sondheim classics like <u>West Side Story</u> and <u>Gypsy</u>. His talent for writing clever, intricate rhymes is more evident here than in any of his other works (at least, any that I\u2019ve seen\u2026 I\u2019ve heard good things about <u>Sweeney Todd</u>). The story is a mish-mash of a bunch of popular fairy tales tied together with an original story about a baker and his wife who are trying to undo a decades-old curse. The performances were <u>amazing</u>. Bernadette Peters, who was an up-and-coming actress in my day, steals the show as the witch, but the entire cast was top-notch.<br /> <br /> I confess I got a little teary-eyed near the end. Though the musical by-and-large is very comedic, the second act \u2013 which deals with the consequences of \u201chappily ever after\u201d \u2013 turns a bit dark, and even the story\u2019s narrator is drawn into the action and killed at one point. Infidelity, treachery, and recriminations abound\u2026 and one of the sub-plots dealt with a son becoming reacquainted with his estranged father, which of course struck a particularly poignant chord with me.<br /> <br /> So I imagine Desiree probably thought it was pretty strange that I had obviously been crying when I returned the DVD to her. Then again, maybe not\u2026 I found her reclining up in the catwalks with Marguerite as she went through some pre-show technical checks. Desiree was naked, but seemed relatively comfortable in that state. I\u2019m still not sure exactly what\u2019s going on between those two, but Desiree seems to be a willing participant, so I guess it\u2019s really none of my business.<br /> <br /> I joined the others in the kitchen, where Gawain immediately asked me if girls still liked ponies after they grew up. After a few of my trademarked confused blinks, I replied in a serious tone. \u201cI grew up in rural Iowa during the gas crisis. We had rodeos and riding contests at the county and state fairs. And I <u>never</u> liked horses of any size. Give me a tricked out Boss Mustang any day; that\u2019s the only pony for me.\u201d<br /> <br /> Gawain\u2019s shoulders kind of slumped, and he muttered something about \u201cback to square one.\u201d He eventually explained that he and Jacob had been trying to come up with some potential activities to share with Molly in their attempt to find out what sort of things she might like. I suggested casting that net as widely as possible, to see what sticks. This derailed the conversation entirely for a few minutes, as Gawain accused me of mixing metaphors, but I stand by my florid speech\u2026 there\u2019s nothing saying a net can\u2019t be sticky, is there? I mean, look at spider webs\u2026<br /> <br /> Gawain had also hit upon the idea of having each of us loan Molly a favorite book, since she apparently reads the encyclopedia if left to her own devices. It seemed like a good idea, though my own favorite authors (like Tolkien and Dumas) might seem a little archaic or heavy-handed to someone who\u2019s not familiar with their literary styles. Instead I offered up a paperback I bought at a used book store a few months back: <u>The Eyes of the Dragon</u> by Stephen King. I bought it because I recognized his name from decent horror novels like <u>Carrie</u> and <u>Salem\u2019s Lot</u>, but much to my surprise, this turned out to be a pretty good high fantasy tale about the somewhat strained relationship between two brothers. <br /> <br /> Anyway, eventually the group had the idea of taking Molly to Disneyland out in Anaheim. I confess to getting a little excited about this; aside from that one day trip to Adventureland in Des Moines, I\u2019ve never been to an amusement park before\u2026 and Disneyland is sort of the holy grail of that particular bucket list item. We\u2019re planning to head out there on Monday, and everybody started chattering at once about what they wanted to do first, and which attractions they were most excited about.<br /> <br /> Of course this only drew attention to the fact that I\u2019m still woefully behind on my pop culture references. We haven\u2019t taken the time to see many cartoons during movie nights, so when someone said that they wanted to get their picture taken with \u201cBelle,\u201d I had no idea what they were talking about, and said so. I should have realized that they meant the protagonist of the <u>Beauty and the Beast</u> film, of course, but I wasn\u2019t thinking about the translation from the French at that time.<br /> <br /> This gave Gawain an idea. After the show that night, he insisted that the rest of the motley catch me up on my Disney films. I protested weakly for a bit that I was too nervous about church the following morning to really enjoy the films, but Gawain got this serious look on his face and told me flat out that he wouldn\u2019t allow me to pace around in my room all night making myself sick with worry, and that he thought giving me something else to focus on might help me to relax for a bit. D backed him up on that, and in the end I think it was probably a good idea.<br /> <br /> Oh, and speaking of the show, I think it went pretty well (considering I was working on no sleep and a case of nerves the size of a Buick). I tried a new number, a ballad from the 80s called \u201cBroken Wings\u201d by a band called Mr. Mister. It\u2019s about attempting to repair a damaged relationship. When I sing it, of course, the lyrics take on a somewhat more literal meaning. \u201cTake these broken wings and learn to fly again\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I noticed that the selkie Day Courtier who calls herself Rowan was in the audience once more. We\u2019ve spoken briefly a few times, and I stopped by her table for a while to chat again that night. She seems like a nice enough girl, though she\u2019s obviously nervous about the tension she senses in the Freehold. She kept glancing across the audience to a table where TJ was sitting, and occasionally he would throw a glare in her direction. Before I left, I told her a little bit about why the Freehold currently seems to be so unfriendly toward her Court, and advised caution on her part. To soften my words, I assured her once more that the Dream House is a haven for <u>all</u> changelings, and that we would never let anything happen to her while she was under our protection. She took my hand briefly and sort of nervously thanked me for my words.<br /> <br /> Damn, she\u2019s cute, and she seems to be interested in getting to know me better. She also seems like a genuinely good person. She mentioned that another reason she was nervous was due to the presence of Salk and Marguerite, both of whom are prominent Night Court members. She said that she joined the Day Court because she genuinely wanted to help people and that she doesn\u2019t care at all about the rivalry with the Night Court\u2026 but she\u2019s not convinced that they feel the same way about her. Once again I did my best to assure her that she was safe with us, and I think I put her mind at ease, at least a little bit. If the interest I saw in her eyes is real, then maybe the two of us could get together some time, or at least strike up a platonic friendship. I think I\u2019d like that.<br /> <br /> After the crowds dispersed, we settled down in the TV room and got started on the Disney movies. We watched five films last night, and most of them were quite good. \u201cThe Princess and the Frog\u201d was probably the weakest of the entries we watched, but it was still exciting and funny enough to keep me interested. The villain \u2013 a voodoo conjure man named Dr. Facilier \u2013 was quite creepy, and ably voiced by a veteran voice actor named Keith David. Seems like he\u2019s a name to watch for.<br /> <br /> Our second feature was probably the best of the evening\u2026 maybe the best animated film I\u2019ve ever seen, if you come to that. Even Julia came down to watch the show with us, as she was an admitted fan of the film. \u201cBeauty and the Beast\u201d is apparently the only animated film which was ever nominated for the Best Picture Oscar, and it\u2019s richly deserved. The story was tight and engaging, the characters were likeable (or despicable, in the case of the villain), and the music was good enough that Disney eventually decided to adapt it into a stage musical. I\u2019m glad I\u2019ve seen it, and I\u2019m sure I\u2019ll see it again before too much time has passed.<br /> <br /> The third film was a loose adaptation of the Hans Christian Anderson story \u201cThe Little Mermaid.\u201d It was also quite good, and I understand that it\u2019s often credited with ushering in the \u2018second golden age\u2019 of Disney films in the early 90s. Again the music was top-notch; most of it had a Caribbean flair that set it apart from more traditional musical theater. The comic relief was side-splittingly funny, but it didn\u2019t detract at all from the love story \u2013 or the family drama \u2013 at the heart of the film. On any other night, I probably would have said it was the best film we saw that day. As it is, it came in third.<br /> <br /> Next up was \u201cMulan,\u201d a film based on a Chinese folk tale about a young woman who disguises herself as a man so that the government won\u2019t press her ailing father into military service. It was good, though not as top-notch as many of the other films we watched. The cross-dressing angle was explored repeatedly in a family-friendly way, which led to a lot of light-hearted moments. The story sort of gently explored the nature of gender roles, and though the moral of the story seemed to be something along the lines of \u201cdon\u2019t underestimate girls; they can do anything boys can do,\u201d I can\u2019t help but feel like some of the humor ended up reinforcing certain long-standing sexual stereotypes. Also, the creators of the film seemed a bit confused about who the barbarian invaders were. They kept calling them Huns, but they were portrayed as Mongols. The latter would have made a lot more sense from a historical standpoint\u2026 not that I claim to be an authority on that subject or anything.<br /> <br /> Our final film of the evening was \u201cThe Lion King,\u201d which I had never heard of before. Several people hastened to inform me that while Disney had originally advertised the film as their first which was not based upon a previously existing story, they had actually lifted most of the characters and large portions of the plot from a Japanese cartoon about an albino lion cub.<br /> <br /> That brought me up short, and I held up my hand for attention. \u201cWait,\u201d I said, \u201care you trying to tell me that this is a big budget movie version of \u2018Kimba the White Lion?\u2019\u201d<br /> <br /> For once it was everyone else who blinked at me. What can I say? They used to show that cartoon on TV all the time when I was a kid, and I loved it. I can still remember watching it on the sofa in our living room with Mom on Saturday mornings. She used to laugh\u2026<br /> <br /> Anyway, if any of the films we watched last night truly rivaled \u201cBeauty and the Beast,\u201d it was that one. The animation was <u>gorgeous</u>. The songs used traditional African instruments and rhythm patterns, and the story was an epic tale of a young man coming of age and finding his destiny. The comic relief characters were never too distracting (and those hyenas could be absolutely <u>chilling</u> in some scenes), and the villains were incredibly vile. Whether Disney owned up to its source material or no, I don\u2019t think anyone can argue against the fact that they produced something truly remarkable.<br /> <br /> So yes, five films intended to take my mind off my troubles. One about a girl who loses her father. One about a girl who has to rescue her father, and how he sacrifices everything in an attempt to save her from her prison in a fairy tale castle. One about a girl who acts out and rebels against her father. One about a girl who dresses as a man to save her father\u2019s life. And one about a lion who has to avenge his father\u2019s death. Whooooooole lotta fathers goin\u2019 on.<br /> <br /> So by the time the final credits rolled on that film, the sun was up and a fifty-pound lead weight had settled back into the pit of my belly. I sort of shakily asked D if she was ready to get dressed for church, and then hastily zapped us both with some Spring Court energy.<br /> <br /> The rest of the motley asked if I wanted them to come to the church with us, as a show of support. I thought about it for a moment, but in the end it didn\u2019t seem like a good idea. \u201cI want you all to know that I appreciate what you\u2019re offering to do,\u201d I said softly, \u201cbut I think I have to do this on my own.\u201d<br /> <br /> D and I showered and dressed, drove across town, and kissed chastely on the front steps. Then she headed into the sanctuary, I went to the choir loft, and the two of us settled in for the longest sermon of my life.<br /> <br /> No, I couldn\u2019t tell you what the sermon was about. I was too nervous; too busy thinking about the conversation to come. Honestly, when the choir sang today, I\u2019m surprised I could produce anything louder than a croak.<br /> <br /> So after the benediction I changed out of my robes and joined D in the sanctuary while dad said goodbye to his parishioners. When the last car had pulled out of the parking lot, he turned to us and motioned for us to join him in his study with a kindly smile.<br /> <br /> I sat in a comfortable chair while he settled into a similar chair across the mahogany expanse of his desk. D settled into a smaller chair behind me after giving my shoulders a squeeze of support. I looked around the office, taking in the various and sundry religious texts and sedate framed photographs. I think I was subconsciously trying to put off the conversation, but dad was having none of it.<br /> <br /> He cleared his throat gently. \u201cNow\u2026 what can I do for you today, my dear?\u201d he asked kindly.<br /> <br /> I sighed. \u201cReverend, I\u2026 I need to tell you a few things. This isn\u2019t going to be easy for me to say, and it\u2019s not going to be easy for you to hear, either. I\u2026\u201d I broke off after a moment. \u201cWow, this is hard,\u201d I muttered to myself. How do you even start to explain the circumstances of a changeling\u2019s existence to someone who\u2019s not in the know?<br /> <br /> He looked concerned. \u201cYou know that you can tell me anything, Lorelei,\u201d he said after a moment. \u201cI will not judge you, and will do what I can to help you.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cI know, Reverend Wells,\u201d I said, \u201cit\u2019s just that you\u2019re probably going to leave this room thinking that I\u2019m crazy. I know I would.\u201d I let that hang in the air for a moment, and then forged ahead. \u201cWhat are your feelings about the supernatural?\u201d I asked in a rush.<br /> <br /> That brought him up short. \u201cYou will have to be more specific,\u201d he replied carefully. It wasn\u2019t the answer I was expecting. I should probably ask him about what exactly he meant by that at some point.<br /> <br /> I thought about it for a moment. \u201cI want to know if you believe in things\u2026 phenomena which can\u2019t be explained by science, but aren\u2019t necessarily religious in nature.\u201d<br /> <br /> He smiled warmly. \u201cEverything is religious in nature,\u201d he opined, \u201cas everything is a part of God\u2019s ordered creation.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled back at that; nothing can stop dad when he gets invested in a religious debate. \u201cOkay, granted,\u201d I said, \u201cbut there are some things people tell stories about which aren\u2019t mundane, but aren\u2019t necessarily related to the scripture. Ghosts, vampires, and the like. Are you willing to accept that some of these things might be real?\u201d<br /> <br /> His brows knit together in thought. \u201cI am not prepared to discount any possibility,\u201d he admitted, \u201cthough I confess that I would need some evidence before lending credence to such tales.\u201d<br /> <br /> I sighed. \u201cIf I could show you <u>proof</u> of the existence of the supernatural, would you be willing to listen to my story?\u201d<br /> <br /> He nodded. \u201cI will listen to what you have to say regardless of proof, Lorelei. Have you encountered one of these creatures? A ghost or a vampire?\u201d<br /> <br /> I shook my head. \u201cAre you familiar with old European fairy stories, Reverend? About how the fairies would abduct people and take them off to their homeland, only to leave duplicates in their place?\u201d<br /> <br /> He nodded again, and then said something which sort of surprised me. \u201cThe changeling stories, yes,\u201d he said in acknowledgement. \u201cDo you fear that someone you know has been replaced in such a way?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes,\u201d I answered softly. \u201cMe.\u201d<br /> <br /> He had nothing to say to that.<br /> <br /> \u201cThey took me and two of my friends from the side of a road near my childhood home,\u201d I said, lowering my eyes so that he couldn\u2019t easily see my tears. \u201cThey replaced me with a duplicate so that nobody would look for me. They <u>changed</u> me in awful, fundamental ways. And then I escaped, and made my way back to the mortal world.\u201d I looked up, wiping the tears from my cheeks. \u201cWould you like to see what they did to me, Reverend?\u201d I asked plaintively.<br /> <br /> He nodded, obviously sensing that this was something I needed to do. I crafted a quick pledge; nothing too binding, just ensuring that he would hear me out and withhold judgment until I\u2019d had my say. Oh, and I tried to impress upon him how very important it is to keep the existence of changelings a secret, too. A few minutes later it was done, and he was sitting back in his chair with wide eyes.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s\u2026 remarkable,\u201d he said, his gaze staying on my wings. \u201cI\u2019ve never seen anything like it. It\u2019s almost angelic\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I shook my head. \u201cThere\u2019s nothing divine about me, Reverend,\u201d I said, \u201cI\u2019m just trying to be the best person I can, like everybody else.\u201d<br /> <br /> I gave him a few minutes to get used to the sight. I saw him darting quick glances at D as well, so I confirmed his suspicion that she had also escaped from Arcadia, though her alterations weren\u2019t as visibly extreme as my own. I told him that he would probably start to see others like us on the streets now that I\u2019d let him in on the secret, but that it would be safest if he paid them no mind.<br /> <br /> Once he\u2019d adjusted to the new world in which he found himself, he posed me the most difficult question of all. \u201cI\u2019m honored by the trust you\u2019ve shown in me, my dear,\u201d he said, \u201cbut may I ask why you have chosen to reveal yourself to me in this way?\u201d<br /> <br /> I sighed. \u201cBecause there\u2019s still one thing I haven\u2019t told you. Maybe the most important thing of all.\u201d<br /> <br /> He quirked an eyebrow. \u201cI\u2019m listening,\u201d he said gently.<br /> <br /> I looked down again, unable to do this face to face. \u201cI told you that I was Taken from the side of a highway near my home. What I didn\u2019t tell you was that when I found my way back, I learned that three and a half decades had passed while I was in Arcadia. I was Taken in 1978. To me, it seemed like\u2026 well, time is funny over there, so I\u2019m not really sure, but I would have sworn that it was no more than a year.\u201d<br /> <br /> He shifted uncomfortably in his seat, but didn\u2019t interrupt me. I pushed on.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhen I got back, I looked for my father. I had grown up in the Midwest, but I soon learned that he had moved to the West Coast, and I followed him out here\u2026\u201d And all of a sudden I couldn\u2019t say any more. The words just stuck in my throat. Luckily, I didn\u2019t have to.<br /> <br /> \u201cJuliette?\u201d he asked in a very small, quiet voice.<br /> <br /> I found my voice again, sort of. \u201cHi, Daddy,\u201d I whispered. I don\u2019t know why I used that particular term; I haven\u2019t called him that since before Mom died. But it felt right, maybe because I felt small and frightened and completely at his mercy in that moment.<br /> <br /> I looked up at him. He looked stricken, flabbergasted, completely at a loss for words. After about a minute, he rose and walked unsteadily toward the door. \u201cI\u2026 I need some water. Will the two of you please excuse me for a moment?\u201d<br /> <br /> He was gone for a few minutes which seemed to stretch into hours. D got up and put her hands on my shoulders, rubbing gently while I sat there and trembled. It was such a comfort to have her there when I was at my most vulnerable. I\u2019ll never be able to thank her enough for the strength her presence gave me. I could never have done what I did without her.<br /> <br /> Eventually we heard soft voices down the hallway. Dad was telling one of his assistants to cancel all of his appointments for the rest of the day. He walked in a few seconds later, looking much better.<br /> <br /> \u201cJuliette,\u201d he said softly as he walked up to me, \u201cI\u2026 I still don\u2019t have the right words to say to you. I don\u2019t know how I should go on from this point.\u201d<br /> <br /> D spoke up for the first time. \u201cYou don\u2019t know how important this is to her, sir,\u201d she said quietly. \u201cIt means everything to her.\u201d Her voice was level, but I could sense the anger brewing beneath the surface. She wanted things to turn out well for me so badly, and she was getting impatient. I took her hand in mine and squeezed it gently.<br /> <br /> I turned back to my father to address his statement. \u201cI know how you feel, Dad,\u201d I said softly, \u201cI feel the same way. Back in Defiance, we\u2026 well, I know you remember it as well as I do. But when I was in Arcadia, none of the stupid little arguments seemed to matter anymore. When I had to fight my way through the thorns to reach the world again\u2026 it was you I was coming back to. I guess I never realized how much you meant to me until I lost you.\u201d<br /> <br /> He smiled grimly. \u201cIt sounds as though we have both changed a great deal\u2026 and learned a great deal,\u201d he replied. \u201cI can\u2019t help but wonder which of us has suffered more in the lesson.\u201d<br /> <br /> He held his arms out, and I stood up, and then we were hugging, and I was crying, and <u>he</u> was crying, and I knew that he really believed me at last. \u201cOh, Juliette,\u201d he said after a moment, \u201cI thought I\u2019d lost you so many times, in so many ways. For God to bring you back to me now, when I had almost given up praying for it\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I tightened my grip on him. \u201cI won\u2019t leave you again, Dad,\u201d I said fervently. \u201cI\u2019m here for as long as you\u2019ll have me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHow long?\u201d he asked, which confused me for a moment, until he explained himself. \u201cWhen exactly were you\u2026 abducted? When was my Juliette replaced?\u201d<br /> <br /> I thought for a moment. \u201cI don\u2019t remember the exact date,\u201d I admitted, \u201cbut it was late May in 1978. A few weeks before I would have graduated from High School.\u201d<br /> <br /> He nodded as though I was confirming his suspicions, but declined to say anything more. Reading between the lines, I\u2019m guessing that those first few months with my fetch were difficult for him. Because of that, for the first time since I got back from Arcadia, I began to hate my fetch a little.<br /> <br /> We caught up for the rest of the afternoon. Dad had a lot of questions, and I was totally elated by the fact that I didn\u2019t have to lie to him about the answers. I told him that I\u2019d wanted to tell him who I was the first time I saw him, but that I had been afraid he wouldn\u2019t believe me. He asked about the Gentry, and whether I needed protection against them, but I assured him that we changelings have our own systems in place for that sort of thing, and that I didn\u2019t want to do anything that would bring him to their attention. He asked about Missy and Jane, and whether we needed to inform their families of their situation, but I advised against it. I told him that there are people working on freeing my friends even now (though I did <u>not</u> mention that I was one of those people), and that it would be pointless to bring these wild stories to their loved ones before their return.<br /> <br /> At some point, D told me that Viscount Augustine had texted her to ask if it was a good time to make his apology to me. She told him it wasn\u2019t, and he agreed to come by at a more convenient moment in the near future. She had also texted the rest of the motley earlier to let them know that things were going well, but that we would be staying at the church for the rest of the afternoon.<br /> <br /> The afternoon wore on, and I realized that we needed to head out if I was going to make it to the show. I invited dad to come by the house for lunch on Tuesday, and he agreed eagerly, saying that he would like to meet my friends. I gave him directions to the place, and he said he\u2019d stop by around noon.<br /> <br /> Then we said our goodbyes. It was\u2026 harder than you might expect. He sort of awkwardly took my hand in both of his as we rose to go. There was a shimmer in his eyes that I had never seen before today. \u201cJuliette,\u201d he said awkwardly, \u201cor Lorelei, if you prefer.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled. \u201cI should still be Lorelei Grace in public\u2026 but of course you can call me Juliette when it\u2019s just us, if you want to.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cJuliette, then,\u201d he said with a smile. \u201cI\u2019m so glad you chose to reveal this to me. I know it can\u2019t have been easy for you. I want you to know that I\u2019ve missed you\u2026 that I love you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI love you too, Daddy,\u201d I said, allowing myself to be drawn into another hug. \u201cJeez, even before I was Taken I couldn\u2019t remember the last time we actually said that to each other. Isn\u2019t that horrible?\u201d<br /> <br /> Dad nodded, but smiled. \u201cWe\u2019re saying it now. Maybe that\u2019s enough.\u201d<br /> <br /> We said our goodbyes, and D held my hand as we walked out to the parking lot together. I could barely see through my own tears. Realizing that I was in no shape to drive, I wordlessly rooted around in my purse and handed my keys to D. She looked at the Corvette logo on the key-fob and grinned like the devil. She\u2019s had her own key to the \u2018vette for months now, of course, but she\u2019s almost never used it, and doesn\u2019t carry it with her often. She knows how much I love that car.<br /> <br /> She was very careful in driving us back to the Dream House, but she opened it up a bit on the Pacific Coast Highway, just to see what it could do. We put the top down, and I stretched my wings out behind me like usual just to feel the air flowing over them, and I laughed with the sheer joy of it, even while I was still crying.<br /> <br /> The others were waiting for us when we got back to the house, and I told them all how well things had gone. I mentioned that dad would be dropping by for lunch on Tuesday, and Gawain \u2013 almost as excited as I was by the prospect \u2013 asked what kinds of food my dad liked. I rattled off a short list of what I remembered of his favorites from 1978. Dad was always a steak-and-potatoes sort of guy; I hope that still holds true.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately I also hurt Marguerite\u2019s feelings again. I mentioned that I didn\u2019t want to shock my dad too much when he stopped by, so I asked Marguerite and Julia to downplay our relationship while he\u2019s here. Marguerite looked really upset and left the room pretty much immediately. I don\u2019t want her to think that I\u2019m ashamed of our love\u2026 I just don\u2019t want to alienate my father right after I\u2019ve managed to connect with him for the first time in\u2026 well, ever.<br /> <br /> Marguerite rejoined us about twenty minutes later, and she seemed to have recovered from her momentary malaise. Just to make sure, I pulled her into my lap and started stroking her hair as lovingly as I could. She started to relax after a few minutes. I don\u2019t think she\u2019s really mad at me this time. I think she understands rationally why things have to be this way for now. But I know I hurt her again, and I feel like shit because of it, even in the midst of this giddy euphoria.<br /> <br /> Gawain also took a moment to talk with us about the possibility of adding Desiree to the motley. When the topic had come up before, we still weren\u2019t entirely sure where Desiree\u2019s loyalties lay, and she herself had told us that she didn\u2019t want the Last Dance to suffer the political fallout of having a known Loyalist as a member. Upon further discussion, we decided that we didn\u2019t give two shits what the rest of the Freehold thought about her inclusion. She\u2019s proven herself to be a good and loyal friend to us all, and if she wants to be one of us, then we all agreed that she should be offered the opportunity.<br /> <br /> Marguerite also said something about how Desiree was now loyal to <u>her</u> instead of the Director in the wake of their last few nights together. While I\u2019m still not comfortable with that aspect of Marguerite\u2019s sexuality, I chose to let it pass for the moment. The last thing I wanted was to get into an argument with her while she was already upset with me.<br /> <br /> We posed the question to Desiree shortly thereafter. Though she didn\u2019t give us a definite answer, I think she was both flattered and intrigued by the offer. She asked for a few days to think about it, which we all agreed was more than reasonable.<br /> <br /> I think it was around that point that I began to realize that I hadn\u2019t really slept for about three days. Spring Court contracts are all well and good, and I\u2019ve pulled multiple consecutive all-nighters before, but eventually the body needs real downtime or it\u2019ll start to break down. Since the tense spring that had been coiled in my gut had finally started to ease up in the wake of my conversation with my dad, I was really starting to feel that wear and tear.<br /> <br /> Calamity noticed and asked if I was okay. I sort of guiltily asked if she thought the show could manage without me that night, since I was pretty wiped out and could use a few hours of power napping. We went over the schedule and decided that the world would somehow be able to go on if I decided to forego dancing around in skimpy clothes for one evening, and I staggered up to my room, stripped, and collapsed on the bed. The last thing I remember before I passed out is D pulling a sheet up over me and whispering \u201cI\u2019m proud of you, Jules.\u201d<br /> <br /> The <u>next</u> thing I remember is an annoying buzzing sound coming from my nightstand. It was dark out; I glanced at the clock and saw that I had been out for about four hours. The show was nearly over. I picked up my phone (the source of the offending buzz; D had set it to vibrate before she left) and saw that I\u2019d received a text. D said that Rowan was asking about me, and asked if I was feeling up to speaking with our selkie guest. I quickly texted her with an affirmative, threw on some clothes, and headed downstairs to check on the crowd.<br /> <br /> I made it to the theater section just in time for Ace\u2019s closing monologue, and made a beeline for Rowan\u2019s table. She gave me a dazzling smile as I approached. \u201cI\u2019m glad you\u2019re okay,\u201d she said as I took a seat. \u201cI was\u2026 disappointed when I heard you wouldn\u2019t be performing tonight. I thought maybe you weren\u2019t feeling well.\u201d<br /> <br /> I returned her smile in kind. \u201cIt\u2019s so sweet of you to be concerned,\u201d I said, \u201cbut I\u2019m fine. Today has been\u2026 stressful, and I haven\u2019t gotten much sleep over the past few nights. I was just catching a little catnap.\u201d<br /> <br /> Her eyes widened in apparent distress. \u201cOh, I\u2019m so sorry\u2026 you didn\u2019t have to get up just for me\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I chuckled. \u201cIt\u2019s okay, Rowan, really,\u201d I assured her. \u201cI was going to get up in half an hour or so anyway. So what\u2019s on your mind?\u201d<br /> <br /> She looked away sort of shyly. \u201cNothing, really,\u201d she muttered. \u201cI just\u2026 don\u2019t have many friends in the area. I come here most nights because I know it\u2019s safe, and because the acts are good, and because\u2026 well, because if I <u>didn\u2019t</u> come here, I\u2019d probably just eat, soak, and sleep.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSoak?\u201d I asked, curious.<br /> <br /> She looked a little sheepish. \u201cYeah,\u201d she admitted. \u201cOne of the quirks of being a selkie, I guess. I\u2026 don\u2019t feel comfortable if I stay away from the water for too long. I get restless, and I can\u2019t really sleep at night if I haven\u2019t put on my sealskin and gone swimming\u2026 or at least had a nice long bath.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded sympathetically. \u201cI think I know what you mean,\u201d I said. \u201cI mean, it\u2019s not the same thing, since I can\u2019t really fly anymore\u2026 but sometimes I just have to head up to the roof and glide for a while, or at least put the top down on my car and feel the wind moving past my wings.\u201d<br /> <br /> We talked for a little longer, and she seemed to relax a bit. Turns out she used to be a choirgirl too. I asked if she still sings, wondering if she might be interested in performing at some point, but she looked so terrified by the notion that I dropped it pretty quickly. She said that she hadn\u2019t spent much time in her old church since she got back from Arcadia, and I thought I detected a hint of regret there. Maybe I should invite her to one of my dad\u2019s services\u2026 though I\u2019m not sure what denomination she is. <br /> <br /> \u201cWhen will I see you again?\u201d she asked a little breathlessly as we were saying our goodbyes.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m off tomorrow night,\u201d I told her, \u201cbut I\u2019ll be back on stage on Tuesday. Think you\u2019ll come by?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWouldn\u2019t miss it,\u201d she promised as she headed for the door.<br /> <br /> I caught a glimpse of something passing between D and Julia as I approached their table, but they clammed up pretty quick when I asked them about it. Sigh\u2026 it\u2019s probably just another stupid bet about how long it\u2019ll take me to get someone into bed (almost certainly Rowan this time). I mean, she\u2019s hot and all, and I think she\u2019s a really sweet, nice person, and she seems to be interested, so of course I\u2019m responding in kind. But is that all people see when they look at me? Are my actions just validating Viscount Augustine\u2019s opinion of me? I don\u2019t want to turn into a caricature\u2026 a parody of a sexually-active young woman. But on the other hand, what good is espousing the virtues of free love if I have to constantly second-guess my own motives and how my actions will look to other people?<br /> <br /> But enough of that. Our second evening of Disney films soon drove all such thoughts from my mind. This time we expanded the scope of our viewing, and watched one \u201ctraditional\u201d animated film, one computer animated film, and one live-action film. All were quite good in my opinion.<br /> <br /> First up was \u201cAladdin,\u201d based on the <u>1001 Arabian Nights</u>. It was quite good, though the genie of the lamp stole pretty much every scene in which he appeared with his zany anachronisms. He was voiced by the guy that played Mork the alien on that episode of \u201cHappy Days,\u201d who evidently went on to have quite a distinguished film career before passing away just a few months ago. All in all, the film was up there with the other \u201csecond golden age\u201d movies, though I think the overblown comedy might have cost the story a little gravitas.<br /> <br /> Next on the slate was \u201cFrozen,\u201d a film about which I\u2019ve heard quite a lot in the months since I escaped from Arcadia. A radical retelling of Andersen\u2019s <u>The Snow Queen</u>, it\u2019s fairly ground-breaking in several ways. The snow queen herself is presented not as a villain, but as a woman frightened of her own power and the harm it can do to those she cares about. Ironically, that fear is what causes her power to rage out of control. Her younger sister tries time and again to save her from herself, and in the end winds up getting hurt. She can only be saved by true love\u2026 and in a touching moment, that love comes not from any of the romantic leads, but from her sister.<br /> <br /> I was enchanted by the film. The music was once again top notch. I recognized the older sister\u2019s voice as the same actress who played Elphaba in <u>Wicked</u>, and of course she was marvelous. The younger sister\u2019s voice wasn\u2019t as well trained, but she did a phenomenal job with the natural talent she had, and worked well within her limitations. Even the comic relief characters were pretty well done (though I still wonder about the wisdom of giving the trolls their own song).<br /> <br /> The last film of the night was \u201cPirates of the Caribbean,\u201d which as strange as it might sound is actually a movie based on a pre-existing theme park attraction. It was primarily an adventure movie, though it had elements of romance, horror, and comedy running through it. The main character was one Jack Sparrow, who flounced and slurred his way into the audience\u2019s heart despite the fact that he\u2019s actually fairly despicable when the film is viewed objectively. It was a fine film, but I\u2019d file that one under \u201cfun romp\u201d rather than \u201ccinematic classic.\u201d<br /> <br /> They must have done something right, though\u2026 that film has three sequels!<br /> <br /> Me, D, Marguerite, and Julia decided to try to catch a few hours of sleep before it was time to pack up Gawain\u2019s van, so we piled into Marguerite\u2019s bed and sort of collapsed into each other. It was nice; there was no urgency, no stress, no bad feelings\u2026 no expectations of anything beyond love and closeness. I fell asleep\u2026 hell, it might have been <u>seconds</u> after my head hit the pillow, with Julia snuggled up against my breast, D pressed into my back, and Marguerite nuzzling her face into my hair\u2026 and I was content for the first time in what felt like weeks.<br /> <br /> I keep hurting Marguerite, and she loves me anyway. I don\u2019t mean to\u2026 I could <u>never</u> mean to hurt her, but that doesn\u2019t change the fact. I have to make it up to her somehow. I <u>have</u> to.<br /> <br /> When the alarm went off a few hours later, I gently disentangled myself from the others and practically leaped out of bed. I raced down the hall, grabbed a super-quick shower, and dressed before the others had really even registered that it was time to get up. I can\u2019t help it; it\u2019s Disneyland! I guess I\u2019m still a kid in a lot of ways.<br /> <br /> Maybe if I bat my eyes and pitch my voice really low and husky, D will win me a stuffed animal at one of the games. I bet she\u2019d be really good at the High Striker. She\u2019d like that; it would give her a chance to show off how strong she is in front of a crowd.<br /> <br /> My dad accepts me, four wonderful girls love me, and I\u2019m going to Disneyland today! Can you blame me for being a little giddy?<br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei Grace</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T02:20:27-07:00","id":925278,"title":"","content":"<b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> Saturday, November 15th <br /> Nine years, seven months, seven days<br /> Days without stabbing: 1<br /> <br /> I am supposed to be getting ready for the show but I'm just sitting here staring at my reflection. <br /> <br /> I spoke to her. It didn't go nearly as badly as I feared it might. She accepted the dream I made though she seemed upset that I'd hurt myself. When I offered to make more dreams she went so far as to try to forbid me before I explained that the vessel would be able to hold more of them. She doesn't want me dead or gone or even hurt. <br /> <br /> I guess that's something. But the whole conversation was awkward and stilted. She was clearly uncomfortable. I felt like she wanted me to stop talking and leave her alone but wasn't willing to say it. And I just couldn't seem to end the conversation. She kept asking me what I wanted and eventually I admitted I missed the way things were between us. She said she didn't know that we could ever be close like that again.<br /> <br /> We started to speak about what happened, but neither of us was really ready to and it didn't go far. <br /> <br /> She hasn't forgiven me and I don't know that she ever will. And the plain truth is that even if she does, she'll never trust me like she did. I don't like it, but the only thing I can do is live with it. <br /> <br /> <br /> Sunday, November 16th<br /> Nine years, seven months, six days<br /> Days without stabbing: 2<br /> <br /> Well, it's been an exciting twenty-four hours. Last night's show went quite well. Leanne was in the audience and afraid of the Grand Maw and being eaten by Charlotte. I am suspicious of how quickly things have developed there but Queen Charlotte can take care of herself and her personal life isn't my business. I told Leanne to wait after the show since Gawain had finished the dream prison and she was polite and didn't try anything with me. And yeah, I do sound disappointed even though I know it would be a terrible idea. <br /> <br /> Salk was there as well and mentioned that the Handmaidens had warned him to stay clear of Leanne. I told him she was a leechfinger and a predator like them. He also mentioned that they refuse to come back to the Dream House after that night with Desiree. Most likely for the best. Part of me is way to interested in finding out exactly what sort of wicked things they'd do to me if they got their claws in me. <br /> <br /> And speaking of Desiree, it seems we may be inviting her into the motley. I like her well enough, but it wouldn't really be my choice. Though I can't say I am against it either. She's certainly shown herself to be a friend but I just don't think of her as family. But Gawain really wants to and she's apparently part of Insincere Marguerite\u2019s harem now. I am not sure how I feel about that, but right now I am not going to get in the middle of it. <br /> <br /> Gawain and Jacob's attempts to help Molly find some idea of who she is when she's not working have taken a turn for the Disney. Seems she'd read a flier for the place at some point and wants to check it out. So we're going Monday and planning to make a day of it. And that brought up that Lori hadn't seen like any of the movies so we launched into the all night marathon last night after the show.<br /> <br /> One might question the wisdom of staying up all night watching Disney movies before going to confront her father and explain the truth of who she is and what happened but it's not like she was going to sleep anyway. We did offer to go with her for moral support but she declined. Just as well most likely. God and I aren't exactly on speaking terms these days and I haven't forced myself to sit through a church service since Snow Globe. I know that's a terrible comparison and I ought to see what a real service is like at some point but this wasn't the time for my religious issues. <br /> <br /> It was a little nerve-wracking waiting for word but after a while DLR texted to say they were going to be there a while which I was pretty sure was a good sign. I'll admit I was hovering about waiting for them to return but once they did between DLR and Julia and Insincere Marguerite I barely got a word in. But it went well. She told him and ensorceled him to show him and he apparently took it well. He's coming by for lunch Tuesday. Which means that sex breakfast will be much less sexy. And apparently Insincere Marguerite isn't okay with Lori not wanting to add being poly to the list of things she'd shocked her father with just yet. She left and cried after Lori asked her and Julia not to display their affections for her in front of him. I can see where both of them are coming from and I really hope this doesn't turn into a thing. Dog knows we're still not entirely okay after Insincere Marguerite and I's falling out. It doesn't help that I can't do anything to help.<br /> <br /> Presently, Lori's napping after going without proper sleep for the past few days. It's Sunday, so still a weekend show but the lightest of them and we've worked on having our last minute substitutions more ready so it shouldn't cause any trouble. The plan is to hit a few more of the Disney movies in after the show and then get a little sleep. For once, I am glad White Maria insists on doing the forms at dawn since I'll have time for my Tai Chi with her and our training. It should help focus and center me, which will be good before diving into a loud and crowded amusement park. But right now, it's showtime. <br /> <br /> <b><br /> Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> I\u2019ve pulled many all-nighters in my time but I have to say that todays was the silliest. But I\u2019ll get to that shortly. Leading up to the all-nighter was a regular day at the Dream House. We were all getting ready for the show. Julia, Lori and De La Rocha went up on the roof to smoke weed while Julia painted. After which Lori finally got to see the dvd of \u201cInto the Woods.\u201d I think she liked it. I assumed that she would. While all of that was going on Calamity went to have a chat with Insincere Marguerite. I don\u2019t know exactly what was said, but given Calamity\u2019s demeanor later it couldn\u2019t have been too bad. My guess is that she apologized for what happened the other day. I\u2019m not sure that explaining her rationale for her actions would have yielded the same response and Calamity would have been more upset if the conversation had gone badly. I hope that those two can begin to mend their relationship. They have always been so close. It is hard to see them so estranged. <br /> <br /> Right before the show I started getting the bar ready for the night and Gawain came over to talk. He wanted to discuss ideas for what to do with Molly to help her socialize more and find hobbies that she enjoys. We figured that maybe in the future we can invite her to come along when we do something as a motley, like bike riding, laser tag or roller skating. Though we did say that if we did laser tag with Molly we\u2019d have to specify that she\u2019s not allowed to go invisible. No powers during laser tag. Overall I think we had some good ideas and I looked forward to seeing what Molly thought of them later.<br /> <br /> Once the show started up we had several of our regulars show up, including TJ. He\u2019s not strictly speaking a regular, but he has been coming to the club more often lately. Gawain later read the man\u2019s intentions and found that he was there to follow and possibly intimidate Rowan and see what she\u2019s up to. When he first arrived at the club he came to the bar first thing to check a double barreled shotgun, as well as some kind of gauntlets with the words \u201csmile,\u201d and \u201cHave a nice day\u201d on them. I think he\u2019s got the intimidation down pat. He didn\u2019t really need all the weapons, but they certainly made an impression. I think that was the point. I feel a little bad for Rowan. She doesn\u2019t appear to be up to anything other than enjoying the show and the occasional talks with Lorelei. However, there are those in the Freehold that are wary of her because she is in one of the diurnal Courts. I don\u2019t think that they have much to worry about. Calamity read Rowan\u2019s fears tonight and the main thing that she is afraid of is Salk and Insincere Marguerite, basically the Night Court in general, and all of the Summer Courtiers.<br /> <br /> Calamity also read Leanne\u2019s fears again to see if anything had changed. Not much had. She is still afraid of the Grand Maw, is now afraid of Madame Spidertoes, as well as being eaten by Queen Charlotte. All valid fears. We should get one of the Spring Courtiers that we trust to read her desires sometime and see what that turns up. It\u2019s easy to be afraid of the Grand Maw, it\u2019s terrifying, but it\u2019s possible to be afraid of something and still have an ulterior motive. I\u2019m just curious to see what she really wants.<br /> <br /> Later at the bar Molly came over to talk to me and Gawain. She wanted to know what he thought of most of the people in the club. He mostly pointed out those that he knew were good people or those that he didn\u2019t know much about. He didn\u2019t specifically say that anyone was bad, though there was at least one person that he didn\u2019t say anything about at all. We also brought up the idea to Molly that she could come along when we next did something as a group. So, we asked her if there was anything that she really wanted to do. She said that she had never been to Disneyland and would really like to go. Gawain and I kind of latched onto that idea and brought it up to the other members of the motley as the evening went on. Lori was all for it, having never been to Disneyland. She\u2019s not the only one. I\u2019ve never been to Disneyland. I remember my parents talking about going but the time never seemed right or the money wasn\u2019t there. There was also the fact that it is a very popular place for tourists and it would be very crowded. We, as a family, had never really done the crowded vacation spot before. I think the busiest place that we went to was St. Petersburg and that didn\u2019t seem so bad because it was a big city. Disneyland is an amusement park with a lot of people crammed in together. Not that I\u2019m saying it doesn\u2019t sound like fun to me now. I have been to smaller places that had rollercoasters and remembered enjoying them, so I\u2019ll say that I\u2019m looking forward to doing that. I\u2019m pretty sure that I can talk some of the other adrenaline junkies in our group to go with me.<br /> <br /> This being a Disney park brought up the fact that there are all kinds of movie inspired rides and games there and that Lori, having been gone for so long, had never seen the movies that these rides and games are based on. Lori was also exceedingly nervous about her upcoming talk with her father. So, we decided on an impromptu movie night consisting of several Disney movies. We watched \u201cThe Princess and the Frog,\u201d \u201cBeauty and the Beast,\u201d \u201cMulan,\u201d \u201cThe Little Mermaid,\u201d and \u201cThe Lion King.\u201d Of all of those films Lori was only familiar with one of them because she knew the story that it was based on. De La Rocha was upset that Disney had stolen the \u201cLion King\u201d story from another source. Apparently \u201cThe Lion King,\u201d was based on an older story called \u201cKimba the White Lion.\u201d Everything else was new for her. She seemed to enjoy all of the movies, though a lot of them had to do with fathers in some way. The movies didn\u2019t seem to make her any more stressed than usual, so I\u2019ll call that plan a win.<br /> <br /> Most of the movies we watched I had seen before. Disney movies are popular in Russia too. So, this was the first time I\u2019d seen some of these movies in English, which was an interesting change. The voices seemed wrong to me, but I guess it\u2019s all a matter of perspective. I saw two of the movies after we\u2019d moved to the United States. Those were \u201cThe Princess and the Frog,\u201d and \u201cMulan.\u201d My sister really wanted to see them so we went together. I liked \u201cMulan\u201d better. There was big battles and creepy bad guys. Lori mumbled something about the Huns should have been Mongols. I think I remember those two groups from history class, but it\u2019s been a really long time. Anyway, I got to see a whole mess of Disney movies, some of which were made before I was born. But to me it felt like I hadn\u2019t seen them in something like twenty years. Time in Arcadia is just messed up.<br /> <br /> So, we stayed up until morning watching movies. I believe Lori and De La Rocha got a Spring Court \u201cpick me up\u201d before they left so they wouldn\u2019t be worn out and tired through the church service and the conversation afterwards. The lot of us offered to go to church with the two of them to show our support, but Lori was nervous and thought that our presence might make it worse for her. Plus, we wouldn\u2019t be able to be there for the conversation itself. That\u2019s where she really needed the support and for that she had De La Rocha. The rest of us weren\u2019t going to be much help so we agreed to stay at the Dream House. Lori said that she\u2019d call when it was over and let us know how it all went.<br /> <br /> Needless to say the conversation went better than Lorelei expected. De La Rocha called us to let us know that things went well and a bit of what happened during the conversation. When they got back Lori also filled us in. She opened with asking her father if he was familiar with the old Faerie tales and if he believed in them. She led into changeling stories and then showed him what she really looks like by enchanting him. She even led him a bit closer to the truth by telling him when and where she was Taken. He figured it out, and thankfully for Lori\u2019s sake, he didn\u2019t freak out. They both broke down crying, but other than that it was a pretty positive experience. It kind of made me wish that could reveal myself to my parents and be accepted back as part of the family. I have missed that closeness, especially with my sister. I see her every now and again, but she\u2019s so busy with classes that she doesn\u2019t come to the club very often. Not that I blame her, school has to come before entertainment. I didn\u2019t appreciate my parents looking out for me when I was a child, but looking back I realized just how much they did to make our childhood happy. My father sacrificed a lot when he was younger to provide for us in Russia and gave up his home so we could emigrate to the United States. I want to go back home and listen to stories that were passed down for generations, and I want to eat my mother\u2019s home cooked meals. We got teased as children for eating \u201cweird food,\u201d but to us it was just food. American food always seemed so greasy, or too sweet. Now I would love to go back to that \u201cweird food.\u201d I would love to go back to my old room and my books. I would love to go back home. But I came to realize a while ago that I can never have that. The imposter that wears my face still has a place in that house, which means that I never will. Dammit.<br /> <br /> On the plus side, as if things didn\u2019t go positively anyway, Lori announced that her father was going to come over for lunch on Tuesday. Gawain lit up like a light and started asking what kinds of things Lori\u2019s dad like to eat. I could see the gears turning in his head. He\u2019s already planning out a menu for two days from now. It will be good of course, everything that Gawain cooks is good. On the slightly negative side of things Lorelei asked Insincere Marguerite if they could keep the nature of their relationship under wraps while her dad is here. I think she didn\u2019t want to overwhelm him with his little girl being bi and a Changeling and being part of a poly relationship with several other women. I can see how that might be a bit much to take in all at once. Marguerite was not happy with the request but said that she would go along with it for the sake of her lover. She left the room for a little while before coming back a little red eyed, but composed.<br /> <br /> Later, after a short nap, Gawain asked to talk to the whole Motley. He brought up the idea of inviting new people into the Motley. In particular, he was interested in asking Desiree. He wanted to make sure that we were okay with the idea. I think pretty much everyone was good with the idea. Everyone agreed to it and I didn\u2019t really get the impression that anyone was agreeing just because the whole group was saying \u201cYes.\u201d Desiree has proved herself to be loyal and forthright so far, so I didn\u2019t really have a problem with her joining our little group officially. I mean, she\u2019s over here frequently enough as it is and sleeps here regularly she might as well be part of the Motley. Insincere Marguerite flat out said that Desiree doesn\u2019t belong to the Director anymore. Once that was settled Lori asked Gawain about how things were going with Chalcedony. He said that things with Juan Carlos were going well, but slowly. Apparently she is still resistant to the idea of being helped, so Juan Carlos has to take things very slowly so as to not do more harm than good inside her head. I hope that he will be able to help Chalcedony and get rid of any residual programing. She seems to be a nice person, but as things were we couldn\u2019t trust her. She was still actively spying for the Director. <br /> <br /> So after all that was discussed I called Luna to see if she\u2019d like to join us in going to Disneyland. She said \u201cyes,\u201d and asked when we were going. I told her how the whole idea came up and how we were trying to help Molly socialize more. Disneyland was actually her idea, we all just kind of latched onto it. Gawain also had the idea of lending Molly some of our favorite books, since it seems that the only thing she\u2019s read before was the Encyclopedia Britannica. That was a little depressing so I went upstairs to get one of my few books, one called Good Omens by Neil Gaiman and Terry Pratchett. I don\u2019t know if she\u2019ll get all the humor in it since her exposure to literature is so limited, but it\u2019s one of the few books that I actually own and I find it absolutely hilarious. I thought that Molly might appreciate the story too. I guess we\u2019ll see how it all goes. Everyone else went and got their favorite books too. Gawain had two to put in the pile, but I think that was to round out the genre\u2019s. One was Redwall and the other was a book based on Halo. Julia provided poetry. Calamity\u2019s contribution was smut. I\u2019m not sure if it was supposed to be a romance novel or what, but it had a really smutty title. Lori put in Eyes of the Dragon, which if I remember right is a book by Stephen King, but it\u2019s not horror. Insincere Marguerite put in a book called Fingersmith. I think it\u2019s a Victorian crime novel with lesbian characters. All in all, I think that we put together a goodly stack of books for Molly to read during her downtime.<br /> <br /> The show was pretty standard for a Sunday night. The only difference is that Lori didn\u2019t perform tonight. She\u2019s been up for something like three days straight so she went upstairs to get some sleep while the show went on. At some point she came down and talked to Rowan. Not sure what that was all about, but it seemed like she specifically came down to talk to the selkie. They flirted lightly back and forth, which is not surprising for Lori, she is a very flirty girl, but it was a little out of the norm for Rowan. Maybe she just had a crush on our feathered songstress. I wouldn\u2019t be surprised. A lot of people have a crush on Lorelei. <br /> <br /> After the show we decided to watch more Disney movies. This time we saw \u201cAladdin\u201d, \u201cPirates of the Caribbean,\u201d and \u201cFrozen.\u201d \u201cAladdin\u201d was fun, and \u201cPirates\u201d was hilarious. During \u201cFrozen\u201d though Lori kept looking at me and smirking. I think she thought the similarity in powers amused her. I think I remember seeing something online about how that movie was supposed to be a retelling of the story of the Snow Queen, though it had taken a serious departure from that original story. I thought the movie was fun, but nothing like the Snow Queen. The Snow Queen was really kind of scary and sad. The boy in the story loses himself to her and forgets all about his life and his home. It honestly reminds me a bit too much of my own time in Arcadia. I don\u2019t remember all that happens in the story. It was so long ago that I actually read it, but the Queen in that story was just too close to the Lady for comfort. It\u2019s entirely possible that the story of the Snow Queen is based on the Lady. People who escaped her could have told their tale to warn others about getting tricked into her realm or her service. Thankfully the movie was nothing like that and had several funny bits as well as a more serious story. <br /> <br /> Sometimes I wonder how many of the old stories are just made up to teach children a lesson, and how many of them are actually survival stories of Changelings who escaped Arcadia and were telling their tale. So many of the old stories are downright frightening and sometimes fantastical. I mean, some are common sense, like \u201cdon\u2019t go walking through the woods at night all alone or the wolves will eat you.\u201d That\u2019s common sense, but children as a species tend to think that they are invulnerable unless it\u2019s instilled in them from a young age that wolves will gobble you up if you go in the woods. Or if you go too close to that lake or river, or basically travel any place that has been labelled as \u201coff limits,\u201d for whatever reason. Other stories like the Rusalka speak of nymphs or spirits that lure people into their domain. What if the Gentry are the basis for some of these old stories? I suppose it makes sense, but I hadn\u2019t really thought of what story my the Lady might have been responsible for. <br /> <br /> But tomorrow is not about the Gentry. It is about Disney\u2019s rather happy and optimistic take on the old stories along with cute animal characters and animated snowmen. It\u2019s about pretty princesses and handsome princes and happy endings. Along with a whole lot of rides and games and junk food. I\u2019m going to focus on that aspect of things. I wonder if they have any throwing games? Maybe darts. They probably don\u2019t have knife throwing. It would be fun if they did. Dangerous for regular folks though I suppose. We\u2019ll see. It will be fun. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> Plans for Monday have taken a bizarre turn I could not have predicted. But not a bad one. Definitely. <br /> <br /> Saturday evening was interesting. I very rarely get visitors to my nest in the catwalks above stage aside from Julia, so I told Desiree to come up and lounge in the altogether while I worked. She did not mind complying, but then we had visitors. Three.<br /> <br /> First Calamity came up, which resulted in Desiree going downstairs. Calamity wanted to talk about us. She missed the deep friendship we had had before. She offered a gift, made from her own body, full of what should be a very excellent dream. Gifts are well and good, but they do not make up for actions. Still, It was a step in the right direction, and came with an admittance of being wrong, rather than an attempt to justify her actions. Rather than highlight her pain she asked about mine. It was very different than when she spoke of it before. Thankfully.<br /> <br /> At the same time, it was awkward. I feel a disquiet with her I cannot simply ignore. My instincts scream at I she is a threat, they want I to escape. I could not simply forgive and forget even if I wanted to. Still, it was a step in the right direction, even if neither of us were sure how to terminate the conversation. Unfortunately.<br /> <br /> I confess Desiree wanting to improve relations with Gloria may have affected my willingness to listen somewhat. I have been helping Desiree deal with wanting to renew her friendship with Gloria, and Gloria\u2019s own reticence. But while I understood, it could not change my feelings. Regretfully.<br /> <br /> When she left and Desiree returned, Lorelei came to visit. Lorelei has spent more time acquainting herself with Desiree\u2019s body, and was not there for a private conversation, so she lingered, undressed. Lorelei came to return her musical and talk about it. I confess I did not listen closely to everything but Lori seemed to enjoy it. She did say it was sad, which was not the impression I had, but I had not seen it. Eventually, Lori went to get ready.<br /> <br /> Lorelei was very nervous about seeing her father. I do not blame her; I would be too. I wish she had let me go, but I respected her decision to not. That decision made sense to me. That decision didn\u2019t hurt.<br /> <br /> Then Julia came up, but she had come to try out the new view with her painting, since Desiree was there to talk to while I was focused. She also took some sketches of the particulars of Desiree\u2019s bare curves. She said Gawain and Jacob were talking about girls liking ponies. Strange.<br /> <br /> That is where I first heard about Monday plans.<br /> <br /> The show itself was smooth, even with people coming and going. When it ended, I took Desiree to my boudoir. I had wanted to take her from The Director. I wish I was the Insincere Marguerite Calamity and Lorelei had shattered. But I was never going to rebuild her without pushing myself, and push myself I did, though not as much as I pushed Desiree\u2019s limits. <br /> <br /> We spent hours in our battle of will and stamina, but not long before daybreak, I saw the look in her eye change. I kissed her passionately. She had yielded, and in doing so finally freed herself. <br /> <br /> I will be honest; it was both of us. She was not tricked. She did not simply give herself like Julia, but she knew what I wanted, she was empathic enough to know what I would try, and she made no effort to protest. Maybe the old Insincere Marguerite could have simply seduced her over, but I had to make do with a cooperative effort. But she wanted to let go. She needed help.<br /> <br /> In the end, though, I think we both were better for it. Sleep, sadly, was not our ally. <br /> <br /> Julia, Desiree and I went down to sex breakfast, and met the Motley, sans Lori and Maria, there; Maria sent a text that all was well, but Lori needed more time talking to her father. Desiree gave us a boost, but at some point faceplaneted on the sofa. There was discussion of Disneyland, however. They had decided to take Molly there, on the basis she did not know what to do, but did have some familiarity with it. I had never been to Disneyland, though I had been to the Paris Disneylad back when it was Euro Disney when I was a girl several times. I did have a birthday there, I think, but memories are fuzzy. Julia, being from Anaheim, had been to Disneyland here several times much like I had in Paris. Regardless, Gawain was downright charmingly excited about helping the girl, and I think his better nature is showing through. Jacob seems pleased as well. He does not smile enough.<br /> <br /> I curled up for a head scratch from Julia till they did get home, at which point Lorelei was elated, and was quite pleased to say her father would be coming\u2026Tuesday. Unfortunately, she also told me she did not want me to acknowledge the love between us to him. Sadly.<br /> <br /> I\u2026I am not actually sure how I reacted. I think I agreed and left the room. I just remember crying and Julia holding I, making a hundred promises she would never hide our love that way. I don\u2019t know why something happens to kick I every time I try to get up, but I felt the confidence from talking to Calamity and bringing Desiree to heel slipping away. I know she did not do it to hurt I. I understand why she felt she had to do that. I am sure I am in the wrong. But it was painful. It was a sting I am still not over. I am trying, trying very hard, not to dwell on it. But it eats at the edges of my mind. Constantly.<br /> <br /> Part of I wonders if I sensed a little elation from Julia that Lorelei wanted to hide our love but she would not, as if this somehow won I over again. It could have been my imagination. I never left either of their sides. Faithfully.<br /> <br /> I eventually returned to the room, and Lori pulled me into her lap and stroked me lovingly. I tried, very hard, to simply settle in. It is still rough. But Lori\u2019s scent is so nice. I still love her so much. <br /> <br /> Anyway, the subject turned to Desiree, though, as Gawain once again recommended adding her to the Motley. Given our experiences the night before, I was more comfortable with it this time. I wonder if she said anything to him about having changed sides. Regardless, the Motley seemed in favor of the addition. I am privately unsure given her passion for Gloria how it will go. Still, she gets along with us well and is a natural for the Dream House.<br /> <br /> Gawain also caught me up on suggesting books for Molly. I suggested <u>Fingersmith</u> by Sarah Waters. I have a copy in English (of both that and <u>Tipping the Velvet</u>), it is a good story of Crime and Intrigue, which I think Molly could relate to and would have interest in (given her idiom), would hopefully help her learn a bit of the 19th Century, it is a lesbian love story, and a good one. But that is just one element of it as a fiction of crime and betrayal. If she enjoys <u>Fingersmith</u> I will loan her <u>Tipping the Velvet</u>.<br /> <br /> I rather like that English word, Fingersmith. Why I picked the novel up to begin with. It describes I on more than one level.<br /> <br /> Finally, Lorelei may have been speaking too much with Rowan, the Selkie. I have no issue with her having Day Court friends, I am friends with Felicity (though because of our taking opposite sides on the Monarch issue things are\u2026very strained with us right now) but she is giving Lori and altogether too rosy idea of what the monsters of the Day Court are like. They feast on shame. Does she not think Rowan does not sup on the shame of women whose bodies do not conform to the beauty of our performers? That she does not feel pride and a belief in the moral superiority of her Court? I suspect her pretty face and big innocent eyes are poisoning Lori against our Court to a degree. It is just a question of if it is deliberate.<br /> <br /> Eventually Lori went to lay down, and I went to work. Desiree rested this time. The show was smooth once again. It was a touch lonely, just the puppets and I, going about my work as I usually do, given the two beautiful women that were with me the night before. Still, I got by. The time alone can be nice. Of course, when I came out I saw Lori had gotten up and was saying goodbye to Rowan. Maybe I do need to talk to Rowan.<br /> <br /> The rest of the evening was spent watching Disney films. Lori made sure to be nice to me. Disney is not my thing, but nonetheless everyone enjoyed it, and Maria was surprisingly passionate about them. Her passions might make for an interesting trip. We asked Desiree about joining us. She had to think. I suspect the inner conflict with Gloria lead to her hesitation.<br /> <br /> Afterwards, Lori, Julia, Maria and I retired to cuddle and sleep a bit. I placed my scent on the girls once again. There wasn\u2019t sex, but that was okay. To hear them breathe, smell their scents, feel their warmth and heartbeats, mingle our limbs\u2026it was a grand tangle we made, and a reminder of the night well spent. Lori\u2019s sent has changed\u2026her hair smells more like her wings, though the texture is unchanged as I run my fingers through it. Julia has a slight after scent of paint and old paper, or perhaps a very old house. Maria has a slight tang of blood, and the sound of a heartbeat\u2026that after a few moments I realized was my own. So intriguing. I wonder if I smell different? I do not to me.<br /> <br /> Now when Luna and Molly get here we go, I believe. I am all packed! I will have so much money when we get back\u2026<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LIX</i><br /> <br /> What does Reverend Wells know about the supernatural, anyway?<br /> <br /> The Disney thing was an off the cuff answer. Boy did the PCs latch onto it. As a note, there was some creative retelling involved on the Kimba thing. De La Rocha had a rant about that in the evening before the show, and Lori recognized that from DLR\u2019s description. So with the timing on that and who noticed, there was some notable variation from what happened. <br /> <br /> A note\u2026<u>Cocklords of Mars</u>, a \u201cGay Martian Sci Fi Epic\u201d is a bad pulp novel that keeps showing up in my games. It has appeared in all but <i>Golden Eagle</i>, but originated in <i>Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</i>. It was fun having everyone think of books that fit their characters to loan to Molly.<br /> <br /> So now they are doing Disneyland first thing next session. That\u2026changed a thing or two in my plans. We shall see how it goes. Join us next time! Comments and Questions welcome!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T15:04:16-07:00","id":927293,"title":"","content":"It's a small touch, but I really enjoy Lorelei's journals mentioning Ace in various ways, if offhandedly, giving the impression that he's still active in the backdrop.<br /> <br /> Changelings at Disneyland. That sounds like an entire adventure in and of itself. In the World of Darkness, who knows what's lurking within the rides, under the streets...heck, even within the costumes. Changelings could have/make all sorts of havoc in that kind of setting.<br /> <br /> ...and now I want to make Herbie into a proper creature within the WoD. :-p Dangit, why do Volkswagen Beetles make such fun cars to bring to life?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 07-06-2016, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T15:05:54-07:00","id":927294,"title":"","content":"Watch out for Captain Jack Sparrow as you wander around Disneyland. If your rings confuse him he will try to acquire them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T17:22:56-07:00","id":927365,"title":"","content":"Heh they did not really try to go exploring. Stuck with the touristy areas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T05:47:43-07:00","id":927572,"title":"","content":"Taidragon: We live in hope that Ace's player will be able to rejoin us at some point, so I try to keep him around as a background presence when I feel that I can do so without compromising the integrity or flow of Lori's journals.<br /> <br /> All: Disneyland was fun, and I look forward to seeing what people think of the various accounts (and to reading those accounts myself, as I'm always curious to see different player/characters' perspectives on events. As a sneak preview, we also got to cover Lori's dad meeting the rest of the motley... but I'll leave the outcome of that meeting a mystery for now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T11:25:02-07:00","id":927701,"title":"","content":"PenitentTom: That's an awesome thing to do. :-)<br /> <br /> You mean her father doesn't meet The Lord Sebastian Vercingetorix Bearrington McGrowlypants III, Esquire and realize that nobody but saints could possibly have brought up such a distinguished and thoughtful bear? Darn, that messes up all my predictions about where this story goes. *takes out a flow chart and crosses out 'Big Dramatic Reunion Musical', 'Ace was secretly a Demon' and 'Everyone in the motley are cousins twice removed'*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 07-07-2016, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T17:30:36-07:00","id":927861,"title":"","content":"It just now occurs to me, but what was the glamour like at Disneyland? In volume, type, and quality?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T03:11:48-07:00","id":928665,"title":"","content":"I let them roll once per hour and assumed all five PC represented Courts could get the bonus. Once/hour is what they get in the Dream House, usually. Just Desire bonus in house, though some songs offer others. <br /> <br /> They did spend a lot despite lack of threats. Competitiveness and hijinx lead to a surprising amount of Glamour being spent, actually. It was a bad day to be a strength test machine.<br /> <br /> I have Gawain's journal and a story for Insincere Marguerite (with hopefully correct French) in hand. Should have something for everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T13:53:18-07:00","id":933036,"title":"","content":"And they go to Disneyland. And, perhaps, misbehaved.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> November 17th, morning<br /> <br /> I talked to an Incubus! I mean, I ducked out in the middle of sex with both a succubus and my girlfriend to do it, which is, you know, probably not my best trade ever, but it was important, to protect Leanne. The show last night went fine. I think. I was kinda distracted. Becky is really, really hot.<br /> <br /> Anyways, the dream my prison caught was in a castle, a bedchamber kinda place. The Incubus was there, who looked like Leanne but more, you know, vampirey. She - well, I dunno if she was a she, but she looked like a she and all. At least then. Not, you know, when she was a fish. I mean, maybe she was a fish then too. I dunno how to tell girl fishes from boy fishes. But anyway she was scared of me and really didn\u2019t wanna fight after I showed right up.<br /> <br /> She was scared enough to offer to make a pledge with me, to show up next time I sleep and tell me what she knows about Hollywood. She\u2019s a, you know, information broker kinda thing and they contracted her to figure out what Leanne was up to. She has more to tell us, tonight, and I\u2019ll have Calamity around to help me think of good questions, so that could be awesome. But before that, Disneyland!<br /> <br /> November 17th, evening<br /> <br /> That. Was. Awesome! Everything I could have hoped for. The rides and the games and the food and the fun and just, you know, everything. I think everyone, even Molly, had fun too. Lori had a bit of a downer moment, when she figured out her frailty was she had to sing when asked. I\u2019m not sure she\u2019ll ever forgive Goofy.<br /> <br /> There was a lot of competitive type things, but I guess that is kinda how we do. I did learn that I am not good at shooting glow in the dark geometric shapes with lasers. Calamity helped keep me from being too embarrassed by my score when she stole my gun and two-gunned it, cause she\u2019s awesome. I am pretty good at hitting things very hard though. Me and De la Roche both broke the high striker machine. I got Calamity a bit stuffed Iago and De la Roche got Lori a stuffed Olaf. Gloria got herself a stuffed Lady, from, you know, Lady and the Tramp. It was pretty cute. She and Desiree got along well, which was awesome. They were chatting and reminiscing and everything. Insincere Marguerite got Julia a Mrs Potts there and then at the ball throwing game, got her a Lumiere. Jacob got a Robin Hood for Luna. She had a crush on him, you know, when she was little. Calamity got me a thing too, a kid\u2019s version of Prince Phillip\u2019s sword and shield, you know, from Sleeping Beauty. I bought one of the plastic knight hats to go with it, so I looked boss.<br /> <br /> I think the castle was my favorite. I hadn\u2019t realized it was a recreation of Neuschwanstein Castle, but it was fun explaining all the quirks about the, you know, history and architecture and everything. Pirates of the Caribbean was fun too. I think that might\u2019ve been Insincere Marguerite\u2019s favorite. Molly didn\u2019t really latch onto anything - well, she did like the Astro Blasters, but she was really super good at it. We did figure out she doesn\u2019t like getting wet though.<br /> <br /> We went to a Beauty and the Beast themed restaurant. Insincere Marguerite tolerated the faux French, for Julia\u2019s sake. And it was kinda adorable. We stayed for the fireworks show too, before we headed back for some movies. The ride back was mostly Calamity giving Molly advice on relationships, since it had kinda flippantly stated that the right person would give good orgasms, and she, you know, didn\u2019t want to give the wrong impression.<br /> <br /> We would up watching Amelie and Princess Bride. Insincere Marguerite was pretty insistent on Amelie, since it\u2019s about a quiet girl figuring out how to deal with people. And Calamity wanted Princess Bride cause... I dunno. Cause it\u2019s fun? It was one of her favorites anyway. I think Molly had fun. And that\u2019s good.<br /> <br /> Now it\u2019s time to talk to an incubus again.<br /> <br /> November 18th, morning<br /> <br /> It turns out the Incubus is named Izikan and likes looking like vampire Leanne. At least that's what she looked like again last night. She was really helpful. It might be kinda cool to have, you know, a network of dream info broker contacts. Then I could know and figure out all sorts of things.<br /> <br /> For now she mostly told us about Hollywood\u2019s worries. According to her, their interests in us were defensive. They wanted to observe how the Diurnal Courts were \u2018taking over\u2019 and also were worried about our powerful guys, like Madame Spidertoes and Tommy. The only thing she knew about the Grandmaw was that lots of folks were having nightmares about it. And she didn\u2019t know anything about the programming, which was a bummer.<br /> <br /> Calamity asked more about Leanne too. Izikan was sent after her cause she was super important over there and knows things they were afraid for us to get our hands on. It does seem to mean she\u2019s more trustworthy. I mean, they wouldn\u2019t, you know, send someone to check whether their spy was saying too much. Right? She also talked about how Leanna was keeping elements of herself too tightly reined in and not allowing her nature to be free. That sounds like it could be dangerous but not, like, being fed to a Gentry levels of dangerous, you know?<br /> <br /> November 18th, afternoon<br /> <br /> I think that went well. Nothing and nobody exploded and Lori\u2019s dad seems pretty cool. Lori says she thinks it went well too, so that\u2019s what\u2019s important.<br /> <br /> Before Lori\u2019s dad showed up, De la Roche told us her first name is Maria. Calamity figured out way quicker than me that she was maybe, you know, the Maria that Twitch is terrified of. She didn\u2019t say, but it was obvious she is. So Calamity\u2019ll be canceling that anonymous order of The West Side Story she was gonna send him. Or was it The Sound of Music?<br /> <br /> Anyway, De la Roche was all harsh on herself about how she forced Twitch into doing, you know, the jerk things he\u2019s done. Which really isn\u2019t fair. He made his choices, you know? That\u2019s on him, even if he was scared. It\u2019s... well, it\u2019s complicated, but it\u2019s not on her. Especially it\u2019s not on who she is now.<br /> <br /> But, happier things - Lori\u2019s dad likes us! And Lori called us all family! He\u2019s big on helping people, protecting them particularly. He was worried about fetches, and whether the Church could do anything, you know, that kinda stuff. He was worried about how we gathered Glamor too, but I told him it was like trees and carbon dioxide, so that was OK.<br /> <br /> We gave him a tour after non-sex breakfast, showing him the House and the Hedgespun stuff and everything. Even the stuff I made, like my sleepy sculpture and stuff, so we got to talking about dreams. He seemed really interested. I apparently did good even though there wasn\u2019t, you know, something I didn\u2019t do - De la Roche didn\u2019t say fuck, Calamity didn't stab anyone and Insincere Marguerite didn\u2019t lick anyone. But it went well.<br /> <br /> And now Lori and De la Roche are going for ice cream, Insincere Marguerite and Julia are chilling, Jacob is practicing ice sculpting and Calamity is working with Annika. Which, of course, means it\u2019s time for me to wipe down tables and sweep the floor.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> When you wish upon a star\u2026<br /> <br /> The last two days have been\u2026 well, it would be clich\u00e9d to say \u201cmagical,\u201d but that\u2019s honestly how I feel. Things are going very well for me right now, and I do not intend to look this particular gift horse in the mouth. With only a single minor moment of existential terror to interrupt my winning streak, I feel like things are finally going my way again.<br /> <br /> So I was sitting in the kitchen waiting for everybody else to get up so that we could get on the road yesterday morning, bouncing up and down on the balls of my feet and basically acting like a kid on Christmas morning. The others were probably pretty amused by how excited I got, but what can I say? Maybe having a dad again is making me want to regain my squandered childhood. D \u2013 God bless her \u2013 seemed to find it cute and charming.<br /> <br /> But business has to come first, of course. Gawain told the lot of us that he had made contact with the incubus which had been dogging Leanne. It seemed to be a reasonable being, describing itself as an information broker. It had been gathering information on Leanne\u2019s activities for the Hollywood Courts, but mostly because it saw a chance for gain rather than out of any political ideals or loyalty. In exchange for its freedom and safety, it offered to give some of its information to us instead of Hollywood. Gawain crafted a simple pledge to bind it to its word, and made plans to meet with it in his own dreams the following night. Calamity is going to go into the dream with him. I had to applaud my motley for going with negotiation first instead of resorting to violence!<br /> <br /> So in any case, by the time we had exhausted the possibilities of this subject, Molly had arrived and we were ready to hit the road. As there were eleven of us, we couldn\u2019t all fit in Gawain\u2019s van, so we took Jacob\u2019s jeep, too. I volunteered to ride in the jeep so that I could feel the wind on my wings, and of course D opted to ride with me. Luna rounded out our group, naturally.<br /> <br /> I put on a suitably pretty ensemble that made me look sexy but wouldn\u2019t get us thrown out of the park. It wasn\u2019t anything fancy, just a dark top with spaghetti straps and a mid-thigh length skirt. D was decked out in her leathers, of course. Marguerite put on a t-shirt and a pair of short-shorts (like me, she was careful not to be too daring today), and even consented to bring a pair of sandals along as a concession to the park\u2019s rules. Julia went all-out, wearing a dress similar to that worn by Belle in Beauty and the Beast, but the skirt was dark-blue-fading-to-purple, which looked fantastic on her. The others just threw on jeans, shorts and t-shirts, of course.<br /> <br /> About an hour later we pulled into the parking lot and made our way toward the front gates. We quickly found our way to Tomorrowland, where Gawain pointed us toward Astro Blasters, which was a sort of combination of ride and shooting gallery. Guests were expected to shoot Laser Tag style guns at glowing alien targets as they\u2019re pulled slowly through the ride environment. The ride tallies up a score for each participant, and at the end of the day the top 100 shooters are displayed at the park\u2019s exit and given a commemorative postcard with their score.<br /> <br /> It didn\u2019t really surprise me that Molly took the top score for the entire day. Though I\u2019d never actually seen her shoot before, I\u2019d heard stories of her legendary prowess with guns of all sorts. Calamity was in the top ten as well, which again was not too surprising, considering that she taught me everything I know about marksmanship. What did surprise me was that Jacob and I were neck and neck, and both of our scores were in the top fifty for the day! When she saw that, Calamity looked at each of us proudly and gave us a You-Have-Done-Well-My-Pupils nod. And I must admit, it\u2019s nice to be recognized for my prowess with a (sorta) combat skill\u2026 especially in the company of my motley.<br /> <br /> After that we stood in line for the legendary Space Mountain. Now at this point, I must confess, the childlike glee I took in my surroundings was replaced by an all-too-adult sense of mischief. I leaned over to D as we were about to board the ride and whispered \u201cso\u2026 we\u2019re riding a roller coaster together, and it\u2019s dark and loud\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> She smirked back at me. \u201cYou\u2019re not going to let this go, are you?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> I thought about it. \u201cWell, considering how often you bring up the fact that you\u2019ve had sex on a roller coaster \u2013 and I haven\u2019t \u2013 I can only assume that it\u2019s something I need to experience for myself,\u201d I returned with my sexiest grin.<br /> <br /> She sighed and rolled her eyes in mock exasperation. \u201cOkay,\u201d she relented after a moment, \u201cI\u2019ll take care of you.\u201d<br /> <br /> The attendants seated us, and D\u2019s hand crept under the waistband of my skirt. It wasn\u2019t very comfortable, and the ride only lasts a few minutes\u2026 but D knows my body <u>really</u> well, and with the two of us working together we managed to get the job done. In fact, I was giving a pretty good O-face when we were captured on camera near the end of the ride. Of course I bought a copy of the photo (from a smirking girl at the exit kiosk).<br /> <br /> I leaned in and kissed D tenderly as we walked back out into the sunshine. \u201cThanks sweetie,\u201d I whispered, \u201cthat was a ride I\u2019ll never forget.\u201d<br /> <br /> She raised an eyebrow in that dead-sexy way she has. \u201cYou know there are like five more coasters in this park,\u201d she husked.<br /> <br /> I chuckled. \u201cYeah, but they\u2019re mostly outdoors and pretty well-lit,\u201d I replied. \u201cI\u2019m as exhibitionist as anyone, but\u2026 well, there are a lot of <u>kids</u> here, D. Think you can handle us just being PG girlfriends for the rest of the day?\u201d<br /> <br /> She looked around surreptitiously to make sure nobody else was listening in, and then whispered \u201cNo day spent with you is wasted, Jules.\u201d She\u2019s so sweet when she doesn\u2019t have to worry about her tough-girl image!<br /> <br /> The lot of us wandered into the Magic Kingdom area next, where Gawain geeked out over the Cinderella castle, which is apparently based on some real medieval structure in Germany. I swear, that guy knows more about the middle-ages than anyone else I\u2019ve ever met. It was interesting at first, but one can only hear so much about crenellations and flying buttresses and voussoirs before you just start tuning it out.<br /> <br /> As we moved toward the next attraction, I spotted someone I\u2019d been looking for. I grabbed Jacob\u2019s arm and dragged him over to stand next to the woman dressed as Princess Elsa. \u201cCan I take a picture of my friend with you?\u201d I asked her. She agreed, and posed next to him. He looked pretty grumpy about the whole situation, and refused to smile no matter what I did. \u201cCome on, Jacob,\u201d I said sweetly, \u201cthere\u2019s no use holding a grudge about something like this. Let it go!\u201d Then I snapped the picture as quickly as I could. So now I have a picture of Princess Elsa laughing uproariously while Jacob flips me the bird.<br /> <br /> And then it happened\u2026 the one smudge on an otherwise perfect day. As I was walking around, taking in the sights and half-listening to Gawain drone on about the castle (again), Goofy came strutting around the corner\u2026 you know, in that way cartoon dogs do. He was surrounded by a gaggle of admiring kids and their parents, and he was talking about the \u201cIt\u2019s a Small World\u201d ride. And then he said it.<br /> <br /> \u201cGawrsh, I\u2019m sure y\u2019all know the words! Sing it with me, boys and girls!\u201d<br /> <br /> And just like that I couldn\u2019t stop myself. The familiar words of the song seemed to well up in my chest, pushing their way up my throat and out of my mouth. It was like trying to hold back a yawn, or a sneeze, or an orgasm\u2026 I could only fight it for so long. I went through one verse and one rendition of the chorus while all of my friends were staring at me like some sort of psychopath.<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026it\u2019s a small, small, wooooorld <u>what the fuck</u>?\u201d I finished a minute later. I caught a glimpse of Jacob filming me with his phone, but I suppose that\u2019s only fair.<br /> <br /> Everybody exchanged nervous glances. \u201cDo you think that\u2019s\u2026?\u201d Gawain asked tentatively.<br /> <br /> Calamity nodded. \u201cWe should probably test it though,\u201d she added. Then she turned toward me. \u201cSorry about this, Lori\u2026 but could you please sing \u2018For He\u2019s a Jolly Good Fellow\u2019 for me?\u201d<br /> <br /> And there it was again. It was like a compulsion; I just couldn\u2019t say no to her request. \u201c\u2026which nobody can denyyyyyy <u>you bitch</u>,\u201d I finished, glaring at her.<br /> <br /> \u201cSorry,\u201d she said again, \u201cbut we had to test it. I think we\u2019ve found your frailty, Lori.\u201d Her sheepish grin turned wry after a minute. \u201cAt least now we know you don\u2019t have to take orders from dog-headed men, though,\u201d she said with a chuckle.<br /> <br /> I apologized for calling her a bitch, then held myself aloof from the rest of the group for a while. D walked with me, her hand firmly around my waist. \u201cIt\u2019s not so bad, as frailties go, babe,\u201d she soothed me.<br /> <br /> \u201cI know,\u201d I replied glumly, \u201cand I\u2019m grateful it\u2019s not something really debilitating. It\u2019s just\u2026 I felt like I\u2019d come so far since Arcadia, and this is just another reminder that I\u2019ll never really escape from that damn cage. I\u2019ll always be what She made me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, well,\u201d she said, subdued, \u201cCalamity\u2019s right, in any case. Now that we know what it is, we can avoid your trigger in the future. C\u2019mon, babe\u2026 don\u2019t let it ruin your day. You\u2019ve been having so much fun so far, and your dad\u2019s coming over to meet everybody tomorrow\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I sniffed once, and then nodded. \u201cYou\u2019re right,\u201d I said after a moment. \u201cOne dark cloud doesn\u2019t spoil a picnic. What do you want to do now?\u201d<br /> <br /> She shrugged. \u201cRide another ride? See one of the shows? Maybe play one of these games?\u201d<br /> <br /> My eyes fell on the High Striker booths, and I felt a naughty grin coming on. I leaned in and batted my eyes. \u201cWin me a stuffed animal?\u201d I asked in a sultry tone. \u201cMaybe\u2026 a <u>bigger</u> stuffed animal than that bear Gawain won for Calamity?\u201d<br /> <br /> I intentionally said this bit loud enough so that both Gawain and Calamity could hear me. \u201cOh, it\u2019s on now,\u201d Calamity said with a grimace. She turned to Gawain and said \u201cyou\u2019re not going to let some trash talking little <u>girl</u> outshine you, are you?\u201d<br /> <br /> I looked into D\u2019s eyes as we approached the games. \u201cRemember sweetie, you\u2019re not just doing this for me\u2026 you\u2019re doing it for the entire Latino community.\u201d<br /> <br /> Each of them paid their entry fee. They stepped up to the platforms together. They hefted and tested their mallets (each of them had taken the heaviest available). Then the glamour started to flow. I couldn\u2019t tell you all of the contracts and tricks they tried, but I know that their mantles were flaring like nobody\u2019s business.<br /> <br /> They swung simultaneously. The weights shot skyward. The bells clanged\u2026 and then both platforms groaned as the springs and fulcrums folded in on themselves and collapsed. Both machines buckled around the strike plates, and there was a groan from the crowd behind us. The hawkers gawped at my friends for a few seconds before dully telling them that they could take any prize they liked and hanging \u201cOut of Order\u201d signs on the attractions.<br /> <br /> Calamity chose a large stuffed parrot (Iago, I think, from the <u>Aladdin</u> film) and spent most of the day with it perched carefully upon her shoulder. D marched straight to a larger-than-life-sized version of Olaf the snowman from <u>Frozen</u>, marched it over to me, and held its stick arms out while dutifully reciting \u201cMy name is Olaf and I like warm hugs.\u201d<br /> <br /> I confess that I haven\u2019t actually compared it to The Lord Sebastian Vercingetorix Bearrington McGrowlypants III, Esquire to see which is bigger\u2026 but I mostly said that just to get everyone\u2019s competitive juices flowing anyway. I feel kind of bad about breaking the attractions\u2026 but I\u2019m sure they\u2019ll be working again soon, and the attendants will have a cool story to tell their colleagues. We had the Olaf doll transported to the exit so that we wouldn\u2019t have to lug it around all day.<br /> <br /> There were other wins as well, of course. Gloria (presumably using Summer Court contracts) won herself a stuffed animal of Lady (the dog from <u>Lady and the Tramp</u>) at one of the still functional High Striker games. Marguerite also tried her hand, and did well enough to win a stuffed Mrs. Potts for Julia. After that, she played some dexterity-based game and won a Lumiere doll (also for Julia, of course, who was radiantly happy with both gifts). Then Calamity turned the tables on Gawain and won him a toy sword and shield at the darts game. Molly won something at darts as well, though I don\u2019t offhand remember what prize she took. And Jacob (also at darts) won Luna a stuffed Robin Hood doll from that movie where everyone was like foxes and bears and shit. I dunno, that movie never made any sense to me even when I was younger. But Luna seemed to love it, and I guess that\u2019s what really matters in the end.<br /> <br /> It would be impossible to describe everything we did today, so I\u2019ll just hit the highlights and sum up the rest. We did most of the coasters. Well, Luna sat out most of those (her gossamer wings are too fragile for that sort of ride), and Jacob or one of the others always waited with her so that she wouldn\u2019t be alone. We did the Pirates of the Caribbean ride together less than twelve hours after we\u2019d watched the movie, which was fun (actually I think that might have been Marguerite\u2019s favorite part of the day; she was almost giddy as she took in the ride, pointing at everything and singing along). We caught a couple of shows and watched a few of the parades.<br /> <br /> Occasionally, Marguerite would wander off by herself for a while, only to return a few minutes later. I realized that she was stealing after the second or third time I noticed this happening, but when I saw <u>what</u> she was stealing I decided against chiding her for her kleptomania. It seems that a lot of college students like to hang out at Disneyland and get high. At the end of the day, Marguerite\u2019s purse was full of more illicit substances than I could name. Most of it was pot, but there also a few bennies, some magic mushrooms, and a not inconsiderable collection of acid. Marguerite remembered that I had expressed an interest in trying ecstasy a while back, and thoughtfully put a few tabs aside for me\u2026 though I decided against trying it that night, as I didn\u2019t know how it would affect me and I had lunch with dad the next day to look forward to.<br /> <br /> I will also note that some of the drugs Marguerite stole were a lot harder. I\u2019m pretty sure that there was some heroin in there, at the very least, and maybe some meth as well. She threw all of that shit in the trash.<br /> <br /> D\u2019s phone rang during one of the parades. She glanced at the caller ID, sighed, and answered. \u201cHello Joan,\u201d she said in a subdued voice, holding her phone away from the street. \u201cNo, I\u2019m sorry, I can\u2019t today. I\u2019m out with Lori. We\u2019re doing\u2026 stuff.\u201d She got a pained expression on her face. \u201cNo, it\u2019s nothing important. We\u2019re just spending the day together. Thought we\u2019d get out of town for a while\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> At this point, the parade passed close by, and the brass band was playing \u2013 you guessed it \u2013 \u201cIt\u2019s a Small World.\u201d D sighed, and her shoulders slumped. \u201cYes, okay? Is that what you wanted to hear?\u201d She rolled her eyes and got an exasperated look on her face. \u201cYou can stop laughing any time now, you know\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I mimed taking the phone from her, and D, resigned, handed it over. \u201cHey Joan!\u201d I said brightly.<br /> <br /> \u201cHello, Lorelei,\u201d she replied, and even I could hear the amusement in her voice. \u201cSo, you convinced de la Rocha to join you for a day at Disneyland?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah,\u201d I said, laughing in turn.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd,\u201d Joan said, obviously relishing the experience, \u201cis she having a good time?\u201d<br /> <br /> I looked at my honey, and looked <u>past</u> the slumped shoulders and grim facial expression. \u201cYou know what?\u201d I said after a moment, \u201cI think she is. I really do.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGood,\u201d Joan said, and I could tell that she meant it. \u201cShe deserves to enjoy a day out with you in a fun environment.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo what\u2019s up?\u201d I asked. \u201cIs everything okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, yes,\u201d she replied. \u201cDe la Rocha had just mentioned a place near the Dream House that offers soft serve ice cream, and had asked if I wanted to join her there some time. I was enquiring as to whether she was free this afternoon.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat sounds great!\u201d I said enthusiastically. \u201cIf you two don\u2019t mind, maybe Andromeda and I could tag along and we could make it a double date. Maybe some time later this week?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2026 we would like that very much!\u201d Joan replied brightly. \u201cNow, before I go, may I speak with de la Rocha once more? I must not miss this opportunity to\u2026 \u2018discuss\u2019 how much she is enjoying Disneyland.\u201d<br /> <br /> I chuckled and handed the phone back to D, and spent the next several minutes watching her roll her eyes and argue with Joan. She can protest all she wants; I <u>know</u> she had a good time while we were there.<br /> <br /> We all had dinner at a <u>Beauty and the Beast</u> themed French restaurant, and despite Marguerite\u2019s grumbling about the authenticity, the food was pretty good. After dinner we headed outside and watched the fireworks show, which was spectacular. The only time I\u2019d ever seen anything that even approached it was this year on the Fourth of July, when D and I went out to the pier to watch the display. What can I say? Small Midwestern towns surrounded by corn fields aren\u2019t big on fireworks displays in the middle of summer, so I guess I never knew what I was missing until I moved to Malibu.<br /> <br /> After the fireworks, it was nearly midnight, and the park started to close down. We made our way to the exit, bade Disneyland a fond farewell, and trooped to the cars with our various plush acquisitions in tow. I stowed Olaf in the back of the van, as holding him all the way back to the Dream House in Jacob\u2019s jeep would have been impractical.<br /> <br /> We didn\u2019t talk much on the way back (at least in the jeep\u2026 I understand that in the van, Calamity did her best to define a good romantic relationship to Molly). Jacob and Luna seem to have the sort of relationship where things don\u2019t need to be said, and they just sat in the front seats enjoying each other\u2019s company in silence. I decided to follow their example, so after I stretched my wings out into the open air, I leaned over and lay my head on D\u2019s shoulder. After a few minutes she put an arm around me, and we stayed that way all the way home\u2026 not sleeping, not talking, not really doing anything except being together. It was <u>glorious</u>.<br /> <br /> Though we\u2019d spent the previous two nights doing nothing but watching movies, Monday is our traditional movie night, so when we got home we invited Molly to stay over and watch a couple of flicks. They were both films we had seen before on previous movie nights, but they were new to Molly, and they both explored the themes of love and romance, so they were topical. <u>Amelie</u> and <u>The Princess Bride</u>, both of which were well worth watching again.<br /> <br /> Once the films wrapped up, I fell into bed with my girls and slept like the dead. It was late morning when I got up, and I had just enough time to make myself presentable and work up a really good case of nerves before it was time for Dad to show up.<br /> <br /> Of course, there was one other matter to take care of first. I had resolved to tell Dad a few things about my friends before he actually met them, and among those things was the fact that D doesn\u2019t go by her first name for \u201ccomplicated\u201d reasons. My sweetie rendered this precaution unnecessary as we were cleaning up, however. She assembled the motley (begging the indulgence of our guests) and revealed her name to all of them. I knew that she had been working up to it for a while, and I\u2019m glad she decided to take the plunge.<br /> <br /> It probably wouldn\u2019t have gone any further than that, but Calamity can sometimes be too sharp for her own good (if you\u2019ll excuse the expression). She chewed on the name \u201cMaria\u201d for a minute or two, and took in my love\u2019s insistence that the name only be used privately\u2026 and then asked if this had anything to do with Twitch.<br /> <br /> D sighed and admitted that it was so. In a rare moment of (relatively) public vulnerability, she admitted that she felt horrible about the things she had done to Twitch in the past. She takes no pride in breaking another\u2019s spirit, and she didn\u2019t want him molested in any way. A few of my friends opined that the things Twitch has done since returning from Arcadia are squarely on his own shoulders, and that he should be punished for them (Jacob and Calamity were at the forefront of this movement); my honey firmly disagreed and repeated that she didn\u2019t want to see the odd little man suffer any more because of what she did to him. Twitch only sided with Darke because the former Winter King promised to protect him from \u201cMaria,\u201d so D feels at least a little responsible for all that\u2019s happened since. The fact that she obviously felt strongly about this put an end to the argument for the moment. Calamity muttered something about needing to cancel a few Amazon orders, and fled the room. I had kept D\u2019s hand firmly in my own under the table throughout this whole exchange, and she gave it a grateful squeeze once things wound down.<br /> <br /> I started pacing around in the entrance hall about ten minutes before Dad was supposed to show up, while everybody else waited in the kitchen. He arrived right on schedule, but his knock on the front door still startled me pretty badly. I opened the door, and there he was\u2026 the Reverend Robert Wells, looking nervous but smiling warmly.<br /> <br /> \u201cHi, Dad,\u201d I said softly. God, I can\u2019t tell you how good it feels to be able to say things like that again!<br /> <br /> He glanced over my shoulder surreptitiously, as though checking to see if anyone else was present. \u201cHello, Juliette,\u201d he replied, and we embraced in greeting.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m glad you could make it,\u201d I said after a moment.<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course,\u201d he said easily, \u201cI want to meet your friends\u2026 to learn more about what happened to you.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cAnd they want to meet you too, Dad,\u201d I said, \u201cbut I should probably warn you about one thing\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> He chuckled good-naturedly. \u201cI understand that your friends might look strange to me, but I believe I have prepared myself for that possibility.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled. \u201cI\u2019m sure you have,\u201d I agreed, \u201cbut I wanted to mention something else. Among\u2026 people like me, the time we spent in Arcadia \u2013 what we call the \u2018Durance\u2019 \u2013 is an intensely personal and often painful subject. If someone brings it up on their own, that\u2019s fine\u2026 but it\u2019s probably best not to inquire about it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI understand,\u201d he said seriously, \u201cthank you for warning me.\u201d<br /> <br /> So I took a deep breath and we walked into the kitchen together. I made introductions, and hands were shaken, and pleasantries were exchanged. By and large I think things went pretty well. Despite her mixed feelings about my request, Marguerite behaved perfectly (though her shadow occasionally embraced my own, which I\u2019m pretty sure Dad noticed). Gawain was exuberant and friendly, and he seemed to put Dad at ease pretty quickly. Calamity was a little more subdued \u2013 maybe conscious of how her appearance might affect my father\u2019s opinion \u2013 but still very gracious. Julia seemed a bit nervous, like she was trying to impress him (which I suppose is natural). Jacob and Luna were typically subdued, but friendly enough. And Ace\u2026 well, he was pretty hung over, so we decided to let him sleep it off in the basement during this particular visit.<br /> <br /> So Dad got to know all of my closest friends. He seemed to take to most of them pretty well after he got over the shock of their appearance. He asked a lot of questions about changeling life. Early on he latched on to the subject of our mantles, which led into a discussion of Courts. From there we ventured into fact that changelings feed off of human emotions. For the first time Dad looked a little worried, and he asked if this harmed the mortals off whom we \u2018fed.\u2019 Gawain fielded his question easily, saying that it was like plants gaining nourishment from sunlight\u2026 it\u2019s something mortals are putting out there anyway, and absorbing it does no harm to the source. Dad looked a little relieved at that.<br /> <br /> Then came the questions. He wanted to know <u>everything</u> about my friends (but then, that was always the case with him, even back in Defiance). What sort of surprised me was that he seemed genuinely interested in what he could do \u2013 or what his church could do \u2013 to help them. He asked if any of them would like his help in reconnecting with their families. Of course, there\u2019s not much he can do for most of them. Calamity\u2019s parents are dead. Marguerite doesn\u2019t <u>want</u> to see her family again. The problems between D and her parents run deeper than the changeling issue. Julia is already on good terms with her parents. Gawain doesn\u2019t remember enough to find his family. And Jacob\u2026<br /> <br /> I tried to encourage Jacob to take my father up on his offer, but he\u2019s adamant that his parents are better off not knowing the truth about him. I think, given time, he might want to try talking to his sister\u2026 but he has to come to that decision on his own, and I won\u2019t push him along that path before he\u2019s ready.<br /> <br /> Gawain took dad on a tour of the house after that, keeping away from private rooms but showing the stage and backstage areas and the wardrobe and such. I think he got a real kick out of showing off the hedge-spun outfits\u2026 both the ones we found in the Hollow and the ones he made himself. Dad was suitably impressed.<br /> <br /> After the tour, Dad said he needed to get going, citing business at the church. I walked him out, and the two of us had another chance to speak privately. \u201cI\u2019m glad you came by,\u201d I said after an awkward moment of silence. \u201cWhat do you think?\u201d<br /> <br /> He considered the matter carefully before answering. \u201cIt\u2019s a lot to take in,\u201d he said after a few seconds\u2019 thought, \u201cbut you seem to have made a good life for yourself here, Juliette, and it\u2019s obvious that your friends care for you deeply.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThey\u2019re good people,\u201d I said fervently. \u201cI know some of them are a little\u2026 unusual, but I want you to know that they\u2019re all good people. I\u2026 please don\u2019t take this the wrong way, Dad. I am so happy that we\u2019ve been able to connect like this after so long. I can\u2019t stress that enough. But before I told you my secret\u2026 when I was lost and alone and afraid\u2026 they were my family.\u201d<br /> <br /> He took my hand. \u201cI think I understand,\u201d he said simply.<br /> <br /> \u201cThere is one more thing I wanted to ask you about,\u201d I said hesitantly as he made for his car.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou can ask me anything, Juliette,\u201d he replied.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell\u2026 when I asked you the other day if you believed in the supernatural, your answer made me think that maybe you\u2019d had experience with something\u2026 inhuman before.\u201d<br /> <br /> He sighed and shook his head. \u201cIt was\u2026 a long time ago, and\u2026 it\u2019s not important right now,\u201d he said mysteriously. Then he looked into my eyes, and the corners of his mouth turned up in a wry grin. \u201cBesides,\u201d he continued, \u201cwe need to save some secrets for the next time, don\u2019t we?\u201d The way he asked it made me think that he had picked up more from Marguerite\u2019s shadow than he\u2019d let on.<br /> <br /> I smiled weakly. \u201cI guess so,\u201d I said, leaning in for one last hug. \u201cI love you, Dad,\u201d I said, getting a little choked up.<br /> <br /> \u201cI love you too, Juliette,\u201d he replied. And then he got in his car and drove off, and I went back inside to talk to the others. And yes, I think I was crying just a little bit, and no, I don\u2019t care.<br /> <br /> First I walked up to Marguerite and gave her a big hug. \u201cI\u2019m sorry I had to ask you to do that, honey,\u201d I whispered to her. \u201cI\u2019ll tell him soon, I promise. I just\u2026 he\u2019s so happy to have his little girl back right now, and I didn\u2019t want to take that away from him so soon.\u201d She nodded and gave me a weak smile. I know she\u2019s still upset, but I think I\u2019m beginning to come up with a plan that might make it up to her.<br /> <br /> Since we still had a few hours before we needed to be ready for the show, D and I decided to call up Joan and Andromeda and see if they wanted to meet us for that ice cream double-date. They were available, so about half an hour later the four of us met at the soft-serve place. I\u2019d heard some of the motley talk about that place, but I\u2019d never actually been there myself; it\u2019s nice.<br /> <br /> The ice cream was good (I had chocolate), and the company was exquisite. I think Joan had a lot of fun teasing D, though my love gave as good as she got, and seemed to enjoy the back-and-forth almost as much as our friend. Andromeda and I chatted amiably about this and that while they went at it.<br /> <br /> As the afternoon was drawing to a close, Joan and I went back up to the counter to order drinks to go. While the two of us were waiting, she hesitantly said \u201cI hear that Andromeda told you our real names.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cI hope that\u2019s okay with you\u2026 Lindsey.\u201d<br /> <br /> She smiled softly. \u201cIt is fine. I would have told you myself if you had asked, Lorelei.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cJuliette,\u201d I said with a wink, \u201cjust in case Rebecca hasn\u2019t told you.\u201d<br /> <br /> The four of us promised to get together again soon, and D and I made our way back to the Dream House. I\u2019ve been writing in this diary ever since, but I really should start getting ready for tonight\u2019s show soon. Plus, I need to talk to Julia and figure out how I\u2019m going to implement my surprise for Marguerite.<br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei Grace</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T13:54:00-07:00","id":933037,"title":"","content":"<b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> So, we all got up bright and early this morning, Lori moreso than the rest of us. One of the first things that Gawain wanted to talk about was the meeting he had with the Incubus. Instead of beating it up and chasing it away he decided to parlay with the creature. They bartered for information on what Hollywood wants with our Freehold and arranged for the Incubus to come to Gawain\u2019s dream the following evening to talk and exchange information.<br /> <br /> Lori, as I said, was rearing and ready to go before any of the rest of us were. Julia came down dressed in a beautiful dress that looked like the dress that Belle wore in \u201cBeauty and the Beast\u201d but was purple and blue. Insincere Marguerite wore a Euro-Disney t-shirt, while De La Rocha wore her usual purples, blacks and combat boots. Luna wore her usual clothes with a long trench coat and boots. It looked nice on her. I wore a t-shirt and jeans. The rest of us wore similar or more summery clothes.<br /> <br /> We took two cars to the park, my jeep and Gawain\u2019s van. We had to fit the whole motley plus Desiree, Gloria, Molly and Luna. Once we arrived at the park we pretty much headed straight for the Astro Blasters ride. It was like a really slow roller coaster with laser guns. Needless to say Molly won for the day, and I do mean that for the whole day, across the whole park. She was damned good. Calamity wasn\u2019t far behind her and ranked up there for the day as well. Lori and I ranked up there too. I was a bit surprised by Lori scoring so high, but she has been taking the same lessons from Calamity that I have, so maybe it shouldn\u2019t have been a surprise. We were not quite as high as the others, but still up there. Luna, Insincere Marguerite and De La Rocha came in just under us. I think the whole lot of us afforded a pretty good showing for the Dream House and Freehold in general if you ask me.<br /> <br /> After that I think the majority of the group went on Space Mountain. Luna and I stayed behind and just watched as the others rode the ride. Luna could not go on the really fast coasters because of her wings so I decided to stay behind and keep her company. It was just as fun to watch the other people in the park scurry around and their reactions to the ride. After that we headed towards Fantasy Land. On the way there I heard Lori exclaim \u201cAh ha!\u201d and ran over and snagged a poor woman dressed as Elsa from \u201cFrozen,\u201d and she proceeded to try and get a picture of the two of us together. She maintained that I should just \u201clet it go.\u201d At which point Elsa laughed and I flipped her off. She got that image immortalized on film. I hope that she is happy with that picture. Not that I begrudge her the opportunity to get it. It\u2019s just not something that I would have agreed to if she had asked. My thoughts last night ran too close to the Lady to find the connection appealing. That said, the poor girl that they had playing Elsa was cute and she looked like she was used to being used for willing and unwilling pictures alike.<br /> <br /> And as if karma isn\u2019t a bitch we discovered shortly after that just what Lori\u2019s frailty is. Some guy dressed as Goofy asked folks around him to sing along with \u201cIt\u2019s a Small World,\u201d and Lori was compelled to do it. I couldn\u2019t resist. I took a video of it on my phone. I know Lori is kind of freaking out about it right now, but we\u2019ll be laughing about it later. We tested our theory that she had to sing if someone asked by requesting that she sing \u201cFor He\u2019s a Jolly Good Fellow.\u201d It worked. She sang it and promptly called Calamity a bitch for making her do it. There was no real heat in her words so I don\u2019t think she actually meant it, and Calamity didn\u2019t take it seriously.<br /> <br /> After that we went to go visit Sleeping Beauty\u2019s castle and Gawain kind of geeked out. Apparently it\u2019s a recreation of the Neuschwanstein Castle in Bavaria, Germany. Mad King Ludwig\u2019s castle. Gawain was keen on explaining the history of the actual castle and all about the architecture. He really is quite knowledgeable about it and seemed to have fun educating the rest of us. Soon after the castle we went to go play some games. Some folks played the strength game. Gloria won a stuffed Lady from \u201cLady and the Tramp.\u201d Insincere Marguerite also won a prize for Julia. It was a stuffed Mrs. Potts from \u201cBeauty and the Beast.\u201d They both did really well. Then Gawain and De La Rocha had their turn and needless to say they won the biggest prizes for their lovely ladies. Gawain won a giant stuffed Iago from \u201cAladdin,\u201d and De La Rocha won a giant stuffed Olaf from \u201cFrozen.\u201d Not surprisingly to us they both broke the games. The employees had to put up an \u201cOut of order\u201d sign after we left.<br /> <br /> While they were breaking the strength game some of us played a throwing game and did pretty well. I afforded myself well and won a stuffed Robin Hood for Luna and Insincere Marguerite won Julia a Lumiere to go with her Mrs. Potts. Around this time Gawain also got a Knight\u2019s helmet along with a plastic sword and shield. It was kind of funny to see a suit of armor wearing a plastic helmet, but the mortals can\u2019t see through the mask, so it worked. Also throughout the day Marguerite has been wandering off and coming back minutes later with her purse getting fuller after each trip. I found out later that she had been pickpocketing money, drugs, and anything else she could get her hands on from mostly College students. There was a surprising amount of hard drugs in the growing stash. I think Insincere Marguerite threw those out and kept the less dangerous drugs for use later on.<br /> <br /> One of the last rides that we went on was the log flume ride. Luna and Julia did not ride it, stating that they did not want to get wet. I did ride it. It was warm out and I wanted to cool down. At least as much as I could in this ever sunny city. After we\u2019d dried off some we went to dinner at the castle from \u201cBeauty and the Beast.\u201d It was passable French food, at least according to Insincere Marguerite. I thought it was pretty good, but I don\u2019t have the most experience with French cooking. I took Marguerite\u2019s word on it. I think everyone enjoyed the meal though.<br /> <br /> After dinner we waited around until they set off the fireworks. It doesn\u2019t matter how old you are, they are pretty. It reminded me of living in Portland. Every July we would go and watch the fireworks. We always did stuff like that as a family. It wasn\u2019t really a holiday that we celebrated, but we liked the fireworks all the same. Sometimes I miss those carefree days.<br /> <br /> When we got back to the Dream House we decided to do our normal Monday night activities and watch movies. Since we had company we decided on watching \u201cAmelie\u201d and \u201cPrincess Bride.\u201d Molly seemed to enjoy herself, which was kind of the point. We had all watched both of those movies in the past, but we re-watched them because \u201cAmelie\u201d is about a girl on her own discovering the world around her and the \u201cPrincess Bride\u201d is about love. In a very simplistic way, but it is about love. So, we watched them again and Molly watched them for the first time. I think a good time was had by all.<br /> <br /> The next morning me and Calamity went to our bi-weekly therapy session. We discussed some things about my family since it came up. The fireworks reminded me of them and my therapist thought that it was worth spending half of our session just talking about my parents. I didn\u2019t really want to keep going since I\u2019ll never see them again, but he thought it was worth exploring. For me it was just a reminder of what I can never have again. I tried to steer the conversation away, but the doctor kept coming back to it. Maybe this therapy idea wasn\u2019t such a good idea after all.<br /> <br /> When we got back there was a couple of important things disclosed to the group. The first was the meeting between Calamity, Gawain and the Incubus. The meeting seemed to go well and they found out what the Incubus was up to. It turns out that the Hollywood courts are interested in the growing Diurnal courts in our area and how we\u2019re handling it. They are also interested in and a little afraid of some of the more powerful members of the Freehold like Madame Spidertoes and Tommy Rawhead. It didn\u2019t know much about the brainwashing of the Hollywood Courtiers and said as much. It said that Hollywood was also interested in how much, if any, information Leanne was giving up about them and their activities. She was fairly highly placed among the Hollywood courts and was the lover of one of the Monarchs. The Incubus has not yet reported back to the Hollywood courts and may not if we can keep its interest here. I don\u2019t know if there was any further plans regarding the Incubus, but Gawain did seem to leave things open ended there.<br /> <br /> Before we all got together and talked me and Calamity went out back and sparred. I think it was a good thing. We have sparred together long enough that we know each other\u2019s moves, but that wasn\u2019t the point. The point was the release, and that is what we got. We needed to let go of extraneous emotion and thoughts and what better way to do that then to focus entirely on fighting? I think it worked for what we needed it for and that was the point. I may be familiar with pretty much all of Calamity\u2019s moves by now, but each day is different. There is also the point that it is damn good exercise.<br /> <br /> After we had showered and gotten ready for the meeting with Lori\u2019s dad De la Rocha called us all together to have a quick talk before he arrived. What she had to say was not what I was expecting. She wanted to explain to the rest of us before the Reverend arrived is that her first name is Maria. He knows her as such and it would seem strange if her friends did not know her by the same name. It was Calamity that put the pieces together. She asked if she was the same Maria that Twitch was so afraid of. Turns out that she is. I was so very tempted to tell her flat out that she was my new favorite person in the world, but she didn\u2019t seem overly happy about the fact that she was the person that Twitch was most afraid of. I suppose I can understand that to some extent. I am not proud of the things that I did while in the Lady\u2019s service, but can\u2019t say that I\u2019ve been faced with those actions face to face. She has. She knows that she is the person that Twitch is afraid of, and that might be something to be concerned about except the fact that Twitch has been a horrible person. He has done horrific things to people of his own free will. He might be afraid that this nebulous \u201cMaria\u201d might find him, but that didn\u2019t make him into a good person. He could have just tried to hide and I wouldn\u2019t have such a problem with him. But no, he had to decide to experiment with people\u2019s brains. With their emotions and fears. He drugged the ever living shit out of a friend of mine to see what he could make him believe. Twitch is not a good person and if he lives in fear of the mythical \u201cMaria\u201d then good. He deserves no less.<br /> <br /> Maria was a little defensive about her past and I added that it was Twitch that made his own choices. No one made him do the things that he did, that was all him. She seemed to think that it was her that drove him to Darke\u2019s side and to follow his orders, but I don\u2019t agree. He could have just hidden. He didn\u2019t need to follow Darke\u2019s twisted orders and do things to people. He didn\u2019t have to remake people into complete strangers. Who knows what he did to Molly and Vik before Grey turned t hem into completely different people. There is still such a thing as free will. Twitch acted of his own free will and for that he will have my enmity. In the end I think we agreed to disagree. De la Rocha has her idea and I have mine. I don\u2019t think she\u2019ll appreciate it but I think she is one of my new favorite people.<br /> <br /> So after all of that we got dressed and ready for Lori\u2019s father to arrive. Calamity was dressed business casual, Lori and De La Rocha were dressed nice, but not quite \u201cchurch nice.\u201d The rest of us wore jeans and a t-shirt. I didn\u2019t feel the overwhelming need to impress Lori\u2019s dad, but I did make sure that my attire was neat. So, Robert, Lori\u2019s father, showed up on time. I think he was a little taken aback by the appearance of a few of us, Calamity, Gawain and Luna in particular. I can see that. Their appearance is the furthest from normal human out of our group. I am just paler than normal and have frost going down my face and arms. Insincere Marguerite is lanky, but no more so than usual. The rest are all fairly normal in appearance if you ask me. Gawain though is a big suit of armor while Luna has beautiful moth wings and Calamity has glass shards coming out of her shoulders and arms.<br /> <br /> Overall I think the meeting went well. There was conversation about what Changelings do and Calamity mentioned the bit about gathering glamour. Gawain explained things in terms of trees and oxygen. He pretty much said that what we do does not harm humans in anyway. We just gather what they give off normally. Calamity also mentioned how much of a rarity that it is that Lorelei got to reconnect with her family. Most of us do not have good relationships or any relationships with our families. Robert offered to be the go between to help us bridge the gap between us and our family. At least one of us already has a relationship with their family, others like me, do not. This is where the whole conversation about fetches started. We explained to Robert what a fetch was. That it was a creation by the Gentry to replace the human that had been taken. We explained that they were made of odds and ends and not perfect copies of the originals. There were always mistakes. Robert seemed to feel for us and wanted to know what he or the church could do to reconnect us with our families. I think most of us turned down his kind offer. I think most of us think that it is too late to try and do that. I for one don\u2019t think that my family would have me back even if they knew about me. I have not been a good person since I\u2019ve been gone and they do not need the complications that I would bring to their lives. It is better that they do not know the truth about who/what they call their son.<br /> <br /> Robert also commented on our mantles. We explained about the Courts and he surmised, accurately, that if we have different Courts then there must be a fair number of Changelings in the area. Gawain confirmed that there are about one hundred of us between Malibu, Santa Monica and Venice Beach. Sometimes I forget just how many of us there are here, and how many there are in other places. How many people have the Gentry taken? How many people have found their way back? Anyway, Robert also asked what the church could do to help us. I think he meant Changelings in general. I don\u2019t know that we really had an answer for him.<br /> <br /> After our talk Gawain took Robert on a tour of the house. They stayed away from our bedrooms, but they went through the stage, backstage and costume areas. Gawain was especially proud of showing off the Hedgespun clothes that we have. I think he also told Robert about dream crafting. I only caught bits and pieces of the conversation but Gawain seemed to be thoroughly enjoying himself, as did Robert. Once the tour was over Lori escorted her father to the door and they said their good-byes.<br /> <br /> Annika showed up about that time for her lessons with Calamity. And Gawain, as per usual, took up broom and dustpan and began to sweep near the stage. I\u2019ve seen them practice, and Gawain sweeping, enough times, so I decided to do something different. I was reminded of glass sculpting when I sat down at the bar to tidy up a bit, which then led to thoughts on ice sculpting. Julia had asked me if I could do an ice sculpture for their wedding and I figured that it wouldn\u2019t be bad to practice. So, I got some ice out of the freezer and began shaping it into different things. At first I was just messing around making different shapes, but then Luna came by and inspiration hit. I started carefully sculpting the ice to look like Robin Hood from the Disney movie. Luna figured out what I was doing pretty early on and stayed to watch me work. I haven\u2019t just let loose and played with ice for a really long time. Since before I came back to \u2018the world.\u2019 I used to be more playful, back before my memories and my conscience came back. I used to create all kinds of figures out of ice, from pieces as small as a chess pawn to grand sculptures that were as big as I was. I tended toward natural shapes, like animals or nature in general, trees, flowers and such. I made several things for the Lady in my time. Depending on her mood she either praised my work or smashed it without a thought. Her moods were mercurial, like the winds, and I never knew how she would receive my little gifts, but I kept making them. When I served her my the Lady was everything. But right now I just want to make pretty things for Luna and my friends. Maybe I\u2019ll start making little ice cubes shaped like flowers. I can put them in the drinks for motley mates or friends. Might be an interesting thing to do for the regular guests as well. It would definitely make the club more unique. I guess it all depends on how long it takes me to make them. Something to look into though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> <b>Care and Feeding</b><br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite DeLisle followed Julia Oldacre into the large attic room Julia had turned into her studio. Julia had changed into a long white dress that was very much covered in paint, while Insincere Marguerite still had on her shorts and French flag t-shirt. Julia turned and smiled at her fianc\u00e9e as the more petite girl sat down cross-legged on the floor.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo you like Pirates, do you?\u201d<br /> <br /> The French girl held up a finger. \u201cNo, I like the romantic fiction of pirates. The sort of\u2026,\u201d she made a rotating gesture with her hands, \u201cThe magic islands and the pirate women and the things. Not real pirates.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course,\u201d the Artist sighed. \u201cBut...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cReal pirates are stinky.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cUm, Bon-Bon?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cStinky.\u201d She said the word emphatically, with a tone of finality.<br /> <br /> Julia sighed good naturedly, looking down as her fianc\u00e9e looked up. \u201cSo you like the ride and the movies, neither of which are stinky?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOui!\u201d<br /> <br /> Julia smiled. Insincere Marguerite usually only spoke French for her. Occasionally Lori. The Artist tried not to frown, to push any jealous thoughts out of her mind\u2026<br /> <br /> \u201cMa petite chou?\u201d The grub cocked her head, trying to read Julia\u2019s expression.<br /> <br /> \u201cSorry Bon-Bon\u2026,\u201d Julia sighed. She considered lying a moment, but decided against it. Her fianc\u00e9e could read her too well. She decided on a dodge instead.<br /> <br /> \u201cI appreciate the Beauty and the Beast toys. I knew you would do well with the ball toss, but I was surprised by the strength test.\u201d<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite blinked at the change of subject. \u201cWell, I mean, the other girls got toys\u2026I couldn\u2019t just, you know, leave you bereft. I am sorry I could not give you something as big as they got.\u201d<br /> <br /> Julia giggled. \u201cYou really worry about that, don\u2019t you?\u201d She knelt to look her lover in the face. Insincere Marguerite\u2019s eyes were searching. \u201cBon-Bon. I am serious. I am happy with you. You are not failing me. But I worry.\u201d<br /> <br /> She took the grub\u2019s hands into hers.<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t want you to think I love you less. You\u2019ve become more empathic, more loving. I love that. I mean, the sex is great, and I love it when you take control, but that is not something we can build a relationship, a marriage, on.\u201d<br /> <br /> This time it was Julia who took a hand to Marguerite\u2019s face. The Darkling\u2019s deep blue eyes were still searching, as if they were looking for something more as Julia looked in them. What could she possibly be looking for but love and admiration?<br /> <br /> The disdain she believed lurked there. Julia had been afraid of that.<br /> <br /> \u201cMa mimi.\u201d This time the Artist spoke French. Insincere Marguerite froze at being called a pussycat. \u201cThere is a scared girl behind your eyes. I see her. Lori is not the only one that can help her. That can help you. Don\u2019t turn away from me. \u201c<br /> <br /> \u201cMiaou?\u201d<br /> <br /> Julia sensed the cat noise indicated uncertainly. Anxiety. She placed her other hand on her lover\u2019s other cheek and kissed her. Hard. The Darkling almost lost her balance, but her lover held her up. She held her face and looked in her eyes.<br /> <br /> \u201cIs that what you needed? Is this what you need? Because damnit that and a whole lot more I will do. I\u2019m serious. I still want to marry you. Do you know what that means? Please stop and think for a moment what that means about how I feel about you, and whether it means I think you have become a lesser person. This is not inertia. This is not me failing to see how you have changed. This is love goddamnit Marguerite. Insincere Marguerite. Whatever you want to be called.\u201d<br /> <br /> Normally, the Darkling would protest at her lack of honorific. At the moment she could not find her voice.<br /> <br /> \u201cI was willing to move out with you when you were broken. I was willing to leave Lori and Maria for you. If I knew I would be with them, I would have never thought I would do that for anyone a year ago\u2026.\u201d<br /> <br /> The taller woman let go, the smaller collapsed briefly into a pile of limbs, before pulling into something approaching a human shape. She looked up at her lover.<br /> <br /> Julia looked down. \u201cThat\u2026that looks painful.\u201d She laughed, nervously. That made Insincere Marguerite smile. She shrugged slightly. \u201cYou get used to it.\u201d<br /> <br /> Julia sat down cross-legged to face her. The grub tilted her head. \u201cWhat do you want to hear? Of course I love you. I believe you love me. That part, that was not in doubt. It is the\u2026,\u201d She clicked once, trying to think, \u201cIt is my abilities, it is\u2026more intrinsic.\u201d<br /> <br /> Julia shrugged. \u201cI saw you get the courage to propose, get Desiree to abandon her former master, bounce back from inadvertent but major emotional pain from one of the dearest people to you, recover from a betrayal from your best friend, and steal enough from a single trip to Disneyland to make a down payment on a boat and a car to pull it. That\u2019s outside the weed and cards. Frankly, that is more impressive than anything you did before this month.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut I don\u2019t\u2026.,\u201d The Darkling paused, considering. Her reverie was interrupted by her fianc\u00e9e putting her hands on her own.<br /> <br /> \u201cMimi I don\u2019t expect you to be okay tomorrow. Calamity and Lorelei hurt you. But\u2026you can\u2019t argue that you are now greater then before, that,\u201d The Artist imitated her love\u2019s cadence, \u201cThat the <i>great</i> Insincere Marguerite has not shown herself to be as great as before, that she is still pulling off the\u2026the\u2026heists impressionnants? That she is a\u2026a voleur formidable?\u201d<br /> <br /> The Lurker simply stared. \u201cI\u2026will try.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBon.\u201d Julia rose and walked over to get her sketchbook, bringing it back. \u201cI need to get the portrait of Desiree ready before she performs. And I would like a very still ball of warm in my lap.\u201d She smiled at her love.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite smiled back. When the Artist was seated, she crawled bonelessly into her lap and curled up into a ball. Julia scratched her head gently while she considered her composition. And just like that, she was fast asleep.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LX</i><br /> <br /> Oh what fun!<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite only used her sandals to get in and maybe once or twice if there was scrutiny, otherwise keeping them in her pack.<br /> <br /> Most of the games were competitive. I had everyone roll Dexterity + Firearms for the shooting game. Molly Nuit was way ahead of anyone else. For the strength game Strength + Athletics. With that, Gawain hit something like 11 success. De La Rocha only hit 10, (both were using both Stone Contract Clauses and she was also using the Summer Clause) but then she used her Professional option to reroll 10s on Athletics (being an Asset Skill) and came out way ahead. I still ruled it broke. Insincere Marguerite got a decent roll by dint of her 5 Athletics (her Strength is still like two) and Gloria got an unusually good roll boosted by the Summer Clause like 9 or 10. I don\u2019t recall the scores on the toss games, but it was Dexterity + Athletics and everyone did well.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite made several Larceny checks over the course of the day, and being what she is, often hit double digits and never did badly. She did get a fair amount of drugs, did throw out all the hard stuff, but also quite a bit of cash and credit cards.<br /> <br /> These hijacks were fueled by the fact the PCs could make frequent glamour harvesting rolls while there. Ironically given both Calamity and Insincere Marguerite made many Dexterity checks over the course of the session, both raised their Dexterity to six afterwards. Or perhaps it made sense.<br /> <br /> For the record, Joan and De La Rocha were not seeing each other for anything romantic. Remember they are old friends.<br /> <br /> I can but apologize for all the probably terrible French in Insincere Marguerite\u2019s story. None of us are really French speakers, and I am the best of us. After some passing around that was the best we could come up it. Most was from Julia, who was not a native speaker herself.<br /> <br /> I think that covers everything, but comments and questions are welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 07-17-2016, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T18:32:02-07:00","id":933185,"title":"","content":"Definitely some chuckle out load moments that I had to share with others.<br /> <br /> Mysteries with the dear Reverend. Interesting.It turns out he's actually a Demon! Or not. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T23:36:33-07:00","id":933283,"title":"","content":"Awesome! ^_^ <br /> <br /> Tonight went really well too. A lot of relationships grew closer, and there was some exploring new directions. I think we all left in a good mood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T08:32:35-07:00","id":933430,"title":"","content":"Good to hear.<br /> <br /> Question though. What happens if someone asks Lori to sing a song she doesn't know the words to?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T10:25:49-07:00","id":933475,"title":"","content":"That's a damn good question, Omenseer. My personal thought is that she'd still be compelled to sing, but would just have to pick some other song. This would keep Lori from avoiding the penalty of the frailty with a loophole. The ultimate ruling would, of course, rest with the Baroness.<br /> <br /> As for your earlier comments re: The Good Reverend, well... you may joke, but I've actually considered that possibility OOC. It seems like a longshot to me, though. I think it's far more likely that Lori's dad is (or was) tangentially associated with one of the Hunter groups. And more likely sill that he merely had some sort of passing encounter with something supernatural (angel, demon, ghost, or what have you) in the past, which might be partially responsible for the radical changes his attitude has gone through between Lori's childhood and the present. Again, pure speculation on my part. The Baroness has been tight-lipped about this, and believe me when I say that nobody is more curious about it than me!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T11:18:04-07:00","id":933495,"title":"","content":"I'd have Lori have to sing, but whether she makes something up, sings something simila, or looks it up and sings it I would leave to her player's discretion as long as she sang ASAP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T00:02:36-07:00","id":934324,"title":"","content":"Lovely entry into the series all around, from the journals to the events that they depict. Even with the drama of Lori's father coming into the secrets of the Malibu Dream House, Lori's fraility coming to light, and certin past offences still not quite being forgiven, the sequence of events feels appropriately, well, fun. I loved the competition between Gawain and De La Rocha, particularly the breakdown of their respective contracts, Julia's enthusiasm matching if not surpassing Lori's (who knows how long she's had that dress stashed away) and how the group reprised past movies to give Molly Nuit a good showing. It really makes the group feel like an open family that doesn't mind more members coming in. I'd praise more details, but then I'd effectively give a summary of the session of my own, which I feel wouldn't be appropriate for someone who hasn't attended one. :-p<br /> <br /> I am left wondering how Molly felt about going to place such as Disneyland though, especially with a background as devoid of a frame of reference as hers. Even for a Changeling, it'd probably seem quite strange.<br /> <br /> Lori's father made me initially think of him being an active part of the Hunter groups, particularly the Lucifuge considering their heavy Christian themes, since certain groups are actually pretty supportive of Changelings (or at least don't consider them hunt-worthy, thank you Mortal Remains). However, the more I think about it the less I really think so. The various groups don't really seem like they'd allow a single agent of theirs roam freely (especially the Lucifuge) without some kind of case, and barring Lori's mother's death there doesn't seem to have been much foreshadowed of what would cause him to take up the Vigil. Granted, I am looking at the game with a degree of separation, so it's entirely possible I'm missing swaths of hints the Baroness has dropped. His behavior does rule him out as being a Hero from the Beast game-lines though - I'm sure that while there are exceptions, my understanding of Heroes generally makes them less than genuine in their generocity. Lori's father goes above and beyond the call of compassion to a bunch of supernatural strangers without any real gain aside from his daughter's happiness.<br /> <br /> As for Lori's fraility, she could potentially sing in acapella (albeit alone) if she knows the general tune of the song but not the words. It depends on how strict the definition of her &quot;singing&quot; is for her fraility though, and I have to wonder what circumstances would bring her to know the tune of the song but not the words - Lori seems to have a good head for lyrics.<br /> <br /> On a bit of a darker note, I am left worried about the victims of Insincere Margeurite's thieving, particularly of the harder drugs she pilfered. While it's ultimately on their heads to go to Disneyland with such drugs at all, addicts can have some...well, very extreme reactions to not having their fix, and the harder drugs tend to have proportionally deeper hooks in that regard. Makes me wonder how many of them would have had to make degeneration rolls from missing that kind of fix (yeah, my imagination goes odd places at times).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T02:16:29-07:00","id":934358,"title":"","content":"It really was a lot of fun. In and Out of character we had a good time. I figured the breakdown of contracts would help with the tests of strength. Julia had been several times with her family to Disneyland, living in Anaheim, is how she had the dress. And you can praise as much as specifically as you want. I suspect we would eat it up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Molly was a bit overloaded. She enjoyed her trip, but it did little to make her feel less like an outsider. Still, she has more context for things, and got to be part of the interaction, not just watching it. Luna spoke to her several times, and helped keep her in the conversation. And yea, it was quite strange to her.<br /> <br /> Lori's dad was completely designed before Penitent Tom or I had read Beast, so nothing touching on Beast there. MDH probably has less crossover than any other CoD game I have ever run. I will say his encounters with the Supernatural were in the past, and he is not a supernatural creature per se. (Did consider making him a Fetch, though, I pulled a similar trick last Changeling game I ran, Beyond the Sea, so being good this time)<br /> <br /> Lori does indeed have a good ear for Lyrics.<br /> <br /> It is true that some trouble was likely stirred up by Insincere Marguerite's thefts. Initially she thought to sell those drugs, but decided against it. Never told the group that, just threw them away. There was likely suffering over it...but then, they brought them to Disneyland. She skipped making Clarity rolls after her Clarity dropped too low for pickpocketing when she lost some to Calamity.<br /> <br /> Thanks as always for the feedback. It is good to get your opinions. I am glad you enjoyed. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T20:00:27-07:00","id":941626,"title":"","content":"The group continues to repair relations, as Lorelei and Insincere Marguerite drift together. But is there jealousy on the horizon? And what secret does Rowan have?<br /> <br /> Also, in non-soap opera, training in Hedge beast fighting and Maria De La Rocha opens up more about her Durance.<br /> <br /> Note Calamity covers two sessions in her journal<br /> <br /> <i>Session LXI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> Once Lori and De la Roche got back from ice cream (after Annika was gone of course) De la Roche pulled us non-girlfriends aside. Well, Lori stayed, for moral support, you know? De la Roche wanted to tell us more about her Durance and Twitch, so maybe we\u2019d be less upset at him. It didn\u2019t really work, but I can see a little where she\u2019s coming from.<br /> <br /> Her Durance sounded pretty horrible. Real, you know, zombie movie-esque, what with the whole dilapidated hospital with mostly mindless creatures lurking beneath. It was good to hear, at least, that she didn\u2019t blame herself for what happened there, in Arcadia, at least anymore than any Catholic feels guilt about anything, apparently. But once she came back, and got her memories back, she feels like she should have let Twitch know, you know, that the Maria from the hospital didn\u2019t exist anymore and wasn\u2019t coming for him.<br /> <br /> And, yeah, well, she probably should have. She had good reasons - well, you know, maybe more like excuses - the shock might have killed him, pledges might have demanded people kill her anyway, that kinda thing. Even if it was a mistake though, even if it was selfish, it\u2019s not a carte blanche for him to do what he likes with no blame. She didn\u2019t take his agency.<br /> <br /> I do feel sorry for the guy. I always have, when I\u2019m not being super judgey. He\u2019s seemed kinda hapless. And, you know, super broken. By Arcadia, not De la Roche. But, he has, by some accounts including his own, done some pretty shitty thing. And without qualms. Those were his choices, how he decided to deal with the fear.<br /> <br /> It does seem like she\u2019s coming to good terms with things though, you know? Being with Lori helps, since she figures they\u2019re soulmates and being taken, and chasing Twitch out was the only way they\u2019d have met. Kinda like me and Calamity being together helps my girl out. Anyway, hopefully our responses also helped, maybe at least a little.<br /> <br /> The show went well, of course. I caught up with Leanne, making sure her dreams had been alright. They had, though she hadn\u2019t noticed the Incubus before either. She did mention that Hollywood had some kind of dream master who had a Morphean dream god patron guy. That... sounds sketchy. And unpleasant, you know, considering those guy\u2019s ties to Gentry already. Leanne didn\u2019t know much about him though, except everyone was afraid of him. The Monarchs even had pledges that he wouldn\u2019t go into their dreams.<br /> <br /> It was super nice talking to her. She\u2019s really pretty and crazy charming. I tried to reassure her about the Autumn Court folks - Moon, Dionysia and Ginny. She was nervous about them spying on her. I guess there\u2019s some tension with her dating Queen Charlotte. I\u2019m not really sure, you know, what's up with that. Moon didn\u2019t mention anything about it when we talked later. <br /> <br /> I did head over to that table after I talked with Leanne, partially because Calamity was over there talking super intensely with Dionysia, while Moon looked nervous and Ginny amused. I brought her a drink with one of Jacob\u2019s awesome new fancy shaped ice cubes in it. After a bit I was, you know, glad I did - they were talking about talecrafting.<br /> <br /> Moon made it sound good at first, talking about breaking the Gentries\u2019 stories and all, you know? But I think there was something more I missed. Cause zie also talked up how it was addictive. The examples didn\u2019t help Calamity and Dionysia\u2019s case much, like using talecrafting to come into large amounts of money only if none of your friends or family had you as a beneficiary of their will/life insurance. Or, say, if you tried to restore tragically lost friendships and it happened because you lose a loved one... not great. Speaking, you know, as a loved one.<br /> <br /> I think I talked her out of it. At least for now. I wasn\u2019t gonna say most of the things I was thinking in front of Dionysia, who is, you know, very pretty and clearly addicted. But Calamity agreed to start small and not without research. The conversation was still kinda getting to me, but I gently reminded her about her rounds and that got her out and about and not focused on it. I kept chatting with Moon. Apparently, Salk\u2019s been courting hir, but zie\u2019s a little unsure. I dunno much about the guy though, so I wasn\u2019t able to help much. Ginny sure wasn\u2019t - she really wanted to punch someone, Salk, Shi, random dude, she didn\u2019t seem picky. She restrained herself for the night though.<br /> <br /> November 19th, evening<br /> <br /> Today was a good day. It even started off good, with Rowan joining the usuals for sex breakfast. She seemed really nervous, especially after Insincere Marguerite, you know, snapped a salt shaker up with her tongue. And even more after Lori stepped out with Jacob. But then she had a talk with Insincere Marguerite and was slightly less so.<br /> <br /> De la Roche, on the other hand, was super relaxed. I guess the being dragged off by her hair thing last night went well? She was complaining her legs didn\u2019t work at least.<br /> <br /> Sadly, she didn\u2019t come with for Viscount Augustine\u2019s Hedgebeast combat training. She had work and plus there was, you know, the whole slap on the wrist thing for her punching the Viscount. He and Old Billy were running things, with Oleander there to wrangle the handful of Hedgebeasts they had to practice with. After, the Viscount treated us to a steak dinner where Percival insisted he was a vegetarian until I suggested he try the tofu steak. <br /> <br /> When we got back, Lori rushed over to Calamity with a new CD she\u2019d gotten. Apparently track eight is super cool. I think they\u2019re planning an act with the two of them which is bound to be, you know, crazy awesome. Whatever the song.<br /> <br /> The show was cool too. I mostly hung out with Gloria and Desiree, who were having a drinking contest. There was giggling. Lots and lots of giggling. Lori made a big announcement about her girlfriends, to make up for, you know, asking Insincere Marguerite to hide their relationship from her dad, I think. It was super adorable anyway. And man the hope in the room spiked when she started off with pointing out she was poly and bi.<br /> <br /> Calamity went off with Leanne tonight. She seems to think it\u2019s a bad idea. I thought she was talking about the talecrafting stuff again at first, the way she talked about it. I dunno why she thinks so - Leanne seems super nice. I mean, Gloria agreed with Calamity. I think the phrase was \u2018Don\u2019t evil Leanne, she\u2019s fuck\u2019. She also threatened me with a blowjob from Desiree if Calamity did sleep with Leanne. I\u2019m not sure how I feel about that.<br /> <br /> Nothing came of that, of course. They were, you know, way, way too drunk. I believe Jacob cut them off when the pretzel throwing started and 95% of the noises they were making were giggles. It was good to see them getting along so well though. Real good. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> If this keeps up, I\u2019m going to have to start inventing new phrases to describe how happy I am. Is it possible to be on cloud ten? Or to be in eighth heaven?<br /> <br /> To clarify, the last two days have been great. Even the bumpy patches have turned out all right in the end, and I think by and large things are on the upswing. The motley\u2019s in a good place, the Dream House is doing great business, and people\u2019s spirits seem to be on the rise in general. And as for my romantic life\u2026<br /> <br /> After D and I got back from our ice cream date with Joan and Andromeda, things got serious for a little while. She\u2019d mentioned that she wanted to talk with Gawain, Calamity, and Jacob\u2026 to go into more detail about her Durance and to help them understand her position on Twitch. I asked her if she wanted me there, and she gave me a noncommittal answer and shrugged. Coming from D, that\u2019s almost like a neon sign pointing straight to her insecurities, so I joined her in the kitchen as the others gathered.<br /> <br /> It wasn\u2019t so bad in the end. I know it\u2019s hard for my love to talk about the things she did in Arcadia, and I know that it frustrates her that none of her friends are willing to let her feel guilty about them. She\u2019s convinced that Twitch was a paragon of virtue before she tore him down and broke his mind. There\u2019s probably an element of truth to that as well, but I can\u2019t help but wonder if she\u2019s looking at the good doctor\u2019s former self through rose-colored glasses.<br /> <br /> She desperately wants some sort of closure for that part of her life. She\u2019s worked so hard to regain the person she was before she was Taken, because she can\u2019t bear to be the thing they turned her into. She doesn\u2019t slink in the shadows. She doesn\u2019t feed off of other people (excepting the occasional bit of health stolen from her opponent in a fair fight). She even explained that her occasional irritation at Calamity stems from our friend\u2019s tendency to accept the changes Arcadia put her through rather than seeking to reclaim her lost life.<br /> <br /> The others agreed that D had given them a lot to think about, but maintained that Twitch had committed heinous acts since returning from the Hedge, and needed to pay for them. D elaborated that part of the reason that Twitch does what he does is that he\u2019s <u>still</u> terrified of \u201cMaria.\u201d He doesn\u2019t know that the monster that tormented him in Arcadia no longer exists; he still sleeps with the light on so that she won\u2019t be able to pull him into the shadows. Part of D\u2019s guilt comes from the fact that she\u2019s been too scared to put his mind at ease on that point. After all, we don\u2019t know what pledges are in place between Darke and Twitch\u2026 the Freehold\u2019s former spymaster might be oath-bound to destroy D if he finds out that she\u2019s Maria.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, and one more thing,\u201d she said softly, giving my hand a squeeze as the two of us sat perched on the edge of the table. \u201cI feel a lot of guilt over what I did to Twitch\u2026 I can\u2019t help it. I was raised Catholic.\u201d She smirked in her usual cocky way, but I could see in her eyes that she was working up to something serious. \u201cBut guilt isn\u2019t the same as regret. I don\u2019t <u>regret</u> anything that happened in Arcadia. I don\u2019t <u>regret</u> chasing Twitch out of the Hospital. If I hadn\u2019t done that, I wouldn\u2019t have met any of you. I wouldn\u2019t have met Lori.\u201d<br /> <br /> She turned so that she was looking at only me, and she took both of my hands in her own. \u201cBoth of our souls were made whole because of what I did to Twitch. Laugh at my superstitions if you want, but I know destiny had a hand in it.\u201d<br /> <br /> I couldn\u2019t speak. All I could do for the next few minutes was stare at my love. I could feel the tears running out of the corners of my eyes, but I know that I was also smiling fit to burst.<br /> <br /> After we dispersed, I pulled D into an empty room and kissed her fiercely. \u201cThank you,\u201d I said after a moment.<br /> <br /> \u201cFor what?\u201d she shrugged.<br /> <br /> \u201cMaria\u2026 what you said in the kitchen\u2026 it was without a doubt the sweetest, most romantic, most <u>beautiful</u> thing anyone has ever said about me,\u201d I said, tearing up again.<br /> <br /> She looked a little uncomfortable. \u201cI\u2019ve said it before,\u201d she pointed out, \u201ca few months back when we were talking about the difference in our ages\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know,\u201d I said, \u201cbut the way you said it just now\u2026 well, I just want you to know that I agree with you one hundred percent, Maria. I don\u2019t\u2026 I mean, with everything that\u2019s been going on, with me singing here and trying to study medicine and preparing to rescue Missy and Jane and everything, I\u2019m not always exactly sure where my life is going. I don\u2019t know where the future will take me. But the one thing I\u2019m absolutely sure of is that in five years, or ten, or fifty\u2026 wherever I am, and whatever I\u2019m doing, you\u2019ll be there with me.\u201d<br /> <br /> She embraced me and kissed me fiercely then. \u201cDamn right,\u201d she said after a moment.<br /> <br /> We disengaged after a few minutes, and I left to get ready for the show. I didn\u2019t have any new numbers that night; just a few torch songs to set the desires flowing, but I think I really knocked them out of the park. It was one of my better nights. I threw D a nod and a wink during my first number, but after that I saw Rowan in the audience, and kept my eyes on her. She seemed keen to return my interest in kind.<br /> <br /> Before I get to the main event, I\u2019ll talk a bit about what else was going on. Molly was back, and seemed to be genuinely enjoying herself (mostly hanging out around the bar and chatting with Jacob). Leanne was there, looking smug as usual. I said hi but didn\u2019t linger at her table\u2026 I haven\u2019t trusted her ever since Jolie warned me against her. I think Calamity spoke more extensively with her later, but I confess my attentions were elsewhere by that point.<br /> <br /> And speaking of Calamity, she hung out with her fellow Autumn Courtiers for most of the evening. Moon, Dionysia, and Ginny were all there, and the four of them seemed to be having a fine old time. I saw Calamity and Dionysia engaged in a spirited discussion about something, though I didn\u2019t eavesdrop to find out what it was. It\u2019s kind of funny\u2026 I didn\u2019t know the two of them knew each other that well, but to look at them you\u2019d think they were the best of chums.<br /> <br /> So fairly early in the evening I dropped by Rowan\u2019s table and promised her that I\u2019d return shortly \u2013 after I\u2019d made the rounds \u2013 so that we could talk properly. Before I made my way back there, I planted myself next to D, who was sitting with Desiree, Gloria, and Julia at their usual table.<br /> <br /> \u201cPlans for the evening, babe?\u201d she asked me, raising an eyebrow suggestively.<br /> <br /> \u201cMaybe,\u201d I admitted, throwing a glance back toward Rowan. \u201cRowan\u2019s back tonight, and she\u2019s been sending me signals\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> D chuckled. \u201cYou gonna club that selkie?\u201d she asked with barely suppressed mirth. I\u2019ve said it before, and I\u2019ll say it again: I love a girl of refined taste and class.<br /> <br /> \u201cNot if you need me tonight,\u201d I said seriously. \u201cI know this afternoon was hard for you\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> D shook her head. \u201cI\u2019m fine, babe. Go have your fun. Julia and Mags will take care of me.\u201d<br /> <br /> I narrowed my eyes. \u201cHow much money do you have riding on this?\u201d I asked under my breath.<br /> <br /> She had the good grace to look guilty as she shrugged.<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay,\u201d I said slowly, \u201cwell, have fun tonight honey. I\u2019ll see you in the morning.\u201d<br /> <br /> As I rose, D threw a triumphant look at Julia, who returned it in kind. As I walked away, Julia and Desiree each took hold of D\u2019s hair and started to pull her out of the room. Curious, I motioned to Rowan that I would be right back and followed them.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat\u2019s going on?\u201d I asked once we had some privacy.<br /> <br /> D\u2019s smile faltered. \u201cYou might not like it,\u201d she warned me.<br /> <br /> \u201cAre you okay?\u201d I asked softly.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh yeah,\u201d she replied with a grin.<br /> <br /> \u201cI won the pool,\u201d Julia offered, \u201cshe\u2019s mine tonight. Not Insincere Marguerite\u2019s\u2026 <u>mine</u>.\u201d<br /> <br /> I allowed myself a little sigh of relief. \u201cSo this is just a sex thing?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> D nodded.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell okay then,\u201d I said with a grin. \u201cLike I said, have fun tonight. I\u2019ll see you in the morning.\u201d I leaned in for a tender kiss \u2013 which was a little awkward, considering that Desiree and Julia still had a grip on her hair \u2013 and we parted for the evening. Confidentially, I think Julia won some sort of bet against D\u2026 but one that D <u>wanted</u> to lose. <br /> <br /> I\u2019ve never been entirely comfortable with D\u2019s occasional need to be dominated. I don\u2019t want to be that to her. I don\u2019t want to be the person who <u>makes</u> her do anything. From time to time it bothers me that she has a need I can\u2019t really fulfill. She\u2019s suggested that I might want to give it a try some time, but I\u2026 I just don\u2019t know if I can. Maybe part of it is because she\u2019s talked about how she left Madame Spidertoes because she was too controlling, and I don\u2019t want to risk falling into that pattern. I dunno. I\u2019m glad she can get what she needs in that respect from Marguerite (and, apparently, Julia).<br /> <br /> In any case, Rowan favored me with a smile that lit up the whole room when I returned to her table. \u201cEverything okay with your\u2026 your girlfriends?\u201d she asked haltingly.<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cThey were just making plans for the evening. I\u2019d probably join them, but you and I haven\u2019t had the chance to talk yet, so\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> We fell into an easy conversation about the beach after that. Rowan loves the beach (which isn\u2019t really surprising, all things considered), while I mostly bemoaned the fact that living with a bunch of darklings has limited my beach time significantly. We actually have a lot in common, considering the obvious differences between us\u2026 bird and seal, air and water, and all that jazz.<br /> <br /> I admit that I was laying it on a little thick. Yes, I was hoping to seduce her, but I swear that I would not have been trying if she hadn\u2019t been responding so obviously to my flirts. And of course I didn\u2019t put any glamour into my efforts; I was just honestly trying to see if I could spark her interest with my natural charms. Using glamour and contracts to seduce someone feels like cheating to me.<br /> <br /> So when she started talking about her house \u2013 a cute but modest cabin by the shore \u2013 of course I leaped at the opening. \u201cIt sounds lovely,\u201d I said breathily.<br /> <br /> \u201cWould\u2026\u201d she began shyly, eyes downcast. \u201cIf you\u2019d like to see it,\u201d she tried again, her voice very soft, \u201cI\u2019d be happy to show you. It\u2019s not far from here.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled and took her hand in mine. \u201cI\u2019d like that,\u201d I said warmly.<br /> <br /> We made it out to the parking lot before she stopped. \u201cLori,\u201d she said, and I could hear the tremble in her voice. \u201cI need\u2026 I need to ask you something.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course,\u201d I said, a little confused.<br /> <br /> \u201cIf this is going where it seems to be going,\u201d she said hesitantly, \u201cthen I need to know. Is this just sex to you? Because I\u2019m not\u2026 I don\u2019t do that. I don\u2019t want to be a one-night stand. I\u2019m not saying that I expect us to be together permanently, or anything, but\u2026 I don\u2019t want\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cRowan,\u201d I said seriously, putting my hands on her shoulders. \u201cI like you. I enjoy hanging out with you, and I like talking with you, and I\u2019m attracted to you. I\u2019m willing to see where this goes, if you are. But even if things don\u2019t work out between us, I\u2019m not going to disappear from your life, okay? I\u2019ll take your calls, I\u2019ll talk to you when you come by to watch the show, I\u2019ll hang out with you when you\u2019re feeling lonely.\u201d<br /> <br /> She sighed. \u201cOkay,\u201d she said after a moment.<br /> <br /> I held up a finger. \u201cNow having said that,\u201d I continued, \u201cthere is something I need you to understand. I\u2019m polyamorous, Rowan, and I have four girlfriends. Anything that happens between us is not going to be exclusive. And you know de la Rocha, the girl I was with earlier tonight?\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cThe Latina with the purple hair,\u201d she said, \u201cyou\u2019ve pointed her out to me before.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019s not going anywhere, Rowan. I need you to understand that, more than anything else. If you\u2019re not going to be okay with that, then we probably shouldn\u2019t go any further. I don\u2019t want you to get hurt. But if you can live with it\u2026 I\u2019d love to see where this is going.\u201d<br /> <br /> She thought about it for a minute, and I could tell that she was really thinking about it. After a bit she gave me kind of a quavery smile and said \u201clet\u2019s give it a shot.\u201d<br /> <br /> We got into her car and she drove us up the coast to her place. Since the course of the evening had been decided, the sexual tension was thick in the air, and Rowan was clearly as eager as I was\u2026 maybe more so. We kept our hands to ourselves for the whole trip, and hardly spoke at all.<br /> <br /> Her house really is a charming little cottage just off the beach, which must have set her back a pretty penny in this area. She kind of nervously showed me around for a bit, but seemed unsure of how to proceed. I suggested a moonlight walk along the beach, and she readily agreed.<br /> <br /> We walked in the surf for a while. My skirt was short enough that I could wade in until it was almost to my knees, but begged off going any deeper. My wings get really heavy when they\u2019re wet, which means I\u2019m no longer much of a swimmer. She didn\u2019t push it, though any fool can see how much she loves the oce