rks at least as hard as any of our performers, but she rarely gets the recognition she deserves for that labor. Can we give her a hand?\u201d We could.<br /> <br /> When the applause died down, I went in for the kill. \u201cShe\u2019s also one of the dearest people in the world to me. But a few days ago, I had to ask her for a favor. It was something that\u2026 well, something that might have made her doubt how much I care about her. It was something that might have made her feel like maybe our relationship isn\u2019t as important to me as it is to her. It might have even made her think that I was ashamed to be seen with her. I was hoping to allay those fears tonight.\u201d<br /> <br /> I leaned in and looked straight into Marguerite\u2019s eyes and spoke into the microphone. \u201cI want to say here in front of God and this audience that I love you Insincere Marguerite, and I don\u2019t care who knows about it.\u201d I set the mic down and pulled her into a deep kiss. There was the usual hooting and cat-calling from the audience, but I don\u2019t think either of us really heard it. <br /> <br /> After the kiss had ended, but before we pulled apart, I whispered in her ear. \u201cIt was always about him, Marguerite, and how it might make him feel\u2026 it was never about you and me.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded, gave me a dazzling smile, and whispered \u201cThank you Juliette. I love you,\u201d before slipping off the stage to thunderous applause.<br /> <br /> So that was nice. Marguerite seemed to need a moment to herself, so I mingled with the crowd while she crawled back into the catwalks to compose herself. Joan and Andromeda were in the audience tonight, and I quickly found myself gravitating toward their table.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat was so <u>sweet</u>!\u201d Andromeda gushed, and her dark eyes had a liquid sheen. <br /> <br /> Joan nodded her approval as well, before looking shyly away and muttering her usual \u201cgood evening, Lorelei.\u201d<br /> <br /> 