 made my way around the rest of the room fairly quickly. In the wake of my earlier announcement, I got enough come-ons and propositions that I could have filled up my calendar for the rest of the month. I declined all of these invitations as politely as I could (telling many of them to ask me again in a few weeks, actually) and made my way up to D\u2019s table. She actually looked a little lonely up there, as Julia was at the Rose &amp; Thorn and Gloria was hanging out at the bar with Desiree.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou did a good thing tonight, babe,\u201d she said as I planted myself in her lap.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat, telling everyone in the world that I love you more than life itself?\u201d I asked with a wink.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, that too,\u201d she said with a grin. \u201cBut I meant what you did for Mags. You made her really happy.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI just hope I\u2019m not screwing things up with Julia in the process,\u201d I admitted with a sigh.<br /> <br /> D shook her head. \u201cShe\u2019ll get over it. She\u2019s insecure, but anyone can see that she and Mags are crazy about each other. The jealousy thing won\u2019t last long now that you two have made up.\u201d<br /> <br /> After final curtain, the two of us wandered down to the bar, where Gloria and Desiree were in the final (hilarious) stages of a prolonged drinking contest. Jacob was overseeing the competition, so I assumed he was keeping things firmly at non-toxic levels. When we arrived, the two of them were giggling uncontrollably and calling each other \u201cslut\u201d a lot. It was actually pretty amusing, though it made me wonder if I\u2019m that silly when I\u2019ve got a few in me. Ah, who am I kidding\u2026 of course I am!<br /> <br /> Desiree upped the ante with her next shot. \u201cDare you to try this,\u201d she slurred at her old friend. Then she walked up to me, poured a shot of whiskey into my mouth and gave me a sloppy kiss wherein she attempted to reclaim as much of the alcohol as possible. I\u2019m not sure if it was the booze or the kiss, but <u>something</u> sure as hell gave me tingles. Desiree pushed the second shot glass toward Gloria and gestured at me impatiently. Gloria glanced at me nervously, but seemed willing to give it a go in the spirit of the dare.<br /> <br /> I thought about it; I really did. Gloria\u2019s hot as hell, and a super nice person to boot, and the events of the evening had my motor running close to the red. But in the end I saw the panicky look just behind her cocky smile and decided to have pity on her. We\u2019re friends. She\u2019s attracted to D. She likes me, but she isn\u2019t romantically interested in me. I didn\u2019t want to screw any of that up, and I didn\u2019t want D to think that I felt like I had to stake a claim on everyone she sleeps with.<br /> <br /> \u201cHang on there, tiger,\u201d I said after a moment. \u201cLet me call in some backup.\u201d I motioned D over, and she participated in the kiss-drinking with a will. I\u2019m pretty sure Jacob cut them both off not long after, and various members of the motley made sure that they made it to their rooms to sleep it off.<br /> <br /> Julia got back about this time, and asked sort of wistfully why Joan and Andromeda were making out in their car in the parking lot. I had to chuckle at that. Marguerite swept in at this point, embracing Julia and giving her a passionate kiss, and the four of us went up to their room together. In the passionate hours that followed, I did what I could to reassure Julia that I love her\u2026 but I did even more to make sure that she and Marguerite were always together in some way. I don\u2019t know if she realized how I was attempting to subtly manipulate the direction of our lovemaking, but I think she appreciated the results nonetheless.<br /> <br /> I thought about taking one of the tabs of ecstasy last night. I was spending time in the company of the woman I trust more than anyone else in the world, as well as two others who are not far behind her in that regard. Under other circumstances, it would have seemed like the perfect opportunity to run that little experiment. But you know what? There was so much passion and pleasure and love and lust and friendship flowing between the four of us that I don\u2019t think the drug was really necessary. Things are okay between Marguerite and I. Julia loves me enough to put aside the jealousy I know she can\u2019t help feeling. And Maria thinks of us as soulmates; two inseparable halves of a perfect whole.<br /> <br /> I was already experiencing about as much ecstasy as I think I could bear.<br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei Grace</b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T20:01:21-07:00","id":941627,"title":"","content":"<b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> Monday, November 17th <br /> Nine years, seven months, five days<br /> Days without stabbing: 3<br /> <br /> So, movies didn't happen last night after all. Well, the others watched, but Becky dropped by to see the show. Gawain and I invited her to join us while we were talking but she made it pretty clear that she was hoping for a different sort of entertainment for the evening. Well, as I am nothing if not a gracious hostess, I saddled up close and began to discuss how best we might see to her interests. And by that, I mean I started whispering absolutely filthy suggestions and promises into her ear (she did kinda start that, what with her whole comment about how it would she didn't want to join the movies since it would be rude to fuck me while the others were trying to watch the movie). And once that got her squirming I nestled in closer and let a hand drift over into her lap. I really really shouldn't have gone quite as far as all of that there in public and all but I just couldn't help myself and hearing those tiny little noises and watching her face as she tried so hard not to draw (more) attention to us and seeing just how brightly Gawain could blush at the whole display was just too intoxicating to resist. Needless to say, the three of us headed out to her place post haste after the show to continue the debauchery at her place. <br /> <br /> At one point, right in the middle of said debauchery, Gawain paused and got the most pained and frustrated expression. He drew back from us both and apologized profusely as he explained that the dream prison had gone off and he had to deal with the incubus before it could escape. We were both understanding, and honestly while the night was far from over at that point neither of us were exactly in dire need at that point. There was, of course, a little teasing about just having to see to each other and Becky couldn't resist a playful quip about Gawain choosing an incubus over a succubus but we both made it clear we did understand. We tucked him into the bed and left him unmolested while he saw to the morphian. And once he was done with that, we did make sure to demonstrate that there were no hard feelings about the interruption... several times. <br /> <br /> It was hard to rouse myself from that bed before sunrise but I did. I took some time to show both Handsome and Beautiful how much I adore them before slipping away to White Maria's for Tai Chi forms and training. It's a little frustrating and more than a little hard not to slip into the knife fighting habits I know so well while working on the Jujitsu with her. I mean, in time I will be blending it all together but keeping my focus solely on the new movements while training is important to learning them. I must say, despite how much time I spent on the floor, it was really good. I was feeling totally grounded from the meditation and I am finding that once you get past the cool demeanor White Maria is very enjoyable company. For one thing, she's not humorless, she has a wit that's as dry and subtle as a fucking razor blade. <br /> <br /> I made my way home afterward and found things were in full swing to prep for the expedition to the Magic Kingdom. Lori was pacing and hopping about impatiently like a little girl. It was adorable and more than a little contagious. Everyone was in good spirits, even Molly. Julia was decked out as Belle's much more Goth sister. (Seriously, that dress is amazing even if it does weigh as much as she does.) The rest of us were all in much more tourist casual. Insincere Marguerite broke out a Euro-Disney tee and a very large and very empty purse that I had no doubt would be full by lunchtime. <br /> <br /> We were too big to all fit in one car but the caravan made it's way cross country without incident. Gawain and Jacob are among the more hijink resistant of us after all. Insincere Marguerite deigned to put a pair of sandals on long enough to get through admission and then shucked them off like they were on fire. <br /> <br /> We started in Tomorrowland. I must say, whoever came up with the idea of combining a laser target gallery with a coaster was brilliant. It was pretty much a real life rail shooter and I might have been happy to ride that one a few more times. Molly proved to be as dead eyed as her reputation and seemed to enjoy making the top spot for the day. Lori was on point and beamed at me a bit when we got to the end and saw the scores. My own wasn't bad. I will confess, I did steal Gawain's gun about halfway through and start two gunning it to bring our overall car average up. I don't know, something about the gun or setup just threw poor Handsome totally off his game. <br /> <br /> From there the day rolled on. I was pushing for the intense coasters though a few of the group weren't inclined. Luna begged off anything too intense due to her wings and Jacob generally stayed with her. Apparently Lori and DLR dealt with the entirely unacceptable matter of DLR having done something sexual that Lori hadn't on Space Mountain. Insincere Marguerite kept slipping away and returning with her purse steadily heavier with smart-phones and wallets and drugs. When we got to the castle Gawain launched in a long winded description of how it was a fairly authentic recreation of Ludwig the Mad's castle which was the model for Sleeping Beauty's castle. He was very excited and I hung on his every word. I'll confess, the details did start to blur a little but I was mostly enjoying the childlike wonder in his voice. <br /> <br /> At one point, Lori spotted an Elsa and was dead set on getting a picture of her and Jacob. He seemed a bit uncharacteristically dour about it, even flipping her off in the end when she told him to just \u201clet it go\u201d. Then a little while later we had the down moment of the day. Goofy was talking to a bunch of kids and decided to lead them all in a the fiftieth or so rendition of \u201cIt's a Small World\u201d we'd heard. And suddenly Lori was singing along with them, which wouldn't have been a thing except that she looked horrified and sounded panicked. She'd apparently found herself compelled to sing. <br /> <br /> We all pretty quickly decided it was clearly her frailty rearing it's head but there was some question as to what exactly it had been. I considered some of what I'd read (I really need to hit the library and do more research on frailties) and decided to try a little experiment. I considered a moment for a song both innocent and not of particular import to Lori and then asked her if she'd kindly sing \u201cFor He's a Jolly Good Fellow.\u201d She did, though I don't recall the 'you bitch' being part of the lyrics. I did apologize but pointed out that at least she now knew she wasn't beholden to furries. That did seem to placate her frown a little and the cloud lifted from her features fairly quickly once we got back to the attractions.<br /> <br /> There was the strength test. We all looked at each other and Gawain and DLR both stepped up to get in line. Then Lori and I looked at each other and things got interesting. We both started to encourage our respective paramours to win us the biggest prize.. loudly enough to make sure the other could hear. And pretty quickly it was a rivalry every bit as over the top as a professional wrestling belt challenge. Though once Lori told DLR that the pride of all Latinos was riding on her I conceded that round to her. Glamor flowed like water in a rainforest and even the unenchanted seemed to feel it. The whole crowd fell a little quiet as they lifted their hammers and locked eyes like something from an old Western. Then they swung and those poor machines just exploded. I hate to admit it, but I think DLR may have had more power in her swing, not that there was enough left of either machine to rate them. The barkers quickly offered up their choice of prizes and pulled out the out of order signs. I took a life sized Iago and perched it on my shoulder and spent the rest of the day making comments in my best Gilbert Godfrey voice. Lori picked an Olaf the snowman. (Still smaller than my great green bear) Insincere Marguerite won Julia a stuffed Ms Potts on one of the machines that didn't get stopped by hammer time and Gloria won herself a Lady from Lady and the Tramp. <br /> <br /> While we were in that area, we drifted to the other games. Jacob and I threw darts at balloons. He won Luna a stuffed Robin Hood (which apparently was something of a childhood crush of hers) and I won Gawain a plastic sword and shield which he promptly bought a matching helmet for and wore the rest of the day. Zod knows that man is adorable. Insincere Marguerite played the skeet ball game and won Julia a Lumiere to go with her growing collection. <br /> <br /> The rest of the day continued in that vein. Insincere Marguerite was quite insistent that we ride the Pirates of the Caribbean and seemed to get really into it. Not the attraction I'd have guessed would resonate with her but it was nice seeing her relax and get into the whole thing so much. We finished up with dinner at a Beauty and the Beast themed restaurant (which Insincere Marguerite tolerated with grace) and then watched the fireworks before heading home. As it was movie night anyway, we invited Molly to join us and pulled out a couple of upbeat favorites to re-watch with her. <br /> <br /> And now I am about to lay myself down with Handsome and have a meeting with a fish (though apparently it looked like a vampire version of Leanne last night.) <br /> <br /> <br /> Tuesday, November 18th<br /> Nine years, seven months, four days<br /> Days without stabbing: 3<br /> <br /> So, the incubus is apparently just a mercenary who was looking into Leanne for Hollywood as a job and was thus pretty willing to cut a deal with us. In exchange for being set free it agreed to visit Gawain's dreams last night and tell us what it knows. I was there this time, which made me glad. Not that Gawain isn't entirely capable in dreams but I like being there at his side and helping him. We really do make an amazing pair in the dreaming and he wanted someone there to press the questioning if needed. But Izikan (the fish turned vampiric Leanne's name apparently) was quite accommodating about telling what it knew and what Hollywood knew and even adding why it had taken a personal interest in Leanne (that being her repressed hunger, hence the whole vampire her look) and promised to leave her be. Gawain and I did thank it and offered it a tidy bit of glamour as payment and invited it to return to our dreams for future business dealings. Having a morphian information broker on good terms could be useful and all in all it seemed like a decent enough chap for a fish. <br /> <br /> Before Lori's father arrived, de la Rocha called the motley together. It seems Lori's father knows her full name and she wanted us to so it wouldn't come out awkwardly during his visit. Once she told us that her first name was Maria it didn't take a rocket scientist to guess that it had something to do with Twitch. And when I asked her reaction made it clear she is the Maria he's terrified of and is (rightfully) worried about what pledges there might be in place against her. Hence the need to keep her name discreet where other Changelings are concerned. There wasn't time to go into things really and she didn't seem comfortable talking too much about it so I excused myself and went to the office to cancel a few Amazon orders I'd placed. Knowing that Twitch was deathly afraid of this Maria I'd ordered a gift copy of \u201cWest Side Story\u201d and \u201cSound of Music\u201d to be delivered to him with just the name Maria on the card. Sadly, as much as I love the thought of him pissing himself over a couple of musicals, stirring the situation up and getting a renewed search for Maria going would be bad news for DLR. Fortunately, they hadn't shipped yet so I was able to change the delivery address to the Dream House. I guess I'll just add them to the collection in the den after they arrive. <br /> <br /> With that bullet dodged, I double checked my clever disguise as a professional business owner and responsible productive member of society before waiting for him to arrive. I am pretty sure all of us were a bit nervous about making a decent impression. Reverend Robert Wells was prompt and was pretty much exactly what I was expecting. He paused, clearly taken back at the sight of us (some more than others, I am pretty sure his gaze lingered on my glass shards quite a few seconds before he managed to meet my eyes). But he handled himself with grace and a quiet friendly manner speaking to us all warmly. He was quite curious and I fear we may have thrown a lot of things at him scattershot. Reverend wells is a smart man and he grasped most of it pretty quickly. He was concerned about glamor until Gawain explained that it was something humans gave off naturally. And at each turn he showed what seemed to be a very genuine desire to know how he or his church could help Changelings. In particular, he seemed keen on trying to help Lost reconnect with their families. It wasn't exactly a thing for most of us but the offer was nice and there are certainly those outside the Motley that might could use such aid. <br /> <br /> After lunch there was a tour and then he was on his way. I'll confess, my parents weren't particularly religious and the mandatory services every Sunday in Snow Globe certainly didn't do much to instill any love for religion in me. As far as God... well if he's there he either couldn't or didn't prevent me from being taken. So I wasn't exactly disposed to like the Reverend even though I was determined to at least try to make a good impression for Lori's sake. But at this point, I have to say the man seems to be quite genuine and caring. <br /> <br /> As Lori's father was leaving, Annika arrived. Gawain took up his broom and I hit the stage. I was feeling good that the visit had gone well and it was nice to just throw myself into my dancing for a couple of hours. <br /> <br /> I was getting ready for the show when DLR and Lori returned from spending the afternoon meeting Joan and Andromeda at the soft serve place and hanging out with them for a while. DLR once again drew us all together to talk. Since there was more time, she wanted to explain the situation between her and Twitch in more detail. I think she was upset that some us (mostly Jacob and I) hadn't seemed inclined to forgive his transgressions after returning. <br /> <br /> She explained about her durance and what she'd been there. That Maria had been a monster, the most dangerous of the lurkers in the hospital setting that had been their Arcadian home. Dr Davis had been one of the shining lights, a saint of a man trying to save people and push back the darkness. I have to say, I find it likely that he wasn't as perfect as she remembers but I can accept that he started out as a good man. And as the smartest and best of the lurkers, Maria took it upon herself to destroy the best of the survivors. She waged a campaign of terror until he fled into the hedge a broken man. She pursued him but ran afoul of Monica's fist before she found him. And when she woke, she was away from Arcadia and some of her old self had come back to her. <br /> <br /> She made a decision that day to reclaim who she'd been before and to never be the monster she'd been. It was, and continues to be, a hard struggle for her. It's why she won't shrink from the sun. It's why she refused to join the Autumn Court. She fights it every day. I cannot imagine how exhausting it must be to deny what she is like that but I respect her determination. <br /> <br /> And she feels an intense guilt for Twitch. If she hadn't broken him then he wouldn't be the worm he is today. She wants closure, to tell him that the Maria he fears is no more but she fears that there are those who would be bound by pledges to destroy her if she did. I don't think it would really matter at this point. The man's a sniveling shadow of what he once was (and I do believe he was a good man even if I suspect she's made him more perfect in her memory) but if he had it in him to reclaim that he would have. But instead he's sold himself to a heartless monster and done unspeakable things for the promise of safety. He's a coward and victim. <br /> <br /> Once again, we countered that Twitch's choices where his own and the consequences of them rested firmly on his shoulders. I don't think she was pleased with our unwillingness to forgive his crimes. But as I see it, no one does terrible things without some reason. Maybe his reasons are better than some but it doesn't change the fact that he's helped Darke to destroy several Changelings and remake them. <br /> <br /> I can certainly understand that she feels guilty but if we held each other responsible for what we did in Arcadia there would be an awful few of us. <br /> <br /> She also spoke of how she feels that it was fate. That it all happened to bring her and Lori together since they were meant to be together. It's very romantic and all but it's crap. Sure, I would have never met Gawain if I hadn't been taken but I wouldn't have lost Stasia or my parents either. And no one can convince me that the world is better off with Calamity rather than Dr Katheryn Moss in it. <br /> <br /> There is no fate but what we make. Of course, as Changelings we can cheat on that front. At the show, Dionysia said something that caught me and we started to talk about tale crafting. She was there with Moon and Ginny for security in case something happened with Hollywood. I've been aware of tale-crafting in general for a while but I'd never really gotten into anything beyond the basic idea of it. Well, tonight I started asking Dionysia about it and she was quite willing to tell me more about how it worked and how to use it to twist fate to match the story I wanted it to. And the idea of being able to magically restore Insincere Marguerite and I's strained relationship had a powerful appeal. The more we talked, the more Moon started to interject about the risks of cruel twists of fate and addiction. Because toying with the universe isn't a light matter and the backlash can be a bitch. Honestly, it didn't take that long for me to realize that as tempting as it was, I wasn't going to be able to pull it off since anything less than flawless perfection risked something nasty making things worse. And to be honest, as much as I miss my Darkling Sister the idea of twisting fate to make her trust me again is just wrong on so many levels. <br /> <br /> But despite my fair certainty that it wasn't as viable an option as I had hoped, I was enjoying the topic and part of me kept hoping that maybe there really was a way to make it work without killing Lori or something. (After all, what would bring us closer again than the death of someone we both love, right?) At some point, Gawain joined us and pretty soon he seemed to pick up on Moon's warnings and started trying to steer me away from the idea as well. <br /> <br /> Eventually, he reminded me that I hadn't talked to the other patrons and I pried myself away to make the rounds. What can I say, the idea of being able to just make everything right again is damn tempting. But I'm not Dionysia. I wouldn't pull it off without a hitch and I'd just end up making everything worse. I can't do that. I have fucked up this motley too much already. I am not going to start screwing with the universe until it kicks us in the junk. <br /> <br /> I was mulling this over as I made the rounds so I guess I was a bit distracted. But then suddenly I was talking to Leanne and it happened. She brushed my hand as we were talking and I missed a beat and started to squirm nervously. Her voice shifted tone and her eyes got a hungry look to them, which set all sorts of things aflutter in me. The flirting was heavy and she started to ask me about our policy on leechfingers rather pointedly. I managed to answer that one at least somewhat coherently. I mean, we don't intervene in anything that's entered into with informed consent so it seemed the reasonable response.<br /> <br /> Damn that woman has my number and she fucking knows it. When she left I watched her go with longing. Shit what the hell is wrong with me? I need to avoid her. If she comes back I need to stay clear of her. I cannot trust myself around her and I sure as fuck don't trust her. I'm just going to have to give her a wide berth. It would be wrong to snub her but nothing more than a simple greeting before I move on to the other guests next time she comes in. <br /> <br /> <br /> Wednesday, November 19th<br /> Nine years, seven months, three days<br /> Days without stabbing: 0<br /> <br /> It's been a good day. I had a good workout with White Maria. The meditation was good, managed to get the lingering unease I was still feeling after last night settled and the practice was fun. I think I am making reasonably good headway on learning. It will be good to have a less lethal and less suspicious way to defend myself than the razorhands. It will also help to increase my ability to avoid being injured while fighting, which I need to be better about. I really am too prone to going all in and leaving myself open. It's impatient and reckless and I should be better than that. I am better than that. <br /> <br /> Got home from that to find that Lori had brought Rowan to sex breakfast. She seemed a bit subdued and quiet but I think it was mainly that she was a little unprepared for the rather open conversation and all. Also, she's leery of Insincere Marguerite (that whole day and night court cycle) but they stepped away to speak briefly and she seemed more relaxed afterward. <br /> <br /> After we ate Gawain, Jacob, Luna and I all loaded up into the van and headed to Viscount Augustine's training session on hedge-beast fighting. He was a good instructor, focusing on theory and the dangers and weakness of the more common beasts to be found in the region. Oleander was there and had brought a few captured creatures for demonstrative purposes. All in all I found the whole afternoon very informative. Hedge-beasts aren't something I know a great deal about and some of the tips and tricks will come in quite handy when I face them in the future. <br /> <br /> Augustine was, of course, civil and formal the whole time. He did take everyone involved out to a decent steakhouse dinner after the lessons. When he's not letting his hidebound notions of morality and honor lead him to foolish choices he's a decent enough man.<br /> <br /> So we got back in good spirits right about time to get ready for the show and Lori was waiting for us. She was a bit disappointed that she'd missed the chance to see Oleander and put the matter with her and Augustine to rest but I doubt the training would have really help her interest. Not that she isn't smart enough to have have followed it but she really lacks any desire to do harm even to a hedge creature if she can avoid it. <br /> <br /> As we were talking, Insincere Marguerite came down in just one of Lori's shirts and nuzzled up to her. It was pretty clear that they'd been spending the afternoon together at that point but it was a little surprising to see her wearing something of Lori's and being affectionate without being subtly possessive. I... I really hate having to guess at how she's doing now that we don't talk anymore. For the most part things seem normal between us now but sometimes it just hits me how completely cut off from each other we still are and it hurts. And it makes me consider doing something crazy like trying to fix things with tale crafting... But as much as I want to wave a magic wand and poof us back to the way we were, I know it doesn't work so easily as that and honestly it would be wrong to just twist and reshape her feelings like that to suit my own desires. I mean, that's only a step removed from what Darke was doing with the Table. The more I think about it (and how fucking tempting it would be to use it if I knew I could do it without making everything worse) the more I think I understand both what makes it so addictive and why Moon was so concerned about my clear interest. No, if I'm going to ever be able to truly call her sister again it will be because I've convinced her honestly to forgive me. And if that means it never happens, then that's on me and it's my own damn fault. <br /> <br /> Geez, that was a sober little tangent now that I'm sitting here thinking about it. At the time, I didn't really have a chance to do more than take note of it before Lori took me by the upper arms and asked me if I'd heard it yet. My blank stare answered her before I could ask her what she was asking about and she whisked me off to the den and pulled out the case for the new In This Moment. I blinked and realized that Monday had been the release. I'd been looking forward to the new album but things have been crazy and somehow it had slipped my mind. She assured me the whole thing was quite good as she cued it up but seemed to feel it was paramount that I heard track eight right away.<br /> <br /> Track eight turned out to be a song called Bloody Creature Poster Girl. I nodded as it started up, I like the band and I figured if Lori was excited then it had to be good... then it got going and as I listened to it I just... Hell's Bells that song could have been written for me. And that was clearly why Lori wanted me to hear it right away. Once it ended I could see she was smiling at the look I had. And we pretty much simultaneously declared that we were putting together an act. If it wasn't already past when we normally started the show prep, I think we'd have started brainstorming it right then and there. As it was, we firmly set plans to work on the act tomorrow afternoon with a plan to have it ready for Black Friday weekend.<br /> <br /> So all in all it has been a hell of a good day and I am in remarkably good spirits. I've had that song on repeat while I was writing and getting ready and I'm pretty sure I'll be singing it under my breath all night at this point. What can I say, when you find your theme song it's kinda magical. <br /> <br /> <br /> Thursday, November 20th<br /> Nine years, seven months, two days<br /> Days without stabbing: 1<br /> <br /> Fuck. I am so fucked... in every sense of the word. Leanne is... amazing. I can certainly understand how that woman has made her way into the bed of all the monarchs in Hollywood and Queen Charlotte's here. Damn but that woman played me like a fine instrument all night and oh by Zod did I sing for her. <br /> <br /> But as tempting as amazing sex can be, it was the leechfingering that did me in. Fuck but as soon as she ran those cool tingling fingers along my skin last night I was done and gone. It was actually worse than when the handmaidens were reeling me in. At least then I thought I was playing along and had some control. But last night I knew that wasn't the case. I knew I wanted.. hell NEEDED to be with her and I couldn't stop myself. I couldn't stop coming round to visit her table. It was hard to leave it and do my rounds and every time I found myself back there. And she could fucking see it. Even as she was telling me I should be running I could see in her eyes that she knew I wouldn't. From the moment she touched my face and I leaned into it and mewled I was fucking hers and we both knew it. She knew it and she liked it. And fuck if seeing that hunger didn't have me squirming and soaked. By the time we left, she might as well have had me on a fucking leash. Hell, I am pretty sure the only reason I wasn't is that she didn't have one with her. <br /> <br /> I... I don't do that shit. Maybe a little when Gawain is particularly Bertilak or when I just need to be taken care of from Becky but I fucking trust them. I know they'd never harm me. I don't trust Leanne one bit and somehow that made everything even more exciting. I was fucking helpless... I was at her mercy and we both knew it. And once we were alone she took no small delight in making it fucking crystal clear she knew exactly where we stood (not that I did any standing in her presence...)<br /> <br /> Fuck. I mean, sure I like being taken. I like it when Becky pins me against a wall and has her way with me. I like it when Gawain lifts me up and carries me to bed. But that's different. I don't submit. I sure as fuck don't beg and grovel. <br /> <br /> Only that is exactly what I did last night. I was so fucked up in my head that I don't remember it all clearly but I remember enough. Half the time I was back in Snow Globe. Laying in the dark, blindfolded and touching myself and dreaming of Them and hating just how much the thought of Their hands on me got me off. I'd forgotten about that. I'd buried those memories until I was there with her cool fingers touching me and reawakening that desperate need. And I felt her draining me, taking the life from me. Everything got hazy. Dreaming and real blurred. I felt things I've only heard about or read about. I never thought I would ever really let go enough to actually feel subspace but that's where I was. In the same moments I remembered those dark fantasies and had them made true. <br /> <br /> Fuck I can't remember everything I said or did but I know that last night Leanne fucking owned me mind, body, and soul. When she said something about not being sure if she was going to allow me to wake up this morning or not I didn't fight it. I couldn't and right that moment I was hers to kill or let live as she saw fit. I remember feeling my breath slipping away as she kissed me hard, the cold blissful oblivion as she sucked the last bits of my essence through that kiss. <br /> <br /> Obviously, she used Spring magic to coax me back from death. But only because she chose to. I fucking placed my life in her hands last night and Zod help me, I want to do it again.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Anyway, so after I got done practicing with ice for a while, De La Rocha and Lori gathered up Calamity, Gawain, Luna and myself to talk privately. De La Rocha wanted to talk to us more about her durance to explain things since we knew about her being the \u201cMaria\u201d that Twitch is so afraid of. She told us that in her durance they were in a hospital setting. There were doctors, and orderlies who worked in the upper levels and lurkers that stayed in the lower levels of the hospital. She was a lurker. In the hospital there was a person that Maria described as a good doctor. He apparently helped a lot of people and she made it her goal to take him down. She was unique among the lurkers in that she remembered her name and kind of led them. So she launched her campaign against the good doctor. His name was Dr. Davis. She followed him and hurt people that he\u2019d just healed and left the name Maria behind as a calling card. She used other terror tactics against him, always leaving her name behind. Eventually Dr. Davis got so frazzled and scared of Maria that he fled the hospital and ran to \u2018the world,\u2019 where he became Twitch. Maria followed him out and started going by her family name. She said that she feels really bad about what she had done to him, but acknowledges that she is a completely different person than she used to be in Arcadia. She has effectively cut herself off from her old self and remade herself into the De La Rocha that we all know. She said that is as close to the person she was before Arcadia as she can get.<br /> <br /> Would that it was so easy for me. I am not so different than I used to be when I served the Lady. I am not quite the same as I was, but I have been sliding back to being Rime a little more than I\u2019d like. There is also the fact that Maria\u2019s story reminded me a bit too much of things that I used to do in the Lady\u2019s service. I would promise to help people get to safety and then leave them cold and alone in some cave or forest. Sometimes I would torment a person or small group that was just trying to get by. It was a game of mine to see how long it took for the person or persons to crack and just start running away. I followed of course, it was more fun that way. Sometimes l legitimately helped people, but they tended to be those that the Lady had expressed an interest in. Everyone else were just playthings for me. I am not proud of what I did before or during the Lady\u2019s service. I grew to not trust people even before she recruited me and treated people badly even then. I stole things that I needed or just wanted or I beat them if I thought they were going to be a threat to me. I am trying to make up for my former actions even now, but I don\u2019t think I\u2019ve gotten very far on that front. I have not had many opportunities to really help someone. Though I suppose helping Molly socialize more is a step in the right direction.<br /> <br /> Anyway\u2026Maria admitted that she thought that following Twitch out of the Hedge was fate since it led to her meeting Lori, her soulmate. Calamity also told Gawain that she never would have met him if she hadn\u2019t been taken. I know that he believes that he never would have made it out of the Hedge if he hadn\u2019t followed her out as she fled. I don\u2019t know if I believe in fate. I don\u2019t like the idea that it was my fate to become a monster, or my fate to realize that. I don\u2019t like the idea that I might have so little control in my life. The girls can go on about fate and their soulmates, that\u2019s fine. In that case, if fate was involved, it had a positive end result. <br /> <br /> And that\u2019s good. I just don\u2019t think it\u2019s fate that led me to where I am now. After I returned to \u2018the world\u2019 I found my family and did reconnaissance until I found out where my sister had gone and followed her here. It was only a matter of time before I got introduced to the courts and joined one of them. That is what Changelings do, they rescue other Changelings and bring them into the \u201cfold.\u201d It\u2019s textbook gathering together in a larger group for mutual protection. There\u2019s just politics involved. I suppose where you have enough people together there is always politics involved. It just happens that way. There\u2019s always a hierarchy. But I suppose that is a topic for another time.<br /> <br /> So, the show went on as usual. Molly was in a particularly good mood when she came by the bar. She took up what has become her usual seat and talked or watched the show. Hailey came by as well, though she was not nearly in as good a mood. She was complaining that Monica and Dominka have hooked up and are spending almost all their time together. Hailey is feeling left out. She is also having problems with her asthma lately. I had almost forgotten that she had asthma since it usually doesn\u2019t bother her at all. I hope that she will be okay. <br /> <br /> My motley mates were being their usual social selves. Calamity went over to talk to Dionysia, Moon and Ginny. Calamity eventually joined them after he noticed his girl having a really intense conversation with Dionysia. Not sure what they were talking about, but it must have been interesting for them all to be talking so intently. After that Desiree and Julia pulled De La Rocha by the hair and started leading her out of the room. Lori intercepted to see what was up, but left a moment later with a smile on her face. My assumption is that they were going off to have some \u201cquality\u201d time together. Lori seemed fine with her soulmate getting dragged off and truth be told Maria seemed perfectly happy being led off by the pair of women.<br /> <br /> Gawain talked to Leanne a little bit later assumedly to make sure that she was okay and to explain what was up with the Incubus that had been in her dreams. After that conversation he came over to the bar to get drinks for himself and Calamity. I decided to put my idea into action and made a couple of custom shaped ice cubes for each of them. I made a little sword for Gawain and a dagger for Calamity. Gawain smiled at the decorative ice when I handed him the drinks. I think he liked them. I\u2019ll have to do that again I think.<br /> <br /> I continued talking with Molly and Luna as the evening went on. Molly was still in a good mood from the trip to Disney Land and from the movie night I think. She seemed to really enjoy herself at both times so I\u2019m going to call that a win for us. I wonder what other activities Molly will like? I guess time will tell.<br /> <br /> Lori was her usual busy self this evening. She seemed to be flirting a little more noticeably with Rowan tonight than she has in the past. I\u2019m assuming that she\u2019s trying to get the shy girl into bed with her. Not that I think Rowan will turn her down. She has been coming to the club fairly frequently and always pays close attention to Lorelei\u2019s acts. That girl is smitten and Lori seems to have a thing for her too, so I\u2019m assuming I know where their evening will end up. Speaking of canoodling, Calamity went over to talk to Leanne and there seemed to be some heavy flirting going on over there. That\u2019s all is seemed to be tonight, but sometimes I worry that Calamity is going to get in over her head when it comes to leechfingers. She seemed to have an unhealthy fascination with the Handmaidens and now Leanne. Hopefully she\u2019ll resist doing anything with Leanne. Yeah, who am I kidding on that one. <br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Well, Lori and Rowan came back to the Dream House for breakfast this morning. Everyone greeted the selkie fairly warmly and se seemed to be mostly comfortable with us. I think she was still a little nervous since a prominent member of the Night Court is a resident of this house. But it all seemed to go well. Shortly after we finished eating Lori asked if she could talk to me and Luna in private. I said sure. I wasn\u2019t sure what she wanted to talk about, but she seemed to be serious. So, we got to another room and Lori blurted out that she was sorry for having pulled the \u201cpicture thing\u201d with Elsa at Disney Land the other day. I was a little surprised but heard her out. She said that she had thought that it might be funny since I\u2019m ice aspected and Elsa is an Ice Queen. She admitted that she hadn\u2019t thought about the Lady when she did it and wanted to apologize if she had upset me with her actions. I admitted to her that the correlation between Elsa and the Lady had occurred to me, but Elsa really is nothing like my former queen. I told Lori as much. I forgave her for the slip and told her that there were no hard feelings. I know that she had not done it intentionally.<br /> <br /> When we got out of her little talk Rowan and Insincere Marguerite were gone. Apparently they had gone off to another room to have their own private conversation. I\u2019m not sure what they talked about but Rowan seemed a little more at ease when she came back into the kitchen with Marguerite. She stayed for a little while longer but ended up going home soon after all of that. Lori walked her out to her car. It was all very sweet. I think Rowan is seriously smitten with our songstress. I just hope that no one\u2019s feelings get hurt. I know Lori wouldn\u2019t do it on purpose, but she really does have a lot of lovers, and most of them have some sort of feelings for her. Not everyone can handle being in so open a relationship though. I do not think I would be comfortable in having more than one lover at a time. When I was sleeping with Insincere Marguerite I had no one else. Now that I\u2019m with Luna I have kept to that sentiment and have not slept with anyone else. I don\u2019t really want to. I guess for me sex is more than just the act. There is an emotional factor. I think Luna and I are in the minority around here, but I\u2019m fine with that. As long as no one gets hurt I\u2019m fine with my friends having multiple partners at a time.<br /> <br /> This afternoon was the day that Viscount Augustine was going to do his lesson on fighting Hedge beasts. So, Calamity, Gawain, Luna and I went to see what the Viscount could teach us. When we arrived we saw that Percival, Sandoval, TJ, Joan, Oleander and Old Billy were already there for the lesson as well. Overall the lesson was pretty interesting. Augustine gave us a crash course in common Hedge beasts and strategies on how to deal with them. Some of it was just plain common sense, some of it was not. Oleander was there to help control the Hedge beasts that Augustine had brought to use as examples. She is skilled with pharmaceuticals and was able to keep the animals from getting too out of hand. I thought she did an admirable job at that. The others seemed more focused on the beasts and fighting them, but I\u2019m not unfamiliar with hunting Hedge beasts. I did so with Rook on occasion. But the beasts are different in different areas of the Hedge and I wanted to see what the local animals were like. After the lesson was over Augustine took us all out for a steak dinner at a fairly nice restaurant. That was an unexpected treat. The food was good and we all had a good time I think.<br /> <br /> Later this evening at the show things got interesting. It seems that Desiree and Gloria got it into their heads to have a drinking contest and they wanted someone to judge and see who won, so they asked me. I figured it would also be good to oversee their little endeavor and cut them off before they drank too much and got alcohol poisoning. Gawain came by at one point and did his best to encourage each of them in their drinking. He seemed to be enjoying the game as much as they were. I made sure that the ladies had plenty of peanuts and pretzels to eat so that they would not be drinking on an empty stomach. I also insisted that they have occasional drinks of water to keep them from getting too dehydrated. Goddess knows that alcohol will dry you out like nobody\u2019s business.<br /> <br /> At the end of one of Lori\u2019s acts she did not leave the stage like usual and instead addressed the crowd. This was all very unusual, but soon made sense. Lori introduced two of her lovers, De La Rocha and Insincere Marguerite and proceeded to tell the crowd just how important these two ladies are to her. She also publically apologized for making Marguerite do something that she didn\u2019t want to do. She didn\u2019t go into details but I know that it was about asking Marguerite to hide the fact that she is also Lori\u2019s lover when Robert came to visit. Lori had Marguerite come down to the stage so she could recognize her as a lover and as the person in charge of lights and technical effects. I know that Insincere Marguerite had been upset by hiding their relationship the other day, but at the end of Lori\u2019s little speech to the crowd she was beaming. I think that really helped Marguerite. She was in a much better mood after that.<br /> <br /> The drinking contest between Gloria and Desiree lasted for a good while. I cut them off when they started throwing peanuts and pretzels at each other and they couldn\u2019t seem to stop giggling. Fortunately, they were very happy drunks tonight and seemed to be really enjoying themselves. It was a change to see them so open around each other. Granted, the tension between them has been lessening of late, but to get completely drunk with someone tends to make you more vulnerable to that person. Now, they were both very drunk so there\u2019s not too much vulnerability going on, but it\u2019s still a big step for them. They even got Lori and De La Rocha involved in the drinking. At one point Desiree poured a drink into Lori\u2019s mouth and then proceeded to kiss the songstress. Presumably getting that drink back in the process. Then Gloria did the same thing with De La Rocha. That was the last drink I let the pair of them have. I figured that was a good place to end their little contest on. I declared the contest a tie since they went drink for drink with each other and I didn\u2019t want to let things continue until someone passed out at the bar. That would be bad for their heath and it wouldn\u2019t look too good for the club either. After the club closed Gawain and I took the ladies to their respective rooms to sleep off the alcohol. I guess we\u2019ll see how they weather the hangover together tomorrow morning. <br /> <br /> Earlier during the show Calamity was talking with Leanne again and those two were definitely flirting pretty heavily. I was a little surprised that they didn\u2019t crawl into each other\u2019s laps right then and there. Eventually Calamity left with the leechfinger, presumably to go back to Leanne\u2019s place. I just hope that Calamity knows what she\u2019s getting herself into. According to Princess Jolie, Leanne gives into her need to feed off of people quite frequently and can be very dangerous. I know that Calamity can take care of herself, but sometimes she has a bit of a self-destructive tendency. I just hope that she comes back to us safe if not sound tomorrow morning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T20:02:41-07:00","id":941628,"title":"","content":"<b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> The visit from Lori\u2019s father was easier on me emotionally than I feared. However, my shadow made mischief while he was here, which was embarrassing. Still, while it was unpleasant not to be able to show affection to either Lorelei or Maria, it was okay, and Lorelei\u2019s father seemed nice enough. Also willful, so I know why Lorelei clashed with him. They are both strong people.<br /> <br /> Beforehand, Maria told the rest of the Motley her name, and I am given to understand later in the afternoon the whole story of her durance. I myself wound up retiring with Julia a while. Julia impressed her passion on me, that she loved me and was not ashamed of me. I confess it was nice, to be told that. Perhaps it seems silly, but looking deep into my eyes and telling me that was really wonderful. I curled up in her lap while she worked. Happily.<br /> <br /> The show went well. Lorelei did wind up seducing Rowan, as I was afraid of. I will speak to her about it like an adult. I don\u2019t want her to misread me; I am not jealous she spent time with another woman. Had I such issues I would be unable to be with her. I don\u2019t like the idea of the Day Court trying to be all good and heroic, when they are not.<br /> <br /> The upside was Maria as a part of this submitted to Julia for the night. And Desiree and I, but mostly Julia. That was a lot of fun. I did not participate as much as assist, but it was still a fun night. Julia and Maria really enjoyed themselves, and I think Maria released a lot of tension. It\u2019s a nice aspect to have between them.<br /> <br /> Cash may or may not have also changed hands.<br /> <br /> They are a happy pile. But I feel more like the vents tonight. Hopefully I will be forgiven, come morning.<br /> <br /> <br /> Today, especially in conjunction with yesterday, was a very very good day.<br /> <br /> Breakfast was fair. Juliette arrived with Rowan, who was quiet. It was punctuated with long silences, possibly due to Rowan\u2019s presence, so when Juliette went to talk to Jacob and Luna briefly, I took Rowan aside. I kindly explained that the house was my territory, she was in it, and while all are welcome during the shows, things work a little different for our courts. However, being gracious, she was fully permitted to come and go, so long as she behaved herself. She promised to. She asked if she was causing I a problem with Juliette. I said no, and she seemed pleased. Everything settled, we returned to the room.<br /> <br /> I had only peered at her from afar, but Rowan is quite charming. Beautiful, friendly, self-effacing, affable, seemingly unaware of her devastatingly good looks and personal charm. Yet single, and Juliette has no apparent romantic rivals, and interested in a committed relationship which, even here in Southern California, she would find easily. Especially if what it took was a case similar to this one in that she had just heard Juliette sing and spoken to her a few times. I was, and am, suspicious. Though to be fair, I developed feelings for Juliette rather quickly myself, though she was far from my only previous object of interest. Or maybe she is a serial killer.<br /> <br /> Or a loyalist, the light dangling before the jaws of the angler\u2026<br /> <br /> Anyway, after breakfast, I had to go back into the vents to consider these events, and what I thought. It was quiet between the walls, between the floors. In such narrow places I focus better; fewer distractions from large rooms. Eventually, I formulated a coherent plan to talk to Juliette, and went to find her.<br /> <br /> First Julia flagged I down. She had been invited by Flores to spend the evening at the Rose &amp; Thorn, but would be returning (sans Flores) tonight. I do need to see Flores again\u2026her work has her not free to come by the Dream House as much as I would like. In retrospect, I wonder if Julia knew what was going to happen and wanted to be away. Julia loves Juliette, but I don\u2019t think it is my imagination that once in awhile a shadow crosses her face when Juliette and I are being\u2026how do you say it in English\u2026I am going to go with affectionate, but that is not what I mean. Anyway.<br /> <br /> I heard her in a room and came out to talk to her. She sort of took I by surprise when she expressed an abiding love and respect, and promised in time she would acknowledge I to her father. There was some passionate kissing in there. I expressed my worries about Rowan, trying to be very careful about how I phrased things. Juliette had not considered any of that, not being a Darkling, and made it clear being honest she was skeptical Rowan had any ill intent, but admitted she could be being manipulated, and vowed that Rowan would not come between us. There was more passionate kissing and my soul was afire. We went up to her rooms and made love.<br /> <br /> It has been some time since Juliette and I had been alone together. It was very intense. My body was awash in her scent, and her body was in mine. We touched lovingly and passionately. Sexually and Intimately. I made love every way I knew how. I am pretty sure I left trailing fingernail trails across her. Eventually, my body could take no more and gave out.<br /> <br /> I woke alone, and took some time to get all my limbs back where they should be\u2026the afternoon\u2019s sex left I all discombobulated. I came down after Calamity, Jacob, Luna and Gawain returned from a seminar on hunting Hedge Beasts. Juliette was talking to them, and I came down wearing only her shirt and hung on her a bit. Then I moved on to get ready for the show.<br /> <br /> I also saw Maria before the show. She wanted to ensure all was well with I. Part was just something she misunderstood; my relative lack of participation the night before was because it was Julia\u2019s party, not because I was not confidant enough. But there was, of course, something to what she was saying. She wanted to I to know she loved I and believed in I, and was not always the best at being tender but she loved I and was glad she and Juliette were involved with I. It was a tender moment, and she was adorably awkward. Maria has a harder time with displays of affection, and that made it more special.<br /> <br /> The show was\u2026I don\u2019t know how to describe it. After her act, Juliette had I throw a spotlight on Maria. She honored Maria as her Soulmate. She then asked I to come down, and there in front of everyone she told I how deeply she loved I, apologized for having to hide her love for I, and promised to do all she could for I. It was\u2026it was\u2026I don\u2019t even know how I should describe it. I kissed her deeply, and told her I loved her too. I think I managed to make it off stage before I wept, but only just. Juliette there she\u2026I\u2026I don\u2019t even know how to write this. I am tearing up now. We declared our love in front of everyone to each other. I still can\u2019t believe it happened.<br /> <br /> Things after were a Blur. Julia arrived, after spending a few minutes watching Joan and Andromeda\u2026well, being loving in their car. She says Juliette is a very lucky woman. I know she is for a lot of reasons. I said I\u2019s goodnights, and retired upstairs with my girls.<br /> <br /> Tonight was a good night, because tonight I was where I belong. I was in the arms of Juliette, in the arms of Maria, in the arms of Julia\u2026we made love not just for pleasure, but for love, for passion. For\u2026to be one, together. I think our little group grew closer tonight.<br /> <br /> And as I look at them, I wonder if Maria may be right about this Soulmate stuff after all.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXI</i><br /> <br /> It\u2019s a really long one, and really late coming out, so not much to add.<br /> <br /> Rowan is, in game terms, a Beast with an unusual treasure and backstory. She is not a special \u201cSelkie\u201d seeming or Kith.<br /> <br /> Not much is coming to me for comments, and I wanna get this out. If you have any questions or comments let me know. The next session we learn more about Rowan, Chalcedony finally wakes up, and everyone finds out Leanne nearly killed Calamity. See you then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T17:21:55-07:00","id":944604,"title":"","content":"The math of Fate and the tapestry of Cause and Effect are complex indeed. So, who is to say that the world is not better for Calamity being in it and not Dr.Katheryn Moss?<br /> <br /> Also, we know that Calamity has a fascination with death and whatnot, but does she have a full blown death wish?<br /> <br /> Are you familiar with the Hegelian model of transformation? While reading all of this, in particular Calamity and DLR portions, I had this thought of Mortal life = thesis, Durance/Changeling life = antithesis, and the crashing of the two in a changeling hopefully resulting in synthesis.<br /> <br /> Also, who soon before Lori needs a separate day planner or personal assistant to keep track of all her lovers' important dates? Keeping track of so many birthdays, anniversaries, blood oaths, etc can be a job all its own. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","user":"omenseer","date":". 08-05-2016, 08:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T02:08:44-07:00","id":944761,"title":"","content":"*chuckles* Short answer Omenseer, Calamity does. Of course, she has a (most likely) unrealistic idea of who she'd have have become if she'd not been taken and a certain lack of self esteem forming that opinion. She does feel that if Snow Globe didn't break her then medical school certainly wouldn't have. Of course, she hasn't really considered that rising to that challenge would have forced her to change. Also, she tends to ignore the things she's done as Calamity that would not have happened which include saving Ginny's life and helping Gawain find the way out of the hedge for starters. <br /> <br /> Calamity does not have a death wish. She has self esteem issues and she is frightfully reckless with her personal safety but she does not actually want to die. There has been a bit of a progression with her intimacy issues and how she feels about the Whispering Voices. On one level, she hates Them for tormenting her. But there is also the fact that she spent a long time in Snow Globe and They were never angry. They were disappointed in her when she wasn't good enough. They told her over and over that They were doing it because They cared. They also were the only being there that showed actual affection and tenderness to her. Early on, she had issues with people being gentle and it reminding her of Them. She was quite drawn to the handmadiens but not until the incident at the pier where she almost blew off the whole business to go with them and let them feed on her. did she realize how deeply that touch affected her. So she is struggling with the positive feelings she had toward the Whispering Voices that the whole affair awoke. At this point, she will learn to get a handle on these repressed emotions and emerge with a better understanding of herself (as long as she manages not to get herself souldrained to death) <br /> <br /> I must confess, I am not particularly familiar with Hegelian transformation. <br /> <br /> I do agree that Lori is going to need a personal assistant to keep up with her lovers at the rate she's going.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T09:37:41-07:00","id":944904,"title":"","content":"The short of it is, you have two opposing but interconnected forces, qualities, ideas, etc. that clash with each other. The portions of the opposing portions that work together or coexist come together while the portions that don't fall away. The two then sublimate, create something new reaching synthesis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T13:50:24-07:00","id":945043,"title":"","content":"And if Lori <i>did</i> get a personal assistant... how long do you figure it would take before the two of them just started sleeping with each other? Nah, she'll just rely on her smart phone to keep her current on important dates and events. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T14:09:38-07:00","id":945053,"title":"","content":"You know, when I read &quot;personal assistant&quot; I thought of a day planner, or a blackberry. Now I'm thinking of Lori hiring a secretary who is actually a Demon. Cargo-ships ahoi.<br /> <br /> But back to the game, it seems Calamity may need something of an intervention, given how giving into her desires has very nearly cost her life and could easily have cost her more. It's understandable why it happened, but still, the world is full of darkness...<br /> <br /> Still, looks like everyone had a fun time this game. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T15:08:48-07:00","id":945085,"title":"","content":"Interesting Omenseer, and I do see how that would apply. I may have to poke further into that. Thanks.<br /> <br /> *grins* Well, if Lori wasn't so pansexual then maybe we could find her an assistant she wouldn't wind up sleeping with. I'd suggest a robot, but given that the only changeling that comes to mind with the mad science/inventing skills is Andromeda...<br /> <br /> Calamity may well need an intervention and I think the motley is prepared to. And yes, while Calamity did not particularly enjoy the fallout, I was enjoying getting to delve into this aspect of her. As both an author and a player, I do generally find that most often the broken toys are the most fun to play with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T19:26:44-07:00","id":945230,"title":"","content":"The kids* have come and answered a lot of that....<br /> <br /> DLR would say that model does not apply to her. She would be wrong, but she would say that. She THINKS she has gotten rid of Maria. Perhaps she is due a backlash where the persona overwhelms her....<br /> <br /> As an aside, anatomy of an NPC for GMs to use and abuse: Maria De La Rocha is an amalgam of like 5 or 6 characters. There was going to be a Chicana punk band, of which I at the time had one picture, the one I am using for DLR. My love letter to the Chicana punk scene. However, as I was fleshing things out, only one (with the pic) had much personality. I came to the conclusion most were empty characters, especially given Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne had a strong well defined personality (and striking picture that all the girls seemed to like) so I moved her to being in a mortal band, as when I have four characters whose personality could be summarized as &quot;Latina Punk&quot; they were perhaps stereotypical. As DLR (who had that name by now) evolved, the band seemed superfluous, so it was dropped. Side note, Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne has had a much smaller footprint than expected. Lori lost interest in her rapidly after sleeping with her, and Insincere Marguerite was hung up on her being Belgian but using her accent and European-ness to get trim, as Insincere Marguerite is kinda arrogant. She has shown up as a ladykiller a few times but not much; I mean she has Interdisciplinary Specialty of &quot;Dexterous Fingers.&quot; Side note on the Side note: More NPCs than not have an Interdisciplinary Specialty. It helps as a thumbnail look into their personality.<br /> <br /> Back on the main line, there was an NPC who was quiet and unassuming called Slug; poor social skills, wallflower, sort of like Mary. However, Slug was &quot;Maria&quot; and had that durance. She had little personality and was not very interesting. But I was toying with DLR and it occurred to be those could be an interesting combination. So I dropped Slug and made &quot;Maria&quot; DLR's dark secret.<br /> <br /> I honestly did not expect any PCs to hook up with DLR, at least more than one night. The cast of MDH is really, really white. While DLR does have a soft spot for white women, she tends to try to date Latinx characters, her torrid relationship with Spidertoes aside. But Lori is kinda irresistible, and she had time to fall for Insincere Marguerite by proximity and Insincere Marguerite being a very in your face sort of woman also. And I have told the story of Julia the would be serial killer upthread. <br /> <br /> Now you know the rest of the story.<br /> <br /> As for a PA, I took it as a program, but then hey robot sex could happen. Happens a lot in<i> Night Train Detective Agency</i> (okay, only Clytemnestra throws it around in Demon Form, and only her spider legs seem mechanical. Counts if you have the fetish I guess)<br /> <br /> <br /> *I say kids. One player is older than me, three are like two years younger. One is admittedly notably younger but I call her kid in seriousness at my peril.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T21:03:30-07:00","id":945264,"title":"","content":"Interdisciplinary Specialty is a very fun merit to take; I have a Beast character who was a football player turned stage actor, and so I gave him the specialty of Acting, which I made the basis for the merit. Surprisingly few rolls had that specialty in it when the sole game he was in was active, but it felt really nice to get the opportunity.<br /> <br /> ...and the idea of Lori having relations with a robot brings to mind an idea I had for a fansplat, basically where objects that were removed from time manage to work their way back and end up wearing the souls of the living. Possession via possession, as I called it. It would basically give the new Tempora (the name in progress) abilities pertaining to how the item was used, such as connecting to particular things, activatable powers and also giving them another form that would come out via these abilities, as well as a major compulsion to fulfill those uses themselves. Haven't thought about the idea in a while.<br /> <br /> Alternate forms beneath the human visage seem to be a staple of the World of Darkness, doesn't it?<br /> <br /> But back to the thread's topic; that's a really interesting thread for how De La Rocha came to be, Baroness. I like how you recognized and cut flat characters, making sure that the cast you had for the players were fleshed out in some manner or another beyond stereotype. From my experience it's not that easy to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 08-07-2016, 12:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T01:47:24-07:00","id":945360,"title":"","content":"Yeah weirdly none of my PCs have Interdisciplinary Specialty. I should fix that.<br /> <br /> Yeah recognizing flat characters is not easy. Well, lemme modify that. It is, but separating out flat characters from characters who have a lot of room to grow is hard. Oleander was initially a creepy poison expert and botanist who had a one sided rivalry with Flores and little else. It was not really until her romance with Lori she came out of her shell, but I figured there was a lot of room there, and I was right. A LOT of the people in clubs in <i>Balance of Shadows</i> were like that too. Tatum and Cindy started off as Natalie groupies without much personality beyond being goth and cybergoth respectively and queer on some level. Both have grown a good bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T13:01:36-07:00","id":950705,"title":"","content":"Okay, Calamity didn\u2019t die at Leanne\u2019s hands, but there is fallout. Suspicion rises at this mysterious new Rowan, and Lori worries about how she is affecting Insincere Marguerite and Julia\u2019s love. Also, news on Chalcedony.<br /> <i><br /> Session LXII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> November 20th, afternoon<br /> <br /> Well that was a hell of a way to start the day. I mean, the start-start was fine - interfering in a tickle/pink lemonade fight between two pretty women isn\u2019t so bad. I didn\u2019t even get pink lemonade poured on me. I don\u2019t think Gloria accepted that me tickling Desiree made up for Desiree tickling her though. But just before I was about to get the breakfast casserole out, De la Roche and Lori got all suspicious about Calamity\u2019s \u2018I\u2019m fine\u2019 and Calamity mentioned that Leanne had run out of glamour healing her...<br /> <br /> That\u2019s bad. That\u2019s real bad. I figured it would be an S&amp;M kinda thing. Calamity likes that stuff, and Leanne\u2019s a Leechfinger and not leery of it like De la Roche is with all that. But that\u2019s too much. After Leanne ran out of glamour, Calamity was still hurt bad enough Desiree had to heal her. I mean, maybe Leanne\u2019s just a shitty healer, you know, or she\u2019d been coming to the Dream House and not gathering glamour for multiple nights so she was low, but probably not. Probably that means she was close to dead. That\u2019s.. that\u2019s not OK.<br /> <br /> The others chewed her out. Well, not really. Like Lori said, they were mostly mad at Leanne. It was, you know, Calamity\u2019s choice, like she kept saying, but Desiree did talk a lot about how good both she and Leanne are at doing bad things to people and it never being their fault. You know, Desiree and Leanne\u2019s fault. I don\u2019t know. She seems nice, you know? But she could have killed her. I can\u2019t lose her. And I\u2019m not good at telling when people are, well, when they\u2019re doing what Desiree said she and Leanne are really good at.<br /> <br /> So, that was breakfast. After that, I, you know, let off some steam at the forge and Calamity worked on the routine for that In This Moment song with Lori. It was a few hours later, I think, when Calamity came and got me cause Moon and Juan Carlos were there.<br /> <br /> They wanted to let us know that Chalcedony\u2019s programming was gone and Queen Charlotte was letting her go. That was good, especially that Queen Charlotte was sticking to her guns with that, despite some of the other monarchs calling for death/exile/imprisonment. There was apparently contention since they still didn\u2019t know if she was a loyalist by choice as well. But now at least she gets to make that choice, you know? It\u2019s a choice most of us made. Admittedly, the fact that the Director seems to be a better dude than most Gentry makes it weird, but still. We can\u2019t just kill anyone whose Durance wasn\u2019t utter shit out of hand. Anyways, Moon and Juan Carlos came by to let us know special, in case she came after us. They didn\u2019t think she would, but she was still upset with us, me and Calamity and Insincere Marguerite particularly.<br /> <br /> That really didn\u2019t make Insincere Marguerite happy. I mean, she wasn\u2019t, you know, happy about any of it except for the Chalcedony getting better part. I think she took it pretty well though. She just needed a little alone time. That made Julia upset though. I don\u2019t really know why. I mean, she was upset cause they aren\u2019t killing Chalcedony too, but that\u2019s cause she doesn\u2019t like Chalcedony and is a little bloodthirsty when, you know, jealous.<br /> <br /> Desiree was also a little jealous and upset. Felicity came by and, you know, she kinda got between Desiree and Princess Joli and now was being all flirty with Insincere Marguerite, who Desiree\u2019s gotten close to. Calamity did point out Felicity was close with Princess Joli and Insincere Marguerite before Desiree entered the picture, but, you know, emotions aren\u2019t always all that rational.<br /> <br /> But after all that craziness, there\u2019s a show. A shorter one than usual, for me and Calamity and Luna - we\u2019re going with Desiree and Gloria to the midnight release of Mockingjay, part 1. I really like the books, and Jennifer Lawrence is pretty awesome. Desiree and Gloria are going early to get tickets, and De la Roche promised to handle security for the last bit so we are free and clear.<br /> <br /> <br /> November 21st, afternoon<br /> <br /> That was a much better second half of the day. Well, for the most part. I mean, Calamity wouldn\u2019t let me toss TJ out on his ear, something crazy about, you know, not breaking any rules, technically. Just benignly being a threatening jerk face, stealing Rowan\u2019s seat and just... being there. Threateningly. All I had was my Contracts of Potential, but still. He did apparently deliver her paper yesterday morning. Tonight we\u2019re reserving her seat, so he can\u2019t do that at least. I don\u2019t care what court someone is, or who says so, no thug makes my House unsafe for someone else.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the movie was awesome and TJ didn\u2019t bother Rowan while Lori was there. It looked like Insincere Marguerite and Julia had a romantic night - we came back and they were slow dancing in the spotlights on stage. And I had a nice night with my girl. Pretty sweet all around.<br /> <br /> For breakfast, we had waffles, which started up a whole conversation about Belgian waffles. There are <u>so</u> many kinds of waffles - I\u2019m gonna have to experiment. We looked them up to see what they were called in Belgium. We figured not Belgium waffles, like how french fries aren\u2019t frites francais or something in France. Liege waffles sound delicious, so that\u2019s my first one, for tomorrow. Of course, that for us talking about \u2018intimate encounters with waffle irons\u2019. I thought Calamity meant sex but apparently she meant torture? It got weird.<br /> <br /> Lori went sailing after breakfast, with Rowan. The selkie asked our permission for it, which was, you know, weird. Then Calamity and Insincere Marguerite got all darkling about it, like maybe she was luring Lori out to where we couldn\u2019t get to her easily. They wouldn\u2019t tell me whether we were really worried about it, so i went ahead and used my Contracts of Potential to see why she wanted her out there. I didn\u2019t get any answer, but I\u2019m sure she\u2019s alright. Mostly sure.<br /> <br /> Maybe I should distract myself. I haven\u2019t found Greg Andrews yet, after all... <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> So I woke up late yesterday morning as a big ol\u2019 ball of happy, surrounded by my darklings, safe and warm and loved\u2026 just the way I like it, in other words. I basked for a while, snuggling up against D\u2019s chest and listening to her heartbeat until the others started to stir.<br /> <br /> We all got kinda-sorta dressed like we usually do (Marguerite started to put one of my shirts on again, but Julia gave her a dirty look and she thought better of it) and headed downstairs in a big knot, murmuring happily to each other in a sleepy yet contented way. I mostly let Julia hang on Marguerite\u2019s arm while I stuck with D, hoping that this would reinforce Julia\u2019s confidence in Marguerite\u2019s feelings toward her. I\u2019m pretty sure D caught on to what I was doing, because she played along beautifully, whispering sweet nothings and occasionally pulling me into a random kiss on our way downstairs.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately our good mood pretty much evaporated when we entered the kitchen. It was obvious that there was some tension in the air, and a few minutes later we learned why: Calamity had spent the previous evening with Leanne Sheets, and had barely survived the experience. Leanne had used her leechfinger abilities to drain Calamity while the two of them canoodled. The Hollywood refugee had healed Calamity as much as she could, but Calamity was still obviously flagging by the time she got home, and Desiree had to patch her up the rest of the way.<br /> <br /> I was livid. I had the distinct impression that the rest of the motley felt the same way. And Calamity just stood there sort of meekly, defending Leanne by saying that she had known what she was getting into and it had been her decision. Desiree chimed in at that point, telling Calamity that Leanne is an expert at subtle manipulation, and she\u2019s made a habit of maneuvering people into making bad decisions which they were convinced were their own ideas.<br /> <br /> In the midst of my rage at how close I\u2019d come to losing a friend, I looked at Calamity. I mean, I really <u>looked</u> at her. I didn\u2019t like what I saw. She looked lost and a little bewildered, like she couldn\u2019t quite process why we were all so upset. I could see her withdrawing, and I didn\u2019t want that to happen. I reached out and took her hand.<br /> <br /> \u201cHey, Calamity,\u201d I said softly, \u201cyou know none of us are mad at you, right? We\u2019re upset because someone hurt you, that\u2019s all. Think about how you\u2019d feel if someone hurt one of us\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cThanks, Lori,\u201d she said just as softly. \u201cI know it was stupid. It was a bad decision.\u201d <br /> <br /> It didn\u2019t occur to me until much later that she hadn\u2019t actually said she wouldn\u2019t do it again.<br /> <br /> In any case, not everything was doom and gloom at breakfast. Gloria and Desiree seem to have mostly patched things up between them, which I know makes them both happy. There was some light-hearted threatening between the two of them (Desiree had been tickling Gloria mercilessly, and Gloria in turn threatened to pour pink lemonade all over Desiree\u2019s head), but anyone could see from the twinkle in their eyes that it was all in fun.<br /> <br /> So before we split up to take care of Dream House business, I pulled D aside for a moment. It wasn\u2019t really private, but I don\u2019t think either one of us cared much about that.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat\u2019s up, babe?\u201d she asked curiously.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou free tomorrow night?\u201d I asked nonchalantly.<br /> <br /> She rolled her eyes. \u201cI\u2019m always free if you need me to be, Lori\u2026 you know that. You always come first.\u201d<br /> <br /> I couldn\u2019t help but smile at that, and I think I might have blushed a little too. I will never get used to hearing that amazing woman tell me how much she loves me. I don\u2019t think I <u>want</u> to get used to it.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo I was thinking, if you didn\u2019t have plans... well, I still have that ecstasy that Marguerite picked up at Disneyland, and I\u2019ve been wanting to try it. But, well, I don\u2019t know how it\u2019ll affect me, and\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> She just kept looking at me, quirking an eyebrow in that infuriatingly sexy way she has.<br /> <br /> I sighed. \u201cDammit, D, I want to be with someone I trust when I do it. And I trust you more than anyone else in the world\u2026 certainly more than I trust myself.\u201d<br /> <br /> She chuckled and leaned in to give me a kiss. \u201cIt\u2019s a date, babe,\u201d she said lightly, \u201cbut does this mean you\u2019ve already got plans for tonight?\u201d<br /> <br /> I shrugged noncommittally. \u201cNot really. Certainly not if you need me for something. But, well, Rowan is supposed to drop by again tonight\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> She laughed again. Sometimes she really is insufferable. \u201cSay no more,\u201d she said with a grin.<br /> <br /> I looked away. \u201cIt\u2019s not like that, and you know it. She\u2019s a really sweet girl, and she\u2019s insecure, and she\u2019s new to this whole scene. I don\u2019t want her to think that I\u2019m avoiding her after what we shared on Tuesday, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> D smiled more seriously. \u201cOkay, I get it,\u201d she said. \u201cGo on, do your thing. Make her feel like the luckiest seal on the beach. I\u2019ll be here for you tomorrow.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks,\u201d I said, kissing her again.<br /> <br /> A few minutes later Gloria walked up casually. \u201cSo\u2026 does this mean you\u2019re free tonight?\u201d she asked D shyly.<br /> <br /> D smirked. \u201cI\u2019ll have to check my calendar. I might be able to work you in\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> They both looked supremely happy with this arrangement, and I managed to push down the twinge of jealousy I felt with only a minimum of effort. D loves me above and beyond everyone else. Gloria is a friend, and doesn\u2019t want to see me get hurt. I repeated those facts to myself a couple of times like a mantra, and the tightness in my stomach seemed to ease up.<br /> <br /> So after that Calamity and I got together on the stage and started choreographing our act. She\u2019s going to be the main focus of course, as the dancer, while I mostly stand in the background and sing. We paced through a couple of options for a few hours. It\u2019s still going to take a lot of work to get it perfect, but I think we have the beginnings of something memorable here.<br /> <br /> We had a few visitors as Calamity and I were strutting and fretting our hours upon the stage (wow\u2026 ain\u2019t I cultured?). First, Felicity stopped by to speak with Marguerite. I don\u2019t claim to know what that was about; I was under the impression that the matter of the Day and Night crowns had come between the two of them, and their burgeoning romance had sputtered and died. And things <u>did</u> seem tense between them, so maybe she had some other reason for gracing our doorstep after all.<br /> <br /> As she was leaving, she ran afoul of Desiree. I know the two of them have never liked each other \u2013 at least not since the matter of Princess Jolie came between them \u2013 but I could have sworn that the temperature dropped ten degrees when they saw each other. I mean, I admit that Felicity hasn\u2019t been my favorite person since the incident with Marguerite a few weeks ago, but Desiree must <u>really</u> hate her.<br /> <br /> Our next two visitors were much more pleasant\u2026 though they were here on somewhat somber business. Moon and Juan-Carlos dropped by. I was about to utter my usual squeal and jump into Juan-Carlos\u2019 arms, but the look on his face brought me up short, so I had to content myself with a sober embrace as I welcomed the two of them into the theater. Calamity and I dispersed throughout the house to get the rest of the motley together, and we let them say what they had to say.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s good news as well as bad. Chalcedony\u2019s dream therapy is finally over, and Juan-Carlos is convinced that she\u2019s now completely free of the Director\u2019s programming. The only issue is that he doesn\u2019t know how extensive that programming was, so we have no way of knowing for certain whether she was a Loyalist by <u>choice</u>. So the Autumn Court has been keeping her sedated and away from the rest of the Freehold\u2026 until now.<br /> <br /> Queen Charlotte put her foot down; she won\u2019t hold another changeling against her will when there\u2019s no proof that she\u2019s done anything wrong. She also won\u2019t allow any other punishments to be meted out (such as exile or execution)\u2026 and I say good for her. Sure, it\u2019s more dangerous to give people the benefit of the doubt, but if we start punishing people for things we <u>suspect</u> they <u>might</u> be guilty of, then where does it end?<br /> <br /> So Chalcedony is being released into the wild, and Juan-Carlos and Moon begged Queen Charlotte to delay that release until they could let us into the loop. Because Chalcedony is pissed at us. <u>Very</u> pissed. And honestly, who could blame her? Nobody really thinks she\u2019ll act against us in a violent way, but it can be hard to tell in these circumstances, so they wanted us on our guard.<br /> <br /> I took Marguerite\u2019s hand during this conversation, because she looked absolutely stricken. I still think Chalcedony was manipulating my French lover, whether through magic or just raw personality, but I also know that she had a major crush on the blue girl, and hearing that Chalcedony is holding a grudge against her couldn\u2019t have been easy. She fled the scene quickly after that conversation. I would have gone after her to make sure she was okay, but I got the impression she wanted to be alone (and anyway, Julia followed after her, and I\u2019m on thin enough ice with her as it is).<br /> <br /> It was almost time to get ready for the show at that point, so I was prepared to head back to my room to get showered and dressed. Gawain approached as Calamity and I were finalizing plans to continue working on our shared act the next day, and told his girlfriend that Gloria and Desiree had invited them to go see some movie premiere at midnight. Calamity hemmed and hawed about it for a while, but eventually I convinced her to take part of the evening off and have some fun. She and Gawain opted to meet the two girls at the theater an hour or so before midnight (tickets were already purchased by that point) so that they wouldn\u2019t miss the whole show. D volunteered to work security for the second half of the show so that they could enjoy themselves in good conscience.<br /> <br /> D seemed to really enjoy herself last night, actually. Reading between the lines, I think she might have appreciated the chance to help out around the Dream House in an official capacity; alone among the motley in residence there, she doesn\u2019t actually work at the theater. I sidled up next to her before the evening ended and sort of casually asked if she was thinking about quitting her job and working security for us full time. She was cagey about her answer. I think she\u2019s privately torn between maintaining her independence and spending more time with the rest of us. I let her know that the option was always there (which might have been the <u>teensiest </u>bit beyond my authority to promise, but I don\u2019t think anyone else would challenge the decision) when and if she was ready for it.<br /> <br /> When I headed out on stage for my first number, I looked over at Rowan\u2019s usual table and was startled to see TJ sitting there, looking smug and surly as usual. I scanned the audience quickly and located Rowan across the room and a little further back than she usually sits, and tipped her a wink in response to her hesitant wave.<br /> <br /> After my number I made my way around the crowd, stopping in to talk to Rowan first to make sure she was okay and to promise her that I\u2019d join her shortly. That sweetheart had bought me flowers and had them delivered to the bar, and I gave her a kiss to let her know how much I appreciated the thought. After that I made the rounds, making sure to talk to all of our regulars (including that mortal guy who keeps asking me out every other night). <br /> <br /> I stopped by Princess Jolie\u2019s table for a while. It was the first time I\u2019d seen her at the Dream House in quite some time, and I wanted to pay my respects. As has happened all too frequently recently, she looked deeply depressed. This time the source of her malaise seemed to be Leanne\u2019s recent tryst with Queen Charlotte. I commiserated with her for a little while as best I could (in the wake of Calamity\u2019s encounter, I found it remarkably easy to bad-mouth Leanne), and made sure she knew that I\u2019d always be around if she needed to talk, but in the end there really wasn\u2019t much I could do to help her.<br /> <br /> Molly was at the bar as usual. We chatted for a little while, but all I really got out of her was that she was going to be shadowing Chalcedony, and that she was worried about that for some reason. Reading between the lines, I wonder if Molly maybe has a little crush on Chalcedony? I\u2019m not sure if that would be a good thing or a bad thing. On the one hand, it could interfere with her duties, but on the other hand\u2026 well, it can only be a step forward if she forms meaningful relationships with other changelings, right?<br /> <br /> In any case, all such thoughts were quickly driven from my mind when I joined Rowan at her table. She confessed that she was pretty spooked by TJ, but I once again assured her that the Summer Courtier wouldn\u2019t dare bother her in the Dream House. She confessed that her anxiety was more about what he might do <u>outside</u> of the Dream House. Apparently he had delivered her paper to her doorstep that morning.<br /> <br /> I was not happy to hear this. I spoke with Calamity, Gawain, and D about the situation, and Calamity agreed to have a talk with TJ. Unfortunately, TJ is pretty good at skating the lines of propriety, and he hadn\u2019t actually done anything actionable against Rowan yet. D promised to escort the two of us to Rowan\u2019s car when it was time for us to leave to ensure that he wasn\u2019t lurking in the parking lot.<br /> <br /> Before too much longer it was time for Gawain and Calamity (and Luna, apparently) to head out to the film. It sounded like fun, actually\u2026 I haven\u2019t been out to the movies since we all went to see <u>Guardians of the Galaxy</u> in August. But this film (<u>Mockingbird</u> or something like that, I think) was part of a series, and I hadn\u2019t seen any of the others yet, so it didn\u2019t seem like a good place to start. Apparently Gawain\u2019s a fan of the books those films are based on, and he was almost giddy with excitement.<br /> <br /> After things wound down, Rowan and I took our leave as well, and D was as good as her word, walking us out and giving me a tender kiss goodbye (which didn\u2019t seem to bother Rowan much, to her credit). A short drive later we were back at Rowan\u2019s place. Things weren\u2019t as intense this time, though there was still more than enough passion to make things interesting.<br /> <br /> We took another moonlight walk along the shore, of course\u2026 it seems so important to her, and it\u2019s a pleasant enough way to spend an evening. We talked a bit more this time too, since neither of us had the sense of urgency present in our first evening together. A couple of times she seemed like she was trying to tell me something, but she didn\u2019t quite work up the courage (at least not then). We did go to bed together eventually, of course, and we did make love, but we also cuddled and kissed more than we had before, which was nice.<br /> <br /> Before we dropped off, she asked me if I\u2019d like to go sailing with her some time. I\u2019d never been sailing before, and I don\u2019t get many opportunities to get out and play in the sun with my schedule, so I eagerly agreed. She sort of hesitantly asked if I might like to go the next day, and I told her that it would be fine as far as I knew, but I wanted to check my schedule with the rest of the motley before making any promises. She allowed as how that would be fair, and we drifted off breathing softly into each other\u2019s hair.<br /> <br /> Rowan joined us for sex breakfast again this morning, and things were a little more relaxed this time. Most of the others were happily chatting about the movie they\u2019d seen the night before, and they seemed to have enjoyed themselves. D and Gloria had hooked up when she got back to the Dream House, of course, and they <u>also</u> seemed to have enjoyed themselves, but I didn\u2019t let it bother me. D drifted toward me as soon as she entered the kitchen and gave me a warm hug and a soulful kiss, and I was suitably reassured that I\u2019m still number one in her heart.<br /> <br /> Rowan brought up the idea of taking me sailing to the others before I even thought about introducing the subject. It was kind of cute, actually\u2026 almost like she was asking the motley\u2019s permission or something. Nobody raised any serious objections, and I tried to sort of reinvent the conversation by telling everyone that I just wanted them to know where I was so they wouldn\u2019t worry.<br /> <br /> In any case, we drove back to Rowan\u2019s place as soon as we were done with breakfast (Belgian waffles, yum!). Well in truth that\u2019s not entirely accurate\u2026 we actually drove to the marina where she docks her boat. I don\u2019t claim to understand the intricacies of sailing a boat (what she calls a \u201csloop\u201d), but I\u2019m not bad at following directions, and my upper body strength is higher than most people expect, so within a few minutes we fell into a steady rhythm and were soaring across the open water.<br /> <br /> When done properly, sailing can actually be a lot like flying\u2026 so of course I enjoyed it immensely. When we weren\u2019t working to turn (or \u201ctack\u201d) the boat, I often drifted to the very front (\u201cprow\u201d) and stretched my wings out to feel the air flowing past in swift currents. It was pretty balmy for November, so I\u2019d worn a pair of short-shorts and a bikini top, and the feel of the sun and the wind on my bare skin was heavenly.<br /> <br /> Sailing is hard work, but it\u2019s also a lot of fun. As you can probably guess from the previous paragraphs, there\u2019s a lot of jargon involved, but I think I managed to pick up on most of it. After the third time the boom smacked my wings painfully, I learned to duck whenever Rowan called out \u201chelms alee!\u201d I know the difference between the main and the jib now, I know how to read the streamers on the sails to see which way the wind is blowing, and I know how to secure a line so that it won\u2019t slip at an inopportune moment.<br /> <br /> Once we got far enough out onto the ocean, we dropped the sails and let the boat drift for a while. I started to sun myself, and Rowan started to talk. She talked a bit about her Durance, and how she came back to the world. She didn\u2019t escape conventionally\u2026 she was cast out when she revealed her true nature to the man who was supposed to be her husband. That\u2019s why she\u2019s been afraid to get too close to anyone since her return\u2026 and why it was so important to her that she show me her seal form before things got too serious between us.<br /> <br /> She was obviously in pain; she was sharing something which was both meaningful and devastating to her. I felt like I should reciprocate, so I told her a little about Missy and Jane, and about the contest, and about how I left them behind when I won my freedom. It still hurts to talk about it\u2026 I broke my solemn promise to my two closest friends and abandoned them to their captivity. Like most of my friends and lovers, Rowan did what she could to assure me that she thought I had done the only thing that I could. It\u2019s remarkable how little that helps.<br /> <br /> Anyway, we\u2019ve been sitting out here on the ocean for an hour or so now, nibbling on sandwiches (I know we just had breakfast, but it\u2019s amazing how much of an appetite sailing can work up) and talking pleasantly about little things. But mostly we\u2019ve just been relaxing and enjoying each other\u2019s company. I\u2019ve been writing in this journal in fits and spurts as we talk, which under other circumstances might seem rude, but Rowan doesn\u2019t seem to mind.<br /> <br /> Am I falling for this girl? No. Not yet, at any rate. We\u2019ve been together twice, and we\u2019ve only known each other for a week or two. Even with D, it took me longer than that to realize the depth of my attraction. But Rowan is so earnest and honest and vulnerable that I find myself wanting to please her, to protect her, and to reassure her that my attraction is genuine. Whether that will be enough to build on in the long run, who can say?<br /> <br /> Although with the way she\u2019s looking at me right now, I\u2019m starting to think I\u2019d better answer that question pretty damned soon. She\u2019s already got it bad, and if there isn\u2019t a future between us, I should probably break things off before she gets too attached. I don\u2019t want to hurt her any more than is absolutely necessary.<br /> <b><br /> Lorelei Grace</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T13:02:11-07:00","id":950706,"title":"","content":"<b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> Friday, November 20th<br /> Nine years, seven months, one day<br /> Days without stabbing: 2<br /> <br /> Well, this morning certainly went better than yesterday. Not being at least mildly surprised that I woke up at all helped. I managed to wake up before the alarm and just laid there watching Gawain sleep and tracing the filigree on his armor lightly. He loves me so much. He treats me so well. He needs me as much as I need him. So why do I insist on doing stupid shit? I don't want to die. I don't. But if that's true then why do I keep trying so fucking hard to? I fight like a madwoman, reckless and careless. When I straight up told Leanne she could do anything she wanted to with me so long as she didn't kill me she refused to agree and I still fucking went home with her. Why do I do this to myself? More importantly, why do I do this to the people who love me?<br /> <br /> And they do. We're family. I could see it yesterday in their eyes as one by one they all expressed their outrage at how close Leanne had come to killing me. They're worried about me and I can't blame them. Hell, I'm worried about me right now. <br /> <br /> Jacob was not pleased in the least to see me drag myself in half dead yesterday morning. Thank goodness Desiree was awake and healed me before the others actually saw me looking that rough. As it was, Jacob did have some things to say about it during the trip to and from therapy. I think he was making a determined effort not to straight up lecture me but he was concerned and upset and bothered by my behavior. Of all of them, I really think he's prepared to stop me from seeing her again whether I want him to or not. I don't want it to come to that but right now I don't know that I can trust myself not to crawl back to Leanne's feet if she crooks her magic finger at me.<br /> <br /> And it's not her. I don't trust her. I don't love her. But she's got what I crave and now she knows it. She's not my girlfriend or domme or anything like that. She's my dealer. First one's free, only time will tell what the next one costs me. Except there isn't going to be a next time. I am not going to do that again. Not with her. Not with the Handmaidens. Not with the Warlock of Night. I cannot trust myself with leachfingers and I sure as fuck don't trust any of them to have such absolute power of me. Maybe DLR but that is not her thing and not our dynamic and way too much like who she was in Arcadia so that isn't going to happen. Hell, I don't want to be that vulnerable and helpless again with anyone, not even Gawain or Becky. I don't want to crave that cold touch... But I do. I do want to have my guilt and my will sucked away. To just not fight and be a good little girl who does what she's told and not be responsible for the pain and harm I always seem to cause. <br /> <br /> But that's a lie. A pretty and seductive lie but still a lie. Going home with Leanne hurt Gawain. It hurt Jacob and Lori and everyone who cares about me. If she'd killed me, they would have hunted her down. And given that she is under Charlotte\u2019s personal protection that would have ended badly for them all. I made a choice and it was a bad one and those consequences are on me. If you stick your head in the lion's mouth you're not blameless when it fucking bites you. It would be easy to say I couldn't help myself but I am not completely helpless. I knew it was a stupid and reckless and dangerous thing to do and I did it anyway. Actions have consequences. Twitch choose to trade his integrity and humanity for promises of safety. When (not if) he pays for torturing his fellow Changelings it will be on his head. Grey choose to operate the Table for Darke and his death is on him. I choose to put him down like the soulless monster he was before he could harm my motley and the binding punishment I'm under as a result is my own damned fault. Weakness is not an excuse. Fear is not an excuse. Anger is not an excuse. <br /> <br /> But where she is concerned, I have been weak and I fear I may be again. And if I don't woman the hell up and reign myself in it is going to end badly and it is going to be my fucking fault. <br /> <br /> I am fucking stronger than this shit. I am Calamity. I am the terrible misfortune that befalls for the wicked in the dark. I am the fucking predator not the prey. I escaped Them. I fucking CUT Them. I tasted Their blood. It was cold and bitter and sharp as razors going down my throat. I freed myself from Them. I never became Their good little girl and I sure as fuck am not going to roll over for some pale imitation of Them. I'm not. I won't. <br /> <br /> I promised Gawain he wouldn't lose me yesterday and I fucking intend to keep that promise. Maybe there is something broken inside me that makes me not care if I live or die sometimes but he does and I care about him. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Well, Calamity came back to us this morning. That is the good news. She came back in less than stellar health. That is the not so good news. She said that Leanne healed her as much as she could, but she still looked bad. Desiree came by and commented that Calamity looked like shit and was just as upset as I was that she was still hurt. She healed Calamity the rest of the way. Once my motley mate was back up to where she should be we split up to get dressed and go to therapy. On the way there, and some on the way back I talked to Calamity about my concerns with her coming back hurt from Leanne\u2019s place. If Leanne healed her as much as she could and Calamity was still that bad off, I\u2019m afraid of how close to death my friend was last night. I tried to express my worries without being too confrontational about it. I was upset that Calamity had chosen to go home with Leanne, but I know that my friend sometimes has something of a self-destructive streak to her. I don\u2019t know if she consciously realizes what kinds of situations she puts herself in. She did admit that she knew that going with Leanne was a bad Idea and that she shouldn\u2019t have done it. She also admitted that she has issues that she needs to work on. I told her that I understood why she might want to go with Leanne, but again expressed my worry for her heath. Calamity tried to reassure me that Leanne did everything she could to heal her, but she ran out of glamour. I told Calamity that was why Leanne was still breathing. If she had hurt Calamity to the point she died or if she had not healed her then I would be hunting down a leechfinger and taking her to task. <br /> <br /> When we got back from therapy Calamity tried to act like everything was normal, but I think she put too much work into the \u201cnormal act\u201d and people got suspicious. It eventually came out that she came back from Leanne\u2019s place still hurt, and that Leanne had run out of glamour healing her. To say that the others were upset would be an understatement. The others were rather worried and a bit angry and made their feelings known. Several people mentioned how dangerous Leanne can be, and Calamity admitted to the group that she shouldn\u2019t have gone and will try not to go with her again in the future. I\u2019m not sure just how much I can trust her to stick to that. Whatever is driving Calamity to be punished is strong. She obviously is turned on by the danger that Leanne represents. I have no idea how to help her get over that, so the best I can do is to keep an eye on her and make sure that she doesn\u2019t go home with Leanne in the future. It will be annoying, much like cutting someone off at the bar, but I\u2019ll take the frustrated looks or sore feelings if it will keep Calamity safe. Luna mirrored my statement that if Leanne hurt Calamity again then she would take out her anger on the leechfinger. That\u2019s the polite way of saying that she\u2019d kill her. Calamity admitted that I had expressed the same sentiment. Luna seemed pleased with that.<br /> <br /> Also during this whole affair Desiree warned Calamity to be careful with Leanne and to be wary around her. She said that Leanne is just as good at manipulating people as she was when she worked for the Director. She used to get people to do whatever she wanted by getting them so caught up in her that they were wrapped around her little finger. She probably still could, by her own admission, but she said she won\u2019t. She was concerned that Leanne was doing something similar with Calamity and that our manager wasn\u2019t seeing it clearly. I don\u2019t know Leanne nearly well enough to make speculations like that, but I do know that she is dangerous and I don\u2019t trust her as far as I could throw her.<br /> <br /> After all of that was talked out Insincere Marguerite asked me if I\u2019d be present while she had a conversation with Felicity when she arrived. I said sure and didn\u2019t have too long to wait before the Day courtier got here. Felicity, Marguerite and I went to a private room to have that discussion. Insincere Marguerite\u2019s main purpose in inviting Felicity over today was to ask her about Rowan and if she knows anything about the Selkie\u2019s motivations towards Lori. Felicity said that she had never seen any indication of Rowan going after girls before, but didn\u2019t think there was anything behind it. She said that Rowan currently lives on the beach in a cabin, works as a lifeguard and owns a boat. The only thing that she did mention was that Rowan\u2019s house felt odd. Not bad, just odd. She also said that she would talk to some people and see what she can find out regarding our frequent Selkie guest.<br /> <br /> Throughout this entire conversation Insincere Marguerite and Felicity were going back and forth with the flirting and comments. Felicity would say that she hated Marguerite, but then pull her into a passionate kiss. The whole conversation went back and forth that way. It was the most sexually charged conversation I\u2019ve ever been witness to. It seems that they both are fascinated by the other, but don\u2019t really like each other. I don\u2019t understand it personally. I am generally not attracted to people that I can\u2019t stand, no matter how pretty they are. I know others are, and these two definitely were in this case. I don\u2019t think they\u2019d be good for each other, but didn\u2019t feel it was my place to interrupt their conversation to tell them that. I may see about having a conversation with just Marguerite about Felicity, but am not sure how to bring that up. I don\u2019t want to seem like I\u2019m worrying about her choice of potential partners overly much. It might be a little too close to the whole situation with Chalcedony. Granted Marguerite was much more submissive with Chalcedony than she was with Felicity, but I definitely still thought there was an unhealthy attraction in both there. I\u2019m not keen on what I saw between Felicity and Insincere Marguerite either, but will have to approach it in a more delicate way.<br /> <br /> One interesting thing was that as Felicity was leaving Desiree leaned against the doorframe and watched as the other woman left. Desiree was acting more than a little intimidating and seemed pleased to watch Felicity leave. I\u2019m not sure what\u2019s going on between those two, but Desiree does not like Felicity. <br /> <br /> After Felicity left Juan Carlos and Moon came by to talk to us about Chalcedony. They have finally cleared out all the programming in her mind that was left by the Director. They are still unsure of her true intentions though. She could be a willing Loyalist like I was, or she could have just been following her programming. Apparently the monarchs had a meeting about Chalcedony and could not come to a consensus on what to do with her. Some people wanted to get rid of the threat altogether by killing her or exiling her. Queen Charlotte was adamant that Chalcedony be set free and be allowed to continue living in the freehold. And since she\u2019s the one currently in charge, she got her way. Chalcedony was supposed to be released about thirty minutes after our conversation with Juan Carlos and Moon started. They also warned us that Chalcedony was not particularly happy with some members of our motley. Specifically, Gawain, Calamity and Insincere Marguerite. At least as far as they could tell from her dreamscape she was unhappy with those three. It is also highly likely that Chalcedony will be watched when she leaves to make sure that she\u2019s not up to anything.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite in particular was upset by the response to the decision regarding Chalcedony, and left the room to compose herself. I don\u2019t think that she liked the fact that some of the monarchs were leaning toward a more permanent solution to the \u201cChalcedony problem.\u201d Nor was she pleased with the fact that Chalcedony seems to be upset with her in particular. That fact likely brings back unpleasant memories for her. And just when she was starting to move past all of that. After Marguerite left the room Julia came in looking for her sweetheart. We directed her to where Insincere Marguerite had gone and she went in that direction.<br /> <br /> Later but still before the show Desiree and Gloria, who had been playful all through breakfast, started asking if anyone wanted to join them to go see Mockingjay this evening before the show is over. Calamity and Gawain seemed interested, as did Luna. I could not leave since I will still need to be working but I did not mind Luna going to see the movie. Desiree and Gloria were going to go and get tickets earlier in the day to make sure that they could all get in. It\u2019s opening night for the movie so it\u2019s likely to be exceedingly busy. Part of me is glad that I could not make the show. A crowd of people that big might be a little hard for me to handle.<br /> <br /> The show was interesting, and mostly seemed to focus on TJ and Rowan. Unrelated to the rest of what happened, Rowan dropped off some flowers for Lori at the bar. I made sure that Lori got them in a timely fashion. After that Rowan went to go sit at what has become her usual seat and found it already occupied by TJ. He was sitting there with his feet up and looking smug and more than a little intimidating. So Rowan went to go sit elsewhere, but TJ kept watching her and intimidating her. At some point during the evening Gawain read TJ\u2019s intentions and found out that the man wants to scare Rowan, but has no plans at all to actually harm her. He just wants her to feel unsafe while she is here. Calamity decided to go over to the man and have a chat with him. I don\u2019t know exactly what was said but I\u2019m assuming she was confronting him about intimidating people in a neutral location. I have doubts that TJ will stop his scare tactics though. He seems to be a rather persistent individual.<br /> <br /> Also on the job intimidating people was De La Rocha, leaning against the wall, watching Leanne and cracking her knuckles. I am not really against this particular campaign since I do not trust Leanne, and she hurt my friend. I know from Calamity that Leanne is still afraid of the Grand Maw, and getting eaten by Queen Charlotte. So she\u2019s staying in town because she\u2019s afraid of being eaten by something in her home town, and now she\u2019s in a new place and is still afraid of being eaten by someone local. I might feel bad for her if she hadn\u2019t done what she did to Calamity and will likely do again to her or someone else. There is also the matter that she has rather quickly become the lover of the currently reigning monarch of the freehold. If that\u2019s not suspicious I don\u2019t know what is. <br /> <br /> While I was tending bar Molly came by to talk. She admitted to me that she has been tasked with watching Chalcedony, but she is conflicted about the task. She doesn\u2019t really want to watch her, but she\u2019s curious about her and I think she\u2019s going to go ahead and do her assigned task. I didn\u2019t really have any good advice for her. I suggested trying to remain objective so her perceptions will not be skewed. I\u2019m not sure how successful she will be, but didn\u2019t want to suggest that she opt out of the job since it\u2019s her first assignment since going back to work.<br /> <br /> Everything that happened tonight has brought up questions. Not that the questions weren\u2019t there before, but still. So many people have been fleeing Hollywood. We know why. The Grand Maw. A lot of people know about it and are fleeing the city for fear that they will be fed to it next. So they come here. Most of the people who have fled here have, since arriving, worked on ingratiating themselves with local individuals. Some of the new arrivals have made plays with monarchs, Leanne for example. Others like Rowan are going for local celebrities like Lori. Lori may not be famous in the city, but she is definitely well known in the freehold and has the ear of the Spring monarch. Even Gloria has made connections with Desiree and the rest of the motley. I don\u2019t think Gloria has an ulterior motive, but I\u2019m not so sure about the rest. Rowan seems sweet and innocent, but then so could I when I really wanted to. I lured many an unsuspecting fool to death or worse because I could appear to be just a nice, innocent guy that wanted to help. Who knows, it might not be an act with Rowan. She might be what she appears to be, but I\u2019m a cynic. I don\u2019t trust people easily, and have life experience that backs up my paranoia. I will continue to keep an eye on Rowan and Leanne.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Rowan and Lori came back to the Dream House in time for breakfast. They were already in the kitchen when the rest of us came downstairs, holding hands and laughing. They seemed to be having a good time of it. Gloria and De la Rocha came in together as well. Everyone is paired up it seems. Desiree was not here for breakfast but Gloria said that she will be back later in the day. Anyway, Gawain made Belgium waffles for breakfast and there was a big conversation about waffles in general. Apparently there are different kinds of waffles all over the place and Gawain started researching it on his phone. I think he plans on making different kinds of waffles for breakfast for the next several days. Sounds good to me. There was also talk about intimate encounters with waffle irons. I think Calamity meant something not sexual with that statement, but that\u2019s how everyone took it. It was kind of disturbing and I tuned out most of the conversation. <br /> <br /> While at breakfast Lori told the group that she would be going out on a boat with Rowan this afternoon. This was greeted with some amount of trepidation, but we all told her that we hoped she had fun. It was almost like a daughter telling her dad where she was going to be, but in this case it was the whole lot of us. I got the impression that the rest of the motley are still not so sure about Rowan\u2019s intentions but were willing to extend some amount of trust that she won\u2019t do anything to our singer while they\u2019re out sailing. <br /> <br /> After all of that people split up to do their own things, and Luna and I decided to go for a drive. I know some of the more scenic areas near here and thought that it might be fun to just be with nature for an afternoon. Next time I\u2019ll suggest we go for a hike. Maybe I can suggest it to the group as a whole and see if anyone is interested in going for a day hike and having a picnic lunch. I know Luna is more comfortable with fewer people around. I mean, there\u2019s a reason why she doesn\u2019t hang out at the Dream House on weekends and that\u2019s entirely to do with the sheer size of the crowds. Plus, she lives in a cabin in the woods. I bet she\u2019d like the idea of a hike. I just need to sell it to the others. <br /> <br /> While we were out Molly called. She sounded upset. She started off the conversation by asking when the bar opened. I knew that wasn\u2019t a good sign. I let her know when we opened, and asked what was wrong. She said that she had been following Chalcedony but that she messed up and now Dahlia is watching Chalcedony. I have an idea of what happened, but will wait until Molly actually tells me what happened before I try and come up with any solutions. I invited Molly to come by later, when the bar opens, and promised that I\u2019d hear her out and see if there was anything I could do to help. Luna even offered to stay and see what she could do. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> My life it is good, but perhaps getting a bit out of hand? The past day or so has had some drama.<br /> <br /> So Lorelei. I adore her. I love her deeply. Last night was wonderful and intense. Today however was for shifting focus to Julia for the day. Apparently my happy return to closeness to Lorelei has made her nervous about us, so I attempted to set that right. Breakfast both yesterday and today I spent in her lap (apart from her trying to climb in mine) and played with her hair. She really enjoyed that. By that I mean not that she was turned on (really, both were quite sated from the night before) but it was fond, as I played the peek-a-boo with it, and made her keep smiling. For my part, I enjoyed the smell, and feel of her face. Also the smell of her neck. Julia just smells good. And giggles daintily.<br /> <br /> All was not completely well at breakfast. Calamity let it slip, probably deliberately, that Leanne had caused her great injury from draining her life, and that she and Desiree had to combine their healing abilities to get her on a more even keel. A number of us really came down on that though Gawain showed admirable self-control.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Desiree and Gloria\u2019s friendship is blossoming. They had matching pajamas and hats. They were adorable \u201cmenacing\u201d each other with tickling and pink lemonade. I hope I contributed to this. I think so.<br /> <br /> We split up, and I recruited Jacob to meet with Felicity with me. Lorelei was practicing an act with Calamity, Maria was watching her and Julia chose to paint and avoid Felicity completely. Of course, Julia was not, as it turned out, my main worry. After the visit, Desiree confronted her aggressively. I had forgotten how much they disliked each other. I confronted Desiree after, but to say she was unrepentant would be an understatement. She <u>hates</u> Felicity. Apparently since she has come back fully into herself, she has come to loathe Felicity even more.<br /> <br /> Now, back with Felicity, she did not know much about Rowan. Nothing especially troublesome, beyond feeling her house was off-puttingly archetypical. That, and that she was upset that I threw in my lot with the Autumn Court. However, our conversation devolved into kissing, as neither of us could really keep our hands, or mouths, off each other. She told me she hated me then kissed me. It was\u2026strange. We left while we each still had our clothes on, barely, only to have her confronted by Desiree.<br /> <br /> Despite being annoyed with Desiree, I was still in a good mood, and had gone upstairs to join Julia when I got word Juan-Carlos and Moon had arrived. They were awaking Chalcedony, after deprogramming her and examining her mind. Unfortunately, there was no determining for certain if she is a Loyalist or not. Some evidence suggested both ways. I do not think she is, but I am aware I could be mistaken. The monarchs fought over her, some even wanting to euthanize her, but Queen Charlotte got angry and declared she would be woken up and that, well, she is High Queen and had possession of her.<br /> <br /> We also discovered Chalcedony is angry with us, including me. It felt like a dagger in the heart. I was overcome. When Juan-Carlos and Moon left, I retreated to the vents; Lorelei had stood by me and held my hand, and I admit made me feel better. Julia, who had not been in the room, also came to me. We talked briefly, but I needed to sleep in the tight, encompassing vent to break the intense feelings of sorrow and anger. <br /> <br /> I wonder if she hates Felicity or Chalcedony more right now.<br /> <br /> The show went smooth. Calamity, Gawain, Desiree, Gloria, and Luna went to see a movie, though Calamity and Gawain were there for the beginning. Maria helped with security and seemed pleased about it. Lorelei was wonderful. I am given to understand Molly will be shadowing Chalcedony overnight. Also Jolie was at the show. Lorelei wound up going home with Rowan, Maria with Gloria. I think Desiree may have met up with Jolie, she asked permission and did not spend the night at the Dream House.<br /> <br /> When everyone left, I asked Julia to meet I on the stage. I put a few lights down, and started a series of tracks before throwing on a suit jacket over my tee shirt and coming down. In the pale spotlight, we slow danced. Sometimes we whispered or murmured, but we felt each other\u2019s warmth as we slowly swayed on stage. Julia would never have gotten on stage in front of everyone and danced, but in the cavernous empty room our swaying was the only movement. Under a series of romantic songs, our whispers were the sounds. She whispered her hopes, her fears. About having my children. About losing me. About marrying me. About shattering our quad with her jealousy. I held her, even when she wept. Even when she wept, we danced.<br /> <br /> Eventually, we could not continue, but did not want to leave and end the magic moment, the still fragile eternity. I fetched a blanket from the catwalks and put it over us, and we slept on stage, I curled up in her arms, music continuing to play. Blissfully. <br /> <br /> Breakfast came too early, and we came in in our clothes and make-up from last night. Julia tried sitting in my lap but while adorable it was ineffective. Breakfast was sedate. Rowan was there, Desiree was not, and everyone seemed more relaxed that the previous night. Lori was going sailing with Rowan, and Luna was going out with Jacob. We decided to head to the attic.<br /> <br /> There is so much going on. Lorelei\u2026Juliette\u2026made me really upset, and doubt myself, but she has really gone out of her way to make love and shower I with kindness. I feel much, much better about things with her. Maria was never a big issue; she is pretty laid back compared to any of us with romance (and nothing else) but even she tried to support I. Julia has been more difficult. She admitted yesterday morning she gets jealous; her other two partners are usually immune due to the nature of our relationship. I think things will work if we stay open with each other. After last night, though, she is so in love with me, and it feels wonderful.<br /> <br /> Felicity and Chalcedony are awkward. Julia hates them both. I don\u2019t like Felicity per se, but there are few that make me burn with desire quite like she does. The feeling is mutual. If we don\u2019t destroy each other we could have quite the passionate affair. But I won\u2019t let it cost me Julia\u2019s love. I think Felicity is as confused as I am. As for Chalcedony, I fear Calamity ruined that forever.<br /> <br /> At least Desiree and Flores are fairly trouble free. Unlike the above two I am involved, it is not just a tension. Though it is not the quad of truehearts, I enjoy the passions we share. We have not spent time with Flores alone in a while. Truly, we should remedy that.<br /> <br /> Now, Julia wants to sketch the face she said she saw gazing at her last night as we danced, and I learned a Spring Court trick from Lorelei to pour my glamour into inspiration. Julia always called me her muse. Now I show my love what a muse I can be.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXII</i><br /> <br /> Desiree was going down to use her Spring contracts to cure Gloria\u2019s hangover and bring her orange juice when she met the Jacob and Calamity coming in. During the morning Desire and Gloria were notable for their matching Calvin and Hobbes Pajamas. <br /> <br /> We looked it up and apparently <u>Mockingjay</u> did come out the day some of the group went for the midnight show<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite picked up the first level of Verdant Spring, hence the last paragraph. <br /> <br /> That\u2019s all that comes to mind. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T14:15:57-07:00","id":951311,"title":"","content":"The mortal seeking Lori's attention made me wonder. Has Lori been with a mortal since coming back as a changeling?<br /> <br /> Also, Lori on the boat caused me to imagine at the end of a rope, wings out, doing a kite thing. Not quite full flight, but maybe an acceptable facsimile?<br /> <br /> Jacob may be paranoid, but he makes an interesting point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T15:36:08-07:00","id":951346,"title":"","content":"Omenseer: Lori has been with mortals since her return from Arcadia, though none of note in the scope of the campaign to date. Her early journal entries referenced brief torrid affairs with various mortals who were pretty much never mentioned again. That was how she liked things at that time; her philosophy was that she could stoke a mortal's desires to their highest level by giving them a taste, and then leaving them wanting more. Of course, her relationship with de la Rocha (and her later relationships with Marguerite, Julia, Oleander, Rowan, Joan, and Andromeda) have sort of put paid to that philosophy... she's decided that she <i>likes</i> getting involved long-term now.<br /> <br /> The &quot;parasailing&quot; idea is interesting... not sure how well it would work in practice with someone like Lori, though. :-)<br /> <br /> And yes, Jacob is paranoid. Seems to Lori that everyone is paranoid lately. She's not sure why nobody trusts her new girlfriend... Rowan is really sweet once you get past the shyness. And I'm sure there's absolutely nothing suspicious or incriminating about her at all...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T16:22:52-07:00","id":951363,"title":"","content":"I'd allow the parasailing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T13:30:57-07:00","id":959412,"title":"","content":"Like sand through he hourglass\u2026<br /> <i><br /> Session LXIII</i><br /> <b><br /> Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> November 22nd, afternoon<br /> <br /> Well, I still haven\u2019t found the guy. To be fair, I did get kinda frustrated and wander off to watch Calamity practice her new routine. I really need to get the other\u2019s help - I just hate to, you know, pull them into my wild goose chase all about me, you know? Anyway, the afternoon went pretty slow.<br /> <br /> Gloria did come by and ask us about Desiree. The two are thinking about getting an apartment together and forming a motley, and that\u2019s a big step, you know, after the kinda betrayal that went down between them. I really do think Desiree\u2019s turned over a new leaf though, and really wants her friend back, so I hope it works out. Calamity agreed with me, about Desiree at least. I hope it works out for them - I mean, I\u2019ll be a little sad if they move out, but it\u2019ll be good for them.<br /> <br /> The show last night went well. Calamity did the really spooky version of that old Little Red Riding Hood song that was just awesome. Desiree performed too, and she was pretty great. Lori was... whew. She was something else. It certainly got Joan riled up. Kinda obviously too - I think Desiree was liking the term eye-fucking. I hope Molly got some good material from the conversation between Lori and Joan. She was trying to, you know, figure out how to be suave and stuff.<br /> <br /> But I\u2019m getting a little out of order. Molly was there cause she, you know, wanted advice about Chalcedony. She\u2019d gotten herself pulled off shadowing the blue girl cause she got spotted after getting \u2018captivated\u2019 by Chalcedony. They\u2019d had a conversation even - Molly gave this big romantic speech about falling into her eyes and losing track of what was going on, but it also meant she didn\u2019t remember what they\u2019d talked about, so she didn\u2019t know how to, you know, have a second conversation.<br /> <br /> I told her she should say the eyes thing to explain. I mean, it was like something from a troubadour\u2019s song, so it\u2019s bound to work, right? I guess you know, me from the future. Hopefully. Anyways, Jacob, Calamity and Desiree all disapproved though. Calamity and Jacob were all about not trusting whether she\u2019s, you know, a loyalist or something. I mean, it\u2019s fair, I guess, but for one, Molly\u2019s not really built for blind trust and for two, treating her like a pariah isn\u2019t the way to make this world more of a home than the Director\u2019s realm.<br /> <br /> Desiree didn\u2019t like it either, but more cause she didn\u2019t like Chalcedony when they were both in Arcadia. She was pretty, you know, cutthroat, I guess, according to Desiree. That\u2019s a different situation though. I mean, it was in Arcadia, and even if she is a jerk for real, people can change and all, and, well, even jerks aren\u2019t always all bad. I don\u2019t remember her being a jerk. Anyways, it\u2019s Molly\u2019s choice to make.<br /> <br /> Hailey was also... helping? She\u2019s a little, you know, bitter about girls and relationships, since that whole deal with Monica and Dominika. I tried to cheer her up some but... she\u2019s not doing great. I dunno what I can do to help, so for now, I\u2019ve got silly stories.<br /> <br /> Lori and Calamity were doing their usual rounds. I was mostly focused on Molly and Hailey, but I did notice when Calamity came back from talking to Madame Spidertoes. She wanted a drink and drank it fast. Apparently, Madame Spidertoes gets, you know, intimidating when she\u2019s upset. And she did not like that Leanne almost killed Calamity. Which is good all around. I hope.<br /> <br /> After the show, I went to go tell Desiree she did well. We talked for a bit - we discussed Molly and Chalcedony and she explained that TJ was an ass because he had low self esteem. Her whole thing there made sense, but I still don\u2019t like him. I guess I do maybe feel a little bad for him though, if she\u2019s right, but not when he\u2019s menacing guests in my house. Anyways, TJ is still an ass and Desiree is amazing, so we stopped talking about him and I picked her and Calamity up instead. Literally, of course. It was a pretty damn good night.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t wanna get out of bed this morning, but it was waffle experiment week, so I had to eventually, you know? I\u2019d ordered some pearl sugar and it had arrived, so I went with Liege waffles first. They worked out perfect. The cinnamon ones were my favorite.<br /> <br /> White Maria was there and let us know not to panic if she wasn\u2019t here for Thanksgiving. Here at the show, of course. I mean, she has been here for, you know, pretty much every show, so we might have gotten a little worried. We wound up deciding to close for the holiday, since Lori, Insincere Marguerite, Julia and De la Roche are gonna be gone to Julia\u2019s and all. Plus, we decided to throw a feast for the Changelings that didn\u2019t have families to visit. It\u2019s gonna be epic - a big fryer, cranberry sauce, sweet potatoes, and everything. I can\u2019t wait! <br /> <br /> <b><br /> Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Well, it\u2019s been a fun couple of days. The last time I wrote I was on Rowan\u2019s sailboat, enjoying the sun and the wind and the smell of the ocean, and while the day and a half that have elapsed since then have been more eventful, I still have that blissful feeling of peace that seemed to settle over me while the two of us skimmed across the waves.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately duty called, and after a few hours we had to make our way back to the dock. We tied up and covered her yacht (and yes, apparently even little sailboats like that one are referred to as \u201cyachts\u201d if they\u2019re privately owned), and she sort of nervously kissed me goodbye in the parking lot. She knew that I was going to spend that night with D, of course, and I think she was trying to give me a little space, because she told me she would see me in a few days. It\u2019s kind of cute to watch her hem and haw and worry about whether or not she\u2019s smothering me with her attention.<br /> <br /> I met up with Calamity for a bit after I returned to the Dream House, and the two of us worked some more on the \u201cBloody Creature Poster Girl\u201d number we\u2019ve been developing together. I think it\u2019s coming along very well, and we should have a show-worthy act put together by next weekend. Calamity is anxious to debut it next Saturday, and I think we\u2019re pretty much on point for that. She\u2019s got a natural talent for dancing, and \u2013 as much as I might hate to admit it \u2013 Annika\u2019s tutelage has really helped that talent to blossom.<br /> <br /> Gloria approached us as we were practicing, and when we hit a lull, she asked if she could talk to us. \u201cSure thing,\u201d I said brightly, \u201cwhat\u2019s on your mind?\u201d<br /> <br /> Gloria was a little hesitant, but after a few seconds she told us that she and Desiree were considering getting an apartment together\u2026 and maybe starting a motley of their own. She wanted to make sure she got everyone\u2019s opinions on whether