 Tension. I am glad it is gripping to you as well. This game has a major drama/supernatural romance element, and that is needed to keep it interesting.<br /> <br /> Jacob has a stable love life. Gawain is involved with Calamity and to a lesser degree Desiree, neither of whom are stable. We get a look at what is really going on with Desiree next session, mostly from Jacob and Insincere Marguerite. Luna is, overall, pretty stable herself, unusual back story aside.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I thought for a moment that Gawain's Bertilak persona might make a comeback after Calamity's misadventure with Leanne, but he seemed to remain perfectly in control.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T19:50:56-07:00","id":963056,"title":"","content":"I suspect he was more worried than angry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T16:36:25-07:00","id":963441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroness Nerak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play?p=961959#post961959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have several Jewish NPCs, but it does not come up as much. I will try to have that come out a bit...she is one of three Jewish Changelings in MDH.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T01:16:23-07:00","id":967824,"title":"","content":"\u2026these are the faes of our lives<br /> <i><br /> Session LXIV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> November 23, evening<br /> <br /> Now that was a nice way to spend an afternoon. Not quite what I expected when I went to talk to Lori after breakfast. We had Brussels waffles this time which were a little, you know, crispier. They maybe weren\u2019t perfectly accurate - I didn\u2019t, you know, by a different waffle iron for it and apparently Brussels waffles are usually a slightly different shape - but the ingredient part was right. The powdered sugar worked nice too, but sugar usually does.<br /> <br /> But I\u2019m getting distracted. In between discussing the relative aerodynamics of peoples\u2019 cars - see, Dominika had come by last night to make sure Monica was, you know, still welcome which of course she was, as long as she didn\u2019t threaten people with cars, you know? It was kinda unfortunate she felt she had to ask, but De la Roche said it was probably just cause she felt guilty and all. Anyway, Calamity mentioned something about helping Gloria and Desiree with moving and IKEA furniture and stuff and that got me thinking about wedding presents in a weird sorta free association thought string.<br /> <br /> So once Julia went off to paint Oleander in her business suit church clothes (though assuredly not like on of her French girls) and Calamity snagged Lori for working on their new act, I interrupted just a little to ask if an armoire that could magic up whatever outfit you might need would be an OK wedding present. And by the time I\u2019d said half of it, she was all but doing the little lip trembly, wide eyes, hopeful smile thing and I\u2019d, you know, promised to make her one.<br /> <br /> It took me pretty much all of the afternoon until it was time to get ready for the show. Carpentry is, you know, a kinda new thing for me, but I had a good idea of what to do for the Hedgecrafting part -silken moonlight, the velvet of new growth, finely tanned dragon hide and the clash of metal on metal. It should be fun - I really do like the wavy, weird quality of the whole Hedgecrating process. It\u2019s nice to have a project too.<br /> <br /> The shows went well, the past couple of nights. Calamity rocked it both times, of course. She\u2019s gotten really good, not that, you know, she wasn\u2019t always awesome. We started telling folks about the Thanksgiving feast last night too. Moon, who was totally smooth chatting up Hailey last night, will probably come, to get out of a second awkward Thanksgiving with Shi. Apparently last year he had invited hir to his family gathering, and zie\u2019d realized halfway through that no one there actually knew Shi. He\u2019d just, you know, stalked them enough to be able to talk about all the things they\u2019d done together recently.<br /> <br /> Hailey was pretty shocked that De la Roche was doing Thanksgiving stuff at all. So was Monica actually and even more so that De la Roche went to Disneyland and enjoyed it. That was, you know, more of an amused shock though. She\u2019d showed up tonight - Hailey hadn\u2019t. I guess Dominika coming by yesterday gave her warning, you know? She was pretty bummed, Hailey was, that Monica hadn\u2019t even let her know she was back safe in town.<br /> <br /> I wish there was something I could do to help that whole situation out. I think I managed to not make it worse at least. It did get a little, you know, awkward when she mentioned being a drama factory. I guess it was mostly just still awkward from when I tried not to mention anything about Leanne while sharing gossip.<br /> <br /> Andromeda was also there tonight, sans Joan. And as soon as Lori got down off the stage, Andromeda walked over and kissed her. I guess that\u2019s how they\u2019re dealing with the whole, you know, eye fucking thing? They seemed happy though and she and Lori and De la Roche were talking most of the the night.<br /> <br /> Calamity made her usual rounds, and the unusual one of checking on Insincere Marguerite in the catwalks. She didn\u2019t seem upset going up or coming back down though, so I\u2019m sure it\u2019s alright. She wound up spending a lot of time with Becky, Princess Joli and Desiree - apparently the Princess is going to join us for movie night tomorrow, you know, as Desiree\u2019s date. It should be fun. Maybe I\u2019ll make something special for dinner as well tomorrow. Unless she just really likes takeout...<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> It\u2019s Monday morning, and I haven\u2019t written anything in this diary since Saturday evening just before the show. I wish that I could say that this is due to the fact that I\u2019ve been existing in a state of blissful peace in which nothing worth recording occurred, but sadly this is not the case. The truth is that I\u2019ve had a pretty bad case of the doldrums lately, and haven\u2019t felt much like writing.<br /> <br /> In any case, on Saturday night I went through one of my standard acts, backed up a few of our other headliners, and then made the rounds of the audience as per usual\u2026 well, maybe a little quicker than usual, in truth. Oleander was there, and I quickly sought her out, planted myself firmly in her lap, and draped my arms around her neck. It had been nearly a week since we\u2019d seen each other at that point, and it was clear that we were both hungry for the contact.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ve missed you angel,\u201d she said simply as I leaned up against her shoulder.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ve missed you too, honey.\u201d I murmured the words into her ear, and then chased it with a light kiss.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo I know you need to stick around here for a while,\u201d she said with a twinkle, \u201cbut I was wondering\u2026 are you going to drag me upstairs to your room tonight, or are we heading back to my place?\u201d It\u2019s always kind of a difficult question in Oleander\u2019s case, since I share my room with D and the two of us heading up there would essentially be tantamount to kicking her out to fend for herself.<br /> <br /> \u201cI have church tomorrow morning\u2026\u201d I began.<br /> <br /> Oleander smiled. \u201cMy place is actually closer to your church, you know\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I returned her smile at that. \u201cJust let me pack up some clothes\u2026 I probably shouldn\u2019t wear this to church,\u201d I indicated the low-cut sparkly evening gown I\u2019d donned for my last number.<br /> <br /> Oleander shrugged. \u201cMight give the congregation a thrill,\u201d she opined.<br /> <br /> I laughed a little. \u201cWhy don\u2019t you come upstairs with me? I wanted to talk with you privately about something, and we can take care of that while I pack.\u201d<br /> <br /> She agreed amiably enough, and a few minutes later we headed up to my bedroom. On the way out, Dominika caught my eye and motioned that she wanted to talk to me (and D, and Gawain and Calamity). Turns out she and Monica are back in town (obviously) and were considering stopping by the Dream House the following evening, and Dominika wanted to make sure Monica was still welcome here in the wake of the\u2026 unpleasantness. Of course we assured her that both she and Monica would always be welcome at the Dream House\u2026 but it made me a little sad that she felt she had to ask in the first place. D opined that our friend is just embarrassed about her actions and trying to work through it the only way she knows how.<br /> <br /> In any case, a few minutes later Oleander was sitting on the messily rumpled bed D and I share while I carefully folded up my church clothes and put them in an overnight bag.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo what did you want to talk to me about?\u201d she asked curiously. \u201cNothing dire, I hope\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I shook my head. \u201cIt\u2019s a good thing,\u201d I assured her, \u201cit\u2019s just private. I wanted to tell you because it\u2019s important to me\u2026 and so are you.\u201d<br /> <br /> She blushed furiously, but didn\u2019t say anything.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo, you know the church I go to every Sunday morning?\u201d I asked. She nodded. \u201cWell, I go there \u2013 or at least I <u>started</u> going there \u2013 because the preacher is my father.\u201d<br /> <br /> Oleander took it in stride, though she was obviously surprised. \u201cThat\u2019s\u2026 wow,\u201d she said after a moment.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah,\u201d I replied, \u201cI guess \u2018wow\u2019 pretty much covers it for me, too. The <u>real</u> news is that he now <u>knows</u> I\u2019m his daughter. D and I told him last weekend, and we explained the facts of Changeling existence to him as well. He took it\u2026 much better than I expected.\u201d<br /> <br /> Oleander\u2019s face lit up. \u201cThat\u2019s great, angel,\u201d she said fervently. Then her brow wrinkled a bit. \u201cDoes he know you\u2019re\u2026\u201d she began hesitantly.<br /> <br /> \u201cGay?\u201d I asked, leaving the somewhat open-ended question of my own sexuality aside for the moment. \u201cYeah. I actually told him about that a few months ago. He\u2019s been very supportive.\u201d<br /> <br /> I took a deep breath and put my hands on Oleander\u2019s shoulders. \u201cI\u2019d\u2026 I\u2019d like you to meet him, if you wouldn\u2019t mind joining me at church tomorrow morning,\u201d I said softly. \u201cI haven\u2019t told Dad that I\u2019m polyamorous yet\u2026 though he can be annoyingly perceptive at times. I\u2019ll probably introduce you as a very dear friend. But he\u2019s met D and Marguerite and Julia already, and I want\u2026\u201d I trailed off vaguely and twirled my fingers in the air.<br /> <br /> She leaned in and kissed me gently on the tip of my nose. \u201cI\u2019d love to meet him,\u201d she answered softly.<br /> <br /> We headed back to her place after that and proceeded with our evening together. I\u2019m sure Oleander noticed that I wasn\u2019t quite as bubbly and enthusiastic as usual, but she didn\u2019t say anything, and did her best to make me feel accepted and loved, which was pretty much exactly what I needed. We made love, of course, but mostly we cuddled and kissed and slept.<br /> <br /> Church was once again nerve-wracking but otherwise pleasant. Oleander, like D, put on a suit rather than a dress, and like D, she can really rock that look. I had a brief solo during one of the hymns today, so she got to see me perform in something <u>other</u> than skimpy, spangly clothes, which I\u2019m sure made a nice change. When I introduced her to Dad as a dear friend she was very stiff and formal (I think she was worried about giving too much away, actually), but he took one look at her and greeted her warmly with a firm handshake and kind words. Did he read more into that introduction than I intended to give away? Who can tell\u2026<br /> <br /> We both headed over to the Dream House for breakfast after church. More waffles. \u201cBrussels Waffles,\u201d apparently, which I can only assume are more <u>specific</u> than regular old Belgian waffles. They were tasty, of course, but I hope Gawain works this out of his system soon. Lorelei cannot live on waffles alone (not if she wants to maintain her girlish figure, at any rate).<br /> <br /> Julia sort of tentatively approached me and Oleander and asked if she could talk with us. That surprised me, since she\u2019s been a little distant lately (though she\u2019d obviously been impressed by the sight of Oleander in a suit). Turns out she wanted to offer to paint a portrait of Oleander for me, since she\u2019s already painted all of my other girlfriends. I was so touched by the offer that I had to gather myself for a few moments before I could answer. Oleander looked at me questioningly, and I was eventually able to mutter out that I\u2019d love to have a portrait if she was willing.<br /> <br /> The two of them went off to make plans. I think they were originally going to set something up for Tuesday, but as Oleander had the time right then, they got started immediately instead. Gawain approached me as they left to ask for my opinion on an idea he had for a wedding present (whether for Joan and Andromeda or for Marguerite and Julia, I\u2019m not sure). He described a Hedge-crafted armoire which could produce tailored outfits on demand, and started going on about the esoteric ingredients he wanted to include, like moonlight and the velvet from new leaves and such. <br /> <br /> I confess that my mind got sort of hazy as I considered the possibilities inherent in such a treasure. \u201cMy birthday\u2019s in February,\u201d I said nonchalantly when he paused. I\u2019d intended it as a joke, but he got this sort of goofy grin on his face and asked if that was the sort of thing that I might enjoy having myself, and I just couldn\u2019t turn him down.<br /> <br /> I spent most of the early afternoon rehearsing with Calamity, working out new steps and moves for our \u201cBloody Creature Poster Girl\u201d number, which is shaping up nicely. I think we should have it as close to perfect as anyone could reasonably expect by its debut next Saturday. I\u2019d sort of absently noted that Jacob and Marguerite had left earlier, but actually called a halt to our rehearsal when they got back, as Marguerite was looking unusually grave. She asked if she could speak with me, and of course I agreed.<br /> <br /> It turns out that the two of them had been to visit Felicity. Jacob had once again agreed to act as \u201cchaperone\u201d for Marguerite, for which I\u2019m grateful, even if it doesn\u2019t seem strictly necessary anymore. This visit was not romantic in nature, however\u2026 Marguerite had wanted to ask Felicity about Rowan since they\u2019re both Day Court. And while our neighbor didn\u2019t know much about my newest admirer\u2026 she did have a few concerns about her house.<br /> <br /> Yeah, that\u2019s right, her <u>house</u> is the concerning issue.<br /> <br /> Turns out there\u2019s no record of the house ever having been bought or sold\u2026 or built for that matter. It seems like it\u2019s always been there. There are no records of any major renovations or repairs. The house\u2019s owner and sole long-term occupant has always been a single woman for as far back as the records go, which is more than a century now. And Marguerite said that Felicity reported a strange feeling of being watched while she was in Rowan\u2019s house.<br /> <br /> What could this mean? Is the house itself some sort of supernatural creature, like a Gentry or a Hedge Beast? Could this be some sort of haunting? I tried to remain calm as I asked what they thought I should do. I got my phone out, thinking that I should call Rowan to warn her of this potential danger, but Marguerite stopped me. \u201cIf she is in her house when you call\u2026 something might be listening,\u201d she said delicately. \u201cFelicity has already offered to approach her at work tomorrow, to see if she has more information.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe shouldn\u2019t go back there,\u201d I insisted. \u201cIf it\u2019s dangerous\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt has done nothing to hurt her in two years,\u201d Marguerite soothed. \u201cFelicity has offered to allow Rowan to stay with her if she likes.\u201d<br /> <br /> I chewed on my bottom lip for a minute. Rowan is <u>my</u> kinda-girlfriend, so I really feel like I should be the one to put her up if her house becomes inhospitable. But on the other hand, I don\u2019t want to tip our hand early if there\u2019s anything we can do to rectify this situation. And besides, guest rooms at the Dream House are running short, and I don\u2019t want to just cavalierly invite her to join me and D in our bedroom.<br /> <br /> I mean, if she would be into that, sure, but\u2026<br /> <br /> In the end, I decided to sit on this information for now. I\u2019m still really worried about my poor selkie, I admit, but I\u2019m not sure what I can do about it until we have more information. I\u2019d resolved to try to subtly tempt her into staying with me that night if she\u2019d turned up for the show\u2026 but she didn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> Calamity and I mutually declared the rehearsal over after that, and I headed up to see what Oleander and Julia were up to. It looked like Julia had just about finished her rough sketch, and Oleander was sitting off to one side relaxing. I walked over to her and leaned up against her shoulder, worried and distressed and still a little depressed for no reason I could easily describe.<br /> <br /> My honey picked up on it immediately (Oleander, I mean\u2026 Julia was engrossed in her art). \u201cWhat\u2019s wrong, angel?\u201d she asked in a whisper.<br /> <br /> Not wanting to disturb Julia, I led her back to my bedroom. \u201cI want to ask you something serious, sweetheart,\u201d I said after a moment. She raised an eyebrow, silently giving me the go-ahead to continue. \u201cDo you like me?\u201d I asked when I couldn\u2019t think of any other way to put it.<br /> <br /> She took my hand in hers. \u201cWhat kind of a question is that?\u201d she asked softly.<br /> <br /> \u201cI know you love me,\u201d I explained hastily. \u201cI don\u2019t doubt that for a second, I promise. But do you <u>like</u> me? I mean\u2026 I\u2019ve been thinking about this a lot recently. What do people see when they look at me? I\u2019m pretty, because I was <u>made</u> to be pretty. I\u2019m a good singer\u2026 but again, some of that is because of what was done to me. And I have so many lovers that I\u2019m actually having difficulty scheduling time to be with all of them. But is that all I am? Take away the singing and the sex, and\u2026 is there anything left?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLori,\u201d she said, squeezing my hand, \u201cI want you to listen to me, okay? You\u2019re a good person\u2026 one of the kindest people I know. You make things better just by being there. I\u2019m not explaining this well, but\u2026 I like the person I am when I\u2019m around you. You\u2019ve changed me for the better. When other people talk about me, they say that I\u2019m cold and distant and a little creepy. You don\u2019t agree with that description of me because I\u2019m <u>different</u> when I\u2019m with you. I like myself better when you\u2019re around, and that has nothing to do with the sex\u2026 though the sex is good as well.\u201d She gave me a wry grin at that.<br /> <br /> I pulled her into a kiss. \u201cThank you,\u201d I said softly, \u201cI think I needed to hear that.\u201d<br /> <br /> We rejoined Julia and Marguerite in the attic \u2013 just in case Julia needed more reference material, we joked \u2013 and it wasn\u2019t long before D returned to the house, having met Joan for ice cream to discuss what was going on with our relationship. D looked at me seriously and said \u201cI need to talk to you privately for a few minutes.\u201d Then she turned and gave Oleander a friendly smile and added \u201cI won\u2019t keep her for too long, I promise.\u201d Oleander nodded good-naturedly and helped me up.<br /> <br /> D kind of sighed as the door to our bedroom shut behind her. \u201cWord is spreading that you and Joan are an item,\u201d she said seriously, \u201cand Joan, of course, insists on shouldering whatever blame she thinks there is. I tried to tell her that everyone involved is an adult, that no one would care about this \u2018indiscretion\u2019 as long as she didn\u2019t make a big deal out of it, but she\u2019s convinced that she\u2019s somehow soiled your reputation\u2026 and Andromeda\u2019s, too.\u201d<br /> <br /> I sort of goggled at that for a minute. \u201cUmmm,\u201d I said after I\u2019d processed it for a bit, \u201cshe knows it\u2019s a little late to close that barn door in my case, right? The cows are already out to pasture. And I\u2019d never say anything against Andromeda, but\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019s been around too, I know,\u201d D nodded, \u201cbut try telling Joan that. She\u2019s convinced that there\u2019s been some sort of transgression here, and she\u2019s trying to take all of the blame on herself.\u201d<br /> <br /> I sat down on the bed and put my head in my hands. \u201cWhat am I gonna do, D?\u201d I asked rhetorically.<br /> <br /> She sat next to me and put her arm around my shoulders, just above my wings. \u201cOnly thing you can do in my opinion is just keep moving forward. It\u2019ll blow over when people find something else to talk about. You and Andromeda can help Joan get past this. I know you can.\u201d <br /> <br /> She kissed me on the temple. It\u2019s one of those oddly sweet gestures that she does all the time when we\u2019re alone but denies hotly when anyone else is around. I started to melt a little, and it suddenly occurred to me that I wanted her opinion on the things I had previously discussed with Oleander. I didn\u2019t open by asking if she liked me this time, though\u2026 I knew well enough how she\u2019d respond to that sort of a question.<br /> <br /> \u201cAm I a stereotype, Maria?\u201d I asked after enough time had passed that I felt I could reasonably change the subject.<br /> <br /> She snorted. \u201cOf course not, Jules. Where did that come from?\u201d<br /> <br /> I shrugged noncommittally. \u201cI dunno. Just thinking about my life, I guess. Sometimes I think all anybody sees when they look at me is how much sex I have, and how many partners. I want to be more than that.\u201d<br /> <br /> Her face turned stony. \u201cDid somebody say something to you, Juliette?\u201d she asked seriously. \u201cIs this about what Augustine said? Because he still hasn\u2019t made that apology like he promised, and if I need to rearrange some teeth\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo,\u201d I said with a soft smile. \u201cIt\u2019s not about the Viscount. It\u2019s not about anyone else, really. This is coming from me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cComing from our patriarchal society, more like,\u201d she grumbled, and my smile grew a little more genuine as I regarded my ranting love fondly. \u201cNobody hangs offensive labels on a man who has a lot of sexual partners, but women in the same situation become pariahs. It\u2019s bullshit, and I don\u2019t want you to obsess over it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI just\u2026 I dunno, I just want to be <u>more</u> than just the \u2018Pretty One,\u2019 I guess,\u201d I said after a minute. \u201cI don\u2019t want that to define who I am. Maybe I should try to focus more on my medical studies. Even if I can\u2019t be a real doctor, I could at least maybe make a name for myself in the Freehold as a decent healer.\u201d<br /> <br /> To her credit, D let my self-deprecating remark pass without comment. \u201cYou are an amazing person, Jules,\u201d she said seriously. \u201cNobody in the motley thinks you\u2019re one-dimensional. We love you, and we like hanging out around you\u2026 and we respect you. You just keep sleeping with as many people as you like. Keep singing like you do until someone important hears you and signs you to a label. Study medicine and become a brilliant neurosurgeon or something. Do whatever you want with your life. And if anyone ever tries to tell you that any of that defines who you are\u2026 fuck \u2018em.\u201d<br /> <br /> So I was completely useless for the next five minutes or so as I composed myself. What did I ever do to deserve two such amazing women in my life? And that\u2019s not even mentioning Julia, Marguerite, Joan, Andromeda, and Rowan.<br /> <br /> Anyway, after I\u2019d cried myself out, I got cleaned up and started preparing for the show. Oleander opted to stick around for the performance, and I started to form the beginnings of a plan at that point. All four of my closest lovers were there, after all\u2026<br /> <br /> Monica showed up, as expected. Halley, having been forewarned of her ex\u2019s plans, opted to stay away for the evening. I think Monica and D are okay now\u2026 not that I ever thought any bad feelings would linger for long. In any case, Monica and Dominika talked up Hawaii quite a bit, and I admit that it does sound like a wonderful place. Monica even started ribbing Gawain a bit about how he ought to take Calamity out there for a weekend.<br /> <br /> Andromeda showed up stag, which I think surprised just about everyone. As soon as she walked in the doors, she located me as I walked the floor and made a beeline for me. I was a little worried about what she might say, I confess. I had thought that she might be a little upset about how my actions had affected her relationship with Joan. Instead, she walked right up to me, put her arms around my neck, and pulled me into a passionate kiss! It was\u2026 hot. Once I realized what she was doing, I returned her passion in kind.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat ought to shut people up,\u201d she muttered with a little smile. \u201cMaybe now that everyone can see you\u2019re not having an affair with my fianc\u00e9e, she can start to put these rumors behind her.\u201d<br /> <br /> I chuckled and gave her a little hug. \u201cI hope so,\u201d I said. \u201cYou know the last thing I want is to cause you two any trouble\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> She waved it off. \u201cIt\u2019ll pass, don\u2019t worry,\u201d she opined. \u201cJoan\u2019s taking it harder than anyone else, of course. I tried to tell her that the three of us are just having a little fun, and that it\u2019s nobody else\u2019s damned business, but\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, D told me,\u201d I affirmed. \u201cShe does seem to want to bear the weight of the world, doesn\u2019t she?\u201d<br /> <br /> Andromeda nodded. \u201cUsually I find it charming,\u201d she said, and we both laughed. I saw her to her usual table, and she asked me if it would be possible for her to speak with de la Rocha at some point. I assumed it would, but my curiosity got the better of me and I felt compelled to ask why.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ve been working on a new machine,\u201d she said with a twinkle in her eye, \u201cbut not one of the usual sort. I got tired of letting Joan support me, so I thought I\u2019d get back in the inventing game. The device is a prototype portable medical scanner. I know that de la Rocha works as an X-ray tech, and I thought it would be nice to get a technician\u2019s input on the device before sending it to the patent office.\u201d Something seemed to occur to her at that point, and the smiled at me. \u201cI know you\u2019ve been studying medicine, too, and I\u2019d love to have your thoughts as well, of course.\u201d<br /> <br /> Even though I\u2019m relatively certain she was just humoring me, I was touched by the thought, and of course I agreed to help however I could. But naturally the conversation quickly went in technical directions I wasn\u2019t able to follow.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s see\u2026 I hobnobbed with the rest of the crowd as well. Flores was there, and was as happy and flirty as ever. Jolie was there too, with Desiree on her arm. It looks like the Princess will be joining us for movie night tonight as Desiree\u2019s plus-one. So that should be fun.<br /> <br /> Calamity\u2019s act came up before mine. She did \u201cLittle Red Riding Hood\u201d again, and really nailed it this time. I\u2019m so proud of her! I\u2019ve been teaching her some of the Contracts of Vainglory recently in the hopes of enhancing the shock effect of our debut next weekend, and she seems to have taken the lessons to heart. She\u2019s not quite able to push her true appearance through the Mask yet, but I\u2019m confident she\u2019ll be able to do so soon. The poor mortals in our audience won\u2019t know what hit \u2018em!<br /> <br /> My number was one I\u2019d done before (\u201cOnly You\u201d by the Platters), but I tried a few new flourishes with it that went over very well. A variety of smoldering gazes were leveled at me when the final high note began to fade, and I seized my chance. I didn\u2019t leave the stage when the number was over, but asked once more to address the audience.<br /> <br /> \u201cI see a lot of familiar faces out there tonight,\u201d I said, tipping a wink to one of our regulars, \u201cand I know some of you have heard this before. I\u2019ll just have to ask you to forgive me for repeating myself. As many of you know, I\u2019m both bisexual and polyamorous. A few days ago, I introduced you to two of my girlfriends\u2026 two of the people who are the most important to me in all the world. I mentioned that they were two of the <u>four</u> people I feel closest to. Well\u2026\u201d I paused and grinned at this point, \u201call four of them are here tonight, and I just couldn\u2019t pass up the opportunity.\u201d<br /> <br /> There was a round of cheers, and I looked up into the rafters. \u201cInsincere Marguerite, would you be good enough to throw a spot on Julia before she slinks off, please?\u201d Marguerite flashed me a grin and nodded, and a second later Julia was bathed in light and covering her face with her hands. \u201cCome on down here, honey,\u201d I called out. She shook her head, but eventually the crowd managed to cajole her into joining me on stage.<br /> <br /> \u201cThis is Julia Oldacre, one of the loves of my life, and the brilliant artist responsible for all of the posters you\u2019ve seen around the lobby. Why don\u2019t you let her know what you think of her work?\u201d The cheers were deafening.<br /> <br /> Julia, blushing crimson, leaned into my microphone and said \u201cI love you, Lori,\u201d loudly and clearly so that everyone could hear her. Then she turned to me and whispered furiously \u201cyou didn\u2019t tell me you were going to do this tonight!\u201d<br /> <br /> I winked at her. \u201cLast week, when I <u>did</u> tell you what I was planning, you bolted,\u201d I explained simply.<br /> <br /> I asked Marguerite to throw a spot on Oleander next. \u201cOleander doesn\u2019t work with us here at the Dream House, so I don\u2019t get to see her as often as the other girls,\u201d I explained, \u201cbut that doesn\u2019t mean she\u2019s any less important to me. She\u2019s an amazingly talented chemist and botanist, and one of the sweetest and most considerate people I know. Come on down here, honey.\u201d She joined us on stage and kissed me simply, then stood back with an \u201caw, shucks\u201d expression on her face.<br /> <br /> D and Marguerite joined us as well, and for the first time my whole family was in the public eye, and I was able to show the whole community how I felt. I gave each of my girls a passionate kiss, and then the five of us ceded the stage to Ace so that he could introduce the next act.<br /> <br /> That was the beginning of a good night for me; something I think I really needed in the wake of my anxiety for Rowan\u2019s safety and my misgivings about my own character. After the show, D and I were of course invited to join Marguerite and Julia in their bedroom. They had picked up Flores at some point, who always makes a pleasant addition to our antics. I looked inquiringly at Oleander, who had been giving me longing looks all evening, and raised an eyebrow in question.<br /> <br /> She sighed and shrugged. \u201cWhat the hell,\u201d she said after a moment. \u201cI\u2019m in if you\u2019ll have me.\u201d No one raised any objections, and the six of us ascended the stairs together, barely containing our excitement.<br /> <br /> As far as I know, the five of them are still lying tangled in a sweaty knot on Marguerite\u2019s bed, snoring peacefully. I extricated myself as gently as I could after the last of them fell asleep and made my way back to my own bedroom. I pepped myself up with Spring contracts, and I\u2019ve spent most of the night reading medical journals (and writing in this diary between articles).<br /> <br /> I know I\u2019m not very smart, but I can make up for my shortcomings if I work hard at studying. I may never be a real doctor, but I\u2019ll do whatever I have to in order to help my friends in the most effective way possible. <br /> <br /> I love singing, and I\u2019ll never stop doing it. I don\u2019t think I could if I wanted to. The same goes for sex\u2026 it\u2019s too much a part of who I am for me to cut it out of my life completely. But I\u2019ll be damned if I\u2019m going to be a stereotype. There\u2019s more to Lorelei Grace than that.<br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei Grace</b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T01:16:57-07:00","id":967825,"title":"","content":"<b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> So, somehow we got to talking about the movie \u201cTitanic\u201d and how it was a good movie. Julia disagreed and even went so far as to leave the room while we talked. I got the impression that she really doesn\u2019t like it. The rest of the group seemed to like the idea so we agreed to watch it on Monday for movie night. It is a long movie so I\u2019m not sure if we\u2019re going to be watching anything else, or just that one. <br /> <br /> Later, at the show, Dominika asked to speak to Lori, De La Rocha and Gawain. I\u2019m not sure what the conversation was about, but it didn\u2019t last too long and Gawain did not come back to the bar in a bad mood or anything. So, I assume it was just some information that she wanted to share or she had a question for my motley mates. A while after that Calamity made her rounds through the club as is her usual habit, but this time she was spreading the word that the Dream House would be open for Thanksgiving for those that had nowhere else to go. I believe she said that Moon and Dionysia will come to dinner on Thursday. I\u2019m sure that we\u2019ll have more, but that is all that have said they\u2019d be coming tonight.<br /> <br /> So, Gawain has been hanging out at the bar the past couple of shows. Not that I\u2019m complaining mind you, I liked the company. It\u2019s been kind fun to have him around. Hailey has also been hanging around the bar being kind of mopey. I have an idea of what she is upset about, so I have not asked her straight out what is bothering her. I do not want to seem like I\u2019m intruding on her private life. Now, Gawain being the gentleman that he is has made it his goal to cheer up Hailey. I don\u2019t think it\u2019s working all that well, given that Hailey was back at the bar again tonight, but it doesn\u2019t hurt to try I suppose.<br /> <br /> I also saw Calamity take Gloria aside to have a chat. I do not know exactly what they were talking about, but I have an idea. Calamity was the only one, that I know of, that Gloria had not had a chance to talk to about Desiree yet and so I think that got remedied. Gloria did not leave looking worried or hurt, so I\u2019m assuming that Calamity endorsed the idea of her and Desiree moving in together. I believe that is what most, if not all, of the motley has said to her when asked. I was cautiously optimistic when she asked me about moving in with Desiree. I have not noticed anything that would imply that she was still serving the Director, so I believe that she has honestly turned over a new leaf. That is pretty much what I told Gloria when she asked me. I think it was smart of her to ask us individually. That way there is no pressure to agree with everyone else if you feel differently than they do.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Today was definitely an interesting day. It started out like most days, with breakfast in the kitchen. Gawain outdid himself and made Brussels waffles this morning, which were delicious. Oleander also came in with Lori, they were both dressed up in nice clothes, so I assume that they both went to church this morning. During our meal the conversation somehow turned to throwing cars. I\u2019m assuming that it was brought up because of the whole fight between De La Rocha and Monica, and the threat of throwing cars. And Lori insisted quite adamantly that no one was to throw her car, the corvette. It was all in good fun though. I doubt that there was actually going to be anyone throwing any cars around any time soon. Once that whole thread died down Julia offered to paint Oleander, who agreed, and the two of them went upstairs. I believe that Oleander was the last of that little group who had not yet been painted by Julia. She is a very talented artist. I\u2019m curious to see the portrait of Oleander when she is done with it.<br /> <br /> After all that is when things got interesting. Insincere Marguerite came up and asked me if I could come with her when she went to go meet with Felicity. The Day Courtier had told Marguerite that she had some information regarding Rowan\u2019s house and wanted to share it with us. I agreed and later in the afternoon we decided to walk there since her house was so close. The weather is still too warm for me, but it was pleasant enough for our walk. The conversation that followed made me completely forget about the heat. Insincere Marguerite admitted to me that in an effort to leave the Director\u2019s service Desiree has chosen to serve Marguerite. She apparently sees Insincere Marguerite as her Keeper and calls her master. I found this more than a little disturbing. Marguerite then told me that things had started when Desiree began flirting with my friend and they started a relationship. Desiree was always the more submissive in the whole thing. She began seducing Marguerite during the fallout of the whole Chalcedony thing, which was, in my opinion, when Insincere Marguerite was most vulnerable. Then Desiree, of her own accord, made a pledge with Marguerite to serve her. It was unasked for, but Desiree told Marguerite that the only way she could leave the Director\u2019s service would be if she was pledged to another Keeper\u2019s service. So she chose Marguerite to be her Keeper!<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite was obviously very upset by this and asked my advice. I am ashamed to say that I didn\u2019t know what to tell Marguerite. She was looking to me for answers and I had none to give. I asked if she trusted her Monarch to talk to about this, and the answer was no. I then suggested Charlotte, but Insincere Marguerite pointed out that the Autumn Court Monarch does not like Desiree in the least. So, that rules out those possibilities. I asked if it might be possible for Desiree to switch her oath to serve the Freehold as a whole, but it seems that Desiree is keen on serving one master, and the person she chose was Marguerite. <br /> <br /> I do not know exactly what is going through Insincere Marguerite\u2019s head, but I have an idea. If this was happening to me I would be panicking and more than just a little stressed out. I believe that Marguerite is feeling much the same thing. She really seems to want a solution to end this. She admitted that she had kept people in Arcadia. She had collected them and was in essence mirroring her own Keeper\u2019s habits. She did not want to go back to doing that here in \u2018the world.\u2019 Nor does she want to put the Freehold in danger. If she does not act as a Keeper for Desiree, then our guest has admitted that she will go back to serving the Director and may become a threat to the freehold. There is only one way that scenario would end and that\u2019s with Desiree\u2019s death. I do not doubt that Lowjack would take care of the situation in a permanent fashion if Desiree should become any kind of threat to the Freehold.<br /> <br /> I asked Insincere Marguerite about at least telling the motley about all of this and she expressed her concerns on how people would react to the news. She was particularly worried about Calamity and her proclivity for stabbing things, in this case, Desiree. She trusted me enough to tell me about all of this because she feels that we are alike in a lot of ways. I think she knew that of all of us, I would be least likely to judge her for this. I honestly do not know how the others would take the news. Calamity would be upset. Whether or not she\u2019d be upset enough to stab Desiree, I\u2019m not sure of, but it\u2019s a distinct possibility. Gawain would be upset I think, but wouldn\u2019t show it as much. Unless he got into one of his more serious moods, then he might say something. I believe Marguerite said that Julia already knows about it so she is taking it well. At least I have not seen any tension between the two lovers. I do not know how De La Rocha and Lorelei would react. De La Rocha would likely react in anger, but I do not know if that anger would be leveled at Insincere Marguerite or at Desiree. Lori is harder to read sometimes. I don\u2019t know if she\u2019d confront Marguerite about it, but I think she would be upset by the whole thing. It might affect the relationship that Insincere Marguerite has with her lovers. They are all so close knit, that if one thing bothers one of them it affects everyone else in the group. So, I can understand Marguerite\u2019s reluctance to tell the rest of the motley what happened.<br /> <br /> I found some relief when I told Lowjack about my past serving the Lady. He seemed to be very understanding and agreed to keep it private. I have no doubt that if I were to suddenly behave strangely or if there might be the possibility that I might go back to Her service then he would eliminate the threat, me. Lowjack is a very practical man. I might suggest that Insincere Marguerite tell Lowjack about the whole situation, but I\u2019m not honestly sure that he would keep his calm at such an admission. I don\u2019t know if he would be more upset at Insincere Marguerite for her role in all of this or if he\u2019d be more upset at Desiree for putting my friend in this position in the first place. It\u2019s not like Marguerite asked for any of this to happen, but she hasn\u2019t reported it yet either. That in and of itself might make Lowjack less happy with Marguerite.<br /> <br /> I just wish I knew what advice to give my friend. I want to be able to help her get out of this situation without putting the rest of the freehold in danger. Granted it wouldn\u2019t be in danger very long once the Monarchs found out. Desiree would be killed before you could say \u201cboo.\u201d But for the most part our motley has grown to like Desiree and don\u2019t want to see her be hurt. I don\u2019t particularly want to see her be hurt either, but sometimes I feel more detached than I\u2019d like. Right now I am kind of annoyed with Desiree for putting Insincere Marguerite in this position. She knew that Marguerite had collected people while in Arcadia, she must have. Why else would she specifically pick Insincere Marguerite to bind herself to? She knew that and yet she still asked Marguerite to do this. She still bound herself to Marguerite. She had to know what this would do to her. This better not be part of some long con. If it is I will let my anger be known. Nobody uses my friends.<br /> <br /> Speaking of friends. While we were talking Insincere Marguerite revealed to me that I had been the only man that she\u2019d been with since coming back to \u2018the world.\u2019 In retrospect I think she was trying to tell me that she still had feelings for me. At the time I was a little wrong-footed by her admission and then she changed the topic so fast I didn\u2019t really have time to react. I hope she knows that I still have feelings for her. I won\u2019t act on them as long as I\u2019m with Luna, but Insincere Marguerite was the first girl that I\u2019d been with since I got back too. I will do whatever I can for her. I hope she knows that. Something tells me that she might not know. I may need to clarify things. I don\u2019t want her to think that I don\u2019t care. She has a special place in my heart.<br /> <br /> All that said, I do have strong feelings for Luna as well. I think Luna and I fit together well and we often react the same way to things that happen. We both reacted the same way when Calamity revealed what had happened with Leanne. The fact that Leanne had healed Calamity as much as she could was the only reason that Leanne was still breathing. Luna admitted her love for me in front of the others when Calamity told her what I\u2019d said. I think it really is love too. I care for Luna a great deal, and am protective of her even if I am fully aware just how dangerous she is. She is still better with those knives of hers than I am with mine. I know this, but I can\u2019t help but be protective of her nonetheless. She is not the greatest with social situations, and neither am I, but we can support each other in such instances. We can be misfits together. <br /> <br /> This whole thing with Insincere Marguerite reminded me of the vow I took when I served the Lady. Everyone that served Her took the same oath on the same day every year. We would gather in the Great Hall and all of us would kneel before the Lady. The first time I took the oath I was a little overwhelmed. I had just been plucked from that cold, dark cave and brought into this shining place. Everything was immaculate and clear. The ever setting sun gave the palace, and especially that room, a rosy glow that permeated everywhere. It was beautiful. I remember kneeling in the Great Hall, surrounded by the Lady\u2019s other servants and feeling awestruck. The Lady had plenty of servants, a good number of them were slaves. They did not take the oath. They were bound to their service in chains. Sometimes literally. Those of us that she deemed worthy were allowed to take the oath of fealty to her. And she had chosen me. So, I knelt with the others and followed along with what they said and did. That was the first time I met Rook. He told me to just follow his example, and I did. In the years that followed I took the oath many more times, and each time I felt that sense of awe all over again. The last time I took the oath was a few months before I was sent to retrieve D\u0336e\u0336l\u0336i\u0336g\u0336h\u0336t\u0336 Diane. I broke that oath with the Lady, but she never officially banished me. I think she had her heart set on \u201crehabilitating\u201d me. I wonder if she still does. <br /> <br /> Anyway, we finally arrived at Felicity\u2019s house and we had an interesting conversation with the Day Courtier. Felicity revealed that she has concerns about Rowan\u2019s house. Apparently the place has no official records, no mortgages or liens. No bills of sale or major repairs. It\u2019s just always been there, and it always seems to have a single woman as the occupant. The name of the woman who lives there has changed over the years, but it always seems to be just one woman living there at a time. Felicity was not overly concerned about Rowan\u2019s intentions. She is not convinced that Rowan is knowingly acting as bait for anyone or has any ulterior motives. In her mind Rowan is exactly what she appears to be.<br /> <br /> So we walked back to the Dream House and continued our talk about Desiree. I still didn\u2019t have any good advice for her and I felt bad for it. I tried to think of things that she might do while she was talking to Felicity but nothing came to mind. I feel helpless in this situation. I know about Insincere Marguerite\u2019s problem and I can do nothing to fix it. The others can\u2019t know, at least not yet, so they\u2019re no help at the moment. I don\u2019t know what else I can do besides be a supportive friend and be there if she needs to vent or talk. I am good at listening. I just wish I was better at helping people fix their problems.<br /> <br /> Once we got back to the Dream House we went to go talk to Lori. We asked to speak to her alone. Marguerite did most of the talking, and told Lori what Felicity\u2019s concerns about Rowan\u2019s house were and why. We made sure to tell Lori that we did not suspect Rowan of having anything to do with the house. We did express our concerns about it though. Insincere Marguerite also said that Felicity had also said that she felt like she was being watched when she was at the house. I know the Felicity did not say that during our meeting this afternoon, so I\u2019m assuming this is something that Marguerite observed when she went to check out the house and look for anything that might incriminate Rowan. Lori was concerned for Rowan but we assured her that Felicity was going to talk to Rowan away from the house, just in case. Lori offered to house Rowan to get her out of the house on the beach, but Felicity said that she would make the offer to Rowan and see if the Selkie wanted to stay with her. I think that would be a good work around. We do not have much more room in the Dream House to board more people. I know that Lori is worried for her lover, but the house doesn\u2019t seem to have done anything bad to its resident so far, we just suggested moving her out of the place as a precaution. <br /> <br /> After that we went to the bar where Insincere Marguerite asked me for a drink. I guess the conversation we had took its toll and my friend needed something with some kick to it. Before I could even pour the cognac Desiree came by and wanted to get Insincere Marguerite\u2019s opinion on furniture for her and Gloria\u2019s future new place. A few minutes later Marguerite came back and I gave her the drink that she\u2019d asked for. As she was finishing her cognac Calamity came over and asked what was wrong. She said that it was unusual for Insincere Marguerite to be drinking in the middle of the day, which is true. Marguerite just said that she had something very personal going on, but that she didn\u2019t want to talk about it. She said that Julia knew about it and was doing what she could to help. Marguerite left off the fact that I knew what was going on, which was fine by me. It might look odd for me to be in her confidence but not the others. It is normal for her to tell everything to Julia since they are so close.<br /> <br /> Later, at the show, there was some interesting goings on. Well, more socially interesting. Andromeda came to the club without Joan, which was a bit unusual. I think there was some rumors going around about Joan being unfaithful to Andromeda because she had been flirting so heavily with Lori the other day. Andromeda soundly put those thoughts to rest by passionately kissing Lorelei as soon as she spotted her. Lori responded in kind. Hopefully Joan will come back to the club soon and things can get back to normal for everyone involved. And speaking of lovers, Dominika and Monica came to the show tonight. Hailey it seems excused herself from tonight\u2019s show, presumably to keep the peace that they\u2019ve got going on.<br /> <br /> So, it seems that I am back to keeping secrets from my friends. Not that I think this is a bad thing in this instance. Insincere Marguerite\u2019s secret could very well cause some serious problems with other members of the motley, but I do know that if she keeps this to herself it will tear her up inside. It\u2019s not the same situation, but before I told the others about me having been a Loyalist it was messing me up. I felt bad that I hadn\u2019t told them, but was certain that they would reject me for it. I can\u2019t tell you how glad I am that I was wrong about the later. Maybe the others will be lenient with Insincere Marguerite. Maybe they will see that she is not to blame and be willing to help? I honestly don\u2019t know. The only thing that I am sure of right now is that I will not betray my friend. If she decides to tell the others and they reject her, I will not leave her to face things alone. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> I have compromised myself. Badly.<br /> <br /> I admitted to Jacob I had taken my first Changeling since returning. Not really Julia, however I fantasized about that. Julia is my partner who I have had control over, but she is my partner. I hope to never imagine a time she isn\u2019t. But it was Desiree who I took from her Keeper. <br /> <br /> It is stupid in retrospect. I could very well lose Juliette, and I told someone who had no reaction to me saying I felt something for him. I would rather kill Desiree than lose Juliette. And I say that as someone who hates killing, and cares for Desiree. But Juliette is too important. Juliette, Maria, Julia\u2026my family.<br /> <br /> As I said tonight, I like our hallway. Juliette and Maria in one room, Julia and I just beside, but we share a hall, a bathroom, a balcony, and each other. We are a family, a real family. A loving family like I never had. Oh yes, the sex it is nice, and like tonight when we took a veritable orchard of beautiful plant women,. Oleander and Flores, it is amazing. The room smells of rose and faint honeysuckle. But in the end, it is the security, the love, the support, of Juliette and Maria and Julia. That is what is important.<br /> <br /> Juliette brought the four of us, and Oleander, on stage tonight. It felt good. She declared her love for all of us. Julia got emotional. I did not but I was always a more reserved girl. But even I held it in. It was harder for fear of losing Juliette.<br /> <br /> I remember her saying she could not love or stay with someone who owned another person. Juliette, I want to trust you, to tell you\u2026I am caught up in this, Desiree has me even as she acknowledges me as her master. This is no joke, and I only realized, talking to Jacob, how scary this is. I can\u2019t lose my family. I will do whatever I must to stay with them. They are my life.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s hard to swallow that lack of independence. <br /> <br /> I was talking to Jacob on the way to see Felicity, as she had important information about Rowan but did not want to come to the house. It turns out Rowan\u2019s house has no record of building, may not be being taxed, and has never been modified significantly enough to keep a record. No trace of a deed, lien, or mortgage. And it has always been there, over a century, all with a single woman living there, though the names have changed. No one knows Rowan well, but the uneasy feeling I had and to a lesser degree Felicity means she takes this seriously. We are assuming it is not Rowan as a willing threat, and Felicity is speaking to her outside the house when she is lifeguarding Monday. She wants her to leave while it is investigated, possibly staying with herself. So that is in action.<br /> <br /> I then spoke to Lori. I laid out my concerns, leaving out only that I had been there, attributing my observation to Felicity. Lori agreed with our assessment\u2026she wanted to call Rowan, but Rowan would likely be home and we don\u2019t know what that would set into motion.<br /> <br /> I hope she stays safe. I love her.<br /> <br /> I also admitted I cared about Jacob. He said nothing. This is part of why I don\u2019t dally with men. It hurt a little, but I must remember for some people sex is utterly meaningless.<br /> <br /> Okay it hurts more than a little.<br /> <br /> And what to do about White Maria? I deeply enjoy our liaisons, but Calamity is correct, it is bad for both of us, recalling our Durances. Calamity is one of the few people who don\u2019t loathe White Maria. I really don\u2019t want to end them, when we are both happy with how they are going, and it quite frankly helps White Maria cope. But I don\u2019t want to hurt either of us. I shall have to keep an eye on it.<br /> <br /> I wish I could trust Calamity not to betray me if she thinks she knows better. <br /> <br /> The faces of my family keep crossing my mind. Juliette\u2026Maria\u2026Julia\u2026beautiful women. I should perhaps come clean; I don\u2019t want to lie to them. But\u2026there should be some mystique, I suppose? A lady deserves her secrets. Well, unless she can solve these problems.<br /> <br /> Maybe Julia and I can brush each other\u2019s hair. Maybe we can get Juliette involved\u2026Maria rarely wants her hair touched. That always helps my nerves. Tomorrow. Yes.<br /> <br /> Sleep now. Hope my heart is lighter when I wake.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXIV</i><br /> <br /> Oh lets see. Where to start<br /> <br /> This session was not heavy on dice rolls, so there is little more to explain. Insincere Marguerite finally had her decision with Desiree, and it\u2019s implications, sink in, so she spoke to Jacob, which wound up having her become more agitated. <br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite was excessively casual with Jacob on their walk, walking on her hands, walking backwards talking to him, etc. Very flirty. It did not get into either journal, I do not think.<br /> <br /> Finally, Insincere Marguerite was gathering cats to spy on Rowan\u2019s house.<br /> <br /> Next time, the Rowan plot begins to come to a head. Comments and Questions welcome. If I owe you a PM I will do it, I am behind on my writing atm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T14:30:25-07:00","id":968142,"title":"","content":"Andromeda: Today she will invent the Tricorder. Tomorrow, a stargate. Who knows where that grey skinned woman will go next.<br /> <br /> A TARDIS, hopefully, if the God Machine doesn't intervene. :-p","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T23:48:30-07:00","id":969705,"title":"","content":"Interesting to see how the takes differ on a same event when reported by a different character wiith the armoire thing with Gawain and Lorelei, then the Marguerite's admitting she still has feelings for Jacob. It helps contrastig their personalities.<br /> Did anyone use kenning on Rowan's house?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T06:04:06-07:00","id":969841,"title":"","content":"Taidragon: I honestly thought about making some reference in Lori's journal to Andromeda's invention resembling a tricorder... she was about the right age to catch the <i>Star Trek</i> hype when the show originally aired, and she's just enough of a closet geek to bring it up around people with whom she's comfortable. I stopped myself at the last moment, mostly because it seemed a little out of keeping with the rest of the journal's tone.<br /> <br /> Anteros: I also enjoy getting different characters' perspectives on the events of the session. In the instance of the discussion about the armoire, Gawain's account is actually by far the more accurate (I think my lips might have actually trembled when we played out that scene, and only a modicum of self-resect stopped Lori from begging). Lori's version is a nearly-subconscious attempt to re-write the scene in such a way that she looks better in hindsight. :-)<br /> <br /> Keep the comments coming, everyone! We love knowing you're reading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T11:59:48-07:00","id":970082,"title":"","content":"PenitentTom: That's cool to learn; Gawain does seem to be more factual with his writing than others, provided he's not fallen into his Lord Bertilak personality, though that doesn't mean he misses details. As I've noted before, I really enjoy the contrast as, even if it's a mistake from the writer OOC, it provides personality to their character. I'd ask if Lori looks up geek culture in the modern times, but considering how many Changeling duties she has, both in and out of the Dream House, she doesn't really have a lot of downtime to really delve in, does she? Not to mention the breadth it'd have gained too...and for some reason that made me think she'd like Farscape. No idea why.<br /> <br /> I take it the armoire is the same one from the suggested tokens in the book? Seems like Gawain has a good idea on how to make such an item. In general he seems to have a great grasp on the unusual items needed to craft such things.<br /> <br /> I wonder if Lori engage in token crafting as well, but by using things such as her own songs as ingredients, or even her own feathers. Probably not the best idea though - after all, her feathers only recently came back to her. I doubt that Lori would be in any mood to lose them again, even if it was for a nice token.<br /> <br /> Also, is it just me or does Evelynn from League of Legends resemble Calamity a lot? Wild red hair, a love of violence and inflicting pain, a penchant for spikes, the stealth of a darkling and a very sensual dance? Eh, I might be playing too much League.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T14:02:12-07:00","id":970192,"title":"","content":"Taidragon: The motley's Monday &quot;movie night&quot; tradition started out as a tool to help Lori catch up on all the pop culture she missed while she was in Arcadia. It's sort of expanded beyond that original mission statement over the sessions, but that was its original intention. That's how Lori picks up info on most of the intervening years, though other things do occasionally pop up in conversation during play. There are still <b>huge</b> gaps in her knowledge, though... for example, she would probably have referred to the aforementioned tricorder as being a device from <i>Star Trek</i> without really feeling the need to add any subtitles. Though she might have heard that the franchise has expanded over the years (and would almost certainly have encountered some mention of the reboot movies), it hasn't really hit home to her that for the last thirty years or so that title has meant something different to the vast majority of the public.<br /> <br /> And no, Lori would not take well to the suggestion that she might want to donate some feathers at this point. She's not vain... okay, well, yes, she's totally vain. It's kind of one of her defining features. Still, if donating her feathers would really help someone (save a life, cure a disease, break a curse, etc.) she'd do so without hesitation; probably without even thinking about it. But to make a Token? No. Lori has no desire to be plucked. If Gawain ever wants to capture one of her songs for such a purpose, however, she'd be happy to help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T14:15:02-07:00","id":970208,"title":"","content":"Lori's journal seems to be pretty accurate overall. Some things are written from her perspective and she is a little off, but that is unusual. She adds some conversation details that may not have been at the table, but not many....usually just her alone with a lover, and I encourage that sort of thing. There is more creative license than most journals...some conversations are rewritten a bit, but she is pretty factual. Not the incredibly detailed and faithful Speed journals, but a player writes such that they enjoy, and I have no issue with putting them up because it adheres pretty well to the session.<br /> <br /> May have been that was from Gawain's player they would have to answer. I will leave the Lori specific questions to Penitent Tom. I will note we have had downtime outside these bursts in activity.<br /> <br /> No one has Kenned Rowans house or actually asked Rowan how she got the house yet. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T01:58:00-07:00","id":970577,"title":"","content":"I will point out that Calamity has used shards of her glass to make vessels for dream crafting and would most likely not really hesitate to use part of herself in crafting a token or as a component. But then, she is Calamity.<br /> <br /> Taidragon - I've never actually played League of Legions, so I am afraid I cannot really say.I may need to do some research though...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T18:01:51-07:00","id":971035,"title":"","content":"Amberghylles: For clarity (pun not intended), Evelynn's a Jungler, a champion who hunts creatures in the spaces between lanes to gain gold/experience and buffs rather than fighting in the lanes alongside everyone else, and waiting for opportune times to jump out and turn the tides of a battle, if not picking off champions when they're vulnerable. Her own abilities allow her to send spikes out on the ground that can damage multiple foes, increase her attack speed or remove effects that would slow her and give her a brief speed boost, as well as a passive ability that makes her invisible when she has not attacked or been damaged after a certain amount of time. <a href=\"http://ddragon.leagueoflegends.com/cdn/img/champion/splash/Evelynn_0.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Here's a link to what her (current) splash art is</a>.<br /> <br /> Really, a lot of the ressemblances are superficial/coincidental. Though Calamity may have her moments, from what I can tell Evelynn's far and away more of a sadist (one of her quotes is literally &quot;I like it when they scream&quot;) and has no compunctions of delivering pain. She actually has more ties to vampires than anything else, given her affinity for blood, bits of lore indicating she contracted vampirism as a child, and her having a &quot;Masquerade&quot; skin. Her dance may be accurate though, given what Anica has been teaching her...<br /> <br /> More properly on topic, how do the players handle indecision over the direction they want their characters to go to? It's a problem that I've had with my characters, and it leads me to spending experiences on things other than what I initially wanted to spend them on, such as wanting to get a particular attribute boosted but then spending those experiences on merits instead. Suffice to say, it makes for a very unfocused build.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 09-16-2016, 09:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T10:01:03-07:00","id":973909,"title":"","content":"Taidragon: I can't speak for the other players, but as far as Lori goes, I don't really have a specific plan for her development beyond a few basic guidelines. I can be a bit of a hoarder when it comes to experiences/XP in these games, so I usually have a bit of a surplus when I decided it's time to spend 'em. When we raise our Wyrd - which we usually agree to do as a group, so no one gets left behind - the first things I <u>always</u> spend points on are raising Lori's Presence and Expression to the new cap. As a result of her Durance (yeah, sure, that's the real reason) she's extremely competitive about her singing ability, and likes to keep herself on the bleeding edge of what is possible. If she was a combat character, I'd likely do the same with her physical stats and relevant combat skills; as it is I try to keep her among the best at what she does well. Beyond that, I usually don't have a focused plan in advance; I let the story dictate where the points go. If she's been going to the firing range in the journals, she'll likely improve her Firearms skill. If she's really buckling down and hitting the books, then Medicine or Academics are likely to get a boost... or maybe Intelligence, if I feel its justified. In the coming months, I hope to demonstrate an increased mastery of Spanish in the journals as she spends more time with de la Rocha and Oleander, so I can justify picking up the Language Merit. What results might not be the most focused or efficient build, but I like the idea that she's learning organically based on the flow of the story.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T13:14:40-07:00","id":976066,"title":"","content":"Time to come back around. Rowan\u2019s story comes to a head, while, Insincere Marguerite\u2019s troubles boil over. No end of drama at the Dream House. Gawain\u2019s player had to miss.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LXV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> I just looked back over my last entry and had to suppress a bitter humorless laugh. Concerns about my reputation in the Freehold? Bring it on. Uncertainty as to Rowan\u2019s safety with regards to her house? Sounds good to me. Existential ennui? Thank you, world, may I have another?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m writing this quickly as the others prepare to go. We\u2019re heading to Oleander\u2019s place, and I thought writing in my diary might be vaguely preferable to sitting around feeling useless and tense. We have to take action <u><u>now</u></u>, since we\u2019re relatively sure that our opponent now views us as a threat\u2026 and I can\u2019t help but wonder if we\u2019re doing the right thing. And even if we are, I have to face up to the very real possibility that by the time this night is over, someone I care about may never trust me again.<br /> <br /> So the day started off well enough. D came to find me in our room when the rest of my lovers began to wake up, and the six of us headed downstairs for sex breakfast. D was wearing a tank-top, which really showed off her physique, much to my approval (and Julia\u2019s, and Gloria\u2019s). When we got to the kitchen, Gawain was already making more waffles (I forget the type this time), so we sat around the kitchen island and the usual banter began. I was engaged in the talk and responded if anyone addressed me directly, but I let most of it flow past me as I finished perusing an article on endometriosis. After a while I found myself leaning up against D and stroking her bicep idly as I read.<br /> <br /> Oleander was one of the first to leave, and I walked her to the front door and left her with a deep kiss. \u201cWe have to find a way to see each other more often during the week,\u201d I opined wistfully.<br /> <br /> She smiled. \u201cJust let me know when you\u2019re available, and I\u2019ll do my best to be non-toxic,\u201d she promised. \u201cBut\u2026 I <u><u>do</u></u> have a job to do. I need to head into the Hedge over the next few days to pick up some supplies, and some of the sites I\u2019ll be visiting are\u2026 not very nice. So let me know now if I need to reschedule that jaunt, please.\u201d<br /> <br /> I shook my head. \u201cOf course I don\u2019t want our time together to interfere with your work,\u201d I explained. \u201cI\u2019m sorry. I wasn\u2019t thinking. I was being selfish.\u201d<br /> <br /> She shook her head. \u201cI\u2019d do just about anything to spend more time with you, angel,\u201d she said softly. \u201cBut I know you have a lot of demands on your time. I\u2026 I <u><u>like</u></u> your other girlfriends. I wouldn\u2019t have slept with them last night if I didn\u2019t. But\u2026 I\u2019m maybe not as needy as some of them, and I\u2019m okay with that.\u201d<br /> <br /> I gave her my best smile. \u201cYou\u2019re amazing,\u201d I said breathily. \u201cI\u2019ll see you next weekend if not before, okay?\u201d She nodded, leaned in for another kiss, and then she was gone.<br /> <br /> Calamity and I were prepared to do a couple of semi-final run-throughs of our number after breakfast, and we wanted Marguerite to be present for at least one of them so that she could get an idea of what sort of lighting and sound would be needed for the act. Calamity went off to talk to Marguerite, and the two of them didn\u2019t show back up for almost twenty minutes. I didn\u2019t mind, I was still blissing out leaning up against D at the time.<br /> <br /> D had left for work by the time Calamity joined me in the theater. I could tell immediately that something was wrong, and I thought she and Marguerite might have had another fight. \u201cWhat\u2019s wrong?\u201d I asked, carefully placing a hand on her shoulder.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s nothing,\u201d she replied automatically.<br /> <br /> \u201cCalamity\u2026\u201d I began, letting my concern show on my face.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s\u2026 nothing I can talk about,\u201d she amended.<br /> <br /> \u201cAre things okay between you and Marguerite?\u201d I asked after a moment.<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cWell, as okay as can be expected,\u201d she said after a few seconds of silence. \u201cShe\u2019s not mad at me or anything like that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAre you safe? Is <u><u>she</u></u> safe?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> Calamity shrugged. \u201cNobody is in any physical danger that I know of,\u201d she said guardedly.<br /> <br /> I quirked an eyebrow. \u201cEmotional danger, then? Spiritual?\u201d Sometimes I have real trouble letting things go.<br /> <br /> Calamity sighed. \u201cI\u2019m sorry, Lori,\u201d she said. \u201cI\u2019m truly sorry. But I <u><u>can\u2019t</u></u> talk to you about this.\u201d<br /> <br /> That\u2019s when it hit me. \u201cYou\u2019ve made a pledge, haven\u2019t you?\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded.<br /> <br /> I took both of her shoulders in my hands. \u201cJust promise me \u2013 you don\u2019t have to pledge, but please promise me \u2013 that you\u2019ll let me know if there\u2019s anything I can do to help, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded again. \u201cI promise,\u201d she said.<br /> <br /> Marguerite approached us after this little conversation, and told me that Felicity had texted her to let her know that she\u2019d had her talk with Rowan\u2026 who was not taking the suggestion that something might be a little \u2018off\u2019 about her house particularly well. I decided to give her a call and see if I could help.<br /> <br /> As Felicity had said, she wasn\u2019t very happy about the assertion that something might be wrong with her house, but she was prepared to play along if it would make me happy. She seemed particularly nervous about staying with Felicity \u2013 whom she doesn\u2019t know very well \u2013 so I asked her if she would prefer to stay with me at the Dream House. She hemmed and hawed for a while, claiming that she didn\u2019t want to put anyone out, but eventually I managed to get her to agree.<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks, Lori,\u201d she said hoarsely as we were saying our goodbyes. \u201cI\u2019ll see you tonight. Love you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLove you too,\u201d I replied without even thinking about it. After I disconnected I realized what I had said, and sort of mentally kicked myself. I\u2019m still not sure how I feel about Rowan, and I don\u2019t want to lead her on. I don\u2019t want to hurt her.<br /> <br /> In any case, something about her tone when she talked about the house made me nervous, and her extreme resistance to the idea of letting anyone examine it set off all kinds of alarms in my head. I called a motley-wide meeting. Everyone was there except D, who was still at work. I explained the situation to them, and told them that I had invited Rowan to stay with us that night. I also explained that I wanted her to stay with me specifically\u2026 both so that I could try to comfort her, and so that I could watch to make sure she didn\u2019t try to sneak out in the middle of the night.<br /> <br /> Marguerite offered to remain in contact with Felicity to make sure things went smoothly when the Day Court arrived to inspect the premises. Calamity and Julia opted to head out to the Autumn Court\u2019s occult library to see what they could dig up on similar situations. They asked if I wanted to go with them, and a part of me really did\u2026 but realistically I\u2019m not much use when it comes to exerting my brainpower, and I\u2019d probably have ended up as more of a hindrance than a help.<br /> <br /> So I spent most of the afternoon fretting and worrying instead of doing anything useful. Marguerite kept me posted, but there wasn\u2019t actually much to tell for most of the afternoon. When Calamity and Julia got back, they had managed to form a few theories about the nature of the house... none of which were particularly encouraging.<br /> <br /> First, as I'd already postulated, the house could be haunted. This doesn\u2019t seem likely for a variety of reasons. First, I\u2019ve been in the house a couple of times now \u2013 I\u2019ve even been alone in it for short periods \u2013 and I\u2019ve never noticed anything that would indicate a poltergeist or other malevolent spirit. Second, Rowan\u2019s obsession with staying in her house seems to be a recent development; she\u2019s left it for extended periods since we\u2019ve met her with no ill effects.<br /> <br /> The second theory is that the house could be a Gentry in disguise. There\u2019s at least one precedent; a Gentry who was exiled and confined to the form of a house. It exerted its powers over the mortals who lived within it, trying to get them to accomplish tasks which it thought would help it return to Arcadia. That doesn\u2019t seem to be this house\u2019s M.O, but then again, every Gentry is different, so we\u2019re at least prepared to humor the notion until it can be disproved. Jacob mentioned driving an iron nail into the house to see how it reacts. Calamity really liked that idea, while Luna seemed to think it would be safest to simply burn the house to the ground before it could drag anyone off to Arcadia.<br /> <br /> The third and most likely theory involves something called a \u201cDionaea House.\u201d Apparently the word is based upon the scientific name for the Venus Fly-Trap plant, and it describes a sentient house which lures people into it so that it can consume them. They\u2019re difficult to detect; the books Calamity and Julia found said that one of the only visible signs of a Dionaea House was their tendency to leave piles of human bones beneath their foundations. They <u><u>have</u></u> been known to use attractive mortals as bait to lure prey in, though\u2026 and these mortals are rarely harmed.<br /> <br /> We\u2019d also uncovered a little more information about the house\u2019s previous tenants. All of them were attractive blonde women in their early twenties. Photos bear this up, though it\u2019s shockingly difficult to dig up any concrete information about any of them beyond their names. The thing is, <u><u>all</u></u> photos of these residents show attractive blonde women in their early twenties\u2026 even those who lived in the house over a period of ten to twenty years. It could be a coincidence\u2026 but you\u2019d think there would be a little variety in the photographic evidence. We even batted around the idea that maybe all of them were high-Wyrd changelings who aged very slowly, but something about that theory didn\u2019t feel quite right.<br /> <br /> I think it was a little before dinner time when everything went completely to shit. Marguerite entered the kitchen a little later than usual, and she was looking unusually grim. I asked her what was wrong, and she told me with a sigh.<br /> <br /> Felicity\u2019s attempt to remove Rowan from her house had not gone well. About five Day Courtiers from LA accompanied her to the house carrying axes. I\u2019m assured that this was merely a precaution, in case the house tried to trap them inside to prevent Rowan from leaving, but it set my newest girlfriend off in a way none of us had predicted. She absolutely refused to leave\u2026 to the point of assaulting Felicity. She actually tried to choke the life out of our Day Court neighbor, and it took two of her companions to separate them. She was taken to Felicity\u2019s house and restrained to prevent her from hurting anyone.<br /> <br /> I couldn\u2019t believe it. If I hadn\u2019t witnessed Rowan\u2019s distress for myself a short time later, I probably <u><u>still</u></u> wouldn\u2019t believe it. Rowan is such a peaceful, non-violent girl\u2026 it\u2019s hard for me to imagine her lashing out against anyone like that, let alone a prominent member of her own Court. I decided that I had to talk to her, and asked Marguerite to arrange it with Felicity.<br /> <br /> A few minutes later my phone rang. I didn\u2019t recognize the number, but I answered it anyway. \u201cHello?\u201d I asked hesitantly.<br /> <br /> \u201cLori?\u201d Rowan\u2019s voice came across the connection. She sounded both tense and out-of-breath, not at all the sweet lilt to which I\u2019ve become accustomed.<br /> <br /> \u201cRowan, sweetie, are you okay?\u201d I asked anxiously.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m\u2026 not hurt,\u201d she assured me after a moment. \u201cThey took me out of my House,\u201d she added a few seconds later. She sounded both affronted and a little scared.<br /> <br /> \u201cI know, sweetie,\u201d I said with as much reassurance as I could. \u201cI\u2019m really sorry about that. I didn\u2019t know they were going to be so blunt about it. But I really think they\u2019re trying to help you, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHelp me?\u201d she asked, as though trying to figure out how that could be possible. \u201cHelp me by taking me away from my House? How is that going to help me? I don\u2019t like it here. I\u2019m not comfortable here. I want to go back to my House.\u201d Yes, she kept using the word, and subtly emphasizing it, which is why I\u2019m capitalizing it here.<br /> <br /> I started to get really scared at that point. \u201cRowan, honey, I want you to listen to me, okay? I know you\u2019re upset, and you have every right to be. But if Felicity is right, you\u2019re in danger while you\u2019re in that house.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHow could my House be dangerous?\u201d she asked. \u201cThat doesn\u2019t make any sense.\u201d<br /> <br /> I tried a different tactic. \u201cIt might be nothing. I hope it <u><u>is</u></u> nothing, and you\u2019ll be back in your house as soon as we can verify that. I promise.\u201d<br /> <br /> She thought about it for a while. \u201cO\u2026okay,\u201d she said at last. \u201cI trust you, Lori. I\u2019ll\u2026 I\u2019ll try to calm down. But\u2026 but this whole thing makes no sense. I wonder if Felicity wants my House for herself? That makes more sense than claiming that my House is somehow dangerous. Or\u2026 or maybe she\u2019s been corrupted by the Night Court, and <u><u>they\u2019re</u></u> trying to get their hands on my House\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I was close to tears by this point. \u201cI really don\u2019t think that\u2019s the case, honey,\u201d I said softly. \u201cThat place has some kind of hold on you. Listen to yourself\u2026 this doesn\u2019t sound like you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2026\u201d she began, then coughed for a moment. \u201cI\u2026 attacked Felicity earlier,\u201d she admitted hoarsely. \u201cI wanted to make sure you heard it from me. I don\u2019t know why I did it\u2026 she was just trying to take me away from my House and I sort of panicked\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know,\u201d I said soothingly. \u201cJust like I know you wouldn\u2019t have done something like that normally. The Rowan I know doesn\u2019t want to hurt anyone\u2026 not even a jackass like TJ who\u2019s been trying to intimidate her left and right.\u201d<br /> <br /> I tried my best to soothe her, and I think it worked to a degree. When we hung up a few minutes later, she at least seemed more rational. And if she wasn\u2019t exactly <u><u>relaxed</u></u>, at least she didn\u2019t feel quite so much like a plucked guitar string.<br /> <br /> D arrived a few minutes later, cocksure as ever. She took in the somber looks, walked up to me and took me into her arms. \u201cIs everything okay, babe?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cNot really,\u201d I replied.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat\u2019s wrong?\u201d she asked. \u201cWho do I have to punch?\u201d<br /> <br /> I told her what had been going on, and she got a determined look on her face. \u201cI need to check on some things,\u201d she said stiffly as she stalked toward the exit.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhere are you going, hon?\u201d I asked. I\u2026 dammit, weakling that I am, I wanted to be able to rely on her strength for a while.<br /> <br /> She turned back to face me and stroked my cheek gently. \u201cI\u2019m going to call Madame Spidertoes,\u201d she said softly. \u201cI\u2019m going to ask her about this list of tenants you\u2019ve uncovered. If they were changelings, she\u2019d know about them.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cThat\u2019s a good idea. The more we know the better.\u201d<br /> <br /> She walked out into the hall. As she walked into an unused room, I faintly heard her say \u201cGladys\u2026 it\u2019s Maria. I need to ask you something\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> She returned a few minutes later with a grim look on her face. \u201cNone of them were changelings, as far as she knows,\u201d she told us. \u201cNot vampires or other supernaturals either\u2026 though that\u2019s a bit harder for her to pin down.\u201d<br /> <br /> I slumped my shoulders. \u201cThanks for trying,\u201d I said.<br /> <br /> Calamity called Dahlia, as by this point it was hard to argue against the idea that the house represented a \u201cdanger to the Freehold and its inhabitants,\u201d and Calamity is pledge-bound to report such things to Dahlia. Though I only heard about the conversation secondhand, I gather that Calamity\u2019s handler is also a bit tense after watching Chalcedony for the past few days. She doesn\u2019t exactly seem to be falling in love with Little Girl Blue like Molly did, though, and that\u2019s at least a little comforting.<br /> <br /> Dahlia sort of impatiently asked if she needed to break surveillance to deal with this situation or if we could handle it, and Calamity opined that we could manage by ourselves (I wish I had her confidence on that score). Dahlia <u><u>also</u></u> suggested that we might want to check with Madame Spidertoes to see if she knew of any way to detect and deal with Dionaea Houses, in case that\u2019s what it is. I was reluctant to have D call her again \u2013 it wasn\u2019t jealousy this time, I was legitimately worried that we would become a nuisance to her \u2013 but D gave me a quick smile and a peck on the cheek and assured me that her former flame wouldn\u2019t mind helping us out in such a situation.<br /> <br /> It wasn\u2019t long before D returned with Spidertoes\u2019 suggestions. Foremost among these was that if it <u><u>is</u></u> a Dionaea House, we might be able to force a reaction out of it by spreading a certain chemical around its base. I can\u2019t remember the name of the chemical right now, but D had written it down, and Spidertoes had told us that we could probably get some from Oleander.<br /> <br /> \u201cShit,\u201d I murmured when D reported this information.<br /> <br /> Everybody turned to look at me. \u201cWhat is it?\u201d Marguerite asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cOleander\u2019s going into the Hedge today. She told me she was going to be toxic for the next few days.\u201d I pulled out my phone and speed-dialed her. \u201cMaybe she hasn\u2019t left yet. I might be able to catch her.\u201d<br /> <br /> Luck was with us; she answered on the third ring. \u201cI missed you too, angel, but I was gonna play it cool and wait a couple of days before I called you,\u201d she quipped once we were connected.<br /> <br /> \u201cHey, honey,\u201d I said by way of a greeting. \u201cI\u2019m afraid it\u2019s not a social call tonight. The motley has to deal with something, and I need a certain chemical, if you can get it for me.\u201d<br /> <br /> She was all business in an instant. \u201cWhatever you need,\u201d she said seriously. \u201cJust name it.\u201d<br /> <br /> I did.<br /> <br /> She whistled. \u201cIs this some sort of a test, angel?\u201d she asked after a moment. \u201cI said I\u2019d get you anything you needed, and I meant it\u2026 but I can\u2019t just give that stuff out. I\u2019ll have to inform Charlotte at the very least. Why do you want it?\u201d<br /> <br /> I told her in brief about Rowan\u2019s house, and said that Spidertoes had recommended we ask her for the chemical. She gave a sigh of relief at that. \u201cIf it\u2019s Spidertoes\u2019 idea, then I\u2019m sure Charlotte won\u2019t have a problem with it. I still have to tell her, though, and it\u2019ll take me a while to prepare a batch for transport. And, Lori\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes?\u201d I asked anxiously.<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t want you handling this stuff. <u>At</u> <u><u>all</u></u>. I haven\u2019t even told Flores that I know how to make it. It can actually weaken the bindings between body and soul, and it\u2019s no joke. I don\u2019t give it out lightly, and I wouldn\u2019t give it out at all if anyone else was asking me.\u201d She chuckled grimly to herself. \u201cGod, I must really have it bad for you. In any case, I\u2019d rather none of you handle this stuff if it can be avoided. Give me two hours to get it ready, and then I\u2019ll come with you and apply it <u><u>myself</u></u>.\u201d<br /> <br /> I fretted about that for a minute. \u201cIf it\u2019s that dangerous\u2026 are you sure about this, sweetie? I mean, maybe we shouldn\u2019t be doing this\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Oleander thought for a minute. \u201cIf this thing is a threat to the freehold, then it needs to be dealt with. And if anything can kill a <u><u>house</u></u>\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay,\u201d I said. I still had misgivings, but I was willing to put them aside for the moment. \u201cText one of us when you\u2019re ready, and we\u2019ll come and meet you at your workshop.\u201d I walked out into the hall and pitched my voice low. \u201cThank you so much for doing this, Imelda. I love you.\u201d<br /> <br /> There was silence for a few moments. I know she doesn\u2019t like that name, but I wanted to do something to impress upon her how serious I was. \u201cThanks for agreeing to let me handle it,\u201d she replied eventually. \u201cI\u2019ll feel better knowing that nobody else is going to get their hands on this chemical. And I love you too, Juliette.\u201d<br /> <br /> We talked among ourselves for a bit as we waited for the signal. When the subject of Chalcedony came up, I mentioned a theory that she might be using Talecrafting to cast herself in the role of romantic heroine\u2026 the character in the book who is accused of wrongdoing, but as people investigate and get to know her, they can\u2019t help falling for her. It\u2019s an interesting theory, and it fits the facts, but I have to admit that there\u2019s not much in the way of direct supporting evidence.<br /> <br /> Rowan called me again while we were waiting for Oleander to get back to us. \u201cHey sweetie, are you okay?\u201d I asked anxiously as I answered the phone.<br /> <br /> She sighed into the receiver. \u201cI asked if I could call you again, and she said yes. I want to be with you, Lori. I don\u2019t want to stay here. You make things better. If I can\u2019t go back to my House, can I at least come and stay with you?\u201d<br /> <br /> I considered it. \u201cI\u2019ll\u2026 I\u2019ll have to check with the others, honey, okay? It\u2019s not just my decision. But I <u>will</u> ask them, and I promise as soon as this is resolved we can spend as much time together as you like. I\u2019ll set aside a whole day if you want.\u201d<br /> <br /> She let out a shuddering breath. \u201cOkay,\u201d she said. \u201cI\u2019ll\u2026 I\u2019ll be patient. Thanks for talking to me, Lori. I love you.\u201d<br /> <br /> I thought about it this time. \u201cRight back atcha,\u201d I said, somewhat lamely, and then the signal was gone. Unsurprisingly, we all pretty much agreed that letting Rowan stay at the Dream House would be a bad idea.<br /> <br /> After a while, D got a text. She glanced down at her phone, then looked up and nodded. \u201cGreen light from Oleander,\u201d she said simply.<br /> <br /> We piled into Gawain\u2019s van and drove over to Oleander\u2019s lab. Most of this entry was written while we were waiting for her call, but I\u2019ve added these last few paragraphs at the lab. Oleander had a few last things to take care of, and didn\u2019t want any of us anywhere near the chemical, so we\u2019ve been cooling our heels here for a few minutes. And it\u2019s given me time to think.<br /> <br /> A few weeks ago, we noticed that Marguerite was acting strangely, in ways that seemed to be out-of-character for her. When things came to what seemed to be a crisis point, Calamity took action, believing her \u201cdarkling sister\u201d to be both under Chalcedony\u2019s sway and in immediate danger. As a result, their relationship was badly damaged, and they are only just now starting to return to the easy friendship they had before.<br /> <br /> Is this situation really so different? Someone I care about is acting strangely, and seems to be under the sway of a powerful magical or psychological effect, and we\u2019re about to respond to that violently. But do I really know Rowan well enough to judge her mental state and take this sort of action? What if her relationship with the house is some sort of weird symbiosis? I have no evidence that either of them has ever harmed anyone directly (aside from Rowan\u2019s assault on Felicity earlier, of course). Do we have the right to strike out against it in such a deadly way without proof that it means this community harm?<br /> <br /> And\u2026 whether she\u2019s under its control or not, will Rowan ever forgive me for this?<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 09-25-2016, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T13:15:17-07:00","id":976067,"title":"","content":"<b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> Monday, November 23rd<br /> Nine years, six months, twenty-eight days<br /> Days without stabbing: 5<br /> <br /> I'm going to stab a house. Well, most likely I'm going to stab it. I've never fought a house before and apparently we're going to spiritually salt the earth it sits on to try to poison it first But once we've pissed it off and weakened it I'll get to stab it. I've got an iron spike and a hammer from Gawain's workshop so I should get to stab it with that (to check and see if it's a Gentry) if nothing else. Beats watching Titanic (well, I guess we might still watch it after this is over. It's not that late. Defeat the monster and then celebrate with a light lunch and movie...) Strangely, I am not as excited (as in my panties are still dry) as I (and anyone who's met me) would normally expect. Is this proof that I'm a better person now? I don't really like it. I'm anxious and uncertain. This isn't fucking fair. It's a problem I can stab in it's gorram face (Siding? Where do you stab a house?) and it's still all fucking complicated and hazy. Times like this I think maybe there is a god, this much fucking unfairness can't be random chance. But I just can't let go of the fact that we don't really know what we're doing. Yeah, that's right, I'm the one not in favor of blindly rushing into something. But dammit, I fucked shit up with Insincere Marguerite and Chalcedony by not thinking things through and despite popular belief I can fucking learn from my mistakes.<br /> <br /> Based on how Rowan is acting something is seriously off and the house is at the center of it. I just can't help but think of Mary and her fetch and the link they shared. The others seemed to doubt it but in the end Insincere Marguerite asked White Maria to go and be on hand to heal Rowan if she starts taking damage from the house fight. Dammit, I should be giddy and dancing in my seat and chanting about getting to fight a house. This responsible shit is seriously overrated.<br /> <br /> Of course, some of the rain on my parade might be from other things weighing my mind down. Oh bloody hell where do I even begin with this mess with Desiree. Hell, I am reluctant to write anything down about it. But apparently we're in the middle of some hurry up and wait here in the van while Oleander finishes getting the Soul Roundup(tm) ready.<br /> <br /> Okay. Start at the beginning then. So this morning started fucking perfectly with me laying in a light doze curled up with Handsome and Beautiful. But my forms and sparring start sharply at dawn with White Maria. So I forced myself out of that heaven and snagged my beautiful dragon a sweet. She knew what I wanted as soon as she blinked sleepily at me and took it, but I teased her about needing a little Spring pick me up so I could go get hot and sweaty with her best friend and she just rolled her eyes and, as the kids are calling it these days, 'poofed' me. Then she yawned and curled up with Gawain to drift back to sleep till a more reasonable hour. I lingered a minute, just looking at the two of them. What the fuck did I ever do to deserve two such amazing people in my life? But you know, the universe isn't fair. We like to complain about that when it fucks us over but it also means that sometimes a twisted little thing like me gets to have her fairytale Knight and her Dragon both.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I tore myself away from watching my lovers sleep like the Darkling I am and hit the road to White Maria's. She was, of course, flawless when she greeted me and we warmed up with our Tai Chi forms and then she set to training me in Jujitsu. Before I started with her, I would never have put much stock in that whole Feng Shui thing but her dojo is truly spiritual. It feels so strange to be relearning things I know so well but this is a whole different outlook and approach to fighting. And it's actually harder coming at it with my skills because I have to not follow my reflexes and instincts. I should ask Jacob if it's slowing me down in our post therapy sparring. I mean, eventually I'll be able to blend the things I've learned together but I have to focus on learning the new before I start to incorporate it into my fighting. I should speak to Luna about how best to merge them as well. Of course, it did not help this morning (was it really that recently? This has been a long day.) that I was worried about White Maria and Insincere Marguerite. Of course, I know now what was actually weighing on my Darkling Sister of late. It's still not the best relationship between them as it's built quite firmly on the lingering traits of who they were in Arcadia but they do both seem to know that and while they're both friends it isn't really my place to go telling them what they should do in the bedroom (or the balcony apparently...) But at the time, I was worried there was something deeper going on and I thought about trying to talk to White Maria about it a couple of times but I never managed to find a way to bring it up.<br /> <br /> Then on my way back things took a turn. I was still musing on the situation with White Maria and Insincere Marguerite and the balance of not getting into their fucking business verses being friends with them and worried. I spotted the Handmaidens as I was cutting through one of the seedier parts of town (what, it's shorter and I can handle myself... and okay maybe I wouldn't be that upset if someone gave me an excuse to do some violence upon their person) So, because I am a suspicious little thing I coasted over and circled back to follow them into the secluded alleyway. I got there in time to see Madam Spidertoes coalesce out of a mass of spiders, which shouldn't have been that shocking given her powerful grasp of the Contract of Fang and Talon and all. But still, knowing that someone can do a thing and watching a mass of spiders come together to form a woman are completely different things. The Handmaidens bowed to her and they spoke briefly in Russian (I think). It was definitely Slavic. Jacob might be able to tell me if I can recall it clearly enough and I ask him. But really it's not a critical detail and I'm not sure I can bring it up without crossing into the (less secret now than it was) alliance between the Night and Autumn courts. Of course, I don't know if this was an official clandestine meeting or an unofficial one. Spidertoes unlocked a door and they all headed inside. I tried to creep in after to satisfy my Darkling curiosity but Madam froze, said something in Russian, and exploded into spiders to start searching the area. So, busted as I was, I withdrew and presented myself.<br /> <br /> Maybe not the best move to reveal myself but I figured maybe I'd get some answers. Madam Spidertoes was aloof and seemed irritated that I was there. I was perhaps less respectful than usual though I wasn't outright rude to her. I can't help it, I dislike anyone being possessive of me and the situation with Leanne still grates on my nerves. I told her straight up that I was curious and she responded that she didn't have enough tea for four and told me to go home. Which did not help my disposition but I was the one eavesdropping and creeping so I let it slide.<br /> <br /> And that is what brought me to draw Insincere Marguerite aside to speak privately after breakfast. She's Night Court so I wanted to share what I'd witnessed to her. Also, if I disappear suddenly someone should know to check the Children's Library for a Calamity-sized cocoon. Though maybe if I'm lucky she'll sic the Handmaidens on me. It's really no secret that I'm a sucker for Leechfingers and as much as I hate to admit it, I would almost certainly enjoy being murdered by those two.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I stepped into a side room with Insincere Marguerite to talk to her and she was quite interested and likewise quite curious about what Spidertoes was up to. And while we were alone, I could see she was still troubled and I reached out to her. She hesitated. She admitted she needed to talk to someone but that she found it hard to trust me not to do what I felt was best even if it wasn't what she wanted. It hurt, moreso because it was true. I could see that she wanted to be able to talk to me. That she wanted the friend I used to be. And it was clear that wasn't who she saw before her. Fuck I thought it hurt when she was angry and afraid of me. But seeing her like that was worse. I offered to make a pledge. She seemed a bit surprised and she shook her head, pointing out how I chafe at being bound. She mentioned how I can tell you down to the hour how long my oath to the Freehold has left. And it's true. I hate being bound by a pledge, even one to do what I would do anyway. But I hate that she can't trust me even more and the truth is she can't. What she can trust in is the Wyrd. So I told her she was right and that my willingness to make this oath was proof of my desire to be there for her and help. Of how much I missed her friendship. In the end, we made one for a year. Maybe... Maybe after that she won't need it. Maybe. But not breaking a magically binding promise means nothing. Especially not after the way I broke her trust. I hate that it has to be this way but it's my own fault and if it allows us to be closer... to get back to even a shadow of the bond we had before... I'll happily bear this particular chain for however long it takes.<br /> <br /> But what she told me. I am afraid to put it in writing. If the wrong people find out it would be the end of her. Her and Desiree both. Beyond that, this is a terrible strain on her. This pulls her back toward the person she was. The person she doesn't want to be anymore. The person she doesn't want to be again. I hugged her and held her and promised I'd help. I reminded her that she was stronger than this. Better than this. Because she is.<br /> <br /> She admitted that part of why she'd been hesitant to tell me is that she feared I would kill Desiree. It was a fair concern honestly. Killing her would solve this. Hell, I'm pushing the limits of my leash by staying quiet about it. But what Insincere Marguerite is doing is preventing Desiree from being a threat to the Freehold. And that's why she did it. She spoke of the desperation in Desiree when she coaxed her into this. How clearly she feared that unless she was stolen from her Keeper she'd lack the strength to disobey him.<br /> <br /> I can understand why she did it. I can understand why she choose Insincere Marguerite. She could see that deep down Insincere Marguerite wanted to do what she felt she needed someone to do. I get it, but that doesn't mean I'm not upset that she's put this on my sister. But Insincere Marguerite believes that she acted out of fear that she can't trust herself and that she wasn't and isn't intentionally trying to corrupt her.<br /> <br /> And, truth be told, I have grown fond of the woman. She has shown herself to be a friend to the motley. I believe she wants to leave her loyalist past behind. I believe that she felt this was the best way, maybe even the only way, to do that. And she choose my Darkling Sister because she knew she would want this. The problem is she likes it too much, and sees how it tempts her back to her old ways. And this is a thing that no Changeling can be. There are few enough lines between us and the Gentry. There are things no Changeling should ever do. Things we cannot allow ourselves to do. Not even for the best of reasons. This is the path that claimed Darke. I cannot let my Darkling Sister be drawn down it.<br /> <br /> Thankfully, I was able to do more than just console and comfort Insincere Marguerite. We spoke about what could be done. Insincere Marguerite is terrified that Lori will find out. She is sure that Lori would not understand and would turn away from her for doing this. She told me that she would kill Desiree before let that happen. I cannot recall her ever speaking so unequivocally about murder. That is not her way. She hates killing. I have no doubt that she means it. I told her that if it comes to that, I will be there. I also told her I would do my best to see that it never comes to that.<br /> <br /> Desiree needs help. She is damaged deep inside. She cannot trust herself without a Keeper to guide her and protect her. She made mistakes, terrible ones, and put herself in a bad place. If the Director had not found her, she would likely be dead by now or worse, living in the hellish limbo of selling herself to afford the drugs to dull the horror of living so desperately. I think she fears that without someone she will wind up back there. Insincere Marguerite said she thought that what Desiree needed was the therapy of the clinic but, obviously, they can't be trusted not to speak of her and Insincere Marguerite's pledge. But I told her Gawain and I could try dream healing. We're both skilled Oneiromancers and she trusts Gawain. Insincere Marguerite listened and there was a glimmer of real hope. If we can help Desiree face her demons and free herself from the need to be kept then my Darkling Sister can release her from her pledge without her being a threat to the freehold and in doing so free herself from the weight and temptation she's taken on.<br /> <br /> Desiree and Lori have both approached me to see what's wrong. I wasn't ready to talk to Desiree about this earlier and I can't say anything to Lori. It was hard to put her off. She was clearly concerned and the fact that I wouldn't say only made her more worried. In the end I did promise her I'd tell her if there was anything she could do to help. I know how deeply she fears and hates being kept. I don't know if it would be the end of her relationship with Insincere Marguerite as my Darkling Sister fears but it would never be the same between them if she found out. I can't be the cause of that.<br /> <br /> And that's part of why I haven't told Gawain yet. I've been avoiding him since my talk with Insincere Marguerite but I'm sure he's got an inkling something is up, elemental he may be but he knows me too well to miss my tells and frankly I have been on edge over this all day. I don't know how he's going to take this revelation. He cares deeply... oh fucking hell, let's be fucking honest, he loves Desiree. I have to explain this carefully. I should do it in a dream. Better to be sure we are completely private until he's got a handle on the situation. I just hope I don't screw it up. This whole situation is a fucking powder keg on a tightrope. One misstep and the whole damn Last Dance could go down in flames.<br /> <br /> But Julia's right, I can't delay either. When we were alone at the library researching what the fuck Rowan's house might be she opened up a bit. Or, more accurately, she let loose and vented. It was actually nice to have her willing to speak to me like that again. Not so nice to see how stressed she is about things. She's really on edge about DLR and Lori not wanting to join in a group love pledge with her and Insincere Marguerite. And despite how my Darkling Sister assured me she was fine with the arrangement between her and Desiree, I think the fact that it's weighing on Insincere Marguerite is bothering her. Both because she loves her and because it's keeping her from being emotionally able to help Julia deal with her insecurities and fears and jealousy. I did want I could, but Julia just can't grasp that some of us aren't comfortable with pledges at all, no matter what it is. Hell, when I pointed out that Gawain and I don't have a pledge either she just demanded to know why not and barely stopped short of questioning my feelings for him. So, yeah, I don't think I was as helpful there but I do think the venting helped her a little at least.<br /> <br /> What I really need right now is a good, hard, knock-down drag-out fight leading into being fucked so fucking senseless that I can't remember my own name more less all of this shit but that is not in the cards for this little monster.<br /> <br /> So, the library gave us some possibilities but nothing definite and our best guess doesn't really match what we know. Trying to sort out a plan was frustrating. We don't know what the damn thing is so we can't be sure how to deal with it. Lori is frazzled and worried about Rowan. Luna is just dead set on setting the house on fire. Jacob is calm but doesn't know what to do any more than I do. DLR called Spidertoes to see if she knew any of the former residents but it seems Rowan is the first Changeling to live in the house. She's only the latest in a long line of young attractive single blonde women to live there. And knowing they\u2019re not Changelings means the fact that none of them seemed to age in the twenty years or so each lived there before just vanishing.<br /> <br /> And apparently Dahlia was feeling left out of the crazy party so when I called her to mention that, you know, there may be a man eating house in the Freehold she went off on a rant. That was weird, I mean, I knew she's got issues when it comes to sex but she's never admitted that her self-imposed chastity was rooted in her firm belief that no one wants to fuck 'leaky' as she put it rather vividly. And trying to point out that having shards of glass growing out through my skin hadn't stopped me from getting around didn't get anywhere. Stranger than the outburst was the call a few minutes later to apologize for it. I am officially worried about her at this point. And I cannot help but worry that watching Chalcedony is at least part of it. Maybe not the root cause, but if she's developing feels for that gorram blue temptress that could be making her whole who would ever want to fuck me issues kick into high gear. I know I hate that bitch and it's making me be even more paranoid than usual but fuck if the shoe fits wear it.<br /> <br /> I've assured Dahlia that we've got this house under control but she wants an update after it's over to