tely and they did. A few minutes later they came back with Marguerite looking like she had before and Calamity acting a little off, like she was upset by something. I could only guess what was said, but if I had to I\u2019d say that Marguerite told Calamity about Desiree. Both Desiree and Lori asked Calamity if she was okay, and both times she said that she was a little upset but okay. She also told them both that she couldn\u2019t talk about what was bothering her.<br /> <br /> A few minutes later my theory was proven right. I asked to speak to Insincere Marguerite alone and apologized for my behavior yesterday. I said I was sorry for being so distant and not being more emotionally available during our talk. I know that she was looking for support and I was sorely lacking in the empathy department. I explained that I\u2019m not good at expressing my feelings and that I\u2019ve actually had problems with that lately. I did not go into details since the conversation was not supposed to be about me. This instance just brought home how detached I\u2019ve become. I don\u2019t like it. What Insincere Marguerite told me yesterday should have shocked me a great deal more than it did, but instead I reacted like I was hearing that it was going to be sunny tomorrow. That is not right. I know that there is something wrong with me, and I\u2019m working on it in my therapy sessions, but nothing has happened yet. Nothing is fixed. I don\u2019t know what I was expecting, but I think it was more than this. I feel like I\u2019ve failed my friend. I should have been more receptive but instead I respond with little to no emotion. What is wrong with me? Am I getting too close to what I was before? Am I becoming more like Rime that Jacob? How do I stop this decent?<br /> <br /> Anyway, Marguerite explained that she had told Calamity about what happened with Desiree and that Calamity had offered to try and help Desiree get over her fear of decision making by doing dream healing with her and Gawain. Insincere Marguerite seemed a little optimistic about that idea, but not really excited. She also had Calamity take an oath to not tell anyone else about the situation with Desiree and to not act on anything related to that problem without first clearing it with Marguerite. In other words, no stabbing Desiree or beating her senseless because Calamity thinks it will solve the problem. This was probably a good idea on Insincere Marguerite\u2019s part. Calamity can be impulsive at times and likely would have reacted in anger if given the opportunity to do so.<br /> <br /> Not long after all that Lori called a motley meeting. We all met up in the living room and she told us what was going on with Rowan. Lori had talked to Rowan earlier and invited the shy selkie back to the Dream House to join us for movie night. Rowan accepted, but during the conversation kept going on and on about how she was upset that people were making her leave her house. It had been decided by a good number of people in the Day court to have Rowan sleep somewhere else for the night so the house could be investigated further. It was not intended to be a permanent arrangement, but the way Rowan was reacting you\u2019d have thought that it was. She kept going on about <i><i>her house</i></i> and how she didn\u2019t want to leave it. Lori was concerned about Rowan\u2019s out-of-character and obsessive reaction to the idea of moving out of her house for a day or two. We discussed ways to get Rowan to leave the house for the night at least, but nothing definitive was decided. Luna suggested that we get Rowan out and just burn the house down. While that may be a good solution to the problem it might hurt Rowan somehow and I brought that up. We should make sure that the connection between Rowan and the house doesn\u2019t go so deep that the selkie would be hurt when and if the house was damaged.<br /> <br /> It was also suggested that we look in the Autumn archives to see if they have any information on what kind of phenomenon might be going on with the house. Calamity and Julia went and had a look around to see what they could find. When they got back they said that they had come across information on a couple of different possibilities. They did not think that the house was haunted so that ruled that out. There were also records of a different house having been a Gentry, but in that instance it only targeted humans and actively tried to stay off the radar of any Changelings. The last option was that it might be something called a Dionaea house, which gets its name from the Venus Flytrap for good reason. Usually those kinds of houses have an inhabitant that acts as a kind of bait and lures other people in. The only problem with this idea is that Lori has slept in that house with no ill effect. Nor has the house tried to do anything to Rowan. In fact, according to research done by Felicity the house\u2019s previous inhabitants were all young women around 20 years old, and they all lived in the house for 10 \u2013 20 years without incident. The eerie thing about that is that no matter when a picture was taken of the women that lived in the house they always looked 20 years old. They did not seem to age at all, and they just suddenly dropped off the radar. There have been no obituaries or anything like that for the previous inhabitants. De la Rocha confirmed with Madame Spidertoes that they were not Changelings. She did not know any of the names, so we\u2019re pretty sure that they were all mortal.<br /> <br /> Got a bit ahead of myself there. Spidertoes wasn\u2019t contacted until after De la Rocha got back from work. Before that happened Insincere Marguerite came into the room and said that there had been some news on Rowan. Apparently the Day courtiers showed up armed with axes in case the house tried to trap them inside or anything like that. They had no plans on using the weapons but wanted to be prepared just in case. We really don\u2019t have any idea what we\u2019re dealing with. Well, Rowan was very upset by the people with axes and got more and more agitated as she packed her bag. Then all of a sudden she snapped and attacked Felicity. She tried to strangle the other Day courtier. The others pulled Rowan off of Felicity and bodily removed her from the house. She was brought back to Felicity\u2019s house to keep her away from the little house on the beach and to keep her safe from herself or anything else. Later she was allowed to call Lori and expressed her concerns that it was Felicity that really wanted to take the house away from her and that is why she wanted to get her out of the place. She expressed concerns that Felicity was being corrupted by the Night Court and that it was really them that wanted her house. Talk about paranoia. She seems to really believe that someone is trying to steal her house from her.<br /> <br /> Several people were really surprised by Rowan\u2019s behavior and Insincere Marguerite said that we all have our baser natures that we don\u2019t usually act on, but sometimes circumstances bring them to the fore. Calamity agreed and I couldn\u2019t help but think of my own baser nature. For a long time I was not a good person. I hurt people, I took them from their homes, I killed people, and all of it for my Lady. I remembered one time there was a girl, I don\u2019t remember her name now, that came across me while I was walking in the woods. She was lost and scared and I figured that I\u2019d play the lost boy and help her out. It didn\u2019t take long to realize that once she\u2019d found her \u201cprotector\u201d she expected to be handed things. She never helped with the hunting and was miserable at making a fire. Of all the important things you\u2019d think that making a fire would be one of the first things that she mastered. But no, she relied on others to do those things for her. Apparently she had been with a small group but suddenly found herself alone one morning. She was