aper so I can analyze them later. The only problem is that I haven\u2019t been doing that so much lately. My journal entries read like mission reports. I don\u2019t like what I see. I don\u2019t want to go back to what I was. I don\u2019t want to become Rime again.<br /> <br /> Anyway, De La Rocha came back after talking to Madame Spidertoes again with another suggestion. Spidertoes had suggested that a certain chemical poison may work to prove if the house is a Dionaea house or not. Apparently we just need to spread some of this stuff around the foundation of the house and wait to see what happens. If the house suddenly starts acting sick then we know it\u2019s a Dionaea house. Granted this stuff will poison just about anything or anyone, but if the house itself reacts then that tells us what we need to know. The poison that Spidertoes suggested is really strong stuff. The only person that can make it is Oleander. So, Lori called Oleander, who had been planning on going into the Hedge today, and talked to her about this chemical. It\u2019s something of a controlled substance due to its strong properties so Oleander would have to tell Queen Charlotte who she is giving this stuff to and why. Oleander didn\u2019t seem to think that this would be a problem since it was Spidertoes that recommended it in the first place. Oleander also said that she would apply the chemical herself. She said it was too dangerous to be handled by those without experience dealing with deadly poisons. And apparently this one not only kills any and all vegetation for about 6 months, it also weakens the connection between a person\u2019s body and soul and can render a physical location as a spiritual dead zone for a while. Talk about scary stuff.<br /> <br /> So, the plan as it stands is to go to Rowan\u2019s house and try driving an iron nail into the wall. I suggested it as if we were hanging a picture. I figured it would confirm whether or not the house is a Gentry in disguise and/or if the house will allow us to make changes to it like adding a new picture. Right now all of the stuff in the house appears to be the same age, like it was all acquired or showed up at the same time. Usually people add knickknacks to their residence over the years and make changes to decorations. This does not appear to be the case with Rowan. So, we\u2019ll try the nail and see what happens. After that we\u2019ll spread the chemical around the base of the house and see what occurs. And before we try anything Calamity said that she needs to call Dahlia to let her know when we\u2019re going in and to call back within four hours of doing so. If we do not call she will assume that something has happened to us and will send help. She had called the Winter Courtier since the house could pose a threat to the Freehold and Calamity is oath bound to report anything like that. Seems like a good precaution to me. I will admit to being curious about what\u2019s going on with Rowan\u2019s house. It should be an interesting afternoon.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> A chronological recounting of the days events is not, I think, the best way to explain what has happened. I will discuss news in my affairs<br /> <br /> <u>Desiree</u><br /> <br /> I spoke to Calamity, possibly against my better judgment, about Desiree. Jacob seemed rather helpless for what to do. Calamity offered her and Gawain\u2019s services to repair her psyche, possibly give her some sort of bolstering of confidence. Enough to, if nothing else, face the world with a Motley and lovers at her back. We cannot trust the Winter Court\u2019s doctors as they would be (rightfully) obligated to report to Lowjack, and that cannot happen.<br /> <br /> This offers I hope. If the pair can fix Desiree, I will happily rescind control of her. I wanted it, I thought, but when faced with the reality, it terrified me. There is a monster behind my eyes and Desiree is bringing it out. No, my relationship with Julia is as much control as I need.<br /> <br /> Calamity is Pledged to not reveal my secret. Even if she thinks she knows better than I, she is unable to act on that. Hopefully.<br /> <br /> Jacob apologized for being distant yesterday. That was nice. He realized he hurt I, and wants to make amends. I am happy to get our issues out of the way.<br /> <br /> <u>Julia</u><br /> <br /> Julia had an explosive venting at Calamity while they were doing research about her fears with Lori. She confessed after. I really, really hoped Lori\u2019s earnest declaration of love last night would be enough, but like many of our kind, she values pledges above words. I have sternly told her to drop the matter. We will work it out, and discuss this when not so much is pressing. We have a wonderful relationship with Lorelei and Maria. I do not wish to see it threatened. I must ask Calamity to keep it to herself.<br /> <br /> I think our family can be a wonderful thing. But Julia must have patience and not be clingy. I love Julia so much. So artistic, so sophisticated. I can appreciate art but I have not her talent for it. But she is a creature of fiery passion, and we must make allowances for that.<br /> <br /> Minor concern, Julia was generally somewhat cool to Oleander, despite the Elemental\u2019s romantic and sexual interest in her for some time. She has not been rude to Oleander, but the short haired butch dressed botanist had little appeal for her for awhile. She has spent a lot more time with her, even sketching her, which is somewhat flirtatious for her, and I have heard them flirting. This is almost certainly purely good; Presuming Lori is not concerned if Oleander and Julia start spending more time together. God I hope this does not bring more drama into the family. At least she is still okay with spending time with Maria and I. If Julia is getting some interest in Oleander, we will see what happens. Femmes are usually more her thing, but then she fell for me hard enough to plow a path to Australia, so one never knows.<br /> <br /> <u>White Maria</u><br /> <br /> Calamity reports she seems well.<br /> <br /> <u>Madame Spidertoes</u><br /> <br /> Was meeting with the Handmaidens. I doubt they were plotting the overthrow of the freehold, but I am damn curious what they were up to.<br /> <br /> <u>Rowan and Felicity</u><br /> <br /> The rest of the updates were positive, if with caveats. This is dark and getting darker and dangerous.<br /> <br /> Felicity met with Rowan, who argued but agreed to leave her house temporarily, at least one night, for safety. Lori spoke with Rowan and noted the possessiveness with which she described her house. I understand possessiveness, but I am given to understand it was unusual for Rowan. However, suspicion turned to certainty when Rowan first resisted leaving for the night then attacked Felicity, choking her. Fortunately, Felicity had goons from the LA Day Court backing her up.<br /> <br /> Before this Julia and Calamity went to the Autumn Court library. This was where Julia had her aforementioned meltdown. They went over several possibilities, but it seemed most likely a Gentry or something called a Dionaea House, some sort of predatory building. The latter seems most likely, they often have a lure, but the possessiveness seems strange, and they are unrelated to Changelings as far as we know.<br /> <br /> Rowan was taken to Felicity\u2019s house. There she was locked away, though she called Lori twice after I gave Felicity permission to have her do so. Felicity did research there, while Maria spoke with Spidertoes and Calamity spoke with Dahlia. Luna kept trying to convince us to burn it outright.<br /> <br /> Poor Lori was not, and is not, taking this well. Rowan\u2019s pleading upsets her, as is Rowan being held against her will by Felicity. But we want to help her. Lori is strong, but compassionate. It is a reason I love her, that Julia and Maria love her.<br /> <br /> Felicity discovered the girls were in the house no more than twenty years each, and best we could tell did not age. Spidertoes did not know their names, and it is unlikely they are Fae. She suggested a compound that Oleander could put her hands on be spread at the base of the house. She also warned us to be careful. Oleander knew of the stuff, but had to tell Charlotte she was using it. She usually denies it exists. She insisted on spreading it herself. Says it is dangerous, damaging even the soul of the one exposed, and that that area would be spiritually dead a bit. Needless to say, it is rare. Still, she agreed (Lori has a way of having people be agreeable) and said she needed time to prepare it.<br /> <br /> The second of Rowan\u2019s calls was around then, begging for company. Did she know? We are setting out now. The affair of the House will be dealt with one way or the other.<br /> <br /> Felicity will be pleased. But I must go.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXV</i><br /> <br /> This was a hard session to do, as a lot of action took place away from the PCs. Still I felt it went well. Made the pacing dramatic. And dramatic pacing was the name of the game here, building tension with Rowan\u2019s dwindling sanity.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite and Julia helped maintain the tension with their issues, though, and it looks like we are building to something.<br /> <br /> So what happens next? You will see next time. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T18:16:56-07:00","id":983657,"title":"","content":"A spiritual dead zone... Might that warrant the attention of the local packs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T23:59:39-07:00","id":983794,"title":"","content":"That was discussed.you will see what happened, tho, in about 24 hours. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T14:06:26-07:00","id":984591,"title":"","content":"In which our heroes go House hunting.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LXVI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Tuesday morning. The House has been dealt with, so that\u2019s one less thing we have to worry about (the aftereffects and consequences are another story, of course, but I\u2019m getting ahead of myself). I am weary, but more than that\u2026 I\u2019m scared, and angry, and depressed. And I just extricated myself from Maria\u2019s sleepy embrace because it just seems wrong to feel that way when she\u2019s holding me. That\u2019s when I should be at my happiest, my most content. Negative emotions seem almost like blasphemy under those circumstances.<br /> <br /> So as you might have guessed, things didn\u2019t go smoothly in our endeavor to deal with Rowan\u2019s House. First, as we were driving between Oleander\u2019s place and Rowan\u2019s, Marguerite got a call from Felicity. Rowan had apparently slipped the net and gone missing. We\u2019re still not sure exactly how she did it. According to her guardians, she didn\u2019t leave by the door, and the room had no windows, so she must have used some sort of Contract. But however she managed it, she was missing.<br /> <br /> Calamity used her Contracts \u2013 the same ones she used to find Mr. Grey a few months ago \u2013 to locate Rowan, and quickly determined that she was somehow directly ahead of us at a distance which would place her roughly in the area of her House. I called Oleander \u2013 who had driven her own car due to her highly toxic state \u2013 to let her know, and she let Gawain pass her and settled into position behind us. It seemed likely that we would find Rowan waiting for us when we got to her House, and I didn\u2019t want the first thing she saw upon our approach to be Oleander in her haz-mat suit with a large spray gun full of poison pointed at her. Oleander agreed with the logic of this stance, and said she would be ready to back us up if necessary.<br /> <br /> When we got there, things were as bad as we\u2019d feared. Rowan sat on her front porch, looking decidedly disheveled. Her usually sleek hair was a rat\u2019s nest, her clothing was in disarray, and she held a wicked-looking harpoon out in front of her with both hands. Even from the driveway I could see that she was twitching and shaking badly.<br /> <br /> Gawain got carefully out of the van, and I followed him. I actually wanted to approach Rowan on my own, but pretty much every other member of the motley (and Oleander) voted this plan down. So defenseless li\u2019l me got to hide behind big, burly Gawain while approaching my newest girlfriend\u2026 who probably weighs a hundred pounds when she\u2019s soaking wet. A soft whisper in my ear let me know that Marguerite was close by as well, invisibly watching over me.<br /> <br /> \u201cRowan sweetie\u2026 can I talk to you?\u201d I called tentatively as we approached.<br /> <br /> She choked up her grip on the harpoon and threw Gawain a seriously dark look, but she also nodded. \u201cJust\u2026 don\u2019t try to hurt my House,\u201d she said in a quavery voice. \u201cAnd\u2026 and don\u2019t get between me and anyone who tries to hurt my House.\u201d Her look turned almost desperate. \u201cI don\u2019t want to hurt you, Lorelei\u2026 I love you. But I have to protect my House.\u201d<br /> <br /> I held my hands out in an attempt to placate her. \u201cNobody\u2019s going to do anything yet,\u201d I said soothingly. \u201cWe just want to talk. We just want to understand what\u2019s going on here, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded, then she sort of half-smiled. \u201cYou don\u2019t have to hold your hands out like that, Lorelei. I trust you.\u201d I wonder if that still holds true in the wake of what happened later.<br /> <br /> I tried to talk her down, I really did. She seemed to take everything I said at face value, and it was like she really <u>wanted</u> to believe me, but whatever hold the House had over her wouldn\u2019t let her drop her guard. She tearfully informed me several times that she wouldn\u2019t hurt me, but could not extend that promise to anyone else. I was able to approach her without incident, but when Gawain tried to do the same, she brandished the harpoon at him in a threatening fashion.<br /> <br /> It quickly became obvious that even though she trusted me, conversation wasn\u2019t going to get us anywhere with Rowan. Though I didn\u2019t realize what was happening at the time, I later learned that while I was trying to talk Rowan down, Calamity was sneaking around the corner of the House with one of Gawain\u2019s iron nails. She drove it into the side of the House in an attempt to determine whether or not it was a Gentry.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m\u2026 still not sure <u>what</u> it was, exactly, but it did <u>not</u> like being stabbed in the side with an iron nail. It sort of rose up off of its foundations first, and all of these little shadows flitted out from under it in every direction before we could react to what was happening. I don\u2019t know what they were. The souls of those the House had consumed? The remnants of its former owners? Its young? Whatever they were, we had bigger problems to deal with at that moment.<br /> <br /> As I said, the House rose up a few feet off the ground, extending shadowy spider-like legs from beneath itself. It started to scuttle away, and of course we weren\u2019t having any of that. Gawain caught Rowan in a bear hug (mostly to stop her from hurting herself) and the others unleashed a flurry of attacks against the wayward structure. Gawain handed the selkie off to me a moment later so that he could join the fray. Ordinarily I\u2019m not much good at restraining people, but Rowan seemed as weak as a kitten. I think Marguerite might have had something to do with that, in retrospect.<br /> <br /> Some of the motley (like Jacob) had difficulty damaging the imposing beast. Others (like Oleander, Julia and myself) opted not to attack it for one reason or another\u2026 I was trying to restrain Rowan while Oleander couldn\u2019t spray her poison at it because the others were clustered in close around it. Luna tossed a Molotov cocktail into the House early on and then kept her distance. In the end, most of the close-in fighting was done by Gawain, Calamity, and D.<br /> <br /> D in particular struck the beast a mighty blow early in the fight, using every trick she knew to enhance her physical strength. She also drained a good bit of its health using her Leechfinger powers. And it\u2019s a good thing, too, because the House quickly decided that she was the biggest threat to its safety, and sort of <u>sat</u> on her. The whole weight of the structure came down atop her, and only her feet were sticking out from under it. I had the insane urge to laugh for a split-second as I remembered that scene from <u>The Wizard of Oz</u> where the Wicked Witch of the East is killed\u2026 and then reality hit me like a baseball bat to the face.<br /> <br /> \u201cD!\u201d I screamed, and the tears began to flow.<br /> <br /> Jacob was beside me a moment later (having given up on the notion of significantly damaging such a large opponent with his knives), and he took Rowan gently but firmly from my arms. \u201cGo,\u201d he said, \u201chelp her.\u201d<br /> <br /> I sprinted the short distance toward D, intent on healing as much of the damage as I could\u2026 but in the end it wasn\u2019t really necessary. The House shifted to attack Calamity, and D was able to extract herself. She had a few bad scrapes and bruises, but all in all it looked like the House had merely inconvenienced her for a while. \u201cMy God, sweetie,\u201d I said in a rush, \u201care you okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cI am,\u201d she said, then turned me to look at a spot four feet away, \u201cCalamity\u2019s not.\u201d<br /> <br /> Seeing that my love was in no immediate danger (well, no more than the rest of us, at least) I rushed over to Calamity and channeled as much power as I could into my healing Contracts. She was in pretty rough shape, but she wasn\u2019t quite gone yet, and I managed to bring her back from the brink. It took several applications of the Contract \u2013 mostly while she was still being crushed under the House \u2013 but by the time the fight was over, we\u2019d repaired most of the damage.<br /> <br /> As I said earlier, D, Calamity, and Gawain were able to beat the living sheetrock out of the House, though all of them had difficulty doing significant damage to something that size from time to time. In the end, I think Luna\u2019s firebomb may have been the deciding attack; the House eventually abandoned the fight and scuttled off into the ocean to quell the flames. Gawain and Calamity were having none of that, and chased it into the waves to deal the final blows.<br /> <br /> The House\u2019s end was horrible. It sort of shriveled and curled in on itself like a dying spider, coming to rest as a heap of rubble in the shallows. Down the pier, I noticed Rowan\u2019s boat doing the same thing, so I\u2019m guessing it must have been an extension of the creature we killed.<br /> <br /> Rowan loved that boat.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Rowan, she went sort of limp and catatonic as the House shivered through its death throes. We got her to the van, and I opened up the medical bag Gawain made me and ran a few tests\u2026 checking her pupils, her response to tactile and audio stimuli, etc. And while I can\u2019t be absolutely sure at the moment, I don\u2019t think this is due to any lingering supernatural effect. She seems to be experiencing a textbook case of shock.<br /> <br /> I threw myself into D\u2019s arms when she approached me and used what strength I had left to heal her (over her protests; she had already refused Marguerite\u2019s offer to let her drain a bit of vitality from her). Then I allowed myself to sag into her embrace for a few minutes while the others made sure everything was really over. Flashing red and blue lights and the distant sound of sirens encouraged us to hurry.<br /> <br /> We loaded up the van and Oleander\u2019s car and lit out for the territories. Unfortunately, we weren\u2019t quite quick enough to avoid police attention, and both Oleander and Gawain soon found themselves tailed by a few black and whites. D nervously informed us that if the cops checked her ID they\u2019d probably find that she has a few priors and maaaaaybe an outstanding warrant in her history, but in the end it wasn\u2019t much of a problem. When Gawain pulled over, the cops <u>did</u> check his license, but they didn\u2019t ask the rest of us for anything. That might have had something to do with me, as I did most of the talking when the officers approached. Plus I might have undone a button or three on my shirt.<br /> <br /> Oleander did not fare as well as we did, unfortunately. Due to her highly toxic nature, if she had allowed the cops to pull her over, it\u2019s fairly likely that she would have poisoned them, and they would have gotten sick or possibly even died. She related this to me when I called to check on her after our own police encounter. She also asked if there was anything we could do to get the heat off of her for a while.<br /> <br /> Calamity, Gawain, and Marguerite opted to come to her rescue. We dropped them off, and the three of them stole a car. Calamity used her Contracts to locate Oleander, and they plotted an intercept course. When they approached the scene of the chase, Calamity sideswiped one of the cruisers, and Marguerite used another Contract to blind the car\u2019s driver. They employed similar tactics against the remaining cops, and eventually both they and Oleander were able to get away.<br /> <br /> I heard about all of this after the fact, of course. They ditched the stolen car and called us for a pickup a few minutes later. I was\u2026 not particularly happy about the methods they had employed, which could have resulted in several dead cops who had only been doing their duty had things gone differently. I made my displeasure known to my friends, and Gawain backed me up with his own disapproving comments. D, on the other hand, only bemoaned the fact that she had missed out on all of the \u201cfun.\u201d She <u>really</u> doesn\u2019t like cops.<br /> <br /> Calamity took my chastisement with good grace, but Marguerite seemed oddly subdued. \u201cI am sorry I upset you, Lori,\u201d she said quietly as we rode back to the Dream House, \u201cI let myself get carried away.\u201d Something about the way she said it convinced me that she was really serious; she seemed honestly worried that I was mad at her.<br /> <br /> I turned toward her and smiled to let her know that this wasn\u2019t the case. \u201cI\u2019m glad you\u2019re okay,\u201d I said softly, \u201cand I can\u2019t thank you enough for everything you did tonight to help Rowan and Oleander. I really appreciate it, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> She smiled back, but still looked a little troubled. \u201c<i>Certainement, </i>\u201d she replied before turning back to Julia. Taking my cue from her, I spent the rest of the ride with my head on D\u2019s shoulder. She put an arm around me after a while, and occasionally I felt a feather-light kiss on the top of my head.<br /> <br /> Desiree, Gloria, and Jolie were waiting for us when we got back to the Dream House, eager to start watching <u>Titanic</u> with us. We put Rowan in my bedroom, with the understanding that D and I would sleep in Marguerite\u2019s room that night. Marguerite and Julia didn\u2019t intend to watch the movie with the rest of us, so they agreed to watch over Rowan while she slept, to make sure there weren\u2019t any lingering effects of the House\u2019s influence on her. Marguerite also called Felicity to let her know how things had gone.<br /> <br /> Marguerite was still acting strangely toward me, so I pulled her aside into a private room to talk with her about it. I had d\u00e9j\u00e0 vu during the first portion of this conversation; it was eerily similar to my talk with Calamity that morning.<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay, what\u2019s going on, Marguerite?\u201d I asked, full of concern. \u201cI can tell there\u2019s something wrong, and I wish you\u2019d let me help you.\u201d<br /> <br /> She didn\u2019t meet my eyes. \u201cI am sorry, Lori, but I cannot tell you,\u201d she muttered at last.<br /> <br /> \u201cDoes this have something to do with whatever you and Calamity talked about this morning?\u201d I asked suspiciously.<br /> <br /> She nodded.<br /> <br /> I sighed. \u201cWell, I won\u2019t ask you to break a pledge or anything like that. But I want you to promise me that you\u2019ll tell me if there\u2019s anything I can do to help, okay? I hate seeing you so upset, and I want you to know that you can tell me anything.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sometimes God laughs at our promises. This is something Dad told me when I was growing up. He didn\u2019t intend it to be in any way sacrilegious, of course\u2026 it was more of a homily about how you shouldn\u2019t make promises about things when you don\u2019t know all of the facts, and about how you have to honor your promises even when you made them foolishly. This was such an occasion.<br /> <br /> It came spilling out of her then. It has to do with Desiree. Our former Loyalist friend has no self-confidence. She doesn\u2019t believe that she is capable of making effective decisions on her own. Consequently, she feels that it is necessary for her to have someone to look after her and \u201cdirect\u201d her actions. When she was a Loyalist, the Director filled this role admirably.<br /> <br /> As she settled into her life in the Dream House, she became concerned. She worried that the Director would seek her out and use her as a weapon against the Freehold, and that she wouldn\u2019t be able to resist him. She sensed something in Marguerite, and came up with a solution. A <u>horrible</u> solution.<br /> <br /> She asked Marguerite to steal her from the Director. She asked Marguerite to become her new Keeper.<br /> <br /> She asked <u>Marguerite</u> to become her new <u>Keeper</u>. And Marguerite agreed!<br /> <br /> Marguerite went on for a while about how she didn\u2019t want to take on that role; she only did it to help Desiree and to protect the Freehold. And she\u2019s been actively trying to find a way to end the situation, to help Desiree to achieve true independence. We can\u2019t take her to the Winter Court\u2019s therapists, because if they found out what Marguerite had done, she\u2019d be exiled or worse. Hell, she\u2019s <u>already</u> been exiled from Paris on suspicion of doing exactly this. Calamity and Gawain are going to try to do some dream healing to repair Desiree\u2019s psyche. If it works, we might be able to resolve the whole situation without any more trouble.<br /> <br /> Except that\u2019s not really the point, is it?<br /> <br /> Marguerite is Keeping another changeling. I\u2019ve tried to get my head around that concept, and I just can\u2019t. She\u2019s always had certain\u2026 \u2018predilections,\u2019 but I never really thought she would go this far. And the more she talked about it, the more I felt my muscles locking up and my mind shutting down. Our embrace became stiff, and my body wanted me to pull away from her. It was instinctual: if she was a Keeper, then I needed to keep my distance.<br /> <br /> And then I looked into her eyes and saw how scared she was. I had told her months ago that I couldn\u2019t be with someone who would do that to another person. She trusted me enough to tell me about this, even knowing how I would feel about it. And I couldn\u2019t help but remember how I had felt when I thought she and Julia would be moving away and leaving the motley\u2026<br /> <br /> I tightened my grip and pulled her into a fierce hug. \u201cI hate this,\u201d I said sharply. \u201cI hate everything about it. But I know you did it for the right reasons. And if you <u>swear</u> to me that you\u2019re doing everything you can to end this situation\u2026\u201d I sighed and lowered my eyes. \u201cI trust you, Marguerite. I love you.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded and sniffed. \u201cWe will see what Gawain and Calamity can do for her, non? And if that does not resolve this\u2026\u201d she looked away from me for a moment. \u201cI would kill her before I would allow this to come between us, Juliette,\u201d she said softly.<br /> <br /> I felt an unfamiliar surge of rage pass up my spine. Yes, that would solve everything. Kill the little bitch who would dare to put my Marguerite in this position. \u201cIf I ever feel that we might lose you to Arcadia over this, I\u2019ll pull the damn trigger myself,\u201d I promised. Then the rage drained away, and we held each other for a little while before I excused myself to join the others in the entertainment room.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t really feel like watching a movie, but I wanted the time to think, and I didn\u2019t want the others to worry about me. As soon as I had said hello to Jolie, I strode over to Julia and kissed her passionately.<br /> <br /> \u201cNot that I\u2019m complaining,\u201d she said breathlessly as we disengaged, \u201cbut what was that for?\u201d<br /> <br /> I thought about it. \u201cFor not making me worry about you today,\u201d I said after a moment.<br /> <br /> Her face clouded over. \u201cWhat\u2019s wrong?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cI just had a talk with Marguerite,\u201d I said. When she just stared blankly at me, I elaborated a bit. \u201cA <u>serious</u> talk.\u201d<br /> <br /> Her face paled even further. \u201cOh God,\u201d she whispered.<br /> <br /> I put a hand on her shoulder. \u201cIt\u2019s okay,\u201d I said. \u201cI\u2019m not very happy right now, but nobody\u2019s yelling or crying or breaking up or leaving. We\u2019ll get through this.\u201d<br /> <br /> The relief on her face was truly beautiful. \u201cOh, thank God,\u201d she said, and returned my kiss with interest. \u201cI should go. I should be with her.\u201d And she bustled out of the room.<br /> <br /> I sat down next to D while the others got the movie ready. \u201cWhat was that all about?\u201d she asked out of the corner of her mouth.<br /> <br /> \u201cLater,\u201d I said shortly, and then lay down with my head in her lap. She sort of shrugged and began stroking my hair and my wings tenderly.<br /> <br /> The movie wasn\u2019t bad, honestly, though some of the romantic drama was a bit overblown in my opinion. It was more than three hours long, and I think I heard someone say at one point that the sinking of the ship was done in approximately real time. To be honest, I was only half paying attention to the action. Most of me was preoccupied with the twin problems of Rowan and Marguerite. At least the story was tragic enough that nobody batted an eye when I began to cry near the end.<br /> <br /> The crowds dispersed after that. I made sure to reiterate my promise to help Calamity in any way I could now that I knew what was at stake. As we staggered down the hall to Marguerite\u2019s bedroom, D pulled me to a stop. \u201cOkay, now you\u2019re going to tell me what\u2019s wrong, Jules.\u201d Her tone didn\u2019t allow for any arguments.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s\u2026 not my place,\u201d I said weakly. \u201cJust a second.\u201d And then I knocked on my own bedroom door softly.<br /> <br /> Marguerite answered a moment later like she\u2019d been expecting us. She briefly told D what she\u2019d told me, and just like me I saw D stiffen and clench. My love is used to dealing with her anger, however, and she was able to force it down before it became a problem.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe\u2019ll talk about this again after breakfast, and it won\u2019t be a problem,\u201d D said tightly.<br /> <br /> \u201cI love you, Maria,\u201d Marguerite said softly.<br /> <br /> \u201cI love you too,\u201d D replied in the same strained voice, \u201cwhich is why we\u2019ll talk about this again after breakfast, and it won\u2019t be a problem. If we continue to talk about it right now, it\u2019s going to become a problem. Good night.\u201d<br /> <br /> Marguerite closed the door, and the two of us retreated to her bedroom. \u201cJesus,\u201d D whispered as we disrobed and got ready for bed. And then, as though that hadn\u2019t quite expressed the full range of her feelings on the subject, she added \u201cfuck.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know,\u201d I said quietly as we slithered beneath the covers together. \u201cI know, babe\u2026 I feel it too. What the hell are we gonna do about this?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOnly thing we can, I guess,\u201d she said, holding me tightly against her, \u201ctry to fix this shit as fast as we can. And if we can\u2019t\u2026\u201d she hesitated, knowing I wouldn\u2019t like what she was going to say.<br /> <br /> I sighed. \u201cI know,\u201d I said again, sparing her the anguish. \u201cWe\u2019ll have to deal with it one way or another. I don\u2019t like hurting people, but I won\u2019t lose Marguerite if there\u2019s any way I can save her. I\u2019m with you on this one hundred percent, Maria.\u201d<br /> <br /> We were both quiet for a while, and I thought she had fallen asleep before I started crying again. She hadn\u2019t. She kissed away my tears before moving to my lips. \u201cHey, Jules, don\u2019t cry,\u201d she said with a warmth the others would never have believed. \u201cWe\u2019ll get through this. You and me, we\u2019re strong. We\u2019re fated. We\u2019re <u>forever</u>. And with Julia and the rest of the motley on our side, we\u2019ll find a way to get Mags out of this shit\u2026 <u>without</u> killing Desiree. I promise.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s not that,\u201d I choked out. \u201cI told her, Maria. Back at Calamity\u2019s birthday party, I <u>told</u> Marguerite that I couldn\u2019t be with anyone who would own another person. I told her that if I ever found out she was doing that, I would leave her.\u201d<br /> <br /> D shushed me gently. \u201cYou\u2019re not a robot, Jules. She did something stupid\u2026 but there are circumstances. And we love her. You can\u2019t be held to something you said in the heat of\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe scares me,\u201d I whispered into Maria\u2019s throat. \u201cI love her so much, but she scares me, Maria. And now I\u2019m afraid she always will.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll protect you, Lori,\u201d D said simply, tightening her grip on me, \u201calways.\u201d But she sounded sad as she said it.<br /> <br /> So it\u2019s with that lovely thought that we drifted off. According to the clock, I slept for about forty-five minutes, and woke up snuggled against D\u2019s chest feeling lonely and unsettled. I could have woken her to talk some more, I suppose, but that seemed needlessly selfish (she\u2019d had a hard day, after all). So I\u2019m sitting at Marguerite\u2019s desk and writing in this journal instead, trying to sort out how I feel about all of this instead.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s not true. I know how I feel about all of this. I hate it. I hate everything about it. But I will stand by Marguerite for as long as I can. It\u2019s what she would do for me, if our circumstances were reversed.<br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei Grace</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> Tuesday, November 24th<br /> Nine years, six months, twenty-seven days<br /> Days without stabbing: 0<br /> <br /> I fought the house and I won. Guess I can also say I fought the law and won. Hell, with all this winning, maybe I should get myself tested for tiger blood.<br /> <br /> Damn, I am so going to need someone to poof me. I haven\u2019t really slept and at this point I\u2019m not going to before therapy. Maybe Lori is up studying again and can help me. Sex breakfast is going to be interesting with everyone aware of the specifics of my Darkling Sister\u2019s relationship with Desiree. I am so, so glad that didn\u2019t go as badly as she feared it would. And relieved to not be keeping secrets from the motley myself. I know that was eating her up and I didn\u2019t really speak to her but she certainly seemed at least a little relieved when she when off with Julia to not watch Titanic. I wish I\u2019d been able to speak to her, but Julia was with her and I\u2019ll see her at breakfast I\u2019m sure.<br /> <br /> I just worry that things are still going to be weird for a while around here. Worse than that, I\u2019m afraid that even though we didn\u2019t have a blowout over it that it\u2019s going to strain relationships. Insincere Marguerite needs Lori and D\u2019s support right now to resist the temptation of who she was. She\u2019s trying to get away from her past, to move forward and be better than that. We need to focus on where she\u2019s going, not where she\u2019s been.<br /> <br /> Geez, I guess I have been listening to Dr Emmett. I sound like her now. But it\u2019s true. She needs support and encouragement right now and Zod knows as loathe as she is to admit to needing help or being less than perfect she\u2019s not going to ask for it twice.<br /> <br /> And all of this is happening right before Thanksgiving with Julia\u2019s parents. At least they\u2019re on board with their daughter being a polyamorous lesbian. I just hope the tensions don\u2019t bleed over and make things awkward. I.. I am going to stop thinking about this now. I don\u2019t need to be going down that mental road right now. I need to make sure word has been spread about the Dream House Thanksgiving. Should double check the order and with Gawain to be sure we\u2019ve got everything we need coming in for the food.<br /> <br /> Fuck. I am learning to hate this time of year fast. Can\u2019t swing a dead cat without hitting a gorram Norman Rockwell picture of a perfect fucking family. I got that fucking lie shoved down my throat in Snow Globe like that fucking picture perfect turkey got stuffed. Got carved up like it too more than once\u2026<br /> <br /> I miss them. I miss them so much. And it\u2019s my own fault. I killed them. No matter what I do I will never change what happened. No matter what I become, I will always be the monster that murdered her parents. Shit\u2026 I said I wasn\u2019t going to go there. Dammit, I\u2019m not going to cry. I don\u2019t deserve tears. I don\u2019t deserve pity. I fucking murdered them. And I can\u2019t even keep myself from fucking crying\u2026 Maybe I should raid the bar.<br /> <br /> Get your fucking act together woman. You are NOT going to show up to therapy shit-faced and crying. You are, however, going to fucking talk to Dr Emmett. about this. Then you\u2019re going to make sure things are actually alright between the quad and that the Dream House\u2019s Thanksgiving is mother fucking flawless. Because losing your family doesn\u2019t make you a special snowflake among the Lost and there are a lot of us feeling it this time of year. And unlike your murderous ass, they actually deserve to have some comfort and not be alone and miserable.<br /> <br /> Jesus Fucking Christ on a Mother-Loving Rascal. I do NOT have time for this maudlin bullshit right now. I think talking to Desiree in her dream must have set this off. I mean, this whole time of year has been ramping me up for it but it was talking to her that tipped it past the boiling point. But I am going to help her. We are going to help her. I believe we can do this. I wasn\u2019t just saying that for her. I do believe she\u2019s got the strength inside her to be her own person again. The Director did this, I have no doubt. He played on her self doubt and her bad choices and convinced her that she wasn\u2019t fit to take care of herself.<br /> <br /> And don\u2019t even fucking start on the comparisons. Desiree make a mistake that ruined her life. I flipped out and murdered two people that loved me. Not the same fucking thing at all.<br /> <br /> Yeah, not even going to go fucking anywhere near sleep right now. Not with my shit so fucking on edge. I don\u2019t need to see the damned puppet show my subconscious would make out of this right now.<br /> <br /> Shit. I am really a mess. I threw myself at that house spirit thing like a madwoman and the thing damn near killed me. I\u2019m better than that. Hell, that\u2019s the shit I\u2019m supposed to be good at and I was fucking up and distracting Gawain and forcing Lori to focus her healing on me. If I can\u2019t even get the fucking stabbing part right what the hell good am I?<br /> <br /> Focus you selfish bitch. Desiree needs your help. More importantly, Insincere Marguerite and Gawain need you to help her. Hell, the whole damn Motley needs this so that thrice-damned pledge can be removed. Get your head out of your ass and fucking help someone for a change. Gawain\u2019s right, she wants to be better. As fucked up as her decision was, she was trying to insure that she wasn\u2019t a danger to the Freehold. She was prepared to do whatever it took to insure that she wasn\u2019t a danger to Gloria. We can work with that. She wants to be better, she just needs a hand getting there.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite is trying to cast off the shackles of who she used to be as well. And Desiree didn\u2019t do this to intentionally drag her down or hold her back. I am sure of that or there would be blood. But this is weighing on her and she needs her family to be there for her to lean on right now. That might include me anymore, but I can help resolve what\u2019s coming between them.<br /> <br /> This isn\u2019t helping. I need to sit down and write out a report on what happened. I can have the rest take a look and send it out tomorrow afternoon. I have to send a copy to Dahlia so she can inform Lowjack. They should be keeping an eye out for whatever those little shadows might have been. The High Queen needs a copy and my own court is the most likely to be able to puzzle out what the fuck that was so one for Charlotte. I might need to take that one in person. I haven\u2019t heard anything from or about Leanne and I\u2019m a little worried. If Spidertoes hurt her for harming one of \u201cher\u201d Darklings without permission then we are going to have words. That woman does not own me and Leanne had permission from the one person that mattered, me.<br /> <br /> Focus Calamity.<br /> <br /> Alright, Augustine needs a copy since those little shadows might be some sort of threat to the Freehold. I suppose it would be tacky to cc Lucien but I\u2019m sure he reads all of Augustine\u2019s messages anyway. And I guess I should go ahead and make it all the monarchs and send a copy to Jolie as well. Fuck it, I\u2019ll just send her copy to Becky. She\u2019s the one that\u2019s actually going to dealing with it. I should go ahead and get to that. Might as well be productive.<br /> <br /> Man, I could really use a drink\u2026 Maybe just one. It\u2019s still a few hours till therapy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 10-09-2016, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T14:07:00-07:00","id":984592,"title":"","content":"<b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> I was right. This was definitely an interesting afternoon. It started off with a phone call to Insincere Marguerite from Felicity. Apparently Rowan got free from the locked room she\u2019d been in and no one knew where she\u2019d gone or how she even got out in the first place. So, Lorelei called Oleander, who was driving separately and let her know what was going on. Calamity then remembered that she has a contract that allows her to find anyone under the same sky, so she used it to see if she could pinpoint Rowan\u2019s location. It appeared that she was already far ahead of us in the direction of her house. We assumed that she had somehow already arrived at the little cabin. This was also passed along to Oleander who maneuvered her car behind ours so she would arrive second. No sense in freaking Rowan out any more than is absolutely necessary.<br /> <br /> When we arrived Rowan was sitting on the front stoop of her house with a harpoon laying across her lap. She had no expression on her face at all. Gawain looked to see what the connection was between Rowan and the building and found that there was an intense relationship there, as if it were a living being. There was no intent on Rowan\u2019s part other than to protect her house. He didn\u2019t even sense any self-preservation intentions from the selkie. Whatever was going on inside her head, she had no intention of giving up or even keeping herself from harm. She just wanted to protect her house. The lack of self-preservation was more than a little disturbing. I have seen it of course, in other people, but they generally don\u2019t get to that point without a lot of trauma or stress. I never got quite to that point when I was in the Lady\u2019s realm. I fought tooth and nail to keep what I had and to take what I needed. Even after I killed those men and fled to the cave where the Lady found me, I did not give up my will to live. I think that must have been part of the reason that the Lady chose me. I did not give into despair, I simply adapted and fought on. I\u2019ll admit that I was close to giving in when the Lady was trying to \u201crehabilitate\u201d me. I was starting to long for the release of death.<br /> <br /> No matter how low I got in her dungeons I found that I still had the will to live when that servant left the door unlatched. To this day I do not know if it was an accident or intentional. I\u2019m fairly certain that the man who did it is dead though. Accident or not it led to me escaping and the Lady would not have forgiven that. I sometimes regret that he died for me, but other times I\u2019m just grateful to be alive. I can\u2019t help it. No matter how low I\u2019ve gotten since coming back to \u2018the world\u2019 I have not gotten to the point where I wanted to die. Not seriously anyway. For a little while after I discovered my fetch and watched my family live on without me I was really depressed. I did not take care of myself the way I should have. I thought I wanted to die, but there was always some tendril of hope or maybe it was just stubbornness. I didn\u2019t want to give up because then she would have won, and I couldn\u2019t let that happen. Something of all that flashed through my head when I saw the utterly blank look on Rowan\u2019s face. I am not close to her really. We\u2019ve talked a few times, but we\u2019re not close. I still didn\u2019t want to see her look so empty though. Maybe my humanity has not all fled.<br /> <br /> When we got to the house Gawain jumped out and put up his swirling armor just in case. Lorelei got out just after him and together they started walking towards Rowan. They got pretty close before she reacted and started to bring her harpoon to bear. They stopped with Gawain slightly in front of Lori. Our songstress then started to try and talk Rowan down. It didn\u2019t really work all that well, but Rowan did reveal that she did not want to hurt Lori, but that she would protect her house. This gave Lori courage and she started inching her way towards her lover. Rowan\u2019s hands moved a bit, but she did not aim the weapon at Lori. Rowan just kept repeating that she wanted to be left to stay in her house.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile the rest of us stayed back near the van, though we had all gotten out. Calamity read the fears of the house and found that she could. The house was afraid of the group in general but Lori in particular. We figured it didn\u2019t like our Spring Courtier since she had the real possibility of getting Rowan to leave the house freely. It seems that the house did not want to be without Rowan either. We debated what we should do as Rowan and Lori continued to talk. Calamity was all for trying the nail idea and before we could really stop her she snuck off to the shadows and made her way around the side of the house. A short time later, we figured right after Calamity drove the nail into the siding, the house actually raised up off of its foundation a couple of feet and sprouted what looked like legs made of shadow. Also, shadows from the house seemed to pour out of the windows and fled. It seems the house was possessed by some sort of spirit or spirits.<br /> <br /> Once the house reacted everything went to shit. Rowan started to move toward the house but Gawain restrained her, soon to be relieved by Lori who held her lover firmly but gently to keep her safe and out of the action. The rest of us attacked the house. I felt just a little under prepared as I rushed toward the house trying to do damage with my knives. Calamity also went at the house with her blades, but she left herself wide open for retaliation in the process. Gawain also went at the house with his sword. After we got our hits in De La Rocha rushed toward the house and hit it hard. And when I say hard, I mean that I heard timbers crack and split and the house groaned. In retaliation the house literally moved forward and sat on De La Rocha. We could still hear her under there and she sounded mad but not overly hurt. We found out later that she had used her leechfinger abilities to drain health from the house and used that stored healing energy to treat the wounds inflicted by the house sitting on her. And yeah, I just wrote out that the house \u2018sat\u2019 on her. Not something that happens every day.<br /> <br /> Everyone tried attacking the house again. Luna threw a Molotov cocktail in through one of the windows while Julia ran forward and tried unsuccessfully to pull De La Rocha out from under the house. Gawain hit the house hard again and seemed to get the structure to react. At this point Lorelei was looking frantic. She was still holding onto Rowan but kept looking towards De La Rocha. I could see in her eyes that she wanted nothing more than to be with her wounded lover, so I made my way over to where Rowan was and offered to hold onto the selkie for Lori. Lori nodded in agreement and we swapped positions. Rowan struggled harder against me, but could not break free. At least not initially. It didn\u2019t seem that she was struggling as hard as a woman her size and build would, so I assumed that Insincere Marguerite had used her abilities to lessen Rowan\u2019s strength for the next little while.<br /> <br /> After that the house seemed to pick a new target and started going after Calamity. As the house got up to go after the razorhand De La Rocha got out from under the structure and Lori just wrapped her arms around her. The house then \u201csat\u201d down on Calamity. Gawain tried lifting the house off of his girlfriend, but even with Calamity\u2019s help it was just too heavy for them to move. Once Gawain realized that he could not move the house it seemed that he put his mind into breaking it into as many pieces as he could and just moving the pieces off of his girl. So, he attacked it a few more times and each time inflicted more damage. De La Rocha also did her part to try and break the structure. Around that time Rowan finally wriggled free of my grasp and started running towards the house. I tried to hold on, but she elbowed me in the solar plexus and knocked the wind out of me, and before I knew it she was squirming free.<br /> <br /> The others by that point had done a good bit of damage to the house, plus the fire that was burning inside was spreading pretty fast. The house got up again off of the ground and started making a \u201cdash\u201d for the ocean. I wasn\u2019t really moving all that fast, but it was making a concerted effort to get to the water to put out the fire. My motley mates kept hammering on the house until it suddenly shuddered and seemed to curl in on itself like an insect curling up when dead. After everything it was kind of satisfying to see it finally stop. Calamity was freed from beneath the house when it made its run for the water. Lori was there in short order to start healing the wounds inflicted by the house. Once everything had settled down we also noticed that the boat had kind of done the same shriveling thing that the house did. Apparently it was part of the same spirit(s) that had infested the house.<br /> <br /> It wasn\u2019t long after that when we started to hear the sounds of sirens coming our way, so we all jumped in the van, or in Oleander\u2019s case her car, and started to drive away. We weren\u2019t quite fast enough though. One police car came after us while a couple more went after Oleander. Gawain pulled over and Lori jumped in the front seat to do the talking while the rest of us hid out in the back and tried to be as quiet as we could. In the end the officer let us off and we started driving back towards the Dream House. At that point I brought up Oleander and Lori got a worried look on her face and called her lover. Oleander explained that she could not risk getting pulled over by the cops because she was still poisonous. She was planning on going into the Hedge later today and protects herself by becoming toxic for the trip. She would make any officers that stopped her ill, so she kept driving. This prompted more cops to follow her and she had a total of three following her when Lori called.<br /> <br /> In short order we came up with a plan to help Oleander. I believe Calamity was mainly behind this, though insincere Marguerite and Gawain jumped on board pretty quickly. The idea was for Marguerite to steal a car and have Calamity use her contract to pinpoint Oleander\u2019s location and drive there. Then they would distract or get in the way of the cops so Oleander could get away. Things mostly worked out too. They caught up to Oleander and Calamity side swiped the officer that was trailing the line and Insincere Marguerite used a contract to temporarily blind the officers and he quickly put on the brakes and stopped. They caught up to the other officers and Marguerite did the same thing to them and they spun out and stopped. One car hit another, but there did not appear to be any injuries. Oleander and Calamity kept driving. Calamity and the rest ditched the stolen car and called us for a pick up. Oleander headed back to her place so she could get to the hedge. I then brought up the question as to what Oleander was going to do with her car. Her plates had been run so the cops would know who to look for. Lori called Oleander about this and the other woman said that she would report her car stolen as soon as she got back from the Hedge. We agreed that was a good idea.<br /> <br /> When we got back to the house Julia looked up the news on her phone. She said that she had seen a news report about a house on Venice Beach that had a bomb go off in it causing it to move several yards from its foundation. I guess that\u2019s one way of explaining how Rowan\u2019s house moved so far from its base. Over all things went well. Gawain and Lori for that matter were not happy about Insincere Marguerite using her contracts to blind the officers while they were driving though. I\u2019ll admit that I hadn\u2019t thought much of it until he brought it up like that. I didn\u2019t think that what she had done was all that bad. It ensured that our friends got away from the police and no one got hurt. I suppose there was the real possibility of some of the officers getting hurt, but that thought hadn\u2019t crossed my mind until later. It\u2019s probably something that I need to pay more attention to in the future. My reactions to things are probably not quite what they should be. I don\u2019t know. Maybe I just got caught up in the excitement of the chase and the fact that our friends got away. It\u2019s not necessarily a sign of Rime coming out in me.<br /> <br /> After the recap of what happened Lori asked to speak to Insincere Marguerite privately. I think that she had noticed that Marguerite has not quite been acting like herself lately. I knew that it was because Marguerite was dealing with Desiree and that whole situation and it was really bothering her. I wasn\u2019t sure what was talked about behind closed doors but got a pretty good idea when they came back out. Lori went up to Julia and kissed her passionately and thanked her for not making her worry. She then went on to say that she had had an important conversation with Insincere Marguerite and that everything was okay and stressed that no one was mad at anyone else. Surprise and then relief flickered across Julia\u2019s face as Lorelei spoke. So, it looks like Marguerite told Lori what was going on and it seems like Lori has taken it better than the Darkling had feared. I am glad. I know that it\u2019s really been bothering Insincere Marguerite to keep such a big secret from her lovers, as well as the rest of us. I got the impression that Lori was going to fill De La Rocha in later, in private. In any case Marguerite looked relieved and a lot less stressed, and that is good.<br /> <br /> So after all of that we all went upstairs to watch the movie Titanic. Desiree and Jolie were waiting for us up there and we all settled in to watch the film. It wasn\u2019t too bad as far as movies go. It had the love story that ended in tragedy, but then that is kind of expected given the subject matter. Several people commented on the fact that Rose never moved on after Jack died. That she never found anyone else. I don\u2019 think that it\u2019s all that odd. I suppose it is given how old she was at the end of the movie, but sometimes if you can\u2019t have the one you love you just don\u2019t want anyone else. I saw a twisted version of that in Arcadia. One of the Lady\u2019s Treasures and a Knight fell in love. The Treasured, Joy had been with several people in the past, flitting from one bed to another until she met Raven. She would pine for him when he was out on missions and spend all of her free time with him when he was back. Then one day Raven didn\u2019t come back. He was sent to retrieve one of the Lady\u2019s denizens but ran into trouble. Apparently the man that had fled got lucky and disarmed Raven and killed him with his own blade. The Lady decreed that the man should die, and he did. After that though, Joy didn\u2019t seem interested in anyone else. She socialized with the other Treasures and sometimes the Knights, but never like she had before. So, yeah I can see Titanic ending with one lover never having moved on. It\u2019s sad, but sometimes that\u2019s just life.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> It has been an eventful night. Good but difficult.<br /> <br /> I confessed tonight to Juliette and to Maria. In Juliette\u2019s case I had not intended to, but after the hard events from earlier, she sensed that something was wrong and I\u2026I lost my composure. I don\u2019t remember how my words spilled out but in time they poured out and I could not stop them; I told her everything. I know I cried, I know my physical integrities were weakened, I could barely stand.<br /> <br /> I have a sort of snapshot memory, leaning on Juliette and crying, her holding I, and my trying to make my knees lock back in place so I would not fall. She shifted her weight and how she was holding I, her hand moved under my bottom so I would not fall. My legs failed, but she held I, breath on my forehead. She said she loved I, and it would not come between us.<br /> <br /> Julia needs to understand this sort of thing is proof that Juliette loves us. It\u2019s not just words. Juliette was upset with I, but rarely I felt more loved. Even when I did something she deeply disliked she\u2026understood. She saw past what I did for who I was. She knew it was the Insincere Marguerite she loved, who wanted to spend her life with her. She saw it in her big blue eyes. She held her close.<br /> <br /> She did not let her go.<br /> <br /> I felt so loved. Warm and secure. Bathed in Juliette\u2019s smell. The tears were not all sad. She held I a few minutes, while I remembered how my legs are put together, and reclaimed my arms. My only great regret is, while I left my heart much lighter, Juliette\u2019s was much heavier.<br /> <br /> Later I talked to Maria, when Juliette led her out to talk to I. I had been watching Rowan, though she was asleep. Julia was with I. Anyway; Maria took it\u2026less well, but not horribly. She like Juliette became distant, and she assured I that it would be fine, tomorrow.<br /> <br /> I saw love in her eyes but she could not make herself touch I. That hurt. But at the same time, I knew she had had a long day. Such a long day. She worked the daytime, and then that evening had spoken with Spidertoes, then\u2026the house.<br /> <br /> I hated to see her go though. I wanted to talk more, but even I myself was very tired. I allowed Julia to lead me back to watch Rowan in Juliette\u2019s room even as Juliette led Maria to my and Julia\u2019s room. Odd, I suppose, when one thinks about it.<br /> <br /> Ah, Rowan made a noise in her sleep but she is fine. Where was I? Last time I left off before we left the house. We met Oleander, who smelled strongly and was highly toxic. She had a trip into the Hedge planned, after all. She had her toxin, and we went to the house. Even Lori and Julia could not get near her.<br /> <br /> On the way to Rowan\u2019s house, Felicity called. Rowan had vanished. She wanted to have Lord Leonidas send warriors, but I told her not to. I said she had to choose him or me. She begged me not to make her choose, but she could not serve two lions.<br /> <br /> She chose me.<br /> <br /> Calamity used her Contracts, and we tracked her to the house. We warned Oleander who delayed her arrival by a few minutes. She had driven separately, due to her toxicity. That would prove to be a problem.<br /> <br /> We arrived at the house. Rowan was waiting outside with a harpoon. Gawain and Lori advanced, but Gawain, very wisely was just standing guard. Lori talked to Rowan and, as she always does, weakened her resolve. Rowan stayed guarded, but Gawain did not escalate. However, negotiations\u2026drug out. Rowan was deeply irrational, the fact she was listening to Lori at all shows how amazing she is. Then Calamity, well, cut the Gordian knot. She stabbed the house with an iron nail. Then all hell broke loose.<br /> <br /> Shadows ran out from under the house. Then it got up. Rowan went berserk, and first Lori then Jacob held Rowan down. I used my powers to weaken and blind first she then the house, and she proved no threat thereafter. The house on the other hand was.<br /> <br /> Calamity, Maria and Gawain did a lot of damage to the house. Jacob tried, bless him. Maria also used her powers to give herself an astonishing amount of strength for a strike, so the house tried to crush her. Fortunately, she had stolen from the house and healed herself. Calamity was it\u2019s next target, but she struggled with it. Gawain struggled to help. Maria took advantage of the movement to get out, but they had trouble escaping.<br /> <br /> Luna, the firebug, hurled a couple bottles in the windows. As the fight went on more and more smoke came out. The house tried to\u2026flee\u2026into the ocean. One of the stranger things I have written here\u2026anyway. Gawain and Calamity ran it down, and that and the fire did it in.<br /> <br /> We had little time; the police were coming. We stayed too long. Both Gawain and Oleander (she drove separately) were pursued. Gawain was stopped, no problem, despite Maria saying she was \u201cheat bait;\u201d they did not check our licenses, just his. Probably due in part to Lori\u2019s wiles. Anyone pulling Oleander over would pass out and possibly die. And having called for back up she would have a lot of authorities after her, and will be toxic for days, so it would likely end badly for her. She is not exactly a combat driver, though.<br /> <br /> After some debate, we pulled over, and Calamity, Gawain and I left the van. I hotwired a car and Calamity used her Oath and Punishment again to pursue. Gawain came along. Calamity established the tone when we caught up and sideswiped a cop. I blinded him so he spun out, leaving two pursuers still coming.<br /> <br /> I waited till they were taking a curve and blinded the second one. Then when the third hit the back of the car when he hit the breaks I blinded him. Remarkably effective, really. Both Oleander and Calamity lost them easily\u2026Oleander\u2019s car was very much not cut out for chases.<br /> <br /> Oleander was very eager to get into the Hedge, having been delayed to the point of risking human lives, and also was stinky, so she went on. The rest of us went to the house; we abandoned the car and Lori met us at a convenience store.<br /> <br /> When we got back, we set up in the family room. Juliette went to scold I a bit for risking police injuries. I suppose I had given in to my nature as a thief a bit too much. I felt contempt for those coming after I. I mean, not Maria level, she really seems to hate police. Still. Anyway that\u2019s when she\u2026we\u2026talked. She asked if I was okay and I said no and I can\u2019t\u2026can\u2019t\u2026I don\u2019t want to hide things from her. I am so tired of that. So I told her.<br /> <br /> Afterwards we came back. She gave Julia a big kiss when we came in, apparently because she did not give Juliette a heart attack or flip out at her at any point. It\u2019s fair. Julia and I went upstairs, to watch Rowan, who as I said was asleep.<br /> <br /> Felicity came by to check on her. We discussed what happened. It was good to see her, though less affectionate as Julia was right there. To her credit, as Julia goes when dealing with Felicity, she was downright civil. Still, it ran the interview short. She wanted to know how serious I was about me versus Lord Leonidas. I reminded her she was his ex. I feel he has too much influence on her. She apparently disagrees. We will see how this goes. I have no desire to further antagonize the Lord of Day.<br /> <br /> Oh who am I kidding. I LOVE antagonizing the Lord of Day.<br /> <br /> Then Maria came up, and Juliette brought her to me. We were both so tired. We did not kiss before sleep. It made me sad.<br /> <br /> Now here I am. Rowan is sleeping in the bed, and Julia is leaning against me. She is asleep, usually. She smells so good. It was a good day, but a hard day, for our family. But I feel better about us. We are strong. Everything for us will be okay, and this will merely strengthen us, as people and as a family.<br /> <br /> I hope.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXVI</i><br /> <br /> The House was far more dangerous to people inside than out. Rowan was, on some level, trying to keep Lori out as well as the rest away. The House, and Rowan, had their physicals halved very early on. This greatly reduced their ability to do much. The House did damage, a fair amount, when it could hit; it damaged Calamity so badly because she sacrificed her defense. The house had high durability and tons of health; the fire did a lot of damage, however, more and more as it spread. Maria did a ton of damage with one hit, but the rest was somewhat marginal\u2026the first time she got an incredible roll to activate the first clause of Stone, as well as dropping 6 Glamour to suck health out.<br /> <br /> So what was it? I think I will keep that under wraps a bit more.<br /> <br /> Car chase was minor but fun. Did not expect a car chase here before <i>Golden Eagle</i>.<br /> <br /> I am out of time, but Comments and Questions are welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T14:42:49-07:00","id":987944,"title":"","content":"After this Rowan incident, I gotta say, Lorelei has nerves of freaking steel to be dealing with about, like, five steady girlfriends, one newer girlfriend and one more potential girlfriend who is herself engaged, all of them with Freehold and generally supernatural drama and mundane PTSD, not to mention her own PTSD (I just assume by default that most Changelings have it in some form). <br /> <br /> While I would never dream of disapproving of Lorelei's polymarous lifestyle, I think she needs to slow down and stop collecting relationships like they're going out of style. Leave some women for the rest of the Freehold and save herself more headaches and heartbreaks. At her current rate, she's going to be dating every single and/or polymarous woman in the Freehold by the end of the Chronicle","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T14:22:50-07:00","id":988395,"title":"","content":"Funny enough, the combat with the house made me think of the film Monster House. Probably for the best there were no trees on the property then.<br /> <br /> It sounds like everyone made good in the fight against the house, even those without sufficient combat skills, from restraining Rowan to diminishing the house to keeping everyone on their feet. It's great when everyone can contribute in these conflicts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T14:58:33-07:00","id":988427,"title":"","content":"Master Aquatosic: Lori is pretty rattled. I will say Joan and Andromeda are more very close friends with benefits, though Joan's feelings are intense. Lori is aware she is overexerting herself, though, part of her hesitation with Rowan. I suspect there will be a girlfriend moratorium of sorts.<br /> <br /> Taidragon: It was a good fight. I am less worried about noncombatants in MDH, as we have some very combat focused characters (Calamity, Gawain, to a lesser degree Jacob) who may go through over a dozen sessions with no fighting at all. This is sort of deliberate as I don't want to pull punches but have to sort of weigh the benefits of a difficult combat. It's less my interest, and I don't want to thin the cast...any combat should be major and dramatic and a good place to die, essentially. <i>Golden Eagle</i> is the exception, it has plenty, and a campaign conceit to deal with it.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the feedback from you both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T15:04:32-07:00","id":988430,"title":"","content":"Anyone would be rattled in Lorelei's situation, but I would be going into a panic attack and curling up in my bed afraid to face the world (never fun when that happens to me) just dealing with more than one partner's drama. She is being admirably calm and in control of her situation given the craziness around her. Sure, a lot is out of her control, but the same can be said of any changeling; even for the most manipulative Court Monarchs.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the clarification on the Joan situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T15:07:43-07:00","id":988432,"title":"","content":"Wait, what do you mean by a girlfriend moratorium? Is the Dream House family (and maybe all their significant others too) going to get together and work out a suggestion for a hard cap on the number of serious romantic relationships any of them can have at one time before their friends are allowed to start advising some social pruning?<br /> <br /> Since I'm asking a bunch of questions anyway, here's two more. Is our Lovely Latina Leechfinger's name &quot;De La Roch<i><b>a</b></i>&quot; or &quot;De La Roch<b><i>e</i></b>&quot;? I've seen it spelled both ways. And on the subject of Maria, who's rolling for her? Still you, Baroness Nerak?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 10-16-2016, 06:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T16:59:13-07:00","id":988521,"title":"","content":"The Last Dance isn't going to get together and pass a moratorium, that would be Lori deciding it. The Last Dance isn't keen on telling each other who they can or can't date. (Though if Calamity keeps up this foolishness with Leanne they might consider it.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T08:59:28-07:00","id":988884,"title":"","content":"Master Aquatosic: Thanks for your interest; we always like hearing that people are reading. As far as Lori's various relationships go, it's not so much that she's braving these shark-infested waters with open eyes and a keen mind... it's more like a failure on her part to recognize or properly deal with the symptoms of her addiction. Lorelei's vice is something I originally termed an &quot;Aphrodite Complex.&quot; Put simply, she feels an intense need to be loved (or at least admired) by just about everyone in her life. And while she <i>does</i> know that this is a problem she has in broad terms, she often ignores or misses the specific cases in which it applies.<br /> <br /> To her current thinking, yes, taking Rowan as a lover in the first place was probably a mistake. She likes Rowan, but at the moment she doubts she'll ever be able to give her the kind of attention she reserves for Maria, Marguerite, Julia, and Oleander. Rowan even told her flat-out when they stated seeing each other that she didn't want a one-night stand; she wanted something which at least had the potential to blossom into a full-blown romantic love affair, and Lori jumped into the situation anyway... because Rowan's feelings for her are intense, and that feeds the part of her that's still trying to be the prettiest bird in the cage. And now, well... she feels like she can't break things off just yet, because Rowan has just suffered a significant trauma and she doesn't need any further shocks just now.<br /> <br /> Her mind is a little clearer as far as Joan and Andromeda are concerned. Yes, Joan's intense passion for Lorelei feeds her addiction as well, but Lori feels like she has a safety net where Joan is concerned. Lori can stop herself from taking that affair too far by reminding herself that she doesn't want to do anything to damage J&amp;A's relationship with each other (her virtue is Loyalty, and they're both good friends whom she really doesn't want to hurt).<br /> <br /> On a related note, the loyalty her many paramours show Lorelei has not gone unnoticed in the Freehold. See her next journal in a few short days for full details. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T13:52:25-07:00","id":989006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play?p=988432#post988432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, what do you mean by a girlfriend moratorium? Is the Dream House family (and maybe all their significant others too) going to get together and work out a suggestion for a hard cap on the number of serious romantic relationships any of them can have at one time before their friends are allowed to start advising some social pruning?<br /> <br /> Since I'm asking a bunch of questions anyway, here's two more. Is our Lovely Latina Leechfinger's name &quot;De La Roch<i><b>a</b></i>&quot; or &quot;De La Roch<b><i>e</i></b>&quot;? I've seen it spelled both ways. And on the subject of Maria, who's rolling for her? Still you, Baroness Nerak?</div> </div> </div> </div>No to the former<br /> <br /> I am rolling for De La Rocha. There are two Latinex musicians with that surname, most notably Zack de la Rocha of Rage Against the Machine. De La Rocha is a love letter to the Chicano Punk movement anyway, so a name associated with Latinex anger seemed fitting. I do not know why Gawain calls her De La Roche. Reasons of his own. And of course for maximum confusion her name is Maria de la Rocha, as the name is written, but she styles herself De La Rocha, since her Changeling name is her last name with extra caps.<br /> <br /> There was a time over a decade ago I had experimented with players rolling for their SO's or siblings or spiritual siblings or whatever in dramatic situations, but to say that proved unpopular is a massive understatement, so I stopped.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite and Julia are thinking a lot about &quot;the family&quot; as they think of themselves, so how Lori balances her love life is obviously something they are concerned about. De La Rocha herself cares less. Lori loves her and will never leave her. Insincere Marguerite and Julia love her deeply and want to stay with her. That's all that matters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 10-17-2016, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T15:50:35-07:00","id":989050,"title":"","content":"Really, romance is a lot like spinning a plate on top of a stick. Some people have a hard enough time keeping one stable - the fact Lori has managed to more or less keep four spinning is an impressive feat. However, as noted, adding Rowan to the mix was a step too far, and with the house Rowan's plate has become a wee bit too fragile to simple let drop...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenitentTom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play?p=988884#post988884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a related note, the loyalty her many paramours show Lorelei has not gone unnoticed in the Freehold. See her next journal in a few short days for full details. :-)</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean Augustine's De-La-Rocha-Berserking comment wasn't an indicator already?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T16:11:36-07:00","id":989060,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2591_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2591\" data-vbnamecard=\"2591\">PenitentTom</a> Huh. So it's actually her mechanical Vice? That explains a lot. I was worried that it was just my subconscious prejudices influencing me. I mean, this doesn't mean they weren't, but at least I was right. Good choice of a Vice on your part. It could even be argued to be the dark side of her Virtue, or that the Loyalty stems from her obsession with being loved.<br /> <br /> Brings up a question about the moment where she found out about Marguerite's secret. Did agreeing to keep the secret and protect Marguerite go along with Lorelei's Vice or her Virtue? As in, did you get back one Willpower or all of it?<br /> <br /> And on the subject of an ultra-loyal group of paramours, a thought occurs. If the word gets out to the general Freehold that Insincere Marguerite has become a sort of Keeper, some of the rumors that will start flying around might finger Lorelei as being her co-Keeper or even the true Keeper behind the scenes, due to well, the ultra-loyal flock of paramours she has. I don't think she would ever do that, but it sounds like the kind of thing paranoid Changelings would totally jump on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 10-17-2016, 07:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T16:14:05-07:00","id":989061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play?p=989060#post989060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the subject of an ultra-loyal group of paramours, a thought occurs. If the word that Insincere Marguerite has become a sort of Keeper, some of the rumors flying around might finger Lorelei as being her co-Keeper or even the true Keeper behind the scenes, due to well, the ultra-loyal flock of paramours. I don't think she would ever do that, but it sounds like the kind of thing paranoid Changelings would totally jump on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the issue that Chalcedony brought up when they sedated her, I'm pretty sure that kind of scandal would destroy the Dream House outright. It would destroy normal businesses, and Changelings are capable of far more hysteria than that...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T16:25:59-07:00","id":989065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play?p=989061#post989061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering the issue that Chalcedony brought up when they sedated her, I'm pretty sure that kind of scandal would destroy the Dream House outright. It would destroy normal businesses, and Changelings are capable of far more hysteria than that...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Exactly. It wouldn't just be a rumor that made people look at them with fear, it would be something that would get them brought before the Courts. They could have ownership of the business taken away from them, or even be executed. And even if their good relations with at least 3/4s of the Seasonal Monarchs saves them from Changeling Law, someone mad that these Loyalists got off so easy would probably murder them in their sleep, give them deadly nightmares, and/or burn the Dream House down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T18:17:12-07:00","id":989109,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7920_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7920\" data-vbnamecard=\"7920\">Master Aquatosic</a>: You know, at the moment I can't remember if I even thought to get Willpower back from that particular scene. If so, I suspect it would have fallen more into the Virtue side of things; Lori sticking with her lover and vowing to protect her secrets despite the fact that said secrets are highly upsetting to her sounds like Loyalty to me. And it's a good thing, too... with all that healing during the House fight earlier, Lori could probably stand to top off her reserves.<br /> <br /> As for the rest of it, well, let's hope it doesn't come to that. While some might call her naive, Lori would find it hard to believe that her friends and neighbors could credit rumors of that sort about her. She's built up a fair amount of goodwill in the area, and while a few suspicious individuals might believe she has selfish motives for &quot;charming&quot; so many of the local changelings, most people who have spent any appreciable amount of time around her can't help but notice her <i>extreme</i> aversion to power play and control games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T21:40:13-07:00","id":989193,"title":"","content":"Just thought of something else. She may have many friends, but she does have at least one potential enemy in the Freehold that could turn rumors like that to their advantage. I won't say who, cause saying it makes it less likely that it will happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T02:00:58-07:00","id":989252,"title":"","content":"The Last Dance has several enemies. Darke, obviously. Lucian, probably. Willow, Olivia, or Salk? The Handmaidens? Chalcedony?<br /> <br /> However, they have a couple things going for them. One is provide an excellent service for acquiring Glamour, and they have been pretty smart about not abusing it. They have not used it to get ahead, or lord over, or as a bargaining chip. So there is not much to legitimately attack the house for. Secondly, the Last Dance has one Spring, two Summer, two Autumn (Official, plus Luna) a Winter, a Night and a Dawn. They have people all over the place Courtwise, making it difficult to be a court vs. court issue.<br /> <br /> They have also (mostly) stuck to major threats to the freehold and looking inward, which means that, for example,. they have almost never blocked Lucian's plans. It's not that Lucian isn't a villain, it's that the LD has not given him reason to mess with them, and a hell of a hornets nest to whack. Now if they start leveraging, politically, this could change; they would still have protections but fucking with them may be something someone like Lucian feels he has no choice but to do. But for now, they are playing it smart.<br /> <br /> They still have obvious enemies, the Hollywood Courts and Darke, for example. I'm tired at this point and rambling but you see the crux of it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 10-18-2016, 05:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T10:46:47-07:00","id":989432,"title":"","content":"I wasn't originally say anything, but I had been seeing a parallel between Marguerite and Lori in regards to the collecting of people.Even though the collection is not intentional, there are some interesting implications to be delved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T12:04:27-07:00","id":989476,"title":"","content":"I think part of the attraction between the two is they are more alike than either would be comfortable admitting. They have almost the same Virtue (Loyal/Loyalty) and one of Insincere Marguerite's Vices (Possessiveness) relate too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T20:10:55-07:00","id":989682,"title":"","content":"Just realized that they both remind me in some ways of Greed from Fullmetal Alchemist. He's always trying to get more people to join his gang of minions, though it's more like a surrogate family than he would like to admit. He is adamant that if someone gives him their loyalty, he is obligated to treat them well, protect them and be generally loyal in turn. I think you see where I'm going with this","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T21:39:57-07:00","id":989715,"title":"","content":"Another parallel is between Lori and Calamity, primarily in their getting into relationships that they really shouldn't due to addiction. It has been noted that Lori is addicted to the love and adoration that her lovers give her, which she managed to balance between Insincere Marguerite, Julia and Maria fairly well, and with a bit of turbulence with Oleander being added in. However, that same addiction has led her to bring in Rowan, which has hit and gone over the peak of what she can handle without overt consequences, and as PenitentTom noted, she can't exactly drop Rowan without causing further damage. Likewise, Calamity though is normally satisfied with with Gawain and Becky as partners, Gawain for his gentleness and Becky for her ability to take Calamity to the extremes she desires (though that is really a gross oversimplification), her torture during her durance has led her to more...unhealthy relationships. Even when knowing that the Handmaidens are not to be given any length of rope lest they hang her, Calamity has let herself fall into their grasp before, and without the rest of the motley would have several times over. Though the Handmaidens didn't go too far, Leanne only stepped in as a medic after she nearly became Calamity's hangman, and even then she required others to completely undo the damage. Even then, Calamity has noted an urge to go back to her, even though she's aware at just how fine and sharp a line she is on.<br /> <br /> Both Lori and Calamity's pasts have resulted in unhealthy relationships brought about by their respective addictions, Lori for love, Calamity for punishment, and both of them are supported by their motley lest the problems grow out of control. The key difference is that while they both derive pleasure from satisfying those addictions, Lori's puts a strain on her partners as they vie for her attention, albeit with Maria having some precedence, while Calamity's puts her own life on the line because she can't resist those who have the means, and lack of restraint, to kill her.<br /> <br /> As noted, I am simplifying these aspects to varying degrees, but I love how they keep evolving over time, and how the characters are growing while making further parallels with one another. It really adds to the idea that everyone is amplifying the growth of their wyrd due to their connections to one another (and, admittedly, having a wellspring of glamour at their disposal doesn't exactly hurt).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 10-19-2016, 12:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T01:27:37-07:00","id":989772,"title":"","content":"I have described Calamity's sexual preferences as being oriented less toward gender or looks and more toward prey and predators. In general, she's not too bad at reigning in her desire to go after those that strike her as prey and often takes her interest as a sign that they need to be protected since other monsters would likely also be drawn to them. So that aspect of her addiction hasn't caused too much trouble.<br /> <br /> But with regard to predators, the one at risk is her and she has this guilt that she carries around that makes her feel that she deserves to suffer. Honestly, as came up during her low points after the incident with Chalcedony, the fact that it would hurt Gawain and Becky and the rest of the motley is a stronger incentive to her than her own sense of self preservation.<br /> <br /> As far as Leanne, she's got a fair presence in the journal for Calamity I'm finishing up right now actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T01:50:33-07:00","id":989780,"title":"","content":"Both Calamity and Lorelei got some things to think about last session. And Insincere Marguerite to a lesser degree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T19:32:37-07:00","id":990214,"title":"","content":"Indeed they did. Calamity also got that really boss ninja knife...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T04:46:49-07:00","id":990897,"title":"","content":"Very nice fight scene in this session! Trying to picture Calamity and Jacob fighting the house with their knives had me chuckling a bit.<br /> Also, I got misty eyed when Lori told DLR that Insincere Marguerite scared her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T08:27:55-07:00","id":990975,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5803_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5803\" data-vbnamecard=\"5803\">Taidragon</a>: More years ago than I'd care to admit, I had the opportunity to meet one of my idols, author Neil Gaiman, at a book signing. He offered a plethora of good advice to burgeoning authors, and one thing that I've always held close to my heart was the opinion that when readers pick up on something wonderful that you never intended, the best course of action is to smile mysteriously, nod, and congratulate them on their perspicacity.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, &lt;nods&gt;, Well spotted!<br /> <br /> Seriously, though, I think one of the reasons I enjoy writing about table-top RPGs as much as I do is that it's a communal experience. As long as you leave enough wiggle-room for your character to grow, there's always the potential for her to grow far beyond anything you could have originally intended. The parallels between Lori and Calamity were nothing I had consciously considered (you'd have to ask Amberghylles for their thoughts from Calamity's perspective, of course), but the two characters have always played well off each other, both for their differences and for the similarities neither really wants to acknowledge. And the idea that Calamity's various relationships might actually be <i>healthier</i> than Lori's would probably hit my poor girl like a slap in the face. Someone should really bring that up IC. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1405_4.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1405\" data-vbnamecard=\"1405\">Anteros</a>: Thanks so much for your comment. One of the ways I define successful art in any medium is in its ability to elicit a genuine emotional response in its audience. The idea that something I created can achieve that on any level is both flattering and humbling. Keep reading... the next session has a couple of bombshells for Lori!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T12:46:07-07:00","id":991071,"title":"","content":"I think how unhealthy Lori's relationships are depends on the person. Most of them are okay...I think the issue may be more number than anything else. Her poly group is an arrangement in which I internet-know some people in (4 men, not 4 women, but nonetheless) and they find it works really really well for them, especially when one of them is in a rough spot, or two. Always depends on the people. It's probably fair to say Insincere Marguerite is in a healthier place mentally because of her relationship with Lori. Not because of anything inherently wrong with a dominant/submissive relationship (I am a very Kink friendly person), but more how that relates to her Durance.<br /> <br /> Rowan is probably the least healthy, but then Rowan is also a little damaged.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T14:56:54-07:00","id":992034,"title":"","content":"The affair of the house is complete, though the aftermath continues. Thanksgiving is almost here but not quite. A moment to breathe.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LXVII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Wednesday night, just before showtime. Okay, so after the rather morose ending of my last journal entry, I took stock of my situation and decided that I really did need to try to get a bit more sleep. Emotional turmoil over Marguerite\u2019s situation notwithstanding, I was physically, mentally, and emotionally exhausted, and Spring contracts can only do so much. So I crawled back into bed with Maria and allowed myself to drift off surrounded by the heat of her body and the smell of her shampoo.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, my respite was to be short-lived. Only an hour or so later, I half-awoke to find myself alone in the bed. I could hear D talking with someone in hushed tones behind me, and could make out fragments of her side of the conversation.<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026leave her alone and let her get some sleep. Don\u2019t you think she\u2019s been through enough over the past few days?\u201d And then, a few seconds later, a heavy sigh. \u201cOkay, I\u2019ll ask her, but that\u2019s all I can promise.\u201d<br /> <br /> Her hand came down ever so gently on my shoulder. \u201cSorry to wake you, babe,\u201d she said softly when I mumbled an interrogative. \u201cJacob and Calamity are here with Rowan. They\u2019re going to take her to the clinic, but she doesn\u2019t want to go. They thought you might be able to help, if you\u2019re up for it.\u201d<br /> <br /> That sort of brought me out of my stupor. \u201cYeah,\u201d I slurred, shaking my head, \u201cgimme just a second.\u201d I sat up on the bed and summoned the glamour necessary to pep myself up a bit. I grabbed my clothes \u2013 the same ones I wore the previous day, since we\u2019d been sleeping in Marguerite\u2019s room \u2013 and joined the others on the landing.<br /> <br /> Rowan was there, and her eyes sort of lit up when she saw me. She half embraced me and half collapsed on me, then pulled herself away sharply. \u201cSorry\u2026 sorry,\u201d she said with alarm. \u201cI don\u2019t mean to crowd you, Lori. I\u2019m sorry.\u201d<br /> <br /> I pulled her into a more sedate embrace. \u201cDon\u2019t worry about it, sweetie,\u201d I said softly. \u201cI\u2019m here for you if you need me, I want you to know that. Now\u2026 Jacob and Calamity want to take you to meet with some people who might be able to help you cope with what happened last night. I think it would be good for you. Will you go with them\u2026 if I come with you?\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded sedately, and a few minutes later we were all strapped into Jacob\u2019s jeep. I kept one of her hands in mine as we sat together in the back seat. She tensed up a bit as we pulled into the clinic\u2019s parking lot, but I managed to soothe her enough to get her into the building.<br /> <br /> We were met in the lobby by a receptionist, a doctor, and a pair of orderlies. \u201cWhat\u2019s going on\u2026 how can we help?\u201d the doctor asked as soon as she got a look at Rowan.<br /> <br /> \u201cI think she\u2019s in shock,\u201d I said. \u201cShe suffered a trauma last night, and she\u2019s been withdrawn ever since.\u201d<br /> <br /> The doctor leaned forward and looked into Rowan\u2019s eyes. \u201cHello, miss\u2026\u201d she began.<br /> <br /> \u201cRowan,\u201d I offered.<br /> <br /> \u201cHello, Rowan,\u201d she continued. \u201cI\u2019m Dr. Kovacs. This is Alex. If you\u2019ll go down the hall with him, he\u2019ll get you something to drink, and maybe some toast if you\u2019re up for it. I\u2019m going to talk to your friends for a few minutes to see what we can do to help you, then I\u2019ll come and speak with you for a while. Is that okay with you?\u201d<br /> <br /> Rowan looked at me helplessly, and I could see the panic bubbling up to the surface behind her eyes. She was clutching at her sealskin like a lifeline. \u201cLori\u2026?\u201d she almost whimpered.<br /> <br /> I leaned in and kissed her forehead. \u201cIt\u2019s going to be okay, sweetie. Dr. Kovacs is going to try to help you get past what happened. I\u2019ll be right out here in the lobby, okay? I won\u2019t leave until I\u2019m sure you\u2019re all right, and I promise I\u2019ll come in and see you before I go.\u201d Something occurred to me at that point, and I backpedaled a bit. \u201cIf the doctors say that\u2019s okay, of course.\u201d<br /> <br /> The doctor nodded noncommittally, and Rowan allowed herself to be led (gently) down the hall to one of the examining rooms. Jacob, Calamity and I began telling Dr. Kovacs what had happened, but the two of them had their own appointments with other therapists, so I ended up telling most of the story myself.<br /> <br /> Dr. Kovacs nodded grimly as I finished the tale. \u201cI thought I recognized the signs,\u201d she muttered to herself. Then she turned back to me. \u201cI\u2019m not sure what it was you dealt with last night, Ms. Grace, but Rowan is displaying symptoms similar to a changeling who is having difficulty adjusting to life outside of Arcadia\u2026 life away from her Keeper,\u201d she elaborated. \u201cIt\u2019s not quite the same thing, of course, but we should be able to employ similar techniques to help her through this. Don\u2019t worry, we have a lot of experience with cases of this type. If you\u2019d like to take a seat, I\u2019ll come and speak with you as soon as I know more.\u201d<br /> <br /> So I sat in the waiting room idly perusing a Spanish-language fashion magazine. I\u2019ve been trying to practice the lingo a bit to get a little closer to Maria, who is sincerely worried that I won\u2019t like hanging out with her friends (and eventually family) if I can\u2019t understand what they\u2019re talking about. And before you ask, no, I\u2019m not nearly good enough to comprehend even a sentence or two of what I was reading, so I mostly contented myself with looking at the pretty pictures.<br /> <br /> Dr. Kovacs returned about ten minutes before my friends\u2019 therapy sessions were supposed to end and led me down the hall to the room where Rowan was resting. \u201cShe asked for you,\u201d she said softly as we looked in through the window. \u201cFor the most part she\u2019s unresponsive, but she\u2019ll talk about you. That\u2019s a hopeful sign. I can\u2019t promise anything, of course\u2026 therapy of this sort is more art than science. But based on my experience with similar cases, I\u2019d say the prognosis is pretty good. It\u2019s going to take time, but we\u2019re probably looking at days of recovery rather than weeks. We\u2019re going to keep her here, if that\u2019s all right.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCan I talk to her?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> Dr. Kovacs nodded. \u201cOf course,\u201d she said. \u201cWe want her to feel safe and give her a sense of stability, and right now you can only help with that. It might be best if you don\u2019t visit her <u><u>too</u></u> often during the recovery phase, though\u2026 we don\u2019t want her to grow dependent upon your presence.\u201d<br /> <br /> I saw the sense in that, and thanked her for her efforts on Rowan\u2019s behalf. Then I stepped into the room. Rowan was lying down on one of those examining tables, sort of curled up on her side. I touched her shoulder, and she sort of tensed up, but then relaxed when she saw it was me.<br /> <br /> \u201cHey, sweetie,\u201d I said softly, \u201care you going to be okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> She shrugged, then nodded. \u201cI think so,\u201d she said softly, sitting up and taking my hand.<br /> <br /> \u201cGood,\u201d I said fervently. \u201cDr. Kovacs and the others here are going to do what they can to help you, okay? Helping changelings deal with traumatic experiences is their job, and they\u2019re really good at it. I\u2019m sorry I can\u2019t stay here with you, but I don\u2019t want to get in the way of you getting better. But I promise I\u2019ll be there for you once you\u2019ve fully recovered, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> Her lip sort of trembled for a moment, but then she nodded. \u201cOkay. Thanks for looking out for me, Lori. I love you.\u201d<br /> <br /> I leaned down and kissed her forehead. \u201cI love you too, Rowan,\u201d I said without hesitation. \u201cGet better soon.\u201d And then I headed back to the waiting room and tried to seem aloof and mysterious\u2026 mostly as a method of holding back tears. Hospital waiting rooms make me emotional at the best of times, and Rowan\u2019s condition only aggravated that stress.<br /> <br /> When Jacob and Calamity were done with their respective appointments the three of us piled back into Jacob\u2019s jeep and headed back to the Dream House, arriving just in time for Sex Breakfast. Gawain is (<u><u>still</u></u>) on his waffle kick, and he had made something he called \u201cHong Kong waffles\u201d this time. They were tasty \u2013 even when spread with peanut butter \u2013 but seemed almost more like a dessert than a breakfast food to me. I have to talk with him about lightening things up for a few days, or I\u2019m going to start getting fat.<br /> <br /> I called Dad after breakfast to see if he wanted to do something together for Thanksgiving. I\u2019d sort of been kicking myself over the fact that I was going to be busy on the first holiday the two of us could celebrate together, but it turned out to be serendipitous, as Dad\u2019s going to be ministering to the needy on Thursday in any case. He jumped at the chance to spend more time with me, however, and asked if Friday would be okay. Though I thought longingly of the fabled \u201cBlack Friday\u201d sales I\u2019d be missing, of course I agreed to meet with him for lunch and spend the afternoon with him as well.<br /> <br /> \u201cWould you like to bring Maria as well?\u201d he asked before we disconnected, and the genuine enthusiasm I heard in his voice nearly brought a tear to my eye.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2026 don\u2019t know,\u201d I said after thinking about it. \u201cI\u2019m not sure if she has her own plans for Friday or not. I\u2019ll ask her,\u201d I promised.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, whether it\u2019s just the two of us or all three, I look forward to seeing you, Juliette,\u201d he added fervently.<br /> <br /> We said our goodbyes and I started thinking about how to spend the rest of my Tuesday. I had a date with Joan and Andromeda that night, so I wasn\u2019t going to be in the show, which left my afternoon relatively free. I had just made up my mind to see if Calamity wanted to put a little more polish on our number when the doorbell rang.<br /> <br /> As Calamity and I were both in the theater at the time, we answered the door together. Imagine my shock when I found Queen Charlotte standing on our doorstep. I dropped into a curtsey and moved aside to let her enter. The deference seemed to amuse her on some level, but I could tell that she had come on serious business.<br /> <br /> \u201cI am here for several reasons,\u201d she began as she entered. \u201cThere is a matter I need to discuss with the Last Dance motley. I would also like to meet with the resident members of my Court. And finally,\u201d she paused and turned her occasionally unsettling gaze in my direction, \u201cI need to speak with you privately, Lorelei.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMe?\u201d I said stupidly. I probably did that thing I do when I\u2019m shocked where I stare at someone without speaking for a few seconds and blink rapidly.<br /> <br /> \u201cYes, my dear,\u201d Charlotte replied. \u201cIs there somewhere we can speak privately?\u201d<br /> <br /> Calamity nodded us toward her office. \u201cI\u2019ll let Julia and Luna know you want to speak with us,\u201d she said as she moved toward the stairs. \u201cAnd\u2026 what about Insincere Marguerite?\u201d<br /> <br /> Charlotte considered for a moment, and then nodded. \u201cOur Dread Esquire may join us as well,\u201d she consented.<br /> <br /> Once we were alone in the office, I gave voice to my curiosity. \u201cWhat can I do for you, Your Majesty?\u201d I asked deferentially. \u201cI am of course at your service\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI need to speak with you about Oleander,\u201d she interrupted me abruptly.<br /> <br /> My heart sank. \u201cWhat about her?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> Charlotte sighed. \u201cLast night she called me, asking for permission to distribute a very potent poison. I refused to grant said permission, citing the need for further investigation into the circumstances, and she immediately asked me if this was a request or an order.\u201d A look of half-amused disbelief settled on her lovely features. \u201cShe said she wanted to know exactly how she would be defying me, so that she would know how much trouble she would be in for.\u201d<br /> <br /> I lowered my eyes. \u201cDammit,\u201d I whispered, \u201cYour Majesty, I\u2019m so sorry. I never meant for Oleander to act against your wishes. Everything was happening so quickly, and I was anxious to do what I could for Rowan, and Madame Spidertoes suggested the chemical\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Charlotte raised a hand and gently placed it on my shoulder. \u201cYou are not in any trouble, Lorelei,\u201d she assured me in soothing tones, \u201cand neither is Oleander. I told her that I would make it a request. But I wanted to speak with you about her defiance and what it might signify.\u201d<br /> <br /> I breathed a sigh of relief when I heard that Oleander wasn\u2019t going to be punished. \u201cAnd\u2026 what is that?\u201d I asked after a moment had passed.<br /> <br /> Charlotte considered the question. \u201cOleander has been allied with the Autumn Court for quite some time now, and she has always been an exemplary subject. Her work has been top-notch, and her loyalty beyond reproach. But \u2013 and I intend no slight when I say this \u2013 before last night, I would have described her as something of a cold fish. I have never before known her to act impulsively based upon emotional mandates.\u201d<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t know what to say to that, so I kept my mouth shut.<br /> <br /> Eventually the Queen turned to look me in the eye. \u201cI have considered this situation carefully, and have come to the conclusion that Oleander\u2019s actions may have less to do with some change in <u><u>her</u></u> personality, and more to do with <u><u>you</u></u>, Lorelei. You inspire an unusual level of loyalty in those around you.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded soberly. \u201cI\u2019m blessed with good friends and faithful lovers,\u201d I agreed, \u201cbut I swear that I never intended to convince her to go against a royal order. I\u2019ll be more careful in the future\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Charlotte held up her hand once more. \u201cRelax, Lorelei. I have already told you that you\u2019re not in any trouble. I merely wonder if you might be able to use this uncommon loyalty to help the Freehold\u2026 and to help a mutual friend in the process.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m of course happy to serve the Freehold in any way I can\u2026\u201d I said immediately. I have <u><u>got</u></u> to learn to keep my mouth shut in situations like that.<br /> <br /> Charlotte smiled again, and there was something predatory in it this time. \u201cIt is obvious to everyone that Jolie is unhappy in her role as Princess. She is a capable ruler, and she truly wants what is best for everyone in the Freehold, but the pressures of the monarchy are wearing on her, and I\u2019m not certain how much longer she will be able to bear them. I\u2019d like you to consider stepping in to take her place.\u201d<br /> <br /> I confess that I hadn\u2019t been expecting that, and had no idea how to respond. I think, for about a minute, for the first time in my life, I was literally incapable of forming coherent thoughts.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt needn\u2019t be right now,\u201d Charlotte went on as I sputtered stupidly, \u201cor even this coming Spring. But I think you would be suited to the role, and I would not see Jolie burdened any longer than necessary. While her relationship with Desiree seems to be alleviating some of her stress\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I couldn\u2019t keep the distaste from my face when her name came up. Desiree is not my favorite person at the moment, mostly due to the burden she\u2019s placed on Marguerite, and with everything else that was happening I found it difficult to conceal that fact.<br /> <br /> Charlotte picked up on my discomfort immediately. \u201cWhat is it?\u201d she asked sharply. \u201cDoes Desiree represent some threat? Is Jolie in danger?\u201d<br /> <br /> I couldn\u2019t reveal what I knew; that would have only served to endanger Marguerite. \u201cNo,\u201d I said slowly, \u201cshe and I had a\u2026 disagreement recently, that\u2019s all. But I don\u2019t think she means any harm.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cVery well,\u201d Charlotte said, after studying my face for a few seconds. \u201cAnd\u2026 your thoughts on my suggestion?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI have no desire to rule,\u201d I managed after a moment.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnother mark in your favor,\u201d Charlotte shot back at me. \u201cYou would take up the crown out of a desire to serve rather than to be served.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2026\u201d I paused for a moment, suddenly shy. \u201cYou really think I would be able to do something like that? You really think the Court would accept me?\u201d<br /> <br /> Charlotte\u2019s look softened. \u201cI do,\u201d she said. \u201cYou command the love of nearly everyone around you, Lorelei\u2026 and you do so almost effortlessly. People wish to protect you, and seek to please you. You bring out their better angels because they do not want to disappoint you. Oleander is perhaps the most obvious example of this trend, but she is far from alone in her affections. You seem to have won Joan over as well, and many in the Freehold thought that was impossible.\u201d<br /> <br /> I shook my head, mostly out of pure bewilderment. \u201cI\u2026 I\u2019ll have to think about this. A lot.\u201d<br /> <br /> Charlotte nodded with something that might have been sympathy. \u201cIt is not a step to be taken lightly, my dear, and I would never insist. All I ask is that you consider my suggestion seriously\u2026 for Jolie\u2019s sake.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cI will. Thank you, Your Majesty. And thank you for being so understanding about Oleander. I\u2019ll be more careful with my requests in the future.\u201d<br /> <br /> I left the office and allowed the Autumn Courtiers to file in. I don\u2019t know what they talked about, and to be honest at the time I was still too stunned to be very curious. I meandered into the kitchen, found D, and dragged her up to our bedroom without a word.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat\u2019s up, babe?\u201d she asked once I had closed the door.<br /> <br /> I told her. She looked almost as stunned as I felt.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo what do you think?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> D shook her head. \u201cYou could do it,\u201d she said without hesitation, \u201cI don\u2019t want you to doubt my confidence in you for a second. And if you decide that you want this, I promise that I will be your biggest supporter. But\u2026 I\u2019m not sure if you <u><u>should</u></u>,\u201d she ended thoughtfully.<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cI don\u2019t really want to be in power. I don\u2019t want the responsibility.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s part of it,\u201d D elaborated, \u201cbut there\u2019s more. You\u2019re a good person, Lori. You want to help your friends. You want to save people. But when you have the entire community under your authority\u2026 you\u2019re going to have to accept that you can\u2019t save everybody at some point. And I think that would hurt you.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cAnd I have\u2026 other responsibilities to consider as well,\u201d I added. \u201cI couldn\u2019t very well go off gallivanting into the Hedge to rescue Missy and Jane if the Freehold was counting on me for guidance. And that\u2019s not even considering\u2026\u201d I broke off.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat?\u201d D asked simply.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m sure I blushed a little. \u201cI\u2019ve been thinking about\u2026 trying to go to college,\u201d I admitted softly. \u201cIf I could get into a local pre-med program that would be ideal. It might take a while, but if I was careful and used my contracts well I could probably go to classes during the day and still work at the Dream House nights\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026but you\u2019d have a hard time balancing all of that with additional duties to the Freehold,\u201d D finished for me. She leaned over and kissed my forehead lightly. \u201cI think it\u2019s a great idea, Jules. Just don\u2019t try to spread yourself too thin.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo\u2026 there was something else I wanted to ask you,\u201d I said after a moment, as we were about to head back downstairs to join the others.<br /> <br /> \u201cShoot,\u201d D said with a grin.<br /> <br /> \u201cI talked with my dad earlier, and we\u2019re gonna get together on Friday afternoon for a good old-fashioned family Thanksgiving,\u201d I informed her. \u201cNeither one of us knew we were going to be reconciled a few weeks ago, and we both made other plans for the day itself.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGreat,\u201d D replied, \u201cI know how much that means to you, babe.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, while we were talking, he asked if you\u2019d like to join us.\u201d She was quiet for a second, so I started babbling to fill time. \u201cI know it\u2019s not really your thing, sweetie, and I\u2019ll totally understand if you\u2019d rather not join us, but\u2026 well, he asked. Unpromted. He thought of it before I could even mention you\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> D smiled and took my hand. \u201cI\u2019ll be there, babe. I like your dad.\u201d<br /> <br /> I gave her hand a squeeze. \u201cThanks,\u201d I whispered, and the two of us managed to share a little kiss before the motley was summoned into Charlotte\u2019s presence.<br /> <br /> (I don\u2019t <u><u>know</u></u> what her meeting with the Autumn Courtiers was about, by the way\u2026 but I can hazard a guess. I think she was debriefing them about the situation with Rowan\u2019s house, and maybe the things we saw skittering away from it when it rose from its foundations. In any case, I\u2019m sure my friends will let me know if there\u2019s anything I need to be concerned about).<br /> <br /> When we were all assembled in Queen Charlotte\u2019s presence (the office was much too small for such a large group, so we just used the theater), she told us that she had been in contact with Skitters, the Autumn Queen of Paris. The other monarch has consented to speak with us about rescinding Marguerite\u2019s banishment. We\u2019re going to meet with her via the computer on Saturday and speak up on my lover\u2019s behalf. With any luck, we\u2019ll be able to convince her to allow Marguerite to visit her old home!<br /> <br /> I\u2019m going to do my best to make that happen, of course. Though we haven\u2019t made any specific plans, I imagine I will probably take point on these talks, as that tends to be my role in this motley. I can also serve as an example of someone who loves Marguerite but is obviously not under her power. For similar reasons, we\u2019ll probably try to keep Julia\u2019s contributions to a minimum, and Desiree should of course be allowed nowhere near the conference.<br /> <br /> Charlotte did warn us that Queen Skitters is\u2026 \u201cunusual\u201d in some respects. She didn\u2019t elaborate other than to say that she obviously did not obtain her lofty position through her poise and charm.<br /> <br /> Marguerite was obviously excited by the prospect of the meeting, though her nerves were showing through a bit as well. I did my best to comfort her, and to assure her that we would do everything in our power to make sure that the meeting went well. I hope that helped on some level.<br /> <br /> I spent most of the rest of the afternoon going through our number with Calamity and getting ready for my date. This has been a really light week for me, cabaret-wise\u2026 I was off on Monday for movie night, last night for my date, and we\u2019re closing Thursday and Friday, so I\u2019m really only doing one show all week (tonight\u2019s). I\u2019d better make sure I top off the glamour.<br /> <br /> So Tuesday was my night to have dinner at Joan and Andromeda\u2019s place (and to watch a feature film, of course). I left D, Marguerite and Julia in each other\u2019s capable hands. Following a somewhat tense conversation after breakfast, D and Marguerite seemed to be okay with each other once more\u2026 and Julia further soothed Marguerite by singing to her throughout the afternoon. <br /> <br /> At around 7:30 I hopped into my \u2018vette and headed across town. Once again Joan met me at the door with an embrace and a kiss, and once again I found myself lost in the wonderful smells of Andromeda\u2019s cooking. I really need to consider trying to arrange for she and Gawain to end up sharing a kitchen one of these meals.<br /> <br /> Dinner was once again magnificent, of course, and the three of us chatted and told stories and laughed through most of it. But then \u2013 wouldn\u2019t you know it? \u2013 that dratted VCR was on the fritz again, and we once more found ourselves faced with the question of how to occupy ourselves for the rest of the evening.<br /> <br /> I hazarded a guess that Joan had lured me into her home under false pretenses with a wink and a twinkle.<br /> <br /> Joan allowed as how she might have suspected the VCR would once again be out of order, and she smiled as she said it.<br /> <br /> So yes, bedroom shenanigans ensued. Andromeda was as bubbly and excitable as ever; the perfect cheerful cure for the weighty events of the past few days. And Joan\u2026 I don\u2019t know what was going on in her honorable head, but she was even more passionate than usual with me last night. Our lovemaking was\u2026 more intense than I\u2019d expected. And no, that\u2019s not a bad thing. And of course, as usual, I tried my best to emphasize their feelings for each other as much as I could. All in all, I have no complaints.<br /> <br /> The three of us woke up this morning tangled in the sheets of their bed. Andromeda got the middle this time, with Joan\u2019s arms around her in a fiercely protective circle and my own right hand resting lazily low on her belly. Andromeda offered to cook breakfast, but I had another idea.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe cat\u2019s out of the bag now,\u201d I said with a wink, \u201cso why don\u2019t the two of you come back to the Dream House with me. You can finally experience the legendary Sex Breakfast!\u201d<br /> <br /> The two of them chuckled at that, and allowed as how that would be a pleasant way to spend the rest of the morning. I also worked a little mischief, I confess. I\u2019d been thinking about what Queen Charlotte said the previous day, about how I inspire uncommon loyalty in my lovers, and can get them to act in ways they might not ordinarily act. I thought I saw a way to test that theory without hurting anyone, and immediately put it into action.<br /> <br /> This flash of inspiration was triggered when Joan opened her closet. Amidst the row of pure white garments I caught a glimpse of a splash of color. \u201cWhat\u2019s that red thing?\u201d I asked innocently.<br /> <br /> Joan frowned. \u201cA dress,\u201d she admitted.<br /> <br /> \u201cA sexy dress?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> Joan shrugged. \u201cYeah,\u201d Andromeda added helpfully. \u201cReally sexy.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019d love to see you in it, Lindsay,\u201d I added wistfully.<br /> <br /> She frowned again. \u201cIt is\u2026 <u><u>feminine</u></u>,\u201d she said, sort of biting down on the word.<br /> <br /> I got up and moved up behind her, pressing myself against her back. \u201cSo are you,\u201d I said softly, running my hands along her curves. \u201cYou\u2019re a beautiful woman, Lindsay\u2026 lots of people think so. I know I do. And I know Andromeda does.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGorgeous,\u201d Andromeda agreed, joining us in front of the closet.<br /> <br /> \u201cBeing feminine doesn\u2019t make you less strong,\u201d I continued.<br /> <br /> Joan sighed, and turned to kiss each of us in turn. \u201cRebecca. Juliette. I thank you. The two of you\u2026 when I am with you, I <u><u>feel</u></u> beautiful.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo\u2026 you\u2019ll let us see you in the dress?\u201d I asked. A glance downward confirmed my suspicions. \u201cAnd the heels that go with it?\u201d<br /> <br /> Andromeda spoke up in support of the idea. \u201cPlease, Lindsay?\u201d she said, those huge eyes of hers shining with innocent longing.<br /> <br /> Joan sighed again, but also chuckled and shook her head. \u201cOnly for you,\u201d she said with a soft smile as she pulled the dress over her head. The results were more than satisfactory. White will always be Joan\u2019s signature color, of course\u2026 but she can really rock a slinky red party dress when she wants to.<br /> <br /> I threw on my nearly equally slinky dress from the previous night, and Andromeda (apparently deciding that she didn\u2019t want to miss out on the fun) decided to dress up as well. Once we were all three dressed to the nines, I decided to push my advantage. \u201cOkay, let\u2019s head over to the Dream House. I guess you ladies will be taking your own car?\u201d<br /> <br /> Joan shook her head, agitated. \u201cI need to change first,\u201d she protested.<br /> <br /> I put a hand on her arm. \u201cNo you don\u2019t, honey,\u201d I said soothingly. It\u2019ll be fine. It\u2019ll just be us and the motley there. We\u2019re your friends. We love you. Okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> She hesitated, but then nodded. \u201cAll right. Only for you,\u201d she said again.<br /> <br /> So of course Joan was a big hit with the family in her sexy red dress, and she suffered through it with good grace. It was enough to make me wonder if Charlotte might be <u><u>right</u></u> about me on some level. I still have no desire to take up the crown, even if it turns out to be possible, but\u2026 if I can help out Jolie by doing so, isn\u2019t it my duty on some level? If she\u2019s not happy in the role, it would be best both for her and for the Court if she stepped aside.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll have to talk with her about this before I make any decisions. I absolutely <u><u>won\u2019t</u></u> do anything unless I\u2019m one hundred percent sure that she approves of it. I would never usurp her power or undermine her authority in that way. And even if she wants this\u2026 even if she <u><u>begs</u></u> me to take on this burden, she\u2019ll have to understand that I need to fulfill my other obligations first. I need to do something about Missy and Jane\u2019s situation before I tie myself to any other responsibilities.<br /> <br /> But in any case, as I was saying, Joan blushed and stammered her way through sex breakfast, but honestly didn\u2019t seem nearly as uncomfortable as I would have predicted. I guess she really is getting used to being around my motley\u2026 and to letting her guard down a little bit in those circumstances. She and Andromeda left just after the meal, both of them giving me parting kisses on their way out.<br /> <br /> A few of my friends decided to head out after breakfast on one errand or another. Luna and Jacob visited the site of Rowan\u2019s house and attempted to track the shadowy things we saw fleeing it the other night. Unfortunately, it sounds like they didn\u2019t have much luck. They were able to pick up a few trails here and there\u2026 though the creatures left no prints in sand or soil, they did disturb the grass as they passed. It looks like they mostly avoided other houses, even turning aside to go around them, but the trails all petered out before any particular destination could be determined. I have a bad feeling that we haven\u2019t heard the last of these things\u2026<br /> <br /> Meanwhile Calamity, for reasons of her own, visited the Autumn Court\u2019s library. I don\u2019t know what she was researching, and she didn\u2019t share that tidbit when she got back. What she <u><u>did</u></u> share was an encounter with the enigmatic Shi. He approached her outside of the Library and asked if she would like to purchase an ornate butterfly knife for six dollars. Being Calamity, of course she agreed immediately. When she received the knife, she noticed that it was very well-made and artistically decorated, with an ivory handle carved with intricate symbols. It was obviously worth much more than six dollars. She turned to question Shi about this, but he had already left.<br /> <br /> While she was in the Library, she encountered Leanne Sheets. Leanne noticed the knife, or Calamity showed it to her or something, and she mentioned in awed tones that it happened to be the signature weapon of the Hollywood Autumn Court\u2019s top assassin. No one seems to know how Shi got it, but chances are it will bring trouble to Calamity (and by extension the rest of us), either from the assassin himself or from whoever has succeeded him (or her).<br /> <br /> So in short, I guess the point of this journal is that I\u2019ve had a lot of weighty matters to distract me from the issue of Marguerite and Desiree lately, and that\u2019s probably for the best. I love her. I truly do. And I will do everything in my power to help her through this, and to see that our relationship survives intact. But every time I start to consider the implications of what Desiree has tricked her into, it makes me so <u><u>angry</u></u> that I just want to scream myself hoarse. I want to lash out at her\u2026 at <u><u>both</u></u> of them, really, and I know that I\u2019d end up saying something that I\u2019d eventually regret if that happened.<br /> <br /> So under those circumstances, maybe it\u2019s not such a bad thing to have a lot on my plate to distract me from that particular set of problems. Like, you know, Rowan\u2019s condition, and the number I\u2019m working on with Calamity, and the shadow-things Jacob and Luna are tracking, and Calamity\u2019s issue with the knife, and our impending meeting with the current Queen of Paris, and my relationship with Joan and Andromeda, and Thanksgiving with Julia\u2019s parents, and Thanksgiving with <u><u>my</u></u> parent, and my secret aspirations of eventually becoming a real doctor, and of course the one thing I can <u><u>never</u></u> forget: the debt I owe to Missy and Jane. And oh yeah, let\u2019s not forget the little fact that one of the most powerful changelings in the Freehold has just essentially asked me to consider taking up the mantle of Queen of Spring.<br /> <br /> What could possibly crop up next?<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> It\u2019s all good\u2026 Looks like things are fine after all. I really shouldn\u2019t have gotten all worked up before I knew what had gone down with Spidertoes and Leanne. Speaking of worked up\u2026 damn if Annika wasn\u2019t going to be here like any minute now I would so be spending some quality time with my birthday present from Andromeda right now. But my precious will have to wait till later.<br /> <br /> You\u2019d think after spending last night with Becky and Gawain I wouldn\u2019t be this spun up this easily but I\u2019m just a needful little monster. Well, that and Leanne\u2019s touch is literally magical\u2026 Fuck the moment those lips brushed my forehead I was completely done and gone. I am pretty sure I actually whimpered. At least I managed to stay on my feet. Not sure how considering the way my knees went weak there but I did. And then she just gave me that knowing smile and left me there all wobbly and wet and needful and mewling\u2026 Damn but that woman has my number and she knows it and she likes it. She seemed quite pleased with herself that she had me right ready to go but then left me stewing. So yeah, Dionysia is the only one that got plowed in the library today. No idea who she was with before I got there but from the way she was fixing her clothes it wasn\u2019t hard to put two and two together. <br /> <br /> Though it was a little less clear why was the girl so uptight about love when we talked. Unless\u2026 Oh, maybe I interrupted her and whoever before they were done. That\u2019d explain it. Anyway, seems pretty certain that La Blue Girl isn\u2019t using tale-crafting to seduce people trying to keep an eye on her. So back to not knowing how she\u2019s mind fucking people. And it certainly doesn\u2019t seem to be temporary. Poor Dahlia. She\u2019s got enough body issues without this shit stirring them up. I really need to figure this out before she winds up as twitterpated as the rest. Just not sure where to go next with things.<br /> <br /> So that idea didn\u2019t pan out. But I did get to see Leanne and it turns out that Spidertoes didn\u2019t do anything horrid to her. Just showed up in her room and warned her to be careful with \u2018her\u2019 Darklings. That still grates on my nerves but Charlotte made a point of reminding me that people who go against her wind up dead in the most unpleasant ways and not even the Autumn Monarch can prevent it. She also made a point of mentioning that anyone who sided with me against her would die as well. Woman knows me well enough to know that\u2019s more likely to cool my jets. And honestly, as much as it does irk me, she seems to mean well enough and it really isn\u2019t a fight I can win. I should just let it go and concentrate on more important things.<br /> <br /> Gawain is in full prep for Thanksgiving tomorrow. Everything seems to be in place. Food, company, karaoke, and an open bar should be enough to get folks through the holiday. Keeping it all running smoothly should be enough to distract me from thinking about my folks\u2026<br /> <br /> And then there\u2019s the show Saturday. Bloody Creature Poster Girl is going to rule. Lori and I have really pulled out the stops and put this one together. I am so stoked for this. Should be a nice turn out for it to. Lots of folks saying they\u2019ll be out to catch the act. I think I am going to have a word with blood before the show. Should be able to sweet talk it into getting the audience\u2019s pulses racing and their blood running hot. Yeah, that should make the act go better and open the door for some fine fun afterward.<br /> <br /> Hmm\u2026 Working out this act with Lori has really been nice. Maybe I should see if I can find something to do with Insincere Marguerite? She really seemed to enjoy being on stage but she seems gun-shy about doing it again. It\u2019d be good for her confidence to nail another number though. I mean it feels so good to be up there and know you\u2019ve got the crowd eating out of your hand. And maybe it would help us get closer. Things are better but it\u2019s still a long way from the way it was before. Yeah\u2026 I\u2019m going to start looking for something suitable for us to do together and pitch that to her.<br /> <br /> Damn, this day is looking up. Leanne hasn\u2019t been harmed or frightened off from me. I\u2019ve got a plan for how to continue patching things up with my Darkling sister. Oh, and I\u2019ve got the coolest knife. I mean, if it really is the trademark weapon of the Court of Fallen Stars\u2019 chief Autumn Court assassin it has to have some kind of really nice enchantment, right? I wonder how Shi got it. I mean, it would be nice to know if I should be expecting a visit from him\u2026 her? It? You know, maybe I should have asked Leanne more about this assassin since she recognized the knife.<br /> <br /> Oh well\u2026 looks like I\u2019m just going to have to go see her again sometime in the near future. Hmm\u2026 you know, maybe I do have time before Annika gets here\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T14:57:35-07:00","id":992036,"title":"","content":"<b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Well today was a fairly eventful day. It started out with me and Calamity meeting up in the kitchen. She didn\u2019t look like she\u2019d slept but insisted that she was fine. I left well enough alone for now since she didn\u2019t seem like she wanted to talk about it. Calamity reminded me that we were going to take Rowan to the Clinic with us to see if they could help her get over the loss of her house. So, I went upstairs and knocked on the door. She was staying in Lori and De La Rocha\u2019s room. Insincere Marguerite and Julia opted to stay up and watch Rowan as she slept to make sure she was okay. Julia answered the door and I explained what we were doing and why. She did not seem overly pleased by my request to wake Rowan, but she did so anyway. Rowan was not really happy to see me. I did hold her down so she could not get involved in the fight with the house, so I believe she is still upset with me. After a few moments Calamity came up and Rowan looked at her with the same expression. I realized that Rowan was not going to willingly go to the Clinic with two people that she disliked and didn\u2019t trust, so I asked her if she\u2019d feel more comfortable if Lori came with us. She seemed to be comforted by that option so I told her I\u2019d be right back and went over to Insincere Marguerite\u2019s room where Lori was sleeping. De La Rocha opened the door naked and demanded to know what I wanted. I will admit that I was a little surprised that she answered the door naked, but I think I managed to hide it pretty well. I explained what was going on and why we needed Lori. De La Rocha, grumpy though she was, got Lori up and I explained again what was going on. Lori said that she\u2019d be right down and went to get dressed.<br /> <br /> So, the four of us went to the Clinic in my jeep. Rowan and Lori rode in the back. I think Lori likes sitting back there since there\u2019s room for her wings and the wind must feel nice on them. Anyhoo, we got to the clinic and talked to one of the Therapists to explain what had happened, and they said that they\u2019d do what they could for Rowan. From what I found out later they are going to keep Rowan at the Clinic for a few days to help her get over the house. They said that her condition is very much like someone who was having a hard time getting over what happened to them in Arcadia, and they are very experienced in helping with that. So, Lori talked with Rowan for a bit before we all left.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile Calamity and I had our regular sessions. I admitted to my doctor that I was feeling a bit homesick due to the holiday. My family only celebrated Thanksgiving a few times since we moved to the United States, since it is an American holiday, but we still embraced it. We had a lot to be thankful for. Dad got a better job when we moved here, as did mom. We didn\u2019t struggle to buy what we needed anymore. So for Thanksgiving we cooked a turkey but usually had some traditional Russian food to go along with it. The last Thanksgiving that I was there for we had Golubtsy and Okroshka. It was really good. Dad made some Kvass too. Maybe I\u2019ll make some for our Freehold\u2019s Thanksgiving feast. It\u2019s not really all that alcoholic despite being fermented so anyone can drink it. So, I talked to my therapist about all of this. He was said that a lot of Changelings get homesick during the holidays since most of us cannot go back to their families. It\u2019s not an uncommon problem. Which made me think of Calamity this morning. She seemed off to me and I\u2019ll bet that she was thinking about her family. She, like the rest of us cannot go home, but for her it\u2019s a little worse. She\u2019s the one that killed her parents so she\u2019s got to be more than a little upset about things. I wish I knew of a way to help her. She deserves to be happy, though I\u2019m fairly sure that she would be the first to tell me that I was wrong on that count. <br /> <br /> So, after the therapy session and our usual sparring match, Calamity and I joined the rest of the motley for breakfast. Gawain was still on his waffle kick and made bergische waffles. They were heart shaped and served with cherries, cream and rice pudding. I thought they were good, though very much like a dessert if you ask me. While we were eating Gawain got a text from Jack with a picture of him dressed like a turkey and the words \u201csoon\u201d by his feet. Gawain responded by dressing like a chef with a ridiculous sized cleaver and send a picture back to Jack. I think they are going to plan something for the Thanksgiving Day dinner. Those two love to ham it up.<br /> <br /> After breakfast I asked to talk to Insincere Marguerite. I wanted to know if it was okay with her if I told Luna what was going on with Desiree. She said that it was fine, so I took Luna aside and explained what was going on. She took things rather well, though she did say that she didn\u2019t trust Desiree. I can understand that sentiment right now. My opinion of Desiree has dropped significantly since I found out what she did to Insincere Marguerite. I\u2019m pretty sure that I can act like nothing is wrong though. I am proficient at hiding my emotions behind my mask, probably a little too well given my conversation with Marguerite when she first told me about Desiree and her need for a Keeper. So, I will treat Desiree as I have been but will keep a closer eye on her to be on the safe side.<br /> <br /> And just so today wouldn\u2019t become dull Queen Charlotte came by the house and said that she needed to speak to us. She wanted to speak to Lori alone first. I do not know what that conversation was about but Lori looked contemplative afterwards. I will admit that I am curious. The next group she wanted to talk to was the Autumn courtiers plus Insincere Marguerite since she is their Dread Esquire. Again, not sure everything that was talked about but I know at least some of it had to do with the shadow creatures that escaped Rowan\u2019s house when we attacked it. Luna told me that she had been tasked with tracking the shadow creatures and asked if I could help her do that tomorrow. I said that I\u2019d be happy to help. It\u2019s been a while since I actively tracked someone/something. Well, I suppose the last time I did it was when we took that Hedge Beast lesson with Augustine. But the last time I really tracked someone was when I worked for the Lady. I frequently was sent out to find and retrieve runaways. It really depended on the Lady\u2019s mood if the runaway was brought back alive or not. Sometimes she just wanted the problem dealt with, in which case I would track down the person running and kill them. Other times, like with D\u0336e\u0336l\u0336i\u0336g\u0336h\u0336t\u0336 Diane, the Lady wanted her back alive. That of course didn\u2019t end the way it was supposed to. Not that it\u2019s a bad thing the way things turned out. I of course still regret little Felicity\u2019s death, but things turned out for the good in the end. Diane is still free, as am I. I sometimes still feel like I\u2019m chained to the Lady. Maybe it\u2019s because I still bear her brand. I wish I could get rid of it, but trying to do that has never ended well. I wonder sometimes why it still has magic. Has the Lady not yet renounced me? Is she still hoping that I\u2019ll come back to her service?<br /> <br /> Anyway, after the talk with the Autumn Courtiers Queen Charlotte wanted to talk to the motley as a whole. She said that she had been in contact with Night Queen Skitters in Paris about Insincere Marguerite and the plan to clear her name so she can go home. Overall the group was happy that the Night Queen in Paris was willing to let us speak on Marguerite\u2019s behalf. The timing however could have been better. It just so happens to come up after Desiree manipulates Insincere Marguerite into being her Keeper. Now the lot of us are going to have to lie to Queen Skitters and say that Marguerite has never kept anyone since she has returned from Arcadia. Some of us are accomplished liars, some not so much. I believe that if Lorelei put her mind to it she could be a good liar. She is a very good actress and performer. She could probably project any front that she wanted to. Calamity can be hard to read sometimes, so maybe she\u2019ll be okay. I am a decent liar, but have been out of practice for a while now. I am hard to read though, so that should help. We probably will not have Julia speak to Queen Skitters. Julia, though she loves Insincere Marguerite very much, is a bit too submissive in that whole relationship and that might not look good overall. So, we set up the meeting with Queen Skitters for early Saturday afternoon. That should give us some time to come up with what we\u2019re going to say and how we\u2019re going to say it.<br /> <br /> The show went on as usual. There were a few notable things that happened, but it was not an overly eventful evening. Early on TJ showed up while Gawain was manning the door and just said that he didn\u2019t do \u201cit,\u201d then he left. Gawain assumed that he was talking about Rowan\u2019s house and let the other man go on his way. It would look rather suspicious for TJ considering that he\u2019d been harassing Rowan for a while before the whole House incident. We know of course that he had nothing to do with it so everything was okay. I also thought it was interesting that representatives of the Day and Night courts were present and sitting at the same table. Have they come to some sort of arrangement or truce? I should probably ask Insincere Marguerite that.<br /> <br /> Had a bit of a nice surprise tonight as well. Molly came to the bar to hang out and talk. I haven\u2019t seen her for a few days so I was curious what she\u2019d been up to. I guess I\u2019d also kind of gotten used to her being at the bar. So, she said that she\u2019d been spending time with Chalcedony and that it has been educational but nice. She asked us how we were and what we\u2019d been up to so Gawain and I did our level best to explain what happened with Rowan\u2019s house and try not to look crazy. I don\u2019t think she believed us at first, but she eventually came around. Then she asked us about Felicity and what we thought of her. She said that Lowjack doesn\u2019t trust her, which doesn\u2019t really come as a surprise. Lowjack doesn\u2019t trust a lot of people. The thing that was interesting was apparently Chalcedony doesn\u2019t trust Felicity either. I can\u2019t help but wonder why. I admitted to Molly that Felicity has been annoying me lately mainly because of her relationship with Insincere Marguerite. I didn\u2019t go into details, but did mention that they were seeing one another. After the show Calamity mentioned that she had talked to Dionysia and she said that Leonidas was not happy with how things went down with Rowan\u2019s house. Apparently Felicity followed Insincere Marguerite\u2019s suggestion to stay away and let us deal with things. I\u2019m assuming that Leonidas wanted her to do something different but instead of listening to her King she followed the suggestion of her paramour. Interesting.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> And yet more waffles. Gawain made Hong Kong style waffles this time. They were interesting, I\u2019ll give them that. Never thought of peanut butter being part of waffles, but you learn something new every day. So, Lori came back to the house after her night with Joan and Andromeda and she got Joan to wear a slinky red dress. I didn\u2019t know that Joan owned anything that wasn\u2019t white. Maybe she borrowed it? In any case, she looked nice. There was some good natured ribbing about her dress and she got a little embarrassed but I think she knows it was all in good fun. In any case Joan was sticking close to Andromeda and Lori. And speaking of sticking close, Insincere Marguerite was kind of clingy with Julia this morning, but she didn\u2019t seem upset about anything. I can only assume that the events of yesterday have got her feeling clingy with her lover.<br /> <br /> At some point we started talking about the movie Titanic and Julia brought up the love scene in the car. She figured that the whole thing would be uncomfortable and said as much. That launched into a whole discussion about having sex in cars and who has done it and who hasn\u2019t. I was a little surprised to find out the Luna had sex in the back of a car with a linebacker before she was taken. She seemed to be really proud of this fact. Others were just as enthusiastic about their experiences. I did admit to Julia that I have never had sex in the back seat of a car. I think she was at least a little relieved that she wasn\u2019t the only one.<br /> <br /> After that people went their separate ways. Calamity went to the Library to do some research and Luna and I made our way back to Rowan\u2019s house to see if we could track those shadow creatures. We looked around thoroughly and found that there were some faint washed out blades of grass and other greenery leading away from the house. The trail did not show up on the pavement or dirt. The path led away from the house and seemed to go in a bunch of different directions. It also seemed to go out of its way to stay away from other houses. That was pretty much all we found out. Doesn\u2019t really give us much to go on, but we do know that the shadow creatures leave grass and other plants kind of pale and washed out. A lot of things can do that to plants though, I\u2019m assuming. So, we came back to report our findings to Queen Charlotte. After we got back we mentioned what we\u2019d found to the rest of the motley.<br /> <br /> Apparently Calamity had an interesting time at the Library. As she was entering the building she was stopped by Shi who asked if she\u2019d like to buy an ornate looking switchblade for something like $6 or $7. Calamity was interested and purchased the knife. When she got inside Leanne recognized the blade and said that it may have belonged to the main assassin for the Hollywood Courts. This leads to several questions. How did Shi get the knife? Is the previous owner still alive and are they going to want it back? They kenned the knife and learned that it is in fact magical in some way, so someone may very well be looking for it. What can of worms did we open this time?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> Today was fairly good. Started early.<br /> <br /> Julia and I watched Rowan all night. We cuddled and talked. I laid out what I needed from her, now, and she discussed her needs. I discussed mine. We were talking when Jacob and Calamity came to take Rowan away. I had missed that detail, distracted by my problems as I was. Julia was protective, but agreed to let her go especially when Lori got involved. We eventually finally got some sleep, but only a couple hours.<br /> <br /> We woke in time for sex breakfast, and commandeered cream and cherries from Gawain\u2019s wafflemaking so Juliette would poof us. She was in an okay mood when she arrived, and sex breakfast went pretty well. I was really was distracted by Julia\u2019s scent. It is delightful, so unique, when I sit with my face hear her chin, her hair making a curtain around I. It is heaven. Golden hair just like mine.<br /> <br /> The conversation lead to discussion of sex in the back of a car. Julia incredulously asked if anyone had not had sex in the back of a car. Jacob hadn\u2019t, but he was the only other. Even shy Luna was bragging about sex with a football player before she was taken as a gay man, and Maria went on about El Caminos. Julia just got disgusted and held on to I.<br /> <br /> Then when we wrapped up Maria wanted to talk to I. We spoke briefly. She wanted I to make a vow I would do all I can to get Desiree free and safe. That I would not impede. She told I she loved I but she had to have my promise. So I gave it. It seemed to ease her mind a little. I wish I could do that for Juliette\u2019s.<br /> <br /> So we went upstairs to dance. Julia wanted more dances. Slow, special. This time, unlike the time on stage, she sang to I. Just whatever song went through her head. Some made up. Some from her childhood. Some more recent. I felt the most lovely, most unbearable weakness.<br /> <br /> I was in a trance when Calamity came up to call us down. Queen Charlotte was there and wanted to talk to members of the Motley. First was about the house. Julia and I will be sending our comments along. Second was she wanted us to talk to Nightqueen Skitters, who is sort of insane, about the fact that I am not Keeping people.<br /> <br /> It feels ill timed.<br /> <br /> Still everyone was supportive, which was a relief. She will Skype in again Saturday and ourselves and whomever we bring will testify in my favor. Flores has asked to. Desiree will not. White Maria offered, and I am a little torn; she is absolutely my type, But would a beautiful treasured saying yes we had been lovers but no, I have never tried to take her would be awkward, especially given we have role played it essentially and she is afraid of and intrigued by it happening.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s all very awkward.<br /> <br /> The rest of the afternoon I fell under the spell of the soothing voice and delicious scent of my fianc\u00e9e, only coming out of my trance in time for the show. Maria, Julia and I were at the stage, and Becky joined us. I need to ask if Calamity has made things official. Things were actually quite busy; Lori had gone to spend the night with Andromeda and Joan, but we still had a good crowd.<br /> <br /> While we were there, Maria asked not to be alone tonight and we obliged. There was no sex, but cuddling. And it was nice. Maria has a slightly different smell than the rest of us, and it is wonderful. She wanted to cling to I, whisper to I that she did not wish to lose I. It was very nice. I slept well. Blissfully.<br /> <br /> Breakfast was fun. Juliette brought and Andromeda and Joan\u2026in a striking red dress in Joan\u2019s case. Joan was a bit shy, but Andromeda was quite cheerful. We didn\u2019t really go easy on Joan, but I was all wrapped up in Julia.<br /> <br /> Afterwards, While Julia and I went to dance. Luna and Jacob went to track the house, while Calamity went to the Library, presumably to talk to Charlotte. Maria went to work. One more day and I will be recharged. I am actually looking forward to tomorrow. We will be together as a family on thanksgiving. A real family. The women I love more than anything. That I would kill for. Die for. Go to Arcadia for. Not return for.<br /> <br /> Let it not come to that.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXVII</i><br /> <br /> Not a lot of die rolling this time.<br /> <br /> Jacob turned down any hints of making him Winter King and Insincere Marguerite was not sanguine about becoming Night Queen, will Lorelei go the same way with Spring Queen? I am not sure any of us know.<br /> <br /> Related aside, Skitters is Autumn Court. She styles herself Nightqueen, but that is due in parts to a lack of those Courts in France. Skitters, of course, is a character in Golden Eagle, and will be making a brief appearance again soon there as well.<br /> <br /> Luna and Jacob did well on their search just not much to find.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite spent most of the session in a trance from Julia\u2019s Nightsinger powers.<br /> <br /> Okay that covers it, I think. Let me know if I missed anything. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T16:32:16-07:00","id":992099,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Lori is a lovely woman, but that is exactly why she should not be Spring Queen. You need someone with enough calluses on their heart to make the tough choices without grief and remorse, but enough morality to know when cruelties are not necessary. Lowjack, Charlotte and Augustine (to a certain extent, he worries me) are competent Monarchs in that respect in my opinion and could help shore her up, but they have to tread carefully enough that the Wyrd doesn't think they're trying to rule during the Spring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T18:54:08-07:00","id":992163,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7920_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7920\" data-vbnamecard=\"7920\">Master Aquatosic</a> I would disagree. Lori has proven herself capable of defending herself, both violently and not, has a lot of political clout (let us not forget that around Calamity's trial, mechanically, Lori had around 17 dice she could use, and her speech moved the present monarchs), and she has likewise proven herself to be compassionate but not naive. True, she's not perfect and as she stands Lori probably isn't in the best condition to become queen, but I do feel she has what it takes to act as a monarch in time. While Summer, Autumn and Winter all have harsh elements to them, Spring is meant more for recovering, jubilation and passions, all of which Lori has in spades.<br /> <br /> Still, we'll have to see how things are handled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T10:02:36-07:00","id":992440,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7920_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7920\" data-vbnamecard=\"7920\">Master Aquatosic</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5803_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5803\" data-vbnamecard=\"5803\">Taidragon</a>: As Lori's player, I think you both raise <i>very</i> good points. In fact, both of these points of view have already been expressed in-game (see Lori's next diary entry - which I have unfortunately not yet begun writing - for more details). The truth is that Lori could definitely - almost effortlessly - command the loyalty of most of her fellow Spring Courtiers if she were to take up the mantle of Queen, but her lack of experience in political matters would be a crippling deficiency in her potential reign. Lori is not by nature a devious person, and she is ill-equipped to recognize plotting in others... in short, someone like Darke, Lowjack, or Torrez would probably find it ridiculously easy to manipulate her actions and decisions.<br /> <br /> Having said that, Lori is not so proud that she would refuse to listen to those around her, so if she could get a cadre of good advisors on her side, she might be able to mitigate her own deficiencies in dealing with the other monarchs and external threats. It's been demonstrated that she inspires loyalty and beneficence in her friends, and she is genuinely interested in making as many people truly happy as possible. In fact, before this plot came up I was sort of subtly hinting to the Baroness that Lori might make a good Joyeux for the Freehold. So she probably has the right personality for the role. Given time to grow into the position, who knows what she might become?<br /> <br /> Of course, as always, everything in this post is my own opinions, and should not be read as gospel truth from the Baroness' mouth... or even foreshadowing. Lori herself doesn't <i>want</i> the crown... but to her mind the issue is far more complicated than a simple power grab (again, see the forthcoming diary entry for a few more details). But however this story eventually develops, it's going to take time. Chances are you won't see any real movement on this front until we've done at least another time-jump or two. What can I say? Lori's Spring Court. We're all about planting seeds...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T13:28:11-08:00","id":999401,"title":"","content":"Thanksgiving at the Dreamhouse. A time to spend with one\u2019s family. Or be maudlin at lack thereof. Either or.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LXVIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Okay, so writing in this journal is probably not the <u><u>best</u></u> cure for a hangover, but it\u2019s what I have available at the moment. D\u2019s still asleep, and I figured I\u2019d give her that last hour or two before the alarm says we\u2019re supposed to be awake rather than disturb her. I\u2019d go downstairs and fix a pot of black coffee, but I\u2019m honestly not sure how many of our compatriots from the Freehold are crashing down there right now. They all partied hearty last night, and I don\u2019t want to disturb <u><u>them</u></u> either. I tried reading a biology textbook, but it quickly became obvious that my brain was not in a very receptive state. So here we are.<br /> <br /> The last couple of days haven\u2019t been bad, really, though there have certainly been gloomy spots here and there. After my last entry I retreated to my bedroom so as to avoid Annika during Calamity\u2019s dance lesson. I was sort of idly reading a medical journal and listening to music when there was a soft knock at my door. Answering it, I found Marguerite standing there, looking faintly amused.<br /> <br /> \u201cI thought you should know,\u201d she said softly, \u201cthat Day King Leonidas has challenged me to a duel over Felicity\u2019s honor.\u201d She stood there for a moment, looking uncertain of how to continue. \u201cI have refused him,\u201d she added when I didn\u2019t respond.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2026 see,\u201d I eventually replied. \u201cAnd\u2026 what year is it today, exactly?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201c2014,\u201d she replied with a grin.<br /> <br /> \u201cI know I\u2019ve been out of the loop for a while,\u201d I said, \u201cand I\u2019m not always up-to-date on current trends and social norms. Did dueling come back into fashion at some point over the past four decades?\u201d<br /> <br /> Marguerite shook her head. \u201cNot that I am aware,\u201d she said, the corners of her mouth twitching.<br /> <br /> I sighed. \u201cWell, at least he didn\u2019t send you a dagger and expect you to do the honorable thing,\u201d I muttered grumpily.<br /> <br /> \u201cI wanted you to know,\u201d she explained, \u201cbecause Leonidas does not take well to being thwarted. The last time we clashed, he burned my house and tried to drop part of a building on me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAre you okay? Do you need protection?\u201d<br /> <br /> She sniffed in that haughty-cute way of hers. \u201cIt is to laugh,\u201d she said with disdain. \u201cInsincere Marguerite is more than a match for him. But\u2026 I do not <u><u>think</u></u> he would strike at me through you\u2026 his precious honor would never allow it. But I wanted you to be aware\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled in what I hoped was a reassuring way. \u201cI\u2019ll be careful,\u201d I promised.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt is probably nothing to worry about,\u201d she repeated. \u201cLeonidas is very charismatic, but not very smart.\u201d<br /> <br /> I shook my head and chuckled a little. \u201cI can\u2019t really fault him for that; I\u2019m the same way,\u201d I said with a self-deprecating smile.<br /> <br /> Marguerite\u2019s face turned deadly serious. \u201cDo not say such things,\u201d she said sharply.<br /> <br /> I tried to laugh it off. \u201cCome on, sweetie, you know I\u2019m no Einstein\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDo not say such things,\u201d she repeated, putting a hand on my shoulder and drawing me close. \u201cYou are beautiful <u><u>and</u></u> intelligent, Juliette. I would not have fallen in love with you if you were vapid.\u201d<br /> <br /> I put my hand on top of hers and smiled through the shimmer that inexplicably settled over my eyes. \u201cThank you, Marguerite,\u201d I whispered, and gave her hand a squeeze.<br /> <br /> The rest of the motley was duly informed of these developments. Calamity already knew, as she was the one who met Olivia Gold at the door when she rather reluctantly delivered her monarch\u2019s challenge. Most of the others seemed to share my opinion of the absurdity of the situation, though Gawain confessed that he had been prepared to offer himself up as Marguerite\u2019s second if it came to that. Sometimes I forget how much all that medieval bullshit is ingrained into his personality.<br /> <br /> In any case, all this talk about monarchs had me thinking, and I decided that it was high time I asked Jolie\u2019s opinion on Queen Charlotte\u2019s rather audacious suggestion. I called Glamour Springs and spoke to Dark Kimberly for a little while. She didn\u2019t know if the Princess was planning to attend the Dream House that night (or for the following day\u2019s Thanksgiving party), but she didn\u2019t think it was likely. Desiree and Jolie have been spending most of their evenings clubbing out of sight of the Freehold at large. But she was currently in residence, and Kimberly opined that she would be happy to meet with me if I wanted to stop by.<br /> <br /> Half an hour later I entered the lobby of Glamour Springs. Dark Kimberly waved me toward the door, telling me that Jolie was meeting with Andromeda, but that they were nearly done and I should just walk right in. I walked past Becky, White Maria and Desiree on my way back (the latter with, I admit, a somewhat frosty look on my face), and soon found myself in the Princess\u2019 office.<br /> <br /> Andromeda had obviously stopped by to run some routine maintenance on the spa\u2019s systems, and she looked <u><u>adorable</u></u> in her work clothes\u2026 coveralls and a tool belt with one of those little \u201cHello My Name Is\u201d nametags pinned to her chest. Where her name should have been there was only a row of cute pink hearts. The two of them concluded their business, and Andromeda gave me a friendly kiss on her way out.<br /> <br /> \u201cHi, Lori,\u201d the Princess said with a smile as I approached. \u201cWhat can I do for you? I hope everything\u2019s okay\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cI just wanted to talk with you privately about something, I said with a glance at the door. <br /> <br /> Jolie nodded, and Becky sort of rolled her eyes, sighed, and closed the door. \u201cNow, how can I help you?\u201d the Princess asked brightly.<br /> <br /> I wasn\u2019t sure quite where to begin. \u201cUmm\u2026 Queen Charlotte stopped by the Dream House yesterday,\u201d I said after a moment. \u201cShe wanted to talk with the motley about the business with Rowan\u2019s house.\u201d I stopped for a second. \u201cHow much do you know about that business?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> Jolie shrugged. \u201cI got a general briefing with the rest of the monarchs, but it wasn\u2019t particularly detailed,\u201d she admitted.<br /> <br /> I briefly outlined the events leading up to the fight from my perspective, making sure to note Oleander\u2019s contributions. \u201cCharlotte asked to speak to me privately,\u201d I went on, \u201cabout Oleander\u2019s actions. You see, the Queen had refused to grant her permission for Oleander to use the toxin, and she\u2026 did it anyway. Because I asked her.\u201d I confess that I hung my head at that.<br /> <br /> Jolie took my chin in one hand and forced me to look into her eyes. I saw genuine concern there. \u201cAre you okay, Lori?\u201d she asked seriously. \u201cIs Oleander? Do either of you need protection?\u201d<br /> <br /> I loved my Princess so much at that moment. The fact that she would have been willing to go against her co-monarch\u2019s wishes to help me was humbling. \u201cNo,\u201d I said with a smile, \u201cCharlotte said she wasn\u2019t going to punish either of us. It was the fact that I was able to command loyalty like that in Oleander \u2013 who is not known for acting rashly out of passion \u2013 that had gotten her attention. She\u2026 she wanted me to consider a proposition.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jolie quirked her head to one side in an unspoken question.<br /> <br /> I sighed again. \u201cShe\u2019s noticed how much the crown is weighing on you, Princess. She wanted me to consider taking it up to spare you any further pain.\u201d<br /> <br /> I think she was truly surprised at that revelation, but she only let it show for a second before she began sizing me up. \u201cIt\u2019s your inexperience with ruling that gives me pause,\u201d she said after a moment. \u201cThat would be my only concern. But we could overcome that, if this is something you want to pursue.\u201d<br /> <br /> I shook my head. \u201cI don\u2019t\u2026 not really. But I want to help you, Jolie. You\u2019re my friend. You believed in me before anyone else in the Freehold even knew who I was. And if I could help you by taking up this burden for you, then I feel like I should. I just wanted you to know that I would never take the crown from you without your express approval. I don\u2019t want to usurp anyone.\u201d<br /> <br /> She turned away and sat down. \u201cI never wanted the crown either,\u201d she said softly. \u201cAfter the affair with Golden Swan, Austin declared that he was unfit to be the Spring monarch, and I was sort of thrust into the role. I never felt I was ready for it. I asked Austin to be an advisor, but he refused, claiming that his failure as monarch was great enough that we shouldn\u2019t listen to his decisions or opinions anymore.\u201d She turned to look me in the eye. \u201cI don\u2019t know if this is something you should do, Lori, but I want you to know that if you <u><u>do</u></u> follow through on it, I won\u2019t do anything to trap you in the position, and I will <u><u>always</u></u> be available for advice and support.\u201d<br /> <br /> I looked at her then. I mean I <u><u>really</u></u> looked at her. I haven\u2019t often employed the Contracts of Spring to read people\u2019s desires; it seems like an invasion of privacy in most cases. But in this case I really wanted to know how she felt, beyond politics and friendship. She\u2019s not easy to read, but I managed to penetrate her fa\u00e7ade and see the desires swimming beneath the surface.<br /> <br /> She wants out. She <u><u>desperately</u></u> wants out, and she was looking at me like a lifeline. Only her resolve not to see anyone pushed into the monarchy before they\u2019re ready \u2013 like she was \u2013 stopped her from saying it. So I guess I had my answer.<br /> <br /> \u201cIf I do this,\u201d I began, trying to keep the tremble out of my voice, \u201cit won\u2019t be immediately. I\u2019m not ready for that level of responsibility; you said it yourself. And I\u2019d need to make sure the Dream House could get by without me\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Jolie shook her head. \u201cIt\u2019s true that you wouldn\u2019t be able to perform every night, but you could rule from there. Even if I step down as Princess, I wouldn\u2019t leave Glamour Springs, so you\u2019d need to establish your own court location.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThere\u2019s something else,\u201d I said, hoping to curb her enthusiasm a little. \u201cI don\u2019t think I\u2019ve ever told you about my Durance, have I?\u201d<br /> <br /> She shook her head. \u201cOnly the basics. I try not to ask; people don\u2019t usually like talking about it.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cI was taken in 1978\u2026 and I wasn\u2019t taken alone. My two best friends are still in Arcadia, and I\u2026 I have to do something about that if I can. If I was Queen, it wouldn\u2019t be right for me to run off into Arcadia to fulfill some personal quest. So I have to make sure I\u2019ve done everything I can for Missy and Jane before I can even consider taking up the Crown.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded and put a hand on my shoulder. I may be reading too much into this, but I could swear she sort of deflated a little. \u201cI understand, Lori,\u201d she said. \u201cI\u2019d never force it on you\u2026 on <u><u>anyone</u></u>. But if it\u2019s something you\u2019re willing to do, I\u2019ll help you if I can.\u201d<br /> <br /> I gave her what I\u2019m pretty sure ended up as a fairly weak smile. \u201cI\u2019ll\u2026 have to think about it,\u201d I admitted.<br /> <br /> She winked and threw me a grin that reminded me of our first meeting almost a year ago. \u201cGood start,\u201d she said with a chuckle.<br /> <br /> So I ambled out of Glamour Springs, returning the pleasantries my fellow courtiers threw in my direction without really thinking about it. I remained in a state of deep thought until I got home, at which point I threw myself into preparing for the show.<br /> <br /> About an hour before opening curtain, I got a call from the Clinic. Rowan wanted to talk to me, and I was eager to get a progress report from her. \u201cHello?\u201d I said nervously as I waited for them to connect me with her.<br /> <br /> \u201cHi, Lori,\u201d she said after a moment. She sounded a little morose, but not nearly as dull or out of it as she had the previous morning.<br /> <br /> \u201cRowan, sweetie, it\u2019s so good to hear from you!\u201d I gushed. \u201cHow are you feeling?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m feeling a lot better, thanks,\u201d she said softly. \u201cDr. Kovacs says there\u2019s still some work to do, but she thinks things are going well. With any luck I should be able to go\u2026 to check out of the clinic by Monday.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s great news!\u201d I said with enthusiasm. \u201cI\u2019ll be there with bells on.\u201d<br /> <br /> She chuckled a bit\u2026 possibly at the image evoked by what I\u2019m coming to realize is probably something of an archaism these days. \u201cThanks, Lori,\u201d she said with feeling, \u201cit means a lot to me. I really miss you\u2026 but I haven\u2019t had the chance to get lonely; I\u2019ve had a lot of visitors from the Freehold. Dr. Bright came by to see me today, and Moon\u2026 along with some woman I didn\u2019t recognize.\u201d My money\u2019s on Dionysia, personally, but I guess there\u2019s no way to know for sure.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd Felicity stopped by today too, and the two of us had a talk. I feel so bad about the way I treated her\u2026 but she was really nice about it. She\u2019s offered to put me up until I get back on my feet. That way I won\u2019t be a burden on your motley\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t ever think that way, honey,\u201d I interrupted. \u201cWe\u2019re always happy to help you, and I want you to know that. We <u><u>do</u></u> have a few people staying with us already at the moment, though\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s fine,\u201d Rowan replied. \u201cLike I said, Felicity\u2019s been great. I mean, of course, I\u2019d <u><u>like</u></u> to stay with you\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLet me talk to the others,\u201d I said, thinking about it. \u201cGloria and Desiree are talking about getting their own place; maybe something will open up. If not, then I\u2019ll come and spend some time with you at your new place as soon as you have it set up, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay,\u201d she said. \u201cLook, Lori, I just wanted to say thanks\u2026 thanks for everything. And\u2026 I\u2019m looking at the sunset outside of my window right now. It\u2019s so beautiful. I guess\u2026 I guess I just wanted to feel like we were watching it together.\u201d I confess that I got a little choked up at this sweet sentiment, but she continued in a rush before I could give it the response it deserved. \u201cI won\u2019t take up any more of your time; I know you have a show tonight. I love you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLove you too,\u201d I said, and we disconnected. I still feel a little bad about saying that to her\u2026 I\u2019m still not certain how deep my feelings for Rowan actually run. But she\u2019s in a delicate place right now and I want her to know that I\u2019ll be there to help her no matter what. I don\u2019t want to make her question my dedication to her recovery.<br /> <br /> As curtain approached, I uploaded my song choices to Marguerite\u2019s computer as usual, and it occurred to me that I should probably let her know what was coming. I pulled her aside and asked if we could speak for a moment. \u201cMarguerite,\u201d I said when she nodded, \u201cI want you to know that the solo I chose for tonight\u2026 it\u2019s not about how I feel toward you. I\u2019m dedicated to helping you through your current troubles, I\u2019m still in love with you, and I\u2019m not trying to make you feel bad or anything like that. It\u2019s more of a general statement of my feelings on the subject. Okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> Marguerite glanced at the file name, then back at me. \u201cI see,\u201d she said seriously, \u201cthank you for telling me.\u201d Then she kissed me, and I knew we were all right.<br /> <br /> So the number in question was \u201cYou Don\u2019t Own Me\u201d by Leslie Gore. I\u2019ve always liked that song, and it has a particularly strong resonance with The Lost, so I figured it would go over pretty well. I also admit that I felt an almost impish glee as I tore away my outer clothing, revealing the burlesque outfit below as I sang the line \u201cdon\u2019t put me on display.\u201d<br /> <br /> Julia was giving me some dark looks during the number, but she went to talk to Marguerite as I left the stage, and came back looking somewhat mollified. I planted myself in her lap (she was already sitting in D\u2019s lap at the time, but my honey didn\u2019t mind). \u201cAre we okay, baby?\u201d I whispered into her ear. \u201cBecause I already told Marguerite that I didn\u2019t intend the song as an attack against her. I\u2019m just venting.\u201d<br /> <br /> She smiled and kissed me on the cheek. \u201cIt\u2019s okay, Lori,\u201d she breathed to me. \u201cI understand now. No harm done.\u201d<br /> <br /> In addition to the usual suspects, Becky was sitting at what has become known as the \u201cGirlfriend Table.\u201d I wonder if she and Calamity have finally made things official. Gawain seems okay with the whole situation, so if the two of them can gain a little more happiness from their association with each other, then I say full steam ahead! Of course, there are those who might say that I\u2019m somewhat biased in my opinions of polyamory.<br /> <br /> I had a few more backup and dance numbers, and as always I schmoozed for a bit. I stopped by Joan and Andromeda\u2019s table for what Ace would likely refer to as \u201ca quick bit o\u2019 snog,\u201d and I made sure to speak with all of our other changeling guests at least briefly, but I honestly spent most of my time with D and Julia (and Marguerite, once her technical duties were done for the night). When the house had emptied, the four of us retired to Marguerite and Julia\u2019s bedroom and fell asleep in each other\u2019s arms.<br /> <br /> Sex Breakfast the following morning was\u2026 interesting. I was completely blindsided by Becky, who confronted me as soon as I walked into the kitchen. \u201cLori, for the love of God please tell me that you get tested regularly for STDs,\u201d she said, obviously somewhat frazzled.<br /> <br /> I stared into her eerie all-white eyes (with my own eerie all-black eyes), and once I determined that she was asking a serious question and not trying to insult me, I answered her honestly. \u201cOf course,\u201d I said, \u201cevery couple of months. I mean, free love is great and all, but it comes with certain risks\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> She sighed with relief. \u201cThank you,\u201d she said, throwing a triumphant smile toward Calamity. \u201cSorry to spring that on you like that, I was just trying to prove a point.\u201d I\u2019m not exactly sure what that was about, but I\u2019m guessing Becky was trying to convince Calamity to take more interest in her own sexual health, which can only be a good thing. <br /> <br /> So that set the tone for the rest of our breakfast conversation, which was a little unusual to say the least. I\u2019m happy to report that both D and Julia get tested at least twice a year (though this is a relatively recent development in Julia\u2019s case, as she was not sexually active before she became involved with Marguerite). Color me relieved. Marguerite declined to answer, which was a little suspicious, but I\u2019m trying to be sanguine about it. I\u2019m told that, as a rule, we changelings are pretty resistant to mundane diseases, but there\u2019s no sense taking chances, right? In retrospect, it\u2019s a minor miracle that I never had any problems like that back <u><u>before</u></u> I was Taken.<br /> <br /> So after a light breakfast \u2013 in deference to the large meals inevitably coming later in the day, Gawain decided to dispense with the waffles and served up fruit and crepes \u2013 the four of us piled into Julia\u2019s car and began the hour-long drive to Anaheim. It was a fun trip; we spent most of the time chatting happily and singing along with the radio. Julia was nervous, but seemed excited to introduce me and D to her parents. She had described them to us as pretty laid back, and that took a lot of the pressure off, so we were looking forward to the meeting.<br /> <br /> We arrived at a pleasant ranch-style home in Anaheim slightly later than we\u2019d hoped (damned holiday traffic), and we were met at the door by a smiling fifty-something woman who greeted us all warmly with hugs. She was\u2026 well, honestly, she was probably about the age I would be if I had lived my whole life outside of Arcadia. She introduced herself as Linda Oldacre, and warmly ushered us into her living room where we were introduced to her husband, John, who gave each of us a firm handshake and a friendly smile.<br /> <br /> I was wearing a casual-but-nice ensemble, hoping to impress Julia\u2019s parents without looking like I was trying to impress them. Marguerite was in a suitably flattering set of clothes which were a bit more sedate than her usual offerings. D of course took this opportunity to wear her purple suit again, knowing how it gets my motor running (and Julia\u2019s, of course). And Julia was in one of her usual long skirt outfits.<br /> <br /> Dinner was ready about an hour later, and Linda asked demurely if Julia and I would mind helping her set the table. I chuckled inwardly at her assumption of gender-roles within our relationship, but let\u2019s face it\u2026 she was pretty much correct on that count. In any case, I didn\u2019t mind helping at all, and the three of us made our way to the kitchen to get things ready while the \u201cmen\u201d talked.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s a real pleasure to meet you at last, Lorelei,\u201d Linda bubbled as we bustled around the kitchen. \u201cWe\u2019ve heard so much about you and Maria from Julia. You make her so happy, and we couldn\u2019t be more pleased. In fact, now that I\u2019ve met you, I can\u2019t say I\u2019m surprised. You\u2019re definitely my daughter\u2019s type.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMother\u2026\u201d Julia began softly.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat do you mean, ma\u2019am?\u201d I cut in smoothly.<br /> <br /> \u201cPlease, call me Linda. Well, you very closely resemble the girls she used to draw when she was little. You have the blonde hair, and the\u2026 body type,\u201d she ended carefully, with an almost imperceptible glance down at my chest.<br /> <br /> \u201cMother!\u201d Julia said more insistently.<br /> <br /> I couldn\u2019t help but laugh at that. \u201cWell, Julia\u2019s had the opportunity to paint me from life several times now, and she obviously put that practice to good use. She has an amazing talent\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Julia, uncomfortable with being the center of attention at the best of times, broke in suddenly. \u201cSo when is grandma getting here?\u201d she asked in a falsely chipper tone.<br /> <br /> Linda\u2019s face fell a little. \u201cOh\u2026 I don\u2019t think she\u2019ll be able to make it this year, unfortunately,\u201d she said, her forced cheerfulness eerily echoing her daughter\u2019s.<br /> <br /> Julia glanced up sharply. \u201cIs she okay?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> Linda shrugged. \u201cShe\u2019s fine, honey\u2026 something just came up unexpectedly, and\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLike something \u2018came up\u2019 when I brought Marguerite to visit the first time?\u201d Julia snapped. \u201cDoes she have a problem with my relationship? Were you <u><u>hiding</u></u> it from me?\u201d<br /> <br /> Linda gave me an apologetic look before turning back to her daughter. \u201cI\u2019m sorry, honey,\u201d she said softly. \u201cWe didn\u2019t want to upset you. She\u2019s from a different time\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo what, she\u2019s just going to avoid me for the rest of her life?\u201d Julia said, her voice rising with real anger now. It was a very uncomfortable situation to witness, and I found myself in the unfamiliar position of trying to make myself unobtrusive as the three of us walked out to the living room together.<br /> <br /> \u201cThere is a problem?\u201d Marguerite asked with an arched eyebrow.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo\u2026\u201d Linda answered, while Julia said \u201cyes\u201d at almost the exact same time.<br /> <br /> Marguerite pulled Julia aside for a few minutes, presumably to figure out what was wrong and try to calm her down a bit. Linda turned to D apologetically, and said \u201cI\u2019m sorry about this, Maria, but would you mind helping us out in the kitchen for a few moments?\u201d<br /> <br /> D seemed as eager to escape the uncomfortable scene as I was, and the two of us finished setting the table while Marguerite and Julia talked. Everyone joined us in the dining room a short time later, and while I won\u2019t say she was all smiles, Julia seemed somewhat mollified.<br /> <br /> Dinner was great, and the pleasant conversation soon washed away the unpleasant aftertaste of Gran\u2019ma Oldacre\u2019s disapproval. John and Linda do seem to enjoy embarrassing their daughter, and they shared many amusing anecdotes with the rest of us over the next hour or so. They also mentioned that they had been involved in a polyamorous relationship themselves when Julia was younger. Julia seemed to know the man who had shared their bed, and was flabbergasted to learn that he had been their lover. As an interesting side note, their third was apparently the first person to recognize that Julia might be gay.<br /> <br /> At one point D was talking with John about her youth, and it came up that she had been involved with a gang. This was news to me\u2026 but then D doesn\u2019t often talk about her childhood, even when it\u2019s just the two of us. \u201cIt\u2019s been years, though,\u201d she said, presumably to mollify the Oldacres.<br /> <br /> Linda turned to face me at that point. \u201cLorelei, were you the one to rescue Maria from that lifestyle?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> I chuckled and took D\u2019s hand in mine. \u201cNo,\u201d I said proudly, \u201cmy honey had already gotten out and made a good life for herself before we met. And I couldn\u2019t be prouder of her.\u201d D smiled and squeezed my hand gratefully.<br /> <br /> I like them a lot. It sounds strange to say this about one of my girlfriends\u2019 parents, but\u2026 we have a lot in common. Like I said, if I had never been Taken, we\u2019d be close to the same age, and there\u2019s a sort of shared cultural experience that I don\u2019t often get from my regular circle of friends. They are open and tolerant, friendly and generous, and absolutely dedicated to their daughter\u2019s happiness. What more could one ask for?<br /> <br /> They\u2019re also trying to find time to come down to Malibu and visit us at the Dream House. Unfortunately we had to put those plans off for a while since we\u2019re closed on Friday, we have our meeting with Queen Skitters on Saturday, and it\u2019s difficult for them to stay out so late during the week due to their work schedules. Hopefully we\u2019ll be able to see them next Friday or Saturday and treat them to a show they\u2019ll never forget.<br /> <br /> We said our goodbyes shortly after dinner and received hugs and best wishes from John and Linda. Julia sort of defiantly told them to tell her grandmother that she was getting married next year, and that her grandmother <u><u>would</u></u> be at the wedding. I hope things work out.<br /> <br /> The drive home started out a little tense, but things eased up after a while. When we got back to the Dream House, the party was already in full swing. We\u2019d missed Joan and Andromeda by about half an hour, unfortunately\u2026 they were off to visit Andromeda\u2019s parents. I hope that went well. I\u2019ll have to remember to ask the next time I see them.<br /> <br /> Gawain had prepared a feast of epic proportions, and the liquor flowed freely from the bar like rain. The others had set up a TV on the covered porch out back for those who wanted to watch football, and Gawain\u2019s various gaming systems were up and running in the media room as well (I personally got my shapely ass handed to me by Moon twice before I gave up the video games as a bad idea).<br /> <br /> Captain Jack made a memorable entrance as usual. This time he burst into the theater area wearing a giant turkey costume, quickly followed by Gawain in a chef\u2019s outfit, brandishing a comically oversized cleaver. The two of them chased each other around the house to the strains of \u201cTurkey In the Straw\u201d for a while to general laughter and applause before changing into (slightly) more sedate clothing and joining the company.<br /> <br /> Mary was there, which was nice. I hadn\u2019t really seen much of her since the unpleasantness earlier this year, and it\u2019s good that she\u2019s getting out and being around people. She seemed just as shy and reserved as ever, though she didn\u2019t blush as much as she used to when we talked. She asked after Rowan\u2019s health, which sort of surprised me\u2026 when I asked about it, she just grinned and looked away, and said that she\u2019d thought the two of them might get along, as they\u2019re both shy Beast-type changelings.<br /> <br /> Marguerite had set up the sound system for karaoke, so for once I got to be the audience while the rest of the Freehold strutted their stuff. Captain Jack was one of the first to perform (\u201cEvery Rose Has Its Thorn,\u201d if I remember correctly\u2026 he called Gawain up on stage to join him in the refrains), and I couldn\u2019t resist\u2026 as the final notes of the song faded away, I shouted out \u201ctake it off!\u201d That got a few laughs; most of the assembled changelings knew that I\u2019d been subjected to that entreaty with some regularity over the course of the past six months. The good Captain declined to strip, however.<br /> <br /> There was a lot of talent on display\u2026 and more than a little \u201ctalent,\u201d as well. Most of the changelings in the Freehold seem to have at least a modicum of musical ability, which is nice to know\u2026 though there are a few exceptions. In my opinion, the performances ranged from professional caliber to wounded camel.<br /> <br /> After I\u2019d had a drink or two (both of Jacob\u2019s home-brewed \u2018kvass\u2019 and something a little harder), of course I couldn\u2019t resist taking the stage from time to time. I mostly sang songs from the 70s, since I knew the words well and wouldn\u2019t have to concentrate on singing them correctly. D got up there and belted out a few punk anthems as well... and she was pretty good, too! But every time she left the stage, the first thing she said to me was \u201cno, Lori, I won\u2019t perform in an actual show,\u201d so I guess I know her feelings on that subject.<br /> <br /> Jacob sang a Billy Joel song twice\u2026 once in English and then again later in Russian. Marguerite performed a couple of songs\u2026 the standout was an lovely upbeat number called \u201cNe Me Quitte Pas.\u201d Calamity did a few numbers in her own signature style, and even Gawain got up there once or twice (his rendition of Bryan Adams\u2019 \u201c(Everything I Do) I Do It For You,\u201d dedicated to Calamity, was\u2026 memorable). I guess the evening\u2019s biggest hit came when Gawain, Jacob, Captain Jack, Sandoval, and Davey got up there and belted out a hilarious parody of \u201cboy band\u201d anthems called \u201cTitle of the Song.\u201d I laughed so hard I nearly peed myself (in a very ladylike fashion, of course).<br /> <br /> Before I got too sloshed, I grabbed D by the arm and gave her my biggest, most soulful eyes, and asked if she\u2019d like to sing a duet with me. \u201cHow about \u2018You\u2019re the One That I Want,\u2019 from <u><u>Grease</u></u>?\u201d I asked pleadingly. She looked doubtful. \u201cOh, come on sweetie\u2026 you can be Travolta,\u201d I wheedled, and eventually she sort of sighed and agreed. Once we got up there, though, she really started getting into it, and belted it out with abandon.<br /> <br /> \u201cI got chills\u2026 they\u2019re multiplyin\u2019!\u201d It was a hell of a lot of fun, and I hope we can do it again some time.<br /> <br /> Okay, now to address the elephant in the room. I have no doubt that when most of my friends recount what happened at the Dream House\u2019s 2014 Thanksgiving Celebration, most of them will probably make note of how comically drunk Lorelei became as the evening wore on. And that\u2019s absolutely true; no sense in denying it. I had more than was good for me, and I\u2019m sure I made a complete ass of myself in front of most of the Freehold.<br /> <br /> But I wasn\u2019t as drunk as I <u><u>seemed</u> </u>to be. I confess I played it up a bit. It\u2019s an old trick I picked up from my party-girl days back in High School. You pretend to be more intoxicated than you really are, so that the bartenders will cut you off before you get really <u><u>dangerously</u></u> drunk and have to worry about passing out. It also gives you an excuse to give in to your carnal urges if you\u2019re in the mood for that, but leaves you lucid enough that you don\u2019t fall prey to creepos who want to seriously take advantage of you in a vulnerable state.<br /> <br /> So late that evening, when D told the others that she was going to see me safely to bed and started carrying me upstairs in her arms, I think she was a little surprised when I addressed her relatively soberly. \u201cSweetie?\u201d I said as I leaned into her shoulder.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, babe?\u201d she asked, kissing me on the forehead.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m drunk,\u201d I said, which made her giggle. \u201cBut I\u2019m not as drunk as you think. It\u2019s been a long day, and I\u2019m gonna get undressed and try to get some sleep when we get up to the bedroom. But you don\u2019t have to worry about me choking or puking or anything like that, okay? I\u2019d like nothing more than to have you snuggled up against me as I fall asleep, but if you want to go back downstairs and enjoy the party some more, don\u2019t worry about me, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks, Jules,\u201d she said as she shifted her grip to open our bedroom door, \u201cbut I think I\u2019d rather just climb into bed with you.\u201d She was blushing a little as she said it, even though I <u><u>know</u></u> she\u2019ll just say it was the alcohol if I ask her about it later. She can be the sweetest girl in the world, and I don\u2019t know why she\u2019s so afraid to admit it.<br /> <br /> So we got undressed, fell into bed together, and pulled up the covers. Thank God for thick walls; despite the ongoing party we were both asleep within minutes.<br /> <br /> I woke up maybe an hour ago without <u><u>too</u></u> much of a hangover (another thing to thank God for, I guess). Like I said at the beginning of this entry, I\u2019m not sure how many of our guests opted to sleep over in the theater, and I don\u2019t want to disturb anyone, so I haven\u2019t been downstairs yet. Sex Breakfast should be starting up soon, though, and after that Maria and I have the afternoon with Dad to look forward to. I can\u2019t wait!<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> Friday, November 27<sup>th</sup><br /> Nine years, six months, twenty-four days<br /> Days without stabbing: 3<br /> <br /> I am calm. After the past couple of days it feels strange and unreal and fragile, like the eye of the hurricane. Like the maelstrom of emotions could come crashing back in at any moment and sweep me away again. I have been erratic and out of control. Though, to be honest, (and right now I really need to be as focused and rational and absolutely honest as I can) I certainly could have handled things more poorly than I did. I was actually fairly coherent for the most part. This is progress. This is me being better even if I am not there yet. And I\u2019ll never be completely fine. I can only work on being closer step by step.<br /> <br /> The forms helped. They helped a lot. I am clear headed for the moment at least. I need to use this moment to figure out what I am going to do when Beautiful and Handsome wake. Last night is a little hazy around the edges here and there but never a blur. I can see now how steadily I unraveled yesterday evening. The harder I tried to push the memories and the guilt away the worse it got. The drinking did not help. That was a mistake. I should not do that again when I\u2019m so emotionally on edge. Lesson learned. It cannot be changed and so now I move forward and don\u2019t make the same mistake next time.<br /> <br /> I need to not make a mistake when they wake. I somehow managed to not ruin things yesterday. I have a chance to make this work. I have a chance to make this happen. I need to not screw this up. I wasn\u2019t in a good place emotionally to deal with this but more critically, I wasn\u2019t ready. I was not prepared. I must do better while I still have the opportunity to.<br /> <br /> I should focus and set my thoughts in order. Leanne. I did not need to talk to her Wednesday. I did not need to go to the Lighthouse at all. I could have spoken to Dionysia while she was here Tuesday night. Charlotte had already told me that Leanne was fine. I went there and I spoke to her because I wanted to see her. I wanted her to touch me. I wanted her to take my light. Despite knowing the danger and despite how clearly the motley made it that they were worried about my clearly reckless behavior I went hoping, without honestly thinking about it perhaps but still hoping to be fed upon. And I did so without making this intention known to anyone because I knew they would not approve. I cannot trust myself around Leanne. I need to avoid being alone with her. I do not trust her with my life and I cannot be so careless with it. Gawain told me he could not lose me. He said it in those exact words. He held me tightly in his arms and he was as honest as only a spirit as pure as his could be. And I told him he wouldn\u2019t lose me but then I went seeking Leanne anyway. I don\u2019t want to hurt him. I really do love him\u2026 I\u2019m just not very good at it.<br /> <br /> I was taken on the eve of my fourteenth birthday. I had Anastasia, who I loved like a sister and maybe more. In time I truly do believe we would have been lovers. But we were not. We were children. We both believed in the true love of fairy tales and romantic comedies. I was taken from that to Snow Globe. Forced, stilted, false relationships with the fleeting desperate and forbidden spark of actual love flickering in the dark like a match against the long winter\u2019s night. The stark truth of this is that I have no idea how to love either of them. Up until yesterday morning, I was still a naive little girl who just believed that being in love was all it took. That everything else just kinda magically fell into place if you had that.<br /> <br /> I knew better. I\u2019ve seen the truth of it all around me. Charlotte and Jolie love each other. But they can\u2019t be together. Love doesn\u2019t magically conquer all. Lori and DLR and Julia and Insincere Marguerite work hard to keep their relationship going. I knew this. Yet, somehow when it came to my own I was still looking through the rose colored lenses of before. And for months I have been waiting for Becky to be ready to admit that we\u2019re not just friends with benefits and when she started openly sitting at the \u2018girlfriend table\u2019 I was overjoyed. Suddenly the relationship I wanted so badly was there and I happily brought it up to her. And I was completely unprepared for her questions. I had no idea what I wanted or needed or expected. I floundered as she asked reasonable questions and grew steadily less pleased with my total lack of answers.<br /> <br /> Because suddenly, I was a clueless teenager trying to be in a relationship with a grown woman who\u2019s seen first hand how poorly things can go when you just dive in headlong without a clue. Worse than that, I\u2019m a clueless teenage girl with serious abandonment issues. Yes, it is my fault and that only makes it worse. The nightmare that flittered though my head instead of sleep before I got up to do my Tai Chi made that clear enough.<br /> <br /> I was back in Bellevue. Back in my parent\u2019s home. I was reliving that day and I knew what was happening but I could not stop it. I couldn\u2019t change what was happening. Only this time, as I fell to my knees and looked down at my bloody hands I knew it wasn\u2019t my parents I\u2019d just killed. I tried to break the dream but I wasn\u2019t fast enough, I couldn\u2019t escape without looking up at Gawain and Becky\u2019s torn bodies.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m afraid I am going to drive them both away. I\u2019m afraid I\u2019m going to wind up alone again, like I was in Snow Globe. I don\u2019t know what I\u2019m doing. I\u2019m just a stupid little girl wearing her mother\u2019s clothes and pretending to be an adult.<br /> <br /> NO. No. I am NOT going to go down this path. I am inexperienced. I see that now, even if I didn\u2019t before. Becky does care about me. She wouldn\u2019t have stayed with me while I was morose over Insincere Marguerite if she didn\u2019t. She wouldn\u2019t have stayed last night if she didn\u2019t. But she\u2019s been hurt before. She\u2019s dealt with what happens when you just dive heedlessly into things. And she doesn\u2019t want to deal with that pain again.<br /> <br /> I have to talk to her. To them both. I have to be honest. I have to admit that I don\u2019t have a clue what I\u2019m doing. But I want this to work. I do love them both. I need them. Becky\u2019s hesitation isn\u2019t a lack of feelings, it\u2019s the experience of knowing that feelings alone aren\u2019t enough. She\u2019s right to want to talk and understand what exactly we\u2019re doing.<br /> <br /> I know I love her. I know I love Gawain. I love them enough to do this right. I love them enough to make this work. I just don\u2019t know how yet. But maybe, if I\u2019m lucky, we can figure it out together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T13:29:05-08:00","id":999402,"title":"","content":"<b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> And the excitement kept coming. Olivia Gold came by to talk to Insincere Marguerite, or at least hand deliver a letter to her. Apparently the letter was a challenge to a duel from Leonidas, the Day King in L.A. Marguerite turned him down and Olivia insulted her, saying she had no honor and calling her names. The insults were from Leonidas and not Olivia. She seemed keen on separating herself from the situation. As it turns out Insincere Marguerite and Leonidas have a history. Apparently Insincere Marguerite filled Leonidas\u2019 house with feces and roaches and in retaliation he dropped a large piece of concrete on her and burned her apartment down. The man seems to hold a serious grudge. So does Insincere Marguerite for that matter. Though I have not seen her do anything of the sort since we formed a motley.<br /> <br /> The show went off without a hitch. Everyone performed well and I think it was received well by the audience. I served drinks as per usual and hung out with Gawain and Luna for a good bit of the night. Though Luna stayed a little bit away from the main part of the bar so she wouldn\u2019t be in anyone\u2019s way if they came up to get a drink. I think she was also trying to keep the number of people around her to a minimum. She doesn\u2019t like crowds so I can appreciate that. Molly came by to talk to me and Gawain about what we have planned for Thanksgiving. So we told her. We\u2019re going to set up a television on the covered balcony with some couches and chairs so people can watch football. We\u2019re also going to set up gaming systems in the entertainment room so people can play games if they want. Not to mention there will be food and drinking and karaoke. Insincere Marguerite has a way to take pretty much any song and set it up so you can sing it for karaoke. I thought that was pretty cool, though I do not plan on singing all that much.<br /> <br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Breakfast started out like usual. Gawain decided this time to make something light for breakfast since he knew we\u2019d all be eating too much later in the day. It was delicious as usual. Then somehow the conversation came up about STD\u2019s and whether or not people in the motley got tested regularly. Becky asked the lot of us pretty much out of the blue. I\u2019m sure it was part of some private conversation that happened earlier, but it was still kinda strange. Everyone assured her that if they had multiple partners they got tested and she appeared to be satisfied.<br /> <br /> After breakfast and a little time had passed Julia, Insincere Marguerite, Lori and De La Rocha all left to go to Julia\u2019s parent\u2019s house for Thanksgiving. I can\u2019t tell you how much I envy her ability to just walk back into her old life like she never left. Well, she had been gone but her parents don\u2019t know that, but she was able to pick up where she left off. Most of us can\u2019t do that. We have to start over from scratch. New names, new place to live, sometimes a new state altogether. Lori was also lucky that she was able to reconnect with her father despite having a fetch and living several states away from where she started. It makes me wonder sometimes if I were to tell my parents who I really am if they would believe me or not. I don\u2019t know. Sometimes it makes me wonder what I would have done with my life if I\u2019d never been taken. Would I have gone to college like my sister? What would I have studied if I did? It's been so long for me that I don\u2019t really remember what my hopes and dreams were when I was a kid. I don\u2019t remember if I had plans for school or what I wanted to be when I grew up. Though I\u2019m fairly certain it wasn\u2019t to become a Knight for a demented winter Fae. <br /> <br /> While Gawain was putting the finishing touches on a couple of dishes I was doing the same for my batch of Kvass. I think it came out pretty good if I do say so myself. As things were getting started out I brought glasses of Kvass to everyone in the motley and explained why I\u2019d made it. They all seemed to like it pretty well, which made me happy. I also made sure to save some for Julia and the others for when they got back from Julia\u2019s parent\u2019s house. <br /> <br /> So, we had a rather large turnout which made Gawain especially happy. He had cooked a lot of food and put a lot of work into all of it, so I think he was glad to have people there to enjoy it all. Right now I don\u2019t remember half the people that showed up, but it was a lot. I do remember that Joan and Andromeda came by, though they had to leave before Lori got back. I think they ended up missing one another by half an hour or so.<br /> <br /> Early on I started out at the bar making drinks for everyone, and some for myself, and Gawain hung out with me for a little bit too. While he was there Felicity came by to talk to him about Leonidas, and assure him that the L.A. monarch is not very happy with Insincere Marguerite, but he is not out to go after the Dream House or the rest of the motley. I was happy to hear that. I really didn\u2019t want him to try and burn down the house just to get back at Marguerite. Felicity also said that she was looking to rent a house for Rowan that was close to the selkie\u2019s work. Felicity apparently feels a responsibility for other Day courtiers in the freehold and takes that responsibility seriously. I thought it was nice of her to offer to rent a place for Rowan to live once she gets out of therapy. I believe that will be within a few days if I remember correctly.<br /> <br /> A couple of hours into the party Jack apparently sent Gawain a text to give him a head \u2018s up that he was about to show up in his turkey costume. When he arrived he ate as much as he could before Gawain came out in his chef outfit. He then proceeded to chase the turkey around the room. Julia and the others came back when the celebration was in full swing, and Jack and Gawain were going all out. I gave all four ladies some of the Kvass that I\u2019d saved for them so they could drink and watch the shenanigans. It was amusing to watch; I\u2019ll give them that. The ladies also seemed to like the Kvass so that was good. A little while later Marguerite left to go set up the karaoke machine. Pretty soon the lights were dimmed and Jack got up on the stage to sing \u201cEvery rose has its thorn.\u201d He invited Gawain up on the stage to do a duet. Together the two of them sang. It was fun.<br /> <br /> After that things kind of blur together. I had a good amount to drink over the course of the night and got roped into singing a number of songs. I remember singing \u201cThe Stranger\u201d by Billy Joel. I think I did \u201cThe Stranger\u201d later in the evening too, but did the second rendition in Russian. I always liked that song when I was growing up and now it has a different meaning for me. I used to routinely wear the face of a stranger when I worked for the Lady. I did more than just try it on. I would become that stranger for days or weeks. However long it took for me to accomplish what I had set out to do. Whether that was lure someone back to Arcadia or return someone who\u2019d escaped. I will admit that I did more of the later, but I did bring a fair number of people to my the Lady. Usually the Lady had her eye on a particular prize, but sometimes she let me use my discretion and pick someone myself. I knew that I had the favor of the Lady when she let me choose who to bring back for the first time. <br /> <br /> The first person I ever choose to bring to the Lady was a young man by the name of Chris Nackowski. He was hiking in the same mountains that I used to as a child, though I didn\u2019t remember that at the time. It was autumn and the leaves were almost all on the ground, and there was a chill in the air. The weather felt like a warm balmy day to me. I decided to take a walk and just found him hiking along the trails alone. I pretended to be lost and he stopped to help me. I told him a story about how I\u2019d been hiking in a cave not far from where we were and I tripped and lost my camera. I was certain I could find it if I had help. He was a nice guy so he agreed to help me find my camera and help me get down to the base of the mountain again. So I led him to a cave and led him deep within until there was a crevice. I told him that my camera had fallen in there but couldn\u2019t reach it myself. He offered to get it if I could lower him down and pull him back up. So I did. Well, I lowered him down anyway. I will give him credit, he did look for that lost camera for a while before he called back up to say that he couldn\u2019t find it. He asked me to pull him back up and I just smiled and said \u201cNo.\u201d I told him that there was another way out, he just needed to follow the path. He was more than a little angry with me, so I decided that I\u2019d let him walk to rest of the way himself and I\u2019d follow by an alternate route. I met up with him some hours later and he was still mad. He grabbed me by the throat and shoved me against a tree. I smiled. He tried to be threatening, but I just grabbed him by the wrist and started to freeze his arm. He let go quickly. I then straightened up and explained to him that if he wanted to live he would follow me. Otherwise I would leave him to freeze in the woods. He elected to follow me, and I led him straight to the Lady. She was pleased.<br /> <br /> I wonder sometimes what happened to Chris. He did not become one of the Lady\u2019s treasures, nor did he become a Knight. The Lady had several other servants in the castle, I think I assumed that he filled one of those positions, though I never did ask. I was not concerned with his fate after I had led him to my the Lady. That was my only interest in him and once I\u2019d completed my task he fled my mind. For all I know the Lady just used him as a test for me and killed him as soon as he was out of sight. As a test though I suppose it worked. I was pleased with myself for making the Lady happy. She lauded me to the other Knights, and even Rook was satisfied with my work. Sometimes it seemed that he was harder to please than the Lady. I thought it was all worth it at the time though. Me and my masks. I was so proud.<br /> <br /> Anyway\u2026There was much singing by everyone. Lori performed \u201cUnder Pressure\u201d early on as well as several other songs as the night wore on. I think she was having fun watching the other people up on the stage performing for a change. De La Rocha sang \u201cKilling in the Name of,\u201d which was pretty cool. I didn\u2019t know she could sing so well. Gawain sang something by Nirvana early on. I think he really likes that band. I believe it\u2019s one of the few things he does remember from his life before Arcadia. Later Gawain got me, Jack, Sandoval, Davie and himself to sing \u201cTitle of this song.\u201d It was pretty funny. I don\u2019t remember having heard it before, but it was hilarious to sing. There was much giggling by us and the audience as we sang that one. Gawain also sang \u201cEverything I do I do for you,\u201d for Calamity. She got all teary eyed after that, though she was quick to wipe the tears away from her face. I sang something for Luna, though I will admit I don\u2019t remember what I sang. It\u2019s all blurring together in my mind. I\u2019ve definitely had too much to drink.<br /> <br /> There was also some conversation going on between Dahlia and Calamity about trying to get Dahlia up on the stage but she thought she\u2019d be humiliated up there like the girl from the movie \u201cCarrie.\u201d This led to a whole conversation about pouring blood over Dahlia\u2019s head before she \u2018goes crazy,\u201d and what would happen. Unfortunately, Mary, who I haven\u2019t seen since the incident with her fetch, was walking nearby at that time. She went more than a little pale at what was being said and I suggested that they change the subject. Lori followed Mary, who had walked away, to make sure that she was okay. I am not certain what was said, but Mary stayed for the rest of the night, so I\u2019m assuming that she was not upset enough to leave. Lori is good that way. She can make people feel better just by talking to them, and people just like to open up to her. She has a good way with people. I think that if she sticks with her studies she\u2019ll make a great doctor or nurse someday. And now it is entirely too late, or early as the case may be, and I am drunk and tired. I am going to sleep. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> This afternoon was exciting! Leonidas challenged me to a duel.<br /> <br /> Olivia Gold, the smug Flamesiren, arrived with a gold envelope from Leonidas. He evidently challenged me to a duel over Felicity. I told her I was ignoring it, and she gave me scripted remarks about how I lack honor or virtue. Thank goodness Maria was not there. Entertaining as Olivia having a beatdown would have been, it would also have been\u2026problematic. Definitely.<br /> <br /> The others were informed. Gawain apparently asked Julia if I needed a second. His heart is in the right place. When I told Juliette, she found a way to needle herself about her intellect. I protested, and I meant it. Juliette is very intelligent. I hate hearing her disparaged. Even by herself. Sadly.<br /> <br /> Felicity actually came this evening. I sat in her lap and we talked, while Maria fondled Julia perhaps a bit more publicly than usual. Had to do with seeing her parents tomorrow, I am sure. Juliette came down to advise me she was going to \u201cshow her teeth\u201d though I am unsure as to whom. She sang defiantly about not being owned. I appreciated her telling me it was not personal.<br /> <br /> We made love after, the family. Julia was the guest of honor. The bonds between us are marvelous. I can but reflect on how happy I am. As long as Julia, Juliette and Maria are with I, I can face anything.<br /> <br /> -o - -o- -o- -o-<br /> <br /> <br /> Thanksgiving went well.<br /> <br /> Breakfast was light, and there was a great deal of fondness from the family. We got dressed, with Juliette and Julia dressed up sweetly, and Maria in a purple suit and shirt. Yum. I added my black and orange leggings to my ensemble and off we went. John and Linda were very nice, and clearly took well to Juliette and Maria. It was funny; Linda invited Juliette and Julia to help in the kitchen, while John spoke to Maria and I. <br /> <br /> That did not last too long, as Julia discovered her grandmother was less approving of us than she thought. Her grandmother had begged off, and apparently was not sick last time we went to Anaheim. She flew into a tearful rage, and Linda asked me to help her. After a bit I managed to get her under control and back in the family room, though she was clearly deeply disappointed. Her mom spoke briefly to her after she came back in, which helped in the immediate.<br /> <br /> Dinner went well. John and Linda happily embarrassed Julia quite a bit, pointing out Juliette\u2019s resemblance to some of Julia\u2019s art subjects. I was asked about France and there was something about Maria having been in a gang. John and Maria got on well. They had some general, non probing questions about our relationship, and seemed pleased\u2026also, apparently they were both involved with a man when Julia was much younger, which came as a shock to her, though it did not to me.<br /> <br /> When we returned, the Dream House was full. I helped Captain Jack pull off his\u2026dramatic\u2026rendition of \u201cEvery Rose has it\u2019s Thorn\u201d while I was explaining the Karaoke system. Calamity had a thing about playing excessively boy American songs. Boys playing at being men. Maria countered with Rage Against the Machine \u201cKilling in the Name\u201d which seemed pretty awesome, honestly. Juliette sang with her a duet from a musical. <i><i>Grease</i></i><i>,</i> I think.<br /> <br /> I sang \u201cEnded with the Night\u201d by Caravan Palace and Julia talked me into \u201cNe Me Quitte Pas\u201d by Regina Spektor. They went over pretty well.<br /> <br /> Felicity showed again, she seems intent on keeping my attention to herself. With the tension with Leonidas, I don\u2019t blame her. And with Desiree out of the house, she feels better about it.<br /> <br /> Juliette was drunk before evening\u2019s end, so Maria took her upstairs. I confess I was tempted by Felicity\u2019s charms, but after the time with her parents Julia wanted time with I. So I went up with her. We had a lovely, loving night.<br /> <br /> Tomorrow Juliette and Maria will go to Thanksgiving lunch with Juliette\u2019s dad. Then, at last, the Christmas decorations will finally come out. I can\u2019t wait!<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXVIII</i><br /> <br /> So Thanksgiving went well. Funny, it being Thanksgiving season in the United States at the time of this writing in real life as well.<br /> <br /> If you usually skip Calamity, there is a whole mess of drama not covered elsewhere.<br /> <br /> It was a good session and I don\u2019t have much to add. Julia had murdered her Fetch by luring her to a well with a letter then tossing her in it, then feigning a car accident to return to her parents. Calamity is the murder happy member of the Motley, but Julia Oldacre is a cold-blooded killer when the situation calls for it. Most don\u2019t realize or acknowledge it; she seems to have no urge to kill so Insincere Marguerite is not too troubled.<br /> <br /> See you next time, but Comments and Questions are welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T14:09:17-08:00","id":999420,"title":"","content":"Feel free to disagree with me, but I kinda sighed and face-palmed when Lori didn't let Rowan take Felicity up on her offer. As tv tropes says, the courts are as much support groups as they are political institutions. Nothing wrong with letting her support group take care of her. She gets support while you get some time to plan what you want to do about your relationship with her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T14:26:27-08:00","id":999434,"title":"","content":"True, but Lori has time to decide. As GM, I anticipate Rowan living in a place Felicity arranges for her...she plans to talk to Lori about that too. But if she doesn't, and I am well fine with that, too. Goodness knows I don't know what is going to happen. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T14:34:12-08:00","id":1005859,"title":"","content":"As the day of Insincere Marguerite\u2019s case being put to Paris draws near, she is faced with the last person she wanted to see now. On the brighter side, Christmas decorating begins, Lori has dinner with her dad, Calamity has an important relationship conversation and Julia makes a discovery.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LXIX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> This entry might be a little disjointed, as I\u2019m sort of nervous-writing at the moment; trying to fill the empty minutes with something constructive as I wait for things to develop. We\u2019re in the Autumn Court\u2019s lighthouse library, talking to\u2026 but I\u2019m getting ahead of myself.<br /> <br /> I was startled out of a reverie yesterday morning \u2013 the day after Thanksgiving \u2013 to the sound of three miniature sonic booms echoing through my aching head. When the phenomenon was repeated, I realized that someone was knocking on my bedroom door. I glanced at the clock and realized it wasn\u2019t even 8:00 yet. D muttered something suitably angry from where she was sprawled on our bed and tossed a pillow at the door. I eventually gave in and walked across the room to see what the hell was going on.<br /> <br /> Calamity was there, looking tense and nervous. \u201cI need to talk to the motley. It\u2019s important,\u201d she said.<br /> <br /> That woke me up a bit. \u201cIs anyone hurt? Who needs healing?\u201d I asked urgently.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo,\u201d she assured me. \u201cNo one\u2019s hurt. It\u2019s just\u2026 we need to talk. Something\u2019s happened.\u201d<br /> <br /> D groaned. \u201cCould you make that any more mysterious, Calamity?\u201d she asked in acid tones.<br /> <br /> Calamity did not relent, and so the two of us threw on some sweats and t-shirts (I grabbed a pair of sunglasses on my way out of the room) and headed down to the kitchen. Everyone was there except Julia and Marguerite, which made sense a few minutes later. <br /> <br /> Calamity told us all that she had caught sight of an intruder as she was coming back from her Tai Chi lesson\u2026 a changeling she\u2019d never seen before. This young woman bolted when she realized she\u2019d been spotted, and Calamity followed her into the backstage area, where the intruder promptly vanished into a mirror. Calamity woke Marguerite and asked her to look into the matter, and Marguerite used her contracts to see what the mirrors had seen\u2026 and then she retreated into the vents.<br /> <br /> Yvette. The mysterious changeling woman was Yvette. This is the last thing Marguerite needs right now.<br /> <br /> Marguerite herself joined us not long after. She was obviously a bit shaken, but she seemed to be handling it well overall. We discussed a few possible reasons Yvette might have to spy on us here (she could be trying to kill Marguerite, she could be trying to return to her keeping, or she could be gathering data for the Paris Courts regarding Marguerite\u2019s current lifestyle), but in the end there wasn\u2019t much we could do about it one way or another. Marguerite went upstairs to soothe Julia and to reassure her that she had no true rival for Marguerite\u2019s affections, and Julia seemed a bit happier after that.<br /> <br /> There didn\u2019t seem to be much point in going back to sleep after that, so I used Spring contracts to pep myself up (along with D and Calamity, who had also opted to stay up rather than heading back to sleep). Jacob and Luna decided to brave the Black Friday crowds and go shopping for some security cameras so that we won\u2019t be blindsided by another intruder in the future. We\u2019ll have to be careful how we use them, however, since we\u2019ll likely have to place them in the changing areas. We\u2019ll need to be very open with our performers about their presence, and I\u2019ll probably have to be the one to review and delete the footage on a pretty much daily basis, since I\u2019m generally in the changing room with the performers anyway. Luna has offered to take up the slack as well, since she\u2019s pretty much the only person currently residing at the Dream House who is not sexually attracted to women. So that\u2019s nice.<br /> <br /> D and I got showered and dressed and basically ready to head over to dad\u2019s place for the afternoon. D didn\u2019t wear the suit this time, but she still dressed in nice, non-torn clothing, which was a nice gesture on her part. I know how much she treasures her punk threads.<br /> <br /> As we were driving over there, D started to open up to me about a part of her life she doesn\u2019t often discuss. Of course, she started out with a cocky joke, but I could tell that she was trying to talk about something she wasn\u2019t comfortable with.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo I probably shouldn\u2019t talk to your dad about the time I spent with a gang, like I did with Julia\u2019s dad, huh?\u201d she asked with a smirk.<br /> <br /> I put my hand on hers. \u201cYou can talk about anything you want with him, Maria,\u201d I said seriously. \u201cYou\u2019re the love of my life and you\u2019re not going away. I want him to get to know who you really are.\u201d<br /> <br /> She kept her eyes downcast. \u201cIt\u2019s not something I\u2019m proud of, honestly,\u201d she said after a bit. \u201cI was a Latina rebelling against my family\u2026 there weren\u2019t many options on the street for me. I got out pretty quickly once I realized that the highest rank I could expect to attain was \u2018Boss\u2019s Girlfriend.\u2019 I never made much of a name for myself; it\u2019s not like I was the terror of the streets or anything.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled. \u201cNot like now, huh?\u201d I asked with a wink.<br /> <br /> She laughed at that. \u201cYeah, I have a few advantages now I didn\u2019t have back then.\u201d<br /> <br /> Due to the early-morning motley meeting, we were actually a little early getting to dad\u2019s place, though he didn\u2019t seem to mind. For the most part, it was a very pleasant afternoon. The three of us talked quite a bit about our lives, and I\u2019m sure dad learned a lot about changeling culture. He asked about our somewhat unusual names first, which led to a discussion about how changelings often try to reinvent themselves after escaping Arcadia. I didn\u2019t tell him the story of how I chose my own moniker, but we did share the joke behind Calamity\u2019s name.<br /> <br /> This brought us to a somewhat disturbing topic of discussion. Apparently, my fetch has reached out and tried to reconnect with dad. She sent him a letter after nearly twenty years of silence. He let me read it. She didn\u2019t really acknowledge the rift that had grown between them, but she expressed a desire to know how he was doing. The letter was postmarked the day after I revealed myself to him.<br /> <br /> This <u>can\u2019t</u> be a coincidence. She must have sensed that I had re-entered my father\u2019s life somehow and reacted in the only way she knew how. There\u2019s no reason to panic just yet; not all fetches are like Mary\u2019s. Becky apparently has a pretty good relationship with her fetch. Luna had several cordial meetings with hers, though they\u2019ve sort of broken that off lately. So even if the woman currently calling herself Juliette Wells decides to drop by for a visit, there\u2019s not necessarily anything to worry about.<br /> <br /> Dad\u2019s going to answer the letter. He says he feels obligated to do so, and I can certainly understand that. He\u2019s not going to mention me, or changelings, or anything he\u2019s learned about her true nature when he writes to her. Hopefully that will be the end of this. I don\u2019t want this to be a big deal. I honestly bear my fetch no ill will, and I\u2019m perfectly content to let her live the life she\u2019s made for herself. I just hope she\u2019ll allow me the same courtesy.<br /> <br /> We were wrapping things up and preparing to take our leave when I decided I couldn\u2019t put it off any longer. \u201cDad?\u201d I said softly as we were about to head for the door.<br /> <br /> \u201cYes?\u201d he asked, then he took in my expression. \u201cWhat is it, Juliette?\u201d he said more seriously.<br /> <br /> I took a deep breath. \u201cI\u2019ve dropped a lot of really heavy revelations on you over the past six months, I know. I told you I was gay. I told you I\u2019m a changeling. I told you I\u2019m your daughter. You\u2019ve handled all of these bombshells better than I had any right to hope you would. I hope you know how much I appreciate that.\u201d<br /> <br /> He smiled indulgently. \u201cI realized long ago that there were two paths before me: wisdom and acceptance, or bitterness and judgment. This path has seemed better to me overall.\u201d<br /> <br /> I took his offered hand. \u201cI agree,\u201d I said, \u201cand that\u2019s why I have one more thing to tell you. One more secret about my life. You might not like it, but you\u2019ve more than earned my trust, and you deserve the whole truth from me.\u201d<br /> <br /> Dad nodded and squeezed my hand in his still remarkably firm grip. \u201cI\u2019m listening,\u201d he said softly. D took my other hand.<br /> <br /> I took a deep breath before I started. \u201cMaria and I are in love,\u201d I said simply. \u201cI honestly believe that she is my soulmate; the one person in this world that I was meant to find. I want you to understand that, because nothing is ever going to change it. But\u2026 but the two of us are still young, and we\u2019re not ready to settle down yet. We have\u2026 we have what they call an \u2018open relationship\u2019 these days.\u201d<br /> <br /> Dad pursed his lips, but nodded again.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou met most of our closest friends when you came by the Dream House,\u201d I went on, \u201cincluding Insincere Marguerite and Julia. And you might have noticed that there was some\u2026 affection between the four of us.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI did,\u201d Dad confirmed. \u201cMiss Marguerite was better at concealing it, but Miss Julia\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> D chuckled. \u201cYeah, Julia doesn\u2019t keep things bottled up,\u201d she agreed. \u201cWe always know when she\u2019s mad about something.\u201d<br /> <br /> Dad sighed. \u201cSo this is something you both agree to?\u201d he asked after a moment. \u201cIt\u2019s a consenting arrangement?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes,\u201d I said, and D nodded her agreement. \u201cI love them both, and so does Maria. And they love us. We\u2019re not as close to them as we are to each other, and they\u2019d almost certainly say the same thing, but\u2026\u201d I trailed off vaguely.<br /> <br /> Dad sighed. \u201cI don\u2019t claim to understand this sort of relationship,\u201d he said slowly, still holding my hand, \u201cand it goes against the way I was raised. But you are my daughter, Juliette, and I love you\u2026 and I can see that you\u2019re not doing any harm to anyone by living this way. You are doing what you do out of love, and you are bringing a bit more joy and light into the world. While I may not agree with this lifestyle\u2026 I do accept it. And I don\u2019t feel that it\u2019s my place to tell you that it is wrong.\u201d<br /> <br /> I pulled him into an embrace, and once more felt the tears running down my cheeks. I sure have cried a lot lately, haven\u2019t I? \u201cThank you, dad,\u201d I said fervently as he carefully laced his fingers together under my wings and returned the hug. \u201cYour acceptance means so much to me, and it\u2019ll mean a lot to Marguerite and Julia to know that they don\u2019t have to hide our relationship anymore.\u201d<br /> <br /> He smiled as we disengaged. \u201cNow,\u201d he said as we were about to part, \u201cthere is one more matter I\u2019d like to discuss. It occurs to me that I should know a bit more about the work you do. I was thinking that I could drop by the Dream House some evening to see the show. Perhaps you could let me know when you\u2019re performing something a bit less\u2026\u201d he twirled his fingers idly for an uncomfortable moment, \u201c\u2026lascivious?\u201d<br /> <br /> I laughed out loud at that. \u201cI\u2019ll check the schedule and give you a call,\u201d I promised. \u201cI\u2019d love for you to see one of our shows!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cExcellent,\u201d he said. \u201cI shall await your call, then. Goodbye, ladies. Thank you for taking the time to visit an old man during this busy holiday season.\u201d He gave me a hug, and then gave <u>D</u> a hug, and then saw us out the door.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell,\u201d I said as we drove back home, \u201cthat went better than I expected. I guess I should give my dad more credit. He really has changed.\u201d<br /> <br /> D nodded. \u201cHe\u2019s a good guy,\u201d she agreed. \u201cI\u2019m sure you picked up on the fact that he probably thinks we\u2019re in an <u>exclusive</u> polyamorous relationship with Julia and Mags, right? I mean, he didn\u2019t seem real wild about it when you first told him that we have an open relationship\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah,\u201d I sighed, \u201cbut it\u2019s enough. I don\u2019t have to hide the most important people in my life from him anymore. He may not know about Oleander, but how often are the two of them going to interact anyway? And as for my more\u2026 \u2018casual\u2019 encounters, well\u2026 I shouldn\u2019t have to tell my dad <u>everything</u> about my life, right? I mean, everybody deserves a little privacy.\u201d<br /> <br /> D leaned over and kissed my cheek. \u201cDamn right,\u201d she agreed. She was quiet for a minute before she added \u201cI\u2019m really glad you did this, Jules. It\u2019ll make Mags and Julia really happy.\u201d<br /> <br /> Things already seemed pretty cheerful when we got back to the Dream House. The motley \u2013 at Marguerite\u2019s insistence \u2013 had begun setting up the Christmas decorations. Gawain carried heavy things around while Marguerite and Calamity scurried around on the walls and ceilings hanging tinsel and garlands. Jacob took care of things nearer to the ground, while Julia sat back with a look of faux-disgust on her face, obviously reveling in her lover\u2019s happiness.<br /> <br /> Marguerite had a Santa hat on. I found another one amidst the boxes of decorations, pinned a sprig of mistletoe to the bobble at its tip, and placed it elegantly on my own head. People took the hint immediately, and I received more than my fair share of kisses over the next few hours. <br /> <br /> I told Marguerite and Julia pretty much immediately that they no longer had to hide their feelings in front of my father, and apologized once again for not opening up to him sooner about our relationship. They were both very happy with this development, and Julia\u2019s face broke into such a guileless, genuine smile that I just had to embrace her.<br /> <br /> Calamity also let us know that Felicity had been by earlier in the day for an unexpected reason. It turns out that she had been very impressed by the motley\u2019s desire to give something back to the Freehold on Thanksgiving, and she wanted to do her part to contribute to the good work. Consequently, she wrote Calamity a fairly substantial check to help cover the expenses of the Thanksgiving party. We all agreed that this was exceptionally kind of her, since none of us had expected any sort of compensation whatsoever.<br /> <br /> When the lion\u2019s share of the decorating had been completed, Marguerite asked if she could speak with me, D, and Julia privately, and of course we agreed. \u201cMy loves,\u201d she began, \u201cI have been meaning to speak with you about something for some time now, but things kept coming up. I\u2026 do not like the person I used to be. Marguerite DeLisle was not a good person. That is why I insist that people call me Insincere Marguerite, because I want to be someone different now.\u201d<br /> <br /> I thought about saying something at this point, but it was obvious that she had more she wanted to convey.<br /> <br /> \u201cI have come to realize,\u201d she continued after a bit, \u201cthat you three only know the new Marguerite, the <u>better</u> Marguerite. That is what \u2018Marguerite\u2019 means to you, and you love that Marguerite. Therefore, while I must still be \u2018Insincere Marguerite\u2019 when others are present\u2026 you three may call me \u2018Marguerite\u2019 in private if you like.\u201d<br /> <br /> There was a lot of kissing after that, in all directions, and everyone expressed their gratitude at Marguerite\u2019s acceptance. D might have said something about how Marguerite will always be Mags to her, but she meant it lovingly, I\u2019m sure.<br /> <br /> While we were all together, I decided to share my thoughts \u2013 and my misgivings \u2013 on Charlotte\u2019s assertion that I could take up the mantle of Spring Queen. I got a lot more of the same opinions I\u2019d heard from D and Jolie\u2026 \u2018of course you could do it, and I\u2019ll support you, but\u2026\u2019 I had to state several times that I don\u2019t actually <u>want</u> the job, but that I\u2019d be willing to take it if it seemed like it would help Jolie and the Freehold. And I also made sure they all understood that I couldn\u2019t even consider the position until we\u2019d done something about Missy and Jane\u2019s captivity.<br /> <br /> And the revelations didn\u2019t stop there! As we knew from our dinner with her family the previous afternoon, she had recently discovered that her parents had also enjoyed a polyamorous relationship in their younger days; they had both been involved with another man when Julia was younger. And a little before she came along, too. That bit\u2019s important.<br /> <br /> Well, Julia decided to look this gentleman up on the internet, and discovered that he is currently a professional illustrator. Now, neither of the people that Julia recognizes as her parents has ever displayed any artistic inclinations\u2026 I\u2019m sure you see where this is going.<br /> <br /> So poor Julia was in a tizzy, wondering what she should do about the whole situation. She wanted advice about whether or not she should approach the gentleman in question online and try to forge some sort of a connection with him. How would he react? How would the rest of her family react? Is this something she should even contemplate? And so on. We soothed her as best we could, of course. I advised her to ask her parents \u2013 and they <u>are</u> still her parents, and will <u>always</u> be her parents, regardless of the facts of biology \u2013 what they thought of the situation. From what I\u2019ve seen, they\u2019re very open and accepting people, and as long as Julia makes it clear that this doesn\u2019t change her feelings toward them, I think they\u2019ll be happy to advise her. She accepted that as good advice, but still hasn\u2019t come to a decision regarding whether she should contact the gentleman himself.<br /> <br /> It was nice not to have to worry about wrangling performers for a show last night. We all just sort of\u2026 hung out and enjoyed each other\u2019s company. There was no structured movie night, no crisis to attend to, and nothing dire hanging over our heads (aside from the twin worries of Marguerite\u2019s hearing the following day and Marguerite\u2019s\u2026 <u>issues</u> with Desiree), we just sat around and talked and joked and generally had a good time. It was nice. It was like having a real family again\u2026 like I used to feel back in Defiance before mom died.<br /> <br /> We got up this morning a little earlier than usual \u2013 though not as early as yesterday, and <u>thanks</u> again for that Calamity \u2013 and began preparing to speak with Night Queen Skitters, from the Paris Freehold. I think we all assumed that we were going to skype the conversation, but much to our surprise, a little after breakfast, Queen Charlotte called Marguerite and told her that Skitters had arrived in the Freehold personally, and wanted to speak with us directly at the lighthouse at our earliest convenience.<br /> <br /> Well, this required a bit of preparation, of course. Meeting royalty in person is a little more formal than talking with them on a small computer screen. I ran upstairs and put on a nice skirt and button-up shirt, but I left my hair down and didn\u2019t put on my church glasses. Most of the others dressed up relatively nicely, though not ostentatiously. D, God bless her, wore her usual punk threads.<br /> <br /> We rode over to the Lighthouse together in Gawain\u2019s van, and when we arrived we were ushered into the stacks to meet our visiting royalty. We weren\u2019t the only ones there to speak on Marguerite\u2019s behalf, either. Princess Jolie was there, and the two of us passed a few pleasant words before I gave my testimony. Other witnesses included Felicity, Flores, Dark Kimberly, Sandoval, White Maria, Gloria, Moon, Dionysia, and Willow Black. Desiree was notable by her absence, of course, but that was by design. The fact that so many local changelings came to lend Marguerite their support can only be good for her case, right? <br /> <br /> Night Queen Skitters (she\u2019s actually the Autumn Court monarch in Paris, but styles herself \u201cNight Queen\u201d because the diurnal courts don\u2019t have much of a presence there) is an\u2026 intense individual. She was never less than cordial to us, though her mannerisms were a bit disconcerting to say the least. Her fingernails were long and knife-like, and she seemed to have an unhealthy obsession with other people\u2019s faces. Like, it was implied that she <u>collects</u> them. When she saw that Gawain\u2019s mien didn\u2019t [u]have/[u] a face, she took pity on him, and asked if he would like to have one of <u>hers</u>. So that\u2019s something, I guess.<br /> <br /> In any case, she wanted to speak with all of us individually, so Queen Charlotte granted her the use of a private room for the duration of her stay. I wasn\u2019t the first to speak with her, but I was near the beginning of the line. I did my best to speak as honestly and passionately as I could about my lover, channeling a bit of glamour into my words to give them a little more oomph, but stopping short of actually using Contracts to sway the Night Queen\u2019s opinion. While I love Marguerite, and would go to any lengths to save her, manipulating the emotions and opinions of others with magic spells always seemed rude to me. And besides, as I said when I wrote about Joan\u2019s trial a few months back, it would be tantamount to admitting that I couldn\u2019t adequately defend my lover without resorting to magic.<br /> <br /> She asked about my relationship with Marguerite, and specifically about any attempts Marguerite may have made to control or manipulate my thoughts and actions. As I said, I answered honestly, admitting that Marguerite has a domineering side, but that when I pushed back against her early attempts to control me, she accepted that resistance and we eventually got past it. Skitters opined that perhaps Marguerite\u2019s need for control was purely romantic or sexual these days, and I didn\u2019t dissuade her from that opinion, noting that several of Marguerite\u2019s other lovers enjoy being dominated and are more than willing to consent to her control in the bedroom.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd does this control extend beyond their sexual encounters?\u201d she asked, fixing me with a piercing stare.<br /> <br /> I smiled. \u201cIt varies from person to person. Some of her lovers are naturally submissive, and enjoy having someone to look after them. But that\u2019s <u>their choice</u>, not hers. Others are submissive in bed but <u>fiercely</u> independent in the rest of their lives.\u201d I smiled as I thought about the love of my life, and how hard she works to prove her independence from everyone, myself included.<br /> <br /> In the end, I think I was passionate and persuasive enough to get my point across. The Night Queen thanked me for my time and my willingness to speak frankly with her, and asked if I would be kind enough to send the next witness in. I agreed, and a moment later I was \u201ctagging out\u201d with Calamity. I\u2019ve been sitting here ever since, at one of the study tables in the library, writing in this diary and chatting occasionally with Night Queen Skitters\u2019 bodyguard, a very small green Wizened woman named Lizette. Lizette apparently has a \u201ctrod,\u201d or a personal passage through the Hedge, which links Paris with Southern California. I guess that explains how they arrived so quickly (and unexpectedly) today.<br /> <br /> Lizette seems nice enough, though I assume she has hidden depths if the current reigning monarch of Paris entrusts her with her care and safety. Before the individual interviews began, we spoke with both Skitters and Lizette about Yvette. Both of them professed ignorance of Yvette\u2019s activities within the Freehold. Lizette went so far as to say that Yvette no longer lived in the Paris Freehold, and that she had broken off contact with them some time ago. For what it\u2019s worth, I believe her, though that does complicate our current situation.<br /> <br /> In any case, it\u2019s high time I put this journal away and stopped fretting about curious fetches, intrusive former lovers, the \u201cissue\u201d with Desiree, and the various and sundry other worrying facets of our lives. With any luck, at least one of Marguerite\u2019s long-standing problems will be solved within the next few hours, and that\u2019s worth celebrating.<br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei Grace</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> Saturday, November 28th <br /> Nine years, six months, twenty-three days<br /> Days without stabbing: 4<br /> <br /> I am a restless little monster. Sitting here in in the Lighthouse Library while Nightqueen Skitters interviews the rest of the motley and the witnesses we\u2019ve brought in one by one. My Darkling Sister\u2019s fate rests in her long and wickedly sharp fingers. She is certainly an interesting woman, I believe the others found her a bit disconcertingly creepy but I don\u2019t believe that she\u2019d be the monarch if she wasn\u2019t shrewd enough underneath that. Of course, maybe I am just biased because she\u2019s a razorhand like myself. At any rate, she has at least presented herself as being open to hearing us all out and giving Insincere Marguerite\u2019s case a fair consideration. I think I made my arguments fairly well and as a fellow darkling the weight of my trust in Insincere Marguerite was not lost on her. Unfortunately, now that just leaves the waiting. I do not idle well.<br /> <br /> I need to stop eying her bodyguard\u2019s weapons. She\u2019s a petite thing but there is a hardened edge to her. While the pair of crossed chainsaws she\u2019s wearing are undoubtedly meant to be intimidating I am quite sure she can actually use them to devastating effect if it\u2019s called for. The thought of fighting someone armed with such a terrifying weapon is\u2026 invigorating. Maybe after this is settled I can ask her to dance. Apparently she\u2019s got a trod between Paris and California. But she seems to have noticed my attention and I fear she may have the wrong idea about my intent. I mean, not that she isn\u2019t pretty but my love life is already complicated right now and trying to seduce one of the people investigating my motley mate would look quite suspect. Eyes on your own paper Calamity. <br /> <br /> Yeah\u2026 my love life. The talking yesterday was good. Becky made it clear she\u2019s not going to come between Gawain and I. She\u2019s a succubus and she\u2019s been the demise of a few relationships that way before and she\u2019s determined not to do so again. Then Gawain and I talked later and on the one hand, it was a little reassuring to find that he doesn\u2019t exactly have all the answers either but on the other I am fucking terrified of screwing this up and I would kill for a damn manual to read. Okay, to be honest, I\u2019d also kill for a sandwich right about now too, but seriously I wish I just had a clue about how to not fuck this up. And I know part of this is that I\u2019m broken and I\u2019m afraid of being alone and I\u2019m pretty sure I\u2019d be willing to agree to just about anything to not lose them and I know that\u2019s not healthy and not what they want and is only going to be a problem in the future but I can\u2019t fucking help myself. I just like this is way too important to be in my completely clueless hands. <br /> <br /> Stop. I am not clueless. I may not understand how to address these things but I know they are there. I know I have issues. I know Becky and Gawain have issues. I know we have to address them to make this work. I am not blind. I also know that I don\u2019t have the answers. So what I need to do is find them. Lori and Insincere Marguerite and Julia and DLR make this poly thing work. I should talk to them about this. Hmm\u2026 Julia\u2019s a bit intense. DLR and I aren\u2019t really that close. Things are better with Insincere Marguerite and I but with everything else right now I\u2019m a little leery of burdening her with this. I\u2019ll try talking to Lori first. Maybe she can give me some advice about how to not fuck this up. <br /> <br /> This isn\u2019t the time or place for it though. And we\u2019ve got the show tonight. Fuck I need to get my head straight for that. I mean, it\u2019s not like I haven\u2019t promised everyone that it\u2019s going to be amazing or anything. Of course, it is going to be fucking amazing. We\u2019ve worked it out. The song is perfect. Lori and I are going to own it tonight. Heh, maybe the Nightqueen and Lizette will come out. As nerve-wracking as the timing of this is with the show, it would be worth it to have them see us on a night when we\u2019re really going all out like this. <br /> <br /> Okay, she definitely noticed me staring that time. Maybe I should talk to her. Of course, complimenting her chainsaws and asking about them would probably come across like some sort of pick up line. Better to just focus on other things.<br /> <br /> Like Yvette. Fuck but I don\u2019t know what the hell we\u2019re going to do about her. Catching her sneaking into the Dream House via mirror yesterday can\u2019t be a coincidence. Nightqueen Skitters and Lizette confirmed that they reached out to try to talk to her about this but said she\u2019d not answered and isn\u2019t in Paris anymore. But I don\u2019t buy into coincidence. I\u2019m sure it was this effort that cued her into where her former Keeper lives now. But the question that matters is what she wants. It could be that she\u2019s afraid that Insincere Marguerite is going to return to Paris and come looking for her. Maybe she just wants to know if she\u2019s changed. Of course, I can\u2019t ignore the possibility that she\u2019s after something less innocent. If some part of her wants to return or worse, if she\u2019s reacting to that the way I would and seeking to kill Insincere Marguerite to avoid giving into that impulse. Even if she doesn\u2019t mean my Darkling Sister harm, her presence is likely not good right now, not with Julia\u2019s insecurity and Desiree. <br /> <br /> Gawain and I need to get to work with her. I\u2019ve been too caught up in this relationship triangle with Becky. I need to settle that but healing Desiree\u2019s emotional damage enough to end the pact between her and Insincere Marguerite can\u2019t wait. <br /> <br /> Breathe. Focus. Luna\u2019s most likely right that after coming close to being caught Yvette is not likely to return for a while and we\u2019ve got the cameras in place to spot her if she does. We know she\u2019s not acting on behalf of the Paris court or with their knowledge. I guess at this point we need to try to find some way to contact her. <br /> <br /> Gawain and I are both talented Oneiromancers and we make a hell of a team. Desiree trusts and cares for Gawain and he cares for her. That\u2019s a huge plus in this sort of thing, we can start from a place of trust rather than have to build one. I\u2019m no expert, but I do have at least some understanding of the therapeutic process after being in it myself. Honestly, we have the best chance of succeeding in helping her.<br /> <br /> Whatever Nightqueen Skitters does decide, we will deal with it. We have a lot of Changelings here to speak in her favor. The simple truth is that she isn\u2019t the person she was in Arcadia anymore. I\u2019m hopeful but no matter what, I will stand with my sister and if it comes to it I will fall with her. I\u2019ve done everything I can. Now I can only wait and see what happens. <br /> <br /> I hate waiting. <br /> <br /> <b><br /> Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Well, we had another interesting start to the day. Calamity got most of us up early to have an impromptu motley meeting. Once she explained what was going on I forgave her for getting us up so early. Apparently she was up early this morning doing Tai Chi and she heard something or someone on the stage behind the curtains. So, she went to go investigate it as quietly as possible. What she found was a woman in a red dress sneaking around behind stage. A moment later the woman realized she\u2019d been spotted and made a dash for one of the mirrors and dove through it. Yup\u2026right through the mirror, like Insincere Marguerite can do. Calamity broke that mirror and cleaned up the mess and then woke us all up. She then woke Marguerite and described the woman in as much detail as she could, which wasn\u2019t much. Insincere Marguerite then looked in one of the other mirrors back stage to see what it saw and she went pale. She said that the woman that had been sneaking around backstage was none other than Yvette, her former companion/slave from Arcadia. Yeah, if that\u2019s not a way to start off the day I don\u2019t know what is.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite and Julia did not come down for the meeting immediately, but Marguerite eventually joined us after a little while. She looked shaken but not as badly as she could have been I suppose. We all talked about what to do to keep people, especially Yvette, from sneaking around behind stage, or anywhere else for that matter. Luna brought up the idea of setting up security cameras in the dressing rooms to keep an eye on things. Lori, or someone else that the dancers trust, will need to be the one that looks at the footage should the need arise. That said Luna also mentioned that she did not think that Yvette would be back in the near future since she got spotted. She is likely spooked and will stay away for a little while at least.<br /> <br /> Now, as to how she got in through the mirrors in the first place. That is the question. Insincere Marguerite ordered some of the mirrors in the dressing rooms from France. It\u2019s possible that Yvette found out which mirrors were being shipped to us and made sure that she was reflected in all of them just in case. She then could have snuck through at any time she thought we\u2019d be asleep. Calamity being up that early in the morning, while not unknown to us, is not common knowledge as far as I know. It was fortunate that she was up to spot Yvette. <br /> <br /> It is still not known exactly what Yvette was able to see either. Calamity saw her when she was heading out, not the other way around, so we don\u2019t know where in the house she went before she was spotted. It is likely that she was here to spy on Insincere Marguerite. It is also possible that she was here to take something or to leave something behind. We\u2019ll have to be extra vigilant in the days to come to see if anything is missing or if something was left. <br /> <br /> Later, at breakfast we all had leftovers from the Thanksgiving meal, as is tradition. It was pretty good. Cold turkey sandwiches are the best. Anyhoo\u2026we brought up the idea of getting cameras again with Insincere Marguerite and she agreed that it would be a good idea. Luna offered to go out and get them and I said that I\u2019d go with her. This was shortly after Lori and De La Rocha both left to go have lunch with Lori\u2019s father, the minister. I was struck again how lucky she is to be able to do that. I hope she realizes that. Though, knowing Lori, she does.<br /> <br /> Shopping for cameras was not as bad as I thought it might be. We went to a security store, which is not a huge spot for Black Friday shopping, so it was not nearly as busy as other places were. Parking was still stupid and the traffic was horrible, but the actual shopping wasn\u2019t that bad at all. We got a few cameras to put up behind stage. They are not too obvious, but are not completely hidden either. It will be known that the area is being filmed by anyone that walks backstage and happens to look in the right places. We will also of course tell the performers that the cameras are there and why. We wouldn\u2019t want them to spot them at a later time and confront us about it. It would look shady on our parts, but if they know from the get go why the cameras are there then there will be less problems.<br /> <br /> As we were getting back from shopping Luna and I spotted Felicity pulling up in her car. We walked slowly so we could meet her at the front door and see what she needed. She asked to speak to whoever handles the financials for the Dream House. I will admit that I was curious, but I led her to the front room while I went off to go look for Calamity. I told Calamity that Felicity was here and the two of them went off to go talk in private. Felicity left a short time later.<br /> <br /> Lori and De La Rocha got back to the Dream House and revealed that everything had gone well with the lunch. They all talked and Lori explained that she was in a relationship with Insincere Marguerite and Julia as well as De La Rocha. Apparently her father took things pretty well. I got the impression that he had some reservations about the whole polyamory thing, but not enough to cause any problems. The other thing that she told us was a little more troubling. She said that her father had received a letter from his \u201cdaughter,\u201d the fetch. Apparently it arrived shortly after Lori first made contact with her dad. So it kind of sounds like her fetch is aware that Lori made contact or felt compelled to reach out to her estranged father. Either one is kind of troubling.<br /> <br /> During all of this Insincere Marguerite, Julia, Calamity and Gawain had been decorating. Luna and I joined in when we got back. It was fun to just hang out with friends and decorate for the holidays, and wear Santa hats. Marguerite was really in the Holiday spirit and wore a nice Santa hat. She found one for me and some for the others. Lori\u2019s had mistletoe tied to the bobble at the tip of the hat. She collected several kisses. Insincere Marguerite was especially excited in general and had too much fun slinking along on the walls to decorate those hard to reach places. Calamity joined her on the walls and between the two of them they got a good bit done. Gawain just started handing up decorations to them and letting them hang them. It was an efficient way to get things done if you ask me. We had decided early on that we were going to do public decorations for the guests and employees to see and enjoy and then do a separate tree just for us later. I think the idea was passed around that we might could ask Oleander to help us find a tree from the Hedge that would look like it had perpetual snow on its branches. I thought that sounded like a great idea. As much as I do not want to be reminded of my time with the Lady, I kind of do miss the snow and the crisp cold air. Winter always seemed so clean and fresh to me. I miss it sometimes, especially here where it\u2019s so hot all the time. But this is where my sister is and where my motley is, so this is where I am. <br /> <br /> While we were decorating and after Lori and De La Rocha joined us, Julia mentioned that her own parents had a very open relationship with another man. Apparently they were friends with this man before and after Julia was born. Julia did some looking into this man, that she remembered as a childhood family friend, and found out that he is a successful professional artist. She said that she had suspicions that this man was her actual father. It would explain where she got her artistic talent from, since neither of her parents are creative in that way. I do not know if she is going to talk to her parents about this or not. I guess time will tell. <br /> <br /> Calamity also revealed to the motley that Felicity had decided to reimburse us for some of the cost of the Thanksgiving dinner. We did spend a good bit of our own money for food and drinks for the feast. We were more than happy to do so and were not expecting recompense, but I will admit that I was not upset that she offered to help offset the cost of the dinner. She also said that Felicity wanted to bring Leonidas to the Dream House to talk to Insincere Marguerite and maybe work things out between them. Calamity made sure that sure that Julia and De La Rocha would behave themselves while Leonidas is here, whenever that is.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Today is the big day. Nightqueen Skitters arrived not long ago with a woman named Lizette. The original plan was to just skype with them, but they arrived at the Lighthouse not long ago. Together they made an imposing pair. Nightqueen Skitters has a rather intense look about her with really long fingers and nails. She seemed fixated on faces and asked some of us if she could have ours. When she got to Gawain she stopped to consider before offering him a face of his own. We all politely declined giving up or receiving faces. Lizette on the other hand introduced herself but was otherwise not all that chatty. She is definitely Nightqueen Skitter\u2019s bodyguard though. She came armed with a pair of chainsaws across her back. They seemed almost huge given her short stature, but I don\u2019t doubt her ability to wield them. Once introductions were over we asked if they knew were Yvette was. The pair looked honestly unsure and stated that Yvette had left the Paris freehold a little while ago and they weren\u2019t sure where she was. We told them that she had paid us a visit in the early morning hours the other day and they seemed genuinely surprised. After that the interviews started. Nightqueen Skitters talked to Insincere Marguerite first. Their talk didn\u2019t take too long and Marguerite didn\u2019t look too upset at the end of it. Though she seemed to be closing off her usual expressive face. I suspect it\u2019s just nerves.<br /> <br /> After Insincere Marguerite, Nightqueen Skitters and Lizette talked to Julia. Julia was keen on being the second person that they talked to and we didn\u2019t see any reason to hold her back. I believe initially we weren\u2019t going to have Julia talk to them given her rather submissive attitude when it comes to Insincere Marguerite, but she was very interested in talking to them. It would have looked strange if we\u2019d prevented her from talking on her fianc\u00e9e\u2019s behalf so we didn\u2019t. After that we all had private interviews in turn. Lori came out of hers with a pleased look on her face. I think that she\u2019s still nervous since a decision has not been made yet, but behaved as though things went well for her. When it was my turn I told Nightqueen Skitters and Lizette that I trust Insincere Marguerite a great deal and believe that she is a good person. I acknowledged that she had done things when she was in Arcadia, but that most of us had done things that we\u2019re not proud of while we were there. I told them that I truly believe that people can change from what they were in Arcadia and become better people, different people. I also said that people need a second chance to change or otherwise they won\u2019t be able to. I believe Insincere Marguerite has been given a second chance and is making the best of it. She has been doing an admirable job of turning her back on what she once was.<br /> <br /> I know more than most how hard it can be sometimes to completely change yourself. Or at least go back on years of habit or training to become someone new. I served the Lady for years loyally. She was my sovereign and I loved her. Finding out what she was really like was hard, as was leaving her. I didn\u2019t really have another choice. I did not want to go back to what I had been and she wasn\u2019t going to take no for an answer. So, I had to leave. I have been given my own second chance and I\u2019ve taken it. I have done my best to change my ways and turn my back on everything that she stood for. What I stood for, for years. I do not deserve the chance that my motley has given me. I do not deserve the leniency that Boss Lowjack has given me, but I will admit that I am selfish and I\u2019ve taken it. I have embraced the chance that my friends have given me and am doing my best to become someone new. Times have been hard lately, but I\u2019ve been trying. I believe that I can do it too. I have the support of my friends. I have the love and confidence of my girlfriend Luna. That more than anything I think has really helped. She is like me in many ways and understands what it is to change. Here\u2019s hoping that Nightqueen Skitters understands as well and sees that Insincere Marguerite has truly become someone new. <br /> <br /> <b><br /> Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> A difficult start to the morning.<br /> <br /> Calamity woke I up because she saw an intruder flee into a mirror, and wondered if my Contact had a way to prevent people from using a mirror that had reflected them without destroying it. I told her I was unaware of any such thing. She had seen a woman in red sneaking through the house near the changing rooms, and on pursuit the woman used Contracts of Reflections to escape through a mirror. The mirrors were among the pretty French mirrors I had selected. I used my contract to look back, and I saw her.<br /> <br /> My Dearest. Yvette. <br /> <br /> Calamity was talking to I. I was shocked I know she was talking about Becky but it all faded. Yvette and I escaping into the Hedge, depending on each other. Going to sleep next to her.<br /> <br /> Waking up alone.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t clearly remember climbing into the vents, but I did. So enclosing. So confining. I felt safe again, surrounded by a tightness. I dozed, and it did not abandon I. I awake hearing talk of I, so I joined them in the kitchen. All but Julia. I told them I was fine. It was sort of true. Everyone was concerned. Yvette could hurt I. It seems likely. Luna insisted on cameras, and went out with Jacob for them. Which was nice. I need to speak to Julia.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Ghosts</span></u></b><br /> <br /> <br /> Two women rush through the winding paths of the Hedge, both are pale, one perfect porcelain, the other lean and feline. Together, they escaped Arcadia. Together, they had overcome the odd mossy hobgoblin that sought to make a meal of them. Now, exhausted, they find a safe place to hide and get a little sleep. They traded watches. Blonde and blue eyed, the lean one watched first. The Hedge was beautiful at night. They had traveled some way, but compromised to move part at night part day, and she hoped to be home under the next cover of darkness. She gazed up at what probably were not stars, but labored to stay awake. A glance beside her showed her why: the perfect features of the woman who meant more to her than anything, who she risked everything to bring with her while she fled. A few hours later, she woke the doll-like woman beside her, and curled into a ball to sleep next to her Dearest, who watched over her much as she had.<br /> <br /> She awoke alone. At first, she panicked. Was her Dearest in danger? She looked for signs of a struggle. Then she noticed Yvette\u2019s things were gone. She had been abandoned. She was alone. Her face went from shocked to devastated slowly. Did she even care enough to escape now? Insincere Marguerite sank down to her knees, into the shadow of the tree, skinny arms around her skinny body. A breeze blew across her, and she began to weep.<br /> <br /> Blue eyes opened. She was in the Dream House now, approaching the \u201chenhouse\u201d. She entered the private hall the family lived in, and knocked on her door. <br /> <br /> \u201cJulia?\u201d<br /> <br /> The door opened. Julia stood in the room. She had been crying, and she had a suitcase. Insincere Marguerite stood, disbelieving, at her fianc\u00e9e packing and sobbing softly. Leaving her.<br /> <br /> \u201cJulia what are you doing?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m\u2026I\u2019m getting out of your way, Insincere Marguerite\u201d Julia didn\u2019t look up.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat? No. No no no no no!\u201d The Darkling raised her voice, hands out in front of her. \u201cWhy? Why would you do that? Why would you leave me?\u201d Fear was in the Lurker\u2019s eyes, the pitch of her voice raised.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou have found your Dearest. Yvette.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u2018But you are\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI will not be number two in your life, Insincere Marguerite. I am sorry. I can\u2019t. It was hard enough to compete with a ghost, but I certainly can\u2019t now\u201d The taller woman turned away.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou are not\u2026you won\u2019t\u2026I proposed to you, Julia.\u201d The French Changeling struggled to keep her words in English. They barely came at all. \u201cThat proposal did not hinge on not finding Yvette.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDo you love her?\u201d The Artist was tense, almost cold.<br /> <br /> \u201cYes.\u201d Insincere Marguerite looked thoughtful. \u201cI am honest with you, so yes. Well, I love the woman I knew, before returning from Arcadia. And the woman she knew, she no longer really exists, whether she loves or hates her.\u201d A shrug.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo I am in the way.\u201d The Nightsinger\u2019s tone was even.<br /> <br /> The Darkling was shocked again. \u201cJulia Lynn Oldacre, you are not \u2018in the way\u2019. You are the woman I shall marry, and spend a long life with. Hopefully a life we spend with Juliette and Maria. But I will be with you regardless. Maybe I can make something with Yvette. Maybe I can\u2019t. But if Yvette cannot accept that you will be Mrs. Insincere Marguerite, than I shall turn her away.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou are not serious.\u201d Julia walked over.<br /> <br /> \u201cHave I ever lied to you?\u201d Insincere Marguerite looked defiant. She also looked up; Julia being half a foot taller she had little choice.<br /> <br /> \u201cGod Marguerite I\u2026Insincere Marguerite I\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou may call me just Marguerite if you wish my love. You and the family. You have won my heart. You have earned it.\u201d<br /> <br /> The Artist clasped her Fianc\u00e9e to her chest and began to weep again. Happy tears. They fell on the Tunnelgrub\u2019s flaxen hair.<br /> <br /> \u201cI won\u2019t leave you.\u201d<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite smiled, listening to Julia\u2019s heartbeat. Today was going to be a good day. They would decorate for Christmas they would be together. The Wyrd had thrown everything it seemed to have at her, preying on her Vices, losing her best friend, a temptation too great, even this old flame reappearing with probably sinister motives. Insincere Marguerite was unbowed. She knew as long as she had her family she could survive anything.<br /> <br /> Even this.<br /> <i><br /> End Session LXIX</i><br /> <br /> Lizette is a PC from <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465832-chronicles-of-darkness-the-golden-eagle-actual-play\">The Golden Eagle</a>. It seemed a safe bet, as she will be very high Wyrd by the end, and it is very unlikely any PC will die (permanently) over the course of that game. Miss Skitters is an Autumn Court Darkling from that game (Not Autumn Queen, that game last had her appear 102 years before <i>Malibu Dream House</i> takes place). Funny story, the Skype vs appearing thing happened because between sessions during the downtime in <i>Golden Eagle</i>, Dearbh\u00e1il (a Spring Fairest PC in that game) decided she wanted to travel to Hollywood and establish a Door there for the Motley. So that changed the course of the present.<br /> <br /> So Yvette was here. That can\u2019t mean anything good.<br /> <br /> We had fun describing the Christmas decorating going on with everyone. Weird to have Christmas stuff going on when it actually is Christmastide. Eh, we will probably hit Christmas in like late spring.<br /> <br /> That should cover the session fairly well. Comments and Questions welcome.<br /> <br /> As a note, changes in the USA have me deeply concerned. I am not just up and fleeing my home, but quite honestly I have to be prepared to leave if things become dangerous. What this means for you is I might abruptly and without warning, and these campaigns end. I don\u2019t want that to happen, but I also want to live. So there you go. Sorry. Be good to yourselves, and nice to each other.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T15:11:55-08:00","id":1005874,"title":"","content":"I know that there are much more important things, but the reminder that Gawain's mien does not have a face brought up so many interesting questions. Like, I understand that the mien is often more metaphorical than physical, and Changelings still have all the organs and fluids of a normal human unless contradicted by a merit, blessing or contract, but it brings up what it looks like to see Gawain, who has no visible tongue or teeth in his mien, do anything with his mouth. Like, does he just drop food down into his armor? Or does it disappear behind the darkness inside him when he closes his mouth? Or do you see him chewing with invisible teeth until he swallows? And would it be impossible to lip-read him?<br /> <br /> And what does it feel like to kiss him or make out with him (or other things that involve tongues :3)? I know that it's possible since it's mentioned a bunch of times. It sounds like it would be similar to kissing him when you are fooled by the Mask, but you can't see what you're interacting with.<br /> <br /> And speaking of semantics about Gawain, is that cape that looks like it's made of a patch of meadow a canon part of his mien?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T02:13:39-08:00","id":1006073,"title":"","content":"I, um, ah, um...<i>pushes Gawain's player in front of herself</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T06:52:14-08:00","id":1006169,"title":"","content":"I was assuming he and Calamity would know best anyway <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T00:24:13-08:00","id":1006617,"title":"","content":"Well, this has come up in game, though not the food/eating part specifically. It has been established that Gawain's mask is the source of his expressions and blushing when teased. I have described the fact that Calamity finds the fact that he is metal to be reassuring as it is very different from the soft touch of her Keeper. Also, him being metalflesh does make him immune to her Hedgehog's dilemma and thus he is the only person she's truly comfortable sleeping with. <br /> <br /> They can and do kiss so I rather imagine that his face is where his mask's is. But as a changeling I guess she would see it the way those who are enchanted do, as a ghost image with the empty helmet behind it... We tend to be a little handwavy about how exactly it works in the games beyond that he can do the normal things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T07:58:07-08:00","id":1006710,"title":"","content":"oh, i didn't realize there was a ghostly image of his face. I thought it was just the helmet. New question, does he bleed? No, seriously, he still takes wound penalties, right? The Mien is so weird and fascinating in how it's both the truth and a lie in different ways<br /> <br /> Wait, if he has a ghostly face image, why did Miss Skitters offer to give him a face?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T09:04:06-08:00","id":1006740,"title":"","content":"I think you're forgetting a major aspect of Changelings <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7920_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7920\" data-vbnamecard=\"7920\">Master Aquatosic</a>; those who use the Wyrd innately don't make logical sense.<br /> <br /> Well, that's not entirely true; there is a logic to Changelings, but it's one that follows fairy-tale logic, and even then it varies from Keeper to Keeper on what that logic actually is. Lori has wings and yet she's not encumbered by them from their weight; Calamity has glass growing from her bones and out of her skin; Oleander is a living tree, yet isn't more heavy than a normal person; Jacob literally has ice growing on his body, yet he doesn't set hypothermia in those who stay near him for too long. Relatively speaking, a living suit of armor isn't all that strange.<br /> <br /> Though to your questions, yes, I imagine he bleeds and takes wound penalties, and when Miss Skitters offered him a face I think it was from the fact he just had a helmet rather than a face like the others on his mien. Remember that though the Mask serves as a face for those without, it's also something Changelings can change with the right merits/skills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T09:08:22-08:00","id":1006745,"title":"","content":"i understand that he can eat and kiss normally. my mind is just curious as to what it looks like. now that i know he has a ghostly face, I have more of an image of what it looks like, even if it still makes no logical sense","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/membe