-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T09:07:47-08:00","id":1009821,"title":"","content":"anyone ever read Un Lun Dun here? Cause the Ungun is such a perfect 5-dot token, saying anything more is spoilers","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T11:21:25-08:00","id":1011149,"title":"","content":"Please stay safe, Baroness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2286-indarkestknight","name":"indarkestknight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T00:47:32-08:00","id":1011893,"title":"","content":"Thanks so much, Indarkestknight.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite is not the only one to have spectres in her past. Now Lorelei and Jacob face shadows of the past, even as they celebrate their successes over the week. How do the different fae react when these shadows fall across theirs?<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite is a short story taking place on the evening during the session\u2019s timeframe.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LXX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Oh my God I can\u2019t even think right now I haven\u2019t slept and the Spring contracts aren\u2019t really helping that much. I just can\u2019t seem to focus my mind on anything. A lot has happened over the past day and some of it was even good so I suppose I\u2019m going to want to remember it and setting it all down here might help to distract me and keep me from completely losing my shit, so here goes.<br /> <br /> Right, so a little while after I finished writing my previous entry the Night Queen came out and thanked us all for speaking with her about Marguerite. She wanted to confer with Lizette for a while, and told us that the two of them would definitely stay to see the show at the Dream House that night before heading back to Paris. Both of them seemed relatively upbeat about the whole thing, so I guess that\u2019s a good sign.<br /> <br /> When we got back to the Dream House, Calamity and I sort of fell into rehearsal mode and attempted to hammer out the last few niggling imperfections in the \u201cBloody Creature Poster Girl\u201d number. We made sure that Marguerite had the lighting cues down, and that Courtney and Teresa were pitch-perfect as the backup singers. When I was sure that we had it as close to perfection as it was likely to get, we put the rehearsals to bed and split up to prepare in our own ways.<br /> <br /> The result was spectacular. It was easily one of the better performances of my career, and I don\u2019t think I\u2019ve <u><u>ever</u></u> seen Calamity dance like that. Gawain and I both gave her a little pep talk before the show. I know I infused some glamour into my words to give her a bit more self-confidence, and I think it helped a little\u2026 but she would have killed it even without the magical help from me. Though it goes against my nature, I knew that this number was all about her dance, so I did what I could to draw attention to her rather than myself.<br /> <br /> People were impressed. Ordinarily I\u2019d be lapping it up and describing the compliments we got, but it doesn\u2019t really seem to matter right now, so I\u2019ll just hit the highlights.<br /> <br /> Joan and Andromeda were there. I stopped by their table and spoke to them briefly. They were both a little upset because Andromeda\u2019s parents had not accepted their relationship as well as they had hoped. The professed reason is because Joan is not Jewish, though Andromeda is relatively certain that it\u2019s really because she\u2019s seeing a woman. So that sucks, but as far as I can tell they\u2019re not letting it come between them, so I\u2019m sure they\u2019ll survive.<br /> <br /> I talked to a lot of other people, but the next one I feel like I should mention is Oleander. She was still mildly toxic, so we couldn\u2019t smooch, but it was the first time I\u2019d seen her since she\u2019d disappeared into the Hedge five days earlier, so I made sure to make time to speak with her. I brought up Charlotte\u2019s little visit, of course, and tried to impress upon her that I didn\u2019t want her getting in trouble with her Court just to help me, but she kept insisting that she\u2019d done the right thing both for me and for the Freehold, and that even if that hadn\u2019t been the case, she\u2019d do anything to help me out.<br /> <br /> God, I hope I can temper that attitude with a bit of reason. The last thing I need on my conscience is for something really awful to happen to her while she\u2019s sticking her neck out for me. I don\u2019t know what I\u2019d do if she\u2019d been seriously hurt last Monday, or if she\u2019d gotten in real trouble with Queen Charlotte.<br /> <br /> I was still pretty high on life at that point, so I made sure she knew that I appreciated what she was willing to do for me, and then asked for her advice on finding a magical Christmas tree in the Hedge. Of course, she almost immediately volunteered to find something suitable for us herself, and wouldn\u2019t be deterred. Jesus, maybe Charlotte\u2019s right about me\u2026 I need to be more careful with the requests I make of my lovers.<br /> <br /> So after that I pretty much planted myself in D\u2019s lap at the \u201cgirlfriend table.\u201d Marguerite and Julia were there, as were Becky and Calamity. We were all being pretty affectionate at that point when we all received a group text from Gawain, telling us that we needed to have a motley meeting after the crowds cleared out. That\u2019s when the first dark shadow fell over the evening, and things have yet to lighten up.<br /> <br /> Becky hung around downstairs while the rest of us made our way to the media room to hear what Gawain had to tell us. It was actually Jacob\u2019s news, though. During the show, a mysterious woman approached him and introduced herself as Moire. She\u2019s apparently an oracle of the Dusk Court, and she had information for him (Gawain called Captain Jack later, and he vouched for her veracity).<br /> <br /> \u201cIt is about Rook,\u201d Jacob said softly.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou have a lead?\u201d I asked eagerly. I know that Jacob\u2019s been hoping to find and redeem his friend for months now, and all of our investigative avenues dried up long ago.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe said that he knows about my sister,\u201d he deadpanned.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh my God,\u201d I said. \u201cIs she okay? Do we need to go to her?\u201d I really need to learn to stop interrupting people.<br /> <br /> Jacob put a hand on my shoulder. \u201cShe also said that he has allied himself with a bird of prey,\u201d he said.<br /> <br /> D caught the look in my eyes, strode over to me and threw her arms around me. I think, in hindsight, that\u2019s the main reason that I didn\u2019t just bolt once I got over the shock.<br /> <br /> Hunting Hawk. I think I always knew in the back of my mind that he was still out there somewhere looking for me. It was na\u00efve of me to believe the Empress would abide by the spirit of our agreement and let me live out my life here on Earth; I was her favorite after all. Of course she sent her most trusted hatchet-man to bring me back.<br /> <br /> It took me a few minutes to process what was being said. The terror was all-encompassing, and there was no room for anything else in my brain. My dreams of becoming a doctor, my improved relationship with my father, even my love for the people surrounding me\u2026 all of it scattered like leaves in a strong wind. All that was left was my intense fear that Hawk would find me and take me back to my cage.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m here, Jules.\u201d<br /> <br /> Those words, whispered into my ear, broke through the dread which had essentially seized up my muscles, and I let myself relax a little. Maria is strong, and brave, and utterly devoted to me. She\u2019s more than a match for Hunting Hawk by herself\u2026 and when he comes for me, she won\u2019t <u><u>be</u></u> by herself. Calamity won\u2019t let him take me. Gawain won\u2019t let him take me. Jacob won\u2019t let him take me. Marguerite and Julia sure as <u><u>hell</u></u> won\u2019t let him take me. The rest of the Freehold won\u2019t let him take me.<br /> <br /> These thoughts allowed me to rejoin the conversation. Besides, there was someone else to think about.<br /> <br /> \u201cSorry,\u201d I said, shaking my head in a futile attempt to clear it. \u201cSorry. Is your sister okay, Jacob? Do we need to go to her?\u201d<br /> <br /> Jacob shook his head. \u201cMarguerite looked in on her through her mirrors. She is fine. She has a houseguest\u2026 another young woman is sleeping on her couch. And Captain Jack said that Moire\u2019s prophecies usually have a little bit of lead time.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo\u2026 how do we deal with this?\u201d I asked, maybe still a teeny bit panicky.<br /> <br /> Jacob shrugged. \u201cI would still like to find Rook and try to help him, if he is willing,\u201d he said simply.<br /> <br /> I thought about that, and nodded. \u201cI\u2026 don\u2019t expect anything to come of it, but if possible we should offer Hunting Hawk the same chance. It\u2019s only fair.\u201d<br /> <br /> D stepped forward, keeping an arm around my waist. \u201cOne thing I want to make very clear right here and now is that Lori is <u><u>not</u></u> going to be used as bait to draw these psychos out of hiding,\u201d she said fervently. \u201cI\u2019m open to just about any other strategy you guys want to try\u2026 but that is <u><u>not</u></u> happening. End of story.\u201d Julia seconded this, and the rest of the group (myself included) rapidly approved the motion. <br /> <br /> I excused myself to get some air after that. While it\u2019s true that I was having trouble breathing by that point, that wasn\u2019t the real reason I wanted to get outside. Thinking about Hunting Hawk made me think about Arcadia, which made me think about that damn cage that was all I knew while I was there, and\u2026 it just felt like the walls were closing in on me all of a sudden. I had to get outside, to feel the open air on my wings for a few minutes, even if I wasn\u2019t flying.<br /> <br /> D followed me out there, of course, as did a few of the others. My honey got this sort of thoughtful look on her face after a moment, and then began to speak. \u201cI have an idea,\u201d she said slowly. \u201cIt\u2019s a terrible idea, but I think I should mention it anyway.\u201d<br /> <br /> The rest of us looked at her expectantly.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell,\u201d she continued after a moment, \u201cHunting Hawk was the main guard that watched over you in Arcadia, right?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cHe was the <u><u>only</u></u> guard we ever saw,\u201d I acknowledged.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo if he\u2019s here\u2026 who\u2019s watching your two friends?\u201d she asked after a moment.<br /> <br /> I thought about that. \u201cIt\u2026 might be the perfect time to rescue them,\u201d I said.<br /> <br /> \u201cBut only if we\u2019re ready,\u201d D cautioned. \u201cIt\u2019s something to think about, but for right now we have to make sure that you, Jacob, and his sister are safe.\u201d<br /> <br /> Julia piped up with a suggestion. \u201cHas anyone told the Winter Court about this yet? I mean, ferreting out Loyalists is what they do, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> Calamity seconded the suggestion. \u201cI\u2019m pledge-bound to report this to them anyway,\u201d she added after a moment.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd I hate to mention this,\u201d Julia continued, \u201cbut we probably need to bring Darke in on this situation. It\u2019s what he does, and he does it very well\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo,\u201d Jacob and I both said at the same time\u2026 but we agreed that the Winter Court as a whole should know about the situation.<br /> <br /> Jacob called Boss Lowjack and let him know what was going on. He was understandably upset by the news, and offered to help us out however he could. He also wanted to bring Darke in on this, but said he would allow us to deal with it \u201cin-house\u201d if that\u2019s what we wanted to do. However, he needed a definite answer by the following day or else he would be forced to act on his own.<br /> <br /> We argued the issue back and forth for a while. Jacob didn\u2019t want to let Darke anywhere near his former friend, and I can definitely see why. For my part, I don\u2019t think we can allow ourselves to employ Darke\u2019s methods no matter what the risk. But the others raised some very valid points, even though I could tell that it galled them to even suggest going to Darke for help. Darke knows a lot more about hunting Loyalists than we do. He has resources that we don\u2019t. And he would have an outside perspective on how to deal with the situation\u2026 one untainted by our fear and worry.<br /> <br /> So in the end we decided to at least consult with Darke before taking any action on our own. Ideally we\u2019d still like to handle this within the motley, but it would be foolish not to take advantage of his expertise.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe will call Boss Lowjack after breakfast,\u201d Marguerite suggested, \u201cand tell him that we will consult with Darke, but that he is not to take any action without our consent. But for now, we all need sleep, no?\u201d<br /> <br /> I did not sleep last night. I knew I wouldn\u2019t. Once we were away from the others, D and Marguerite and Julia swept me into an embrace and held me as I trembled and cried and muttered to myself like a crazy person. I was rambling; nothing I said made any kind of sense. Hell, it probably still doesn\u2019t. I know I told them that Hunting Hawk probably didn\u2019t know me as Lorelei Grace, since I chose that name after I escaped from the Empress. She always called me Rainbow. He usually called me Whore, when he bothered to speak with me at all.<br /> <br /> Or maybe I talked about that before I went to bed. I don\u2019t know.<br /> <br /> There was no sex last night. For once I truly wasn\u2019t in the mood.<br /> <br /> I got up before the others and went to church. If Rook and/or Hunting Hawk are watching us, they probably don\u2019t know that we know about them, and we don\u2019t want to tip them off to that tidbit by varying our routines. D went with me and Marguerite shadowed us, since the group doesn\u2019t want me going off by myself until this situation is resolved. We spoke to Dad briefly, and I\u2019m pretty sure he picked up on the fact that something was bothering me, but I didn\u2019t tell him what\u2019s going on at that point.<br /> <br /> We had sex breakfast around noon as usual. I had used Spring contracts to pep myself up before church, but even after that I couldn\u2019t muster up any true enthusiasm for the day. I don\u2019t remember what we ate, but Jacob called Lowjack and informed him of our decision, and he invited us to meet with Darke at his bar in half an hour to make our plans. We agreed.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t claim to remember much about the plans we made either; talking about this situation feels almost like a dream to me now. I know Darke said they had not been able to locate Rook, but they had eyes on a Loyalist in L.A. they thought was Hunting Hawk. I gave him every bit of information I could remember about the Empress\u2019 jailor, and that seemed to confirm his suspicions.<br /> <br /> Hawk has been living in L.A., off the grid and under the radar. He hasn\u2019t yet attracted the attention of the Day or Night Courts. He seems to be having difficulty adjusting to this world\u2026 the fact that he can\u2019t fly here and the smog in the atmosphere are forcing him to reevaluate his usual hunting tactics. He\u2019s been observing me from a distance \u2013 no one really seems to know for how long \u2013 but now that he\u2019s got an ally, it seems like he might be ready to make his move at last.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll be honest, I don\u2019t really know how we decided to proceed either. There was talk of bringing Jacob\u2019s sister in on the secrets of Changeling society, ensorcelling her\u2026 though Jacob still doesn\u2019t want to tell her who he really is, even if we end up doing that. But if she\u2019s aware of the real danger posed by Rook, we might have an easier time protecting her from him.<br /> <br /> Honestly, we could probably take care of Hunting Hawk pretty easily at this point if we wanted to. The problem is that we have no leads on Rook\u2019s location at the moment, and Darke is hoping that Hawk will lead us to him. If we spring a trap on Hawk, Rook will almost certainly get wind of it, and he\u2019ll go to ground, making it that much harder for us to resolve this situation once and for all.<br /> <br /> There were a few plans thrown out there. We talked about sending Jacob\u2019s sister (or possibly Davie disguised as her) to an art exhibition in L.A. on Wednesday, to try to lure Rook out of hiding. We also discussed spreading rumors that the Empress had sent another servant after me, and that servant would be taking me back through the Hedge at a particular time and place. That might work\u2026 Hunting Hawk was always desperate for the Empress\u2019 approval, and the idea that someone might steal his glory on this particular hunt would probably raise his hackles like nothing else.<br /> <br /> Darke asked a few questions about my Durance at that point, so that if we go with the latter plan he\u2019ll be able to make the \u201csecond hunter\u201d convincing. It seems strange now, but he pointed out something that had never occurred to me before: all of the Empress\u2019 songbirds were girls. Hunting Hawk was the only man I ever saw in that place, and he was also the only guard I ever encountered. It seems logical to assume that the Empress employs only males as guards, and only females as pets.<br /> <br /> Enough of that. I don\u2019t want to talk about this situation anymore; I just want it to be <u><u>over</u></u>. We have a show tonight. I have to perform, and I can\u2019t let anyone who might be watching know that anything is wrong. I pride myself on my acting ability, but this might well stretch me to my limits. I\u2019ll have to draw on every ounce of professional pride I possess to keep from falling apart out there tonight. The show must go on, but\u2026 this is Hunting Hawk. He represents everything that I\u2019ve been trying to escape for almost a year now\u2026 everything that I endured for three and a half decades. Servitude. Enslavement. Humiliation. The subjugation of my very <u><u>being</u></u>.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve never been this scared. Not when Mary\u2019s fetch was trying to kill us. Not when the Mothership attacked. Not even when I had to tell my Dad the truth about who and what I am. I know Maria and the others will protect me. I know that I am as safe here with them as I could be anywhere in the world. But what can I say? Fear isn\u2019t rational, and Hunting Hawk is the boogeyman who has haunted my dreams ever since I escaped.<br /> <br /> God, I will serve Your will in this as in all things, but I <u><u>beg</u></u> You to spare me this fate. May Hunting Hawk not take me back to the Empress\u2019 service. May he not harm my dearest Maria, or Marguerite, or Julia, or any of my other friends and loves. May Jacob\u2019s sister Elena be kept from whatever terrible fate Rook plans for her. And please, God\u2026 grant me the courage to face Arcadia again, so that I can rescue Missy and Jane at last.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> Sunday, November 28<sup>th</sup><br /> Nine years, six months, twenty-two days<br /> Days without stabbing: 0<br /> <br /> I am a fucking monster. I almost forgot that. I came so close to forgetting that. I let myself get lost in stupid little girl with dreams of living happily ever after and dancing. This time yesterday I was drunk with happy. The meetings with Nightqueen Skitters and her guard Lizette were over and they seemed satisfied that whatever the situation might have been that it seemed clear that Insincere Marguerite was not a loyalist or Keeper now. The show was shaping up to go off perfectly. Handsome gave both Lori and I a nice inspirational talk and Lori used her magic to inspire us both. I even called upon the goblin vow I made with Blood to ask it to make the crowd \u2018hot blooded\u2019 for the show. I promised to bleed or draw blood in the heat of passion before dawn. I figured that throwing myself into that number would have me in the mood for such anyway. And I was certainly in that mood before dawn, just not the way I was expecting to be.<br /> <br /> The Dream House was packed. I was nervous but we\u2019d really put in the effort on this one. I called on the Vainglory Lori had taught me and once the lights flared and the music started\u2026 Fuck it was amazing. I threw myself into it and I fucking nailed it. Everything was perfect. It felt so damn good. I lost myself in it like the best sex or the hardest fight. And the GLAMOUR\u2026 Oh the glamour, feeling all of the lust and desire and fear and hunger and need rolling off the crowd. And even afterward, as I worked the room. I could feel the looks and I couldn\u2019t help but strut across the floor with my mien still showing thanks to the Vainglory. I was flirty and feeling the mix of hunger and fear as I did so\u2026 I was flying. I got into a long chat with Lizette about chainsaws and incendiary weapons that was way more sexual than it should have been until the Nightqueen elbowed her companion and we were both reminded that there were mortals about. I floated to the girlfriend table and my Dragon. I had thought about trying to avoid Beautiful given the sort of mood I knew I\u2019d be in but despite the prey in the room I wanted to be with her and she made no move to stop me from kissing her hard and hungry and showing her what I wanted.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I was on top of the fucking world right about then, sitting close and teasing her subtly as she growled and teased back. Lori and DLR were getting a little frisky as well. And I guess that\u2019s why Handsome sent the text out that we needed a motley meeting. I could see that he looked guilty but really worried and I knew something was wrong. I told Beautiful to wait for me and she agreed to. I should have known better and sent her home but in the moment I just couldn\u2019t imagine anything bringing me down. <br /> <br /> Stupid of me to think that. I dance and I sing about being a monster... about being dangerous. I make light of it. I play at it as if it\u2019s just some fun little game. A little thrill to the fucking. But the monster inside me isn\u2019t fur lined cuffs and a little slap and tickle. It\u2019s nails and razors and blood and screaming. And as soon as it became clear what was going on it hit me like a fucking tidal wave. I thought I was so much better. I thought I had it under control. I thought I was ready to think about playing house and being some sort of fucking happy little girlfriend. Like I could keep it caged with a white picket fence.<br /> <br /> Rook knows about Jacob\u2019s sister and he\u2019s formed some sort of partnership with Hunting Hawk. Jacob is worried about her. Lori is shaken. I tried to reassure them both but it was so fucking hard to focus. I want them DEAD. I want to hunt them and kill them and see them ended. They\u2019re threatening my motley, my family\u2026 But honestly, that part of me doesn\u2019t really care. It\u2019s a rapid dog straining at its leash because it has prey its allowed to hurt and maim and kill. Prey I am allowed to hurt and kill. I want to hurt them. I want to end them. I want to feel their blood on my glass and see the light fade from their eyes. I don\u2019t have to hold back. I don\u2019t have to feel guilty. They deserve to hurt and bleed and die. They deserve the Calamity that is going to befall them.<br /> <br /> I won\u2019t let them take my motley, my friends. I won\u2019t let them harm them or anyone else. I will do want ever it takes to see that those I swore to protect remain safe. Darke was brought up. The others are leery of working with him. I should be but this is what he does. He hunts loyalists and he\u2019s the best at it. He\u2019s a bigger monster than they are. He\u2019s the monster we need right now.<br /> <br /> I am afraid that he\u2019s the monster I will be some day. After the meeting I had to go back to face Becky. I walked out and lingered on the balcony, looking at her sitting there playing some silly little game on her phone with one claw-tip as the Christmas lights blinked and turned her white hair into a silken rainbow that swayed and danced impatiently about her shoulders. I had to just watch her for a long moment, and then when I did finally approach, I watched as she turned and her expression went from bright to deathly serious. Even without being a Spring Courtier or a succubus she could tell something was wrong. I wasn\u2019t very coherent. I did manage to explain what had happened, but at the time I couldn\u2019t find the words for how I was feeling. How all those months of therapy and meditation and working at laying this darkness to rest had just evaporated. I hugged her and sent her on her way. I wasn\u2019t about to kiss her and let her feel what I wanted.<br /> <br /> I turned, planning to head down to the basement and work on the heavy bag until I either broke it or my hand. But Jacob was there and had his knives. He just looked at me. \u201cYou need to spar.\u201d It wasn\u2019t a question. I think he needed it too. The usual banter and friendly comments were absent. We fought hard in the dark and in silence, even as we exchanged nicks and cuts with little more than a hiss to acknowledge them. I\u2019m not sure either of us really felt better, but it did wear us both out enough to sleep.<br /> <br /> Today hasn\u2019t been much better. We met with Lowjack and Darke. We talked to them about the situation and tried to make plans. Darke\u2019s people have been aware of and watching Hunting Hawk though they didn\u2019t know who he was after. It wouldn\u2019t be hard to move on him but we need to draw Rook out. Lots of planning and ideas. I tried to be constructive but I know my focus was off. I want those two dead. I want them to hurt and suffer. I know we need to give Jacob a chance to talk to Rook. Closure if nothing else. He needs to be able to say he at least tired to save him. I know enough of his own turn to doubt that he alone is going to be able to sway Rook. I could be wrong. I want to be wrong. I also want to be right because I want to fight Rook. I\u2019ve heard Jacob talk about his skills. I want to dance with him, not the practice of sparring but the real thing, the life or death Thunderdome two enter one leaves dance. I want to feel his blood on my skin as I run my glass fingers along his bones. I want to taste his razor kisses. I want to know if Hunting Hawk\u2019s feathers are are soft as Lori\u2019s. I can only imagine that he\u2019s as gorgeous as she is and I want to cut that perfect skin and destroy that beauty.<br /> <br /> I need to focus. This is wrong. This is sick. Even if they do deserve it\u2026 And they do. They deserve to be punished and I am made for it. I want.. I need\u2026 Why shouldn\u2019t I savor their just desserts? Why should it fall on someone who will regret or anguish over delivering the pain and vengeance they deserve? I want their pain. I\u2019m already broken\u2026 why should someone else have to become a monster when I already am one?<br /> <br /> Is this why the Voices haven\u2019t come looking for me? Is this what They wanted me to become? Are They just waiting for me to return and take my place with Them, punishing the naughty girls and boys in the darkness? Or is it that They really don\u2019t care? Perhaps my escape meant nothing more than needing a new Jane. No\u2026 I CUT Them. I HURT Them. I was the only one that struck back at Them. That has to mean something. It has to.<br /> <br /> But if that were true, why haven\u2019t They come after me for it?<br /> <br /> Fuck. There is a show tonight. I need to push past all of this and focus. My motley needs my head in the fucking game right now. Lori and Jacob need me. I\u2026 I can rise about this. I can keep this in check and be reasonable. This is about protecting them, not destroying Rook and Hunting Hawk. I am not going to give into these urges.<br /> <br /> I need to go and do my forms. I need to find my balance and my focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T00:48:27-08:00","id":1011894,"title":"","content":"<b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> I am exhausted. Today has been a very long day for more reasons than one. Before the show I told the motley of my suspicions that Yvette might have left something behind or taken something when she was here spying on us. The lot of us searched the house from top to bottom and didn\u2019t find anything missing or added. So there\u2019s that at least. One good thing to happen today. After that we all went our separate ways to prepare for the show. The ladies did one last run through of their act and started to get dressed. Gawain swept while they practiced, and I stocked up the bar. We went through a good bit of alcohol during the Thanksgiving get together. Considering how many guests we had I\u2019m not surprised, but I still had to restock for the show, so that\u2019s what I was doing.<br /> <br /> At the show Lori and Calamity debuted their new act to thunderous applause. It really was very well done. I watched from the bar as they danced and sang to the song \u201cBloody Creature Poster Girl.\u201d I forgot the band\u2019s name, but I\u2019m not forgetting the name of that song any time soon. It was apropos to Calamity in a lot of ways. When she lets the \u201cmonster\u201d out during a fight I can see the similarities.<br /> <br /> We had several influential people as our guests tonight at the show. Desiree was there with Jolie and Gloria. Nightqueen Skitters and Lizette were present as well. Apparently after the interviews they had tea with Madame Spidertoes and then came to the show. They seemed to be in good spirits so hopefully they found everything with Insincere Marguerite to be satisfactory. At least I have not heard otherwise. I wonder when or if they are going to reveal their findings to Insincere Marguerite to let her know if she can return to Paris or not? I\u2019m assuming that they will, but it didn\u2019t happen tonight. At least not that I know of.<br /> <br /> And speaking of things that we\u2019re not sure of yet. Molly came to the bar, as has become her habit, and started talking to me and Gawain. She has been doing well and is still spending a lot of time with Chalcedony. She even offered to talk to the azure girl and see if she might be willing to come back to the Dream House sometime in the near future. Gawain expressed an interest in this and explained that he wanted to be able to apologize to Chalcedony in person for everything that happened at the club. I can understand that. He wants to make amends. I would apologize, but find that I still don\u2019t trust her. Maybe how things were handled was not the best, but it was the best we could do at the time. I guess for my part I just want Chalcedony to prove that she is not up to something. I\u2019m not sure how she\u2019s supposed to do that, but I am worried about the attraction that so many people feel towards her after they watch her for any length of time. I will be rather upset if she hurts Molly in any way.<br /> <br /> The bar is where so much happens. Tonight a Dusk courtier by the name of Moire came up to me and said that the pursuer knows about my sister and that he has acquired a bird of prey. The words made my blood run cold. I questioned the woman a little bit to find out who she was and how she knew this. She told me her name and court and that she is a seer. She said that she saw this and wanted to warn me of what was coming. After she left I told Gawain and he called Jack to verify that Moire is in fact a Dusk courtier and seer. He confirmed that she is both. He also said that her predictions usually have a little bit of lead time so it will not likely come to pass in the very immediate future. So, we have time to prepare. I talked over possible options with Gawain and we came up with a few. I could tell Elena that we overheard something said at the bar that concerned her and wanted to warn her of possible trouble. The question as to why someone would go after her would come up and we don\u2019t have a good reason in mind. On the flip side we could tell Elena what we are and show her our true selves and let her know that she is in danger because she is my friend. I am a target and someone might use her to draw me out. The good thing about this plan is that it is the truth. Nothing that comes up later will refute what we say so we won\u2019t get caught in a lie later on. I just won\u2019t mention that she is my sister. She has been happily believing that the fetch is her Jacob. Who am I to disillusion her? The last option that we came up with was to have Insincere Marguerite check in Elena\u2019s mirrors and make sure that she is okay now. I was wholeheartedly behind that plan for tonight.<br /> <br /> So, Gawain looked around the room and saw how things were going and sent out a text message to the motley that we needed to meet after all of the customers had left. Left to their own devices I think most everyone would have split off in pairs or more and headed off to their respective bedrooms. I hated to spoil everyone\u2019s mood, but the information I had was important and the others needed to know about it, especially Lorelei. So, after everyone except Becky had left we had our talk. Becky waited downstairs while we talked upstairs in one of the rooms. The result was pretty much as I expected. Everyone got serious. Calamity looked mad, and Lori was a combination of in shock and terrified. She was often guarded by Hunting Hawk, which is who we believe the \u201cbird of prey\u201d in Moire\u2019s prophecy to be. Lori for her part went out on the balcony to get some fresh air while the rest of us discussed options. Calamity mentioned that since this was a possible threat to the freehold she was oath bound to tell Dahlia about it. I agreed that the Winter king needed to know and called Lowjack. I explained to him what I was told and what we thought it meant. He asked if we wanted to take care of it ourselves, let Darke handle it, or work with Darke to capture Rook and Hunting Hawk. If we handled it ourselves he said that he wanted a pledge from the lot of us that we will do our utmost to capture and/or kill them. I told him that I\u2019d have to talk things over with the motley and he said that he needed to know first thing tomorrow what we\u2019d decided. Makes sense to me. He would have to move fast to put people and/or resources in place. While I was on the phone Insincere Marguerite checked in on Elena\u2019a mirrors and found her to be asleep with a friend sleeping on her couch. So, she is safe. I am glad.<br /> <br /> After I got off the phone with Lowjack I told them what he said. We talked things over for a bit. Gawain even brought up De La Rocha\u2019s idea of going into Arcadia to rescue Lori\u2019s friends while Hunting Hawk was in \u2018the world.\u2019 It seemed like a good idea, but had one problem. It left things open for Hunting Hawk to come in to Arcadia after us and block us from getting back out. We agreed that we needed to take care of Hunting Hawk before we could make our run on Arcadia to free the two girls still there. After that discussion we talked about what we wanted to do with Rook and Hunting Hawk. I think Calamity was all for just killing them outright, but I explained again that I wanted to try and give Rook the opportunity to leave the Lady\u2019s service of his own free will. He was a friend for many years. I hate to have to fight him. I will if I have to though. Lori expressed a similar wish that Hunting Hawk be given a second chance. We weren\u2019t sure that Hawk would be interested in changing sides. He doesn\u2019t have the same kind of close relationship that Rook and I had. He just saw the girls as a distraction for the Violet Empress\u2019s affections. On more than one occasion he called Lorelei a whore. If he had been a Knight of the Lady\u2019s and said something like that of one of her Treasures he would die a long and painful death.<br /> <br /> In fact, there was one man years ago, at least years ago in Arcadia, that had been brought before the Lady so she could decide what she wanted done with him. He had managed to harm one of her Knights in a fight. He was captured and brought before Her and the court. We were all summoned to the court, Knight, servant and Treasured alike. I can\u2019t remember what his initial crime was, but I do remember why and how he died. He was desperate to escape and managed to get away from the Knight restraining him, taking a knife from the man\u2019s belt as well. In a bid to be let out of the palace alive he grabbed one of the Lady\u2019s Treasures and pulled him in front of his body to use as a shield. The doomed man had put the knife to the Treasure\u2019s throat and threatened to kill the man if he was not let out of the palace. I have rarely seen the Lady so angry. Well, maybe when she found out about my betrayal. She was pretty mad about that. Anyway, the escapee started walking backwards pulling the Treasure with him when he suddenly came upon Rook. Rook stepped out of the shadows and swiftly and cleanly disarmed the man before handing off the knife to me and restraining the escapee again. The Treasure was not hurt, but he was rather shaken. The Lady was livid. She ordered that the man be brought to her dungeons and that she would deal with him personally. We could hear the man\u2019s screams for days after that. At the time I wondered what the Lady was doing to him to make him cry out so, but now I have a pretty good idea of what she did. The Lady took attacks or insults to her Treasures as attacks or insults against herself, and dealt with them accordingly. Those that used such crude insults against her Treasured were rarely seen again.<br /> <br /> We discussed the situation a little bit longer before all agreeing that we needed to sleep on it before we came up with a plan of action. We were all kind of leaning in the direction where we take care of the situation ourselves with some help from others in the freehold, likely Darke. After everyone started heading to their respective rooms I made a quick stop to my room to grab my knives and stopped Calamity who was on her way to the gym downstairs. She looked like she needed to work out some frustration and anger, and I know I did so I suggested that we spar. It was probably the most intense and quiet sparring match we\u2019ve ever had. Neither of us felt up to banter, or pointing out weaknesses in defense, we just fought hard and brutal. Both of us ended up with multiple cuts and bruises from our sparring match, but we barely made any noise when we got them. Maybe a slight grunt or hiss of pain, but for the most part we just pushed through the discomfort and kept going until we were exhausted. Afterwards we just nodded at each other and went to our respective rooms to clean up and sleep. I think we both needed that.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> We had agreed last night that keeping up appearances was important, so Lorelei despite feeling scared, went to church this morning as is her usual habit. De La Rocha went with her for support, and I believe that Insincere Marguerite followed them to keep an eye on them just in case. It seemed the prudent thing to do. We need Rook and Hunting Hawk to believe that we don\u2019t know that they have plans against us, or that we have plans of our own against them. The more we can predict their moves the better for us, and we\u2019ll be able to do that if we can control what happens and when, with our daily lives. Besides it would be to our benefit to lure them into a false sense of security.<br /> <br /> Today\u2019s breakfast was a serious affair as we continued our discussion on Rook and Hunting Hawk. We went back over the ideas brought up last night and decided that we did want to deal with it ourselves, but see about getting Darke\u2019s help in carrying out our plan. I\u2019m not sure any of us were super keen on working with Darke on this, but he is very good at his job, and his job is finding loyalists. I do not like the man, but I will trust him to do his utmost to capture Rook and Hunting Hawk. The others agreed with me, so I called Lowjack and told him that we\u2019d decided on what we wanted to do. I explained our plan, and he said that he could set up a meeting with us and Darke to go over the particulars. He also said that he would be there if we wanted. I said that would be a good idea. Plan of action in hand, we met with Darke and Lowjack thirty minutes later.<br /> <br /> The meeting with Darke was actually rather cordial. We were all focused on the situation at hand and did our best to work out a plan of action. Darke said that he knew about Hunting Hawk. He sent Vik to keep an eye on him in L.A. Apparently Hawk is getting used to \u2018the world\u2019 and discovering just how different things are. For one, he cannot fly here. His abilities are also somewhat limited as well. I remember the first time the Lady sent me to \u2018the world\u2019 to do recon on a potential acquisition. I had to get used to the idea that my powers were muted somewhat from what they\u2019d been in Arcadia, and things just felt weird, different. It took some getting used to. After a couple days of acquainting myself with how things are in \u2018the world\u2019 I got on with my mission. Anyway, Darke knows where Hunting Hawk is, but does not know where Rook is, though he knows that Hawk has been in contact with someone in L.A. recently. It is possible that he\u2019s communicating with my former brother in arms. <br /> <br /> During our discussion we agreed that we would not go ahead and scoop up Hunting Hawk even though we know exactly where he is. We need him to lead us to Rook, so we will leave him free for the moment. We also talked about ways to lure Rook out and get him to enact his plan. It is unlikely that he will actually hurt Elena. His target is me, and Hunting Hawk\u2019s is Lorelei. So, my theory is that he will use Elena to lure me out so I will go to her rescue. He can then attack me or have Hawk do it. I\u2019m not sure of their plan to lure Lori out, unless they hope to get the lot of us. I know he is a good fighter, but taking on the whole motley, plus Luna, would be suicide. There are at least five seasoned fighters among that group and it would just be the two of them. Unless Rook has gathered allies he would be better served trying to get me alone. We\u2019ll see how it goes though.<br /> <br /> One idea that Darke mentioned was that there was an art display in downtown L.A. We could have someone disguise themselves as Elena, maybe Davie, and go to the art show. This would give Rook an opportunity to capture \u201cElena\u201d, or whatever else he has planned, while keeping my real sister safe. This option would probably necessitate me telling Elena what I actually am and what is going on, but I am willing to do that. I do not think that she would react too badly to the revelation of what we are. I don\u2019t know if I\u2019m going to mention being her brother or not. I don\u2019t know if I should. I suppose I can ask my motley mates what they think I should do. I know that Lori has had success in telling her father what she is, so maybe Elena would be accepting of who I am as well. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> <u><b><b>Colloquy</b></b></u><br /> <br /> <br /> Maria de la Rocha leaned on the door to the bathroom in the henhouse. She looked at Insincere Marguerite DeLisle, who stood in the doorway of her own room, and Julia Oldacre, who was pacing in the hall. The sound of the shower was audible, and the pleasant clean smell was emerging, but the three women had no trouble hearing each other.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019s scared. We need to protect her. We can be with her all the time. Even in the bathroom if needs be.\u201d<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite pushed out of the doorway, to lean bonelessly against the wall next to the Latina. \u201cWe will. I have personally declared her under my protection.\u201d Blue eyes looked deeply into brown.<br /> <br /> \u201cI know, but I am worried. I won\u2019t admit in front of her but\u2026I don\u2019t know anything about this Hunting Hawk. I know Jules is afraid of him. Very afraid.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe often irrationally fear the minions of our Keepers. They seem near invulnerable, omniscient. We fear them. But they are like us. Only more pathetic.\u201d Green eyes looked from brown to blue.<br /> <br /> \u201cI also need to protect you from Yvette.\u201d This time the brown-eyed women pointed at blue. \u201cWe don\u2019t know her goals, but I suspect they are to kill you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe won\u2019t.\u201d Green eyes darkened.<br /> <br /> \u201cJulia is absolutely correct.\u201d Insincere Marguerite\u2019s airy French accent was harder to hear over the shower, but both girls managed. \u201cI know Yvette as well as she knows herself. She cannot kill me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m not willing to bet on that.\u201d The accent this time was Latin American. \u201cJules is willing to let me guard her. You need to be too, Mags. I mean, mind yourself of course, but please let me keep a watch.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat are you intending?\u201d The artist moved to lean against the door to her room, opposite the Latina and her fianc\u00e9e.<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t have a precise plan. He is a stalker though. I was a stalker. I know how to watch. Separation from the herd. Fatigue from fear, from running. It was my Durance.\u201d The Latina\u2019s voice was low.<br /> <br /> The French woman moved in front of her. Blue eye met brown. \u201cIs this\u2026part of yourself you should be channeling? You have repressed that Maria for a very long time.\u201d The Darkling cocked her head, looking up slightly at the Leechfinger. \u201cI would not want it to\u2026overtake you.\u201d<br /> <br /> The Nightsinger\u2019s eyebrow quirked. A small nibble of her lip.<br /> <br /> \u201cAh, you are sweet Mags but\u2026no. I mean, I am not schizophrenic. I do remember my Durance. Unfortunately, as I have gotten stronger I remember it better.\u201d She broke eye contact to look to her right. \u201cI don\u2019t have to feel instincts to remember them.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIf you say so.\u201d The Lurker seemed unconvinced, but moved from in front of the Latina, sitting in a boneless pile on the floor. Meanwhile the green-eyed Artist paced watching her lovers very carefully.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnyway, main thing is, we stick together, we get through this.\u201d De La Rocha sounded confident, and she was. \u201cLori and I will go to church together tomorrow, but we will all stay close otherwise.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s a good idea. Let her take some solace and comfort from her faith.\u201d Julia nodded.<br /> <br /> \u201cI will come along in show, hein? I can remain mostly out of sight and disappear quickly, but if something does happen I can be a third defender from the shadows.\u201d Blue eyes glanced up at brown.<br /> <br /> \u2018Or warn the others if we get grabbed and pulled away somehow.\u201d The Leechfinger nodded.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s not going to happen, you said so yourself.\u201d Julia\u2019s voice was challenging.<br /> <br /> The Latina looked exasperated. \u201cIt\u2019s dumb not to have a plan ready. We all need to stick together and support each other. Just if you tail us remember Yvette is out there-\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI am not even sure Lorelei noticed Bon-Bon and I are even in the room most of the evening. It\u2019s hard to be supportive when you barely exist to her. There is you, and there is only you.\u201d The green-eyed Artist pointed almost accusingly at Maria, interrupting her. \u201cBon-Bon and I will protect her, but I am not going to lie to myself and say we have any significance to her right now.\u201d <br /> <br /> \u201cI agree that would be nice, but relationships are not about supporting people at their best, Julia.\u201d De La Rocha was calm, her brown eyes steely. \u201cI mean nothing by this except what I say when I say you are new to really being in a relationship, and being in a relationship means supporting the other person even when they are being an absolute shit, as long as they are not abusive, and Jules is being neither an absolute shit nor abusive.\u201d A sigh. \u201cInsensitive sure, but she is afraid for her damn life. Most of us would be.\u201d Brown eyes met green.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite rose and put skinny arms around Julia. The Artist put her head on the shorter woman\u2019s shoulder, or approximated it as best she could. Blue eyes gave an appreciative look to brown. Julia turned slightly. \u201cSorry.\u201d<br /> <br /> The Witchtooth was dismissive. \u201cAh, it\u2019s nothing. Don\u2019t worry. As I say, we are all in a relationship, and we support each other. That means me for you when you get jealous. Just don\u2019t get psycho-jealous.\u201d<br /> <br /> Julia chuckled despite herself. \u201cDo I seem psycho-jealous?\u201d<br /> <br /> Both other women looked at her. There was an uncomfortable silence.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell I am not going to hurt any of us!\u201d She sounded exasperated. De La Rocha and Insincere Marguerite gave each other a look. The Blue eyed one smiled slightly.<br /> <br /> The water stopped.<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay main thing is, half of us are in potential danger, and we all need to let this make us stronger, not push us apart. We need to be there for each other.\u201d The brown-eyed woman switched back to her more authoritative voice when she heard the shower had ended.<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course,\u201d Julia nodded, she looked to her fianc\u00e9e, who smiled lovingly at her.<br /> <br /> The brown-eyed girl looked back. \u201cTrust me, Timebomb, she will notice.\u201d<br /> <br /> Before Julia could respond Lorelei Grace emerged, a towel wrapped around her, her black eyes afraid. She was, Insincere Marguerite reminded herself, the most beautiful changeling she had ever\u2026loved.<br /> <br /> \u201cHow are you?\u201d The green-eyed girl spoke first.<br /> <br /> \u201cBeen better.\u201d A weak smile. \u201cI don\u2019t think I am up to any\u2026you know.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s fine.\u201d The colors spoke in unison.<br /> <br /> Maria de la Rocha put her arms around Lorelei and Insincere Marguerite. \u201cDon\u2019t worry ladies, as long as I am here, you two have nothing to worry about. Lori leaned against her lover and closed her eyes. Insincere Marguerite squirmed like an unhappy cat in arms to squeeze out of the Latina grip, until she felt the firmness of the bicep against her. Despite herself, she smiled a moment.<br /> <br /> Perhaps Maria can be allowed certain little displays, she thought.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXX</i><br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite would be deeply offended if I did not note she actually did a monologue on stage , playing the befuddled foreigner with the strong accent talking about the Christmas decorations in a red and green striped floppy tophat and matching socks. Did not get as many successes as the Bloody Creature Poster Girl team, but did okay for herself.<br /> <br /> Lorelei, Calamity, and Insincere Marguerite boosted performances with Verdant Spring, Calamity having it cast on her Lori and Insincere Marguerite boosting themselves. Calamity and Lori also used Vainglory, and Calamity got a die from her Goblin Vow with Blood to make the audience hot blooded. She ha to shed blood in passion after, which with the mood killed lead to the sparring.<br /> <br /> This is a slightly difficult story to do given the themes of <i>Malibu Dream House</i>. One thing going on as a recurring idea is that in the Lady by the Sea Freehold, some of those who fight Loyalists are scarier and frankly more evil than the Loyalists themselves. The times Loyalists or potential Loyalists have come up, they tend to be more sympathetic than the Loyalist hunters. Compare Desiree or Chalcedony to Lucian Torrez, Master Darke, Doctor Bright, or Twitch. Even some non-hunters, like Madame Spidertoes, Tommy Rawhead, Leanne, or the Handmaidens seems to be dangerous customers, or generally frightening or offputting somehow. Even some PCs struggle with their demons, be it Insincere Marguerite\u2019s fighting Gentrihood, Calamity fighting becoming an utter monster, and Jacob\u2019s trying to thaw. These internal struggles are more how the claws of Arcadia grasp at the PCs. This is a deliberate deviation from the usual presentation in <b>Changeling: The Lost</b>, though the Loyalists goals are still horrible and must be foiled, and the Gentry are of course truly frightening. But after Loyalists played a huge role in <i>Beyond the Sea</i>, my last <b>Changeling</b> campaign, I wanted something different.<br /> <br /> But these Loyalist foes exist, and really, it was time they appeared. They won\u2019t become campaign villains; The Motley would be wise to fear others of their kind more than these hunters, or at the very least, those wolves in sheep\u2019s clothing that can appear thus. Still, no harm in making them sweat a little.<br /> <br /> Apparently Master Darke\u2019s low drawl was irritable for players to impersonate.<br /> <br /> Okay I think that covers it. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T15:28:03-08:00","id":1012210,"title":"","content":"I was wondering when Rook would come up again. Your reasons for not focusing on the Loyalist enemies make a ton of sense and I've been enjoying all of the entries, but it had seemed like a lot of other shoes were taking their sweet time to drop, with everything being very slice-of-life. Heck, I don't think Rook had been mentioned at all in the past few entries, which was a bit weird considering how big a role it seemed like he was going to have in the story. Speaking of time anyway, how long has it been in-game since Rook escaped Darke's clutches? If it's been a few months, Jacob might be right to fear that he actually has gathered some allies.<br /> <br /> Also, speaking of weirdness, is it just me, or is the Lady by the Sea Freehold sort of uncomfortably almost allied with the Director, at least in the case of stopping the Grand Maw? I have only played one game of Changeling, so I don't know if these temporary and tenuous alliances are more common than I thought in high-level campaigns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 12-12-2016, 06:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T17:49:14-08:00","id":1012893,"title":"","content":"Just because the Freehold and the Director share a goal of stopping the Grand Maw doesn't make them Allies. There has been no actual cooperation between them. If Hollywood had not captured and reprogrammed Desir\u00e9e as a spy who then got help rather than killed we would not know about the Director's intention to stop Hollywood. <br /> <br /> That said, I suppose someone might suggest actually working with Him... But it ain't gonna be Calamity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T15:20:43-08:00","id":1016275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amberghylles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play?p=1012893#post1012893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because the Freehold and the Director share a goal of stopping the Grand Maw doesn't make them Allies. There has been no actual cooperation between them. If Hollywood had not captured and reprogrammed Desir\u00e9e as a spy who then got help rather than killed we would not know about the Director's intention to stop Hollywood.<br /> <br /> That said, I suppose someone might suggest actually working with Him... But it ain't gonna be Calamity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Point taken. Still want to know how long it's been since the night of the battle against the forces of The Mothership. 2 months? 3 months? half a year?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T16:32:50-08:00","id":1016308,"title":"","content":"I am going to ballpark like 5 months-ish. I think that happened in early summer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T16:45:49-08:00","id":1016315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroness Nerak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play?p=1016308#post1016308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am going to ballpark like 5 months-ish. I think that happened in early summer.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> thank you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T23:03:41-08:00","id":1019086,"title":"","content":"And then sometimes a game goes in a completely unexpected direction.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite is a short fic which takes place at the end of the session, parallel what others are talking about doing during the last bit.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LXXI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Okay, so maybe things are starting to look up. I\u2019m still terrified by the fact that Hunting Hawk and Rook are out there, and I can\u2019t claim that I\u2019m <u>pleased</u> with the way my friends handled our most recent crisis\u2026 but I think I\u2019m starting to get a handle on the situation, and my panic is beginning to recede.<br /> <br /> Jacob texted his sister Elena during the afternoon, hoping he could meet with her to bring her into the fold regarding his status as a changeling and thus give her some idea of what she\u2019s up against while Rook is stalking her. Unfortunately, she was reluctant to even speak with him, sending terse responses about how it \u201cwasn\u2019t a good time to talk.\u201d Of course this just made him more worried, and he began to insist that they meet. She eventually agreed, so long as he came to meet with her alone.<br /> <br /> This sent up red flags for all of us, of course. Gawain agreed to head to Elena\u2019s place with Jacob. He said he\u2019d stay outside so as not to alarm the girl, but that way he\u2019d be close enough to help if Jacob needed backup. So Jacob walked into his sister\u2019s apartment alone\u2026 and into one of the strangest plot twists any of us had ever encountered.<br /> <br /> Elena\u2019s houseguest is a Ukrainian girl named Natasha. Her father is apparently politically important back home, and she was visiting relatives in the States when some sort of trouble broke out in the Mother Country. Now Russian intelligence agents are trying to capture her to use as leverage against her father. She knew she was being followed by at least one such agent, and suspected that there might be more of them. She had taken refuge with Elena because her English is not so good, and Elena was one of the few people she had met in the States who speaks Russian. Now they were pretty sure the apartment was under surveillance, and both girls were afraid to leave.<br /> <br /> Though perhaps not the best time for it, Jacob decided to play his trump card. He told Elena that he was a changeling, and told her that if she would trust him, he could get the two of them out of the building unobserved by any mortal force. Though both girls were hesitant to accept his admittedly crazy-sounding plan, they agreed that they had little choice in the end. Jacob created a gate to the Hedge, called Gawain, and a few minutes later the four of them arrived at the Dream House.<br /> <br /> Once the rest of us were caught up on the situation, we held a quick motley meeting and agreed that we needed to enchant the two mortal girls so that they could get the full picture of what was going on. As I pointed out, Elena needs to be able to recognize Rook when and if she sees him. I think it was Jacob\u2019s idea to craft a pledge which would allow the two girls to see changelings as we really are\u2026 and in return would allow the rest of us to speak and understand Russian, so that we could communicate directly with Natasha.<br /> <br /> The two of them took it\u2026 remarkably well, all things considered. Both girls were obviously a little freaked out by the whole revelation, but neither one reacted with violence or disbelief, and both accepted that we\u2019re the good guys in this situation. Natasha thanked us for our help, and promised to offer her own help when the time comes to deal with Rook and Hawk.<br /> <br /> We allowed as how it would be okay for the girls to take in the show, as the people following them would have no reason to look for them at the Dream House. Calamity and I reprised our \u201cBloody Creature Poster Girl\u201d number, and it went <u>very</u> well\u2026 possibly even better than it had at the premiere. With the two of us both giving our all to every performance, it pretty much ensures a number the audience will remember for the rest of their days\u2026 especially with the amount of glamour we were throwing around. It\u2019s a good thing emotions run high during that particular act, or we\u2019d both be operating at a deficit.<br /> <br /> Oh, and Marguerite performed a little comic monologue on stage as well, playing the French tourist confused by American customs and other such tropes. It was the second time she\u2019s done it, and once again it went over quite well. I meant to mention that in my last entry, but I was (perhaps understandably) distracted by other matters at the time.<br /> <br /> In any case, I really wasn\u2019t up to my usual evening of schmoozing and drinking in the adoration, so my plan was to make the rounds quickly and then retreat upstairs with my girls. I had sort of tearfully confessed to Julia earlier that day that I was particularly afraid for her, since the Empress loves talented singers, and her voice is so lovely, so she knew that I was feeling vulnerable, and started steering things in that direction almost as soon as I got off the stage.<br /> <br /> However, there was one guest in the audience who required special attention. None other than Lord Leonidas, the leader of the area\u2019s Day Court contingent, had decided to grace our establishment with his presence. Now, considering the history between him and Marguerite, I thought it might be best if we cleared the air between us.<br /> <br /> Apparently he had the same idea. He was remarkably forthright and direct in his speech, but seemed pretty even-tempered for the most part. He was a Beast-type changeling. His head was that of a lion, which was more than a little intimidating, but he seemed to be doing his best to put us all at ease. He was speaking with Marguerite when Calamity and I arrived at the table, and he was quick to assure us that the Dream House had nothing to fear from him, despite his recent challenges to our French comrade. In point of fact, he denied trying to kill Marguerite a year ago, and implied that she might want to look at members of her own court for that little offense (namely the Handmaidens).<br /> <br /> He was highly complimentary of our little cabaret, and promised that he would visit again soon. I tried to show him the deference due to a monarch (called him \u201cmy lord\u201d and such), but he waved it off as \u201cappreciated but unnecessary.\u201d In all honesty, I think Calamity was more impressed with him than I was\u2026 she was eyeing him like a rare steak by the end of our conversation.<br /> <br /> So as usual I planted myself in Maria\u2019s lap after I\u2019d spent an appropriate amount of time playing the social butterfly. When her strong arms are around me, the fear goes away for a while, and I know I\u2019m as safe as I can be. Marguerite and Julia were similarly engaged, and when the club started to empty, the four of us made our way upstairs to bed. Things between us were tender and comforting, and all four of us drifted off to sleep much earlier than usual\u2026 I was finally able to relax for a bit while the three of them surrounded me.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, a blissfully restful night was not in the cards for me. I awoke a couple of hours later to an insistent pounding on the door of Marguerite and Julia\u2019s room. I think I said something witty, like \u201cwhuzzit\u201d in response, and Gawain\u2019s urgent reply was that I was needed downstairs for healing, and that the matter was critical. <u>That</u> woke me up.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t have time to find a robe that would cover me (obviously I can\u2019t wear the other girls\u2019 robes since I have to accommodate my wings), so I grabbed a towel from the bathroom and wrapped it around myself as we headed downstairs. What I saw was both sobering and upsetting\u2026 Natasha had been shot, and her wounds were serious. I looked at the simple improvised bandage Jacob had been holding to the wound.<br /> <br /> \u201cWho dressed this?\u201d I asked as I gathered my glamour for the healing.<br /> <br /> \u201cI did,\u201d Jacob said softly, backing away to give me space.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou saved her life,\u201d I said tersely. \u201cGood work.\u201d<br /> <br /> Luckily, the bullet had passed through her body cleanly; there was no debris to dig out. There was a lot of blood though, and I\u2019m pretty sure even more was seeping into her punctured lung. The bullet also cracked one of her ribs as it passed, unless I miss my guess. I poured as much glamour as I could into her body, trying to guide the healing energies to the places they were most needed. It took a couple of tries, but in the end I breathed a sigh of relief and wiped the sweat off my brow.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe should be okay now,\u201d I said as I took the proffered bathrobe from my honey\u2019s outstretched arms and slipped into it. \u201cShe\u2019s going to have one hell of a bruise in the morning, but it\u2019ll heal pretty quickly.\u201d<br /> <br /> Once she was sleeping it off, Calamity attempted to explain what had happened, but to be honest I didn\u2019t want to know. The gist of it was that she, Natasha, Jacob and Luna had gone back to Elena\u2019s apartment to see if they could catch Natasha\u2019s stalkers in the act and deal with them in a more permanent fashion. In the ensuing fracas, Natasha was shot. I am told that the people who were watching her are no longer an issue, and she believes that whoever is behind this kidnapping attempt is likely to give it up as a bad idea now.<br /> <br /> So I went back to bed a smidge more tense and grumpy than I had been, but still surrounded by people who love me and relatively assured of my own safety. This time we were allowed to sleep the morning through until it was time for sex breakfast\u2026 to which our new houseguests were of course invited. Natasha seemed to enjoy the experience, and gave as good as she got, but I think Elena got pretty embarrassed by the end of the meal.<br /> <br /> Since it\u2019s Monday, the motley has the day off, and we spent most of the day relaxing around the house and making tentative plans for how to deal with Rook and Hunting Hawk. It turns out that Elena <u>was</u> planning to attend that gallery showing in LA on Wednesday, so it sounds like that will be the perfect time for us to try to nab Rook\u2026 assuming he takes the bait. There was some back and forth among the motley about whether or not Elena should serve as said bait (I came down on the side of having Davie impersonate her, if you\u2019re wondering), but I don\u2019t think anything was decided. Once Rook is taken care of, we should be able to take down Hawk relatively quickly.<br /> <br /> Of course, I had something else to occupy my afternoon\u2026 Rowan got out of the clinic today! Maria insisted on accompanying me when I went to meet her there, and to be honest I wouldn\u2019t have had it any other way. She makes me feel safe, and I need that right now. Felicity was there when we arrived, and the three of us spoke pleasantly for a while until Rowan entered the waiting room. She was a little more subdued than usual, but I suppose that\u2019s not surprising.<br /> <br /> Felicity offered to take the three of us out for a nice lunch so that we could discuss what happens next. Over soup and salads, she told Rowan that she had secured a small apartment near her job, and that Rowan would be welcome to live there until she got back on her feet and found another place. Rowan accepted this generous offer, saying with a sideways glance at me and D that she didn\u2019t want to impose on us. I took her hand in mine.<br /> <br /> \u201cRowan, honey, you know you\u2019re always welcome to stay with me. Don\u2019t ever think of it as an imposition. But I think it will be good for you to get your own place\u2026 it might help the healing process.\u201d<br /> <br /> Rowan nodded. \u201cThe doctors at the clinic thought so too. And I can still come and visit you at the Dream House, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> I gave her one of my best smiles. \u201cOf course, any time you want. And I\u2019d love to see your new place once you have it set up the way you like it.\u201d D gave my hand a squeeze at that, which reminded me that I should probably let Rowan know what was going on in my life. \u201cNow, having said that, there\u2019s something I need to tell you, and I don\u2019t want you to freak out.\u201d<br /> <br /> Rowan\u2019s face fell slightly. \u201cIt\u2019s nothing dire, I promise,\u201d I said in response. \u201cIt\u2019s just that we\u2019ve gotten word that there\u2019s a Loyalist holing up in LA. One that works for my Keeper. He\u2019s probably in town hoping to bring me back to Arcadia.\u201d<br /> <br /> Both Rowan and Felicity made anxious noises, and Felicity went so far as to ask if I required the protection of the Day Court. I tried to reassure them as best I could. \u201cIt\u2019s okay,\u201d I said soothingly, fighting down my own fear for their sakes. \u201cI\u2019m not taking any unnecessary risks. That\u2019s why D is with me today; I\u2019m not traveling alone. My motley\u2019s working on the problem, and the Winter Court is aware of the issue. I\u2019ll be fine\u2026 but I probably won\u2019t be dropping by your new place until things are resolved.\u201d<br /> <br /> Rowan nodded. \u201cThat makes sense,\u201d she said. \u201cAnd I can still see you at the Dream House in the meantime. Say\u2026 tomorrow night?\u201d she asked hopefully.<br /> <br /> \u201cWouldn\u2019t miss it,\u201d I said, leaning in for a brief kiss.<br /> <br /> Things wound down after that, and Felicity and Rowan left to take a look at her new place. D and I headed back to the Dream House. So most of the rest of the day has been spent chatting and playing video games. I\u2019ve mostly amused myself by observing the ever-shifting social dynamic of the house. I feel like I should note two matters of concern before I bring this entry to a close.<br /> <br /> First, Calamity is quite fond of Natasha. I don\u2019t think I\u2019ve ever seen her take to someone so quickly\u2026 unless you count her instant attraction to Leonidas last night, I suppose, but this seems to be more of an emotional connection and less about pure sex for her. Under ordinary circumstances I\u2019d be fine with this\u2026 but I\u2019m also relatively certain that Natasha hasn\u2019t told us the whole truth about her current situation, and that could mean more trouble down the line.<br /> <br /> The second thing I noticed was even more disturbing. I\u2019ve told Jacob on several occasions that I think he should be honest with Elena about his identity, but he\u2019s resisted the notion. Well, this might be the time to force the issue. It looks to me as though Elena has a bit of a crush on Jacob, which is awkward in an Oedipal sort of way. I think Jacob picked up on it as well, so maybe he\u2019s reconsidering his stance on the issue.<br /> <br /> So the girls are staying with us for the next few days\u2026 at least until Rook is dealt with, which means that they\u2019ll be joining us later tonight for Movie Night. I\u2019m not sure what we\u2019re watching yet, but I\u2019m sure it\u2019ll be fun. Now if I could just get rid of this low level of background terror that still seems to permeate everything that I do, I\u2019d be sitting pretty. Hopefully by the next time I write anything in this journal, the situation with Rook and Hunting Hawk will be resolved.<br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei Grace</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> Monday,December 1st<br /> Nine years, six months, twenty-one days<br /> Days without stabbing: 0<br /> <br /> I killed a woman last night. I don\u2019t know her name. I think she was Russian. Really about the only thing I know for certain is that she was pretty. She had pale blue eyes like ice. I watched them go so wide as my glass caressed and parted her flesh. I savored the soft gasp of pain because she was too hardened to give up a proper scream. I watched the light in those pretty orbs flicker and go dim as her warm blood spilled over my hands. She deserved it. She was hunting Natasha along with the sandy haired man. She shot her and damned near killed her once it became clear they weren\u2019t going to capture her. I know she deserved it because her blood tasted like sin when I licked it from my glass. It was a good kill. It felt right. It felt good\u2026 so very good. There was no doubt in my mind. She fired that shot and sealed her fate. I was the Calamity she deserved and I ended her as was right and proper and just. As I was meant to.<br /> <br /> Yeah, that is exactly what I felt last night when it happened. No remorse. No guilt. I killed her and I enjoyed it. There was nothing but the monster. And the whole sense of\u2026 purpose? Of right. Not just that it was right for her to be punished but that it was right for me to do it. I am not sure where that came from exactly but it scares me. I let myself become lost in it. That wasn\u2019t human. That was Fae. Hell, I am still way too calm about the whole thing even now. I mean, I killed that woman. I should feel\u2026 something. Maybe I\u2019m in shock or some shit. Maybe it\u2019s just that there isn\u2019t time for me to deal with it beyond the rational. Maybe. Or maybe I am just a broken sadistic monster.<br /> <br /> No. That thinking doesn\u2019t help. I have to be reasonable. I have to look at this objectively so I can deal with it. So I can change it. So I can control it. I was so out of control last night. I thought I had a handle on this. So what in the ever loving hell happened? It hit me hard and it just wouldn\u2019t let up. Even the forms didn\u2019t entirely help. I was more focused but I was still off the rails.<br /> <br /> It was reckless to go in like we did. It was careless and if not for Jacob\u2019s quick first aid and Lori\u2019s Spring magic Natasha would have wound up dead. I am supposed to be fucking better than that but I wanted it. I wanted the hunt. I needed the prey. I should have kept that urge in check. But I wanted it so badly. And Natasha was so eager to go after them. And yes, I did want to show off for her. That girl reminds me way to much of my Anastasia. The fire and fearless devil may care attitude. That cocky determination. But she isn\u2019t my Stasia. It\u2019s not right for me to project those feeling on her. Just because she\u2019s here and she thinks Calamity is cool. Just because she acts the way I want Stasia to when I reconnect with her.<br /> <br /> This isn\u2019t right. It isn\u2019t fair to her. It\u2019s reckless and dangerous. I\u2019m acting like a fool to impress her and it could have ended much worse than it did. I have got to reign it in and stop coming at her like a freight train. I mean, she does seem to be into me but pressuring her while she\u2019s under my protection is wrong. And the fact that I am chasing a ghost that she reminds me of rather than actually being interested in her is wrong.<br /> <br /> I need to find Stasia. I have to face her. This mess with Natasha is just proof. I am never going to be able to just walk away from her without some closure. I can push it down but something brings it back and it\u2019s not the least bit diminished. My feelings for her run deep and strong and I cannot ignore them. I have to do this before I can commit to anything with Becky. Hell, I can\u2019t honestly commit to Gawain while this is lingering inside me. Back in Snow Globe Stasia was the one thing I could never bring myself to give up. I couldn\u2019t forget her. At my weakest moments, I endured rather than surrender. I was prepared to die rather than forget her.<br /> <br /> And that\u2019s what scares the shit of me about finding her. If she\u2019s bitter and broken and hates me for what my fetch did it will hurt me worse than They could have ever dreamed of. But what if she\u2019s put it behind her? What if she\u2019s over it? What if she\u2019s just moved on with her life? As horrible as it would be to see hate in her eyes, it would kill me if there was nothing there.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite knows where she is. She tracked her down and sent her a mirror. She\u2019s looked in on her. She says she\u2019s fine. I had assumed that she hadn\u2019t had a chance to look before things happened with Chalcedony because she hadn\u2019t said anything to me about it. Why didn\u2019t she tell me she\u2019d found Stasia? Why didn\u2019t she let me know? What is she hiding from me? When I asked her she was so nonchalant about it. She just said that of course she\u2019d looked since she\u2019d said she would. Since she is my friend.<br /> <br /> It felt good to hear her call me that. But now\u2026 now I\u2019m consumed with these doubts. She had to know how much this means to me. So why did she keep it to herself?<br /> <br /> Stop it Kat. If she was hiding something she wouldn\u2019t have told me that she\u2019d found Stasia. Things did go to shit between us. She said she\u2019d looked in on her. If there was something there, she would have either told me or she\u2019d have kept it from me. And as weird as I get about Stasia maybe she felt it would be best to check on her for me and not send me off the deep end by bringing her up. Maybe she wasn\u2019t finished getting a good idea of things. I can\u2019t just jump to conclusions. I have to talk to her about this and ask her why.<br /> <br /> Breathe. You were crazy yesterday. You were pressuring poor Natasha when she she was tired and afraid. You threw yourself at Leonidas like a whore in heat. Gods above and below that was embarrassing. The man was here trying to clear the air. And as much as I hate to admit it, his claim that he wasn\u2019t the one that tried to kill Insincere Marguerite makes sense. That is more the Handmaidens\u2019 style than his. Not that coming after her with a posse to beat the shit out of her would have been any sort of fair fight but it does seem to fit with what I know about him and the Day Court better.<br /> <br /> Breathe. Yesterday was not a good day. But it was the first time some of this was really brought out in a while. You didn\u2019t handle it with flawless grace. You made mistakes. Mistakes are human. Human like you. You will do better. Tomorrow we talk to Dr Emmett. She\u2019ll help look at how things went wrong. We\u2019ll find a way to do better next time.<br /> <br /> I am stronger than this. I can control myself. I will control myself.<br /> <br /> I need to let Calamity go. I need to find a way to be Kat again. I need to take my name back.<br /> <br /> I cannot continue to be so reckless and chaotic. Handsome and I are going to help Desiree and the two of them are talking about relationships. I need to sort myself out. This is serious and I am going to fuck it all the hell up for everyone if I can\u2019t learn to reign in hurricane Calamity. I need to figure out what I want. What I need. I can\u2019t build a relationship if I\u2019m the unstable link.<br /> <br /> I should talk to Lori about how she manages. I know this seems like a terrible time for it, but maybe turning her thoughts away from the past and back to the future and what\u2019s right in her life would be good for her.<br /> <br /> Tonight is movie night. I have no idea what we\u2019re watching but my family will be together for it. I need to make sure everything is ready. The show must go on.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> I\u2019m going to have to keep a low profile after today. It started out a little worrying and escalated from there. I texted Elena to see if we could get together later today to talk. I said that I had something important that I needed to talk to her about. She said that she couldn\u2019t come to the club later. She was very curt in her responses and a little vague. I asked if she could come over now and again she said that she couldn\u2019t come. I was starting to get worried so I asked Insincere Marguerite if she could look through Elena\u2019s mirrors and see what was going on. I may have interrupted something between Marguerite and Julia, but their door was open so I figured it was okay to knock and ask my favor. Insincere Marguerite looked through the mirrors and said that Elena and another girl were in the apartment and had a chair under the handle of the front door. This concerned me so I asked Elena if everything was okay. She again was vague in her answer, so I asked if I could come to her apartment to meet her. She said that I could come over, but had to be alone. This again was worrying to me, but I agreed. I told the rest of the group what was going on and Gawain said that he\u2019d come along with me in case I needed back up.<br /> <br /> We arrived at Elena\u2019s apartment shortly after I told Elena that I was on my way. Gawain stayed outside, but near the door while I went ahead and knocked. Elena answered the door, let me in then relocked the door and replaced the chair under the handle. I asked what was going on and Elena and her new friend Natasha explained it to me. It turns out that Natasha is a Ukrainian who came to the U.S to visit relatives and somehow met Elena. They became friends because Elena was one of the few people in the area that can speak Russian. Natasha explained that her father was someone important back in Crimea and that he had requested that she come home to be with her family. Apparently Natasha didn\u2019t want to go home, or felt that something was wrong. She was a bit vague on the details, though she was proud of being of Cossack heritage. But she did say that there was a Russian agent following her around and she had spotted him outside of Elena\u2019s apartment. That explained the locked and barred door.<br /> <br /> I offered to help them get out of Elena\u2019s apartment unseen but that I needed to explain something first. I then explained, badly, about Changelings and a little about the situation with Rook. I basically said that he might try and get to me through her. I said it was because we were friends, but almost told her the truth. In retrospect I should have told her then, but I thought that it wasn\u2019t the right time for that, so I left that bit of information out of the discussion. I reiterated that I could get them out of the apartment unseen but that they\u2019d have to trust me. They said that they could do that. I then told them about Gawain waiting outside and that it would be good if he came with us. So, they let him in and I opened a gate to the Hedge through the door to her kitchen. We waited a moment as soon as we\u2019d walked through the gate for the girls to get their bearings. They both seemed a bit shaken, but were okay other than that. I scouted the path ahead and had Gawain stay with the girls in case of trouble. We did not encounter anything dangerous on the way to the Dream House, for which I was thankful. We escorted the girls inside and introduced them to the rest of the motely and explained what was going on.<br /> <br /> We continued the discussion about Rook and how we planned on drawing him out by having someone disguise themselves as Elena and go to the Art Exhibit in L.A. Elena said that she had actually been planning on going to that show and volunteered to go and act as bait. I did not like that idea in the slightest and tried to explain that it could be dangerous. Elena stuck to her idea of acting as the bait. She always could be as stubborn as mom when she put her mind to it. I had forgotten about that. I guess there are a lot of things that I have forgotten about home and my family. I still have a lot of blanks but every once and awhile something will trigger a memory and I\u2019ll suddenly remember something, like Grandpa\u2019s birthday. We had gone back to Russia to celebrate it. It was a lot of fun. I\u2019ll admit that it was refreshing to be surrounded by people who spoke my native language. We got some trinkets for Grandpa that were obviously American as well as some good winter boots. I think he enjoyed the snow globe of the Space Needle in Seattle. Grandpa was 75 then, but that was three years ago in real time. I hope that he is still with us. Hopefully after I tell Elena about who I really am I can get some news about our family.<br /> <br /> After we talked about the art show in L.A. I proposed that we make a pledge with Elena and Natasha, though I phrased it differently than that. I wanted them to be able to see us as we are. Plus, I worked in something for my motley mates so they could speak Russian. I figured that would make conversing with Natasha that much easier. I am happy to say that besides an exclamation of surprise here and there, there was no negative reaction to what we actually look like. I think there was an \u201cOoo\u201d at Lorelei\u2019s wings and a bit of surprise at Calamity\u2019s glass, but that was about it. I think they\u2019re taking this whole thing rather well. Though I will admit at the beginning of the day I had not anticipated not only telling my sister about Changelings, but a complete stranger.<br /> <br /> Later in the afternoon, after the girls went off to lay down for a bit. It had been a long day already. Insincere Marguerite asked if she could talk to me. I said sure. Turns out that she wanted to talk to me about Elena. She suggested that it would be a good idea for me to tell Elena that I am her brother. She said that right now might not be the right time, but suggested that I tell her after all of this business with Rook is over so she can go back to her apartment to be alone to process everything if she wanted to. I thought that sounded like good advice and I said as much.<br /> <br /> As it turns out, Natasha reminds Calamity of her old childhood friend, Stasia, whom she had a crush on. So, tonight before the show Calamity was flirting rather blatantly with Natasha and the Ukrainian was flirting right back. Apparently Stasia was also something of a troublemaker back in the day and that also resonated with Calamity. We don\u2019t really know anything about Natasha. She has told us some things about her family, but it was all very vague. No specifics. I can\u2019t help but wonder what is really going on with that girl. She has already gotten my sister involved in International problems. I don\u2019t know what her real goals are. I hope Calamity, and everyone else for that matter, doesn\u2019t get hurt.<br /> <br /> The show went well. Insincere Marguerite reprised her monologue from last night about not understanding American customs, especially around the holidays. Little things like not being able to decorate for Christmas before Thanksgiving is over. Thanksgiving is an American holiday, so we were not limited in what date we can start decorating in our native countries. I thought it was funny since I could relate to a lot of what she was saying. Sometimes I still don\u2019t understand some American customs, and I\u2019ve lived here since I was twelve.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Lori and Calamity did an encore of their \u201cBloody Creature Poster Girl\u201d act tonight. And just as with the first time, it was well received and got a lot of applause. Lori did not do her usual amount of socializing afterwards though, but she did show her face here and there. One person that she specifically talked to was Leonidas. Insincere Marguerite also made her way over to his table to talk. For her part Marguerite stretched out and reclined on his table. Rather bold if I do say so myself. Anyway, it seems that he wanted to assure her that the Dream House did not need to fear any retribution from him because of her turning down his duel. He also implied that he didn\u2019t have anything to do with the building falling on her before we became a motley. It was suggested that the Handmaidens might have had something to do with that particular incident. I\u2019m not sure how much of what he said I believe. He seemed earnest enough, and it was decent of him to come by and let us know that he had no intentions of coming after the Dream House. The thought had crossed my mind I will admit.<br /> <br /> Calamity continued to flirt with Natasha after assuring that she and Elena had a good time at the show. About the same time Luna moved closer to me at the bar and asked about Elena and Natasha and if they were a couple. I explained the situation with them. That they were friends, but not dating each other. After that Luna suggested that she and I go looking for the man that was following Natasha and see what we could find out. Natasha overheard this and said that she had a picture of him if that would help. We said that it would. Calamity also came over and looked at the picture. She then said that she could find him using the picture and we could go directly to where he was. She used her scrying power and discovered that he was with a red headed woman and they were searching Elena\u2019s apartment. Calamity jumped on the back of her bike with Natasha carefully hanging on, while Luna and I followed in my jeep. It took a little bit of work to keep up with Calamity as she sped through town, but I managed it. We got to Elena\u2019s apartment in no time at all and all started sneaking up toward the door. I\u2019m not sure who they spotted, but they knew that someone was out there. The intruders upped the stakes by throwing a flash bang grenade out the door. It went off and temporarily blinded Natasha and Luna but not Calamity and I. We managed to look away in time to save our eyesight.<br /> <br /> The sandy haired man and red headed woman both came out of the apartment at the same time and Calamity and I rushed forward to incapacitate them. At least I was aiming to incapacitate. Calamity it seemed had different plans. Anyway\u2026 Calamity hit the guy with a quick attack and I knocked him out. In retaliation the woman shot Natasha, badly wounding her. I quickly ran to Natasha and started to use my shirt as a bandage. I ripped the bottom off so I could secure the makeshift bandage as tightly as possible. While I was working to save a life Calamity was doing her utmost to end one. She stabbed the woman then killed her when the woman was incapacitated. I do not think that was strictly necessary. From one perspective I can see why she did it. Well, I can see why I might have done it. The woman was a liability and could have caused problems later. I know that train of thought is not right. It\u2019s what Rime would have done, which is why I did not kill the sandy haired man, and I bandaged his wounds. I did not want to be responsible for the death of another human being. I do not know if Calamity was thinking strategically or just with her anger. My guess is the latter, and that\u2019s not a good thing.<br /> <br /> By that time we heard police cars arriving so I gathered up Natasha and we fled back into the apartment and reopened the hedge gate. We took the man with us and bandaged him on the other side then sent him back through. We knew that there was no way that he was going to tell us anything that we wanted to know so we decided to leave him behind to deal with the police. In retrospect we probably should have just dropped him off somewhere else so the police couldn\u2019t question him, but in the heat of the moment we didn\u2019t think too strategically. We just reacted. I have a bad feeling that this whole thing is going to come back and bite us in the ass later on.<br /> <br /> So, we came back through the hedge gate at the Dream House and rushed into the house. We saw Gawain, who was waiting for us, and told him that Natasha needed healing right away. It was bad. Gawain ran upstairs and grabbed Lori, who came downstairs wrapped in a towel. She quickly went to work healing the Ukrainian girl. She asked who bandaged her and I admitted that I had done it. She said that I had saved Natasha\u2019s life. I was happy that I\u2019d been able to help her. I don\u2019t know Natasha well at all but I didn\u2019t want to see her die. I just nodded my acknowledgement and backed away to give Lori more room to work. I didn\u2019t think that it was appropriate for me to bring up the fact that Rook is the one that taught me so much about first aid, and that I\u2019d had plenty of practice using it in the field. On more than one occasion Rook would get hurt and I bandaged him up and took him back to the Lady\u2019s realm. And on more than one occasion I bandaged myself up and hobbled on back to Arcadia. Not everyone that the Lady sent me after was an innocent, and not all of them were helpless. I met several people that defended themselves quite well. So, I\u2019d had my practice at field dressing wounds, and was just grateful at that moment that I\u2019d had the practice so I could do my part in helping Natasha. So, Lori managed to completely close up all of Natasha\u2019s wounds which just left bruises that would heal by morning. Sometimes I am in awe of Spring Court magic.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> So breakfast started off much like normal. There was the usual banter which Elena started to turn red at. It was then explained why we call it Sex Breakfast, or I should say it was over explained. I\u2019m pretty sure Elena learned more in ten minutes in our kitchen than she ever wanted to know. I don\u2019t blame her. I have lived with these guys for a while now and sometimes I still feel a flush coming on. I don\u2019t blush like a normal person any more, but I can feel it regardless.<br /> <br /> Also at breakfast Elena asked me if Natasha was okay. She said that her friend had been acting strange all morning. I told her that Natasha was fine, but had been shot at and hit last night. I did not go into details on how badly hit Natasha was, but left if vague. I did assure Elena that Lori had healed Natasha completely and that her friend was fine. It was after this that the over explaining happened and Elena eventually fled upstairs in embarrassment. And right after she left both Julia and Lori told me that I need to tell her that I\u2019m her brother. I agreed with both of them, but said that right this instant was not a good time. I don\u2019t know when a good time is going to be, but wanted to give it a little more time.<br /> <br /> After that Lorelei and De La Rocha left to go pick up Rowan from the clinic. She was getting out today and going to be moving into a new place, courtesy of Felicity. I thought that was rather nice of the Day courtier, but she does seem to feel protective and responsible of the other Day courtiers in town. Shortly have they left Gawain and Calamity went to go meet Desiree for ice cream. I thought it best if someone stayed at the house and made sure that Elena and Natasha were safe, so I volunteered to do that. I figured that something to take their minds off of what happened last night might be a good thing, so I asked if Elena and Natasha would like to play a video game. The girls were not big into gaming, and truth be told neither am I, but we agreed on Rock Band and picked out our instruments and started playing. Natasha sang, Elena played guitar and I played bass. It was fun. I am not the best bass player in the world but I held my own against the game. Natasha was a pretty good singer and Elena is not bad on guitar. After we quit playing the game we just hung around and talked. Other people were starting to come back at that point. It was around that point that I realized that Elena has the beginnings of a crush on me, and possibly Natasha. That is so not good. I need to nip that in the bud right off. Julia and Lori were right. I need to tell Elena who I really am before her feelings go any further.<br /> <br /> So, yeah. As soon as I put this book down I\u2019m having a little private conversation with my sister, and hope she forgives me for keeping things a secret for so long.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> <b><u>It\u2019s Pretty Much a Sex Thing, Yeah</u></b><br /> <br /> Julia Oldacre entered the spare room, taking a moment to lock the door after her fianc\u00e9e, Insincere Marguerite, followed. She watched the way the other woman moved, graceful, yet bizarre, as her shoulders and legs moved unnaturally, her steps almost flowed like a humanoid of water. Still, she was quite pretty, incredibly graceful and elegant, and her accent was enough to melt a girl\u2019s heart. Then there were her eyes. Julia spoke up before she could get lost in them.<br /> <br /> \u201cYour show last night was delightful, Bon-Bon.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you.\u201d The more petite Darkling replied with an affectionate smile. \u201cThat was probably my last silly little monologue for a while, but I enjoyed it, the audience enjoyed it, and it was a good distraction from everything going on, hein?\u201d She sat down on the couch.<br /> <br /> Julia nodded. \u201cThis has been crazy, Bon-Bon. Russian spies, seriously? As if it were not strange enough.\u201d<br /> <br /> The other woman shrugged, sitting and putting claw tips on the ends of her fingers on her right hand. \u201cIt makes sense to me. Rook must have noticed their activity. That is how he knew about Elena. Perhaps the Russian element got his attention. It makes more sense to me now, not less.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou think they are connected to Rook?\u201d The younger woman rummaged through her bag.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, but if they had lived, I bet they could have accidentally helped us stumble upon him. Or maybe he was there that night, to look for clues behind them once they helpfully opened the door.\u201d The feline lady looked at her hand, admiring the attached claws.<br /> <br /> \u201cDo you think Calamity would have noticed if he were there?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNon,\u201d The feline turned to her fianc\u00e9e. \u201cCalamity uses magic to hunt. People who have poor Clarity make poor hunters without it, as they have difficulty noticing things in their environment. It is a reason those who hunt among the Kind have to be careful of their own Clarity. Eventually, you kill for fun, your Clarity slips, and you don\u2019t see the knife at your back, or your quarry\u2019s trail. It\u2019s why few Changelings who hunt with little regard for their victims never last long. They die or wind up in Arcadia.\u201d<br /> <br /> The Artist was rummaging in her purse, thus missed the significant look from the Lurker. \u201cWhat do you think of her fixating on this Natasha?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe reminds her of her old, how do you say, \u2018not-girlfriend?\u2019\u201d Insincere Marguerite began applies the claws to the last couple fingers of her left hand. \u201cCalamity asked about my looking in on her back when we were friends. Not that we are not now to some degree. Calamity is intelligent enough to know the difference though. I am not worried.\u201d A thoughtful pause. \u201cMostly.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMostly?\u201d Julia pulled a lion half-mask from her bag, and was fluffing out the mane.<br /> <br /> \u201cI am not certain, and I do not have a theory per se, but I do not think Natasha is being honest with us, and I do not think Natasha is her real name. I could be mistaken but\u2026I do not think I am.\u201d The Tunnelgrub admired her other hand. \u201cI suspect she knows she has Calamity wrapped around her finger, but I don\u2019t think her facade is anything more than trying to make her more sympathetic. I mean, she could be a drug dealer who was hunted by gendarmes. But I don\u2019t think she is, say, Rook\u2019s agent or means us harm.\u201d<br /> <br /> Julia held the half-mask up and looked at it. \u201cYou don\u2019t really seem all that worried Bon-Bon. About the Loyalists I mean.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOne of the few advantages to living in this city of homicidal maniacs is there is a flush supply of acceptable victims in the form of Loyalists. If the Bridge-Burners ever succeed and close Arcadia off, I will flee. But right now? They are walking into a death trap full of fae eagerly waiting for them.\u201d She paused to look at the half-mask in Julia\u2019s hands. \u201cBut right now? I just hope Jacob and Calamity get some closure before the Summer or Winter Court aggressively eviscerate their enemies.\u201d<br /> <br /> Julia giggled darkly. \u201cI could do an art piece on that. A couple of wolves entering a den of lions.\u201d Insincere Marguerite gave her an odd look, which Julia either did not notice or ignored.<br /> <br /> \u201cI thought you handled Leonidas\u2019s arrival well, Bon-Bon. Speaking of lions.\u201d She held the half mask up to her face a moment without putting it on. \u201cGrr I was chased off by Insincere Marguerite!\u201d She said in a deeper voice.<br /> <br /> The other Darkling smiled. \u201cIt was far from our first meeting.\u201d She reached over toward Julia, and the Artist handed the mask over. \u201cYou could have flirted with him less.\u201d She said as she did so.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite waved a hand dismissively. \u201cIt keeps him off guard. Besides it would be rude not to flirt back. Still, he did a good job of being ingratiating, and did not even bring up the whole duel thing.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDid he bring up, you know, trying to kill you?\u201d<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite threw a glance over her shoulder. \u201cDenied it, actually. Oh, he admitted he planned to have me beaten up in the street, but said that the Day Court did not go setting people\u2019s houses on fire with heavy cement on them, which I suppose is true somewhat. He implied it was the Handmaidens.\u201d<br /> <br /> Now it was Julia\u2019s turn to make a dismissive sound. \u201cWhatever, he just did not want to admit it in the den of a superior lioness.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSpeaking of which\u2026.\u201d Insincere Marguerite slowly, almost ritualistically, put the leonine half mask on. Julia felt a shiver as her fianc\u00e9e pointed to the spot on the floor in front of her. Julia walked over and knelt there, feeling the claws on her face, as she gazed into Insincere Marguerite deep blue eyes. She could fall in the shimmering blue irises and never escape, pulled by an inexorable tide to the darkness of her fianc\u00e9e\u2019s pupils, where she would descend, never to see light again.<br /> <br /> Julia Oldacre smiled. She could deal with that.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXXI</i><br /> <br /> So, explanation for the fic title. At the start of the session, Jacob walked in on Insincere Marguerite and Julia engaged in basically what is happening at the end of the fic. Gawain\u2019s player pointed out it was \u201cprobably a sex thing,\u201d and when it came up OOC in the session (which it did a few times) they would say something like \u201cTotally a sex thing.\u201d So the title is, well, an acknowledgement of that, since the \u201csex thing\u201d-ness was never confirmed nor denied in session.<br /> <br /> Calamity passed her Clarity check, so realized killing the woman was wrong. Jacob did not need to make one, as he did not kill anyone specifically. Natasha took exactly seven lethal, so she had begun bleeding out. The two humans, skilled as they were, really had no chance against Calamity, Jacob, Luna and Natasha.<br /> <br /> In Relationship drama, Calamity alluded to it but Desiree and Gawain are kind of a \u201cmore official\u201d thing now. They are (obviously) not exclusive but at least for now Desiree is interested in being with Gawain at least part of the time. Calamity is not explicitly part of the arrangement, but Desiree is okay with her.<br /> <br /> Okay, well next session is prep for the mission, movie night, and more hijinx. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vamp