:1023149,"title":"","content":"Insincere Marguerite doesn't kill. She was a stalk them and bring back to her lair to keep the pretties in the darkness with her sort of predator in Arcadia.<br /> <br /> During the game, I don't think she's actually killed anything. Her preferred role in combat is to strike enemies with weakness and blindness while remaining invisible or out of range. <br /> <br /> Calamity and Julia are the murderous Darklings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T11:05:11-08:00","id":1023349,"title":"","content":"Then what happened to that guy she was telling her story too in her first pre-game entry? Did he survive? Or is that non-canon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T11:45:28-08:00","id":1023363,"title":"","content":"It's probably a case of character still being formulated then. The character since creation has expressed repeatedly disgust with killing in game.<br /> <br /> I suspect in the story she had not topped off Smoke or Darkness, and no escape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T00:48:15-08:00","id":1025026,"title":"","content":"Preparations for the battle with the Loyalists. Conversations to reveal family status. And Julia\u2019s\u2026interesting painting. No Calamity or Gawain journal, but both were present. <br /> <br /> <i>Session LXXII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> And so it begins. I\u2019m sitting here writing in this journal as the others endlessly pore over our plans, hoping to cover every eventuality before we drive to LA to attempt to spring our trap on Rook and Hunting Hawk. It seems more constructive than sitting here and quietly pondering how useless and afraid I suddenly feel.<br /> <br /> The last couple of days haven\u2019t been so bad, all in all. Movie night was fun; Elena and Natasha joined us for a double-feature of stop-motion animated films chosen by Julia. Both were directed by a man named Henry Selick (and <u>not</u> \u2013 and I\u2019m told this point is vitally important \u2013 by the famed Tim Burton), and both were enjoyable on many levels\u2026 though I think the first made many of us uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> The film in question was called <u>Coraline</u>, and it was based on a children\u2019s book written by Neil Gaiman (the same author who wrote those <u>Sandman</u> comics Julia lent me last summer). On the surface it was just a creepy kid\u2019s adventure story about a little girl who runs afoul of supernatural predators and displays uncommon bravery and pluck in overcoming them. Beneath the surface, it made me wonder if Mr. Gaiman has had personal experience with Arcadia. The film\u2019s villain, a doppelganger of Coraline\u2019s mother with buttons sewn into her face where her eyes should be, was <u>definitely</u> Keeper material. Now don\u2019t get me wrong; it was a fun film\u2026 it\u2019s just that a lot of us were sort of cutting our eyes back and forth at each other when certain things happened.<br /> <br /> The second film was called <u>The Nightmare Before Christmas</u>, and it was a lot of fun (and had slightly less potential to send changelings into bouts of PTSD). The idea behind it is that the king of Halloween (a dapper grotesque by the name of Jack Skellington) is out exploring one day when he discovers Christmas, and decides that he would like to bring people joy instead of scaring them for a while. He takes on the mantle of Santa Claus and royally screws things up, while his political enemies seize their opportunity at home. It was cute, charming, and in places hilarious. I think we all enjoyed it immensely.<br /> <br /> Jacob had the most drama on Monday night, however\u2026 he told Elena that he\u2019s her brother! She took it\u2026 well, I suppose. She had to leave the company for a while to process it, but that\u2019s only to be expected (Dad did the same thing when I revealed my identity to him). She returned before the end of the night, and seemed to have made peace with the revelation, though she was still a bit shy and unsure of herself for the rest of the evening.<br /> <br /> After the films I retired with D, Marguerite, and Julia. I wouldn\u2019t have minded a little hanky-panky that night, actually, but didn\u2019t feel like initiating anything. What can I say? The others were being so sweet and supportive and loving that I just got caught up in the emotional sharing, and it felt like it would have been wrong to interrupt that just for a few hours of carnal gratification.<br /> <br /> Tuesday was pretty uneventful for me until the show. One thing I should mention is that Elena spoke up at Sex Breakfast and asked how she could help us in our efforts against Rook and Hunting Hawk. She got a sort of determined look on her face and said that she would \u201cdo what she could to help out her brother.\u201d She gave Jacob\u2019s shoulder a squeeze as she said it, and I found that very encouraging.<br /> <br /> The idea of putting her at risk while we go after Rook was repulsive to me, however. After a quick chat with the motley, I gave Davey a call and asked if he could drop by the Dream House for the show tonight, since the motley wanted to ask him for a favor. He agreed to listen to our pitch (in exchange for us waiving the cover charge), and we all settled into our normal routines.<br /> <br /> Elena also asked a fairly sobering question at one point\u2026 she wanted to know how she could tell if <u>she</u> was a fetch. That\u2019s\u2026 a pretty <u>good</u> question, actually. As far as I know there\u2019s no foolproof way to know who is a fetch and who isn\u2019t until they reveal themselves and begin to degrade like Mary\u2019s fetch did. I\u2019m not sure if she has reason to believe that she might be a fetch, or if it was just idle curiosity, but the question certainly gave us all a lot to think about.<br /> <br /> As the afternoon wore on, we got a visit from an unexpected friend: Austin dropped by. He wanted to talk up his chestnut party to the local changelings at the Dream House tonight, and courteously decided to clear it with us first. Though opinions of the party itself are mixed among the motley, we all agreed that there was no harm in letting our friend do a little impromptu advertising among the Lost community this evening.<br /> <br /> I still haven\u2019t decided if I\u2019m going to attend or not. I know, it seems like a no-brainer, right? A big, organized sex party with a competitive element to it\u2026 you\u2019d think I\u2019d be the first in line. But lately I\u2019ve been rethinking that side of my life quite a bit. I don\u2019t know if I\u2019m finally getting enough erotic attention from my bevy of girlfriends to satisfy me, or if I\u2019m starting to question my own nymphomania at last, or if I\u2019m just distracted by Hunting Hawk\u2019s presence in the area, or what. Maybe it\u2019s just the anonymity and lack of meaningful emotional bonds between partners that has me less than enthusiastic\u2026 I usually like to have some genuine connection to my lovers, however tenuous or fleeting it might be.<br /> <br /> Anyway, we agreed to let Austin talk up his little soiree, and then went our separate ways to prepare for the show. Before I got into my usual routine, however, Julia wanted to show me a painting she had been working on. It was undeniably beautiful, but a little (to use Marguerite\u2019s word) \u201ccreepy.\u201d The painting depicted Julia and Marguerite \u2013 inexplicably the same height \u2013 dressed in Edwardian wedding finery, obviously engaged in the final stages of some sort of mutual suicide pact while guests (presumably from their respective wedding parties) raced to stop them from following through. The romantic side of the painting was obvious\u2026 Julia and Marguerite would rather die than live in a world which would not allow them to be together, which is oddly sweet. But the morbid aspect of the scene was a little overwhelming, and though I could appreciate the quality of the work, it was too dark for my taste. I tried to give an honest assessment of the painting without hurting my lover\u2019s feelings.<br /> <br /> Calamity and I didn\u2019t perform our \u201cBloody Creature Poster Girl\u201d number last night; we\u2019re giving it a rest at least until the weekend. I did a couple of my standbys; nothing I had to think too hard about. I\u2019ve been so distracted by recent events that I haven\u2019t really had time to work on anything new.<br /> <br /> Rowan didn\u2019t seem to mind, though. I caught her eye as soon as I came out on stage the first time, and tipped her a wink and a smile, which she returned with interest. After I was done on stage, I stopped by her table first. I told her that we had some motley business to take care of (implying that it had to do with the Loyalists in town but not stating it directly), and apologizing for the fact that she\u2019d have to fend for herself while we dealt with it, but promising that I\u2019d see her soon and be all hers for the rest of the evening.<br /> <br /> Austin was enthusiastic in his advertising, and he managed to get a fair number of people to sign up for his chestnut party. After speaking briefly with D and myself, he said he would mark us both down as \u201cmaybes.\u201d I\u2019d say that\u2019s fair. I\u2019m pretty sure Calamity is going, though I don\u2019t know for certain about any of the others. Andromeda is pretty excited about it, and I understand that the orders for her special products are picking up. Joan was less enthusiastic about the party, and declined to discuss the event directly.<br /> <br /> So after the bulk of the crowds cleared out, the motley met with Davey. He had apparently assumed that we wanted him for some sort of sex thing\u2026 I\u2019m not sure if that\u2019s a sad reflection on our motley\u2019s reputation in the Freehold or if that\u2019s just the sort of thing that people usually call on Davey for. In any case, once he understood the situation he was more than happy to offer up his aid. He\u2019s going to impersonate Elena at the art show so that Jacob\u2019s sister won\u2019t actually be in any real danger. I have to hand it to him\u2026 he didn\u2019t bat an eye at the danger to himself, he was just eager to help us resolve the situation however he could.<br /> <br /> I should probably note that Shi also joined us for this planning session. No one invited him, and I\u2019m not sure why he felt the need to be there, or what sinister fun he might be planning. However, none of us were confident of our ability to make him leave, and we all knew that if we tried to force him out it would just strengthen his determination to be a part of the meeting, so in the end we decided to bear it. I hope nothing too bad comes of his involvement.<br /> <br /> D, Marguerite, and Julia went off to have some fun with White Maria after the meeting. I\u2019m pretending that I didn\u2019t notice the eager way D was looking at White Maria during the conversation leading up to our parting\u2026 I prefer to think that my love has gotten over her dislike of the other girl rather than admitting that she\u2019s probably looking forward to abusing that poor submissive thing. Sigh. I guess as long as it\u2019s consensual\u2026<br /> <br /> And hey, maybe D was just excited by the fact that White Maria seemed to be wearing nothing under her robe aside from (working) Christmas lights. That little wrinkle certainly seemed to please Marguerite\u2026<br /> <br /> I rejoined Rowan in the theater area after the meeting, took her by the hand, and led her up to my bedroom. I know that I haven\u2019t been much in the mood for lovin\u2019 lately\u2026 but in this instance, Rowan\u2019s feelings were both more delicate and more important than my own. She needed to know that things haven\u2019t changed between us\u2026 that I don\u2019t blame her for what her House did, and that I don\u2019t judge her for how she acted when she was under its influence. So I took her to bed, and the two of us made love slowly, lovingly, and passionately until we fell asleep in each other\u2019s arms.<br /> <br /> I woke up the next morning to see her sitting up on her side of the bed, watching me\u2026 and smiling. I mean, <u>really</u> smiling for the first time since the incident with her House. It was good to see, and it gave me hope that she might really be recovering from the trauma she suffered.<br /> <br /> \u201cMorning,\u201d I said, smiling in turn and stifling a yawn.<br /> <br /> \u201cMorning, Lori,\u201d she returned softly, leaning in for a gentle kiss.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou staying for breakfast?\u201d I asked once we disengaged.<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cI can stay for a little while\u2026 but I don\u2019t want to get in the way of whatever it is your motley is planning. Besides, I need to get back to my new place\u2026 I\u2019m still trying to get it how I like it,\u201d she said a little shyly.<br /> <br /> \u201cI can\u2019t wait to see it,\u201d I replied. \u201cLet me know when it\u2019s ready, and I\u2019ll stay over at your place next time, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cJust\u2026 give me a couple more days to get everything perfect,\u201d she said with that cute little nervous flutter of hers.<br /> <br /> Sex Breakfast was business as usual. Once the guests had cleared out, we settled down and began making our plans for that evening. Though things started out simply enough, our tactics shifted and mutated enough that after a while it seemed like we were planning for nearly any eventuality. Davey will be on-site, impersonating Elena. Calamity will use a contract to impersonate Natasha. D will be there incognito, with her distinctive hair pulled up under a hat and her mask strengthened to make her skin look darker. Julia will be there openly, which makes sense since that gallery has shown her own work on more than one previous occasion. Marguerite, Molly Nuit, and Jacob will be waiting in the wings, invisible (yes, apparently Jacob <u>can</u> do that now). Gawain and I will be down the street at a local caf\u00e9, hopefully far enough away that we won\u2019t attract attention but near enough to lend our assistance if it becomes necessary.<br /> <br /> I know it\u2019s irrational, but I\u2019m scared. I\u2019m finally starting to piece together the shattered remnants of the life the Empress took from me\u2026 and now one of her agents has arrived in the area to take me back. I <u>know</u> my friends won\u2019t let that happen, and I\u2019d place every cent I have on them in any confrontation against Hunting Hawk. But that doesn\u2019t stop me worrying. She took so much from me before. Please, God, I\u2019m begging you\u2026 don\u2019t let her take anything else.<br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei Grace</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Okay\u2026so I nipped things in the bud. I asked Elena if I could talk to her in private and she agreed. I then explained about fetches and how they are usually left behind when someone is taken. I then told her that it was no coincidence that my name was Jacob. It took a moment for that to process in Elena\u2019s mind, but I could tell as soon as it did. She said that explained some things. I told her that time passes differently in Arcadia than it does here, and that sometimes people are gone for just moments and years have passed for them, or they are gone for decades and only a short time passed for them in the Fae realms. I said that where I\u2019d been taken time passed quicker there and I aged more than the two years that passed in \u2018the world.\u2019 She seemed to take it all in stride but did say that she needed to do some thinking by herself. I said that would be fine and to find me later if she had any questions.<br /> <br /> All of this made movie night a little more awkward than it could have been, but it was a good thing that I told Elena the truth. It would not be good for her to develop feelings for me that are not appropriate for a sibling. I did not want to hurt her feelings any more than I had to. So, we watched \u201cThe Nightmare Before Christmas,\u201d and \u201cCoraline.\u201d \u201cThe Nightmare Before Christmas\u201d was fun and entertaining. \u201cCoraline\u201d was kind of disturbing for those of us in the room that were Changelings. It bore more than a little resemblance to Arcadia and our Keepers. Coraline had a choice to accept the Other Mother\u2019s offer of a happy life in the Other World, but she refused. She did not want to have buttons sewn into her eyes and lose her ability to go home. The Other Mother started out as a sweet and attentive mother, but when Coraline refused her offer to stay she became much more terrifying. It reminded me of The Lady. The Lady started out as a friendly and sweet Queen that only wanted to help the poor young man she found freezing in a cave. During my service to her she was a fair monarch, if a bit cold. She always treated me and Rook well and we were happy to serve her. That was until I refused to do her work. I refused to bring Delight back to The Lady\u2019s realm and then I met the other side of my Queen. Just like Coraline met the other side of the Other Mother.<br /> <br /> After the movies were over most of the group decided to go to sleep. Some of us however decided that it would be a good idea to keep a watch. So I took a watch with Luna. Calamity took a watch with Natasha and Gawain took a watch by himself. Nothing happened, which was good. Calamity and I left for our therapy sessions early in the morning. On the way there Calamity admitted that she went a little too far in subduing the Russian agents. She knows that she was wrong and that she wants to be better. That she should be better. She also said that she was planning on talking to her therapist about what happened with the Russian agents at today\u2019s session. I did not blame her for what happened. I did not criticize her actions to her face because I knew that it would not do any good. She obviously feels bad about what happened and realizes that she needs help to be better and to not do anything similar in the future. <br /> <br /> When we got back from therapy Gawain was starting to make breakfast for the lot of us. I made the usual large pot of coffee and doled it out the way people liked it. I know that Elena prefers tea, so I made her a cup of Darjeeling. So, Gawain made quiche for everyone and it was delicious, as usual. I don\u2019t think I\u2019ve ever had anything made by Gawain that wasn\u2019t great. I believe that Natasha and Elena agreed that Gawain\u2019s cooking was good. <br /> <br /> While we were enjoying Gawain\u2019s excellent food we discussed our plans for Wednesday. Gawain suggested that we call in Davey and see if he\u2019d be willing to impersonate Elena and go to the Art show in L.A. Elena had originally said that she would act as bait at the Museum but to my satisfaction no one seemed keen on letting her do that. I don\u2019t know what I would do if anything happened to my sister. Right now she is my only real connection to my family. I haven\u2019t even considered approaching my parents yet. That would entail telling the Fetch what he is and sometimes that doesn\u2019t go so well. I only have to think of the incident with Mary\u2019s Fetch to see that. And despite not looking so much alike any more she is still my twin. We had always shared a close bond that I treasured. A lot of people fight with their siblings, and while we did do that on occasion, we also got along really well. I don\u2019t want to lose that. I don\u2019t want to lose her. She even asked if it might be possible that she was a Fetch. I told her that I did not believe that was the case. I do not remember seeing her in The Lady\u2019s realm and I know that is something that I would have noticed. I do not want to consider the idea that the young lady that I have been talking to since I got back has not been my real sister. <br /> <br /> So instead Davey was called and he agreed to stay after the show to talk to us about what was going on. We did not explain on the phone what we needed him to do. We figured we\u2019d just tell him in person later tonight. After that was taken care of Gawain and Calamity went over to Desiree\u2019s house to start working on the dream healing to help her get over her fear of making decisions. Hopefully this will work. It is not good for Insincere Marguerite to have to play the part of Desiree\u2019s Keeper. It does nothing good for my motley mate nor does it do anything good for Desiree. She needs to realize that we all make good and bad decisions and that it is just a part of living. No one is perfect. Goddess knows that I\u2019ve made some good and bad decisions in my time. I thought at the time that serving The Lady was a great idea. Turns out that it wasn\u2019t really. It was actually one of my bigger blunders and I ended up hurting a lot of people, but I can\u2019t take it back. I can\u2019t undo the decision to serve her or what I did in her service. <br /> <br /> On a lighter note Austin came by to talk to the group about his upcoming Chestnut party. I think some people were interested in going. I was not one of them, but others seemed interested nonetheless. We also told him that he could inform patrons at the club about his party as long as he wasn\u2019t too disruptive. He agreed and came back for the show later in the day. He made his rounds like he said and wasn\u2019t too pushy or anything about it. He did not however tell Shi or Molly about the partly. I guess he either knows that they\u2019ll say no or he didn\u2019t want them to come for some reason. I didn\u2019t ask which was the case.<br /> <br /> The show itself went smoothly. Lorelei was as graceful and amazing as always. The other singers and dancers did their usual wonderful jobs, but Lori always seems to shine the brighter. I think she likes that. Anyway, I talked to my usual group of people tonight. Molly was again at the bar and she asked if I was up to anything interesting lately. I hesitated for a moment before admitting that we were in the process of laying a trap for a Loyalist soon. She was interested in this and became more serious. She offered her help when and if we should need it. I told her that I would call her when we had finalized our plans. Molly may be a bit na\u00efve when it comes to normal social interactions, but she is a pro when it comes to hunting down Loyalists. She knows how to tail them, silent and invisible. And she knows how to fight should the need arise. So I thought she would be a good addition to the team on Wednesday. <br /> <br /> After the show Shi stayed along with Davey. It didn\u2019t seem like there was much of a way to get rid of Shi so we just explained to Davey what we wanted him to do. He agreed to disguise himself as Elena on Wednesday in order to keep her safe. We then planned out a bit more of what we were going to do. Calamity would go disguised as Natasha. Someone would use the power called Cobblethought on her to make her resemble the Ukrainian girl. Insincere Marguerite and I would go into the museum, invisible, to make sure that nothing happened to Davey. There are so many doorways in the museum that it would be ridiculously easy for Rook to make a gateway to the Hedge and make off with \u201cElena.\u201d We didn\u2019t want anything happening to Davey, nor did we want Rook to get away. Julia also volunteered to go to the museum to keep an eye on things, but not be part of the group. She is a frequent enough patron, and sometime contributor of art that it will not look out of place for her to be there. <br /> <br /> Meanwhile we needed someone to stay at the house just in case Rook got wise to our plans so Gawain asked Joan, Andromeda, Gloria and Desiree to stay behind on Wednesday to keep an eye on Natasha and Elena. They all readily agreed to protect the girls while we hunted Rook and possibly Hunting Hawk. I guess the biggest problem that we are going to have is that the museum is going to be full of people and security guards. We have to figure out how we\u2019re going to get Rook out of there without alerting too much attention to ourselves. I suppose the most likely solution is to open a gate to the Hedge and pull him through with us. Not all of us will need to be involved in that, just those that are actively subduing him. Julia for example can leave of her own accord after we get Rook. This is all presuming that things go according to plan of course. There is only so much planning we can do. So much is up in the air about what Rook will do and how we will handle it. He is smart. He may figure out that something is going on and get out while he can. He is going to be more wary of our Freehold after his run in with Darke. I can\u2019t blame him for that though. All we can do is plan based on what information we have and improvise where necessary.<br /> <br /> After we discussed our plans for Wednesday Lori left to go speak to Rowan and Calamity started regaling Natasha with tales of her outrageous exploits, like opening a gate to the hedge in the door of a car that was plummeting off a cliff to the ocean below. She was definitely showing off for our guest. And while she was doing that I called Darke to let him know what we had come with as far as plans go. He said that he would have to call Dahlia and let her know as well so she could track Hunting Hawk. The plan was for her to pick him up as soon as we have Rook in custody. All of that sounded good to me. We\u2019ll see how it goes in practice.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> It is Wednesday morning. You would not know by the normalcy of the day so far that later today we\u2019re going to try and spring a trap on a Loyalist that may or may not still want to kill me. Sometimes I wonder if I should be trying to rehabilitate Rook. I do not know if he will be amenable to changing sides or not. I do not even know if he will be amenable to letting me continue breathing. Darke and Twitch did some pretty horrific things to him so he may just want to kill the lot of us if he could. I remember the good times that we had as partners, but I shouldn\u2019t forget that when I betrayed the Lady he was quick to attack me and take me down. He almost killed me in that fight. Granted he did immediately take me to the Lady to be healed. I think he went further than he intended that particular day. I do not know how far he is willing or able to go now. If Darke\u2019s programming works as it was intended it may not be possible for him to hurt me directly. That doesn\u2019t mean that he isn\u2019t clever enough to find a way to get around that if he wanted to though. I guess it won\u2019t hurt to try and convince him to change sides. If he fights back too strenuously or hurts too many people then it may be necessary to kill him. We won\u2019t know what happens until later today, so I suppose there is no point in worrying about it right now. Yeah, now if that advice would only work.<br /> <br /> So, breakfast went like normal. We had a couple of extra guests today. Rowan and White Maria had joined some of the ladies last night for a good time and stuck around to have breakfast with the group. We had general conversation until they left. Once they were gone Julia asked us if we would like to see her latest painting. She was especially proud of it and wanted to show it off to the rest of us. We agreed and went up to take a look. Insincere Marguerite went first, then Lori and De la Rocha. Then the rest of us. I will give it one thing, it is very beautifully painted, if a bit disturbing in its content. The painting is of Julia and Insincere Marguerite both in wedding dresses standing close together and holding guns to each other\u2019s heads. The look of absolute love was plain in their eyes and expressions. In the background there was a large mob running towards the couple, presumably aiming to separate the couple and keep them from pulling the trigger. Like I said very pretty, but disturbing nonetheless. <br /> <br /> After we took a look at Julia\u2019s painting we talked some more about out plans for the afternoon. De la Rocha came up with the idea of tucking her hair up under a cap and wearing that and some plain clothes to keep her disguised. At first I did not think it would work, but thinking about it some more made me thing that that it just might work. De la Rocha is noticeable because of her purple hair extensions and very visible clothing. If she were dressed in drab clothing and hid her hair she could blend in with the rest of the nondescript crowd. That way she could curse or bless anyone that needed it. Basically she could give the allies good luck and the bad guy\u2019s bad luck at her choosing. It sounded good to me. Also, Molly could be there invisible with her gun if it was so needed. And Marguerite would be there to keep an eye on \u201cElena\u201d at all times. I plan on going along invisibly as well, but that is to keep Davey safe and to capture Rook if I can. I would prefer to be there when we take him down. I do have a personal interest in this whole endeavor after all. Here\u2019s hoping that all goes well. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> Circumstances remain overall favorable for me.<br /> <br /> Juliette recovers well from her surprise at discovering Hunting Hawk was in the area. Last night she actually made love. Without me, sadly. But Rowan was there, and she is not as much for the\u2026togetherness\u2026we bring.<br /> <br /> For me, yesterday White Maria texted me and requested a purgation for the evening. She does that sometimes\u2026since our first evening she finds these little sessions helpful for her. Of course, they involve regressing to her Durance. I play the role of her Keeper. It\u2019s\u2026an uncomfortable role, these days.<br /> <br /> Which is a good sign for I, I suppose.<br /> <br /> Maria and Julia were there last night. Maria channels her distaste for White Maria into such things I think. Maria has had something of an\u2026edge\u2026to her past few nights. Maybe because we all took some nights off from carnality. Whatever it is, she has an edge.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it occurs to me, when things settle, I might try to get White Maria some help from Calamity, like Desiree is getting. It\u2019s a dicer situation because if she was not struggling with issues with her Durance, it would be harmless fun. I may need to talk to Calamity about it.<br /> <br /> I have also been getting a flurry of texts from Felicity. I will need to see her for dinner soon. <br /> <br /> Meanwhile Natasha and Elena are doing okay under our care. Jacob finally broke the news, and while Elena was upset, she seems to have recovered. Jacob seems okay too. Natasha, for her part, made a serious play for Julia\u2019s, well, not affections so much as attentions, I suppose. Julia likes her women a bit more feminine than Natasha\u2019s more intensely butch aesthetic, so it did not work in Natasha\u2019s favor. Natasha was all about going after the Loyalists, but I think we have talked her out of such displays of bravado. Hopefully. I will privately advise Andromeda to keep a particular eye on her.<br /> <br /> And Elana asked how she can know if she is a Fetch. Concerning, perhaps.<br /> <br /> Calamity asked me about Stasia, who Natasha reminds her of. This time why I had not said anything. I simply said I had not completed my investigation before I got\u2026sidetracked, by issues between us, which was true.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve been keeping the hold decorated for Christmas. I hope we get the second tree from Oleander. I am still putting decorations up here and there. I wonder if anyone noticed I swapped our usual muzak for French Christmas carols?<br /> <br /> At least White Maria was feeling Christmassy. She was wrapped in Christmas Lights and Tinsel under her Kimono. Ah, she does know what I like.<br /> <br /> Movie night was awkward with them because of Jacob\u2019s revelations. Somehow, in the sense of somehow meaning because of Julia, <i>Coraline</i> and <i>Nightmare Before Christmas.</i> Julia was so happy. Those movies, the latter particularly, always put her in a pleasant mood.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Julia, so she has been thrashing about for how to paint something that would represent our love and depth of devotion to each other. She recently completed her first attempt to do that. It\u2019s lovely. It\u2019s also creepy. A representation of herself and Iself is in it, both in Fin de Si\u00e8cle bridal gowns, with a large wedding party, two really, rushing toward us in the background. \u201cJulia\u201d and I are the same height, rather than she being several centimeters taller, and we stare into each other\u2019s eyes with what I have to admit is brilliantly rendered both deep abiding love and deep abiding sadness.<br /> <br /> We also have pistols pointed at each other. It is a suicide pact, and the painting captures the final moment of life for these two versions of ourselves. The onlookers rush to prevent it but will not be in time. The subjects will be together in death, if they cannot in life. <br /> <br /> Aside from the subject matter the painting is incredibly good. Jarringly intense. I just find it a bit disturbing. You know, seeing an I about to die. <br /> <br /> But we have Loyalists to find. We will soon be going to the art show, and we have a decent plan. Maria, almost unrecognizable in plainclothes, will be there to bless and curse as needed. Julia will be there as, well, an artist patronizing the show. Molly, Jacob and I will be sneaking around to jump out if Rook gets too close. I am well able to incapacitate. Davey and Calamity will be disguised as Elena and Natasha there. Meanwhile Juliette, Gawain, and Luna will be nearby at a caf\u00e9 as reinforcements. Oh but how can it go wrong?<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t mind hunting Loyalists as long as there is Christmas music.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXXII</i><br /> <br /> Nah Lori, that is not actually vitally important (waits to be pummeled by her player).<br /> <br /> Chestnut parties\u2026man I would so never go near one of those.<br /> <br /> The Dream healing of Desiree actually started, as Jacob indicated. Gawain began the process by guiding Desiree to recall the most significant turning points in her life to help him and Calamity better understand her and what she's been through. It also laid the groundwork for his future dream healing work where he plans to walk her back through those same moments to ask her how she would handle them now to show her how she's learned from them and is, in fact, better at making decisions now than she was then. He got extra dice.<br /> <br /> Okay so I have a treat for you. Gawain\u2019s player has not had time for journaling, really, but they have not lost interest. Rather, they have made a relationship chart for the game; all the IC romances, from married characters to one-night stands, up through session 72. I will be posting it next week; the big charts and call outs for each Motley member. Look for it Saturday, and then back to normal journaling in two weeks. Hope you enjoy. Comments and questions welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T16:20:11-08:00","id":1026209,"title":"","content":"The concept of &quot;am I a Fetch&quot; is a really interesting one, and it hits a bit close to home since, when I was around 18, I realized that...well, what was to say that anything around me was real? If I was? It hit me with a massive depression that it took me a long time to make peace with. I can imagine something like that happening in-universe happening to those who know about Changelings...and I wonder about the impact it would have if it turned out they actually <i>were</i> a Fetch. They'd be prepared for the revelation, but the consequences would likely be dire, even if they didn't go insane, and meeting their Changeling counterpart would likely be...well, awkward.<br /> <br /> ...and now I have a weird scenario where a Changeling reveals himself to a room of people, tells them one of them is a Fetch, and watches the ensuing chaos.<br /> <br /> ...and another, more long term game where a bunch of people, all Fetches, band together and half withstand, half learn about their Changeling selves. Players who live and or empathize with their Changelings could, potentially, merge with them and become their Changelings counterparts. A sort of reward for good roleplaying and progression of character.<br /> <br /> Anyways, more pertinently, I really enjoyed how this chapter went on. Revelations made, people becoming closer, and plans in the making. Of course, now that Lori has written &quot;what else could go wrong&quot;, it's inevitable that something does. Like Hunting Hawk coming in instead of Rook, or someone normal getting involved...or the building exploding or something. Boiler leaks happen. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I can't wait to see how the chart turns out, and it's great that Gawain's player is still in the game in spite of a lack of time to AP it. The Actual Plays from everyone else has, as always, proven to retain their excellence, and I love seeing all the facets of the different characters.<br /> <br /> Also, regarding Davey, what does he look like, Mask and Mien wise? He's part of the Spring court, which combined with Lori's idea of him potentially being asked to attend sexy things on a regular basis means that he's pretty handsome. However, it's also ambiguous if he's good enough with contracts to make himself look like another or he's just that good when crossdressing, so I'm not sure if he's handsomely pretty as well...<br /> <br /> Bah, curiosity. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T17:25:40-08:00","id":1026235,"title":"","content":"I am certainly glad you enjoyed reading about our session. Something does, of course, go wrong; there is some foreshadowing of what it is, as well. <br /> <br /> Gawain's player does a LOT of journaling. This game has 3 other regular journals and one other frequent one, and Gawain tends to be something of an overview. I suspect it is a juggling of their free time. But yeah, Gawain is very active in the game, just like the others. Actually we get a Gawain journal next time.<br /> <br /> Davey looks like very bishi man of east asian decent. He is a Darkling Mirrorskin, and a skilled shapeshifter. There is some question if the handsome bishi guy is even his real appearance. He comes off as slightly affable and goofy, with an on again off again relationship with Dark Kimberly, but during the Greening it was revealed that he sometimes helps the Summer Court hunt Loyalists, and I have mentioned OOC offhandedly there was at least one time they interacted with someone who was actually Davey in disguise.<br /> <br /> Last night's session was exciting, and had some very good character moments, as the PCs took on the loyalists, and an unexpected thing or two happens.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T20:25:54-08:00","id":1026291,"title":"","content":"The chart is either gonna clear everything up orraise even more questions.<br /> <br /> Glad to know Gawain is doing well. Combat monster Metalflesh or not, he is the most precious cinnamon bun, too good for the World of Darkness (just occurred to me as I wrote that this sounds like what Calamity's been Expressing). Plus, hoping he gets some help with at least making peace with his head-mate, Lord Bertilak.<br /> <br /> One problem though. I thought Riddle-kith just disguised your mien to look like another kith. How would that allow her to look like a specific mortal? Especially since just the fact that she has a Mask and Mien would tip the Loyalists off that it's not Natasha","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T12:59:56-08:00","id":1026659,"title":"","content":"I'll make sure Gawain's player sees that. XD<br /> <br /> Davey is not using Contract of Mirrors. He is a Mirrorskin. <br /> <br /> ETA: Misread that. Calamity used Cobblethought from Dreams. I think only IM has mirrors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 01-04-2017, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T16:40:43-08:00","id":1028330,"title":"","content":"Ok, it is the off week, but Gawain's player made some cool relationship charts for keeping track of who is sleeping with who in the MDH.<br /> <br /> A couple caveats. This covers events in game. Mostly. Some partners from before the campaigns are there (Insincere Marguerite having slept with Yvette and the Handmaidens, for example) but Lori's various mortal paramours are not listed, since they have not appeared. Missy and Jane are not there either. There were also some sweeping things not included as they were not specific. For example, Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne has &quot;slept with more than half of the women in the freehold&quot; but only has a couple partners listed from events in play. So it is exhaustive for what has happened in play, but not necessarily character histories or everything going on in The Lady By The Sea.<br /> <br /> Okay, here we go<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i169.photobucket.com/albums/u223/LeRoienJeune/ChangelingRship_zpsswnfzobt.jpeg\" target=\"_blank\">Full Chart</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i169.photobucket.com/albums/u223/LeRoienJeune/Gawain_zpspyovzzil.jpeg\" target=\"_blank\">Gawain</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i169.photobucket.com/albums/u223/LeRoienJeune/Lori_zpscxgl5fux.jpeg\" target=\"_blank\">Lorelei</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i169.photobucket.com/albums/u223/LeRoienJeune/Calamity_zpsr1w3290d.jpeg\" target=\"_blank\">Calamity</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i169.photobucket.com/albums/u223/LeRoienJeune/Jacob_zpsqsmjqvmy.jpeg\" target=\"_blank\">Jacob</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i169.photobucket.com/albums/u223/LeRoienJeune/IM_zpsuwipeekc.jpeg\" target=\"_blank\">Insincere Marguerite</a><br /> <br /> Color scheme is Green=Spring, Red=Summer, Brown=Autumn, Blue=Winter, Yellow=Day, Black=Night, Gold=Dawn, Grey=Dusk. The Directional Courts have not played a role yet so are not present.<br /> <br /> We had a running joke that there is achievements, like &quot;A (Wo)Man For All Seasons&quot; for sleeping with a member of each Seasonal Court. &quot;Night and Day&quot; for one of each of the Diurnal Courts, and &quot;Dusk Till Dawn&quot; for Dawn and Dusk. At this point, Insincere Marguerite is our only Woman For All Seasons and only Lorelei is Night and Day. Lorelei, Gawain, and Calamity only need to seduce a Winter Courtier though, and Insincere Marguerite and Felicity are likely to give in any day now. Is funny to talk about through.<br /> <br /> Next session is more about violence than sex, though. Join us next week as the group confronts Rook and Hunting Hawk, and have something of a surprise with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 01-07-2017, 08:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedb