by court with names, kiths, seemings, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T12:55:20-08:00","id":1032279,"title":"","content":"The Last Dance Motley sets an ambush for two dangerous Loyalists. They were unprepared, however, for two questions: 1) Will there be any repercussions on the psyche of a member, and 2) what happens if they succeed?<br /> <br /> Everyone has a journal, including Gawain. Gawain and Insincere Marguerite are short fictions. Gawain\u2019s all happened at the table; it is the battle at the climax of the session. Insincere Marguerite is more of a recap as journal, and did not take place at the table. Depending on the tastes of the readers, some might want Lori\u2019s overall recap before Gawain\u2019s for better context, but that is up to you. Also people who don\u2019t usually read Jacob\u2019s may want to give it a look this time. It\u2019s different.<br /> <br /> Enjoy.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LXXIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> Gawain took a deep breath of the crisp forest air. He felt full of life, bolstered by the hope of an honorable resolution and the successes of the night. Hunting Hawk had been captured and Lori had brought De la Rocha back to herself before she had killed the loyalist. They\u2019d grabbed Rook without a fight and stopped the Summer Court from summarily executing him, there in the parking lot, like a dog.<br /> <br /> He stretched, preparing for the fight to come. He was glad Lori hadn't come, that she'd stayed at the edge of the forest with Insincere Marguerite. This wasn't a place for her, for either of them. Insincere Marguerite hadn't even let Julia come to the club to grab Rook, so she was safe as well. He looked over at Jacob. This hadn\u2019t gone down like the Ice Elemental had wanted, but it didn\u2019t show on the Russian man\u2019s face. Not that much ever did. He glanced at Rook. He was similarly impassive, sitting in a meditative pose in the center of the clearing. His eyes were locked on Jacob.<br /> <br /> Gawain had to respect the man\u2019s resolve. He didn\u2019t agree with it - loyalty was a sword that should cut both ways and the Lady didn\u2019t seem to be holding her end of it, from Jacob\u2019s telling of it. But it was Rook\u2019s choice to make, his loyalty to give. And with that loyalty, he couldn\u2019t make the only pledge the accept to let him go free. Promising he\u2019d leave Jacob, his motley or even the entire Lady by the Sea freehold alone wasn\u2019t enough for any of them, and promising he\u2019d never abduct anyone was too much for him.<br /> <br /> Given that, and the fact that no one was willing to consider holding him hostage until he agreed to be, as he put it, a \u2018gold-star, bake sale participating citizen of the freehold\u2019, there weren\u2019t many options left. Rook had asked the favor of dying on his feet, fighting for a way home. Jacob had granted it.<br /> <br /> When the loyalist stood up, the six champions took their places around him, Jacob and Luna with their knives, Calamity with her glass, Molly with her Uzi, De la Rocha with her fists and Gawain with his zweihander. Rook acknowledged each of them in turn, and then, without any formal call, the fight began.<br /> <br /> Calamity struck first, a quick jab testing his defenses. He moved fluidly around her strike, not avoiding it completely, but causing her glass blades to skitter across the swirling darkness that surrounded him. Jacob followed up quickly, taking advantage of his distraction to score a slice under his brother\u2019s ribs. Rook hissed through clenched teeth.<br /> <br /> The taller man struck back, almost quicker than Jacob could respond. His blades went deep, but still cut into nothing but the icy flesh Jacob had conjured up. Icy water soaked his shirt, puddling on the ground beneath him. The two brothers locked eyes.<br /> <br /> After a brief moment Rook\u2019s widened as Molly shot a quick controlled burst into his back. He staggered, regaining his balance just in time to move so that De la Rocha\u2019s fist just barely missed his nose. His chest heaved as he leaned away from her, but he snapped back into a ready position, trying to fend off Luna\u2019s knife. He was slowing though, the sheer weight of their numbers wearing him down. The knife cut down his arm, dispelling a swath of darkness and revealing a line of red.<br /> <br /> Gawain was the last of the Changelings to swing, his movements precise. His contracts with Summer and Dawn roared through him and he felt the weightiness of the blow even as he began his swing. Rook moved to get out of the way, to block the blow, but he moved too slowly and there was too much momentum behind the blow. The zweihander sliced completely through his wrist, then his neck.<br /> <br /> Gawain fell to his knees as the corpse did, the rush of his Contracted power leaving him all at once. He took a deep, shuddering breath as he gave the dead man a warrior\u2019s salute, Calamity stepped over and laid a hand on his shoulder. He laid a hand over her, patting it gently but not looking at her, or at the head that rolled over near him.<br /> <br /> Jacob picked up the head, cradling it and gently closing Rook\u2019s eyes. Gawain laid down his sword and, after looking to Jacob for permission, gathered up the body, laying the severed hand on top of it. He laid it out on the backseat of the van and Jacob clambered up to sit beside it, still holding the head. Gawain looked at him.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe\u2019ll bury him in the Hollow?\u201d<br /> <br /> Jacob paused. \u201cA pyre.\u201d<br /> <br /> Gawain nodded and took a deep breath as if to speak, but then let it out and turned back for his sword. He handed his keys to Calamity on the way.<br /> <br /> On the ride home, Gawain cleaned his sword. It was a soothing, repetitive task and he lost himself in it, trying to forget the all too familiar feeling of his sword slicing through a neck, burying his deep feelings of satisfaction at justice delivered. He couldn\u2019t have told you how far the impromptu fighting ground had been from the Dream House, but his sword was clean when they got home.<br /> <br /> Some part of Gawain\u2019s brain registered surprise at Madame Spidertoes\u2019 presence at their fountain, but she wasn\u2019t a threat and he had a duty to fulfill. He gathered up Rook\u2019s body again and made directly for the hedge gate, not wanting the girls inside to see the body. Calamity, Jacob and Luna followed.<br /> <br /> Calamity pulled Jacob aside once the pyre was built and Rook\u2019s body had been laid out on it. She spoke earnestly, a hand on his shoulder. \u201cYou tried. You gave him a chance.\u201d<br /> <br /> He nodded, his expression stiff. \u201cI still watched a good friend kill my brother.\u201d<br /> <br /> Gawain moved away, not wanting to eavesdrop anymore. After another moment, the two parted and Jacob lit the pyre, Luna standing nearby. It was a solemn affair, and when the fire was down to embers, Jacob turned without a word and went inside the Hollow house. Gawain watched Luna follow him, until Calamity took his hand and led him out of the Hedge.<br /> <br /> Desiree was waiting for them, and took his other hand after a moment of hesitation to see if she was welcome. She smiled up at him worriedly, but he managed a weak smile for both of his girls as they walked back into the Dream House.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Shit.<br /> <br /> Of all the ways I saw that confrontation going, of all the horrible things my imagination had dredged up from the darkest corners of my mind, I have to admit that reality has once again surprised me. Even without conscious intent, it seems that the Empress and her servants are still finding new and interesting ways to hurt me and those I care about.<br /> <br /> Calamity quoted some military aphorism before we left the Dream House to hunt Loyalists: \u201cno plan survives contact with the enemy.\u201d We had talked our strategy through ad nauseum in the hopes that we could come up with a contingency for anything Rook might try, but the one thing we failed to account for was our own unpredictability. Now things have gone to hell in a handbasket, and I\u2019m forced to contemplate something I would have said was unthinkable yesterday because my love finds herself at risk unexpectedly.<br /> <br /> To start at the beginning, we drove to L.A. and set our plans in motion yesterday afternoon. Davey and Calamity (disguised as Elena and Natasha, respectively) browsed the gallery, while most of the rest of the motley and Molly Nuit hovered close by, either invisible or in disguise. D was one of the latter, she had tucked her distinctive hair up under a large hat, swathed herself in drab colors, and strengthened her Mask to make her skin appear darker. Gawain, Luna and I were stationed down the street at a trendy caf\u00e9\u2026 close enough that we could lend support if necessary but far enough away to avoid notice (or so we hoped).<br /> <br /> Calamity had offered to take away my fear using Autumn Court contracts before she entered the gallery. I thought about it, but in the end I decided not to take her up on the offer. God gave mankind fear for a reason; it keeps us sharp, it keeps us out of unnecessary trouble, it keeps us <u><u>alive</u></u>. I believed that I could overcome my fear if necessary, and that I might very well need the edge it would give me before this confrontation was over. I still believe I made the right call.<br /> <br /> We were all in contact with these teeny-tiny headsets that linked us together through our phones. I tried to be nonchalant about this technology, but it wasn\u2019t easy. I mean, this is some Dick Tracy level shit here! Communication devices so small that a casual observer won\u2019t even notice that they exist? And apparently this technology is common enough these days that if anyone <u><u>did</u></u> notice it, they\u2019d probably just assume that we were having mundane phone conversations with other people. Wonders of the modern age, man\u2026<br /> <br /> Anyway, it wasn\u2019t long at all before \u201cElena\u201d got a text in Russian from one of her fellow students, who was also at the gallery (luckily we had included Davey in our pledge with the girls, so he could understand and respond to the text). We were in contact with Elena back at the Dream House, and she told us that the student in question was a casual acquaintance, but not a close friend. We almost universally agreed that Rook had set his trap.<br /> <br /> Davey and Calamity responded to the text, and agreed to meet the sender at the little caf\u00e9 inside the gallery. Once there, it was obvious to Jacob that this fellow was indeed Rook in disguise. I\u2019m not sure how he disguised himself, but apparently he had certain tics and habits that Jacob recognized, so in the end it was all for naught. He told the \u201cgirls\u201d that he had spotted some of the people following Natasha outside of Elena\u2019s apartment, and that it wouldn\u2019t be safe for them to return there. Davey let Calamity take the lead here, and she played the part brilliantly. The two of them agreed to head to a safe place he knew until the heat died down. He gave them an address, which turned out to be the location of a pretty seedy club nearby. Still, they played along and agreed to meet him there, though the club wasn\u2019t open yet, so they had to wait for about ninety minutes before departing.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Gawain, Luna and I approached the gallery, thinking that we might be able to nab Rook as he left the building. As we walked into the gallery\u2019s parking lot, I happened to glance up at the sky and noticed something odd\u2026 at least it was odd for L.A. There were four large birds circling directly overhead. They were obviously raptors of some sort\u2026 hawks or falcons, I would guess. I felt a chill go up my spine and called the others\u2019 attention to the birds.<br /> <br /> And then it happened. The boogeyman who has haunted my dreams for the last year stepped out from behind a parked van. He wasn\u2019t as tall as I remembered, but he still towered over me\u2026 he was nearly as tall as Gawain. He was dressed in blacks and browns, and his sharp features were drawn up in a cruel grimace of triumph. His eyes glittered yellow under his sharp brows, and he walked with a fluid grace many dancers would envy.<br /> <br /> \u201cStop,\u201d he said sharply as we approached.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat do you want?\u201d Gawain asked, moving to stand in front of me.<br /> <br /> \u201cI just want her,\u201d Hawk said, inclining his head in my general direction, \u201cI have no quarrel with the rest of you or your Freehold.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, well, that\u2019s not gonna happen,\u201d Gawain said simply, drawing a knife (he\u2019d left his big-ass sword in the van, as it tends to attract attention).<br /> <br /> \u201cSo that is how it\u2019s going to be?\u201d he asked in response.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt doesn\u2019t <u><u>have</u></u> to be this way, Hawk,\u201d I said desperately, and then everything went to hell.<br /> <br /> I can only assume that my comment about the birds carried over the headsets and got her worried. She leaped out of the shadows between two cars and barreled into Hawk. I didn\u2019t recognize her at first due to the drab clothing, the scarf she suddenly had wrapped around the bottom half of her face, and the vicious, feral way she attacked. But it was the love of my life\u2026 it was my D.<br /> <br /> She nearly killed him in the first few seconds. She ripped at him, tearing at his flesh like a beast\u2026 but she was utterly silent the whole time. Hawk panicked and ordered his birds to attack us while he struggled to throw her off. One of them dived straight at me. I had just enough time to realize that it was some sort of Hedge beast before its talons scraped at my right eye. My vision went red and blurry.<br /> <br /> A couple of seconds later Gawain knocked the bird away from me. I barely noticed; my entire attention was captivated by what was happening between D and Hunting Hawk. She had an insane predatory gleam in her eyes that I had never seen before, and I realized that she was going to kill him if I didn\u2019t stop her.<br /> <br /> \u201cD!\u201d I shouted hysterically. She turned to regard me, pausing in her rampage for a moment. \u201cDon\u2019t kill him,\u201d I said soothingly, \u201che\u2019s not worth it.\u201d She cocked her head at me. I could tell I was getting through to her. And then Hawk took advantage of her distraction to lash out against her. Her Leechfinger powers absorbed the brunt of that first blow, but it was enough to send her back into a killing rage.<br /> <br /> While Gawain and Luna took care of the birds, I kept my attention fixed on the melee between D and Hawk. I called out to her again, and I could tell that she was there, listening to me, but her instincts had a powerful hold on her. I should have known that forcing her into a position where she had to hunt from stealth would awaken that part of her, but, well\u2026 I\u2019d never seen her that out of control before. They both took some licks over the next thirty seconds or so, but D gradually began to calm down and started turning her attacks more toward holding him and less toward dealing direct damage.<br /> <br /> I reached into my purse and pulled out my pistol, sliding the safety back as I drew. \u201cHawk!\u201d I shouted, demanding his attention. \u201cCall off the birds and stand down. I am trying [u]<u>very[</u>/u] hard not to kill you right now, and you are <u><u>not</u></u> making it easy for me!\u201d<br /> <br /> Hawk glared at me, then sort of slumped in D\u2019s arms. He gave a quick whistle, and the two remaining birds flew away. Gawain gently took Hawk from D\u2019s grip as I approached.<br /> <br /> \u201cSweetheart?\u201d I asked in a quavering voice. Her eyes turned to regard me from the depths of her disguise. Her pupils were dilated to such a huge degree that her eyes almost looked like mine. \u201cBaby,\u201d I tried again, \u201cit\u2019s okay now. I\u2019m here. I\u2019m okay.\u201d<br /> <br /> She took a hesitant step toward me, but didn\u2019t speak. I closed the distance between us. She didn\u2019t shy away, but she made no move to embrace me\u2026 or even approach me.<br /> <br /> I reached up and touched her face. Her skin was pale and waxy, and felt clammy to the touch. I tugged gently at the scarf covering her lower face. She didn\u2019t want me to do that. I\u2019m not sure if she was ashamed or if she was just instinctively shying away from my touch. In any case, when I pulled the scarf away, I saw that her mouth was set in a ghastly rictus grin. I pulled her closer to me, and the rigid expression began to twitch.<br /> <br /> Her hat fell off as I was kissing her, and her luxurious black and purple hair spilled out, and she was my love again.<br /> <br /> \u201cUmm,\u201d Gawain cleared his throat from a million miles away, \u201cI\u2019m pretty sure this guy is gonna die in the next few minutes unless we can stabilize him.\u201d<br /> <br /> D breathed deeply. \u201cGo on, Lori,\u201d she said softly. \u201cI\u2019ll be okay now.\u201d<br /> <br /> I bandaged Hawk\u2019s wounds as best I could in the parking lot, but I didn\u2019t waste any healing magic on him. I <u><u>did</u></u> use Spring contracts to heal the worst of D\u2019s wounds, and then to fix my own eye. Hawk had passed out at some point, and Gawain put his unconscious form in his van, and the four of us rode over to the club to lie in wait for our other quarry.<br /> <br /> D held on to my hand for dear life the whole way over there. I did my best to be a comforting presence, and to reassure her that this changes <u><u>nothing</u></u> between us\u2026 and much to my own relief, I\u2019ve found that it <u><u>doesn\u2019t</u>. </u> I\u2019ve seen her at her worst now, and I\u2019m happy to report that I\u2019m just as much in love with her as I was before. I haven\u2019t been calling her Maria, though\u2026 I didn\u2019t want to evoke her time at the Hospital any more than absolutely necessary.<br /> <br /> The confrontation with Rook was almost surreal by comparison. We just sort of surrounded and restrained him in the club\u2019s parking lot when he arrived. For a few seconds he tried to persist in his act, as though hoping to convince us that he was really just a normal mortal student. Davey changed his appearance at that point into the most intimidating person he could think of\u2026 Lucien Torrez stood there cracking his knuckles in a threatening way, the gemstones in his cufflinks glittering in the lights of the parking lot. That\u2019s right, it was Davey\u2019s patented Lucien Disguise With Diamonds\u2122. That thought might have been the only thing that made me smile all night.<br /> <br /> Then Jacob appeared out of nowhere and called him by name. Rook let the fa\u00e7ade drop, and a tall, thin man with ashen skin, colorless eyes, and short, spiky dark hair stood before us.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell,\u201d he taunted, \u201cyou managed to catch me. And it only took a third of the Freehold to do it this time. Bravo.\u201d<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think any of us knew quite what to say to that\u2026 a fact which seemed to amuse Rook further. We had done it; we had captured both of the Loyalists targeting our motley\u2026 and now that we had them, we didn\u2019t know quite how to proceed. Vic had shown up to take Hawk into custody, so at least he was no longer our problem for the time being.<br /> <br /> Things almost turned deadly at that point. Gawain spotted someone on a rooftop across the street\u2026 a changeling with a strong Summer mantle which nevertheless did not illuminate his face. This particular someone had a rifle aimed at Rook. Gawain stepped into the line of fire and the sniper fled the scene. We\u2019re all thinking of Louie Guo at this point, but I guess it doesn\u2019t really matter considering how the rest of the evening went.<br /> <br /> Rook threw us another wry grin as things settled down. \u201cSo what happens now? Am I to be executed, or perhaps offered the chance at glorious rehabilitation? Perhaps I could become a gold-star member of the Freehold? Participate in the bake sales and so on?\u201d<br /> <br /> Gawain \u2013 who had been acting sort of high-on-life throughout this whole encounter \u2013 made some quip about how he would get a discount on baked goods if he did, but most of us didn\u2019t really see anything humorous in the situation. Jacob mostly stayed quiet through the conversation that followed\u2026 he knew Rook very well, and I think he already suspected how the evening would end for his erstwhile brother.<br /> <br /> We tried. We <u><u>really</u></u> did try. I want to make that perfectly clear. But, well\u2026 Rook is a man of honor, and refused to betray his Lady. And while there\u2019s a part of me that truly does respect that sort of loyalty, I am really beginning to <u><u>hate</u></u> the sound of that damn word. \u201cHonor\u201d caused White Maria to demand Dark Kimberly\u2019s death earlier this year. \u201cHonor\u201d nearly got Joan killed or exiled when she demanded that the monarchs refrain from asking Andromeda to use the Table again. Hell, D was defending my \u201chonor\u201d when she clobbered Viscount Augustine a few weeks ago (still waiting for that apology, by the way). And yesterday, Rook\u2019s \u201chonor\u201d prevented him from accepting the out we tried to give him.<br /> <br /> \u201cI cannot betray the Lady,\u201d he said over and over. And then he said it again, with a vicious cut of his eyes in Jacob\u2019s direction, \u201cI am a man of honor.\u201d<br /> <br /> We tried everything we could think of to convince him. Gawain pointed out that honor has to flow both ways, and that the Lady did not give her servants the treatment they deserved, as evidenced by Jacob\u2019s case. But Rook wouldn\u2019t budge. Apparently, he called upon her of his own free will and bargained with her for his life. From his point of view, she upheld her end of the bargain, and honor dictated that he had to do the same. I tried to appeal to his sentimentality, asking if there was anything about his life before Arcadia that he would like to reclaim. He looked away and said softly \u201ceveryone I knew before is dead.\u201d<br /> <br /> He asked us if we were going to lock him up ourselves, claiming that he would die before going under Darke\u2019s knives again. We assured him that Darke was no longer in charge of the Winter Court, and I\u2019m certain he knew how inimical incarceration is to most changelings. He offered to make a pledge with us that he would never return to the Lady By the Sea Freehold; that he would never bother any of us again. It didn\u2019t take us long to realize that this sort of a pledge wouldn\u2019t be enough.<br /> <br /> \u201cGuys,\u201d I said solemnly after a minute, \u201cif he makes that pledge and then takes some little girl in Boston to be the Lady\u2019s newest plaything, that\u2019s on us.\u201d<br /> <br /> The others nodded. We offered to craft a pledge stating that he would never again take a mortal to Arcadia, but he refused to go so far. \u201cI must serve my Lady\u2019s wishes above all else,\u201d he said as he declined the offer. \u201cWill you at least give me an honorable death? Will you allow me to fight for my freedom? I will take you all on at once, if you like. I have no illusions regarding my chances of success, but at least I might gain a bit of satisfaction from taking one or two of you with me as I fall.\u201d<br /> <br /> And the others started talking about it. I mostly held myself aloof from the conversation when it became plain that they intended to grant Rook\u2019s request. \u201cGuys,\u201d I said, \u201cwe can just hand him over to the Courts. Let them decide the best course of action.\u201d<br /> <br /> Gawain shrugged. \u201cHe asked for an honorable death. We can grant that.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jacob nodded. \u201cI owe him this much,\u201d he said quietly.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe are not the government,\u201d I argued. \u201cThis is an execution. We don\u2019t have the right to decide that for ourselves.\u201d<br /> <br /> It was mentioned that Boss Lowjack had essentially given us free rein to resolve the situation however we saw fit, which I had really hoped people would forget. Resigned, I allowed the others to finish talking this out, and we drove Rook to a nearby park.<br /> <br /> \u201cI want no part of this,\u201d I said softly when we arrived. \u201cIf this is what you all think is best, then I won\u2019t argue against it any more, but I won\u2019t sit there and watch six of my best friends slaughter someone. I\u2019ll try to stay close in case anyone needs healing, but <u><u>please</u></u> be careful.\u201d<br /> <br /> Marguerite opted to stay with me, and the two of us sat miserably on a bench while the others did what was necessary (Julia had gone home after the rest of us left the gallery, so she was mercifully exempt from the whole conversation). We talked quietly about what had happened to D while we waited for the others. We were far enough away from the battle that we couldn\u2019t hear the clash of arms or any screams, but we caught the soft tattoo of Molly\u2019s Uzi at one point, and knew that the fight was underway.<br /> <br /> When it was over, the others rejoined us, mercifully unhurt (apparently Rook had hit Jacob once, but his elemental armor absorbed the brunt of the attack). They used Gawain\u2019s van to transport Rook\u2019s body, so D and I opted to ride home in Marguerite\u2019s car. Jacob said that he wanted to burn Rook on a pyre in the Hollow, as that was the custom for the honored dead in the Lady\u2019s realm. It seemed appropriate to allow him the ceremony, but I felt like my presence would have been intrusive.<br /> <br /> Madame Spidertoes was hanging around the fountain when we got back. I don\u2019t know how she knew something was wrong, but she made a beeline for D as soon as we arrived. \u201cMadame,\u201d I said guardedly as she approached.<br /> <br /> \u201cIs she all right?\u201d she asked anxiously. And then, directly to D, \u201care you all right, my dear?\u201d<br /> <br /> D looked at me, and then nodded.<br /> <br /> I saw it as my place to come to her rescue. \u201cShe\u2019ll be okay, Madame,\u201d I said softly, \u201cbut it\u2019s been a difficult evening for us. She needs to rest and recover. I promise I\u2019ll take good care of her. If you\u2019ll excuse us\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> She gave me one of her unsettling, unwavering stares, and then nodded her assent. \u201cOf course. But please come to see me when you are feeling up to it, my dear. I do worry so\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> D nodded again in response, and Madame Spidertoes bade us goodnight.<br /> <br /> The show was still going on, so we sort of slipped in the back so as not to interrupt the performance. We let Elena know that the situation had been handled, which I\u2019m sure was a great relief for her. Joan and Andromeda took their leave shortly after we arrived. Desiree sort of attached herself to Gawain, who had kind of deflated a bit in the wake of Rook\u2019s defeat. Gloria looked a bit stricken when she caught a glimpse of D\u2019s face, and I did my best to reassure her that D would be fine, but needed a little time. She seemed satisfied with that answer.<br /> <br /> D \u2013 <u><u>Maria</u></u> \u2013 was frisky last night. I get that; she wanted intimate contact with the people who knew her best. As soon as we got home, she got into her leathers, making sure to choose some of the brightest colors. She was desperate to put aside the stealthy predatory creature she had been, and her bombastic in-your-face normal personality reasserted itself with a vengeance. I reciprocated in kind, and Marguerite and Julia did the same (though Marguerite opined that D needs to get in touch with that part of herself more often to prevent it from surging forward as it did last night).<br /> <br /> So much fun was had by all during the evening hours, and we all fell asleep exhausted in a big pile just like old times. D was acting pretty much like herself again by the time Sex Breakfast rolled around, and I had high hopes that things would soon be back to normal for the motley. Sure, there was the inevitable conversation with Hawk to deal with, and I truly wasn\u2019t looking forward to it even then, but it honestly seemed like our most pressing issues had already been resolved. What a laugh that turned out to be!<br /> <br /> So I asked Jacob to call Boss Lowjack and see when I could talk to Hawk. I wasn\u2019t really hopeful that he could be rehabilitated and turned into a productive member of the Freehold, but I knew I had to speak to him anyway, to see what I could learn about Missy and Jane. I\u2019ve put off their rescue for far too long as it is, and Hawk\u2019s presence represents an exceptionally good opportunity to gather intelligence on our enemy. Marguerite suggested that I might want to give it a day, to process everything that was going on, but in the end I decided that I wanted to get it over with.<br /> <br /> Boss Lowjack was more than happy to accommodate our request; he\u2019s not wild about the idea of keeping Hawk restrained any longer than is necessary. He asked that we give him two hours to get the sedatives out of Hawk\u2019s system. According to Doctor Bright, Hawk should be lucid but weak when we speak to him, which is just about <u><u>perfect</u></u> as far as I\u2019m concerned. Lowjack made the arrangements, and I began the process of psyching myself up to confront one of my personal demons.<br /> <br /> Then Jacob got a call from Doctor Bright. He wanted to make sure that we left Hawk alive following our interrogation, because the Winter Court wanted to conduct their own questioning. It seems that Hawk\u2019s dreams are haunted by a monster\u2026 the same monster who haunts Twitch\u2019s dreams, in fact. The infamous \u201cMaria.\u201d Doctor Bright feels that this creature represents a clear danger to the Freehold, and that the Winter Court needs to gather as much intel as possible if they\u2019re going to deal with it.<br /> <br /> <b> <u><b><u>FUCK!</u></b> </u> </b><br /> <br /> I will not lie to myself here in my private journal. The first image that popped into my head when I heard that news was one of me shooting Hawk in the head immediately following our interrogation. I could claim that he was coming out of his stupor, trying to escape. I could even claim a hysterical hatred of one of my jailors; it happens to changelings all the time. I doubt anyone would question my actions too intently, even if the Courts were disappointed at the lost opportunity to find out more about Maria.<br /> <br /> Would I <u><u>really</u></u> do something like that? I asked myself that question internally, and the answer is hell yes. In a New York minute. It\u2019s not because I hate Hawk, though I do hate that son-of-a-bitch, and I probably always will. But to protect my love I would do anything, cross any line, betray any abstract principle. If it\u2019s a choice between staying true to my own ideals or keeping her safe, I will choose her every time. Even the sanctity of life doesn\u2019t hold a candle to her in my mind, and that\u2019s\u2026 honestly kind of a little scary. In the face of this crisis, all of my carefully-reasoned arguments against executing Rook last night disappeared like tissue paper in a hurricane.<br /> <br /> I took a breath to steady myself, and took D\u2019s hand in mine. She wasn\u2019t trembling, exactly, but she was tense. \u201cOkay,\u201d I said once I had my own emotions under control. \u201cAs I see it we have two options here. We can either come clean about D\u2019s identity\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Gawain interrupted me at this point. I\u2019m guessing he knew what \u201coption B\u201d was going to be, and he didn\u2019t want to hear me say it. I am in his debt, because I didn\u2019t want the others to hear me say it either. I\u2019m still prepared to go through with it, though, if it comes to that. And yes, I\u2019ll do it myself, so that none of my friends have to bear the responsibility. My God, I sound like Calamity.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the others talked over how best to break the news to the Freehold. The problem is \u2013 and has always been \u2013 that we don\u2019t know what pledges are in effect regarding Maria. It\u2019s possible that Twitch has deals in place with Darke and other members of the Freehold to \u201cdispose of\u201d Maria if she ever shows up looking for him. We need to make sure that all of these deals are rescinded before we reveal Maria\u2019s identity.<br /> <br /> I think it was Gawain who came up with the idea of getting Madame Spidertoes to break the news to those in power. She can tell the monarchs that she knows who Maria is, and swear to the fact that Maria is not a threat to the Freehold. She can demand that Maria\u2019s safety be guaranteed before the information is related, and everyone will just assume that Maria is a local Darkling, without necessarily making the connection to D in case things go sour.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a good plan, and I\u2019m glad he thought of it. I <u><u>desperately</u></u> hope that it works. I still need to talk to Hawk, though\u2026 the information he can provide about Missy and Jane and the Empress\u2019 realm is too important, and I wouldn\u2019t bet one red cent on his survival after the Courts get through with him. Based on the way I was acting toward D during the fight, he has to know that she\u2019s important to me, and I wouldn\u2019t put it past him to do whatever he can to hurt her as a way to get to me, just out of spite. So we have to get ahead of this.<br /> <br /> The only problem with Gawain\u2019s idea as I see it is Twitch. I know that I\u2019ve argued in the past in favor of D revealing herself to him, just to get it off her chest, but\u2026 well, I\u2019m afraid of what he might do. No matter what sort of pledges we put in place to protect her, he\u2019s a wild card. I mean, he\u2019s never been the most stable of individuals in the first place, right? Who knows how he might react when confronted with the darkest of his nightmares, the creature who drove him to the brink of insanity? How would any of us react to that?<br /> <br /> I\u2026 my God, even if Gawain\u2019s plan makes it so that I don\u2019t have to kill Hawk, I\u2019m sitting here seriously contemplating the fact that I might have to kill Twitch just to keep my family safe. I don\u2019t want to, but\u2026 like I said earlier, if it\u2019s a choice between the unthinkable and losing my dearest love, well\u2026 it\u2019s surprising how quickly the unthinkable can become thinkable.<br /> <br /> Plus, you know, I\u2019m already a murderer. What I did to Annabelle back in Arcadia proved that. At least this time a case could be made that I would be doing it for the right reasons. I hope to God it doesn\u2019t come to that. <br /> <br /> It\u2019s nearly time to go.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T12:55:53-08:00","id":1032280,"title":"","content":"<b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> Thursday, December 4<sup>th </sup><br /> Nine years, six months, eighteen days<br /> Days without stabbing: 0<br /> <br /> We fought the loyalists last night and we defeated them both. You\u2019d think that would be the end of it but nothing is ever that simple is it?<br /> <br /> I was worried that despite our best efforts at planning something would go off the rails and that\u2019s exactly what happened. Well, someONE went off the rails. (For a change it wasn\u2019t me.) I had no idea D was such a fucking time-bomb. And here I had figured Julia was the one we needed to worry about. But apparently Lori\u2019s girl hasn\u2019t left her Arcadian self as far behind as she\u2019d led us all to believe. And while it is undoubtedly for the best that Lori was able to talk her down from killing Hunting Hawk outright it certainly would have made our lives easier. Because now the Winter Court knows he\u2019s seen Maria and they\u2019re going to interrogate him about it and there is no way they won\u2019t connect the dots to Lori. No one is the motley is going to let them come for one+<br /> of our own quietly but from the way Lori was acting once it came out, I am worried about just how far she\u2019s prepared to go. After all, she loves D and we all know that love makes you stupid.<br /> <br /> It was pretty clear that going to the Winter Court and telling them was the only way to get ahead of this. Either that or making sure that Hunting Hawk doesn\u2019t survive his chat with us. But considering that Dr Bright called to specifically inform us that they needed him alive it would really look bad no matter what story we give to explain it. Gawain brought up Spidertoes since she knows and she cares about D and it wouldn\u2019t give anything away about Maria\u2019s identity beyond the fact that she\u2019s a Darkling for Spidertoes to speak on her behalf. It\u2019s the best shot we\u2019ve got. Of course, even if the Winter Court accepts that D isn\u2019t a threat to Twitch anymore there is the question of what pledges might be in place to protect him. And even if they aren\u2019t sworn to act they might not want to let it go. (Oh\u2026 maybe I\u2019ll get to point out how much she deserves a second chance to Darke? I would enjoy getting to throw that line in his face.) Of course even if they are all willing to put this in the past there is Twitch himself. I mean, as much of a fucking coward as he is when he\u2019s not high a fucking kite it seems unlikely he\u2019d have the balls to act directly but fuck knows what the little weasel might do to try to get rid of her or get back at her. I can\u2019t imagine there is any way she\u2019s not going to be pledge-bound against harming him and he is a member of the Freehold in good (enough) standing that I can\u2019t kill him even in self defense. So yeah, this mess is going to get messier before it it\u2019s over.<br /> <br /> And I\u2019m worried about Jacob. I don\u2019t think he really expected Rook to break from the lady but in his heart he wanted him to. Because, you know, he still loved his brother in arms. I\u2019ve tried to make sure he knows I\u2019m here to talk to without pushing. Not that I have any answers for him but talking helps. Of course, I\u2019m not sure he wants to talk to any of us right yet. I am pretty sure it wasn\u2019t just the hangover that had him quieter than usual this morning on our way to therapy. I hope I can manage to give him the space to deal with what he\u2019s feelings without seeming uncaring or unsympathetic.<br /> <br /> At least Rook had a good death. I know Lori and Marguerite weren\u2019t happy with it but what were the other options really? We couldn\u2019t let him go free without a pledge he was firmly unwilling to make. And turning him over to the courts? Even if holding another against their will wasn\u2019t such a sin Rook was too skilled and clever and dangerous to keep prisoner. He\u2019d have been a huge risk to the Freehold for no real gain. No, they would have executed him. What we did was allow him to die the way he wished.<br /> <br /> No, it was a good fight and an honorable death. I was privileged to be part of it and I can only hope for as much when my own time comes.<br /> <br /> At least Handsome seems to be on an even keel this morning. He\u2019d called upon his contracts to see things through and so at the end of the fight he crashed. And while we all fought, he is the one that laid the final blow. He is the one that killed his friend\u2019s brother. But Desiree was here last night and she said all the things he needed to hear that I couldn\u2019t figure out the right words for. Hell, she even took care of me while she was at it. I\u2026 seeing them curled up asleep this morning after I\u2019d slipped out to get ready for therapy\u2026 She\u2019s not my Knight or my Dragon but yeah, I am fond of that girl and I can\u2019t find it in my Darkling heart to doubt that the affection and tender concern she gave us last night was real. And standing there, I realized that part of me was glad to know that she\u2019d be there for Handsome when something eventually happens to me.<br /> <br /> Yeah, that fight last night has had me thinking about my own demise. Dr Emmett, as usual, had some uncomfortable questions when I mentioned it to her this morning. She pointed out how reckless I am in dangerous situations. I couldn\u2019t exactly argue with her about that, though I wasn\u2019t last night. But it wasn\u2019t that I was more worried about being killed. It just felt like it would have been, I don\u2019t know, disrespectful to not fight Rook to the best of my skills. She never said it outright but I am pretty sure she thinks I\u2019ve been trying to get myself hurt or killed because I feel like I deserve it for what I\u2019ve done. And hell\u2026 I can\u2019t say she\u2019s wrong. I mean, I certainly haven\u2019t gone in thinking that but when you look at my behavior objectively it\u2019s not hard to see it. I\u2019m just not really sure how to change what how I feel deep down. And right now there is way too much else going on for me to be navel gazing.<br /> <br /> I do need to talk to Beautiful about us, about the things she made clear when we spoke last, about where we\u2019re going. But most importantly, I have to talk to her about Stasia. I cannot make promises without knowing what, if anything, lies between the two of us now. And I have to work my nerve up to face her for good or ill. I have to know.<br /> <br /> But this is not the time for it. We\u2019ve got to deal with the mess with D and Twitch. And I need to find a way to be there for Jacob. And there may never be a better opportunity to rescue Lori\u2019s friends from the Violet Empress. I need to help Gawain finish Desiree\u2019s dream-healing. No, I don\u2019t have time to dreg up my tragic back-story right now. My motley needs me too much.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> I know that things weren\u2019t likely to end any other way, but it still doesn\u2019t seem real. I don\u2019t want to accept that Rook is dead. I had hoped that he might be willing to leave the Lady\u2019s service. Some small part of me was hoping that we could have that close relationship that we had in the past once more. Realistically I knew he wouldn\u2019t leave Her. He was one of her best Knights. I knew that if anything the treatment he received from Darke and Twitch would push him away from wanting to stay here. He did make some good points though when we offered him a place. He asked what he was supposed to do if he stayed here. If he was supposed to be a good citizen and go to bake sales. I can understand that. I had to get used to the normalcy of this place. We were both used to going out on missions for the Lady. There was excitement and adventure when we worked for Her. He didn\u2019t want to leave that. He didn\u2019t want to leave Her. He gave her his word that he would serve her loyally and he does not did not go against his word. He offered to make a pledge with us that he would not try to bring me back to the Lady or go after anyone else in the Lady by the Sea Freehold. This essentially meant that everyone outside of our little Freehold was still fair game, and I knew that the others wouldn\u2019t go for that. They did not want anyone else to be taken by him back to the Lady. Truth be told I didn\u2019t want anyone else being taken back to the Lady either, but I was tempted to take him up on that offer. I wanted him to live.<br /> <br /> When it became apparent that we were not going to go with the \u201cleave Jacob alone\u201d pledge he asked that we give him the opportunity to fight for his freedom. He said that he\u2019d fight us all if we wanted even though he knew his odds were not good. He said that he would at least like to try and take some of us down with him before he died. And he knew that it was coming. He knew. Once I revealed myself and told him to drop the disguise I think he knew that the jig was up. There wasn\u2019t going to be a way that he could talk his way out of this situation. He did comment that it only took a third of the Freehold to take him down. He said that with a wry smile that I remembered so well. So, he requested to be given the chance to fight for his freedom. He knew what was going to happen and he didn\u2019t want to die like a dog. He wanted to die on his feet with his blades in his hand. I understood that. I agreed with that. The others had mixed feelings about Rook\u2019s idea of a final fight. Calamity and Gawain were behind it, as was Luna, I think. Lori and Insincere Marguerite were not for it at all. They argued against it in fact. I wanted to tell them that if that was going to be Rook\u2019s final request then I was going to honor that. I hated it, but I knew where he was coming from. He wanted to die as he lived.<br /> <br /> So we fought. It was not a long fight at all, as I knew it would be. In a matter of moments my brother died. For my part I didn\u2019t try and soften my blow. If anything I tried my best to be the one that took him down. I wanted my brother to die at my hands if he was going to die at all. I knew it wasn\u2019t likely. He\u2019s too good a fighter to be brought down with one hit. In the end he managed one good hit on me, but my ice armor absorbed it all so he never drew blood. The others hit him with varying degrees of success. In the end it was Gawain that brought him down. As soon as I saw my friend swing his big blade I knew that my brother was going to die. In that moment I kind of hated Gawain. He took my brother from me. I knew that none of my friends were going to pull their punches. I knew they were aiming to kill. That was the whole point of the fucking fight. But to that last moment I still didn\u2019t want Rook to die. I know that Gawain was only honoring my brother\u2019s final request, but I was still mad at him for taking Rook from me.<br /> <br /> Never again will I see that wry smile on his face. Never again will I hear that wit and dry humor that I came to love so much. He had a unique way of looking at the world and for a while he shared that with me. He was always the more experienced of the two of us. He was always the teacher, but there came a time when we became equals. It was at that point that I realized how much he meant to me. At that point in time I didn\u2019t remember my sister, but I knew instinctually that I was missing something. I was missing my other half. And Rook filled that place in my heart. We hunted together. We killed together. We even, after our work was done, got drunk together. We were quite familiar with \u2018the world,\u2019 and knew how to get alcohol when we wanted. We\u2019d pick someone\u2019s pocket and get the money we needed to buy liquor or coffee. It wasn\u2019t very often that we did that, but it was fun. It was our time. The Lady let us have our time in \u2018the world,\u2019 as long as we had completed our tasks for her first.<br /> <br /> After the fight Gawain kind of slumped to his knees. I think he\u2019d been hyping himself up with powers and they all fled him at the same time. A small vindictive part of me hoped that he felt bad about when he\u2019d done. He\u2026he decapitated Rook in one swing. When it was all over I knelt down and picked up Rook\u2019s head and closed his eyes. There was no surprise in them. There was no anger. There was just determination and understanding. Gawain gathered up Rook\u2019s body and carried him to the van. I climbed in with Rook to keep him company as we made our way back to the Dream House. The plan was to bring him back to the Hollow and build a pyre for him there. The ground was always frozen in the Lady\u2019s realm so we never tried to bury our dead. We always built a pyre for them, and Rook was no exception. We gathered wood and dry underbrush to help things catch fire. I laid Rook carefully out on top and lit the fire myself. If anyone was going to send him to his final peace it was going to be me.<br /> <br /> I stayed with Rook until the pyre had completely burned out. I don\u2019t know how long it took. While I watched I cleaned Rooks knives. I had decided to keep them as a memento. Later, I got some kind of alcohol from the Dream House\u2019s Hedge reflection and toasted my brother. I think Luna stayed with me the whole time. Calamity and Gawain started out with us, watching. I remember Calamity asking if I was okay and for some reason I felt like being brutally honest, so I said \u201cNo.\u201d I told her that I had just watched a close friend kill my brother, and that no, I was not okay. I may have also mentioned that I was planning on getting spectacularly drunk. The rest of the time I just remembered my time with Rook and drank. I drank a lot. By the time the fire burned down to ashes I was well and truly drunk, but some reckless part of me wanted to keep drinking. I think that some small part of me thought that it wasn\u2019t right that Rook was dead and I wasn\u2019t. We were supposed to go down together, defending each other\u2019s backs. The fact that I had a hand in killing him was like ice in my veins. I think Luna stopped me from drinking enough for me to kill myself. She directed me to my room in the Hollow and I fell asleep. I wish I could say that my sleep was peaceful, but it wasn\u2019t. I knew it wouldn\u2019t be, and I know that it won\u2019t be for the foreseeable future. I suppose I deserve that though.<br /> <br /> My dreams were about the parking lot of the club where we caught him. At the time I had thought of half a dozen ways that I could disrupt or stop my friends from capturing Rook, or at least getting away with him. It almost always ended in blood, but not all of it mine or his. I thought of ways to get him out of there so that he might survive the encounter, but I did none of them. Some part of me feels like I betrayed him. Like I should have stopped my friends from capturing him. I knew it was futile though. We were not the only ones there. There was a Summer court assassin there as well. I think it was Louie Guo. He was up on a rooftop not far from the club that we were at. He was aiming his rifle at Rook before Gawain disrupted his line of sight by stepping in the way. Guo stood down and let us handle the situation. I confirmed for myself that Rook would not have harmed Elena. He just wanted to use her as bait. In a plea to get Rook to leave the Lady, Lori asked him what he remembered of his past. If he had anyone to go back to. He answered that everyone that he cared about had died before he joined the Lady. He had called upon the Death of Winter and she had answered and saved his life. Everyone else that he had cared about had died in that harsh winter. Ever since that day he served the Lady faithfully. I knew at that point that no matter what we said or did it would fall on deaf ears. He was Hers now and forever.<br /> <br /> I know logically that there was no way to save him. At least not without dying myself. Part of me wishes that I had joined him and tried to fight our way free, but I know how that would have ended. I know that I would be dead alongside my brother. But isn\u2019t that how things should be? Shouldn\u2019t I have laid down my life to save him? What the fuck is wrong with me? I know why I chose the side I did, but what made me do that? I thought that I could redeem him. I thought that I could save the Freehold from him. Those things I could have done. I could not have saved anyone else from him though. Is that what made me stop and check my actions? Is that why I didn\u2019t support my brother? I didn\u2019t want anyone else to be taken back to the Lady\u2019s realm. Did I really help kill my brother for a bunch of strangers? For a bunch of people that he may or may not take back to the Lady\u2019s land? What the fuck is wrong with me?<br /> <br /> Realistically I know that I would not see my friends be taken back to Arcadia. I would not see them be prisoners of the Gentry once again. But for a little while there I seriously doubted my own actions. At some point the lives of my friends became more important than the life of my brother and I\u2019m not exactly sure when or where that happened. I know that I would not betray my friends, yet I was tempted to in order to save Rook. I was so close to acting against them all. What would they think of me now? What would they think of me if they knew that I had been a hair\u2019s breadth away from betraying them for my brother? What right do I have now to stay here among them?<br /> <br /> Early this morning Calamity came by the Hollow to get me up. She brought water and coffee as a peace offering. She asked if I was up to going to therapy this morning. For an instant I was tempted to throw the coffee back at her and tell her to go fuck off, but I didn\u2019t. It took me a minute before I decided that I should probably go to the clinic this morning. I needed to talk to someone that would not judge me for my actions, for my thoughts. I know that my friends would say that they were there if I needed to talk, but I don\u2019t know how many of them would be willing for me to actually vent what I was thinking about Rook, about what happened, and about them. Calamity offered to listen and I admitted that I missed Rook. Calamity reiterated that I have friends to talk to if needs be. I am still not certain that they would really want to hear my thoughts right now.<br /> <br /> So I went to the clinic this morning. I went into my therapy session with the intention of venting about everything, but at least half of the time I stayed silent. I found that given the opportunity I could not speak. I wanted to rant about the injustice of it all, but couldn\u2019t. I did tell the therapist what had happened and to some extent what Rook meant to me. I could not fully convey that though. How do I explain how important he was to me in an hour? How do I explain the number of times that he h\u0336a\u0336s\u0336 had saved my ass, and how many times I returned the favor? We worked so closely for so many years. How do I explain that to people except to say that he was my brother? The thing is that I also have to take into account what they think of me for what I say. I have to consider how my words reflect on me. If I align myself too closely with Rook then my loyalty to this Freehold and my motley comes into question. If I show too much emotion over the death of my brother then people will start to wonder if I really aren\u2019t a loyalist myself. How do I be honest with people without being completely honest? They don\u2019t want to know the truth. They don\u2019t want to know what thoughts are actually going through my head right now. They don\u2019t want to know how much I hate them all for celebrating the death of my brother.<br /> <br /> They all get to go back to their lives and pretend nothing happened. They have their little orgies and act like all is right with the world. How the fuck am I supposed to fake that? How the fuck am I supposed to act like everything is alright and that I\u2019m right as rain? Truth is that I can\u2019t. I don\u2019t know what is going to happen to me because of it, but I can\u2019t pretend that nothing happened. I can\u2019t pretend that I didn\u2019t just lose one of the most important people in my life. I\u2019ll have to fake at least some of it though. They can\u2019t know how I actually feel. I would just put too much suspicion on me and my actions. I honestly don\u2019t mean the Freehold harm, but they would think I do if I told anyone what is really going through my head. I can\u2019t even really tell my therapist what is going through my head. I\u2019m sure that to some extent they report on suspicious activities or thoughts to the monarchs, and my thoughts would definitely be considered suspect.<br /> <br /> On the plus side to all of this I hear that Hunting Hawk was captured and turned over to the Winter court for holding. There was apparently a bit of a fight in the parking lot of the museum, in which De la Rocha defended her lady love from the loyalist who wanted to return her to her Keeper. Gawain and Luna were there as well helping to fend off some birds of prey that Hunting Hawk had called upon to help him. They managed to convince him to send the rest of the birds away and then handily knock him out. Something about Lori pulling a gun on him and yelling at him. I don\u2019t know the particulars.<br /> <br /> So, after therapy Calamity and I skipped our usual morning sparring match. I was not in the mood to fight with blades so soon after Rook\u2019s death and I think that Calamity figured that out. She said that she was not up to sparring and I just agreed with her. We went into the house where everyone else was and had our usual breakfast. I was still a bit hungover, but covered it up with more coffee and Gawain\u2019s excellent cooking. Lori and the others discussed what they wanted to do with Hunting Hawk. It was decided that Lori would ask him some questions focused on what happened to the two girls that she left behind when she fled Arcadia. So, I called Lowjack and explained that Lori and some others wanted to speak to Hunting Hawk that morning. He said that he would need at least two hours to have the man conscious. Apparently they were keeping him sedated so he couldn\u2019t escape. I think I\u2019d rather be locked up than drugged into oblivion, but that is just me. That was fine by Lori, so we planned to meet at the clinic in about two hours.<br /> <br /> Shortly after that Dr. Bright called me back to say that they had a vested interest in talking to Hunting Hawk after we did. Apparently he has been dreaming of the same Maria that haunts Twitch\u2019s dreams, or I suppose nightmares. In any case he was dreaming of her, which makes me wonder exactly what happened in that parking lot. I told Dr. Bright that his plans made sense and that I would pass along the note to the others. I came back to the kitchen and told them all what Dr. Bright had revealed to me. To say that Lori and De la Rocha were nervous was the understatement of the year. At that moment I would not have put it past Lori to have murdered the man that dared to malign her beloved. Just the look in her eye. It was revealing. Anyway, we all discussed options. Lori said that we had two options. We could admit that De la Rocha was Maria and get ahead of things or we could kill him. At least I\u2019m fairly certain that\u2019s what she was going to say before Gawain interrupted with his idea to contact Madame Spidertoes and get her involved in all of this. We could admit that the \u201cMaria\u201d that Twitch and Hunting Hawk dreamed of was a Darkling, but not exactly who it was. Madame Spidertoes is a well know advocate of all the Darklings in the Freehold. We could admit that Maria was among us but that she didn\u2019t mean any harm and was not a threat to the Freehold. She really has changed her ways since she left Arcadia, so that\u2019s not a lie. I was behind the idea to admit to Spidertoes who Maria really was. It is harder to keep a lie going when someone starts to poke holes in it. It\u2019s easier to have as much of the truth be a part of your story as possible. De la Rocha was trying to completely distance herself from who she was, which I admire, but which is hard to fully achieve. The truth was going to come out at some point considering there are those living that remember who she was. It was not feasible or advisable for De la Rocha to continue lying anymore. Coming clean to Madam Spidertoes first was the best option we had to getting control of the situation. Or at least telling Madame Spidertoes what was up and getting her support. I think it was mentioned that she already knew De la Rocha\u2019s secret. Which makes sense. They used to be lovers after all.<br /> <br /> Now I have to put my mask back on. I have to pretend that everything is okay. That I got my grief out with the pyre and the drinking. Truth is I don\u2019t know when this feeling will end. I don\u2019t know if I want it to. I have to remember him. I have to keep him alive in my thoughts at least. If I accept his passing then it would feel like I\u2019m giving up on his memory and I can\u2019t do that. Not now. Not yet. I know I won\u2019t be able to explain this to the others. How do I explain to them that despite the pain he caused me, the things he did to me in Her service, he was still my brother and I am still his? I guess I am still the monster after all.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> <b><b>It\u2019s Pretty Much a Recap Thing, Yeah.</b> </b><br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite and Julia Oldacre entered the spare room again, this time not locking the door. Julia did close the door after sticking her head out, while Insincere Marguerite leaned bonelessly against the couch.<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay so now that Maria is with Lori, what exactly did happen over there?\u201d Julia turned with her back to the door.<br /> <br /> \u201cI was not there when Maria had her\u2026moment. Apparently they were planning to move into the gallery when they caught sight of circling Hedge-Hawks. Hunting Hawk challenged them and was attacked by Maria, who was lying in wait. In addition to her drab clothes and hat, she had a scarf on apparently. The stand in for the scrubs.\u201d<br /> <br /> Julia smiled. \u201cI really hate I missed that, I mean\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Her fianc\u00e9e gave her a hard look. \u201cAnyway, she was attacked by most of the birds, though one injured Juliette. He hurt Maria but she,\u201d a dismissive gesture, \u201capparently recovered with his stolen light. Gawain kept him from fleeing by controlling the steel in some cars. He sent the birds away in exchange for his life. Or, something like that.\u201d<br /> <br /> Julia tilted her head. \u201cDarkling to Darkling, is it not a good thing that Maria is getting more in touch with that part of herself? I mean, I love the Maria de la Rocha who used to pretend she wasn\u2019t watching me paint on the roof, and who finally gave in and moved in with us, and will fight for us at the drop of a hat but\u2026we are Darklings. We can\u2019t repress that forever.\u201d<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite gave her a scolding look. \u201cC'est vrai, mais her being overwhelmed like that under uncontrolled circumstances is bad. I think she needs to channel it some and not run from it, but I want Maria to be De La Rocha, not Maria the crawler.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut we\u2019ll help her!\u201d Julia walked close enough Insincere Marguerite had to look up to look her in the eye. The Lurker was never sure if she did that on purpose when they argued, but she did not like it. At least in this context. She frowned a defiant frown.<br /> <br /> \u201cTelling her what to do will push her away. You know this. She must do as she wishes. This this this snapping and going after Hunting Hawk all the sudden leads to problems. Problems we are having to bring in Madame Spidertoes to solve.\u201d Julia would never admit it, but her flustered fianc\u00e9e waving her hands and struggling to stay in English was adorable. She had to stifle the urge to do it back at her. It would not go well.<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course you are right, Bon-Bon.\u201d Julia walked away from Insincere Marguerite. Not far, but enough to give her the space that the eight inch height difference did not leave the smaller woman craning her neck up. And giving her time to stifle a giggle. \u201cSo after that?\u201d<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite sat down on the couch. \u201cWell Rook was disguised as a friend of Elena\u2019s from school, Andrew apparently, and had messaged her phone. They met, and he was trying to guide her to a nearby club. We decided to do an ambush there. Juliette\u2019s group went on ahead, while Calamity and Davey followed Andrew\u2019s car, and I followed at a distance, my appearance changed and Jacob and Molly invisible in the back. When we got there, Davey took the initiative and changed to look like Lucian, which gave us all a start but caught Rook off guard enough that fighting was not necessary. \u201c The Darkling looked up, then down. \u201cThen Gawain spotted Louis Guo on an opposite roof with a sniper rifle.\u201d<br /> <br /> Julia\u2019s eyes widened. \u201cLouis? He was there? No one mentioned that.\u201d She walked over.<br /> <br /> \u201cYes, well.\u201d A small shrug. \u201cGawain imposed himself between the sniper and target, and we moved into the van to talk. There was a lot of talk. A lot of,\u201d The Lurker\u2019s voice was filled with contempt, \u201chonor, machismo, the sort of aggravating guy stuff Joan buys too much into, despite being smart enough to know better. \u201c<br /> <br /> \u201cDid anyone go after Louis?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNon, we had more immediate problems. Like sounding like Day courtiers jerking the circle.\u201d<br /> <br /> Julia raised an eyebrow. \u201cI don\u2019t think I know what that means?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot important.\u201d Dismissively. \u201cAnyway, they decided a duel to the death was the only way to do it. They dropped Juliette and I off, and went into the woods. A short time later, Maria messaged us to tell us it was over. I do not know exactly what happened.\u201d<br /> <br /> The Artist cocked her head. \u201cDid Maria take over again?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGiven she was herself when we drove back, and when the message was sent, I do not think so, no. We all came back in my car, where we got the message about Madame Spidertoes.\u201d<br /> <br /> Julia sat down, then interjected, \u201cYou should have seen her. I\u2019ve never seen her like that. She was pensive, scared. And\u2026ah\u2026maybe less\u2026cohesive? Her whole body was moving, some in strange ways.\u201d The Artist looked excited. \u201cShe said something was wrong with Maria. I had heard you guys were coming back, so I was able to assure her, but she insisted on waiting at the fountain.<br /> <br /> Her fianc\u00e9e blinked. \u201cAh well, that is disturbing. I learn more and more that I do not wish to make an enemy of Madame Spidertoes. Anything else while you were here?\u201d<br /> <br /> Julia shook her head. \u201cNot really. Andromeda commented she was happy that I was happy here working, but said the really missed the\u2026quirkiness\u2026of the Lady By The Sea having a resident artist who painted people from rooftops. My lurking is missed, apparently.\u201d<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite nodded. \u201cBut of course, the mysterious, beautiful woman who watches from high above, engaged in the painting, vanishing when approached. The whole thing it resonates with romance and mystery. I wager quite a few miss you, hein?\u201d She gave a playful grin.<br /> <br /> \u201cToo bad for them I\u2019m yours.\u201d The Artist rose and walked over to the door. \u201cOtherwise we just chatted some.\u201d A mischievous look crosses her face. \u201cAnd we talked about Lori.\u201d She smiled fondly at her love. \u201cSpeaking of me being yours, my dear, I don\u2019t suppose you might wear the lion mask again before too long\u2026?\u201d<br /> <br /> Her betrothed smiled and nodded as she rose, and Julia\u2019s grin was giddy as they walked out.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXXIII</i><br /> <br /> The Hawk fight: The Hedge Hawks did little damage but making called shots to the eyes to cause the Blinded Tilt. Gawain used Contracts of Elements: Metal for car-bending. I was describing the scene and deliberately altered the pitch and cadence of my voice when Maria attacked. I was describing slowly, the spoke louder and much faster describing her attack, mimicking the sort of jump scares from a zombie movie. Maria shrugged off nearly lethal damage using her Leechfinger powers to heal herself. Lorelei had to keep making Persuasion rolls to try to goad her toward lucidity. It was a powerful scene, with Hawk and Maria fighting in the cars while others dealt with the dive bombing. Gawain\u2019s quick thinking was probably all that stopped Hawk from either escaping or dying depending on Lori\u2019s success with Maria.<br /> <br /> The Rook fight: Not quite as satisfied here, but when you have Gawain, Calamity, Jacob, De La Rocha, Luna and Molly vs. a dude, dude is going to die, and dude is going to die fast. He is lucky he made it as long as he did. Your precious cinnamon roll was empowered by his Contracts of Potential and was an utter juggernaut. Jacob\u2019s Elemental Blessing proved a lifesaver as he shrugged off six lethal from a single hit with it.<br /> <br /> Other stuff: Jacob made a (difficult) Empathy roll to positively identify \u201cAndrew\u201d as Rook. Remember that Elemental weakness. Gawain\u2019s being supercharged by Contracts of Potential meant he was the only one to beat Louis Guo\u2019s excellent Stealth roll to get in position to snipe Rook.<br /> <br /> Maria was a low blow, but one I had been attempting to telegraph for a while. Not one caught onto her removing the identifiers she uses to keep her distance from the ravening Maria\u2026so much was going on, after all.<br /> <br /> Now what will come of it? Join us in two weeks and see. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T13:51:11-08:00","id":1034850,"title":"","content":"To quote F\u00fcd from Mighty Magiswords, &quot;Oooh, drama.&quot;<br /> <br /> Anyway, good stuff. Looking forward to the Hunting Hawk talk. Also, Lori's frustration honor was interesting and got me thinking about internal versus external honor and the Horizontal Honor involved with the Count Vincent debacle a while back.<br /> <br /> Question Baroness. Are you familiar with the Persona JRPGs? Particularly 3 and 4?<br /> <br /> Hope your holidays went well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T17:05:30-08:00","id":1034950,"title":"","content":"I too think honor is bullshit. kindness is good, justice is good at times and helping those who need it is great, but the stupid things honor makes you do is pointless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T17:06:47-08:00","id":1034952,"title":"","content":"Also, are we ever going to find out what was going on with Rowan's spooky house monster? Was it just a horror?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T17:46:28-08:00","id":1034963,"title":"","content":"Internal honor tends to be fine. Its the external honor when things can get messy and/or stupid. Then again that depends on the honor code being used by the group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T18:03:49-08:00","id":1034974,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure i understand what you mean by internal and external honor. Could you please explain it to this ignorant youngling?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T18:33:23-08:00","id":1034982,"title":"","content":"External honor is a matter of esteem (horizontal) and praise (vertical) within a social group. Internal honor is the code or standard one holds oneself to.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T18:47:02-08:00","id":1034991,"title":"","content":"I dunno then. Rook's problem had as many internal aspects as external ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T18:58:59-08:00","id":1035001,"title":"","content":"I concur.<br /> <br /> My statement was in reaction to your blanket comment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T07:40:41-08:00","id":1035217,"title":"","content":"blanket comments are usually a bit stupid I'll admit","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T23:43:29-08:00","id":1036466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play?p=1034850#post1034850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anyway, good stuff. Looking forward to the Hunting Hawk talk. Also, Lori's frustration honor was interesting and got me thinking about internal versus external honor and the Horizontal Honor involved with the Count Vincent debacle a while back.<br /> <br /> Question Baroness. Are you familiar with the Persona JRPGs? Particularly 3 and 4?<br /> <br /> Hope your holidays went well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Count Vincent?<br /> <br /> No I have not.<br /> <br /> Holidays were fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category