I'd agree. I don't get into JRPGs as well ( I tend to develop a specific character in mind that often clashes with their style, but I don't think badly of them. My main RPGs are Dragon Age: Inquisition, Dragon Age: Origins, Vampire: Bloodlines, Kingdoms of Amalur: Reckoning and Star Wars: The Old Republic, in roughly that order) but I hear very good things about that series.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T22:30:49-08:00","id":1037052,"title":"","content":"I tend to watch the games for the story. Couldn't get into playing them either.<br /> <br /> Played all of those except Amalur. Good choices all around <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T23:14:09-08:00","id":1040456,"title":"","content":"In the aftermath of the battles with the loyalists, the Motley faces their pasts. Also, finds out why Madame Spidertoes does not do diplomacy.<br /> <br /> Not that I am saying anything bad about Madame Spidertoes.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LXXIV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei Diary</b><br /> <br /> Okay, things have once more settled down a little, and while I won\u2019t claim that everything is peachy-keen, at least we all seem to be in a better place than we were this time yesterday. We\u2019ve gotten some closure on the matter of Hawk, we\u2019re hopeful that things are in a stable place as far as the Maria situation is concerned, and I\u2019ve managed to learn a bit more about my father\u2019s mysterious secret. Oh, and we made the first real, solid step toward rescuing Missy and Jane, too\u2026 which is both exhilarating and terrifying for me.<br /> <br /> We called Madame Spidertoes just after I finished writing my last entry, and once she understood what was at stake, she arrived at the Dream House a disturbingly short time later. We told her about the situation, and asked her to intervene on D\u2019s behalf\u2026 by speaking with the Winter Court and assuring them that Maria is not a threat to the Freehold, and that any action taken against her will invite the Madame\u2019s most extreme displeasure. She agreed to do what she could at once, and asked if any of us would like to accompany her to speak with Boss Lowjack.<br /> <br /> I decided to go along with her, figuring I could just drive on over to the clinic afterwards for my interview with Hawk. A few of the others had the same idea, so there were a fair number of us in Lowjack\u2019s bar to witness what happened next. I never want to get on Madame Spidertoes\u2019 bad side. I mean, I\u2019ve known that for a while, but I\u2019ve never actually seen her angry before, and it makes an impression. She told Lowjack in no uncertain terms that certain things were going to come to light about Maria in the near future, and that Maria had reformed and was not a danger to the Freehold. Then she went on to suggest what a bad idea it would be for anyone to act against Maria in any way.<br /> <br /> Lowjack\u2019s whole body was tight as he addressed Madame Spidertoes\u2019 concerns. \u201cI assure you, your word is good enough for me, Madame,\u201d he said in clipped tones. \u201cIf you say that Maria is not a danger to us, then we\u2019ll take no action against her. I\u2019ll speak with the other monarchs about it. It\u2019s my understanding that the only pledges in place require the Court to protect Twitch from Maria, not to harm her in any way. I\u2019ll double-check on that, of course, and make any necessary adjustments as quickly as possible. Now, could you please send the spiders away?\u201d<br /> <br /> I had been so focused on their confrontation that I hadn\u2019t noticed the thousands of spiders creeping into the room from all corners. They kept their distance from most of us, but seemed to have no compunctions against sidling right up to Lowjack\u2019s feet. After a few tense seconds, Madame Spidertoes smiled, and her little pets flowed out of the room like water. \u201cThank you,\u201d she said softly. \u201cI appreciate your cooperation in this matter.\u201d And just like that it was over.<br /> <br /> I thanked Boss Lowjack before we left the bar, and apologized for Madame Spidertoes\u2019 in-your-face manner during the preceding conversation. While I\u2019m grateful for anything Gladys can do to help my sweetie out of this predicament, I hadn\u2019t expected her to be quite so threatening during our opening salvo. I guess it\u2019s an Autumn Court thing. Anyway, Boss Lowjack didn\u2019t seem to hold it against me, and was certainly motivated to make sure D is kept safe from any fallout of Hawk\u2019s debriefing, so I\u2019ll call that one a win.<br /> <br /> As we walked back to our cars, Calamity drew me aside and offered to take my fear away again. I thanked her for the offer, but once more declined\u2026 albeit for a very different reason this time: I\u2019m not afraid of Hawk anymore. He was dangerous when we didn\u2019t know what he would do, when he was hiding in the shadows hoping to swoop in and spirit me off to Arcadia without alerting the others to his presence. But now? He\u2019s sedated, confined, and under heavy guard. I have my motley all around me. I have the power here, and I\u2019ll be damned if I\u2019ll let him terrorize me under those conditions.<br /> <br /> Dr. Bright met us at the clinic. He asked us very politely to leave Hawk in a condition to answer more questions following our visit. He also asked if he could leave a closed-circuit camera running in the room\u2026 he didn\u2019t insist, but I didn\u2019t see the harm in allowing it. Maria is as safe as she can be with Spidertoes\u2019 protection in place, so I didn\u2019t think Hawk would say anything that would implicate us unduly. Also, despite the somewhat bloodthirsty tone of my previous entry, I no longer had any reason to kill him.<br /> <br /> My gun was still in my purse, though.<br /> <br /> The interrogation was much simpler than I thought it would be. Hawk really didn\u2019t have much information that I didn\u2019t already know, though in the end it was Marguerite who really salvaged the situation. Hawk glared at me disdainfully as we entered, sitting perched on the edge of his chair like a dumb-ass.<br /> <br /> \u201cI suppose you\u2019re wondering why I\u2019m here,\u201d I began.<br /> <br /> \u201cNot at all,\u201d he interrupted. \u201cYour plan is obvious. You intend to trade me to Her Majesty in exchange for the other whores\u2019 freedom.\u201d<br /> <br /> That stopped me short, and I had to take a moment to recover. Of all the plans I had conceived to bring Missy and Jane home, that one had never occurred to me. And for good reason.<br /> <br /> \u201cHawk,\u201d I said after a moment, \u201cdo you really think she would make that trade?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course,\u201d he said immediately. \u201cI am Her Majesty\u2019s most trusted servant. I am far more valuable to her than a couple of empty-headed twitterers.\u201d<br /> <br /> I sighed a little at that. \u201cHawk\u2026 you were the help. I\u2019m sure the Empress trusted you a great deal, but\u2026 she trusted you to guard <u><u>us</u></u>. <u><u>We</u></u> were her most treasured possessions. Do you really think she\u2019d give us up for a glorified watchdog?\u201d<br /> <br /> He sniffed derisively. \u201cYou don\u2019t know what you\u2019re talking about, whore,\u201d he said, but he didn\u2019t offer any further arguments. Someone clearly has a very high opinion of himself.<br /> <br /> Yes, yes, I know\u2026 kettle, thou\u2019rt black.<br /> <br /> \u201cLook, Hawk,\u201d I said seriously, \u201cthere are only so many ways you can come out of this situation. The Freehold is going to try to rehabilitate you, and when they realize that they can\u2019t, they\u2019re going to execute you. If you can offer me something \u2013 some bit of information that might help save Missy and Jane, maybe \u2013 I\u2019ll talk to the people in charge about changing that outcome.\u201d<br /> <br /> He thought about that for a moment. \u201cIf you will not trade me for your friends, then I do not know what I can offer you. You know where they are within Her Majesty\u2019s domain. I followed you into the Hedge less than an hour after you left, so very little had changed.\u201d<br /> <br /> That brought me up short. He\u2019d left less than an hour after me, but arrived almost a year later. This rescue mission instantly became a lot more complicated.<br /> <br /> He was still talking. \u201cThere are other guards, of course, though none as trusted or capable as myself, and none of them are allowed near the songbirds.\u201d<br /> <br /> Marguerite cleared her throat. \u201cPerhaps a bargain could be struck after all,\u201d she mused. \u201cIf Monsieur Hawk returns to the Empress\u2019 realm, he would return to his post guarding your friends, non? Perhaps he would be willing to\u2026 look the other way when we arrive to liberate them\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I thought about it for a moment, and it seemed like the best option. \u201cWhat do you say, Hawk? Would you make a Pledge to allow us in and out of the Empress\u2019 Palace? We wouldn\u2019t ask you to help us, just refrain from stopping us. If you\u2019ll agree to that, I\u2019ll talk to the monarchs about releasing you.\u201d<br /> <br /> He pondered the offer for close to a minute, but I\u2019m pretty sure inside he was jumping at his chance to escape the Freehold with his feathers intact. \u201cI agree,\u201d he said at last.<br /> <br /> Marguerite crafted the Pledge, which also placed a time limit upon our rescue attempt. The Pledge is good for a decade (I\u2019m assured that it will remain in place until the proscribed time has passed for <u><u>everyone</u></u> involved, which is helpful). Hawk will not try to stop us or alert the Empress\u2019 forces to our presence when we go to rescue the girls, and in return I\u2019ll speak to the monarchs on his behalf. We made sure to inform him that the monarchs might place their own conditions on his release (like a pledge that he\u2019ll never return to the Freehold). I also told him that the Winter Court was probably going to ask him about the creature that attacked him in the parking lot, and that it would help his case if he was both honest and thorough in the information he provided. He was still willing to agree to our terms.<br /> <br /> We informed Dr. Bright that we were ready to leave, and made sure that he was aware of the deal we made with Hunting Hawk so that he wouldn\u2019t die during the Winter Court\u2019s interrogation (it turns out the caution was unnecessary; he had seen the whole thing on the closed-circuit camera).<br /> <br /> It was getting close to showtime by that point, so we headed back to the Dream House and began setting up for the evening\u2019s entertainment. I realized after a bit of thought that I\u2019d have to let Dad know what was going on at some point before I left to rescue Missy and Jane\u2026 it would be unforgivably cruel to disappear for God-knows-how-long again without warning him in advance. He\u2019d expressed curiosity about the shows we put on before, and as it was a Thursday, I figured it would be safe enough to invite him over. A short phone call later and everything was set.<br /> <br /> I\u2026 hadn\u2019t counted on Calamity\u2019s new act. She had decided to perform an AC/DC number called \u201cMistress for Christmas,\u201d and one look at her outfit was enough to firmly indicate that she was choosing to interpret the title\u2019s first word in a very specific manner. I confess that I panicked for a second and rushed up to her when I first saw her, telling her that my Dad was in the audience. She looked sort of chagrinned and asked if I wanted her to change and do a different act, but we were only a few minutes to curtain at that point.<br /> <br /> Thinking things over for a minute, I decided to let her go through with her original act. Dad\u2019s appearance was a last-minute change, and it wouldn\u2019t be fair for me to pull rank as the theater\u2019s Artistic Director and disrupt our set schedule because I\u2019d invited him over on a whim. In the end Dad was a little rattled by Calamity\u2019s act, but he weathered it fairly well (Gawain was good enough to distract him through the worst of it). And at least she didn\u2019t single him out specifically with any of her innuendo. And hey\u2026 anyone could tell that she was enjoying herself out there, so I guess it all worked out for the best in the end.<br /> <br /> As for me, I debuted my own Christmas number\u2026 my own smoky rendition of the Eartha Kitt classic \u201cSanta Baby.\u201d I strutted out in a fairly brief Santa Claus outfit, complete with hat and red fishnets and played to a pretty warm reception from the crowd. I might have toned down the sexual aspects of the performance the teensiest bit\u2026 but hey, my nearly 80-year-old Methodist preacher father was in the audience, so sue me. It still went over very well.<br /> <br /> After I had strutted and fretted my hour upon the stage (have I used that one before? I feel like I\u2019ve used that one before.), I schmoozed for a shorter-than-usual time and then joined Dad at his table. Consequently, I didn\u2019t get to meet the two Night Courtiers who had come from LA to check out the Dream House and invite us to their own club\u2026 but I\u2019ll talk more about that when and if we take them up on their offer.<br /> <br /> Oh, I should mention one other thing here. Elena has been a little down recently, due to both coping with Jacob\u2019s revelation and struggling with questions about her own identity. I introduced her and Natasha to my Dad last night, and suggested that they talk quietly about their experiences while I worked the crowd. Dad\u2019s always been a good listener, and I\u2019ve found recently that he can be a very calming influence on us troubled souls.<br /> <br /> Anyway, as the evening drew to a close, Dad smiled as I sat down across from him. \u201cYou are very talented, J\u2026 Lorelei,\u201d he said after a moment. \u201cBut then, I have always known that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you, sir,\u201d I said in response. \u201cAre you enjoying the rest of the show?\u201d<br /> <br /> He frowned slightly, but nodded. \u201cYou and your friends have achieved something remarkable here. And while I cannot claim that everything I have seen is entirely to my taste, the joy you bring to your audience is obvious.\u201d He cleared his throat softly before continuing. \u201cYour friend Calamity\u2019s act was\u2026 unexpected.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know,\u201d I said quickly, \u201cshe debuted it tonight. I hadn\u2019t seen it before, and I didn\u2019t know what she was planning when I invited you to come over. By the time I found out about it, it was too late to change the lineup. I\u2019m sorry if it offended you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI was not offended,\u201d he was quick to reassure me, \u201cmerely caught a bit off guard. She has a lot of passion.\u201d<br /> <br /> I had to laugh at that. \u201cThat she does,\u201d I agreed. Then I turned serious. \u201cReverend, could I speak with you privately for a few minutes?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course, Lorelei,\u201d he said, and took my hand as I led him out of the public areas and into an empty room.<br /> <br /> \u201cNow, what is this all about?\u201d he asked when we were alone. \u201cI\u2019ve noticed that you have been a bit distant of late\u2026 it\u2019s why I was so glad to receive your invitation tonight. What\u2019s been bothering you, Juliette?\u201d<br /> <br /> I gathered my thoughts. \u201cI\u2019m sorry about that, Dad,\u201d I said first. \u201cThere\u2019s been\u2026 well, there\u2019s been a little bit of danger in my life recently. We discovered just before last weekend that there was a Loyalist in town\u2026 that\u2019s what we call changelings who work for the Gentry willingly. This Loyalist was someone I knew\u2026 a man we called Hunting Hawk. He worked for the Empress, and it seemed likely that he was in town to try to take me back to her. We didn\u2019t know how closely he was watching me, so I didn\u2019t want to draw attention to our relationship.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI understand,\u201d Dad nodded. \u201cI assume this is also why Maria joined you at church last weekend. Are you safe? Is there anything I can do to help?\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled and took his hand. \u201cIt\u2019s over now, Dad, though I appreciate the offer. We managed to capture Hunting Hawk yesterday, and the Freehold is deciding how to deal with the situation now. But there\u2019s something else\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> He waited patiently for me to continue.<br /> <br /> \u201cI might have to\u2026 go away for a while,\u201d I said hesitantly. \u201cI might not be able to give you much warning. But I don\u2019t want you to worry if you don\u2019t see me for a couple of months, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> He frowned, and his brow creased. \u201cYou are being suspiciously vague, Juliette,\u201d he said with disapproval.<br /> <br /> I had to chuckle. \u201cYes, I suppose I am. Sorry, Dad\u2026 old habits die hard. Let me start over. We learned some things from Hunting Hawk, and we managed to strike a bargain with him. I think this bargain might help us rescue Missy and Jane. It\u2019ll be dangerous\u2026 but I <u><u>have</u></u> to help with the rescue when the time comes. I\u2019m the only person in the Freehold who\u2019s ever been to the Empress\u2019 domain, and\u2026 I promised.\u201d <br /> <br /> I was trying not to let my tears show by the end of this little speech, but I think he saw them anyway. He reached out and pulled me into his arms. \u201cI understand, Juliette,\u201d he said. \u201cOf course you want to help your friends\u2026 it\u2019s the right thing to do. I\u2019m <u><u>proud</u></u> of you,\u201d he added gruffly.<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks, Dad,\u201d I said, \u201cbut remember that time flows differently in Arcadia. So even during a quick trip there, months or <u><u>years</u></u> could pass on Earth. I just\u2026 I\u2019ll tell you before we go so that you won\u2019t have to wonder, but I don\u2019t want you to worry even if it seems like I\u2019m not coming back, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> He nodded. \u201cI\u2026 might be able to help you,\u201d he said hesitantly. \u201cI am far too old to participate in such activities myself, of course, but I have some... \u2018supplies\u2019 which might be of use to you. You are welcome to them if you think they would help.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat sort of supplies?\u201d I asked, confused.<br /> <br /> He shifted uneasily. \u201cPistols, rifles, armored clothing, ammunition\u2026 explosives,\u201d he said after a moment.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat?\u201d I asked, dumbfounded. \u201cWhy do you have all of that stuff, Dad?\u201d<br /> <br /> He didn\u2019t meet my gaze. \u201cIt\u2019s from another time,\u201d he said after a moment, \u201ca chapter of my life which is long since over.\u201d<br /> <br /> I raised an eyebrow at that. \u201cYou\u2019re being suspiciously vague, Dad,\u201d I commented with the hint of a grin.<br /> <br /> He gaped at me for a moment before laughing with what seemed like genuine amusement. \u201cI suppose I am at that, Juliette. Very well. After your fetch left home, I was\u2026 lost, I suppose. Directionless. My congregation began to drift away from me, because I had lost my drive. They came to me when I was at my lowest point, and offered me something I desperately needed: they offered me a purpose.\u201d<br /> <br /> There was something wistful in his eyes, like he was remembering good times, but there was also a sadness in his voice. I realized that I\u2019d been hearing it all along. \u201cThey called themselves The Long Night. They told me that there were monsters in the world, and over the course of the next few weeks, they <u><u>proved</u></u> it to me. Monsters stalked the city streets at night. Ageless, soulless horrors feeding upon the innocent, ruling from the shadows, manipulating the world over the course of generations\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cVampires,\u201d I said softly. \u201cI\u2019ve never met one that I know of, but I\u2019ve heard that they\u2019re real. There\u2019s supposed to be this club in L.A\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThose days are far behind me now, Juliette,\u201d he said, the sadness more pronounced now. \u201cI took to my new life with gusto, and I was <u><u>good</u></u> at it. I killed many of them, and left no clues behind as to my identity. And then one night\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat?\u201d I prompted gently after a few seconds.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe was about your age. She was one of them, but somehow different. She was frightened\u2026 not of me, but of what she had become. She had never asked to be a vampire, you see. She had not wanted to be \u2018embraced,\u2019 as they put it. She was trying to make the best of her impossible circumstances, and she didn\u2019t want to die. I let her hide from the Long Night in my home\u2026 but they eventually found her.\u201d<br /> <br /> He turned away, and his shoulders slumped as if with weariness. \u201cI lost my taste for the hunt after that. After all, if one vampire could be a good person, who is to say that there are not other good vampires out there? Who is to say that some of those I killed were not\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I took his hand and squeezed it. \u201cIt\u2019s okay, Dad,\u201d I said when he turned to look at me. \u201cThere\u2019s no rulebook for dealing with this sort of thing. You thought you were protecting people at first, and when you learned more about the situation, you stopped. And for what it\u2019s worth, speaking as someone who was kidnapped and mystically transformed against my will, I think you made the right choice.\u201d<br /> <br /> He smiled grimly. \u201cThank you, Juliette,\u201d he said softly. Then he seemed to remember something. \u201cOh\u2026 there is one more matter we should discuss before I take my leave. Your friends Elena and Natasha\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah,\u201d I said, \u201cElena\u2019s having a hard time dealing with the whole changeling thing, and I thought you might be able to help see her through that.\u201d<br /> <br /> Dad shook his head. \u201cActually, I wanted to speak with you about Natasha. She has been living with Elena for a while now, but is unable to contribute to her host\u2019s expenses, and this is beginning to put a strain on Elena\u2019s finances.\u201d He looked away for a moment. \u201cI have offered to take her in for a while. I thought you should know.\u201d<br /> <br /> That brought me up short. \u201cOkay,\u201d I said after a few seconds had passed. \u201cI know your heart\u2019s in the right place, Dad, and I know you want to help her. I\u2019d never say anything against that impulse. But there are a few things you should know first.\u201d<br /> <br /> He raised an eyebrow. \u201cIs she\u2026 supernatural in some way?\u201d he asked. It\u2019s so weird that my life is at the point where that\u2019s the first question my father thinks to ask about one of my friends.<br /> <br /> I shook my head. \u201cNot that I know of,\u201d I said. \u201cBut there have been people looking for her\u2026 dangerous people. She claims that they\u2019re agents of her father\u2019s political enemies, but privately some of us have wondered if her family might be involved in Russian organized crime. So just... be careful, okay? If anything strange happens around her, promise that you\u2019ll give us a call so we can look into it.\u201d<br /> <br /> He nodded. \u201cI will. Thank you for telling me.\u201d<br /> <br /> Then we hugged. Is it weird that a hug from my Dad is still the high point of my day\u2026 even on a day which included significant personal landmarks? I mean, it sounds horrible to say it, but when I was growing up back in Defiance I never particularly <u><u>liked</u></u> my father. And I always got the feeling that he didn\u2019t particularly like me either. I mean, I knew even then that deep down we loved each other, but there\u2019s a difference. We irritated each other; grated on each other\u2019s nerves. And that was even before I started actively <u><u>trying</u></u> to embarrass him.<br /> <br /> Now\u2026 well, things between us are like they were in my earliest memories\u2026 before we lost Mom. I can\u2019t lose that. I need to talk to Natasha before she moves in with him, to make sure that she\u2019s alert to all threats; that she won\u2019t let any harm befall him. I can\u2019t let anything happen to my Dad now that we\u2019ve finally found each other again.<br /> <br /> So in any case, we said our goodnights and I made my way up to Marguerite\u2019s room, where she, Julia, and D were waiting for me. They helped me release some of the tension that had built up in my muscles over the course of the day (and I returned the favor, of course), and then I slept like a stone for about eight hours.<br /> <br /> Sex Breakfast the next morning was interesting\u2026 and I confess I was a little giddy about learning Dad\u2019s secret past, and <u><u>might</u></u> have bragged about my badass vampire-slayer father the <u><u>teensiest</u></u> bit in front of my friends. It occurs to me now that Dad might not like me talking about that, since he played it so close to the chest even in front of me. I\u2019ll have to ask the others not to bring it up around him; I don\u2019t want to dredge up painful memories unnecessarily.<br /> <br /> I also mused that a story about someone who went around killing vampires for the greater good might make a good movie or TV show, and several of my friends gave each other meaningful looks. I can only assume that such a film or show became popular at some point during the three and a half decades I missed, but I\u2019m sure I\u2019ll catch up with it sooner or later.<br /> <br /> I also caught myself perching on the edge of my chair a couple of times. It felt very natural to sit that way. My friends were all good enough <u><u>not</u></u> to point out that this was the very behavior for which I had earlier mocked Hunting Hawk, and I\u2019m grateful for that. Besides, Marguerite really seemed turned on by the pose, if her smoldering gazes are any indication.<br /> <br /> Luna asked to speak to us as a motley after we\u2019d eaten our fill, and the news wasn\u2019t good. She\u2019d been going over the video footage from our new surveillance cameras, and had discovered that Yvette had been in the Dream House again. She\u2019d gotten in through another mirror, of course, and in the footage she appeared to be casing the joint. At one point she approached one of Julia\u2019s posters\u2026 one that depicted me. Though it was difficult to tell what she was doing without sound, she appeared to be assuring my image that she would \u201crescue\u201d me from Marguerite\u2019s clutches. Joy.<br /> <br /> We need to deal with this, and we need to do it soon. Marguerite is adamant that Yvette not be harmed, and I get that, though I think Calamity believes she\u2019s being unreasonable. We need to find a way to approach her without spooking her so that we can talk to her about what she\u2019s been doing. We might be able to convince her that Marguerite has really changed, and that we don\u2019t need her protection. We might be able to solve this one peacefully.<br /> <br /> One idea we discussed was the possibility of asking Night Queen Skitters if we could use Lizette\u2019s path through the Hedge to approach Yvette in Paris. She might feel more comfortable meeting with a few of us on her home turf, though Marguerite probably shouldn\u2019t be present for that initial meeting. I like this idea a lot, for a variety of reasons\u2026 not the least of which is, y\u2019know, that it would allow me to visit Paris!<br /> <br /> Moving on. I called Princess Jolie after we\u2019d discussed the matter of Yvette for a while, and let her know about the deal I\u2019d struck with Hunting Hawk. She was really supportive, and suggested that I speak with Queen Charlotte next, since she\u2019s the current reigning monarch. Jolie didn\u2019t think Charlotte would object too strenuously to our plan, and felt confident Lowjack would go for it as well. Augustine would be the only real hurdle we\u2019d need to vault. A part of me is thinking that we can leverage the apology he still owes me against any objections he might raise\u2026 but on the other hand, it\u2019s probably not a good idea to antagonize him when we need his approval. Y\u2019know, especially when D\u2019s position in the Freehold might still be precarious, and he\u2019s probably still a little sore at her about that whole assault and battery thing.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I called the Lighthouse and spoke with Moon, and ze told me that Charlotte wasn\u2019t particularly busy today and that she would probably be able to see me without an appointment if I just stopped by. I announced my intentions, and most of the rest of the motley opted to go with me to show their support (Gawain and Calamity decided to stay back to continue their work with Desiree\u2019s dream healing).<br /> <br /> We arrived at the Lighthouse a short time later, and Charlotte received us graciously. I apologized to Leanne, but asked her to give us some privacy since I really wasn\u2019t comfortable discussing our deal with Hawk in front of her. She agreed readily enough, and a few minutes later everything was set. Charlotte took a little convincing, but not much.<br /> <br /> \u201cI confess that I had assumed you had come to talk to me about something\u2026 else,\u201d she said with a sidelong glance at D.<br /> <br /> My honey bristled at this statement. \u201cYou got something you want to say to me?\u201d she asked belligerently.<br /> <br /> \u201cD\u2026\u201d I said quietly.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, I want to get this out in the open, babe,\u201d she said with real heat.<br /> <br /> Charlotte looked chagrinned. \u201cI had merely assumed, considering Madame Spidertoes\u2019 reaction to the Loyalist\u2019s news about Maria\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah?\u201d D said, narrowing her eyes.<br /> <br /> Charlotte sighed. \u201cWe all know how Spidertoes feels about you, de la Rocha,\u201d she said softly. \u201cAre you Maria?\u201d<br /> <br /> D puffed herself up even more. \u201cWhat if I am? Is that gonna be a problem?\u201d<br /> <br /> Charlotte shook her head. \u201cNot for me,\u201d she said simply.<br /> <br /> D backed off\u2026 slightly. \u201cOkay, then,\u201d she replied. <br /> <br /> And that was the end of that. I have <u><u>got</u></u> to talk to my honey about antagonizing monarchs. It\u2019s a bad habit that\u2019s going to come back to haunt her someday.<br /> <br /> So we all headed back to the Dream House to decompress before the show. Julia\u2019s been painting, Marguerite and D are just hanging out, Jacob is brooding, and Gawain and Calamity are still working with Desiree. I decided to spend some quality time with the birds out at the fountain in the hopes that I could get past whatever block is still keeping me from real flight. And it worked\u2026 sort of.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d been practicing the Contracts of Fang and Talon, and had recently mastered a clause that was supposed to grant the user the movement abilities of their totem animal (in my case, songbirds). I had thought this might be the answer to my prayers, but much to my frustration I found that I still couldn\u2019t fly. I can <u><u>jump</u></u> truly prodigious distances when I have the contract active, and I can glide for much longer times thanks to the added altitude, but true flight is still beyond me.<br /> <br /> So, in exploring the most advanced clause of the Contract in the hopes that it would give me another chance at the brass ring, I kinda sorta might have\u2026 turned myself into a bird. A little bit.<br /> <br /> I was a small bird\u2026 I\u2019m ashamed to admit that I don\u2019t know the exact species. From what I could see of myself, I was mostly bright green, with red, gold, and blue feathers on my wings and chest\u2026 I\u2019m guessing I was something vaguely tropical. I could still speak normally, but I could also sing and trill exactly like a real bird. And I could fly. <u><u>Really</u></u> fly! I spent the next hour or so blissing out on the sensation before duty demanded that I return to my usual shape and get ready for the show.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a little surprising with all the trauma I\u2019ve been through, but sometimes I really like the person I\u2019ve become.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> Friday, December 5<sup>th </sup><br /> Nine years, six months, seventeen days<br /> Days without stabbing: 1<br /> <br /> I am not a happy monster. And yes, I am a fucking monster. Clearly that\u2019s what they think I am despite what they\u2019ve said so why should I fucking bother to pretend I\u2019m anything else. They don\u2019t believe I have enough self control to talk to Yvette without stabbing her. Well fine, if that\u2019s what they want then maybe I will just ignore the woman breaking into our house night after night. Serve them right when she fucking murders them in their fucking sleep.<br /> <br /> I want a fucking drink but I can\u2019t right now. I\u2019m just writing in here while we wait for Desiree to fall asleep so Handsome and I can do the dream healing. Because they didn\u2019t want me there to talk to Queen Charlotte about sparing Hunting Hawk so he can help us sneak into the Violet Empress\u2019 realm to rescue Lori\u2019s friends. They\u2019ll want me there for THAT at least.<br /> <br /> I need to fucking clear my head. Handsome trusts me to help him fix the damage in his girlfriend\u2019s mind and I am not going to fucking let him down. Desiree needs our help. We\u2019ve been making real progress with her. I think she\u2019s starting to have some confidence in her ability to guide her own fate. We\u2019ve got a lot of work to do rebuilding her psyche where bad luck and the Director have torn it down but I have no doubts at this point that we can help her do it. <br /> <br /> My workout with White Maria this morning was good. My \u2018Mistress for Christmas\u2019 number went over really well last night. If Lori had bothered to tell me she was inviting her father I\u2019d have waited to debut it till tonight but she didn\u2019t let me know till curtain. Still, this is a fucking burlesque house and despite her concerns the old man managed to go the whole night without a case of the vapors.<br /> <br /> Julia\u2019s parents are apparently going to be here Saturday and she\u2019s likewise concerned about what number I\u2019m going to do in the lineup. Though she\u2019s less worried about me scandalizing them than she is about me seducing them. Apparently if I fuck her parents we can\u2019t be friends anymore\u2026<br /> <br /> And Jacob is keeping me at arm\u2019s length just like the rest of the Motley. He\u2019s trying to act like he\u2019s fine but I know that game too fucking well. I\u2019m worried about him. Luna\u2019s there for him and I don\u2019t know if he\u2019s opened up to her but at least he doesn\u2019t seem to be pushing her away. I\u2019m not sure what I can do to help and I don\u2019t want to pressure him. I just don\u2019t like standing idly by when he\u2019s hurting but it might be the best thing I can do right now.<br /> <br /> I shouldn\u2019t be upset with them. Of course they don\u2019t trust me. I\u2019m a murderer. I\u2019m sick inside. Even if I can control the darkness in my heart, it\u2019s still there. I felt it when we visited Hunting Hawk. The urge to cut that perfect skin. The urge to run my jagged glass down those glorious wings. He\u2019s beautiful and I wanted to ruin him. I ached to hear him whimper and watch his wounds weep tears of blood for me. I felt it when I was flirting with to that pretty little raveness last night. I wonder what she\u2019s heard about me? Was she blind to the terrible things I wanted to do to her or was that part of the allure of the dance? Maybe I\u2019ll find out when we visit the Unseelie Court.<br /> <br /> No, if anything, Gawain is the one that\u2019s foolish for trusting me. Desiree looks so pretty and innocent and soft laying there asleep. She\u2019s better for him than I am. Because as much as I do want to help her\u2026 Right now I also want so very much to hurt her.<br /> <br /> Because I am Calamity.<br /> <br /> And I will always be Calamity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T23:15:01-08:00","id":1040457,"title":"","content":"<b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Things are still spinning and it\u2019s not the alcohol this time. I close my eyes and I see Rook\u2019s last moments. I see Gawain\u2019s final sword stroke. I see Rook\u2019s pyre. Little things keep reminding me no matter how much I try and take my mind off of it. I smelled smoke on a patron that came to the bar to get a drink and my mind flashed to the other night. I actually had to pause a moment before I made his drink to make sure I would do it right. I haven\u2019t had that moment of doubt since I first started bartending. I covered it up by cutting a fresh lemon wedge for the drink while I thought about what went into it and in what quantities. Thankfully I only had the one moment of hesitation tonight. The doctor said that I should expect things like that to happen.<br /> <br /> So, my therapist recommended that I keep writing in this thing. Keeping track of my daily activities and all that. He said that it would be cathartic to get all my feelings out on paper rather than internalizing it. Logically it all makes sense, but I\u2019m not sure how much I\u2019m going to actually write in this book. I would much rather be hitting something really hard.<br /> <br /> Okay\u2026the day continued with Calamity calling Madame Spidertoes and asking her to come to the house so we can talk about the situation with Maria. She agreed to come over and we had our little talk. She seemed very concerned about De la Rocha\u2019s mental state. She kept making sure that De la Rocha was okay. No one explained to me what happened, but from the conversation, I assume that De la Rocha came a little too close to being what she had been in Arcadia for her, or anyone else\u2019s, comfort. Lori it seems, talked her down and Spidertoes was still worried about her former lover despite the latina\u2019s assurances. In any case Madame Spidertoes agreed to speak on De la Rocha\u2019s Maria\u2019s behalf to the monarchs.<br /> <br /> I can understand getting too close to one\u2019s old self all too well. When we got back from the clearing after the fight with Rook I just went straight to the Hedge with the others to set up the pyre. You\u2019d think that my first thought would be to assure my sister that I was okay, but nope, I didn\u2019t do that. I stepped into the role of fellow Knight and honored my fallen brother first. I still need to talk to Elena, but I don\u2019t know what to tell her. Do I just say that the problem has been taken care of and he won\u2019t be back to hurt her or anyone else? Or do I tell her the truth about Rook\u2019s final moments and admit to my sister that I just helped kill someone? I think this is why the Lady never wanted her Knights to have family or to remember them. It causes too much conflict. I don\u2019t know what to do. I can\u2019t tell Elena what I\u2019ve done. I don\u2019t know if she\u2019d understand. I was surprised that my motley understood, or at least could sympathize with my past. How do I tell Elena that her brother is a killer? Even in this one instance? I helped kill a man who was my friend. How do I even explain to her about the closeness I shared with a man that as far as she knew was out to hurt me? Fuck. I don\u2019t know what to do.<br /> <br /> I need to get back on track here. The doctor said that I should write my journals like I always have in the past, so I suppose that includes going over what we did. Some of it matters in the long run I suppose and I\u2019m going to want to remember that stuff. I also want to remember how supportive Luna has been this whole time. She hasn\u2019t said much, which is fine. I haven\u2019t been very communicative lately either, but she\u2019s been there for me. I don\u2019t deserve her.<br /> <br /> Our first stop was to go talk to Lowjack at his bar. We all went. I suppose to show solidarity, or maybe give character testimonials if need be. I don\u2019t know. I just wanted to get out of the house. So, we went to Lowjack\u2019s bar. We explained what was going on and Madame Spidertoes got more than a little intimidating towards the end of our talk. Spiders were actually crawling towards my monarch. Lowjack assured the Darkling elder that he had no intentions of harming Maria and asked nicely if she could call off the spiders. She eventually did. I think Lowjack was starting to get nervous about all the spiders. I know I was. It was more than a little creepy if you ask me.<br /> <br /> After that we went to go talk to Hunting Hawk at the Clinic. Doctor Bright let us know that the loyalist was free of drugs and may be a bit lethargic, but his mind was clear. That was fine by me. I was ready if he tried anything. I think most of us were prepared in case he tried to harm Lorelei. I don\u2019t know if he had any intention of doing that, but we had such a large group in his room that it would have been stupid for him to try anything. In any case Lorelei started questioning him about the Empress\u2019s defenses, the number of guards she has, who would replace Hunting Hawk since he was gone. He didn\u2019t know the answer to most of her questions, but he was being cooperative. Most of what he did know and tell us was not the most useful information, but I suppose something is better than nothing. With Rook I didn\u2019t need to ask those kinds of questions. I knew the answers and then some. Lori however was kept in a cage the whole time so she didn\u2019t get to see much else besides her immediate surroundings. Hunting Hawk was willing to talk. He just wasn\u2019t very useful. He did a good bit of preening too as he sat there perched on the chair. He was proud about having been the Empress\u2019s favorite hunter. I had to point out to him that he knew very little for someone that was supposedly held in such high esteem by his mistress.<br /> <br /> Is it a step back for me to say that I was proud of the trust the Lady showed me when I was in her service? I knew the names of all of her Knights, all of her Treasures, and most of the servants. I knew where people were deployed and generally what they were assigned to do. I knew guard rotations and routes. I could tell you what subjects were under her scrutiny and why. Some I know she wanted to recruit to serve her. Others were troublemakers that she was keeping an eye on with the intention of having them eliminated if they proved themselves to be a danger. On more than one occasion I was sent out with Rook to eliminate those kinds of threats. Generally, they were the \u201chero\u201d types who tried to gather together others and form a resistance against the Lady. The Lady hated the \u201chero\u201d types. They caused her no end of trouble. I was more than happy to eliminate the things that vexed my Lady.<br /> <br /> Hunting Hawk on the other hand is a simple guard with an over imagined sense of importance. He knows nothing of his own Lady\u2019s plans and is therefore worthless to us. He\u2019s not a very good guard either. The others came up with an oath for him to take where he promised to not come after Lori again and to look the other way when we go to Arcadia to retrieve Missy and Jane. They put the time frame for this oath at ten years due to the time disparity between the Empress\u2019s realm and \u2018the world.\u2019 Fortunately for us he sees the girls as worthless to the Empress and has no problems allowing his charges to be whisked away. Any guard caught doing that in the Lady\u2019s realm would be flayed alive. Her Treasures are just that, treasured. I have a feeling that if we actually go ahead with this plan and let Hunting Hawk go and return to Arcadia that he will be killed by the Empress for not doing his duty. Not that I have a problem with that. I would actually rather that we killed him here and just solved the problem all at once, but the others seemed to want to be charitable towards him for some reason. They were less than charitable when it came to Rook, but they\u2019ll let Hawk go free. If the Empress doesn\u2019t kill him there\u2019s no telling whether or not he might be sent out to find new prizes for her. Granted, it\u2019s not likely, but it could happen. But the others seem fine with letting him go. Don\u2019t they realize that if Hunting Hawk comes back without his charge then the Empress is going to get suspicious and wonder why? If he never came back at all she would rightly assume that he got caught. That is a fate that all loyalists face when they come to \u2018the world.\u2019<br /> <br /> I was only ever caught twice when I came to \u2018the world.\u2019 The first time was some freehold in Northern California. I was caught in the Hedge after unsuccessfully going after a runaway. I was headed back to get Rook when the Freehold\u2019s Blackbird Bishops caught me trying to leave. They beat me senseless then handcuffed me, and stuffed me in a small dark room. Unfortunately for them there is a way to dislocate one\u2019s thumb so you can get out of handcuffs. So, I dislocated my left thumb, got out of the cuffs and waited for my chance. It came a couple of hours later. I surprised and overpowered the man they had sent to get me and then ran for it. I\u2019m not the fastest runner, but I only had to be fast enough to get away from them for a short time. Once I got out I headed for the hills, which I knew rather well, and slipped through a gate to the Lady\u2019s realm. The second time I got caught was when I was sent to retrieve Delight. That was a failure on my part, though I suppose something good did come of it. I started to remember myself just enough to question the Lady. Just enough to decide that I didn\u2019t want to go back. I knew the Claire Falls Freehold wouldn\u2019t take me in, but it gave me the hope that some other Freehold might.<br /> <br /> Both times I got caught the Freehold that had me was planning on killing me. So I don\u2019t understand why we\u2019re giving Hunting Hawk the chance to leave when we killed Rook. Hawk isn\u2019t as much of a threat as Rook was, so I suppose people figure that letting him go will be okay. But Rook did say that he would promise not to come back for me or anyone else in the Freehold. He said that he would take an oath to that end, and he never broke his word. He would have kept it. I know, I know, he might have gone to a different community and taken someone back to the Lady\u2019s realm, but right at this moment it doesn\u2019t seem all that important. I miss my brother. I know I hadn\u2019t seen him for a long time before now but the possibility was always there. If I really needed to I could have left him a note at a dead drop and met up with him. But now, there is no possibility of ever seeing him again. I just burned his body. He\u2019s gone.<br /> <br /> Anyway\u2026after talking to Hawk and making that pledge we headed back to the Dream House. Most of the afternoon passed in a blur. I do remember that I had been tempted to see if Luna wanted to spar barehanded but I didn\u2019t really want to hit her so I didn\u2019t. The problem is that I want to hit someone or something hard and not have to pull my punches. I want to do damage to something. For that reason, I probably wouldn\u2019t make a very good sparring partner just now.<br /> <br /> The show was a little more exciting than usual. Lori\u2019s dad was in the audience, which was interesting when Calamity came out on the stage in bondage gear and did her number. The reverend\u2019s face went a little pink at that, but Gawain did a pretty good job distracting him at key points. Also, later in the evening Lori introduced my sister to the reverend. I guess so Elena will have someone to talk to that also knows about Changeling affairs and can sympathize with her. It\u2019s good to have a support network. Mr. Wells also talked to Natasha and offered her a place to stay since Elena can\u2019t afford to keep buying groceries for two. From what I heard she tentatively said yes.<br /> <br /> Apparently two new Night Courtiers from L.A. came by the club tonight as well. They had heard about what happened at the club parking lot with Rook and were curious about the motley. Calamity, Insincere Marguerite and Julia all went over to talk to them. Their names are Corvis and Corbin. They gave Calamity passes to their own club to give to the rest of us so we could see their place. Could be interesting I suppose. I\u2019m also curious about their interest in us. Why are they curious about one little motley that\u2019s not even in their town? I can see why they\u2019d be interested in us capturing Rook. That was in their own backyard. I suppose their interest stems from that whole thing. I still don\u2019t trust them though.<br /> <br /> And now to finish that bottle of vodka that I started on last night. My therapist suggested that I stay away from alcohol for the next few days so I can deal with the death of my brother with a clear head. But that\u2019s the thing. I don\u2019t want to deal with Rook\u2019s death with a clear head right now. I want to get drunk and forget about it. I want to be able to forget that he\u2019s gone and I do that better if my faculties are impaired.<br /> <br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> It didn\u2019t work. I am d\u0336u\u0336n\u0336k\u0336 \u0336r\u0336 \u0336 drunk off my ass and I still r\u0336e\u0336m\u0336m\u0336e\u0336m\u0336b\u0336r\u0336 remember e\u0336b\u0336e\u0336r\u0336y\u0336 everything. I still remmembr remember the good times with my brother. I think about coming back from missions and getting r\u0336e\u0336w\u0336r\u0336d\u0336e\u0336d\u0336 rewarded by the Lady for our hard work. She\u2019s the one that gave Rook his knives. The ones I have now. She gave them to him for doing a job well done. We had gone out to take down a rebellion that has had started up in the hills. The Lady sent Rook and I out to kill the leaders and maybe make an e\u0336s\u0336x\u0336a\u0336m\u0336p\u0336l\u0336 example of some of the others there so other p\u0336e\u0336p\u0336l\u0336e\u0336 people wouldn\u2019t get the same idea in their heads. We did our recon and found out who the ones in charge were and then snuck up on them in the night. We cut the throats of the leaders and let the others wake up in the morning to find the body\u2019s of t\u0336h\u0336e\u0336r\u0336e\u0336 \u0336t\u0336h\u0336i\u0336e\u0336r\u0336 \u0336 their friends laying there. Only one person woke up before we left and we make and an example out of him too. There was much in the way of s\u0336e\u0336c\u0336r\u0336e\u0336a\u0336m\u0336i\u0336n\u0336g\u0336 \u0336i\u0336n\u0336 screaming in the morning. Then while they were running a\u0336r\u0336u\u0336n\u0336d\u0336 around not knowing what to do Rook and I a\u0336t\u0336t\u0336a\u0336k\u0336e\u0336d\u0336 attacked quick and chased off the rest of them and teling telling t\u0336 \u0336h\u0336e\u0336m\u0336 them not to piss off the L\u0336a\u0336y\u0336d\u0336 Lady. It has had been a pretty e\u0336f\u0336e\u0336c\u0336t\u0336i\u0336v\u0336e\u0336 effective r\u0336e\u0336b\u0336a\u0336l\u0336l\u0336i\u0336e\u0336n\u0336 rebellion and we m\u0336a\u0336k\u0336d\u0336 made pretty effective warning. And for that the Lady honored us. I was made a full Knight in her service and Rook was gifted with his daggers. He carried them always.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Well today was an interesting day. I nursed my hangover with coffee and good food. I almost didn\u2019t eat, but experience has told me that it is better to have something in your stomach, so I ate. I had two cups of coffee and listened like the rest to Lori\u2019s story. I\u2019m not sure if her father wanted her spreading details of his past, but apparently Lori thought it was too cool for words and had to share. Turns out that in the past the good Reverend Wells was a vampire hunter in a group called the Long Night. It seems that he offered some of his old equipment to Lori if she needed it when we finally go to Arcadia to rescue her friends. Plus, time passes differently there than it does here. Hunting Hawk only left half an hour after Lori did, but it\u2019s been just shy of a year here. There\u2019s no telling how long we\u2019ll be gone when we go to the Empress\u2019s realm. It will likely just be minutes or hours there but much longer in \u2018the world.\u2019 Time passed faster in the Lady\u2019s realm than it does here. I spent 2 years in real time in her lands while it was so much longer there. So, I had the opposite experience that Lori did as far as the passage of time goes. We\u2019ll have to put things in place to handle a long absence on our part, like the running of the shows and managing the business side of things.<br /> <br /> Anyway, after Lori told us about her dad\u2019s past she called Jolie to get her opinion on the deal that was made with Hunting Hawk. Princess Jolie suggested that her fellow Spring Courtier call Queen Charlotte and talk to her about it. So, Lori set up an appointment to meet the Autumn Monarch this afternoon. Gawain and Calamity were going to work with Desiree on doing some more dream healing, and the rest of us were going to go to the Lighthouse.<br /> <br /> Before we left though Luna had some news. Apparently the cameras we installed caught Yvette coming through the mirrors again. The young woman looked at a portrait of Lori and then promised the picture that she would help to rescue her. It seems that Yvette is under the impression that our songstress is being held against her will. Insincere Marguerite seemed to take it all in stride. She suggested that someone leave Yvette a note and ask to meet to talk things over. She was adamant that her former lover not be harmed in any way, and looked at Calamity. I\u2019m not sure what she thought the razorhand was going to do, but she apparently thought that our motley mate might do Yvette some harm. Marguerite also suggested that we contact Nightqueen Skitters in Paris and see if the elder Autumn Courtier can help us find Yvette so we can set her straight.<br /> <br /> After all that Calamity and Gawain went off to do some dream healing with Desiree while the rest of us went to go talk to Queen Charlotte. The Queen was understanding of the whole thing and seemed to approve of our plans and the deal that was made with Hawk. The only excitement to that meeting was when De la Rocha confronted Charlotte about the whole Maria thing. De la Rocha implied that the Queen had looked right at her when the topic of Maria was brought up. Queen Charlotte flat out told De la Rocha that she was fine with Maria and all that entailed. She had no problems with it.<br /> <br /> Must be nice to have the kind of protection that De la Rocha does. She is protected by Madam Spidertoes, and that protection is unequivocal and definite. Spidertoes will protect Maria/De la Rocha with all that she is, which I\u2019ll admit is a good deterrent. She is old and powerful and very protective of her Darklings. While I have revealed my past to Lowjack, I do not think that I have the same kind of protection that De la Rocha does. Lowjack will look out for me as much as he can but it is not unconditional. I know that protection might expire. So in the meantime I have to make sure that I don\u2019t do anything that might cause suspicion to fall on me. I wonder how far I can go in my mourning of my friend before it looks suspicious? I dare not push it though. I can\u2019t blow up like De la Rocha did and get a handwave and understanding words. I have to watch what I say and what I do. Maybe I\u2019ll go out into the woods and take out my frustrations on some trees. Fewer witnesses that way. Though I suppose the gym downstairs would work as well. There is a heavy bag down there that I can take out my anger on. And my knuckles will last longer against the heavy bag than they will a tree.<br /> <br /> I know that I should be feeling more than this right now. I am angry and I miss Rook, but I still feel somewhat hollow too. Like some important part of me died the same time Rook did. What do I fill that void with? Can I fill it? I don\u2019t know if I should admit these feelings to my friends or even my therapist. I don\u2019t know how they would react. Would they think they think that I\u2019m letting the death of a Loyalist affect me too much, or would they understand that I just lost my brother? I want to say the latter, but I don\u2019t know. I just don\u2019t know. It\u2019s not fair. None of it. I know it wasn\u2019t likely that I was going to get my brother back, but I didn\u2019t want him to die. I should have tried harder. I should have said more. At the time all the arguments I had come up with just fled. I was so happy to see him in front of me and looking healthy. I couldn\u2019t come up with any good reasons for him to leave the Lady. I was too busy thinking of ways that we could both get out of there with minimal blood shed on our parts. With all of the motley there and Guo up on the roof it just wasn\u2019t going to end well and I knew that. Rook knew that. I just wish that it had ended differently than it did.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> It is unusual for me to feel guilt.<br /> <br /> But with everything going on, I do so. I feel some guilt that I am happy. Very happy. Deliriously happy. I have emerged from tribulations victorious. My relationships are going well, and I am hopeful of new ones. I just hope nothing casts a shadow.<br /> <br /> Julia has been in good spirits with the engagement. It has increased her productivity, and her passions. She paints like I have never seen. She glides smiling through the house, ethereal, beautiful. If I had to leave all my lovers for her, I sooner would then give her up.<br /> <br /> Of course, Maria calls her Timebomb for good reason. I confess some worry at her darker passions at times. Her recent painting was beautiful but disturbing. But that is her way.<br /> <br /> Things with Juliette and Maria are in a better place. Spidertoes met with Lowjack and was\u2026perhaps a tad bit more protective of her and hostile toward threats than necessary. Maria is willing to consider indulging her Darkling side a little now and then\u2026but not now. She needs to shore her identity up. Julia shall have to be disappointed. I worry a little her current bombasticness is a front and her holding onto herself is fragile, but I suspect it is more her needing to assert herself.<br /> <br /> With Hunting Hawk being dealt with and Maria relatively safe, Juliette is doing well. Worried about Maria, but well. But also, focused on her friends in Arcadia. I suspect we will deal with that sooner than many of us are ready for. But to Insincere Marguerite it is old hat to swipe Changelings out from under their Keeper\u2019s nose. Why, I employed one of my old tricks with Hunting Hawk as prisoner, having him promise to look the other way if we snuck in. Having a very different view of his importance than Juliette did, he agreed. It should be no bother to recover the girls. I am eager to impress Juliette with it. I know I will.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll be seeing Felicity tonight. It will be the next step in the dangerous dance we have had since we met in Los Angeles. In the between time, I wrecked her boyfriends house, inadvertently sabotaged his relationship with her, which lead to her moving out of LA, possibly inadvertently sabotaged her relationship with Princess Jolie\u2026I\u2019m honestly not sure why she is even speaking to me\u2026except that I inadvertently sabotaged them by being sexy and as she says \u201cregal\u201d which strikes I as strange. Still, dinner should be good, and she seems eager to see I. We will see where the night goes\u2026<br /> <br /> And Yvette is around. Julia says I should be worried, but I am not. I cannot imagine Yvette would really harm I. I would not tell Julia, but I positively hunger to meet her again. Yvette and I had something really special, that no other relationships have had. Unfortunately for her, I am marrying Julia. Fortunately for her, this does not necessarily cut her out of the equation.<br /> <br /> My love life is almost as complicated as Juliette\u2019s. I should probably deal with that. Or just be happy with it.<br /> <br /> Outside romance, concerned about Jacob. He has internalized a lot. It\u2019s dividing him from us, and he is cold to any affection from I. I suspect he has been damaged by this, probably more so than Maria. I am unsure what to do about it. I am glad he has Therapy. I\u2019d check with Calamity to make sure he is going, but she has distractions, one of which is the small shade on my garden.<br /> <br /> Calamity is fixated on Stasia, I think. She has been rather in a mood. Stasia is at the core of it. I am stepping up investigating the girl to give her more information. But she also is upset I don\u2019t want her talking to Yvette. Given her track record I think it would be imprudent to have her speak to her. She has \u201chelped\u201d me twice; the first time was the Motley collectively, she killed an operator of the table, got herself bound to a pledge, and made it so only Andromeda could use the table, which lead to her damage of the mind. The second time she destroyed my relationship with Chalcedony and the our friendship, the former of which she has taken no steps to repair. If she is sore I don\u2019t want her to do what she has repeatedly failed to do, and if she did with Yvette I could never forgive her. And she needs my forgiveness quite often, it seems. Someday Calamity will accept her actions have repercussions. But this has not occurred yet.<br /> <br /> Despite the good times I have put myself in a mood. I will write no more for now.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXXIV</i><br /> <br /> Of course, a tendency to challenge Monarchs aggressively can\u2019t possibly cause De La Rocha problems later on down the line.<br /> <br /> There is not a lot that calls for a lot of explanation really. Insincere Marguerite put forth a pledge with Hunting Hawk like she had learned from her Keeper. The crossover of Calamity\u2019s song choice and Lorelei inviting her dad were funny. Speaking of which The Long Night may be known to fans of <b>Hunter: The Vigil</b>.<br /> <br /> Hope to see you next time, Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T04:31:36-08:00","id":1040557,"title":"","content":"What does IM mean when she says that Calamity doesn't realize her actions have repercussions? She can be a bit impulsive, but she also carries around a lot of guilt about it and is continually trying to think beyond her momentary desires. Am I just misunderstanding what it means to not realize actions have repercussions? I'm not exactly very forward-planning myself","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T10:52:25-08:00","id":1040766,"title":"","content":"I suspect it is both out of irritation and less not understanding completely and more like say teaching a child. The journals come recently off the spat, and both women are irritated by it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 01-30-2017, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T12:25:53-08:00","id":1040810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroness Nerak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play?p=1040766#post1040766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect it is both out of irritation and less not understanding completely and more like say teaching a child. The journals come recently off the spat, and both women are irritated by it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> still confused. i get that it's because IM's not seeing this objectively, but not sure what you're talking about with &quot;like ...teaching a child&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T16:07:08-08:00","id":1040963,"title":"","content":"Calamity as a character has a tendency to rail against and try to change the consequences of her actions and despair when she cannot. She killed her parents, but is learning powers to try to get forgiven by them. She counts down time till she ceases to operate under the consequences of her killing Mr. Grey and brings it up almost every session. She made repeated attempts to get her relationship with Insincere Marguerite where it was after betraying her over Chalcedony without actually going to Chalcedony and took time to approach it really considering her feelings. <b>None of this makes her a bad character. Calamity is a good character and I like her. her behavior makes sense and is consistent. </b><br /> <br /> Calamity damaged her relationship with Insincere Marguerite both with her part in grabbing Chalcedony and how she handled the affair after. Both permanently damaged her friendship with her Seeming-mate. Insincere Marguerite believes that if Calamity does as usual with perceived threats, she will kill or anger Yvette and then beg for forgiveness again and sulk visibly around the house until Marguerite gives in in frustration like last time, as Calamity's track record is not good with these things. <br /> <br /> To be fair to Calamity she is correct that like many abusers, Insincere Marguerite underestimates her victim's ability to fight back. Speaking as GM, she is certainly well mentally and physically capable of hurting or killing Insincere Marguerite. Granted, to be fair to Insincere Marguerite and Lorelei, I as GM expect if Calamity confronts her, it will lead either to violence or threats of violence that will make it hard to have a peaceful resolution, because Calamity nearly always does one of those things. She is the Quietus of the group to make a <i>Night Train</i> comparison.<br /> <br /> Again, none of this is a condemnation of the character. She was taken as an adolescent, was essentially trapped in an adolescent role in Arcadia, and is still somewhat trapped in an adolescent mindset. This means she irritates various other characters including Insincere Marguerite and Lorelei, the former of who is, to be fair, the easiest to irritate in the group, and NPCs like Julia who is, to be fair, easily irritated by whatever irritates Insincere Marguerite. Conflict makes things interesting, and Calamity puts the most ripples in the water of the PCs. This means she contributes well to the drama, as if everyone did the right and mature thing, the game would get dull. And that Calamity is <i>trying</i> to do the right thing makes her sympathetic. <br /> <br /> But it means things like Lorelei and Insincere Marguerite not wanting her to confront Yvette makes sense too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T17:15:20-08:00","id":1040979,"title":"","content":"got it, Calamity thinks she can get rid of consequences with enough effort and time and she also generally is stuck in perpetual teenage rebellion. now i get what you're saying. Yep, I see a lot of me in that. I never really rebelled, but I can never really convinced myself that i can't just regress back to when the world was less big and scary without any consequences, despite rationally knowing that it's impossible and I need to accept adulthood","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T17:17:54-08:00","id":1040982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroness Nerak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play?p=1040963#post1040963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conflict makes things interesting, and Calamity puts the most ripples in the water of the PCs. This means she contributes well to the drama, as if everyone did the right and mature thing, the game would get dull.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mention that CoD gives mechanical incentives in the form of Beats and Willpower for doing that kind of stuff. That's always been an idea I've had a love-hate relationship with. More love though these days","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T18:10:43-08:00","id":1041012,"title":"","content":"It's a question of group. With the right group, conflict like that can be good. One just has to step from Actor to Author stance and be able to discuss it and be sure even conflict between PCs does not become conflict between players (unless that is what the group wants, though it seems foreign to me). Different groups have different levels of acceptable conflict, IC and OOC, and as long as that does not change all is well. I really don't think anyone has an OOC desire to throttle, say, Calamity's player as they do a good job separating, and care about the good of the game rather than just their PC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-b