color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T14:07:08-08:00","id":1047875,"title":"","content":"Time to check back in with the crew at the Dream House. There is much drama and excitement this time.<br /> <br /> For those more fond of dramatic tension, Gawain offhandedly mentions a major event in discussing things in his journal. You might want to read Lorelei\u2019s first then Gawain\u2019s if that is something that might bug you. If not have at. Also, as a note, Calamity and Insincere Marguerite get a little racy, as they occasionally do. Nothing severe, but wanted to mention.<br /> <i><br /> Session LXXV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Gawain\u2019s Memories</b><br /> <br /> Today was certainly an interesting day. For starters, I got us our fire breathing piranhas! It turned out easier than I was expecting - they stayed put the first time I summoned them up out of Desiree\u2019s dreams. I moved their water bubble into the filled moat around the Dream House and they took off. They\u2019re adorable (they did come from Desiree\u2019s dreams after all) and sometimes, even when you can\u2019t see into the water, you can see where they are from the bubbles and plumes of steam that shoot up occasionally. I really, you know, don\u2019t think it\u2019s fair of Insincere Marguerite to call them violent. Just because they are the unique carnivorous non-sentient animal (that I know of) that prefers their meat cooked doesn\u2019t make them more violent than any other carnivorous animal. She just got all Beaker-y when I pointed that out though, so...<br /> <br /> In other news, Calamity\u2019s getting serious about tracking down Anastasia. She pulled me and Becky aside to talk about it, saying things like she didn\u2019t want to make promises and stuff before she\u2019d talked to her old friend. Becky kept looking at me, and one time even asked me if I was OK (she\u2019s very good at taking care of people, you know?) and I didn\u2019t get it - I figured Calamity was talking about the whole being specific about relationships thing that Becky brought up, or maybe was just responding to the whole De la Rocha proposing to Lori thing and I wasn\u2019t really thinking about following suit anytime real soon and I don\u2019t *think* that sort of thing is contagious...<br /> <br /> Anyway, I realized a little later that Calamity maybe meant any kind of relationship stuff. All kinds of relationship stuff. I didn\u2019t say anything, right then. I mean, it\u2019s not like I\u2019m gonna say \u2018no, you can\u2019t go reconcile with the one person that you never forgot in all your time in Arcadia, the person who the thought of catalyzed your escape, because you might choose her over me\u2019. That just seems like, you know, a super dick move. And it\u2019s not like that\u2019s what she meant for sure anyway. She just wants to know, before... before anything else. Lots of things could happen. Like Calamity said, Anastacia\u2019s probably not gonna be all smiles and welcoming gestures, since Calamity\u2019s Fetch was pretty awful. But lots of things could happen, and I do think talking to Anastacia is the best thing for her, however it turns out. <br /> <br /> I\u2019ll always have hope.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Omigod omigod <u>omigod!!! </u><br /> <br /> How do you\u2026 I mean, I can\u2019t even\u2026 I mean, how am I supposed to talk about this rationally? My brain is so scrambled that it\u2019s frankly a miracle that I didn\u2019t fall on my ass and make a fool of myself on stage tonight. I didn\u2019t get a wink of sleep on Thursday night, and it\u2019s looking like tonight (which is almost over as I write this anyway) won\u2019t be much better. Whenever they\u2019re around me, all of my friends keep glancing at me and chuckling, so I <u>know</u> I must be acting like an idiot. But I don\u2019t care!<br /> <br /> Okay, Lori, time to try your best to get those little grey cells working and put things in sequential order. Otherwise there\u2019s no way in hell this entry is going to make sense when you come back and read it a few years down the line\u2026 and if there was ever an entry worth coming back to, this is going to be it!<br /> <br /> Where did I leave off with my last entry? Right, I had just discovered that I could turn myself into a bird, and was completely overcome by the joy of flight. I shared my new talent with my nearest and dearest, and most of them seemed to be fairly impressed. The ability to fly and go unnoticed \u2013 well, relatively unnoticed, anyway\u2026 there aren\u2019t that many rainbow-colored tropical songbirds in the area \u2013 could be a real boon to us in the future.<br /> <br /> Then it was time to get ready for the show. As I was getting ready to head backstage, D pulled me aside with a serious look on her face. \u201cWhat\u2019s up, babe?\u201d I asked, concerned.<br /> <br /> \u201cSpidertoes is going to be here tonight,\u201d she said soberly. \u201cMe being in danger earlier\u2026 it rattled her. I\u2019m going to sit with her and hold her hand\u2026 possibly literally. I just wanted to let you know ahead of time so it didn\u2019t come as a shock.\u201d<br /> <br /> I took her hand in both of mine. \u201cD,\u201d I said, \u201cthanks for telling me, but you know I trust you, right? Help out your ex. God knows she\u2019s helped us lately.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI won\u2019t sleep with her,\u201d D said dully. \u201cI know you don\u2019t want me to. And because I love you and I trust you, I\u2019m going to be honest here\u2026 that\u2019s probably the <u>only</u> reason I won\u2019t sleep with her.\u201d<br /> <br /> My chest tightened. \u201cD\u2026\u201d I said softly.<br /> <br /> She shook her head. \u201cIt\u2019s okay, Lori. It\u2019s not about this rule chafing me or anything like that this time. I won\u2019t sleep with her because I\u2019d never do anything to upset you, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> I averted my eyes. \u201cI\u2019ve been thinking about this \u2018rule\u2019 lately, actually,\u201d I said softly, \u201cand it\u2019s not fair. You\u2019ve been so good about this whole open relationship, and then I throw this jealousy and mistrust in your face\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s okay,\u201d she said again, and leaned in for a kiss. \u201cDon\u2019t say or do anything on the spur of the moment. Give it some thought.\u201d<br /> <br /> I solemnly promised that I wouldn\u2019t make any snap decisions, and went backstage to get dressed. I thought about Spidertoes, and D, and me, and tried desperately to focus on my performance (\u201cThe Christmas Song\u201d by Nat King Cole, done as sultrily as I could manage). Glancing up at the Girlfriend Table, I saw that Oleander had come by, and she was chatting idly with Julia. Marguerite had left before the show for a date with Felicity (and don\u2019t get me started on what a train wreck <u>that\u2019s</u> sure to be, but I digress), leaving her assistant to manage the lights and music for the evening.<br /> <br /> During my first number, I noticed Tamara Chance talking to D. The two of them left Spidertoes\u2019 table and had an animated discussion off to one side of the theater. It didn\u2019t look like either of them was angry or violent, but D was obviously emotionally engaged in whatever was passing between them. Tamara left after a minute or two and headed back to the bar.<br /> <br /> I approached D as soon as I had a break and asked what that was about. \u201cI\u2019m going to meet with Twitch,\u201d she said in response. \u201cThe two of us are going to talk things out. He\u2019ll have the chance to say what he needs to say to me, and I\u2019ll have the chance to apologize for what I did to him. We\u2019ll meet at the clinic. Neither of us will be allowed to have any weapons. It\u2019ll just be the two of us in the room together, and our conversation will be private\u2026 but each of us will be allowed to bring friends who will observe the meeting from behind glass. If either of us gets violent, our friends will be able to stop things from going too far.\u201d<br /> <br /> I put a hand on her shoulder. \u201cThis is a good thing, right?\u201d I said comfortingly.<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cDefinitely\u2026 but it won\u2019t be easy.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll be there,\u201d I promised, and she gave me a hug (right there in front of everyone, too). \u201cFor now, though, I need to get backstage and wrangle the performers.\u201d <br /> <br /> I made my way up to the girlfriend table after my last number, and planted myself between Julia and Oleander. I\u2019m sure they noticed that I was tense; my hands were probably shaking. I was a ball of nerves, and both of them eventually asked me what was wrong. I started spouting off about Spidertoes and D, and their relationship, and how it makes me sick to my stomach sometimes to think that one of my honey\u2019s exes has that much pull over her. I apologized to Oleander for dumping my emotions all over her like that, and she just smiled and squeezed my hand and said \u201cno problem, Angel, I like it when you confide in me.\u201d<br /> <br /> And it hit me like a bolt from the blue. I will never get over my anxiety about Spidertoes unless I confront it head-on. If D sleeps with her and comes back to me and nothing changes, then it proves what I claim I\u2019ve known all along: that we were meant to be together and nothing can ever come between us. If she continues to keep her distance because I\u2019m asking her to, then I\u2019ll stay tense whenever the two of them get close to each other (physically or metaphorically).<br /> <br /> I got up abruptly and strode toward the bar. I asked Jacob for a double-shot of bourbon. He asked me if I was all right (which was apparently hilarious to Tamara and Halley, who had been propping up the bar all evening), and I replied that everything was hunky-dory, or some such nonsense that he saw through instantly. Whatever, he gave me the drink anyway, and I downed it in one gulp.<br /> <br /> Thus fortified, I approached D and Spidertoes. They both greeted me warmly, and I made sure to express my heartfelt gratitude to Spidertoes for the actions she had taken on D\u2019s behalf. She graciously accepted my thanks, and nodded her assent when I asked if I could speak with my love alone for a few minutes.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat\u2019s this all about, babe?\u201d she asked as I led her to a vacant room.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ve changed my mind,\u201d I said. When she stared at me blankly for a couple of seconds, I decided that it might be helpful to elaborate. \u201cAbout Spidertoes,\u201d I continued. \u201cIf you want to sleep with her tonight, then\u2026 that\u2019s okay with me.\u201d<br /> <br /> D looked at me like I\u2019d sprouted horns. \u201cWhat?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cI trust you,\u201d I said. \u201cI love you. I <u>know</u> that you love me. And I <u>know</u> that you\u2019ll come back to me, no matter what. So I\u2019m going to let go of my jealousy and insecurity. If you tell me it\u2019s just sex, then I\u2019ll take you at your word. Have fun tonight, if that\u2019s what you want to do.\u201d<br /> <br /> D took my hand. \u201cAre you sure about this, babe?\u201d she asked. When I nodded, she narrowed her eyes. \u201cAnd this <u>isn\u2019t</u> going to make you mad or hurt you, right?\u201d she asked as a follow-up.<br /> <br /> I nodded again. \u201cI\u2019ll be okay,\u201d I promised. And yes, I realize that I\u2019m probably editing my memory to make myself appear more collected and mature than I actually was, but I\u2019m still pretty proud of the fact that I at least managed to keep my voice level and stop myself from tearing up.<br /> <br /> She leaned in for a kiss. \u201cThank you,\u201d she said softly as we disengaged.<br /> <br /> \u201cI love you, D,\u201d I said as she turned away.<br /> <br /> She turned back, winked, and grinned at me. \u201cI love you too, Lori,\u201d she said, and her voice was deadly serious.<br /> <br /> So I was kind of a wreck when I got back to the Girlfriend Table. Oleander was quick to comfort me, and Julia \u2013 God bless her \u2013 was a rock even though I know she was fighting off her own insecurities at the time. \u201cThose two aren\u2019t compatible long-term,\u201d she said to me over and over again.<br /> <br /> \u201cLook,\u201d Oleander said with an arm around my waist, \u201cif this is a bad night, I understand. I can head back to my place and plan to see you in a few days\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo,\u201d I said a little sniffily. \u201cI need you tonight.\u201d I looked over at Julia. \u201cI need you both tonight\u2026 if that\u2019s okay.\u201d<br /> <br /> The two of them looked at each other and nodded. In truth, Julia looked a little relieved; I don\u2019t think she wanted to spend last night alone either. The three of us headed upstairs before the crowds thinned out. I didn\u2019t want to see D and Spidertoes leaving together; I was afraid I wouldn\u2019t be able to keep my composure. What followed was a night of slow, comforting love. We <u>made</u> love, sure\u2026 but we mostly held each other and gave comfort (which I\u2019m sure was a little awkward for Oleander, but she bore it like a champ). I cried more than a little, and made each of them solemnly swear that they wouldn\u2019t <u>tell</u> D that I had cried. The last thing I wanted was for her to feel guilty for having hurt me when I practically pushed her into the act myself.<br /> <br /> So no, I didn\u2019t sleep last night. I don\u2019t think Julia did, either, though I\u2019m pretty sure Oleander drifted off at some point (she doesn\u2019t keep the same late hours as the rest of us regularly). I tried to read a medical journal, but just couldn\u2019t keep my mind on it. I staggered down to breakfast as soon as I thought anyone else might be awake (and still ended up sitting around by myself for the better part of an hour).<br /> <br /> D arrived just as Gawain was starting to cook, looking tired but satisfied. I quirked an eyebrow at her as she strutted into the kitchen. \u201cYou have fun last night?\u201d I asked, trying to put just the right amount of swagger into the question to draw attention away from how needy I suddenly felt.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh yeah,\u201d she said as she strode up to me. \u201cBut it\u2019s good to be home,\u201d she said more quietly as her arms settled around me. <br /> <br /> She sat down in one of the chairs, and I planted myself firmly in her lap, snuggling up against her and keeping myself squarely in her embrace. I tried not to be too clingy as we chatted, joked, and ate with the others, but I also communicated that I wanted her arms around me, and she seemed happy enough to oblige.<br /> <br /> Marguerite arrived a bit later, and Julia sort of let out the breath that she had been holding since the previous evening. Marguerite was cagey about how things had gone with Felicity, but seemed very pleased with herself. Joy. At least she was also sensitive to Julia\u2019s mood, and became quite solicitous after a few minutes.<br /> <br /> \u201cBon-bon,\u201d Julia said after Marguerite had broken her fast, \u201cyou said the two of us could take a walk on the pier together after you got back. Are you still up for it?\u201d<br /> <br /> Marguerite nodded. \u201cOui,\u201d she allowed in lazy French.<br /> <br /> Julia turned and looked pointedly at D. \u201cWould anyone <u>else</u> like to take a romantic walk along the pier?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> D sighed and turned to me with a twinkle in her eye. \u201cYou up for a walk, babe?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cI\u2019d love to spend time with you today, D,\u201d I said, \u201cbut I\u2019ve got to try to meet with Augustine this afternoon to make sure he\u2019s okay with the deal we made with Hawk.\u201d I turned back to Julia. \u201cWhy don\u2019t you two go ahead; D and I will take our own walk later.\u201d Everyone seemed happy with this arrangement, and the two of them bid the rest of us farewell.<br /> <br /> I got Old Billy\u2019s number from D and let him know that I\u2019d be by later to speak with his monarch, and he confirmed that Augustine was free from three to six that afternoon. \u201cYou want me to come with?\u201d D asked after I\u2019d hung up.<br /> <br /> \u201cAre you kidding?\u201d I asked. \u201cIf I had my way you\u2019d never leave. Just promise you\u2019ll behave this time, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> D snorted her derision. \u201cI promise I won\u2019t punch him unless he really deserves it,\u201d she growled after a moment.<br /> <br /> \u201cD,\u201d I said, \u201cI\u2019m serious. You\u2019ve got to stop antagonizing the monarchs. It\u2019s going to get you in real trouble one of these days.\u201d<br /> <br /> She shrugged it off. \u201cMaybe I wouldn\u2019t have such a problem with them if there was a Latino monarch\u2026 if there had <u>ever</u> been a Latino monarch in this Freehold.\u201d<br /> <br /> I knew it was a mistake as soon as I said it, but sometimes my mouth bypasses my brain. \u201cWhat does that have to do with anything?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> D\u2019s look darkened immediately. \u201cI guess there\u2019s nothing wrong with the setup if you\u2019re white,\u201d she muttered.<br /> <br /> I put my arms around her neck. \u201cSorry, honey,\u201d I whispered, \u201cI wasn\u2019t thinking. My idea was that a person\u2019s race doesn\u2019t necessarily make them a better leader\u2026 but of course that kind of thinking doesn\u2019t work if any group is being marginalized. I didn\u2019t mean to upset you.\u201d<br /> <br /> Her expression cleared a bit. \u201cI know,\u201d she said, giving me a squeeze. \u201cAnd hey\u2026 at least you\u2019re not Julia-crazy.\u201d She rolled her eyes. \u201cThank God you\u2019re not Julia-crazy. I like that you\u2019re not that possessive.\u201d She chuckled fondly. \u201cDid you hear her and Mags arguing about names earlier? Mags doesn\u2019t want to take Julia\u2019s name because it\u2019s \u2018too English,\u2019 and she doesn\u2019t want to let Julia take <u>her</u> name because she thinks her family are all horrible people.\u201d<br /> <br /> I laughed fondly. \u201cSilly argument. It doesn\u2019t matter who has what name as long as they love each other. I\u2019m sure they\u2019ll come to their senses soon enough.\u201d<br /> <br /> There was an awkward silence. I <u>hate</u> awkward silences; I always feel the need to fill them. Maybe that explains why I decided to mercilessly tease my love.<br /> <br /> \u201cI wouldn\u2019t mind taking your name, you know,\u201d I said with a wink.<br /> <br /> The blood rushed into her cheeks so quickly that I was honestly afraid she was going to faint. \u201cExcuse me,\u201d she mumbled as she bolted for the door, \u201cI have to go sit alone in the dark for about fifteen minutes. I\u2019ll be back before we go to see Augustine.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cD\u2026\u201d I said, but it was too late. I couldn\u2019t help but laugh a little at how easy it is to push her buttons sometimes.<br /> <br /> True to her word, she came back into the kitchen about a quarter of an hour later. I turned to face her, and noted with pride that most of her capillaries had closed once more, and she had regained her usual porcelain pallor.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sorry I teased you, honey,\u201d I said.<br /> <br /> She gave me a piercing stare. \u201cIs\u2026 is that something you really want, babe?\u201d she asked, and I knew that the time for teasing was over.<br /> <br /> I thought about it seriously for a few seconds, then shrugged. \u201cYeah,\u201d I said simply. \u201cI mean, not like <u>right now</u> or anything, but\u2026 when I think about the future, and where I want to be in five, ten, or fifty years, well\u2026 you\u2019re always there with me, D. You feel the same way, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> She didn\u2019t reply immediately. She looked at me. I mean, she <u>really</u> stared at me. Intently. After almost a full minute had passed (another one of those damned awkward silences), something changed in her eyes. She let her breath out in a rush, but got this funny little grin that only touched the corners of her mouth. \u201cFuck it,\u201d she said in a voice almost too low to hear.<br /> <br /> Then she got down on one knee. I could feel my eyebrows shooting up into my hairline.<br /> <br /> She took my left hand in both of hers. My mouth fell open in utter shock.<br /> <br /> \u201cJuliette, will you marry me?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not a question that anyone should answer lightly. It\u2019s a real commitment, and every aspect of what it means to you as a person should be carefully considered before answering yes or no. When it works, a marriage is a compact one enters into for the rest of one\u2019s life\u2026 and for changelings in particular that can be a very long time.<br /> <br /> Luckily, I\u2019d already considered all of that long ago. I\u2019ve known for six months or more what my answer would be when and if D ever got around to asking me. I think I managed to gasp out a \u201cyes\u201d almost before she finished the question.<br /> <br /> I pulled her to her feet and into my arms and we kissed. When we disengaged, Maria had this sort of goofy grin on her face (I can only imagine that it mirrored my own). Then she gave a mock-scowl. \u201cJulia\u2019s gonna kill me for doing this while she was out,\u201d she muttered to herself.<br /> <br /> \u201cDo not worry,\u201d Jacob said unexpectedly from across the room. A second later both of our phones chimed. It seems that our quick-thinking Russian friend had snapped a photograph of D proposing and then texted it to the motley.<br /> <br /> D\u2019s phone rang an almost impossibly short time later. \u201cYeah?\u201d she asked as she answered it. \u201cWell, no, it\u2019s not like I planned it or anything. No, I didn\u2019t have a ring. No, we haven\u2019t picked a date\u2026 Christ, Julia, it\u2019s only been like ninety seconds since I asked her!\u201d<br /> <br /> After my honey had successfully fended off the interrogation, we started talking seriously again. \u201cI was serious before, you know,\u201d I said as the talk turned to names. \u201cI wouldn\u2019t mind taking your name, if it\u2019s okay with you. I mean, I\u2019d be replacing my own fake name with your real name, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> D shrugged. \u201cWhen you put it that way, it makes sense. We have plenty of time to decide, though.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe should head over to the church to talk to Augustine soon,\u201d I said. \u201cYou guys want to come with?\u201d<br /> <br /> Most of the remaining motley decided to accompany us, but Gawain hemmed and hawed for a minute. \u201cI\u2019d like to go with you, but I really need to hit the grocery stores if we\u2019re going to host Julia\u2019s parents for dinner tonight. I was thinking Greek\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI could go shopping for you,\u201d Desiree offered. \u201cI\u2019m not Augustine\u2019s favorite person anyway, so I was going to skip the meeting.\u201d<br /> <br /> Gawain made a list and gave Desiree a little money. I made sure to thank her for her kindness. Maybe it\u2019s the giddiness of the engagement speaking, but I\u2019m beginning to think I\u2019ve been a little unfair to her lately. It\u2019s true that what she did isn\u2019t good for Marguerite, but she honestly thought it was the best way to protect the Freehold from the Director. And I\u2019m sure Gawain and Calamity will have her ship-shape in no time.<br /> <br /> I confess that I\u2019ve missed having her as a friend. No one else around here is quite as big a theater fan as I am.<br /> <br /> In any case, the meeting with Augustine went very smoothly. Billy ushered us into his presence, and there he was in all of his Summer Court majesty.<br /> <br /> He received us graciously, and with a sidelong glance at D, he approached and took my hand. \u201cMiss Grace,\u201d he said, \u201cI know you have business with me, but before we address it, I believe I owe you an apology. The things I said about you a few weeks ago were said in the heat of the moment, and were both unkind and untrue. Please accept my most sincere contrition.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled at him. What can I say? I was still high on the proposal, and in the mood to be forgiving. \u201cThank you, Viscount,\u201d I replied. \u201cI accept your apology, and assure you that the incident in question is already forgotten. I know that the blood of the Summer Court runs hot, and I want you to know that I appreciate all that you do to keep this Freehold safe.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou are kind to say so, Miss Grace. And I am glad my previous outburst no longer comes between us. Now\u2026 how can I help you today?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAre you aware of the Loyalist who was caught in LA a few days ago, Viscount?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> He nodded.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd are you aware of the bargain my motley made with him?\u201d I continued.<br /> <br /> \u201cYes, Miss Grace,\u201d he said somewhat hesitantly. \u201cIt is a little unusual to allow such a villain his liberty\u2026 but I understand that the greater good is served if we can effect the rescue of two others by his release. Your compact has my blessing, if that is what you came to ask.\u201d<br /> <br /> I gave him a smile. \u201cIt is. Thank you, Viscount,\u201d I said.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh,\u201d D piped up from somewhere behind me, \u201cLori and I are also getting hitched. Thought you might want to know.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCongratulations!\u201d Augustine said, and he sounded genuinely pleased to hear the news. \u201cThe love you two share is obvious to all. I would like to offer up this church for the ceremony\u2026 but then, I imagine Miss Grace would prefer to hold the wedding in her own church.\u201d<br /> <br /> I hadn\u2019t even begun to think about details like that yet, but he was right, of course. \u201cThat would be my ideal,\u201d I replied, \u201cbut we\u2019ll let you know when we have some firmer plans in place. Thank you so much, both for the offer and for your congratulations.\u201d<br /> <br /> We took our leave after that. I spent most of the ride home thinking about wedding things \u2013 dress, cake, ring, and so on \u2013 and looking at my friends. D was deliriously happy, and I know her well enough to know that it was genuine. Gawain seemed really happy as well. There was something brittle about Calamity\u2019s affected good humor, and I privately vowed not to do anything to rub my domestic bliss in her face more than was strictly necessary. And then I looked at Jacob\u2026<br /> <br /> \u201cShit,\u201d I murmured quietly to myself as I took in his expression. He\u2019s pleased that D and I are getting married, he really is. But he can\u2019t really be <u>happy</u> right now; not after what happened to Rook. I really thought about how he must feel for the first time\u2026 Rook was a brother to him for years. The two of them were the closest of friends. And we had to put him down. And he had to <u>watch</u>. And then, less than twenty-four hours later, he had to stand by and watch as we released another Loyalist that none of us even <u>like</u>. It must seem so unfair to him.<br /> <br /> When we got back to the Dream House, he sought me out to let me know that Boss Lowjack had also agreed to support our deal with Hawk. That made all four of the monarchs, and I breathed a sigh of relief.<br /> <br /> Before Jacob could retreat, I took him aside for a bit. \u201cYou\u2019re\u2026 probably sick of people asking how you\u2019re doing,\u201d I said by way of an opening.<br /> <br /> He gave me a wry grin and nodded.<br /> <br /> \u201cLook, Jacob\u2026 I\u2019m really happy right now and I can\u2019t pretend otherwise, but I haven\u2019t forgotten the loss you suffered on Wednesday. I can\u2019t claim to know how you feel right now, but I want you to know that I do <u>understand</u>. What happened to Rook was awful, and the fact that we agreed to let Hawk go the next day wasn\u2019t fair. I don\u2019t even <u>like</u> that dick, and I would never have agreed to it except\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt serves the greater good,\u201d Jacob said quietly. \u201cYou want to rescue your friends. I do not blame you for that. I will help you rescue them if I can.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you,\u201d I said, \u201cbut that\u2019s not what this is about. I know\u2026 I know you have a lot of things to work though, and I know you have Luna to help with that, but\u2026\u201d I struggled to find the right words. After a moment I found them. <br /> <br /> \u201c<u>You\u2019re</u> my brother, Jacob,\u201d I said at last. \u201cYou and Gawain and Ace are the only brothers I\u2019ve ever had. You mean so much to me, and I just want you to know that\u2026 that I\u2019m sorry about what happened to Rook, and that I\u2019ll give you your space, but I\u2019m here if there\u2019s anything I can do for you. Okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> He nodded. \u201cOkay,\u201d he said quietly. \u201cThank you.\u201d I\u2019m still not sure how he took that little speech. He can be really hard to read sometimes.<br /> <br /> Marguerite and Julia got back a little later, and of course there were many rounds of congratulations and much wedding talk. Julia <u>insisted</u> that D and I recreate the moment of the proposal (<u>twice</u>). She\u2019s asked more than once if we want to get married at the same time they are and have a double ceremony\u2026 and she\u2019s using language that suggests this is something that really appeals to her. We haven\u2019t given her an answer yet\u2026 D would probably be okay with either option, but there\u2019s a part of me that wants this event to just be about the two of us. I still love Marguerite and Julia, and I hope the four of us stay together forever\u2026 but I kind of want the actual <u>wedding</u> to be about me and D.<br /> <br /> We also talked a bit about what D and I were going to wear. Of course I\u2019m going with a traditional wedding dress (backless, natch), but D is uncertain as to whether she should wear a dress or a suit. I offered up my opinion that she looks damned hot in a suit\u2026 but of course if she wants to attend her own wedding in a dress then I\u2019m not about to object.<br /> <br /> Then Julia started in on the name question again, and offered up the idea that all <u>four</u> of us could take D\u2019s last name as our own. There was some support for this idea\u2026 but I\u2019m not sure how I feel about it. For one thing, that name is so much a part of D\u2019s identity in this Freehold that it might muddy the water if the rest of us take it as our own name. For another\u2026 well, while I\u2019m happy sharing most parts of my life with Marguerite and Julia, I think I kind of want this for myself.<br /> <br /> Plus, I\u2019m pretty sure \u201cLorelei of the Rock\u201d was a mythical siren of the Rhine River in Germanic myths, and considering my own vocation and reputation in the Freehold, that is just too badass for words, and I don\u2019t particularly want to share it. So, nyah. I might just decide to be a little selfish on this point.<br /> <br /> I called my Dad once I was finally able to escape from Julia\u2019s clutches. \u201cHello, Juliette,\u201d he said as he answered the phone, \u201cthis is a pleasant surprise. I wasn\u2019t expecting a call quite so soon after we spoke the other night.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI have news, Dad,\u201d I said, and I\u2019m sure he could hear the giddiness in my voice. \u201cAre you sitting down?\u201d<br /> <br /> He chuckled. \u201cYou have always had a flair for the dramatic, Juliette, but I am an old man. Pray do not belabor the suspense.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMaria proposed to me this morning!\u201d I gushed.<br /> <br /> Dad was quiet for a moment, and I got a little worried, but he must have just been surprised, because he sounded truly happy when he started to speak. \u201cCongratulations, Juliette!\u201d he said. \u201cAny fool can see how much you love her\u2026 and likewise any fool can see how fierce her desire to make you happy is. I only wish\u2026 well, I think that, had your mother survived, she would have quite liked Maria. As I do, of course.\u201d<br /> <br /> It was the highest praise I could think of. \u201cThanks, Dad,\u201d I said, getting a little choked up. \u201cLook, with the necessity of keeping the existence of changelings a secret, I can\u2019t let you give me away at the wedding, but D and I both want you to be a part of it. Would you\u2026 I mean, do you think you could maybe\u2026 perform the ceremony?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course,\u201d he said, and I thought I could hear him getting a little choked up in turn. \u201cI would be both honored and delighted.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks, Dad. Look, I gotta go\u2026 Julia\u2019s parents are coming over for dinner and I promised Gawain I would help him in the kitchen. I\u2019ll see you tomorrow, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> In point of fact, Gawain was already hard at work in the kitchen, which turned out to be a good thing as John and Linda arrived shortly after that. There were hugs at the door, and I got to spring the news by saying \u201cof course you remember my fianc\u00e9e, Maria,\u201d after which Julia confirmed that yes, we were newly engaged, and there was another round of hearty congratulations.<br /> <br /> Dinner was fantabulous, of course. True to his word, Gawain had made a delicious Greek-style dinner that I don\u2019t think I\u2019ll ever forget (most of it seemed to be wrapped in grape leaves). I couldn\u2019t afford to stuff myself right before a show, so I nibbled a few choice morsels and then made him promise he\u2019d put some in Tupperware in the fridge for me to snack on later.<br /> <br /> The subject of my supposedly voracious attraction to blondes somehow came up during dinner as well\u2026 I think someone might have mentioned that Gawain likes redheads when John and Linda were introduced to both Calamity and Desiree as his girlfriends, and then one thing led to another. John looked me up and down and then turned to his wife and told her that she\u2019d better watch out for me. I laughed it off with the others, but it sort of set the mood for the rest of the evening: both of them were very flirty, much to Julia\u2019s chagrin.<br /> <br /> There were a number of suggestions from my friends for numbers I could perform tonight. \u201cWedding Bell Blues,\u201d \u201cChapel of Love,\u201d \u201cWhite Wedding\u201d\u2026 in the end I decided <u>not</u> to announce our engagement to the audience just yet. When I hit the stage for my first number, I was instantly glad of that decision. Rowan was in the audience.<br /> <br /> As soon as I was free I joined her at her customary table. \u201cHi, sweetie,\u201d I said after a quick kiss hello. \u201cIt\u2019s so good to see you. How are you? How are things at your new place?\u201d<br /> <br /> She gave me a shy smile. \u201cI\u2019m doing much better now, thanks. I think I have my\u2026 my new home just about ready to receive visitors, if you\u2019re up for it.\u201d<br /> <br /> There was such hope in her eyes as she said that. For a split second I hated what I knew I had to do. \u201cThat\u2019s great, honey,\u201d I said fervently, \u201cand I can\u2019t wait to see it. But tonight\u2026 tonight\u2019s probably not the best time. You see\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> She raised an eyebrow quizzically. \u201cYes? Is everything okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> I sighed. \u201cYes, honey. Everything\u2019s fine. It\u2019s just that\u2026 D proposed to me today, so I need to spend the evening with her.\u201d<br /> <br /> Rowan\u2019s face fell. \u201cOh,\u201d she said simply.<br /> <br /> I took her hand in mine. \u201cRowan, honey, this doesn\u2019t change how I feel about you. D and I have discussed this. We\u2019re going to have an open marriage. Nothing between the two of us has to change.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh,\u201d she said again. \u201cWell, congratulations, I guess.\u201d Her smile was more than a little fixed, and it broke my heart.<br /> <br /> \u201cI do want to see your new place, Rowan. I want to spend time with you. Maybe tomorrow night? Or Tuesday, if that\u2019s better\u2026 we have our movie night thing on Monday, but I\u2019m sure the others wouldn\u2019t mind if you came by for that\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, maybe,\u201d she said, obviously distracted. \u201cI\u2019ll have to think about what would work best. I\u2019m\u2026 I\u2019m looking forward to it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay,\u201d I said, \u201cjust let me know so that I can plan for it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWill do,\u201d she said with false cheer. She squeezed my hand gently. \u201cDon\u2019t let me keep you, Lori,\u201d she said softly. \u201cI know you have\u2026 other obligations tonight. I\u2019ll\u2026 I\u2019ll see you soon.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCount on it,\u201d I said, and leaned in to give her another kiss. I\u2019m not sure if she actually flinched away from me a little bit or if it was just my imagination running away with me.<br /> <br /> She left about five minutes later. The show wasn\u2019t even over yet.<br /> <br /> That reminds me\u2026 Oleander wasn\u2019t at the show tonight, and she left before the proposal this morning. She\u2019s the only one of my steady girlfriends who doesn\u2019t know the news. I should probably stop by her place after church and tell her in person.<br /> <br /> I had to have one more conversation before I could lose myself in my fianc\u00e9e\u2019s arms. I asked Natasha if the two of us could speak in private, and she consented readily enough. I told her that I knew that my father had offered to take her in, and just asked her to be mindful of his safety. I don\u2019t think she would intentionally do anything to hurt him, mind you\u2026 but some very dangerous people had been after her very recently. I asked her to call us first if she had any reason to think that they might make another attempt to capture or kill her. The last thing I need is for my father to get caught in that sort of crossfire, bad-ass retired vampire hunter or not.<br /> <br /> Though she didn\u2019t seem to think much of my concerns, she did promise to alert me if she felt that <u>either</u> of them was in any danger. I feel a lot better about that whole situation now.<br /> <br /> So D and I slipped out just as the show was ending. Honestly, it was sort of a relief to avoid the usual hob-nobbing for once. We drove out to the pier together, and finally got that romantic walk. We walked with our arms around each other\u2019s waists, and talked about whatever silly things happened to pop into our minds. We paid a street vendor too much for a couple of warm beers. We sat on a wobbly bench and kissed in the moonlight, oblivious to the crowds around us. And I thought to myself \u201cif this is what I have to look forward to for the rest of my life, well, I think I could be content with that.\u201d Life is good.<br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei de la Rocha</b><br /> (tee-hee)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T14:07:43-08:00","id":1047876,"title":"","content":"<b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> Sunday, December 7th<br /> Nine years, six months, fifteen days<br /> Days without stabbing: 3<br /> <br /> So\u2026 Becky was certainly in a mood last night. I'd say she rode me hard and put me up wet, but that would imply she ever let up more than long enough to hit us both with enough healing magic to keep things going. It was certainly not how I had expected the night to go but I am not fucking complaining. She needed to hunt and I needed to have my ability to form coherent thoughts driven out of my head. And no offense to Dr Emmett or White Maria but it was way more enjoyable than meditation. I ought to be passed out but after convincing her to teach me (as Insincere Marguerite would put it) the poofing I just had to try it out. I seem to have done it well enough. My brain\u2019s still a little hazy, feels kinda like I\u2019m floating while the rest of my body is quite delightfully ragged (I am not Spring enough to learn actual healing, despite how useful that trick would be to know.) It\u2019s not that I doubt she\u2019ll heal me, but sleep tends to reset her succubus conditioning and she was, as I said, in quite the mood last night. I\u2019m most likely being overly worried. So far she\u2019s never been embarrassed or ashamed or bothered by anything she\u2019s done no matter how far from her usual temperament it is. I cannot imagine being so calm and accepting of having another person's desires imprinted on you like that. Of course, I guess she had to either embrace being exactly the fucktoy her partner wants or give up sex. And she does like sex. Also, she does enjoy knowing that she did everything you wanted her to even if you wouldn\u2019t or couldn\u2019t admit to wanting it.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know if she was like that before or if her Keeper did that to her but ultimately it\u2019s who she is now and she\u2019s at peace with it. I don\u2019t think I will ever be. I hope not at least. I would never want to be so comfortable bending her to my will that it didn\u2019t give me at least a little pause. But she trusts me. She wouldn\u2019t keep coming back to me if she didn\u2019t. She wouldn\u2019t be entertaining the notion of any sort of commitment if she didn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> My Dragon and my Knight. I don\u2019t deserve either of them and certainly not both of them. Then again, the universe isn\u2019t fair. It\u2019s random and uncaring. As hard as I find it to understand how they can sometimes, they\u2019re with me because they love me. (And we all know what love does to a person.) And I love them back. I love them too much to not be honest with them about Anastasia Zelenko.<br /> <br /> I can\u2019t help but feel like she and I would both be better off if I just stayed away. I\u2019m happier here with my motley and my lovers and this life than I have any right to be. Why am I risking all of that on the ghost of my feelings for a woman I haven\u2019t seen in so long? And what do I even feel for her? We were best friends, practically sisters. Hell, closer than most of the actual sisters we knew. We shared our first kiss together but what would that have actually meant? Would we have really become lovers? I feel so sure of it now, looking back but how can I be? And if she hasn\u2019t seen the Sinister Bitch since High School then what is seeing me going to do? I\u2019m going to walk into her life and reopen those wounds. What right do I have to do that to her just because I can\u2019t let go of these memories?<br /> <br /> But what if it\u2019s not just me that can\u2019t let it go? What if she still wonders what happened and why it all went so wrong? What if those wounds aren\u2019t really healed? I think that frightens me almost as much as her slamming the door in my face and refusing to talk to me. What if my explanation answers the questions that she\u2019s been plagued by all these years? What if\u2026 What if she\u2019s missed me as much as I missed her? What if we kiss again, not as two uncertain and clueless teenagers but as the two halves of the same soul that the forces of time and Arcadia couldn\u2019t keep apart?<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know what\u2019s going to happen but I do know that I have to find out. I have to do this. I just hope that this doesn\u2019t bring everything I have with Beautiful and Handsome crashing down like the Tower of Babel.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s really not the right time for this but given how things work I\u2019m not sure there will ever be a perfect time. I need to do this before we go to rescue Lori\u2019s friends. If we\u2019re gone months or years and I return to find she\u2019s gone or something\u2019s happened to her I would always regret missing my chance. I need to do this before I make any promises to Handsome and Beautiful. I\u2019m not planning to do anything drastic just because D proposed to Lori. But seeing the four of them and all makes me realize that even without such a formal gesture there is something just as real and strong growing between us. I owe it to them to be honest about this and I can\u2019t do that until I discover what, if anything, still exists between Stasia and myself.<br /> <br /> Yeah, this has certainly been a week for all of us. The fallout from D\u2019s past as Maria is still settling. It brought Spidertoes to the Dream House Friday night and took D back to her web afterward. And Insincere Marguerite wasn\u2019t back from her date with Felicity till sex breakfast, so Julia and Lori were both more than a little on edge. I honestly can\u2019t say what the fucking hell was going on with D and Spidertoes. Maybe it was D proving to herself she did know how to quit Spidertoes since she did turn right around and propose to Lori yesterday morning. That certainly had Lori giddy all day. (And D despite her denials.)<br /> <br /> I can\u2019t say things were quite as positive for Julia and Marguerite. I mean, Julia\u2019s way less secure than Lori on the best of days and Marguerite, as is her way, strutted in grinning like the cat that eaten the canary. She did head out to spend the afternoon at the pier with Julia but she treated the whole thing with a rather cavalier attitude. And honestly, I can\u2019t see anything good coming out of this for either Felicity and Marguerite. I fear this whole whatever-the-fuck-it-is they\u2019re doing is going to end badly all around. But given how things stand between Marguerite and I unless it reaches the point of either Julia or Felicity trying to murder her all she wants from me is for me to mind my own damn business. (And really, given how she\u2019s acted toward me with this whole Yvette business even then I suspect she\u2019d rather I stay out of it.)<br /> <br /> Not that I have too much room to talk about bad decisions after that stunt I pulled with Dark Kimberly. I mean, things with her and Annika have been \u2018on hold\u2019 for months now and they really need to either call it or find some way to get back together. But they haven\u2019t and until they do Dark Kimberly is my friend\u2019s girl. But fuck, she\u2019s just\u2026 so\u2026 tempting\u2026 I got a taste of her submissive side that night with her and Davey but that isn\u2019t his thing so we didn\u2019t really delve into it. And oh how I want to delve all the way to the sweet chewy core of that little tootsie pop. So, when I hit the floor last night after doing my Mistress for Christmas number and saw her there I just\u2026 I went for her. I\u2019ve been kinda wanting to pull my own version of that knife trick from Aliens on someone for a while now and I knew that she was the perfect choice given what the fear would do to her. And Annika wasn\u2019t there (because I wouldn\u2019t have done it in front of her, I\u2019m not THAT tacky). So I came up and leaned into her back, rubbing against her as I slid my left hand down her arm to splay her fingers and then cover them. I whispered, \u201cDon\u2019t move,\u201d into her ear and then I brought my knife around and did a flurry of mumbletypeg around her hand before lifting the knife, spotless of course, to her face and then slithered into the chair beside her. Her eyes were saucers and her breath was quick and shallow (and doing wonderful things to her breasts\u2026) I flirted pretty shamelessly with her and teased her shin under the table with the toe of my boot since I still had my red leather dominatrix outfit on from the act and I know the girl\u2019s got a thing for boots. At the time I told myself I was just teasing her to get that out of my system before I moved over to Becky so I wouldn\u2019t put her in that space (I mean, we have done that and she has assured me she was okay with it but I am not comfortable making Beautiful submissive when she\u2019s so not normally.) But truth be told, I wanted to make the poor thing squirm and if Becky hadn\u2019t been there I would most likely have taken that little pretty home and seen just how deep her rabbit hole goes. Because yeah, on top of all the relationship madness I am caught up in I need to add fucking my mentor and friend\u2019s not-quite-ex to the mix.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile Jacob is still dealing with Rook\u2019s death and I still seem to be able to do fuck all to help him. He has Luna and I did make sure to let him know I was here if he needed me. I know he has to hate people crowding him and I really am trying to give him his space but I want so badly to do something. Of course, I\u2019m not sure there IS anything I or anyone else can do to help right now. He\u2019s got to work through this on his own. But just because I know that doesn\u2019t mean I have to like it.<br /> <br /> At least Desiree managed to help Handsome get the hedge house\u2019s moot stocked. Ever since Ace put that bug in his ear about fire-breathing piranha he\u2019s been trying to get his Cobblethought up enough to make it happen. Apparently he convinced her to dream of fire-breathing piranha for him while I was keeping my vigil to make sure that Yvette didn\u2019t, you know, fucking murder everyone in their sleep. And so yesterday they headed into the hedge and he plucked a school of oddly adorable little beasties (because it was Desiree dreaming of them after all) out of her head and set them loose in the moot. I love seeing him kinda goofy like that and I\u2019m rather proud of myself for only being a tiny bit jealous that it was Desiree sharing that moment with him rather than me.<br /> <br /> It turned out to be a bit of a busy afternoon. Despite being quite giddy, Lori wasn\u2019t quite too twitterpated to get on about seeing to the arrangements for our deal with Hunting Hawk. We all headed over to the Summer Court\u2019s church where Viscount Augustine was, as usual, formal and noble and decent. He delivered that apology to Lori he\u2019d promised and agreed that saving two others from Arcadia was more important than executing a loyalist. And he did seem to like the idea of the poetic justice of Hawk\u2019s likely fate at his Keeper\u2019s hands after his betrayal. D informed him of the wedding and he offered the use of his church. I think Lori\u2019s angling to do it at her Dad\u2019s even if she can\u2019t exactly have him in the ceremony having him preside does seem like a good way to make him a part of it and I know she wants that. I\u2019m glad she has such a good option to include him. Really. I am happy that my motley mates have managed to reconnect with loved ones.<br /> <br /> And speaking of parents, John and Linda were warm and quite friendly (and quite flirty actually). They don\u2019t know about Changelings so it was a little awkward to explain how the motley wound up together and running a burlesque house but we managed well enough. And they certainly did seem to enjoy the show. I didn\u2019t avoid them exactly, but I did let the others do the lion\u2019s share of the hosting. I mean, with Jacob\u2019s sister and Lori\u2019s dad and them there have been a lot of healthy and happy and not murdered family around. However, I have been a good little monster and managed to keep my shit together rather well I think. No one has taken me aside to ask me if I\u2019m okay which is good. I don\u2019t want them to not be happy and I don\u2019t want them to feel like they can\u2019t show that happiness around me.<br /> <br /> But fuck did my folks keep coming to my mind every time I looked at Julia\u2019s parents sitting there still so very much in love with each other. Thankfully, my Dragon was quite happy to provide me with ample distractions. So I guess it\u2019s really no mystery why I was so ready to be the prey she wanted to hunt and claim violently.<br /> <br /> Of course, considering that no one else seems to think there\u2019s any reason to be concerned that Marguerite\u2019s former sex slave has an open door into our house I probably shouldn\u2019t have let my Dragon carry me back to her lair last night. But as long as I\u2019m the only one that\u2019s going to stand watch and insure Yvette doesn\u2019t murder us all in our sleep I needed the contract to revive myself. And no matter what they think of me I will continue to watch over them, because the motley is family and I won\u2019t let them come to harm if I can prevent it.<br /> <br /> And now the sun\u2019s coming up. I can feel it\u2019s unwelcome presence even if I can\u2019t see it\u2019s baleful gaze yet. I should go join Beautiful in bed before it\u2019s time to head back to the Dream House. I can\u2019t safely sleep with her but I can at least hold her and play with her hair and be there when she wakes up.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> If one more person asks if I\u2019m \u201cokay\u201d I\u2019m going to yell or hit something. Maybe just hit something. I know that I\u2019ve been trying to act like everything is fine, but something must be slipping for so many people to ask me the same question. I suppose a couple of them shouldn\u2019t surprise me, they were from motley mates. Though one of the \u201care you okay\u2019s\u201d came from Hailey. I will admit that I was not expecting that. Makes me wonder how much other people know about what happened. I\u2019m assuming the Freehold knew about the two Loyalists and the Monarchs would assure the public that at least one of them was dead and the other will not be a threat. But how did it come to be known that I was so personally connected to one of them that I would be upset by his passing? Or am I giving away more than I intend with my demeanor? What do people know?<br /> <br /> I figure that the motley knows that I\u2019m not at my best. They know how upset I got when I found out what Twitch had done to Rook. I broke a door after the chat with that little bastard. So, they know that I\u2019m upset that he\u2019s dead. It\u2019s still a bit much to keep asking me if I\u2019m okay though. They know that I\u2019m not. When they ask though, I lie. I say that I\u2019m mostly okay. That implies that I\u2019m still a little off about things, but getting better. I don\u2019t know if the latter is true for me. I feel just as angry right now as I did when he first died. I know that I need to figure out how to get past that, but right now it\u2019s all I have so I\u2019m holding onto it as hard as I can.<br /> <br /> So, on the positive side of things, Lorelei has learned a new trick. Apparently she has been learning contracts that allow her to communicate with birds, which does answer some questions I\u2019ve had lately. The new thing is that she now can actually transform herself into a bird. She can still talk to us as if she was human, but she\u2019s in reality a small, brightly colored bird. She seemed to take great delight in flying about when she was showing us her new form. I will admit that I was happy for her. It must be freeing to be able to fly again. For me it was a joy when I was in the Lady\u2019s realm to be able to manipulate snow and ice. I\u2019m working on getting those abilities back now, but I remember how it made me feel to be able to summon snow to me and have it whirl around me. I felt so alive.<br /> <br /> After Lori told us her news we all split up to go our separate ways. The ladies for the most part went to go get ready for the show. It was still several hours until show time, so I went to the basement and decided to take out some of my anger and frustration on the heavy bag. My Luna stayed close the entire time. She just stood in the doorway and watched as I lost myself to the anger and loss. I really did lose track of where I was and when I was. I just knew that I wanted to hit something, and so I did. I tried to wrap my knuckles, but tape only does so much when you are hitting a bag as hard as I was. I\u2019m lucky I didn\u2019t sprain a wrist. I was following Rook\u2019s advice the whole time though. Keep my wrist straight and follow through with my body to make the strike harder. And Luna just stood there through all of this. I really wish I could open up to her right now, but my throat just seems to close up when I think about it. I want her to know how much I need her, and I think she does. She has been staying close to me even though it\u2019s the weekend. I know that she really doesn\u2019t like the crowd over the weekends at the Dream House, but she has stayed with me since Wednesday night. I don\u2019t deserve her.<br /> <br /> After I\u2019d been going at the heavy bag for a while Calamity came downstairs and offered me a bottle of water and asked if I was okay and let me know that she was there to listen if I needed to talk. I nodded my thanks and started to unwrap my knuckles. I was right. They were still split and bloody. That\u2019s fine with me. I think I needed the pain anyway. They cleaned up okay though. They didn\u2019t really look at that bad to me. Part of me wanted to say more than just a quick \u201cthanks\u201d to Calamity, but I had the same problem talking to her that I\u2019ve had with Luna. I don\u2019t think I\u2019m really ready to talk to anyone about Rook just yet. I don\u2019t want to hurt their feelings. I know Calamity and the others mean well, but I just can\u2019t talk about it right now.<br /> <br /> The show went well. Annika headlined for the night and Lori and Calamity did their usual excellent job on their numbers. I think Calamity was trying to do really well so she could show off to her mentor. Lori always does really well. I looked for Insincere Marguerite, but I think I remembered that she was on a date with Felicity. I guess we\u2019ll see how that goes. Meanwhile, I mainly paid attention to who was at the bar. Luna, Molly and Hailey stayed at the bar pretty much the whole night. I talked briefly with Molly. She seems to be doing fine. She said that she will be spending some time with Chalcedony tomorrow night and is looking forward do it. And as I mentioned before Hailey actually asked if I was doing all right. I told her that I was mostly okay and didn\u2019t really elaborate. Again, I wasn\u2019t sure how much she knew and wasn\u2019t about to give more away than I had to. It\u2019s one thing to talk to motley mates about Rook and what happened. It\u2019s something else entirely to talk to those who do not know about Rime.<br /> <br /> When I tend bar I also tend to \u201cpeople watch.\u201d It is interesting to see how people react to different acts, or just towards each other. So, I noticed when Tamara went over to talk to De La Rocha. The conversation seemed intense and I think Lori got worried and made her way over to see what was going on. After that Tamara came over to me and explained what was going on. She said that she was arranging a meeting between Maria and Twitch so they could talk out their differences. Or at least M\u0336a\u0336r\u0336i\u0336a\u0336 De La Rocha can explain that she has changed and doesn\u2019t want to hurt him. The same cannot be said for me but that is another thing entirely. Tamara wanted to let me know because it affected someone in my Court, Twitch, and it affected someone in my motley, De La Rocha. I thanked her for the information. I will admit that I am curious to see how that meeting goes. It is well known how scared Twitch is of Maria, so I\u2019m wondering how he\u2019s going to handle it when they\u2019re in the same room. On the plus side rules were laid down for the meeting. No one will be armed and each person can have someone with them for support. I figured De La Rocha asked Lori to be there with her. I do not know who Twitch will ask to be by his side.<br /> <br /> Then to top it all off Tamara asks if I was doing okay. She knows about Rime and my connection to Rook, so it was not unexpected to have her ask. It\u2019s the first time I\u2019ve seen her since he died, so I guess she wanted to take the opportunity to make sure that I was okay. I guess I should be flattered that so many people are worried about me, but right now I\u2019m just finding it more annoying than anything else. I know I shouldn\u2019t though. I know that they mean well and they are trying to be supportive, but I think sometimes the anger just turns off the logic in my brain and I just get annoyed. I want to just yell at them that of course I\u2019m not okay. How is there any way that I could be okay after helping to kill my brother. Don\u2019t get me wrong, I\u2019d be just as upset about things if I had nothing to do with Rook dying. I just don\u2019t know why people keep asking. This whole thing set off a conversation between Tamara and Hailey who started commiserating about being Wizened and they started complaining about anything and everything. It was kind of fun to listen to.<br /> <br /> After Tamara left to go back to her own table Lori came up to the bar and ordered a double shot of bourbon. I was a little surprised by the request, but poured her the drink. She then proceeded to down the shot all in one go. I felt the need then to ask if she was the one that was all right. It\u2019s not usual for her to come over and get a hard drink after the show, let alone while she does her usual socializing after her numbers. She then walked over to the table that De La Rocha and Spidertoes were sitting at and talked to them both for a bit before going off to the side with De La Rocha. They talked for a bit, Lori looked a bit stressed, but covered it up pretty well. Then De La Rocha went back to the table and Lori left. I have no idea what that was about but I\u2019m thinking that it is related to the fact that De La Rocha left the Dream House tonight with Madame Spidertoes. I don\u2019t think that Lori and De La Rocha are having problems with their relationship, but they do have an open one. So, I\u2019m assuming De La Rocha just went home with Spidertoes for an intimate night. After they parted ways Lori went to go talk to Oleander and Julia and the lot of them headed upstairs after a while.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> The number of people asking me if I was okay was down to a minimum today, for which I was grateful. I also managed to fall asleep without drinking last night which was a nice change from the past couple nights. Again Luna stayed close, which has been more of a help than I really realized at first. She is my steady constant and I think I have needed that. I need to tell her how much I appreciate her.<br /> <br /> Not all was right when we went downstairs for breakfast. Apparently Gawain did not sleep very well at all and was lagging. He hasn\u2019t had problems with nightmares in a while so it took me a bit off guard, but I offered to help him with breakfast and made sure that he had plenty of coffee. Overall the food came out good, so it ended up working out in the end. On the plus side Gawain was, after breakfast was over, successful in making those fire breathing piranhas to put in the moat around the Hollow. He was excited about it as was Ace. I think Ace was the more excited of the two, but Gawain was close behind. It was kind of funny to watch their faces as Gawain described how he made them using Cobblethought from Desiree\u2019s dreams. It turns out that Desiree agreed to help Gawain in his endeavor by intentionally dreaming of fire breathing piranha last night. My motley is so strange.<br /> <br /> After that things kind of happened fast. Lori announced that she needed to make an appointment to meet with Augustine about the whole Hunting Hawk deal and make sure that he\u2019s good with it. While she was getting that set up Insincere Marguerite and Julia talked about going on a romantic walk at the pier. Not before they had flustered De La Rocha by talking in general terms about marriage. I\u2019m not sure how the conversation came up. It might have been to do with talk about who\u2019s name Insincere Marguerite and Julia were going to take when they got married. De La Rocha got nervous and excused herself to go hide in a closet for fifteen minutes. While De La Rocha was hiding Julia and Insincere Marguerite left for the pier. And after the time was up De La Rocha came back and asked if Lori was looking at marriage. She said eventually she would like to make things more permanent. Lori tried to reassure her lover that she wasn\u2019t expecting anything any time soon and was more than willing to wait however long it took. De La Rocha said something along the lines of \u201cOh fuck it,\u201d and got down on one knee and proposed to Lorelei. Lori didn\u2019t even take a breath before she said \u201cYes.\u201d De La Rocha got up after that and they hugged. It was a very touching scene, and I got the whole thing on my camera. After they had calmed down a bit I sent a couple of the pictures to Lori\u2019s phone. I don\u2019t know if I\u2019ve ever seen a look of such pure joy on Lori\u2019s face. It was nice to see.<br /> <br /> Shortly after that I went over to talk to Gawain. I wanted to get his opinion on what I should tell Elena. At first he wasn\u2019t sure, but he thought about it for a bit before answering. He said that I should probably tell her that the situation was resolved with him and if she asked admit that it ended in a fight. He didn\u2019t suggest going into any details, just that it\u2019s over. I thought that sounded pretty good, though I was sure at the time that Elena would have questions that I couldn\u2019t answer.<br /> <br /> Once Lori and De La Rocha were composed, the lot of us, Lori, De La Rocha, Gawain, Calamity, me and Luna, went to go talk to Augustine. I think we all figured that if he needed reassurances that Hawk would uphold his end of the bargain, or had questions as to the soundness of the plan, we could help. I\u2019ll admit that I was curious to see if he would buy what we were selling. He received us graciously, and without prompting, apologized to Lorelei for what he had said a little while ago. Lori explained what the deal was between her and Hunting Hawk and what things had been worked into the oath itself to keep the freehold safe. He seemed amenable to the deal and gave it his seal of approval. She also told Augustine of our assumption that Hawk will be killed himself for failing his Mistress, but that he seemed unaware of the possible danger. Win win for us. Augustine seemed to agree.<br /> <br /> Once we got back to the house I called Lowjack for Lori to see if the Winter monarch was okay with the deal that we\u2019d made with Hunting Hawk. He seemed to be fine with the oath as we\u2019d worked it out. I told him that I would let her know he had given the plan his seal of approval. He then in a roundabout way asked if I was doing okay and offered his bar should I need to have a drink or two. I said something along the lines that I may not be able to drive home and he offered a place for me to stay if that should happen. I told him I appreciated the offer and might take him up on it. When I got off the phone I went to go talk to Lorelei. I told her about Lowjack\u2019s acceptance of the deal with Hawk. She seemed happy enough with that and then asked if we could talk privately. I said sure and we went off to the side to talk. She then apologized for what happened with Rook and acknowledged that it wasn\u2019t fair how it all worked out. That Rook died and Hunting Hawk gets to go back to Arcadia. I told her that I understood logically that Rook was more dangerous than Hawk and that things had to go the way they did regardless of how I felt about it. She also offered her ear should I need to talk to someone. I appreciated her offer, but like the others I don\u2019t think I\u2019ll be able to take her up on it just yet. I don\u2019t know if I can talk about things right now. The thing that kind of surprised me was that she said that she saw me as a brother herself. It took me a little off guard, but it made sense. In a short period of time these people have become like a family and I said as much. I was touched by what she said and tried my best in that moment to acknowledge the sentiment. At the end I promised her that we would get her friends back from Arcadia. I didn\u2019t elaborate past that. I didn\u2019t think I needed to.<br /> <br /> After that things got more lighthearted. A group of us helped Gawain cook a Greek dinner for Julia\u2019s parents who\u2019d been invited to join us for a meal before the show. They accepted, so Gawain decided that he was going to go all out. Several of us helped and I think it all turned out pretty good. Before our guests arrived it was revealed to all those who might interact with Julia\u2019s parents that they did not know about the Lost or that their daughter had been taken. As far as they knew she never left. We all promised to keep any mention of our Freehold or circumstances to ourselves. Overall the Oldacres seemed to enjoy the food and the company. They were remarkably understanding and tolerant of the many poly relationships in the house. I think something was mentioned about them having an open relationship themselves. So, things all seemed to work out well. They enjoyed the show and the company, which was the whole idea.<br /> <br /> After the show the Oldacres left and everyone split off into groups. Calamity went off to go talk to Becky and Gawain about something, and Lori went to go talk to Natasha. I\u2019m not sure where Insincere Marguerite and Julia went off to, but I had a pretty good idea. I was just starting to look for Elena when Lori and De La Rocha left to go take their own romantic walk on the pier. So, I found Elena and asked her if we could talk. We went to a private room and I told her that the situation with Rook had been resolved. She seemed to immediately understand that he was dead and I acknowledged that it had ended in a fight. She nodded her understanding. I don\u2019t know if she truly accepts what happened or not. She was a little distracted. She wanted to know if Natasha had been involved with Rook and all that mess. I assured her that Natasha was not involved with Rook and that Rook was only after me. He had no other targets in the Freehold. I think I reassured her that her friend was not involved with known Loyalists, but I didn\u2019t try and tackle the issue of what Natasha is actually mixed up in. I don\u2019t fully know what she was really involved in. We haven\u2019t looked into that further yet. I\u2019m not sure if the others want to pursue that question or not. I will have to bring up the subject soon.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know if Elena was fully satisfied with the explanation that I gave her about what happened, but she did not ask for clarification. I don\u2019t know if she knows the impact that Rook\u2019s death has had on me. Surely she must have noticed my change in behavior, but to her credit she has not said anything. I don\u2019t know what I would tell her anyway. I can\u2019t explain how important Rook was to me without explaining my past as Rime, and that is not a topic I want to bring up with my sister just yet. I have just revealed myself to her and she is still processing all that I\u2019ve told her already. I don\u2019t need to add this additional information into the mix just yet. I don\u2019t know if I will ever be able to tell her about Rime. How do I tell my twin sister that I am a monster with her brother\u2019s face? How do I explain to her the things that I have done and why I did them? She\u2019s only eighteen. I don\u2019t know if she\u2019ll understand any of it just yet. I don\u2019t know if I want her to.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> I confess everything is endlessly splendid.<br /> <br /> Juliette and Maria are engaged. Maria proposed to her spur of the moment yesterday. Sadly Julia and I were not there. Still, the moment is most important to them both, though I wish I had been.<br /> <br /> Julia really wants us all to marry at once, perhaps with a vow between couples. At this point I confess I want this too. But I am unwilling to push; there could also be a joining of us as couples later. I think we are better as two and two as four rather than a four where jealousy could reign.<br /> <br /> This joy comes after what could have been a contentious night. I went to see Felicity, the Day Courtier who I rather desire. Julia was rather unhappy about it. I had intended Julia to bond with Juliette and Maria, but there was a twist. Madame Spidertoes had arrived, and was sitting with Maria, who held her hand. Apparently Juliette had a crisis of conscience after Maria told her she would keep her promise not to go home with her. She told Maria that with her assurance Maria would return to her. Maria agreed. Juliette met up with Oleander, and she and Julia retired together. They did not stay down to see Maria leave.<br /> <br /> Over two years ago, when I arrived in Los Angeles from Montreal, I met Lady Felicity. The Mistress of Lord Leonidas of Day, we clashed immediately, but there was sexual tension from the first. One or two snippy meetings happened, but when I assaulted Leonidas\u2019s house, I searched for her rooms. She was gone. When it turned out she now lived so close to where I did, I wondered if it was a coincidence.<br /> <br /> At dinner she confessed having gone to some effort to track I down. She used divination, and set up a household nearby when unable to find I exactly. But she had not simply waited. Seeking to make a place in the Lady By The Sea, she met Jolie, and they clicked quickly until she discovered Jolie fed on the spiritual essences of people. Eventually she found out exactly where I was, and we met again. We had a wonderful, romantic dinner. She suggested we should begin a romance. I said I would have to speak to the others. She appealed to I to take the high road and consider committing myself to her. I told her I was committed to three other women. She asked I to leave.<br /> <br /> I remember vividly my first time with Julia. The feelings, the intensity. The union. The hunger. Similarly, I remember my first time with Juliette and Maria. Glorious, we four. Felicity was much like that. We argued in the front door she shoved I, and I grabbed her. She pushed I against the wall. We kissed. She thrust one curled hand into my shorts, the other up my shirt. I wrapped my leg around her back and bit her neck, tasting blood as I felt the lightning bolts through my body. I may have been the lioness, but she was quite an animal as well. Our Mantles roiled and clashed. It would be a stretch to say we made love; we fucked in the doorway, then we fucked on the stairs, then we fucked in her room. It was magnificent.<br /> <br /> Still, I returned to my girls the next morning. On the way I mulled her request over in my head. Not that I would leave any of my beloveds, but a torrid romance with Felicity might be fun. At least until one of us tries to kill the other. Which given how opposite we are in many ways could happen.<br /> <br /> I arrived at sex breakfast just a little behind Maria. Things were\u2026calm\u2026though Juliette was very clingy with Maria and Julia with me, which left Oleander in bit in the cold. I made sure Julia and I gave her attention. We discussed cuisine for dinner with the Oldacres, and settled on Greek. I had promised Julia a turn on the pier as a romantic walk to keep her happy; she enjoys the occasional promenade with her black parasol.<br /> <br /> We left a bit early, however, and missed the proposal. Julia was as I say fairly disappointed. I figured it was spur of the moment anyway, but still, she was terribly disappointed for someone who dislikes romance, hein?<br /> <br /> We got back just before the others did from checking with Viscount Augustine about Hunting Hawk, in time to prepare for dinner. While Gawain and several of the Motley worked on dinner, Maria, Julia and I kicked around last name conversation. I think Juliette is considering taking Maria\u2019s last name. Julia and I had discussed that I was not inclined to Oldacre and she wanted to change hers anyway, but I feel no loyalty to the DeLisle family. There was chatter when Juliette got there of all going De La Rocha. We will see.<br /> <br /> This assuming we change at all.<br /> <br /> John and Linda arrived and were good company for dinner. Julia introduced everyone, and Juliette gave her good news. Julia did not quite stifle the urge to talk about her ceremony ideas, but we mostly just let them be happy with it. Everyone was well behaved; Julia was not yet prepared to tell them the truth of our condition, which made some questions a little awkward, but we got through with everyone, I think having a good time. I should note even Calamity behaved well.<br /> <br /> John and Linda are terribly flirty people. Not that it is a problem. Usually.<br /> <br /> They did seem to really enjoy the show. They sat at the \u201cgirlfriend table\u201d with Maria, Rowan, Julia, Becky, and Desiree. Juliette, Calamity, Gawain and I made our way round eventually. Juliette and Maria were like the turtledoves. Rowan for her part did not remain all night; Juliette sat and talked to her, and almost certainly told her about her engagement. Rowan gave her caring smiles, but left looking stricken after. I would have gone after her if I thought I could help.<br /> <br /> There was a big discussion with Calamity, Becky and Gawain. I am not sure it\u2019s nature precisely. Afterwards Calamity and Becky left together and Gawain and Desiree also retired together.<br /> <br /> I can only wonder what Jacob thinks of our complicated love lives. Alas, he keeps a counsel his own these days. I am thankful for Luna and her willingness to be there for him.<br /> <br /> As I say, John and Linda enjoyed the show. I believe they divided the dancers up between them. It was sort of amusing. As I say, flirty. It is strange how reserved Julia is by comparison. I mean, the culture in that house must have been odd. Still, I adore my little artist. Well, not so little artist. She is very tall. Anyway, They had fun, and since rooms were full we put them up at a hotel nearby so they would not have to drive to Anaheim so late. They are appreciative, and we promised to see each other soon.<br /> <br /> Juliette and Maria retired together. I checked with White Maria, who was there with Dark Kimberly, but she was on an even keel and did not need my particular therapy, and was also a little disturbed by Calamity for some reason.<br /> <br /> So Julia and I had a private night, which was nice. I am sure the cuddles were good for her. We chatted about Maria and Juliette, wondered about Jacob a bit and talked about her parents. It was sweet<br /> <br /> I well understand if Juliette and Maria want their own ceremony. I mean, on some level I want my own ceremony. It\u2019s just after the fallout from Chalcedony, I know it would devastate I to not be with them, so I lean toward the joint thing. It would also take pressure off Maria. But we have time to discuss it.<br /> <br /> Like I say I am pretty happy right now. I am not sure what direction things with Felicity and Yvette are going to take though. I will presume for now Calamity is not breaking her word and just leaving the Yvette thing alone. I like to believe she can at least be counted on for that. As for how they will resolve it is hard to say.<br /> <br /> Still these are good days and I should enjoy them. It took me some time to get here.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXXV</i><br /> <br /> Not much to add. Cobblethought is a crazy power. Really, Contract of Dreams is underrated. There was talk of using it to get to Bellevue, but it would be a bit too many jumps after doing the math.<br /> <br /> Tamara and Hailey had a conversation about how Jacob keeping being asked if he was okay is what being a Wizened is like all the time, which lead to cheerful grousing.<br /> <br /> De La Rocha\u2019s exact line was \u201cYou know what? Fuck it.\u201d Before proposing. Ever the romantic, that one.<br /> <br /> Side note a Fairest Shadowsoul showed Friday from LA and talked to most of the Motley, but went unmentioned for some reason.<br /> <br /> The journals tell the tale fairly thoroughly. But if you have comments or questions they are welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 02-13-2017, 04:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T15:25:29-08:00","id":1047924,"title":"","content":"Well call me a Mage because I have so many questions!<br /> <br /> 1) Were you trying to make me sad with that scene of gorgeous dorkery between Ace and Gawain? It just makes me feel anew the pain of his player's departure<br /> <br /> 2) Are we ever going to learn what the fuck was going on with Rowan's house? My current favorite theory is some sort of weird Spirit-Claimed nonsense, but i don't know if they can animate a house like that, or whether you're including Spirit world stuff.<br /> <br /> 3) When did Gawain get serious with Desiree? That one kinda blindsided me, but then again, I'm pretty dense. No one really ever flirts with me, so I don't know what it sounds like<br /> <br /> 4) Are White Maria and Dark Kimberly escapees from the Director? Are they Dream House performers? Are they Summer Court? Or am I just totally lost on what their place in this is, despite remembering something about a feud over a murdered friend that had that scary Summer Court guy involved?<br /> <br /> 5) What stunt did Calamity pull with Dark Kimberly?<br /> <br /> 6) Speaking of him, what was his name again? He was an Ogre who was a lawyer and a gang leader with drug connections, and was basically almost as powerful politically as Viscount Augustine. And what was his kith? Was he shark-like or am I just thinking of one of the character examples from the rulebook?<br /> <br /> 7) Also, was Becky part of that feud I mentioned in question 4? I can't remember<br /> <br /> 8) Becky is just with Calamity, right?<br /> <br /> 9) Also, she's Jolie's bodyguard, right?<br /> <br /> 10) Can you remind me who Tamara and Hailey are again? I don't remember anything about them? Have they been mentioned before?<br /> <br /> 11) Annika is Calamity's dance teacher, right? I barely remember her<br /> <br /> 12) Who is Vic Twilight? Have we met him yet?<br /> <br /> 13) You said you had a chart of all the characters with Seemings, Court affiliations, etc., but i can't find it. in lieu of asking about more people, could I just ask for a new link to that chart, please?<br /> <br /> 14) And one more thing. None of you have answered my question (which I asked multiple pages ago) about whether the grass cape Gawain's reference image has is part of his Mien in-game. So, is it?<br /> <br /> once again, a great read. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 02-12-2017, 06:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T23:44:27-08:00","id":1048089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play?p=1047924#post1047924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well call me a Mage because I have so many questions!<br /> <br /> 1) Were you trying to make me sad with that scene of gorgeous dorkery between Ace and Gawain? It just makes me feel anew the pain of his player's departure</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, Wait, no.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) Are we ever going to learn what the fuck was going on with Rowan's house? My current favorite theory is some sort of weird Spirit-Claimed nonsense, but i don't know if they can animate a house like that, or whether you're including Spirit world stuff. </div> </div> </div>As I say, it was one of those strange WoD things that don't seem to make sense. Unknown Mysteries or whatever. More things in heaven and earth\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) When did Gawain get serious with Desiree? That one kinda blindsided me, but then again, I'm pretty dense. No one really ever flirts with me, so I don't know what it sounds like </div> </div> </div><br /> Recently. After she and Gloria more-or-less moved out to stay with Flores at the Rose &amp; Thorn, Gawain hooked back up with her over soft serve, and they wound up getting close again between healing visits. Gawain had largely stopped journaling at that point, and I don't recall but most likely Calamity was ranting about something else, she was the other one there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4) Are White Maria and Dark Kimberly escapees from the Director? Are they Dream House performers? Are they Summer Court? Or am I just totally lost on what their place in this is, despite remembering something about a feud over a murdered friend that had that scary Summer Court guy involved? </div> </div> </div>White Maria and Dark Kimberly are not from the Director. I don't <i>think</i> either of their Durances have been discussed, though I may be wrong. Neither performs at the Dream House. Both are Spring Court White Maria (Treasured Fairest) is there almost every night. Both are Spring Courtiers. White Maria trains with Calamity some mornings, and Insincere Marguerite Dommes for her now and then, helping her cope with her Durance (hopefully). Dark Kimberly (Chatelaine/Drudge) hooked up with Calamity and has had a will they or won\u2019t they with Davey, but got involved with Annika for awhile, till they broke up due to\u2026many things. Mostly. Sort of. They did feud over the death of Sundown Kwan, who Dark Kimberly did not act to save. Known for being Goth and continually cleaning up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5) What stunt did Calamity pull with Dark Kimberly? </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s discussed in Calamity\u2019s journal. Short answer is Mumbly Peg.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6) Speaking of him, what was his name again? He was an Ogre who was a lawyer and a gang leader with drug connections, and was basically almost as powerful politically as Viscount Augustine. And what was his kith? Was he shark-like or am I just thinking of one of the character examples from the rulebook? </div> </div> </div>Lucian Torrez. Stonebones/Render, no shark aspect. Basically played by clean shaven Brian Thompson.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 7) Also, was Becky part of that feud I mentioned in question 4? I can't remember </div> </div> </div>Yes. Also blamed Dark Kimberly for Sundown Kwan\u2019s death.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 8) Becky is just with Calamity, right? </div> </div> </div>Correct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 9) Also, she's Jolie's bodyguard, right? </div> </div> </div>Correct. The Claviger, so the Spring Court Guardian. Most often acting as Jolie\u2019s bodyguard, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 10) Can you remind me who Tamara and Hailey are again? I don't remember anything about them? Have they been mentioned before? </div> </div> </div>Tamara Chance is Winter (Oracle) and often worked at Lowjacks, was treated as a daughter by him, and was his main supporter before he became Winter King. She had a couple sexual encounters with the Handmaidens and nearly died, leading Lowjack to menace the local Night Courtiers, including Insincere Marguerite. Hailey (Inventor/Gremlin) is Summer Court Grey Alien, who was favored by Andromeda and she wound up altering then Hailey seduced her to help her escape. Andromeda pursued with the Table, leading to all that bullshit. Eventually when the Mothership came, Hailey entered and warned the PCs as she struggled with it\u2019s control over her. She hates Andromeda, and Joan hates her. Andromeda is trying to get over her feelings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 11) Annika is Calamity's dance teacher, right? I barely remember her </div> </div> </div>Yes. Other main headliner at the Dream House. German Dancer taken in the 30s, the other ex lover of Madame Spidertoes. Was involved with Dark Kimberly. Dietrich Homage. Was involved with Golden Swan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 12) Who is Vic Twilight? Have we met him yet? </div> </div> </div>A couple times. One of the two Manniken Elementals made by Master Darke, along with Molly Nuit from rewritten loyalists. Now works for Lowjack. One of the only two Black NPCs with Dominika (Sadly; I should get on that.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 13) You said you had a chart of all the characters with Seemings, Court affiliations, etc., but i can't find it. in lieu of asking about more people, could I just ask for a new link to that chart, please? </div> </div> </div>It is due for updating. I will put it up Saturday as an off-week thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 14) And one more thing. None of you have answered my question (which I asked multiple pages ago) about whether the grass cape Gawain's reference image has is part of his Mien in-game. So, is it?<br /> <br /> once again, a great read. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ll leave that for Gawain\u2019s Player.<br /> <br /> If you need clarification lemme know.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T04:12:21-08:00","id":1048163,"title":"","content":"No need for clarification, this is all good. Thanks for humoring my insane amount of questions","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T