Ogre Gargantuan<br /> Moir\u00e9 Wizened Oracle<br /> <br /> <b>Day</b><br /> <br /> Lord Leonidas Beast Hunterheart<br /> Olivia Gold Fairest Bright One/Flamesiren<br /> Felicity Fairest Treasured/ Bright One<br /> Rowan Beast Swimmerskin<br /> <br /> <b>Night</b><br /> <br /> The Warlock of Night Darkling Leechfinger/Nightsinger<br /> Willow Black Beast Windwing/ Hunterheart<br /> Scarlet Noir Darkling Leechfinger/ Whisperwisp<br /> Natalia Darkling Leechfinger/ Moonborn<br /> Salk Darkling Nightsinger/Whisperwisp<br /> Corvus Darkling Lurkglider<br /> Corbin Darkling Whisperwisp<br /> Della Strype Fairest Shadowsoul","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 02-26-2017, 05:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T14:51:28-08:00","id":1055400,"title":"","content":"There is ring shopping, and Calamity\u2019s childhood friend returns. Not all is well with Rowan, and here and there jealousy is starting to rear its head.<br /> <br /> As a note, different journals cover different events, so this is a session that if you usually read a couple you might want to hit all of them. Lori goes into more detail about ring shopping, Jacob goes into more detail about his walk, Insincere Marguerite described the encounter with Calamity\u2019s childhood friend and is the only one to mention Captain Jack\u2019s visit.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LXXVI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Okay, checking psyche\u2026 examining shifting mood parameters\u2026 recalling events of the last twenty-four hours\u2026 yep, still giddy.<br /> <br /> So after returning to the Dream House in the wee hours of the morning and hastily scrawling down my last \u2013 probably nearly incomprehensible \u2013 diary entry, D and I pepped ourselves up with Spring contracts, grabbed a quick shower, and got dressed for church. Since I knew Dad was probably bursting at the seams to congratulate us in person, I would have begged her to come with me\u2026 but I didn\u2019t even have to ask.<br /> <br /> The sermon was about love and partnership, and I sincerely doubt that was a coincidence. I didn\u2019t mention the engagement to any of my friends in the choir; I sort of wanted to wait until I had a ring to show off. This whole proposal was so spontaneous that I guess we\u2019re sort of doing things backwards, but I don\u2019t care. It was easy to raise my voice to the heavens today; I half felt like I was flying already.<br /> <br /> D was waiting for me in the pews after I had changed out of my choir robes, and the two of us made our way to the tail-end of the line of parishioners speaking with Dad at the doors of the church. \u201cLorelei,\u201d he said warmly, taking my hand in his, \u201cyour voice was, as always, an inspiration to us all. And Maria, I am always happy to see you among my humble flock. And I understand\u2026\u201d he said with a surreptitious glance at the departing congregation, \u201cI understand that congratulations are in order!\u201d<br /> <br /> D smiled and took Dad\u2019s hand firmly. \u201cThanks, padre,\u201d she said, and then her cheeks colored ever so slightly and she lowered her gaze. \u201cThank you, sir,\u201d she started again. \u201cI\u2019m sorry I didn\u2019t stop by or call to ask for your blessing first, but it just sort of\u2026 <u><u>happened</u></u> yesterday morning. I mean\u2026 I love Lori very much, and I\u2019ve never been as sure about anything in my life, but\u2026 the proposal itself was\u2026 unplanned.\u201d<br /> <br /> Dad nodded sagely. \u201cI understand. It was much the same when I proposed to Juliette\u2019s mother, actually. When God shows you that a given time and place is right, it is foolish to delay.\u201d He got sort of a misty look in his eyes. \u201cA few months ago, I had believed myself alone in this world, bereft of my family. Then, in a miracle beyond imagining, my Juliette was returned to me. And now, our family grows once again. Welcome, Maria.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you, sir,\u201d she said, allowing herself to be drawn into a somewhat awkward hug. \u201cI\u2019ll do everything I can to keep her safe and happy.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know you will,\u201d he responded. \u201cOh\u2026 and you may continue to call me \u2018padre,\u2019 if you like. Of course, that form of address is more properly applied to a Catholic or Anglican priest, yet\u2026 from you, I find the term endearing.\u201d<br /> <br /> D\u2019s face broke into a genuine smile. I think he made her day with that.<br /> <br /> There was one more person I had to tell before we started informing the Freehold at large. Oleander\u2019s house is relatively close to the church, so I asked D if she wouldn\u2019t mind heading over there for a few minutes. She dutifully agreed, and about fifteen minutes later I was knocking on her door.<br /> <br /> \u201cHey, Angel,\u201d she said as she opened her door, \u201cthis is a pleasant surprise.\u201d She glanced over my shoulder at my car in the driveway. \u201cDe la Rocha can come in if you want, Lori\u2026 it doesn\u2019t bother me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks,\u201d I said, \u201cbut I can really only stay for a couple of minutes. We have a full day planned. I\u2026 wanted to tell you about something in person before you hear it from the Freehold\u2019s grapevine. You see\u2026 just after you left yesterday, D proposed to me.\u201d<br /> <br /> There wasn\u2019t even a flicker of negative emotion on her face. \u201cCongratulations!\u201d she said immediately with a dazzling smile.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re okay with it?\u201d I asked, a little surprised after Rowan\u2019s reaction the previous night.<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course,\u201d she said, \u201cI\u2019m not stupid, Lori. I\u2019ve known this was coming for a long time. And not to be self-deprecating, but\u2026 I knew it wasn\u2019t going to be <u><u>me</u></u>. You and de la Rocha make each other very happy, and I\u2019m happy for both of you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you so much!\u201d I said, throwing my arms around her neck. Though she hadn\u2019t been toxic the previous day, I guess I was making sort of a dangerous assumption there\u2026 but I also know that she would have warned me if it wasn\u2019t safe for us to touch. \u201cD and I have already talked about it\u2026 we\u2019re going to have an open marriage. I still want to spend time with you, Imelda\u2026 I still love you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cRight back at you, Angel,\u201d she said as we disengaged. \u201cThanks for coming by to tell me in person\u2026 you didn\u2019t have to do that, but I appreciate it. Now go on\u2026 I\u2019m sure the two of you have a lot to discuss.\u201d She turned toward the driveway and called out \u201ccongratulations!\u201d D shot her a thumbs-up in response.<br /> <br /> As we were driving back to the Dream House, however, D started asking questions, some of which really blindsided me. \u201cSo, do you want to go ring shopping today, or Tuesday?\u201d she asked (that one didn\u2019t blindside me so much). \u201cI <u><u>have</u></u> to go to work tomorrow, since I took Friday off, but I could make time the day after\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cToday is fine,\u201d I said with easily-penetrated false nonchalance. \u201cWe\u2019ve got all afternoon; five or six hours until I really need to be back for the show. That should be enough time.\u201d<br /> <br /> D sighed. \u201cI\u2026 Lori, I don\u2019t know shit about wedding rings and jewelry and shit like that,\u201d she said after a minute. \u201cI want to get you something you\u2019ll really like, but I don\u2019t want to fuck it up, and I probably will.\u201d<br /> <br /> I laughed. \u201cD, you could get me a ring out of a box of crackerjacks and I\u2019d be thrilled with it,\u201d I said. Then something occurred to me. \u201cDo they still have those? Crackerjacks? Do people still know what they are?\u201d<br /> <br /> That broke the tension a little. \u201cYeah,\u201d she replied, \u201cbut I don\u2019t think they put the prizes in them anymore.\u201d<br /> <br /> That threw me for a loop, as the prizes were always sort of the <u><u>point</u></u> of getting crackerjacks in my opinion. Without them, you\u2019re left with stale caramel-covered popcorn.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnyway,\u201d D continued after a moment, \u201cI was thinking about asking Julia for advice. She\u2019s already done all the research and looked into the local stores and stuff, so\u2026 would you mind if she came with us?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSure,\u201d I said, \u201cit\u2019ll make her happy, too. Actually\u2026 I\u2019ve been meaning to ask you something about Marguerite and Julia. I know they\u2019re both pushing for a combined wedding, but\u2026 I\u2019d really like my Dad to oversee our ceremony, and I kind of want it to be about just you and me. Does that make me selfish?\u201d<br /> <br /> D sniffed. \u201cNah,\u201d she said. \u201cIt\u2019s your wedding. Most people only get like three or four of them in a lifetime, so you want it to be perfect, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBite your tongue,\u201d I quipped back. \u201cThis bird mates for life. But anyway, I was thinking\u2026 I don\u2019t think I want to have a combined wedding, but I do want those two to know how much we care about them. Maybe it\u2019s time we finally said yes and pledged ourselves.\u201d<br /> <br /> D nodded. \u201cI\u2019d be okay with that,\u201d she said after thinking about it for a moment. \u201cIt\u2019s not really a concession\u2026 just taking a different step to distinguish the relationships a little. I\u2019ll talk with Mags about it when we get back, and let her talk to Julia. That\u2019ll probably go better for everyone.\u201d<br /> <br /> Things were quiet for another couple of minutes, and then D spoke up again. \u201cBabe?\u201d she asked softly (here comes the blindsiding).<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDoes one of us have to\u2026 like\u2026 convert now? And if so, which one?\u201d<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t understand the question at first. \u201cI\u2026 don\u2019t understand the question,\u201d I said.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, you\u2019re a Protestant and I\u2019m a Catholic,\u201d she elaborated quietly. \u201cI mean, I\u2019m not a very <u><u>good</u></u> Catholic, and I haven\u2019t really even <u><u>thought</u></u> much about being a Catholic for the last few years, but now\u2026 well, I\u2019m getting <u><u>married</u></u>.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh,\u201d I said. I confess that D\u2019s religion has come up so infrequently that I hitherto hadn\u2019t even considered it a factor. \u201cWell\u2026 I\u2019m not going to ask you to join the Methodist church. If you decided to do so, I\u2019d be thrilled, but if not, it\u2019s not going to make me unhappy, if you see what I mean. As for me converting to Catholicism\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I chuckled. \u201cDad might actually take that worse than the \u2018gay\u2019 and the \u2018changeling\u2019 revelations, honestly. My faith is important to me, D\u2026 but if that\u2019s what it takes for us to be together, then I\u2019m in.\u201d<br /> <br /> D shook her head. \u201cI\u2026 I don\u2019t think so. I\u2019ll look into it, see what the church has to say, but don\u2019t worry about it too much for now. I wouldn\u2019t ask you to do that anyway\u2026 but there\u2019s a part of me that wants to get married by the laws of the Holy Church. It\u2019s\u2026 more important to me than I thought it would be.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cI get it; you want to do this right. You might only get three or four chances, after all\u2026\u201d I threw her a smirk to let her know I was teasing.<br /> <br /> \u201cEyes on the road, wise-ass,\u201d she shot back at me. \u201cAnyway, worst case scenario as I see it, we have two ceremonies. I looked it up; there\u2019s a Catholic church in L.A. that will perform marriages for lesbians. Though if we have a traditional Catholic ceremony, it\u2019ll probably take all day, so we might want to set aside a whole weekend\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m going to have to meet your family some time,\u201d I said quietly after a moment. It\u2019s always been a sore spot with D.<br /> <br /> She sighed. \u201cI know. I\u2019m working up to it. I just want to punch them all so bad every time I see them\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I thought about it. \u201cWhat about your brother? You get along with him okay, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cHim I only want to punch with one fist,\u201d she admitted.<br /> <br /> \u201cMaybe you could introduce me to just him first, before we go for the whole family experience. Sort of get our toes wet before we dive in head first\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded again. \u201cNot a bad idea, babe. I\u2019ll give it some thought\u2026 and I\u2019ll give you some warning before I set anything up.\u201d<br /> <br /> So we got back to the Dream House about this time, had crepes, and spoke with Marguerite and Julia about engagement ring shopping. Julia was excited by the prospect and offered to help us out almost before D asked her. <br /> <br /> Gawain overheard the conversation, and sort of shyly asked if any of us would like him to specially craft a set of wedding bands (speaking to all four of us, you understand). I don\u2019t think any of us hesitated in taking him up on his very kind offer\u2026 Gawain\u2019s metalwork is absolutely <u><u>beautiful</u></u>, and I can\u2019t think of any more special or appropriate way to celebrate the occasion. He looked pleased by our enthusiastic responses, and shuffled off to his forge to practice.<br /> <br /> I think Marguerite was planning to come with us as we looked at engagement rings, but fate conspired against her. Okay, so some backstory first. Calamity\u2019s best friend before she was taken was a girl named Stasia. One of Calamity\u2019s biggest regrets has been that her fetch basically destroyed her relationship with Stasia. It did horrible things to her, causing her to hate Calamity with a fiery passion. Calamity has been hoping to rectify this for some time, and after doing some digging on the internet, Marguerite managed to locate her old friend in a suburb of Seattle. Calamity then asked Marguerite to check up on Stasia and make sure she was safe, and Marguerite sent her a mirror, and has been looking in on her periodically.<br /> <br /> Well, Calamity decided that it was time to make contact at last, and asked Marguerite to take her to Seattle so that she could speak with Stasia. Of course Marguerite agreed\u2026 her relationship with Calamity may never be what it used to be, but we <u><u>are</u></u> still a motley, and we support each other however we can. So she couldn\u2019t join us in the ring-shopping expedition.<br /> <br /> I pulled Calamity aside before any of us left the Dream House. I told her that I knew she had to speak with her friend, and that she had to do it alone, but I wanted to make sure she knew that I would be there for her afterward, for anything she might need. It sounded a little feeble in my own mind, since there was very little I could do to help her through the most difficult part of this trial, but I think she appreciated it nonetheless.<br /> <br /> So\u2026 ring shopping. Julia knew a couple of good places in the area, and offered up plenty of great advice on the type of ring, stone, and setting\u2026 which was nice, since neither D nor I had any idea of what we were looking for. Julia\u2019s parents know someone who owns a chain of jewelry stores\u2026 all hand-crafted stuff, which makes it quite nice even if it\u2019s maybe not the cheapest. We looked in a few places she knew, but ended up going back there.<br /> <br /> In the end, we settled on a fairly simple ring\u2026 simple but <u><u>beautiful</u></u>. It\u2019s a plain slim yellow-gold band without etchings or traceries in it. The gem is a three-quarter carat round-cut brilliant white diamond, surrounded by four tiny diamond chips to give the setting a little body.<br /> <br /> I am frankly in love with this ring. We kept looking after we saw it, and even visited a few other stores, but I knew almost as soon as I tried it on that it was perfect. They didn\u2019t even have to resize it for me. D hemmed and hawed about getting a ring with a bigger stone, and they had some lovely examples\u2026 but this ring has an understated elegance that I can\u2019t help but admire. D signed a few papers, and I walked out of the store wearing it.<br /> <br /> Oh, and while we were filling out the paperwork, Calamity texted the motley to let us know that things had gone well and that Stasia would be joining us for the show! Of course I was super-happy for my gal pal, and immediately texted a response to the tune of OMG-congrats-smiley-face-smiley-face-smiley-face-less-than-three. I think I\u2019m finally starting to get the hang of this texting thing!<br /> <br /> By a fortunate coincidence, most of us arrived back at the Dream House at around the same time. Calamity\u2019s friend Stasia is an attractive woman in her thirties with a two-tone punk hairstyle that really suits her. Calamity had enchanted her, so she could see us as we really are, and though she was obviously a bit overwhelmed by the whole situation, it seemed like she was taking it remarkably well. When I mentioned this to her, she sort of smirked.<br /> <br /> \u201cI always knew something had happened to Kat,\u201d she said by way of an explanation. \u201cHer behavior changed overnight\u2026 and she somehow spontaneously became left-handed at the exact same time. I had always assumed it was some sort of government cloning project\u2026 but this makes sense too in a weird way.\u201d<br /> <br /> She\u2019s really smart, and incredibly perceptive. She has a wry, sarcastic streak a mile wide. I\u2019d call her bitter, but considering what Calamity\u2019s fetch put her through, I guess that\u2019s understandable. In any case, it\u2019s not hard to see how she and Calamity became such good friends as children; they each have this sardonic wit that plays really well off each other. Watching them together, you can see how they used to be as kids.<br /> <br /> It honestly made me a little melancholy, as it sort of reminded me of the way Missy, Jane and I used to finish each other\u2019s sentences and have ideas that just clicked together. I have to rescue them. I <u><u>have</u></u> to.<br /> <br /> D approached me a couple of hours before the show. \u201cCan I talk to you for a second, babe?\u201d she asked seriously.<br /> <br /> \u201cSure, honey,\u201d I said, giving her a quick kiss. \u201cWhat\u2019s on your mind?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m gonna head out for a while,\u201d she said. \u201cI might not be here when the show starts, but I\u2019ll be back before it\u2019s over, I promise. Okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course,\u201d I said. \u201cWhat\u2019s up?\u201d<br /> <br /> She shuffled her feet a bit. \u201cI\u2026 need to tell Gladys about the engagement,\u201d she said after a moment. \u201cI owe it to her to tell her in person.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course you do,\u201d I said softly, pulling her into a hug. \u201cI understand, Maria, don\u2019t worry about it. Do you\u2026 think she\u2019ll take it well?\u201d I asked, trying not to show how very nervous that question made me.<br /> <br /> D shrugged. \u201cI doubt she\u2019ll be particularly <u><u>pleased</u></u> by the news, but I don\u2019t think she\u2019ll be angry or anything like that. Look, Lori\u2026 Friday night was our last goodbye, and she realizes that. When we split up before, there was a big fight, and the last thing I said to her before I left her was that I hated her. It\u2019s not true. We were so close once\u2026 Friday night was the way our relationship <u><u>should</u></u> have ended.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cTake all the time you need. And D\u2026 I\u2019m sorry that my stupid jealousy stood in the way of that last night for so long.\u201d<br /> <br /> D kissed me. \u201cNo worries, babe\u2026 totally not your fault. I had two years to make it happen before I ever met you, remember?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay,\u201d I relented. \u201cWell, do what you have to do. Make sure she\u2019s okay, and\u2026 thank her again for me, for keeping you safe.\u201d D nodded, we kissed, and my fianc\u00e9e headed out to inform her old flame of our impending nuptials.<br /> <br /> I had rearranged that evening\u2019s acts once already to cover for Calamity\u2019s potential absence, but since things went so well with Stasia, she was eager to strut her stuff, and I found myself shuffling the program once more. Calamity wanted to do her \u201cMistress for Christmas\u201d number, and I suggested that the two of us should show off a bit with \u201cBloody Creature Poster Girl.\u201d Gwen and Sarah grumbled a bit about having their solo acts bumped from a weekend show, but I promised I\u2019d let them take the stage next Friday and Saturday, respectively.<br /> <br /> And speaking of those two\u2026 apparently they hooked up with Julia\u2019s parents on Saturday night. John and Linda are a bit more adventurous than I had previously believed, and were happy to take advantage of their surroundings by inviting a couple of attractive young ladies to join them at their hotel. My two backup singers were giggling about it (they said the Oldacres had some really good weed), but I admonished them not to brag about it in front of Julia.<br /> <br /> I did tell Marguerite about the incident, so that she could shield her dearest love from the information more effectively. Unfortunately, she also had some news for <u><u>me</u></u>. It seems that Felicity had been intending to grace us with her presence last night, but had been forced to change her plans following a phone call from Rowan. My shyest girlfriend is not taking the news of my engagement well, and intended to get \u201cblackout drunk,\u201d but wanted to make sure she had someone else around for safety\u2019s sake. Felicity agreed to keep her company, which is some comfort, at least.<br /> <br /> I wanted to call her up and comfort her, but rationally I knew that would probably be the worst thing I could have done. She needs to process this, and she needs to work through it without me distracting and confusing her. If I run to her while she\u2019s hurting, I might be able to make her feel better\u2026 but it wouldn\u2019t help her really deal with things in the long run. I don\u2019t want to make things worse.<br /> <br /> I hate feeling helpless when someone I care about is suffering.<br /> <br /> No. I\u2019m not going to get depressed or feel sad about this; not when I have so much to be happy about. I refuse.<br /> <br /> The show went well. I gave my performances my all, and let me tell you Calamity gave me a run for my money. She\u2019s really taken to life in the spotlight, and I think she put everything she could into those <u><u>particular</u></u> acts in an attempt to impress her old friend. As usual, in our shared act I sort of angled my glamour to keep the audience\u2019s attention on her\u2026 but I really opened it up during my later solo, and I think I gave most of our patrons a night to remember.<br /> <br /> Speaking of our patrons, Joan and Andromeda were there, so I sidled up to their table after I\u2019d finished performing for the evening. I\u2019d been wearing my new ring all night, of course, but I made sure to put my hands on the table fairly conspicuously anyway. Joan was oblivious at first, but Andromeda squealed after a moment and said \u201cwelcome to the club!\u201d<br /> <br /> I guess Joan thought she was talking about my bisexuality or something, because her brow furrowed as she said \u201cwhat are you talking about? She\u2019s already in the\u2026 oh,\u201d she said as she glanced at my hand. Then her face split in one of those rare, genuinely happy smiles of hers. \u201cCongratulations, Lorelei. I am certain you and de la Rocha will have a long and happy life together.\u201d Sometimes I forget that even before Joan and I became lovers, she and D were best friends.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I chatted with the two of them for a while before joining everybody at the girlfriend table. Gawain was already there, and he let me know that Moon wanted to speak with me if I was available. Now, I like Moon, but ze has never really gone out of hir way to speak with me, so I was a little confused about this. It turns out that ze wants me to speak with Dionysia. Ze thinks that hir friend is maybe a little too fond of Talecrafting. In fact, ze thinks she might be addicted to it.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know a whole lot about Talecrafting, but I am given to understand that this is a serious issue. Talecrafting is incredibly dangerous if used recklessly, and while Dionysia is reputedly <u><u>very</u></u> good at it, it\u2019s only a matter of time before something gives. Eventually, reality will sort of snap back at her, and she\u2019ll suffer some sort of dire consequence. No one wants that, but every time Moon tries to bring this up in conversation, Dionysia pooh-poohs hir concerns and claims she has it under control. Ze thinks that I might have more luck, since, well\u2026 I have the reputation in this Freehold of being very persuasive. I agreed to give it a shot, though I warned hir that I don\u2019t know Dionysia very well, so she might not be particularly inclined to listen to me. <br /> <br /> Moon also wanted to tell me about something else\u2026 something too cool for words! Apparently Oleander has been working on a way to help us when we eventually travel to the Empress\u2019 realm to rescue Missy and Jane. She\u2019s been developing\u2026 something. Some sort of tracking doohickey. It will have Hawk\u2019s scent, and it will be able to follow him through the Hedge to the point where he enters Arcadia proper. With luck, it should help us find Her realm more quickly.<br /> <br /> No, I don\u2019t know what it is, exactly. Moon made reference to something called a \u201cwheeled warrior,\u201d but like most references made by most people in this Freehold, I had no hope of understanding it. Still, the next time I see Oleander, I need to remember to give her a big sloppy kiss. You know, an extra one. To thank her for her efforts.<br /> <br /> D made her way back around that time, and as usual I planted myself in her lap, threw my arms around her neck, and luxuriated in her presence. Seriously. While I did my best to join in on the conversations around us, I was mostly just sitting there thinking about my honey and how strong and smart and soft and sexy and\u2026 and\u2026 and she smells nice. Have I ever mentioned that before? Well she does.<br /> <br /> After the crowds emptied out, a bunch of us headed up to the Dream House\u2019s exterior balcony and dipped into Julia\u2019s quality supply of cannabis. There was a lot of talk\u2026 most of it was explaining things to Stasia, as I recall, but there tended to be two or three conversations going on at any given time, so I could be wrong. I know that both Jacob and I talked about the weird time-dilation effect of Arcadia, albeit from different directions. I know we talked about fetches, and how they can be perfectly innocuous (like Becky\u2019s) or incredibly dangerous (like Mary\u2019s).<br /> <br /> I also know that at some point, Stasia talked a bit about her own life. The appreciative glances she gave me and several of the others over the course of the evening was more than enough to indicate that she likes women, but I\u2019ve sort of filed that information away until I can determine how Calamity would feel about that. It\u2019s obvious that she loves Stasia a great deal, but I\u2019m not yet sure what <u><u>kind</u></u> of love that is, or how she would feel about sharing her.<br /> <br /> Stasia <u><u>also</u></u> mentioned that she\u2019s a professional photographer. She went to a fine arts school hoping to make a living as an artist, and nearly washed out before she discovered a talent for photography. She sort of casually mentioned that one of the fringe benefits of the job was that she got to spend a lot of time with attractive young women, and I took that as my cue. I produced a business card from my purse and handed it over to her.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe Dream House keeps me pretty busy most of the time,\u201d I said, \u201cbut I occasionally do some modeling work. Let me know if you ever want to set something up; I\u2019d love to work with you.\u201d She had a sort of oh-my-God-I-just-hit-the-jackpot look on her face that did good things for my ego, so I\u2019m guessing I might get a nibble from that direction in the not-too-distant future.<br /> <br /> The conversation quickly dissolved into giggles and innuendo after that. Stasia\u2019d had a rough day, and she was clearly flagging. Calamity escorted her to a guest bedroom and the rest of us said our goodnights. D and I decided to spend the evening with Marguerite and Julia, and I think all four of us were pleased with the results. I know D talked to Marguerite about our thoughts on the joint ceremony thing, but I don\u2019t think Marguerite has brought it up to Julia yet, so I kept my mouth shut. Err\u2026 I didn\u2019t ask about that particular topic. Heh.<br /> <br /> Anyway, my three darklings are snoring softly in a tangle of limbs on Marguerite and Julia\u2019s bed while I sit across the room, writing in this diary and sort of idly reading a medical textbook at the same time. I should really stop using the Contracts of Spring so flippantly; my body is going to need real REM sleep soon, or it\u2019s going to drive me batty (or battier, if you prefer). But with all that\u2019s been going on lately, my studies have really slipped, and I am not smart enough that I can afford to let that happen. I need to keep sharp. There will always be people who need my help, and I have to make sure I do everything I can to provide it.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> Monday, December 8<sup>th </sup><br /> Nine years, six months, fourteen days<br /> Days without stabbing: 4<br /> <br /> Stasia is here! She\u2019s staying at the Dream House sleeping as I write this. It\u2019s\u2026 well it\u2019s like a dream come true. Even if I could fall asleep I\u2019d be afraid to. And.. and she said the same thing as we walked along the walkway to the guest room. She knew. She knew the Sinister Bitch wasn\u2019t me. She knew it wasn\u2019t the girl she loved\u2026 Loved. That is how she said it, past tense. Even if she knew deep down it wasn\u2019t really her Kat that was doing those things to her it hurt her. It wounded her in a way I don\u2019t think she\u2019s ever really recovered from. I told Insincere Marguerite I\u2019d set my vendetta against the Sinister Bitch aside until after I\u2019d gotten Stasia\u2019s side of it when she offered to seek her out for me. Well, Stasia was prepared to shoot me in cold blood today if I\u2019d reached for my coffee with the wrong hand. That tells me all I need to know. By my blood and glass there WILL be a reckoning and that filthy thing WILL pay for what she did to my Stasia, but that\u2019s not a matter for tonight.<br /> <br /> No, tonight I\u2019m still reeling over having my blood sister back. Also, I think I may still be a little high from Julia\u2019s weed. She\u2019s never been exactly shy about it but I am pretty sure she broke it out to smooth the whole shock of learning about Changelings and getting to know the motley. I should thank her tomorrow. I do think it helped Stasia relax and let her guard down. She kept getting excited and caught up in wanting to know everything about the fae and then catching herself and remembering the emotional walls she\u2019s apparently been building since I was taken. But I did see the girl I knew in there, a flicker of that devil-may-care girl who approached everything with a fearless strength and a damn-the-torpedoes battle-cry. She was always brave enough for the both of us. And no matter how foolish or scary her scheme might be I was right there at her side because someone had to take care of her.<br /> <br /> But then I got taken. I had no one to lead the charge and she had no one to watch her back.<br /> <br /> We need to talk. There\u2019s so much I still need to ask her. So much lost time. I still love her. I always will. But I don\u2019t really know her anymore. And she doesn\u2019t know the woman who showed up on her doorstep this afternoon either. I think bringing her here was a good idea but we need a long private chat. I also think it was just as well that we didn\u2019t have a chance to do it tonight. We\u2019re both still trying to accept that this is really happening, that we\u2019ve found each other again. But soon, before she returns to Bellevue, we\u2019ve got to sit down and see where things stand.<br /> <br /> Soon, before someone makes more than just innuendo and bedroom eyes at her. Not that she wasn\u2019t eyeing the quad with a hungry look of her own. Insincere Marguerite even asked me straight up if it would be alright for her to fuck Stasia. I told her I wasn\u2019t going to tell my friends what they can or can\u2019t do but I really was caught off guard by the question and it showed. Just like when Julia texted me earlier and asked about telling Stasia about Gawain and Becky. I love Anastasia. My love for her was the only thing that kept me going in my darkest moments in Snow Globe. And the thought of having her back in my life makes me giddy enough to cartwheel along the faux battlements of the walkway. But I love Gawain and Becky. I am IN love with them. I don\u2019t think what Stasia and I had is dead but those embers are burned down pretty low and I\u2019m not sure things will ever be quite the same. Maybe if we\u2019d gotten past the awkward uncertain first crush stage but we never got the chance. They stole me before we could share more than that one shy kiss. <br /> <br /> I mean, she is still beautiful and I most certainly find her attractive. But let\u2019s be completely honest here, I have shards of glass growing through my skin. I smell like blood. Getting intimate with me is hazardous. I\u2019m not a pretty songbird with glorious feathers or an exotic lithe vixen with a two foot tongue. It bothers Becky that we can\u2019t ever completely relax in each others arms. That I can\u2019t trust myself to sleep with her instead of sitting awake holding her all night. And her feelings for me were the weapon the Sinister Bitch used against Stasia. Even if she wanted to revive them how could she ever really forget that? And it\u2019s not the physical intimacy I really want and need from her. It\u2019s the sister, the confidant, the partner in crime. I should talk to Insincere Marguerite after breakfast and make sure she knows I really am okay with her and Stasia fooling around, at least as long as she doesn\u2019t make any promises of emotional commitment she can\u2019t keep. But from what I\u2019ve seen so far, I don\u2019t think Stasia has any intention to let herself get attached like that again.<br /> <br /> And I really need to talk to Becky. I should have called her this evening but this seems like a face to face matter. I know yesterday morning wasn\u2019t easy for her. She wanted me to be happy and to reconnect with Stasia but after our talk she knew there was a chance she\u2019d lose me to a ghost from my past, right after she finally broke down and admitted that she had serious feelings for me. Maybe that\u2019s why she was going out of her way to be even more menacing toward Desiree than usual. (Though the little noose her hair tied itself into was fucking adorable.) I\u2019ll stop by after Maria and I do our forms and let her know how things went and reassure her that she is still my beautiful dragon and I am still very much hers. Maybe she can stop by for breakfast or movie night. I\u2019d like to introduce her to Stasia. I think they\u2019d get along. (Okay, I HOPE they get along since they\u2019re my bestie and my girlfriend.)<br /> <br /> And I really should sit down and talk to Gawain alone about things as well. I mean, he has been amazing and supportive. Hell, he seemed downright disappointed that he couldn\u2019t go with us to Bellevue. All of them have done so much to support me in this. The motley really is my family. Which makes me so glad that Stasia is getting along with them all so well. She\u2019s really the only part of my old life that\u2019s left and being able to integrate her into my new life is frankly amazing. I wouldn\u2019t have thought it could happen but seeing Lori and her dad and Jacob with his sister made me hope. And hope scares the fuck out of me. Because when you have hope you open yourself up to real pain. But as well as things have gone I can\u2019t help but feel hopeful. I can\u2019t help but feel like this visit is the beginning of a new chapter in the misadventures of Stasia and Kat.<br /> <br /> Fuck, it\u2019s going to hurt like hell if this goes wrong but right now I just can\u2019t stop smiling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T14:52:04-08:00","id":1055401,"title":"","content":"<b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Today started off a little tense this morning. Gawain made crepes for breakfast, which as always was delicious, but there was a bit of tension between Desiree and Becky. Apparently Becky stayed with Calamity last night and Desiree stayed with Gawain. The problem is Becky really doesn\u2019t like Desiree and wants to do her harm. There were not so subtle indirect threats going on. So, yeah things were a little strained. On the positive side of things there was talk of wedding and engagement rings and several of the ladies got all excited. Well, mostly it was Lori and De La Rocha getting excited about shopping for a ring for Lori and Julia and Insincere Marguerite getting excited for them. When the topic of wedding rings was brought up Gawain asked if the ladies would be interested in homemade rings. Everyone seemed rather interested in that and Gawain left for his forge to practice making rings. After that Calamity announced that she wanted to go to Seattle, via mirror, to go and visit her friend Stasia. Insincere Marguerite agreed to take her by way of mirror. Calamity has wanted to make amends with her childhood friend for some time now and has just recently found her with Marguerite\u2019s help. I offered to come along for moral support, but didn\u2019t realize how tiring transporting other people through mirrors could be so I agreed to stay behind. It would just be Insincere Marguerite and Calamity going. After that De La Rocha, Julia and Lori went ring shopping.<br /> <br /> While the ladies were going shopping I asked Luna if she\u2019d like to go on a hike in the woods with me. She readily agreed and we packed a backpack with water and snacks to take with us. It\u2019s been a while since we just went walking in nature and I wanted to do something nice for Luna since she\u2019s been so understanding of late. I know that I\u2019ve not been the easiest to be around for the past few days. I don\u2019t know if that will change much going forward, but I didn\u2019t want to keep Luna at arm\u2019s length anymore. While we were walking Luna asked if I understood the whole dynamic between Calamity/Becky and Gawain/Desiree. She was confused how Gawain and Calamity still get along so well when people that each of them see dislike each other so much. I think she figured that there would be tension there. I admitted that I was just as confused as she was about that whole thing. I would imagine that things would get strained between my motely mates, but they seem to be able to make it work. Don\u2019t ask me how, but they do.<br /> <br /> So, while we were walking I thanked Luna for being so understanding lately and for being there for me even though it was the weekend. I know how much she prefers her alone time when it\u2019s busy at the Dream House. She said something along the lines of \u201cOf course, I\u2019m your girlfriend.\u201d Like it made perfect sense. I suppose in a way it does. Things can get so complicated between people that I\u2019d understand if she or the others didn\u2019t get why I was so upset by Rook\u2019s death. I said as much. I really would understand. To them he was just someone that was hunting me down and attempting to bring me back to the Lady\u2019s realm. They only saw him at the end, defiant and bold. They didn\u2019t know him like I did. He did care about me at one point. I don\u2019t know how much he cared for me at the end though. He may have just been annoyed with me for making him bring me back, or he might have been angry with me for turning my back on our Lady. I know when I first defied him in Claire Falls he was surprised and a bit angry. He took out his anger on me when we fought, but as soon as he realized that he\u2019d gone too far in injuring me he immediately brought me to the Lady to be healed. Things didn\u2019t get much better after that, but I thought I saw regret on his face on more than one occasion while the Lady did her best to break me. I just wish things didn\u2019t have to end between us the way that they did.<br /> <br /> Luna for her part admitted to me that she would be devastated if something happened to me, and I told her that I felt the same way. I don\u2019t know if I show that often enough, but I do feel that way. I know that I can be hard to read, and that is I suppose entirely my own fault. I have gotten so used to wearing masks over the years that I do it unconsciously now, even when I don\u2019t want to. So, I admitted to Luna that I don\u2019t know what I\u2019d do if I lost her. She has become so important to me in such a short time. We mesh well, like two sides of the same coin. In a way it is scary to have such strong feelings for another person. It gives that person control over you. They can manipulate you or hurt you if they so desired. I suppose it\u2019s all about trust though. I trust Luna not to manipulate or hurt me, and I think she trusts me to do the same for her. I would never intentionally harm my Luna.<br /> <br /> When we got back to the jeep our phones chimed. I checked my messages to see one from Calamity saying that she was coming back to the Dream House with a guest, her friend Stasia. I guess things worked out between them. At least enough for Stasia to agree to visit us in California. We got back to the house about the same time that everyone else did. Julia, De La Rocha and Lori got back from shopping shortly before we did, but we all made it back in time to meet Calamity\u2019s childhood friend. Everyone was very welcoming to Stasia. Julia and Gawain decided to show her up to the guest room since she\u2019ll be staying with us for a few days. Apparently there was some tension during their meeting, but Calamity and Stasia managed to work it out. I\u2019m glad that my motley mate was able to rekindle the friendship with Stasia. Calamity deserves some good things in her life.<br /> <br /> This whole situation made me think about my friends in High School and if they were still friends with my fetch or not. I haven\u2019t asked Elena yet about all of that stuff. Nor have I asked her about how our family is doing. I need to do that sometime soon. I am curious to know how everyone is doing. Friends and family were important to me before I was taken. I can\u2019t help but wonder if the little shit continued those friendships or if he let them slide like he did our culture. I know enough about him to know that he goes by Jake most of the time now and pronounces his name the American way if he does go by Jacob. I think he\u2019s trying to be as American as he can. Maybe he got tired of being teased for speaking with an accent. Maybe he got tired of not understanding some American customs. I don\u2019t know. I just know that he has gone against everything that was important to me when I was in his shoes.<br /> <br /> It wasn\u2019t that long before the show started up. I served drinks as usual and talked to Molly and Luna while they kept me company. Molly asked if anything was new and I told her about the fire breathing piranha in our Hollow\u2019s moat. I think she was amused. I know I was. Gawain was so proud of the accomplishment. I know he\u2019s been trying for a while now to create the fish and have them be permanent rather than disappear after a short time. It was also a nice safe neutral topic to talk about. I really didn\u2019t feel like fielding any questions about my emotional state, and thankfully I didn\u2019t have to.<br /> <br /> As usual, the ladies did a wonderful job performing on the stage. I think Calamity, or Kat as Stasia calls her, was trying to show off for her childhood friend. Lori did her part to help spotlight Calamity\u2019s performance as well. They are just too talented.<br /> <br /> After the show Julia invited everyone to join her on the balcony for marijuana. I accepted the invitation. I think I\u2019d only over smoked pot once before when I was a kid. Elena and I had gone to a party at a friend\u2019s house and someone broke out a pipe. The parents were gone so we decided to give it a try. I don\u2019t remember it doing much for me at the time but thought it might be time to give it another try. I will admit that I did feel a bit light headed after smoking Julia\u2019s weed. I probably smiled more too. Not sure about that. I would have to ask Luna if I actually smiled or if I just felt like it on the inside. Anyway\u2026conversation took some interesting turns. Kidnapping got brought up and it was explained to Stasia why we are all so opposed to it. We would never hold someone against their will since it was done to all of us. None of us would do it now anyway. It wasn\u2019t that long ago that I had no qualms about taking people against their will and bringing them to the Lady\u2019s lands. Somehow during my relatively short stay with the Claire Falls freehold I regained something of my humanity. Something of my old self came back. Enough at least for me to turn away from the Lady\u2019s orders and defy my friend. I don\u2019t think that I can ever go back to what I was before the Lady. Too much has happened. Too much has changed. I have seen things that I cannot un-see and I have done things that I cannot undo. A part of me wishes that I could go back to being that na\u00efve child, but another part of me doesn\u2019t. I found a good friend and brother in Rook. We worked well together and enjoyed each other\u2019s company. He may never have betrayed the Lady and was working to bring me back, but I can\u2019t forget the good times we had. I can\u2019t forget my brother and I don\u2019t want to. I am not too keen on remembering all the things that I have done as Rime, but I don\u2019t want to forget my friend.<br /> <br /> We also talked about the passage of time between Arcadia and \u2018the world.\u2019 Lori mentioned that time passed much slower in the Empress\u2019s realm than it did here. Something like thirty-six years has passed in \u2018the world\u2019 compared to the one year or so that passed in Arcadia. For me it was the opposite. More time passed in the Lady\u2019s realm than it did here. I was only gone from \u2018the world\u2019 for two years, but so much more time passed in Arcadia. My guess is close to fifteen or twenty years. I still don\u2019t look quite that old though. My appearance was somewhat frozen in time, so to speak, since I started serving the Lady. I don\u2019t know for sure how long Rook served the Lady. I know it was for a good deal longer than I had, but I never flat out asked him. He was not the most forthcoming about his past, even with me.<br /> <br /> Overall Stasia was rather curious about us and our experiences. She had taken it pretty well when Calamity enchanted her back at her house so she could see her friend as she is. Stasia took it all in stride when she saw the rest of us and just seemed to want to know all about us, our freehold, the political system we have etc\u2026 Our appearances didn\u2019t faze her that much at all. I suppose I should give her credit for that. She has not been judgmental at all. She has just been curious. She is not na\u00efve though. I got the impression that she is a fairly jaded person most of the time, but this was something new and she wanted to know about. She was also high, so that might have played a part in her curiosity as well.<br /> <br /> All in all it was a pretty good day. I enjoyed spending time with Luna and meeting Calamity\u2019s friend was nice too. I suppose I was reminded a bit too much of my own past with the conversation topics that came up, but that happens regardless of what I do. I can\u2019t help but remember things, and more and more comes back to be every day. At least more about my former life does. I remember my time as Rime pretty clearly. It\u2019s just before that time that there were gaps. I\u2019ve also realized that I have lived longer as Rime than I have as Jacob. Not by much, but Rime has made up more of my years than that little Russian bookworm did. I certainly remember more years as Rime than I do as Jacob. Maybe that\u2019s why it\u2019s so easy to slip back into those old habits. They are more ingrained in me than anything I did as a kid. I suppose it will just take time to rediscover who Jacob is now. He certainly isn\u2019t who he was at sixteen. Would that I were. Life might be simpler if I was that boy again.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> Today has proven to be productive. I helped Calamity get her friend Stasia here to visit, and have taken steps to repair their friendship. She did a fairly decent job with the conversation and did not send things spiraling out. So I am pleased.<br /> <br /> Sex Breakfast went well. Spirits were high from the proposal yesterday. Oleander took it reasonably well, apparently. Maria wanted to go ring shopping, and Julia had experience, so she and Juliette went with her out after breakfast. They did select a ring, and it is lovely, so Juliette and Julia both sport rings now. I would have gone, but was drawn away by commitments.<br /> <br /> Calamity wanted to go and visit Stasia. Gawain and Jacob both volunteered to help, but it needed to be a private conversation, and taking many extra people with me is a strain. Mirror travel is remarkably tiring. Gawain went to practice making rings (to eventually make four wedding bands) and Jacob went to hike with Luna.<br /> <br /> We arrived in a Starbucks, and walked the couple of blocks to Stasia\u2019s house. The neighborhood was lower middle class, but the houses fairly nice. Calamity wished to speak alone to her, so after a failed attempt to dismiss me, she acquiesced to me hiding nearby. I was reminded Stasia is very pretty. Despite the stammering at the front door and tripping over her words, she eventually got Stasia to let her in. Stasia leaned with her arms in the doorway, in a pose I might expect from Maria. She never dropped her guard.<br /> <br /> Inside she made coffee while Calamity waited and I climbed in the window. It soon became apparent she knew something was wrong with Calamity\u2019s fetch and that she had realized Calamity\u2019s parents had been murdered, when she noted she was pointing a gun at my Motley mate and was using her phone waiting for five minute check ins. In this case, Calamity\u2019s blunt honesty worked; she got Stasia to let down her guard. Once Stasia saw Calamity for what she was, she sympathetic, though she remained cold about Calamity\u2019s parents.<br /> <br /> Not that she apparently cared for them.<br /> <br /> After some back and forth Calamity suggested talking to me, so I retreated back out the window and knocked on the front door. I introduced myself, and we set about to discussing Stasia visiting. As a photographer between assignments, her schedule was flexible. Calamity suggested, and I backed up, a visit to Malibu. She, perhaps taken in by surreality of the situation agreed, after ending her check-ins. She packed, and we traveled through the mirror home.<br /> <br /> We arrived back in Malibu about the same time the others got there. Stasia was introduced to everyone, and then Julia and Gawain took her stuff up to the room Elena had been using till today. Julia filled her in on the state of relationships and drama on the way up. I presume she walked slowly.<br /> <br /> We got ready for the show. Apparently The Oldacres had picked up two of our singers, and had sex at their hotel room. Go John and Linda, I guess. Juliette told me she and Maria had decided they would prefer separate ceremonies, but were open to the pledge. This made sense. I said I would tell Julia. She was liable to take it badly unless phrased just so. I would not mind a minor ceremony to link the two couples. We will see. They are up for the pledge, which is good.<br /> <br /> Midway through, I found out Felicity had not come, as Rowan was with her getting drunk. I wrestled with it, but eventually told Juliette. I think I made the right decision. She was unhappy, but glad Rowan had someone there. Juliette is such a lovely person.<br /> <br /> After the show (and after Gawain and Captain Jack had a chase scene around the room) we all went to the back porch to toke and chat a bit. Stasia seemed very happy with her luck, going on about her mundane day plans, and asking us all sorts of questions about the House, about Faerie Politics, about Courts, etc. She seems cleaver, and interested in possibly moving down. Things got flirty, which was at least in part my fault. It usually is.<br /> <br /> Stasia is cute, so afterwards I asked Calamity about the potential for a fling. I am fairly certain she mentally undressed most of our group, and I did her. So long as she is not bothered by my being left handed.<br /> <br /> Odd. Julia and I are lefties, and Maria and Juliette are right handed. That gives us a certain\u2026symmetry, doesn\u2019t it.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Calamity said it was okay, but was very halting. I must consider this. Frankly, what I need to tell her is she needs to either pursue Stasia or be okay with someone else doing so, or encourage her to not move to Malibu (or with her money, Santa Monica). My worry is she will simply brood over her childhood friend as we are a very\u2026enlightened hold.<br /> <br /> My hard decision is Felicity. I confess disappointment she did not come tonight, though I respect her for taking care of Rowan. We have been simmering since our union Friday. It is a question how to handle things going forward. We need to talk. I may should also get Juliette\u2019s view, she having the relationship with Oleander outside our quartet. I am closer than casual with some women like Desiree and Flores, but no one so pronouncedly intense outside the four but Felicity.<br /> <br /> I have a lot to think about.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXXVI</i><br /> <br /> Lorelei was right and Insincere Marguerite wrong about the timing of saying they wanted separate ceremonies. De La Rocha talked to Insincere Marguerite earlier in the day as Lori said.<br /> <br /> So only Insincere Marguerite saw the whole \u201cCaptain Jack dressed as Tarzan swinging down from the rafters with the extendable butt grabber\u201d thing as worth even a side mention. I am not sure at this point what he has to do to merit mention from the others. I am sure if there was a Gawain it would have been mentioned, though.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Insincere Marguerite, she used Contract of Reflections to get to Seattle, is why she had to do it. Weirdly, she has Mirrors and Reflections (Ace also has Mirrors, no one else has Reflections). Reflections gets punishingly expensive to use on others, but it is fairly long distance travel. Speaking of Contracts, Lorelei and Calamity both frontloaded their shows with Vainglory and Verdant Spring, which gave them successes well into the teens if not twenties. Lorelei also being a Minstrel of course went above and beyond even that.<br /> <br /> Stasia I played <i><i>heavily</i></i> queer coded, much like Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne. Obviously not all the queer folks are played that way, but the sort that one might guess even if she did not actively show preference.<br /> <br /> Dionisia is a Fatemaker, so more easily avoids cruel twists of fate but is still subject to addiction.<br /> <br /> Okay, hope you enjoyed. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 02-26-2017, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T21:06:30-08:00","id":1055525,"title":"","content":"What? Captain Jack came around and he barely got a mention? I feel robbed. It was nice having what was basically a purely gay Lord Flashheart around. <br /> <br /> And on the note of Stasia, her reactions to all of this make me suspicious. Besides, it's a rule of the universe that Calamity can never be happy for more than two entries in a row. Something's gonna go down","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> <