o, as came out more in the session than the journals, when Calamity's parents were mysteriously murdered she suspected something was up. The initial conversation was tense, with Stasia holding a gun on Calamity until she was sure that she wasn't there to kill her as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T11:29:42-08:00","id":1055718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play?p=1055525#post1055525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What? Captain Jack came around and he barely got a mention? I feel robbed. It was nice having what was basically a purely gay Lord Flashheart around.</div> </div> </div> </div>I KNOW RIGHT! He had an extendable butt grabber! Pearls before swine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And on the note of Stasia, her reactions to all of this make me suspicious. Besides, it's a rule of the universe that Calamity can never be happy for more than two entries in a row. Something's gonna go down </div> </div> </div>What is suspicious, out of curiosity?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> P.S Those Ace entries never really materialized, so as an alternate proposal, what do you all think of having your own TV Tropes page? Been meaning to make an account and learn how to format pages for a while now anyway </div> </div> </div>I mean, if it makes you happy...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T15:07:04-08:00","id":1055813,"title":"","content":"Largely, how well she took the &quot;Calamity murdered her own (admittedly shallow, but still) parents&quot; thing, even with the initial standoff. Also, how well she took the whole &quot;magic is real and so are evil kidnapping fairies that replaced your best friend/crush with a evil traitorous cheerleader bitch&quot; thing, even if she had always suspected something was weird. Fairly sure that stuff calls for a Integrity Breaking Point roll. Also, all the mentions of her asking questions about details like Court politics and such, that would be useful to anything from anti-fae hunters to True Fae. And last but not least, Calamity is too happy and the Wyrd hates happiness. So either something's wrong with Stasia, Calamity is going to have to go into hiding after getting fingered for murdering her Fetch (we all know she's gonna do it and I for one am gonna cheer) or the Wyrd is going to sic the Furies on them for trying to escape their Fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T11:57:32-08:00","id":1056255,"title":"","content":"Stasia believed, true or not Calamity's parents supported her Fetch's ruining her life. She was still harshly accusatory about it. She did have to make a Integrity check, when she went through the mirror, she passed but got a version of Spooked making her highly inquisitive.<br /> <br /> Stasia suddenly had her old best friend returned, and take her to a Burlesque House which was full of attractive queer fairy women who were all super nice and most of whom were flirty. There was some danger, true, but she has not shied away from danger. There was free pot. I won't say she is not a little suspicious, but right now she desperately wants all this to be real.<br /> <br /> The other thing going on with Stasia is she does have something of a solid context for all this: The show <i>Lost Girl</i>. Really anything the PC don't say is different she presumes is like <i>Lost Girl</i>. She is even a girl with a Ukrainian background with a Fae bestie. She has adopted some of the show's terminology. It's been reflected in some of her many questions, including stuff about etiquette and how they feed on people, and her being quick to believe she understands about stuff like the Malibu Dream House being neutral territory or how Succubi work when Calamity mentioned Becky. The characters don't know this, but I mentioned it OOC in Sunday's session. Her understanding of what is happening still mimics the show more than how things actually work. So for the moment, she seems to be be in her favorite show, sort of? <br /> <br /> Calamity is not necessarily destined to be unhappy, though she brings a lot of misery down on herself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T13:18:41-07:00","id":1061595,"title":"","content":"The above paragraph on my last comment has some major insights into Staia's mindset, if you have not already read it.<br /> <br /> Our little family has a guest! And of course more going on besides. Let\u2019s check in on the Last Dance. No Calamity this time, though her player was there. <br /> <br /> <i>Session LXXVII</i><br /> <b><br /> Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Time passes, and life goes on, and I find myself ever-so-slightly less giddy with each passing day. Now don\u2019t get me wrong; the thought that sometime in the near future Maria and I will be <u>married</u> still makes me deliriously happy every time it drifts past my consciousness, but I\u2019m finding that both this information and the feelings it engenders have been incorporated into my status quo remarkably quickly.<br /> <br /> So once my girls finally decided to get up and face the day, the four of us descended to sex breakfast en masse. Most of the rest of the house was already up, and Gawain was displaying his culinary prowess by making his trademark delicious crepes. Stasia once again proved her perspicacity just after breakfast by cornering Marguerite against a wall and asking her directly if she had sent her a mirror which had mysteriously arrived a few months earlier. Marguerite was mock-cagey with her answer, but it was obvious to the other girl that she was responsible. Stasia is <u>smart</u>. We need to remember that in the future.<br /> <br /> D had to work, and it was obvious that she wasn\u2019t really looking forward to the experience. I thought I\u2019d do what I could to mitigate her misery, and offered to pick up lunch at her favorite restaurant and bring it by the hospital about three o\u2019clock, hinting that she might enjoy showing me off to her co-workers as her fianc\u00e9e. Her eyes lit up at the suggestion, and she agreed at once.<br /> <br /> Stasia and Calamity went off after breakfast to spend the day together and get reacquainted. None of us really wanted to get in the middle of that reunion of old friends, so we decided to disperse. Gawain mentioned that he was going to run by the Lighthouse and maybe take advantage of the Autumn Court\u2019s library to research a few contracts which might be able to help him with his dream healing endeavors, and I opted to tag along on the chance that I might be able to speak with Dionysia about her \u201cproblem.\u201d I took my own car, though, as I knew that I wouldn\u2019t be able to stay long if I wanted to keep my lunch date with D.<br /> <br /> So the two of us approached Moon at the library. Gawain asked about the contracts he wanted to research, and Moon told him where he could find more information. Ze also let me know that Dionysia was in residence, and wished me the best of luck in talking to her.<br /> <br /> I found her in the stacks, looking as delectable and mysterious as ever, and greeted her as lightly as I could. \u201cLorelei,\u201d she said with a smile, \u201cthis is an unexpected pleasure. Congratulations,\u201d she said with a wink and a nod at my ring. \u201cNow what can I do for you?\u201d<br /> <br /> I won\u2019t even try to recreate the actual conversation here. I started out by asking her about Talecrafting in a general sort of way; I hope she just thought that I was curious about the art itself. I don\u2019t know a lot about how it works, and if I <u>had</u> been interested in learning more about it, I couldn\u2019t have picked a better teacher than Dionysia. She\u2019s widely regarded as the Freehold\u2019s expert.<br /> <br /> She is obviously enamored of her craft. She waxed poetic about how life has a tendency to fall into predictable patterns, and how this trend is even more pronounced among changelings, who are after all creatures of the Wyrd. I let her go on about it for a few minutes. I have to admit that the subject is fascinating, but I don\u2019t think I\u2019ll be putting aside my microphone in favor of weaving reality any time soon. For one thing, it\u2019s a very complex and difficult discipline to master. For another, it\u2019s <u>dangerous</u>.<br /> <br /> Dionysia mentioned \u201ccruel twists of fate\u201d several times (I\u2019m not sure if any part of that should be capitalized or not). This is essentially what happens when reality pushes back against a Talecrafter\u2019s meddling and reasserts itself. The consequences can be dire\u2026 both to the Talecrafter and to her subjects. Dionysia \u2013 due both to her nature and to her extensive experience \u2013 is exceptionally good at avoiding these cruel twists of fate, but she is not so arrogant as to assume that she\u2019s immune.<br /> <br /> I seized my opportunity at this point in the conversation. \u201cAre there any other dangers associated with Talecrafting?\u201d I asked innocently. \u201cI\u2019ve heard that some people get sort of addicted to it\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Dionysia shrugged it off. \u201cIt\u2019s a danger, of course,\u201d she said, \u201cbut one that\u2019s easily circumvented by the diligent. True masters of Talecrafting are always alert for signs of addiction in themselves, and take steps to prevent it from taking hold.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, sure,\u201d I said with a nod, \u201cbut, I mean, it can be really hard to spot addiction in <u>yourself</u>. That\u2019s part of what makes it so insidious.\u201d<br /> <br /> She shook her head. \u201cAs I said, it\u2019s always a danger, but I for one am careful to treat the craft with the respect it deserves. I know what I\u2019m doing, Lorelei.\u201d<br /> <br /> I\u2019d been expecting her to push back, and I figured it was time to play my trump card. \u201cHey, I\u2019m not trying to convince you of anything here, Dionysia,\u201d I said in what I hoped was a placating tone. \u201cYou\u2019re the expert. All I know about Talecrafting is what you\u2019ve told me over the last few minutes. But\u2026 well, I <u>have</u> dealt with my share of addictions over the years, and those who suffer from addiction are almost never the first to spot it. It\u2019s the same old story, over and over.\u201d<br /> <br /> It was subtle, but I think I got the reaction I was hoping for. Her eyebrows shot up the tiniest bit, and she nodded slightly. \u201cThat\u2019s\u2026 an interesting observation,\u201d she admitted. \u201cYou\u2019ve given me a lot to think about.\u201d<br /> <br /> I thanked her for speaking with me, got her to promise to stop by the show the following evening, and bade her farewell. On the way out, I stopped to fill Moon in on how our conversation had gone. Ze seemed pleased, and said ze would be at the show the next evening as well. I think ze is hoping we\u2019ll be able to make a bit more progress with Dionysia if we speak with her together.<br /> <br /> So I called in an order to D\u2019s favorite hole-in-the-wall, and thirty minutes later she rushed up to me in the break room at the hospital and frenched me like there would be no tomorrow. Sometimes I think she overcompensates, but who am I to dissuade my honey from public displays of affection?<br /> <br /> \u201cMissed you, babe,\u201d she said when she came up for air.<br /> <br /> I threw her a wink. \u201cIt\u2019s only been about three hours, D,\u201d I chided with a grin.<br /> <br /> \u201cThree to many, if you ask me,\u201d she growled back.<br /> <br /> \u201cDamn right,\u201d I shot back. \u201cI missed you too, sweetie.\u201d<br /> <br /> Something that sounded suspiciously like an \u201c<u>awwwwwww</u>\u201d drifted up from one of the occupied tables, but D silenced the offender with a glance. The two of us sat down at an open table and proceeded to eat a light lunch while chatting idly with each other and with a few of D\u2019s friendlier co-workers. There were more than a few congratulations offered up, most of which seemed to involve people giving D a hearty slap on the back.<br /> <br /> Eventually my love couldn\u2019t put it off any longer; she had to get back to work. She left me with another passionate kiss and a promise that she\u2019d be back in time for movie night. For my part, I settled back into a couch and finished reading a magazine article on an experimental treatment for tachycardia. Twenty minutes later, I left as well.<br /> <br /> Julia met me at the door when I got back to the Dream House. \u201cMarguerite told me,\u201d she said as the two of us walked upstairs together.<br /> <br /> I caught her eye. \u201cAbout how I wanted separate ceremonies?\u201d I asked softly. She nodded. \u201cAnd you\u2019re okay with that?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> She smiled after a moment. \u201cOf course I am,\u201d she said. \u201cI know I tend to get caught up in things, Lori, but I understand how you feel. And it\u2019s not like we\u2019re not all going to be involved in <u>both</u> ceremonies, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> I pulled her into a hug. \u201cYou don\u2019t expect me to get married without my Maid of Honor, do you?\u201d I asked through my tears.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd\u2026 Marguerite said you were re-thinking the idea of a Pledge between the four of us,\u201d she said hesitantly. \u201cThis isn\u2019t just some ploy to get me to shut up about a joint ceremony, is it? Because I swear you don\u2019t have to do that\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I kissed her. <u>Hard</u>. \u201cJulia,\u201d I said softly after we\u2019d parted, \u201cthat\u2019s not what this is about. Maria and I\u2026 this proposal just has us thinking about our lives a little differently, that\u2019s all. I\u2026 I want to be married to Maria. <u>Me</u>. I want to be Lorelei de la Rocha. But the two of us\u2026 we never want to be parted from you and Marguerite. We want you to know that. We want the rest of the Freehold to know it. And we want the <u>Wyrd</u> to know it.\u201d<br /> <br /> She gave me a watery smile. \u201cThat\u2019s what I want too,\u201d she whispered, and then leaned in for another kiss.<br /> <br /> Everyone was back in time for movie night, though before the frivolity began Gawain asked to speak to the motley. He wanted to tell us about the cool Goblin Contracts he had researched, and with good reason. Apparently he discovered a <u>lot</u> of ways to enhance his abilities while he\u2019s in someone\u2019s dreams, which can only help with that dream-healing and dream-combat stuff he\u2019s so into. Considering how much good he\u2019s already done for the Freehold with those skills, I can only see that as a good thing.<br /> <br /> He\u2026 well, he also mentioned another Contract. One which could be of some use when the time comes to rescue Missy and Jane. This Contract allows a changeling to spy on a member of the Gentry without being detected. If we could see what the Empress is up to when we sneak into her Realm, that information could prove invaluable. It could make or break the whole mission.<br /> <br /> The thing about Goblin Contracts is that there\u2019s always a catch. Regular Contracts are exploitable, with loopholes and clauses that allow you to come out ahead. Goblin Contracts can be significantly more powerful, but it always comes at a cost. In this case, if one of us uses the Contract to spy on the Empress, that person\u2019s Keeper will<u> instantly</u> know where they are.<br /> <br /> Obviously this means that I can\u2019t be the one to use the Contract. Though I\u2019d be happy to shoulder the burden rather than allow any of my friends to face that terrible risk, it would eliminate the element of surprise if the Empress suddenly knew that I was near, and the element of surprise is one of the few things we have going for us. <br /> <br /> Marguerite has offered to use the Contract. On the surface, it seems like a perfect solution\u2026 she believes that Mama Lion is dead, and even if this isn\u2019t the case, the two of them had a good relationship. But\u2026 dammit, I\u2019m not entirely sure she\u2019s right about Mama Lion. The Gentry scare me, and I love Marguerite, and I will <u>not</u> do something that will put her in danger. Maybe it would be better to just forget about this Goblin Contract and do the best we can without it.<br /> <br /> There was some discussion as to which films we should watch last night. In the end we decided upon an unlikely pair of flicks, as different from each other as possible.<br /> <br /> The liquor was flowing freely all evening. Marguerite had a bottle of expensive cognac out, while I opted for more affordable Kentucky bourbon as usual. I offered to pour my French lover a shot, but she turned her nose up at my less refined alcohol. Sensing an opportunity for fun, I shrugged, turned away, and said \u201cI don\u2019t know why you\u2019re giving me that look, Marguerite\u2026 when you scratch the surface, cognac is really just snooty bourbon.\u201d<br /> <br /> Of course that set her off like nobody\u2019s business. \u201cSnooty Bourbon\u201d became the catch-phrase of the evening, guaranteed to set most of us laughing and to send Marguerite into paroxysms of Gallic indignation. I tried to make nice at one point, telling her that I had only said it to have a little fun and maybe get her goat a little bit, but she was having none of it. \u201cThere will be no getting of the goat!\u201d she sniffed with one of those cute little \u201chrmph\u201d noises she makes when she\u2019s in a tizzy.<br /> <br /> Anyway\u2026 first up was a fantasy kung-fu extravaganza called <u>Crouching Tiger, Hidden Dragon</u>. This was apparently an attempt by Chinese studios to elevate the martial arts film beyond its roots in the cheap chop-socky beat-em-ups that Jane used to love so much. I confess that kung-fu films were never really my thing, and while this one was head-and-shoulders above any I\u2019d ever seen in terms of quality, something about it still left me cold. Don\u2019t get me wrong; it had some <u>gorgeous</u> cinematography, and the stunts and martial arts were almost enough to make one believe in magic. But from a story standpoint the second act had real pacing issues and the romantic sub-plot struck me as saccharine and insipid (and this is coming from someone who is still googly-eyed over recently becoming engaged).<br /> <br /> Ahh, whatever. A lot of the others really enjoyed it\u2026 including but not limited to Calamity, Stasia, and the love of my life.<br /> <br /> The second film was called <u>Johnny Dangerously</u>\u2026 and yes, someone does point out to the main character at one point that his last name is an adverb. It was incredibly silly, but hilarious for all of that. It was a send-up of old depression-era gangster stories, and played against tropes so old that even I recognized most of them. One of the funniest \u2013 and apparently most quotable \u2013 characters in the film was a rival \u201ctough guy\u201d gangster who liked to issue veiled threats by alluding to people who had crossed him in the past. \u201cYou shouldn\u2019t oughta hang me on a hook, Johnny. My father hung me on a hook once\u2026 <u>once</u>!\u201d<br /> <br /> It was good goofy fun, but I confess that it didn\u2019t require a lot of brain power to follow, and as I was relaxing into my love\u2019s oh-so-strong embrace, I found myself more often than not eschewing the entertainment of the film in favor of making out with her subtly. I kissed her neck a fair amount, and her ear, and eventually her lips. Julia and Marguerite were engaged in similar activities next to us, and I don\u2019t think these acts went unnoticed by the rest of the group.<br /> <br /> \u201cI should\u2026 go back to my room,\u201d Stasia said, red-faced, after the final credits had rolled.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat\u2019s your rush?\u201d I asked, pitching my voice low.<br /> <br /> She seemed taken aback for a few seconds. \u201cOh\u2026 was there an invitation implicit there?\u201d she asked after a moment.<br /> <br /> I glanced at Calamity, who gave me a slight nod. Then I looked to my lovers. \u201cWhat do you say, girls? Is there room for one more tonight?\u201d <br /> <br /> They all allowed as how we could squeeze in tight together to make room, and the four of us led a rather dazed-looking Stasia to our boudoir for an evening of fun. She kept muttering something to herself that sounded suspiciously like \u201cI must be dreaming, there\u2019s no <u>way</u> this is really happening.\u201d<br /> <br /> Stasia had told us that she doesn\u2019t \u201cdo\u201d relationships, so the usual disclaimers about how last night was only a bit of fun seemed unnecessary. I know that I usually like to be the center of attention in group romps like that, but there was sort of a silent agreement between the four of us that we would show Stasia a night she wouldn\u2019t soon forget, so most of the action was centered on her this time around. I\u2019m guessing Calamity had briefed her on how sex with me tends to go, because she made a point of feeding me a single piece of chocolate before things got too intense, and I was consequently able to keep her energy levels high for the entire night.<br /> <br /> So last night was fairly\u2026 \u201cfrolicsome,\u201d and I think everyone involved had a wonderful time. The five of us staggered downstairs in various stages of dishabille for Sex Breakfast the next morning, and Stasia quickly turned the talk once more toward the facts of changeling life. She seemed to know or guess a fair amount already, though not all of her assumptions were completely on the money. For instance, when the subject of glamour came up, she asked if that was how we \u201cfed\u201d on humans\u2026 and I don\u2019t think any of us had ever really thought about it in those terms before. It almost made it sound a little sinister.<br /> <br /> I thought back to when we had tried to explain the whole glamour thing to my Dad a couple of weeks ago, and remembered something Gawain had said then. \u201cThink of emotional glamour as being sort of like sunlight,\u201d I said, \u201cand we\u2019re the plants that depend on it. We\u2019re not really <u>taking</u> anything from the sun\u2026 it gives off its light regardless of what we do. We just take advantage of that fact.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI see,\u201d Stasia said after considering this analogy for a moment. \u201cAnd\u2026 these Courts you keep talking about. Is it like the Seelie and Unseelie? The Dark and the Light? Do I need to declare myself to them or anything to prevent misunderstandings?\u201d<br /> <br /> We sort of laughed that one off. \u201cThe courts are more like support groups than a real ruling body,\u201d Gawain said. \u201cThey won\u2019t mess with you unless you mess with them first. I mean\u2026 some courts like a particular flavor of glamour, so they might try to scare you or make you angry or something, but they\u2019d have no reason to hurt you unless you\u2019re making trouble for them.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cExcept for the Day Court,\u201d Marguerite chimed in. \u201cThey are terrible people. You can make all of the trouble for them you desire.\u201d I gave her a withering stare, and she amended her statement. \u201cExcept for Lori\u2019s girlfriend Rowan. She seems nice. Oh, and I am sleeping with a woman named Felicity\u2026 I would appreciate it if you did not antagonize her just now.\u201d As she had essentially covered every Day Courtier Stasia was likely to meet in this Freehold by that point, I let it drop.<br /> <br /> Stasia\u2019s wry wit surged forward again as we were cleaning up from breakfast. \u201cIt figures that the first time I come to Malibu would be in December,\u201d she said bitterly.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat\u2019s wrong with December?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> She shrugged. \u201cNothing, but it\u2019s not exactly beach season, is it?\u201d she asked. \u201cKat and I were talking about hitting the beach today.\u201d<br /> <br /> I laughed. \u201cHoney, it\u2019s like seventy-five degrees and gorgeous out there,\u201d I said. \u201cI\u2019d <u>love</u> to go to the beach, if you two don\u2019t mind the company.\u201d<br /> <br /> As I\u2019d hoped, the rest of the motley \u2013 eventually including even Julia \u2013 decided to come along as well, and we made an afternoon of it. Some of us went surfing, some worked on our tans, and some went wading. Luna stayed on the beach for the most part, citing her delicate wings as an excuse not to get in the water. \u201cTell me about it,\u201d I commiserated at one point. \u201cI know I have a different and less serious set of problems, but dammit\u2026 these things get really heavy when they\u2019re wet!\u201d Luckily, my wings also afford me a bit of an advantage where balance is concerned, and I rarely had to worry about falling off of my surfboard.<br /> <br /> We once again decided to play beach volleyball\u2026 but this time Calamity thought it might be more fun to challenge some of the local mortals to a game instead of playing against each other. It didn\u2019t take me long to find some challengers (okay, so I might have overplayed it a little bit, commenting on how I really wanted to jump around on the beach for a while and displaying my bikini to its best advantage), and within about five minutes we had a game going.<br /> <br /> Those poor bastards. They never knew what hit them.<br /> <br /> Ahem. As I was saying, we won the game quite handily, and I\u2019m certain that all of us were as gracious in victory as we could possibly manage. Not that this was particularly gracious where hyper-competitive souls like Calamity and my fianc\u00e9e were involved, of course. Me\u2026 I was happy just as long as people were giving me the occasional admiring glance.<br /> <br /> So a good time was had by all, and we made our way back to the Dream House in plenty of time to get ready for tonight\u2019s show\u2026 which is honestly what I should be doing now. I keep going back and forth in my mind about whether I want to announce my engagement on stage at some point. A part of me really wants to shout my joy for all the world to see, but another part insists that this is private, that the whole wide world doesn\u2019t need to know how happy I am. I\u2019ve been wearing my ring pretty much everywhere, and I\u2019m sure that some of our regulars have picked up on that fact\u2026 I dunno. I\u2019ve still got a few hours to decide.<br /> <br /> Life is good. I\u2019m going to rescue Missy and Jane, and as scary as that is to me, it\u2019s still good news. I live with a lot of wonderful people who all love me in one way or another. My dad and I finally have the sort of relationship fathers and daughters are <u>supposed</u> to have. I have a good job that lets me use my talents to support myself and do a little good at the same time. And I\u2019m getting married to the most wonderful girl in the world. Most of these things wouldn\u2019t even have been <u>possible</u> in 1978. I hate to say it, but I keep revisiting a conversation we had almost six months ago, and, well\u2026 maybe my life <u>is</u> better for having been sent to Arcadia.<br /> <b><br /> Lorelei Grace</b><br /> <b><br /> <br /> Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> It\u2019s been five days since Rook died and today went on like nothing happened. Everyone has just slipped back into their normal life and it doesn\u2019t seem fair. I wish I could do that. I\u2019ve been acting like all is well, but I\u2019m not sure how much longer I can fake it. I guess time will tell on that one. Today at least started off like any other. Gawain made crepes, I think to show off to Stasia, and everyone was there. Calamity was downright cheerful. I think she\u2019s still riding high on the fact that her childhood friend has been so accepting of everything and agreed to visit. Stasia for her part had a lot of questions which the lot of us did our best to answer. We explained about the courts and the emotions associated with each one as well as glamour. She also asked us questions about the traditional faerie stories and whether or not cold iron and church bells would really harm us. The old stories do have some basis in fact of course, but no one that I know if in the freehold is susceptible to cold iron or church bells.<br /> <br /> After our round of twenty questions everyone broke off to do their own thing for the most part. I know that Lori went to the Autumn Court Library to talk to Dionysia, while Gawain went to research dream contracts. Stasia and Calamity went to the Pier for the day. I\u2019m not sure what Insincere Marguerite and Julia were up to. I think De La Rocha had to work. For my part, Luna and I decided to watch Netflix today. We found Firefly and decided that was a good choice and sat down to enjoy hours of space cowboy fun. I think I saw some episodes when I was a kid, but didn\u2019t remember much about the show. I just knew that people had said that it was good. They were right. It also made a good distraction for me. It helped me forget about Rook for a while. I will admit that I was tempted to drink myself stupid this afternoon and watch TV, but decided against it. At least I decided against the drinking myself stupid part. I don\u2019t think Luna would have appreciated a drunk Jacob, though in my defense I\u2019m not a loud drunk. I tend to be quiet. But then when am I not quiet?<br /> <br /> When Gawain got back from the Lighthouse he had some interesting news. He had been researching contracts that would allow him to be better at Dream healing and Dream combat and came across some that might be helpful. He also came across a contract that would allow the user to spy on the exact whereabouts of a Gentry. The idea was that we might be able to use this contract to see where the Empress was before we started on our mission to rescue Jane and Missy. There\u2019s a catch though. There always is with Goblin contracts. If you use this particular contract your own Keeper will know in that moment exactly where you are. It doesn\u2019t make sense for Lori to use it since we want to keep the Empress blind to her location. Insincere Marguerite volunteered to be the one to use the contract, stating that her Keeper is likely dead. Not to mention they had a good relationship when Marguerite was in Arcadia. I don\u2019t know if we want to take the chance that Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Keeper is really dead. She might be alive and quite mad at finding her favorite pupil gone. On the other hand, I could use the contract. As far as I know the Lady already knows where I am. She does allow for some autonomy among her Knights, but it makes sense that Rook would have relayed my location to her after he got free from Darke. We didn\u2019t discuss this contract very long or very seriously so I didn\u2019t bring up the fact that the Lady probably knows where I am. If we talk about this contract again I will bring it up then. <br /> <br /> So tonight was movie night. I had almost forgotten about that. We, the motley plus Luna and Becky, decided to watch Crouching Tiger, Hidden Dragon and Johnny Dangerously. I suggested the second movie. I remember seeing it as a kid in Russia and thought it was hilarious. It mostly stands up to the test of time if you ask me. Crouching Tiger was pretty good if you like wire kung-Fu movies. Some of the action was a bit silly, but it had a good story and I enjoyed it. I did drink during the movies though. Marguerite had brought a bottle of cognac and everyone else had different drinks too. I had the stereotypical vodka. What can I say? I like it. Especially the good stuff that we get for the bar. Anyway, there was much teasing going on about what people were drinking. In particular, it was pointed out that cognac is the \u201csnooty bourbon\u201d and Insincere Marguerite was teased for liking it so much. There was also something about getting her goat. It took me awhile to remember what that turn of phrase meant, but it was used several times. Marguerite was a bit indignant about being teased, but it was all in good fun. <br /> <br /> Truth be told I\u2019m still drunk now as I\u2019m writing this. I\u2019m starting to sober up unfortunately but I still have a nice buzz going on. I wasn\u2019t the only one to get drunk or at least tipsy though. I think the ladies, Julia, Insincere Marguerite, Lori and De La Rocha, were all in a good mood. They were certainly flirting a lot with Stasia and making out with each other. It got a little more intense than I think Luna was comfortable with and she moved to my other side to get further away from the quartet. Shortly after the movies were over they, including Stasia, went upstairs for the evening. No need to ask what those guys are going to get up to. I will admit that I was a little surprised that Stasia agreed to go up with them. At least right now. I was expecting that little tryst to take a little longer to happen. Shows you what I know.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> This morning Calamity and I drove to therapy together as usual. It was a quiet ride in the jeep. Calamity was still in a good mood and I didn\u2019t want to bring her down so I stayed quiet for the most part. The session was less than helpful. Dr. Sullivan wanted to talk to me about Rook, and that was the one topic I really didn\u2019t want to discuss. He knows how I feel about it. That hasn\u2019t changed in the past six days. So why talk about it? What could be gained by doing that? So we moved onto more neutral topics. The doctor asked if I\u2019d sparred with anyone in the last week or so and I answered truthfully, that I hadn\u2019t. I haven\u2019t been in the mood to spar with anyone. I have been in the mood to fight, but not spar. The difference being anyone fighting me would get hurt and I don\u2019t want to hurt my friends. Realistically I know that Calamity can handle herself, but it wouldn\u2019t be good to actually aim to do real damage. We usually leave little scratches as reminders of where the other person left themselves open, but we don\u2019t actually aim to hurt. I guess I\u2019ve been afraid that in my anger I would aim to hurt or I\u2019d forget to pull my hit and actually do harm. I admitted to the doctor that I\u2019ve been too angry to fight lately and he suggested that I try and go back to it, but be mindful of where and when I am.<br /> <br /> So, we got back to the house in short order. Again it was a fairly quiet trip home. We made small talk but didn\u2019t get into anything serious. We arrived to find Gawain cooking omelets, so I started making coffee to everyone\u2019s tastes. Another fairly normal day. Nothing to indicate that my world got knocked on its side six days ago. I guess I\u2019m just too good at creating masks to wear. People have stopped asking if I\u2019m okay, which is not a bad thing per say, it\u2019s just I thought it would last longer. I don\u2019t know what I want honestly. I want people to act like the world is not all right, but for them it is. Shit, Lori and De La Rocha just got engaged. They should be happy and they are. They\u2019re over the moon in love. Insincere Marguerite and Julia are going over their own wedding plans again and getting all excited themselves. Realistically I know that Rook was nothing to them and they don\u2019t have any reason to be upset over his death. I guess I just wanted someone to feel the same way. Back in the Lady\u2019s realm if one of the Knights was killed in the line of duty we all mourned. Even the Lady did. But here, I am the only one that feels bad about his death. I am the only one that will mourn my fallen brother. I just have to get used to that.<br /> <br /> So, anyway. We all had breakfast. Stasia looked like she\u2019d had a good time and Lori and De La Rocha looked overly pleased with themselves. I\u2019m glad that they all had a good time. I figured that they would, but it\u2019s still nice to see. After we ate I asked Calamity if she wanted to spar. I figured that I\u2019d take my therapist\u2019s advice and get back to a normal routine and sparring is part of that on Tuesdays and Thursdays. So I asked. Calamity for her part was eager to get back into it and we both went upstairs to get changed into sweats. We went outside and began our \u201cdance.\u201d After a little bit Stasia came out to watch and Calamity, within seconds, changed her attacks and parries to something with more flair. I think she was aiming to impress her childhood friend. She was more acrobatic than usual. Despite showing off she was still pretty focused on the fight itself. I left her a couple of reminders and she gave me one or two as well. For my part I went more back to my old style of fighting than I have in a while. I guess I just wanted to make sure that I hadn\u2019t forgotten anything. Rook was the one that taught me to wield a blade, and despite learning a new style from Luna ad Calamity I don\u2019t want to lose what my brother taught me. It kept me alive for years. <br /> <br /> Before I knew it there was talk of going to the beach today. I think there was something said about the Chestnut party tomorrow. We had also made plans to go to L.A and check out the club called the Unseelie Court. In the end I think we all decided on going to the Unseelie Court over Austin\u2019s party. After that though the beach was brought up and we all agreed that it would be fun. Stasia was a little worried that it might be too cold to go to the beach, but we assured her that it was plenty warm out to go to the beach. It is always warm enough to go to the beach here. So, we all piled into the van with our surf boards and headed for the beach.<br /> <br /> I will admit that I did have fun. I enjoyed surfing and watching the others surf as well. I made sure to spend time on the beach with Luna since she didn\u2019t want to get her wings wet. I can understand that. They look rather delicate. The others all seemed to be having a good time as well. Insincere Marguerite was doing her best to show off on the surf board. Balancing in ways that are just not possible for humans. I think everyone was showing off to some extent. After we had tired of surfing we decided to play a game of volleyball. Only this time we didn\u2019t match the \u201cLovers\u201d vs. the \u201cFighters.\u201d We decided to play as a motley and challenge some poor fools that were on the beach to a game. Lori made sure that they knew that she\u2019d be playing in her bikini, which probably enticed quite a few of the guys to come on over. In the end we decimated them. The game was not fair. Insincere Marguerite used her abilities to do things they couldn\u2019t match. I think the others did as well. I do have to admit that I played as well as I could too, which was better than the other team. What can I say, I\u2019ve had a lot of practice at moving fast.<br /> <br /> After the game was over we hung around for a bit longer, but eventually packed up our stuff and headed back to the Dream House. I will admit that going to the beach was a nice distraction from darker thoughts. It only works for so long before something reminds me of Rook, but it was something of a respite anyway. Of course then I feel bad for having fun and he obviously can\u2019t. I guess that I fit better into the Winter Court than I had originally thought. To start it was just because of my connection to ice, but now I\u2019m getting some practice at the whole sorrow thing. In some ways everything that has happened makes me wonder if Rook would have mourned me if he\u2019d succeeded in killing me in the clearing. That and if he\u2019d gotten away from my motely mates. Would he have mourned for me the way I grieve for him? I don\u2019t know. Part of me feels like he would have in some small way. We were brothers for years. It takes more than a couple months of strife to erase that kind of bond. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> Things continue marvelously. Yesterday was wonderful, and today as been good as well. Sex Breakfast was smooth, Gawain made crepes to show off. Stasia seemed to fit in well. She had a list of fae questions. Quite a bit were special protocols and such. I, of course, suggested she not trust the Day Court. Because I am helpful. Juliette, however, did not seem to appreciate it. I suppose she always tries to see the best in people.<br /> <br /> After breakfast, she buttonholed I about the mirror, saying I sent it. I, of course, never confirmed such a thing, but of course did nor directly deny it. She was standing with I against the wall with her arms folded so she was right in my face looking down, and kissed my cheek at the corner of my mouth when I narrowly avoided having to confess. Exactly.<br /> <br /> I spent much of the day relaxing with Julia. Julia and I relaxed while she painted. One of myself reclining and looking very French eighteen century. Then we brushed each other\u2019s hair and she sang to I a bit while brushing mine. Jacob and Luna were watching <i>Firefly</i>, the others were out. <br /> <br /> We talked about wedding stuff. We will each be brides for ourselves, and she will be Maid of Honor for Juliette. I will be whatever Maria decides I am for her part. Gawain is giving away Juliette and Jacob is giving I away. Julia is being given away by her dad. I am unsure again about Maria. Julia has, I think, accepted the decisions about the separate weddings, the idea of the pledge is one pleasing to her. Especially if there is at least a low key ceremony. <br /> <br /> Spirits are high throughout the house. Calamity and Stasia got back from the tour of the city as Gawain got back from the Library. Once Juliette was back too, we talked about some Contracts Gawain found out about. Goblin Contracts. He found several to enhance his skills in dreams, and one that allows spying on a Gentry. This sounds useful to me. It also allows one\u2019s keeper to know where they are, but if Mama Lion is alive I am where she sent me anyway, broadly speaking, so I am sure it would be no issue. Juliette was jittery, so we decided to leave it for now.<br /> <br /> We wound up seeing <i>Crouching Tiger, Hidden Dragon</i> and <i>Johnny Dangerously</i>. There was talk of seeing <i>Blue is the Warmest Color</i>, but it was decided combined with <i>Crouching Tiger</i> it would be a pill. Maria described it as \u2018very European\u201d in a way I did not find flattering. `<br /> <br /> Actually they kept teasing I. Juliette called Cognac \u201cSnooty Bourbon\u201d and they seemed intent on making me talk about getting the goat. I actually got rather aggravated with them. That and Gawain talking about a \u201cRacist side of the bed.\u201d Juliette and Maria were quick to smooth ruffled fur, but it was still aggravating.<br /> <br /> Neither movie was really the sort I liked, so I distracted myself making out with my lovers. The innuendo was going pretty heavy for a movie night\u2026more so than usual. Stasia just watched while the four of us were fooling around. Luna and Jacob tried to ignore us and Calamity was having fun with Gawain and Becky. <br /> <br /> With all the nuptials talk and planning the four of us wanted, even needed, to be together. I had been languidly sampling the kisses of each over the past few hours, finding them to my liking, so was eager. And Julia was doing her foot thing. As we got up it seemed that Stasia was rather riled up, so we elected to take her upstairs with us. She was enthusiastic and eager. Of course. Julia was warm and yielding. Juliette was giving and demanding. Maria was powerful yet submissive. And I was, of course, absolutely perfect, as I should be.<br /> <br /> A night of fire and exploration lead to a morning of sleep. Then it was time for sex breakfast. We discussed the Chestnut Party vs. the Unseelie Court, and I think all of us decided to go to the Court. I confess being slightly pleased to have the excuse.<br /> <br /> We discussed shopping for the club, with Juliette and Julia\u2019s eyes lighting right up, but Calamity suggested Stasia may want to see the beach. Maria is not working today, as she is tomorrow, and so we can shop then and spare her. Besides she wears appropriate clothing most of the time. We changed into our bathing suits and went down; after a jest about Juliette becoming distracted in her room by her girls, she made a point of being down in only ten minutes. <br /> <br /> We began with some surfing; everyone but Julia surfed. My fianc\u00e9e she just sat under the big black beach umbrella looking over her sunglasses at us. There was some excellent surfing, Juliette is getting better at using her wings to catch wind, and did very well. I of course was most impressive, I did a head stand on the board in which I was standing on my own head. Sort of. It was impressive, trust me. <br /> <br /> After that we challenged some of the people on the beach to volleyball, six of them against Juliette, Maria, Gawain, Calamity, Jacob, Luna, and I. Stasia and Julia watched. Julia often over her sunglasses again. The game was\u2026not close. Maria and Gawain had powerful spikes and I, well, obviously showed myself to be a master player. The others did fine too.<br /> <br /> And now we relax before the show. With Movie Night last night and Unseelie Court tomorrow night, it\u2019s our one show we are part of for a bit. I\u2019m filling in with lights, since I was filled in for on Friday. Hoping for a smooth one tonight. But now I must get ready.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXXVII</i><br /> <br /> To be fair, in Stasia\u2019s position I would react pretty much just like that to the girls coming on to me.<br /> <br /> The Contracts Gawain was looking into are in Swords at Dawn, as is the rules for Talecrafting. <br /> <br /> Unfortunate timing for no Calamity, there was a fair amount of RP with she and Stasia on the pier. They talked about how both their lives had taken turns they did not expect, their previous relationship and how it impacted their future, dating and the Motley, stuff like that. <br /> <br /> There were Athletics rolls for the surfing, as well as volleyball. Which they largely aced. Insincere Marguerite with her redlined Athletics tended to roll highest, but as I allowed Strength or Dexterity for volleyball powerhouses like Gawain and De La Rocha gave her a serious run for her money. <br /> <br /> I think that\u2019s everything, but feel free to ask if I missed something. Comments and Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T20:08:29-07:00","id":1061706,"title":"","content":"I take it back, no wonder Stasia's taking this so well. This must be the best week of her life, the lucky so and so","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T20:09:37-07:00","id":1061707,"title":"","content":"And poor Jacob. Life is good for everyone but him and I know from experience how much worse that makes it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T00:08:15-07:00","id":1061742,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it was an unfortunate session to be unable to finish Calamity's journal. Both with her getting the chance to talk one on one with Stasia about things and because I'd talked to Jacob's player a bit about the sparring. I do rather like how Jacob and Calamity's sparring is often the point where they let their respective emotional guard down.<br /> <br /> At this point, I intend to roll the partial journal into the next and cover both sessions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T02:18:07-07:00","id":1061765,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Luna is helping best she can, but even Insincere Marguerite seems unaware of how messed up he is. And yes, Stasia is having a good time of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img item