:[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T15:20:34-07:00","id":1089426,"title":"","content":"Noooooooo, not my metal cinnamon bun! Oh cruel world, this is too much<br /> <br /> I'll miss him, but life is life and it comes before even the best of games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T23:52:45-07:00","id":1089614,"title":"","content":"It's a shame that Gawain's player needs to sacrifice playing in this game. I hope that things are and continue to be going well for them, and that they get some downtime in their future...though sex breakfast may require someone else to take the mantle of Greatest Chef Ever.<br /> <br /> Actually, it does make some sense for Gawain to move elsewhere, however (I don't say 'move on', because that sounds remarkably close to his motley being a phase). By my understanding, those of Dawn tend to wander from freehold to freehold, and tend to be seen as good omens for it. Of course, Gawain going elsewhere won't mean a bad omen, just...well, he's needed elsewhere. Whatever the case, I can't wait to see what kind of sendoff he's given, even if it'll be sad to see him go.<br /> <br /> ...on a side note, with Master Aquatosic's comment, I don't believe Gawain has ever made cinnamon buns (I'm aware of the term, just thinking literally). Seems a bit odd, given his baking prowess, but there you go.<br /> <br /> ...posts should not be written just before slumber. It makes them terribly messy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T00:09:25-07:00","id":1090612,"title":"","content":"We have some general ideas for how to write him out with respect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T13:39:26-07:00","id":1095222,"title":"","content":"Lorelei came face to face with Hunting Hawk. Calamity found Stasia. Jacob faced down Rook. Now it\u2019s Insincere Marguerite\u2019s turn to look her past in the eye.<br /> <br /> Calamity\u2019s player had to miss, but Calamity provides an intermission as we see her and Stasia in Seattle. <i>Night Train</i> fans might recognize a few places from that game.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LXXXII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Okay, so I <u><u>think</u></u> things have taken a turn for the better over the past few days, but I guess we\u2019ll have to wait and see how everything pans out before we endorse that particular diagnosis. Sigh\u2026 maybe I <u><u>am</u></u> reading too many medical books like D says.<br /> <br /> In any case, as things were winding down at Sex Breakfast on Sunday, Jacob mentioned that Molly had told him that Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne was regretting her decision to sever her association with the Dream House\u2026 or at least that she seemed to view her time here fondly. I admit that this piqued my interest\u2026 Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne can really wail on that guitar of hers, and she\u2019s cute, and she was always a real crowd-pleaser back when she was performing for us. Plus, well\u2026 I was never as close with her as I am with some of the other girls, but we did have that one night together last Spring, and I\u2019ve always thought of her as a friend. It\u2019d be nice to have her around again.<br /> <br /> We all agreed that we didn\u2019t want to seem too eager to get her back; we wanted to remind her of how much fun she\u2019d had performing at the Dream House so that she\u2019d make her own decision to return. With that in mind, Marguerite suggested we all head over to the Rose &amp; Thorn, since Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne has been hanging out there a lot recently, and it would give us an excuse to visit with Flores in any case.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, Marguerite had been referring to Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne as her \u201cfavorite Walloon,\u201d which confused Jacob to no end. I took it upon myself to tell him that a Walloon is a French-speaking Belgian\u2026 and then spent the next few minutes wondering how I knew that little tidbit myself. I can only assume that I learned it in High School, though most of my memories of that time are hazy at best\u2026 dimmed by sex, drugs, alcohol, time, and Arcadia.<br /> <br /> In any case, the lot of us (minus Calamity, who was escorting Stasia back to Portland so she could start making preparations to move down here) headed over to the Rose &amp; Thorn for a couple of hours. Flores greeted us all with friendly hugs as soon as she spotted us, and promised to try to make it by the Dream House some time in the next week. As it turns out, Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne <u><u>was</u></u> there\u2026 in fact, she was sitting at a table with Monica, Dominika, and Dark Kimberly. White Maria was also there, but she was sitting off by herself with a strange expression on her face. More on that later.<br /> <br /> The group of us made our way to the Muscle Beach crew\u2019s table, where we were greeted with varying levels of enthusiasm (Monica sarcastically asked who D was, but D laughed it off with everyone else). We had a blast, and mostly let the conversation flow where it would. Dominika spent some time flirting with Jacob and complimenting his sexy accent before D stepped in and warned her \u2013 in a friendly way \u2013 that unlike most of us at the Dream House, Jacob isn\u2019t polyamorous, and is in a very fulfilling relationship with Luna. I think Dominika was a little disappointed, but she took the hint with good grace and toned things down a bit after that.<br /> <br /> The long and the short of it is that Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne is cautiously optimistic about returning to work at the Dream House. She still has misgivings over the way our motley handled the situation with Chalcedony, and I was quick to agree that things had gotten out of hand, and none of us were happy with the results. Marguerite backed me up on this point vehemently, which I think might have mollified Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne a bit further.<br /> <br /> She also asked what had been going on around the Dream House, and I sort of idly held out my left hand to show her my ring. Strange as it seems to me, she hadn\u2019t heard about the engagement yet, and offered up her congratulations in a somewhat stunned tone of voice. Then she cut her eyes over at D, looked back at me, and smirked. \u201cThis doesn\u2019t mean you\u2019re being taken off the menu, right?\u201d she asked with a wink.<br /> <br /> I laughed. \u201cNo, D and I have discussed it, and we\u2019re going to have an open marriage,\u201d I assured her.<br /> <br /> \u201cThen I\u2019m absolutely in favor of the match,\u201d she said with a chuckle, \u201cthough I never thought anybody would be able to tie de la Rocha down. Seriously, though\u2026 congratulations, you two.\u201d She lifted her glass in our direction. I know the two of them have never really gotten along in the past, but they seemed to put that aside as we sat and chatted.<br /> <br /> I think Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne is going to come by the House soon and sign back up. I don\u2019t want to jinx it or anything, but that\u2019s the vibe I get from her. So that\u2019s nice.<br /> <br /> While we were there, I asked Dark Kimberly about White Maria. Oddly, even after that whole \u201cyou should commit suicide\u201d thing, the two of them seem to have settled into a sort of friendship these days. A lot of us have noticed that White Maria hasn\u2019t been by the Dream House much lately, and she used to be our steadiest regular customer. While it wouldn\u2019t be entirely truthful to say that I\u2019d been worried about her, I had noticed her absence, and wondered about it.<br /> <br /> Dark Kimberly said that White Maria had been going through a few things recently. Some of it she didn\u2019t feel was her place to share (and I get that), but what she <u><u>did</u></u> tell us was distressing enough. White Maria\u2019s family is currently visiting from China, and they\u2019ve brought someone with them\u2026 the man they want her to marry. Apparently she comes from a very aristocratic family, and arranged marriages are still a thing among that set. Who knew?<br /> <br /> Well, obviously, White Maria\u2019s not cool with this state of affairs, but she\u2019s afraid of standing up to her family for fear of alienating them. I completely understand that point of view, but I\u2019m afraid she\u2019s going to have to either take a stand or knuckle under, and for my part I\u2019m hoping she does the former. I mean, my upbringing was <u><u>extremely</u></u> strict and traditional (by American standards, at least), but Dad never tried to regulate my romantic life. Well, he disapproved of every boy I ever dated, of course, but I\u2019m given to understand that this is a fairly normal trait among fathers. We never actually got into a shouting match over all of the sex I had in High School either, come to think of it. I used to think that he was just clueless; that he didn\u2019t know what I was doing, but that can\u2019t be right\u2026 he\u2019s always been a remarkably sharp man, and I had a reputation in that town.<br /> <br /> I seem to have wandered from the point. We discussed a few ways in which we might be able to help White Maria, but most of them were either illegal or dangerous (or both). Dark Kimberly suggested that I might be able to seduce her intended in a public way \u2013 apparently having casual sex with a white girl would be shameful enough for White Maria\u2019s family to cancel the wedding \u2013 but I\u2019d rather not get into the habit of using sex to get people in trouble. It seems wrong to me, and though I\u2019d like to help White Maria out, I don\u2019t actually have anything against her nebulous fianc\u00e9.<br /> <br /> I eventually made my way over to her table (Marguerite accompanied me) and spoke with her briefly. I asked after her, telling her that the Last Dance had been a little concerned since she hadn\u2019t been at her usual table for the past few days. She waved it off without explanation, but told us that \u201chopefully\u201d she would be able to return to the Dream House soon. I feel bad for her, but beyond enacting sitcom-worthy plots to foil her family\u2019s marriage plans, I don\u2019t really see what else we can do. I wonder if Calamity knows? She\u2019s closer to White Maria than the rest of us (well, except maybe for Marguerite), and I know she\u2019d want to help\u2026 but considering Calamity\u2019s go-to method of helping her friends, that might not be the best option. I mean, presumably White Maria\u2019s intended is not a member of the Freehold in good standing\u2026<br /> <br /> That\u2019s a problem for another day, though. Things started to wind down as soon as we rejoined the Muscle Beach crew at their table. Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne made some frustrated noises about how Marguerite had successfully seduced White Maria (Marguerite wasn\u2019t exactly being subtle about their relationship while we were talking), but I don\u2019t think there was any real rancor in it. It was getting kind of late by that point, and we still had a show to prepare for, so we headed out soon after.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t actually stick around for much of the show that night; D and I had already made plans. Considering how the evening was scheduled to proceed, I decided to belt out Elton John\u2019s \u201cSaturday Night\u2019s Alright for Fighting\u201d as my lone solo\u2026 and yes, I was aware that it was Sunday, thank you very much. I think it went over well enough, though it wasn\u2019t one of my better performances.<br /> <br /> As soon as I was done for the night, I headed to the wardrobe and borrowed the trashiest outfit I could reasonably be expected to wear to a public place, changed, and met D outside. The two of us hopped on to my honey\u2019s bike and made our way down the coast. We hit a couple of skeezy biker bars that night, and worked together to start fights in every one of them. Of course, I mostly held myself aloof from the actual fighting, preferring to let D handle that side of things.<br /> <br /> She had a blast, I know. If I\u2019m being perfectly honest, I suppose I should admit that I enjoyed the experience too. Oh\u2026 not so much the actual violence itself, but being the object of so many base desires, the cause of so many arguments and collisions\u2026 it was intoxicating, and I\u2019ve always had a hard time resisting that sort of thrill.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t <u><u>think</u></u> anybody was too badly hurt tonight. D knows what she\u2019s doing, and is remarkably good at pulling her punches when she\u2019s being careful. She <u><u>did</u></u> put one guy through a plate-glass window at one point after he grabbed my ass, but other than that I think the worst injuries I saw were cuts and bruises. I never felt obliged to use my healing powers; I was sure her opponents would be able to sleep it off for the most part.<br /> <br /> The Dream House was mostly quiet when we got back. D went up to our room to \u201cprepare\u201d for me (bar fights always get her motor running) while I decided to swing by the wardrobe to return the outfit I\u2019d borrowed. I\u2019m glad I did. Marguerite was in there. And she wasn\u2019t alone.<br /> <br /> Yvette stood there, backing away from Marguerite and pointing a pistol at her. Marguerite had an odd, hungry look on her face, and seemed to be advancing on the other girl.<br /> <br /> I announced myself softly as I walked into the room, and Yvette swung the pistol around to point at me, before jerking it back toward Marguerite. I\u2019m happy to report that I kept my cool during this ordeal. \u201cCalm down,\u201d I said as firmly as I could. \u201cMarguerite, I\u2019m here honey. Come back to me. Yvette, there\u2019s no need for violence. Please put the gun down.\u201d<br /> <br /> Marguerite began to emerge from her fugue state at the sound of my voice. She looked at me, and I saw the woman I love looking out of her eyes instead of a grasping, needy thing. For her part, Yvette seemed surprised that I knew her, but she got over that quickly enough. She didn\u2019t lower the gun. \u201cI\u2019ve waited so long for this,\u201d she said in very good English. \u201cYou don\u2019t know what she did to me\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI do,\u201d I said softly, trying to draw her attention back to myself. \u201cShe\u2019s told me about it. I\u2019m sorry you went through that, Yvette, but that\u2019s not who she is anymore. She\u2019s not a threat to you now.\u201d<br /> <br /> Yvette shook her head. \u201cShe doesn\u2019t have me, but she has you\u2026 and those other girls. It\u2019s all happening again\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s not,\u201d I assured her. \u201cMarguerite doesn\u2019t control me. I\u2019m with her because I <u><u>want</u></u> to be with her. It\u2019s the same with the others. We\u2019re all free\u2026 and so are you. If you want to leave, nobody is going to stop you. But I can\u2019t let you hurt her.\u201d<br /> <br /> Yvette sniffed, but didn\u2019t lower the gun. \u201cShe lets you call her that? Without the adjective?\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cShe does. Look, Yvette, I know this is something you need to work through. You might not believe this, but Marguerite needs to work through it too. I think it would be healthy for both of you if you could talk about this\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Tears sprang up in the corners of our visitor\u2019s eyes. \u201cThis isn\u2019t how it was supposed to be. This isn\u2019t how I imagined it. I\u2019ve\u2026 I\u2019ve never seen her like that\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Marguerite was a wreck. She wasn\u2019t hysterical, but it was easy to see that she was miserable. \u201cI brought you out of Arcadia,\u201d she whispered. \u201cI <u><u>saved</u></u> you. And you left me\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I could tell that Yvette didn\u2019t share this particular view of the situation, but at this point our conversation was interrupted by the sound of approaching footsteps. I know my love\u2019s tread well enough by now to recognize it, and cursed silently in my head. The last thing we needed at that point was D blundering into the situation. She\u2019d see Yvette threatening two women she loves, and her rage would take over, and either she\u2019d kill the poor confused girl or get shot trying.<br /> <br /> \u201cD!\u201d I called out through the door.<br /> <br /> There was a brief pause. \u201cYeah, babe? You okay? I got tired of waiting.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m fine,\u201d I assured her, \u201cand so is Marguerite. She\u2019s in here with me. We have company, but before you open that door, I need you to know that we\u2019re all okay, and we\u2019re dealing with the situation. You got that?\u201d<br /> <br /> D grunted noncommittally, and opened the door. I could see the murder in her eyes.<br /> <br /> \u201cBabe,\u201d I said firmly, dra