br /> \u201cNever doubted it for a second,\u201d I chimed in.<br /> <br /> \u201cGood,\u201d Marguerite replied simply, and then she was gone.<br /> <br /> D, calmer now that we were out of immediate danger, swept me up into her arms and carried me up to our bedroom. I made a quick unromantic detour to deliver the promised note, and then allowed myself to be drawn into my fianc\u00e9e\u2019s arms for the duration of the night. And what a night! Though we were both still concerned over Marguerite, we let our passions run wild, and for a goodly portion of that night there didn\u2019t seem to be room in that bed for anything else. It was good.<br /> <br /> Monday was our lazy day, of course. Most of the drama happened at Sex Breakfast itself, where I had to carefully explain the previous evening\u2019s events to Julia in such a way that she wouldn\u2019t go all crazy with anxiety. Of course, her mind immediately went all insecure and shit, and both D and I had to reassure her multiple times that Marguerite would never leave her. Even in the depths of her misery, she had taken pains to reassure us both on that point. This seemed to calm Julia down a bit, but she was still very clingy when Marguerite eventually joined us.<br /> <br /> Brightstar and Neon were planning to drop by early and spend the afternoon with us before movie night proper started, so as soon as Sex Breakfast was over, I grabbed a shower and started sprucing myself up a bit. I think D and some of the others were a bit amused that I was getting dolled up for an evening of sitting around the house and watching movies, but so what? Whatever is happening between Brightstar and me is fresh and new, and I\u2019m going to give it my best. She deserves nothing less.<br /> <br /> When our guests arrived, it was positively <u><u>cute</u></u><u>.</u> Brightstar was even more excited than I was; she was in some cases <u><u>literally</u></u> bouncing off the walls. We gave the two of them an <u><u>actual</u></u> to