Now, it\u2019s settled and that\u2019s enough of that for tonight. Agreed?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAgreed.\u201d Calamity tipped back her glass and emptied it then lifted the empty to get the waitress\u2019 attention. The woman sauntered over and swapped the pair\u2019s empty glasses for a fresh drinks a moment later with a smile and a flirty wink. As she swayed away Calamity smirked as Stasia eyed her retreating form. She leaned closer to Stasia and glanced over as well. \u201cSo, you just come here for the music do you?\u201d<br /> <br /> Stasia didn\u2019t look away as she sipped her drink. \u201cI never said that, Kat.\u201d <br /> <br /> <br /> The drizzle fell steadily swirling in the faint winter\u2019s breeze and soaking into the clothes to sap away any warmth. It was more insidious fog than rainfall making the wide branches of the tree Anastasia was waiting under useless to keep it at bay. The woman huddled in her coat and rubbed her arms before pushing away from the ineffectual shelter and crossing to where her childhood friend stood as still and almost as pale as the marble statues that dotted the vacant grounds around them.<br /> <br /> \u201cKat?\u201d<br /> <br /> Calamity blinked and turned her head slowly. Rivulets of rainwater dripped from her hair and ran down her face.<br /> <br /> \u201cKat, it\u2019s cold out here. Come on. Let\u2019s go.\u201d<br /> <br /> Calamity looked back to the headstones. \u201cI should have brought flowers.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNext time Kat. We\u2019ll bring flowers next time. Come on.\u201d She reached for the woman\u2019s arm, touching her upper arm gingerly, carful to avoid the shards of glass glistening in the rain. \u201cJeezus girl, you\u2019re cold as ice.\u201d She drew her hand back and reached for the zipper on her coat. \u201cI tried to tell you to bring a coat. This isn\u2019t California you know.\u201d<br /> <br /> Calamity turned and shook her head, reaching to stop Stasia from unfastening her coat. \u201cNo,\u201d she said quietly, \u201cI\u2019ll just ruin it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhatever,\u201d Stasia said as she finished removing the coat and wrapped it around Calamity\u2019s shoulders cautiously, \u201cI can get another coat.\u201d She shivered and rubbed her arms.<br /> <br /> \u201cNow you\u2019re cold,\u201d Calamity frowned and sighed.<br /> <br /> \u201cYes I am.\u201d<br /> <br /> Calamity gave the headstones a final look and then turned and started walking away. \u201cWe should go back to your house and change before we run errands.\u201d<br /> <br /> Stasia turned to follow her and reached to put an arm around her friend. \u201cYeah. We\u2019ll get changed into something dry and then grab some coffee to warm\u2026 fuck...\u201d She hissed and jerked her hand back, bringing a bloody finger to her lips.<br /> <br /> \u201cSorry...\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cWell, that\u2019s the last stop. Now I just have to make sure I\u2019ve got somewhere to move into by the first of the year.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou can stay at the Dream House as long as you need to.\u201d<br /> <br /> Stasia paused and then nodded. \u201cI know and I appreciate it. But I need my own space Kat.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course. I just want to help.\u201d<br /> <br /> Stasia nodded. \u201cRight.\u201d<br /> <br /> The car got quiet for a moment and then Calamity looked up and cocked her head to the side and squeaked out \u201cSo what are we going to do tonight Brain?\u201d<br /> <br /> Stasia shook her head. \u201cSeriously Kat? Of all the things you missed you picked Animaniacs?\u201d<br /> <br /> Calamity shrugged. \u201cThe Internet liked it and it was on Netflix so I checked it out. I ended up binge watching it a couple of months back with Gawain.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh Kat\u2026 You really haven\u2019t changed.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat? It\u2019s funny...\u201d<br /> <br /> Stasia shook her head again and smiled. \u201cSo, I have to take you to Kiki\u2019s while we\u2019re here.\u201d She lifted her finger to cut Calamity off before she could speak. \u201cAnd before you ask, no, they don\u2019t deliver.\u201d<br /> <br /> Calamity smirked. \u201cAlright. So good food?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot really. I mean, it\u2019s not bad but that\u2019s not why we\u2019re going. It\u2019s\u2026 well\u2026 you\u2019ll see.\u201d<br /> <br /> Calamity lifted an eyebrow. \u201cOkay. Well, now you\u2019ve certainly peaked my curiosity. So, are we going to that club you mentioned after?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe Grindhouse? Um\u2026 I\u2019d thought about it. But I wasn\u2019t sure since you\u2019re, well, spiky and all.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cEven if they can\u2019t see the glass people try to avoid the shards unconsciously and I can be quite the careful monster when I want to be.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cKat. You\u2019re a fae not a monster.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m violent and dangerous and I like hurting people. That makes me a monster. But it\u2019s okay because I choose to hunt other monsters.\u201d<br /> <br /> Stasia shook her head. \u201dI think you really do it because you want to protect people. If I believed you were a monster we wouldn\u2019t be here right now.\u201d <br /> <br /> \u201cOkay. Okay. But can we at least agree that monster sounds cooler and more badass than fairy?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cKat!\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Calamity sighed as she watched the horizon shift from black to deep blue. It was clear for a change, the kind of morning she\u2019d looked forward to as a child. She pulled Stasia\u2019s coat tight since her glass had already poked through it the day before and shifted in the cheap plastic patio chair. The rasp of the back door drew her attention. \u201cWhat are you doing up?\u201d<br /> <br /> Stasia smiled and moved to set a pair of steaming mugs on the little table before settling into the matching chair to the one Calamity was in. \u201cWatching the sunrise with you,\u201d she answered, \u201cI\u2019m surprised you didn\u2019t wake me up. You never used to let me sleep through it. I wasn\u2019t sure you still did it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t usually. It just doesn\u2019t feel the same now.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCreature of darkness and all that, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah\u2026 Something like that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou and me both sister.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T13:40:53-07:00","id":1095223,"title":"","content":"<b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> \u2026Okay\u2026went to a maudlin place there. The rest of the day went pretty well. Calamity and Stasia when back to Seattle so Stasia could put some things in order for her move to Santa Monica. They traveled via mirror to make the trip a bit shorter time-wise. After that I told the rest of the motley about my conversation with Molly. She told me about Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne and her possibly wanting to come back to sing at the Dream House. I should have mentioned this when Calamity was still here, but it slipped my mind until Insincere Marguerite got back from dropping them off. The others took it as good news and started making plans to go talk to Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne this afternoon. Our plan was to go to the Rose and Thorn, since she hangs out there a lot, and see if we could talk. So, we all packed into Gawain\u2019s van and headed over. Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne was at a table with a few others, Dark Kimberly, Monica and Dominika. It was mainly Lori that did the talking. She asked Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne if she\u2019d be interested in coming back to work at the Dream House, saying that we missed her and could really use her talent on stage. Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne for her part said that she was interested in the idea of coming back, but wasn\u2019t sure about actually doing it. I think she was still a bit upset about the whole Chalcedony thing. She did say that she would swing by the club soon though, so maybe she will come back to work for us in the future.<br /> <br /> After that talk turned to White Maria. Lori asked where she\u2019d been, since she has been noticeably absent from the club for the past little while. Kimberly said that she\u2019d had some stuff come up and was dealing with it. She didn\u2019t go into details, but it didn\u2019t sound like she was in any trouble or anything. That just opened up a whole different can of worms though. It turns out that Maria is from a noble Chinese family, who can trace their lineage back to Noble families way back when. This becomes a problem for her because her parents have come to the United States and brought a man for their daughter to marry. No input from White Maria about this whole thing mind you, they just decided that this guy would make an acceptable husband because of his own lineage. This whole thing is a little messed up if you ask me. So anyway, her parents are visiting and Maria is rebelling in little ways here and there in such a way that she won\u2019t actually get caught by her parents. She doesn\u2019t have a job here, and relies on them for income, so she doesn\u2019t want to lose that. She also doesn\u2019t want to marry this stranger. Dark Kimberly half-jokingly suggested that Lori seduce the intended groom to make him look \u201cunsuitable\u201d for marriage. I\u2019m not sure if Lori is actually going to act on that suggestion. She did not get a picture of the guy and doesn\u2019t know how to find him so I\u2019m assuming that it\u2019s not a serious idea at the moment.<br /> <br /> Once the conversation with Dark Kimberly was done, Lori, Julia and Insincere Marguerite went to go talk to White Maria. They weren\u2019t actually going to ask about her arranged marriage. I think they were just going to mention that they\u2019d missed her at the club lately. While they were gone Dominika kind of flirted with me about my accent. Apparently she really likes it. I hadn\u2019t really given it much thought. I do remember getting teased for it in High School before I was taken, so I assumed that it just sounded funny. Though I suppose in retrospect I should take anything that happened in High School with a grain of salt. Teenagers tend to tease people about the dumbest things, so they are not necessarily a good judge of what sounds good and what doesn\u2019t. I was flattered that Dominika was flirting with me, but I\u2019m not really good at dealing with stuff like that. I don\u2019t have a lot of experience with it. Fortunately for me De La Rocha came to my rescue. She flat out told Dominika that I was already taken and that Luna and I were not poly. I think the newest addition to our freehold took the hint after that. At least she was still friendly but didn\u2019t flirt as much anymore.<br /> <br /> Once we left the Rose and Thorn conversation turned to our families and our relationships with them. Some people like Julia and Lori have managed to maintain or rekindle that relationship. Others have not. Insincere Marguerite for one was happy to not be connected to her family anymore. She remembers growing up and being proud of her lineage and her looks. Her family is rather racist and Marguerite was growing up into that same mindset. Being taken to Arcadia saved her from that fate, and she admits that she is a better person now than she used to be when she was younger. For my part I have managed to reconnect with my sister but that\u2019s it. I have not even tried to reintroduce myself to my parents for more than one reason. First off is my fetch. He still lives at home with my parents. They don\u2019t know that their son was taken and replaced. They think the lazy little shit is their boy. It would be problematic to return now and try and convince them that I am really their son, when they already have someone that looks like him living in the house. The other problem with the fetch is what he would do if confronted by me. I do not know if my fetch knows what he is or if he\u2019s completely unaware. If he knows or figures out what he is he might cause problems or potentially hurt someone. If Mary\u2019s fetch taught us anything it\u2019s that we need to be really careful when dealing with our doppelgangers.<br /> <br /> The show passed as it normally does, with Lori doing wonderfully on stage. Not that the other dancers weren\u2019t great, but they don\u2019t have special powers that aid in their performance. Anyway, at the bar I had a few visitors. Molly was there, as has become her habit when she is not out with Chalcedony. Tamara was also there. She said that Lowjack had given her the night off to relax. I asked her when the conversation between Maria/De La Rocha and Twitch was going to happen. She said that it would be soon. Part of me wants to witness that. I know I won\u2019t be actually present for the talk. That will just be De La Rocha and him, and maybe one friend each. But I want to see his reaction to meeting Maria. I guess it\u2019s a vindictive part of me that wants to see him be afraid of her. I still haven\u2019t forgiven him for what he did to my brother. That probably makes me petty, but I don\u2019t really care.<br /> <br /> After the show De La Rocha and Lorelei went out to some sleazy bars and started fights. Lori was going to get guys to hit on her or wait until someone was inappropriate, and then De La Rocha would come in and defend her lady love and beat the snot out of the poor sod. I\u2019m assuming that they had fun. They usually do when they do this. Granted, they\u2019ve only done the whole bar hopping/fight thing a couple of times so far, but they\u2019ve always seemed to be in good spirits when they got back. I didn\u2019t see them return tonight, so I guess I\u2019ll just have to ask them tomorrow.<br /> <br /> **** **** **** <br /> <br /> Breakfast was interesting this morning I\u2019ll give it that. Luna came by to join us for our meal. I was glad to see her. Then, before we were even done eating, Lori came out with the news that Yvette was here at the Dream House last night. Apparently, she came through one of the mirrors backstage and came across Insincere Marguerite. She came armed with a pistol and pointed it at her former captor. Lori walked in about then and talked to Insincere Marguerite, who was regressing just a bit to her former self. Then Lori talked to Yvette and eventually got the French girl to put the gun down. They talked. Lori tried to explain to our guest that Marguerite had changed since escaping Arcadia, and that she was with Insincere Marguerite of her own free will. I don\u2019t know how much of what Lori said was believed by Yvette, but she tried. De La Rocha also came in on this little scene. She did her best to console Marguerite, who was on the floor crying her eyes out. It seems everyone was rather upset. Yvette for her part apparently seemed concerned that Insincere Marguerite was so upset. I guess she didn\u2019t expect her former captor to break down in front of her. Lori also told Yvette that she was free to visit, but asked if she would please call first and let us know that she was coming. I believe Lori was thinking of Calamity and what could be a less than positive reception should Yvette show up unannounced again.<br /> <br /> I was not happy to hear that Yvette had gotten into the house again and had aimed a gun at my motley mates. I knew that we had not replaced the mirrors backstage. The cost would have been prohibitively high from what I understand, so we elected to leave them there and just keep an eye out. That didn\u2019t exactly go to plan last night. Yvette managed to get in, armed, and confront Insincere Marguerite. The others were about as pleased about the whole thing as I was, but we remained calm and planned to talk to Yvette the next time she came by. Julia for her part was the most upset about the whole situation. I think she thought that Insincere Marguerite was going to leave her and go back to Yvette since they\u2019d talked and will probably talk again. Marguerite and Lori both reassured the artist that no one was leaving anyone, and that Marguerite still loved Julia. <br /> <br /> Once that was done, I told Luna about the fight with the Thorn Dragon. After making sure that I was okay, she was happy to hear all about it. She was genuinely interested in the fight and expressed an interest in joining us the next time that we went on a hunt in the Hedge. I said sure. I would love to go hunting with my Luna. Going hunting with both Luna and Calamity would be great. Two of the best fighters I know watching my back. It would just be like old times with Rook when we hunted in the Hedge or in the Lady\u2019s realm. I remember one time Rook and I had a break and decided to blow off some steam and go hunting. We went into the Hedge to do so because the quarry is always more interesting there. We came across something that resembled a bear. It was a bit smaller than a brown bear, which was probably good because those things can get really big. Rook and I tracked it and followed it to just outside its lair. We checked to make sure it wasn\u2019t a female before we attacked it. If it had been a female guarding her young it would have been possibly more relentless a fighter and we wanted the option to back off if we couldn\u2019t take it down. Turns out that it wasn\u2019t that bad a fight. It was certainly dangerous, but we both made it out intact and not too badly wounded. We brought the bear back to the Lady\u2019s realm to skin it and preserve the meat. We drew lots and Rook won, so he got the pelt. We shared the meat though. It was pretty good.<br /> <br /> After all of that we discussed movie night and what we were going to watch and what we were going to do for dinner. Neon and Brightstar came over this afternoon, which is one reason why we decided to go out to eat. The other reason was that we hadn\u2019t done it in a while. The only downside was that Julia revisited her fears that Insincere Marguerite would leave her because Yvette is back. She was assured that this was not the case, but was still rather clingy with Marguerite throughout the day. Julia also admitted that when she was younger she had been somewhat self-destructive. She had fantasies about hurting herself, but she never acted on them. Lori confided that she was kind of self-destructive in her own way. She experimented with alcohol and drugs as well as being promiscuous. I had bouts of depression when I was younger. I guess it came from leaving my home behind and having to start over in a new place. I had the support of my parents and my sister, so I knew I wasn\u2019t alone. I don\u2019t think I\u2019ve ever had self-destructive tendencies though. <br /> <br /> For dinner we eventually decided on going to a seafood place called Duke\u2019s. It was very fancy. A lot fancier than I\u2019d originally been thinking we\u2019d do. My suggestion had been for Indian take out, but no one else seemed interested in that idea. Everyone latched onto the seafood idea though and we all decided on the place. Lori offered to cover the meal once we were there. It was pretty good. I got tilapia. I don\u2019t know if I\u2019d ever had it before, but it was delicious.<br /> <br /> We ended up deciding on two Christmas films due to the upcoming holiday, A Christmas Story and Christmas Vacation. They are both very popular movies and funny. I saw them both when I was still living in Russia. Tonight was the first time I\u2019d seen Christmas Vacation in English though. A Christmas Story I\u2019ve seen since we moved to the United States. Everyone else seemed to be enjoying the movies as well. Brightstar mainly stayed close to Lori, and later they went off together. Neon was enjoying herself with Julia, Insincere Marguerite and De La Rocha. She seemed a bit shy at first, but the threesome soon won her over. After the movies were over we all split up and went our separate ways. Which brings me to the present and my little bout of insomnia. Luna is asleep next to me. I love watching her sleep. Her wings twitch when she dreams. It\u2019s so cute. But I\u2019d never say that out loud. It would just embarrass her and she would eviscerate me. Well, not really. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> Last night, after the show, I saw Yvette again.<br /> <br /> Julia and Desiree had gone upstairs to enjoy each other\u2019s company, and I was due to join them. I had made one last stop to say goodnight to the puppets when Yvette stepped out of the shadows with a pistol. I was not prepared for this.<br /> <br /> I clearly recall putting my hands up, but gazing on her I felt a rather primal hunger. A feeling she was mine. It was not sexual lust, per se, more a desire to possess. It was rather disconcerting, honestly. It felt wrong that she did not belong to me, that she had\u2026escaped. But the memories are fuzzy. What I clearly remember is her constantly talking, accusing and apologizing in turn, saying she hated I, then Juliette coming out of nowhere. I had forgotten she had gone out with Maria rather than just going to bed. She was trying to talk Yvette down, and Yvette was swinging back and forth between pointing the pistol at she and I.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t remember the conversation. Yvette was saying awful, evil true things about I. Juliette wore her down though, and eventually Yvette collapsed into a sobbing heap, bemoaning her failure. She dropped the gun. Juliette held her, then Maria came in. That or Maria came in before, I don\u2019t remember. Maria held I\u2026well\u2026best as she could, I was losing cohesion due to being upset I think, but built up more and more rage as Yvette kept saying I was an evil monster who had to be stopped. Juliette had to send her away eventually, and Maria lowered I to the floor and left.<br /> <br /> Yvette eventually slipped away herself, crawling through a mirror. Juliette asked her to come back but while she was\u2026noncommittal, she did not reject it. She almost left the safety off on her gun, but I did say something\u2026I remembered her flicking it off vividly. Maria returned. Then Juliette held I. By the time this was done, I was not in the mood for what awaited in my room. So I hid in the vents, and Juliette agreed to give them a note.<br /> <br /> I think that is how it went. I was terribly addled. Sort of a blur. Not exactly sure when Maria left, for instance.<br /> <br /> Yvette really hates I. I was so afraid it was true and it is. I don\u2019t know what I can do now. How can I just leave this? How can I just let it, just wait for her to return? I feel a need to talk to her that eats at I, even now. Even with how wonderful a time I had tonight I keep thinking about her. I need to resolve this. I feel like I am on fire. I need to deal with this.<br /> <br /> Julia of course fears I will replace her with Yvette. This is not the case. I promised her my hand, and she will have it. I want to marry her. I mean, I may want to be with Yvette too, if it turns out right, we have such history but no, Julia will not lose I. I just need to convince Julia however I feel about Yvette Julia is first in my heart. But she has been clingy all day. Clingy even as Julia goes. I don\u2019t know what I can do to convince her I won\u2019t leave her. Maybe should talk to Juliette.<br /> <br /> Other things, well, we dropped by Rose &amp; Thorn, and spoke to Flores, but also Marie H\u00e9l\u00e8ne. She had wanted to come back, but was torn because of how things with Chalcedony went. Juliette and I managed to bring her around. And she and Maria had some banter. That Walloon certainly has swagger and pride. She has never turned her attention on I. I feel somewhat relieved at that.<br /> <br /> Also, discovered White Maria is not angry with us. She has some problem Dark Kimberly did not reveal, but also that her parents have come to the area with a young man they want her to marry. She is descended from aristocracy apparently, and only marries \u201cworthy\u201d suitors. Sounds familiar. She does not want to be owned by a man (or woman\u2026usually), but family honor, and a desire to not to lose her allowance, has lead her to apparently accept it. She has not been to the Dream House because apparently such \u201cillicit\u201d places would be bad if caught in. So like the Day Court. But despite following her personal honor, she has thrown herself into some risqu\u00e9 situations, like letting herself be bedded by Flores. She does not want to try to be caught, but it is almost like she wants to be. Which she does? We discussed a number of options, from robbing her parents to scare them into leaving, to having Juliette be caught seducing her young man. We will discuss it further.<br /> <br /> Juliette and I did speak to her briefly. She was polite. Also Dominika flirted with Jacob. It was adorable. She and Monica were there, and Maria spent part of our conversation catching up with those two.<br /> <br /> Well we got back, and there was a show, and Juliette and Maria slipped out, and then I was confronted by Yvette. And what I feared more than being dragged to Arcadia came true.<br /> <br /> The next morning, Julia absolutely clung to I. She and Desiree did not notice I was missing for a few hours. Admittedly, they are both very distracting women. Still, she stayed with I, and needed, and still needs, constant reassurance.<br /> <br /> Neon and Brightstar came over, and that was a good distraction. Juliette was of course very focused on Brightstar and their burgeoning romance. But she did not ignore I, of course. We four stayed with them, Jacob, Luna (who had come back after the weekend) and Gawain busied themselves with whatever they do.<br /> <br /> That night, we watched The Christmas Story and National Lampoon\u2019s Christmas Vacation. Neither were quite my taste. The former particularly. I don\u2019t tend to like stories about bullying anyway. Or a fascination with guns. Especially having had a gun pointed at I the night before.<br /> <br /> As things wound down, Juliette and Brightstar found themselves cuddling, and Neon found herself in Maria\u2019s lap with her fingers in my mouth and Julia stroking her neck. Curiously, she attempted to get Juliette and Brightstar out of the room before giving in to the irresistible, but Maria forestalled that by kissing her and she just sort of melted into her. Once she was rather thoroughly shivering and moaning, Juliette and Brightstar left us, and we soon found ourselves in my room, where we found ourselves turning on Neon\u2019s lightshow several times of the course of the night.<br /> <br /> Poor girl collapsed of exhaustion, eventually. I don\u2019t think she had experienced anything like that. Julia and I cuddled a bit, then, ceding one side to Neon and Maria. Wonderful and surprisingly intense as that was (Neon\u2019s emotions rage like wildfires when she finally unleashes them) I really want to sleep in the vents again, but I think Julia will have a meltdown if she wakes and I am gone. I\u2019d prefer Neon not have to deal with that, nor Julia, honestly, so I stay.<br /> <br /> I hope Yvette contacts us soon. Even after the wild intense night with Neon, I still have the heavy ball in the pit of my stomach. This waiting must end.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXXXII</i><br /> <br /> Okay, what is there to add.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite did regress somewhat when faced with Yvette. Lorelei snapped her back with those sledgehammer socials she has. The encounter itself was RP\u2019d, beyond that. And yes, perhaps, I enjoyed complicating matters with De La Rocha.<br /> <br /> Lorelei\u2019s player actually did research and picked a real restaurant in the area. Admittedly ex post faco, but still.<br /> <br /> That is about it, but Comments and Questions are welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T01:25:41-07:00","id":1099060,"title":"","content":"I love that phrase, &quot;sledgehammer socials&quot;. Entirely appropriate for Lorelei, and her greatest weapon, but still hilarious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T12:33:12-07:00","id":1099246,"title":"","content":"Yeah, most of the games have someone who can talk nearly anyone into nearly anything (Lorelei here, Natalie Knight in Geist or Clytemnestra in Demon) and they are as effective in social contests as the combat ones are in combat ones. Calamity and Insincere Marguerite have some ability in the social area, just not as much as Lori.<br /> <br /> I think Sledgehammer is an apt visual, though not to imply she can't be subtle. (one of her strengths; in this game, Calamity can only really do blunt force of personality, and Insincere Marguerite only does subtle, but Lori can do both)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T13:48:57-07:00","id":1100206,"title":"","content":"Calamity returns, and things settle in. A Motley member is freed from a troublesome oath, and a very old mystery is cleared up. But confrontations are on the horizons for De La Rocha and Insincere Marguerite.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LXXXIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> So, this has been an eventful day and a half. And it doesn\u2019t look like things are going to slow down much by this weekend, either.<br /> <br /> I woke up yesterday morning to find Brightstar gazing at me and smiling. I swear that girl has more energy than anyone else I\u2019ve ever met! I could have lain there with her for hours, but the faint smell of sizzling bacon was drifting up from the kitchen, so the two of us stretched, threw on some clothes, and went downstairs to join the others for Sex Breakfast.<br /> <br /> Neon seems to have enjoyed herself in the company of my three lovers, and there was much teasing of her from all sides. This included a few gentle ribbings from yours truly, though I also made sure to favor her with more than a few smoldering glances, too. In truth, I probably made the poor girl a little uncomfortable, which is too bad\u2026 but I think I also managed to convey my interest fairly effectively. When she and Brightstar left a short time later, the cheerful girl was enthusiastically urging her friend to \u201cgo for it.\u201d<br /> <br /> Oh, Calamity and Stasia had returned by this point, having begun the process of relocating Stasia from Seattle to the greater Malibu-Santa Monica area. They seem to have enjoyed the trip, though Calamity was obviously a little mystified by her old friend\u2019s taste in entertainment. I don\u2019t claim to understand everything they said\u2026 something about a band singing about being the love slaves of the guy who founded Wendy\u2019s. Probably <u><u>not</u></u> a number we need to perform at the Dream House.<br /> <br /> Jacob\u2019s birthday is Sunday, and we started talking about what he\u2019d like to do to celebrate the big event (Strip Twister didn\u2019t seem like his cup of tea). After a brief discussion, he decided that he\u2019d like to go out camping\u2026 with the whole motley along. Well, Sunday is the last church service before Christmas, and Dad would never forgive me if I missed my solo carol, so I was prepared to bow out and offer my regrets, but it turned out that it wasn\u2019t necessary in the end. Sunday is also the Solstice, so Boss Lowjack will be taking the reins of power from Queen Charlotte, so Jacob suggested that we head out on Friday, spend the night in the woods, and return on Saturday. Since Annika headlines on Friday nights, the House can probably spare me (grrr).<br /> <br /> Well, naturally there was some good-natured grumbling from those among the motley who feel that nature is best viewed through a window, but everyone agreed in the end (particularly when copious amounts of alcohol and cannabis were mentioned). While Jacob \u2013 with a straight face \u2013 informed Marguerite that she should probably bring at least one pair of shoes along, I took great delight in offering to take Julia shopping for a nice pair of khaki shorts.<br /> <br /> Well, yes\u2026 because I have to live up to expectations, of course I started talking about going shopping for camping outfits. What? I have to plan for these sorts of things, you know\u2026 any outfit I buy has to be specially altered before I can even try it on, so if I know I\u2019m going to need a certain type of clothes, I try my best to take care of the shopping early. Then I glanced at D \u2013 who was wearing nothing but one of Julia\u2019s long t-shirts \u2013 and asked what she had planned for the afternoon.<br /> <br /> She shrugged. \u201cDunno, babe. I was thinking I\u2019d just lounge around the house and glory in the fact that I don\u2019t have to put on pants today.\u201d<br /> <br /> So I decided to stay in after all. And no, we didn\u2019t spend all afternoon in a single long bout of debauched lovemaking\u2026 we just hung out and enjoyed each other\u2019s company for the most part. There were kisses and snuggles thrown in there, of course, but despite what some people might think of me, I don\u2019t spend every free moment having sex.<br /> <br /> Our pleasant afternoon together was interrupted when D got a phone call. She glanced at the caller ID, and her face fell. \u201cSorry babe, I have to take this privately,\u201d she said, giving my shoulder a squeeze. \u201cBe right back.\u201d<br /> <br /> A few minutes later she <u>was</u> back. \u201cWhat\u2019s up?\u201d I asked, anxious.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m meeting with Twitch at 3:00 on Thursday,\u201d she said simply. \u201cYou and one other member of the motley will be able to search him for weapons first. They\u2019re going to pat me down too\u2026 mostly as a formality so that he won\u2019t be singled out, I think. We\u2019ll be put in a room with two doors together. You guys will be able to look in on the meeting, but you won\u2019t be able to hear what we say. His people will be in the same situation.\u201d<br /> <br /> I reached out to pull her into an embrace. \u201cThis is a good thing, right?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cWe both need to get past it. But\u2026\u201d she trailed off.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat\u201d I asked gently.<br /> <br /> She sighed. \u201cI have to wear my scrubs. And for at least part of the meeting, I\u2019m going to have to put on a mask. He needs to see that the person he\u2019s talking to is really the \u2018Maria\u2019 he\u2019s been so afraid of for so long.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou gonna be okay with that?\u201d I asked, and then mentally smacked myself. I\u2019d only meant to ask if she was comfortable with revealing that much of who she used to be, but I realized a split-second after I\u2019d said it that my question could be interpreted as doubt on my part that she could rein her darker impulses in.<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cI can handle it, Lori,\u201d she said with a sad smile.<br /> <br /> \u201cI know,\u201d I said, backpedaling, \u201cI shouldn\u2019t have even asked that\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, it\u2019s cool,\u201d D said, kissing my forehead. \u201cI don\u2019t want us to have the kind of relationship where we can\u2019t ask each other those sorts of questions. I think that\u2019s part of what went wrong between me and Spidertoes.\u201d<br /> <br /> I kissed her. \u201cIt\u2019s not that I felt I <u><u>couldn\u2019t</u></u> ask you,\u201d I assured her, \u201cit\u2019s that I realized I didn\u2019t <u><u>need</u></u> to. I know you can handle it. You\u2019re Maria de la Rocha. You\u2019re amazing. You can handle <u><u>anything</u></u>.\u201d<br /> <br /> She gave me that adorable bashful smile she hides from everyone else, and then returned the kiss with a muttered \u201cthanks.\u201d We sort of relaxed for about an hour after that, watching something pointless on the TV as I settled comfortably into the crook of her arm.<br /> <br /> Eventually, though, I had to get up and start getting ready for my dinner date with Joan and Andromeda. After making <u><u>sure</u></u> that D would be okay on her own for a while, I got spruced up, put on one of my slinkiest dresses, adjusted my coiffure, and motored over to their place.<br /> <br /> Joan met me at the door. \u201cWelcome, Lorelei,\u201d she said softly as she ushered me into the living room. \u201cAlas, our VCR is still in the shop. We called the repairman earlier today, but he is as yet uncertain how much longer it might take to effect repairs.\u201d<br /> <br /> I had to chuckle at the complexity of her story. \u201cWhatever shall we do to pass the time?\u201d I asked. What can I say? I know my role in this little fantasy. In answer, Joan pulled me into a fierce embrace and kissed me passionately. So I guess that answered that.<br /> <br /> Something occurred to me as we were sitting down to dinner. I thought of something that might help to protect D a little bit during her meeting with Twitch, and I decided to go for it. \u201cRebecca,\u201d I asked hesitantly.<br /> <br /> \u201cYes?\u201d she turned to look at me expectantly.<br /> <br /> \u201cI need to ask you for a favor. I\u2019m not sure if it\u2019s even possible, but if it is, you\u2019d be helping me and de la Rocha out a lot.\u201d<br /> <br /> She gave me a dazzling smile. \u201cYou know I\u2019ll help you however I can, Juliette,\u201d she said in answer.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell\u2026 a couple of weeks ago you were talking with D about a portable medical scanner you were developing. I was wondering if you have a working prototype yet.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cYes,\u201d she said slowly, \u201cwhy?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI was wondering if I could borrow it for an hour or so\u2026 say, on Thursday, around three o\u2019clock?\u201d<br /> <br /> Joan\u2019s eyes narrowed a bit. \u201cThat is\u2026 a remarkably specific request,\u201d she noted.<br /> <br /> \u201cD\u2019s going to meet with\u2026 someone,\u201d I said, not knowing how much they knew about the situation. \u201cIt could be intense. We\u2019re going to be allowed to search the other party before the meeting, and I confess I\u2019d feel a lot better if I could be <u><u>certain</u></u> he wasn\u2019t concealing a weapon.\u201d<br /> <br /> Andromeda put her hand on mine. \u201cOf course you can borrow it,\u201d she said at once. \u201cIt\u2019s pretty big, but I\u2019ll show you how to break it down so that it\u2019ll fit in the trunk of a car, and how to reassemble it when you get there. This isn\u2019t the machine\u2019s intended use, but it should work. The only snag might come if the subject tries to smuggle in a weapon made of organic materials\u2026 like a knife made out of human bone or something.\u201d<br /> <br /> Well, that seemed pretty unlikely to me \u2013 if anything I\u2019d bet on Twitch sneaking in a syringe of something deadly \u2013 so I thanked her for her generosity and gave her a big kiss. Things got pretty mushy from that point, but we <u><u>did</u></u> manage to finish our meal before making our way to their bedroom. I really enjoy the time I spend with those two, and I can\u2019t tell you how glad I am that they\u2019ve decided to include me in their lives. And, well\u2026 I guess it\u2019s not really accurate to call the relationship I share with them \u201cno strings attached,\u201d but the strings in question are those of friendship and affection without the limitation of jealousy, so they\u2019re strings I\u2019m happy to accept.<br /> <br /> Anyone who only knows Joan casually would never believe how warm and gentle she can be in intimate situations. Take this morning, for instance. When I dragged the two of them with me to Sex Breakfast, they were far from the only paramours in evidence, and talk soon turned raunchy as per usual. Dark Kimberly \u2013 who had spent the night in the company of Marguerite, Julia, and D \u2013 was happily decrying the benefits of being a slut, and looked to Joan and Andromeda for support.<br /> <br /> Joan looked affronted. \u201cIt is not like that,\u201d she said solemnly. \u201cThe time we spend with Lorelei is\u2026 it is very loving. It is not something sordid. It is beautiful.\u201d<br /> <br /> Dark Kimberly quirked an eyebrow as she looked me up and down, but confined her comments to \u201cI bet it is.\u201d<br /> <br /> Desiree was also present, having spent the night with Calamity and Gawain. In fact, the three of them had something of an announcement, once the rest of our guests had departed\u2026 Desiree has been cured! She no longer feels compelled to be \u2018owned\u2019 by someone she sees as more capable than herself, and seems ready to start making her own decisions at last. I couldn\u2019t be happier\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026or so you\u2019d think.<br /> <br /> Don\u2019t get me wrong; I\u2019m thrilled that Desiree\u2019s doing better and feeling more independent. And I was <u><u>beyond</u></u> thrilled that she wanted to dissolve her \u2018arrangement\u2019 with Marguerite. But seeing her there\u2026 in that company\u2026 it sparked something. Some lingering memory or nagging doubt brought up when I was re-reading my old diary entries a few days ago surged forward, and I knew that I had to talk to her.<br /> <br /> After most of our guests had left, but before she went to speak with Marguerite, I asked Desiree if I could speak with her privately. She agreed readily enough, with perhaps a bit more hesitation than I\u2019m used to seeing in her.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat can I do for you, Lori?\u201d she asked once she and I were sequestered in my room.<br /> <br /> \u201cI want to ask you something,\u201d I said bluntly. \u201cBut before I do\u2026 Desiree, I want you to know that I\u2019m not accusing you of anything, and I\u2019m certainly not blaming you for anything, okay? You\u2019re my friend. I care about you. The two of us are finally on good terms again, and I don\u2019t want to do anything to screw that up, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> She quirked an eyebrow. \u201cNoted. Now what\u2019s this all about?\u201d<br /> <br /> I sighed. \u201cYou\u2026 you remember pretty much everything that you did while you were acting under Hollywood\u2019s programming, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded slowly. \u201cYes,\u201d she allowed.<br /> <br /> She didn\u2019t look away, but she looked sad and wary. It upset me. \u201cWell,\u201d I went on, \u201cyou may remember that Dark Kimberly was shot at the Rose &amp; Thorn during that time\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> She lowered her eyelids and sighed. \u201cAre you trying to ask me something, Lori?\u201d she said wearily.<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cDid you do it?\u201d I asked after a moment.<br /> <br /> She didn\u2019t meet my eyes. \u201cWould it matter if I did?\u201d she asked quietly.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt would,\u201d I said, just as quietly, \u201cbut let me explain. I know that if you <u><u>did</u></u> shoot Kimberly, you did it because of their programming. You had no choice, and I don\u2019t blame you for it. I know you\u2019d never do something like that now. But\u2026 if you <u><u>didn\u2019t</u></u> shoot her, then the culprit is still out there, and we\u2019re all still at risk.\u201d<br /> <br /> She looked at me helplessly. It was nearly answer enough.<br /> <br /> I held out my hands and took hers. \u201cDesiree,\u201d I said, \u201cI know why you\u2019d want to keep something like that a secret. When you came out of the programming, you were desperately trying to convince the Freehold that you weren\u2019t a threat. I wouldn\u2019t have brought it up either, if I\u2019d been in your place. And\u2026 I know you\u2019re still struggling to earn the Freehold\u2019s trust. And you [u]<u>are</u>/u] my friend. So\u2026 I won\u2019t tell the Courts, if that\u2019s what you want.\u201d<br /> <br /> She looked up, a flicker of disbelief in her eyes. \u201cI have your word on that?\u201d she asked. I nodded. She didn\u2019t try to make it a Pledge. I guess she knew that with me, she didn\u2019t <u><u>have</u></u> to.<br /> <br /> \u201cHollywood\u2026 didn\u2019t know how best to use my abilities. They were clumsy. They wanted to do something publicly to demoralize the Freehold, and they thought an assassination would do the trick. They didn\u2019t want me to take out any of the monarchs\u2026 just someone who was well-liked by pretty much everyone. The two most likely targets were Kimberly and Flores. I\u2026 even under hypnosis, I couldn\u2019t bring myself to hurt Flores. She\u2019s too important to me. So it was Kimberly. But I\u2019m not good at violent public displays, so I botched it and only grazed her.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cThank you for trusting me with this, Desiree,\u201d I said after a moment. \u201cI\u2019m sorry I made you relive it, but I think it\u2019s important. Now\u2026 I think you have an appointment to keep with Marguerite.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. She still seemed a little subdued, but I\u2019m hoping that will pass with time. I\u2019ll keep her secret unless she gives me a damned good reason not to\u2026 I mean, it\u2019s not like any of it was really her fault, right?<br /> <br /> D had left for work, and I still had a few hours before I needed to worry about getting ready for the show, so I decided to spend my time reading. I didn\u2019t actually have time to absorb much, however, as my phone rang a short time later. It was an international call. It was Yvette.<br /> <br /> I spoke earnestly with her for a little while. She was wary, but I thought I detected a bit of steel beneath her nerves\u2026 the determination that the situation between her and Marguerite needs to be resolved one way or another. She wanted to set up a meeting, but was very cautious about speaking with Marguerite here at the Dream House\u2026 in her \u2018lair,\u2019 if you will. I assured her (again) that the Dream House is a guaranteed safe haven for <u><u>all</u></u> changelings, and that no one would try to stop her from leaving at any point.<br /> <br /> In the end, I decided to have her come by on Saturday afternoon. We sort of tentatively set the meeting for around 3:00pm, which should give us ample time to get back from our camping trip with Jacob and still be vaguely prepared for the show that night. I told her that I\u2019d have to run it by the others first, but that I would call or text shortly to let her know.<br /> <br /> I met Desiree on the stairs on the way up to the attic to talk to Julia and Marguerite. She looked a little rattled, but managed to let me know in a shaky voice that she was no longer bound to Marguerite. I gave her a hug to let her know how happy that made me, and she returned it with thanks\u2026 but also stated that she really needed to get out of the House; to get away from Marguerite until her current anxiety passed. I get that, and I\u2019m sure Gloria will be able to help her through her current circumstances.<br /> <br /> Marguerite was posing and Julia was painting when I got to the attic, and I regretfully had to ask if they could take a break so that I could speak with them. Marguerite was cautiously optimistic when I mentioned that Yvette wanted to talk, though her face fell when I mentioned that she needed closure before she could move on. I get the impression that Yvette wants to put this whole issue to bed so that she can stop obsessing over Marguerite, while Marguerite wants to rekindle what the two of them used to have. Frankly, I\u2019m not sure what to hope for myself.<br /> <br /> I tried to prepare Marguerite for the possibility that things wouldn\u2019t turn out like she hopes. She wasn\u2019t happy about it, but accepted that this might be the way the wind is blowing. Now, I\u2019ve never been in that sort of a relationship before \u2013 unless you count my time as the Empress\u2019 pet, and I <u><u>don\u2019t</u></u> \u2013 but it seems to me that Marguerite\u2019s ideal solution probably isn\u2019t in the cards. I just can\u2019t see Yvette coming back to her and everything being hunky-dory between them; it doesn\u2019t make sense from the other girl\u2019s perspective. If they can make a clean break \u2013 preferably an amicable one \u2013 it might be best for everyone concerned.<br /> <br /> Including Julia. Maybe <u><u>especially</u></u> Julia. Now don\u2019t get me wrong; I don\u2019t think Marguerite would actually set Julia aside for anything, but the taller girl\u2019s anxiety is hard to watch sometimes. She was almost in tears over the situation; a part of her was convinced that Marguerite would get back together with Yvette and run away with her in a fit of passion. Marguerite tried to assuage her fears, but wasn\u2019t really getting anywhere. I took Julia\u2019s hands in my own.<br /> <br /> \u201cJulia,\u201d I said firmly, \u201cthink about how you feel right now.\u201d<br /> <br /> She sniffed. \u201cI don\u2019t know what you mean,\u201d she said softly.<br /> <br /> \u201cThink about Marguerite,\u201d I replied. \u201cThink about how she makes you feel. Now\u2026 can you imagine <u><u>anything</u></u> that would make you leave her?\u201d<br /> <br /> She sniffed again and shook her head.<br /> <br /> I smiled. \u201cThen, honey, you have to have a little faith\u2026 because Marguerite feels the same way about you.\u201d<br /> <br /> She glanced over at her true love, who threw her a smile and nodded helpfully. I think Julia felt a bit better after that.<br /> <br /> The three of us went downstairs to check out the camping equipment Jacob and Luna had picked up for this weekend\u2019s excursion. It looks like for the most part it\u2019ll be two people to a tent (I don\u2019t really need to write out the pairs, do I?), and everyone gets their own sleeping bag\u2026 though I\u2019m pretty sure they got the kind that can zip together. I made a show of looking over all of the supplies, but who am I kidding? Jacob and Luna know more about that sort of thing than I ever will, so I\u2019m sure they got everything we could possibly need.<br /> <br /> After a brief discussion with the rest of the motley, I called Yvette back to let her know that Saturday at 3:00 would work fine, and she sort of nervously agreed to meet us then. I hope this turns out well.<br /> <br /> Marguerite cornered me after the call to thank me for setting up the meeting. She also wanted to request that I spend the evening with her, Julia, and D\u2026 which of course was what I\u2019d planned to do anyway, so I was happy to acquiesce. The last few evenings have been busy, and it\u2019ll be nice to spend some time with my regular girlfriends again.<br /> <br /> After that, I decided to seek out Julia for a little one-on-one chat. I knew that, despite our earlier talk, she was still feeling a bit insecure about Marguerite\u2019s feelings, and something had occurred to me that I thought might make her feel a little better. Once the two of us were alone, I pointed out to her that Marguerite has been calling Yvette by her name for the last few days\u2026 at least since Monday night. She used to refer to the other girl as \u201cDearest\u201d all the time; it was a long time before any of us even <u><u>knew</u></u> her proper name. That revelation seemed to make Julia feel a bit better, so I\u2019m glad it occurred to me to share it.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Jacob and Calamity have started one of their little sparring matches out in the yard. It was amusing to watch Stasia yelp and cover her eyes every few seconds as one of them seemed to score a telling hit against the other, but the novelty wore off quickly, and I decided to record these events instead. But D should be getting off work any time, and I need to get ready for tonight\u2019s show, so I guess I\u2019ll put the diary away for now. Hopefully by the next time I write my love will be a little more at peace with her past\u2026 and Twitch will too. I really want to believe that their meeting will go well. But I\u2019ll be ready for anything, just in case.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Today started early, just like all Tuesdays. Insincere Marguerite went to go get Calamity and Stasia from Seattle, and brought them back. I then got together with Calamity and we went to our usual therapy sessions. I wasn\u2019t particularly in the mood to go to therapy today, like last time, but figured that Calamity wouldn\u2019t take no for an answer and would just wake me up and make me go. So, we went. I still didn\u2019t talk much about Rook. It\u2019s been almost two weeks since he died, but it still feels like yesterday to me. So instead I talked about other stuff, including the fight with the Hedge Dragon. I figured that Sullivan would see that as a good thing. Getting out with a motley mate to do activities together. He seemed to think that it was a bit reckless though, even though I assured him that Calamity and I were fine and had not been in serious danger. I tried to reassure him that I was well prepared to go hunting in the Hedge without stressing the fact that I\u2019m good at killing things. Making note of one\u2019s violent talents is probably not a good thing to do with a shrink, so I downplayed that bit. He still seemed to think that it had been reckless of us to go hunting without a larger group. In the end we had to agree to disagree. I don\u2019t think he quite realized just how much practice I\u2019ve had at fighting and killing. I\u2019ve been doing it my entire adult life, and part of my teen years. Conflict has been a constant companion for a long time. If I\u2019d been in any real danger from the Dragon I would have backed off to regroup.<br /> <br /> After therapy we got back to the house in time for Sex Breakfast. As per Its name there was some talk about sex. In particular some people were lightly teasing Neon for her night with the ladies. It was all in good fun and she certainly seemed to have enjoyed herself, so no harm done. At one point we reminisced about Insincere Marguerite\u2019s birthday when we all played Twister, and I mentioned that I had a better idea in mind for my birthday. So, I told the group that my birthday was coming up this Sunday, but since that\u2019s when the Courts change over power I figured we\u2019d do something for my birthday on Friday. Lori asked what I had in mind and I said camping. I haven\u2019t been camping just for fun in a long time. My family and I used to do it all the time when I was a kid. Around my and Elena\u2019s birthday we would go camping in the mountains. Everyone seemed to like the idea, which made me glad. I should probably text Elena and see if she wants to join us. We just need to get some tents, sleeping bags, cooking gear, and probably some backpacks for folks. Insincere Marguerite jokingly asked if there were any stores that you could get tree stand from, for her to sleep in, and I said that there probably were. There was also discussion of shoes, and I told Marguerite that she might want to bring a pair since the weather is going to be cooler in the mountains than it is here. And if I have anything do to with it, it will get colder still.<br /> <br /> After Neon and Brightstar (who is a very bubbly person) left, we talked about more personal matters. Insincere Marguerite mentioned to Calamity that Yvette had come by and they had talked. Well, Lorelei and Yvette had talked and they discussed how Lori doesn\u2019t need saving and how much Marguerite has changed. Yvette didn\u2019t seem to wholly believe her, but agreed to call the next time she wanted to visit. We also talked about the problems that White Maria is having with her arranged marriage. Insincere Marguerite brought up Kimberly\u2019s idea of seducing the fianc\u00e9, and Calamity agreed that idea had merit. She also said there was one other thing that we could do. It was assumed by a few people that she meant killing the fianc\u00e9 and she said that she was joking about that second idea. Stasia was convinced from the beginning that her \u201cKat\u201d would only joke about such a thing. The rest of us were less sure, but didn\u2019t say anything. Calamity has killed \u201cproblem people\u201d in the past because of something that they might do, which is why she got in trouble with my Court in the first place. <br /> <br /> Marie H\u00e9l\u00e8ne also got brought up, which reminded De La Rocha about a fight that she got into with the other girl. Apparently, it was epic, and painful sounding, but she seemed to remember it rather fondly. She went on at length on how Marie H\u00e9l\u00e8ne punched her in the breast. In retaliation for that De La Rocha then put the other woman through some drywall, which left Marie H\u00e9l\u00e8ne senseless but, as De La Rocha put it, still twitching. I can\u2019t really comment on De La Rocha\u2019s idea of fun though, considering that I like to get into fights myself. After that Insincere Marguerite and Julia went out for an afternoon together. Not sure where they went, but it was probably somewhere romantic. Lori also left shortly after that conversation. It seems that she had a rendezvous with Joan and Andromeda this afternoon. No question about what those three are going to get up to. <br /> <br /> After Lori left De La Rocha told the rest of us about the upcoming talk with Twitch. Apparently, they have set a date and time. It will be this Thursday (Dec. 18<sup>th</sup>) at 3:00pm. They are going to meet in a location that has a room with two doors and a one-way mirror. This will allow each person to have their own entrance and exit, and guests can watch the conversation. They will not be able to hear what is said, but they\u2019ll be able to see how things go. Both De La Rocha and Twitch will bring two people with them to the talk. Those two people will pat down and search the other person and make sure no one is armed. Other people can come too, but they need to stay in the observation room. Everyone wants to make sure that Twitch is safe from Maria, but also that Maria is safe from Twitch. He is the one that really holds a grudge against her and is more than a little scared. Fear makes people do stupid things sometimes, so we\u2019re going to make sure that no one is armed. Maria also said something about having to wear a mask. I\u2019m not sure of the real significance behind that, but I have an idea. If she wore a mask during her durance it might bring her closer to what she used to be. I got the impression that De La Rocha wore a mask the day we were following Rook, when Hunting Hawk found them, and something happened between those two. I\u2019m assuming that she got a little too close to the old Maria that day. De La Rocha also commented to me that she wanted to make sure that everyone that went was going to be okay with the meeting. She implied that if it was just going to make someone, i.e. me, mad then it might upset people around that person. I assured her that I\u2019d be fine. I am still mad at Twitch for what he did to Rook, but I really want to see how he reacts when confronted by the one person he fears above all others. It\u2019s a little vindictive I suppose, but at this point I don\u2019t care. I kind of want to see him squirm. I can put my anger aside for that.<br /> <br /> The show went off like usual. Lori was absent, but Calamity did her usual wonderful job. As did the other performers, but as I\u2019ve mentioned, my motley mates have an advantage in that department. Hailey and Molly hung out at the bar again, which led to some interesting conversations. Stasia at one point decided that she wanted to pick up Hailey and came over to the bar. The pair of them started flirting. This left Molly a bit confused. She wanted to know why people went through a flirting \u201cstage\u201d in order to just sleep with one another. I answered that people like to have a bit of lead-in to the actual act. Sometimes there is flirting but no sex. Hailey interrupted Stasia to confront Molly about the elemental\u2019s comments. Molly replied that she thought it would be rude to talk about her friends behind their backs so she did it in front of her face. Hailey conceded that she didn\u2019t mind her talking about her to her face, she just didn\u2019t want to get interrupted while she was flirting with someone. I can see that. I wouldn\u2019t want to get interrupted, but that\u2019s mostly because I\u2019m not very good with people and I want to make sure that I do it right. I am much better at dealing with threats or other such things. Personal interactions are not my strong point.<br /> <br /> The others seemed to have a good night as well. The \u201cgirlfriends,\u201d as Julia, Insincere Marguerite, and De La Rocha\u2019s table has been dubbed, decided that they were going to seduce Dark Kimberly. She certainly didn\u2019t seem to mind all the attention and they soon disappeared upstairs. Calamity and Gawain also had an evening planned, though not for sex. They had plans to get together with Desiree and do some dream healing. Hopefully these continued sessions will bear fruit soon.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Well, it has been two weeks since Rook was killed. I still feel like I should have tried harder to bring him over to our side, but a part of me knows that he never would have left the Lady. I can\u2019t help but wonder \u201cwhat if?\u201d though. What if he had joined us? What would he do in the freehold? Would he really have been happy? What if we had decided to let him go with a promise to not come back to the Lady by the Sea freehold? He would have honored the contract I know that. He was a man of honor if nothing else. He was a good friend. Dammit, I miss him.<br /> <br /> Anyway, we had several guests this morning. Dark Kimberly stayed the night with the \u201cgirlfriends,\u201d Hailey stayed with Staisa, Desiree stayed for dream healing, and Joan and Andromeda came back to the Dream House with Lori. So, we had a rather full house. Things did get a little tense when Hailey and Andromeda realized that they were in a room together, but nothing came of it, so that\u2019s good. For her part Dark Kimberly was rather pleased with her evening. She was particularly blunt about it too. It would take more than that to offend anyone in the group though. So, she had a good time. Her only complaint was that she was feeling rather sore this morning. I don\u2019t need to know any more details.<br /> <br /> After breakfast our guests left. Then everyone, it seemed, wanted to take a look at the camping gear that we got. I think they all approved. They seemed happy with our purchases, and deferred to our knowledge on what sort of gear we would need for a night of camping. I\u2019m hoping that we can make camping an activity that we do together often. I enjoy being in the woods. You\u2019d think that after all my time camping early in my durance, I\u2019d get sick of it. I didn\u2019t like certain aspects of it when I was alone. Before the Lady. I didn\u2019t like having to constantly watch my back at night just in case some enterprising shit decided to steal my stuff. I didn\u2019t like having to fight to keep what gear I was able to gather together. I didn\u2019t like having to hunt when game was scarce. I do really like nature though, so there were some good points early in my durance too. I had nights where I knew that no one was around, so I could relax my guard just a bit. Enough to enjoy the sights, sounds and smells of the forest. Any time I camped in a pine forest was particularly nice. Pine needles make for a soft bed and they smell really good. I remember one time I had been hiking a particularly long time to get away from other people. I hadn\u2019t seen sign of another human for days so I when I made camp in a pine forest one night I knew that I was relatively safe. I had a soft and sheltered place to sleep. I hadn\u2019t gotten that good a night\u2019s sleep in a long time. It was very restful. <br /> <br /> We all talked about the upcoming trip, which made me happy in and of itself. I\u2019m glad that people are looking forward to the trip. It won\u2019t be for very long this time, just one night, but maybe on future trips we can spend a couple of days out there. And of course, since we were talking about camping all sorts of horror movie tropes came up. Lori joked that she\u2019d be the first to disappear since she was the promiscuous blonde. I don\u2019 think we\u2019d settled on who the survivor would be. There was also talk about fighting off bears, cougars and snakes. I seriously doubt that we\u2019ll have any such trouble, but Calamity and I assured everyone that they would be safe from the wildlife.<br /> <br /> One bit of news this morning was when Insincere Marguerite told the rest of us that Yvette would be coming to visit on Saturday afternoon. I assured her that it would be doable for us to get back to the Dream House in time for the rendezvous. I do want to make sure that others in the motely will be allowed to be present for the meeting. I\u2019m not sure Yvette would want to be in a room alone with Insincere Marguerite anyway, but I figure it would be safer for all involved if there were other people there. I mean the last time that Yvette came to our house she brought a gun and aimed it at two of my motley mates. I want to make sure that she is not armed this time. <br /> <br /> And some really good news this morning: Lori told the rest of us that Desiree been released from her pledge with Insincere Marguerite. She was freaking out just a bit though, so she had plans to stay with Gloria for the day. I can\u2019t tell you how happy I am that Insincere Marguerite is free of that pledge. I know it was weighing on her mind, and not in a good way. She was really uncomfortable with the whole thing, but agreed to do it to keep the freehold safe. Now that Desiree has been \u201cfixed,\u201d things should go back to normal. I guess we\u2019ll make sure that Desiree still has a support system here with our motley, should she need it. But she should now be able to function on her own without getting directions from an authority figure. She\u2019s strong, she should be able to handle it. <br /> <br /> After all that was over I realized that Calamity and I had not gotten the chance to spar yesterday, so I asked if she wanted to do so today. She was up for it, so we changed clothes and met out in the back yard. We had a small audience there to watch, at least part of the match anyway. Lori and Stasia stayed to observe. Right from the beginning I could tell that Calamity was aiming to show off for her friend. She used more flashy moves than utilitarian, and included more acrobatics than usual. I could tell she was having fun though, so I stepped up my game and matched her move for move. I didn\u2019t go quite as flashy as Calamity did, but I tried to put a little extra effort into the work out. It was kind of fun to watch the reactions from our audience. Lori, having seen us before, was impressed but not surprised by our fight. Stasia on the other hand was covering her face half of the time and had a worried look on her face through most of it. I don\u2019t think she was expecting to see us spar with live steel, or to move so fast. It was kind of funny to see her reaction though. Calamity doing those acrobatic moves here and there gave me a few opportunities to sneak a peek at the ladies watching us. Normally I wouldn\u2019t have a chance to look anywhere but where Calamity\u2019s glass was coming from. This time though I had a few seconds here and there. It was fun. Lori left before we were done, I\u2019m assuming to get ready for the show. Staisa followed a little bit after that. I\u2019m not sure if she was able to watch the rest of the match. Our fights can be a bit intense for us, so I can only assume that it must have been intense for her to watch us. In the end though, I had to concede the fight to Calamity. She got more strikes in on me than I did on her. It was still fun though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> <b><b>Backstage</b></b><br /> <br /> Backstage, Insincere Marguerite sat on the rail for the steps going up to the catwalks. Clad in her usual hot pants and t-shirt look, this time with just a question mark, she looked underdressed compared to the other two women. Maria de la Rocha was in her leather and fishnet punk threads, leaning against the wall across from her in the way cool people are wont to do, purple and blue colored head to toe, while Julia Oldacre sat on the stairs in a flowing evening gown, looking as old fashioned as Maria did modern. She wore her usual black and deep purple, contrasting her fianc\u00e9e\u2019s bright colors. She was looking at her ring.<br /> <br /> \u201cI spoke to Juliette, we will be together tonight. I know we all missed her.\u201d The haughty girl\u2019s French accent was lovely to hear. There was equally cocky response from the Latina, whose accent was almost as thick. \u201cI knew I was going to be. I wasn\u2019t sure about you two. I guess I can make room.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe talked to Yvette. So there will be a conversation. Which of us are going to be with you? I can\u2019t imagine you would pick Calamity, and Jacob might be awkward.\u201d Julia looked up at the other seated Darkling.<br /> <br /> \u201cJuliette I think. Maria had intense hostile emotions on display when they first met\u2026understandably,\u201d She quickly added the last part, as she saw the slightly skeptical look in the punk\u2019s shadowed eyes. \u201cAnd I think you might be a little\u2026volatile Julia.\u201d Her tone was sympathetic.<br /> <br /> \u201cI guess volatile is the nicer way to put it.\u201d The Artist looked up at her, moving to idly twist some strands of her long hair. \u201cI just can\u2019t help it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, you will see that I am not leaving you. And you are a very creative person. An artist! Your temperament might make times like now difficult, but it serves you well in your craft, love,\u201d The Tunnelgrub\u2019s tone and expression were sweet and soothing.<br /> <br /> \u201cHey I am an artist too! And creative! I never punch the same person exactly the same way twice!\u201d There was the cocky grin on the Leechfinger\u2019s face again.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd also perhaps temperamental, hein?\u201d This time Lurker\u2019s tone and expression were playful.<br /> <br /> \u201cPssssh The Clam is still the one who goes violently off the rails way more than me. I am good right up until she gets some anger management.\u201d A dismissive hand gesture.<br /> <br /> \u201cApart from tossing Gloria up on the wall and holding her by the throat?\u201d There was a tilt of Marguerite\u2019s head.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh that\u2019s all settled. We get along super now.\u201d De La Rocha waved her hand again. \u201cHonestly Jules is the only reason she and I aren\u2019t dating now. We still hook up pretty regularly. Will be again soon, I am sure.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd you threatened Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne if she tries to pick her up.\u201d The Tunnelgrub said offhandedly.<br /> <br /> \u201cDid I do that?\u201d The Witchtooth cut her eyes, looking away.<br /> <br /> \u201cIs Lori stopping you from being involved more seriously?\u201d Julia looked up.<br /> <br /> \u201cNah, but that whole thing about girlfriends outside the family?\u201d The Latina made a circular gesture at the group, \u201cToo complicated for me. You guys are different; I mean we are all in love. Someone not involved with anyone else in the family is stress I don\u2019t need.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSpeaking of stress you don\u2019t need, you ready to speak to Twitch tomorrow?\u201d The Nightsinger gave a birdlike tilt of her head this time.<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2018Course.\u201d A casual chin lift. \u201cIt will be done and over. Super easy. Just got to pick the right mask.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMask?!?\u201d Both her partners exclaimed at once.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah. It\u2019s nothing big. Just a mask.\u201d She gave a slight shrug. The other two looked at each other and back.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou are sure this is a good idea, my sweet?\u201d Insincere Marguerite sounded pensive.<br /> <br /> \u201cI can hack it, okay? I know what I can do. That whole Hunting Hawk thing was stressful. He was coming for Jules. That\u2019s all. No Hunting Hawk here.\u201d The Latina stood up from her lean.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo it was not Hunting Hawk you were already AWOL from where you were supposed to be. You had made a direct line for Lori, I don\u2019t even want to think about why.\u201d<br /> <br /> The relaxed demeanor dropped immediately and she pointed at Julia. \u201cHey at no point was I going to hurt, or grab, or impede or anything else Lorelei. Accuse me of anything else but even when lost in that hunt I would not have hurt her. If you think I would\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe doesn\u2019t. Relax.\u201d The Lurker\u2019s tone was casual, but there was steel in it.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2026sorry.\u201d The bluster was gone. The Leechfinger looked sheepishly up at where Insincere Marguerite, who regarded her with an aloof curiosity, was sitting. Marguerite\u2019s foot dropped down and brushed Julia\u2019s face. The Artist kissed it.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe are just worried about you.\u201d De La Rocha was fixed in place with the cat\u2019s eyes and soothing voice. \u201cIf you say it is fine, we believe you. \u201c<br /> <br /> \u201cI am, thanks though.\u201d She watched Julia\u2019s increasing fascination with the dangling foot. \u201cYou know, we should get back to the room. They are gonna need this area soon and, uh\u2026.\u201d<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite smiled and hopped down, taking Julia\u2019s hand. \u201cA good idea I think. Shall we?\u201d<br /> <br /> The Artist smiled and rose to her feet, taking holding her fianc\u00e9e\u2019s arm. De La Rocha pushed off the wall and joined them after a glance behind.<br /> <br /> \u201cWait, were you perving the dressing room from there?\u201d Julia looked back at her.<br /> <br /> The Punk\u2019s eyes got large, and a little shifty. \u201cNah, was just time to go. Something was afoot.\u201d<br /> <br /> The couple turned back and stared at her, and De La Rocha shrugged helplessly. First Marguerite then Julia giggled, and they made their way in to their usual table.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LXXXIII</i><br /> <br /> Okay, pretty good recaps, as for what was left out\u2026<br /> <br /> They did not so much seduce Dark Kimberly as De La Rocha just picked her up and carried her out with them as they walked by. Dark Kimberly is shy of five feet and built small, so the Goth was easy to pick up especially strong as De La Rocha is.<br /> <br /> In all reality, Calamity herself rolled out the last bit of the dream healing to free Desiree. Calamity\u2019s player is going to focus more on Dream stuff as we go.<br /> <br /> I think that covers it, but as always comments and questions are welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T15:58:07-07:00","id":1100236,"title":"","content":"Huh, so all of Lori's tops have back slits or a low back? Interesting, I don't think the Mask would cover that. It's almost like a small minor Frailty in a way. I guess its one of the weird little habits and mannerisms that Changelings tend to pick up. I wonder how she hides them in her more conservative outfits. The many situations the Mask inspires are Just so fascinating XD squee. It makes my inner analysis nerd so happy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T19:58:15-07:00","id":1100308,"title":"","content":"Yeah &quot;what are normal people seeing&quot; can be an odd if fun game to play with Changelings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T14:27:33-07:00","id":1100587,"title":"","content":"And Beasts","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,