target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-18T13:14:37-07:00","id":1105160,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to check on the Dream House Motley! For unrelated reasons, no journal for Calamity or Insincere Marguerite, but Lorelei and Jacob should get us through. Let\u2019s check in.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LXXXIV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> That was not easy. I mean, progress was made, and I can only see that as a good thing\u2026 but if anything it only heightened my awareness of how far we still have to go.<br /> <br /> This isn\u2019t making any sense. I need to start at the beginning to give the preceding statements a little context. Jeez, I must really be rattled.<br /> <br /> Okay, so\u2026 Wednesday. Yeah. Wednesday night was good. The show went well, I think. My lone solo was a sultry-sexy re-working of Louis Armstrong\u2019s signature piece \u201cWhat a Wonderful World.\u201d Now, obviously I didn\u2019t even attempt his trademark subterranean growl; I lifted the melody a couple of octaves and put my own spin on it, all while wearing filmy, diaphanous white clothing. It\u2019s sort of wistful, hopeful, and uplifting, and I think the audience took to it well. Might have to do that one again some time.<br /> <br /> Several representatives of the Spring Court were present, most of them seated together at the same table. I chatted with Princess Jolie for a bit, and asked Austin how his Chestnut Party had gone (apparently it was a rollicking success; Andromeda debuted a new invention called the \u201cHarbinger of the Void\u201d and special orders are pouring in from all quarters). But the real reason I made my way over to that table was Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne.<br /> <br /> It was nice to see her back in the Dream House, and she seemed to be enjoying herself as well. I knew that if we could get her back through the doors she\u2019d remember how much fun it was working here. I think we\u2019re well on our way to renewing her contract. She said she\u2019d stop by the business office within the next few days to hammer out the details with Calamity.<br /> <br /> She <u><u>also</u></u> pulled me into her lap and started making out with me fairly aggressively. Okay, that\u2019s not entirely fair\u2026 I mean it\u2019s not like I was fighting against the notion or anything. Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne is hot, and I confess that I was pretty eager to keep her in a good mood at that point.<br /> <br /> Still, duty called, and there were other guests to think about. The Night Courtier known as \u201cV\u201d had dropped by from LA, and the two of us spent a few moments chatting as well. He\u2019s a little hard to read, but I think he was enjoying himself. Natasha and Elena were also there, and Stasia was flirting pretty heavily with both of them for much of the night (I don\u2019t think Jacob was particularly happy about that, actually). I spoke briefly with both of them. Things seem to be going well between Natasha and my dad, by the way\u2026 she said that they \u201crespect each other\u2019s space.\u201d Wonders never cease!<br /> <br /> Of course, I eventually wound up sitting in D\u2019s lap, and it wasn\u2019t too much later that she decided to carry me upstairs to our bedroom. I admit that I might have encouraged her a bit\u2026 Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne was still eyeing me like a raw steak, and I really wanted to spend that night with D, considering what she had on her plate for the next day. So I tipped Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne an apologetic wink, mouthed the words \u201crain check,\u201d and allowed myself to be carried away from the theater by the one I love.<br /> <br /> We actually ended up spending the night with Julia and Marguerite, as it turned out. It had been a while since I\u2019d been with all three of them together, and I think D privately wanted to be surrounded by her lovers to help bolster her for the impending confrontation. There was a bit of hanky-panky, of course, but by and large I think the four of us just held each other, spreading warmth and comfort evenly between the quad.<br /> <br /> Okay, so the next day (Thursday; yesterday as of this writing) was when all the really big shit went down. Breakfast was pleasant enough, and D had that little bit of extra swagger that she only gets when she\u2019s really nervous about something. She barely ate. I\u2019m sure the others noticed, but nobody called attention to it (which is probably a good thing\u2026 if she\u2019d gotten embarrassed she might have gorged herself to make a point and gotten sick during the meeting itself). <br /> <br /> The only other thing that seems worth mentioning about breakfast is that Stasia seemed to be upset with Jacob. I eventually gathered that she had toned down her attempts to seduce Elena at his request, and refocused her attentions on Natasha. Natasha, not happy with being Stasia\u2019s second choice (and possibly a little miffed that Stasia seemed to be doing better with Elena that she had) turned cold and shut down. Stasia is now convinced that Jacob \u201cowes\u201d her for that debacle. I\u2019m not sure how she figures that, but I guess it\u2019s none of my business anyway.<br /> <br /> I ran by Joan and Andromeda\u2019s place after breakfast. Andromeda gave me a quick tutorial on how to disassemble, reassemble and operate her new medical scanner. She is an <u><u>amazing</u></u> inventor, and I\u2019m sure her star is on the rise. I guess she must have heard something about the meeting through the Freehold grapevine, because she squeezed my hand and gave me a quick kiss for luck before I left.<br /> <br /> We drove to the clinic in a few groups. I had the scanner in the trunk of my car, so D and I had a few minutes of alone time. Whenever I wasn\u2019t shifting gears, I made sure that my hand was on hers. I think she appreciated it, though of course she\u2019d never admit to a case of nerves.<br /> <br /> The room they had set aside for the meeting had two big windows and two doors\u2026 one on each side of the room. The motley and I were arrayed in a short hallway behind one of the windows, while a few Winter Courtiers backed Twitch up from a similar hallway behind the other window. A third hallway connected the two so we could discuss how the meeting was going with our counterparts. In addition to Twitch, Doctor Bright was there, as were Molly Nuit, Tamara Chance, and Boss Lowjack.<br /> <br /> Molly and Tamara gave D a cursory pat-down to make sure she wasn\u2019t concealing any weapons, while I simply had Twitch walk through the arch formed by Andromeda\u2019s scanner. He agreed readily enough, and a few minutes later everyone concerned was reasonably assured that no weapons of any type were present. At last it was time. D went to get changed, and I think all of us in the Last Dance tensed up a bit.<br /> <br /> As we were waiting for her to finish changing, I spoke briefly with Twitch. \u201cMr. Twichowicz,\u201d I said softly, \u201cI wanted to thank you for doing this. I think it will be good for both of you.\u201d<br /> <br /> He gave me a watery smile and shook my hand gently. \u201cI hope so,\u201d he replied simply.<br /> <br /> D came back a few minutes later wearing her scrubs, and the two of them entered the meeting room from opposite sides. No one outside of the room could hear what was said, and I guess none of us will ever really know what they talked about for sure. D would probably tell me if I asked her, but I\u2019m sure it was an intensely personal and private conversation.<br /> <br /> At first Twitch was pretty nervous. He kept maneuvering so that D was further away from him\u2026 but the two of them were still talking, and neither one looked likely to start anything violent. At some point, he asked her to put her mask on. She complied\u2026 and that\u2019s when things got really tense.<br /> <br /> My love started exhibiting predatory behaviors, on (I hope) an unconscious level. She circled around him from time to time, keeping the distance between them at a constant no matter how he shifted or moved. At one point, D turned so that I could see her face, and I noted that her pupils were almost fully dilated, making her eyes look sort of like mine. Twitch\u2019s anxiety was obviously ratcheting higher with each passing minute, and after a while he started knocking on the door on his side of the room. Someone opened it, and he exited the chamber.<br /> <br /> A moment later, Doctor Bright walked over to our hallway. \u201cTwitch has asked for a short break, so that he can gather his thoughts and compose himself,\u201d he said softly. \u201cAre there any objections?\u201d<br /> <br /> I shook my head. \u201cI think that\u2019s a good idea,\u201d I concurred. I opened the door and called inside. \u201cMaria?\u201d I said softly. Her head snapped around as she looked at me. \u201cTwitch wants a break. Come on, honey, let\u2019s get you some water or something, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> Maria slipped out of the room and into the hall. She\u2019d obviously regressed a bit, but the difference wasn\u2019t quite as shocking or pronounced as it had been in that parking lot with Hunting Hawk. I pulled her close, into a tight hug, and pulled her mask aside. She tried to stop me briefly, but didn\u2019t put much effort into this token act of resistance. That ghastly rictus grin was there, but it faded pretty quickly.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019s <u><u>beautiful</u></u><u>,</u>\u201d Julia sighed from somewhere behind me.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019s <u><u>always</u></u> beautiful,\u201d I countered firmly without looking away. \u201cYou okay, babe?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course,\u201d she said with a grin that approached her usual demeanor. Her eyes were still widely dilated, though. \u201cI\u2019ve got it all under control. I think it\u2019s going well, don\u2019t you?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re doing great,\u201d I said with a smile. \u201cOnly\u2026 I think maybe you should take the mask off for the rest of the meeting.\u201d<br /> <br /> Her forehead furrowed. \u201cWhy?\u201d she asked. \u201cI can handle it.\u201d<br /> <br /> I thought about that. \u201cI know you can,\u201d I said fervently, \u201cbut the whole point of putting the mask and the scrubs on was so that Twitch could see that you\u2019re really the Maria he remembers, to put his mind at ease that you\u2019re no longer after him. He\u2019s seen that now. There\u2019s no need to wear it any longer.\u201d<br /> <br /> She looked down. \u201cLori,\u201d she said softly, \u201cyou don\u2019t need to worry about me, okay? I got this.\u201d<br /> <br /> I kissed her. \u201cD, this isn\u2019t about what you can or can\u2019t handle. I know how emotional this meeting is for you, and I am so proud of how well you\u2019ve done so far. But the mask brings out a certain darkness in you, and I think it\u2019s making Twitch nervous. That\u2019s\u2026 counterproductive. I think it would be better if you didn\u2019t wear it, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> That\u2019s when Calamity spoke up. \u201cD, can\u2019t you see how scared this is making Lori?\u201d She meant well, and I don\u2019t blame her for what she said, but if I could have stopped her from saying it I would have. I mean, in all honesty, she was <u><u>right</u></u>. I was scared. Scared of losing the tough in-your-face chicana to the slinking creature of darkness\u2026 but that\u2019s not what D needed to hear.<br /> <br /> \u201cBut\u2026 you love that part of me too, right?\u201d D asked, her eyes widening and her voice gaining an edge.<br /> <br /> I pulled her into a kiss. \u201cOf <u><u>course</u></u> I do,\u201d I said once I had come up for air. \u201cI love <u><u>every</u></u> part of you, Maria, and nothing is ever going to change that. Got it?\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cGot it,\u201d she promised me.<br /> <br /> \u201cNow, having said that, I still think it would be better for <u><u>Twitch</u></u> if you didn\u2019t wear the mask for the rest of the meeting. Think you can do that\u2026 for me?\u201d<br /> <br /> She rolled her eyes, and her grin softened a little. \u201cHad to bring out the big guns, didn\u2019t you? Fine, if Twitch is okay with it, I won\u2019t wear the mask for the rest of the meeting.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll check with his motley,\u201d I said, before striding around the corner to compose myself.<br /> <br /> Doctor Bright met me halfway. \u201cIs she alright?\u201d he asked, concern evident in his voice.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019ll be fine,\u201d I assured him, \u201cthough\u2026 I think it might be for the best if she didn\u2019t put the mask on again.\u201d<br /> <br /> He nodded. \u201cI concur,\u201d he said simply. \u201cI don\u2019t know if you employed any Spring Court talents during that meeting, but to my untrained eye it seemed that Miss de la Rocha was a bit at war with herself. She has held herself in check\u2026 so far. But I feel that we should all be ready to act quickly if necessary.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cD will be fine,\u201d I said as firmly as I could, \u201cbut it doesn\u2019t hurt to be prepared\u2026 for both of their sakes.\u201d<br /> <br /> The second part of the meeting started shortly thereafter. In a lot of ways it was less stressful than the earlier portion had been\u2026 but it was not without its hiccups. D did not put the mask back on, and Twitch seemed to accept that. The two of them shook hands several times, and had what appeared to be a quite amiable conversation.<br /> <br /> And then I noticed that D was keeping her face pointed away from me at all times. It struck me that she was doing it deliberately. I walked around to the Winter Court side of the room and asked meekly if I could join them; Boss Lowjack raised no objection. Molly seemed to be taking everything in stride, but Tamara was quite agitated\u2026 she looked almost aroused. Doctor Bright was focusing his attention on the conversation with the intensity of a searchlight. I joined him at the window.<br /> <br /> \u201cIs Twitch okay?\u201d I asked hoarsely.<br /> <br /> Doctor Bright nodded. \u201cHe\u2019s fine. I don\u2019t think he\u2019s aware of her inner struggle at all. He\u2019s not the most socially perceptive of individuals.\u201d<br /> <br /> I haven\u2019t often used the Contracts of Fleeting Spring, as reading another person\u2019s desires can be a slippery slope when it comes to privacy. I\u2019ve <u><u>never</u></u> used them on D, and I thought I\u2019d never need to. But at that moment, I was worried about her. There was something in her eyes that made me more than a little frightened on Twitch\u2019s behalf. So I concentrated for a moment and let the glamour flow through me, and in less than a minute her heart was laid bare.<br /> <br /> Her most potent desire was to make things right with Twitch; to put an end to the bad blood between them and ease his mind about her intentions. But that desire was only <u><u>barely</u></u> winning out over her instinctive urge to drag him off into some dark place and drain his life until all that remained was a desolate husk.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019s got this,\u201d I said, in what I hope was a comforting tone of voice. \u201cIt\u2019s a struggle for her, but she\u2019s strong. I trust her.\u201d<br /> <br /> Doctor Bright nodded uncertainly. I can\u2019t blame him for his doubt. It was a member of his own motley who was most obviously at risk from the encounter, and he doesn\u2019t know D as well as I do.<br /> <br /> The touchiest moment came right at the end of the meeting, when Twitch unexpectedly pulled Maria into a hug. She stiffened, and I saw her eyes go wide and that rictus grin start to spread\u2026 and then she gently patted his back and pulled away. I hurried over to the other side of the room so that I could be there when she came out.<br /> <br /> \u201cSee, I told you,\u201d she said somewhat stiffly as she returned my welcoming embrace. \u201cNo sweat. I\u2019m in control. I didn\u2019t carry him off. I didn\u2019t kill him, even though it would have been so easy. I didn\u2019t give in to her\u2026 to my own darkness, I mean, even though he was the only one who ever got away from me\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> The growling edge in her voice almost set me crying, but I held it in for her sake. \u201cYou did great, honey,\u201d I said, still holding her, \u201cI\u2019m so proud of you.\u201d<br /> <br /> She shrugged and came back to herself a little bit. \u201cI guess\u2026 I guess I need to stop thinking of Maria as a separate person from me, huh?\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cYou need to come to terms with that part of yourself. She\u2019s a part of you\u2026 and so she\u2019s <u><u>amazing</u></u>. But pushing that part of you down and suppressing it will only lead to trouble in the long run.\u201d<br /> <br /> Julia stepped forward eagerly. \u201cI can help you come to terms with it\u2026\u201d she said in a rush, and then, sort of distantly, \u201cI need to paint you.\u201d<br /> <br /> I chuckled. \u201cDown girl,\u201d I said with a wink to let her know that I wasn\u2019t really jealous. \u201cWe\u2019ll all help. But tonight she\u2019s mine.\u201d<br /> <br /> I admit that I was clingy as we drove back to the Dream House. D and I got back later than the others since we had to stop off at Joan and Andromeda\u2019s place to return the scanner. The doors weren\u2019t open yet when we got home, but the pre-show buzz was already starting. Which is why I felt a little guilty about what happened next.<br /> <br /> \u201cCalamity,\u201d I said softly, approaching my friend with my arm still firmly linked with D\u2019s, \u201cI\u2019m sorry about this, but do you think the show will be okay without me tonight? I don\u2019t feel much like performing or socializing.\u201d<br /> <br /> D\u2019s eyes got kind of wide and she whispered \u201cshit\u201d to herself. Calamity allowed as how I could take the night off, which was really nice of her considering that I\u2019m not going to be performing for our Friday night show either. I rearranged a couple of acts from our mortal performers and that was that. D and I headed up to bed.<br /> <br /> She held me, and I held her, and I\u2019m pretty sure I probably cried at some point, but for the most part it was just about us being together. She assured me over and over that she had the darkness under control, and even mentioned that Twitch was going to stop by the Dream House for a performance at some point, and the two of them were going to sit together and chat. I\u2019m not worried about that meeting; a bright public place like that shouldn\u2019t evoke too many predatory impulses in my love.<br /> <br /> \u201cD,\u201d I said as she blustered, \u201cI read your desires while you were talking to him.\u201d<br /> <br /> She stopped dead and sighed. \u201cShit,\u201d she said again, \u201cI forgot that was something you could do.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m not trying to embarrass you,\u201d I said earnestly, clasping her hand in both of mine, \u201cbut I know how close things came in there. Again, I\u2019m <u><u>so</u></u> <u><u>proud</u></u> of you for keeping control in that situation. You handled it as well as anyone could have, I think, and you and Twitch should both feel a lot better about the situation now that everything\u2019s out in the open. But having said that\u2026 this isn\u2019t something that\u2019s just going to go away. You need to find a way to deal with it\u2026 pushing it down and denying it isn\u2019t going to work forever.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cI know,\u201d she said. \u201cWe\u2019ll work it out. I know you\u2019ll help me, Jules. I just\u2026 I don\u2019t like you seeing me like that. That\u2019s not the girl you fell in love with\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I kissed her hard. \u201cIt <u><u>is</u></u>,\u201d I said firmly, \u201cit\u2019s just a different part of her. I wasn\u2019t <u><u>afraid</u></u> of you, Maria, I was worried about how it could affect the situation between you and Twitch. I swear that\u2019s all it was.\u201d<br /> <br /> I could have said more. Maybe I should have, but things were going so well between us that I didn\u2019t want to risk things devolving into an argument (even a mild one). I could have told her that I think she might benefit from joining Jacob and Calamity at their therapy sessions\u2026 the clinic has some top-notch psychiatrists, and I\u2019m sure they know a lot of techniques to help changelings deal with suppressed dark sides in a healthy manner.<br /> <br /> I could have told her that no matter what happens, I will always love her, and I know that she will never hurt me. I could have mentioned that if she ever gives in to her dark side completely, I\u2019ll be there. In the worst-case scenario, I\u2019ll lure evil people into whatever dark lair she settles in so that she can feed appropriately and effectively\u2026 because that life would be better than living as a jet-set movie star queen without her.<br /> <br /> We didn\u2019t join Marguerite and Julia last night, and there wasn\u2019t much in the way of libidinous action between us either. We mostly held each other and kissed and slept. It was nice, and I had my emotions firmly under control again by the time we got up this morning.<br /> <br /> Most of Sex Breakfast was taken up by discussions of our impending camping trip (we\u2019re actually supposed to leave in a few minutes, so I\u2019ll wrap this up). There was one noteworthy interruption, however\u2026 Desiree strode into the room, bold as brass and naked as the day she was born. Most of us let it go with an appreciative ogle, but Luna got distinctly uncomfortable and made as if to leave the room. Before that could happen, we convinced Desiree that it would be appropriate for her to put some clothes on.<br /> <br /> \u201cSure,\u201d she said brightly. \u201cSorry, Luna,\u201d she called out sincerely as she left, \u201cI didn\u2019t mean to upset you. I only did it because Insincere Marguerite told me not to!\u201d So the motley had a private little chuckle about that.<br /> <br /> Well, like I said, the motley is getting dressed and packing up the vehicles (no \u2018vette this time; I am <u><u>not</u></u> driving my baby up into the mountains with all that dust and pine sap and falling acorns and\u2026 and <u><u>nature</u></u> around), so I guess I\u2019d better say ta-ta for now. By the next time I write in this journal, I\u2019ll probably have had hot cocoa and toasted marshmallows and sang \u201cKum ba yah\u201d and all that Girl Scout shit I never got to do when I was a kid. And as much as I like to give Jacob shit for his \u201cback to nature\u201d birthday wish\u2026 I must admit that I\u2019m really looking forward to this.<br /> <br /> D is strong, and we love each other. I can put aside my anxiety for the moment and have a good time celebrating my friend\u2019s birthday.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> After sparring Calamity and I went our separate ways to get ready for the show. Calamity needed to shower and change, and I needed to shower and make sure the bar was fully stocked. It didn\u2019t take too long to get things ready for the show, so that was good. At the show I was happy to see Elena there. That made it easy for me to tell her about the upcoming camping trip and to see if she wanted to join us. She said that it sounded like fun and agreed to come along. I don\u2019t know if my family kept up the tradition of camping on our birthday while I was gone. I figured I would have heard about it from Elena if the little shit had decided he didn\u2019t want to go. So, I get to go camping with my sister after what feels like forever. It won\u2019t be quite like it was when I was a kid, but I do plan on seeing about making it snow, so that will at least help it feel more familiar.<br /> <br /> Also during the show, after I\u2019d gone back to the bar, Stasia approached me and asked if I had any problems with her trying to seduce my sister. I will admit that I was a little surprised by the question, but happy that she even asked it. I think it would have gone badly if she had just assumed and had done it anyway. I told her that I thought it would make things awkward. I was also not so sure that my sister was interested in girls or in even having a one night stand. I know Stasia is not looking for a relationship with anyone. She is just \u201ctesting the waters\u201d so to speak. Even if Elena was interested in girls I don\u2019t think she\u2019d appreciate just being someone\u2019s one time conquest. So, I warned Stasia away from Elena and she said that she\u2019d back off, which she did. The rest of the night she tried to pick up Natasha, which didn\u2019t go as well as she was hoping, but at least it wasn\u2019t my sister. Elena for her part seemed a bit relieved when Stasia backed off. She asked me at one point if I\u2019d warned her off and I admitted that I said it might not be a good idea if Stasia pursued her original plan.<br /> <br /> Later in the evening, after they had performed, Calamity and Lori visited with some people. Most notably Princess Jolie, Ginny, Austin and Marie H\u00e9l\u00e8ne. There was a good deal of flirting, and Lori at least made out with Marie H\u00e9l\u00e8ne. She also asked Austin how his Chestnut party went. Apparently, it went just fine. We had missed it due to our visit to the club in Los Angeles, which was just fine by me. I hadn\u2019t planned on going to Austin\u2019s party anyway. I know Calamity at least had been thinking about it, but I\u2019m not sure how many other people in the motley had been seriously considering it.<br /> <br /> Calamity was also busy this evening. After she left Jolie\u2019s table she went to go talk to Dark Kimberly about White Maria and her wedding situation. Calamity wanted to know if Kimberly had a picture of the fianc\u00e9 so she could go into his dreams and find out how he felt about the whole marriage thing. Dark Kimberly suggested going into the dreams of the parents and trying to persuade them that marrying their daughter off to some stranger was a bad idea, no matter how nice his family tree is.<br /> <br /> Around that time Lori went over to talk to Natasha. She was curious to see how Natasha was liking living with her dad, the good preacher. It seems like everything is going well for those two, which is good. I know that Natasha needed a real place to stay. Not just crashing on a friend\u2019s couch, but a real place. I was also happy to hear that Lori\u2019s dad seems to be doing well with the arrangement too. He seems like a nice guy. <br /> <br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> This morning was another day for therapy. I went even though I didn\u2019t especially feel like going. Like last time I figured Calamity would physically drag me there so there didn\u2019t seem to be much point in fighting about it. Things went a bit better this time. I told Sullivan about the upcoming camping trip, and he seemed much more interested in that than he did with my hunting trip in the Hedge. He seemed to think that the camping trip was a healthier thing to do with my friends and sister. It certainly is a more mundane thing to do. I don\u2019t think that the hunting trip was all that reckless. We let people know where we were going. And it\u2019s not like Calamity and I aren\u2019t more than capable of taking care of ourselves. Anyway, he liked the idea of camping. Even when I mentioned that I was going to make it snow. <br /> <br /> When we got back from therapy Stasia wanted to have a word with me. Apparently, she struck out with Natasha last night and holds me responsible since I didn\u2019t want her to seduce my sister. She said that I owed her one. I\u2019m not sure how I\u2019m supposed to repay her for that. I\u2019m not sorry that I warned her off Elena. I\u2019m pretty sure that Elena isn\u2019t sorry that I told Staisa not to pick her up. Elena is still young, and as far as I know is not the most experienced person when it comes to sex or relationships. Not that I\u2019m much better, but Stasia is. I didn\u2019t want my sister to get coerced into something that she might regret later.<br /> <br /> The afternoon is when all the exciting stuff happened. Because that\u2019s when the meeting between De La Rocha and Twitch took place. When it was time we all piled into the van and headed for the Clinic. They had a room set up for the meeting. There were three entrances, one on either side of the room and one on the side. Before the two would be allowed into a room together they had to be searched. Twitch went through the medical scanner that Lori borrowed and had set up earlier. De La Rocha was patted down by Molly and Tamara. Before anything started Calamity looked to see what Twitch was afraid of, and came back with the obvious, Maria, and a few unexpected things. He was wary about the uneven number of doors and something about the differing sizes of eggs that he had for breakfast this morning. That man really is scared of everything. He had plenty of support though. Several members of the Winter Court were there. Dr. Bright, Lowjack, Tamara and Molly from what I remember. I was there too, but wasn\u2019t exactly there to support Twitch. I just wanted to see how things went down.<br /> <br /> The meeting started off tame. De La Rocha, or I guess I should call her Maria, started off in her regular clothes and then after a little while put scrubs on over her clothes. Twitch was a little more nervous at that and backed off just a bit. Maria closed the distance. When Maria put her mask on Twitch backed off some more and she again followed. Her body language changed at that point. Her posture became more hunched and her pupils were really dilated. Twitch was scared but didn\u2019t panic which was probably good. I got the impression that if he\u2019d bolted Maria would have chased him. At that point Twitch called for a break and each person left through their own door. Lori, who was extremely tense, coaxed Maria out of her mask, and underneath it was a rather disturbing grin. After a few moments, the rictus smile started to leave Maria\u2019s face and she became De La Rocha again. When she went back in the room she stayed in her scrubs but left the mask off. We assured her that she could handle the situation and that she was doing well. She seemed to think she was being weak by not putting the mask back on. I guess I can see that to some extent. She wants to be able to say that she conquered her darker side even while wearing the same things that she did in Arcadia. I personally thought she was getting a bit too close to her old self, but that is like the pot calling the kettle black. I\u2019ve gotten pretty close to Rime in the recent past. I don\u2019t need to be casting aspersions on anyone else\u2019s efforts to deny their baser instincts.<br /> <br /> I can see some similarities between Maria\u2019s durance and my time in Arcadia. We were both predators, though she didn\u2019t technically work for the Gentry. We both hunted down targets and killed them. I\u2019m assuming that she used her leechfinger abilities to kill her prey. I just used my knives. There are some differences though. I didn\u2019t kill all my quarry and had other responsibilities as well. One of my more mundane jobs was to occasionally guard the Treasures. The Lady wanted to make sure that her Treasures were safe, and that they stayed in the palace. Sometimes a Treasure would escape, or try to. Delight had been the first Treasure in a long while to actually make it out of the Lady\u2019s realm and back to \u2018the world.\u2019 A lot of the Treasures seemed to be happy with their place in life. Desire certainly liked her lot. She lived up to her name and seduced a good number of the Knights, including myself. Normally I turned down her advances, but one time I was in a really good mood and felt like celebrating with someone. Rook, myself and a couple other Knights had managed to put down a rebellion that had actually gotten pretty organized before we found them. It was a hard day\u2019s fight, but we won the day and we were all lauded by the Lady when we returned. So, I was in a good mood, and Desire\u2019s offer came at just the right time, it seemed.<br /> <br /> During the last part of the meeting Twitch seemed to be doing a bit better. He kept touching Maria, I guess to reassure himself that she wasn\u2019t going to hurt him. He kept shaking her hands and at one point gave her a hug. I thought for sure with the hug that Maria was going to slip. She certainly seemed on edge. Those of us watching seemed to be reacting in different ways too. Dr. Bright seemed upset, Lowjack was unreadable, Lori was white-knuckling the window sill, Tamara was probably a little more turned on by Maria than she should be, and Molly just seemed interested. She didn\u2019t seem to pick up on what was happening in the background of the meeting. When the meeting was over Maria was keen to say that the Gentry don\u2019t get to decide who she is. I think she was closer to being the Maria of old than she\u2019d like to admit, but she did keep things in check throughout the whole meeting. She didn\u2019t slip, though it seemed close a couple of times. <br /> <br /> For the most part I agree that the Gentry don\u2019t get to decide who we are. In some ways though they helped to create who we are. Whether their influence is direct or not they still have some sort of impact on what kind of person we become while in their realm. That influence follows us even after we escape. I am certainly not the person I was before I was taken. I don\u2019t really remember much about who I really was. I remember some things that happened but I don\u2019t know who I was inside. It was so long ago, and I\u2019ve changed so much in the time that I\u2019ve been gone. I remember liking to read when I was younger. I would go to the library and check out books on myths from around the world. I wanted to know how different cultures explained things. I think I got teased for being such a bookworm in school. I have vague memories of that. I\u2019m just not that person any more though. I don\u2019t read nearly as much anymore. I didn\u2019t really read at all while in the Lady\u2019s service. I didn\u2019t have the time. Sometimes I would purloin a book from someone that I was sent to catch. Some people would hold onto books as though they were precious. I didn\u2019t understand taking up valuable space in their pack with books instead of necessary things, but some people did it. And so, I got to read every so often when I was in Her service, but it wasn\u2019t by any means a regular thing. Overall, I\u2019m just a different person than I used to be. I am far from the innocent child that I used to be. Sometimes it seems like my memories belong to a completely different person. Like it wasn\u2019t me at all. So, the Gentry may not get to decide who we are, but they certainly shape who we become.<br /> <br /> After the meeting Lori and De La Rocha went to talk privately. While they were gone Julia expressed an interest in painting a portrait of Maria with the scary grin that she wore after taking off the mask. Insincere Marguerite and I both expressed concern with that plan. I don\u2019t really think that\u2019s an aspect of herself that De La Rocha is really going to want to have captured forever on canvas. We tried to explain why it might be a bad idea, but I\u2019m not sure that Julia was really listening to us. She had that look on her face like when she\u2019s planning something artistic. Shortly after that the ladies got back and we all went out for dinner at an Italian restaurant. It was pretty good. Lori for her part stayed close to De La Rocha throughout the whole meal and after. When we got back to the house Lori and De La Rocha went upstairs by themselves. Lori even skipped the performance tonight. Calamity did her usual wonderful job on stage.<br /> <br /> Later, at the bar, Molly had a question and decided that I was the best one to explain things to her. She wanted to know why Dr. Bright had seemed so upset during the meeting and why people, like Lori, were acting tense during it. I explained to her that people were nervous because De La Rocha was perhaps a little too close to being Maria and they sensed it. Her body language changed when she got closer to being the old Maria. Her eyes dilated. Her mannerisms changed. She was becoming a different person, and most people watching picked up on that. It seems that Molly didn\u2019t, so I explained a bit of what we saw, of what I saw. I told her about the creepy smile that Maria had on her face when she first took the mask off. I think she understood better when we were done talking. She was not happy with it, but she understood. She said that she should be better at picking up on subtleties that the rest of us saw, but she hadn\u2019t. It is her job to be a spy. She felt that she should be better able to pick up on stuff like that, and in this case, she didn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> I think tonight was the night that Calamity was going to go into the dreams of one of White Maria\u2019s parents and see if she could influence their opinions about arranged marriages. I\u2019ll have to ask her tomorrow how that goes.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Well, I can\u2019t say that today didn\u2019t start off interestingly. Everyone gathered for breakfast in the kitchen, as per usual. What wasn\u2019t as per usual was Desiree showing up completely naked. I\u2019m used to Lori and the others coming down only wearing t-shirts, but not completely nude. Well, there was that one time that Lori acted as a table for Julia to eat off of her body for the artist\u2019s birthday. That was the exception though. Most people took it in stride when Desiree came in undressed today. I was not the most comfortable person there though. And I could tell that Luna was not comfortable either. The others may be used to people just walking around naked, but I\u2019m not. I suppose it helps that Desiree has been the lover of most of the people in the motley aside from myself. I don\u2019t know who else she\u2019s slept with and to be honest I don\u2019t really want to know. I don\u2019t keep track of my friend\u2019s sex partners. Eventually Desiree took pity on those of us that were not overly thrilled at her state of undress and put a t-shirt on. <br /> <br /> But now it\u2019s time to finish packing and get ready for the camping trip today. I\u2019m looking forward this. I hope the others don\u2019t mind the snow.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXXXIV</i><br /> <br /> Not much behind the scenes to add. Twitch and DLR both had to make Resolve + Composure rolls, to deal with the phobia and maintain control respectively. Other PCs could make Empathy rolls to follow what was happening (with DLR, Twitch was pretty transparent.)<br /> <br /> Other stuff\u2026Stasia was tearing through doors working on seducing Elena at a good clip; she stopped because of Jacob. Though she may have been a bit irritated by his reactions. And Desiree being a Romancer (and Dancer) appeared nude and conforming to the desires of her audience. Maybe she was just defying Insincere Marguerite. Or maybe she was reminding the Motley just how desirable she is. Or maybe both.<br /> <br /> Calamity\u2019s Number was \u201cNight Shift\u201d by Siouxie and the Banshees, not covered as Lori was away. Lovely song, due note it is horribly NSFW if you check it out on Youtube.<br /> <br /> Okay, well that covers it, I think. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency<