 camping the rest of the day. The drive started with Stasia discussing with Calamity her desire to seduce Elena. Being sure Calamity \u201chad her back,\u201d a concept I find questionable. I mean, Calamity thinks she does. But she is very good at finding ways to double cross even dear friends while claiming to have their back. She does not really understand relationships, I find to be the kindest way to look on her. Anyway, ignoring that she did, in fact, betray Stasia proving I right (as she almost always does), Juliette got involved in the conversation sort of on Stasia\u2019s side, once it became clear Stasia had no intention of dirty tricks. <br /> <br /> Somehow this became a conversation about the Euro, and international borders and boarder controls in the European Union. I think Juliette brought up currency. We actually hit all sorts of subjects between Juliette asking if we were there yet. Our car was the family, Calamity, and Stasia, while the other was Jacob, Luna and Elena, so it was cozy.<br /> <br /> We set up camp, Julia and I to a tent, Juliette and Maria to a tent, Jacob and Luna to a tent, Calamity and Stasia to a tent and Elena on her own. We sang a good deal of Christmas songs. Well, I sang a good deal of Christmas songs, but most of us sang at least some Christmas songs and I did sing some in English. We fixed all sorts of food, had toilets way too far away, and Jacob made it snow. Very Christmassy. He was sort of standing guard when we went to bed, though based on Elena\u2019s demeanor Stasia did in fact get in her tent. Stasia was, of course, inscrutable. Jacob was, however, well aware.<br /> <br /> We returned in time to see Yvette the next day. I was glad to get back to the house. We prepared a bit and Yvette arrived. Looking lovely. I had a whole elaborate idea where the conversation would just be Juliette and I with her, but the Motley was there, and I was reluctant to have them leave, so they didn\u2019t, though Stasia was not present. I did not need my sordid past paraded in front of her.<br /> <br /> As I say Yvette was beautiful, of course. All dressed smart and very very French. She kept some distance, but seemed less nervous. I could write pages just over and over and over about the meeting, but the short version was she seemed happy but nervous to see me. Attracted but afraid. She was clearly torn between wanting to be close and wanting to feel safe, which I understand. I did my best to be affectionate and to reassure her. I got a few looks from people when I was more forward, but I had to do something, after all. <br /> <br /> In the end, we reluctantly separated. Calamity spoke with her, but both seemed encouraged by the conversation. She headed out through her mirror. The room, the building, was emptier for her being gone. I was emptier. But it is Christmas. I will not be brought down on Christmas. The Christmas spirit shall work for I!<br /> <br /> Afterwards, we went to work doing the show. I had a lot of time to think up in the rafters. It was difficult, but the puppets were there for I, as they always are, and we spoke at length. When the show finally ended, I wished them goodnight and went down to the floor. Julia had recruited Desiree, still playful as ever, for our evening. Juliette went with Oleander, and Maria had picked up Gloria. Desiree was all kisses even before we were upstairs. And once we were, she proved a most pleasant distraction for Julia and I. <br /> <br /> At least while awake. I think the vents, and my regrets, are calling my name.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXXXV</i><br /> <br /> Let\u2019s see, not much mechanically. Some survival rolls to see how fast tents went up. Insincere Marguerite absolutely abused the first clause of Separation to walk on everything but the ground (her frailty does not allow shoes on bare earth, not that she wears shoes) so that was interesting.<br /> <br /> Stasia is an absolute sledgehammer for getting through doors. Admittedly, Elena was not really rolling against her.<br /> <br /> Never mentioned, but a couple woke just before dawn to hear Julia singing <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Y0uNJp15p3M\" target=\"_blank\">O Willow Waly</a> (content warning: Maybe not the best choice to play alone in a dark room, actually forget what I said, do that.)<br /> <br /> I think that covers everything. Regardless comments and questions are welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T16:28:58-07:00","id":1111879,"title":"","content":"Ooooh Stasia, what have you wrought upon yourself? I doubt that Jacob will have much retribution for going back on the agreement, but the fact she did it at all, much less so soon and blatantly...well, suffice to say, she's in a spot of bother now. I'm a little surprised that Stasia's so willing to do so, too, given how careful she's been regarding Changelings and their lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T19:56:34-07:00","id":1111957,"title":"","content":"The sweet lure of the flesh makes pretty fools of us all. Except asexual and demisexuals, the lucky so and sos","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T11:57:40-07:00","id":1112257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play?p=1111879#post1111879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooooh Stasia, what have you wrought upon yourself? I doubt that Jacob will have much retribution for going back on the agreement, but the fact she did it at all, much less so soon and blatantly...well, suffice to say, she's in a spot of bother now. I'm a little surprised that Stasia's so willing to do so, too, given how careful she's been regarding Changelings and their lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a few complicating factors here. One is while Stasia did agree not to seduce Elena, it was informal, and non-descriptive, she never made a promise. It went something like.<br /> <br /> S: &quot;Hey Jacob, can I pick up Elena?&quot;<br /> J: &quot;No. I don't want you to do that&quot;<br /> S: &quot;Okay&quot;<br /> <br /> So she never exactly gave her word she wouldn't. She did not the night she asked. She acknowledged Jacob's answer. Jacob has claimed she promised not to, which is not true. Secondly, Elena both invited her in, and initiated festivities. Now, Stasia was basically responsible for this. Elena hasn't seduced anyone in her life before. In game terms, Stasia battered the doors and gave the suggestion. But this is all semantics. She slept with her when she knew Jacob would not approve. The one real thing on her side is, Elena was interested, and initiated contact after the initial meeting of her own accord. While Elena never told Jacob she was intrigued by Stasia, one often does not with a sibling. Jacob interpreted that as Elena being relieved Stasia was told no. All this happened before Stasia got through her doors. Elena found the roguish girl intriguing. None of that means this was a good idea, but it is significantly less cut and dry than Jacob makes it out to be. And at the end of the day, it is Elena's body, and Elena's heart to break.<br /> <br /> Now totally OOC, I talked about this with Jacob and Calamity's players before it happened. I wanted to ensure they were okay with things falling out this way. It was still possible Stasia would fail to seduce Elena, but very very unlikley. Elena was not even rolling to resist. It was a potential source of drama. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T13:19:03-07:00","id":1112299,"title":"","content":"Ah, now that makes a lot more sense. Promises and oaths are sancrosanct for Changelings, but this is certianly more of a grey area. I like the mistakes made in-character regarding it, too. I wonder how it's going to play out...<br /> <br /> Also, I know that this is probaly something that doesn't need to be said, but I'm really happy that there's a GM who talks with the group before introducing drama into the mix. I've learned from experience that drama in the wrong place that splinter a gaming group, and just...yeah. Thumbs up to the Baroness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T13:36:16-07:00","id":1112893,"title":"","content":"I appreciate the comment.<br /> <br /> This had a lot of potential to be twitchy; I do not worry about my group, we cooperate very well, but there were several variables involved. One, it involves directly the two members with the fewest compunctions about fighting (or killing) people.For anouther, it involved someone Jacob's character created and of whom Jacob is protective, and that can be a sensitive topic depending on relationships. But it all worked out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T01:51:43-07:00","id":1115849,"title":"","content":"I m surprised how blase Lori was about it. I also have to wonder how cool everyone would have been if Stasia had been male.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T06:28:12-07:00","id":1115920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play?p=1115849#post1115849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I m surprised how blase Lori was about it. I also have to wonder how cool everyone would have been if Stasia had been male.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is a very good point that I hope Jacob will bring up. Age is not just a number. It has meaning in power differentials. Power differentials that are more visible to society when a man has more power, but are present in all relationships","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 07-14-2017, 09:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T07:46:05-07:00","id":1115943,"title":"","content":"Omenseer,<br /> <br /> Just to be clear on this point, Lori is <i>not</i> okay on any level with someone being forced or coerced into sexual activity. Seduction is more of a grey area with her... she employs it herself, and usually thinks of it as harmless fun. To her mind, Stasia isn't really doing anything wrong... Elena seems to <i>want</i> what's happening to happen, at least on some level. While it's true that Elena might not be emotionally prepared for the whirlwind one-night stand that Stasia intends, she's legally an adult, and will never lose that naivet\u00e9 if she doesn't get some real-life experience at some point. Stasia wasn't forcing herself on Elena, or trying to get her drunk or stoned prior to the seduction attempt. She &quot;played fair,&quot; so there's no harm, no foul to Lori's mind.<br /> <br /> As far as Lori is concerned, gender doesn't really enter in to the equation here. She'd feel much the same way if Calamity's friend had been Stephen rather than Stasia. Elena. Is. An. Adult. She can make her own decisions, and should be allowed to make her own mistakes. And yes, I know that this is a na\u00efve and simplistic view of the situation, but that's the character.<br /> <br /> Lori is also an only child, and while she gets Jacob's desire to protect his sister, she doesn't really have anything like a sibling bond in her life for comparison. She thinks he's just being overprotective and sheltering Elena too much.<br /> <br /> In all honesty, the truth of the situation probably falls somewhere between Lori and Jacob's opinions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T12:49:57-07:00","id":1116071,"title":"","content":"I think it\u2019s an interesting question, and there is a lot to unpack. Note at no point am I speculating on what Lori is/should be okay with.<br /> <br /> I think, in general, in the 2010, yes, non-bigots are going to be more okay with a woman seducing someone than a man. And I think there are valid and non-valid reasons for this.<br /> <br /> Sex initiated by women is less likely to involve some form of coercion, statistically speaking (since we are looking at this from outside not having seen the specifics of conversation.) That\u2019s not to say (because I have to, despite it being obvious) all men do this. I know lots of men who don\u2019t. Most, at least I hope. Second, a woman with a woman is more an even risk between two parties. Unless one of the women is a transwoman who both hasn\u2019t had surgery and isn\u2019t on HRT, pregnancy is not a risk between women. STD risk is equal. And women don\u2019t have the social status above other women that men often do.<br /> <br /> OTOH, a lot of people are less okay with men due to a false perception it is dirtier or one sided (automatically) if a man is involved. Or just that men wanting a hookup are somehow taking advantage in a way women are not. It\u2019s weird and unfair. They conflate men with PUAs, when most men are not that breed. Or the whole conquest thing. And not only does the attitude demonize men, it removes women\u2019s agency. Like she can\u2019t choose to hook up with a man.<br /> <br /> All that said, this is the view in Southern California in a queer friendly area in modern day, or by enlightened people talking online (I am in NC, not exactly a bastion of tolerance, though I am essentially in a city). Broadly speaking? It would be viewed as worse. Much worse. An evil predatory lesbian corrupting a straight girl. The lesbian is a slut so now this other girl is a strumpet too. The predatory lesbian is a trope, and an awful one, and one all too many would read into the situation.<br /> <br /> And let\u2019s unpack something else. Say Elena is Alan. Being seduced by a woman. Would people object to that? More than this? Less? In my experience, that would be okay, assuming Stasia is not her teacher or boss. And in this case it is a magazine photographer and a college student, so no real world power differential beyond one is early 30s the other 19.<br /> <br /> Me? I think any combination of genders should be able to hook up if they want, and it is is consensual and non coercive. Punishing men for hookups is as stupid as punishing women for them.<br /> <br /> And to be fair, in at least the LBT women\u2019s community, you see more relationships with larger gaps, because statistically a huge number of women who identify as LBT are under 25. If I wanted to hook up with a girl, odds are I would have more luck with a woman under 30, not because I am ageist, but because most girls who are open to themselves about being into girls are under 30. The numbers are not close; it\u2019s over twice as likely as my age group. LBT women have also traditionally been a smaller dating pool, doublely since Biphobia and Transphobia are sadly still things. And annoying realities like Bi women were often punished for getting involved with women and rewarded for men (and even now, \u201cwill my family talk to me\u201d can be a deciding factor, according to some) and, because of how generations affect attitudes, more bi women are going to have family who are okay with it who are younger.<br /> <br /> Now, I don\u2019t see what transpired between Stasia and Elena as innately good or bad. Stasia did go against her acknowledging Jacob did not want the hookup, and her implied agreement, though she never actually promised. It\u2019s a dick move. On the other hand, I firmly believe no family member should be able to step in and deny a family member\u2019s right to date someone else if everyone involved are adults. There are so many stories of family members denying people the right to see same sex lovers you could cry, though this is not necessarily the case (Though Jacob did declare Elena is not into women for her). To me, at the end of the day, it\u2019s a hookup.<br /> <br /> I think it is an interesting conversation though. As I said at the beginning, there is a lot to unpack. I think it is good the game brought it out and made people think. As I say so very often, \u201cIt\u2019s complicated.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T13:17:17-07:00","id":1116077,"title":"","content":"&quot;It's complicated&quot;: See Life.<br /> <br /> Also, the predatory Lesbian thing you mentioned had not occurred to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","user":"omenseer","date":". 07-14-2017, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T13:18:16-07:00","id":1116078,"title":"","content":"I forgot the part about Jacob assuming his sister was straight Yeah, both sides are working on one or another shitty social assumptions. But ain't that just a big ol' CofD setting theme right there: no one has all the answers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T14:15:56-07:00","id":1116109,"title":"","content":"Omenseer: Pretty much. Sooner folks figure out life is complicated the better. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Master Aquatosic: Indeed. Part of what makes it interesting<br /> <br /> <br /> And thanks all in this discussion for mature and intelligent commentary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T12:32:14-07:00","id":1116942,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s Winter Solstice, and the Winter Court takes control of the city. And that means a party. And our Dream House friends will be part of it.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LXXXVI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Christmas Day is just around the corner, and the excitement is almost palpable in the air\u2026 particularly whenever Marguerite is present, but I think we all feel it to some degree. I think I\u2019m just about done putting the finishing touches on my presents for everyone. It\u2019s difficult to work on them without any of my friends or lovers finding out what I\u2019m up to, but I\u2019ve been able to grab a spare moment here and there. I hope they\u2019ll take the gifts in the spirit in which they\u2019re intended\u2026 as something that I\u2019m putting my heart and soul into, rather than something I\u2019m spending a lot of money on. I think the motley will get it\u2026 I\u2019ve never been particularly stingy with my money in the first place, and I wanted to do something <u><u>truly</u></u> special for my closest friends instead of just dropping cash on a designer handbag or something.<br /> <br /> Though I admit, I saw an <u><u>adorable</u></u> handbag that would look <u><u>perfect</u></u> on Gawain\u2019s shoulder the other day\u2026<br /> <br /> Ahem. In any case, Oleander was a good sport about getting up early on Sunday to join me at church. It was the Christmas service, of course, and Dad had asked me weeks ago to do a solo befitting the season. I decided to go with \u201cO Holy Night,\u201d as it\u2019s always been one of my favorite holiday songs. It practically screams Christmas, but plays up the religious significance of the holiday rather than the secular aspects. Plus\u2026 I admit that it doesn\u2019t hurt that it gave me the chance to show off a little bit, as it requires a vocal range (and a set of pipes) not often displayed in your average church choir. So that was a blast.<br /> <br /> I got a standing ovation for my rendition, which was a little unusual for our sleepy little Methodist church, but I took it with a smile and a nod that wasn\u2019t quite a bow (it didn\u2019t seem appropriate given the venue). I also got a very pleasant surprise when I looked out to locate Oleander among the congregation\u2026 Marguerite had slipped in at some point. She was standing a few rows back from Oleander and applauding with the rest. I threw her a toothy smile to let her know that I\u2019d noticed her and appreciated her presence.<br /> <br /> I looked for her after the conclusion of the service, but she was nowhere to be found. I guess she must have slipped out quietly with the rest of the congregation as I was changing out of my choir robes. Dad commented on her presence (she had shaken his hand on her way out), and I made plans to join him for at least one meal later this week\u2026 possibly dragging Maria along with me, depending on her mood. Christmas with my Dad! I never would have thought it possible a few months ago.<br /> <br /> Oleander joined us briefly for sex breakfast after driving me back to the Dream House, but she couldn\u2019t stay for long, as she had a few things to take care of before the big coronation later that evening. I made sure to thank Marguerite for coming out to support me at the church that morning, and she said \u201cyou are welcome\u201d with a shy little smile. D had spent the evening in Gloria\u2019s company, and the two of them seemed to have enjoyed themselves, which\u2026 my God, I think that fact is actually starting to make me <u><u>happy</u></u> now. I guess I\u2019ve come a long way over the past few weeks. Getting over the thing with Spidertoes probably helped a lot.<br /> <br /> I spent most of the rest of the afternoon hanging out with my girls and getting ready for the party that evening. D was opting for a casual approach, but I figured that since I\u2019d be performing it would only be right to dress up a little. I put on a sparkly sky blue evening gown that showed off my curves. Someone at the coronation even wryly referred to me as \u201cElsa\u201d at one point, so I guess the reference wasn\u2019t lost on people.<br /> <br /> The coronation itself was fun! I opened the festivities with a song at Boss Lowjack\u2019s request. He\u2019d asked me to put my own spin on Simon and Garfunkel\u2019s \u201cA Hazy Shade of Winter,\u201d which seemed appropriate given the circumstances. When he made the request, he specifically mentioned a remake from the 80s with which I was unfamiliar, so I looked it up. The Bangles sort of jazzed up the song a bit, adding electric guitar to the instrumental portions and upping the tempo, but the beautiful core melody remained the same. I\u2019ve always liked that song; personally I think it\u2019s one of Paul Simon\u2019s better efforts.<br /> <br /> I began to regret my decision to wear a tight evening dress after a while. For one thing, it was pretty cold at the coronation, and I hadn\u2019t brought a coat. Of course, D came to my rescue pretty quickly, tossing her leather jacket around my shoulders (I had to fold up my wings, of course, but it was a nice gesture). It was warm, and it smelled like her, which was nice.<br /> <br /> One of the reasons it was so cold at the coronation is that the event was held at an ice skating rink. Now, there was no way in hell that I was going to get out there and make a fool of myself in that dress. Though I\u2019m not a bad ice skater, I was most certainly <u><u>not</u></u> attired appropriately for the activity. Most of the others got out there at one point or another, though. Jacob and Luna just looked like they were having a good time, but Marguerite and Calamity couldn\u2019t resist strutting their stuff and showing off for the crowd.<br /> <br /> D and Julia kept me company on the sidelines; neither of them wanted to get in the way of whatever private competition Marguerite and Calamity had going. We spent most of the evening people-watching, honestly. Most of the Freehold was there, and I passed a few pleasant words with just about everyone. I got to see Joan and Andromeda, which was nice\u2026 they seemed just as happy as ever. Oh, and Flores came by to say hello too, which is always fun.<br /> <br /> I did ask Boss Lowjack if he\u2019d mind if I sang another number, and he gave me the \u201cbe my guest\u201d gesture. So while many of my friends were gliding and twirling around on the ice, I lilted my way through \u201cWinter Wonderland.\u201d So I guess I got a secular Christmas classic in on Sunday as well. What can I say? I love this season! I mean, maybe not as much as Marguerite does, but still.<br /> <br /> As things were winding down, it looked like Flores was going to come home and spend the evening with the four of us. After a while, I noticed Calamity subtly pointing Stasia in our direction as well. As her bestie seemed intrigued by the notion of forming a sextet with us, we allowed as how that would be fine. At the time I wondered why Calamity would do that\u2026 but in hindsight I\u2019m guessing that she planned to spend the evening with Becky and didn\u2019t want Stasia to have to ride home with Jacob (who was still sore about the whole seducing his sister thing).<br /> <br /> So that\u2019s how the rest of my evening went. I know I write this a fair amount, but honestly the rest of the night passed in a sort of haze of pleasure and flesh. Flores and Stasia seemed to get along really well, but then again, I guess that\u2019s not really surprising where Flores is concerned.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m sure we all looked particularly smug as we descended to sex breakfast on Monday morning. I mean, it\u2019s hard <u><u>not</u></u> to look smug when you\u2019re walking downstairs in the company of five beautiful women in various states of dishabille. As usual, D and I sort of paired off as we got to the kitchen, and Julia claimed most of Marguerite\u2019s attention. Flores and Stasia remained aloof (well, as aloof as Flores ever gets, at least).<br /> <br /> Not much else to talk about as far as that breakfast goes\u2026 aside from the fact that Jacob took Stasia aside to have a little talk, presumably about her intentions toward his sister. I don\u2019t know what was said in that little private conference, and to be perfectly honest, I don\u2019t want to know. Stasia seemed okay after they both returned, in any case. I personally think Jacob\u2019s taking this overprotective brother thing a little further than he should\u2026 but it\u2019s none of my business, so I\u2019ve kept my mouth shut on the subject. Y\u2019know, mostly.<br /> <br /> The rest of the day was sort of a lazy stretch for me. It was Monday, so we had movie night to look forward to, and got to put aside the hustle and bustle of our usual pre-show routines. D had to go to work, of course, and I once again brought up the possibility that she could quit her job at the hospital and come to work for us at the Dream House full time.<br /> <br /> She sighed. \u201cI\u2019d like that, babe, I really would,\u201d she said earnestly, \u201cand I swear I\u2019m thinking about it. But the problem is, if I quit my job as an X-ray tech, and then ever wanted to go <u><u>back</u></u> to that sort of work, it would be a real pain in the ass to get recertified.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded sympathetically. \u201cI get it,\u201d I said, \u201cI hadn\u2019t thought about that side of things. I\u2019m just, well\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> She quirked an eyebrow at me. \u201cWhat?\u201d she asked gently.<br /> <br /> I looked away, sure I was blushing twelve shades of crimson. \u201cI\u2019m just imagining a time when I <u><u>don\u2019t</u></u> have to say goodbye to you three days out of every week,\u201d I mumbled, probably nearly incoherent.<br /> <br /> She chuckled. \u201cI\u2019ll give it some more thought,\u201d she promised as I walked her to the door. \u201cOr, you know, you could get your ass into a local college and start working on that medical degree you\u2019re always talking about. Then one of these days I could work at <u><u>your</u></u> office.\u201d<br /> <br /> That gave me pause for thought, even if it was obviously intended as a joke. I mean, even assuming I could get into a pre-Med program at a local college, I\u2019d have at least six or seven years of school before I could even get a residency anywhere, let alone set up my own practice. And that\u2019s assuming I could go to school full-time, which is\u2026 not incredibly likely considering my commitment to the Dream House, my plans to rescue Missy and Jane, and the possibility (however small) that I might need to take over the position of Spring Queen sometime within the next few years.<br /> <br /> Still\u2026 medicine <u><u>does</u></u> call to me as a profession, and most of those obligations aren\u2019t going anywhere, so\u2026 isn\u2019t it time I got my ass in gear and started taking the first steps?<br /> <br /> In any case, D left me on the doorstep with a kiss and a promise that she would seriously consider the possibility of coming to work for the Dream House full-time as security. I wandered upstairs, where I found Julia painting a portrait of Flores, with Marguerite lazing languidly off to one side. It seemed like a peaceful environment, so I grabbed a textbook from my room, returned to the attic, and sprawled out on a sofa to read.<br /> <br /> It seemed like no time at all had passed before D was back and it was time for movie night to begin. As Calamity had missed the previous week\u2019s selection of holiday comedy classics, she selected a couple of her own favorite Christmas movies for us to view this week. And, well\u2026 I mean, the movies weren\u2019t bad or anything\u2026 and they both took place at Christmas-time, so I guess they qualified, but\u2026 let\u2019s just say that Marguerite was <u><u>not</u></u> well pleased by the selections.<br /> <br /> The first film was called <u><u>Gremlins</u></u>, and was a sort of horror-comedy mishmash from the 80s about these tiny, mischievous creatures who are prone to transforming into real monsters based on nonsensical dietary restrictions. Like, they can\u2019t eat anything after midnight. I tried to raise a few logical questions about how ludicrous that particular aspect of the film was, but apparently that nit has been well and truly picked on the Internet over the past twenty years or so, and Julia had a quick response to each of my hypothetical queries on the subject.<br /> <br /> Honestly, the film wasn\u2019t bad once you just accepted certain concepts as a given. There were one or two really effective jump-scares late in the film that had me clinging to my honey and squealing in alarm, though by and large the film seemed to be a comedy. There was one truly horrific scene, in which the main character\u2019s love interest describes the <u><u>awful</u></u> reason why she doesn\u2019t like the Christmas season. I saw Marguerite discreetly remove herself from the media room as that scene came up. She returned a short while later, and seemed to be okay again.<br /> <br /> The second film was a straight-out action movie (also from the 80s) called <u><u>Die Hard</u></u>. It\u2019s about a New York cop who travels to LA on Christmas Eve in the hopes of reconciling with his estranged wife. He gets caught up in a hostage situation, and is forced to prove what a badass he is by taking down all of the bad guys pretty much single-handedly. The main villain was played by Alan Rickman, whom I remembered from that <u><u>Robin Hood</u></u> movie we watched a few months ago (heh\u2026 buttcakes!). And the hero was played by Bruce Willis, whom I have seen in a few other things over the past year, as he\u2019s fairly prolific.<br /> <br /> So we talked about quite a few things as the final credits rolled. I\u2019d never heard of taking off your shoes and making \u201cfists\u201d with your feet in pile carpet as a cure for jetlag, so I posited that this was just something the writers dreamed up so that the hero would have to pick broken glass out of his bare feet later in the film. Marguerite wanted to make the (perfectly valid) point that just because a film is set during the month of December, that does not make it a \u201cChristmas film\u201d per se. Julia, on the other hand, seemed personally outraged by the fact that Bruce Willis was seen as something of a sex symbol when the film was originally released.<br /> <br /> So we talked about that for a while. I didn\u2019t get the big deal, honestly. I mean, he wasn\u2019t like an Adonis or anything, but he had a hard body and a certain rough charisma that was very appealing. I wouldn\u2019t kick him out of bed\u2026 not that this is setting the bar particularly high, I\u2019ll admit. But most of the others seemed to agree with me on that score. Calamity thought his badass-ness made up for his lack of conventional good looks. D came down on my side, stating that while Mr. Willis might not have been a Chippendales dancer or anything, there is a certain appeal to the strength the character exhibited. And Luna just shrugged and admitted that she used to have something of a crush on the man in any case.<br /> <br /> Julia eventually gave up the argument, which was probably wise on her part, as I think the group as a whole was about ten seconds away from using the discussion to tease her about being one of the only true lesbians in the House. I hope she realizes that we only tease her because we care about her. God, I love her so much, I\u2019d hate to think that I was actually making her feel bad over something like that. My relationship with Julia tends to get overlooked sometimes compared to the deep eternal feelings I share with my soul mate and the drama that often surrounds my relationship with my French lover. But that doesn\u2019t mean my feelings for Julia are any less profound, or any less real. I may be marrying Maria, but I fully intend to share the rest of my life with all three of them, and Oleander too if she wants it.<br /> <br /> We also talked for a bit about shaking things up for our last show before Christmas (which is\u2026 technically later today, as I write this). Marguerite and I are going to do a duet, and Marguerite and Calamity are going to share a number as well\u2026 but I\u2019ll write about the specifics of those acts in my next entry, so I can write about how they went over. I think Calamity is also going to reprise her \u201cMistress for Christmas\u201d number, and I\u2019ll probably roll out \u201cSanta Baby\u201d again too. I think I\u2019m looking forward to the show almost as much as Marguerite is, though of course she\u2019s grumbling about \u201clast minute substitutions\u201d and \u201cneeding the practice.\u201d<br /> <br /> I swear, at this time of year she is absolutely <u>adorable</u>!<br /> <br /> So the four of us retired to our chambers after that, by which I mean Marguerite and Julia\u2019s room\u2026 for some reason I can never convince the Darklings to join me in my own bedroom, what with the big picture window opening up on the balcony and all. After a relatively sedate round of lovemaking, the three of them have finally drifted off, and as per usual, I\u2019ve been reading medical journals, writing in this diary, and musing \u2018pon the mysteries of life while I listen to them breathe.<br /> <br /> Christmas is coming\u2026 my one and only Christmas as Lorelei Grace, assuming I go ahead with my plans to take D\u2019s last name. I guess I\u2019d better make the most of it.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> Tuesday, December 23<sup>rd</sup><br /> Nine years, five months, twenty-nine days<br /> Days without stabbing: 8<br /> <br /> I am quite the contented little monster this morning. I am sitting on the floor beside the bed writing so I can lean back and let Beautiful\u2019s hair nuzzle my neck. It\u2019s so soft\u2026 like Their touch but warm rather than cold. I really don\u2019t want to leave her and go to therapy but it\u2019s important. And avoiding Jacob won\u2019t make this business with our sisters go away. I really do wish Stasia hadn\u2019t gone after Elena so soon after telling Jacob she wouldn\u2019t. I mean, if I\u2019m being honest here, part of it is that I\u2019m jealous. But I get that he\u2019s worried about his sister and I know all to well how adverse Stasia is to relationships. Elena\u2019s a nice girl. She\u2019s sweet and innocent. I don\u2019t think anyone knows the difference between love and lust at that point (or even that there is one) and I think he\u2019s right that she\u2019s going to get her heart broken at least a little. I just hope it doesn\u2019t end messy and make things awkward. I\u2019ll talk to him on the way to the clinic and see where we stand. Perhaps we can avoid the inevitable breakup from being a bad one. I do hope so. Jacob and I are particularly close and I\u2019d hate for that to change.<br /> <br /> Mmm\u2026. Man it was so nice to have Beautiful all to myself yesterday. It really is unfortunate that her position as Claviger keeps her busy so much of the time. We do gets a few nights together (and oh what nights they are\u2026.) but spending a whole day relaxing and playing games and just walking the pier hand in hand and laughing together was really wonderful. I kinda wish Handsome could have joined us but he\u2019s been rather scarce of late. I am not sure just what he\u2019s been up to but I\u2019m a little worried. I mean, he claims to be busy but I\u2019ve seen him working and he\u2019s never quite so keen on being alone when he\u2019s on something. I guess he might be scrambling to finish his holiday gifts but\u2026 I just don\u2019t know there isn\u2019t the eagerness or excitement that he gets when he\u2019s focused on a project. Something\u2019s bothering him and he\u2019s keeping it from me. I don\u2019t like it but for now at least all I can do is give him the space he clearly needs and wait.<br /> <br /> At least I\u2019m not idle. The plan to get White Maria out of her arranged marriage (When exactly did my life become a Korean soap opera?) is actually coming together. She\u2019s going to give her parents my number as her wedding planner. Lori and I will be meeting them since Lori can speak convincingly about wedding stuff and back me up. Once White Maria\u2019s mother starts to talk over and take over it will give me the opening to bring up her total disregard for her daughter\u2019s wishes. I just need to pull the whole Inception bit on her father before then. I should have done that last night but there was a dragon that needed to be slain\u2026 several times. And it\u2019s not like we\u2019ll meet up till after Christmas so I have time.<br /> <br /> Mmm\u2026 and speaking of dragons\u2026 I have a little time before I need to head down to meet Jacob and someone is awake and dragging her claws along my glass...<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Today started like most Sundays. Lori came back from church all dressed up with her hair pulled back and wearing her glasses. This morning was a little different though. It seems that Insincere Marguerite went to the church to listen to Lori sing. I\u2019m assuming that it was because this was going to be the big Christmas sermon. Marguerite seemed pleased with herself and Lori was her usual happy self. And then there was breakfast. Insincere Marguerite was lounging across the laps of Desiree and Julia. De La Rocha was there with Gloria and Oleander was with Lori. Apparently Lori spent the night at Oleander\u2019s place and the pair went to church this morning. They both came back to the Dream House for breakfast. I like Oleander. She is a nice person.<br /> <br /> Not much else happened this morning, but this afternoon was definitely more busy. Today was the day that Lowjack was going to get crowned as reigning monarch of the freehold. Everyone got dressed up nice. Most people went with fairly laid back nice outfits. Lori wore a spangled blue dress, Stasia wore a suit, Luna and I wore slacks and a nice shirt. Calamity though dressed up in something a little more showy than the rest of us. She decided to wear the \u201cWicked Queen\u201d dress, with the plunging neckline and high collar. I\u2019m not sure what prompted her to go all out for this event. She doesn\u2019t even like Boss Lowjack. She might have worn it to conceal the knives that she brought with her. Not to harm anyone mind, just to show off with Jack.<br /> <br /> Jack made his usual outrageous entrance. He ice skated across the rink, dancing as he went. Then Calamity threw a knife at Jack and he caught the blade in his teeth. They must have practiced that. After he caught the knife he jumped off the ice rink and skateboarded through the crowd. He came back once the music was done. Not the flashiest thing that he\u2019s done in the Freehold, but it was definitely a \u201cJack\u201d entrance.<br /> <br /> Once everything calmed down Tamara opened the ceremony with a few words and introduced Lori, who had agreed to sing a song for the occasion. She sang \u201cHazy Shade of Winter.\u201d I thought it was pretty good, and given the applause after she was done, the rest of the crowd agreed. Lowjack made a short speech about the change of power and his role in the Freehold. After that Lori sang \u201cWinter Wonderland\u201d while people ice skated on the rink that had been set up for this event. Luna and I went skating. Neither of us was particularly showing off, we were just skating for the fun of it. Calamity however decided that she wanted to show off and skated really well on the other end of the rink. She was doing twirls and jumps pretty well in that long dress of hers. Insincere Marguerite also skated really well, but she stayed away from Calamity so neither would show the other one up. It worked out. Both women got to show off their stuff on the ice. They seemed to be enjoying themselves too, which is the important part.<br /> <br /> After skating I wandered around and talked to a few people. I complemented Tamara on her introduction and spent some time talking to Molly. For her part Molly has been doing well. She hasn\u2019t been up to anything particularly interesting, just the usual. We talked for just a bit before going our separate ways. After that Lowjack came up to me and asked to speak to me in private. He then asked if I would be willing to be a part of his emergency response team in case something should happen in the Freehold. He said that he needed people that he could trust and that were capable to be a part of the team. I believe that Molly and Vik are also a part of this group. Lowjack also said that if anything should happen I was more than welcome to invite Calamity to come along and help. He said that he didn\u2019t want to talk to Calamity about it since she is oath bound to serve the Winter Court and he didn\u2019t want it to come across as an order. He just wanted her to be involved if she wanted to. I told him that I would be honored to be a part of the team and that I\u2019d pass along the message to Calamity.<br /> <br /> When it was time to leave, Calamity went home with Becky, but not before setting it up so Stasia went home with Lori, the rest of the trio and Flores. I think that she was trying to keep Stasia from being alone with me just in case I was still sore about what happened on the camping trip. I will give her credit for being loyal to her friend. It\u2019s just frustrating when she keeps supporting her friend without thought to how her actions or the actions of her friend will affect others. I thought I could trust Calamity, and I guess for most things I can, but when it comes to Stasia her friend will always come first.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Sometimes I\u2019m not sure how we get onto the topics we do at breakfast. It came up that Calamity is grumpy much of the time during the day. She defended herself saying that she is a Darkling and that her reactions to things are based on that distinction. It seems to fit. Rook was a Darkling, and he was frequently short or seemingly cold with people during the day. He was just much more comfortable at night and thus more personable. I got to see both sides of my partner on many occasions. We carried out missions for the Lady during the day and night. It just depended on Her whim or what was more appropriate to carrying out our orders. I guess the same could be said for Calamity. She does her job during the day or night depending on need, and is friendly for the most part, but can be a bit \u201cgrumpy\u201d sometimes. It also depends on circumstances, but I suppose that\u2019s true for all of us. What is happening around us dictates how we act or react to things.<br /> <br /> After breakfast Julia and Flores went upstairs to do some painting. At least Julia was going to paint her guest, possibly to be used as a decoration on the Dream House walls or maybe for the Rose and Thorn, I\u2019m not sure which. The talk of paint continued and the idea of body painting came up. Calamity suggested that they do something with body painting on stage. That idea wasn\u2019t necessarily tabled, but it was dropped after a few minutes. And that somehow brought up the idea of Julia and De La Rocha doing something on stage at some point. I\u2019m not sure why that came up, but I was under the impression that it had come up before and was just being reintroduced to the group for consideration.<br /> <br /> Stasia had left the conversation near the end and I left to go find her. I wanted to have a private word with her without getting sidelined by Calamity trying to keep her friend \u201csafe.\u201d So, I finally caught up with her and we had a chat. I expressed my displeasure at her breaking her word to me. Stasia for her part was vague about whether or not she had actually slept with Elena or not. She said that she doesn\u2019t discuss who she has sex with to anyone. She doesn\u2019t want to damage anyone\u2019s reputation, nor does she want to put someone at risk by revealing a relationship that some people might disagree with. I conceded that point. I can understand that, but the main sticking point for me was that we had an agreement and she ignored it. She did say flat out that she did not seduce Elena but would not say anything more on the matter. I don\u2019t know if I believe her entirely. She was flirting heavily with Elena all day and into the night. She could have instigated things. I have no way of knowing. I know that Elena will not discuss this matter with me. She would be too embarrassed and it would be awkward anyway. Stasia might have just done a whole lot of flirting and let Elena make the first move. Then technically she would not have seduced my sister. It\u2019s all semantics. If Stasia hadn\u2019t been flirting so heavily with Elena then it\u2019s likely that nothing would have happened. She may not have directly seduced her or instigated things, but she certainly manipulated the situation to end the way she wanted it to.<br /> <br /> Now, I acknowledge that Elena is an adult and can make her own decisions. I am mainly upset that Stasia went against her word. We did not make an oath or anything, but we had a verbal agreement. She asked if she could seduce my sister. I said no, that it would make things awkward, and she said \u201cokay.\u201d I took that to mean that she would back off and stop flirting so heavily with Elena. Apparently, what it meant was that she would not directly seduce my sister, she would just manipulate Elena into seducing her. Stasia has not confirmed that is what happened and nor will she, but from Elena\u2019s demeanor I\u2019m assuming that is what occurred.<br /> <br /> After the conversation with Stasia I went to go find Luna and told her about what was going on. She agreed with Stasia\u2019s policy of not talking about the people that she sleeps with. I really do understand that. It\u2019s to keep people\u2019s reputations intact and keep them safe. My point of contention is Stasia breaking her word, however informally it was given. I mean what was the point of her even asking me how I felt about it if she wasn\u2019t going to listen to what I said? So, I vented to Luna for a bit about the whole mess. Luna asked if I wanted her to go talk to Elena about what happened with Stasia. I said no for the moment. It would just embarrass Elena and I don\u2019t want her to feel bad about anything that happened.<br /> <br /> Later in the afternoon Calamity went to the pier with Becky. I guess they are trying to make up for not seeing much of one another recently. While they were gone Insincere Marguerite skipped through the house singing Christmas carols in French and handing out flowers to everyone in the Dream House, changeling and human alike. She was in a very good mood. She really does love this season.<br /> <br /> Once everyone gathered back at the house we got \u201cmovie night\u201d underway. We watched Gremlins and Die Hard. While not explicitly Christmas movies, they do have holiday elements in them and so they were deemed worthy of the holiday movie night. Insincere Marguerite was a little more critical of them being holiday movies, but she stayed with us to watch them nonetheless. She was especially upset about the fact that McClain was barefoot through most of the movie and ended up walking over broken glass with his bare feet. Marguerite was a bit sensitive about that, seeing as she walks barefoot pretty much all of the time. Lori then made some comment about the actor using stunt feet to walk over the glass, which led to conversations about the stunt butt in Prince of Thieves, which led to the whole butt cake thing. I have some strange friends.<br /> <br /> Conversation then came around to Insincere Marguerite and Calamity doing a number tomorrow based on the children\u2019s movie \u201cHow the Grinch Stole Christmas.\u201d Marguerite would dress up as a \u201cWho\u201d from the movie in her stripy socks, and sit up on a wall singing the main song. Calamity would then come slinking on stage painted green and wearing the Grinch\u2019s outfit. They also talked about Insincere Marguerite and Lori doing a duet of the song \u201cBaby it\u2019s Cold Outside.\u201d Insincere Marguerite was a bit nervous about performing with so little prep time so Calamity suggested that Marguerite make a pledge with her to give her a boost to her singing ability for the last performance of the year. It sounded like Insincere Marguerite was going to take her up on the offer. Regardless of any oaths made, I know that Insincere Marguerite will do just fine on stage.<br /> <br /> And that\u2019s about it for the day. I\u2019m fairly certain that the others think that I\u2019m over reacting to the whole thing with Stasia and Elena, and maybe I am to some extent, but I don\u2019t think I\u2019m completely off base here. It\u2019s about the agreement. I don\u2019t have any problem with Elena sleeping with another woman. I may think that she will probably get hurt when she realizes that Stasia is in it for the one night stand only, but I don\u2019t think I\u2019m off base for not wanting to see my sister get hurt. As I\u2019ve told Stasia, the thing that bothered me the most was her breaking her word. Granted this was not a life and death situation, but why would she bother asking my opinion on the matter if she had no intention of following through with my wishes? Yes, I realize that technically she may not have seduced my sister, which means she didn\u2019t technically break her word, but it\u2019s all semantics at that point. She knew that I didn\u2019t want her to keep flirting with Elena or to sleep with her. She knew how I felt about the whole matter. She just didn\u2019t care.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know what to do. I have talked to her and expressed my dissatisfaction with her actions but I wasn\u2019t planning on drawing it out much further than that. I know that Calamity would get involved to protect her friend and I don\u2019t want tensions to come up between us. She is one of the few people that I can be myself with and not have to worry about showing too much of the monster. But she is good friends with Stasia and we might lose something of what we have if I pursue things with Stasia. It\u2019s just going to be hard. I consider myself a man of his word. I try very hard not to make promises that I can\u2019t keep. It was essential in the Lady\u2019s realm to keep your word. Her realm could be very dangerous and it was important to know who you could trust and who you couldn\u2019t. I\u2019m not completely na\u00efve. I didn\u2019t necessarily trust everyone that gave me their word, but it really mattered when it came to working with Rook and the other Knights. We had to be able to trust one another. If Rook promised to meet me at a certain place and time, he would be there. If he promised not to do something he wouldn\u2019t do it. I was conducting an experiment one time with someone who\u2019d found their way into the Lady\u2019s realm. The young man, thinking that I was a friend, promised to return my knife once he came back from hunting. I wanted to see if he\u2019d actually do it. So, I made Rook promise not to kill the man regardless of what happened. The man could have turned on me and try to kill me with my own blade, or he could make a run for it, counting himself lucky enough to have fooled me. I wanted to see what he\u2019d do. He ran. They almost always run.<br /> <br /> And now I have this situation with Stasia. I can\u2019t trust her word; that much is certain. I won\u2019t try and elicit any more promises or agreements out of her. She won\u2019t keep it if it doesn\u2019t suit her to. It\u2019s too bad things didn\u2019t go better with her. It\u2019s funny. Rook would have kept his word if he had promised to stay away from this Freehold. He would have stayed away. I would have never seen my brother again and he his, but he would have kept his word. And he was the \u201cvillain.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> So I am going to be back on stage tomorrow night. The big Christmas show.<br /> <br /> First doing \u201cYou\u2019re a Mean One, Mr. Grinch\u201d with Calamity. I am going to be wearing stripy socks and striped top, sitting on the bit of brick wall scenery., while Calamity dances. She will be in green body paint and\u2026costume to be determined, but probably Domme-oriented. I will have to do a different approach to vocals, as my voice will not go really, really low. But I am sure I can purr something out.<br /> <br /> Then \u201cBaby It\u2019s Cold Outside\u201d with Juliette. I will be the Wolf, Juliette the Mouse. We will both be in Santa hats, I think, but costumes to be determined. We discussed hot pants and a suit jacket and tails for I. It could work.<br /> <br /> Needless to say there will be a lot of practice today! It\u2019s going to be a grueling day, but I am very excited about the Christmas show. It is so close to Christmas! I feel it in my bones!<br /> <br /> We watched Christmas movies last night, Die Hard, which might be the most American movie I have ever seen, and Gremlins, which is not really my favorite. Die Hard is\u2026if you boiled down the most obnoxious typical American stereotype, which is the hero. Also, feet being cut up, which was awful. Neither Julia nor I needed to see that. Gremlins has the Santa Claus story, and I don\u2019t like that either.<br /> <br /> I guess what bothers me is that they, Calamity especially, talk about how they are great Christmas movies. They are not. They take place at Christmas; it is a backdrop. A setting. It would have been little change but scenery to have them take place any other time of year. Saying they are Christmas movies is obnoxious, self-centered, and clearly a sign of a boorish lack of ability to interpret literature or cinema. Calamity is impossible to argue with, so I didn\u2019t. Only in America by Americans could two movies full of violence and horror be called \u201cChristmas Movies.\u201d<br /> <br /> One the other hand, the lady from Paris Lizette really resembled the Gremlins, didn\u2019t she?<br /> <br /> After movie night, my loves and I retired to bed. I have to say, it is rejuvenating to have us all unite at the end of the day. Even if someone just wants to relax, someone is always eager. It is all very nice, and warm, and cozy. Yes cozy may be the word in English that fits well.<br /> <br /> But that was the end of the two days. A lot happened before that.<br /> <br /> Day before yesterday was the Solstice Party. Boss Lowjack became the ruler of the Hold. All the Winter Courtiers were present, which is unusual for any gathering in The Lady by the Sea. I did not talk to many. No there was a circle of ice with bridges over, and a frozen pond in center, and I took the opportunity to skate all over. I did twirls, dashes, leaps\u2026I managed to make a jump over a bridge, and twirl high in the air. Juliette did some lovely singing, including \u201cHazy Shade of Winter\u201d though it was different than what I am used to, but then it often is. Winter Wonderland also, later.<br /> <br /> The spirits were high for a Winter Court gathering, focusing on the snowy aspect, not the Sorrow aspect. I suppose there is little snow and much sorrow in LA. It was a nice time, and I got to show off. Calamity and Jacob did too. It was fun.<br /> <br /> And of course, we paired or grouped off. Flores was eager to spend time with Juliette, Julia, Maria, and I. We were heading out when we found we had to be Stasia\u2019s ride\u2026Calamity rolled out with Becky. Jacob with Luna, of course. So we now had her, and she was very eager to get involved with us. She did\u2026and I think four is better than six. But we all had fun, and that was what was important.<br /> <br /> I really like Flores\u2026she is sweet, and smells nice, and has a lot of fun with us. I am not sure Stasia knew what to think. Julia worked on a portrait of her this afternoon before movie night. One for her club, special colors and paints to make it almost glow in the lighting.<br /> <br /> Oh, Speaking of Juliette singing, she was singing \u201cO Holy Night\u201d at church Sunday morning. I slipped out to attend as I wanted to hear her sing more Christmas songs. I love it when Juliette sings Christmas songs. I am so lucky to have her. As a lover.<br /> <br /> Methodist ceremonies are different from Catholic. More clapping.<br /> <br /> But it is soon the final pre Christmas show, and I have much preparing to do. So back to sleep, in among all the sweeties. I love them so.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXXXVI</i><br /> <br /> Oh, Marguerite that clapping is only when Lori sings. And as long as we are talking about Insincere Marguerite I gotta disagree about the Die Hard thing.<br /> <br /> Calamity and Insincere Marguerite both racked up a ton of successes doing the skating, both being six Dexterity and six Athletics. Calamity edged her out but then Marguerite used her Parkour to turn it into a rote action and sent her successes into the stratosphere. Rote actions are crazy.<br /> <br /> Captain Jack may have stolen the show with his performance, a long dancing jumping skating (roller and ice) bit of work to the sound of Spandeau Ballet\u2019s <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ntG50eXbBtc\" target=\"_blank\">Gold</a> which was something.<br /> <br /> Fun Session, and we are very close to jumping ahead to the end of April. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 07-16-2017, 03:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T00:27:03-07:00","id":1117115,"title":"","content":"Question: Does Jacobs carry his knives on him regularly? Also, good to see him being open with Luna.<br /> <br /> After Calamity's comment about Gawain. I have this image in my head of Gawain standing dead at his forge his last task completed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T06:02:22-07:00","id":1117164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play?p=1117115#post1117115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After Calamity's comment about Gawain. I have this image in my head of Gawain standing dead at his forge his last task completed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh noes!!!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T13:50:48-07:00","id":1117420,"title":"","content":"Omenseer: He does, yes.<br /> <br /> Last night we got to and through Christmas Morning, So next set of journals will cover the end of this segment of the story, last pre-Christmas show, Christmas Eve, and Christmas Morning. Gifts are opened, Insincere Marguerite drags most of the Motley out caroling, There is a second talk between Stasia and Elena, loves are kindled, and former enemies sit in the audience and chat.<br /> <br /> We will be starting up again with Walpurgis Night, The PCs getting the Dream House as their own, and two weddings a bit over a month away. Gawain and Ace will be out of the Motley (he could not leave till Walpurgis) and Luna added.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T13:27:02-07:00","id":1122789,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s the final show before Christmas, Christmas Eve, and Christmas Day as we wrap up this leg of Malibu Dream House. We get some story, we get some downtime, (from some characters, others will be covered start of next session) as we have the final (in world) session before Walpurgis Night. Settle in!<br /> <br /> <i>Session LXXXVII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary<br /> </b><br /> Happy Holidays, everyone!<br /> <br /> I\u2019m writing this in the waning hours of Christmas Day, 2014, sad to see the holiday season (and its effect on Marguerite\u2019s personality) fading, but excited at the prospect of a new year and all the new experiences it will bring. For one thing, 2015 will almost certainly bring my own wedding to someone I didn\u2019t even know last year, but who quickly worked her way into my heart and became the most important person in the world. We\u2019re talking about setting the date sometime in June.<br /> <br /> Not much happened during the day on Tuesday, but the show was <u>amazing</u>. I guess word must have spread that we were closing for the rest of the year and planning a special Christmas show, because I don\u2019t think we\u2019ve played to a crowd that large since we opened last May. Most of the Freehold showed up to see us, along with a sizeable number of mortals, both enchanted and otherwise. We were very nearly filled to capacity, and Calamity and Gawain were fretting about whether they\u2019d need to start turning people away to avoid violating the fire codes!<br /> <br /> So Marguerite \u2013 who had been frantically rehearsing both of her duets all day \u2013 got to stand in the spotlight again, and her numbers went remarkably well. She and Calamity (who also reprised her \u201cMistress for Christmas\u201d number) did a sultry song-and-dance number set to the Christmas classic \u201cYou\u2019re A Mean One, Mr. Grinch.\u201d Marguerite put her own special spin on the song (raising it by a couple of octaves, naturally) while Calamity slinked and capered around wearing green body paint and\u2026 not much else, really. I assume she researched the city ordinances before putting that costume together to avoid violating any of our various licenses.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not sure which of them had a better time with that number, though I suspect it was Calamity. She even worked the crowd during the later portions of the show while still wearing her \u201ccostume.\u201d<br /> <br /> Marguerite and I did a more traditional duet a little later. We performed the classic call-and-response song called \u201cBaby, It\u2019s Cold Outside.\u201d I took on the traditionally female role, while Marguerite sang the masculine parts. That song, when performed in a certain way, has always been full of sexual tension, and we decided to play that side of things up as much as possible. The audience ate it up, particularly as many of our regulars knew that the two of us are in a relationship, and picked up on the not-so-subtly hidden subtext.<br /> <br /> I closed out the second set with my one solo of the evening, reprising my \u201cSanta Baby\u201d number from earlier in the month. I usually try to be fairly modest in this diary, but I have to say that this was one of the better performances of my life (so far, at least). The audience seemed to agree with that assessment, if the standing ovation and wolf-whistles I got were any indication. I let myself practically ooze sexuality as I swayed around the stage in red lingerie, singing breathily and singling out regulars in the audience. Oh, and when I got to the line \u201cforgot to mention one little thing\u2026 a ring,\u201d I held up my left hand and let my engagement ring glitter in the spotlight. The changelings in the audience all knew about the engagement already, of course, and most of our regular mortal customers had probably spotted it before as well (I haven\u2019t exactly been shy about wearing it), but the audience still erupted into cheers of congratulations.<br /> <br /> And speaking of my affianced, I spotted her fairly early in the evening sitting at a table with none other than Twitch. The two of them were chatting like old friends every time I looked in on them, and D had a hand companionably on his shoulder\u2026 which might have been to comfort him. He was obviously nervous about the crowd, but seemed to be reining it in admirably\u2026 and none of his discomfort was directed at Maria herself. She later confided in me that he had asked if they could take a more secluded table in the back, but she had put her foot down and steered him toward a prominent, well-lit location. Still and all, despite his apparent demophobia, he left us later that evening with a smile and a friendly handshake.<br /> <br /> I said earlier that most of the Freehold turned up for our last show of the year, and I meant it. Hell, even Gunnar Friday was there, and I don\u2019t think I\u2019ve seen him at the Dream House since the incident with Mary\u2019s fetch. I stopped by Joan and Andromeda\u2019s table and chatted with the two of them for a while. We discussed our various religions, and I learned that D used to occasionally attend mass with Joan, which I never knew. Andromeda, being Jewish, celebrates Hanukkah rather than Christmas, but the spirit of the holiday is very similar in my opinion (though I confess that I know almost nothing about Judaism). I could have given them their gift, of course\u2026 but I hadn\u2019t given out the others to my motley-mates yet, and I didn\u2019t want to risk spoiling the surprise. The three of us made plans to meet up for dinner between Christmas and New Year\u2019s, and I got goodbye kisses from both of them.<br /> <br /> I made my way to the bar area next, where I found Julia. She had gravitated toward the bar rather than sitting alone at the Girlfriend Table, as D was elsewhere and Becky hadn\u2019t shown up at all. I found out why Julia was propping up the bar shortly thereafter\u2026 it turns out that she had sent an anonymous email to Yvette, letting her know that Marguerite would be performing that night. Yvette was indeed there, and when Marguerite\u2019s duties allowed, she joined her former lover at her table. Julia was understandably tense and nervous about this state of affairs.<br /> <br /> \u201cHey,\u201d I said, settling in next to her and putting an arm around her shoulders. \u201cYou okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded, but her face remained just this side of miserable. \u201cI will be,\u201d she said after a moment. \u201cIt\u2019s my own doing, after all. Bon-bon loves this season so much\u2026 I thought she deserved to be happy tonight. Her happiness is more important than mine.\u201d<br /> <br /> I leaned in and kissed her. \u201cThat is so\u2026 God, Julia, I am so in love with you right now.\u201d<br /> <br /> She smiled, but it was still a sad smile. \u201cThanks, Lori,\u201d she said simply.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou need me tonight?\u201d I asked. I\u2019d made tentative plans to spend the evening with Brightstar, but I knew that my newest lover would understand if Julia really needed me. She\u2019s very considerate that way.<br /> <br /> Julia shrugged. \u201cI\u2019ll be okay. I\u2019m a little melancholy, but I\u2019m not suicidal or anything. Whether my mood improves, well\u2026 I guess that\u2019ll depend on how the evening ends for those two.\u201d<br /> <br /> I gave her a small hug and another tiny kiss. \u201cMaria and I\u2026 you know we\u2019re here for you if you need us, right honey?\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cI know,\u201d she said, and then looked quickly to make sure no one was listening in. \u201cThanks, Juliette,\u201d she said once she was satisfied on that score.<br /> <br /> I made my way up to Yvette\u2019s table next, and was greeted warmly by the two of them. \u201cI\u2019m so glad I came tonight,\u201d Yvette said earnestly. \u201cThe show was magnificent. You are very talented. Were you the one who invited me?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> I shook my head. \u201cI\u2019m glad you came, of course,\u201d I said with a smile, \u201cbut the email actually came from Julia.\u201d I indicated the tall blonde at the bar with a nod.<br /> <br /> Marguerite looked down at her true love, nodded, and raised her glass in thanks. Julia replied in kind, but stayed at the bar.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe is okay, no?\u201d Marguerite asked me quietly.<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cShe will be, when she\u2019s in your arms again,\u201d I said seriously.<br /> <br /> Marguerite blinked. \u201cShe thought that I would not be staying with her tonight? But\u2026 it is Christmas time!\u201d<br /> <br /> I sighed. \u201cYou know how she gets\u2026 she\u2019s insecure. She\u2019ll be fine by the end of the evening.\u201d<br /> <br /> Yvette looked distraught. \u201cI\u2026 do not wish to cause problems. Miss Julia seems like a nice person, and she was thoughtful enough to invite me tonight. I do not wish to cause her distress.\u201d<br /> <br /> I shook my head. \u201cDon\u2019t worry about it, Yvette. Really. You\u2019re not causing problems. Everything will be fine. Julia just needs the occasional\u2026 reassurance. Please, enjoy the rest of your evening. And come back whenever you\u2019d like.\u201d<br /> <br /> I left the two of them to continue their talk. I don\u2019t know exactly how things went between them, but I know that Yvette left at the end of the evening, and I never saw the two of them behaving as anything more than old friends. True to her word, Marguerite spent the rest of the night with Julia.<br /> <br /> I made my way back to D after that and let her know that everything was fine, and that she could pursue any other plans she might have made for the night without worrying about Julia. She breathed a sigh of relief and surveyed the playing field.<br /> <br /> \u201cHmm,\u201d she said thoughtfully, \u201cmight drop by Gloria\u2019s table and see if she\u2019s doing anything this evening. Or maybe Neon. I could do with a good light show tonight. Unless\u2026\u201d she glanced over at me at this, \u201cunless you had plans in that direction, babe. You trying to get both of them strobing for you at once?\u201d<br /> <br /> I chuckled, but it was a deep, throaty sort of laugh. The thought of D and Neon together had set something off in me, and I think that was about when I decided how I wanted the rest of the evening to go. \u201cActually,\u201d I said breathily, \u201cmost of my fantasies about Neon involve her getting into bed with the two of <u>us</u>,\u201d I said, indicating the love of my life with a nod. \u201cYou see, I\u2019m not sure if you\u2019ve ever noticed or not, but I sort of have this thing about the color purple\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> D laughed at that, and slipped an arm comfortably around my waist. \u201cWhat do you say, babe\u2026 want to go for it? I know you had plans with Brightstar, but you want to try for a foursome? Really light up that Christmas tree?\u201d<br /> <br /> My pulse quickened at the thought. \u201cLet\u2019s do it,\u201d I said huskily.<br /> <br /> Thus began the seduction. With D by my side, those poor girls never had a chance. Brightstar was adorably oblivious to what we intended at first.<br /> <br /> \u201cOnly trouble is,\u201d D said faux-innocently as she snuggled up next to Neon, \u201cMarguerite and Julia need time together tonight, so there\u2019s only one bed available between Lori and I.\u201d<br /> <br /> Brightstar\u2019s brow furrowed. \u201cI don\u2019t want to put you out,\u201d she said with what sounded like genuine concern. \u201cLori and I can take the guest room, if that\u2019s okay. Or maybe go back to my place\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I did my best to smile and smolder at the same time. \u201cThere might not be any need for that,\u201d I said softly. \u201cThere\u2019s no reason anyone has to make that sacrifice.\u201d<br /> <br /> Brightstar looked confused. \u201cBut if you and I are spending the evening together, and de la Rocha and Neon are doing the same thing\u2026 how is that possible?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> Neon sighed. \u201cI believe these ladies are attempting to bed both of us at the same time,\u201d she said, affecting annoyance but clearly intrigued by the idea.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh,\u201d Brightstar said, understanding at last. And then, as the implications set in, \u201coh!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIs that something you might want?\u201d I asked, running the tips of my fingers over the back of her hand. \u201cI mean, it sounds like a hell of a lot of fun to me, but I don\u2019t want things to be awkward\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo!\u201d Brightstar said quickly. \u201cI mean, it\u2019s okay. I\u2019d like\u2026 I mean, I think\u2026\u201d She closed her eyes for a couple of seconds, and then opened them and looked at her roommate with a smile. \u201cI\u2019m up for it if you are,\u201d she said hopefully.<br /> <br /> Neon, still pretending scorn, nonetheless agreed to give it the old college try. A few minutes later we were all upstairs in our room, and clothes were flying. I will note that Neon and Brightstar tended to shy away from each other during the act itself, which I suppose is only to be expected. But I <u>did</u> notice that Neon flared <u>very</u> brightly whenever Brightstar said or did something that struck her as particularly innocent or na\u00efve.<br /> <br /> So the four of us staggered downstairs on Christmas eve morning, all of us exhausted and sore in the best possible way. I tried not to look too pleased with myself as the rest of the motley took in my disheveled appearance and the identities of my partners (so much purple!). Marguerite and Julia looked equally content, though not quite so mussed. In fact, both of them gave me big hugs as we entered the kitchen.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe four of us shall be together tonight, no?\u201d Marguerite whispered softly in my ear as we embraced.<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course,\u201d I said with a smile, \u201cit\u2019s Christmas. It\u2019s a day for family. Besides, I have to make sure you\u2019re in bed by midnight, young lady.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd\u2026\u201d she said, a bit louder, turning to address the rest of the motley, \u201cperhaps we will all go caroling tonight?\u201d<br /> <br /> I agreed immediately, of course, as did most of the motley. Jacob and Luna opted to stay behind, though Marguerite pouted at them relentlessly. I think she was hoping Jacob would make it snow on us while we sang. Alas, \u2018twas not to be. Calamity was all for it, and even made some reference to \u201cwassailing,\u201d which confused Marguerite to no end. I tried to explain the old Germanic term, but she was having none of it, and insisted that she was being accommodating enough by not demanding that we sing all of the carols in their \u201coriginal French.\u201d Sigh.<br /> <br /> So much of the rest of the day was spent relaxing and preparing for our musical excursion that evening. The doorbell did ring once, though, in the early afternoon. Calamity answered it and signed for a package addressed to me. I opened it in front of the others, not knowing what to expect.<br /> <br /> It was a sweater. A hand-knitted sweater. And it was <u>beautiful</u>. It had two holes in the back, perfectly sized and placed for my wings, and it was soft and warm, and felt like it would be the <u>perfect</u> garment for gliding. The card included said simply \u201cMerry Christmas from Rowan.\u201d<br /> <br /> I know I teared up a little at that. I pulled out my phone and was about three millimeters from calling her when I remembered that I\u2019m not supposed to do that before she\u2019s ready to talk to me. I dialed Felicity instead.<br /> <br /> \u201cHello?\u201d she asked after a few rings.<br /> <br /> \u201cFelicity,\u201d I said, not trusting my voice to say more.<br /> <br /> \u201cLori!\u201d she answered when she recognized my voice. \u201cMerry Christmas! To what do I owe the pleasure?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI just\u2026 I got a package today,\u201d I said slowly. \u201cFrom Rowan.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, good, it got to you in time,\u201d she replied. \u201cShe was hoping you\u2019d have it by Christmas.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI just\u2026 I know I\u2019m not supposed to reach out to her until she\u2019s ready,\u201d I said with a small hitch in my voice. \u201cI was hoping you could give her a message for me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course,\u201d she agreed immediately.<br /> <br /> \u201cJust\u2026 just tell her that I love it, and that I said thank you,\u201d I said in a rush.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll be happy to,\u201d she said warmly. There was a pause. When she started speaking again, her voice was soft and compassionate. \u201cIt\u2019s not forever, Lori. Give her another week or so, then we\u2019ll see where things stand.\u201d<br /> <br /> I was still pretty choked up, but I think I managed to hold it together pretty well. \u201cThanks, Felicity,\u201d I said at last. \u201cI won\u2019t take up any more of your time. Merry Christmas.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026and a Happy New Year,\u201d she said as a farewell.<br /> <br /> So I put the sweater on and spent the rest of the afternoon among the people with whom I\u2019m closest. As twilight fell, the group of us gathered in the main hall and prepared to spread joy and love throughout our corner of the greater Malibu/Santa Monica area. Marguerite had gone all-out, printing up little song books and everything (they had the words \u201cMerry\u201d and \u201cChristmas\u201d on the back and front covers, respectively, so that the sentiment would be legible to those facing us as we sang). Marguerite put on the suit she\u2019d worn for our number the previous evening. I was still wearing the sweater Rowan had given me. Most of the others were dressed in their regular clothes, although there were some cute holiday accents here and there. My love had small Christmas ornaments arranged artfully in her hair. She\u2019d done something similar on the previous evening, actually, though my attention had been distracted by other aspects of her appearance at the time.<br /> <br /> We asked Jacob and Luna if they wanted to join us one more time, but they remained steadfast in their intention to remain behind. The experience was\u2026 nice, actually. It was fun to go around singing without having to put a lot of glamour into my performance, or use contracts to make myself extra-sexy. I still gave the singing my all, of course\u2026 just without supernatural help. People seemed to enjoy the experience, and I guess that\u2019s the main point.<br /> <br /> And when I say \u201cpeople,\u201d I\u2019m talking about my motley as well as our various audiences. Marguerite was obviously overjoyed by the whole situation, but I think the others got into it after a while too. Though D is too macho and Julia too Goth to ever admit it, I caught glimpses of big guileless smiles on their faces whenever they thought nobody was looking. My family has a softer side after all. Oh, and speaking of Julia, she somehow managed to suppress the hypnotic quality of her singing voice while we were caroling. Good for her!<br /> <br /> When we got back a few hours later, we found that Jacob and Luna had not been idle. They\u2019d prepared a few batches of Christmas cookies and some truly superb eggnog! The lot of us sat around talking and joking and generally enjoying each other\u2019s company until it was time for bed. Marguerite was as excited as a kid, and it took a lot to settle her down. The atmosphere was friendly and loving rather than erotically charged, though, and I think all four of us fell asleep with decidedly more innocent-looking smiles than usual.<br /> <br /> I will give her credit: Marguerite let the rest of us sleep until nearly 10:00am before waking us on Christmas morning. I didn\u2019t use contracts to pep anyone up\u2026 the fuzzy-muzzy feeling seemed natural in that setting, and if anything it just added to the mood. The whole motley gathered \u2018round the tree, and we handed out presents. So many of us had apparently crept down into the main parlor during the night and slipped presents under that tree that it\u2019s a Christmas miracle that none of us ran into each other in the process!<br /> <br /> So the gifts were a varied and heart-felt assortment. Jacob made things out of leather for most of us\u2026 I got a beautiful braided leather band for my hair, D got a nice duster (black and purple, natch), Calamity got sheaths for her knives, and so forth. He also enlarged, printed, and framed the picture he took on his phone when D proposed to me. It\u2019s probably my favorite <u>ever</u> picture of me looking that confused and terrified. Calamity gave out little worked glass baubles, each of which contained a specially crafted dream tailored to our individual personalities. I wish I had that sort of ability, honestly. Julia gave everyone hand-painted portraits of their significant others, and of course they were all beautiful.<br /> <br /> My own gifts to most of the motley might have seemed cheap or self-aggrandizing by comparison, but I <u>think</u> everybody accepted them in the spirit in which they were intended. So I haven\u2019t written anything about these gifts in this journal yet, because I sleep with three darklings, one of whom has already demonstrated that she will occasionally go through the private belongings of her paramours after they fall asleep. Yes, D, I remember how you found out about Gloria\u2019s programming, and if you\u2019re reading this now, don\u2019t worry about it. I have no real secrets from you, as I hope you realize by now.<br /> <br /> In any case, I\u2019ve been working on a mostly unexplored aspect of my musical skills over the past month or so\u2026 composition. I managed to come up with approximately a dozen songs with which I\u2019m relatively happy, and it occurred to me at some point that most of them were inspired by one or more of my current circle of friends. Mostly the motley, of course\u2026 with a few very close exceptions, like Oleander, Rowan, Joan, and Andromeda (and Captain Jack\u2026 but maybe the less said about the hidden Track 13 the better). So I practiced until I got pretty good at playing all of them on the piano \u2013 the Hedge House provided a piano when I needed privacy, which was nice of it \u2013 and then rented a few hours in a small \u201cvanity\u201d recording studio. I had the CDs pressed, and a few hours with Ace\u2019s Photoshop program later, I had covers and lyric sheets printed.<br /> <br /> I hope everyone likes them. I mean, the pledge I made with Princess Jolie all those months ago ensures that I have a decent amount of money\u2026 but I wanted to give my nearest and dearest something that couldn\u2019t be bought with money, something that contains a little bit of my soul. And hey, I may not be Bob Dylan or Elton John, but I flatter myself into thinking that I can string together a few words and chords into something at least a little meaningful.<br /> <br /> There were other gifts exchanged as well, of course. Too many to record here, honestly, so\u2026 highlights! Marguerite gave me a beautiful golden locket, with a picture of her and a lock of her hair inside. Julia gave me the aforementioned paintings\u2026 an original of D with a cocky grin on her face and prints of herself and Marguerite. The two of them went in together and got me a clutch with an image of a bird turning into an angel on the side, and a set of seat and windshield covers for the \u2018vette, covered in images of shapely stockinged legs. Luna gave me a knife. I mean, it\u2019s a nice knife, with a compass in the handle and everything, but\u2026 it\u2019s a knife. Still, at least it shows that she was thinking of me, and that she cared enough to get me a gift.<br /> <br /> D gave me an absolutely <u>gorgeous</u> necklace. It hangs a little lower than I\u2019m accustomed to, which I\u2019m pretty sure was a conscious choice on her part to encourage me to wear tops with plunging necklines. She also got me a few plastic anatomical models\u2026 the kind medical students use for practice. She knows me so well\u2026<br /> <br /> My own gift to her (besides the music) was a new set of biker leathers, including boots, gloves, and a new jacket. They were tailored to her exact measurements \u2013 about which I flatter myself that I know more than a little \u2013 and the cut is designed to display her natural beauty and sensuality to its best advantage. The leathers are in black, with understated purple highlights designed to complement the color of her hair. And, y\u2019know, also designed to drive me into hitherto unknown heights of passion.<br /> <br /> I almost asked her to model it for me right then and there, but noon was fast approaching, and I had to go meet Dad for lunch. D came with me, of course, and the three of us had a fine old time celebrating the season. I gave Dad a copy of the CD as well, though I know most of it isn\u2019t really his type of music\u2026 but I\u2019d also recorded a second, shorter album of myself playing and singing a few of my favorite hymns. I guess on some level I must have wanted to demonstrate to him that I\u2019m not just attending his church to be close to him, I\u2019m also serious about my commitment to Christianity. I know\u2026 when I first realized that about myself you could have knocked me over with a feather. Maybe one of my own.<br /> <br /> So we had a great lunch with ham and turkey and all the trimmings. The congregation really provides for Dad around the holiday seasons, so there was plenty of delicious food for everyone. Dad told us to eat as much as we wanted, as he couldn\u2019t possibly finish it all and Natasha is away with family for the holidays. I imagine he\u2019ll probably donate the leftovers to a local soup kitchen or something.<br /> <br /> After we\u2019d exchanged gifts and stuffed ourselves to an obscene degree, we talked for a while. We told Dad that we\u2019re planning to set the wedding sometime in June, probably a week or so after Marguerite and Julia have their own ceremony. He promised he\u2019d keep his calendar free, but urged us to let him know as soon as we\u2019d set a date. He let us go with a tearful hug and a fervent \u201cMerry Christmas\u201d for each of us, and we made our way back to the Dream House.<br /> <br /> And here we are, full and happy and in love and surrounded by friends in a place that feels more like home to me than any place has since Mom died. It\u2019s been a hell of a year, and it looks like next year is shaping up to be just as eventful. Let\u2019s face it, if all of my plans pan out, then by next Christmas I\u2019ll have my GED and be enrolled in a pre-med program at some local college. Missy and Jane will be free of the Empress, and maybe living here with us (or at least close by\u2026 I think they\u2019d like California). I could very well be training to take on the role of Spring Queen at that point, though that one seems like kind of a longshot to me. Oh, and I\u2019ll also be <u>married</u> to the most wonderful girl I have ever known.<br /> <br /> And on that note, I think I\u2019ll close out this entry. I\u2019m running out of unused pages in this diary anyway; I\u2019ll need to pick up another one soon. <br /> <br /> Merry Christmas to all, and to all a good night!<br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei Grace</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> Thursday, December 25th<br /> Nine years, five months, twenty-seven days<br /> Days without stabbing: 10<br /> <br /> Christmas really is a magical time. I swear I never imagined Insincere Marguerite could be so cheerful. It\u2019s adorable and more than a little contagious. Not that I\u2019m normally grumpy or anything. Actually I\u2019m surprised that she hasn\u2019t rattled the vents yet. I figured she\u2019d have us all up at the crack of dawn so I poofed myself and stayed up. And since I was up, I slipped out and watched the sunrise from the roof. Still doesn\u2019t feel like it used to but the ritual of it was relaxing and as the sky lightened I realized I was actually comfortable just being alone with my thoughts. It wasn\u2019t the first time but it was the moment when it hit me how not so long ago that wouldn\u2019t have happened. My life isn\u2019t perfect but I\u2019m honestly happy and I am better than I was. I\u2019ve still got plenty of work to do before I\u2019m the person I want to be and I don\u2019t doubt there will be setbacks but it really feels like it\u2019s actually possible. I could practically hear Dr Emmett\u2019s I told you so. <br /> <br /> And on that note, I did chat with Jacob before therapy Tuesday morning. It\u2019s not that Stasia went after Elena as much as it\u2019s that she asked him and said she\u2019d back off when he told her he\u2019d prefer she not go there and then turned right around and did it. And honestly, that bothers me a bit. I mean, my blood sister has always been a bit looser with the truth than me and it\u2019s something I\u2019ve never been completely alright with. But she\u2019s been my best friend so long I can\u2019t remember her not being part of my life and Jacob completely understood when I told him that meant I would stand with her no matter how I felt about what she\u2019d done. It wasn\u2019t as awkward as I feared and we\u2019re still good. And despite the heavy rehearsal schedule to get Insincere Marguerite ready for the last show we still managed to get a good sparring session in afterwards. <br /> <br /> She was clearly more than a little nervous about the show and I can\u2019t say I entirely blame her. I mean, sure, when the horse throws you you have to get back on and all, but maybe that first ride doesn\u2019t need to be the Kentucky Derby. But Lori spent the afternoon working with her and I did what I could when we were practicing our number. Plus I made a pledge with her to boost her performance. It wasn\u2019t a big one and really it was more to shore up her confidence than anything else. And when the show came around, she nailed both her numbers and managed to be in an even brighter mood, though some of that may have also come from Yvette\u2019s decision to attend the show.<br /> <br /> And she was hardly the only one. We had one of our highest turnouts in terms of both total numbers and Lost. I belted out Mistress for Christmas and then slipped into some body paint and an even skimpier outfit for You\u2019re a Mean One Mr Grinch with Insincere Marguerite and it\u2019s not like my Christmas Domme outfit really left much to the imagination. I think Tiffany nailed it when she was looking me over to make sure the paint was even and remarked that I looked like I was ready for Star Trek porn. But I had a blast slinking about and even ended up doing the rounds without covering up. Now that I think about it\u2026 maybe we should consider some theme nights. Totally have to pitch it to Lori at some point. I mean, her wings would get in the way of anything too elaborate but I could so rock a set of leek and double bladed light-saber.<br /> <br /> Anyway, as I said, the house was packed. Twitch was there and spent the night sitting with D. Both she and Jacob restrained themselves and so he left as alive as he arrived. Gunnar was there with Moon and Dionisia, apparently Queen Charlotte made a point of keeping him quite busy during her reign. Neon and Brightstar from the Unseelie Court were there and ended up spending the night with Lori and D. Elena shared a table with Stasia, which made me a little nervous since Elena is very inexperienced and Stasia has gone to great pains to make sure I know her commitment issues run deeper than the Mariana Trench. But I spoke to Stasia quietly while Elena was saying her goodbyes to Jacob and she assured me that it wasn\u2019t an impending train wreck and that they just hit it off and liked each others company. I know she wouldn\u2019t lie to me, I just hope she\u2019s not misjudged the situation. I\u2019m not getting any sort of romantic vibe from Elena either but I haven\u2019t really spent time around her since the trip and all. <br /> <br /> I did also catch Yvette before she left, though not alone as I had kinda hoped to. Insincere Marguerite walked her to the women\u2019s room and I followed them in. I did interrupt a hug but it didn\u2019t seem like it was a prelude to anything more. It was a touch awkward so I made the nice to see you as a proper guest and you\u2019re always welcome if we know you\u2019re coming comments and an offer to help out with the Oneiromancy if I could as brief as I could without making it obvious that I was playing chaperon and trying to judge where things stood between them. I\u2019m more than a little leery of that situation. I do care for Insincere Marguerite but this is the object of her deepest obsession here and even if she doesn\u2019t cross a line Julia might. Honestly, it\u2019d just be simpler all around if Yvette decided to just stay clear of the Dream House now that she knows her former captor isn\u2019t going to come hunting her but that doesn\u2019t seem to be in the cards. <br /> <br /> Joan and Andromeda were also present and I got by and gave them their Christmas presents. It sparked a bit of religious discussion, being that Andromeda is Jewish but she was happy to receive a gift. That sort of prompted a conversation with Joan that I wasn\u2019t expecting. She mentioned that she found prayer very grounding and offered to talk with me about my faith since that is often something we Changelings have some trouble with. Well, much like with Lori, I don\u2019t really begrudge her faith and it clearly is important to her and is good for her. That said, I kinda brushed it off with a comment about going to church every Sunday in Snow Globe, which very much did not quietly end the discussion. She was rather adamant that that wasn\u2019t a real church and certainly not God\u2019s church. I really did not want to get into it with her since I like Joan and my feelings on God are anything but kind. If God is real than either he couldn\u2019t or worse yet didn\u2019t do anything to protect an innocent thirteen year old girl from being taken and tortured horrifically so asking me to bend a knee and thank him for that? Not going to happen and I\u2019m not going to just nod and pretend for Joan or Lori or anyone else. But I don\u2019t hate them for believing so I don\u2019t want to lash out at their beliefs and be a dick either. Thankfully, Joan did let it drop before I had to admit just how I do feel about the whole thing. <br /> <br /> Well, eventually everyone else settled on the evening\u2019s configuration of sexual partners and wandered off so I took out the picture Dark Kimberly had sent me (of White Maria\u2019s parents, not of herself) and settled in to Inception her father. It went quite well, just like with her mother. They are both primed and ready for the idea that they should respect their daughter\u2019s desire to make her own choices. Lori is on board with helping to keep up the ruse that we\u2019re wedding planners and to help me convince them. I am confident that we\u2019ll be able to bring them out of the dark ages on this at least.<br /> <br /> After all of that yesterday was pretty calm. There was the usual sex breakfast hi-jinks and during that Insincere Marguerite brought up caroling. I said I\u2019d love to g a wassailing and once it was explained that was the same thing we all agreed except Luna and Jacob. <br /> <br /> Those two opted to stay in and spend some quiet time together (which suits them both honestly) and made Christmas cookies and egg nog for everyone to share when we returned, which was a nice surprise.<br /> <br /> It was fun. We decked out in Santa hats and seasonal colors and Insincere Marguerite printed up songbooks. Everyone had a blast walking the neighborhoods nearby and singing. No one we accosted proved immune to the power of our holiday cheer. It really was great.<br /> <br /> Then we shared egg nog and more holiday music and sat around the tree quietly for a bit before we all slipped off to bed.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, vent rattling came about 10am and we all drifted in for the festivities. It felt nice to gather with the motley, with my family. I remember Christmas in Snow Globe, year after year, the fake family and the whole Norman Rockwell perfectness of it. But it never came close to the real thing. The only thing that could have made it more perfect was Becky, but I\u2019m going to see her later to exchange gifts. <br /> <br /> The dreams went over well with people. I had hoped they would. I\u2019m glad I was able to make something for them all. And Lori had a similar spirit in her gift, a CD with songs she composed for each of us. I am listening to it now and it is really good. Her talents run so much deeper than most expect. <br /> <br /> Julia painted pictures for each of us, not of ourselves but of the one we love. Gawain\u2019s portrait really captures his heroic nature and the one she did for him of me is, well, quite striking and flattering if I do say. <br /> <br /> Jacob made gifts for most out of leather, though for me he got me a book about glassblowing. It\u2019s a pretty hefty tome and goes into a lot of specifics, meant for someone intending to set up a kiln and take up the art. Of course, my contract with glass isn\u2019t quite the same but I think I can still learn a lot from it. I suspect it wasn\u2019t entirely an accident that he got me something aimed at one of my creative rather than destructive interests. I\u2019m looking forward to reading through it and figuring out how to apply the techniques to my contract. <br /> <br /> So, currently Lori and D are off to see Lori\u2019s father and Jacob\u2019s meeting up with his sister. I envy them more than a little and I\u2019m happy for them to have managed to reconnect with their family. And as crass as it may sound, having Stasia back means more to me than anyone else from before. I wish I could undo that tragic night. I wish I\u2019d waited to go home, or that they\u2019d moved and not been there. So many if only\u2019s\u2026 I will never stop regretting what I did that night. I will never forget that I have it in me to be that monster. But the truth is there is no way for me to undo what happened. There is no point in looking backward. In a few days I\u2019m heading up to help Stasia load up a truck and move her things. Guess I\u2019ll have a use for that contract of Stone besides firing Max without breaking my wrist. <br /> <br /> So yeah, I\u2019m going into the new year with my blood sister, my knight and my dragon, and my family. It\u2019s going to be a good year<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T13:31:11-07:00","id":1122792,"title":"","content":"<b>Jacob\u2019s Journal </b><br /> <br /> As per usual I got up early this morning so I could go to therapy. I met up with Calamity and we started off. On the way to the clinic she apologized for backing Stasia in her attempts to seduce my sister. She said that she and Stasia were like sisters, so she went along with what her friend was doing out of habit. She then expressed concerns that having done so would ruin our relationship and she didn\u2019t want to do that. She wanted to make sure that things were still okay between us. I told her that I understood why she did what she did. I would back my brother\u2019s plans when we still served the Lady. If he had survived the introduction to my motley then I might still have backed his plans, within reason, if something came up that necessitated such a thing. I just can\u2019t help but think that if I\u2019d said the right thing at the time then I might have been able to save his life, but I froze. I couldn\u2019t come up with the right words. Any argument that I could think of in that moment seemed silly and not worth mentioning. I knew that there was just some things he wasn\u2019t going to agree to. I knew how loyal to the Lady he was and in that instant I couldn\u2019t think of a good enough reason to get him to leave her. So, I understand loyalty. I know what it is to stand by someone, even when doing so will hurt another person. Granted at the time I didn\u2019t particularly care if I hurt other people. I was not a very good person. In this situation though, I don\u2019t think it was Calamity\u2019s intention to hurt me. In the moment she did what she had always done and supported her friend and sister. So, when she asked if we were still okay, I said that we were. I don\u2019t want to lose her friendship. She is one of the few people in this freehold that I know won\u2019t judge me for my past actions, or for any future ones. So, we cleared the air and went to our therapy sessions.<br /> <br /> Therapy itself was not very noteworthy. Dr. Sullivan approved of me accepting Calamity\u2019s apology for what she did on the camping trip. He thought that I handled it in a healthy way and didn\u2019t let the situation come between us as friends. I suppose that is a good thing. Reacting to something in a healthy manner is preferable to being considered reckless or destructive. I could have reacted in ways that would have damaged my relationship with Calamity and possibly put a wedge between me and Stasia. Still felt a little condescending though. Being praised on choosing the \u201cright\u201d choice was a little annoying. Not that he really put it in those kinds of terms. It just felt a little bit like getting praised as a child for doing the right thing.<br /> <br /> So\u2026after we got back from therapy there was breakfast, and after breakfast Stasia asked to have a word with me. She started walking to a private room so I followed. She said that she had talked to Elena and had gotten permission to discuss what happened on the camping trip. She admitted that she had slept with my sister, but explained that Elena had instigated things. I still think Stasia manipulated the situation to get that result, but I didn\u2019t bring that up during our talk. She did admit that she had been trying to charm Elena though, so I guess that is something of an admission to that end. I reiterated to her that I was mainly upset by her breaking her word. I asked her to stay away because Elena had seemed uncomfortable when they first met and I didn\u2019t want my sister getting pressured into anything. Around that time I noticed that Stasia\u2019s pocket was lit up just a bit. It didn\u2019t take long to figure out that her phone was on and probably recording the whole conversation. I continued a little more carefully than I had before, but I honestly didn\u2019t have to really censor what I was going to say to her. Stasia told me that after that first night Elena had texted her and they\u2019d talked. Then they flirted on the camping trip and my sister asked Stasia back to her tent. I admitted that I had been unaware of any of that. Stasia also assured me that she had talked to Elena about what kind of relationship she intended if they slept together. So, presumably Elena knew from the start that this was going to be a one night stand. I guess that was okay with her. Stasia also wanted to make sure that I had no plans of doing anything to her. I assured her that I had no intention to hurt her. She asked if we were okay, much like Calamity did earlier, and I said that we were. If Elena did honestly instigate things and knew straight out that it wasn\u2019t a long-term thing, then I suppose I can\u2019t fault what happened. I\u2019m still a little upset by Stasia\u2019s reaction to things. She could have said \u201cno,\u201d or suggested they wait, but she didn\u2019t. I suppose the healthy thing would be to let this go and not dwell on it any more. I will try, but I will admit that I am protective of my sister. I don\u2019t want her to get hurt.<br /> <br /> As Staisa was leaving the room I called her on the recording. She looked chagrined but admitted that she had recorded the conversation just in case Elena wanted to listen to it later. She didn\u2019t think my sister would want to hear it now, but may in the future. She thought that Elena might be too embarrassed to want to listen to her brother talk to her one-time lover about their relationship. I can\u2019t help but wonder if she\u2019s also set it to record in case I did something to her. It could be her insurance policy. Or at least it would be evidence of what I\u2019d done. Stasia is just paranoid enough to do it, so I\u2019m assuming the recording served a dual purpose. I don\u2019t suppose I can fault her on that. She knows how dangerous I can be with a blade. It would be remiss of her to not take precautions.<br /> <br /> Tonight was the last show of the year and Lori, Calamity and Insincere Marguerite went all out for their performances. They were really good. I managed to catch bits and pieces of the show between serving and making drinks. We were crowded tonight. A lot of Changelings came to see the final show, as did mortals. We had a few guests that I wasn\u2019t expecting too. Twitch took up De La Rocha\u2019s offer and came by for a show. They sat together in one of the center tables and talked amicably for the night. I think the little shit actually enjoyed himself. He didn\u2019t look too spooked or anything, though I do think that the crowds got to him once or twice. Yvette was also there. After her performance, Insincere Marguerite went over to her former lover\u2019s table and they talked for a good bit of the night. They also seemed to be getting along really well.<br /> <br /> Throughout all of this I noticed that Julia was sitting by herself and looking rather sad. So, I made up a non-alcoholic drink that I knew Julia liked and went over to her table. I asked if she was okay and she admitted that she was not doing great. I could tell who she was watching so I tried to reassure her that Insincere Marguerite loved her very much and would always come back to her. Marguerite was not going to leave Julia over a former lover. I know that there are still some feelings left behind between Yvette and Insincere Marguerite, but things are much stronger between her and Julia. During our conversation, Julia admitted that she was the one that invited Yvette to the Dream House tonight. She wanted to make Insincere Marguerite happy and she would do this at the expense of her own happiness. She said it was more important that Marguerite be happy than herself be happy. In that instant I knew that Julia did not need to be alone. She was working herself up and probably imagining all kinds of bad things, like Marguerite leaving her for Yvette. So, I invited her back to the bar and kept her company. At one point Lori came by to talk to our melancholy motley mate and essentially told Julia the same things I did, though she was probably more convincing. Julia is in love with Lori and vice versa. She will listen to her lover over me any day, and that\u2019s fine. I just didn\u2019t want Julia to be so alone and depressed at what should be a happy time of year.<br /> <br /> After she left Julia Lori went over to talk to De La Rocha. Pretty soon that pair was going over to chat up Neon and Brightstar. There was conversation and then some blushing on Brightstar\u2019s part. Considering all four later went upstairs together I figured that my motley mates decided to seduce our guests for the evening. I\u2019m assuming Brightstar has never done that before. Which is not a bad thing. I\u2019ve never had multiple partners at one time. I tend to be a one lover at a time kind of guy. Plus there\u2019s the fact that my girlfriend is not into multiple lovers at a time either, and I\u2019m happy just being with her.<br /> <br /> The evening wrapped up shortly after all that. Calamity went to see Yvette off while she was saying goodbye to Insincere Marguerite. Not sure what was said, but Calamity came back in a good mood, so I\u2019m assuming she got to relay whatever message she had for the French girl. Also, before she left I talked to Elena briefly. I wanted to see if she\u2019d up to coming by the Dream House on Christmas day so I could give her the present I made for her. She said to just text her the time. I then told her good night. Thankfully it wasn\u2019t too awkward. I know that Elena knows about my conversation with Stasia about the camping trip. My goal tonight was to just act like nothing out of the ordinary had happened. The last thing I wanted to do is embarrass my sister.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Christmas eve. Insincere Marguerite was really happy and it showed. At breakfast she was already making plans to go caroling with everyone tonight after dinner. She asked if I wanted to come along, but I said that I don\u2019t sing. Luna wasn\u2019t all that interested in going either, so I told Marguerite that we would stay at the house tonight if that was okay. Insincere Marguerite looked a little disappointed, but didn\u2019t say anything else about it.<br /> <br /> Later in the day Lori got a package in the mail. It turned out to be a handmade sweater from Rowan. It even had holes in the back for Lori\u2019s wings. It was a rather thoughtful present if you ask me. Lori really liked it and immediately put it on. After that she called Felicity to pass along her thanks to Rowan for the beautiful gift. Lori was a bit subdued for the rest of the day. I guess things are still on the mend with Lori and Rowan.<br /> <br /> After dinner Insincere Marguerite got everyone together to go caroling. During the day she had made up song books for everyone and even printed \u201cMerry Christmas\u201d on the covers so their audience could read it. She really does go all the way when it comes to Christmas. Luna and I saw them off and I said I hoped that they had fun. Once they were out the door I told my plan to Luna. I have not done much in the way of Christmassy stuff so I wanted to do something nice for everyone. My plan was to make a batch or three of Christmas cookies and some eggnog. She agreed that was a good idea and helped me make the food. We even got food coloring to put in the dough and frosting to make things more festive. I figured the others would be gone for a couple of hours so we had plenty of time to get things done. I was right. We got three batches of cookies done and out on plates before our singers came back. When they got back we surprised them with our holiday cookies. Everyone liked them, and the eggnog. I hope that Insincere Marguerite was a little less disappointed that we didn\u2019t come singing with them. I wouldn\u2019t have had time to make the cookies if I\u2019d gone out with them. Plus, I think it made a good surprise for the end of the day.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> It\u2019s Christmas day and Insincere Marguerite let us sleep all the way until 10:00am. I was surprised. I thought she\u2019d wake us up earlier than that. So, we all padded downstairs and I got the coffee going so we could all wake up better. I texted Elena and she headed on over to the Dream House. And even before the coffee was done Marguerite was passing out presents. Calamity handcrafted glass vessels and put a dream in each one and gave them out to everyone in the motley. It was beautiful. Lori went all out and composed songs for each of us and had CDs made for all of us. I haven\u2019t listened to the whole thing yet, but it\u2019s pretty good. I liked the song that she wrote for me. Julia gave everyone a painting of their significant other, so I got a gorgeous painting of my gorgeous Luna. Not exactly sure where I\u2019m going to put it, but I\u2019ll find some place for it. Then there was Insincere Marguerite. She made lockets for all of her lovers that included a picture and a small lock of hair inside. It thought that was rather sweet. I followed in the tradition and made presents for everyone. I made braided leather hair band for Lori, as well as a framed picture of when De La Rocha proposed to her. I knew that photo was going to come in handy. For Calamity I got a glass blowing book. I know that she doesn\u2019t technically blow the glass, but it had some techniques in there that I thought she\u2019d find interesting. For Luna I made a pair of leather sheathes for her knives. I know that her current ones had been starting to get worn. For Insincere Marguerite I found a French Christmas carol CD on amazon and made her a pair of \u201cshoes\u201d without soles so she can go into restaurants that require shoes without actually covering the soles of her feet. For Julia I got her a nice set of brushes and made a leather roll up brush holder for them and for De La Rocha I made a black leather duster. I even put purple highlights here and there. For Gawain I made a leather bound book so he can record his forging designs and keep a record of what works and what doesn\u2019t. And last but not least I made a study backpack for Elena and put designs along the edges so it was more than utilitarian.<br /> <br /> So overall it was a very nice holiday season. I think that Insincere Marguerite being so excited about it made it all the better. And despite what happened on the camping trip I found it to be enjoyable. It\u2019s been a long time since I camped just for fun and it was nice to do that with friends. Plus, I enjoyed the snow. I know the birds were upset with me for that, but I don\u2019t really mind. I really wanted to do something familiar for my birthday. And I\u2019m glad that Elena got to share it too. I didn\u2019t ask if the little shit that wears my face kept up the tradition of camping on our birthday or not. I guess a part of me didn\u2019t want to know. I suppose I should ask at some point. If for no other reason than I\u2019m curious. But anyway, the holiday was nice this year. I couldn\u2019t celebrate it with my parents, but I could celebrate it with my new family, which was just as good. Merry Christmas!<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Gawain left. I\u2019m not even sure why. He just said that it was time for him to move on and that he felt that he had done all he could here. I think there was a real reason why he was leaving but he didn\u2019t share it with the rest of us. He just packed up all of his things and then told Calamity and the rest of us that he was going. Within minutes he had his van loaded up and he was gone. It just seemed so sudden. I\u2019m sure it\u2019s something that he\u2019s been contemplating for a while now, but he didn\u2019t say anything to anyone about it before now. I guess in retrospect I could tell something was bothering him. He\u2019d been distancing himself from us for a while now. He\u2019d kept more to himself lately and didn\u2019t participate in what the rest of us where doing. He didn\u2019t come on the camping trip, though he allowed us to use his van, and he didn\u2019t go caroling with the others. It started before that though, but just in little ways. It was so close to the holiday season that I thought he was just working on presents or something else in his forge.<br /> <br /> Needless to say, Calamity was devastated. She keeps telling everyone that she\u2019s fine, but we all know that for the lie that it is. When he left Lori gave her a hug, but forgot to take into account Calamity\u2019s glass, and got cut a little bit. Calamity discovered in that moment her bane is that she cannot draw innocent blood, and Lori is most definitely innocent. Calamity felt really bad about it, but Lori brushed it off saying that was the risk you take when you get close to anyone. I know Calamity understood what it meant but I think it was too soon for her to take it to heart. So, Calamity has kept busy doing work and performing. She hasn\u2019t been affectionate with anyone, not even Becky, and I know how much she loves that woman. Their faces light up when they see one another and they always come downstairs smiling when Becky stays the night. But Calamity has been standoffish with everyone lately, even Becky. She has continued to go to therapy sessions, but she doesn\u2019t instigate conversation on the ride there or back. I have even managed to keep her sparring after our sessions, but even that she is not as animated during. She fights fine, but it\u2019s all muscle memory. She\u2019s not really interested in what she\u2019s doing. There\u2019s no spark in her eyes as she lands a hit or evades my blade. She\u2019s just kind of going on autopilot. I was hoping that the sparring would bring her out of her funk, but it hasn\u2019t really been working. I\u2019ve tried engaging her in conversation a few times, but she\u2019s shut down even further whenever I\u2019ve tried doing that, so I stopped. I\u2019m not trying to push her even further away than she already is.<br /> <br /> To take up the slack in Gawain\u2019s leaving, De La Rocha has started working at the Dream House full time as our bouncer. She even quit her job as an X-ray tech at the hospital. I know how much she liked that job, so it was something of a big deal when she announced to the rest of us that she had left her hospital job to work here. I know that Lori was happy to have her lover working at the House. It ensured them both that they would have plenty of time to spend with one another. And if there is another couple more in love with one another, besides Julia and Insincere Marguerite, I haven\u2019t seen it. So far, De La Rocha has been enjoying the new job. She hasn\u2019t had to get too rough with anyone in asking them to leave the Dream House so far. There was only really one guy that didn\u2019t believe De La Rocha when she told him to leave. He was a big guy and didn\u2019t think that one small Latina could remove him from the premises. He was wrong and soon learned his lesson. De La Rocha does not bluff.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Lori completed her GED recently and did really well on the test. She was worried that she\u2019d fail, and seemed to be convinced that she\u2019s not very bright. I hope this goes a good ways towards convincing her that she is just as smart, if not smarter, than anyone else in the motley. I guess all those late nights of reading instead of sleeping paid off. Though I\u2019m still convinced that she\u2019d have done just as well if she didn\u2019t stay up all night. I guess we just have to see what her plans are from here. Is she going to go to college, and if so what for? I\u2019m assuming she wants to study medicine given her nighttime reading habits. I think she\u2019d make a good doctor. She does have the Spring Court abilities which let her heal, but she\u2019s also knowledgeable about the topic and really good with people. I guess we\u2019ll see what happens.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> It\u2019s been rather busy around here lately. I\u2019ve been trying to get Calamity to do more things with the motley and stop hiding away in the office. I\u2019ve arranged a couple of hiking trips into the mountains in the past few weeks. We all brought food and water for a quick lunch and cameras to take pictures. Okay\u2026most people just brought their phones and took pictures that way, but it all worked out the same. I got some great pictures of Lori and De La Rocha being cute together and well as a couple of good shots of Julia and Insincere Marguerite. Once or twice I even saw a small glimmer of the old Calamity in her eyes when we saw something particularly breathtaking, but then it would disappear just as quickly. I\u2019m taking it as a sign of success that we\u2019ve even managed to elicit just a small response out of her. We just need to get her to accept that Gawain is gone and to move on with her life. I know that she loved him. I know that they were great together, but he\u2019s gone. No amount of moping is going to bring him back. He needed to leave for reasons I don\u2019t know, but he felt he needed to go. And now Calamity needs to move on. I had to move on when Rook died. I will admit that sometimes I still fall back into darker thoughts when I remember my brother\u2019s last day, but I have to remind myself that I can\u2019t change what happened no matter how much I want to. I just had to get used to the fact that he was gone. And not to sound harsh, but Calamity just has to get used to the fact that Gawain is gone too. He\u2019s not dead, but I got the impression that he wasn\u2019t coming back.<br /> <br /> So, we had Lori\u2019s birthday party the other day. It was fun. I think I even saw a flicker of a smile on Calamity\u2019s face when Dark Kimberly jumped out of the cake that we\u2019d wheedled in for the party. A fun time was had by all. I made a braided leather bracelet for Lori to match her hairband as a present. I think she liked it. I have plans to make something for all four of the quartet as wedding presents. I just have to figure out what to make. I had been thinking of doing something that matched, but each woman has their own tastes so it might be good to make something different for each one. I could just have some common theme or design on each one. But that\u2019s in the future. Which has a specific date now. Insincere Marguerite and Julia are going to get married on June 6th and Lori and De La Rocha was going to get married on the following weekend, June 13th. Then they are all going to go on a honeymoon together. Not sure where they\u2019re going yet, but wherever they go it will be fun.<br /> <br /> On a different note, Elena and Stasia have continued their friendship. They spend a good bit of time together and talk frequently but they are not romantically involved. At least as far as I can tell. In light of that I have warmed somewhat towards Stasia. She did not just dump my sister flat, which had been a concern. I suppose I should have realized that Stasia wouldn\u2019t do that to my sister, but at that point I didn\u2019t know her and had no idea what she would or wouldn\u2019t do. And my first instinct when dealing with new people is to not trust them. I learned rather quickly when I was just trying to survive in the Lady\u2019s realm that I couldn\u2019t trust anyone. They were all out for themselves and were not my friend. That attitude has carried over to \u2018the world,\u2019 though I try not to let that be my first instinct. It\u2019s just habit. But in any case I\u2019m happy to say that they are friends and seem to have a good relationship going.<br /> <br /> Ace also mentioned that he was going to be leaving the motley too. He has been dropping hints and talking about leaving for a while now so it wasn\u2019t a surprise. He made it official though. He\u2019s going to be leaving before Walpurgis night. I will be sad to see him go, but he said that he wanted to move on and see new places. He liked working at the Dream House with us, but felt that if he stayed too long he would stagnate. He is a very dynamic person, so I suppose that it makes sense that he would want to keep moving. We will miss his unique presence in the house.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite\u2019s birthday trip to Paris has also been discussed. It won\u2019t happen for a while yet, but it\u2019s never a bad thing to plan in advance. Our plan is to use a door that Ms. Skitters and Lizette have established between Los Angeles and Paris. It will certainly be quicker than flying and none of us will need to apply to get a passport under our assumed names. Our identities will hold up to most scrutiny, but I\u2019m not sure they\u2019d hold up to that. I\u2019m looking forward to the trip though. I have never been to Paris. I guess I have to learn some French, won\u2019t I?<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> So, Lori finally convinced De La Rocha to go to therapy with me and Calamity. I think Lori\u2019s concerns were that De La Rocha keeps too firm a hold over the side of her that is Maria. She doesn\u2019t let the darker side out at all, which is not good. Compartmentalization is not a healthy way to deal with things. Trust me, I know. I saw how different she acted when she was closer to being Maria. She is a different person when she takes on that name. She needs to learn to combine the two. I know, easier said than done, but I\u2019m sure De La Rocha will get the help she needs at the Clinic. They have certainly done wonders for Calamity. Though she is still depressed about Gawain leaving she keeps going to therapy. I don\u2019t know if she talks about Gawain to her therapist or not. She is slowly coming around though. I just hope they can help De La Rocha reconcile her darker side, so there is not such a stark difference between Maria and De La Rocha as people.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> The topic of going into Arcadia to rescue Lori\u2019s friends came up again today. We likely will not be leaving until after the weddings, but conversations about the upcoming trip to get them back has come up again. I will admit that a part of me is looking forward to seeing what the Empress\u2019 realm looks like. I got to travel quite a bit when I worked for the Lady. I was an envoy several times and got to see a number of different Keeper\u2019s lands. M\u0336y\u0336 The Lady never had any dealings with the Violent Empress as far as I know. At least not while I was in her service, so her realm will be new to me. I know that we are going there to rescue Lori\u2019s friends, so it\u2019s not a sightseeing trip, but I am still curious. It will also be something of a departure from my past actions to remove someone from Arcadia instead of bringing them back to a Keeper\u2019s realm. The irony has not been lost on me, but that\u2019s is fine. There\u2019s also the fact that the last time I went willingly to Arcadia I was still a Loyalist. This time though will be different. It helps, I think, that we\u2019re not going to the Lady\u2019s realm. It won\u2019t be familiar to me and I won\u2019t be tempted to fall back into old habits or patterns while I\u2019m there. I also like to think that I\u2019m a different person than I used to be. I still haven\u2019t admitted to my therapist that I was a Loyalist. I have told him that I did things that I regret while in Arcadia, but haven\u2019t given him any specifics. I\u2019m still not sure who he reports to. I know he\u2019d report to Lowjack, which is fine. He already knows. But I\u2019m not sure if Sullivan would report to any of the other monarchs, and I don\u2019t really want to take the chance that he will. So, I have been vague about most of my past and I know he feels that me holding back has hampered my recovery. He has said as much in one or two sessions, but hasn\u2019t pushed me to reveal what I don\u2019t want to so far. In any case I have told him about our upcoming rescue mission and he has expressed concerns for our welfare, but I\u2019ve assured him that we\u2019ll be okay. We\u2019re going to have a guide to get us there, which I didn\u2019t mention, and there will be a number of us going. Some of us have had more experience in Arcadia than others. Insincere Marguerite and I have traveled quite a bit between realms and can help support our friends who have less experience than we do. At least I\u2019m hoping that my past experience will come in handy for something. It will mean that my past has helped my future in some small way. And that is something that I can live with.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> This has been the best Christmas of my entire life.<br /> <br /> So the eve of Christmas Eve (I think that is how I use the English) was our last pre-Christmas show until Saturday. I practiced all day. It was very well attended, and it went very well. I sang a sultry \u201cYou\u2019re a Mean One Mr. Grinch\u201d while Calamity did a little dance with it. I myself was up on a false wall. I had a stripy top and stripy socks, while she had the green body paint and one of her more fetish-y outfits. Certainly not from a cartoon, we. Then I did \u201cBaby It\u2019s Cold Outside\u201d with Juliette, and we had Santa Hats. I wore a suit, she dressed femme. It all went very well I think. She was the Mouse, I the Wolf. Perhaps I should get on stage more.<br /> <br /> After (still in the suit and hat) I went down to the audience. Yvette was there! It turned out later Julia had informed her I was performing. I spent the evening sitting with her, and chatting, and flirting. I think the Spirit of Christmas was on my side. Well that and remembering what she likes and dislikes, though she is not the same person she was. Still the whole thing went rather well. Yvette is beautiful. I want to be close to her. However, my heart is spoken for. I told her as much.<br /> <br /> While we were talking, Maria spent much of the night having presumably less romantic conversation with Twitch, but she seemed to be herself. She was very much Maria in her usual look apart from a couple Christmas ornaments in her hair. Julia sat by herself mostly, but Juliette and Jacob both stopped in to talk to her. Juliette herself was all over the place, including a flirty visit with Joan and Andromeda, but ended up spending quite some time with Brightstar and Neon, and she and Maria conspired to work together to seduce both. Brightstar seemed ready to stay the night anyway (she had her overnight bag) but they managed to snag Neon too, which Juliette seemed most pleased about.<br /> <br /> Before this she stopped by to say hi to Yvette and we talked, as a group and briefly she to I. She was worried about Julia, and I assured her I would be taking care of Julia that night, and she should have fun with my fellow Night Courtiers. Soon after they left, people were leaving so I took Yvette around the Dream House. We went up and I introduced her to the puppets. We almost kissed up there, but did not. I returned her to the mirror she came in (the ladies room) after she had been reflected in a smaller mirror in the catwalks that we could have her use on her next visit. Calamity followed us into the restroom while we were having our goodbyes\u2026, which was jarring, but she clearly meant well. She remained and talked while we stood awkwardly. We kissed after she realized we wanted to be alone and had walked out. Then (very quickly after) Yvette was through the mirror and gone.<br /> <br /> I went back and found Julia who actually looked mildly surprised to see I. She needn\u2019t have been. I kissed her there as publicly as I could with the house mostly cleared out, and took her upstairs. Our night had perhaps less of the lightshow compared to Juliette\u2019s and Maria\u2019s, but we had a good time. I love Julia Oldacre deeply. I am marrying her after all.<br /> <br /> Last Christmas Eve I was alone in the House. Decorations were up, no power, but I did my best. I would look at them and sing Christmas songs. I remember running through the house singing, imagining the party I was attending in my mind, but then I would remember, I was alone. Sadly.<br /> <br /> This Christmas Eve at breakfast I talked everyone into Caroling. Well, almost everyone Jacob and Luna did not wish to go. Odd the Winter Courtier did not wish to indulge in a Winter tradition. Anyway, Calamity kept calling it Wassailing, but that is not proper English. She should know, being (very) American. After breakfast, Juliette got a handmade sweater from Rowan in the mail. She still loves Juliette, it seems. That added a touch of melancholy, and perhaps confusion, to my love.<br /> <br /> But there was no time for melancholy, it was soon time for Caroling! We all went out for it, I putting Santa Hats on each head. Maria demurred, but agreed to put the little ornaments back in. I printed out songbooks for everyone and book covers with Merry on one side and Christmas on the other. We walked until our feet hurt and sang until our voices hurt, and then came back for the eggnog and cookies Jacob and Luna had prepared. The rest of the evening was quiet and full of companionship, but we retired before too late, Juliette commenting on little hoofbeats on the roof. The family stayed together, as it should be. I was (and am) happy.<br /> <br /> Apparently they don\u2019t actually do \u201cscary ghost stories\u201d in America whatever the song says.<br /> <br /> Last Christmas morning I opened presents under the tree, alone. I mean, I sang Christmas songs, but I was alone. Presents I had made myself and wrapped myself and put under the tree myself, because there was no one else. I put the tree so the light shone through, as the building still had no power, and gave the illusion the lights lit up. But I was alone. I admit, I cried. Helplessly.<br /> <br /> This Christmas morning I rattled the vents at ten. Later than Juliette was worried I would. I am not unkind. Usually. We all trundled downstairs to the tree, the Motley, Luna, and Stasia. Juliette kissed everyone (with varying intensity) under the mistletoe. We opened presents. The family enjoyed the lockets, and everyone ooed and aaahed over the paintings we got from Julia of our lovers.<br /> <br /> Julia gave I lovely paintings of herself holding flowers and looking wistfully into a darkened sky and I leaning over a rafter with a playfully seductive look on my face, and prints of a smirking Maria in her leathers leaning on a wall and Juliette singing on stage looking significantly at the viewer. Juliette recording a song for I about I. Maria got I thin sheepskin gloves and a black leather choker with a silver cat silhouette.<br /> <br /> Outside my lovers, Calamity gave I a dream stored in a glass ball, Jacob gave I some footcovers that do not cover the bottoms of my feet he handmade in leather as well as a CD of French carols. And Luna gave I a knife. A fancy knife but a knife. Odd.<br /> <br /> The party broke up for awhile while Juliette and Maria went to have lunch with her father, but that is okay. They were back. Tomorrow we visit the Oldacres.<br /> <br /> Last year on Christmas I was all alone in the world. Not this year. This year I have lovers, a Fianc\u00e9e, good friends, power and running water. I am thankful. This Christmas I will remember as long as I live. Happily.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Yesterday was Juliette\u2019s Birthday and Valentines Day. Juliette had Dark Kimberly jump out of her cake, and gratefully assisted her with getting the frosting off. It was a fun day. Her favorite \u201cgift\u201d may have been Maria leaving her old job to be bouncer/doorman for us. Means less money for the family, but we do fine, and see Maria more.<br /> <br /> I enjoy celebrating the birthdays of members of the family, and love Juliette very deeply. Fond as she is of attention, having her special day she had a ball. It really was quite the party, and well attended at that.<br /> <br /> I almost suggested, given Dark Kimberly\u2019s known proclivities, Juliette put her on the St. Andrews but I didn\u2019t. We got a St. Andrews Cross on Candlemas that we put in the room with the punching bag. It\u2019s sturdy, and Andromeda designed it so it could hold Maria even when she strained, though not if Contracts were used. And Juliette (with Separation) Julia (With Fleeting Autumn) and I (in general) can get out if needed on our own, though there is a hidden key reachable from the shackles. Pushing Maria harder and harder into her passions while remaining solidly in control of her was getting more and more difficult for someone like I whom she could easily throw around like a rag doll. With the cross I can push her harder and deeper into our shared mindscape. Calamity might want to use it as well; she hasn\u2019t yet, but she likes that sort of thing, though she is much, much more into giving out pain than I am, and while Maria and Julia are submissive, Julia does not care for pain really and Maria only wants what will drive her on, which I am comfortable with.<br /> <br /> While I mainly got it for Maria, Julia has some interest in being the damsel in distress. We also may use it with White Maria, who has returned since Calamity used her Oniromancy to help convince her parents to let her choose who to marry. Like her namesake, she likes to be pushed. Juliette has no interest in such at all, which is fine, and I promised not to try to talk her into getting on it. Maria thinks if she tries it she will enjoy it, as Juliette enjoys sensation and especially for Julia it is all about sensation, but she agreed not to push her. Maybe she will come around in time, when she sees it as something we explore together, not mimicking a torture scene or dungeon.<br /> <br /> And of course Calamity can\u2019t be chained on it or she will destroy it.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Calamity, she is still handling Gawain leaving poorly. I am sympathetic. It seemed very sudden, though he got more and more withdrawn at the end before vanishing just before New Years. She is taking it hard. I am there for her as I can be, but I can only do so much. Stasia is having more luck. I hope things improve.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Today we promenaded on the Santa Monica Pier on the afternoon of the Vernal Equinox, as Jolie retakes control of the city. Lowjack was not a bad ruler, very quiet. I wore some tight bellbottom pants, a tasseled midriff showing shirt, and sunglasses. Julia really, really liked the outfit. I will have to bear that in mind. Juliette seemed to like it too, just less\u2026intensely. Maria seemed neutral, beyond not crazy about me showing less leg.<br /> <br /> We have wedding dates settled, as we intended to before Spring. Julia and I will marry on the evening of Juin 6th, a Saturday, then Juliette and Maria will on Juin 13th, a week later. Then a week\u2019s honeymoon, arriving back by the 20th for the show. Also, we are traveling to Paris after Halloween this Novembre. It should be fun. Just for a few days; with the Door we were shown by Lizette and Skitters, getting back and forth will be quick. I am looking forward to it.<br /> <br /> But before any of that is Walpurgis, and the night we get full control of the Dream House. We will refresh our pledge on the 25th of Avril; Luna will join and Ace and Gawain out. Ace is moving on after Walpurgis.<br /> <br /> A lot is going on, and it will be a busy year. I am so excited.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXXXVII</i><br /> <br /> Not a great deal to add, honestly. Lorelei, Calamity and Insincere Marguerite got sky high results for their performances. For Lori and Insincere Marguerite it was their personal records. (Calamity\u2019s was still the opening <i>Bloody Creature Poster Girl</i> performance.) All three used Vainglory and Verdant Spring to boost their rolls in addition to anything else. DLR passed a fairly straightforward Resolve + Composure with two bonus dice not to get predatory.<br /> <br /> Obviously, behind the scenes both Ace and Gawain had to drop due to changing schedules in life over the years. Calamity did lose Clarity from Gawain leaving but did not gain a derangement.<br /> <br /> Expect Lorelei and Calamity\u2019s takes on the downtime next time. And I will see you then, as they emerge on Walpurgis Night. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T01:29:59-07:00","id":1123799,"title":"","content":"I am not going to lie here, Gawain's departure kind of threw me for a loop. I had been expecting for there to be more of a revelation on why he had to leave the group, while also giving a reason as to why he was going alone (if you pardon Ace's own departure). The lack of one being present feels...abrupt to say the least, which is odd considering the early lead-up we got about said departure. I am aware that these journals are delayed, both in being written and collected in general, but the way it was included in Jacob's journal makes it seem like the news only happened before the session, leaving little chance for preparation.<br /> <br /> I apologize if that comes across as overly critical about such a major development. It is just that previous major developments have had more narrative behind them so that they didn't feel so strange, whereas Gawain's departure happens with little fanfare.<br /> <br /> Granted, Gawain leaving the motley without them following him isn't an easy narrative to spin, especially since he was such a key member of the group and a major love interest. Him leaving is an understandable reason, and it is best not to make it into a huge scene about a player leaving. It is just that I am struggling to think of why the character is leaving as he is. Perhaps more light will be shined upon it when we get more than just Jacob's journal on the matter...or at least some rational from other characters.<br /> <br /> It probably doesn't help that the documentation regarding it occurs almost immediately after talk of Christmas, when Calamity gains a lovely painted image of Gawain from Julia. Unfortunate timing there.<br /> <br /> Again, I apologize if this seems like complaining or being overtly critical. I'm just...well, confused by what was a nessecity.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, so that I am not just fixated on one facet of this session, it sounds like the characters had an amazing Chistmas. In general, the holidays sound like things that Changelings could get very fantastical with, given their talents and (for a lack of a better term) the magic at their disposal. Not sure how Autumn court would go about a Halloween party though. I get the feeling they would be a bit too...well, good at it.<br /> <br /> Also, it was great reading Insincere Margeurite being so excited for once...and heartrending when her previous Chrismas was elaborated on. So glad she has gone up in the world, in so many ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T03:03:52-07:00","id":1123813,"title":"","content":"There are OOC reasons that it was handled that way. I can't really say more than that. The best option was to move on, and let the game heal. The rest of the aspects of why the decision was made are not going to be aired out here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 08-02-2017, 06:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T11:09:00-07:00","id":1123945,"title":"","content":"I understand; consider the querie resolved. Thank you for the prompt response Baroness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T15:52:50-07:00","id":1124049,"title":"","content":"No problem, thank you.<br /> <br /> As for the second part I agree, and thought that last session went especially well. IM's before and after experiences (touched in first in the short story awhile back now this) humanizes the character a bit more, and the ending of her being togather with them this year feels very christmas-y.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T14:03:38-07:00","id":1128570,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s been about four months. It\u2019s Walpurgis Night, one year from the founding of the Dream House. What events are taking place at the Lady by the Sea?<br /> <br /> This time we have Calamity and Lorelei\u2019s coverage of the downtime. <br /> <i><br /> Session LXXXVIII</i><br /> <b><br /> Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Okay, so maybe it took me a <u>tiny</u> bit longer than I\u2019d intended to pick up a new blank book to use as a diary. Like, maybe\u2026 four months or so. My bad. Things have been slow for a while, and\u2026 well, there were some things I didn\u2019t feel particularly keen on dwelling on at the time, too. But yesterday was a <u>very</u> important day for my motley, so I guess it\u2019s time to take up the quill and continue this chronicle once more.<br /> <br /> Okay\u2026 how to sum up the last hundred-plus days? Well, first thing\u2019s first. I\u2019m going to get the painful part out of the way quickly, like ripping off a band-aid. Gawain left. It was\u2026 really sudden, though I suppose the signs were there in hindsight. He\u2019d been distancing himself from the rest of us for some time, gallivanting off into the Hedge to gather ingredients for that little fox thing he was making, or closeting himself at his forge for hours at a time. He started moving his stuff out of the Dream House just after Christmas while Calamity was in Seattle helping Stasia pack up for her big move, but he asked us not to tell her about it. He wanted to tell her himself\u2026 and I don\u2019t think any of us believed we had the right to take that away from him.<br /> <br /> I feel his absence every day. Sometimes it\u2019s almost physical, like sliding your tongue over that place where you lost a tooth when you were a kid. He was a true friend, a lover, a brother\u2026 and now he\u2019s gone. I don\u2019t blame him for leaving\u2026 his reasons (which were his own and not mine to discuss here) made sense, and he\u2019d thought them through to their logical conclusions. I don\u2019t hate him for choosing to walk away from us. I could never hate him, not in a million years. But it hurts. And what kills me about this is that I know that no matter how much his leaving hurt <u>me</u>, it\u2019s peanuts compared to how Calamity feels.<br /> <br /> She\u2019s\u2026 she\u2019s like a completely different person sometimes. It\u2019s hard to watch. She\u2019s usually so strong, so together, so sure of herself and everything around her. Now it\u2019s like the one thing she was absolutely sure of in her life has been taken away from her (which I suppose isn\u2019t that far from the truth), so she\u2019s not certain of <u>anything</u> anymore. He broke up with her when she got back from Seattle, but since he\u2019d already moved all of his stuff out of the Dream House, he made a clean break of it and didn\u2019t linger afterward.<br /> <br /> I rushed up to her and threw my arms around her as the tears started up. She tried to twist away from me, but I didn\u2019t allow it. I felt two of her shards sink into my flesh, and the pain came, and the blood started to flow. \u201cYou\u2019re hurt, Lori,\u201d Calamity said with a quaver, but I just kept holding on to her, knowing that she needed it then. \u201cThat\u2019s the chance you take whenever you get close to <u>anyone</u>, though,\u201d I said as we hugged. A little Hallmark, sure, but I think she needed to hear it.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, we were <u>forced</u> to disengage a few seconds later. I heard a slight hissing noise, and Calamity sucked in her breath in obvious pain. I backed away, and noticed that my blood was <u>sizzling</u> against Calamity\u2019s skin, leaving angry red weals when it had been wiped away. That was our first clue as to the nature of Calamity\u2019s frailty. For a while we weren\u2019t sure of the details; she didn\u2019t seem to react to most other blood in that way. She says now that it\u2019s because my blood is \u201cinnocent.\u201d I\u2019m not so sure about that, but until we have more information I guess it\u2019s the best theory available.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s see, what else? Well, Marguerite and D have a new toy to share. It\u2019s a sexual harness called a \u201cSaint Andrew\u2019s Cross,\u201d which binds its subject spread-eagled to an X-shaped frame. They had to order it specially from Andromeda, and it\u2019s much stronger than the versions available commercially. D can\u2019t escape from the bonds without activating Contracts. I\u2026 I don\u2019t judge people\u2019s kinks, as a general rule, and I certainly have no objection to D and Marguerite exploring that side of their relationship. But I won\u2019t deny that the cross makes me uncomfortable. I don\u2019t even like being in the same room with it. Both D and Marguerite have subtly implied that I might enjoy the experience if I chose to join them on one side or the other of that kind of play, but\u2026 I just can\u2019t. I can\u2019t be bound again, and I <u>won\u2019t</u> do that to another person. Not even if they\u2019re willing.<br /> <br /> Sometimes it depresses me that I can\u2019t share in that part of D\u2019s life. But at least she can get her kicks with Marguerite and be back in my arms a few hours later. And she doesn\u2019t judge me for this one streak of prudishness, for which I\u2019m eternally grateful.<br /> <br /> Oh, and speaking of my fianc\u00e9e, D\u2019s working at the Dream House full-time now. When Gawain left, we had a vacancy in the security staff, and D very sensibly pointed out that we needed someone to fill that void who could handle the sort of supernatural audiences we get on a daily basis. So she gave her notice at the hospital and quit her job as an X-ray tech. I have mixed feelings about this. I mean, of course I\u2019m over the moon about the fact that she no longer has to leave me at the Dream House to go to work three days a week. More time with my honey is a definite plus no matter how you look at it. But I know she was clinging to that job as part of her defiance of a stereotype, and I can tell that giving it up was a real wrench for her. But she\u2019s vowed to maintain all of her certifications so that she can take up the job again at some point in the future, so that\u2019s okay.<br /> <br /> In other news\u2026 I think things are pretty much done between me and Rowan. A part of me is really sad about that, as she\u2019s a wonderful, beautiful, kind-hearted woman, and anyone would be lucky to earn her affection. But I think in the end it\u2019ll be better for both of us that we broke things off. Kinda. Sorta. I mean, after New Year\u2019s we mutually decided that it would be better to spend some time apart. She needs someone who can devote everything to her, and she deserves someone like that. And I just can\u2019t do that, with all of my other relationships and commitments. Plus, I\u2019m getting married, and her old-fashioned values won\u2019t allow her to get past that simple fact (and that\u2019s not a criticism, just an observation). She doesn\u2019t feel it would be right to become an accomplice in my \u201cadultery.\u201d<br /> <br /> Still\u2026 there have been moments of weakness. The most prominent of those came in late January, when she was very lonely and maybe a little drunk. I might have had a few drinks that night myself, come to think of it. And she started talking about how much she missed me and how much she loved me and how beautiful I was and she looked at me with those big soulful eyes of hers and\u2026 well, dammit, I just was not equal to the task of saying no to her. We spent the night together. It was good\u2026 but it wasn\u2019t right. It wasn\u2019t <u>healthy</u> for either of us. I\u2019d bet you money that Rowan cried about it later\u2026 I know I did. D tried to comfort me by telling me that everyone makes mistakes and that if the worst thing about me is that I love too much, well, there are worse faults\u2026 and that helped, a little. But I have to be stronger than that in the future. I have to be <u>better</u>.<br /> <br /> But enough dwelling on the negative. Speaking of \u201cbettering myself,\u201d I do have some progress to report on my academic endeavors. I spent most of January studying, boning up on basic math, history, science, and the like\u2026 and I took the GED. I passed with flying colors, if I may toot my own horn for a moment. I mean, it wasn\u2019t <u>easy</u> or anything like that\u2026 I only did so well because I put in the work. I\u2019m sure someone really smart could have just breezed through it, but that\u2019s neither here nor there. The upshot of this rambling paragraph is that Lorelei Grace is now officially a High School graduate\u2026 which is something Juliette Wells could never boast. Well, okay\u2026 technically my <u>fetch</u> graduated High School, but the <u>real</u> Juliette Wells never did. Dad was ecstatic, and he <u>insisted</u> upon taking me and Maria out to dinner to celebrate.<br /> <br /> I have also sort of quietly filled out and submitted a couple of college applications for the Fall semester. As far as I know, nobody else knows about that\u2026 not even D (though it\u2019s always possible that Marguerite knows, I suppose). I just\u2026 if things don\u2019t go my way, I don\u2019t want people to pity me. I don\u2019t think I could take that. Plus, there\u2019s a very real chance that we won\u2019t be around when the Fall semester starts up at all\u2026 but that\u2019s a different topic, and I\u2019ll get to it soon enough. Until then, I\u2019ll just quietly volunteer to check the mail every day so that I can intercept any letters from Santa Monica College or UCLA.<br /> <br /> And while we\u2019re on the subject of personal growth, I should probably mention that Maria\u2019s started going to therapy with Jacob and Calamity. She resisted for a few weeks, and pointedly pretended not to know what I was talking about for a few weeks more, but eventually I managed to convince her that the psychiatrists employed by the Winter Court might be able to help her come to grips with her darker nature. I\u2019m hoping that she\u2019ll be able to integrate the old \u201cMaria\u201d personality in a healthy way, to prevent it from surging forward like it did with Twitch and Hunting Hawk last December. It\u2019s probably too early to tell if there\u2019s been any progress, but here\u2019s hoping.<br /> <br /> So February 14th 2015 rolled around right on schedule. I used to hate sharing a birthday with Valentine\u2019s Day \u2013 all my old boyfriends in High School used it as an excuse to only get me one gift, for example \u2013 but I\u2019m a bit more sanguine about it now. It fits my nature, so why not own it? Technically, by the mortal calendar, I turned fifty-five years old. As near as I can tell biologically, I\u2019m about twenty years old. And finally, according to my driver\u2019s license, I just turned twenty-two (which I admit is mostly because I wanted to be able to buy booze when I obtained my new identity). So I guess you can take your pick as to which birthday it was.<br /> <br /> I admit it\u2026 I pouted a little when I came down to breakfast that morning and none of my girls were naked and covered with food, but it was mostly in good fun. And the party the motley threw that night more than made up for it. All of my closest friends were there (including but not limited to the motley, Oleander, Brightstar and Neon, Rowan, Joan and Andromeda, Captain Jack, Princess Jolie, Desiree, and Gloria)\u2026 and the piece de resistance was a <u>huge</u> cake containing none other than Dark Kimberly in an itsy-bitsy teeny-weeny black-and-purple French bikini. She looked unbearably sexy covered with icing, and I expressed my appreciation with a long lingering kiss. \u201cI\u2019ve never had this flavor of cake before,\u201d I said huskily, \u201cbut I like it.\u201d<br /> <br /> That night was an exercise in sybaritic excess, and I couldn\u2019t be happier about it. So many birthday kisses!<br /> <br /> I should probably mention that Brightstar is kinda-sorta officially my girlfriend now, too. I know, I know\u2026 I\u2019m spreading myself too thin again, but this is a little different. She\u2019s not as needy as some, and she\u2019s perfectly willing to share me with the others. We always have a lot of fun when we hang out together, and she\u2019s positively <u>cute</u> in her efforts to ensure that she\u2019s not stepping on any toes when she spends time with me. I don\u2019t actually see her as often as I do any of my other girls, but we\u2019ve both agreed that what we\u2019ve found is definitely more than casual.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve also settled into a comfortable friendship with Neon these days. The two of us have slept together a few times, both with Brightstar and with D (yummy), though I think both of us are considering our relationship more along the lines of \u201cfriends with benefits\u201d than anything truly romantic. Although thinking along those lines\u2026 well, I know I shouldn\u2019t meddle, but I couldn\u2019t help but notice that the one time Neon and Rowan met each other, there was a bit of a spark. Mostly from Neon, it\u2019s true, but\u2026 I know she likes \u201cinnocent\u201d girls (like Brightstar) and feels the urge to protect them from the world. And you don\u2019t get much more innocent than Rowan. I wonder if Neon might eventually be able to give Rowan the attention and devotion she needs and deserves?<br /> <br /> The seasons turned as expected in March, and Princess Jolie once again took the mantle of leadership in our little community. It was a lovely ceremony as always, and yours truly was once again asked to sing (I gladly accepted, of course). After the party, the motley and I headed out to the Pier to relax for a bit. Marguerite decided to give me and Julia a bit of a treat, and got dolled up in 60s-inspired clothing. It wasn\u2019t anything too ostentatious, really\u2026 just some flared-cuff pants and a fringed top, but she wore it well. It made me nostalgic for my own youth, and judging by the looks Julia was giving her beloved, she <u>really</u> liked the aesthetic.<br /> <br /> That was around the time that we finally set dates for our respective wedding ceremonies. We had all agreed that we wanted the ceremonies to be close to each other, but not on the same day. This was mostly because we are all going to have major roles in both of the weddings, and it seemed like it would be exhausting to do everything at once. Marguerite and Julia are going first as they\u2019ve been engaged longer, on June 6th. Maria and I will be getting married the following weekend, on June 13th. The four of us will honeymoon together during the week following the second ceremony. I think we\u2019ve just about decided on St. Martin. I initially pushed for Hawaii after hearing Monica talk it up last year, but as long as I\u2019m with the girls I love someplace warm and tropical, I\u2019ll be happy. And hey! I hear St. Martin has parrots. Nobody looks at you funny if you talk to parrots\u2026<br /> <br /> There are ten thousand details I could bring up about the weddings at this point, but I\u2019d just be working myself into a lather about it for no good reason. In like six weeks I\u2019m going to be <u>married</u>. To a beautiful punk-rock Hispanic woman. In California. In 2015. Process all of that for a minute, Juliette, and then try to wrap your brain around it. No, it\u2019s too big. But I feel like I should mention a few important details.<br /> <br /> Yes, Gawain finished the rings for the four of us and delivered them quietly one day when he knew Calamity would be away. He seems to be doing well. I\u2019m glad.<br /> <br /> Yes, I\u2019ve been fitted for a dress, chosen the style, and paid my deposit to a Changeling-friendly tailor in L.A. (the same one who made those pajamas D bought for me last year, actually). I\u2019m confident that she can create a <u>beautiful</u> wedding dress which both shows me off to my best advantage and accommodates my unusual anatomy.<br /> <br /> Yes, D has decided upon her outfit for the ceremony as well, as have Marguerite and Julia (as \u201cbest man\u201d and maid of honor respectively). It\u2019s going to be a wedding to remember, I can promise you that. As a side note, I have also been fitted for my bridesmaid dress as Julia\u2019s maid of honor. Considering her Gothic leanings, I shouldn\u2019t have worried\u2026 but it\u2019s nice to know I won\u2019t be in frilly pink taffeta or anything.<br /> <br /> Yes, we\u2019ve chosen the venues for the ceremonies and the receptions. It should come as no surprise to anyone that both receptions will be held at the Dream House. I mean\u2026 we have a venue that\u2019s perfectly suited to serving food to a large number of people, the stage can serve as a small dance floor, and we\u2019re already set up for music and such. We\u2019d be fools not to take advantage of that.<br /> <br /> Yes, the details of the cakes and the rest of the food have been settled, including wine and other alcoholic beverages. Yes, invitations have been printed and are about to be sent out. Yes, the minister has been hired (duh!). Yes, I have the paperwork in order for my impending change of nomenclature, though I won\u2019t actually submit it until the day itself. Yes, we\u2019re going to make sure that we\u2019re back from our honeymoon in time to attend the Summer Court\u2019s Solstice festival. Yes, yes, yes\u2026<br /> <br /> There, see? A lather. Breathe, Lori. Everything is on track. Six-and-a-half weeks from now you\u2019ll be Lorelei de la Rocha. And after that\u2026<br /> <br /> After that we\u2019re finally going into the Hedge to rescue Missy and Jane. Once the Summer Court is in power, the motley is going to join me as I return to Arcadia and attempt to rescue my two friends from the Violet Empress. I\u2019m\u2026 not thinking too specifically about that trip just yet, as I\u2019m afraid I might lose my nerve. The Empress frightens me more than just about anything else in the world\u2026 but I have to rescue them, if it\u2019s still possible. I <u>have</u> to.<br /> <br /> If we\u2019re quick enough, I <u>might</u> still be back in time for the Fall semester\u2026<br /> <br /> Oh, and assuming the timing works out, the motley has also made tentative plans to visit Paris on or around Marguerite\u2019s birthday, as a special treat for her. Yep, just for her. Not like I\u2019ve been dreaming about seeing the City of Love for my entire life or anything like that\u2026<br /> <br /> I just want to say one last thing before I return to current events. A couple of weeks ago, Luna decided to finally take the plunge and join the motley officially. So I have a new sister of sorts, who still kind of scares me sometimes but I know will protect me and my loved ones with everything she has. I haven\u2019t asked if she\u2019ll be joining us in Arcadia yet, but I can\u2019t deny that her skills would be invaluable, so I sort of hope so.<br /> <br /> Well, I think I\u2019ve hit most of the bullet points of the last four months, which brings us to the present. As I said at the beginning of this entry, yesterday was a very important day for the motley for a variety of reasons. First and foremost, it was Walpurgis night, which marked the end of our one-year obligation to the Freehold to operate the Dream House with an eye toward creating a ready glamour supply for its occupants. It was also the one-year anniversary of our opening night show.<br /> <br /> We decided to mark the occasion with a special night of entertainment. The main show was open to all, but the after-show was strictly for Platinum Pass holders (in other words, Changelings). We went all-out and pulled out all the stops, making sure to give our customers a show they would never forget. It served as a great example of how much our respective talents have improved over the past twelve months, actually.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t debut any new numbers last night, but I did revisit an old favorite. A year ago, I opened our very first show with Labelle\u2019s \u201cLady Marmalade,\u201d which I had not performed since. As it\u2019s a real crowd-pleaser, and allows a lot of our regular backup singers and dancers to strut their stuff, I decided that the time had come to dust it off. Marguerite opted to sing backup for me on that one this time, which was fun. The number was\u2026 memorable, as I\u2019d intended. I probably haven\u2019t performed that well since our Christmas show, at least.<br /> <br /> Calamity and I also did our \u201cBloody Creature Poster Girl\u201d number, which never fails to rile up the crowds. I gave it a bit of a twist this time\u2026 one which I should have thought of long ago. After the incident with the Briar Wolves last year, I couldn\u2019t bring myself to throw out that cute sundress I\u2019d worn while I was serving as bait\u2026 even though it was slashed to holy hell and covered in blood. Well, it occurred to me that it would go very well with that number. I added a bit of runny mascara, and suddenly I really looked the part. And Calamity\u2019s dance was, as always, stunning.<br /> <br /> Ace and Marguerite also reprised their popular numbers. In Ace\u2019s case, this meant his now-legendary one-man show version of <u>Mad Max: Beyond Thunderdome</u>. Marguerite regally belted her way through \u201cNon, Je Ne Regrette Rien,\u201d strutting across the stage and glancing imperiously at the darkened audience. They ate both numbers up, of course.<br /> <br /> I was free for the latter parts of the show, so I spent my time mingling with the audience as per usual. Okay, so <u>maybe</u> I hang out by the doors more than I used to, leaning up against my fianc\u00e9e in her tight black \u201csecurity\u201d t-shirt and maybe occasionally fondling her biceps or something, but who can blame me?<br /> <br /> Everyone who was anyone was there last night. All four monarchs were good enough to show up, as were most of our regulars. Monica even brought a new girl along\u2026 a pretty black girl named Angelica. I spoke with her for a bit; she seemed nice to me and maybe the tiniest bit flirty. I could tell that Monica was already harboring a major crush on the new arrival, though, so I didn\u2019t pursue that particular romantic avenue last night (even though Monica\u2019s track record would seem to indicate that this crush of hers is destined for disaster). Turns out it\u2019s a good thing I went that way.<br /> <br /> White Maria was there, blissfully single\u2026 oh yeah, I never wrote about that, did I? Well, Calamity\u2019s dream shaping worked like a charm, and she and I (posing as wedding planners) were able to convince White Maria\u2019s parents to call off the arranged marriage. So that\u2019s okay.<br /> <br /> I got hugs and kisses from most of the usual suspects\u2026 Joan and Andromeda, Princess Jolie, even Captain Jack (who had somehow managed to slip into the background of my \u201cLady Marmalade\u201d number\u2026 dressed just like my other backup singers!). The Princess was quick to tell me that all of the monarchs were pleased as punch at the work we\u2019d done with the Dream House, and they counted the experiment as a flying success. She\u2019s\u2026 kind of back with Felicity now? It\u2019s hard to explain. Our neighbor is seeing Jolie on a provisional basis, but still seems pretty hung-up on Marguerite. Personally I think that ship has sailed. Felicity should wake up and realize that she\u2019s got a chance with someone most of the Freehold would give their right arm to date.<br /> <br /> But that\u2019s neither here nor there. I actually spent most of my time last night in the company of <u>another</u> monarch\u2026 Queen Charlotte. Now, the Autumn Queen and I have never been particularly close, but she was really laying on the charm last night, and I ate it up like Gawain\u2019s crepes. I\u2019ve always loved being the center of attention, and she was lavishing me with the sort of attention that\u2019s very hard for me to ignore. I excused myself before things went too far; there was still the after-party to think about at that point.<br /> <br /> Rowan was there, and she was\u2026 a little twitchy. I always feel so bad when I see her like that\u2026 it\u2019s obvious that she\u2019s still hung up on me, and I hate the fact that my presence hurts her. But I can\u2019t be what she wants, and I really think it will be better for her in the long run if we make this a relatively clean break.<br /> <br /> Oleander was there, and as per usual I planted myself in her lap and lost myself in her embrace for a while. She\u2019s doing well, and it was nice to see her during the week for a change. We\u2019ve made tentative plans to get together this weekend for a nice romantic dinner.<br /> <br /> Brightstar and Neon were there along with a few other members of the Unseelie Court (I think I saw Della heading off with Marguerite and Julia after the show, actually). Brightstar sort of coyly asked if she could expect my company last night. At that point, I still didn\u2019t know what my plans were, so I gave her a noncommittal answer. Neon was as cynical and acerbic as ever, but I\u2019ve learned to see the smile behind the scowl when it comes to that one.<br /> <br /> D <u>also</u> asked me if I had plans for the night, which nearly made me reconsider the plans I was in the process of making. \u201cWell...\u201d I said, looking down and feigning little-girl innocence, \u201cI think Queen Charlotte might have been trying to <u>seduce</u> me.\u201d<br /> <br /> D\u2019s brow wrinkled. \u201cBe careful with that one, babe,\u201d she said softly and seriously. \u201cShe\u2019s hungry. I can tell.\u201d<br /> <br /> I gave her a smile. \u201cYou know me,\u201d I said, hoping to reassure her.<br /> <br /> \u201cYep,\u201d she said, not backing down, \u201cand I know how you get when someone wants you that much.\u201d<br /> <br /> I leaned in to kiss her. \u201cYou want me to back off?\u201d I asked, looking her in the eye so that she could tell I meant it.<br /> <br /> She sighed. \u201cNo,\u201d she said after a moment. \u201cJust promise me you\u2019ll be careful.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI promise,\u201d I said. That being the case, D opted to go and see what Brightstar and Neon were up to, and I continued to mingle. <br /> <br /> There were some grumbles from the mortal regulars when we emptied the club at the end of the show, but I don\u2019t think anyone was seriously upset. Once only changelings remained, the monarchs called our motley up to the stage. There was a short speech about how the Freehold appreciated all that we had done in its support, and praising our efforts to build the Dream House into both a safe haven and a smorgasbord of free glamour, and a round of applause from our peers.<br /> <br /> We were released from our pledge officially (though technically the terms of the pledge had expired at midnight anyway). Those who wanted to were free to leave the Dream House, while those who opted to stay were given the choice of taking partial ownership of the structure and its assets. Most of us opted to stay.<br /> <br /> Ace decided to leave.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s right, our Liverpudlian friend\u2019s wanderlust finally got the better of him, and he\u2019s decided to light out for the territories. In his own words, he has decided to \u201cwalk the Earth, like Kane.\u201d Sigh. <br /> <br /> I\u2019m really going to miss him. In the wake of Gawain\u2019s departure, it\u2019s particularly hard. I know both of them are still out there, but they\u2019re not <u>here</u>. They\u2019re not a presence in my life every day, and it\u2019s like\u2026 I don\u2019t know, it\u2019s like phantom limb syndrome or something. I\u2019m acutely aware of the absence, and it\u2019s like an itch that I can\u2019t scratch. I just hope the sensation eases with time.<br /> <br /> Jacob\u2019s the only boy left in the motley now. Most of the Freehold is looking at him like they don\u2019t know whether to envy or pity him.<br /> <br /> But hey, let\u2019s focus on the positive for now, shall we? It\u2019s official; I\u2019m now part owner of the Dream House, instead of just an employee. D\u2019s got a stake as well, as she\u2019s now the Summer Court\u2019s representative in the endeavor (though relations between her and Viscount Augustine remain cordial-yet-frosty at the best of times).<br /> <br /> So things were winding down, and even our changeling guests started saying their goodnights. I was getting questioning glances from several directions, so I decided to play it cool. I took a seat alone at a table near the stage to see who would approach me first. It was very nearly a tie\u2026 Brightstar got up first, but as soon as she saw what was going on, Queen Charlotte also rose and swept in, taking my hand and kissing it before the poor Night Courtier could even approach.<br /> <br /> \u201cMight I expect the pleasure of your company tonight, Lorelei?\u201d she asked, her voice heavy with desire.<br /> <br /> I looked over at Brightstar, who mostly looked confused, but not upset. \u201cA moment, your Majesty?\u201d I asked. Charlotte answered with an imperious nod.<br /> <br /> I took Brightstar\u2019s hand in both of my own. \u201cWould you mind if I took a raincheck tonight, sweetie?\u201d I asked softly.<br /> <br /> She shook her head. \u201cIt\u2019s fine,\u201d she said, maybe a tad disappointed but not angry. \u201cI\u2019m sure I can find some way to occupy my time.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou want to get together some time over the next few days?\u201d I asked. \u201cJust the two of us. We can even make it a real date, and do dinner and a movie or something, if you want.\u201d<br /> <br /> She threw me a smile that (literally) lit up the room. \u201cSounds great. I\u2019ve got plans for the next couple of nights, though. Sunday okay with you?\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cIt\u2019s a date,\u201d I promised. D latched on to Brightstar and Neon as they left, and I say good for her. I\u2019m sure all three of them had a wonderful time together last night.<br /> <br /> Things didn\u2019t end so happily for everyone, unfortunately. Monica and Angelica had some sort of falling-out at some point during the evening, though I didn\u2019t learn the truth of it until later. All I knew at the time was that Angelica didn\u2019t want to leave with Monica, so D and the L.A. girls offered to give her a lift to the apartment where the Freehold is putting her up. She accepted, which made Monica unhappy but was probably for the best in the long run.<br /> <br /> Before I left for the evening, I noticed Calamity walking out of the theater with a grim look on her face and a phone in her hand. Begging Charlotte\u2019s pardon, I followed her to see what was up. I managed to gather from her end of the conversation that Angelica had recently escaped from the dreaded Director, and that she was pissed at Monica because our verdant friend had spilled those beans to Calamity. This set off all sorts of alarm bells in my head, but Calamity assured me that she and her Winter Court handlers had the situation well in hand.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t relax until D and I had texted back and forth several times, and she let me know that she and the others had dropped Angelica off and were all fine. That was a load off my mind.<br /> <br /> I rejoined Charlotte in the rapidly emptying theater a few moments later. I turned a smoldering look on the predatory monarch once we had relative privacy. \u201cI\u2019m all yours, Your Majesty,\u201d I said breathlessly, and she gave me this\u2026 <u>look</u>. I really don\u2019t know how else to describe it, but it held me in place like a butterfly pinned to a card. She walked toward the doors, crooking her finger at me, and I followed her like a shot. I didn\u2019t even grab a change of clothes or an overnight bag.<br /> <br /> Last night was\u2026 wow. I mean, just\u2026 wow. Charlotte knew what she wanted, and she just took it, regardless of my feelings on the subject. Okay, that sentence makes it sound brutal and nonconsensual, and it was neither of those things. It\u2019s more like\u2026 she had little regard for what specific actions or attentions I wanted at any given moment, and concentrated more on her own desires. Fortunately for me, part of what she desired was to give me enough pleasure to leave me a gasping, quivering heap of flesh.<br /> <br /> Again, this description is making something wonderful sound horrible, and that\u2019s not my intention. All I mean to say is that Charlotte is a powerful, decisive woman, and she knows how to turn those qualities into pure erotic gold. I <u>wanted</u> to please her by submitting to her desires\u2026 I wanted it more than anything at the time. She\u2019s so strong. I mean that both literally and figuratively, though I don\u2019t think she\u2019s quite as physically powerful as my fianc\u00e9e. But her force of personality is something to behold.<br /> <br /> But as much as the events of the night seemed to be all about her\u2026 that wasn\u2019t really the case. There was one point where she was on top of me, sort of holding me down, and she brought my arms up over my head and gripped both of my wrists in one of her hands. I couldn\u2019t pull away, and it started to really bother me. I didn\u2019t think she would <u>hurt</u> me or anything, but\u2026 I don\u2019t like being constrained like that. It lasted maybe six seconds before she looked into my eyes\u2026 and let go. She brought her hand down and gently caressed the side of my face, and then we were kissing again and things were back on track.<br /> <br /> She saw that it was bothering me, and she stopped. I didn\u2019t even have to say anything. <u>That</u> more than anything else convinced me that last night wasn\u2019t as one-sided as it seemed.<br /> <br /> She held me as I fell asleep, protectively\u2026 almost possessively, but in a nice way. She was not still holding me when I woke up, the way D sometimes does, but that\u2019s okay too. The two of us got dressed in amiable silence, and she offered to drive me back to the Dream House. I gratefully accepted the offer, and (sensing her ulterior motive) invited her to the now-legendary Sex Breakfast tradition.<br /> <br /> Plus, I wanted to show off my conquest. Or conqueror, I suppose.<br /> <br /> Sex Breakfast was fun (as always) but some heady revelations followed. D brought Brightstar and Neon by, and made a big deal about hoping that Angelica didn\u2019t turn out to be an enemy, since she\u2019d spent considerable time during their ride to her place admiring the new girl\u2019s legs. Well, of course I had to pout a bit at that, and after breakfast I changed into an outfit that shows off my own legs to their best advantage. D did not complain.<br /> <br /> Calamity was conspicuously absent from the early portions of the meal, but that\u2019s been fairly common over the last few months as well. She arrived just as people were getting ready to go, and asked to speak with the motley privately. It turns out that she, Jacob, and Luna had an evening that was possibly even more interesting than mine (though not as enjoyable).<br /> <br /> Angelica isn\u2019t the only new arrival in the Freehold. Another young woman by the name of Hannah also turned up within the last day or so. She appears to be a Wizened of some stripe, and her Durance was held in a Library in Arcadia. In any case, she was also staying at the temporary lodgings where Angelica was housed, and after D and the others dropped Angelica off last night\u2026 Hannah unexpectedly tried to kill her. She failed in large part due to the fact that Molly was there keeping an eye on Angelica (ironically), and fled the scene.<br /> <br /> Calamity got the call about this, and she used Contracts to track Hannah down. Jacob and Luna decided to accompany her, and the three of them found her on the nearly deserted pier, talking on a phone in Russian with a machinegun lying at her feet. Jacob later told the other two that Hannah seemed to be speaking to elements of the Russian mob, asking to be picked up with \u201cno civilian casualties.\u201d As she\u2019s a Wizened, my friends knew that the machinegun might animate and shoot at them at any moment. They turned themselves invisible (more Contracts) and approached with caution.<br /> <br /> As I understand it, Jacob tossed the machinegun into the ocean while Luna restrained Hannah and Calamity tried to prevent the situation from going too far south (I\u2019m so proud of her!). Once she realized that they weren\u2019t going to hurt her, she called off the mob and started to talk.<br /> <br /> Turns out she had attacked Angelica because she knew that the other girl had come from the Director, and knew how dangerous his pawns can be. She\u2019d seen Angelica talking to some of the Director\u2019s \u201cextras\u201d in the Hedge, and didn\u2019t want her to pose a threat to the Freehold. Calamity and the others calmly informed her that Angelica was already under surveillance by the Freehold for exactly that reason, and she agreed to be escorted to Lowjack\u2019s bar for debriefing.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t claim to know what they talked about there, but I gather that Lowjack is attempting to court Hannah \u2013 who shows a leaning toward the Winter Court in any case \u2013 as an asset\u2026 possibly one he can use to get a foothold inside the Russian mob. Angelica, on the other hand, is a problem that needed an immediate solution. So Calamity spent the rest of the night and morning in Angelica\u2019s dreams.<br /> <br /> Angelica had tentatively agreed the previous evening to submit to Calamity\u2019s Dream Healing so that the Freehold could be satisfied that we\u2019d dealt with any hidden programming she might have\u2026 but only on the condition that Desiree was present. This raised something of a red flag, because Desiree had previously professed not to know the newcomer. In any case, Calamity caught a ride with Boss Lowjack to the hospital where Angelica was convalescing following Hannah\u2019s attack. Desiree met her there, and the two of them got to work on her dreams.<br /> <br /> From what I understand, Desiree distracted Angelica while Calamity went to work rooting out and eradicating the programming. Having been \u201cdistracted\u201d by Desiree on more than one occasion myself, I can only assume that Angelica had no complaints. Calamity quickly found a set of buried instructions which would compel Angelica to get close to someone \u2013 just about anyone \u2013 make herself indispensable to them, and then engineer events so that the object of her affection would become one of the monarchs. That\u2019s clever\u2026 the Director isn\u2019t targeting people in power directly, he\u2019s targeting ordinary citizens and then maneuvering them into positions of power. I don\u2019t think we would have seen that one coming. And I can\u2019t help but wonder\u2026 who would she have targeted?<br /> <br /> Calamity was just about done removing the programming, and was about to exit the dream when she noticed something else\u2026 something <u>much</u> more frightening. Angelica was completely caught up in Desiree by that point\u2026 to such a degree that she stopped recognizing Calamity\u2019s presence at all. As far as she was concerned subconsciously, Calamity might as well have already left. And that being the case\u2026 her second set of programming kicked in. Calamity caught it just before she would have left.<br /> <br /> And it\u2019s a damn good thing she did. Angelica\u2019s hidden directives would have caused her to seek out a place within the Freehold where changelings gather (like, y\u2019know, the Dream House, or the Rose &amp; Thorn, or tonight\u2019s Beltane party at Glamour Springs) and do as much damage as possible, preferably with high explosives. Thank God Calamity was able to discover this plot and stop it before it became a tragedy!<br /> <br /> That\u2019s\u2026 pretty much where we left things. D approached me as the group was breaking up to make preparations for the fete tonight, and asked if I was okay with the fact that she\u2019d slept with Brightstar without me present. That made me smile, and I told her that I was fine with it. I\u2019m long past the point where I worry about her affections straying; I have more faith in our love than that. And I\u2019ve found that I actually <u>like</u> it when my various lovers form bonds like that; it actually makes things <u>less</u> awkward in a weird way to know that we all care about each other on some level.<br /> <br /> So that\u2019s what\u2019s going on now, New Diary, plus a little update on how things have developed over the last few months. A little bitter with the sweet, perhaps\u2026 but I have no complaints overall. My family has lost a couple of members, but we\u2019ve also gained a sister, and we\u2019re still strong. I\u2019m finally starting to pick up the pieces of the life that was taken from me thirty-seven years ago\u2026 and maybe to reach for something bigger and better than that life ever would have been. And with a lot of hard work and a little luck, soon I\u2019ll be able to give Missy and Jane that same chance.<br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei Grace</b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T14:08:10-07:00","id":1128571,"title":"","content":"<b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> Thursday, April 30th<br /> Nine years, one month, twenty-three days<br /> Days without stabbing: too damned many<br /> <br /> I promised Dr Emmett that I would start writing these again so here I fucking am. Just re-read the last few entries and it was all I could do not to just burn the damn thing. But then I might forget what happened. I might forget just how colossally fucking stupid I was. I might forget that They were right. No, I need to keep it and remind myself that when you let your guard down you get fucking stabbed.<br /> <br /> Because that\u2019s what I did and he sure as fuck ran my twisted little black heart right the hell through. I wish he had taken that damned Final Fantasy sword of his and actually run me through with it. At least it would only have hurt for a few moments.<br /> <br /> But it was nothing so clean or so merciful. Insincere Marguerite had mirror traveled Stasia and I up to Bellevue where we loaded up her things into a one way rental to move her into her new place in Santa Monica. There was laughing and good cheer. The Stasia and Kat road-trip movie. Only it ended with Gawain waiting to tell me was leaving. His things were already gone. He\u2019d already told the others.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t tell him goodbye. I\u2019ve replayed that moment in my head. I\u2019ve imagined it a million different ways. In my head I have told him I understood and been civil. I\u2019ve thrown myself at him and begged him not to go. I\u2019ve even carved him asunder. But the truth is I didn\u2019t manage to say anything at all. I just stood there dumbstruck while my entire world collapsed around me until he reached for my shoulder and called my name. Then I shrieked at him and fled. I haven\u2019t seen him since. I haven\u2019t spoken to him and I don\u2019t intend to. There\u2019s nothing to say and nothing I want to hear him say at this point.<br /> <br /> Lori found me first, or maybe the others just kept their distance for fear that I\u2019d lash out at them. She threw her arms around me carelessly. I tried to pull away but I wasn\u2019t even aware until too late. She hugged me tightly and in my weakness and my pain I needed that. I felt my glass pierce her perfect skin and even in the midst of everything it sent a tiny sliver along my nerves because the monster is always there. I didn\u2019t want her to let go but I tried to pull back before she hurt herself more. She told me it was a risk you take getting close to someone. At the time I wasn\u2019t in any shape to process what she was trying to tell me and the moment was interrupted by the hissing of her blood burning me. Because of course that was when we found my frailty. The blood of innocents burns me like the unwholesome thing I am.<br /> <br /> I couldn\u2019t help but remember that final moment in Snow Globe. The Whispering Voices holding me as I lashed out at Them madly. The scent of Their blood and the taste of it. The sadness and shock in Their cry as They dropped me. The way Their blood burned my mouth and throat and skin just like Lori\u2019s did.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve managed not to embarrass myself like that since for the most part. I\u2019ve held my shit together and done my job. I guess I haven\u2019t been exactly fun to be around most of the time but there hasn\u2019t been any more crying and acting like a damned teenage girl or any of that bullshit.<br /> <br /> I just want it to all go away. The hurt and the betrayal and the pain. And if that means I lose the \u201cgood\u201d emotions too then so be it. Maybe if I forget what they feel like the memory of them and the knowledge that they were all lies won\u2019t hurt anymore.<br /> <br /> I forgot what They taught me. I thought I could be a woman. I thought I could be someone\u2019s lover. But I can\u2019t and playing dress up and pretend doesn\u2019t change that. What I am is a monster and only misery and pain come from trying to pretend otherwise.<br /> <br /> I tried to tell him that I couldn\u2019t be his girl, that the most I could offer was to be his monster. But he lied to me and said that was enough. He lied to me and said he\u2019d love me no matter what. He lied to me and told me he\u2019d never leave me. And the worst part is he made me believe it. He made me think that maybe even a thing as wretched and cruel as me could be loved. He tricked me into believing that I was a princess and that I was going to live happily ever after with my handsome prince.<br /> <br /> But I\u2019m not the princess. I\u2019m not even the wicked step-mother. I\u2019m the shadow in the night. I\u2019m the thing that waits, hungry and patient to take those that stray from the light. I\u2019m the monster that punishes the wicked. I\u2019m the bloody comeuppance that claims the villain so the hero doesn\u2019t have to get his hands dirty. I\u2019m the thing that murders the wicked step mother and feasts on her screams. I\u2019m the calamity that befalls those who deserve it and I won\u2019t ever let myself forget that again.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve tried to keep busy, to distract myself from dwelling on this. I guess that\u2019s part of why I stopped writing. My sessions with Dr Emmett haven\u2019t exactly been the most productive. She\u2019s frustrated. Not that she\u2019d admit to such, but I can see it. She knows I\u2019m holding back and she keeps telling me that she can\u2019t help me unless I open up. But she doesn\u2019t understand. How can a fucking human know what it means to survive Arcadia? I\u2019m not like her. I\u2019m not like the other pathetic\u2026 No, I\u2019m Calamity. I hurt people and I like it. It makes the glass fucking sing when I cut into their soft, weak flesh and draw out the sweet blood and sweeter screams. Killing is more intimate, more pleasurable than sex to me. And it\u2019s not because I\u2019m sick or broken or wrong, it\u2019s because I\u2019m a goddamn monster. I\u2019m the fucking bogeyman that murders bad children and stacks their limbs like cord-wood. Because this is all nothing but a fucking fairy-tale. I forgot what part I\u2019m meant to play and I was punished for it. But how can I make her understand that when she\u2019s never seen it for herself? When she thinks I\u2019m human like her? No, she\u2019ll just try to convince me to pretend to be something I\u2019m not again. To open myself up again. I won\u2019t make that mistake again. But if I stop going or if I tell her the truth she\u2019ll tell my handlers. Can\u2019t have that. Lowjack knows that I\u2019m not his monster the way Dahlia is. He\u2019d have her kill me without hesitation if he knew that I\u2019d stopped trying to live the lie. Well, maybe not. I mean he does have me on a nice tight leash for another nine years. But he would put me in a kennel and muzzle me if he thought there was a chance I might slip my leash and he most certainly would make sure this little monster didn\u2019t get to have any fun at all.<br /> <br /> And now D\u2019s joined Jacob and I. Good little monsters all of us, trying to learn how to be people and play nice. Not because she wants to but because Lori wants it. Because she\u2019s in love. She\u2019s given up her apartment and her job and now she\u2019s trying to be the good little girl Lori wants. It\u2019s sickening to watch her and know that I was just as pathetic trying to remake myself for Gawain. At least Jacob and I still spar after most sessions. I know he\u2019s worried about me and he wants to help. But what is talking about it going to do? I know I\u2019m miserable, he knows I\u2019m miserable, why sit around talking about how miserable I am? Nothing but a waste of time. No, we\u2019ve been working to hone our skills rather than just play around and we\u2019re both stronger for it.<br /> <br /> He\u2019s not the only one. Insincere Marguerite has been weirdly attentive. Just when I\u2019d resolved myself to her being forever cold to me because she couldn\u2019t admit that treacherous blue cuntsnake had her wrapped around her finger she\u2019s starts acting like we were before. It\u2019d be easy to fall back into it myself but as mercurial as her friendship has proven to be I\u2019m not going to make the mistake of letting her that close again. Still\u2026 as a fellow Darkling and all it is nice to have a friend who gets it, for however long it lasts this time.<br /> <br /> And all the goddamn wedding planning doesn\u2019t help. To their credit, everyone has made an effort to at least keep it down to a dull roar around me. And yeah, love is amazing and wonderful and all that horseshit. And I have agreed to be part of the weddings because I\u2019m not a total colossal bitch. I mean, just because I\u2019m not happy doesn\u2019t mean they don\u2019t deserve to be for however long this particular \u201cforever\u201d lasts. So I just nod and keep my fucking mouth shut and go about my business.<br /> <br /> I know they worry and I do appreciate that they care. I really do. But I am just not happy right now and there\u2019s nothing anyone can do about it. I know it sucks. I know I\u2019m being a dour bitter bitch. Why the fuck do they think I keep trying to stay the hell out of the way? If I\u2019m busy in the office or practicing or whatever then I\u2019m distracted from what a total clusterfuck my feelings turned into and they don\u2019t have to put up with me. Everyone wins. But instead people keep insisting on dragging me along on things to try to \u2018cheer me up\u2019.<br /> <br /> Stasia\u2019s been one of the worst culprits by far, but she\u2019s also pretty damn good at it. She keeps dropping in, usually when I am particularly ill tempered, (it\u2019s almost as if someone keeps tipping her off) and it\u2019s always the same game. She knows I\u2019ve got work to do and she knows I\u2019m fine but she\u2019s bored or she\u2019s just gotten wind of something cool or just an all work and no play makes Kat a dull girl and drags me off. And honestly, being around her does distract me from feeling like shit. I just feel bad at how hard she\u2019s working to try to drag me through this emotional bog\u2026 I\u2019d do the same for her of course, but still, I feels guilty about it.<br /> <br /> Sadly Becky hasn\u2019t been anywhere near as patient. I guess I shouldn\u2019t blame her. I haven\u2019t been fun to be around. I just thought\u2026 I guess I believed that she loved me too. I was such a stupid girl. Oh my Handsome Knight and my Beautiful Dragon what a lucky girl am I. But it was all a lie. All of it. Becky\u2019s a monster in her own way just like me. Hollowed out inside and waiting to be filled up with whatever I or anyone else wants. The perfect lie. The perfect fuck. I was always so worried about what I made her feel\u2026 made her want\u2026 And what\u2019s inside me right now? What I was feeling right after he fucking abandoned me? I\u2019m not enough of a monster to make her feel that. But now I guess it doesn\u2019t matter. I haven\u2019t seen or talked to her in over a month now. Guess she decided if we weren\u2019t going to fuck she\u2019d rather spend her time with someone that did just want a meat puppet to act out their fantasies.<br /> <br /> There. Written down. Spelled out. I don\u2019t fucking feel any better. Waste of goddamn time. And as tonight is Walpurgisnacht, I don\u2019t have time to fucking waste. It\u2019s the big anniversary show. All of the monarchs will be there and as reigning monarch Jolie will hand over the deed afterwards to make an official show of the Dream House becoming ours. I wish I could feel excited about that. But Gawain won\u2019t be there and at this point I\u2019m afraid Becky will only be there because she has to be as Claviger. I should figure out something to say to her. No, I\u2019m not going to chase after her like a puppy. She\u2019s made her feelings (or I should say lack thereof) clear.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s just\u2026 I\u2019m fucking lonely and I\u2019m so goddamn tired of sleeping alone.<br /> <br /> Friday, May 1st<br /> Nine years, one month, twenty-two days<br /> Days without stabbing: one more<br /> <br /> Well that was a wild ride Mr Toad. We spent the afternoon preparing for the show and as soon as we opened the doors the local Changelings started to roll in. The monarchs were all there and the folks who came out to see the ceremony and some who just figured it was going to be a hell of a show. That last one drew a pretty strong mortal showing for a Thursday. And we did not disappoint them. We rolled out a collection of our top numbers from the year and everyone went all out on them. I even helped smuggle Captain Jack in to join the backup dancers on the opening number which seemed to please him. He\u2019s been almost as upset with Gawain leaving as the rest of the motley so I\u2019ve been helping him out with the hi-jinks.<br /> <br /> We let Ace reprise his one man Thunderdome act since it was his final night at the Dream House. He let us know when we renewed the motley pledge that he would be leaving once he\u2019d finished with his oath. Too long in one place apparently, time for him to walk the Earth like Cane again. But we did add Luna to the pledge since she\u2019d decided to finally accept our invitation to officially join.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite also took to the stage, singing backup for Lori on the \u201cLady Marmalade\u201d opener and performing \u201cNon, Je Ne Regrette Rien\u201d. It\u2019s the first time she\u2019s hit the stage since the Christmas show, maybe someone should see about coaxing her out more often.<br /> <br /> Lori and I did \u201cBloody Creature Poster Girl\u201d and I won\u2019t lie, with the Vainglory flowing, once that music started up it was almost enough to make me forget. Right up until I looked out to find Princess Jolie\u2019s table and saw that Becky wasn\u2019t there. I didn\u2019t break stride and I did put my all into the performance but the moment was most certainly broken.<br /> <br /> I mean, things aren\u2019t good between us right now but I thought she was at least still my friend. But she wasn\u2019t there. It wasn\u2019t just that she hadn\u2019t made an effort to be present. As the Claviger, she had to make arrangements NOT to be. I guess if I still had any doubts about it being over that put them down.<br /> <br /> In a sick way, I\u2019m kinda glad for what ended up happening. I didn\u2019t have to think about it or deal with it last night. Though now I\u2019m wondering about the Spring Court Beltane orgy tonight. I know she\u2019ll be there. Maybe it would be better if I wasn\u2019t. I certainly can\u2019t do anything stupid if I\u2019m not there. Because right now I really want to grab a fistful of that silky hair and kiss her hard and make her want me to take every last bit of anger and frustration I\u2019ve got built up out on her perfection while she begs and screams. But I can\u2019t do that. I mustn\u2019t do that. Because I don\u2019t want her to see how badly I want to hurt someone right now. Because I don\u2019t want to twist her around and force her to desire something I know she wouldn\u2019t otherwise. Because at that point she just might agree to let me torture her and I don\u2019t trust myself not to.<br /> <br /> No. I should stay home. Even if I don\u2019t go after Becky the whole point is to hook up and there\u2019s no one there that wants what I want to dish out. So I\u2019ll either end up alone or disappointed when someone discovers that when I say bleed or draw blood I\u2019m not joking. No, I should just stay home and spend another night with my Christmas present from Andromeda. Hell, with everyone gone I could even go all out and set it up in the rec room so I can watch porn on the big TV while I jackhammer myself sore.<br /> <br /> Wow, that\u2019s a pretty fucking pathetic mental image. But after spending the night and half the day watching what Desiree did to Angelica I am a fucking needful little monster.<br /> <br /> Alright, I should get this down in order and sorted out in my head so I can write up a report on it for Lowjack. So yeah, once the show was winding down I hit the floor to mingle. Even if Becky hadn\u2019t shown up I still needed to speak to the monarchs and there were friends that had made the effort to come out for the occasion to greet.<br /> <br /> But before I got far, Monica drew me aside to talk to me about one of the two new arrivals to the freehold. Angelica is a very pretty fairest with Spring Court leanings that I could clearly see already had Monica firmly by the short and curies. She is also one of the Director\u2019s, a fact that Angelica and made Monica swear not to reveal and the woman had very nearly obeyed. Thankfully she wasn\u2019t (quite) so completely twitterpated as to keep a threat of that magnitude to herself. I told her I was going to have to talk to Angelica and she got all panicky because she wasn\u2019t supposed to tell anyone. I suggested that she bring it up and see if she could get the woman to agree to talk to me.<br /> <br /> I went from there to Desiree, since she was there with Gloria. I drew her aside and asked her about Angelica and the story that she\u2019d given Monica about leaving after being passed over for some really big part. Desiree claimed not to know her and seemed perplexed by the tale. According to her, the Director picked people for roles and groomed them, there wasn\u2019t any sort of infighting and conflict over who\u2019d get a part. So that\u2019s odd but then it\u2019s likely everything she remembers is an elaborate production leading up to her \u2018escape\u2019 (unless of course it\u2019s a lie because she\u2019s a willing loyalist.)<br /> <br /> At that point I had nothing to do but mingle and wait. I got by all the tables and made some small talk. Nobody else had anything really pressing to talk about. It was all congratulations and the smallest of small talk. I didn\u2019t mind, I wasn\u2019t really in the mood to talk. But I guess word\u2019s gotten around that I\u2019ve been in bitch mode lately. One more reason not to go to Beltane I guess. Or maybe the best reason to go.<br /> <br /> Anyway, once the show was done and the mortals had been cleared out we had the ceremony. It was simple but nice. Jolie said a few words and they gave us the deed for show (the legal paperwork had actually already been taken care of) and there was cheering and all. It\u2019s been a long strange year getting here. There was hugging and smiling and it really struck me that I was the only one that didn\u2019t have a lover there to share the moment with. Kinda put a bitter spin on the whole thing for me but the sooner I get used to that the better. And even if she\u2019s made it clear we\u2019re never going to be in a relationship, my blood sister was there. And the motley. I\u2019m not alone. Just fucking single.<br /> <br /> Well, at that point everyone else was moving into the lighting round of who\u2019s going to get in my pants tonight. I could see Monica and Angelica were lingering so I made my way over there. And it became very clear very quickly that Monica had not managed to speak to her about me. So I sat more or less patiently while they stepped away to \u2018have a word\u2019. Monica came back in tears and Angelica wanted to continue our discussion in private. It was a reasonable request and I figured I could take her if she tried anything. (And she wasn\u2019t a member of the Freehold in good standing yet even) But there was nothing but talking. I explained the situation and that it was almost certain that she had programming. She claimed to know nothing about any of it and tried to assure me of her innocence. She then said she couldn\u2019t do it right then because she was too upset and then asked for, of all things, Desiree to be present.<br /> <br /> Well, I made some rather telling comments about Monica\u2019s inability to not fall head over heels for every stray she found in the hedge and sent her on her way with a warning that we needed to get this done sooner rather than later. Then, figuring that due to being a loyalist or her programming she\u2019d either be trying to escape or contact her people with that bit of info about Monica I called Lowjack and brought him up to speed on the situation. He agreed to put someone on Angelica.<br /> <br /> As I was talking Lori showed up wanting to know what was going on and told me that D, Brightstar, and Neon were giving Angelica a ride since Monica was so upset and all. I promptly called D to warn her and then explained the situation to Lori. She was worried and kept up texting with D until she got an all clear that they\u2019d dropped the target off.<br /> <br /> I headed downstairs for a drink since I wasn\u2019t ready to face Becky\u2019s absence without a pep talk from Captain Morgan or Mr Daniels. As I sipped my drink I started to explain what was going on to Jacob but before I got far my phone rang. It was Dahlia letting me know that the other new arrival, a wizened named Hannah, had tried to murder Angelica and been driven off by Molly.<br /> <br /> So I activated Relentless Pursuit and told Jacob and Luna we had a hunt. Jacob lent me his keys since I have to be the one actively pursuing my prey. We took off for the pier, which was empty. She was there, talking in good but not native Russian. Jacob was able to translate that she was calling for a pickup. We considered how best to move since Lowjack wanted her alive to answer questions. Since we were all able to vanish that made getting close easy. At Luna\u2019s suggestion, Jacob grabbed the gun she had guarding her and pitched it into the ocean, Luna grabbed her since I couldn\u2019t without cutting her on my glass, and I put my glass to her throat to convince her to come quietly since her wizened contracts couldn\u2019t animate it. It all went without a hitch. Hannah didn\u2019t seem very interested in a fight anyway and certainly not under those conditions. She agreed to come with us but asked if she could call off her contacts. We let her write a text and Jacob read it before she sent it. Maybe I should ask him about learning Russian since it does keep coming up.<br /> <br /> The ride to Lowjack\u2019s bar was uneventful and once we\u2019d arrived Hannah proved quite amenable to talking. She\u2019d been taken by a Gentry from a library oriented realm and made into a librarian. But she\u2019d made use of her prior skills with a knife to kill a guard and distract the others by getting blood all over the books (clever girl). As she was making her way through the hedge, she saw Angelica being escorted by some of the Director\u2019s extras and then when she arrived saw that she\u2019d promptly seduced Monica and thus, to repay us for our hospitality and because apparently even among the other Gentry the Director is considered a jerk she decided to murder Angelica as a parting gift before leaving to rejoin the Russian mob. It seemed like she was being upfront to me and I told Lowjack as much. He agreed and told her he wanted to speak to her before releasing her. Seeing as I had nothing better to do I offered to stay and watch her.<br /> <br /> But as it turned out,I did have something better to do. Angelica was under sedation at the hospital. So Jacob stayed to watch our new friend while I went to go ahead and do the Oneiromancy on Angelica. Since she\u2019d agreed to it with Desiree present, I called her and asked her to meet me at the hospital. Moon graciously gave her up and I believe gave her a ride to the hospital since she didn\u2019t have a car there when I met up with her.<br /> <br /> Desiree asked me if I trusted her, which seemed an odd question but I said I did. Which as true enough given how much I\u2019ve been in her head. We entered and Angelica seemed to recognize Desiree, who moved in quickly and began to flirt the other girl up to distract her. I started looking for the programming. It felt weird doing it alone. I mean, Desiree was there but she wasn\u2019t dream working. It was a lot more subtle than before, clearly the Director has improved his techniques in response to us being onto him. I took it slowly, trying to not just unravel the threads woven into her mind but also to read them. It took longer, but considering that by that point Desiree had\u2026 well seduction isn\u2019t really the word for it. That implies give and take\u2026 well, I guess there was only it was all Angelica giving and all Desiree taking. I\u2019ve never seen her take charge of a situation like that. She had that girl wrapped around her finger tighter than a fat mobster\u2019s pinky ring.<br /> <br /> Free to work without Angelica paying me any mind, I picked the commands apart. Latch onto someone and earn their trust. Get into their bed and their dreams and plant the seeds of a dream poison that would open the way for the Director to program them and then help them work their way into one of the thrones. So a programmed agent as monarch that never spent time in the Director\u2019s domain. Devious stuff.<br /> <br /> By the time I\u2019d finished, Desiree had gone from using her Spring contracts to make every one of Angelica\u2019s deepest fantasies come true to just changing the woman\u2019s desires with them to whatever suited her fancy and Angelica had eagerly agreed to it. I paused, I mean I have done some dream sex but this was intense. It hadn\u2019t really occurred to me that once you\u2019ve taken full control of someone\u2019s dream they can\u2019t pass out no matter what you do or how many times you do it. Definitely some potential there.<br /> <br /> At this point, Angelica was so far gone she ceased to able to even register that I was there, which combined with the work I\u2019d done removing her programming triggered another set of instructions. A set that was supposed to activate only if the first were removed and only after the Oneiromancer was gone. I almost didn\u2019t notice. And once I did look, what I found was a shock. Simple commands to seek the most crowded gathering of changelings and to suicide bomb them to kill as many as possible. I removed it and then saw that Desiree was pretty much just waiting for me at that point. Angelica\u2019s dream self was limp as a rag doll. She was still dreaming but her mind was completely past responding or registering anything. It was a bit frightening and awe inspiring both.<br /> <br /> We exited the dream and only then realized it was well into Friday. I told Desiree what I\u2019d found and her initial reaction was shock and denial. She tried to claim the Director wouldn\u2019t do something like that second program. But I was firm and after a bit she accepted the truth of what I was telling her. I did tell her I expected an explanation about what was going on with her and Angelica but added that it could wait as she was clearly exhausted and very upset with the revelations about the Director\u2019s willingness to commit acts of mass murder. Frankly, even with the Spring magic I\u2019d used I was a bit tired and very much famished by this point so I wasn\u2019t going to push her. But I am going to mention to Lowjack that she hasn\u2019t explained herself yet when I send him my report. I don\u2019t know why Angelica insisted on her being there and I can\u2019t help but suspect that the Director might have something up his sleeve for his wayward agent.<br /> <br /> It was a pretty quiet ride back to the Dream House. I didn\u2019t really explain anything to Gloria and she didn\u2019t seem to be keen on prying. I guess we both seemed like we weren\u2019t in the mood to talk. They dropped me off as folks were streaming out of sex breakfast. Queen Charlotte was among them having made good on her flirting with Lori. She\u2019s certainly been on the prowl since she and Leanne went their separate ways. And given how frisky Desiree\u2019s distractions had made me, I felt the need to mention ever so casually that the pledge was over and she nodded. Then she asked me if I wanted it there or if I would prefer it at a later date when it wouldn\u2019t need to be so \u201cperfunctory\u201d. I told her it would be a shame to rush it and she gave me that knowing little smirk of hers. You know, now that I think about it she might have been giving me the eye as I walked away after that. Well, maybe. Most likely just be wishful thinking because I\u2019m horny as fuck right now. Guess I\u2019ll find out whenever we do actually get around to that less \u201cperfunctory\u201d kiss.<br /> <br /> Well, I laid into the remains of breakfast with a bit of a sigh (I do miss Gawain\u2019s cooking) and once it was just the motley I made sure everyone was up to date on the whole series of events. And now that I\u2019ve got my thoughts down I can take a long cold shower and tidy it up for Lowjack. Then, provided nothing else catches fire, maybe I\u2019ll mope about Becky and dither about going to Beltane and what I\u2019m going to wear if I do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Luna joined the motley! She approached me about it a few days ago, and she made it official today. We were more than happy to welcome her in. I guess she figured that she was pretty much in the motley anyway, so she might as well make it official. So we added her this afternoon. After she made the pledge we went out for a picnic by ourselves. It was nice to get away with my Luna for the afternoon. At some point in the future we\u2019ll have to all go out for a picnic, just \u2018cause, but today I wanted it to be about Luna and me so we went alone. It was fun.<br /> <br /> I also used today\u2019s excursion as an excuse to practice speaking French and Spanish with Luna. Those of us in the motley that didn\u2019t already know those two languages have started studying them so we\u2019ll be able to speak in each other\u2019s native languages. It could also come in handy if we need to discuss something in private, but don\u2019t have the luxury of going somewhere alone to talk. As long as those around us don\u2019t speak French or Spanish we\u2019re good. I suppose I should ask and see if anyone wants to learn to speak Russian. It is not the easiest language to learn, or so Lowjack tells me, because you need to learn a whole new alphabet on top of everything else. English was not very easy for me to learn way back when, but I have noticed some similarities in words between the two romance languages I\u2019m learning and English. They have a common root or something. Or the romance languages influence English at some point. I think German also influence English too, which is what makes it so complicated to learn. French and Spanish are easier to learn by comparison. I know that I probably have a horrible accent when I speak either language, but I\u2019m getting better. Heck, I still have an accent with I speak English, and probably always will. At least Insincere Marguerite cringes a little bit less when I open my mouth to speak French. I\u2019m working on it.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Well, it is Walpurgis, and it has officially been one year since we opened the Dream House. We had a really big turnout for the show tonight. All four of the monarchs came by to watch, as well as Brightstar and Neon from out of town. Spidertoes was there with Moon, and even Twitch showed up. He has been making it a more regular occurrence for him to come to watch a show. He usually sits with De La Rocha. There was even a new girl there with Monica. The new girls name is Angelica. She\u2019s a Fairest, and associated with Spring. At least that\u2019s what I got from looking at her. There is also apparently another new girl named Hannah that arrived a day before Angelica did, but she was not at the club tonight. And as has become usual Hailey, Gloria and Molly hung out at the bar. Molly recently learned that her name is also a reference to a drug. Ecstasy, I think. So, she wanted to change her name to something else with better connotations. I made a couple suggestions and she said that she\u2019d think them over. I suggested Katarina, Talia and something else that I\u2019m blanking on right now. I am more familiar with Russian names so that\u2019s the direction I went. If she chooses to go with something more English sounding that\u2019s fine too. I just want her to be happy with her name. I was not able to take back my family name, but I insisted on taking back my given name. At that point I was carrying enough secrets. I didn\u2019t want everything about me to be a lie.<br /> <br /> The show went really well. All the ladies performed amazingly, especially my motley mates. Lori did a song that she opened with a year ago, so she came full circle on that. I believe that was the intention. Calamity reprised her act with Bloody Creature Poster Girl, and even let her mein show through so people would see the glass. It was appropriate to the song, and it worked well. The audience was none the wiser that they were seeing Calamity as she really is.<br /> <br /> After their performances, Lori, Calamity and Insincere Marguerite went out to talk to folks in the crowd. Lori talked to everyone it seemed. She spent a good bit of time talking to the monarchs and her girlfriends. She even made her way over to talk to Monica and Angelica. Calamity made her rounds as well. At one point, she went off to the side to talk to Monica. I found out later what they were talking about. But I\u2019ll get to that in a minute. I did a little bit of socializing myself. I talked to each of the monarch in turn and brought them their drinks personally. Each of them has a favorite drink and they all like them made a certain way. Having an eidetic memory sure has been helpful when it comes to bartending.<br /> <br /> After the show was over an announcement was made by microphone that there was going to be a meeting of the something or other society and that non-members needed to leave. I can\u2019t remember what they called the society, but it essentially referred to the freehold. So, all the Changelings stayed and the mortals left. Well, most of the mortals. I think Stasia stayed to watch. In a short ceremony, the monarchs announced that it has been a year to the day since we started running the Dream House, and per our contract the place was now ours. Jolie made a speech about it and Augustine signed the deed over to us. It was understated but nice.<br /> <br /> After that was over Calamity left to go talk to Angelica. I\u2019m not sure exactly what was said, but I do know that Monica left alone and crying, and Angelica was taken back to her temporary apartment by De La Rocha, Neon and Brightstar. Lori left with Charlotte, which was a bit of a surprise, but De La Rocha seemed okay with it. After Angelica and the others left Calamity came over to the bar and explained what was going on. Apparently, Angelica escaped from the Director and Monica had been worried about possible programming. So, Monica talked to Calamity about it. Angelica got mad at Monica because our Blackbird Bishop had promised not to tell anyone. That explains why Monica left in tears and Angelica seemed angry. In any case, Calamity explained all of that to me. Then while she was in the middle of explaining she got a phone call from Dahlia saying that Hannah had attacked Angelica. Molly, per Lowjacks instructions had just arrived to keep an eye on Angelica. I guess Calamity called him to let the monarch know what was going on. Dahlia wanted Calamity to find the attacker so she used one of her contracts to find out where Hannah was.<br /> <br /> Luna and I volunteered to go with Calamity and track down the new girl. Calamity had to be the one driving, so I let her drive my jeep. She explained to Luna what was going on while she drove. When we got to the pier we all snuck up on Hannah and observed her before we acted. She was standing alone, talking on the phone in Russian. She is not a native speaker of Russian, but her accent was really good. She\u2019d had a lot of practice. She also had a sub machine gun near her, that could easily be animated by her if the need should arise. It had been explained that she is a Wizened and they have that ability. So, we came up with a plan. Luna would grapple Hannah, while I went for the gun and disposed of it. Calamity would then come up and put a knife, or in her case glass, to Hannah\u2019s throat and we\u2019d talk. Our plan went down perfectly. Hannah was completely taken by surprise. Luna grabbed her and I got rid of the gun. We then directed her over to my jeep and we all drove over to Lowjack\u2019s place to have that conversation. On the way I had her text her Russian friends and explain that she wouldn\u2019t need anyone to come and get her after all. Calamity drove, Luna watched Hannah and I made sure that Hannah typed what we wanted her to.<br /> <br /> Hannah explained that she had escaped from Arcadia and had come across Angelica in the Hedge. She had seen the Fairest dismissing some of the Director\u2019s \u201cextras.\u201d They deferred to her, which set off warning bells for Hannah. She then made it a point to keep an eye on the Fairest and see what she was up to. After De La Rocha and the others dropped Angelica off and she went in to her apartment, Hannah came in and attacked her with a knife. Molly then jumped out of the shadows and shot at Hannah, who fled. Then we caught her. She explained to all of us that she knew how dangerous the Director and his people could be. Apparently, she had contact with the Directors people while she was in Arcadia. She was taken to a vast library and her task was to look after the books. In order to escape she slit the throat of another librarian. The blood spurted all over the books which distracted the other librarians leaving Hannah free to escape. It was clear that our guest has no qualms about killing people out of hand.<br /> <br /> During our conversation, we also found out that Hannah is connected to the Russian mob. That would explain why she was speaking in Russian earlier. Apparently, they have been looking for her since she was taken. I think they assumed that she was taken by mortals. Not sure how she explained the Gentry to her mob contacts, or if she\u2019s tried yet. So, Lowjack got her to cooperate and she agreed to be locked up for the night until we could get things straightened out with Angelica. The plan was originally to have Calamity and Dahlia stand guard for the night, but then Lowjack mentioned that Angelica was in the hospital getting treated for her injuries and was currently sedated. Calamity said that this would be the ideal time to do dream healing on the sleeping woman. It was also a matter of some priority because she was aware that others knew about her origins and she might have programming in place that would turn on if discovered. So, I stayed to guard Hannah and Calamity went to the hospital to heal Angelica.<br /> <br /> I found out after breakfast the next day what happened with that. After our guests left, which included Charlotte, Strype, Neon and Brightstar, we had a motley meeting. Well, later in the day we did. Calamity explained that she had called Desiree to help her with the dream healing. Angelica had been insistent when she talked to Calamity earlier that Desiree be present for the healing. Desiree said that she didn\u2019t know Angelica, but the new girl sure seemed to know her. So, Desiree and Calamity went in. Desiree acted familiar with Angelica and got her to relax and generally distracted her from what Calamity was up to. Calamity found the programming and started to take it apart. Apparently, Angelica had orders to insinuate herself with someone in the freehold and dream poison them so they would follow her orders. She would then have them work at becoming a monarch and the Director would have an agent highly placed in the freehold.<br /> <br /> Calamity worked on removing the programming until later in the morning. It took her a while to find out the initial orders and get rid of them. Then just as she was about to leave, and Angelica had forgotten she was there, Calamity noticed a deeper set of orders that were placed in the Fairest\u2019s mind. The secondary orders were, if discovered, to take out as many people in the Freehold as possible, in as bloody and brutal a way as she could. Possibly involving explosives. She would have had a couple of targets. The Dream House is heavily attended, as is the Rose and Thorn. That and there is the upcoming Beltane party. That would have a lot of people at it too. When this last command was discovered Desiree became upset. She claimed that \u201che wouldn\u2019t do that!\u201d I\u2019m assuming that she meant that the Director wouldn\u2019t go so far. It seems that her perceptions have been proven wrong. His programming this time around was much more complicated than it was in the past, and he had put in those secondary orders and buried them deep. His tactics have changed. He knows that we\u2019re finding the programming and removing it from his unsuspecting loyalists. If he\u2019s putting in orders to kill members of the Freehold it\u2019s only a matter of time before one of his agents succeeds. In this case Monica came across Angelica in the Hedge and directed her back to \u2018the world.\u2019 The Director might get lucky and have one of his agents find their way into the Freehold without it being known that they are his. If they can feign having come from a different Keeper then it might cause trouble for us.<br /> <br /> On the plus side to all of this, Lowjack it seems is working on making Hannah his connection to the Russian mob. Hannah has seemed honest enough with her intentions. She was concerned about Angelica and what she might do and took it upon herself to sort out the problem before anything happened. She just happens to have a more permanent way of dealing with the problem. I don\u2019t know if I agree with her strategy, but I can see the reason for it. Killing Angelica, or any of the Director\u2019s people, would be an effective way of removing the threat. The problem comes in when you take into account that the people in question have no idea that they have hidden programming in their minds. They are not lying when they tell us that they are not loyal to him. At least they believe that they are free of him and his influence. It doesn\u2019t seem fair to kill them before they have even committed any crimes.<br /> <br /> Overall it\u2019s been a fairly eventful couple of days. We got possession of the Dream House and helped deprogram an unwitting spy for a dangerous Gentry. We might also have a connection to the Russian mob, or at least Lowjack might. That could possibly come in handy, especially if we need to keep an eye on the less seen parts of the city. If he\u2019s nothing else, Lowjack is a man who prepares. I wonder if we can get any information about why Russian men (agents?) were after Natasha that time. And maybe if they\u2019re still after her? I\u2019ll admit to still being curious about that. It led to a pretty bloody fight and one dead woman. It might be nice to know what was going on with that whole situation, since Natasha is still evasive about the details. I guess time will tell on that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> The Last Dance now owns the Malibu Dream House! I am pleased!<br /> <br /> Yesterday was a very good day. We spent much of the afternoon meeting to discuss the show and working on it. When the time came everyone did well! With all the Monarchs in attendance, Juliette did \u201cLady Marmalade\u201d, with me backing her up. Well, one of the people backing her up. Calamity did \u201cNight Shift\u201d, the Siouxsie and the Banshee\u2019s version (thanks Julia for that) \u201cBloody Creature Poster Girl\u201d with Juliette. I, of course, did \u201cNon, Je ne Regrette Rien\u201d and had my choreography of \u201cIt\u2019s a Sin\u201d be displayed as well. It may have been Juliette\u2019s best performance, even topping the Christmas show. Even Calamity almost seemed happy. I had not been on stage since then myself, though it did go well. So this was good.<br /> <br /> As well as the Monarchs, we had a lot in the audience who came out in support, as well as people who just wanted to see what promised to be a kick ass show, as the Americans say. The place was packed. It got lighter when the mortals left and the Monarchs came on stage to officially grant us ownership of the land and business. The feel was celebratory. There were varying amounts of enthusiasm from the Monarchs, but they were generally pleased.<br /> <br /> Some drama going on in the background\u2026Monica brought a very cute black girl with sometimes glowing eyes to the show, and while they were like turtledoves at first Calamity talking to them provoked a fight. I will have more on that later. Juliette also seemed to have a\u2026difficult conversation with Rowan. Rowan seemed to be readying to throw herself at her, and given how that went down last time Juliette wisely shut it down.<br /> <br /> Juliette had rather the pick of the litter. Oleander, Brightstar, and Rowan were waiting in the wings, at least until Rowan\u2019s bid for her attention failed\u2026but apparently Charlotte was intrigued. Charlotte does not seem to be involved with Leanne anymore, and has been indulging with people as she gets over it, and she seemed to have her sights set on Juliette. By this point Strype was regularly having at least one hand in my clothes, so I was a little distracted. I left the standoff to take her into the basement, with Charlotte, Brightstar and Oleander all watching Juliette, the tension only broken by Monica sobbing softly.<br /> <br /> Strype liked our St. Andrews in the basement. She made some attempt to get me on it but oh no, Julia and I had her on it quickly, and she was soon wildly impressed with my talents and completely under my control. After an intense half hour so we retired upstairs after making sure she was hydrated. It remained intense, if not at all romantic. She said it was the closest she had ever come to falling in love, though.<br /> <br /> I have three lovers. I don\u2019t feel confidant I can manage more. Not and be good to them. I don\u2019t know how Juliette does it. It helps that Oleander is\u2026very independent and not too demanding I guess. She might have a hard time with a single lover of our emotional needs.<br /> <br /> Sex breakfast was interesting. Charlotte as well as Brightstar and Neon were there. Calamity was late, but present. It turns out that pretty girl with Monica, named Angelica, was from the Director. She told Monica in trust, but Monica (wisely) told Calamity. When she realized they had a fight. She reluctantly agreed to dream treatment, given the other Director girls. Brightstar, Neon and Maria were going to Brightstar and Neon\u2019s townhouse, so they agreed to drop off Angelica as she was not going back with Monica.<br /> <br /> However, she was not the only arrival, there was also a Winter Courtier Wizened named Hannah. Hannah tried to ambush and kill Angelica at the apartment they were set up with, but Molly was there to watch Angelica on Calamity\u2019s recommendation and saved her. Hannah escaped, and Jacob, Luna and Calamity tracked her down. Turns out before her librarian durance, she was with the Russian mob. They forestalled mobsters coming for her and took her to Lowjack, who determined she knew of the Director and believed Angelica was a loyalist who was controlling Monica. Which may have been true.<br /> <br /> As Angelica was sedated, Calamity went to cure her, taking Desiree by Angelica\u2019s request, apparently. Desiree distracted Angelica so Calamity could work. Desiree does not act all sexy, she is often demure, but that girl can be seduction incarnate, her Romancer side working to her advantage. Anyway, Calamity fixed the programming, as well as a more complex extra set of instructions to set off a bomb in either the Dream House or Rose and Thorn! Thank goodness for Calamity and Desiree.<br /> <br /> I did get a message from Desiree as well. She wants to be part of whatever carnality I get involved in at Beltane tonight. Should be fun.<br /> <br /> So good anniversary night! Everything was lovely. Some drama, but when is there not drama. And Beltane tonight. Should be fun.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXXXVIII</i><br /> <br /> Oh God this was a long set of journals. I am not sure much requires a lot of explanation. Hannah had Contracts of Animation going with her gun. Calamity passed a perception roll to notice the extra programming. That\u2019s about it beyond RP.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s Beltane; that means a Spring Court party! But perhaps Calamity and Jacob may not care to attend. Check it out next time. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T04:39:33-07:00","id":1128756,"title":"","content":"Glad I didn't actually have to wait till next April for this nyeh-heh-heh-heh. Now for my disjointed, rambling reaction.<br /> <br /> When Lori called herself a prude, I gotta say, I burst out laughing for a long time. It would have been awkward if anyone else was in the room.<br /> <br /> Calamity's doing about as well as expected (though I have hope from her actions she's not regressing as much as she feels she is), but it seems Jacob is starting to... I guess heal is the word. The scars will always bring back the bad feelings, but I think he's in a better place for now. So that's good.<br /> <br /> So glad someone's keeping up the tradition of Captain Jack antics, but it just won't be the same without our knight in shining armor, may his quest be glorious and victorious.<br /> <br /> Our favorite motley's enemies in Hollywood are being remarkably silent, but as I trust you greatly as an ST Baroness, this happily just makes me all the more worried. I wonder if it will go to all-out war *giggles darkly*<br /> <br /> I wonder how long it takes The Director to groom his sleeper agents? We've had a five month gap here where he could have sent in any number of sleepers. Gosh, do I love paranoia!<br /> <br /> And a what if question: If Calamity had missed the second trigger, where were you planning on having Angelica do her attack?<br /> <br /> And lastly...are you going to roleplay Beltane? *pulls out popcorn and appropriate sundries*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 08-14-2017, 07:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T09:52:20-07:00","id":1128858,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7920_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7920\" data-vbnamecard=\"7920\">Master Aquatosic</a> - To be fair, Lori does describe her unwillingness to indulge bondage play as her &quot;one streak of prudishness,&quot; but I'm glad you were amused. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, on the subject of what happens regarding the Beltane party, Lori would like the following statement registered. Ahem:<br /> <br /> &quot;I told them so.&quot;<br /> <br /> Seriously. I threatened to post this during play last night, but didn't want to be rude. Also, I was having too much fun observing the consequences. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> You'll get the full story in our respective journals in a couple of weeks. As always, thanks for reading and commenting!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T13:01:30-07:00","id":1128933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play?p=1128756#post1128756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Glad I didn't actually have to wait till next April for this nyeh-heh-heh-heh. Now for my disjointed, rambling reaction.<br /> <br /> When Lori called herself a prude, I gotta say, I burst out laughing for a long time. It would have been awkward if anyone else was in the room.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like Penitent Tom said, it was a specific case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Calamity's doing about as well as expected (though I have hope from her actions she's not regressing as much as she feels she is), but it seems Jacob is starting to... I guess heal is the word. The scars will always bring back the bad feelings, but I think he's in a better place for now. So that's good.<br /> <br /> Our favorite motley's enemies in Hollywood are being remarkably silent, but as I trust you greatly as an ST Baroness, this happily just makes me all the more worried. I wonder if it will go to all-out war *giggles darkly*<br /> <br /> I wonder how long it takes The Director to groom his sleeper agents? We've had a five month gap here where he could have sent in any number of sleepers. Gosh, do I love paranoia!<br /> <br /> And a what if question: If Calamity had missed the second trigger, where were you planning on having Angelica do her attack?<br /> <br /> And lastly...are you going to roleplay Beltane? *pulls out popcorn and appropriate sundries* </div> </div> </div><br /> I am going to roleplay Beltane, well some of it. Lorelei and Insincere Marguerite attended, Jacob and Calamity got up to other stuff.<br /> <br /> So...about the second trigger. I had a Come to Jesus moment with the players, in which I warned them I would be playing up the effects of low Clarity (hallucinations , delusions, lack of touch with reality) and that something was in the city that can do things to really warp senses of reality for PCs with less than 5 Clarity. As Jacob and Calamity had four months of therapy, a peaceful four months with nothing bad, and a fair amount of Aspirational XP and normal XP, I <i>strongly</i> recommended raising Clarity to 5, at least. Jacob's player did so. Calamity's did not.<br /> <br /> Let's just say you would be wise to not at any future point trust what Calamity experiences without another PC watching, and that things have already happened that were not what Calamity thought they were. Not everything is tainted, but things are different in certain ways than Calamity thinks they are. I am not specifically saying the extra programming is a figment of Calamity's imagination, but I also did not say it isn't. But saying what I would have done would be telling.<br /> <br /> As for Hollywood...the PCs have not been dealing with them, but a number of NPCs have. Tommy Rawhead, Gunner Friday, and Vic Twilight among others have been conspicuously absent as they have been working against them. That said...see the paragraph above last. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Thanks for the feedback and glad you are enjoying.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T14:16:27-07:00","id":1134607,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s Beltane, but not everyone is going to the celebration. Meet some new faces and explore the decadence of the Lady by the Sea.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LXXXIX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Beltane has come and gone, and momentous things are still moving within the Lady by the Sea Freehold. And while I have a lot I could say about appropriate activities during carefully planned community events\u2026 well, I\u2019ll let my friends\u2019 actions speak for themselves. Personally, I can\u2019t complain about how the party (and its aftermath) went.<br /> <br /> So I was bustling about yesterday, fretting over what to wear to the party like a stereotype, when Marguerite approached me and asked for my advice. She\u2019d gotten a few suggestive texts from Desiree indicating that the redhead would appreciate Marguerite\u2019s company that evening. Okay\u2026 so maybe they were less \u201csuggestive\u201d and more \u201cdamn near pornographic.\u201d Desiree has been doing so well lately\u2026 Marguerite was understandably hesitant to do anything that might cause her to backslide.<br /> <br /> I wasn\u2019t sure entirely what to make of the situation, but my best guess is that Desiree felt betrayed by what she learned about the Director\u2019s plans in Angelica\u2019s dreams the previous evening, and she was searching for someone to provide a little stability in her life. I advised Marguerite to tread carefully. I think it\u2019s for the best if Desiree knows that she can rely on her friends for support in difficult times, but that she shouldn\u2019t come to rely on any of us <u>too</u> much\u2026 particularly Marguerite. She agreed to handle the situation with kid gloves, which set my mind at ease.<br /> <br /> It was around this point that Calamity, Jacob, and Luna walked in and informed us that they intended to spend the evening hunting Hedge Beasts, and wanted to make sure that we knew where they were to avoid the \u201cunpleasantness\u201d that happened last time. I probably did my trademarked confused blinks before blurting out the following.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou can\u2019t. We have the Beltane party tonight.\u201d<br /> <br /> Marguerite arched an eyebrow at me in apparent amusement. \u201cYou are telling Calamity what she can and cannot do now?\u201d she asked. Calamity \u2013 even more than the rest of us \u2013 tends to buck back against arbitrary restrictions like that. Telling her not to do something is a sure-fire way to get her to do it.<br /> <br /> \u201cShit,\u201d I said, a little flustered, \u201cof course not. I only intended to <u>remind</u> our friends that we have an important social engagement scheduled for tonight.\u201d<br /> <br /> Calamity looked at me, surly and depressed as usual. \u201cLook, Lori,\u201d she said softly. \u201cI don\u2019t want to go to a drunken fuck-party tonight. It\u2019s not my scene right now. I\u2019m depressed and I\u2019m angry and instead of taking it out on you guys and the rest of the Freehold, Jacob suggested I work some of it out in a constructive way, doing something that needs to be done. Plus\u2026\u201d she hesitated for a moment, then continued in a rush. \u201cBecky\u2019s going to be there.\u201d<br /> <br /> I took her hand carefully. \u201cCalamity,\u201d I said, \u201cI\u2019m not trying to tell you how to live your life, but\u2026 we live in a small closed community of about fifty people. You\u2019re going to have to face her sooner or later.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cI know,\u201d she admitted, \u201cbut tonight, most of those fifty people are going to be at Glamour Springs. If I see her there, I\u2019m going to do something stupid, and both of us are going to end up embarrassing ourselves in front of just about everyone we know.\u201d<br /> <br /> I pulled her into a hug\u2026 again, very carefully. \u201cOkay,\u201d I said reluctantly, \u201cI think this is a bad idea, but I won\u2019t try to stop you, if you think this will help. Just promise me that you\u2019ll be careful and that you\u2019ll call me if you need me.\u201d<br /> <br /> She gave me a grin that didn\u2019t touch her eyes. \u201cWe can take care of ourselves, Lori,\u201d she reminded me.<br /> <br /> \u201cI know you can,\u201d I said, \u201cbut you guys are my friends and I love you, so I\u2019m gonna worry until you get back. So promise me, please.\u201d<br /> <br /> They dutifully gave their promises and filed out, leaving me a little sad and distracted as I tried to figure out what to wear. D opted for a (non-bathing) outfit which would showcase her impressive muscles, of course, and offered a few salacious comments as I was picking out a bikini.<br /> <br /> \u201cGot your eyes on anyone tonight?\u201d I asked in an offhand way.<br /> <br /> She saw right through it, as usual. \u201cFigured I\u2019d see what the playing field looks like before I make any decisions,\u201d she said noncommittally. \u201cWhy?\u201d<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t meet her eyes. \u201cI was hoping the two of us could spend some time together tonight,\u201d I admitted. \u201cI\u2019m not asking you not to pick anyone else up, just\u2026 maybe consider whether I could be a part of your evening too?\u201d<br /> <br /> She wrapped her arms around my waist from behind (nestled snuggly between my wings), and I was invincible again. \u201cOf course, Jules,\u201d she whispered into my ear, \u201call you ever have to do is ask.\u201d<br /> <br /> So I had that to look forward to, which brightened up my afternoon and evening considerably. I eventually decided on a very brief bikini (not like Marguerite-thong tiny, but still more daring than I usually wear outside of the Dream House) which quickly gained D\u2019s seal of approval. It was a balmy May 1st, so I didn\u2019t even bother with a jacket or sarong or anything like that this time.<br /> <br /> In the end, we decided to take two cars rather than piling into Marguerite\u2019s Volvo. D and I took the \u2018vette, of course, while Marguerite and Julia opted to take the beetle. We wanted two vehicles so that we\u2019d have the option of splitting up to be with different partners, of course\u2026 but I also really like showing off in that \u2018vette, and it just won\u2019t fit all four of us comfortably (even if Marguerite climbs into the glovebox).<br /> <br /> So most of the Freehold was present at Glamour Springs last night, and things were already off to a roaring start when we arrived. D sauntered off to see if she could scare us up some additional company for the evening, but I was almost immediately pulled into a conversation with none other than Joan and Andromeda. It seems that our resident Defender of the Faith and My Favorite Martian were looking to broaden their experience a bit, and were looking for advice about another third lady to bring into their bedroom. I considered for a moment, and scanned the crowd briefly before coming up with the <u>perfect</u> candidate.<br /> <br /> \u201cFlores,\u201d I said after a moment.<br /> <br /> Andromeda\u2019s face lit up immediately. \u201cOf course!\u201d she said. \u201cShe\u2019s adorable, and very open to stuff like this.\u201d<br /> <br /> Joan looked less certain. \u201cI will\u2026 consider it,\u201d she said guardedly.<br /> <br /> I took her hand in mine. \u201cJoan,\u201d I said softly, \u201cif this is something the two of you want to do \u2013 something that will bring you closer together, like the time that the three of us spend together \u2013 then you won\u2019t find a better-suited person in the Freehold. Flores is kind and earnest and honest to a fault. She\u2019s also beautiful, and an experienced lover.\u201d<br /> <br /> Andromeda helpfully noted that if the two of them <u>did</u> want to spend the evening with Flores, they needed to move quickly, as her company was certain to be in high demand. I left the two of them to it\u2026 but I think they went forward with their new daring experiment. I hope the three of them had fun.<br /> <br /> Almost as soon as I left that private conference, Princess Jolie approached me. My heart did this little flip like it does every time I see the Princess, and I gave her a little curtsy by way of greeting. She returned the favor with a smile, a hug and a kiss on the mouth\u2026 and then told me that she had approached me for business, not pleasure. I confess that I pouted a bit when she said that. Can you blame me?<br /> <br /> The reason she approached me turned my frown upside-down pretty quickly, but it does require a bit of backstory. See, several of my friends belong to exclusive societies within the Changeling community called \u201centitlements.\u201d Gawain\u2019s group specializes in dream healing, Jacob\u2019s group helps to find refuges for Changelings fleeing the servants of the Gentry, and so forth. I\u2019d never really given it much thought until a couple of months ago, when I heard about a group calling themselves the \u201cPilgrims of the Endless Road.\u201d<br /> <br /> The Pilgrims are a loose collecting of Changelings who have dedicated themselves to becoming well-rounded individuals. Specifically, they try to do this by identifying their own weaknesses and doing what they can to shore up those aspects of their lives. Someone who is intelligent and yet physically frail might take up a rigorous exercise regimen to build up their strength and agility, for example, while a powerful fighter who is burdened by crippling shyness might go out of his way to make new friends and overcome his handicap.<br /> <br /> This immediately made me think of my own efforts to learn medicine. Anyone who spends more than a few minutes with me will tell you that I\u2019m something of a social butterfly, and my Gentry-enhanced looks give me certain advantages in that arena. The years I\u2019ve spent as a dancer (not to mention lugging around these wings for the past God-knows-how-long) have similarly built up my strength and stamina to levels most people don\u2019t really suspect. But the one area in which I\u2019ve always come up short is my intelligence\u2026 I\u2019m still your stereotypical dumb blonde, no matter what my friends and lovers might say.<br /> <br /> I first recognized that this had to change when I started practicing the Spring Court healing contracts about a year ago. Though I could speed along the healing process for my friends, I simply didn\u2019t know enough about how the human (or near-human) body is supposed to work to be particularly effective at it. So I started to read medical textbooks and periodicals, hoping that some of it would stick around long enough to make a difference. And while I wouldn\u2019t go so far as to say that I have an aptitude for it or anything \u2013 I still have to read most of this stuff three or four times before I really get it \u2013 I <u>did</u> discover that I <u>like</u> studying medicine. It makes me feel like I might actually be able to make a difference in this world for the better. It makes me feel like maybe someday, someone might admire me for more than my looks.<br /> <br /> (I\u2019m not talking about D or Marguerite or Julia or any of my other friends or lovers here, by the way. I know that they love me for more than my appearance\u2026 but they\u2019ve all gotten to know me well, and they can see things about me that aren\u2019t immediately apparent to casual acquaintances. I\u2019m hoping that someday, people I <u>don\u2019t</u> know well will think of me as more than just a pretty face and a nice set of tits).<br /> <br /> In any case, the Princess had heard that I had been asking questions about the Pilgrims, and wanted to let me know that two of them were passing through the Freehold, and were in fact present at the Beltane feast. She offered to introduce me to them, and I accepted. Which is how I ended up speaking to representatives of an organization I hope to join dressed in nothing but a teeny bikini. Sigh.<br /> <br /> Peg Powler and Jimmy Squarefoot are obviously Brits. Jolie warned me before I met them that I might have difficulty understanding them, but I figure the past year of living with Ace left me more than amply prepared, and we were able to communicate just fine. I think they\u2019re both Ogres, but I\u2019m not completely sure of that. We spoke amiably for a few minutes (they\u2019re both enjoying their time in the Freehold, though Jimmy seemed oddly certain that spending too much time here would turn them both gay) before getting down to brass tacks.<br /> <br /> I told them that I\u2019m interested in joining the Pilgrims, and they allowed as how that might be possible. They wanted to speak with me privately in a more sedate and comfortable setting before making a final decision (which I completely understand), so we arranged to meet the following afternoon at the Dream House. I offered to comp them two tickets to the show afterward, which they seemed to appreciate. Free glamour is not to be scoffed at.<br /> <br /> So it was with more than one butterfly in my stomach that I went back to the main floor and started looking for D. I suppose it must be like preparing for a job interview\u2026 though I\u2019ve never actually <u>had</u> a job interview\u2026 unless you count that meeting with Jolie where I was offered the job at the Dream House\u2026 but I didn\u2019t <u>know</u> that was a job interview until it was nearly over\u2026 you know what, never mind. Bad analogy.<br /> <br /> In any case, I spotted D hanging out near the far wall of the Glamour Springs complex, and made my way over to her. She was chatting up Dominika, who would occasionally giggle and fondle my fianc\u00e9e\u2019s biceps (see, it\u2019s not just me). Her face kind of fell as I approached, but I threw her a smile that seemed to reassure her. \u201cDon\u2019t worry, Dominika,\u201d I said softly once I was close enough. \u201cI just wanted to talk to D for a minute. I wouldn\u2019t dream of interfering with any plans the two of you have made. Although\u2026\u201d and here I batted my eyelashes theatrically, \u201c\u2026if you\u2019re not too strongly opposed to the idea, I wouldn\u2019t be averse to <u>joining</u> you two tonight.\u201d<br /> <br /> Dominika\u2019s eyes widened, and she sort of nodded, and allowed me to lead D a short distance away. I told her about the Pilgrims and my meeting the following day, and she was super-happy for me.<br /> <br /> Moon stopped by to talk to me as I was finishing up this conversation, and any fool could tell that ze was very upset. Ze said that Desiree had been avoiding hir in the wake of their evening together, and ze didn\u2019t know what ze had done wrong. I did my best to console hir, letting hir know that Desiree had suffered an unfortunate shock which had nothing to do with their encounter, and merely needed time to recover. I suggested that ze give Desiree her space for a couple of days, and promised to speak with her about the situation on hir behalf.<br /> <br /> Then D and I went back to chatting up Dominika.<br /> <br /> I got a call a few minutes later. It was Calamity. \u201cHow bad is it?\u201d I asked with a sigh.<br /> <br /> Calamity sort of chuckled. \u201cWe\u2019re all okay, Lori,\u201d she said, and then, in response to something one of the others said (my money is on Luna), she added \u201cwell, okay, I could do with a little of your Spring Court magic when you get home, if you\u2019re up to it. But we all made it back to the Dream House, so don\u2019t worry about that. But look\u2026 if Monica is there, can you pass along a message for me? There are a metric butt-load of the Director\u2019s Extras in the Hedge tonight. Like\u2026 two dozen or so. And they\u2019ve learned some new tricks.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLike what?\u201d I asked, curious.<br /> <br /> \u201cSome kind of hypnotic dance,\u201d she said, waving it off, \u201cand they\u2019re coordinating their attacks now. They\u2019re a lot more dangerous than they used to be. Oh, and we also picked up another new arrival. She calls herself Carla and\u2026 you know what, never mind. You\u2019ve got to see her to understand. Just let Monica know, please.\u201d<br /> <br /> I promised to pass along this disturbing news, and the three of us quickly moved to do so. As I was looking for Monica, I noticed a few things that gave me pause. Desiree <u>was</u> at the fete last night\u2026 and she was bare-ass naked. She was following Marguerite around like a puppy, but it didn\u2019t look like Marguerite was abusing her position of power, so I let it go for the moment. And hey, at least she didn\u2019t have Desiree on a leash. No, that was Annika and Dark Kimberly. Sigh. Oh, and I did mention Moon\u2019s concerns to Desiree, at which she gave me a Great-This-Is-All-I-Need-Right-Now sigh.<br /> <br /> In any case, I dutifully told Monica about the proliferation of Extras in the local Hedge. Dominika engaged in some light teasing of her ex, but I don\u2019t think Monica took it personally. She <u>did</u> look a little glum about maybe having to leave the Beltane party \u2013 and Dionisia, whom she was currently lifting over her head in a bizarre form of flirting \u2013 but she brightened up a bit when I told her that my motley had disposed of quite a few of the invaders. She promised to meet the new girl and look into things in the Hedge the following day, and turned her attention back toward everyone\u2019s favorite Talecrafter.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo,\u201d I said as we moved away from the two of them, \u201cyou two ready to get out of here and let the rest of our evening commence?\u201d<br /> <br /> Dominika nodded. \u201cLet\u2019s get out of here before we run into anyone <u>else</u> who\u2019s prettier than me,\u201d she said in that delightful island lilt of hers.<br /> <br /> I took her head in my hands and made her look into my eyes. \u201cDominika, sweetie,\u201d I said softly, \u201cyou are one of the most beautiful women I have ever <u>seen</u>. Don\u2019t ever let anyone make you feel differently.\u201d<br /> <br /> Well, the \u2018vette isn\u2019t really built for three people, so I told Dominika that she\u2019d have to sit on D\u2019s lap on the way to the Dream House. She didn\u2019t seem to mind the inconvenience, luckily. Twenty minutes later we pulled up to the House, and I told the two of them to give me a minute while I saw to Calamity\u2019s injuries.<br /> <br /> The three of them were in the kitchen when I walked in, and it took me a moment to process what I was seeing. I think my exact words were something along the lines of \u201cokay, what can I do to help oh my God what the holy <u>FUCK</u> happened to you?\u201d<br /> <br /> Calamity and Jacob\u2019s clothes were torn, and they were bloody pretty much <u>everywhere</u>, though Jacob\u2019s Elemental contracts had absorbed the brunt of the attacks against him. Calamity, on the other hand, looked like she was only barely conscious, struggling to remain sitting upright in a straight-backed chair. The newcomer, a cute girl with big eyes and a fluffy tail, looked nervously on from the sidelines.<br /> <br /> The story unfolded as I saw to Calamity\u2019s injuries. The three of them had come across nine of the Extras, who seemed to be pantomiming some sort of tea party as they approached. The three of them turned invisible and attacked, taking out several of their opponents within the first few seconds. Then one of the Extras began dancing, which sort of froze Calamity in place. A few of the others attacked her in rapid succession, and she went down, unable to defend herself. They repeated the process on Jacob, who fared better. Before any of them could target Luna, she used a Contract to animate the local Hedge, killing the <u>hell</u> out of several more of them and driving the rest off.<br /> <br /> Thank God she was with them. We might never have seen them again if not for her.<br /> <br /> It took a couple of applications of the healing contract to get Calamity on her feet again, but eventually I was able to close her wounds (even the most persistent of them). She was still pretty badly bruised when we said goodnight, but a bit of rest and relaxation should see her right.<br /> <br /> We introduced ourselves to Carla briefly. She\u2019s\u2026 odd. I\u2019ve been back long enough to see for myself the impact that anime \u2013 what we used to call \u201cJapanimation\u201d back in the day \u2013 has had on American culture, but apparently this effect runs deeper than I had previously suspected. There\u2019s a whole society built up around the veneration of these \u201ccatgirls\u201d that frankly just mystifies me. I mean, yeah, Carla is cute, but having been Taken in the late 90s, she seemed to take it as a given that she\u2019d be able to write her own ticket now that she\u2019s a real catgirl. Personally, I don\u2019t see why that makes her any more desirable than a bird-girl like me, or a sheep-girl like Mary.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m wandering from the point. Carla was an anime-enthusiast when she was Taken, and still knows next to nothing about the Gentry or changeling society, so Monica\u2019s going to have her hands full with that one.<br /> <br /> In any case, my fianc\u00e9e and I escorted our guest up to our bedroom and proceeded to rock her world. Well, okay, maybe that\u2019s not entirely fair; Dominika gave as good as she got, and she was an enthusiastic and talented lover. I am relatively certain that a good time was had by all.<br /> <br /> So we staggered downstairs in various states of undress late the following morning, looking forward to a nice hearty sex breakfast. The three of us weren\u2019t quite able to make the entrance that Marguerite and her entourage did, what with Desiree and White Maria carrying her reclining form on their shoulders, and Julia feeding her grapes like some sort of decadent Roman emperor or something, but that\u2019s not really my scene in any case.<br /> <br /> Calamity and Carla came up from the basement together, but it didn\u2019t look like they\u2019d been up to anything naughty down there\u2026 they were both bleeding again. I didn\u2019t ask for all the details, but apparently Calamity startled the new girl just after she woke up, and the kitten unleashed her claws\u2026 and then promptly hurt herself on Calamity\u2019s glass. Sigh. I fired up the ol\u2019 healing contracts again. I swear, that girl is going to be the death of me.<br /> <br /> So as per usual lately, I volunteered to check the mail. And as per usual, nothing from any of the colleges I applied to. Dammit! The suspense is killing me. I\u2019d even be relieved to see a rejection letter at this point; at least then I\u2019d <u>know</u>.<br /> <br /> Monica arrived not long after, and took Carla under her wing\u2026 blushing and stammering again. Double-sigh. That girl sure does love heartbreak.<br /> <br /> The rest of us spent a while discussing the significance of the Extras in the Hedge. The Director is obviously adopting new tactics, and the monarchs need to know about it. Calamity offered to take on that duty, and is going to speak with Old Billy to make sure that the Summer Court is aware of what the Extras can do now. But what is his game? Obviously he sent Angelica as a spy and saboteur\u2026 but could he also be in some way behind the arrival of Hannah and Carla? Those three have all arrived within the last few days, and prior to that it had been more than half a year since we\u2019d seen a new face around here.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Carla\u2026 the catgirl said that she had encountered some of the Extras while wandering through the Hedge, and they had completely ignored her. She even walked right through the middle of a crowd of them, and they showed no sign that they even noticed her presence. So even if our new arrivals <u>aren\u2019t</u> sent directly by the Director\u2026 could he be channeling or herding recent escapees toward us for some reason? Maybe he wants to deluge the Freehold with new faces so that we\u2019re less likely to recognize the real threats?<br /> <br /> I dunno; I tend to leave the heavy strategizing to smarter people. And besides, I had other things to focus on. As the conversation ebbed, I retreated to my bedroom and started getting ready to meet with Peg and Jimmy. I put on a nice ensemble\u2026 not quite church clothes, but a button-up shirt, a skirt, and leggings, and spent a little time on my hair and make-up. What can I say? I want to make a good impression on these two. If the Pilgrims decide to take me under their wing (ironic, no?), I\u2019m sure they\u2019ll be able to teach me a few novel ways to shore up my weaknesses, which I\u2019m going to need when we head back into Arcadia to rescue Missy and Jane.<br /> <br /> Ah! That\u2019s the door! They\u2019re here!<br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei Grace</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> Saturday, May 2nd<br /> Nine years, one month, twenty-one days<br /> Days without stabbing: 0<br /> <br /> You know, one would think that skipping the sex party would mean not winding up with a couple of strangers aggressively ramming things inside me but one would be wrong. As I was wrapping up writing a report on the details of my Oneiromancy with Angelica for the monarchs Jacob showed up at the door to the office and asked me if I was planning to go to Beltane. He seemed to know my answer would be no and he just happened to have an alternative suggestion that didn\u2019t involve me being alone. Maybe I should be annoyed at the big brotherliness, but I do know he means well and his solution was to go into the Hedge with he and Luna hunting hobgoblins, which was a way better idea than going to some stupid drunken fuck revel and watching Becky hook up with someone that isn\u2019t me.<br /> <br /> So I went up to get ready and ran into Lori and Marguerite talking. Lori asked me what I was going to wear and I told her I wasn\u2019t sure, most likely my biker leathers. She kinda blinked at me and I added that it seemed good for hunting hobgoblins. She really was aghast at the idea of me not going to Beltane. We went back and forth a bit, but she seemed to accept that maybe it wasn\u2019t where I needed to be tonight. I mean, she is right about me not being able to avoid Becky forever and that so isn\u2019t my plan. This not talking bullshit ain\u2019t going to fucking cut it. But at this point I don\u2019t expect it to be a pretty conversation and I don\u2019t much want a fucking peanut gallery watching us have it. Too damn much work disposing of the extra bodies if it goes really bad.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I ended up wearing the leather armor Gawain made for me. I wasn\u2019t going to but it\u2019s really good, decent protection without slowing me down. I should see if I can find someone to replace it so I can pack it away with his portrait but I\u2019m not going to refuse the protection just because he made it for me till then.<br /> <br /> We hit the hedge and used dreams to get a read on things. Holy fuck was it a target rich environment. Got my glass and lady-bits all atingle. But I reigned myself in and we stepped back out to call Old Billy and give him a head\u2019s up to pass along so nobody decided to stagger home from the party via the hedge and got jacked up. He started up about some fucking app or some shit but he did agree to pass the word along.<br /> <br /> And that done, we returned to the task of fucking up some monsters. I let Luna and Jacob take point, trailing quietly along while they tracked a larger group down. Turned out to be the Director\u2019s fucking extras having some kind of goddamn mime tea party. I mean, beggars can\u2019t be choosers and all but I really was hoping to taste some blood. We quickly agreed upon a fall back point and all three went lightshy.<br /> <br /> The initial charge was beautiful. We weren\u2019t completely sure if being invisible would be that useful against things without faces or eyes but if they knew we were there they ignored us. I exploded mine like an angry teenager ripping into the stupid over-sized stuffie her ex won at some sketchy sideshow game on the pier while Jacob and Luna attacked with more caution and less rabid gusto. To be fair, their relationship hasn\u2019t gone fucking pear-shaped yet. We\u2019ll see if they\u2019re so damned calm then won\u2019t we? Of course, now that I think about it, that is going to suck. Maybe I\u2019ll get lucky and one of them will die or something before their relationship sours so I don\u2019t have to pick sides in the breakup.<br /> <br /> But yeah, back on track, once we\u2019d hit them, things got weird. Apparently the Director has upgraded the apparatus recently. One of them started some sort of dance or something and I just\u2026 stopped. All I could do was watch and at the same time the others turned on me with precision and attacked. They carved me up pretty good in short order. Next thing I know, Luna\u2019s bandaging me while all hell\u2019s breaking loose around us. Like hail and thunder and the fucking trees attacking (like actually swinging their branches and grabbing with their roots, none of that lame Shamma-lamma-ding-dong suicide pollen crap). Even the motherfucking rocks were throwing themselves at the last couple of extras as they fled. They\u2019d pulled the same cheating trick with Jacob apparently but his elemental toughness had taken the brunt of their initial attacks and then Luna dropped the hammer. Damn, that woman has some fine tricks up her sleeve.<br /> <br /> Despite being able to walk under my own power, I let Jacob help me since the alternative was getting fucking carried apparently. We were walking back to the Dream House portal when we came across Carla, cat-girl mecha pilot from planet Neko. Overly long story short, her keeper apparently recreated a bad harem anime and keeps dropping unsuspecting guys in as the leader of the mecha squad, only instead of them leading the squad to victory and getting their justly earned reward of cat-girl fucking they all end up getting brutally killed off by the space demon. It\u2019s like some sort of twisted how it should have ended joke or something. Anyway, after getting shot down due to the loser of the week\u2019s lack of skills Carla managed to crash in the hedge instead of back in her realm. She\u2019s really got no clue how all of this shit works and was completely lost so we agreed to let her tag along with us back to reality.<br /> <br /> She\u2019s a bit ditsy, as befits a cat-girl I guess. I tried to explain a few basics while we were walking but she didn\u2019t seem to really get it that she was just drawn into a story. Luna clearly doesn\u2019t like her and really wanted to just kill her. Me\u2026 well she is adorable and kinda hapless\u2026 I can only imagine all of the absolutely delicious little whimpering and mewling and begging I could coax out of that little kitten\u2026 Mmmm\u2026 but I really should stop imagining that since it would be bad form to break out the Harbinger of the Void while Lori is trying to make a good impression with the Pilgrims of the Endless Road.<br /> <br /> She met them at the party last night (guess they were looking for the perfect fuck or something) and they dropped by to interview her presently about joining. She seems nervous. I\u2019ll just keep my head down and try not to stab anyone while they\u2019re here.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Monica was too busy hooking up last night to do her duty so we put the kitty up in the guest room. Lori and D had snagged Dominica but after we called to let them know I needed some heals she stopped by on the way to fucktown to make a big deal over my injuries while she patched me up.<br /> <br /> I spent the night lurking just in case the stray decided to try something but she just curled up and slept. When she emerged this morning I dropped out of the shadows behind her to test her reflexes. Kitten\u2019s quick and those dainty little claws aren\u2019t just decorative. She slashed me fairly well though she ended up cutting herself on my glass, which spiced my cut with the burn of her sweet innocent blood. She didn\u2019t seem overly amused and Lori gave me one of her long suffering sighs when she healed us both up while I cooked up a pair of steaks for us. Kitty likes meat apparently and I sure as fuck wasn\u2019t going to cook a steak and not have one myself.<br /> <br /> Marguerite got carried in by Desiree and White Maria while Julia fed her grapes. So clearly she had a good night. Desiree was ribbing White Maria, who seemed unusually uncomfortable with whatever had happened and seemed ashamed at being reminded about it. Seems Marguerite took things to a new level last night. Fortunately, she had some words with Desiree before I had to get sarcastic with her. And Red did claim she just wanted White Maria to loosen up since she had seemed happier last night than she ever does when she\u2019s being her usual prim and proper self. I\u2019ll bring it up with White Maria Monday morning and make sure everything\u2019s cool.<br /> <br /> Anyway, sex breakfast rolled on like it does and Monica showed up to pick up her newest romantic mistake so she\u2019s not my problem for the moment. And now it\u2019s about time for me to head over to see Old Billy along with Luna and Jacob and let him know what we found out with the extras new tricks.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Well today was an interesting day all around. Most people in the Dream House were starting to get ready for the Beltane party. Most everyone that is except Calamity. She was busy in the office doing paperwork. I know a stalling technique when I see one. So, I ran an idea past Luna before I did anything else. I then knocked on the office door and asked Calamity if she was planning on going to the Beltane Party. She said that she wasn\u2019t, and didn\u2019t have a better idea when I asked what she was going to do. So, I asked if she\u2019d like to go hunting in the Hedge. I don\u2019t know if my idea was the healthiest way to deal with Calamity\u2019s issues, but it would get her out of that office and out doing something productive. I think my therapist and I have a different idea of what constitutes productive, but that\u2019s okay. Calamity jumped on the idea like it was a lifeline and went ahead to tell Lori what we were planning to do. At first Lori was almost insistent that Calamity go to the party, but eventually relented when Calamity pointed out that there would likely be a scene with Becky there and she didn\u2019t want to deal with that tonight. So, Lori got her to promise to call if we needed any help, and Calamity agreed.<br /> <br /> So, Luna, Calamity and I got prepared and made our way into the Hedge. I took a \u201clook\u201d around using a contract and determined that there was a lot of activity in the area today. I do mean a lot. So, I looked around and found tracks for a group of Extras, about nine of them. So, we decided to follow that group and see about taking care of them. We snuck up on them and found them acting out what looked like a dinner party. They were serving trays or plates and putting things down on a table. The whole nine yards. They didn\u2019t seem to notice us, but we didn\u2019t want to take any chances. I don\u2019t know if they could actually see us since they don\u2019t technically have eyes, but we decided to use a contract and turn invisible. We then all surprise attacked at the same time. It was very effective. Calamity took out her target in one strike. Luna and I wounded ours, but they were still standing after we took a step back. After that is when the trouble started.<br /> <br /> The Extras did something to mesmerize Calamity and she just stopped moving. Two more of the Extras piled on top of her and both hit her hard. She went down under their attacks. The extra in front of me did the same thing and I found myself unable to move. It then attacked me, but I was able to soak the hit with my elemental ability. I was ready to keep attacking when I realized that Calamity was lying on the ground bleeding out. Panic flared through my heart and I started to move towards my fallen friend. Luna must have felt the same thing, only add fury to the mix. She animated the Hedge around us so it was viciously attacking the Extras. I mean everything was attacking them. The vines and brambles, the rocks on the ground, everything. Her power was tearing them apart but leaving us unscathed. The remaining Extras fled. She then took the opportunity to see to Calamity\u2019s wounds and stop the bleeding. Calamity insisted on standing up on her own once she came to, but I wouldn\u2019t let her. I insisted on helping her stand and walk, and if she didn\u2019t agree to that then Luna and I would carry her back to the Dream House. Calamity realized that I wasn\u2019t bluffing and allowed me to help her start walking out of the Hedge.<br /> <br /> As we were heading home we came across a young woman in the Hedge. She appeared to be a cat girl with furry ears and tail. She told us that her name is Carla and that she is a cat girl mecha pilot from the planet Neko. Someone had a seriously strange durance. We tried explaining to her that she had been held captive in a place called Arcadia, but she kept insisting that it was the planet Neko. She had been looking for a way \u201cback to earth.\u201d Well she found it. Relatively speaking. I don\u2019t know how much of our explanations penetrated her mind, but we tried. We told her that we\u2019d lead her out to \u2018the world,\u2019 and arrange for someone to explain what happened and where she is now. She was already familiar with California. She seemed to think that she\u2019d have it made as a cat girl and would be very popular. She was disappointed to learn that mortals can\u2019t see her ears and tail, and will only see her as a regular human girl. I\u2019m not sure why she thought she\u2019d have it made. I guess it must be an anime thing.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately for Carla she was seriously annoying Luna, and my girlfriend threatened to stab her on multiple occasions. I don\u2019t really blame her. Carla was getting a little irritating, but I was trying to be patient and put up with her talking until we could get her to the Dream House and into Monica\u2019s hands. She usually deals with the new arrivals so we figured she could deal with Carla too.<br /> <br /> When we got back to the Dream House we called Lori and let her know that we needed her assistance. I let her know that we were all fine, but needed a bit of healing. We also let her know that we found a new Changeling in the Hedge and needed Monica\u2019s assistance in dealing with her. Lori told Monica what was up but it turned out that the Blackbird Bishop was busy that evening, so she\u2019d come by in the morning. I know Luna was not happy to be putting the cat girl up for the evening, but we didn\u2019t really have much choice. We couldn\u2019t leave her in the Hedge and there wasn\u2019t really anyone else that we could foist her off on. So, we agreed to house her for the night. Eventually Lori came back to the house with De La Rocha and Dominka. Lori took one look at Calamity and swore a blue streak. She then got down to business and healed Calamity almost entirely. It was impressive to say the least. I\u2019m glad that we have Lori in our motley. I think she is almost single-handedly responsible for most of us still being here.<br /> <br /> After that Calamity cooked up a pair of steaks for her and Carla. Apparently cat girls like meat. Once they were done eating we escorted Carla down to the basement guest room and showed her in. She said \u201cThank you\u201d and curled up on the mattress to sleep.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not sure what Calamity was thinking was going to happen. She stayed up all night watching the guest room to make sure that Carla didn\u2019t get up to anything. I understand that. She was hiding up on the ceiling, holding onto support beams. I can understand that. But when Carla walked out of the room this morning Calamity dropped down behind the cat girl and scared the living daylights out of her. That\u2019s what I don\u2019t understand. Was she expecting a different response? Carla, scared, turned around and used her claws to attack Calamity. Unfortunately for the cat girl she ended up also cutting herself on Calamity\u2019s glass. The pair of them, bloody, came upstairs and Lori got upset all over again about Calamity getting hurt. She was also upset about our guest coming up bloody. I don\u2019t think anyone expected that.<br /> <br /> A short while later Insincere Marguerite was carried into the kitchen by White Maria and Desiree with Julia walking along side feeding her lover grapes. It was a strange entrance to say the least, but not the strangest I\u2019ve seen. They all seemed to be enjoying themselves in any case. They all then sat down to eat breakfast. While they were eating, Lori went out to get the mail and came back in with Monica a short while later. I guess the Blackbird Bishop arrived while she was outside. She ended up joining us for breakfast too. Overall, we had a pretty full kitchen this morning. Everyone seemed to be enjoying themselves, which is good. Calamity was in an especially good mood, teasing Carla, and laughing whenever she startled or scared the cat girl. I was happy to see Calamity smiling, but perhaps not for the reasons that she was. I know Calamity sometimes goes down a dark path I her mind, but she doesn\u2019t usually show it, or give in to it so blatantly.<br /> <br /> After breakfast was over Carla left with Monica and the motley had a discussion about whether or not we think that the cat girl is a loyalist or not. Some people thought she might be from the Director, but others disagreed. It\u2019s true that her story does not line up with previous spies sent from the Director. They tend to know where they\u2019re from, they just don\u2019t realize that they\u2019ve been programmed before they were let go. Luna didn\u2019t trust her at all and was all for killing her outright as a precaution. I conceded that I didn\u2019t trust her either and told my lady love that we would keep a close eye on the cat girl.<br /> <br /> On another, more positive note, Lori got dressed up nice this afternoon in expectance of some guests. She apparently will be meeting two members of the Pilgrims of the Endless Road entitlement and set up a time to talk for this afternoon. She has been interested in joining this group for a while. I know she\u2019s been working on bettering herself in a variety of ways including physical skills and mental ones. I helped her learn more about tracking and camping in the Hedge a while back, and she\u2019s been studying those medical textbooks day and night. Usually instead of sleeping. I think she\u2019s been better about actually sleeping at night lately, but she still studies a lot. The Pilgrims are all about bettering oneself, so I personally think that Lori would make a good candidate, but it\u2019s not my opinion that really matters I guess. It\u2019s the two reps that are coming. Here\u2019s hoping she makes it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> Beltane went well.<br /> <br /> While preparing I got a series of pleading texts from Desiree, wanting my company. They were needy and out of character, so I showed Juliette. We agreed it likely had to do with the revelation concerning The Director yesterday, and I would not be harming her or was in danger, so I agreed. Just then Calamity came in, begging off to go hunting with Jacob. Not too surprising. Maybe actually healthy for her.<br /> <br /> Maria went to assist as Angelica was moved from the hospital so we could heal her. She was back in time to prepare for Beltane. And we all dressed up, well, Julia dressed to the nines, Juliette and I in bathing suits (with a t-shirt for I) and Maria wore leather, shockingly.<br /> <br /> Julia and I went in Julia\u2019s Bug (admittedly more stylish than my Volvo) while Juliette and Maria went in her Vette (admittedly more stylish than the Bug). Desiree was with me soon as I entered, sticking close. Also, for some reason, in the altogether. Juliette was waylaid by Joan and Andromeda shortly after entering, and Maria wandered off by herself. Desiree and I went to a hot tub while Julia socialized, to kiss and cuddle a bit.<br /> <br /> Julia eventually reappeared with White Maria in tow, and she asked if she could join us. I told her only if she was prepared to get suitably depraved. She nervously acquiesced, so we went to her house, stopping to shop briefly on the way.<br /> <br /> I will give White Maria this; she did not balk at anything she was asked to do, however depraved. Even Desiree got nervous once. But the four of us had a most excellent time; even we did push the boundaries a bit further than most of us usually would on a normal night. Julia really has a wild side when she lets herself go, and I am not sure White Maria was prepared for it. But I will say no more; I promised White Maria I would not talk about the things she did, or were done to her. Which is probably for the best. I guess she should be glad Calamity did not come by for practice that morning, I can\u2019t imagine what she would have said about the living room, and at least she could not have seen the boudoir.<br /> <br /> It may have been a bit much, is what I am saying.<br /> <br /> Once we got up, cleaned up everything that that would rot, and showered, we headed out for sex breakfast. I had White Maria and Desiree carry me in like an empress while Julia carried a dish at my arm level with some of the grapes we had left. Juliette and Maria had Dominika, who was looking lovely and in a very good mood. Calamity, Jacob, and Luna were there, as was Carla, a Beast they found in the Hedge. White Maria was pretty quiet\u2026.she was still a bit wide eyed and letting the last night sink in. Desiree got to be more and more of her usual self as time went on, and Juliette spoke a little to her about Moon, who apparently was getting somewhat attached after they slept together on Walpurgis.<br /> <br /> About the time our visiting Fairest headed out, Monica headed in to pick up Carla. I hope things go better than they did with Angelica.<br /> <br /> So, Calamity, Jacob, and Luna got in a battle with some extras hunting in the hedge. They won, but the extras displayed new powers and stunned Calamity and Jacob as the fight went on. They still pulled it out, and killed five extras. They also met the Beast Carla who is cat aspected. She seemed\u2026fetish-y, honestly. Sweet and innocent and talking about being a mecha pilot from the planet Neko. A bit saccharine for my Darkling nature.<br /> <br /> Calamity and Carla had bloodied each other a bit, and Calamity was in a very, very good mood despite needing healing. I don\u2019t think I want to know.<br /> <br /> Juliette met some members of the Pilgrims of the Endless Road named Peg Powler and Jimmy Squarefoot, both of which had strong English accents, apparently. They will be coming by here soon, to discuss what Juliette needs to enter their Entitlement, and Calamity is headed out to warn the Summer Court about the new abilities the Extras have.<br /> <br /> I wonder if White Maria will dare to show her face tonight. It should be a fun night regardless.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXXXIX</i><br /> <br /> The extras were using a channeled power to paralyze Calamity and Jacob. Dangerous on their own, this removed Defense, which was bad, as well as immobilization. To their credit, Calamity and Jacob both came very close to resisting the contested roll.<br /> <br /> Luna used Contracts of the Wild, specifically the final Clause, and got nine successes. The results were devastating.<br /> <br /> I went with my best Northumberland accent for Peg Powler and Jimmy Squarefoot. It was fun. They griped a lot about the weather. Neither looked like the Froud Faeries picture, obviously. Honestly both were now unused <i>Night Train Detective Agency pictures.</i><br /> <br /> As a strictly OOC note, the picture for Carla is one I have used in <b>Deadlands: Lost Colony</b> for my <i>Shadow Valley Colonial Rangers</i> game for a barmaid that was being courted by a vampire, then in <b>Demon the Descent</b> for <i>Night Train Detective Agency</i> for a Colony Werecat, also a waitress. I guess Carla will become a waitress? Regardless, both other girls were trouble, so I think OOC there were some red flags with the picture.<br /> <br /> Pilgrims of the Endless Road are in <i>Swords at Dawn</i> I think? Meanwhile in her dreams Insincere Marguerite is being courted by the Lost Pantheon from <i>Lords of Summer</i>.<br /> <br /> Okay well I think that covers everything, but as always comments and questions are welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T14:47:30-07:00","id":1134620,"title":"","content":"Jimmy is not exactly right. It's not so much that the Freehold turns you gay so much as it's a giant magnet for everything gay and fae. So if you're here, you're probably gay already <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> That said, to a serious and soon to be regular feature of these comments: Calamity's Hallucinations This Session.<br /> <br /> Calamity's Hallucinations Count: 0<br /> <br /> Search me, i can't find anything she's seen that hasn't been confirmed by Jacob this session. I guess you're saving the juicy bits for later eh, mon ami?<br /> <br /> EDIT: unless Neko-chan here isn't actually an innocent...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 08-27-2017, 05:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T15:40:26-07:00","id":1134641,"title":"","content":"There was actually something, but she did not actually mention it in her journal and only she saw/heard it, so...<br /> <br /> It may come up next time. Your sharp eyes did not miss it.<br /> <br /> Really it is more fair to say Bi than Gay, but then Jimmy is an old fashioned fellow. He will get over it, I am sure.<br /> <br /> Thanks as always for feedback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T15:53:14-07:00","id":1134644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroness Nerak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play?p=1134641#post1134641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really it is more fair to say Bi than Gay, but then Jimmy is an old fashioned fellow. He will get over it, I am sure.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>My apologies. I sure hope he will too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T22:40:43-07:00","id":1134757,"title":"","content":"Nothing to apologize for, Master Aquatosic. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T00:57:26-07:00","id":1134781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroness Nerak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play?p=1134641#post1134641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really it is more fair to say Bi than Gay, but then Jimmy is an old fashioned fellow. He will get over it, I am sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure he'll have a gay ol' time when he does. ;D<br /> <br /> But seriously, great journals and game as always. It's great seeing the motley grow in various ways, even though they've come so far since their start. Lori is advancing with an entitlement, Jacob is keeping on top of Calamity's woes, even Calamity is showing maturity and not refusing to wear protection in spite of the pain for the person who made it. Insincere Marguerite's growth is more subtle - she feels more empathetic than I remember her being.<br /> <br /> I have to say, as skilled as Luna has been established before, I didn't expect her to be quite so potent as she was with the Extras. The lady is not to be messed with in any capacity, be it directly or through her motley.<br /> <br /> Carla is an interesting character; it's not just that she's completely unaware of what she endured (though we have had Brightstar before her), but that her durance really resonated in a way that...well, kept her from being terribly aware of what happened. Also the fact that her durance really didn't seem to like harem anime and...yeah, Jacob had it right. Carla had a <i>really</i> strange durance. I love it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T18:42:25-07:00","id":1135013,"title":"","content":"Insincere Marguerite is definitely more empathetic than she was. She is letting people &quot;in&quot; to her heart. With entitlements, the plan is for Lori and Insincere Marguerite to get into their entitlements this time, Calamity to get into her second (Jacob does not have interest in a second at this time). They are all growing, if Calamity is having more than her share of setbacks.<br /> <br /> To some degree, Luna got lucky with a very high roll, though that Clause is pretty potent.<br /> <br /> Glad you are amused with Carla. She does not appear in the next session (though there was a discussion about her which will probably be brought up in Calamity's journal) she will be back soon. Next session has the last &quot;new&quot; character for a bit, and the turmoil from her, plus Desiree and Felicity's intense dislike comes to a head.<br /> <br /> Thanks much for the feedback. It is always nice to hear.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T19:44:27-07:00","id":1135034,"title":"","content":"Wait, I didn't know you could stack Entitlements. Huh. The more you know. Fae are weird<br /> <br /> That must make you look like ultra-rare hybrid breed pets to Gentry and Privateers though","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 08-28-2017, 10:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T02:08:36-07:00","id":1135101,"title":"","content":"I've generally allowed a second Entitlement for people with over 5 Wyrd if there is no conflict with the existing one.<br /> <br /> That may be a House Rule...I don't recall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T13:22:34-07:00","id":1139257,"title":"","content":"It is a house rule. I dug up my house rule list.<br /> <br /> So we begin to settle in, but there is still a new gal to meet. Lets see what the new normal is. No Calamity journal, but she was present.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XC</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Okay, so it\u2019s two days later and I finally have both the time and the inclination to write some more. Brightstar is zonked out on her bed across the room, splayed out and snoring\u2026 she\u2019s <u>adorable</u>. Poor girl must have worn herself out last night, which is something I don\u2019t often see with her. Luckily, I had Spring contracts to keep me going, or I\u2019d never be able to match her energy.<br /> <br /> So where did I leave off? Oh, right\u2026 well, as it turns out, the doorbell <u>wasn\u2019t</u> Jimmy and Peg, it was some FTD guy with a huge bouquet and a big box of chocolates for yours truly. The attached card was from Joan and Andromeda, thanking me for my suggestion the previous evening. I guess the two of them enjoyed their time with Flores, which is nice to know. So long as they\u2019re still willing to dally with <u>me</u> from time to time, I\u2019m truly happy for them.<br /> <br /> The next ring at the door <u>was</u> Jimmy and Peg, and I met them on the doorstep and sort of nervously invited them in. I introduced them to the rest of the motley before we got down to business. They let me know that the first step would be a brief informal interview, and asked me if there was some place a little more private in which we could conduct it\u2026 though they were quick to let me know that it was fine if I wanted other members of my motley present.<br /> <br /> So D consented to join me, and the four of us adjourned to a private room for a little while. In the end, it wasn\u2019t so bad. Jimmy and Peg are actually a lot of fun to talk to, and if I hadn\u2019t been so nervous about, y\u2019know, the judging and all, I probably would have really enjoyed the conversation. The two of them have an easy back-and-forth in which japes and mockery cover an obvious mutual respect and admiration. So while their words seem to cut deep with every sentence, you can tell that there\u2019s very little each wouldn\u2019t do for the other.<br /> <br /> What they wanted from me turned out to be remarkably simple in the end. Peg told me that she was going to email me a brief questionnaire which they would use to assess my strengths and weaknesses\u2026 or at least my own perceptions of my strengths and weaknesses. She asked that I be as honest as possible, but told me that the Pilgrims are aware that a person\u2019s opinions of their own abilities aren\u2019t necessarily the most accurate, so it would serve more as a baseline than a final assessment. Once they had an idea of what they were working with, they\u2019d subject me to a series of tests over the next week to see if I\u2019m a good candidate for the Pilgrims.<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t mean to imply nothin\u2019 \u2018bout you here, love,\u201d Jimmy growled at one point, \u201cbut just so as to be clear, we ain\u2019t supposed to fraternize with the people we test. Got to keep things professional, like.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cUnderstood,\u201d I said immediately. \u201cThat makes a lot of sense.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI only bring it up,\u201d he said with a wry grin, \u201cbecause I\u2019ve noticed Peg\u2019s eyes droppin\u2019 below your neck more\u2019n once since we got here.\u201d<br /> <br /> Peg jabbed him with an elbow. \u201cSomeone\u2019s anglin\u2019 to sleep in the hall at the hotel tonight,\u201d she spat back at him.<br /> <br /> Once that was out of the way they asked me a few basic questions about my abilities so that they\u2019d know what to expect from the questionnaire and could start planning the sort of tests I\u2019d be required to undergo. \u201cWell, I\u2019ve always been good with people,\u201d I said after a moment\u2019s thought, \u201cand Arcadia left me with certain gifts that enhance those abilities.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTell me about it,\u201d Peg muttered.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m also pretty physically fit,\u201d I said. \u201cI don\u2019t know much about fighting or anything, but dancing and gymnastics keep me limber, and I\u2019m stronger than most people think. The place where I really struggle is with my\u2026 well, my mental acuity. I\u2019ve never been very smart,\u201d I admitted.<br /> <br /> D looked like she was going to say something, but kept quiet when I threw her a significant look. \u201cThat\u2019s actually part of why I wanted to join the Pilgrims,\u201d I said after a moment. \u201cI\u2019ve been trying to study medicine for the past year or so on my own time to help with my healing contracts, and I\u2019ve been struggling. I mean, I only just got my GED a couple of months ago, so a lot of the complicated medical stuff is way beyond me. I thought the Pilgrims might be able to help me shore up that side of my life.\u201d<br /> <br /> Peg and Jimmy exchanged a glance. \u201cAll right, love,\u201d Jimmy said gently, \u201cI think we\u2019ve got enough to go on. We can start the plannin\u2019 now.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo\u2026 what sort of tests can I expect?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> Peg shrugged. \u201cWe\u2019ll see. We won\u2019t spring anything on you unexpectedly, though. All tests will be announced in advance; you\u2019ll never have to wonder if you\u2019re being tested in secret. Changelings\u2026 don\u2019t do well with that sort of thing, and we try to avoid inciting paranoia. But just for example\u2026 you say you\u2019re not very good at fighting. Well, you might have to go a round or two with Jimmy here.\u201d She let out a little chuckle when she saw my expression. \u201cDon\u2019t worry, pet, we don\u2019t expect you to <u>win</u>.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay,\u201d I said. \u201cI\u2019ll complete your survey tomorrow afternoon, as soon as I get back from church. Will that be all right?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBrilliant,\u201d Jimmy said, \u201cand if you\u2019ve the time, we can get started on the assessment right now. I can run you through some basic physical tests in the backyard, if you\u2019re amenable?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSure,\u201d I agreed.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhy don\u2019t you change into something you don\u2019t mind getting\u2019 dirty,\u201d he suggested, \u201cand then meet us \u2018round back.\u201d<br /> <br /> So I put on some sweats and nervously walked into the backyard. After assuring Peg and Jimmy that my wings are not as fragile as they appear and would withstand me being thrown to the ground a few times, we began the first set of tests. I think I acquitted myself fairly well\u2026 they ran me through some basic High-School-Gym-Class activities designed to evaluate my strength, agility, and stamina. My performance mostly backed up my earlier statements: while I might never be a professional athlete, I can hold my own when it comes to physical activity.<br /> <br /> Julia, Marguerite, and D gathered to watch me from the back balcony. I suppose I could have gotten annoyed or nervous at that, but, c\u2019mon\u2026 when have I ever objected to having an audience for\u2026 well, <u>anything</u>? It was even oddly comforting, in a way, knowing that they were up there rooting for me.<br /> <br /> Peg and Jimmy seemed satisfied with my performance, and accepted the free tickets to that night\u2019s show with their thanks. They headed out shortly thereafter to get cleaned up and pick up some dinner, and I started to get ready for the show. I only had two big numbers that night, but one of them was an ensemble debut, and I wanted to make sure I gave it my all.<br /> <br /> Early in the show, Marguerite got a call or text or something and had to run. I didn\u2019t get the whole story at that point, but I later learned that Felicity and Desiree had gotten into a fight at the Rose &amp; Thorn\u2026 and apparently it was a real doozy. They were throwing Vainglory around like nobody\u2019s business, and most of the club\u2019s patrons had already fled in abject terror when Marguerite arrived. The two of them were brandishing broken bottles at each other, and each had scored several cuts on the other. Marguerite \u2013 summoning all of her willpower to approach them \u2013 managed to talk them down, and got them both to go to Glamour Springs for healing. I\u2019m glad they\u2019re both okay, and I truly hope that they find a way to work through their differences soon.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, I had a show to do, dammit! My first number was just a re-hash of one of my usual torch songs, but it got a good response from the audience, and warmed them up for the stuff to follow. My second number of the evening was our closer, the all-cast rendition of the classic Beach Boys song \u201cCalifornia Girls.\u201d My initial pitch for the number was to have one of the other performers sing it, and we\u2019d bring out various dancers to fill the roles of the girls mentioned in the song. Yours Truly would have been \u201cthe Midwest Farmer\u2019s Daughter,\u201d naturally, as I hail from Iowa. But most of the cast thought it would go off better if I was the singer, so that role ended up going to Tori, who I believe grew up in Fresno. Go figure.<br /> <br /> In any case, Wilson and Love\u2019s magic harmonies captured the audience like nothing else at the show had (and I suppose the home-state advantage didn\u2019t hurt either), and the whole ensemble was bowed off the stage to thunderous applause. As I was thanking the audience and informing them that drink service would continue for another half an hour (I miss Ace), I caught a glimpse of something up in the balcony that piqued my interest\u2026 a flash of light purple, almost the exact same shade as the highlights in D\u2019s hair.<br /> <br /> I made my way up there and found a young changeling woman I\u2019d never seen before sitting there. As I said before, her hair (all of it) was almost exactly the same purple shade as D\u2019s. Her eyes were a startling Liz Taylor violet, and her lips gleamed a dark plum color. I glanced down at her hands to see if her nails continued the color scheme, but it was hard to see them in the dim light through the black lace gloves she wore. She smiled as I approached.<br /> <br /> \u201cHi,\u201d I said brightly, extending a hand. \u201cI\u2019m Lorelei Grace, but most people just call me Lori. Welcome to the Dream House.\u201d<br /> <br /> She took my hand and shook it with a grin. \u201cThank you. My name\u2019s Veronica. I\u2019m from Venice Beach, but I don\u2019t make it to the northern end of the Freehold very often. A friend of mine recommended this place, and I\u2019ve got to say that she undersold it. You\u2019re very talented.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you!\u201d I said, sitting in the offered chair. \u201cChangelings are always welcome here. I hope you\u2019ll come again.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDefinitely,\u201d she said, \u201cthis place is great, just like Rowan said.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, you\u2019re a friend of Rowan\u2019s?\u201d I asked. \u201cShe\u2019s a sweetheart. The two of us\u2026 well, we were kind of involved for a little while.\u201d<br /> <br /> She quirked an eyebrow at that, and I felt the need to elaborate. \u201cShe\u2026 she wanted more out of the relationship than I was able to provide,\u201d I fumbled after a moment.<br /> <br /> She looked me up and down. \u201cShe wanted <u>more</u>?\u201d she asked, incredulous.<br /> <br /> I laughed at that. \u201cIt\u2019s not like that. You see, I\u2019m poly, and Rowan really needs \u2013 really <u>deserves</u> someone who can devote everything to her.\u201d<br /> <br /> She chuckled. \u201cI did not expect that. I guess I\u2019m still not used to the California lifestyle.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh? Where are you from?\u201d I asked, curious as always.<br /> <br /> \u201cDes Moines\u2026 in Iowa,\u201d she replied.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo shit!\u201d I exclaimed in surprise. \u201cI\u2019m from Iowa, too! Not one of the big cities\u2026 just a little town you\u2019ve probably never heard of called Defiance.\u201d<br /> <br /> She scrunched up her forehead in thought. \u201cI don\u2019t know\u2026 maybe on a weather report or on the news or something.\u201d<br /> <br /> I had to laugh. \u201cNot on the news\u2026 nothing interesting ever happened in Defiance.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, I\u2019m a metropolitan big city girl, all right,\u201d she smirked. \u201cStill\u2026 small world, huh?\u201d<br /> <br /> We ended up talking for a good twenty or thirty minutes after that. It turns out that we have a lot in common, even aside from the midwestern thing. It wasn\u2019t even like there was a lot of flirting; we just got along really well. She\u2019s fun to talk to.<br /> <br /> I realized at some point that I was neglecting our other guests, so I reluctantly said my goodbyes and started circulating among the thinning crowd. D joined me after a moment with a smirk and a wink. \u201cThinking of adding another blonde to your collection?\u201d she asked in an insufferably knowing way.<br /> <br /> I blinked. \u201cWhat are you talking about?\u201d I asked, genuinely surprised.<br /> <br /> That brought her up short. \u201cThe new girl. You were chatting her up, right?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe were just talking, that\u2019s all\u2026 but she\u2019s not a blonde, so I don\u2019t see how that\u2019s relevant.\u201d<br /> <br /> D glanced back. \u201cAre you feeling all right, babe?\u201d she asked. \u201cThat\u2019s one of the blondest blondes I\u2019ve ever seen. Her hair is almost\u2026 metallic, like gold.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s purple, like yours,\u201d I shot back. \u201cThat\u2019s why I first noticed her.\u201d<br /> <br /> So it turns out that everyone sees Veronica\u2019s hair, eyes, and lips as different colors. When she had returned from the Rose &amp; Thorn, Marguerite also saw her as a blonde. Julia saw dark hair, spangled with flecks of starlight. Oleander saw it as green, with dappled highlights like sunlight on leaves. It didn\u2019t take us long to realize that everyone was seeing the colors that they found most attractive.<br /> <br /> So D and I had a long, deep, and serious discussion in which I teased her relentlessly about which one of us <u>really</u> has a thing for blondes. I confess that a part of me was just glad that my own hair color so closely resembles my honey\u2019s ideal.<br /> <br /> I had made plans to spend the evening with Oleander, so with one last jibe I left D in Gloria\u2019s capable (blonde) hands. Oleander and I stayed at the Dream House while the two of them went back to Gloria\u2019s apartment.<br /> <br /> As always, Oleander and I had a great time during the night. Not much to tell about church the next morning, honestly. Dad and I have sort of privately resolved not to interact too much where the congregation can see us, since we might give something away as my wedding approaches and our emotions run high. So I sat and sang and listened and basically basked in the warm feelings that always seem to surround me in that place, and afterward I came home for Sex Breakfast.<br /> <br /> Oleander cleared out pretty early on, and for once I was grateful for that\u2026 mostly because it was immediately clear to me that something was really bothering D. I cornered her away from the others and asked her what was wrong.<br /> <br /> \u201cNothing\u2026 well, nothing\u2019s <u>wrong</u>, exactly,\u201d she prevaricated.<br /> <br /> \u201cD,\u201d I said, forcing her to look at me.<br /> <br /> She sighed. \u201cGloria told me that she\u2019s in love with me last night,\u201d she blurted out at last.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd\u2026 that\u2019s a bad thing?\u201d I asked, forcing down the brief surge of jealousy I always feel whenever D gets close to anyone else.<br /> <br /> She shrugged. \u201cI\u2019m so happy with you, Jules,\u201d she said simply, \u201cand I love what we have with Julia and Mags. I just\u2026 I don\u2019t know if I can handle any more relationships outside of that. I don\u2019t want to fuck anything up.\u201d<br /> <br /> I pulled her into a kiss. \u201cMaria, you know that I\u2019ll be with you forever, right? I mean, I\u2019m deadly serious about that. No matter what happens to us, no matter what you do, or I do, or anyone else does\u2026 I\u2019ll never leave you. I need you like I need air.\u201d<br /> <br /> She smiled and pulled me into a hug. \u201cI know,\u201d she said. \u201cI\u2019m not really worried about us. But I don\u2019t know if I can do what you do, babe. I don\u2019t know if I can be what she wants and still be with the three of you. And I don\u2019t want to hurt her either.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay,\u201d I said, kissing her forehead. \u201cWell, I can\u2019t really make this decision for you, but I\u2019ll help you any way that I can. If you decide you want to do this, I\u2019m behind you one hundred percent, okay? I like Gloria, and I promise I won\u2019t make things difficult\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> D snorted. \u201cI know you\u2019re not a hypocrite, Lori,\u201d she assured me.<br /> <br /> We rejoined the others, who were discussing the fight between Desiree and Felicity. I know those two have never gotten along, but this confrontation really seems out of character for both of them, the more I think about it. I mean, when we had that trouble last Highsummer, the two of them sniped at each other, but each also said that they didn\u2019t really want to <u>harm</u> the other. The more I thought about it, the more it reminded me of the incident between Becky and Dark Kimberly last year, where Flores ended up getting hurt. At the time, we\u2019d discussed things like Summer Court contracts and Bedlam as possible causes of the outburst\u2026 I wonder if something similar could be at work here?<br /> <br /> After we\u2019d chewed that topic to death, the chief topic of conversation became\u2026 Veronica. Apparently my motley has decided that she might be a threat, and they\u2019re going to treat her as such. I understand caution, really I do\u2026 but this just smacks of paranoia to me. I mean, she\u2019s not even a new arrival to the Freehold\u2026 she\u2019s just someone we hadn\u2019t met before, for crying out loud! And Marguerite and Calamity are talking about following her home and checking up on her background like she\u2019s some sort of criminal!<br /> <br /> Thank God this sort of behavior wasn\u2019t prevalent when I first came to the Freehold. I mean \u201cwelcome to the Lady by the Sea, please join us in Room 101\u201d isn\u2019t exactly the friendliest way to greet newcomers. I know that the Director and the rest of the Gentry pose a real threat to our population, and I promise that I\u2019m taking it seriously\u2026 but shouldn\u2019t someone have actually <u>done</u> something wrong before we start treating them like a criminal?<br /> <br /> Whatever. I decided to leave the conversation before I said anything I\u2019d regret. Calamity actually seems motivated to do something for once, and even if I don\u2019t agree with what she\u2019s doing, I don\u2019t want to snuff out that burst of animation before it can reignite her passion for life. So I removed myself from the debate and went upstairs to work on the survey for the Pilgrims. It was fairly extensive, and it took more than an hour to complete. I tried to be accurate about my abilities while retaining my modesty, and brutally honest about my faults. I don\u2019t want to set unrealistic expectations for Peg and Jimmy.<br /> <br /> I mostly spent the afternoon being available as a comforting presence for D while she was working through the thing with Gloria. The show rolled around as per usual, except that I made sure I was out front as the guests were arriving this time instead of hiding away in the dressing rooms. When Gloria walked through the front door \u2013 looking uncharacteristically glum \u2013 I walked up to her and threw my arms around her in a big hug.<br /> <br /> \u201cHey, Lori,\u201d she said with some dejection.<br /> <br /> \u201cHi, sweetie,\u201d I said with as much warmth as I could muster. \u201cLook, I know what you\u2019re going through right now, and for what it\u2019s worth I want you to know that I\u2019m in your corner, okay? The final decision has to be D\u2019s... but I promise I\u2019m not going to make trouble. I\u2019m rooting for you.\u201d<br /> <br /> She gave me kind of a watery smile and squeezed my hand. \u201cThanks, Lori. It means a lot,\u201d she said after a moment. Then she ambled off to sit at the girlfriend table, still looking just this side of miserable. Poor girl.<br /> <br /> Veronica was there again as promised, and asked me with no small amount of enthusiasm if I might be available after the show to hang out. I told her that I\u2019d check my social calendar, but promised that if it wasn\u2019t possible we could make other plans for later in the week. She took a seat at the same table she\u2019d frequented the previous evening, and I had to head backstage to wrangle our performers.<br /> <br /> It was a pretty good show for a Sunday night. I debuted one new number\u2026 not an incredibly sexy selection for a burlesque house, but I think it went over pretty well regardless. I sang Carole King\u2019s \u201cYou\u2019ve Got a Friend,\u201d thinking of both Gloria and Veronica as I performed. I wanted them both to know that I\u2019m in their corner, and that I\u2019ll lend them whatever support they might need from me. Of course, Veronica probably doesn\u2019t even know she\u2019s under suspicion yet, so the subtext was almost certainly lost on her.<br /> <br /> After my solos I worked the crowd\u2026 and remembered that I <u>did</u> in fact have standing plans for the evening. Brightstar was there, and I\u2019d told her a few days previous that we could spend the evening together. I stopped by her table and spoke with her and Neon for a bit, and I confirmed our plans, but begged time to walk the crowd a bit more before we left. Brightstar agreed readily enough.<br /> <br /> D and Gloria caught up with me as I made the rounds, and both seemed a little happier. \u201cWe\u2019re not gonna label it for now,\u201d D explained, her arm around Gloria\u2019s waist. \u201cWe\u2019re not gonna call it a \u2018relationship,\u2019 but we agree that we\u2019re more than just friends with benefits. We\u2019ll see where it goes from there.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m glad,\u201d I said, giving my fianc\u00e9e a passionate kiss and Gloria a chaste peck on the cheek. \u201cYou two spending the evening together, then?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIf that\u2019s okay with you,\u201d Gloria said quickly. \u201cYou\u2019ve been really good about this whole thing, Lori, and I don\u2019t want to monopolize de la Rocha\u2019s time\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s okay,\u201d I said, \u201cI promised Brightstar we could spend the evening together anyway. You two have fun. Take our bedroom. And\u2026 congratulations.\u201d<br /> <br /> D leaned in for another smooch. \u201cThanks, babe,\u201d she said softly. \u201cI\u2019ll see you in the morning, okay?\u201d And she gave me a look that made it a promise.<br /> <br /> I made my way up to Veronica\u2019s table after that. \u201cSo,\u201d she asked with a twinkle, \u201cwhich of them is your girlfriend?\u201d<br /> <br /> I chuckled and pointed, rapid-fire, at various people around the room. \u201cGirlfriend, girlfriend, girlfriend, fianc\u00e9e,\u201d I explained. I felt a little like a kindergarten student playing Duck-Duck-Goose.<br /> <br /> She laughed softly. \u201cYou really have gone native, haven\u2019t you?\u201d<br /> <br /> I shrugged. \u201cIn part, I guess. My Durance also\u2026 opened me up to new experiences, in a way.\u201d<br /> <br /> We chatted for a bit, and eventually she asked me again if I had time to hang out with her that evening. With regret, I informed her that I wasn\u2019t available, but asked her to come back on Tuesday evening, and promised to keep my calendar clear for her then.<br /> <br /> Her face fell. \u201cOkay,\u201d she said, a little dejectedly.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sorry, Veronica,\u201d I said. \u201cI\u2019m having a great time talking with you, and I\u2019d really like to continue, but I\u2019d forgotten that I already made plans with Brightstar. It wouldn\u2019t be fair to ask her for a raincheck now\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, it\u2019s cool, I get it,\u201d she said with a smile that looked a little forced. \u201cI\u2019ll see you Tuesday, then.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLooking forward to it,\u201d I promised her.<br /> <br /> So it was with a little regret that I rejoined my most energetic girlfriend at her table. She, Neon, and I headed back to their place after things had died down a bit, and she helped me forget my troubles for a while. I considered trying to get Neon to join us for a while\u2026 but she and Brightstar always seem kind of uncomfortable when they\u2019re around each other in sexual situations, so I discarded the notion pretty quickly.<br /> <br /> As I said at the beginning of this entry, Brightstar is currently nigh-comatose on her bed, so I thought I\u2019d write this entry to organize my thoughts. With any luck, the others will have vetted Veronica by the time I make my way back to the Dream House, and I\u2019ll be able to enjoy movie night without all this pesky angst weighing me down. Though I suppose I should wrap this up and do something useful with myself in the meantime. The tests are about to begin, and I don\u2019t want to disappoint the Pilgrims!<br /> <b><br /> Lorelei Grace</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> So, the Pilgrims of the Endless Road showed up. Turned out they were a pair of Brits named Peg Powler and Jimmy Squarefoot. They seemed nice. They talked with Lori for a couple of minutes and explained a bit of what they were going to do today and said that if she wanted anyone with her that was fine. Lori then introduced the Pilgrims to the rest of the motley, but only asked De La Rocha if she would go with her for the meeting. De La Rocha of course said \u201cyes,\u201d and the rest of us did our own thing. <br /> <br /> For our part Calamity and I went to go talk to the Summer Court about what happened in the Hedge and what\u2019s going on with the Extras. We arrived just as Hailey was talking with Billy, Louie and Ji Wen Ja. When we walked in Hailey was holding a rifle of some kind in her hand, then suddenly it disappeared. I\u2019m assuming that she made it invisible since we were there and she didn\u2019t want us to see it. I\u2019ll have to follow up on that. Anyway, after Hailey left we told the rest what was going on with the Extras in the Hedge. About the sheer numbers and their unusual activity. We also mentioned that Carla was able to walk through a group of the Extras without being harassed by them. They told us not to spread that last detail around. They didn\u2019t want people jumping to conclusions about Carla\u2019s loyalties and doing something that can\u2019t be taken back. They did tell us to inform Boss Lowjack about the Extras and Carla, but no one else unless they needed to know. We agreed that was a prudent measure to take. When we got back to the house I made sure to call Lowjack and let him know what we\u2019d seen and experienced.<br /> <br /> As it turns out Lori was getting tested this afternoon. Peg and Jimmy wanted to see how physically fit she is and how good she is at different athletic tasks. From all accounts, she fared well. I believe that she admitted to them that she was not a good fighter. They said that was fine. Apparently, they also gave her some \u201chomework\u201d to do. I think she had to fill something out with her own estimations on how well she would do at different kinds of tasks. It\u2019s hard to be honest about your own capabilities, especially with strangers. It\u2019s easier to admit faults to your friends, but if she wants to make it into the Entitlement then she\u2019ll need to be honest.<br /> <br /> The show went well tonight. Peg and Jimmy came by. I think Lori comped them a couple of tickets so they could see the show for free. There was also a new changeling in the crowd. She showed up pretty early, before most other people. She had interestingly colored hair. It was kind of earth toned with green and hints of blue. It reminded me of the color of Luna\u2019s wings. She also has the mantle of a Summer Courtier. I made a note to ask about her later. Also, pretty early in the evening Stasia and Elena came by to say \u201cHi.\u201d They were bickering good naturedly about a party that they\u2019d gone to where Stasia had to keep an eye on my sister because she drank too much. Elena, in her own defense, said that it was not her intention to get drunk. The drinks she got had more of a kick than she was expecting. I knew I wasn\u2019t going to convince Elena not to drink. Hell, we had alcohol on special occasions when we lived in Russia as kids. So, I took it upon myself to let her know which drinks she should avoid in the future. The list wasn\u2019t too long so I think she\u2019ll remember them all. It was good to see Stasia and Elena getting along so well. I had been worried that Stasia might drop Elena after they\u2019d slept together since she doesn\u2019t do relationships. Apparently though she turned this one night stands into a friendship. I can live with that. I had just been worried before that my sister might get hurt, but I don\u2019t think that\u2019s something I\u2019m going to have to worry about.<br /> <br /> There was a bit of excitement tonight. At one point I noticed Julia running upstairs to show Insincere Marguerite a text on her phone and Marguerite got upset and ran out toward the front of the house. I got worried that something serious was going on so I told Jack, the assistant bartender, to watch the bar and took off after her. I met up with her at the front of the house and asked what was wrong. She explained hurriedly that Desiree and Felicity were at the Rose and Thorn fighting. This wasn\u2019t just some friendly disagreement kind of fight either. This was an all-out, broken bottle kind of fight. I asked Insincere Marguerite if she needed any help. She said no and jumped through a nearby mirror. I will admit that I was tempted to follow her in my jeep, but figured that everything would be over by the time I drove to the other club. I know it takes a good bit of extra effort on Marguerite\u2019s part to take other people through mirrors with her, which is why I didn\u2019t ask.<br /> <br /> After I got back I noticed that Calamity went over to talk to the new girl. She seemed to be gesturing to different people around the club and I realized that she was pointing out all the members of our motley. I wondered why she was doing that. It\u2019s all well and good to introduce your motley to new people, but I didn\u2019t know if this woman had even been vetted yet. I\u2019m not sure if Calamity knows something that I don\u2019t about the new girl. I\u2019ll have to ask later. Then, after a short bit Lori also made her way over to the new girl\u2019s table, and they talked and flirted for a while. I guess they found something in common. They both certainly seemed to be enjoying themselves.<br /> <br /> Calamity left shortly after the show was over to bring Desiree back to the Dream House. She said that she was going to do some Dream Healing on Desiree to see if she\u2019d been Dream Poisoned or anything. We were trying to figure out what might have caused the fight between Felicity and Desiree. Sure, those two don\u2019t like each other, but it\u2019s never come to blows in the past. It sounds like Desiree started the fight by slapping Felicity. Felicity then jumped across the table and attacked Desiree. It was her that escalated the fight by breaking a glass bottle and trying to cut Desiree\u2019s face. It sounds like it got bloody and intense. Apparently, they were both using the \u201cBeautiful yet Terrifying\u201d Spring Court power and most everyone fled the club. Some people just hid underneath tables. It was a mess. Insincere Marguerite managed to get between the two women and convince them to stand down. Not sure what would have happened if she hadn\u2019t arrived when she did.<br /> <br /> So, Calamity came back with Desiree and they went upstairs to do some Dream Healing. There were concerns that some contract or other kind of power had been used against the two ladies to get them to fight like that. Calamity checked Desiree tonight. I wonder if anyone is going to take a peek into Felicity\u2019s head and see if anyone had been messing with her. It was brought up that this fight seemed an awful lot like the fight between Becky and Dark Kimberly a while ago that led to Flores getting hurt. We had thought that something called Bedlam may have been used against those two, and it seemed like it may have been used against Desiree and Felicity tonight. Well, that\u2019s one theory anyway. There are other things that can incite people to fight that may have been put into play. Dream Poisoning being one of them. I guess we\u2019ll find out in the morning what Calamity finds out.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> So, at breakfast things got interesting. Conversation of course turned to the new girl at the club last night. It was inevitable that she was going to come up. We\u2019ve had so many new arrivals lately, and she could have been the latest on an ever-growing list. It turns out that she says she\u2019s from Venice Beach, so she\u2019s not a new arrival after all. Then conversation turned to what color we saw her hair as. I thought it was a strange question to ask, until everyone that saw her said a different color. It seems that the not so new girl is a Romancer, Polychromatic and appears to everyone in the way that they most desire. So, Lori saw her with purple hair and violet eyes. De La Rocha saw her with blonde hair and light eyes. Insincere Marguerite also saw her as a blonde. Lori kept teasing them about that throughout breakfast, and I don\u2019t think she\u2019s gonna let go of that any time soon since they\u2019re always teasing her for having a \u201cthing\u201d about blondes. To be fair most of the teasing was with De La Rocha, but Marguerite got some too. I guess turnabout is fair play. <br /> <br /> So, Calamity, being cautious, texted Dahlia about Veronica and what was known about her so far. She said that she was from Venice Beach, but Dahlia did not know about any Veronicas from that area that were in the Summer Court. Dahlia suggested that if one of our motley was going to sleep with Veronica that they should go back to her place so we can get an address for her. An address would make checking her out easier and Dahlia said as much. Calamity then shared her suspicions with us. Calamity specifically said that if Lori should sleep with the newbie then she should take down Veronica\u2019s address. Lori was a bit indignant about that, saying that she wasn\u2019t necessarily going to sleep with Veronica. The idea was then brought up that if no one in the motley was going to sleep with Veronica then someone should follow her home the next time she shows up so we can get her address. Lori argued against this course of action, seeing it as unnecessary and paranoid. Calamity and most of the rest of us argued that we were just being cautious. We have had a lot of newcomers that arrived with programming from the Director in their heads. Veronica could be a loyalist and not know it. Or she might be a willing one. We don\u2019t know anything about her except that she may not live where she says she does. That in and of itself sets of warning bells in my head. Why lie about where you live unless you have something to hide?<br /> <br /> I certainly lied enough times when I worked for the Lady. I would sometimes pretend to be a new arrival, or I would claim to be from some other town. Usually if I claimed another town it was far enough away so it wasn\u2019t easily checked. If people had been more cautious about me when I arrived in their freeholds then I might have been caught a lot sooner than I had been. If the people of Claire Falls had done a background check on me when I first arrived, then things might have gone down differently there. If I knew that I was being investigated I would have backed off and tried a different tactic. I probably wouldn\u2019t have been captured, and little Felicity might not have died when Rook came looking for me. Things might have been different if they\u2019d just thought to ask the right questions. I remember when I first arrived in Claire Falls. I said that I was a new arrival, but gave the name of a different Gentry as my Keeper. It was one of the Lady\u2019s allies, still winter aspected, but decidedly not her. If \u0336D\u0336e\u0336l\u0336i\u0336g\u0336h\u0336t\u0336 Diane had known that I was from the Lady\u2019s realm then she might have realized who I was. I had to be careful not to trigger her memory before I was able to retrieve her. It almost worked too. If Travers hadn\u2019t suddenly got suspicious of me on that last day then I might have made it back to the Lady with Diane. But he had a bad feeling about me and decided to follow Diane and I when we left the house. He can be quiet when he wants to and I didn\u2019t hear him coming up behind me until it was too late. He jumped me from behind and proceeded to beat the ever-living shit out of me. Diane, who had begun to suspect that I wasn\u2019t really taking her for a walk, backed away but tried to convince Travers to stop. He didn\u2019t. It took Liam and a couple others to pull the ogre off of me, and by that point I was barely conscious. I remember Liam kneeling down beside me and putting his hand on my shoulder. I felt warm for a moment before I passed out. I think that I had been dying and he kept me from the brink. At least it certainly felt like the last time that I was at death\u2019s door. I don\u2019t know if I ever really thanked him for saving my life. I would like to be able to do that, and show him that I have turned over a new leaf like he\u2019d hoped. But showing up in Claire Falls might be problematic for me. I\u2019m pretty sure that Travers would kill me on sight regardless of evidence that I\u2019ve changed. And I don\u2019t know if sending a letter would be wise either. It would be postmarked here and that would give them a way of finding me. At least it would give Travers a way to find me if he so desired. I don\u2019t think Liam would try and find me with the intention of doing me harm. He was always the reasonable one. He was keen on trying to sway me over to his side, and renounce the Lady. Too bad it didn\u2019t work then.<br /> <br /> Anyway, after our conversation I called Lowjack to talk to him about the issue with the Extras in the Hedge. I told him how they were acting and what happened with them. I suggested that they send someone into the Hedge to see if they reacted to someone that was \u201cLight shy\u201d or if they reacted at all if someone just walked through their ranks without intending harm. Lowjack seemed to think that this was a good idea, but suggested that it not be me because I had coaxed a response out of them the last time that I went to the Hedge. I also told him about Veronica and our ideas concerning the possibly new Changeling. He said that he had Dahlia already on it. I was heartened to know that my Monarch was already on top of the issue. That meant that we wouldn\u2019t have to investigate ourselves. I\u2019m sure that Calamity was with me when the idea came up to investigate Veronica, but Lori was decidedly not. She seemed to think that we should take Veronica at face value and believe that what she said was true. I am generally not one to believe that what is said is necessarily true until it is proven to be so.<br /> <br /> Later in the afternoon, after the show started, things got interesting again. Well, to me they did. Hailey was at the bar and I decided to take a chance and ask her about the interesting rifle that she had with her yesterday. She acknowledged the gun and said that it was a disintegration rifle. I said that sounded interesting and asked her to let me know as soon as it was available to the public. I don\u2019t expect it to be available to someone like me for a while, but am still interested in it. Granted, I am more of a knife kind of guy, but am willing to entertain the odd gun here and there. <br /> <br /> I\u2019m not sure what is going on with the freehold right now. We seem to have more and more escapees from Arcadia flooding in, and not all of them appear to be from the Director. My gut tells me to be wary of anyone that is new just because of past history with the Director and his programed people. I don\u2019t know what to make of Carla yet though. She doesn\u2019t even seem to think that her experiences in Arcadia and the Hedge were all that strange. She just wanted to get back to Earth like it was a normal thing to want to do. She didn\u2019t understand when we told her that she\u2019d been taken to a place called Arcadia and that she had managed to escape that place altogether. It was also interesting that Monica showed up to the show tonight without our intrepid cat girl. I wonder what is going on with her that she could not join the Blackbird Bishop for the night. I\u2019ll have to make sure to ask about that soon. I am curious to see what became of Carla and her Planet Neko. <br /> <br /> <b><br /> Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers<br /> </b><br /> I have been doing quite well, as have my beloved trio of girls, but a lot is going on around us.<br /> <br /> I met the Pilgrims Juliette was keen to work with, Peg Powler and Jimmy Squarefoot. They seem nice as Ogres go. Not Monica nice, but nice. They met the Motley, then had an interview with Juliette and Maria. After that they went out back to test Juliette on her basic physical capabilities. Julia and I watched from the balcony. Nothing too strenuous, and Juliette did okay.<br /> <br /> The show was where things got interesting. I got a message while working it that Felicity and Desiree were fighting at the Rose and Thorn. I messaged Julia to come up and take over, and rushed out to get to a mirror\u2026I happened to not have one in the catwalks. Jacob followed, and slowed me a little, but I explained some without stopping for him and found one to drive through into Flores\u2019 office. From there I rushed out to confront the girls.<br /> <br /> I was not prepared for how bloody it was. Not because they were badly hurt, but because they had glass bottles and were swinging at faces. They were wrapped in Mantles of Beauty and Terror, and it was everything I could do to not flee in terror. They looked like Archangels at war, and the room had cleared, short a few cowering people. I could not lay a hand on either, but when Desiree was thrown, and moved to physically interpose. They both love I, and did not want to hurt me. That stopped the fighting, though they were both bleeding everywhere, their clothes were red with blood pouring from their faces. Flores healed them, and Becky and Dominaka collected them to bring to Princess Jolie.<br /> <br /> According to Flores, Felicity approached Desiree, who was cuddling with Angelica in a booth. They argued, and Desiree struck Felicity with powerful open handed slap which made her hit her head on the booth, and leapt across to attack her. The powers started up at that point. Both blazed with Vainglory so Flores was not sure who started with the weapons but she thought it was Felicity. Angelica for her part fled in terror, hiding under a jeep outside.<br /> <br /> Once I was sure Flores was okay, I jumped back to my room and dashed through the shower to get all the blood off me. Then returned for the end of the show. I think Felicity and Desiree were not actually hurt too much, but it was an ugly scene.<br /> <br /> After the show but before sleep I explained the whole scenario to the Motley. Calamity went to Glamour Springs. We also discussed yet another newcomer, Veronica, who is a Romancer and Polychromatic Fairest, and from Juliette\u2019s home R\u00e9gion. Specifically Juliette was asking about her hair and lips. She saw them as vibrant purple. I had to admit seeing her as blonde haired and blue eyed. I did see a shock of black there, though. Julia saw her hair as black and sparkled, with gothic black lips and stars in her eyes. Oleander saw green, with dappling like shadows from trees. Maria, to her chagrin, admitted seeing hair of spun gold, which Juliette clung to with glee. Maria likes to tease Juliette about liking blonds, despite all her own sexual partners having blonde hair, including Gloria. Juliette indulged in gleeful revenge.<br /> <br /> Eventually she took Oleander upstairs, and Maria went to see Gloria. After last night, Julia and I were happy to just rest in each other\u2019s arms. We both needed a recharge after the unbridled carnality of the night before.<br /> <br /> The conversations continued at Sex Breakfast. There were comparisons between Felicity and Desiree\u2019s fight and the argument between Becky and Dark Kimberly that lead to Flores being injured when she interposed herself, something I fortunately did not think of to make me hesitate when I moved between Felicity and Desiree. Calamity was certain of a connection. On a brighter note, we quizzed Jacob and Calamity on Veronica\u2019s hair, lips, and eyes.<br /> <br /> Given the stress and concerns of it all, I texted both Felicity and Desiree, confirming they are okay. Then Julia and I went upstairs, for her to paint and me to read, mess with my phone, and inspire her. Then we watched some Netflix and got ready for the show.<br /> <br /> The show went smoothly, no emergencies this time. Juliette was wonderful as always. Maria was talking intensely\u2026not flirting, but talking with Gloria all night, and it turned out near the end while she is not going to have anything like what she has with Julia, Juliette or myself, she is not going to pretend her relationship with Gloria is just friends, or just friends \u201cwith benefits\u201d to use the American term. They are not in a committed relationship, as we four are, but they are not just friends who sleep together. The fact that with a handful of exceptions Gloria is Straight (and sees herself as such) is one reason to worry less about her flipping out about the upcoming nuptials, I suppose. One issue with Felicity or Desiree were both wanted more from me, and I dislike having that hang over our relationship. If Gloria is being honest with what she wants, I see no issue or clouds on she or Maria\u2019s horizon.<br /> <br /> I also went to talk to Veronica. The conversation went pleasantly. She had talked to Juliette earlier in the night, and Juliette had her perhaps a bit in a sensual state of mind, as she does. I flirted, she gingerly flirted back. She is very beautiful, and seemed shy when I started flirting. We spoke of Paris, that she has never visited, and she complimented my accent several times. We rather got on, I have to say. She did have lovely black lace gloves that Julia coveted. I will have to bear that in mind. For her, I don\u2019t care for covering up. I mean she wore a long gown to a hot spring.<br /> <br /> As the night wound up, Julia told me White Maria wanted to come up with us. I didn\u2019t expect it after Beltane but she wanted something a little more\u2026caring and a little less daring. I was worried we pushed her too far. On some level she appreciated what happened, but was in no hurry to repeat it. We have a fun little evening with some necking and sleeping but no wild sex.<br /> <br /> But she is up and dressing to meet Calamity for meditation, and I am getting back in bed. Julia would never forgive me if she woke and we were both gone. When I am up for real I will check with Felicity and Desiree again. In the meantime, I will snooze as White Maria is heading out the door. I wonder if I will have a strange temple dream again\u2026<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XC</i><br /> <br /> As Insincere Marguerite reported, Desiree and Felicity were using Mantle of Beauty and Terror while fighting, and Elegant Protection (Separation) as well. So a lot of ferocity but not a lot of damage. IM\u2019s account of the time immediately preceding her vanishing to the Rose &amp; Thorn was a bit more accurate than Jacob\u2019s.<br /> <br /> While there was no Calamity journal, it should be noted she had a tense conversation with Angelica, spoke to Flores, and walked back to see Jolie and Felicity in a lightly compromising situation. She went back and entered Desiree\u2019s dreams, finding no poison but she was in significant emotional turmoil.<br /> <br /> Lori had to make a few rolls for her tests\u2026she did fine, physical for the outside (each attribute plus Athletics) and mental (Intelligence and Wits) for the inventory.<br /> <br /> I think that covers it. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T21:21:31-07:00","id":1141307,"title":"","content":"Finally caught up... With MDH anyway. Dang it Life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T01:13:16-07:00","id":1141342,"title":"","content":"Nice to have you back on board.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T10:48:28-07:00","id":1141463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroness Nerak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play?p=1141342#post1141342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice to have you back on board.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tee hee <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, rather like the Harem bit. I wasn't expecting that. Curious to see where Carla and that whole thing goes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T14:01:26-07:00","id":1143576,"title":"","content":"Harem bit?<br /> <br /> The mysterious stranger returns to the Dream House. Lorelei, Calamity, and Insincere Marguerite work on joining their Entitlements. And Calamity goes drag racing.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XCI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know\u2026 I can\u2019t decide\u2026 it\u2019s hard for me to figure out how to talk about what\u2019s happening to me in coherent thoughts. I think I\u2019ve reached another personal plateau\u2026 and this one has taken me to dizzying heights. I\u2019ve been feeling the changes gradually over the past few days \u2013 and certain things lead me to believe that I\u2019m not alone among the motley in that respect \u2013 so I guess I\u2019d better give an account from the beginning.<br /> <br /> Okay, where did I leave off last time? Right\u2026 I\u2019d spent the night with Brightstar at her place so that D and Gloria could use our bedroom, since they didn\u2019t want to disturb Desiree. Well, Brightstar drove me home late the next morning, and we arrived back at the Dream House just in time for Sex Breakfast. Calamity was there, and was a little more animated than has been common for her lately. Apparently Stasia had promised to take her out that afternoon so that they could have \u201cfun that doesn\u2019t involve murder,\u201d and she was looking forward to it.<br /> <br /> D and Gloria were also there, and they both seemed remarkably happy and mellow. When I asked them about it, D mumbled something about how they had shared a tender evening together and \u201ctalked more\u201d than they usually do during their rendezvous. I guess she\u2019s serious about taking things to the next level with Gloria, and most of me still sees this as a good thing. Dammit, Lori, if anyone should understand this, it\u2019s you: D loving Gloria doesn\u2019t mean she loves you any less. Does your love for Oleander in any way lessen what you feel for D? Then shut up and roll with it.<br /> <br /> Calamity\u2019s murder talk made Brightstar nervous, so she endeavored to change the subject by asking me who I planned to set Neon up with. I told her that I thought Neon and Rowan would be good for each other, and though she expressed a little concern over the Day Court/Night Court thing, she agreed that Rowan definitely seems to be Neon\u2019s type. We\u2019re sort of tentatively planning to have the two of them meet \u201cby chance\u201d at the Dream House one night, and see where things go from there. Apparently Calamity was just as uncomfortable with the relationship talk as Brightstar had been with the murder talk, so she retreated into the office as we discussed the possibilities.<br /> <br /> Peg called me up as thing were winding down and let me know that the Pilgrims had decided upon my next test. They wanted to test my mental acuity, and had a series of computerized challenges for me to attempt. She told me that they could bring the tests to me, or I could meet them at the Lighthouse and take the tests there. As it was a nice day (and I really didn\u2019t want to have any members of the motley looking over my shoulder as I made a fool of myself), I opted for the latter option.<br /> <br /> As I was pulling the \u2018vette out of the garage I beheld an unusual spectacle\u2026 namely a glittering golden Mustang pulling into the parking lot. Stasia waved at me from behind the wheel, and I pulled up next to her. \u201cNice ride,\u201d I commented with an arched eyebrow.<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks. It\u2019s not mine,\u201d she explained. Since it seemed unlikely that the car was stolen \u2013 I mean, it\u2019s not exactly unobtrusive \u2013 I let that pass without further elaboration.<br /> <br /> \u201cStabitha\u2019s in the office,\u201d I informed her. \u201cShe\u2019s really looking forward to your non-murder fun day.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks,\u201d she said again, and then she shut down the engine and headed inside.<br /> <br /> I pulled up to the Lighthouse about twenty minutes later and made my way inside. I spoke with Moon at the front desk briefly; ze\u2019s still pining after Desiree, but seems a little more together about the whole thing now. I advised hir to give the redhead her space for a while to let her recover from the shock she\u2019s experienced lately, and ze agreed that this was probably for the best. At least ze\u2019s not lacking for companionship\u2026 ze told me that ze\u2019d gone home with Peg after the Beltane party.<br /> <br /> I found Jimmy and Peg in the Library itself, and they escorted me to a private room with a computer. \u201cNow don\u2019t worry none, love,\u201d Jimmy said kindly, \u201cwe\u2019ve selected this test based on your self-assessment, so it should be well-suited to you. It\u2019s designed for people with roughly your level of education. It\u2019s <u>not</u> designed for people who are missin\u2019 a few decades, because\u2026 well, because there <u>aren\u2019t</u> any tests like that. But we did the best we could.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nervously took my seat and began. The tests didn\u2019t take all that long, and they honestly weren\u2019t as difficult as I\u2019d thought they would be. Peg went to pick up some ice cream from the nearby Dairy Queen while Jimmy proctored me. Peg returned just as I was finishing up, and she had a sundae for her partner. Those two give each other a lot of shit, but they\u2019re pretty good together, all in all.<br /> <br /> Jimmy printed out the grades of my tests, and the two of them looked over the results. \u201cExcellent scores,\u201d Peg said with a wry grin, \u201cseems you\u2019ve undersold yourself to us, love.\u201d<br /> <br /> I sputtered at that one. \u201cI think you might have given me an easier test than you intended,\u201d I said quickly. \u201cIt wasn\u2019t very hard at all.\u201d<br /> <br /> Peg chuckled. \u201cNo worries, love,\u201d she said amiably. \u201cWhile these tests show a level of intelligence far higher than you reported on your self-exam\u2026 it pretty much tracks with my independent assessment. It\u2019s about what I expected.\u201d<br /> <br /> That made no sense to me. \u201cBut\u2026 my grades in High School were terrible,\u201d I said weakly.<br /> <br /> \u201cDid you give a shit back then?\u201d Peg asked with an arched eyebrow.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell\u2026 no,\u201d I had to admit. I\u2019d been more concerned with partying, getting laid, and infuriating my dad back in those days. After Kyle dismissed me as a vacuous bimbo, I\u2019d never really seen the <u>point</u> in studying very much.<br /> <br /> \u201cBut you\u2019ve been applyin\u2019 yourself lately,\u201d Jimmy rumbled, \u201cstudying medicine, you said.\u201d I nodded at that. \u201cWell, I\u2019m bettin\u2019 you had to look up more than a few words in order to understand those texts and articles. And bone up on a bit of math to work out dosages and dilution percentages and such.\u201d<br /> <br /> Peg nodded. \u201cYou\u2019ve a good head on your shoulders, Miss Grace, when you make up your mind to use it.\u201d<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know about that, but I\u2019m pleased that I did well on their tests. The next round, unfortunately, didn\u2019t show me in quite as favorable a light. The three of us met up at a local gymnasium, and Jimmy and I each donned a pair of boxing gloves and stepped into a ring. Peg was quick to assure me that she didn\u2019t expect me to knock Jimmy out or anything like that; they just wanted to see how well I could handle myself in a fight.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo tricks now,\u201d Jimmy said as we stepped into the ring. \u201cNo glamour.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded and approached him with trepidation. The next minute could have been the most humiliating of my life, but in the end I suppose it wasn\u2019t that bad. I know pretty much <u>nothing</u> about the so-called \u201cSweet Science,\u201d and I decided pretty early on that I just wasn\u2019t going to be able to land a hit past Jimmy\u2019s guard, so I opted to focus on my footwork\u2026 namely by dancing around his attacks and nimbly stepping aside whenever he threw a punch at me.<br /> <br /> It worked pretty well for a while. I mean, he landed a few hits on me here and there, but for the most part I was twisting or backing out of the way at the time, which served to minimize the force of the impact. A couple of minutes into the match, however, Jimmy got tired of messing around and just clocked me a good one right in the ol\u2019 kisser. I staggered backwards and it was all I could do to keep from falling on my ass.<br /> <br /> Luckily, I managed to remain standing until Peg struck the bell, signifying the end of the match. \u201cNot bad,\u201d she said as she walked out and put a stabilizing hand on my shoulder.<br /> <br /> \u201cI never even hit him,\u201d I managed to slur out, still a little dazed.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, but you\u2019re still standin\u2019 after a couple of minutes in the ring with Jimmy, and that\u2019s no mean feat for someone with no prior experience,\u201d Peg elaborated.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh,\u201d I said. She kept fading in and out of focus, and I wished she would stop it. \u201cCan I sit down now? I really think I need to sit down.\u201d<br /> <br /> Dominika stepped up into the ring from out of nowhere, her dark eyes shining as she approached with a Mona Lisa smile on her face.<br /> <br /> I think I said something witty, like \u201cyou\u2019re very pretty,\u201d as she started channeling glamour into a healing contract.<br /> <br /> She nodded as she ran her fingers over my rising bruises. \u201cPrettiest girl in the room, before you showed up,\u201d she muttered as she went to work. What a sweetheart!<br /> <br /> In any case, after Dominika worked her magic on me my head cleared as much as it ever does, and I decided to head back to the Dream House. A strange sight met my eyes as I pulled into the driveway\u2026 Jacob was standing on the pinnacle of the roof, holding his daggers and looking vaguely menacing. I pulled the \u2018vette into the garage, walked back out to the front of the house, and called up to him.<br /> <br /> \u201cHey, Jacob!\u201d I called out.<br /> <br /> \u201cHello,\u201d he said in response.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhatcha doin\u2019?\u201d I asked innocently.<br /> <br /> \u201cJulia is painting me,\u201d he replied.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, okay. I\u2019ll be right up,\u201d I said, heading for the door. When I reached the roof I found that Julia was indeed painting Jacob\u2026 while Marguerite and D made out a few feet away. The painting was breathtaking, of course, and it was a gorgeous day, so I sat down and joined my little family in enjoying it.<br /> <br /> When Julia had finished, we adjourned to the entertainment room. Calamity and Stasia got back shortly thereafter, looking incredibly pleased with themselves. \u201cDrag racing on the costal roads,\u201d Calamity elaborated when I threw her a questioning look. \u201cWe won three races. It was amazing!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCongrats,\u201d I said, trying not to think about how dangerous it must have been for them to drive at breakneck speeds against another vehicle along a twisty road between a solid rock wall and a sheer drop into the Pacific Ocean. \u201cI boxed with an Ogre this afternoon.\u201d So then I had to explain that, which led to offers from both Calamity and Jacob to teach me the basics of hand-to-hand combat. Though it\u2019s not really at the top of my list of things to learn, I accepted their kind offer, since learning how to shore up your weaknesses is really in the spirit of the Pilgrims.<br /> <br /> Stasia had brought the movies for movie night, which was\u2026 interesting. The first was a farcical action spy movie called <u>D.E.B.S. </u>, which at times focused on a lesbian romantic sub-plot between the main character and the arch-villain. The movie was silly and irreverent, but a lot of fun, and not something that required a lot of higher thought in order to enjoy. Calamity seemed particularly fond of one of the few male characters in the film: the villain\u2019s main henchman, who called himself Scud. She went so far as to propose that the Dream House needed a minion like that\u2026 though I <u>think</u> she was mostly joking about that. Mostly.<br /> <br /> The second film was called <u>Girltrash! All Night Long</u>. I expressed a little doubt when the title was first brought up, but Stasia assured me that it was a quality film. And you know what? She was right! It was a musical about a group of girls trying to get to a \u201cBattle of the Bands\u201d sort of event, with \u2013 once again \u2013 a heavy overtone of lesbian romance (which I suppose is not surprising, considering that Stasia is the one who picked the films). The story was fun, the girls were hot, and most of the songs were surprisingly good, employing as they did the lost art of vocal harmony\u2026 so I\u2019ll count it as a win. I confess that I liked it enough to check my phone before the credits rolled to see if I could purchase the film from Amazon (I can).<br /> <br /> The feel-good all-girl romance had my lovers and I in the mood for tenderness, so we excused ourselves pretty quickly after the second film and made our way to Marguerite and Julia\u2019s room. Yes, we made love, but we also held each other and kissed and hugged and just took comfort in the shared warmth and affection. I love my life.<br /> <br /> Having stayed up all night the previous evening trying to wear Brightstar out, I decided to catch some real shuteye after things had cooled off a bit. I fell asleep with Maria snuggled up against my chest, the clean scent of her hair in my nose and the feel of her heart beating against my breast wiping away the aches and pains of the day. Julia was nestled snugly on the other side of her, and Marguerite rested bonelessly (and damn near weightlessly) above us.<br /> <br /> So yesterday morning there was something in the air\u2026 I\u2019m not sure what it was. It was like the tingling tension you get before a thunderstorm (more on that later), but it was deeper somehow\u2026 more significant. It was like the Wyrd itself was humming and thrumming around us. I think most of us felt it to some degree, but by unspoken agreement we didn\u2019t discuss it out loud.<br /> <br /> I made waffles for Sex Breakfast. Not like fancy Gawain waffles or anything\u2026 just simple batter in a waffle iron. But nobody complained, and a couple of people even came back for seconds, so I\u2019ll count the experiment as a success. Jacob, Calamity and D had gone off to therapy, and they were a little late coming back since Calamity had to stop by a Red Cross station and donate blood\u2026 I think it had something to do with a Contract she\u2019d enacted to improve her drag racing skills, but I confess that I didn\u2019t ask for the details.<br /> <br /> I had my first \u201ctraining session\u201d with Jacob and Calamity after breakfast. We didn\u2019t actually spar like they usually do, but they took turns teaching me the basics of unarmed combat\u2026 mostly jujitsu, to be precise. Since I\u2019ll probably never be a real physical powerhouse, they focused on teaching me how to use my dexterity to wrong-foot my opponents and use their strength and momentum against them. It was\u2026 fun, actually, though I prefer to think of it as an exercise regimen rather than dwelling on how they\u2019re teaching me to hurt people.<br /> <br /> Jimmy and Peg ran me through another couple of tests this afternoon. This time we met at a local school\u2019s athletic field and they had me run laps to test my endurance. Now, I may not be Frank Shorter, but I\u2019m not entirely unaccustomed to prolonged physical activity either, and I flatter myself that I have decent breath control and muscular stamina. I think I did pretty well, if I do say so myself, though I didn\u2019t set any records for speed or distance. Peg and Jimmy seemed pleased, at any rate.<br /> <br /> So I returned to the Dream House about mid-afternoon in bike pants and a sports bra, prepared to hit the shower and start getting ready for the show. I noted on the way in that a storm seemed to be brewing, and chalked up the oppressive atmosphere I\u2019d been feeling all day to a drop in barometric pressure. Julia nabbed me on my way up the stairs.<br /> <br /> \u201cLori,\u201d she said seriously, \u201cI want you to go up on to the roof and make her come down, please.\u201d<br /> <br /> I blinked a couple of times. \u201cWho?\u201d I asked after a moment.<br /> <br /> \u201cBon-bon,\u201d Julia elaborated. \u201cShe\u2019s up on the roof, and there\u2019s a storm coming. I tried to get her to come in, but she keeps saying that she\u2019s fine, and won\u2019t listen to me. She\u2019s not fine; a storm is about to break. It\u2019s dangerous. I want you to convince her to come in.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded, seeing the sense in her concerns. \u201cOkay, I\u2019ll try,\u201d I agreed.<br /> <br /> Sure enough, Marguerite was perched on the edge of the roof, her head erect, staring into the heart of the gathering darkness. The wind was high, and it was starting to rain. Her hair whipped around her, but the water didn\u2019t seem to touch her.<br /> <br /> \u201cMarguerite, sweetie?\u201d I asked tentatively. \u201cAre you okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI am fine,\u201d she said softly but clearly, \u201cthere is no need for you to worry.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhy don\u2019t you come in, honey?\u201d I asked after a moment. \u201cIt\u2019s not safe out there. Julia\u2019s worried about you, and she asked me to make sure you\u2019re okay.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI am fine,\u201d she said again. \u201cI am communing with the storm. I have to\u2026 I must finish this, before I can come inside. I am sorry to worry you, Juliette\u2026 and please tell Julia that I am sorry to worry her as well. But I must do this.\u201d She frowned. \u201cPlease leave me for now. It is difficult to do this while I am talking to you. I will not be long now.\u201d<br /> <br /> I took that as my cue to vacate the roof. Julia was waiting at the bottom of the stairs, just as anxious as ever. \u201cI\u2026 don\u2019t think we can interfere with this, honey,\u201d I said seriously. \u201cWhatever\u2019s happening out there reeks of Wyrd-with-a-Y. I\u2019ve felt it building all day. I think she\u2019ll be okay, but she has to see it through.\u201d<br /> <br /> Julia nodded, and I kept her company while we waited for Marguerite to descend. I really should have been getting ready for the show\u2026 but Julia really needed me, and I wasn\u2019t just going to abandon her to deal with Marguerite\u2019s odd behavior alone. Luckily, she actually did come downstairs about fifteen minutes later, and she seemed a lot more like herself. \u201cI need to dream,\u201d she said simply. \u201cI will be up in time for the show.\u201d And with that, Julia escorted her back to their room.<br /> <br /> So I set about prettying myself up\u2026 somewhat more rushed than usual due to my abbreviated schedule. I only had one solo tonight, but it fit my mood perfectly: flirty and peppy and fun. \u201cQueen of Hearts\u201d is an upbeat little pop-country number popularized by Juice Newton a few years after I was Taken. It\u2019s about the inevitability of love despite the likelihood of heartbreak (or at least that\u2019s my take), and I find it utterly charming. The crowd seemed to like it, too. Maybe I should dip in to optimistic country numbers more often\u2026 oh, who am I kidding? That\u2019s a shallow pool to say the least.<br /> <br /> I worked the crowd for a bit as the show went on. I wasn\u2019t sure why at the time, but I was full of nervous energy; I had ants in my pants, as dad used to say. That odd psychological pressure still seemed to charge the atmosphere, and I couldn\u2019t seem to stand still. At times it was almost physical, like an itch, or a building sneeze or something. So I moved from table to table, greeting the regulars and lingering with the changelings, as their presence seemed to ease the anxiety a bit.<br /> <br /> Joan and Andromeda were there, and they wanted to personally thank me for suggesting they spend Beltane evening with Flores. Apparently things went well\u2026 not that I ever doubted it for a second. Joan was apparently quite taken with Flores\u2019 breasts, a fact which Andromeda delighted in rubbing in. Both were quick to assure me that they still desired my intimate company, and we\u2019ve tentatively set up a dinner-and-a-feature-film date for Thursday night. Alas, I suspect their VCR will still be on the fritz.<br /> <br /> Juan-Carlos Hypnos was there to speak with Calamity. I\u2019m not sure exactly why, but I assume it has something to do with all the dream healing she\u2019s been doing recently. I know that he was in frequent contact with Gawain, and had even been sponsoring him as a member of his entitlement, so maybe he\u2019s eyeing Calamity as a new prot\u00e9g\u00e9 or something. I confess that we didn\u2019t speak much; I just planted myself in his lap and traced my fingers over his chest. I swear, that man has <u>exquisite</u> muscle tone. I spent a few minutes using him as a personal practice model for my medical studies, identifying his pectorals, abdominals, trapezius, triceps, biceps, deltoids, lats\u2026 and gluteus. Very important muscle, the gluteus.<br /> <br /> Veronica was also there, and I made sure to spend a good bit of time with her, as I\u2019d promised we could hang out after the show. I introduced her to the rest of the motley, and to a few of my other friends, before taking her to meet D\u2026 who was shamelessly flirting with Juan-Carlos. I once more planted myself in his lap, but this time I made sure not to ignore the rest of the conversation.<br /> <br /> I should probably explain my thoughts a bit here. I fully intended to honor my commitment and spend as much time hanging out with Veronica as she wanted. However, I\u2019d also noticed Marguerite flirting with her a little earlier, and she\u2019d seemed receptive. As Juan-Carlos is one of the most accomplished male lovers I\u2019ve ever had, it seemed prudent to keep him interested in case Veronica opted to spend her evening in my French lover\u2019s company instead of my own.<br /> <br /> As it turned out it wasn\u2019t necessary. After we stopped beating around the bush and started speaking plainly, Veronica indicated with an adorable blush that she thought she would enjoy spending the evening with <u>both</u> Marguerite and me. I made sure that Juan-Carlos would be available the following evening, and the two of us led our guest up to our boudoir. D opted to entertain Juan-Carlos herself last night, and Julia took her leave and headed over to see Flores at the Rose &amp; Thorn.<br /> <br /> Veronica was unfamiliar with the intimate touches of women, so Marguerite and I dedicated ourselves to giving her a memorable evening. We also saw her without her black silk gloves for the first time\u2026 and found out why she wears them. Both of her hands and lower arms are pretty badly burned; an eternal reminder of her escape from Arcadia. It was obvious that she was uncomfortable revealing this to us, so as soon as she did so I made sure to bend over and kiss the back of her hand in a courtly gesture of affection. I think she appreciated it.<br /> <br /> Most of last night was about Veronica, though she was eager to reciprocate, and her enthusiasm made up for her lack of technique. Though I confess, even after I had been satisfied, I still felt that odd pressure, like something momentous was about to happen. That humming, tingling throb returned, and seemed to suffuse my whole body. My wings in particular itched, and it was hard for me to get to sleep even after Veronica and Marguerite had exhausted me.<br /> <br /> I woke up this morning before the others\u2026 and nearly screamed. Feathers littered the mattress around me\u2026 my feathers. They\u2019d been coming in so well over the past six months or so that I\u2019d held out hope that my wings were healing at last. I felt the tears spring into my eyes as all of that progress, all of that <u>hope</u> lay sad and desolate on Marguerite\u2019s bed.<br /> <br /> I made my way out into the hallway and then into the bathroom. Turning side-on and looking at my wings in that mirror was one of the hardest things I\u2019ve ever had to do. You can imagine my relief when I saw that my wings were fine. Better than fine. Healed. New feathers have grown in, pushing out the previous set. Pinions of green and red and blue and gold, as big as the feathers of an Andean Condor. Down as soft and fluffy as sea foam. I tried to spread them, and with the added span from the longer pinions, I hit both of the bathroom walls. Along the room\u2019s <u>long</u> axis. When I brought them down to my sides, I could <u>feel</u> them catch the air. My breath caught in my throat, and the tears started to flow.<br /> <br /> I ran into my room, ignoring the sleepy interrogatives from D and Juan-Carlos for the moment. Ignoring underwear, I threw on a pair of sweatpants and that sweater Rowan made for me last Christmas. My love sat up slowly, the sheet falling away from her breasts, looked at me blearily, and croaked out \u201cbabe?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll be right back,\u201d I said through my sobs, and I ran to the exterior balcony door. I threw the door open as Juan-Carlos was asking what was going on in sleepy Spanish. I sprinted to the edge of the balcony before D could respond. I spread my wings as far as they would go, lifted them, and pushed them down as hard as I could, just as I leaped over the railing.<br /> <br /> And I flew. I flew. I <u>flew! </u><br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t glide lazily to the ground, I pushed myself into the sky. I felt the thermals pulling me in different directions, and I adjusted myself almost subconsciously. I swooped, I soared, I dove\u2026 hell, I might have even looped the loop once or twice. It was natural. It was instinctive. It was <u>easy</u>.<br /> <br /> I landed on the balcony again a few minutes (or a hundred years\u2026 something like that) later. D and Marguerite were there wearing oversized t-shirts and oversized smiles. Veronica and Juan-Carlos, dressed in their clothes from the previous evening, were making nervous small-talk on one corner of the balcony. There were lots of kisses and hugs and tearful congratulations. And then I fell to my knees, unabashed and unashamed, and thanked God for giving me back my wings.<br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei Grace</b><br /> <br /> (GM\u2019s Note: yer welcome <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> <b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> Monday, May 4th<br /> Nine years, one month, nineteen days<br /> Days without stabbing: 2<br /> <br /> It\u2019s been a good day. I\u2019m\u2026 happy? Well, maybe more like content at this point but I definitely hit happy for a while earlier. That\u2019s something that hasn\u2019t happened in a while now. Not since New Year\u2019s. Since before Gawain left. And it still feels like part of me is missing but for a while today I actually managed to not notice it. Unsurprisingly, it was Stasia\u2019s handiwork.<br /> <br /> Sex breakfast was sex breakfast. What can I say, now that I\u2019m the only one there that isn\u2019t fucking every night it just isn\u2019t as much fun. Or maybe it just reminds that he\u2019s gone. But once the talk turned from sex to trying to hook Rowan and Neon up (because you know, it\u2019s just not possible for someone to be single and happy) I retreated to the office to keep from saying something unpleasant and moody because everyone is just better off when I keep my bitchiness to myself. That and I did actually have some work to get done before whatever grand adventure Stasia had planned for us.<br /> <br /> And I was rather curious what she had planned. And yes, mixed in with all the grump I was actually looking forward to it. As soon as she got there, I knew this was not just the usual mission to drag Kat out and try to cheer her up. I mean, she was driving this tricked out classic mustang that was painted fucking metallic gold. I mean, seriously, that thing would have embarrassed a 70\u2019s blacksplotation movie pimp.<br /> <br /> As it turns out, the owner, in addition to clearly having a smaller cock than I do, has a super hot trophy wife who has a thing for hotshot street racers (clearly further proof of the owner\u2019s lack of sexual prowess) and she apparently makes quite the habit of hooking up with the ones that impress her, though apparently Stasia was the first woman. Most likely due to the severe lack of female street racers rather than lack of than inclination I would guess but I can\u2019t say as I never actually met the woman, only had her pointed out to me in the crowd of onlookers.<br /> <br /> So, clearly the stakes where high and Stasia had perhaps overstated herself as a bad-ass street racer just a touch. So as soon as I suggested a little fairy magic to help her out it was pretty clear that had been her plan all along. Maybe I should have been a little annoyed at her assuming, but it just felt so much like old times. So I whipped up a pledge to give her the sharper reflexes and mad racing skillz she needed in return for bringing movies for movie night (which I knew she\u2019d already picked out and had with her) while also reminding her that I can\u2019t let her off the hook on a pledge no matter much I might want to. So by the time we got there, she had the mojo to back up her fast and furious swagger (something Stasia needs no magic to boost).<br /> <br /> It was a twisty stretch of highway, solid wall on one side and sheer drop on the other. Everyone there was seriously hardcore. Our wheels where the gaudiest but it was a feast of high octane barely street legal speed demons. The other drivers were naturally unimpressed that a pair of women had the gall to decide to be racers rather than prizes which only made us both kick the trash talk and bravado up to eleven. By the time Stasia was up for her first run, we\u2019d found the bookies. There was some serious money being tossed down. Neither of us had the kind of bank most of the others were laying down but the odds were heavily against us silly girls who thought we could play with the big boys. Oh man was it sweet rubbing it in when we collected our winnings. Not as awesome as actually racing but damn close.<br /> <br /> We ended up with three runs and Stasia offered to let me take the wheel for the second of them. I used my Goblin Vow with Blood to give myself the same edge I\u2019d given Stasia and promised to donate a pint after therapy which suited Blood well enough. With the extra moves I was able to smoke my opponent as smoothly as Stasia put her two down. And by the last run it was actually one of the better drivers since we\u2019d proven we actually could drive. Let me tell you, random person reading my diary I guess, it was a HELL of a rush screaming through those turns with a wall of rock on one side and sheer drop on the other. I guess Ace really was right that \u201cor death\u201d really does makes everything better.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t end up getting another turn since we got the incoming cop alert right after Stasia\u2019s second run. So we settled our bets and skedaddled along with as everyone else.<br /> <br /> Stasia and I had already planned on doing dinner together and since we had a fat stack of cash and a drug dealer\u2019s ride we decided to hit the most upscale steakhouse we could find and crash it in our denim and leather. To be fair, I\u2019m pretty sure at least the ma\u00eetre d\u2019 had seen it before (or maybe he was just that damn good at being unfazable) and we did enjoy some mighty mighty fine food while (mostly) not pulling a Blues Brothers on the place.<br /> <br /> We rolled into the Dream House full of fine food and feeling rather damn pleased with ourselves. I\u2019ll confess, I was kinda looking forward to seeing everyone's faces (especially Lori\u2019s) when we told them about our wild and dangerous adventure. I was not expecting Lori to have her own hi-jinks to share. But apparently as part of her testing for the Pilgrims of the Endless Road she\u2019d spent a few rounds in the ring with Squarefoot and managed to stay on her feet even if she didn\u2019t actually land a decent blow on him. She was rightly proud of herself and both Jacob and I were quick to offer to have her join us during our sparring if she wanted to pick up at least some basics. She\u2019s apparently going to take us up on it at least tomorrow. That should prove interesting. I\u2019ve been studying with White Maria but I\u2019m not sure how Jacob is at unarmed fighting.<br /> <br /> But the tale-telling didn\u2019t last too long since we had movies to watch. I wasn\u2019t sure what to expect from Stasia and I am honestly quite glad that I was in such high spirits. I don\u2019t think either of those movies would have sat well with my usual mood of late. Both were very lesbian romances. Apparently the directors are a couple and it showed (not in a bad way but just there was a similarly quirky vibe to them both) Neither was overly serious and honestly they were fun even if it was ultimately a happily ever after ending to them both. Like I said, not a pair of movies that would have meshed with my usual mood of late but I enjoyed them despite that. And there was fun banter (when folks weren\u2019t too busy making out\u2026) and Jacob did up a round (or two) of cocktails between the movies.<br /> <br /> And as everyone paired off Stasia asked if she could crash at the Dream House since she\u2019d been drinking and really didn\u2019t want to drive the world\u2019s most noticeable car home and risk getting a ticket and ruining things before she\u2019d gotten the trophy wife into bed. I was happy to agree and then as we had the den to ourselves we ended up firing up the console and spending a bit playing before she begged off to get some sleep.<br /> <br /> I did thank her for a wonderful day and tried to apologize for being such a colossal bitch these past few months but she waved that off by reminding me that we were blood sisters. And just as we were on the verge of having an awkward Hallmark moment or something we both kinda stopped and called it a night.<br /> <br /> After I walked her to the guest room I slipped up onto the roof and perched there a bit watching till the light went out and then just staring at her window. Yeah, I know it was creepy but I\u2019m a Darkling, it\u2019s what we fucking do. As I was sitting up there I thought about things. I never gave up on her in Snow Globe. I would die before I gave up on her. But what if she gives up on me? Gawain did. Becky has. But I managed to stop myself before I fell completely down that rabbit hole. And now I need to get some sleep. I\u2019ve got therapy in the morning. Maybe I\u2019ll actually talk to Dr Emmett about it. That\u2019s the whole point of going after all.<br /> <br /> <br /> Tuesday, May 5th<br /> Nine years, one month, eighteen days<br /> Days without stabbing: 3<br /> <br /> I am not going to call her. I am not going to call my ex-girlfriend in the middle of the fucking night while drinking and beg to see her. Hell, at this point it\u2019s not even about the sex\u2026 I mean, yeah it\u2019s been nothing but solo missions for way too long but honestly what I want more than anything is just to be fucking held. Is that really so much to ask for?<br /> <br /> <br /> Jesus\u2026 that sounds so fucking pathetic\u2026 That shit is fucking weak Calamity\u2026 You\u2019re better than that. You are not going to fucking call her and go groveling. You are not the one that stopped coming around. You are not the one that skipped Walpurgis. You are not the one that walked the fuck away when your girlfriend fucking needed you the most. You are not going to fucking call that bitch.<br /> <br /> Hell, at least Gawain had the balls to fucking tell me he was dumping me.<br /> <br /> <br /> Shit, I should slow down. I haven\u2019t hit the booze this hard in a while and the captain is most definitely starting to make it happen. Fuck\u2026 What the hell is wrong with me? Just when I feel like maybe I\u2019m starting to get my shit sorted out I\u2019m suddenly right back where I started. It\u2019s done. It\u2019s over. It\u2019s been four months. I need to let this goddamn shit go. But like everything else, that is way easier said than done.<br /> <br /> I guess I should have guessed that was what Juan Carlos wanted to talk to me about when he texted me this morning. I mean, sure as fuck wasn\u2019t because he wanted to roll around with the broken glass girl. But it just\u2026 I just couldn\u2019t even think of it at the time. In hindsight I guess it\u2019s for the best, since it meant I was still in a decent mood. I mean, I had a fairly good session with Dr Emmett and Jacob and I\u2019s meeting with Dahlia wasn\u2019t exactly roses and sunshine but things are at least in motion regarding the current crop of new arrivals. They haven\u2019t decided that I need to deal with any of them yet at least.<br /> <br /> And coaxing Lori out to start her on some training in close quarter combat after her bout with Squarefoot last night was nice. It felt good to share some of what I\u2019ve been learning from White Maria with her and to see what Jacob knew. His own training is much more direct than mine, which is a bit odd considering that even though he is stronger than me, he\u2019s still got more speed and precision than raw power. Though when I was explaining that I thought it would be worth it for Lori to focus on a softer style like mine I think he was considering the idea as well. And once Lori got called away by the Pilgrims for today\u2019s testing (running and endurance apparently) we did start our sparring without blades but I clearly had the upper hand so we switched to our knives pretty quickly. And once we got to going I actually started to feel that sense of being in the moment, of dancing\u2026 of zen. I haven\u2019t been on my rhythm like that since... well since Gawain left. But after the awkward start Jacob really poured his all into it because he was in truly rare form. As good as my dance was, his was better. It didn\u2019t matter though. Even as the thunderstorm rolled in to force us to head back inside I think we were both feeling like we\u2019d had our best spar in a long time.<br /> <br /> I hit the shower and got ready. I\u2019d put \u2018Little Red Riding Hood\u2019 in as my number for the night since I was feeling it after yesterday afternoon\u2019s shenanigans and I haven\u2019t had time to iron out a new number yet. I don\u2019t think I will ever be able to just whip out an act as spontaneously as Lori can. Once I got downstairs, I saw that Juan Carlos had already arrived so I slipped out to have a word with him as unprepared as a bug flaying across a highway for the emotional semi I was about to get hit by.<br /> <br /> Yeah. I know. That sounds pretty fucking melodramatic right there. I should have expected what he was there to talk about. And even though I didn\u2019t, it shouldn\u2019t have been such a fucking big deal. But he was there because there isn\u2019t a member of the Family of Silent Nights in the area any more. And he wanted to ask if I was interested in taking up the mantle. And suddenly it just all came flooding back like it hadn\u2019t been four goddamn months since Gawain left me. And I was not fucking ready for it. I don\u2019t know. Maybe it was just that replacing him added some weird finality to the whole thing, like somehow it meant he really wasn\u2019t coming back even though I knew he wasn\u2019t. Like it made it real or something. I don\u2019t fucking know. I just know it sucker-punched me like an invisible ogre. But I did manage to tell him I was interested. I mean, I have been picking up where Gawain left off with most of the dream work in the area. And I am a damn good Oneiromancer. As good as him\u2026 maybe even better.<br /> <br /> Still, it threw me for a loop and left me feeling off kilter for the rest of the night. Thankfully I was able to focus on my number and not drag the show down (not that Lori couldn\u2019t have saved it.) After the show I tried to talk to Marguerite about it when she stopped to ask me about Veronica but I couldn\u2019t really figure out where to start and she was more than a little impatient to get on with the night\u2019s conquest. And Lori was perched in Juan Carlos\u2019 lap so I didn\u2019t try to interrupt beyond making sure he knew I would make sure I was available whenever he needed me to be for the tests. Though she ended up going off with Veronica and Marguerite and leaving him in D\u2019s hands for the night. All that prompted Julia to head off to spend the night with Flores. I ended up at the bar and considered trying to talk to Jacob about it but he and Luna were busy being all happily in love so I elected to just confide in the wisdom of Captain Morgan instead. Speaking of which, I do believe he\u2019s got some more life advice for me... <br /> <br /> <br /> Love makes you stupid. Sometimes well past the point were it\u2019s cold stony dead. I\u2019m not even sure what exactly I feel about this situation. I\u2019m confused. I\u2019m glad my skills are being recognized. But I\u2019m also feeling this weird guilt because this is Gawain\u2019s thing and I\u2019m taking it over. And at the same time I\u2019m feeling this vindictive glee that it\u2019s Gawain\u2019s thing and I\u2019m taking it away. And I know it\u2019s all dumb because he\u2019s gone and it\u2019s not about him and I shouldn\u2019t fucking care anyway and why can\u2019t I stop fucking caring and why does this still fucking hurt and how do I make this shit stop.<br /> <br /> <br /> Rum. Rum makes the hurting stop. Only I\u2019m out and I\u2019m too tired to go get another bottle and I have already had too damn much and I\u2019m fucking drunk and I should just stop and put this stupid book down and go the fuck to sleep before I write anything else stupid in here and and all I want is someone to fucking hold me and tell me this is going to fucking be alright but it\u2019s not because it never is because They were right\u2026 I\u2019m not a good girl and nice things don\u2019t happen to monsters and noone is ever going to love a monster like me\u2026<br /> <br /> I outta go find nother bottle. They\u2019re all too busy fucking to notice. Not that they\u2019d care anyway. Noone wants to listen to me whine and cry. Fuck. I dun\u2019t want to listen to me anymore. The Voices were right\u2026 They told me noone else could love a wicked girl. They told me my parents were happier without me. They held me in the dark and dried my tears and They told me They loved me. They tried so hard to make me a good girl but They couldn\u2019t. And then I hurt Them. I cut Them and tasted Their blood and I left Them. I tell everyone I was alone in Snow Globe\u2026 But I wasn\u2019t\u2026 The Voices were there. They were always there. They held me and loved me and instead of loving Them back I cut Them because I hurt everyone that loves me. I hurt Them and then I left Them. And I ran straight into Handsome. And he loved me and he held me until I hurt him too. I hurt him until he left me. Beautiful loved me and even though it cut her skin and made her bleed she held me... But I hurt her and she left me too.<br /> <br /> And now I\u2019m alone in the dark\u2026 because that\u2019s where monsters belong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T14:04:19-07:00","id":1143580,"title":"","content":"<b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> For me today was a mostly average day. For others it was far more exciting. It started off like usual, with Sex Breakfast in the kitchen. Calamity got back from sparring and meditating with White Maria just before we all started eating. I made coffee though for some reason mine seemed a little too hot for me this morning. Maybe because it was the first cup poured out of the carafe? I don\u2019t know. Anyway, conversation eventually came around to relationships. Brightstar asked about Neon and Lori brought up her idea of getting Rowan and Neon together since they both need someone. She seemed pretty convinced that they\u2019d hit it off and make a cute couple. I think she just wants Rowan to be happy, which is nice. I\u2019m just not sure that setting her up with someone is the way to go about doing that. Who knows though, it might work. In any case, Calamity got fed up with the conversation topic and stomped off in the direction of the office. She hasn\u2019t liked any talk concerning relationships since Gawain left. Shortly after that Lori got a text from Peg about her upcoming test. It seems that they want to give her a computerized test to evaluate her intelligence as well as a follow up evaluation of her physical fitness.<br /> <br /> On her way out Lori ran into Stasia who pulled up to the Dream House driving a metallic gold mustang. Stasia came inside and immediately asked for Calamity. We directed her to the office and the pair of them talked. When they left they both looked excited about what they had planned for the day. I wasn\u2019t sure what it was, but both ladies were keen about getting on with it. We told them to have fun and they left in the mysterious gold mustang. We figured the car wasn\u2019t stolen given how ostentatious is was. It would not be hard to spot, and if you\u2019re stealing a car the idea is to not be spotted. So, we figured it wasn\u2019t stolen but no one asked where it had come from. I guess this way if asked we have plausible deniability.<br /> <br /> So, after Lori left Julia came up to me and asked if she could paint me. She said that she really wanted to paint me perched up on the roof holding my knives with the night sky behind me. I thought about it for a moment and said \u201cSure.\u201d I haven\u2019t really sat for any of her paintings specifically and thought that it might be fun. She doesn\u2019t sell the private stuff to outsiders so I wouldn\u2019t have to worry about it getting out. So, I said yeah and followed her up on to the roof. Insincere Marguerite and De La Rocha followed us up. They didn\u2019t do much besides kiss and keep us company. In the end the painting came out really good. Julia then asked if I\u2019d like a painting of Luna and I said yes. She asked what setting I\u2019d like it to be in and I answered immediately that it should be in the woods. That is where Luna is the happiest and I like to see her smile like that.<br /> <br /> So, it turns out that Calamity and Stasia went drag racing. Stasia had borrowed the car from a pretty girl that she has a crush on and who\u2019s boyfriend is out of town. So, that\u2019s where she got the car. They went to a particularly winding, ocean facing road and proceeded to race. Both Calamity and Stasia won their races. Stasia won two and Calamity won the other. After the third race they settled up with the bookies and got their money. Then the whole lot of them took off since the police were coming. Apparently, they made off pretty well with the betting and Stasia impressed the girl that she was interested in.<br /> <br /> Lori on the other hand went to the Autumn Court Library to take her tests. She said that she surprised herself by doing better than she expected but didn\u2019t elaborate on that. I figured that she would do well. She\u2019s a smart girl. She just underestimates herself in that department. She did go into detail about sparring with Jimmy though. She had to box him in a ring for a few minutes and stay standing if she could. She was very excited about the fact that she managed to remain conscious. It was apparently a near thing, but she managed to dodge and weave enough to avoid most of Jimmy\u2019s blows. The couple that he did land were pretty substantial and Lori was reeling. But she was still standing when the bell rang so she passed that test. She was very happy about it. This of course led to Calamity and I bringing up the idea of teaching her more hand-to-hand fighting techniques. Lori seemed interested but wasn\u2019t super excited by the idea. We figured we could start tomorrow morning at our usual sparring time on Tuesdays.<br /> <br /> And then there was Movie Night. The movies were provided this time by Stasia and she chose two queer friendly movies. One was called D.E.B.S and the other was Girl Trash!. Seriously, there is an exclamation point after that movie\u2019s title. Luna only sighed a little bit during the first movie. It was kind of silly, but wasn\u2019t too bad. It was about a secret organization of spies that employs students to go out on missions. The music wasn\u2019t too bad but I\u2019m not sure that Luna appreciated all of it. In between the two movies I thought we could all use a short break, so I made cocktails for the lot of us. They were generally well received. The second movie was in my opinion better than the first. It had a more serious story. At least it wasn\u2019t as silly. It was a Battle of the Bands kind of plot which was fun. The good band wins the day and the girl gets the girl. The music was good too. I think Luna enjoyed the second one better than the first.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Calamity and I went to our usual therapy sessions this morning and as we were leaving Calamity said that she needed to go donate some blood. I asked why and she said that she\u2019d made a pledge with blood to be able to drive better yesterday afternoon. Apparently, there was a couple of contracts made. One for each driver so they could do their best. The one for Calamity though came with a unique price. So, we swung by the Red Cross and Calamity did her civic duty. I waited in the lobby for her and tried to ignore my itching arms. Not sure why they were itchy. I didn\u2019t have any mosquito bites that I knew of. I managed to push it to the back of my mind and waited. Once Calamity was done we started to head out, but got stopped by Dahlia. She had a couple things to discuss with us before we left. First off, we talked about Veronica. The not so new girl apparently moved into her current apartment on May 1st. She had stayed at an apartment in Venice Beach for a while but her old landlord was very tight lipped when it came to giving out information about prior tenants. He wouldn\u2019t do it without a court order, which Dahlia didn\u2019t have. One of Dahlia\u2019s theories is that Veronica is cursed in some way to make sure that bad luck follows her. We can\u2019t confirm her backstory because of a bunch of different reasons, all of which make things look suspicious. But Dahlia wasn\u2019t positive that Veronica was anything other than what she presented to the Freehold. I mean she didn\u2019t say that she didn\u2019t think the new girl wasn\u2019t a loyalist or anything, just that she wasn\u2019t sure. She\u2019s still suspicious as hell of the other woman though. Dahlia said that she usually gets a gut feeling about people, either good or bad, but wasn\u2019t getting one from Veronica. Not exactly sure what that means, but Changelings tend to follow their intuitions, so maybe there is nothing shady going on with the new arrival. Personally, I\u2019m not sure. But, then I tend to be rather suspicious of people in general.<br /> <br /> To counterpoint that, Carla doesn\u2019t check out at all. They don\u2019t have any information about her Keeper at all in the records and certain things don\u2019t add up. If she was made into a catgirl because the Keeper was essentially a fan boy, then she would have been a fairest. Instead she is a beast, which implies that she was required to develop claws for a reason. We just don\u2019t know why. Hannah on the other hand checks out completely. She has been a font of knowledge about her Keeper and her powers match her durance. The only concern that people have about her is her somewhat violent tendencies. Then there is Angelica. She is also actively being watched, but then we already knew that. The only troubling thing with her is that she seems to be sleeping with Desiree. That is probably not a good thing.<br /> <br /> After we were done talking to Dahlia we headed back to the Dream House and talked to Lori about training her in hand to hand fighting. She agreed and we all changed into our work out clothes. Calamity is more practiced in different hand to hand techniques but I\u2019m not that bad myself. Calamity just happens to be practicing with White Maria on some mornings, and the style that they do is a good match for Lori. It uses the weight and power of the attacker against them to good effect. The style I learned was similar but did rely on some strength to back up the punches and kicks. When Rook started teaching me to fight bare handed he emphasized moving out of the way and redirecting attacks. He then incorporated weight training into the training so I would have the strength to back up my strikes. I have done my best to continue on that same path. For Lori though we just started out on the basics like stances and how to make a fist so you won\u2019t break your hand. Sounds really simplistic, but when you\u2019re hitting something hard like someone\u2019s face you want to make sure you don\u2019t break anything of yours in the process. We went into a little more detail than that, but not too much. We wanted to her to grasp the basics before we got too in depth.<br /> <br /> After Lori excused herself Calamity and I got down to sparring. We continued the unarmed training for a bit, but it was obvious that Calamity was better at it than I was. I think she didn\u2019t want me to be frustrated the whole time so we switched over to knives after a short while. I really am more comfortable when I have blades in my hands. I guess that says something about me. Not sure what it says, but it probably isn\u2019t all that good. In any case we sparred like we haven\u2019t done in a long time. Calamity was really in the zone this afternoon and I stepped up to match her enthusiasm. It was a lot of fun. I think all told I would have won if it had been an actual fight, but it was close and we both did really well. It was good to see Calamity in such a positive mood. It hasn\u2019t happened for a long time. Since Gawain left. I know the big guy had his reasons for leaving, but he really did do a number on Calamity when he left like that. It was hard to watch her spiraling down into despair. She reached the point where she was just angry all the time. Lately she\u2019s been getting better, which has been heartening. Now today, with the sparring, it was like seeing the old Calamity looking at me. It was good to see. I think we would have kept going if the Thunderstorm hadn\u2019t started rolling in. The thunder broke our concentration and we both looked at the sky. We decided that was as good a time as any to stop and we both went inside. I hadn\u2019t even noticed, but during the sparring match I managed to forget about the itching in my arms. It even spread to my back and legs, which was really annoying. I figured it was just the sweat and endeavored to scrub the itch away in the shower. It didn\u2019t work.<br /> <br /> While we were sparring Lori went with Jimmy and Peg to do some long-distance running. She came back as the storm was moving in and Julia snagged her almost as soon as she walked through the door. She asked Lori to see if she could get Insincere Marguerite off of the roof before the storm really broke. I was a little concerned, but Marguerite is not one to recklessly put her life in danger. I figured that she would know when she needed to come inside, but Lori went up to make sure anyway. Apparently Insincere Marguerite was communing with the storm. Not exactly sure what that was all about, but she was completely dry when she came back in and Lori was not. Our winged friend had wet hair and feathers but Marguerite was dry as a bone. Not sure how she managed that, but there you have it. After that Insincere Marguerite went upstairs to lay down. Julia went with her.<br /> <br /> Those two remind me of a couple I knew in Arcadia. One was a Knight for the Lady, the other was a servant to another Gentry. It was one of the Lady\u2019s allies, so it wasn\u2019t uncommon to make trips between realms. The Knight, Alex, would accompany me on occasion, when Rook was off on a solo mission, to the other Gentry\u2019s lands. When we arrived, we would relay our message or gift, whatever the Lady had sent us for, and then we would enjoy the hospitality of the other monarch before making the journey back. I talked to acquaintances or rested while Alex went off to find his beau. I believe his name was Gregory. I think they thought that they were being discreet, but the Lady knew about their little affair. The Lady asked me on one occasion if I thought that Gregory was proving to be too much of a distraction for Alex to do his duty. I answered that the other Knight was first and foremost loyal to her. His affections for Gregory were secondary. I was unfortunately proven wrong shortly after that. The Lady devised a test for Alex. He was supposed to kill Gregory. I think the whole thing had been devised by both Gentry, otherwise He would have been upset with the Lady. In any case Alex would not harm Gregory despite being ordered to. They both paid the price for that failure. So did I. I spoke on his behalf and was mistaken in my assertions. I was more careful after that with what I said to the Lady in regards to other people. Tragedy aside though, they remind me of Julia and Insincere Marguerite because of their devotion to one another. It\u2019s so pure.<br /> <br /> The show went off great, as usual. All the ladies did their best and the crowd was appreciative. And speaking of appreciative, I think most of the ladies were appreciating the view that Juan Carlos provided when he walked in the club. That man just can\u2019t seem to keep a shirt on his body. If he is wearing one it always seems to be in the process of falling off. I noticed Luna watching him occasionally. I think she would have been watching him a little more often if she hadn\u2019t been sitting at the bar with me. I don\u2019t think she wanted to give the impression that she was interested in him over me. He is hard to look away from though. Even I have to admit he\u2019s good looking. In any case he came to the club to talk to Calamity. He specifically asked after her so we know it wasn\u2019t coincidence. My theory is that he came by to talk to her about Dream healing. She\u2019s been doing a lot of it lately. There may be a need to take a peek into one of the new arrivals dreams to make sure that they are on the up and up. I guess we\u2019ll find out soon enough what that meeting was all about.<br /> <br /> After Lori and Calamity finished their acts they mingled with the crowd. Lori ended up sitting in Juan Carlos\u2019 lap on a couple of occasions. I\u2019m not exactly sure what was going on. She seemed to be flirting with him exclusively like she had designs on him for the evening, but then Lori made her way over to Veronica\u2019s table and her attentions switched. She seemed to be more interested in the not so new girl after that. She even took her around to make introductions. Lori brought her up to the bar and I said \u201cHi.\u201d I was polite and friendly and offered her a drink. She seems like a nice girl. Of course, so did Desiree and it turned out that she had been a loyalist for the Director for a good long while before she finally turned her back on him. So, I\u2019m still holding my judgement on the not so new girl until she proves herself one way of the other. Lori and Veronica continued to make their rounds and ended up talking to Insincere Marguerite. Not sure what the three of them were talking about but I can guess given the way that Veronica\u2019s face was turning red.<br /> <br /> Calamity made her own rounds through the crowd. I saw her talking to Insincere Marguerite at one point and they looked serious. I\u2019m not sure what they were talking about but it was something that Calamity was not willing to joke about. I don\u2019t suppose it\u2019s my business but I will admit that I was curious about what they were discussing. After that Calamity met up with Hannah and they talked for a bit. They both seemed friendly and had smiles on their faces. I guess Calamity was taking Dahlia at her word when she told us that Hannah had been vetted already and was deemed not a danger to the Freehold. I myself have not had much opportunity to talk to Hannah. I\u2019m honestly not exactly sure what we\u2019d talk about. I\u2019m not good at making small talk with people I don\u2019t know well. Hell, I\u2019m not good at making small talk in general. I suppose that\u2019s the price I pay for being an elemental.<br /> <br /> In any case I need to remember in the morning to ask Luna and see if she can see any sort of rash on my back to explain the itching. I haven\u2019t noticed anything on my arms or legs, but figured it couldn\u2019t hurt to ask.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Luna sat up in bed and looked out the window. Something had woken her. The sun was starting to come over the horizon, but she was used to that. Keeping the hours that she did meant that she slept through many sunrises. She didn\u2019t know why this one should be different. Her wings fluttered as she sat there thinking. \u201cIt\u2019s just my imagination,\u201d she said quietly and lay back down next to her boyfriend. She snuggled up close to his back and put an arm around his waist. She drew it back in surprise and fear. He was cool to the touch. She sat up again in a mild panic and knelt next to Jacob. She rolled him over onto his back and put her palm on his chest. She was careful to avoid the Lady\u2019s brand that decorated his chest, right over his heart. She left her hand there for a moment before shakily moving her fingers to touch the side of his neck. She closed her eyes and she sat back down. She sighed but left her hand where it was.<br /> <br /> Jacob stirred and looked up at his lady love. \u201cWhat\u2019s wrong Luna?\u201d He reached up and wiped a tear that was running down her cheek. Luna started and put her hand over her heart for a moment.<br /> <br /> \u201cI was so worried,\u201d she admitted quietly. \u201cWhen I touched your shoulder, you were cool. I was concerned.\u201d<br /> <br /> The elemental sat up and laid his hand on his arm. He looked at his girlfriend. \u201cI feel normal to me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou wouldn\u2019t know you were cold unless your hands were warm love. All of you is cooler than you should be.\u201d She traced her hands along his body following the paths of frost that covered his skin in places. She looked at him in confusion. \u201cYour frost never came this far before, did it?\u201d<br /> <br /> Jacob looked down at his arms and legs and shook his head. \u201cNo, it didn\u2019t,\u201d he smiled. \u201cThe itching has stopped too.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cItching?\u201d Luna cocked her head to the side.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, I was itchy pretty much all day yesterday.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhy didn\u2019t you say anything about it?\u201d Luna nudged Jacob\u2019s shoulder with her finger.<br /> \u201cIt was just itchy. It\u2019s not like I was in pain or anything. I know enough by now to tell you if I was in pain.\u201d He smiled and touched her outstretched hand covering it with his.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat do you think this all means?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t know.\u201d He paused for a moment. \u201cI felt funny before when my powers increased the last time. Maybe that\u2019s what has happened now? Maybe I\u2019m just getting closer to my nature. That could be why I\u2019m cooler than I was before.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMaybe.\u201d Luna allowed. \u201cIf you\u2019re getting closer to what you were in Arcadia then I guess it makes sense that your skin would be colder to the touch.\u201d She looked him in the eye. \u201cYou feel okay though?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, I feel fine. More than fine actually. I suppose I should be tired being up this early, but I\u2019m not.\u201d He smiled. \u201cI feel alive.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou would tell me if you thought something was wrong, wouldn\u2019t you?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course I would Luna. You know I would.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay.\u201d She reached out with her other hand and took his in both of hers. \u201cI just worry about you sometimes.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m fine.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know. But you have to admit that sometimes you don\u2019t tell people when something is wrong with you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou know that I\u2019ve gotten a lot better about that in the past few months.\u201d He smiled and kissed Luna gently on the lips. \u201cSometimes I don\u2019t think that there is honestly anything to worry about, but I tell you anyway. I tell Lori so she can heal me if needs be.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThis is true. After that hunting trip you took in the Hedge with Calamity you came back injured and you told Lori about it.\u201d Her smile dimmed for a moment. \u201cYou waited a while before you told her though. You should have told her as soon as you got back.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt wasn\u2019t bad, and we didn\u2019t want to interrupt Lori. She was with someone.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe would have stopped whatever she was doing to come back here and heal the pair of you.\u201d Luna reclaimed her hand and poked him in the chest, just to the left of his brand.<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay, okay. You win. We should have told Lori sooner than we did. And we did the last time we went into the Hedge. We called Lori right off, you know that, you were there.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s because Calamity could barely stand under her own power. Even your skewed sense of what constitutes a real injury realized that she needed healing.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jacob reached up and stroked the side of Luna\u2019s face. \u201cI don\u2019t want to fight.\u201d He smiled. \u201cRight now, I just want to hold you. Can we do that?\u201d<br /> <br /> Luna reached out for his hand and squeezed. \u201cYeah we can do that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGood.\u201d The elemental lay back down and gently tugged his lover down next to him. \u201cI hope that my cooler skin won\u2019t stop you from wanting to snuggle.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course not, love.\u201d The corners of her mouth bent up. \u201cI\u2019m always up for a snuggle.\u201d </i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> I am a god. In a manner of speaking.<br /> <br /> The dreams have come to a head, and a powerful storm broke out over the Dream House. I felt them speaking to me, and I went outside. Both Julia and Juliette went out and spoke to me, but I got them to go inside. We finished our conversation, the Wyrd and I, and I began to change into one of the Lost Pantheon.<br /> <br /> This morning, I feel more powerful than ever before. It almost scares me.<br /> <br /> Despite the sense of building, it has been a good few days. Monday was a fun day of laughs and love. After a friendly sex breakfast where Maria shared the good news of her relationship with Gloria, Julia talked Jacob into posing for a painting. Stasia and Calamity had gone to hang out like old times, and Juliette went to do her testing for the Pilgrims, an order similar to, but very different from, the one I joined. I confess, while on the roof, Maria\u2019s playful flirting drew my attention. We spent quite a bit of time cuddling on the roof while Julia painted. She did not really mind but teased us. Nothing sexual, but it was good fun, and lingering kisses.<br /> <br /> Juliette and then Calamity returned, and we watched Stasia\u2019s movies. Juliette had done an intelligence test, then boxing! Calamity had been drag racing! An exciting day.<br /> <br /> The movies were good. DEBS was a spy movie where the villain and the lead spy fall in love, and both are women, giving it a very queer feeling. The girl with the faux French accent was very attractive but her accent was grating. Others found her funny, though, and the \u201cFrengish\u201d comment was funny. I of course do not speak Frenglish. Luna became a fan when Erasure was played. Overall, it was a good movie.<br /> <br /> Girltrash! All Night Long was the other movie. It was full of queer women. It had a run to a band competition, and a romance. I really enjoyed it. Very good characters and wonderful songs. Some was a bit sad, but overall a very cheerful movie, and the girls were cute. I think we all had favorites. Daisy was very, very pretty\u2026she and Tyler were mine.<br /> <br /> That got people in the mood. Maria was very much turned on by it all, and she got the four of us to come to bed. The four of us, together, making love, as it was meant to be. I love all three of them more than I can ever say. There is a rightness when I am with them no one else, however wild, can ever match. Even Yvette.<br /> <br /> In the night, I found my way to the heart of the temple, it was to myself. I was the god of this temple, gazing in the eyes of my own statue.<br /> <br /> I was distracted at breakfast, but it was a very nice time. Mostly just general chatting; Juan Carlos was coming to visit Calamity. Of course, Juliette was excited, and not for the Razorhand. Still the power was in my head, and I was distracted. I was drawn into the vents for a while after we split up, until I felt the storm come. I went out\u2026.I felt the glamour surrounding me. I was growing more powerful. Rain and hail fell around me but not on me. Julia asked me to come back, but I had to finish. Then Juliette came out and I told her the same. They love me, but I had to commune. Then I had to dream. I told them to go down then laid down a bit.<br /> <br /> I walked up the steps of the temple, and I opened the door.<br /> <br /> After I woke, I came down during the show, and saw Veronica there, among other people. Angelica and Desiree were there, together, so I went to speak to them. They are something of a couple currently, not girlfriends but going out, spent most of the day together. I went and mentioned this to Calamity, who brought up her suspicions about several visitors. She also gave me good news about Juan Carlos, who was is looking to have her join the Family of Silent Nights. We discussed that, and she touched on the various newcomers. I managed to extract myself eventually\u2026she seemed very keen to discuss them, but my head was already swimming with waking dreams and waxing power.<br /> <br /> I spoke to Veronica, flirting, but left her to Juliette. I did introduce Julia. Juliette was mostly splitting her time between she and Juan Carlos, practically drooling on him. I think Veronica was unsure she was getting Juliette, so I nudged. She was interested in the two of us. Shy but intrigued. I had a word with Julia to ensure she was okay (she said she would pay a call on Flores) and we retired with Veronica. I am pleased to say we utterly overwhelmed her. She enjoyed endless bliss, until she could take no more and fainted. Then we made love a little, and fell asleep in each other\u2019s arms.<br /> <br /> In my dreams, I stood at the temple, to address my worshipers. I felt power fill me, as my destiny aligned me against the Gentry. When I awoke I felt powerful. I can achieve the destiny set before me by Mama Lion without joining her, or becoming one of Them.<br /> <br /> -o-o-o-o-o-o-o-o-o-o-<br /> <br /> JULIETTE IS FLYING!<br /> <br /> <i>End Sessions XCI</i><br /> <br /> Oh what needs discussing here?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aR4zXRdh73I\" target=\"_blank\">Girltrash! All Night Long</a> (trailer not even kinda safe for work) and <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xk3y6T-0NNc\" target=\"_blank\">D.E.B.S.</a>are two of my favorite movies, Girltrash especially. If you like Queer women, musicals, and stories of romance or rock and roll this punk rock musical might work for you. Related to the stillborn Youtube series, but the movie has a <i>dramatically</i> different tone (and is a musical). It also has all the members of, and features the lead singers of, Killola and the Dollyrots. DEBS is good too, of course, and has prominent cool straight female characters too, if that\u2019s your thing. I mean must both be good I don't usually link trailers <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So the whole group moved to Wyrd 7. Let\u2019s see what that meant, given many had Kiths not covered by <i>Equinox Road.</i><br /> <br /> <u>Lorelei</u><br /> <br /> Fairest: As per <i>Equinox Road</i><br /> <br /> Windwing: As per <i>Equinox Road</i>, plus Merit<br /> <br /> Minstrel: 9 again on Expression rolls when giving a musical performance<br /> <br /> Frailty: In addition to the compulsion to sing, when bound, Lorelei panics. She cannot make any meaningful attempt to escape unless she spends 1 Willpower, including Strength or Dexterity rolls, or using a Contract like Separation.<br /> <br /> Lori is meriting up her Windwing Blessing to be able to actually fly.<br /> <br /> Lori is working on joining the Pilgrims of the Endless Road.<br /> <br /> Minstrels are from <i>Night Horrors, Grim Fears</i>. The Pilgrims of the Endless Road are from<i> Swords at Dawn</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Calamity</u><br /> <br /> Darkling: As per <i>Equinox Road</i><br /> <br /> Razorhand: +1 Damage on her knife hand.<br /> <br /> Whisperwisp: Upon spending a Glamour, can whisper for an entire scene to a target, rather than once.<br /> <br /> Frailty: In addition to her allergy to innocent blood, Calamity is compelled to repair broken glass unless she spends 1 Willpower.<br /> <br /> Calamity is upgrading Hedgehog\u2019s Dilemma so she can spend 1 Glamour and withdraw her shards for a scene. On popping back out, they cause 1 Lethal damage. This is expected to be upgraded.<br /> <br /> In addition to being in the Sacred Band of the Golden Standard, Calamity is working on joining the Family of Silent Nights.<br /> <br /> Whisperwisps and Razorhands are from <i>Winter Masques</i>. The Family of Silent Nights are from<i> Dancers in the Dusk</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Jacob</u><br /> <br /> Elemental: As per <i>Equinox Road</i><br /> <br /> Snowskin: As per <i>Equinox Road</i><br /> <br /> Coyote: When spending a Willpower on Manipulation rolls, she can roll 5 dice instead of 3, like he does with Persuasion and Subterfuge.<br /> <br /> Frailty: In addition to being unable to harm children, Jacob has an allergy to hot or warm beverages, taking 1 Bashing per turn he drinks them.<br /> <br /> Jacob is not pursuing any other Entitlement beyond the Knighthood of Utmost Silence at this time.<br /> <br /> Coyote are from <i>Winter Masques</i>. The Knighthood of Utmost Silence is from <i>Lords of Summe</i>r.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Insincere Marguerite</u><br /> <br /> Darkling: As per <i>Equinox Road</i><br /> <br /> Tunnelgrub: As per <i>Equinox Road,</i> plus Merit<br /> <br /> Lurker: 9 again on Larceny rolls (redundant for her due to Professional Merit)<br /> <br /> Frailty: In addition to being unable to walk on bare earth in shoes, If any sort of tracker, noisemaker (like a bell) or anything similar is placed on her person, clothes, or pocket, she is unable to remove it, or compel anyone else to, unless she spends 1 Willpower. She can allow it to be removed, or request if the other party can reasonably decline.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite is meriting her Tunnelgrub Blessing so she can spend 1 Glamour and roll Stamina + Athletics and pass through any opening that will allow her, including under doors, through cracks, and through pipes, like the Puddle Merit from <b>Changeling: The Dreaming</b> (her second Sluagh Merit with Prehensile Tongue). When not active, she is treated as if she had spent a Glamour on Tunnelgrub. Note Tommy Rawhead already possessed this ability.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite has joined the Lost Pantheon.<br /> <br /> The Night (Moon) Court is from <i>Winter Masques</i>. Lurkers are from <i>Victorian Lost</i>. The Lost Pantheon is from <i>Lords of Summer</i>.<br /> <br /> I think it was mostly straightforward, but if there are Comments or Questions they are welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 09-24-2017, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-08T13:03:14-07:00","id":1148098,"title":"","content":"The Transformations setting in, the Motley process the changes, and meets guests from the Courts of the Dragon<br /> <br /> <i>Session XCII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Okay, I\u2019ve had a day to cool down and think about the regrowth of my wings and what that means, and I think I\u2019m just about in a place where I can talk about it rationally (or as rationally as I ever talk about anything, at any rate). It has to be a sign of my growing connection to the Wyrd. It\u2019s obviously a huge deal, with repercussions both for myself and for those who are close to me, and it almost certainly has a cost\u2026 but by and large I\u2019m choosing to view it as a positive development.<br /> <br /> So I stayed up there flapping and wheeling and looping all over the place for\u2026 actually, I\u2019m not sure exactly how long it was, but it was probably a couple of hours at least. I swooped down and landed in the parking lot when I saw Calamity arriving back from her morning meditations with White Maria. She looked\u2026 different, somehow, but I was kind of wrapped up in my own stuff at that point, so it took me a minute to figure out exactly <u><u>how</u></u> she looked different. Her shards were smooth and sleek, like finely honed blades instead of jagged shards sticking out higgledy-piggledy.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re flying,\u201d she said as I approached.<br /> <br /> I was a little out of breath and still kind of giddy, so I think I might have responded with some witty rejoinder along the lines of \u201cYuh-huh.\u201d Then I took in the state of her, and made my own observation. \u201cYour shards\u2026 they look\u2026 <u><u>healed</u></u>,\u201d I managed to pant out as the sweat poured down my face.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah,\u201d she agreed, \u201cand that\u2019s not all. Check this out!\u201d Then she sort of scrunched up her face for a second, and the shards retracted into her flesh. \u201cPretty cool, huh?\u201d she asked with a grin.<br /> <br /> I gave her a careful hug as a way of expressing my feelings. There was no danger of injury, since the shards had completely retracted\u2026 but they left blood spots on her skin, and I was still wearing the sweater Rowan had given me for Christmas. I absolutely <u><u>cannot</u></u> get bloodstains on that; it\u2019s irreplaceable.<br /> <br /> It wasn\u2019t just us, either. It looks like most of the motley has experienced an increased connection to the Wyrd, and it\u2019s manifesting in a variety of ways. Aside from Calamity and I (and Marguerite, who had to deal with whatever was going on with that storm), it wasn\u2019t immediately noticeable. In fact, I couldn\u2019t see much of a change in Luna and Julia at all, though Luna seemed particularly quiet and broody (even for her). D had gone even paler than she used to be, but it was a fairly subtle change. The frost has crept further down Jacob\u2019s arms, and his body temperature seems to have dropped significantly (by which I mean that he\u2019s actually cool to the touch now).<br /> <br /> Eventually I realized that with all of this talk about our motley and the Wyrd, we were neglecting our guests, and attempted to rectify that situation. It was getting pretty late by that point, though, and Veronica said she needed to head out. I opted to walk her to her car, and she accepted.<br /> <br /> \u201cSorry I\u2019ve been so distracted,\u201d I said as we walked, \u201cI had a really good time with you last night.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMe too,\u201d she said after a moment, \u201cand don\u2019t worry about it\u2026 what you\u2019re going through is enough to distract anyone.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo I\u2019ll see you again soon?\u201d I asked hopefully.<br /> <br /> \u201cSure,\u201d she said with a smile, \u201conly\u2026 probably not tonight. I can\u2019t spend <u><u>every</u></u> night here, can I? And I need to think some things through, and figure out who I am now.\u201d<br /> <br /> I took her by the shoulders and looked into her eyes. \u201cYou\u2019re Veronica,\u201d I said firmly.<br /> <br /> She rolled her eyes a bit. \u201cYou know that\u2019s not what I meant,\u201d she began.<br /> <br /> \u201cI know,\u201d I said, \u201cbut I think you needed to hear it anyway. What happened last night doesn\u2019t change who you are, Veronica, and I wouldn\u2019t have slept with you if I didn\u2019t like that person a lot. Still\u2026 I know it can be a lot to take in. I kind of agonized over taking that step myself, back in Arcadia. So take whatever time you need, and know that I\u2019m here if you need to talk, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay, thanks,\u201d she said as we reached her car. \u201cI guess\u2026 I guess I just need to think about a few things. It\u2019s kind of a familiar feeling, if you know what I mean. I mean, you and Insincere Marguerite were my first girls, but sometimes it seems like my life has been a series of flings like this\u2026 trying desperately to get close enough to make a connection with someone, to feel like I mean something, like people value me. It feels great while its happening, but then it\u2019s over and I start the whole process over again\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I blinked. \u201cHave you been reading my diary?\u201d I asked after a moment.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat?\u201d she asked, confused. \u201cNo, of course not\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt was a joke,\u201d I said to mollify her. \u201cI just meant that I\u2019ve had thoughts like that for most of my life. The language is a little different, but the meaning is the same.\u201d<br /> <br /> She really looked at me for a second, like maybe she thought I was teasing her or something, but in the end she seemed to be satisfied with what she saw. I feel like the two of us have even more in common than I\u2019d previously imagined; like we\u2019ve made a real connection. I can only hope that she feels the same. And no, I\u2019m not thinking of \u201cadding another girlfriend to the stable\u201d as D later oh-so-eloquently phrased it. I just think maybe I\u2019ve found a kindred spirit; someone who could be a true friend.<br /> <br /> I met Juan-Carlos as I was heading back inside, and he gave me a quick hug and kiss and promised that he would see me later that night, after he had taken care of some other business in the Freehold. I\u2019m glad he\u2019s getting things done; I\u2019d hate to think that D and I were monopolizing his time unfairly. On the other hand, I also hate the thought that he\u2019d pass through town without stopping by the Dream House to\u2026 \u201csay hello.\u201d<br /> <br /> As Sex Breakfast was winding down, I got a phone call. I glanced at the caller ID, expecting to see Jimmy or Peg\u2019s name\u2026 but much to my surprise the call was from Princess Jolie. I answered, and the Princess asked if she could drop by the Dream House to speak with the motley. I polled my nearest and dearest to see if they had plans (they didn\u2019t), and told her that would be fine. She said she\u2019d drop by in about half an hour, and I sprinted up the stairs, took a quick shower, blow-dried my hair, threw on a fetching dress, and touched up my make-up. I probably shouldn\u2019t have rushed so much; I finished and came downstairs with easily twelve seconds to spare.<br /> <br /> Turns out that we were scheduled to receive some unusual visitors at the show that night, and the Princess wanted to give us a heads-up. The background in a nutshell is that Viscount Augustine has been reaching out to the Directional Courts in L.A. in the hopes of forming an alliance of sorts against Hollywood. Though they\u2019ve been reluctant to agree to anything formal, they have sent someone to us as an emissary. Becky\u2019s been looking after this visitor quietly, and tonight she\u2019s going to bring her to the show. Jolie wanted to make sure that we knew what was at stake so that we could afford her every courtesy and keep an eye out for any potential threats.<br /> <br /> The emissary\u2019s name is Laughing Carp, and she\u2019s apparently a dragon\u2026 though she was described as almost unbearably cute (more thoughts on that later). She\u2019s friendly and easy-going to a fault, and she is a member of the Eastern Court, which focuses on the emotion of Envy. Well, thought Lorelei with a wink and a grin, I\u2019m sure I can provide for our guest on <u><u>that</u></u> account.<br /> <br /> Jolie also wanted to let us know that we had <u><u>another</u></u> visitor from the Directional Courts in town, and that she would likely grace the Dream House with her presence that night as well. Unfortunately, her business was not as pleasant as Laughing Carp\u2019s. Soon Hee Kwon is a professional monster hunter, and she\u2019s been dispatched by the Courts of the Dragon to take down some sort of Hedge beast. The current theory is that Hollywood has unleashed a shape-shifting, madness-aggravating creature to wreak havoc upon the Lady By the Sea Freehold. This creature apparently isn\u2019t very <u><u>good</u></u> at assuming the identities of others\u2026 but Ms. Kwon is a stranger here, so it might be difficult for her to ascertain if someone is acting strangely. Hence, she decided to drop by the Dream House to get the lay of the land. She\u2019s a member of the Western Court, which focuses on Honor. Now what the hell kind of song could inspire <u><u>that</u></u> emotion in mortals, I wonder?<br /> <br /> We thanked Jolie for the heads-up, and I walked her out (seems to be my job lately, doesn\u2019t it?). As we paused in the foyer, I sort of shrugged and decided to take the plunge. \u201cSo\u2026 I can fly now,\u201d I said plaintively, spreading my wings a bit so she could take in the new look.<br /> <br /> Her face broke into a guileless grin. \u201cThat\u2019s great!\u201d she said, taking my hands in her own. \u201cI know how much you\u2019ve missed it, Lori. I just\u2026 I hope it doesn\u2019t come at too high a cost.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat do you\u2026 oh,\u201d I said as her words sunk in. \u201cRight. Frailties. I hadn\u2019t thought about that,\u201d I admitted.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt still shouldn\u2019t be anything too severe,\u201d Jolie hastened to assure me, \u201cthough if you get much more powerful\u2026 well, let me just say that the little problem your motley helped me with\u2026 hadn\u2019t always been a problem.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll be careful,\u201d I said. \u201cHonestly, now that I can <u><u>really</u></u> fly again, I don\u2019t particularly care if I get any more powerful\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMight not be your choice, unfortunately,\u201d Jolie lamented. \u201cBut hey, I\u2019m here for you if you need any advice, or sympathy, or just an attentive ear. Okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay,\u201d I said. We kissed on the doorstep, and she took her leave.<br /> <br /> So I had no sooner returned to the kitchen when my phone rang <u><u>again</u></u>, and this time it <u><u>was</u></u> Jimmy Squarefoot. \u201c\u2019Allo, Pet,\u201d he said when I answered. It\u2019s sometimes hard to tell with him, but he sounded a little disconsolate to me.<br /> <br /> \u201cHi, Jimmy,\u201d I said brightly. \u201cWhat can I do for you today? Skiing? Escape room? High-stakes poker?\u201d<br /> <br /> He chuckled a bit at that, which had been my real goal with the suggestions. \u201cActually, just callin\u2019 to let you know that we won\u2019t be testin\u2019 you today, Pet. Peg\u2019s gone off to see her family, and I\u2019m\u2026 not so welcome \u2018round their place.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh,\u201d I said, not really knowing what else to add. \u201cSo\u2026 what are you up to today?\u201d<br /> <br /> He seemed genuinely surprised by my interest, but after a moment he replied. \u201cFigured I\u2019d just drive around town for a bit, and take in the sights like,\u201d he said.<br /> <br /> That sounded pretty depressing to me, and of course I couldn\u2019t just let it stand. \u201cYou\u2019re welcome to drop by here,\u201d I said brightly. \u201cWe could, I dunno, play video games or watch a movie or something. Whatever you want.\u201d<br /> <br /> There was a pause. \u201cYou sure, Pet?\u201d he asked. \u201cI wouldn\u2019t want to put you out\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNonsense,\u201d I fired back immediately, \u201cyou\u2019re always welcome here, Jimmy. I don\u2019t like the thought of you wandering around lonely all day.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell,\u201d he said after considering the offer, \u201cthat\u2019s awful decent of you, Pet. If you\u2019re sure you don\u2019t mind\u2026 I\u2019ll drop by for a bit.\u201d<br /> <br /> So about twenty minutes later he showed up at the door, looking as sheepish as I\u2019ve ever seen him. \u201cThanks for havin\u2019 me, Miss Grace,\u201d he said as I welcomed him into the house. \u201cLike I said before, Peg\u2019s off to see her people, so I figured I\u2019d make myself scarce. They\u2019ve got a wee bairn,\u201d he said by way of explanation.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s\u2026 a child, right?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> He nodded. \u201cNo sense scarin\u2019 the poor kid. \u2018Sides, Peg\u2019s da don\u2019t much care for me. Thinks I\u2019m just tryin\u2019 to marry posh,\u201d he said conspiratorially. Well, I don\u2019t know about that \u2013 I probably wouldn\u2019t characterize Peg as \u201cposh\u201d for one thing \u2013 but I know how it can be when things are tense between you and your paramour\u2019s family. Hell, I\u2019ve never even met D\u2019s people, and I said as much.<br /> <br /> We commiserated about that for a while until the love of my life swaggered into the room. \u201cSo, Squarefoot,\u201d she said cockily, \u201cwant to punch the shit out of each other for a while?\u201d<br /> <br /> He got this sort of gleam in his eye. \u201cAye,\u201d he said as he rose, \u201cI might be able to accommodate you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou two have fun,\u201d I said as they moved toward the door. <br /> <br /> He turned back to face me. \u201cI hate to put you out any more, like, but\u2026 think I might be able to stay for dinner, too?\u201d<br /> <br /> That seemed to come out of nowhere, but I wasn\u2019t about to turn him away. \u201cThink you\u2019ll work up an appetite, eh? I guess I can whip something up in the kitchen, like\u2026 I dunno, steak and kidney pie or something.\u201d It was the first vaguely British dish I thought of, and I just blurted it out.<br /> <br /> Jimmy graced me with a look of such gratitude that I felt my heart sinking like a stone. \u201cAye, Pet,\u201d he said with a guileless smile, \u201cthat sounds a right treat, if I\u2019m not puttin\u2019 you out, like.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo trouble,\u201d I laughed sort of nervously as they headed out to the backyard. Where the hell is Gawain when you need him, right? Half a minute later I burst into Calamity\u2019s office in a panic. \u201cI need to figure out how to cook steak and kidney pie in the next two hours or so,\u201d I said, hysteria edging in.<br /> <br /> Calamity grinned. \u201cTo the Internet!\u201d she proclaimed like Sherlock Holmes when the game was afoot.<br /> <br /> A few minutes later, armed with a printed recipe, we checked the freezer and discovered to our mutual astonishment that we actually had most of what was required for the dish, and what we didn\u2019t have we could improvise with similar ingredients. Lucky for me I live in a house with a very well-stocked kitchen\u2026 and one which recently housed a British expatriate. Between Calamity and I we managed to get everything assembled and simmering on the stove within about half an hour of starting. It took about ninety minutes to cook the filling, and then another half hour or so to bake the crust. While it was baking, I mashed some potatoes and Calamity steamed some mixed vegetables.<br /> <br /> D and Jimmy came in from the backyard as things were cooling on the counter, looking exhausted but pleased with themselves. They were bruised and battered, but this had been a friendly match, and Jimmy had provided the necessary healing magic.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou went five minutes with this guy, babe?\u201d D asked me, obviously impressed. \u201cHe hits like a truck!\u201d<br /> <br /> Jimmy chuckled. \u201cLook who\u2019s talkin\u2019,\u201d he muttered fondly. \u201cYou gave me a hell of a workout, lass.\u201d Then he took a deep breath through his nose, and his eyes widened. \u201cI thought you was jokin\u2019 before\u2026 that smells wonderful, it does!\u201d<br /> <br /> So we sat down and enjoyed the tasty \u2013 if somewhat heavy \u2013 British dish together. At some point Marguerite came downstairs wearing that t-shirt with her own face on it, but she took one sniff of the kitchen and turned up her nose at the fare, expressing her opinion that the Revolutionary War had really been an attempt by the American colonies to get <u><u>away</u></u> from British cuisine and leaving with an adorable \u201chrmph.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jimmy said goodbye after that and ran off to meet Peg, and the rest of us set about preparing for the show. I was a little worried that the rich food would sit heavily in my stomach, but I seem to have worked past it by the time curtain rolled around. Calamity and I did the \u201cBloody Creature Poster Girl\u201d number again at her request, but I only had one solo act. Well, sorta solo, in any case\u2026 Roberta backed me up with that amazing deep voice of hers. It was an emotional number from the 80s called \u201cTotal Eclipse of the Heart,\u201d by Bonnie Tyler. I remember how big \u201cIt\u2019s a Heartache\u201d was when I was Taken\u2026 I always knew she\u2019d go far.<br /> <br /> In any case, in order to stir up some Envy glamour for our guest, I headed out into the audience and performed mostly from the stage of Juan-Carlos\u2019 lap. I figured just about everybody in the audience was probably envious of at least <u><u>one</u></u> of us.<br /> <br /> I spoke with our esteemed guests briefly after my second number, joining Calamity at their table. Laughing Carp is\u2026 well, the only word I can think of to describe her is <u><u>adorable</u></u>. She was bubbly and friendly and eager to please, and I felt myself liking her immediately. Calamity was clearly flirting with her \u2013 whether due to legitimate attraction or out of some desire to hurt Becky I don\u2019t know \u2013 so I decided to play the wingman (ha!) and keep things light between us. Besides, I already had plans for the evening.<br /> <br /> Soon Hee Kwon, on the other hand, has definite potential. She comes across as a real badass; a no-nonsense sort of ass-kicker. Leather jacket, steely gaze, and in-your-face attitude. I\u2019m very familiar with the type\u2026 I\u2019m marrying one of them next month, after all. Unfortunately, after a minute or two of pleasantries, her attention seemed to wander from me back to Calamity. I threw a few flirts her way later in the conversation, and she seemed receptive\u2026 so maybe she had just decided that I wasn\u2019t a threat and turned her attention in more \u201cdangerous\u201d directions. <br /> <br /> I offered to introduce her around, and she started asking questions. Well, one question, mainly. She wanted to know who might be targeted if someone wanted to destabilize the Freehold. A number of possibilities occurred to me: the monarchs, of course, and Becky, and Monica, for starters. The only person I could think of who she hadn\u2019t already met was Joan, though. She still thanked me for the information, and we closed the evening on good terms.<br /> <br /> I also spoke briefly with Dominika, and thanked her once again for the healing she gave me on Monday. She waved off my thanks and told me that she was glad to help, and we spent a few minutes discussing Peg and Jimmy. Apparently Dominika has a hard time understanding their accents. I don\u2019t know if living with Ace for a year left me better prepared to handle that particular challenge or not\u2026 his Liverpudlian drawl doesn\u2019t sound much like their nasal Northern speech to me, honestly.<br /> <br /> So things began to wind down around that point, and I eventually meandered over to the table from which Juan-Carlos and D were throwing me impatient glances (well, okay, that was mostly D; Juan-Carlos was playing it cool). I sidled up with a smile and allowed the Latin stud to kiss my hand.<br /> <br /> \u201cBuenos noches, mi sirena,\u201d he said, making me blush. \u201cDo you have plans for this evening?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cUh huh,\u201d I said, nodding and displaying my refinement. \u201cI was going to let you and my fianc\u00e9e carry me up to the bedroom so that the three of us can spend the whole evening engaging in a series of exhausting debauched sex acts.\u201d<br /> <br /> He looked over at D and quirked an eyebrow. \u201cAnd you, my dear? Is Lorelei\u2019s proposal to your liking as well?\u201d<br /> <br /> D shrugged and grinned like a shark. \u201cNothing good on TV tonight,\u201d she said after a few seconds.<br /> <br /> He sighed in mock exasperation. \u201cIt would seem that I am at your mercy, ladies,\u201d he said with apparent resignation as he swept an arm under me and picked me up lightly. \u201cLead on, I am at your disposal. I ask only that you leave enough of me to stagger from your bed tomorrow morning; there are still those within this Freehold who require my aid.\u201d<br /> <br /> D and I both swore scouts\u2019 honor that we\u2019d be good (hmmm\u2026 D in a girl scout\u2019s uniform? I\u2019ll have to think about that one), and then let our passions take the lead. Did we show him a good time? Of course we did. Did we wear him out? Yes, but we got no complaints from the gentleman in question. Have D and I re-confirmed our occasionally-in-question bisexuality? A big fat yeppers to that!<br /> <br /> So I let the two of them drift off, then picked up a medical journal and started to study. After an hour or so of that, I started writing this journal. But now Juan-Carlos is awake, and he\u2019s beckoning quietly for me to rejoin him and D in the bed, and I think I might just take him up on that offer. The idea of making every moment count has its merit\u2026 but there\u2019s also something to be said for taking the time to lie back and luxuriate in the arms of people who care about you, too. Especially after a workout like that.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Well this morning was certainly interesting. Lori had gotten up early and was actually flying outside my window. Flying! Not just gliding down to the ground, but actually flying. I guessed at that point that at least one other person in the motley had grown in power as well. So, I figured I\u2019d go ahead and get up and make coffee. I made myself a cup and as soon as I took a sip I got burned. I\u2019m usually good with hot coffee. It was one of the treats I had when I worked for the Lady and I came to \u2018the world.\u2019 This morning though it was just too hot. I tried cooling it down by increments and found that anything warmer than room temperature was too hot for me. Now since room temperature coffee is gross, I just added ice to mine and made it iced coffee. I will admit that I was a little disappointed. Hot coffee kind of served to warm me up. It was a treat. Like apples used to be when I was in the Lady\u2019s service. Now though, hot coffee is out of the question. At least apples are still an option.<br /> <br /> Eventually everyone came in for breakfast. Calamity got back from her sparring with White Maria and Lori flew down to meet her. They walked in together. The others joined us soon enough. Veronica and Juan Carlos were guests this morning. I think Veronica stayed with Lori and Insincere Marguerite and Juan Carlos stayed with De La Rocha. Veronica seemed a little embarrassed but okay other than that. The group of us started talking about how we\u2019d changed overnight. Lori was particularly excited about being able to fly now. Calamity\u2019s glass seems to have evened out a bit. It is smooth and sharp now instead of being jagged and sharp. It\u2019s more like knives. She can also retract the glass if she concentrates on it. It leaves wounds when she lets the glass back out, but for a short while she can be assured that she won\u2019t accidentally cut anyone. Insincere Marguerite didn\u2019t look changed to me, but then she did have a \u201cconversation\u201d with a storm yesterday, so something is different there. I could not tell how Julia had changed, but De La Rocha looked paler than usual. Luna did not look changed to me either, but her demeanor was off so I\u2019m assuming that there was something different. I told myself that I\u2019d talk to her later about that. As for myself, I told folks that my temperature had gone down and everyone in the motley leaned over to touch my arm and feel for themselves. Lori even commented that my frost came further down my arms than it had in the past.<br /> <br /> I will admit that I was a little disturbed by my own changes. I was trying not to think about it earlier this morning when I was snuggling with Luna, but things came back all at once and I felt uneasy all over again. My power has been increasing lately and I\u2019m getting closer and closer to what I was when I worked for the Lady. I guess I pray that the changes are only skin deep because I do not want to become Rime again. I care for my friends and do not want to go back to being the unconcerned person I used to be. The physical changes just serve to remind me of him though. As Rime I was cold in attitude and in actual temperature. I had frost over a good bit of my body and I had greater control over snow and ice than I do now. I haven\u2019t really used my snow powers lately. Not since the camping trip when I made it snow for a couple of hours. I miss it. The snow and ice. I find myself missing it and I don\u2019t know if that\u2019s just because I grew up where we had a distinct cold winter, or if it\u2019s because I\u2019m getting closer to and closer to Rime. I don\u2019t feel particularly different, aside from the temperature thing. I still feel like I did yesterday and the day before. It is hard to be objective though. I could be changing slowly and not even realize it. I trust Luna and the others to let me know if I go too far though, so I guess I\u2019m still okay.<br /> <br /> Somehow, we did get on the topic of seasons in California, or I should say the lack of seasons in California. Julia attests that there are distinct seasons, but I don\u2019t see it. It\u2019s just warm all the time. There are times it\u2019s warm and dry and times it\u2019s warm and a little less dry. I don\u2019t understand all the people walking around in December with jackets on. It\u2019s still like 60+ degrees outside. That\u2019s nice and warm in my book. Granted my \u201cbook\u201d may be a bit skewed, but I contend that 60 is still on the warm side. Lori at least agrees with me. She admits that California does not have seasons. She grew up in the Midwest, so she had her fair share of snow in the winter. She however likes the weather here. Veronica was also reminiscing about snow. I think she comes from somewhere near where Lori grew up. Speaking for myself though, I miss seasons. And I would still miss them even if I wasn\u2019t an ice-aspected elemental.<br /> <br /> So, after our guests left Calamity let her glass come back out and Lori healed the resulting wounds. She also told us why Juan Carlos had come by the Dream House the other night. He was here to induct Calamity into the Family of the Silent Night. I could tell that she felt awkward about that since Dream Healing was Gawain\u2019s thing and that was his entitlement before he left. Calamity has done her own good bit of Dream Healing and I believe that she deserves the honor of being in that group.<br /> <br /> After that little revelation things got a little more interesting. Princess Jolie called and said that she needed to talk to us. Lori in particular, but she didn\u2019t mind if the rest of us where there. So, she came over about half an hour after she called. She told us that we, as a freehold, were hosting a representative from one of the Directional Courts and she would be coming by the Dream House tonight. Her name is Laughing Carp. Apparently, she is a Draconic Swimmerskin. I think she\u2019s part dragon is what it comes down to. Becky has been acting as a bodyguard to Laughing Carp so far. In addition to our diplomat, we also have another visitor from L.A. called Soon Hee Kwan. She is a monster hunter from what I understand. She is here hunting down a Hedge Beast that was set loose on us by Hollywood. This beast can mimic people, but is not perfect, so if you know someone well you will likely pick up on the fact that they are acting off if they have been replaced. Apparently this beast\u2019s main goal is to sow discord amongst groups and can cause some people to plunge into a dreamscape if they have a less than stable hold on their sanity to begin with. All Changelings are a little bit crazy, but if we stay away from people, humans, too much we tend to become more fae and lose our grip on reality. I like to think that I have gained back a bit of that in the past few months. Well, I did until I woke up this morning with a lower body temperature than usual. I don\u2019t know what\u2019s going on with me.<br /> <br /> So, we talked about Hedge Beasts and visiting Directional Courtiers for a bit until Lori got a phone call from Jimmy Squarefoot. They will not be doing any testing today since Peg is with her sister and niece for the day. Lori felt bad when he said he\u2019d be driving around town alone, so she invited him over to the Dream House to watch a movie or something. He arrived a little while later and after a short talk with De La Rocha decided to forgo the movie in favor of trying to knock each out in the back yard. I\u2019d say they were going to spar, but they were hitting far harder than I usually do when I spar with someone. They were leaving bruises. They seemed to be enjoying themselves immensely, so who am I to complain? Before the duo went outside to punch the shit out of each other Lori joked about making steak and kidney pie since they\u2019d likely be hungry after sparring. Jimmy seemed interested in that idea, so while the duo was hitting each other Lori went to Calamity for help in finding a recipe for steak and kidney pie. Then they started cooking.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile Luna was upstairs getting painted by Julia. I watched for a good bit of the time. Luna seemed a little off to me and I wanted to keep her company today if I could. Julia herself was in a really good mood and did a wonderful job on the painting. After they were done I took Luna aside and asked her if she was okay. I had noticed her acting a little more broody than usual and wanted to make sure. Everything was alright. She said that she was in the process of reconciling the beast side of her and the human side of her personality and that she\u2019s still off kilter today. I guess she also increased in strength along with the rest of us and it\u2019s making the beast side stronger, just like it made my elemental side stronger. I told her that I would be here if she needed to talk and that she could tell me anything. I hope she knows that I mean it. I hope that they all know that they can come to me if they need to talk. I\u2019m sometimes, okay most times, not the best at social situations, but I do my best to be supportive. I will do whatever I need to, to keep my motley safe and happy.<br /> <br /> After painting and sparring we all gathered in the kitchen to eat British food. Insincere Marguerite made a cute little noise and walked out of the kitchen. I guess British food is not in agreement with her French sensibilities. The rest of us tried the Steak and Kidney pie and found it to be pretty good. While we ate we talked and joked around. There was something about Insincere Marguerite using her tongue to hollow out a loaf of hard bread, which led to questions about whether someone\u2019s tongue would stick to me since I\u2019m cooler now. I said that they wouldn\u2019t, I\u2019m not that cold. There was also a joke about gluing me to the Dream House since I\u2019m the last guy left here. All the others have left. It was all very silly, and I\u2019m sure that Jimmy got an interesting look at the inner workings of her motley. Hopefully that\u2019s a good thing for Lori.<br /> <br /> The show tonight went off great, as usual. The ladies did really well and wowed the crowd, including our new guests. After their acts Calamity and Lori started making their rounds through the crowd. Calamity went to talk to Becky, which had to have been awkward, and with Laughing Carp and Soon Hee Kwan. There was flirting from what I could see. Calamity seemed cordial to Becky and flirted with Laughing Carp. Lori arrived a little while later and the pair of them did their best to make a good impression on our L.A guests.<br /> <br /> I will admit that I got distracted from watching that group when Molly asked me a question. She wanted my opinion on something. She said that she is curious about who she used to be before the \u201cTable\u201d was used to change her. Her current self is only a little over a year old and she doesn\u2019t have the same experiences that shape a person as the rest of us do. She wanted to know what kind of person she used to be. She said that it might be possible to find out what she used to be like by doing Dream Healing or something similar. I was a little unsure what to say at first, but then thought about it. If I was in her shoes I would be really curious about who and what I used to be too. I mean, it wasn\u2019t just her personality that was erased. She used to be a different type of Changeling altogether. I think she used to be a beast of some sort. Her whole being was changed. If that had happened to me I would want to know about my old self. The danger, I guess, lies in the fact that she used to be a Loyalist. As cautious as that might make me I don\u2019t think that she would completely go back to being her old self if she found out who she used to be. She has been Molly for a while now and is starting to find an identity with that name and her current job. Hell, I used to be a loyalist. I know who I was before and I know who I am now. I\u2019ve only been \u201cJacob\u201d for a little over a year too. I was Rime for a good deal longer than that before, and I haven\u2019t gone back to being him even though I know about him. I told her that I can introduce her to Sullivan, my therapist, and we can see if he can help her. We made plans to meet up before I got to my session in the morning. I did remind her that I like who she is now. She has the right to find out who she used to be, but I wanted her to know that we like her as she is regardless.<br /> <br /> Talking with Molly about her dilemma made me think about myself, and I guess the rest of the motley for that matter. It is true that we all used to be someone different before we were taken. Arcadia changed us all. Forged us in good and bad ways to be someone new. Some of us accepted our new state while others fought tooth and nail to remain who they were. Calamity fought so hard to remain Kat. She did all she could to remember her friend Stasia and to retain some scrap of who she used to be. And in a living hell, she managed to do it. She came out the other side different. She is a far darker person than she used to be, but there is still a part of Kat within her and I think Stasia really helps to bring that out. Lori was forcibly changed to be a Keeper\u2019s prize. A Treasure. She was made to be a songbird, and she accepted and embraced that. Since she escaped she has recognized these changes and uses them to her benefit. No one can deny that she is an excellent singer. Julia, I don\u2019t know as much about. She is an exceptional artist and I think she used those skills to escape Arcadia. Insincere Marguerite is a better person than she used to be, before she was taken. She admits this. She does have a clingy side now, which makes her want to hold onto those she loves. Some might say that she is a bit too clingy, but she is managing it. De La Rocha also has her dark side. Maria. She has a tight rein over her darker impulses. I\u2019m not sure how much she has truly accepted the darker side of herself, but she is trying and that is all any of us can do. My sweet Luna was completely remade when she was in Arcadia. She used to be a different person altogether. A different gender, a different being. I happen to like who she is now. I know that she has her own dark side. She channels it well though. Keeping poachers out of her forest does wonders for her mood. Maybe I should suggest we have some sport soon. Then there is me. I was not changed for the better when I was in Arcadia. I embraced the darker side of my nature. I embraced the cold and the dark and I became Hers. I don\u2019t know how she did it, but one Treasure, one woman woke me up. She helped me remember who I used to be. She helped me decide to leave the Lady. I can\u2019t deny who I used to be. It has shaped who I am now. What I am now. I just hope that Molly finds some meaning in who she used to be, but continues to embrace who she is now. We are all of us changed, and sometimes not for the better, but we have embraced that change. I hope she does too. I like who my friend is now. I don\u2019t want to see her leave, in any way, but it\u2019s not fair to deny her the truth either.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XCII</i><br /> <br /> Jimmy wanted dinner to use Contracts of Stone to heal from his punch out. De La Rocha took advantage of the meal to do the same.<br /> <br /> And we meet two very different Draconics. Laughing Carp was adapted from a character I had in Scion as an NPC. She is fun to play. The Courts of the Dragon corresponds to Chinatown. The fourth major court in the area is covered\u2026White Maria had mentioned them before.<br /> <br /> The group continues growing into their new skins next time. Join us then. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T21:22:31-07:00","id":1149306,"title":"","content":"I remember Laughing Carp. Ah the memories.<br /> <br /> No Calamity or Marguerite?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T22:26:52-07:00","id":1149317,"title":"","content":"Oh, right you would <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Awesome.<br /> <br /> Nah, due to extra work hours and writing burnout, respectively. They will return.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T00:06:57-07:00","id":1149334,"title":"","content":"Indeed.<br /> <br /> Whenever they can. This is a luxury after all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> What an earlier comment. The Harem thing I was referring to was the Planet Neko and subverted harem setup that the Keeper does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T13:36:48-07:00","id":1152008,"title":"","content":"Ah gotcha.<br /> <br /> In their new more powerful forms, our heroes set to their various goals. A plan is decided upon, new acts are done, and a decision is made by an old friend.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XCIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> This has been an\u2026 \u201cintriguing\u201d twenty-four hours. Most of it has been very pleasant (to say the least), but I\u2019ve also got a lot to think about. The time has been set for my final testing by the Pilgrims of the Endless Road, so I now have yet <u><u>another</u></u> event coming up in mid-June to stress over in addition to two weddings \u2013 one of which is my own \u2013 a honeymoon, and the planned excursion into Arcadia to rescue Missy and Jane. And speaking of that\u2026 well, shit\u2019s about to get real, as the kids are apparently saying these days.<br /> <br /> So I woke up yesterday morning when D tried to subtly wriggle out from between Juan-Carlos and myself so that she could meet Calamity and Jacob for their therapy session. My memories of that particular scene are a bit fuzzy; I know that I kissed her and put a hand on her hip and tried to get her to stay with the two of us, but she was adamant, saying something about how she was only doing the therapy in the first place because she\u2019d promised me that she would, and she wasn\u2019t going to break that promise. She left me with another kiss, and pushed me gently into Juan-Carlos\u2019 embrace, and then she was gone and I fell back into a peaceful slumber.<br /> <br /> I woke up yet again a few hours later with the smell of brewing coffee in my nose and Juan-Carlos\u2019 hands on my waist. His lips were at my throat and, well\u2026 one thing led to another. We made slow, sensual, comfortable love for a little while, which was a nice change from the previous evening\u2019s vigorous pounding. Once we\u2019d both been satisfied, he got dressed, I threw on a robe, and we made our way downstairs to breakfast.<br /> <br /> Calamity was making crepes.<br /> <br /> I\u2026 for a minute I didn\u2019t know what to say. I didn\u2019t want to call attention to it, honestly. Crepes were sort of Gawain\u2019s thing, and we haven\u2019t had them at the Dream House since he left more than four months ago. I hope this means that she\u2019s moving on\u2026 and I think maybe it does. Marguerite quietly praised her culinary endeavor after the first bite, and her response was a sober \u201cI thought it was time.\u201d<br /> <br /> Dominika had spent the previous evening with Julia and Marguerite\u2026 or so I thought at first. She seemed a little put out about something, and when Marguerite said that she needed to talk to the motley after Sex Breakfast, our Caribbean friend left in sort of a huff. Julia gave Marguerite a meaningful look, and the latter followed Dominika out to set things straight. When I asked about it, Julia just said that Marguerite had spent the evening alone in the vents, and Dominika was maybe a little insulted by her lack of interest. Makes sense to me.<br /> <br /> After our guests had said their farewells (Juan-Carlos had business in San Diego today, but will be back tomorrow to speak with Calamity about the entitlement thing), Marguerite asked us to adjourn to a room where we could speak comfortably for a while. Then she dropped a bombshell on us: she\u2019d spent most of last night planning the best way to rescue my friends from the domain of the Violet Empress.<br /> <br /> She came up with two plans. The first was more straightforward, but \u2013 in Marguerite\u2019s opinion \u2013 less likely to succeed. We would travel as a group, slip into the palace as unobtrusively as possible, take out any resistance as quickly and quietly as we could, and then secure the girls and slip out again, hopefully avoiding the Empress\u2019 notice entirely. Marguerite was a little vague on the details, but she asserted that over-planning such an endeavor would leave little room for improvisation when unexpected complications inevitably crop up.<br /> <br /> The second plan will be more dangerous, but Marguerite believes it will be more likely to succeed. In this plan, we split up into several groups. Jacob and Luna will attempt to quietly take out the guards at the front gate of the palace. Calamity will seek out and incapacitate Hunting Hawk so that the Empress will be unable to send him after us when she realizes what has happened. Julia will be our rearguard, preferably waiting just outside of the Empress\u2019 domain and preparing to paint us an exit if possible. Marguerite, D, and I will slip into the palace itself, free Missy and Jane, convince them to accompany us, and head out.<br /> <br /> Marguerite looked at me seriously and asked if I trusted her. Of course I answered in the affirmative. \u201cBon,\u201d she said after a moment, \u201cbecause this plan will require you to show more trust in me than you have ever needed to before.\u201d<br /> <br /> She went on to explain that she has a magic sack. Since neither D nor I could ever hope to match Marguerite when it comes to stealth, she wants to put us both in the sack and transport us past the Empress\u2019 security safely. She\u2019ll remove us when she reaches Missy and Jane, at which point all <u><u>four</u></u> of us will re-enter the sack while she sneaks us out again.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m\u2026 not wild about this part of the plan, to be honest. I\u2019ve made no secret of the fact that I don\u2019t like being bound or confined in any way. But I <u><u>have</u></u> to be there when Marguerite meets Missy and Jane. I\u2019m the only one they might trust enough to leave the cage. And there\u2019s no way D will leave me alone in that realm, so she\u2019s got to be there too. Besides, as Marguerite pointed out, if we have to muscle Missy and Jane into the sack, D\u2019s our girl. I really hope it doesn\u2019t come to that, though.<br /> <br /> Marguerite assures me that being in the sack won\u2019t be like being locked in a small room or anything like that. D and I should be in a comfortable form of stasis, to hear her talk\u2026 not incapacitated but in a sort of dreamlike state. It doesn\u2019t sound so bad, but getting in there in the first place\u2026 no. If this is the best way to rescue Missy and Jane, then I\u2019ll get past my problems. I\u2019ll <u><u>make</u></u> myself do it, if I have to. Maybe I can take D and Marguerite up on their offer to get on the St. Andrew\u2019s Cross at some point to sort of test the waters. I don\u2019t like it, but I should probably get used to the idea in a comfortable setting before we have to do it for real in Arcadia.<br /> <br /> Still, whenever I\u2019ve pictured \u201chopping in the sack with D\u201d following our wedding, this is <u><u>not</u></u> how I\u2019ve imagined it.<br /> <br /> Marguerite feels that this is the best plan because it acknowledges our established roles within the Wyrd\u2026 we\u2019re playing our assigned parts, I suppose. Marguerite is a stealthy burglar. D is my strong protector. I am the silver-tongued diplomat. Jacob and Luna are our ambush predators. Julia is the mystical artist. Calamity is the deadly assassin.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Calamity, Marguerite\u2019s original plan had Julia backing her up when she fought Hunting Hawk. I was the one who suggested that Julia might be better employed securing our exit, considering how she originally escaped Arcadia. Marguerite thought that was a peachy keen idea, and turned to ask Calamity if she was comfortable fighting Hunting Hawk alone.<br /> <br /> She nodded, a serious look on her face. \u201cI\u2019m not going to fight him,\u201d she explained calmly, \u201cI\u2019m going to murder him from the shadows.\u201d<br /> <br /> I\u2019m\u2026 not sure how to feel about that. I <u><u>hate</u></u> the idea of killing someone unnecessarily\u2026 but I think this might <u><u>be</u></u> necessary in the long run. And I\u2019m willing to compromise my principles if it means rescuing my friends, and making good on the promises we all made before I left them to rot in that place. So I just nodded and didn\u2019t say anything.<br /> <br /> And with that, the serious talk was over. Marguerite mentioned an act that she wanted to debut that night; I heard her out and gave my approval for her to go ahead with it. People started to disperse after that, and I made my way to the roof alone. D asked where I was going, but didn\u2019t follow me when I told her, and I\u2019m grateful for that. I don\u2019t know what to think about all of this. It\u2019s really going to happen, and I think we have a good chance of making it work\u2026 but I still had a lot to think about. The possibility that Missy and Jane are lost to us by now. The probable murder of my one-time tormentor, Hunting Hawk. The sack. The Empress. I\u2019m going back\u2026 back to Her. It\u2019s a lot to take in.<br /> <br /> So I sat perched on the edge of the roof, brooding (if you\u2019ll excuse the expression). I was only up there for about half an hour, however, when my phone rang. I glanced down at the caller ID and saw that it was Peg, so I answered immediately.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou ready for your final assessment challenge, Pet?\u201d she asked once the pleasantries were out of the way.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou betcha,\u201d I answered brightly. Honestly, most of their tests have been sort of fun, and I had no reason to expect this one to be any different.<br /> <br /> \u201cThere\u2019s an old closed-down shopping centre on the other side of Santa Monica. Some of the locals have helped us set up a\u2026 well, let\u2019s call it an obstacle course for now. We\u2019d like to see what you make of it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSure thing,\u201d I said. \u201cJust text me the address and I\u2019ll get dressed and head on over. Depending on traffic, I can probably be there in, say\u2026 thirty minutes or so?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBrilliant,\u201d she said. \u201cWe\u2019ll see you then.\u201d<br /> <br /> So I let the others know where I was going, threw on a modest workout outfit, and drove across town. Peg and Jimmy met me at the entrance\u2026 and they were accompanied by two people I knew at once. Halley looked excited about something, and fidgeted throughout the conversation that followed. Twitch looked nervous\u2026 but then, Twitch almost <u><u>always</u></u> looks nervous about something.<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay, Pet,\u201d Jimmy said as I approached the small group, \u201cyour friends here have helped us set up a series of obstacle courses, mostly in the access hallways between the stores of this shopping centre. We want to see what you can make of them. Each hallway will contain a series of mobile lasers. They\u2019ll all move in different fixed patterns. Touchin\u2019 one of the lasers won\u2019t hurt you in any way, but it\u2019ll alert us to your presence and location, and freeze the simulation for five minutes. If you trip any of the lasers, you can either wait five minutes for it to start up again, or start over from the beginnin\u2019\u2026 your choice. The four of us will also be stationed in those hallways, keepin\u2019 an eye out for you, like. We want you to try to get through the whole course without trippin\u2019 any of the laser sensors or gettin\u2019 spotted by any of us. Understand?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYup,\u201d I said, \u201csounds like fun.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAny questions before we begin?\u201d Peg asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cJust one,\u201d I said after thinking about it for a moment. \u201cAre you placing any restrictions on Contracts or other supernatural gifts?\u201d<br /> <br /> Peg and Jimmy conferred quietly. After about a minute, they turned back to me and Jimmy held up two fingers (but not in an impolite way). \u201cNo turnin\u2019 invisible,\u201d he said, ticking off one finger, \u201cand no walkin\u2019 through walls. Other than that, Bob\u2019s your uncle.\u201d<br /> <br /> I felt a wicked grin coming on, but I think I managed to suppress it. This was going to be <u><u>easy</u></u>. \u201cI understand,\u201d I said aloud.<br /> <br /> \u201cAll right then,\u201d Peg said, \u201cwe\u2019ll get into position and get started.\u201d<br /> <br /> They left me alone in a small office, told me to wait for the signal, and then moved off to station themselves in various places around the mall\u2019s innards. A few minutes later I heard a shrill whistle, and set my plan in motion. I gathered up the necessary glamour from my internal reserves, and let go of my human form. A few seconds later, I was a tiny, brightly colored bird.<br /> <br /> Slipping through the first series of lasers was simplicity itself. They all moved in very limited, predictable patterns (mostly up and down or back and forth), and I probably wouldn\u2019t have had much trouble with it even in human form. As a tiny bird, I just looped and soared through the grid with ease, and made the other side in seconds flat. Figuring that one of the sentinels would likely be watching the exit of that corridor, I kept close to the ceiling and tried to glide as much as I could, keeping the flapping of my wings to a minimum. Sure enough, I spotted Jimmy not far away, but I don\u2019t think he saw me.<br /> <br /> The second set required a little more thought, but not much. Some of the lasers moved in curved arcs rather than straight lines, but they still for the most part moved either back and forth or in a circuitous path that repeated itself every few seconds. I might have had a bit of trouble with that one if I\u2019d been my usual size and shape; it would have been difficult to prevent one of those arcing beams from clipping a wing at the very least. As a small bird, it was pretty easy, though. Peg nearly spotted me as I zipped out of the corridor; I think she heard the flutter of my wings, but she returned her attention to the course after a moment of fruitless searching.<br /> <br /> Halley was watching the <u><u>entrance</u></u> of the third corridor, and I almost missed her in my eagerness to proceed. I don\u2019t think she knows that I can turn into a bird, though, so she paid no attention to me as I flapped by her. This corridor gave me more trouble than the previous two, because the movement of the laser beams was asynchronous. They were set to different timing cycles, so places that were safe to stand during <u>one</u> cycle for the first ceiling-mounted light were no longer safe during its <u><u>next</u></u> cycle. I had to study the way the beams moved for nearly two minutes before I felt confident that I could make it through the corridor. It was a close shave, but I managed to pull it off in the end.<br /> <br /> The fourth and final corridor was the toughest of all, as I probably should have expected. The beams moved in loops and whorls. Each beam followed a predictable pattern, but the patterns were complicated, and they were not in sync with each other. Also, some of the beams shut down when they reached the end of their route and took a few moments to reset back to the beginning, while others just moved back and forth without interruption. After a minute or two of trying to figure out how to proceed, I decided \u201cfuck it,\u201d and just made a mad dash for the other side, figuring that it would be better to trust my reaction speed than my tactical observation skills in this particular instance. There were a few close shaves, but I made it. As I expected, Twitch was at the far end of the corridor, so I had to hold in my tweets of glee. Hell, for all I know Twitch might even be afraid of birds\u2026<br /> <br /> I fluttered into the \u201cfinish line\u201d area and resumed my human form. Once I\u2019d caught my breath, I called down the hallway that I was done. The four of them shut down the lasers and joined me a few moments later. Halley excused herself, asking if she could start telling the rest of the Freehold about the laser maze (and maybe charging admission).<br /> <br /> \u201cNot bad, Pet,\u201d Peg said with a nod, \u201cnot bad at all!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo what now?\u201d I asked, more than a little nervous.<br /> <br /> Peg and Jimmy exchanged a look. \u201cI think we\u2019ve got enough information to accurately assess your abilities, Pet,\u201d Jimmy said after a moment. \u201cNext step is we give you a month to think about yourself, then we give you a <u><u>real</u></u> test\u2026 a test you can either pass or fail. It\u2019ll be a test of the areas where we think you\u2019re at your weakest.\u201d<br /> <br /> Peg took up the thread from there. \u201cYou can spend the next month training however you like, with whoever you like. Now, we know you\u2019re getting hitched next month, so if you want to schedule the test for after the wedding, we\u2019ll understand\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I thought about it for a few seconds, but decided I didn\u2019t want to push back the rescue operation any more than was strictly necessary. \u201cHow about the week between the two ceremonies?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cIf you\u2019re sure, that\u2019ll do,\u201d Jimmy allowed.<br /> <br /> \u201cWill I know what I\u2019m being tested on?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> Peg shook her head. \u201cThat\u2019s part of the test,\u201d she explained.<br /> <br /> \u201cIf you fail, you can test again in two years,\u201d Jimmy added helpfully.<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay,\u201d I said, struggling to take all that in. \u201cWell, thank you for your consideration, I guess. I\u2019ll do my best not to let you down.\u201d I\u2019m pretty proud of myself, actually\u2026 the rising panic didn\u2019t start to overtake me until I was almost all the way home. I was sort of desperately singing along with the radio to try to keep my composure.<br /> <br /> Calamity was in the process of calling a motley meeting when I walked in. \u201cEverything okay?\u201d she asked when she took in my expression (and the fact that I was still quietly singing \u201cWannabe\u201d by the Spice Girls under my breath).<br /> <br /> \u201cI have a month to try to learn how to do everything I don\u2019t already know how to do,\u201d I explained frantically.<br /> <br /> \u201cCalm down,\u201d she said. \u201cExplain it from the beginning.\u201d I did, and she smiled at the state of me. \u201cThink it through,\u201d she advised. \u201cThey\u2019re not going to ask someone who has never had any training to perform open heart surgery, or anything like that. They tested you for a reason. Think about where you did well and where you didn\u2019t do so well, and try to shore up those areas, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> I thought about it, and it made sense. \u201cWell,\u201d I said after a moment, \u201cI did pretty well in most of their tests\u2026 but when they had me box Jimmy, I never actually <u><u>hit</u></u> him or anything, I just tried my best to dodge a lot.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHand-to-hand combat,\u201d Calamity said with a nod. \u201cJacob and D and I can help you with that. Don\u2019t stress over it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay,\u201d I said, taking a deep breath. \u201cOkay. I can do this. The Pilgrims are reasonable people. They just want to make sure that I recognize the same deficiencies they do, and that I\u2019m taking steps to improve myself. Thanks.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAny time,\u201d she said.<br /> <br /> Turns out she wanted to talk with us all about the bugaboo that Hollywood has sent to sow discord in the Lady by the Sea. She\u2019d met with Soon Hee Kwon earlier and gotten a bit more information, and wanted us all to keep our eyes peeled for certain tell-tale signs, like people acting out of character or lashing out at each other for no good reason.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell,\u201d I said after thinking for a moment, \u201cwe\u2019ve had like five new people show up in the Freehold over the past week or so. If I was trying to infiltrate, I\u2019d probably choose to impersonate one of them. Then it would be harder for people to tell if my act wasn\u2019t perfect.\u201d<br /> <br /> Calamity allowed as how this was reasonable, and said she\u2019d pass that on to Miss Kwon. She also suggested that the monster-hunter might want to speak with Monica, as she tends to deal pretty closely with all of the newcomers, and might be able to pick up on any subtle signs via kenning.<br /> <br /> Something else occurred to me as we were about to adjourn. \u201cWait\u2026 you said to watch out for any strange violent outbursts, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> Calamity nodded. \u201cIf your Clarity is low, this thing can apparently make you see and hear things that aren\u2019t really there, and this can cause people to lash out\u2026 particularly if they\u2019re already tense or paranoid.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t know about you,\u201d I said slowly, \u201cbut that makes me think about\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026what happened at the Rose &amp; Thorn!\u201d Calamity finished my sentence for me. She was dialing almost before she finished talking. Though I only heard her half of the conversation that followed, I gather that this was <u><u>exactly</u></u> the sort of intel Ms. Kwon wanted, and that she promised to look into it as soon as she could.<br /> <br /> Well, after that was settled, we split up to prepare for our respective evenings. It turns out that Calamity and Marguerite were <u><u>each</u></u> debuting new numbers last night (hoping to get a feel for the response before rolling them out for the weekend shows). I felt it was my duty as creative director to check up on their progress, but they both seemed to have things well in hand. Calamity\u2019s act was a number called \u201cI Don\u2019t Wanna Wake Up\u201d by a singer I\u2019d never heard of called Ivy Levan, while Marguerite\u2019s was a jazzy little song called \u201cStray Cat Strut.\u201d What I saw of both acts looked great to me, and I look forward to seeing them in action over the weekend.<br /> <br /> I was not at the show last night, of course, because I\u2019d made plans to join Joan and Andromeda for dinner and a feature film. So once again I showered, blow-dried, perfumed, and dressed to the nines in an oh-so-slinky black sheath dress that I <u><u>adore</u></u>, and made my way across town to their place (making sure that D wasn\u2019t neglected first, of course\u2026 I think she had plans to see Gloria).<br /> <br /> The ever-expanding saga of Joan and Andromeda\u2019s VCR troubles has been a source of some amusement for me since before Christmas, and I was looking forward to seeing what had gone wrong with the darn thing this time. I thought I was prepared for just about anything Joan could throw at me in that regard as I rang the doorbell.<br /> <br /> I was wrong.<br /> <br /> Joan answered the door with a long-suffering look on her face. She was wrapped nearly head-to-toe in videotape. \u201cYou will not believe what just happened to our VCR,\u201d she commented dryly.<br /> <br /> I couldn\u2019t help it, the laughter just burst out of me, and I nearly doubled over with it. Joan was obviously pleased with the reaction.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m glad you enjoyed that, Lori,\u201d Andromeda piped up from within the house. \u201cShe\u2019s been planning it for <u><u>days</u></u>.\u201d<br /> <br /> Joan shrugged. \u201cIt seemed a good use of a two-dollar videotape,\u201d she said simply.<br /> <br /> \u201cBravo,\u201d I commented through my continuing giggles, \u201cwell done!\u201d<br /> <br /> It took us nearly fifteen minutes to get Joan untangled from that mess, but none of us were complaining. During that time, both of them thanked me again for suggesting that they might want to spend some quality time with Flores. I gathered from their glowing reviews that they enjoyed the experience quite a bit, and hope to repeat it sometime soon.<br /> <br /> As we were sitting down to dinner, Joan spoke softly. \u201cLorelei,\u201d she said, her gaze oddly shy, \u201cyour wings\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah,\u201d I said, spreading them a little to show them off, \u201cthey\u2019ve really filled out, haven\u2019t they?\u201d I hadn\u2019t consciously been trying to draw attention to them, but\u2026 ah, hell, I <u><u>am</u></u> proud of them, and I was pleased that Joan had noticed their improvement.<br /> <br /> \u201cTo tell you the truth,\u201d I went on, \u201cit scared the hell out of me when it happened. I woke up the other morning and the bed was covered with feathers. I thought they\u2019d all fallen out.\u201d<br /> <br /> Andromeda rolled her eyes a little. \u201cWell, to be fair, you <u><u>do</u></u> tend to leave feathers in the bed, dear,\u201d she said with a twinkle.<br /> <br /> \u201cNot like this,\u201d I said, shuddering at the memory. \u201cI guess when the new ones grew in, they sort of pushed most of the old ones out. It was hard for me to look in the mirror after that, but\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThey\u2019re beautiful,\u201d Joan said, almost reverently.<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you, sweetie,\u201d I said, taking her hand in my own. \u201cBut that\u2019s not all\u2026 they\u2019re functional now, as well.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou can fly?\u201d Joan asked, her eyes widening.<br /> <br /> \u201cYep,\u201d I said, and I couldn\u2019t hold back the smile.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, here we go,\u201d Andromeda muttered fondly from across the table.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd\u2026 are they\u2026 sturdy?\u201d Joan asked. When I just looked at her quizzically, she elaborated. \u201cAre they strong enough that you might be able to\u2026 to carry someone?\u201d<br /> <br /> Something sounding suspiciously like a snort erupted from Andromeda. \u201cYou want her to Lois Lane you, Joan?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> Joan nodded sheepishly.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell,\u201d I said, \u201cI haven\u2019t tried carrying anyone yet, and I don\u2019t want to make promises I\u2019m not sure I can keep. But I\u2019ve always been stronger than I look, and I\u2019d be willing to give it a try. Maybe\u2026 after Sex Breakfast tomorrow, if you ladies would like to join us.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe would like that very much!\u201d Joan replied immediately. Andromeda, giggling, concurred.<br /> <br /> With that out of the way, we concentrated on eating the excellent meal Andromeda had prepared, and on talking and laughing and generally having a good time. I know I\u2019ve said this before, but I\u2019m so glad those two have chosen to include me in their lives. We\u2019re not dating\u2026 I\u2019m not involved with them like I am with D or Marguerite or Julia or Oleander or Brightstar. But I feel so close to the two of them. If we\u2019re not quite soulmates, then I think we\u2019re still closer than friends (or even friends-with-benefits, as the kids are <u><u>also</u></u> apparently saying these days).<br /> <br /> So after dinner, with nary a working VCR in sight, we retired to the boudoir for our usual shenanigans. And it was so nice. Andromeda and I snuggled in close face-to-face while Joan pressed herself against my back and straightened and preened my wings. Things were mostly very tender last night, and I could feel their warmth and their love seeping in to me from all sides. And yes, I guess in a way I do love them\u2026 both of them.<br /> <br /> After I\u2019d worn them both out, I gently extricated myself from their arms, zapped myself awake, and started reading medical journals and writing this diary. I can\u2019t afford to let my studies slip, and my days are going to be even more packed now that I need to start combat training so that I can pass the Pilgrims\u2019 test. I\u2019m not one to complain, but looking at the two of them lying there in each other\u2019s arms, I\u2019m actually a little jealous. I wish I could just relax like that from time to time. I want to be there with them, sleeping and grinning and basking in the love and attention. I\u2019d never do anything to come between them (y\u2019know\u2026 so to speak), but I want what they have.<br /> <br /> I know that D loves me. I know that Marguerite and Julia and Oleander love me. I know that Brightstar loves me, though maybe not as intensely as the others. I know that, in their own way, Joan and Andromeda love me. Hell, I might even include Juan-Carlos in that category, if we\u2019re expanding the definition of love here. And I know that I have to be <u><u>better</u></u> than I am now; lives could depend on it someday. But sometimes, I desperately wish I could put down the books and the boxing gloves and the <u><u>responsibility</u></u> and just let somebody tell me that everything is going to be okay because she\u2019ll always be there.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T13:37:42-07:00","id":1152009,"title":"","content":"<b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> Thursday, May 7<sup>th</sup><br /> Nine years, one month, sixteen days<br /> Days without stabbing: 5<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a man asleep in my bed. My skin\u2019s still warm with the memory of his touch and his scent lingers on me as I sit here. I\u2019m sore in all the right ways\u2026 he coaxed me and teased me and played every inch of me like a virtuoso with a well tuned instrument until I screamed and sang in pleasure so many times I lost count.<br /> <br /> He\u2019s not Gawain\u2026 but I\u2019m not Gawain\u2019s monster anymore. I\u2019m not anyone\u2019s monster now. And oddly enough, I\u2019m kinda okay with that. Not entirely\u2026 not yet\u2026 but I will be.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know if the increase in my connection to Wyrd was part of it but I think it was. I\u2019ve grown stronger. My glass has changed, it\u2019s not as broken and jagged as it was, it\u2019s sharper and stronger, blades more than shards now. And if I focus, I can draw it inside. It\u2019s hard and it hurts like hell when it pierces my skin again but I\u2019ve gained some control over it. It\u2019s not just some thing I brought back that\u2019s embedded inside me\u2026 it\u2019s part of me. Maybe it always was but I feel less at odds with it now. It\u2019s hard to explain, but I just feel less at odds with it\u2026 with that part of myself I guess.<br /> <br /> And as the motley often does the others have also grown more powerful. Lori can actually fly now. It was quite a shock to see her soaring through the air that first time. And the look on her face\u2026 blissful\u2026 whole\u2026<br /> <br /> The others aren\u2019t as dramatically different but the shift affected us all. Jacob\u2019s colder and can\u2019t tolerate warm beverages. Marguerite was communing with a thunderstorm and there is most certainly something different about her presence, an air of majesty about her. And she\u2019s put together a plan for the rescue of Lori\u2019s friends. It\u2019s a good plan, one that plays to our strengths and to the role the Wyrd expects of us since trying to go against that will only make it conspire to twist things until we\u2019re forced to. Better to work with it on our terms than deal with that. Of course, just because it\u2019s a good plan doesn\u2019t mean it\u2019s going to be easy. And it\u2019s made the whole thing very real. But I have no doubt that we can pull it off.<br /> <br /> But that\u2019s not until after the weddings and honeymoon are over and there\u2019s plenty of more pressing business on my plate. Like passing my testing with Juan Carlos to join the family of Silent Nights this afternoon or actually sitting down to talk to Becky face to face tonight. Oh yeah, and there is also the little matter of that mind warping monster Hollywood sent us like a belated Christmas gift. (I guess it\u2019s still better than a fruitcake\u2026)<br /> <br /> Of course, it\u2019s thanks to the Court of the Dragon\u2019s monster hunter Soon Hee Kwon that we know about the hedge beast and have a handle on how to spot and fight it. She\u2019s an intense one to be sure and most certainly peaked Stasia\u2019s interest. For my part, I found myself drawn to the other visiting dragon. Laughing Carp is an emissary from the Chinatown courts visiting while some of our folks work with them against Hollywood, or as she herself puts it \u2018collateral\u2019. She is adorable and I want to do such terrible things to her\u2026 which I am pretty sure only serves to make her more interested since, as Becky put it, she\u2019s sexually attracted to fire. Of course, that only makes my glass tingle all the more\u2026<br /> <br /> But right now she\u2019s Becky\u2019s charge and that makes the whole situation awkward. Or maybe it just made me want to flirt with her in front of Becky more. I don\u2019t know. That\u2019s why I called her and asked her to come to the Dream House tonight. She and I can speak privately while D watches over the sexy little magicarp. It needs to happen. We have got to settle the air between us. Of course, I don\u2019t know exactly what I\u2019m going to say. I miss her. I miss the intimacy we shared. But she hasn\u2019t been there. Not even for Walpurgis, which was a pretty big deal and she didn\u2019t even bother sending word that she wouldn\u2019t be present. I guess it shouldn\u2019t be a surprise that things fell apart, neither of us is any good at the whole relationship thing. But I still care about her and I miss my friend. I just hope that she\u2019s still that. At least she did agree to talk and I\u2019ll know one way or the other where we stand after tonight. And yeah, it\u2019s not a coincidence that I found someone to fuck me senseless (pretty literally given that he\u2019s a Nightsinger\u2026) because I\u2019m not walking into this horny as a teenager.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I suspect it\u2019s for the best that Juan Carlos will be coming by before the show to test me. I\u2019m pretty confident that I\u2019ll be able to handle it as long as I have my wits about me. I\u2019ve done some impressive Oneiromancy and I\u2019m a talented dreamcrafter. It still feels a little strange to not have Gawain there at my side in dreams and I doubt I\u2019ll ever be as strong as the two of us working together were. But I am good at this, damn good. And I can make a real difference for people. I have made a real difference for Andromeda and Desiree and even Angela. This will only make my skills stronger, make me better. I just have to focus and show him what I\u2019m capable of.<br /> <br /> I should also take the opportunity to speak o him about Molly. I doubt there are many cases quite like hers but it seems reasonable that he might have helped a changeling recover memories lost to Arcadia or have some thoughts on how to do so. I saw first hand how Snow Globe stole people\u2019s pasts and identities away from them. I understand why people like Twitch are afraid of her remembering but the simple fact is that turning her into Molly was no better than The Whispering Voices trying to make me Jane. For good or ill, she deserves to know who she was and to decide who she wants to be and anyone that wants to try to take that away from her can go fuck themselves.<br /> <br /> Hmmm\u2026 and speaking of fucking\u2026 It would seem Salk isn\u2019t as asleep as I thought he was and is whispering into my ear about the decidedly wicked things he still intends to do to me before the night is over. And my but it\u2019s quite the list so I had best get to it if I don\u2019t want to be late for my meditation with White Maria.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Today started off like any other Thursday. Calamity, De La Rocha and I went to therapy at the clinic. I talked to Sullivan about random stuff. It wasn\u2019t really focused today and that was fine. I\u2019ve had a lot on my mind with Molly\u2019s situation and everything. I didn\u2019t want to bring it up to Sullivan yet since he hadn\u2019t met with Molly. I think he was going to do that a little later in the morning. I made a note to ask her how it went later. After therapy Calamity announced that she needed to go to the store and get some fruit. She said that she wanted to make crepes for breakfast and who was I to stand in her way? We haven\u2019t had crepes since Gawain left and the fact that Calamity wants to make them seems like a positive sign. Maybe she\u2019s starting to get past the heartache that his leaving caused? One can only hope.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, there was some tension at breakfast this morning. Apparently, Dominika stayed the night with Julia and Insincere Marguerite, but Marguerite spent the entire evening thinking in the vents. I think they started to smooth things over when Insincere Marguerite walked Dominika out to her car, but I\u2019m not positive about that. I was not privy to their conversation and it seemed rude to ask. Juan Carlos was also a guest this morning. I think he stayed with Lori and De La Rocha last night. He stayed a little later than Dominika did, but not too much longer. He had business to attend to so we said our goodbyes. After they left Insincere Marguerite pulled us all aside and talked to us. She had said earlier than she had something important to discuss and she wanted to wait until non-motley folks had left. So, she pulled us all into the meeting room and told us what she had spent much of the evening thinking about.<br /> <br /> Turns out she stayed up the whole night thinking about our upcoming trip to Arcadia to rescue Lori\u2019s friends Missy and Jane. She came up with a plan for us once we get into the Empress\u2019 realm. She proposed that we break up into three groups. Luna and I would be one. Marguerite, Lori and De La Rocha would be another and Julia and Calamity would be the third. We would split up once we got into Lori\u2019s Keeper\u2019s lands. Insincere Marguerite would put Lori and De La Rocha in a special sack and she would sneak past the Empress and to the cage that holds Lori\u2019s friends. And yes, this is the same sack that Insincere Marguerite used when she was in Arcadia and brought back her own Prizes. She hid the thing in the Hedge so she would not be tempted to use it. We will have to retrieve it for this part of the plan to work. Marguerite was pretty confident that she could get past the guards in the palace and get to the cage, but only if Lori and De La Rocha stayed in the sack. I know that Lori in particular looked a little less than thrilled by that aspect of the plan, but agreed that she is not the stealthiest of people. De La Rocha admitted the same. Together the three of them would convince or otherwise get Missy and Jane into the magical sack and Marguerite would sneak the lot of them back out. Sounds easy, but I have a feeling that it will be anything but.<br /> <br /> The rest of us are to go after Hunting Hawk and the other guards. Luna and I will take out the outer guards from stealth while Calamity goes after Hawk. Julia was originally going to go with Calamity until it was suggested that she work on \u201cpainting\u201d a way for us to get out of Arcadia. Insincere Marguerite felt that this plan would work to our strengths and talents. I will admit that I do have a history of hunting people in Arcadia and the Hedge. I did it quite frequently as the Lady\u2019s Knight. I have also gone hunting in the Hedge since coming back to \u2018the world,\u2019 but I\u2019ve only hunted Hedge beasts or Extras. I have not intentionally hunted down another person in some time. I suppose that it will come back to me, but I\u2019m not so sure that it\u2019s something I really want to become familiar with again. I know that it\u2019s not really that different from hunting Hedge beasts, so it shouldn\u2019t really make a difference. But part of me can\u2019t help but think that hunting Hedge beasts and people should be very different things instead of just trading one prey for another. I\u2019m sure that Sullivan would have a field day with all of that, but I\u2019m not so certain I\u2019m going to tell him about our upcoming trip to Arcadia. At least not for a while. There are probably all kinds of things that he\u2019d have to say about it. I\u2019m sure that it will be counterproductive to my therapy sessions to go back to the place that made me a monster. It\u2019s not the Lady\u2019s realm, but it\u2019s still Arcadia. It\u2019s close enough. Add to that the fact that my job once we get to Arcadia will be to hunt down and kill or incapacitate people. In all practicality I should not think of my mission as either/or. It would be logical to just kill the guards so they can\u2019t raise the alarm or follow us on our way out. And that in and of itself would probably have Sullivan spinning. It\u2019s not the mindset of a healthy individual. I know that I\u2019m not close to where I was before I was taken. I don\u2019t know if I can go back to that. I\u2019ve seen too much. I\u2019ve done too much. I just can\u2019t let myself get too close to being Rime though.<br /> <br /> After Insincere Marguerite dropped that little bombshell on us she told us that she had been admitted into an entitlement called the Lost Pantheon. Apparently, they are all about fighting the Gentry and making sure that they are not a threat. I can\u2019t help but wonder if that has something to do with her communing with that thunderstorm the other night. She did say that she was stronger than she had been in the past and was committed to her fight against the Gentry.<br /> <br /> Calamity and I went to the backyard to spar once that conversation was over. I think we were excited to have some sort of plan for our trip to Arcadia. It feels more real now than it had in the past. So far is has always been this nebulous event that will happen in the future, but now we have a plan and a timeframe for when we\u2019re going to leave. The plan is to go after the four ladies all get back from their honeymoons. After that we won\u2019t have any definitive plans that are time sensitive. We don\u2019t know how long we\u2019re going to be in Arcadia. It was only thirty minutes for Hunting Hawk when he started to chase after Lori, but for her it was several months. This way if we are gone for several months we won\u2019t miss anything important.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Calamity and I traded blows with more energy than usual and it was good to see the old Calamity out there once more. She started coming around on Tuesday and seemed to continue the trend today. Unfortunately our sparring session was cut short when Soon Hee Kwon called to talk to Calamity. She said that she would be coming by the Dream House in thirty minutes to talk to her about the Hedge beast that had been sent to us from Hollywood. Calamity asked if I\u2019d like to join the conversation and I said sure. We both decided to get cleaned up and were ready to go by the time our Korean guest arrived.<br /> <br /> Soon Hee Kwon arrived promptly and we showed her to the lounge where we could talk. She began by telling us about the Hedge beast that she was hunting. It targets people and tries to sow discord by impersonating people and causing trouble. It can act suspiciously or attack people so it can get others to go after whoever it duplicated or whoever they implied was up to something. They can also affect those that are closer to their Fae side by making them see things that aren\u2019t there. They can create a \u201cdream world\u201d in which you see someone you know attack a friend for example. So, it could make it look like Becky was attacking Lori and anyone that tried to stop you from going after Becky might look like an Extra or something like that. It\u2019s insidious if you ask me. Calamity asked if her Contract with Oath &amp; Punishment would allow her to track the beast, but it apparently doesn\u2019t work. When the beast takes on the guise of someone the power reads it as that person, not as a Hedge beast. Soon Hee Kwon said that Kenning might help to out the creature. If you Kenned someone that should be a Changeling and they read as something else, then you know that you have the beast in front of you. The only problem is that Calamity and I are both a bit too close to our Fae sides to be able to do that. You have to have a firmer grip on reality and a stronger connection to humanity to be able to Ken.<br /> <br /> Soon Hee Kwon also said that the creature is essentially a plant, which made me suggest that we should talk to Oleander about a chemical or something that would affect plants but not humans. Soon Hee said that Oleander would be her next stop after leaving us. This also led to the discussion about using Contracts that affect plants to attack it since attacking it with knives would not be feasible. This thing would look like a human/Changeling to everyone in the Dream House, so if we attacked it there the crowd would see us attacking and killing a person, not a creature. That would lead to trouble from the get go. So, we discussed different abilities that we have that can affect plants. Luna and Calamity both have access to powers that let them affect plants and I can freeze them pretty effectively. We just need to be able to identify it and we have a few different ways to fight it.<br /> <br /> After Soon Hee Kwon left Lori got back from her latest test with the Pilgrims. She suggested, once she heard what we\u2019d been talking about, that the beast might impersonate a stranger, like one of the new arrivals. We don\u2019t know them well enough to know what is normal behavior for them so they might be ideal targets to duplicate. This brought up the idea of De La Rocha texting Monica to see if she can Ken the new arrivals. She would have a reason to do random checks with the newbies so it would not be odd for her to show up. She could Ken them without them being the wiser. Calamity called Soon Hee Kwon to see if we could involve Monica in the hunt for the Hedge beast. Our Korean Hunter agreed that Monica would be an asset, so De La Rocha continued with her text. Lori and Calamity also brought up the fight between Desiree and Felicity as being out of character for both ladies. They dislike each other but have never been violent before. Someone then remembered that Angelica had been there at the same table and that it could have been possible that the beast impersonated her and got the fight started before she fled. If this is the case then the beast has already started on its mischief. Calamity called Soon Hee about that incident and the hunter got excited, saying that was just the sort of activity that she was talking about.<br /> <br /> Lori then told us about her most recent test with the Pilgrims. It seems that they set up an obstacle course of sorts in an old abandoned mall with the help of Twitch and Hailey. It was an elaborate set up with lasers going in different patterns and timers. Lori had to make her way through the course without the lasers hitting her. She also had to get past Twitch, Hailey, Peg and Jimmy without being seen. It was supposed to be a test of how well Lori could figure out the pattern and timing of each set of lasers and avoid them. They said any Contracts were fine as long as it didn\u2019t allow her to walk through walls or turn invisible. So, Lori told us with a smile on her face how she got through the course. She turned into a bird! A little, colorful songbird. She managed to fly and swoop through the lasers and avoid all of the people that were watching out for her. She also said that in one month they will do one last test/assessment to see if Lori can get into the Pilgrims. They tentatively scheduled the test for in between the two weddings in June. They will decide after that if Lori can get into the Pilgrims. If she doesn\u2019t get in this time she can reapply in two years. They sure do seem to have a rigid requirement for entry into their entitlement. I hope Lori makes it.<br /> <br /> After that people spent some time getting ready for the show. It went off great. Insincere Marguerite had a number this time and it went over really well. She performed with Marie H\u00e9l\u00e8ne. It was good to see her on stage again. I think they did a song called \u201cStray Cat Strut.\u201d And boy can Marguerite strut. Calamity also did an act, and as is her usual did really well. There were a lot of appreciative fans in the crowd and they let their pleasure be known. I had the usual folks at the bar tonight. Hailey was at one side of the bar and Molly was at another. Luna held up the end like usual. I managed my time moving between all three ladies, chatting and making drinks for a while. At one point though, I got curious and asked Molly how the meeting with Sullivan went. Apparently he said that it should be possible to unlock her old memories. She also said that she talked to Twitch about the whole idea and he was wholeheartedly against it. He said that she used to be really bad person and was extremely dangerous. He said that she used to seduce people and then kidnap them or return them to the Gentry. Sounds a lot like what I used to do, only I didn\u2019t seduce people. I usually just tricked them into following me.<br /> <br /> Molly also talked to Chalcedony about the idea of unlocking her memories. The blue girl agrees with Twitch and said that she didn\u2019t think it would be a good idea for Molly to do that. She didn\u2019t disagree as vehemently, but still advised against it. I\u2019m not sure what her reasoning is though. I told Molly that if this is something that is really important to her then she should see what she could do to unlock her memories, but cautioned her that once she remembers her past she can\u2019t un-remember it. She will have to live with what she finds out. I was a little concerned that her personality might change and made some allusions to that as well, but didn\u2019t go on too long about it. I don\u2019t know if remembering her past will change how she acts now. She has a lot of good memories to go on these days. She did say that she didn\u2019t feel whole without her memories. I tried telling her that she\u2019s just as much a real person as anyone else. Having memories of your past don\u2019t make you whole, they just help guide your actions. I don\u2019t think that she really believed me though. She was adamant that she\u2019s not a real person. That\u2019s she\u2019s just a doll that the Table created. Twitch had said something that probably didn\u2019t help much overall. He did admit that they kept certain traits of Molly\u2019s old personality, Shayna, around because they thought that they would come in handy when she worked as their agent. I\u2019m sure that little tidbit just reminded Molly that her current self was created and probably wasn\u2019t conducive to helping her get over the fact that she has a big blank spot where her past memories should be.<br /> <br /> While we were talking the idea of Dream healing occurred to me and I mentioned it to Molly. I said that Calamity is really good at Dream healing and might be able to help her remember her past in a more safe and controlled way. I didn\u2019t say those words exactly, but said that it might be better to view the memories while in a dream. Molly thought that this was a good idea so when Calamity looked in my direction I motioned for her to come over to the bar. She arrived moments later. Molly explained what was going on and Calamity said that she\u2019d be more than happy to help Molly remember her past. She was rather gung-ho about the whole idea actually. She did caution Molly that once she remembers her past she won\u2019t be able to just forget it again, and that she has to be sure that she wants to see the good as well as the bad aspects of her past self. Molly seemed sure that she wanted to go ahead with the Dream healing idea and asked if Chalcedony could be there in the dream with them to offer support. I wasn\u2019t so sure that Chalcedony would want to be there since she thinks this is a bad idea, and Calamity said that she didn\u2019t think it would be good for her to be there. She said that the healing should just be her and Molly. Molly eventually relented and asked if Chalcedony could be there in the room while they did the Dream healing. I told Molly that I would be there too to offer my support. I left off the part about me not trusting Chalcedony to be left alone in the Dream House while everyone slept. Which reminded me. Molly thanked me for not putting down her relationship with Chalcedony like others do. I don\u2019t trust Chalcedony overly much but I can see how much Molly really likes her. She probably even loves the blue girl. If I say anything bad about Chalcedony I would just be pushing my friend away and I don\u2019t want to do that. So, I smiled and said something noncommittal, but did say that I wanted to support my friend.<br /> <br /> One thing that Molly asked me to do before we did the Dream healing was to talk to Lowjack, Master Darke or Doctor Bright about who Shayna was and what kind of person she was. I think Molly wanted to have another opinion on the type of person she used to be before she \u201cmeets\u201d her past self in dreams. I told her that I\u2019d talk to Lowjack and get back to her about that. It seemed like a good idea to me. Lowjack would have known what Shayna did and how she did it. He didn\u2019t authorize the use of the Table to change her, but he would have been aware of her as a loyalist before she was changed. He could offer some insight into the person that she used to be.<br /> <br /> All of this talk about past memories made me think about just how much past actions shaped me as a person. Calamity said as much too. She said that the past, the good and bad, shape who we are. I agree, so I guess I can see where Molly is coming from. She doesn\u2019t have a past. Nothing to shape who she is except the past year\u2019s worth of memories. She is so awkward socially because she literally doesn\u2019t have much practice at interacting with people. She\u2019s a good spy and fighter because those are the skills that they kept when they remade her. It isn\u2019t fair. I have to believe that knowing who and what she was in the past will not change Molly too much. It will of course change how she views certain things, but I have to believe that she will also remember her present self and her current friends. Not all loyalists are irredeemable. I wasn\u2019t. I don\u2019t know exactly how D\u0336e\u0336l\u0336i\u0336g\u0336h\u0336t\u0336 Diane did it. I don\u2019t even think that she did it on purpose, but the more time I spent in her company the more emotions I felt. The more I connected with the people around me as just that, people. They weren\u2019t targets anymore. Even Travers. That man wants to kill me. He almost did, but he\u2019s still a person in my mind. Just not a very nice one. I came back from being Rime. I came back from being a loyal Knight to the Lady of the Winter Winds. I didn\u2019t come back to who I was before I was taken. I have already said that I just changed too much, saw too much, and did too much to be that boy again. I can\u2019t go back. I can only go forward. I just hope that my friend takes that journey forward with me.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XCIII</i><br /> <br /> Let\u2019s see\u2026<br /> <br /> Lorelei had to make a series of Dexterity + Athletics and Dexterity + Stealth rolls. She got boosts to the Stealth rolls due to her size, and the Athletics rolls required notably fewer successes. It seemed fun.<br /> <br /> So Insincere Marguerite\u2019s show involved her in a beret, black leather jacket, white top braless and cigarette pants, and strutting around singing Stray Cat Strut. Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne similarly attired, sat at the edge of the stage tearing up a guitar. Insincere Marguerite also thickened her accent up, and made several indefinite articles definite \u201cI\u2019m the ladies cat!\u201d not a. She gender swapped a few lines \u201cSingin\u2019 the blues while the lady cats howl/\u2019Wild stray cat you\u2019re a real gone gal\u201d and at the end had three cats run onto boxes on the backstage and sway to the music. Less specifics on \u201cI Don\u2019t Wanna Wake Up\u201d Beyond Calamity\u2019s bringing a Dominatrix vibe. Both girls rolled well, but not, like, Lorelei well. Both sued Vainglory, and Insincere Marguerite used Verdant Spring and had Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne assist her.<br /> <br /> I think that covers everything, but Comments and Questions are welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments