{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T23:38:15-07:00","id":1152126,"title":"","content":"The last paragraph in Calamity's journal mentions him by name. Salk has not eaten anyone anyone is aware of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T12:05:13-07:00","id":1152252,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7920_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7920\" data-vbnamecard=\"7920\">Master Aquatosic</a>: You might possibly be thinking of Charlotte, the Autumn Monarch, who is rumored to have that particular hunger. She's a Black Widow-style Beast, if I remember correctly. The only other character I can think of who <i>literally</i> had that problem is Mary, when her Clarity slipped due to her Fetch's actions. Jolie, the Spring Monarch, used to devour people's creative essence, though the Table fixed that. And there are any number of Leechfingers out there who will snack upon the life-energy of their paramours (pretty much all of them except De la Rocha, I think... though the Handmaidens and Leanne Sheets stand out in my memory).<br /> <br /> As always, thanks for reading and commenting! Though the average number of journals has diminished, it's nice to know that people are still following.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T12:59:49-07:00","id":1152265,"title":"","content":"I could swear that one of the proprietors of the Rose and Thorn preyed upon mortals in some way","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T16:12:29-07:00","id":1152321,"title":"","content":"Aha, I see your mix up.<br /> <br /> -The Rose &amp; Thorn is run by Flores, the Spring Elemental. No preying on anyone there she is an innocent. That's where the recent Felicity/Desiree fight happened.<br /> <br /> -The Unseelie Court is run by Corvus and Corbin, both Night Court Darklings. (with the other motley members being Strype/Della and Brightstar, both Night Court Fairest, Neon/Electra, a Night Court Elemental and The Grue/Howard, a Night Court Ogre). There was a strong implication Corbin and least, and possibly sometimes Corvus as well, ate mortals, or or drank their blood, or otherwise did something bad to them.<br /> <br /> Salk the Night Court Darkling actually has nothing to do with that Motley. He is sort of a free agent looking out for Night interests in the Lady By the Sea, often assisting Willow Black, the Night Court Beast who is their Ambassador (who does hang out at the Rose &amp; Thorn a lot) with stuff so she does not get her pinions dirty and has some plausible deniability. He supported Insincere Marguerite when the option was there for her and Felicity the Day Court Fairest to try to assert control in the name of their Courts to get crowns, but Insincere Marguerite decided not to and Felicity backed down due to she and Princess Jolie putting pressure, so Salk went to plot something else.<br /> <br /> Does that help? Any questions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T20:59:14-07:00","id":1152391,"title":"","content":"Ah, thank you. That helps. I remember that storyline now. Though is it normal to have that many prominent clubs in one place in California? Especially since they all seem friendly rather than competitors. Am I just a naive young man or is it for the sake of the story?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 10-24-2017, 12:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T00:19:33-07:00","id":1152419,"title":"","content":"Well, Rose &amp; Thorn is in Santa Monica while the Unseelie Court is in Los Angeles. In Greensboro which is a medium sized city in North Carolina they have two Queer clubs alone, much less other types, and I went to several clubs in San Fransisco while there as well that just catered to Goths, so not unusual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 10-24-2017, 04:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T12:51:48-08:00","id":1156131,"title":"","content":"Molly agonizes over what to do but comes to a decision. Calamity is tested for the Family of Silent Nights. Insincere Marguerite tries for the affections of an old flame.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XCIV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Gwuff. That\u2019s about where I am mentally right now. I don\u2019t know if I\u2019ve actually <u><u>slain</u></u> the dragon, but I certainly seem to have worn her out for a while. So I\u2019ve decided to take a few moments to gather my thoughts and try to plan for the future. It\u2019s hard to prepare for a test when you don\u2019t know what you\u2019re being tested on, but I have a month to shore up my weaknesses, and I intend to make the most of it.<br /> <br /> So I woke up yesterday with Andromeda snuggled up against me and Joan stroking my feathers and looking fondly down at us both. Jesus. I probably won\u2019t ever be involved with them like I am with my regular girlfriends \u2013 and I don\u2019t think either of them really wants that, in all honesty \u2013 but you can\u2019t say there\u2019s no love between us. You can\u2019t say that it\u2019s just casual.<br /> <br /> So the two of them followed me back to the Dream House in Joan\u2019s car, and we all sat down to Sex Breakfast together. In addition to Joan and Andromeda, the motley was joined by a few others yesterday morning. Gloria was there, having spent the night with D. Veronica was there, having spent the evening in Marguerite and Julia\u2019s company\u2026 and Salk had apparently spent the previous night with Calamity. Julia was busy at the stove as we arrived, preparing cheese omelets for everyone and saying the words in French (I <u><u>still</u></u> don\u2019t get it; apparently there has been a mutual unspoken agreement not to explain the reference to me or something).<br /> <br /> Conversations at Sex Breakfast were as ribald as ever; though they took a turn for the philosophical as Salk left. He claimed that he was \u201cgoing back into the world to fulfill his dark purposes,\u201d which sent Joan into sort of a tizzy. I mean, she knew that he was joking, but couldn\u2019t seem to process <u><u>why</u></u> anyone would find that funny. In her mind, there\u2019s nothing humorous about claiming to be evil, whether seriously or in jest. We each tried to explain it in our own way. I held up D as an example of a \u201cbad girl,\u201d with my attraction to her indicating that I found that trait desirable, but Joan dismissed that out of hand, as she knows that D is a good person at heart and that her \u201cbad girl\u201d acts never truly pass beyond the realm of the misdemeanor.<br /> <br /> Joan also offered her opinions regarding what the Pilgrims might see as my weakness, and it\u2019s both remarkably perceptive and something I never would have thought of. She thinks that I might have to endure a test of willpower\u2026 that I might have to resist giving in to temptation for as long as possible. That\u2019s\u2026 well, it\u2019s true that I\u2019m a creature of impulse, but I\u2019m not sure how I should go about training for that sort of thing, honestly. I suggested spreading a pint of double chocolate-chip ice cream over D\u2019s breasts and then not licking it off for half an hour, but she flat-out refused to help me. Can you believe it? Maybe if I said please and gave her a pouty look\u2026<br /> <br /> Gloria and I had a brief conversation about the attraction of bad girls, as she has taken note of Miss Soon Hee Kwon these past few days, and mentioned that she might make a play for the Western Dragon. I mentioned my own intentions along those lines, and she sort of sighed and looked resigned. I hate that. I didn\u2019t mean to discourage her in any way. I tried to cover up my chagrin by joking that we could always attempt to seduce Ms. Kwon together, but that only made her more uncomfortable, so I let the subject drop. I asked D about it later, and she says that while Gloria likes me, she has a bit of an inferiority complex when it comes to me. I\u2019ll have to be more careful what I say around her in the future.<br /> <br /> Veronica left shortly after Salk, and I walked her out with a promise that we could meet up and hang out soon (and I hope we can). She also told me that she\u2019d be seeing Rowan soon, and I asked her to pass along my best wishes. Julia called me aside after that and asked me to speak with Marguerite about our corn-fed compatriot. She believes that Veronica is developing an unhealthy attachment to Marguerite, who in turn claims that nothing serious will develop between them. In typical infuriating Marguerite fashion, she opined that it would be strange if Veronica <u><u>wasn\u2019t</u></u> falling in love with her. I know that her arrogance is mostly a show to hide her own insecurities\u2026 but I\u2019d be lying if I said that it never irritates me.<br /> <br /> In any case, I promised to speak with Veronica about this the next time I saw her, and then launched into my own rather nervous request. I had D join us for this, and explained that I\u2019m increasingly bothered by the notion that when we go to Arcadia to rescue Missy and Jane, I might freeze at the last minute and be unable to enter Marguerite\u2019s magic bag. I know how important that aspect of the plan is, and I fully intend to give it my best, but\u2026 voluntarily confining myself in that way just goes counter to my nature, and I don\u2019t want to get all the way there and then discover that I simply can\u2019t go through with it.<br /> <br /> Marguerite told me that we could test it out as soon as she had the bag in hand. She\u2019s tasked Yvette with retrieving it, and our other French friend has sent a chimaera into the Hedge to do so. She also suggested that I speak with Yvette about the experience beforehand, as she had been in the bag several times and might be able to alleviate my fears a bit. Fortunately, she was making the journey from Paris that very night to see Marguerite\u2019s new act.<br /> <br /> D gave me a searching look. \u201cBut\u2026 you were going to suggest something, weren\u2019t you?\u201d she asked quietly.<br /> <br /> I nodded, and took the plunge. \u201cI trust you \u2013 all three of you \u2013 more than anyone else in the world,\u201d I began, \u201cand I know you\u2019ve been trying to talk me into getting on that cross in the basement\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> D shook her head. \u201cLori, I\u2019ve been thinking about that\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I cut her off. \u201cI just thought that it might\u2026 help me get used to the idea, if we could try it out under controlled circumstances\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt won\u2019t work,\u201d D said flatly.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhy not?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s not built for someone with your\u2026 <u><u>physique</u></u>,\u201d she said delicately.<br /> <br /> Now usually, when someone mentions my \u201cphysique\u201d in that way, they\u2019re talking about my boobs, so I confess that I was confused for a couple of seconds. Then it hit me. \u201cMy wings,\u201d I said, \u201cthere\u2019d be no space for them if you strapped me to that thing.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe could strap her in on her stomach,\u201d Julia piped up helpfully.<br /> <br /> D shook her head immediately. \u201cThat would be <u><u>way</u></u> too uncomfortable. Look, babe\u2026 I appreciate the thought, but it\u2019s not really practical, and\u2026 I know it wouldn\u2019t be fun for you. It\u2019s something Marguerite and I enjoy because we can have fun with it, but it wouldn\u2019t <u><u>be</u></u> fun for me if I was hurting or upsetting you. Got it?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI got it,\u201d I said with what was probably a fairly watery grin, \u201cnot everybody gets their kicks in the same way.\u201d<br /> <br /> At which point the conversation devolved into a discussion of some of the more bizarre kinks out there. It was speculated that there are probably at least a few people out there who are turned on by undercooked bacon (and no, I\u2019m not one of them, just for the record. Eww). We moved back into the kitchen, where Joan gave me an expectant look.<br /> <br /> I had to giggle a little. \u201cWell, I think it\u2019s about time for me to head outside and stretch my wings a little,\u201d I said with a wink. Joan was at my side like a shot, leaving Andromeda stifling her mirth in the breakfast nook. So the two of us headed outside, and for once the golden-haired princess swept the knight in shining armor into her arms instead of vice-versa. I put one hand around her waist and the other behind her knees and launched myself into the sky. And it\u2019s a good thing that I\u2019m stronger than I look, because carrying another fully-grown person \u2013 even a relatively petite person like Joan \u2013 is no joke when you\u2019re flying.<br /> <br /> But it was worth it to see the look of pure, unadulterated joy on Joan\u2019s face as we swooped and soared around the property. She laughed. I mean <u><u>Joan</u></u> actually <u><u>laughed</u></u>. I\u2019ve seen her ecstatically happy before (what can I say? I\u2019m good at what I do), but I don\u2019t think I\u2019ve ever seen her look quite so\u2026 carefree before. Of course, I\u2019m not one to talk\u2026 I can still feel the big goofy grin spreading across my face every time I spread my wings and launch myself into the air. Still\u2026 she wears it well.<br /> <br /> So we flew around until I got tired and had to land, at which point Joan threw her arms around my neck and gave me a big kiss. \u201cThank you,\u201d she whispered, and I almost think I saw the shimmer of tears in her eyes.<br /> <br /> \u201cAny time,\u201d I said, and I meant it.<br /> <br /> She and Andromeda took their leave after that, and it was just the motley in the Dream House again. Calamity brought up a fun idea\u2026 turns out that there\u2019s a new <u><u>Mad Max</u></u> movie coming out next weekend, and she thought it might be fun to get everyone together to see it at the premiere. I remember how much fun it was to watch the other movies with her last year, and pretty much agreed on the spot. D, Jacob, and Luna are in as well, and I think I heard Calamity say that Stasia would be coming along too. Half-joking, I suggested that we raid Ace\u2019s old closet and put together some costumes\u2026 and the idea took off. Of course, I\u2019m not really going to borrow anything of Ace\u2019s\u2026 it wouldn\u2019t fit anyway, and when have I ever turned down the opportunity to engage in a little specialty outfit shopping?<br /> <br /> Julia got me alone early yesterday afternoon to elaborate on the situation with Marguerite and Veronica, and I have to admit that her opinions about Veronica\u2019s feelings toward Marguerite probably have a bit more evidence to support them than I had previously assumed. See, after their lovemaking was over, Marguerite used one of her contracts to, erm\u2026 \u201ctake up residence\u201d <u><u>inside</u></u> Julia for the duration of the night. Yeah, Marguerite slept in her fianc\u00e9e\u2019s womb\u2026 though I\u2019m still not sure exactly how. And Veronica was apparently put out that <u><u>she</u></u> wasn\u2019t the one chosen for this particular \u201chonor.\u201d<br /> <br /> I guess something of my shock must have shown on my face, because Julia gave me a smile. \u201cYou should really try it sometime,\u201d she said with enthusiasm.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat?\u201d I asked, as usual the picture of eloquence.<br /> <br /> \u201cI wouldn\u2019t really know, but I imagine it feels sort of like being pregnant,\u201d she elaborated.<br /> <br /> I was still trying to think of ways to explain that I don\u2019t particularly <u><u>want</u></u> to know what it feels like to be pregnant at this point in my life when we were saved by the bell. The doorbell, in fact.<br /> <br /> Juan-Carlos came by this afternoon to put Calamity through her paces in preparation for inducting her into the Family of the Silent Nights. I tried to make myself unobtrusive while he was around \u2013 I didn\u2019t want to distract from the very serious reason he was there \u2013 so I mostly hung around in the theater putting the finishing touches on my act for the evening. The final testing took about an hour, and of course Calamity passed with flying colors. I didn\u2019t ask for details \u2013 Calamity looked a little shaken up \u2013 but I understand that she had to weather some sort of custom-made dream to prove that she could maintain her wits and focus amidst adversity.<br /> <br /> Juan-Carlos offered to take her out to dinner to celebrate her new membership in his Entitlement, and said that the rest of us were welcome to come along as well (though he only covered Calamity\u2019s bill). So the motley gathered and we went to a relatively nice steakhouse in Santa Monica. Our stars really must be on the rise, because they seated us without a second glance, even though Marguerite was typically shoeless and Juan-Carlos was just as typically shirtless. I guess it\u2019s true what they say about beach towns: no shirt, no shoes, no problem!<br /> <br /> The food was good, and for the most part the conversation was light and flirty. But at one point Calamity started asking about using dream therapy to unlock blocked memories. She used general terms when speaking with Juan-Carlos, but it wasn\u2019t hard to figure out who she was talking about from the context. Still, since she obviously thought it was important to keep things on the Q.T., I let it pass, resolving that we\u2019d have a conversation as soon as we got back to the Dream House and had a little privacy.<br /> <br /> As it turns out there was no need to force the issue; Calamity called us all together to discuss Molly\u2019s case on her own. It turns out that Molly has been speaking with Jacob for the past few days about the possibility of learning more about who she used to be, before Darke and Grey used the Table to remake her. The problem is that by all accounts she used to be a bad person. Like, a <u><u>really</u></u> bad person. So there\u2019s the possibility that she might revert to the Loyalist she used to be if she remembers that part of her life.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s\u2026 not an easy decision to make, though it probably <u><u>should</u></u> be. I mean, Molly had her whole life stripped away against her will, and she wants to know where she came from. In a vacuum, there\u2019d be no question about whether she has that right. But there could be dire consequences for a <u><u>lot</u></u> of people if we just blithely go ahead with this course of action. Jacob has spoken with Boss Lowjack about this situation, and he agrees that we can\u2019t really deny Molly\u2019s request\u2026 but he\u2019s going to be taking precautions. And though I hate the necessity for things like that, I confess that I\u2019m glad.<br /> <br /> Calamity agreed to speak with Molly at the show that night, and we split up to get ready for the show. The show itself was a lot of fun, and a lot of people showed up to see it. My solo number didn\u2019t come up until the second set, so I made my way up to the balcony to speak with Yvette relatively early in the evening. She and Marguerite were flirting with each other pretty shamelessly\u2026 but I let it pass without comment. Either I trust my French lover or I don\u2019t, and I intend to err on the side of trust until I have a good reason not to. Marguerite has proven many times that she\u2019s not the same person she used to be.<br /> <br /> Oh, and speaking of Marguerite\u2026 that new act of hers was <u><u>spectacular</u></u><u>!</u> She had the choreography pitch-perfect, and I\u2019m sure people will be talking about the \u201cdancing cats\u201d in the background for days. Her singing was nothing to sneeze at either. Is it too much for me to start referring to her as my prot\u00e9g\u00e9, do you think?<br /> <br /> In any case, talking with Yvette actually did make me feel at least a <u><u>little</u></u> more comfortable about the idea of being stuffed into Marguerite\u2019s magic sack. According to Yvette, actually being in the sack isn\u2019t bad at all\u2026 you\u2019re in a floaty, dreamy sort of stasis, and you\u2019re not really aware of the passage of time. She also said that <u><u>getting</u></u> into the sack can be a little nerve-wracking\u2026 she always felt a brief moment of panic at the loss of control. And oddly enough, the fact that she mentioned that panic actually comforted me on some level\u2026 it let me know that she was being completely honest and not just telling me something to calm me down.<br /> <br /> I noticed around this point that Calamity \u2013 whose new act was also a big hit \u2013 was <u><u>finally</u></u> talking to Becky. She led her sometimes-girlfriend out of the audience just as I was heading backstage to get dressed for my number. I glanced back at Becky\u2019s table and noticed that D was there babysitting Laughing Carp. I also noticed that Soon Hee Kwon was there, with one booted foot resting cockily on the table, and allowed myself to become intrigued by the possibilities.<br /> <br /> So my number last night really wasn\u2019t anything special in and of itself. It\u2019s a song I\u2019ve done a few times before (mostly during the four months during which I wasn\u2019t really journaling), and while it usually got a good response from the audience, I never considered it part of my A-game. But last night was different\u2026 I don\u2019t know if the stars were aligned just right, or if something about my mood made the difference, but for whatever reason I put on what I consider to be one of the best performances of my life to date.<br /> <br /> The song was \u201cDream Lover\u201d by Bobby Darin, with a couple of our regular girls performing backup vocals. I know, right? Not exactly what most people would consider a show-stopper, even if the person singing it is a hot girl dressed in suggestive nightwear and <u><u>not</u></u> changing the gender of the song\u2019s subject. But whether it was the elation of getting my feathers back, the wonderful night I\u2019d spent with Joan and Andromeda, the thought of rescuing my friends, or the plans which were already forming in my head regarding how I might spend the rest of the evening, something just sort of clicked, and I ended up bringing the house down. Serious standing-ovation time.<br /> <br /> So I left the stage, threw a loose kimono-style robe on over my sexy pajamas, did not tie the sash, and worked the crowd for a little while before meandering over to the table where Becky, Calamity, Laughing Carp, and Soon Hee Kwon were sitting (D had gone back to the door when Becky returned to the table). Ms. Kwon looked me up and down appreciatively, and I liked what I saw in her eyes. I sat down next to her and started to make small talk.<br /> <br /> Eventually I ended up in her lap. At one point she leaned forward and breathed on my neck. I could feel the gentle heat of her fiery breath against my skin as she held my hair carefully out of the way. \u201cSo,\u201d she whispered, \u201cMiss Grace, have you ever experienced the irrational fear that you might one day be eaten by a dragon?\u201d<br /> <br /> I grinned at the innuendo, showing my own teeth a little. \u201cActually, I find the idea quite intriguing,\u201d I replied.<br /> <br /> \u201cReally?\u201d she said with a predatory smirk. \u201cWell, I think this is something we should definitely talk more about\u2026 but I have one little bit of business to take care of before I\u2019m free for the evening. I need to speak with Desiree.\u201d She paused and sighed. \u201cShe\u2019s probably not going to like what I have to say.\u201d<br /> <br /> I turned around and spotted her across the theater. \u201cShe\u2019s over there,\u201d I pointed out helpfully. \u201cCan\u2026 can I be with you when you talk to her? It might make her feel more comfortable\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Soon Hee thought about it for a moment. \u201cI don\u2019t mind if she doesn\u2019t. But\u2026 some of what I have to say to her might be about things she doesn\u2019t want bandied about. If she asks you to leave, or says she doesn\u2019t want to discuss it in front of you, I\u2019d appreciate it if you could make yourself scarce.\u201d<br /> <br /> I solemnly promised to do so, and we made our way across the room to where Desiree was sitting with Gloria and Molly. I hadn\u2019t really thought about it before, but it makes a lot of sense that Molly would want to get Desiree\u2019s perspective on her own current situation\u2026 after all, Desiree recently had to attempt to integrate a buried personality into her existing psyche in a healthy way.<br /> <br /> The three of them greeted us, and Soon Hee asked if she could speak with Desiree privately. I offered a private room as the venue, and assured her that I\u2019d be there if it made her more comfortable. Gloria was okay with it, and Molly excused herself to head back to the bar to talk to Jacob some more. The three of us made our way out of the theater shortly thereafter.<br /> <br /> The conversation that followed wasn\u2019t much fun. Soon Hee explained the situation with Hollywood\u2019s hobgoblin saboteur to Desiree, and went on to postulate that Desiree had twice been the victim of the beast\u2019s tricks already. I brought up the incident at the Rose &amp; Thorn, but didn\u2019t know what the other incident might have been. Soon Hee started talking about something involving White Maria, but Desiree just turned kind of red and shut down that avenue of conversation before I could learn more.<br /> <br /> She also mentioned that she believed Desiree had been struggling with her Clarity lately. While I\u2019ll admit that her behavior has been a little squirrelly over the past week or so, I never would have guess that it might have been caused by a drop in her Clarity. I... hope there\u2019s some way we can help her, but I confess that when Clarity issues come up, I usually just try to keep quiet and hope for the best. I don\u2019t know what else I can do.<br /> <br /> Soon Hee suggested that Desiree head straight home, not bring anyone with her, and not communicate with anyone until the next day. She told Desiree that she wanted to follow her around for a day, and offered the option of either doing so openly or covertly\u2026 whichever made the other girl more comfortable. Desiree eventually opted for covert surveillance, in the hopes that this would draw the creature out so that we could get this whole situation resolved quickly.<br /> <br /> She was pretty shaken up by the whole conversation. I did what I could to comfort her, but she decided to head out pretty much immediately after. As we walked back into the theater, D approached me. Eying Soon Hee up and down, she asked with a cocky smirk, \u201cyou got plans for the evening, babe?\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cIf you\u2019re okay with that, honey. Miss Kwon and I were going to play with fire a little bit.\u201d<br /> <br /> D chuckled knowingly. \u201cSure, have fun,\u201d she said simply.<br /> <br /> I took her hand in mine. \u201cWe need to set some time aside for us,\u201d I said seriously. \u201cI mean, like all four of us, of course\u2026 but also just for you and me. Soon.\u201d<br /> <br /> D leaned in and kissed me. \u201cYeah,\u201d she agreed, \u201csoon. But you have fun tonight.\u201d She glanced up at the balcony. \u201cI\u2019ll see if Gloria\u2019s free. Or maybe\u2026 maybe see if Julia needs me.\u201d<br /> <br /> I followed her gaze and noticed that Marguerite and Yvette were still flirting heavily. I sighed.<br /> <br /> \u201cTell me how that\u2019s not going to end in tragedy,\u201d D muttered to herself.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019s a big girl,\u201d I said softly, \u201cwe have to trust her. We have to trust that she\u2019s changed.\u201d<br /> <br /> I apologized to Soon Hee and asked her to give me a moment, and D and I joined Marguerite, Yvette, and Julia at their table. Marguerite was trying to convince Julia to join the two of them for the evening, and Julia was attempting to beg off, and Yvette mostly looked uncomfortable about the whole thing. Julia looked at me and D like we were lifelines, and I took one of her hands in mine.<br /> <br /> \u201cJulia, honey, I want you to listen to me please,\u201d I said seriously. \u201cAlmost a year ago, now, I fell in love for the first time. It was wonderful, but it was also scary, because I was terrified of losing it. And then you and Marguerite invited the two of us into your bed, and I didn\u2019t know what to do. That night was one of the best of my life, but like I said before, I was also terrified. But <u><u>because</u></u> I spent that night with you, and D came back to me more in love than ever\u2026 I am so much more secure in our relationship than I would have been otherwise. Do you understand?\u201d<br /> <br /> Julia looked into my eyes, and gave me a watery smile. \u201cI think so. Thanks, Lori.\u201d For her part, Marguerite made her opinions of my little speech known in a more physical way, with a long deep kiss.<br /> <br /> After the three of them had left, D gave a little fist pump, kissed me on the cheek, and said \u201cyou\u2019re the best, babe. I\u2019m gonna see if Gloria wants to head back to her place.\u201d<br /> <br /> Something clicked in my head. \u201cIf you go back there, be careful,\u201d I said seriously. Then I filled her in on the details of the situation with Desiree. \u201cKeep an eye on her, okay? There\u2019s no telling what she might do \u2013 or what that creature from Hollywood might <u><u>make</u></u> her do \u2013 in her current state.\u201d<br /> <br /> D considered. \u201cYou know what, maybe the two of us should just take the downstairs guest room,\u201d she decided at last.<br /> <br /> And that\u2019s when the last person I expected walked through our front doors.<br /> <br /> Chalcedony. I haven\u2019t even <u><u>seen</u></u> her since she was taken from the Dream House last year for de-programming. I\u2019m not sure if she\u2019s actually harboring a grudge, or if she honestly doesn\u2019t feel safe here in the wake of what happened to her. And if that is the case\u2026 who could blame her, really?<br /> <br /> Calamity quickly filled me in on the situation. It turns out that Calamity had spoken with Molly earlier in the evening about unlocking her lost memories, and the two of them decided to start what could end up being a lengthy process tomorrow night. They decided to perform the dream therapy here at the Dream House, since it\u2019s a place both Molly and Calamity feel comfortable, and there\u2019s lots of assistance available if it becomes necessary. And to get Molly acclimated to this environment, Calamity offered to let her stay the night in our guest room. And to increase her sense of security, she wanted her friend Chalcedony to join her.<br /> <br /> I met Chalcedony as she entered, thinking that it might be best if I was our main point of contact with the azure ing\u00e9nue. No offense meant to my nearest and dearest, but most of the others aren\u2019t quite as objective as they maybe should be when it comes to Chalcedony. She eyed me warily as I approached, but made no move to avoid me.<br /> <br /> \u201cChalcedony,\u201d I said, in what I hoped was a friendly, welcoming voice.<br /> <br /> \u201cLori,\u201d she replied. She didn\u2019t offer me her hand or anything, but I didn\u2019t sense any overt hostility from her either.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s\u2026 look, it\u2019s really good to see you again,\u201d I said fervently.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m just here for Molly,\u201d she said quickly. \u201cShe needs me. I don\u2019t want to hurt her like I did Ginny\u2026\u201d I heard a note of genuine regret in her voice at that.<br /> <br /> \u201cI know,\u201d I said in reply, \u201cbut\u2026 I\u2019m glad you came anyway. If you\u2019d care to follow me, I\u2019ll take you up to the guest room.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded and fell into step behind me. Once we\u2019d cleared the common area, I turned to face her. \u201cLook, Chalcedony\u2026 I know you\u2019re only here because Molly needs you, and I know that you\u2019re still not comfortable with me or my motley. And I get that; nobody blames you for feeling that way. But, now that you\u2019re here\u2026 I\u2019d just like to say that I\u2019m sorry. We all genuinely regret the way things went down.\u201d<br /> <br /> She looked into my eyes searchingly for about twenty seconds, and then looked away. \u201cThanks,\u201d she said simply. And that was the end of that. We knocked on the door, Molly answered, the two of them hugged, and I left them to their own devices.<br /> <br /> Soon Hee was waiting alone at the same table when I returned to the theater. \u201cAll done?\u201d she asked with a raised eyebrow and obvious amusement. \u201cNobody else needs to be greeted, spoken to, kissed goodnight and tucked in?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSorry,\u201d I said sheepishly, \u201cbut I think that\u2019s the last of it. I\u2019m all yours for the rest of the evening.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSounds great,\u201d she said in reply. \u201cAre we staying here, or heading back to my hotel?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell,\u201d I said, thinking, \u201cmy fianc\u00e9e and her girlfriend are staying in the guest room downstairs tonight, so our room should be free.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cExcellent,\u201d she said, \u201cjust point me in the right direction.\u201d Then she stood up and swept me off of my feet (literally). She carried me up the stairs and into my bedroom. She threw me on to the bed. She removed my clothing quickly and efficiently, tossing it negligently into a random corner. Her own clothes followed quickly thereafter, and wanton carnality ensued.<br /> <br /> She\u2019s\u2026 wow. She\u2019s intense. The only experience I can really compare it to is when I slept with Queen Charlotte. Soon Hee knows what she wants and goes for it. She was very aggressive with me, but never cruel or inconsiderate. She used her flames to enhance the act; warming me in all the right places and mixing sensations in unexpected ways. It was often ecstatic and occasionally a little uncomfortable, but never actually painful or unwanted. I adored every moment of it, and I flatter myself in thinking that she enjoyed the experience as well.<br /> <br /> It took a while, but I think I finally wore her out. She\u2019s sleeping now, and I\u2019m trying desperately to concentrate on my studies and putting it off by writing in this journal. I can\u2019t let my medical studies fall by the wayside, and I\u2019m going to have far less time over the next month, what with wedding and honeymoon plans, running the Dream House, planning the rescue, and all the <u><u>other</u></u> training I\u2019ll be going through. I\u2019ll be joining Jacob and Calamity\u2019s sparring sessions starting next Tuesday, and D has offered to teach me some of the basics of boxing as well. I know I don\u2019t have a lot of time to learn everything I might need to know to impress the Pilgrims, but\u2026 well, here\u2019s hoping.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T12:54:35-08:00","id":1156134,"title":"","content":"<b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> Friday, May 8<sup>th</sup><br /> Nine years, one month, fifteen days<br /> Days without stabbing: 6<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a beautiful night and I\u2019ve got the roof to myself. Everyone is entwined with their evening\u2019s fling. I am not comfortable with Yvette staying the night with Marguerite, even if Julia is with them. I am glad they\u2019ve moved forward but this feels like a step in the wrong direction given their past. I just don\u2019t think there can ever be a healthy sexual relationship there given what transpired in Arcadia. But hey, maybe I\u2019m wrong. Maybe it will all be fine. Yeah\u2026<br /> <br /> Or maybe it\u2019s just that her last giant mistake is in the guest room right now. Chalcedony is here to lend moral support to Molly, who\u2019s staying over tonight to acclimate before we do the dream healing tomorrow to try to recover her lost memories. Objectively, she seems to be on the level and given that I haven\u2019t spoken to her since she was deprogrammed I really ought to give her a chance. Molly certainly loves her. But fuck it, I don\u2019t like her and I don\u2019t trust her and I\u2019m glad Jacob is going to be in the room to watch my back while I\u2019m working tomorrow night.<br /> <br /> And I\u2019m nervous as hell about what the Oneiromancy is going to dredge up. I guess technically it will be my first dream healing as a Sister, not that I wouldn\u2019t have done it anyway. I\u2019m not exactly big on asking permission for my actions. But being part of the Family of Silent Nights gives me more opportunities to grow my skills and makes people more likely to come to me for help. Dreams are powerful and dangerous and while all of us are aware not everyone has the strength of will and ability to fight back the nightmares and the dream poisons. And perhaps even more than that, not everyone can use dreams to help\u2026 to heal\u2026<br /> <br /> Wow, that sounds so cheesy but fuck it, I like being able to give someone a happy dream. I like being able to help. It feels good. And soon I\u2019ll be able to trap nightmares. Now that I\u2019ve passed my trial I can train and learn from Juan Carlos and the others.<br /> <br /> The trial wasn\u2019t what I expected. It wasn\u2019t a test of my skills or fighting prowess, hell I was told I had to deal with it without resorting to fighting. I guess it makes sense. The Family doesn\u2019t approach anyone that hasn\u2019t demonstrated that they\u2019ve got skill. But what they test is resolve and mental stability. (Yeah, that one is SO my strong suit isn\u2019t it?) And Juan Carlos knew just what to hit me with. I was trapped back in Snow Globe and trying to find my way out. There were ways, but each was blocked by a guardian\u2026 Timmy. Mr Grey. Dad. Mom. And damn him, but they weren\u2019t angry. No, nothing that easy. They were sad\u2026 they were disappointed\u2026 I\u2019d hurt them. I\u2019d killed them. They accused and recriminated me. They were cold and bitter. But I had to face them to pass. I had to face my actions. I had to admit that I\u2019d wronged them and endure their jeering and dismissal and insults. I had to stand before my own guilt calmly, without giving into the urge to fight or flee. Well, I might not have been a rock, but I stood. I looked them each in the eye and took their abuse without yielding. I admitted what I had done. I admitted I was wrong. And just as I emerged, surrounded by those I had wronged a swarm of enemies came. They cried out as they were attacked, swept away from me and overwhelmed before I could get past the faceless hordes to save any of them. They begged me to help them\u2026 to protect them\u2026 and then cursed me for failing them again as they died. I did struggle at first but then I caught myself and I forced myself to remember it was a dream. They were dead. These nightmares could do nothing to them. I had already hurt them and they were beyond any further suffering. I steadied myself and focused rather than raging mindlessly against the monsters.<br /> <br /> And that was why I passed. Because I didn\u2019t break down and let myself get lost in the dream. It is crucial to remain focused and never lose sight of where I am or what I am trying to accomplish. Misdirection and deceit and trickery to trap the unwary. Fear to break the weak. Juan Carlos seemed pleased that I passed and perhaps even a little surprised by my strength. I don\u2019t blame him. I haven\u2019t exactly been stable and even I was a bit surprised at just how steady I managed to be. I think the meditation training with White Maria has really paid off in that respect. I am going to make sure I take the time to center myself before starting with Molly tomorrow and I shall have to let White Maria know next time I see her.<br /> <br /> And I should also let her know I\u2019ve talked to Becky. She hasn\u2019t brought it up more than in passing but I know it can\u2019t be easy to be the friend stuck in the middle of an awkward situation like that. I mean, we didn\u2019t even have a proper breakup or anything. I don\u2019t think either of us really knew where things stood so there was no way she could. I\u2019m glad I called Becky and told her we needed to talk. After facing down Juan Carlos\u2019 dream I likely would have put it off otherwise. I did make sure to get my act in the first part of the show and not schedule myself for anything in the second act. I figured I\u2019d either be with Becky or in no fit shape to perform. As it turned out, I spent most of the evening sitting with her and the visiting dragons. And I did flirt a bit with Laughing Carp (as Lori clearly had flirting with Soon Hee covered) but not quite the hot and heavy like before. I\u2019ll chalk that up to it being way too damn long since I\u2019d been with anyone and a bit of being upset with Becky. Don\u2019t get me wrong, I DO want to play with that adorable little water dragon and I don\u2019t believe she is quite as clueless as she acts but Becky was genuinely concerned that I was going to harm the girl and cause a diplomatic incident so I am dialing it back a bit.<br /> <br /> So\u2026 we\u2019re still friends. And Becky has zero issues fucking her friends so despite the fact that I\u2019m alone tonight our amazing sexual chemistry isn\u2019t a thing of the past. As far as what else we are\u2026 not sure. I drew her to the media room so we could speak in private and as soon as we were alone she just crossed her arms (and her hair\u2026 which was fucking adorable even if it was a serious moment) and waited. And as soon as I started talking it just hit me that she wasn\u2019t angry (really) or sad or anything as much as she was just\u2026 resigned. Of course it didn\u2019t work. It never works for her. She\u2019s a friend and one hell of a good time but she\u2019s not The One. She\u2019s never the girl you take home and love. She\u2019s just the fucktoy you play with until you find that girl.<br /> <br /> And I knew, on some level, about her issues. She\u2019s never comfortable really talking about it and while it\u2019s clear she\u2019s been down this road a few times I don\u2019t know the whole story. But I knew she was afraid to make that attachment, to let her guard down enough to love someone and be hurt by them. So\u2026 so yeah the second I started to draw back she withdrew because of course I didn\u2019t really love her. Because no one really loves her. Doesn\u2019t that sound familiar\u2026<br /> <br /> And maybe I was too lost and hurt to really see it but I hurt her. We both needed each other but neither of us was willing or able to reach out. I feel like a bitch for hurting her now. But I was reeling from Gawain leaving. And even now I don\u2019t know. I want to push past and reach out to her and love her the way she deserves to be loved. And yes, I do fucking love her. But right now, that idea fucking terrifies me. What if she\u2019s too damaged to ever trust me and love me back? What if she leaves me like Gawain did? Part of me is screaming and yelling at me to run away from her before she can. But I just can\u2019t shake that moment when I realized it was like looking into a mirror.<br /> <br /> Goddammit\u2026 We are both such fucking broken things inside\u2026 and I want to fix her\u2026 but I just don\u2019t know if I can.<br /> <br /> No. No more whining. I am fucking Calamity. I am strong enough to face down whatever demons Molly\u2019s got in her past. I am strong enough to fight past Becky\u2019s fears and defenses. I don\u2019t need Gawain\u2019s strength, I\u2019ve got my own. I am not his monster anymore. I am my own goddamn monster and I am fucking strong enough.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> The House was once again host to several guests this afternoon. Lori came back to the house with Joan and Andromeda in tow. Desiree and Veronica had spent the night with Julia and Insincere Marguerite, and Gloria had spent time with De La Rocha. All in all it was a pretty full kitchen. Conversation was light for the most part. Calamity brought up the idea of us going to the opening night of Fury Road next Thursday night. I asked Luna, who seemed interested, and told Calamity that we were in. The other members of the motley all agreed and Calamity planned to go and get tickets later. There was even talk of dressing \u201cin character\u201d for the movie, i.e.: in leather. Lori seemed interested in that and I think the rest of us tangentially agreed to do it too. Things did get a little more interesting after Salk stood up to leave and said that he was off to do some evil deeds. Or something like that. Joan, ever the literal one, was distressed by the idea of someone intentionally going out and doing bad things. The idea of the bad boy/girl was brought up and Joan said that she did not find it attractive at all. Lori pointed out that De La Rocha has the bad girl image, but Joan shot that down by pointing out that she knew that De La Rocha was actually a good person. Remind me to make sure that Joan never finds out about my past. I\u2019m not sure that she\u2019d see me in the same way that she does now. To be honest I\u2019m not actually sure how she sees me now, but it can\u2019t be that bad because she hasn\u2019t confronted me about anything. I mean, there are known ex-Loyalists in the freehold, but they were all from the Director and all had been programmed to serve him. Well most of them. Desiree seemed to serve him out of a genuine desire to do so, and Joan hasn\u2019t come down on her for anything. Maybe Joan wouldn\u2019t have a problem with me? Though, I\u2019m not sure I\u2019m curious enough to find out.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Joan, it was kind of funny. After everyone was done eating Lori made some comment about going outside to stretch her wings and Joan was by her side in an instant. Lori didn\u2019t look surprised by the other woman\u2019s action so I assumed this was prearranged. So, the pair of them went outside and Lori scooped up Joan into her arms and took off into the sky to fly around the backyard. I gotta give her credit, Lori is stronger than she looks if she can pick up another person and fly around seemingly effortlessly. Lori was obviously having fun and Joan also seemed to be rather enjoying herself. The smile spread across her face was almost childlike. It was nice to see.<br /> <br /> Another interesting thing was brought up at breakfast. Lori was talking about the fact that the Pilgrims would be testing her on her weaknesses and trying to figure out what those were. Joan suggested that Lori\u2019s impulse control might be tested. Lori really is a creature of the moment, so I suppose I can see that. Lori made the joke about spreading ice cream on De La Rocha\u2019s breasts and then not touching it for 30 minutes. I\u2019m not sure that\u2019s exactly what Joan had in mind, funny as it is. Joan also suggested that they might test Lori on her need to be liked by everyone. I hadn\u2019t really thought much about it, but she has a point. Lori really does like to have folks think good things about her. She\u2019s a performer so she likes to be the center of attention, but it\u2019s more than that. Lori doesn\u2019t want anyone to think badly of her. It\u2019s like she\u2019s insecure and needs people\u2019s approval. I don\u2019t know what she could feel insecure about. She\u2019s bright, kind, generous and an amazing performer. I can think of several people who would love to be in her shoes.<br /> <br /> After our overnight guests left another one showed up on our doorstep. This time it was Juan Carlos. Apparently he was here to test Calamity to see if she was good enough to be inducted into the Family of the Silent Nights. I was sure that Calamity would pass whatever test he posed to her. While she was getting tested I went to go talk to Lowjack about Molly. I brought up Molly\u2019s plan and asked him what kind of person Shayna was before the Table was used on her. Lowjack reiterated what Twitch had said for the most part. Shayna was not a good person. She was an accomplished liar, was more than capable of violence, and held a great animosity towards Changelings for some reason. This is probably why she so faithfully served her Master, though we\u2019re not exactly sure who that was. Like I said, Shayna was a very good liar and it\u2019s not known what was truth and what was lies when she spoke. She didn\u2019t elaborate on her Durance either. Lowjack said that we pretty much have three options as far as Molly goes. We could forbid her from remembering her past. In this case she would likely resent us. In that case I would probably lose a friend. The second option is that we let her go through the Dream Healing to remember her past and she doesn\u2019t like what she finds out. In this case her personality would likely change somewhat based on her old thoughts and feelings. I guess this is the best-case scenario. The last option would be that Molly completely reverts to who she used to be and the Winter Court would be forced to kill her for the safety of the Freehold. I really don\u2019t like this possibility. We agreed that it was Molly\u2019s right to find out about her past, and that we shouldn\u2019t stop her. I told Lowjack that I would let him know when and where the Dream Healing would take place. I then headed back to the Dream House.<br /> <br /> I got back shortly before Calamity was done being tested. She came downstairs looking rather shaken up. Juan Carlos gave me a significant look, so I made an Irish coffee for Calamity and gave it to her. She seemed to appreciate the gesture and drank it in short order. She did not elaborate on what exactly the test entailed but I could tell that it was something that really unnerved my friend. Given Calamity\u2019s personality I would say that she had to face past demons. She doesn\u2019t blink in the face of violence or threat. She tends to react to such things with anger and a firm hand. The only thing that I have seen bother her this much was when she admitted that she had killed her parents during the Truth or Dare game. I don\u2019t know if that\u2019s all she saw or if there was more. I wasn\u2019t planning on asking her though. That had to have been a deeply personal experience and I\u2019m not going to intrude on that. Juan Carlos, in an effort to lighten the mood, offered to take Calamity out for a steak dinner. He invited the rest of us too, and we all agreed. So, we went out to a nice steak house and had good food. I\u2019m not sure how we got in to be honest. Insincere Marguerite was, as usual, not wearing shoes, and Juan Carlos was essentially not wearing a shirt, but somehow we got in. I guess it\u2019s best not to look the gift horse in the mouth.<br /> <br /> When we got back from dinner Calamity called a motley meeting. We seem to be doing a lot of those lately. She wanted to tell the motley about what was going on with Molly. So, she and I explained the situation and what the options were. Lori brought up the point that Molly remembering her past might have bad consequences. The rest of us agreed, but no one could deny that it was her right to know about who she used to be. For good or ill I think this is going to happen.<br /> <br /> The show itself went like normal. All the ladies were great onstage. Lori really outdid herself tonight too. It wasn\u2019t a new number, but she really seemed to put her all into it. The crowd definitely liked it. After all of that the ladies made their usual rounds through the crowd. Calamity went over to where Becky was sitting and then the two of them got up and left the room. I\u2019m assuming that they went off to have that long overdue talk. Lori went over to talk to Yvette, who joined us for the show tonight. I\u2019m not sure what the conversation was about but Lori seemed a little less tense leaving the table than she did walking to it. Must have been something positive.<br /> <br /> After that I talked to Molly about what Lowjack had said. I told her that it was pretty much agreed upon that Shayna had not been a good person. She was violent towards Changelings and lied a lot. Molly was still had her mind set on remembering her past though, despite the warnings from me and others. I admitted to her that I was afraid that she might not like what she found out, and she would be unable to forget it again. I can admire her conviction in this matter. I just hope that it all works out for the best. I also suggested to Molly that she talk to Desiree since she had experience in regaining her memories all at one time. She might be able to tell Molly what to expect. I had brought the idea to Desiree earlier in the day with the idea that Molly could talk to her after the show. Desiree agreed and I sent Molly over to talk to the former Loyalist. Molly was a little hesitant at first since her perceptions of Desiree are colored by Chalcedony\u2019s deep-seated hatred for her. I eventually convinced Molly that it would be okay and she went over to talk to the other woman.<br /> <br /> Molly came back after talking to Desiree. She\u2019d only been gone a few minutes, but they did talk. Apparently Desiree told Molly that her personality would change once her memories came back, and that she would be a different person than she is now. Desiree didn\u2019t think that the past memories would completely subsume Molly\u2019s current personality though, so that was good. I think this whole thing just made Molly more excited to do this, so I texted Calamity and she came over to the bar so we could talk about when and where we were going to do this. Molly said that she would be comfortable doing the Dream Healing at her place, Chalcedony\u2019s place or the Dream House. I thought about it for a moment before suggesting the Dream House. I told Molly that this was going to bring back some bad memories and she might not want that experience associated with her apartment or Chalcedony\u2019s place. Those locations should still be seen as safe havens for her. Molly agreed and Calamity and I briefly talked about where to do it. We agreed on the guest room over the garage. Calamity also suggested that Molly sleep in the guest room tonight so it would be familiar to her tomorrow night and she would be comfortable there. So, yeah. We\u2019re going to do this tomorrow night. Once we had the details all planned out Molly acknowledged that she knew that the Winter Court would have an assassin nearby during the Dream Healing. I hadn\u2019t mentioned it out loud, but Molly is not a fool. She knows how the Winter Court works. If the situation had been different and it was someone else trying to retrieve their memories then she likely would have been the assassin waiting in the shadows.<br /> <br /> After things started to wind down Molly said that she was ready to go on up to the guest room. She asked if Chalcedony would be able to come over and spend the night with her. We said that would be fine and Molly went on to call her not-girlfriend. Chalcedony showed up a short while later. I believe Lori greeted her when she arrived and told her that she was happy to see her. Chalcedony has not been back here since <i><i>that</i></i> night, but she came for Molly so I guess that says something. We showed the pair up to the guest room and left them to get settled in. I went back down to the bar to finish up my shift. I ended up talking to Hailey for a bit. She wanted to make sure that Molly will be okay. She had overheard some of what had been said and she was concerned for her friend/drinking buddy. I tried to reassure her that Molly would be fine, and that she was in good hands. I hope I sounded more confident than I felt. <br /> <br /> I will admit that I am still a little afraid of what might happen tomorrow night. I don\u2019t want to lose my friend, but in some way no matter what happens I will lose her. She will not be the same person that she is at this moment. She will be different. Shaped by her past like the rest of us, and I don\u2019t know what that will do to her. Molly will lose the innocence that she has. She is not an innocent, I know that, but she seems like one in certain situations. The joy that shone on her face when we went to Disneyland was a sight to see. But after tomorrow night she will look at the world with more jaded eyes and that wonder will disappear. I don\u2019t know for certain that she will become jaded, but it seems likely given what I\u2019ve heard about Shayna. Shayna carried violence in her heart and there is usually something bad that puts it there. People who respond with violence are usually jaded. I was. Hell, I still am. I wonder what name she will go by once she remembers her past? Will she stick with Molly or go back to Shayna? And is that even her real name? It seems likely that it\u2019s a pseudonym. Molly had been asking before about changing her name. I wonder if this will push her to doing just that. It would make sense if she does. She will not be Molly anymore, and she will not completely be Shayna, so I guess a new name would be appropriate. This is all dependent on the healing going well I know. I am trying to be positive about this. I really don\u2019t want to have to kill another friend.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XCIV</i><br /> <br /> Lorelei got like 44 successes on her show. Calamity got 16 and Insincere Marguerite (assisted by Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne) got 15. Vainglory is pretty potent.<br /> <br /> Calamity is now a member of the Family of Silent Nights<br /> <br /> Molly\u2019s story is careening toward a major point. We all wait to see what happens. Meanwhile a creature stalks the city.<br /> <br /> See you next time. Comments and Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T02:01:55-08:00","id":1156262,"title":"","content":"A good while ago, Baroness, we discussed the merits of a Changeling being able to discard their own past completely, willingly or not. I love that you've hit upon the downsides of such an action; namely, having no past innevitably causes someone to try and rediscover it, which ruins the very act of hiding it away to begin with for better or worse. If there's anything that drives humanity, it's curiosity, which is also one of its greatest weaknesses. Very much looking forwards to the resolution.<br /> <br /> I admit, my interpretation of Lorelei's test would be that it would be combat, or her conviction to saving a life if it means ending one. I hadn't considered them being will based. It's a cool interpretation, and another development I'm looking forward to. Also, how on earth do you all keep track of the dice Lorelei rolls for her socials? Do you have a bucket of dice on hand, a digital dice roller, or just use a handful, roll them, count the successes, then reroll them until they stop succeeding?<br /> <br /> It really has been that long since Chalcedony has appeared. My how time flies. It's good that she's appearing in a supportive role, rather than as a threat. Rounds her character out nicely.<br /> <br /> Speaking of rounding out, Calamity is moving in an interesting direction. She's filling in for Gawain in the Family of Silent Nights at the Dreamhouse, she's recognising the faults of her own actions (while also appreciating why said actions happened) and, in a way, she's even becoming a doctor for Changelings in their dreams. Much like her glass, Calamity is smoothing her rough edges out and maturing greatly as a person. That's not to say she's not capable of being rough - her glass still cuts after all, even if it's smoothed out - but its not her default reaction to many things anymore. Good times and bad ones are allowing her to grow. It's a really cool evolution.<br /> <br /> Similarly, its interesting seeing how Yvette remains someone Insincere Margeurite is unable to move on from. True, Margeurite has changed over time (for better or worse), but she hasn't ever really let go of Yvette. It's an addiction she can't quite shake, though she is at least able to handle it relatively safely. Let's just see if she ends up getting burned over it...<br /> <br /> As for Jacob, very cool (not a pun) seeing him being so supportive of everyone in spite of the distance being an elemental gives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T07:08:10-08:00","id":1156331,"title":"","content":"*singing* Omelet Duuuuuu Fromaaage!!! Totally forgot she missed out on when television cartoons started going up in quality again<br /> <br /> So many reactions.<br /> <br /> First off, 44 successes?! Holy crap, high wyrd Changelings are amazing! What kind of godly dice pool was she rolling, even on an extended roll?<br /> <br /> On Joan's idea about the &quot;coolness&quot; of evil, it's interesting how my opinions on this have changed over the years. I'm not a perfect person by any measure and I've hurt people in the small ways we all do when we're upset or tired or both. But I don't feel comfortable even pretending to be evil in a game anymore. I still find spookiness cool, but I don't find the confidence of evil overlords and predatory creatures of the night as fascinating as I used to, because I can't stop thinking about the people who get hurt by it when it plays out in real life.<br /> <br /> Is the shirtless thing Juan-Carlos' Major Frailty? Cause that is hilarious, awesome and hilariously awesome.<br /> <br /> Also congrats to Calamity! Glad to see that I was right that she was doing better than she thinks. She's coping, and that, along with not killing anyone, is all we can ask. (just saw I was preempted on this by Taidragon...damnit). Did Juan-Carlos make every aspect of that dream, or was it a general theme of &quot;start in place you hate, face those you've wronged and remember its all a dream&quot; that fills in the details depending on the dreamer?<br /> <br /> And speaking of her, Calamity Delusion Count: 1 overall. I'm starting to wonder when it will come into play.<br /> <br /> I had to look up sexy pajamas, since I hadn't really seen those before. I'd like to say that some of what I saw looked neither warm nor comfortable, thus failing on both points of pajamas, though honestly, failing on either point is an auto-fail too.<br /> <br /> Anyways, final thought. I know this has come up before and I've said nothing, but it feels weird to have Changelings in-universe acknowledge the official names for their Kiths, Seemings and especially their Clarity meter. Like, real psychological stability can't be rated on a scale from one to ten, so why would they do that? I know some contracts tell you someone's exact Clarity level, but I assumed that in-universe it just gave you a general sense of their level of stability. And why wouldn't they just call it sanity? Most of the party at least (IM excluded) don't seem to think of themselves as that psychologically inhuman.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Having someone try to rediscover your past doesn't seem like an inherent problem with erasing your past as much as it is a problem with peoples' reactions to it. Though I guess that's just a semantic distinction. The bigger problem I see is having no anchor (or even Anchors). Without a past, you have no experiences to draw on to color your actions, for better or worse. To gain empathy for others problems, you'd have to go through all the mundane negative experiences all over again: getting yelled at for mistakes you didn't make, losing a pet or loved one, your first heartbreak, etc. Plus, maybe this is not a universal problem, but for me, my past extends beyond my lifetime to the history of my people. Without that past to ground part of my identity, I'd feel very lost and out-of-place, just like Molly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 11-06-2017, 10:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T13:11:44-08:00","id":1156454,"title":"","content":"Taidragon: Thank you! I am glad you have enjoyed, and trying to see it from Molly's POV is interesting. Her case is different from Desiree's, where it was all sort of accidental, Molly stewed on it awhile then had to know.<br /> <br /> Keeping track of Lorelei's dice for socials is her player's job. I will let them explain.<br /> <br /> Chalcedony is a peculiar case. We see a lot more of her in last night's session.<br /> <br /> Yes it is nice to see Calamity shifting gears toward a good end rather than bad.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite's Wyrd and story and Yvette's Wyrd and story are closely tied. Eventually the Wyrd would compel them to find each other. Yvette lacked the drive to ever escape Arcadia on her own. Insincere Marguerite got her home. Yet no two ways about it, Insincere Marguerite abused her. Only in Arcadia when she was out of her mind, but she abused her. Can one ever come back from being an abuser? What does someone do to be forgiven? Do they have any right to ask? And will they abuse again? Yvette has loved, and hated, Insincere Marguerite very much for some time. It is unlikely to ever be only one, but loving is more than edging out hating at this point.<br /> <br /> Master Aquatosic: I will defer to Lorelei's player on die pool size.<br /> <br /> Playing evil is a way to explore and deal with one's demons. Some people make peace with their demons early on. Some never do.<br /> <br /> No one knows what Juan-Carlos's frailties are. It could be...Insincere Marguerite can't wear shoes on bare earth.<br /> <br /> Calamity chose to buy up her Clarity, which is part of why Desiree, not Calamity, is the beasts chew toy.<br /> <br /> Pajamas are weird to me in general. For kids, sure, but putting on clothes to sleep must just be a thing in cooler climes<br /> <br /> I presume Changelings have found certain kith tendencies by now and given them names. I know different GMs handle this differently.<br /> <br /> I am glad people empathize with Molly. I tried to stress her emptiness (even her kith being Manniken has a sort of resonance of falsehood)and I think it made her current predicament easier to empathize with.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Last night we had the Dream Healing, and a showdown between Molly and Shayna. We find out why Molly was a loyalist before. There are long talks with Chalcedony. There is a short dance party. Insicnere Marguerite and Yvette struggle to find their new place in each other's lives. Join us then...though feel free to continue the above discussions I am enjoying them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T14:52:44-08:00","id":1156486,"title":"","content":"Thanks for commenting, everyone! As always its nice to know that people are interested. It's been a great story so far, and like the rest of you we players are looking forward to seeing where it goes.<br /> <br /> So, Lorelei's social dice pool is... complicated. I have a cheat sheet in my character folder to make things a little easier when it comes to rolling up her performances, and I'll try to replicate it here. Keep in mind that this is when Lori is going all-out and using all of her abilities to their utmost, and this is by far her best pool... other social rolls are significantly less impressive, though still potent. This also assumes that some of the contracts and abilities listed below are already active when the roll comes up, and thus their activation cost doesn't affect the cap on Glamour spent in a round.<br /> <br /> <b>7</b> dice for Presence - Lori maxed this out when her Wyrd went up<br /> <b>7</b> dice for Expression - Lori likewise maxed this skill out as soon as the cap was raised.<br /> <b>1</b> die for Specialization (Singing, Dance)<br /> <b>1</b> die for Adroitness - for her recently renewed Pledge to look after the Spring Court's interests in the Dream House<br /> <b>2</b> dice for Striking Looks<br /> <b>2</b> dice for Fame 2<br /> <b>2</b> dice more for Striking Looks when Splendor of the Envoy's Protection (Vainglory 3) is invoked<br /> <b>12</b> dice when Lorelei spends 6 Glamour on the roll... as a high-Wyrd Fairest she gets 2 dice for each point of Glamour spent on the roll, and she typically spends one less than the cap.<br /> <b>7 </b>dice or <b>7 </b><i>successes</i> - depending on whether or not she gets an exceptional success invoking Songs of Distant Arcadia (Vainglory 2).<br /> <b>SUCCESSES</b> dice - when Font of Inspiration (Verdant Spring 1) is invoked<br /> <br /> So right there we have either <b>41+SUCCESSES</b> dice rolled, or <b>34+SUCCESSES</b> dice rolled <b>+7 </b><i>automatic</i> successes, depending on the activation roll on Songs of Distant Arcadia. There are also a few other wrinkles to consider. Since there are no official rules for high Wyrd Minstrel kith changelings, it was house-ruled that Lori gets 8-again on Expression rolls <i>not</i> used to activate a power. Her basic Minstrel kith power allows her to spend single point of Glamour to re-roll any failed dice on an Expression roll, essentially making it a rote action (this is why she typically spends one less than the cap to add dice to the initial roll). This means that she is by and large usually rolling around 40 dice, adding seven auto-successes, re-rolling all failed dice once, and re-rolling successes until they come up as failures. As this is a social roll, she also rolls 5 additional dice separately which are only applied to members of the Spring Court, thanks to her Mantle.<br /> <br /> So in the most recent journal, she resulted in 44 successes (48 with the Spring Court). She kinda/sorta surpassed that in the most recent session (journal pending), which resulted in 45 successes (46 with the Spring Court). I'll beat that 50 threshold sooner or later!<br /> <br /> Honestly, as the Baroness mentioned in a recent conversation we had, it's kind of ridiculous what powerful Changelings are capable of when it comes to Expression rolls. Even Marguerite and Calamity, who have each been performing professionally for less than a year and don't have <i>nearly</i> the number of advantages that Lori does, fairly routinely roll 15-20 successes. If you go by the general guidelines in the Chronicles of Darkness rules, that's the equivalent of a once-in-a-lifetime experience; something you'd witness once and then remember forever. We've essentially had to scale up our expectations when it comes to this particular set of skills in this game.<br /> <br /> So that's the breakdown. I'll be happy to answer any questions I can, if anyone is still reading through all the math and mechanics!<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> I realized that I oversimplified above. The high-Wyrd kith blessing the Baroness came up with for the Minstrel kith was actually to give them a more reasonable 9-again on Expression rolls. This becomes 8-again when compounded with the 9-again from Lori's Professional Training merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2591,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","user":"PenitentTom","date":". 11-06-2017, 06:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T15:24:54-08:00","id":1156499,"title":"","content":"As a brief aside, the only reason Insincere Marguerite is getting ~15 successes is she is is getting about a third of them from being assisted by <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne. Last session she rolled 3 successes and got 7 from Vainglory, 5 from extra dice from Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne's successes.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T18:55:36-08:00","id":1156537,"title":"","content":"Starting to think that the Wizened artisans and artists that complain about their stuff never measuring up to the best mortal work are underselling themselves","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T21:38:15-08:00","id":1156570,"title":"","content":"System-wise anyway yes","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T21:40:15-08:00","id":1156574,"title":"","content":"That's an impressive layout for Lorelei's powers. I can only imagine the feeling of breaking through each success-threshold over time. Was it a deliberate accumulation of merits, contracts and abilities, or an accidental discovery that sort of snowballed?<br /> <br /> I should clarify that my question was less on how Lorelei's dice pool got so big, and more the literal logistics on how you all rolled it. I knew you all weren't just taking a fistful of dice as Lorelei's dicepool, I just wasn't sure how you guys managed all the dice for the rolls. Still, very interesting to learn the backdrop for Lorelei's sledgehammer socials.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm actually a little surprised that, with Lorelei such a potent singer, there hasn't emerged a rival of some sort to challenge her. In my experience, games where that kind of potency is attained tends to have power-creep settle in to prevent players from getting too complacent and overconfident in their abilities. Mind, the ST in that scenario tended to accumulate players who power-gamed the system to the best of their abilities, so it may just be the approach they adopted to deal with that kind of scenario...<br /> <br /> Dangit Baroness, now you've made me even more hyped for the resolution than before. Now I have two Changeling events that I'm seriously looking forward to (the other being the second edition kickstarter). XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T05:17:43-08:00","id":1156638,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5803_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5803\" data-vbnamecard=\"5803\">Taidragon</a>: Lori's impressive Expression die pool wasn't something I actually <i>planned</i>, though I admit that I tend to prioritize powers and merits that will help her out in that area when spending experience. Less so lately, of course, what with the Pilgrims probing for weaknesses.<br /> <br /> As for the physical act of rolling dice, well... I do it the old fashioned way. My Sunday night dice bag contains 40 ten-siders (what can I say? I play a lot of <i>Chronicles of Darkness</i> and I have GMed multiple <i>7th Sea </i>campaigns, both 1st and 2nd edition. I have a lot of d10s). I pour 'em out on the table, put however many I don't need for the roll back in the bag - or alternately borrow one or two from another player - and start rolling. I separate the successes from the failures first, then re-roll the failed dice once (rote action) and separate again. Double-fails go back in the bag. I count what's left on the table, then re-roll (8-again), separate the new failures, count successes, and add to the previous total. Repeat as necessary. After I have a total, I add any automatic successes generated by Contracts and then roll five more dice using the same methods and add that for any Spring Courtiers in the audience. It can take a minute or two to tally up the results, as you can probably guess.<br /> <br /> Lori's pretty focused on Annika as a rival, though that hasn't come up in journals as much lately as it did early in the campaign. And, of course, that animosity is almost certainly one-sided, as I've never seen any indication that Annika has any negative feelings about Lori... or deigns to notice her at all, which of course just makes it worse for Lori. If the Baroness chooses to introduce a new rival, Lori will meet that challenge with her usual poise and grace, and probably won't fantasize nightly about clawing her eyes out in public. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> On the other hand, there's a lot going on in the game right now, both in general and with Lori personally (impending wedding, potential return to Arcadia for the rescue mission, tests with the Pilgrims, ten thousand romantic entanglements, etc.), so adding a professional rival right now might be laying it on a bit thick. Ultimately not my call, though, and I rarely complain about Lori having too much screen-time (<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> again).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T12:43:46-08:00","id":1156769,"title":"","content":"It's possible Lori may have a rival come up. Annika is performing, but she is still not quite the Annika of old. Rivalry could be good, long as it stays professional.<br /> <br /> That said? Lori has a lot going on. She has nuptuals soon, and a trip to Arcadia, and joining the Pilgrims. She is pretty pressed in with stuff even ignoring worries about Desiree or Molly or he budding feelings for Veronica, or managing her 5 current girlfriends plus the couple. She has a lot on her atm.<br /> <br /> I'll also note, and this is a total aside not really addressing the suggestion, just a peek into my mind, one thing with MDH is how good a singer Lori is, or thief Insincere Marguerite is, or assassin Calamity is, or Warrior Jacob is, is very secondary in terms of the focus of the game. The game is about how Lori holds to her values and stays true to herself and her faith, how Insincere Marguerite takes herself off the path to becoming her abuser (or follow her into damnation), Calamity overcoming Snowglobe to become a force of good (or decend into madness and a brutal end) and Jacob thawing to become a good and more human person (or cold calculating killer). Indeed, many characters actual supremicy in their idiom is both a useful tool and a step toward damnation. It's all about how they react to the stories. The rival could work for showing what sort of person Lorelei is, but the time now is not right<br /> <br /> Thanks for ideas an suggestions, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T04:05:24-08:00","id":1156957,"title":"","content":"Thank you both for the comments about Calamity. I am glad you're enjoying her. Obviously, the plan was for her and Gawain to remain an item but alas that had to be changed due to Gawain's player leaving the game. It was rather a conundrum finding a reasonable reaction for her that didn't mire her into being no fun to play or deal with. The time jump helped since it let the bulk of her grief pass by off camera and have us pick back up with her ready to start to move forward. Oneiramancy has always been a fairly strong suit of hers (Wits+Empathy is a very mechanically good roll for her as a Darkling Wisperwisp) and the dream aspects are something I as a player found really interesting. It was a focus for Gawain and his player so Calamity always played a supporting role there. So her moving from that to a main role is both filling an ooc void and works rather well for her development. The Dreamwork was were she'd had several of her high points of helping people (Andromedia and Desiree in particular) so it's a good area for her to focus on as something she sees herself as good at besides murder. Self image and self loathing have always been weaknesses of hers so having that as a conterpoint to her 'I'm just a monster' is good. <br /> <br /> Personally, I am rather pleased with the way she's developing. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T08:59:45-08:00","id":1157763,"title":"","content":"So, at what threshold does an art or task become Sublime? As the philosophy kids like to put it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T23:54:56-08:00","id":1157890,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure. If 5 is an exceptional success, 25? (5x5) 50 (5x10) 25 seems more reachable, depending on if you think that makes it better or worse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T13:11:27-08:00","id":1160621,"title":"","content":"Molly takes the final plunge to unlock her lost memories. Yvette wakes beside a woman she has loved, and hated, for a very long time. Chalcedony returns to the Dream House.<br /> <br /> Note that the journals are particularly disparate in their coverage, focusing on very different things.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XCV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> I woke up late yesterday morning held tight in a dragon\u2019s embrace, like a princess in a really weird fantasy tale. Soon Hee\u2019s attitude wasn\u2019t possessive; it was more protective\u2026 kind of like Joan, actually. Who knew that a dragon and a knight in shining armor would have so much in common when it came to intimacy?<br /> <br /> In any case, we cuddled for a little while after she woke up, then got dressed and made our way downstairs to the kitchen. No one was working on breakfast yet, so I got started on some bacon and eggs while Jacob got the coffee going. Calamity was there, and D and Gloria staggered in from the basement guest room a few minutes later. D looked pleased with herself, and Gloria looked a little embarrassed. I admit I was intrigued, and asked what was up.<br /> <br /> \u201cGonna have to call Andromeda,\u201d D admitted with a smirk, \u201cI broke one of her toys.\u201d<br /> <br /> I felt my eyebrows moving toward my hairline. \u201cThe cross?\u201d I asked. Seeing an answering nod, I looked over at Gloria. \u201cYou two <u><u>did</u></u> have fun last night.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGuess I\u2019ve gotten a little stronger lately,\u201d D said, grinning.<br /> <br /> I ambled over to her and wrapped my arms around her bicep. \u201cDon\u2019t stop on my account,\u201d I murmured happily, pressing myself up against her hard body. Then I had to get back to the eggs before they burned.<br /> <br /> Julia descended a few minutes later, making apologies for Marguerite and Yvette, who were apparently involved in a serious discussion up in her room. Once I had ascertained that everything was all right \u2013 Julia\u2019s still a little twitchy about the situation, honestly, but it doesn\u2019t really seem like Marguerite is actually backsliding \u2013 I made a few plates for the three of them, and she excused herself to get back to it.<br /> <br /> Soon Hee left shortly after breakfast, stating that she needed to get to Desiree\u2019s before the other girl began the business of the day. I walked her to the doorstep, where we shared a lingering hug and kiss, and then watched her walk to her car. A visible transformation swept over her as she departed; I could see her bearing become more erect, more purposeful. It wasn\u2019t as though she was forgetting the night we\u2019d spent together; it was more like she knew that she needed to concentrate on the task ahead of her, so she allowed herself to slip into her usual no-nonsense persona to better accomplish that task.<br /> <br /> I spent most of the afternoon working on my new act as the others went about their own chores. I\u2019m not certain, but I imagine Calamity and Jacob were both preparing for Molly\u2019s impending dream healing session in their own ways. Marguerite and Julia, who had actually come down to the kitchen briefly as I returned from seeing Soon Hee out to her car, spent most of the day up in their room, continuing the ongoing conversation with Yvette, trying \u2013 I presume \u2013 to work out some sort of equitable relationship between the three of them. D mostly watched me work, occasionally shaking her head in wry amusement at my choice of song.<br /> <br /> The show rolled around right on schedule, and we played to a packed house, as usual for a Saturday night. It was a pretty good show all around, with Calamity and Marguerite reprising their new acts and me debuting my own. One of the comments I\u2019d seen a few times on our feedback cards was about how I rarely sing recent or current music, so I thought I\u2019d fix that. As anyone who\u2019s turned on a radio in the last six months or so can attest, Taylor Swift\u2019s \u201cShake It Off\u201d is ridiculously catchy, and I thought I\u2019d give it a whirl with a little suggestive dancing in a skimpy, spangly outfit. Damn near burned a hole through that stage, too. I\u2019ve still got it.<br /> <br /> I caught D applauding with the rest of the audience and blew her a kiss. With all the girls I date and fool around with, the sight of her still cuts right to the heart of me sometimes and reminds me of how deeply I love her. I ambled over to the door after leaving the stage and allowed myself to be drawn into a strong embrace.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou even make that drivel sound good, babe,\u201d she said cockily.<br /> <br /> \u201cHey, pop songs are popular for a reason,\u201d I shot back, \u201cthey\u2019re catchy. But I\u2019ll take it as a compliment, so thanks.\u201d I leaned in to kiss her softly. \u201cYou got any plans for tonight?\u201d I asked her.<br /> <br /> She shrugged. \u201cNothing specific,\u201d she admitted. \u201cYou?\u201d<br /> <br /> I shrugged in turn. \u201cNot really. Oleander\u2019s not here, so she must be toxic. And I\u2019ve been thinking\u2026 it\u2019s been a while since you and I had a night to ourselves.\u201d<br /> <br /> She leaned in so that no one else could see her face and gave me a soft, tender smile. \u201cSounds perfect, Jules,\u201d she whispered to me. \u201cI figure most of the motley will probably hang around after the show to make sure everything\u2019s okay with Calamity and Molly, but after that\u2026 it\u2019s a date.\u201d<br /> <br /> I mingled a bit after that. Veronica and Rowan were sharing a table, and I stopped by to speak with them both. I let my ex know that my feathers had filled out, and she asked to see them (I obliged of course). I told her that I can <u><u>really</u></u> fly now, and she immediately expressed an interest in joining me for a flight at some point (just like Joan). I brought it up mostly so that I could thank her again for that amazing sweater she made for me at Christmas, though\u2026 it\u2019s <u><u>perfect</u></u> for flying. Even in California, it gets cold up there!<br /> <br /> Oh, I also brought up Julia\u2019s concerns about Veronica\u2019s attachment to Marguerite, though I did so fairly subtly if I do say so myself. After speaking with her about it, I think Ms. Oldacre is probably overreacting. Sure, Veronica has been a little overwhelmed and maybe a little star-struck by both Marguerite and myself, but she\u2019s not exhibiting the sort of obsessive behavior I\u2019d feared based on Julia\u2019s assessment. So that\u2019s a load off my mind.<br /> <br /> I also spoke briefly with a few of our other guests. Angelica and Dominika were sharing a table, so I made sure to greet them both warmly. Angelica seems a little depressed; she thinks that something she\u2019s saying or doing is turning people against her. I can sort of see her point\u2026 both Monica and Desiree started out as very close friends, and \u2013 from her point of view \u2013 one has proven untrustworthy while the other has drifted away for no apparent reason. Without going into specific details, I did my best to assure her that Desiree is just going through a rough patch at the moment, and that she shouldn\u2019t take the redhead\u2019s strange behavior personally.<br /> <br /> Once the club had pretty much emptied out, the motley (plus a few associates like Gloria and Yvette) gathered on stage for an impromptu \u201cdance party\u201d as D put it. Calamity and Jacob took Molly and Chalcedony upstairs for the dream healing, and the rest of us just sort of sat around mingling, dancing, and trying hard not to think about how that little exercise could go horribly wrong.<br /> <br /> In the end we needn\u2019t have worried\u2026 probably. A couple of hours after last call, Jacob, Calamity, Chalcedony, and Molly descended to the theater area. Molly was obviously shaken, and I think Chalcedony was a little disturbed by the changes in her friend too (not to mention the fact that she\u2019s still uncomfortable in the Dream House), but I didn\u2019t sense any real hostility from either of them. Molly said that she wanted to be alone to think about all of her restored memories, and Chalcedony offered to escort her home.<br /> <br /> According to Calamity, the dream healing went as well as can be expected. I didn\u2019t really get all of the specifics, but to hear Calamity tell it, Molly had to navigate the dreamscape, opening doors and unlocking information while her previous personality stalked her. This previous personality waited to strike; it <u><u>wanted</u></u> Molly to remember who she used to be. Calamity warded it off for a while, and was able to weaken it significantly\u2026 but in the end Molly had to defeat it herself, which makes sense. She <u><u>did</u></u> defeat it, which according to Calamity means that her current personality should still be intact. Now we just have to wait and see how that personality incorporates the knowledge of who she used to be and what was done to her.<br /> <br /> We all offered Molly our best wishes, but it was clear that she needed time to process everything, so after a few words she took her leave. Marguerite, Julia, and Yvette retired to their room shortly after that, and after bidding farewell to Gloria, D and I followed their example.<br /> <br /> We made straight for the bed once we got upstairs, but not in the usual way. I wanted to hold her, and have her hold me, and revel in the closeness of her, and in the love. It would be a lie to say that I\u2019ve never doubted the strength of D\u2019s feelings for me. In my darkest moments, when she was with Gloria or Spidertoes, I have occasionally been afraid that I would lose her to another woman. We each have so many distractions, so many other demands on our time and our attention that it\u2019s easy to forget how important we are to each other. That\u2019s why times like last night are so vital to our relationship.<br /> <br /> We each love other people. Hell, we <u><u>both</u></u> love Marguerite and Julia, and I don\u2019t think either of us would trade what we have with them for anything. But I think that every once in a while it\u2019s important for us to spend an evening together, to remind ourselves of <u><u>why</u></u> we\u2019re getting married next month.<br /> <br /> Oh my God. We\u2019re getting <u><u>married</u></u>. Next <u><u>month</u></u>. Oh my God.<br /> <br /> Ahem. As I was saying, D and I spent the rest of the evening together. We did make love, softly, slowly, and tenderly, and spent the rest of the evening snuggled in each other\u2019s arms. I may have cried a little, and I\u2019m not ashamed to admit it. It would be remiss of me not to note that D did <u><u>not</u></u> cry; she just held me and smiled at me, because she could tell that I wasn\u2019t crying because I was sad or upset. I guess I was crying because what we felt for each other was too big to express any other way. Or something. You know.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t make D go to church with me this morning; she just looked so damned cute curled up on the bed that I couldn\u2019t bring myself to wake her. As usual, I sat through the sermon in the choir loft, sang one solo, spoke briefly with Dad about the wedding, and left the sanctuary feeling refreshed, renewed, and ready to face the day. No mail on Sundays means I didn\u2019t have that particular stress to worry about either, which was a relief. Still, I wish at least one of the colleges I applied to would send me <u><u>something</u></u>. It\u2019s getting pretty late in the game here!<br /> <br /> By the time I got back to the Dream House, Sex Breakfast was in full swing, with Julia once more manning the omelet station. Okay, in fairness to her, she was making breakfasts to order, but she was always happy to recommend her favorite dish in that odd perky French of hers. Yvette looked as mystified as I did, which was gratifying.<br /> <br /> So apparently the two of them \u2013 Julia and Yvette, that is \u2013 are\u2026 an item now? Dating? Friends with benefits? I don\u2019t know quite how to describe it, and I have to say I\u2019m more than a little surprised by this development, considering Julia\u2019s attitude of just a few days ago. Apparently Yvette and Marguerite are rekindling something between them, and Yvette has expressed an interest in being with Julia as well. I\u2019m not sure if Julia genuinely reciprocates the other girl\u2019s interest, or if she\u2019s just going along with it to make Marguerite happy, but she\u2019s agreed to give it a try. Oh, and both Marguerite and Yvette herself were quick to assure everyone that Yvette has no intention of causing trouble with any of our established \u201cfamily.\u201d So that\u2019s nice.<br /> <br /> So the five of us decided to spend the day together on the pier, hanging out and just generally enjoying ourselves. I\u2026 honestly, I sort of agonized over that, as there are about ten billion things I should have been doing today: studying my medical journals, training with Jacob and Calamity, working on wedding preparations\u2026 the list goes on and on. But, well, those girls are my family now, and I need to be a part of their activities, or else what\u2019s the point of all the other stuff? I mean, what am I working so hard<u> <u>for</u></u> if not to build a life with them?<br /> <br /> So I tried not to fret about everything on the horizon as I strolled or sat with the three girls I\u2019m closest to, talking and laughing about nothing much at all. I did my best to keep Yvette engaged, too\u2026 you know how I hate those awkward silences. I think \u2013 I <u><u>hope</u></u> \u2013 bringing her in to the group is a positive thing. I know that she reminds Marguerite of a time that might be best forgotten, but\u2026 but I trust Marguerite. I\u2019ll be trusting her with my life and my freedom and that of my friends in a few weeks, so I have to trust her judgment when it comes to Yvette as well.<br /> <br /> I should go. It\u2019s almost time to get ready for tonight\u2019s show.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> Sunday, May 10<sup>th</sup><br /> Nine years, one month, thirteen days<br /> Days without stabbing: 0<br /> <br /> The Oneiromancy was a success. She isn\u2019t the same, but she is still Molly, not Shayna. Because of me, that self is no longer lurking and hiding inside her waiting for a chance to resurface and Molly has her memories back for better and worse. But I should sort this into logical order and begin at the beginning shouldn\u2019t I?<br /> <br /> Sex breakfast was fairly typical though after a bit Marguerite, Julia, and Yvette\u2019s absence became notable. But before it reached the point of someone going up to check on them Julia appeared and explained that Yvette and Marguerite were in deep conversation about what this meant and collected some food for the three of them before returning. I guess it\u2019s a good thing they\u2019re not rushing into whatever they\u2019re doing but it still strikes me as a bad idea. But it\u2019s not my place to tell Marguerite who she can or can\u2019t fuck and I doubt either she or Julia really care about my opinion on the situation so I\u2019ll just keep my thoughts to myself and hope that it doesn\u2019t blow up too spectacularly.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t dwell on that impending train wreck too long, as I had the dreamwork with Molly last night to focus on. I spent the afternoon working with Juan Carlos on learning more about dream prisons and how to make them. In what I am sure will surprise no one I am planning to use my glassworks as the vessels much the same as I tend to do for my dream crafting. And having gone over it, there are many similarities to the physical component in each case. All in all, it was a well spent afternoon, definitely the sort of focus to keep me from fretting too much over the night\u2019s task. I know Molly was antsy and I did feel bad for making her wait till after the show but given the situation I didn\u2019t want to rush the contingency plans Lowjack had set up. That and I wanted to make sure I was brimming with Glamour from the show.<br /> <br /> The show went amazingly well as always. Desire may not truly be my emotion of choice but it still feels downright intoxicating to be so flooded with it. I can hardly imagine how good it must make Lori feel. It\u2019s almost assuredly the vast amounts of Glamour we deal in here that have fueled our rapid gains in power and having such a ready and ample supply is something most Lost would envy but I can\u2019t help but feel a nagging thirst for that darker spike of fear sometimes. It\u2019s just in my nature to crave something more savory than sweet I guess.<br /> <br /> I did slip away a little early to do a set of forms and center myself before the Oneiromancy, but I still made the rounds first. I took a few minutes to speak to White Maria, both to thank her for teaching me since the Tai Chi really has proven useful to me and to let her know that things were on the mend between myself and Becky. She did seem pleased by that since we are among the few she considers friends. And she was pleased when I said that I had no intention of ending my meditations with her. Even if I\u2019ve reached a point where it\u2019s not so much teaching as simply having a partner she does enjoy it, which I was glad to hear since I look forward to that time as well. <br /> <br /> I also visited with Hannah and Willow Black since they\u2019d come in together. Willow usually frequents the Rose and Thorn so it struck me as a little odd. Hannah made some casual mention to it being a business meeting but left it at that. Normally, I would be more suspicious of the Night Court\u2019s ambassador meeting with a weapons dealer but I know that Lowjack\u2019s got Hannah on a leash and given the situation between LA and Hollywood it makes sense for them to be arming up. Plus I am quite sure that if there is anything stabworthy going on I\u2019ll hear about it in due time.<br /> <br /> And on the topic of stabbing, Dahlia was also making one of her rare visits. She confirmed that she was there as the contingency if things went badly with Molly and had dressed for the occasion in a schoolgirl outfit just in case it came to having to put her down. Thinking about now, I know that should strike me as creepy if not just downright nonsensical but what can I say\u2026 It\u2019s a Snow Globe thing\u2026 At any rate, I hung about with her and we chatted about proper murder fashion and other girly things for a bit until the conversation got into sex or more specifically Dahlia's lack of it. I do have to admit, being a waterlogged corpse-girl isn\u2019t sexy and yeah, anyone who isn\u2019t turned off by that is probably creepy even by Snow Globe standards. But there are ways. Mortals can\u2019t see through the mask, especially if they were in a suitable environment to not notice like, say, a hot spring? I mean yeah, it\u2019s an obstacle but it\u2019s not insurmountable. Honestly, I think she just likes being able to use it as an excuse to complain about not getting any. Though she did let slip her fondness for Supernatural as fodder for buffin the muffin\u2026 I haven\u2019t had time to get into it but from what I\u2019ve seen the cast is handsome. I need to do a bit of research (because I KNOW the internet will have far more than I ever wanted in terms of sexy fiction about this) and see about whipping up a a nice little dream where Dahlia is only wet and leaky in not and sexy ways. I am sure she will thank me for it (might also decided to stab me for it, but then that could be fun too...)<br /> <br /> Anyway, once I\u2019d given Jacob the head\u2019s up that Dahlia would be present and had helpfully volunteered to see to any stabbing needs while I was busy (like.. you know\u2026 a certain la Blue Girl who would be present) I stepped out to focus and get ready.<br /> <br /> Once the time arrived, Jacob and I joined Molly and Chalcedony in the guest room. Everyone was a bit nervous and I reiterated with Molly that while I was going to be there and that I would do everything in my power to protect her and guide her through the flood of memories safely that there were risks and that there really was no turning back once we did this. She acknowledged and said she needed to know, that she understood it wasn\u2019t going to be pleasant or easy but even a painful past was better than just nothingness. It was pretty much the same conversation we\u2019d already had about it but I needed to be sure her conviction wasn\u2019t wavering and it seemed important to make sure Chalcedony (and Dahlia) heard her confirm her need to do this.<br /> <br /> We went under and even before I started to work she was steering herself toward the right sort of dream. It took the shape of a vast network of vaulted rooms, locked and secure and maze-like. I entered the dream and together we started to search through the boxes and files together. Right off, I caught a glimpse of a tiny orange kitten and as we continued, it kept appearing to watch us with eyes the exact same shade of gray as Molly\u2019s. Molly was intent on the searching and either didn\u2019t notice or didn\u2019t pay any mind to the other. I kept an eye out for the little feline as I started to pull and tug at the dream, to draw out the secrets we wanted and the things they\u2019d locked away and buried with the Table.<br /> <br /> I drew upon a lot of my glamour to push past all of the blocks and false trails and layers of conditioning to not remember. It wasn\u2019t just forgotten, it was buried\u2026 hidden away\u2026 but we pressed on, We opened doors that were hidden to look like walls and avoided the paths that just looped back upon themselves endlessly. It was slow but we moved forward and I could feel us getting closer, I could feel the ways that we weren\u2019t supposed to go. And as we finally broke past yet another locked door and into a room with a file cabinet that I knew, just knew had actual memories inside I spotted the kitten again, sitting atop it with its paw on a folder, watching us and waiting. It mewed and jumped into the darkness, vanishing but that folder was the representation of the first bit of Molly\u2019s lost memory.<br /> <br /> From there I proceeded a little more cautiously. The cat kept darting about the edges of our vision, ducking into the right path or mewling at us from the correct path as we threaded our way deeper. Molly was finding more and more of her lost memories, as she picked up the folders or opened the sealed boxes in the dreamscape, flickers of the actual memories she was experiencing danced about the edges.<br /> <br /> I picked up bits and pieces along with her, but I kept my main focus on the dream, both because I needed to watch the other and because I didn\u2019t want to intrude too deeply in what she was remembering. I got enough. A sister lost, caught in the crossfire between two Courts and killed. An angry and determined woman setting out to avenge her against monsters that no one else would believe existed. A Gentry\u2019s honey lies of how these things had invaded a world they had no place in. A promise to help, to make her strong enough to fight them\u2026 to send them back to their world were they belonged. Shayna drank it in, angry and hurt. She accepted the offer, believed the lie that it simply wished to make amends for its wayward brethren\u2026 to make right what they had made wrong.<br /> <br /> I turned my focus away as she remembered the turning and the hunting and her eventual fate at the hands of Darke and Grey and Twitch. The cat, Shayna, had grown stronger with each resurfaced memory. She\u2019d wanted Molly to remember. To remember the hate and the pain and the bitterness. To remember how she\u2019d been broken and tortured.<br /> <br /> As I suspected, as Molly was being swept up in the torrent of remembering Shayna appeared, creeping up and stalking her. Stronger now, no kitten or housecat but a tigress. The huntress driven by a burning rage too strong for even the Table to extinguish completely. Seeing her I understood the way this dream would end. One part or the other would triumph and the other would be subsumed as the woman became whole. And seeing that fierce creature before me I had no doubt which it would be. Even if Molly had been aware, which she wasn\u2019t. Her dream self was standing, holding a folder and reading it, reflecting how the flood of memories was sweeping her up. Shayna was stalking across the sandy floor of the arena that we had suddenly been standing in all along. Drumming like heartbeats echoed. I saw Shayna tense and crouch. I knew that it had to be Molly that defeated her or this would all slip away, that for me to end Shayna would only do what Grey had failed to accomplish with the Table.<br /> <br /> I drew upon the lessons I\u2019d picked up back when Gawain and I had been learning dream combat together. I focused on both myself and on warping the fabric of the dream at the same time. With a snarl, I lept forward just as Shayna was starting to unfurl. As she lept into the air I drove in and slashed as her side, carving a bloody furrow down one flank that sent her spiraling right into the spikes that rose from the sand. She tried to twist but still hit them hard, spinning as one pierced her and she pivoted on it before falling atop the jagged points. For a moment I was afraid I\u2019d overdone it and cost Molly her chance to regain the lost part of herself but no, Shayna wasn\u2019t defeated.<br /> <br /> She rolled, snapping the wooden spikes off and rising, bloody and swaying but still intent on her prey. Molly was still unaware as she roared and charged, slashing the woman deeply with her claws and sending her staggering to land face down in the sand. Shayna roared and shook off the broken spike still dangling from her side, then charged toward the prone figure. I sprinted closer, preparing to hurl myself between them to try to protect Molly but the woman rolled over and brought up her gun, sighting down on the charging tiger and firing calmly. The lone gunshot rang out and echoed as Shayna dropped. Molly pulled herself up and moved closer, kneeling down as Shayna began to dissipate and dissolve into an orange mist. Molly\u2019s eyes flickered brightly as she inhaled, breathing in the mist until it was gone.<br /> <br /> And I sat up awake. My pulse was racing and I had to blink to get my eyes to focus. Ignoring the abrupt calls of both Jacob and Chalcedony I looked over and saw Molly sitting upright and still. I took a breath and nodded as she blinked slowly and looked about.<br /> <br /> As soon as I was fairly sure she was awake I quickly informed everyone present (especially the one I couldn\u2019t see) that Molly had come out victorious. I then added a very brief explanation of what had happened (though I downplayed just how I am absolutely sure that Shayna would have devoured Molly without my help)<br /> <br /> Chalcedony tried to fuss over her but Molly was still in shock struggling to process the flood of memories. She said she needed to be alone and wanted to return to her apartment, to a place more familiar while sorting everything out. The others were a bit unsure but I assured them it sounded like a good plan and Molly departed promptly. Chalcedony followed after, wanting to follow and insure she made it home alright, which I did agree with since Molly was a bit out of it.<br /> <br /> From there it was letting everyone waiting downstairs as well as Lowjack know that it was done and had been a success. That part was a bit of a blur as I was feeling downright hollowed out from the rush of glamour I\u2019d thrown behind smashing through the barriers and then fighting Shayna. It wasn\u2019t too long before everyone had finished congratulating me and drifted off to bed down with their respective collection of lovers which suited me well enough, I was tired and ready for some regular sleep by that point. Even if I was curled up alone, I fell asleep happy and I slept hard.<br /> <br /> This morning went well enough. The mood was still high and I was feeling rather pleased with myself. I did it. I helped Molly. Yvette had remained again and after breakfast she and the quad all went off to see the pier. Before Jacob or I could decide what we were going to do with ourselves, Molly returned to talk. She was dressed in something downright slinky and for once seemed both aware of it and comfortable with that. We settled in and spent the afternoon talking about things she remembered about her life before and what she remembered of how she\u2019d taken up the path of revenge and been tricked by the Gentry. How after a while she\u2019d given into the hate and didn\u2019t really care if she was actually the same thing as the prey she was hunting if it meant she could destroy the monsters that she blamed for her sister\u2019s death. She\u2019s not the same, but she is still Molly. And now she remembers the good and the bad and the ugly parts of her past. It\u2019s true, it could have gone wrong. Shayna was as insane as Mary\u2019s fetch. But it was Molly\u2019s call and it was her right and hers alone to decide if it was a risk worth taking.<br /> <br /> And I think it was the right thing. She\u2019s whole again. None of us are made of only good things and happy memories. But it\u2019s our failures and our mistakes that we learn from. She\u2019s still taking it all in a bit, but I think she\u2019s happier knowing than forever wondering. And I made that happen. I\u2019m the one that laid her demons to rest and put her broken pieces back together.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Today started with another full house. Soon Hee Kwon was there with Lori, Gloria was with De La Rocha and Yvette stayed with Insincere Marguerite and Julia. I know that Chalcedony stayed with Molly last night but she was not here for \u201cbreakfast.\u201d Apparently she left earlier and said that she\u2019d be back to pick up Molly for the afternoon. Molly herself looked a little disheveled but otherwise okay. I say that Yvette stayed the night with two of the quartet, but they did not all come down for breakfast. Julia came down to get food for everyone. So I made up a tray of coffee for the three of them and Lori put plates of eggs and bacon on there. Julia brought the lot up to the two other girls. It seems that Insincere Marguerite and Yvette were having some serious conversation about their relationship and didn\u2019t want to interrupt it with something like food. Hopefully they have worked out all that they needed to. <br /> <br /> Molly has been increasingly worried, or at least anxious, about the Dream Healing tonight. Lori told Molly that she was strong and would do just fine tonight. That seemed to lighten the Mannikin\u2019s mood. Soon Hee also said something that I thought was interesting. She said that Molly was surprisingly sane for a Changeling. I guess this kind of makes sense. We all tend to relate more to the humans we\u2019re around or the Changelings that we associate with. Sometimes that can lead to individuals that are a little less connected to the world around them. Madame Spidertoes comes to mind. Not that we say anything bad about Madame Spidertoes, but she is a little less entwined with the mortals around her than other people are. I\u2019ve always kind of thought of it as how close to the fae we are. Or how close to what we were in Arcadia. I think I\u2019ve gotten a little further away from Rime than I was a few months ago, but I\u2019m not sure how sane Soon Hee would say that I am. I still have fae tendencies. Calamity has also gotten better lately. She is more stable and even tempered than she has been in the past. I\u2019m going to go out on a limb and say that the therapy that we\u2019re both going to is probably the reason for both of us. It can only be a good thing, right?<br /> <br /> So, I kept Molly company until Chalcedony came back to the Dream House to pick her up. Hopefully the blue girl can help Molly take her mind off the upcoming Dream Healing. I know that she\u2019s probably excited and more than a little nervous about the whole thing, but it doesn\u2019t pay to worry about what will happen. So it\u2019s a good thing that her friend was there to help distract her. For my own part, I distracted myself by spending the day with Luna in the woods looking for poachers. We did find a couple of guys that needed to be taught a lesson, but they didn\u2019t really fight back. I think they were probably a bit drunk and thought that they had a good idea. It didn\u2019t take much to convince them otherwise. <br /> <br /> I got back right before the show started. Just in time to see Insincere Marguerite finally come downstairs to socialize with the rest of us. She was in a really good mood, so I\u2019m assuming that her talk with Yvette went well. I\u2019m not sure what they worked out, but then again I haven\u2019t asked. I\u2019m not really sure that it\u2019s my business what arrangements they came to. As long as nothing adversely affects the motley, or either of them, then I guess I\u2019m fine with whatever they have worked out. <br /> <br /> The show itself went off great. Lori was amazing as always and Calamity and Insincere Marguerite were excellent. All three brought the house to their feet. It\u2019s actually become rather routine that they do that well. I mean, tonight was excellent but they have all gotten so good at their craft that it\u2019s hard to tell if they make any mistakes. I don\u2019t think that any of them have made any mistakes in a good long while, which I\u2019m sure our customers appreciate. Hell, even if those three made mistakes the crowd would forgive them. They love those three.<br /> <br /> So, while the ladies were wowing the crowd I was busy playing referee with Molly. Specifically making sure that she did not have too much to drink tonight. I know she was nervous and I can\u2019t fault her for wanting to sooth those nerves with alcohol, but drinking is not the answer to everything. Especially not Dream Healing. So, I made sure that Molly did not drink too much tonight. I let her have a couple of drinks to take the edge off of her anxiety but made sure that she stayed sober enough to deal with the Dream Healing later. She was going to have to deal with remembering a lifetime\u2019s worth of memories all in one go and I figured that she better have her wits about her to do just that. <br /> <br /> At one point Calamity came over to talk to me while Molly was nursing her second drink. She said that Dahlia was here to keep an eye on the Dream Healing to make sure that all went well tonight. I know Dahlia\u2019s skill set so I know that she was here to kill Molly should the worst happen. I suppose it is a courtesy that she told us why she was here in the first place. I probably could have been happy not knowing who the Winter Court had sent to keep an eye on things, but I suppose there was some comfort in knowing that it was someone that is really good at her job and would make sure things ended quickly if they had to end at all.<br /> <br /> Right after the show Calamity went to a quiet room to meditate for a few minutes before it was time for the Dream Healing. During that time I gathered up Molly and Chalcedony and walked with them up to the guest room. Soon after Calamity joined us. She reiterated to Molly that things might go badly if we go through with this, but Molly still wanted to do it. Molly also asked if Calamity would see the memories as they go by. Calamity said that she would, there was no way around that, but that she wouldn\u2019t tell anyone else what she saw. Molly seemed satisfied by that and she laid down to get comfortable. Funny thing is Molly was the only not one that seemed really nervous about this whole thing. Chalcedony took Molly\u2019s hand as soon as her friend laid down and after that she kept looking around the room. She was almost jittery. She didn\u2019t even look at her cell phone. She just kept holding Molly\u2019s hand. I think she was anxious about the Dream Healing and about being back at the Dream House. This is the first time in a long time since she\u2019s spent any time here. I guess I can\u2019t blame her considering what happened last time she was here. <br /> <br /> It didn\u2019t take long for Molly and Calamity to fall asleep so Chalcedony and I talked a bit to pass at least some of the time. Chalcedony said that she knew Molly really loved her but admitted that she wasn\u2019t sure if she was able to love anyone in return. I guess that answers why she\u2019s not been in any serious relationships. Casual ones she seems fine with, but not the more serious ones. Unfortunately for her a lot of woman seem to fall head over heels in love with her. She also said that Molly spoke highly of me. I reciprocated and told her that Molly said the same of her. I didn\u2019t see a reason not to tell her that. I may not trust her fully but there\u2019s no reason for me to not be polite.<br /> <br /> After what had to have been a few hours Molly\u2019s eyes shot open and she sat up in bed. Calamity sat up at the same time, also awake. At Chalcedony\u2019s questioning look Molly said that she was fine but needed time to think about what she had learned. She was pretty brusque with her not-girlfriend and left the room shortly after. She said that she was heading to her apartment. Chalcedony left shortly after her lover did, saying that she was going to make sure Molly got home safely. After those two had left Dahlia also popped up and said that she was going to follow Molly as well. I doubted that it was to make sure the Manikin got home all right. I looked to Calamity to see if she would tell me anything. All she said was that Molly won, and that she was herself. She also said that Molly remembered how she had been manipulated into the Hedge and into being a Loyalist. She apparently also remembered why she did what she did as a Loyalist. I can see how that would give someone a lot to think about.<br /> <br /> All of this made me think of my own situation. I was sort of manipulated into the Hedge, but there was no trickery involved in me becoming a Loyalist. I did that of my own free will. The Lady came to me and asked if I would serve her and I gladly said yes. I don\u2019t know what made Molly become what she was, but from the way Calamity phrased things it sounds like Molly became what she was due to circumstances forcing her to change. That didn\u2019t make her any less dangerous when she was Shayna, but it is an explanation. I don\u2019t have a good excuse. I didn\u2019t know exactly all what would be involved in working for the Lady but I knew that it would give me power and anything that gave me an edge over the other inhabitants was a good thing. The first time she told me to retrieve a Changeling from \u2018the world\u2019 I didn\u2019t think twice. I just went to that small town in Washington state and grabbed the young man that thought he could get away from the Lady. He didn\u2019t want to come back so I \u201cconvinced\u201d him that it would be in his best interests to follow me back. His name was Thomas. He was the first, but he certainly wasn\u2019t the last that I dragged back to Arcadia. I was not a good person in that place, which is why part of me doesn\u2019t want to go back. I promised Lori that I would help her retrieve her friends though, and if I can help save someone from Arcadia then I will do it. I have a lot to make up for and I don\u2019t feel like I\u2019ve done a lot to make that right. Maybe helping to free Lori\u2019s friends will help even things out a little bit? I can hope, right?<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> This day has just really started for me but it\u2019s already been interesting. We all ate breakfast and drank our coffee as usual. Nothing special there. After that though Lori, Insincere Marguerite, De La Rocha, Julia and Yvette all went to the pier. They seemed to want to spend the afternoon together, and the pier is a good place to do that. After they left I called Molly to make sure that she was okay. She left in a bit of a hurry yesterday and I was concerned about my friend. She said that she was fine and would be by later to talk. Turns out \u201clater\u201d was 45 minutes. Molly arrived wearing a low cut slinky dress. I will admit that it looked good on her, but I didn\u2019t want to dwell on why she was wearing something so revealing. Maybe Shayna wore more sexy clothes as a rule of thumb and Molly is going back to that habit. I guess there\u2019s going to be a lot of things that I\u2019m going to have to relearn about my friend.<br /> <br /> Molly said that she wanted to talk to me and Calamity about a bit of what she remembered. I think she wanted to make sure that we understood where she was coming from. She said that she had a sister years ago. Her sister was working for some Changelings, though she didn\u2019t know what they were, and got caught up in some violence and killed. Molly, or Shayna, got angry and wanted to make her sister\u2019s killers pay, so she chased them. She had been a Hunter in her mortal life, so in theory this shouldn\u2019t have been a difficult task. The Changelings responsible ended up leading her deep into the Hedge though and got her well and truly lost. Shayna got found by the Gentry and \u201cremade\u201d so that she could work freelance to return Changelings to Arcadia. She didn\u2019t know that there were good or bad Changelings, just that beings like them were responsible for her sister\u2019s death. She didn\u2019t just work for one Gentry, she worked for several, returning their wayward runaways. That explains why she had a deep-seated hatred for Changelings and why she was more than willing to use violence to solve any problems. Molly said that she understood why Shayna did what she did and wanted to make sure that it made sense to us too.<br /> <br /> I can\u2019t throw stones here. I accepted the Lady\u2019s offer because it would give me power over the other people that lived in her realm. It was those other people that had hurt me and others throughout the years and I had gotten sick of being the victim. So, I worked for the Lady and brought back any one of those bastards that tried to flee. I guess I thought that they deserved what they got. The Lady brought me up from my lowest point. I was ready to die. I didn\u2019t really have much in the way of prospects at that point. So, I can see why people like Rook or Shayna would agree to serve the Gentry. I understand why they did what they did. It took me a while to really grasp that what the Gentry did was wrong. Things made so much sense when I served the Lady. The people that lived in her realm where her subjects. She could do what she wanted with them because she was their Queen. People like me, her Knights, retrieved those that ran away, we protected her borders and acted as emissaries with other Kings or Queens. It made sense from a certain point of view. It took D\u0336e\u0336l\u0336i\u0336g\u0336h\u0336t\u0336 Diane to help me see that what the Lady and the others did was wrong. I finally saw the runaways as innocent victims. Victims like little Felicity who liked popsicles. I guess, or hope, that Molly has seen the error of her ways as well. She knows why she did what she did in service to the Gentry, but she has changed. She protects the Freehold now. I just hope that her recent memories have put some perspective on her old views of Changelings. We are a mixed lot, some good, some bad, and some in between. I guess time will tell on where Molly falls in that spectrum. My guess is that she will be in the grey area, with me. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> Matters have progressed with Yvette.<br /> <br /> I have tried to avoid any relationships beyond Juliette, Julia, and Maria. I see Juliette struggle to keep her girls happy, and while Maria is doing fine with Gloria, owing to Juliette\u2019s love of trying new people, those two have had time to bond. I\u2019ve been a bit wild but I am trying to keep to a few good, dear lovers. My family, Desiree, White Maria, Flores. People to me who Andromeda and Joan are to Juliette.<br /> <br /> So now Yvette enters the mix. Yvette has missed me, and yearned to get closer. We have history, and her fear is diminished. She has loved, and hated, me very much. I am not sure she will ever be completely one or the other, may no longer be capable, but she has swung very distinctly toward love.<br /> <br /> My feelings are strong. Her feelings are strong. It keeps us being lovers at arms reach difficult. Two nights ago she asked us to be more. She went to bed with Julia and I\u2026she has some feelings for Julia for much the same reasons I do; Julia is an artist, talented, mysterious, feminine and sophisticated. She does not love her like she does me, but an attraction is there.<br /> <br /> We spent the night making love, and most of the day talking, showing briefly for breakfast. What we tentatively got worked out is Yvette and I are going to give things another try, but she must respect my engagement to Julia and do nothing to interfere with Maria or Juliette. She was willing to accept those terms. She made her interest in Julia very clear, and they will be an item as well. We watched the show together, and Julia sketched us together.<br /> <br /> I preformed. It went well. Not Juliette well or Annika well, or even Calamity well, but well. Stray Cat Strut is a good show for me.<br /> <br /> The next day we went to the pier together so Yvette could get to know us all. It was fun. Juliette went out of her way to be very nice, and Maria was flirty. I think Yvette had a positive view of everyone. That\u2019s what I want.<br /> <br /> I am nervous. Yvette is\u2026strong. It took a long time to break her will, and her head is high again. She also is a strong woman in general, a Treasured. I think her feelings are somewhat mixed. Her passions overwhelm her, but what when they reach equilibrium? I am nervous.<br /> <br /> Other things go on. Molly has undergone a sort of dream surgery from Calamity and has remembered her past self. She was here today in a slinky dress, speaking to Calamity and Jacob. She appeared more confident. Both women involved. We had a dance party while Calamity worked. It was strange.<br /> <br /> But back to Yvette. Is this a mistake or will she fit right in my freaky family? Only time will tell.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XCV</i><br /> <br /> At the show, Calamity and Insincere Marguerite got same number of successes as before, at least for the bulk of the audience. Lorelei managed to hit 45.<br /> <br /> We handled the dream sequence well as we could. There was one round of Dream Combat, and Calamity used her Dream fighting style to great effectiveness. I think it is in Rites of Spring.<br /> <br /> Molly was complicated from a story perspective. With the build up and tension, I did not want just a happily ever after, but I did not want to run the PCs standing by and watching their friend be lost in favor of an evil Loyalist either. So I settled on a Dream battle; it was time to have Calamity look good again anyway, and I was confidant as a GM she would do well. As a Whisperwisp particularly. And she did.<br /> <br /> The end result was complicated, but favoring Molly over Shayna. Now we see what she does going forward.<br /> <br /> Starting next session. Comments and Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T13:33:37-08:00","id":1164874,"title":"","content":"A show, people start practicing new acts, Calamity has a plan.<br /> <br /> Journals are a bit more Spartan as holiday craziness and work stuff meant everyone had less time than usual. Plenty of good writing though.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XCVI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> I confess that I\u2019m not in the best of moods right now, so this entry might be a bit terse when compared to my typically ebullient prose. The motley is formulating a plan to deal with the Hedge monster thingummy, and the specifics of said plan have me\u2026 anxious? Angry? Maybe somewhere in between\u2026 is \u201cangrious\u201d a word? Have the contraction-obsessed denizens of this strange new millennium come up with that one yet?<br /> <br /> These negative vibes are actually a fairly recent development\u2026 most of yesterday saw me in a peachy keen mood. Calamity, Marguerite and I spent most of the afternoon rehearsing for the Sunday night show and kicking around ideas for some new numbers. Each of them had a few good ideas, but they were mostly songs that I didn\u2019t know so I\u2019ll have to hear \u2018em a few more times before they really stick. The one that stands out was Marguerite\u2019s idea to do a sultry rendition of \u201cTrust In Me,\u201d the song sung by Kaa the Python in the Disney animated version of <u>The Jungle Book. </u><br /> <br /> We had a pretty good crowd at the show that night, and the performances were excellent as usual (though confidentially I wasn\u2019t as \u201con\u201d as I had been on the previous evenings). I hob-nobbed briefly with the usual suspects, and passed a surprisingly amicable five minutes chatting with TJ. He\u2019s planning to attend the wedding next month (and honestly seemed both surprised and charmed to be invited), and promised that he wouldn\u2019t make trouble while he\u2019s there. \u201cI ain\u2019t crazy enough to start shit with that chick at her wedding,\u201d he chuckled, glancing over at D.<br /> <br /> Molly was there again, dressed in another hot, slinky little party dress. She was receiving more than her fair share of attention (some of it, I admit, from me\u2026 though I\u2019m not going to push anything until she\u2019s had a little time to get her bearings). Foremost among her admirers was one Soon Hee Kwon, who seemed intent upon enjoying Molly\u2019s company that evening. Alas, \u2018twas not to be, as Jacob ran interference for his friend until she regained enough focus to let the monster hunter down easily.<br /> <br /> Peg and Jimmy were there last night too. I stopped by to speak with them for a bit, but they seemed to be on a date, so I didn\u2019t want to take up too much of their time. They seemed to be doing well; they said they enjoyed the show and took the time to ask after my studies. It\u2019s comforting to have two such patient and interested mentors among the Pilgrims; neither of them seems concerned at all about my impending test.<br /> <br /> I spent most of the evening at the table frequented by White Maria, Dark Kimberly, and Becky. The first two exchanged a lot of barbed comments, but most of it seemed to be in good fun. It was affectionate\u2026 like when Missy and Jane used to call me \u201cslut\u201d as a term of endearment back in High School. I mean, sure, a lot of people used to call me that \u2013 the term was more than apt, after all \u2013 but coming from those two, it always made me smile.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s nice to see White Maria and Dark Kimberly getting along, even in that strange way. The two of them spent so much of the last year sniping at each other and making threats that <u>anything</u> would be an improvement, but this\u2026 it\u2019s almost like they\u2019re taking the first real steps toward rekindling the friendship they used to enjoy. I hope they take a few more, because I\u2019ve never met <u>anyone</u> whose life wouldn\u2019t be improved by a few more friends.<br /> <br /> Becky and I sat off to the side, each of us occasionally offering wry commentary in order to keep the banter going. After a while, though, Calamity arrived and took up most of Becky\u2019s attention. And speaking of rekindling relationships, I have rarely been happier to see two people get back together. At this point, it really doesn\u2019t look like Gawain\u2019s coming back, and Calamity needs a stabilizing influence in her life. She gets companionship and love from the motley (occasionally even physical love when she needs it), but her relationship with Becky can give her romance. And no matter what she might have to say on the subject, she <u>needs</u> a little romance in her life.<br /> <br /> So as the crowds began to dwindle the two of them made their way to Calamity\u2019s bedroom together. White Maria, Dark Kimberly and I kept the banter going for a little while, but eventually things began to die down. I waved D over, thinking vaguely that it would be nice to sleep in her arms again that night and settled comfortably in her lap once she had taken her seat.<br /> <br /> A few minutes later, Marguerite strode up and addressed White Maria imperiously. \u201cGo upstairs to my bedroom and take off all of your clothes,\u201d she said.<br /> <br /> White Maria rose, nodded, and walked away.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, I guess that\u2019s my cue to leave,\u201d Kimberly sighed with resignation, and she did.<br /> <br /> \u201cJulia and I will be entertaining White Maria this evening,\u201d Marguerite said after a moment. \u201cIf you like, you ladies would be welcome to join us.\u201d<br /> <br /> I glanced over at D, who shrugged nonchalantly\u2026 but I could see the fire in her eyes. \u201cMight be fun,\u201d I allowed.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah,\u201d D said, \u201cbut tomorrow night, after the movies\u2026 the four of us should be together. <u>Just</u> the four of us. Okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> Marguerite dropped her domme-face for a second and smiled tenderly. \u201cOf course. I would like nothing better. I am certain Julia will feel the same.\u201d<br /> <br /> So the three of us headed upstairs after that, to find that Julia and White Maria were waiting for us\u2026 the latter naked as promised. As one might expect, a night of wanton carnality followed, though I didn\u2019t get into it as much as the others did. I\u2019ve never been particularly comfortable with dominance games on either side\u2026 well, not since I returned from Arcadia in any case. I mean, I don\u2019t object to that sort of thing on principle \u2013 White Maria obviously consented to the treatment, and in fact seemed to get off on it as much as any of the others \u2013 but it just doesn\u2019t press my buttons. So I didn\u2019t engage in the mock-abuse, and contented myself with vanilla sex for the most part.<br /> <br /> So we woke up this morning tired, sore, and sticky and made the mutual decision to head down to Sex Breakfast. We threw on some clothes and D scooped me up to carry me down as per usual. Julia pouted. \u201cHow come Juliette always gets carried down the stairs?\u201d she said, mock-sulky. White Maria had left the bedroom some time earlier to do Tai Chi with Calamity in the backyard, so I was okay with Julia using my real name.<br /> <br /> I glanced at D, and her eyes sparkled. \u201cAll right,\u201d I sighed, \u201cput me down.\u201d<br /> <br /> Then <u>I</u> picked up Julia and carried her down the front staircase. It wasn\u2019t easy; she\u2019s a bit taller than me, and those long dresses of hers are not the lightest of garments, but luckily carrying around these wings for the past God-knows-how-long has really strengthened my upper body. And as Julia is well aware, I have a surprising amount of strength in my lower body as well, so lifting with my legs wasn\u2019t a problem.<br /> <br /> Julia started making breakfast\u2026 largely composed of bacon (though Jacob and Calamity opted for corned beef hash). I expressed the opinion that bacon was a super-food, as it\u2019s the sort of thing that you add to other foods to make them better. This innocent comment started a debate, as apparently \u201csuperfood\u201d is an actual term people use these days to describe foods that are supposed to be healthy in a variety of ways. Avocados, quinoa, acai berries, kale\u2026 mostly shit like that. While I admit that some of those can be tasty with the appropriate preparation\u2026 I\u2019ll still take bacon any day of the week.<br /> <br /> So Calamity would occasionally feed morsels of bacon to Becky, sometimes dipped in maple syrup. I\u2019d never tried that before and\u2026 damn, it\u2019s good. I had to force myself to stop after a while, as I really can\u2019t afford to indulge in that way very often. My body is my bread-and-butter as a burlesque dancer. But it did call to mind a discussion from last week, so I decided to investigate further.<br /> <br /> \u201cBecky,\u201d I asked, \u201cyou like bacon, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMm-hmm,\u201d she nodded with a smirk around her latest mouthful.<br /> <br /> \u201cHow about undercooked bacon?\u201d I asked, seizing the moment. \u201cDoes that do anything for you on a visceral level?\u201d<br /> <br /> Becky looked at me like I was crazy, and swallowed. \u201cNo,\u201d she said simply, and then \u201cgross.\u201d<br /> <br /> I shrugged. \u201cWe were discussing it before, and Julia is of the opinion that every potential fetish exists somewhere. The specific example was someone who gets turned on by undercooked bacon.\u201d<br /> <br /> Becky shuddered and shook her head. \u201cI\u2019ve had just about every fetish you can imagine at one point or another,\u201d she said after a moment, \u201cbut that one\u2019s never come up.\u201d<br /> <br /> After we finished up, Becky offered to give White Maria a ride home, which the other girl gratefully accepted. I walked the two of them out, mostly so that I could check the mail again without anyone looking over my shoulder. Still nothing from either of the colleges. Dammit.<br /> <br /> When I got back to the kitchen the conversation had turned to more serious topics, and that\u2019s when my good mood popped like a balloon.<br /> <br /> Calamity and Soon Hee Kwon have come up with a plan to capture the rogue Hedge Beast that\u2019s been terrorizing the Freehold lately. A plan that involves drawing it out in a place where we can be ready for it. A plan that involves using my fianc\u00e9e and another of my girlfriends as <u>bait</u>. Yeah, I\u2019m not happy about that.<br /> <br /> Okay, so here\u2019s the reasoning behind this oh-so-delightful plan. Oleander is known as a reclusive researcher, and she has a reputation of being \u201ccreepy\u201d in the Freehold. D, on the other hand, likes to mix it up, and is known to have a hair-trigger temper (she <u>did</u> assault the Summer Monarch last year, after all, so I guess that\u2019s understandable). Both of them, on the outside, might <u>look</u> like changelings who don\u2019t have a very good grip on their Clarity. But, once you get to know them, they\u2019re both actually remarkably stable people.<br /> <br /> So the two of them might appear to the Hedge beast to be ideal targets for its powers, even though in reality they\u2019d probably be almost entirely resistant.<br /> <br /> So why these two, you might ask? Surely there must be other changelings in the Freehold who also fit those requirements, you might say. And to my mind, you\u2019d be absolutely right! So why, then, are two of the women I love being asked to put themselves in harm\u2019s way for the good of the Freehold?<br /> <br /> Because of <u>me</u>. Because they\u2019re both in love with me, there\u2019s a natural point of contention between them which the Hedge Beast might hope to exploit. Now, there hasn\u2019t been any trouble between D and Oleander for <u>months</u> now; the two of them actually get along pretty well. But again, the beast doesn\u2019t know that, and that would seem to give it a convenient avenue of attack.<br /> <br /> D and Oleander have each been consulted about this, and both of them have given their consent to the plan. I know in my heart that I don\u2019t really have anything to worry about here\u2026 hell, both of them were selected for this operation by Soon Hee precisely <u>because</u> of the fact that the creature\u2019s powers won\u2019t affect them. And if it comes to a fight, well\u2026 I\u2019ve never met anything that could take D down, and Oleander deals with Hedge creatures all the time in her capacity as the Autumn Court botanist. And Soon Hee says that the creature is most likely to try to run rather than risk a fight in any case.<br /> <br /> But dammit, cornered animals are dangerous, no matter who you are. Two people that I love \u2013 one of whom will presently be my <u>wife</u> \u2013 are putting themselves on the line for this. And even if it\u2019s silly\u2026 I\u2019m worried.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t want to talk about this anymore. I don\u2019t want to <u>think</u> about this anymore. Maybe I\u2019ll go see if I can crack the leaderboards on a few more <u>Rock Band</u> songs.<br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei Grace</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> Monday, May 11th<br /> Nine years, one month, twelve days<br /> Days without stabbing: 1<br /> <br /> Man\u2026 I have said it before and I\u2019ll say it again, love makes you stupid. But right now I am feeling so fucking gloriously stupid that I just don\u2019t care. Why? Because Becky came to the show last night and did not leave until after sex breakfast.<br /> <br /> Actually it was better than just Becky being here for the show without her current charge in tow. She came in with White Maria and Dark Kimberly and they all sat together like they used to. It\u2019s nice to see that trio coming back together after what\u2019s happened. I mean, it was understandable but as I consider all three of them friends it was hard to see them at odds like that. As tempting as it was to make a beeline for their table after my acts, I was sure that once I\u2019d joined them I wouldn\u2019t be leaving again (and I was right about that).<br /> <br /> First off, Soon Hee was there and waved me over. She was concerned about the skullfucker. Yes, I\u2019m sure it has some actual name but no one has told me and it\u2019s probably something dull anyway so I have taken it upon myself to give it a cool name before I kill it. Anyway, she was concerned that the skullfucker was laying low and wouldn\u2019t attack Desiree again for a while to avoid drawing attention. So she was thinking we needed to lure it out and wanted my input for Changelings that might seem like likely targets (especially if they weren\u2019t as vulnerable as they might appear) that might be willing to act as bait for a trap. My best suggestion was Oleander, since she already knew about it and fit the crazy rep but not actually crazy part. And once I\u2019d mentioned her, it occurred to me that there was also the whole love triangle with D and Lori thing that could offer it a tempting vector to cause havoc. Soon Hee seemed rather pleased with the idea. Of course, we had to make sure Oleander was agreeable and I wasn\u2019t going to ask her without talking to Lori about it first. So Soon Hee agreed to come by Monday afternoon and headed for the bar, zeroing in on Molly like a heat seeking missile. I considered following since I knew she was still getting her head on straight but she was at the bar and I knew Jacob would watch over her.<br /> <br /> I hit the other notables briefly. Well, I skipped TJ since I still haven\u2019t forgiven Porkchop for intimidating Rowan in my club. While speaking to Moon I brought up Oneiromachy since ze is one of the more experienced Oneiromancers about. Ze wasn\u2019t exactly enthusiastic but did agree it was good to be in shape and offered to spar with me to help me get my nightmare fighting skills up to task. We didn\u2019t work out the details, so I\u2019ll need drop by the Lighthouse to discuss times and such when I get a chance.<br /> <br /> Once I\u2019d made the rounds I pulled my glass in, which still just feels\u2026 weird, before making my way over to the table. Becky turned, pretending she hadn\u2019t been watching me out of the corner of her eye and rose as I got near. Then she stepped in and wrapped herself around me like she\u2019s never been able to with the shards out. And I hugged her back like she was the last life preserver on the Titanic. As strange as it feels to hold me glass inside, it felt pretty fucking good to be able to throw my arms around her without having to worry while we kissed. Honestly, I am surprised no one made any \u2018get a room\u2019 comment or anything but I guess they were all too glad to see us together again (or maybe just enjoying the show). At any rate, we did eventually find it necessary to breathe and I slipped into Becky\u2019s lap as soon as she sat down and leaned in with my arms around her. Her hair stroked me and for a bit we just enjoyed being close and affectionate while the conversation rattled on. I learned that Princess Jolie had taken it upon herself to see to Laughing Carp for the evening and send Becky for a night off. I am guessing the timing of this right after Beautiful and I had our talk is not a coincidence. I really must remember to thank her next time I see her.<br /> <br /> Then Marguerite came by and without so much as a hello just ordered White Maria to go upstairs and strip. Without a pause, she continued on her way clearly expecting to be obeyed. And White Maria did (well, she immediately rose and headed off at least.) About that point Becky asked about my plans for the evening which I answered with another deep hungry kiss. She then smiled and joked about a tour. I chuckled and then realized that while the playroom was installed before we completely stopped talking it was past the point where things were good between us and she hadn\u2019t seen it. I rose and reached to take her hand and lead her off.<br /> <br /> She seemed a little surprised that we went down rather than up but said nothing. I was relieved to see the door was unlocked. Shortly after getting the cross installed in there Marguerite and I did have a talk about that as the two most likely to be entertaining in there to insure that no one walked in on anyone unless it was intended as part of the fun. I opened the door and turned to take both of her hands and draw her in with me as I backed in so I could watch her face. Beautiful\u2019s eyes widened a bit as she took in the toys and the cross and she whistled softly as she commented that we had indeed made some improvements since she\u2019d last taken the tour.<br /> <br /> She moved to the cross as I closed and locked the door, complimenting the construction and correctly guessing it was Andromeda's handiwork. I turned and stepped over, pausing just before reaching her. I drew breath to ask her if she was sure she was alright with what was about to happen before I imposed my desires upon her any further.<br /> <br /> I guess she saw the look in my eye because she cut me off before I got a word out. \u201cWe\u2019ve already had this conversation Calamity.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know,\u201d I answered with a shrug, \u201cBut I care about you and I don\u2019t want to hurt you.\u201d<br /> <br /> She smirked as she pulled me in close and leaned in to brush her lips against my own as she spoke in a low breathy whisper. \u201cI think we both know that\u2019s exactly what you want right now.\u201d She laughed softly as the signs of both my embarrassment and arousal made themselves quite apparent and then drew back enough to look me in the eyes seriously. \u201cYou may not be the only one that can make me want this, but you are the only one I trust enough to let do it.\u201d Suffice to say there wasn\u2019t a whole lot more talking after that (though at one point Becky did question the wisdom of teaching me that Spring rejuvenation magic).<br /> <br /> Eventually, I carried a very sated and well used succubus up to my room for some tender cuddling until it was time to slip away for Tai Chi with White Maria. And since we were both at the Dream House, we opted to use the outdoor stage. It\u2019s not as nice as her dojo by any stretch but it was much more convenient. I did touch on things with Marguerite, but again I was being overly concerned. I mean, I knew that nothing would have happened that Maria didn\u2019t want but just like with Becky I felt better having a confirmation. Anyway, we didn\u2019t dwell on that long and had a good session together.<br /> <br /> Once everyone started to gather in the kitchen I did consider pulling my glass back in again so I could curl up in Becky\u2019s lap again but it takes a toll so I opted to pull her into my (careful) embrace instead and she was quite content with the arrangement. Breakfast was nice, banter as usual but with the added bonus of getting to feed Beautiful syrup soaked bacon\u2026<br /> <br /> Like all good things, it did end. Becky give White Maria a ride home and then the conversation turned to the topic of the plan Soon Hee and I had worked out the night before. Lori was, as I expected, not pleased with the idea. But she did agree with the logic and she wasn\u2019t going to speak for Oleander and D, both of whom did agree to at least discuss the plan.<br /> <br /> So once Soon Hee and Oleander were both there we got into the plan for killing the skullfucker and ironing out the details of it. As a minor wrinkle, Oleander was still very toxic so she showed up for the planning session in an NBC suit and we had to plan on delaying until she was safe to be out in pubic again but I think we have everything in place and will soon rid the Freehold of a serious menace.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I\u2019m rather a happy Calamity right now. Since Becky was here last night I\u2019m not going to be so greedy as to ask her to movie night when she\u2019s on a long term bodyguarding mission and all, but I am going to see if Stasia is interested. Oh\u2026 I should have told Becky about Thursday night and asked her about joining in the Fury Road premiere hi-jinks. I should go ahead and do that before I forget. Also, need to sit down and do some research for that dream I\u2019m making for Dahlia. Oh yeah, and sort out my new act for this week. Guess I really should wrap this up and get to work shouldn\u2019t I?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> The rest of the afternoon passed by rather quickly. The ladies practiced their acts for the show or tried to figure out what their next act would be. And then before I knew it, it was show time. Molly came back still dressed in that slinky dress from earlier. Dark Kimberly, White Maria and Becky all came and sat together at a table. That hasn\u2019t happened for a long time now. I guess they finally got past all the bad feelings and memories. It\u2019s good to know that some healing has been going on in the freehold. I also noticed Jimmy and Peg in the audience. I guess Lori made an impression on them if they\u2019re still coming back for her shows while they\u2019re in town. I wonder what their final test for her is going to be?<br /> <br /> As usual all three ladies from the motley did really well on their acts. I swear that our audience is getting spoiled. Anywhere else they go to see a live act is not going to be as good as a show they\u2019ll see here. I may not get to see all the acts, but when Lori, Insincere Marguerite or Calamity is on stage not many people are ordering drinks, they\u2019re just staring up at the stage. It gives me a bit of a break and an opportunity to watch the show myself. I have some talented friends.<br /> <br /> Molly came by the bar as per usual tonight. I asked how she was doing with all the new memories and she said that she was doing okay. She said that she knew what she was thinking when she made past decisions. She knew why she did what she did, but she doesn\u2019t understand why she did those things. She said it\u2019s like looking at her past with new eyes. She knows the thought processes that led her to make those decisions, but her thought processes have changed. Before, as a Beast, she was ruled more by her passions. Now she is more analytically minded. There is a degree of separation between her past memories and who she is now it seems. She knows why she did what she did, but also knows that she would not make the same decisions now. I wish I could say that the same was true for me. I don\u2019t have that separation. I wouldn\u2019t do things the same way now as I did back then, but I don\u2019t have a new perspective really. I know why I did what I did. I know why I joined the Lady. Looking back at my situation when she appeared to me, I wish I could say that I would have refused her offer if knew what it was going to lead to. I\u2019m honestly not sure that I would have. I was in a really bad place. She came by just before I was about to give up. I know that\u2019s not coincidence. It was planned that way so I wouldn\u2019t refuse her offer. I suppose if I had to do things over again, armed with the knowledge that I have now, I might be able to refuse her offer. I just remember the hunger and the cold. The all-pervasive cold. When she kissed my cheek and the cold went away, I felt a relief that I hadn\u2019t known for a long, long time. I was Hers in that instant. I don\u2019t know if I\u2019d be strong enough to resist that feeling of relief even knowing what I do now. Would I be able to forgo the chance at being a brother to Rook? I just don\u2019t know.<br /> <br /> Thankfully my thoughts did not go to such depressing places while I was working. I talked to Molly some more about random things, but nothing too important. I also watched Lori and Calamity work the crowd. There was a lot going on at the table with Becky, White Maria and Dark Kimberly. Lori went over to talk and the banter seemed to go back and forth. No one seemed to get offended even though I could tell things were getting animated. That\u2019s good. A little later Calamity went to that table, talked to Becky for a bit and they both went off together. Insincere Marguerite came over, said something to White Maria and the other woman headed off to go upstairs. Not sure what Marguerite said, but I figured it had something to do with their plans for the evening.<br /> <br /> While some of that banter was going on Soon Hee came over to the bar and started flirting heavily with Molly. Molly herself seemed interested but more than a little overwhelmed, so I decided to intervene. I asked if I could speak to Molly alone for a moment and asked the Manikin if she was okay with Soon Hee flirting with her. Molly seemed conflicted. She was still dealing with regaining her memories and figuring out who she is now, but she did seem interested in Soon Hee\u2019s advances. She took a minute or two to get her bearings and went back to talk to Soon Hee. Molly did not go off with the monster hunter, but they seemed to part on amicable terms. I\u2019m assuming that they\u2019ll hook up with each other at a later time. And that\u2019s fine by me. I just wanted to make sure that Molly didn\u2019t regret any decisions she made while still reeling from her past\u2019s revelations.<br /> <br /> I guess in some ways the \u201csecond chance\u201d that Master Darke gave to Shayna worked. It took some extreme measures if you ask me, but it worked. Shayna is gone, replaced by Molly, who is my friend and a good person. I don\u2019t know if Darke had such measures in store for Rook before he escaped or not. Part of me is glad that Rook escaped when he did. He may have come back with less than honorable intentions, but he was himself. He died as he lived, fighting and serving the Lady. I don\u2019t know what I would have done if Darke had changed Rook into someone new. I don\u2019t know if I would have tried to be friends with that new person or not. It would probably have been too painful. Seeing him every day, but him not remembering who he was or who I used to be to him. I still haven\u2019t forgiven Twitch for what he did to Rook under Darke\u2019s orders. I don\u2019t support the use of torture, and that\u2019s exactly what they did to my friend. Rook may not have been the greatest person, he might have been considered a bad person, but I know why he was the way he was. I understood where he came from. Even if he was a bad person, he didn\u2019t deserve what they did to him. No one does.<br /> <br /> In some ways Darke\u2019s \u201csecond chances\u201d were a little too close to the Lady\u2019s idea of a \u201csecond chance.\u201d She was going to break me down and remake me into a loyal Knight. She started breaking me, and I have to admit that it worked. I was about ready to give in. Again. If she had managed to remake me that time then I don\u2019t think there would have been anything that could have brought me back to being Jacob. Delight helped me once, but I don\u2019t think it would have worked a second time. I guess I just hope that Darke didn\u2019t do similar things to Shayna before remaking her with the Table into Molly. I can\u2019t agree with those methods. They are too close to what the Lady was doing. I am glad to be friends with Molly though, and she wouldn\u2019t be here if Darke hadn\u2019t done what he did. If he hadn\u2019t used the Table then Shayna would have been killed and I would never have met Molly. I\u2019m torn. I don\u2019t like Darke\u2019s methods, but I can\u2019t ignore the fact that they ended up giving me a good friend. And I\u2019m happy that Molly has regained her lost memories. Things will not be the same between us from here on out, but hopefully we\u2019ll make it work. I will miss the na\u00efve Molly who loved new book suggestions, but I am looking forward to getting to know the new Molly all over again.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Today started like a usual Monday. Calamity and White Maria went out to the backyard, entirely too early, and worked on meditation and Tai Chi. I applaud their dedication, but have to admit that I enjoy sleeping a little bit longer after a show night. Who\u2019d have guessed that I\u2019d become so accustomed to my creature comforts? I lived for so long without such things. Granted I did enjoy the odd hot coffee here and there when the Lady sent me on missions to \u2018the world,\u2019 but I have gone far past hot coffee now. I\u2019ve actually gotten used to sleeping on a soft bed, with soft pillows and enjoying leisure time in bed with Luna. Not to say that the Lady did not provide her Knights with suitable accommodations, they were just more spartan than what I have now and I have more free time than I ever did while in the Lady\u2019s employ. Rook would say that I\u2019ve gotten lazy, and maybe I have. I don\u2019t know what else I would do though. I train regularly with Calamity, and soon to be Lori, but I don\u2019t have missions to go on here like I did with the Lady. I do inventory regularly and stock up on stuff that we\u2019re running low on, but it\u2019s not the same. I don\u2019t know what\u2019s got my thoughts going down this line anyway. I like my leisure time. I like my life. Though I guess I do miss the excitement sometimes. That was one thing I could certainly say about working for the Lady. My days were never boring.<br /> <br /> And back to current times. Calamity was in a really good mood today. I think it had something to do with the fact that Becky stayed the night. Those two haven\u2019t had a night together for a long time. I know Calamity was hurt when Gawain left, and her relationship with Becky seemed to end at the same time. I\u2019m not sure why neither woman approached the other to end the silence before now but I\u2019m glad it finally ended. Those two are good together.<br /> <br /> Julia was once again making breakfast. This time though she was taking orders. I decided to be different and asked if she could make corned beef hash. I knew that we had some in the pantry, but just haven\u2019t made it for myself in a long time. After reading the label to see how to prepare it Julia had it cooking within minutes. Calamity said that it sounded good and asked for some herself. I thought it came out pretty good. It\u2019s definitely an American thing, but I enjoy it.<br /> <br /> After breakfast Becky offered to give White Maria a ride home, which she accepted. So, our two guests left. After they were gone Calamity called the motley together to have a chat. She wanted to tell us what she had talked to Soon Hee about last night, which was about hunting the Hedge beast. They had come up with the idea of drawing the creature out with a pre-planned argument/disagreement between two ladies. Those ladies in particular would be Oleander and De la Rocha. Both women could appear on the outside to be less stable than other members of the freehold. Oleander is a loner most of the time since she is frequently toxic, and De la Rocha\u2019s temper is well known. The creature, not knowing the freehold well, may not realize that both women are actually rather more stable than they appear. The point of contention could be that they both are in a relationship with Lori. The idea is to make it look like they are at odds with one another over Lori\u2019s affections. That is definitely something that the beast might take advantage of. Lori was hesitant at first about this plan and I don\u2019t blame her. It involves two of her lovers in a way that could end with one or both of them getting hurt. Okay, it\u2019s not too likely that De la Rocha would get hurt, but it is possible that Oleander might. On the plus side Oleander is one of the people in the freehold that can subtly do damage to the Hedge beast. The Darklings in our motley are the other main subtle damage dealers against this thing as well. I could do damage to it since it\u2019s a plant, but my methods are not exactly understated. If this thing attacks in the club I can\u2019t very well whip out my ice powers and not make a huge scene in front of the crowd of onlookers.<br /> <br /> I will admit that I\u2019m feeling a little useless in this whole endeavor with the Hedge beast. Unless this thing attacks in the parking lot or somewhere else that is private I can\u2019t do anything to help stop it. I don\u2019t think that will be the case though. This thing seems to thrive on the chaos it causes so it is likely to strike when there is a crowd of people around. Lots of witnesses to see what confusion it creates. I just don\u2019t know what I can do to help. I feel like my skills should come in handy to the motley in some way. I just don\u2019t have the most pedestrian skillset. I\u2019m good at infiltration and violence, and maybe mixing a good Cosmopolitan. Those skills don\u2019t lend themselves to many situations. So, as far as most of the freehold knows, I\u2019m the drink guy. I\u2019d like to be known for more than that, but there haven\u2019t been many opportunities. Not, I guess, that I should be hoping for more violent situations to come up. Sometimes I do though. I guess I just want the opportunity to make up for the things I did as Rime. I have a lot to make up for. Not that the freehold knows that, but I do. My motley knows. My monarch knows. Even Darke knows. He figured out some things while he was torturing Rook, but got the rest of the story when we were hunting my former partner after he escaped. I just want to do some good to wipe out some of the bad things I\u2019ve done. I just don\u2019t know how much good I\u2019m doing mixing drinks and doing inventory.<br /> <br /> I know that I\u2019ve done some good by being a friend to Molly and others. I have given them support when they needed it, and I know that I have appreciated that same support on occasion from my motley mates. They didn\u2019t have to accept me for who I am. They didn\u2019t even think twice before accepting me, before helping me. I know I don\u2019t deserve their support and acceptance but I find that I\u2019m selfish and don\u2019t want to give it up. I just want to give back something more substantial than making margaritas for customers. I just don\u2019t know how to do that.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XCVI</i><br /> <br /> Sometimes I kinda wish this game had the \u201cblow by blow\u201d style journal we had in Night Train; I was on fire Rping White Maria and Dark Kimberly insulting each other back and forth as they spoke to Lorelei and Calamity.<br /> <br /> A word on Merits; A reminder Becky Wan has a merit that causes her to reflect the fetishes of the focus of her attention, so he has similar to Calamity when with Calamity. This does give her EVEN MORE social dice, but it also has some odd roleplaying wrinkles. Similarly, Oleander\u2019s immunity to plant-based toxins are part of her kith,but her ability to make herself highly toxic with them is a merit, similar to how Calamity\u2019s glass and Insincere Marguerite\u2019s tongue and ability to slip under doors are merits.<br /> <br /> The new Jungle Book movie has not come out, so Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Trust in Me song is based on the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WHMwgtlqJM4\" target=\"_blank\">Siouxsie and the Banshees</a> version<br /> <br /> Soon Hee is using contracts of Moon and Lucidity to weigh people\u2019s Clarity. Those are in Rites of Spring and I think Dancers in the Dusk.<br /> <br /> Okay I think that covers the session comments and questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T20:13:28-08:00","id":1165507,"title":"","content":"Lovely to see more from the Dream House, and for new developments to come up. Molly really seems to have lucked out with how her memory situation has turned out, even if she's still muddling through it all, though it helps she has the motley as a support network. Jacob does a lot more for the group than he seems to appreciate, but from experience I know how it can feel like you're not contributing to a situation positively when there's an entire group pulling their weight.<br /> <br /> On a side note Baroness, for the merits you made for Insincere Marguerite and Calamity, were those ones you simply offered the players for them to buy, or ones that were asked for by them...or something that was kind of simply made on a whim?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T16:11:59-08:00","id":1165695,"title":"","content":"Jacob is quiet but a participant.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite's merits were picked out of Kithbook: Sluagh, both her older and newer, and the group as a whole okayed the first one. Calamity's was an effect that was formalized as a merit after the game started...we had played loose with game effects at first but decided to make it a merit. Gawain's man of steel merit was conceived at that point. When we hit Wyrd 7 I asked if anyone wanted any major changes and Puddle was picked, as was Lori's flight.<br /> <br /> But I never gave out a list or anything. Does that help?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T16:28:21-08:00","id":1165697,"title":"","content":"Very much so, thank you. This is partially from the buzz that the Changeling: The Lost kickstarter is giving off, and I'm getting ideas for (potentially) hosting my own game when it comes out. It also made me ponder on a character I have in the wings who has fountain pen nibs for fingernails and ballpoint pen horns, and whether producing ink from those points should be a merit or not. Your games in general are a great inspiration for what can be done in Chronicles of Darkness without going into depressing areas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T17:51:33-08:00","id":1165714,"title":"","content":"Thanks! Yes Changeling gives us a lot of interesting options for kiths and Seemings and such, and tweaking it to make just the right monster seems cool. I enjoy Urban Fantasy more than horror, and while I certainly do have some horror in games, a lot of it is Urban Fantasy, and I see very little issue, with that. It makes for fun games. If you wind up putting up logs or anything like that let me know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T13:32:04-08:00","id":1168427,"title":"","content":"No plan survives contact with the enemy. Some plans start to go awry even before then. Meanwhile love blooms and madness echoes.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XCVII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> So remember how I was so irritated a couple of days ago about how my nearest and dearest had developed a plot to capture the rogue Hedge Beast utilizing two of my lovers as bait? Oh, for those halcyon days of ignorance and bliss! It turns out that our quarry is far cannier than we ever realized, and several of our compatriots have paid the price for our complacency (boy, that word-a-day calendar is a marvel!). In fact, one of our friends very nearly paid the ultimate price.<br /> <br /> So not much happened on Monday after my last entry, though a conversation did start about how we might make Missy and Jane more comfortable in the Dream House after we rescue them. If they\u2019re anything like me, they\u2019re going to have a serious case of culture shock for a while, and Julia thought it might help if we made things look a bit more familiar for them. Of course, she couched it in fairly insulting terms, stating that maybe we could make their room look more like the 70s without being \u201ctoo much of an eyesore.\u201d Honestly! As if the only valid aesthetic is the new millennium\u2019s Spartan sense of understatement!<br /> <br /> So our itinerary for movie night was once again selected by Julia, who unsurprisingly decided to go with a couple of gothic fantasy tales\u2026 albeit with a more humorous bent this time around. <u><u>Beetlejuice</u></u> was the more light-hearted of the two, though it definitely had a dark edge to it. The story was about a family who moves into a haunted house\u2026 but the haunting was told largely from the point of view of the ghosts, the house\u2019s previous residents. As they\u2019re new at the haunting game and not very good at it, they hire a professional poltergeist (the titular \u201cBetelgeuse,\u201d amusingly mispronounced for the rest of the film) to oust the newcomers for them. Once the genie is out of the bottle, however, they find that his brand of mayhem is more than they bargained for, and ally themselves with the mortals in order to oust the troublesome spirit once and for all.<br /> <br /> It was a pretty good film overall\u2026 the moral was maybe a little ham-handed, repeatedly beating the viewer about the head and shoulders with the need to let go and move on, but the action was exciting and humorous enough to keep the audience engaged. I\u2019m told that the main actor also played Batman in a couple of films, though most members of the motley were quick to warn me against seeking them out. Julia was the exception; she seemed to remember the films\u2019 aesthetics fondly.<br /> <br /> The second film was called [u]<u>Lost Boys</u>[/ u], and was a more straightforward tale of good versus evil in a California town overrun with vampires. One wonders why a group of vampires would choose to take up residence in a state known for its long sunshiny days, but I suppose that\u2019s beside the point (and as we know for a fact that there are at least a few vampires living in L.A., I guess it\u2019s not so far-fetched after all). In any case, the film was pretty silly overall, but genuinely entertaining for all that, and one of the main characters was a boy who had the interesting perspective of going through the transition from human to something supernatural, which I think all of us could relate to in some way. Except maybe Stasia, Natasha, and Elena, who had joined us for the evening.<br /> <br /> Oh yeah\u2026 <u><u>that</u></u> provided some additional drama which I really didn\u2019t need as well. First of all, Elena started having an asthma attack sometime during one of the films, and couldn\u2019t find her inhaler. Stasia produced a spare from her own bag, which raised a few eyebrows. For a pair of casual friends, those two seem an awful lot like they\u2019re dating\u2026 but their will-they-won\u2019t-they back and forth isn\u2019t what irked me about our guests for the evening.<br /> <br /> At one point, Natasha (or \u201cTash,\u201d as the other two have taken to calling her) asked me if I could think of any way to get Dad off her back about something. I asked her what she meant, and she told me that he keeps asking her if she\u2019s running or selling drugs for her Russian contacts, and it\u2019s getting annoying. Well, I know how Dad can be when he gets a bee in his bonnet about something, but that wasn\u2019t the aspect of her situation on which I chose to focus.<br /> <br /> \u201c<u><u>Are</u></u> you selling drugs?\u201d I asked simply after a moment.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat? No!\u201d she said indignantly\u2026 a little <u><u>too</u></u> indignantly for my taste.<br /> <br /> \u201cDad\u2019s pretty sharp,\u201d I pushed a little, \u201che\u2019s usually right about things like this.\u201d<br /> <br /> She rolled her eyes. \u201cHe <u><u>is</u></u> sharp,\u201d she admitted, \u201cbut I promise that I\u2019m not selling illegal drugs out of his house. I told you that I wouldn\u2019t bring trouble down on him, Lori, and I meant it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay,\u201d I said, but couldn\u2019t just let it go. \u201cSo what <u><u>are</u></u> you doing that\u2019s got him so worked up?\u201d<br /> <br /> She sighed and looked away from me. \u201cI might \u2013 <u><u>maybe</u></u> \u2013 have a line on certain prescription drugs\u2026 things that some people want or need, but are pretty hard to come by in their circumstances. Nothing too bad\u2026 just stuff like Ritalin, Viagra, Demerol\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re selling prescription drugs illegally,\u201d I said, trying to keep the disapproval in my voice at manageable levels.<br /> <br /> \u201cTechnically I\u2019m selling candy,\u201d Natasha said with a wink, \u201cthe pills are a free gift I give out to my best customers. Selling them would be illegal.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNatasha,\u201d I said softly, thinking over everything I\u2019ve learned in the last year, \u201cthose drugs are regulated for a reason. Doctors have to be familiar with a patient\u2019s medical status before they feel comfortable prescribing them. Just as an example, Viagra can be really dangerous for those with certain types of hypertension\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> She shrugged. \u201cNo one\u2019s forcing them to buy it,\u201d she said. I heard in her voice the echo of the arguments we used last year as rationalizations when we learned that Jacob was selling heroin for Darke. Maybe I\u2019m a giant hypocrite, but this is my <u><u>Dad</u></u> we\u2019re talking about, so sue me.<br /> <br /> \u201cPlease,\u201d I said softly, looking into her eyes, \u201cthink about talking with my Dad about this, okay? He won\u2019t judge you, and he\u2019s really good at helping people in your situation. He\u2019ll get you back on track. In a way I envy you\u2026 I wish he\u2019d been more like this back in the 70s\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Something softened in her eyes as she looked at me. \u201cOkay,\u201d she replied simply, \u201cI\u2019ll think about it.\u201d<br /> <br /> D expressed her opinions on the subject a few minutes later as we were heading off to bed with Julia and Marguerite. \u201cShe\u2019s trying to hook up with you,\u201d she said with a chuckle.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat?\u201d I asked. \u201cYou think she\u2019s trying to impress me by putting Dad in this position?\u201d<br /> <br /> D shrugged. \u201cYou obviously like bad girls,\u201d she said with a twinkle.<br /> <br /> Maybe she\u2019s right, but if so, it wasn\u2019t a very good attempt at seduction. <br /> <br /> The rest of the evening drove Natasha out of my mind, though. As promised, the four of us spent the night together in one big loving embrace, and it was wonderful. I honestly don\u2019t know what I would do without the three of them, and I don\u2019t know how I ever could have thought my life was worthwhile before they were in it. Back when I first came to Malibu, it was all about sex and desire, and I thought that real emotional love didn\u2019t enter into the equation at all. I was obviously an idiot back then.<br /> <br /> Tuesday was when things took a nosedive into the crap-heap. Oh, it didn\u2019t start out that way. D got out of bed, stretching and grumbling this morning in order to go to therapy with Jacob and Calamity. I extracted myself from the tangle as well in order to do a little studying. I heard Marguerite stirring, but Julia latched on to her and firmly demanded that she stay in bed instead of retreating to the vents so that she wouldn\u2019t be alone.<br /> <br /> When D and the others got back from therapy, I joined them outside for our sparring practice, dressed in my usual workout gear of bike pants and a sports bra. I think I\u2019m starting to pick up the basics of self-defense. We\u2019re starting off with unarmed combat practice\u2026 essentially boxing but without the formal structures surrounding the sport. While I won\u2019t claim that I\u2019ll be golden gloves worthy any time soon, I\u2019m at least a little confident that I am better prepared to defend myself in a fight situation than I was a few weeks ago.<br /> <br /> Sex Breakfast proceeded apace with more bacon, and morning became afternoon. Then D got a text, and everything turned to shit.<br /> <br /> The text was from Gloria. Apparently Desiree and Chalcedony had gotten into a fight at the Rose &amp; Thorn, and according to my love \u201cGloria totally lost her shit.\u201d She left me with a kiss and a promise to call and let us know what was going on, and hurried out the door to see what she could do.<br /> <br /> I called up Glamour Springs after she left, heading outside to check the mail as I did so (still nothing, dammit). Dominika answered and told me that Desiree had attacked Chalcedony with no provocation, and when Chalcedony retaliated, Gloria knocked her out with a chair to protect her roommate. Court representatives were already on-site, seeing to everyone\u2019s injuries\u2026 and Desiree had been taken into custody. Though I didn\u2019t get the details at that point, the general consensus was that her Clarity had dropped to dangerous levels, and that we had almost lost her to the madness as a result.<br /> <br /> Thinking that the hedge beast had stolen a march on us, I asked if anyone had informed Soon Hee Kwon about this, and Dominika informed me with a worried edge in her voice that no one had been able to contact her. The last anyone had seen of her was last night at the Rose &amp; Thorn, where she had been flirting pretty heavily with Oleander. I quickly concluded that conversation \u2013 securing a promise that they\u2019d call me if they found her \u2013 and tried to call Soon Hee, but got no answer.<br /> <br /> I informed the others of this new information, and Calamity immediately headed out to the Winter Court\u2019s clinic to see if she could do anything with Dream Therapy to help Desiree. I called Oleander to see if she knew where Soon Hee might be, but to no avail. She confirmed that the two of them had been flirting the previous evening, and that she\u2019d been intrigued by the possibilities of a liaison with the pretty dragon, but she\u2019d still been toxic, and so reluctantly had to decline the other\u2019s invitation.<br /> <br /> And that\u2019s not all\u2026 oh no! See, things got even more fucked up after that. The Spring Court called in Laughing Carp to use contracts to locate Soon Hee, and when they found her in a local hotel room, she was in pretty rough shape. In fact, she nearly died that night. It was pretty obvious that she had been poisoned. The Court called in Oleander to do what she could for Soon Hee, and as promised, Dominika called me to let me know the situation. I quickly informed the others and headed out the door to the hotel in question.<br /> <br /> Oleander and Becky were there when I arrived. Soon Hee was in no shape to answer questions; she was still unconscious. Oleander quickly confirmed that she had been poisoned, and did what she could to help the other girl. She was stabilized in short order, but it would still be several hours before she woke up.<br /> <br /> Becky turned to face me, her expression dark. \u201cLori, I\u2019m sorry, but I need to speak with Oleander alone for a few minutes. Could you give us the room, please?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSure,\u201d I said uncertainly. I went to give Oleander an affectionate hug, but she was still toxic, so we had to table that notion for a bit.<br /> <br /> Of course I listened at the door. I love Oleander, Becky looked like she meant business, and haven\u2019t you learned by now that I\u2019m an insatiable busybody in any case?<br /> <br /> The conversation quickly grew heated. Becky stopped just short of accusing Oleander of sleeping with Soon Hee to poison her. Oleander maintained her position that she hadn\u2019t gone anywhere with the dragon. They raised their voices. Before things could go any further than that, I went back into the room.<br /> <br /> \u201cSorry, I didn\u2019t mean to eavesdrop,\u201d I lied, \u201cbut you guys were being pretty loud. Oleander, honey, forgetting what you <u><u>know</u></u> about last night, and just examining the symptoms\u2026 does it look like Soon Hee is suffering from the effects of the poison you\u2019re currently emitting?\u201d<br /> <br /> Oleander sighed but nodded dutifully. \u201cYes. She\u2019s exhibiting signs of sexual activity, and her body is reacting as though she\u2019s been exposed to a large amount of my toxins. It\u2019s as if she\u2026\u201d she lowered her gaze and blushed cutely here. \u201cIt\u2019s like she went down on me last night. A lot. But I swear I didn\u2019t\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know,\u201d I said softly. \u201cYou never have to swear to me, Oleander, I know you wouldn\u2019t lie about something like this. But is it possible that some power was used against you\u2026 something that might force you into the act and then blur your memories of it?\u201d<br /> <br /> Her eyes widened. \u201cI\u2026 I had some pretty intense dreams last night,\u201d she admitted. \u201cSoon Hee had gotten me pretty hot and bothered, so I didn\u2019t really think much about it until just now, but\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I gave Becky a meaningful glance.<br /> <br /> She wasn\u2019t convinced at first. \u201cOleander\u2019s too together for the creature to affect her,\u201d she pointed out.<br /> <br /> I was prepared for that argument. \u201cBut Desiree isn\u2019t,\u201d I said, \u201cand she\u2019s familiar with Spring Court contracts involving desire\u2026 and she\u2019s powerful enough to invoke bedlam if necessary, too.\u201d<br /> <br /> Becky\u2019s eyes widened. \u201cGood point,\u201d she said. \u201cIf you\u2019re right about this\u2026 shit, this thing is devious.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt also means that the creature would know that it can\u2019t affect Oleander directly, or else why would it use Desiree as its cat\u2019s-paw? Fuck, there goes our plan.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMaybe not,\u201d Oleander piped up. \u201cIt might still try to use its powers on de la Rocha. Hell, this might even give us something else plausible to fight over\u2026 she\u2019s worried that you\u2019re not safe with me anymore.\u201d<br /> <br /> I called up Flores to see if she could confirm this version of events. She was under the impression that Oleander and Soon Hee had left together, but confessed that she didn\u2019t actually witness it (she was with Desiree at the time, which explains why the redhead was at the Rose &amp; Thorn this morning). Still, it\u2019s the best working hypothesis we have at the moment, so we\u2019re running with it. If we\u2019re right, it\u2019s a good thing that Soon Hee is so tough\u2026 otherwise she never would have survived Oleander\u2019s poison. I shudder to think about what that might have done to my girlfriend.<br /> <br /> Oleander said that Soon Hee should wake up some time that afternoon, and she would be okay to go to the Dream House that night. This would give us the chance to catch her up on everything\u2026 and might deter the hedge beast from trying anything at the Dream House before we\u2019re ready. Soon Hee should be nowhere near when we spring our trap, lest we make the beast skittish.<br /> <br /> I took my leave after that and headed back home to catch up the others. Calamity arrived back shortly after I did, and reported that Desiree was making progress, but wasn\u2019t out of the woods yet. The Winter Court are keeping her restrained, sedated, and isolated to keep the creature from using her again. According to their experts (read: Doctor Bright), another hit like that and we would have lost her permanently.<br /> <br /> So it was with less than my usual cheerfulness that I prepared for last night\u2019s show. My spotlight solo last night was a peppy, cheery number, and I just wasn\u2019t feeling it. Still, the show must go on and all that stuff, right? So I set about rehearsals, wardrobe and makeup as usual, and made sure that everyone else was in place to take up the slack if anything <u><u>else</u></u> should come up.<br /> <br /> The number in question actually went remarkably well, and I was able to push my personal feelings aside for the good of the performance. I had Belinda, Tara, and Heather come out first in matching outfits and start the opening harmonies of \u201cLollipop\u201d by the Chordettes. Then I came on stage, decked out in that red and white striped cheerleader outfit and broke into \u201cI Want Candy\u201d by the Strangeloves. It got what is becoming my usual standing ovation\u2026 lately it\u2019s gotten pretty difficult to find new ways to up my game.<br /> <br /> I was not much in the mood for socializing last night, but I did check in at a few tables. First and foremost, I stopped to chat with Soon Hee and make sure that she was all right. She wasn\u2019t at her best, but she seemed to be mostly recovered. She confirmed that she had spent the previous night with Oleander, and started feeling sick pretty much immediately after the festivities. I made sure that she understood what had happened and wasn\u2019t holding a grudge, and updated her on our plans to capture or kill the hedge beast.<br /> <br /> I checked with D, and as I\u2019d assumed she was planning to spend the night with Gloria, who was still pretty shaken up over the incident with Desiree and Chalcedony. I gave both Gloria and D a hug and let them know that I was fine with that. They ducked out together later, pretty much as soon as the show was over.<br /> <br /> I said a quick hello to Rowan and Veronica before heading up to Neon and Brightstar\u2019s table. When Neon got up to freshen their drinks, I pointed Rowan out to Brightstar, and she quickly agreed to help me get her on Neon\u2019s radar. I introduced the four of them to each other, and I think things went pretty well.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d sort of decided to spend the evening with Brightstar, as D was otherwise occupied and Oleander was still mildly toxic. But watching those four chat with each other, I allowed my plans for the evening to evolve, and started including Veronica in my flirts as well. She and Brightstar seemed to get along pretty well, and while I doubt they would have ended up together without me facilitating the situation, neither seemed averse to the idea. This left Neon and Rowan with only each other to talk to\u2026<br /> <br /> Okay, I admit it\u2026 I was also just plain horny. Big surprise, right?<br /> <br /> \u201cSorry to put you out,\u201d Brightstar said to Rowan with an adorably-dimpled grin, \u201cbut it looks like my plans for the evening are going to keep me here. Would it be possible for you to give my friend a ride home?\u201d That devious little minx!<br /> <br /> Rowan agreed in short order\u2026 and I fancy there was something of a spark there. More on Neon\u2019s side, of course, but that might just be Rowan\u2019s natural shyness at work. For what it\u2019s worth, I hope the two of them do hit it off\u2026 Rowan is exactly the sort of innocent soul that Neon needs to counter her natural cynicism, and Neon\u2019s single-minded devotion could potentially give Rowan the undivided attention she deserves from a romantic relationship. Though I admit to feeling a few pangs when I see one of my exes with someone new\u2026 it\u2019s past time. And I\u2019m happy for them both\u2026 or at least I look forward to being happy for them both.<br /> <br /> So the three of us hugged and kissed our friends goodbye and retired to my boudoir as the last of the guests trickled out. We frolicked for a bit, and then the two of them passed out. I half-heartedly started reading a few medical journals, but I\u2019m too worked up about what happened with Desiree and the hedge beast to really focus on anything. I\u2019ve been writing in this journal and watching my two lovers sleep peacefully across the room as I wait for the sun to come up.<br /> <br /> This should all be over in the next twenty-four hours. God, please let this all be over in the next twenty-four hours. I want to be able to sleep like that for at least a night or two. I want all of my stress to come from worrying about my college applications, and my upcoming test with the Pilgrims, and my wedding next month. I don\u2019t want to have to worry about which of my friends is slowly being driving insane and forced to hurt those around them. I don\u2019t want to have to worry that one of those friends might be a doppelganger just because they\u2019re acting a little off. I don\u2019t want to have to worry that everything we\u2019ve built here in the Freehold might come crashing down around us due to one clever saboteur.<br /> <br /> I guess this entry has turned into a sort of prayer, so I\u2019ll close it in the appropriate fashion. Amen.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> Tuesday, May 12<sup>th</sup><br /> Nine years, one month, eleven days<br /> Days without stabbing: 2<br /> <br /> For once, I am seriously looking forward to seeing Dr Emmett Thursday. I can whine to her about my petty problems and she\u2019ll listen and at least pretend to care. Not that the others wouldn\u2019t, but with all the shit going down they\u2019ve got way more important things on their minds. Hell, you know it\u2019s bad when the thought of killing the damned skullfucker isn\u2019t even enough to get my motor running.<br /> <br /> I should be focused on that\u2026 but instead my mind\u2019s spinning over things I shouldn\u2019t be upset about. I am sorely tempted to hit the rum but I know it will only make me even more fucking melancholy. Fuck but I wish I could have done more than just talk to Becky. As much as it was nice to hear her voice it can\u2019t hold me close. It really doesn\u2019t fucking help that I left Desiree in Gawain\u2019s arms in the dreamscape. I mean, it was what she needed, a strong protective presence\u2026 a safe place. Just\u2026 fuck\u2026 Damn you Gawain\u2026 I was so used to being alone in the dark and you had to go and fucking ruin me.<br /> <br /> I shouldn\u2019t be upset. He left her too and after the damned skullfucker nearly broke her she needed a rock. And it\u2019s not just that\u2026<br /> <br /> Stasia and Elena are a couple. I don\u2019t think they realize it yet but it was pretty clear at movie night. I should be happy for them. I should be glad Stasia found her princess. It\u2019s just\u2026 I clung to that fantasy in Snow Globe and it\u2019s not easy to admit it\u2019s never going to happen. But it\u2019s not. I\u2019m not the girl she fell in love with. That girl would have reacted with horror at the idea of reckless drag racing along the mountain highways until Stasia drug her along squealing. She\u2019d have loved it but never would have admitted to it. She was never brave enough to do things like that without Stasia taking the lead. But now I\u2019m right there with her. Partners in crime\u2026 thick as thieves\u2026 And I am happy with that. I really am. I just have to let that old dream go. And that\u2019s apparently harder than I\u2019d like.<br /> <br /> But I will deal with it. Maybe I\u2019ll never be Dr Katheryn Moss but I am Sister Calamity, Gilded Aspirant. My blade slays monsters and nightmares alike and my dreams lift and heal weary minds. I\u2019m not Anastasia\u2019s princess but I am her blood sister and nothing will come between us. And yes, Gawain is gone but he brought me back and held me together when I couldn\u2019t do it myself. But maybe I needed him to let me go to realize that I can stand by myself.<br /> <br /> Damn, I guess I have picked up a bit after all that time with Dr Emmett. Still, it will be good to talk this over with her. I need to be focused. The skullfucker has to be put down before it does any more harm. It damned near turned Oleander into a murderer and killed Soon Hee. Plus seeing Desiree reduced to a shattered husk of the strong and self confident woman I helped her become was heartrending. I can\u2019t let this damned thing do that to anyone else and while I know the one that trained it is marked for death the Monarchs of Hollywood will pay for sending this monster.<br /> <br /> But there\u2019s nothing I can do tonight. I need sleep before Tai Chi with White Maria. Becky should be asleep by now, I think I\u2019ll close my eyes and join her.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Things were more lighthearted this evening. At least for me they were. The others seemed to be having a good time. Eventually though conversation turned to Missy and Jane. Not sure how it came up, but people were talking about how to make them feel more comfortable once we get them back to \u2018the world.\u2019 It was suggested that they stay at the Dream House for a little while to get their bearings. I suggested the guest room over the garage. Julia made some comments about the 70\u2019s having bad taste but planning on decorating some of the house in that style to make them feel more at home. Lori took offense at the \u2018bad taste\u2019 comment and argued that it wasn\u2019t bad, just different. Earth tones and all that. I don\u2019t really pay close attention to how houses are decorated in different decades so I kept quiet on that subject. Then later Stasia came over for Movie Night per Calamity\u2019s invitation and asked if Natasha and Elena could come too. The group agreed so we had three more guests to watch movies with. I did not get to comment on the movies with my sister since she was sitting close to Stasia, but it was still good to be able to spend time with her and my Luna. Luna for the most part was pretty quiet during the movies. We whispered a bit here and there, but mostly we just cuddled in each other\u2019s arms in silence. It\u2019s nice to be able to do that. <br /> <br /> We eventually decided on our movies for Movie Night. Julia suggested a couple of movies that I\u2019d never seen. One was called Beetlejuice and the other Lost Boys. I had at least heard of Lost Boys, but not the other one. I thought they were pretty good. Beetlejuice had a lighthearted approach to death. In the movie, how you died determined what kind of job you had in the afterlife. Suicides were civil servants. Two of the main characters were a couple that had been killed in a car accident and ended up haunting their old house. The character Beetlejuice was chaos incarnate. He was fun though. For the most part. Lost Boys was not as lighthearted. It had some funny scenes in it, but it had some horror bits to it too. It was about vampires in a small California town and a young man that gets lured into being one of them. That might have hit a little close to home for me. There was more than one occasion when I convinced someone to serve the Lady willingly. She didn\u2019t personally recruit all of her people. So that was left to me, Rook and some of the other Knights. Her servants didn\u2019t always last that long so it was up to us to replenish the numbers. We each had our own methods of recruiting people. I tended to trick them into it. Rook worked from the shadows and made them think it was their own idea. Some Knights physically persuaded people to join the Lady. I always found that they lasted longer if they joined willingly. But back to the movie. Overall, I thought it was pretty good. A bit close to home, but pretty good.<br /> <br /> There was one interesting thing that happened during the movies. Elena started coughing and couldn\u2019t seem to stop. I could hear her breath wheezing a bit from where I sat and I started to get worried. I don\u2019t have an inhaler here. Then Stasia pulled one out of her pocket and gave it to Elena. Generally, those things are prescription and you don\u2019t just give them to people you don\u2019t trust or know very well. It would also make sense to only give something like that to someone that you plan on spending a lot of time with. So, the pieces started clicking into place. Was Stasia dating my sister? After the movie was over and our three guests left that was the first question that people started asking me. I honestly said that I didn\u2019t know. I now have suspicions but nothing solid. I wonder if I can bring it up casually the next time I talk to my sister? I\u2019m not entirely certain how I feel about those two dating. I was against them getting together in the beginning because Stasia has repeatedly said that she doesn\u2019t do relationships and I didn\u2019t want Elena to get hurt. Now, it seems that they might be dating. Stasia really does seem to be sweet on my sister though. She was attentive during the movie and of course had a backup inhaler for her. That shows me that Stasia is thinking of more than just herself. If she hurts my sister though she will regret it. She may be friends with Calamity and all that, but no one hurts my family.<br /> <br /> Before that happened though Natasha asked Lori if there was a way to get her dad to get off her back about something. Apparently Lori\u2019s dad suspects that Natasha is dealing drugs and is offering to help her get away from that. Natasha kept insisting that she wasn\u2019t dealing illegal drugs, but the rest of us weren\u2019t so sure. She was acting a bit defensive. Not to mention that Lori\u2019s dad is a canny guy, he picked up on possible trouble, so there is something going on with her. She eventually admitted that she is dealing in prescription drugs. She says that she sells candy at the college and \u201cgives\u201d away prescription drugs as a special present for her customers. Basically she\u2019s selling stuff like Ritalin and Viagra to name a couple. Lori looked concerned and was pretty adamant that doctors prescribe those kinds of things to people only after looking at their medical history and making sure that the drug will not be harmful. Viagra can cause problems with people who have heart conditions. I was backing Lori up on this as a bad idea, but I suppose that\u2019s like the pot calling the kettle black. I do deal in illegal drugs so I don\u2019t really have a leg to stand on as the saying goes, when it comes to this topic. Granted I do not sell nearly as much heroin as I used to. I told Darke that I wanted to slow down my distribution so I don\u2019t get the Dream House in any trouble. He wasn\u2019t super pleased with that but didn\u2019t say no, so I took that as a tacit okay. Maybe someday I can get away from the drugs altogether.<br /> <br /> After that things got a little more lighthearted. There was discussion about Stasia and Calamity and drag racing. Elena tried to get me to convince Calamity not to encourage her friend into doing something so dangerous. She was really worried that they might get hurt. I wasn\u2019t sure what to say. Calamity isn\u2019t going to listen to me about doing dangerous stuff. Hell, we\u2019ve both done dangerous stuff when it comes to going hunting in the Hedge. I understand that Elena is worried about Stasia getting hurt because Calamity wanted to go racing. Stasia is the one that introduced Calamity to the drag racing in the first place anyway. I tried to warn them about the dangers of sharp turns but Calamity just said that she could open a doorway to the Hedge using the car door and they\u2019d be safe. I hope it doesn\u2019t come to that.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> So\u2026Tuesday certainly started out pretty interesting. Well, the therapy was the same as usual. I expressed my dissatisfaction with my lack of doing anything productive for the Freehold. I admitted that I felt that I wasn\u2019t making up for my past in any real way and I wanted to do that. I need to do that. Sullivan seemed to be of the opinion that just being a good friend to my motley mates and those around me will be enough to \u201cmake up\u201d for my past. I could hear the quotes he put around that phrase. I don\u2019t think he understands the things I\u2019ve done. Granted I don\u2019t think I\u2019ve given him too many specifics on my past deeds, but I have stressed that I was not a good person. Just being a good friend is not going to wipe the red from my ledger. I need to do things, good things, to help people. To make a difference. Sometimes I don\u2019t know if I\u2019ll ever be able to make amends for my past actions. There\u2019s just too much.<br /> <br /> Anyway\u2026back to Tuesday. Lori joined Calamity and I for training after we got back from therapy. Lori was dressed in a tank top and bicycle shorts and ready to go when we got out back. We worked on the basics of hand to hand combat today and she did well. She has a very stable center of balance, probably because of her wings. There\u2019s not going to be many people that will be able to grab her from behind or even pull her off her feet once she gets some practice in. She really seemed to enjoy herself, so I felt good about being able to help in some small way. It was mainly Calamity doing the teaching, but I piped up with a few tidbits here and there and made a good practice partner for her to try a move out on, or to be the one that tries to \u201cattack\u201d her.<br /> <br /> After breakfast is when things got interesting, so to speak. De la Rocha got a text from Gloria asking her to come over to the Rose and Thorn and said that Desiree was having a meltdown. Desiree had been restrained and Gloria was freaking out, so De la Rocha went over to see if there was anything she could do to help. So, it turns out that Gloria came by the club this morning to pick up Desiree who\u2019d spent the night there with Flores. They met up downstairs where Chalcedony just happened to be. For some reason Desiree flipped out and attacked Chalcedony. Chalcedony fought back and Gloria started beating on Chalcedony with a chair until the blue girl stayed down. She wasn\u2019t badly hurt or unconscious, she just decided that staying down might end the fight. The Winter court folks were called in from the Clinic to restrain and help Desiree. <br /> <br /> Now all of this was very suspect. Desiree doesn\u2019t just flip out and attack people unless something is going on. We figured the Hedge beast has affected her or left some idea in her head and she acted on that idea when she saw Chalcedony. Seeing as this was likely the work of the Hedge beast we thought to call Soon Hee. The problem was no one knew where Soon Hee was, and she wasn\u2019t answering her phone. This didn\u2019t look good at all. The Spring court got Laughing Carp to use one of her Contracts and she located Soon Hee. Turns out that she was in a hotel room, and she wasn\u2019t doing well. Lori and I went to the hotel to see what we could do to help. Oleander and Becky were there already. It looked like Soon Hee had been poisoned so they called in our resident expert to see if she could figure out what poison had been used. Things got more than a little messed up after that. Soon Hee was exhibiting symptoms similar to the poison that Oleander had been toxic with last night. Now, the botanist said that she had flirted with Soon Hee and they were more than a little interested in one another, but that she had gone home alone and fantasized about being with the Directional courtier.<br /> <br /> Ideas, and not quite accusations, were flying around all over the place and the only one that explained everything was this. It looks like the Hedge beast had influenced Desiree last night into using Spring Court Contracts on Oleander, peaking her desire and blurring her memories of the evening. Oleander then slept with Soon Hee, inadvertently poisoning the Monster Hunter. On the plus side, Oleander had the antidote for the poison and administered it to the affected woman as soon as she could. She said that Soon Hee would be out for a while longer but should be up and about by show time tonight. I think the idea had been to have Soon Hee show up at the Dream House just to ensure that the creature didn\u2019t try anything there tonight. The creature seems to know who she is and took measures to specifically target her last night. We have been underestimating this thing. It\u2019s clever. More clever than we anticipated, which led to a series of unfortunate events last night and this morning.<br /> <br /> While we were at the hotel dealing with Soon Hee and all that, Calamity went to the Clinic to see if there was anything that she could do to help her friend, possibly with Dream Healing. She was let in after undergoing a test to make sure that she was really herself and not the creature in disguise. Doctor Bright had a chemical that was designed to be injected. It was an herbicide, but it doesn\u2019t do anything to humans. So, he injected Calamity with that and confirmed that she was who she said she was. She then talked to Desiree for a bit, who was sedated but awake, comforting her friend and promising to bring some comforts from home to the clinic for her. Calamity also did a bit of Dream Healing which helped stabilize Desiree where she\u2019s at, but didn\u2019t repair any of the damage that the Hedge beast has done. Her grip on reality has been severely shaken and she\u2019s holding on by a thread. Apparently, we came really close to losing her to madness altogether. <br /> <br /> All of this is more than a little messed up. I don\u2019t like being played and yet we were. That Hedge creature played us like fiddles and almost took a friend of ours away from us. I am more than a little annoyed at it and hope that it decides to come to the club when there are no guests. I know that won\u2019t be the case because it thrives on the chaos it causes, but I want to be able to do something to it. I want to take it down a peg or two. Maybe three.<br /> <br /> The show must go on. Isn\u2019t that what they always say in show biz? So, the lovely ladies of our motley got their acts together, literally and figuratively, and wowed the crowd once more. We had a lot of our usual guests tonight but the one person that didn\u2019t show up that I noticed right away was Molly. She hadn\u2019t mentioned giving tonight a miss so I texted her to make sure that she was okay. She replied back pretty quickly that she was fine, so I left it at that. I also talked to my sister to see if she wanted to join us at the movies on Thursday. I also mentioned the lot of us dressing \u201cin character\u201d for the movie and she admitted that it might be fun to do that, but seemed a little unsure of herself on that point. So, I pointed out that Lori has great taste, and loves to shop and could probably help her put together a suitable outfit for the night. I\u2019m fairly certain that Lori will have fun shopping for Elena. Hopefully Elena will have fun shopping with Lori. <br /> <br /> <i>End Session XCVII</i><br /> <br /> Desiree used Bedlam, for the record.<br /> <br /> So in the discussions between Calamity and Dr. Bright, it was noted that Desiree had dropped from 5 to 1 Clarity essentially over the course of this story. She had 6, but lost one when Gawain left, and was vulnerable to the creature. She was the back up chew toy after Calamity and Jacob raised their Clarities.<br /> <br /> Mechanically not much else to cover. Stasia wears a belt with keys, film, and odds and ends in pouches and packs which was why she had the inhaler\u2026she has a lot of space to carry stuff there. Calamity used various dream healing techniques to stabilize Desiree but she has a long way to go. She is out of commission for awhile. Soon Hee will be recovered soon enough, but she has been pressed out of the creature ambush. Looks like it is up to the player characters, huh?<br /> <br /> I think that covers it, but comments and questions are welcome.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T17:41:58-08:00","id":1172460,"title":"","content":"Happy New Year. I am utterly swamped, but I do have time to get this formatted and get this out. Confrontation with a monster this time.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XCVIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Now <u>that\u2019s</u> a bit more like it! Things have taken a much brighter turn over the past few days, though there have been a few bumps and hiccups along the way. Still, I\u2019m confident that this change signifies a turning point in our lives, and that things are going to be okay in the end.<br /> <br /> So Wednesday dawned bright and early for most of us a little before noon (Calamity was the exception; as usual she was up doing her Tai Chi thing with White Maria). Having actually slept for once, I gently extricated myself from the tangle of Brightstar and Veronica\u2019s limbs and headed for the shower. The two of them were awake and making awkward conversation when I returned, so the three of us threw on some simple clothes and headed down to Sex Breakfast.<br /> <br /> So early on most of the conversation revolved around a couple of made-for-TV movies with the odd title of <u>Sharknado</u> (the sequel had the surprisingly functional subtitle \u201cThe Second One\u201d). I don\u2019t claim to understand the attraction of such a film, though I suppose they could be considered plain ol\u2019 goofy fun. Of course, it\u2019s been decided that we shall view the duology for movie night next Monday. Sigh.<br /> <br /> Marguerite was amusing herself by using contracts to change her hairstyle (and various other facial features). This was all good fun for a while \u2013 the mohawk was particularly memorable \u2013 but then she started imitating <u>me</u>\u2026 and that is a situation up with which I will not put. Hey, at the moment my entire livelihood is based on my image, and I consider it something of a brand. I have to protect it, so I firmly asked her to quit it. She pushed me a little at first, changing so that she had my face but her own hair, but I think she saw that I wasn\u2019t kidding pretty quickly, because she stopped after a while.<br /> <br /> After I\u2019d walked our guests to their respective cars and checked the mail (still nothing from the colleges, dammit), talk turned to the impending ambush of our unwanted Hedge guest that evening. We solidified the timing of the whole thing, trying to set it up so that as many people as possible would be available to help if necessary, and D set up a group text in her phone that she could send with the push of a single button to let us know when the creature made its move. I was still pretty nervous at that point, but it seemed to me even then that we had prepared for most eventualities, so I kept my worries to myself.<br /> <br /> Then came the portion of the day I like to call \u201cmandatory fun.\u201d Stasia and Elena came over and the group of us went out on a shopping excursion to make sure everyone was adequately prepared to dress up for the <u>Fury Road</u> premiere the following evening. Ooh, my outfit is going to be so <u>hot</u>! Tight leather pants and a matching halter-bustier sort of thing, fingerless gloves, makeup in dark shades, and a metric ton of hairspray should give me a memorable image. Most of the others did their own shopping, but I helped out a bit when it came to Elena. Though we joked about assless chaps \u2013 that always seems to come up when people discuss the <u>Mad Max</u> movies, have you noticed? \u2013 in the end we went with something a bit more modest. I managed to talk her into the tight leather pants, but settled for a bomber-style jacket for the top, with bushy faux-fur around the collar. And she\u2019s going to stop by the Dream House before we leave so I can help her with her hair and makeup.<br /> <br /> We headed back to the Dream House after the appropriate outfits had been obtained, but Calamity turned right around pretty much as soon as we got back and went out again, claiming she had to meet Lucien Torrez. She wanted us to know in case she didn\u2019t come back. Fortunately, she got back about an hour later with quite a story to tell. Apparently, she had agreed to meet with Lucien at a local bar neither of them usually frequented. He had a request for her\u2026 one which nearly broke my heart when she told us about it upon her return.<br /> <br /> Lucien had a son named Paco. I say \u201chad,\u201d because apparently Paco was killed recently by some of Lucien\u2019s rivals. Paco had never been involved with his father\u2019s more \u201ccolorful\u201d endeavors, and had done his best to remain aloof from that lifestyle. Lucien had respected his son\u2019s wishes in this matter, and things had been cordial between them because of it. Lucien doesn\u2019t know exactly who decided to murder his boy in order to send him a message, and he wants Calamity to find out. To honor his son\u2019s wishes, he doesn\u2019t want his organization to have any part in this investigation\u2026 he doesn\u2019t want this to be a criminal endeavor.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not an idiot. I know that if Calamity finds the person or persons responsible for this heinous act, that party is likely to meet a very sticky, unpleasant end\u2026 either from Lucien\u2019s people or from Calamity herself. Calamity very carefully skirted around the issue of what she was going to do when she discovered the guilty party\u2019s identity, and I didn\u2019t press the issue. I\u2026 I can\u2019t really <u>blame</u> Mr. Torrez for wanting revenge in this situation. I remember how I felt when Mary\u2019s fetch killed that little girl. I don\u2019t even want to <u>think</u> about how I\u2019d feel if something like that happened to one of the motley, or Dad, or Oleander, or D\u2026 but I know I\u2019d want whoever was responsible to suffer for what they had done.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t agree with what Calamity and Lucien are doing. It makes me uncomfortable to think about it. But I do understand it, and I don\u2019t feel it\u2019s my place to interfere. I wish it wasn\u2019t Calamity who was mixed up in this, but she\u2019s a grown woman, and I can\u2019t tell her how to live her life. There\u2019s a darkness inside of all of us, but hers is so much more violent and brittle, and if she has to indulge it from time to time\u2026 well, at least it\u2019ll be against someone who legitimately deserves punishment this time.<br /> <br /> Please, God, as different as we are, I love her, and I don\u2019t want her to get hurt. Please look after her in the dark days ahead.<br /> <br /> In any case, I was obviously fairly uncomfortable during this conversation, so I seized upon Julia\u2019s interruption like a lifeline. Calamity was talking about how she planned to visit the morgue that evening and ask Paco\u2019s body what had happened to it when Julia slipped into the room and asked a bit frantically if one of us could try to get Marguerite to stop playing in the humidifier. And yes, she meant <u>in</u> the humidifier. Marguerite was using some new contract or other power to sort of liquefy her body, and was moving through the inner workings of the device in a determined sort of way.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat <u>can\u2019t</u> be hygienic,\u201d Julia commented somewhat faintly as we approached.<br /> <br /> \u201cMarguerite, honey,\u201d I called, feeling a bit nauseous myself, \u201ccould you come out here please?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOui!\u201d Marguerite replied brightly as she rematerialized next to the machine. \u201cIt was not working properly. I believe I have cleared the blockage and dealt with the problem.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh,\u201d I said, not really knowing how to respond to that. \u201cOkay. Thanks. But do you think you could\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut of course!\u201d she said with a wink, and she dove back into the small device.<br /> <br /> I turned back to Julia and shrugged. \u201cI got nothing,\u201d I said simply.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s almost hypnotic,\u201d D said, bending over to examine the machine more closely, \u201clike a lava lamp\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> And as I\u2019m starting to feel a bit queasy again in recounting that scene, I think I\u2019ll just move on, shall I?<br /> <br /> So the show itself went well last night, aside from any pre-planned shenanigans involving uninvited hedge beasts. I made sure that my solo came up relatively early on the docket so that I would be available to offer any necessary healing or other required assistance. The number in question was \u201cOut Tonight,\u201d from a musical called <u>Rent</u>. I discovered it a few months ago when I was looking into the performance history of Idina Menzel of <u>Frozen</u> and <u>Wicked</u> fame. It\u2019s actually loosely based on the plot of the Puccini opera <u>La Boheme</u>, if you can believe that, but is set in a more modern version of Bohemia\u2026 New York\u2019s Greenwich Village, and addresses more modern issues such as discrimination against homosexuals and the AIDS crisis. I think D really <u>wants</u> to like the musical \u2013 y\u2019know, on a political level \u2013 but she makes sort of a face every time I put the soundtrack on, so I play it sparingly.<br /> <br /> In any case, the song is about a young woman who \u2013 despite some rather noteworthy situational disadvantages \u2013 longs above all else to head out into the city after dark and make the most of her life. \u201cI wanna commit a crime, wanna be the cause of a fight, wanna put on a tight skirt and flirt with a stranger.\u201d Unsurprisingly, it speaks to me, and I thought it would be a peachy keen number for our little venue. The crowd ate it up, and their enthusiastic response left me feeling a little dizzy as I descended from the stage.<br /> <br /> Maybe that makes what almost happened next a little easier to understand. A contingent of Night Courtiers from L.A. had gathered at one of the tables, and I headed over there to say hello. This group included Strype, Corbin\u2026 and the Handmaidens. They were all very complimentary. Chit-chat turned to subtle flirts, which quickly evolved into not-so-subtle innuendo, and before long I found myself being passed from lap to lap as the four of them stroked my wings and my ego in equal measure. I\u2019m not sure what would have happened if that had gone on uninterrupted, but there\u2019s no question that they had my motor running.<br /> <br /> After maybe twenty minutes of this, I felt a different touch on my shoulder\u2026 gentle, but firm and much stronger than the light caresses I\u2019d been enjoying. I looked up and into the eyes of the love of my life. \u201cHey babe,\u201d I sighed, still a little blissed out.<br /> <br /> \u201cCan I talk to you for a minute?\u201d she asked. It wasn\u2019t quite a growl.<br /> <br /> \u201cSure,\u201d I said. Begging the pardon of the Night Courtiers, I allowed her to lead me out of the crowd. \u201cWhat\u2019s up?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cJust wondering what your intentions are for tonight,\u201d she said, looking a little abashed but still kind of upset. \u201cYou want to sleep with all four of them or something?\u201d<br /> <br /> I looked at her and did my best to put on a neutral expression. \u201cWould that bother you?\u201d I asked seriously.<br /> <br /> She looked down. \u201cHell, I can\u2019t blame you, Lori\u2026 that action looks hot as hell. And I don\u2019t want to dictate who you sleep with. I never want to do that\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSweetie,\u201d I said, gently forcing her to look at me again, \u201cthat\u2019s not what\u2019s happening here. You\u2019re not making decisions for me\u2026 I\u2019m asking how you feel about something, and then taking that into account when I make my <u>own</u> decision. I can see that this is bothering you, so I\u2019ll call it off. It\u2019s not worth making you worry, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> She smiled a little at that, and there was a little shimmer around the corners of her eyes that I will never admit I saw. \u201cThanks, babe,\u201d she said, \u201cyou\u2019re the best.\u201d<br /> <br /> The two of us walked from the periphery of the theater back toward the center, and that\u2019s when Oleander stormed up, looking peeved. \u201cYou going to monopolize Lori\u2019s time again tonight, de la Rocha?\u201d she asked in acerbic Spanish. \u201cShe\u2019s my girl too, you know!\u201d<br /> <br /> D\u2019s nostrils flared as she whirled on Oleander. \u201cI\u2019m not letting you alone with her until I\u2019m damn sure you\u2019re not going to poison her like you did Soon Hee,\u201d she spat back, clenching her fists. Then I saw her reel for a split second, and one of her hands shot into her pocket, and several nearby cell phones chimed.<br /> <br /> I scanned the audience for the source of the disturbance, but I didn\u2019t see anything unusual. I confess, this might be partly due to the inappropriate tingles I got from two of my lovers pretending to fight over me. Don\u2019t get me wrong; I never want to see the two of them actually come to blows over me (privately I\u2019m absolutely sure that D would win in an fair fight between the two of them\u2026 but I\u2019m equally sure that Oleander would take precautions to make sure D was poisoned by the contact, so it might be a Pyrrhic victory at best). But there\u2019s some obscene, perverse kernel somewhere deep within me that likes the idea that these girls love me enough to fight over me, and, well\u2026 my body responded to the action whether I wanted it to or not. Damn id.<br /> <br /> In any case, most of my allies were less distracted, and they quickly picked up on the fact that a middle-aged man none of us had ever seen before was showing more than a casual interest in the fracas. It was later explained to me that Calamity, Luna, Oleander, and Madame Spidertoes all used Autumn contracts on the beast at the same time. If the target had been a human, nothing would have happened. As it was, the hedge beast died nearly instantly, and those of us who could see behind the Mask saw him turn into some sort of withered plant creature over the next few seconds. Poor sod.<br /> <br /> People noticed the older gent collapse, and Oleander forced her way toward him, quickly forgetting her supposed quarrel with D. She flashed her credentials briefly, then got the hedge beast\u2019s body out of there toot sweet. She made some reassuring noises to the mundanes about how she would make sure he got the help he needed, which seemed to put their minds at ease. Nobody cared to examine the situation too closely; illness and infirmity make most people uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> So the motley entered the second half of the show with much lighter hearts, and the evening lost some of the tension we\u2019d been working under. I gave the Night Courtiers my regrets, which led to a few disappointed grumbles, but I\u2019m sure they\u2019ll all get over it. Besides, if I hadn\u2019t been so besotted with their attention earlier, I probably would have remembered that I\u2019d promised D I wouldn\u2019t sleep with the Handmaidens last Summer. All of the motley did.<br /> <br /> So after that was taken care of, I made the rounds. I made sure to speak with Madame Spidertoes before she left. She was gracious as always, complimenting my performance, and I thanked her as kindly as I could for once again gracing our establishment with her presence. \u201cNot at all, my dear,\u201d she said indulgently, \u201cI find this club very entertaining. The perfect place to unwind.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI should thank you for your help earlier as well,\u201d I said sincerely. \u201cThat creature had been a real thorn in our sides, and was pretty damned clever to boot.\u201d<br /> <br /> She waved aside my thanks as unnecessary. \u201cMaria informed me of the plan earlier this evening, and I decided to lend my aid for her sake.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you,\u201d I said again. \u201cI didn\u2019t want her to be the bait, please believe me. But Soon Hee told us that the creature wouldn\u2019t be able to affect D with its powers, and she volunteered. I\u2019ve been so worried these last few days\u2026 it\u2019s even distracted me from fretting about the wedding.\u201d<br /> <br /> An awkward silence followed that statement. Moon stood up after a moment. \u201cI\u2019ll just freshen your drink, Madame,\u201d ze said softly, and then quickly left the table.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019ll be there, won\u2019t you?\u201d I asked after a moment. \u201cAt the wedding, I mean? It would mean so much to both of us\u2026 but especially to Maria.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cOf course,\u201d she said calmly, \u201cI would not dream of missing it.\u201d<br /> <br /> There was another awkward pause at that. Almost a full minute passed before she spoke again. \u201cAnd yet I hear that you will be leading Maria back into Arcadia,\u201d she said at last, and her voice held a dangerous edge.<br /> <br /> I sighed, but didn\u2019t let my eyes drop from hers. \u201cYes,\u201d I said after a moment. \u201cI\u2019m sorry. But I <u>have</u> to go back; I made an oath. And she won\u2019t let me go alone.\u201d<br /> <br /> Spidertoes held my gaze for a bit longer. She didn\u2019t look away; she didn\u2019t even <u>blink</u>. Finally she nodded. \u201cOf course she wouldn\u2019t,\u201d she said with something that sounded almost like fondness in her voice. \u201cIt is therefore in my interest to offer you what assistance it is in my power to grant. What can I do to help, my dear?\u201d<br /> <br /> I was flabbergasted. We\u2019d talked privately about asking her for help with this mission before, but had never actually made any moves in that direction. I didn\u2019t know what to say. \u201cI\u2026 I don\u2019t know what to say,\u201d I said. \u201cThank you so much, Madame! Any advice or supplies you could provide would be most appreciated!\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded with the ghost of a smile on her face. She looked thoughtful for a moment, and then reached into her handbag. When her hand emerged, she was holding something about the size of a large beer can, which seemed to be made of the same stuff as a spider\u2019s egg sac. She handed it to me gingerly, admonished me to handle it with care, and then started to speak.<br /> <br /> \u201cIf you find yourself outmatched by the forces of the Gentry,\u201d she said solemnly, \u201cthrow this into their midst. Then turn about and run as quickly as you can. Do not stop running until you have completely left the vicinity.\u201d She thought for a moment longer, and then added \u201cand it might be best if you did not look back, either.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you,\u201d I said again, placing the strange item carefully on the table before me. \u201cI sincerely hope we don\u2019t need to use it; our plan is to rely more on stealth than strength of arms. But I\u2019m glad we\u2019ll <u>have</u> it, just in case.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded again. \u201cIt is always best to be prepared,\u201d she agreed.<br /> <br /> Moon apparently decided that it was safe to return to the table at that point, so the rest of our conversation was pretty much idle small talk. Things were starting to wind down by that point, so I stashed the spider-grenade-thingummy somewhere safe in my bedroom \u2013 nowhere near my underwear drawer, thank you very much \u2013 and spent the next hour or so hanging out with Oleander. I\u2019d arranged to stay the night with her, since she was still kind of messed up about the situation with Soon Hee the other night.<br /> <br /> I noticed that Molly spoke with D late in the evening, and that their conversation didn\u2019t seem to end to her satisfaction. When I asked D about this later, she said that Molly had told her she intended to speak with Gloria about the incident with Desiree and Chalcedony the other day, and D had told her that if she harmed or threatened Gloria, D would \u201cpunch her until candy came out.\u201d Subtlety, thy name is Maria de la Rocha.<br /> <br /> I sincerely hope nothing bad comes of this, but I don\u2019t think it\u2019s likely. My impression of Gloria\u2019s mood indicates that she\u2019ll probably start apologizing for hitting Chalcedony as soon as Molly brings it up. She seemed to feel bad about her part in that fracas, but didn\u2019t know what else she could do to help her friend. I hope that will put an end to the matter in Molly\u2019s eyes, and we can all get back to our lives and put this whole hedge beast mess behind us.<br /> <br /> So I grabbed an overnight bag, kissed my fianc\u00e9e goodnight, waved to Calamity and Jacob (who were heading off on business of their own), and let Oleander sweep me off my feet for the rest of the evening. And what an evening it was! I\u2019m not sure if she was still feeling vaguely guilty about the part she played in poisoning Soon Hee or what, but she treated me like a <u>queen</u> last night. Soft music, chocolate-covered strawberries, and dancing slow and close by candlelight. A hot bath scented with rose petals. A long, slow, sensual massage with exotic oils that seemed to relax my muscles and wake up my body at the same time. And of course that led to us making love. Slow, soft, erotic, <u>perfect</u> love.<br /> <br /> God, I love this woman. She\u2019s not a part of the motley, so I don\u2019t see her as often as I see D, Marguerite, and Julia, but that doesn\u2019t mean I love her any less for all of that. If things had gone differently, I might have been marrying <u>her</u> next month. I don\u2019t know what I would do without her. I\u2019m so thankful every day that Maria is so understanding about this, and that she has also found other people to love. I don\u2019t know what I would do if I was forced to choose between them.<br /> <br /> No, that\u2019s not true. I know what I would do. I know <u>exactly</u> what I would do, and I\u2019ve known for the better part of a year now. But I also know that it would break my heart to do it.<br /> <br /> Oleander is asleep now. I tried my best to reciprocate the sort of treatment she was giving me. I know I probably fell short on several levels, but I also know that she\u2019d never see it as such. After her third or fourth peak, we just lay there holding each other and kissing softly as she gasped out the word \u201cangel\u201d over and over again. She fell asleep not long after with a smile on her face and the tracks of her ecstatic tears on her cheeks. How in the hell could anyone ever describe this woman as a \u201ccold fish?\u201d<br /> <br /> And now I\u2019ve taken enough time with this diary. The rest of the evening will be devoted to reading, studying, praying\u2026 and planning the perfect way to greet my sleeping dryad in the morning. I noticed earlier that she had eggs, potatoes, and various peppers and onions in the fridge\u2026 I\u2019m thinking that I can probably manage a couple of nice Spanish omelets in a pinch.<br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei Grace</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> Wednesday, May 13th<br /> Nine years, one month, ten days<br /> Days without stabbing: 0<br /> <br /> The skullfucker is dead. The plan when off without a hitch. Oleander and D started arguing and when it tried to put the whammy on D we zeroed in on it and let loose the withering contracts and the damnable thing shriveled up like the Wicked Witch of the West. Fucker never had a chance, hell it barely had time to show its \u2018oh shit\u2019 face before it keeled over deader than fuck. Oleander announced that she was a doctor and she and D swept the \u2018poor man\u2019 into the back. I took the mic and assured the crowd that an ambulance was on the way and he\u2019d be fine and not to worry, which no one wanted to do anyway so it went over and the incident was swiftly forgotten.<br /> <br /> Looking over the shriveled up husk later it was hard to imagine it was the source of so much injury. I wish we could have found a way to put the Skullfucker down sooner but at least it won\u2019t harm anyone again. It\u2019s no longer a threat to the freehold. We killed it and I have no doubts that the one that trained it will follow soon enough (assuming they\u2019re not already dead). But this is not over. Hollywood has crossed a line this time. They have attacked us and they will pay for their wickedness\u2026 they will pay in blood and tears. Calamity will come for them in the night and they will get the punishment they deserve.<br /> <br /> But first, there is another who must be dealt with. I don\u2019t have his name but I can find him. Paco described him well enough for me to hunt him. He\u2019s a murderer. His hands are stained with innocent blood and soon enough mine will be stained with his. He\u2019s a monster and he deserves what\u2019s coming. He deserves me.<br /> <br /> Oh I am not blind to the irony of that. I am a monster as well, one surely as deserving of punishment and pain as he is for my sins. But I cannot undo those evils and I cannot deny that there is a savage hunger in my twisted little heart for blood and pain and screaming. What I can do is only feed that appetite on those that deserve to suffer. On those monsters that do not restrain their darkness. I have no illusion about Lucien. He\u2019s a monster as well. I know his hands are as wet with innocent blood as any, but even if he has wronged this man his son had no part in it. Paco\u2019s shade confirmed that he had indeed walked away from his father\u2019s dealings. And yes, I suppose Lucien is taking advantage of my inclinations by bringing this to me but the man has lost his son and his need for vengeance is understandable. If someone killed Stasia or a member of the motley I would not rest until they suffered for it.<br /> <br /> Of course, I haven\u2019t told most of them about this. Only Jacob knows the full story. Because he is like me, a murderer\u2026 a monster. We\u2019re not the killers we were anymore, but that sort of stain never washes off the soul. We have it in us to do terrible things and sometimes terrible things must be done. Why should someone who hasn\u2019t already tainted themselves shoulder that? If we can be the ones to do it and spare some brighter soul from the darkness then why shouldn\u2019t we? I\u2019ll never be innocent again but if I can let someone who is remain that way I will. But to be innocent means not truly understanding what it is to be a monster. Jacob can understand why I need to do this and he can help me be sure that I am not deceiving myself like I did with Mr Grey. <br /> <br /> But I have done all I can for this night. I have confirmed that Lucien didn\u2019t deceive me about Paco and I have enough to hunt his killer. I have to find time to slip away and track him. Tonight was fairly simple since I did tell Lori and the rest that I was going to find out from Paco\u2019s shade who killed him but I need to do this without drawing their attention. I also need to speak to Jacob. I wanted him to have my back at the morgue in case it was some sort of trickery and I need someone to know what I\u2019m doing in case something goes wrong. But this isn\u2019t a threat to the freehold or someone who\u2019s harmed us. This is me feeding my need for bloodletting. This is murder. I\u2019m not going to ask him to be more of a party to it than he already is without being sure he is willing.<br /> <br /> Tomorrow is therapy. I can\u2019t tell Dr Emmett what I am really up to. Instead I will talk about Stasia and Elena and going to see Fury Road and Becky\u2026 My outfit for the movie premiere is downright scandalous. I had been threatening to do up something for Humongous or Auntie (since I am a villain) but once the shopping got going I ended up jumping on the minimal tight leather train. Busting out the lace up leather pants and that spiderweb harness that I wore (if one can describe such a verb to that collection of thin leather straps) back at Midsummer. I mean, I have to glue the damned thing on to prevent getting arrested for indecency but I am way more fond of that thing than I ought to be. I\u2019ll have to send Becky a picture of myself in it and ask if she\u2019s sure she can\u2019t slip away to go with us. Actually.. no, I know she would be there if she could. But I\u2019m still sending her a picture, just with a when should I wear this for you instead of guilt. Or maybe\u2026 Maybe I should just preview it in her dreams. Hmm\u2026 Yeah, I like that idea. And um, look at that, it just happens to be time for bed. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019 Journal</b><br /> <br /> Breakfast was kind of silly if you ask me. Somehow we got onto the topic of the movie \u201cSharknado\u201d and its sequel and whether or not it was a good movie. I think it was universally agreed to be a bad movie, but some people felt that it was still worth a watch. It was then suggested that we watch it and its sequel for the next movie night. I am tempted to bow out of that movie night altogether. I think it came out while I was in Arcadia, but I\u2019ve heard enough about it to know that I probably don\u2019t want to see it. I guess I\u2019ll see what Luna wants to do. If she doesn\u2019t want to watch it maybe the two of us can go out for dinner at that good Indian place in town. It would be nice to have an evening alone with my Luna. She didn\u2019t say anything this morning about the movies, so I\u2019ll just have to remember to ask her later. I\u2019m not sure what our guests thought about the movies. At least through part of the conversation I was making coffee for Veronica, Brightstar and Gloria. The first two stayed the night with Lori, and Gloria brought De la Rocha back and stayed for breakfast. I think our breakfasts have gained some notoriety. <br /> <br /> After that Insincere Marguerite started showing off her abilities with Contracts of Mirror and changed her hair to a mohawk, then she mimicked Lori\u2019s hair, then Lori\u2019s face and hair. All of that came out of the next conversation about dressing up for the Fury Road movie tomorrow. And while Insincere Marguerite looked cute with a mohawk I think she looked better with her normal hair. <br /> <br /> Once our guests left we finalized our plans for dealing with the Hedge Beast tonight. De la Rocha will be at the door and able to ken anyone that looks suspicious. Basically anyone that is alone, or new and people don\u2019t know well enough to know if they\u2019re acting strange. She was going to start a text and save it for later, letting us know when she spotted the Hedge Beast. Or at least when/if it tried to use its powers on her. We had a trap all planned out for it. We would have De la Rocha and Oleander had an \u201cargument\u201d over Lori\u2019s affections. Or something about De la Rocha saying that Lori wasn\u2019t safe with Oleander after what happened the other night. The plan was to entice the beast into trying to use its powers on De la Rocha and she could pinpoint who it was disguised as. <br /> <br /> After the more serious conversation things turned once again to Fury Road and the need to go shopping for clothes. We called Elena to see if she\u2019d like to go shopping to get something to wear to the movie premiere. She said sure and ended up bringing Stasia with her. The rest of us were not surprised to see Stasia show up with my sister. Those two seem joined at the hip lately. So, most of us went shopping. Some of us, like De la Rocha, already had leathers to wear. Others, like me and my sister, needed to get some. I opted for just some black leather pants and a t-shirt. I have boots already. Lori had my sister try on several outfits. All of which Stasia said were flattering. I watched the interaction between those two while we shopped to see if they were actually dating or not. From what I could tell they are not dating yet, but it looks like Stasia would like to. She is definitely interested in Elena, but was trying to not push things. She even toned down her responses to the different outfits that Elena tried on. I think she wanted to respond with more enthusiasm, but figured that might make Elena uncomfortable. All good signs in my book. Stasia seems to be thinking of my sister\u2019s feelings and that is all I can ask in this situation.<br /> <br /> Calamity went off to make a phone call and came back a few minutes later to say that she was leaving to meet Lucien Torrez at a bar that neither of them has ever been to, so they could have a private conversation. This whole thing sounded kind of sketchy and she realized this so she told us where she was going just in case she didn\u2019t come back in a timely fashion. She wasn\u2019t gone that long and when she came back she explained to the group that Lucien wanted her to sneak into the morgue and ask the shade of someone he knew, a relative, who killed them. She explained that he had sought her out because she was sneaky, discreet and knows the Contracts of Shade and Spirit. I had a feeling that there was more to it than that but did not push it in front of the others. My initial plan was to wait until I could get Calamity off by herself and ask her when we had privacy.<br /> <br /> As it turned out Insincere Marguerite took that opportunity to decide to play around inside the humidifier. I\u2019m not sure what she finds so amusing about it, but she went back and started playing in it again after Julia got her out the first time. While the rest of the group was distracted by Insincere Marguerite and her antics Calamity actually took the opportunity to talk to me in private. She told me the details that she had left off in her explanation to the group. Lucien was indeed looking for someone to talk to the shade of a relative. His son. Apparently his son, who was not involved in Lucien\u2019s crime world in any way, got caught up in the violence surrounding his father\u2019s life. Someone intentionally targeted the young Latino man and killed him in an effort to lure Lucien out, and to get him to do something stupid. Lucien was of course angry about this whole situation and he wanted someone to go after the person that had killed his son and leave a message for others that they should not fuck with Lucien. He didn\u2019t want the message to come from the criminals, but instead he wanted it to be seen as coming from a grieving father. Calamity agreed to help him and to \u201ctake care\u201d of the person that killed his son. She asked me if I could at least help her with breaking into the morgue. She needed someone to act as a lookout, so she could sneak in and talk to the young man\u2019s shade. I agreed to go with her. <br /> <br /> I realize that by agreeing to help Calamity with this endeavor that I am tacitly agreeing to help kill someone. I have at least agreed to help with the morgue part of this job. I have not specifically agreed to help her hunt down the person responsible for killing Lucien\u2019s son, but I probably will. I know that I should not be agreeing to do this. Killing is what Rime was good at. Killing is what Rime had no qualms about doing. I have reservations about this whole thing, but I also understand why Calamity agreed to do this. We may not agree with Lucien\u2019s criminal activities, but he has done us a good turn or two in the past. He was a big help in dealing with Mary\u2019s fetch. Now I suppose it is time to return the favor. Someone killed his son. Someone killed his innocent son. I am under the impression that if his son, Paco, had been involved in the criminal life then Lucien would not be nearly so upset by this. I think it angers him even more because his boy was an innocent. I think that if Paco had been involved in the criminal life, Lucien would have just taken care of the payback by himself. This was different though. He didn\u2019t want it to come from his organization. He wanted it to be personal. So, he enlisted the services of someone who is capable and willing to do the job. He said that Calamity could get her motley involved in this and of everyone she chose me to confide in. She trusts me to help her do this. <br /> <br /> I guess the question is, can I kill again? This is not in self-defense. This is premeditated. This will be Calamity and I intentionally hunting down and killing someone. I know that the person we\u2019re looking for is guilty of murder. They are far from innocent in all of this. I\u2019m sure that they\u2019ve killed far more people than just Paco. So, it will be serving justice for Paco and whoever else this person has killed. I honestly don\u2019t know if I trust the system to properly deal with this person. The way that we plan on finding out who the killer is, is not exactly admissible in court. They wouldn\u2019t believe us if we told them we just asked the victim who did it. There is not a lot of evidence to link the killer to the crime. In all likelihood Paco\u2019s killer would get away with it. So, if we take it upon ourselves to kill this person then we will be acting in place of the law. But can I do it? Can I kill someone again? I\u2019m no innocent. I know that. I have done things that I\u2019m not proud of, and here I am considering doing something similar again. I know that it\u2019s not the same. This person is guilty. They killed an innocent man. This time the killing would be justified. I guess that\u2019s what really makes this different. I have a particular skill set. Violence is in that skillset. I don\u2019t know how else I\u2019m supposed to help keep this Freehold safe without using violence. I certainly can\u2019t talk anyone into turning themselves in to the police. I\u2019m not a skilled enough investigator to find the evidence we need to convict the killer. I am however good with my knives. I can do something with my knives that will help remove a dangerous element in our community.<br /> <br /> I suppose that I should get ready for the show. I still have a bit of restocking to do before people start showing up.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> The show went well, as always. It may have gone a little too well for Lori though. The Handmaidens, Strype and Corbin were all there in similar outfits and wearing similar expressions of lust on their faces. They only had eyes for Lori, and when our songstress went over to their table they made sure to heavily and shamelessly flirt with her. They kept petting Lori\u2019s arms or wings. It was a little disconcerting to watch actually. I was glad when De la Rocha went over to the table to ask to talk to Lori alone. De la Rocha had talked briefly with Calamity then went over to the Night Court table to retrieve her girlfriend. She took Lori aside and started to talk. Shortly after that Oleander started over and I knew that the motley was about to spring the trap for the Hedge beast. And it all went according to plan. When Oleander came over and the \u201cargument\u201d started an older mortal man in the crowd seemed to be playing particularly close attention to the goings on. He watched carefully as the fight started and he got noticed. De la Rocha sent her text and identified the culprit. I think she has also kenned him to make sure. Then within seconds he started to shrivel and die. I found out later that he had been simultaneously attacked by Oleander, Calamity, Luna and even Madame Spidertoes. Apparently when De la Rocha talked to Madame Spidertoes earlier in the evening she explained w hat was going on and the elder Lost decided to give us a hand once we had our target. All in all it worked rather well. To all the Changelings in the crowd it looked like a once human looking plant being started to shrivel and die. To the humans in the crowd it just appeared that an audience member suddenly had medical problems. Oleander quickly announced that she was a doctor and moved to \u201chelp\u201d the ailing man. The \u201cman\u201d was then moved to the back room and we assured the rest of the crowd that help was being called and the man in question would be just fine. <br /> <br /> After all the excitement I talked to Molly for a bit at the bar. Molly was not in the best of moods overall. She was rather upset about Gloria beating her friend Chalcedony with a chair. She wanted to confront Gloria and tell her that she was upset about what happened and not so subtly threaten her if she ever does something like that again. I managed to convince her to take things in steps. First she needed to talk to De la Rocha and explain why she was upset and that she was going to talk to Gloria soon. That way De la Rocha would not get this information secondhand and decide to pay Molly back with violence. The conversation between those two did not go badly per se, but it was not great. De la Rocha told Molly that if the Winter Courtier threatened or hurt her girlfriend then she would beat Molly until \u201ccandy came out.\u201d Molly, understandably, felt bullied by this whole confrontation. I must say that I would feel threatened too. I suggested to her that instead of threatening Gloria, which would piss off De la Rocha, that she just tell Gloria that she was upset by what happened and didn\u2019t want it happening again. I implied that Molly did not need to vocally threaten Gloria because her reputation would precede her and the threat would be implied without actually saying anything. I think she agreed that my plan would be a good plan. I offered to go with her if she wanted the company. I\u2019m not sure if De la Rocha would be upset with me for siding against her girlfriend, but I want to support my friend Molly if I can. Molly doesn\u2019t have a large support structure as it is, and I want her to know that I am there for her if she needs me. I am one of the few people that knows about her full circumstances and whether or not she knows it I understand having done things in the past that are not necessarily good. I have started to wonder if I should tell Molly about having been a Loyalist for the Lady. I think she would understand my own circumstances as well, which I think would let her know that she is not alone. We are not the only former Loyalists in the Freehold, but most of the other ones that have been confirmed were brainwashed into following the Director\u2019s orders. Molly and I were not forced against our wills to serve the Gentry. Molly was pretty much tricked into serving them. They seemed to be the answer to getting revenge for her sister. I don\u2019t really have an excuse for my actions. Some might say that I\u2019d been forced by past events into following the Lady. I don\u2019t know if I agree with that. I know I changed a good deal while I was in the Lady\u2019s realm, but I didn\u2019t have to go down the dark path that I did. I don\u2019t know. I guess I figured if I told Molly about my past then she might feel like she had a kindred spirit.<br /> <br /> After the show is when things got interesting. Calamity and I went to the hospital to visit the morgue and see if we could find the body of Paco. Getting in was easy. We both used a contract called Light Shy and snuck in invisibly. We encountered one lock that took a bit of time to bypass, but Calamity got through it without much trouble. After that we heard two voices arguing just before the door to the morgue itself. They were not morgue attendants given the conversation that they were having. One of them was talking to the other about losing something and maybe looking a second time to see if they just missed it. Given where they were having their argument I assumed that it was a body that they had misplaced. One of them said something about reporting back to their sire, which sounded like something out of a vampire movie. So, I assumed that we were dealing with vampires. Given conversations in the past we know that they actually exist, we\u2019ve just never met any before now. We tried to sneak by them, but they knew that we were there. They even knew that there were two of us. They asked us to show ourselves. We did not, but Calamity assured them that we were not there to mess with them, we just needed to talk to one of the bodies in the morgue. We did not specify who. They introduced themselves as Serena and Viktor. Calamity gave them her name, but I stayed silent. We had lost the element of surprise. I didn\u2019t want to lose all of our advantages. <br /> <br /> We went into the morgue and quickly found Paco. Calamity went to work using a contract from Shade and Spirit and summoned the ghost of the young man in question. Serena and Victor came in shortly after we\u2019d started. They\u2019d been continuing their argument in the hall, but eventually decided to come in. While Serena went looking for their missing body, Victor watched Calamity work. We were able to ask Paco five questions. What we found out was that he did not know his killer, he did not know why he was killed, and that he was not involved in criminal activities. We also got a very detailed description of the killer and a last message for his father. He wanted us to pass along to Lucien that it wasn\u2019t too late for him to get out of this business. I don\u2019t think Lucien will listen to the advice of his son, but we\u2019ll pass it along nonetheless. While all of this was going on Victor was paying close attention to us and the spirit. I could see and hear Paco, so I\u2019m assuming that the vampires could too.<br /> <br /> After we were done Calamity revealed herself to Serena and Victor. She talked to the pair for a few more minutes before she pulled a couple of complementary tickets to the Dream House out of her pocket and invited the two of them to a show. Serena and Victor explained that they were looking for the body of someone that needed to be disposed of in a confidential matter because of possible evidence that could be gleaned from it. They just wanted to make sure that the body was labelled to be burned without an autopsy being performed. The problem is that the body that they were looking for was not there, nor did it look like it had ever been there. They said that they were going to look through the morgue\u2019s computers to see if they could find a record of where the body they were looking for had gone to.<br /> <br /> Meeting up with Serena and Victor was interesting and fortuitous for us. They had disabled the cameras in the morgue when they came in so Calamity did not need to expend the energy to make herself invisible again. I remained unseen the whole time just because I didn\u2019t want to give anything away. I suppose it was not strictly necessary since we invited them to come to our club, but I trained for years to be silent and stealthy and not give away my position unless absolutely necessary. Hunting for runaways in the Hedge involved precision and patience, so I practiced those qualities a great deal. Sometimes it\u2019s hard to give up years of habit and training, so I stayed invisible. We left on good terms with the vampires though so that\u2019s good. The trick after that was to find the guy, and once that was done we had to decide what to do and how to do it. <br /> <i><br /> End Session XCVIII</i><br /> <br /> Okay, quick summary. Monster was killed (yay!) Lori sang something from Rent (yay!) and Calamity got a job from Lucian (yay?) and they met vampires on the job (\u2026.yay?). I need to roll though.<br /> <br /> Comments and Questions more than welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-14T13:40:40-08:00","id":1176054,"title":"","content":"An assassination and a trip to the movies. Just a normal Thursday.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XCIX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary<br /> </b><br /> At the risk of repeating prior hyperbole\u2026 omigod omigod <u>omigod</u>! Today has been\u2026 well, a year ago I might have called it the best day of my life so far. As it stands, what with D proposing and me reconciling with my dad\u2026 I guess it comes in third, maybe? And with my wedding and the rescue of Missy and Jane coming up within the next month, it\u2019ll probably be demoted even further. But still, it\u2019s been a banner day, and I don\u2019t want to diminish that with further quibbling.<br /> <br /> Okay, slow down and breathe, Lori. Take things in order to give it the proper context. Oleander drove me back to the Dream House for Sex Breakfast following a night that was, in its own right, pretty damned spectacular. Calamity and Jacob had just returned from therapy when we got back. D skipped so that she could spend more time with Gloria, who\u2019s still pretty freaked out by what happened last Monday and by\u2026 other things I\u2019ll get to in a moment. I\u2019d made a couple of Spanish omelets for us back at Oleander\u2019s place, so we weren\u2019t particularly hungry\u2026 so I made a few more for the rest of the motley while I sat out this second breakfast.<br /> <br /> That morning\u2019s (rather infuriating) conversation revolved around the menu for Marguerite and Julia\u2019s wedding reception. Apparently they\u2019re having trouble finding a chef, because Marguerite is insisting on traditional French cuisine. Okay, if that was the only issue it wouldn\u2019t be a problem at all; California has a <u>lot</u> of great cooks to choose from, many of whom specialize in French cooking. But Marguerite is insisting that the chef they choose actually <u>be</u> French, and the one Julia had previously vetted turned out to be Belgian. This\u2026 seems a bit unreasonable to me, but it\u2019s her wedding, and I\u2019m not going to argue with her about it.<br /> <br /> We also solidified plans for a theme night\u2026 something we\u2019ve talked about before but hadn\u2019t made actual plans for. Next weekend \u2013 if we can get the details worked out in time \u2013 we\u2019re going to perform all of the songs from the musical <u>GirlTrash!</u> I\u2019ll be singing lead on most of the solo numbers, and taking on the role of Colby in the ensemble pieces. I even convinced D to take on Tyler\u2019s few solo lines, which will mark her stage debut at the Dream House! And it only took me a year or so of wheedling to convince her! Score!<br /> <br /> I walked the guests out as per usual. Much to my surprise, it was Gloria rather than Oleander who asked to speak with me privately. First, she wanted to thank me for allowing her to spend so much time with D lately, considering the week she\u2019s had. Of course I told her not to worry about it; I knew she\u2019d had a rough time with everything that was going on with Desiree, and Oleander needed me the previous night anyway. But it turns out that her week has been even more fucked-up than I thought.<br /> <br /> See, last weekend her fetch was killed in a car accident. She hasn\u2019t been in contact with her family at all, and they don\u2019t know anything about her status as a changeling, or Arcadia, or any of that. The funeral is this weekend, and she wanted my advice about whether or not she should attend. I really didn\u2019t know what to tell her.<br /> <br /> See, her fetch was about twenty years older than her, but Gloria still looks <u>exactly</u> like she did in the 80s. She thought it might be considered in poor taste to show up at her own funeral looking like a younger version of herself. Her parents or friends might recognize her, and think that she was an imposter, or possibly even her own illegitimate daughter or something. On the other hand, it seems needlessly cruel to allow her family to believe that their only daughter is dead, when she could possibly ease their minds on that score so easily. D\u2019s told her a few general things about my own situation, and so I seemed like the logical person to ask for advice on that score.<br /> <br /> I almost wish that wasn\u2019t the case, because I had no earthly idea what to tell her. I mean, my situation was quite different from hers\u2026 my father and my fetch were estranged, he already had knowledge of the supernatural (not that I knew that at the time, of course), and I\u2019d slowly introduced myself to him and let him get to know me over the course of most of a year before I revealed myself to him. But for all that, I can\u2019t deny that reconciling with him has been one of the high points of my life since my return from Arcadia.<br /> <br /> In the end I advised her to go to the funeral, but to play down her resemblance to her past self if possible. Wear concealing clothes, and try to hide that distinctive hair with a hat or scarf or something. The \u201chat, long coat, and sunglasses\u201d look isn\u2019t that uncommon in the greater L.A. area, so she shouldn\u2019t draw too many stares that way. I told her that she should use the weekend to scope out the situation discretely, and that if there was a possibility that revealing herself to her parents might go well, that she should go for it\u2026 but carefully.<br /> <br /> So I left her with that to think about as she drove home, kissed Oleander goodbye, and checked the mail (nothing yet). Then I put on some workout clothes and engaged in a bit of self-defense training with Calamity and Jacob. I think things are coming along, though it\u2019s slow going. Luna was watching carefully the whole time, with a thoughtful expression which she didn\u2019t bother to explain until the next day.<br /> <br /> Oh, and there\u2019s one other conversation I should mention before I move on. I can\u2019t remember how it came up exactly, but D and I started talking about\u2026 well, about children. About <u>having</u> children, not to put too fine a point on it. There are complications, naturally (as D so eloquently put it, \u201cspit don\u2019t make babies), but with certain contracts \u2013 some of which Marguerite already knows \u2013 it would be possible for the two of us to have a child of our own someday. And that\u2019s\u2026 well, it bears thinking about. It\u2019s not something that I want to do right now, or even soon, really, but\u2026 dammit, I <u>do </u>see myself becoming a mom someday.<br /> <br /> D was flippant about it, like she usually is when she\u2019s nervous about something serious. She asked if I would make <u>her</u> carry and bear the child, since I\u2019d almost certainly be focused on my career. I responded with a joke of my own, of course. \u201cSure, D, I\u2019d love to see you pregnant. Barefoot, too, if possible. Now go make me a sandwich.\u201d She jabbed me lightly in the arm and gave me a grin, but then admitted that she would do that for me, if I wanted her to. The baby thing, not the sandwich.<br /> <br /> I hugged her, then admitted that I\u2019d always thought I\u2019d be the one of us to get pregnant someday (via magic, artificial insemination, an agreed-upon mutual friend, or what have you). But we don\u2019t need to think about it yet; those days are still a long way ahead of us. I opined that if any of the motley was likely to get pregnant any time soon, I\u2019d put my money on Julia. D\u2019s eyes widened, and then narrowed. \u201cShe\u2019d better discuss it with the rest of us first,\u201d she muttered darkly, and that closed the subject for the moment.<br /> <br /> We had the evening off since we were going to the <u>Fury Road</u> premiere that night, so most of the afternoon was spent lazing around or planning for future shows. As the evening wore on, however, people (including Stasia and Elena) began to congregate around our suite of bedrooms and bathroom, and we all prepared for our night on the town. A lot of my friends asked for my help with their costumes, and I was happy to provide my expertise (though of course I saved my A-game for myself). Elena opted for a more sedate look than I would have chosen myself, but I think she still looked pretty hot when all was said and done. D, Jacob, and Luna \u2013 eventually, after she saw what I did with her boyfriend\u2019s image \u2013 also consented to be dolled up by yours truly, and the results spoke for themselves.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s worth mentioning that Marguerite had gone that extra mile to make herself look good. She was wearing this sort of tube-top thingummy, and I guess she decided that it wouldn\u2019t look right unless she, umm\u2026 \u201cfilled it out\u201d a bit more than usual, so she had used her powers to copy someone else\u2019s chest. She declined to mention from whom she had taken those particular assets. Even Julia, our resident connoisseur of breasts, couldn\u2019t quite identify the source.<br /> <br /> (It probably goes without saying, but I know they weren\u2019t mine. She had settled on a set about halfway between our respective bust lines. I don\u2019t know if she did it because of my reaction to her imitating me the other morning, or if she just thought that would be a step too far on her own, but I appreciated it.)<br /> <br /> As I like to get the most out of prep like that, I had informed our substitute MC and lighting girl of when we were planning to leave, and timed our exit so that it was during an act break. True to form, the MC announced us, they threw a spot on us, and the whole crowd got to see us all dolled up in our post-apocalyptic duds. There was a wave of applause, more than a few wolf-whistles, and a number of appreciative comments thrown in our direction. Some of the others looked uncomfortable at the attention, but of course I ate it all up.<br /> <br /> Okay, I admit it. I had to think about my nascent medical studies for a couple of minutes to keep the inappropriate tingles in check. No, I don\u2019t think I have a problem. Why do you ask?<br /> <br /> The film was a lot of fun. Probably not a classic for the ages or anything like that, but a great action flick. It\u2019s pretty impressive how the director managed to make a whole enjoyable film out of what was essentially one extended car chase scene. Before seeing the movie, I wouldn\u2019t have thought that was possible. I think we all enjoyed it, but Calamity got more out of it than the rest of us combined. I think she\u2019s already planning to see it again with Becky as soon as possible.<br /> <br /> After we got back home, Calamity, Jacob, and Luna changed into street clothes and went out again, presumably to follow up on the search for Paco\u2019s killer. I didn\u2019t ask where they were going, figuring it was safer not to know. Instead, I joined my girls up in Marguerite\u2019s room and lost myself in love and pleasure for the rest of the evening. I admit I might have been a bit needier than usual, but I think I managed to stop just short of clingy, and D didn\u2019t seem to mind. I fell asleep in her very strong embrace with my head pillowed on her breast, and for a wonder I didn\u2019t get up again until late morning.<br /> <br /> Calamity was disturbingly chipper at Sex Breakfast, and she stood at the stove making pancakes as the rest of us trickled in looking disheveled and satisfied. I was going to keep up my policy of ignorance in regards to Calamity\u2019s errand, but to an extent the matter was taken out of my hands. There was a ring at the doorbell, and when we answered it, all we found was a package addressed to Calamity. It contained a single six-sided die, which I am told is a powerful totem which will allow her to influence fate itself up to six times. I\u2019d heard rumors of such a token before, and most of the stories caution that such things are incredibly dangerous if used flippantly\u2026 but with our impending excursion into Arcadia, it\u2019s too powerful an item to discount out of hand.<br /> <br /> Calamity claimed that the token was a gift from Lucien Torrez as thanks for completing the \u201cerrand\u201d he had set her. As I said, I didn\u2019t inquire further about the details, but I assume Paco\u2019s killer is either dead or very <u>very</u> unhappy right now. I hope Calamity\u2019s hands are clean of this murder, and I hope even more that she didn\u2019t drag Jacob and Luna into this mess, but either way, I suppose I should just be grateful that it\u2019s done.<br /> <br /> Conversation was all over the place this morning, from what I remember. I know that I drew the minor ire of several of my motley-mates by bad-mouthing boysenberry as a \u201choity-toity\u201d substitute for good old-fashioned blueberries in pancakes. I was in the minority on that issue, but I stand by my opinion. Calamity also mentioned that she had given a couple of comp tickets for tonight\u2019s show to a pair of vampires she met the other day in a morgue in L.A. (I didn\u2019t ask). She said they seemed like decent enough folks who wouldn\u2019t make trouble if we didn\u2019t make trouble for them, and I solemnly vowed not to mention the fact that my father was a badass vampire slayer in the early 80s.<br /> <br /> Oh, I also mentioned the spiderbomb thing that Madame Spidertoes gave me the other night. D was a little more familiar with the item in question, and quickly went upstairs to ensure that it would no longer be stored in our room. Apparently when the shell is broken, it hatches millions of tiny spiders who slowly attack any living creature with which they come into contact. If said creature should die from this attack, their body hatches out millions more of the spiders, creating a possibly endless cycle of death and rebirth and potentially spreading the destruction endlessly.<br /> <br /> Eww. I mean, I\u2019m exceptionally grateful to Madame Spidertoes for offering us this powerful weapon for use against the Empress\u2019 forces, but still\u2026 eww.<br /> <br /> So I went out to check the mail as per usual, not expecting much. When I got to the box, however, there was a pretty big envelope for me, folded over, jammed into the box, and printed with a return address from the Admissions Office of UCLA. My breath caught in my throat and my hands shook as I struggled to open the envelope. Inside was what looked like a registration package, but I still didn\u2019t want to get my hopes up until I found the single printed sheet with my name at the top.<br /> <br /> \u201cMs. Grace,\u201d I read, \u201cit is our pleasure to inform you that you have been accepted as an undergraduate student in the Pre-Medical program at the University of California at Los Angeles\u2026\u201d the rest of the words blurred through my tears, and my breath returned to my lungs in a rush. I quickly let it out again in a loud squeal\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026which, come to think of it, probably sounded like a scream. Most of the rest of the motley came rushing out of the front door, looking concerned. The sole exception was D, who alone among my friends knew that I had applied for admission and probably guessed why I had been so keen to check the mail every day. Plus, I suppose she knows me well enough to distinguish my happy screams from my terror screams. She\u2019s heard enough of both over the past year\u2026<br /> <br /> So several people were asking me questions at once, trying to determine what was up. I found myself quite unequal to the task of communicating the situation verbally, so I settled for thrusting the letter into D\u2019s hands. She glanced at it, gave me a dazzling smile, said \u201cthat\u2019s awesome, babe\u2026 I knew you could do it,\u201d and then handed the letter to the next person in line.<br /> <br /> So there was a hearty round of congratulations and inquiries as to why I hadn\u2019t told them I was applying. I tried to explain it, but I don\u2019t think I did a very good job. The real truth of the matter is that I didn\u2019t want them to know about it if I didn\u2019t get in. I didn\u2019t want to bring people down and make them pity me. And even though I know it\u2019s unlikely\u2026 I didn\u2019t want them to be disappointed in me. I didn\u2019t want to see it in their eyes when they looked at me.<br /> <br /> D brought up the fact that we might be in Arcadia for a few months (Earth time), which would place us past the start of the Fall semester. I\u2019ve been thinking about that a lot, and I know that the risk is too great for me to discount out of hand. Ideally I\u2019d like to start my college career this Fall, but just in case, I\u2019ll fill out any paperwork necessary to postpone or defer my enrollment to the Spring semester, and leave it with someone I trust (probably Oleander). If we\u2019re not back by the start of the semester, I\u2019ll have her submit it so that my status as a student will be secure. No harm in being prepared, right?<br /> <br /> First thing I did after everyone started to disperse was call Dad. He picked up on the second ring, as usual. \u201cGood afternoon, Juliette,\u201d he said warmly. \u201cTo what do I owe the pleasure?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI wanted you to be one of the first to know,\u201d I said giddily. \u201cI just got a letter in the mail. It\u2026 it was an acceptance letter to UCLA\u2019s pre-med program.\u201d<br /> <br /> There was a stunned silence on the other end of the line. \u201cThat\u2019s\u2026 that\u2019s <u>wonderful</u> news, Juliette!\u201d Dad said once he\u2019d processed it for a minute. \u201cI am so proud of you!\u201d<br /> <br /> I never get tired of hearing that from him.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe have to celebrate,\u201d he said after I\u2019d thanked him. \u201cI\u2019d like to take you out for a meal. I know that you\u2019re busy on the weekends, of course, but do you think you could\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course,\u201d I said, \u201cI\u2019d love that. I probably shouldn\u2019t miss any of the shows, but how about lunch tomorrow?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cPerfect,\u201d he said, \u201cI\u2019ll make reservations somewhere nice. Do you think Maria would like to join us?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll have to ask her to be certain of her schedule,\u201d I said, \u201cbut I\u2019m sure she\u2019d love to.\u201d<br /> <br /> We concluded the call after a bit of chit-chat, and I asked D if she could make it to lunch tomorrow, and texted her affirmative response to Dad so that he could make the reservations accordingly. Then I snapped a picture of the letter with my phone and texted it (separately) to Oleander, Brightstar, and Joan &amp; Andromeda. I got a torrent of responses almost immediately.<br /> <br /> Brightstar was the first to get back to me, with an enthusiastic \u201cOMG that is so awesome! Congrats and best wishes!\u201d<br /> <br /> Oleander\u2019s read \u201cCongratulations, Angel. I know you\u2019ll do well.\u201d<br /> <br /> Joan\u2019s response was similarly sedate and congratulatory, but Andromeda sent me <u>three</u> texts entirely composed of a line of \u201cEEEEEEEEs\u201d with an exclamation point at the end, which served to convey her excitement admirably well. I may have this sexy thing down pat by now, but I can\u2019t hold a candle to her when it comes to <u>cute</u>.<br /> <br /> I was too antsy to sit still for the rest of the afternoon, and I announced to everyone that I needed to fly for a bit. Julia stayed out on the back balcony watching me for a while, smoking weed. Jacob joined her there eventually, and I swooped and twirled and performed loop-the-loops for the sheer joy of it. I can\u2019t get over how much I love that feeling. I don\u2019t think that\u2019ll change any time soon.<br /> <br /> Eventually Luna joined me up in the air. She was brandishing a spear, but even that couldn\u2019t spoil my mood. \u201cWould you care to practice some aerial combat?\u201d she asked politely when I swooped near her. It seemed like a prudent thing to do, both in case it comes up on my Pilgrims test next month and just in general, so I quickly agreed, and for the next hour I tried to avoid a series of mock spear attacks from her. Of course, she\u2019s <u>much</u> better at that sort of thing than I am, and she whacked me good a couple of times, but she took care to never actually <u>hurt</u> me, and she offered me a number of great pointers on how I might improve my flying technique and adapt certain moves to combat situations.<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course,\u201d she said drily at one point, \u201cthis will only be useful to you if you face another airborne opponent at some point. If your foes are on the ground, I recommend you simply stay in the air and shoot them.\u201d Makes sense to me.<br /> <br /> Once I was too exhausted to continue flying, I persuaded D to help me clean up in the shower and then plopped on our bed to rest up for tonight\u2019s show. I\u2019ve been too keyed up to actually sleep, so I started writing in this diary. <br /> <br /> It\u2019s happening. I mean, it\u2019s <u>really</u> happening at last! I\u2019m taking the first steps toward becoming a doctor, someone who can really make a difference in this freehold for the better. I mean, I know I\u2019ve got a long road ahead of me before I can add those letters to my name. I doubt I\u2019ll be able to take too many hours of classes per semester; it\u2019ll be stretching my time and resources to even be considered a full-time student. So that\u2019s four years of undergraduate work, followed by probably four more years of medical school (assuming my grades allow me to stay with the program). Then at least three years of residency\u2026 maybe as many as seven. So\u2026 at least eleven years before I can even think about setting up my own practice, or taking a permanent position at a local hospital.<br /> <br /> But think of it. Someday I could really be <u>Doctor</u> Lorelei Grace de la Rocha. I suppose on some level it\u2019s a shame that I can\u2019t use my real name, but let\u2019s be honest\u2026 Juliette Wells was never going to go down this path anyway. Now that I\u2019ve taken this step, I feel vindicated. Now, I feel like I might actually be something more\u2026 something more than I would have been without Arcadia, but <u>also</u> something more than just what they made me.<br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei Grace</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> Friday, May 15th<br /> Nine years, one month, eight days<br /> Days without stabbing: 0<br /> <br /> Mmm\u2026 I\u2019m a happy little monster today. I might still be just a little drunk on fear glamour. Oh Zod I haven\u2019t soaked up such delightful terror since\u2026 oh fuck I\u2019m not even sure when the last time I got to indulge like that was. Such sweet sweet candy\u2026 So yes, Paco\u2019s murderer is no more and I sent quite the message if I do say so myself.<br /> <br /> I am hard pressed to think of anything else that could have topped off the night like that little adventure did. Fury Road is fucking amazing. Folks rolled in early to start getting ready and Lori was in demand. Once folks saw what she did with Elena they were lining up for the chair.<br /> <br /> I took the opportunity to speak to Stasia while she was trying to watch the object of her affections getting dolled up without being obvious. She didn\u2019t really try to deny her interest once I broached the subject. But with her track record of ruining serious relationships she\u2019s leery about making a move. It doesn\u2019t help that Elena\u2019s still not entirely comfortable with being attracted to a woman, more less the idea of being involved with one. Plus there are issues with the family, in particular those relatives still living in Russia. So even if Elena was interested in more it would mean choosing Stasia over family and Stasia knows a time bomb of resentment and regret waiting to explode into a bitter and angry breakup when she sees one. So for now she\u2019s determined to enjoy it for what it is while it lasts until Elena finds a guy she can take home. I really didn\u2019t have anything to say. I hate it but it sounds like she\u2019s got an accurate read on the situation. All I could do was hug her (gingerly of course) and promise to be there for her. Though I should, at some point, talk to Jacob about his family. Once bitten is twice shy and Stasia\u2019s been bitten by the unaccepting family more than once. So maybe she\u2019s seeing what she expects rather than the truth. Could also be that she\u2019s terrified of screwing things up so she\u2019s looking for excuses not to try. I don\u2019t know. But I do know I saw love in her eyes and heard pain in her voice. And I love my sister too much not to at least try to do something.<br /> <br /> But once Lori finished with Elena the conversation ended and the both of us threw ourselves into the prep. I decked myself out in just enough tight leather to avoid a public indecency charge and let myself run wild with the makeup while Lori worked her magic on D and then Jacob (which surprised me a bit) and even Luna. Luna initially declined but changed her mind after seeing what Lori had done with Jacob. I think she wanted the pair of them to match honestly, and they certainly did make quite the dangerously sexy couple.<br /> <br /> The transformation I wasn\u2019t prepared for was Marguerite. She\u2019s been showing off her contract of Mirrors recently so I guess it shouldn\u2019t have been quite the shock but when she came out from dressing she\u2019d gone with a rather small leather halter that hugged a set of breasts a good two cups up from her normal size. And once I got over the initial shock, I do have to say she wore them rather well. I may have to give that contract some thought myself...<br /> <br /> So once we were all ready and assembled, we headed out. Lori had made arrangements for us to be announced and spotlighted as we left of course. She beamed as the crowd murmured and hooted while most of the others either smiled or bore it with grace. I just threw my shoulders back and kicked my strut up to eleven, I mean if I didn\u2019t want \u2018em to look I wouldn\u2019t have worn that outfit.<br /> <br /> We were far from the only ones decked out at the premiere. It was a loud and rowdy crowd with some really wild outfits that even rivaled our spectacle. And the movie itself\u2026 Damn, I may have to see if it\u2019s legal in California to marry a movie, or at least bear it\u2019s spawn. I am so going to be going back and seeing it again and I am going to own that thing once it comes out. First thing after it was over I called Becky to find out when I was taking her to see it. We settled on Tuesday since I have made it clear that watching it is going to have me in the mood to do things to her. Many things. Repeatedly. Until we\u2019ve both run out of glamour for the poofing.<br /> <br /> Ahem. Well, so I was already flying pretty high when we got home and peeled out of our outfits. It wasn\u2019t super late (you know, for us creatures of the night) and I had a good enough impression of Paco\u2019s killer for Oath and Punishment. And so, since I didn\u2019t have anyone to unwind with I decided to at least do some recon on my target. Jacob and Luna were waiting downstairs, dressed and ready to go when I came down. I made it clear that I wasn\u2019t asking either of them to be more a part than they already were since this wasn\u2019t motley business. They made it equally clear that they had no intention of letting me do this without backup. So that was that and we all piled into Jacob\u2019s jeep. I explained that I needed to drive to maintain the pursuit and Jacob relinquished his keys to me.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d seen my prey sleeping when I activated the contract and knew he wasn\u2019t too far away. The neighborhood was nice and quiet. As we approached the house it looked like the rest on the street but Jacob and Luna both tensed up. Jacob told me not to slow down and to drive past. I hadn\u2019t planned to park in front of it anyway but I just nodded and headed on along. Apparently, he\u2019d spotted the snipers watching us and the cars full of thugs at the ready.<br /> <br /> A couple of blocks away we stopped and considered our options. I realized that while I hadn\u2019t exactly planned to rush in do it tonight, the notion of pulling away now, even to gather more intel didn\u2019t appeal to me. And honestly, we had the spot and returning later would only risk being recognized. At the very least, I was going in for a look. Lightshy would let me waltz right past the snipers and other guards outside. Jacob did not like the idea of me going alone, but Luna pointed out that not even the three of us were going to fight that many guards and my odds of being undetected were better solo.<br /> <br /> So I called upon the Wyrd and vanished. It was indeed a simple matter to slip up to the house. Less so to get the side door unlocked and open but not too much so. As soon as it started to open, I heard the distinctive click of weapons at the ready and rolled away from the doorway before the pair of guards opened fire. I waited as they approached and looked about, trying to come up a logical reason for the door to have unlocked and opened when there was clearly nothing there. As soon as they moved out to look around, I slipped inside and followed the pull toward my prey.<br /> <br /> He was upstairs in a room with two guards at the door. I paused to consider how to deal with them. One man was already babbling about how Lucien Torrez was in league with the devil while his partner tried to get him to calm down. Well\u2026 it was just too tempting not too whisper to poor Manuel. I told him he was going to die. That they were all going to die. He started to get agitated and it only got worse when his partner told him he didn\u2019t hear anything. I kept teasing the poor thing while his partner radioed that they needed someone to replace him. Reading his fears I saw that he was almost phobic of bats and I considered using Cobblethought to pluck one out of his nightmares as the replacement arrived, but the hallway wasn\u2019t that big and all that random gunfire would have made it crowded. Pity\u2026 I would so have enjoyed hearing that little piggy squeal in terror. But he wasn\u2019t the one I was there for so I crawled up the wall and clung to the ceiling to stay out of the way while they sent him away. I leaned down, hanging from the ceiling between them and the door unseen. It was tense and more than a little exhilarating. I could feel the men behind me, all but touching back to back as I worked until the lock clicked over. Then in a single smooth motion I pushed the door open and dove up and in, flattening myself against the ceiling inside the room even as the guards outside turned to face the equally startled guard inside and a few rounds peppered the floor.<br /> <br /> My prey was sitting up in his bed, pistol in one hand and a taser in the other. His bodyguard was similarly armed. The guards from the hallway stepped in cautiously and began to argue with the bodyguard inside about how locked doors do not open themselves. While my prey was right there and easily within reach, there really wasn\u2019t a way I was going to finish him and escape, even using the space under the bed as a hedge gate, without getting my pretty little ass (along with the rest of me) shot full of holes. The crew was agitated and I was hearing references to the devil and witches and at least one guy was actually swatting at the empty air. The waves of fear washed over me as I clung there like a very unfriendly neighborhood spiderman. I saw the old man lick his lips and suddenly inspiration struck. My prey wasn\u2019t a plantbeast from the hedge but the withering would still have an effect. I concentrated and watched as he gasped and started cough. His men all turned as he wheezed and gasped out for water.<br /> <br /> His bodyguard started to move to the adjoined bathroom when I pumped another wave of Autumn magic into my victim. This time his coughing was a dry raspy hacking and he fell back against the headboard, drawn and haggard like a man lost in the desert. His lips cracked as his eyes glazed over before his head fell back limply. The guards were shouting and moving to full bore panic at this point. A couple were tearing apart the room searching while the one was swinging wildly at the thin air and one just fell to his knees crying and praying to the Lord to spare him. I drank it down with a shudder and kept my focus on the old man, wringing the life out of him like a damp rag. His skin started to tighten and shrivel as his breath rattled past those cracked lips. A trickle of blood so thick it was like oil ran down his chin. The men wailed and watched in horror as he continued to just wither and shrivel up before their eyes until he looked like the guest of honor at some museum\u2019s Egyptian exhibit.<br /> <br /> At that point, I took in a slow deep breath and basked in the panic and horror for a moment before I slithered along the ceiling back out to the hallway, leaving the chaos behind me and making my way out and back to the jeep. I told Jacob and Luna it was done as I curled up in the back seat with a dreamy sign of contentment. Since they were curious, I filled them in on what had transpired while Jacob drove us home. Once there, I floated up to my bed and curled up contented and fear drunk to sleep soundly till shortly before dawn.<br /> <br /> Meditation with White Maria went well. Perhaps it should have bothered me more, but my prey had killed an innocent and earned his fate. I had no doubt Paco wasn\u2019t his first victim but he was certainly the last. He\u2019d deserved what happened. As had his minions who\u2019d witnessed it. And yes, it felt fucking amazing. And yes, I know it shouldn\u2019t. I know it means I\u2019m broken inside. I know I\u2019m a monster. But so long as there are other monsters\u2026 monsters that prey on the innocent and the weak... for me to sate my needs with then I can live with what I am. After all, only a monster like me can deliver the sort of punishment they truly deserve. <br /> <br /> I got back to the Dream House before the others were up so I decided to make pancakes for everyone because pancakes are delicious. Lori gave me a few looks as I danced about and sang to myself by the stove and once the package with the Drama Die arrived I\u2019m pretty sure everyone that wanted to could connect the dots. But she didn\u2019t ask and I didn\u2019t tell. I think it helped that talk of a powerful token led to talk of our rescue mission and that led to Lori mentioning that Madam Spidertoes had given her an egg-sac from some sort of very powerful hedge spider creature to use as a weapon against the Empress\u2019 troops. DLR was familiar with it and quite concerned about making sure it was handled with extreme care.<br /> <br /> While she was off to take care of that Lori went to check the mail. I\u2019ve noticed she\u2019s been keen on it and I figured she was expecting something but I had no idea it was something as big as her college acceptance letter. Which she announced with a scream that brought us to the yard in a hurry. And once she explained, (well once she shoved the letter into D\u2019s hands so she could) everyone was overjoyed. Lots of hugs and tears of joy and congratulations until Lori took off to fly. I drifted out to the back porch to watch, staying down rather than heading up to the balcony where Julia was firing it up.<br /> <br /> I just sat there watching her fly. She is so beautiful. People keep telling me that the person I was isn\u2019t gone. They talk about going back to school and following my dreams of being a doctor and helping people. Lori is doing just that. She found her father and rebuilt her relationship with him. She\u2019s got a place in this world. She\u2019s actually going to med school (well, pre-med at the moment but she\u2019s on track). She\u2019s proof it can be done. Proof that I could be that girl I once was again.<br /> <br /> But the truth is\u2026 I don\u2019t really WANT to be the girl I was. I\u2019m strong and I\u2019m dangerous and I\u2019m loud and I fucking like it. I still want to make the world better, but I can do that in ways she never could. I can touch people\u2019s dreams, find those that are lost in them and guide them back. I can destroy the monsters who prey on people like the girl I was now. I can put a stop to men like Anton who murdered a good man just to strike at his father. Yes, I do still think the world would have been better with Dr Katheryn Moss in it, but it\u2019s just going to have to fucking settle for Calamity because that\u2019s who I am and I ain\u2019t going anywhere anytime soon.<br /> <br /> Though speaking of dreams, I should go and put a few finishing touches on the one I made for Dahlia since I asked her to come to the show tonight so I could give it to her.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> So, therapy went well this morning. I talked to Sullivan about the upcoming movie and how we were all going to dress up for the occasion. I focused mainly on the positive things going on in my life. I did mention the Hedge Beast. It\u2019s dead and can\u2019t cause any more trouble so I didn\u2019t think we really needed to keep it secret any longer. No need to worry about causing a panic. I think Sullivan actually already knew about the beast anyway. He was there when Desiree was brought in, so he must have known something was going on. Anyway, I described how we took it down and he was suitably impressed with how well our plan worked. I had been expecting something to go wrong, but thankfully it all went according to design. When we got back to the house the others were making breakfast. Lori seemed to be on a Spanish omelet kick and was making them for anyone who asked. Then conversation moved on to food as well, specifically food that was going to be served at Julia and Insincere Marguerite\u2019s wedding. Marguerite was very adamant that the person making the food needed to be from France. They could not be from any other country. The chef had to be a French person making French food. I can understand wanting to have good native food, but a chef doesn\u2019t need to be a native of a country to make good food from that country. She was insistent though. I think the chef that Julia found was from Belgium and that was not acceptable. I don\u2019t understand. It was fun to listen to the conversation though.<br /> <br /> Conversation then switched to upcoming songs that the ladies were going to sing for a show and they settled on doing the music from the movie \u201cGirl Trash!\u201d There is a lot of good music in that movie and the others jumped on to the idea. I think everyone was going to do a different song and the others would back them up. All in all I think there are something like seven songs that they\u2019re going to do. Should be a good show. I\u2019m looking forward to it.<br /> <br /> After breakfast Lori, Calamity and I practiced in the backyard. Luna watched from the sidelines. I think Lori is getting pretty good, and she\u2019s only had a couple of lessons. She\u2019s a dancer so she\u2019s graceful and doesn\u2019t have a difficulty repeating movements that we show her. We just have her do a certain move a number of times and it gets into her muscle memory. We also explain what each move is used for and how it can be used. I ended up getting thrown or knocked onto my butt a good number of times today, but if Lori learns something from it then it\u2019s all worth it.<br /> <br /> After that it just seemed like time was on fast forward. Later in the afternoon Elena came over with Stasia to get changed for the movie. While folks were getting changed Calamity took Stasia aside to talk to her. Normally I wouldn\u2019t listen in but I heard her say something about Elena, so I did. Calamity it seems wanted to talk to Stasia about whether or not she wanted a relationship with my sister. Stasia answered that she did, but wasn\u2019t sure if it would work out. Elena might not be able to travel back to Russia to visit family as often if she was in California all the time, plus she isn\u2019t sure what our parents would think about my sister being in a lesbian relationship. I\u2019m not sure of that myself. I know my parents moved here for better work opportunities, but they have enjoyed the social freedoms that the United States offers as well. They are a bit traditionalist though, so I guess I\u2019m not sure where they would fall on that issue. <br /> <br /> Anyway, Lori did hair and make-up for a number of people, including me and Elena. Lori went easy on me, but I could tell that she must have done something right because Luna seemed interested in my new look. Elena was really pretty in her outfit and with her hair done up. I\u2019ve never seen her wear anything so daring. I think she was a little embarrassed about the whole thing, but she didn\u2019t let it bother her overly much. We made a show of leaving the Dream House during an intermission so everyone in the crowd could see our outfits. We got a number of appreciative looks from the crowd. I do have to admit that I was a little unnerved being at the center of so much attention, but I just zoned out the stares and continued walking out the door. I knew what I was getting myself into when I agreed to get all dressed up, so I have no one to blame except myself. I guess it was a little fun. I was told I looked good and I got to show off a little bit. The quiet bartender wearing leather on his body and product in his hair.<br /> <br /> The movie was a lot of fun. I know the whole group really liked it. Julia especially really liked Furiosa. She thought the character was really pretty. I had to agree. I think Luna did too. Hell, I think we all did. I know we all have fun. We got lots of appreciative looks and compliments on our outfits too. Overall, I thought the evening was a success. We pulled off all that we intended to and had fun doing it. I\u2019m not sure if there\u2019s going to be many more opportunities to wear my new leather pants, but I have to say that I\u2019m glad I didn\u2019t get the really tight ones. Luna liked the way those looked on me, but the looser ones were much more comfortable. And I am a sucker for comfort. I\u2019m not a hedonist by any stretch, but I have found that I enjoy my creature comforts since I got back from Arcadia. A nice comfy bed to sleep in, coffee to start the day, plenty of food to eat whenever I\u2019m hungry, and a beautiful woman who loves me. Sometimes I don\u2019t think I deserve my Luna, but I don\u2019t want to give her up. I think she\u2019s good for me.<br /> <br /> So, after the movie we all went back to the Dream House. Some of us changed and went right back out again though. Luna, Calamity and I all piled in my jeep. I let Calamity drive since she was using her Contract to find Paco\u2019s killer and had to be the one driving the vehicle. We made it to L.A in good time and found the neighborhood pretty easily. The surprise came when we started driving down the street the killer lived on. I was keeping an eye out and noticed several concerning things. There were two snipers up on rooftops watching the street. There were people concealed in parked cars on the sides of the street and there was a camera closely following my jeep as we drove down the street. I told Calamity to keep driving and explained why. We agreed to go about a block over and sneak up to the building. After a quick discussion we agreed that it would just be Calamity that went in after Paco\u2019s killer. I was not super happy about that since I wanted to be able to watch Calamity\u2019s back, but she was really the best suited to get in and out unnoticed.<br /> <br /> Calamity got through an alarmed door, but she couldn\u2019t hide the fact that the door seemed to be opening and closing of its own accord. So, the guards opened up with machine guns near the door. I was concerned, until a couple of minutes later Calamity texted me to say that she was okay and had not been hit. She then snuck upstairs and took care of the target. She told us how she had terrorized one poor shmuck by using an ability to whisper in his ear, promising to kill him. In the end he was begging for a priest, thinking that he was hearing a demon. She then managed to get into the killer\u2019s room, apparently his name was Anton, and she used the same contract that she used on the Hedge Beast. She could not safely get down to Anton to cut his throat or stab him anywhere else, so she used the one power that she has that can be used at a distance and the source of the attack is not obvious. Anton and the men in the room with him were freaking out, but they couldn\u2019t stop what they couldn\u2019t see. And in short order Anton was dead. After that Calamity snuck out of the house and back to where we were waiting for her. We piled in the jeep and headed home. Overall it was a productive night.<br /> <br /> So in the end I didn\u2019t end up killing anyone tonight. I certainly enabled someone to do so, but I didn\u2019t actually use my knives to end someone\u2019s life. I suppose that is probably a good thing. I know that Anton was not a good person and was guilty of killing an innocent man, so it was justice for the dead that we passed down. I can\u2019t help but think that I skirted the edge of right and wrong with this one. Anton deserved what he got. He was a killer. We couldn\u2019t prove it enough to get him arrested and even if we did, he\u2019d probably beat the charges. There wasn\u2019t enough evidence to link him to the crime otherwise it would have been police watching the street and not thugs. I will give him this though, he knew retribution was coming and was prepared for it. Well, at least as prepared as a mortal can be. He didn\u2019t expect something other than human to be coming for him. He didn\u2019t expect us to be able to bypass his protections as easily as we did. All his men know is that one guard swears that there was a demon whispering in his ear and then shortly after that their boss basically dehydrated to death in front of their eyes. There was nothing they could do to stop it. They just weren\u2019t prepared for us. They weren\u2019t prepared for Calamity. Who knows what kind of rumors are going to be spreading about Lucien now? I\u2019m sure at least some of those guys now believe that he\u2019s in league with demons or something like that. It\u2019s kind of funny in a morbid sort of way. I don\u2019t know if we\u2019ll ever know what the fallout from tonight\u2019s actions is going to be. I don\u2019t know if Lucien will share what happens with us. It\u2019s not really our business I suppose. We served our purpose and now we\u2019re out. I will admit to being curious though.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> This morning Calamity was especially chipper. That\u2019s the only word I can really use to describe her mood. She was chipper. Her good mood paid off for everyone as Calamity offered to make pancakes for the whole motley. Everyone seemed to enjoy that. After breakfast, and a strange conversation about boysenberry, Calamity then showed the rest of us what she had gotten on the doorstep this morning. Apparently, Lucien left her a token. Like, a magical token that can influence fate in the user\u2019s favor. It is a pretty powerful totem from what I understand. Something that can actually influence fate has got to be strong.<br /> <br /> Then the big surprise for the morning came. Well, early afternoon. Lori went to go get the mail, as has become her habit, and a minute or so later we heard her scream. We all ran outside to see what was wrong. She tried to start talking a couple times but couldn\u2019t seem to get the words out, so she just handed a letter to De la Rocha. De la Rocha then smiled and said congratulations to Lori. It turns out that Lori got accepted into the pre-Med program at UCLA! Talk about good news. We all congratulated her and there were hugs all around. After the hugs Lori looked at us with a flushed face and said that she needed to fly, and she went to the backyard to do just that. She ended up flying for a good bit of time. I think she was up there for about forty-five minutes when Luna went outside with a spear and joined Lori in the sky. She asked if Lori wanted to practice her aerial dodging skills. Lori said sure and they started going at it. Lori was already warmed up from flying so she started off pretty well and only got better from there. They both seemed to be having fun, which was nice to see. I watched from the balcony with Julia. Julia had decided that smoking some pot was in order so I got something of a contact high while watching my Luna and Lori flying around in the backyard. It was fun though, so I didn\u2019t mind.<br /> <br /> I think Lori\u2019s hope was to start school in the next semester, but it\u2019s not certain that we\u2019re going to be back from Arcadia before the school year starts. She may need to delay her enrollment for a semester until we get back. I know that she doesn\u2019t want to do that, but she may not have a choice. We\u2019re going to Arcadia, and time doesn\u2019t pass the same there that it does here. At least in most realms it doesn\u2019t. In the Violet Empress\u2019 realm time barely passes there while it goes by much more quickly here. I mean Hunting Hawk only waited half an hour before he left to go after Lori and a year or so had passed here since she arrived. So, we don\u2019t know how long we\u2019ll be gone. We could be gone for months, or longer. Hopefully we won\u2019t miss too much while we\u2019re away. I know that I\u2019m going to have to explain where I\u2019m going to Elena. She will be worried if she doesn\u2019t hear from me for months on end. I can\u2019t just leave her in the dark after I\u2019ve worked so hard to get her back. I know that she will likely not be happy about me going back to Arcadia, but I can\u2019t let Lori go alone. She\u2019s like family and her friends are important to her, and if they\u2019re important to her then they\u2019re important to me. I would do anything for Elena, so it follows that I will go to great lengths to help my motley mates. I just hope that Elena will understand. <br /> <br /> <i>End Session XCIX</i><br /> <br /> Just a few comments<br /> <br /> Yes, Andromeda is officially adorable. Her picture is adorable enough but I play her as being pretty much the cutest grey alien girl ever.<br /> <br /> As much commentary as Insincere Marguerite\u2019s boob job got, the striking change she did with Contracts of Mirror was the over foot long punk spikes for hair in blue, white and red. She used Skinmask for that.<br /> <br /> Calamity killed Anton using Contracts of Eternal Autumn, repeatedly hammering him with Brother to the Ague while hidden with Lightshy from Contracts of Smoke and clinging to the ceiling with Boon of the Scuttling Spider from Contracts of Darkness. Really she was having to fuel her Contracts on the fear she was generating, which was, to be fair, a lot.<br /> <br /> Okay that covers it. Tonight we do session 100. I look forward to reporting on it. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-14T21:48:01-08:00","id":1176184,"title":"","content":"There's something really profound about the last line in Lorelei's journal, referenced in Calamity's as well, that really sums up what I want out of a World of Darkness game, or any tabletop really; &quot;Now, I feel like I might actually be something more\u2026 something more than I would have been without Arcadia, but <u>also</u> something more than just what they made me.&quot;<br /> <br /> The idea that someone so innately changed can genuinely become better than both who they were and what they were made to do in their durance is a very potent theme for me, and I love that every one of the player characters has done this. Lorelei is a performer with a world class voice, but she's also aiming to not just be a supernatural healer but a<i> natural</i> physician; Calamity is a terror in the night with a hunger for pain, but she's also a dreamweaver and likewise a healer; Jacob's skills with a blade and penchant for stealth are as strong as they were in his loyalist days, but in spite of his Elemental nature he was the basis of Molly's support network, helping her overcome her depression over her lack of memories and re-experiencing life again; Insincere Marguerite is still a smooth and confident thief, but she's a force of personality and she knows how to keep someone with instabilities like Julia satisfied. Everyone is not only going beyond what the roles Arcadia set for them but building off those roles into branches they otherwise wouldn't have accessed in a mundane life.<br /> <br /> Sadly I've yet to really get this kind of results from a game, but I'm looking forwards to when I do.<br /> <br /> Something else I'd like to note is that I love the moment that Calamity realizes, after finding no avenues of using her usual methods of assassination via stabbing, she did have a ranged means. It comes off as a real organic moment when someone realizes, &quot;Wait, I have another method I can use,&quot; after they'd been using another tried and true method. Granted, Calamity needed to use the fear in the room to fuel it, but it's still a fun scene.<br /> <br /> Also, Baroness, as a storyteller, what kinds of experiences (if any) do you feel justifies a player taking four and then five dots in a skill? Relatively speaking dots in a skill are cheap (at least in Chronicles of Darkness) yet the higher dots represent general mastery over all fields that skill has. I've had at least one ST who has restricted use of those dots until later, and words online of others who do the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T02:03:27-08:00","id":1176726,"title":"","content":"It is a good line.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite is a particularly vivid example, being a racist Front National supporter with contempt for most she met. While still struggling with her elitism and temptation to become what her Keeper was, she is a MUCH better person than either before or than her keeper made. But all the PCs really doing well with that.<br /> <br /> Yeah, it was come up with at the scene. A lot of good, inventive use of Contracts there. I was pleased with how it went.<br /> <br /> Honestly? I don't limit that much. This is actually kind of easy to justify in Changeling, where the PCs bodies are warped to suit tasks, and most of the PCs are often literally superhuman in their fields. Most PCs in MDH only have 4-5 in a small handful of Skills. Now Attributes, those are often pretty high. Sorry I don't have much to add...I just tend to play loose with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T13:08:10-08:00","id":1180227,"title":"","content":"Session 100. What a crazy ride it\u2019s been. And we are far from done.<br /> <br /> <i>Session C</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> One Hundredth Entry (wow, seriously? One hundred? I guess so. Wow!):<br /> <br /> So it\u2019s been about a day since I last wrote in here. Things have been fairly quiet, compared to the events of the last week or so, but sometimes that can be a good thing. After Luna and I had exhausted ourselves with aerial combat training, we hit the showers (separately; she\u2019s a cutie but I know she\u2019s not interested and the last thing I wanted to do was tease her or make her uncomfortable after she\u2019d been kind enough to spend her afternoon sparring with me). Then I fixed myself a salad and prepared for the Friday night show.<br /> <br /> The show itself was fun, if not spectacular by our standards. Marguerite and Calamity both performed and did very well, as always. I crooned away at some of my usuals, including \u201cIt Had To Be You,\u201d an old Frank Sinatra number. It was something dad used to listen to back in the day. It was more smooth and sultry than sexy, but I think I managed to wring a pretty good reaction out of the crowd in any case.<br /> <br /> And speaking of the crowd, I noticed a few\u2026 \u201cinteresting\u201d groups as I scanned the audience during my numbers, and made a mental note to visit them each to say hello. I chatted idly for a while with Dominika and Angelica, who seemed to be there together but not <u><u>together</u></u> together, if that makes any sense. I likewise spoke briefly with Dark Kimberly, White Maria, and Becky, but I knew that Calamity was going to hit that table as soon as her duties permitted, so I didn\u2019t take up too much of their time.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Calamity, she pointed out a couple of newcomers to the club early in the evening, and identified them as Viktor and Serena, the vampires she had met the other day in LA. As soon as decorum and my own duties allowed it, I sauntered up to say hello to the two of them.<br /> <br /> Now, I confess that I know zip about vampires, except what I\u2019ve gleaned from books and movies over the years\u2026 and considering how spotty that sort of information can be when it comes to faeries and changelings, I wasn\u2019t about to take any of that at face value. I suppose I could ask my dad for more information, but he obviously doesn\u2019t like talking about that part of his life, and I don\u2019t want to upset him unnecessarily.<br /> <br /> Having said all that, those two seem to be okay. They have an easy, teasing sort of friendship that soon reminded me of the bond shared by Jimmy and Peg (though I don\u2019t think Viktor and Serena were romantically involved). It was soon obvious that they knew as little about us as we knew about them, and Viktor half-jokingly asked if they had to worry about getting whisked off into Disney-style madcap adventures when they dealt with us. He intimated that Serena might enjoy such an adventure, but she seemed reluctant to embrace his idea.<br /> <br /> I laughed it off with a wink as Calamity joined me at their table, and told them that the Dream House was a safe place for all, and that they shouldn\u2019t have to worry about anything like that while they enjoyed our hospitality. Viktor went on to say that they had been careful not to bring anything iron into our house, or to accept any gifts or offer any thanks. Calamity and I sort of looked at each other, and then started to giggle.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe appreciate the thought,\u201d I said after a moment. \u201cWe really do. It\u2019s very considerate of you to think of things like that. But for the most part the old stories are just that\u2026 stories.\u201d<br /> <br /> Calamity gestured to the table in front of us. \u201cYou\u2019ll notice that we have salt shakers on all the tables, too,\u201d she went on to elaborate. \u201cYou might come across individuals among our society who can\u2019t touch iron or salt, or hear church bells, or whatever, but those aren\u2019t hard and fast rules for everyone.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo what about you guys?\u201d I asked curiously. \u201cShould I avoid arranging to meet you in religious supply stores or Italian restaurants?\u201d<br /> <br /> They glanced at each other and looked about as amused as we had a moment before. \u201cNah, all of that\u2019s pretty much garbage. It\u2019s just sunlight with us, really.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWow,\u201d I said after a moment. \u201cSo\u2026 you two are really immortal?\u201d<br /> <br /> They gave each other another knowing look. \u201cWell\u2026 technically, maybe,\u201d Serena said after a moment. \u201cBut you almost never come across a vampire older than a century or so. I mean, think about it\u2026 everybody has bad days, and all it takes is one <u><u>really</u></u> bad day to end your existence for good. People with normal lifespans get into car accidents all the time, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIf you do come across a really old one,\u201d Viktor elaborated, \u201cmost of the time it\u2019s because they\u2019ve spent a while asleep. Serena was like that for a little while\u2026 I came across her after she\u2019d had a rake handle through her chest for seven years or so. If the barn she was in had burned down and she\u2019d been exposed to the sun\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat must have been rough,\u201d I commented, trying to imagine it.<br /> <br /> Serena shrugged. \u201cIt wasn\u2019t too bad. You\u2019re not really conscious of much when you\u2019ve been staked. Culture shock after I woke up took some getting used to, though.\u201d<br /> <br /> I rolled my eyes. \u201cTell me about it. I walked out of this world in 1978, and stumbled back into it in 2014.\u201d<br /> <br /> Calamity took up the thread when the two of them only looked blankly at me. \u201cTime flows differently in Faerie, like in the old stories. You can wander into the mists and spend one night there, then come back to find that decades have passed for everyone else.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnyway,\u201d Viktor said, \u201ccould\u2019ve been worse for Serena. See, there was this one guy who was acting the fool and needed to be taught a lesson\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThey don\u2019t want to hear about that,\u201d Serena cut in quickly.<br /> <br /> \u201cSure they do,\u201d Viktor said, grinning. \u201cOr at least\u2026 <u><u>she</u></u> does,\u201d he amended, indicating Calamity.<br /> <br /> Serena sighed. \u201cFine,\u201d she said after a minute.<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay, so this one guy was acting up, giving in to his bloodlust and killing wantonly and gruesomely. There\u2019s no cause for that sort of behavior; there\u2019s no reason to hurt people when we feed, and that sort of thing just draws attention and puts the rest of us in danger. So we police ourselves and keep it under control. This guy\u2026 we locked him in the trunk of his car and put it in the ocean for a couple of weeks. He couldn\u2019t breathe\u2026 but he didn\u2019t have to. The fish ate his eyes.\u201d<br /> <br /> That was unpleasant and gross, so I chose to focus on a different aspect of what he had said. \u201cSo, you don\u2019t kill people when you drink their blood, and I assume drinking their blood doesn\u2019t turn someone into a vampire, right? That make sense, otherwise there\u2019d be piles of bloodless bodies all over the place.\u201d<br /> <br /> Viktor nodded. \u201cWe like to keep a low profile.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s the same with us,\u201d I said. \u201cNow, I know what you\u2019re thinking \u2013 everybody has the same question when they first meet me \u2013 and yes, they\u2019re real,\u201d I said with a smirk. Obviously I was referring to my wings, which were still visible due to the contracts I had used earlier. What else? The two of them chuckled at the wordplay. \u201cBut most of the people here are going to go home convinced that I was wearing an elaborate, very well-made costume. The faerie magic helps to keep us concealed, because\u2026 well, because most humans don\u2019t really <u><u>want</u></u> to know the truth when you get right down to it.\u201d<br /> <br /> Viktor looked around nervously. \u201cSo\u2026 we can\u2019t see you as you really are unless you let us. That\u2019s why she looks different than she did the other night?\u201d He indicated Calamity, who had also employed a bit of Vainglory for her act.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s about the shape of it, yeah,\u201d Calamity agreed.<br /> <br /> He sighed. \u201cWe\u2019re completely surrounded, aren\u2019t we?\u201d he asked.<br /> <br /> I grinned. \u201cThere are a fair number of us here tonight, yes,\u201d I said, \u201cbut you\u2019re safe here. We\u2019ve offered you our hospitality, and this place is a sanctuary. And not everyone here is a changeling. Not even by half. If we didn\u2019t let regular mortals in, this place wouldn\u2019t do us much good.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat do you mean by that?\u201d Serena asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou feed on blood,\u201d Calamity explained, \u201cand we feed on\u2026 well, it\u2019s a kind of energy produced by human emotions. Anger, fear, desire, sorrow\u2026 we can sustain ourselves with any strong emotion, though most of us prefer certain flavors over others. Lori here is an expert at teasing specific emotions out of our mortal patrons so that our changeling friends don\u2019t go hungry.\u201d I blushed at the compliment, but hey, she\u2019s right\u2026 it is what I do best.<br /> <br /> The conversation went on for a few minutes before I realized that I\u2019d been neglecting some of our other guests, and excused myself. \u201cPlease come back any time,\u201d I said sincerely. \u201cAnd tell Jacob at the bar that I said to comp you each a drink. Do you drink\u2026 wine?\u201d I asked, pitching my voice all husky and low.<br /> <br /> The two of them showed grins that looked a little forced, but they took it with good grace. \u201cSorry,\u201d I said after a moment, \u201cI couldn\u2019t resist. Seriously, though, it\u2019s been good speaking with you, and I hope you\u2019ll both come back soon.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sure we will,\u201d Serena promised, and that was that.<br /> <br /> My final table of the evening included Rowan, Neon, and Veronica. I was a little thrown at first by the lack of Brightstar, but Neon quickly explained to me that my girlfriend is spending the evening with one of her boyfriends. As I kinda-sorta hoped to have other plans that night anyway, I didn\u2019t let it get me down too much. Plus, I was <u><u>very</u></u> happy to learn that Veronica was there as a sort of chaperone for Rowan and Neon on their date!<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s great!\u201d I said enthusiastically as I took a seat at their table. \u201cI must admit, I thought you two would be good for each other and I hoped you\u2019d hit it off. I\u2019m glad to hear you\u2019re giving it a try, and I hope things work out for you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks,\u201d Rowan said softly, looking down and blushing. \u201cElektra is\u2026 a very kind person.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe is,\u201d I agreed, and then turned to Veronica. \u201cAnd how did you get roped into this?\u201d I asked with a grin.<br /> <br /> She rolled her eyes. \u201cRowan asked me to come as a favor, and then she looked at me with those big soulful eyes, and she looked so helpless\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m familiar with the look,\u201d I said, chuckling.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo I get to sit here smiling through uncomfortable silences and snippets of awkward conversation all evening,\u201d she continued mock-bitterly.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, I don\u2019t want to take up too much of your time,\u201d I said after a moment. Veronica shot me a dirty look, but I think she understood that as Rowan\u2019s ex, I didn\u2019t want to steal focus from her current romantic endeavor. \u201cI did want to tell you about something exciting, though. Neon, you might have already heard about this from Brightstar\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Neon thought about it for a second, and then smiled and nodded. \u201cOh, yeah. Congratulations, Lori.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks,\u201d I said, feeling the big goofy grin starting to spread. Turning back to the other two, I began to elaborate. \u201cI got a letter in the mail this morning. I\u2019ve been accepted into the pre-med program at UCLA for the Fall semester.\u201d<br /> <br /> Rowan got up, walked around the table and gave me a big hug. \u201cThat\u2019s wonderful, Lori. I\u2019m so happy for you. I know you\u2019ll do well.\u201d Veronica also offered me her congratulations with a thumbs-up and a somewhat watery grin.<br /> <br /> After a couple more minutes of socializing, I made my way to D at the entrance. She greeted me with her usual hug and kiss, which I guess the patrons are starting to get used to, as we didn\u2019t draw nearly as many wolf-whistles this time. \u201cHey babe,\u201d she said with a cocky grin, flexing her biceps and drawing the word \u201csecurity\u201d tight across her chest.<br /> <br /> \u201cHey, hot stuff,\u201d I said leaning up against her. \u201cGot any plans for tonight?\u201d<br /> <br /> She shrugged a little. \u201cNothing specific yet. I can find something to do with myself if you\u2019ve got plans, though.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cActually,\u201d I said warmly, \u201cI was hoping to make plans with you.\u201d<br /> <br /> She put an arm around me and kissed my forehead. \u201cYou got it, babe,\u201d she said simply.<br /> <br /> \u201cOnly if you\u2019re sure,\u201d I said after thinking about it for a minute. \u201cI know Gloria\u2019s had a rough week\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> D shook her head. \u201cI talked to her earlier,\u201d she explained. \u201cShe\u2019s okay for now. Tomorrow night, though\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSay no more,\u201d I said. \u201cI\u2019ll see if I can stay with Oleander, or Julia and Marguerite or something.\u201d<br /> <br /> I let things sink into a comfortable silence between us as the final acts wound down. After a minute or two, I spoke again. \u201cSo Gloria told me that you suggested she speak with me about\u2026 about her family,\u201d I said.<br /> <br /> D nodded. \u201cHope that was okay, babe. I didn\u2019t mean to overstep\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I waved off her concerns. \u201cOf course. I didn\u2019t mind talking to her\u2026 I just wish I\u2019d had better advice to give. I mean, there are a lot of differences between her situation and mine, and she has to be careful about taking that step. But, for all of that\u2026 if she <u><u>can</u></u> reconnect with her family, I think she <u><u>should</u></u>.\u201d<br /> <br /> D nodded again, this time with a sagely air. \u201cFigured you\u2019d say that. I think it\u2019s what she needed to hear, too.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo you two have gotten pretty close, huh?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> She shrugged, looking vaguely uncomfortable. \u201cI guess. It\u2019s\u2026 she feels it more than I do. She\u2019s in love with me, but I\u2026 well, I feel something for her. We\u2019re more than friends, more than friends with benefits, but\u2026 it\u2019s not on the same level for me as it is with Julia and Marguerite. It\u2019s not like it was with Spidertoes.\u201d<br /> <br /> I leaned in to her embrace. \u201cI love the fact that you didn\u2019t even feel it was necessary to include me in that evaluation,\u201d I said softly.<br /> <br /> \u201cLori, you know you\u2019re on a whole different level\u2026\u201d she started.<br /> <br /> \u201cI know,\u201d I interrupted her, \u201cwe <u><u>both</u></u> know that about each other, and it doesn\u2019t need to be said. I\u2019ve never had that before\u2026 that sort of confidence in a relationship. I like it.\u201d<br /> <br /> She looked into my eyes. I\u2019m not sure how or when she got so good at deciphering my emotions from my solid-black orbs, but damned if she can\u2019t read me like a book. \u201cSo I guess it\u2019ll just be the two of us tonight?\u201d she asked, kissing the top of my head again.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019d like that,\u201d I admitted. \u201cI love that you\u2019ve been so good about all the poly stuff over the last year, D\u2026 but sometimes I just want to have the most wonderful girl in the world all to myself for a while.\u201d Clearly embarrassed, D moseyed off to tell Marguerite and Julia about our plans for the evening.<br /> <br /> Things wound down a bit after that. The crowds thinned and then were gone, leaving only the house\u2019s residents and Natasha, who had apparently arranged to stay in the guest room. I found this curious, but didn\u2019t ask about it until the next morning. As the last of the stragglers were heading for the door, music started to play from the overhead speakers, and Marguerite and Julia began a stately waltz on the stage. I\u2019m not entirely sure, but I think the music might have been one of the orchestral pieces from <u><u>The Nightmare Before Christmas</u></u>. D and I joined them on stage for a few passes. It was fun.<br /> <br /> Then we headed up to bed, undressed, and lay in each other\u2019s arms for a while, kissing and cuddling and talking for the next few hours. We talked about the wedding. We talked about college. We talked about family, and music, and love, and life. And yes, we made love. It was slow and passionate and tender, as it tends to be when it\u2019s just me and her. It\u2019s more about real, tangible, lasting love than lust and immediate sexual urges, so I don\u2019t go in for as much of the kinky stuff in that situation.<br /> <br /> Okay, so I might have asked her to call me \u201cdoctor\u201d once or twice, but that\u2019s it.<br /> <br /> The next morning dawned a little earlier than usual for Maria and I, as we had our lunch with dad scheduled. So we were up, showered, and dressed before most of the motley even made it to the kitchen for Sex Breakfast. We didn\u2019t eat anything, but joined in the banter as usual. Natasha was still there, and I finally learned why she had stayed the night in the first place. Turns out that she and Elena and Stasia had planned to go see a movie the previous night (<u><u>Fury Road</u></u> again, actually), but the other two had been so lovey-dovey with each other that the plans sort of disintegrated and Natasha had left in disgust, tired of being left out of all the conversations.<br /> <br /> I tried to commiserate with her, telling her about my own experience as a third wheel with Missy and Jane in Arcadia. I don\u2019t know if Missy was into Jane before we were Taken, but I\u2019m pretty sure Jane had always harbored something of a secret crush on our raven-haired friend. There were times when the two of them only had eyes for each other, and I had to turn my back in the middle of the night and pretend to be asleep. Some of the things they said to each other\u2026 well, it was pretty embarrassing to witness. Add to that the fact that I know what it\u2019s like to come home drunk in the middle of the night and face one of Dad\u2019s lectures, and I think I have a pretty good idea of why Natasha wanted to stay at the Dream House. Poor thing.<br /> <br /> Marguerite and Julia had gone out dancing in LA the previous night, and then watched the sun rise over the boulevard before heading back to the Dream House. I used contracts on both of them to restore their energy (what Marguerite calls \u201cthe poofing\u201d), and D and I departed for lunch.<br /> <br /> We met dad at a nice little steakhouse in Santa Monica and enjoyed a pleasant lunch together. Of course we talked a lot about the wedding, and about college, but we also talked about other things. D mentioned the possibility that if she keeps up with her X-ray tech certifications, it might be possible for her to work for me someday. I opined that I always pictured her working <u><u>with</u></u> me instead of for me, but that was a side track that was mainly based in semantics and didn\u2019t really go anywhere.<br /> <br /> That got D talking about why her job as a tech had been so important to her\u2026 which were a lot of the same reasons I had for applying to UCLA, actually. It was an act of defiance against the Gentry, proof that she could be more than what they made her, but also more than what she\u2019d started as. She was doing something to help people rather than just joining a gang or stalking innocents from the shadows. Once again I felt bad about having selfishly convinced her to quit and come to work at the Dream House.<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t want to do anything that\u2019s going to put a strain on our relationship, babe,\u201d I said, taking her hand.<br /> <br /> \u201cBut this <u><u>will</u></u> put a strain on your relationship,\u201d dad chipped in softly. \u201cIt would strain <u><u>any</u></u> relationship. You will be attending college, working, and taking on any number of other responsibilities. You will have less time for each other, and that will become a point of contention. You will argue, and you might find yourself shouting at each other from time to time when it all periodically becomes too much for you. And then you will remember how much you mean to each other, and apologize, and you will emerge from the incident stronger for it. I have confidence in you.\u201d<br /> <br /> I had to blink away a few tears before I could choke out a simple \u201cthanks, dad.\u201d Because he\u2019s right, of course. College and med school are going to be <u><u>hard</u></u>. It\u2019s going to test us. If I was less than one hundred percent certain that we could weather those tests, it wouldn\u2019t be worth it. But I am, so it is. It is on so many levels, for what it means to me, and for what it might mean to the people I could help.<br /> <br /> We nailed down a few more details for the wedding and dad settled the bill. I offered to take care of it, of course, but he wouldn\u2019t hear of it. \u201cWe are celebrating your achievement, Juliette,\u201d he said firmly, \u201cand my pride in that achievement. Allow me to demonstrate that pride with this small token gesture, at least.\u201d I let him pay. It made him happy.<br /> <br /> Dad gave each of us a hug before we parted and headed back to the Dream House. And here we are. D\u2019s fretting over how Gloria\u2019s doing at the funeral, and I don\u2019t want to take away from those worries by distracting her, so I\u2019m writing in my diary and thinking about my numbers for tonight\u2019s show. I\u2019ve filled out the registration forms for UCLA (I did what I could online, and dropped the rest in the mail while we were out).<br /> <br /> The next chapter of my life is about to start, what with college, marriage, the Pilgrims, and Missy and Jane all just around the corner. It\u2019s exciting and scary all at the same time. But with D and my friends at my side, come what may, I know I can face the challenges ahead.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> Saturday, May 16<sup>th</sup><br /> Nine years, one month, seven days<br /> Days without stabbing: 1<br /> <br /> I should be a perfectly contented little monster but of course I\u2019m not. Because nothing is ever as simple as it should be where I\u2019m concerned. At least the weirdness is more or less contained within the borders of Calamityville for the moment.<br /> <br /> Anyway, things began simply enough last night. The show was solid. It\u2019s nice to see Marguerite performing regularly. Zod knows it\u2019s intimidating to share a stage with Lori but she\u2019s good and is certainly finding her style and getting more comfortable in front of the lights. My solo number was also well received. I may have to dip into Garbage\u2019s catalog again sometime.<br /> <br /> And the house was full, as it usually is given our reputation. Man, it\u2019s going to make a lot of folks sad when we head into Arcadia. I really hope we don\u2019t lose too much time there. Not that we wouldn\u2019t be able to build our following up again in short order I guess. But still, our adoring fans will miss us. And in addition to said fans, we had several of the Lost present (though I do imagine we count some of them in the previous group).<br /> <br /> Neon and Rowan were being chaperoned on their first date by Veronica (who made a most fetching third wheel). Dominika and Angelica were there without a chaperon but it was cool since they weren\u2019t on a date. The usual barflies were joined by Natasha, who had left the totally-not-a-date between Stasia and Elena that she\u2019d been invited to. Dahlia was there for her dream date with the Winchesters even if she didn\u2019t know it yet. And joining White Maria and Dark Kimberly was Beautiful who had gotten the night off and decided to drop by for a surprise date.<br /> <br /> Dahlia was suspicious of my good mood but I played it off without giving her a straight answer and then distracted her with my gift. She asked about when to use it but didn\u2019t press for more explanation than my assurance that it was a present for her enjoyment. I confess, I really kinda wish I could see her expression when she wakes up from that. I was super pleased with how the finishing touches I put on it turned out.<br /> <br /> Also among the non-dating couples was Viktor and Serena, the vampires from the morgue. Lori was chatting them up and I joined in. We had some pleasant conversation and traded a few basic tips about each others kind. Turns out they enforce the vampiric don\u2019t be a colossal dick and ruin it for everyone rule, though apparently without being allowed to actually end folks. (I so feel them on that restriction\u2026) However, they have apparently found some very creative alternatives. I learned a long time ago that if you\u2019re doing it right, death isn\u2019t a threat, it\u2019s a privilege and these two clearly get that. But as Lori was present, we didn\u2019t dwell on that too long. Perhaps next time they drop by I\u2019ll be able to talk shop more.<br /> <br /> And from there I made the rounds. Even if I hadn\u2019t noticed the way Beautiful was watching me I would have waited till I was done to stop off at that table because once I got there I wasn\u2019t leaving. So, after making the both of us wait I sauntered over, drawing my glass in as I did so I could slide into her lap and fall into a long deep kiss. A couple of years later give or take, we came up for air and I greeted the others. So, Becky is still guarding Laughing Carp but Sandoval had apparently taken over for her on short notice to give her the night off. The four of us chatted pleasantly and it came up that Becky had been looking at training someone to help her with her duties and give her more time for.. other things. Which is to say, us. That\u2019s some deep water for both of us and we know it so I was fine with her focusing more on the how of making this happen rather than what it meant.<br /> <br /> And that required finding someone she felt could do the job to train. Which it turns out is Angelica. I was a bit surprised, not that I didn\u2019t think she was wrong but just that I didn\u2019t realize that the woman had Becky\u2019s particular set of skills. (Okay, I was also surprised that Becky would trust someone who escaped from the Director enough\u2026 but I did say she was free of his influences and she trusts my abilities.) She explained that Angelica is more capable than most realized and so we ended up heading over to speak to her and Dominika. She agreed to step outside and show me and the four of us strolled outside.<br /> <br /> I was not prepared for what happened. Angelica was, apparently, some sort of full on Old Testament angel back in Arcadia. Wings of fire and flames shooting from her eyes and the whole shebang (and apparently she even used to have a flaming sword to boot.) I was taken aback, but it wasn\u2019t till she spoke that things went weird. She spoke in a thunderous chorus, the same words just with a lot of reverberation and echo. It shouldn\u2019t have reminded me of Them but it just caught me off guard and suddenly I was remembering Their voices\u2026 the sadness and tenderness in Them as They gathered me up after, holding me and soothing me. And something inside me just went sideways and suddenly I wanted\u2026 no, I needed that feeling.<br /> <br /> I managed not to let it show too much, certainly not more than could be explained by surprise. We spoke a little about her ability and such, I was mainly focused on trying to reign in the\u2026 oh for fuck\u2019s sake, call a spade a fucking spade Calamity\u2026 I was dealing with trying to get a grip on the sudden drop into subspace.<br /> <br /> Once Dominika and Angelica left, Becky turned her gaze upon me and it suddenly dawned on me that because of how she\u2019s wired the rather abrupt shift in my sexual desires and caused a corresponding shift in her own. And while she was clearly a bit surprised, as soon as I saw the hunger and dark promises in her eyes my will to fight back up evaporated. I can\u2019t say I recall the words exactly, but she did hold back to ask if I was alright and I pretty much straight up told her that being reminded of my Keeper had sent me right the fuck into a submissive spiral and asked (I did manage to wait till we were alone before the begging started) her to take me upstairs. I mean, I didn\u2019t quite lay it out in those words but Beautiful is smart and she knows me well enough to fit the pieces together.<br /> <br /> And while I am being honest about this, it\u2019s not the first time I\u2019ve had this reaction. The whole reason I am such a fucking slut for leechfingers is that their cold and hungry touch reminds me of the silken one that wrapped about my bloody and broken body when They were done. It\u2019s not healthy. I don\u2019t like it and I\u2019m not sure what the hell to do with this realization. I mean, it\u2019s not like I didn\u2019t realize that letting Leanne or the handmaidens have their way with me was a terrible idea even without fully admitting to why. Thankfully, Desiree\u2019s threat to Scarlet seems to have left them gun-shy (though they were in the Night Court pack hot for Lori the other night so that may be wearing off) and I\u2019m not sure what Leanne\u2019s been doing with herself since she and Charlotte ended their fling. But sooner or later it\u2019s going to come up again and I honestly have no idea how that\u2019s going to play out at this point.<br /> <br /> What I do know is that Beautiful assured me that she was quite okay with my odd behaviour last night as I walked her out after sex breakfast. We are still on for our date Tuesday. I should do something special (I mean, besides taking her to the best movie ever made) maybe take her some place nice before\u2026 I should speak to White Maria Monday about a good Chinese place. Or, given her standards, an acceptable one.<br /> <br /> At least I haven\u2019t been too off kilter today. Jacob and I had a really good bit of sparring. Much as I do like teaching Lori, it was nice to just let go and clear my head of everything but the play of steel and muscle for a while. I called to check on Desiree after that. According to Dr Bright, she is doing as well as can be expected. He mentioned that Gloria had been wanting to visit and asked my opinion. It seemed like a good idea to me, her friend and roommate seems like a good anchor to reality for her. I\u2019m planning to visit her myself here before the show. I know Oneiromancy isn\u2019t well-suited to rebuilding her connection to reality but I am going to speak to her therapist about how dream therapy could aid them while I\u2019m there. Desiree is a friend and I take care of my friends.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> After all the excitement this afternoon the evening seemed dull by comparison. At least for me that is. We had lots of folks come to the show, as has become the usual. Hailey and Molly hung out at the bar keeping me company. My Luna was at work, so it was nice to have someone to talk to in between making drinks. Some guests of note tonight were Viktor and Serena. The two vampires from the morgue. They shared a table and seemed to enjoy themselves during the show. There was also Rowan, Neon and Veronica present for the show. From the way they were sitting it looked like Rowan and Neon were on a date and Veronica was there as a friend, or in some similar capacity. They all seemed to be enjoying themselves as well. It was good to see Rowan there. She has been absent for a while and only recently started coming back to the club. I think she took the break up with Lori hard. She seems to be bouncing back though, which is good. She is a sweet person.<br /> <br /> After the show Lori and Calamity made their rounds through the crowd. Pretty early on Lori made her way over to the vampire table to talk to Viktor and Serena. They seemed to get along well. At least their conversation was amicable and they smiled a lot. At one point Lori gestured to the bar, so I assumed that she was letting them know that I\u2019d take good care of them if they needed a drink. I wouldn\u2019t be surprised if she comped them a couple of drinks too. The pair didn\u2019t come up to the bar after that so I\u2019m unsure, but I\u2019m sure I\u2019ll find out soon. Calamity also came over to the vampire\u2019s table and the four of them continued the conversation. I\u2019ll have to ask what they think of our newest guests.<br /> <br /> Later Lori made her way over to the table with Rowan, Neon and Veronica and they all chatted for a bit. Lori seemed really happy for Rowan and Neon, which backed up my theory that they were on a date. They all seemed to be having fun, including Veronica. She was there as a friend I guess, but didn\u2019t seem to feel left out of things.<br /> <br /> As far as my evening goes I talked to Natasha for a while. She came to the bar and ordered a drink. I carded her and she produced an ID that said she was twenty-one. I\u2019m not sure that it\u2019s real, but I didn\u2019t quibble over it. I gave her the drink she ordered and she began to vent. Apparently, she is feeling like a third wheel when it comes to Stasia and Elena. It seems that all three of the were supposed to go out to see Fury Road again, but the other two were completely focused on the other and ended up leaving Natasha out of things. I don\u2019t think the movie thing happened. So, Natasha is feeling left out while my sister and Stasia make \u201cgoo-goo eyes\u201d at one another. I tried to be sympathetic but wasn\u2019t sure how to really \u201cfix\u201d that situation. I suggested that perhaps once the newness of the relationship (or not a relationship) wears off the pair of them will not leave Natasha out of the dynamic quite as much. After Natasha ordered her second drink I asked her if she had a way home other than driving herself. I was concerned that she was planning on drinking more than was safe. She said that she hadn\u2019t thought of that and asked if she could stay at the Dream House for the night. I said that was fine and let her have her drinks. I did cut her off before she got too drunk. I didn\u2019t want her to suffer a monster hangover in the morning.<br /> <br /> I also talked to Molly for a bit. There wasn\u2019t all that much to catch up on. Her life has been moving along uneventfully. She had been assigned by Lowjack to follow someone the other night. I was curious but didn\u2019t ask who she was watching. She\u2019d probably tell me, but I wasn\u2019t sure if that was information that should be known. In retrospect I wish I had asked her. My curiosity is piqued and I can\u2019t exactly go and ask her now. Maybe the next time I see her at the bar I\u2019ll ask and see if she answers. I talked to Hailey too. Again, nothing important. Just general life stuff. I didn\u2019t tell either woman about the errand that Calamity, Luna and I took the other night. Torrez came to Calamity in confidence. It seemed like it would be unwise to let anyone outside the motley know that there was any connection between the Summer Courtier and us. I think he asked that it stay between the motley in any case, so I didn\u2019t mention it.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Breakfast was good as usual. We had guests over as has also become the norm. This time it was Becky, who had stayed with Calamity, and Natasha who had slept off having drunk too much last night. Food was good and appreciated by all. Conversation ran the gamut from sex with Julia\u2019s parents to vampires. I think the earlier conversation started up because Julia wanted to make sure that no one in the motley was having relations with her parents. I think that she thought it would make things awkward later, and she is probably right. We also talked about our out of town guests Viktor and Serena. Natasha for her part was surprised that vampires even exist. It was confirmed that they do, and that they have much the same restrictions on revealing themselves to mortals as we do. They also don\u2019t need to kill a human when they feed on them. They can just take a little bit and it would be like the person had just donated some blood. I hadn\u2019t thought of it, but it makes sense. Otherwise everyone would know about them due to the bodies everywhere.<br /> <br /> After that conversation died down Lori and De la Rocha, who had not joined us in eating, said that they were going to head on out and meet with Lori\u2019s father. Apparently they had made plans to meet up and go out to a steak house for lunch to celebrate Lori having been accepted into UCLA. I am happy for Lori. I\u2019m glad that she was able to reconnect with her father and to get accepted into such a good school. She has aspirations to becoming a doctor, and I for one think that she will do great at it. She is a lot smarter than she gives herself credit for, plus she has a genuine desire to help other people. I don\u2019t really remember if I had picked out something that I wanted to study if I got to go to college. You\u2019d think with my memory the way it is that I\u2019d recall something like that, but I still have some blanks here and there. I guess that part of my life is still a bit hazy. I hadn\u2019t really thought about going to school now. I have a decent job at the Dream House and a pretty good life here too. I probably don\u2019t deserve what I have, but I\u2019m not willing to give it up either. It may not be the most exciting life, but it\u2019s mine and I\u2019m happy with it.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session C</i><br /> <br /> Surprisingly little to say. We all had dinner out (Gawain\u2019s player joined us!) and then had the game. Mostly RP, we meet our vampires.<br /> <br /> I will note that since Insincere Marguerite extemporaneously asked Lori for \u201cthe poofing\u201d a while back that has become our term for it IC and OOC. It even came up with our Spring Courtier who had the power in Golden Eagle, though I don\u2019t think it was ever called that IC.<br /> <br /> We pass about 18 days, to June 3<sup>rd</sup>, 3 days till Insincere Marguerite and Julia Oldacre get married. Two weddings, a trip to Arcadia, and a honeymoon are imminent. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 01-28-2018, 04:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T13:28:47-08:00","id":1180230,"title":"","content":"So, you could say we're coming up on Two Weddings and a (potential) Funeral? Sounds about right.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm surprised that both sides were as open about their abilities as they were, not to mention that Vampire society seems a little less spooky than it's presented in the books. I guess that little reduction in the overall intersplat paranoia level is just part of your general genre tendency for shifting WoD from Horror to Dark Fantasy (or Paranormal Romance arguably for this campaign). Plus, I guess a city with only a little Covenant presence would be a little less monstrous. Or I'm too cynical about WoD vamps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T15:01:43-08:00","id":1180257,"title":"","content":"My games are more Urban Fantasy and Supernatural Romance than horror, really. They actually said very little about their society per se; they pooh-poohed most weaknesses, noted their masquerade (which they were able to guess the Changelings had too) and made vampires sound fairly benign. Both are Carthians, too.<br /> <br /> Not saying they were being puppetmasters, just that they made vampires sound like something Changelings did not need to worry about without outright lying about anything. Who knows what Faeries can do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T13:39:42-08:00","id":1181218,"title":"","content":"I rather like how diplomatic both sides were. Neither the Vampires nor the Changelings were too forthcoming yet they explained some of the general facts about their respective sides; they were friendly but not overtly so; they established they have their own masquerades but also that their respective feedings weren't lethal. It was a good first meeting (well, discussion) of the respective factions.<br /> <br /> Also, I've been looking back at the previous posts here, somewhere near the start. It's really surprising not only at how things changed, but at how long certain elements have been in the story. I suppose that's the beauty of having Actual Plays around - you get a history to look back on, rather than just a memory. It's really cool.<br /> <br /> Also, Baroness, I see you've gotten certain images hosted elsewhere. Congratulations. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T17:32:35-08:00","id":1181286,"title":"","content":"Yeah, It's a reason I reward people for journals. To me, the record of the game is important both short and long term.<br /> <br /> And yeah and I went ahead and at least got the currently running games some pics back up. Plan to with Demon, CoD, and Vampire too<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T13:09:08-08:00","id":1184853,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s been about three weeks. Two weddings and a trip to Arcadia are bearing down on us, as well as bachelorette parties, a test, and a honeymoon. Nerves are building as the big days ahead, as a visitor arrives even as these are on our heroes minds.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> And once again I have let the journaling slide for a bit. I promise myself that I\u2019m not going to forget, and then one thing comes up, and another, and another, and before you know it two and a half weeks have gone by with nary a single entry. I mean, I <u><u>have</u></u> been really busy lately, what with helping to plan two weddings and a bachelorette party, a honeymoon, a rescue mission, and daily training in\u2026 well, just about everything, to make sure that I\u2019m as prepared as I can be for the Pilgrims\u2019 test next week.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s right, Marguerite and Julia\u2019s big day is just two days away! The bachelorette parties are tomorrow night, and I meet with Jimmy and Peg the following Monday for my final exam with the Pilgrims (so, y\u2019know, even if things go poorly in the test itself, at least I\u2019ll have movie night to look forward to). And four days after that are the bachelorette parties for me and D. And the day after that I\u2019m getting <u><u>married</u></u>\u2026 a word which I can\u2019t seem to say aloud lately without stammering. Then there\u2019s the honeymoon. And when we get back from that\u2026 Arcadia. And then college.<br /> <br /> So yeah, the foreseeable future is pretty packed.<br /> <br /> The last two and a half weeks have been pretty quiet, aside from the wedding preparations and the fact that the four of us are all slowly going crazy with a strange combination of stress and bliss. Julia seems to be okay for the most part; she\u2019s walking around with her head in the clouds, clearly over the moon about her impending nuptials. Marguerite has been remarkably quiet and reserved (for her). It\u2019s not like she\u2019s having second thoughts or anything like that; it\u2019s more like the full weight of what she\u2019s about to do is finally starting to hit her. The two of them have been spending their nights separately for close to a week now. I guess it\u2019s to build the anticipation or something.<br /> <br /> D and I have not been so restrained (though I haven\u2019t asked if she wants to abstain for a week before the wedding like they are yet). D\u2019s sort of in the same boat as Marguerite as far as pre-wedding jitters go\u2026 she\u2019s happy but nervous as all get-out, though she\u2019s better at hiding it (so far). As for me, well\u2026 I\u2019d like to think I\u2019m handling it all pretty well, mostly focusing on my friends\u2019 wedding, and my party planning duties, and my Pilgrim training. It still hits me occasionally, and I\u2019ll laugh or shudder suddenly in the middle of an unrelated thought. God knows what I\u2019ll do after Monday, when I don\u2019t have anything else to distract me anymore.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s see, other than that\u2026 well Calamity\u2019s relationship with Becky seems to be progressing nicely, and she\u2019s as happy as I\u2019ve ever seen her\u2026 which is far preferable to the destructive spiral of depression she\u2019d been in for the previous four months. Jacob and Luna are still chugging along, and their relationship seems as stable as ever. I\u2019ve continued my training in unarmed combat, and have picked up the basics of knife fighting from Jacob and Calamity as well, though I doubt I\u2019ll ever be as good as either of them\u2026 they make it all seem so effortless. I\u2019ve also had Andromeda teach me the basics of computer applications, so that I don\u2019t feel quite so at sea in this brave new world.<br /> <br /> Things picked up again at last night\u2019s show, and not necessarily in a good way. I only had one solo number, so I decided to dress the part and pretty much stay in that outfit for the entire night. I pulled my hair back tightly, applied dark lipstick and eye shadow, and slipped into a sheath dress I like to call \u201cthe Grinch\u2019s Heart,\u201d because it\u2019s black and at least two sizes too small. Needless to say, I had to be careful how I sat for the rest of the evening.<br /> <br /> Anyway, once I\u2019d slinked my way through Robert Palmer\u2019s \u201cAddicted To Love,\u201d I started working the crowd. Joan and Andromeda were there, and both asked me how I was doing. I was forced to admit that the closer we get to W-Day the more of a nervous wreck I\u2019ve become, and they offered to help me deal with the stress in some creative ways. I seriously considered their offer, but in the end I took a rain check so that I could spend the evening with D.<br /> <br /> Joan and Andromeda have both promised to be at Julia\u2019s bachelorette party tomorrow night, though in Joan\u2019s case I had to spend a few minutes reassuring her that it was unlikely to devolve into orgiastic shenanigans. I\u2019d be worried that Julia\u2019s shindig might be stealing potential guests from Marguerite\u2019s, but I\u2019m pretty sure D\u2019s not planning a gala event in any case\u2026 last I heard she was just going to take Marguerite through the mirrors to a Paris gay bar and get her laid. Good for her!<br /> <br /> So I bade a reluctant farewell to my bestest friends-with-benefits, and began to circulate the crowd again. There was one new face; an attractive changeling lady with icy characteristics but an obvious Spring Court mantle. She was rocking a low-cut red dress, and I\u2019d noticed her looking at me earlier, so I decided to introduce myself.<br /> <br /> \u201cWelcome to the Dream House,\u201d I said as I took the proffered seat at her table, \u201cI\u2019m Lorelei.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSiobhan,\u201d she replied with a small smile and a handshake. (Pronounced shuh-VAHN, by the way\u2026 I had to look up how to spell it). \u201cI\u2019m new to the area, and I\u2019d heard that this was a good place to meet local changelings. Well, this and one other place\u2026 but I\u2019m not much of a club dancer,\u201d she admitted.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, you should check out the Rose &amp; Thorn sometime anyway,\u201d I said. \u201cFlores runs a great club. Lots of atmosphere, and a wonderful place to pick up some glamour. So what brings you to Malibu?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI have been sent from the Court of Fallen Stars as an ambassador,\u201d she said without pausing. \u201cWe heard that you already have such emissaries from the Court of Fallen Angels and the Court of the Dragon, so we thought it prudent to send one of our own.\u201d<br /> <br /> It took all of my considerable self-control to avoid a sitcom-worthy spit take. The Court of Fallen Stars. Hollywood. Dammit.<br /> <br /> We made small talk for a few minutes until I could reasonably excuse myself without being rude. I\u2019m not sure what sort of changeling she is, exactly\u2026 I\u2019d wager there\u2019s some snowskin in her, like Jacob, but there was something birdlike about her as well. It mostly manifested in the way she moved her head when she was intent on something\u2026 sort of quick and jerky, cocking it to one side and looking at the object of her interest from odd angles. I found myself making a conscious effort not to emulate her once I noticed it.<br /> <br /> One thing that she said made me perk up and take notice\u2026 she planned to visit the reigning monarch the next day. I made a beeline for Calamity once I\u2019d extricated myself from her table, just to make sure she knew about all of this. She had already spoken with Siobhan herself, and assured me that Becky was already aware of the Hollywood girl\u2019s intentions to visit Jolie the following morning. Between the two of us, we then made the rounds to discreetly inform the rest of the motley.<br /> <br /> I told D first, and she offered to give Gloria a call to see if her girlfriend knew anything about the newcomer. I headed across the room to the bar to let Jacob and Luna know what was going on (Calamity handled Julia and Marguerite), but almost as soon as I got there, I saw D turn even paler and nearly drop her phone. I hurried back to her side to ask what was wrong, and got there just as she was hanging up.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat was Gloria,\u201d she said once she\u2019d calmed herself a little. \u201cShe\u2019s met Siobhan, though they didn\u2019t travel in the same circles. Said she always seemed nice enough, but maybe a little odd. And\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe didn\u2019t know if it was an official position\u2026 it\u2019s not one we have in this Freehold, anyway. She said that it was common knowledge that if you did something to piss off the Spring Court, they\u2019d sic Siobhan on you. She\u2019s very good at stalking people, apparently, and when she catches them, she\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c<u><u>What?</u>\u201d </u> I asked again.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe eats their eyes,\u201d D finished quietly.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a good thing I didn\u2019t have a drink, or nothing would have stopped me from spitting that time. \u201cEww,\u201d I said instead.<br /> <br /> \u201cI know, right?\u201d D replied.<br /> <br /> I hastened to give Calamity this new information, and she called Becky again, so it\u2019s a good bet the monarchs knew about it shortly thereafter. Calamity seemed certain that they\u2019d assign someone to watch Siobhan carefully\u2026 someone like Molly. That made me feel a bit better about the situation.<br /> <br /> I mean, seriously, who sends the fucking Corinthian as a peace ambassador?<br /> <br /> Anyway, things wound down after that, and people began to pair off as the crowds dwindled. D and I ended up inviting Julia to share our bed last night, and nobody had any complaints about those arrangements. D got up first to head to therapy with Jacob and Calamity, with me rising second to train with them when they got back. Julia remained luxuriating in our bed until Sex Breakfast was on the table (I made pancakes).<br /> <br /> Turns out that Hannah had spent the night with Calamity, and she joined us for the now-famous Sex Breakfast\u2026 though she may have been a bit disappointed, as the banter seemed unusually tame compared to our typical conversations. We started talking about Europe (and Marguerite\u2019s impending trip there), which led to one of the strangest discussions of Lichtenstein the world has ever known. Julia mentioned that when she was younger, she had thought Lichtenstein was ruled by a lich, and how disappointed she was when she found out that this wasn\u2019t so. I opined that this would be counter to the laws of nature, and Julia said that she scoffed at such laws, and insouciantly asked if I was going to call the Nature Cops on her. After a bit more discussion, we decided that if the Nature Cops do exist, Luna would be their official representative to the Malibu-Santa Monica area.<br /> <br /> Like I said: weird.<br /> <br /> After our guests had left for the day, we received another unexpected visitor. Boss Lowjack swung by the Dream House with Gloria and Tamara in tow. He wanted to debrief us on Siobhan and share information. The Hollywood emissary met with Princess Jolie this morning, and the meeting seemed to go well. Based on information Gloria volunteered, it seems like Siobhan might even be on the level\u2026 she\u2019s well-liked enough to be good at the ambassadorial gig, but not well-connected enough to get out of it. Nobody had yet read her desires or fears or anything (I kicked myself at that; if only I\u2019d thought to do that when we met the previous night!), but she doesn\u2019t seem to be consciously hiding anything.<br /> <br /> Of course, with Hollywood that doesn\u2019t necessarily mean anything. She\u2019s probably got hidden programming somewhere in that attractive blonde head of hers. Hell, it seems like they program just about <u><u>everyone</u></u> in that Freehold, even people they have no intention of sending to the Lady by the Sea, like Gloria. And even if she<u> <u>is</u></u> exactly what she seems to be\u2026 well, Hollywood will still have a spy and a contact within our Freehold now. As Calamity pointed out, even normal legitimate ambassadors are essentially spies when you get right down to it. And if Siobhan sets up shop here permanently, then Hollywood will have a foothold, or a beachhead, or\u2026 some other vaguely anatomical metaphor meaning a way to get inside our defenses.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m worried about this, but I don\u2019t think there\u2019s any way we can stop it. Denying Siobhan the right to settle here as an open ambassador would be seen as an insult, and acting preemptively to stop her from hurting anyone would be tantamount to an act of war. Never mind the fact that they\u2019ve sent spies, assassins, and monsters against us repeatedly\u2026 this time it looks like they\u2019re trying to establish legitimate political relations with us, and the Lady by the Sea <u><u>won\u2019t</u></u> be the first party to act aggressively in this situation.<br /> <br /> Oh, one other thing I should probably mention. One of Lowjack\u2019s spies (probably Molly, I guess) went through Siobhan\u2019s room carefully to make sure she wasn\u2019t bringing weapons or other dangerous contraband into the Freehold. She didn\u2019t find anything overtly hazardous, but she <u><u>did</u></u> find several suspicious vials of fluid. A sample was taken and given to Oleander, who determined that it was sugar water laced with a highly addictive chemical developed by the CIA for interrogations. The chemical has no other adverse effects, but the physical and mental dependency becomes almost insurmountable after only a few doses, at which point the addict will do almost anything to get another hit.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s possible that Siobhan intends to use this on someone in the Freehold to coerce their cooperation with whatever nefarious scheme she might have in mind. Lowjack warned us all to be cautious, and told us that if we suddenly felt a strong desire for more of whatever we were eating or drinking we should report to the Winter Court clinic for detox. One dose should only result in a few days\u2019 worth of headaches. But it seems more likely that Siobhan <u>herself</u> is hooked on the stuff, and the Court of Fallen Stars is using it to ensure her loyalty. If so, they\u2019ve got her on a very short leash, and we\u2019ll need to watch her even more closely. Oleander\u2019s trying to synthesize something that will help the drug\u2019s victims, but it\u2019s a slow process and she can\u2019t promise anything yet.<br /> <br /> So post-breakfast conversation was a bit heavy, to say the least. When Lowjack and Tamara took their leave, Gloria opted to stay to spend time with the motley. She asked how I was doing at one point, and I replied with what has become my standard answer to that question of late, that I was \u201ctense and frantic.\u201d She asked if there was anything she could do to help, and seemed genuinely concerned. When I replied that I just had to work through it, she suggested that I might enjoy a back massage, and said with some pride that she was pretty good at them.<br /> <br /> I glanced at D, who nodded and urged me to take her up on her offer. \u201cYou won\u2019t be sorry,\u201d she said with a smirk.<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay,\u201d I said, \u201cyou\u2019re on.\u201d And then something else occurred to me. \u201cActually, there is something else you might be able to help me with, if you don\u2019t mind,\u201d I said.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat is it?\u201d Gloria asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, I don\u2019t want to put you out, but if you\u2019re not doing anything tomorrow afternoon I could really use some help setting up for Julia\u2019s bachelorette party,\u201d I admitted. The bride-to-be herself had promised to make herself scarce during the preparations so as not to ruin the surprise, and D and Marguerite were going to be off in Paris. I tend to plan big, so I could use every extra set of hands I could get. Particularly strong Summer Court hands like Gloria\u2019s.<br /> <br /> She was happy to offer her assistance once she understood what I was asking, and made arrangements to stop by the Dream House around one o\u2019clock. Then she, D and I retired to my bedroom. I slipped my robe off my shoulders (a simple act which is always somewhat complicated by my wings) and asked where she wanted me. She gave me an appreciative glance \u2013 nothing overtly sexual, just acknowledging my body as aesthetically pleasing, I think \u2013 and then nodded toward the bed. I lay down on my stomach, and she got to work.<br /> <br /> Oh my God that woman has magical hands. I mean, I don\u2019t have a whole lot of experience with giving or receiving massages, but I\u2019d imagine that she\u2019s at least of professional caliber. Everything... the weddings, the parties, the tests, the show, it all seemed to melt away while I lay there quietly humming and moaning to myself as she worked out all of the kinks. She stayed with me for about an hour, after which time I think I could have fallen asleep if I wanted to. I was so relaxed that my body felt like a thick liquid, and when I stood up to thank her, my legs were a little unsteady.<br /> <br /> D is a lucky woman. I shared this opinion once Gloria had taken her leave, and D confided in me that Gloria had shared the same opinion regarding me (err\u2026 that D is a lucky woman because she has me as a girlfriend, that is). I arched an eyebrow at this, and D kind of rolled her eyes and then began to elaborate. Gloria appreciates that I am a beautiful woman (blush), but she is more sexually attracted to women who are more aggressive and \u201cmasculine.\u201d Still and all, she\u2019s said privately to D on more than one occasion that she might sleep with me \u201cif she was drunk enough.\u201d<br /> <br /> I let the conversation drop after that. I mean, it bears thinking about\u2026 as I\u2019ve said before, Gloria\u2019s very attractive and a super-nice girl to boot, and I\u2019d be lying if I said I\u2019d never considered the possibilities. But she\u2019s a friend, and I don\u2019t want to screw up that friendship for a night of unbridled passion. And she\u2019s D\u2019s girlfriend\u2026 the only one of D\u2019s girlfriends who is not also <u><u>my</u></u> girlfriend. I don\u2019t know if that\u2019s important to my love or not, but if it is, I don\u2019t want to take it away from her. So I guess my motto in this situation will be \u201cproceed with caution.\u201d<br /> <br /> The show is only a couple of hours away, and it\u2019s our last show for the next few days (we\u2019ve closed the venue over the weekend for a couple of \u201cprivate functions,\u201d namely the bachelorette party and the reception), so I suppose I\u2019d better prepare to give it my all. Not that I don\u2019t <u><u>always</u></u> give it my all, but you know what I mean. Plus, if I focus really-extra-super-hard on tonight\u2019s show, then I don\u2019t have to think about\u2026 other things.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> Thursday, June 4<sup>th</sup><br /> Nine years, eighteen days<br /> Days without stabbing: 20<br /> <br /> So The Court of Fallen Stars has sent us a new monster, this one apparently likes to eat eyes. Oh, and the twist is that she\u2019s here as an \u201cambassador\u201d since they apparently figured out that we have official envoys from The Court of Dragons and the Night and Day courts of LA. Which does mean there is no diplomatic way to turn her away but really at this point why are we even pretending to be diplomatic? I mean, they sent the gorram mindfucker and it was only by dumb luck that no one fucking died. Personally, I think we should send their envoy back to them in a box\u2026 (better yet, just her eyes\u2026)<br /> <br /> Though to be fair (yeah, I know, foreign territory for this little monster) Siobhan is pretty and well mannered enough. And according to Gloria (who also cued us in on her role as official eye eater for the Spring Court) she\u2019s important enough to speak for them but not important enough to get out of this gig. So, technically expendable enough that she won\u2019t be missed if we murder the fuck out of her for what her Freehold has done. And not honestly in a position to be the one calling the shots. Also, almost assuredly under programming and addicted to some CIA developed super addictive drug that serves no purpose besides addicting you and making you suffer terrible withdrawal. So\u2026 yeah more of a victim of their fuckery than one deserving to be harmed. Which means we\u2019ve got a monkey-fighting spy here in our Monday to Friday freehold. Upside, apparently Tommy\u2019s enough of a nuisance for them to risk sending her to her death to try to convince us to recall him.<br /> <br /> So yeah, not a problem that can be solved with stabbing. However, Oleander is working to see if she can duplicate the drug so perhaps it is a problem that can be solved with hugs and friendship. Wouldn\u2019t THAT learn them for sending her? Okay, sarcasm aside, if our theories are correct she does deserve to be freed from their control (not to mention that I wouldn\u2019t exactly mind giving her some special hugs) so this plan does have merit. The ones that do deserve it are, yet again, out of reach. Seriously, the monarchs of Hollywood really need to die the slowest and most painful of deaths.<br /> <br /> But it\u2019s all out of my bloody little hands at this point anyway. She showed up here last night to get a feel for the freehold and we let the powers that be know. Today she\u2019s at Glamour Springs playing diplomat. Unless she directly harms me or mine I\u2019m not going to do anything to her without word from Lowjack or Charlotte and if it does come to murder I suspect someone else will get to have all the fun. Dahlia or Hannah most likely.<br /> <br /> And speaking of Hannah, apparently she was under the impression that I only enjoyed sex with women that submitted. Which\u2026 makes me wonder what she thinks about my thing with Beautiful. Though I suppose it\u2019s not exactly a secret how Becky\u2019s wired so she wouldn\u2019t have to be into it the rest of the time. Still\u2026 It bears looking into. I won\u2019t have anyone thinking ill of my dragon because she\u2019s with me.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, it was a very carnally satisfying night. Hannah is quite talented with her hands and after some of the things she did with Contracts of Animation I may have to talk to Andromeda about learning that myself. We might dally again at some point since we both found the experience deeply (and frequently) satisfying. However, I fear the comradery of sex breakfast may have been a little lost on little miss murder. At any rate, I should make her a dream at some point. And Dahlia has made it clear she certainly would not object to me making her another one. Pity the two of them don\u2019t hit it off better, I bet the three of us could really paint the town red if we had a girl\u2019s night out.<br /> <br /> Ah well, I suspect it\u2019s for the best that\u2019s unlikely to ever happen. And I do have Julia\u2019s bachelorette party tomorrow, which I doubt will be overly bacchanalian (despite rumors of Dark Kimberly jumping out a cake again.) Alas, I don\u2019t foresee myself getting to lick icing off her this time either. Another thing that is most likely for the best. Maybe I should speak to Annika about sharing her pet\u2026 or perhaps it would be better if I didn\u2019t. She might say yes.<br /> <br /> And then this weekend is the kickoff to wedding week. I\u2019ll be glad when it\u2019s over. I love my motley mates and I am pleased that the quad is so stupidly in love and I want them to be happy but this whole thing is making everyone even crazier than usual and the combination of saccharine lovey dovey with hair pulling stress (often simultaneously) is wearing my ass out. That and people keep dropping hints about Becky and I. I mean, yeah, we\u2019re in a relationship. We are, I suppose, girlfriends. It is most certainly about more than just sex. There are very real and very complicated feels tangled up in it like a ball of yard that\u2019s been molested by kittens. But we don\u2019t have to host a grand parade and pageant to prove to anyone how we feel about each other do we? I mean\u2026 unless we wanted to do it because we wanted to and not because it\u2019s expected of us. And fuck, but yeah every now and then I remember how much this whole madness used to be like one of my ultimate dreams. But I also used to have an obsession with sunrises and Lisa Frank stationary.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know. I don\u2019t even know that Becky would want to be tied down like that. I mean she seemed ready enough to let go when I was spiraling down after Gawain left. I love her, I do. But I look at Lori and D or Marguerite and Julia and I can\u2019t help but think of how lost and devastated they\u2019d be without the other. It scares me to think of being as lost and broken as I felt when he left again. And it scares me to know that there are people that could devastate me like that. And it scares me that I spent so much time alone that I\u2019d rather risk going through that hell again that than go back to it. And that makes me wonder if I\u2019m as in love with Becky as I think or if maybe I\u2019m just so fucking terrified of being alone or so in love with the idea of not being alone.<br /> <br /> Fuck, too much thinking. I need to shake this off and get ready for tonight\u2019s show. Hell, maybe rabid dingoes will attack or something and let me just forget about everything for a few glorious minutes. Maybe that\u2019s my whole problem. It\u2019s been way too fucking long since I had a real fight. I seriously need to bleed or draw blood.<br /> <br /> But not at the wedding. I will NOT fuck up the wedding.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal. </b><br /> <br /> It\u2019s been a few weeks of the same old stuff, but tonight things got interesting again. The night started out like usual. Hailey and Molly were at the bar with me and Luna. We were people watching and noticed Lori talking to Andromeda and Joan. Especially Andromeda interacting with Lori. They were being really cute. Andromeda nipped Lori on the nose and Hailey got all fed up. She was tired of Andromeda being the accepted one. She was saying that everyone liked Andromeda and shunned her, even though it was Andromeda that abused Hailey in Arcadia. Hailey said that what Andromeda did to her was actually worse than what her Keeper did to her while she was there. I wasn\u2019t exactly sure what to say to her. She wasn\u2019t wrong. There are a good number of people in the Freehold that treat Hailey worse than they do Andromeda. I tried to reassure her that she had friends and to focus on that. She couldn\u2019t change what was going on with Andromeda, but she could pay more attention to the positive things in her own life rather than focusing on what she was missing. I don\u2019t know how much I got through to her with that, but her complaints petered out after a little bit. I think she was internalizing her griping after that, but I tried to do what I could for her. She has been a regular at the bar for a while now and we\u2019ve talked on many occasions. She\u2019s not a bad person, and I want her to see that. I guess we\u2019ll see what the future brings. Maybe she took my words to heart.<br /> <br /> After all of that is when things got more interesting. Calamity came over to the bar and said that she needed to talk to me. So, we went to the end of the bar with Luna and she explained what was going on. Apparently, there is a new person in town from Hollywood. Her name is Siobhan and from a glance I could tell that she\u2019s a snowskin and possibly a beast. She had twitchy head movements, like a bird. In any case, she is apparently here to act as an ambassador of peace. She wants to make sure that we are on the same page as Hollywood is about keeping up the peace that we have. Or supposedly have. They have sent a number of critters our way trying to fuck with people\u2019s heads or dreams. The Hedge beast they sent did some serious damage to Desiree and led to another person getting poisoned. Those don\u2019t seem like the acts of a group that wants peace with us. Our assumption is that she\u2019s here to spy on us. Gloria also knew something about Siobhan. She said that Siobhan is an enforcer of sorts for the Spring Court. If anyone truly angers the Court she stalks after them and then cuts out their eyes and eats them. Yeah, that\u2019s messed up. Then that poor shmuck has to get back into the Spring Court\u2019s good graces again to get their eyes healed. Talk about a twisted arrangement.<br /> Tommy and Vik have been in Hollywood for a while now and we\u2019re pretty sure that they know about Tommy. I think he\u2019s been doing little things here and there to mess with them, but nothing on the level of what they\u2019ve done to us. I don\u2019t believe that they know about Vik. He\u2019s good at being unnoticed when he wants to. Hopefully Vik can get us some valuable information on the Hollywood Freehold. He\u2019s our own spy over there. Tommy is as well, but they are aware of him so he can only get so much accurate intel. I\u2019m aware that it\u2019s a pot and kettle situation. We are kind of annoyed that they sent a spy into our Freehold, fulling knowing that we have our own spy in theirs. To be fair though, they started messing with us before Vik and Tommy were sent. I think they realize how close we are to taking the fight to them and they\u2019re trying to get on our good side now and make peace. If things escalate I don\u2019t know who will come out the better for it. I expressed my concern that Hollywood might try something while we were gone, but Luna pointed out that the Freehold is hardly vulnerable without us. That and Madame Spidertoes has apparently been in a \u201cmood\u201d lately. If Hollywood tries anything and Madame Spidertoes retaliates I almost feel bad for the attackers. Almost.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Therapy came and went. Sullivan expressed concern once again about me going back to Arcadia. I mentioned it a little while ago, since I\u2019ll be missing who knows how many sessions while we\u2019re gone. He didn\u2019t seem to think that it would be healthy for me to go back to the place that messed me up in the first place. He knows why we\u2019re going and where. It\u2019s not like I\u2019m going back to the Lady\u2019s realm or anything. I\u2019m not saying that it won\u2019t be dangerous, but we need to get Lori\u2019s friends out of there. Hopefully they won\u2019t be too far gone. Arcadia can take its toll on your mind. It changes the way you think and not necessarily for the better. Some people get used to the confinement and accept it. They don\u2019t know how to function as a free person any more. Desiree had that problem to some extent after she got back. She needed to have a \u201cmaster\u201d until she could find a better, healthier, way to deal with freedom. Hopefully Missy and Jane will be able to accept their freedom and find a better life in \u2018the world.\u2019 I think Lori is hoping that they might decide to stay in the Freehold. I have no idea if they\u2019ll want to stay or go back to their home. We don\u2019t know if they\u2019ll be able to go home. I should probably mention that to Lori. She can do a search for Missy and Jane in \u2018the world\u2019 and figure out if they have fetches and if so where they are. It might be good to have that knowledge before we get them back so we\u2019ll be able to answer the inevitable questions that they\u2019re going to have.<br /> <br /> After that was breakfast. We had Hannah and White Maria there as guests. Hannah stayed with Calamity and I\u2019m not sure who Maria stayed with. Hannah was a bit of a surprise, but I think she is fascinating to Calamity so it was only a matter of time before they hooked up. Lori made pancakes for everyone and I made the coffee. From there things got silly. There was talk of Canada, Belgium and Lichtenstein. Julia apparently as a child thought that a Lich ruled Lichtenstein. Like I said, silly. Then we got to talking about Nature\u2019s laws and if there are Nature cops to enforce those laws. We kind of came to the conclusion that Luna is something of a Nature cop. She keeps the forests around here free of poachers and safe to travel in.<br /> <br /> A little while after our guests left Lowjack gave me a call and said that he was going to swing by with Tamara and Gloria for an update on certain things. I said that was fine and informed the group what was going on. When he arrived we all convened in the common room and got to talking. Last night Molly was sent to follow and investigate Siobhan. This is what she found out. Siobhan had a small pistol, possibly a garter or ankle pistol, and several small bottles of and unknown liquid. Molly took a sample and it was sent to Oleander to analyze. Her investigation also turned up that Siobhan is connected to dangerous people in Hollywood, but is not too highly placed. She has enough reputation and power to be sent as an envoy, but isn\u2019t so high up on their totem pole that she would be overly missed if she didn\u2019t come back. They took a risk sending an ambassador to our Freehold and they know that. Unless she tries something she\u2019s safe, but Hollywood might not know that. We know that they are a little more morally flexible than we are here, and will dip to do things that we won\u2019t. Or at least, what we haven\u2019t yet. If they push us too far I\u2019m not sure how the Monarchs will react. There were also concerns about Siobhan having programming of some sort, like the other ones, or even an incubus hidden in her dreams to pass along. I think the Monarchs are going to have Soon Hee take a look and see how sane Siobhan is while we can utilize her powers to do so.<br /> <br /> Lowjack suspects that Hollywood sent Siobhan to go about having Tommy removed from their Freehold. He has been making trouble for them every time they do something to us and is hiding in an inconvenient place for them to go looking for him. The pipes under the city. He is protected by steam and hot water pipes that can keep people away from him.<br /> <br /> While we were talking Oleander called Tamara with an update on what that liquid was in Siobhan\u2019s room. It turns out that it is sugar water laced with a special chemical. I can\u2019t pronounce the name let alone spell it, but it is highly addictive. Its sole purpose in existing is to physically and psychologically addict people to it. It is likely that this is the leash that they are using on Siobhan to keep her loyal to them and doing what they want her to do. Makes me wonder what kinds of things they are going to ask her to do if they need that kind of leverage over her. This substance is also not lethal, so Siobhan shouldn\u2019t be harmed by it unless she stops taking it. Then she\u2019ll go through a withdrawal that just sounds unpleasant.<br /> <br /> After Lowjack left Gloria mentioned that Siobhan used to be friends with Desiree in the past and that she might be interested in checking up on her old friend while she\u2019s in town. We don\u2019t know for certain if Siobhan has plans along those lines or not, but I can tell you without asking that she won\u2019t see Desiree. They won\u2019t let her. Desiree is on shaky enough ground as it is. She doesn\u2019t need someone from her past making an entrance just now. With all this talk about Hollywood we all agreed that we were happy that none of us ended up in the Court of Fallen Stars. I\u2019m not sure how the others chose this Freehold, or if they just came out of the Hedge near here. I followed the trail that led me to my sister, so I was going to end up here regardless. I am happy that Elena chose to go to school here though. I\u2019m not certain that a place like Hollywood would have been good for my darker impulses. I\u2019m fairly certain that if I hadn\u2019t found such good friends and s supportive environment I might have gone back to Arcadia with Rook or used my skills for the wrong sorts of activities. I\u2019m not perfect now, I know that. I\u2019m far from it, but I\u2019m a better person now than I used to be. I was cold and manipulative when I was Rime. As I\u2019ve mentioned many times I do miss certain aspects of my life as Rime, but now that my conscience has been thawed out I remember what is right and wrong. I try to do the right thing, but I know I fall short more often than I should. I guess I\u2019m still morally grey but at least I\u2019m not as bad as I used to be. So, in all finding my self in the Lady by the Sea freehold has been a good thing for me. Diane gave me a nudge in the right direction and my friends have helped me in continuing that path here.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CI</i><br /> <br /> Session was fun. Siobhan is a Beast, and eats eyes directly without cutting them out.<br /> <br /> Couple comments came up not recorded I wanted to record.<br /> <br /> When the eye eating of Siobhan came up, Julia responded with \u201cHow Unreasonable.\u201d Off the cuff and I thought it was funny.<br /> <br /> Hannah was telling a story when Calamity arrived. She was talking about rather than killing a guy, she put a grenade in his girlfriend\u2019s mouth and rigged it so the boyfriend opening the door set it off. Hence Calamity hugging her and offering to be picked up by her. Calamity is a bit messed up.<br /> <br /> White Maria stayed with Insincere Marguerite.<br /> <br /> Bachelorette parties next time. Then we have a wedding. See you then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T22:55:26-08:00","id":1185026,"title":"","content":"Quick note, no Bachelorette party. There was an exciting show (with new record roll) and then a whole crazy love drama and we did not get to them. They will start the next one. Still a fun session I look forward to sharing in two weeks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T06:22:55-08:00","id":1185132,"title":"","content":"Um. Wow. Hannah's story is incredibly messed up. Can you say guilt by association and ludicrous gibs? I mean, that's some supervillain/Hostel-level shit right there (disclaimer: have never seen Hostel). Also, had to look back to see who Hannah was. Says a lot about Changeling paranoia and the tone of this campaign that I could totally forget about someone trying to kill another person and getting off scot-free (not complaining, just commenting, it honestly just might be my memory). Speaking of moral high ground, I feel like it's only due to <br /> <br /> Question time: Anything going on with our kawaii ditzy catgirl that just isn't coming up? And speaking of her, is her really buying into the story of her Durance reflected in a lower Clarity level?<br /> What's your plan if a PC dies or is captured in Arcadia? Will the player take over an NPC (considering there's now an unusual amount of NPCs in the motley) or have to roll up a new character? What exactly is Tommy doing in Hollywood? Mechanical sabotage? Stealing shit? Targeted Leg-breaking? Mooching on their glamour sources?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T16:29:32-08:00","id":1185768,"title":"","content":"Hannah is pretty much a sociopath. She is intended to be scary. One recurring theme in MDH is there are people on this side of Arcadia that are scarier/more twisted/more evil than the loyalists are. (though not the Gentry, that would go against the grain a bit). Hannah is part of that scheme. Most of the Lady by the Sea members are good people. Some of them (for instance, Hannah, Lucian, Darke, Bright) are not without being Loyalists and more evil than any loyalist who has appeared, and others are not outright evil but capable of horrors because they feel they do what must be done (Joan, Lowjack, Dahlia, Oleander) and sometimes err on the side of violence. An then there are a few almost indistinguishable from Gentry themselves (Spidertoes, Tommy Rawhead) but are fairly benign to the local fey.<br /> <br /> Carla should be coming back up soon, but probably when things resume post Arcadia trip. Part of the reason I had the time jump was I am trying to get to and through the weddings, honeymoon, and Arcadia so that can be done and we can sit down and get really entrenched in a lot of interesting things forming a tapestry of events again. So probably not much from Carla short term, but will happen.<br /> <br /> My off the cuff answer is I am hoping no one dies or is trapped in Arcadia. My longer answer is that would be something to discuss with the player. I do generally keep an ongoing plan for how to deal with Calamity dying, not because I want her to (I don't) but given her aggression and reckless fighting style the only reason she is alive is combat is so rare. Her player has back up characters.<br /> <br /> Tommy came up in conversation Sunday night OOC, I will paraphrase<br /> <br /> &quot;The trainer of the hedge beast is dead, by the way. He got dragged into a storm drain, and was not seen again till several hours later he was ejected in bloody chunks from the backfiring toilet of one of the monarchs. The position for hedge beast trainer has not been refilled.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T16:40:57-08:00","id":1185770,"title":"","content":"Ok, so terrorist campaign on an already unstable Freehold. This will only lead to good things for our heroes and the local mortals. *munches popcorn expectantly behind a padlocked cold iron door with a plate-glass window, with iron sword at the ready*<br /> <br /> Once again, not complaining, as this is the Chronicles of <i>Darkness</i>, but Lorelei is really deluding herself if she thinks her Freehold has its hands clean. Though at least they're trying to clean up their act lately on the &quot;brainwashing and coercion&quot; thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 02-13-2018, 07:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T16:21:15-08:00","id":1186117,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7920_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7920\" data-vbnamecard=\"7920\">Master Aquatosic</a> - You're not wrong. Lori was not privy to the specifics of Tommy's activities in Hollywood, and to an extent that's deliberate on her part. Despite her own protestations, she's not <i>stupid</i>... she just prefers not to think about certain things. As a case in point, deep down inside she <i>knows</i> that Calamity killed someone for Lucian Torrez recently, but if she doesn't confirm it by asking, then she can pretend it never happened. She is fairly naive when it comes to power-plays of this sort, and is honestly happier that way. I suspect that if she ever actually pursues the Spring Crown, she's in for something of a rude awakening when it comes to how the Freehold actually runs... and may soon come to understand why Jolie is so desperate to get rid of the title!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T12:55:03-08:00","id":1189446,"title":"","content":"So I lied about the bachelorette party, sorry., Some drama (IC) and we did not get to the party. Still, should be fun. Enjoy!<br /> <br /> <i>Session CII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Figured I\u2019d update my journal while I have a few precious moments to myself; the preparations are in place and the party\u2019s not set to start for another hour or so. I doubt I\u2019ll have much free time over the next few days, so I thought I\u2019d better get my thoughts down while I have the chance.<br /> <br /> The first thing I want to mention is last night\u2019s show. It was our final show of the weekend, as we\u2019ve closed the Dream House for the bachelorette party and the reception, so I thought I\u2019d give the people something special. I had two acts last night. The first was sort of a treat for our regular customers; a sequel to the Robert Palmer number I\u2019d done the previous evening. I put on the same dress and did my hair and makeup the same way, and belted my way through \u201cSimply Irresistible.\u201d I don\u2019t think it went over quite as well as I had hoped it would, but it still got my standard ovation, so I\u2019ll chalk it up as a success overall.<br /> <br /> The second number though\u2026 that was something special. We saved it for the final number of the evening, and it ended up being the proverbial show-stopper. Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne (wearing a t-shirt with a reproduction of one of Julia\u2019s posters of me on the front) broke out her guitar, and the two of us shouted our way through Meat Loaf\u2019s \u201cParadise by the Dashboard Light.\u201d It was an <u><u>enormous</u></u> amount of fun to sing, and each of us did everything we could to support the other. I took the traditionally male role in the song, and Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne \u2013 still providing guitar accompaniment \u2013 came in at the end to cover the female vocals. You should have heard the audience go wild when she stepped forward in her own spotlight and scream out \u201cstop right there!\u201d I think the changelings in the audience were a little amused that our resident one-night ladykiller was taking on the role of the person who wanted a commitment, but she really sold it.<br /> <br /> I think I can say without hyperbole that this was the most successful number I\u2019ve ever performed. It certainly got the best response from the audience, and I was happily thanking people for their congratulations for the rest of the evening.<br /> <br /> We had a pretty good turnout. Rowan and Neon were there for their second date, and once again Veronica was acting as a chaperone, looking bored and vaguely uncomfortable with the whole situation. I briefly considered offering to share the evening with her\u2026 but Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne made a beeline for her as soon as we left the stage, and I really wanted to stay with D again last night, as we\u2019d decided to emulate Marguerite and Julia and not sleep together for the week before our wedding. So after saying a quick hello to the three of them, I moved on.<br /> <br /> I had noticed Oleander, Gloria, and Yvette sitting together at a table on the balcony, and I was intrigued, so I headed over that way. Oleander promptly offered me a seat next to her\u2026 which I ignored in favor of plopping myself sideways in her lap (she didn\u2019t seem to mind). After a nice kiss hello, I asked how everyone was doing, implying if not stating my curiosity about the unusual gathering of girlfriends.<br /> <br /> The truth of the matter surprised and touched me. The three of them have formed a sort of mutual support network for when the motley ventures into the Hedge later this month. I\u2019ve been so focused on how it\u2019s going to affect <u><u>us</u></u> that I hadn\u2019t really considered how difficult it will be for those we\u2019re leaving behind\u2026 the ones who care about us. I started to tear up a little, but I think I kept it in check.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m hoping that we\u2019ll only be gone a couple of weeks,\u201d I said softly. \u201cThe plan is to get in and out as quickly as we possibly can.\u201d<br /> <br /> Oleander smiled grimly. \u201cYou know that\u2019s probably not an option, right Angel?\u201d she asked quietly. \u201cI know where you\u2019re going. Personally, I\u2019m just hoping you guys are gone for months rather than years\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I lowered my gaze. \u201cI know,\u201d I said, and let that stand for a bit. After a moment, I perked up a bit. \u201cThat reminds me\u2026 I want to ask you to do something for me if you don\u2019t mind.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnything, Angel,\u201d she said with a smile.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019d like to start my college career in the Fall semester,\u201d I explained, \u201cbut I\u2019m enough of a realist to know that it might not be possible. I don\u2019t want to have to reapply when we get back, so I\u2019ve filled out deferment papers so that I can start in Spring or next Fall if necessary. I can\u2019t think of anyone I\u2019d trust more to deliver them to the University if I\u2019m not back by the cutoff date, if you wouldn\u2019t mind.\u201d<br /> <br /> She kissed me softly with a smile. \u201cI\u2019d be happy to,\u201d she said, \u201cjust make sure you give me the papers and the dates before you leave.\u201d<br /> <br /> After that, talk turned to happier subjects. I mentioned that D and I would be eschewing each other\u2019s intimate company over the course of the next week, and gave Oleander and Gloria a wink. \u201cWe\u2019ll be counting on you two to take up the slack,\u201d I joked. They grinned and gave each other a high five.<br /> <br /> After that, I spent the rest of the evening hanging out with D. I told her about our girlfriends\u2019 support network, and she agreed that it was a great idea. \u201cI admit,\u201d she said quietly after a moment, \u201cthat I\u2019ve thought long and hard about asking Oleander to go with us. She knows more about survival in the Hedge and Arcadia than anyone else in the Freehold.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know,\u201d I replied just as softly, \u201cand I\u2019ve thought about it too. But please don\u2019t mention it to Oleander. She\u2019s too important to the Freehold for us to take her away for God knows how long, and if I asked her to come\u2026 if I even <u><u>hinted</u></u> that I wanted her to come with us\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019d drop everything,\u201d D finished my thought. \u201cYou\u2019re right, though\u2026 we can\u2019t do that with Hollywood acting up and everything else that\u2019s going on.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo,\u201d I said, changing the subject, \u201cyou\u2019re gonna spirit Marguerite away to Paris after breakfast tomorrow. Just promise me you won\u2019t lose your heart to some French girl and forget about me while you\u2019re there.\u201d<br /> <br /> D chuckled and kissed me on the forehead. \u201cNot a chance, Jules,\u201d she said with a grin, \u201cmy heart\u2019s got a one-French-girl limit, and Marguerite\u2019s already in there. I\u2019ll come back to you. I\u2019ll <u><u>always</u></u> come back to you.\u201d<br /> <br /> I was reduced to a sniffling blob for a few moments after that, and eventually excused myself to pry Marguerite and Julia apart. Apparently the last five days of abstinence (well, abstinence from each other, at least) have been taking their toll, and the two of them were all over each other after the show, making out like teenagers in a dark movie theater. I broke them up before things got too lascivious, and they ended the night with separate partners, as per their previous agreement.<br /> <br /> I had also heard that Angelica was making the rounds of the Dream House and speaking with all of the present members of the Spring Court\u2026 but she hadn\u2019t spoken with me yet. Before I left the theater for the evening, I looked for her, and discovered that she had been trapped in the gravity well of Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne and Veronica\u2019s frantic snogging (as Jimmy and Peg might say). I made my way up to them and cleared my throat significantly.<br /> <br /> After promising that I would return Angelica intact, the two of us sought a bit more privacy on the back balcony. It turns out that Angelica is going to be taking on some of Becky\u2019s duties as a sort of co-claviger, and she wanted to know what we Spring Courtiers expect from someone in that position. I told her that I didn\u2019t feel qualified to judge her martial abilities, and that I thought it was more important for the claviger to be someone who put the needs of the Court ahead of their own.<br /> <br /> She thanked me for my input and then showed me why she\u2019s being considered for the position. Her take on the Contracts of Vainglory is\u2026 unique. Apparently she filled a very specific role for the Director in Arcadia\u2026 that of an archangel. When she activates her abilities, she grows flaming wings and possesses an aura of majesty that can stop most people in their tracks <u><u>instantly</u></u>. I can certainly see how that would be useful for a claviger\u2026 she could stop fights and small riots before they even start, and give people a chance to cool down a bit.<br /> <br /> After I\u2019d repaired the hinge of my jaw so that my mouth would close again, I offered to walk her back in to the theater. \u201cMarie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne and Veronica will never forgive me if I steal you away from them tonight\u2026 but I\u2019m keeping my options open for the future if you\u2019re amenable, okay?\u201d She grinned, leaned in, and gave me a soft kiss, mischief and a hint of orange fire flickering in her eyes.<br /> <br /> I joined D at the door once again as the last few stragglers were finishing their drinks and heading out. \u201cReady to hit the sack, sweetie?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, in just a minute,\u201d she replied. Then, giving me a significant look, she continued her thought. \u201cYou know, I\u2019m really going to miss you over the next week.\u201d It would have been an incredibly sweet moment if she hadn\u2019t been addressing my boobs directly.<br /> <br /> I rolled my eyes and took her by the hand. \u201cCome on, Casanova,\u201d I said with false exasperation, \u201ctime for you to sweep me off my feet for one last night of sin before you make an honest woman of me.\u201d<br /> <br /> Afterward, as I lay in her arms, I remember asking her something in a quavering voice. \u201cMaria?\u201d I asked, nearly a whisper.<br /> <br /> \u201cHmm?\u201d she replied, clearly sleepy.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe can still do this, right? I mean, for the next week. Hold each other? Not naked, not in bed, but\u2026 we can still do this, can\u2019t we?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course, Jules,\u201d she said, a little more awake.<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay, good,\u201d I said with a little sigh, as I snuggled into the crook of her arm. \u201cI can go for a week without having sex with you if I have to, but\u2026 I don\u2019t think I could last a week without this.\u201d<br /> <br /> She pulled me in a little tighter, but her embrace was still gentle. She knows how strong she is, and she\u2019s always very careful not to hurt me. \u201cTry to stop me, Jules,\u201d she breathed into my ear, and then chased it with a kiss. \u201cIf anyone gets in my way when I want to hold you, I\u2019ll\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026punch them until candy comes out?\u201d I asked with a sleepy giggle.<br /> <br /> \u201cDamn right!\u201d she agreed.<br /> <br /> We must have fallen asleep shortly after that, because I don\u2019t remember anything else except feeling warm and safe, watching the slow rise and fall of her breasts, and feeling the sweet whisper of her breath on my forehead as I drifted off.<br /> <br /> We joined the others for Sex Breakfast as per usual this morning, though D and Marguerite were more fully dressed than usual when we came downstairs. Conversation was a little less goofy that usual too\u2026 we mostly just spoke excitedly about the upcoming bachelorette party. It was all I could do not to blurt out some of my plans and spoil the surprise. Once we\u2019d all finished eating, Julia and I kissed D and Marguerite goodbye, and they took their leave, heading through the mirrors for the City of Lights.<br /> <br /> There was a knock at the door just as we were finishing the dishes. \u201cThat\u2019ll be Gloria,\u201d I said, moving toward the entrance hall. \u201cShe\u2019s a little early.\u201d<br /> <br /> Well, turns out it <u><u>wasn\u2019t</u></u> Gloria, it was Doctor Bright. As I don\u2019t think the good Doctor has ever graced our home with his presence before (maybe once when we first opened, now that I think of it), I was more than a little curious about his presence this morning. And any fool could tell that he was upset about something. He asked to speak with Julia, so I called her into the room. Turns out that after the show last night, she paid a visit to Desiree, and as she had been all keyed up from the time she spent with Marguerite, one thing led to another. Doctor Bright explained in an annoyed voice that Desiree is still fragile, and that in his opinion she wasn\u2019t ready for the intense emotional shifts that often accompany the tender act of love. After chastising her briefly, he recommended that she contact him the next time she felt any amorous urges toward his patient.<br /> <br /> Julia made herself scarce after that so that we could get to work on prepping for her bachelorette party. A few minutes after she left, there was another knock at the door. \u201cThat\u2019s Gloria for sure,\u201d I said, and made my way toward the entrance. Strike two! Elena stood on the doorstep in an agitated state, and quickly asked to speak with her brother. The two of them headed for the relative privacy of the office while Calamity, Luna and I started unrolling and hanging the black velvet.<br /> <br /> Gloria actually <u><u>did</u></u> arrive next, but almost as soon as I let her in, Jacob came out of the office and asked if I could help Elena with something. She was in a state because last night, following a fit of drunken revelry, she and Stasia had agreed to become girlfriends and to tell their respective families about each other. As often happens following such fits of drunken revelry, she was having second thoughts in the cold light of the morning.<br /> <br /> \u201cDo you care for her?\u201d I asked, consciously avoiding the L-word.<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course I do!\u201d she replied a bit hotly. \u201cShe\u2019s the only person I\u2019ve ever\u2026 slept with. I wouldn\u2019t have done that if I didn\u2019t care for her.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut you don\u2019t want to be her girlfriend?\u201d I asked, a little confused.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo!\u201d she said, and then \u201cyes! I don\u2019t know. It\u2019s complicated. I just\u2026 I was really drunk last night, and I\u2019m not sure I\u2019m ready to take that step yet. But I don\u2019t know if I should tell her that or not. I\u2019m afraid that if I go back on it now I\u2019ll screw things up between us. I just want things to keep going like they are. I mean\u2026 she was really drunk last night too\u2026 maybe she doesn\u2019t even remember the conversation. Maybe I shouldn\u2019t bring it up at all.\u201d<br /> <br /> I had my doubts about that plan of action, and I said so in gentle terms. If Stasia and Elena are going to build something meaningful between them, they need to be honest with each other. And if they\u2019re going to be getting drunk and intimate again, it\u2019s not practical for Elena to have to keep straight what she\u2019s sharing and what she\u2019s keeping secret.<br /> <br /> I also advised her to keep the \u201cgirlfriends\u201d issue separate from the \u201ctelling their families\u201d issue. I understand that her family is pretty traditional, and that she\u2019s afraid she\u2019ll be disowned if she comes out to them. And I <u><u>really</u></u> don\u2019t want to downplay how serious that concern is, but\u2026 well, look at my own story. My dad used to be a total fire-and-brimstone type, but he\u2019s mellowed a lot over the years, and next weekend he\u2019s presiding over my wedding to a Hispanic Catholic woman. The love of one\u2019s child can be a powerful catalyst for change in the right circumstances, so you never know.<br /> <br /> In the end, I agreed to speak with Stasia when she arrived for the bachelorette party, ostensibly to see if she remembered the conversation itself and to sort of feel out her opinions of the situation, and then text Elena with whatever information I uncovered. In reality, I agreed to this plan mainly to give myself a little time to come up with a better solution. Any fool could see that those two needed to talk to each other about their relationship, but Elena at least was not mentally prepared for that meeting.<br /> <br /> So Elena left through the back door and Jacob and I rejoined the others, who were laying out the black lace tablecloths at that point. By coincidence, Calamity had just received a call from Stasia, who wanted to stop by the Dream House a little early, as she had \u201csomething important\u201d to discuss with our motley-mate. The more I thought about it, the more I realized that we needed to bring Calamity in to our little conspiracy. She\u2019s Stasia\u2019s best friend, and the sassy Ukrainian is more likely to confide in her than in either Jacob or myself. I pulled Jacob aside to mention this, and he agreed that it was the right play.<br /> <br /> So I called Calamity into the office (Gloria was starting to get pretty annoyed at all of the secret meetings by this point; Luna took it all in stride as usual) and spilled the beans. Calamity agreed that the situation needed to be handled carefully, as Stasia\u2019s past failed romances have left her a little bitter and pessimistic about romance in general. If Elena pulls back too strongly from the proposed relationship, Stasia\u2019s likely to overreact and end things entirely. After discussing our options, we decided that the best option would probably be to speak with Stasia first to prepare her for the conversation so that we can work through her initial negative reaction first and formulate a more moderate response to the actual event.<br /> <br /> I think things went pretty well all in all. Calamity and I spoke with Stasia once she arrived (in the middle of setting up the centerpieces with their dribbly black candles). Well, okay, Calamity spoke with Stasia by herself until I decided to butt in and add my two cents. What? I wasn\u2019t eavesdropping or anything\u2026 okay, in truth, I was totally eavesdropping. But goddammit there will be <u><u>no</u></u> scary relationship drama at my Julia\u2019s bachelorette party! As Maid of Honor, I saw it as my duty to ensure that her special day wasn\u2019t marred by angry, tear-filled break-ups.<br /> <br /> So yes, I joined the conversation after a while. Stasia took the initial news of Elena\u2019s cold feet just as badly as Calamity had predicted, but we were able to talk her down from her self-destructive implosion spiral. My central thesis statement in this situation was as follows.<br /> <br /> \u201cLook, Stasia, the key thing to take away from this is that neither one of you want to lose what you already have. We need to focus on that instead of on what might be coming. Tell Elena that you want to be with her no matter what, and that it doesn\u2019t matter who else knows about it or what you call it, and everything will be okay. Get ahead of her nerves and own the conversation and everything will be fine.\u201d<br /> <br /> When I contacted Elena about the situation, I told her in non-specific terms that Stasia remembered the conversation and wanted to talk with her about it, but that neither of them wanted to lose what they had. I advised her to be honest about her feelings, as a relationship based on lies and hidden doubts is less likely to stand the test of time.<br /> <br /> When the two of them got together as we were putting the finishing touches on the theater, it wasn\u2019t as contentious or dramatic as it could have been\u2026 thanks in large part, I flatter myself, to the efforts of Calamity, Jacob, and myself. The two of them are still together, and I <u><u>think</u></u> their relationship is stronger now. Stasia admitted that she wanted to be more to Elena, but she didn\u2019t insist on any particular label or timetable for their life together, and they\u2019re still considering moving in together.<br /> <br /> Wait a minute, hold the phone! Moving in together? I glanced at Jacob, and though he\u2019s ridiculously hard to read most of the time, I think this was the first he\u2019d heard of that little item too. Well, I suppose their business is none of mine at the end of the day. I\u2019ll let big brother worry about that.<br /> <br /> Now, I should probably stop writing and start getting into my dress. The party is set to start in about half an hour, and we have a few weirdos in this Freehold who habitually arrive early for every engagement. The dress I\u2019m planning to wear is fetching, but it involves putting on a corset, and I don\u2019t have D, Marguerite, or Julia to help me lace it up, which complicates matters a bit. I\u2019m really looking forward to enjoying the fruits of my labors, though. I\u2019ll write more in a day or two to record how everything went.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei Grace</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> Thursday, June 4<sup>th</sup><br /> Nine years, eighteen days<br /> Days without stabbing: 20<br /> <br /> Well that was one hell of a last show before we shut down for the wedding all weekend. The place was packed to the fire code\u2019s gills despite it being a Thursday. The show rolled along with everyone doing some really solid numbers but, of course, it was Lori\u2019s closer that blew everyone away. She and Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne put their spin on that Meatloaf classic \u2018Paradise by the Dashboard Lights\u2019 and they absolutely owned it.<br /> <br /> Roan and Neon where there for another date. They make such an adorable couple but clearly Veronica was a little frustrated playing chaperon and was dressed to impress (which apparently Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne was since she spent the evening with her as soon as the closing act was done and they left together).<br /> <br /> Angelica was there talking with White Maria. I joined them and discovered that she was asking the various Spring courtiers what they considered to be the traits of a good Clavier. I didn\u2019t catch it, but I believe White Maria\u2019s specifications were, as always, exacting. She moved away to ask the others (though I don\u2019t believe she escaped the gravity well of Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne either and left with her and Veronica)<br /> <br /> Needless to say, both White Maria and I know why Becky is considering training someone. I admitted to a little of my concern there and White Maria proceeded to lay out exactly what Becky needed out of a long term partner and even offered to advise me on whether or not things I\u2019m planning are a good idea or not. I think, honestly, she\u2019s as determined to make this work as either Beautiful or myself, which I take as a compliment since it means she feels I am worthy of Becky. (I should remind myself of that the next time I have doubts. I mean, she\u2019s a tougher critic than Mikey and the Russian judge combined.)<br /> <br /> At one point it came up that Siobhan and Leanne had met up at the Rose and Thorn and left together in high spirits. I made a (mostly) joking comment about needing to leave and make some poor life choices and White Maria firmly advised me against it, then proceeded to make an effort to distract and engage me to prevent me from running off to do anything foolhardy. It was sweet of her. You know, I would not have believed the two of us would end up being so close not that long ago. But she really is one of my closest friends.<br /> <br /> And now that everything has wound down, I\u2019m here waiting for Beautiful to be asleep so I can join her in her dreams. I\u2019m thinking I\u2019ll show up wearing something in innocent Catholic schoolgirl\u2026 I may not be a succubus but I do know what gets my favorite one\u2019s motor running.<br /> <br /> <br /> Friday, June 5<sup>th</sup><br /> Nine years, seventeen days<br /> Days without stabbing: 21<br /> <br /> Well that\u2019s a fucking bullet dodged. But it looks like Stasia and Elena will not be having an ugly blow up in the middle of Julia\u2019s bachalorette party. I\u2019d ask what I\u2019ve done to deserve this but I already know\u2026<br /> <br /> But thankfully Lori and Jacob decided not to keep Elena\u2019s tearful admission of waking up and realizing that she\u2019d been overly honest and unrealistic while drunk to themselves. So at least we\u2019re not in one of those painful British comedies of errors that are only funny if you ignore the way people\u2019s lives are falling the hell apart. And once they did tell me I knew that the only answer was an honest conversation between the pair. I also knew that Stasia was not going to react well AT ALL to Elena having second thoughts about her I don\u2019t care shout it from the rooftops we\u2019re in love position.<br /> <br /> In the end I think my approach was the right one. Stasia arrived early and I took her aside (Gloria was so not pleased with all of the skulking and plotting in the back room while she was left working on the decorations poor thing). I told her what was going on and then Lori and I talked her down from her knee jerk reactions. Once she\u2019d actually thought about it she understood all to well about how Elena had been carried away by emotion while logic was pickled by alcohol and that the return of it didn\u2019t mean her feelings weren\u2019t there just that maybe she wasn\u2019t as ready to take such a plunge without all that liquid courage. And we pointed out how devastated she was at the prospect that she\u2019d ruined things.<br /> <br /> Jacob called his sister and we let the pair of them take the back room. And yes, I did follow invisibly ready to drop a whisper in Stasia\u2019s ear if she needed. But it wasn\u2019t needed. As I thought, once she got past her initial flare of panic and self protective fleeing she understood Elena\u2019s position and was more than prepared to calm her lover and assure her that they could take things at a less all or nothing pace. I slipped away to let them actually have their privacy once it was clear we had avoided flaring emotions setting off explosive baggage and sending everyone running to lick their wounds. I mean, sure, I think they\u2019d have gotten to the place to have that honest conversation afterwards, but depending on how badly it went they might never have actually done it or it might have been a long time wasted. And yeah, it really did strike a bittersweet feeling to hear Stasia talk about not being in love like this since she was thirteen.<br /> <br /> But I\u2019m not that girl anymore. And there is\u2026 too much has happened even if I could somehow be her again. But Elena. Elena can be her princess. Elena IS her princess. And I\u2019m happy to have helped them avoid a fight that didn\u2019t need to happen.<br /> <br /> But this whole thing just makes it even more clear that I need to talk to Beautiful. She\u2019ll be here soon and she\u2019s staying till after the wedding. It\u2019s the longest we\u2019ve spent together in hell, maybe ever. But she\u2019s changing her whole life around to make that sort of thing possible in the future. A future she wants me to be a part of.<br /> <br /> I want that so much and at the same time it scares the piss out of me. I look back at all the times I wrote how I couldn\u2019t understand how Gawain could love a thing like me and how he keep saying he knew and loved me anyway\u2026 that he would always love me no matter what\u2026<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not fucking fair. She\u2019s not the one that tore my twisted little heart out but I can\u2019t stop. I can\u2019t push this fear down. I can\u2019t silence this voice in my ear that\u2019s telling me that she\u2019ll leave me the way he did. That no one can love something as sick and evil and twisted as I am. I can\u2019t stop hearing Their voices telling me how no other could want a nasty hateful girl like me.<br /> <br /> I love her so much. I just wish I wasn\u2019t so bad at it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Tonight\u2019s show was one to remember. All the ladies did really well on their acts, but Lori and Marie H\u00e9l\u00e8ne were outstanding in theirs. They did \u201cParadise by the Dashboard Light\u201d by Meat Loaf. And those two rocked it. I think it might have been Lori\u2019s best performance to date, and that\u2019s saying something. Marie H\u00e9l\u00e8ne was great and did her best to make Lori look good. I think it paid off. I know the audience sure appreciated it. Nobody was ordering drinks during that song.<br /> <br /> After their acts the ladies went around and did their usual social butterfly stuff, and talked to a lot of different people. Lori talked to Oleander, Yvette and Gloria for a little while. Lori looked like she was a combination of happy and sad at the same time. I later found out that those three ladies are starting something of a support group for all the \u201cgirlfriends\u201d while our motley is away in Arcadia. I think she thought it was a good idea. So did I. I wonder if they\u2019d be up to allowing my sister to join their little group, if she wants to that is. My motley and I are Elena\u2019s main contacts within the Changeling community here, and if she wants to get information while we\u2019re gone I\u2019m not sure how she\u2019s going to do that if she\u2019s not connected to some more people. I\u2019ll have to bring that idea up to Lori and see what she thinks.<br /> <br /> Later in the evening I got a call from an unexpected source. Flores called to say that Siobhan and Leanne were at her club and getting along really well, and that they had plans to leave and go \u201cpaint the town red.\u201d I don\u2019t really trust either of them, so I talked to Molly about it. She flat out asked me if I wanted her to go out and follow the pair to see what they got up to. I thought about it for a minute and then said yes. Like I said, I don\u2019t trust them and want to know what they\u2019re doing. I don\u2019t know if I technically have any authority to send Molly out on missions like that, but she volunteered and left quickly after our talk. Siobhan and Leanne are probably not up to anything untoward but I figured it would be better to play it safe rather than be sorry if something happened. I did not hear back from her tonight.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Today is definitely shaping up to be a more interesting day. While we were finishing up breakfast Dr. Bright came by to talk to Julia. Apparently she went to visit Desiree last night and they ended up getting intimate. Dr. Bright was upset about that because he didn\u2019t want Desiree to suffer any setbacks because of intense emotions, good or bad. He warned her to ask him before she visited Desiree for any reason next time. Julia agreed. After he left Julia, and the rest of us, said our farewells to De La Rocha and Insincere Marguerite. They were leaving to go to France for Marguerite\u2019s bachelorette party. We wished them a good time and they left through the mirror. Handy way to travel that.<br /> <br /> After our motley mates left there was another knock on the door. This time it was Elena. She was obviously upset about something and asked to speak to me privately. So, we went to the side room to talk. Turns out that she and Stasia had had a rather fun night last night. There was a lot of alcohol involved and they both got pretty drunk. Things were said though that are now giving my sister possible second thoughts. They had talked about telling friends and family about them going out, specifically about being girlfriends. That was what had Elena so upset this morning. She doesn\u2019t regret her relationship with Stasia in the least, but she doesn\u2019t know if she wants to call them girlfriends. It seems that she is mainly freaking out over the whole label. She was also unsure about how our parents would react to the announcement. So, she was upset. She wanted to talk to Stasia about things, but didn\u2019t want to hurt her friend\u2019s feelings. I advised her that above all else she should be honest with Stasia. Hiding or lying about things now would likely come back to bite her in the ass later. I wasn\u2019t sure really how to proceed besides talking to Stasia and being honest about how she felt, so I asked if Elena minded if I brought Lori in on this. She said fine and I went to get my motley mate. Lori came in and also advised Elena to be honest with Stasia. She said that she should make sure that Stasia also understood that she does not want to lose her, that she is just unsure about the label of being girlfriends. Elena said that she wasn\u2019t sure if Stasia even remembered the conversation since they were both drunk and asked me and Lori if we could ascertain whether or not Stasia remembered anything from the night before when she came over later today for the bachelorette party for Julia. We said that we would do our best and text or call her to let her know what we found out. Elena then left so she could seemingly arrive for the first time later in the afternoon.<br /> <br /> Once Elena was gone Lori asked me if I minded getting Calamity involved in this whole situation. She knows more about the relationship between Stasia and Elena than we do, and is best friends with Stasia. After I thought about it for a moment I agreed that it was a good idea. Calamity would know how to talk to Stasia about this whole thing so she didn\u2019t freak out or get overly upset or angry. So, we brought Calamity into the side room and explained the situation to her. That Elena doesn\u2019t want to lose Stasia but is afraid of labels. Elena had said that she would rather lie to Stasia than lose her. Calamity agreed to talk to Stasia, and did so a little while later when she showed up at the door. So, Stasia and Calamity talked while the rest of us decorated the Dream House for Julia\u2019s party. When voices got raised Lori went in and added her two cents to the conversation. I didn\u2019t hear much of what was said but heard enough to know that Stasia started to freak out and Calamity and Lori talked her back down. They both told Stasia that she needs to talk to Elena as soon as she arrives, and that she should be honest herself, but also listen to what Elena is saying.<br /> <br /> Once that conversation happened Lori texted Elena telling her to come by the Dream House before the party started so she could talk to Stasia. Elena arrived a short time later and went into the back room with her \u201cnot girlfriend\u201d to talk things over. I again didn\u2019t hear much of what was said. I tried not to actively listen in. Elena and Stasia deserved the privacy, so I tried my best to honor that. They came out of the room a little while later looking calm and a little red eyed. I assume that things got a little emotional for them in there. They said that they had worked things out, and even went so far as to mention in passing moving into the same apartment. So, I assumed that things went fairly well between the two of them. I am happy for them. I had my concerns about Stasia in the beginning, I\u2019ll admit that. Stasia had loudly said that she wasn\u2019t into relationships other than one-night stands and I didn\u2019t want my sister to get hurt. Now it seems that the shoe is on the other foot. Elena is the one unsure about the relationship bit and Stasia is all into it. I just want Elena to be happy. If Stasia makes her happy then I am happy. If Stasia ever does anything to intentionally hurt my sister I won\u2019t be quite so sanguine about the whole thing though. Just saying.<br /> <br /> Back in the early days when I was in Arcadia I thought about my sister a lot. I didn\u2019t know in the beginning that the Lady had sent a fetch in my place. I thought that Elena would be upset that I had been trapped in the cave. I wanted nothing more than to get back to her and my family. For a while she was my guiding light. People say that twins have a unique relationship even among siblings. I always felt that was true of us. I knew that I had to survive so I could get back to my sister. As time passed I knew that Elena would not be happy at what I had to do to get by in the Lady\u2019s realm, but I knew that I had to get back. I had to find my way home. When I entered the Lady\u2019s service she did something that made me forget about my life in \u2018the world.\u2019 I forgot about my sister and my new goal had been to please the Lady of the Winter Winds. Sometimes I feel like I have to make up for that in some way. I know realistically that it wasn\u2019t my fault that I forgot my mortal life, but the feeling still persists. I suppose that I could have moved on with my life once I made sure that Elena was okay. I could have left her to her own life. I didn\u2019t though. Once my memories came back I started missing my sister all over again and wanted nothing more than to be a part of her life in whatever way I could. In the beginning it was just as a friendly face. I have been blessed that I was able to tell her the truth and that she believed me. I have my sister back and I will do whatever I have to in order to keep her safe and happy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> It is a somewhat nerve wracking time for me a good time but rough.<br /> <br /> I get married in less than forty-eight hours to Julia Oldacre.<br /> <br /> Tonight is the bachelorette party. I return to Paris for the first time in a very long time with Maria. That is nerve wracking enough. We are going to a \u201cdyke bar.\u201d She promised not to start a fight there. I will hook up with some French girl who I do not even know. Probably.<br /> <br /> I am not having second thoughts, it is just making me very nervous and I am having trouble with holding consistency. My form is sufficiently liquid that keeping cohesion is somewhat difficult when I get really stressed about it. Frequently.<br /> <br /> Julia has suggested she and I not share a bed for seven days before the wedding. The first several days were easy. I usually slept in the vents. I like sleeping in the vents. Usually. But things have gotten somewhat difficult, and I think that I do two things to deal with stress, go into especially narrow and small places (like the vents) and sex. Narrow places are easy. With Julia not as an option I have spent a few nights elsewhere, with Maria and with Yvette. Happily.<br /> <br /> Somehow she seems to be doing fine with everything. I can\u2019t imagine how she is having an easier time of it than I. I mean do not get me wrong Julia and I indulged in some passionate kissing the other night but still slept separately. It\u2019s hard to keep my hands off of her.<br /> <br /> I guess everything is sinking in and I am freaking out and I miss Julia. I hope Juliette and Maria are handling everything okay. Maria is certainly trying to seem okay. Juliette\u2026is nervous. I think everything with my wedding and her wedding and the test, they are all weighing on her. It is bad enough two women getting married but four we are lucky we have the Malibu Dream House not Malibu Mad House.<br /> <br /> I am looking forward to this, but I will be very glad when it is all over. It\u2019s getting to me.<br /> <br /> Definitely.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CII</i><br /> <br /> So there was a lot of RP this session not much plot advancement, but it was good RP. With a handful of bonus dice from Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne Lorelei managed to hit 55 successes on her rendition of \u201cParadise\u201d that lead to a lot of celebration. The scene with Stasia and Elena was unexpectedly good, and we had a good time with it. Wound up not having time for the bachelorette party, but eh, worth it for the good scene.<br /> <br /> Next time expecting a bachelorette party and who knows maybe a wedding.<br /> <br /> So we have started a new game. Blue Rose: Cat\u2019s Cradle is a Blue Rose 2<sup>nd</sup> edition game using the AGE system. The game includes 5/6 of the players from <i>Malibu Dream House</i>, and all four of the current roster. It\u2019s my first real Fantasy game since Exalted, short a brief flirtation with the D20 Warcraft game. It\u2019s not WoD or CoD but we are having fun with it, and would love to have you join us for it. Journals and discussion can be found <a href=\"https://roninarmy.com/threads/7255-Blue-Rose-Cat-s-Cradle-(Actual-Play)\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. Hope to see you there.<br /> <br /> Regardless, glad you are here! Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 02-25-2018, 04:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T13:30:52-07:00","id":1194344,"title":"","content":"Now <i>this</i> time we have a bachelorette party and a wedding. Join the group for fun and hijinx<br /> <br /> <i>Session CIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Well, one wedding down and one to go. I suppose it\u2019s \u201cthe big one\u201d as far as I\u2019m concerned (though Marguerite and Julia\u2019s wedding was of course monumental in its own right, and I\u2019d never say anything to diminish that). I still have my test with the Pilgrims tomorrow to distract me, but I imagine most of the rest of the week will see me degenerating into a quivering pile of raw nerves as I prepare to become Mrs. Lorelei Grace de la Rocha.<br /> <br /> Julia\u2019s bachelorette party went well, I think. Everyone seemed to have a good time at least, though I\u2019m perhaps not as creative as I could be when it comes to planning fun sexy party games. Julia showed up right on cue, about twenty minutes after the rest of the guests, and made appropriately impressed remarks about the new gothic d\u00e9cor of the Dream House\u2019s theater area. And in that respect I do have to toot my own horn at least a little\u2026 everything was draped in black velvet, with black lace tablecloths and dribbly black candles on every table.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d decked myself out no less opulently, of course\u2026 in a gothic gown with flowing black and red skirts and a fair (though ecologically friendly) approximation of an actual Victorian whalebone corset cinched tightly about my waist. It wasn\u2019t the most comfortable ensemble, but it did serve to give my voice a nice breathless quality for the remainder of the evening. I topped it all off with a black lace veil.<br /> <br /> Andromeda had brought a large, multi-pipe hookah, and Julia and I both supplied a little weed, and of course Jacob had agreed to serve as bartender for all of us wild and crazy girls, so things got a little spicy pretty quickly. There was a karaoke machine\u2026 for the guests, of course. It was my night off, and Julia\u2019s voice is not for public consumption. But much of the evening was dedicated to an impromptu game of truth or dare. And just like at the game our motley played together over a year ago, we placed a minor pledge on everyone forcing them to tell the truth or to smell faintly of rotten eggs for the rest of the evening.<br /> <br /> There were too many of us for just one game, so we divided it up by tables. I found myself at a table with the bride herself, Flores, Veronica, and Yvette. I know Calamity was at a nearby table with Becky, Stasia, Elena, and White Maria. A third table contained Joan, Andromeda, Neon, Brightstar, and Rowan\u2026 and so forth. I\u2019m pretty sure a good time was had by all, with varying degrees of embarrassment and intoxication.<br /> <br /> I couldn\u2019t begin to remember all of the questions, answers, and dares that flew between us (see the previous paragraphs re: intoxication), but a few stand out. Yvette asked me what the most depraved thing I had done with Marguerite was, and just like last year\u2019s fateful truth or dare game, I was forced to admit to a particularly kinky sex act\u2026 the same one, in fact. It seems like I\u2019m destined to bring that up every time we play that particular game for one reason or another. Julia asked me an interesting question\u2026 she wanted to know who I\u2019d most like to be the \u201cfather\u201d of a child I carried, out of everyone in the Freehold, excepting those I\u2019m already in committed relationships with. That\u2019s an interesting question as far as changelings are concerned, as certain contracts mean that you can\u2019t necessarily rule out women as potential \u201cfathers.\u201d<br /> <br /> I thought about it for a while, as there are actually a lot of good candidates. Joan sprang to mind\u2026 she\u2019s stalwart, and brave, and absolutely dedicated to those she loves. She\u2019d be an amazing protector for a potential family group\u2026 but I know that sort of thing would cause tension between her and Andromeda, and even in a hypothetical situation like that I\u2019m not willing to risk what those two have together. I thought about Princess Jolie, but her duties as monarch mean that she probably wouldn\u2019t have a lot of time to devote to a potential family of that sort. And of course the off-the-cuff answer was Captain Jack \u2013 any child the two of us had together would obviously be <u><u>amazing</u></u> \u2013 but he\u2019s not interested in girls. In the end, I went with Flores\u2026 she\u2019s so kind and sunny and nurturing that I can\u2019t help but think she\u2019s going to make an excellent mother someday. She gave me a radiant smile and a slight blush as I attempted to articulate those thoughts.<br /> <br /> Flores herself asked me who out of all of my lovers past and present I would <u><u>least</u></u> like to have my father walk in on me with. That\u2019s a tough question, honestly, because for the most part those flings of which I\u2019m less than proud occurred back in Defiance before I was Taken, and those names would have meant less than nothing to the people gathered at the table. Privately, I think I\u2019d probably go with Sam Barnes, who defiled me in the vestry of Dad\u2019s old church just after he got his driver\u2019s license. Add to that the timing of when he left Defiance for good, and, well\u2026 I don\u2019t ever want Dad finding out I had sex with him, and then doing the math to work out how old I was at the time. Yeesh, I was a messed up kid.<br /> <br /> In any case, I decided that just giving the name would be meaningless, and that going into details as to why would be icky, so I opted to take a dare in the spirit of the game. Flores got an almost naughty grin on her face, then said \u201cI dare you to stand up right now, walk across the room, and give Gloria a big, deep, sensual kiss.\u201d Shit. I don\u2019t think she knew how I\u2019ve kind of fantasized about that for a while, but stopped myself out of respect for both D and Gloria\u2019s feelings. I don\u2019t think she realized that such a dare could have been harmful on a certain level\u2026 Flores would never suggest something that might cause problems. She probably just thought that she was breaking down barriers between the two of us.<br /> <br /> But a deal is a deal and a dare is a dare, so I got up, took a deep breath, and walked across the room. Gloria\u2019s table had been laughing and joking in one corner, but they all sort of fell silent as I approached. \u201cGloria,\u201d I said as I came to a halt in front of her chair, \u201cI like you and respect you, and I want you to know that I\u2019m doing this on a dare, as part of the game.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded, a little confused. \u201cOkay,\u201d she said.<br /> <br /> I leaned in and kissed her. Anyone who knows me knows that I don\u2019t do anything like that halfway, so I made it count. A few seconds in I opened my mouth, and she followed suit, and our respective tongues came into play. All told, it lasted maybe half a minute. And dammit if it wasn\u2019t a <u><u>good</u></u> kiss, too! When I pulled away, Gloria actually looked a little dazed, and gave me a faint, slight smile. \u201cWow,\u201d she said softly, and I echoed the sentiment.<br /> <br /> Maybe there\u2019s a way that the two of us could be together sometime without diminishing what she has with D? No, focus Lori. This is not the time for that sort of speculation. Besides, she ended up going home with Oleander, who was at her table for the truth or dare game.<br /> <br /> So when the time came for me to ask Flores a question, I decided to go deep and meaningful rather than embarrassing. \u201cFlores,\u201d I asked gently, \u201cyou\u2019ve been with a lot of people in this Freehold, both male and female, and we all know that you care about every one of us. But is there anyone for whom those feelings go deeper? Is there anyone who\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDare,\u201d she cut in quickly, with a somewhat panicked look in her eyes. I honestly wasn\u2019t expecting that, and I didn\u2019t have a good dare ready, so I just gave her the same dare she gave me, only with Oleander instead of Gloria. Might have been more fun a few months ago, before the two of them actually hooked up, but it was all I could think of at the time.<br /> <br /> My other dare came from Veronica, but for sort of an odd reason. The \u201ctruth\u201d question she asked me was the old classic bar game \u201cmarry-fuck-kill,\u201d with the field of options consisting of the current sitting monarchs of Malibu and L.A. At first I had Jolie as my chosen \u201cfuck\u201d option\u2026 but she\u2019s such a genuinely good person underneath it all that I quickly changed her to \u201cmarry,\u201d and put the scary-hot Charlotte in the \u201cfuck\u201d position. The problem came with \u201ckill,\u201d honestly\u2026 I don\u2019t really like the idea of killing anyone, and even though I don\u2019t know the Warlock or Leonidas well, I don\u2019t want to think that way about either of them. So after giving two-thirds of an answer, I still ended up taking the dare.<br /> <br /> Veronica thought about it in a moment, and then decided that I should walk around and spank the ass of every blonde in the room\u2026 not hard enough to hurt, but definitely hard enough that they\u2019d feel it. So no stealth-spanking. I looked up at her, giving her my best smolder, and said \u201cyou know I don\u2019t see you as a blonde, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> She shrugged. \u201cI\u2019m <u><u>not</u></u> a blonde,\u201d she said after a moment.<br /> <br /> Flores was confused. \u201cWhat? Yes you are!\u201d she said indignantly.<br /> <br /> I left the two of them to sort that out and began making the rounds. There were a lot of blondes there last night, let me tell you. Some, like Gloria, took it with good grace, laughing it off as the silliness that it was. Others, like Andromeda, played their part to the hilt, making sexy noises as the slap connected. Still others \u2013 I\u2019m looking at Rowan and Joan in particular \u2013 seemed embarrassed, but they were still good sports about it. \u201cI would not do this for anyone but you, Lori,\u201d Joan whispered from behind flaming cheeks. On her face, I mean\u2026 like I said, I didn\u2019t hit anyone hard.<br /> <br /> My question to Veronica was kind of a softball despite her spankening ways\u2026 since we share a relatively common background, I asked her to tell me about her happiest memory of life back in Iowa. She looked down at her lap for a minute. \u201cIt\u2019s kind of embarrassing,\u201d she said, \u201cand very redneck, but here goes. When I was fifteen, my brother \u2013 who was seventeen \u2013 said or did something mean to me. I don\u2019t honestly remember what it was, exactly, but that\u2019s not part of the happy memory, so it doesn\u2019t really matter, I guess. Anyway, I stole dad\u2019s keys, and I\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat?\u201d I asked, curious as to where this was going.<br /> <br /> \u201cI chased him around for nearly an hour. On a tractor.\u201d She grinned at the thought.<br /> <br /> I had to laugh at that. \u201cI love it!\u201d I said. \u201cSibling revenge courtesy of John Deere!\u201d<br /> <br /> Veronica shrugged. \u201cI feel bad about the spanking thing now\u2026 I mean, you answered most of the \u2018truth\u2019 question, and still took that dare, and you gave me an easy out instead of retaliating. I can totally take a dare to make up for it, if you want.\u201d<br /> <br /> I would have let her out of it; I\u2019m not usually the vindictive type. But at that moment, Rowan \u2013 looking about three heartbeats away from fainting with embarrassment \u2013 climbed up onto the stage and began timidly attempting to explain how heterosexual intercourse is supposed to work, using visual aids including but not limited to a vacuum cleaner and a sock monkey. I presume this was Andromeda\u2019s work. It was cute, and it was funny\u2026 but it was also obvious that Rowan was genuinely uncomfortable, and I couldn\u2019t help but feel bad for my former girlfriend.<br /> <br /> \u201cSorry about this,\u201d I muttered to Veronica. I browsed on my phone for about fifteen seconds and then handed it to her. \u201cI want you to stand up on top of the table right now and sing this song as loud as you can, please.\u201d<br /> <br /> Veronica was a good sport about it, though she looked more than a little embarrassed in her own right. Still, the spectacle of a beautiful girl standing on a table and doing a little dance while belting out \u201cThe Major-General\u2019s Song\u201d from <u><u>Pirates of Penzance</u></u> is apparently enough to distract people from almost anything. Her voice isn\u2019t bad, either\u2026 untrained, but she has some natural talent. And her familiarity with the melody and the ease with which she kept up with the patter makes me wonder if she\u2019s maybe got a little amateur musical theater in her background.<br /> <br /> After the truth or dare games wound down, I decided it was time to serve the cake. Of course, we had two\u2026 a real cake and a hollow one filled with a little surprise for Julia. This is probably the part of the bachelorette party of which I\u2019m proudest\u2026 and I thank God that Dark Kimberly was willing to be a good sport about it. That\u2019s right, when they wheeled out the comically oversized cake, Kimberly burst forth in full Lydia-from-Beetlejuice regalia, dancing slowly to the music with a typically stoic expression on her face. And yes, there was a striptease element to her performance, but in deference to the less uninhibited guests, it didn\u2019t go too far.<br /> <br /> After cake was served, we set up the sound system for karaoke, and most of the crowd tried their hand for at least one song. There weren\u2019t a whole lot of stand-out performances, honestly\u2026 but everybody seemed to have fun, which is the important thing. I do remember Andromeda doing a particularly cute and bouncy rendition of a very vulgar song I didn\u2019t know. I mostly demurred (it was my night off, after all), but I couldn\u2019t resist Oleander when she gave me those big soulful eyes, so the two of us got on stage and did our own take on \u201cIslands in the Stream.\u201d<br /> <br /> I spent most of my time, however, flirting with Yvette. Most of the rest of our little quad has already slept with her, and I was tired of being the odd girl out. She\u2019s hot, she\u2019s nice, she\u2019s French, and I wanted to spend that night with her. I checked with Julia early on in the evening, and she was fine with it, as long as I wasn\u2019t averse to her joining the two of us\u2026 which sounded like a peachy keen idea to me. <br /> <br /> Yvette herself played the coquette at first, but I could tell that she was interested. At one point late in the evening, she handed me a tube of lipstick and asked me to help her reapply it. As I\u2019m fully aware of my classic seduction techniques, I took the hint and applied the lipstick to my own lips, then kissed it on to hers. She responded enthusiastically, and that set the tone for the rest of our evening.<br /> <br /> Once everyone had left, we decided to leave the cleanup until the following morning and the three of us headed up to bed. As we all had a big day coming on Saturday, we let ourselves drift off after just a <u><u>little</u></u> bit of debauchery, and slept comfortably in each other\u2019s arms until it was time to get up for Sex Breakfast. Though not incredibly vigorous or overly prolonged, the sex was good, and I can honestly say that I went to sleep fully satisfied. The other ladies voiced no complaints, so I can only assume that they had similar experiences.<br /> <br /> I rose first, as per usual, and headed down to the kitchen to start making omelets, hoping the smell would rouse the others. D met me in the kitchen, yawned, stretched, and kissed me gently as the butter was melting in the pan. \u201cHey, sweetie,\u201d I said brightly, \u201chow was Paris?\u201d<br /> <br /> She rolled her eyes. \u201cThings\u2026 didn\u2019t exactly go as planned,\u201d she admitted.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh no,\u201d I said, my brow furrowing with concern, \u201cis everything okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah,\u201d she hastened to inform me, \u201cnothing\u2019s actually <u><u>wrong</u></u>. It\u2019s just that\u2026 well, Marguerite hooked up with these two French coeds, but I didn\u2019t meet anybody there. So we went back to the hotel, but the walls were pretty thin, and I got sick of listening to them\u2026 did you know that there are girls in France who actually say \u2018ooh la la\u2019 when they\u2019re not joking?\u201d<br /> <br /> I giggled at that. \u201cSo what did you do?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, I went out walking,\u201d she continued. \u201cAnd who do you think I should run into? Marguerite\u2019s fetch. She looks just like our Marguerite would if she ate as much as a healthy person, by the way. So, I\u2026 well, I walked up to her and punched her in the face.\u201d<br /> <br /> My eyes widened. \u201cYou didn\u2019t,\u201d I said.<br /> <br /> \u201cI did,\u201d she assured me, looking somewhat proud of herself. \u201cWhat? Her picture is on the Front National website, babe. She\u2019s a racist bitch. She had it coming.\u201d<br /> <br /> I had to admit that she had a point, so I didn\u2019t argue further with her.<br /> <br /> The two of us \u2013 and the rest of the motley, sans Marguerite and Julia \u2013 spent the rest of the afternoon making the Dream House ready for the wedding. I won\u2019t go into too many details on the ceremony itself\u2026 I can always just look at the wedding album or something if I want the memories later. But I will say that it was a <u><u>beautiful</u></u> ceremony. Dark, considering Julia\u2019s particular aesthetic, but <u><u>beautiful</u></u> nonetheless.<br /> <br /> Marguerite wore a white dress, Julia wore a black dress. There were a few trained Hedge beasts carrying parts of Julia\u2019s dress\u2026 crows bore the ribbons attached to her waist, while some sort of bipedal rat creature carried the train. I\u2019m pretty sure Oleander had something to do with this, as I occasionally caught glimpses of her in the audience blowing on a silent whistle, and this seemed to coincide with the Hedge creatures\u2019 actions in subtle ways.<br /> <br /> I sang prior to the brides\u2019 entrance, Jacob escorted Marguerite up the aisle, and Dad performed the ceremony itself. I think it might have been the first time he\u2019s seen so many of