=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T12:51:03-07:00","id":1210132,"title":"","content":"My original plan was a roll when they entered and then a chance to gain a point on success of their mission. I was, however, on day 10 of oral pain that lead to an extraction the afternoon after the game, and it slipped my mind. I wound up not requiring the rolls because it did not come up until post game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T00:49:14-07:00","id":1210326,"title":"","content":"It's great everyone managed to get in and out without dying...though granted, Calamity nearly didn't there. Thank goodness for Luna and her swift actions, and Jacob and his stealthiness.<br /> <br /> On the note of Calamity, gosh dangit Calamity, stop throwing incredibly deadly wrenches into the Baroness' plans. XD In all seriousness, she really does have a tendency to do that. We love her though, and congrats to her for solo'ing what was supposed to be a tough encounter. It probably wasn't the most dignified victory she's ever had, but points for it all the same.<br /> <br /> Interesting that nobody had to use the goblin fruit Oleander gave them. Probably for the best too, given how they were generally a last-resort sort of deal. One hopes they don't need to resort to them any time soon either.<br /> <br /> Really, the adventure was great fun to read, and a satisfying payout to the buildup that has been coming ever since the start of the series. Here's to the newcomers, and the returning rescuers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T02:16:06-07:00","id":1211720,"title":"","content":"Calamity makes everything more interesting. Her player and I also might have miscommunication when I said &quot;coming in hot&quot; She did stab, for the record, just was...unfortunate for everyone.<br /> <br /> Yeah the fruit was back up in case it went to shit. I did not particularly want them to lose, but I wanted them to win by their own merit.<br /> <br /> Thanks so much <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I think everyone was quite pleased with it. And of course, plenty of drama to come.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T01:45:44-07:00","id":1212564,"title":"","content":"So, Records don\u2019t really exist of my first changeling game, <i>Beyond the Sea</i>. A few records were done, but they were either on physical paper, make no sense without context, or were embedded peacemeal in a PDF. I have been asked about it several times. However, I managed to find a solitary journal which actually references several events in that game in a fairly amusing way. Check out a summery journal for the Motley of Illaron Highborn (Spring Fairest) Trace Eventide (Spring Darkling) Olivia Mortwight (Autumn Darkling) Mr. Bones (Winter Darkling) as told by Marian Etta, Autumn Elemental. I present it for your amusement on this off week for <i>Malibu Dream Hous</i>e.<br /> <u><br /> Intermission: Beyond the Sea</u><br /> <br /> <i>Session ????</i><br /> <br /> <b>Marian Etta\u2019s Notes</b><br /> <br /> Last night's lesson: do not anger or get the attention of an angry and extremely powerful ghost. To demonstrate this lesson, we will use Olivia. Olivia, whom was jealous of the affections and attentions given to Marney by Illaron, changed her shape into a pile of leaves and tripped Marney while she was walking. Note: this is the same Marney who is owner of the Captain's Cottage hotel and possessed by the angry and powerful ghost of her father &quot;the Captain.&quot; As a result of her actions against Marney, Olivia was visited in her bathroom by the Captain. The ghost attempted to drown Olivia, but she escaped by breaking and crawling out of the bathroom window. Also note that the Captain could have prevented Olivia from escaping through the window, yet he did not, which indicates that perhaps this was simply a warning. After all, Olivia only tripped Marney, which did not actually cause her any physical harm. But such an action has shown Olivia to be a threat to Marney's well being, hence, the &quot;warning.&quot; Third note: as proof of how powerful the Captain is, Mr. Bones found a &quot;signature&quot; (which is something only powerful spirits can leave behind) in the form of two water soaked boot prints on Olivia's bathroom floor.<br /> <br /> In contrast to Olivia's example, Mr. Bones will demonstrate how to not get the anger and attention of an angry and extremely powerful ghost. The ghost named Amelia, who has been given a huge amount of power from the evil entity sleeping under our town I call &quot;Steve,&quot; recently left the Heather House. The Heather House is an extremely deadly haunted house, with a closet full of the ghosts of children trapped inside until the ancient magic clocks inside the house chime 11:00pm. At that hour, the child ghosts will possess and kill any living being inside the house, but they return to their closet every night at the last stroke of midnight. Amelia had previously attempted to possess the entire Heather House with her power, but was not completely successful. However, Amelia did possess the windows and doors in the house, which prevented the Wyrd Sisters from having their afternoon tea parties inside. It should also be noted that Amelia is the sister of my girlfriend, Christina, who owns the Lonely Lady hotel and is the vampire guardian protecting the town from &quot;Steve.&quot; As Amelia is getting power from &quot;Steve,&quot; Mr. Bones was wise to send me to check on my girlfriend's welfare, as &quot;Steve&quot; would probably be happy if such a guardian were to come to harm. Also note that it is the middle of the day when I rush into Christina's bed chambers to check on her. Luckily, I have the power to hear ghosts if they are around me and are not attempting to be silent, which Amelia was not. Thanks to the power of new technology, I quickly text message Mr. Bones that Amelia is indeed in Christina's bedroom, and he needs to come help, as he can see ghosts who have not manifested on this side of the shroud and I cannot. I also succeed in waking up Christina from her day slumber and inform her that a ghost is in her room. As I am not Olivia or Mr. Bones, I ran from the bedroom because I choose not to deal with angry, powerful ghosts. After I leave, Mr. Bones is able to hide and witness the reunion of the sisters. Christina is able to use a vampiric power to astral-project herself from her sleeping body to talk to Amelia. To my delight and relief , Mr. Bones discovers that Amelia's will is strong enough that she is able to fight off &quot;Steve\u2019s&quot; control long enough to talk to her sister without hurting her. After leaving Christina, Amelia is later found in the secret room under the Heather House, but she was last witnessed as simply sitting in the room and is not currently causing trouble as of the writing of this diary entry.<br /> <br /> Today's lesson: Love triangles are unpleasant and should be avoided. Today's demonstration is brought to you by Olivia, Illaron, and Monica. Olivia and Monica are good friends. Monica has been one of Illaron's repeat lovers in the past, and she is rather fond of him. Olivia has recently requested that Illaron become Olivia's exclusive boyfriend and lover. Illaron has accepted Olivia's request, and as a result, Monica is unhappy. Trace, as acting Spring King, has ordered Monica to take a vacation until her emotions are under control and will not affect her job. Fortunately, Monica agreed to such an arrangement and is currently staying in my hotel for relaxation and reflection.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session ????</i><br /> <br /> Because have a horrific Abyssal Entity in the game the PCs will call it Steve.<br /> <br /> Okay well that is a glance at the <i>Beyond the Sea game</i>. Next week back to <i>Malibu Dream House</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T14:59:42-07:00","id":1215906,"title":"","content":"Our heroes are back home, adjusting to the time they have been gone. Meanwhile, their new guests try to adjust to being back home with varying results.<br /> <br /> Calamity\u2019s player was ill and unable to make so she was not present for the session.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CVII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> We\u2019ve been home for about a day and a half now, and while it would be an overstatement to say that everything is perfect, I really can\u2019t complain about recent events in my life. Missy, Jane, and Trinh each bear watching (for different reasons), but I think with time and a little patience things will start to normalize.<br /> <br /> I woke up yesterday morning surrounded by my closest lovers, and just lay there basking in their nearness, feeling their smooth skin against mine, and listening to their slow even breaths\u2026 until the rumbling of my own stomach woke Maria up. The two of us did our best not to disturb Julia and Marguerite as we rose, but by the time we were ready to descend to the kitchen, all four of us were awake and ready for breakfast.<br /> <br /> The first thing I found upon heading downstairs was a neatly printed note from Calamity. Apparently Becky has swept her off her feet and shanghaied her to an undisclosed romantic vacation spot for a few days. Well, they\u2019ve both earned it. I hope they enjoy themselves.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve sort of unofficially taken over cooking duties in recent months, though there\u2019s still a bit of trade-off here and there. As I was the first one to the kitchen this morning, I decided to try a little experiment. Kimberly\u2019s kept the fridge well-stocked in our absence, and I had no trouble preparing a traditional American breakfast for the motley and our various guests. Coffee, orange juice, toast, bacon\u2026 and eggs.<br /> <br /> I remembered my initial gut reaction to the sight and smell of cooked eggs when I first returned from Arcadia, and I thought it might serve as sort of a litmus test for how far gone our three rescued girls were. Sure enough, when they descended a short time later, Jane and Missy both sort of blanched at the thought of eating eggs\u2026 though Trinh set to with gusto.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s okay,\u201d I said softly, taking my friends\u2019 hands in my own. \u201cIt\u2019s going to take time, that\u2019s all. You\u2019re <u><u>not</u></u> birds, no matter what she tried to do to you\u2026 but nobody expects you to come back all at once.\u201d I gave them each a plate with bacon and toast, and Jacob prepared a few mugs of steaming coffee. \u201cWe\u2019ll get there together, girls\u2026 I\u2019ll help you however I can.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jane and Missy gave each other a significant look, though I didn\u2019t fully understand it until later in the day.<br /> <br /> At some point I realized that I was being a bit rude. \u201cSorry, Trinh,\u201d I said with a sigh. \u201cI don\u2019t mean to ignore you. It\u2019s just that these two have been my best friends since like 1970, and I\u2019ve spent the last two years obsessing over how to rescue them, so I\u2019m a little focused right now.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s not a problem,\u201d she assured me. \u201cI understand.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, for now, just assume that any offer I make to the two of them extends to you too, okay? Even if I don\u2019t explicitly say so.\u201d She agreed that this would work, and then turned back to the remains of her breakfast.<br /> <br /> So I was sipping my coffee and browsing through the local newsfeed on my phone when the first shoe dropped. It seems that local L.A. fashion model Trinh Jackson was at a party last night when she suffered some sort of nervous breakdown. She became extremely agitated, and rushed from the party, yelling that some nebulous person or group was after her and intended to do her harm. Looks like Trinh\u2019s fetch has sensed that she\u2019s back in the world, and is not taking it well.<br /> <br /> I asked to speak with Jacob privately, shared the news story with him, and asked if he could contact Boss Lowjack and see what the Winter Court could do to help. He agreed to do so, and a short phone call later he reported that Lowjack had assigned Molly to gather information about Trinh\u2019s fetch so that the Court could assess the situation. If the fetch can be reasoned with, we\u2019ll get the two of them together and see if it will be possible for them to co-exist, or maybe even merge. If not\u2026 well, they\u2019ll contemplate other solutions if it becomes necessary. One or the other of them may have to leave the area if they\u2019re both going to survive, though Lowjack commented that if the fetch was forced to leave L.A. it would probably mean career suicide for her. Privately, I wonder if it wouldn\u2019t be better for everyone if Trinh were to leave the area\u2026 it would get her out of Jane\u2019s jealous view.<br /> <br /> Poor Trinh doesn\u2019t seem to know what to do about this\u2026 ideally she\u2019d like to get some semblance of her life back, but she doesn\u2019t want to hurt her fetch if it can be avoided. \u201cI try to go through life without hurting anyone else,\u201d she said\u2026 which sounds like a peachy keen philosophy to me. Plus she\u2019s cute, and sexy as hell, and at least bi-curious\u2026 but I\u2019m pretty sure that if I slept with her, Jane at least would view it as a betrayal, and I\u2019m not willing to do that.<br /> <br /> I also sort of glanced at a few websites to try to catch up on everything I\u2019d missed while I was away\u2026 and I admit that I paid more attention to the pop culture world than politics. There\u2019s a new <u><u>Star Wars</u></u> movie in theaters\u2026 like the seventh in the series, I think. I had hoped that something noteworthy might have happened in the world of musical theater as well, but all I found were a bunch of references to a show about the American Revolutionary War, or something like that. Meh, whatever\u2026 not really my area of interest, but I\u2019ll probably download the music at some point anyway.<br /> <br /> So before long it was time for me to meet my Dad. D asked if she should come along with me, and of course I told her she was welcome to join me if she wanted\u2026 she\u2019s his daughter-in-law, after all, and I knew he\u2019d be happy to see her. I invited Missy and Jane to join us as well, but they demurred, stating that they weren\u2019t ready for that quite yet. I have to keep reminding myself that they don\u2019t know how much Dad has changed over the years\u2026 in their minds, he\u2019s still the stern, disapproving preacher who used to call their parents whenever the three of us got into trouble as kids.<br /> <br /> Dad was ecstatic to see us, of course. I have to keep reminding myself that it\u2019s been six months for everybody else, even if it feels like only a couple of days to me. He pulled me into a hug as soon as the door was open, and had plenty of affection left over for Maria as well. He looks\u2026 good. Like, [u]<u>really/</u>[u] good. Stronger and more robust than before. \u201cI see Oleander\u2019s visits have done you some good,\u201d I commented with a grin.<br /> <br /> He raised an eyebrow in mild confusion. \u201cOleander?\u201d he asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cImelda,\u201d I explained. \u201cIt\u2019s sort of a nickname.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAh,\u201d he said with a nod. \u201cYes, her vegetables and herbal remedies are quite remarkable. I feel better than I have in years.\u201d<br /> <br /> We talked for an hour or so about how things have been going. Of course, I gave him a basic rundown of the events of our journey \u2013 supplemented here and there by D\u2019s blow-by-blow accounts of the various fights \u2013 and he filled me in on the important events of the latter half of 2015. Natasha is still living with him, though she was out at that particular moment. She\u2019s doing well, if somewhat obviously depressed by her third-wheel status with Elena and Stasia.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s probably going to get worse before it gets better,\u201d I commented with an irrepressible grin.<br /> <br /> \u201cI am aware,\u201d Dad said. \u201cElena texted Natasha last night with the news. She went out by herself not long after.\u201d<br /> <br /> We talked about Missy and Jane for a bit. Dad has done some digging and tracked down what\u2019s left of their families. Missy\u2019s mom and dad started fighting after her fetch\u2019s death, and apparently went through a bitter and acrimonious divorce. They\u2019re both still alive, but not speaking to each other. Jane\u2019s dad started hitting the drink pretty hard around the same time, and unfortunately died of liver failure a few years later. I\u2026 find that difficult to accept. Sherriff Lassiter was always such a straight arrow back in the day\u2026 solid, dependable, and friendly. Jane\u2019s going to have a hard time with that news. At least her mom is still alive, and in relatively good health.<br /> <br /> Dad wants to meet with the girls as soon as they\u2019re ready, to do what he can to help them acclimate to the world. I warned him that it might be a few days, and he was willing to accept that as a necessity. I\u2019d really like to get the two of them talking with one of the therapists at the Clinic as quickly as possible, but I imagine they\u2019re probably closed for the holidays. Maybe I could request an emergency counseling session or something; I\u2019m sure Boss Lowjack would be willing to accommodate me if I explained the situation to him.<br /> <br /> We returned to the Dream House after a few hours to find most of its inhabitants up in the attic loft. Julia had begun painting a series of images commemorating our adventures in the Hedge. I made an offhand comment that we could arrange them in sequential order and have a hell of a comic book, which set Julia off like you wouldn\u2019t believe. \u201cFirst of all,\u201d she said icily, \u201cI don\u2019t read \u2018comic books.\u2019 They\u2019re <u><u>graphic</u> <u>novels</u></u>.\u201d So for the rest of the afternoon, all I had to do to tease her was say the words \u201ccomic book\u201d (or, if I was feeling particularly mischievous, \u201cfunnybook\u201d). It was fun, and some of the others even joined in from time to time.<br /> <br /> I got a text from Dark Kimberly during this time, asking (with a somewhat desperate tone) if I intended to perform that night, as a host of changelings intended to attend the show. I was flattered, and of course I\u2019m never one to turn down the opportunity to strut my stuff in front of my nearest and dearest, so of course I replied that I would love to smiley-face smiley-face smiley-face less-than-three. This led to a discussion of texting and emojis with Missy and Jane, which ballooned into a discussion of the evolution of cellphones themselves over the years. I confess, a lot of this info was new to me as well, and I discovered a few things about my own phone which I had not previously known.<br /> <br /> We eventually retired to the media room to give Missy and Jane a taste of the music they\u2019d missed over the past four decades or so. D had suggested at breakfast that each of us pick three songs from post-1978 to give them a proper sampling. This conversation was sparked when she played a bit of a song called \u201cLaid\u201d for the two of them to illustrate how some of the restrictions on music had eased up over the years.<br /> <br /> \u201cSee,\u201d I said with a grin as I took in Missy and Jane\u2019s somewhat shocked expressions, \u201cmusicians can sing about sex and drugs these days without disguising it with lyrics about roller skates and tambourines.\u201d<br /> <br /> Incidentally, when I complained that I was at a disadvantage when it comes to \u201cnew\u201d music, D rolled her eyes and said \u201cwhat, are you telling me that you don\u2019t know three songs from the last thirty-seven years?\u201d I allowed as how I could probably come up with something, and then turned the tables on her by asking if she could name three songs from <u><u>before</u></u> 1978. She eventually did\u2026 though she cut it really close with \u201cDancing Queen.\u201d<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t actually remember every song provided by everyone, but a few stand out for various reasons. Jacob played a song called \u201cHole In the World\u201d by the Eagles\u2026 a group which was popular when we were Taken, but broke up shortly thereafter for nearly twenty years. That song was one that they composed upon getting back together in the late 90s. Maria demonstrated how the restrictions upon language and subject matter in music had eased over the years by playing Rage Against the Machine\u2019s \u201cKilling In the Name Of.\u201d<br /> <br /> One of Julia\u2019s songs was \u201cDragula\u201d by Rob Zombie, a rockin\u2019 club dance song from around the turn of the century with repetitive, shouty lyrics and heavy guitar work\u2026 a hell of a lot of fun to dance to! I should think about working out an act with that one at some point. It\u2019s too bad Ace isn\u2019t around anymore; his voice would have been perfect for the singing on that one.<br /> <br /> Marguerite and Luna picked somewhat more sedate numbers for the most part, with a bit more broad coverage of the time period. Marguerite picked songs we\u2019ve performed at the Dream House from time to time like \u201cStray Cat Strut\u201d and \u201cLa Plage de St. Tropez,\u201d while Luna went for songs with a bit more popular appeal, like \u201cWelcome to the Jungle\u201d and one I hadn\u2019t heard before, \u201cWalking on Broken Glass\u201d by Annie Lennox. That\u2019s another one I might have to perform sometime.<br /> <br /> My own selections were carefully selected to display female vocalists from different eras with distinct styles. I started them off with \u201cWalkin\u2019 On Sunshine\u201d by Katrina and the Waves, because I love the upbeat optimistic feel of it. \u201cBring Me To Life\u201d was next, with Amy Lee\u2019s haunting vocals and Evanescence\u2019s hard-rock orchestration bringing the conversation into the new millennium. Finally, I topped it off with Lady Gaga\u2019s \u201cBad Romance\u201d to introduce a modicum of electronica into the mix. The girls seemed to like that one, so maybe I\u2019ll introduce them to more of her work over the next few days.<br /> <br /> There was a little bit of tension at one point when Jane pointed out that she never expected to see me in a lesbian relationship\u2026 let alone an <u><u>interracial</u></u> lesbian relationship. This set D\u2019s teeth on edge, of course, and she took further offense when Jane persisted in calling her a Mexican. \u201cI\u2019ve never even <u><u>been</u></u> to Mexico,\u201d she protested loudly, \u201ccan you <u><u>please</u></u> call me a Latina?\u201d When Jane protested that she wasn\u2019t familiar with the culture beyond a few stereotypes\u2026 well, things started to get a little out of hand.<br /> <br /> \u201cMaria!\u201d I said loudly at one point when she started to advance on my friend. She whipped around to glare at me, and I took her hand. \u201cShe doesn\u2019t know what she\u2019s saying and doing wrong yet,\u201d I soothed, giving her a squeeze. \u201cIt\u2019s going to take time. None of us had ever really met any Latinas back in Iowa. I know this is important to you, but\u2026 please be patient. For me.\u201d<br /> <br /> She took a couple of deep breaths, then turned back to Jane. \u201cSorry,\u201d she said, and it sounded like she meant it. \u201cPeople like me\u2026 we get the shaft a lot in modern society. It\u2019s made me a little defensive.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jane looked at the floor. \u201cI\u2019m sorry too,\u201d she said after a moment. \u201cI really don\u2019t mean to offend you. I just\u2026 everything\u2019s so different now\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI went through it too,\u201d I said, giving Jane\u2019s shoulder a squeeze. \u201cHell, I almost called the FBI on Jacob the first time we met\u2026\u201d That got a few laughs from those gathered, and even a smile from Jacob himself (though he admitted that an FBI investigation at that point would have been problematic, as his cover identity wasn\u2019t as extensive back then).<br /> <br /> After things got back to normal, we tried to explain the mechanics of glamour to our three newcomers. All three of them seemed cautiously enthusiastic about attending the show that evening. I offered to lend some more of my clothes to the three of them, and Jane, Missy and I retreated to my bedroom to pick out suitable ensembles.<br /> <br /> Once the three of us were alone, Jane confided that Missy had tried to convince her to return to Arcadia during the previous night, but Jane had refused, and Missy was unwilling to make the journey alone. I asked Missy if this was true, and she tearfully admitted that it was.<br /> <br /> \u201cEverything here\u2026 it doesn\u2019t feel <u><u>real</u></u>,\u201d she said after a moment. \u201cIt\u2019s like my life before was a dream and this is a dream and the only thing that makes sense to me is being back in our cage\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I pulled her into an embrace. \u201cI know it\u2019s hard,\u201d I whispered. \u201cI thought about going back a few times myself when I first escaped. But you have to accept it, Missy\u2026 <u><u>this</u></u> is reality. If anything, the cage was the dream. And you don\u2019t have to go through it alone\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cI know,\u201d she sniffed, \u201cI know you and Jane won\u2019t leave me, Jules\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAbsolutely,\u201d I said, \u201cbut there are other people who can help you too. The Winter Court has a Clinic in town, with therapists who specialize in helping changelings adjust\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTherapy?\u201d Jane asked. \u201cYou mean like a shrink?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s nothing to be ashamed of,\u201d I said. \u201cNot these days. Jacob, Calamity, and Maria all speak with a therapist regularly. They wouldn\u2019t be treating you for a disorder or anything, just helping you work through some monumentally heavy shit.\u201d<br /> <br /> We picked out a couple of pretty dresses for the two of them that fit relatively well, and prepared to head downstairs to await the opening curtain. Before we left the room, I sort of hesitated, trying to work up the courage for what I knew I had to do.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat is it, Jules?\u201d Jane asked after a moment.<br /> <br /> \u201cCan I tell you two something?\u201d I asked softly.<br /> <br /> \u201cSure,\u201d Missy said, looking concerned.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2026 I have to say this. I\u2019ve needed to say this for almost two years now.\u201d I looked up at the two of them and felt the tears start to spill. \u201cI\u2019m sorry,\u201d I said, choking slightly on the words. \u201cI\u2019m <u>so</u> sorry, girls.\u201d<br /> <br /> The two of them looked at each other quizzically, then back at me. \u201cFor what, Jules?\u201d Jane asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cI left you,\u201d I said simply. \u201cI <u><u>swore</u></u> that I wouldn\u2019t, and then I <u><u>left</u></u> you there to rot. I\u2019m sorry. I was so scared and I thought I wouldn\u2019t get another chance to escape and I\u2019m <u><u>sorry</u></u>\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Then the two of them were hugging me. \u201cShh,\u201d Jane said, stroking my hair, \u201cyou came back, Jules. That\u2019s all that matters.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe don\u2019t blame you, Jules,\u201d Missy added, \u201cwe never did. You\u2019re one of us.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIf it\u2019s important to you\u2026 we forgive you,\u201d Jane said.<br /> <br /> It <u><u>was</u></u> important to me. I was a wreck for the next twenty minutes or so\u2026 it made me glad that I hadn\u2019t applied my stage makeup yet. \u201cThank you,\u201d I eventually managed to gasp out. \u201cI\u2019m sorry I fell apart like that. I just\u2026 I\u2019ve been living with the guilt for so long. You two are so important to me\u2026 I love you both. It\u2019s so good to have you back.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe know how much you risked to come and get us, Jules,\u201d Jane said. \u201cWe\u2019re not going anywhere.\u201d And then her voice sort of hardened as she looked over to Missy. \u201c<u><u>Are</u></u> we?\u201d<br /> <br /> Missy shook her head. \u201cI\u2019m grateful. I just\u2026 it\u2019s\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHey,\u201d I said, taking her hand, \u201cit\u2019s okay. You\u2019re not alone; we\u2019ll help you deal with it. Jane\u2019s not leaving you for anything, and neither am I. And though I know you don\u2019t know them well, the rest of the motley is here for you too. Hell, the same could be said for the whole Freehold.\u201d<br /> <br /> So eventually I got the two of them dolled up for the company and the three of us headed downstairs. We had a huge crowd last night, mostly composed of changelings who wanted to welcome us back into the Freehold. I figured I\u2019d give them a real show, so I picked a song I\u2019d done previously and added it to the schedule (that way nobody had to learn new blocking, lighting, etc.). So I pulled on the fishnets and the leather and crooned my way through Madonna\u2019s \u201cLike a Virgin,\u201d doing my best to squeeze every last drop of desire I could out of the mortals in the crowd. <br /> <br /> It went well. It was good to be back.<br /> <br /> So of course the majority of my evening was spent mingling with the gathered changelings and trying to catch up on recent events. I stopped at Joan and Andromeda\u2019s table first, gratefully accepting hugs and kisses from both of them. Any fool could tell that they were genuinely ecstatic to have me back. That sent a warm rush from my heart throughout my whole body. It\u2019s humbling to know that people really care about my welfare.<br /> <br /> Of course I asked if they had started planning their nuptials yet. They got engaged before any of us in the motley, but they still haven\u2019t set a date. They were cagey about the answer, and I got the feeling that I had inadvertently hit upon something of a sore subject. Not that there\u2019s any strife between the two of them\u2026 it\u2019s more that they\u2019re still trying to win over Rebecca\u2019s family to the notion of their relationship. Honestly, they\u2019re more upset by the fact that Joan is a Gentile than that she\u2019s a woman. Lindsey is proud and steadfast in her faith, and has no desire to convert\u2026 and understandably wants the ceremony to be meaningful and official in the eyes of the church. But she\u2019s willing to accept that Rebecca\u2019s faith is no less important to her, so they\u2019re thinking about having two ceremonies.<br /> <br /> I took both of them by the hand and gave them my best smile. \u201cJust as long as I\u2019m invited to both of them,\u201d I said.<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course,\u201d Joan said at once.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe wouldn\u2019t think of having our wedding without you,\u201d Andromeda assured me.<br /> <br /> I promised both of them that I would join them for dinner and a feature film as soon as I could, but made sure to caution them that I wanted to stay close to Missy and Jane for a while in case they need me. Both expressed their hope that we could share an evening soon\u2026 but they totally understood why I might need to delay that rendezvous. \u201cOf course the welfare of your friends must come first,\u201d Joan said seriously. \u201cWe would expect nothing less of you, Lorelei. It is one of the reasons we care for you so deeply. You are truly a good person.\u201d<br /> <br /> Nothing gives one\u2019s ego a boost like having a paragon like Lindsey compliment your moral fiber! Gosh!<br /> <br /> I mingled a bit with everyone, but the next time I actually sat down for an extended conversation was when I reached the Spring Court table. Princess Jolie was as effervescent as ever, and again I could tell that she was genuinely happy to see me. We chatted for a bit about this and that. I gave her a \u201chighlights reel\u201d of our journey to Arcadia and back, and pointed out Missy and Jane across the theater (and Trinh, of course). She caught me up on the local gossip, including the fact that she is indeed sort of seeing Queen Charlotte again. I noted that Angelica didn\u2019t seem particularly pleased when this tidbit came out.<br /> <br /> I stopped by the bar next to chat with Jacob, Stasia, and Elena. Halley was there as well, but Molly was conspicuously absent (I assume she was shadowing Trinh\u2019s fetch, but I don\u2019t know for sure). I stayed just long enough to say hi to everyone, then moved on. It sounded like Elena and Jacob were having a pretty heavy conversation about how things went down with their family when Elena came out at Thanksgiving, and while I\u2019d love to be able to offer her some comfort or sage advice\u2026 it\u2019s really not my place. That was a family matter, and I didn\u2019t want to intrude.<br /> <br /> I made my way to the door and snuggled up next to my wife for a few minutes. We had the usual conversation about who was going to be doing what that evening, and after the requisite assurances that we were each other\u2019s top priority, we agreed that our other lovers deserved some attention that evening. \u201cUnless you want to get in on a threesome with me and Gloria,\u201d D said with a smirk. \u201cShe\u2019s so hard up for me that she\u2019d probably agree to it if you want to take advantage of the situation\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I thought about it. It\u2019s something I\u2019ve fantasized about more times than I can count\u2026 but that would have left Oleander out in the cold. While I know that my lover would never begrudge me the chance to have some fun on the side\u2026 she had been six months without me, and I didn\u2019t want her to think that I didn\u2019t appreciate her patience or everything that she\u2019s done to help me, my friends, my motley, and my father. \u201cAs <u><u>incredibly</u></u> tempting as that offer is,\u201d I said with heat, \u201cI\u2019m going to have to take a rain check. Think she\u2019ll still be up for it in a couple of days?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sure we\u2019ll convince her,\u201d D said with assurance. Then she looked across the theater, caught Gloria\u2019s eye, and snapped her fingers.<br /> <br /> Gloria rose and made her way across the theater, looking slightly panicky. \u201cIt\u2019s happening tonight?\u201d she asked with a nervous glance at me. \u201cI was hoping to get at least a little drunk first\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> D chuckled at that. \u201cCalm down. I\u2019m all yours tonight.\u201d<br /> <br /> I took her hand. \u201cIt\u2019s good to see you Gloria. I just\u2026 I know a lot of people sacrificed a lot so that I could help out my friends in Arcadia. I wanted to thank you for your patience and understanding over the last few months.\u201d<br /> <br /> She gave me a real smile and a quick hug. \u201cNo problem. It\u2019s good to have you back\u2026 all of you,\u201d she said as we disengaged.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m probably going to spend the evening with Oleander, if she\u2019s okay with that,\u201d I told the two of them. \u201cYou two have fun catching up, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> As I was walking away, I could swear I heard D mocking her gently under her breath. \u201c\u2019It\u2019s happening tonight?\u2019\u201d she mimicked. Gloria smacked her arm lightly, but made no other protest.<br /> <br /> My next stop was to speak with Rowan and Neon. The two of them are officially dating now (no chaperones required!) and it looks like things are going really well for them. I examined my feelings about that as frankly and honestly as I could, and was relieved to discover that I am <u><u>truly</u></u> happy for them. They seem very comfortable together, and any fool can see that they\u2019re head-over-heels for each other even if they\u2019re not as publicly demonstrative as some couples.<br /> <br /> Both expressed a hearty relief that we\u2019d made it back from Arcadia without losing too much time. Neon told me that Brightstar planned to attend the show the next night (which I believe is the last show before the Dream House closes for the holidays), so I made a mental note to keep that evening clear for her. Neon also told me that she was spending that night with one of her mortal paramours, a boy named Devin. Apparently things have gotten serious between the two of them. When she saw the doubt on my face, Neon was quick to assure me that Devin knows about me and is fine with Brightstar continuing to see me. So that\u2019s a relief.<br /> <br /> The rest of the conversation was a little odd, in that Rowan felt the need to apologize for her actions following the destruction of the House. It turns out that her connection to the psychic parasite had actually altered her brain chemistry on some level, flooding her system with endorphins and serotonin, upon which she had become dependent. Robbed of her connection to the House, she had been deprived of the chemicals and had sunk into a deep depression.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh my God!\u201d I said, reaching out and taking her hand. \u201cYou poor thing. Are you okay now? Is there something I can do to help?\u201d<br /> <br /> She smiled and patted my hand gently. \u201cThank you, Lori,\u201d she said softly, \u201cbut once we realized what was going on, the Freehold had Andromeda take a look at me. She\u2026 did something to fix the problem. I\u2019m not really sure what, but she fixed me.\u201d<br /> <br /> My alarm must have shown on my face, because Rowan squeezed my hand. \u201cShe didn\u2019t use the Table, if that\u2019s what you\u2019re worried about,\u201d she assured me quickly. \u201cI\u2026 don\u2019t really know what it is, but I know it\u2019s bad news. I heard her saying that the procedure would be easier if she had access to \u2018the Table.\u2019 But she managed without it, and I\u2019m okay now.\u201d<br /> <br /> I let out my breath in a sigh of relief. \u201cI\u2019m so glad,\u201d I said. \u201cLook, honey, I\u2019m sorry I put you through all of that stuff last year when you were already dealing with so much\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t,\u201d Rowan interrupted me. \u201cIt\u2019s okay, Lori. You couldn\u2019t have known. And everything turned out for the best\u2026\u201d She glanced fondly at her date, and I saw that her other hand was firmly in Neon\u2019s grasp.<br /> <br /> I took that as my cue to leave the lovebirds alone, and moved on a few minutes after that. I had one last stop to make before I retired for the evening. I dropped by Monica\u2019s table and asked if I could introduce her to a few people. She agreed readily enough, and a moment later we were sitting at the table with Missy and Jane (and close enough to Trinh so that she could join the conversation as well).<br /> <br /> \u201cMonica, these are my friends, Melissa Garfield and Jane Lassiter. And this is Trinh Jackson. The three of them have just returned from Arcadia, and I thought you might be able to spend a little time with them and help with the adjustment period. Ladies, this is Monica. I know she looks a little scary at first, but she\u2019s a real sweetheart, and she serves as the Freehold\u2019s unofficial welcoming party.\u201d<br /> <br /> The five of us fell into a conversation at that, and while nothing official was set up, the girls now know how to contact Monica when they\u2019re ready to get out of the house and start integrating into changeling society. Monica is used to dealing with people who are still a little shell-shocked by their ordeals in Arcadia, and she was quick to put the three of them at their ease.<br /> <br /> <br /> As the conversation ebbed, I noticed that Missy and Jane were both eying me somewhat hungrily, and\u2026 it awakened certain stirrings within me. These were the girls who first introduced me to the idea of love within my own gender, after all. I\u2019ve missed their touch for the last two years. When Monica moved on, Missy leaned in to kiss my cheek.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou were amazing up there, Jules\u2026 I mean Lorelei,\u201d she said.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah,\u201d Jane agreed, \u201cit was pretty damned hot.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks,\u201d I acknowledged with a grin, \u201cI\u2019ve had a lot of practice since I escaped, and I\u2019ve picked up a few tricks.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo we were talking,\u201d Missy said softly, \u201cand we were wondering if you wanted to\u2026\u201d She couldn\u2019t seem to finish the sentence, but I could see where it was going.<br /> <br /> I leaned over to her and kissed her forehead. \u201cI do,\u201d I sad after a moment, \u201con two conditions. First, unfortunately, it can\u2019t be tonight. I owe it to Oleander to spend tonight with her. She did so much to help us rescue you, and\u2026 and she might be the reason my Dad is still alive today. And from everyone\u2019s perspective except mine, it\u2019s been even longer since she\u2019s been with me than since you two have.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jane nodded at that. \u201cThat makes sense,\u201d she said after a moment. \u201cBut the offer stands\u2026 we\u2019ve really missed you, uh, Lori.\u201d<br /> <br /> Missy\u2019s brow wrinkled in thought. It was <u><u>adorable</u></u>. \u201cWhat\u2019s the other condition?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> I smiled, and took them each by the hand. \u201cI don\u2019t think you\u2019ll mind this one,\u201d I promised her. \u201cI just want you both to promise me that anything we do won\u2019t come between the two of you. I love you both, and I always will\u2026 but what the two of you have is special, and I don\u2019t want to cause any bad feelings or strife between you.\u201d<br /> <br /> The two of them looked at each other for a few wordless moments, and then each nodded to the other. \u201cDeal,\u201d Jane said definitively.<br /> <br /> So at long last, after what felt like hours of schmoozing and hobnobbing and other such nonsensical words that mean socializing, I made my way over to Oleander\u2019s table. Her face lit up when I approached, and she started to greet me. I promptly settled into her lap and silenced her with a deep, passionate kiss that lasted several full minutes. She gasped for air when I finally let up, smiled at me, and said \u201cnot that I\u2019m complaining, Angel, but what was that for?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat,\u201d I said, \u201cwas just a down payment to give you a little taste of how grateful I am for everything that you have done for me over the past eighteen months or so. That was for the goblin fruits, and the homunculus, and the straw for Missy last night. That was for loving me. But most of all,\u201d and at this I couldn\u2019t stop the tears from rolling down my cheeks, \u201cthat was for taking such good care of my Dad while I was away.\u201d<br /> <br /> She reached up with one hand and wiped my tears away. \u201cOf course, Angel,\u201d she said softly. \u201cHe\u2019s one of the most important people in your life. And\u2026 you\u2019re <u><u>the</u></u> most important person in my life.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAre you free tonight?\u201d I asked breathily from about two inches away.<br /> <br /> Her smile was so big that I could see her teeth\u2026 a rarity where Oleander is concerned. \u201cIf I <u><u>had</u></u> made plans for tonight, Angel, I would cancel them. No matter what they were.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd\u2026 would you mind staying here with me instead of going back to your place like we usually do? D\u2019s going over to Gloria\u2019s, so we\u2019ll have the room\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> She looked a little surprised by the request, but not upset. \u201cThat\u2019s fine with me. Why do you\u2026 oh,\u201d she said, as her eyes flicked over to Missy and Jane\u2019s table. \u201cI get it. How are they doing?\u201d<br /> <br /> I shrugged. \u201cIt\u2019s a process,\u201d I said. \u201cTrinh\u2019s okay; she wasn\u2019t in Arcadia that long. Missy\u2019s having trouble adjusting her mindset\u2026 I think she still thinks of the Durance as \u2018home.\u2019 Jane\u2019s doing better with that side of things, but she\u2019s having more trouble adjusting her attitudes and behavior to her new reality. But they\u2019ll get through it. They\u2019re strong.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd they\u2019ve got you to help them,\u201d Oleander said with a smile. \u201cAnd you\u2019ve got all of us.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThank God,\u201d I said, using the simple turn of phrase as a prayer.<br /> <br /> Things died down after that. D and Gloria had already left, and the theater was clearing out. Marguerite and Julia tried to pick up Trinh, but she got cold feet at the last minute and balked (I think they might have ended up going to bed with Desiree, though). When the last of the guests had departed, I led Oleander up to my bedroom and proceeded to demonstrate the depth and breadth of my gratitude for everything she does to me. I don\u2019t think I even scratched the surface, but I look forward to continuing the demonstration in the future.<br /> <br /> I actually slept last night, with Oleander snuggled up against my chest, our arms around each other. My internal clock is completely out-of-whack, either from our recent time-slip jaunt in Arcadia or from all the all-nighters and poofing I\u2019ve been doing over the past year or so. Whatever the reason, I woke up about ninety minutes before it was time to start on Sex Breakfast, so I\u2019ve been writing in this journal and watching Imelda sleep.<br /> <br /> She is thoughtful and considerate and more beautiful than most people in this Freehold seem to realize. I love her. She is not my D, my Maria, mi esposa\u2026 but she is mi amor all the same. I need to find some way to show her what she means to me\u2026 some way other than sex. I want to do something to prove that though she may not be my wife, she is never far from my thoughts.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s something I\u2019ll have to think about. But for now\u2026 I think I\u2019m just going to crawl back into bed for a little while.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei de la Rocha</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Today was not what I expected. I figured it would be just more introduction stuff for the newbies, and it was to some extent, but not all of it. We woke up for breakfast and found that Calamity and Becky had left a note for us letting us know that they had gone off on some romantic holiday by themselves. Sounded like a plan to me. I know those two really like each other and I think having some time just for themselves will be a good thing for both of them. They just need to figure out that the other person is the one for them and stick together. Hopefully this little break will help them do just that.<br /> <br /> Breakfast was fine. There was conversation about what it means to be a Changeling, all that stuff that I figured we\u2019d be talking about. The funny side to breakfast was Lori made eggs, bacon and toast for everyone and Missy and Jane almost turned green at the idea of eating eggs. Trinh, who\u2019d been in Arcadia far less time, ate them up just fine. The other two are going to need to get used to eating regular foods again. Lori assured them that they will soon remember that they are not birds, and will get used to being in \u2018the world\u2019 once more. I\u2019m not sure how much of that they believed just now, but it will sink in soon. There were some people that the Lady sent me to bring back to her realm that were grateful that I\u2019d come for them. They had gotten so used to being in Arcadia that they were having a really hard time getting used to \u201cnormal\u201d life again. Some people fought back, which wasn\u2019t unexpected, but some of them thanked me when I returned them to the Lady. I just hope that Lori\u2019s friends don\u2019t start wanting to go back to the Empress. I hope that they find a place in \u2018the world\u2019 and get used to the idea of being free once again. If they went back to Arcadia Lori would be devastated. She felt so bad for leaving them behind in the first place that I\u2019m not sure how she\u2019d react if they went back voluntarily now.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Lori. She was catching up on her news online this afternoon and came across and interesting article that she brought to my attention immediately. It appears that one Trinh Jackson, local model and minor celebrity, went a bit crazy last night about the time that we returned and started going on about the \u201cpeople that were out to get her.\u201d Lori suggested that I call Lowjack, which I thought was a good idea. He will know how to handle a possible threat from another fetch. So, I called him and explained what happened. He expressed his concern and said that he\u2019d put Molly on it to determine exactly what the fetch was up to and if she was going to be a threat to the real Trinh or not. I told him that I would talk to Trinh herself and see what she wants to do. She may not have a choice, but we\u2019ll see how things work out.<br /> <br /> So, I went upstairs to the attic to speak to Trinh. She was watching Julia paint, while Insincere Marguerite was doing the same. Marguerite was not dressed, which didn\u2019t seem to faze Trinh. I guess that makes sense. She was kept naked in a cage for a while. She probably got used to the whole naked thing. Anyway, I told Trinh about fetches in general and what we\u2019d discovered her fetch had done when we got back to \u2018the world.\u2019 I gave her the options. She could leave town and set up a new identity elsewhere, confront the fetch and see what happens, or try and approach the fetch peaceably and see if they can come to an arrangement. Trinh latched onto that last idea like a lifeline. I\u2019m not sure if that\u2019s going to work or not, but it could. Once Molly gets back to Lowjack we\u2019ll have a better idea of what sort of mindset the fetch is in and we can make plans from there. I just hope that it doesn\u2019t go \u201coff the rails\u201d like Mary\u2019s fetch did. That was just a bad scene all around, and it really messed up Mary. Come to think of it, we don\u2019t see Mary much around anymore. I know that she had some issues with coming too close to her beast side and craving human flesh. That is probably why she hasn\u2019t been seen in a while. Keep her away from temptation and all that.<br /> <br /> Later in the afternoon Luna came back from talking to her bosses. She explained that she had been doing \u201cwork\u201d in Africa for the past six months and finally arrived back. I don\u2019t think that I could have pulled that off, but she has a certain force of personality that people listen to, so hopefully all will be well with her Ranger job. I happen to like her job. It fits her well, and it\u2019s fun to help out on occasion when she finds would-be poachers. Dr. Sullivan never did approve of me terrorizing people in the woods with Luna. I think he thought that it was taking a step backward towards my old self as Rime. He\u2019s probably right, but it\u2019s just too much fun.<br /> <br /> Lori was talking to Missy and Jane and they expressed that they were having trouble adapting to life in \u2018the world.\u2019 So Lori brought up the therapists at the Winter Court being really good resources. They initially balked at that idea. I think that they had the idea that you only go to therapy if you\u2019re crazy, but we tried to reassure them that therapy is for anyone that needs to talk to someone and I admitted that I see them regularly as does De la Rocha, Calamity and others. I think they finally came around to the idea that it might be good for them to talk to the therapists, but as of yet have not set up an appointment or anything. <br /> <br /> Then De la Rocha came up with the idea of all of us recommending some of our favorite songs from the last 30 plus years to Missy and Jane so they have something to listen to, to help them catch up on music that they missed. I\u2019m sure this will also lead to other questions, like what the songs are referring to and such, so it should be a good way to help them reacclimate to \u2018the world.\u2019 De la Rocha suggested that we each come up with three songs, so I suggested \u201cHole in the World\u201d by the Eagles. I like that song and figured they\u2019d know the band. They\u2019ve been in business forever. I also listed \u201cWherever You May Roam\u201d by Metallica and \u201cFreak Like Me\u201d by Halestorm. I thought they might like the strong female vocals from that band. Plus, the song is really cool. Luna suggested \u201cWalking on Broken Glass,\u201d \u201cWelcome To the Jungle,\u201d and \u201cWake Me Up Before You Go-Go.\u201d Also good songs. I\u2019m not sure off the top of my head what other songs people suggested. I know that \u201cBring Me to Life\u201d by Evanesce was on the list, as was \u201cDominion Mother Russia\u201d Or something along those lines. I\u2019ll be honest I paid closer attention to the title when the words Mother Russia came up. There was also \u201cKilling In the Name Of.\u201d I think De la Rocha suggested that one.<br /> <br /> While we were talking a little bit of tension came up between De la Rocha and Missy and Jane. I think it was mostly Jane, but it came about because the new girl didn\u2019t know what terminology to use to refer to our Latina motley mate and used the term Mexican. De la Rocha was offended by that because she\u2019d never been to Mexico and wasn\u2019t from there. Eventually cooler heads prevailed, namely Lori and some others, and we agreed that vocabulary would be another good thing for our \u201cLadies out of time\u201d to learn. Some people, like De la Rocha, get particular at what they are called, but Jane had no way of knowing the term Latina before this afternoon. We\u2019re going to need a crash course on cultural changes of the past 30 years I think. Lori even admitted that when she first met me she almost called the FBI on me because I\u2019m from Russia. The Cold War was big when she was taken and not an issue when I was born, so that thought had never occurred to me. I\u2019m glad in the end that she didn\u2019t call them. At that point my identification would not have held up to Federal scrutiny.<br /> <br /> Then there was the show. The show itself went fine. Lori wowed Missy and Jane by singing a Madonna song up on stage. I don\u2019t think they were expecting the level of talent that our lovey Lori has when it comes to singing and performing. I tended bar like usual and talked to the regulars. Molly was off keeping an eye on Trinh\u2019s fetch, so I talked to Hailey about my trip to Arcadia and some of the highlights of the trip. I left out the bit about Mama Lion leaving a way in for us and a couple other things, but focused on us getting the girls out and fighting off the Empress\u2019 loyalist and guards. She was particularly interested in the different forms that our mounts in the Hedge took. She smirked at me when I admitted that mine was a horse made of ice. What can I say, I\u2019m ice-aspected. I can\u2019t help it.<br /> <br /> I also talked to Elena, which is where I spent a good bit of time. Stasia realized that we needed to talk and made her way off to talk to someone else so I could have a private word with my sister. I asked about our parents\u2019 reaction to her news and especially the \u201clittle shit\u2019s\u201d reaction. Apparently when she said that things did not go well it was an understatement. Things tanked hard. They invited Elena home for the Thanksgiving Holiday and Elena asked if she could bring a date. They said sure and they made the drive all the way up to Portland. When our parents greeted Elena at the door they were shocked to see another girl with her. It seems that the \u201clittle shit\u201d reacted poorly to the news as well and got into a brief confrontation with Stasia. Our parents threatened to call the cops and Stasia eventually backed down when Elena said that they were leaving. Our parents gave her an ultimatum. Elena could stay and be part of the family if she gave up Stasia. Well, that wasn\u2019t going to happen, so Elena left. I get the impression that our parents don\u2019t want her to come back as long as she\u2019s dating a woman. Well, they can go stuff it. I was admittedly cautious about Stasia in the beginning, but not because she was a woman. I couldn\u2019t care less about that. I just didn\u2019t want Elena to get hurt. Well, Stasia has proved that she cares about my sister and has been treating her right. That\u2019s all I want. I want Elena to be happy, and if Stasia makes her happy then good. If our parents can\u2019t accept that then they can kiss my ass.<br /> <br /> I gave my sister a hug and reminded her that she is surrounded by people that care about her and she has a woman that loves her a good deal. I reminded her also that she will always have my support. I don\u2019t plan on going anywhere so as long as she needs me I\u2019ll be there for her. She admitted that she was really glad that I was back and said that she might be a little more clingy than normal for a little while. I said that was fine and that I\u2019m always happy to help. When things calmed down a bit I congratulated her on her engagement with Stasia and told her how happy I was for the couple. I also suggested that maybe sometime soon we could go on a camping trip to the mountains again. It was exactly a year ago that Stasia and my sister hooked up. I thought it might be good to go camping again to remind them of that night, and to celebrate our birthday. She seemed interested in that, so I just need to bring up the idea to the rest of the motley and we\u2019ll see how many people want to join us this time.<br /> <br /> I can\u2019t express enough how mad it makes me that my parents, our parents, rejected Elena based on the gender of her date for the holidays. I thought that they were better than that. I know that they are pretty traditional but they\u2019ve always shown support in our interests and dreams. I just never thought that they\u2019d go this far. That they\u2019d make an ultimatum to Elena. Them or Stasia. Elena would have been miserable if she gave up Stasia and she would resent our parents for making her do it. This way she\u2019s hurt by the rejection, but she at least has someone by her side that loves her unconditionally. Well, besides me that is. I\u2019d be remiss if I didn\u2019t admit to wanting to get back at the \u201clittle shit\u201d at least for his actions that day. Part of me was almost tempted to get him good and lost in a cave somewhere cold, but that may be going a bit too far. If I was still Rime I\u2019d be making a road trip already and getting ready to reintroduce the \u201clittle shit\u201d to his maker. Actually, he is a fetch. It\u2019s not like I\u2019d be stranding a real person in Arcadia. I would just be returning him to the Lady. I am so very tempted to do that. I know Calamity would help if I asked her to. The others might be a little reticent about the whole idea, especially Lori. I\u2019ll have to think on that. Would it be worth it to possibly incur the wrath of the Lady just to get back at the matchstick boy that hurt my sister? I\u2019ll have to give that one some thought. <br /> <br /> <i>End Session CVII</i><br /> <br /> A lot more RP than rolling this session. The only thing left out was an extended conversation about how everyone met. This was covered in the journals, and a previous Lori journal covered that same essential conversation in some detail, so it was left out.<br /> <br /> The music picking was fun.<br /> <br /> Calamity\u2019s player is back to fighting fit so she will be along next time. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T02:19:49-07:00","id":1220474,"title":"","content":"Holy crap it\u2019s almost Christmas. Final Show till New Years, Christmas Eve fun, plots to murder two Fetches, plots to avenge another and have a positive reunion with a third. Oh yeah, and helping the new girls acclimate.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CVIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> So Wednesday, December 23<sup>rd</sup> dawned bright and early\u2026 and Oleander and I, taking our cue from the rest of the house, rose somewhat later. I was still among the first to make it to the kitchen, so I took it upon myself to start on breakfast. I figured we\u2019d had enough fancy Frenchified food for the time being, and started in on a batch of good old-fashioned blueberry pancakes. Though Marguerite made displeased noises about how \u201cAmerican\u201d the meal was (I might have teased her just a <u><u>tiny</u></u> bit by calling them \u201cflapjacks\u201d a few times), she tucked in with all the others when the pancakes were in front of her.<br /> <br /> The kitchen was actually pretty crowded that morning, what with the motley, Missy &amp; Jane, Oleander, and Gloria hanging around\u2026 not to mention the unexpected bonus of Calamity and Becky, back from parts unknown to rejoin polite society! \u201cParts unknown\u201d turned out to be a rented beach house down the shore. I made some nervous comments about how one can\u2019t trust beach houses these days, but Calamity assured me that this particular beach house showed no tendencies toward either murder or malicious mind control.<br /> <br /> I brought up a few potential acts for that evening\u2019s show\u2026 the last show of the season, if you don\u2019t count next weekend\u2019s big New Year\u2019s Eve extravaganza. We decided to hit a few of our old favorites\u2026 Christmas crowd pleasers that we knew would play well with our regulars and wouldn\u2019t require a whole lot of planning for new choreography or lighting effects. With that taken care of, I felt confident in planning a few other activities for the rest of the afternoon.<br /> <br /> Oleander bade me farewell after she\u2019d eaten her fill of pancakes, telling me that she would be heading into the Hedge soon, and would likely be toxic for the next few days. She nevertheless promised to stop by on Christmas day to say hello and wish me a happy holiday.<br /> <br /> \u201cI only regret that I won\u2019t be able to offer you a Christmas kiss, Angel,\u201d she said with sorrow.<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t worry about it, sweetie,\u201d I said, offering her another kiss before she left. \u201cYou\u2019ll be my own little sprig of mistletoe\u2026 full of the Christmas spirit, making me yearn for a kiss, and mildly toxic. Plus,\u201d I added with a wink, \u201cI\u2019m pretty sure you could take out a Norse god if you set your mind to it!\u201d She laughed at the (admittedly forced) witticism and said one more goodbye.<br /> <br /> Oh, I should also mention that Jacob asked the motley (plus a few close friends like Elena, Stasia, Missy &amp; Jane) if we wanted to go out camping again as sort of a late birthday celebration for him and Elena. Apparently they did that a lot as kids, and I think reviving the tradition at the Dream House might help Elena to feel like she\u2019s a part of a family again. Of course we all agreed that it sounded like great fun, and Jacob set about making the preparations.<br /> <br /> Monica showed up just after Sex Breakfast to take our trio of new arrivals on a tour of the Freehold, and maybe get them some new clothes of their own (the Freehold provides a small stipend for new arrivals just for expenses like that). Jane asked before they left if I could introduce them to my guy in L.A. so that they could get whatever outfits they picked out altered to account for their wings. I gave the shop a call, and Antoine agreed to meet us there later that afternoon. He\u2019s such a sweetie-pie, taking time during the holidays to help us out!<br /> <br /> D also went out just after Sex Breakfast. It seems that Twitch had heard that we were back in the Freehold, and had invited her out for lunch so that they could catch up. I suspect that he also wanted to reassure herself that she was still the friend he\u2019s come to know rather than the monster that used to haunt his nightmares, and I trust that she was able to reassure him on that count. At least, when I asked her about it later, she told me that things went well. \u201cI still feel it, deep down inside,\u201d she confessed, \u201cbut I know how to handle it better now. Especially in well-lit, crowded places like that.\u201d<br /> <br /> So while most of my friends were out, I spent my time on the computer, trying to set up a schedule for my first semester at UCLA. The news is mostly good\u2026 I should be able to get in to a few AP tests before mid-January, and if I do well enough I might be able to place out of as many as 12-15 credit hours, which will just about make up for the semester I missed while we were in Arcadia. You never know, right? Doesn\u2019t hurt to try. What\u2019s more, since this first semester is going to be filled with general education courses, I\u2019ll probably be able to take most of my classes online, and cluster the others in such a way that I\u2019ll only need to drive to campus two or three times a week.<br /> <br /> Oh, before I move on, I should mention that once again the Christmas season has worked its magic upon Marguerite\u2026 she\u2019s so <u><u>adorable</u></u> at this time of year! Though Kimberly had organized the holiday decorations long before we returned, she had confined her efforts to the public areas of the Dream House. Marguerite had dug out a few more decorations and was stringing them up in the hallways and in our private rooms, singing Christmas carols in French all the while. And of course, I frequently found her dangling just above my head holding a sprig of Mistletoe out expectantly.<br /> <br /> When the girls got back, Monica asked to speak with me briefly, so we let the three of them freshen up. Her assessment of my friends\u2019 psychological state was troubling, but not particularly surprising to me. Missy seems to have a relatively mild form of agoraphobia; she tends to get nervous in big, wide open spaces. Monica noted the tendency in Missy to retreat from her surroundings, and her longing to return to the cage that\u2019s all she\u2019s known for the past God-knows-how-long. Jane\u2019s better about integrating into her current surroundings, but she reacts <u><u>very</u></u> negatively to any suggestion that she and Missy be separated\u2026 even temporarily and within shouting distance of each other. At least she didn\u2019t think any of them were even remotely likely to be Loyalists.<br /> <br /> I thanked her for her insight and pulled out my phone. I don\u2019t often contact the monarchs directly (other than Princess Jolie), but I keep their information in my phone for emergencies. In about thirty seconds I was speaking with Boss Lowjack. I apologized for bothering him, and asked if it might be possible to get Missy and Jane into a counseling session within the next day or two. He checked his schedule (we commiserated about the prevalence of computers in modern society), and allowed as how he would be able to fit them in at 10:30 the next morning. He asked if Trinh would need counseling as well, and I told him that I\u2019d ask her, but to assume that she\u2019d be fine for the time being unless he heard otherwise from me.<br /> <br /> I wanted to try something before we went out, so I asked our three new arrivals to join me in the backyard. I tried to explain the basics of flight to the three of them\u2026 how our wings really <u><u>shouldn\u2019t</u></u> allow us to fly based on the laws of physics, but our connection to the Wyrd can overcome those limitations if it\u2019s strong enough. I made sure to let them know that they probably wouldn\u2019t be able to truly fly for a while, but that they might be able to glide if they wanted to try.<br /> <br /> Missy and Jane were all for it, and honestly\u2026 they took to it really quickly. About as quickly as I did when I first returned to the world, actually. Trinh was a harder sell\u2026 she\u2019s still close enough to the human she used to be that she can\u2019t really believe that she\u2019s <u><u>capable</u></u> of flight yet. She took a few test glides off the raised outdoor stage, but wouldn\u2019t even entertain the notion of jumping from the balcony or the roof like the rest of us.<br /> <br /> So the four of us piled into the van and headed out after half an hour or so of flying lessons. The \u2018vette is one of my favorite things ever, but it is not practical when you need to transport more than two people. Before turning toward L.A., I ran us into Malibu proper and took the girls by Wildfox. The Freehold is generous in helping new arrivals get on their feet, but they have limited resources, so most of the girls\u2019 new wardrobes had come from thrift shops and Goodwill. I thought I\u2019d treat them to something a little fancier, since my bank account is pretty flush after gathering interest for six months with no expenses.<br /> <br /> I grabbed the attention of one of the fashion consultants and asked her to find a few fashionable backless dresses for my friends. She brought out a load of good options for each of them, and I let them pick their favorites. Trinh made some earnest noises about paying me back when she saw the price tag, but I just smiled and said \u201cMerry Christmas\u201d and left it at that.<br /> <br /> Traffic was light today, so it only took us about forty-five minutes to get to Challenges in L.A. Antoine picked me out as soon as we entered the store and rushed up with a big smile on his face. He kissed me on each cheek (I returned the favor) and then turned his attention on my friends. It looked for a moment like he was going to offer them the same treatment, but he took in their nervous demeanor and held back at the last minute.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know who originally ensorcelled Antoine, but the changelings of L.A. and the surrounding counties owe him a debt of gratitude. Like many of the more exotic changelings in the area, I can\u2019t buy my clothes off the rack, and doing my own alterations (cutting slits in the back of shirts and dresses to accommodate my wings) results in sloppy frayed edges that won\u2019t stand the test of time. Antoine alters clothing professionally, doubling and sewing up the edges and adding extra sleeves or whatever else might be necessitated by a changeling\u2019s unorthodox physique.<br /> <br /> Wing-slits are apparently a pretty easy alteration; Antoine said he had a template for his equipment that makes things go pretty quickly. He took a few measurements from each of my friends and said he would be done within the hour. We browsed the shop and chatted idly for a bit while we waited. I had the opportunity to observe Missy\u2019s agoraphobia for myself\u2026 whenever her gaze strayed to the window, she got this sort of thousand-yard stare as she glanced up at the sky. I sincerely hope that someday she\u2019ll be able to appreciate the freedom the open sky represents to people like us\u2026 but I won\u2019t try to rush her into it.<br /> <br /> We hurried back to the Dream House after the alterations were finished, and arrived with about twenty minutes to spare before curtain. I rushed into wardrobe and makeup, and saw Missy and Jane to the same table they\u2019d claimed the previous evening. We once again played to a packed house; the Christmas show is fast becoming a much-anticipated tradition at the Dream House.<br /> <br /> Marguerite and I paired up once more for our \u201cBaby It\u2019s Cold Outside\u201d duet, and Calamity and I broke out our \u201cBloody Creature Poster Girl\u201d staple. The two of them also did their own numbers (which both earned thunderous applause). I\u2019d originally intended to go with my \u201cSanta Baby\u201d number, but decided at the last minute to substitute something with a little more soul. I slinked my way across the stage to the bluesy strains of Charles Brown\u2019s \u201cPlease Come Home for Christmas,\u201d and soaked up the desire I felt every time my thigh showed through the slit in my gown.<br /> <br /> I mingled with the crowd after my last number, speaking with Siobhan (who seems to be settling in well), Moon and Dionysia, White Maria, and various and sundry other members of the Freehold. Dark Kimberly is apparently working to solve her Fetch\u2019s murder, which occurred while she was in Arcadia, but she isn\u2019t having much luck. The motley has agreed to help her with her investigations if we can, because\u2026 well, because that\u2019s just the sort of thing that we do, I guess.<br /> <br /> I spent a lot of time with Missy and Jane, of course, and made sure they would be ready to go by 10:00am the next morning. Talking them into the counseling session was easier than I\u2019d expected, actually\u2026 the hard part was getting them to agree to join me for lunch with Dad following their appointment. I also introduced them to Neon and Brightstar, so they\u2019ve met all of my official girlfriends now. Trinh asked if I had individual nicknames for each of them, and I realized that I don\u2019t. Aside from calling my wife \u201cD,\u201d I don\u2019t really have nicknames for any of them. I mean, I tend to call people \u201csweetie\u201d when I feel close to them\u2026 but that\u2019s not confined to my girlfriends or lovers.<br /> <br /> Which brings me to that night\u2019s festivities. I\u2019d told D earlier that Brightstar was going to be there that night, and asked if she was okay with that. She gave me her usual cocky grin and a soft kiss, and said \u201cnot at all, babe. You want some alone time with her, or you want to spend the evening with both of us together?\u201d And all of a sudden I <u><u>did</u></u> want that. I wanted it more than I could say. If it had been Oleander instead of Brightstar I wouldn\u2019t have gone for it, but I know my girls well enough to know that she\u2019d be okay with it.<br /> <br /> So I led D up to Neon and Brightstar\u2019s table, and the four of us sat around making small talk for a while. When the crowds started to thin, I turned to Brightstar with a mock-serious expression on my face. \u201cHoney?\u201d I said sweetly.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, babe?\u201d she replied.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ve got a little bit of a dilemma here,\u201d I admitted.<br /> <br /> Her brow wrinkled cutely in sympathy. She\u2019s such a sweetheart. \u201cHow can I help?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell,\u201d I began, \u201cit has to do with all of these convoluted timelines. Like, I know that from your perspective, it\u2019s been about six months since the two of us have been together, and I want to acknowledge that and give you the attention you deserve from me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks!\u201d she said brightly with a dazzling smile.<br /> <br /> \u201cBut on the other hand, from <u><u>our</u></u> point of view, Maria and I have been married for less than two weeks, and we still have that newlywed feeling going on, so I want to spend some time with <u><u>her</u></u> as well. Now\u2026 how in the world can I reconcile those feelings so that <u><u>everyone</u></u> gets the attention they deserve?\u201d I admit to hamming it up a bit at this point, batting my eyelashes and grinning innocently.<br /> <br /> Brightstar\u2019s own grin widened, and she glanced over at Maria. \u201cI think I can come up with a few suggestions along those lines, but I\u2019d need to discuss them with the two of you in private,\u201d she said after a moment. And so began an evening of distraction that ended up being an odd combination of marathon and sprint\u2026 hell, Brightstar is the only person I know who probably <u><u>could</u></u> sprint an entire marathon.<br /> <br /> When the three of us finally wore each other out, I allowed myself to be drawn into a few hours of blessed sleep. Brightstar snuggled up against my chest, and D nestled between my wings (she\u2019s gotten really good at that over the past couple of years) and put her arms around me\u2026 around <u><u>both</u></u> of us, actually. I fell asleep after a few moments of that, and I think Brightstar did as well. I can\u2019t speak for her, but I know that I\u2019m never as comfortable as I am when D has me in her embrace. I know for certain that nothing can hurt me while she\u2019s protecting me.<br /> <br /> I have a vague memory of D leaning over and kissing my cheek as she got up for therapy the next morning. \u201cAdios, mi amor,\u201d she whispered, and pulled the sheet up over the two of us. I think I managed to mumble out something like \u201cluvyu\u201d before sinking back into the warm clouds I was dreaming about.<br /> <br /> The next time an alarm went off, unfortunately, it was for me. I managed \u2013 with difficulty \u2013 to extract myself from Brightstar\u2019s slumbering embrace, threw on a dress, and headed down the hall to gather Missy and Jane. They were already awake when I got there, and if they weren\u2019t exactly enthusiastic about their upcoming counseling, at least they were resolved to go through with it.<br /> <br /> The three of us met D, Calamity, and Jacob as they were coming out of the Clinic. The latter two decided to head home, while D stuck around to hang out with Twitch so that she\u2019d be available for lunch with Dad after the appointment. As it turns out, the counselors wanted to speak with Missy and Jane without me present, so I ended up hanging out with the two of them as well. D is still a bit edgy around Twitch, but she\u2019s gotten much better about reining her predatory impulses in when he\u2019s present. I never doubted her ability to do so, but still\u2026 I\u2019m proud of the progress she\u2019s made.<br /> <br /> (In point of fact, she was probably less nervous around him than I was on this particular occasion. Not that I was afraid he would hurt me, or that I would do anything to him\u2026 it had more to do with the fact that his office at the Clinic is decorated in post-apocalyptic horror-movie surgeon style. I have never in my life seen that many syringes, and they all seemed to be pointing at me no matter where I stood in the room. Sigh. I suppose it\u2019s good practice for when I become a doctor and have to deal with needles all the time\u2026)<br /> <br /> When the hour was up, Dr. Bright asked to speak with me privately. He has the same concerns over Missy and Jane that I\u2019ve already enumerated elsewhere\u2026 namely that Missy is sort of a flight risk (no pun intended) and that Jane has the capacity to commit great violence if she is provoked. His assessment only bore up my own analysis of the situation\u2026 but it was still hard to hear. I mean, to think that sweet Melissa, who always loved eating outside in the sun during lunch period, might prefer the gilded comforts of the Empress\u2019 cage. And Jane, well, she was always feisty and kind of sarcastic, but I never really thought of her as a violent person before. It nearly brought tears to my eyes, which would have been super embarrassing in front of Dr. Bright.<br /> <br /> But to be fair, I\u2019m not really the same person I was before I was Taken either. It\u2019s not their fault. They were in Arcadia too long, and it took its toll on them. It\u2019s my responsibility to help them, and damn it, I\u2019m going to do my utmost no matter what it takes.<br /> <br /> Dr. Bright had a few suggestions as to how we might deal with the situation. First, he stated that under no circumstances should the two of them be forcibly separated. They tried at first to give Missy and Jane separate counseling sessions, but even <u><u>suggesting</u></u> that made both of them very agitated. Well, okay, I could have told them that and saved them the trouble.<br /> <br /> Dr. Bright is also providing a mild sedative\u2026 mostly for Missy. He\u2019s giving a bottle to Jane and another to me, just in case. It might help her sleep a little better, but he cautioned us not to use it for that purpose over an extended period to avoid creating a dependency. It could also be useful if she begins to suffer anxiety attacks, which is a real possibility over the next few weeks. Again, I have no problem with this suggestion so long as the drug use doesn\u2019t get out of hand.<br /> <br /> His third suggestion was\u2026 problematic. He <u><u>strongly</u></u> recommended fitting the two of them with ankle bracelets, like criminals. These devices would be networked to an application on the motley\u2019s phones. If the two of them went into the Hedge, the app would alert the rest of us, and tell us the point at which the two of them had left the world so that we could retrieve them before it was too late. I see the sense in this, I really do, but\u2026<br /> <br /> I told Dr. Bright that I\u2019d take his suggestion under advisement\u2026 but I knew even then that I would only do it if the two of them agreed willingly to the precaution. I absolutely <u><u>will</u> <u>not</u></u> treat the two of them as prisoners; that\u2019s contrary to <u><u>everything</u></u> I\u2019m trying to achieve with them.<br /> <br /> Luckily it wasn\u2019t an issue. I explained the Doctor\u2019s recommendations to the two of them. Missy balked at the tracking device at first, but Jane \u2013 seeing that look in her eye and truly wanting to save her from herself \u2013 nodded and said \u201cI\u2019ll do it\u201d pretty much immediately. Missy, realizing that there\u2019d be no point in refusing the anklet if Jane had one, resigned herself to wearing one.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s not forever,\u201d I promised them both, hugging them close. \u201cIt\u2019s just until you acclimate to the Freehold. Once you\u2019re comfortable here, they\u2019ll come off. You have my word.\u201d<br /> <br /> Once they were both fitted, we picked up the prescriptions at the front desk, downloaded the app on my phone, and made our way back to the van. From the clinic it was just a short ride over to Dad\u2019s house. He greeted us warmly at the door, favoring me and Maria with vigorous hugs and Missy and Jane with somewhat more reserved embraces.<br /> <br /> \u201cBefore we eat,\u201d Dad said as soon as everyone is seated, \u201cthere is something I\u2019d like to discuss privately with Juliette. If you would excuse us\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I followed him into his office and closed the door behind me. \u201cWhat\u2019s up, Dad?\u201d I asked. \u201cIs everything okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes,\u201d he said, but I heard a certain heaviness in his answer. \u201cI\u2026 while searching through some old documents the other day, I\u2026 I <u><u>found</u></u> something, Juliette.\u201d He produced an unsealed envelope from his desk. \u201cI feel that it is my duty to give this letter to Jane, but I wanted to speak with you about it first.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat is it?\u201d I asked, a little confused.<br /> <br /> He sighed. \u201cBen Lassiter and I were never close friends, but he was a member of my congregation. I spent some time ministering to him during his decline, following the death of Jane\u2019s Fetch and the dissolution of his marriage. This is a photocopy of a letter Jane\u2019s Fetch wrote just before\u2026 just before the end.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat does it say?\u201d I asked, uneasy.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou may read it, if you like,\u201d he said, handing me the envelope.<br /> <br /> It wasn\u2019t pleasant reading. Jane\u2019s Fetch seemed to know that the end was near when she wrote that letter. She seemed resolved toward her fate. She felt that the world would never accept the love that she had found with Missy (the letter was written in 1981), and rather than hide what they had together in such a world, she preferred to go out in a blaze of glory. Though she didn\u2019t exactly <u><u>plan</u></u> to die in a daring daylight robbery\u2026 she was realistic enough to know that this was a likely eventuality. She apparently thought this was preferable to forcing Missy into that sort of life.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a little more beneath the surface of the letter, unless I miss my guess. I believe that the Fetch <u><u>knew</u></u> on some level that she wasn\u2019t the real Jane Lassiter. I don\u2019t think it was a conscious knowledge; it was more like a feeling of vague detachment from the world and people around her (except for Missy\u2019s Fetch). If that\u2019s the case, she might have wanted to end their lives to spare Missy the revelation that <u><u>she</u></u> wasn\u2019t real either. So I\u2019m wondering if that might have played a part in their fate as well.<br /> <br /> It rang a little too close to the girls\u2019 current situation for my liking. Jane and Missy already feel that same sense of disconnection from the world in which they find themselves, and I really don\u2019t want them reading that letter and feeling like suicide is a viable alternative to learning to cope with their circumstances. While I agree with Dad that they deserve to know what the letter contains\u2026 I\u2019m thinking that the time just isn\u2019t right.<br /> <br /> \u201cDad,\u201d I said seriously, \u201cI\u2019m not sure if they\u2019re ready to read this letter yet.\u201d<br /> <br /> He sighed. \u201cI found that letter while I was looking for something else, the night that you returned from\u2026 from that other place,\u201d he said after a moment. \u201cI can\u2019t help but feel that Providence was at work in that, Juliette.\u201d He looked away for a moment, and then looked back at me. \u201cBut you are far more familiar with the circumstances than I am, and you know the two of them well. I will trust your judgment in this.\u201d<br /> <br /> I took his hand in my own. \u201cAnd I trust yours, Dad. I promise that I <u><u>will</u></u> give them this letter, if you\u2019ll leave it in my possession. I just\u2026 I want to give them a little more time to adjust to the world before I challenge their place in it, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> He squeezed my hand gently. \u201cVery well,\u201d he said with a smile.<br /> <br /> The two of us rejoined Missy, Jane, and Maria in the sitting room and talked for a while. Dad was brilliant, putting the two of them at their ease as well as anyone has since they got back from Arcadia. Though I couldn\u2019t help but notice that the two of them were always very stiff and respectful in their replies to his questions, and always called him \u201cReverend Wells.\u201d<br /> <br /> When it came up naturally in conversation, he was quick to assure the two of them that he had no problem with their relationship. \u201cLove is both beautiful and rare in this world,\u201d he told them, \u201cand I have come to realize that the <u><u>fact</u></u> of love is more important than the <u><u>object</u></u>.\u201d He\u2019d said something like that to me when I first came out to him last year, now that I think of it.<br /> <br /> He also had a refrigerator full of food donated by his congregation. \u201cMy flock treats me very well,\u201d he explained, \u201cno matter how I might try to dissuade them. I have a number of vegetables, and turkey and ham. Which would you prefer?\u201d<br /> <br /> Missy and Jane looked at each other for a moment, and I think I saw them turn ever so slightly green. \u201cHam,\u201d they replied in unison. No surprises there, though I still think a hearty meal of good fried chicken would do wonders for their world view.<br /> <br /> So we had a lovely lunch and a good deal of pleasant conversation. Dad made sure to tell Missy and Jane that they were welcome in his house and his church at any time, and that he would be happy to do whatever he could to help them get their bearings and start their new lives together (I think that simple adverb at the end of his sentence did more to win Jane over than anything else he said or did). The farewell hugs were a little less reserved, and we chatted amiably on our way back to the Dream House. It kept Missy from staring out the side windows and getting all tense, at any rate.<br /> <br /> We heard the tell-tale sounds of sparring from the backyard when we got back. Jacob and Calamity started sparring without me! Can you believe it? I raced upstairs and changed into a pair of bike pants and a sports bra, taped up my knuckles, and joined the two of them on the outdoor stage for a bit of combat practice. While I still don\u2019t like the idea of actually getting into a real fight, it\u2019s great exercise and in keeping with my role as a Pilgrim of the Endless Road. I\u2019m getting better, too\u2026 but I have to work on overcoming my instincts. At this point, every time someone lands a blow I tend to launch myself into the air to get out of reach. As Jacob pointed out, I need to have other options available to me in case I\u2019m threatened in a space where such a retreat isn\u2019t possible.<br /> <br /> D didn\u2019t participate in the sparring, unfortunately, though I understand why. She headed off to the Children\u2019s Library to see Madame Spidertoes, who had been inquiring as to her health since we returned. I\u2019ve been meaning to speak with Gladys myself since we get back\u2026 I really need to thank her for the spider-bomb, and to let her know that it was used to good effect in Arcadia. But this didn\u2019t seem like an appropriate time, so I decided to postpone that duty for a few more days.<br /> <br /> Missy and Jane joined us outside eventually (Trinh had already been watching), having apparently been driven out of the house by Marguerite\u2019s Christmas spirit. \u201cShe kept trying to hug us,\u201d Missy said, looking vaguely embarrassed.<br /> <br /> \u201cIs that a problem?\u201d I asked as I caught my breath.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell\u2026 she\u2019s a cat,\u201d Missy elaborated, not meeting my eyes.<br /> <br /> \u201cMissy,\u201d I said, gently pushing up on her chin until we were face-to-face, \u201cshe\u2019s not a cat. And you\u2019re not a bird. Right?\u201d<br /> <br /> Missy sighed. \u201cYeah, I know,\u201d she allowed. \u201cIt\u2019s just\u2026 instincts, you know?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know,\u201d I said, \u201cit\u2019ll take time. But Marguerite loves me, and she knows how important you two are to me. She\u2019ll never do anything to hurt you, and will do whatever she can to protect you. I swear.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay,\u201d she smiled. \u201cI believe you, Jules. Like you said, it\u2019ll just take some time.\u201d<br /> <br /> After we\u2019d all gotten cleaned up, Marguerite cornered us in the theater as a group. \u201cWe shall go out for the caroling tonight, non?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> Most of us allowed as how the caroling would be delightful, but Jacob and Luna held out against the jolly Christmas tradition. For a while. Because unlike last year, Marguerite\u2019s childlike glee was eventually able to wear down even Ebenezer Khrushchev, and he agreed to come out and have some fun with us. Once we\u2019d scored the Russian vote, Luna wasn\u2019t far behind. And I even managed to convince Missy and Jane to join us!<br /> <br /> As soon as the sun went down we hit the road. We caroled at the homes of several of our friends, including Dad, Elena and Stasia, Felicity, and Joan and Andromeda. We also hit a few Freehold fixtures, like the Lighthouse and Augustine\u2019s church. I didn\u2019t spend any glamour or put too much into my performance; it was all about having fun and spreading the spirit of the season, not about inspiring desire or harvesting glamour. Most of my friends seemed to be on the same wavelength. Jacob has a surprisingly pleasant baritone singing voice, by the way. Julia mostly demurred, speak-singing so as not to activate the powers inherent in her voice.<br /> <br /> But the real surprise came when Missy and Jane started to get into it. It\u2026 it was like we\u2019d never been apart, and it was <u><u>powerful</u></u>. The three of us fell into easy harmonies, and our voices complemented each other beautifully. The two of them mostly backed me up last night, but I think that\u2019s just because they were still reluctant to take center stage themselves (so to speak). The first time it happened, our other friends just sort of stopped and stared for a few minutes, and I could tell that they were all thinking the same thing I was\u2026 how long before we can get those two on our stage?<br /> <br /> The only little spikes of negativity came when some well-meaning audience member requested an encore. It happened twice, and both times I just sort of launched into whatever song they had asked for without preamble. The others were good about covering it up, but it was unsettling to have my frailty laid bare during what was otherwise a very pleasant experience. I tried not to let it spoil my evening.<br /> <br /> When we\u2019d tired ourselves out we headed back to the Dream House. We gathered in the theater for about an hour, sipping hot chocolate and chatting softly near the big tree Kimberly had set up in there. At one point, Julia got up on the stage and started <u><u>really</u></u> singing. I got that dreamy, floaty feeling, and the world seemed to recede while I listened to her hypnotic voice. Usually I can\u2019t remember much about her performances, but I took care to note the song this time\u2026 she sang \u201cSilent Night.\u201d As the song that led me out of Arcadia the second time, I think that particular carol will always resonate with me.<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay, everybody,\u201d I said when the conversation started to ebb, \u201ctime for all good boys and girls to be in bed.\u201d I glanced at the tree and the bare floor underneath it. \u201cLook, I know we missed most of the shopping season, and there\u2019s probably not going to be a lot of gift-giving in the morning. But I just wanted to say one thing while we\u2019re all gathered together like this.\u201d<br /> <br /> I looked over the faces of all of my closest friends. \u201cEveryone in this room has already given me the best gift I could possibly ask for,\u201d I said fervently, \u201cand I will never forget it. I love you all.\u201d I moved around the room, kissing each of them\u2026 some on the lips, some on the cheek or forehead as I deemed appropriate.<br /> <br /> \u201cSome of you,\u201d I said, letting my gaze linger on Marguerite, Julia, and especially my Maria, \u201chave given me even more than that\u2026 more than I could ever have asked for\u2026 more than anyone could possibly deserve. I am so grateful, so fortunate\u2026 and I swear that from now on I will do everything in my power to make sure that you all feel as lucky as I do right now.\u201d<br /> <br /> There wasn\u2019t much to say after that, and we retired to bed. Maria, Julia, Marguerite and I retired to their bedroom, and sank into a warm mass beneath the covers. We kissed a bit and held each other until we all fell asleep, and stayed that way until late Christmas morning\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026which is now. For a wonder, I actually woke up before Marguerite, and I\u2019ve been letting the three of them sleep while I jot down my thoughts. I\u2019m taking a break from hitting the medical journals for the next few days; I figure I\u2019ll have more than enough studying to do once the semester starts up in January. And honestly\u2026 that tangle of limbs under the sheet over there is looking more and more inviting the longer I sit here writing.<br /> <br /> Ah, hell with it. I\u2019m going back to bed for a while. Merry Christmas!<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei de la Rocha</b></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T02:20:30-07:00","id":1220475,"title":"","content":"<b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> Friday, December 25<sup>th</sup><br /> Eight years, five months, twenty-eight days<br /> Days without Stabbing: 5<br /> <br /> It\u2019s Christmas and everything is going well, which has me nervous and on edge. I can\u2019t help but recall how perfect everything felt this time last year and how hard and fast it all went to shit. But Becky is here, asleep in my bed. I\u2019m watching her as I write this. The peaceful expression\u2026 the way her hair ripples and shifts about\u2026 She\u2019s beautiful. She came last night to be here to spend Christmas with me. While we were gone she spent her time training Angela to take up her duties so she could do things like this. So she could be with me. So we could be together. She whisked me away to a rented beach house Tuesday and we spent the day together, just the two of us. No court duties for her. No mysteries or rescues or drama for me. Just us alone together talking and laughing and while we didn\u2019t spend all (or even most) of our time fucking we barely let go of one another. Holding hands or kissing or even just sitting close together. And even once we returned, we\u2019ve been doing it. I didn\u2019t know she was coming over last night but when she showed up it made me almost burst into tears of relief to not sleep alone. I think she can tell I\u2019m dealing with the ghosts of last year and has been trying to make sure I know she\u2019s here and not going anywhere. But it\u2019s not just about me. To her, I was gone half a year and while she hasn\u2019t outright said it I\u2019m pretty sure she was worried I wouldn\u2019t come back.<br /> <br /> And let\u2019s face it, I almost didn\u2019t. Throwing myself into Ocras\u2019 path was damned effective but damned reckless. And I didn\u2019t even hesitate. To be fair, I was expecting a broken arm not a nearly fatal plummet. But I was fully expecting to be injured and it didn\u2019t even give me pause. Even as it was happening, as I felt my arm shatter and the impact ripped me loose from the rafters and the pair of us started to fall all I felt was a savage glee at the startled cry of pain and the glimpse of fear in her eyes before we hit the ground. It wasn\u2019t until we were traveling back through the hedge that it even hit me that in my zeal to murder Ocras I\u2019d broken my promise to Stasia and Becky to be careful.<br /> <br /> And now I am back and I can\u2019t stop thinking about what would have happened if Luna hadn\u2019t been there to tend my wounds and fly me out. Or if Lori hadn\u2019t been such a skilled healer that she could put my Humpty Dumpty ass back together again. Who would have drawn the short straw and been the one who had to tell Becky? Or Stasia? How could I so carelessly risk hurting them? Dr Emmett seems to think that being aware of this unhealthy lack of concern over my well-being is progress. Admitting something is wrong is the first step to fixing it and all. I don\u2019t know about that but I do know that I have to do something before my dumb luck runs out. So yeah, looks like I\u2019m not done with Dr Emmett and the clinic just yet.<br /> <br /> And as always there are far more important things going on than my whining and navel-gazing. Stasia proposed to Elena upon our return. It\u2026 seeing her... Seeing the way she looked at Elena as she brought out the ring\u2026 She\u2019s found her princess. Maybe if things had been different it would have been me. But They took me and the Sinister Bitch betrayed her. I\u2019m just glad she was wrong about not being able to love again.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, it\u2019s not all happy. Elena took Stasia with her to Thanksgiving with her parents and they were apparently not okay with her dating a woman. Seems Jacob\u2019s fetch was particularly toxic and nearly came to blows with Stasia which I have no doubt would have earned him an ass beating had Elena\u2019s parent\u2019s not threatened to call the police if Stasia did not leave. And then they issued an ultimatum that if Elena left with Stasia she wouldn\u2019t be welcome to return. Jacob is furious with the Little Shit for taking a bad situation and making it worse. He was seriously considering sending the Little Shit back to his maker but I dissuaded him from what the Lady would likely consider an insult at best and a declaration of war at worst. Better to just deal with him ourselves. However, as soon as we started to discuss how it came up that Jacob has avoided his fetch (for obvious reasons) and doesn\u2019t know that much about the Little Shit or his routine. I offered to spy for him since I won\u2019t set the Little Shit off the way Jacob would. And that gave me an idea. I have put off dealing with the Sinister Bitch for much the same reason. So I suggested that we strangers on a train this shit (yeah, I know it\u2019s not exactly how it works but it\u2019s my damn metaphor) So while I\u2019m scoping out the Little Shit he\u2019s going to do likewise on the Sinister Bitch and then we\u2019ll figure out what to do about them both.<br /> <br /> The hitch is that the Little Shit lives with Jacob\u2019s folks in Portland, which is a bit of travel time. So I\u2019ve spoken to Marguerite and she\u2019s agreed to use mirror travel to get me there provided I\u2019m spying and not murdering. Which I agreed to. This is Jacob\u2019s kill and I\u2019m not going to steal it from him.<br /> <br /> But before we can start that we've got Jacob and Elena\u2019s birthday camping trip. Seems like it\u2019s working on becoming a tradition. I know Jacob\u2019s planning to make it snow again, but I guess Stasia won\u2019t have to sneak into Elena\u2019s tent this year. I believe we\u2019ll have Lori\u2019s friends with us and Beautiful has agreed to come along. Hopefully she won\u2019t be too disappointed that we\u2019ll be the only ones without an air mattress though I am sure I can find some way to make it up to her\u2026<br /> <br /> And at some point I\u2019m supposed to meet her fetch. I knew that she was on good terms with her but apparently it\u2019s more than I (or almost anyone else) realized. Apparently shortly after her return Beautiful went to kill her fetch but she pleaded for my dragon to spare her husband and adopted daughter. That gave Beautiful pause and she did some deep desire reading and found her fetch wasn\u2019t aware of what she was or the Gentry or anything of that sort and so she ended up sparing her. And apparently since then her fetch has developed a few interesting and very useful abilities (in particular the ability to make duplicates) that she uses for Beautiful in exchange for being protected. I\u2019m one of only a handful that know about it. She\u2019s entrusted me with one of her most important secrets. She\u2019s\u2026 really serious about this. And that makes me so fucking happy\u2026 And so fucking terrified that I\u2019m going to fuck it all up.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Becky and Calamity came back this morning just in time to have blueberry pancakes with the rest of us. Lori was cooking while I, as usual, was making coffee for everyone. Or whatever drink they wanted. Sometimes someone will ask for tea. While we were all enjoying our breakfast, I brought up the idea of going camping this upcoming weekend to celebrate me and Elena\u2019s birthday. It was a hit last year so figured it would be appreciated this year. Everyone readily agreed, even Jane and Missy seemed interested. I assured them that I would get camping gear for them. I figured that I\u2019d get a tent that is designed for four or more people so it will have a bigger opening and more room to accommodate their wings. Trinh also expressed an interest in coming so I assured her as well that we\u2019d get a tent and sleeping bag for her. She seemed a little reluctant to have someone buy her gear, but I assured her that if she didn\u2019t want to keep it then it would get used by our motley in the future.<br /> <br /> After that we talked a bit about our trip to Arcadia. I think some folks got to hear some parts of the story that they hadn\u2019t heard before. Then to change the topic, I think, Lori brought up the idea of having Missy, Jane and Trinh try gliding off of the roof. Trinh didn\u2019t want to jump off the roof or balcony so I suggested that they start with taking a running leap off of the backyard stage. It\u2019s high enough off the ground that they should be able to get a little bit of air. So we all went out back and the three new girls took turns jumping off the stage. Missy and Jane picked it up pretty fast. Trinh took a little more time to get it, but she eventually did. I think she just wasn\u2019t as used to the idea of having wings as the other two were. They all thought that was fun so I\u2019m going to count that as a success. My assumption is that Lori suggested that so the girls, especially Missy and Jane, would have something fun to associate with \u2018the world.\u2019<br /> <br /> While all of that was going on Calamity approached and asked why I was in a bad mood. I guess I was projecting more than I intended to, or she\u2019s just gotten better at reading me. I told her what happened with my sister and Stasia at Thanksgiving and admitted that I was angry at the \u201clittle shit\u201d for doing what he did. I admitted that I had thought of the idea of taking him back to the Lady\u2019s realm to return him to his maker. I also acknowledged that my idea might not be a good one since it would draw the Lady\u2019s attention my way and I don\u2019t want that. The longer she forgets that I exist the better things are for me. So, Calamity and I talked over our options. I suggested that we get an idea of what the \u201clittle shit\u2019s\u201d routine is, but I can\u2019t do it since he would react to my presence. Calamity said that she could follow him around and we could find a way to lure him away from the house and his friends. Then we could do whatever we wanted to him. I think it was implied that we\u2019d kill him, but I suppose that just scaring him might also be a viable option. I don\u2019t know which one I\u2019d prefer at this exact moment. I will admit that I have resented him for a long time now. How dare that parody of a human being take over my life? Then I try to remind myself that I wouldn\u2019t have been able to take my life back anyway. I look too old now to be able to assume my old role in the family.<br /> <br /> After we had discussed what to do with my fetch Calamity admitted that she was also curious to see what her own fetch was up to and find out what kind of person she is. She calls her fetch the \u201csinister bitch.\u201d I think I remember Calamity saying something about her fetch being left handed and she was right handed, hence the name. It does make me wonder how observant her parents were if they didn\u2019t even notice that their only daughter suddenly started writing with the opposite hand. So, we came up with the idea that Calamity could spy on my fetch and I could spy on hers. I\u2019m not sure if Calamity has it in mind to kill her fetch or not. I agreed to tail her though and find out what kind of person she is. I did not agree to go further than that as of right now. Who knows, maybe she is a decent person.<br /> <br /> It is a really long drive between here and Portland so Calamity asked Insincere Marguerite about using her mirror power to get her closer to Oregon. Marguerite asked what she wanted to do and Calamity explained that she wanted to trail my fetch and get an idea of his schedule and what kind of person he is. She assured Insincere Marguerite that she had no intentions of harming the fetch at this time. Marguerite agreed, but stated that it would have to wait until after the holidays. I suppose that\u2019s fair. Insincere Marguerite loves this time of year and is not going to want to miss anything for an errand, especially if that errand would take her away from town for an extended period of time. Plus, there\u2019s the fact that I think that she didn\u2019t want to hurt anyone at Christmas time. Or plan to.<br /> <br /> Once everyone had their fill of gliding around the backyard Monica took the three newbies out to see the important sites of the Freehold. Like the different monarchs, the clubs, etc...and to get some clothes of their own. They were only back for a relatively short time when Lori suggested that they go out to the place where she gets her outfits altered to accommodate her wings. They came back with a fancy new dress each and their new shirts augmented with holes for their wings. I guess Lori decided to take them out for something special as well. They were all chatting and smiling when they got back so I\u2019ll call that little outing a success too.<br /> <br /> The last show of the year went rather well. Our lovely ladies pulled out a couple of numbers that they did at the end of last year, but they were no less popular this time around. Insincere Marguerite and Lori did their duet of \u201cBaby it\u2019s Cold Outside,\u201d then Lori and Calamity did \u201cBloody Creature Poster Girl,\u201d and then each lady did one song of their own. For my part I was holding down the fort at the bar. I talked to Hailey for a bit before taking Molly aside to discuss things with her. I wanted to know how her tailing job went. It turns out that the fetch of Trinh Jackson is paranoid but doesn\u2019t know who or what is after her. She is convinced that someone or something is though. She\u2019s even gone so far as to take up with friends of her ex-boyfriend who have criminal connections and guns. She\u2019s got them keeping an eye out for her. Right now Jackson is at a high level of awareness and is running mostly on adrenaline. Molly suggested that we wait until she crashes from that high and talk to her after she has exhausted herself. After that we can set up a meeting between Trinh and her fetch.<br /> <br /> While I was talking to Molly I also asked her for some tips or tricks of the trade that she might be able to share with me. She didn\u2019t ask why I wanted to know how to tail people unseen, she just gave me some suggestions and tips. She suggested learning a contract called Contract of Mirrors, which ironically has nothing to do with mirrors. With enough practice you can change your face to look like that of someone else. It also takes less effort if you have a small token from the person you want to look like. Something like pocket change from their dresser, a paperclip from their office, something small like that. It also helps to have a nondescript car. That unfortunately rules my jeep out. They tend to stand out on the road given that they are normally taller than most other vehicles on the road. I may have to see if I can borrow Molly\u2019s car when I follow Calamity\u2019s fetch around. We\u2019ll see.<br /> <br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> And then there was therapy. For everyone it seems. De la Rocha, Calamity and I left for our sessions pretty early. Calamity asked De la Rocha if she had talked to Madame Spidertoes yet, since apparently the elder Changeling has been looking for Maria since we got back. De la Rocha said that she hadn\u2019t but would soon. And then I got to talk to Sullivan. I did my best to reassure him that everything had gone well in the Hedge and in Arcadia. I again left out the bit about Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Keeper leaving a bag of goodies for her in the Hedge. I know that Marguerite is not actively serving Mama Lion, but some others that don\u2019t know her very well might make assumptions. I didn\u2019t want my motley mate to get in trouble for something she had no control over. I don\u2019t think Sullivan was very impressed by how many guards I took out while we were making our escape. I think he thought that was a step backwards for me. At least he made notes about it and asked how I felt after killing those men. To be honest I didn\u2019t really feel much of anything. I told him that I was relieved that I was alive, and tried to give him the impression that it was completely a matter of kill or be killed. That wasn\u2019t untrue. It was kill or be killed. I suppose that I could have tried to go for incapacitating the guards instead of killing them, but to be honest it was just easier to go for the killing blow and look for the next target. That way I didn\u2019t have to slow down and make sure that I hit non-vital spots. When fighting them if they didn\u2019t fall down I knew that I had to hit them again, somewhere more fatal. I didn\u2019t have to worry about getting a knife in the back from a downed but still alive guard. And again, I didn\u2019t explain all of that to Sullivan, I just played up the survival aspect of the situation and tried to get his attention on the awesome throw that Luna did with that spiderbomb. Chucking it right at the foot of a Gentry was a gutsy thing to do. I love my Luna.<br /> <br /> Anyway, as we were leaving therapy Lori, Missy and Jane were just arriving for theirs. Apparently Lori had talked to Lowjack or someone at the clinic and set up an appointment for her two friends. It just so happened that their appointment was right after ours. Calamity and I said our \u201chellos\u201d and headed back to the Dream House. De la Rocha said that she was going to wait for Lori and the others. She had plans to hang out with Twitch. I am happy that Maria is finding closure by working with him and interacting in a normal way, instead of feeling like she should be tracking him down. What I\u2019m not happy about is that Twitch is enjoying himself while they talk. I was happier when he was just terrified all the time. It served him right for all the shitty things that he did to people. He should be worried about retribution.<br /> <br /> After leaving the Clinic we headed back for the House. Then we set to making breakfast for everyone. We had crepes this time. Julia\u2019s suggestion. I again made the coffee, and acted as a gofer getting whatever Calamity needed out of the fridge. I figured that I might as well do something to help with the food. Making coffee doesn\u2019t take much effort. Food and coffee was enjoyed by all. Then once White Maria and Brightstar had left I brought up information that I got about Trinh\u2019s fetch, and Molly\u2019s idea to wait a bit until she\u2019s tried and then we can try to set up a meeting. I assured her that we would have someone there that is good at talking and negotiations as well as someone there that is capable of keeping her safe. I figured Lori would do the talking but didn\u2019t want to promise her presence before I\u2019d gone over the idea with my motley mate. I figured Calamity and I would provide the protection just in case things go pear shaped.<br /> <br /> Lori, Missy and Jane all went to Lori\u2019s dad\u2019s house for lunch after leaving their therapy session. I guess things went better than Missy and Jane feared that they would. I think they were afraid that he was going to be the harsh man that he was 30+ years ago, but he\u2019s apparently mellowed a lot since then. He seems like a very friendly, tolerant man to me. He is keen on helping Changelings where he can, and I\u2019m sure that he\u2019s interested in helping Lori\u2019s childhood friends reacclimate to \u2018the world.\u2019 So, after they got back from lunch Lori joined Calamity, Luna and myself for some sparring. We started out before Lori got back since we don\u2019t have to hold back when it\u2019s just the three of us. We can go all out and not have to worry about hurting anyone else. Once Lori joined us we switched to hand to hand training and slowed things down a bit so she could see the moves that we were doing. Then we showed her how to do them. It was fun. Trinh watched. I think she enjoyed herself. I was a little surprised that De la Rocha didn\u2019t join us, but apparently, she went to go meet up with Madame Spidertoes. Towards the end even Missy and Jane came outside. I don\u2019t think they initially came out to watch though. I think they were trying to avoid getting hugged by Insincere Marguerite.<br /> <br /> After sparring Lori told us that the therapy went pretty well. She admitted that the counselors at the Clinic thought that Missy and Jane might be tempted to run back to the Hedge so they were fitted with tracking anklets so we\u2019ll know if they leave the freehold. Lori then told us all about the app that we needed to download so we could keep track of the two newbies. We got that done in short order. She also mentioned that Doctor Bright prescribed a mild sedative to help Missy with any anxiety attacks that she might have. It seems that she in particular is afraid of open spaces. After having been kept in a cage for a while I can understand that.<br /> <br /> Calamity informed the group of something that happened a while ago, like years ago, but was getting attention again. Apparently Dark Kimberly\u2019s fetch was killed before she got back from Arcadia. And not in an innocent \u201cit was all an accident\u201d kind of way. She was tied up and brutally murdered. Dark Kimberly has been looking into it since it happened, but there\u2019s only so much that she can do since she looks just like her fetch and it could cause some problems if she were seen. The motley expressed an interest in helping her find out who killed her fetch. I suggested that we should acquire the help of someone that speaks the language just in case we need a translator. I\u2019m not sure who we\u2019d get, but the list isn\u2019t that long.<br /> <br /> And to finish out the day the whole lot of us, me and Luna included, went out to sing Christmas carols. I was initially going to turn down the offer to sing, stating that I\u2019m not a good singer, but Marguerite pleaded with me until I gave in and agreed. It wasn\u2019t long after I caved that Luna said she\u2019d come too. We went to a bunch of our friends or family\u2019s places, which was good. I don\u2019t like singing in front of strangers. I hated chorus when I was in Middle School and everyone had to participate. At least when we go to High School we got to choose our electives and that wasn\u2019t one of them for me. I may not have liked it because back then my English was not all that great and I had a thick accent.<br /> <br /> Then after we got home we got a special treat. Julia got up on stage and sang \u201cSilent Night\u201d to the motley. It was kind of haunting, but beautiful. She really does have a great voice. I counted that as a Christmas present to the rest of us. None of us had time to shop for presents, so there\u2019s not going to be a lot of unwrapping going on this year. I guess we\u2019ll just do little things here and there for each other in place of traditional gifts. Merry Christmas!<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CVIII</i><br /> <br /> If you are playing along at home, in addition to the duets Calamity did \u201cMistress for Christmas\u201d and Insincere Marguerite did \u201cWinter Weather\u201d<br /> <br /> It was largely skimmed over (Though Jacob dedicated a paragraph to it and Lori touched on it) that the murder of Kimberly\u2019s Fetch came up. When she returned she could not take back her life because her fetch had been found dead in the truck of a car with hands and feet bound and eventually, slowly choked on a gag and tie around her neck. Dark Kimberly referred to being murdering her in the first person \u201cI am trying to find the people who murdered me\u201d and clearly took it personally, since her fetch seemed a lot like her. As a result she left LA and changed her appearance, eventually becoming a Goth. She still wants to find who murdered \u201cher\u201d and spoke to Calamity and Lori, and Calamity filled in the group.<br /> <br /> I think that covers everything but comments and questions are welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 05-20-2018, 05:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T15:10:18-07:00","id":1220632,"title":"","content":"Thank you so much for finally making &quot;Changelings have to have custom clothes that still don't look too weird&quot; canon in your game. I do wonder how Calamity deals with the glass spikes when she doesn't want to retract them. Does she just wear ripped clothing and play it off as a punk/goth style choice?<br /> <br /> Also, glad to see all the new plot hooks going on, even though it can't be long before we get a reprisal from the Empress (that's her name, right) or a visit from Mama Lion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T00:27:05-07:00","id":1220748,"title":"","content":"Well, while it doesn't tend to come up in the journals, Lori tailoring clothes to fit her wings has been mentioned fairly often in game. As for Calamity, she tends to perform in corsets or sleeveless off the shoulder dresses and wear similarly sleeveless halter necked blouses or short sleeved business casual with open shoulders. When she's dressing down she does tend to simply go with the ripped tee/jacket. In general she goes through clothing (much the same as bedding) and just replaces things as they're damaged. For instance, I know there was a journal where she decided to wear a lacy nightie for Gawain and mentioned the fact that she was only going to be able to wear it the once since it would be ruined by her glass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T07:46:14-07:00","id":1220830,"title":"","content":"We have discussed this issue as a gaming group a few times over the years, and I believe the general consensus goes something like this:<br /> <br /> The Mask affects clothing that's <i>currently</i> <i>being worn</i> by changelings, but does not affect other clothes in their collection. Someone looking at Lorelei when she's wearing a t-shirt for instance would not notice the two slits cut in the back of the shirt to accommodate her wings; just as the Wyrd edits the wings themselves out of the onlookers' consciousness, it takes care of minor details of that sort that would make her stand out as odd or unnatural. However, if someone came across Lori's laundry basket and started going through her things (eww, get out of there you pervert!), they might wonder about the holes in the backs of all her tops, which could lead to awkward questions. And though it's never come up, I assume that if such a person were to see Lori wearing one of those tops <i>again</i>, they might see the slits cut in the back because they're <i>expecting</i> to see them.<br /> <br /> As always thanks for reading and commenting. I'm already hard at work on Lori's journal for last night's session, in which no bears were harmed.<br /> <br /> P.S. - Yes, Lori's Keeper is known as the Violet Empress, often abbreviated simply as &quot;the Empress.&quot; :-) In character, we're all sort of hoping Marguerite's Gentrified Bearing merit will put her off our scent... since the Empress never actually saw Lorelei during the rescue mission, maybe she'll assume that the thief was actually Mama Lion (who is known for such raids) or something like that. Out of character, I'm sure it won't be long before someone remembers that we <i>did</i> leave a direct witness to the rescue behind... though Lori will never admit it, we <i>really</i> should have killed Hunting Hawk when we had the chance...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T11:23:16-07:00","id":1220883,"title":"","content":"It looks like my players have already answered this better than I could. ^_^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T12:53:51-07:00","id":1224419,"title":"","content":"Christmas Day and Camping this time with your friends from the Malibu Dream House. But the new guests find some of the things around the house a bit\u2026unusual.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CIX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Mmmmm\u2026 I woke up this morning as part of an achy, uncomfortable, sweaty pile of body parts, with three people (and two slightly crushed wings) jammed into two zipped-together sleeping bags. The sleeping bag and tent were designed to help stave off the chilly wilderness nights\u2026 which meant we were stewing in our own juices in the ever-present 76 degree heat of Southern California.<br /> <br /> Like I said\u2026 Mmmmm. A girl could get used to this!<br /> <br /> So Christmas morning dawned somewhat earlier than most of us are used to in the Dream House, as we were all serenaded by the dulcet tones of Christmas carols sung with a French accent drifting out of the vents. Yes, Marguerite had decided that we had slept long enough, and was eager to get Christmas Day started. The lot of us headed down to Sex Breakfast with varying degrees of enthusiasm\u2026 but even the grumpiest and sleepiest among us had a noticeable undercurrent of good cheer. A few applications of Spring contracts later, and we were quite a merry bunch.<br /> <br /> Calamity got breakfast started as soon as we were all assembled. I moved to help her, but Missy and Jane headed me off and asked if they could speak with me privately for a few moments. Since they were both obviously nervous about something, I followed them into the theater.<br /> <br /> \u201cUmm, so\u2026\u201d Missy began, noticeably uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> Jane took over from that point\u2026 but oddly she seemed just as uneasy. \u201cSo, did you know there\u2019s some sort of altar in the attic?\u201d she asked after a moment.<br /> <br /> I chuckled and breathed a sigh of relief. \u201cYeah,\u201d I said, \u201cthat\u2019s Julia\u2019s. She\u2019s Wiccan\u2026 it\u2019s a Neo-Pagan religion based on venerating the Earth, sort of a druidic tradition that\u2026\u201d I trailed off at their blank looks.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo,\u201d Missy tried again, \u201cit\u2019s not a Satanic thing?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo!\u201d I said, a little shocked myself. \u201cIt\u2019s\u2026 it\u2019s just a different religion. She\u2019s not evil, I swear.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe saw some of her paintings, too,\u201d Jane admitted, \u201cthey\u2019re beautiful, but kind of disturbing That one with her and Marguerite holding pistols to each other\u2019s\u2019 heads\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I sighed. \u201cAt least you didn\u2019t see the one with the double hanging,\u201d I said with some resignation. The Goth movement was just getting started when we were Taken, but it hadn\u2019t made much headway in Defiance. \u201cLook, Julia\u2019s artistic sensibilities are a little morbid\u2026 it comes of being a darkling. But she\u2019s a good person at heart, just a little different. I swear.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cKay,\u201d Missy said with a watery grin. \u201cAnd\u2026 we also checked out the basement while we were looking around, and\u2026\u201d she didn\u2019t seem able to continue that thought.<br /> <br /> I sighed again, I couldn\u2019t help it. \u201cSo you found the playroom,\u201d I said. \u201cIt\u2019s not my thing, but some of the other girls really enjoy it.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jane\u2019s eyes widened. \u201cSo it\u2019s like a sex thing?\u201d she asked. A moment later she had a follow-up question. \u201cA <u><u>voluntary</u></u> sex thing?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course,\u201d I assured them. \u201cNobody uses those toys unless they want to be there. There are hidden release buttons I can show you if you want\u2026 that way nobody can ever use them against you in the future. No changeling would <u><u>ever</u></u> lock another up against their will\u2026 that\u2019s one of our most important rules.\u201d<br /> <br /> Once we had that straightened out, the three of us returned to the kitchen. I helped Calamity as much as I could with the cooking, and the two of us started planning for that evening\u2019s Christmas feast as well. There was a lot to do, and though we are lucky enough to live in a house with a fully-stocked larder and a commercial-grade kitchen, getting the timing down so that everything would be ready at the proper time took some serious scheduling. In the background I could hear Missy and Jane interrogating Julia about her religion (\u201cI don\u2019t believe in Satan, and even if I did, why would I want to summon him in my house?\u201d).<br /> <br /> D and Trinh entered the kitchen a short time later. My wife was showing off by firing small laser blasts from her fingers. Yes, that\u2019s right\u2026 I am married to a Latina woman who can shoot lasers from her fingers (I admonished her to be extra careful with this newfound skill, as those fingers frequently\u2026 well, you get the picture). Apparently it\u2019s some sort of Summer Court thing; I found out later that Gloria can do it too (although she is less likely than D to make cute little \u201cpew-pew\u201d sounds when she does it).<br /> <br /> Sex Breakfast conversation hit all sorts of topics, as usual. Marguerite\u2019s disdain for French Canadians came up <u><u>again</u></u>, and Trinh asked if this attitude extended to Cajuns (she\u2019s from Louisiana). Apparently it does not, as Marguerite feels that the Cajun people at least have the decency not to call themselves French. This got us talking about Cajun food, about which Trinh knows quite a lot. She\u2019s offered to help us prepare a Cajun meal one of these days, and to teach those of us who wish to learn how to prepare such meals for ourselves in the future. As a diligent Pilgrim I saw it as my duty to pick up this skill if I can.<br /> <br /> Plus\u2026 red beans and rice, Andouille sausage, jambalaya, gumbo\u2026 yum!<br /> <br /> The question of frailties came up at some point as well, and had to be explained to Missy, Jane, and Trinh. They took the information in stride\u2026 I think they\u2019re all really starting to get a handle on this changeling thing. I wish I\u2019d had someone to guide me through the growing pains in those early days. We discussed a few of our own minor frailties, and warned them that knowingly exploiting another changeling\u2019s frailty is considered almost unspeakably rude. They all solemnly promised not to ask me to sing anything, knowingly break glass in front of Calamity, give Jacob anything hot to drink, etc.<br /> <br /> I\u2026 didn\u2019t talk about my other frailty. I don\u2019t even like to think about it, honestly. And hey\u2026 D still claims that she <u><u>has</u></u> no frailties of which she\u2019s aware, which I know deep down is a crock. But I suppose I can\u2019t blame her\u2026 frailties tend to be very personal and somewhat disturbing. I don\u2019t like talking about mine either. And hell, D still hasn\u2019t told any of the others when her <u><u>birthday</u></u> is, for crying out loud\u2026 I only know because it came up when we were doing to paperwork to put our marriage through.<br /> <br /> So in the course of our discussion about frailties, our little jaunt to Disneyland came up. The girls are now fully aware of the reasons for my eternal feud with Goofy, which the rest of the motley can\u2019t seem to help bringing up from time to time. I laughed it off with everyone else, telling Calamity that she should take a cue from Jacob and learn how to \u201cLet It Go.\u201d That got a laugh from most of those assembled, but had to be explained to the newcomers.<br /> <br /> We whiled away about twenty minutes outside after breakfast. I flew up to the roof and tossed a few clay targets in the air so that D could shoot them down with her finger lasers. Yes, I just wrote that sentence in my diary. Aside from the question of finger lasers, I thought to wonder aloud why we have a supply of clay targets at the Dream House, but nobody could satisfactorily answer that question, so I let it pass after a while.<br /> <br /> Most of the rest of the afternoon was devoted to preparing a Christmas feast which will not be soon forgotten. We had a turkey, we had a ham, we had roast beef (I took up my old habit of referring to the latter as \u201croast beast,\u201d which had Calamity calling me Cindy Lou all afternoon, but whatever), and that\u2019s just the main courses. Sweet potato casserole, mashed potatoes, cranberry sauce, mixed vegetables\u2026 we really covered all the bases this time. And for a wonder we actually seemed to schedule the cooking so that everything was ready at approximately the right time!<br /> <br /> We had a few other people over for dinner, aside from those currently living in the house. Becky stuck around, of course, and Stasia and Elena stopped by to spend the evening with us as well. Gloria came by too, since she hasn\u2019t yet been able to reconnect with her mortal family. Oleander dropped by for dinner, but she was still mildly toxic, so we had to content ourselves with chaste Christmas hugs and air-kisses.<br /> <br /> Conversation was lively, and ranged all over the place, from cyber-security to Goth Day at Disneyland to the torture chamber in our basement. Turns out Stasia and Elena know about that\u2026 Calamity gave Stasia a key before we left for Arcadia, and it was strongly implied that the two of them had\u2026 \u201cenjoyed\u201d the accoutrements of that room on more than one occasion. You could color me shocked at the time (no offense, but Elena seems kind of vanilla about such things at first glance), but after certain other facts came to light the next day\u2026 but I\u2019m getting ahead of myself.<br /> <br /> Dinner came out well, and was enjoyed by all. Afterward most of us gathered in the theater for a little karaoke (Oleander had to leave, unfortunately). D asked if there was anything I\u2019d like to hear her sing, and I asked her to sing me anything by the Beatles. She got this look in her eye\u2026<br /> <br /> \u201cAnything with a <u><u>melody</u></u>,\u201d I specified. \u201cNo \u2018Revolution 9\u2019 or \u2018Wild Honey Pie\u2019 or anything like that, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> She grinned and bore it, and when her turn came up she gave a fair rendition of \u201cCome Together.\u201d I know it\u2019s not her kind of music, so I made sure to show my appreciation once she\u2019d finished with a big hug and kiss. \u201cAnything you\u2019d like to hear me sing?\u201d I asked, figuring fair was fair. \u201cAnything at all?\u201d<br /> <br /> She settled on a song I\u2019d never heard of called \u201cPunk Rock Girl\u201d by the Dead Milkmen, and carefully phrased the suggestion in such a way that I wouldn\u2019t be compelled to sing it or anything unpleasant like that. It\u2019s\u2026 well, it\u2019s not really to my taste at all, but like I said, turnabout is fair play.<br /> <br /> There were a few other standout performances. Jacob did a nice tenor rendition of a Russian Christmas song for us, which proves that he can get into the spirit of the holiday when backed into a corner. I performed \u201cLet It Go\u201d for Missy, Jane, and Trinh\u2019s benefit, since they had expressed an interest after my earlier reference to the Disney song. I got Missy and Jane up on stage with me to show off our harmonic chops with Three Dog Night\u2019s \u201cOld Fashioned Love Song,\u201d and it went over like a house on fire. Trinh strutted her stuff with Paula Abdul\u2019s \u201cStraight Up,\u201d and Marguerite sang her own take on the Brenda Lee holiday classic \u201cRockin\u2019 Around the Christmas Tree.\u201d Finally, Gloria belted out a power ballad from the 80s called \u201cEvery Rose Has Its Thorn.\u201d<br /> <br /> Oh, I should also mention that Calamity surprised us all with a soulful rendition of \u201cWe\u2019re All Alone,\u201d a song I\u2019ve performed for audiences at the Dream House before. The reason I single it out as noteworthy is that she sang it at Becky\u2019s request, and the song seemed to have some significance to our dear claviger. Though I\u2019d never point it out aloud to either of them, I found this very sweet. What can I say? I\u2019m a romantic at heart.<br /> <br /> And so the evening wore on, with music and food and wine and pleasant conversation. As it got later, people started drifting off to bed, realizing that we\u2019d need to get up early the next morning to head out for our camping trip. I glanced over at D to see what her intentions were, and she threw me a smile, and then turned to Gloria. \u201cSo,\u201d she asked her girlfriend with suppressed mirth, \u201cis tonight the night?\u201d<br /> <br /> Gloria looked at me, swallowed, smiled, and nodded. \u201cI think it might be,\u201d she said hesitantly.<br /> <br /> D headed to the kitchen for a bottle of chardonnay. Gloria couldn\u2019t seem to meet my eyes in the meantime. \u201cIs this\u2026 I mean, do you really want this, Lori?\u201d she asked me after a moment.<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cIf you\u2019re sure this won\u2019t come between you and D... and won\u2019t adversely affect our friendship, then there\u2019s nothing I\u2019d like more. Hell, I\u2019ve thought you were hot ever since I saw you pinned to the wall on your first night here\u2026\u201d Her smile grew a little more genuine at that, but I could tell that she was still a little tense.<br /> <br /> D got back a moment later, and the three of us headed up to the boudoir. Our lovemaking fell into a pattern wherein two of us concentrated on bringing pleasure to the third. Maria knows me well enough that she put me in the hot-seat first, and\u2026 wow. Those two are both really strong. Gloria\u2019s not as strong as Maria is, but she\u2019s still <u><u>really</u></u> strong. They were gentle with me, and always made sure that I was where I needed to be, if you know what I mean, but I could feel the strength in their muscles the whole time, like steel hiding under silk.<br /> <br /> Gloria got to be the center of attention next. D and I have a lot of experience working together in that way, and we make a great team if I do say so myself. Plus, as much as I like being the center of attention, I must also admit that I enjoy showing off my skills. I think Gloria appreciated my efforts, based upon her reactions. And D knows her well enough by now to give me a few pointers about the things she particularly likes, so we had that going for us too.<br /> <br /> Finally, Gloria and I saw to D\u2019s needs. We didn\u2019t try anything fancy; we just let her know in no uncertain terms that she was surrounded by girls who loved her. The evening ended with all three of us sweating and breathless, Gloria and I looking fondly at each other across D\u2019s upper chest as she wrapped her strong arms around the two of us.<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you,\u201d I whispered once things had calmed down. \u201cThank you both so much for sharing this with me. You\u2019ve made me feel so special\u2026 you\u2019ve made me so happy.\u201d They both expressed similar thoughts, and we started to drift off. I closed my eyes as I said the last two words I wanted to say that evening: \u201cMerry Christmas.\u201d<br /> <br /> We woke up earlier than usual (again) the next morning, and headed down to breakfast. Things were a little less rambunctious than usual, as we were busy preparing for our trip into the mountains, but a few barbs and double entendres still slipped in here and there. Most notably, Trinh \u2013 who is currently using the basement guest room \u2013 made a few pointed comments indicating that Stasia and Elena might have made use of the \u201ctorture dungeon\u201d last night, and that she might have overheard a bit of their play. Elena was so embarrassed by this talk that she slipped under the table to avoid the stares.<br /> <br /> Sudden inspiration struck as we were talking excitedly about that day\u2019s camping trip. \u201cHey, Gloria,\u201d I said with animation, \u201care you doing anything today? You want to come with us?\u201d<br /> <br /> She looked surprised to be asked, but pleased. \u201cIt sounds like fun, if you\u2019re sure it won\u2019t be too much trouble.\u201d<br /> <br /> I glanced at D. \u201cNo trouble at all,\u201d I said, \u201cexcept that we won\u2019t have enough tents\u2026 unless you\u2019d like to share with me and D. It\u2019ll be cramped, but I\u2019m sure we could squeeze you in.\u201d<br /> <br /> D nodded enthusiastically. \u201cWe can work it out,\u201d she agreed.<br /> <br /> Gloria chuckled. \u201cOkay then, I\u2019m sold. We can even take my car if you want, since there\u2019ll be like fourteen of us.\u201d<br /> <br /> It turned out to be sort of a stroke of luck, actually, as Gloria\u2019s SUV proved <u><u>really</u></u> useful in transporting not only the fourteen of us, but all of our luggage and equipment. Gloria, Maria, Missy, Jane, and I ended up in the SUV. Calamity, Becky, Trinh, Marguerite, and Julia took the van. Jacob, Luna, Elena and Stasia piled into Jacob\u2019s jeep. Twenty minutes after breakfast was done, we were on the road.<br /> <br /> The trip was largely uneventful; I found myself singing along with Gloria\u2019s 80s radio station more often than not, chatting with Missy and Jane, and looking at the beautiful Southern California scenery out of the windows. At one point I got a text from Julia. Apparently Trinh\u2019s continued gentle teasing of Stasia and Elena now indicated that \u2013 contrary to preconceived notions \u2013 it was actually <u><u>Stasia</u></u> who was bound to the St. Andrew\u2019s Cross while Elena held the crop. It\u2019s always the quiet ones\u2026<br /> <br /> So a couple of hours later we pulled into the park and started unloading the vehicles. Backpacks have been\u2026 tricky for me since my return from Arcadia; they\u2019re never comfortable and I have to be very careful to avoid pulling out feathers when I\u2019m wearing them. I commented on this, and D offered to carry my gear. I tried to refuse her (we had three other girls with wings in the same boat after all), but she wouldn\u2019t hear of it once the idea entered her mind.<br /> <br /> The hike itself was fun; nothing strenuous, just a pleasant nature walk. I spoke with several of the local birds, who seemed happy enough. Jacob told me to warn them that he was going to make it snow later that night, and I tried, but\u2026 y\u2019know, they\u2019re <u><u>birds</u></u>. I doubt they remembered the warning for more than a few minutes. Marguerite slipped on and off the path, walking nimbly on <u><u>top</u></u> of the soft carpet of fallen leaves and brush without sinking into it, and looking inordinately pleased with herself. She didn\u2019t even object when I called her Legolas.<br /> <br /> We got to the campsite with a few hours of daylight left and set about pitching our tents. D, Gloria and I managed to get ours set up pretty quickly (not as quickly as Jacob &amp; Luna or Elena &amp; Stasia, of course, but they\u2019re the real experts at that sort of thing in the party), but some of the others had a bit of trouble. Missy and Jane fumbled with their tent for a while, and I eventually went over to help them, explaining a few of the minor innovations which have arisen in camping gear over the past forty years or so.<br /> <br /> Trinh was having trouble of a different sort. She kept getting frustrated when little things went wrong, which of course just led to more minor mistakes. Eventually it came out that Trinh was feeling guilty about the trouble her presence in the world was causing her Fetch. \u201cHere I am having fun with good friends, and she\u2019s holed up in some seedy little crack-house afraid for her life\u2026 because of me!\u201d<br /> <br /> We tried to assure her that none of this was actually her <u><u>fault</u></u>, but she was inconsolable for a while. In the end it was Elena who got through to her, talking quietly with her about her identity issues and the things she can and can\u2019t control. She also made sure that Trinh\u2019s tent was set up properly so that she could sleep securely that night. After a while, Trinh gave Elena a tearful hug, and apologized for teasing her about what she and Stasia had gotten up to the previous evening.<br /> <br /> We set up a campfire, sang traditional songs, told scary stories, and generally had a fine old time. I think Calamity was a little disappointed that she didn\u2019t get to fight a bear while we were out there \u2013 she\u2019d been talking about the possibility for the last few days, despite protests from our resident park ranger \u2013 but other than that the experience was fully enjoyed by all.<br /> <br /> Jacob did make it snow for a little while, which provided a nice bit of ambiance for our annual winter camping trip. It made things a little chilly, which encouraged people to cuddle up close to each other. I think Maria was probably in hog heaven, with me snuggled up to one side of her and Gloria on the other. I remember how good it felt the first time I got to be with D and Oleander at the same time, and I\u2019m glad I could help her feel that way as well. I mean, we\u2019ve both been with Marguerite and Julia plenty of times, but this is different\u2026 this is bringing together two loves who have always had a bit of distance between them. It\u2019s creating a new bond.<br /> <br /> Once the talk started to die down, I yawned and stretched theatrically and indicated that I\u2019d be heading to bed soon. \u201cAt least this time I <u><u>know</u></u> I double-checked,\u201d I said as I rummaged around in my pack. \u201cI\u2019ll be able to sleep in my nice warm paja\u2026 <u><u>dammit</u></u> D!\u201d Once again, my flannel PJs had disappeared from my pack. I caught her exchanging a wink with Marguerite, so I\u2019m guessing there was some collusion from the French faction in this conspiracy.<br /> <br /> So the three of us retired to our tent, got undressed, and <u><u>somehow</u></u> managed to squeeze into two sleeping bags which had been zipped together. We played a bit, and there were plenty of kisses (and other things) exchanged, but due to the tight confines things were really more tender than erotic. Once again we fell asleep with D between us, but I made sure that my hand reached across my wife\u2019s stomach to rest on Gloria\u2019s waist, and after a while I felt her hand settle onto my hip. I cooed contentedly as the three of us drifted off.<br /> <br /> I woke up about an hour ago, and extricated myself from the sleeping bag as quietly as I could. The other two stirred, but didn\u2019t rise with me. I\u2019ve been writing in this diary and watching a <u><u>gorgeous</u></u> sunrise over the eastern ridge of the mountains. The birds are singing\u2026 and I cannot tell you how utterly beautiful that song is when you can understand it. Unfortunately, there aren\u2019t human words for it, so I won\u2019t even try to convey its meaning here.<br /> <br /> Once the others are awake, we\u2019ll have a light breakfast, break camp, and hike back to the cars and head back to Malibu and back to our lives. We have Trinh\u2019s Fetch to deal with, and the New Year\u2019s Eve show to plan, and a thousand other things to worry about\u2026 but those are concerns for later. For now, I\u2019m just going to listen to the birds and revel in their joy as it mirrors my own.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei de la Rocha</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Sometimes my life feels surreal in some ways. Today was the second time I\u2019ve been woken up on Christmas day by someone singing Christmas carols in the vents. Insincere Marguerite loves this time of year and decided that we had all slept long enough and she wanted us up so we could all enjoy the holiday. So we all got up and made our way downstairs. Calamity made it to the kitchen before Lori this time and started cooking breakfast. Pancakes, bacon, eggs, toast, it was all good. I of course made the coffee. Iced for myself and hot for everyone else. Conversation turned to the camping trip tomorrow and about whether or not we had all the gear we needed. I assured folks that we had what we needed to go camping for one night. It was kind of amusing actually. Before I entered the Lady\u2019s service I technically camped all the time. There are no cabins in the Lady\u2019s realm. There are no shelters, except the occasional cave here and there. It is a harsh place. And I lived there for years. In the snow. With no tent. No sleeping bag. And this group here is concerned about camping for one night in the hills of California where the temperature doesn\u2019t know how to go below 65 degrees Fahrenheit. Though to be fair my plan was to lower the temperature a bit so it would more easily snow tomorrow night. Still, it won\u2019t get close to freezing. I know Lori is familiar with the snow, she\u2019s from Iowa, and my sister knows about camping in the winter, but I\u2019m not so sure about the rest. The motley at least has experienced camping with me once before, so they know what to expect. It\u2019s going to be fun, even if Calamity does keep going on about knife fighting a bear.<br /> <br /> Later in the afternoon folks started coming over to help prepare Christmas dinner. Elena and Stasia came over to help and just be here. My sister apologized to me for being clingy. I told her that it was fine. I understood why she needed to be near family right now and told her that I would always be there for her. I feel bad that I wasn\u2019t there at Thanksgiving when our parents rejected her in the first place. She couldn\u2019t come to me because I was gone in Arcadia. I wouldn\u2019t trade the trip to Arcadia for anything. We did a lot of good there. We freed three innocent people, but I do regret the fact that I wasn\u2019t here when my sister needed me the most. Thankfully she had Stasia to lean on.<br /> <br /> Conversation took an interesting turn. Apparently Missy and Jane went exploring the house this morning and came across Julia\u2019s Wiccan altar in the attic and the sex toys in the basement. They thought that the altar was some sort of Satanic thing I guess. Lori assured them that it was okay. No devil worship in this house. It was interesting though, when the sex toys came up, my sister and to some extent Stasia got sheepish for lack of a better word. I guess that they had made use of the toys in the basement while we were gone. I\u2019m not going to ask. It\u2019s none of my business, but it was kind of funny to watch my sister\u2019s face turn red and see her sink below the level of the table top.<br /> <br /> After all that De la Rocha wanted to continue showing off her new ability. She can now shoot lasers from her fingertips, and she was targeting little bits of paper that were set up around the room for her to target. They decided to take it further and have Lori go up on the roof and throw some clay pigeons off the side so De la Rocha can target them with her lasers. Julia joined her up on the roof. It was fun to watch and all, but I thought it might be good to do something fun for Elena. So, I asked her if she\u2019d like to go ice skating in the backyard. I told them that I could freeze water on the stage so we could go skating. Elena and Stasia both agreed that sounded like fun so I did just that. It was good to see Elena smile. She\u2019s been doing it so much less than usual since Thanksgiving, and I just wanted to make her happy. To take her mind off of what our parents did. Of what the Little Shit did. I think it worked for a little while, and that\u2019s all I can really hope for isn\u2019t it? Reality always has a way of reinserting itself into your perceptions no matter how much we try and avoid it.<br /> <br /> Once the target practice was done De la Rocha gave Missy and Jane a crash course in internet security so they\u2019ll be safer when they are surfing the web or checking their emails. It\u2019s second nature to me, but when we started talking about it and explaining it to those two I realized just how much information they need to know. Hell, they need to learn about the internet and email before they can learn about network security. I take my hat off to De la Rocha for tackling that burden.<br /> <br /> Then there was preparation for dinner. Trinh, Lori and Calamity were the main cooks in the kitchen, but the rest of us pitched in here and there. There was a lot of food, and it all needed to be done around the same time. Don\u2019t want the potatoes getting cold while we\u2019re waiting on the turkey. Talk about first world problems. I just reread that last sentence and started laughing. In the Lady\u2019s realm I was lucky to have a fire to cook food over. A lot of times I just ate the meat raw. I didn\u2019t have much choice in the matter. Cooked is always better, but sometimes you have to do what you have to do. Not so anymore. I think I\u2019ve gotten used to having regular meals, which still feels a bit surreal if you ask me, but I expect it now. I\u2019ve stopped hiding snacks in my go bag, though I still have a go bag. I can leave at a moment\u2019s notice if needs be. And through all of the cooking Missy, Jane and Julia were having a cordial argument about whether or not Satan exists. Julia says he doesn\u2019t, but the other two disagree. I don\u2019t know if Satan exists, but I do know there are evil beings in \u2018the world\u2019 and beyond. The Gentry are not all pure bitch evil, but a lot of them are in my opinion. They have too much power and it goes to their heads. What\u2019s the saying? Absolute power corrupts absolutely. That\u2019s the Gentry.<br /> <br /> Dinner was good. The food all came out at the right time and was enjoyed by all. We even had a few extra guests. Gloria and Oleander came to celebrate the holiday with us. Oleander was still a bit toxic from her trip to the Hedge, so she didn\u2019t stay too close to anyone else, but I know that Lori was especially happy to have her there. Elena got a bit teary-eyed a couple of times but Stasia and I were there for her. Despite being a little bit melancholy during the meal I think my sister had fun. Conversation ran the gamut from reminiscing about De la Rocha hitting Augustine with a church pew to Changeling frailties. Some of us admitted what our frailties were. I said I couldn\u2019t drink hot drinks anymore. Hence me always making myself iced coffee. Lori has to sing if she\u2019s asked to, Insincere Marguerite can only walk barefoot on the bare earth, and Calamity has to repair any glass broken in her presence. Some, like De la Rocha said they hadn\u2019t noticed any frailties, or they didn\u2019t tell what theirs were. They tend to be rather personal things. My thing with the hot drinks is annoying, but not overly personal. Calamity on the other hand is hurt if innocent blood touches her. That was something that she did not want to explain to the newbies, and I don\u2019t blame her. I\u2019m sure that I have another frailty, but I\u2019m not sure what it is. I guess it just hasn\u2019t come up.<br /> <br /> After dinner was over there was karaoke. Insincere Marguerite got the equipment all set up and people started singing. Some people requested songs from their significant others. Some people just sang what they wanted to. I got pressured into singing, so I decided to do a traditional Russian Christmas carol. Insincere Marguerite managed to find the music for it and I sang to the best of my ability. I wasn\u2019t very good, but that wasn\u2019t the point. I wanted my sister to have a bit of home this holiday season. I think the best was when Lori, Missy and Jane all went up to sing in harmony. They really are very good together.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> We actually got up in the morning today. It is a departure from our norm, but it was nice to see the morning sun. Usually our work hours are not conducive to getting up too early in the morning. So, we had French toast for breakfast. Calamity cooked. It was good. Then everyone finished packing their bags and we loaded up the vehicles. In total it was the motley, plus Trinh, Jane, Missy, Becky, Gloria, Stasia and Elena all going with us. That\u2019s a lot of people to go camping. I had to make sure that I had a big enough campground in mind for all those people to set up tents and have enough room. In the end we had the van, my jeep and Gloria\u2019s SUV loaded up and ready to go. Getting there with the whole convoy in tow was interesting. Had to make sure that no one got separated from the group. I tried to lead as best as I could, but gave those that were driving the address so they could plug it into their phones if needs be.<br /> <br /> Once we got there we made an impressive line of people all hiking into the woods. I led them past the closer camping spots and past a pretty waterfall. I thought they\u2019d appreciate the scenery. Plus I wanted to be far enough away from other campers that they would not keep us awake and we would not disturb them with our own shenanigans. Everyone seemed to like the spot I had picked out, and thankfully no one asked how I knew where the good camping spots are. I would have lied of course. I wasn\u2019t about to admit to non-motley mates that I know these hills so well because I frequented them as a Loyalist for the Lady. Granted I haven\u2019t really admitted to my motley mates why I\u2019m familiar with these hills. They have never asked, so I haven\u2019t volunteered the information either.<br /> <br /> At some point while we were walking Calamity brought up the idea of stabbing a bear again, which annoyed Luna I think. At least Luna, very sternly, told Calamity in no uncertain terms that she was not going to be baiting or stabbing any bears during this camping trip. I mentioned that it was generally a good idea to give bears a wide berth and not go looking for a fight with one. I remember before I served the Lady trying to avoid bears in the woods. It was hard. They were generally interested in any food that people had and would come looking for it. They caught their own of course, but it was easier to take it from the humans. Us. I had to abandon a camp site on several occasions. Only going back for my gear when I was sure the bear had left. After the first time I wouldn\u2019t unpack anything unless I needed it. It made it easier if I needed to leave in a hurry I could just grab my bag and run. So, did what I could to talk Calamity out of stabbing a bear. At the end I think she was just having fun with us. <br /> <br /> Of course this whole conversation about bears led to talk about other bears which led to Care Bears, Strawberry Shortcake and My Little Pony. Basically, a lot of tv shows for young kids from the 1980s. I have not seen really any of them. I have heard of My Little Pony. They restarted that one and I\u2019ve seen it on Netflix. It was a strange conversation all around. Eventually though we made it to the campsite and everyone started setting up their tents. The motley was pretty good with their tents. They went camping with me last year, so they at least had that practice. Missy and Jan got theirs up though it took some time. Trinh though had some problems and started to get upset. Elena, having already gotten her tent up, offered an ear and to help with the tent. Trinh admitted that she was upset because she was out here having fun while her fetch was scared and hiding. Elena tried to reassure her and told her that no matter what she was doing her fetch would be reacting the same way. The only thing we could do about it was give it some time and then we\u2019ll see about getting the two of them together and see what happens.<br /> <br /> After the tents were up we cooked dinner. It was pretty good if I do say so myself. We seasoned some vegetables and wrapped them in tin foil to cook, while we grilled some steaks over the fire. After we finished eating we told scary stories and Lori insisted on singing campfire songs. It eventually broke down in to conversation, which went back to bears for a bit, but not hunting them. We also talked about other things that we might run into in the woods like werewolves. Someone asked if Luna had ever seen or met a werewolf. She deflected the question and all subsequent questions regarding that topic which makes me think that she has and can\u2019t or won\u2019t talk about it. Before that I wasn\u2019t sure if they actually existed. I was willing to believe though. We\u2019ve met vampires. We\u2019re faeries essentially, why not werewolves too? De la Rocha then changed the topic to the fact that Lori\u2019s dad used to be a vampire hunter. Missy and Jane were especially interested in that. I don\u2019t think they could reconcile the man that they knew back in the 1970s with who he became later or who he is now for that matter.<br /> <br /> While conversation was going on I stepped away from the camp for a few minutes to work on getting it to snow. It took just a bit longer this year than last but it was worth it. It snowed for a good couple of hours and the temp dropped a bit. At least enough so that the snow stuck around for a little while. The birds, like last year, were mad at me for making it snow so I asked Lori to apologize for me. Gloria commented that the snow was surreal, not bad, just surreal. I told her that it used to be a family tradition for our family to go camping on me and Elena\u2019s birthday, which just so happened to be in December. And since we lived in Oregon it snowed in the mountains in the winter. I wanted to keep up with the tradition and so when we go camping in December it\u2019s going to snow. She accepted that. I think pretty much everyone was fine with the snow. It gave everyone excuses to cuddle up together and snuggle in their tents. Like that wasn\u2019t going to happen anyway, but it was still an excuse.<br /> <br /> Everyone had retired to their tent except for Trinh. I asked Luna to wait a moment before going to bed and asked the new arrival if she was okay. She didn\u2019t seem keen on talking. She just said that she needed to think. I accepted that and told her that if she needed anything to just let us know. She nodded at that and went back to staring into the warm coals from the fire. I felt bad just leaving her alone, but she didn\u2019t seem to want any company just then. So, Luna and I went to our own tent and did our own snuggling. And now it\u2019s entirely too early in the morning and I\u2019m writing in this book. Time to stop. Luna will be up soon.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CIX</i><br /> <br /> Mechanically, not a lot to cover. I think I had mentioned Julia\u2019s religious bent early on but it had been awhile. And the furniture in the, ah, playroom they had gotten the during the last winter\u2019s break. In game there was the clear implication Stasia and Elena had come in and used it. It made for some funny scenes with the two.<br /> <br /> To clarify Trinh is not herself Cajun (not that Lori actually said she was) just had friends who were and enjoyed the cuisine. Trinh herself is Afro-Vietnamese.<br /> <br /> Knife fighting bears really was discussed to distraction.<br /> <br /> Okay I think that covers it. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T02:13:15-07:00","id":1227987,"title":"","content":"The visitors struggle to adapt. Trinh gives into despair. Melissa gives into rage. But on the other side of struggle is hope, and all the visitors experience ends on high note.<br /> <br /> Calamity\u2019s player is relocating so no time for a journal.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Okay, so, well\u2026 there have been a lot of ups and downs over the past few days, but by and large I think we\u2019ve come out on top. There are a few facets of my life that definitely bear scrutiny, but I honestly believe that progress is being made, and I can only see that as a good thing.<br /> <br /> So as I said in my last entry, I got up pretty early on Sunday morning so that I could watch the sun rise. I neglected to mention that after I had disentangled myself from D and Gloria in those sleeping bags and exited the tent, I took a few moments to stretch\u2026 much to Stasia\u2019s apparent delight, as I had neglected to dress myself first. I threw her a grin and a wink and ducked back into my tent to rectify that little oversight.<br /> <br /> By the time we got the campfire going again and started cooking the sausages, most of the rest of the camp was awake. Calamity and Becky were the last to emerge; I guess they must have had a pretty good night. Unfortunately, not everyone was so chipper\u2026 Trinh looked awful. And I don\u2019t mean that in a \u201cshe looked like she didn\u2019t sleep well\u201d sort of way; she was actually physically hurt.<br /> <br /> I beckoned her over and got to work healing the worst of her injuries, though she was still pretty badly bruised after I finished. I tried to gently question her about what had happened, but she was adamant that she didn\u2019t want to talk about it, and when I pressed a little harder she became agitated and irritable, so I let it be. Elena spoke softly with her for a bit away from the rest of us, but I got the impression that she wasn\u2019t any more forthcoming with Jacob\u2019s sister than she had been with me.<br /> <br /> We broke camp after breakfast and hiked back down to the cars, and once again D refused to let me lug my own pack. While I admit that a backpack chafes a bit as it moves back and forth between my wings, I was far from the only person with that problem on our little wilderness expedition, and it was actually kind of embarrassing to be singled out in that way. Still, the sunlight and the breeze were pleasant, and it was hard to be gloomy when surrounded by all of that beautiful scenery.<br /> <br /> The ride back to Malibu was a little more subdued than the ride up into the mountains had been, but we soon got over that. Sublime\u2019s \u201cWhat I Got\u201d came on the radio at one point, and I almost immediately started singing along with it. Gloria joined me after a few lines, and eventually even D picked up the thread of the lyrics. Missy and Jane didn\u2019t know the song yet, of course, but they were laughing and clapping along with the rest of us by the time the final chorus started up. Things were a little more animated after that.<br /> <br /> We coordinated by phone and stopped at a McDonald\u2019s for lunch on the way home. There was some grumbling about the fast food, but I pushed for it as a sort of object lesson for Missy and Jane\u2026 that even in this strange new world, there are some constants. Sure the menu has expanded, and the signs stating the number of Big Macs sold are now expressed in the billions rather than the millions\u2026 but it was still a familiar environment for the two of them, and they could order from the menu by memory without getting blank stares from the attendants.<br /> <br /> When we got back to the Dream House, we all settled in at the bar and started deciding what we were going to do that night. The alcohol flowed freely, and I even broke out a bottle of fifteen-year Macallan and poured a couple of shots for Missy and Jane\u2026 figured I still owed them the drinks I\u2019d promised to swipe from Dad\u2019s liquor cabinet before we were taken.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, that was gonna be a big night,\u201d Jane reminisced, a little starry-eyed. While she didn\u2019t elaborate, I gathered that she\u2019d planned to make a move on Missy after I\u2019d passed out that evening. That could have been\u2026 awkward if it had happened back then. Whatever else can be said about our time in Arcadia, I\u2019m glad that it\u2019s allowed them to explore their relationship in that way.<br /> <br /> Conversation swerved wildly all over the place, touching upon such subjects as the uncomfortable tendency for 1950s music to talk about romancing underage girls and the rampant stereotyping of female athletes in certain sports as lesbians. When tennis came up, Jane mentioned Martina Navratilova, whom she apparently recognized as gay even back in the 70s. She must be pretty sharp; we\u2019re talking about a time when most of Middle America was still struggling with the idea that Liberace was gay\u2026<br /> <br /> After an hour or so of shooting the bull, Gloria reluctantly bade us farewell, and gave both D and me passionate goodbye kisses and bright happy smiles, which I returned with spades. After the door closed behind her, D turned to me with a curious look.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo, are you two, like\u2026 dating now?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> The question caught me off-guard. \u201cI\u2026 I\u2019m not sure,\u201d I admitted. \u201cHow would that make you feel?\u201d<br /> <br /> She smiled, so guileless and genuine that I couldn\u2019t question its truth. \u201cI\u2019d love it,\u201d she said immediately. \u201cThe more of you that get involved with each other, the easier it is on me. Less relationship calculus to deal with\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, I\u2019ve always been attracted to Gloria,\u201d I said after a moment, \u201cyou know that. And she\u2019s a good person, and a friend. So I\u2019m up for it if she is\u2026 but I don\u2019t want to push her or pressure her into anything. So let\u2019s just give her a little time and see where it goes for now.\u201d<br /> <br /> Unfortunately a couple of less pleasant conversations followed. First, Luna informed us all that she <u><u>had</u></u> in fact met several werewolves in the forests near where we had camped. She\u2019d only hedged around the subject the previous evening because, and I quote: \u201cYou never know when they might be listening.\u201d Apparently they value their secrets just as much as the changeling community\u2026 which I guess isn\u2019t all that surprising. I apologized for not letting the matter drop when I should have.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s okay,\u201d she assured us, \u201cthey wouldn\u2019t have hurt us without a good reason. And nothing else supernatural is going to intrude on a werewolf pack\u2019s territory, so the woods are pretty safe by and large.\u201d So I guess that\u2019s okay.<br /> <br /> As the shadows lengthened, Trinh decided that it was time to come forward and talk about what had happened to her. And it wasn\u2019t good. She tried to kill herself.<br /> <br /> See, apparently Trinh went walking by herself late that night and got to thinking about her Fetch. Being a very empathetic sort, she\u2019d been feeling simply awful about the rough time her Fetch has been having since she returned to the world. She despaired. She started to feel like maybe she didn\u2019t belong in the world after all\u2026 like maybe she could spare her Fetch some pain if she just took matters into her own hands. So she stepped off a cliff.<br /> <br /> Luckily, she changed her mind at the last possible moment, and spread her wings to slow her fall. It only helped so much, as evidenced by her state when we woke up this morning, but it probably made the difference between life and death.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sorry,\u201d she said contritely, avoiding our eyes. \u201cYou\u2019ve all given up so much to help me, and I\u2019m truly grateful. What I did was selfish, and disrespectful of everything that all of you have sacrificed to give me this chance. I hope you can forgive me.\u201d<br /> <br /> I moved forward first. \u201cThere\u2019s nothing to forgive, Trinh,\u201d I said, pulling her into a hug. \u201cJust\u2026 promise me that if you start to feel this way again you\u2019ll <u><u>talk</u></u> to us before you do anything drastic, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> Trinh sniffed and hugged me back. \u201cI promise\u2026 but I won\u2019t be doing it again.\u201d<br /> <br /> The others offered their sympathies as well. Jacob said that he would call up Boss Lowjack to see how things were going with Trinh\u2019s Fetch, and maybe hurry things along a little. Calamity offered to give Trinh pleasant dreams to offset some of the nightmares her inner turmoil had caused.<br /> <br /> The real shocker came when Missy stepped up and offered Trinh a nervous hug. \u201cI\u2019m glad you\u2019re okay,\u201d she said softly. \u201cI know things were a little tense between us back in the cage, but I don\u2019t want you to die or anything.\u201d Trinh got a little choked up at that. Jane looked a little surprised, but did not disagree with Missy\u2019s sentiment.<br /> <br /> Conversations started roaming all over the place again after that. I mentioned that I needed to get by Joan and Andromeda\u2019s place at some point in the next few days to see if their VCR had exploded, and then I had to explain that whole thing to the newcomers. Much to my surprise, Missy piped up at this point.<br /> <br /> \u201cAndromeda\u2026 she\u2019s the little Jewish alien girl, right?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah,\u201d I said, without really thinking about it.<br /> <br /> \u201cHow\u2019d you know she was Jewish?\u201d D asked curiously.<br /> <br /> \u201cI heard her swearing in Yiddish,\u201d Missy admitted.<br /> <br /> \u201cSince when do you speak Yiddish?\u201d Jane asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cI only know a few words\u2026 mostly curse words,\u201d Missy said. \u201cI had a Jewish friend in kindergarten and first grade. She taught me a little bit.\u201d<br /> <br /> I pondered that for a moment. \u201cThere was a Jewish family living in Defiance? I never knew that,\u201d I commented.<br /> <br /> \u201cThey moved away when we were really young,\u201d Missy explained. \u201cI\u2026 don\u2019t think they found the town very welcoming. That always seemed kind of stupid to me. I liked her, and I cried when she moved.\u201d So I had that to think about.<br /> <br /> I also made tentative arrangements to set up a shoot with Stasia at some point in the next few weeks. She really wants to add some shots of me to her portfolio, and I must admit that it would be nice to get back into circulation in the L.A. fashion scene. I\u2019ve been planning to model for her for over a year now, but we never found the right time\u2026 what with wedding plans and our extended trip to Arcadia and all. And if we don\u2019t take care of that soon, I\u2019ll have to schedule it around classes and study sessions and such.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ve been thinking about that a little,\u201d D said when I mentioned my impending academic career, \u201cand I had an idea.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh?\u201d I asked, intrigued. D has mostly remained aloof from my college plans, aside from offering me encouragement.<br /> <br /> \u201cWould you consider taking Twitch on as a tutor?\u201d she asked. Before I could even process the request, she started defending it. \u201cI think it would be good for both of you. He\u2019s gotten a lot better since last December, but I know you could help bring him out of his shell even more\u2026 help him get his confidence back. And I mean\u2026 he used to be such a selfless, good soul. Spending time with someone like you might help him to remember what that was like. And I think it would be helpful for you as well. I mean, he\u2019s\u2026 he\u2019s soon to be the second-best doctor I know.\u201d<br /> <br /> I chuckled and took the compliment with good grace. \u201cI think it\u2019s a fine idea,\u201d I said, \u201cas long as it\u2019s okay with him, I\u2019d be happy to explore the possibilities.\u201d<br /> <br /> I am perhaps sugar-coating my own opinion of this arrangement the tiniest bit. I still find Twitch more than a little creepy, and I\u2019d be lying if I said that I was entirely comfortable in his presence. He\u2019s done awful things. I know that D blames herself for putting him in the position to do those things\u2026 but he still did them. But beyond my own discomfort\u2026 I still think it\u2019s a good idea, and I still think it\u2019s worth a shot. Twitch has a <u><u>lot</u></u> of medical experience, and I\u2019m sure his insight and tutelage will be invaluable during the long road ahead. And if I can help him along the way, isn\u2019t it my duty to at least <u><u>try</u></u> to do so?<br /> <br /> (You see, D? I may not be entirely comfortable with the idea, but I\u2019m still going to go through with it, and all of my own volition, so you can stop fretting about it. And yes, I know that you\u2019re still reading my diary from time to time, and no, it still doesn\u2019t bother me. I love you.)<br /> <br /> As the Dream House hadn\u2019t reopened for business yet, we had the evening free, and decided to educate Missy and Jane as to some of the pop culture they had missed. While I pitched a few popular franchises like Star Wars, Lord of the Rings, and the recent Marvel films, in the end we decided to start with a couple of films which require less of a time commitment.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d seen both <u><u>Blade Runner</u></u> and <u><u>The Fifth Element</u></u> before, but it was fun to revisit them. I asked both Missy and Jane the tortoise question from the beginning of the first film, and was met with blank looks. \u201cI\u2019d turn it over so it was upright,\u201d Missy said flatly, \u201cwho wouldn\u2019t?\u201d Jane agreed, so I guess neither one of them is a replicant. I\u2019m pretty sure I would have noticed in any case, but one can never be too certain.<br /> <br /> By the time the movies were over Jacob had contacted Boss Lowjack, and we\u2019d tentatively planned to approach Trinh\u2019s Fetch late the following morning to see what we could do about reconciling the two of them. I set my phone to wake me up around nine o\u2019clock. Trinh was nervous about the meeting, but happy that things were moving forward.<br /> <br /> All through the second film, Missy and Jane had been making eyes at me as I leaned back in Maria\u2019s strong embrace. Now, anyone who knows me could have determined that I was interested, and D was no exception. As the credits rolled, she leaned in, kissed my forehead, and whispered that she would be happy to stay with Marguerite and Julia that evening if I wanted to explore other options. I turned that into a real kiss before I stood up, crossed the room, and joined my oldest friends on the loveseat.<br /> <br /> The evening was\u2026 well, it\u2019s difficult to describe, really. I mean, maybe it wasn\u2019t as meaningful to the two of them as it was to me\u2026 it\u2019s only been like six weeks since we\u2019ve slept together from their perspective after all, while for me it\u2019s been over two years. Aside from being my best friends, and one of my few links to my life before Arcadia, they were my first female lovers. They opened my eyes to a world of opportunities I might never have known without them. Would I be involved with any of the wonderful women I know today without them? Would I be married to my soulmate? Well, I like to think so\u2026 but who really knows?<br /> <br /> So the long and the short of it is that I decided to show the two of them how much I\u2019d missed them to the best of my ability. Jane may have recognized her own sexuality first, but I\u2019ve had an extra couple of years of experience with a couple of dozen women, and I\u2019ve picked up a few tricks. I demonstrated my abilities to give the two of them a night they wouldn\u2019t soon forget. No, I didn\u2019t use all of my best techniques; got to save something for next time, right?<br /> <br /> So when my phone alarm chimed the next morning the guest room bed was a mess. Three naked girls, six large wings, loose feathers strewn everywhere, and various pillows and sheets tangled about us\u2026 to say that the queen-sized bed was a bit cramped is something of an understatement, and nobody could move without inconveniencing someone else in some way. Luckily, I\u2019ve had a lot of practice extricating myself from such tangles, and a few minutes later we had disengaged and begun preening each other\u2026 straightening feathers and what-not. It was\u2026 disturbingly familiar, actually.<br /> <br /> Oh, I should probably mention that last night was the first time Missy slept in a bed without the straw. Presumably as a courtesy to me, the two of them had cleaned all of the scratchy stuff off of the bed and piled it neatly in a corner of the room (well, as neatly as you can pile loose straw, at least). Jane was visibly relieved to be done with it, and even Missy didn\u2019t seem to have any trouble sleeping last night\u2026 though in retrospect I might have had something to do with that, as I did my best to wear them both out.<br /> <br /> I made waffles for breakfast, and that went over pretty well. Calamity had been out for Tai Chi with White Maria, but she was back by the time the coffee was poured, and she and Becky were <u><u>adorable</u></u> together. This opened up the discussion on Calamity\u2019s famous \u201clove makes you stupid\u201d theory, and thankfully most of those assembled came down on my side of the question. Jane raised a particularly valid point in my opinion when she said \u201cit\u2019s all a matter of context. Nothing I do so that Missy and I can be safe together could ever be stupid.\u201d<br /> <br /> Unfortunately Calamity\u2019s mood darkened a bit when her paramour left after breakfast to spell Angelica at Glamour Springs. I tried to brighten her mood a bit, but it was an uphill battle. It\u2019s been almost exactly a year since Gawain left her, and that memory is weighing heavily on her. \u201cHey,\u201d I said to her quietly once I\u2019d gotten her alone, \u201cstop worrying about it. She won\u2019t leave you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know,\u201d she replied, \u201cbut I never thought Gawain would leave either\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFour days \u2018til New Years,\u201d I said bracingly. \u201cIt\u2019ll get better after that. Until then, I\u2019m here if you need me, okay?\u201d She didn\u2019t look particularly convinced, but she agreed to give it the old college try. Dammit! I hate it when my friends are suffering and I can\u2019t do anything for them!<br /> <br /> Enough talk about that, though\u2026 we had another problem to deal with. We decided that we should only bring those essential to the mission along to see Trinh\u2019s Fetch. Just about everyone agreed that I should be there, as I\u2019m pretty good at talking people down from bad decisions. D immediately stated that she would go along to protect me in case things went south, and everybody immediately recognized that there would be no point in arguing with her. Jacob came along since he essentially arranged the whole thing with Boss Lowjack, and Calamity opted in to make sure that the Fetch didn\u2019t present a danger to the Freehold, as she\u2019s oath-bound to keep an eye out for such things. Finally, Marguerite joined us as a sort of secret weapon; she can discreetly keep an eye on Trinh\u2019s private conversation so that we can respond quickly if necessary.<br /> <br /> Half an hour later, the five of us plus Trinh were outside of a nice house in one of the higher-class suburbs of L.A. Boss Lowjack was parked nearby; he got out of his car and approached us as we pulled up. \u201cHere\u2019s how I\u2019d like to do this, if everybody\u2019s amenable. The Fetch and her bodyguard are inside; the latter will shortly be taking a little nap.\u201d Here he paused for a minute, and then indicated me. \u201cThis is awkward\u2026 I\u2019d like <u><u>this</u></u> Mrs. De la Rocha and I to enter first and let the Fetch know that she\u2019s safe and that we\u2019re trying to help her resolve her current difficulties. Once that\u2019s taken care of, we\u2019ll see where things go. I\u2019ll send Lori out to let the rest of you know how we proceed, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> We all agreed that this would be a workable plan of action, and the two of us headed to the door. A fairly large, intimidating man answered, and was in the process of asking us what business we had there when Lowjack pulled a syringe out of his coat pocket and plunged it into the man\u2019s neck. He was out cold in seconds\u2026 though of course I never doubted this, it\u2019s clear that Oleander really knows her stuff. Lowjack caught the guy as he fell and arranged him comfortably on a rug in the front hallway. He took the man\u2019s pistol out of its holster and placed it on an end table nearby.<br /> <br /> We found Trinh\u2019s Fetch in the living room, and she gazed at us in bleary-eyed fear. It was clear that she still hadn\u2019t had much sleep. \u201cWho are you people?\u201d she asked in a frightened voice. \u201cWhat happened to my guard?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHe wasn\u2019t very good,\u201d Lowjack cut in smoothly. \u201cLook, Miss Jackson, I want to assure you that we don\u2019t mean you any harm. I specialize in conflict resolution, and an interested party has asked me to see what I can do about your current troubles. I assure you that nothing untoward will happen to you while you\u2019re under my care. Worst case scenario is that when I leave this house, you\u2019ll be in exactly the same situation you are now. If things go as I hope they will, you\u2019ll have nothing further to worry about, and you\u2019ll be able to get on with your life. What do you say, will you let me try to help you?\u201d<br /> <br /> Her eyes narrowed a little. \u201cWhat do you charge for this service?\u201d she asked suspiciously.<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t worry about that; it\u2019s all been taken care of,\u201d he assured her. \u201cNow if you\u2019d like to head upstairs for a few minutes and freshen up, I can get things set up in the kitchen and prepare to bring in the other party. Don\u2019t worry about anything; we\u2019ll have our own people ensuring your security the whole time. I\u2019ll fix us something to eat, and my associate will bring them in while you\u2019re upstairs, if that\u2019s all right.\u201d<br /> <br /> Her eyes flicked to me, and I saw a flash of recognition in them. I thought at first that she\u2019d had some vision of me through Trinh\u2019s eyes or something\u2026 but I don\u2019t think that\u2019s actually the case. I was starting to make a name for myself in the L.A. fashion scene before we went into Arcadia, after all, and Trinh\u2019s Fetch has been a part of that world for years now. \u201cOkay,\u201d she said cautiously after a moment of consideration.<br /> <br /> \u201cExcellent,\u201d Lowjack said with authority. \u201cJust let me take care of everything. Meet us in the kitchen as soon as you\u2019re ready.\u201d<br /> <br /> She excused herself, and I followed the Winter King into her gleaming modern kitchen. He began pulling items from the fridge and the pantry seemingly at random and started preparing what looked like a four-star lunch on autopilot. \u201cWhen she gets back,\u201d he said, \u201cI want you to bring Trinh, Jacob, and Calamity into the house. I\u2019ll try to prepare her for Trinh so that she won\u2019t make a scene; I want the other two in here playing heavies to back up my earlier claim that we\u2019d have security in place. Keep de la Rocha on the door just in case. And I\u2019d like Insincere Marguerite to observe the meeting from stealth and let us know if we\u2019re needed.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTen-four,\u201d I said, and then headed out to make it so.<br /> <br /> Things went fairly well overall, with only a few hiccups along the way. The worst of these came while Trinh and the Fetch were talking and I was waiting in the hall to give them their privacy. The dulcet tones of my wife drifted in from the front door. I believe she was saying something along the lines of \u201cwrong house, Ese!\u201d There was a shouted response which went something like \u201cout of the way, bitch!\u201d and then a resounding thud.<br /> <br /> I hurried to the door to find D standing over the unconscious form of a thuggish young man. I checked his vitals and determined that he was going to be all right (though he\u2019ll probably have a hell of a bruise and a bad headache when he wakes up) and looked up at the love of my life. \u201cYou okay, sweetie?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cSure,\u201d she shrugged. \u201cMust be the other guy\u2019s relief. He was\u2026 rude.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI heard,\u201d I agreed. We moved him into the living room with the other guy (leaving him on a rug in the hall had seemed needlessly cruel when there were comfy sofas just a few feet away), and I put his gun on the end table with the other one.<br /> <br /> Lowjack spent a few minutes examining both of the goons\u2019 cell phones. When I asked what was up, he replied that he was trying to learn each man\u2019s texting style so that he could reply to any messages they got from their organization and hopefully keep our activities secret for a little longer. I thought that was pretty cool and useful, and in the spirit of my entitlement, I asked if he would share any tips or tricks with me. He pointed out a few things I never would have considered on my own. Not just grammatical stuff, but things that are unique to texting, like whether each man used emojis, and whether or not they tended to catch the changes made by the auto-correct feature.<br /> <br /> Marguerite texted us periodic updates on how things were going. For the most part, I think the meeting went very well. Trinh started off explaining the whole Arcadia thing in gentle terms, talking about the two of them as two halves of the same being rather than claiming to be the original and calling her Fetch an imposter. I\u2019m guessing Lowjack coached her a little about how best to handle that side of things earlier. Trinh\u2019s Fetch was overwhelmed by the revelation, but did not appear angry or violent at any point.<br /> <br /> The two of them seem to be nearly identical in outlook and personality\u2026 both have a sort of \u201cdo no harm\u201d philosophy when it comes to the world at large. The only snag came when Trinh learned that her Fetch had gone vegan at some point in the last ten years or so. The Fetch is pretty gung-ho about the lifestyle, but Trinh really enjoys eating meat, so who knows which of them will win out when and if they eventually merge. Considering that I was afraid the Fetch would get violent or go catatonic when she first saw Trinh, I\u2019d say the vegan thing is an acceptable hiccup.<br /> <br /> Y\u2019know, as long as she gives us that Cajun cooking lesson she promised before any vegan thing happens. Red beans and rice with tofu just does not sound appetizing to me.<br /> <br /> In the end, nothing was decided for good today. Trinh\u2019s Fetch wants some time to think about it, and to sleep on it. She knows how to contact us when she\u2019s reached a decision, or if she decides that she needs more information. We thanked Lowjack for his help, piled into the van, and headed back to the Dream House.<br /> <br /> Luna looked as uncomfortable as I\u2019d ever seen her when we returned. \u201cLori,\u201d she said, \u201cI need you to talk to your friends. They got into an argument with Julia. I separated them before things went too far, but\u2026 Julia is very upset.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShit,\u201d I murmured. \u201cThanks for letting me know. I\u2019ll take care of it.\u201d<br /> <br /> I found Julia in the theater, fuming. \u201cShe owes me an apology,\u201d she said at once, loudly, when I walked up.<br /> <br /> \u201cWho does, sweetie?\u201d I asked calmly, taking a seat next to her. \u201cAnd why?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMelissa,\u201d she growled. \u201cWe were in the attic. I was painting\u2026 you know, some dark and mysterious forest landscapes inspired by our camping trip.\u201d Well, the woods of Southern California are about as far from dark and mysterious as woods get, but I let that pass for the moment. \u201cThen she started interrogating me about my religion. Then she got insulting. She called me a witch, and accused me of casting spells and transforming children and\u2026 and\u2026 subverting your religion! Lori, I\u2019m not even that devout, but that\u2019s no reason for her to <u><u>insult</u></u> me like that!\u201d<br /> <br /> I took her in my arms. \u201cYou\u2019re absolutely right, honey,\u201d I soothed. \u201cI\u2019ll talk to her about this, I promise. In the meantime\u2026 you have every reason to be upset, but I want to ask you to be patient with her.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI think I\u2019ve <u><u>been</u></u> pretty patient,\u201d she snapped.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou have,\u201d I agreed, \u201cand I\u2019m grateful for that. But these are exceptional circumstances. You\u2019re in the right, and she\u2019s in the wrong. I\u2019m not questioning that. But she\u2019s dealing with some pretty heavy shit right now. It doesn\u2019t excuse what she said, but\u2026 can you be patient for a little longer? For me? Please?\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded, and kissed me, but I could see the shimmer of tears in her eyes. She was <u><u>really</u></u> upset. \u201cThanks, honey,\u201d I said softly. \u201cI love you, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLove you too,\u201d she said after a moment, and then \u201cwhere\u2019s the damned punching bag?\u201d<br /> <br /> Calamity and Marguerite took her downstairs, and I made my way up to the guest bedroom. I knocked on the door. \u201cIt\u2019s me,\u201d I said a moment later, after nobody had answered.<br /> <br /> \u201cThank God,\u201d Jane muttered as she opened the door. \u201cPlease talk to her, Jules.\u201d<br /> <br /> Missy sat on the bed, looking toward the window, her golden wings quivering with agitation. I walked up and sat down next to her, and put my arm around her shoulders. \u201cWant to talk about it?\u201d I asked softly, and she took in a shuddering breath.<br /> <br /> \u201cSorry,\u201d she said eventually, \u201cbut I don\u2019t like it here, Jules. Everything is so different from what I know and what I understand. I mean, Julia is a <u><u>witch</u></u> and everybody\u2019s just <u><u>okay</u></u> with that? What kind of world is this? It doesn\u2019t make any sense!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know it\u2019s different, Missy\u2026 I went through it too. But if you stick it out, it will get better. I promise.\u201d<br /> <br /> She looked me in the eye then, her inky black pools gazing into my own. \u201cI don\u2019t want to \u2018stick it out,\u2019 Jules,\u201d she said, and I could hear the pain in her voice. \u201cI\u2019m tired of things not making sense. Everything made sense back in our cage. I understood how everything was supposed to work there. I want to go back.\u201d<br /> <br /> It broke my heart to hear it. \u201cPlease don\u2019t say that, Missy,\u201d I begged. \u201cI know it\u2019s hard, but\u2026 we went through so much to get you back. I missed you so much. It would\u2026 I don\u2019t want to lose you again\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou could come back with us,\u201d she said without much force, \u201cback to where we all belonged\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou didn\u2019t belong there, Missy,\u201d I said, maybe a little more sharply than I had intended. \u201cIf you had really belonged there, they wouldn\u2019t have had to change you to make you fit in. And\u2026 no offense, but I\u2019m never going back there.\u201d<br /> <br /> She turned to look at Jane, who got a sort of deer-in-headlights expression. \u201cYou\u2019d go back with me, wouldn\u2019t you Jane?\u201d she asked, a little desperately.<br /> <br /> Jane looked down. \u201cOf course,\u201d she said after a while. \u201cI\u2019m never leaving you again, Missy. I love you.\u201d<br /> <br /> I couldn\u2019t let the idea gain any traction. \u201cShe\u2019d go back for you, Missy,\u201d I said softly, trying to grab her attention, \u201cbut will you stay for her?\u201d<br /> <br /> She sighed. \u201cDamn you, Jules,\u201d she said under her breath. Then she turned to really look at Jane, and I don\u2019t think she expected what she saw there. \u201cYou really don\u2019t want to go back, do you?\u201d she asked seriously.<br /> <br /> Jane shook her head. \u201cI like being free,\u201d she admitted, \u201cbut I won\u2019t let you go back alone. But\u2026\u201d She trailed off, and seemed to be gathering her courage for something. \u201cBut if we stay here, if we don\u2019t go back to the cage\u2026 we can get married.\u201d She seemed to be inordinately interested in her own feet, and it was hard to hear the next thing she muttered. \u201cIf you\u2019ll have me, of course.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay,\u201d Missy finally rescued Jane. I looked back to her, and she still had tears on her cheeks, but she was actually <u><u>smiling</u></u>. Like, <u><u>really</u></u> smiling. \u201cWe can stay. I\u2019ll try to do better. And yes, I\u2019ll marry you, if you\u2019re asking.\u201d<br /> <br /> So that lightened the mood a bit, and there was no more talk of going back to Arcadia. I promised to take them by a jewelry store in the next few days so that they could make things official. And that reminded me\u2026<br /> <br /> \u201cMissy,\u201d I said soberly after a while, \u201cI really need you to apologize to Julia.\u201d<br /> <br /> She sighed. \u201cYeah, I probably should,\u201d she agreed.<br /> <br /> \u201cLet her know that it wasn\u2019t really about her religion,\u201d I advised, \u201cit was about how overwhelmed you feel by all the differences in the world. Tell her that you understand that her religion isn\u2019t like the stereotypes. Show her that you\u2019re not a bigot. I mean, you had a Jewish friend back in Defiance, where nobody else would have given her the time of day, so I <u><u>know</u></u> that\u2019s not who you are.\u201d<br /> <br /> It still felt like there was one more thing I had to say. \u201cYou know that she\u2019s not \u2018subverting\u2019 me or anything, right? I mean, her religion doesn\u2019t even come up all that often. And I\u2019m a much more devout Christian now than I ever was back in Defiance.\u201d<br /> <br /> Missy accepted this news without argument, so we descended en masse to the theater where the good news was spread. At a glance from me, Missy dutifully walked up to Julia and said \u201cI\u2019m sorry I called you a witch.\u201d<br /> <br /> Julia, who was holding an ice-pack to her right wrist (she really should have taped her hands up before she hit the bag), snorted. \u201cI <u><u>am</u></u> a witch,\u201d she said in acid tones.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh,\u201d Missy said, a little abashed. \u201cWell, look, I\u2026 I don\u2019t really <u><u>get</u></u> this world anymore, and it sort of freaks me out sometimes. So\u2026 I\u2019m sorry I offended you, and I promise I\u2019ll try really hard not to do it again. Okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> Julia looked inclined to argue, but sighed as I took her hand in mine and applied a little healing magic. \u201cOkay,\u201d she said softly after a moment. \u201cWe\u2019re good. And\u2026 congratulations.\u201d<br /> <br /> So that\u2019s about where we left things. Not much left to do other than prepare for dinner and our <u><u>official</u></u> movie night. We\u2019re thinking of showing <u><u>Girltrash!</u> </u> again, as most of us quite enjoyed it and we think Missy and Jane would be similarly enthralled. So I\u2019ll wrap up this entry and throw on something comfortable. But not <u><u>too</u></u> comfortable\u2026 that movie always gets Maria\u2019s motor running. So, y\u2019know, I\u2019ve got that to look forward to.<br /> <br /> I love my life.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei de la Rocha</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> There are certain things I don\u2019t like waking up to, and one of them is a companion being injured pretty badly. In this case it was Trinh. We woke up and got out of our tents only to find that Trinh was up and looking rather rough, and not in the \u201cnot enough sleep\u201d kind of way. She was bruised and bleeding and she refused to talk about it. A number of us asked what happened but she wouldn\u2019t say anything. Elena even tried to talk to her alone, but to no avail. Eventually we decided to let it go and let her keep her secret. Though I did tell her that if she mysteriously acquired more injuries we were going to revisit the conversation. She agreed and allowed Lori to heal her. She also admitted when Lori asked that there was no one else that needed healing, it was just her. She also said something about it being stupid and impulsive, which brought to mind attempted suicide. She would not confirm anything though. So that was something to wake up to.<br /> <br /> After that was dealt with as much as it was going to be at the time we made a breakfast of omelets with all the remaining food from the cooler so we wouldn\u2019t have to carry it all back with us. Some people insisted in cooking their sausage links over the fire with a stick, but I stuck with the \u201ceverything omelet.\u201d I will admit that it was easier camping when I was a kid to keep things cool. We just put the cooler in a snow drift and that kept our food cold. We had good seals on the coolers too, so animals couldn\u2019t smell the food and help themselves to our breakfast while we slept.<br /> <br /> Once breakfast was over and we had cleaned up the campsite we got ready to leave. I made sure that everyone picked up every bit of trash, even it if it wasn\u2019t ours, so we could dispose of it properly on the way out. Driving back we rode in the same cars as we did on the trip to the mountains, which meant I was sharing my jeep with Luna, Stasia and Elena. I mentioned that we should set up the meeting with Trinh\u2019s fetch as soon as we could. Trinh was not in a good place and it seemed to be because she was feeling bad about her fetch being miserable. Though I suppose it was probably a good thing that she was with us instead of being alone. We couldn\u2019t stop whatever happened, but Lori could heal her. And who knows what she might have tried if she was alone in the house. Luna later admitted on the way back that she has met werewolves, in that forest in fact, but they don\u2019t like to be talked about. They especially don\u2019t like to be talked about by someone who promised to keep their existence a secret.<br /> <br /> On the way back home we stopped at McDonald\u2019s for lunch. We arranged the stop by phone and all pulled in to a McDonald\u2019s relatively close to the Dream House. I think Lori wanted to show Missy and Jane some things that hadn\u2019t changed over the years. They are still making the same sandwiches and the only thing that has really changed was the number of people served on their sign. It\u2019s now in the billions instead of millions.<br /> <br /> When we got back to the Dream House we all dropped off our stuff in our rooms and gathered at the bar. Everyone was drinking and I ended up acting as bartender for a lot of people. I didn\u2019t mind. I like my job and don\u2019t mind doing it on the weekends for friends. Conversation went all over the place from music to sports and everything in between. It was mainly about a lot of older songs having to do with trying to hook up with underage girls, or female athletes and which sports were considered mainly lesbian activities. Tennis was one of them that is apparently seen as a gay sport. Like I said, our conversation went all over the place. Luna also told the others what she had told me. About the werewolves and how they might have been listening in on our conversation. Lori apologized for not letting the subject drop last night when it first came up. All was forgiven though, so it\u2019s all good. I think some of the others were a little bit wary of camping in those woods again, but Luna assured them that the werewolf pack would keep the area free of threats. She specifically said spiritual threats. I didn\u2019t see that as a reason to not go there again, but we\u2019ll see how it goes next year at this time if anyone wants to join me.<br /> <br /> Trinh eventually did come clean so to speak. She apologized for worrying all of us and admitted that she had gone for a walk early this morning and came to a cliff. She said the view was beautiful and thought that it might be a nice last thing to see and she impulsively jumped. She changed her mind at the last minute and spread her wings and slowed her fall. I guess it was a good thing that we had the three newbies try out their wings on the stage in the backyard. If Trinh hadn\u2019t practiced enough to know how to glide then she might have hit the ground at full speed whether she wanted to or not. She was very apologetic about the whole thing and assured us that it had been impulsive and stupid and she wasn\u2019t going to try it again. We did our best to assure her that she is not a bad person and is not intentionally hurting her fetch. I guess the best thing that we could have done is get the verbal agreement that she will not try and kill herself again and just keep an eye out for her.<br /> <br /> After the serious stuff was over, or at least the life and death serious stuff, talk turned to Lori starting up at college in the Spring. Lori said that she was looking forward to it, even though she\u2019d have to drive between here and L.A. a couple times a week to go to classes. All of the introductory and general Ed. classes will be online. So that will make things a bit easier to start with. This then led to De la Rocha suggesting that when she gets into the pre-med classes that she see if Twitch can tutor her. He was apparently a very good doctor before he was taken and before Maria terrorized him in Arcadia. She said that the arrangement might help Lori with her classes and it might help Twitch ease up somewhat. De la Rocha admitted to the whole group, newbies included, what she did to Twitch in Arcadia and it wasn\u2019t nice. She targeted him specifically because he was the best doctor there. She would kill all the patients that he was working to save, that other doctors couldn\u2019t, but he could due to his skill. She helped turn him into the quivering man that he is today. Normally that might make me feel bad for him, but he didn\u2019t torture Rook because he was twitchy. He tortured Rook because in his mind the ends justified the means and he wanted to make Rook \u201csafe.\u201d Of course, the process to make someone safe in his book involved torture and a lot of drugs. I still won\u2019t forgive him. He nearly drove one of my best friends mad. Hell, I\u2019m not sure how stable Rook was at the end. I wish things had gone differently with him. I miss my friend.<br /> <br /> We also talked about more benign stuff like what we were going to do that evening. In the end we decided to watch some movies. Those movies ended up being <i><i>Blade Runner</i></i> and <i><i>Fifth Element</i></i>. Before we started the movies though I called Molly and Lowjack to get advice on how to move forward with the meeting with Trinh\u2019s fetch. I didn\u2019t go into details but did say that the sooner the better. In the end we decided on drugging the fetch\u2019s bodyguard and going over as a group around 10:00 am. After I hung up with Boss Lowjack I talked to the others about the plan and we agreed that 10:00 am sounded good. Trinh looked relieved and happy to have a meeting set up. I\u2019m just glad that Lowjack was so accommodating with me. I know Trinh promised not to do anything stupid, but the waiting was making her miserable, and I\u2019m glad we were able to relieve a little bit of the tension by getting the ball rolling on this whole situation. Now I guess we\u2019ll see how it goes. Hopefully they can come to a peaceful resolution.<br /> <br /> The movies were fun. I had seen them both before, but it was fun to watch them over again with folks that hadn\u2019t seen them. Mainly that was Missy and Jane. <i><i>Blade Runner</i></i> kind of made me think of the Changeling condition. At least if replicants were secret instead of publicly known about. We aren\u2019t quite human and yet we\u2019re trying to fit into human society. Some, like Madame Spidertoes, don\u2019t try very hard to fit in. They tend to be recluses. Then there are those like Lori who are going to school and taking modeling jobs and singing on stage. She is very much involved in human society. There are even those that are hunting us down. Sometimes to kill us, usually to just bring us back to Arcadia, but we are being hunted. Not all of us thankfully, but enough of us.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Well, that went a lot better than I was expecting. I know, I know I\u2019m not known for being the most positive person so the fact I was expecting things to go pear shaped isn\u2019t much of a surprise. Still, it was nice to have something go right for us. At least where fetches are concerned. So most of us went with Trinh to go meet her fetch. It was me, Lori, Calamity, Insincere Marguerite and De la Rocha. Our plan was for Marguerite to peek in on the meeting through a mirror and for De la Rocha, Calamity and I to be there in case things went badly. Lori was there to help with the talking. Turns out that we didn\u2019t need to do much talking, or anything at all really. We met Lowjack outside and he gave us a quick rundown of what was going to happen. He wanted to just go in first with Lori and then bring others of us in later after introductions had been made. From what I gathered Lowjack went in and presented himself as a kind of fixer. Someone that helps resolve personal issues with other people. He told the fetch that his services were already paid for by another party and that she had nothing to worry about money-wise. He even made lunch, according to Lori. After the initial meeting he brought in me and Calamity and introduced us as his bodyguards, there to keep Ms. Jackson safe. She seemed to be taking it all in stride. Then he introduced Trinh to her and there was the expected surprise. Trinh explained that they were two halves of the same person and had become separated. No mention of who was \u201creal\u201d and who wasn\u2019t. I think Lowjack coached her on what to say. After that we left Trinh and Ms. Jackson to talk and the rest of us stepped out of the room. Lowjack said that he\u2019d used a number of contracts on Ms. Jackson and could find no evidence that she was or is working for the Gentry. So that\u2019s good.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite kept us up to date on what was happening in the meeting. It seems that both women are very similar in thought and attitude. The only difference that really came out was that Ms. Jackson is a vegan and Trinh is not. Lori expressed concern about Trinh teaching us to cook Cajun food before she merges with her fetch just in case the combined person doesn\u2019t eat meat. I had to agree with that. I like Cajun food.<br /> Anyway, while we were in the house waiting for the two ladies to work things out a man came up to the front door. De la Rocha was outside keeping watch for just such an occasion and told the man he had the wrong place. The man was probably a friend of the guy that was inside the house. The guy inside was taking a drug induced nap in the front room and couldn\u2019t come out to talk. The guy outside told De la Rocha to get out of the way, only in far less polite terms, and she decked him. He went down like a lead weight and she dragged him into the front room to join his friend. Lowjack took the time to go through each of the texts on their phones so he could reply as them if the need came up. It did, and he apparently did a convincing enough job because we didn\u2019t get any more unwanted guests.<br /> <br /> After a relatively short time the meeting broke up amicably. Both women expressed gratitude for the meeting and that they would be in contact again soon. Ms. Jackson was going to get some much needed sleep and Trinh was going to come back to the Dream House. As we drove back I couldn\u2019t help but think about fetches. I know that they have some part of themselves that is from the original. It makes me wonder what of me is in my fetch. He\u2019s obviously lazier than I am. His primary goal appears to be to play in a garage band and mooch off of my parents. He is also prejudiced. I\u2019m not. I don\u2019t know if staying home with mom and dad all the time rubbed off on him, but I remember being more accepting growing up. I had a friend that was gender non-conforming. Maybe my parents didn\u2019t remember hir. I don\u2019t know. I don\u2019t know what had to change in my fetch to make him the way he is. I don\u2019t like him and still want to hit him, but I\u2019m reconsidering doing him permanent harm. He\u2019s not a real person. I know that. Elena knows that, but my parents don\u2019t. I would be hurting them, and despite what they did to Elena I still don\u2019t want to hurt them. I\u2019m also pretty sure that I would lose some respect in Elena\u2019s eyes if I had something to do with her \u201cbrother\u201d disappearing. I actually have my sister back. I have a good relationship with her and I find that I don\u2019t want to jeopardize that. I\u2019ll still watch Calamity\u2019s fetch for her, but I think I\u2019ll call off the surveillance on the little shit.<br /> <br /> We were all riding a little high when we got back so we were a little surprised when Luna came up to Lori and said that she needed to talk to her friends right away. She said that Missy had said some really bad things to Julia about her being Wiccan and corrupting Lori and the rest of us. She also said something about Julia being a Satanist. There was more to it than that, but I didn\u2019t catch all the details. Lori went off to talk to Julia, then Missy and Jane. Several minutes later Lori, Missy and Jane came downstairs and Missy apologized to Julia about the things that she said. She went on to explain that a lot had changed since her day and she\u2019s still getting used to things. Alternative religions were frowned upon and usually thought of as Satanic in some way. Even Judaism was looked down on in her home town. She also said that she is having a hard time adjusting to the world as it is and lashed out at Julia because of her own inner turmoil. Julia accepted and I think they mostly made peace. They also broke the news that Jane proposed to Missy and she said yes. Not that any of us were expecting a different outcome from that particular situation.<br /> <br /> So over all it\u2019s been a pretty good day. I was prepared this morning to have to put down a fetch, but that didn\u2019t happen. They actually worked things out and may look into merging back into one person. I\u2019ve seen one extreme reaction from a fetch so it was a nice surprise to see the other end of the spectrum. It also helped me make a decision on what to do with my own fetch, so that\u2019s good too. Then Missy and Jane get engaged. There was a little bit of tension in between all that, but it seems to be mostly worked out. All in all pretty good. Now, I wonder what movies we\u2019re going to watch tonight?<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CX</i><br /> <br /> While the RP was pretty intense this time, it was the focus, and much of what occurred was well covered by our chroniclers. Two things stand out as downplayed or missing.<br /> <br /> Lori downplayed the talk about creepy obsessions with age. Maria acquiesced to singing \u201cWhat I Got\u201d only after noting she would never sing \u201cWrong Way.\u201d When lead to a lot of talk of 50s and 60s songs in that car being about older men having sex with underage girls. It came up again later, but was dwelt on less.<br /> <br /> The other thing was Maria expressed hope Twitch could be Winter King someday. Calamity and Jacob privately bristled at that\u2026I believe Jacob noted he would never bow to him. They did not confront Maria I don\u2019t think, though.<br /> <br /> I think that covers it. Comments and Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 06-17-2018, 05:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T01:55:37-07:00","id":1231542,"title":"","content":"Lorelei gets an amazing offer, but learns terrifying secrets. Jacob and Calamity have a heart to heart about their fetches, and Insincere Marguerite makes a certain model an offer to flex her bisexuality she can no longer bear to refuse.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Oh sweet mother of almighty <u><u>fuck</u></u> what have I gotten myself into this time?<br /> <br /> I really have to learn how to say no to people when they ask me for something. It wasn\u2019t even a song I was asked for this time; it was closer to a dance. Y\u2019know, metaphorically speaking.<br /> <br /> Of course, my life didn\u2019t immediately complicate following my last entry; I had close to a day of respite between Missy\u2019s feud with Julia and the unexpected onset of the next chapter of my life. After indulging in a light supper, we settled into a relatively standard Monday movie night. Most of us had already seen the two films we selected, but we all thought they might be appropriate for the newly-engaged Missy and Jane. We started off with <u><u>Girltrash!</u> </u>, and while the lyrics and subject matter might have come as something of a shock to my oldest friends, they quickly got caught up in the music. Musicals in general are something familiar to them, and I think the somewhat adult nature of the show might have evoked fond memories of the three of us watching <u><u>Cabaret</u></u> together back in the day.<br /> <br /> We followed that up with <u><u>The Princess Bride</u></u>, because, well, as Maria put it, \u201cnobody can seriously object to <u><u>The Princess Bride</u></u>.\u201d She\u2019s right, too\u2026 that simple little fantasy romance is one of my favorite films that I\u2019ve seen since I got back, and Missy and Jane seemed to find it as enchanting as I did.<br /> <br /> As the sweet romantic overtones of the film settled into peoples\u2019 consciousness, we started to pair off for the evening. Missy and Jane excused themselves almost immediately after the final roll of the credits, making goo-goo eyes at each other that melted my heart. Calamity and Becky weren\u2019t far behind them, and Jacob and Luna followed shortly thereafter, along with Marguerite and Julia, who ended up drawing Trinh into their orbit (she seemed more than a little shell-shocked the next morning, but I\u2019m sure she\u2019ll be fine).<br /> <br /> D\u2019s passions had been stoked by <u><u>Girltrash!</u> </u>, and since when have I ever been able to resist her? She carried me off to our bedroom, and the two of us spent the rest of the night showing each other how very much in love we still are. I have a lot of girlfriends. Some are nearly as close to me as my wife (the other day Marguerite referred to herself and Julia as my \u201cbrides,\u201d which I suppose works as well as any term). But with my Maria\u2026 my love for her is all-encompassing. Without it, I have no idea what I would be. The fact that she obviously feels the same way about me is humbling.<br /> <br /> I have a dim, fuzzy memory of Maria getting up for therapy the next morning. In my semi-conscious state, I tried to convince her to stay with me, even though I know how much good the therapy sessions have done for her over the past few months. She chuckled. \u201cGo back to sleep, mi amor,\u201d she said as she brushed a lock of hair out of my face. \u201cI\u2019ll be back in a couple of hours. I\u2019ll carry you down to breakfast when I get back\u2026 you always liked that.\u201d<br /> <br /> I drifted off again almost immediately, and the next memory I have is of her strong arms lifting me off the bed. \u201cTime for breakfast,\u201d she said.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m not dressed,\u201d I protested weakly.<br /> <br /> \u201cNot my fault,\u201d she said with a smirk. \u201cI told you I would carry you down to breakfast when I got back. It\u2019s not my fault if you\u2019re not ready\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I squirmed for a couple of seconds until she let me put a long sleep shirt on, and then allowed her to hoist me into her arms once more. \u201cYou really do get off on this, don\u2019t you?\u201d she asked as I put my arms around her and nuzzled the crook of her neck softly.<br /> <br /> \u201cKnowing that my wife is the strongest person in the tri-state area?\u201d I said, stroking a bicep lovingly. \u201cYeah, I admit it\u2019s kind of a turn-on.\u201d<br /> <br /> Julia was cooking that morning, and as expected she made crepes and omelets. I opted for one of the latter, which proved interesting as I ate the entire meal with D still holding me up (come to think of it, it was probably even more difficult for her). Eventually I got her to set me down, and something like a normal Sex Breakfast ensued.<br /> <br /> I reminded everyone that I had made a dinner date with Joan and Andromeda that evening, and people started talking about what they wanted to do. Most of the couples decided to spend the evening with each other semi-exclusively, and romantic plans like walks along the beach and spending time at the pier were discussed. It was almost enough to make me sorry I was going to miss out, but Joan and Andromeda have waited more than half a year to be with me, and it wouldn\u2019t be fair to them to delay our rendezvous any longer. Plus\u2026 I\u2019ve missed the two of them, even though from my perspective it\u2019s only been a few weeks since our last dinner date. And I couldn\u2019t wait to see what was going on with that gosh-darned VCR this time.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo\u2026\u201d Jane began sheepishly at one point, \u201cyou mentioned that you knew a couple of good jewelry stores in the area, Jules\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> My excitement kicked into high gear, and I turned to Missy. \u201cWould you mind sitting in Jane\u2019s lap for fifteen minutes or so?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> She blinked, looking a little confused. \u201cNo,\u201d she said eventually, \u201cof course not.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGood, then we can take my \u2018vette,\u201d I said. \u201cJust give me a few minutes to get dressed and freshen up, and we can head out whenever you\u2019re ready.\u201d<br /> <br /> I slipped into a slinky red dress and a set of matching heels, grabbed an implausibly small handbag (really just large enough for my cell phone, keys, and a few credit cards, if I\u2019m being honest) and met the two of them in the garage. Twenty minutes later we were parking at that jewelry store run by John and Linda\u2019s friends\u2026 the one where D bought <u><u>my</u></u> engagement ring. They have some lovely rings, and I was sure Jane could find something she both liked and could afford.<br /> <br /> Oh, right\u2026 the money thing. Well, apparently Jane and Missy have been experimenting with making pledges, and their first attempt has borne fruit. The two of them have a pledge with each other (I didn\u2019t ask for the details, but I can probably guess at the terms in broad strokes), and the boon they\u2019ve been granted is a moderate financial windfall. So when I offered to help Jane make the down-payment on a ring, she declined and told me that she had it covered.<br /> <br /> When we first walked into the store, Jane announced that she was there to buy an engagement ring for her girlfriend, and indicated Missy. In point of fact, she announced this just a little bit louder than was strictly speaking necessary\u2026 she still expects people to disapprove of her lifestyle, and is willing to defend it violently if necessary. In a lot of ways, she reminds me of my love\u2026 I think that\u2019s why the two of them clashed as much as they did at first.<br /> <br /> In any case, Missy and Jane found a ring that suited them, and began the process of purchasing it. At around that point, I got a text from Princess Jolie, stating that she needed to speak with me at my earliest convenience, and could be at the Dream House at any time. I texted back that I was out ring shopping (again), and that I would be back within an hour or two, at which point I would be at her disposal. Sweet, accommodating, agreeable Lori\u2026<br /> <br /> Oh, I have one more pleasant experience to relate before things get serious. I plugged my phone into the car\u2019s sound system while we were driving and finally started listening to the soundtrack to <u><u>Hamilton</u></u>, a musical which got some major positive buzz while we were away in Arcadia. It\u2019s\u2026 good. It\u2019s more than good, in truth\u2026 it\u2019s phenomenal. I think it was a bit of a hard sell for Missy and Jane at first, as it\u2019s fairly avant-garde from a 70s perspective, but\u2026 wow.<br /> <br /> The rap and hip-hop styles of the songs allow the performers to convey a <u><u>lot</u></u> of information in a short period of time; some of those songs are so rapid-fire that they make Gilbert &amp; Sullivan patter songs seem plodding in comparison. The idea of using modern \u201crebellious\u201d music to represent the colonies and more traditional \u201cBritish Invasion\u201d style songs for the repressive regime of King George is brilliant. And casting performers of diverse races and ethnicities as the founding fathers is downright inspired. Who cares if the original George Washington was a rich white man? That\u2019s no reason that a young black boy from Detroit can\u2019t aspire to be what he was to this nation. Hell, that\u2019s what America is supposed to be <u><u>about</u></u>, isn\u2019t it?<br /> <br /> Maria doesn\u2019t care for musical theater like I do\u2026 but I think she\u2019d dig what this show represents anyway.<br /> <br /> Jolie was at the Dream House by the time we returned, with Angelica and Becky in tow. They were all dressed formally (well, Spring formally at any rate, in drop-dead sexy dresses). Jolie gave me a kiss hello, but it was instantly apparent to me that her mood was deadly serious.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat can I do for you, Princess?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cI need to speak with you, Lorelei,\u201d she said gravely. \u201cI\u2019d prefer to do so privately, but I won\u2019t object if you want your motley present. Outside of the motley though, I must insist that this matter remain confidential.\u201d Something about the way she said it (coupled with the I\u2019m-Not-Leaving-You-Jules look I was getting from D) made me opt to include the motley in the meeting. D, Jacob, Luna, and Calamity joined us; Marguerite and Julia were busy chatting up Trinh at the time.<br /> <br /> \u201cAs you know, Lorelei,\u201d Jolie began once we\u2019d all made ourselves comfortable in relative privacy, \u201cthe strain of the monarchy has weighed heavily on me over the last few years. I\u2019ve decided that, for my own sake, I need to set the crown aside\u2026 at least for a little while. The other monarchs are aware of my desire, and they\u2019ve agreed\u2026 as long as I can present them with a strong candidate for my replacement.\u201d<br /> <br /> My heart jumped into my throat. \u201cI\u2026 see,\u201d I said stupidly, waiting for her to continue.<br /> <br /> Jolie gave me a faint smile, and took my hand in hers. \u201cI spoke with Austin first, but he flat-out refused to even discuss the matter with me. I\u2019d like my replacement to be someone who is universally liked by the Spring Court\u2026 hell, by the entire Freehold if possible. Someone who can stand above the petty politics and factions that arise amidst changelings in our situation. And someone who has a well-established base of operations from which she can hold court and listen to the concerns of her constituents. I have two potential candidates in mind, as well as a few backup options. You are my first choice, but if you decline the offer, I can always ask Flores. If she doesn\u2019t want it, well\u2026 White Maria has the brains and the skills to be Queen, but there are courtiers who would be reluctant to follow her\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I think I said something witty and clever, like \u201cI\u2026 uh\u2026\u201d while sitting there with my mouth hanging open for a few seconds. Finally something she\u2019d said made it through my brain and back to my mouth. \u201cDon\u2019t you think Flores is a little\u2026 I mean, I love Flores. She\u2019s a great friend and I\u2019ll never say anything against her. But\u2026 and this is <u><u>me</u></u> saying this\u2026 I mean, she\u2019s so <u><u>innocent</u></u>\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Jolie sighed. \u201cOne term as Queen would cure her of that,\u201d she muttered darkly. \u201cLook, Lori\u2026 I came to you first after Austin declined because I honestly believe that you\u2019d be the best candidate for the job. But I will never insist you take on this burden, and if you do, I\u2019ll be happy to help you however I can with counsel or whatever else you might need. So\u2026 what do you say?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2026 uh\u2026\u201d Again, I was the picture of elegance and grace. \u201cI\u2026 don\u2019t know if you know this or not, Princess, but\u2026 I\u2019m starting up at UCLA in a few weeks\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019d heard,\u201d she nodded. \u201cCongratulations.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, my question is \u2013 and I\u2019d like a completely honest opinion on this, please \u2013 do you think I could give the office the attention it needs and still devote time to my studies <u><u>and</u></u> the operation of the Dream House?\u201d<br /> <br /> She paused to give the question serious consideration. \u201cWell\u2026 there will be a lot of overlap between the time you spend running the Dream House and the time you spend holding court as Queen\u2026 or at least that was my experience with Glamour Springs. A lot of your duties will consist of presenting yourself to your courtiers and listening to their thoughts and needs\u2026 from what I understand that\u2019s pretty much what you do <u><u>already</u></u> every night once you\u2019re done on stage. As for your academic career\u2026 I couldn\u2019t really say. You know your capabilities better than I do, but I think you\u2019d be alright, for what it\u2019s worth.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay,\u201d I said, \u201cthank you.\u201d After a moment or two of uncomfortable silence, I spoke again. \u201cI\u2019d like some time to think about this, please,\u201d I said, keeping my eyes lowered, \u201cand some time to talk it over with my motley. When do you need my answer?\u201d<br /> <br /> Jolie nodded, perhaps expecting this prudent response. \u201cI need to give my decision to the other monarchs by no later than New Year\u2019s Eve,\u201d she said, \u201cso I\u2019ll need to know by Thursday. Of course, the sooner I have an answer from you the better\u2026 especially if I end up needing to make other arrangements.\u201d She paused for a minute, and then took one of my hands in hers. \u201cLook, Lori\u2026 I\u2019m sorry to drop this on you at the last minute. I\u2019d hoped to give you more time to think about it\u2026 more time to prepare. But then you were in Arcadia for so long, and you had so much to deal with when you first got back.\u201d She looked away and quickly hid the pain that slashed across her face. \u201cBut I have to do what\u2019s best for the Freehold, and I have to do what\u2019s best for myself, and\u2026 I can\u2019t do this for another year right now. I\u2019m sorry.\u201d<br /> <br /> I squeezed her hand. \u201cI want to help you,\u201d I said softly, \u201cI really do. I just have to think about this for a while. I\u2019ll\u2026 I\u2019ll give you my answer as soon as\u2026 as soon as I can.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jolie and her honor guard took their leave after that, and I gathered the motley \u2013 the <u><u>whole</u></u> motley this time \u2013 to discuss the issue. Valid points were raised on both sides of the issue. Everyone was careful to tell me over and over that they thought I could do this, and that they would support me no matter what decision I made. I appreciated the vote of confidence\u2026 I just wish I had a little more of it myself.<br /> <br /> D fumed a bit as she opined that Jolie was trying to manipulate me. \u201cBringing up Flores was dirty pool,\u201d she seethed quietly. \u201cNow you <u><u>have</u></u> to take the crown or else you end up dumping it on her, and we all know she\u2019s not ready for it. On the other hand, you could call Jolie\u2019s bluff\u2026 now if you say no she <u><u>has</u></u> to offer the crown to Flores.\u201d For what it\u2019s worth, I think Maria\u2019s wrong about that\u2026 I don\u2019t think Jolie would do that to me. Maria thinks I\u2019m being na\u00efve, and I think she\u2019s being overly cynical. And of course, each of us finds that trait endearing in the other.<br /> <br /> Jacob said that he thought I would be a good monarch because I could provide a \u201ctempering\u201d influence on the others. To his mind, Augustine is overly zealous and Lowjack is coldly calculating, and I might be able to inject a little compassion into the mix. And from my own admittedly myopic self-evaluation, I\u2019d say he\u2019s probably right about that\u2026 at least I\u2019ll probably come down on the side of moderation rather than action more often than either of those two, if only because I\u2019ll be terrified of making an irreversible mistake.<br /> <br /> In my opinion, the strongest new argument on the \u201cpro\u201d side of things came from Marguerite. \u201cThis is a new experience for you,\u201d she said, \u201cso maybe you should take it on in the spirit of your entitlement.\u201d That gave me pause for thought, so I withdrew to my bedroom and dialed up Peg.<br /> <br /> \u201cHello, Pet,\u201d she yawned once we were connected.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, shit,\u201d I mumbled, \u201cit\u2019s the middle of the night where you are, isn\u2019t it? Sorry Peg\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo worries, Pet,\u201d she said, sounding a bit more chipper. \u201cWhat can we do for you?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI, umm\u2026 I have a question for you,\u201d I began, and then thought about the situation a little more. \u201cIt\u2019s a question I have to phrase in very general terms, I\u2019m afraid.\u201d<br /> <br /> She chuckled. \u201cGo ahead,\u201d she said.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, as you know, we\u2019re back in the world, and we\u2019ve resumed management of the Dream House,\u201d I told her. \u201cAnd my college career is about to start up in a few weeks, too. Now another opportunity has presented itself. It\u2019ll take a lot of time and dedication, and I\u2019m worried about spreading myself too thin. But I feel a certain obligation to embrace this opportunity for a variety of reasons, and I\u2019m not sure what the right thing to do is, so\u2026 help?\u201d I\u2019m sure that last word came out as a plaintive whimper.<br /> <br /> \u201cSister Lorelei,\u201d she said seriously once she realized how serious I was, \u201cthe Pilgrims of the Endless Road are here to encourage you to be your best self\u2026 to make sure that you take every opportunity to improve yourself. But the entitlement was never meant to push things on you if you can\u2019t handle them. Taking too much on yourself doesn\u2019t do anything for you\u2026 it just ensures that you can\u2019t make the most of <u>any</u> of your training. So I guess what I\u2019m tryin\u2019 to say is\u2026 take it on if you feel you can, but don\u2019t feel like you have to because you\u2019re a Pilgrim.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay,\u201d I said after I processed that. \u201cThanks. Look, I\u2019m sorry I woke you Peg. I appreciate the advice. Give Jimmy a kiss on the cheek for me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI will,\u201d she promised. And that was that. I know she did her best to advise me without having all the facts, but\u2026 her advice didn\u2019t really offer much help.<br /> <br /> D found me about fifteen minutes later. \u201cYou gonna be okay tonight?\u201d she asked. \u201cI\u2019m supposed to meet Gloria in about an hour, but I can cancel if you need me\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo,\u201d I said. \u201cI can\u2019t cancel on Joan and Andromeda, it wouldn\u2019t be fair to them. You have fun tonight. Give Gloria a big sloppy kiss for me. I\u2019ll be okay.\u201d I could tell that she wasn\u2019t really convinced, but I could also see that she trusted me to tell her if I really needed her.<br /> <br /> And so it came to pass that I was more than a little distracted as I drove across Santa Monica in my slinky red dress. Even the feeling of the wind in my wings wasn\u2019t enough to distract me from my thoughts. It didn\u2019t help that Lin-Manuel Miranda was shouting from the car\u2019s speakers about how he wasn\u2019t going to throw away his shot for most of the trip. But I knew that Joan and Andromeda were really looking forward to my visit, and they deserved nothing less than my best, so I put on my happy face as I walked up to their door.<br /> <br /> Joan answered my knock with a radiant smile. She\u2019s not always the most perceptive of women, but she knows me fairly well by now, and saw through my brittle smile in about three seconds. \u201cLorelei,\u201d she said, pulling me into a warm embrace, \u201cis everything all right?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m fine, Joan,\u201d I said, as chipper as I could manage. She gave me a serious look, and I sighed. \u201cOkay, I\u2019m not fine,\u201d I admitted, \u201cbut I will be. I had a meeting with the Princess earlier today, and I have a lot on my mind. It\u2019s not something I\u2019m allowed to talk about,\u201d I added when she started to make sympathetic noises.<br /> <br /> Andromeda emerged from the kitchen, grinning in that adorable way she has. \u201cWell whatever it is, I think we can help you put it out of your mind for a little while,\u201d she said with a twinkle.<br /> <br /> Dinner was lovely, as usual. Andromeda made steaks this time, and they were cooked and seasoned to perfection. Joan displayed remarkable patience, and waited until after we\u2019d had our dessert (gelato) to suggest that we move into the living room for a feature film.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d been waiting to see what they had planned for this portion of the dinner, and I was not disappointed. As I walked into the living room, what should I see perched atop the television set but a comically oversized VCR, obviously made of overstuffed plush. It had big googly eyes on top. The front of the doll boasted a lenticular panel which seemed to flash \u201c12:00\u201d if you tilted it back and forth. A tag on the bottom of the toy labeled it as \u201cVince the VCR.\u201d<br /> <br /> I couldn\u2019t help myself. All of my worries and cares slipped out of my mind as I desperately tried to process what I was seeing, and after a moment, I burst out laughing.<br /> <br /> \u201cI am glad you like our new VCR,\u201d Joan said stoically, with just a hint of a grin twitching at the corners of her mouth.<br /> <br /> \u201cJoan found him back in September,\u201d Andromeda confided. \u201cShe\u2019s been waiting for you to get back ever since, just so she could use this one. If you like him, he\u2019s yours.\u201d<br /> <br /> I was laughing so hard that tears ran down my cheeks. I picked up Vince and hugged him to my chest. He\u2019s the softest and cuddliest household appliance I\u2019ve ever encountered, and he\u2019s currently occupying a corner of my room, beside that life-sized Olaf doll that D won me at Disneyland.<br /> <br /> I was able to hold on to that feeling, that sense of freedom from obligation, for the rest of the night. Joan and Andromeda kept me on the verge of ecstasy until all three of us were exhausted, and we drifted off to sleep in a sweaty tangled heap.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, it seemed like no time at all had passed when the three of us woke up, and my problems were right there waiting for me once again. The two of them followed me back to the Dream House for Sex Breakfast, though, and that was fun. Most of the banter that morning revolved around teasing Julia. She maintained that she was above the sort of base and lustful activities the rest of us engage in, and of course we couldn\u2019t let it go at that. The crowning moment came when Marguerite asked me to remove my shirt. Since I\u2019m <u><u>me</u></u>, of course I complied, and Julia went sort of catatonic for a few seconds while she focused on my breasts. So I guess that answered that.<br /> <br /> Missy, Jane, and Trinh were re-introduced to Joan and Andromeda. One of them asked \u201cexactly how many girlfriends do you have, Lori?\u201d and I was forced to do a quick head-count (I came up with about eight steady girlfriends if you include Gloria, which I\u2019m not sure I do as of yet). This led to a discussion of my \u201cofficial\u201d girlfriends, which caused Jane to ask if some sort of government registration was required for that status, and\u2026 well, hilarity ensued. The sheer number of women I\u2019m currently involved with makes one think, of course\u2026 but I don\u2019t think I could stand to give any of them up. I love them all in one way or another.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s when it struck me\u2026 I have the capacity to love just about anyone to some degree. I genuinely want to help as many people as I can. I don\u2019t want to see anyone get hurt\u2026 including people I don\u2019t particularly like. And there are enough different people who care about <u>me</u> that I can be reasonably certain I\u2019ll always have a viable support network when and if I get into a situation I can\u2019t handle by myself.<br /> <br /> I have to do it. I have to take this burden from Jolie. I\u2019m capable of doing this, and it\u2019s my duty to the Freehold to be the best monarch I can be. Will I ever be as effective as Jolie, or Charlotte, or Augustine or Lowjack? I don\u2019t know (though I flatter myself that I at least won\u2019t descend to the depths of villainy represented by Darke). But I\u2019ll do the best that I can until a better candidate comes along to take up the cause.<br /> <br /> I asked to speak with the motley privately, begging the indulgence of our guests. Joan and Andromeda took their leave at this point; Becky had left some time earlier for Glamour Springs. Missy and Jane retreated to the guest room\u2026 they\u2019ve pretty much only had eyes for each other for about two days now, so that didn\u2019t really surprise anyone. Trinh also made herself scarce.<br /> <br /> Once we were alone, Calamity opened with the suggestion that we all head into L.A. that evening to check in with our friends at the Unseelie Court. \u201cCount me in,\u201d I replied, \u201cI think the girls would really enjoy it too, if that\u2019s okay with everyone.\u201d There were no objections, so it was settled.<br /> <br /> Calamity also wanted to run a new number by me for the big New Year\u2019s show. \u201cI\u2026 well I really wanted to make sure it was okay with you first,\u201d she explained. \u201cFirst of all because you\u2019re our creative director, but more importantly because you\u2019re my friend, and I won\u2019t do it if it\u2019s going to offend you.\u201d<br /> <br /> The song in question is called \u201cRevelations 22:20,\u201d and it is\u2026 wow. The song itself is slow and sultry and sexy and damn near <u>perfect</u> for a venue like ours. The lyrics\u2026 that\u2019s where the problem comes in. The performers mix innuendo and outright sexual imagery with Christian religious themes, and the combination is incredibly shocking in some cases. After listening to the song, I tentatively gave my okay for Calamity to perform it \u2013 I\u2019m all about freedom of expression, after all \u2013 but reserved the right to pull it from our schedule at a moment\u2019s notice if I found out that my Dad was going to be in the audience for a given show. Calamity agreed.<br /> <br /> Then I said what I had to say. \u201cI\u2019ve decided to take Jolie\u2019s offer,\u201d I said simply. \u201cI think I can do this if I have your support. I think I have to.\u201d<br /> <br /> The response was guarded, but generally positive. Calamity contacted Becky and confirmed that Jolie was in residence at Glamour Springs, and would be there for the rest of the afternoon. I took my leave and climbed into the \u2018vette once more.<br /> <br /> Twenty minutes later I walked past the reception desk at Glamour Springs, stopping for a moment to say hi to Chalcedony and Carla (the former and I even had a brief, pleasant \u2013 albeit somewhat stilted \u2013 conversation, so that burned bridge continues to mend). The door to Jolie\u2019s inner sanctum stood open, so I just walked on in. Four people awaited me inside. Desiree had Angelica up against a wall, but it didn\u2019t look like she minded, and the air was heavy with flirtation. Becky stood stoically next to Jolie, who sat regarding the other two with obvious amusement.<br /> <br /> She took in my mood with a glance. \u201cAngelica, Desiree,\u201d she said, instantly commanding their attention, \u201cget a room.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou don\u2019t have to ask me twice,\u201d Angelica replied, and the two of them exited, closing the door behind them.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll do it,\u201d I said quickly once they were gone. I didn\u2019t trust myself to belabor the point.<br /> <br /> \u201cExcellent,\u201d Jolie said with a brief sigh of relief, \u201cI can\u2019t thank you enough for this, Lori. Now\u2026 do you want your briefing now, or should we set something up for later?\u201d<br /> <br /> I gave a heavy sigh. \u201cI\u2019ve got an hour or two now, so we might as well get this over with,\u201d I said. In retrospect, I kind of wish I\u2019d put it off a little longer. I could have preserved my innocence for another day or two.<br /> <br /> Okay, I have to get this out of the way before I write anything else down here. D, Marguerite, I <u><u>know</u></u> that you two occasionally read my journals, and I don\u2019t mind. I don\u2019t have any secrets from you two, or from Julia. I love you all, and I <u><u>know</u></u> that you would never betray my trust. That\u2019s the only reason I\u2019m writing this stuff down at all. I feel the need to purge it by committing it to writing; otherwise it\u2019ll just fester inside and make me feel terrible. But this is some seriously heavy shit, here, and I cannot stress enough how important it is to keep it a secret\u2026 even from the rest of the motley. I\u2019ll tell them myself as soon as I feel that they need to know. But there are multiple lives on the line here, and every additional person who knows our agents\u2019 secrets makes things that much more dangerous for them.<br /> <br /> What followed was a quick-and-dirty rundown of the Lady by the Sea\u2019s campaign against Hollywood. As it turns out, the cold war isn\u2019t nearly as cold as I had assumed. We currently have four main agents working on the downfall of the Hollywood Courts and the Grand Maw. Each of them is working independently of the others and using their individual talents to strike at our enemies in different ways.<br /> <br /> The Monarchs call them the Four Horsemen.<br /> <br /> Even in the privacy of her throne room, Jolie never called any of these agents by their names. What kind of surprised me is that based on information our group has gathered over the past year or so, I already <u><u>knew</u></u> about three of them. The fourth came as\u2026 something of a shock. To put it mildly.<br /> <br /> Death was the easiest of the Horsemen for me to identify. He\u2019s been waging a campaign of pure terror on Hollywood from beneath the city. He\u2019s never seen. He strikes from stealth. He kills in terrible, messy ways which send a message to any of our enemies who might want to act against us. He makes sure that the worst of our enemies are afraid of their own shadows. He is Tommy Rawhead.<br /> <br /> Famine has been working to destabilize Hollywood\u2019s power base. He\u2019s waging a scorched-earth campaign to make it more difficult for our enemies to harvest glamour on their home turf. I didn\u2019t get \u2013 or particularly want \u2013 all of the details, but apparently he\u2019s using black magic to prevent the Hollywood changelings from drawing sustenance from human emotional energy. The only issue is that this spell also makes it more difficult for other supernatural beings in the area to feed as well, and we don\u2019t want to make enemies of the local vampires and such. Famine is Gunnar Friday.<br /> <br /> War has been waging a more traditional ground campaign against Hollywood. He\u2019s incredibly skilled at guerrilla warfare, and he\u2019s been picking his targets carefully to avoid detection. Quick surgical strikes from safe positions and carefully timed extractions ensure that he remains safe while his victims never stand a chance. War is Vic Twilight.<br /> <br /> Pestilence is\u2026<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know if I can write this.<br /> <br /> Pestilence is one of the Freehold\u2019s most intelligent members. She\u2019s an expert in toxins and contagions of all sorts. She\u2019s been working on our ace in the hole; a chemical which will directly attack any fae creature with which it comes into contact, and cause reality to reject its magical nature. The eventual hope is that this will provide a way to assassinate the Grand Maw, to remove Hollywood\u2019s A-bomb. If we can do that before they get the rogue Gentry fully under their thumb\u2026 we win.<br /> <br /> At the moment, however, the toxin is imperfect. It\u2019s incredibly virulent, and it spreads through contact, but we don\u2019t know if it will affect a full-blown Gentry the way we need it to. Changelings who are exposed to it\u2026 well, it was described to me as sort of an extreme case of magical organ transplant rejection. If I was exposed to this stuff, for example, assuming I didn\u2019t die outright, I\u2019d probably lose all of my kith abilities for a time, and would likely lose my eyes and my wings permanently. It sounds <u>horrific</u>. It\u2019s not the intended use of the contagion, but still.<br /> <br /> I felt sick to my stomach. Of course by this point I had deduced Pestilence\u2019s identity, but I didn\u2019t trust myself to speak. Jolie pressed on. \u201cActually, Lori, that\u2019s another reason I wanted you to succeed me. You see, last year Pestilence\u2019s loyalty \u2013 which had never been in question before \u2013 was compromised. She\u2019d been dutifully working on this toxin in secret for quite some time, and we were all impressed with her progress. Then one day, completely out of the blue, she just\u2026 gave some of it away. Because her girlfriend <u>asked</u> her to. And when we confronted her with this, she refused to promise that she wouldn\u2019t do the same thing again in the future.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShit,\u201d I murmured quietly. \u201cGod, Princess, I swear I had no idea\u2026 I would never have asked her to compromise herself like that\u2026 to put the Freehold at risk like that\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know,\u201d Jolie said, taking my hand once more. \u201cIn fact, I\u2019ve been your champion behind the scenes ever since. The work the Horsemen are doing is far too important to leave anything to chance, and some of the monarchs felt that you represented a dangerous wild-card where Pestilence is concerned. Death enjoys what he\u2019s doing too much to ever go against our plans, and War\u2019s loyalty to the Freehold is unquestioned\u2026 but most of us don\u2019t fully trust Famine. He\u2019s dealing with powers we don\u2019t completely understand, and that makes him unreliable. We can\u2019t afford to lose confidence in another Horseman at this point; it puts the whole plan on shaky ground.\u201d<br /> <br /> She sighed. \u201cAs I said, some of the monarchs felt that it was too dangerous to leave Pestilence vulnerable to your charms. I persuaded them that it was worth the risk to keep you active due to the glamour you bring into the Freehold and your popularity with\u2026 well, everyone. Now, of course, it won\u2019t be an issue. Now that you\u2019re in on the plan\u2026 now that you\u2019re becoming a monarch you\u2019ll be able to make sure that Pestilence\u2019s work remains intact.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cI suppose I will at that,\u201d I said. \u201cIs there anything else?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cA few minor details about the way the Freehold runs, most of which you probably know already,\u201d she said. \u201cThere are certain powerful people who are consulted whenever the big decisions are made.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLike Madame Spidertoes?\u201d I asked. \u201cI know the Freehold defers to her whenever a darkling is involved\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Jolie smiled. \u201cHonestly, that\u2019s more of a courtesy these days\u2026 she almost never goes against the monarchs\u2019 decisions. But yes, that\u2019s the sort of thing I\u2019m talking about. Honestly, Charlotte isn\u2019t the Autumn Queen because she\u2019s particularly powerful or knows more than others about evoking fear\u2026 she\u2019s just the best at glad-handling all of the other powerful Autumn Courtiers. Tommy, Madame Spidertoes, Annika, and Oleander\u2026 they\u2019re all very strong, and they all have very\u2026 \u2018quirky\u2019 personalities. Charlotte is a miracle worker when it comes to wrangling them.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo that\u2019s the sort of thing I\u2019ll be doing?\u201d I asked. \u201cTrying to keep the peace between various members of the Spring Court?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s a big part of it,\u201d she admitted, \u201cwhich is one of the reasons I wanted you for the job. Of course, compared to the Autumn Court, managing our people is easy. And though it\u2019s not an <u><u>official</u></u> part of the job, I\u2019ll also be counting on you to keep the peace between Augustine and Lowjack. They\u2019re not enemies per se, but they approach problems from very different angles. Augustine sees Lowjack as a bit of a dishonorable schemer, while Lowjack thinks of Augustine as a blunt instrument.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGot it. And the policy on sharing any of this information?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> She lowered her gaze. \u201cSecrecy is paramount,\u201d she admitted. \u201cHollywood has spies everywhere. Siobhan is only the most obvious of their spies. They\u2019ve been trying to determine the identities of our Four Horsemen for a couple of years now, and would almost certainly do everything in their power to murder them if they uncovered that information. The more people who know about this, the more likely it is that something will slip eventually. Now having said that, most of the monarchs have their confidantes. Lowjack tells Tamara just about everything. Becky and Angelica are privy to Court business as well. So I\u2019m not going to tell you to keep this from anyone. Just use your best judgment, and remember what\u2019s at stake.\u201d<br /> <br /> There was only one other thing I wanted to know. \u201cAnd\u2026 Lucian Torrez?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> She scowled. \u201cLucian is one of the most dangerous men I know. He has something on Augustine, and he pulls his strings in ways both subtle and overt. Best not to get on his bad side. If you ever do, I only have one bit of advice. I\u2019ve seen Lucian frightened exactly <u><u>once</u></u> since I came to this Freehold. One day, Lucian pushed a little too hard, and Augustine got fed up with him\u2026 he told Lucian that if he wanted control that badly, Augustine would gladly give up the crown so that Lucian could step in and run things directly. Lucian backed down. He didn\u2019t look like a man that didn\u2019t want to step out of the shadows\u2026 he looked like a man who was scared for his life. I don\u2019t know what the deal is there, but you might be able to use it if you ever get into a tight spot with him.\u201d<br /> <br /> It was a lot to take in. \u201cI understand. Anything else?\u201d<br /> <br /> She looked into my eyes for a moment, and then smiled sadly. \u201cNothing that can\u2019t wait,\u201d she said, putting a hand on my shoulder. \u201cI expect you\u2019ll want to get back home. You have a lot to think about. So get some rest\u2026 that\u2019s an order from a friend who is still your Queen for another two days.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay,\u201d I said, giving her a weak smile.<br /> <br /> And then I left.<br /> <br /> I turned down the radio as I drove back. I wanted to be able to hear myself think, and music doesn\u2019t often leave room in my head for much else. I drove back to the Dream House, keeping to the speed limit for once, and parked in the garage. I walked in through the theater and made my way straight for the bar, where I grabbed a bottle of non-snooty bourbon and a clean glass. I poured myself a stiff drink while the others approached.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou okay, Lori?\u201d Calamity asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah,\u201d I said, downing the drink quickly.<br /> <br /> Jacob shot me a disbelieving glance, and asked if he needed to take my keys.<br /> <br /> I shook my head. \u201cOkay, no, I\u2019m not really okay,\u201d I amended my previous response. \u201cBut I will be. I just need to think about some things.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLike what?\u201d Calamity asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cLike\u2026 things I learned while I was talking with Jolie about taking over the crown,\u201d I replied. \u201cThings that I can\u2019t really talk about right now. Look, I would trust you all with anything, you know that, but I just\u2026 I can\u2019t talk about this stuff right now. I promise I\u2019ll tell you the instant I can, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSure, Lori,\u201d Calamity replied, but she seemed a little glum.<br /> <br /> \u201cHey babe,\u201d D said as she walked up to the bar. \u201cYou ready to hit the club tonight?\u201d<br /> <br /> I sighed. \u201cI don\u2019t feel much like dancing right now,\u201d I said to general astonishment.<br /> <br /> D put her arms around me. \u201cI\u2019ll stay here with you,\u201d she offered. She was disappointed, but completely willing to sacrifice her evening for my sake.<br /> <br /> I gave her a smile. \u201cNo, you go on ahead and have fun, sweetie,\u201d I said. \u201cI just doubt I\u2019d be very good company tonight.\u201d<br /> <br /> She resisted briefly, but eventually consented to go with the others. Missy and Jane were only a slightly easier sell; they could tell that something was wrong almost instantly and wanted to do something to help me. It complicated matters that I couldn\u2019t even tell them about the whole Spring Queen thing; they were completely in the dark. In the end, they agreed to join the others for a night on the town, though. I made D promise to keep an eye on them.<br /> <br /> Once everyone was out of the house, I sat alone in the dark for a hundred-count, then pulled out my phone and speed-dialed Oleander. She picked up on the third ring. \u201cHello, Angel\u2026 this is an unexpected surprise!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAre you toxic today?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cOnly a little bit,\u201d she replied.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo you could whip up an antidote if I needed to see you?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cSure\u2026 I could have it ready any time.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGood. I need to see you,\u201d I said.<br /> <br /> \u201cMy evening\u2019s completely free as of now,\u201d she replied.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll be there in twenty minutes,\u201d I said. \u201cLove you.\u201d I hung up after she replied in kind.<br /> <br /> She met me at the door as I arrived, a pill and a bottle of water in hand. I took them both from her carefully, swallowed the pill, and downed about half of the bottle. \u201cHow long?\u201d I asked by way of a greeting.<br /> <br /> \u201cAbout ten minutes,\u201d she answered, clearly a little confused by my bizarre behavior. She doesn\u2019t always pick up on social cues\u2026 but she knows me more than well enough to determine that something was wrong.<br /> <br /> We sat around her kitchen table and made awkward small talk for the next ten minutes. \u201cSafe now?\u201d I asked, standing up.<br /> <br /> She glanced at her watch. \u201cShould be,\u201d she agreed.<br /> <br /> I planted myself in her lap and put my arms around her neck. \u201cI need to talk to you about something serious,\u201d I said.<br /> <br /> Her brow knit slightly. \u201cOf course, Angel. You can tell me anything. What\u2019s on your mind?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2026 learned a few things today,\u201d I began, trying to work up my courage, \u201cthings I think we should discuss. But before I start, I want you to know one thing.\u201d<br /> <br /> She gave me a nervous smile. \u201cYou\u2019re starting to scare me a little,\u201d she admitted.<br /> <br /> \u201cI love you,\u201d I said. \u201cNothing we\u2019re about to talk about changes that. Nothing ever could. I just want you to know that I will always love you\u2026\u201d I took a deep breath and closed my eyes, and then took the plunge. \u201c\u2026Agent Pestilence.\u201d<br /> <br /> The color drained out of her face in about a second, and for the first time since I\u2019ve known her, she looked like she might be sick. \u201cWhere did you hear that name?\u201d she asked faintly.<br /> <br /> I tightened my grip on her shoulders. \u201cJolie is stepping down as Spring Queen at the turn of the year,\u201d I told her, \u201cand it looks like I\u2019ll be taking her place. I was\u2026 \u2018debriefed\u2019 on the ongoing conflict with Hollywood this afternoon.\u201d<br /> <br /> She exhaled a sigh of relief. \u201cOh, thank God,\u201d she muttered, \u201cI had no idea how I was going to handle that. Nobody is supposed to connect that name to me. Look, I can give you a progress update if you want. Things are very promising, actually\u2026 I\u2019ve managed to tweak the toxin so that instead of just simple rejection of Arcadian features, the virus causes <u><u>violent</u></u> rejection, so we\u2019ve achieved a weaponized state. I\u2019m confident that in time I\u2019ll be able to\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> She went on like that for a few minutes, citing scientific minutiae that I could only barely recognize from my epidemiology texts, let alone comprehend. From what I could gather, though, it seems like she really is making progress, and given a little more time we should have a potent weapon to use against the Grand Maw. The only question is whether we\u2019ll achieve that before the Hollywood Courts gain complete control over the Gentry. The arms race is on, and I\u2019ll shortly be an active part of it. Huzzah.<br /> <br /> \u201cJust\u2026 promise me one thing,\u201d I said softly when I could get a word in edgewise. \u201cJust promise me that you\u2019re taking every precaution with this thing. It seems like it could be incredibly dangerous with just the slightest misstep\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course I am,\u201d Oleander said, pulling me back into her arms and giving me a squeeze. \u201cYou know how careful I am with my lab. Hell, Angel, I have contingency plans in place that will completely purge everything in the interior of the lab if it becomes necessary\u2026 including me.\u201d<br /> <br /> Well <u><u>that</u></u> certainly makes me feel better. Sigh.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd don\u2019t worry,\u201d she continued, \u201ceven if Hollywood did somehow get their hands on this stuff, they don\u2019t have access to my delivery mechanism, so they couldn\u2019t use it.\u201d She paused for a minute and thought about it. \u201cWell\u2026 technically I suppose they could use it, but they\u2019d have to expose the virus manually, and anyone who did that would be dead pretty much instantly.\u201d<br /> <br /> I let the conversation drift after that. I wanted to forget my troubles. It didn\u2019t work. Oleander and I spent a romantic evening together, and it was very nice, and we reveled in the love that we obviously feel for each other. And now she\u2019s sleeping the sleep of the just, and I\u2019m frantically scribbling my thoughts down in this diary, desperately trying to make sense of all this new information\u2026 and all of these new responsibilities.<br /> <br /> I texted D that I was spending the night at Oleander\u2019s, that I would see her in the morning, and that I was fine. I lied. I\u2019m not fine. And it doesn\u2019t look like I\u2019m going to be fine again anytime soon.<br /> <br /> I keep coming back to something Oleander said a few hours ago. She told me in no uncertain terms that Hollywood didn\u2019t have access to her \u201cdelivery mechanism\u201d for the deadly Pestilence virus. And the more I think about that, the less I like it. Because I have a sneaking suspicion that Oleander wasn\u2019t talking about a clever mechanical device for aerating the virus over a specific area. I think she was talking about her own unique physiology. I think she\u2019s going to\u2026 to <u><u>impregnate</u></u> herself with that horrific stuff and unleash it on Hollywood <u><u>herself</u></u>. And that means that \u2013 assuming everything goes <u><u>right</u></u> with this plan \u2013 she\u2019ll be dangling herself in front of the Grand Maw like a worm on a hook.<br /> <br /> As Oleander\u2019s girlfriend, I <u><u>can\u2019t</u></u> let that happen.<br /> <br /> As a monarch of this Freehold, I may <u><u>have</u></u> to let that happen.<br /> <br /> What the hell am I going to do?<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei de la Rocha</b></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 07-01-2018, 05:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T01:56:28-07:00","id":1231543,"title":"","content":"<b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Okay\u2026.we ended up watching <i><i>Girl Trash!</i> </i> and <i><i>Princess Bride</i></i> tonight for movie night. Two movie nights in a row, but it was all good. Missy and Jane seemed to like <i><i>Girl Trash!</i> </i> and had cute little smiles on their faces when we watched <i><i>Princess Bride</i></i>. It is a fun movie so that was all good. Overall the night was a success.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> So today in therapy I brought up what my parents and fetch said to Elena at Thanksgiving. I admitted that I was upset by their actions. Sullivan latched onto the fact that I was being very supportive of my sister, which is good. I wanted to tell him \u201cDuh, of course I\u2019m being supportive, she\u2019s my sister,\u201d but I didn\u2019t. I just replied that she\u2019s my twin and left it at that. He was taking my reaction to the situation in a good way and telling me that he was proud of my reaction to the events. I think he\u2019d be a little less proud of me if he knew what I\u2019d been considering doing with my fetch. I\u2019m pretty sure that he would see it as murder even though the little shit isn\u2019t a real person. If I were to kill him he would just fall into his component pieces. I\u2019m sure ice would be in there somewhere. I have already decided to let him be though, so I figured there was no point in bringing this up with Sullivan. I wonder if I admitted to him that I\u2019d been contemplating killing my fetch, would he be required to tell someone about it? He couldn\u2019t tell the mortal police without compromising the Freehold. Would he tell Boss Lowjack since he\u2019s in charge at the moment? I\u2019m not sure if Boss Lowjack would be upset at me taking out my own fetch. It\u2019s not a member of the Freehold in good standing. It\u2019s not even human. I\u2019m not going to find out though. Best to play this one close to the chest.<br /> <br /> When we got back from therapy Julia was making crepes and cheese omelets for everyone. Insincere Marguerite loves crepes so it was no surprise that they showed up on the menu for today. Lunch was a fairly quiet affair over all. After it was over Lori took Missy and Jane out to go looking for an engagement ring for Missy. I\u2019m sure that they had fun.<br /> <br /> Once I could be sure that we\u2019d have a private conversation I talked to Calamity and let her know that I was calling off the investigation into my fetch. I explained that if I did anything to it then it would hurt my parents because they still think that it is their son. Killing it might also upset Elena. She knows that the fetch isn\u2019t a real person, but it walks and talks like one and killing it would practically be the same as killing a person. Calamity took this all in stride and agreed that Elena might not understand if I killed the little shit. I did tell her that I would still look into following her fetch and see what it is up to and what kind of person it is. The scary thing about Calamity\u2019s fetch is that it has a child. Not adopted, but an actual child. That shouldn\u2019t be possible. It does happen in rare cases though, and the result is usually a soulless abomination. Right now it is apparently still acting like a child which is all for the good. Of course this is all rumor, but I\u2019ve heard this from a couple of sources so it might hold some water. I\u2019m assuming if Calamity actually gets close to the fetch and her family then things might change. Hence me going to take a peek. If I remember right the children of fetches can see us as we are. Or at least sometimes they can, so I may not be able to blend as well as I\u2019m hoping to. I\u2019m going to see about using that contract that Molly taught me and see if that works.<br /> <br /> Later, when Lori and the two lovebirds got back Princess Jolie stopped by for a visit. She wanted to talk to Lori about something private. She said that she didn\u2019t mind the motley hearing what she had to say, but we had to promise to keep it to ourselves for now. So, Missy and Jane went off to entertain themselves and Insincere Marguerite and Julia took Trinh away to talk. So it was just Lori, me, Luna and Calamity there for the talk. The talk turned out to be pretty serious business. Jolie wants to take some time off from being Spring Queen and is trying to find a replacement. She thought that Lori would make a good monarch. She has a level head on her shoulders and is pretty much universally liked by not just the Spring Court but the Freehold in general. Lori, to say the least, was overwhelmed. I\u2019ve never seen her at such a loss for words. Jolie did say that she would need an answer pretty soon because she was going to make the announcement on New Year\u2019s. She did mention that if Lori didn\u2019t want to do it then she was going to ask Flores. Lori managed to respond to that and brought up the fact that we were all thinking. Flores is liked by pretty much everyone, but she is such an innocent. She might not be up to handling the politics of the Freehold.<br /> <br /> After Jolie left we talked for a little while longer about Jolie\u2019s offer. We all told Lori that we\u2019d support her if she wanted to take on the mantle of Spring Queen. I offered that I thought she would be a good influence on the other monarchs. She is down to earth and thinks with her heart first, which makes her an empathetic and kind person. We discussed the pros and cons of her doing this. One thing that came up that I had forgotten about is that Lori is going to be starting college in the Spring semester, so sometime in January. That is going to take up a good bit of time. Plus she performs at the Dream House. If she decides to take on the mantle of Spring Queen she may need to do fewer performances. The club though would make a good place for her to hold court. Insincere Marguerite also brought up the fact that Lori is a Pilgrim of the Endless Road now and they might be of the opinion that she should do this because it is an opportunity to do something new and different. She did not decide then what she wanted to do, and that\u2019s fine. Lori needs time to think things over. We can\u2019t make the decision for her, nor should we. This is something big and she needs to figure it out on her own.<br /> <br /> Once all the excitement was over people started splitting up to do things with their significant others. Lori got ready to go over to Joan and Andromeda\u2019s house to have dinner and \u201cwatch a feature film.\u201d As far as I know the feature film aspect of the night has never taken place due to a broken VCR. It\u2019s not like she\u2019s actually there for a movie anyway. Julia and Insincere Marguerite went to the Pier and Luna and I went for a moonlit walk on the beach. We haven\u2019t done anything alone for a while and thought that it might be nice to spend some time alone with my Luna. She seemed pleased by the idea and we went to the beach. We also got some ice cream from a soft serve place.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll never get bored of watching the moon reflect in the water and of seeing the same moonlight dance across my Luna\u2019s beautiful wings. It makes them look iridescent. The Lady\u2019s realm is always in twilight. Not quite day and not quite night, so I have found ways to enjoy the day time and night time in \u2018the world.\u2019 Sunset will always remind me of the Lady. I can\u2019t help that. I lived in Arcadia too long for that not to be an association. But here in \u2018the world\u2019 I can enjoy the night time with my lover.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> I\u2019m worried about Lori. She was fine this morning when she got back with Joan and Andromeda for sex breakfast, but later this afternoon she was less than good. Okay\u2026so the day started out like any other. The sex breakfast conversation may have been a little more risqu\u00e9 than usual but it was all in good fun. There was conversation about lust and Julia got teased for lusting after people. She insists that she doesn\u2019t and that she does not feel such base emotions. She got proven wrong when Lori took off her shirt and stood in front of Julia. Julia couldn\u2019t keep her eyes off of Lori\u2019s breasts and eventually gave in to temptation and buried her face in Lori\u2019s chest. It was kind of cute. After she pulled away Julia looked sheepish and said that there was nothing to see. Julia eventually asked Lori to put her shirt back on and conversation continued, this time about sexuality. Though they did veer into the question of how many girlfriends Lori has. I think the answer was eight, if you count Gloria. Lori doesn\u2019t count her yet, so she insists on seven. And that\u2019s just who she\u2019s romantically involved with. She has several more partners. I don\u2019t see how she keeps it all straight and how she keeps some people from getting jealous over others. I think it would be too much trouble. I\u2019m quite happy with just my Luna.<br /> <br /> Later in the afternoon Lori called a motley meeting, so Trinh, Jane and Missy excused themselves while we talked. Lori said that she was going to take Jolie up on the offer and become the next Spring Queen. She then went to Glamour Springs to talk to Princess Jolie about her decision. Apparently Jolie also elected to give Lori a crash course in what she was going to need to know to be Queen. Lori said that she could not tell us what she learned, but I could tell that it was something that shook her up rather badly. The first thing she did when she got back from Glamour Springs was head straight for the bar and pour herself a good stiff drink. She kept a hold of the bottle and looked for all the world like she was going to do her best to make a dent in the contents. I asked her if I needed to collect her keys and she looked up at me for a moment before putting the bourbon back on the shelf. She said that she would stop there just in case she decided to go out tonight.<br /> <br /> The plan had been to all go out to The Unseelie Court, but Lori said that she had a lot to think about and would not be joining us. Missy and Jane looked a little disappointed but there were plenty of people there to keep an eye out for our two girls out of time. The club was fun. Luna and I danced and had a couple of drinks. We watched the others have a good time and head off Corbin and Strype before they could reach Missy and Jane. That was mainly De la Rocha I think, but everyone kept an eye out for that pair. Insincere Marguerite and Julia kept a particularly keen eye on Trinh. We got back to the Dream House somewhat late and Lori was nowhere to be seen. Apparently she was going to spend the night with Oleander. At least according to De la Rocha, that\u2019s where she went. Makes me wonder why Lori felt she could find solace with Oleander when she couldn\u2019t with her wife. Whatever the reason it\u2019s probably a good one. And maybe someday Lori will tell us what she learned that upset her so much. I know that what she learned was probably for Monarch eyes only, but I hope she knows that she can trust us to keep a secret, and we will do our best to support her regardless. I know what it is to keep secrets. They weigh down on you. I hope Lori will be up to keeping hers. I have a feeling that the less people that know about it the better.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXI</i><br /> <br /> Oh let\u2019s see.<br /> <br /> <i>Girltrash! All Night Long</i> is just the best. This was your regularly scheduled plug for best lesbian punk musical around. Talking of entertainment, Rev. 22:20 Dry Martini Mix is a slow, sensual gothy song that is a HELL of a lot of fun to dance to at Goth clubs, though serious content warning for the lyrics.<br /> <br /> Okay this little twist has been building for awhile and does constitute a shift in the campaign. Gotta keep things fresh! Similarly, the Horseman revelation has been implied, but now you know what Tommy, Gunnar, Vic and Oleander have actually been up to. Gunnar is of course using the same magic he was in the story of Mary\u2019s Fetch, remember?<br /> <br /> Speaking of Fetches, some indecision it seems about that. I am not even sure where this will go.<br /> <br /> I totally saw one of those stuffed VCRs in a mall ages ago, but can\u2019t find it on the internet now (I tried to find a picture for a prop on my phone, but no dice).<br /> <br /> Okay, New Years happens tonight. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T13:40:06-07:00","id":1235323,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s New Years Eve as the Motley rings in 2016. Poor bastards.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Okay, in a few hours I will <u><u>officially</u></u> be the Spring Queen, and my nerves are really starting to make themselves known now. But oddly, it\u2019s not the coronation itself that has me trembling like a newborn colt. I mean, let\u2019s face it\u2026 if there\u2019s one part of this job that I\u2019m very well suited to, it\u2019s the public events. A little face-time with the Freehold, a short speech, and an hour or two of schmoozing\u2026 I was born for that sort of thing. It\u2019s everything that comes <u><u>after</u></u> the coronation that has me worried.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t sleep at all the night after I accepted the crown and got that terrible debriefing from Jolie. I sat there watching Oleander sleep, loving her with all of my heart and yet uneasy about the things she was doing for the Freehold. When we\u2019d talked about it that evening, she\u2019d been so <u><u>proud</u></u> of what she had accomplished, describing the fascinating effects of the toxin with clinical detachment. She was talking about violent organ rejection \u2013 about horrible, agonizing deaths \u2013 with <u><u>clinical</u> <u>detachment</u></u>. It doesn\u2019t change the way I feel about her\u2026 not really. But\u2026<br /> <br /> Once the sun was in the sky, I wandered into Oleander\u2019s kitchen and dialed Dark Kimberly. I had decided that my first duty as a monarch was to demonstrate to the Freehold that we\u2019d have a smooth, seamless transition. That meant looking like I was prepared to take the reins of power with hardly a second thought; like I\u2019d be prepared for any unexpected eventuality. And in a group like the Spring Court, as silly as it might sound, that meant obtaining a fabulous new outfit as quickly as possible.<br /> <br /> Kimberly answered on the fourth or fifth ring. \u201cHello?\u201d she moaned out groggily.<br /> <br /> \u201cKimberly,\u201d I said softly, \u201cit\u2019s Lori. I hope I didn\u2019t wake you\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s fine,\u201d she said with just a touch of peevishness.<br /> <br /> \u201cGod,\u201d I said, \u201cI\u2019m sorry. I just\u2026 I need to ask you a favor. I desperately need a new hedgespun dress, and I need it by tonight. I\u2019ll pay you, of course\u2026 double whatever you usually charge for something like\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLori,\u201d she said, cutting me off, \u201cI\u2019ll be happy to help you. Don\u2019t worry about the cost right now. But this needs to be a longer and more involved discussion. Are you going to announce it tonight, then?\u201d<br /> <br /> That brought me up short. \u201cYou know?\u201d I asked. Jolie had been pretty adamant that we not spread word of the change beyond the motley.<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course I know,\u201d she said with a yawn, \u201cI\u2019m your event planner. I was going to stop by the Dream House pretty early today anyway, to finalize a few things. What time can my team and I show up without worrying about waking anyone?\u201d<br /> <br /> I thought about it for a second. \u201cEveryone\u2019s usually up and at breakfast by noon,\u201d I said. \u201cJeez, Kimberly, I\u2019m even sorrier now for waking you\u2026 if I\u2019d known you already had things in hand, I never would have\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t worry about it,\u201d she said again, \u201cthere\u2019s still time for me to catch another couple of hours of sleep\u2026 and after that I\u2019ll be too busy to care. And Lori\u2026 congratulations.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks,\u201d I said, and we disconnected.<br /> <br /> I slipped back into bed with Oleander and continued to not sleep for the bulk of the morning. She eventually got up and we both showered and headed over to the Dream House. In addition to the usual suspects and the girls, Becky and Gloria were there. Trinh was cooking up some sizzling sausages at the stove. She had them carefully divided into three groups\u2026 \u201cweak,\u201d \u201cspicy,\u201d and \u201chow I like them,\u201d as she put it. The former two were seasoned with traditional Cajun spices, while the latter had some Vietnamese spices thrown into the mix. Some of the more daring members of the motley \u2013 like Calamity and D \u2013 tried the really spicy ones, with varying degrees of comedic results. I stuck with the spicy for the moment; they were plenty hot enough for my tastes. I did have a tiny nibble of the <u><u>really</u></u> spicy sausage later, but it made my eyes water and I lost the ability to speak for several minutes (much to everyone\u2019s apparent amusement).<br /> <br /> I asked how everybody had enjoyed the Unseelie Court. It sounds like they had fun. D quietly acknowledged that she had kept an eye on Missy and Jane all evening, and had scared off a few predators. Those two were maybe a little bit overwhelmed by the Court, but they took to it well after they acclimated to the sensory overload.<br /> <br /> Maria, Calamity, Jacob, Missy and Jane had gone to therapy that morning, and Calamity reported that the Winter Court\u2019s therapists believed Missy and Jane were progressing well, and that it would no longer be strictly necessary to keep the ankle bracelets on them. They still bear watching, and the therapists were less pleased with how reliant upon each other they still are\u2026 but they don\u2019t think that my best friends are a true flight risk anymore. So it was with a great deal of relief that I produced the key and removed the anklets from their shapely calves.<br /> <br /> (It was a relief in more ways than one, actually\u2026 I mean, not to be crude, but those things really hurt when you bang your shin on one of them in the heat of passion.)<br /> <br /> At some point we began talking about our respective ages, and I got a bit of a shock. Oleander has never really talked much about her past. It obviously makes her a bit uncomfortable, and I haven\u2019t wanted to pry. I have always known that she\u2019s older than me\u2026 hell, she looks like she\u2019s somewhere in her 30s, and I know her connection to the Wyrd is at least as strong as mine, so I\u2019ve always assumed she\u2019s older than she looks. But I didn\u2019t expect to learn that she had already escaped Arcadia and been back in the world for six years when I was <u><u>born</u></u>. It doesn\u2019t bother me, mind you\u2026 but it did surprise me.<br /> <br /> There were a few other revelations as well, which elicited varying degrees of surprise. Annika fled Germany when the Nazis took power in the 30s. Tommy is at least a hundred years old, though he hasn\u2019t been active in this Freehold for that long. And Madame Spidertoes has been heard on various occasions to speak of the Terror \u2013 as in the French Revolution \u2013 as though it was something she witnessed personally. Wow.<br /> <br /> So we were still nibbling on sausages and shooting the shit when Dark Kimberly and her coterie arrived. Accompanying her were Davie, Andromeda, and \u2013 for some bizarre reason \u2013 TJ. When I asked about his presence, he simply commented \u201cI like the pageantry,\u201d though he eventually admitted that he was really there in case anyone needed him to lift something heavy. Though there was some light banter and some sharing of sausages (both Kimberly and TJ had the extra-spicy version, and again, hilarity ensued) for the most part we got straight down to business.<br /> <br /> Kimberly had a lot of questions regarding how I wanted the coronation to go\u2026 some of them about things that I hadn\u2019t even considered. The drama queen in me wanted a big reveal, so I asked Kimberly to keep the identity of Jolie\u2019s successor a secret until the coronation itself. She said that Jolie intended to send an email out later that night announcing her abdication, and that she would alter the email so that it stated that the next Queen would be announced at an event the following day. We set the event at Glamour Springs so as to preserve the mystery.<br /> <br /> All in all, I decided to go for an elegant, understated ceremony. We\u2019re going to have a live band providing soft jazz for ambiance. There\u2019s no particular dress code for the guests, excepting that I want everything to be tasteful. According to Kimberly, Austin\u2019s coronation was fairly debauched, with no clothing allowed beyond a certain point. Though I know my reputation in the Freehold, I decided to go for something a little more modest than that.<br /> <br /> Maria will be by my side when I accept the crown. My motley will be gathered around me in a show of support. I want to assure the Court that even though I\u2019m inexperienced, I\u2019ll have a lot of capable and competent advisors backing me up.<br /> <br /> I went