dliner in past tense terms\u2026 and was vaguely surprised to realize that I\u2019m starting to <u><u>think</u></u> of it in that way as well. I mean, I doubt the two of us will ever be really close or anything, but\u2026 I just don\u2019t see the <u><u>point</u></u> of maintaining that sort of hatred anymore. Maybe I\u2019m\u2026 I dunno, growing as a person or some shit.<br /> <br /> Much of the rest of the day was spent preparing for our New Year\u2019s Eve show. It was a significant production for several reasons: it was our first show back after closing for the Christmas holiday, it marked the motley\u2019s official return to our positions as managers, and it marked Missy and Jane\u2019s professional stage debut. The two of them had agreed to back me up on a couple of numbers that evening to sort of get their feet wet before headlining their own acts. I set them up with recordings of the songs in question so that they could familiarize themselves with the lyrics and harmonies. We sketched out some rough choreography too\u2026 mostly so that Marguerite would know how to light us, as we\u2019ve always been pretty good at reading each other and reacting accordingly.<br /> <br /> And speaking of Marguerite\u2026 as the hour of the show approached, I noticed her walking around, obviously distracted and clearly shell-shocked about something. I approached her and asked if everything was alright, and she shook her head without answering. I took her in my arms. \u201cWhat\u2019s wrong, sweetie?\u201d I asked, starting to get really concerned.<br /> <br /> She looked into my eyes. \u201cI saw\u2026 the thing,\u201d she said mysteriously.<br /> <br /> It took me a moment before I realized that she must have read my last diary entry. \u201cOh, honey,\u201d I said hugging her tighter. \u201cI know. It\u2019s awful, and I don\u2019t know what I\u2019m gonna do about it\u2026 or if I even <u><u>should</u></u> do anything about it, and\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShh,\u201d she said, taking a turn as comforter. \u201cYou will do what is right, ma cherie,\u201d she said softly. \u201cIt is what you always do. And because of this\u2026 you will be a <u><u>good</u></u> leader. And I will follow you\u2026 to Hell and back, if necessary.\u201d<br /> <br /> I felt the tears in the corners of my eyes and forced them back. I guess I\u2019d better get used to doing that; I can\u2019t afford to break down in front of people anymore. \u201cThank you, my love,\u201d I said simply, and kissed the top of her head.<br /> <br /> I found D just before the doors opened for the evening. \u201cMaria,\u201d I said as I embraced her from behind, \u201care you free tonight?\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cI\u2019m always free if you need me, babe\u2026 you know that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGood,\u201d I said. \u201cI <u><u>do</u></u> need you. I\u2026 everything is about to change, sweetheart, and I think I need to be with my wife tonight.\u201d<br /> <br /> She squeezed one of my hands. \u201cNot everything, Jules,\u201d she whispered. \u201cSome things will never change. Anyway, I\u2019m all yours after the ball drops and we clear this place out, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> I acknowledged her gratefully and slipped backstage to get ready for my first number. I opened the show tonight\u2026 and unlike most nights, I took the opportunity to come out on the stage and address the audience directly before my first number began.<br /> <br /> \u201cHi,\u201d I said with a smile as the applause died down. \u201cYep, we\u2019re back\u2026 and we\u2019re back full-time starting tonight. It\u2019s good to see so many familiar faces out there after our extended leave of absence\u2026 we love our regulars. And I have a little something special planned to reward your patience.\u201d <br /> <br /> I let that sink in for a few seconds before I continued. \u201cAs many of you know, I\u2019m not originally from the west coast. I\u2019m a transplant\u2026 a corn-fed hick from the Midwest, in fact.\u201d Pause for laughter. \u201cOne of the questions I\u2019ve gotten the most frequently since we opened is \u2018are there any more like you back home?\u2019 Well, tonight I\u2019m here to answer that question\u2026 and the answer is a resounding <u><u>yes</u></u>!\u201d<br /> <br /> Missy and Jane stepped out from behind the curtain to thunderous applause. Missy wore a sparkly form-fitting golden dress to match her wings; Jane had on a nearly identical dress in bottle-green. Each of them smiled and waved at the crowds (Missy blew little kisses left and right). I knew that they\u2019d do well on our stage; after the Empress no performance seems particularly daunting.<br /> <br /> \u201cThese are my two oldest friends, Missy and Jane,\u201d I went on once I could get a word in edgewise. \u201cWe grew up together, and we\u2019ve been singing together for as long as any of us can remember. They\u2019ve graciously agreed to help me out with a little number we think you\u2019ll like.\u201d<br /> <br /> And we launched into a medley of popular Queen songs. It was sort of my little joke\u2026 I didn\u2019t want to reveal my status as the next monarch to the crowd, but I wanted to give them a little hint. We started with \u201cBohemian Rhapsody,\u201d then segued into a series of other hits both large and small\u2026 \u201cCrazy Little Thing Called Love,\u201d \u201cSomebody to Love,\u201d \u201cI Want to Break Free,\u201d \u201cKiller Queen,\u201d \u201cYou\u2019re My Best Friend,\u201d \u201cUnder Pressure,\u201d and, after turning our backs to the audience with a wiggle, \u201cFat Bottomed Girls.\u201d It went over like a house on fire; we got plenty of whoops, cat-calls, and wolf-whistles, and more than our share of appreciative laughter too. It felt <u><u>divine</u></u> to be performing with them again, and I could see from their faces that they felt the same way.<br /> <br /> We headed backstage to thunderous applause. \u201cOh my God that felt <u><u>amazing</u></u><u>!</u>\u201d Missy gasped as the next act moved on stage. Jane added an enthusiastic nod. I take it they enjoyed the glamour rush as much as I do.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo\u2026 we can count on you two to join our regular cast of performers?\u201d I asked with a grin.<br /> <br /> \u201cAbsolutely,\u201d Jane said, hugging Missy close against her.<br /> <br /> The two of them joined me for my second number around eleven o\u2019clock. Since neither of them has mastered the Contracts of Vainglory well enough to let the mortal audience see their wings, I loaned them a couple of my old choir robes (our sizes are close enough that they fit okay, and they\u2019ve already been modified to account for the wings). We did a soulful rendition of Madonna\u2019s \u201cLike a Prayer.\u201d It was maybe not as big a hit as the Queen m\u00e9lange, but it went over well in its own way.<br /> <br /> After that I hit the crowds. Most of the changelings were talking about an email they had all received earlier that evening\u2026 Jolie had sent out a group mail announcing that she would be stepping down as monarch with the turn of the year, and that her successor would be announced at a special coronation event on New Year\u2019s Day at Glamour Springs. There was plenty of speculation as to who that might be\u2026 and yes, my name was mentioned among the potential candidates. In a way that was comforting\u2026 it showed that the Freehold believed I was a likely and worthy successor. Other speculations included White Maria, Austin, and Desiree. I thought this last choice was a little odd, since a little more than a year ago she was a known Loyalist\u2026 but Jolie\u2019s affection for her is well-known, and I guess people thought that might have affected her judgment or something.<br /> <br /> I spoke with a few people and tried to play it coy, giving noncommittal answers when asked about the succession. My standard response was something along the lines of \u201cI guess we\u2019ll all find out tomorrow,\u201d which seemed the least likely to arouse suspicions. Unfortunately I think I tipped my hand to White Maria when I told her that I wasn\u2019t at liberty to discuss the issue further.<br /> <br /> She\u2019s\u2026 not doing well. She\u2019s taking what she sees as Marguerite\u2019s rejection extremely hard, and it\u2019s wearing on her. The two of us have never been that close, but I do consider her a friend, and it was hard to see her suffering like that. I tried to comfort her as much as I could, but she\u2019s going to have to work this through on her own. I tried to put Marguerite\u2019s decision in more palatable terms, telling her that Marguerite knew she wouldn\u2019t be able to give White Maria the attention she deserved while she was in so many other relationships, but I\u2019m not sure that it helped. In any case, I offered my services if she needed a shoulder to cry on or just a sympathetic ear. Unfortunately she\u2019s so divorced from her emotions that even talking about them is difficult for her.<br /> <br /> \u201cLook, I need to go,\u201d I said after a while, \u201cI\u2019m ignoring our other guests. But if you need anything, just flag me down, okay? I\u2019m here.\u201d<br /> <br /> She took my wrist gently as I started to move away. \u201cThank you,\u201d she said softly. \u201cThank you for trying to help me, Lorelei. You\u2019re a good friend. And\u2026 congratulations,\u201d she added with a more characteristic smirk.<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks,\u201d I said, smiling and squeezing her hand in turn. \u201cCondolences might be more appropriate,\u201d I added under my breath as I walked away. I don\u2019t know if she heard me or not.<br /> <br /> I tried to speak with everyone before midnight. Joan was there for the whole show, and Andromeda \u2013 who had presumably been kept busy planning for the coronation \u2013 joined her a bit later. Elena and Stasia were both there, and I had Calamity extend an invitation to the party to both of them. Unless I miss my guess, they\u2019ll be the only two mortals in attendance. I thought about inviting Dad to see my (literal) crowning achievement, but, well\u2026 it\u2019s going to be a Spring Court party, and even without Austin\u2019s nudity bylaws in place, things can get pretty raunchy. I\u2019ll tell him on Sunday after church.<br /> <br /> I also spoke with Veronica for a while. She\u2019s doing well, and seems a bit happier now that she\u2019s not constantly playing chaperone for Neon and Rowan. According to her, those two are much happier and more secure in their relationship now that they\u2019ve taken things to the next level. I was so happy to hear that\u2026 even though I feel these little niggling pangs of regret at the thought that I can\u2019t enjoy their amorous company anymore (they consider their relationship monogamous, and I wouldn\u2019t interfere with that for the world).<br /> <br /> I briefly introduced Veronica to Missy and Jane, and the four of us joked about forming a \u201cMidwest Farmers\u2019 Daughters\u201d club\u2026 though of course none of us actually grew up on farms. Unfortunately, we didn\u2019t get much of a chance to chat as a group; Missy and Jane were drawn into Marguerite\u2019s orbit fairly early on (more on that later). But Veronica and I ended up speaking for almost half an hour. God I\u2019ve missed her\u2026 we always fall into such an easy rapport. We have so much in common\u2026<br /> <br /> We started handing out free flutes of champagne at ten minutes to twelve. With one minute to go, I got up on the stage, and a few of our regular performers joined me. I started the countdown at ten seconds, and when the clock struck twelve we all shouted out \u201cHappy New Year!\u201d and launched into a harmonic version of \u201cAuld Lang Syne.\u201d Everybody drank champagne and hummed along (almost nobody knows all the words to that song) and generally had a grand old time. Happy 2016!<br /> <br /> Marguerite and Julia had been recruiting people from around the theater for a \u201cSex Party\u201d in the basement, and they seemed to have a fair number of participants lined up. I leaned up against D as the crowds started to thin and bemoaned the fact that we hadn\u2019t been invited with a mock pout. D leaned in and whispered that she had told the two of them that I wanted some private time with her tonight, so that made sense.<br /> <br /> Missy and Jane <u><u>did</u></u> opt to join the party, which sort of surprised me at first. Jane hastened to explain to me that they were merely going to observe this time, to see how the toys in the basement are used. You know, for future reference. I guess the two of them weren\u2019t affected by their time in the cage the same way I was\u2026 I can barely even stand the <u><u>thought</u></u> of being restrained like that. But in any case, I told them that I understood, and that I wouldn\u2019t judge them if they did decide to participate. I gave them each a New Year\u2019s kiss, told them to have fun, and allowed myself to be led upstairs by my wife.<br /> <br /> \u201cI really do need to sleep tonight,\u201d I said as we ascended. \u201cBig day tomorrow.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut\u2026 only <u><u>after</u></u> the first sex of the New Year, right?\u201d Maria asked with a twinkle in her eye.<br /> <br /> \u201cNaturally,\u201d I agreed with a chuckle, \u201cthat goes without saying.\u201d<br /> <br /> So there was that. And if the lovemaking <u><u>maybe</u></u> didn\u2019t last as long as it usually does, well, that\u2019s okay too\u2026 it was still perfect.<br /> <br /> I gave us a few minutes to hold each other before I spoke. \u201cMaria,\u201d I said softly, \u201cI really need to talk to you. I need to tell you some things.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat\u2019s up, Jules?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cDo you read my diary?\u201d I asked plaintively, trying to keep any trace of accusation out of my voice.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2026 have,\u201d she replied guardedly.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s okay,\u201d I said, stroking her hair. \u201cI don\u2019t mind. There\u2019s nothing in there I\u2019d want to hide from you. There\u2019s nothing about me that I\u2019d <u><u>ever</u></u> want to hide from you. But I take it from your response that you haven\u2019t read it lately?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo,\u201d she admitted.<br /> <br /> So it came out. I told her everything about my briefing with Jolie. I told her everything about the Four Horsemen, including my suspicions about Oleander\u2019s \u201cdelivery mechanism.\u201d She\u2019s now as well-informed about the Freehold\u2019s war plans as I am. Needless to say, she swore to keep it all to herself, even among the motley.<br /> <br /> \u201cJesus,\u201d she breathed after I had finished.<br /> <br /> \u201cI know,\u201d I said.<br /> <br /> \u201cJules, I\u2026 I don\u2019t want to offend you, but\u2026\u201d she seemed to stammer for a second. \u201cDammit, there\u2019s no other way to say this. Oleander\u2026 when she\u2019s not with you, she\u2019s different, and\u2026 I\u2019m not gonna lie, the thought of her with something like that toxin at her command scares the shit out of me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t see that side of her\u2026\u201d I began.<br /> <br /> \u201cI know,\u201d she replied. \u201cAnd I\u2019m not saying that she\u2019s an evil person or anything like that. She\u2019s developing this stuff so that we can take out the Grand Maw and put a stop to this war in the simplest, most efficient way possible. She\u2019d never use it just to cause pain and suffering, or anything like that. But if she honestly believed that setting this stuff loose on the Hollywood Freehold was the most logical course of action, she\u2019d do it in a heartbeat.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat won\u2019t happen,\u201d I asserted.<br /> <br /> \u201cNot if she knows how it would make you feel,\u201d she opined.<br /> <br /> So that gave me something to think about. We talked some more. I cried. She held me. And God, eventually I fell asleep, even with all of that on my mind. I hadn\u2019t slept at all the previous night at Oleander\u2019s, and in the rush and frenzy of the preparations I hadn\u2019t even bothered to use contracts to pep myself up.<br /> <br /> D woke me this morning by kissing both of my eyelids gently until I stirred. \u201cC\u2019mon, Jules,\u201d she said softly when I rolled over. \u201cLots to do today. C\u2019mon, babe\u2026 you know if it was up to me I\u2019d let you sleep as long as you want, but\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m up,\u201d I said groggily, \u201cjust\u2026 give me a few more minutes, okay? Give me a little more time to just be Mrs. De la Rocha before I have to go and be somebody else\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFive minutes,\u201d she said grudgingly. She set the alarm and lay back down with me, and we kissed and cuddled and held each other and okay, yes, I might have drifted off to sleep again, however briefly. But I was exactly where I wanted to be\u2026 where I <u><u>chose</u></u> to be. And God knows when I\u2019ll have the luxury of a choice like that again.<br /> <br /> We got up, got showered, got dressed, and got prepared to face the day. Trinh had the leftover sausages re-heated by the time we made it to the kitchen, and today they were supplemented by eggs and toast. The usual suspects were all assembled, including Becky and White Maria, who seemed a bit more relaxed than she had on the previous evening. I hadn\u2019t really thought of this before, but I guess one side benefit of me taking the crown will be that as Claviger, Becky will be able to keep an eye on me and spend time with Calamity at the same time\u2026 so that\u2019s nice.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, not all is well in the Freehold. Okay\u2026 I don\u2019t actually <u>know</u> that anything is going wrong, but circumstances are certainly suspicious. It turns out that two out of three of our Director escapees went MIA last night. Angelica disappeared an hour or so before midnight, even though she had been scheduled to guard Jolie at that time. Chalcedony had planned an evening with Molly, but she cancelled at the last moment. And while Desiree was present at the Sex Party downstairs all night, Marguerite reported that she <u><u>did</u></u> withdraw from the action for about fifteen minutes at one point, and seemed to be doing something with her phone.<br /> <br /> Calamity had gotten the information about Angelica and Chalcedony from Dahlia, who was of the opinion that the two of them were up to something nefarious. Actually, Jacob already knew about Chalcedony from Molly, which at least implies that Little Girl Blue\u2019s absence started a little earlier than Dahlia thought. As the motley discussed the situation, it occurred to me that both Chalcedony and Angelica were present at Glamour Springs the other day when I accepted Jolie\u2019s offer to take up the crown. The meeting itself was private\u2026 but after Jolie\u2019s Freehold-wide email last night, it wouldn\u2019t have been too difficult for either of them to put the pieces together.<br /> <br /> What could this mean? All three of them were Taken by the Director\u2026 but we thought we\u2019d removed their programming long ago. Desiree and Chalcedony both lived in Hollywood for a time\u2026 but we removed <u><u>that</u></u> programming as well, and as far as we know, Angelica has never had any contact with the Court of Fallen Stars. Still, it\u2019s looking more and more likely that they were reporting the change of regime to <u><u>someone</u></u>\u2026 which means that my first few days in office might be more interesting than I\u2019d like. Transitional periods are usually regarded as an ideal time for enemies to strike. My only consolation is that Jolie has never been at the forefront of the war effort, so maybe these hypothetical foes won\u2019t feel it\u2019s worth the effort to strike now.<br /> <br /> And what about Desiree? She didn\u2019t disappear. It\u2019s possible that her part of this is just a stupid coincidence. I want to believe that. I <u><u>like</u></u> Desiree, and I want to believe that she\u2019s still the friend I\u2019ve come to cherish. But I can\u2019t afford to <u><u>assume</u></u> that this is the case. Marguerite has offered to swipe her phone and check the records of her calls, texts, and emails to see what she was doing last night. And though I hate the necessity of invading her privacy, I think it <u><u>is</u></u> necessary\u2026 if only to disprove our suspicions. What we\u2019re going to do about the other two, I have no idea.<br /> <br /> So here I sit, a few scant hours from taking over leadership of the Spring Court in Malibu and Santa Monica. I have just learned that one of my lovers constitutes a quarter of our forces in a shadow war I didn\u2019t even know existed. I have to worry about a trio of potential spies for one of several possible enemies, one of whom is one of my clavigers. And with all of this going on in the back of my mind, I still have to find a way to convey a sense of calm assurance to pretty much everyone I know, so that they won\u2019t fall prey to the panic I can feel pretty much constantly clawing at the back of my mind.<br /> <br /> At least I don\u2019t have to face these trials alone. Maria will not let anything happen to me. Oleander is working tirelessly in the background to stop this war before it can start. And as Marguerite reminded me just before our little meeting broke up, she\u2019ll follow my lead \u201cto Hell and back.\u201d<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei de la Rocha</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> It seems that there are a number of us going to therapy these days. De la Rocha, Calamity and I were joined by Missy and Jane for our morning sessions. All went well. We even got some good news regarding Missy and Jane. The therapists there said that the pair was no longer as severe a flight risk as they used to be, and if we feel comfortable with it we can remove their ankle bracelets. We said that we would talk about it with the rest of the motley before we made a decision but we were pretty sure what Lori and the others would say about it. Lori also had the key to remove the anklets so the decision could be put off past the therapy sessions. <br /> <br /> When we got back to the house it was to Trinh cooking sausages, eggs and toast for breakfast. She made three kinds of sausage, mild, hot and how she likes them, which was to all evidence really hot. A few people tried them how she likes them and ended up drinking cups of milk and sweating at the hairline. I stuck with the hot ones as did a few other people. Russian food is not known for its spice, so I figured I should probably stay away from the really hot ones. They were tasty. Everything was. Conversation came up about Missy and Jane\u2019s anklets and Lori agreed to remove them right then and there, so that was that. <br /> <br /> After breakfast we had some guests arrive to talk to Lori about coronation stuff. It was Dark Kimberly, Andromeda, Davie and T.J. Lori got all the details worked out. She doesn\u2019t want anyone to know who will be succeeding Jolie until the change of power actually takes place, so they arranged to have the coronation at Glamor Springs. Lori also asked Dark Kimberly about a new dress, so Kimberly got some measurements so she could make that happen. I think it\u2019s going to be a Hedgespun dress the way those two were talking. Makes sense. If it was any other kind then Lori could just buy it off the rack. There was also talk about food, music and decorations. Dark Kimberly also asked the rest of us if we needed anything for the big day. Lori said that she would like her motley to be with her when she is crowned, so that means that we will be in the spotlight too. I told Kimberly that I had a suit that I was going to wear and just took her up on the idea of having a water bottle under my chair.<br /> <br /> Throughout the whole time that Dark Kimberly and the others were there Kimberly and Trinh traded words back and forth in Vietnamese. I have no idea what they were saying, but at least some of the time it sounded like arguing. Then once Dark Kimberly had left Trinh told the rest of us that Kimberly speaks Vietnamese like she was affiliated with organized crime. That led to an explanation about Dark Kimberly\u2019s past when she was younger. We kept things vague, but did explain that as a teenager she had been involved to some extent with organized crime, but that she had gotten out of that life.<br /> <br /> Conversation then turned to Dark Kimberly\u2019s girlfriend, Annika and Lori explained how she had come to the freehold and what she does for the Dream House. That then led to conversation about how old some of the members of the Freehold are. Annika herself fled the Nazis and came to America in the 1930s. Oleander admitted that she escaped from Arcadia in 1954. Even Lori was surprised at that one. Tommy was brought up as well. No one knew how old he was, just that he was old and didn\u2019t come to the Freehold straight from Arcadia. He did some traveling first. Spidertoes also came up. Someone said that she speaks about the Terror in France as if she had actually been there, so that puts her a good ways back too. There are a good number of old and powerful changelings in this Freehold. I don\u2019t think Hollywood really thought things through before they started fucking with us.<br /> <br /> The afternoon passed pretty quickly. People practiced for the show tonight, including Missy and Jane. Apparently, they were going to do a medley of Queen songs with Lori. Cute. But before the show Insincere Marguerite came into the room looking really upset and just kind of went up to Lori and muttered something to Lori about the \u201cbad stuff.\u201d Lori\u2019s expression went from confused to understanding in a moment and she hugged her lover tightly. I have no idea what that was all about but neither of them looked inclined to talk about it so I didn\u2019t ask.<br /> <br /> During the show everyone did great. Missy and Jane backed up Lori for the Queen medley and it was really good. Those three can harmonize really well. I guess it makes sense. They had a lot of time to practice singing together while in Arcadia. Missy and Jane weren\u2019t even shy or nervous about performing in front of a packed hall. Another perk to having performed so much for the Violet Empress I guess. Singing in front of a room full of changelings and humans probably doesn\u2019t come close to having to perform for a gentry. Also during the show Jolie sent out an email to the Freehold that she would be stepping down as Spring Queen and her successor would be announced at Glamour Springs tomorrow night.<br /> <br /> After the show Lori and Calamity made their rounds through the crowd. I saw Lori talking to White Maria for a bit. There seemed to be some tension there, but I\u2019m not sure what it was about. Calamity on the other hand went to talk to Stasia and Elena. I saw her present them with a dream that she had made just for them. It was in a beautifully crafted glass sphere that Calamity had made.<br /> <br /> And because of the date we made sure that everything was wrapped up show-wise before midnight so we could ring in the New Year with our audience. Me and the other bartenders started handing out champagne flutes and pouring champagne before midnight. Once the clock struck midnight we all cheered and started singing that New Year\u2019s song. I don\u2019t know the name of it. Everyone also toasted to the new year and we refilled glasses until we ran out of champagne. I made sure that I was close to my sister as the clock was counting down. She held out her hand and I took it so that we\u2019d be holding hands when the new year changed over. I think it was really important to her that we celebrated the new year together as family. Luna was also next to me. I reached out and took her hand too and gave it a squeeze. I really am lucky to have my Luna and my sister in my life.<br /> <br /> After all of that people went back to socializing. I talked to Molly for a bit. She was all dressed up and said that she had originally had plans to go out with Chalcedony tonight, but her paramour called at the last minute and said that something had come up and she had to cancel their plans. Molly mostly went on about having wished that she\u2019d known in advance that her plans were going to fall through so she could have changed into more comfortable underwear. I\u2019ve seen women\u2019s underwear in stores and catalogs. The things that women will wear because it looks good is astounding. I\u2019m glad that men\u2019s undergarments are much more practical. For the most part. Hailey was also there and we talked for a few minutes. She seemed to be doing fine. At least until Andromeda came in later in the evening and then Hailey became distressed like she usually does when the other woman shows up in her presence. I can understand Hailey\u2019s reaction to Andromeda. I think if I was back in \u2018the world\u2019 with the person that had tortured me in Arcadia that I\u2019d be upset too. <br /> <br /> As the evening was wrapping up Molly came up and said that she\u2019d been invited to go to Insincere Marguerite\u2019s sex party in the basement tonight. She asked me if she should go or not. I didn\u2019t answer yes or no to that one. I just said that there would likely be use of sex toys and that most of Marguerite\u2019s partners came away from the experience a little shell shocked, but that they almost always went back for more later. I guess that helped her make up her mind because she decided to turn down the offer and headed home when the club was closing down for the night. Everyone split off with their partners and headed for bed, or the basement.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Well today started off interesting. There was breakfast as usual, and we had guests also as usual. Desiree, White Maria and Becky were all there. Conversation happened and eventually our guests left. Then Calamity called a Motley meeting and we all gathered in a private room. Apparently, Calamity had gotten a text from Dahlia and had some interesting news to pass along. Some of it kind of affected Lori, and all of it was suspicious. It seems that last night both Chalcedony and Angelica disappeared for most of the night and didn\u2019t show up until this morning. This led to cancelled plans with Molly, which I brought up to the group since it established about what time Chalcedony left. The unfortunate thing about Angelica leaving when she did was that she was supposed to be protecting Jolie at the time. She\u2019s only been back in \u2018the world\u2019 for about six months so I\u2019m surprised that she was made a claviger anyway, but someone must have thought that she was trustworthy enough to do the job. Unfortunately for her Angelica seems to be proving them wrong with this whole disappearing act. Lori also brought up the fact that both Chalcedony and Angelica were present at Glamour Springs when Lori showed up to have her talk with Jolie. It would not be hard for them to put together what the talk was about given the email that was sent out last night. Desiree did not leave during this time, she was at Marguerite\u2019s party, but she did step aside for a little while and seem to be doing something on her phone. Insincere Marguerite offered to pick her pocket and see what she could find out about what Desiree had been up to last night. Julia offered to distract Desiree so she didn\u2019t think to look at her phone while Insincere Marguerite had it.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not sure what was going on last night but it is suspicious that all three of the local women who had been taken by the Director exhibited odd behavior last night. Two of them leaving at the drop of a hat for places unknown and the third taking time away from her lovers to do something on her phone. One would normally think that Desiree would be too distracted to even think about her phone while she was having sex with Marguerite and the others. All three women had programming removed that the Director had placed there. We thought that this removed any compulsions they had to do the Director\u2019s bidding. And that might have been true. The programming might be gone, but it is also possible that they are serving the Director out of loyalty and of their own free will. So, yeah, I\u2019m not sure what is going on but it definitely warrants someone looking into it. If that someone happens to be us so much the better. <br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXII</i><br /> <br /> Role-playing heavy this time. Not too much to add to the account.<br /> <br /> There was a lovely conversation with White Maria and Calamity where White Maria just kept throwing words like \u201cSlattern\u201d and \u201cStrumpet\u201d describing Dark Kimberly and Sundown Kwan. OOC we kept cracking up.<br /> <br /> I sadly can\u2019t remember specifics now, but Calamity and Dahlia had another immensely fucked up conversation. Mostly her saying horrifying things in a deadpan. The gal needs help.<br /> <br /> Okay, hope you enjoyed. Comments and Questions welcome.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T01:43:02-07:00","id":1239938,"title":"","content":"Lori and Marguerite are not miserable enough. We should do something about that. So sit back and enjoy the coronation and Lorelei\u2019s first actions as monarch. Calamity was unable to make so is around but not active in the story.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Sigh. I have been Spring Queen for less than twenty-four hours, and already I\u2019ve been forced to compromise my principles and endanger two people I care about in service of some nebulous \u201cgreater good.\u201d I knew this wasn\u2019t going to be easy \u2013 Jolie didn\u2019t abdicate because she got sick of kissing babies and presiding over ribbon-cutting ceremonies, for crying out loud \u2013 but I didn\u2019t expect the burden of leadership to be so immediately apparent.<br /> <br /> So Kimberly and I were in nearly-constant contact for the last few hours before the coronation ceremony, making sure that everything was just right and hashing out the last few details of the party. That girl is a wonder, and I\u2019m not surprised that Jolie told me she considers her to be the Spring Court\u2019s secret weapon. I have <u><u>never</u></u> seen anyone accomplish so much with so little in such a short time. Some of her connections frankly scare me a little bit\u2026 which came to light when I quipped that I was disappointed by the lack of dancing bears in our plans.<br /> <br /> There was a pause on the other end of the line. \u201cAre you serious about that?\u201d she asked after a moment. \u201cBecause I\u2019ll see what I can do, but it probably won\u2019t be legal.\u201d I assured her that I was joking, and that I deeply appreciated everything she was doing to make the transition memorable.<br /> <br /> The motley and I arrived a little before the rest of the guests and entered Glamour Springs quietly through the side entrance. Kimberly met us there and assured us that everything was ready, and that we didn\u2019t need to worry about anything. Then she presented me with the most <u><u>beautiful</u></u> dress I have ever seen. It was made to my specifications, but Kimberly had obviously put a lot of herself into its design and construction. I\u2019m no seamstress or fashion designer, after all, so she had taken my somewhat vague descriptions and interpreted them through the lens of her vast amount of experience with those crafts.<br /> <br /> The dress itself is a dusky red color which constantly shifts between darker and lighter hues. It\u2019s made primarily from sunlight falling through tree branches on rose petals. It\u2019s as soft and smooth as silk, and feels amazing against my skin. The bodice is worked with tiny shimmering pearls on threads so thin they\u2019re nearly invisible\u2026 made from drops of morning dew suspended in intricate spider\u2019s webs. The veil and train are a diaphanous fabric that floats around the rest of the dress like wisps of morning mist. I\u2019d considered enlisting the help of the local songbirds to carry the train, but I didn\u2019t want them to get trapped inside Glamour Springs or anything like that\u2026 and the dress was so light that it wasn\u2019t really necessary in any case.<br /> <br /> In that dress, I <u><u>felt</u></u> like a monarch for the first time.<br /> <br /> As the Freehold began to gather, I invoked the Contracts of Vainglory to give my appearance a bit of a regal boost. I figured that most of the Freehold is used to seeing me perform at the Dream House, where I almost always have those clauses in effect, and they\u2019d be expecting me to look impressive. But that was all the magic I employed. As I\u2019ve said a few times before in this journal, using magic to sway people\u2019s opinions or force them to view me in a positive light seems like cheating to me. It\u2019s almost like admitting that I need to use magic to get them on my side, and that\u2019s not the image I want to project.<br /> <br /> The coronation ceremony was open to all members of the Freehold (plus a few special invited guests like Stasia and Elena), though as it was billed as a Spring Court function, only a few people outside of my court opted to attend. Ji Wen Ja, Louis Guo, and T. J. provided security, but they were the only people allowed to carry weapons. This caused a bit of a stir when they checked us at the door and found a large carving knife in Julia\u2019s handbag (apparently she carries it everywhere for \u2018self-defense\u2019) but other than that things went relatively smoothly.<br /> <br /> Once a big enough crowd had arrived, Kimberly brought Shi into the \u201cbackstage\u201d area. He had used his abilities to mimic my appearance\u2026 sorta. He\u2019d overestimated my bust by about a cup size (possibly deliberately), but adjusted the illusion accordingly once I\u2019d pointed this out. The idea was that people would figure out the secret before the big reveal if I was not seen to be at the party, so Shi was going to serve as my stand-in while I waited in the wings.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo,\u201d Kimberly said when Shi was about to head out and start mingling, \u201cwhat about Missy and Jane? Are they going to be up on stage with your motley, or do you want them in the crowd with Shi?\u201d<br /> <br /> I looked at the two of them for a moment, considering. I wanted to let them know that they\u2019re family to me, and yet\u2026 they\u2019re not officially part of the motley yet. They haven\u2019t made the pledge, so the Wyrd doesn\u2019t recognize them as a part of our little family within the Freehold. I didn\u2019t want to muddy the waters, but I also didn\u2019t want to make them feel rejected if at all possible.<br /> <br /> Jane broke the silence first. \u201cWe\u2019re not part of your motley?\u201d she asked plaintively.<br /> <br /> I smiled and took a hand from each of them. \u201cNot yet,\u201d I said. \u201cYou\u2019re family. You\u2019re two of my closest friends. But joining the motley is a little more involved than that. There are oaths and responsibilities to consider. It\u2019s not something to be taken lightly. We\u2019ll talk about it soon, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> Jane nodded. \u201cWe understand,\u201d she said, and Missy nodded in turn. \u201cWe\u2019ll just hang out in the audience with\u2026 this person,\u201d she ended delicately, indicating Shi with some obvious nerves. I can relate\u2026 talk about your \u201cfox in the henhouse\u201d situations!<br /> <br /> After everyone had arrived, Kimberly led us to our places, and Jolie got up in front of the assembled changelings and started her speech. She talked about what an honor it had been to serve as our monarch, and how she felt it was time to step aside in favor of new leadership, and how she would still be available to serve in whatever capacity was required of her.<br /> <br /> When she reached the end of her prepared remarks, Kimberly gave me a gentle prod, and I walked out onto the stage\u2026 in full view of my people. Jolie turned to regard me, and gave me an encouraging smile. I did my best to emulate it, and to project confidence and serenity to the gathered changelings. When I reached the front of the temporary dais, Jolie knelt before me.<br /> <br /> Jolie. Knelt. Before. Me. As she did so, the crown that\u2019s been a part of her mantle since I met her faded away, and I could <u><u>feel</u></u> my own crown appearing around my head. On me, the Vernal Crown appears as a sort of halo of green light around my head, rising to three distinct points. The first time I caught a glimpse of it in a mirror was\u2026 a bit of a shock, to say the least.<br /> <br /> Maria joined me on stage a moment later, looking proud and (hidden under the surface) maybe a little nervous.<br /> <br /> \u201cI give you your new Spring Monarch,\u201d Jolie said to those assembled, \u201cMistress Lorelei de la Rocha. Joining her on the stage, her consort, Maria de la Rocha.\u201d The rest of the motley followed in short order and arranged themselves in a semi-circle behind the two of us. All of the Spring Courtiers in the audience dropped to one knee; the various and sundry other members of the Freehold \u2013 including my three co-monarchs \u2013 bowed at the waist.<br /> <br /> About the title\u2026 well, every monarch since I arrived in the Lady By the Sea Freehold has had a different honorific, and I thought I should continue the tradition. \u2018Mistress\u2019 seemed appropriate, since it conveys a sense of authority and has an obvious sexual subtext, which plays into my reputation and personal legend within the community. A year ago I probably would have gone with something different, but I think it\u2019s been long enough since Master Darke was ousted that I can avoid the stigma of having a similar title.<br /> <br /> In any case, I moved forward to address the crowd, and a hush settled. I indicated that they should rise, and they did so. I won\u2019t try to repeat everything I said, but I\u2019ll hit the high points. \u201cMy father is one of the wisest people I\u2019ve ever met,\u201d I began, \u201cand I\u2019ll never forget something he said to me more years ago than I\u2019d care to admit. He told me that taking a position of leadership in a community like this is not about gaining personal power or prestige\u2026 it\u2019s about accepting a burden of service.\u201d<br /> <br /> They seemed to like that, so I went on. \u201cThe Lady By the Sea has been the greatest home I\u2019ve ever known. You took me in two years ago, when I had nothing to offer you in return. You trusted me with awesome responsibilities, and I\u2019ve done everything I could to prove worthy of that trust. I hope I\u2019ve succeeded.\u201d<br /> <br /> More applause; it was going well. \u201cAs many of you know, last year my motley and I returned to Arcadia on a rescue mission. Since our return, all of the greatest friends I\u2019ve ever had have lived as part of this Freehold.\u201d I saw Jane nudge Missy at that, and the two of them gave me dazzling smiles.<br /> <br /> \u201cIn any case\u2026 all I\u2019m really trying to say is that when Jolie first approached me about taking up the crown, I wasn\u2019t sure what to do. I eventually decided to accept, not because I want to wield power over the people of this Freehold, but because I feel obliged to do what I can for them.\u201d<br /> <br /> I said a few more things to round the speech out, but that was the general gist of it. As I wrapped things up, there was a bit more applause, and people began to mingle. I was preparing to join them when I noticed that one of the pools across the room was beginning to bubble and ripple dramatically. A few seconds later, Captain Jack burst up from beneath the surface, flanked by several accomplices in SCUBA gear. He was wearing a fair approximation of the outfit I had worn on stage the previous evening\u2026 and he immediately launched into a similar rendition of Madonna\u2019s \u201cLike a Prayer,\u201d accompanied by music from an unseen source. It was obviously a tribute to my own performance\u2026 but stopped well short of mocking or parody. He was actually <u><u>really</u></u> good, and of course his glistening physique didn\u2019t hurt things either. He was like some sort of latter-day Adonis\u2026 or \u201cMadonnis,\u201d I suppose.<br /> <br /> He and his accomplices made for the door after a verse and a chorus. I walked back to the microphone and chuckled to show that I wasn\u2019t upset. \u201cWell, I guess now it\u2019s <u><u>really</u></u> official,\u201d I said as the Captain made his exit to general amusement.<br /> <br /> I spent the rest of the party speaking with various people, accepting congratulations, and answering questions about my policies and the specifics of my court. I intend to hold court at the Dream House most evenings, and will continue to speak with the local changelings and hear their pleas and grievances after my performances. I will also make myself available during the day to any changeling who has business with me, excepting only those times at which I have classes scheduled (most of my classes this first semester will be online; I\u2019ve managed to schedule the rest for mornings and early afternoons on Tuesdays and Thursdays). Of course, the Dream House itself will still be a haven for <u><u>all</u></u> Changelings, not just those of the Spring Court.<br /> <br /> A few of my conversations stand out. Chalcedony approached me at one point, looking nervous and uncomfortable but not angry or upset. \u201cCongratulations, Mistress Lorelei,\u201d she said after a moment.<br /> <br /> I took her hand. She stiffened, but didn\u2019t pull away. \u201cChalcedony,\u201d I said seriously, \u201cI know we\u2019ve had our differences, but you\u2019re one of my people now, and I want to make sure you know that I will do everything I can to represent your best interests. I know you aren\u2019t comfortable coming to the Dream House, and I completely understand that. So if you need to speak with me, just give me a call, and we\u2019ll set up a meeting somewhere else, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> She offered me a weak smile. \u201cThank you,\u201d she said softly. \u201cI really appreciate that. You know, Molly\u2019s been trying to get me to go back there more often\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re always welcome, Chalcedony,\u201d I said softly. \u201cWe look forward to seeing you at the Dream House again\u2026 when you\u2019re ready.\u201d<br /> <br /> The other three monarchs each approached me individually and offered their congratulations and best wishes, as did Olivia Gold and Willow Black, representing the Day and Night Courts respectively. Augustine\u2019s greeting stands out in particular. \u201cWelcome, Lori,\u201d he said, which led to a short discussion on the proper etiquette for monarchs addressing each other\u2026 apparently given names are appropriate when we speak to each other, unless we\u2019re doing so in front of others in an official capacity. As we were in a relatively secluded corner at that point, the familiar address was fine.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m happy to see you rise to prominence,\u201d he confided in me. \u201cI have nothing against Lowjack and Charlotte, of course\u2026 they are both capable and effective monarchs in their own right. But it will be nice to have another moral voice upon the council\u2026 another who will bring her good Christian values to the table. I look forward to working with you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you, Augustine,\u201d I said softly (if he has another name, I don\u2019t know it). \u201cRest assured that I will do everything in my power to rule as morally as I can, while still protecting our people from\u2026 the present threats.\u201d<br /> <br /> It would be negligent of me not to mention that I noticed Julia singing softly to Desiree off in a secluded corner at one point, presumably as part of our earlier plan to give Marguerite the opportunity to steal her cellphone. I also noticed Marguerite and Jacob speaking with Boss Lowjack a little later\u2026 but as I wasn\u2019t informed about the specific results of these encounters, I\u2019ll save further discussion of them until later.<br /> <br /> It eventually started getting late, and many of the guests began to leave. Those who remained were mostly looking forward to the typical Spring Court \u201cafter-party.\u201d It\u2019s something of a tradition among the Court of Desire in this area to hold a sort of sexual free-for-all after important events. Kimberly had told me that this was the case before the coronation, and asked if I wanted to continue the tradition, and if so if I wanted to restrict the guest list.<br /> <br /> In the end I decided to uphold the tradition, and to make the event open to all who wished to attend (yes, even T.J.). What can I say? While I\u2019m certainly taking my duties as a new monarch seriously, among those duties is a mandate to keep my people happy and content. Continuing \u201cfun\u201d traditions like the occasional orgy is one way to do that. And participating in the festivities myself helps to communicate the fact that I see myself as one of them.<br /> <br /> Plus, I like sex.<br /> <br /> In the end, about a dozen people made use of one of the large guest rooms at Glamour Springs last night. Maria was the only other member of the motley who joined in the fun. I\u2019m glad she was there. The only other non-Spring Courtier present was Willow Black, the Night Court envoy. I\u2019d never had the pleasure of her company before, so that was nice. Jolie opted in, which was <u><u>also</u></u> nice, as it\u2019s been entirely too long since the two of us have dallied together (and this time D got to join in the fun too!). Kimberly, Flores, Angelica, Desiree, Dominika, and Carla (who had earlier spooked Missy and Jane by constantly looking at them and licking her chops) rounded out the list of lovely ladies, while Sandoval and Davie provided the man-candy. I saw the two of them exchange a discreet high-five as the clothes started coming off\u2026 and who can blame them?<br /> <br /> It was a very pleasant evening. Eleven attractive people \u2013 four of whom I\u2019d had no prior carnal knowledge \u2013 all giving of themselves to honor the occasion and to congratulate me on what they saw as my windfall. Sigh\u2026 if everything about this job was public appearances and guilt-free orgies, I\u2019d probably be just fine.<br /> <br /> So most of us yawned and stretched our way awake late this morning. Everything was amicable, and people chatted without pretense as we gathered our clothes and got ready to face the day. I made sure to kiss everyone goodbye before Maria and I headed back to the Dream House, achy and sticky and thoroughly satisfied.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately the news wasn\u2019t great when we got back. Marguerite <u><u>had</u></u> managed to pilfer Desiree\u2019s phone while Julia distracted her, and had managed to access her texting history. The texts we were interested in were back and forth between her and Angelica. Angelica had texted her during the Sex Party the other night, and said she needed to meet with Desiree in private. Desiree had responded in the negative. There was some back and forth that wasn\u2019t quite arguing, and at one point, Desiree had stated that she no longer worked for \u2018him,\u2019 and neither did Angelica.<br /> <br /> Well, shit. It seemed pretty obvious to us at that point that at least Angelica, probably Chalcedony, and maybe Desiree are all still at least partially in the thrall of the Director. Desiree at least seemed to be fighting his influence, though if she\u2019s really on the side of the angels it begs the question of why she didn\u2019t tell us that something mysterious was going down. Y\u2019know, like Halley did a year and a half ago when she sensed the approach of the Mothership.<br /> <br /> Jacob and Marguerite had reported all of this to Boss Lowjack at the party last night. It seemed like the right thing to do, as he\u2019s in charge of intelligence in the Freehold.<br /> <br /> But the topic up for debate as D and I returned for Sex Breakfast was whether or not Marguerite should use whatever hold over Desiree she still has to get more information. That we <u><u>need</u></u> more information about this situation isn\u2019t really in question. But having Marguerite exert her influence over Desiree seemed like a bad idea for <u><u>both</u></u> of them. Unfortunately, that\u2019s just what Boss Lowjack wanted Marguerite to do. What he <u><u>ordered</u></u> her to do, in fact.<br /> <br /> I can only assume that he\u2019s not as familiar with Marguerite as we in the motley are. If he really wanted her to get that information at any cost, he should <u><u>never</u></u> have phrased it as an order from her monarch. Marguerite bucks against authority almost as much as D does. I understand how important it is for us to find out what the Director is up to; I really do. And maybe that\u2019s why I did what I did next.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not proud of it. But after thinking about the situation for a few minutes, I realized that things were more complicated than they first seemed. The timing of this event was too convenient for it to be a coincidence; the fact that all three of the Director\u2019s local escapees started acting squirrelly right as Jolie announced her resignation at least hints at some sort of strike during the transition period. Desiree had access to information we desperately needed; information that we might need <u><u>soon</u></u>. Marguerite had the most simple and straightforward way to access that information at her elongated fingertips. Add to that the fact that she\u2019d been given a direct order from the sitting monarch, and there seemed to be only one solution.<br /> <br /> I\u2026 spoke up in favor of Lowjack\u2019s idea. But I didn\u2019t do so in a straightforward manner; I knew Marguerite would balk at any suggestion that she toe the line or go with the flow. I approached the issue obliquely, playing up how vital it is for us to get that information quickly. I emphasized how the issue was too important for her to make the decision based solely upon her dislike of being ordered to do anything. Finally, I made a subtle reference to the fact that I myself might be at risk, if the succession is really what triggered these events.<br /> <br /> Marguerite decided to see what she could get from Desiree. She called the other woman up and told her that she needed to see her. Julia suggested that it might be best if Marguerite had backup in the room with her, so Jacob slipped into one of the offices just before the redhead arrived and made himself invisible.<br /> <br /> I understand that it wasn\u2019t pretty. While Desiree was there, I hung out in the theater singing little snippets I remembered from Wagner, and occasionally Beethoven\u2019s \u201cOde to Joy\u201d (haven\u2019t had much of an excuse to practice my German lately, and I was starting to get a bit rusty). When I saw Desiree walk out sort of stiffly about twenty minutes later, I rushed into the office to see what was what.<br /> <br /> Marguerite was obviously shaken. Desiree had tried desperately to divert the topic of conversation, going so far as to try to seduce Marguerite at several points during their talk. Only Jacob\u2019s silent intervention (a reassuring hand on Marguerite\u2019s back) had stopped Desiree from completely derailing the conversation. She\u2019d\u2026 well, Desiree\u2019s unwillingness to betray the Director was still so strong that Marguerite eventually had to assert herself as the other girl\u2019s Master\u2026 something she had sworn both to me and to herself she would never do again. It had shaken her badly\u2026 but she got what we needed in the end.<br /> <br /> The Director sent out a signal to his agents the other night. It manifested as a sort of ghostly carnival music that only they could hear. They were supposed to contact him for further instructions. Desiree ignored the call. Presumably Angelica and Chalcedony did not. So we have three potential loyalists, all of whom are members of my Court and therefore my responsibility now\u2026 and one of whom is my Claviger, entrusted with ensuring my safety in times of trouble.<br /> <br /> Marguerite was a little shell-shocked. She wasn\u2019t as bad as she had been during the\u2026 unpleasantness with Chalcedony a year ago, but she was still clearly bothered by what she had been forced to do. By what I had <u><u>manipulated</u></u> her into doing. Yeah, it wasn\u2019t my conscious intention, but that\u2019s still pretty much the long and the short of it.<br /> <br /> She looked at me, and I saw a little bit of fear and insecurity in her eyes\u2026 the sort of thing she never shows to anyone outside of the family. At least a small part of that was probably due to the fear that I would not approve of her asserting her dominance over Desiree in such a blatant way. I couldn\u2019t let that continue, so I rushed up to her, threw my arms around her, and kissed her forehead.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m so sorry you had to do that, sweetie,\u201d I whispered as I kissed her hair again. \u201cAnd I can\u2019t express how grateful I am that you were willing to make that sacrifice. I love you.\u201d<br /> <br /> She slumped against me slightly and returned my hug. \u201cMerci, ma cherie,\u201d she whispered back.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, today\u2019s drama didn\u2019t end there. We called a motley meeting to discuss how we should proceed now that we have that information. Jacob had called Lowjack to let him know what we had learned, of course, but we still needed to decide what we were going to do about it. We discussed speaking with Angelica first\u2026 maybe trying to lift her phone like we had with Desiree (once Marguerite had regained enough glamour to do so), but that seems like a risky proposition to me. Angelica is more observant than Desiree for one thing, and while I could technically call her in to fulfill her duties as Claviger whenever I want to do so, it might raise her suspicions if I choose to do so without a plausible reason.<br /> <br /> Lowjack had mentioned an alternative\u2026 allowing our suspects to be questioned by the Winter Court while under the influence of some of Twitch\u2019s concoctions. Apparently he has a serum of some sort that dampens creativity\u2026 while it doesn\u2019t exactly force people to tell the truth, it makes it difficult for them to come up with plausible lies. Or at least, this is how Twitch pitched it to Lowjack\u2026 but as Lowjack said, Twitch really likes injecting people with things, so he might have oversold its effectiveness. Most of the motley didn\u2019t think this was a good idea. D, naturally, was Twitch\u2019s staunchest supporter, and whole-heartedly endorsed letting him take a crack at Angelica.<br /> <br /> The other thing Boss Lowjack wanted to stress was that he didn\u2019t want word getting out that Angelica was under suspicion, because as an escapee of the Director, her reputation might never recover from such an accusation\u2026 even if she turned out to be innocent in the end. I think he has a valid point, and we all agreed to proceed with caution in her case.<br /> <br /> And then there\u2019s the matter of Chalcedony. Hoo boy, that one really blew up in our faces. Despite what I said to her at the coronation last night, I have never fully trusted her, and this new information would seem to lend credence to those private doubts (or not-so-private; I think most of the motley agrees with me on this). Julia has never liked Chalcedony, and at one point she stated fervently that if Little Girl Blue ever does anything to hurt Marguerite again, she\u2019d kill her.<br /> <br /> This set Marguerite off in a way I don\u2019t think any of us expected\u2026 though maybe we <u><u>should</u></u> have, given the day she\u2019d had. She <u><u>exploded</u></u> at Julia, screaming that nobody was killing anybody under any circumstances. While I agree with the sentiment and I certainly don\u2019t think we should take such drastic action without absolute proof of wrongdoing, I still think that Marguerite has a bit of a blind spot where Chalcedony is concerned. She stormed off to cool down up in the catwalks, and the meeting sort of degenerated from there. After a hasty conversation with D, I put my arms around Julia and tried to calm her while my wife went up to speak with Marguerite.<br /> <br /> We <u><u>did</u></u> manage to get the two of them calmed down and talking again, which is good. The four of us are going to spend the evening together \u2013 with no other partners \u2013 which I think we all need about now.<br /> <br /> Luna has agreed to stay at the Dream House tonight to make sure she\u2019s available if we need her. I know she doesn\u2019t like the crowds we generate on the weekends (and tonight will probably be even busier than average, as at least a few local changelings will probably want to get a look at the new Spring Queen), so I really appreciate her making that sacrifice. She said to think nothing of it, and that she\u2019d probably take a couple of days during the coming week to get back to nature, as she doesn\u2019t feel comfortable staying away from the woods for too long.<br /> <br /> So here I sit, trying to prepare for tonight\u2019s show and stressing over both the Loyalist issue and how I treated Marguerite earlier. Have the pressures of the monarchy <u><u>already</u></u> changed me that much? It doesn\u2019t seem possible. Maybe I was like this all along, and it\u2019s taken the stress of the situation with Marguerite to make me see it. But that doesn\u2019t seem quite right either\u2026 I don\u2019t know.<br /> <br /> Marguerite, if you\u2019re reading this sweetie, I\u2019m sorry. I didn\u2019t make the conscious decision to manipulate you; I would never do that. And I promise that I\u2019ll take more care in the future. Like I said earlier, I love you, and I\u2019m sorry for what you went through earlier today, and I\u2019m exceedingly grateful for the information you were able to gather. I\u2019ll talk with Boss Lowjack as soon as I can, and I\u2019ll make sure he understands that we can\u2019t put you in that position again.<br /> <br /> Okay, I need to stop dwelling on this stuff. We have a show starting in less than an hour, and I need to be ready to give it my all. I just hope that when the final curtain falls, I can maybe gain a little clarity on this whole situation and figure out what I need to do.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei de la Rocha</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Well, today definitely ended up being more exciting than I was expecting. The coronation went without a hitch. Dark Kimberly contacted Lori before the event to let her know that her dress was done and to ask her what she wanted to do about the \u201cafter partly.\u201d Apparently there is usually an orgy after the Spring monarch coronation to celebrate. Lori elected to let anyone who wanted to come be there. She also stipulated that there should be no weapons allowed at the coronation. I did not want to leave my daggers behind, but I complied with Lori\u2019s wishes on this one. I left my knives at the Dream House. I believe Luna and Calamity did the same. Julia on the other hand did not. She had her carving knife in her purse. We got that all worked out though, so it was fine. So, we all met up at Glamor Springs and went in a back entrance so we wouldn\u2019t be seen by the guests. There was no real reason why our motley would be there if Lori wasn\u2019t becoming the Queen. There Lori got changed into her new Hedgespun dress, which was beautiful. Dark Kimberly really outdid herself. The dress looked like it was made of sunlight on roses with dew drop pearls and a flowing veil that could have been made, and probably was, of morning mist. Lori looked radiant. Her smile lit up the room. No pun intended. We also discussed security. Ji Wan Ja, Louie and T.J were all doing security for the event. And the first two were the only ones allowed to carry weapons. T.J is his own weapon. That man is huge. And to make things believable Shi disguised himself as Lori and accompanied Missy and Jane in the main room. That way folks would think that Lori was there and not wonder where she really was.<br /> <br /> We stayed in a side room with Lori while Princess Jolie made a speech to the crowd. I don\u2019t remember the specifics. I was too busy paying attention to Lori and how nervous she was. I was also kind of nervous myself. The motley was going to go out with Lori to support her after she\u2019d been introduced. Then, sooner than I think Lori was hoping for, Jolie finished her speech and introduced Lori as the new Spring Queen, and De la Rocha as her consort. Then the rest of us filed in and took our places behind Lori in a semi-circle. She knelt in front of Lori as she passed along the crown to my friend. The other monarchs, who were there, all bowed respectfully but remained standing. Everyone in the room knelt at the announcement and then Lori made her speech. She talked about the responsibility of a monarch being to serve the people and some other stuff. Again, I was paying attention to a lot of stuff at that exact moment. If I didn\u2019t know Lori so well I wouldn\u2019t have been able to tell how nervous she was, but she pulled it all off like a champ.<br /> <br /> After Lori was done with her speech there was some noise coming from the pools across the room. Then suddenly Captain Jack emerged from the center pool wearing a dress much like the one that Lori wore last night. Then coming out of the two pools surrounding that one were back up singers for Jack. They all had diving gear on except Jack. Then Jack went into singing <i><i>Like a Prayer</i></i> as a tribute to Lori. He actually did a really good job singing almost exactly like Lori did last night. The crowd was impressed, and Lori said something along the lines that now it was official. After that there was a lot of mingling and congratulating going on. Tamara came up to me to talk for a bit. She was looking out of place since LowJack was busy elsewhere. So we talked for a bit. She commented that things were going to get interesting for the motley now that Lori was a monarch. I asked what kinds of things would change and she brought up personal examples. She is Boss Lowjack\u2019s assistant and has to deal with complaints and inquiries frequently. On at least one occasion someone who was upset threatened her because they could not threaten him. Lowjack did not take kindly to someone threatening the woman he sees as a daughter and threatened them right back. That man can be scary, and I\u2019m pretty sure he doesn\u2019t bluff so they believed him. Tamara also mentioned Lowjack shooting someone that had threatened him to his face. He just killed the man and calmly had someone clean up the mess afterwards. After that he just went back to work like nothing happened. No shaking hands, nothing. I was not really surprised to hear about that. Lowjack is a man that knows how to get things done and he strikes me as the type to do the hard stuff himself when necessary.<br /> <br /> Sometime later in the party I noticed Julia singing softly to Desiree. If it had been anyone else I wouldn\u2019t have looked twice, but I know how Julia\u2019s singing effects people, so I paid attention. Sure enough a moment later Insincere Marguerite picked Desiree\u2019s pocket/purse and lifted her phone. She then went to a nearby wall and leaned against it and went through the phone. After she was done she slipped the phone back in Desiree\u2019s purse and came over to talk to me. She told me what she had found. It turns out that Angelica was trying to get Desiree to meet up with her last night, but Desiree turned her down. Desiree texted that they \u201cdon\u2019t play that game anymore.\u201d Or something along those lines. Angelica didn\u2019t acknowledge that and continued to try and get Desiree to meet her. Desiree then flat out said that she doesn\u2019t work for <i><i>him</i></i> anymore and neither does Angelica. After hearing that I said that we should report this to Lowjack. Insincere Marguerite agreed and I went ahead and gathered up Boss Lowjack and Tamara. Tamara was being eyed by Carla so I figured I\u2019d rescue her too. Lowjack said something to tease Tamara and she actually called him Daddy when she replied. I\u2019ll admit that was a little surprising, but I suppose it shouldn\u2019t have been.<br /> <br /> After that we all went to a side room where Marguerite was waiting and we told him everything that we had found out. We discussed options. We said that we could have Angelica summoned to meet with Lori since she was the Spring monarch now. And while she was at the Dream House we could have Julia distract her while Insincere Marguerite acquired her phone and checked it. Lowjack did say that no matter which route we take to keep it within the motley. We don\u2019t want anyone else in the Freehold getting wind of the possibility that Angelica may be a loyalist. It would ruin her reputation regardless of what we find out in the end. He also pretty much flat our ordered Insincere Marguerite to question Desiree about the chats and find out anything else that Desiree knows. He was polite about it, but it was an order nonetheless.<br /> <br /> After all of that we went back to the Dream House. Well, Lori and De la Rocha stayed behind to enjoy the \u201cafter party,\u201d but the rest of us elected to go back home. We all split into our own pairings and enjoyed a night with loved ones.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Saturday dawned bright and relatively early. Lori and De la Rocha came back to the Dream House and we filled them in on what we found out last night from Desiree\u2019s phone and about our conversation with Boss Lowjack. Marguerite and Lori were both a little annoyed at Lowjack for ordering Insincere Marguerite to question Desiree. Marguerite does not like to be ordered, nor does she like to use her influence over Desiree to make her do things. Lori phrased it differently and backed up Lowjack\u2019s wishes. She said that we really needed to know what Desiree did, but she phrased it in such a way so Marguerite did not immediately balk at the idea. So, we invited Desiree over to talk. Julia did not want Marguerite to be alone with our guest and insisted that someone be in the room with her. We debated who could do it for a little while before it was suggested that I could be invisible and still be there as back up for Insincere Marguerite. I think that Desiree knew something was up when she walked into the room with Marguerite, presumably alone. She \u201copened\u201d the discussion with an attempt to seduce Insincere Marguerite. After it looked like she was getting distracted I carefully made my way over to the pair and gently nudged Marguerite in the ribs to get her back on track. It worked for a bit. Marguerite tried to get the conversation going again before Desiree started to derail things again. Insincere Marguerite started over and told Desiree to stop. She then faltered a bit when she started asking about the texts between Angelica and Desiree. I put my hand on Marguerite\u2019s shoulder to show her that I supported her and was there if she needed me. Marguerite then rallied and flat out asked Desiree about what was going on. In the end she had to order Desiree to talk. It wasn\u2019t pretty. Desiree didn\u2019t want to discuss the topic at first but eventually complied and even called Insincere Marguerite \u201cMaster.\u201d Marguerite looked devastated at that but kept going. Eventually we found out that The Director sends out a musical signal to his people. It sounds like Carnival music and they know that a message with instructions will follow. Desiree immediately responded to Angelica\u2019s texts in the negative but never got any instructions. Once we had the information we needed Insincere Marguerite dismissed Desiree and the other woman left the Dream House. I don\u2019t think she was too pleased with being ordered to talk either.<br /> <br /> <br /> After Desiree left I dropped the contract I was using to remain invisible and gave Marguerite a hug. She looked like she really needed it. Lori came in a moment later and took Insincere Marguerite into her own arms and held her tight. After a minute Marguerite calmed down and we talked about what we had learned. I opted to call Lowjack and brought him up to speed on what we had found out. He agreed that we needed to find out any information that we could from Angelica\u2019s phone. He did warn me that if we decided to confront her directly that she can inspire awe and fear in equal measures with one of her contracts. I\u2019ve seen Lori do it in the Hedge once. It was memorable. I\u2019m sure that Angelica could do it just as well. If that happened it would be difficult for us to capture her if she decided to run. So, we thought that inviting her over and sneaking the phone would be the better option. I said that we should try that option first. We don\u2019t want to play our hand too early and ruin the surprise. Lowjack also brought up the idea of bringing her to him and he could have Twitch inject Angelica with something that would make it difficult for her to lie. Now, while the idea has a certain appeal I don\u2019t trust Twitch as far as I can throw him and don\u2019t want him shooting anyone up with anything. Especially if there might be side effects that are not fully documented yet. Angelica may be a loyalist, we don\u2019t know for certain yet, but I\u2019m not going to subject her to Twitch\u2019s methods if I can help it.<br /> <br /> So we discussed things with the whole motley and it was agreed that we should have Insincere Marguerite pick pocket Angelica\u2019s phone first and see what can be found out that way. If necessary we will confront her directly and hopefully be prepared if she decides to use her awe/fear power to get us to stand down. While we were talking about Angelica, Chalcedony came up. Julia really doesn\u2019t like the blue girl and said that if Chalcedony should prove to be a threat that she would stab her. Insincere Marguerite got really upset by that idea and vehemently argued against it. She even rounded on Julia for making the suggestion. Julia herself was upset at Marguerite reaction to her, but believed that her idea had merit. Marguerite stormed off and went up to the catwalks to sit with the puppets up there. After a moment De la Rocha went up after her to calm her down. Lori talked to Julia to do the same. Eventually they got Julia and Marguerite to make up. Things were not back to normal per say but they were closer than they had been.<br /> <br /> While things were being worked out with Insincere Marguerite and Julia, my sweet Luna offered to stay the weekend while all of this was going on in case she was needed. She is one of the few in the motley that may have an innate defense of sorts against Angelica\u2019s fear inducing powers. Her, Calamity and Julia all have powers that can help themselves and others resist fear effects. Handy that. I thanked Luna for being willing to stay over the weekend. I know that she relies on her time in the woods to recharge and center herself. Maybe sometime this week the two of us can go off to the forest and chase poachers, camp, hike or just spend time together. Whatever we do it will be worth it.<br /> <br /> Hopefully all of this will be resolved soon. This situation is causing a lot of stress for a lot of people and I don\u2019t like seeing my friends so upset. Lori is stressed about being the newly elected Spring monarch and on top of that she has to deal with the fact that it looks like two of her court may be loyalists. Insincere Marguerite is stressed because she had to use her influence over Desiree to get the other woman to talk. Julia is stressed because her lover blew up at her for suggesting that we may need to take Chalcedony out of the picture. I didn\u2019t want to make things worse, so I didn\u2019t mention that I agreed with Julia. Chalcedony seems to have some sort of influence over woman in general and it\u2019s causing problems. It has compromised Insincere Marguerite\u2019s thinking and it has Molly completely smitten. Even Lowjack doesn\u2019t like the influence that woman has on his operative. It\u2019s mostly a one-sided relationship. Molly loves Chalcedony, but the reverse is not true. Molly knows this, but still does pretty much whatever the blue girl wants her to. Hopefully that influence is lessened somewhat by the fact that Molly has her memories back and a better sense of self.<br /> <br /> These past two days have just been nuts. I don\u2019t know what the future is going to bring, but as Tamara has anticipated I bet it will be interesting. Here\u2019s hoping that we are up to dealing with whatever comes our way.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite</b><br /> <br /> Everything has gone disastrously.<br /> <br /> Well, not everything. Juliette\u2019s coronation has gone very well. She is now Spring Queen. I do not envy her. Better scuttling in the shadows, am I. To skitter happily. I could have been Queen of Night in the Lady by the Sea. I do not regret not. But Juliette was lovely, radiant, and beautiful. Seeing her in that gown I fell in love with her all over again. I think the whole family did. And an excellent speech, and it was moving to see the entire Spring Court, and a few more, bow to her.<br /> <br /> I wish that were all that were on my mind.<br /> <br /> The Director is causing trouble, somehow aware of the change in the wind. We suspected Desiree, Angelica and/or Chalcedony of some possibility of mischief. Desiree, being our friend, was the first approach. Julia distracted her while I swiped her phone. Fortunately nothing damning, but problematic texts with Angelica. Obviously, Desiree is not a woman who would betray us, but why she said nothing about Angelica possibly being up to something is troublesome. Boss Lowjack ordered me to interrogate her, knowing that she obeys me. I did not agree but I did not disagree either.<br /> <br /> The next day I reluctantly invited Desiree over after talking to Juliette and everyone else. Jacob hid in the room where we were to meet, cloaking himself from sight. Desiree played coy, seductive, and I kept losing myself in her deep dark eyes. Eventually I began to push, and she grew evasive. Jacob put his hand to my back to remind me, and I realized I had to do something drastic. Against my better judgment, I told her her\u2026Master\u2026demanded answers and she complied, obeying I completely and without any hesitation or emotion. She heard music that indicated a message from the Director was incoming (she had never mentioned this to the Court even when turning over information to them) and that when Angelica messaged her she suspected she had too. She noted Angelica never confirmed it but played coy, using their relationship to try to get Desiree to come. Desiree eventually ended the conversation. She seemed\u2026relieved\u2026when I took control of her, almost leaning into her loss of will and self, visibly drinking in my power over her. I play games of control with White Maria and sometimes even my Maria, but both women know my control over them ends when they say the right word, or when the scene ends. This was real. Desiree\u2019s eyes pleaded with me to accept her surrender again. I neither accepted nor refused it. I sent her away. I had broken my promise to myself never to control her again. I failed myself.<br /> <br /> Juliette was incredibly supportive. She held I, when I needed her to so very much. I shook, but when she held me, and I felt her hair on her shoulder, and smelled her scent, I felt so much better. I calmed. I felt like I could deal with it. Jacob supported me as well. Appropriately.<br /> <br /> I had a few drinks and went to be alone, though I allowed Julia to join me, but Jacob called for a meeting. I clashed fiercely with Julia there over Chalcedony. I will not allow anyone to murder her. That Julia even mentioned it was horrifying. I stormed off. Maria came and found I, and got I to acquiesce to Julia joining me. We hashed it out. I still oppose any form of violence on Chalcedony and will not permit it.<br /> <br /> This comes in a complicated time. While not a relationship, Julia and I have been close to Trinh, and we have spent a lot of time together. It is fun, and she is not jumpy about me like Jane and Melissa are. I had to let White Maria know I simply could not handle a fifth relationship a while back; I already worry that I am stretched too far with Julia, Juliette, Maria and Yvette. We will see my relationship with Yvette is less intense. She gets home middle of next week. It has been awhile for me, but over six months for her since we have spoken beyond phone. I miss her.<br /> <br /> Still this has been very stressful. I did not need this with Desiree, Angelica or Chalcedony to happen now. Especially Desiree and Chalcedony. Juliette and Jacob were so suspicious of Chalcedony, but even Julia, who usually has my back was that way. I mean it is good given stuff like happened with Desiree she is willing to disagree in public, but not this time! I hope to get things straightened out and find the truth for myself. Some may see villains, I see people needing help. Let\u2019s not be Darke, or Lucian.<br /> <br /> Please?<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXIII</i><br /> <br /> Well that was a time eh?<br /> <br /> As I have mentioned I give Romancers (like Desiree, or Veronica) a bonus to Manipulation rolls in any role that their striking looks would apply. In addition to the difficulty picking them out. Desiree is a dangerously seductive woman, and Jacob twice prevented IM from giving in to her wiles. I required a Clarity roll for both women when they fell into the Keeper/Servant rolls. IM had a one die penalty but passed (with one success) Desiree\u2026I have not told anyone the results of her roll.<br /> <br /> Lori herself explained the powers she used. The Coronation was fun and really was the bulk of the session. Lori does have the crown powers now.<br /> <br /> Lori\u2019s player would be disappointed in me if I did not mention the Madonnis pun was said out loud at the game, not a witticism come to later.<br /> <br /> I can\u2019t think of anything else requiring notation, but as always Comments and Questions are welcome. We love hearing from you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 07-29-2018, 04:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T02:33:33-07:00","id":1245076,"title":"","content":"Lori and Calamity work to get to the bottom of the issue with the potential loyalists. All three make an appearance at the Dream House. Lori begins to suspect a fourth figure is involved as Calamity meets up with a Demon Hunter.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXIV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> This is not getting any easier\u2026 though I suppose I had no right to expect that it would.<br /> <br /> Saturday night\u2019s show rolled around right on schedule, and while the crowd wasn\u2019t <u><u>huge</u></u> or anything, we still had a respectable showing (even for a weekend). Marguerite was still upset and opted not to perform, which pleased Sandra as she got to spotlight her new number in front of a larger audience than she\u2019d anticipated. Calamity did perform, but seemed to be a little distracted\u2026 her moves were still impeccable and her stage presence magnificent, but I could tell that her mind was elsewhere.<br /> <br /> For my main solo I did a breathy rendition of Leonard Cohen\u2019s \u201cLight As the Breeze,\u201d which really got the audience going. I love Cohen\u2019s music, I really do\u2026 and apparently he produced a lot of his best work while I was in Arcadia. I almost hate to say it, but\u2026 well, in most cases I prefer to hear <u><u>other</u></u> artists\u2019 renditions of his work. His deep, scratchy, soulful voice is wonderful at communicating pain and sorrow\u2026 but I think his true genius is as a poet and songwriter rather than as a performer, sort of like Bob Dylan. I gave the song a sort of gospel/blues flair, inspired by a version recorded by Billy Joel in the late 90s.<br /> <br /> It was nice to be able to draw in all of that lovely desire and replenish my somewhat depleted glamour reserves, too\u2026 though I was nowhere <u><u>near</u></u> as drained as poor Marguerite. Since she\u2019d blown most of that glamour while trying to help me figure out what\u2019s going on with our three Director escapees, I decided to do what I could to help her. It was tiring, but by focusing my mental energy on my new crown I was able to sort of super-charge her efforts to harvest glamour. I guess it makes sense in a way\u2026 Spring is the season of bounty and renewal, after all.<br /> <br /> I visited a few of the usual suspects, but didn\u2019t attempt to lure anyone into my boudoir\u2026 Marguerite needed the family last night, and the family\u2019s needs are <u><u>always</u></u> paramount. Still, I passed a few minutes hobnobbing here and there. I made sure to let Kimberly know how very impressed I had been with her handling of the coronation ceremony. That girl is a marvel, and I fully intend to make use of her in the future for any planning or organizational duties which might come up.<br /> <br /> The other two changelings in the audience who particularly stand out\u2026 well, I can\u2019t talk about one without mentioning the other. First\u2026 Chalcedony was there, propping up the bar with Molly. It was obvious that she was at least a little uncomfortable, but she was doing her best to suppress that knee-jerk reaction for the sake of her companion (Molly looked ecstatic). I settled in by the bar and started a conversation. At first, Chalcedony tensed up noticeably\u2026 her hand clenched over Molly\u2019s in a subtle death-grip. I did what I could to put her mind at ease, talking about soothing, comforting, <u><u>familiar</u></u> things until she fell into the easy flow of the conversation. I never tried to overtly reassure her that she was safe at the Dream House, or do anything else that might remind her of that awful day more than a year ago. I think she appreciated that.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2026 I\u2019m going to try to come back here more regularly,\u201d she said after a while. \u201cI think it\u2019s time. I\u2019m not going to dance here\u2026 not yet, anyway. It\u2019s been a long time since I really danced, but I don\u2019t think I could\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I gave her a genuine smile. \u201cWe understand,\u201d I said softly. \u201cLook, Chalcedony\u2026 I can\u2019t tell you how happy it makes me to see you here. And just let me know when you\u2019re ready to get back up on that stage. There will always be a place for you here.\u201d<br /> <br /> She looked down at her lap, but smiled. \u201cThanks, Your Highness, that means a lot to me,\u201d she said softly. I\u2019m still not used to hearing the honorifics, honestly, but at least this time I managed to avoid staring at her like an idiot or otherwise making a fool of myself.<br /> <br /> The topics of our conversation sort of wandered all over the place after that. It turns out that Chalcedony knows Veronica, which is sort of interesting, and that she was casually acquainted with Rowan and Neon through our mutual friend. During one conversation with the three of them, Rowan had waxed rhapsodic about the joys of sailing on the ocean, and Chalcedony had become curious about the experience, having never enjoyed it herself. I told her that I had been out on Rowan\u2019s boat a few times, and had enjoyed it immensely.<br /> <br /> \u201cGood,\u201d she said. \u201cI\u2019m supposed to go out on the water with Jolie tomorrow. She mentioned the other day that she was looking forward to doing a little boating now that she finally has a little free time, and when I told her about my interest in her hobby, she invited me to come along.\u201d<br /> <br /> Well, that sent all kinds of red flags up in my head, considering everything we had heard and learned about Chalcedony\u2019s recent activities. I excused myself as soon as I could do so without arousing her suspicions, and made my way gradually over to Jolie\u2019s table.<br /> <br /> \u201cGood evening, Your Majesty,\u201d she said with a radiant smile as I approached, \u201cthe show was spectacular, as always. I look forward to coming here more frequently, now that I\u2019m not so tightly bound to Glamour Springs.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019ll always be welcome here, Princess,\u201d I said (I\u2019d been told that it\u2019s a sign of respect to refer to former monarchs by their titles, and my respect for Jolie knows no bounds). \u201cI look forward to seeing you more often.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMe too,\u201d she said, pitching her voice low. She was playing things flirty, and as always I responded in kind. What can I say? I\u2019ve always had a thing for Jolie, and that hasn\u2019t changed just because our respective positions in the Freehold have flip-flopped.<br /> <br /> In any case, we talked for a while about this and that, and eventually I turned the conversation toward her little sailing trip the next day. She confirmed that she was indeed planning such an expedition, and seemed unconcerned about her own safety. \u201cAfter all,\u201d she said, pooh-poohing my concerns, \u201cI\u2019m a water fae\u2026 if anything dangerous happens, I can always just slip over the side and swim away. I can breathe water, you know.\u201d I did not, in fact, know that, but it did a lot to assuage my worries, so I let it go after that.<br /> <br /> As things were winding down, Desiree and Angelica stopped by and made a beeline toward me, but it was nothing serious. Angelica just wanted to hash out a schedule for her claviger duties. Becky will be able to take on more shifts and still spend time with Calamity now that I\u2019m Spring Queen, but we hadn\u2019t formalized any sort of duty rotation as of yet. I asked her to come back for an hour or so on Monday afternoon so that we could get something set in stone, and later confirmed that time would work for Becky as well.<br /> <br /> Once the last of the guests had left, Marguerite descended from her perch, and the family withdrew to her room. Marguerite was a little needier than usual last night, but I think most of us expected that, and we were all eager to let her know that we would always be there for her. I hope we reassured her on that count, as there was a lot of love in that room\u2026 not just lust, but true, compassionate, romantic, committed love.<br /> <br /> As per usual on a Sunday morning, my phone alarm blared into a room of grumbling darklings entirely too early, and I staggered to the shower, washed, shampooed, rinsed, blow-dried, and primped myself awake. I put on a typically sober church ensemble and drove to the chapel humming quietly to myself. As always, it was a lovely service, and as I sort of expected (and half-dreaded), Dad pulled me aside afterward and asked if he could speak with me.<br /> <br /> \u201cThere is something different about you today, Juliette,\u201d he said with a pointed glance just above my head.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell\u2026 this is a new skirt,\u201d I replied, deciding to tease him gently for a moment.<br /> <br /> He nodded, not looking at my outfit at all. \u201cAnd quite fetching,\u201d he said wryly, \u201cbut I was referring to something\u2026 else.\u201d<br /> <br /> I sighed. \u201cSo you noticed the crown, huh?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt is\u2026 difficult to miss,\u201d he admitted. \u201cDoes this symbolize some sort of change in your status within the changeling community?\u201d<br /> <br /> Damn, he\u2019s sharp! \u201cYes,\u201d I admitted. \u201cEarlier this week my friend Jolie asked to speak with me. She\u2019s served as the Freehold\u2019s Spring Queen for a few years now, and had decided that it was time for her to step down. She offered the title to me, and after considering for a day or two, I accepted.\u201d<br /> <br /> Dad considered that for a minute. \u201cSo you have assumed a bit of local authority? You are the queen now?\u201d<br /> <br /> I shook my head. \u201cI\u2019m one of four. Our political system shifts with the seasons of the year. I won\u2019t actually be the reigning monarch until late March. But yes\u2026 you\u2019ve got the basics right.\u201d<br /> <br /> He pulled me into a hug. \u201cCongratulations, Juliette,\u201d he said fervently. \u201cI always knew that you had something like this in you.\u201d And I could see that he meant it. And I could see <u><u>pride</u></u> in his eyes. Real, genuine parental <u><u>pride</u></u>. It was all I could do to hold the tears back until I got to the \u2018vette.<br /> <br /> I stopped by Lowjack\u2019s bar on my way back to the Dream House. He was the only one there when I arrived\u2026 and I mean that literally: no patrons, no changelings, no Tamara, nothing. He greeted me warmly as I entered and asked what he could do for me.<br /> <br /> \u201cI was wondering if I could talk with you privately for a few minutes, John,\u201d I said. That\u2019s another thing I\u2019m going to have to get used to\u2026 calling Boss Lowjack by his first name.<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course, Lorelei,\u201d he said, tacitly acknowledging that this form of address was fine with him. \u201cShould I close the bar while we speak so we\u2019re not interrupted?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIf you would,\u201d I replied.<br /> <br /> He put a sign out that read \u201cClosed, Back in 5 Minutes\u201d and led me back to his office. \u201cSo what can I do for you?\u201d he asked once we were both seated.<br /> <br /> \u201cI wanted to talk with you about our Director situation,\u201d I said slowly, \u201cand specifically about how we need to approach it moving forward.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHas more information come to light?\u201d he asked, interested.<br /> <br /> \u201cI think you\u2019re as current as anyone,\u201d I said. \u201cJacob told you about what Marguerite learned from Desiree yesterday, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> He nodded. \u201cI got a full report.\u201d<br /> <br /> I looked down at my lap. \u201cI know how important it is that we get as much information as possible about the Director\u2019s actions. I agree with you one hundred percent on that score. That\u2019s why I did what I could to convince Marguerite to help us out by talking to Desiree. But I want you to know what it cost her.\u201d<br /> <br /> His eyebrows scrunched slightly. \u201cIs she all right?\u201d he asked.<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cI think so. But that relationship \u2013 the relationship we exploited yesterday \u2013 it isn\u2019t healthy for either of them. You see, when they fall into those roles, Desiree sees Marguerite as a surrogate Keeper. That\u2019s why Marguerite kicked back so hard when you asked her to crack the whip.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShit,\u201d he said quietly, \u201cthat was our best source of information.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know,\u201d I said, \u201cand I\u2019m sorry to do this. But Desiree is a member of my court, so she falls under my protection. And Marguerite\u2026 she\u2019s in my motley. She\u2019s more than that. She\u2019s family. So I\u2019m asking if we can put our heads together and come up with another way\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course,\u201d he said immediately. \u201cYou\u2019re right; the welfare of our citizens \u2013 <u><u>all</u></u> of our citizens \u2013 has to be our first priority. If I\u2019d known more about the nature of their relationship, I wouldn\u2019t have pushed her. I\u2019ll refrain from doing so in the future. In fact, since all three of our suspects are Spring Courtiers, I\u2019m inclined to step away from this investigation entirely and let you handle it your way.\u201d<br /> <br /> I blinked a couple of times; I couldn\u2019t help it. \u201cYou want <u><u>me</u></u> to take over the investigation?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> He nodded. \u201cI don\u2019t want you to feel that I\u2019m trying to control Spring Court affairs; that\u2019s not how I run things.\u201d<br /> <br /> I regained my composure, and I think I managed to keep the desperation out of my voice when I said \u201cbut you\u2019ll still offer advice if I ask for your help, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> He chuckled. \u201cOf course,\u201d he said.<br /> <br /> I should clarify here that Boss Lowjack never <u><u>insisted</u></u> (or even <u><u>requested</u></u>) that I take the matter out of his hands. It was more like he was offering to let me take up the reins, since all three of our primary targets are members of the Spring Court. While the Winter Court officially oversees matters of spycraft in the Freehold, he saw it as a courtesy to let me handle this particular matter \u201cin house,\u201d if you will. My decision to (mostly) do so has more to do with me wanting to prove that I\u2019m up to this Queen thing than with any pressure I might have felt from Lowjack.<br /> <br /> We talked about a few other things. I mentioned that Angelica would be stopping by the Dream House the following day to set her claviger schedule, and told him that we intended to try to get a look at her phone then, to see if we could corroborate or disprove any parts of Desiree\u2019s story. We discussed Desiree <u><u>herself</u></u> for a good long while. Most of the monarchs are\u2026 let me just say \u2018concerned\u2019 about her, as she\u2019s too damn good and manipulating people and no one ever knows exactly where they stand with her. I also told him that Chalcedony was going out with Jolie for a short cruise that day, which he took about as well as I had. At my request, he assigned Dahlia to watch the two of them and make sure Chalcedony didn\u2019t get up to anything untoward.<br /> <br /> I promised I\u2019d keep him in the loop if we learned anything, and he let me out (changing the sign to indicate that the empty bar was once more open). I drove back to the Dream House, where Sex Breakfast was well underway. Trinh let us know that she planned to cook us a Cajun-style feast on Tuesday morning, and I made arrangements to be there during the prep phase to learn what I could about cooking that style of food.<br /> <br /> I pulled Marguerite aside for a moment and let her know that I had spoken with Lowjack and that she wouldn\u2019t be asked to use her influence over Desiree again. I thanked her again for doing what she could to help the investigation, but assured her that we would find other methods in the future. She was very happy about that (which warmed my heart), but gave me a very serious look before we rejoined the others. \u201cI would do this again \u2013 this and more \u2013 if you asked it of me, Juliette,\u201d she said, deadly serious.<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you,\u201d I said, giving her a kiss. \u201cI promise I\u2019ll do everything I can to make sure I never <u><u>have</u></u> to ask it of you again.\u201d<br /> <br /> Conversation at breakfast was more political than suggestive that morning\u2026 and I can\u2019t say I particularly enjoyed the change. We started discussing the 70s as a decade, and I explained to Missy and Jane the rather annoying tendency people today have to equate the entire decade with a few cultural touchstones, like Disco culture. I\u2019ve tried over and over again to make people understand that those trends didn\u2019t even <u><u>start</u></u> until the decade was nearly over, but to little effect.<br /> <br /> In any case, I tried to explain that the overwhelming cultural theme of the 70s was disillusionment\u2026 the nation coming to grips with the fact that the high ideals of the 60s didn\u2019t hold up in a practical setting, and that the idealistic leaders of yesterday were destined to become the disappointing oppressors of tomorrow. <u><u>That\u2019s</u></u> why I chose <u><u>Jaws</u></u> as the perfect film to represent the 70s when we did that themed movie night. \u201cIt had nothing to do with the damn shark,\u201d I explained yet again, \u201cit was about how the government <u><u>reacted</u></u> to the shark\u2026 how they betrayed their people for the sake of commerce and political expedience.\u201d I sort of trailed off after that, as people were giving me glassy-eyed stares.<br /> <br /> D then opined that the 70s served as a crucible to corrupt the rebellious fighters of the 60s into a nation capable of electing Ronald Reagan as president. I paused for a moment to explain to Missy and Jane that yes, she meant <u><u>that</u></u> Ronald Reagan. My wife <u><u>really</u></u> doesn\u2019t like Reagan. She explained her reasoning, and it seemed sound, though one can never really tell when Maria starts ranting like that. She ended the conversation by saying that she was going to head into town and start punching anyone who looked like they were old enough to have voted for Reagan. I <u><u>think</u></u> she was joking about that\u2026<br /> <br /> Marguerite headed into the vents after breakfast for a little quiet contemplation. Julia went up to the roof to paint (for essentially the same reason, I guess), and Calamity and Becky joined her. Jacob and Luna went into the woods for the afternoon, and it spontaneously turned into an overnight trip at some point.<br /> <br /> I took Missy and Jane aside for a serious talk. Ever since Friday night, when they\u2019d asked whether they were a part of my motley, I\u2019d been meaning to explain to them exactly how that whole deal works. So I spent an hour or so detailing the pledges and other responsibilities inherent in joining a group like ours, and exactly how serious a commitment it is. They were a little overwhelmed at first, but cottoned to the notion quickly.<br /> <br /> After I was sure they understood what they\u2019d be getting into, I asked if they were serious about joining our motley. They conferred briefly, and then came to the conclusion that they both really wanted to be in motley with <u><u>me</u></u> in particular. They like my friends, and they would not mind being in the greater motley\u2026 but the driving force in their minds was to keep the three of us together. I can relate.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve heard stories of changelings who belonged to more than one motley, but it\u2019s rare. The main reason that it\u2019s rare is that if those motleys ever come into conflict, someone who belonged to both would be forced to break an oath to <u><u>someone</u></u>, which is a very serious thing when the Wyrd is involved. Add to that my commitment to the Spring Court and to the Freehold in general, and you can see why I might not want to be pulled in too many other directions. The two of them understood this once I explained it, and agreed that joining the larger motley would be the best option if the others would be willing to have them.<br /> <br /> Marguerite popped her head out of one of the vents and gave her immediate approval (Missy and Jane seem to be mostly over the sense of unease they got from her feline demeanor, by the way). I went up to the roof and asked Julia and Calamity. Julia gave her consent almost immediately, which choked me up a little considering the recent trouble between her and Jane. Calamity was a little more guarded in giving her consent, stating the very valid concern that she doesn\u2019t really know either of them very well at this point\u2026 but she also said that she trusted my judgment and wouldn\u2019t object if they wanted to join.<br /> <br /> D got back shortly thereafter, and I managed to interrupt a spirited debate between her and Julia regarding the merits of skirts versus pants long enough to get her okay on the Missy and Jane question as well. I called Jacob\u2019s cellphone and he and Luna both agreed too (Luna stating wryly that members of the motley with wings were starting to catch up to those without wings in numbers). So with that settled, I hunted down my best friends and gave them the good news. I think we\u2019re going to make it official within the next few days, and I couldn\u2019t be happier.<br /> <br /> Sunday night showtime was fast approaching, so I went off to start my preparations. Somehow D and Julia\u2019s earlier skirts-vs-pants argument had resulted in a promise that I would wear a pair of tight leather pants during my solo that evening. I\u2019m still not entirely sure how that happened, but I grinned and bore it (those pants did make my ass look good, after all, and when have I ever objected to that?).<br /> <br /> I was doing an updated version of the Ronettes\u2019 \u201cBe My Baby,\u201d based on a cover by another girl-band called the Dollyrots. I think I knocked it out of the park, but as usual it\u2019s up in the air as to whether the applause was for my singing voice, my figure, or some combination of the two. It topped off my glamour reserves nicely, though, so I\u2019ll take it.<br /> <br /> I noticed Jolie was in the audience again, seemingly no worse the wear for a day spent on the ocean with Chalcedony. I made up my mind to speak with her before the end of the evening, but alas, \u2018twas not to be. Gloria was there as well, chatting happily with D and occasionally throwing me a wave. The only other member of the audience who stood out was a new face\u2026 an attractive redhead with dazzlingly bright, reflective green eyes. She obviously wasn\u2019t human, but she didn\u2019t have a mantle, so she wasn\u2019t a Changeling either. Curiouser and curiouser\u2026<br /> <br /> Unfortunately the vast majority of my evening was decided by someone who showed up about halfway through the show. Desiree slipped in quietly and made a beeline for the backstage area, and then up into the rafters to speak with Marguerite. She descended about twenty minutes later, looking decidedly disgruntled and walking toward me with a determined air. \u201cIs there somewhere we can speak privately?\u201d she asked without preamble.<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course,\u201d I said, and led her toward the kitchen. \u201cWhat\u2019s this all about, Desiree?\u201d I asked once we were alone.<br /> <br /> She started talking about Angelica\u2019s relationship with the Director in general terms. She was defending her girlfriend fervently, and asking me to take it on faith that she wasn\u2019t working against the Freehold in any way. She made a few disparaging remarks about Chalcedony as well, but admitted that she couldn\u2019t prove any wrongdoing on the other girl\u2019s part either.<br /> <br /> She claimed that Angelica had been manipulated into meeting Chalcedony in the Hedge when the Director\u2019s call went out on New Year\u2019s Eve. The two of them wanted to discuss how best to respond to that call, but could not agree upon the best method of doing so. She claimed that Angelica didn\u2019t want to betray her new home, but that she was afraid to come forward\u2026 afraid that she would be driven out as a potential Loyalist.<br /> <br /> \u201cDesiree,\u201d I said, taking her hand in mine, \u201cyou are my friend, and I want to believe what you\u2019re telling me. I truly do. And both you and Angelica are members of my Court, and therefore under my protection. But this is too big for me to sit on\u2026 the safety of the entire Freehold could be at risk. Do you think Angelica would be willing to talk to me directly about this? If what you say is true then I promise you Angelica will be safe\u2026 we\u2019ll keep her connection to these events quiet so that her reputation in the Freehold won\u2019t suffer. But I can\u2019t help you \u2013 either of you \u2013 unless you trust me.\u201d<br /> <br /> She thought about that for a moment, and then stepped away and pulled out her phone. I stayed within earshot (I admit, to make sure she wasn\u2019t giving the other girl instructions or cues\u2026 my I\u2019ve gotten suspicious lately, haven\u2019t I?) but didn\u2019t interrupt their conversation. A few minutes later she disconnected, and let me know that the claviger was on her way.<br /> <br /> When she got to the Dream House a short time later, Angelica told me a very similar story\u2026 similar but not identical. Angelica said that Chalcedony had accused Desiree of being behind the fact that so many of the Freehold\u2019s denizens seem to fall in love with her (Chalcedony, I mean). She was a little hazy as to <u><u>why</u></u> Desiree might want lots of people falling for her, and in my opinion Chalcedony is just a little too willing to blame Desiree for anything which causes her problems.<br /> <br /> Also, Desiree referred to the Director\u2019s points of contact with his agents as \u201cdead drops.\u201d Angelica did the same\u2026 at first, with Desiree prompting her. When left to her own devices later in her tale, however, she used the term \u201crendezvous,\u201d which to me implies that the three of them were meant to meet with someone else\u2026 someone more firmly in the Director\u2019s employ.<br /> <br /> I thanked the two of them for coming to me with this information, and asked if they would be willing to give the same information to Boss Lowjack. I assured them that he would be just as committed to keeping the investigation discreet as I was. After discussing the situation between themselves, they agreed on the condition that I be present for the questioning, and I gave Lowjack a call (it\u2019s nice to have his direct number for situations like this).<br /> <br /> \u201cGood evening, Lori,\u201d he said once we were connected. \u201cWhat can I do for you?\u201d<br /> <br /> I gave him a brief rundown of how my evening had gone, and told him that the girls were willing to speak with him at his earliest convenience. I offered to ferry them over to his place right then, actually, but he had a different idea. \u201cWhy don\u2019t you bring them by tomorrow morning. In the meantime, send me an email containing everything you can remember about what they told you tonight. I\u2019d like the opportunity to go over it and think about how to best proceed with questioning them.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cUnderstood,\u201d I said. \u201cI can have that to you in about twenty minutes. I\u2019ll talk to the two of them, and the three of us will be at your place at, say\u2026 ten o\u2019clock tomorrow morning?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019ll be fine,\u201d he agreed.<br /> <br /> Once that mess was out of the way, I thought I might just be able to catch some of our regulars before they left for the evening. Alas! Just as I was finishing up my email to Lowjack (making sure to mention the \u201cdead drop/rendezvous\u201d discrepancy), Calamity found me in the kitchen. She wanted to talk about the newcomer\u2026 and I admit that it was probably information I needed to know.<br /> <br /> The mysterious stranger\u2019s name was Caoimhe O\u2019Rourke (pronounced something close to \u201cKee-vah\u201d if you can believe that; I had to look up the proper spelling), and she was looking for someone. Apparently one of the dancers Kimberly employed while we were in Arcadia disappeared suddenly after quitting without notice. Her name was Sabrina Watson, and Kimberly had left a handwritten note in her personnel file that she was \u201ctrouble.\u201d<br /> <br /> Oh, and apparently she was also a demon.<br /> <br /> A demon.<br /> <br /> A fucking <u><u>demon</u></u><u>!</u><br /> <br /> I <u><u>so</u></u> do not need this shit right now.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it seems that Caoimhe belongs to a group that hunts these demons. It sounds sort of like that \u201cLong Night\u201d organization Dad told me about, but I don\u2019t think these are the same guys. For one thing, according to Calamity Caoimhe had taken on some of the characteristics and powers of these demons herself, to help with her hunts. That sounds downright Faustian to me, but as I know next to nothing about these people or how they operate, I don\u2019t feel qualified to judge the wisdom of their actions.<br /> <br /> Caoimhe wants to meet with Kimberly to see if she can pick up any leads on how to find Sabrina the Teenage Demon, and Calamity agreed to set up the meet (Kimberly wasn\u2019t present for that particular show). Calamity <u><u>also</u></u> assured me that she had made Caoimhe aware of the Dream House\u2019s status as a sanctuary, and of the fact that any violence committed here would be visited with swift retribution. Caoimhe agreed to abide by our rules, though she was obviously disappointed, because (in her words) \u201cthey\u2019re much easier to kill with their tits out.\u201d Classy.<br /> <br /> I spoke with Marguerite briefly next. She was upset with Desiree, but didn\u2019t seem devastated like she had the other day. Apparently Desiree had come to her first with the information, but Marguerite had turned her away, only communicating with her through those creepy puppets she keeps up in the rafters, and eventually getting so frustrated that she just told Desiree to come to me with her information directly. Her standoffish attitude seems a little odd to me, considering how close those two usually are\u2026 but I may be reading too much into this. Marguerite might just be pulling back a bit in the wake of what happened between them on Saturday.<br /> <br /> The last of the stragglers were heading out when I returned to the theater. Jolie was long gone, so I missed my opportunity to see how her outing with Chalcedony had gone. D and Gloria were hanging out by the door giving me questioning glances, so I ambled over to them.<br /> <br /> \u201cHello, ladies,\u201d I said with a yawn and a stretch as I approached. \u201cIt\u2019s been a hell of a day, and we are feeling the pressures of the monarchy most keenly,\u201d I said with an overblown longsuffering sigh.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat do you need?\u201d D asked, pulling me into her arms.<br /> <br /> \u201cBasically I just need to get laid,\u201d I elaborated.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo,\u201d D glanced at Gloria, \u201cwhat sort of sleeping arrangements do you want tonight, babe? How many lovers would it take to help you forget your troubles?\u201d<br /> <br /> I let a coy grin settle on my face as I glanced at the pair of them. \u201cI think I\u2019d be fine with two,\u201d I said softly, \u201cif they were the <u><u>right</u></u> two, and they were willing.\u201d<br /> <br /> D gave Gloria a look, and the blonde beauty smiled and shrugged. \u201cSure, I\u2019m game,\u201d she said happily, \u201cI\u2019ve never slept with a queen before.\u201d (I refrained from commenting at this point that I had, in fact, slept with two).<br /> <br /> So the three of us made our way to our bedroom and proceeded to make slow, sensual love (which, by mock-royal decree, had to include one of Gloria\u2019s heavenly backrubs) until we fell asleep together. I only slept for about four hours though, before I woke up and couldn\u2019t seem to drift off again. I slipped out of their arms as gently as I could, and I\u2019ve been sitting at my desk ever since, writing in this diary, staring at the two of them snuggled up against each other and wondering how I could ever have thought that their feelings for each other could be a bad thing.<br /> <br /> Sigh. On top of everything else, I suppose I\u2019m going to have to talk with Gloria about our relationship at some point. She\u2019s a great friend, a passionate lover, and an incredible woman all around. My feelings for her are\u2026 I don\u2019t know. They\u2019re intense. While they\u2019re not on the same level as my feelings for Marguerite or Julia or Oleander\u2026 I just don\u2019t know.<br /> <br /> I know that D wants the two of us to get together in a more formal way, and I\u2019m open to that if Gloria is. But I can\u2019t afford to spread myself too thin, especially now that I have so many additional duties. If tonight proved one thing, it\u2019s that I can\u2019t count on having time to hobnob and shoot the breeze with my friends after shows anymore. Less time for my own pursuits means less time for my girlfriends. And I don\u2019t want another situation like I had with Rowan\u2026 I still feel bad about the pain our relationship caused her.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if this is something Gloria wants\u2026 I don\u2019t think I can say no to that either. It would make Maria happy. It would make <u><u>me</u></u> happy. If it would also make <u><u>Gloria</u></u> happy, then who am I to deny it?<br /> <br /> In any case, it\u2019s almost time for me to get up anyway, so I\u2019ll probably pep myself up with Spring contracts and see if anyone wants to join me in the shower. Then it\u2019s off to meet Desiree and Angelica to witness their debriefing with Boss Lowjack. Then I\u2019m supposed to meet with Angelica and Becky to hash out the whole claviger thing. Then comes movie night, when I might have to oversee a meeting between Dark Kimberly and a demon-hunter. Then\u2026<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei de la Rocha</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> So, the show tonight was interesting. Well the events that happened outside of the actual acts were interesting. Chalcedony actually came to the Dream House with Molly. Molly was happy as a clam to have her lover there with her, but Chalcedony was not as sanguine about the whole thing. At one point Desiree came into the club with Angelica. They headed straight for Lori to talk. Chalcedony saw this and immediately tensed up. It was noticeable, at least by me it was. Molly put her hand over Chalcedony\u2019s and the blue girl calmed down somewhat but she was still tense. It is obvious that Chalcedony really, and I do mean <i><i>really</i></i>, doesn\u2019t like Desiree. I talked to both women for a while catching up with Chalcedony. I asked what she\u2019d been up to lately. She mentioned having gone to San Diego. I guess that happened while I was in Arcadia because I don\u2019t remember her leaving. She also said that she was going on a boat trip with Princess Jolie tomorrow. I wished her a fun afternoon and continued to pour drinks. Hopefully Jolie will be okay. I don\u2019t trust Chalcedony, but there\u2019s no real point to hurting Jolie now that she\u2019s no longer the Spring queen. Lori also came over to talk to Chalcedony. It was very general conversation. Mostly Lori doing her best to put Chalcedony at ease while she is in the club. I only heard bits and pieces of the conversation, but then I wasn\u2019t really trying to listen in.<br /> <br /> After the club was closed and all the guests had left Insincere Marguerite finally came down from the catwalks, where she\u2019d been for the entire night. She had done the lights and such for the acts, but she was also up there to stay away from everyone else. It seems that she did not feel like socializing very much tonight, well except with her puppets. After the motley was all together Lori let us know what the conversation between Angelica, Desiree and herself had been about. Angelica had not yet met with Lori to discuss her claviger duties, so they made arrangements for Angelica to come by the Dream House on Monday afternoon to work out the details. If things work out on Monday maybe we can have Insincere Marguerite pick Angelica\u2019s pocket so we can get an idea of what was said the other night when the call from the Director came.<br /> <br /> Should be interesting tomorrow. Luna said that she\u2019d stay at the House this weekend. I never get to see my Luna on the weekends unless we have specific plans. So tomorrow will be fun.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Well, we certainly did have an interesting conversation at breakfast this morning. Everyone gathered for Sex Breakfast as per usual. Lori and Marguerite were a couple minutes late. They had something to talk about before they ate. That and Lori was a little late in getting back from church today. I guess she probably had to have a talk with her dad about the crown that appeared over her head. He can see that and it deserves an explanation. I hope he took the news okay that his daughter is now a monarch. Lori didn\u2019t really say anything about it.<br /> <br /> De la Rocha was in rare form, going on and on about Ronald Reagan. Missy and Jane had to be told by Lori that they were in fact talking about the actor. I didn\u2019t know that President Reagan had been an actor. I\u2019m sure it was brought up in history class, but that was such a long time ago that I can\u2019t remember it. You\u2019d think I could considering that I have eidetic memory, but there\u2019s just some things that are missing from my childhood. Anyway, De la Rocha was roasting the former president. Eventually we got onto other topics, but Reagan kept coming up later. After lunch De la Rocha kept going on about finding people that were old enough to have voted for Reagan and punching them in the face. This would put her targets in their 50\u2019s or older for the most part, so I hope that she was joking. She did go out riding, but I know Lori at least talked to her before about the hitting of older people.<br /> <br /> Becky and Calamity went up to the roof to watch Julia paint which left me and Luna wondering what to do. I asked if she\u2019d like to go to the forest and harass poachers. She smiled at me and said \u201cyes.\u201d So, we headed for the woods. Before we actually got into the forest Lori called asking if we\u2019d mind if Missy and Jane joined the motley officially. I asked Luna and she said that she was fine with it. She even said that it would help even out the number of folks with wings to the folks without wings. I don\u2019t really know Missy or Jane very well, but then I didn\u2019t know my other motley mates at all before we made that Pledge. I figured that if I can make a Pledge with complete strangers, then letting acquaintances in would be okay too. I told Lori that we were okay with it and she happily hung up the phone.<br /> <br /> After that it didn\u2019t take long to find someone doing something stupid. We caught one guy who had set up a hunting nest in a tree. He hadn\u2019t done anything yet, so we \u201cconvinced\u201d him that it was in his best interests to leave. Another guy had actually killed a deer and was getting ready to clean and skin it. We snuck up on the dumbass while invisible and had fun whispering things in his ears. It was hilarious. His head was pretty much on a swivel. He kept looking around trying to see the owner of the voices, but we stayed out of reach. Mostly. I did grab his shoulder at one point and boy did he jump. My hands are cold, which was the point behind that little bit. He freaked out at that point and started running for his car. He almost left his rifle behind but managed to grab it before fleeing. There was nothing that we could do for the deer. It was dead. So, we finished cleaning and skinning it and prepared the meat to be salted or frozen. I figured we\u2019ll bring some of it back to the Dream House tomorrow and we can have venison steaks or maybe stew. Some of it we salted so Luna would have a supply of food at her cabin if the need should arise. Some of it we had for dinner. I love camping out with my Luna.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXIV</i><br /> <br /> Just to avoid unnecessary suspense, Insincere Marguerite\u2019s fit of pique with Desiree was focused around the fact that Desiree tried to convince her to sort of nudge/manipulate Lori into dropping any concern about Angelica. She argued Angelica had done nothing wrong so no need to besmirch her reputation. IM agreed, but refused to manipulate Lori. That, and the general irritation with the situation, lead to her using puppets to talk to Desiree until she became frustrated and left.<br /> <br /> Caoimhe is one of the Lucifuge. They are discussed more in Hunter: The Vigil. Being that the game is this far along she has something of a power boost but the theory and basics are the same, just not scale quite as much.<br /> <br /> I think that covers the events of the session. The early days of the rule of Mistress Lorelei continue in two weeks. As always, comments and questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T09:11:31-07:00","id":1245120,"title":"","content":"So, small d demon (practically anything), or big D Demon (Unchained)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T12:37:23-07:00","id":1245159,"title":"","content":"Small d, in this case.<br /> <br /> <i>Malibu Dream House</i> is unlikely to see much GMC. I keep encounters with other supernaturals rare and straightforward if mysterious as the focus is heavy on the Changeling community. It has occasionally come up in <i>Balance of Shadows</i>, not a major thing but another mystery out there. It deals with all the weird shit <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 08-12-2018, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T11:55:31-07:00","id":1249503,"title":"","content":"Apologies for the delay, just got access again on my desktop<br /> <br /> The investigation into the potential loyalists continues, but just as there starts to be movement the Demon hunt comes to a head.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Okay\u2026 what in the ever-mother-lovin\u2019 <u><u>fuck</u></u> just happened?<br /> <br /> I keep going over it in my head, trying to figure out when exactly today went so completely off the rails, and further trying to figure out if there was anything I could have done to prevent it.<br /> <br /> Well, things started out okay. I woke up this morning from a dream I can\u2019t remember. Maria\u2019s strong arms were around my waist, and I similarly had my arms around Gloria, whose head was pillowed on my left breast. Though I really hated to disturb the idyllic scene, it was less than an hour until I was supposed to meet Desiree and Angelica at Lowjack\u2019s bar, so I stroked their hair and kissed them each softly as I wriggled out from between them. They settled into each other\u2019s embrace, and I pulled the sheet up over the two of them before heading to the shower.<br /> <br /> I returned to the bedroom to dress after my shower, kissed my slumbering lovers, and quietly told their insensate forms that I would be back later for Sex Breakfast. I headed over to Lowjack\u2019s bar, and met Desiree and Angelica in the parking lot. Lowjack greeted us as we entered, and thanked us for coming. He led us to a back room. It was sparsely furnished, but contained a single table with two chairs on either side of it. He took a seat on one side, and indicated that I should sit next to him. Desiree and Angelica sat opposite us.<br /> <br /> The questioning was fairly gentle on the surface of things. Angelica and Desiree each repeated the stories they\u2019d told me on the previous evening, with the details pretty much the same. Lowjack asked for clarification on a couple of points, but otherwise mostly just sat and listened. I kept quiet for the most part myself, occasionally interjecting with a question of my own, or to verify the parts of their stories that I could. I tried to subtly suggest throughout the interview that I was on their side, looking out for their best interests, and I <u><u>think</u></u> it worked\u2026 though it\u2019s always hard to tell with Desiree.<br /> <br /> In the end, Lowjack offered to get the two of them drinks while we discussed what we had heard (for the record, Angelica took him up on the offer and accepted a rum while Desiree contented herself with water). Once we were out of earshot, we talked about how best to proceed. He\u2019s still letting me take the lead on this investigation, but was happy to suggest a few possible options.<br /> <br /> He\u2019s been very helpful throughout this whole situation. And though I don\u2019t want to think this way, a small cynical part of me wonders about his motives for that. I mean, don\u2019t get me wrong\u2026 I honestly believe that John has the best interests of the Freehold at heart, and that he really wants to do what\u2019s right when it comes to the possibility of Loyalists among our people. But I can\u2019t help but wonder if he\u2019s subtly manipulating me at the same time. Of the options he presented me, one clearly seemed to be the best\u2026 and now I\u2019m wondering if that\u2019s mostly due to the <u><u>way</u></u> he described them on some level. He\u2019s been very supportive ever since I talked with him about Marguerite\u2019s situation, and he made it very clear that he didn\u2019t want to do anything to risk her safety or Clarity\u2026 which was <u><u>exactly</u></u> the right thing to say to get me firmly on his side.<br /> <br /> In any case, he listed three potential avenues of investigation. First, we could ask or order Angelica to take us to the site of the Director\u2019s \u201cdead-drop\u201d and look over the area for ourselves. Second, we could ask the two of them (and potentially Chalcedony) to consent to questioning while under the influence of Twitch\u2019s drugs. Finally, we could pursue the latter course <u><u>without</u></u> their consent.<br /> <br /> I opted to check out the dead-drop location first, while leaving open the possibility of resorting to Twitch\u2019s drugs at a later date if necessary. Lowjack agreed, asking me if we could follow up on this investigation the next day. He also asked if I would agree to have the two of them placed under surveillance until they lead us to the rendezvous point, and I told him that I would, but that I wanted him to \u201cconvince\u201d me that it was necessary in front of the two of them so that they would still think of me as an ally. He agreed.<br /> <br /> We talked about a couple of other things before rejoining the two of them. I pointed out that Angelica obviously knew more than she was saying, as she had once or twice slipped up when talking about the dead-drop location and stated that she was supposed to \u201cmeet him\u201d there. Lowjack also opined that Chalcedony\u2019s rant about how Desiree was causing people to fall in love with her was surprisingly plausible, as that phenomenon had done more harm than good to her reputation in the Freehold over the years. And last but not least, I let him know about the demon and demon hunter. He was not pleased by this last little morsel of news, let me tell you.<br /> <br /> I like Desiree. I want to believe that she\u2019s still the friend I knew. But I can never be certain of <u><u>anything</u></u> she says, and that scares me a little. Lowjack mentioned the possibility that she had been in deep cover for so long that she\u2019s actually become <u><u>incapable</u></u> of telling anyone the whole truth about anything, which blows my mind. For what it\u2019s worth, he doesn\u2019t think she intends any harm to the Freehold\u2026 at worst, he thinks she\u2019s planning something bad for Hollywood which could have unintended repercussions on the Lady by the Sea. Like, y\u2019know, freeing the Grand Maw and setting it loose on our enemies.<br /> <br /> We spoke with the girls again, and Lowjack presented our plan to them. Angelica wasn\u2019t wild about the surveillance idea, and I could tell that Desiree was even <u><u>less</u></u> enthusiastic about it. I asked John if such actions were really necessary, and he presented a very well-reasoned argument about how he just wanted to keep an eye on them so that if things turned sour at the dead-drop, he\u2019d know that the Director\u2019s forces had another source of information in the Freehold.<br /> <br /> I looked seriously at Angelica. \u201cIf you want me to go to bat for you on this, I will,\u201d I told her, \u201cbut it might help us put these rumors to bed once and for all if we can ease Boss Lowjack\u2019s mind about your innocence. I\u2019m truly sorry for the invasion of your privacy, but if you think you can manage it for one day\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> She glanced at Desiree, who shifted her posture subtly (I\u2019m not one hundred percent certain, but I interpreted it as a grudging show of respect toward Lowjack and I regarding how we\u2019d handled the scene). Finally, Angelica nodded. \u201cIt\u2019s fine,\u201d she said. \u201cI won\u2019t pretend to be happy about it, but I won\u2019t object.\u201d Desiree similarly agreed to be placed under surveillance, and that was that.<br /> <br /> I headed back to the Dream House for Sex Breakfast, which was well underway when I arrived (Calamity made omelets). There was a large amount of silly banter being thrown about\u2026 much of which seemed to involve my wife taunting Julia by talking about semen, for some reason. I mean, there were also plenty of references to dicks, which <u><u>also</u></u> made Julia adorably uncomfortable\u2026 but as Luna pointed out, Julia really had no room to complain, as we have far more conversations about boobs than about dicks most days anyway.<br /> <br /> Leaving that aside for the moment, Trinh also wanted to let us know that she would be meeting her Fetch for lunch early that afternoon, and asked if we felt it would be necessary to have someone watching her. I called Lowjack, who said he would check to see if Molly was free. He didn\u2019t seem too worried, as the two of them were meeting at a very public hamburger restaurant (one that serves veggie-burgers, of course) and it would be unlikely that the Fetch would want to start something with so many witnesses around. I conveyed this information to Trinh to ease her mind a bit, and told her to give one of us a call if she needed us for any reason. Much to my surprise (and Trinh\u2019s, I think), Missy actually gave her a hug before she left the house, telling her to be careful.<br /> <br /> Lowjack had also asked me \u2013 while making absolutely certain that I knew he wasn\u2019t requesting anything \u2013 if Marguerite had ever asked Desiree point-blank what her plans for the Freehold were. I pulled Marguerite aside during breakfast briefly and posed the question, again trying to assure her that we weren\u2019t asking her to do anything regardless of her answer. She thought about it for a bit before replying carefully that she had never asked the question directly, but that Desiree had told her many times that she did not want to harm the people of the Lady by the Sea, and she didn\u2019t think the other girl would have lied about that, as those conversations occurred when Marguerite\u2019s hold over her was at its strongest. I conveyed that information to John dutifully, and we moved on.<br /> <br /> I had one other private conversation before Sex Breakfast ended\u2026 this time with Gloria (D was present as well). Gloria had been acting sort of dazed all throughout breakfast, rarely joining in conversations and occasionally muttering the word \u201cboobs\u201d to herself. It was sort of flattering, even if most of it was obviously put on as kind of a joke.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo\u2026\u201d I said awkwardly, not sure how to proceed.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo?\u201d she asked, still teasing me just a little.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo I think maybe it\u2019s time we talked,\u201d I said after a moment. \u201cAbout us,\u201d I elaborated.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re probably right,\u201d she said with resignation. \u201cLook\u2026 I\u2019m very fond of you, Lori, and I mean that. I\u2019ve really loved the time we\u2019ve spent together over the past couple of weeks. But the thing you have to understand is\u2026 I want a boyfriend. I <u><u>miss</u></u> having a boyfriend, having a man close to me, holding me, with all the scents and feelings associated with that. Don\u2019t get me wrong, I love women, it\u2019s just\u2026 different.\u201d<br /> <br /> I thought I knew where she was going with that lead-in, so I sort of hung my head in resignation and said \u201cI understand.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat being said,\u201d she continued softly, \u201cthere\u2019s no way in hell I\u2019m breaking up with Maria. I\u2026 I can\u2019t even consider it at this point. So I guess what I\u2019m trying to say is\u2026 well, if we\u2019re going to see where this thing between us is going, I just need you to be okay with me maybe seeing a guy at some point. He\u2019d have to be okay with me staying with Maria anyway, so I guess adding another girl into the equation probably wouldn\u2019t make too much of a difference.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled then to show her how happy her words made me. \u201cI\u2019m okay with it, Gloria. I\u2019ve had to give a very similar speech more than once over the past couple of years, in fact. And yes\u2026 if you\u2019re sure, I\u2019d love to see where things are going between us. If I\u2019m being completely honest\u2026\u201d I looked away for a moment, not sure how to proceed.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat?\u201d she prompted.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, you know that when you and D first got involved, I had a little problem with my jealousy. What I\u2019ve never told you is that\u2026 well, it wasn\u2019t always <u><u>you</u></u> I was jealous of.\u201d<br /> <br /> She gave me a dazzling smile, and we kissed, and Maria joined us, and I guess that sort of sealed the deal. So I have another girlfriend now. She sort of announced that we were dating to the rest of the motley when we returned to the kitchen, and she sounded as excited about it as I was. \u201cI need to go,\u201d she said after a few minutes, \u201cbut do you want me to come back for movie night tonight to celebrate our new status?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSure!\u201d I said, genuinely looking forward to it.<br /> <br /> So Trinh and Gloria left within about ten minutes of each other, and we turned our attention to other matters. Calamity called Dark Kimberly and asked her about the mysterious Sabrina Watson. Kimberly elected to stop by the Dream House personally, as apparently the fact that we were asking about Sabrina warranted a longer and more involved conversation.<br /> <br /> The long and the short of it is that Kimberly\u2019s note in Ms. Watson\u2019s file was accurate: that girl was nothing but trouble. She never got into any trouble <u><u>herself</u></u> to hear Kimberly tell it, but she was a bad influence on our other mortal performers. Her mere presence seemed to bring out people\u2019s worst impulses (more on this in a bit), and several of our regulars who had been steady as rocks up until they met her began to have problems with drinking, drugs, and other such vices. Kimberly had just about reached the end of her rope when the girl quit without notice and disappeared.<br /> <br /> Kimberly was surprised to learn that Ms. Watson was an actual <u><u>demon</u></u>, but upon reflection she said it made a weird kind of sense. She offered to call a few contacts she had made at other local clubs to see if she could locate Sabrina, and the rest of us agreed that this sounded like a pretty good idea. A couple of hours later she reported that Sabrina had worked in some pretty seedy places in L.A. \u2013 strip clubs mostly \u2013 but that none of Kimberly\u2019s contacts had seen her recently.<br /> <br /> Calamity brought up the fact that she could use her contracts to locate Ms. Watson fairly easily, but she was reluctant to do so until we had spoken with Ms. O\u2019Rourke and were ready to begin our pursuit (I think it had something to do with the contract\u2019s catch, actually).<br /> <br /> Angelica stopped by briefly to hash out her schedule with me and Becky. Since Becky hangs out at the Dream House a lot anyway thanks to her relationship with Calamity, she\u2019s going to take the lion\u2019s share of the shifts from here on out. Angelica will take more shifts during shows so that she won\u2019t have to hang around the Dream House too often during the day. It took a little back and forth, but I think we eventually settled on a schedule that works for everyone.<br /> <br /> As we were waiting for Caoimhe to arrive, Calamity got a text from Trinh. Her Fetch wanted to invite her back to her house to continue their conversation, and Trinh wanted advice on how to proceed. I texted Lowjack to ask if Molly had eyes on Trinh, but he told me that she had been busy and unable to tail our houseguest. Marguerite offered to slip through the mirrors into the Fetch\u2019s house and make sure that things remained copacetic between them. I thanked her with a fervent kiss, and she left us with a smile and a wave.<br /> <br /> We didn\u2019t have to wait long for Caoimhe to show up; she arrived well before curtain for her appointment with Dark Kimberly. I don\u2019t know quite what to make of Caoimhe, honestly. She\u2019s hot as hell (if you\u2019ll pardon the expression), but her attitude is a little off-putting. Still, she was friendly enough once she\u2019d established that we wanted to help her in any way that we could. She thanked Kimberly for her information, though she seemed a bit disappointed that we couldn\u2019t be of more help to her. She apparently has the ability to see people\u2019s sins, which is why she was so wary of Calamity when they first met\u2026 she could tell that Calamity had killed her own parents, among others.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know what she saw when she looked at me. I didn\u2019t ask. Frankly, I don\u2019t want to know\u2026 though I could hazard a guess.<br /> <br /> Calamity stepped forward. \u201cI might be able to help a little more, but there\u2019s a condition,\u201d she said. \u201cI can track Sabrina with magic, but as soon as I use the ability we\u2019ll need to get going, and I\u2019ll need to drive. We\u2019ll have to keep up the pursuit until we catch up with her\u2026 no rest breaks. So obviously I\u2019ll need to be there when you confront her. And I want in on the kill.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sigh.<br /> <br /> Jacob spoke up at this point. \u201cI will go with you as well,\u201d he said quietly.<br /> <br /> Double-Sigh.<br /> <br /> Caoimhe shrugged. \u201cThe more the merrier,\u201d she said. \u201cJust\u2026 prepare yourselves, okay? When she\u2019s backed into a corner, she will reach into your soul and force you to act upon your darkest impulses, and you\u2019ll feel compelled to do so. It\u2019s hard to resist.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI should go with you,\u201d I said, remembering the last couple of times Calamity and Jacob had gone off hunting together. They <u><u>always</u></u> need my healing abilities, and I didn\u2019t want them having to drive God-know-how-far to get to me while injured.<br /> <br /> \u201cI would recommend against that, <u><u>my</u> <u>Queen</u></u>,\u201d Becky said pointedly. She\u2019d been quiet throughout the whole conversation, and to be honest I\u2019d almost forgotten she was there. So much for keeping Caoimhe in the dark about Changeling politics.<br /> <br /> I sighed. \u201cBecky, I\u2019m not going to let my motley head off into a dangerous situation like this without me there to provide healing. Come along if you must\u2026 that way you can keep an eye on me <u><u>and</u></u> spend some quality time with Calamity.\u201d<br /> <br /> She gave me a hard look, and then nodded. \u201cAs you wish,\u201d she said at last with a small bow. I don\u2019t think she was particularly happy about it, and later I caught her muttering something under her breath about how she just had to accept that Spring Queens will keep insisting on ignoring her advice and doing dangerous things.<br /> <br /> Once that was settled, Calamity did her thing. \u201cShe\u2019s in L.A.,\u201d she said after a moment, then made an immediate bee-line for the van, followed by Caoimhe, Jacob, Becky, myself, and D (who obviously wasn\u2019t about to let me go off to fight a demon without her). We hit the highway and burned rubber toward the metropolis\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026and ended up right smack in the middle of rush hour traffic. Calamity was able to keep her tracking magic going in the thick of the traffic for a while, but she could tell that Sabrina was on the move, and if we stayed too long in a single spot the magic would become much more taxing. I glanced at the gridlock around us and shrugged helplessly. \u201cI\u2019m sorry, Calamity,\u201d I said, \u201cbut I don\u2019t see what else we can do\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Calamity had her own ideas. She, Caoimhe, and Jacob got out of the van and started walking (apparently Sabrina was only a few cars ahead of us at this point). I hastily slid into the driver\u2019s seat to provide us with a quick getaway if necessary and to avoid creating the spectacle of a driverless vehicle in the middle of the street. L.A. traffic can be murder during rush hour\u2026<br /> <br /> Okay, so let me set the scene. Sabrina was in a car a few vehicles ahead of us, along with another woman. Calamity, Jacob, and Caoimhe were walking between the lanes like the stars of some action movie or other, while the good people of L.A. blared horns and shouted at each other all around us. Becky, D, and I remained in the van at this point.<br /> <br /> Sabrina obviously noted their approach, but Calamity managed to break the passenger\u2019s side window of her car and stab her once before she could react. Caoimhe did something demony-magicky, and the car was suddenly filled with fire. Jacob dashed to the driver\u2019s side and wrenched the door open, trying to get the other woman out of the car.<br /> <br /> Sabrina must have used her mojo around this point, because Calamity suddenly broke off her attack and lunged at the occupants of a nearby BMW. There were four people inside, and they were all pretty sharply dressed. I later heard Calamity refer to them as \u201cadvertising executives,\u201d but I\u2019m not sure if that was something she knew or if she was just assuming. And, let\u2019s face it; with well-dressed people in a BMW in L.A. it\u2019s a pretty safe guess in any case.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Calamity pulled one of them out of the car and\u2026 well, she just tore into him. She did a real number on him, and even from a distance I could tell that the poor man was going to die if he didn\u2019t receive medical attention <u><u>immediately</u></u>. I threw Becky an apologetic glance, muttered \u201ccover me,\u201d and got out of the van. I rushed forward and began to invoke my healing contracts on the man\u2026 only to see that Calamity was already savaging another of them.<br /> <br /> It looked like Jacob had managed to get the other woman out of the burning car, but Sabrina \u2013 now displaying a few overtly demonic traits \u2013 had clawed her way through the roof and was exerting her powers on the crowd (or maybe it was just normal L.A. rush hour insanity\u2026 who can tell?). A large man leaped out of the cab of a pickup truck and fired an indecently large revolver into the air, shouting \u201canarchy!\u201d at the top of his lungs. An elderly gentleman got out of his sedan and began to tear off all of his clothes, proclaiming to all who would listen that the Rapture had arrived. A large athletic black man took it upon himself to stop Calamity\u2019s rampage, and tackled her to the ground. And so forth and so on\u2026<br /> <br /> Things were getting out of hand, and I could only think of one way to handle the situation. I flapped my wings once and rose about six feet into the air. I summoned all the glamour I could muster and wrapped it around myself like a robe. I set it alight and allowed every spark of majesty I could assemble to flare up, giving me a beautiful yet terrifying aura (Rapture-man stepped up his religious strip-tease at that, actually). <u> \u201c<u>Enough!</u>\u201d </u> I shouted imperiously.<br /> <br /> Damn near everyone within about fifty feet of me beat feet and ran or drove away. A few people fell to the ground and prostrated themselves. There were some exceptions, though. My motley-mates were spared the brunt of the contract\u2019s properties. Becky\u2019s used to the Contracts of Vainglory, and has had practice in resisting their effects. And for some reason, the big guy fighting Calamity was able to shake it off as well.<br /> <br /> Both Sabrina and Caoimhe decided to high-tail it. I felt a little bad about scaring Caoimhe like that, but I <u> <u>had</u></u> to do something to stop the carnage, and I didn\u2019t know of any way to exempt her from the contract. She cleared out of the area pretty quickly; Sabrina wasn\u2019t so lucky. Jacob tagged her pretty good with his knives, and Calamity finally managed to shake off her mojo and finish the job. <br /> <br /> I turned toward the other wounded and did everything I could for them. By the time I\u2019d healed the second BMW victim, the black guy who had been (unwisely) grappling Calamity, and the woman from Sabrina\u2019s car, my reserves were running pretty low. I mean, I still had plenty of glamour left, but healing spells are pretty draining on an emotional level, and I was feeling pretty tapped by the time I drifted back to the van.<br /> <br /> I shut down the terrible aura after we\u2019d gotten an acceptable distance away from the scene. I\u2019d gotten three texts during the fracas. The first was from Brightstar; it simply said IS THAT YOU? I called her and apparently there were confused internet reports of an angel rising in the middle of downtown L.A. There was no direct evidence beyond some grainy \u201cobviously faked\u201d videos, and leading experts were already debunking the stories. Witness accounts were confused, and no two stories completely matched up. I told my girlfriend that yes, I was behind it, and that I\u2019d explain it all more fully the next time I saw her.<br /> <br /> The second text came from Julia, and it went to Jacob and Calamity too. She had been painting on the roof and had seen strange lights and smoke rising from the direction of L.A. She wanted to know if we were all right, so I gave her a call and assured her that all was well. Which it was. Kinda. I mean, none of us were hurt and no innocents were killed in the fracas. We took down a demon. Process that for a minute. A <u> <u>demon</u></u>. Part of me really wants to tell Dad\u2026<br /> <br /> The third and final text was from Marguerite. She wanted to let us know that a group of rough-looking men had shown up outside of Trinh\u2019s Fetch\u2019s house while the two of them were talking. They were looking for the Fetch\u2019s ex-boyfriend, and refused to believe that he wasn\u2019t inside. Apparently he was involved with organized crime on some level. I hurriedly texted her back, suggesting that she take both Trinhs through a mirror to the Dream House to keep them safe. She did so, and let me know when they were all safely away.<br /> <br /> So now I\u2019m sitting in the back of the van while Calamity drives us back to Malibu. We\u2019re probably going to be a little late for movie night\u2026 I hope Gloria isn\u2019t too disappointed. Oh, and Caoimhe\u2026 I hope she\u2019s okay. Her car is at the Dream House after all. I guess we can reimburse her for whatever she has to pay for a taxi or one of these Uber things or whatever.<br /> <br /> But for now I don\u2019t even want to think about anything but movies and my girls. Hell, I don\u2019t even know what we\u2019re supposed to watch tonight\u2026 except that it won\u2019t be <u> <u>The Exorcist</u></u> \u2026 apparently that movie still sends Missy into fits of existential terror. Is it wrong that I actually find that kind of cute?<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei de la Rocha</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Today at breakfast we had an interesting if somewhat uncomfortable conversation. Lori came back from talking to Lowjack. She met him along with Angelica and Desiree at his bar and they talked about the other night. We discussed the fact that there are loyalists in the world with Missy and Jane and they seemed confused that anyone would willingly serve a Gentry. That is where things got uncomfortable for me anyway. I know why I served the Lady. I know why I betrayed myself and my fellow Lost and joined her ranks. I wanted to live. I suppose I could have kept on going like I had been, but it was a hard life. I nearly died several times and I didn\u2019t want that anymore. So, when she offered me a place I was more than happy to take it. Calamity tried to explain that in the case of the Director he usually put some sort of programing into the minds of those in his realm. This makes just about all of them loyalists whether they know it or not. Insincere Marguerite explained that she served Mama Lion, but her Keeper didn\u2019t really live up to that name. She rewarded Marguerite when she brought someone back with her and so she kept doing it. De la Rocha told her story as well. She served the Gentry in that she tormented Twitch and others like him. I stayed silent on the whole matter in any case. After that we started talking about how we\u2019d been taken. Apparently Lori, Missy and Jane were all taken when they were walking down the street. De la Rocha and Calamity admitted that they don\u2019t remember being taken. I just said that I\u2019d been hiking in the mountains. <br /> <br /> After that Calamity brought up the fact that a demon had been dancing for our club in the past. An honest to god demon, and she was being hunted by a woman named Caoimhe. Caoimhe was hunting the demon because she was causing trouble no matter where she went, and according to Dark Kimberly who came by later, she was doing the same thing here. She had gotten a few of our dancers in trouble with drugs and such. Not cool. I realize that I\u2019m being a hypocrite here, but none of our girls should get into trouble with drugs. Dark Kimberly said that Sabrina Watson was a good dancer and very flexible during her acts but that she was trouble from the get go. She tried limiting her work to get her to leave but that didn\u2019t work. Then one day Sabrina just stopped showing up to work. Kimberly took that as a blessing and didn\u2019t look into it much further. She didn\u2019t go looking for her or anything. <br /> <br /> While all of that was going on Trinh said that she was going to go to lunch with her fetch at a bar and grill place that had food for both of them. Lori called Lowjack to make sure that this was okay and he said it would be fine. He said that if Molly was free he would have her tail the pair, but he felt confident that it would be okay since it was a very public place. <br /> <br /> Later Angelica showed up to discuss Claviger duties with Lori and Becky. They eventually worked out that Angelica would watch Lori while she was performing and at the club. Becky would watch her the rest of the time since she\u2019d be around. It seemed the most equitable arrangement. Both women agreed and that as they say was that.<br /> <br /> A short while later Trinh called and asked if it would be okay if she went back to her fetch\u2019s house. We agreed that it should be fine but said that we were going to send Insincere Marguerite to keep an eye on things through the mirror. Molly was not available to keep an eye out for them so we did for ourselves. Trinh was cool with that and we left them to their own devices.<br /> <br /> Caoimhe came by the house later to discuss what we\u2019d found out about the demon, Sabrina. We told her what she\u2019d been up to and she didn\u2019t seem surprised at all. There was some concern though. Apparently some dancers from other clubs ended up missing after Sabrina had been there for some time. We weren\u2019t missing any of our dancers which was good, but still concerning that women had gone missing from other places. Caoimhe also admitted to us that she could read a person\u2019s sins. This would explain why she was apparently so cautious with Calamity last night. I didn\u2019t see the interaction but I can get the picture. That little revelation made me wonder what kind of things she got from me. I have committed enough sins in my life to fill a whole closet. Did she read the kidnapping or murder from me first? I don\u2019t know if I want to know. The others probably didn\u2019t have similar worries. At least they don\u2019t have quite the dark things in their closets that me and Calamity do. Okay, maybe Marguerite, but I still don\u2019t think that she was being overtly bad when she did those things. Anyway, Caoimhe also warned us that Sabrina had the ability to make us do things. She could influence our will. That didn\u2019t sound great to me, but we were determined to take care of the problem.<br /> <br /> Calamity offered once we\u2019d talked for a bit to use her contract to find Sabrina. She could track where the wayward demon dancer had gone, but she would have to be the one driving when we went to go looking for her. Having seen this in action I understood the sense of that. I also volunteered to go with her in case she got into any kind of trouble. Lori looked at us like we\u2019d gone nuts, but then volunteered to come with us as well. I think her intention was to heal us if needs be and/or get us out of trouble. This of course led to Becky saying that she\u2019d come along to keep Lori safe and De la Rocha volunteering as well. De la Rocha wasn\u2019t going to be outshone by anyone when it comes to keeping her lady love safe.<br /> <br /> We drove for a bit before we got stuck in traffic. Nothing unusual, but Calamity started getting a really strong feeling that if we didn\u2019t immediately pursue our quarry then we were going to miss her entirely. Calamity is not one to lay about so she immediately got out of the van and started making her way forward. I jumped out and followed. Caoimhe had also had enough and came forward. She pulled out a shotgun and headed forward. My plan was to watch Calamity\u2019s back and help when needed. This worked up to a point. Calamity reached Sabrina and attacked the woman who was a passenger in a car. Sabrina immediately retaliated and made Calamity attack an innocent person in a nearby car. A moment later and the car that Sabrina was in was engulfed in flames. Seeing no other option I ran forward and yanked the driver\u2019s side door open so the innocent woman could get out. Sabrina tried to get herself out of the car but was unsuccessful. Calamity was still attacking an innocent man so I continued to work on getting that woman out of the car. I managed to pull her to the asphalt and away from the flames. There wasn\u2019t much that I could do for her at that point. I wanted to, but my attention was torn away by Sabrina wrenching her way out of the roof of the car. She was showing more and more demonic traits as the incident kept going.<br /> <br /> Around this time Lori, De la Rocha and Becky all left the car and headed forward to see what they could do. They came across the fight. Lori immediately tended to the man that Calamity had been attacking and stabilized him. Caoimhe shot her automatic shotgun at Sabrina inside the car and I pulled the innocent driver away from the flaming vehicle. She was a little worse for the ware, but again there wasn\u2019t much that I could do for her at the moment. She was not bleeding out or anything, so I figured that I would see to her wounds in a moment. <br /> <br /> It was soon after all that the crazy people came out. That\u2019s the best way that I can describe them. One young man jumped out of his car with a pistol and fired it into the air. Another guy tackled Calamity in an effort to stop her from hurting any more innocents. Then an older man got out of his car, stripped naked and started shouting about the rapture. A woman also grabbed her child and ran out of her car. She looked like she was just trying to get away from all of the violence. It was all very chaotic. I know that Calamity continued to try and attack folks in suits in a car. They kind of looked like they could be Ad Executives, which may have reminded Calamity of her fetch. Which is another thing that we\u2019re going to have to deal with soon.<br /> <br /> The anarchist guy with the gun finally decided that Sabrina, who was seriously starting to show off those demonic features, needed to go and shot at her. Caoimhe also agreed and fired her shotgun at the demon. I got into the fight proper and slashed at Sabrina with my knives. I didn\u2019t do much since she was still up on the car, but every little bit helps, right? At that point Lori launched herself in to the air and used that \u201cterrible beauty\u201d power of hers. She yelled \u201cEnough!\u201d at the group and all the mortals started to flee, save one. The one guy that resisted was the guy that had been attacking Calamity to keep her from doing more damage. <br /> <br /> After that the fight picked up its urgency. Calamity jumped up on the car with Sabrina and stabbed the demon. She hurt her pretty badly with that strike. I came forward with my knives and hit her fairly well before Calamity attacked the demon again, killing her. This whole time Lori was running around healing and/or stabilizing anyone that needed it. Becky got fed up with the one guy still attacking her girl friend and decked the guy that had been attacking Calamity. He went down like a sack of potatoes and Lori ran forward to check on him. She ended up having to use her healing contracts to help him too considering how much damage Becky had done to him with that last hit.<br /> <br /> While all of that was going on Insincere Marguerite texted Lori about strangers showing up at Trinh\u2019s fetch\u2019s house and asking what she should do. I think Lori quickly replied back that if she deemed it necessary she should take them back through the mirror to the Dream House. Given our guests when we got home I guess she deemed it necessary. It sounded like the people that had come calling were friends of Trinh\u2019s fetch\u2019s boyfriend. And as we know he has connections to those involved in crime. It was a good thing that Insincere Marguerite was keeping an eye on things. Otherwise things might have gotten dangerous.<br /> <br /> After the fight we dragged all those that had been injured off to the side of the road so they wouldn\u2019t get hurt once traffic started back up again, and we knew that was coming soon. We also took the opportunity to flee the scene in our van and head home. It was a bit interesting navigating our way out, but we managed to do it in pretty quick time. When we got back to the house Lori looked exhausted and it was no wonder. She had used her healing powers on several people during the incident with Sabrina, all of them innocent bystanders. I know I didn\u2019t get hit, and it seems that Calamity didn\u2019t get hit either. Caoimhe had fled the area when Lori used her power on the crowd and got an Uber ride back to the Dream House. She didn\u2019t seem all that pleased with the running away part of the afternoon, but she was happy when she was told that Sabrina the demon was no more. <br /> <br /> <br /> I will admit that it was nice to be in a fight with a straight up bad guy. It was inconvenient that it was in the middle of the highway, but Lori scaring all the folks away made things a little easier. I\u2019m still convinced that there is going to be fallout from this whole thing though. Surely someone got the fight, or part of it, captured on their phone. Who doesn\u2019t go around with out the phone these days? Whatever the case may be, I think it\u2019s going to cause more problems for the motley down the line. Time will tell though. Time will tell. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> I fortunately have begun to feel a little better. Stresses with Chalcedony, Desiree and more are upsetting, and I have spent much of my time up in rafters with my puppets (Belle Marie and I had an argument with Desiree the other night) or in the vents. I have spent some time with Wife and Brides, of course.<br /> <br /> Juliette has been good to me. All of them have, but while I got a bit upset before Juliette has gone out of her way to make me feel more secure, and I am happy with that. Julia has never failed to be by my side and\u2026Maria is helping, in her own way. It is nice when we are all together. Natural and as it should be.<br /> <br /> Today started a bit better. Rather than Maria yelling about presidents, we discussed veganism and the theoretical effects in terms of sex. Mostly, this was to tease Julia, and Maria did so happily, but without taking things too far. Trinh jumped in too\u2026she is far from wanting to become a vegan, and has promised a delicious breakfast tomorrow. It was rather fun and while Julia got a bit horrified she was not too upset. If only she was not so entertaining when she was horrified, carrying herself with an air of dignitas like she does just exacerbates it.<br /> <br /> Juliette took me aside to discuss Desiree. Last breakfast she apologized for me being in the position I was in and promised not to again, and this time was related. With the understanding she was not asking, suggesting, or telling me to, she asked if Desiree ever discussed goals or intentions with me. I told her the truth, that Desiree spoke of feeling at home here and promising she intended no harm to anyone in the hold. While it did not thoroughly please Juliette I believe she was happy for that, at least. She also spoke privately to Gloria, about something else that turned out to be semi formalizing their relationship. Juliette is unafraid to stretch herself thin apparently.<br /> <br /> Then some meetings. First Dark Kimberly discussed the apparent Demon, Sabrina, which included discussion of the acts she did. She proved both talented and flexible. I try to be open minded, but Demon sounds ominous. Then Angelica came by for Spring Court business. While all this was going on Trinh, who had gone to meet her Fetch, asked about going back to her Fetch\u2019s place. It was noted I could infiltrate with ease, so we agreed, telling Trinh and then I went myself.<br /> <br /> The conversation was largely positive. Trinh-Fetch was still intent on the Veganism, while Trinh-True did not want to take it up. She was horrified by putting animal meat in their body. Trinh-True was not unfair, but fairly firm, saying she did not want to mislead her doppelganger. There was also some pleasant childhood discussion, they sang a song together laughing, and Trinh-Fetch spoke of a gnawing emptiness and feeling of falsehood. Trinh-True said that would go away when they merged.<br /> <br /> It was interesting. I never even considered merging with my Fetch. You would never fit her in me and she is still as foul as ever. It pains me, now, to see that this is not a glitch, but a reflection on who I was. I am thankful for my being Taken, that it has helped me grow past that horrid shrew I was.<br /> <br /> My reverie was broken by pounding on the door by two or three men demanding to see \u201cAntoine\u201d, which is apparently Trinh\u2019s ex. She said he was not there. Trinh-Fetch seemed scared, so Trinh-True said she would call me from the mirror, which was my cue to enter the room. Quickly, I used my mirror trick to move them one at a time to the Dream House, which was tiring. Trinh-True wanted me to move Trinh-Fetch first, and there was no time to argue. I brought Trinh-True across next, after threatening to taunt the men on the other side of the door a second time. That confused them.<br /> <br /> They are settled in, now, and talking. Juliette and Maria are apparently off with Jacob and Calamity about the Demon business, so I am keeping an eye on the Trinhs\u2019.<br /> <br /> Ah, there is Julia, and it seems like she has an urgent update. More later.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXV</i><br /> <br /> Well that was fun.<br /> <br /> Okay lets see\u2026I have a Downtown LA random behavior chart that I finally got to pull out and use to account for the behavior of people during an obvious supernatural encounter in traffic. Each of the people described popped up on a different round, and some of them got initiatives. Who did not flee when Lori went apocalyptic was just fall of the dice, though the odds favored Becky the guy trying to restrain Calamity rolled very lucky, while Caoimhe and Sabrina got crappy rolls despite the odds also favoring them. It was a raucous good time.<br /> <br /> Lori picked up some Devotees out of it (as per the Merit in Equinox Road) and next week you will get a short story on that between sessions.<br /> <br /> Beyond that the age old question of \u201cDo Vegans Swallow?\u201d came up at Sex Breakfast, it lead to ruminations on Swallowing and Fallatio and Penises in general and left Julia rather horrified. But it was mostly going on in the background of the more \u201cimportant\u201d conversations. Also amusing was Luna, who is usually quiet, had a lot to say this time, and referenced her past as a sexually active gay man a couple times.<br /> <br /> But for now we can all enjoy the fallout of all this in addition to our usual exciting ongoing plot. For certain definitions of \u201cEnjoy.\u201d Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T13:43:13-07:00","id":1252841,"title":"","content":"Hey folks. Sorry about the lack of between week story, but I have had some connection issues with the site. I plan to put it up next weekend. Hopefully.<br /> <br /> But a session has come and gone and the investigation continues. The world of darkness creeps in a little further.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXVI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> So life goes on and the world continues to turn, and even something like fighting a demon in the middle of L.A. rush hour traffic begins to fade into memory as the problems of the present assert themselves. On the bright side of things, it now looks as though I won\u2019t have to deal with any Loyalists among my courtiers\u2026 at least not yet. The downside of that revelation is that we\u2019re back to square one when it comes to locating the potential spy within our ranks.<br /> <br /> In any case, we made it back to the Dream House right around the time the opening curtain was rising on the show, and made our way upstairs for movie night. D had selected the films, and I suppose I shouldn\u2019t have been surprised that she picked a pair of classics filled to the brim with teenage rebellion (and have I mentioned before how weird it is to refer to films which hadn\u2019t even been released yet when I was taken as \u201cclassics?\u201d I have? Okay then). I was vaguely familiar with both <u><u>The Warriors</u></u> and <u><u>The Outsiders</u></u> from the novels, but had never seen the films. I enjoyed both, but I must admit that we had ample\u2026 \u201cdistractions\u201d during the viewings, so I might need to see them both again at some point in order to fully appreciate them.<br /> <br /> First of all, D got a text about half an hour into the first film and headed downstairs to check on something. After maybe ten more minutes, she texted me to let me know that she had to keep an eye on a developing situation in the theater, and wouldn\u2019t be back up for a while. I polled the rest of the motley, sighed, and paused the movie. We were all curious about what was going on, and it was clear that we weren\u2019t going to be able to concentrate on anything else until that curiosity had been satisfied.<br /> <br /> I found D at her usual spot by the entrance. She\u2019d found the time to don her \u201cSecurity\u201d T-shirt, and was pointedly keeping an eye on an Asian lady I didn\u2019t recognize. When I asked my wife about her interest in the newcomer, she replied quietly that the woman seemed to have an unhealthy interest in Dark Kimberly. Once she pointed it out, I saw what she was talking about\u2026 her gaze was intent on our Assistant Manager, and it seemed like she was trying to figure something out.<br /> <br /> Calamity and I used contracts to determine a few things about the guest. First, Calamity determined that her greatest fear was\u2026 the sun. Well, <u><u>that</u></u> was informative, of course, as we all sort of immediately assumed that she was a vampire. I used a similar contract to pick up on the lady\u2019s desires\u2026 specifically in regards to Kimberly. What I learned came as a bit of a shock. First, she wanted to know how a supposedly dead woman was helping to run a club in Malibu. Second, she wanted to know how Kimberly was connected to the \u201cLost Angel\u201d that had appeared earlier that day in L.A.<br /> <br /> I kind of sighed as I shared this information with the other two. It was a good thing that we were all keeping our eyes on the guest, as she visibly reacted to our conversation from half a room away. We then talked out loud about speaking to her directly, and when she nodded, Calamity and I crossed the room to her table (D decided to keep her post by the door and come in as backup if necessary).<br /> <br /> The young-looking woman introduced herself as Kathy, and spoke to us pleasantly with a thick Vietnamese accent. When we asked her about her interest in Kimberly, she tried speaking in two different languages (I\u2019m pretty sure they were Vietnamese and Korean), then sighed when neither of us responded. \u201cI will talk with you about this,\u201d she said, \u201cbut not here. Not in such a public place.\u201d<br /> <br /> She joined us in the office, and we dropped the pretenses. \u201cOkay,\u201d I said softly, \u201cwhat\u2019s your interest in Kimberly? Do you intend her any harm?\u201d<br /> <br /> Kathy shook her head. \u201cI am just here for information,\u201d she replied without a trace of her accent. \u201cI want to know how a dead woman is suddenly alive again and running a burlesque house in Malibu. I know that she is not Kindred\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> We talked her through Kimberly\u2019s situation, using mostly general terms. Calamity focused on the fact that the woman who was killed was not Kimberly at all, but a replacement created by the fae\u2026 which helped to explain why there had been no body in her coffin when Kathy\u2019s associates had exhumed it\u2026 clothes, yes, but no body.<br /> <br /> As far as I could tell, Kathy\u2019s interest in Kimberly\u2019s case mostly had to do with something they call the Masquerade\u2026 to wit, keeping mortals unaware of the existence of vampires (or, as she requested I call them, \u201cKindred\u201d). Kimberly\u2019s Fetch had been killed in a fairly obvious, public way, and it had resulted in further mob violence, so it was fairly well-known that she was deceased. The Kindred of L.A. didn\u2019t want a newly-created vampire blowing the secret for the rest of them, so they sent Kathy to assess the situation.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, it should be obvious to you now that Kimberly isn\u2019t related to\u2026 your people,\u201d I said delicately. \u201cHowever, we appreciate the necessity of keeping things from the public eye. So if it will help you out, I can speak with Kimberly about staying off the stage for a few weeks\u2026 as a gesture of goodwill.\u201d<br /> <br /> Kathy nodded. \u201cI appreciate that,\u201d she said, \u201cbut speaking of secrecy, I had another question. Am I correct in assuming it was you we heard about in L.A. this afternoon?\u201d<br /> <br /> I sighed. \u201cThose were\u2026 extreme circumstances. We were hunting a dangerous individual\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cA demon,\u201d Calamity cut in, with no small amount of pride.<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cThings went south quickly. Innocents were getting hurt. I did the only thing I could think of to contain it until we could deal with the situation and get out of there. The nature of our powers means that there won\u2019t be any good pictures or video of me, and most of the mortals who saw me will wake up tomorrow morning convinced that it was all a dream or a hallucination or something\u2026 that they couldn\u2019t have seen what they think they saw.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cA useful trick,\u201d she admitted. \u201cDid you get the demon?\u201d<br /> <br /> Calamity took up the thread. \u201cOh yeah. It\u2019s not a threat anymore.\u201d<br /> <br /> We spoke for a little bit longer, and in the end arranged for Kimberly to speak with Kathy directly. I hoped that in this way we could both communicate why Kathy thought it was necessary for Kimberly to lie low for a while and give Kimberly a little closure by getting Kathy to share what she knew about her Fetch\u2019s murder. I hope we achieved both of those goals.<br /> <br /> Kimberly also told us that Caoimhe had dropped by earlier to pick up her car, and did not seem to be holding a grudge. The two of them planned to meet for coffee the next day, and Caoimhe is going to drop by for a show in the near future\u2026 so I\u2019ll have the opportunity to apologize for stranding her in L.A. in person. I still feel really bad about that.<br /> <br /> We made our way back upstairs after that to resume the movies. In our absence, Julia and Marguerite had begun making out. Marguerite was naked, and Missy and Jane were looking on at the two of them with noticeable interest. We <u><u>did</u></u> start the movies again\u2026 but Marguerite didn\u2019t put her clothes back on. Ah, what do I care? I was snuggled in between D and Gloria\u2026 so I was right up there on cloud nine with them.<br /> <br /> There was some discussion of Kathy and why she had come to our establishment that evening\u2026 but oddly most of this revolved around her name. It is apparently common practice for people of different ethnicities to adopt American nicknames when they move to (or are born in) this country. This is largely so that they won\u2019t have to teach everyone they meet how to properly pronounce their original names\u2026 but there\u2019s also an element of distancing themselves from what can be perceived as an \u201cethnic\u201d background. D of course ranted against this practice for a few minutes, and for the most part I found myself agreeing with her point of view this time\u2026 it\u2019s a shame that our culture seems intent on stifling diversity in that way.<br /> <br /> Becky did chime in at one point to note that her actual given name is, in fact, Becky. Not even Rebecca\u2026 Becky. So there\u2019s that.<br /> <br /> D, Gloria, and I retired together after the movies and more snugglage ensued. We eventually drifted off with Gloria in the middle this time\u2026 now that all three of us are officially romantically involved, it seemed only fair that she get her turn. And yes there was sex, but mostly there was cuddles and, y\u2019know\u2026 talk. It was nice.<br /> <br /> D had to get up early for therapy the next morning, so for once I got to stay in bed with somebody while she slipped quietly in and out of the room showering and getting dressed. It was nice to be able to sleep in a bit \u2013 especially in the arms of a lovely girlfriend \u2013 though I guess I probably shouldn\u2019t get used to the sensation. I\u2019ll be starting classes in a week or so, after all.<br /> <br /> In any case, Gloria and I had made our way down to Sex Breakfast by the time D, Calamity, Jacob, Missy, and Jane returned from therapy. As soon as we were all assembled, Trinh began the promised lesson in Cajun-style cooking. She added a few Vietnamese spices into the mix as well (and wrote down their names phonetically so that we could restock at a local Asian market when necessary), but she was also careful to teach us how to cook more traditional Bayou fare as well.<br /> <br /> Oh, I should talk about Trinh\u2019s Fetch, too\u2026 since we were starting to run a little short of available accommodations at the Dream House, Trinh opted to put her Fetch up at a local hotel until she felt comfortable returning to her home. So that was taken care of, and the Fetch didn\u2019t have to share a kitchen with us while we were preparing all of that delicious-smelling meat.<br /> <br /> And boy was the result <u><u>scrumptious</u></u>. Becky went so far as to comment that she had thought people mostly came to Sex Breakfast for the sex\u2026 but she was rapidly coming around to the idea that the breakfast portion was at least as enticing. Julia nodded vigorously at this, claiming that she had put on thirty pounds since coming to live at the Dream House. I expressed a bit of disbelief at this, as Julia is still remarkably thin, but she insisted that this was the case.<br /> <br /> \u201cPerhaps it is the little one,\u201d Marguerite interjected with a twinkle in her eye.<br /> <br /> As you can guess, that stopped conversations cold all around the room. \u201cYou\u2019re joking,\u201d I said, stunned. \u201cTell me you\u2019re joking.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019d better be joking,\u201d D muttered darkly from beside me.<br /> <br /> \u201cI am joking,\u201d Marguerite said after a moment.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re not pregnant?\u201d I asked Julia.<br /> <br /> She shook her head. \u201cNot as far as I know,\u201d she commented with a shy smile.<br /> <br /> \u201cAs far as you know?\u201d I asked. D continued to glower.<br /> <br /> Julia shrugged. I turned to Marguerite, who shrugged as well, but continued to grin like the Cheshire Cat. \u201cAnything is possible,\u201d she said, \u201cparticularly for a shape-changer. We have\u2026 experimented.\u201d<br /> <br /> And so the conversation turned\u2026 much to Gloria\u2019s amusement. I swear that girl has a wicked streak a mile wide; she actually encouraged us to keep talking about pregnancy every time talk started to turn toward another subject (she thought it was hot). My opinion on this subject is fairly simple\u2026 the four of us are a family. If Marguerite and Julia want to expand that family with a child, then I don\u2019t think Maria and I can reasonably object\u2026 but I <u><u>also</u></u> think it would be courteous for the two of them to discuss the matter with us before acting upon it.<br /> <br /> At some point the talk turned to <u><u>me</u></u>, and Marguerite cheekily asked if I would ever want to have a kid of my own, and if so\u2026 whose? I confess that I might have blushed a little and looked at my feet for a while before I answered. \u201cI mean\u2026\u201d I said sheepishly, \u201csure, someday, like\u2026 <u><u>years</u></u> from now, when I\u2019m not going to college and working a full-time job <u><u>and</u></u> serving the Freehold as a political leader. As for who\u2026\u201d I looked at D and I knew there was no other answer.<br /> <br /> She made a show of sighing and appearing exasperated, but the answering look she gave me was one of pure love. \u201cShit, guess I\u2019d better learn those contracts over the next few years,\u201d she said after a moment.<br /> <br /> I should also mention the evolving social dynamics of the group for a moment before I move beyond Sex Breakfast. While Calamity and I were learning to cook, Marguerite and Julia were brushing each other\u2019s hair. Now there\u2019s nothing unusual about that\u2026 but Missy and Jane had opted to join them. They were sitting there around the breakfast table, all brushing each other\u2019s hair in a big circle. Hell, at one point D even joined them (I can\u2019t blame her; I would have done so myself if I hadn\u2019t been absorbed in the cooking lesson).<br /> <br /> So when I had a few moments I pulled Missy and Jane aside and spoke to them privately. \u201cSo what was that all about?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> Missy replied. \u201cWe, umm\u2026 sort of slept with the two of them last night,\u201d she admitted, looking a little sheepish. \u201cHope you\u2019re not mad, Jules.\u201d<br /> <br /> I pulled the two of them into a tight hug. \u201cOf course I\u2019m not mad,\u201d I said with perfect sincerity. \u201cYou two are always free to have sex with anyone you want as far as I\u2019m concerned, as long as you occasionally come back to me\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course,\u201d Jane said, as though there was never any question in her mind. \u201cWe\u2019re a team. So are you the reason those two are so good at grooming feathers?\u201d<br /> <br /> I chuckled at that and allowed as how that might be the case.<br /> <br /> I had to high-tail it to meet Lowjack after breakfast, and Marguerite, Calamity and Jacob went to check out Trinh\u2019s Fetch\u2019s place. From what I understand, they\u2019ve pretty much cleared the Fetch to return to her house. Marguerite checked the mirrors, and it looked to her like the men who were looking for the Fetch\u2019s ex-boyfriend were pretty half-hearted about it\u2026 even if she had been home, they probably wouldn\u2019t have done more than ask her some questions and look vaguely threatening. So she\u2019s probably going to check out of the hotel and head back home tomorrow afternoon.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, I met Lowjack, Desiree, Angelica, Joan, and Twitch at a local Hedge entrance. Twitch expended the glamour necessary to open the gate, and Angelica led the way to the dead drop/rendezvous point (Desiree was still claiming that she didn\u2019t know where it was, which makes sense since she was stationed by the Director in Hollywood rather than Malibu). The trip was mostly uneventful, though at one point a large dog-like creature popped its head up cautiously out of the thorns to one side of the path. Twitch fired that massive syringe-gun of his at it twice, and it dropped insensate to the ground. Lowjack examined it, checked his phone, and gave Joan a nod. Joan then put her sword through its head. I later learned that he had checked a prototype app created by Oleander and found that the creature we had encountered is considered highly dangerous to changelings.<br /> <br /> John <u><u>did</u></u> have to remind Twitch \u2013 twice \u2013 not to keep his finger on the trigger of that syringe-cannon, though.<br /> <br /> It didn\u2019t take us long to reach the site in question, and it was fairly obvious that it was associated with the Director. The vines lost their thorns in that area, and twined together in a way that resembled curtains. We examined the scene as thoroughly as we could, but didn\u2019t find anything of use.<br /> <br /> Twitch used contracts to communicate with the vines directly. Though their responses were very general, they did provide us with at least a few of the answers we were looking for. The vines reported that neither Desiree nor Angelica had been to that location within the last week or so. Chalcedony \u2013 or at least someone the vines described as \u201cthe Blue Lady\u201d \u2013 <u><u>had</u></u> in fact passed by that location, but had not met anyone, left anything, or picked anything up. The only person who had recently made use of the rendezvous point was a lady with red hair\u2026 someone that <u><u>wasn\u2019t</u></u> Desiree. Though Twitch tried to get a more specific description, the vines weren\u2019t able to tell him anything more than that.<br /> <br /> So we have another mystery on our hands. This red-headed woman could be any of a number of people in the Freehold. From the information we have, it could have been anyone from Calamity to Jolie (though I\u2019m personally certain it was in fact neither of them). It could have been someone using a contract or kith ability to disguise themselves. It could have been someone like Veronica, whose hair appears to be a different color to any given observer. And that\u2019s not even taking into account mortal tricks like wigs and hair dye.<br /> <br /> Twitch offered to use a goblin contract to get more information at one point. He said that he could make the local Hedge manifest a fruit, and if he ate that fruit while remaining in the area, he would be able to glean a lot more specific details about what had gone on there recently. Unfortunately, the fruit became useless if it was removed from the immediate vicinity, and the drawback of that contract\u2026 well, Twitch said it would render him unconscious and leave his body vulnerable to possession by any Gentry with particularly strong ties to the area.<br /> <br /> I glanced at John, and the two of us simultaneously told Twitch not to do it. He shrugged, and said \u201care you sure? I figure there are enough of you here to put me down if anything goes wrong\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled. \u201cThanks for the offer, Dr. Twichowicz,\u201d I said softly, \u201cbut Maria would never forgive me if I put you in that position.\u201d<br /> <br /> He nodded. \u201cOkay,\u201d he said simply as we were packing up and preparing to head back to the World. \u201cHow is Maria doing, by the way? We should really set up another lunch\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> We talked for a while as we walked. At one point he sort of squinted and really looked hard at me. \u201cI never noticed it before,\u201d he said after a moment, \u201cbut there\u2019s something of the chirurgeon about you, isn\u2019t there?\u201d<br /> <br /> I couldn\u2019t help but smile at that. \u201cIt\u2019s relatively new,\u201d I admitted. \u201cWhen I joined the Pilgrims before my motley went to Arcadia I took on another kith. I guess the Wyrd is trying to encourage me to follow through on my medical studies.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWonderful,\u201d he said brightly. \u201cAnd speaking of which, congratulations on your acceptance to UCLA. They have a fine medical program. Maria is\u2026 she lights up when she talks about how proud of you she is. I would like you to know that if I can ever be of any assistance to you in pursuing your studies, I am at your disposal.\u201d<br /> <br /> D had told me that she was going to bring this up with Twitch, so I wasn\u2019t completely surprised by the offer. \u201cThank you,\u201d I said. \u201cI\u2019ll probably be taking mostly general education courses for at least the first year or so, but I\u2019ll let you know if I ever need any tutoring.\u201d<br /> <br /> Once we were out of the Hedge, John and I conferred about what to do next. There doesn\u2019t seem to be any point to keeping surveillance on the drop site\u2026 the Director is sure to know that it\u2019s been compromised, so he probably won\u2019t use it again. And while we know neither Angelica nor Desiree made use of the site, we aren\u2019t any closer to figuring out who our spy actually <u><u>is</u></u>.<br /> <br /> I thanked both Desiree and Angelica for their patience and cooperation, and told them how glad I was that we could close the book on this investigation once and for all. Neither one was incredibly happy with the situation, but neither seems to blame me for the intense scrutiny they\u2019ve been under, so there\u2019s that. Angelica told me that she would be at the Dream House that night for her Claviger duties, while Desiree opted to spend the evening alone. Apparently the two of them are \u201ctaking a break\u201d following the events of the last few days. A part of me feels bad about that, but I suppose it\u2019s understandable.<br /> <br /> I drove back to the Dream House and filled the others in on the results of our excursion. I also told D about Twitch\u2019s offer, and her face nearly split with her smile. \u201cI never even asked him,\u201d she told me. \u201cAnd how about him offering to sacrifice himself for the good of the Freehold? That\u2019s like something he would have done\u2026 y\u2019know, <u><u>before</u></u>.\u201d I agreed that Twitch (or \u201cAnton\u201d) was making wonderful progress, and then had to hurry off to get ready for the show.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve only been scheduling a single number for myself most nights, working on the theory that my constituents might require my time. Last night\u2019s number was \u201cHello\u201d by Adele\u2026 mostly because I wanted to challenge myself a little, I think. I mean, she\u2019s one of the most talented female vocalists in the industry today, and if my rendition of the song compares favorably to hers, then I\u2019ll know I\u2019ve really achieved something significant. I think it went over pretty well, if not as spectacularly as I had hoped.<br /> <br /> I made the rounds and spoke with a lot of people last night. First I stopped by the bar to chat with Chalcedony and Molly again. Chalcedony is still uncomfortable in the Dream House, but not nearly as uncomfortable as she was before. I think that\u2019s a good thing\u2026 if she can get over what happened to her here all those months ago, it must mean that the House\u2019s reputation in the Freehold has recovered to a large degree. Of course, I kept that conversation light and fun, and steered it away from any topics that might trigger negative memories for her. She did ask me how the monarchy was treating me. My answer was noncommittal, but generally positive.<br /> <br /> Next on the docket was Joan and Andromeda\u2019s table. Andromeda leaped up as I approached and threw her arms around me, giving me a big juicy kiss on the lips in the process. Joan, by contrast, stood and gave me a courtly bow and a chaste kiss on the hand. \u201cMistress Lorelei,\u201d she said softly.<br /> <br /> \u201cMy white knight,\u201d I replied with a smile before taking a seat at their table.<br /> <br /> Like Chalcedony, they also asked how I was coping with the monarchy, and I felt free to be a little more honest with them. \u201cIt\u2019s\u2026 there\u2019s a lot more to it than I ever imagined,\u201d I admitted. \u201cIt\u2019s a lot to deal with\u2026 but I think I\u2019m starting to get a handle on it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLike what?\u201d Andromeda asked. \u201cIs there anything we can do to help?\u201d<br /> <br /> Joan coughed softly. \u201cPerhaps these are matters Lori cannot discuss with us,\u201d she said, giving her fianc\u00e9e a significant look.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh,\u201d Andromeda said, looking a little crestfallen. \u201cI just thought she was talking about planning the Greening.\u201d<br /> <br /> Shit. I hadn\u2019t even thought about that.<br /> <br /> We talked a bit more and made tentative plans to get together \u201csometime,\u201d and then I moved on. I dropped by Jolie and Felicity\u2019s table\u2026 they were there together, but not <u><u>together</u></u> together. They <u><u>also</u></u> asked how I was coping, and I basically bared my soul to Jolie, though I used general language to avoid spilling Freehold secrets to Felicity. Jolie was sympathetic. \u201cI was able to assimilate all of that stuff gradually over the course of my reign,\u201d she said. \u201cI\u2019m sorry I had to dump it all on you at once. That must have been rough.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah,\u201d I said, \u201cbut I think I\u2019m starting to get a handle on it. What I meant was that\u2026 well, there are things I never used to think about. Decisions I made without a second thought. Now, I have to stop and think about how everything I do reflects on the Freehold\u2026 and how it affects my people.\u201d I chuckled grimly. \u201cBelieve it or not, that actually makes some decisions <u><u>easier</u></u>\u2026 but not many of them.\u201d<br /> <br /> I stopped by the door next and chatted with D for a bit. She had been trading insults with T.J. for a while, and the two of them had a conspiratorial air about them. Try as I might, though, I couldn\u2019t get anything out of either of them. I <u><u>hope</u></u> they were just planning to meet up at some point and beat the shit out of each other. It\u2019s a thing they do from time to time.<br /> <br /> Last up was the table containing Dark Kimberly, White Maria, Becky, and Calamity. I sat there listening to the banter between Kimberly and Maria for a while as they also traded insults across the table. It was sort of like watching a tennis match, honestly. But hey\u2026 I\u2019d rather have them indulging in that strange species of friendship than sending each other suicide weapons any day of the week.<br /> <br /> White Maria <u><u>also</u></u> asked how queenship was treating me, and offered her assistance in planning the Greening. And sigh\u2026 I suppose I should get on that. I mean, we\u2019ve got a few months, but arranging a venue and entertainment and catering and all of that is probably going to be a massive undertaking. White Maria said that Jolie had utilized her in the early days of her reign for those purposes, and that she would not be averse to acting in that capacity again. So I\u2019ve got her in my corner for that at least.<br /> <br /> Once people started to leave, I moseyed over to D again and let myself sag into her strong embrace. She asked if we were picking anyone up, and I left it up to her. In the end, we decided to spend the night with Marguerite and Julia (who were all for that plan), though I did suggest that at some point in the not-too-distant future I\u2019d like to explore the possibility of inviting Missy and Jane to join the two of us in bed. D said she\u2019d be fine with that, so I think I\u2019ll move forward with those plans in the next few days.<br /> <br /> For now\u2026 once again I find myself unable to sleep following the best efforts of three girls to wear me out. I\u2019m sitting at Marguerite\u2019s desk writing this entry and flipping through a medical journal\u2026 but who am I kidding? Mostly I can\u2019t sleep because I\u2019m worried. I\u2019m worried about how being the Spring Queen is affecting my character. I\u2019m worried about the mysterious red-headed informant the Director has placed in our midst. I\u2019m worried about starting college next week. I\u2019m worried about that little display the other day in L.A. \u2013 I <u><u>know</u></u> that\u2019s going to come back to haunt me somehow. So instead of getting a good night\u2019s sleep like I\u2019m supposed to, I\u2019m back to my old stand-by of pepping myself up with Spring contracts. It\u2019s nice that I have that method to fall back on\u2026 but I\u2019m sure it can\u2019t be healthy in the long-term.<br /> <br /> Sigh. Maybe I can slip in under Marguerite and settle into Maria\u2019s arms without waking them. That always calms me down and makes me forget my troubles. Here\u2019s hoping.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei de la Rocha</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Well, movie night sort of happened. We picked out the movies and started to watch them, but got interrupted halfway through the first one when De la Rocha got a text from someone downstairs saying that she was needed. So, she left to go see what was up. Those of us that were left discussed popcorn and I got some bottles to make drinks. After a little while De la Rocha texted Lori to let her know that everything was okay, but that she was going to need to stay downstairs for a bit. This peaked our curiosity so Lori, Calamity and I all went downstairs. It turns out that a human looking woman was checking out Dark Kimberly in more than a brief appreciative manner. So, Lori read her desires and Calamity read her fears. As it so happens the woman was specifically curious about how a dead woman was helping to run the club and was wondering if she was connected to the \u201cangel\u201d from earlier today. As for fears, she seemed to be mostly afraid of the sun, which was telling in and of itself. We discussed this briefly. The woman seemed to notice right off that we were talking about her so Calamity and Lori went over to find out more. They talked for a bit before starting to go to the office to continue their conversation. I decided to join them but stayed toward the back. I didn\u2019t think our guest would try anything but figured that the more of us there in case the better.<br /> <br /> Our discussion went well. It turns out that our guest, Kathy, is a kindred. That\u2019s the fancy way of saying that she was a vampire. At least that\u2019s the word that they use for themselves. Sounds fancy though. I suppose that we have some fancy names for ourselves too. I\u2019ve heard some refer to us as \u201cLost.\u201d It\u2019s apt, but still kind of important sounding. Anyway, Kathy revealed that she actually knew a good deal about Changelings and that some of us had been reading her fears and desires. We knew that kindred could tell if someone was supernatural in some way, but we did not know that they could tell if we used our powers on them. I\u2019m not sure if they all can do that but she can. She said that her interest in Dark Kimberly was not harmful. She said that she recognized our assistant manager from the news a while back when she was killed. Kathy and her superiors were concerned that she had been raised from the dead as a special kind of kindred. She even said that they had exhumed her coffin and found nothing but a dress inside. We explained the concept of a fetch to Kathy so that she would understand that Kimberly had not been raised from the dead. It was just a copy of her that had been killed while she was away. While this may have resolved issues with the kindred she said that there was still going to be problems with other groups in the city. Kimberly\u2019s fetch\u2019s death was very public and it might be noticed that she\u2019s still alive. We said that we would talk to Dark Kimberly about limiting her stage time and keeping her public presence to a minimum. Kathy agreed that would be good.<br /> <br /> Kimberly being alive could raise some mundane problems as well. Kathy said that Kimberly\u2019s fetch was killed because she made some decisions that the head of a gang didn\u2019t agree with. Specifically she decided to date one head over another and she was killed by the slighted one. Then there\u2019s something about one of the heads of a gang was killed in retaliation for her death. If it was discovered that she is alive then there might be gang repercussions to worry about. Since Kathy seemed to know so much about Dark Kimberly\u2019s fetch\u2019s death we asked if she\u2019d be willing to talk to Kimberly to answer some questions. Kimberly has been investigating her fetch\u2019s death with varying degrees of success. We figured that this could prove to be helpful in that regard. Kathy agreed to disclose what she knew about the whole situation.<br /> <br /> The last thing that we talked about was the incident in L.A this afternoon. Kathy was curious what had happened, so we explained in general terms what had gone down. Calamity flat out said that we had been hunting a demon and caught up with it in rush hour traffic. Kathy seemed to take that in stride. Lori explained that what she did would have a temporary effect on people. For the most part they would think it was a dream or forget the details of what happened altogether. Their recollections should be hazy and they might think that the whole affair was something that they imagined or exaggerated. Like I said before. Time will tell on that.<br /> <br /> After we were done talking to Kathy we brought in Dark Kimberly so the two of them could have their own discussion. Kimberly made sure that we trusted Kathy not to do anything, which we did at that point, and they started talking to one another in rapid-fire Vietnamese. They seemed to get along, at least their voices weren\u2019t raised or anything, so we left them to it. After that the rest of us went upstairs to finish watching the movies. Before we could start though De la Rocha went off a bit about people taking American nicknames when they move here or visit. Kathy was obviously not our new guest\u2019s real name, but that\u2019s what she went by. A lot of people do that, including the \u2018little shit.\u2019 He goes by Jake now. At least he did the last time I was up there. I never did. I made people say my name as it was supposed to be said rather than compromising myself and bowing to the lowest common denominator. My name really isn\u2019t that hard to say. Most people\u2019s names aren\u2019t. It\u2019s just a matter of practice to say it correctly. So, De la Rocha went on for a bit about that and Becky chimed in that people of the same ethnicity will generally use their actual given names when they talk, they just use nicknames when talking to Americans. Becky also went on to say that sometimes other Chinese folks wouldn\u2019t believe that her name is actually Becky. Her name is not Rebecca and she shortens it to Becky. Her given name is actually Becky. That little tangent went on for a bit, but eventually we got back on track with the movies. I honestly don\u2019t remember a whole lot about them right now. I was so lost in thought while we were watching that I don\u2019t think the movies really stuck in my memory. It also didn\u2019t help that Insincere Marguerite was completely naked and snuggling and kissing Julia. That was kind of distracting too.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> For once Calamity wasn\u2019t the first person downstairs getting ready to go to therapy. When she eventually did make it down I asked her what was up. She said that she wasn\u2019t looking forward to meeting with Dr. Emmett because she thought that they would be judgmental about the whole affair with the demon. I guess I hadn\u2019t thought about that. I wondered at that point what Sullivan would think of our little escapades in L.A. It turns out that didn\u2019t have to worry too much about the whole thing. Sullivan was a little concerned that I would just jump out of the car and follow Calamity through traffic to approach a target during rush hour. I know it wasn\u2019t ideal, but I couldn\u2019t just let Calamity go alone. She needed backup, and that\u2019s me. We have each other\u2019s backs when there\u2019s trouble. And that demon was trouble. She had already gotten some of our dancers mixed up in drugs. Yeah, I know, pot meet kettle. But this is different. They are innocent girls. They don\u2019t deserve all the trouble that comes along with drugs. Hopefully they can get cleaned up and be none the worse for wear.<br /> <br /> And with sex breakfast came conversation. The situation with Trinh\u2019s fetch came up and Calamity offered to go \u201cchat\u201d with the men that had come by her house to rough her up. Lori really didn\u2019t want to know what we were going to get up to. She kept going on about plausible deniability. So, we didn\u2019t make any definite plans while Lori was still here. Before anyone went anywhere there was a Cajun cooking lesson. Calamity and Lori were learning from Trinh how to make a yummy Cajun breakfast, with spicy sausage and everything else. I listened in on the lesson. It didn\u2019t sound all that hard. I may have missed some details since I was busy making coffee for everyone, but I think Trinh wrote it all down in a notebook so we can follow those directions in the future if we need to. She even wrote down the pronunciation for the Vietnamese spices that she added in along with their names written out in Vietnamese so if we go to the market we can just show the paper to the shopkeeper. You wouldn\u2019t think that Vietnamese and Cajun foods would go together so well, but you\u2019d be wrong. Together they are tasty.<br /> <br /> While the cooking was going on a good number of the girls were engaged in a hair brushing circle. One person would brush the hair of the person in front of them and so on in a circle. There was also conversation. It was commented that sex breakfast wasn\u2019t just about the sex talk anymore. It was about some really good food. At that Julia admitted that she had gained thirty pounds since moving in here. No one believed that she had gained that much weight since she\u2019s still so skinny, but she insisted that she had. She even mentioned that her doctor said that she was at a healthy body weight now. Then the jokes began about her being pregnant. Julia insisted that she wasn\u2019t, but it kept going. Gloria thought the idea was great and kept bringing conversation back to pregnancy every time it strayed. They even brought up the question to Lori about if she could be impregnated by anyone who would it be. She picked De la Rocha, no surprise there. This given the fact that there are some contracts that can allow body shaping. Apparently Julia and Insincere Marguerite have experimented with that which is why the pregnancy thing seemed like a possibility. Then they asked me when I was going to ask Luna to marry me. I responded that that conversation would be held in private. I haven\u2019t talked to Luna about marriage yet because we haven\u2019t really known each other that long, plus it\u2019s like there\u2019s something in the water. Everyone is getting married. I don\u2019t want it to seem like I\u2019m just jumping on the bandwagon and asking Luna because everyone else is doing it. I\u2019m not even sure how she would feel about the whole idea anyway. It is a conversation that we need to have at some point soon though. I will admit that.<br /> <br /> After the conversation wrapped up and the breakfast plates had been cleared Lori said that she had to go to meet with Lowjack, Angelica and Desiree. We waved her off and then me and Calamity talked about checking out Trinh\u2019s fetch\u2019s apartment. We thought backup might be a good idea so we asked if Insincere Marguerite would like to join us. She agreed. We also told Trinh what we were up to and she offered to come with us and act as bait. We looked at one another for a moment before agreeing to her offer. We all rode over in one car and Trinh went to the front door. Marguerite snuck around the side and slipped in through a screen window. I\u2019m not sure that I want to know how she does that. Anyway, Calamity and I waited in the car just in case there was trouble or if anyone showed up to watch the place. No one showed up outside. Inside Trinh looked around and let us know via text that it looked like the guys had possibly let themselves in the front door and looked around but nothing obvious was stolen. Insincere Marguerite then looked in the mirrors to see what they saw. What she saw reflected there backed up Trinh\u2019s assessment. They just looked around for a bit and left. They didn\u2019t even look around that energetically either. It was more of a half-hearted walk through. After that Trinh and Marguerite left and we all headed home. I think that Calamity was a little upset that no one was there for her to \u201ctalk\u201d to, but overall it worked out well. Trinh\u2019s fetch\u2019s apartment seems to be safe to return to. Last night Trinh put her fetch up in a hotel so her fetch wouldn\u2019t have to go home. I think we can honestly say that it\u2019s probably safe for her to go back.<br /> <br /> Shortly after we got home Lori also arrived back. She looked introspective so we traded notes on what we had found out. We shared our exploits at the apartment, which didn\u2019t amount to much, but it was information that we didn\u2019t have before. Lori then told us what had happened with her. Apparently she met not just Lowjack, Angelica and Desiree, but Joan, Molly and Twitch as well. Joan, Molly and Twich were there as protection against Hedge creatures. Molly had a semi-automatic rifle, Twitch had his syringe gun and bandolier, and Joan had her signature blade. The lot of them made their way through the Hedge pretty much uneventfully. At one point a Hedge beast stuck its head up out of a bush, only to be shot in short order by Twitch and that syringe gun of his. The creature fell right over and Lowjack looked through an app on his phone to see if the creature was dangerous or not. It seems that it was because he gestured to Joan and she walked over and neatly put her sword through the beast\u2019s head.<br /> <br /> After the dog creature was taken care of they continued on and found a part of the Hedge where the vines seemed to lose their thorns and hung down very much like curtains. Angelica did not want to go forward. She was too nervous. So, Joan and Twitch investigated the area. Joan said that there were no messages inside the drop point and it didn\u2019t look like it had been used. Twitch \u201ctalked\u201d to the vines and they said that they had seen a redheaded woman go inside within the past few days but said that it was not Desiree. They specifically did not recognize her. They also said that the \u201cblue woman\u201d walked by but did not enter within the past few days as well. We assumed that they meant Chalcedony. She fits the description that the vines gave rather well. Right before they left Twitch offered to try a goblin fruit that would allow him to see in greater details exactly what had a happened in that area. The downside to that would be that it would leave his body unconscious and him in a trance like state. It would also leave his mind open to a passing Gentry to invade. It might even call out to any that were nearby. A small part of me thought that the risk was worth it, but then another part of me said that not even Twitch deserves to be attacked in such a way by a Gentry. I may not like the man, but that is a whole other level of bad. Plus those that he was with could have been hurt, not just him. So, I\u2019m glad that Lori and Lowjack pretty much shut down that idea immediately. On their way back apparently Twitch offered to help Lori with her studies. I guess he found out that she\u2019s going to be studying medicine and thought that his knowledge could be of some use. Lori took him up on that offer when she gets done with the prerequisite classes and actually starts the medical stuff.<br /> <br /> If a temptation such as Twitch had been presented I don\u2019t doubt that a nearby Gentry would have taken up the offer. I know the Lady used to go wandering in the Hedge just to see what she could find. Sometimes she was capricious and mischievous. She was always mercurial though. Her moods could change like the winds, which is why we always did our best to stay on her good side. For the most part we succeeded. Sometimes we didn\u2019t though. One time we came back empty handed. We were supposed to have returned a pair of lovers that had escaped into the Hedge. While we were hunting them we were set upon by loyalists from another Gentry. To this day I have no idea if the lovers escaped or if they got captured by the other loyalists. We didn\u2019t see them. The other group was a good bit larger than just the pair of us and they used that to their advantage. I thought we handled ourselves pretty well considering the odds, but the Lady didn\u2019t think so. She wanted those lovers returned to her. At that moment in time they were her favorites. So, we paid for that failure in blood. At the time we were not happy with our punishment, but we thought that she was within her right to punish us. We had failed in our duty to our the Lady and she rightfully taught us the error of our ways. Now of course I just look back on the incident and see a precursor to what happened when Rook brought me back after I failed to return Delight. Though she did take that second offense much harder than the first. I had after all actively defied her. I wasn\u2019t planning on going back to her. My plan at that time was to get to the Hedge and disappear. But that didn\u2019t happen. Rook took me back and I paid for my transgressions with blood and pain. Sometimes I wonder if she is still mad at me for what I did, or if her ever-changing nature has finally moved on to something else. I can only hope that it has. She is not someone to be trifled with.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXVI</i><br /> <br /> Woo fun. Kathy was a Mekhet vampire for those playing along at home. The PCs brought up her condition first, so she did not volunteer it, and I don\u2019t think she ever mentioned her Clan.<br /> <br /> Not much else calling for detailed discussion. Insincere Marguerite makes a lot of use of Contract of Reflections. It is almost kinda a signature for her since Calamity and Jacob also make a lot of use of Smoke and Calamity also uses Darkness. Oath and Punishment would likely be signature for Calamity, Vainglory for Lorelei\u2026Insincere Marguerite and Calamity have a little, but both just enough to enhance shows. Plus Lorelei, Calamity and Jacob each have their seasonal contracts. Anyway\u2026<br /> <br /> That about covers it, but comments and questions are welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-18T12:10:42-07:00","id":1255302,"title":"","content":"Not time for an update yet, will be one as usual, but here is a short story for you by Lorelei\u2019s player.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Devotees</b></b><br /> <br /> Kellie Ann Flowers approached the church with some trepidation. It wasn\u2019t in the best part of town, and when you live in Los Angeles, that can be a very serious situation. On the other hand, it was a <i><i>church</i></i>\u2026 and her life to date had conditioned her to consider such places safe havens. She hemmed and hawed on the sidewalk for a moment \u2013 long enough to attract the attention of a few rough-looking young men on the corner \u2013 before making up her mind and ascending the building\u2019s front steps.<br /> <br /> <i><i>I have to know</i></i>, she thought to herself with resolution. <i> <i>I have to find out more about what really happened.</i> </i><br /> <br /> It had only been a day since the hospital had discharged her, and only two days since she had nearly died. Of course, the E.R. surgeons who had admitted her didn\u2019t think the incident had been that serious. By the time they\u2019d put her in the ambulance, she\u2019d only had a few minor burns and some reddening of her skin\u2026 painful but not dangerous. No one had believed her when she told them that she had actually been <i><i>inside</i></i> the burning car for nearly twenty seconds\u2026 that she had <i><i>felt</i></i> her skin blackening and flaking off.<br /> <br /> \u201cI know,\u201d the sympathetic nurse had said while taking her blood pressure, \u201cwhen you go through something like that, it can feel like it lasts forever. You\u2019re just lucky it didn\u2019t <i><i>really</i></i> last that long, sweetie.\u201d<br /> <br /> She didn\u2019t understand. <i><i>None</i></i> of them understood, and she desperately needed <i><i>someone</i></i> to understand\u2026 which is what had brought her to the church in the first place.<br /> <br /> The sanctuary was locked up tight, but the Fellowship Hall was open, and the lights were on. Long tables filled the room, and a counter separated a small kitchen at one end. At the far end of the hall, a set of stairs led down to the basement. The room appeared to be empty.<br /> <br /> \u201cHello?\u201d Kellie Ann called out hesitantly.<br /> <br /> \u201cDownstairs,\u201d a gruff, masculine voice responded.<br /> <br /> Kellie Ann walked across the empty room, the click of her high heels echoing eerily off the bare walls. The stairs were bordered by a rusty metal railing covered in layers of peeling blue paint. She descended carefully, keeping one hand firmly on the rail. The heels were <i>not</i> made for stairs.<br /> <br /> The room at the foot of the stairs was some sort of youth fellowship headquarters. The floor was covered by a hideous multicolored threadbare carpet, and a number of sofas and armchairs in various stages of disrepair were arranged in a rough circle around the center of the room. The cinderblock walls were painted an institutional shade of mint green, and sported many inspirational posters or advertisements for local Christian rock concerts.<br /> <br /> An older man dressed in a cheap suit sat in the armchair opposite the stairs, while a younger man in a tight black t-shirt and camouflage pants paced restlessly around the center of the room. The older gentleman had a severe lined face and flyaway salt-and-pepper hair that descended into a somewhat unkempt beard. The younger man was heavily muscled, with neatly trimmed short black hair and a tidy goatee. Both turned to regard her as she descended, and both looked oddly familiar to her. The room was otherwise empty.<br /> <br /> \u201cGreetings, my dear,\u201d the older man said, rising and approaching her. \u201cHave you come because you have accepted the inevitability of the End Times?\u201d he asked, his intonation making the capital letters clear.<br /> <br /> \u201cUmm,\u201d Kellie Ann mumbled uncomfortably, \u201cI don\u2019t know about <i><i>that</i></i>. I saw your ad in the <i><i>Times</i></i> classified section\u2026 about the\u2026 y\u2019know, the Angel?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIndeed,\u201d the older man said with a smile. \u201cI thought I recognized you\u2026 you were there, Miss, weren\u2019t you?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe burning car,\u201d the younger man said, snapping his fingers, \u201cyou were the driver!\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cI was out with a\u2026 a co-worker, when all that weird stuff started happening. I\u2026 I don\u2019t remember it very clearly, but I know someone pulled me out of the car after it started to burn, and I know that she\u2026 she <i><i>healed</i></i> me. Somehow.\u201d<br /> <br /> The older man regarded her shrewdly. \u201cThere are hundreds of people discussing what the press are referring to as the \u2018Lost Angel Incident,\u2019 Miss\u2026 why join our little group?\u201d<br /> <br /> She shrugged. \u201cI need to find out more\u2026 more about her. I was searching the Internet when I came across your classified ad. You\u2019re right, there are lots of groups forming out there\u2026 but your ad was the only one I saw that mentioned the <i>colors</i>.\u201d<br /> <br /> He grinned slightly. \u201cThe colors, Miss?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHer wings,\u201d Kellie Ann said in reply. \u201cThey weren\u2019t white like an angel\u2019s would be on television\u2026 they were a bunch of different colors, like some sort of tropical bird. Red and blue and green and gold. Anyway\u2026 nobody else is talking about the <i><i>colors</i></i>, and none of the pictures or videos on the Internet are clear enough to make them out\u2026 so I figured you guys must have been there too.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes!\u201d the older man said with fervor. \u201cWe were so privileged. I confess that at first I believed the end times had come at last, and began preparing myself for the Blessed Ascension\u2026 much to the chagrin of my wife, I am afraid.\u201d<br /> <br /> The younger man snorted. \u201cStarted tearing his clothes off right in the middle of the street,\u201d he commented, still staring at Kellie Ann as though he was trying to place her face. \u201cLook, no offense, but we should make sure you are who you say you are, too, so\u2026 what color was the Angel\u2019s halo? Can you tell me that?\u201d<br /> <br /> Kellie Ann smiled. \u201cNo offense taken. It was green\u2026 a beautiful green like sunlight on summer grass. And kind of\u2026 pointy.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe checks out,\u201d the man said with a wry grin. \u201cAnyway, I\u2019m Stan. They call me \u2018Bad Stan\u2019 most of the time,\u201d he added. He extended a hand and shook hers firmly.<br /> <br /> \u201cRobert,\u201d the older man said reproachfully.<br /> <br /> \u201cI like Stan,\u201d the younger man replied with an edge to his voice. For the first time she noticed that he had a pistol strapped to his waist.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou ought to embrace your Christian name,\u201d the older man insisted. \u201cThere is nothing wrong with the name Robert Palmer.\u201d<br /> <br /> Kellie Ann chuckled. \u201cRobert Palmer?\u201d she asked. \u201cYou mean like the\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes,\u201d Stan said through gritted teeth, \u201clike the pop star from the eighties. <i>Please</i> call me Stan, Miss.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay,\u201d Kellie Ann said with a nod, before turning back to the older man.<br /> <br /> \u201cCharles Nelson Grissom,\u201d he said, extending his hand in turn.<br /> <br /> \u201cGrissom like the astronaut,\u201d Kellie Ann acknowledged, \u201cone of the Mercury Seven.\u201d<br /> <br /> The old man smiled. \u201cMy third cousin once removed,\u201d he said proudly. \u201cAnd you are\u2026?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, sorry,\u201d Kellie Ann said with a nervous laugh. \u201cMy name is\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cRoxy?\u201d Stan asked, squinting at her. \u201cRoxy Stiletto?\u201d<br /> <br /> She closed her eyes and sighed. \u201cThat\u2019s my stage name,\u201d she muttered, her cheeks beginning to burn. \u201cWhen I\u2019m not working, I\u2019m Kellie Ann Flowers.\u201d<br /> <br /> Stan whooped and slapped his thigh. \u201cI knew I\u2019d seen you somewhere before!\u201d he said with triumph. \u201cShit, I stuffed a twenty into your garter not three weeks ago!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLanguage, Robert,\u201d Grissom chided. He turned toward Kellie Ann with what he probably thought was a kindly expression. \u201cRegardless of your occupation, my dear, you are welcome here. After all, the Good Book tells us that Jesus Himself ministered to the prostitutes\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHey!\u201d Kellie Ann said indignantly. \u201cI\u2019m a <i><i>dancer</i></i>, not a <i><i>hooker</i>, </i> okay? I just\u2026 I moved here from Spokane a year or so ago and things didn\u2019t turn out like I planned, and everything is so <i><i>expensive</i></i> in the city, and I\u2019m <i>trying</i> to get into an online program to get a degree in something, but I haven\u2019t gotten any nibbles yet\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Grissom held out his hands to placate her. \u201cI apologize, Miss Flowers,\u201d he said softly, \u201cI spoke out of turn.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo,\u201d Stan said, leaning against one of the sofas and stroking the handle of his pistol idly, \u201care we gonna talk about the Angel or what?\u201d<br /> <br /> Grissom nodded. \u201cA harbinger of the End Times, sent by God to warn his people that the Age of Judgment is nigh,\u201d he said, as though stating the obvious.<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t know about that,\u201d Stan rebutted. \u201cThe Angel appeared during rush hour on the gridlocked streets of L.A., and gave us the shock we needed to get moving again. I think it\u2019s a sign that we need to break free from our own complacency and throw off the shackles of unearned authority. No man has the right to rule another, and no matter how entrenched the establishment might be all it takes is a few right-minded freedom-loving individuals in the right place to\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhoa,\u201d Kellie Ann broke in. \u201cYou think the Angel wants you to\u2026 what? Start a revolution?\u201d<br /> <br /> Stan blinked. \u201cWhat else could it possibly mean?\u201d he asked, clearly confused.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe first thing she did after she rose into the air was to <i><i>stop</i></i> all the violence,\u201d Kellie Ann reminded him. \u201cShe shouted, and everyone stopped fighting and either fell to the ground or ran away.\u201d<br /> <br /> Stan smiled smugly. \u201cShe shouted \u2018enough!\u2019\u201d he replied. \u201cAnd after that the cars started moving again. See? Enough stagnation. Enough gridlock. Enough of the rigid hierarchies of laws imposed by those who think they\u2019re above the common\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOr enough of this world, perhaps?\u201d Grissom opined. \u201cEnough sin. Enough suffering. Better to call the faithful to their eternal reward in heaven than to allow them to languish in this Hell on Earth.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re dreaming, old man,\u201d Stan said, his voice rising in annoyance. \u201cEnd of the world? That\u2019s science-fiction bullshit. It\u2019s an escapist fantasy propagated by those who\u2019d rather make excuses than do something to improve the world they live in. When I was in the Army\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Kellie Ann raised an eyebrow. \u201c<i><i>You</i></i> were in the Army?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> He shrugged. \u201cFor a little while. Corps of Engineers. Got drummed out for insubordination\u2026 totally trumped-up charge.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cColor me shocked,\u201d Kellie Ann muttered.<br /> <br /> \u201cIn any case,\u201d Grissom said, clearing his throat, \u201cwhatever this visitation might signify, I think we can all agree that we have witnessed something truly special, truly\u2026 unearthly. Yes?\u201d<br /> <br /> Stan nodded. \u201cCan\u2019t argue with that,\u201d he said.<br /> <br /> Kellie Ann agreed. \u201cShe <i><i>healed</i></i> me,\u201d she elaborated. \u201cI was <i>on </i><i><i>fire</i></i> for fifteen or twenty seconds, and look at me now\u2026 a couple of fading shiny spots and some red patches like a bad sunburn. I\u2019m not a doctor, but\u2026 shouldn\u2019t I be lying in a burn ward talking to some specialist about skin grafts right about now?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes!\u201d Grissom said. \u201cYou weren\u2019t the only one, either. The woman with the knives attacked two men in a nearby car, and injured the one brave fellow who tried to stop her. All three should have died from what I saw, but she blessed them with her touch, and their wounds closed.\u201d<br /> <br /> Kellie Ann thought about telling them more\u2026 about how the woman calling herself Sabrina Watson had muttered darkly about how \u2018they\u2019 were after her just before the insanity began. Sabrina had always been odd\u2026 Kellie Ann had never really liked working with her, but somehow she always ended up doing whatever Sabrina told her to anyway. Like two days ago, she had found herself driving Sabrina back to her apartment, where the two of them intended to indulge in a little Ecstasy. Kellie Ann had never done drugs before; she was proud of the fact that she had remained clean since she arrived in L.A\u2026 but Sabrina had made it sound like so much <i><i>fun</i></i><i>\u2026</i><br /> <br /> But just before the flames had erupted within the car, Sabrina had glared out of her window at the redheaded woman with the knives, and had hissed out two words: \u201c<i><i>kill them</i></i><i>.</i>\u201d The woman had spun around, breaking off her attack immediately and turning her attention on the occupants of a nearby BMW. At the time, Kellie Ann had thought the woman was just a random crazy\u2026 but she had seemed so <i><i>intent</i></i> on harming Sabrina prior to that point. And then, as the heat haze rippled and the flames distorted her vision, Kellie Ann had been almost <i>sure</i> that she had seen a pair of <i><i>horns</i></i> poking through Sabrina\u2019s hair\u2026<br /> <br /> The signs seemed clear enough to Kellie Ann\u2026 her current lifestyle was putting her on the road to Hell. The Angel represented a chance at redemption.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo, a sign from God then, whether of the End Times or not,\u201d Grissom said magnanimously, breaking her reverie. \u201cWhat are we to do about it, if we cannot even agree upon what it means?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWish we could ask her,\u201d Stan said after a moment. \u201cIf she\u2019s really divine, she should know what\u2019s best. And we should do whatever we can to help her with whatever mission the Big Guy\u2019s sent her here to accomplish.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe three should continue to meet, if nothing else. We must discuss this further\u2026 and as no one else \u2013 my own dear wife Ethel included \u2013 seems to have retained a clear memory of the incident, I think it is logical to assume that we three have been <i><i>chosen</i></i> for some greater purpose. We should keep our eyes open for further signs\u2026 further appearances of the Angel. If we can find her again, I am certain that all will be made clear.\u201d<br /> <br /> Kellie Ann raised an eyebrow. \u201cOh, I know where we can find her,\u201d she said simply.<br /> <br /> The two men goggled at her. \u201cWhat?\u201d Grissom asked, astounded.<br /> <br /> She pulled a small, weathered piece of paper out of her purse and unfolded it, revealing a printed advertising flier. The woman in the picture was unquestionably the Lost Angel. \u201cYeah, I recognized her as soon as I saw her. She sings and dances at a club out in Malibu\u2026 she\u2019s kind of a local legend. She\u2019s supposed to be <i><i>really</i></i> good. She disappeared for about half a year after she got married, but I hear she\u2019s back now. Goes by the name of Lorelei Grace.\u201d<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Regular update Sunday. See you then. Comments and Questions welcome<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-18T13:59:08-07:00","id":1255333,"title":"","content":"Mwuahahahaha! Cultists!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-18T16:39:12-07:00","id":1255361,"title":"","content":"Very cool story; I really like that PenitentTom gave some input into the consequences of their own actions. Did PenitentTom create the characters, or did they expand upon characters already created?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-18T17:24:18-07:00","id":1255371,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5803_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5803\" data-vbnamecard=\"5803\">Taidragon</a> - The characters themselves were introduced by the Baroness in the session. Kellie Ann was written into the scenario, while I believe Grissom and Stan were results pulled from a &quot;random LA crazies&quot; table. I fleshed them out a bit, named them, and purchased them with experience via the &quot;Devotees&quot; Merit (which I believe is in Equinox Road). I can't wait for them to show up in a session... poor Lori's reaction is likely to be priceless!<br /> <br /> As always, thanks for reading and commenting. It's always nice to have confirmation that people are actually reading our scribblings...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-19T07:22:50-07:00","id":1255480,"title":"","content":"Honestly, reading these entries is the highlight of my day. I always look forward to reading them, and I do so much to inspire my own understanding of the game lines. I can't thank the players, and the baroness, enough for having them here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-19T11:25:15-07:00","id":1255541,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5803_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5803\" data-vbnamecard=\"5803\">Taidragon</a> - Thanks so much for saying that. I can't tell you how much it means to us to get feedback and generate discussion on this forum; how much it means to know that people are reading. It makes it that much easier to put pen to paper (metaphorically) every other Monday and keep writing these entries. It's one thing to look at the Views on this topic tick up... but at the end of the day that's just a number. Hearing people's thoughts and having tangible proof that they've actually read and enjoyed the entries rather than just glancing at the forum is a huge boost to our motivation to keep going with it.<br /> <br /> I know the number of journals per session has diminished and fluctuated over the last year or so. Losing Gawain's player was a blow; they routinely produce great in-character documents for just about every game in which they participate. Calamity's player has had to deal with a recent schedule shift, and IM's player has a lot of creative demands on their time, so those two are no longer as consistent as they used to be with the journals (but hey, Real Life intrudes, and all of us understand that). I myself recently started a new job, and find myself with less time to write than I'd like... but I'm going to try to keep putting these journals out there as long as people want to read them. I've already done the most recent entry; I'm sure the Baroness will post it this Sunday as per usual.<br /> <br /> Many thanks again to Taidragon, Vent0, and everyone else who reads and/or comments on this thread!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T13:59:21-07:00","id":1256792,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to check back with our hero and heroines. Note if you missed it a short story was posted above since the last session.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXVII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Habbibiddy.<br /> <br /> Ahem. So the good news is that I actually <u><u>did</u></u> manage to get another couple of hours of sleep following my last journal entry; nuzzling up to Maria always calms me down and makes me feel at peace (and Julia and Marguerite\u2019s presence didn\u2019t hurt either). The four of us tromped down to Sex Breakfast a few hours later, groggy and fuzzy but generally fairly happy.<br /> <br /> I took up the frying pan this time and made pancakes for most of our little extended family (though Marguerite requested French Toast, and I \u2013 accommodating pushover that I am \u2013 obliged her). I may not be a top quality chef, but I flatter myself that I can flip a flapjack as well as many a short-order cook at least, and things turned out pretty well. Julia made herself an omelet but I think that was mostly so she could spout out \u201comelet du fromage!\u201d a few more times. And no, in case you\u2019re wondering, people <u><u>still</u></u> haven\u2019t explained to me why they think that\u2019s so funny.<br /> <br /> Talk turned to what we were going to do for the day. I had no particular plans myself, but figured something would probably come up if I sat and listened to <u><u>other</u></u> people\u2019s plans for long enough. Marguerite announced that she was going to spend the afternoon rehearsing, as she intended to return to the stage that evening. D had some nebulous plans to spend the afternoon with T.J., but wouldn\u2019t tell me what that was all about (frankly I was afraid to ask). Trinh said that she was going to spend some time apartment hunting\u2026 a daunting task, since she wanted to get a nice place that wasn\u2019t going to rope her into an extended lease since she might be merging with her Fetch soon.<br /> <br /> We talked about that for a little while too\u2026 things are going well between the two of them, and they think they\u2019re almost ready to merge. They just need to work out a few things. As strange as it seems, the vegan thing is really one of the major roadblocks coming between them\u2026 the Fetch wants to exact a promise from Trinh that she won\u2019t \u2018taint\u2019 their shared body by eating meat after they\u2019ve merged. Trinh is reluctant to make that promise, which is keeping the two of them from arriving at the sort of harmonious trusting relationship that makes the merging process possible. I\u2019m sure they\u2019ll work something out eventually; it\u2019s just going to take a little time.<br /> <br /> Calamity initially stated that she was going to do some digging on Luther Henderson, the brave soul who tried to tackle her in the middle of that rush hour fiasco a few days ago. It was eventually suggested that she might want to check out his dreams first, as that would be a good way to ascertain his true character without possibly provoking another fracas. Calamity allowed as how that was a good suggestion, and put her espionage plans on hold for the time being.<br /> <br /> Missy expressed an interest in learning more about working with dreams, and Calamity generously offered to teach her a bit when she was ready. Jane commented softly to me that whenever Missy starts to feel overwhelmed by reality, the two of them have taken to retreating into dreams for a while. That sort of environment is a little more familiar to Missy, and helps to calm her down until she can face the day again. That sounds like a fine idea to me, as long as Missy doesn\u2019t become too dependent on it\u2026 but it doesn\u2019t sound like that\u2019s what\u2019s happening. She just regards dreams as a safe place to fall back to until she can gather her wits.<br /> <br /> So Missy and Jane mentioned that they\u2019d like to spend some time out at the pier, and asked if I\u2019d like to come along. Well that sounded like a fine way to spend a free afternoon, so of course I said yes. Julia had been planning to paint on the roof, but changed her mind when she heard us talking, and asked if she could come along and bring her sketchbook. Well, that pretty much KOed my idea of taking the \u2018vette, but that was okay. When Calamity and Becky decided to join us as well, we opted to take the van anyway.<br /> <br /> And yes, I asked Jacob and Luna if they wanted to come with us, and as usual, was turned down. I know that Luna doesn\u2019t like crowds, and I understand it on an intellectual level\u2026 but it\u2019s so far from my own personality that I have a hard time wrapping my brain around it. I can\u2019t really sympathize with the idea that someone would rather spend their time cooped up in relative isolation when they could be out enjoying a beautiful day with their friends. Add to that the fact that Luna\u2019s seemed a little down recently, and you can understand my concern. I mean, she\u2019s always very reserved compared to the rest of us, but I think something\u2019s been bothering her lately, and I wish she\u2019d talk with me about it. That\u2019s supposed to be my role in this motley, isn\u2019t it? To help support the others emotionally? Well, I guess Luna\u2019s got Jacob for that, but still\u2026<br /> <br /> Nope, not gonna get mopey about that afternoon. I had a wonderful time at the pier, and I think the others did too. Julia quickly clambered up on top of one of the fishing shacks and started sketching the crowds. Becky and Calamity found a relatively quiet corner and quickly got cutesy and lovey-dovey, which was <u><u>adorable</u></u>. I hung out with Missy and Jane, the three of us strutting our stuff and making everyone aware that we were the hottest girls there. And yeah, we got hit on a lot. And yeah, we ate it up.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo,\u201d I told one guy with a grin, \u201c<u><u>those</u></u> two are engaged. I\u2019m married to a <u><u>different</u></u> hot chick. But don\u2019t worry, we\u2019re all very\u2026 open.\u201d Once he\u2019d picked his jaw up off the planks, I blew him a kiss and handed him a Dream House business card. What can I say? There\u2019s no harm in doing a little advertising while I\u2019m having fun, right?<br /> <br /> About an hour into our stay I got a text. When I checked my phone I was surprised to see that it was from Olivia Gold, the Day Court\u2019s ambassador to our Freehold. \u201cI need to speak with you,\u201d the text said, \u201cwhen would be a good time?\u201d I sent back that I was out of the office at the moment but would be back about 4:00, and she acknowledged that she would see me then. So I had to inform the others that our fun afternoon had acquired a deadline, but everyone took the news with good grace.<br /> <br /> Olivia was at the Dream House when we arrived. She said that she wanted to talk to me, but didn\u2019t object to the motley being present. \u201cI know that I\u2019m not a member of the Spring Court,\u201d she began formally, \u201cand I know that you\u2019re not obliged to do anything for me. But I had a good working relationship with Princess Jolie\u2026 she sort of looked out for the affairs of Day Courtiers in the Freehold, and I thought I would see where we stood with this matter.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded thoughtfully. \u201cI\u2019ll help you if I can, Olivia, as long as it doesn\u2019t compromise the well-being of my own courtiers,\u201d I said.<br /> <br /> Olivia sighed. \u201cThank you. Actually, I thought you\u2019d want to hear about this anyway, considering your history. It\u2019s Rowan. Somehow, word has gotten out that she\u2019s involved with a Night Courtier, and\u2026 well, people aren\u2019t taking it well. There\u2019s been some minor vandalism at her house. Nothing too severe so far, but I\u2019m afraid it might escalate.\u201d<br /> <br /> I pursed my lips. \u201cWhat\u2019s been done? And who\u2019s responsible?\u201d<br /> <br /> Olivia shrugged. \u201cNothing has been permanently damaged. There\u2019s been some spray paint, both on her house and her car. As for who\u2026 I don\u2019t know. My first impulse is to say it\u2019s Night Courtiers from L.A., but I\u2019d be lying if I claimed that there aren\u2019t certain members of the Day Court who are capable of this as well.\u201d<br /> <br /> I sighed in turn. \u201cThank you for bringing this to my attention, Olivia. Rowan and Neon are both friends, and neither one of them deserves to be treated this way. I\u2019ll think it over and do what I can to help them.\u201d<br /> <br /> Olivia nodded and thanked me. \u201cOne more thing,\u201d she said before she left. \u201cI know you\u2019re close to her, but I hope you\u2019ll consider the likelihood that Insincere Marguerite is the one who spread the news that the two of them were involved.\u201d<br /> <br /> D surged forward at that, but I caught her shoulder in a gentle but firm grip. \u201cI doubt that very much,\u201d I said rather coldly. \u201cShe\u2019s on friendly terms with both of them, and I doubt she\u2019d want to see them hurt or bothered in this way. But I\u2019ll certainly bring this matter to her attention.\u201d<br /> <br /> After Olivia had vacated the premises, I waited for a break in Marguerite\u2019s rehearsal and gave her the news. As I expected, she was as surprised and chagrinned by the situation as I had been. She offered her opinion that the vandals were most likely Night Courtiers, and were probably not acting at the behest of their monarch. \u201cThey see it as the betrayal,\u201d she explained, elaborating on the antipathy between the Day and Night courts, \u201cand they are afraid to lash out at Neon. She is a member of the Unseelie Court motley, and they are all afraid of Corvus and Corbin. Particularly Corbin. Rowan is meek; she is an easier target.\u201d<br /> <br /> I sighed. \u201cI should probably talk with Rowan and Neon tonight,\u201d I said. \u201cI\u2019ll give Neon a call and see if they can drop by the show this evening.\u201d<br /> <br /> D pulled me aside for a moment. \u201cI got an idea, babe,\u201d she said quietly. \u201cSee, I can probably convince T.J. to stake out Rowan\u2019s place and keep an eye out for these vandals. He\u2019d be <u><u>happy</u></u> to do it. He can knock a few heads, maybe break a few bones, and make sure they know not to pull that shit in our Freehold again.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cI\u2019ll consider it,\u201d I said after a moment. \u201cBut if we go ahead with that plan, I don\u2019t want anybody killed\u2026 or even too badly hurt. The last thing I want to do is provoke a conflict with our allies in L.A.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cT.J. knows when to pull his punches. He can make someone <u><u>wish</u></u> they were dead without getting close to actually killing them.\u201d<br /> <br /> So I had that to think about. I actually called Brightstar first to see what she knew about the situation. She was happy to hear from me as always, of course, and had gleaned quite a lot from Neon. Her roommate was at work when I called, but Brightstar was sure she\u2019d be happy to hear from me, and would be happy to drop by the club that evening if it was possible. Brightstar herself is going to stop by tonight, so I\u2019ve got that to look forward to.<br /> <br /> I called Neon next. I told her what I\u2019d found out about their situation and asked if the two of them could drop by the club that night. She tentatively agreed, stating that she\u2019d text me or something if their plans changed. I also warned her that T.J. might be hanging around Rowan\u2019s place that evening as a sort of deterrent, and asked her to let Rowan know so that she wouldn\u2019t get too freaked out by his presence. The last time he was hanging out around her house uninvited he nearly scared the daylights out of her.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I gave D the go-ahead to put T.J. on the job. I\u2019m hoping that by setting an example with the vandals, we\u2019ll send the message that messing with Rowan is just as dangerous as messing with Neon (though I doubt T.J. will take a bite out of anyone\u2019s face\u2026 yeah, Neon gave me a few more details about the Corbin anecdote). Hopefully he\u2019ll send a few of the scumbags running back to L.A. scared shitless and maybe a little battered, and that\u2019ll convince the rest of them that fucking with members of my Freehold is a bad idea.<br /> <br /> Jesus, would you listen to me? What the hell is happening to me lately? Is it simply the fact that I\u2019m now responsible for the well-being of others that\u2019s causing me to make these violent decisions? Or is it the old adage about power corrupting already at work? I mean, I don\u2019t <u><u>want</u></u> to hurt these people\u2026 do I? I just want them to stop screwing with my friends and constituents. But\u2026 if this situation escalates, someone could get <u><u>really</u></u> hurt; maybe even <u><u>killed</u></u>. I can\u2019t allow that. I have to nip this in the bud, and that means I can\u2019t afford to use soft options. I have to act decisively.<br /> <br /> Maybe I should have asked the other monarchs for their advice before making this decision\u2026 but I can\u2019t just go running to John every time a crisis comes my way. I\u2019ll never earn the Freehold\u2019s respect that way. No, in the long run I think it\u2019s better to act on my own and make a mistake than to let myself be led by the other monarchs. But Jesus\u2026 I just asked an angry pig-ogre to break bones for me. Not my finest hour.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the show must go on, and last night was no exception. I\u2019d spoken with Missy and Jane several times about performing for us, and they both seem to like the idea\u2026 though there are certain caveats. They\u2019re happy to back me up on the stage for now, but neither is comfortable performing solo for the audience yet\u2026 it\u2019s too close to what the Empress required of us back in Arcadia. I completely understand that, and I\u2019m more than willing to let them adjust to the idea at their own paces.<br /> <br /> The three of us got up on stage together during the early part of the show for a little a capella vocal harmony with an old favorite. \u201cAfternoon Delight\u201d by Starland Vocal Band is a lot of fun to sing with those two, and the three of us used to spontaneously launch into it all the time back when we were in high school. It was sort of a vicarious thrill\u2026 the lyrics are very sexually suggestive, but the tune is so jaunty and innocent sounding that a lot of people don\u2019t catch the meaning behind the words at first.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t mention it to Missy and Jane. Maybe they\u2019ve forgotten about it. Maybe they\u2019re getting over their trauma. Who knows? But that was the song the three of us were singing just before we were Taken. That was the song that drew the Stranger\u2019s attention to us. You\u2019d never know it to look at the two of them, though\u2026 they were obviously having a lot of fun with me out there. Maybe the happy memories of our high school days overpowered the song\u2019s negative connotations.<br /> <br /> I did the queen thing for a while and wandered the crowd talking with people and making myself available to hear their opinions and complaints. For a wonder, most people seemed to just be there to enjoy the show, and I only had to \u201cdon the crown\u201d for a couple of guests.<br /> <br /> First on that list, obviously, were Rowan and Neon. They both thanked me for doing what I can to help them even though they\u2019re not courtiers, though Rowan expressed chagrin over the fact that Olivia had gotten me involved in her troubles at all; she\u2019d hoped to spare me that stress.<br /> <br /> \u201cSweetie,\u201d I said seriously, taking her hand, \u201cyou may not be a member of my Court, but you are and always will be a dear friend. <u><u>Both</u></u> of you are. Part of the reason I took up the Crown was to serve the people of this Freehold, so I\u2019m glad Olivia came to me when she did. If I can fulfill my duties as a monarch and help a friend at the same time, then I\u2019m happy to do what I can.\u201d<br /> <br /> The three of us chatted for a bit after that, and I got a few more details about their situation\u2026 most of which seem inconsequential now. Rowan was quick to tell me that nobody had actually hurt or threatened her, they were just defacing her property. Neon reiterated with a sigh that the culprits were probably Night Courtiers from L.A. who disapproved of their relationship.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe conflict between Day and Night is usually a good thing,\u201d she said as the conversation moved on. \u201cThe rapidly shifting leadership and attitudes of the courts make it almost impossible for the Gentry to understand us. They can\u2019t plan an effective strategy to take us down because a plan that works against one Court almost certainly won\u2019t against the other one, and the balance of power goes back and forth so quickly. So it pays for us to be opposed\u2026 it\u2019s just irritating when it targets someone I care about.\u201d<br /> <br /> I suppose that makes sense, though it seems to me that the Seasonal Court model of government works well enough with far less problems. But it didn\u2019t seem politic to state it that baldly.<br /> <br /> Before moving on, I mentioned that Brightstar would be spending the following evening with me, and suggested \u2013 on T.J.\u2019s recommendation, actually \u2013 that Rowan might want to stay with Neon that night. That way, any retaliation the Night Court might plan against T.J.\u2019s vigilante activities wouldn\u2019t land on their heads. They agreed that this was a good plan and decided to go with it.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d noticed one guest sitting by himself in a shadowy corner\u2026 a corner that wasn\u2019t usually shadowy, in fact. It\u2019s been a long time since we\u2019ve seen Vic Twilight in our little cabaret, and knowing what I do about his recent activities, I thought it would be best to welcome him back personally.<br /> <br /> \u201cYour Majesty,\u201d he said softly as I pulled up a chair and sat beside him.<br /> <br /> \u201cMr. Twilight,\u201d I acknowledged.<br /> <br /> \u201cJust thought I\u2019d stop by and pay my respects,\u201d he said politely.<br /> <br /> \u201cI appreciate that,\u201d I said, flashing him a grin. \u201cAnd I\u2019d just like to say, knowing what I now know, that I appreciate all of your efforts on behalf of the Freehold. I know you\u2019re putting yourself at great risk on a daily basis to make sure that the rest of us remain safe\u2026 and you\u2019re doing it without much in the way of recognition.\u201d<br /> <br /> He flashed me a toothy smile. \u201cJust doing my job, ma\u2019am,\u201d he said. \u201cYou got any special requests the next time I go out?\u201d<br /> <br /> I shook my head. \u201cI trust that you know your business far better than I ever could Mr. Twilight,\u201d I replied. \u201cIf that changes, though, I\u2019ll make sure to let you know. So how are things going on that front?\u201d<br /> <br /> He shrugged. \u201cNot much to report. Only thing I\u2019ve noticed is that there\u2019s a new party drug on the street. Not sure what it is, but when a mortal takes it, they become like a fountain of glamour for a few hours, then completely dry up for a few days.\u201d<br /> <br /> Interesting. Is it possible that the Hollywood Courts are trying to counteract the effects of Gunnar Friday\u2019s starvation tactics? Or maybe they want to distribute this drug in a particular location to create a beacon of glamour\u2026 something they could use to lure the Grand Maw where they want it to go after they unleash it. Neither is a particularly comforting possibility.<br /> <br /> \u201cFriends of yours?\u201d Vic asked after a moment, indicating Missy and Jane with a nod of his head.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah,\u201d I said. \u201cYou might recall that my motley went back into Arcadia last year. They\u2019re the reason why. We brought them back with us.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI see,\u201d he said. And then, after a somewhat awkward pause, \u201cmay not be my place to say this but\u2026 you be good to Oleander, okay? That lady is one of the only people in the Freehold I feel like I can talk to, and she\u2019s been so happy since the two of you got together\u2026 she deserves something like that. She was terrified the whole time you were gone. I never seen her like that before.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know,\u201d I said. \u201cI felt horrible putting her through that. And I promise that I <u><u>will</u></u> be good to her. You\u2019re right\u2026 she\u2019s special, and she deserves the best I can give her.\u201d <br /> <br /> I caught Jacob\u2019s attention at the bar and gave him a pre-arranged hand signal. He nodded, and I turned back to Vic. \u201cYour next drink is on me, Mr. Twilight,\u201d I said. \u201cThank you again for your service, and please come back any time.\u201d<br /> <br /> Though I hobnobbed a bit more, I found myself gravitating toward the girlfriend table, where D and Gloria were making a spectacle of themselves. They were apparently in a somewhat giggly and playful mood, and each was attempting to drop an ice cube down the shirt of the other. It was amusing to watch, but was perhaps not the most dignified way they could have comported themselves in our place of business (and the current seat of the Spring Court).<br /> <br /> I had considered trying to rope D into bed with me, Missy and Jane last night\u2026 it\u2019s something I really want to do at some point, and everyone seems open to the possibility. But looking at the two of them, I could tell that D and Gloria were planning to be together (with or without me), and I just couldn\u2019t bring myself to sabotage their evening. Plus, dammit, I wanted in on that action.<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay,\u201d I said once I\u2019d finally managed to get their attention. \u201cHere\u2019s what we\u2019re going to do, ladies. I\u2019ll make a wager with you. If I win, you two have to act your age and conduct yourselves like grown women for the rest of the evening.\u201d<br /> <br /> D nodded suspiciously. \u201cAnd if I win?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> I shrugged. \u201cI\u2019ll do anything the two of you want for the rest of the night. <u><u>Anything</u></u>,\u201d I reiterated unnecessarily.<br /> <br /> D\u2019s eyes lit up. \u201cOkay, I\u2019m in.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMe too,\u201d Gloria piped up.<br /> <br /> I put my elbow on the table and extended my hand in the classic arm wrestling pose. \u201cLet\u2019s rock,\u201d I said with a twinkle and a wry grin.<br /> <br /> Of course, my wife can casually pick up and toss a Pontiac, so the result of our contest was a foregone conclusion\u2026 as I\u2019d intended all along. Those two ladies are\u2026 very strong. I mean, I\u2019ve known that D is a powerhouse for years, and I knew intellectually that Gloria\u2019s Summer Court contracts make her stronger than she appears, but\u2026 wow. They put me through my paces last night, and I couldn\u2019t be happier.<br /> <br /> The usual suspects went to therapy this morning, so Gloria and I were alone in the bed when she started gently shaking me to let me know that breakfast was ready. I think I responded to her hungry entreaties with something witty like \u201cnuh-uh. Legs don\u2019t work no more.\u201d She rolled her eyes in mock exasperation, called me a big baby, made me put on a long shirt, and then carried me downstairs while I leaned into her shoulder in a stupor.<br /> <br /> D got a text while we were eating and started chuckling. Apparently T.J. had met with some success while staking out Rowan\u2019s home. A couple of guys pulled up and prepared to continue their campaign of vandalism. T.J. punched the hood of their car, driving his fist into the engine block and effectively scrapping the vehicle. He then told the two perpetrators to decide which of them would live and which would die. He didn\u2019t actually harm either of them as far as I know; they ran away and he didn\u2019t bother to chase them. He continued to watch the house for the rest of the night in case they came back for a little retribution. He doesn\u2019t think that\u2019s likely, but wants to be thorough just in case. He did ask that someone spell him in that duty for an hour or two so that he could take care of a few necessities. D and Calamity opted to take care of that duty.<br /> <br /> So here I sit, glad that the Rowan situation seems to have been resolved so quickly and painlessly, and looking forward to another energetic evening with my lover from L.A. And in the back of my mind, with every day that passes, I become just a little bit more terrified of the fact that I\u2019ll be attending college classes starting next week.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei de la Rocha</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Today was the day for questions that I don\u2019t have the answers to, but that will come later. The day started like usual with Calamity going to train with White Maria early this morning while the rest of us slept. When we did get up we made breakfast like usual. Lori cooked pancakes for everyone except Insincere Marguerite. She made French toast for her. I made coffee like usual. The conversation is what made breakfast interesting. I suppose it always does, but today we touched on some topics that we don\u2019t usually visit. Someone asked Marguerite why she doesn\u2019t sleep in a bed very often, and why she sleeps in the vents when she doesn\u2019t. Insincere Marguerite replied that after having had a concrete slab dropped on her chest and her apartment set on fire while she slept she\u2019s entitled to be a little wary about sleeping somewhere so vulnerable as a bed. I think the rest of us had to concede that. It would be a shitty way to wake up. <br /> <br /> After we ate we talked about what we were going to do for the day. Insincere Marguerite said that she was going to spend the afternoon rehearsing since she hasn\u2019t performed in a few days. Trinh said that she was going to look for apartments online. She wanted to find a place that wouldn\u2019t lock her into a long term lease. The others ended up deciding on going to the Pier to hang out. Lori asked if Luna and I would like to join them but we declined. Luna is not a big fan of crowds so she tends to not like the pier so much. I can respect that. I am not great with crowds either. The Lady\u2019s realm was not the most crowded place so I only ever had to deal with a handful of people at a time. Even in Her court there were only ever a few people. Most of her subjects were just plain terrified of her. The rest of us were wary of course, but I didn\u2019t truly fear her until after I betrayed her. That was the first time that her anger was truly focused on me.<br /> <br /> Before everyone left though there were a couple other things brought up. Calamity said that she was interested in checking out that guy that attacked her during the highway incident. He seemed a pretty selfless type, putting himself in danger like that to stop Calamity when she couldn\u2019t stop herself. The rest of us talked her into checking on him in his dream before actually meeting him in person. She took his driver\u2019s license the other day when he was unconscious so she has his picture. She can go into his dreams any time. After some consideration she agreed. <br /> <br /> Trinh also had some news. Apparently she and her fetch are close to an understanding that will allow them to merge into one person soon. They just need to work out a couple of details. Like whether or not the merged them would eat meat or not. Her fetch wanted her to promise that she wouldn\u2019t eat any meat at all after they merged, but Trinh was a little hesitant to make that promise. Things like that tend to be binding for us, so it would be a big deal if she promised not to eat meat and then went back on that later. I guess we\u2019ll see how they get that worked out in time. <br /> <br /> After everyone left Luna confided in me that she had thought about merging with her fetch, but there are obvious problems. One of the biggest among them is the fact that if they merge they will be in Luna\u2019s body, which doesn\u2019t look anything like her fetch\u2019s body. He is a \u201che\u201d for one thing. And he would be missed. He has a life. He has a career as a stand-up comedian. Not to mention his mother would miss him. And Luna can\u2019t really get involved in his life as a friend. She might slip up and call their mother \u201cmom\u201d by accident. Plus he tends to get fixated on Luna, which might cause problems. Especially if he doesn\u2019t know what their true relationship is. After our serious chat we just sat down to watch some Netflix. It was a light, fun afternoon.<br /> <br /> Later in the afternoon, around 4:00pm Lori and the others got back from the Pier and met Olivia Gold, who showed up right before they did. It seems that someone has taken an issue with Rowan and Neon dating and has decided to vandalize the selkie\u2019s house and car letting their displeasure be known. Olivia had an understanding with Jolie about Day Court issues and thought that Lori might take up where her predecessor left off. Olivia thought that it might be Night courtiers from L.A but didn\u2019t rule out the possibility that it could be Day courtiers doing it. After Olivia left Lori talked to Marguerite about the issue and she agreed that it was probably Night courtiers that did the vandalizing. After that Lori called both Neon and Rowan to see if they could come by the club tonight and talk about the situation. She also asked De la Rocha to talk to T.J. about defending Rowan\u2019s house tonight to prevent anyone else from doing any damage to her house, however minor. <br /> <br /> The show is where all the conversations happened and where the long time absentees showed up. We haven\u2019t seen Vik in a long time, not since he was sent to Hollywood to deal with problems there. But he was at the show tonight. Lori went over to talk to him. At one point during the conversation she made a signal to me that his next drink should be on the house. I acknowledged that and made sure that we had the spirits that he likes. Lori also talked to Neon and Rowan about what has been going on lately. I\u2019m assuming that she let Rowan know about T.J.\u2019s presence at her house and what he was doing there. It would be remiss of Lori to leave that bit off. I\u2019m not sure what else was talked about, but I\u2019m assuming they got all the details worked out.<br /> <br /> Calamity made her rounds as well. She stopped by to talk to Jolie and Desiree who were sitting together. Again, I\u2019m not sure what was said, but Desiree at least seemed to be in a better mood than before Calamity arrived. Perhaps she got to purge some negative emotions on her friendly sounding board. Again, I don\u2019t know. It wasn\u2019t really my business so I didn\u2019t ask.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, at that bar Luna was commiserating with me that she was feeling jealous of Trinh and her fetch and their ability to make peace and merge. Or at least that\u2019s what they\u2019re planning on doing once they work out the whole meat thing. Luna was just upset because her situation is so much more difficult than theirs. I tried commiserating with her. I did admit that one thing that bothered me about my fetch being in existence was that there was no way that I could go back to being my parents\u2019 son. One, I look too old, and two I don\u2019t know if I\u2019m even recognizable as him anymore. Could I pass myself off as Jacob Mikalev anymore? The same worries were voiced and I reiterated that it would be a bad idea to start off any relationship with lies. I know, pot meet kettle, but it\u2019s true. I got lucky that things turned out okay for me. I don\u2019t deserve the friends that I have and I don\u2019t really deserve their forgiveness for lying to them for so long. We did kind of hastily enter a contract with one another to become a motley, but since then I lied to them for a while before my past as Rime finally came out. I got lucky, but things done usually work out so well. I don\u2019t want to see my Luna ruin a chance at a relationship before we can figure out how to make it happen with her fetch. I may need to see if Luna would be okay talking with maybe Lori and Calamity about this. Lori is good with people and Calamity is Luna\u2019s closest friend besides me. Maybe they can help?<br /> <br /> **** **** **** <br /> <br /> Okay, so this morning was kind of interesting. We had breakfast like usual. This time though we had steak and eggs. I think that\u2019s one of my favorite things to have for breakfast. When I lived in the Lady\u2019s realm I ate a lot of meat. It was one of the main staples. One just had to go hunting and hope that the Lady was being generous with the game that day. So, steak and eggs reminds me of the good times I had in Arcadia. Rook and I cooking over an open fire in the woods. Chasing our quarry afterwards. It was a simpler time. Less political bullshit going on. If someone did something that the Lady did not approve of then they were punished and let go or killed depending on the severity of their crimes. <br /> <br /> Anyway, we went to therapy and all was good. I didn\u2019t have anything really interesting to talk to Sullivan about. I mentioned that friends of mine were having trouble being accepted as a couple and what we were trying to do to help them. Sullivan wanted to kind of run with that but I\u2019m not having any problems being accepted in my relationship with Luna or anyone else for that matter. Overall it was a kind of boring session.<br /> <br /> When we got back is when the interesting stuff happened. Lori got a text from De la Rocha with a request from T.J. He wanted a quick break to grab some food so Calamity and Becky headed over to spell him. Meanwhile T.J. shared some of what happened last night with De la Rocha who shared it with Lori. Apparently a couple of people showed up and were getting ready to vandalize something when T.J. stepped out and messed up their car really badly. I think something was said about punching through the engine block? Cool or scary? Maybe both. Anyway, that stopped them in their tracks and then T.J. threatened bodily harm on the two shmucks who decided that it was better to just run away, and he let them. He wasn\u2019t really going to hurt them, but they didn\u2019t know that. Overall it seemed to work rather well. Hopefully those that are doing this to Rowan won\u2019t decide to escalate things. It is one possible way for them to respond. They might also learn their lesson and leave Rowan and Neon alone, but something tells me that it will take more than one scare for that to happen. And to be honest they are only really targeting Rowan. Neon is part of the Unseelie Court motley, which is pretty well feared. Most people are really wary of Corbin and to a lesser but still not an insignificant degree, Corvus. So they go after the one with seemingly no support structure. How wrong they are. If this motley will take on a possessed house to save Rowan, we\u2019ll confront a few vandals, no problem. <br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXVII</i><br /> <br /> Okay what needs to be added\u2026Calamity did visit Luther\u2019s dream, and glean information, though she did not reveal herself. Poor girl also found herself running into depressing conversations that night, one after the other. I think she wound up doing Poe\u2019s \u201cAngry Johnny\u201d while Insincere Marguerite did Fiona Apple\u2019s \u201cCriminal\u201d. There was a lot of chatter about Fetches this time.<br /> <br /> I think that covers it, but Comments and Questions are welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-25T01:46:00-07:00","id":1257126,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s interesting what being in a seat of power will do to people. Like many responsible people, Lori is having to compromise on her morals to protect people quickly, quietly and efficiently, though fortunately here she doesn\u2019t need to sanction anything more than a scare. I like that while she is deliberating on what can be done, she isn\u2019t hesitating or quibbling on it either - Lori is trying to stand on her own decisions, even if mistakes are made, and taking what her motley offers her as candid. It\u2019s a good sign Lori isn\u2019t letting the power get to her head, as is the fact that she\u2019s self evaluating to make sure that isn\u2019t the case. Also, I loved that subtle touch of Lori pacifying D with a touch to the shoulder; it speaks volumes of both the respect between them and their character, and is another good sign Lori\u2019s stability regarding her political position.<br /> <br /> This is something of a thought I\u2019ve been running over for a while, but I get the feeling that Jane would fit in pretty well in the Summer court. Less as a combatant, mind, but given how she was rather adamant about dealing with Trinh at the start, and how she wasn\u2019t all that surprised about how her Fetch acted out, it\u2019s clear she\u2019s got a firebrand in her. If she figured how to instill that into others...suffice to say she could be a very dangerous bird. Then again, that is just one aspect of herself, and a darker one she hasn\u2019t shown much in the way of diving into as of late. Missy has given me some twinges towards the Winter court, but that\u2019s mostly due to how she has displayed dismay over being out of Arcadia. It\u2019s hard to tell where either of them may go if they join the Freehold (if they haven\u2019t already made oaths in any case). <br /> <br /> Calamity\u2019s delving into Luther is an interesting turn for her. Granted, I don\u2019t believe she has anything bad planned for the guy, but I can\u2019t help but feel that this is more than idle curiosity about a selfless person. I wonder what will come after having gleaned some of his character. It\u2019s cool that she\u2019s becoming a mentor figure in her own right to Missy, given she didn\u2019t have any formal training for her own dream prowess.<br /> <br /> Jacob and Luna\u2019s relationship is lovely to keep reading on, especially with how open they are with one another. Well, \u201copen\u201d may not be the right term, but they are a quiet, incredibly stable couple who appreciate each others\u2019 faults and virtues, talk about their problems and simply enjoy spending time with one another. It\u2019s great seeing Luna open up about her desire to merge with her Fetch, even with the sizeable differences between their respective lives, and Jacob not questioning it whatsoever. I look forward to seeing how it resolves. I doubt that Sullivan is going to be getting quite as candid a discussion in the future though.<br /> <br /> And as for Insincere Marguerite, I always thought that the vents was more from her cat theming than anything relating to her encounters with the Day court. Cats enjoy enclosed spaces for safety, and for warmth as well, and it only fits for a master thief to slip through the air ducts to get to what she wants. Still, that makes rather a large amount of sense in hindsight...<br /> <br /> Sorry if that\u2019s a bit rambly; as always, loved this instalment of the journals, and I can\u2019t wait to see what comes in the future. Thanks for the hard work guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 09-27-2018, 07:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-27T13:23:57-07:00","id":1257637,"title":"","content":"Yeah Maria is scrapper, and tends to jump in when any of her girls are threatened. Lori is doing a good job, I think. Missy is currently leaning Spring, while Jane is somewhere between Spring and Summer, and Trinh is leaning Autumn, but none of that are set in stone. Missy is not so much hiding from the fae as desperately seeking the familiar. She is so used to Arcadia, and even on earth Southern California in the 2010s is not much like Iowa in the 1970s. Everything has changed, and even good changes can be scary when reality seems arbitrary and quicksilver. Only Lori and Jane seem static, and she is clinging desperately to them, and freaks out if not in the presence of either for very long. Without those pillars from her old life she would have joined the ranks of the Mad within days. In the end she (and her sanity) are struggling the most, and Jane is just trying to be stable, brave and okay for her...and to some degree she is faking it till she makes it, but that is fragile, and if it falls apart it will fall apart hard. Lori is wise to not let them off on their own yet.<br /> <br /> Calamity seems to want, even need, some good in the world to fight her cynicism. That is my read anyway.<br /> <br /> Yeah I enjoy Jacob/Luna (Jana?). Luna is definitely the still waters run deep sort of NPC. She is quiet, and humans just confuse her. Her struggle with wanting her old place and old life but to keep new is interesting as a GM in her head. Jacob and Calamity are humanizing Luna more, who was a lot more feral when she began interacting with the PCs. She speaks in long sentences like anyone else, and while not comfortable with civilization she is not a watching predator as much as reluctant participant. Not that the predator is not there.<br /> <br /> It's a bit of both. Insincere Marguerite is not a Beast or Fairest, but has some inclinations both ways (She has Fang and Talon 5 on the Beast side, and Reflections 5 Vainglory 2 Separation 1 on the Fairest) and she has a lot of feline mannerisms, from her tendency to sit on furniture or high places like the catwalks to hiding in small spaces like the vents. Her paranoia is a factor too, but she likes to hide in the vents even when not sleeping, and just watch or listen to others from her hiding place. It is very cat like.<br /> <br /> Rambly is fine we enjoy feedback. Sorry about the delay in replying been crazy this week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-29T14:39:06-07:00","id":1258040,"title":"","content":"Huh. Did not expect Lori to get cultists before Marguerite. Ten bucks says the rapture one tries to exorcise her when he sees her act. Another ten says Mr. Seize the Means of Production (unless he's actually a right-leaning revolutionary, I couldn't tell) thinks Marguerite is some sort of corrupting demon and tries and hilariously fails to beat her back to hell to save the angel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-01T08:16:10-07:00","id":1258392,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7920_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7920\" data-vbnamecard=\"7920\">Master Aquatosic</a>: IM's player and I had both previously considered the &quot;Devotees&quot; Merit, at the point when our Wyrd made purchasing it possible. I can definitely see what you mean, what with IM's entitlement marking her as a sort of &quot;goddess&quot; and such. And honestly, I probably wouldn't have dropped the experience on the Merit if the circumstances hadn't been so very perfect... such a rich array of randomly-generated crazies (each pre-built with a ready-made Derangement) dropping in her lap at a time when Lori found herself revealing her &quot;angelic&quot; Fae nature in such a flagrant way. It wasn't really planned, but it was too good an opportunity to pass up.<br /> <br /> I don't know what the Baroness has in mind for Grissom, Stan, and poor Kellie Ann... I'm as curious as the rest of you to find out. &quot;Seize the Means of Production&quot; is a fair assessment of Stan; though he might rankle at being called a Marxist. He thinks of himself as more of a radical Anarchist. His philosophy runs along the lines of &quot;good men should have the right to govern themselves so that unscrupulous men in power can't exploit them.&quot; I'm honestly not sure what Lori will make of Stan and Grissom; some of it is going to depend on the circumstances of their introduction. Kellie Ann, however, is <i>definitely</i> her type... pretty, perky, blonde, and with the sort of delicious naivete that tends to attract Lori's interest. I don't see that ending well...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-01T12:08:50-07:00","id":1258420,"title":"","content":"Hooking up with someone who sees her as a higher being of perfection and good? It has been a long time since I've felt so conflicted in my reaction to a story. Here's a summary of my feelings<br /> <br /> Oh god no/ALL THE HELLS YES/but jesus christ this will get heavy/I need so much more popcorn<br /> <br /> If Lori wasn't already so understanding of Marguerite's problematic relationships, this would probably be the point in the story where she would start to sympathize.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-07T13:35:54-07:00","id":1259455,"title":"","content":"Lorelei (who focuses on Presence) is more the Charismatic leader, while Insincere Marguerite (who focuses on Manipulation) is almost more a femme fatale, though both are competant at the other attribute, and Lori has higher Presence than Marguerite has Manipulation, 7 vs 5. Lorelei shines bright while Marguerite smiles from the shadows. Its easier for Lorelei to gain followers, essentially. And yeah, she is sympathetic just not always approving.<br /> <br /> As conflict erupts again outside Rowan\u2019s house, Lori second guesses her decisions (and defends Camptown Races, but she does not second guess that). Calamity goes to find Luther. Jacob helps his sister with her struggles with family and Luna with her internal struggles, and Insincere Marguerite argues with her former Monarch.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXVIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Another day, another shit-storm I never could have anticipated.<br /> <br /> Okay, maybe that\u2019s not entirely fair. I was actually <u><u>worried</u></u> that something like this might happen, now that I think about it\u2026 but, well, the response seems extreme to me.<br /> <br /> This doesn\u2019t make any sense. I should start over.<br /> <br /> Okay, so yesterday started off as kind of a lazy day. Most of us didn\u2019t really have any specific plans beyond lounging around and doing a little light prep for the Thursday night show. I somehow got embroiled in a\u2026 \u201cconversation\u201d with Julia and Maria regarding the racial insensitivity of certain songs. D opined, for example, that it would be impossible for a white person to sing \u201cCamptown Races\u201d without being racist. I sort of bristled at that, and Julia came down somewhere in the middle. Somehow Al Jolson\u2019s infamous black-face routine in <u><u>The Jazz Singer</u></u> got dragged into the conversation as well, with Julia bringing up the fact that Jolson was actually a great supporter of black music, and that he performed in blackface as an attempt to give such music broader exposure (it was only in later years that blackface performances came to be viewed as intrinsically racist).<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t like being told I can\u2019t sing certain songs just because I\u2019m white,\u201d I said, working to keep my voice even. \u201cJust because a piece of music has a certain historical or cultural context, that doesn\u2019t mean that me singing it makes me a racist.\u201d D sort of conceded the point without actually backing down from her stance. Missy and Jane looked on from a safe distance. They\u2019ve learned not to provoke Maria on this sort of an issue.<br /> <br /> Eventually \u2013 somewhat to my surprise \u2013 the three of us actually reached something of an accord on the subject. I asked D if she would think it was a racist act if I started singing \u201cLa Cucaracha\u201d in her presence, as that traditional Spanish jingle has become something of a stereotype in regards to those of Mexican descent. D thought about it, and eventually replied that while it wouldn\u2019t make me a racist, it could be regarded as culturally insensitive, as it might indicate that the performer \u2013 as an outside observer of the culture in question \u2013 thought her audience could be reduced to a clich\u00e9. I took her point, and we closed the discussion amiably.<br /> <br /> While this was going on, Calamity and Becky were out investigating Luther Henderson. I think Calamity\u2019s sort of fixated on him since the L.A. rush hour incident. I\u2019m not sure if that\u2019s entirely healthy, but at least her interest seems to be benevolent rather than violent this time. In any case, they found out that Mr. Henderson lives in a primarily Chinese neighborhood which is threatened but not directly controlled by a Vietnamese organized crime syndicate. Mr. Henderson has made himself something of a nuisance to them\u2026 enough to keep the criminals away from his apartment complex, but not enough for them to attempt any sort of permanent solution.<br /> <br /> Calamity wants to help Mr. Henderson. I think that\u2019s admirable, but I question whether our interference is going to make things better or worse\u2026 <u><u>especially</u></u> in light of what happened later that night, actually. Antagonizing these criminals on his behalf might invite the sort of retribution he\u2019s managed to avoid so far, and that\u2019s the last thing we want. Add to that the fact that he lives in L.A., which is <u><u>way</u></u> outside of our jurisdiction. On the other hand, Calamity is very good at scare tactics, and she\u2019s used them on organized crime figures effectively in the past. So maybe I should just trust her and see where this goes. I confess, it\u2019s nice to see her employing her talents on the side of the angels (so to speak) this time.<br /> <br /> So not long after Calamity and Becky returned it was time to start prepping for the show. I made a few arrangements with Marguerite to swap out my number for something a little more unorthodox\u2026 mostly because I wanted to see if I could pull it off. They Might Be Giants is a band that\u2026 defies classification. They often seem to be a comedy band, but on other albums or in other songs they can get quite dark and serious. They\u2019ve done kids\u2019 music, but they\u2019ve also done avant-garde adult fare.<br /> <br /> I chose a number from their 1990 album <u><u>Flood</u></u> called \u201cBirdhouse In Your Soul.\u201d Despite the name of the song, it\u2019s not really about birds or birdhouses or anything like that\u2026 the whole thing is more of an extended metaphor for light and electricity. So I began the number with all the house lights down and a single spot shining tightly right on my face. Once the metaphor became obvious, I pressed a cleverly concealed button and the act\u2019s trick came into play. See, I\u2019d borrowed an outfit from Calamity and Jack\u2019s \u201cHigh Voltage\u201d duet number, and activating the outfit caused\u2026 \u201ccertain areas\u201d of the skimpy dress to light up in electric blue. Yeah, it was a little gimmicky, but it got a good reaction from the crowd (especially from Gloria and Maria, for some reason).<br /> <br /> I made my way around the crowd for a bit after my number. A few of my courtiers were in attendance, but nobody seemed to need anything in particular from me, so I just greeted them all pleasantly and moved on. White Maria \u2013 goaded here and there by Calamity and Becky \u2013 was hurling insults at pretty much every member of the Freehold, so I made certain not to linger at that table. I know she doesn\u2019t <u><u>really</u></u> mean the horrible things she says\u2026 but I still don\u2019t particularly enjoy hearing them.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d noticed that Elena was present, propping up the bar and talking primarily to Jacob, but Stasia was nowhere to be found. That sent up a little red flag in my head, and I made my way over to see what was up. It turns out that things weren\u2019t as dire as I\u2019d feared, though there was still a bit of drama to sort through. Stasia had gone out for an all-day photo shoot, leaving Elena to fend for herself until she returned. Unfortunately (or maybe fortunately) this was the day that Elena\u2019s mother chose to call.<br /> <br /> It was the first time she\u2019d reached out since that disastrous Thanksgiving dinner. She obviously misses her daughter and wants to be involved in her life\u2026 but she still doesn\u2019t want to <u><u>admit</u></u> that Elena\u2019s life is what it is. Every time Elena tried to talk about Stasia, her mother just ignored her and acted as if she hadn\u2019t spoken at all, carrying on with whatever she\u2019d said before. I don\u2019t know if she\u2019s actually in denial about her daughter\u2019s choice of lifestyle or if she\u2019s just coping with it the only way she knows how, but it\u2019s not healthy, and it\u2019s not going to work out for her in the long run.<br /> <br /> Elena looked at me as she was saying this, and then said \u201cJacob suggested that Reverend Wells might be able to\u2026 I don\u2019t know, talk to my parents or something.\u201d<br /> <br /> I\u2019m sure my eyes lit up at that. \u201cJacob, you\u2019re a mad genius,\u201d I said softly. \u201cThat\u2019s brilliant! Of course I\u2019ll talk to my dad. I\u2019m sure he\u2019ll be happy to help you any way that he can. He\u2019s been where your parents are now, and he\u2019s gotten through it, so he knows the process. If anyone can help, he can, and I know he\u2019ll want to\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMy parents live in Portland,\u201d Elena cautioned, \u201cand they\u2019re not likely to visit me here anytime soon\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe\u2019ll work out the logistics later,\u201d I assured her. \u201cLook, I\u2019ll see my dad on Sunday if not before. I\u2019ll make sure I mention it to him then, and I\u2019m sure he\u2019ll get in contact with you so that you can work something out. Just let us know if we can help, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> There was one other tidbit Elena let slip that caught my interest. Apparently she and Stasia met with Joan and Andromeda recently so that they could coordinate their respective weddings so that they wouldn\u2019t clash. It looks like Joan and Andromeda will be getting married in May, while Stasia and Elena are planning for a June ceremony (I like those). Unfortunately, Stasia said something at the dinner which upset Joan, and Elena\u2019s maybe a little worried that they\u2019ve offended my white knight.<br /> <br /> Personally, I blame Stasia\u2019s obsession with that <u><u>Lost Girl</u></u> TV show. I mean, sure, the show\u2019s pretty good (and the main character is mega-hot), but the fictionalized Fae of the series are close enough to the reality of changeling life that a few misunderstandings are bound to crop up in those areas where fact and fiction diverge. For example, Stasia casually mentioned during that dinner that our motley \u201cowns\u201d her.<br /> <br /> Sweet merciful crap, was that ever the wrong thing to say to someone like Joan!<br /> <br /> Elena and Stasia tried to smooth things over, and Andromeda kept Joan calm enough to avoid an incident, but it\u2019s clear that this little slip of the tongue has created a bit of tension between the two couples. I told Elena that I\u2019d speak with Joan and Andromeda the next time I saw them and try to smooth things over.<br /> <br /> I left her to her brother\u2019s care after that. I know that she had a few other things on her mind \u2013 and my instincts tell me that most of those things had to do with Stasia \u2013 but I don\u2019t think anything is seriously wrong there. She did get pretty hammered last night, but I knew Jacob would cut her off before things got dangerous, so I left them to it.<br /> <br /> I finally made my way up to Brightstar\u2019s table. Before I got within five feet of her, she leaped from her chair and into my arms, embracing me and smothering me with kisses. \u201cIt\u2019s good to see you too, sweetie,\u201d I giggled when I came up for air. \u201cYou want it to be just us tonight, or did you want to see who else we could convince to join us?\u201d My eyes darted over to Veronica\u2019s table. It\u2019s been a while since I\u2019ve slept with her, and that purple hair\u2026<br /> <br /> Brightstar had other ideas. \u201cOh, anything is fine with me as long as I\u2019m with you, Lori,\u201d she said with a brilliant smile. \u201cI kinda thought it would just be the two of us tonight, but\u2026\u201d She bit her lip cutely.<br /> <br /> \u201cBut?\u201d I asked with a twinkle.<br /> <br /> \u201cBut I confess that I\u2019m curious what it would be like to get all the wings together on top of me\u2026 maybe I\u2019d look like that thing from <u><u>A Wind in the Door</u></u>,\u201d she said, nodding toward Missy and Jane.<br /> <br /> I laughed out loud at that. Finally, a pop culture reference that I actually <u><u>get</u></u><u>!</u> It\u2019s nice to know that Madeleine L\u2019Engle\u2019s works are still held in high regard.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, <u><u>all</u></u> the wings might be tough,\u201d I said with a glance at Trinh. \u201cIt\u2019s\u2026 complicated.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat, because the dark-haired one is into the Vietnamese girl, and the light-haired one doesn\u2019t like it?\u201d Brightstar asked in a very Brightstar way.<br /> <br /> I chuckled. \u201cIt\u2019s a little more complicated than that, but essentially\u2026 yeah.\u201d<br /> <br /> The two of us walked over to Missy and Jane, and I made formal introductions. \u201cThis is my girlfriend Brightstar,\u201d I said to open. \u201cShe\u2019s one of the official girlfriends.\u201d<br /> <br /> Missy frowned and her forehead wrinkled adorably. \u201cAre we not official?\u201d she asked, obviously distressed.<br /> <br /> I took her hand. \u201cYou\u2019re my best friends,\u201d I said, giving her a squeeze. \u201cYou\u2019re family.\u201d<br /> <br /> This mollified Missy, but gave Brightstar pause. \u201cThey\u2019re <u><u>family</u></u>?\u201d she asked nervously.<br /> <br /> I laughed once more. \u201cNot literally. Not <u><u>biologically</u></u>.\u201d<br /> <br /> Brightstar sighed in relief. \u201cOh, okay then,\u201d she replied, her good humor immediately restored.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo we were wondering,\u201d I forged ahead, giving my best friends a significant look, \u201cif you two would like to join us this evening\u2026 maybe get to know Brightstar a little better?\u201d<br /> <br /> Jane shrugged but smiled, looking my most energetic girlfriend up and down appreciatively. \u201cI\u2019m all for it,\u201d she said. Missy quickly acquiesced as well.<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay, but before we make our way upstairs we\u2019re going to stop by the bar, and each of you is going to give me a peanut. Trust me, you\u2019ll be glad you did.\u201d<br /> <br /> They shrugged, but they\u2019ve lived as Changelings long enough now not to question the occasional odd request. We made our way to Trinh\u2019s table next, and I offered her the same invitation I\u2019d given Missy and Jane. She looked very intrigued by the possibilities\u2026 then glanced at something over my shoulder and quickly but politely declined the invitation. I gave it a few seconds before I turned around, to make sure Jane could get her finger away from her throat or whatever, and the four of us made our way upstairs.<br /> <br /> Sex with Brightstar is always energetic and exhausting, and even with the three of us working in concert to wear her down, I had to employ multiple castings of the Gift of Warm Breath to keep us all going. That clause restores depleted energy, but it does nothing to ease the muscle aches and joint pain that come with that much strenuous exercise, so the four of us stumbled downstairs somewhat stiffly the next morning, our noses filled with the scents of Calamity\u2019s cooking. She\u2019d made Becky\u2019s favorite breakfast. Have I mentioned how <u><u>adorable</u></u> she\u2019s become lately? Well she has, no matter what she says.<br /> <br /> Anyway, things started to fall apart just after Becky left \u201cto make sure her apartment hadn\u2019t burned down,\u201d to use her own words. I\u2019d told her that I planned to grab a cat-nap before the show, and as such would not require a Claviger\u2019s presence, but she mentioned calling Angelica in anyway, and I figured it wasn\u2019t worth arguing over.<br /> <br /> Then D got a text from T.J. She\u2019d spent the night at Gloria\u2019s place, and I was kind of lost in a happy-sleepy fog, nuzzled up against her shoulder when her phone buzzed. \u201cShit,\u201d she said loudly, glancing down at the message.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat is it?\u201d I asked, snapping myself out of my daze.<br /> <br /> \u201cT.J.\u2019s hurt. He got attacked last night. I don\u2019t have all the details, but it looks like at least a dozen guys came down on him as revenge for driving those two off the other day. He called in help from Percival and Shi, and they won in the end, but\u2026 they took T.J. down. He\u2019s all right,\u201d she said in answer to my anguished look, \u201cthey just knocked him out. But I mean\u2026 <u><u>damn</u></u><u>!</u>\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAre Percival and Shi okay? Was anyone killed?\u201d I asked, sitting bolt upright.<br /> <br /> D answered T.J.\u2019s text as quickly as she could. \u201cPercival was roughed up pretty badly. Shi seems to be fine. As far as T.J. knows, nobody was killed, but a couple of their attackers didn\u2019t leave under their own power; they had to be carried off. The street by Rowan\u2019s house is a mess\u2026 there are no bodies or anything, but there\u2019s a lot of blood and the cops are all over it.\u201d<br /> <br /> As soon as all of this came to light, Marguerite offered to head to L.A. to speak with both the Warlock of Night and our friends in the Unseelie Court to see what she could uncover. She grabbed a mirror and put it in the back of her car so that she could effect a quick getaway if necessary, and then sped off down the road.<br /> <br /> \u201cFuck,\u201d I swore softly as I thought the situation over. \u201cI need to call Augustine.\u201d<br /> <br /> I stepped out of the room and did just that. The Viscount answered my call promptly and let me know that he\u2019d heard about the fracas. I filled him in on the events leading up to the fight, and he considered them grimly.<br /> <br /> \u201cFirst of all, Lorelei,\u201d he said firmly, \u201cI want you to know that you did nothing wrong. You acted to defend a friend and a citizen, and attempted to put an end to an untenable situation as quickly and neatly as possible. There is no need to blame yourself for what came after.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you,\u201d I said, a little choked up. Augustine must be more insightful than I\u2019d previously thought; he pretty much hit the nail on the head with that one. I\u2019d been terrified that I\u2019d sparked some sort of all-out war between the Lady by the Sea and the Courts of Fallen Angels.<br /> <br /> \u201cT.J. and Percival will be fine; a few members of your court have already seen to the worst of their wounds. Percival holds T.J. in high regard, and when his friend was struck down, his retaliation was swift and decisive. Some might call it a bit\u2026 excessive,\u201d he continued delicately. \u201cBut that is neither here nor there. What concerns me is how Percival and Shi were able to respond to T.J.\u2019s request for assistance so quickly\u2026 almost impossibly so.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat had occurred to me as well,\u201d I told him (truthfully, though other details of the incident had taken precedence in my mind). \u201cI suppose I should speak with Percival about it at some point.\u201d<br /> <br /> I could <u><u>hear</u></u> Augustine\u2019s frown over the phone. \u201cIf you think that is best,\u201d he said delicately. \u201cBut I caution you to pay no heed to any insults he might hurl in your direction. Percival is a valued member of the Summer Court, but interacting with him directly can be\u2026 distasteful.\u201d<br /> <br /> He gathered himself, and then gave me his final words on the subject. \u201cWhether we reply to this assault with the olive branch or the sword is not my decision at this time, though I suspect that Lowjack will wish to speak with one or the other of us soon. I shall call him and make certain that he is aware of the situation.\u201d<br /> <br /> I thanked him again and we disconnected. I called Charlotte next. She had also already heard about the incident in question, and like Augustine she was quick to inform me that she did not think any of my actions to date had been inappropriate. \u201cA friend, who is under your protection, asked for your help and you gave it to her,\u201d she said patiently. \u201cYou were well within your rights to do so, and none of us blame you for wanting to come to her aid.\u201d<br /> <br /> That brought me up short. \u201cWait a minute,\u201d I said, puzzling through it. \u201cActually, Rowan <u><u>didn\u2019t</u></u> ask for my help. She didn\u2019t want me to get involved at first; said she didn\u2019t want to trouble me\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Charlotte chuckled. \u201cThat is very like her, from what I understand.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt is,\u201d I agreed, \u201cbut that\u2019s not my point. My point is that I was first made aware of this situation by Olivia Gold.\u201d<br /> <br /> There was silence on the other end, and I imagined that I could almost hear my co-monarch\u2019s teeth grinding together. \u201cJolie looked after the interests of our Freehold\u2019s Day Courtiers because of her occasional relationship with Felicity,\u201d she said in a measured voice, \u201cbut I do not believe she ever fully trusted Olivia Gold. And I do not like that woman.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe struck me as manipulative as well,\u201d I agreed. \u201cDo you think she engineered this whole thing?\u201d<br /> <br /> Charlotte paused to think for a moment before answering. \u201cI would not go so far as to claim that,\u201d she eventually said, \u201cbut I doubt very much that her reason for bringing the matter to your attention was pure altruism.\u201d<br /> <br /> We chewed that over for a few moments before moving on to the subject of Percival and Shi\u2019s involvement. While Charlotte agreed that questioning Shi would almost certainly prove to be an exercise in frustration, she also cautioned me about speaking with Percival. \u201cHe is rude, he is arrogant, and he is one of the most dangerous people in our Freehold,\u201d she said. \u201cIf my sources are correct, he actually took one of his foes\u2019 <u><u>arms</u></u> as a trophy last night. He is reputedly contemplating having it stuffed and mounted.\u201d<br /> <br /> I quickly swallowed my gorge and bade my co-monarch farewell, then rejoined the others. Everyone in the motley got a group text a couple of minutes later. Marguerite had reached the Warlock of Night, and was convinced that neither the Warlock nor the Handmaidens knew anything about the brawl. She was quite certain that this wasn\u2019t some sort of political move on the part of her Court, and I trust her judgment in that regard. I know she would never lie to me about something this important; our family means far too much to her.<br /> <br /> The Warlock seemed to believe that Marguerite was accusing her of something, and Marguerite was trying hard to convince her that this wasn\u2019t the case. When the Warlock asked if we were demanding \u201cweregild\u201d \u2013 or tribute \u2013 as reparations for the harm done to our Freehold, I told Marguerite to stall her until I could consult with Lowjack. Though I was personally inclined to let it pass as long as things didn\u2019t escalate further, he <u><u>is</u></u> the current reigning monarch.<br /> <br /> I speed-dialed John, and he picked up with a wry quip on the third ring. \u201cLowjack\u2019s Last-To-Know Headquarters,\u201d he said with a sort of weary longsuffering grace.<br /> <br /> \u201cSorry, John,\u201d I said by way of greeting. \u201cI assume you already know pretty much everything about what went down last night?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cI assume so as well,\u201d he replied, \u201cbut why don\u2019t you tell me what happened in your own words, and we\u2019ll see what we come up with.\u201d<br /> <br /> I told him my story, and I think I surprised him twice. The first tidbit was the fact that Olivia Gold had alerted me to the situation. Lowjack shares Charlotte\u2019s opinion of Olivia; he doesn\u2019t trust her as far as he could throw her. Ordinarily I\u2019d take this with a grain of salt, as John doesn\u2019t really trust <u><u>anyone</u></u>, but I think he\u2019s on the money with this one.<br /> <br /> He was also unaware of the fact that Marguerite was currently speaking with the Warlock of Night. I conveyed Marguerite\u2019s messages to him, and he paused briefly to consider. \u201cPlease pass along the following message for me,\u201d he said after a moment. \u201cWe believe that the incident last night was the act of one motley acting <u><u>exceptionally</u></u> foolishly, and not a sanctioned act of the Night Court itself. Therefore, no reparations are necessary at this time. Should the incident be repeated, however, we will be forced to regard it as an official act of the Night Court, and take the appropriate actions in response.\u201d<br /> <br /> I promised to relay the message and thanked him. \u201cLori,\u201d he said seriously before we disconnected, \u201cyou did the right thing. Any of the monarchs would have done the same to protect one of our citizens\u2026 especially a friend. None of us could have predicted what came after.\u201d<br /> <br /> I thanked him again and then quickly called Marguerite. I passed along Lowjack\u2019s words. Marguerite wasn\u2019t thrilled to be the bearer of what amounted to a thinly veiled threat\u2026 and who can blame her? The Warlock is nothing if not unpredictable. But she took to her duty with good grace, and reported back a few minutes later that the Warlock seemed to have accepted John\u2019s message at face value. Hopefully that means this whole fubar situation is now over and done with.<br /> <br /> I dialed Neon next, figuring she\u2019d probably be more coherent than Rowan if the two of them had heard about the situation. When she answered, I asked her what she already knew.<br /> <br /> \u201cOnly that the police want to talk to my girlfriend,\u201d she said with a bit of an edge, but then sighed and seemed to relax a bit. \u201cFortunately I can provide her with an alibi\u2026 she was nowhere near her own house last night.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThank goodness,\u201d I muttered. \u201cLook, I\u2019m sorry things got this far out of hand, okay? I never thought the vandals would step things up to this degree\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIf they thought the Day Court was involved, they might have considered it a matter of saving face,\u201d Neon piped up. \u201cMost of us\u2026 we don\u2019t want to fuck with the seasonal courts if we can help it. We don\u2019t have a Spring Court here in L.A. to patch us up afterward\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> That gave me an idea. \u201cLook, I hate to ask, but according to\u2026 an eyewitness, some of the assailants were pretty badly hurt. One\u2026 might be missing an arm.\u201d<br /> <br /> There was a brief pause. \u201cMissing an arm?\u201d she repeated carefully.<br /> <br /> \u201cA bit,\u201d I confirmed. \u201cInsincere Marguerite is heading over to the Unseelie Court right now to put her head together with your motley. Could you maybe keep an eye out for any Night Courtiers who might be sporting new injuries\u2026 or maybe are just suddenly missing with no explanation? I\u2019d really hate for this to go any further\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, I\u2019ll keep an eye out alright,\u201d she said, fuming a little. \u201cThis whole thing started because they targeted my girlfriend. I\u2019ll keep my ear to the ground, and if I hear anything, I\u2019ll pass it on.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks, Elektra,\u201d I said. \u201cNow, get back to Rowan; she needs you more than I do right now.\u201d<br /> <br /> So that\u2019s where we stand. My little attempt to scare off a few vandals has resulted in more violence than I would have thought possible. T.J., who was only doing this as a favor for me and Maria, was badly hurt and could have been killed if not for the timely intervention of a couple of his good friends. Percival, who wasn\u2019t involved in this situation at all, was also badly hurt. Several Night Courtiers who were probably just in town to stand up for their <u><u>own</u></u> friends were maimed\u2026 maybe permanently, since Spring healing contracts are in short supply in L.A. And while <u><u>all</u></u> <u><u>three</u></u> of my fellow monarchs have taken pains to assure me that I\u2019m not to blame for last night\u2019s violence\u2026 well\u2026 I kind of <u><u>am</u></u>, and nothing they say is going to change that.<br /> <br /> I can\u2019t afford to fall apart over this\u2026 not right now, anyway. It\u2019s Friday, which means we have a weekend show to prep for tonight. Fridays are always crowded, and I can\u2019t let the Freehold see me crumble in a time of crisis. I have to be bold and self-assured and sympathetic, or they\u2019ll start to lose confidence in my leadership. Or the <u><u>Wyrd</u></u> will start to lose confidence in my leadership. And I can\u2019t afford to be the weak link in the Lady by the Sea with the threats of Hollywood and the Grand Maw looming over us.<br /> <br /> I think I want to be with Maria tonight\u2026 or maybe Oleander, if Maria has other plans. I just\u2026 I just want to be with one person who loves me, who can hold me and comfort me without judging me if I decide I need to cry. I took up the Crown, and I won\u2019t forsake it at the first sign of trouble\u2026 but for a few hours at least I\u2019d just like to be poor, flawed, vulnerable little Lori again.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei de la Rocha</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> The past couple of days have definitely been interesting. For me it started at the show last night. For others it started earlier in the day yesterday, but we\u2019ll get to that. The show itself was nothing overly special. I mean all the ladies did a fantastic job up on stage, and Lori even wore that light up outfit that Calamity had from a prank with Captain Jack. It was interesting. She did a song from a band called They Might Be Giants called Birdhouse in Your Soul. It was kind of quirky but she made it work. The light up outfit certainly didn\u2019t hurt. While all of that was going on I couldn\u2019t help but notice that Elena was at the bar all by herself. I made sure to swing by and find out what was going on. It turns out that Stasia was away on an all-day photo shoot somewhere and would be back around 3:00am. That was all fine and good except that mom had to choose tonight to call Elena to talk. The talk went about as well as you could expect I suppose, except the fact that mom purposefully didn\u2019t listen to anything that Elena had to say about Stasia or the upcoming wedding in June. Mom just pretended like Elena hadn\u2019t said anything and went back to what they had been talking about before that. I wish I could have slapped my mom in the face for that and I generally don\u2019t wish violence on my own parents. But this passive aggressive bullshit is too much. She should face what is going on and either tell Elena that she doesn\u2019t approve or admit that she loves her daughter and accepts her for who she is. The only thing my mother accomplished tonight was to drive her daughter to the bar to drink. I suggested that Elena have Lori\u2019s father, Reverend Wells talk to mom (and maybe dad) and see if he can help them understand and accept their daughter. He went through the same thing himself so maybe he could be a good resource to call upon.<br /> <br /> That whole conversation with Elena wasn\u2019t all sad though. Elena told me that Stasia had talked to Joan and Andromeda about wedding plans so they wouldn\u2019t step on each other\u2019s toes and made some comment about being owned by our motley. This needless to say did not go over well with Joan. Elena tried to explain that it was in reference to a TV show and not meant literally. I think Andromeda tried to help calm her down too. Elena thought that they had succeeded but was still concerned enough by it to mention it to me. I said that I would mention it to Lori so she could talk to Joan.<br /> <br /> While I was talking to Elena, Lori and Calamity decided to come by and make sure everything was okay. They noticed that Elena was at the club by herself and wanted to make sure that everything was okay with Stasia and their relationship. Elena mentioned the whole phone call thing and got the same reaction from Calamity and Lori that she got from me. We all supported her and tried to do our best to cheer her up. When Elena told Lori of my idea to include her father in the conversation my motley mate called me a mad genius and said that idea just might work. I don\u2019t often come up with ideas that could be described as \u201cmad genius\u201d so I suppose I should take that as a compliment.<br /> <br /> After the show Elena stuck around waiting for Stasia to pick her up. She had made arrangements with her fianc\u00e9e earlier, so Stasia knew where to come to pick up Elena. That also gave Elena license to drink enough to get drunk and not have to worry about how she was going to get home. I will admit that I don\u2019t like seeing my sister drunk, but I couldn\u2019t really fault her for wanting to forget about things for a while. I still cut her off before she got too drunk. A slightly drunk and unsteady on her feet sister is one thing. An falling down shitfaced sister is another, so I made sure she didn\u2019t get shitfaced. She got a bit more than a nice buzz and was in a good mood when Stasia came by to pick her up.<br /> <br /> Stasia came by around 3:00am to pick up Elena and was immediately intercepted by Calamity. I think my motley mate wanted to head her off at the pass and explain why her fianc\u00e9e was drunk before any further conversation was had. I think Calamity also talked to Stasia a bit about the whole \u201cowning\u201d thing that she talked to Joan about. I didn\u2019t hear it all and frankly was paying more attention to my sister at that point in time. Stasia then made her way over to my sister and asked if she wanted to go home. Elena was more than happy to do that so the two of us helped her get to Stasia\u2019s car. Elena did seem to sober up a bit in the night air, so that was good. I did mention to Stasia my idea of getting Reverend Wells involved in the whole conversation with my parents and that seemed to calm her down a bit. She was not happy with the way our mother had handled the conversation with Elena tonight.<br /> <br /> Then today started off interesting. Everyone gathered for breakfast. That is nothing unusual, nor is Calamity making Becky\u2019s favorite breakfast for her. They make such a cute couple. Anyway, Calamity told us what she and Becky had been up to yesterday afternoon. Apparently the pair of them went to go visit Luther Henderson, the man from the highway incident. Calamity wanted to get an idea of what kind of person he was so they were going to check out his place while he was at work. They got there and found that he lives in a fairly nice neighborhood. Nothing too fancy, but not too bad either. It was a gated community with nice houses and lots of older Chinese neighbors. Calamity and Becky however noticed that not all was right in that part of town. They spotted Vietnamese Tong graffiti on buildings nearby, but not directly on Luther\u2019s house or anything. It seems that they claim that territory, but maybe aren\u2019t so invested in the housing development as of yet. Becky worked her magic and talked to some of the Chinese folks to get an idea of what kind of person Luther is. They said that he is protective of the folks that live in in the neighborhood and has even confronted some of the Vietnamese Tong about some things. He has not made a big enough nuisance of himself to become a target as of yet, but he has stood up for his neighbors in the past. He seems like a stand-up kind of guy to me. There was also some talk about Luther having a friend on the Police force. That should make things more interesting.<br /> <br /> While this conversation was going on Gloria was handing old records to Insincere Marguerite. I was curious at first and paid attention. Marguerite for her part was using a contract to de-age the records so they were back to their original state. Calamity saw this and ran to get a strip of photos like you\u2019d get from a photobooth. She then asked if Insincere Marguerite could use her contract on that. Marguerite did. It looked like the photos were of Stasia and Calamity as kids, before Calamity had been taken. It made me wish that I had a photo of me and Elena from when we were kids. I have a keepsake. I have the handkerchief that I dropped in the ice cave when I first arrived in Arcadia. I wonder if I should get Insincere Marguerite to make it like new, or leave it aged and weathered from being in the ice for so long? I think I\u2019ll leave it as is for now. If I have Marguerite \u201cfix\u201d it then it will be like that time didn\u2019t happen, but it did and that is something that I want to remember. I want to remember finding that cave by shear providence and coming across this bit of cloth stuck in the ice. It sparked a memory. A memory of my childhood, which is all that I needed to escape. I freed the handkerchief from its icy prison and held it tight as I escaped that frozen hell. Yeah, it\u2019s best to leave that as it is. I can\u2019t erase the past. Nor do I want to.<br /> <br /> It was around that time that De la Rocha got a text from T.J. and a whole big thing got revealed. Apparently last night T.J. got into a fight with about a dozen Night Courtiers from L.A. They all showed up at Rowan\u2019s house to start something. Good thing that Rowan was at Neon\u2019s place for the evening! Anyway, a fight ensued and T. J. was badly outnumbered. He managed to get a message out and called for help. Within a short time Shi and Percival both showed up to help and the fight turned into one huge mess. T.J. was taken down and Percival saw red. He is a bit of an asshole, but he is protective of his friends and apparently T.J. is his friend. He proceeded to tear apart Night Courtiers like they were made of tissue paper. Specifically the one that took T.J. down. He actually cut that man\u2019s arm off and kept if for a trophy! Yeah, that got the appropriate amount of awe and unease from my motley. T.J. and Percival are thankfully okay. They were seen to by some Spring Courtiers last night and are doing alright now.<br /> <br /> This whole thing sparked several phone conversations. Lori called Augustine to talk to him about what happened and go some more details. Insincere Marguerite also volunteered to go to L.A. to talk to the Warlock of Night and find out what happened, if she knew anything to begin with. She was also going to talk to the Unseelie Court about what happened. Calamity called Queen Charlotte, as did Lori. I\u2019m not sure if they realized that they were overlapping, but it\u2019s all good. There were probably different details discussed with each conversation. While conversations were going on Insincere Marguerite texted Lori to let her know that she was speaking to the Warlock of Night. The Warlock had initially assumed that we were accusing her of something, but Marguerite did her best to assure the monarch that we had no such intentions. She also let us know that the Warlock and the Handmaidens did not know of the attack at Rowan\u2019s place last night and were quite surprised to hear of it.<br /> <br /> One of the interesting things about this whole situation was how Percival and Shi arrived to help T.J. so fast. I assume that he called them for help, but they still arrived within an unreasonably short amount of time. Not that I\u2019m complaining mind you. I prefer T.J. in the land of the living, but it was still odd. The other odd thing that came up was something that Lori mentioned to Lowjack when she talked to him on the phone. This whole situation with Rowan and Neon and people vandalizing her stuff wasn\u2019t brought to Lori\u2019s attention by Rowan or even Neon. It was Olivia Gold. The Day Courtier. Lowjack apparently doesn\u2019t trust that woman and I\u2019m starting to come down on his side. I hadn\u2019t really given much thought to the woman before now, but her involvement in this whole situation is sketchy at best.<br /> <br /> The conversation between Insincere Marguerite and the Warlock of Night continued and the Warlock asked if our freehold was going to ask for any weregild on behalf of our injured residents. The question was brought to Lori\u2019s attention who brought it up to Lowjack during their conversation. He said that we would treat the incident as if it had been committed by a very foolish motley running afoul of our Courts and nothing more. He was not asking for any weregild in recompense. He did say however that if the Night Court cannot rein in this motley and stop them from further action then he would treat this as if it had not been an isolated incident and react accordingly. Insincere Marguerite passed along the message, veiled threat and all, to the Warlock of Night, who apparently took it with good if not happy grace.<br /> <br /> After that Lori talked to Neon who said that the police had been calling and wanted to talk to Rowan about the whole situation. There was apparently a lot of blood and damage left in the wake of the fight and the neighbors had called the police last night. Thankfully Rowan had been at Neon\u2019s place all night and had an alibi for where she had been last night. Neon however did tell Lori that she was uncertain if the Night Court would have sent such a large force to Rowan\u2019s house just to protest the relationship between Day and Night Courtiers. She thought that something bigger was going on with the Day Court.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m personally not sure what is going on with this whole thing, but it is messed up. I can understand rivalry between Courts but this is ridiculous. When violence starts it tends to just be met with more violence. It has to stop somewhere. Hopefully the Warlock of Night can rein in whoever was behind the attack last night and we can keep the Day court from retaliating. I don\u2019t think we have to worry about the Summer Court coming after them. Augustine seems to be a pretty level-headed guy. I just have a feeling that more is going to come of this before it is all said and done. I just hope no one else gets seriously hurt in this whole mess.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXVIII</i><br /> <br /> Oh Lori, sweetie. Anyway, other details\u2026<br /> Calamity has been doing \u201cAngry Johnny\u201d by Poe (which is an awesome song) while Insincere Marguerite has been doing a modified version of \u201cGirls Like Girls\u201d by Hayley Kiyoko (which is gay as hell) changed to be more seductive or croon-y.<br /> <br /> Some names from way earlier in the Campaign. The Summer Court is not as prone to spending as much time at the Dream House. TJ is pretty much The juggernaut so him going down is kind of a big deal. His health goes way into double digits and his armor is embarrassing.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite was using Contract of Hours to de-age objects.<br /> <br /> Okay, well, I think that covers it. Comments and Questions welcome!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-08T06:50:04-07:00","id":1259582,"title":"","content":"Penitent Tom was totally psyching us readers out with that intro. I totally thought it would be the arrival of her unwanted cult","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-08T07:19:03-07:00","id":1259589,"title":"","content":"Huh... believe it or not, that intro was not intended to deceive. In her previous entry, Lori <i>did</i> worry that her actions might spark some sort of reprisal from the Night Court of L.A., and that's what she was referencing with those first few sentences. As far as the Devotees go... I wrote that short story pretty much immediately after I spent the experience to purchase the Merit, but the Storyteller is and has always been the good Baroness, and it's her decision when to introduce a new element to the story. Having said that, I don't think you'll have too much longer to wait for that trio's introduction...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-08T13:11:37-07:00","id":1259652,"title":"","content":"So last night's session included the following phrases: &quot;basically a plus-sized Wookalar,&quot; &quot;Did you see the Nazgul in the back?&quot; &quot;...I think they are going to take Lori's soul,&quot; &quot;We try not to say Mr. Gone's name out loud,&quot; &quot;I think she might even be TOO French, &quot; &quot;Did someone say fist fuck?&quot; and &quot;TWO HOT LATINA BIKERS CALAMITY. TWO HOT LATINA BIKERS&quot; Also Calamity ties someone to a chair. Join us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theon