t a pleasant thought.<br /> <br /> Anyway, after that little talk I chatted with Molly for a bit. She asked after Elena and I explained the whole situation to her. The messed-up phone call with our mother, Elena getting upset. Elena getting drunk and Stasia showing up to take her home. I did mention that we might have someone that can talk to our mother and see if she can be reasoned with. If anyone can do it, I believe that Reverend Wells can. I hope. I really want my mother to come to her senses and accept my sister for who she is. You can\u2019t just ignore such a big part of someone\u2019s life like that. It\u2019s ridiculous. <br /> <br /> As the evening was wrapping up and people were leaving I noticed something interesting. The trio from L.A. left together and I noticed Molly slipping out the door after them surreptitiously. I\u2019m not sure if anyone from the motley talked to her about those three or if she just knew what was going on from another source. I didn\u2019t tell her about them being there. But she took it upon herself to sneak out after them. Hopefully she will bring back something interesting or at least informative.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Saturday morning dawned early and we ignored it. Then noon came around and we started getting up. We all gathered in the kitchen for breakfast. Even Lori came back to the house with Jolie and Desiree in tow for food. Julia was making eggs and toast while Trinh was working on cooking up more of those delicious sausages. I made coffee for everyone that wanted it. Conversation eventually made its way around to the trio from L.A. and what we were going to do about them. We seemed to come to the consensus to treat it as a one-time thing and leave it be. If they come around again then we might have to have a talk with them and find out what they want. After a little longer Lori asked our guests if they wouldn\u2019t mind giving us some privacy so we could have a motley meeting. They agreed. Jolie and Desiree actually left while the others just left the room and let us talk. <br /> <br /> So, what Lori wanted to talk to us about, and this included Luna on speakerphone, was Mr. Gone showing up and what she found out from him. It seems that he is also of the opinion that Hollywood is behind the whole fiasco. He did apparently find it interesting that Olivia Gold was the one that informed Lori of the situation with Rowan and Neon. Not sure how she works into this whole situation. She is originally from L.A. not Hollywood. Anyway, Mr. Gone explained that the individuals that were involved in the fight are in various stages of healing. The ringleader for the group, the one that went after T.J. with such enthusiasm, is in a coma after the beating that he received. Lori offered to send some Spring Courtier healers over to help see to their injuries. He declined the offer for now, but said he might take her up on it in the future. Calamity also offered to go into the dreams of the ringleader to find out anything that she could about the reasons behind the fight. The Night Courtier said that dream healing had been attempted without too much success as of now. Mr. Gone offered his assistance in our investigation of the incident, but Lori said that Boss Lowjack would likely want to handle the investigation \u201cin house.\u201d Lowjack confirmed her assumptions when she called him last night. Apparently Lowjack also suggested that we let it slip to Olivia Gold that the Night Court in L.A., specifically Mr. Gone, has asked to assist us in our examination of the incident. This might get her to decide to cooperate more with Lowjack and his investigation rather than have to deal with the notorious Night Courtier himself.<br /> <br /> Lori also told us why she had been keeping some things to herself since becoming Spring monarch. She has learned information that is vital to the fight against Hollywood and wanted to keep the circle of people that know the information small in order to keep our operatives safe. She also had concerns that if we were to be captured and tortured we would be unable to divulge any information about said operatives if we didn\u2019t have that information in the first place. I suppose it makes sense. If it was just the possibility of physical torture then I am fairly certain that I could withstand whatever they could come up with. It took a Gentry to almost break me last time. But that isn\u2019t a guarantee. As Twitch has proven you can break someone with the right combination of drugs. He certainly did a number on Rook while he had him in custody. Then there is also the possibility of someone forcing their way into our dreams. We are lucid dreamers, so we would know that someone was breaking in but I\u2019m not positive that I could keep all my secrets from them. I\u2019m not as experienced in the dreamscape side of things. Calamity would be better prepared to deal with that kind of assault. So, while I admit to being curious as to what kinds of things Lori is keeping secret, I can understand why she is doing so.<br /> <br /> After our talk we all went our separate ways. I met up with Luna and Elena to go for a hike in the woods. We invited Stasia go with us but she declined. She\u2018s not much of a hiker. That\u2019s fine though, we had fun anyway. I think Lori had her little chat with Olivia Gold while I was out. I\u2019ll have to ask how that went.<br /> <br /> I dropped Elena and Luna back off and headed back to the Dream House after our hike. And when I walked in the door Calamity came up to me and said that she needed to talk to me. Apparently she had been in contact with a couple people regarding the gang in Luther\u2019s neighborhood and what she could do about it. One of those people was Kathy, the kindred woman that we talked to previously. Kathy doesn\u2019t have any issues with Calamity dealing with the gang in the area, though she did warn Calamity that if she took out all them members of the gang another one would just take their place. Kathy also apparently mentioned that there might be a demon in the area. I\u2019m not sure how we got to be the \u201cgo to\u201d people for dealing with demons when we\u2019ve only ever fought the one, but it seems that we are. The last time things didn\u2019t go that great for us. It wasn\u2019t a total disaster, but it was pretty bad. If Lori hadn\u2019t been there to heal people it would have been worse. So, Calamity asked if I\u2019d be interested in helping her deal with the possible demonic problem. She also explained that there was something going on at the location where the temperature was really hot. I told her that I can lower the temperature in an area pretty well, so I could help. I\u2019m not positive that this is the wisest thing to do, but demons seem to be pretty much all bad news, so the problem needs to be dealt with. I should probably call Luna and see if she wants in on this. She will likely want to be there to make sure I don\u2019t get in over my head, which is fine by me. I like having her watch my back. I wonder if we can get Caoimhe to help us too? She was effective in the last fight. If this in fact a demon then she might be a good person to have with us this time as well. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> Yvette has returned from her vacation. I spent quite a lovely evening with her last night. She has spent a long time thinking, after we went to Arcadia, about our history. She still does not forgive me. But\u2026she has decided that she still loves me, and she knows I won\u2019t hurt her and\u2026she still wants to be with me, but I must never try to control her. This\u2026is complicated. I mean I do not try to control people, of course, but I like being in charge. I have come to decide it is a test, of sorts.<br /> <br /> Still, last night was wonderful. Sweet and romantic. I had hoped Julia would join us, but she demurred to spend the evening with Maria, Melissa and Jane. Yvette and Julia are getting along best they can, honestly\u2026I almost think at this point Yvette may be the more jealous one. Julia is after all my wife.<br /> <br /> Also last night M______ was here. Not on a hunt, M______ was actually there in the stead of the Warlock, applying a more\u2026rational\u2026eye to the situation with Rowan. Apparently he and Juliette made arrangements they were pleased with. I spoke with M______ briefly, and it was cordial. I generally have avoided his attention, something I am pleased with.<br /> <br /> Anyway, such a lovely romantic night. Yvette arranged for rose petals and wine, and we danced, drank and made love. So few I connect with that way\u2026only Julia and my brides Maria and Juliette.<br /> <br /> Breakfast was good, Julia actually made omelets in tandem with Trinh making sausages. I will miss her cooking when she moves out. I walked out Yvette and returned to spend some time with Julia, who was painting. Her mood was good\u2026her night was more cuddling than sex on her part, with Maria spending more time acquainting herself with the avian maidens. I lay with my head in her lap and just sort of dozed much of the afternoon, bringing up drinks and snacks.<br /> Jacob apparently went hiking with Luna, while Calamity talked to a Night Fairest named Rosalita who I don\u2019t know very well, and Juliette did Monarch stuff under Maria\u2019s watchful eye, including meeting Olivia Gold, a meeting I deliberately missed. I think I had the better day.<br /> Tonight I will sing my \u201cGirls Like Girls\u201d by Hayley Kiyoko. I do a more low seductive version, not the more poppy version. Not that I dislike the poppy version, but it is less suitable. Yvette had not heard it and was terribly amused by it. Julia likes it too, unlike her usual more gloomy stuff.<br /> <br /> Apparently everyone is going to go fight demons after the show. Is there nothing better to do on a Saturday night? I suppose I shall have to go as well.<br /> <br /> Juliette is so displeased\u2026<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XIX</i><br /> <br /> I actually created Gone for this storyline, rather than having had him in reserve for awhile. What can I say, I got inspired.<br /> <br /> Calamity dealt with her plot looking in on Luther. She contacted Kathy (who asked if she wanted to kill a Demon) and Corbin, who pointed her to Rosalita. She gave Corbin contact information to pass along, but Rosalita showed up instead. Rosalita is a Fairest Shadowsoul and Render. Gone is\u2026complicated, lets say.<br /> <br /> And of course the Devotees made an appearance. Yay!<br /> <br /> Okay well I think that covers it. Comments and Questions welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-06T19:03:09-08:00","id":1265188,"title":"","content":"Many apologies for the delay, I have been sick and suffering back pain. But I have journals to get up, so here we go.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Sigh. I know I\u2019ve said this before, and I hate repeating my sentiments\u2026 but with everything that\u2019s happened over the past twelve hours or so, I just can\u2019t help it, so here goes.<br /> <br /> I do <u>not</u> have time for this shit.<br /> <br /> So the last time I wrote we were preparing for the Saturday night show and I was seething about the fact that Calamity had signed up for another demon-killing mission in L.A., putting paid to my own plans to seduce Rosalita into my bed and share her with Maria. And yes, I could have simply let Calamity and Jacob see to the demon-killing, but considering how our last effort in that arena went, it seemed logical to assume that my presence would be helpful for healing and crowd management. I would have felt <u>awful</u> if I had stayed home and people had been hurt as a result.<br /> <br /> Prior to the show, Marguerite was walking around in an\u2026 interesting outfit. She was wearing all bright pink, including a pair of comically oversized sunglasses. She held a small transistor radio as she danced about, blaring out 60s music. Calamity and I asked her what was up with that, but all she\u2019d say is that Julia hates that outfit, so she was taking advantage of her absence to flaunt it (you might recall that the other Mrs. Oldacre was spending the early portion of the evening speaking with Willow Black at the Rose &amp; Thorn).<br /> <br /> My solo number last night was, in my opinion, pretty sub-par. The audience still ate it up, so I didn\u2019t let it get to me, but as distracted as I was by recent events, it wasn\u2019t my best effort by a long shot. So I put it behind me and decided to focus on mingling with the crowd, as there were a fair number of notable guests present.<br /> <br /> First, T.J. was there, looking as big and boisterous as ever. D had already been by his table a couple of times by the time I made it out there, and he seemed to be okay, but I thought it was incumbent upon me to make my pleasantries as well. \u201cHey, T. J.,\u201d I said softly as I pulled up a chair.<br /> <br /> \u201cHighness,\u201d he said with a nod.<br /> <br /> \u201cHow are you?\u201d I asked after a moment.<br /> <br /> He shrugged. \u201cCan\u2019t complain,\u201d he said noncommittally.<br /> <br /> I sighed. \u201cI meant, how are you physically\u2026 how\u2019s your recovery coming?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh,\u201d he said, and seemed maybe a little embarrassed. \u201cI\u2019m doin\u2019 okay, Highness,\u201d he said after a moment. \u201cPretty much patched up now.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd Percival?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cHe\u2019s an asshole,\u201d T.J. said without missing a beat, \u201cand there ain\u2019t no cure for that. But I hear he\u2019s healed up okay.\u201d<br /> <br /> I chuckled at that, and we chatted for a few minutes about Percival and his role in the Summer Court. Oddly enough, we eventually landed on the idea that he acts as a sort of opposite number to Flores. It\u2019s not as odd as it sounds at first\u2026 Percival can start a fight with just about anyone, and Flores can defuse any violent situation with those big puppy-dog eyes of hers. Plus, they pretty much loathe each other (as much as Flores is capable of loathing anyone, that is).<br /> <br /> Eventually I couldn\u2019t avoid it any longer. \u201cLook, T.J.,\u201d I said finally, \u201cI\u2019m sorry about what happened to you at Rowan\u2019s place. If I\u2019d known it was going to get that out of hand, I\u2019d never have asked you to do it\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> He shrugged. \u201cAnd I woulda done it anyway. Honestly, I still feel kinda bad about how I treated Rowan a year ago\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled at him. \u201cDon\u2019t worry; it\u2019ll be our secret. But seriously, thanks T.J. You put yourself out there because I asked you to, and you got hurt in the process. And I won\u2019t forget that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks, Highness,\u201d he said. \u201cMeans a lot.\u201d<br /> <br /> I bought him a refill (chocolate milk and vodka\u2026 what the fuck?) and moved on, allowing Calamity to slide into the seat as I left. Julia caught my eye as she returned from her sojourn to the Rose &amp; Thorn, so I walked across the floor to speak to her before she took her seat.<br /> <br /> \u201cMission accomplished,\u201d she said simply, \u201cI talked with Willow about the investigation and dropped\u2026 that name a few times. I think she got the message; she left right after our conversation.\u201d<br /> <br /> I kissed her. \u201cThanks, sweetie,\u201d I said, \u201cI hope that makes things a little easier on John\u2019s people.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo,\u201d she said after an indecently brief pause, \u201cwho\u2019s that?\u201d She indicated Rosalita\u2019s table by inclining her head.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, she stopped by earlier today to talk with Calamity. I introduced myself, and\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Julia smirked. \u201cYou made friends?\u201d she suggested with a raised eyebrow.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah,\u201d I agreed. \u201cActually, I feel kind of bad about that whole situation, because I invited her here tonight so that I could, umm\u2026 \u2018introduce\u2019 her to Maria, and now I\u2019m probably going to have to bail on that whole situation because Calamity signed us up to kill another demon in L.A\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> So then I had to explain that whole mess. Julia valiantly offered to entertain Rosalita until the rest of us returned, but as I still didn\u2019t know at that point who was going with Calamity and who would be remaining at the Dream House, I was noncommittal with my response. \u201cI imagine Maria would still like to enjoy her company tonight\u2026 though I doubt very much if she\u2019d mind you joining in as well.\u201d<br /> <br /> A quick conversation with D later and everything was set. She <u>really</u> didn\u2019t want me going into L.A. on a demon hunting mission without her, but I could see that she was also looking forward to spending some time with our tough-girl guest. Eventually she accepted my insistence that she stay and enjoy herself. \u201cAfter all,\u201d I said, \u201cI\u2019ll be with Calamity, Jacob, Becky, and Caoimhe\u2026 and I can take care of myself.\u201d<br /> <br /> She smiled and stroked my cheek <u>so</u> gently. \u201cI know you can,\u201d she said, leaning in for a kiss. \u201cIf you\u2019re sure\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> So with that out of the way, I only had one more important conversation to see to before the end of the evening, and it was one that I was kind of dreading. I mean, I <u>spoke</u> with other people \u2013 Missy and Jane and Trinh all passed a few words with me, and I shared a quick kiss with Gloria \u2013 but there was only one other person with whom I needed to have a serious talk. And the bitch of it is that it was probably <u>nothing</u> compared to the talk I\u2019m going to have to have with her tonight.<br /> <br /> Oleander sat alone at her usual table and threw me a dazzling smile as I approached. I\u2019d seen her talking with Calamity earlier, so it didn\u2019t actually surprise me when she said \u201cI understand we\u2019ll need a rain check for our usual date night, eh Angel?\u201d<br /> <br /> I grimaced. \u201cI\u2019m so sorry, sweetie\u2026 believe me, I\u2019d much rather spend the evening with you\u2026\u201d It seemed impolitic to mention the hot Latina biker chick I\u2019d been lusting over for most of the afternoon, so I let it lie.<br /> <br /> She leaned in and kissed my nose. \u201cCalamity explained the situation to me; I understand. I can\u2026 if you want me to, I can take another day away from my research and come back tomorrow\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course I want you to,\u201d I said fervently, giving her a smile. \u201cLook, I promise I\u2019ll keep tomorrow night free, okay? If you can make the time to be here\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cI\u2019m non-toxic right now, so all I have to do is put off injecting myself with anything interesting for another day. Not a problem. My\u2026 my <u>project</u> is coming along. Maybe not as quickly as I\u2019d like, but I am making progress\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know you can do it, honey,\u201d I said warmly. \u201cI have total confidence in your abilities. And if you ever need anything from me, all you have to do is ask\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> She gave me a squeeze, and we chatted about simple things for a few minutes. I confess that I unloaded a bit on her\u2026 I didn\u2019t spill state secrets or anything, I just sort of let her know that the responsibility had been weighing on me, and that the stress was starting to affect my performances.<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t worry, Angel,\u201d she said when I brought this up. \u201cOn your worst night, you\u2019re still better than anyone else I\u2019ve ever seen\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> The sheen must have shown in my eyes, because, she sort of sighed and looked slightly panicky. \u201cDid I do that wrong? That was supposed to be a compliment. I know I\u2019m not very good at being romantic\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I leaned in and kissed her. After we separated, I did my best to reassure her. \u201cI think you\u2019re <u>very</u> good at being romantic,\u201d I said. \u201cYou always seem to know <u>just</u> what to say to make me feel better.\u201d<br /> <br /> Before we parted, she gave me a gift. Reaching into her handbag, she pulled out a syringe and a small bottle. \u201cIf you get into bad trouble, Angel,\u201d she told me softly, \u201cinject someone with this. It will make their bones grow long, sharp thorns. It should be enough to take them out of whatever fight you\u2019re in. If you want to end the effect, force them to swallow this,\u201d she handed me a single pill out of the bottle. \u201cIf you give it to them within the first minute, they should recover.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHow long does the effect last?\u201d I asked, feeling slightly nauseous.<br /> <br /> She thought about it. \u201cThe thorns will quickly start to pierce their organs; after that the question is moot.\u201d<br /> <br /> I chose to focus on the positive aspects of the situation. \u201cThank you so much for looking out for me, sweetie,\u201d I said, <u>very carefully</u> stowing the syringe and pill in my purse and leaning in to give her a kiss. We said our \u2018til next times after that, and I sort of loitered around the exit chatting with D, waiting until Caoimhe showed up so that we could all head into L.A. together.<br /> <br /> Calamity approached me before then with a serious look on her face. I thought I knew what she was going to say, but she surprised me big-time. \u201cLori,\u201d she said soberly where nobody could overhear us, \u201cI talked to Oleander a little while ago, and she\u2026 said some things. I thought you should hear about it.\u201d<br /> <br /> I\u2019m sure I blinked a couple of times at that. \u201cOkay,\u201d I said, \u201cwhat sort of things?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell,\u201d Calamity began, \u201cI was talking with her about tonight\u2019s mission\u2026 trying to let her know that it was my fault the two of you weren\u2019t going to get your usual Saturday night together. And Rosalita and Kathy came up in the conversation, and I mentioned maybe helping Luther out with those gangsters in his neighborhood. I told her that I was trying to make sure I only did violence for the greater good.\u201d<br /> <br /> I\u2019d heard it before, so I just nodded.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, she said some things that made me think. She told me that it was kind of a slippery slope\u2026 that even if violence is committed for a good reason, it can be damaging to one\u2019s sanity. So that gave me pause\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled. \u201cI\u2019m glad to hear that,\u201d I admitted.<br /> <br /> \u201cBut then she started talking about how damaging your sanity could be dangerous to the people closest to you, and how you have to keep a tight rein on that sort of thing to avoid hurting those people\u2026 unless things had gotten to the point where a great sacrifice was necessary to protect the ones you love, at which point your sanity doesn\u2019t matter anymore.\u201d<br /> <br /> She looked helplessly at me. \u201cLori\u2026 I don\u2019t think she was talking about me there at the end\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> So there we have it. Of course it didn\u2019t take me long to figure out what that little speech meant. My sweet Oleander is close to completing the toxin for use against Hollywood, and she\u2019s convinced that she\u2019s going to have to deliver it <u>personally</u>. She doesn\u2019t expect to survive the experience, but she\u2019s willing to do it to protect me and everyone else in this Freehold. So she\u2019s taking risks in developing the toxin\u2026 doing things which could damage her Clarity. And she\u2019s convinced that she\u2019s doing it for the greater good.<br /> <br /> I may be off when it comes to some of the specifics, but I\u2019m convinced that the above paragraph is at least close to the truth of the matter. I couldn\u2019t breathe for a second. I couldn\u2019t meet Calamity\u2019s eyes. I turned away. \u201cI need a minute,\u201d I said as I started to walk away.<br /> <br /> Her hand landed gently on my shoulder, carefully placed so as not to risk cutting me. \u201cLori\u2026 are you okay? Was it something I said?\u201d<br /> <br /> I turned back to her and forced a smile, though my vision was pretty shimmery by that point. \u201cI\u2019ll be okay. Thank you for telling me, Calamity. I just\u2026 I need a few minutes to compose myself, okay? I\u2019m going up to my bedroom\u2026 I\u2019ll get ready to go while I\u2019m up there. Come find me when Caoimhe gets here, please.\u201d<br /> <br /> So I retreated to my bedroom, shut the door, and started to cry. I hadn\u2019t been at it long when Marguerite found me and asked me what was wrong. As she\u2019s one of the two other people in the motley who know what Oleander is actually doing for the Freehold, I felt like I could talk to her. I tried to keep my composure as I hastily gave her the basics of what Oleander had said, and my beliefs as to what that signified.<br /> <br /> She held me, and did her best to comfort me. \u201cWe will not allow this to happen,\u201d she assured me. \u201cWe will save her. If nothing else, you can order her not to sacrifice herself, non?\u201d<br /> <br /> I shrugged. \u201cI\u2026 don\u2019t like giving orders to\u2026 to people who are close to me. And\u2026 well, usually, with Oleander, all I have to do is ask, or even just<u> hint</u>, and she tries her best to please me. But this time\u2026 I\u2019m not sure if even an order will be enough.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe will save her,\u201d Marguerite said again, stroking my feathers in a comforting way. \u201cYou will not be alone in this, Juliette. We will all help, and we will save her.\u201d<br /> <br /> I let the tears flow freely, and I held her, and I kissed her, and I think I eventually got around to thanking her once my wits had returned to me. Once I\u2019d regained my composure, she bade me adieu and returned to the others downstairs. I touched up my makeup and put on some traveling clothes (a leather jacket, a tight red top, and black miniskirt, fishnets, and boots). I was just heading downstairs when Calamity came to meet me.<br /> <br /> \u201cEverything okay?\u201d she asked, concerned.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m dealing,\u201d I replied. \u201cSorry to worry you.\u201d<br /> <br /> So Calamity, Becky, Jacob, Caoimhe and I piled into the van and headed for L.A. just after midnight. Calamity explained along the way that we\u2019d be parking in the lot of a large club, where our \u201cclients\u201d would be waiting for us in a limousine. Two of us would be allowed to meet with them directly in the limo, though the rest would be able to listen and contribute to the conversation over those Bluetooth headset thingummies.<br /> <br /> And that\u2019s just what happened. Calamity and Jacob went into the Limo (mostly because Becky refused to allow herself to be separated from me, I think) and got the whole story from an important-looking vampire in a suit who called himself Uncle Peng (Kathy, or \u201cWhite Bone Princess,\u201d was there too). They wanted us to enter the nearby club, then descend to the secret club <u>beneath</u> that club, seek out a creature named Da Ji, and put an end to her. They were willing to pay us $125,000 for this\u2026 or $1,000,000 if we could do it without damaging the club or involving the authorities.<br /> <br /> Calamity and Jacob were a little wary of this deal\u2026 it seemed a fairly large sum for what we were being asked to do. (Or is it? How much do people pay to contract-kill demons these days? What\u2019s the going rate for that sort of thing?) Peng gave us a few more hints as to the nature of the beast\u2026 namely that she styles herself as a nine-tailed fox, a powerful malevolent spirit from Asian mythology. He also told us that it often seems that there are multiple versions of her wandering the club, and that it would be part of our job to determine which of them was the real Da Ji.<br /> <br /> And so began the evening\u2019s adventure. Kathy led the five of us into the crowded dance club, and we quickly made our way across the floor to an unmarked door between the restrooms. On the way, I bumped hard into someone. When I turned to apologize I found myself gazing into the hooded and cloaked chest of Mr. Gone. \u201cCan I help you with something, Your Majesty?\u201d he asked, a hint of annoyance creeping into his voice.<br /> <br /> \u201cSorry,\u201d I said, flustered. \u201cI\u2026 dropped your name a few times earlier today while speaking with Ms. Gold about the matter we discussed last night. I thought it might help to loosen her tongue a bit when Boss Lowjack\u2019s people question her. I didn\u2019t mean to inconvenience you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAh, I see,\u201d he replied. \u201cI\u2019ll just be off, then.\u201d And he faded away into the crowd.<br /> <br /> The mysterious doorway led to a small room containing a short stairway leading down to the <u>real</u> club. We had been told that the place catered to supernaturals, specifically Kindred and \u201cYao Guai,\u201d as they call changelings. We saw a number of representatives of both camps last night, as well as a variety of mortals. I didn\u2019t get the sense that anyone was there against their will. Apparently some mortals really get off on it when vampires feed off of them. Go figure.<br /> <br /> The club itself was\u2026 red. I mean, like <u>really</u> red. Lush red carpeting covered many of the floors. Red draperies covered the walls and hung from the ceiling, stirring slightly with the air currents. The furniture was red. Everything was lit by red-tinted lights. There were rooms with aquariums filled with exotic fish, and the red lighting made it look like they were swimming in thin blood. I\u2019m sure it was a perfect example of vampire-chic, but honestly the overall effect was a little nauseating to me.<br /> <br /> Oh well\u2026 at least my top matched the d\u00e9cor.<br /> <br /> We were led to a lavish sitting room and asked to wait while our hosts ascertained whether Da Ji would consent to meet with any of us. Kathy translated most of this, as many of the Kindred and changelings present spoke primarily in an Asian dialect with which I was entirely unfamiliar (I think it might have been Thai, but that\u2019s just guesswork based on what I\u2019ve gleaned from various menus over the last couple of years).<br /> <br /> At one point a darkly beautiful changeling woman entered the room and beckoned to me coyly, implying that she would like to spend intimate time with me. I glanced over at Becky, who sort of rolled her eyes, and declined as politely as I could. The fae woman sidled up closer, leaned down, and whispered in my ear at that point. \u201cYou are seasonal,\u201d she said in thickly-accented English. \u201cThis is not your territory. We need to talk privately\u2026 <u>now</u>.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded in understanding, then gestured to Becky. \u201cMy guardian?\u201d I asked simply. Becky stood up and drew nearer to me.<br /> <br /> The fae woman seemed to consider, glanced at my crown, and nodded. She strode from the room, beckoning that we should follow. She led us to one of the oddest boudoirs I\u2019ve ever seen. The floor seemed to be a thick pane of glass, under which flames were burning brightly. The floor was warm, but not as painfully hot as it should have been.<br /> <br /> The woman \u2013 whose name turned out to be Malai \u2013 sat on the bed in the center of the room and looked me up and down. \u201cWhere did you come from, and what are you doing here?\u201d she asked bluntly.<br /> <br /> I nodded to her. \u201cMistress Lorelei of the Spring Court, from the Lady by the Sea Freehold,\u201d I introduced myself. I held a hand out to indicate my companion. \u201cBecky Wan, Claviger of the Spring Court.\u201d<br /> <br /> Malai raised an eyebrow. \u201cNot from Hollywood, then?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo,\u201d I said with some finality. \u201cAnd we\u2019re here hunting a demon on behalf of some of your business partners.\u201d<br /> <br /> Her eyes widened. \u201cDa Ji?\u201d she asked. \u201cShit! Best of luck,\u201d she said wryly.<br /> <br /> \u201cLook, we\u2019re not here to step on anyone\u2019s toes,\u201d I said in what I hoped was a soothing voice. \u201cPart of our mandate on this little excursion was not to disrupt the activities of the club any more than absolutely necessary. And I\u2019m sorry to show up here unannounced; we weren\u2019t aware that any changelings were involved in this place until we got here.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay, I got it,\u201d Malai said after a moment. There was a bit more banter\u2026 some of which included the not-so-subtle suggestion that we use the bed to prevent people from speculating as to the reason for our little meeting. In the end I declined, deciding that it was more important to get back to my friends.<br /> <br /> I returned to find Kathy negotiating with an androgynous person in a smart suit to determine how many of us would be allowed into an audience with Da Ji. Calamity was having fun with one of the serving girls, tugging on a short length of rope which was attached to her collar whenever she wanted to freshen up her drink. The girl seemed into the game, so I can\u2019t really fault her for taking advantage of the situation. There was a part of me that longed to revel in the desire and lust of that place too\u2026 I think something about it was bringing out all of our darker urges.<br /> <br /> They had really good bourbon, though.<br /> <br /> Anyway, eventually it was declared that Da Ji would speak with two members of our party, and we were left trying to decide who should meet with her. As both the highest-ranking member of our party (politically speaking, at least) and our resident social butterfly, you\u2019d think I would have been a shoe-in for that job, but \u2018twas not to be. See, I can\u2019t go into a potentially dangerous situation like that without my Claviger present\u2026 which would have precluded anyone else from sitting in. So in the end, once more, it was Calamity and Jacob who ended up in the hot-seat and took on the burden of meeting our unknown opponent. <br /> <br /> Caoimhe, for her part, was starting to rethink the whole undertaking, and let us know quietly that she thought we should cut our losses and get out while we still could. I was inclined to agree at that point\u2026 one of the monarchs from a neighboring Freehold getting involved in something which might damage a prominent Night Court establishment could cause trouble for the Lady by the Sea. I asked Calamity and Jacob to exercise caution, but told them both that I trusted their judgment. And I had the syringe Oleander had given me in my purse if things got ugly.<br /> <br /> Now, I will confess that I don\u2019t know the first thing about what went down in that meeting\u2026 all I know is that Calamity and Jacob came out of it about half an hour later in agreement that pursuing the contract on Da Ji would be a bad idea. Something about how there were nine of her, and one of them wasn\u2019t even on the premises, and we\u2019d have to kill all of them before she regenerated any of them\u2026 it was this whole big thing. But if <u>Calamity</u> of all people decides that trying to kill someone is a bad idea, I tend to accept her judgment on that.<br /> <br /> We had no idea how long Jacob and Calamity were going to be in their meeting, and there\u2019s only so much you can do in a club like that without succumbing to its \u2018charms,\u2019 so when a commotion started up in the hallway outside of our little waiting room, I sat up and took notice. A number of security guards were rushing past the door, along with Malai and another changeling I didn\u2019t recognize (he looked like a vaguely humanoid shaggy beast with a skull for a head). I asked Kathy what was going on, and she inquired on my behalf. It turned out that a small group of people were in the club upstairs, and they were looking for someone, and they were making trouble. Like, \u2018call the police\u2019 levels of trouble.<br /> <br /> My heart dropped like a stone when I heard that. \u201cWho are they looking for?\u201d I asked with a sigh.<br /> <br /> Kathy posed another question to one of the security guys outside, and then turned back to me, her expression carefully blank. \u201cThey appear to be seeking an attractive blonde woman with wings,\u201d she deadpanned.<br /> <br /> \u201cJesus wept,\u201d I muttered under my breath. \u201cLook, I\u2019m sorry about this. If you\u2019ll let me up there, I\u2019ll try to defuse the situation before it gets any further out of hand\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Kathy relayed this, and one of the security guys started shaking his head vigorously. Mr. Skullhead, though, looked me up and down and laughed contemptuously. \u201cI\u2019d like to see these guys try to stop you from doing whatever the hell you want,\u201d he said good-naturedly. \u201cC\u2019mon, let\u2019s see what\u2019s going on up there.\u201d<br /> <br /> I followed him down the hall and up the stairs with Becky in tow. Caoimhe opted to wait for the others, and I asked her to let them know where I was and what I was doing. Mr. Skullhead led the way, occasionally moving security guards out of the way as if they were chessmen, and then held the door to the dance hall open with an \u201cafter you\u201d gesture. I walked out of the stairwell and into the back of a mob.<br /> <br /> Okay, I\u2019m overstating. But everyone was leaving the club in a big group, making it really hard for anyone to actually move. I glanced over at Becky, who gave me an \u201cI got nothing\u201d shrug, and then did something I\u2019ve always wanted to try. I raised myself up with all the authority I could muster, and just started walking forward with a purpose. And you know what? It worked! People who saw me coming practically stumbled to get out of my way, which caused a sort of peristaltic motion in the crowd as a whole. It just\u2026 parted for me, and soon I found myself in the open air\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026being blinded by flashing blue and red police cruiser lights. So much for deescalating the situation before it got out of hand. I found Uncle Peng speaking to the officer who seemed to be in charge of the situation. Well, that and yelling at his chauffeur, who had apparently allowed the troublemakers to drive off in Peng\u2019s limo\u2026 which contained the payment he had promised Calamity in return for killing Da Ji. Once he had disentangled himself from the authorities, I pulled him aside and let him know that we could probably recover the limo as soon as Calamity emerged from the club.<br /> <br /> That happened about five or ten minutes later. Calamity spoke to Peng briefly, while Jacob and Caoimhe made a bee-line for me and Becky at the van. I gave Calamity the quick and dirty version of the evening\u2019s events when she joined the rest of us, and she invoked the Contracts of Oath and Punishment with an air of resignation, and climbed into the driver\u2019s seat. \u201cThey\u2019re not far,\u201d she said as we pulled out onto the street.<br /> <br /> \u201cNot far\u201d turned out to be a dilapidated building a couple of miles away. An old man sat on the front stoop, grinning toothlessly and holding a hand-made sign which read \u201cIt\u2019s not a crack house, it\u2019s a crack home.\u201d The limo was nowhere in sight. I looked at Calamity doubtfully, but she insisted that the troublemakers were inside.<br /> <br /> \u201cHello?\u201d I called out with some trepidation as we stepped into the building\u2019s front room. I caught snippets of whispered conversation from nearby, but couldn\u2019t make out more than one word in three (though I could have sworn I heard a female voice indignantly tell one of the others to \u201cput that crack back where you found it!\u201d).<br /> <br /> I sighed. \u201cLook, it\u2019s obvious that you three have something you want to say to me. Why don\u2019t you come out here so we can discuss this situation like civilized people?\u201d<br /> <br /> They shuffled out into the entranceway looking a bit sheepish. And yes, it was the same three from the previous night\u2026 the old man in the shabby suit, the muscular young guy with the soulpatch and the guns, and the busty young blonde with the amazing blue eyes.<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay, what\u2019s this all about?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> The older guy fell to one knee. \u201cHow may we serve you, oh Divine One?\u201d he asked.<br /> <br /> I think I responded with a witty rejoinder along the lines of \u201cW\u2026 what?\u201d<br /> <br /> The blonde took up the thread at that point. \u201cYou\u2019re clearly here on Earth doing God\u2019s work, like Michael Landon, and we want to help you!\u201d she said with obvious enthusiasm.<br /> <br /> I blinked a few times, vaguely conscious of the fact that a giggling Caoimhe was recording the whole scene on her phone, until something the girl had said penetrated. \u201cMichael Landon? From <u>Little House on the Prairie</u>?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> She shrugged. \u201cI dunno; I never watched it. I think he was on <u>Touched By An Angel</u> or something, though. One of those shows about angels doing God\u2019s work on Earth.\u201d<br /> <br /> The older man said something under his breath that sounded like \u201c<u>Highway to Heaven</u>,\u201d but offered up no further commentary.<br /> <br /> \u201cBut, umm\u2026 I\u2019m not an angel,\u201d I said, feeling absurdly apologetic about that fact.<br /> <br /> Three slightly out-of-sync variations on \u201cyes you are!\u201d bombarded me from all quarters.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, I\u2019m not!\u201d I protested. \u201cLook, it\u2019s true that I\u2019m\u2026 I\u2019m not like other people, but I\u2019m not divine. I\u2019m just a regular girl trying to do the best I can\u2026 just like you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAh, I see,\u201d the older man said with an infuriatingly knowing wink. \u201cYes, of course. Just a normal girl. And no one shall hear any differently from us.\u201d<br /> <br /> Okay, so it became obvious at this point that I wasn\u2019t going to convince them of the truth with logic. Caoimhe was snickering behind me, and I got the impression that the others were only just holding it in. I decided that the time for subtlety was over.<br /> <br /> \u201cAlright, fine,\u201d I intoned, spreading my wings and drawing myself up to my full height. \u201cYou have passed the test. Your faith shall be rewarded. I am indeed an agent of the Divine Work, and I may well have need of your talents ere long. But we must be cautious; for the Enemy has spies everywhere\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m not afraid of them!\u201d the young guy said, drawing a pistol from the waistband of his pants.<br /> <br /> I gave him a sad smile. \u201cBut they might seek to strike at you through those you hold dear,\u201d I explained. \u201cSo it is important for now to maintain our secrecy. We must not act too soon. Please, my friends, return to your homes. I will call for you when I have need of you.\u201d<br /> <br /> They gave me awed looks and solemnly agreed to return to their homes and lie low until they heard from me. I am\u2026 not na\u00efve enough to believe that this will be a permanent solution, but hopefully I\u2019ve bought myself some time with that little bit of theater. I took their names and contact information, and asked them where they had stashed the limo. It was only a couple of blocks away, and Calamity set off to reclaim it, asking us to meet her back at the club.<br /> <br /> Okay, so my (sigh) loyal followers include:<br /> <br /> Charles Nelson Grissom, a septuagenarian religious fanatic who is convinced that the Rapture is imminent, and that he must prepare for the Glorious Ascension\u2019s arrival by shedding all of his worldly possessions (most notably his clothes).<br /> <br /> Robert Stanley Palmer (who prefers to be called Stan), an ex-military anarchy enthusiast with a chip on his shoulder the size of Montana. He goes everywhere armed, and seems willing to act violently with only the slightest provocation.<br /> <br /> And Kellie Ann Flowers, a positively <u>adorable</u> blonde stripper originally from Washington State. She seems to be the most stable of the trio, but she\u2019s way too willing to believe in things. Not just believe them, but believe in them. Still, she\u2019s a real cutie-pie\u2026 and there but for the grace of God goes one Juliette Wells, if my life had gone a little differently.<br /> <br /> Their cars were nowhere near us at that point, so I ordered them an Uber. Once they were gone, the rest of us took the van back to the club (the homeless guy waved us a cheerful goodbye as we left) and met up with Calamity. Uncle Peng offered to give Calamity $500 for returning his limo (the cash was still inside), but she turned it down, telling him that we had done this favor as a courtesy since we were not able to complete the task for which we were originally brought in.<br /> <br /> It was about three o\u2019clock when we started back for the Dream House. I called Maria, knowing that she would still be awake, and she picked up on the third ring. \u201cHey babe,\u201d she said, somehow sounding exhausted and worried at the same time. \u201cEverything okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe\u2019re okay,\u201d I assured her. \u201cThe demon hunting didn\u2019t go as planned, but nobody\u2019s hurt and we\u2019re heading home now. If you four aren\u2019t too tired, maybe I can join you for a little bit when we get back.\u201d<br /> <br /> She yawned. \u201cWe\u2019re pretty wiped out now, but I\u2019m sure we\u2019ll perk up when you get back.\u201d<br /> <br /> I paused before going on. \u201cD, I need to tell you something, but you have to promise not to laugh.\u201d<br /> <br /> She thought about it for a second, and I could hear her smirk. \u201cNo can do, babe,\u201d she said with relish. \u201cI don\u2019t make promises if I don\u2019t know whether I can keep them. Not to you. Not ever.\u201d The obvious sincerity of this statement helped to offset her infuriating refusal.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll take that as a yes,\u201d I said obstinately. I then launched into a description of our meeting with my three biggest fans. I wasn\u2019t even halfway through before the giggles started, and she was at full gale-force laughter before much longer. \u201cYou promised!\u201d I groused when she could hear me again.<br /> <br /> \u201cI did not!\u201d she retorted. \u201cSo those three weirdoes think you\u2019re an angel, and they won\u2019t accept any other explanation, huh? And you just played it up? Figures\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI couldn\u2019t think of any other way to get them out of there, okay?\u201d I said. \u201cThey weren\u2019t listening to reason; even I couldn\u2019t talk them out of their delusion. At least this way I got them to leave us alone for a while\u2026 I bought us some time to think about how to deal with the situation.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHey, I\u2019m not criticizing you, babe,\u201d D said with a chuckle, \u201cspare me your almighty holy wrath, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> I sighed with resignation. \u201cLook\u2026 it\u2019s been a stressful evening, and I could use some help unwinding. Think you and the others will be up for it? I should be home in another fifteen minutes\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe\u2019ll be waiting in the kitchen,\u201d Maria promised. \u201cI\u2019ll make sure everyone\u2019s got a little snack ready for you, so you can help us out with the poofing.\u201d<br /> <br /> And so the evening went. For a while it seemed like Caoimhe might join us \u2013 I pepped her up with contracts along with the others \u2013 but she declined in the end, stating that she wanted to make sure she was properly groomed and prepared before hopping into bed with us. So I accepted a rain check from her and contented myself with the company of my wife, my brides, and the lovely Rosalita, after I had given them all a little energy boost.<br /> <br /> We wore each other out all over again, of course. It doesn\u2019t take long to run through a lot of energy when you\u2019re with someone like Rosalita. She\u2019s very forceful, and likes to have things her own way. I think D in particular really enjoyed her company, though the rest of us had no complaints either.<br /> <br /> So here I sit, tired and achy and once again separated from a tangle of lovers\u2019 limbs by a few feet as I record the night\u2019s events in this diary. It\u2019s certainly been a night for unprecedented occurrences. I saw the inside of an exclusive club run jointly by vampires and changelings. I saw the Night Court\u2019s most feared enforcer summoned by nothing more than the repeated use of his name. I saw Calamity exercise discretion and back down from a fight she knew we couldn\u2019t win. And I saw three disturbed people fall on their knees in reverence as they called me an angel.<br /> <br /> And may God forgive me for the little thrill I felt when that happened\u2026<br /> <b><br /> Lorelei de la Rocha<br /> </b><br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Come to find out there is more than one kind of demon in the world. Who knew? Not us obviously. The evening started like normal, with a show. Lori, Calamity and Insincere Marguerite did really well as always. Then they did their socializing thing. Insincere Marguerite wore an interesting pink outfit with oversized sunglasses and an old transistor radio playing 60\u2019s music. Lori wore the outfit from her performance, complete with visible wings. Lori talked to several people, and it all seemed to go well until she talked to Calamity, who moments before had been talking to Oleander. Not sure what was said but Lori left that conversation upset and went upstairs, presumably to her bedroom. For my part I talked to Molly and found out that she had followed the trio of people from L.A. and found out where they lived. She also found out that the woman doesn\u2019t want the other two to know where she lives and they are all keenly interested in Lorelei. Molly said that they might take to following her around. They didn\u2019t show up tonight so I figured we had some time before they came around again.<br /> <br /> Caoimhe arrived after the show ended and we all piled into the van to go to the club where the demon was. It was me, Calamity, Lori, Becky and Caoimhe. It seems that the plan was to meet there and send two of our number to meet Kathy in the back of a limo. We talked amongst ourselves and decided on me and Calamity. So, we gave radio earbuds to our friends so they could listen in and climbed into the back of the limo. There was a man named Uncle Peng there as well. They explained what they knew of the demon. Her name is Da Ji and she styles herself as a nine-tailed fox. She can also make clones of herself, that don\u2019t necessarily look like her, so you never know if you\u2019re talking to her or not. Kathy, also known as the White Bone Princess, said that there would be kindred, mortals and Yao Guai (Changelings) in the club. It was not known how old Da Ji is or how many duplicates there would be. <br /> <br /> Once in the club we walked through the upstairs part and Lori actually bumped into Mr. Gone. Apparently because she had mentioned him several times during her conversation with Olivia Gold he just kind of showed up where we\u2019d be. She explained what happened and he left. We then went to a door at the back that led downstairs. The downstairs club was in all shades of red. The walls, carpets, even the lighting was red tinted. There were aquariums that had red tinted light shining through them too. It was all very surreal. Not long after we got there a tall Changeling woman approached Lori and propositioned her. Lori initially turned her down but then after the other woman whispered something in her ear she agreed and both her and Becky left with the woman. They retuned to our table a few minutes later, so nothing romantic happened, and Lori let us know that the club was half owned by Night Courtiers and the other woman, Malai, was just making sure that we weren\u2019t up to anything that might cause an incident. Lori explained that we were just there for Da Ji and Malai just said \u201cgood luck.\u201d<br /> <br /> While Kathy negotiated with Da Ji\u2019s representative to see how many of us could actually meet with the demon some of us got drinks. I just got a water. The club was making me feel a little on edge as it was and I figured that I better have my wits about me if I was going to be fighting a demon in a short while. Caoimhe got water as well while Lori got a bourbon and Calamity got some rum. The waitress then tied one end of a rope to the table and the other end to a collar around her neck. That way we could just pull her back when we needed her. Calamity seemed to have fun making use of that system when her rum was gone and she wanted to order a refill. It was decided that only two of us could go and meet with Da Ji, so Calamity stood up since she\u2019d been the one initially asked about this. After a bit of talking it was decided that I should go with her. Normally I\u2019d say Lori should have gone, but she would have needed to take Becky with her and that would add up to too many people. So I went with Calamity to meet the demon. We were shown into a room with beautiful Asian woman in make-up and an elaborate headdress. Some small talk was made but it was clear right off the bat that she knew why we were there. She eventually said as much. She offered to make a counter offer to the one we\u2019d been presented by Uncle Peng. Da Ji offered to not fight us and she would extend to us her friendship and her influence in Malibu. That send warning bells through my head as soon as she said it. She mainly tried to sweet talk Calamity with promises of breaking the chains that bound her and letting her be free to do as she pleased. The kind of scary thing was that it seemed that Calamity was kind of nodding along with the demon\u2019s suggestions. I know that Calamity does feel a little constrained. She has that oath that she took to work for the Winter King because she killed Mr. Grey. Da Ji tried to seduce me too, asking if she was the most beautiful woman that I\u2019d encountered. I deflected the question saying that I\u2019d leave her wondering about that. I think she knew from the beginning that I was not falling for her wiles the way Calamity was. After a few minutes of this Calamity used her contract to whisper in my ear that this was a fight that we could not win and that we should leave. She also said that there were nine copies of the demon and only eight of them were in the club. I agreed, and we eventually turned down her offers of alliance and made our way out of the room and back to the table.<br /> <br /> When we got out Lori and Becky were gone. They had apparently gone upstairs to deal with an issue, so Caoimhe, Calamity and I made our way upstairs. We had to get past security personnel that were trying to keep folks out of the upstairs part of the club. In fact, they had mostly cleared out the upstairs altogether. We managed though and made our way outside. We found Lori and Becky and caught up on what had happened. At least as much as we could in a short period of time. It turned out that the three crazies from L.A. followed Lori to the club tonight and came in specifically looking for her. They caused some chaos before leaving and stealing Uncle Peng\u2019s limo. With the payment inside. That\u2019s a lot of money and Peng was naturally upset. After he was done talking to the police officer on the scene we told him that we could track down his limo and bring it back. So, Calamity used her contract of oath and punishment to track down the trio. We found them at a crack house a few blocks away. The limo was not in sight, but we figured they\u2019d be able to tell us where the car was once we talked to them. Lori called out for them and they eventually came out of hiding. I think the younger guy, the anarchist, was picking up some drugs while he was there. Yeah, classy folks. They came out and were immediately deferential towards Lori. They kept going on about what her instructions were and the grand plan of heaven, or something like that. They honestly thought that she was an angel of god! It was kind of funny. I guess I can see it. Her wings were still openly visible to mortals throughout this whole situation. She had done that during her act and they were still there while she was confronting the crazies. She tried so hard to convince them that she was just a normal woman, but they didn\u2019t believe her. They obviously believed that she was an angel and wouldn\u2019t be persuaded. So, Lori ran with their delusion and told them all that she didn\u2019t have any plans for them right away but needed them to lay low for now. That the agents of the enemy were all around and she needed them to stay out of their sight for now. She said that she would have instructions for them later and got their contact information before they left. Lori also got the location of the limo before she let her devotees go. Calamity went after the limo and Lori called an uber to pick up the trio and take them home.<br /> <br /> On the way home Lori called De la Rocha and told her what happened. I could hear the laughter from where I sat. I think Lori\u2019s wife was rather amused at what happened with the trio tonight. Calamity on the other hand was still preoccupied. I know she had been expecting a fight and had geared up for that, but it didn\u2019t happen. No fight. No bloodletting. I know that she was disappointed. I was tempted to see if Calamity wanted to deal with some of the gangsters that were threatening Luther\u2019s neighborhood tonight just so she could get that fight that she so desperately wanted. I didn\u2019t though. It was too late and I figured that they\u2019d all be asleep. I also wasn\u2019t really sure that violence wasn\u2019t the best thing for Calamity tonight anyway. Da Ji really tugged at Calamity\u2019s strings and I think that she still had that on her mind as we were heading home. Maybe I should have insisted on going after some gangsters tonight. I know that Becky reflects back her lovers\u2019 wants and accommodates them. I don\u2019t want her to get hurt tonight because Calamity is in the mood for violence and Becky will take it no matter what. Hopefully Calamity will be in better control of her emotions and won\u2019t actually hurt her lover, no matter how consensual it is. <br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXX</i><br /> <br /> It\u2019s been a stressful time and I am still under the weather, so not much to add. But I or a player can answer questions. Da Ji is not a Demon in the Descent or Inferno Sense. Anything more is a spoiler. Comments and Questions are welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T05:57:36-08:00","id":1265251,"title":"","content":"Hope you feel better soon. Take whatever time off you need to rest.<br /> <br /> Anyone, please don't PM if I'm right, but I wish to speculate on the nature of Da Ji. Now, the simplest answer is that she's a Charlatan or some sort of ancient and evil Hob, but i think we are past the point in the story where that would be a satisfying answer.<br /> <br /> But, I've read bits of your Golden Eagle game journals, so I know that you all have a good grasp on Werewolf stuff. So I think she is some sort of spiritual phenomena related to foxes and sin. Perhaps an ancient and powerful Fox-Claimed, probably by a spirit who fed on essence related to the Kumiho legends. The ability to split could be a unique power. I believe there was some sort of minor template fox shifter in 1e who came from a special type of Claiming with ancient bound fox/mischief spirits<br /> <br /> Another theory is that she is some sort of Fox Host. That could explain the multiple bodies that are all connected. But what would a Fox Host do to the Gauntlet? Make burrows like the Beshilu? Poach spirits in the Hisil to shape the local emotional landscape? I don't see any obvious answers there.<br /> <br /> I would like to know the players' theories if I can","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T21:26:42-08:00","id":1265449,"title":"","content":"You have some excellent, logical ideas there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T13:58:14-08:00","id":1268626,"title":"","content":"A Dark gathering. A desperate battle. My goodness they have gotten powerful, haven\u2019t they?<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXXI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> I\u2019ll be honest, I\u2019m not really sure if I want to write this entry right now or not. I just\u2026 I don\u2019t even known how to feel. Sometimes I think the worst thing about being a monarch is that I have to know things I don\u2019t want to know.<br /> <br /> The day started off well enough. D and I got up early (I had to pep us both up again following our night with Rosalita and the rest of the family) and got showered and dressed up for church. We met Angelica in the parking lot\u2026 since she\u2019s a Christian, she\u2019s offered to take up the Claviger duties while I\u2019m at church so that Becky can sleep in on Sunday mornings. D came along this week so that there would be someone Angelica knew in the congregation (and to prevent any misunderstandings regarding Angelica from forming in the back of Dad\u2019s mind).<br /> <br /> After the sermon the three of us waited until the crowds thinned and then D and I introduced Angelica to Dad. He was, of course, pleased as punch to hear that the Freehold provides someone to look after my safety, and greeted her warmly. Once those pleasantries were out of the way, the three of us returned to the Dream House for Sex Breakfast. Becky took one look at my staid button-up shirt, plain grey skirt, ponytail and glasses, and asked wryly if I was actively <u><u>trying</u></u> to turn Angelica on.<br /> <br /> After breakfast \u2013 pancakes a la Calamity \u2013 we decided to split up for what promised to be a lazy afternoon. Calamity was working on some project of her own, Jacob took in a museum with Stasia and Elena, and D and I settled in for a lazy afternoon with our best gal-pals. Of course, as you can probably guess from the paragraphs above, a quiet day just wasn\u2019t in the cards.<br /> <br /> Things started off well enough\u2026 Gloria dropped by to hang out for a few hours before taking in our evening show. She greeted us all warmly (D and I got a kiss each), then passed along a message for me. Augustine wanted to talk to me at my earliest convenience regarding the motley\u2019s recent demon-hunting activities. As much as I would have liked to spend the rest of the afternoon lazing around with my wife, brides, girlfriend, and best friends\u2026 I didn\u2019t have anything actually <u><u>planned</u></u> for the day, so I figured I should probably attend to my queenly duties.<br /> <br /> Becky and I drove out to the church together. Just before we got there, we each received a text from Calamity; she and Jacob were heading out to the park to help Luna with something. I figured the three of them could probably handle just about anything those woods could throw at them, and didn\u2019t give the matter much further thought.<br /> <br /> Augustine greeted me warmly when I entered and ushered me back into his office. \u201cThank you for coming so quickly,\u201d he said after a moment. \u201cI hope you didn\u2019t regard my message as a summons\u2026 that wasn\u2019t my intent.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled as we shook hands. \u201cNot at all. I had a free afternoon, and was happy to come.\u201d<br /> <br /> We got down to business after that, and I told Augustine everything I knew about demons. Knowing what I do about the Viscount, I was careful to frame my descriptions in a certain way. He\u2019s both a military commander and a good Christian (and fellow Methodist), and finding out that there are actual <u><u>demons</u></u> in the world might cause him to take unnecessary action against them\u2026 and such actions might get good people hurt.<br /> <br /> In the end, I agreed to keep him apprised of the situation, which I figured couldn\u2019t hurt. I don\u2019t think he\u2019ll move against Da Ji; I tried to frame her as a very powerful supernatural creature rather than an actual demon. If he does decide that some action is necessary, I\u2019ll do what I can to talk him out of it, or at least get him to delay his plans until we\u2019ve worked through the mess with Hollywood. We don\u2019t need another front in this war right now.<br /> <br /> We chewed things over for a while, then Becky and I headed back to the Dream House. We couldn\u2019t raise Jacob, Luna, or Calamity on our phones, but we knew they would likely be out in the woods without reception so we didn\u2019t worry too much.<br /> <br /> That changed as time crept forward. Two hours before curtain we still hadn\u2019t been able to contact the three of them, and I was really starting to worry. I called up Kimberly to act as manager for the evening, and let Jacob\u2019s assistant know that he might be going it alone that night.<br /> <br /> Maybe an hour later, when I was nearly frantic with worry, I got a call from Calamity. I nearly sobbed with relief when her name came up on my caller ID. \u201cCalamity, is that you?\u201d I answered as quickly as I could. \u201cWhere are you? Are you all right?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s okay, Lori,\u201d Calamity said soothingly. \u201cLuna is hurt but she\u2019s stable; Jacob and I are fine. We\u2019re on our way back now\u2026 should just make showtime.\u201d<br /> <br /> I sighed, and let the tension drain from my body just a little bit. \u201cWhat happened?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> Her response both chilled my soul and warmed my heart. Over the course of the next few minutes, she told me how she and Jacob had arrived at the park entrance to find Luna pacing, obviously agitated and visibly upset. She told the two of them that a child had gone missing in the woods, and asked Calamity to use her tracking abilities to find the little girl. Calamity did so\u2026 and received a vision of the girl being led away by a tall, thin creature whose arms were draped in vines.<br /> <br /> None of them knew who or what this creature was, so they immediately rushed to the girl\u2019s aid. Luna flew the two of them out there as quickly as she could (she must be very strong\u2026 I\u2019m not sure I could still fly while carrying two fully grown adults). When they arrived, the situation became horribly clear\u2026 the creature was a Gentry, and it was attempting to Take the little girl. It had already created a Fetch to replace her.<br /> <br /> Calamity described the fight in full, but I\u2019ll just hit the highlights here. The three of them were able to surprise the Gentry, doing phenomenal damage to it before it realized they were coming. Luna attempted to get the girl away from the monster, but she fought back, punching and kicking and screaming that she didn\u2019t want to leave her \u201cnew friend.\u201d The Gentry attempted to flee while the Fetch guarded its flank, the latter spewing shards of glass at them from its open mouth. Calamity and Jacob both pounded the Gentry, giving it little opportunity to retaliate. Luna took the Gentry down with a parting shot as it opened a portal to the Hedge, and the Fetch didn\u2019t last long after that.<br /> <br /> Luna was the only one who was significantly hurt in the fight\u2026 but her wounds were severe. According to Calamity, most of those wounds were sustained while she attempted to shield the child from harm with her own body. I told Calamity that Becky, Kimberly and I would all be waiting for them at the Dream House, and that we would make sure Luna made a full recovery. Calamity thanked me, assured me once again that they were okay, and started to disconnect.<br /> <br /> \u201cCalamity,\u201d I said before she could do so. \u201cLook, I know I\u2019m not always the most supportive when it comes to you guys putting yourselves in danger. But\u2026 you guys did something <u><u>amazing</u></u> today. You spared that girl the Hell that we know all too well. Good work.\u201d<br /> <br /> I had Marguerite hold the opening curtain for a few minutes to accommodate our friends\u2019 arrival. Luna scowled as my courtiers and I descended on her. \u201cOh, all right, you can heal me, but don\u2019t make such a <u><u>fuss</u></u>,\u201d she grumbled as we saw to her wounds.<br /> <br /> Just after our regular M.C. opened the show, I walked out on stage (to thunderous applause, natch) and begged the audience\u2019s indulgence. \u201cI promise we\u2019ll get to the acts soon,\u201d I said with a grin, \u201cbut for now I\u2019d just like a moment of your time. I\u2019d like to recognize a few of our regulars. They were nearly late to the show tonight\u2026 because they were in a nearby park, assisting the authorities in searching for a missing child. They found the girl and stopped the <u><u>monster</u></u> who wanted to kidnap her. They don\u2019t want to be identified, so I\u2019m not going to use their names or anything like that\u2026 but I think they deserve a little recognition anyway. So let\u2019s take a moment to give them a round of applause, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> The response was deafening.<br /> <br /> I ran a quick substitution for my first solo of the evening\u2026 \u201cThese Dreams\u201d by Heart. It seemed appropriate, as we had a large contingent of Night Courtiers from L.A. in the audience that evening\u2026 like, a round dozen. Corvus, Corbin, Strype, V, Rosalita, Salk, the Handmaidens, Malai, the guy I was calling Mr. Skullhead (his real name is Grendel), an attractive Asian girl I hadn\u2019t met before named Tara, and a woman I hadn\u2019t met named Mari Lwyd (Marguerite assures me that this is the proper spelling\u2026 it\u2019s pronounced like \u201cMary Lloyd\u201d). The number went over very well, and our Nightly friends seemed to appreciate the lyrics. \u201cDarkness on the edge, shadows where I stand\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Marguerite joined the Night Courtiers when she could, bringing their number up to thirteen. Their shadows entwined and reshaped, occasionally acting out famous tableaus like the Last Supper, the climax of <u><u>Twelve Angry Men</u></u>, and a random orgy scene. Calamity and I also stopped by early in the evening for a round of introductions, and to see what brought so many L.A. Night Courtiers to our humble establishment.<br /> <br /> Turns out they were trying to come to some sort of consensus on the best way to deal with the Lady By the Sea. That\u2019s not a euphemism\u2026 they were actually trying to find a good way to coordinate their dealings with us to prevent future misunderstandings like the incident with T.J. the other day. Most of the powerful L.A. motleys were represented, excepting only those who were directly involved in the brawl at Rowan\u2019s place. Salk was there as a consultant, since he and Marguerite are well-known in our freehold and have the lay of the land.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, getting that many Night Courtiers to agree on anything is a trial to say the least. It seemed to me that they spent most of the evening verbally sniping at each other rather than discussing the matter at hand. And some of the barbs were pretty pointed, leading me to believe that it was more than just idle banter. Rosalita and her motley-mates <u><u>really</u></u> don\u2019t like Corbin, for example, and the animosity seems to be mutual (though that might just be a natural response to their hostility). More on that situation in a minute.<br /> <br /> I knew that the Night Court situation was the most politically significant thing happening in the club that night, but there wasn\u2019t much I could do about it until they came to some sort of a consensus, so I asked Marguerite to keep me apprised of the situation and wandered off to see to our other guests. Aside from the usual weekend suspects, the most notable of these was Siobhan. Calamity and I passed a few moments speaking with the unsettling emissary from Hollywood. She seems to have settled in nicely, and looked for all the world like someone who was simply out to enjoy a pleasant night at our club.<br /> <br /> Of course, I still don\u2019t trust the little eye-biter, but that\u2019s neither here nor there.<br /> <br /> I spent a lot of time at Oleander\u2019s table, mostly sitting in her lap, chatting about simple things and assuring her that she\u2019d have my complete attention once the Night Courtiers had figured out where they stood in regards to the Lady By the Sea. She seemed happy, and I don\u2019t think she picked up on the discomfort I felt at the thought of the conversation I knew we had to have later that night. She smiled and laughed while we talked, and she had that light in her eyes that nobody else ever seems to know is there.<br /> <br /> Calamity and I dusted off our \u201cBloody Creature Poster Girl\u201d number to show off for the out-of-towners, and it went over very well. She asked for a moment of my time as we were getting off-stage. Corbin had spoken with her earlier, and confessed that she was afraid that Rosalita was actually going to try to kill her. Calamity asked me to read Rosalita\u2019s desires to see if this was actually the case, or if Corbin was just being paranoid.<br /> <br /> I haven\u2019t often used the Contracts of Spring to invade people\u2019s privacy in that way, but I figured this would be for a good cause. Reading a specific desire \u2013 particularly one that the subject is trying to keep buried \u2013 is more difficult than just reading surface urges, but it can be done if one is determined. I had to put a lot of determination into the effort, but in the end I got it done.<br /> <br /> Corbin is right. Rosalita wants her dead. What\u2019s more, this wasn\u2019t just a passionate desire to do violence to someone she didn\u2019t like\u2026 she felt a righteous <u><u>need</u></u> to kill Corbin, and honestly seemed to feel that such an act would be justified. With a sigh