But I can\u2019t let you attack Corbin here.\u201d<br /> <br /> She started to protest, and I put a finger to her lips. \u201cThis is my <u><u>home</u></u>,\u201d I said. \u201cThis is the seat of the Spring Court in Malibu. I can\u2019t let you commit violence against another changeling here; not one who has been offered hospitality and sanctuary. A year ago, a changeling was attacked here\u2026 she wasn\u2019t hurt, but she was subdued, bound, and placed into custody. It took our reputation <u><u>months</u></u> to recover. I like you, Rosa, and I trust you when you say that something needs to be done about Corbin\u2026 but I need you to respect my wishes in this matter.\u201d<br /> <br /> She wasn\u2019t happy with my judgment, but she accepted it. \u201cOkay,\u201d she said a little sullenly, \u201cnot here.\u201d<br /> <br /> I gave her a thank you kiss and escorted her back to her table. I privately told Calamity about that little conversation, and I think she warned Corbin that Rosalita would be gunning for her. As horrible as it sounds, I have to keep reminding myself that as long as their grudge doesn\u2019t play out on my turf, it\u2019s none of my concern. I have enough to deal with trying to keep my own citizens safe.<br /> <br /> The show was over and the theater was starting to empty when Marguerite asked me to speak with her fellow Night Courtiers once more. They had at last come to a decision they could all live with. They wanted to appoint one of their number as a spokesperson, so that we\u2019d have a single point of contact within the L.A. Night Court; someone we could approach if unexpected trouble started or we needed to venture into L.A. unexpectedly (as we had when hunting Da Ji on the previous evening).<br /> <br /> They wanted someone unbiased to decide who the ambassador should be, and that duty fell to me. I considered the options before me. I obviously couldn\u2019t choose anyone from either the Unseelie Court or Rosalita\u2019s motley; the animosity between them was so great that neither group would accept a representative from the other. I found myself liking Grendel immediately, but I had just met him and Malai on the previous evening, so I didn\u2019t know much about them. Salk seems to be even-handed and level-headed, if perhaps a bit manipulative, but he spends most of his time in Malibu and Santa Monica, so he might not have the best sense of the L.A. atmosphere. The handmaidens\u2026 no. Just no.<br /> <br /> In the end I decided to go with V. I\u2019ve only met him a few times, but he\u2019s always struck me as being both fair and not easily rattled. He doesn\u2019t owe allegiance to any particular faction, and he\u2019s on relatively good terms with everyone. I don\u2019t know if I made the right decision, but I did the best I could, and for the moment I\u2019m reasonably pleased with the results. The present Night Courtiers seemed to agree with me, and the decision was unanimously ratified on the spot.<br /> <br /> With that taken care of, I made my way over to Oleander. \u201cHey, Angel!\u201d she said brightly as I approached. \u201cEverything taken care of? You want to head upstairs?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cActually,\u201d I said softly, \u201cwould you mind if we went back to your place tonight? I\u2019ll have to get up early tomorrow to sign into my online classes, but I\u2019d like a little privacy if you don\u2019t mind\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSure,\u201d she said, and we said our goodbyes and made our way to our cars. Half an hour later we were in her kitchen. She\u2019d put a bottle of wine out to chill, and was fussing with some incense when I spoke up.<br /> <br /> \u201cImelda,\u201d I said softly.<br /> <br /> She stopped dead, and didn\u2019t turn to face me. \u201cSomething wrong, Angel?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t know yet,\u201d I said. \u201cLook, honey\u2026 I\u2019m so glad to be here, and I really do appreciate everything you\u2019re doing to make tonight special. I promise we\u2019ll get back to our date night as soon as possible, but I need to talk to you about something important first, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded and turned back to me, all business. \u201cTrouble?\u201d she asked. \u201cIs it something to do with the\u2026 the project?\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cIn a way,\u201d I admitted. \u201cI\u2019ve been listening to you, and talking with Calamity about something you said last night. I\u2019ve been thinking a lot about the whole situation, and I need to ask you\u2026 Oleander, are you planning to deliver the toxin <u><u>personally</u></u>?\u201d<br /> <br /> She sighed and lowered her eyes. \u201cOnly if I have to,\u201d she said. It was almost a whisper.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou can\u2019t,\u201d I said immediately. I didn\u2019t plan to say it; it just slipped out. It wasn\u2019t an order from the queen; it was a childish negation\u2026 a scared little girl denying a hard truth she couldn\u2019t accept.<br /> <br /> \u201cJuliette,\u201d she said, looking me in the eye this time, \u201cI promise you that I\u2019m working on another solution. I don\u2019t want to die. For the first time\u2026 well, <u><u>ever</u></u>, I\u2019m actually <u><u>happy</u></u> right now. If I can find another way, a <u><u>better</u></u> way to deliver the toxin, I promise you that I\u2019ll use it. But if not, well\u2026 it\u2019s worth my life to keep you and the rest of the Freehold safe. If anything happens to me, you\u2019ll be alright\u2026 you have Maria\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t even,\u201d I snapped. \u201cYou think that just because you\u2019re not my <u><u>only</u></u> lover, I won\u2019t be devastated if you die? I love you, Imelda, and I\u2019m not just going to stand aside and let you put yourself at risk.\u201d<br /> <br /> She looked slightly abashed at that. \u201cI just meant\u2026 that you have people who can help you get through the tough times. Maria, Marguerite,