on of that sort would prove too much of a temptation.\u201d She looked me square in the eye when she said the next bit. \u201cLowjack is worried that he\u2019d have to put Dr. Twitchowicz down if something went wrong.\u201d<br /> <br /> I let out my breath and thought about it. I\u2019m sure Twitch would be able to help Oleander with her current endeavor, but I can\u2019t dismiss Lowjack\u2019s concerns. Maria would never forgive me if Twitch got hurt or killed because I pulled a few strings. Plus\u2026 I have a responsibility to consider the safety of the Freehold, and I can\u2019t say that John\u2019s fears about what Twitch might do if he got his hands on such a weapon are entirely invalid. But on the other hand\u2026 Maria has a lot of faith in Twitch, and she\u2019s been a really good influence on him. If she can try to keep him grounded\u2026 he might be able to help Oleander without risking his life and his soul.<br /> <br /> \u201cI have to think about it,\u201d I said after a moment. \u201cI can\u2019t promise anything. I won\u2019t try to go behind John\u2019s back or override his command on this. But I\u2019ll talk to him about it, and see if we can come up with a way to address his concerns.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cThank you, Angel,\u201d she said simply.<br /> <br /> \u201cJust let me say one more thing,\u201d I replied. \u201cI start college classes tomorrow. That\u2019s something\u2026 well, something I never even knew that I <u><u>wanted</u></u> before I was Taken. I might actually be a doctor someday. It\u2019s still years down the road, but\u2026 well, I\u2019m actually starting to think that it\u2019s going to happen now. I got that from you\u2026 well, you and Maria, mostly. You\u2019re so smart, Oleander, and\u2026 and you\u2019ve always believed that I\u2019m smart too. Maybe not as smart as you, but smarter than I\u2019ve ever given myself credit for. I don\u2019t know if I would have had the courage to apply to UCLA if it hadn\u2019t been for you. And eight or ten years down the line, when I\u2019m standing there receiving my license to practice\u2026 in my head it\u2019s always <u><u>you</u></u> that\u2019s standing there with me.\u201d<br /> <br /> She sighed and lowered her gaze. \u201cThat\u2019s not fair,\u201d she said softly.<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t care,\u201d I said, maybe a smidge petulant. \u201cI\u2019m not going to apologize for wanting you to live, Oleander.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m working on it, Angel,\u201d she said, pulling me into a tight embrace, \u201cI swear.\u201d<br /> <br /> So we put the heavy issues aside for the time being and tried to enjoy the rest of the evening. We drank the wine, gave each other massages, took a bath together while listening to music, and made slow, sensual love until about twenty minutes ago, when she drifted off and I started writing in this journal. I should be trying to sleep; I start my online general education classes in a few hours, and I have a Bio lab on campus on Tuesday morning. I know it\u2019s not healthy for me to keep relying on Spring contracts to stay awake and alert. But I have too much on my mind.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know if I can do it. I don\u2019t know if I can convince John to let Twitch help Oleander with her research. I don\u2019t know if I can ask Twitch to risk his soul in that way. I don\u2019t know if I can face Maria with this weighing on my soul. I don\u2019t if I can keep shouldering all of this responsibility while working at the Dream House and going to college.<br /> <br /> Most of all, when the time comes, I don\u2019t know if I can ask someone I love to sacrifice herself to save all of those I\u2019ve sworn to protect. I\u2019m begging you, God, please don\u2019t put me in that position. And if You do\u2026 please help me to do what\u2019s right.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei de la Rocha</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Well today certainly was a unique day. It started off with Sex Breakfast like usual. Calamity cooked pancakes for everyone while I made coffee. Then we all split off to do our individual things. Lori had a meeting with Augustine at his church, Calamity was working on a dream for someone \u2013 I think Dark Kimberly \u2013 and Luna was at work. I\u2019m not sure what the others were up to. I started off going to a museum with my sister. It\u2019s been awhile since we did something with one of her interests. Last time we went hiking. I thought checking out some paintings and maybe photographs if Stasia wanted to join us would be fun. My day got interrupted by a text from Luna. She said that it was important and that she needed help at the park. I apologized to Elena and Stasia and headed on over to the park where I met Calamity and Luna by the entrance. Luna was very straightforward. She held out a photograph of a little girl and a teddy bear toward Calamity and asked her if she could find the girl. She went missing while her family was hiking in the woods. Calamity quickly used her contract to find out where the girl was, and it was nowhere near us. She even got a glimpse of the girl and her surroundings and saw a tall man with vines all down his arms near her. Luna immediately grabbed Calamity under the arms and told me to hold onto her back. Then she took off into the sky and flew at quite a good clip through the woods to the location that Calamity was directing her towards. The trip was rather exciting and a little bit scary. I trust Luna with my life, so I knew that she wouldn\u2019t crash us into a tree or anything, but I still had my heart in my throat a good part of the way.<br /> <br /> When we got close we could tell that it was either a Gentry or a Loyalist attempting to take the child. There was also a fetch of the little girl next to the vine covered man. Well, we didn\u2019t need to discuss options to know that we needed to act right away and we did. Luna flew in fast, aiming above the