r somewhere to play. Eventually though we got her calmed down enough that she was not a flight risk anymore. While I was doing my best to calm down the child Luna used her radio to call in a helicopter to take us all back to the park entrance. I then gave Luna my hoodie to wear to cover up the blood on her clothes so her coworkers wouldn\u2019t worry overly much about her. She was going to be healed in a short period of time anyway, no need to worry them unnecessarily. Also, if they noticed how hurt she was then they would insist on taking her to the hospital and she would be forced to heal normally to avoid the questions raised by our Spring Courtiers contracts. Best to avoid all that if we could. Anyway, we got back to the entrance to the park and reunited the child with her parents. They were ecstatic and thanked us profusely. We had to say that the kidnapper got away but wouldn\u2019t be coming back any time soon to bother anyone else. We couldn\u2019t exactly explain that we shot him and he turned into a pile of vines. That would lead to questions and we didn\u2019t want to answer them. So, officially the would-be kidnapper got away and there will likely be future searches in the woods for him. They might have Luna patrol a little more frequently for a while. Not sure yet what the fallout from this is going to be.<br /> <br /> Once we had cell phone service again Calamity called Lori to give her a heads up that we were going to need healing when we got back to the Dream House. Calamity gave her the cliff notes version of what happened over the phone and then we headed back for the house. Lori, Becky and Dark Kimberly were there as well just in case. Lori healed Luna as much as she could and Becky finished up the job. Luna insisted that they not make a fuss over her, but I think Lori did a little bit anyway. After Luna showered and changed it was good to see the blood gone. I will admit that I felt bad that she\u2019d been hurt that badly in the first place. If I hadn\u2019t changed focus and tried to hit the Gentry then the fetch would have been dead before it could have hit my love with broken glass. I just really wanted to land the killing blow. I didn\u2019t land a final blow at all. At that point it was defensive and trying to escape back into the Hedge. I wanted to make sure that it didn\u2019t get back there, and thankfully Luna carries a gun as a matter of course. And you can go defensive all you want, you\u2019re not going to block or parry a bullet. They have a tendency to just go straight through the target.<br /> <br /> Lori was proud of all of us for helping to stop a Gentry from taking someone, so at the beginning of the show she announced to the crowd that three regular customers had helped save a little girl from a kidnapper but that they wanted to remain anonymous. We got a round of applause from the audience. It was nice.<br /> <br /> Then to make things more interesting almost all of the Night Courtiers from L.A. came to the club tonight. They filed en masse up to the balcony seats and took over a few tables up there. Insincere Marguerite spent as much of the evening as she could with them. She did her number and then went back upstairs. Even our new friends from last night came by. Malai, the woman that tried to seduce Lori, came by the bar and ordered drinks for everyone. I committed them all to memory and had my assistant help me make the drinks and deliver them. He dropped off his tray and went back down to the bar while I stayed up there and talked with the Night Courtiers a bit. It was mostly them trying to shock me with questions about whether or not one of them could go down on another one during the show. I said it would probably not be a good idea, especially when it was revealed one partner was particularly loud. I think they were expecting more of a reaction out of me and I was sorry to disappoint, but it just wasn\u2019t that shocking to me. I regularly go to something called \u201cSex Breakfast\u201d and there is frequently talk of sex, sex toys, and other fetishes. I\u2019m just not bothered by it. At one point in the night Corbin used a contract to whisper in my ear and apologize for the behavior of her friends and hoped that I didn\u2019t take anything personally. I couldn\u2019t reply back the same way so I just made sure to make eye contact with her from the bar and gave her a nod and a salute with a drink.<br /> <br /> Later in the evening Marguerite texted Lori to see if she would be willing to pick a liaison between our freehold and the L.A. motley\u2019s. Lori agreed and she, Calamity and I made our way up there. This was also Calamity\u2019s second and Lori\u2019s third visit to the Night Courtiers. Earlier Lori said that she had to \u201cread\u201d someone up there and offered to help me bring the refill of drinks up to them. She then talked privately to Rosalita. After all that though we went up to discuss who would be the liaison among the L. A. Courtiers. Lori considered for a few minutes and then suggested that V be the liaison. He agreed readily enough and the other Night Courtiers there all seemed to think that it was a good idea and gave their blessing as well. Shortly after that the Night Courtiers left and the three of us talked amongst ourselves for a bit. It turns out that the reason that Lori \u201cread\u201d Rosalita and then talked to her in private was because she had been making numerous threats to Corbin throughout the night. I caught a bit of it when I delivered drinks, but not all of it. According to Rosalita, Corbin has a history of torturing and killing innocent humans indiscriminately. The way it was described I\u2019m assuming that Rosalita knew one of the humans and wanted to take revenge on the other Night Courtier. Lori had told Rosalita not to attack anyone while at our club, so we could maintain our neutral status. Calamity warned Corbin that Rosalita was thinking of hurting her, so she would be on guard. I will admit that I don\u2019t know Corbin very well, so I don\u2019t know if she is actually guilty or not. Insincere Marguerite confirmed that there are rumors that she does things like that, but there is no proof as far as she can tell. If these are things that she did in the past and has since changed then I can\u2019t really judge her for that. Pot and Kettle and all that. If she is still doing it though, then that\u2019s different. She should not be allowed to continue doing whatever harm she might be engaging in.<br /> <br /> After everyone had left and we were getting ready to go to bed Luna apologized to me for putting me in danger this afternoon. I think she was feeling bad that she was the one to bring me into a confrontation with a Gentry. I told her not to worry about it, that I was happy to help. She said that she didn\u2019t want to lose me, and I reciprocated. I don\u2019t want to lose my Luna either. I still feel bad for not killing the fetch when I had the chance. I went after the Gentry instead, which was a mistake. If I had stayed focused then my Luna wouldn\u2019t have gotten hurt at all. The fetch wouldn\u2019t have had the opportunity to hurt her or anyone else for that matter. I think that Luna was affected by this whole deal because it was a child that was almost abducted. I can understand that. I have a soft spot for kids too. Things are so simple for them. It\u2019s fun to talk to them. They are so straightforward and almost blunt. They don\u2019t have the same verbal filters that adults do. They don\u2019t know that they need them. Anyway, Luna seemed particularly upset by the fight with the Gentry, so I assured her that I was fine and pointed out that we had the rare opportunity to stop a Gentry from taking someone to Arcadia. It\u2019s all fine and good to rescue people that had already been taken, like Missy and Jane, but to stop them from ever experiencing that in the first place feels good.<br /> <br /> It felt especially good to me to be a part of stopping the Gentry. I\u2019m glad that Luna contacted me and said that she needed help. I have a lot to make up for and being part of a group that stopped and killed a Gentry felt good to me. It feels like I have done something to make up for all the shitty things that I did when I worked for the Lady. It was also a little poignant. The last time that I stopped someone from taking an innocent to Arcadia was when I confronted Rook when he came looking for Diane. Diane will never know how close she came to being taken back to the Lady and I will always remember the look on Rook\u2019s face when he realized that I wasn\u2019t joking, that I was actually stopping him. That encounter ended in a fight too, but I didn\u2019t have any backup that time and I was already hurt. The odds were not great, but I took the shot anyway. I was not going to allow Diane to go back to the Lady. And today, I was not going to allow that little girl to be taken to Arcadia. She was so young too. She couldn\u2019t have been more than seven or eight years old. What the hell did a Gentry want with someone so young? I don\u2019t even want to think about that. I\u2019m just glad we saved her, even if she was annoyed with us for taking away her play partner. She didn\u2019t quite understand what I was trying to tell her and I didn\u2019t want to freak her out so I didn\u2019t keep going for too long after telling her what the vine man wanted to do. She seemed convinced that he was going to take her somewhere to play. I\u2019m wondering if that\u2019s why that Gentry preyed on children in the first place? Because they are more trusting and believe that the stranger has good intentions. Adults are more cautious and are harder to take. I should know. My targets tended to be older than the little girl. I would go after college students and sometimes High School seniors, but usually college students. I\u2019m not a big guy, so I couldn\u2019t overpower most of the people that I went after, so I had to trick them into coming with me. Some followed me because I was going to show them a great place to party. Others came to my aid when I said that I needed help to save a younger sibling or locate a lost camera. I always tricked them into going where I wanted them to go. One guy fought back when he realized what I was doing. It was not a great moment for me. He was stronger than I was and I had to resort to dirty fighting and liberal use of contracts to stop him from escaping. I eventually froze over the way out and managed to wear him down by making it colder and colder in the cave. The cold doesn\u2019t bother me, so I could make it as cold as I wanted until he gave up. That\u2019s why I don\u2019 t play tricks anymore. Doing stuff like that puts me too close to being Rime and I\u2019m determined to not fall that far ever again.<br /> <br /> Today I got the opportunity to foil the plans of a Gentry and help at least temporarily kill him. He\u2019ll be back, and he likely won\u2019t be happy. Hopefully he\u2019ll think twice about hunting in my Luna\u2019s forest again. I\u2019m not even certain if this was a Gentry that is known to come into this area or if he was someone new to the area, trying his luck hunting in our freehold. If he decides to come back though I\u2019ll be ready for him. I\u2019m more than willing to kill him again if that\u2019s what it takes to convince him that hunting in our territory is a bad idea. I\u2019ve killed Gentry before. I did so in the Lady\u2019s employ on two occasions. I suppose those are two incidents that I can still be proud of except for the fact that I was doing it on the orders of a mercurial winter queen. One of the Gentry that Rook and I took down was someone that had been trying to steal one of the Lady\u2019s Treasures. He almost succeeded. Then he died. When he came back he did not try again. The other Gentry was someone that had insulted the Lady personally. I\u2019m not sure what he said exactly but it was bad enough to warrant her summoning her two favorite Knights and having us hunt him down and murder him. And now I can add one more to the list of Gentry that I\u2019ve helped kill. The fight today was much easier than those past fights had been. But today we got lucky. The Gentry was focused on getting back to the Hedge with or without the little girl, so he didn\u2019t attack us. There was also more of us, and Luna had a gun. Never underestimate the destructive power of a handgun. In those past fights it was just me and Rook and our knives.<br /> <br /> I should tell Luna about those past kills. I should also thank her for the opportunity to help take down a Gentry. She may have been upset because I was in danger, but I was in the safest company I can think of. I had Luna and Calamity watching my back and they are two of the deadlier changelings that I know of. I\u2019m glad I was able to help. I think I would have been upset to have missed the fight, so I\u2019m glad that she contacted me when she did. I know that Elena and Stasia will understand why I needed to leave. I will tell my sister what happened later today when I get a chance. Not sure that I want to trust that conversation to a cell phone or email though. Maybe we can try the museum idea again. Or maybe they will come to the club? We\u2019ll see how it works out. And now it is time to sleep. It is later than I\u2019d like to be trying to fall asleep, but I just had to get those thoughts down on paper. Thing become more clear for me when I write them down.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXXI</i><br /> <br /> The Gentry they fought was actually beefed up from the one in Autumn Nightmares, but still spent most of the fighting having to dodge having lost most of their health from the surprise attack right at the start of the fight. Really trying to flee into the portal. There was just too much for him to deal with, especially being shot. The players enjoyed the high tension combat scene anyway.<br /> <br /> The Night Court was a menagerie of odd. All sort of bizarre and creepy appearances. I had fun with the background\u2026there were 13 with Insincere Marguerite there. Last Supper, or Blasphemous spin on Last Supper, was a favorite, along with eyes wide shut, Twelve Angry Aen, Annabelle Chong\u2019s record setting gang bang, etc.<br /> <br /> Most of the Night Courtiers had appeared previously. Tara and Mari Lwyd were new\u2026I think they were the only ones. Mari Lwyd has been in the game for years, just not actually, you know, appeared.<br /> <br /> Anyway, that is all I have for now but comments and questions are welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 11-18-2018, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-02T14:06:25-08:00","id":1272456,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to return to our harried friends in Malibu. Another unexpected development, this time not on the changeling side.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite covers the past two sessions in her eyes.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXXII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> I\u2019ll be honest with you\u2026 this is not how I saw my first day as a college student going.<br /> <br /> Okay, to be perfectly fair, in my pre-captivity days I never really saw myself as a college student at all; I mean, four more years of school (at least) after I\u2019d finally freed myself from that hated institution at long last? Who needed that? But now that I\u2019m back and dedicated to improving myself so that I can become a real doctor someday\u2026 well, this isn\u2019t exactly how I\u2019d pictured the events of my first day in higher education.<br /> <br /> How many freshman girls spend the night before classes start up a sleepless wreck? Well, probably a fair number of them, now that I think about it\u2026 but how many of those do so because they\u2019re afraid they might be forced to sacrifice one of their lovers to a massive inhuman monster in order to save the lives of those who have entrusted her with their safety? I\u2019m willing to bet that\u2019s a somewhat rarer breed.<br /> <br /> So it wouldn\u2019t be entirely accurate to say that I \u201cwoke up\u201d Monday morning, but I did gently extricate myself from Oleander\u2019s embrace when the alarm went off, quickly silencing it and telling her to go back to sleep. She muzzily promised to meet me back at the Dream House in a few hours for Sex Breakfast, and I got dressed, pepped myself up with contracts, and made my way home. Almost nobody else was up when I got there; just Calamity, on her way out the door to meditate at White Maria\u2019s place. She handed me a steaming cup of coffee, we exchanged pleasantries, and I planted myself in front of the laptop.<br /> <br /> So I took three online courses this morning, and will be returning for more every Monday, Wednesday, and Friday through the end of the semester (I\u2019ll be spending Tuesday and Thursday mornings on campus taking two science courses and one associated lab). It didn\u2019t take me all that long to watch the intro videos and join the course message boards, though that might just be because it was the first day of class.<br /> <br /> I placed out of most of the basic English, Math, and language requirements, so I\u2019m not actually that far behind. I\u2019m spending this semester taking care of a few of the other general education requirements, like World Literature and Social Sciences, and knocking out a few prerequisites, like Chemistry, Life Sciences and \u2013 sigh \u2013 Calculus. I can already tell that the latter is going to be my biggest challenge this semester, but my French Romantic Literature course looks like a lot of fun. Reading Dumas into the wee hours of the morning will make a nice change from perusing medical journals.<br /> <br /> I wrapped things up about twenty minutes before Sex Breakfast, so I made my way into the kitchen and started frying up some frozen hash browns. Calamity was the first to join me, and she cheerfully took over the cooking duties when my phone rang a few minutes later. A glance at the caller ID told me that the call was from my Dad, which surprised me a little.<br /> <br /> \u201cNot that it isn\u2019t a lovely surprise,\u201d I said by way of a greeting, \u201cbut to what do I owe the honor this Monday morning?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cJuliette,\u201d he said, and he sounded tired to me. \u201cGood morning. I hope you are well. I\u2026 I need to ask a favor of you, with the understanding that you are free to say no if you choose.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled fondly at his attitude. \u201cDad,\u201d I said, \u201cyou know I\u2019m always happy to help if you need me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you,\u201d he said, and it was nearly a sigh. \u201cI have a\u2026 houseguest. A young woman who has need of a safe place to stay for a while.\u201d He paused, and seemed to be working up his nerve to say the rest (I found it oddly endearing). \u201cShe is a vampire. A relatively young one, as I understand it. Her\u2026 mentor was recently killed, and her faction is politically unpopular in Los Angeles at the moment.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd you want her to stay here?\u201d I asked, curious.<br /> <br /> \u201cThere is more,\u201d he admitted. \u201cMy old comrades-in-arms, the Long Night, are searching for her. I fear they might know that I am offering her shelter. If they come for her, I would prefer they not find her here. I can deal with them if I have to, but I might not be able to protect her if they come in force\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAre you safe?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cI will be fine, Juliette,\u201d he said. \u201cMy concern is for Dakota.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll need to talk it over with the others,\u201d I said after thinking about it for a moment. \u201cI\u2019m not the only one who lives here, so I can\u2019t make the decision by myself. We\u2019re about to have breakfast, so I\u2019ll bring it up to the others and give you a call back in an hour or so, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> He sighed again. \u201cThank you,\u201d he said. \u201cOh, and\u2026 if I remember correctly, you have an\u2026 \u2018ability\u2019 which allows you to restore a person\u2019s flagging energy? If you could see fit to dropping by for a few moments regardless of your decision, I would be much obliged. I did not sleep last night.\u201d<br /> <br /> Heh. That makes two of us. \u201cOkay, no problem,\u201d I said. \u201cI\u2019ll call you after breakfast, and see you a little while after that. Take care of yourself, Dad. I love you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI love you too, Juliette,\u201d he said before he disconnected.<br /> <br /> Sex Breakfast was in full swing by the time I made it back to the kitchen, giving lazy hugs and kisses to my wife, my brides, my lovers, and the rest of my friends. As we ate, I related Dad\u2019s request to the others. We all agreed that we\u2019d like to help this \u201cDakota,\u201d but there were several complications. First, we didn\u2019t really have any extra rooms available\u2026 though Trinh quickly gave us the answer to that problem.<br /> <br /> \u201cLook, you guys have been really kind to me these last few weeks, and I\u2019ll never forget it. I hope to be moving into my own place soon anyway, and I\u2019ve imposed upon your charity for long enough. I\u2019ll give Monica a call and see if she can put me up somewhere for a few days.\u201d<br /> <br /> We were all quick to assure her that she didn\u2019t have to do that, but she was insistent that someone else should have the right to benefit from our generosity for a while. And, as she was staying in the basement guest room anyway, it seemed like the perfect place for us to house a fugitive vampire.<br /> <br /> Becky brought up another consideration. \u201cWho is she going to eat?\u201d she asked bluntly. This opened a huge can of worms, as it shone a light on how little we actually know about vampires and their habits. We have some contacts among L.A.\u2019s vampire population\u2026 but if Dakota\u2019s faction is as unpopular as Dad says, we don\u2019t want to tip them off to her presence with too many questions. We <u><u>did</u></u> know that most vampires prefer to feed harmlessly and anonymously, and as long as Dakota agreed to abide by those guidelines, I didn\u2019t see the harm of offering her asylum.<br /> <br /> Before calling my Dad I decided to take care of something else. I asked Maria if I could speak with her privately for a few minutes. I\u2019m not going to give a word-for-word account of the conversation that followed, but the long and the short of it is that I wanted to get her opinion on the idea of Twitch working with Oleander to attempt to find a safe way to deliver our toxin to the Grand Maw. After irritably asking me to call her friend \u201cAnton\u201d instead of \u201cTwitch,\u201d she had a lot of good advice on the subject.<br /> <br /> (Since it\u2019s obviously so important to Maria, I\u2019ve decided not to call her friend \u201cTwitch\u201d anymore\u2026 not even in my private diary. She has a point\u2026 the nickname is pretty derogatory, and it pokes fun at the poor man\u2019s vulnerability. So from here on out, he\u2019ll be Anton or Dr. Twichowicz within these pages.)<br /> <br /> She thinks that Dr. Twichowicz could help Oleander, but recognizes the dangers such work might pose (both to the Freehold and to Anton himself). She thinks that if he does snap and do something dangerous, it will be because he falls victim to fear. When something frightens Anton, that fear tends to build within him until he becomes irrational. D believes that if we can suppress Anton\u2019s fear, he should be alright, and able to contribute his expertise to the project.<br /> <br /> I asked her if she would consider meeting with Anton between his sessions working with Oleander. Maria seems to have a calming influence on him these days (and isn\u2019t that ironic?), and I think her presence might help to keep him grounded; keep him in touch with his better nature. She agreed that it couldn\u2019t hurt, and said she\u2019d be happy to try as long as he was up for it. I decided to drop by Lowjack\u2019s bar later that afternoon to speak with him about the possibility, and Maria offered to go with me.<br /> <br /> Before that, though, we had to deal with the vampire issue. I called Dad and let him know that a few of us would be by shortly, and that we had a way to get Dakota from his place to the Dream House without being observed. Oleander and I drove over in the \u2018vette, since both of us are known friends of Reverend Wells, and we could visit him without raising suspicions. Calamity and Jacob traveled through the Hedge to meet us there.<br /> <br /> Nothing could have prepared me for the sight that greeted me when he opened the door for us. Dad was wearing his cassock \u2013 unusual enough when he\u2019s home and not at the church \u2013 but it was immediately obvious that he was wearing some pretty bulky body armor underneath it. Sturdy black leather boots were laced up tight on his feet, and black gloves with hardened grip-pads clasped my hands when he led me inside. Completing the image was the fact that some species of assault rifle was slung on his back.<br /> <br /> \u201cExpecting trouble?\u201d I asked, perhaps a little faintly.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt does no harm to be prepared,\u201d he responded with a chuckle. \u201cInside, quickly now. I fear the house is being watched.\u201d<br /> <br /> Oleander began taking his vitals over his mild protests as I summoned up the glamour necessary to open a door to the Hedge. Calamity and Jacob were waiting on the other side, just as we\u2019d arranged, and they slipped quietly into the house. Once we were all present, Dad quietly entered the guest bedroom, asking us to wait for him to wake Dakota.<br /> <br /> We stood around awkwardly for a few minutes while muffled sounds of conversation drifted out of the darkened guest room. Eventually, Dad emerged and beckoned to us. \u201cShe\u2019s ready to meet you now. I\u2019ve told her that you can keep her safe, but haven\u2019t revealed\u2026 anything else about you. I\u2019ll continue to watch the front\u2026 that car has circled the block slowly twice now.\u201d<br /> <br /> We entered the bedroom to see Dakota sitting up in the bed, blinking blearily and glancing nervously at the blackout curtains on the windows. She was\u2026 surprisingly <u><u>normal</u></u> looking, actually. Very pretty, with brown hair, fair skin, and startlingly bright eyes\u2026 but not someone you\u2019d see on the street and think \u201cthat\u2019s a vampire.\u201d She smiled nervously at us as we entered, and I returned the favor.<br /> <br /> \u201cDakota?\u201d I asked, and she nodded. \u201cMy name is Lorelei. I\u2019m Reverend Wells\u2019 daughter. He\u2019s asked us to take you somewhere you\u2019ll be safe for a while, and we\u2019ve agreed as long as it\u2019s okay with you. We know about your\u2026 special circumstances.\u201d<br /> <br /> She stood up and extended a hand. \u201cReverend Wells thinks I\u2019ll be safe with you, and I trust him. Thank you. Sorry for the trouble\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Calamity took up the conversation from there. \u201cWe have a way to get you to our place without anyone seeing you go\u2026 but you\u2019re going to have to trust us. Can you travel in sunlight if you\u2019re wrapped up?\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded, but looked a little uncertain. \u201cI have to be <u><u>completely</u></u> covered, though.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe\u2019ll have to wrap you up in a blanket, then,\u201d Calamity said. I knew what she was thinking\u2026 the sunlight in the Hedge isn\u2019t <u><u>natural</u></u> sunlight, and it <u><u>might</u></u> not harm Dakota\u2026 but none of us really wanted to risk her safety on that supposition.<br /> <br /> Dad\u2019s voice filtered in as we were working out the details and Calamity was giving Dakota the basic facts of changeling life. \u201cYou might hear a shot in a moment or two,\u201d he called out calmly. \u201cNothing to worry about.\u201d<br /> <br /> I held up a finger and adopted a false smile. \u201cJust a sec,\u201d I said, edging out of the darkened room. Dad was seated at the front window, pointing a long rifle at something in front of the house.<br /> <br /> \u201cEverything okay?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cEverything is fine,\u201d he said evenly. \u201cThe car stopped across the street. The driver is watching the house. I intend to warn him that continuing his surveillance would be most unwise. One moment\u2026\u201d He squeezed the trigger gently, and the kick barely seemed to affect him at all\u2026 despite the fact that he was using a <u><u>very</u></u> large gun. I confess that I jumped a little at the sharp <u><u>crack</u></u> that echoed through the house.<br /> <br /> He turned back to me and smiled a few seconds later. \u201cHe ran off into the woods,\u201d he said with a quiet chuckle. \u201cI fired a shot into his car\u2026 not near the man himself. I doubt he will be back\u2026 but it might be best for me to take a short vacation.\u201d<br /> <br /> I put a hand on his shoulder. \u201cAre you going to be okay, Dad?\u201d I asked. \u201cDo you want to come back to the Dream House with us? We wouldn\u2019t mind putting you up\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> He laughed softly again. \u201cI thank you for the offer, Juliette, but that would simply lead anyone who might pursue me straight to Dakota. Once the Long Night realizes that I no longer have her, I expect they will leave well enough alone.\u201d His eyes were shining, and the color in his cheeks was better than I\u2019d seen it in ages.<br /> <br /> I leaned in and hugged him, feeling my chest flatten against the body armor under his robe. \u201cPlease promise me you\u2019ll be careful,\u201d I whispered as the others filed into the room. \u201cDon\u2019t take any unnecessary risks. I couldn\u2019t bear it if something happened to you\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI will be fine, Juliette,\u201d he said softly, returning my hug. \u201cI shall call you when I have settled in somewhere\u2026 and every day thereafter until I return, if you like.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cPlease do,\u201d I said.<br /> <br /> Calamity and Jacob took Dakota into the Hedge, and Oleander and I left a few minutes later. I think Oleander could tell how worried I was about Dad\u2019s situation, because she was quietly affectionate the whole way back. The others had already arrived by the time we returned, and we all gathered in the basement to speak further with Dakota.<br /> <br /> Okay, important details. Well, just like Kathy, she doesn\u2019t like the \u201cV-word,\u201d and asked that we refer to her people as \u201cKindred.\u201d She\u2019s a member of a group called the \u201cInvictus,\u201d and the faction currently in power in L.A. call themselves the \u201cCarthians\u201d (we didn\u2019t pry yet as to their conflicting ideologies). She can (and usually does) feed safely and relatively anonymously, and promised to do so while she\u2019s staying with us. And it turns out that she can drink changeling blood, too\u2026 Calamity let her drain a bit of her blood, and she seemed to enjoy the experience immensely. Like, enough that I admit to being kind of curious as to what it feels like to have a \u0336v\u0336a\u0336m\u0336p\u0336i\u0336r\u0336e\u0336 kindred drink from <u><u>my</u></u> veins.<br /> <br /> Dakota also told us something that gave me pause. She mentioned that at some point, in a tense situation while she was on the run, Dad had taken her by the arm. When he touched her, it sort of\u2026 dampened her vampire powers. She ordinarily enjoys enhanced strength and speed, but at that moment her abilities were very nearly human. Curiouser and curiouser, as Alice might have said.<br /> <br /> We also enchanted Dakota so that she could see changelings as we really are. And yes, she asked me if I was an angel. And <u><u>yes</u></u>, she asked me if I was the one who showed up in L.A. last week (jeez, did <u><u>everyone</u></u> hear about that?). We introduced her to the rest of the Dream House\u2019s residents, and then let her rest until nightfall. You should have seen Missy and Jane beam when Calamity introduced them as part of the motley\u2026 they haven\u2019t taken the oath yet, but it\u2019s nice to know that people are starting to think of them as part of the family.<br /> <br /> While Dakota was napping, Maria and I drove out to Lowjack\u2019s bar. Tamara was working the bar, and she told us that John was in and that she\u2019d let him know we were there. Maria and I reminisced about that place \u2013 it\u2019s where we first met after all, so I think we both still regard it with a certain fondness \u2013 and a few minutes later, Tamara emerged and told us that the King would see us.<br /> <br /> John greeted us warmly and offered me a chair (Maria remained by the door, leaning up against the frame like James Dean). He asked me if I had any more unpleasant bombshells to drop on him, and quipped that it would be nice not to be the last to know for once. I laughed it off with him, and told him that I wasn\u2019t there to surprise him, but to talk about something else.<br /> <br /> I told him that Maria knew about what Oleander was doing for the Freehold, and that we could speak freely in front of her. He took this news in stride, and asked me what was on my mind. I laid out our ideas about how Anton might be able to help Oleander develop a safer way to distribute our toxin, about Maria\u2019s idea of suppressing Anton\u2019s fear so that he wouldn\u2019t do anything irrational, and about how Maria herself might be able to help keep him grounded. I told him that it wasn\u2019t my intention to countermand his decision on the matter; that\u2019s why I wanted to discuss the situation with him privately.<br /> <br /> Lowjack sort of sighed and steepled his fingers as he considered my words. \u201cLorelei,\u201d he said carefully after a moment\u2019s thought, \u201cI want you to know that I didn\u2019t make that decision lightly. From a tactical standpoint, Oleander is a valuable asset; she probably has the most brilliant mind in the whole Freehold. And on a personal note, the last thing I want to see is her throwing her life away now that she\u2019s finally found happiness with you.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded at that, keeping my emotions carefully in check. The last thing I wanted was for John to think that I was trying to sway him with overly emotional displays. \u201cBut\u2026?\u201d I asked, prompting him to continue.<br /> <br /> He shrugged. \u201cBut\u2026 nothing, really. I just want to remind you that unless things come to a head with Hollywood <u><u>very</u></u> quickly \u2013 and I desperately hope that they don\u2019t \u2013 the decision will no longer be in my hands. When the monarchy passes to you, you\u2019ll be able to rule how you like on this matter. Until then\u2026 well, I\u2019ll make a deal with you. If it looks like things are coming to a crisis point, and Oleander still hasn\u2019t come up with an alternative delivery method on her own, I\u2019ll sign off on your plan. Fair?\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded slowly, though I realized he was essentially placating me with a promise he thought was unlikely to come up. \u201cThank you, John,\u201d I said after a moment.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnything else?\u201d he asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, actually\u2026\u201d I said with a slight grin. \u201cWhen I told you that I didn\u2019t have any surprises for you, that was a bald-faced lie. There is something you should probably know.\u201d<br /> <br /> I launched into a brief explanation of Dakota and how she came to be in our care. Lowjack knew a bit