nd my octogenarian father strangely attractive when he was in his badass soldier-of-fortune mode. I found myself joining Julia\u2019s ongoing crusade against the notion of anyone in the motley seeking sexual encounters with anyone else\u2019s parents. At one point I told Calamity that although I had promised not to pull rank against anyone in the motley, if she persisted in making innuendos about my dad, I\u2019d make a fucking royal edict against it.<br /> <br /> We had just decided on that night\u2019s movies (<u><u>The Empire Strikes Back</u></u> and <u><u>Return of the Jedi</u></u>, to further Missy and Jane\u2019s education regarding the pop culture of the last forty years or so) when my phone rang again. Glancing at the caller ID, I was surprised to see that the Santa Monica PD was reaching out to me. Turns out that Dad had informed the cops that he was going out of town, and had listed me as a point of contact if anything should happen to his house. Something did.<br /> <br /> The cops were calling to let me know that someone had attempted to break into the place. They had caused a commotion, a neighbor had called them, and the perpetrators had run off. The cops had no reason to believe that the burglars had made it into the house, so they were willing to let the incident go without further investigation. I told them I\u2019d stop by to make sure everything was in order, and that I\u2019d call them if I found anything amiss.<br /> <br /> So about three picoseconds after I disconnected with the fuzz, I speed-dialed my dad. \u201cSomething I can help you with, Juliette?\u201d he asked, his voice the picture of innocence.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, Dad\u2026 I just wanted to make sure you were okay. The cops called me to let me know that someone tried to break into your house.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI am <u><u>fine</u></u>, Juliette,\u201d he said. \u201cI\u2019m in a safe place. I haven\u2019t gone far. I\u2019m in Venice Beach, if you\u2019d like to know.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay, good to know. Now perhaps you\u2019d like to tell me why Dakota believes that your touch somehow suppresses her supernatural powers?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot over the phone,\u201d he said dryly. \u201cLet us just say for now that I have always been able to dissuade those who might wish me harm.\u201d<br /> <br /> I sighed. \u201cOkay, keep your secrets for now. But someday, when you get back into town, you and I are going to have a <u><u>much</u></u> longer conversation about this, young man.\u201d He laughed out loud at that. \u201cWell, I\u2019m going to take Becky and head by your house to make sure everything is okay. I\u2019ll call you once I\u2019ve scoped the place out. Anything I should know?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDo not enter by the front door,\u201d he said instantly, \u201cgo in through the back porch. I left a\u2026 surprise at the main entrance.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWould this \u2018surprise\u2019 involve firearms or explosives, by any chance?\u201d I asked wryly.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt might,\u201d he said, and laughed again. I haven\u2019t heard him laugh as much as he has today since\u2026 I don\u2019t think I\u2019ve <u><u>ever</u></u> heard him laugh this much. It\u2019s heartening\u2026 but also a little worrying. I hope he doesn\u2019t start seeking out this sort of situation. I do <u><u>not</u></u> need this kind of stress on a regular basis.<br /> <br /> We disconnected a little later and I found Becky. She gave me this look that clearly said For-All-Her-Faults-I-Never-Had-To-Put-Up-With-This-Kind-Of-Shit-From-Jolie, but agreed to come along with relatively good grace. The cops had cleared out by the time we pulled up, and the house looked deserted. I noticed when we pulled up that the front door was cracked, and the lock appeared to be damaged, but didn\u2019t dare open it to find out more.<br /> <br /> We entered through the back door (noting that one of the windows had some sort of grenade rigged to go off if it was opened) and found the house mostly undisturbed. It looked like the Long Night agents had forced the front door, setting off a shotgun which had been loaded with rock salt. There was a little blood around the door, but not enough to indicate a truly serious injury. I\u2019m guessing the trap scared the intruder off, and they left the rest of the house untouched.<br /> <br /> I called Dad to let him know what was what, and he talked Becky through disarming the grenade trap by the kitchen window (apparently it wasn\u2019t an explosive, but contained some sort of soporific gas). He was still pretty cavalier about the whole situation. A part of me wonders if he was just trying not to make me worry about him\u2026 but I don\u2019t really think that\u2019s it. He\u2019s <u><u>enjoying</u></u> the danger on some level, and I think that worries me more than the danger itself.<br /> <br /> So with the booby traps safely disarmed and the house once more secured, we made our way back to the Dream House for movie night. I think everyone enjoyed the classic <u><u>Star Wars</u></u> goodness, though Marguerite was still sulking that nobody else wanted to watch <u><u>Amelie</u></u> instead. Maybe we can take an afternoon in the near future and watch that together\u2026 she\u2019s been so supportive of me since I took up the mantle of Queen; I should make an effort to spend some time with her and show her my appreciation. I know I don\u2019t have a lot of free time these days, but if nothing else maybe I can convince the others to show it next movie night, paired with something else funny and romantic, like <u><u>Princess Bride</u></u>.<br /> <br /> So that was my day in a nutshell. Matriculation, exsanguination, negotiation, and investigation. (Okay, I admit it. I\u2019m showing off now. To myself. In my private diary. God, that\u2019s sad.) But now the movies are over and people are going their separate ways\u2026 mostly to their beds, but a few are staying up to keep Dakota company. For my part, that big old bed looks particularly inviting with my wife lying in it, and I\u2019m going to make the most of the next few hours by luxuriating in her strong embrace.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei de la Rocha</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> I guess when it rains it pours. Lori came back this morning with news about her father and what was going on with him. She had to explain to Missy and Jane that he had been a vampire hunter in the years that they were gone and that he was still involved somewhat with that life. He used to be a part of a group of people called the Long Night. They were a group of hunters that specifically went after vampires. The Reverend Wells was initially on board with their ideas and methods, but soon ran into a young vampire girl that was an innocent and didn\u2019t deserve to be killed. He tried to defend her and failed. She died. This morning he talked to Lori about another new vampire girl named Dakota. This new vampire had run afoul of the vampires in the area, history to be explained, and the Long Night. We discussed whether or not we could safely look after a vampire and came to the conclusion that we needed more information. We don\u2019t know what she can drink. We knew that it had to be blood, but we didn\u2019t know if it had to be human or if it could be animal or Changeling. Our plan was to go to the Reverend Wells\u2019 house and talk to Dakota ourselves. We weren\u2019t sure if anyone was watching his house, so we came up the idea of approaching from two different directions. Lori and Oleander, who are known to visit the Reverend Wells, would go in Lori\u2019s vette. Calamity and I would take our hedge mounts and enter through the gate that Lori would open for us. All went according to plan.<br /> <br /> We arrived at the house and went in through the gate that Lori opened in the coat closet. We arrived to meet the Revered Wells wearing body armor under his robes, a belt with grenades on it and an automatic weapon on his back. The man was obviously prepared for any eventuality. We introduced ourselves and talked to him a bit about what vampires can eat etc\u2026 It turns out that he knows more about how to kill vampires than how to keep them alive, but at least knowing their weaknesses would be useful information too. We don\u2019t want anyone using Dakota\u2019s weakness against her while she is under our protection. He did say that he thought younger vampires could feed on animals. A few minutes later we got to speak to Dakota herself. She seemed to be a pleasant enough girl. She was nervous with all the new people but seemed to take it mostly in stride. When we asked her what she could eat she confirmed that she could in fact eat animal blood and didn\u2019t think that Changeling blood would cause her many troubles. This of course required us to explain to her what we were. We boiled it down to being people who\u2019d been taken from our home by the fae, and then escaped later. We told her that we\u2019d been changed by the fae and had special abilities like opening a gateway to a magical land that could take her unseen to a safe place. She seemed a bit hesitant about the whole thing at first but was quickly reassured by the Reverend Wells that we were there to help her.<br /> <br /> While we were talking to Dakota Revered Wells said from the front room that he was going to fire a shot out the window with his rifle. He assured his concerned daughter that it was just going to be a warning shot at the car across the street that had stopped to watch the house. He fired his one round and hit the car. The man inside fled into the woods behind the car. We took that as our opportunity to leave and head for the Dream House. The plan was that Oleander and Lori would leave via their car just like they arrived and Calamity, Dakota and myself would head back to the Dream House. Now because the Hedge is just as every bit bright as \u2018the world\u2019 we wrapped Dakota up completely and carried her through the Hedge to our waiting mounts. We rode back to the house and met Oleander and Lori there. We got Dakota safely inside and downstairs into the basement where there are no windows.<br /> <br /> We talked to Dakota some more when we got to the Dream House. She explained that she was part of a group called the Invictus. Those in charge were in a group called the Carthians. Dakota\u2019s \u201csire,\u201d the one that made her what she is, was a known Invictus to those in charge and was allowed to live in the area but was told not to \u201cembrace\u201d anyone else, which means make them a vampire. He disobeyed that order and embraced Dakota, and now that young girl is caught in the crossfire. Literally. The Carthians came after Dakota and her mentor, killing her mentor in the process. They tried to kill Dakota but she got away. This got the Long Night involved who started hunting the fledgling vampire. I don\u2019t know how vampire politics work, but it seems to me that someone should be judged on their merits before being summarily executed. It apparently doesn\u2019t work that way in vampire society. Though I suppose that I should call them Kindred. Dakota was somewhat adamant that we use the term Kindred instead of vampire when talking about her kind. That\u2019s not the first time we\u2019ve heard that either. Kathy was kind of insistent, from what I\u2019ve been told, that we should call her and her kind Kindred.<br /> <br /> After we\u2019d talked for a bit about Kindred society we asked her about her eating habits and things like that. What we needed to do to make sure that she stayed safe and healthy while in our care. She said that she could in fact drink animal blood and didn\u2019t think that there would be a reason why she couldn\u2019t drink Changeling blood. So, I guess as a gesture of good will, Calamity offered to feed her some of her blood. Before we did this though we ensorcelled her so that she could see us as we really were. This led to a few questions about why Calamity had glass and if Lori was the \u201cangel\u201d from the L.A. highway the other day. We explained that we\u2019d all been taken by different fae and therefore came back changed in different ways. Calamity explained Snowglobe in a nutshell. Lori told about the transformation into a bird and being ordered to sing. I simply said while showing off the frost on my arms that I had been taken somewhere cold. That seemed sufficient an explanation to me. So, Calamity offered some of her blood to Dakota to make sure that that would be a viable option. We showed Dakota what we were first so she wouldn\u2019t be taken off guard or hurt by Calamity\u2019s glass. It also seemed the thing to do since we were welcoming her into our home.<br /> <br /> Dakota also mentioned that when Reverend Wells grabbed her arm to get her to come with him she felt like her Kindred powers were suppressed. Like her strength, which should have easily overcome his, was too weak to resist his. Shortly after we finished out talk Lori\u2019s dad called to say that he was leaving his house and taking a short vacation away from town for a few days. He said that he had left a note on his door for those that had been watching. He also said that he\u2019d called the police and asked them to keep an eye on his house due to folks stalking him and watching his house.<br /> <br /> Then Lori went to Lowjack\u2019s bar to talk to him about our guest and the problems associated with protecting her. I guess she wanted to do that in person rather than over the phone. I suppose it makes sense. I wouldn\u2019t want to talk about shooting at cars from windows to keep hunters away over the phone. While she was doing that Calamity and I sparred in the backyard. We haven\u2019t done that in a while. It seems the past few therapy days we were busy doing other stuff and didn\u2019t get around to it. So we went all out. It was fun. Luna watched from the sidelines. Once when we were taking a break Luna off handedly mentioned that the Rangers had found an old body buried in the woods. They had been looking for the kidnapper since Luna said that he likely did not survive. Instead of finding him, which wasn\u2019t going to happen, they came across an old kill of Luna\u2019s and she was worried that they might find others. Her gaze told me that we would talk more about this matter later.<br /> <br /> Once Lori got back we started discussing what we were going to do for Movie Night. We went through a few options, including some that we\u2019ve watched a few times before. <i><i>Amelie</i></i> came up as an option but it got shot down. We ended up deciding on <i><i>The Empire Strikes Back</i></i> and <i><i>Return of the Jedi</i></i> so Missy and Jane could see how the series turned out. We figured we\u2019d inflict the prequel movies on them later. After they\u2019d seen the classics. It wasn\u2019t long after that conversation ended that Calamity went downstairs to greet our guest when she woke up. I think she is interested in our new guest. Particularly after Dakota fed on her. Calamity really seemed to enjoy the experience. So, we all gathered upstairs and talked some more about the Changeling situation. We explained about the time differences between Arcadia and \u2018the world,\u2019 and how some of us were gone for a long time, while others not much time at all, but we were all changed by it. During our conversation Lori\u2019s phone rang again. This time it was the police. They said that she had been listed as a point of contact should anything happen at Reverend Wells\u2019 house. Apparently the Hunters tried to break in, so they called Lori. Lori then called her dad and they talked about what had happened. Reverend Wells asked Lori to check out the house if she wanted to, but to not go in through the front door. He implied that it had been boobytrapped. So, Lori and Becky went to the house and found that the front door had indeed been opened and the rock salt shotgun had been triggered. There was blood on the floor, but not enough to indicate a serious injury. The only thing that they did was disarm a smoke grenade trap that was on the window, with instructions from Lori\u2019s dad. They came back and let us know what had happened.<br /> <br /> Later in the evening when we were going to bed Luna started talking to me about the body that they found in the woods. She is seriously worried about them finding the others that are buried out there. She doesn\u2019t want them thinking that a serial killer is at work. Nor does she want scrutiny on herself. She then asked if I was a good friend. I got the referenced and just said yes. I asked about how many other bodies were likely to be out there and she wasn\u2019t sure. They had all been killed a long time ago, but she figured there was at least a couple more. I didn\u2019t ask, but she assured me that they were all bad people. One of them would stalk women in the forest and another did the same but with children. Both sick individuals. We then talked about where we could put the bones. It was briefly brought up that we could dump them into the ocean, but I\u2019m not sure where we could do that and not get spotted by someone. Luna suggested that we involve Calamity in our planes and I agreed. So, Luna went and got her student and the three of us talked for a bit. We agreed that we would go out tomorrow night and move the remains, which should just be bones at this point. I suggested that we leave the woods through a gate to the Hedge, but that would require us to find something suitable to act as a gate. I\u2019m sure that we can find a fallen tree somewhere that makes a good shape to use as a door.<br /> <br /> Somehow I wasn\u2019t surprised that Luna had some literal bodies buried out there instead of the figurative skeletons in the closet. I know that my Luna does not suffer fools lightly. She usually just torments them until they leave the woods or until they stop doing whatever it was that they did. I\u2019ve helped her on some of those trips and found them to be quite fun. I think she was expecting me to be more shocked than I was. I won\u2019t say that there wasn\u2019t something of a surprise in my mind when she told me what was going on, but I know my Luna. She protects those that she feels are innocent, especially children, and I\u2019m not surprised that she went as far as killing someone to keep those innocents safe. I\u2019m not a stranger to doing questionable things. I\u2019ve done some bad things in my time, but this isn\u2019t that. What my Luna has done is to help those in the community whether they realize it or not. She just helps in a more definitive fashion than others might. I love my Luna and nothing will change that. And if that means helping her rebury old bodies then I will do that with her. I will keep her and her secrets safe.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> Today Juliette brought a vampire into the Dream House. And not just any vampire: A vampire from a group our vampire friends hate. A veritable Day Court vampire I think. The Rowan of vampires? I doubt it. Obviously.<br /> <br /> They had to smuggle her out of her father\u2019s house, which likely caused Juliette some odd flashbacks.<br /> <br /> She seemed to settle in fine. Calamity got her to bite her because she is strange. Then she and Jacob went knife fighting in the back yard. Because.<br /> <br /> Juliette is strained by a lot of what is going on, between the vampire and the demons and worries about\u2026things\u2026. with her position\u2026.I am worried about her. I am trying to be there and supportive just as much as I can. Trying to be a friendly face she knows is there for her. It is the best I can do.<br /> <br /> Julia is doing well. I don\u2019t think she really approves of the vampire adoption and demon hunts and what have you, but she goes along with it. Maria, on the other hand, seems to enjoy it. Which is good, I suppose.<br /> <br /> Yvette should be back around tomorrow and I look forward to it. She is trying to reconcile our relationship and her personal feelings related to events in Arcadia. She loves I, but she also fears I. I wish I knew what to suggest to help. Maybe the Therapists, though I am unsure if I want her talking about what I did to her in Arcadia with them.<br /> <br /> We watched the second two Star Wars movies tonight for Melissa and Jane. It was much the same as last time I saw them. Trinh has moved out to make room for the vampire. Bad deal.<br /> <br /> Also they did not want to see <i><i>Am\u00e9lie</i></i>. I do not understand why they would not want to if we are re-watching. It is my favorite movie and the favorite movie of all the puppets! I really do not understand them sometimes.<br /> <br /> Oh apparently Calamity, Luna and Jacob fought a Gentry yesterday. Terrifying. Of course, it seems foolish for the Gentry to even try to send people here anymore. We are full of psychopaths and sociopaths.<br /> <br /> I am neither, of course.<br /> <br /> Oh, there was a big Night Court meeting here last night, which did not break out into any fights, though Rosalita apparently wants to shoot Corbin. Such a violent girl. Pretty, but violent. The Night Court can be a bit anarchistic at times, and sometimes these little meetings help get everyone on the same page. I can only guess what the others, less used to our little quirks, thought of the mad little group in the Dream House last night.<br /> <br /> It appears Julia is about ready for bed, and so am I. Such an elegant girl I married. I am pleased with my decision. And such an artist. Yes I, too, I think am ready for bed.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXXII</i><br /> <br /> The Long Night is a thing from Hunter: The Vigil if you have forgotten. No, they can\u2019t generally dampen vampic abilities with a touch, though.<br /> <br /> Dakota is a Daeva, for those playing along at home. References have been made to a west coast conflict between Invictus and Carthians, though generally in the background. Only one offhand reference that may or may not have made it into a journal here, but it was also mentioned in <u>Night Train Detective Agency</u>, my <b>Demon game</b>, a couple times, though the PCs did not fully grasp the particulars there either.<br /> <br /> Lorelei\u2019s comments on Lowjack warm my heart as a GM. I am not a particularly manipulative/charismatic person, so when I can nonetheless play someone that way well enough it elicits comments, I am doing well.<br /> <br /> Okay, I think that covers it. Comments and Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 12-02-2018, 05:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-15T21:31:54-08:00","id":1274664,"title":"","content":"Okay they have a pet vampire being hunted by mortal hunters and an increasingly bizarre political situation. What more could go wrong?<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXXIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> I suppose I was na\u00efve not to expect this sort of thing when I took up the mantle of Queen. It\u2019s just been one thing after another lately, with no pause in between crises to stop and take stock of my life. Still, all things considered, I suppose Tuesday was a better day than Monday\u2026 which really speaks to how worried I am about my Dad, considering that Tuesday saw one of my girlfriends placed in a horrible spot and the Dream House playing host to a powerful demon.<br /> <br /> But first thing\u2019s first: I had my first day as an actual college student today! Like, on campus, surrounded by professors and other students and lecture halls and labs and quadrangles and all that shit. UCLA is pretty damned imposing, with all that brick and tile nestled under the nearby skyline of the city itself. I scheduled my classes so that I\u2019ll have lectures for both Organic Chemistry and Biology every Tuesday and Thursday morning, but only one lab on each of those days (today was the Chem lab).<br /> <br /> D sat on the bed snickering and watched me dress four or five times until I found an outfit I could live with\u2026 a pretty, just-above-the-knee skirt, a tight sweater, and a pair of sensible pumps that wouldn\u2019t hurt my feet if I had to walk across campus quickly. I put my glasses on and tied my hair up in a ponytail\u2026 but not the sober, straight-haired nape-of-the-neck ponytail I wear to church. I left my hair artfully tousled and pulled it up high to keep it from brushing against the tops of my wings when I moved. D said I looked like \u201cthe smartest cheerleader on the squad.\u201d She can be such a <u><u>bitch</u></u> sometimes. I love her so much\u2026<br /> <br /> Becky met me in the kitchen as the others were getting ready for therapy. We\u2019d talked it over and decided that she or Angelica should accompany me to UCLA; at least for the first few weeks. While non-students aren\u2019t allowed in the classrooms and labs, they\u2019ll be able to keep an eye out for trouble while I\u2019m between classes, or walking to or from my car. And UCLA is too close to Hollywood for one of our monarchs to venture there alone and unprotected.<br /> <br /> So Becky walked with me between classes, and hung out on campus while I was otherwise occupied. She talked a lot about picking up some cute college student for a quickie, and I think she might have actually done so at least once. The two of us got a lot of attention whenever we walked across campus together, and of course we ate it up. We each got a few party invitations, a couple of crude come-ons, asked out for half a dozen cups of coffee, and one proposal of marriage (I held up my ring with a smile at the last).<br /> <br /> After my lab, I found her talking to someone I actually recognized\u2026 Mari Lwyd of the Night Court. She had gotten word that a couple of changelings with seasonal mantles were hanging out on the UCLA campus, and had dropped by to investigate. I suppose that makes sense\u2026 they\u2019re a lot closer to Hollywood than we are, so unfamiliar seasonal courtiers probably set off alarm bells with them. We apologized for showing up unannounced and let her know that we\u2019d be on campus a couple of times a week for the foreseeable future, and parted on good terms.<br /> <br /> Lowjack had left me a voicemail while I was in class, asking me to stop by his bar on my way back into town. Begging Becky\u2019s indulgence, I made the slight detour, and twenty minutes later we were walking into the nearly deserted bar (hey, it was like two o\u2019clock on a Tuesday afternoon). John greeted us warmly and invited us into his office.<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you for coming,\u201d he said with a weary sigh. \u201cI wish I had better news for you, but this is something that probably shouldn\u2019t wait. You see, Siobhan came to me this morning. She had spotted someone she recognized at the Dream House the other night\u2026 a dangerous fugitive from Hollywood. She wanted to warn me that we had a killer in our midst.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWho?\u201d I asked. It seemed like the only question that mattered.<br /> <br /> \u201cGloria McKenzie,\u201d he said softly.<br /> <br /> She uses her family name so infrequently that it actually took me a minute to register what he had said. \u201cGloria?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cI thought you should know,\u201d he said gently. \u201cSiobhan sent word to the monarchs in Hollywood, and they forwarded some evidence. I have it here, but I warn you that it isn\u2019t pleasant.\u201d<br /> <br /> He showed me a couple of photos on his computer screen. The first showed four corpses, all of which had been burned beyond recognition. The second was a picture of Gloria buying gasoline at a service station with a prominent time-stamp. Taken together the implication was clear, but individually\u2026<br /> <br /> \u201cThese are\u2026\u201d I began.<br /> <br /> \u201cFake,\u201d John finished my sentence for me. \u201cI know. They\u2019re not very good. Honestly, I could probably do better if you gave me twenty-four hours. Siobhan seemed pretty convinced, though\u2026 I think she was honestly afraid that Gloria was a danger to us. I\u2019ve informed her that Gloria is now a member of this Freehold in good standing, and that we would respond poorly to any action taken against her.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you,\u201d I said quietly. \u201cSo what\u2019s our move? What do you need from me?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSiobhan came to me because I\u2019m the current reigning monarch,\u201d Lowjack explained. \u201cI thought I ought to inform Augustine, as he\u2019s Gloria\u2019s monarch. But I wanted to tell you first, since the two of you are close.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cI agree, Augustine should be brought in on this\u2026 and probably Charlotte, too, so we\u2019re all on the same page. But I don\u2019t want to make that decision without Gloria\u2019s input. Can you give me a couple of hours to talk it over with her first, please? I\u2019ll give you a call as soon as I\u2019ve cleared it with her.\u201d<br /> <br /> John allowed as how that would work, and Becky and I took our leave. I actually handed my keys to Becky and let her drive me home while I made a few calls. Gloria was at work, but she agreed to stop by the Dream House when she got off so we could talk in person. She also admitted that she had no other plans for the rest of the evening, which at least gave us something to look forward to.<br /> <br /> Maria was just coming back from a late lunch with Anton when I called her, and we arrived back at the Dream House at around the same time. Before we had the chance to talk, however, I was distracted by something\u2026 something that actually made me smile, if you can believe that. As I walked through the theater I noticed Missy dancing on stage. She was oblivious to my presence, as she was totally absorbed in whatever music was playing on her headphones.<br /> <br /> And Jane was nowhere in sight.<br /> <br /> It was the first time since we got back from Arcadia that I had seen her alone and looking <u><u>comfortable</u></u>. When I could do so without startling or embarrassing her, I caught her attention. \u201cJane\u2019s sleeping in the other room,\u201d she told me, \u201cso I thought I\u2019d let her rest and listen to some of the music Julia recommended. Some of it is pretty good!\u201d<br /> <br /> I couldn\u2019t help but smile; she sounded so much like her old, pre-Empress self. \u201cI\u2019m glad you like it,\u201d I said. \u201cI\u2019ll leave you to it for now; we can catch up later. Have fun!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks,\u201d she said, \u201cI think I will\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> So I had that to bolster me as I told my wife what Hollywood was saying about our girlfriend. Maria responded to Lowjack\u2019s news about as well as I had expected her to\u2026 which is why I wanted to talk to her alone first. \u201cThose sick bastards!\u201d she ranted. \u201cThis is going to wreck her\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt sucks,\u201d I agreed, \u201cbut what you have to remember is that it\u2019s <u><u>Hollywood</u></u> that\u2019s doing this. Lowjack didn\u2019t believe their lies even <u><u>before</u></u> he talked to me. The Freehold will stand with Gloria. You have my word on that.\u201d I think that calmed her down at least a little bit.<br /> <br /> We sort of quietly enjoyed each other\u2019s company for a bit while we waited for Gloria to arrive. When she did, the two of us quickly swooped in and asked to speak with her privately. Once we were safely ensconced in our bedroom, she allowed her normally cheerful expression to slip a little bit. \u201cIs everything okay? Am I in some sort of trouble?\u201d she asked plaintively.<br /> <br /> D and I looked at each other at that. \u201cNot as such,\u201d I said softly. \u201cYou haven\u2019t done anything wrong, honey, and nobody is upset with you. But I had a conversation with Boss Lowjack earlier today, and it concerned you. There\u2019s\u2026 something you should know.\u201d<br /> <br /> She took it remarkably well, considering what she was being accused of. As I\u2019d hoped, she followed the leanings of her Court and responded first with anger rather than grief or hysteria. \u201cAfter what they did,\u201d she said, her voice tight and trembling a little, \u201cthey\u2019re saying that I killed my motley? They\u2019re saying that I killed <u><u>Andy</u></u>? He was my <u><u>boyfriend</u></u>!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sorry, honey,\u201d I said, and Maria and I took her in our arms, holding her between the two of us. \u201cI just want to make it clear that <u><u>nobody</u></u> in the Lady By the Sea thinks you actually did this. You\u2019re one of us now, and any action Hollywood takes against you will be considered an act of war. And Siobhan knows it.\u201d<br /> <br /> She managed to calm down a bit after a while, though she was obviously still very upset about the accusations leveled against her. Who could blame her? The <u><u>monsters</u></u> who murdered her best friends are trying to pin the crime on her. Who <u><u>wouldn\u2019t</u></u> be pissed about something like that?<br /> <br /> She didn\u2019t want to be alone that night, so she stuck to her original plan to attend the show and stay with Maria and me that night. She planted herself at the Girlfriend Table when we opened the doors for the evening, sitting with Missy, Jane, Julia, and Dakota. Yvette had been around during the day (she and Marguerite had apparently spent the day walking around Paris), but she opted not to stay for the show this time.<br /> <br /> Calamity had also been busy during the afternoon, apparently. She dropped by to visit Luther Henderson at his apartment. You remember Luther, right? He was the large heroic man she nearly killed last week in L.A. during the freeway debacle. Well, she\u2019s been keeping her eye on him, and she decided that she needed to apologize for hurting him. What surprised the hell out of me was that he apparently <u><u>accepted</u></u> her apology! She spent nearly an hour at his place, and by the time she left she had ensorcelled him, and he had given her a Tupperware container full of homemade pasta. Who knew?<br /> <br /> So, the show. I chose last night\u2019s solo for Gloria. After the initial shock of her situation had passed, she quipped that it would be sort of bad-ass if there were wanted posters with her picture on them posted around Hollywood. With both that and her general taste in music rattling around in my brain, it wasn\u2019t hard for me to decide that I wanted to perform Bon Jovi\u2019s \u201cWanted Dead or Alive.\u201d I didn\u2019t have a lot of time to prep choreography, so it wasn\u2019t my finest performance by a long-shot, but Gloria seemed to enjoy it, if the kiss she gave me when we spoke after the number was any indication.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, she wasn\u2019t the only person at the club last night who deserved special attention. Before the show, Calamity let the rest of us know on the Bluetooth thingies that we had not one but <u><u>two</u></u> monster-hunters in the crowd\u2026 and that they were stalking a special sort of prey. Soon-Hee Kwon was there, along with a young lady named Nakamura, who Soon-Hee called the \u201csecond best monster hunter in the Courts of the Dragon.\u201d They were there because our club had attracted the attention of one Pipa Jing\u2026 a known demon and associate of Da Ji.<br /> <br /> I made my way up to Soon-Hee\u2019s table first, as she was the known quantity among that trio. She flashed me a naughty grin and gestured to her lap as I approached. I smiled and settled in as she slipped her arms around me. Over the course of the next three minutes she told me why Pipa Jing was so dangerous\u2026 and I really wish I could remember more of that conversation, because I\u2019m sure it was very important. But at the same time as she was talking to me, she was <u><u>breathing</u></u> on my <u><u>neck</u></u>. It was\u2026 very distracting. I\u2019m sure that there were little licks of flame caressing the crook of my neck\u2026<br /> <br /> Goodness but it\u2019s gotten hot.<br /> <br /> \u201cDid you know that I\u2019m Spring Queen now?\u201d I sort of moaned when she paused to take a breath.<br /> <br /> \u201cCongratulations,\u201d she whispered, running what felt suspiciously like a long forked tongue up my throat.<br /> <br /> \u201cI mean, I don\u2019t <u><u>call</u></u> myself a Princess like Jolie did, but isn\u2019t there a tradition of dragons devouring...\u201d I let myself trail off at that point, and she threw me another wicked grin.<br /> <br /> \u201cGod I wish I wasn\u2019t on duty right now,\u201d she said with feeling.<br /> <br /> \u201cA rain check, then,\u201d I promised. \u201cI kind of made other plans tonight anyway.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou should check on Calamity first, though,\u201d Soon-Hee said, all business again as I rose from her lap. \u201cShe\u2019s been talking to Pipa Jing for a while, and that\u2019s never a good thing.\u201d<br /> <br /> So I said my goodbyes and made my way down to the table where Pipa Jing sat surrounded by empty glasses. According to Jacob she\u2019d been pounding back Harvey Wallbangers for most of the night, but she didn\u2019t seem even a little bit tipsy. She and Calamity were deep in conversation when I approached, but it seemed innocuous enough.<br /> <br /> Pipa Jing is\u2026 compelling in a strange way. I don\u2019t know how to quantify it with words, but she has a way of seeming so reasonable and agreeable that it\u2019s hard to contradict anything she says. She was very complimentary, praising both the Dream House and the performances, and commenting upon the large number of \u201cYao Guai\u201d in attendance. And when I asked her why she had come\u2026 she smiled. It was warm and inviting and just a little bit naughty, and clearly all for me. I didn\u2019t want to like it, but I kind of did.<br /> <br /> She said that she had come to invite us back to Da Ji\u2019s club in L.A. We had apparently made quite an impression upon the club\u2019s denizens, and they were eager to see us again. She told me that Malai was quite taken with me, and something about the way she said it very nearly made me blush (not sure what that was about; I\u2019m not usually much of a blusher). She only asked that we give them a little notice before our next visit. \u201cWe\u2019d like the opportunity to tailor the experience to your particular\u2026 tastes,\u201d she said with a sultry purr.<br /> <br /> I threw her a mysterious smile of my own before I answered. \u201cUnfortunately, my time isn\u2019t my own lately,\u201d I said. \u201cI don\u2019t know when I\u2019ll get the chance to enjoy another evening in the city\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> She pouted. \u201cWell, the invitation stands,\u201d she said after a moment, \u201cand I\u2019m certain we could make it worth your time. Just let us know when you\u2019d like to drop by, and we\u2019ll show you an evening you\u2019ll never forget.\u201d She said her goodbyes after that, and Calamity and I sort of let out a collective breath.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not thinking about going back to the House With No Name (as Soon-Hee called Da Ji\u2019s club)\u2026 not really. But I must admit it\u2019s fun to toy with the idea. It has the allure of the forbidden. But no. I won\u2019t go back there. Y\u2019know\u2026 probably.<br /> <br /> I spoke with most of our other guests for at least a little while, including the enigmatic Nakamura. She wore a trench coat and a broad-brimmed hat (Maria said that she looked like someone called \u201cCarmen San Diego,\u201d but as usual I didn\u2019t get the reference), and once I got close it was easy to see why\u2026 she has no face. Like, the front of her head is smooth as an egg. Still, she seemed nice enough once she got to talking. Her mantle was like a shimmering heat haze that seemed to pulse in time with my heartbeat.<br /> <br /> Eventually I found myself up at the Girlfriend Table, sitting on Gloria\u2019s lap and allowing her to seduce me. Dakota looked a little embarrassed, but I\u2019m sure she\u2019ll get over it. Missy and Jane had long since been tempted away by Marguerite and Julia (much to Maria\u2019s chagrin\u2026 I\u2019ve promised her that we can try to bed my two best friends tomorrow night, and I think she\u2019s really looking forward to it). So I confess that I wasn\u2019t really paying much attention to the room as the show ended and the crowds began to disperse\u2026 my face was pretty much glued to Gloria\u2019s.<br /> <br /> Once the last of the guests had departed, Gloria stood up, carrying me in her arms. Then D walked over and picked <u><u>her</u></u> up while she was <u>still</u> carrying me, and carried us <u><u>both</u></u> upstairs to the bedroom. Shenanigans of the best sort ensued, involving nudity, adult situations, mature themes, and even some harsh language from time to time. I set my phone to wake me up in time for my online classes the next morning, and the three of us drifted off. Gloria slept between me and Maria, with our hands laced together over her chest. I could have just lay there like that all night, enjoying the closeness\u2026 but I <u><u>really</u></u> needed to sleep (Spring contracts can only take you so far), and it wasn\u2019t long before biology caught up with me.<br /> <br /> So it turns out I\u2019m still trying to work out the timing of this \u201conline learning\u201d thing. I probably set my alarm for about an hour earlier than I really needed to, considering that I don\u2019t have to shower, dress, and drive into L.A. to take those classes\u2026 I can just throw on a t-shirt and some sweatpants, fire up the laptop and I\u2019m golden. So I\u2019ve been hanging out on the back balcony taking in the morning air and writing in this diary, occasionally glancing into my bedroom and fondly checking on my wife and our girlfriend.<br /> <br /> This Queen gig may dump ten thousand pounds of shit on me on a daily basis, and I may have caught the attention of a couple of all-powerful demons from an L.A. sex club\u2026 but I have to admit that the good parts of my life are still pretty fucking fantastic.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei de la Rocha</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Today started like a typical Tuesday, but it certainly didn\u2019t end that way. At least not so far. It started as usual with us going to therapy. Lori went to L.A. to go to classes, her first on campus classes too. She certainly dressed to impress. She wore a small, tight skirt and a small, tight sweater. I don\u2019t think she needed to dress like that just for class, but Lori does like the attention, so I\u2019m assuming that\u2019s why she dressed like that. Before everyone went their separate ways we discussed what we were going to do with Dakota while most everyone was away. It was decided that if any hunters came to the Dream House then we would secret Dakota away into the Hedge. Calamity pointed out that the humans couldn\u2019t follow us there. I almost suggested that we let the hunters do just that and follow us into the Hedge. Then we could leave them, but that seemed too much like something that Rime would suggest, so I kept my mouth shut on that. I was good at tricking people into following me into the Hedge and Arcadia. I really don\u2019t need to revive that part of myself.<br /> <br /> Calamity, De la Rocha, Missy, Jane, and I went to therapy as per usual. It was boring. I didn\u2019t have much to talk to Sullivan about. I certainly wasn\u2019t going to discuss my planned extracurricular activities for tonight with him. I think he would say that it is a step back for me and that it would hinder my recovery. That\u2019s probably true, but I was still going to help Luna move the bodies. That wasn\u2019t in question. After therapy we went back to the house and had our usual post-therapy workout in the back yard. We sparred with live steel like we have been for a while now. We each got a couple of scratches, but nothing more than that. We\u2019re good enough to not hurt each other when we spar.<br /> <br /> When we were finishing up our match Lori came outside and told us some interesting and upsetting news. It seems that Hollywood has decided to frame Gloria for the deaths of her motley mates, including her boyfriend. They put together some pictures of Gloria buying gasoline at a local station and the charred remains of her motley. Siobhan apparently came to Lowjack today to say that she had seen Gloria at the club and informed him that she believed her to be a murderer. Lowjack told her that Gloria was a member of the freehold in good standing. I don\u2019t know what else he said, but it sounded like he had stood up for Gloria to Siobhan to some extent at least.<br /> <br /> Luna also came by and privately complained to me that the Park Rangers were continuing their search in the woods for more bodies. They seem convinced that there are in fact more, and have made observations that the one body they found seemed to have been killed in a ritualistic fashion. Luna was upset by this because they were continuing to search for bodies in her woods, and because they said the killing looked ritualistic. She has hang ups about religion and I guess she associates that word with religion. It\u2019s not necessarily related. I think it just means that there was some pattern, or special way that the killing was committed. I haven\u2019t asked Luna about that yet. She seemed really upset this afternoon, so I figured that I\u2019d put off that conversation for later.<br /> <br /> Later that afternoon, going on evening, Calamity went to go pay a visit to the man that had tackled her on the highway the other day, Luther. She has been curious about him since the incident and has been looking into him and his affairs. She said that she wanted to apologize for what happened that day. I\u2019m assuming things went well since she returned with a Tupperware container full of spaghetti sauce and a smile on her face. I think she\u2019s going to go back there. She also said that she had offered to help him with the gangs in his neighborhood should the need arise. I know she\u2019s been wanting to get involved with that whole thing. I\u2019m just surprised that she made the offer of help to Luther before she actually did anything. I half expected her to go off on her own some day soon and deal with the gang members that she came across. Sometimes I worry about her.<br /> <br /> Once everyone was back Lori gathered the motley, plus Missy and Jane and told everyone about the accusations that Siobhan made and what she told to Lowjack. Lori assured us that Lowjack thought the whole thing was faked and said that he could come up with more convincing \u201cevidence\u201d if given the time to do so. While impressive, that statement was also a little concerning. I know that Lowjack is good at taking care of things behind the scenes, and is good at helping people disappear if needs be. I guess if he can make fake IDs then he can photoshop pictures to show what he wanted them to show. Good if used the right way I guess. Scary if he ever decided that someone in the freehold was a liability. He could fabricate whatever evidence he wanted for whatever crime he thought of. I do trust him though. He has helped me and has been good on his word to keep my secret just that, secret.<br /> <br /> At the show is when things started to get more interesting. De la Rocha used the Bluetooth radios to inform the rest of us that Soon Hee and a friend had come to the club and each checked some extensive weaponry at the door. In an effort to find out what was going on Calamity went over to talk to Soon Hee. She also ended up talking to Soon Hee\u2019s friend, who I found out is called Nakamura. She is an interesting woman. A monster hunter like Soon Hee but with one major difference. She has no face. It was actually a little disconcerting to look at her, but she mostly kept her face hidden under a hat while the show was going on. De la Rocha was especially unnerved by the whole lack of facial features of any kind. Calamity also said that Soon Hee was at the club tonight because she was following a demon friend of Da Ji\u2019s named Pipa Jing. Pipa Jing is apparently a close friend of Da Ji\u2019s and is just as dangerous to people as Da Ji is. Soon Hee warned Calamity that Pipa would try and manipulate and coax her and the rest of us into coming back to the club and there they would get their hooks in us. I don\u2019t know if she was exaggerating or not, but she seemed pretty adamant that Pipa Jing being at the club was a bad thing and would lead to bad things for us if we weren\u2019t careful.<br /> <br /> The interesting side to all of that for me was when Pipa came over to the bar to get another drink. She had already had like ten or twelve Harvey Wallbangers and I was hinting that I might cut her off, but she insisted that she was fine and truthfully she acted fine. She didn\u2019t stumble or slur her words at all. So instead I asked if she had driven here. She said that she\u2019d walked. So, I didn\u2019t need to keep up appearances and confiscate her keys. It would have looked strange for anyone watching for me not to try and cut her off or otherwise make sure that she stayed safe tonight. At the implication that I might cut her off she changed her drink order to a Black Widow instead. I shrugged and made her the drink. She knows how much alcohol she can drink before she gets impaired. I didn\u2019t feel like arguing with a demon in the middle of the bar about how many drinks she should be allowed to have.<br /> <br /> After all of that Calamity made her way over to Pipa Jing\u2019s table to talk to her. Lori talked to Soon Hee for a bit then made her way over to talk to Pipa as well. They all talked amicably for a few minutes before Lori finally pulled Calamity away from the table. I will repeat what I wrote before. I\u2019m worried for Calamity. Those people, Pipa and Da Ji, both cater to people\u2019s worst impulses, and they are targeting my friend. Calamity is tempted to give in to those darker desires. I know this. I just don\u2019t want her getting tempted into doing something that she can\u2019t undo.<br /> <br /> Once the show was over people split up into groups. Calamity, Luna and I waited until everyone had left before we gathered up our gear for our late-night excursion. Luna provided me with a Ranger\u2019s uniform to wear. Calamity had to do without since she would rip whatever she put on. Luna wore her uniform as well. If questioned we would be Rangers doing late night work in the forest. We also brought tarps, shovels, flashlights and rope as well as our usual assortment of weapons. I don\u2019t go anywhere without my knives, and Calamity is a weapon. Luna had her knives and her gun on her. I suggested that we not use our flashlights unless absolutely necessary since they could be seen from a long ways off and we were trying not to attract attention to ourselves.<br /> <br /> Once out there we quickly realized that we were being tracked by something. From the noises Luna said that it was a mountain lion. I ran into them from time to time when I went camping as a kid, but not too often, so I was glad to have Luna with me tonight. She assured us that it probably wouldn\u2019t do more than make noise at us until we left its territory. She also said that if it came close to look it straight in the eye because that would intimidate it. We nodded our understanding and continued on our way. The first body was easy enough to find and dig up. Calamity used a contract to increase her strength so she did most of the digging, which was fine by me. We gathered up the bones and any remaining clothes or items that might have been in their pockets. The second body went much the same as the first. We stopped to dig up the third body and I could tell that Luna was nervous. We asked her what was up and she said that she had stopped hearing the mountain lion a little while ago, but she still heard noise in the woods a around us. We all assumed that we were being followed so Luna called out a challenge, introducing herself as Jessica Linton of the Park Rangers, and asking whoever was in the woods to show themselves. They did. We heard them get closer all around us, and one guy showed himself but still stayed somewhat in the shadows. He asked why we were there, and Luna repeated that she was a Ranger. This didn\u2019t impress him. He repeated his question so Luna asked him if they were Uratha. He seemed to hesitate at that. He asked us if we were digging up bodies and Luna admitted that we were but explained that they had been evil men in life. That they had targeted children and women. He didn\u2019t say anything to that, so I assumed that the explanation made sense. Luna then said that we do not hunt what they hunt and that we had done nothing to take away their prey. That seemed to be enough for them\u2026<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> It\u2019s been a fairly relaxing day. I spent much of it after breakfast in Paris with Yvette. We had a wonderful time. We took a lovely walk along the Champs-\u00c9lys\u00e9es and stopped at a couple caf\u00e9s to talk and catch up. I had a calzone at one with a lot of basil and a lot of cheese that was good. Little tea cakes at another. She has successfully reclaimed her old life, it seems. Thus she was away until very recently. She admitted she is still struggling with our past, and we are slowing down our sexual connection a bit. Not stopping, but trying to keep her able to enjoy it. She does, but she often feels awful afterwards. This is not what I want to happen. I suggested the fae friendly psychologists at our hold, as she has no immediate options. She has some recommended psychologists for fae but not trained the way the Winter Court apparently did. We will see. We did do some cuddling at her townhouse, and listened to music. She intended to attend the show, and returned with me, but she was tired. Partly due to the emotional conversation, partly simply due to walking all over town. She wound up going home. I admit driving everywhere in America my own walking stamina is not what was in Paris. Cars to get anywhere. Why do they think this is a good thing? Americans are silly. Anyway.<br /> <br /> I want to help her with her issues but I may be the least able to. Perhaps I can speak to Juliette about it. Julia is sympathetic but she does not really understand? I don\u2019t think so. She spent the day working on some paid commissions. She was happy to see me home, and I promised her a cuddle tonight. Juliette was in class and met briefly with Lowjack, and Maria went out to the pier then met Twitch.<br /> <br /> It turns out Siobhan fingered Gloria as a wanted fugitive. The killing of her Motley. Siobhan apparently really thought Gloria did it? She would be wise to avoid Maria for awhile. Gloria was upset, especially about being accused of killing her boyfriend. I admit I do not blame her for this.<br /> <br /> The show went fine, I did my \u201cGirls Like Girls\u201d song I have been doing. Juliette did some of the Bon Jovi which made Gloria happy at least. After my performance I made my way up to where Julia, Melissa, Jane, Gloria and the vampire were. The latter met Yvette and they got along. Apparently. We made a hairbrushing circle. Without the vampire or Gloria. Gloria apparently had plans with Juliette and Maria.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile a demon from the mysterious place Juliette, Calamity and Jacob went to visited, and two hunters, Soon Hee and someone without a face named Nakamura were tracking her. No violence was had.<br /> <br /> After awhile, Julia, Melissa, Jane and I decided it was a shame we could not all kiss each other deeply in the balcony, so we went to the catwalks for it. I told the vampire we were introducing them to the puppets. I am very clever.<br /> <br /> Eventually we decided it was a shame to have (most of) our clothes on with all this kissing going on, so confirmed all was well and the demon was behaving herself and retired to my and Julia\u2019s room. Melissa and Jane are a fun couple to play around with. I did not anticipate it but it turned out well.<br /> <br /> And now it is time to get up. Sadness. But I am out of write and thus, excuses to stay in bed. And Melissa stole this once and started reading aloud but stopped when she read the Yvette stuff and gave it back, so I need to talk to her. She is not my wife or bride.<br /> <br /> Seriously Americans, private property! I mean I let all these people stay in my house!<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXXIII</i><br /> <br /> If Da Ji is about, Pipa Jing is not far behind. She is another character from <i>Investiture of the Gods. </i> Nakamura is a classic Noppera-B\u014d Yokai. They are a favorite of mine. In game she is a South Mirrorskin/Moonborn. Meaning I have now had one of every Court in the game but North as a PC or NPC. I need to post my updated NPC list here. Soon Hee is a West Beast, and Laughing Carp is an East Fairest.<br /> <br /> Last time I ran <b>Changeling</b>, my <i>Beyond the Sea</i> game, I had a bunch of Asian Fae in the Courts of the Dragon and like none outside it (that game had no Sun or Moon or Dawn). This time I decided while there would be Courts of the Dragon I would not make them excessively mysterious or antagonistic, unlike that game. This game I have White Maria, Dark Kimberly, Becky Wan, Davey, Louis Guo, Ji Wen Ja, Moon, Shi, Tara, Malai, Trinh Jackson, and Rosalita (mixed in the latter two cases, Trinh is also black, Rosalita Hispanic) as non Courts of the Dragon folks. I am doing better. Anyway.<br /> <br /> Only scene with little description was Calamity\u2019s meeting with Luther. It was surreal, with me describing his cooking the meet, sauce and pasta at different stages as it went on. I may have made people hungry. He eventually got enchanted, and Calamity left with a new friend and sample. Luther is generous and helpful to a fault. Hopefully it won\u2019t get him killed.<br /> <br /> Don\u2019t worry I am sure the next session will be nice and normal. Join us then. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 12-16-2018, 12:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T07:02:50-08:00","id":1274708,"title":"","content":"Hahahahaha!<br /> <br /> Please tell me the marriage proposal was RPed. That image is priceless.<br /> <br /> Also, Calamity, demons and an opportunity to go full-on Punisher/Spawn? There is not enough popcorn in the world for this. I need to find a foodstuff with more powerful &quot;happily watching batshit crazy emotional trauma&quot; symbolism. Hmmm....maybe I should contact The Director about that...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T12:32:33-08:00","id":1274753,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7920_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7920\" data-vbnamecard=\"7920\">Master Aquatosic</a> - Sorry to disappoint; the scene wasn't actually RPed. Most of Lori's time on campus was hand-waved (though I did obsess over how she dressed for her first day as a real college student, and it was mentioned that she attracted a lot of attention). When we got back to the Dream House, D asked Lori and Becky how many marriage proposals they got, and Lori replied &quot;just the one.&quot; I extrapolated when writing the journal, and the Baroness didn't object. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2591-penitenttom","name":"PenitentTom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T12:46:13-08:00","id":1274755,"title":"","content":"Yeah there is some shit with demons and demon hunters going down as they finally get more involvement with the Courts of the Dragon and Court of Fallen Angels. Granted, it could lead to problems between them depending on how it goes, and the players get to decide if they want to be peacemakers if that happens. I guess part of it depends on how hands off they decide to be with the club and it's foxy owner.","signa