br /> <br /> <br /> <b><b>South</b></b><br /> Nakamura Oyamada Darkling Mirrorskin/Moonborn (Dragon)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>West</b><br /> Soon Hee Kwon Beast Draconic/Fireheart (Dragon)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><b>Courtless</b></b><br /> Hunting Hawk Beast Windwing/Hunterheart<br /> Ocras Beast Cleareyes/Windwing (Deceased)<br /> Rook Darkling Razorhand/Mirrorskin (Deceased)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <u><u>Vampires</u></u><br /> <br /> <b><b>Carthians</b></b><br /> Sasithorn Daeva Duchagne<br /> \u201cUncle\u201d Peng Daeva Anvari<br /> Serena Gangrel Bruja <br /> Viktor Gangrel Bruja<br /> Kathy Hong \u201cWhite Bone Princess\u201d Mekhet Qedeshah<br /> <br /> <b><b>Invictus</b></b><br /> Dakota Lake Daeva Toreador<br /> <br /> --<br /> Happy Holidays. \u201cSee\u201d you Sunday next for Fish Men and cases of the Collywobbles. Comments and Questions welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-29T22:27:19-08:00","id":1277453,"title":"","content":"Our heroes take a break from their stressful schedules to reflect on Fishmen and collywobbles.<br /> <br /> Note last week I published a list of Changeling and Vampires that have appeared in the <i>Malibu Dream House</i> to help you keep things straight.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXXIV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Collywobbles and Fish-Men. That\u2019s what my life has been reduced to.<br /> <br /> Okay, so that\u2019s an oversimplification, and I\u2019m well aware of it. In all honesty, yesterday and today have served as a welcome diversion from the pressures of the monarchy\u2026 it\u2019s almost like the motley is getting back to its Scooby-Doo-esque roots. If Gawain was here, things would be almost like old times.<br /> <br /> Anyway, following my last entry I blazed through my online classes and did a bit of the required reading until the rest of the House got up for Sex Breakfast. I busied myself in the kitchen while Jacob made coffee, offering people omelets du fromage, eier mit k\u00e4se, huevos con queso, and whatever-the-hell-Jacob-said-that-phrase-was-in-Russian. I may not be Trinh, but I flatter myself that I can prepare a good old-fashioned multi-lingual American breakfast with the best of them.<br /> <br /> We sort of split up after breakfast. I wrangled a promise from Missy and Jane that they\u2019d join me and the wife that evening, then settled in to rehearse a new number with Marguerite. Becky fretted about heading off to enjoy the afternoon with Calamity until I pointed out that I\u2019d be staying in the Dream House \u2013 which is pretty much my seat of power \u2013 and protected by Maria, who can handle just about anything. When I put it that way, my loyal claviger happily agreed to take the rest of the day off and spend some time with her girlfriend. Missy and Jane went upstairs so Julia could paint a portrait of the two of them, and I dunno what Jacob and Luna got up to.<br /> <br /> So Marguerite\u2019s idea was to do a sultry rendition of Danzig\u2019s \u201cMother\u201d with simple staging, so that she could stay in one relatively small part of the stage under a solitary spot. On the edge of that spot would be her musical accompaniment\u2026 namely me, playing along on the piano in a sparkly evening gown. We\u2019d toyed with similar ideas a few times in the past, but hadn\u2019t hit upon anything that really clicked until recently. There was also the issue of finding a song which my still somewhat shaky piano skills could handle, of course\u2026 but we seemed to have hit a winner, and both of us wanted to practice a bit more before debuting the number that evening.<br /> <br /> Once we had it down pat, we talked for a bit. Marguerite wanted to talk about Yvette, who is still having some trouble adjusting to their relationship. According to my bride, Yvette often feels low following her trysts with Marguerite, as if she\u2019s somehow failed or given in to something shameful. She recognizes intellectually that this isn\u2019t really the case, but she can\u2019t just turn off her feelings. Marguerite wants her to speak with the Winter Court\u2019s psychiatrists, and I personally think that\u2019s a great idea. They\u2019ve worked wonders on like two-thirds of the motley, after all.<br /> <br /> I also agreed to speak with Yvette on Marguerite\u2019s behalf. Now I\u2019m no shrink, but most people seem to think that I have at least a modicum of insight and empathy, so I agreed to do what I could. Personally I think she needs to adjust her view of the situation slightly\u2026 to recognize how much Marguerite has changed since Arcadia and to personally own the fact that she\u2019s a big part of that. It would be a way for her to acknowledge the past but view their relationship as a victory rather than a concession. But that\u2019s just my two cents. Like I said, I\u2019m no shrink, and I\u2019m actually kind of dreading the psych courses I know I\u2019m eventually going to have to take at UCLA.<br /> <br /> I talked to Dad on the phone for a bit before it was time to start preparing for the show. He\u2019s doing well, and seems to think that the danger is passing rapidly\u2026 he\u2019s planning to come back to town in a day or two. I asked him on Calamity\u2019s behalf if he knew the names of any of the Long Night operatives who might be looking for him, and he thought about it for a moment and told me that he could probably find out if I gave him a day or two. Calamity wants to use the information to track the vampire hunters down with Contracts, and while I disapprove of preemptive violence on general principle, I have to admit that it sounds like a better idea than just sitting around here waiting for them to attack and then hoping they\u2019ve given up and gone away.<br /> <br /> I also asked Dad if he\u2019d had any luck locating a new safe haven for Dakota. I made sure that he knew she was welcome to stay with us for as long as necessary, but I really think she\u2019ll be better off with kindred who are used to providing for her\u2026 special needs. Which reminds me, she\u2019s going to need to feed again soon, and I called dibs this time.<br /> <br /> What? Calamity looked like she <u><u>really</u></u> enjoyed it\u2026<br /> <br /> Jacob overheard the tail end of my conversation with Dad and told me that he might have another option for Dakota. He was very mysterious about the whole thing, so I assume it\u2019s something hush-hush to do with either the Winter Court or his entitlement. He couldn\u2019t promise anything, but said he\u2019d investigate the possibilities and get back to me.<br /> <br /> So that brings us to last night\u2019s show. The acts were good; in addition to providing musical accompaniment for Marguerite\u2019s new number, I debuted a new duet, roping Charlie into being my partner at the last minute. \u201cDon\u2019t You Want Me\u201d by The Human League is more fun than traditionally sexy, but I think we managed to turn a few heads between the two of us. I wore a low-cut, \u201cfun\u201d dress while Charlie strutted around the stage looking smug in a pair of tight leather pants. His ass looked amazing, too\u2026 I know he\u2019s got a boyfriend, but maybe he\u2019s bi?<br /> <br /> No, Lori. Focus.<br /> <br /> Ahem. We had a fair number of changelings in the audience last night, as well as a few special mortal friends like Stasia and Elena. My first stop as I made my rounds was at the table occupied by my favorite Night-and-Day couple, Rowan and Neon. They both greeted me warmly, and Rowan sort of nervously handed me a giftwrapped package, and apologized for being a little late. Upon opening it, I found that she\u2019d kept up the Christmas tradition of giving me hand-knitted garments\u2026 this time a pair of warm leggings that perfectly complement the sweater she gave me last year. I can\u2019t wait to try them on and get up into the stratosphere! I gave her a big hug in gratitude and she beamed happily.<br /> <br /> We talked about them for a bit \u2013 they haven\u2019t had any more trouble with the Night Court \u2013 but I confess that I was a little distracted. A conversation at the bar had caught my eye\u2026 Calamity and Jacob were talking to Stasia and Elena, and both Calamity and Stasia looked entirely too pleased about something. Rowan was just saying that she and Neon were going to thank T.J. \u2013 who was currently speaking with my wife at the door \u2013 for his recent help when I saw Stasia and Calamity give each other a high five. Something obviously had to be done.<br /> <br /> \u201cExcuse me for just a scootch,\u201d I said, making a beeline for the bar.<br /> <br /> In the end it was so much worse than I feared. Stasia and Elena had gone exploring earlier in the day and had come across an abandoned building. Blithely ignoring the \u201cno trespassing\u201d signs clearly posted all around the place, they slipped into the building and started to make out. After they\u2019d had their fun, they started really looking at the place, and Stasia noticed a few irregularities. There were strange concealed switches all over the place, and when they were all flipped, a secret door opened, revealing a vast hidden basement complex.<br /> <br /> Yes, of course they continued their exploration. They found a labyrinthine complex of indeterminate purpose. There was writing in Cyrillic all over the place, and the lower levels of the complex were flooded. Both girls described the eerie sensation of being watched as they moved through the area, and when Elena did a Pippin and accidentally kicked something so that it loudly clattered down a set of stairs, that feeling only intensified. They fled the scene, and in their haste they didn\u2019t close the secret door behind them.<br /> <br /> So yes, <u><u>of</u> <u>course</u></u> Calamity wants to go back to this place and face whatever horrors might dwell within. She\u2019s privately convinced that they\u2019ve found some sort of cold war laboratory, and that it\u2019s infested with cannibalistic Russian Fish-Men. Jacob had already offered to go with her by the time I made it to the bar, and there\u2019s no way in Hell I\u2019m going to let those two put themselves in that sort of danger without me there to kiss their boo-boos all better.<br /> <br /> We decided to hold off on the expedition until the following afternoon, since most of us had plans for the evening and none of us really wanted to go snooping around a creepy abandoned Soviet installation in the dead of night. Calamity headed up to the Girlfriend Table to inform Becky of our plans (mainly so that I wouldn\u2019t have to\u2026 it\u2019s good to be the Queen) and I made a beeline for another table\u2026 this one inhabited by Veronica and Desiree.<br /> <br /> Turns out the two of them are trying out the idea of being together, and I say good for them. They don\u2019t know if they want to make a serious try at a relationship yet, but they seem pretty good together. After a few minutes of chit-chat, the two of them slid their chairs around the table and positioned themselves to either side of me. Turns out that they wanted to try to seduce me together, to see if their respective powers would increase exponentially when used together.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sorry,\u201d I said with a gasp as one of them breathed on my neck, \u201cbut I\u2019ve made other plans for the evening\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGood,\u201d Desiree said in response.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt wouldn\u2019t be much of a test otherwise,\u201d Veronica elaborated.<br /> <br /> \u201cI promised Maria\u2026\u201d I said, my resolve weakening.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019ll understand,\u201d Desiree reasoned.<br /> <br /> \u201cMissy and Jane kept tonight free for me\u2026\u201d I mumbled as my eyes fluttered shut.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sure they\u2019ll find some way to occupy themselves,\u201d Veronica purred.<br /> <br /> I sort of lost some time after that. I have a vague memory of a tongue in one of my ears at some point, and feather-light touches creeping ever higher along my legs, but my next clear recollection was of the distinctive sound of Maria clearing her throat.<br /> <br /> \u201cHi, honey,\u201d I sort of half-moaned as I forced my eyelids open.<br /> <br /> She quirked an eyebrow at me. \u201cYou need to be rescued, babe?\u201d she asked nonchalantly.<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cThey\u2019re working together to try to <u><u>seduce</u></u> me,\u201d I explained (possibly unnecessarily). \u201cAnd I <u><u>told</u></u> them we had plans tonight, but they wouldn\u2019t listen\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay then,\u201d she said, and she swooped in and scooped me up in her arms and started to carry me away to the Girlfriend Table.<br /> <br /> \u201cCome back tomorrow night,\u201d I called back to the pair of them softly, \u201cor maybe Friday. Or just call me if you want to set up another time\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> They allowed as how they might contact me soon, and I let Maria deposit me on a chair next to Becky and Missy. I let the conversation wash around me until I started to regain my faculties a bit, so I\u2019m not certain exactly how the talk turned the way it did\u2026<br /> <br /> Poor Missy. At some point, while talking about something that made her uncomfortable, Missy made the mistake of saying that it \u201cgave her the collywobbles.\u201d Now, growing up forty-plus years ago in Defiance, that was the sort of thing that you just heard everywhere and took for granted. In Southern California in 2016, the phrase is decidedly less common. People didn\u2019t let that go for close to an hour, and I\u2019m convinced that the only reason they stopped saying it at that point was because Jane sent us all a surreptitious text to let us know that Missy was starting to get genuinely upset about it.<br /> <br /> Once the crowds cleared we started to break up and head to bed. Becky and Calamity sauntered off together, of course, and Julia and Marguerite had invited Trinh to join them to compensate for the temporary loss of Missy and Jane (who seem to have really bonded with the Oldacres). That left me, Maria, and my two best friends to keep each other company, just as I had planned.<br /> <br /> Maria\u2019s been hoping to get the three of us into bed together practically since we got back from Arcadia, and I don\u2019t think she had any complaints about the results. It gets a little crowded on that bed when you try to cram four people into it\u2026 especially when three of those people have enormous wings attached to their backs. But we didn\u2019t mind snuggling up really close. And Missy, Jane and I long ago learned the best ways to spoon without spraining anything or accidentally pulling out any feathers.<br /> <br /> So an hour or two of passion gave way to a few more hours of blissful slumber surrounded by many of those closest to me. It\u2019s been so long since I slept alone that I\u2019m starting to wonder if I\u2019d be able to sleep without the warmth of a lover lying next to me\u2026 without the feel of their heart beating against my own skin. I\u2019ve been blessed in that way. Loneliness isn\u2019t something I really have to worry about anymore.<br /> <br /> The four of us rose early as usual this morning. The shower in my bathroom isn\u2019t really big enough for four, so we paired off\u2026 the Ms and the Js (that is to say, Maria and Missy showered together, and Jane and Juliette did likewise). The three of them got dressed and headed off to therapy with Jacob and Calamity while Becky and I headed into L.A. for my second day on campus.<br /> <br /> Work began in earnest in the lecture classes today, and I had my first Bio lab. I confess that I spent a few minutes idly flirting with Trish, a cute brunette who happens to be my new lab partner, but we managed to stick to business once we actually had a task to complete. I find that I\u2019m actually sort of <u><u>enjoying</u></u> being back in classes, which is something I didn\u2019t really expect considering my somewhat adversarial history with High School in general. Maybe the fact that I\u2019ve worked so hard to get here \u2013 that I <u><u>want</u></u> to be here; that I\u2019m actually <u><u>paying</u></u> to be here \u2013 is causing this radical shift in my attitude. Whatever. I\u2019m not going to question it; I\u2019m just going to accept it as fact.<br /> <br /> We didn\u2019t run into Mari Lwyd or any of the other L.A. courtiers on this particular trip, so Becky and I hopped into the \u2018vette and headed back to Malibu as soon as the lab was dismissed. When we got back, we found that Trinh had cooked breakfast, and had thought to save each of us a plate, which was very nice of her. And it was the mild sausage, which was even <u><u>nicer</u></u> of her.<br /> <br /> So now breakfast is done \u2013 even for us latecomers \u2013 and everyone\u2019s starting to get excited about heading out to this abandoned lab or whatever it is. And I have to confess, I\u2019m excited too. Like I said earlier, it\u2019s starting to feel like old times, before we settled in and became all respectable. Before I became Queen. And as much as I might have railed against the dangers we faced back in the old days, I have to admit that it felt nice to be part of a team like that. If we can recapture that feeling, even just a little bit today\u2026 well, maybe facing down a horde of communist Fish-Men won\u2019t be so bad.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei de la Rocha</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> \u2026They left us to our evening and we left them to theirs. I think they said that they were hunting a werecat. I honestly didn\u2019t know that they existed. I knew about werewolves, but that\u2019s just because of my association with Luna. So, overall our evening was a success. We dug up the bodies and did our best to cover up the fact that we\u2019d been digging holes in the ground. We put sod back where we could and covered the rest with leaves or other kinds of underbrush. Hopefully anyone looking won\u2019t notice that the ground has been disturbed. It would not be good if the other Park Ranger\u2019s noticed that the ground was broken in different places. They might think that the killer came back to move the bodies and had some inclination that the Rangers were doing a search. As far as I know the finding of the one body has not been made public knowledge, which means that the only people that know about the body would be Rangers. That would make a short list of suspects.<br /> <br /> Eventually we got the bodies moved and got back to the Dream House. It was nearly dawn by the time we did get back, so Calamity had to take a quick shower and head right back out to meet White Maria for meditation and Tai Chi. Luna and I showered and headed for bed. I for one was a bit sore. I did help with the digging and we all helped actually carrying the bodies, so I\u2019d say I got my exercise in for the day, well night.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Today started out as kind of a lazy day. We had breakfast. Lori made cheese omelets for everyone and called them something different depending on the native language of the person getting them. She said it in French for Insincere Marguerite and Julia, Spanish for De la Rocha and I think she mumbled something in German. I thought I\u2019d help with her education and tell her how to say cheese omelet in Russian. She just looked at me when I said that. I don\u2019t think she was keen on learning any new languages. So, I just smiled and accepted my breakfast. I almost told her what coffee was in Russian when I handed Lori her cup but restrained myself at the last moment. After breakfast we all split up and went out separate ways. I know that Julia went upstairs with Missy and Jane to paint them. I think Lori and Insincere Marguerite were practicing their number for tonight. Luna and I claimed the television in the game room and proceeded to watch Netflix. We ended up binge watching some Daredevil. It was good. The guy that they go to play Matt Murdock makes a good blind man. His mannerisms and how his eyes wander is really spot on. He is a superhero with super senses, so it\u2019s not all realistic, but it\u2019s pretty good. His portrayal reminded me of someone in the Lady\u2019s realm. It was one of the Lady\u2019s favorites. A woman called Twilight. She had dark dusky skin and midnight black hair. I don\u2019t know how she ended up in the Lady\u2019s realm. I just know that she was one of the Lady\u2019s most prized Treasures. Twilight was blind, but once she knew her way around the palace she could get from place to place as if she were sighted. The Lady never let Twilight wear sunglasses, so everyone could see that her eyes wandered, but it did nothing to detract from her beauty. I hope that she\u2019s okay. She was always nice to Rook and me when we were in the palace. <br /> <br /> Early on I went out to get drinks and I overheard Lori talking to her dad on the phone about the Long Night vampire hunter\u2019s names and if he knew any of them. It sounded like she was seeing if it might be possible for Calamity to track one of these guys back to where they\u2019re staying. She also asked him if he had any leads on finding a new place for Dakota to live so we can move her out of the basement. I stuck around for a moment and when she got off the phone, I told her that I might know of a way to relocate Dakota safely but I\u2019d have to ask someone first if it was possible. I figured that the Knighthood of the Utmost Silence does that kind of stuff for Changelings, we might be able to do it for a vampire. So, after I talked to Lori I called Lowjack and we discussed the options. His main concern was just how we would feed Dakota while she was in our safehouse. I will admit that I had the same concerns. I told him that I would ask Dakota how often she needed to eat and see what kind of time frame we were looking at. Lowjack also mentioned that vampires can be put in a kind of suspended animation if they are staked through the heart. I thought that would kill them, but apparently it does not. He also mentioned freezing her in a freezer truck with the temp dropped really low. I don\u2019t know if Dakota will go for either of those options, but we\u2019ll see what comes of our research. There has to be a way to get her safely out of the city and into friendly company without too much bodily harm to our guest.<br /> <br /> Then came the show like usual. This time though both Insincere Marguerite and Lori introduced new acts. I thought that they were well done. I didn\u2019t realize that Lori could play piano so well, but she did a really good job when she accompanied Marguerite on stage. My interest however was taken up by other things. Stasia and Elena were at the show and came to the bar to hang out. Apparently Elena wanted to tell me about what she and her fianc\u00e9e had been up to and see if I\u2019d be interested in going with them the next time. It turns out that they were hiking in the woods nearby and found an old abandoned building and decided to investigate it. They \u201cinvestigated\u201d each other for a bit, which was probably too much information for me to hear, before exploring the building. In it they found several levers that if turned opened a secret hatch. Now, these levers were not easy to find, and the hatch was well hidden, but Stasia is nothing if not persistent and she found them all. They then went down the hatch into an underground part of the building to explore what they had found. From what they said it seemed like a lab of some sort and all of the signage was in Cyrillic, which was interesting. They found some paperwork, but nothing had a date on it so they don\u2019t know how long this place has been there. At one point Elena accidentally kicked something down the stairs and it made a loud crashing noise. Then they heard the sound of running water. After that they said that the feeling of being watched, which had been present since they went down the hatch, increased and they fled back up the stairs.<br /> <br /> They wanted to go back to see what else they could find, but wanted someone to go with them. I of course said I would go. And by that point Calamity had come over to join the conversation. She came over initially to talk to her friend but ended up getting roped into the conversation about abandoned buildings in the middle of the woods. They didn\u2019t want to include Luna at first, but I convinced them that it might be a good idea. If there was something in the woods Luna might know more about it than they do. And she did. Apparently there have been problems in the past of people going missing in that area of the woods. It makes me wonder if someone else discovered the same hatch that Stasia did and they got themselves in trouble. Somehow this brought ideas of Russian fish men to Calamity\u2019s mind and she kept going on about stabbing them. Honestly, we don\u2019t know what\u2019s down there, but for all we know there might be fish men. The bottom levels of the complex are all underwater so it\u2019s impossible to know what\u2019s really down there. I\u2019m curious what the place was and why it was so well hidden in the first place.<br /> <br /> At some point Lori came by the bar to see what we were up to. She had gotten curious when she saw us all hanging out and Calamity and Stasia high fiving one another. So, we explained to her what Stasia and Elena had found and what we had planned next. We were going to go back and if nothing else close that hatch since they left it open when they fled. Lori seemed exasperated with us, but said that she was coming along with us to keep us in one piece in case of trouble. She seems to think that we go looking for trouble. I suppose that is a valid concern when we intentionally go hunting hedge beasts but this time it was just going to be some semi-urban exploring. We should be fine, though I\u2019m not complaining that she wants to come too. It should be interesting. We decided to go tomorrow afternoon, so we\u2019d be able to get a good night\u2019s sleep before out little adventure and we\u2019d be able to explore the building and it\u2019s basements in the daytime.<br /> <br /> Later, after Lori and Calamity had gone off socializing with the guests in the club Insincere Marguerite came over to talk and asked if I had a kit to go urban exploring with. I admitted that I did not but admitted that a kit would be good to have. She said that people tend to bring stuff like chalk and candles to find their way back out as well as flashlights and other kinds of markers. She asked if Elena and Stasia had gone with a kit, and I said that Elena is a very practical girl and I\u2019d be surprised if she had gone without something like that. I asked if Marguerite wanted to join us and she said that she would like to if it was okay. I told here that of course it was okay if she came with us. She has a lot more experience urban exploring than we do, so we\u2019d be nuts to turn her down. I guess I just need to get some chalk, candles and stuff to make my own kit for this little trip that we\u2019re taking tomorrow.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> I may have had to get up early this morning, but I was in a good mood. I am looking forward to our trip this afternoon. So, Calamity, Missy, Jane, De la Rocha and I all got up and went to therapy. Sullivan noticed that I was in a good mood and asked why, so I told him what we were up to. I left out the bit about Elena and Stasia feeling like they were being watched. I just focused on the mysterious building and wanting to check it out with friends. I\u2019m not sure how much Sullivan really supported my idea of urban exploring, but he didn\u2019t tell me that I shouldn\u2019t do it. He just told me to be careful and to not get caught. I think he was just as concerned about the trespassing aspect of things as Luna was last night. She still agreed to come with us though. I assured him that we would be careful and that I\u2019d let him know what we found at our next session. He seemed somewhat mollified by that. At least he didn\u2019t try and talk me out of it.<br /> <br /> Then there was sparring and food. In that order. I don\u2019t know what we\u2019re going to find in that old lab, or whatever it is, but I figured that it couldn\u2019t hurt to be on our toes when we go there. And nothing gets me in a heightened state of awareness better than sparring with a skilled opponent. After that though we showered and came back down for breakfast. The food was good and the conversation was pretty much par for the course. There was teasing and talks of bosoms. We finally told De la Rocha about our pans and she was all about joining us once she realized that Lori was coming with us. Calamity went into her fish man story again and Trinh offered to fry up whatever fish men/creatures we found down there. I don\u2019t know if I want to eat anything that we find in that lab or whatever it is, but I\u2019m still keen on going. I can\u2019t wait to find out what\u2019s down there.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> What a day. A lot of successes, a lot of strangeness.<br /> <br /> I talked to Juliette about the act idea. I will be doing \u201cMother\u201d by Danzig as a low sultry song. Juliette will be on piano. I think it can go well. And it will be nice to perform with her. So we practiced much of the afternoon. I did ask her about Yvette, and she supported my idea of Yvette going to therapy locally. While she understood Yvette\u2019s struggle, she was unsure how to advise past that.<br /> <br /> Also around breakfast, Julia and I spent time cuddled up with Melissa and Jane. We seem to have gotten closer to that couple, and they are very dear people. Julia even decided to paint the pair of them. Jane is protective, and Melissa is sweet like honey. According to Juliette they are even beginning to function apart. We will see how things go and how close we get, but they have really opened up to us, which makes me happy. Definitely.<br /> <br /> Juliette dropped significant hints she wanted to be with Melissa and Jane for herself and Maria, so I called Trinh, and she agreed to come by for a good snuggle\u2026and breakfast!<br /> <br /> The show went well, there performing with my bride Juliette. Her wonderful piano playing was very helpful. Afterwards, I dedicated much of my attention to Trinh, as did Julia. However, as always, my Motley found themselves to be in no way bored.<br /> <br /> Apparently Stasia and Elena found a building that had a hidden area, which has a lot of Cyrillic writing. Part of it is underwater, which lead Calamity to babble about stabbing\u2026unseen\u2026fish men. I think Calamity may be ill. I should check her again. Anyway, there was much excitement about that from the less well-adjusted of the Motley.<br /> <br /> Though I do admit some more Urban Exploring would be fun. I took Jacob on a trip when he wanted to learn more about us. Maybe he enjoyed it too much\u2026<br /> <br /> Juliette wished to go, but only because, of course, she wisely had concerns about Calamity and Jacob. She and Maria sat with Melissa and Jane and discussed the Collywobbles. Yes, an English word I do not know. They said it over and over again to make fun of me I think. It was rather irritating. I did not sleep with any of them.<br /> <br /> Julia stayed with Trinh and I, and we had a lovely night. Trinh is a really fun person. That morning, we had breakfast, Trinh cooked, and it was delicious. Juliette was at school with Becky, so not there. We discussed in impeding exploration going on, Trinh, for her part, said if we killed a fish man, she would cook it.<br /> <br /> Trinh is odd.<br /> <br /> I talked to Yvette a bit today, and I think I convinced her to try Therapy. I will go with her. Maybe I can repair relations with her further.<br /> <br /> But for now, we get ready to explore an abandoned decaying building. Eh, it could be worse.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXXIV</i><br /> <br /> Oh yeah. The collywobbles. You know it is not always about you Mrs. Oldacre.<br /> <br /> The fishmen thing was 100% Calamity. I am not sure where it came from either. She is kind of an odd duck.<br /> <br /> So what is down there? Find out next time. Comments and Questions welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T21:36:31-08:00","id":1280444,"title":"","content":"The group travels to abandoned building in the mountains and what they find is strange beyond what anyone could have expected.<br /> <br /> Stay for a chilling story guaranteed to give you the collywobbles.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXXV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> That was either one of the most terrifying experiences of my life, or a refreshing return to form for our monster-fighting motley. Or maybe that\u2019s just the supernaturally-induced anemia speaking.<br /> <br /> Ahem. So spoiler alert, as the kids are saying these days\u2026 the secret subterranean facility Stasia and Elena uncovered the other day did not in fact contain Commie Fish-Men, much to Calamity\u2019s chagrin. The truth of the place was far stranger \u2013 and far more dangerous \u2013 than any of our theories could have predicted, and I get the collywobbles just thinking about it.<br /> <br /> So I descended from my boudoir fully prepared for urban exploring\u2026 by which I mean I had put on a pair of tight rubber pants that really flattered my ass and grabbed a pack prepared by people with far more experience. I walked right into an argument between Marguerite and Gloria. Gloria wanted to come along with us, and Marguerite didn\u2019t think it was a good idea to include another \u201camateur.\u201d Of course tough-as-nails Gloria bristled at that, and it fell to Maria and me to soothe her frazzled ego.<br /> <br /> In the end nine of us piled into the Mystery Machine and headed out on this routine expedition (I can make my own complicated mixed pop culture references that nobody in this day and age gets, dammit). The final roster was me, Maria, Marguerite, Calamity, Jacob, Luna, Stasia, Elena, and Becky\u2026 the latter intending to wait outside of the facility and secure our escape route. Since we\u2019d almost certainly lose cell reception as soon as we set foot in the place, we also brought a pair of walkie-talkies. Becky was given one of them, and yours truly was entrusted with the other.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s right\u2026 I was the highest ranking member of the party, the medic, <u><u>and</u></u> the one with the radio. Every single World War II movie I\u2019d ever seen was screaming that I\u2019d be the first one taken out. Joy.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t know how long it would take us to fillet all the fish-men, so I called up Dark Kimberly and asked her to take over management of the show for the evening. She agreed to do so, and quickly started contacting our regular performers to let them know that we\u2019d have to shake up the planned lineup a bit. I also called John, just to let him know where we\u2019d be in case we didn\u2019t come back. I think that poor man is honestly starting to dread hearing from me\u2026<br /> <br /> It took us more than an hour and a half to drive and hike up to the facility in question. It didn\u2019t look like much from the outside; just your basic small industrial building. It was fairly nondescript. You wouldn\u2019t look twice at a place like that if it wasn\u2019t out there in the middle of nowhere, surrounded by woods.<br /> <br /> It wasn\u2019t so bad at first, though things got very creepy pretty quickly. The hatch was standing open just as Stasia and Elena had described it, and we descended into the depths with some trepidation. Marguerite and Calamity took point, the former on the walls and ceilings while the latter remained on the floor with the rest of us. Jacob and Luna took up the rear-guard position so that nothing could sneak up behind us. That left Maria to guard us non-combatants in the middle.<br /> <br /> D was\u2026 quiet as we moved through the industrial corridors. I didn\u2019t think much of it at first, but as time passed, she seemed to withdraw more and more into herself. She hung back from the group, or moved off to a side, and seemed to stick to the shadows wherever possible (which was a lot of places, as the whole subterranean complex was unlit and we were relying on flashlights to see). More on that in a moment.<br /> <br /> We saw enough of the Cyrillic writing for Jacob to tell us that it wasn\u2019t actually Russian. Stasia added that it wasn\u2019t Ukrainian either, though neither of them recognized what the language actually <u><u>was</u></u>. We eventually found ourselves in something resembling a small kitchenette or office break room. They had a small refrigerator and a single-burner stove, but no microwave. The equipment looked a little old-fashioned (even to me, though it probably wouldn\u2019t have elicited much of a comment in 1978). There was a flag on the wall, but none of us recognized it at the time.<br /> <br /> In addition to the door through which we had entered, four hallways converged on this area. Stasia and Elena told us that they had explored two of those hallways; one of them ended in a block of offices while the other terminated in a stairway to the flooded lower levels. We decided to explore the top level further before venturing down, and selected one of the other passageways.<br /> <br /> The hallway was long and institutional, almost clinical. It terminated in a metal door leading to what turned out to be a supply closet, with three sets of windowed double doors opening at various points along its length. All three of these were bound shut with heavy chains and secured with large padlocks. Calamity, peering through one of the windows, said that she could see a crouched figure huddled up in one corner of one of the rooms, and both Marguerite and Jacob confirmed it.<br /> <br /> Calamity asked D to break the chains to open the door, but D didn\u2019t respond immediately, and I suggested that maybe someone should pick the lock instead so that we could re-secure the door if necessary. I confess that I mostly wanted to draw attention away from the fact that my wife was starting to regress a bit into her Arcadian state. Nevertheless, Stasia stepped forward and started to pick the lock.<br /> <br /> I should have anticipated the trouble, I suppose. The odd, unearthly atmosphere of the place, the feeling of being watched and stalked, and the clinical appearance of the hallways all combined to create an ambiance certain to awaken bad memories in my wife. I surreptitiously did a little kenning to see if we\u2019d somehow slipped into Arcadia\u2026 into the Hospital. We hadn\u2019t. Something big and magical had happened in that place a long time ago, but whatever it was, it wasn\u2019t Fae in nature. I breathed a sigh of relief.<br /> <br /> I walked up to Maria, who was standing up against the far wall in the shadows, her eyes wide and unblinking and her pupils highly dilated. At least she hadn\u2019t developed the rictus grin yet. \u201cBabe?\u201d I said as I slipped up beside her.<br /> <br /> She nodded.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou okay?\u201d I asked softly.<br /> <br /> She nodded again, but didn\u2019t speak.<br /> <br /> I sighed. I hated to do it, because I didn\u2019t want her to think that I had no confidence in her, but the longer she stayed in that place the worse it was going to get. \u201cSweetie,\u201d I said, taking one of her hands in my own, \u201cI think you should head upstairs and back Becky up. I\u2019d feel better knowing that you\u2019re guarding our backs.\u201d<br /> <br /> She stared at me for a moment, then nodded, squeezed my hand, and sort of\u2026 loped back the way we came. She\u2019d run doubled over on two legs for a while, then push off the floor with her knuckles. Once she was out of sight, I counted to twenty and then pulled out the walkie and called Becky. \u201cMaria\u2019s on her way out,\u201d I said softly.<br /> <br /> \u201cIs that what that sound is?\u201d Becky replied. \u201cThank God.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIf she\u2019s not out there in five minutes, call and let me know,\u201d I said sharply. She promised to do so, and I put the walkie away.<br /> <br /> Stasia had managed to get the door open by that point, and we discovered\u2026 nothing. Well, not <u><u>nothing</u></u>, but there was nobody in the room. The room had windows, though\u2026 windows that looked out upon\u2026 dirt, since we were underground. But it was obvious at this point that the structure hadn\u2019t been <u><u>designed</u></u> as an underground complex.<br /> <br /> Calamity used a couple of contracts at this point. First, she gave herself the ability to see and hear ghosts, and discovered that the room\u2019s occupant hadn\u2019t fled as far as we\u2019d thought. She told us that the ghost didn\u2019t speak English, but seemed to respond when Jacob spoke in Russian. Calamity used another contract to allow the rest of us to hear the ghost, and we played the strangest game of telephone in which I\u2019d ever been involved.<br /> <br /> The ghost was a woman who had been employed as a scientist in that facility in 1962. Between her testimony, the flag, and a map we\u2019d found, we were able to determine that the facility was originally built on the side of a mountain about a hundred miles from Sofia, Bulgaria. It had been a super-science weapons research laboratory during the Cold War. They\u2019d been researching teleportation via radio waves \u2013 an idea they had gotten from some mysterious (presumably supernatural) source \u2013 and they had succeeded, kind of.<br /> <br /> She said that their early subjects came back <u><u>changed</u></u>. They spoke in strange cadences, and their eyes seemed darkened somehow. They possessed great strength beyond anything a mortal should have, and they were dangerously insane. Those first few subjects managed to get loose, and used the machine to teleport the entire facility and everyone in it. Most of the inhabitants went insane. Those few who retained their wits managed to lock the rest away on the facility\u2019s lower levels, and then flood those levels.<br /> <br /> The ghost lady was killed by her own husband\u2026<br /> <br /> She told us a few other things as well, though her knowledge of the events since her death was spotty at best. She mentioned that there was another ghost in the building, and that this other ghost was dangerous. It was insane, and able to use its powers to affect the physical world. We decided to avoid the passageway we\u2019d neglected earlier, as that was supposed to be this other ghost\u2019s domain.<br /> <br /> The ghost seemed to believe that shutting down the machine would put a stop to the creatures below, but that posed several problems. First, the machine was underwater and behind the sealed hatch. So to even get to it, we\u2019d have to risk letting the creatures loose and either drain the water or swim to it. Marguerite offered to come back at some point with SCUBA gear, since she is very stealthy and can see in the dark without a light source, but we all pretty much vetoed that idea immediately. None of us wanted to put her in that sort of danger.<br /> <br /> We all agreed, however, that it would be foolish to leave without checking to make sure the creatures below were as tightly confined as the ghost believed. If they got loose, they could wreak awful destruction across the Freehold and beyond. So, resigned, we made our way toward the stairway and began to descend.<br /> <br /> We\u2019d only made it down about one landing when it struck. Something grabbed hold of Calamity\u2019s ankles and tried to pull her off the stairway to her death. Luckily Jacob and Marguerite acted quickly, grabbing at her wrists and pulling her back to safety. The creature let go of Calamity and plummeted into the darkness below, but not before we got a quick look at it. According to Calamity, it looked like the ghost we\u2019d just been speaking with, but with a horribly broken neck.<br /> <br /> The creature survived the fall; according to Marguerite\u2019s darkvision, it was hobbling around on the bottom level with a fractured tibia poking out of its leg. It was no fool; it didn\u2019t want to tangle with all of us when we were expecting it. It taunted us in what I can only assume was Bulgarian, trying to lure us down to face it. It must have had friends down there\u2026 but we opted not to go any further.<br /> <br /> In a shocking display of good sense, we pretty much unanimously agreed that discretion was the better part of valor. As we were discussing this, the creature crept quietly back up the stairs brandishing something in its hand. Marguerite kept a surreptitious eye on it, and when it threw its weapon at Calamity, she was ready for it, and caught the projectile one-handed. Elena softly said something along the lines of \u201chey, that\u2019s my flashlight,\u201d and the creature limped away once more.<br /> <br /> We withdrew pretty quickly after that, heading for the exit by the most expeditious route and sealing the door tightly behind us. Jacob and Luna did a quick search of the building\u2019s perimeter to see if any of the creatures had escaped. They were able to determine that something with child-sized feet had left the building relatively recently, and then returned some time later, and Calamity used another contract to make sure that whatever had left those tracks was back where it belonged before we sealed the building off.<br /> <br /> Becky and Maria were waiting for us at the van, Becky looking a little spooked and Maria still uncharacteristically quiet. Luna called the Forestry Service to see if anything odd or violent had occurred in the area over the last few days; there was one report of a missing hiker, but he had turned up the next day no worse for wear. She said she would check on him tomorrow anyway, just to see if he has dark eyes or speaks with strange inflections.<br /> <br /> I had three missed calls and one voicemail from my Dad. His message was fairly agitated, asking me to call him as soon as I got it, so I did so.<br /> <br /> \u201cJuliette,\u201d he said with a sigh of relief as soon as he picked up.<br /> <br /> \u201cHi Dad,\u201d I said, \u201care you okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI am fine,\u201d he replied. \u201cI think I shall probably return home tomorrow; things should be safe enough. But what about <u><u>you</u></u>? I\u2026 I had a feeling earlier today that you were in danger. I called you several times but received no answer. I contacted the Freehold, and was informed that you were exploring some abandoned and potentially monster-infested ruin?\u201d<br /> <br /> I chuckled at the description. \u201cYes, that\u2019s true as far as it goes,\u201d I told him. \u201cThe facility was left open a few days ago, and something could have gotten out and harmed my people, so it was our duty to make sure that didn\u2019t happen. But I was pretty safe. Maria and Becky were here to protect me, along with most of the rest of the motley. We\u2019re heading home now, and we\u2019ve sealed the ruins behind us.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m very glad to hear that,\u201d he said fervently.<br /> <br /> \u201cDid you find any names for Calamity to investigate?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cI should have something for you by the time I return to Malibu,\u201d he assured me. \u201cPerhaps you could come over and help me unpack\u2026 and maybe even stay for dinner?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019d love to,\u201d I said, \u201cas long as it\u2019s an early dinner. I can\u2019t miss a Friday show. Maybe I\u2019ll even bring the missus along.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMaria is always welcome here,\u201d he replied. \u201cShe\u2019s family.\u201d<br /> <br /> We said our goodbyes, and I called Lowjack again. I asked if he could meet with the motley on our way back into town at the bar, and he hesitantly agreed. \u201cIs it as bad as you thought it would be?\u201d he asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cWorse,\u201d I said.<br /> <br /> There was a pause. His next question was posed lightly, but I could hear how deadly serious he was behind the joke. \u201cDid you find a massive theater with duplicates of all of us in residence?\u201d he asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo,\u201d I said. \u201cI did a little kenning while we were there, and the place wasn\u2019t Arcadian. It was both more mundane and a lot stranger, in a weird way.\u201d<br /> <br /> He chewed on that for a moment. \u201cI can be there in forty-five minutes,\u201d he said.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe won\u2019t be far behind you,\u201d I promised him.<br /> <br /> The ride back into town was pretty quiet for the most part. I spent much of it snuggled up between Maria and Marguerite, trying to give and receive comfort in equal measure. Maria came back to herself for the most part during the ride. She was still very quiet, but she was definitely coming back from wherever she\u2019d been.<br /> <br /> We arrived at Lowjack\u2019s in time to witness Halley\u2019s exit. She was stuffing something that looked suspiciously like a laser rifle into a duffel bag as we entered, but did everything she could to draw attention away from that fact. She apologized for not coming by the Dream House much lately, and promised that she\u2019d rectify that situation as soon as she could.<br /> <br /> John had Tamara lock the door and put up the \u201cBack in Five Minutes\u201d sign after Halley left, since there were too many of us to comfortably fit in John\u2019s office. We gave him the run-down of everything we had seen and learned in the facility, and he considered it carefully. \u201cYou did exactly the right thing,\u201d he said after a moment. \u201cYou assessed the threat, then got out to report it. Most importantly, you sealed the complex off so that nothing could get out. I\u2019ll probably call a meeting of the four monarchs within the next few days so we can discuss a more permanent solution to the problem. I know your schedule, Lorelei, and I\u2019ll try to work with it. I\u2019d just ask that Luna let me know what she learns from this missing hiker as soon as possible\u2026 we might have to make it an <u><u>emergency</u></u> meeting, depending on the results of that investigation.\u201d<br /> <br /> He had noted aloud at one point that Maria wasn\u2019t acting quite like herself. I know why he pointed it out; we were discussing a supernatural threat that possessed people and caused them to act oddly, after all. Maria responded as you might expect, asking him if he would prefer it if she threatened to kick his ass through the bar\u2019s front window. John seemed to accept that, and moved on.<br /> <br /> He and I spoke privately in his office before we left, and I explained why Maria was acting differently in general terms. I told him that I would keep an eye on her over the next few days just to be on the safe side, but that he shouldn\u2019t worry about her being a danger to the Freehold or anything like that. I don\u2019t know if he took me at my word or not, but he at least had the grace to pretend that he trusted my judgment on that matter, so I\u2019ll count that as a win.<br /> <br /> When we got back to the Dream House, well\u2026 I probably <u><u>technically</u></u> could have participated in the show if I\u2019d rushed to clean up and get into costume and makeup, but\u2026 nah. As Queen, we exercised our royal prerogative to play hookey and relax for an evening. I took a luxurious hot shower, washing my hair at least twice to make sure I got all the dust and cobwebs out of it. I considered taking John\u2019s suggestion and using something called a \u201cbath bomb,\u201d but I\u2019m not really much of a bath person anymore with the wings. The only reason I\u2019m able to indulge with Oleander is that she has a detached tub at her place, so it\u2019s easier to drape my wings over the edge.<br /> <br /> After my shower I threw on a t-shirt and some sweatpants and headed to the Media Room with Maria. We decided to watch a couple of silly, mindless action movies on Netflix, and I snuggled up close to her and just basked in the love. After the first flick was over, she leaned in and apologized. I didn\u2019t have to ask her what it was for.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou never have to apologize to me for that, Maria,\u201d I said. \u201cI love every part of you and I always will. And we all struggle against our Arcadian selves\u2026 do you know how hard it is for me to be in this house while a show is going on and <u><u>not</u></u> rush down there to prove that I\u2019m better than the rest of the performers?\u201d<br /> <br /> We left it at that and put on another movie. As midnight approached, I remembered that I actually <u><u>did</u></u> have another commitment that evening, though it was one that wouldn\u2019t take me away from Maria for long. After the flick was over and the House had started to empty out, I made my way down to the theater and found Dakota. We made small talk for a minute or two, and I let her know that Dad would be coming back into town the next day.<br /> <br /> \u201cLook, I just want to thank you guys again for putting me up like this,\u201d she said sincerely. \u201cYour dad is a wonderful guy, but\u2026 there\u2019s not a lot to do at his place. I really appreciate your hospitality.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe\u2019re happy to have you,\u201d I said, \u201cthough that does remind me of something. I know you\u2019ve been kind of limited in your ability to feed lately. Are you feeling a bit\u2026 peckish?\u201d<br /> <br /> She grinned shyly. \u201cI could eat,\u201d she said softly after a moment.<br /> <br /> I held out both of my arms, stroking along my inner wrists, and then inclined my head at a coquettish angle.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhere do you want it?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> I tugged at the neck of my t-shirt, exposing my throat. She leaned in, bared her fangs, and\u2026 golly.<br /> <br /> I mean\u2026 wow.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d heard about the heightened sense of pleasure people feel when vampires feed on them, and it was one of the reasons I\u2019d been so curious to experience it for myself. The reports were not exaggerated. While it might be a bit much to refer to the experience as \u201corgasmic\u201d \u2013 and I consider myself something of an authority on the subject of orgasms \u2013 I can certainly see how some people might become addicted to the sensation.<br /> <br /> I was pretty woozy, so Dakota offered to carry me up to my bedroom. I\u2019m not sure if it was the blood loss or the post-feeding haze, but I don\u2019t think I could have walked under my own power at that point. In fact, I have a dim recollection of seeing Marguerite, Julia, Missy and Jane frolicking in the upstairs hallway wearing nothing but edible body paint, though that might have been a hallucination.<br /> <br /> Dakota tucked me in and went back downstairs, and D showed up a few minutes later. By that point I\u2019d used Spring contracts to replenish my blood, leaving only a warm blissful feeling. We peeled off our clothes and slipped under the covers, sharing our love as only two people who know each other exceptionally well can. Then I set the alarm, slipped back into her embrace, and let everything else fall away from me until it was time for class this morning.<br /> <br /> Life can be pretty grand, even when it decides to throw you the occasional curve ball. Like, y\u2019know, Bulgarian teleport zombies.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei de la Rocha</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Well that could have gone better. Not that anything bad happened to us. Not really, but we did find out some stuff that just makes the problem of the industrial building in the middle of the woods a little bit more pressing. Part of me wishes that Stasia hadn\u2019t been so clever in figuring out how to open that hatch, and another part of me is glad that we know about the problem so we can do something about it. Lori made a few calls before we left to take care of things in case we were out longer than expected. She called Dark Kimberly to manage the show and Lowjack so someone in a position of authority would know where we had gone. So, we all piled into the van and headed towards the woods. It was me, Luna, Calamity, Insincere Marguerite, Lori, De la Rocha, Stasia, Elena and Becky. Becky was coming along so she could wait by the entrance with a walkie talkie in case we needed her to call for help. The trip through the woods was uneventful; the trip into the complex was not.<br /> <br /> Getting in was fine. We started laying a trail of tea candles so we could find our way back out. We packed a good bit of supplies, which I thought was a good idea. We brought flashlights, tea candles, glowsticks, food, water rope, and empty bottles (just in case). We started where Stasia and Elena had already been and found the same signs that they told us about. They were in fact in Cyrillic but they were not in Russian. I wasn\u2019t exactly sure what they said, so we kept going. We found our way to the break room which had four other doors leading off from it. There was a flag on the wall, but I couldn\u2019t remember which country it went to. I took a picture so we could look it up later. We decided to start down a hall that Stasia and Elena had not been down. We knew which hall led downstairs, but we wanted to check out the level we were on first. We found what appeared to be an infirmary, but the doors were shut and locked with chains and padlocks from the outside. They were trying to keep something or someone inside for some reason. Around that time I noticed Lori talking to De la Rocha, who wasn\u2019t looking very good. De la Rocha was very quiet and stayed in the shadows. I\u2019d say her face was expressionless but her eyes were very much alive. Like she was a big cat in the jungle hunting prey. Lori asked De la Rocha to go back to the surface, and she eventually agreed and left the way we had come.<br /> <br /> Stasia picked the lock on the door to the larger area and we were about to go in when Calamity got a look at something through the window on the door. It looked like a human figure sitting huddled on the floor with their back to us. I looked through the window and saw the same thing. After making sure that we were all seeing that we walked inside. As soon as we got inside we didn\u2019t see the figure any more. Lori used an ability to see if there was anything magical in the area. She said that something really big had happened there a long time ago, but it wasn\u2019t Arcadian in nature. Meanwhile Stasia and Elena were looking around and found a map of the facility and the surrounding area. It depicted someplace close to Sofia in Bulgaria. Calamity then used a contract to see if there were any ghosts in the area and apparently she spotted one. She tried talking to the ghost but they didn\u2019t speak a language in common. I guessed that if the ghost could read the Cyrillic on the signs then she might understand another similar language. So, I asked Calamity to ask the ghost if she could hear me. She said yes. So I said \u201cHi\u201d to the ghost and asked her how she was doing in Russian. The ghost apparently understood because she answered back in Russian. Calamity then used another contract to give us all the ability to hear the ghost. I then proceeded to ask her questions about what was going on.<br /> <br /> As we discovered it seems that the ghost and this facility were originally from Bulgaria. At first the ghost woman, I never did ask for her name, kept trying to show us how to get out of there, but eventually answered my questions. It seems that they were doing experiments using radio waves to try and move people from one location to another. As it turns out they were successful, but something went wrong. When the person they transported came back they came back changed. Their eyes were dark, as if clouded with grey or black cataracts. They also had a different inflection when they spoke, and certainly not least, they were just plain crazy. And the last experiment that they did moved the entire structure from Bulgaria to the United States. This caused almost all of the people in the building to go crazy and start attacking those that had not changed. I think the ghost that I was talking to had been killed by her husband. I also asked about the flooded lower levels. She said that they lower levels had been sealed off and flooded to kill the people that had gone crazy. The ghost also told us about a machine that was still running that was keeping her spirit there. She said that there was a way to drain the water if we wanted to get down there and turn the machine off. She suggested that it was the machine that had caused the people to go crazy. I got directions on how to do that should we want or need to.<br /> <br /> Around that time Calamity heard another ghost scream from an adjacent hallway. The ghost that we\u2019d been talking to said that the ghost down that hall was crazy and could hurt the living. Makes me wonder how many other people found this place, and if so did they make it out alive? One would think so considering that the hatchway was closed and sealed. Marguerite offered to go down into the flooded area by herself if we could find a scuba tank for her to use. I think this idea was universally shot down by everyone there. Insincere Marguerite offered to take a mirror with her so she could escape quickly if the need arose. Stasia argued that diving into that place would be akin to cave diving, which is extremely dangerous. It would be hard to find her way back out before her oxygen ran out. In the end I think that we talked Marguerite out of going alone. <br /> <br /> We decided as a group to at least take a look at the hatch, and that is where we ran into trouble. Calamity started walking down the stairs and almost immediately something grabbed a hold of her ankle and yanked hard. Calamity started to fall down the stairs and Marguerite and I reached out and grabbed a hold of her before she could fall. I held onto Calamity\u2019s hand while Marguerite grabbed her waistband. Together we managed to pull Calamity back up and onto her feet. The thing that latched onto her ankle was a woman, with an obviously broken neck and dark eyes. The woman fell after we shook her off and she landed several floors down on the metal stairs. There was a splash. Insincere Marguerite, who had a contract active that allowed her to see in the dark, said that the woman broke her leg, but seemed to be undeterred. This was not heartening. The woman was dead, but not a ghost and physical damage didn\u2019t do all that much to slow her down. We talked for a bit about what we should do next when Marguerite said that the woman was creeping back up the stairs holding a flashlight in her hand. Insincere Marguerite said that it looked like the woman was going to throw it. So, Calamity waited until she did and then caught it when it came flying up. The woman scampered a way down a hall when she saw that. I suggested that we go back to the surface and close the hatch so we could talk in peace and not have to worry about being attacked while we made our plans. Lori was all over that idea and we eventually convinced the others that it was the right choice. Calamity was a little reluctant, but in the end she agreed that we needed a safe place to formulate a plan.<br /> <br /> As if the body attacking us wasn\u2019t disturbing enough Calamity said that the woman that attacked her on the stairs was the body of the ghost that we\u2019d been talking to. I wish I had gotten her name. The interesting thing was that the body of the ghost was barely wet, only up to her ankles, and it was really well preserved for someone that had been dead since 1962. Yeah, I asked the ghost what the last year she remembered was and that\u2019s what she said. Her body should have been falling apart at the very least, skeletonized at the most, but she wasn\u2019t. That means that there could be more mobile bodies down there like her. Out of the water and still moving around. After we had locked the hatch again we wanted to make sure that no one had escaped the lab, so we searched for tracks. It turned out that there were child sized footprints leading away from the hatch. They led us away and into the woods and then back to the hatch. So, whoever had left realized that they were in the middle of nowhere and went back to the lab. Calamity used a contract to see if she could find out exactly where the owner of those footprints was. She saw that the child was inside the complex with two or three other people making booby traps. So, I guess that means that they know we\u2019re coming back. Or they have a suspicion that we are. I guess that just means that if we come back to this place, or if someone comes in our stead, we or they will need to be extra cautious. It\u2019s not just urban exploring anymore. It\u2019s something else entirely.<br /> <br /> Since we knew that the child thing had gotten out Luna called the Forestry Service to see if anything had happened while the door was open. They said that a hiker had gone missing but had turned up that evening unharmed. That was good news but we wanted to make sure that nothing had attached itself to the hiker. Luna offered to do what she called a wellness check to make sure that the man was okay. We agreed that tomorrow would be a good time and that she should go alone. Having non-rangers with her would be suspicious to anyone and especially to whatever beings were inhabiting those bodies. <br /> <br /> So, we discussed what we should do with the lab. Someone suggested that we just fill in the whole place with concrete. Someone else suggested that we go inside and try and kill all of the zombies. I\u2019m not sure of a better word to use. They are definitely dead and yet they are still moving around. I think the going theory is that when the building was transported something replaced the souls of the people with something else. Something alien or supernatural we don\u2019t know. It kind of makes sense seeing as we talked to the ghost of a woman that just tried to kill Calamity by pulling her down the stairs. We came up with several people to call, but in the end we decided to start by telling Lowjack what was going on. Lori took it upon herself to call the reigning monarch and give him a preview of what had happened. She asked him if we could all meet as soon as we got back to the city. He agreed and we all decided that Lowjack\u2019s bar would be a good place to talk. <br /> <br /> Before we left the woods Lori also checked her voicemail and found that she had several messages from her father. She called him and found out that he had a feeling that she was in danger and kept trying to reach her to see if she was okay. Lori assured him that she was fine and they made plans to meet for dinner tomorrow. I think he also might have some names of the vampire hunters, so Calamity can track them down. I want in on that if she goes after one of them. Even if it\u2019s just recon, I want to know what they\u2019re up to.<br /> <br /> We all met at the bar and talked. We told Lowjack everything that we\u2019d seen and learned. He suggested that he call a monarch meeting in the next few days to discuss what to do with the Bulgarian facility. After that Lori talked to Lowjack privately in his office. Not sure what that was about. Probably monarch business. I will admit that I\u2019m curious about the things that Lori now has to deal with, but I get a feeling that it is probably something that I don\u2019t want to know about anyway.<br /> <br /> After our meeting with Lowjack we went back to the Dream House. We decided that after the day we\u2019d had that we didn\u2019t want to have to deal with the show so we let our back up people take care of everything. Luna also said that she was thinking of going to the hiker\u2019s house tonight and doing a stealthy check to see if the guy was really okay. I said that I could be invisible, literally, and offered to come along. Luna agreed and we went to the guy\u2019s house. We parked a little ways away and Luna transformed into a moth to go check out the house. She came back about twenty minutes later saying that she had seen the man and his eyes and that they were normal. Reassured that nothing untoward had actually happened we headed back to the Dream House. I left the bar in the good hands of my back up and went upstairs with my lovely Luna. She is a pretty moth and a beautiful woman. I\u2019m lucky to have her. <br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXXV</i><br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite was using Fang and Talon to see and hear well in the dark, and Darkness to creep along the walls and ceiling. Calamity used Shade and Spirit to see and talk to the ghost and allow the others to hear her.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s unlikely the PCs will ever have the full story on what really happened on a metaphysical level. I am going to drop a simplified explanation behind a spoiler here, as while my players have heard it, others may or may not want to know yet as the characters investigate. This is not the full story of how\u2019s and whys, just what, in game terms, occurred.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> So, from a Mage\u2019s perspective, the Shadow and Underworld are sort of \u201cbeside\u201d the physical world, while the realms Supernal are above. Below even Inferno are the Lower Depths. Some discussion takes place in <i>Summoners</i> of this place (see the Stranger Shores chapter).<br /> <br /> Regardless, a system was given to these Soviet scientists to try to convert people to radio waves and back\u2026except it did not really do that. It drew people into the Lower Depths and what returned was not precisely them anymore. They wanted to open a way from whatever awful place they had visited to here, and managed to conceal their nature long enough to try to move the whole building, which went way off track and wound up in the USA. A few people escaped and sealed it off, until the young lovers found it<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Also if you are curious the flag they saw on several papers and one wall is <u><a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/87/Flag_of_Bulgaria_%281948-1967%29.svg\" target=\"_blank\">here</a></u>\u200b\u200b\u200b. I passed around my phone while players scratched their heads.<br /> <br /> <br /> Okay comments and questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T07:49:16-08:00","id":1280474,"title":"","content":"I assume that's the USSR-era flag of Bulgaria or some internal district of Bulgaria?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T12:36:26-08:00","id":1280531,"title":"","content":"It's one of them. Bulgaria had like 3 or 4.I found matching the right flag of the right year was more research than expected, given looking up Communist Bulgaria's flag got one they started using in the 1970s, which was not that one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-26T21:45:42-08:00","id":1282962,"title":"","content":"There is a show, a traffic jam adventure, and some dress up. Let\u2019s check in. Note Marguerite covers past two sessions.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXXVI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Things seem to be settling down a bit\u2026 oh God, did I actually just write that down? I should know better than to jinx myself like that, particularly right before I head out to my first official meeting with all three of the other local monarchs.<br /> <br /> So by yesterday morning, my online classes had already faded into a sort of routine, and I managed to plow through the video lectures and assigned readings with an hour or so to spare before most people woke up for Sex Breakfast. I decided to do something useful, found a recipe online for a tasty-looking breakfast casserole, discovered that we had everything we needed in our well-stocked kitchen, and set to work.<br /> <br /> Fry up some hash browns and a couple of pounds of sausage, combine both with a bit of finely shredded cheddar, place in rectangular pan, pour in half a dozen beaten eggs (well, I doubled the recipe\u2026 there are a lot of us living in this house), and cook for three quarters of an hour. Easy-peasy, right? Well, I figured it was simple enough that even I couldn\u2019t muck it up too badly\u2026 but even I was surprised with how well the dish turned out. Everyone was super complimentary when I served it up. Lorelei de la Rocha\u2026 cabaret singer, monarch, med student, and domestic goddess! The Pilgrims would be proud\u2026<br /> <br /> If only the conversation at breakfast had been as delightful as the fare. But no, after a hasty admonition not to spread nasty rumors about Bulgarian Teleport Zombies before the monarchs could decide upon a course of action, somehow we started talking about Mount Everest, and a horrific place high on its slopes with the deceptively cheerful name of \u201cRainbow Valley.\u201d Apparently it got its name due to all of the would-be mountain climbers who have perished there, leaving behind perfectly preserved corpses in various brightly-colored parkas. Ick.<br /> <br /> As if that wasn\u2019t bad enough, conversation then turned to what the Hedge might be like in such a place. I honestly don\u2019t even want to think about that too much\u2026 but the subject has a sort of insidious lure about it. I mean, would there even <u>be</u> a Hedge connected to such a barren, lifeless wasteland? The places I\u2019ve been in the Hedge have always seemed like they were positively <u><u>teeming</u></u> with life, and the borderlands are supposed to reflect the parts of the world they touch\u2026<br /> <br /> Anyway, we split up after Sex Breakfast to pursue our own activities. Calamity and Jacob drove to L.A. to harass some Vietnamese gangsters (I thought it better if I didn\u2019t ask). Luna did her follow-up visit to that lost hiker, and determined that he had not been adversely affected by whatever Bulgarian Teleport Zombie had temporarily left the underground facility the other day. Missy and Jane continued posing for their portrait with Julia and Marguerite, and D and I eventually joined them for an hour or two, after I\u2019d taken care of a bit of work that needed doing to prepare for that night\u2019s show.<br /> <br /> D and I left the Dream House about four o\u2019clock to meet Dad at his place for an early dinner. He had made it back into Malibu safely, and the house was thankfully free of booby-traps by the time we got there. Dad was also dressed in his regular clothes instead of the cassock-and-body-armor ensemble he\u2019d been sporting the last time we met. Color me at least a little relieved.<br /> <br /> He seemed pretty certain that the Long Night had given up on hunting Dakota, or at least that they had given up on getting her location from him. I wasn\u2019t so certain about that, so I asked once more if he knew the names of any of his stalkers. He gave one name up. He was pretty certain that one of his pursuers was a man by the name of Alfonso Esquivel. I told him that this would be enough information for Calamity to track the hunter and make sure that he had actually pulled up stakes and abandoned the hunt.<br /> <br /> \u201cPlease understand,\u201d Dad said earnestly, \u201cthat Alfonso is not an evil man. He is simply a bit\u2026 overzealous. He has a reason to hate vampires. He was unable to protect several members of his congregation from the depredations of a few particularly vile specimens. I would not like to see him killed.\u201d<br /> <br /> I gave him what I hope was a reassuring smile. \u201cWe just want to make sure he and his friends have really given up the chase,\u201d I assured him. \u201cI\u2019ll ask Calamity to observe and report, not engage.\u201d I knew she probably wouldn\u2019t be happy about that, but I promised to try anyway.<br /> <br /> He also mentioned that the Reverend Alfonso Esquivel has uncanny luck. Like, little things will start going wrong for anyone who openly opposes him, seemingly without explanation. And he\u2019ll have uncommonly good luck in any such encounters as well. So there\u2019s that to consider in the coming days.<br /> <br /> After that I let talk turn toward other matters for a while, and the three of us had a nice dinner. Once everyone was nice and relaxed, I brought up the other subject I\u2019d wanted to discuss.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo,\u201d I said casually, \u201ccare to tell me more about this \u2018feeling\u2019 you had yesterday? The one that somehow alerted you to the fact that I was in a dangerous situation?\u201d<br /> <br /> He shrugged casually. \u201cI don\u2019t know that there is much more to say on the matter. I felt that you were in danger, and it worried me, so I called you. When you did not answer, I tried Maria, Marguerite, and finally Julia, who told me that you were, err\u2026 \u2018hunting Russian fish-men,\u2019 I believe.\u201d<br /> <br /> I chuckled a bit at that (D laughed out loud). \u201cWell, we didn\u2019t find any Russian fish-men,\u201d I admitted, \u201cthough we did talk a lot about that possibility before we left. What we did find was\u2026 you know what, the details aren\u2019t important right now. The threat is contained for the moment, and we\u2019re all safe and sound. But how did you <u><u>know</u></u> that something was going on at that particular moment?\u201d<br /> <br /> He shrugged again. \u201cIf you want an explanation, Juliette, then I am afraid you will be disappointed. I cannot explain it any more than you can. I simply felt a strong urge to call and make certain that you were safe.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHave you ever had this feeling before?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> He nodded. \u201cYes, though not so intensely,\u201d he admitted, \u201cand not for a very long time. The last time I felt such powerful trepidation regarding your safety, it came to nothing\u2026 or so I believed at the time. I later discovered that you had been kidnapped by faeries and replaced by a simulacrum,\u201d he elaborated dryly.<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay, fair enough,\u201d I replied. \u201cAnd one more thing\u2026 Dakota says that when the two of you were running from the Long Night, you took her by the arm, and she felt like her vampiric powers were\u2026 muted, somehow.\u201d<br /> <br /> He smirked. \u201cI am certain she did feel that way,\u201d he said.<br /> <br /> I narrowed my eyes. \u201cYoung man,\u201d I began with an edge in my voice.<br /> <br /> He actually laughed at that. \u201cNot all of the hunters of the Long Night have such gifts, but it is not unheard of. While in physical contact with a vampire, I can make them believe that their powers are suppressed to a degree. It does not always work, depending upon the vampire in question.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd are their powers actually suppressed, or is it all in their heads?\u201d I asked, curious.<br /> <br /> \u201cDoes it matter?\u201d he replied mysteriously.<br /> <br /> \u201cI guess not,\u201d I replied, resigned to learning no more. \u201cSo, these powers are\u2026 what, exactly? A natural ability of yours? Something you learned from your days as a hunter? A gift from God?\u201d<br /> <br /> He smiled gently. \u201cI like to believe they are the latter,\u201d he admitted.<br /> <br /> Talk turned to less important things for a bit after that, and D and I said goodbye after a while so that we could get back to the Dream House in time to prep for the Friday night show. When we got back home, we found that Julia had been playing dress-up again. Marguerite was wearing a suit, which looked quite sharp on her, and seemed pretty pleased with herself. Meanwhile, Missy was strutting about the place in a gorgeous Regency gown, looking as happy and bubbly as I\u2019ve seen her since we got back from Arcadia. Jane was following her around, looking like she was half in a daze, but mostly just happy to see the girl she loves in such an ecstatic state.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m <u><u>really</u></u> glad those two are settling in and making a life for themselves here. I\u2019d really hate to have to go back into Arcadia to rescue them again. I mean, I\u2019d do it, but I\u2019d really hate to have to.<br /> <br /> We had a few noteworthy guests at the show last night, including Halley, Mari Lwyd, and Joan and Andromeda. I\u2019m sure my face lit up when I saw that last pair, and of course I spent most of my free time that evening with the two of them. Calamity \u2013 who arrived just after the opening curtain from her excursion to L.A. \u2013 entertained Mari Lwyd, and I later learned that the two of them ended up spending the night together as well. Jacob tended the bar and kept Halley and Molly entertained, as usual.<br /> <br /> Missy and Jane clearly had eyes only for each other that evening. Marguerite and Julia were disappointed by that \u2013 they\u2019ve really taken a shine to those two since we got back from Arcadia. D saw how things were developing between Joan and Andromeda and me, and offered to console our brides for their loss that evening. That seemed like a peachy keen idea to me.<br /> <br /> Conversation wandered this way and that throughout the evening, most of it flirtatious. Andromeda spoke at length about her latest invention, which she described as being a cross between a massage chair and a sybian. I was intrigued by this erotic innovation, and asked if she needed quality control testers in a deliberately casual voice. But according to Andromeda, the prototype isn\u2019t ready for human testing yet.<br /> <br /> Joan has never actually slept over at the Dream House before, and she was hinting that she would like to change that, so I offered to give the two of them a private tour of the house with a wink. Of course they accepted, I led them up to my bedroom, and the usual frivolity ensued.<br /> <br /> I think my guests enjoyed the novelty of staying in my room for once. Joan in particular seemed fond of the back balcony and the early morning sunshine. And I confess, seeing my white knight smiling and stretching in the sun, with hardly a care in the world, her soft smile reserved solely for me and her fianc\u00e9e\u2026 well, I think it was good for my soul.<br /> <br /> I made breakfast again, though nothing as fancy as the casserole, just some eggs and toast this time. Conversation was more pleasant this time around, and after our guests had vacated the premises, I shared what I\u2019d learned from Dad with the rest of the motley. I think Calamity is planning to track down the Reverend Esquivel later today or tomorrow, and she\u2019s agreed to at least attempt to confine her activities to surveillance and report back, so we can decide how to proceed as a group. I\u2019m personally hoping the Long Night has pulled up stakes and left town, but then I\u2019m an incurable optimist.<br /> <br /> As for me, well\u2026 John has called a meeting of the monarchs, just like he said he would. We\u2019re going to discuss how we should deal with the threat posed by the subterranean Bulgarian facility in the woods. I\u2026 wish I knew what the right thing to do was. I mean, I know that we have to do <u><u>something</u></u>; the chance that someone else might stumble into it and release what\u2019s trapped within is too much of a risk. But sending people \u2013 <u><u>my</u></u> people \u2013 into that place to try to effect a solution\u2026 well, I\u2019d hate to be responsible if something tragic happened to one of them.<br /> <br /> And <u><u>still</u></u>, with all of this heavy shit going down\u2026 I find myself obsessing over what I\u2019m going to wear to my first official meeting with all three of the other monarchs. Is that sick or what?<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei de la Rocha</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> We started the day with breakfast casserole. It was good; Lori made it. It was a bit of a departure from the quick breakfasts we usually have, but it was good. I made coffee and helped Lori tend one pan while she dealt with another. Once everyone had come down for breakfast we started talking, as per usual. We started off with the serious stuff first, the bunker. We all agreed to keep the story about the bunker under wraps until the monarchs could have their talk about what to do about the facility in question. Then somehow we got on to the topic of climbing Mt. Everest. I think someone had said something about \u201cit was there,\u201d as in doing something because the challenge is there. I said that was all fine, but said that Rainbow Valley is still depressing. Then we started talking about Rainbow Valley and the frozen bodies that litter the place in multicolored jackets and gear. Their bodies will never be retrieved because to do so would likely kill the person trying. The Valley is high enough up that oxygen starts to get really thin and if you don\u2019t make it to base camp, you don\u2019t make it at all. Like I said, depressing. Then someone asked if there was likely to be a version of Everest in the Hedge and I think we agreed that there probably is and that it would be a bad place. The Hedge can be beautiful in places don\u2019t get me wrong, but it is also in some ways a twisted version of \u2018the world.\u2019 Arcadia can be beautiful in places too, but I don\u2019t recommend visiting there either. The Lady\u2019s realm is a frozen wonderland at times and an icy hellhole at others. In some ways I still miss it.<br /> <br /> After breakfast we all split up to do our separate things. Luna went to the hiker\u2019s house to do an official wellness check. She had to go alone, since it would have looked strange to have a civilian there with her on official Ranger business. So, I went with Calamity to find one of the Vietnamese gangsters that had been threatening Luther\u2019s neighborhood. She used oath and punishment to follow him and I let her drive my jeep. I thought that we\u2019d stand out less if we drove the jeep than if we took her motorcycle. Plus it would be a more comfortable ride for me. Holding onto Calamity would have been tricky with all those glass shards of hers. Anyway, we tracked the guy we had a picture of to a hotel in L.A. It appeared that he was working on an A/C unit in the hotel with some others. He was actually at a legitimate job. Not wanting to draw unnecessary attention we just waited in the parking lot until he left. Hotels tend to have a lot of cameras and I wasn\u2019t sure what Calamity\u2019s intentions were. I didn\u2019t want her, or me, getting arrested for harassment or worse.<br /> <br /> While we waited we were approached by Mari Lywd. She came up to the side of the jeep and said that we were surrounded by Day courtiers, some of which were armed. There was at least one sniper rifle trained on us. I felt stupid for not seeing them until after she pointed out all of their hiding places. They were well hidden, but I should have seen them before that. I used to be a lot more cautious. I think Rook was right. I have gone soft. Anyway, she left and the leader of the Day courtiers came over to talk. He introduced himself as Victor, and we talked. He asked us where we were from. After hearing where he asked to see our driver\u2019s licenses so he could verify that. Apparently Hollywood has been sending people into L. A. claiming to be from our Freehold. Some of those people then went on to burn down buildings. Not a very neighborly thing to do if you ask me. That explains the welcome we got if they\u2019ve had arsonists coming to town trying to blame us for it. Hollywood is getting desperate and it\u2019s starting to piss me off. I understand the subterfuge. Trying to sow discord between L. A. and The Lady by the Sea makes sense tactically. Get us fighting on two fronts. It just pisses me off because my home is one of those targets.<br /> <br /> After we got things worked out with Victor we traded contact information and they went their way and we stayed in the parking lot waiting on the gangster. Eventually he and his friends left. So, we followed the guy and his buddies through rush hour traffic. That was probably not the best thing we could have done, but we wanted to have that confrontation with them away from security cameras. In retrospect we should have taken Calamity\u2019s bike, but things worked out for the most part. Everyone got stopped in deadlock traffic. There was a utility vehicle that had some traffic blocked and it was just packed every where else. Since we were stopped Calamity decided to get out of the jeep and walk up to the Vietnamese gangster\u2019s car and have the confrontation right there and then. I don\u2019t know what she said to them, but I did see her put her hand \u201cthrough\u201d the window\u2019s glass as if it weren\u2019t there. That must have freaked those guys out something good. After a few minutes she came back to the jeep. I had moved over to the driver\u2019s seat just in case traffic started moving again, so she climbed into the seat next to me. She said that she had delivered her message and they understood that Luther\u2019s neighborhood was off limits. All that and she didn\u2019t draw any blood.<br /> <br /> While Calamity was having her little \u201cchat\u201d with the gangsters road rage reared its ugly head again and a guy in a nearby car got upset with the utility folks. So, he climbed out of his car, not wearing any pants mind you, and threw an open plastic bottle full of piss at one of the utility guys. That was just plain disgusting, and it started a fight. I think a little bit ended up getting on Calamity, but she was amazingly calm about it and did not retaliate. The guy with no pants also happened to have a pistol, which he\u2019d been waving around in the air. The utility guy had a claw hammer and they started going at it. Calamity showed restraint and refrained from doing anything about the mix up on the highway this time. A third guy jumped into the fight upset that his family had been frightened. I\u2019m sure seeing their father brawling with two other men on the highway didn\u2019t help matters though. In the end it didn\u2019t matter what his intentions were. In time the cops showed up and arrested the guy with no pants, the utility guy that had been fighting him and the third guy who was defending his family\u2019s sensibilities. They also towed the guy\u2019s car and moved the utility vehicle. I maneuvered our way through traffic after that and we got to the Dream House in pretty good time. We got there just as the first act was starting. Calamity wasn\u2019t due to perform for a while, so she had time to go backstage and get ready. I took over at the bar and Johnny covered for one of the waitresses who was out sick, delivering drinks to tables.<br /> <br /> The show was wonderful as usual. I don\u2019t know how my motley mates consistently perform at such a high level. They are crazy good at what they do and the audience loves it. Not that I\u2019m complaining mind you. I just don\u2019t know how they do it. But while they were performing I was entertaining guests. I spoke to Molly, which was nice since I haven\u2019t seen her in such a long time. We caught up and I told her a bit about the adventure this afternoon. It turns out that Molly has been spending a lot of time with Chalcedony these days. I also talked to Hailey, who as usual was staring angrily at Andromeda. After a while Lori spent some time at Joan and Andromeda\u2019s table so the other girl didn\u2019t really notice Hailey\u2019s attention. Either that or she just ignored it. I made sure that Hailey had anything she needed and tried to keep her company too. We also had Mari Lywd as a guest tonight. I thought that was kind of funny considering our little interaction this afternoon. That may have been the reason why she came for all I know. Which is fine. She\u2019s a decent person.<br /> <br /> The other fun thing that happened at the show was Missy and Jane arrived with Missy in a new regency style dress. She was almost dancing around, obviously loving the dress, with a cute smile on her face. Jane was just enjoying watching her. It\u2019s nice to see those two so happy and unconcerned. They were so tense when they first arrived. When they first got here I was sure that one of them would try to run back to the Hedge and that the other would follow them. I\u2019m glad that I was wrong.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Another day, another breakfast. Food was good. Once again cooked by Lori. We talked about trivial things until Joan, Andromeda and Mari all left. Once they were gone Lori told us about what she had found out from her father yesterday. She had gone to have dinner with him and they had talked about certain things. He had a name for one of the vampire hunters, the leader of the Long Night in fact, Reverend Alfonso Esquivel. She had apparently talked to Calamity last night and elicited a promise from her that she would do no harm to the Reverend. Lori explained that should Calamity, or anyone else for that matter, start to mess around with Alfonso they might find themselves on the losing side with luck. Apparently the man has some ability that makes things go well for him and not so well for anyone trying to do something to him. I don\u2019t know if these powers will affect simple surveillance or if it just happens when someone has ill intentions against the man himself. Lori also said that there is some history there and that he has good reasons to hunt vampires. My motley mate implied that the powers he has are god given, which made Calamity back down a bit when it came to causing problems for the Long Night member.<br /> <br /> After all that Lori got ready to go to a meeting with the other monarchs. They are meeting today to talk about the Bulgarian facility and possible solutions. Personally I think we should get a good number of combat ready folks together and all go down there and see what we can do about the walking dead. They aren\u2019t mindless, as evidenced by the fact that Calamity saw them setting traps, which is bad for us. We don\u2019t know what their intentions are. We also don\u2019t know what that machine does, and if it has anything to do with the zombies then I\u2019m more than happy to turn it off. I will also be happy if turning that thing off frees the ghosts in the facility. It can\u2019t be a good thing to be tied to such a place. Hopefully we can resolve these problems soon. I guess we\u2019ll find out later today what the powers that be have decided. It\u2019s still weird that Lori is one of them. I guess the true test of things will be when Spring comes along and she is the reigning monarch. She\u2019ll still have support from the other monarchs, but it will be her that everyone goes to with problems and issues. Hopefully things will go smoothly for her, and if they don\u2019t well then we have her back.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insincere Marguerite\u2019s Whispers</b><br /> <br /> Things have mostly been quiet here.<br /> <br /> A couple days ago, I wound up exploring a former experimental facility. It was Bulgarian so expectations were low (Though it could have been Albanian I guess but I am unsure they discovered anything), but we found some ghosts and some form of ambulatory corpse. The monarchs are taking care of it, I believe. It was a fun exploration and I hated I could not see the rest of the place, but needs must.<br /> <br /> I did not recognize the Communist Bulgarian flag because I only recognize important flags. We encountered a ghost early on who Calamity used contracts to see and had us all able to hear. She did speak Russian, so Jacob could translate, because no one bothers to learn Bulgarian. The only important thing they have done is kill a man with an umbrella. I could have gotten us into the room faster, but Stasia wanted to show off for her girl and I am of course a being of infinite kindness.<br /> <br /> Maria started to regress, so Juliette kindly got her out. She seemed fine tonight, hopefully it did not harm her self-esteem too much.<br /> <br /> But after Jacob and I saved Calamity from the foot zombie we decided to leave, despite not having seen the whole place. Still I think it was the best action. I retrieved our tea candles on the way out because Julia becomes a bear if she runs out of candles. But not a Russian bear. That would be strange.<br /> <br /> That night Melissa and Jane joined us for fun with edible body paint. Thank goodness for the poofing or I would not have had the energy after a day with a lot of walking. There were shrieks and cuddles and fun sex.<br /> <br /> Yesterday was a fairly quiet day. Calamity was off intimidating Vietnamese people and Juliette and Maria went off to meet Juliette\u2019s dad after watching Julia paint Melissa and Jane and chatting with me. Julia got some clothes in and spent time dressing Melissa and I up while Jane remained outside her arm\u2019s length. Wisely. I have a nice suit now. I don\u2019t really like suits.<br /> <br /> Also Julia was poking fun at me having small breasts. She is cruel.<br /> <br /> The show went well. I spoke with Calamity about going back to the odd demon bar. Given I am of the Lost Pantheon, Chinese demons work for gods, and my Court is involved in the cartel (?) running the place, I figured I would come in from a position of strength. Get a tour of the grounds, et cetera. Hopefully Calamity will damage herself less in my company.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, we are going off so she can spy on priests soon. I am getting dressed first of course. I am not wearing a suit.<br /> <br /> Anyway Juliette went off with Joan and Andromeda for the night and Julia and I got Maria out of the deal. Julia was somewhat captivated by Melissa in a Regency gown she got her, but not as much as Jane was, and they have yet to acknowledge other people exist again.<br /> <br /> My breasts are not small they are perfect for me.<br /> <br /> Anyway, after breakfast Calamity wanted to spy on priests after a long day of intimidating Vietnamese people and talking to Day Courtiers so we are off to do that. Hopefully there will be no Day Courtiers.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXXVI</i><br /> <br /> Rainbow Valley is one of those things that I am kinda fixated on, and of the places I find fascinating it is the one I never, ever want to visit.<br /> <br /> The session had more references to Bloodlines, as the hotel Calamity and Jacob visited was the Empire Arms Hotel from Downtown LA, and there was an offhand reference to Jezebel Locke from the game.<br /> <br /> I got to use my random LA encounter chart again.<br /> <br /> Okay, hope you enjoyed. Comments and Questions are welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T01:52:08-08:00","id":1286392,"title":"","content":"All ready to check on our group in Malibu? Some of the gang made some interesting choices. Let\u2019s check it out together.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXXVII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> So I met with all three of the other monarchs for the first time yesterday. I expected to be nervous, and I was. I did <u><u>not</u></u> expect the immediate aftermath of that meeting to be much more stressful than the meeting itself. Nor did I expect the uncomfortable revelations of the next day to be nearly as troubling.<br /> <br /> I swear, one of these days I\u2019m going to staple Calamity\u2019s lips together.<br /> <br /> So after Sex Breakfast yesterday, I threw on a sober grey skirt, a white button-up shirt, and some sensible heels, and drove out to the modest hotel where the meeting was to be held. Dark Kimberly met me in the parking lot. Since she had been to a few of these meetings in the past, she gave me a crash course on the proper etiquette and a few opinions on the relationships between the various courts.<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t interrupt anyone when they\u2019re talking,\u201d she began. \u201cIf you absolutely need to communicate with one of the other monarchs when someone is talking, whisper the message to me, I\u2019ll tell the other monarch\u2019s second, and they\u2019ll pass it along. If Charlotte feels strongly about something and you have no opinion on the subject, vote with her. The Spring and Autumn Courts have always had a good, supportive relationship, and it\u2019s best to foster that if you can do it without compromising yourself. Augustine and Lowjack don\u2019t really like each other, but that\u2019s not likely to be a big issue today.\u201d<br /> <br /> Then she gave me a once-over with a lint roller and tucked a single strand of hair back into place. It was a little humiliating, but I\u2019m glad I had her in my corner.<br /> <br /> In the end it wasn\u2019t as bad as all that. John had reserved a meeting room in the hotel, and business was conducted in a manner more reminiscent of a corporate retreat than the emergency meeting of a local government. Each monarch had a table to themselves; Charlotte and I faced each other across the central table while John and Augustine managed to keep their glowering to a minimum.<br /> <br /> Each of us had our seconds present as well. Tamara was John\u2019s second, to nobody\u2019s surprise. Moon was there with Charlotte, which was apparently a little unusual\u2026 Kimberly told me that she usually brings Madame Spidertoes along. I guess she was busy today. Augustine had Old Billy with him. It was nice to see him again; he doesn\u2019t tend to frequent the Dream House and it\u2019s been a while since we last saw each other.<br /> <br /> John called the meeting to order and let me take center stage for a while. I told my story without embellishment, including every detail I could remember. Well\u2026 almost. I didn\u2019t mention Maria\u2019s temporary regression, but I didn\u2019t really see that as anyone else\u2019s business; it wasn\u2019t related to the threat posed by the lab. The other three paused to take in everything I was saying (even John, even though he already knew it all), and then we started to discuss our options.<br /> <br /> Augustine, to nobody\u2019s surprise, wanted to send a well-armed strike force into the facility to clear it out. We all agreed that this was a necessary first step, but the question was what to do with the facility itself and the machine it contained after this initial clean-up operation concluded. Several options were bandied about. We all agreed that we\u2019d rather not alert the government or military to the facility\u2019s existence; none of us wanted whatever arcane technology the Bulgarians uncovered being picked apart in some top secret Area 51-type place. I half-heartedly suggested that we should fill the place with concrete and bury it deep\u2026 but the facility is so large that it would be prohibitively expensive to do so.<br /> <br /> I think it was John who suggested a small force of engineers and demolitions experts to follow the strike force in and make sure that the machine was shut down and decommissioned permanently. Of course the obvious candidates for this team were Andromeda, who has the keenest technological mind I\u2019ve ever encountered, and Halley, whose Gremlin powers would be invaluable.<br /> <br /> We just had to figure out how to keep them from killing each other long enough to get the job done.<br /> <br /> \u201cAndromeda doesn\u2019t have anything against Halley,\u201d I said firmly. \u201cIt\u2019s Halley\u2019s grudge \u2013 understandable though it might be \u2013 that\u2019ll be the problem.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe could bind her with an oath not to harm Andromeda,\u201d Augustine asserted.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd we won\u2019t send the two of them in alone,\u201d John added. \u201cWe can send in one representative from each of our courts to keep an eye on them.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCalamity is fond of Andromeda,\u201d Charlotte opined, \u201cand she has first-hand experience with the facility.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLeaving only the Winter Court,\u201d John mused. \u201cI could send Twitch in\u2026 he\u2019d be able to incapacitate Halley safely at a moment\u2019s notice if she tries anything.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnton\u2019s a good choice,\u201d I agreed, \u201cbut if any of your people can speak or read Russian, that might be more helpful. Calamity could allow them to communicate with the ghosts in there\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd any technical schematics would likely be in both Russian and Bulgarian,\u201d John agreed. \u201cIt might be best to send Hannah, then\u2026 her expertise with explosives might come in handy, too.\u201d<br /> <br /> So that decided it. We set the time of the strike for early Monday afternoon, and each of us agreed to put out an open call to our courtiers for volunteers to be on the strike team, and before we left the hotel I asked Kimberly to draft an official email to the court and send it to me for approval. I would have written it myself, honest\u2026 but I had another hurdle to overcome, and I wanted to give it my complete attention.<br /> <br /> I stopped by Joan and Andromeda\u2019s place on my way home. They were pleasantly surprised to see me\u2026 at first. As I explained the situation and outlined the monarchs\u2019 plans for dealing with it, Andromeda began to nod in comprehension, and Joan\u2019s expression got darker and darker.<br /> <br /> \u201cI do not like this, Juliette,\u201d she said tightly. \u201cHalley will do anything to strike out at Rebecca\u2026 she would gladly accept the penalties of breaking an oath to seize her chance.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe\u2019re going to take every precaution,\u201d I assured her. \u201cYou\u2019ll be on-site as part of the strike team, and Calamity will be with her the whole time.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe need not be a part of this at all,\u201d Joan insisted.<br /> <br /> \u201cNobody else in the Freehold understands complex machinery as well as Rebecca,\u201d I said firmly. \u201cWe might need that expertise.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThen Halley should not be a part of this,\u201d Joan said, her voice rising.<br /> <br /> Andromeda spoke up next. \u201cHer gremlin powers will be really useful on a job like this,\u201d she said softly. \u201cHer expertise will be invaluable\u2026 we\u2019ll need her on the team. I <u><u>designed</u></u> Halley\u2026 I created every aspect of her to the tiniest detail.\u201d That little tidbit was more than a little disturbing, but I decided to put a pin in it for the time being and focus on the matter at hand.<br /> <br /> Joan\u2019s cheeks reddened, and her eyes narrowed. \u201cIf anything happens to her,\u201d she practically hissed as she turned back to me, \u201cI shall take my vengeance on all of those responsible.\u201d<br /> <br /> I sighed, but didn\u2019t lower my gaze. \u201cYou\u2019ll have to include <u><u>me</u></u> in that number,\u201d I said.<br /> <br /> Joan didn\u2019t flinch. \u201cUnderstood,\u201d she said harshly, and then spun around and stormed from the room.<br /> <br /> Andromeda gave me a helpless look and squeezed my hand gently. \u201cJust\u2026 give us some time alone,\u201d she whispered, giving me a quick kiss on the cheek. \u201cI\u2019ll talk to Lindsay. She\u2019ll come around.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded and took my leave. The drive back to the Dream House wasn\u2019t fun, but I managed to keep myself from falling apart until I\u2019d parked the \u2018vette in the garage and entered the House. Gloria and D were there, playing what looked like some form of strip chess. \u201cCan I talk to you privately for a minute?\u201d I asked my wife. She took one look at my eyes and stood up immediately.<br /> <br /> I spent the next twenty minutes or so breaking down in sobs and trying to coherently explain why to the love of my life. She put on her tender, gentle face and soothed me as best she could. \u201cJoan\u2019s angry,\u201d she said quietly, \u201cand she\u2019s scared of losing Andromeda. She\u2019ll come around, you\u2019ll see.\u201d I suppose it\u2019s a real testament to their friendship that D didn\u2019t get all growly and protective when she heard about Joan\u2019s implied threat.<br /> <br /> Once I\u2019d composed myself, we had an impromptu motley meeting. I shared the results of the monarchs\u2019 conclave with my nearest and dearest, and they in turn let me know what they had been up to.<br /> <br /> Calamity, Jacob, and Marguerite had gone into L.A. again to track down the Reverend Esquivel and his fellow Long Night vampire hunters. They had managed to track them down to a disused church rectory, and through a combination of stealth and larceny had learned quite a bit. Marguerite had even managed to make a mirror copy of Esquivel\u2019s phone, which was providing a wealth of good information.<br /> <br /> Somehow, the hunters had figured out that Dakota was hiding out in a theater. We\u2019re still not sure how they got that information, but it obviously wasn\u2019t specific, as they were systematically searching theaters in L.A. rather than little cabarets like ours in the surrounding area. In one of these theaters \u2013 the old Nocturne, which has been out of commission lately due to some minor fire damage \u2013 they came across something for which they were not prepared.<br /> <br /> An email to their Long Night compatriots described it as some sort of humanoid cat-beast. It could apparently slip from one shadow to another, and used this ability to surprise the hunters, putting one of them in the hospital and frightening the rest away. The wounded man was their ex-military weapons expert, so their hunting activities had been curtailed for the near future.<br /> <br /> Jacob and Calamity know something about this creature, which they referred to as a \u201cwere-cat.\u201d A pack of local werewolves is looking for it, claiming that it is a homicidal maniac. The two of them were cagey about how exactly they knew about this, which makes me more than a little suspicious\u2026 but I decided that I had enough to deal with already and let the matter drop. The two of them were all for telling Luna to inform the werewolves of the cat\u2019s location. Marguerite, with her affinity for all things feline, bristled at the very suggestion, and insisted that we speak to the were-cat first. I\u2019m filing that under \u201ctomorrow\u2019s problems\u201d for the time being.<br /> <br /> This situation presented a number of difficulties. Though the Reverend Esquivel and his friends weren\u2019t likely to stumble across Dakota any time soon, it also seemed unlikely that they would simply give up the chase until they had found their quarry. Jacob offered to look into the possibility of getting Dakota to a safe house, and I told him to do so, but to keep it as a \u201cPlan B\u201d for the moment.<br /> <br /> Everyone was looking at me, and I realized what I\u2019d said. \u201cSorry,\u201d I muttered, \u201cI guess I\u2019m still in monarch mode. I don\u2019t mean to order you all around; I\u2019m not the Queen of you guys. I meant that as a suggestion, not an order. It just seems to me that we should keep this in-house if we can\u2026 at least until we get an update from my Dad.\u201d<br /> <br /> We discussed a few other things, including speculations on those who were likely to volunteer to help clear out the Bulgarian facility. D was pretty sure T.J. would want to be a part of the expedition, and opened up her phone to share a picture of her buddy brandishing the dented bumper of a large truck. Apparently he\u2019d had a \u201cdisagreement\u201d with the truck\u2019s owner, who had tried to shoot him and then run him over. Big mistake.<br /> <br /> We all broke up after that to prepare for the show. Jane approached me to see if I wanted her and Missy to back me up for a number, and I decided to go all-out as a method of coping with my guilt over the situation with Joan and Andromeda. I kept myself in reserve for most of the night, introducing a few acts and singing backup or playing the piano outside of the spotlight. Marguerite\u2019s new rendition of Bowie\u2019s \u201cI\u2019m Afraid of Americans\u201d was a big hit, and Calamity\u2019s \u201cLittle Red Riding Hood\u201d staple went over like a house on fire as usual.<br /> <br /> Then, for our big finale, Missy, Jane and I hit the stage, each in a sparkly low-cut gown with our own spot. After a brief musical introduction, we launched into the classic Motown hit \u201cAin\u2019t No Mountain High Enough.\u201d It was\u2026 exhilarating. With those two backing me up, there\u2019s <u><u>nothing</u></u> I can\u2019t do, and I started to remember that as the familiar notes rose up from the stage, and from the three of us. They were putting everything they had into supporting me, and their support meant <u><u>everything</u></u>. Joan\u2019s anger, the dangers posed by the Bulgarian facility, the vampire hunters in L.A\u2026. it all faded away, and the music came pouring out of me. It was the best performance of my life by a wide margin, and the three of us left the stage buoyed by thunderous applause, hugging and kissing each other as we giggled giddily.<br /> <br /> I left the two of them to their own devices after assuaging their fears about the possibility of attending one of Julia\u2019s Wiccan rituals, and began to mingle with the crowds. Jolie, Desiree, and Veronica were there once more, and they once again exerted all of their not inconsiderable seductive wiles in an attempt to lure me into their fiendish clutches. But once again \u2013 with great regret \u2013 I had to refuse their generous invitation. I left them with a heartfelt plea to return the following evening. I\u2019ll just have to wait and see if they do.<br /> <br /> The reason I had to turn them down was that Oleander was there. I made my way up to her table, and she scooped me into her lap and planted a long kiss on my lips. \u201cMissed you, Angel,\u201d she whispered when we came up for air, and I returned the sentiment.<br /> <br /> We sat there talking quietly while the crowds cleared out. At some point before we left, my phone chimed, and I saw that I had received an email from Joan. If I printed it out, it would probably be four or five pages long\u2026 but in the end all she was really saying was \u201cI\u2019m sorry.\u201d I felt my eyes starting to water, and quickly tapped out a short reply. \u201cLindsay, apology accepted. Thank you. Love, Juliette.\u201d<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve been very careful about using that word with her over the last year. I never want to do anything to come between her and Rebecca. I don\u2019t feel the same way about the two of them that I do about Oleander, or Marguerite and Julia, or Maria. But I do love them, and I think they love me too. And I think she needed to hear it.<br /> <br /> So Oleander and I went back to her place and spent a nice romantic evening together, and even managed to grab a couple of hours of sleep before I had to run off to church. Oleander didn\u2019t join me this time, but she met me back at the Dream House afterward for Sex Breakfast. Conversation was light and flirty as usual\u2026 but unfortunately the after-breakfast discussion served only to increase my stress.<br /> <br /> First, Calamity dropped a bomb. Last night after the show, she called up Viktor, our vampire friend in L.A. She not only told him about the Long Night hunters in his territory, but let slip that Dakota was under our protection as well. This posed several problems. First, it seemed likely that the vampires would do something about the hunters, and I\u2019d promised my Dad that we\u2019d try to avoid harming them unnecessarily. Secondly, Viktor belongs to a group called the Carthians\u2026 the same group that\u2019s currently hunting for Dakota.<br /> <br /> Ironically, the first situation is less likely to become a problem. Viktor had told us that his people like to handle problems quietly, and killing a group of hunters in L.A. is likely to draw too much attention to them. They prefer to mislead and misdirect, drawing the hunters away from their territory with a trail of false clues and half-truths. So as far as that goes, Calamity\u2019s little indiscretion might have been a stroke of luck after all.<br /> <br /> Viktor assured Calamity that he had no intention of hunting Dakota down\u2026 but we don\u2019t really know him that well, and I don\u2019t think any of us were prepared to risk the possibility that he was lying about that. We decided to move Dakota as soon as we could safely do so. Jacob made a few calls to see if we could temporarily place her in one of his Entitlement\u2019s safe houses, and I called Dad to see if his contacts were ready to get her out of town. He hadn\u2019t heard anything yet, but promised to check with his people and get back to us.<br /> <br /> I guess we can be relatively certain that the vampires won\u2019t make a move until tonight at the earliest, what with the sunlight and all. So we have a few hours to figure something out. But I can\u2019t believe that Calamity just went and\u2026 and <u><u>told</u></u> the vampires about Dakota. No, that\u2019s not entirely true. There\u2019s a part of me that finds it all too easy to believe. This is the same side of her that killed Mr. Grey a year and a half ago. She saw the hunters as a threat to the motley, and she acted to counter it, regardless of how the rest of us might have felt about the situation.<br /> <br /> Moving forward, I\u2019ll have to think about what information I can trust her with.<br /> <br /> I hate the fact that I\u2019ll have to think about that.<br /> <br /> In other news, Marguerite reported that Reverend Esquivel had sent another email to his contacts, indicating that he\u2019d had a dream last night about being hunted by shadowy supernatural forces. We don\u2019t know if this vision refers to the fact that my motley-mates were spying on him yesterday or the possibility that the local vampires are now onto him, but in the end it doesn\u2019t really matter. Calamity dutifully texted Viktor with this new information, and we adjourned the meeting.<br /> <br /> God, I\u2019m tired, and it has nothing to do with the fact that I got very little sleep last night. This situation with Calamity\u2026 I do not need this shit right now. I know that she does what she does because she loves us and wants to protect us, and I don\u2019t blame her for that impulse. But her judgment isn\u2019t always the best, and she has no patience for the long game. I know now that I was right to keep the Freehold\u2019s plans for the Hollywood situation to myself. God only knows what she would do in some misguided attempt to protect the Freehold, or to ease the burden on my soul.<br /> <br /> So I\u2019ve got angry paramours, a guilty conscience, inquisitive vampires, general education classes, and determined redheads to deal with. I need a fucking vacation.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei de la Rocha</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> I\u2019ve never snuck up on a priest before today. While Lori was going to meet with the other monarchs, Calamity, Insincere Marguerite and I went to go check on the Last Night vampire hunters. Calamity used her contract to track the leader, Alfonso Esquivel, and get a peek at what they were doing. It turned out that they were holed up somewhere with crosses on the walls and there was a table with a map on it. It appeared that there were three of them in the room, including Alfonso. So, Calamity drove my jeep to the location the contract directed her towards. We parked a little ways off so they wouldn\u2019t see the car and snuck up to see what they were doing. The whole time things felt off. I don\u2019t know how else to explain it. They didn\u2019t see us and no one bothered us, but things just felt different when we were spying on them.<br /> <br /> We listened in and discovered that they know that Dakota is in a theater, but they don\u2019t know which one. They have been able to scry on her location and only see glimpses of the inside of the club, so they don\u2019t know exactly where she is. I\u2019m assuming that they saw a stage and went from there. It also seems that they used to have four members in their group but one of them is currently in the hospital. They went to the Nocturne theater and discovered that it had a supernatural inhabitant. There was a fight between the hunters and the individual in the theater and the hunters ended up fleeing after one of their number was mauled by the creature. It seems that they came across the werecat that the werewolves had been looking for. The hunters didn\u2019t know what the creature was at first, only that it was fast and dangerous. I also managed to get the name of the hospital that their friend was in and what room number. If we need to pay him a visit we\u2019ll be able to. It sounds like he\u2019s gonna be there for a few days at least.<br /> <br /> We found out that Alfonso was emailing someone that he knew to get more information about the creature they encountered in the theater. We decided that we needed to get his phone so we could see what correspondences have been going on so far. So, Insincere Marguerite snuck in and pickpocketed Alfonso\u2019s phone. She then used a mirror and a contract to make a duplicate of the phone that would last until sundown. She then put the phone back and exited the building. While she was doing that, I was taking note of what theaters they had already checked and which ones were still on their list to visit. So far they have only gone to theaters in L.A. Their map has L.A. and Santa Monica on it, but not Malibu, so they haven\u2019t thought of looking in our neck of the woods yet, which would give us time to move Dakota before they even got close. Calamity also read Alfonso\u2019s surface fears before we left and found out that he is afraid of the father of a teen that he failed to save. While I feel bad that he failed to save someone, I\u2019m glad that his current thoughts were not about killing Dakota because of some threat that she might pose.<br /> <br /> After we left the church where Alfonso and his friends were hiding out we started looking at the phone and reading his correspondences. That\u2019s when we discovered that the creature in the Nocturne theater was the werecat. We figured that we might need the phone past sundown, so I suggested that we clone it, though I wasn\u2019t sure who we would get to do that. Calamity then took it upon herself to call Hannah and see if she could help. It turned out that Hannah has human friends that can do just what we needed. So, we got Hannah\u2019s friends to clone the phone using an old phone that Marguerite had picked up to clone it to. The Reverend Esquivel\u2019s cloned phone is pink and sparkly. At least it stands out, right? Also, after we got back to the House Calamity called Luna and left her a message to have her call one of us back when she got back in cell range. We wanted to bring up the matter of the werecat to her and see if she might be able to let the werewolves know that we\u2019d found their quarry.<br /> <br /> A little while after we got back from our little expedition Lori got back from her meeting with the monarchs. As things stand the plan is to have a strike force go in on Monday early afternoon and take care of the walking dead monstrosities and then shut down the machine. Everyone will meet at noon so they can go in around 1pm. The strike force will be a group of volunteers who go in and see what we can do about the things walking around and taunting us in Bulgarian. I plan on volunteering for that. If we run into any of them and need to know what they are saying then I might be able to communicate with them in Russian, provided the rest of them speak it as well as the ghost did. After we drain the lower levels and take out the walking dead we\u2019ll send in a four person team to deal with the machine itself. The team will consist of Hailey, Andromeda, either Twitch or Hannah and Calamity. There is also a plan to have an oath placed on the two mechanics so they can\u2019t harm one another. I don\u2019t think Andromeda would try anything against Hailey, but the opposite is not necessarily true. Calamity can deal with either of them or if any threats come up. Hannah can also speak Russian and is very familiar with explosives if they\u2019re needed. Twitch, if he goes, can subdue Hailey if she were to try and hurt Andromeda. I\u2019m not sure if they decided on Hannah or Twitch to go for the Winter Court. The other courts are well represented in the plans.<br /> <br /> After Lori told us about her meeting we told her about what we\u2019d been up to. We explained what the Long Night were up to with the theaters and what they\u2019d found in one of those theaters. We didn\u2019t go into details about how we knew that werewolves were looking for a werecat just that we\u2019d found it and had left a message with Luna to have her call me or Calamity back. Insincere Marguerite expressed an interest in trying to talk to the werecat before we tell the werewolves where it is just so she can see what its side of the story is. Marguerite is very feline in nature and said that dogs usually bully cats and wanted to make sure that wasn\u2019t happening in this case. I wasn\u2019t sure how wise an idea it was to have Insincere Marguerite talk to the werecat, but she insisted so I think we figured we\u2019d let her do it. We also explained about the phone that we\u2019d copied using the mirror and what we were going to do with it. <br /> <br /> Before the show Calamity went downstairs to talk to Dakota and let her know about the vampire hunters and what they\u2019re up to. She let her know that they are still a ways away from finding her and that we would find another safe place for her to go since the Dream House has been compromised. Dakota was concerned but not overly worried that we would be able to find a safe place for her soon. <br /> <br /> Then there was the show, and holy shit did our ladies do well. I don\u2019t think I\u2019ve ever seen Lori put on a performance like that. She was backed up by Missy and Jane, who also did a great job. Calamity and Insincere Marguerite did wonderfully too. Like I\u2019ve said before, I don\u2019t know how they keep doing it and how they keep improving. I mean, I know that practice makes perfect, but I thought they were all pretty close to perfect before. Goes to show what I know about show biz. <br /> <br /> I talked to Molly at the bar and asked what she\u2019d been up to since I haven\u2019t seen her for the past few days. She said that she was spending a lot of time with Chalcedony lately. She also mentioned that Chalcedony had sought out professional counseling and was talking to a therapist. I\u2019m assuming that some of what she needs to talk about was what happened at the Dream House, but it seems that some of it is about her relationship with Molly. We switched topics and started talking about the upcoming raid on the Bulgarian facility. Molly will be there to back up the strike force. She will likely be hidden and armed with a rifle. She is a force to be reckoned with when she has that rifle, so I\u2019m happy that she will be backing us up.<br /> <br /> Luna also called me back to ask what was up. I told her about the werecat that the hunters found in the theater and that Insincere Marguerite wanted to talk to it before we sent the werewolves after it. I don\u2019t know if the werecat is a man or woman. I don\u2019t think the hunters knew that either. The attack on them was too fast and we only have their information to work with on that front. So, I guess we\u2019ll let Marguerite go in and have a chat with the werecat before we inform anyone else of its whereabouts. I wanted to suggest that someone go with her just in case, but I don\u2019t know how the werecat would take that. It might be seen as an act of aggression, sending multiple people to talk to it. Maybe she can go with her invisibly and with several other stealth contracts up to keep the werecat from detecting that anyone else was there? I\u2019ll ask Marguerite her opinion on that.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> This morning we had a bit of a surprise. After our guests had left we started talking about what was going on right now, and Calamity had a bit of news to tell us. It turns out that last night she had called Viktor and Serena to ask them if there was anyone actively looking for Dakota. They are on the opposite side of the disagreement with Dakota. Dakota is with the Invictus and Viktor and the others are on the side of the Carthians. I don\u2019t know any more about the groups besides their names though. Calamity was roundabout in her query, but it would have been plain to anyone that she is protecting Dakota and wanted to know if anyone was actively looking for her. Viktor said that no one was searching for her at the moment, though if they happened to spot her they were instructed to bring her in to their factions leader. <br /> <br /> Calamity also told the vampires about the Long Night hunters and where they were located. She even went so far as to give them the name of the hospital one of their members was in and the room number he was in. Viktor said that there might be a conversation between them and the hunters, but they would likely not initiate any violence. If they kill all the members of the Long Night that are in town then even more will come to town to take their place and start hunting vampires indiscriminately. Viktor said that they would likely just urge the hunters to leave town and not harm them. Before I could say anything Lori expressed the concern that had popped into my head. Now the other vampires know where Dakota is and might come looking for her. We need to move her and we need to move her fast. If they decide to stake the place out then we might not be able to move her without them knowing where she\u2019s going, and that would just defeat the purpose. Lori called her father to see if he had any more information on a hiding place for Dakota. He said that he\u2019ll talk to his guy and see if they\u2019ve found a safe house for her yet. I told Lori that I would look into my option and see if my entitlement\u2019s safe house was still an option.<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite also mentioned that she had read on the phone that Alfonso had had a dream that he was being followed or chased. Basically that someone was after him. This could mean that he knows that someone from the motley has been looking after him or that someone from Viktor\u2019s group has been following him. I don\u2019t know how fast they work, but it\u2019s possible that they have started their work already. I sometimes had targets that seemed to know in advance that someone was after them before I even started hunting them properly. They seemed to have that uncanny sense that their life was in danger and reacted accordingly. They were always the canniest of targets and made for the most fun. They would usually offer quite a good chase before I could catch up to them. It always ended the same. Either my target was in my Lady\u2019s employ or s/he was dead. I did say that I was good, didn\u2019t I? I\u2019m on the opposite side of the equation now though aren\u2019t I? Now I\u2019m the one that needs to keep the prey alive as opposed to the one that is hunting them down. In this case I want to keep Dakota alive and Alfonso and his goon squad away. I also need to think about the vampires that may or may not want to have a \u201cchat\u201d with Dakota. Alfonso may feel like he is the one being targeted but for us the target has always been Dakota. I suppose that we will need to see what Alfonso and his team does in reaction to this dream of his. We will still need to move Dakota, but we may or may not need to do anything more in regard to the good Revered Esquivel. I guess time will tell on that count.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXXVII</i><br /> <br /> Fun!<br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite used Contract of Reflections to duplicate the phone.<br /> <br /> The Nocturne Theatre is another location from Bloodlines.<br /> <br /> A \u201cWere-Cat\u201d would be a member of the Colony, a different breed of shifter from War Against the Pure for Werewolf. Colony have appeared in other storylines, most notably Noriko Oyamada in Geist: Balance of Shadows.<br /> <br /> Okay well I think that covers it. Comments and Questions welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T13:44:37-08:00","id":1291594,"title":"","content":"In the build up to the raid on the base, our heroes find they have other problems<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXXVIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> It\u2019s zero hour. In a few short minutes, most of my motley and I will head into the abandoned Bulgarian research facility to offer our aid to the Freehold\u2019s efforts to rid the area of psychotic teleport zombies. Though the past day has been a bit less fraught than the days which immediately preceded it, I can\u2019t say that it has been entirely free of drama. It\u2019s caused me to reflect on a few things\u2026 and taken my private musings to some very dark places.<br /> <br /> So after my last entry, most of the rest of Sunday was pretty uneventful. I prepped a number for the show and spent what remained of the afternoon hanging out with my girls. It was a relatively pleasant way to spend the day, Julia\u2019s inexplicable fondness for the film called <u><u>The Craft</u></u> notwithstanding. At some point the conversation turned to unusual sexual fetishes, and Julia let slip that D had shared with her a few images of women fellating the barrels of various guns. I confessed that I didn\u2019t get it, and Calamity proceeded to drive the subject into the ground\u2026 presumably in an attempt to deflect attention away from her earlier lapse of discretion with regards to our L.A. kindred friends.<br /> <br /> I <u><u>don\u2019t</u></u> get it, but I might have played that fact up a bit to keep the conversation going and to keep Calamity happy. I mean, Calamity is the one who taught me everything I know about gun safety, for crying out loud. Later I sort of quietly asked D if she wanted the two of us to act out any of her fetish pics, but she waved it off as unimportant. \u201cI don\u2019t even own a gun\u201d she said with a smirk\u2026 which vanished when I reminded her that I <u><u>do</u></u>. She reiterated that she had no interest in doing the gun sex thing, she just likes looking at the pretty pictures.<br /> <br /> Jacob, Becky, and Calamity eventually headed out to Lowjack\u2019s to join in on the planning session for the upcoming assault. I didn\u2019t get many of the details \u2013 I\u2019m relatively firm in my resolve to stay topside and provide medical support from the fallback camp \u2013 but I gathered that they came up with a viable strategy for clearing the base. Part of this strategy involved some preliminary work by a few members of my motley\u2026 but I\u2019m getting ahead of myself.<br /> <br /> I opened and closed the show last night, bookending the performance with \u201cWilkommen\u201d and \u201cCabaret\u201d from <u><u>Cabaret</u></u>. I\u2019ve performed both before, though not in a while, and I think I did well enough.<br /> <br /> It was a fairly slow Sunday night, but there were a few guests of note. Most of these seemed to be clustered around a single table, talking loudly and making raucous jokes. This unlikely assembly was composed of Halley, Molly, T.J., Monica, Hannah, and Dahlia. They seemed to be buying each other strange drinks and generally having a fine old time. They also referred to themselves \u2013 frequently and vocally \u2013 as \u201cMurder, Inc.\u201d<br /> <br /> I stopped by that table a few times during the evening, but by and large I left that bit of socializing to Calamity. I did try to help Monica guess what T.J.\u2019s initials stand for, but neither one of us got it right by last call. Personally I thought \u201cTyrone Jenkins\u201d was as likely as anything\u2026<br /> <br /> I had hoped that Desiree, Jolie, and Veronica would make good on their threat to return that evening to continue their attempts to seduce me, but in the end only Desiree was there. I spent a lot of time at her table, just\u2026 talking. And yes, I could tell from three tables away that this absolutely <u><u>infuriated</u></u> Becky, but I didn\u2019t care. Desiree is my friend. She seemed a little down, and as she\u2019s one of my courtiers, I figured it was my duty to get to the bottom of it.<br /> <br /> The long and the short of it was that Jolie and Veronica were out on a date, and she was feeling a bit glum. This was not, as I first assumed, because she was feeling like a third wheel, but rather because her solitude had given her time to reflect upon her new paramour.<br /> <br /> \u201cI like Veronica a lot,\u201d she confided in me, \u201cbut I have to admit that I have\u2026 questions about her past.\u201d<br /> <br /> She went on to explain that no matter how she\u2019d asked, Veronica had always skillfully deflected the conversation away from her background, and had never shared anything about her Durance. When Desiree asked me, I had to admit that Veronica had never volunteered any of those details to me, either. Most of our conversations involved our pre-Arcadia lives, since we both grew up in Iowa.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019s too good at redirecting questions,\u201d Desiree said. \u201cShe uses a lot of the same techniques I learned from the Director. I flatter myself that I\u2019m pretty good at getting people to open up about things they don\u2019t like to talk about, but I can\u2019t get <u><u>anywhere</u></u> with her\u2026 she stonewalls me every time.\u201d<br /> <br /> This wasn\u2019t the first time someone close to me has expressed doubts about Veronica. Personally, I don\u2019t think there\u2019s anything solid behind these misgivings\u2026 Veronica is a good friend of mine and I don\u2019t want anyone to cast unwarranted aspersions on her character. But as a local monarch, I can\u2019t really afford to dismiss these pervasive opinions either.<br /> <br /> \u201cLet\u2019s not make too much out of this just yet,\u201d I advised. \u201cBut\u2026 I trust your instincts in this, Desiree. Keep your eyes and ears open, and please let me know if you discover anything. I don\u2019t want to think Veronica is a threat\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t either,\u201d Desiree cut in anxiously, \u201cbut\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut there\u2019s too much at stake for us to be careless,\u201d I finished for her. \u201cThanks for telling me about this, and like I said, please keep me informed if you learn anything more.\u201d<br /> <br /> She promised to do so, and we let the subject drop. Desiree told me a bit more about her past, and she really opened up this time. At some point I casually dropped the word \u201cwhore,\u201d meaning to use it in a light-hearted playful way and completely forgetting that Desiree was actually a prostitute for a while before her Durance (thank God I didn\u2019t actually <u>call</u> her a whore, even as a joke). She took it in stride, but mentioned that it was actually surprising how much of popular culture becomes very uncomfortable when you have something like that in your background.<br /> <br /> She also mentioned that before her brief stint as a prostitute she had been a member of The Family, a weird New Age cult that was around and making headlines even back before my own Durance. She confided in me that she used to seduce people as a way of indoctrinating them into the cult\u2026 something she obviously regrets to this day. \u201cIt\u2019s one thing to have sex with people for money,\u201d she said dejectedly, \u201cbut it takes a special kind of horrible to sleep with people as a method of bringing them into a brainwashing cult.\u201d I assured her that her secret was safe with me, and that it didn\u2019t change my affection for her, and we moved on.<br /> <br /> After that our talk turned to more pleasant matters. Okay, I admit it, I\u2019d worked myself up a bit anticipating a seduction, so I confess that I started flirting with her a bit. She didn\u2019t seem to mind, and after a while my attentions even seemed to cheer her up. So as the place quieted and started to empty out, we found ourselves contentedly making out, blind to the rest of the world. My lovely wife came up at some point, cleared her throat, and asked if the two of us wanted company for the evening, and we happily accepted her offer.<br /> <br /> And so the night passed, and morning found me struggling to slip out from between D and Desiree without waking either of them. I pepped myself up with Spring contracts, slipped into the Media Room, and settled down with my laptop to attend my online classes. Got an A on my first assignment for French Romantic Lit, by the way. Speaking as a girl who was always a solid C student in high school, that gave me all kinds of warm fuzzies. I guess Dad was right all those years ago\u2026 I just needed to apply myself to excel.<br /> <br /> Jacob and Calamity had apparently just gotten in when I got up, though I didn\u2019t find out about that until a little later. Sex Breakfast was the usual cacophony of innuendo and victuals, but the real revelations came afterward, when our guests (okay, Desiree was the only real \u2018guest\u2019 in attendance this morning)) had vacated the premises.<br /> <br /> First of all, Calamity and Jacob revealed where they\u2019d gone during the wee hours of the morning. They had apparently \u2018borrowed\u2019 a heavy-duty machinegun from the U.S. Navy with the intent of using it in the assault on the Bulgarian facility. They were cagey about the details of the operation, but I gather that everything went smoothly, and they both assured me that they intended to return the weapon before the GIs missed it. I\u2026 can\u2019t say that I approve of the theft, however temporary it might be, but I must admit that I\u2019m glad we\u2019ll have such a powerful ace in the hole when the time comes to face the teleport zombies.<br /> <br /> We had this conversation in full view of Missy and Jane, who had been giggling in the corner with Marguerite and Julia (I guess the Wiccan ceremony thing went well last night). This brought up another point I\u2019d been thinking a lot about lately. As we were about to disperse to head out to the Bulgarian lab, I asked to speak to everyone for a minute. First, I asked Jacob if Luna was planning to join us for movie night. When he responded in the affirmative, I asked everyone if they would be okay with inducting Missy and Jane into the motley officially that evening.<br /> <br /> Everyone was okay with it, including the duo in question. Missy was typically sincere and enthusiastic in her desire to be invited into our extended family, and of course Jane was quick to agree once she saw how much Missy wanted it. So we have that to look forward to following what is likely to be a harrowing afternoon cleaning up the mistakes of the last century.<br /> <br /> So here I sit, riding in the van on the way to the facility and hastily jotting down this short journal entry. I admit that I\u2019m more than a little scared, even though I probably won\u2019t even need to set foot in the dangerous parts of the building. A lot of people that I care about are going down there\u2026 and some of them are putting themselves at risk because I\u2019m <u><u>asking</u></u> them to. Is this what it is to be a leader? I\u2019ve done plenty of dangerous things over the past few years, but I don\u2019t think I fully understood until now just how much more difficult it is to stand back and ask other people to do the same\u2026<br /> <br /> Joan will never forgive me if anything happens to Andromeda, no matter what she might have said in her email last night. I know that, and I accept it. And it\u2019s only right, because I\u2019ll never be able to forgive myself either. But the threat posed by that technology is too great for us to stand aside and do nothing, and Andromeda represents our best chance to deal with it safely and permanently. Sometimes, a leader has to risk something she cares deeply about for the good of those who have entrusted her with their welfare.<br /> <br /> I understand now. I pray it doesn\u2019t come to this, and I will do everything in my power to avoid it\u2026 but if things come to the crisis point with Hollywood sooner than we expect, I know that I\u2019ll <u><u>have</u></u> to sacrifice Oleander. And God help me, but after this little object lesson in responsibility I think I actually <u><u>can</u></u> make that sacrifice if I have to. I hate myself more than a little for even thinking that, but I can\u2019t deny it either.<br /> <br /> I need a drink.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei de la Rocha</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Things are getting planned and it won\u2019t be long now until those plans get implemented. Calamity, Becky and I went to Lowjack\u2019s bar to meet with people to talk about the plans for the upcoming raid on the Bulgarian facility. We met up with Shi, Oleander, Louie, Joan, Billy and Dionysia. It seemed that Billy was the one making the final plans, but everyone was putting in their two cents on what they thought should happen. So, the plan as it stands now is that a stealth team, consisting of Calamity, Dahlia and Insincere Marguerite will go in first and see about disarming any traps that they come across. The second wave would consist of those of us that were there to take out the main body of the enemy. I think the stealth group was going to watch our backs to make sure no one snuck up on us. They are also sending in a big machine gun to start the assault when we open the hatch. The assumption is that there will be a mass of undead things trying to get out from where they\u2019ve been trapped all this time. Especially if they hear the door starting to open. The catch is that we needed to acquire the machine gun from the Navy first. It was decided that Calamity and I would \u201ccollect\u201d the gun from the base before sunrise. Apparently Louie had some contacts at the base that are all set to disable the security cameras and other security measures. Lowjack also came in to give Calamity a burner phone to use in case she needed to contact someone. It seems that Louie also obtained this phone from Seattle last November. So, it\u2019s not traceable back to us. It was also stressed that if anything should go wrong then we should flee into the Hedge and leave the gun behind. It was not worth it to get caught by the military trying to steal from their warehouse. We didn\u2019t need the gun that badly. After the meeting Calamity wanted to talk to Lowjack. I stuck around since she didn\u2019t tell me to leave. She wanted to clarify with him that she would be allowed, if necessary, to kill Hailey if she tries anything against Andromeda tomorrow. Lowjack said that she should look for non-lethal ways to handle the situation first, but if that didn\u2019t work then she was authorized to kill Hailey. Calamity didn\u2019t want to accidentally break her oath to Lowjack by killing a member of the Freehold in good standing. After we left I asked Calamity as a favor if she could find a way to subdue Hailey that didn\u2019t involve killing her. I have grown fond of Hailey and I don\u2019t want to see her hurt. She has been through enough in her life, she doesn\u2019t need that life to end early when she has years ahead of her.<br /> <br /> Once we got back to the Dream House we told everyone else the plans. Lori didn\u2019t want to know too much about the machine gun heist. I think she wanted plausible deniability later if she were to be questioned. Makes sense to me. I mean, I would probably want to know what was going on if I were not involved, but then I am a curious type. Anyway, the afternoon went by quickly. Everyone did their own thing. I think Missy and Jane had been watching \u201cThe Craft\u201d earlier. Julia always gets excited about that movie. Lori had been doing her online classes. I think they were just about done by the time we got back from Lowjack\u2019s bar. <br /> <br /> Later at the show we had a number of guests, as usual, but these folks were more rowdy than usual. The rowdy group consisted of Hailey, Molly, TJ, Hannah, Monica and Dahlia. They were making a sort of game out of ordering each other fruity drinks, overly strong drinks, etc\u2026 They were having fun though, so I suppose that\u2019s what matters. Hailey offered to pay me $50 to deliver a White Russian to someone while shirtless. I declined. I\u2019m generally not one to be an exhibitionist, especially in public. Plus I don\u2019t like showing off my brand. It reminds me too much of the Lady and I don\u2019t like answering questions about it. I guess for most people their durance is a sensitive subject, but for me it\u2019s a little more than that. I can talk about the time before I served the Lady to people, if they asked. I\u2019m not proud of some of the stuff I had to do to survive, but I\u2019m even less proud of the stuff that I did while in her service. I don\u2019t feel like reliving it myself, let alone sharing my shame with others. Plus there\u2019s the whole \u201cthey\u2019d never trust me again,\u201d thing. I mean, my motley does, but then they know me better than the freehold does in general. The majority of the Freehold would likely be less than willing to forgive a Loyalist. They tentatively forgive the Director\u2019s pawns but I think that is mainly because they were programed to do the things they did. I don\u2019t have that excuse.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Okay\u2026that was a thing. I just stole a machine gun from the U.S. Navy. Okay\u2026Calamity and I just stole a gun from the Navy. It was pretty cool, I\u2019ll admit that. We went to the address that we were given to pick up the panel truck that we were going to need to transport the gun off of the base. It had to be a nondescript delivery truck that showed up and left so as to not attract notice. When we picked up the truck it was surrounded by inconspicuous men in inconspicuous cars. I think that they are part of the Tong. They didn\u2019t approach us so we didn\u2019t approach them. Figured it was safer that way. We took the truck and drove to the base. They let us through the checkpoint without any hassle and we pulled up to the side and parked the truck. We then activated our contracts to make us be able to pass without leaving any trace and to make us invisible. On the way to the warehouse we saw a Chinese menu on the ground. Calamity picked it up and discovered that there was an 8-digit number written on the inside of it. We assumed, correctly, that it was the access code to the keypad at the door. The guard on duty took that moment to make a phone call and he stepped away from the corner, giving us free access to the warehouse. We got in and closed the door behind us quietly. Inside there were three of the machine guns we were looking for and several boxes of ammunition right under a sign reminding people to store the ammunition away from the guns. Someone was nice and forgetful which benefitted us greatly. Hell, there was even a hand truck nearby. So, I loaded the hand truck up with all the ammo I could find and Calamity used a contract to enhance her strength and just picked up the machine gun. We took our finds out to the truck and loaded it up as quickly and as quietly as we could. I even put the hand truck in the back instead of leaving it behind. I figured we could use it to return the gun to its place. And then we just drove away. They let us back out through the gates without comment and we continued on our way back to the rendezvous point. Shi was there waiting for us. We hopped out of the truck and let him drive it off while we got back in my jeep and headed back to the Dream House in time for Breakfast.<br /> <br /> Sex Breakfast was the same as usual. Talk of sex, porn and other \u201cbehind closed doors\u201d kinds of topics. It eventually strayed to safer topics when Lori brought up the idea of inducting her childhood friends into the Motley. We all agreed that we\u2019d like to have them be part of the group and they readily said yes when asked. Lori asked if we could have them take the pledge later today after we get back from dealing with the Bulgarian facility. That was amenable to everyone else so we penciled that in for later this afternoon. And now we need to be getting ready to go to the facility. We are all meeting there with whatever gear and/or weapons we want to bring. <br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXXVIII</i><br /> <br /> Oh boy. So, the heist was fun. Inside job. Unrealistic I am sure\u2026or at least, I hope. I guess one never knows these days.<br /> <br /> Julia, Insincere Marguerite Missy and Jane had a Wiccan Esbat ritual. No magick of any sort being done.<br /> <br /> I\u2026think\u2026that\u2019s everything? Comments and Questions welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T14:11:56-07:00","id":1295650,"title":"","content":"And so the times comes. The Descent.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXXIX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary </b><br /> <br /> Okay, it\u2019s all over now. I hope. I mean, probably. There are a few niggling doubts and details that we need to double-check, but I\u2019m pretty sure we\u2019re past the worst of the Bulgarian teleport zombie threat. Y\u2019know, like, ninety-eight percent sure.<br /> <br /> So on the surface (literally), my day wasn\u2019t nearly as stressful as that of much of the rest of the Freehold. We gathered at the site of the subterranean Bulgarian research lab a little after 1:00pm, and a large chunk of the able-bodied and combat-ready citizens of the Lady By the Sea were present and accounted for. It was sort of fun at first, like a social gathering. Then Augustine started dividing the assembled troops into teams.<br /> <br /> First up was the stealth team, including such notables as Marguerite, Calamity, and Dahlia. Their job was to slip into the lower corridors unnoticed, report on our enemy\u2019s numbers, and disable any nasty surprises they might have left us. They weren\u2019t supposed to engage unless there was no other choice\u2026 or a good opportunity to take a small number of enemies alone presented itself.<br /> <br /> The second \u2013 and largest \u2013 group was the strike team, led personally by Viscount Augustine. I\u2019m not going to try to list everyone who participated in this group, though a few notables do stand out. Jacob was there with his knives ready. T.J. was as happy as I\u2019ve ever seen him, brandishing a huge club that seemed to be constructed from the bumper and grill of a semi truck. Becky, Shi, Molly, Percival\u2026 the list goes on and on. This group was to sweep into the complex after the stealth team had given their reports and leave nothing standing.<br /> <br /> The third group was our hand-picked team of demolitionists: Andromeda, Halley, Anton, and Calamity (again). Once the strike team had cleared the building of all obvious threats, the four of them would descend and do what they could to take out the machine. Though we hoped that most of the danger would be over by the time they went in\u2026 I think we all knew that they\u2019d still be taking a terrible risk.<br /> <br /> Finally, there was my team\u2026 the healers. It was me, Jolie, Desiree, Flores, and Angelica, backed up by Maria (who could both serve as a bodyguard and use her Leechfinger abilities to provide backup healing if necessary). Our job was to keep an eye on the exit and provide a stable fallback position and triage camp should our enemies prove stronger than we anticipated.<br /> <br /> A few notes before I get to the action. First, Halley and Andromeda were actually talking to each other, and it seemed to be fairly civil. Well, I say \u201ctalking,\u201d but \u201ccommunicating\u201d is probably closer to the mark. They were each producing a series of tones that didn\u2019t sound like they could possibly come from a human larynx\u2026 Andromeda\u2019s were melodic and Halley\u2019s dissonant, but they still seemed to produce a strange but beautiful alien tune when taken together. I couldn\u2019t make heads or tails of it, but Anton said he occasionally caught the gist of what they were saying.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s amazing,\u201d he said excitedly. \u201cMr. Grey used to talk like that from time to time, and I picked up a few phrases here and there. They can describe everything about a weapon, including how to disassemble and maintain it, with only three or four notes\u2026 just by varying the pitch and duration slightly. Imagine what we could accomplish if our own communications were that efficient\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I allowed as how it was pretty amazing, and then continued to walk amongst the troops, offering what encouragement I could here and there. I made sure to speak to Joan, and once again offered my sincere apologies for putting Andromeda in danger. Joan\u2019s face remained impassive, but she told me that she understood that I had to do my duty. Then she kissed my forehead and quietly told me that she loved me. I responded in kind, and barely kept my tears in check. It wouldn\u2019t do for the queen to cry on the eve of battle, now would it? Have to keep morale high.<br /> <br /> It wasn\u2019t my party, though, so when the time came to give the requisite St. Crispin\u2019s Day speech, that honor fell to Viscount Augustine\u2026 and he did a great job, too. With their spirits bolstered, our brave troops entered the facility\u2026 leaving the engineering and medical teams to bide our time topside.<br /> <br /> So most of my afternoon was spent nervously chatting with my fellow Spring Courtiers and trying not to <u>look</u> nervous so that I could give the illusion of confidence and control. I bantered with Jolie a bit, pouting that she and Veronica hadn\u2019t returned with Desiree to attempt to seduce me last night. She countered that I\u2019d had my chance, which only deepened my pout\u2026 but I consoled myself by asserting that the rest of the Spring Court still loved me (a statement eagerly confirmed by Desiree, Flores, and Angelica). I also playfully asserted that she was trying to get back at me for turning her down when she asked me to be her consort two years ago\u2026 a statement which she cheerfully denied with a twinkle in her eye.<br /> <br /> This back-and-forth was occasionally punctuated by news from Augustine, transmitted via a walkie-talkie. Each time it squawked at me, my heart leapt up into my throat\u2026 but the news was usually good. The first level was clear, and Madame Spidertoes was dealing with the resident ghosts. The stealth team had disarmed the traps on the second level. The zombie-things in that area had been defeated. No casualties or serious injuries on our side. That sort of thing.<br /> <br /> When they were ready to open the doors to the lower levels, Gloria emerged from the complex to fetch the machine gun. Both D and I gave her hugs and kisses, and admonished her to be careful. \u201cRemind me never to get on T.J.\u2019s bad side,\u201d she said with a shudder, and went on to describe how our porcine friend had almost single-handedly crippled the first wave of the opposition, leaving the rest of the strike force to mop up the dregs that remained. Then she bolstered her strength with Summer contracts, hefted the bulky weapon, and walked back into the facility. I\u2019m not ashamed to admit that I said a silent prayer for my newest girlfriend\u2019s safety.<br /> <br /> We could occasionally hear \u2013 or <u><u>feel</u></u> \u2013 the roar of combat from somewhere deep below us. The reports continued to pour in. The door was opened and unguarded. The stealth team was moving in to reconnoiter. And finally, the walkie crackled one last time.<br /> <br /> \u201cMistress Lorelei,\u201d Augustine\u2019s voice came through amidst the static, \u201cI need to ask for your opinion.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course, Viscount,\u201d I replied. \u201cWhat can I do for you?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe have cornered the infected scientists,\u201d he said. \u201cThey want to surrender. I know what\u2019s at stake, but\u2026 it is against my inclination to do harm to those who are attempting to relent honorably.\u201d<br /> <br /> I thought about it, I really did. Killing someone who isn\u2019t actively trying to hurt me or my friends is against <u><u>my</u></u> nature too. But in the end, it was just too dangerous. The Freehold was depending on us to keep it safe. I knew that we couldn\u2019t risk whatever the Bulgarians had unleashed in 1962 spreading.<br /> <br /> I sighed. \u201cI understand, Viscount,\u201d I said, \u201cbut I don\u2019t think we can let them live. They\u2019re crafty, and they want to spread throughout this world like a virus. We have to make sure that doesn\u2019t happen. But\u2026 having said that, you\u2019re the War Leader of this Freehold. Whatever you decide, I\u2019ll back your play.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you,\u201d he said after a moment. And then, quietly, \u201cmaybe we can offer to euthanize them painlessly.\u201d<br /> <br /> In the end, it wasn\u2019t to be. Calamity acted without orders. She and Dahlia killed the infected scientists before Augustine could pronounce his decision. She saw a threat and she neutralized it without consulting anyone else. <u><u>Again</u></u>. And this time\u2026 I really can\u2019t even fault her for it, though I\u2019m sure there will be consequences. <u><u>Again</u></u>.<br /> <br /> The engineering team moved in after that. I don\u2019t know much about what they faced down there; I got everything secondhand. I know that there was no more physical resistance, but the machine itself had some sort of insidious defense mechanism. According to nearly everyone who was down there, it sort of\u2026 got inside your head. It tried to make you do things that were not in your best interests. According to Halley and Andromeda, the device attempted to download its own schematics directly into their brains.<br /> <br /> It failed, of course. I\u2019m confident that both Andromeda and Halley were able to fend off the intrusive presence. Anton and Calamity too, for that matter. I have to be.<br /> <br /> Once the machine was\u2026 dead, I guess? Once that problem was taken care of, Augustine pulled everyone out, because our demolitions experts had set shaped charges on the device with a twenty minute timer. Luckily, everyone was safely aboveground before the explosives went off, which collapsed the bottom floors of the facility entirely. Now the machine is not only dead, it\u2019s buried deep.<br /> <br /> A few things I should mention before I wrap this up. The first is the nagging doubt in the back of my mind that we\u2019ve seen the last of this place or its strange infestation. My reasoning behind this is twofold. First, not everything about the Bulgarian facility got buried when the bomb went off. Anton brought one of the scientist\u2019s bodies back with him for study. I think he\u2019s hoping he can determine more about what caused the breach and how the infection spreads by examining the remains. Though I\u2019m worried about further contamination\u2026 I have to admit that the medical student in me knows that an autopsy is one of the best ways to investigate an infection\u2019s propagation and pathology.<br /> <br /> It might be moot anyway. Anton <u><u>also</u></u> told us that there was something in the air down on those lower levels\u2026 something alien. He took a few samples, and he and Oleander are going to put their heads together and study it to see what it is and try to determine if it has any detrimental effects on changeling or human biology. Like I said before, of course the threat of contamination bothers me, but I know that if there is further danger, our best chance of overcoming it lies in studying those samples.<br /> <br /> After all of our precautions, nothing came of the Andromeda/Halley feud today. They worked well together, in fact\u2026 though I don\u2019t think this heralds an end to the schism. Andromeda would really like to patch things up, but Halley is having none of it, if I read their body language correctly after they left the facility. Halley actually stormed off and left the site not long after that, forcing Augustine to call her back so that she could properly seal off the upper levels of the building.<br /> <br /> I told everyone assembled that their next drinks at the Dream House were on me, and got a pretty big round of applause for that. I meant exactly what I said, too\u2026 I don\u2019t want Jacob to comp them; I want him to put those drinks on my personal tab. As Spring Queen, I\u2019m one-quarter of the reason they were out there risking their lives, and I want them to know that their courage and determination are appreciated.<br /> <br /> Which leaves the question of Calamity. I don\u2019t know everything that happened down there, and I honestly don\u2019t <u><u>want</u></u> to know. But something <u><u>seriously</u></u> spooked her. We were chatting about something on the way home \u2013 I honestly don\u2019t even remember what it was, but the possibility of further violence came up \u2013 and Calamity said in this desultory voice \u201cI don\u2019t care; someone else can stab him.\u201d I turned to her and asked what was wrong. She vaguely described some sort of experiment the possessed scientists had been running in the basement\u2026 something involving human remains and metal parts. I think she was about to say something else about it, but she stopped herself. Whatever it was, it really bothered her.<br /> <br /> I did feel the need to point out that there would likely be some fallout from her decision to cut out the middleman and kill those surrendering scientists. I was quick to let her know that I actually thought she\u2019d done the right thing this time. This wasn\u2019t like the situation with Mr. Grey; those creatures posed a clear and present danger to everything we hold dear, and they were obviously trying to capitalize on the rules of engagement to spread their infection among the Freehold.<br /> <br /> But on the other hand, Augustine is recognized by the Wyrd as the war leader of the Lady By the Sea. While I don\u2019t always agree with all of his decisions, we can\u2019t have soldiers undermining his authority left and right either. If the Wyrd decides that he\u2019s not an effective leader, it could spell definite trouble for us down the road. We don\u2019t want his role in our story to be undermined with the threat of Hollywood looming.<br /> <br /> I tried to give her a bit of space as we got home and prepared for movie night. I don\u2019t know what we\u2019re going to watch yet, but requests came from several people to make it something lighthearted; something we could watch while doing some serious drinking. Sounds like a good plan to me.<br /> <br /> But before that\u2026 we have Missy and Jane\u2019s official swearing-in ceremony! The two of them apparently went out shopping with Julia while we were otherwise engaged today and bought new dresses for the occasion. I\u2019m glad they\u2019re properly excited about taking this step\u2026 I know I am. It\u2019ll be <u><u>amazing</u></u> to have them as part of the family\u2026 y\u2019know, officially.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei de la Rocha</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> And just like that it\u2019s over. We all gathered in the woods near the hatch to prepare. Everyone broke up into their respective groups. The stealth team was talking together, Lori was with the healers that were going to stay topside, and I was with the infiltration team. I know Lori walked around giving hugs and kisses to all of her girlfriends and Calamity talked to a few people outside of the stealth team. Then it was time to go. Calamity, Dahlia and Insincere Marguerite went in and scouted out the first floor. They didn\u2019t find any traps there, so they then sent in Madame Spidertoes to deal with the ghosts. She did so in a few short minutes and came back out. Then we went in and waited on the first floor while the stealth team cleared traps out of the second floor. There were a few tripwires and altered hotplates down there. I think the idea was that we would trip on the wires and then fall on the hotplates, which were rigged to give off an electrical charge and start on fire. Actually, not sure if they were supposed to start fires, but they did when nudged by Calamity. She found a yardstick and pushed one to see what happened. After that they pushed them all to the sides of the hallway. This alerted the zombies that were down there to come and see what had tripped their traps. They searched all over the place looking for the infiltrators but couldn\u2019t find them since they were all three invisible and sticking to the walls and ceiling. Then it was our turn. TJ led the main attack force wielding his bumper/grill that he got from the semi that hit him. He hit all five zombies in one swipe. Then others of us rushed in. TJ took out two with a second swing. I took out one zombie, Augustine killed one, and Ji Wen Ja killed the last. It was over in moments. While all of that was going on Calamity was killing the child zombie, which was hiding in the vents, and Dahlia and Marguerite were moving the rest of the hotplate traps. I heard Calamity\u2019s gunfire as I dealt with the zombie in front of me.<br /> <br /> After all of that we prepared to go down to the next level. Hannah and Molly set up the big gun by the entrance and once the door was opened they started firing. They didn\u2019t continue long because it was obvious that there was no one coming up the stairs. Sandoval had even summoned a sand elemental to fight, but it was not needed. The stealth team then went in and discovered a few locked offices as well as two waterlogged men that had managed to hook up a generator to the ceiling lights when the water level receded a bit. They seemed happy with their accomplishment. They then sent for me to sneak in so I could translate what the two guys were talking about. Turns out that it was just them discussing how to go about surrendering to the U.S. forces that they figured were invading the facility. They were making sure that their IDs were in order even after being under water for so long. Apparently, they were laminated or something because they seemed legible to me. I went back to tell Augustine and the others what I\u2019d heard. Some people were of the opinion that we should just kill them. Augustine wanted to accept their surrender. He conferred with Lori topside for a moment to see what she thought about the situation. But as luck would have it, the decision was taken out of Augustine\u2019s hands by Calamity. She wanted to just kill them so she motioned for Dahlia to follow her and they both went back down the hall and quickly and quietly took out the two scientists that had been talking. Augustine was not happy when he found out what had happened but said that he\u2019d talk to Calamity about that later.<br /> <br /> Once the scientists were dead then it was time to move the technical team in. I led Hailey down to the lab that Calamity described as having the machine in it. Hailey assured me that she could shut it down just by looking at it. It took more concentration than I think she was expecting to have to use but Hailey was able to use her gremlin abilities to short out the machine and one of the two generators that was in the room with it. Then Andromeda and Twitch came down and the two girls started working together to take apart the machine. They talked together using melodic sounds. Each girl had their own sound but they meshed really well together and the resulting sound was beautiful. Twitch apparently could translate what they were saying. I learned later that he had heard Mr. Grey speak that language many times and learned to at least understand what was being said for the most part. So, Andromeda and Hailey shut down the machine and then placed a shaped C-4 charge on it with a twenty-minute timer. We all evacuated the building and closed the hatch. Twitch left the lab with one of the scientist\u2019s bodies to examine later. I thought that it was a bad idea bringing the body out of the facility in the first place. Who knows what it\u2019s been tainted with and Twitch is going to expose the freehold to it. Speaking of exposure though, there was something in the air down in the lower levels that Twitch could see was there but didn\u2019t know what it was. He said that he would take the samples that he took back to his lab and analyze it to see what it was. Hopefully it was nothing bad, because several of us got exposed to whatever it was in the act of cleaning out the final floor and taking out the machine.<br /> <br /> And that was a nasty piece of work, that machine. Part way through taking it apart Andromeda and Hailey had to stop and step away from the machine as it tired to download the information on how to create it into their brains. It seemed almost sentient. Then there was the feeling that I got in my head when I went near it, before it was shorted out. It felt like cotton or something was filling my brain and it kind of buzzed at the base of my skull. Calamity mentioned feeling the same thing, which made me feel a little bit better. At least it wasn\u2019t just me that the machine was sending bad vibes. It\u2019s not good that it was doing that at all to us, but I don\u2019t like getting singled out by evil machines. Or evil anyone for that matter. So, the charge went off and there was a resounding thud sound and the ground trembled. Insincere Marguerite went back down briefly to see how far she could get. She stayed on the first floor and said that the stairwell leading down to the lower levels was collapsed. Hopefully that means that the whole thing is buried under a fuck ton of debris and dirt and we won\u2019t have to worry about it again. \u2018Cause if something/someone figures out how to get down there and play with the remains of the machine I\u2019ll be pissed. I suggested welding the hatch shut so it couldn\u2019t be opened no matter how clever some hiker happened to be. The idea was approved and they said that they\u2019d come back with the equipment to do just that. We didn\u2019t happen to have any of it with us at the time.<br /> <br /> After it was all over Andromeda tried again to talk to Hailey about making up but it didn\u2019t work out. They worked really well together taking the machine apart, but when it comes to regular social interactions Hailey doesn\u2019t want to have anything to do with Andromeda. I don\u2019t blame her in the least. The person that turned her into what she is today is still walking around free and with everyone\u2019s support. Hailey is the outcast for some reason, and the victim in this whole mess. I can\u2019t claim to be lily white as far as what I did in Arcadia, but at least I never forced someone to be my lover. I can see why Hailey is so upset about the whole situation. I wish I could do more for her, but I don\u2019t know if she\u2019d welcome any help from an outside source. I\u2019ll just keep doing what I can to be a supportive friend.<br /> <br /> Once everything was done people started splitting up to head back to their respective homes. There is still the machine gun to return to the Navy, but that will happen a little bit later. Not sure if Calamity and me will be the ones returning it or not. We\u2019ll figure that out later. I think before any of that happens we\u2019re going to have movie night. I\u2019m not sure what we\u2019re going to be watching yet. I guess a lot of stuff is still up in the air. Regardless though it\u2019s time to end this and get on with whatever happens next.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXXIX</i><br /> <br /> Oh lets see.<br /> <br /> Augustine had his reasons for being twichy about the surrender thing. That will (probably) come up this session.<br /> <br /> So Calamity found the child sized zombie hiding in a ventilation shaft, and invisibly crept up and fired her sawed up shotgun into their head. Calamity was, perhaps creepily cheerful about this. Saw also saw a person, in connected pieces, kept alive by a generator on the bottom level. The limbs tried to move when it saw her, and Calamity put them out of their misery. This caused a Clarity check she passed; yay for dice from Meditation. More the seeing and understanding it than the killing. She hid the madness inducing thing from everyone else, even Dahlia and Insincere Marguerite never saw it.<br /> <br /> So is this the end? Well, that remains to be seen. Join us for the next chapter and find out. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T14:25:38-07:00","id":1299396,"title":"","content":"The Motley adds two. The aftermath of the raid on the lab continues. Someone new joins the freehold. Lori beds them.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXXX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Welcome, one and all, to the latest installment of \u201cQueen Lorelei drowns her anxieties in sex and alcohol!\u201d Shows twice daily, two drink minimum.<br /> <br /> So we were lounging around the Dream House on Monday afternoon, fresh from the fight, waiting until it was time to induct Missy and Jane into the motley officially. The two of them were excited by the prospect\u2026 Missy was nervous and a little jittery while Jane was trying her best to look like she was taking the whole thing in stride. Julia had taken the two of them out shopping, and they had picked up some nice new fancy dresses just for the occasion.<br /> <br /> I got a phone call from Monica just before we started the ceremony. She had a new arrival with her, a girl named Tanner Horsley, and she was taking her around the Freehold to meet the monarchs. \u201cI know you\u2019re not performing tonight,\u201d she said, \u201cand I want to bring her to the show tomorrow night. But if you can spare a little time, I\u2019d like to introduce you in a more private setting first.\u201d<br /> <br /> Of course I told her to bring Tanner by, but asked for a little time to conclude our motley business first. She agreed to stop by about two hours later, which I figured would give us more than enough time for the simple induction ceremony.<br /> <br /> The ceremony itself <u><u>was</u></u> simple\u2026 but no less meaningful for that. Missy and Jane swore to love, honor, and respect the rest of us, and we swore likewise about them. They are under our protection now, and they\u2019ve sworn to protect us to the best of their ability as well. If they uphold this oath \u2013 which I\u2019m sure they will \u2013 they should gain a special insight into each other\u2019s hearts, and their life here should be prosperous. Those of us who hadn\u2019t depleted our glamour in the Bulgarian facility, like yours truly, helped to seal the pledge with a modicum of our power.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s official now\u2026 they\u2019re really a part of our family in the eyes of the Freehold. I couldn\u2019t be happier about that!<br /> <br /> We quickly made plans to celebrate the evening by taking in a late movie\u2026 actually going out to a movie instead of staying in for our regular movie night. Since none of us had seen the new<u> <u>Star Wars</u></u> flick, we picked up tickets online and waited for Monica to arrive. When she got there, she was accompanied by a <u><u>really</u></u> cute young woman. That\u2019s right, the Lady By the Sea has gained another looker. I don\u2019t know what it is about this place, but it certainly seems to attract the beautiful people.<br /> <br /> Tanner Horsley is blonde, vaguely punkish, and extremely pretty. Her lightly tanned skin and <u><u>gorgeous</u></u> bone structure lead me to believe that she might have some Native American blood. She has a very direct, in-your-face attitude that suits her, and she\u2019s sharp as a tack to boot. She asked us all a lot of very insightful questions about the Freehold, and told us that she\u2019d done the same with the other monarchs. We did our best to answer honestly so that she\u2019d have a clear idea of what she\u2019ll be getting into by settling here.<br /> <br /> She didn\u2019t go into a lot of detail about her Durance, which is perfectly understandable, of course. She did mention that she had been a knight, and I asked if she\u2019d met Joan yet (she had not). She was apparently the \u201cearth knight\u201d back in Arcadia, the champion of that particular element. She didn\u2019t elaborate on what that meant, and I chose not to pursue the subject further until I got to know her better.<br /> <br /> More on that later.<br /> <br /> After the two of them took their leave, the rest of us headed out to the movie. It was\u2026 well, I thought the movie was pretty good, though it was obvious that it played upon a nostalgia that I just don\u2019t feel. I mean, I really liked the original <u><u>Star Wars</u></u>, and I\u2019ve been fond of the sequels and prequels I\u2019ve been shown since I returned from Arcadia as well. But there were a lot of call-backs and visual cues in <u><u>The Force Awakens</u></u> that probably meant a lot more to people who grew up with the originals, or have had forty years to obsess over them, and those didn\u2019t tug at quite the same heartstrings in me.<br /> <br /> Whatever. It was still a good adventure flick, and I think it served its purpose in distracting Calamity from the things she saw during the raid, so I\u2019ll call it a successful evening out. We picked up a couple of pizzas on the way home, ate them in the media room, and then staggered off to bed in the wee hours of the morning, with most of us having gotten pretty drunk in the meantime. Jacob was making drinks to order, which meant that the less experienced among us \u2013 namely Missy and Jane \u2013 got to try some things they\u2019d never had before, like Fuzzy Navels and Mudslides. I mainly stuck to the bourbon, and Marguerite mainly stuck to the Snooty Bourbon. Maria, Marguerite, Julia, Missy, Jane and I all ended the night in bed together, of course, and we celebrated our two new motley members\u2019 pledge until we all passed out.<br /> <br /> Which of course happened about two hours before I had to get up, get showered, and drive into L.A. with Becky for my Tuesday morning classes and lab. Nothing unusual happened on campus today. I did okay in my classes, though I maintain my opinion that if my professors want my best efforts, they shouldn\u2019t give me such cute lab partners. It\u2019s very distracting.<br /> <br /> Sex Breakfast was well underway by the time we got back to the Dream House, and the usual banter was very much in evidence. Calamity and D were discussing the relative merits and drawbacks of punching Tom Jones in the dick for some reason (Calamity seemed to think it was important to avoid ruining the singer\u2019s pretty face, while Maria was in favor of punching the poor Welshman in general). When I asked why anyone would <u><u>want</u></u> to punch Mr. Jones (or \u201cSir Tom\u201d as I\u2019m told he should rightfully be called), they both sort of blinked at me.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell\u2026 what if he disrespected you?\u201d D asked after a moment.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhy would he do that?\u201d I asked flatly.<br /> <br /> \u201cUmm, I mean\u2026 well he <u><u>might</u></u>. It\u2019s possible,\u201d was her somewhat lame response.<br /> <br /> I just sort of let it drop and moved to a different conversation after that. To my dearest love, the punching itself is more important than the \u201cwhy\u201d of the punching.<br /> <br /> Turns out that Missy and Jane want to go back to Defiance at some point. Oh, not for good or anything like that, they just want to visit the old homestead. They\u2026 actually they want to visit their own graves. Of course I said I\u2019d head back there with them when the time was right \u2013 Mom\u2019s grave is there, after all, and I haven\u2019t visited her since before we were Taken \u2013 though I cautioned them that we\u2019d have to be careful. My fetch is still in that general area.<br /> <br /> Julia also finished her painting of Missy and Jane. They\u2019re going to get it scanned and have a large print made for themselves, and I suggested they could use it on their wedding invitations when they get to that point. What floored me was that they wanted <u><u>me</u></u> to have the original as a gift. \u201cWe never would have gotten out without you, Jules,\u201d Jane said to me, \u201cand we want you to know how much we appreciate that.\u201d I couldn\u2019t even <u><u>try</u></u> to stop my tears, and I pulled them both into a fierce group hug to show my own gratitude.<br /> <br /> And what did I do with the rest of my afternoon? Why, deal with a Freehold crisis, of course! I\u2019m really starting to understand why Jolie was so eager to give the crown away.<br /> <br /> I got a call from Augustine just after breakfast wrapped up. He wanted to let me know that Halley had contacted him to inform him that she woke up that morning with the knowledge of how to build another teleportation device fully formed within her head. At present she feels no compulsion to actually <u><u>build</u></u> such a device, but she could if she wanted to. Augustine called me first as a courtesy, because he thought Andromeda \u2013 a member of my court \u2013 might have had a similar experience.<br /> <br /> Of course I dialed up Andromeda at once. She was chipper enough when she answered, but once she realized why I had called she got very quiet. She did confirm that she also had the knowledge of how to create the device, and also assured me that she had no intention of actually doing so, but I could tell that she was scared.<br /> <br /> Eventually Joan\u2019s voice replaced Andromeda\u2019s on the line. \u201cLorelei. What did you <u><u>say</u></u> to her?\u201d she growled at me.<br /> <br /> I tried to explain the situation to Joan, but she was having none of it. \u201cAndromeda poses no threat to this Freehold, Lorelei. I will not see her intimidated or threatened over this\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cJoan,\u201d I said sharply, and then decided to rein it in a bit. Push Joan and she just pushes you back twice as hard. \u201cLindsay. You know me. You know how I feel about you and Rebecca. I hope you know that I would never do anything to hurt her\u2026 that even if the whole Freehold was threatened, I\u2019d try <u><u>everything</u></u> else before I even considered a course of action that would hurt her in any way.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2026 I know that,\u201d she allowed, \u201cbut\u2026 she\u2019s so upset\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sorry that I upset her,\u201d I soothed, \u201cbut it\u2019s an upsetting situation. That machine poses too great a risk for us not to address it. Can I tell you what I\u2019d like to do now?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes,\u201d she said softly.<br /> <br /> \u201cI want someone to go into her dreams and take a look around. It should be someone she trusts\u2026 ideally I\u2019d like to use Calamity if she\u2019s up for it. I\u2019d like her to see if we can excise this knowledge safely, or, failing that, wall it off from the rest of her mind so that she can\u2019t access it\u2026 so that <u><u>no one</u></u> can access it. Do you think that would be worth a try?\u201d<br /> <br /> Joan sighed on the other end of the line. \u201cI will ask her. And Lorelei\u2026 Juliette. I am sorry. When Rebecca is threatened or upset, I just\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know, Lindsay,\u201d I said. \u201cI know how much she means to you. I\u2019m just asking you to stop and think if something like this ever comes up again. I\u2026 can\u2019t put Rebecca\u2019s safety ahead of the Freehold\u2019s, but I swear to you that I will do everything I can to find a solution that is as easy on her as possible. Okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> There was a pause. \u201cVery well,\u201d she said after a moment. \u201cI suppose I cannot ask for more than that. Rebecca has agreed to try the dream healing solution. Thank you for looking out for her. And Lorelei\u2026 Juliette\u2026 we love you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI love you too,\u201d I replied, \u201cboth of you. Thank you for understanding.\u201d<br /> <br /> I sought out Calamity after we disconnected, and filled her in on the situation. Of course she agreed to do what she could for both Halley and Andromeda. She also told me that she didn\u2019t feel like any particular esoteric knowledge had been downloaded into her brain. She wasn\u2019t sure if that was because she and Anton never got too close to the machine while it was functional, or if it was because she lacked the specific technical knowledge foundations to build something like that in the first place. She suggested that I check on Anton just in case, and that seemed like a prudent precaution to me.<br /> <br /> I called John and filled him in on the situation. Augustine hadn\u2019t contacted him yet, and for a moment I was afraid I\u2019d jumped rank, but John waved off my concerns when I expressed them. \u201cAugustine and I don\u2019t really get along,\u201d he reminded me, \u201cbut he\u2019s a man who knows and values his duty. He\u2019s probably just making absolutely sure that he has all of the facts before he makes his report.\u201d<br /> <br /> John conferenced Anton in on our conversation, and he confirmed that he had felt no intrusive alien knowledge in his brain either. I asked for his opinion regarding Halley and Andromeda\u2019s experience, and he became very excited. He was careful to issue disclaimers before making any controversial statements, but said at one point that ideally he\u2019d like to be able to study any physiological changes their brains are undergoing as a result of exposure to the machine. He said time and again that he didn\u2019t want to harm either of them in any way, and after a moment I suggested that he speak with Andromeda to see if her portable scanner could be modified to give him the biochemical information he needs.<br /> <br /> He hasn\u2019t come to any conclusions regarding the autopsy or the strange chemicals he found in the air in the facility yet, but for the moment he doesn\u2019t think that the majority of us are in any real danger. He did note that the chemicals seemed to be composed of exotic particles not typically found on Earth. In fact, the only similar samples he could find a reference to came from the large hadron collider, where scientists have succeeded in creating miniature black holes for a tiny fraction of a second at a time. \u201cThey\u2019re basically like pieces of dead stars,\u201d Anton reported excitedly. Joy.<br /> <br /> So I had all of that rattling around in my big ol\u2019 empty head as I took the stage for the show. The number I chose for tonight was the Dusty Springfield classic \u201cSon of a Preacher Man,\u201d which I feel went very well. As soon as I announced my intention to perform that number, however, Maria felt it necessary to point out to me, Missy, and Jane that Dusty Springfield was a lesbian. Honestly, it\u2019s like she thinks we were totally oblivious to the world around us just because we were raised in the 70s. I drily informed her that we already knew that. Dusty was publicly involved with a woman when I was seven years old, for crying out loud!<br /> <br /> Oh, in addition to our usual line-up, we debuted a new act\u2026 Missy and Jane, singing a duet, without backing me up! They chose \u201cI Got You Babe\u201d by Sonny and Cher, which actually becomes pretty poignant when it\u2019s sung by a same-gender couple. The themes shift from youth against establishment to true love enduring despite societal restrictions. The two of them really knocked it out of the park in any case, and the audience ate it up. I made sure to give them both congratulatory kisses as they left the stage, and they both seemed giddy with their success. I think they\u2019re going to fit in just fine around here.<br /> <br /> I did the Queen thing and circulated amongst my people after my solo number. Halley was there, and Calamity and I made a bee-line for her as soon as we were both free to do so. I pitched the dream healing idea, and she went for it in a big way. When we had a moment of relative privacy, she also made sure to let me off the hook in another way that is\u2026 honestly a little worrying.<br /> <br /> \u201cMistress Lorelei,\u201d she said formally, \u201cI\u2019m glad you\u2019re looking for safe ways to deal with this threat. But I want you to know that if dream therapy doesn\u2019t work, I understand that more drastic measures might need to be taken. In plain language, I\u2019d rather have you kill me than become a danger to this Freehold. Just\u2026 just tell me that you need to sedate me or something. I\u2019d rather not know it\u2019s coming.\u201d<br /> <br /> I closed my eyes. \u201cThank you,\u201d I said, trying to honor her intent rather than the ghastly specifics of her request. \u201cI appreciate your dedication to our safety, I really do. But we\u2019re not even considering options like that yet. We\u2019re going to do everything we can to make sure that <u><u>everyone</u></u> makes it out of this intact.\u201d<br /> <br /> I listened into bits of a conversation between Calamity and Trinh, who was apparently running an investigation as a way to prove herself to the Autumn Court, which she hopes to join shortly. Something about a family keeping aborted fetuses in jars in their basement as a way of controlling their hungry ghosts\u2026 I didn\u2019t listen too closely to the details after that\u2026 thank God Jolie just asked me to help run a nightclub.<br /> <br /> It occurred to me at some point that my motley seems to have \u2018graduated\u2019 to a higher standing in the Freehold. Time was, the monarchs would have come to us to look into something like Trinh described. Now, those jobs go to the newcomers, and we get to hear about it in the aftermath. Hell, I <u><u>am</u></u> a monarch now\u2026 I guess I should start parceling things like that out to my constituents when they come across my desk instead of bringing them straight to the motley to deal with.<br /> <br /> I found a more pleasant diversion in talking with Monica and Tanner at their table. Tanner was very complimentary about the show, and obviously impressed by the motley\u2019s performances. We talked about her thoughts regarding the Freehold and the various monarchs, and before long we were flirting lightly. A few minutes later I felt her bare foot rubbing up against my calf under the table.<br /> <br /> One thing led to another, and when the crowds thinned, Monica left alone and Tanner ended up in my bed. I did my best to show her a night she\u2019d never forget, and I think she appreciated my efforts. She certainly gave as good as she got, in any case, and I have no complaints about the way my evening ended. We fell asleep clutching each other, breathing softly into each other\u2019s hair, with our bodies pressed close.<br /> <br /> I hope the other monarchs don\u2019t see this as some sort of unfair recruitment practice. I need to make sure that Tanner knows that I\u2019ll still be open to sleeping with her even if she joins another Court. But, I don\u2019t know\u2026 that just sounds a little conceited to me, like I think she won\u2019t be able to resist me now that she\u2019s sampled my body.<br /> <br /> She\u2019s still sleeping now, snoring softly, splayed out, and beautiful. As usual, I woke up relatively early and decided to do a little reading and writing. I want nothing more than to just climb back into that bed and revel in the shared warmth and affection\u2026 but I have online classes to attend. Sigh. Oh well, maybe she\u2019ll still be asleep when I\u2019m done.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei de la Rocha</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Our late afternoon was pretty mundane compared to earlier in the day. We inducted Missy and Jane into the motley. They had even gone out and gotten new dresses to wear for the occasion. Seems like just yesterday when I first took the motley pledge with this group of then strangers. We didn\u2019t know each other save for our names and we agreed to become a motley then and there. I\u2019m not sure why I joined the motley back then. I didn\u2019t know these guys and with a motley you have to be able to trust the others. I suppose that there was a certain amount of protection built into the pledge itself as we promised not to hurt one another intentionally. I can honestly say that it all worked out though. I have come to see the others as a family. One that I can and have trusted with my life. I trusted them with my secret and I haven\u2019t regretted it. That said, I haven\u2019t told Missy or Jane about having been a Loyalist and probably won\u2019t for a while, if ever. I know that they are good friends with Lori, but I don\u2019t know them very well. I\u2019ve only known them for a month so far, and that is not enough time for me to trust someone. That and I\u2019m not sure what their reaction would be. They are still fresh out of Arcadia. Knowing that I used to do essentially the same job that Hunting Hawk did would likely not sit well with them. But that is not something that I have to worry about as of now. I have no intention of telling them about my past just yet. Maybe in the future if they have proven that I can trust them with that information I\u2019ll tell them. But not yet.<br /> <br /> After we inducted Lori\u2019s friends into the motley Monica brought a new arrival by the Dream House to meet Lori. Monica was introducing her to all the monarchs. The new girl\u2019s name is Tanner Horsley and she is an earth elemental of some kind. She seemed rather more inquisitive than most new arrivals tend to be. She wanted to know about the good things that the Freehold has to offer as well as any downsides. She was rather specific in her questions and I couldn\u2019t help but get the feeling that maybe she wasn\u2019t so new after all. Tanner said that she had been a knight of earth back in Arcadia. I\u2019m not sure what kind of life she had before she was taken, but I wasn\u2019t sure if her experience in Arcadia would lend itself to the types of questions that she was asking. We answered all of her questions though we did not give away anything that wasn\u2019t already public knowledge. She just seemed a lot more together than most newbies are. Most folks are too shell shocked, or maybe culture shocked, to even think about the pros and cons of where she was and the strengths and weaknesses of the place. I guess I just don\u2019t trust her. Not that that is surprising or anything. I don\u2019t trust people easily. I guess time will tell whether or not she is telling the truth and just happens to have a very adaptive mind, or if she is not as new as she claims to be. <br /> <br /> Once Monica and Tanner left we started talking about what movies we wanted to watch for movie night. We couldn\u2019t really agree on something lighthearted to watch. Then someone suggested that we see what movies were out in theaters, so we looked. And lo and behold the new Star Wars movie was out. It\u2019s called The Force Awakens, and it was really good. I have always liked the Star Wars movies and this one did not disappoint. After the movie we talked about going out for pizza, but the conversation went off in weird directions, mostly about who was going to pair off with who and other sex stuff. Several people also commented that they would like a drink, which is all well and good but someone would have to stay sober to be the designated driver, and I didn\u2019t want to have to be the responsible one. So I suggested that we just get take out pizza and head back to the Dream House where I could make everyone whatever drink they wanted and we didn\u2019t need to watch how much we drank since we were already at home. The others agreed with that idea and we got a few pizzas to split between the lot of us and headed back to the Dream House. While everyone was eating I started taking requests for drinks and I made a variety. Missy wasn\u2019t sure what kind of drink she\u2019d like so I asked if she liked fruity drinks. She said yes, so I suggested a Fuzzy Navel. They are fruity, frozen and not too alcoholic. Jane didn\u2019t want anything too fruity so I made her a Mudslide. The taste of alcohol is pretty well covered up by the chocolate flavor, and it\u2019s not too strong either. I figured it would be a good drink for someone that is not used to drinking but didn\u2019t want to look like that was the case. The others are more used to drinking and so I made whatever it was that they wanted. I didn\u2019t worry too much about the strength of what they were having. I know what they can handle, and how much, so it was all good. Then we all split up. The majority of the group went to Lori and De la Rocha\u2019s bedroom, Becky and Calamity went to Calamity\u2019s room. Luna and I went to mine. And now it\u2019s probably time for me to stop writing and go to sleep.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> And just when I thought things were over, they\u2019re not. Though things started out like normal. We had a breakfast of French toast and Canadian bacon. Calamity made it. It was good. Then there was conversation about punching Tom Jones. I\u2019m honestly not sure how that started up. De la Rocha was a big proponent of punching him in the junk. She asked me at one point who she was not allowed to punch and I replied with someone that she was allowed to hit. Tom Cruise. I do not respect that man, or the way he treats people. I also do not like Scientology. So I said that she could hit Scientologists. She was okay with that. So was Calamity. Then De la Rocha shared hospital stories with us. Apparently in the past she has had to deal with random people asking her for Demerol. Not that she\u2019d given anyone the idea that she could get this stuff. She was an X-ray tech, they just assumed that someone in scrubs could get them Demerol for their \u201cbrother.\u201d Needless to say it didn\u2019t work. She\u2019s also apparently had someone hit her for one reason or another. I guess they were upset that she left the room while they were getting X-rayed. She can\u2019t stay for every X-ray, just like I can\u2019t take a drink with everyone I serve, it\u2019d be bad for her health. Then on a brighter note Julia finished a painting of Missy and Jane. Nothing creepy about it, just a nice picture of the two of them. They decided to give it to Lori and just keep a print for themselves. Their way of thanking her for getting them out of Arcadia. <br /> <br /> Later Lori got a call from Augustine. She talked to him in private for a while and then brought Calamity in on the conversation. Eventually she brought the topic of concern to all of our attention. It seems that Hailey woke up this morning with the knowledge of how to build that fucking machine in her head. She became concerned and notified Augustine about it. Lori became worried that Andromeda might be experiencing the same thing and called her lover to ask. It turns out that her fears were well founded. Andromeda woke up with the same information in her head and was kind of freaking out about it. Calamity suggested that someone should talk to Twitch and see if he had any of the knowledge in his own head. He was close to the pair of them and listening closely to what was going on. He is also a chirurgeon and so she thought that might be affected. So, Lori called Lowjack and they checked in on Twitch. He does not seem to have been affected by the machine in any way. At least none that he\u2019s told the rest of us about anyway. Hopefully that is true. Anyway, it was Lori that had suggested doing dream healing on Hailey and Andromeda to see if that might work to either remove the information or to block it off from their active memory. I thought it was a good idea. Calamity helped Molly remember her past through Dream healing. Maybe there is a way to do the opposite? I guess time will tell on that one. Here\u2019s hoping.<br /> <br /> And conversation about much the same thing happened after the show. Hailey was drinking fairly heavily at the bar tonight and after their numbers Calamity and Lori made a beeline for the bar to talk to her. They were vague in their speech, but if you knew what was going on it was obvious what they were talking about. They brought up the idea of dream therapy as a way to get rid of or block the information on how to build the machine. Hailey agreed to that and said that she is thinking about what she knows but feels no compulsion to make it. If that should change she said she would let someone know immediately. She also gave Lori permission flat out to poison her if she should become a danger to the Freehold. She just asked that it be given as an injection meant to help stop her from doing anything with the knowledge, but actually be something lethal. She wanted to remain ignorant of her impending death should it come to that. After that heavy thought Calamity and Lori left and went about their usual rounds in the audience. They also went to talk to the new girl, Tanner, who came to the club to watch the show. Not sure what they talked about, but it seemed amicable. After those two left I brought Hailey another drink, even though I\u2019d been slowing her down previously. I figured she could use one more after having that conversation.<br /> <br /> Thankfully no other heavy conversations came up and those at the bar were able to relax. I cut Hailey off after a little bit longer and made sure that she drank a good bit of water before she left. I wanted her to be able to make it home alright. I figured that I might have to call her a taxi, but that turned out to be unnecessary. She was really the only person that I had to keep a close eye on too, which was good. Sometimes I need to keep an eye on multiple people. There\u2019s one guy named Curtis that I\u2019m pretty sure is an alcoholic. He comes to the show frequently and almost every time he comes I need to cut him off from the alcohol after a point. He was not in tonight, so I didn\u2019t need to keep an eye on him as well. Small favors.<br /> <br /> Once the show was over and the crowd gone people once again split up to go their own ways. This time though Lori went upstairs with Tanner by herself. De la Rocha went her own way. I\u2019m still not sure about Tanner, so having her go off with one of the reigning monarchs two days after she\u2019s been back in \u2018the world\u2019 is a little concerning. At least to me it is. I know that Lori tends to see people in the best light possible right from the beginning, whereas I don\u2019t. I can\u2019t afford to. Well, I guess it\u2019s not so important now if I miss someone\u2019s true intentions, but in the past I\u2019ve needed to be careful about those that I interacted with because most people couldn\u2019t be trusted. Before I joined the Lady I was betrayed more times than I\u2019d like to admit because I was too na\u00efve and trusted the wrong people. I swore to myself that I wouldn\u2019t let that happen again and so I am skeptical of people\u2019s intentions from the start. I just hope that Lori doesn\u2019t pay for her own naivet\u00e9 in this instance. If Tanner hurts Lori I\u2019d say that I\u2019d go after her in return, but truthfully De la Rocha would beat me to the punch (literally) on that one. Here\u2019s hoping that Tanner is on the up and up. I don\u2019t want to see my friend get hurt. <br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXXX</i><br /> <br /> I honestly don\u2019t remember why they were talking about punching Sir Tom in the dick. These conversations just happen. I do remember IM opined that the universe seems to punch the Welsh in the junk as a matter of course.<br /> <br /> Metaphorically, I assume.<br /> <br /> Not a lot of rolling, Missy and Jane got added to the Motley, most of the rolls were to perform. <br /> <br /> Anyway, more to come. Comments and questions welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T13:36:29-07:00","id":1303396,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to return to the swirling drama in Santa Monica.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXXXI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Could this be some sort of karmic retribution for all the amazing experiences I had last year? Getting married to the girl of my dreams, getting my feathers back, joining the Pilgrims of the Endless Road, getting accepted to UCLA, successfully rescuing Missy and Jane and the like? Because if it\u2019s not, I confess that I think I must be due for a break in the near future.<br /> <br /> So I got up this morning and tried to be careful not to disturb Tanner, who was snoring contentedly in my arms. I threw on a T-shirt and some sweatpants and headed to the media room to attend my online classes. Things were going pretty well right up until about halfway through my French Romantic Literature class, when my phone rang. Checking the caller ID I saw that it was Anton, so I paused the lecture and answered it.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, good, you\u2019re awake,\u201d Anton said as soon as I\u2019d connected. \u201cWhat should I call you, anyway? You\u2019re the Spring Queen, so it seems like you should be Mistress de la Rocha, but you\u2019re also my best friend\u2019s wife, so maybe just Lorelei or even Lori\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> He sounded like he was going to keep going unless I stopped him, so I cut in as gently as I could. \u201cJust \u2018Lori\u2019 is fine, Anton,\u201d I assured him. \u201cNow\u2026 to what do I owe the pleasure this morning?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSorry, I guess I\u2019m a little jittery right now,\u201d he explained, \u201cI haven\u2019t really slept since the raid on the facility the other day. But I\u2019ve had some of the Spring Court crack, so I\u2019m good to go for now. Anyway, I think we\u2019ve made a breakthrough with those exotic particles. Oleander\u2019s been working with me, and we have an idea of what\u2019s going on and how we might be able to address the problem.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s great!\u201d I said with enthusiasm, which just goes to show that I do not have the keenest sense of when the world is about to go completely to shit.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s fascinating, really,\u201d Anton continued with obvious relish. \u201cThe particles are repeatedly opening microscopic black holes for the tiniest fraction of a second. These singularities aren\u2019t open long enough to do any real damage, but they do allow information to pass through from whatever\u2019s on the other side. This information takes the form of radio waves, but it\u2019s not on the AM or FM spectrums\u2026 it\u2019s closer to the frequency of human neural waves.\u201d<br /> <br /> I took a moment to absorb all of that. \u201cSo\u2026 Halley and Andromeda are picking up alien <u><u>thoughts</u></u>?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s about the size of it,\u201d Anton agreed.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhy aren\u2019t the rest of us affected?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cSome of us \u2013 those who were closest to the device while it was active \u2013 probably are,\u201d Anton explained. \u201cWe just don\u2019t have the knowledge base or inventive genius to interpret the information, so our brains are ignoring it. Now thus far, only the schematics for the machine have been coming through these breaches\u2026 but we don\u2019t actually <u><u>know</u></u> what else might come through, given time.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay, so as long as the particles are active in our peoples\u2019 brains they pose a threat,\u201d I said. \u201cEven if we can get rid of the knowledge itself, the signal will just replace it. Any ideas?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI have a device that should allow us to identify the foreign particles so that they can be surgically extracted,\u201d he said, \u201cbut it still needs a bit of testing. I can probably have it ready in a day or two.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd you can remove the particles without harming the patients?\u201d I asked anxiously.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m confident that I can, with you assisting me,\u201d he shot back immediately.<br /> <br /> So that\u2019s when the static started up in my ears and the grey started to creep in from the edges of my vision. I think I might have let out a few dry croaks before my throat opened up enough for regular speech. \u201cAnton,\u201d I said in a voice barely above a whisper, \u201cI\u2019m a freshman in a pre-med program. I\u2019m taking <u><u>general</u></u> <u><u>education</u></u> courses right now. And you want me to perform <u><u>brain</u></u> <u><u>surgery</u></u>?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re the only uncompromised chirurgeon in the Freehold,\u201d he explained. \u201cYou have a gift for medical procedures, and you didn\u2019t go down into the facility with the rest of us. And if the signal starts to affect me during the procedure, you can sedate me until the surgery is done.\u201d He gave me a few seconds to digest that, then seemed to feel that he needed to say more. \u201cI can give you something to calm your nerves if you want. It\u2019ll help you focus. Though it has side effects. You might notice yourself developing an unhealthy obsession with Jane\u2019s Addiction. There are other side effects as well, but they\u2019re not permanent, so I\u2019m sure you can deal with them. Just keep in mind that there are no tiny bears inside Andromeda\u2019s brain and you\u2019ll be fine\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnton,\u201d I heard Oleander\u2019s voice in the background, \u201cslow down. Let her digest what you\u2019re saying.\u201d<br /> <br /> It gave me the kick in the ass I needed. \u201cOf course I\u2019ll help however I can,\u201d I agreed quickly. \u201cHave you told anyone else about this?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou were my first call,\u201d Anton said. \u201cI was going to call John next\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLet me take care of that,\u201d I suggested. \u201cYou get some rest. And Anton\u2026 good work.\u201d<br /> <br /> Anton promised to get some real sleep, and I passed a few words with Oleander before we disconnected. Then I called John to let him know what was going on. Yep, once again I found myself the bearer of bad news to the current reigning monarch. He quipped that one of these days I\u2019d just call him up and ask if he wanted to get a cup of coffee or something.<br /> <br /> So I told him what was going on, and he was cautiously optimistic about Anton\u2019s plan. He offered to spread the word to Augustine and Charlotte, figuring that I had enough on my plate already, and I gratefully accepted. I knew that there was one conversation I couldn\u2019t put on anyone else, though. \u201cJoan will take the news better if it comes from me,\u201d I said with resignation, and Lowjack allowed that this was probably true. He\u2019s going to disseminate the information to the rest of the monarchs, though, and presumably either he or Augustine will let Halley know about our plans.<br /> <br /> I decided to finish my classes for the day before I faced that particular challenge, and by the time I was done Calamity had returned from her morning meditations. I tried to play it cool, but she knew immediately that something was wrong, and it wasn\u2019t long before she\u2019d gotten the whole story out of me. I promised that I\u2019d tell the whole motley after Sex Breakfast\u2026 but there was something I had to do first.<br /> <br /> I went out onto the back balcony and hit the speed-dial button on my phone. She answered on the second ring. \u201cLori\u2026 Juliette,\u201d she yawned, \u201cwhat a pleasant surprise. To what do I owe the pleasure?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLindsay,\u201d I said softly. \u201cI need to speak with you and Rebecca. It\u2019s important. Can I join you at your place in a little while?\u201d<br /> <br /> There was a slight pause, and her voice was grave when she responded. \u201cCertainly. Give me some time to shower and dress, please.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course,\u201d I said, \u201cI\u2019ll be there in ninety minutes or so. And Lindsay\u2026 I love you both. I promise.\u201d<br /> <br /> There was another awkward pause, but I believe Joan\u2019s voice was a little softer when she answered. \u201cWe shall see you when you arrive,\u201d she replied.<br /> <br /> I felt the need to experience a little bit of freedom from my responsibilities (however temporary the reprieve might be), so I launched myself into the sky and flew for a while. It helped, but not as much as I\u2019d hoped it would. Endorphins are wonderful things, but they don\u2019t actually distract you from the actual circumstances of your life, so they can only go so far. Still\u2026 I do love flying, and I felt marginally more prepared to meet with Joan and Andromeda by the time I landed.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately I had more immediate problems to deal with. Tanner was awake when I entered my room to change, and it was obvious that she was dealing with some pretty heavy shit. She doesn\u2019t remember much about her life before Arcadia, but one of the things that she was relatively certain of was that she was straight. Apparently sleeping with me has undermined one of the few touchstones she had to connect her to her previous life.<br /> <br /> So yeah, she was a little messed up about it, which made me feel terrible. I tried to talk her through the rough spots, but she\u2019s going to have to work through these issues on her own. I brought up the Winter Court\u2019s therapists, but I don\u2019t think Tanner\u2019s quite ready to take that step yet.<br /> <br /> I apologized for having to run when she was having a crisis, showered, changed, and drove over to Joan and Andromeda\u2019s house (pausing only to grab a piece of toast from the kitchen on my way out, despite the fact that Trinh was over and breakfast smelled <u><u>delicious</u></u>). It was hard to ring that doorbell, and Joan\u2019s face when she answered the door wasn\u2019t encouraging, but she nodded me inside and escorted me into the living room.<br /> <br /> I told them what Anton had discovered about the nature of the exotic particles, and how the knowledge had been implanted in Andromeda and Halley\u2019s brains. Andromeda was almost as fascinated as Anton had been. Then I took a deep breath and prepared to take the plunge. \u201cAnd there\u2019s only one way we can think of to solve this problem\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Andromeda piped up at this point. \u201cTransfer my consciousness into a positronic brain, delete the dangerous information, and then replace my real brain with it to avoid future infections?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat?\u201d I said, confused. \u201cNo! Anton\u2019s working on a machine that will allow us to identify the exotic particles and remove them\u2026 surgically. Wait,\u201d I said, holding up a hand as Joan opened her mouth to object, \u201cthere\u2019s more. I\u2019ll be assisting with the surgeries. Since I took on the chirurgeon kith last Summer, I have an aptitude for operations of this sort. I won\u2019t let anything happen to her, Lindsay, I swear. I\u2019ll\u2026 I\u2019ll pledge to it if you want me to.\u201d<br /> <br /> Andromeda put her hand on top of mine. \u201cI trust you, Juliette,\u201d she said simply.<br /> <br /> \u201cAs do I, of course,\u201d Joan said softly. \u201cIf Rebecca will consent to the surgery, I will raise no objections.\u201d I could see how much it cost her to say that, so I got up and gave each of them a warm hug.<br /> <br /> \u201cI expect you two will want some time alone to process this,\u201d I said, making for the door. \u201cAnton says his machine won\u2019t be ready for a day or two. I\u2019ll let you know as soon as we have a timetable.\u201d<br /> <br /> Andromeda piped up as I was about to leave. \u201cI\u2019m a chirurgeon too,\u201d she pointed out. \u201cI could assist with the other surgery\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I sighed. \u201cI\u2019m sorry, honey,\u201d I said heavily, \u201cbut you know Halley would never allow it. But if we determine that any of the others who were down there need the procedure, I promise I\u2019ll let you know.\u201d<br /> <br /> So I left her a little glum on the doorstep and drove back to the Dream House. Sex Breakfast was nearly over, but they\u2019d saved me a plate of Trinh\u2019s yummy Cajun cooking. The food was good, but I didn\u2019t have much of an appetite, and I\u2019m sure the others noticed that I didn\u2019t participate in much of the usual banter either. I kind of settled in with Missy, Jane, Marguerite and Julia when they formed one of those hair brushing circles, and for a while it helped. It was comforting and familiar, reminding me as it did of how we used to preen and groom each other back in Arcadia. Still, it probably came as no surprise when I asked to speak with the motley privately after breakfast.<br /> <br /> Most of our guests had left by that point, and Tanner opted to spend some time in the theater in quiet contemplation of her current situation. Missy and Jane made to leave at first as well until I reminded them that they were part of the motley now. \u201cNo more secrets between us,\u201d I said half-truthfully, as there are still some things I\u2019ve learned in my role as Spring Queen that I haven\u2019t shared with most of the motley.<br /> <br /> So I shared the details of Anton\u2019s plan with the others, and as you might imagine, I started getting worked up about the fact that I\u2019ll be expected to perform <u><u>brain</u></u> <u><u>surgery</u></u> in a day or two. The others were remarkably good at helping me not to completely lose my shit over it. Calamity pointed out that the Wyrd wants me to be a doctor these days, and that I now have supernatural gifts which will assist greatly with the task at hand. Maria told me that she\u2019d seen Anton\u2019s machine, which involves remotely controlling tiny surgical implements from a full-sized console, so the procedure would probably seem more like playing a video game than more traditional neurosurgery. And Julia\u2026<br /> <br /> It was Calamity\u2019s idea. Julia offered to sing for me that afternoon so that I could get some real, restful sleep. It was brilliant\u2026 I knew I\u2019d never be able to relax without some form of assistance, be it magical or chemical. So I allowed myself to be led back up to my bedroom, where my Gothic sweetheart sat on the bed and cradled my head in her lap, stroking my hair and singing softly until my thoughts got all fuzzy and weird. And people say that I have a bewitching voice\u2026<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t remember much of the next few hours, though I know I dreamed. I have the sense that I was drifting along in the gentle currents of a broad, slow river, listening to the haunting melody that seemed to flow from my heart itself. I could tell by the currents of the warm waters and the distant sound of a roar that I was headed toward a great waterfall, but it didn\u2019t matter\u2026 I knew that being swept over its edge would only bring me into the embrace of my Dark Lady. So that was a thing that happened.<br /> <br /> Julia was good enough to wake me up in time to get ready for the show, and I actually did feel a lot better for having slept. I sang backup and danced in a few numbers last night, but only had one big solo. I decided to go with a slow, simple song by Phil Collins called \u201cIn the Air Tonight.\u201d It seemed appropriate, given the root of the problem to which Anton, Oleander and I were currently applying ourselves. It went over well enough, though it lacked the staging and theatricality of many of my numbers.<br /> <br /> Missy and Jane sang backup for Marguerite on one of her numbers, and it was a smash with the crowds (of course). I\u2019m glad that they\u2019re comfortable enough with people other than me to share the stage now; I think their progress over the last month has been amazing, and I couldn\u2019t be happier. The two of them also took center stage for a number of their own, an 80s crowd-pleaser called \u201cAlone\u201d by Heart. I think Julia might have had something to do with their selection, and she backed them up on the piano. It was <u><u>magical</u></u>.<br /> <br /> Of course there was additional drama at the show itself\u2026 was there ever any doubt? I noticed right away that V had stopped in for a visit. As he\u2019s our official liaison with the L.A. Night Court, I thought it would be best if I spoke with him early to see what he needed. Turns out that he just wanted to let us know that the Court of Fallen Stars have been up to their old tricks again. They destroyed a building in the Night Court\u2019s territory and tried to pin it on the Lady By the Sea, leaving evidence claiming that it was an act of retaliation for the violence visited upon our people in defense of Rowan and Neon.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt was clumsy work at best,\u201d V assured me softly, \u201cand none of us believed it. But we thought you should know\u2026 didn\u2019t want any further misunderstandings. Oh, and there\u2019s one more thing.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat\u2019s on your mind?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe\u2019ve made several overtures of alliance to the Courts of the Dragon, but they haven\u2019t been very receptive so far. They think we\u2019re chaotic and dangerous\u2026 and of course we are, but generally only to each other. We know that the Lady By the Sea has diplomatic relations with them, and we were hoping you could put in a good word for us\u2026 let the Directional Courts know that your alliance with us has worked out well for everyone.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cI can see the sense in that. If we\u2019re all united against Hollywood, that can only be a good thing. I don\u2019t have a lot of contact with the Courts of the Dragon personally, but I\u2019ll pass along the word to the other monarchs. I\u2019m sure they\u2019ll see the advantages of your suggestion.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks, Your Majesty,\u201d he said with a small smile and a nod. And that\u2019s when we had to cut our conversation short. Across the room, Trinh \u2013 who had been speaking quietly with Calamity \u2013 screamed and jumped out of her seat. Calamity salvaged the situation by assuring the other guests that Trinh was fine, and that she had just been surprised by something innocuous, but I could tell there was more at play, so I excused myself and made my way quickly to their table.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat\u2019s going on?\u201d I asked discreetly when I could.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou remember how Trinh was looking into that occult family that kept the fetuses in jars in their basement?\u201d Calamity asked. When I nodded, she continued. \u201cWell, there are three ghost children watching her now. I used a contract to spot them, and\u2026 accidentally let her see them too. It spooked her.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo, wait, there are ghosts here right now?\u201d I asked nervously.<br /> <br /> Calamity nodded. \u201cOne over there, one on top of that table in the corner, and one about two feet to your left.\u201d<br /> <br /> I took a step to the right. \u201cYou\u2019re going to handle this situation?\u201d I asked quietly.<br /> <br /> Calamity nodded. \u201cI\u2019m going to take Trinh to the Children\u2019s Library tonight; Madame Spidertoes will be able to protect her. That should at least give us time to come up with a long-term strategy.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded my agreement to her plan. \u201cOkay. Be careful, both of you.\u201d<br /> <br /> Once they\u2019d made their exit \u2013 having stopped off at the bar to get Trinh a fortifying drink first \u2013 I wandered over to the door and leaned heavily against my wife\u2019s shoulder. Her arm came up immediately and settled around my waist, drawing me in. \u201cYou need me tonight, babe?\u201d she asked, her brow wrinkling as she took in my demeanor.<br /> <br /> \u201cYes,\u201d I said gratefully. \u201cI\u2019m sorry if you had other plans, but\u2026 I really do. Everyone\u2019s been so good about talking me down and making sure I don\u2019t completely lose my shit over this situation, and they\u2019ve been doing a really good job, and I appreciate it. But now\u2026 I really need about twenty minutes with someone I trust so that I can completely lose my shit.\u201d<br /> <br /> D nodded. \u201cI get it,\u201d she said, completely without judgment, \u201cI\u2019m yours tonight, babe.\u201d<br /> <br /> And so my evening went. And you know what? After I\u2019d let myself freak out for a little while, and let D cradle me and soothe me, I actually did feel better. Don\u2019t get me wrong; I\u2019m still incredibly nervous about the procedure that lies ahead, but at least now I recognize that I don\u2019t have any other options. There\u2019s no one else in the Freehold who is as qualified for this task as me\u2026 aside from Anton and Andromeda, who are not going to be available for all of these surgeries. And when they <u><u>are</u></u> available, they\u2019ll be with me.<br /> <br /> I can do this.<br /> <br /> I <u><u>have</u></u> to do this.<br /> <br /> I promised Lindsay. I gave her my word, and she\u2019s trusting me with the most important thing in her life. I owe it to her to give this my best shot.<br /> <br /> So I made sure that D knew how much I love her and how much I appreciate the support she gives me, and then we both drifted off to sleep. I got up entirely too early this morning, showered, and drove into L.A. with Becky for my on-campus classes (which passed quietly and without incident today). At some point, Oleander sent me a packet of information on my phone, including the specific physiological data on the regions of the human brain which concern us and an audio file of the signal itself.<br /> <br /> By the time we got back to the Dream House, Sex Breakfast was nearly over. There had been a bit of excitement that morning, as Calamity picked Trinh up from the Children\u2019s Library \u2013 freshly warded against further ghostly interference \u2013 and brought her back to the Dream house to pick up her car. Luckily they thought to check the car before Trinh drove it home, and found that it was dangerously low on brake fluid. Like, there was enough to get her out of the parking lot and on to the Pacific Coast Highway, after which her brakes would certainly have failed. The brake lines weren\u2019t cut, and there were no leaks in the system itself\u2026 the fluid was just <u><u>gone</u></u>.<br /> <br /> Well, Calamity took Trinh to a local auto parts store and bought her some brake fluid to top off her tank, and all was well by the time I got back. All the talk about ghosts led Missy and Jane to ask for my opinion on something\u2026 they wanted to know if I thought it would be morbid for them to get their picture taken standing on their own graves. Honesty forced me to admit that it seemed in poor taste, which of course set Julia off like nothing else. To her somewhat odd aesthetic, that image seems like the height of romantic art.<br /> <br /> Julia had more to say as well, this time about Tanner. She\u2019d talked to the poor girl the previous afternoon and had learned some shocking details. Tanner doesn\u2019t remember much about her life before the Durance, but one of the few things that\u2019s come back to her is\u2026 that she killed a man. And it <u><u>wasn\u2019t</u></u> in self-defense. Putting that together with other things I\u2019ve heard her say, I think she might have been involved in a large-scale riot at some point.<br /> <br /> So I gave Tanner a call after breakfast just to check on her. She seemed a bit more together today, and apologized for falling apart in front of us yesterday. I assured her that no one would blame her for being a little confused when she had so recently returned to the world. I once again recommended the Winter Court\u2019s therapists, and also offered a more proactive way in which she might regain her past.<br /> <br /> I told her that Calamity was a talented dream healer, and that she would be happy to sift through Tanner\u2019s dreams and help her sort things out. Tanner sort of nervously asked if Calamity would <u><u>see</u></u> everything that Tanner dreamed about, and I told her that it was different for everyone (which is my understanding of how dream healing works; I have no first-hand knowledge of it). Some people see very straightforward visions of past events while with others it\u2019s more symbolic. Tanner said she\u2019d think about it, but didn\u2019t sound too enthused by the idea.<br /> <br /> She did say that she\u2019d like to see me again, though. Apparently her confusion over her sexuality didn\u2019t diminish her enjoyment of the act. So that\u2019s nice.<br /> <br /> So here I sit, searching the internet and all of my medical books and journals for any information I can find on the basic precepts of neurosurgery, or on the structure and function of the human brain itself. I figure the specific details of brain surgery won\u2019t be too useful to me, because as Maria pointed out, Anton\u2019s machine isn\u2019t like any surgical implement known to modern medicine. So instead I\u2019m trying to learn as much as I can about the different parts of the brain and how they function so that I\u2019ll know what to seek out and what to avoid. I figure this might also help if I need to use healing contracts to repair any\u2026 \u2018minor mishaps\u2019 that might crop up along the way.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a lot to know, and not much time to learn it. I don\u2019t intend to sleep before the procedure; all of my time will be devoted to study. Thank God for Spring contracts. And while we\u2019re at it\u2026 please, God, don\u2019t let me fuck this up.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei de la Rocha</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Apparently other people had a more interesting morning than I did. The most interesting thing that happened to me was when Tanner came downstairs for breakfast and asked the group if she looked gay. I wanted to reply that \u201cgay\u201d didn\u2019t have a look but figured that would be insensitive to her feelings. Thankfully Calamity picked right up on the fact that Tanner was having an internal crisis and started talking to her. Lori chose that moment to come back from a morning fly and settled right in to a hair brushing circle with Missy, Jane and others. Lori then asked Tanner how she was feeling, and our guest opened up a bit, saying that she was worried about the fact that she enjoyed gay sex. I gathered that last night was the first time that she had ever had sex with a woman before and she was unsure how to process that. Again, I let others field that issue. Trinh make breakfast this morning with Calamity\u2019s help. It was good. We saved some for Lori until she got back from her outing.<br /> <br /> After breakfast most of our guests left. Tanner went to the backstage area while the motley had a conversation. Lori broke the news that she had gotten a phone call from Twitch this morning about what\u2019s going on with Andromeda and Hailey. It seems that there are some sort of foreign particles in their skulls that are creating microscopic black holes in their brains and continually downloading the information on how to build the machine into the their heads. The same is happening to the rest of us exposed to those particles in the air, but our brains don\u2019t have the context or knowledge to be able to process the information so it\u2019s not really doing anything to us at the moment. The fear is that the signal might change and it could start downloading other information or directives into our heads. I was not happy to hear about this. Lori was even less happy about it because it seems that she will need to be the one to assist Twitch in removing the particles from people\u2019s brains. Actual brain surgery! Yeah, definitely not a fan of that, but I like the idea of being controlled or turned into one of those \u201czombies\u201d from the facility even less. And of course all of this is why Lori was quietly losing her shit earlier and needed to fly to calm down. I don\u2019t think she\u2019s up for brain surgery, despite how supportive Calamity was when we all talked. Calamity kept reassuring her that she would do fine because she is a chirurgeon and connected to the Wyrd. I guess before our motley meeting Lori already talked to Andromeda and Joan about what was going on and what needed to happen. I\u2019m not sure how that conversation went but my guess is that Andromeda took it better than Joan. I wonder if anyone has told Hailey yet?<br /> <br /> The afternoon passed without any more drama. Luna, Calamity and I helped Becky move some of her stuff into Calamity\u2019s room. I suppose that it is about time for her to start moving in. Her relationship with Calamity is pretty serious and they spend a lot of time together. It only makes sense. I think while we were doing that Julia talked to Tanner about the gay sex thing. Hopefully she will help our guest calm down about the whole thing.<br /> <br /> Later, at the show, things got interesting again. The show itself went great. Lori and Calamity wowed the crowd like always, and Missy and Jane backed up Insincere Marguerite on her number. They were all really good. I think Missy and Jane are becoming more and more comfortable with singing in front of the crowd. I know that they used to have to sing for the Violet Empress, but this is a bit different. Lots more people and less intensity from the crowd. After their numbers the ladies made their way through the crowd and Calamity stopped at Trinh\u2019s table. I\u2019m not sure what was said but after a few minutes of talking Trinh jumped back with a shout. She quickly calmed down and Calamity assured the audience that nothing was wrong. A little while later Calamity brought Trinh to the bar to get a drink and I found out what the exclamation was all about. It turns out that Trinh has been looking into a house that has ghost children present. The owners have jars of aborted or miscarried fetuses in the basement and they employ the ghosts of these children to do stuff for them. Talk about messed up. Seriously messed up. So, Trinh went to this house the other day, and today she felt like she was being followed. She asked Calamity to see if she could tell if anyone was following her. After looking for mundane stalkers and coming up empty Calamity tried a contract that allows her to see ghosts. This contract unfortunately also let Trinh see the three Chinese child ghosts that were surrounding her. She had a brief moment of panic and then Calamity brought her over to the bar to get a drink and calm down. It seems that the ghosts were interested in taking Calamity\u2019s eyes because she could see them, but they did nothing to actually try and do that. After a short while the ghosts left. I can see why Trinh needed the drink. I would be freaked out too if I knew that ghosts were following me all over the place.<br /> <br /> After the show was over Calamity escorted Trinh to the Children\u2019s Library so Madame Spidertoes could see to the ghosts that were following her. I stayed up until Calamity got home just to make sure that everything went alright. Angelica stayed up with me and we talked. This was the first time that I\u2019d really had a conversation with the claviger. We mostly made small talk about how long each of us has been in the Freehold and what having a monarch in the motley is like. I admitted that I think Lori keeps some things to herself when it comes to monarch business, but other than that it hasn\u2019t changed things all that much. We may be involved more closely in the things that are going on in the Freehold, but we\u2019d likely have been involved in them anyway. Calamity got back relatively quickly and said that Madame Spidertoes was going to make it harder for the ghosts to find Trinh. I\u2019m not sure how one goes about doing that but I\u2019m not doubting her abilities when it comes to ghosts. She knows more about that than I ever will.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Therapy went well this morning. I talked to Dr. Sullivan a little more about the raid on the Bulgarian facility. I told him about the exotic particles that are likely in my brain and he shared my concern about that. I told him that there was a way to get rid of them but it would require me to trust Twitch enough to do brain surgery on me. I suppose I would trust him more if Lori was there to keep him honest. I don\u2019t even know if I\u2019m going to need the surgery or not. I probably will though. We don\u2019t know what these particles might do in the future so it would make sense to remove them from everyone that was affected. I just don\u2019t know how many people that\u2019s going to be. At least Calamity, Dahlia, Insincere Marguerite, Twitch, Andromeda, Hailey and myself. I think that we were the only ones that went down to the lower level of the facility for any extended amount of time. I think that someone is working on a scanner to detect these particles so we should know soon enough who has them and who doesn\u2019t. After that we talked a bit about my lack of trust in Twitch. I told Sullivan that I still haven\u2019t forgiven him for what he did to Rook. It was torture plain and simple. He used various drugs and who knows what else on him until they broke him. Rook may have been after me at the time, but he was still like a brother to me. I can\u2019t forgive Twitch for what he did. Not now, maybe not ever.<br /> <br /> After therapy Calamity picked up Trinh from the Library and brought her back to the Dream House to pick up her car. Trinh asked Calamity to look over her car for her and my friend found that most of the brake fluid in the car was gone. There was enough to give the illusion of brakes for a short time, but not enough in the lines to do much else. They went to an auto parts place to get more and top it off. The working theory is that the ghosts from last night sabotaged her car in order to get rid of her. Scary stuff that. Ghosts can be invisible and intangible when they want but can become solid if they want to as well. That makes them extremely dangerous if they are after you, as evidenced by the brake fluid in Trinh\u2019s car.<br /> <br /> We discussed the ghosts over breakfast which led to conversation about Missy and Jane wanting to have a picture taken of them standing over their own graves. They wondered if that was morbid or disturbing. I thought it was kind of morbid but didn\u2019t say anything. They seemed so pleased with the idea and I didn\u2019t want to pop their little bubble of happiness. I think they wanted Julia to take a picture of them and then do a painting from the picture. It\u2019s all well and good but they\u2019d have to go back to Iowa to do the picture and hope that they didn\u2019t run into anyone that might recognize them. I think that would be the main danger in doing something like that. Then that conversation led to them asking what happened to the little piece of themselves that the Gentry used to make the fetches. They wanted to know if they would have gotten that back since their fetches were dead. De la Rocha said that the only way to get back that piece of yourself is to merge with your fetch. Otherwise that piece is just lost. It\u2019s kind of sad in a way. The Gentry take something from you that you can never get back. I mean they take your life away and change you into something else. Something that they want or need, and we can never go back to who we used to be. I guess that\u2019s just made all the more clear by the fact that we literally lose a piece of ourselves to the creation of the fake that takes our place. I suppose that there are a few lucky ones that never had a fetch so they don\u2019t have to worry about having lost a piece of themselves, but they were still changed against their will. The Lady didn\u2019t change me herself into a loyal servant, I suppose I changed myself, but it was due to the environment and situations that I found myself in. I\u2019d like to think that I wouldn\u2019t have become Rime if I hadn\u2019t been exposed to so much stress and danger. I guess I\u2019ll never know the answer to that one. I was Rime and I guess I just have to live with that and vow to never go back to that person again. Thankfully I have good friends and my Luna to keep me from backsliding. I don\u2019t know if my friends know just how much they have helped me. Just being understanding about my past has been a great relief. I don\u2019t know how I can pay them back other than just being there for them, so that\u2019s what I\u2019m going to do.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXXXI</i><br /> <br /> Just some ghost children. No big deal. I am sure it won\u2019t be a problem.<br /> <br /> I will note Twich said that with the side effects of the drug, Lori wouldn\u2019t necessarily get fixated on \u201canything after Ritual de lo Habitual\u201d so not the later Jane\u2019s Addiction stuff. This conversation is what happens when I ad lib. I had this random humorous thought of him saying the drug would make her like the Spin Doctors, but I make Spin Doctors references time to time and figured if I actually had him say something I would pick a different band. In the moment my brain picked Jane\u2019s Addiction. If something started playing in your head you are welcome.<br /> <br /> Also man this game is like 19<sup>th</sup> Century anti radio propaganda, innit?<br /> <br /> Anyway so there it is. Hope you are enjoying. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T19:26:30-07:00","id":1307103,"title":"","content":"It can\u2019t rain all the time<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXXXII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> As guilty as I know I\u2019m going to feel in a few hours\u2026 I think I really needed that.<br /> <br /> So after my last entry, Calamity headed over to the Lighthouse to make a formal report to Charlotte about the \u201cghost children\u201d issue. While I didn\u2019t get the whole story, I understand that the Directional Courts (like, as a whole) have some sort of contract with a Chinese family in L.A. preventing the Courts of the Dragon from acting directly in this matter. The mortal family has become a little uppity lately, and the Courts of the Dragon want us to de-claw them.<br /> <br /> Though they didn\u2019t share the specifics of their plans with me, I think Calamity and Marguerite are going to sneak into their house and try to find a copy of the original contract. Jacob isn\u2019t invited along this time, because the family also has some nebulous contract with the Winter Court which might cause problems for him if he inadvertently broke it by acting against them. I\u2019m not invited either, because\u2026 well, I suppose because I\u2019m a political figure now, and anything I do has to be viewed through a lens of how it reflects upon the Freehold as a whole. Consequently, I didn\u2019t ask for too many details, though I know that Calamity has consulted Madame Spidertoes on this matter in case she develops a case of the hauntin\u2019. How they\u2019re going to deal with the possibility of hopping vampires \u2013 a notion that predictably filled Jane with a species of giddy curiosity \u2013 I have no idea.<br /> <br /> It occurred to me that I needed to speak to Charlotte myself, so I sent her a quick text asking if I could meet with her briefly at the Lighthouse later that afternoon. She quickly texted me back, saying that she\u2019d be free in a couple of hours, and I promised to bring the coffee. A quick talk with Jacob later and I knew exactly how she likes her caffeinated beverages. It\u2019s nice to have a friend who\u2019s a bartender with a photographic memory. As I waited for the time to tick by, I read another couple of articles on neurosurgery to help prepare for the coming procedures.<br /> <br /> I walked into the Lighthouse at the appointed hour bearing two cups of steaming Starbucks. Both Trinh and Madame Spidertoes were there, and they seemed to be involved in some sort of back-and-forth flirtation, though Trinh was clearly a little nervous about the situation. When she asked to speak with me privately, I did what I could to alleviate her anxiety, though I did caution her to handle anything that might develop between her and Gladys with an extreme level of care. I don\u2019t think Madame Spidertoes would intentionally do anything to hurt Trinh\u2026 but she\u2019s so alien and unearthly at times that it\u2019s hard to tell how she\u2019ll react to just about anything. More on that in a bit.<br /> <br /> Charlotte received me graciously, and thanked me for the coffee. Once we\u2019d passed a few pleasantries, I brought up the matter of the Diurnal and Directional Courts in L.A. Charlotte has more extensive contact with the Courts of the Dragon than any of the other monarchs, and I tend to be our local point of contact with the Courts of Fallen Angels, so it seemed logical that the task of forging a truce between those entities would fall to us. I told her about V\u2019s visit on the previous evening, and mentioned how well our own alliance with the Night and Day Courts seemed to be working out. Finally, I brought up my opinion that having all of the other local courts presenting a united front against the Court of Fallen Stars could only be a good thing.<br /> <br /> \u201cI agree with you, Lori,\u201d she said after a moment\u2019s consideration, \u201cand I\u2019ll do what I can to present your case to the Courts of the Dragon. The South and East Courts probably won\u2019t take too much convincing, but the North and West Courts will be a harder sell.\u201d I thought about the bubbly and effusive Laughing Carp, and then compared that mental image with Soon-Hee Kwon, my beautiful dragon lover\u2026 and privately agreed with my co-monarch\u2019s assessment.<br /> <br /> Still, Charlotte agreed that it would be best if our various allies weren\u2019t sniping at each other or constantly watching their backs for signs of betrayal while the true enemy sat back and laughed, so she agreed to see what she could do. I thanked her profusely and made my way out of the Lighthouse.<br /> <br /> On my way out, I came across Madame Spidertoes, who looked bemused and maybe a little shocked. \u201cI fear that I have upset Trinh,\u201d she said when I asked her what was wrong.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat happened?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cI merely told her that she was the most beautiful colored girl I had ever seen,\u201d she replied.<br /> <br /> I managed to stop myself from visibly wincing, which may be the high point of my acting career to date. \u201cGladys,\u201d I said as kindly as I could, \u201cI know you didn\u2019t mean to upset her, but people of color \u2013 African Americans \u2013 don\u2019t like to be called that these days. It reminds them of a time not too long ago when they were treated as less than human. It\u2019s considered very rude.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh dear,\u201d she said, composed as always but obviously chagrinned beneath the surface. \u201cI did not mean to insult her\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know,\u201d I replied. \u201cI\u2019ll talk to her and try to calm her down. I\u2019ll let her know that it wasn\u2019t intentional.\u201d<br /> <br /> She smiled that always-unsettling smile at me. \u201cThank you, my dear,\u201d she said, patting my hand affectionately. \u201cAnd do give Maria my love, please.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course,\u201d I promised.<br /> <br /> Trinh was hanging out in the parking lot when I walked out, sort of caught between fuming and shaking. \u201cShe can\u2019t call me that,\u201d she said as I approached. \u201c<u><u>Nobody</u></u> can call me that\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know, sweetie,\u201d I said soothingly. \u201cIt was a terrible mistake, and I\u2019m so sorry you had to be on the receiving end. You have every right to be upset, but I\u2019d like to ask you to take a step back and try to see things from an outside perspective, if you can. Madame Spidertoes is old\u2026 I know she doesn\u2019t look it, but I think she\u2019s <u><u>centuries</u></u> old. There\u2019s so much history in her mind, and I don\u2019t think she always lives in the here and now. You know how memory can be, how a sight or sound or smell can take you back to another time. Well, you have to remember that she lived through whole decades where that was the most polite way to describe African Americans\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Trinh sighed and shook her head. \u201cI guess I can see that,\u201d she admitted grudgingly.<br /> <br /> \u201cI swear to you, she didn\u2019t mean to offend you. I explained why what she had said upset you, and her surprise was genuine. But she\u2019s also incredibly smart, so I don\u2019t think she\u2019ll make that mistake again. So I\u2019m asking you to give her another chance.\u201d<br /> <br /> Trinh took a deep breath. \u201cOkay,\u201d she said at last. Then we talked about the possibility of her performing at the Dream House some time soon. After we\u2019d exhausted the possibilities of that topic of conversation, we flirted for a while and I might have kinda-sorta set the wheels in motion for the two of us to have sex at some point. What? She\u2019s hot as hell, and it seems like Jane has maybe started to get over her homicidal dislike of Trinh, so sue me.<br /> <br /> So I drove myself home and read some more articles on the structure and function of the various parts of the human brain until it was time to get ready for the show. As I was heading downstairs, I came across Julia, and each of us said we needed to talk to the other at the same time. My own reasons were kind of selfish, I admit\u2026 I wanted to ask her if she\u2019d sing for me again once Halley and Andromeda\u2019s surgeries were done. I\u2019ve been so damn <u><u>tense</u></u> lately that I could really use something to take the edge off. Of course, kind and giving lover that she is, she agreed immediately.<br /> <br /> Julia\u2019s topic actually surprised me a bit. She wanted to ask if I was okay with her and Marguerite spending so much time with Missy and Jane. I admit that after her initial clashes with Jane, I was taken a little off-guard by how well those four seem to get along, and I\u2019d be lying if I said that it didn\u2019t make me the <u><u>teensiest</u></u> bit jealous from time to time\u2026 but no. I love all four of them. Missy and Jane are my best friends, my sisters, and my lovers. Julia and Marguerite are all of that as well as my brides. If the four of them get along really well, why should I object? As long as they all agree to share each other with me from time to time, of course.<br /> <br /> So show time rolled around as usual, as has become my custom these days, I sang and danced backup for a few numbers but only did one solo act myself so that I\u2019d have time to circulate amongst my people. \u201c\u2026Baby One More Time\u201d was an early effort by pop sensation Britney Spears, and while it\u2019ll never be considered a classic of American music, it\u2019s catchy as fuck, and it goes well with my look and my style. It went over really well in any case, and I\u2019m sure I\u2019ll get plenty of requests to perform it again in the future.<br /> <br /> Calamity and Marguerite wowed the crowds as always, of course, though I\u2019m convinced that Calamity\u2019s new act was calculated specifically to enrage me. She performed a parody song by Weird Al Yankovic called \u201cLike a Surgeon,\u201d which of course plucked the strings of my anxiety like Eric Clapton at a Saturday night jam session. I know she didn\u2019t do it to upset me, but this mischievous side of hers is getting out of hand. I should probably talk with her about that soon. Marguerite, on the other hand, brought Trinh onto the stage to assist with her act, setting in motion Trinh\u2019s stage debut and echoing the conversation the two of us had earlier at the Lighthouse. She got a taste of the glamour that performing at our little cabaret can provide, and hopefully she\u2019ll want more and sign on as a regular performer soon.<br /> <br /> After leaving the stage, I stopped by the bar first to speak with Halley. I wanted to reassure her that I wouldn\u2019t let anything happen to her, that I had my shit together and that Anton and I knew exactly what we were doing. Ironically, I think she ended up offering me more comfort than I offered her. She told me that she trusted me, that she was confident in my abilities, and that she knew I had her best interests at heart. She even apologized at one point for bad-mouthing Andromeda. It\u2019s clear that she still loathes Rebecca, but she knows that the other alien girl and I are close, and she doesn\u2019t want to disparage my friends in front of me.<br /> <br /> My next stop was at Tanner and Monica\u2019s table. Tanner seemed a little more stable; I think she\u2019s starting to deal with what happened between us. I still feel like shit about that; I have got to learn to start thinking with my head rather than my\u2026 y\u2019know what, I\u2019m gonna go with \u201cheart\u201d and leave it at that. Monica favored me with a mildly disapproving look as I joined them at the table\u2026 not like she was mad at me or anything, but more of a \u201cyou really should have known better\u201d sort of look. Still, the three of us had a pleasant conversation about how Tanner is settling in, and I think she\u2019ll be okay given a little more time to\u2026 consider her situation. Calamity renewed her offer to assist with dream therapy, and the Winter Court\u2019s therapists were brought up once more.<br /> <br /> Once I\u2019d passed a few words with just about everyone, I made my way up to the Girlfriend Table and took a seat next to Gloria. \u201cHey Lori,\u201d she said a little disconsolately, \u201chow are you holding up?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI won\u2019t lie, I\u2019m stressing pretty bad,\u201d I admitted, \u201cbut what\u2019s up with you, honey? You seem a little down\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s nothing,\u201d she asserted, but then continued. \u201cHollywood is still insisting that I killed my motley. Siobhan asked Lowjack to consider extraditing me again.\u201d<br /> <br /> I took her hand. \u201cI\u2019m so sorry, sweetie,\u201d I said as kindly as I could. \u201cYou know I won\u2019t let that happen, right? This queen gig has to be good for something\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Gloria smiled. \u201cLowjack already told me I had nothing to worry about. The whole situation just has me down, I guess. But don\u2019t worry about me, Lori\u2026 you\u2019ve got enough on your plate already. How can I help? Would a backrub help?\u201d<br /> <br /> I sighed. \u201cIt probably would,\u201d I admitted, \u201cbut I shouldn\u2019t take the time away from my studies. I need to cram as much expertise into my skull as I possibly can before crunch time\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> She leaned in and gave me a soft, gentle kiss. \u201cJust think about it, okay? I\u2019ll be here if you need me\u2026 if you want me here.\u201d<br /> <br /> I had to smile at how shy she can still be from time to time. \u201cAlways,\u201d I assured her.<br /> <br /> Maria joined us as the crowds thinned, and the three of us fell into an easy conversation. I bitched and moaned some more about what I was being asked to do and about how many responsibilities have been heaped upon me since I took up the Spring Crown. For the most part, the two of them took it with good grace.<br /> <br /> Maria took my hand at one point. \u201cLook, babe,\u201d she said, \u201cif it makes you feel any better, I\u2019m pretty sure you\u2019d be doing this surgery even if you <u><u>weren\u2019t</u></u> the Spring Queen.\u201d<br /> <br /> And you know what? It <u><u>did</u></u> make me feel better. She\u2019s right. Anton didn\u2019t ask me to assist him because I\u2019m the queen and it\u2019s my responsibility to protect my citizens. He asked me because I\u2019m the best person for the job. He would have asked me even if I hadn\u2019t agreed to take up the monarchy. Yes, it\u2019s a lot of responsibility, and the price if I fail is way too high\u2026 but I can\u2019t turn my back on Andromeda, Halley, and the others who need the gifts the Wyrd has given me. I can continue to obsess over how nervous that makes me, or I can put it behind me and do what needs to be done.<br /> <br /> Once the last of the guests had left, the three of us retired to our bedroom. I\u2019ve said it before, and I\u2019ll say it again\u2026 Gloria has magic hands. She worked the knots out of my back and turned me into a quivering pile of boneless flesh. Oh, and the sex that followed was nice too.<br /> <br /> What? I realized at some point that the last three articles I\u2019d read all contained essentially the same information, so it seemed pointless to continue to spend every moment studying. A nice evening of \u2018distractions\u2019 surrounded by girls who love me, followed by a few hours of real sleep\u2026 it probably did me more good than continuing to cram for the rest of the evening would have anyway.<br /> <br /> So now I\u2019m sitting around writing in this diary and getting ready to do my online work for college. I expect Anton will give me a call sometime today to tell me that his machine is ready. And when that call comes, I will not be a nervous wreck. I owe it to my patients to be calm, confident, and to radiate an aura of assurance. I will do my best to assist Dr. Twichowicz and make sure that my people are safe from the alien radio signals.<br /> <br /> I just pray that my best is enough.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei de la Rocha</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> And just when I thought the weirdness was over. Calamity went to the Lighthouse to talk to Queen Charlotte about what\u2019s been going on with Trinh and discovered a whole bunch of stuff. Apparently there is a really rich, really old Chinese family in the area named Xiaohou and they have some dirty secrets in their basement. Literally. They have jars and containers and vases all containing the fetuses of aborted or miscarried children in their basement. Some are so old they just have a name and a date attached to them. They then somehow summon the ghosts of these children to do their bidding, but the ghosts appear as 8 or 9-year-old children. The family also has a \u201chopping vampire\u201d in their house. Apparently, it is a type of vampire that is squatting down and has a paper charm on its head that keeps it immobile. If the charm is removed it hops up and attacks. I guess that\u2019s one way to protect your house. I guess I would prefer the old-fashioned way and get a dog or install a security system. Dogs rarely turn on their owners for example. I don\u2019t know if hopping vampires distinguish friend from foe or not and I don\u2019t really want to find out to be honest.<br /> <br /> So, this Xiaohou family has two women that can do the blood magic to control the ghost children. It seems to be a matrilineal kind of gift. I guess that makes sense. It is dealing with the ghosts of children. This family also has ancient contracts in place with the Directional courts and the Winter court so no one from any of those groups can do anything directly against the family. I guess that\u2019s why the Autumn court got involved. They deal with the creepy stuff and don\u2019t have to worry about any old contracts getting in the way of them investigating the family or its practices. It also turns out that the new people in charge of the family are somewhat disrespectful of the old ways and of the Directional courts in general. They used to pay tribute in the form of glamour to the Directional courts, but they don\u2019t even do that anymore.<br /> <br /> Calamity\u2019s current mission is to go to the Xiaohou house in a few days after the ghosts are not so riled up and look for copies of the contracts between the Directional and Winter courts and the family. Queen Charlotte suggested taking pictures of the documents or somehow making copies of them so we can look over the fine print and look for loopholes. If Changelings are good at one thing it\u2019s creating contracts that benefit themselves in some way. This could be in the form of a loophole or something that the family is supposed to do for us. The Directional courts don\u2019t have any copies of the old contracts here in the Unites States. They might have copies in China, but we don\u2019t have easy access to those documents and we can\u2019t really contact anyone over there to get copies.<br /> <br /> When Calamity got back from the Lighthouse she told everyone in the motley about all of this stuff. De la Rocha then suggested that we talk to White Maria about the Chinese mysticism side of things. She might have an idea of how the ladies control the ghosts and why they appear as young children instead of fetuses. I thought it sounded like a sound plan. I think Calamity was going to be the one to talk to White Maria. If it didn\u2019t happen after the show Calamity could talk to her tomorrow morning when she goes to work on her meditation. Made sense to me. After that the afternoon went by pretty quickly. I watched some Netflix with Luna and we just enjoyed each other\u2019s company.<br /> <br /> Pretty soon it was time for the show. Calamity did a song called \u201cLike a Surgeon\u201d for her act, which made Lori get annoyed for a bit. The song is a parody of Madonna\u2019s \u201cLike a Virgin\u201d done by Weird Al. I thought it was funny but see how it could be taken to be in poor taste by our Spring Queen who has to perform surgery in the next day or so and is more than just a little freaked out by the prospect. For the most part though I paid attention to what things people were doing at the bar. TJ and Molly were having a contest to see who could make the taller stack of random objects, and Calamity came over to watch. They were using empty peanut bowls, plastic cups and TJ even had a car headlight in his. I\u2019m not sure where he got the headlight and I wasn\u2019t going to ask, but he had one. The conversation between those two got weird after a while. TJ claimed to be Jewish at one point but said that he wasn\u2019t Kosher. Then the conversation turned to who would even eat TJ and if it would be considered cannibalism. Then the Donner party came up and that whole thing had to be explained to Molly who hadn\u2019t learned about that yet. Then Lori came over to the bar to talk to Hailey about the upcoming surgery. Hailey had been told by someone what was going on and told my motley mate that she had the utmost confidence in her abilities. I\u2019m not sure if this boosted Lori\u2019s feelings regarding the upcoming surgery or not. I think it did a little though. After a little while Calamity and Lori left the bar to make their rounds. I\u2019m not sure what they talked about, but the conversations seemed to go well for both of them. Overall it was a very weird and interesting evening.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXXXII</i><br /> <br /> Insincere Marguerite, keeping with her Bowie kick, did \u201cHeart\u2019s Filthy Lesson.\u201d And I kinda think that \u201c\u2026Baby One More Time\u201d will, like it or not, be a classic. I could ramble on, but that is not what you are here for.<br /> <br /> There was also a whole thing about Maria\u2019s quinceanera, but it will be covered next time.<br /> <br /> Next time Brain Surgery and Chinese Demons. See you then! Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T00:33:28-07:00","id":1310493,"title":"","content":"Lorelei begins brain surgery. Calamity finds herself conducting some supernatural espionage.<br /> <br /> Note Jacob\u2019s player had to miss, so he is absent this time. It is presumed he was in the hold as normal.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXXIV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> So the last twenty-four hours have done a lot to both ease my existing worries and add several new ones to the pile. While I\u2019m a bit more confident that Anton and I can perform the necessary procedures to rid our friends of the alien particles\u2019 influence\u2026 I\u2019m concerned about how the stress of these surgeries is affecting one of my lovers. Oh well\u2026 whatever else one might say about living in the Lady by the Sea freehold, it certainly isn\u2019t boring.<br /> <br /> I was nervously going through my online classes on Friday morning, sort of dreading the inevitable call from Anton. Sure enough, he contacted me at about 10:30, and I paused the video lecture I\u2019d been watching and greeted him as warmly as I could. He was satisfied that his machinery was up to the task at hand, and asked me if I could come by that afternoon to get some practice in and meet with our patients. I pushed down the nervous flutter that started up in my stomach and told him that I\u2019d drop by after Sex Breakfast.<br /> <br /> It was a little difficult to focus on classes again with that looming over me, but somehow I managed to muddle through, even though I know I didn\u2019t submit my best work. Sex Breakfast provided other distractions, as Missy recruited me into protecting her from Jane and the Oldacres, who had apparently ganged up on her during the previous evening\u2019s festivities and tickled her mercilessly. She fervently declared everything within arm\u2019s reach of her a \u201ctickle-free zone.\u201d I figured she could use my support, so I slipped up behind her, encircled her waist with my arms, and cupped my wings protectively around the two of us.<br /> <br /> It ended badly, of course, with Calamity sneaking up behind us and tickling us <u><u>both</u></u>, but it did serve to remind me of how very much I care about Missy and Jane. We made tentative plans for all six of us to spend that evening together, and I left for the Clinic feeling marginally more positive about the day\u2019s direction. Maria came with me to provide moral support (both to me and to Anton, I think). I was glad she was there, though it did end up causing certain\u2026 complications.<br /> <br /> So the first thing I noticed when I reached Anton\u2019s lab was Dr. Bright\u2026 twitching and stammering in a corner. Apparently he had insisted on being present for the procedure, and Oleander objected to his tone. She tased him. I can\u2019t even begin to relate how shocked I was when I heard about that. She seemed really tense and on edge when I talked with her about it, and I remembered hearing her say that she hadn\u2019t been getting much sleep lately. She\u2019s got so much on her plate already\u2026 I know that dealing with the fallout of the Bulgarian facility is important, but it was wrong of us to add to her burdens in this way.<br /> <br /> In any case, Dr. Bright did decide to leave us to our own devices once he was steady enough on his feet, and Anton showed me his new surgical machine. It\u2019s <u><u>amazing</u></u>. It\u2019s a sort of x-ray viewer coupled with a pair of tiny robotic arms which are slaved to much larger arms, which in turn are operated by the surgeon. Anton showed me how to equip and activate the device, and Halley was good enough to let me get acclimated to its use by offering her head for practice (we didn\u2019t engage the surgical arms at this point; we just tested the x-ray and calibrated the systems).<br /> <br /> It was remarkably intuitive, though I\u2019m not sure if that was something endemic to the machine or if it had more to do with my own chirurgeon proclivities. Whatever the reason, using the device was <u><u>easy</u></u>.<br /> <br /> Anton asked when I\u2019d be ready to proceed. \u201cNo time like the present,\u201d I said with a nervous laugh.<br /> <br /> Anton thought about that for a minute. \u201cOkay,\u201d he said cautiously, \u201cbut we should probably schedule the procedures at least a day apart. I\u2019d like each of us to get a full night\u2019s sleep between the surgeries. These procedures are going to be exhausting in more than just the physical sense.\u201d<br /> <br /> I saw the sense in that. It only left the question of who should go first. Both Halley and Andromeda volunteered, but in the end we decided to go with Halley. Her rationale for wanting to go first was a little upsetting, though.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou can practice on me; nobody will care if I die,\u201d she said matter-of-factly.<br /> <br /> Andromeda pursed her lips at this, but held her silence.<br /> <br /> \u201cHalley,\u201d I said seriously, \u201c<u><u>nobody</u></u> is expendable here. I don\u2019t want you to think that way. All of you are going to make it through this, I promise.\u201d<br /> <br /> After I managed to convince Andromeda to go home, my wife approached me and asked if I\u2019d like her to use her changeling gifts to bless my endeavors. She was almost shy about it\u2026 it\u2019s not something she usually does, but when the need arises she can use contracts to grant good fortune to certain specific tasks. I gratefully accepted any help she could give me, and she worked her magic, and I immediately felt a lot more confident about the whole situation.<br /> <br /> Then Anton and I got to work. The operation itself took less time than I thought it would. Working together and spotting for each other, Anton and I systematically worked our way through the various parts of Halley\u2019s brain and excised the foreign particles. And you know what? It wasn\u2019t that hard. I mean, it was intense, and I had to take care not to miss anything, but it was like I got into a sort of groove while I was concentrating on the work, and things just sort of fell into place for me. I guess Calamity and the others are right\u2026 this is the sort of work I was born to do.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d bet dollars to donuts that we got one hundred percent of that black hole crap out of Halley\u2019s head, and as soon as Calamity excises the remaining memories of the device via dream therapy, I\u2019m confident that we\u2019ll be able to put this whole sorry business behind us.<br /> <br /> I stepped out into the hallway to call Andromeda after we\u2019d concluded the procedure. I wanted both to assure her that Halley was alright, and to let her and Joan know that we had things well in hand and would be ready to complete her own procedure the following morning. I was not prepared for what I saw when I stepped back into the lab.<br /> <br /> \u201cDo you have any idea how crazy you sound?\u201d Oleander snapped at Anton.<br /> <br /> \u201cBack off, bitch,\u201d Maria roared, placing herself between the two of them. \u201cYou do not get to talk to him like that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat did you call me?\u201d Oleander asked. Her eyes narrowed, and her hand strayed toward her taser.<br /> <br /> \u201cTry it,\u201d Maria said softly. \u201c<u><u>Please</u></u> try it\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMaria! Oleander!\u201d I said as imperiously as I could. \u201cStop it, both of you. What\u2019s going on here?\u201d<br /> <br /> They all three turned to look at me (Anton looked half-terrified), and there was silence for a moment. Oleander spoke first. \u201cThe particles you two removed from Halley\u2019s brain,\u201d she said tightly, \u201cDr. Twichowicz wants to <u><u>keep</u></u> them. In a <u><u>jar</u></u>.\u201d<br /> <br /> I looked over at Anton, who shrugged. \u201cI don\u2019t want to use them,\u201d he said defensively, \u201cI want to study them. I\u2019m not really sure how we\u2019d dispose of them anyway, and I thought it would be better to keep them where they could be observed than to throw them away somewhere and have to worry about them later.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded at that. \u201cOkay, Anton, I see the sense in that. Keep them for now. I\u2019ll consult with the other monarchs and let you know what we decide. Maria, please give me a moment and then we can go. Oleander\u2026 I\u2019d like a word.\u201d<br /> <br /> The two of us walked out into the hall for some privacy. I\u2019ve\u2026 never seen her like that before. She hid it well, but her hands were shaking as we talked. It was obvious that she was still furious. \u201cShe threatened me. She can\u2019t do that\u2026\u201d she muttered almost to herself.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sorry about that,\u201d I said in what I hoped was a soothing tone. \u201cYou know how Maria gets when someone she cares about is threatened or disparaged\u2026 she\u2019s really invested in Anton\u2019s recovery.\u201d<br /> <br /> She glowered for another minute or so, and then sighed. \u201cI know,\u201d she said after a moment. \u201cAnd she\u2019s been good for Dr. Twichowicz. But this issue is too important to use kid gloves. We can\u2019t leave something that dangerous in the hands of\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cImelda,\u201d I said, taking her hands in mine, \u201cyou have to have a little faith. Trust him\u2026 or at least trust me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI do,\u201d she said. \u201cYou\u2019re pretty much the only person I really trust. I\u2026 I didn\u2019t even know that was <u><u>possible</u></u> for me\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThen trust me now,\u201d I soothed. \u201cI\u2019ll take care of this, honey. Why don\u2019t you go home, take the rest of the day off, relax, and get some sleep, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> She put up a token resistance, but in the end she agreed. I walked her out, and then wandered the building for a while in search of my wife. I found her when I noticed a couple of scared-looking nurses peeping into a side room, and heard the screeches and groans of distressed metal. D was in the room twisting the legs of a table into intricate pretzel shapes.<br /> <br /> I was absurdly reminded of the pictures Julia dug up a couple of days ago\u2026 something Maria\u2019s parents or brother had posted online. My love as a fifteen-year-old girl at her quinceanera\u2026 purple dress, long black hair brushed over one shoulder, a smile that showed both her perfect teeth and the cutest dimples I\u2019ve ever seen. It was a far cry from the seething bundle of rage I saw at that moment. And God I love them both.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou okay, sweetie?\u201d I asked as I approached and put my arms around her. My word, but her muscles are impressive.<br /> <br /> \u201cNever better,\u201d she said with false nonchalance. I could feel that she was still tense.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019s under a lot of pressure,\u201d I said softly.<br /> <br /> \u201cDoesn\u2019t give her the right to talk to Anton like that,\u201d D retorted venomously\u2026 but I knew her anger wasn\u2019t for me. \u201cShe as good as called him crazy, Lori. You know what that can do to someone like Anton? You know how much progress that can wipe out in just a few seconds?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnton\u2019s fine,\u201d I said soothingly. \u201cHe\u2019s got you to prop him up when he starts to backslide. And he\u2019s got me, too. But Oleander\u2026 she didn\u2019t mean it that way. I think she\u2019s just tired and stressed.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDoesn\u2019t make it okay,\u201d my love spat again.<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course it doesn\u2019t,\u201d I replied, \u201cbut it maybe makes it a little more understandable. Give her a break, okay? For me?\u201d<br /> <br /> D nodded, but I could tell she wasn\u2019t quite ready to let it go. \u201cYou want to head home?\u201d she asked to mask her irritation.<br /> <br /> \u201cSure,\u201d I said. \u201cYou drive, though\u2026 I need to call John.\u201d<br /> <br /> So we slipped out past the terrified nursing staff and made our way to the parking lot. John answered on the second ring, and for once I got to tell him that I was calling with <u><u>good</u></u> news. \u201cThe first surgery is done,\u201d I said with a sigh. \u201cHalley\u2019s now officially black-hole-particle-free.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s great news, Lori,\u201d he said with as much enthusiasm as he ever gives anything.<br /> <br /> \u201cThere is something we should probably discuss,\u201d I said after a moment. \u201cAnton has the particles we extracted contained for now, but he and Oleander got into an argument about how we should proceed. She thinks we need to dispose of them utterly, and I agree with her in theory\u2026 but Anton raised some very valid points. We don\u2019t know <u><u>how</u></u> to permanently dispose of this stuff, and if we seal it away somewhere it might become a big problem for the future. Anton feels that we should keep the particles on hand so that they can be observed and studied.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHmmm,\u201d John said as he pondered, \u201cI see the sense in both points of view. Look, I don\u2019t claim to be an expert when it comes to particle physics, so I don\u2019t really feel qualified to make an absolute ruling on this matter. My suggestion would be that each of the four monarchs appoint two members of their court to an advisory panel. The eight of them could then discuss the matter and come up with the best resolution. How does that sound?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSounds good to me,\u201d I replied, immediately thinking that Andromeda would be a shoe-in for one of the Spring Court\u2019s seats. Still not sure about the other advisor, though.<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay, I\u2019ll pitch it to Augustine and Charlotte,\u201d John continued. \u201cI don\u2019t anticipate much resistance to the idea.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThere\u2019s more,\u201d I said after a moment.<br /> <br /> There was a pause on the other end of the line. \u201cIs this about why Dr. Bright was subjected to a taser attack this afternoon?\u201d he asked drily after a moment.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah,\u201d I said. \u201cLook, John\u2026 I\u2019m worried about Oleander. She and Maria almost came to blows after the procedure, and combined with the taser incident\u2026 it isn\u2019t like her.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI agree,\u201d John said. \u201cI\u2019ve never seen her act impulsively before\u2026 except where you\u2019re concerned. This is\u2026 a disturbing trend.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI hope it\u2019s just stress and overwork,\u201d I said, \u201cbut even if that is the case\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe can\u2019t afford to have her go off the rails right now,\u201d John finished my sentence. \u201cI agree. And I\u2019m not insensitive to your feelings for her either, Lori. My recommendation is that she leave the rest of the surgeries to you, Anton, and Andromeda, once she\u2019s clear of the infection. Let Oleander focus on her other project and get some rest in the meantime.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAgreed,\u201d I said, \u201cbut let me tell her. She\u2026 she\u2019ll probably take it better coming from me.\u201d<br /> <br /> John agreed, and the conversation kind of wound down after that. D drove us home, at which point we separated with a kiss. She headed for the basement to knock the shit out of a few punching bags, and I pulled back onto the highway and made my way to Oleander\u2019s place.<br /> <br /> She looked tired as she answered the door. \u201cAngel,\u201d she said with a watery grin, \u201cnot that I\u2019m complaining, but to what do I owe the pleasure?\u201d<br /> <br /> I sighed, stepped inside, and pulled her into a hug and a kiss. \u201cI wanted to talk to you about what happened at the clinic, honey,\u201d I said with resignation.<br /> <br /> It\u2026 wasn\u2019t a fun conversation. My love doesn\u2019t like being sidelined, especially when she feels that she has valuable expertise to contribute to an important problem. I heard a lot about how she was the most qualified person in the Freehold to oversee the extraction of the particles, and how their ultimate dispensation was too important to be decided in committee. Then she asked me something that completely floored me.<br /> <br /> \u201cAre you ordering me to step away as my Queen,\u201d she asked, \u201cor are you asking me as my girlfriend?\u201d<br /> <br /> It stung, and I let that show a little bit as I answered her. \u201cAsking,\u201d I said softly, \u201c<u><u>always</u></u> asking, sweetheart. I love you, and I\u2019m worried about you. Okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> She closed her eyes. \u201cOkay,\u201d she said. \u201cI trust you, Lori. I\u2026 I never really thought I could have that with anyone. But I trust you. I\u2019ll leave the surgeries to you and Twichowicz.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you,\u201d I said fervently, pulling her into another embrace.<br /> <br /> \u201cBut I want an apology from de la Rocha,\u201d she said firmly as we disengaged. \u201cI\u2019m not making that a condition of my agreement, but\u2026 I want an apology. I don\u2019t think we can stay friends if I don\u2019t get one.\u201d<br /> <br /> I frowned at that. \u201cI\u2019ll\u2026 I\u2019ll ask her,\u201d I said timidly. \u201cYou know how proud she is, but\u2026 I\u2019ll pass it along.\u201d<br /> <br /> We made plans for her to attend the show on the following evening, and for us to spend the night together afterward. After that\u2026 she asked me to leave. I\u2026 I don\u2019t think she\u2019s ever actually <u><u>asked</u></u> me to leave her alone before. It was\u2026 not much fun, and it didn\u2019t make for a very fun drive home.<br /> <br /> D was still in the basement when I got home, but she wasn\u2019t punching the bag\u2026 she and Jane were actually talking, and it seemed like Jane was helping her work some things out. It warmed my heart to see it\u2026 especially after the way the two of them clashed when we first brought my best gal-pals out of Arcadia.<br /> <br /> I relayed Oleander\u2019s request, and it went over about as well as you might think it would. D\u2019s adamant that if anything, she\u2019s owed the apology, and she\u2019s not willing to bend even a little bit on that point. I\u2019m hoping at some point cooler heads will prevail and I can get the two of them to patch things up\u2026 but even I\u2019ll admit that it seems like kind of a longshot at the moment.<br /> <br /> I had to boogie to get ready for our Friday night show after that. Weekend shows are always big, so we all did our best to bring our A-games to the stage. Calamity and Marguerite teamed up to sing \u201cUnder Pressure,\u201d which is both one of my favorite Bowie songs and one of my favorite Queen songs. They gave a marvelous performance, and despite Marguerite\u2019s misgivings about Calamity\u2019s ability to sing like an Iranian, I think she did a fine job (even though I\u2019m pretty sure Freddie Mercury was born and raised in Zanzibar).<br /> <br /> I performed two numbers myself. First, Missy and Jane backed me up on Madonna\u2019s \u201cLike a Prayer.\u201d I\u2019ve wanted to perform that one for a while, but it never felt right until I had the two of them to support me. I gave each of them one of my old choir robes to wear, which gave the whole number a nice pseudo-religious feel. Me? Well, my dress was as spangly and abbreviated as ever, naturally. The crowd ate it up, and as always when those two are supporting me, I felt like I was able to reach new heights.<br /> <br /> I also did a smaller, more sedate number near the end of the show. One of my favorite songs by Pink Floyd has always been \u201cBrain Damage,\u201d from their seminal <u><u>Dark Side of the Moon</u></u> album. I\u2019d been looking for an opportunity to sing it for a while now, but wanted to wait for a rare show in which our audience didn\u2019t contain Halley, as I thought it might be sort of triggery for her. As she was resting following her surgery last night, it seemed an opportune time to indulge myself. Without the girls backing me up it didn\u2019t go over quite as well as the Madonna song did, but I enjoyed it, so I\u2019ll call it a success.<br /> <br /> We had a couple of guests who stood out among the crowds. One table housed Rosalita and Tara, our Night Courtier friends from L. A. They had come by to take in the show, and apparently had some sort of romantic arrangement for the evening. Tara seemed to have settled into a subservient role for the time being, and was doing everything Rosalita told her to do meekly and without question. Rosalita wasn\u2019t above using this to her advantage, either\u2026 sending the poor girl off to fetch us drinks and ordering her under the table to give me a foot-rub.<br /> <br /> Eventually I sauntered off to speak with the other guests. Desiree and Veronica were there, and the three of us chatted for a while. Though I\u2019m sure Desiree still has her doubts about Veronica, she\u2019s always been damned good at hiding her emotions, and I don\u2019t think Veronica suspects anything as of yet. For the most part we didn\u2019t discuss anything particularly important\u2026 though it did come up that the third member of that little romantic triangle, Jolie, was rumored to be spending the evening with one Queen Charlotte\u2026<br /> <br /> In any case, after things settled down I joined Maria, Marguerite, Julia, Missy and Jane at the girlfriend table. (Jesus, I just realized that if I go by my birth name every single member of that sextet starts with an M or a J. What are the odds?). In any case, once the house was clear and secured, the six of us drifted upstairs for an evening of giggles and orgasms. It was nice. It felt\u2026 <u><u>right</u></u> for the six of us to be together. It felt like we were a whole family, like we belonged together. I don\u2019t know if all of the others felt the same way, but I don\u2019t think I was the only one.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t want to lose that. I want things to always be that way.<br /> <br /> And it\u2019s no use; my body has now been conditioned to wake up ridiculously early every morning no matter how little sleep I get. I still have an hour or two before I have to get ready for Andromeda\u2019s surgery, so I\u2019m sitting here, writing in this journal, and looking across the room at the five of them, and just\u2026<u> <u>loving</u></u> them, I suppose. I can\u2019t really describe it any other way, and I can\u2019t seem to focus on anything else at the moment.<br /> <br /> Meh. There are worse ways to spend a morning.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Lorelei de la Rocha</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> \u201cCalamity? Where are you? I\u2019m on my way...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo! I\u2019m fine Becky. This isn\u2019t a call for backup.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI can hear screaming.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cUm\u2026 Yeah\u2026 Don\u2019t worry, I\u2019m outside and safe. But I\u2019m waiting for Soon Hee to get here so it\u2019s going to be a while before I\u2019m home and I didn\u2019t want you to worry.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCalamity, I love you but I worry about you when you go to get a drink of water.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHEY NOW!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLove, you have the most remarkable talent for finding trouble I have ever known. Remember the pier? I left you alone for five minutes...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe old bat deserved it. That poor girl she was yelling at was in tears.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know. My point is that you and trouble have a relationship that would make a lesser woman than myself jealous.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay. Fair enough. But honestly, I\u2019m fine.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI believe you. And thank you for calling and letting me know. I was seriously wondering what you\u2019d gotten into since you\u2019ve been gone so long. What happened to just going out to meet this Mr Ox and talk?\u201d <br /> <br /> \u201cWell, I did find his shop. I was driving past that run down strip mall with the Pioneer Chicken Stand. And where old Roger Dodger's was supposed to be I spotted a little curio shop without a name looking like it came straight out of a bad horror movie. So I pulled up and went in and the inside was even more stereotypical and he\u2019s sitting there in the smoky dimness, little old Chinese man with cataracts behind the counter. I mean seriously clich\u00e9. But it does make you wonder if he and shop look like that because they\u2019re a reflection of our shared subconscious archetype or if he\u2019s been doing this so long that the archetype is based on him. I might should ask him next time.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOr, just a thought, maybe you should not make a habit of visiting with an emissary of the Celestial Bureaucracy tasked with sorting the souls of the damned into their proper Hells. At least tell me you didn\u2019t ask him if he had a Mogwai or anything.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cJust because I typically choose not to behave doesn\u2019t mean I don\u2019t know how to. I am well aware of the power he has and the fact that even if my soul isn\u2019t within his pervue he is still extremely dangerous. I was perfectly respectful.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAlright. So, you found him and you asked him about the Xiahou family then?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI did. And in response he decided that he wanted to tell me a story about someone who wasn\u2019t a member of the family. And so I listened as he told me about someone named Johnny. Seems that this Johnny convinced some poor girl half his age that he loved her. But after Kim fell for his wicked whiles, he brutally murdered her and skinned her.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAh yes. Boy meets girl. Boy flays girl. It\u2019s a tale as old as time.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIndeed. And then he continued. You see Johnny runs the Red Lantern Lounge for his father and while the police can prove that Kim went there, they can\u2019t prove that she and Johnny actually spent time together or that he had anything to do with her disappearance. Mr Ox shook his head at that and told me how sad it made him when someone so wicked escapes justice. I agreed it was indeed a tragedy. And that\u2019s when he gestured to a blackened and shriveled but still slowly beating human heart on the shelf next to my elbow. He explained that it was Kim\u2019s heart and that if it could somehow find its way back and be reunited with her skin that she would able to teach Johnny the error of his ways. And it just so happens that Johnny was keeping her skin at the nightclub.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo, he asked you to bring the heart to the skin?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh no. He didn\u2019t ask me to do anything. And he certainly did not offer me any sort of reward for being the agent of Johnny\u2019s misfortune.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut you decided to do it out of your own desire to see justice served, didn\u2019t you?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI did! And I know that like any right minded sort, seeing someone like Johnny get the bad luck they deserve will make Mr Ox happy. And happy people are often generous.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd you decided to go and do this straight away?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, I did leave the shop with a still beating heart containing a vengeful ghost in my pocket. I didn\u2019t really want to bring it home.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI cannot actually fault you for that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo I found the club and despite the cheeky bouncer\u2019s efforts I slipped inside. Kim\u2019s heartbeat sped up as I got closer so we played a little game of hotter and colder until I figured out that it was in an employee\u2019s only back room. I lifted the key from the bartender\u2026 Oh man, I hope she made it out alive. She really was cute\u2026 Anyway, I got into the back and found the skin. It was in a room set up for ritual bloodletting.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, so Johnny\u2019s not just some garden variety psycho, he\u2019s an evil sorcerer.\u201d <br /> <br /> \u201cSeems that way. I could tell it was real magic but couldn\u2019t pin down the specifics. I took some pictures...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cPurely for research purposes, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cUmm\u2026 Yes? I\u2019m hoping White Maria might be able to make more sense of it. At any rate, that\u2019s when I noticed that some of the blood that had been collected was packed in a box addressed to the Xiahou family.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo by doing this thing that Mr Ox wanted done but didn\u2019t ask you to do you just happened to find a lead on the people you went there asking about.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYep.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay, well that\u2019s a little unsettling but I guess if you\u2019re going to wander about with a dead girl\u2019s cursed heart in your pocket at least you did turn up something useful. So, is this the point where you explain the screaming and tell me why you\u2019re waiting for Soon Hee?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI was getting to that. So, in addition to the whole bloodletting chair, there was also a woman, drugged and bound and wrapped in the skin. It was\u2026 well kinda like watching a snake shed its skin but in reverse. I\u2019m not exactly sure why they were making her look like Kim, but I figured it couldn\u2019t be for a good reason and unconsciousness isn\u2019t consent so I peeled the skin off her. Thankfully, it didn\u2019t seem to have really gotten ahold of her because came away easily and left her fine. And so, I put the wildly beating heart in the flayed human skin and that\u2019s when things shifted gears from Edgar Allen Poe to Steven King. I\u2019ll be honest, I was expecting a ghost. You know, wrathful spirit to torment Johnny and haunt his dreams. Drive the bastard to madness and suicide with guilt while everyone around him was confused by his crazy talk. But it seems Kim is more of the explode forth in a shower of blood that fills and animates the skin and sprouts blood knives before charging into the club shrieking to carve a bloody path of mayhem and death on her way to find Johnny sort.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, sounds like she\u2019s just your type Love.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell\u2026 I mean\u2026 maybe...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo you set the spirit loose on a bloody rampage in what I am going to tell myself was as much a den of iniquity as it sounds like.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes. And I couldn\u2019t leave the ritual victim just laying there naked and unconscious in the middle of all that. So I carried her out and cut her loose. But then it occurred to me that trying to transport a naked and drugged woman home on the back of bike was both logistically challenging and very likely to led to a conversation I did not want to have with the police. And even if it didn\u2019t, it would lead to questions I didn\u2019t want to answer with Lori.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo you called Soon Hee?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah. I figure I did the save her from an evil ritual part so I\u2019m hoping she can cover the watch the girl till she wakes up and give her some clothes and a ride home part. That and it would be terribly rude to cause a mess like this and not give her a head\u2019s up.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCalamity\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI love you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI love you too Beautiful.\u201d <br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXXIV</i><br /> <br /> Mr. Ox (who I shamelessly stole from <i>Bloodlines</i>) previously appeared in a significant role in <i>Geist: Balance of Shadows</i> and in a minor role in <i>Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</i>. He apparently gets around.<br /> <br /> Sorry for the delay getting them up. Comments and Questions are welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-19T13:59:21-07:00","id":1313187,"title":"","content":"Ready to catch up with gang in Malibu? Let\u2019s check in.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXXXIV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> It\u2019s been about a day since my last entry, and I\u2019m feeling generally more positive\u2026 but tired. I know I could pep myself up with Spring contracts, and I\u2019m doing that fairly regularly, but those don\u2019t help with the sort of spiritual exhaustion that I\u2019m currently experiencing.<br /> <br /> I dragged Maria out of bed yesterday morning just after I finished my last entry, pulling her gently from between Jane and Julia and trying my best not to disturb any of the others. Alas, my efforts were in vain: Marguerite woke up, and got out of bed long enough to slip her arms around me and offer a few sweet words of encouragement. \u201cYou will be brilliant, my sweet,\u201d she whispered in my ear before releasing me, \u201cAndromeda is lucky to have you as her surgeon.\u201d So that was nice.<br /> <br /> Maria grumbled a bit about the early wake-up call, but when I reminded her that we needed to go perform brain surgery on her best friend\u2019s fianc\u00e9e it cleared her head pretty quickly. A short drive later and we were at the clinic, and Maria had once more used her contracts to bless my efforts.<br /> <br /> Joan and Andromeda were there when we arrived. Joan was nervous, of course, but she did her best not to show it, and she was quick to assure me that her trepidation had nothing to do with her opinion of my skills. I tried to project an air of confidence to put both of them at their ease, and much to my surprise only a little of it was feigned. Our success with Halley\u2019s surgery on the previous day had boosted my confidence more than I thought.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m guessing Oleander took my advice and got some rest, because she wasn\u2019t present for the surgery this time. Anton and I got to work as soon as the machine was prepared, putting Andromeda under and doing a systematic search of her brain for the mysterious foreign particles. Things were a little more complicated than they had been with Halley\u2026 the particles were far more plentiful and more\u2026 <u>organized</u>, if that makes any sense. They seemed to fall into complex patterns, whirling around each other like electrons or galaxies, and every time we struck out at one it sent the others caroming into each other, ricocheting around the inside of her skull like pool balls.<br /> <br /> It took a while to get them all, to say the least. We had to double-check each other\u2019s work several times before we were satisfied with the results. But between Anton and me, I\u2019m confident that we were able to clear the\u2026 infestation from her mind. A little bit of Calamity\u2019s dream therapy and she should be right as rain. <br /> <br /> When I passed along the good news, Joan expressed her feelings with a fierce embrace and a passionate kiss. Then she took her love home to rest. If Andromeda is feeling up to it, the two of us will perform the operation on Anton this afternoon. After that I was hoping that the two of them would be able to take care of any remaining surgeries to give me time to see to some of my other obligations. Well\u2026 we\u2019ll see how that goes.<br /> <br /> Anton did say that he wanted to at least take a look inside the heads of everyone who\u2019s had extensive contact with the particles, including Calamity, Jacob, and Marguerite. He also wants to look inside <u>my</u> head, since I\u2019ve spent so much time with the subjects and performed surgery on them. I asked him (half-jokingly) if this would ruin my hair, and he kind of sputtered that this would only be the case if he actually had to perform surgery to excise the particles; the diagnostic would be non-intrusive.<br /> <br /> He also wants to check out Oleander. I saw the sense in that, and agreed to pass along his recommendation to her, but at the time it was a conversation I <u>really</u> wasn\u2019t looking forward to.<br /> <br /> And speaking of unpleasant conversations, another one cropped up unexpectedly at breakfast. There I was, enjoying a bit of toast and speaking fondly of the fact that I\u2019d be able to put the surgeries behind me in another day, when Jacob interjected flatly \u201cI will not allow Twitch inside of my head.\u201d<br /> <br /> Maria\u2019s eyes narrowed, but she kept her anger in check. \u201cI\u2019m sure you meant to say Anton,\u201d she growled evenly, \u201cand why not?\u201d<br /> <br /> Calamity cut in at that point. \u201cHe doesn\u2019t really have to answer that, does he?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cEnough,\u201d I said before Maria could get too worked up. I closed my eyes, put my fingers to my temples, and managed \u2013 just barely \u2013 to hold back my tears of frustration. \u201cJacob, Calamity\u2026 I understand your reservations. Anton did some horrible things when he was under Darke\u2019s thumb, but he\u2019s changed. He\u2019s trying to be better, and I promise you that he won\u2019t do anything unwholesome during the surgeries\u2026 he just wants to help. If you insist, I\u2019ll be there for the procedures, but\u2026\u201d and here I opened my eyes to let them see how exhausted I was, \u201c\u2026I could really use a break.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jacob frowned and looked inclined to argue, but Calamity took him by the arm and led him outside to spar for a while. D continued to grumble. \u201cIf Anton can forgive me for what I did to him,\u201d she said, her voice dangerously soft, \u201cit shouldn\u2019t be so hard for other people to forgive him for what <u>he\u2019s</u> done.\u201d<br /> <br /> I settled in behind her and slipped my arms around her waist. \u201cI agree,\u201d I soothed her, \u201cbut the others haven\u2019t spent as much time with him as you and I have, my love. They haven\u2019t seen firsthand how much he\u2019s changed. It\u2019s going to take time.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t worry,\u201d she said, taking one of my hands in hers, \u201cI\u2019m pissed, but I\u2019m not going to get into a fight with them over this. They\u2019re in the motley. But having said that\u2026 I\u2019m gonna head down into the basement and punch the bag for a while to let off some steam.\u201d <br /> <br /> Jane followed her downstairs after giving me a significant look. I\u2019m glad the two of them are bonding after their relationship got off to such a rocky start. Both of them looked a bit happier when they returned to the kitchen about half an hour later, and there was even banter between the two of them about doing a little naked wrestling.<br /> <br /> So that kind of set the scene for the rest of the afternoon. I discussed that night\u2019s act with Missy and Jane for a while (they agreed to back me up once more), which gave D a little more time to cool down, and then the three of us followed her into the basement. Jane and D <u>did</u> engage in a bit of naked wrestling while Missy and I watched, but it wasn\u2019t a serious competition in any wise. The two of them spent as much time giggling together as anything else.<br /> <br /> So we were all in a much better mood when we emerged from the depths of the Dream House to prepare for that evening\u2019s show. That only improved when Calamity sought me out backstage to let me know that she and Jacob had tentatively agreed to allow Anton and Andromeda to perform their surgeries. While they don\u2019t really trust Anton himself yet, they at least agree that he won\u2019t act against them when the venue is so public.<br /> <br /> I elected not to pass that little detail along to Maria when I told her that they\u2019d changed their minds.<br /> <br /> And speaking of Calamity\u2026 when I was glancing at the newsfeed on my phone I came across a story about a massacre in Chinatown. It had happened late the previous evening at a rather seedy club, and witnesses gave confused descriptions of the club being attacked by a shrieking woman wielding knives and covered in blood. Knowing as I did that Calamity was looking into the matter of the Xiahou family for the Autumn Court, it didn\u2019t take me long to put two and two together.<br /> <br /> When I asked her about it, she assured me that she wasn\u2019t the mystery knife lady, but that she was tangentially involved in that mess. And then I did something that\u2019s <u>very</u> hard for me\u2026 I let the matter drop. Whatever happened to Calamity, she was safe, and she had been acting under the aegis of the Autumn Court, and she had informed Soon Hee of her activities before leaving the scene. So it\u2019s in the hands of Charlotte and the Courts of the Dragon now. As callous as it might seem for me to say that\u2026 God, I have enough on my own plate right now without taking on extra worries, don\u2019t I?<br /> <br /> Speaking of Soon Hee, she was in the audience last night, so of course I stopped by to say hello and allow myself to be ogled for a little while. She seems to be doing well, though we really didn\u2019t talk for too long. I got the impression that she was there on business, so when Calamity approached I made myself scarce so the two of them could talk.<br /> <br /> Halley was back last night, and she seemed to be doing well enough. I stopped by the bar just long enough to make sure that she was feeling alright, but didn\u2019t want to distract her from the animated discussion she was having with Yvette. Those two seemed to really hit it off, though I didn\u2019t notice any particular romantic spark between them.<br /> <br /> My big number last night was a slow and sexy rendition of a tune from the 80s: \u201cShe Drives Me Crazy\u201d by a band called the Fine Young Cannibals. Missy and Jane took to it well, and as always their support boosted my own performance into the stratosphere. I\u2026 still can\u2019t really express how good it feels to have them back in my life. Every time I try to tell them how much I missed them or how much I love them I almost start to cry. It\u2019s gotten even more intense since they\u2019ve sort of unofficially joined the family that I share with Maria, Julia, and Marguerite. <br /> <br /> They do so much for me, pouring their glamour into every performance when they back me up. I need to make sure they understand that I\u2019ll be happy to do the same for them\u2026 all they ever have to do is ask.<br /> <br /> After my number I visited a couple of tables. Jolie was there with Desiree and Angelica (though the latter was not present in a romantic capacity), and I stopped by to chat with them. The usual flirtation ensued, though I don\u2019t think any of us were taking it particularly seriously (though I\u2019d still love to get Jolie, Desiree, and Veronica in bed with me at some point). I also spoke briefly with Angelica about meeting me at church so that Becky could take the following morning off.<br /> <br /> Once I\u2019d said hello to everyone else I made my way up to Oleander\u2019s table and settled in. She greeted me with a smile that was maybe the tiniest bit sheepish and gestured to the chair next to her. I leaned in for a kiss first, and then settled in. \u201cHow are you, sweetie?\u201d I asked after a moment.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m feeling better today,\u201d she said quietly. \u201cI slept\u2026 well, I slept <u>a</u> <u>lot</u> yesterday and today, and I think it helped. Sorry if I scared you. I\u2019ve already apologized to Anton about the things I said yesterday\u2026 after thinking about it, he raised some very valid points about the particles.\u201d She paused for a moment. \u201cHow did it go with Andromeda this morning?\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled. \u201cShe\u2019s right as rain. She\u2019s recovering with Joan right now, but if she\u2019s up for it the two of us are going to take a look inside Anton\u2019s head tomorrow afternoon and see if surgery is necessary.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGood,\u201d she said fervently, \u201cthen she and Anton can take care of the rest of the surgeries and <u>you</u> can get some rest, Angel. Everyone who went down to that bottom story should get checked.\u201d She paused for a moment and then sort of sighed. \u201cI should probably be checked as well; I\u2019ve spent enough time around those particles over the past week.\u201d<br /> <br /> I thanked God internally for His mercy when she said that. \u201cThat\u2019s a good idea,\u201d I agreed, taking her hand and squeezing it. \u201cWe can\u2019t afford to take chances with this, and I don\u2019t want to risk losing you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m not going anywhere, Angel,\u201d she said softly, and in her eyes she looked like herself to me again. I didn\u2019t see any hint of the harried, angry woman she had been on the previous morning. Now don\u2019t get me wrong\u2026 seeing her in that state didn\u2019t change how I feel about her in the least. But it was nice to have her back on a more even keel again.<br /> <br /> We talked a bit more as things wound down in the club. She knows about the advisory council the monarchs are forming to discuss how to deal with the particles once we\u2019ve collected them all; in fact Charlotte has already asked her to serve on the committee. This brought up the fact that I still had to appoint the two representatives from the Spring Court. Andromeda seems like a shoe-in, but I was at a loss to come up with a second name. Oleander opined that Austin would be a good choice if he would agree to serve (which he probably won\u2019t). Much to my surprise, her other suggestion was White Maria, due to her extensive knowledge of the mystic arts.<br /> <br /> Eventually the club started to clear out. \u201cYou ready to head upstairs?\u201d I asked her as the crowds thinned.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhenever you are,\u201d she agreed softly. Then her eyes darted toward the door, where Maria was chivvying a few stragglers out into the parking lot. \u201cIs\u2026 is she going to give me that apology?\u201d she asked after a moment. Her voice hardened as she said it.<br /> <br /> I sighed. \u201cImelda,\u201d I said softly, \u201cyou know how proud she can be when it comes to things like this\u2026 when she thinks she\u2019s being challenged. She\u2019ll come around. I\u2019m asking you to give it a little time. Please. For me.\u201d<br /> <br /> Oleander nodded tersely. \u201cI don\u2019t\u2026 I don\u2019t want to cause any trouble for you, Angel. I won\u2019t make trouble. But\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know,\u201d I said, giving her hand another squeeze.<br /> <br /> I checked in with Maria and got my kiss goodnight, then joined Oleander upstairs. Our evening was slow and soft and tender, and the two of us actually got to sleep at a reasonable hour (well, for the Dream House anyway). She fell asleep nestled up against me, looking\u2026 at peace with the world. It was enough.<br /> <br /> She was still like that when I woke up half an hour ago, and for a wonder I managed to extricate myself from her embrace without waking her. I turned off the alarm so that she could sleep in while I went to church. Honestly, I\u2019m not sure why I bother to set the damn thing anymore; I never sleep long enough to need it these days. But you know the one time I decide to go without it would be the one time I\u2019d oversleep\u2026<br /> <br /> Anyway, I should wrap this up and get ready for church. And after that, what will hopefully be my final brain surgery for the foreseeable future.<br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei de la Rocha</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> I think I did a bit of backsliding today. Lori got back from doing surgery on Andromeda this morning and said with confidence that Twitch and Andromeda could handle the rest of the surgeries from here on out, freeing her to her other duties as Queen and as a student. I objected saying that I would not allow Twitch to go anywhere near my brain. Calamity backed me up when De la Rocha objected to my statement. I think I offended De la Rocha on two fronts. I called him Twitch and I said that I don\u2019t trust the man with my brain. De la Rocha has lately become a staunch supporter and ally to Twitch. I think it\u2019s probably because she feels so bad for torturing the man in Arcadia. She wants to make up for it now and is overly protective of him in return. I still remember what he did to Rook. He drugged and tortured my brother until he didn\u2019t know who he was or where he was from. I\u2019m sure that De la Rocha would like to believe that Twitch is an innocent and would never do that without coercion from Master Darke. I tend to think that he may have been acting under orders from Darke, but he did those things willingly. <br /> <br /> Calamity suggested that we go out back and spar. I had some aggression that I needed to work out so I agreed willingly enough. Calamity and I went all out for a few minutes before we settled into a more sedate routine. It was more like a dance with knives than actual fighting. She assured me that she didn\u2019t like the idea of Twitch being in her head any more than I did but pointed out that having to do the surgeries on more people was causing Lori undue stress. It was not my goal to cause my friend more worry or anxiety. So as much as I really didn\u2019t want to I agreed with Calamity to allow Twitch to do my surgery. She made the point that it would be far too public a setting for him to get away with doing anything to either of us. We did make an arrangement though. If Twitch hurts me then Calamity will kill him slowly, and if he hurts Calamity then I will leave the bastard stranded in the Lady\u2019s realm. Yeah, probably not the best thing for me to actually do, but I was mad and I really don\u2019t like him. I couldn\u2019t think of a worse thing to do to him. Though I suppose that if I just left him there he might be able to find his way out again by finding a gate to the Hedge. Maybe I\u2019ll blind him and leave him deep in the woods there. That would certainly make it harder for him to find his way out again. So like I said, I think I did a bit of backsliding today. Thing is, I don\u2019t feel too bad about it. Because I meant what I said. I will fucking strand him in that hell if he hurts my friend. And I know that my friend will kill him slowly if he hurts me. With that agreement in hand we went back into the house and told Lori that we changed our minds and would allow Twitch to do the surgeries on us as long as Andromeda was there to help. I saw relief on her face when Calamity said that, and I felt bad for having made Lori worry about the whole thing. <br /> <br /> I know that Twitch is capable when it comes to the surgeries and that it will probably be good to let him do it, I just don\u2019t trust the man. Lori said that the surgery on Andromeda went well but took longer than it had on Hailey because the particles were more plentiful and \u201cacting\u201d differently. They behaved like little universes or collections of electrons orbiting a central mass. It sounded disturbing to me. I wonder if it\u2019s because Andromeda waited a day to do the surgery? Maybe the particles are getting more organized? I don\u2019t know. Hopefully there won\u2019t be any issues when it comes time for Calamity, Insincere Marguerite and I to have our surgeries. Who knows? Maybe it only affected their brains because they interacted with the machine. That doesn\u2019t seem too likely though considering the particles were in the air down there and we all breathed them in. I just don\u2019t like this whole situation.<br /> <br /> Later in the day, at the show, I talked to Hailey to see how she was doing after her own surgery. I wanted to assure her that I was happy that she was okay and that it was a success. She said that everything went well. They put her under and she had some strange dreams, but that was the extent of it for her. She said that she feels fine and hasn\u2019t noticed any side effects. I admitted to her that I was not looking forward to my own surgery, but did not mention the agreement that Calamity and I came to if Twitch should do something to one of us. If anyone knew what I was planning on doing to the man if he should fuck with Calamity then they would try and stop me and I don\u2019t want that happening. I really shouldn\u2019t be contemplating stranding someone in Arcadia. I know it\u2019s wrong, but don\u2019t know if I have it in me to torture a man anymore. Just the thought of it brings back bad memories of my own torture and I don\u2019t like the flashbacks.<br /> <br /> I should stop that line of thought right now. I\u2019ll never get to sleep if I keep thinking about all that stuff. Just the idea of having brain surgery scares the shit out of me. It\u2019s not made any better by the fact that Twitch will be one of the ones performing it either. Maybe I should have a drink or three to help me sleep? I wish my Luna were here right now. I could use an understanding ear.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXXXIV</i><br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think there is too much to be added here. Insincere Marguerite and Calamity mostly did not wander off to do their own thing. While the surgeries were more challenging, Twich used his Wizend skills to boost the machine significantly so between that and very high die pools each they are crushing the rolls easy.<br /> <br /> That was the only big mechanics thing. Comments and Questions are always welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-16T14:21:08-07:00","id":1318944,"title":"","content":"We return to Malibu. I sum this up in two words: Hopping Vampires<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXXXV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Sweet Buddha on a bagel. You know, when I got up on Sunday morning, I actually thought I might have <u>less</u> stress in my life by the end of the day. I was looking forward to it. Sigh. Maybe someday I\u2019ll know what it\u2019s like to have a day without a crisis.<br /> <br /> The day started out well enough. I woke up nestled in Oleander\u2019s embrace, and she looked so peaceful and content in her sleep that I had to smile. I decided not to disturb her, and set about getting ready for church as quietly as I could.<br /> <br /> A pleasant surprise awaited me downstairs as I was walking to the car\u2026 Missy and Jane were there, dressed nicely and smiling beatifically. They asked if they could join me at church that morning (Missy with admittedly more enthusiasm than Jane). \u201cWe figured it was finally time,\u201d Missy said as I pulled them into a hug.<br /> <br /> So Dad had three angels in his congregation this morning. Four, if you count Angelica (who as usual met me at the church so that she could fulfill her duties as claviger), though of course her angelic nature isn\u2019t as obvious as ours most of the time. Still, I think the familiarity of the church setting provided some comfort for Missy and Jane\u2026 and I know Dad was thrilled to see them there, though he also seemed a little weirded out by their presence. Possibly because he presided over their funerals about thirty years ago.<br /> <br /> We passed a few words with Dad before heading back to the Dream House for Sex Breakfast. Calamity was making crepes, and as usual they were delicious. Conversation centered mostly around D trying to convince Missy and Jane to put on schoolgirl outfits and perform a song called \u201cAll the Things She Said\u201d by a group called t.A.T.u., and Julia being horrified by the very idea. I don\u2019t claim to understand all of the nuances of the argument\u2026 something about how the Russian girls who originally released the song were attempting to profit on the notoriety of being underage girls in a lesbian relationship (which they apparently were not).<br /> <br /> In any case, after breakfast it was time for Maria and me to head over to the clinic for Anton\u2019s surgery. I asked Oleander if she wanted to join us, but she declined with a somewhat frosty look at my wife. I think she\u2019s still waiting for that apology, which isn\u2019t particularly likely to be forthcoming any time soon\u2026 but that\u2019s a problem for another day.<br /> <br /> Oh, I almost forgot. Yvette asked to speak with me before Maria and I left. She had spent the previous evening in deep conversation with Halley, and naturally the two of them had discussed their current relationships with Marguerite and Andromeda \u2013 their former abusers \u2013 respectively. Yvette said she had been given a lot to think about, but wanted to hear things from Andromeda\u2019s point of view if possible. As I was going to meet Andromeda at the clinic, I promised to pass along her request and see if I could arrange a meeting for the two of them. Of course, I cautioned her to be careful how she spoke to Andromeda, as she still harbors very deep affections for Halley\u2026 and her fianc\u00e9e is <u>very</u> protective of her.<br /> <br /> \u201cHow protective?\u201d Yvette asked with a saucy smile. \u201cIs she like de la Rocha? Is she like <u>two</u> de la Rochas?\u201d<br /> <br /> I gave the question the serious thought it deserved. \u201cJoan is\u2026 more protective than Maria,\u201d I said slowly, \u201cbut not as likely to lash out suddenly. She\u2019ll give you a warning glare before she strikes.\u201d<br /> <br /> So I left her with that to think about, and Maria and I headed over to the Clinic for what I hope was my final neurosurgery for at least a little while. Anton was sanguine about the whole thing. \u201cI have every confidence in you,\u201d he said fervently, \u201cyou have a remarkable talent for this sort of work.\u201d Coming from someone as skilled as Anton, that\u2019s a high compliment indeed. I think I might have blushed.<br /> <br /> In any case, the surgery went well. Andromeda is almost as skilled as Anton, and she used her Wizened powers to coax a little more cooperation out of Anton\u2019s machinery as well. Coupled with Maria\u2019s ability to manipulate chance and fortune, we didn\u2019t have much trouble with the procedure. Anton\u2019s brain didn\u2019t have as many of the particles in it as Andromeda\u2019s or Halley\u2019s had, but there were still more than a few in there. Still, I\u2019m confident that the two of us were able to clean them out completely in the end.<br /> <br /> Andromeda and Anton are going to work together to finish checking people out in the coming week. Calamity, Dahlia, Jacob, Marguerite, and Oleander are still on the docket. I mentioned that I should probably be checked for particles as well, since I\u2019ve spent so much time around them over the past few days, and Anton offered to scan my head then and there. Thankfully, the scan came up clean, and there was no need to perform the actual surgery on me.<br /> <br /> I did speak with Andromeda about Yvette, and she promised to stop by that evening with Joan. I was careful to warn her that Yvette had only heard the story from Halley\u2019s point of view, but I also told her that the French girl was eager to hear about things from her side as well. I promised to stop by and see how things had gone at the end of the show\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026unfortunately I didn\u2019t know that I was going to have more than enough problems of my own to worry about.<br /> <br /> So I made my way home and spent the rest of the afternoon preparing for the show, little knowing that I wouldn\u2019t actually be performing at all that evening. While I was still wrangling the performers before opening curtain, Calamity gave the Bluetooth device in my ear a buzz, letting me know that we needed to talk.<br /> <br /> \u201cSerena\u2019s here,\u201d she said once we had a little privacy. \u201cOur kindred allies in L.A. wanted to let us know that there\u2019s a plague of hopping vampires on the loose. They sent her here to make sure that we were safe and that we didn\u2019t blame them for any of the fallout.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat was nice of them,\u201d I said brightly.<br /> <br /> Calamity sighed. \u201cUnfortunately, as soon as she walked through the door she could sense that we had another kindred here.\u201d<br /> <br /> I had forgotten about Dakota and her political inconveniences. \u201cShit,\u201d I said.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s what I said,\u201d she commented.<br /> <br /> I thought quickly. \u201cGet her to my Dad\u2019s place through the Hedge,\u201d I suggested. \u201cI\u2019ll call him to let him know you\u2019re coming. Get back as quickly as you can.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded and headed to the floor to let the others know what was going on, and then detoured to the basement. I pulled out my phone and speed-dialed Dad, who picked up on the fourth ring. I could tell that he was winded when he answered.<br /> <br /> \u201cTo what\u2026 do I owe the pleasure, Juliette?\u201d he asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cSorry to disturb you, Dad,\u201d I said, \u201cbut we need to move Dakota back to your house. Another vampire is here. She came in peace, to help us out with a little problem. But she can sense that there\u2019s another vampire in the house. We need to move Dakota to keep her safe.\u201d<br /> <br /> Dad pondered for a second. \u201cMy house should be safe enough,\u201d he agreed. \u201cThe Long Night has moved on. Unless you think they might track her back to me as you move her\u2026?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCalamity\u2019s going to take her through the Hedge,\u201d I explained, \u201cthat should be safe enough.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll get home as soon as I can,\u201d he said, panting a little.<br /> <br /> It occurred to me that I hadn\u2019t asked one fairly important question. \u201cDad\u2026 where are you?\u201d<br /> <br /> He hesitated to answer. \u201c\u2026out,\u201d he said mysteriously.<br /> <br /> \u201cAre you hunting hopping vampires?\u201d I asked directly.<br /> <br /> He sighed. \u201cWhat would bring you to ask such a question?\u201d he asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cI know what\u2019s going on out there, Dad,\u201d I said. \u201c<u>Please</u> go home. Meet Calamity and Dakota. And stay <u>safe</u>.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cVery well,\u201d he said. After another long pause, he added, \u201cyour friend Calamity wouldn\u2019t happen to have any Dragon\u2019s Breath ammunition, would she?\u201d <br /> <br /> \u201cDragon\u2019s Breath\u2026 what?\u201d I asked with my typical poise and grace.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ve run through quite a bit of it tonight. I fear I may have irreparably damaged my shotgun in the process\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2026 I\u2019ll ask her,\u201d I promised<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you. I love you, Juliette,\u201d he said.<br /> <br /> \u201cLove you, Dad,\u201d I responded, and he broke the connection.<br /> <br /> I used the Bluetooth to reach Marguerite, and asked her to have Imogen take my solo for the evening. I gave her the basics of what was going on, and she didn\u2019t question my decision to stay off the stage for the evening. But\u2026 my own concerns didn\u2019t excuse me from my duties as Spring Queen, so I circulated among the crowd and spoke with people nonetheless.<br /> <br /> I hadn\u2019t been at it long when Calamity (who did not have any Dragon\u2019s Breath ammunition) called to let me know that she and Dakota had made it to Dad\u2019s house, and that he had likewise returned safely. My relief lasted all of five seconds before she informed me that Dad intended to head back out and continue his hunt, and that he had invited her along.<br /> <br /> I sighed. \u201cDo you think there\u2019s any way of talking him out of it?\u201d I asked wearily.<br /> <br /> She thought about it. \u201cI doubt it,\u201d she said.<br /> <br /> I closed my eyes and forced the tears back. \u201cCalamity,\u201d I said once I\u2019d regained my composure, \u201ckeep him safe. <u>Please</u>. Make sure he comes back to me safely. I can\u2019t lose him.\u201d<br /> <br /> She actually stopped back by the Dream House before heading out, and Jacob decided to go with her. They invited Maria as well, and I could tell that a part of her really wanted to go\u2026 but a bigger part of her wanted to stay with me when she knew I needed her support. Dad didn\u2019t come in\u2026 presumably either because he didn\u2019t want to have to explain the body armor to the other guests or because he was afraid I\u2019d convince him not to go back out at all. Personally, my money\u2019s on the latter.<br /> <br /> So I flitted from table to table for the next several hours, trying to lose myself in conversations with my friends and neighbors and desperately attempting to bury the crushing anxiety which constantly threatened to overwhelm me. Desiree and Veronica were there once more, and this time Tanner was with them. I didn\u2019t really sense any romantic spark or sexual tension between the three of them\u2026 but that might be because Tanner had a tendency to blush violently crimson and stammer uncontrollably every time I spoke to her.<br /> <br /> I also finally asked White Maria if she would be willing to represent the Spring Court on the Freehold\u2019s committee to decide how to best dispose of the exotic particles from the Bulgarian facility. She agreed almost immediately, and despite Andromeda\u2019s private doubts, she didn\u2019t seem the least bit nonplussed about serving with the alien girl. I think she might have been about to make a typical White Maria comment about Andromeda\u2019s libido, but she held herself in check this time.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Andromeda, she spent most of the evening in a private conversation with Yvette. I joined her and Joan at their table after they had concluded their talk. Andromeda was emotionally drained, and \u2013 somewhat predictably \u2013 Joan was seething at the idea that someone had upset her beloved. Andromeda seemed to have things well in hand, though, and the two of them left together shortly thereafter.<br /> <br /> I spoke with Yvette next. She was satisfied with her talk with Andromeda, though a bit disturbed as well. According to her, Andromeda seems incapable of understanding why Halley can\u2019t forgive her for her past mistakes. \u201cIt is like\u2026 she thinks it was like pushing another child on the playground,\u201d she explained, \u201csomething that should fade with the passage of time. She truly does not understand the magnitude of what she did to Halley.\u201d That jives with what I\u2019ve noticed myself, though I never really put it in those terms.<br /> <br /> I wonder if maybe she might benefit from speaking with some of the therapists at the Clinic? I brought it up with Joan briefly before they left, and she promised to consider it.<br /> <br /> I stopped by Serena\u2019s table at some point, and we chatted for a while. I made sure to thank her \u2013 and by extension the kindred of L.A. \u2013 for dropping by to make sure we were safe during the infestation. She waved that off as unimportant, but shortly thereafter looked down at a text and furrowed her brow. When I asked what was up, she sort of sighed.<br /> <br /> \u201cThere\u2019s a hunter in the Malibu area,\u201d she admitted. \u201cHe\u2019s kind of a badass. We all thought he was retired, but we\u2019re getting reports that he\u2019s out hunting the Jiangshi tonight. I don\u2019t <u>think</u> he\u2019d be dangerous to your people, but you might want to put the word out to avoid him anyway\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I closed my eyes and tried to keep my voice level. \u201cAre your people planning to do anything about this hunter?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> She shook her head anxiously. \u201cOur basic protocol with him is to avoid him whenever possible. He doesn\u2019t seem to be actively hunting kindred anymore, so it seems best to just leave well enough alone. If he wants to help us with the Jiangshi problem, so much the better\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe Reverend Wells is my father,\u201d I said softly. That brought her up short; she didn\u2019t seem to know what to say, so I continued. \u201cHe\u2019s not a danger to your people as long as you leave him alone. He had a change of heart about kindred long ago.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cThat tracks with what we know,\u201d she admitted. \u201cThere are even some confused reports of him <u>helping</u> kindred when they\u2019re in trouble, though we can\u2019t verify any of them. He\u2019s got nothing to fear from us as long as he doesn\u2019t start trouble.\u201d There was another awkward pause, and eventually she started speaking again. \u201cSo he\u2019s your dad, huh\u2026 just how old are you?\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled a little. \u201cI\u2019ll be fifty-six next month,\u201d I admitted.<br /> <br /> She looked me up and down. \u201cYou look damn good for your age,\u201d she said with a smirk. It didn\u2019t occur to me until later how ironic that statement was, coming from a vampire.<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks,\u201d I accepted the compliment. \u201cI spent a lot of time in Arcadia\u2026 the faerie lands. Time\u2019s different there.\u201d She took that in stride, referring to it as a \u201cBrigadoon situation.\u201d We spoke for a bit longer, but eventually my restlessness forced me to move on.<br /> <br /> I retreated to the girlfriend table as the crowds began to thin. I asked quietly if my family would mind staying with me that night, and all five of them agreed that they would lend me their support. I felt a little bad about that, as I knew that Marguerite and Yvette had planned to spend a romantic evening together, but both of them assured me that it was fine. \u201cI know that Insincere Marguerite would do the same for me, if I truly needed her,\u201d Yvette said with a smile, \u201cand I am a bit fatigued by my earlier conversation in any case.\u201d<br /> <br /> Still, I knew that I wouldn\u2019t be able to get to sleep until I was sure that Dad was safe. Luckily, Calamity and Jacob got back just before the last of the stragglers left, looking winded but not badly hurt (a quick application of my healing contracts saw to their injuries). Their hunt had been successful, and both were quick to assure me that Dad was fine. I thanked them both profusely for keeping him safe, but they told me that he barely needed it.<br /> <br /> The relief flooded in, and I allowed the tension to go out of my shoulders. I felt giddy, which might help to explain what I did next. As I was heading toward the stairs to join my family, I paused, turned, and favored Calamity with a subtle smile. \u201cCalamity,\u201d I asked with a wink, \u201cwhat was the final score?\u201d<br /> <br /> She gaped at me for half a second, and then laughed out loud. \u201cSix,\u201d she said after a moment. \u201cYour Dad took out two of them himself.\u201d<br /> <br /> I felt something swelling up inside me at that. Incongruously, I think it might have been pride.<br /> <br /> Dad called me a few minutes later to let me know that he was back at home, and that he and Dakota were both safe. \u201cThank God,\u201d I said fervently. \u201cDo you have any idea how worried I\u2019ve been?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCome now Juliette,\u201d he said drily, \u201cI think we both know that you owe me a few nights of sitting up worried to death.\u201d<br /> <br /> I chuckled at that. \u201cFair enough,\u201d I allowed. It was pretty late by that point, so we wrapped up our conversation quickly, and I promised to visit him soon. Then I made my way upstairs, undressed, and lost myself in the arms of my various lovers. It was a very emotional evening\u2026 I\u2019m sure I cried at some point, though I don\u2019t really remember the specifics. Maria, Marguerite, Julia, Jane, and Missy were all there for me in every way that I needed, and eventually, despite the distractions and frustrations of the day, I was able to fall asleep.<br /> <br /> I love them all. I don\u2019t know what I\u2019d do without their support and affection. When I\u2019m with them, I actually <u>feel</u> like a queen.<br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei de la Rocha</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Damn. That\u2019s all I have to say. Damn! Not in a bad way though. I was just damn impressed with how well Lori\u2019s dad takes care of vampires. I can see why the local vampires prefer to leave him in peace and not anger him. It all started at the show. Serena showed up to warn us that there was a problem with hopping vampires in town. Apparently the rivalry between those two Chinese families that Calamity has been dealing with has escalated and they both released hopping vampires on the city. Not the greatest idea if you ask me. It doesn\u2019t seem like they have any other purpose other than causing chaos. They don\u2019t seem to be directed to attack the other family or its members. They just seem to be roaming the city. So Serena came to warn us and to help keep us safe from any that might try to get in or attack any of the customers. The problem came when Serena said that she had sensed another vampire in the house. She was sensing Dakota. That was problematic, so Calamity got Dakota ready to go while Lori called her dad to see if Dakota could stay with him for a little while. If she wasn\u2019t in the house then Serena wouldn\u2019t feel her presence or do anything to her. The Reverend Wells said that he\u2019d be happy to keep an eye on Dakota but he was busy at the moment. It seems that it was out hunting the hopping vampires. Lori insisted that he meet up with Calamity at his house and allow the Darkling to accompany him if he was going to go back out after more vampires. He agreed. A short while later Calamity called me to see if I\u2019d be interested in joining them and I said sure. I mean, how many opportunities does one get to hunt hopping vampires? <br /> <br /> So, Reverend Wells and Calamity picked me up and we started hunting. Wells had some sort of a detector that he used to find a hopping vampire in a parking lot. We dispatched it easily. We then went to a nearby car park and dealt with several more. They tried to ambush us, but I heard them coming. That was the fight that Reverend Wells really distinguished himself. At one point he used a shotgun loaded with \u201cDragon\u2019s Breath\u201d ammunition. Basically, phosphorous rounds. They do bad things to the shotgun barrel when used but are damn effective at taking out vampires in one shot. The rest fell pretty easily. One started to run away but Calamity jumped after him and took him out quickly. After that we started hearing sirens so we decided to leave. I didn\u2019t relish the idea of explaining to a cop why I was armed with several knives and an illegal pistol. Revered Wells was also wearing his body armor, so he kind of stood out. His body armor was pretty extensive too. It was designed to keep someone safe from vampires. Calamity and I only really needed to worry about the vampire\u2019s claws. Changelings are immune to becoming vampires from their bite so we just wore our leathers. Calamity did get hit once so we called Lori after we had snuck into the house to let her know we were back. We didn\u2019t want to show off our gear to the customers. Lori met us upstairs and healed Calamity\u2019s wounds. He had already left but she also made sure that her father didn\u2019t need any attention. He didn\u2019t. I don\u2019t think he got touched during the fight at all. He is damn spry for a man pushing eighty. We assured Lori that her father was unhurt and very good at hunting vampires. He was very careful and professional. I don\u2019t know if that alleviated any of Lori\u2019s concerns or not. After everyone was sorted out I went about cleaning my knives. I wanted to be able to tell Luna about my evening but she was out working. I know she would appreciate the tale. She might have wished to have been part of the fight, but it didn\u2019t work out that way this time. If the hopping vampires continue to be a problem maybe she can join Calamity, the Reverend Wells and I for another night of vampire hunting.<br /> <br /> After we were cleaned up Calamity and I joined Lori downstairs and talked to Serena about our evening\u2019s activities. She did tell us that her people were a little concerned when they heard that a vampire hunter was heading for the Dream House, but Lori assured her that the hunter meant no harm to Serena or her friends. He was just out taking care of the hopping vampires. Serena admitted that she had heard of him and had a good deal of respect for him. In the end Lori admitted that the hunter was her father. I think she wanted to impress upon Serena that her dad meant no harm to her or her fellows. I think she wanted to make sure that there were no miscommunications between anyone and that her father would be safe from Serena and her friends. Serena seemed more than willing to leave things be. <br /> <br /> After all of that I returned to the bar and Elena motioned me over. I went to her table and sat down to talk. She basically just wanted to see if Luna and I would be free to go out to dinner with her and Stasia on Tuesday night. I said that we\u2019d be happy to join her. I will admit that I asked if she was okay. She seemed a bit down, but she assured me that she was fine. She was just feeling a bit homesick for our family. I can understand that. She just wanted to get together with the family that she has here, so I agreed on Luna and I\u2019s behalf. I even suggested that we all go ice skating after dinner. I haven\u2019t been in a long time and I don\u2019t know when the last time that Elena went skating was. I figured it would be fun. It was something that we did as kids, so it might bring back memories of home. I am hoping to create new memories for her here though. I\u2019ll admit that I wasn\u2019t keen on Stasia in the beginning, but I\u2019m glad that she\u2019s here for my sister now. She has been a constant for my sister while things are moving and changing in Elena\u2019s life. She has been so supportive and never wavered. I will admit that I was wrong about Stasia and I\u2019m happy that I was wrong. I am also glad that I was able to reconnect with my sister. It has been good for both of us. It was hard for me living so close to my sister but having her not know who I was. I was also so far from our parents. I couldn\u2019t go home because of my fetch. Now though, I have come clean to Elena about who I am, and it has been great. We were always close growing up. Things don\u2019t feel exactly like they did when we were younger, but they\u2019re getting there. <br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXXXXV</i><br /> <br /> The version of Jiang Shi presented here was changed somewhat from <i>Night Horrors: The Wicked Dead</i>. A lot of the ideas were taken from there, but also tinkered with to make their creation less unusual.<br /> <br /> As a reminder Reverend Wells has been fed a mysterious diet by Oleander making him more spry.<br /> <br /> I think that covers it, Comments and Questions welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-01T22:15:24-07:00","id":1321828,"title":"","content":"The group takes a breath from recent events, to enjoy some films. Meanwhile, Jane Lassiter\u2019s struggle becomes apparent<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXXXIX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> And the trend continues. While things seem to be settling a bit as far as matters of the Freehold are concerned, I have been given yet another personal matter to fret over. Okay, to be fair this was something I was already a little concerned about, but I\u2019d honestly thought they were getting past everything\u2026<br /> <br /> No. Focus and calm down, Lori. The three of us will get through this together. We always have, and now we have Maria, Marguerite, Julia, and the rest of the motley to support us. This <u>isn\u2019t</u> going to become a problem.<br /> <br /> Monday morning started off typically enough\u2026 I woke up and gently extricated myself from the rest of the family, headed into the media room, closed the door, and logged into my online classes. Things are going well, by the way\u2026 though I haven\u2019t gotten very many grades back yet, I think I\u2019m working toward an A-B average so far\u2026 maybe even straight As for the first time in my life. Dad will be thrilled, though I\u2019m not looking forward to the inevitable \u201cI-told-you-all-you-had-to-do-was-apply-yourself-properly-Juliette\u201d speech. Sigh. I suppose he\u2019s earned it.<br /> <br /> I was just finishing up when the others descended for Sex Breakfast. Calamity was working on a hearty breakfast of eggs and toast, and conversation mostly centered around what we were going to watch that evening for movie night. We eventually settled on one of Calamity\u2019s suggestions and one of Julia\u2019s: \u201cWho Framed Roger Rabbit\u201d and a 90s remake of \u201cThe Addams Family\u201d respectively.<br /> <br /> Conversation actually got sort of heated when it came to the latter film, though everyone present who had seen it had also enjoyed it. Julia spoke fondly of the Addams Family in general (both the film and the original TV show) and of the character of Wednesday Addams in particular, whom she viewed as something of a role model. I confess that this didn\u2019t make much sense to me until after I\u2019d seen the film, as my memories of the character from TV were largely of an unabashedly cheerful young girl, albeit one with a somewhat morbid world-view.<br /> <br /> I spent the afternoon mostly relaxing \u2013 \u201cchilling\u201d as the kids apparently say these days \u2013 and occasionally working on a few ideas for new numbers. This was mostly to distract myself from the fact that Marguerite was at the clinic undergoing brain surgery. I wasn\u2019t <u>really</u> worried of course\u2026 Anton and Andromeda have both proven that they\u2019re more than capable of clearing the particles from our brains. And of course, Marguerite was fine in the end. She did have some of the exotic particles in her brain, but not nearly as many as Andromeda or Halley \u2013 or even Anton \u2013 and they weren\u2019t as organized as they had been in Andromeda\u2019s head.<br /> <br /> The two of them were able to remove the particles with no problem\u2026 and the incision was so small that you can only find the scar if you know exactly where to look, and I\u2019m sure that\u2019ll clear up given a few days of healing too. With her hair brushed into its usual style you can\u2019t even tell that she\u2019d had the procedure at all.<br /> <br /> So the movies were fun. The first one was an imaginative blend of live-action and animation, in which human actors interacted with famous cartoons. The story was a noir mystery about someone who actually discovers a way to kill cartoons, and then pins his horrible acts upon an innocent rabbit named \u2013 naturally \u2013 Roger. The rabbit partners up with a human detective who hates cartoons, but of course the two of them eventually become friends and solve the mystery together. The best thing about the movie honestly was the sheer number of cameos from famous cartoon characters. It must have cost the filmmakers a fortune to get all of the rights\u2026<br /> <br /> The remake of the <u>Addams Family</u> was probably a better film overall, though it didn\u2019t have the \u201coh wow\u201d effect of the cameos from the first movie. Still, it was very well acted and scripted. The comic timing was amazing, and the actor playing Gomez was good enough that I didn\u2019t miss John Astin at all after about fifteen minutes.<br /> <br /> After the movies we retired for the evening. Marguerite spent the night with Yvette, and asked that D and I keep Julia entertained (which we were of course happy to do). Missy and Jane decided to devote the evening to each other, and spent the night in their own room. Though of course I love spending time with all of them\u2026 I must admit that it was nice to have a little more room on the bed in which to stretch out.<br /> <br /> The next morning was Tuesday, so I got up early to head out to college. Much to my surprise, Missy met me in the hallway as I was heading for the door and asked if she could speak with me. I had a little time to spare before I had to hit the road, so of course I agreed.<br /> <br /> Turns out Missy is still a little worried about Jane. She thinks the Empress was grooming Jane to be a predator\u2026 a bird of prey like Hawk or Ocras. She says that Jane insists on seeing other people as either predators or prey\u2026 and that some people are specifically <u>her</u> prey. People like Trinh.<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t get me wrong,\u201d Missy said when she saw the look on my face. \u201cShe likes Trinh now. She doesn\u2019t want to hurt her. But I think she feels like she might <u>have</u> to hurt her soon. Like she\u2019s supposed to\u2026 well\u2026 <u>eat</u> her.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat makes you think that?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> Missy looked sheepish. \u201cShe bit Trinh when we slept with her. Not hard enough to do any real damage, but hard enough to hurt. I think Trinh liked it a little bit\u2026 she thought it was just a little kinky fun. But I saw the look in Jane\u2019s eyes when she did that\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I sighed, closed my eyes, and pinched the bridge of my nose. Missy looked horrified. \u201cJules\u2026 I\u2019m sorry. I didn\u2019t mean to add to your worries\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I shook my head. \u201cDon\u2019t worry about it. I <u>want</u> to know about things like this. I want to help you two however I can. You\u2019re my best friends. I\u2019ve loved you both since long before we were lovers\u2026 you know that, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> She smiled. \u201cI know,\u201d she said.<br /> <br /> \u201cLet me talk to her. I\u2019ll set aside some time either tonight or tomorrow\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t tell her I told you,\u201d Missy said quickly.<br /> <br /> \u201cI won\u2019t,\u201d I said, then threw her a crooked grin. \u201cI\u2019ll say I noticed it myself\u2026 you know, pretend to be as perceptive as everyone seems to think I am. You can be with us, or I can talk to her alone. Whatever you want.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cI\u2019ll think about it.\u201d<br /> <br /> I wanted to say a few more things before I left. \u201cMissy,\u201d I said, \u201cwhatever\u2019s happening to Jane\u2026 it\u2019s a part of her now. If you love her \u2013 and I <u>know</u> that you love her \u2013 you\u2019re going to have to learn to love that part of her too.\u201d I told her a bit about how Maria regressed when she was stalking Hawk, and how terrified I was of losing her\u2026 and how I came to accept that the Hospital\u2019s \u201cMaria\u201d was an inseparable part of the woman I love. I even came to see the beauty in her darkness (with a little help from Julia).<br /> <br /> So that was on my mind as I made the drive into L.A. for Tuesday classes. Becky and I chatted about this and that on the way, and as usual she hung out in the quad being awesome while I attended my lectures and lab. I flirted for a bit with Paige and Brandon as we were cleaning up\u2026 I couldn\u2019t help it. They\u2019re both so cute, and I have the sneaking suspicion that if I can get together with both of them at the same time they might realize that they have a romantic spark with each other. Yep, totally doing it for them. Not me. Shut up.<br /> <br /> We made it back to the Dream House in time to catch the end of Sex Breakfast, wherein we discussed which Looney Tunes character we most resembled. Oddly enough, there weren\u2019t many direct correlations\u2026 Calamity was compared to the Tasmanian Devil, Elmer Fudd, and Yosemite Sam at various points, but none seemed quite right. Julia opined that Marguerite\u2019s clever deceptions and propensity for wearing drag made her a good match for Bugs Bunny. I figured I\u2019d be relegated to the role of that cat from the Pepe le Pew cartoons or something, but D insisted that I was \u201cthat chick from <u>Space Jam</u>,\u201d whatever that means. The conversation sort of fizzled after that.<br /> <br /> Most of us didn\u2019t have much to do that afternoon, so it was kind of a lazy day. Missy gave me a significant look, and I took the hint, figuring there was no time like the present. I asked Jane if I could speak with her privately, she agreed, and the three of us went upstairs to my bedroom and closed the door.<br /> <br /> It wasn\u2019t a pleasant conversation, though there was no acrimony or recriminations to my knowledge. Jane has made so much progress over the last month\u2026 but she hasn\u2019t come as far as I thought. Come to that, neither has Missy, though her issues don\u2019t seem to be as dangerous or pressing as Jane\u2019s.<br /> <br /> Missy was right; Jane is clearly still struggling with the changes the Empress had initiated in her just before her escape. Trinh won\u2019t be truly safe until and unless Jane finds a way to deal with these cravings\u2026 this <u>certainty</u> that Trinh was put on this Earth to be her next prey. She recognizes that these feelings are inappropriate in her new situation, but she can\u2019t seem to shake them entirely.<br /> <br /> What\u2019s more, Jane seems to have sort of edited her own memory to some degree. She remembers taking the lead when the three of us killed Annabelle, and she remembers doing it because Annabelle was her prey. I had to work really hard to convince her that <u>I</u> had initiated that attack, and I had done it because I was jealous of the other girl\u2019s singing talent. If Missy hadn\u2019t backed me up on that point, I don\u2019t think I would have been able to convince her at all.<br /> <br /> She kept asking me the same question: \u201cwhat do you think I should do about this?\u201d Sigh. Like she expected me to just have all the answers. I truly wish I could say something to make everything better\u2026 but life just isn\u2019t that easy.<br /> <br /> I gave both of them the best advice I could, of course. I suggested that Jane speak with Calamity about finding positive ways to channel her predatory urges\u2026 ways that could help the Freehold, the motley, and especially Missy. I also strongly urged her to discuss these feelings with her therapist\u2026 the Winter Court clinic\u2019s employees are trained to help changelings deal with their Gentry-inspired cravings, and they know more than I ever will about coping with that sort of urge.<br /> <br /> In Missy\u2019s case, I once again told her that she was going to have to learn to live with Jane\u2019s dark side\u2026 to love it, even. She gave me a little smile when I said that, and admitted that it was nice to know she had such a fierce protector. It makes her feel safe to know that Jane will go to any lengths to protect her.<br /> <br /> Jane wanted to be alone for a while after that (I think she eventually did speak with Calamity about her situation), so Missy and I were left to our own devices. I was glad. There was one more thing I wanted to ask about, and I wasn\u2019t sure if I could trust Jane\u2019s memories completely.<br /> <br /> \u201cMissy,\u201d I said softly once we were alone. \u201cMy memories of Arcadia are still kind of confused, so I need to ask you something. When you and Jane talk about\u2026 what happened to Annabelle, you mention that we killed her and then\u2026 ate her. I have no memory of that part of it. Did we really\u2026 did I\u2026?\u201d<br /> <br /> Missy sort of lowered her eyes. \u201cJane ate most of her,\u201d she answered in a hoarse whisper. \u201cI know I had a little, though. As for you\u2026 I don\u2019t know. I <u>think</u> so, but I\u2019m just not sure.\u201d So I had that to think about too.<br /> <br /> Missy shared one final theory with me\u2026 one that I find all too plausible, as horrific as it is. Missy believes that after Jane killed and devoured Trinh, her final test would have been to do the same to Missy herself. I could tell that she was really freaked out by this notion, so I did my best to comfort her. \u201cThat would never happen, Missy,\u201d I said firmly\u2026 and I believed every word of it. \u201cIf that was the Empress\u2019 final test, then Jane would have failed it. She would never have hurt you for <u>anything</u>.\u201d<br /> <br /> Missy sniffed. \u201cI know,\u201d she said softly. \u201cDeep down, I\u2019ve always known that. And the Empress would have killed us both for it.\u201d<br /> <br /> I pulled her into a hug. \u201cGood thing we got you out when we did, then, huh?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah,\u201d she said, hugging me back. \u201cLook, Jules, I know it hasn\u2019t been easy taking us in and dealing with all of this stuff. I just want you to know that we appreciate it all. We know you have a lot of more important stuff on your plate these days\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNope,\u201d I said firmly. \u201cNothing\u2019s more important to me than making sure you two are safe and happy. Well\u2026 you and Maria and Marguerite and Julia and the rest of the motley, of course. You\u2019ll always be my number one priority.\u201d<br /> <br /> Missy thanked me and headed off to rest before the show. I started my own pre-show rituals, which gave me a bit of time to myself to think. I meant what I said to Missy. My friends will always come first. That\u2019s not in question. But is it <u>right</u>? I\u2019m the Spring Queen\u2026 in a couple of months I\u2019ll be the sitting monarch of the Freehold. Do I have the luxury of considering my friends\u2019 welfare above anyone else\u2019s? What if someday I\u2019m forced to choose between Missy\u2019s life and Dark Kimberly\u2019s, or Tamara\u2019s, or Percival\u2019s? Is it <u>right</u> for me to prioritize the safety of those who are close to me over those who might have more important roles to play in the Freehold?<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know. I guess if something like that ever comes up I\u2019ll just have to do my best and pray that God will grant me the wisdom to make the best choice. Until then, I\u2019ll just muddle through like everybody else.<br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei de la Rocha</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> It\u2019s been a pretty uneventful past couple of days. I mean it was sort of eventful yesterday when Insincere Marguerite went to the clinic to get the particles removed from her brain. Twitch and Andromeda performed the surgery and she came out if it okay. I know logically that nothing bad should happen when Twitch does the surgery on me, but I\u2019m still not looking forward to it. I don\u2019t like the man and don\u2019t particularly trust him. He drove my best friend crazy with torture and drugs. I don\u2019t even know what Rook\u2019s true intentions had been when he left Arcadia to find me. Was he sent to kill me? Would he have done it even if he was? Would he have brought me back to the Lady instead? Or would he have let me go? Probably not the latter, but who knows. I\u2019ll never know now. Unless the Lady sends someone else to come after me I\u2019ll never know what her true intentions are towards me. She must know that I\u2019m still alive, and she must know by now that Rook isn\u2019t. So, what are her plans? I wish that I knew. The longer that it takes her to send someone else the more nervous I get. I don\u2019t know what she\u2019s planning, but it probably isn\u2019t good. She was rather angry at me when Rook brought me back the first time. She nearly tortured me to death that time. If I hadn\u2019t of managed to escape I\u2019m certain that I\u2019d be dead now. So essentially, I\u2019m living on borrowed time. It\u2019s only a matter of her putting together another recovery mission before my life gets difficult again. I hate the waiting.<br /> <br /> Anyway\u2026yesterday afternoon Luna came over and we caught her up on what has been going on lately. She was sorry to have missed the hopping vampire hunt, but she was doing important work. It would have been nice if she could have joined us, but I\u2019m not going to begrudge her her work. I know that she finds it fulfilling. I don\u2019t enjoy my work as much as I\u2019m sure she likes hers, but there are still some moments that are rather enjoyable. I like surprising the customers by remembering what their favorite drink is or knowing so many drink recipes in the first place. I have had more than one person order an obscure drink and be surprised that I didn\u2019t have to look at a drink guide.<br /> <br /> Drinks aside we started talking about what movies we were going to watch for movie night. Several ideas were bounced around before we finally decided on \u201cWho Framed Roger Rabbit,\u201d and \u201cThe Addams Family.\u201d \u201cWho Framed Roger Rabbit\u201d was not my first choice but everyone it seemed wanted something lighthearted to watch. So, we went for those two movies. After that decision was made Luna, Calamity and I went out to the backyard to spar. It was a good workout. It seems like it\u2019s been a long time since I last got to spar with my Luna. She is wicked with those knives of hers. I used to see a lot of Luna\u2019s style in Calamity\u2019s moves but lately her style has been evolving. I think it\u2019s because she studies other martial arts with White Maria on Monday mornings. The attacks are mostly the same, it\u2019s just how she defends and moves in general that has been changing. It\u2019s an interesting development and keeps me on my toes. I\u2019ll have to see if I can emulate some of those moves and see if I can return the favor.<br /> <br /> I think it was during our sparing time that Insincere Marguerite went to the clinic. She came back fine though, so that was good. It wasn\u2019t that long after she returned that we watched the movies. Everyone seemed to like them both. Lori seemed especially taken by \u201cWho Framed Roger Rabbit.\u201d She kept commenting on the characters that showed up. There were a lot of famous cartoon characters in that movie. Then there was \u201cAddam\u2019s Family.\u201d Julia really enjoyed that one. She said, and I believe her, that Wednesday Addams was her role model when she was younger. Lori talked about how Wednesday was more upbeat and cheerful in the TV show, but that\u2019s not really the case in the movie. I guess I\u2019ll have to take her word on it. I\u2019ve never seen the TV show.<br /> <br /> Then there was today. Not much happened. I went to therapy like usual this morning. I shared my concern about the Lady\u2019s motives with Sullivan but he seemed to be of the opinion that I shouldn\u2019t worry about it so much if there has been no indication that she has enacted any plans regarding me. He didn\u2019t say that I shouldn\u2019t worry at all. He just implied that I shouldn\u2019t worry quite as much. I don\u2019t think he realizes just how dangerous she can be. Her moods change drastically from happy, which can be downright scary, to angry, which is worse. When the Lady is in a good mood people die. When the Lady is in a bad mood they wish they were dead. And last I saw and experienced, she was really angry at me. Usually Sullivan has some pretty good advice for me, but when it comes to Her I think I\u2019ll listen to my own gut. She has got to be planning something. She was upset enough when I broke up her favorite team. Now the loyal one of that pair is dead, and I\u2019m still alive and free in \u2018the world.\u2019 I just don\u2019t think that she\u2019s going to stand for that too much longer. She can be patient though, at times, so she may just be biding her time. I\u2019m not sure what for. Maybe for me to get complacent and a little too comfortable in my life here. Whatever is going on in her mind, I need to stay vigilant. Sullivan says that I should relax more, but for once I don\u2019t think I\u2019m going to take his advice. He\u2019s never been hunted before. I know what it\u2019s like to be both the hunted and the hunter and I much prefer the latter. <br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXXXIX</i><br /> <br /> Jane\u2019s condition had been hinted at, but only lightly. It is always fun to have them discuss movies.<br /> <br /> Comments and Questions are welcome<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T14:34:15-07:00","id":1324559,"title":"","content":"Stasia finds something new and terrifying. There is talk of babies. Possibly more terrifying.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXXXVII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Mmmmm\u2026 that was nice. More than \u2018nice,\u2019 really, but my vocabulary isn\u2019t at its best right now; I think my brain might be a little starved for oxygen, and, umm\u2026<br /> <br /> You know what, I\u2019m going to need a few minutes.<br /> <br /> Okay, I\u2019m back. Where was I, and what was I talking about? The show. Right. So the Tuesday night show went well enough. The crowd was light, but that\u2019s to be expected from a weekday show. Calamity debuted a new dance number called \u201cA Little Wicked.\u201d Its lyrics included some not-so-subtle references to regicide, which I\u2019m sure amused her to no end. It\u2019s enough to make a nascent queen a bit nervous.<br /> <br /> Naaah\u2026 she\u2019s said it a thousand times before: Calamity keeps her magically binding promises. I\u2019m probably safe for now.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m kidding of course. I love Calamity, and I know that she loves me. I think it\u2019s probably impossible for two people to irritate each other as much as we do unless they really care about each other deep down. She\u2019s just so reckless all of the time, and I worry about her\u2026 even more so now that I\u2019m a monarch and she\u2019s nominally under my protection. I\u2019m sure that\u2019s only going to get worse as Winter turns to Spring\u2026<br /> <br /> Anyway, Marguerite took the night off, so there was no new material from her direction (though I think she\u2019s planning to debut something fresh this weekend). For my own solo\u2026 oh, I\u2019ve pretty much resigned myself to only doing one solo act per night, with the option to sing or dance backup on a few other numbers as the situation demands. That way I have more time to spend among my constituents. Anyway, for my own number, I did a sultry version of the Shondells\u2019 \u201cI Think We\u2019re Alone Now,\u201d which went over pretty well with the scant crowds and served to refresh my diminishing glamour reserves nicely.<br /> <br /> Once the hobnobbing began, my first stop was the table containing Becky, Dark Kimberly, and White Maria. I spoke pleasantly with all three of them for a few minutes, first telling Becky that I had no specific plans for the evening so she was free to pursue her own interests if she liked. Then White Maria and I spoke about the first meeting of the committee. It sounds like they\u2019re making progress, albeit slowly. There are a lot of powerful, temperamental people on that committee (including but not limited to Madame Spidertoes, Oleander, Halley, and Andromeda), and from what White Maria shared with me the first meeting was mostly dedicated to setting boundaries for the discussion and establishing a common terminology so that everyone would be on the same page.<br /> <br /> I have every confidence that our people will come up with a viable solution to the problem of the particles. There\u2019s a part of me that\u2019s desperately impatient to put the whole matter behind us as quickly as possible, but the logical part of my brain recognizes that the quickest solution is rarely the most effective\u2026 and we really need an effective solution to put this situation to bed for good. I trust the committee\u2019s judgment enough that I\u2019m allowing my metaphorical muscles to unclench ever so slightly on this issue.<br /> <br /> As luck would have it, God decided to place <u>another</u> issue before me last night.<br /> <br /> As I was wrapping up the conversation with White Maria, my glance fell upon a table near the bar. Jacob and Luna had gone out earlier that evening on a double-date with Stasia and Elena, and the four of them were taking in the later portions of the show. Calamity had joined them at their table, and she and Stasia were discussing something animatedly, with lots of body language and hand movements clearly signaling their excitement.<br /> <br /> I guess my brow must have furrowed or something, because White Maria immediately asked if everything was okay.<br /> <br /> \u201cSorry,\u201d I said, \u201cI think I\u2019m going to have to cut this short.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnything I can do?\u201d White Maria asked conscientiously.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo,\u201d I assured her, \u201cit\u2019s probably nothing. It\u2019s just that the last time I saw Calamity and Stasia looking that happy about anything, events started to spiral and we ended up having to form a committee to decide how to deal with the fallout.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sure you\u2019ll handle it, Your Majesty,\u201d White Maria said with a slight smile and a nod.<br /> <br /> I probably threw her a somewhat doubtful look; Calamity doesn\u2019t respond well to being \u2018handled,\u2019 and I don\u2019t expect Stasia would react to it any better.<br /> <br /> White Maria\u2019s look grew a bit more thoughtful. \u201cI\u2019m serious, Lorelei,\u201d she said after a moment. \u201cI have every confidence that you\u2019ll be a fine monarch. You are intelligent, resourceful, and you care more about your people\u2019s welfare than your own.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re going to do a great job, Lori,\u201d Dark Kimberly interjected from down the table.<br /> <br /> \u201cYes,\u201d White Maria cut in sardonically, \u201cI believe that\u2019s the high school drop-out version of what I just said.\u201d<br /> <br /> Calamity is right about those two. Whatever might be in their past, there\u2019s genuine affection beneath the hostility. I gave them my best smile, and quietly thanked <u>both</u> of them for their words of encouragement.<br /> <br /> So in the end it wasn\u2019t as bad as it could have been\u2026 y\u2019know, probably. Stasia\u2019s working on a piece for a local magazine about something that happened in Santa Barbara back in the late 70s. Apparently she\u2019s found snippets of video footage on the internet which points to a secretive cabal practicing ritual magic in the area at about that time. Based on the footage, it seems likely that their ritual involved a human sacrifice. The footage is degraded and fragmented, and she\u2019s been trying to piece together a complete picture of the event.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s more, of course. People have investigated this matter before, and though they didn\u2019t get very far in their attempt, it seriously freaked them out. Stasia says that the reporter who ran this story about twenty years ago disappeared quietly, and none of the magazine\u2019s other employees will touch the story or go anywhere near Santa Barbara. New footage recently surfaced on the internet that purports to fill in some of the gaps in the story, but Stasia is pretty certain that it\u2019s fake. There are also a few references online to genuine scenes from the original recording that do not appear in the most complete video that Stasia was able to construct, so it seems likely that there\u2019s more footage out there if one knows where to look.<br /> <br /> This also stirred something in my memory\u2026 something I\u2019d been told a couple of years ago just after I first arrived in Malibu. Something <u>did</u> happen in Santa Barbara back in the late 70s or early 80s, and nobody seems to know exactly what. Suffice to say that nobody has heard anything from any of the changelings who used to live there since that time, and no new changelings have settled in the area since. Changelings who pass through the city report that the area feels <u>wrong</u> somehow. So there\u2019s that lending credence to Stasia\u2019s story as well.<br /> <br /> So yes, of course Calamity and Jacob want to check it out and see what they can uncover. Aside from their natural curiosity, there\u2019s also the fact that Stasia might get hurt if she looks into this herself, and the two of them are particularly invested in her safety (come to that, I don\u2019t want anything to happen to the plucky photographer either). I\u2019ve sort of resolved to keep my nose out of it for the time being, though I have offered my advice on a few points. Chief among these contributions was the recommendation that they speak with Madame Spidertoes about whatever went down forty years ago, and that Calamity inform Charlotte of what she\u2019s doing.<br /> <br /> With that taken care of, I circulated a bit more amongst our other guests. I checked in with Moon and Dionysia before settling in with Desiree and Veronica. We chatted for a bit (the two of them were planning to go out with Rowan and Neon on Rowan\u2019s boat the next afternoon) before I turned up the flirtation. They\u2019d both been friendly enough before, and it was clear that they wouldn\u2019t mind including me in their fun that evening.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou want to come back to my place?\u201d Veronica asked as things wound down.<br /> <br /> \u201cSure, as long as you don\u2019t mind me bringing along my laptop and jumping on your wifi,\u201d I replied. \u201cI have online classes tomorrow morning.\u201d They had no problem with that, so I said a quick goodbye to Maria (who was planning to head over to Gloria\u2019s place after the show), threw on a few pieces of lacy lingerie under my traveling clothes, and headed for the door.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d almost made it out when Becky put a hand on my shoulder. \u201cJust give me a moment to get ready and I\u2019ll follow you out, my Queen,\u201d she said stolidly.<br /> <br /> I took in her expression, and then glanced up at Calamity, who had already pulled in her glass for the night. \u201cYou don\u2019t have to come with us, Becky,\u201d I said quietly. \u201cI\u2019ll be fine.\u201d<br /> <br /> She shook her head. \u201cIt\u2019s my duty,\u201d she maintained. \u201cI took an oath to protect the Queen. The Freehold\u2019s enemies would be foolish to attack you here at the Dream House, but while you\u2019re away with only one or two non-combatants around you\u2026 well, they might leap at the chance to destabilize the Freehold. So please give me a minute or two to get ready\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I sighed and turned toward my companions. \u201cSorry about this, but would you ladies mind a change of venue for tonight\u2019s festivities? Would it be okay with you if the three of us stayed here tonight?\u201d<br /> <br /> They both allowed as how that would be fine with them. Veronica even quipped sarcastically that neither of them had ever stayed the night at the Dream House before, so they might enjoy the novelty of it for a change. Becky gave me a grateful nod and made her way back to Calamity as the three of us ascended toward my boudoir.<br /> <br /> As usual, a very pleasant evening ensued, and I got up far too early so that I could do my online work for college, leaving my paramours slumbering in my bed, wrapped up in each other\u2019s arms. I was just finishing up when they wandered toward the staircase, speaking softly on their way to Sex Breakfast.<br /> <br /> \u201cAll I\u2019m saying is that you don\u2019t have to be embarrassed by it, Veronica,\u201d Desiree was telling the other girl softly. \u201cTake off the gloves; nobody\u2019s going to care about the burns.\u201d<br /> <br /> I decided to put in my two cents. \u201cShe\u2019s right, honey\u2026 you\u2019re beautiful, and you\u2019re among friends here. You don\u2019t have to hide anything from us.\u201d<br /> <br /> Veronica <u>did</u> take her gloves off, though she was clearly still uncomfortable with the idea of having her injuries out there for everyone to see. Still, it went well\u2026 nobody commented on her scars throughout breakfast, and she gradually relaxed as the talk wandered this way and that.<br /> <br /> Calamity had made good on her promise to speak with Jane the previous evening, and I think the conversation will be good for Jane. She\u2019s agreed to speak with her therapist about her predatory urges, and Calamity is going to try to help her find a constructive way to channel those impulses. Jane\u2019s going to start sparring with Calamity and Jacob (and me, if I can ever scrape together the time to take that up again). And Luna has offered to show her a few moves from a style she developed to take advantage of her limited flight abilities. Come to think of it, I might want to sit in on some of those lessons, too\u2026 one never knows when such skills might come in handy, and we Pilgrims must always strive to better ourselves in a wide variety of ways.<br /> <br /> At some point Julia started talking about becoming a mother, and that sparked something in my memory. I sidled up to Maria and Gloria and asked the former if she\u2019d made any progress in learning those body altering contracts from Marguerite. She indicated that she\u2019d mastered the relevant clauses with a nod. I asked if there was something she wanted to tell me, and she got this sort of look in her eye\u2026 like she wanted to use the contract and take me right there on the table, in front of everyone. Though of course that would have been wildly inappropriate\u2026 I confess that the exhibitionist in me was pretty damned turned on by the thought. In the end discretion won out, though, and we tabled the discussion for the time being.<br /> <br /> So Julia was asking which of us was likely to get pregnant first, and I made some noncommittal noises about how I was currently going to college (with the intention of eventually moving on to post-graduate medical studies) and shouldering a local political burden as well. I just don\u2019t think I\u2019d be able to devote the time and attention a child would deserve at the moment. As my school situation isn\u2019t likely to lighten up for at least eight to ten years, Julia will probably be the first of us to embark upon that particular journey.<br /> <br /> We also talked a bit more about Stasia\u2019s mystery video, and Calamity let us see the footage she had assembled and restored. Julia was able to shed a bit of light on what was going on\u2026 the people seemed to be doing something she referred to as \u201ccalling the corners.\u201d It\u2019s apparently a fairly common component of Wiccan ceremonies\u2026 but she also said that the people in the video didn\u2019t seem to be observing any religious rites. It was more like they were attempting to achieve a magical result without the trappings of any particular religion, like Hermetic Philosophers in the Middle Ages.<br /> <br /> She also confirmed that one of the people in the video could have been a human sacrifice. If so, she was probably willing, as she did not appear restrained or distressed in any way. If the process was as devoid of religious trappings as she says, the sacrifice probably served as a mystical battery of sorts, to boost the effect of whatever ritual they were performing in the first place. In some ways, I think that makes it even worse.<br /> <br /> One final note\u2026 one of the participants in the ritual almost certainly wasn\u2019t human. She was very tall \u2013 as tall as Julia or taller \u2013 but excruciatingly thin, and the way that she moved was subtly wrong\u2026 like she was attempting to emulate human movement without practicing it first. It\u2019s possible that this was an affectation to make her seem more dangerous and mysterious than she really was, of course\u2026 nah, on second thought, we\u2019re not that lucky.<br /> <br /> Calamity went out after breakfast to have her surgery and to speak with Charlotte and Spidertoes about the situation in Santa Barbara. The surgery went well; she had small amounts of the exotic particles in her brain, like Marguerite had, but they weren\u2019t organized or particularly active. Anton and Andromeda were able to remove them all within an hour or two, and let her leave with a clean bill of health shortly thereafter.<br /> <br /> Charlotte gave her blessing for Calamity to investigate Santa Barbara, but warned her to be cautious (insomuch as that is possible with Calamity). Spidertoes had a few more tidbits to share with Calamity about the situation, though she was careful to inform her that she didn\u2019t really <u>know</u> anything for certain. Santa Barbara is inaccessible from the local Hedge, for example, and Kindred are similarly averse to settling there. If it wasn\u2019t for the mysterious disappearance of all of the area\u2019s changelings at the same time, I might theorize that the magicians were simply warding the area against interference from supernatural creatures.<br /> <br /> After the rest of the breakfast crowd had dispersed, I found Maria in the theater, watching Missy and Jane rehearse a new number. \u201cSo,\u201d I said as I settled into her lap and slipped my arms around her neck, \u201cI believe there was something you wanted to tell me at breakfast?\u201d<br /> <br /> She looked at me and something started burning in her eyes. \u201cRight,\u201d she growled, and a minute later her underwear hit the floor, and mine followed suit. She\u2019s\u2026 really good at this new contract. Her new equipment was impressive but not ostentatious, and the sight of it set my loins ablaze. She took me right there on the table, unwilling to wait even another second to indulge her desires. We were not quiet. I don\u2019t know how long we kept it up, but I know that I peaked more than once. When we came up for air, Missy and Jane were nowhere to be seen.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat was\u2026 fun,\u201d I panted, pushing sweaty locks of hair out of my eyes.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re not\u2026 going to make me do that\u2026 every time, are you?\u201d she asked, pressing her body up against mine.<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course not,\u201d I said with a chuckle. \u201cI married\u2026 the greatest woman\u2026 on the planet, and she\u2019s all I want.\u201d I paused to kiss her, softly grope her once more completely feminine form, and let that sink in for a moment. \u201cStill, it might be fun every once in a while\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Maria laughed and pulled me into a tight embrace. After we\u2019d recovered, we got dressed and headed up to the media room to waste a bit of the afternoon before showtime. I\u2019ve been writing in this diary while we\u2019ve got some light-hearted series streaming on Netflix. Just the two of us. We\u2019re not fighting evil, or making love, or planning a show\u2026 we\u2019re just together, quietly enjoying each other\u2019s company. There hasn\u2019t been enough of that lately.<br /> <br /> I love my wife, and I thank God daily for bringing us together.<br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei de la Rocha</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Tonight has definitely been an interesting night. I went out to dinner with Stasia and Elena and heard the most interesting things. First off, I told Elena about the upcoming surgery and explained that it was a routine procedure and that I would be fine afterwards. I wasn\u2019t completely honest with her at that point. I had no sure way to tell if I would be alright., but I had hopes that I would be. I didn\u2019t want to unnecessarily upset my sister if I didn\u2019t have to.<br /> <br /> After that we talked about her wedding to Stasia. She was concerned about the reaction of most of the Russian Orthodox priests in the area. She was concerned because Stasia was not Russian Orthodox, and Ukrainian, <i>and </i>they were asking someone to conduct a gay wedding. I can understand the situation. The best I could do was suggest that they talk to Revered Wells and see if he had any suggestions for them. I wish that I had more advice to give to my sister, but I didn\u2019t. I gave up my religion when I entered the Lady\u2019s service. The closest that came to her was the Three Ladies. In Russian literature there is talk of the three sisters that had the purviews of morning, afternoon and midnight. That is the closest that I came to religion when I was in the Lady\u2019s service. Something so primal and guttural appealed to the Lady. So, I followed the Three Ladies, and worshipped the one and only Lady of the realm. She preferred it that way and at the time I was happy to oblige.<br /> After we were done talking about the wedding Stasia brought up another matter. She mentioned the fact that she was investigating a story that could possibly involve Changelings. An old story was brought to her attention and she decided to go after it. Apparently, there is footage of a ritual all over the internet in pieces. It is in at least four pieces. The footage that does exist shows rituals taking places and apparently the sacrifice of a young woman. She did not appear to be bound or anything though we could not rule out drugs.<br /> <br /> At the show Stasia motioned for Calamity to join us and she told her story of the ritual footage, most of which was supposed to have taken place in Santa Barbara. The thing that came to my mind when I thought of Santa Barbara was the fact that there were no Changelings in that city. The place was completely devoid of our kind and has been since the late 70\u2019s, early 80\u2019s. No one is completely sure what happened there, but there is consensus that something happened and the resident Changelings got out or disappeared entirely. Calamity mentioned that she would talk to Madame Spidertoes or Queen Charlotte about the whole affair and see if they knew anything about it. At some point we even called over Lori and told her what our plans were. She was carefully optimistic of our plans and warned us to be safe. She did want us to fully investigate the Santa Barbara thing and see if we could find out anything more before we actually went there. Her reasoning was that a lot of Changelings went missing there and we don\u2019t know what happened to them. She doesn\u2019t want the same thing to happen to us.<br /> <br /> What came up next was on a different topic. Calamity came to me and Luna asking if it was alright if Jane joined us for sparring in the mornings. Apparently Jane has been dealing with some issues of her own and needs to do something physical to work them out. I do not know specifically what is going on with her, but the fact that combat practice was brought up as a possible outlet is somewhat concerning. I know the in the beginning that Jane was not fond of Trinh. It is possible that Jane felt something predatory towards the other woman and needs to work out those feelings before she actually does something to Trinh. That is all fine with me as long as she does not harm our friend. I know that Jane is now a motley mate and that I should be more concerned about her welfare, but I am also concerned about Trinh and her well-being. There was also some talk about teaching Jane some flying and/or gliding combat tips. Calamity suggested that Luna might be able to do that. Luna seemed amenable to it, so I suppose that\u2019s all good. I know that it\u2019s probably moot to try and stifle any predatory predilections that Jane might have. The best we can do at this time is to point her in the right direction and hope for the best.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> And things just keep going. This morning at Sex Breakfast there was actually talk about sex, in particular fertilization of eggs. This led the ladies to discuss who would get pregnant first. Lori said that it would not be her because she still had to work on finishing her degree and she had responsibilities as the Spring queen. I\u2019m not sure where the others fell in that whole conversation. I intentionally didn\u2019t listen too closely since it was none of my business and it was a little embarrassing anyway.<br /> <br /> After that conversation the research that Stasia is doing came up. Stasia had sent the footage she had put together from the different pieces of the ritual to me and Calamity last night. So, Calamity showed Julia the footage this afternoon with the hopes that our resident Wiccan might recognize some of what was going on. In fact she did. She said that the people were calling the four corners (directions), and the footage showed them calling the North, East and South. The ritual itself was to make something called a cone of power. It sounds like they were trying to channel a whole lot of energy in to something or to do something. The question is what. Unfortunately the footage only shows the beginning and end of what they were doing. Not the middle part, which would explain what exactly their goal was. Julia also said that the ritual was ceremonial magic. There were no religious overtones at all. The disturbing pat of the videos is that at the end there is a young woman lying dead. One would guess that sacrificing a human life would generate a lot of energy or power. I just don\u2019t know what they were doing. Hopefully our research will bear fruit. Julia also pointed out that one of the women walking around in the videos, with the girl who gets sacrificed, doesn\u2019t move quite right for a human. She\u2019s not a Changeling though since we\u2019d be able to see that on the film. The other question is, what is she? On the positive side \u2013 I suppose it\u2019s positive \u2013 is that the young woman that gets sacrificed was not bound in any way. It appears to have been voluntary, though we can\u2019t rule out the possibility of her having been drugged. Julia said that she would ask her parents about the footage and see if they can find out anything more through their coven. As it turns out they don\u2019t have a copy of the tape but they have friends that do. They\u2019re going to try and borrow the vhs tape so we can watch it. Guess we\u2019ll need to find a VCR.<br /> <br /> Once we were done talking about human sacrifice we got onto the topic of regicide and what the reactions would be to our current monarchs getting killed. I think it was agreed that if Lori or Lowjack were killed their backups would take over after the initial shock. Lori has Jolie and Lowjack has Tamara. Queen Charlotte would be a different matter altogether though. If she were killed the consequences would be far reaching. There would be chaos in the Autumn court until they could find someone that fit all the requirements to manage the diverse group that is their court. Augustine doesn\u2019t have a successor either, but the job description for him is a little less involved than it is with Charlotte. Kind of a depressing conversation to have in the first place, but then it\u2019s not the strangest thing that we\u2019ve talked about in our motley.<br /> <br /> That conversation wrapped up and then it was time for Calamity\u2019s surgery. I drove her to the clinic since I wasn\u2019t sure if she\u2019d be okay to drive herself back afterwards. I knew from what Lori had said that they wouldn\u2019t fully sedate Calamity. They would just give her something to relax. Apparently you need to be conscious when they are doing brain surgery so they can get feedback from the patient. There are also no pain receptors in the brain, so it doesn\u2019t actually hurt. Small favors I guess. Anyway, Calamity came through the surgery with flying colors. They managed to remove all of the particles from her brain and she is good to go. She was still relaxed when they finished so it was good that I was there to drive her back to the house. The medication that they gave her didn\u2019t last long, so she was pretty much back to her usual self soon after we got home. After a fairly short time she left to go to the Lighthouse and talk to Madame Spidertoes and Queen Charlotte. I guess we\u2019ll find out what they have to say about the whole thing later.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXXXVII</i><br /> <br /> Not much mechanical to discuss. The Contract being thrown around for Reproductive Purposes is Mirrors.<br /> <br /> It should be noted that yes, it came up Wiccans don\u2019t sacrifice people. There was a bit of practical magic(k) discussed that mostly came up in Jacob\u2019s Journal (Calling Corners, Cone of Power, etc). Not a full Witchcraft 101 but concepts.<br /> <br /> Those who also enjoy <i>Balance of Shadows</i> will note that, yes, I did a story about an old film turning up there, too. This is not the same story. I just think the idea of something like that surfacing a mystery to investigate is a super neat idea I could not resist having come up. With that game done I have been debating moving Desiree (the police officer) to LA though.<br /> <br /> Speaking of other games, the Santa Barbra mystery has actually been referenced not only earlier in <i>Malibu Dream House</i> but <i>Night Train Detective Agency</i> and <i>Balance of Shadows. </i>Will the Last Dance Motley get to the bottom of it, or is this something different? Stick around and find out.<br /> <br /> Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 07-14-2019, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T17:18:31-07:00","id":1324581,"title":"","content":"So D is now a humanshifter par excellence?<br /> <br /> Niiiiiiiceee","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-28T14:02:37-07:00","id":1327960,"title":"","content":"Once again, Stasia has stirred the shadows of the past. What has stirred with them.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXXXVIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Well that certainly escalated quickly. The last day has seen several developments on the \u201cSanta Barbara ritual\u201d front, and we\u2019re currently getting ready to head there ourselves to take a look around and see what we can find out firsthand.<br /> <br /> So things started out well last night\u2026 the show was <u>exceptional</u>. On a lark, I decided to do something fun and asked Missy and Jane to join me on stage for a light-hearted rendition of Beyonc\u00e9\u2019s \u201cSingle Ladies.\u201d It was cool to just let go and have a ball on stage with my best friends\u2026 and we were able to use the lyrics to show off our respective engagement rings (okay, Jane\u2019s was a prop, since she bought the ring for Missy, but still). We probably got the best response we\u2019ve ever had from that number\u2026 when the lights came up, the whole house was quiet for a few seconds and then the applause was <u>deafening</u>. The glamour hit us like a tsunami\u2026 there was no way even all three of us together could absorb it all, and the effect was dizzying.<br /> <br /> So we were more than a little giddy as we left the stage to hobnob and mingle with the crowds. Well, actually\u2026 I left to hobnob while Missy and Jane went backstage to prep for their second number. The two of them came out about half an hour later and harmonized perfectly on a classic rendition of \u201cAfternoon Delight.\u201d I could tell that Missy at least was more than a little nervous about performing that song \u2013 I saw Jane run to the bar before they went on and get Missy a shot of something strong \u2013 and I can\u2019t really blame her for that.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t particularly like performing that song myself; and aside from that one time the three of us performed it together a couple of weeks ago (when I was trying to prove a point) I haven\u2019t sung it since 1978. I think a deep, superstitious part of me was always slightly afraid that it would attract the Stranger\u2019s attention again.<br /> <br /> It didn\u2019t happen, of course, though things did get\u2026 \u201cinteresting\u201d shortly after their second number. I\u2019d made my way up to a table shared by Dominika and Angelica, and we were chatting pleasantly about this and that when my attention was drawn to a table across the room. My attention was drawn to this table because it had just been flipped over violently\u2026 by Julia.<br /> <br /> It looked like she and Stasia had gotten into some sort of altercation, and it was clearly on the verge of becoming physical. Begging my companions\u2019 pardon, I excused myself and made my way across the room, noting as I went that Maria, Calamity and Jacob were also en route. Marguerite and Elena were already at the table trying to defuse the situation. When the rest of us got there, Calamity placed a soothing hand on Stasia\u2019s shoulder and I likewise gently restrained Julia. \u201cCalm down, both of you,\u201d I said gently but firmly. \u201cLet\u2019s take this somewhere more private so we can work whatever it is out.\u201d<br /> <br /> The group of us headed back to the kitchen to get to the bottom of things. Turns out that Julia had contacted her parents and a few other members of her coven on Stasia\u2019s behalf, hoping to help her with her current investigation. Her coven <u>does</u> have a copy of the videotape Stasia\u2019s looking into, and it seems to be a more complete version than the one Stasia\u2019s been able to compile from the clips available on the internet. But the coven considers it an important relic, and they\u2019re wary of letting outsiders view it.<br /> <br /> Julia was saying that she might be able to get Stasia permission to view the tape under supervision, but that she couldn\u2019t simply provide the tape itself for Stasia\u2019s use because it would be against her religion to give such an important relic away to an outsider (a \u201ccowan\u201d to use her word). Stasia was frustrated by this news, and made some sort of disparaging remark about the rules of Julia\u2019s religion, and\u2026 things escalated from there.<br /> <br /> It took a couple of minutes to calm them both down enough that they were willing to discuss the issue cordially, but I think we got there in the end. Stasia commented at one point that she takes issue with religious strictures of that sort because her parents justified kicking her out of their house as a requirement of their religion. I\u2026 can\u2019t even begin to guess how that must feel. I\u2019ve had a pretty rough life in some ways, but in others I\u2019ve been unusually blessed. Despite Dad\u2019s earlier fire-and-brimstone days, by the time I came out to him he was perfectly willing to accept me for who and what I am.<br /> <br /> Stasia also hinted that her parents found out about her romantic leanings thanks to a tip from Calamity\u2019s fetch. If I\u2019m interpreting the situation correctly, Calamity\u2019s \u201cSinister Bitch\u201d mailed them photos of Stasia being romantic with another girl. Calamity seemed pretty shaken up by this revelation, though she has no reason whatsoever to feel guilty for something her fetch did. I felt it would be best to drop the subject entirely at that time.<br /> <br /> In any case, Stasia apologized after speaking quietly with Calamity for a few minutes, and Julia accepted her apology. We talked it out for a bit to try to make it plain exactly what Stasia wants from the tape, and how it can be achieved, and why she wants it. Ideally she\u2019d like to take a physical copy of the videotape to the offices of the magazine which is currently employing her, so that she can run the tape itself through some machine or other and have the data recorded on it analyzed by a special computer program. She told us that the technicians who operate that machinery could almost certainly put the tape back together and return it without damaging it. Julia said she\u2019d take that information to the coven, assure them that the technicians wouldn\u2019t view the contents of the tape, and if necessary offer to let some of them be present for the whole process.<br /> <br /> Though Stasia would really like to obtain the tape itself, she was willing to accept these terms, and the two of them shook hands and seemed to be mostly okay with each other by the end of the night. I even saw Stasia approach Julia alone as we were closing up the club for the night and apologize again\u2026 it was unprompted and seemed very genuine. So here\u2019s hoping this trouble won\u2019t go any further.<br /> <br /> We returned to the floor after that, and I had to explain everything that had gone down to D, who had returned her customary post at the door when the rest of us went into the kitchen. \u201cNever thought Julia would be part of the first fight I\u2019d have to break up,\u201d she muttered with dark amusement.<br /> <br /> I had a few other conversations of note before we closed up for the evening. I\u2019d noticed early on that both Grendel and V from the L.A. Night Court were present for the performance, and that Calamity had spoken with them early in the evening. I made my way up to their table to see if they needed anything. It turned out that they were investigating the recent disturbances in Chinatown and wanted to know if we had any information for them.<br /> <br /> \u201cIf you already spoke with Calamity, you probably know as much as I do,\u201d I told them. \u201cThe Autumn Court might have more information, though\u2026 and they\u2019re our primary point of contact with the Courts of the Dragon, too. If you\u2019d like I can pass your contact information along to Queen Charlotte and ask her to give you a call.\u201d <br /> <br /> V thanked me for this kindness and produced a business card from somewhere, and I slipped off to make the necessary arrangements. I think Charlotte was a little surprised to hear from me, to be honest. I quickly explained the situation to her. \u201cAnd since you know more about this whole situation than I do, I thought you might be better suited to\u2026 regulate the flow of information,\u201d I said delicately.<br /> <br /> \u201cI appreciate the courtesy,\u201d she said, and sounded like she meant it. \u201cJust text me V\u2019s number after we disconnect and I\u2019ll take care of the rest.\u201d I did so, and I assume she contacted him later. Either way, it\u2019s out of my hands now.<br /> <br /> As things started to quiet down, I drifted to the Girlfriend Table and joined my various friends and lovers. Julia wanted to talk about the Dream House possibly playing host to an avant-garde act called the \u201cTinmen.\u201d Her parents thought they would be a good fit for our quirky little club. I\u2019m\u2026 not sure I concur with that assessment, but I\u2019ve agreed to listen to some of their music and consider it.<br /> <br /> According to Julia, the band is entirely composed of people who have been fairly badly burned. The urban legend is that they used to be a group of homeless people who were the victim of a cruel attack while they were staying under a bridge, but nobody seems to know if that\u2019s true or not. They play Theremins tuned to different frequencies, and they always perform in total darkness (it\u2019s a condition of their performance contracts). It could be an interesting change, and the cross-advertising might bring in some new business\u2026 but an act that only performs in total darkness is sort of antithetical to the mission statement of most burlesque houses. We\u2019ll see how it goes.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d been making not-so-subtle suggestions to my wife and various other regular lovers as the evening wore on, so I was not particularly surprised when the six of us (Missy, Jane, Maria, Julia, Marguerite, and myself) retired to my bedroom together after the doors had been shut and the lights turned off. There was some good-natured joking about how we were going to have to reinforce the bed before too long. At least, I think it was joking. Honestly, I should probably have Andromeda come by and take a look at it\u2026 she did wonders with making that cross in the basement impervious to Maria\u2019s super-strength, and my poor California King is starting to groan occasionally when all six of us get frisky on it at the same time.<br /> <br /> But that was a problem for another day (note to self\u2026 do not put that problem off until it becomes immediate). Last night I was content to allow myself to be ravaged until I passed out from pure bliss. As usual, I did my share of ravishing as well, of course, and I flatter myself that I wasn\u2019t the only one to lose consciousness due to an overload of pleasure.<br /> <br /> I was, however, the only one to have to get up early the next morning for college classes (though more than half of my bedmates had to get up slightly later for counseling). Becky and I drove into L.A. together, and as usual she hung around the quad sipping coffee and flirting with various students while I attended two lectures and a lab. Traffic was a bear on the way back, so we actually missed most of Sex Breakfast.<br /> <br /> We weren\u2019t the only ones who were out and about this morning, of course. Maria, Calamity, Jacob, Missy and Jane all went to therapy, and it sounds like they made some good progress. Missy and Jane stayed behind for a bit to speak with Jane\u2019s therapist together; I\u2019m guessing that means that Jane was true to her word and discussed her predatory urges with him, and I can only see that as a step in the right direction. <br /> <br /> Jacob, of course, had his surgery today. I know he wasn\u2019t looking forward to the experience, but he met it with his typical stoicism, and Calamity stuck around to reassure him that everything was on the up and up. They found some of the particles in his brain, but not many, and they were able to remove them without further incident. Now if only we knew what to <u>do</u> with these particles now that they\u2019ve been extracted we could put the whole incident to rest.<br /> <br /> It looks like for the most part, conversations at breakfast were centered around the mysterious video and whatever had happened in Santa Barbara forty years ago. The others were happy to catch us up on things. Julia had managed to upload the video to the cloud and get Stasia access to it, so I guess things between them have settled down a bit.<br /> <br /> Julia\u2019s parents had viewed the footage again, and come up with a few more clues for us. For example, most of the scenes aside from those where the actual ritual was taking place included at least one Theban rune, which I gather is a sort of secret alphabet employed by magicians. This rune might be scratched into a wall, or scorched into the floor, or reflected in a mirror, or what have you. They\u2019d worked on translating the runes, but thus far they\u2019d had no luck in teasing any sense out of them. Maybe if the footage was placed in the proper order\u2026<br /> <br /> But having said that, Julia\u2019s dad is pretty convinced that the order of the footage <u>itself</u> is in some way important, like it\u2019s been arranged in that order deliberately as some sort of code. Who knows?<br /> <br /> We called a few other local experts to see if they had any input. First, Calamity contacted Viktor in L.A. to ask what he knew about kindred affairs in Santa Barbara. I think he was a little annoyed at her for waking him up in the early afternoon, but he still passed along a lot of interesting (and troubling) new information. He doesn\u2019t know what happened in Santa Barbara in the 70s, but whatever happened, it was bad for the area\u2019s kindred. Apparently there\u2019s a sort of cult among vampires that operates as a hive mind. No one can read their thoughts; all you get is a Roman numeral if you try. And pretty much every vampire in the area became a part of that cult when this went down. The area\u2019s kindred don\u2019t go there anymore.<br /> <br /> Jacob called John to get his thoughts on the subject, too. Lowjack didn\u2019t have a lot of new info for us, but he shared his own experiences in Santa Barbara. He looked into the disappearances around the time that they happened, but didn\u2019t turn much up. While he was there, he had the uncanny feeling that he was being watched\u2026 like, the whole time.<br /> <br /> I called my dad, figuring that he might have heard something about the incident during his years with the Long Night, as the incident so profoundly affected the vampires that were their prey. He sort of wryly informed me that he was not currently fighting hopping vampires as he greeted me, and I had to chuckle at that. Once I\u2019d explained the situation, he hummed in thought for a moment.<br /> <br /> \u201cI do recall something of that situation, though I was not in the area at that time,\u201d he said. \u201cIt was either late 1978 or early 1979, I seem to recall. There was an outbreak of madness in the Santa Barbara area\u2026 a large number of people were committed to a local mental institution. The Long Night investigated at the time, but did not uncover anything useful. I believe the madhouse was shut down in the 80s, but the structure is still standing.\u201d<br /> <br /> I thanked him for the information and we said our goodbyes. I took this information to the others, and a quick search on the internet proved that dad was right: the old asylum is still standing, but has been sitting empty for some time. Apparently it\u2019s a favorite site for urban exploring, though the websites warned that the place had a bad reputation. It\u2019s supposed to be haunted. With everything we\u2019ve seen over the past few years, we\u2019re taking the rumors seriously. Plus\u2026 the websites also mentioned that at least two urban explorers had disappeared while investigating that place.<br /> <br /> The good news is that the paper files and records are still in the hospital itself according to multiple reports. The bad news is that they\u2019re in the basement, which is pitch black and supposedly haunted by something known as \u201cthe Crawler,\u201d a human-sized creature which skitters along the ceilings and preys upon the unwary. Joy. The site is also protected by more mundane measures; there\u2019s a high fence around the property and a security guard on duty 24/7.<br /> <br /> We conferred briefly about how to proceed, and quickly decided that there was no time like the present to investigate a spooky abandoned mental institution. It\u2019s Thursday, so tonight\u2019s show should be able to cope without us. We don\u2019t have college or therapy in the morning, so if we get held up out of town we won\u2019t miss too much. And I think we all want to at least begin our exploration while it\u2019s still light outside\u2026 even the darklings agreed to that stipulation. I did see Becky sort of clench up when I started talking about how \u201cwe\u201d should probably head out\u2026 I know it\u2019s not common for a monarch to take such a direct role in things like this, but I can\u2019t let my friends head into danger alone. I\u2019m just not wired that way. <br /> <br /> I confess that I couldn\u2019t resist having a little fun with her, and I mock-ordered her to stay behind and guard the Dream House while the rest of us went to Santa Barbara. She must have seen the twinkle in my eye, because she just sort of crossed her arms, squared her shoulders, and said \u201cno way.\u201d Of course I was joking; I\u2019d have <u>begged</u> her to come along if she hadn\u2019t clearly been inclined to do so anyway.<br /> <br /> So now we\u2019re getting dressed and gathering up our weapons and generally getting ready to enter the fray. Jacob has been overseeing the packing, making recommendations about what we should take with us and how we should arrange our packs. He strongly advised us all to bring breathing masks, as the place might be chock-full of asbestos insulation\u2026 but I put my foot down when it came to Maria. I don\u2019t want her wandering around an abandoned hospital with a face mask on. I\u2019d rather risk the respiratory damage in her case.<br /> <br /> I sincerely hope that this place is just what it appears to be\u2026 a creepy old abandoned asylum. But who am I kidding? We\u2019re never that lucky.<br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei de la Rocha</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Tonight was not what I was expecting it to be. The show went really well. I mean, more so than usual. It went REALLY well, at least according to the audience it did. I will admit that it went better than most shows, but I\u2019m not a great critic on what is good and bad according to the masses. I thought it was good anyway. Anyhoo, I talked to Lowjack while part of the show was going on. He said that he had dealings with folks in Santa Barbara during the time I was asking about. He said that he had to clean up a lot of messes with teamsters that had suddenly left the area. He knew that the local Changelings had left, but no evidence pointed towards a mass disappearance. At least there were no reported mass disappearances of people from that area during that time. I suppose that is good. The people in question didn\u2019t go missing, they just legitimately left the area or were otherwise accounted for.<br /> <br /> So, at the show the ladies did really well. Lori and her friends from Iowa did a song called \u201cSingle Ladies.\u201d It was really well received, as I said earlier. Not long after their show there was a disturbance in the audience area. Julia threw a drink at Stasia and overturned a table in front of the other woman. Apparently she had been upset by something that Stasia had said about her religion. It seems that Stasia had called Julia\u2019s religion LARP\u2019ing and had implied that it was nothing more than roleplaying. We all gathered at the table in question and decided to take the conversation behind closed doors. We talked about differences in religion and that Wiccan was not LARP\u2019ing. We eventually came to the point of the conversation which was the video tape. Calamity talked to Stasia privately for a moment or two and then we all got back together in the kitchen. We discussed options for viewing the tape. I suggested that the coven come to where Stasia\u2019s equipment was to view the tape if it was not possible to bring Stasia\u2019s equipment to the coven. We agreed that it was important that the tape in question not be damaged in any way since it was still important to the coven. We have the cloud share version, but apparently it\u2019s not the same as viewing the actual tape. <br /> <br /> Once the conversation was over, I went out to talk to Elena. She said that she understood where Stasia was coming from. As did I. Stasia had given up her religion when her parents kicked her out of the house for the crime of being gay. They had cited their religion as the reason that her lifestyle was wrong in the first place. Elena didn\u2019t quite understand why Stasia would go so far. She had not denounced her religion when mom and dad had decided to reject her based on her personal choices. She knew that they were likely citing their religion as the reason why they rejected her relationship with Stasia, but she had not given up her faith in response. I guess it\u2019s just a matter of personal choice. I\u2019m glad that Elena didn\u2019t decide to turn her back on the faith. I know it means a lot to her. It meant a lot to me when I was younger. I wouldn\u2019t want her to have to deal with the loss of our family as well as the loss of her religion. I know it\u2019s something that she turns to when things get tough. <br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Today was the big day. We all went to therapy. Me, Calamity, Missy, Jane and De la Rocha. That part went fine. Well, to be honest it all went fine, but I was still nervous about the whole thing. After therapy it was my turn to have surgery to remove the foreign particles from my brain. As it turns out there were fewer in my brain than in Calamity or Insincere Marguerite but still some there that needed to be taken care of. Obviously I came through the surgery okay, otherwise I would not be writing this journal. I am loathe to admit that Twitch did an okay job on my brain surgery. Damn, just saying it like that. I can\u2019t believe that I let him into my head. It all turned out okay though, so I\u2019m not too upset. I still don\u2019t trust him as far as I can throw him. I\u2019m sure it was all made better by the fact that Andromeda was there. <br /> <br /> After all that was done we went back to the house to discuss things. The main thing that we needed to talk about was the video of the ritual. Julia\u2019s parents were able to get a copy of the VHS tape so we could view it. It is still out of order, but we discussed borrowing it so we could run it through Stasia\u2019s machine and get a more refined copy of the video. The order on the VHS tape is still off though. We are unsure why, but figure it is probably to cover their intention or it is set up as a riddle of sorts. Maybe putting the ritual in order will actually make something magical happen if it is replayed. We don\u2019t know. I brought up the inhuman woman in the video. Perhaps she was influencing things in some way? She seems to be in most of the shots in any case. Hopefully we\u2019ll find something useful by viewing the whole video. I\u2019m sure that it must be more informative than the footage Stasia has accrued so far, but we still don\u2019t know for sure. Here\u2019s hoping.<br /> <br /> After we had that discussion Lori said that she would talk to her father about what happened in Santa Barbara in the late 70\u2019s/early 80\u2019s. She got back to us rather fast after talking to her dad and he said that a whole bunch of people were committed to a mental hospital around that time. The hospital itself still stands but has since been abandoned. It is said that the paper records of that time still remain on the hospital grounds, but that they are in cabinets in the basement. The problem is that the basement and other dark areas of the hospital are home to \u201cthe Crawler.\u201d Apparently s/he crawls along the ceiling of the hospital basement and touches the head or shoulders of those that come that far down. That obviously piqued everyone\u2019s interest, in a good or bad way. The place is also said to be haunted. It might be the work of this \u201cCrawler,\u201d but I don\u2019t know for sure. There might be some legitimate ghosts in that place. Lucky for us Calamity is good with dealing with ghosts. I\u2019m fine with the real-life physical threats. I\u2019ll leave the incorporeal ones to her.<br /> <br /> Lucky me, we\u2019re going there this afternoon. I don\u2019t know if I\u2019m looking forward to this or not. I\u2019ll make sure to pack several flashlights and glow sticks. I also suggested based on the age of the place that we pack face masks in case of asbestos. Lori took me aside and asked if I was seriously asking De la Rocha to go into an abandoned hospital wearing a face mask. I allowed that she had a point and that asking De la Rocha to wear a mask might be a triggering event for her. I still think that face masks would be a good idea though, but De la Rocha doesn\u2019t need to wear one. We just need to be careful of kicking up any white dust. Here goes nothing. Wish me luck. <br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXXXVIII</i><br /> <br /> Lorelei, backed by her best friends, got 73 success on her performance. 74 with the Spring Court.<br /> <br /> Okay, so this touches on Wicca and Ceremonial Magic a fair bit, which I tried to treat with appropriate respect given none of are in fact Wiccan. I am fairly well read on the subject so I felt like I did okay. Julia is Gardnerian, so very\u2026testy\u2026about secrets of the Coven. (None of us are Catholic, Orthodox or Jewish, either, and I have tried to approach those similarly respectfully when they became plot relevant). Obviously Stasia\u2019s words don\u2019t represent my opinions etc. I think it is useful to learn about other faiths, and as an amateur theologian, I try to represent them fairly.<br /> <br /> I think that covers the concepts. Comments and Questions are welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-28T18:08:23-07:00","id":1327994,"title":"","content":"Roman Numerals eh...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-11T14:18:46-07:00","id":1330444,"title":"","content":"The Motley goes exploring an Abandoned Sanatorium outside Santa Barbra. I am sure it will be quiet and nothing exciting will happen.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXXXIX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> That was terrifying\u2026 one of the most harrowing experiences of my life. I\u2019m not sure if it was intrinsically more frightening than the Bulgarian facility, but due to\u2026 certain circumstances, that place had me far closer to the edge of terror than I\u2019ve been since\u2026 well, since we went back to Arcadia, I guess.<br /> <br /> So following my last entry, the nine of us got dressed and packed for urban exploring and piled into the van together. It was me, Maria, Marguerite, Julia, Calamity, Jacob, Luna, Becky, and Stasia (who Calamity insisted must come along, and who frankly would have just followed us on her own anyway if we\u2019d tried to make her stay behind). The ride out there took almost two hours, most of it spent driving along the Pacific Coast Highway. Calamity and I swapped stories about racing along that street (though in my case it was more of a high-speed chase than a race), and I spent a lot of the trip singing along with the radio. I even got to do that thing where we went into a tunnel and lost the radio station for a minute, and I kept pace with the song so that we were still synced up when we exited the tunnel.<br /> <br /> It was edging on toward late afternoon when we arrived on the outskirts of Santa Barbara. We were not in the city itself, and as such we did not experience any supernatural feelings of being watched or anything like that\u2026 but the place was creepy enough without any help. We parked around the back of the building, on the opposite side from the security guard\u2019s post. The whole complex was surrounded by a high chain link fence, but it was obvious that the guards weren\u2019t the most vigilant of sentries.<br /> <br /> Most of my companions clambered over the fence without much trouble, though Luna and I opted to fly over instead. I also took pity on Julia. She\u2019s never been the most athletic of ladies, and even though she\u2019d consented to wear pants on this expedition instead of one of her typical long skirts I could tell that the fence was going to give her trouble. So I carried her over in my arms. As we began to descend, I thought I heard her whisper \u201ccan you read my mind?\u201d Not sure what that was about.<br /> <br /> We circled carefully around the outside of the building, scoping out the possible points of ingress. One window was open, and a power cord dangled out of it, though none of us were particularly optimistic about it supporting our weight. I flew up to scope things out, and found that the cord was attached to a surge protector, which in turn was connected to an old-model television (though none of this was actually connected to any power source that I could see). The room also contained a bed with associated linens\u2026 and the bed was made. The room looked like it had seen recent use.<br /> <br /> We opted to enter at a different window; one that overlooked a large storage bin (there were no windows on the ground floor, which I suppose makes sense for an asylum). It wasn\u2019t difficult to climb on top of the bin, climb up a short distance along the wall (a single foothold had been helpfully gouged out of the masonry) and slip in through an open second-story window. Of course, once again Luna and I just flew up there as per usual and slipped in behind the rest of the party.<br /> <br /> Here\u2019s where things start getting a little weird. So as soon as we were all in the room, we started noticing things flickering and flashing on the edges of our peripheral vision. It was distracting, and the temptation to try to track the movement was insidious. Several of us (namely myself, Calamity, and Jacob) gave in to the temptation and turned toward the strange will-o-the-wisp lights.<br /> <br /> We immediately found ourselves in the same hospital, and yet not the same. It was lit, and inhabited, and clearly still in operation. Though we could see and communicate with each other, there was no sign of our other friends. A nurse approached us, told us that visiting hours were over, and asked to see our visitor\u2019s badges, but I managed to talk her down, and she walked away pushing an orderly\u2019s cart as she went.<br /> <br /> It soon became clear to us that we were still physically in the abandoned asylum; we could feel gentle taps and tugs on our clothing as our friends tried to communicate with us. Eventually I realized that someone was using Morse code and started jotting down a series of dots and dashes. Calamity remembered how to translate it\u2026 well, she remembered <u>enough</u> in any case; she and Stasia had learned it as kids so they could communicate in secret. She translated a brief message communicating our friends\u2019 anxiety about our state. They could hear us when we spoke, but stated that we were for the most part just standing around gazing blankly at whatever was in front of us.<br /> <br /> After a few minutes of this Calamity suggested that we try using meditation techniques to focus our perception on reality. It wasn\u2019t easy; that hallucination was pretty damned persistent, but after a few moments of closing my eyes and regulating my breathing I found myself back with my friends in the present. Most of them expressed relief that we had returned to them. After a moment I noticed that Julia was holding Maria\u2019s wrist. My wife was silent and subdued, but gave my hand a squeeze when we returned to ourselves. She was obviously reverting at least a little bit, but her pupils hadn\u2019t dilated, she wasn\u2019t skulking in the shadows, and she didn\u2019t try to shy away from me. Maria had come to the surface, but D was still there. And I smiled, kissed her, and let her know that I loved both aspects of her.<br /> <br /> Once we\u2019d regrouped we decided to head for the stairs and make our way down to the ground floor. We passed an orderly\u2019s cart as we approached the stairs\u2026 and it was moving back and forth with the wind, mimicking the motions of the cart in our shared hallucination. The sparks and flashes on the edges of our vision intensified as we entered the lobby, and those among us who had not already succumbed to the otherworldly visions found themselves driven to distraction by the visual pyrotechnics. Calamity suggested that they try a few meditation techniques, and that seemed to reduce their irritation to manageable levels.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately we weren\u2019t given a lot of time to look around. There was an unearthly scream, and Calamity \u2013 who had used her contract to be able to see and hear ghosts, and had inadvertently included Stasia in the effect \u2013 told us that a spectral girl rushed past us and fled up the stairs. Reevaluating our strategy, we decided to pursue her upstairs and see if we could learn anything from her.<br /> <br /> Luna had brought a walkie-talkie, and managed to find the frequency used by the security guards. The guard on duty noted the disturbance in the asylum, but apparently strange sights and sounds aren\u2019t unusual in that building, and he indicated that he wasn\u2019t going to enter the building to investigate it.<br /> <br /> We followed the sound of the ghost girl\u2019s yells until we found her, though only Stasia and Calamity could actually see her. With a bit of patience and an effort to reassure the ghost girl that we meant her no harm we were able to glean a bit more about the asylum itself and its tragic history. She said that her name was Holly, and that she had been committed to the hospital while she was still alive. Her information was incomplete (and possibly not terribly reliable), but it was still more than we\u2019d had before we spoke with her.<br /> <br /> Holly told us that there were bad things on \u201cthe lower levels,\u201d implying that there was more than one basement or sub-basement. She also told us that \u201csomething bad\u201d had happened upstairs, on either the third floor or in the attic. She didn\u2019t know exactly what this \u201csomething bad\u201d was, but she told us that it had something to do with a woman who had magma for eyes. Her description of this woman bore a striking resemblance to the strange thin woman we\u2019d seen on Stasia\u2019s video footage. Holly offered the opinion that whatever the \u201csomething bad\u201d was, it was what was keeping her spirit tied to the hospital. She was unable to do anything about it herself, however. Most of us took pity on the poor girl, and we unanimously decided to head upstairs to see if we could do anything to help her find the rest she\u2019s earned.<br /> <br /> Holly either wouldn\u2019t or couldn\u2019t join us upstairs, but told us that whatever \u201csomething bad\u201d had happened up there had happened in a secret chamber of some sort. Stasia looked at the maps she\u2019d brought along and found two possible locations for such a chamber. We found a door into the first space in the back of a closet. The room inside didn\u2019t tell us much; everything inside it had been burned to a charred, blackened mess. Though we have no way to be certain, it seemed likely that someone had set the fire specifically to conceal evidence of some past misdeeds.<br /> <br /> The second secret room provided a bit more fuel for our speculation. We found the remains of a young man\u2026 presumably the urban explorer who had been lost in the hospital, as the body was only a year or two old. He looked like he had hanged himself, though he may have had help with that. Though I found no evidence of defensive wounds on the body, it was obvious that his hands had been bound at the time of death.<br /> <br /> The ceiling of this room had partially collapsed, allowing access to the attic space above. Maria became very agitated as we entered this room, and began gently trying to pull away from me\u2026 not like she was attempting to escape my grasp, but more like she had spotted something and was eager to investigate it. \u201cMaria,\u201d I said softly, and she turned to regard me seriously. \u201cI\u2019m going to let you go, because I trust your instincts in this place. But please don\u2019t go far\u2026 I need you. Okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. I released her hand, and she scampered up into the attic. The rest of us followed. We found the remnants of a large ritual circle up there along with several more bodies, though these had obviously been dead for much longer. We also found a large number of bullet holes in the walls of the chamber, implying that those bodies had died through violence rather than as part of some magical ritual. While we were looking around, Maria found the source of her agitation, and tackled someone that the rest of us could not see.<br /> <br /> Our unseen observer turned out to be one Cara, a vampire who believed that she was a mouse. Once we\u2019d convinced her that we did not mean her any harm, she was friendly enough. She was able to fill in a few of the blanks about what had happened back in the 70s and 80s. She remembered the \u201cbad people\u201d doing a ritual back then, and whatever they did was indeed responsible for converting the area\u2019s kindred to that strange hive-mind cult. She was not affected by the ritual because the hospital itself was apparently warded against supernatural influences of that sort. As she had only left the hospital for brief feeding periods in all of the intervening time, she wasn\u2019t certain what had happened to the area since\u2026 though she speculated that something had gone wrong with the ritual, as the original perpetrators no longer seemed to be around.<br /> <br /> When we asked about the woman with the magma eyes, Cara confirmed that she had been a part of the rituals in the hospital, though she had never perceived the woman to have lava for eyes. She also confirmed that the basement levels were incredibly dangerous, though she expressed those dangers in terms of \u201ccats.\u201d But she told us that not everything in the basement was dangerous... apparently the Crawler \u2013 which she called \u201cNathan\u201d \u2013 is merely mischievous and likes scaring people. She also mentioned a friend named Dave, who is apparently a cockroach. I asked if he was a real cockroach or a metaphorical one, but she didn\u2019t seem to understand the question.<br /> <br /> So while we were questioning Cara, a few of us detected the sound of someone coming up the stairs. I kept Maria with me while Marguerite went to check the noise out. A few moments later I caught sight of Marguerite\u2019s arm beckoning me from around the corner. My heart dropped like a stone, but of course I headed for the stairwell like a shot. I had a horrible feeling that I knew what I would find there.<br /> <br /> \u201cDad?\u201d I asked incredulously. Sure enough, there he was, wearing his cassock-and-body-armor ensemble, wielding a shotgun with a flashlight taped to the barrel.<br /> <br /> \u201cHello, Juliette,\u201d he said with a slight smile.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat the f\u2026\u201d I began, then had the presence of mind to self-censor. \u201cWhat are you doing here?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCome now, Juliette,\u201d he said with maddening calm, \u201csurely you did not expect me to sit at home and do nothing when I knew you were venturing into a dangerous supernatural hotspot such as this?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cUh, yeah,\u201d I said, inexplicably fifteen again. \u201cKinda did, Dad. I\u2019m a grown woman; protecting me isn\u2019t your job anymore. Technically it\u2019s Becky\u2019s, and she\u2019s here <u>doing</u> that job. You\u2026 don\u2019t take this the wrong way, but you\u2019re not a young man anymore, and I can\u2019t lose you\u2026 not again.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI might say the same thing about you, Juliette,\u201d he replied softly. \u201cAnd besides, I am your father. It will <u>always</u> be my job to protect you.\u201d He turned and began walking down the hallway with the air of someone who had concluded his conversation beyond the shadow of a doubt. I had no choice but to follow him. I honestly did not know that he still had the capacity to infuriate me like that. It reminded me of my teenage years in Defiance\u2026 which was paradoxically kind of nice.<br /> <br /> In any case, back with Cara the others had managed to put together a few more things. The warding spell that protected the asylum from whatever the big ritual was had required a human sacrifice, and based on what Cara told us about the process it seemed logical to assume that Holly had been that sacrifice. She was bound to the premises by the magic, and Julia thought that if we managed to free her spirit the protection spell would fail.<br /> <br /> That being the case\u2026 we offered to take Cara with us when we left. It seemed like the only decent thing to do. The poor girl has been relying upon the protection offered by the spell for more than thirty years, and her isolation has clearly taken its toll upon her (well\u2026 maybe\u2026 we don\u2019t actually know how crazy she was <u>before</u> the isolation). We discussed a few options, including using Dad\u2019s contacts to find her a new safe haven and handing her over to our kindred contacts in L.A. Pretty much anything would be better than leaving her there.<br /> <br /> So there was nothing for it after that but to venture down into the basement at last. It was pitch black down there, and most of us opted to wear glow-sticks around our necks so that we could find each other easily if we got incapacitated and separated (Marguerite demurred, and as she was our forward scout and stealth expert, it was hard to argue with her reasoning on that point). It wasn\u2019t hard to find the records room\u2026 but I don\u2019t think any of us had fully appreciated the difficulty of the task set before us until we saw it for ourselves. The room was a shambles, with papers strewn all over the floor with no rhyme or reason to their location.<br /> <br /> We were in that room for several hours total. After about an hour I\u2019d managed to locate Holly\u2019s file, and Jacob had found Cara\u2019s. Both suffered from some form of paranoid delusions according to the attending psychiatrists, though we posited that in Holly\u2019s case it was possible that she was <u>actually</u> seeing supernatural creatures that others simply couldn\u2019t recognize. The file also recorded the fact that she\u2019d had a child while in the asylum and recorded the details of the girl\u2019s later adoption. Dad posited that reuniting Holly with her lost daughter might help to resolve whatever issues are binding her spirit to the mortal plane, so we kept the file for later reference.<br /> <br /> It took more than an hour more to sort the pile of files by date of admission, but we eventually managed to find what we had originally come for\u2026 a week in early 1979 in which almost a dozen new patients were admitted with similar symptoms, diagnosed for the most part as schizophrenia. Their files had addresses and the details of the incidents which led to them being committed, so we have a few more avenues of investigation open to us now. Hopefully this will help us track down some residue or remnant of the ritual that caused all of this madness.<br /> <br /> The whole time that we were going through the files nothing happened\u2026 but as we were making our way back to the stairs, Maria became very agitated. She took hold of my arm and started pulling me urgently toward the stairs\u2026 not like she was trying to get away from me, but more like she <u>really</u> wanted me to get out of that basement as quickly as possible. After a few seconds of this we heard a rushing sound, which got louder and louder as whatever it was approached us. Finally the rushing resolved into a series of overlapping babbling voices. Only Calamity and Stasia could see the creature due to her earlier use of contracts\u2026 and I\u2019m not sorry about that even a little bit. Calamity described it as a sort of conglomeration of spirits bound together by unearthly forces\u2026 but spared us any further details. Since we already had what we had come for we fled before it and retreated back up the stairs.<br /> <br /> So all that was left after that was to gather up Cara and head out of the facility. Before we left, Dad had Calamity use her contracts again so that he could speak directly with Holly. He promised to do what he could for the poor girl, and begged her to be patient for a few more days while he looked into the matter. A short climb down from the second story later and we were ready to depart.<br /> <br /> Maria and I opted to ride back to the Dream House in Dad\u2019s car, partly so that Cara wouldn\u2019t be too crowded in the van but mostly so that we\u2019d have the chance to talk. And as we got further and further from Santa Barbara, two things happened.<br /> <br /> First, Maria came back to herself and became more talkative. I think this little excursion was good for the two of us. I think she was able to get in touch with the dark parts of herself that she keeps hidden from the world, and she realized that those parts have their place within her. She used the gifts the Hospital had given her to keep us safe and to help us reach our goals. And this time I wasn\u2019t afraid of her\u2026 and I wasn\u2019t even afraid <u>for</u> her. I was glad when she started talking to me again\u2026 but I never doubted that she would even for a second.<br /> <br /> Second, my irritation at Dad faded as we got further from the danger that the asylum represented. I started to really think about what he had done and <u>why</u> he had done it, and I found it hard to stay mad at him. I mean\u2026 my Dad cares enough about me to put himself in that sort of a situation just to make sure that I\u2019m safe. And while I\u2019d still prefer that he not place himself in jeopardy on my account\u2026 I\u2019d do exactly the same thing for him, and it\u2019s heartwarming to realize that we have that sort of relationship.<br /> <br /> So as we sped along the dark Pacific Coast Highway getting closer to home, I gently pulled away from my wife\u2019s arms, leaned forward, and placed a hand on Dad\u2019s shoulder. \u201cDad?\u201d I said quietly.<br /> <br /> \u201cYes, Juliette?\u201d he responded, sounding tired but resolute.<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks for looking out for me,\u201d I said, giving his shoulder a squeeze. \u201cI may not approve of you taking on risks like this, but\u2026 thanks. I love you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI love you too, Juliette,\u201d he replied, reaching back with his own hand and giving mine a pat. I leaned back after a moment and allowed a smiling Maria to kiss my happy tears away.<br /> <br /> And honestly, I can\u2019t think of anything else that needs to be said.<br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei de la Rocha</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Well today was one hell of a day as it turns out. We went to the abandoned hospital to explore. It was me, Luna, Lori, De la Rocha, Insincere Marguerite, Julia, Calamity, Becky and Stasia. We all piled into the van and headed out. Before that though we packed for the upcoming adventure. We made sure to pack flashlights, glowsticks, chalk and markers, rope and water. Marguerite also brought along a mirror big enough for each of us to climb through should the need arise. Thankfully it didn\u2019t, but it was a near thing.<br /> <br /> So, we got to the hospital and parked around back, opposite of where the security guard was stationed. We then looked for a way in. In the process we found an outdoor extension cord hanging out of an open window. Lori flew up to find out what was up and discovered that the power cord was plugged into a power strip and a television. The end on the ground wasn\u2019t plugged into anything so I\u2019m not sure where or if the person that was staying there got power. Yeah, there was someone staying in the room. There was a bed all made up and the place was relatively clean. Lori flew back down. We couldn\u2019t go in that way, so we found another way in through a second story window. We climbed up on an adjacent shed to get in. It looked like others had used the same entrance over the years, so we followed suit. Once inside we noticed that there was a sort of light just at the edges of our vision. Everyone saw this except Stasia so we figured it was a Changeling thing. We also heard wheels moving down the hall outside the room we found ourselves in. At the same time Calamity, Lori and I gave into temptation and concentrated on the light. We then found ourselves in a well-lit, clean and in use hospital. There was a nurse in front of us asking for our visitor passes. It was as if we\u2019d been transported back in time. I let Lori and Calamity do the talking. If we had actually found ourselves in the 1980\u2019s it would not look good for one of our number to be speaking with a Russian accent. Calamity eventually convinced the nurse that we were with the government and she left us alone.<br /> <br /> Not long after that Lori said that she felt someone gently pulling on her hair and we figured it was probably the others trying to get our attention. This put to rest the idea that we\u2019d actually been transported in time. Lori noticed that there were taps coming in patterns and figured out that it was Morse code. Stasia and Calamity apparently knew Morse code when they were younger. We translated most of the message and discovered that we hadn\u2019t gone anywhere. They said that we were just standing around, though they could hear us when we talked. Calamity suggested that we all meditate to bring ourselves back to reality, and a few minutes later we had all centered ourselves enough to do just that. We investigated the sound that we\u2019d heard from the hallway and discovered that there was a cart moving of its own accord back and forth in the hall. Stasia insisted that it was the wind, but we had seen the nurse also pushing a cart. Calamity then decided to see if there was a ghost pushing it and activated her ghost sight. She accidentally included Stasia in the power and neither of them saw anything pushing the cart. So, apparently it was just the wind. How mundane.<br /> <br /> Just to be complete we checked the room that had the power cord coming out of it and found just what Lori had seen. A relatively clean room with a made-up bed and a TV. We continued down to the first floor and were in the process of looking for a way down to the basement to find the records when Calamity opened a door and a screaming female ghost literally ran through her and up the stairs. We all heard the screaming, but only Calamity and Stasia had seen the ghost. And as it turned out Luna had found the guard\u2019s frequency on her walkie-talkie and had tuned to it to listen in on their conversations. Apparently, the guard had heard the screaming too and was letting someone know that the strange stuff that didn\u2019t happen was happening again. So, it seems that the lady ghost had a habit of screaming and it wasn\u2019t just our presence that caused the disturbance. Good to know.<br /> <br /> We briefly investigated the front desk but didn\u2019t find much that was useful. While we were there Julia suggested that some of us, or at least she, let herself give in to the strange light we all kept seeing at the corners of our vision to see what we could find out from the past. The rest of us, mostly me, Calamity and Lori all said that it might be a bad idea to try and go there again. It might be too hard to get back from. The light was getting more annoying for some, so they tried the meditation exercises that Calamity had shown us and they said that the light retreated a little bit. So that was good. After that Calamity said that she wanted to go upstairs and talk to the ghost. So, she and Stasia made their way upstairs. The rest of us followed a moment later. De la Rocha was quiet like she seems to get in institutional situations, but she held Lori\u2019s wrist and followed where her wife led. A short while later Calamity found the ghost and got some answers. We ended up with more questions but we did find some stuff out. We got her name, Holly, and that she\u2019d been in the hospital for a while before she died. She did not remember what caused her death. In fact she had a lot of gaps in her memory. She did remember a very tall, thin woman that would come to the hospital, but she was not a nurse or doctor. She wore civilian clothes. The distinct thing about her from Holly\u2019s perspective was her eyes. The ghost said that the woman\u2019s eyes looked like they were full of lava. We weren\u2019t sure exactly what was going on with that, but it seemed to us that the ghost might have in life seen supernatural individuals as they actually are. We found evidence later in her file that corroborated that, but I\u2019ll get to that in a bit. First thing\u2019s first. We asked Holly about the rest of the hospital and she said that there was something in the basement but it wasn\u2019t a ghost. She did say that it could hide. All she would say about the upstairs was that it was bad. Bad things happened up there. We mentioned the ritual and she said that she knew that a ritual of some kind had taken place up there but didn\u2019t know specifics.<br /> <br /> After that we checked Stasia\u2019s map of the place and went upstairs. Insincere Marguerite managed to find a very well hidden door in the back of a closet. It led to a very small room that showed evidence of having contained a fire at some point. There were burn marks on the floor and walls and it looks like some furniture and books were burned in the middle of the floor. From what was left of the pages it seems like it could have been handwritten journals. We couldn\u2019t really make anything more out about them. That discovery prompted us to look at the room\u2019s mirror image on the other side of the hall. There\u2019s something to be said about symmetrical architecture. Anyway, we found another hidden door in the back of another closet. This one also led to a small room, but this one was not empty. It contained the body of a young man. It appeared to be the young man that went missing and was never found a year or so ago. He was lying on the floor but there was evidence that he\u2019d been hanged. A rope was around his neck. A chair had been kicked across the floor, and part of a rope hung from the rafters. The thing that was odd about the scene was the fact that his hands were tied behind his back. Lori took a closer look and couldn\u2019t find any signs of a struggle, so if he was hanged by someone else then they didn\u2019t leave a mark. It could be that the teen stood on a chair with a rope around his neck and intentionally tied his own hands behind his back so he couldn\u2019t save himself if he changed his mind mid-hanging. Unless we find his ghost however that is likely to be a mystery that we won\u2019t be able to solve.<br /> <br /> We did see that some of the ceiling tiles had been disturbed in the small room so Insincere Marguerite went up to take a look, since she can see in the dark. As she was doing so De la Rocha was kind of freaking out. She really wanted us to follow her. Marguerite came down a minute later with news that there were several bodies up there but they had been dead longer than the young man. They were mostly skeletonized. De la Rocha climbed up through the ceiling and pretty soon we all followed suit. We found eight skeletons in the attic and bullet holes in the walls. We did not find any guns so it was not likely a suicide pact. Whoever did the killing, or at least some of it, survived and took all the guns with them. While we were looking at the bodies De la Rocha was following something in the attic. We didn\u2019t see anything, but in this particular situation we figured that she was on to something. Her durance molded her into a consummate hunter, and now she was stalking something. Suddenly she pounced and whoever she\u2019d tackled let out a cry and became visible. Lori kenned the woman and found out that she is a vampire. We knew that they could turn invisible, but we hadn\u2019t figured that there would be any vampires living in an abandoned hospital. She is tall and gaunt and has no hair. She is also not the prettiest woman out there, but I believe there are extenuating circumstances at work here. She said that her name was Cara and that she\u2019d been a patient at this hospital long before she had been turned, and long before it had been shut down. She kept referring to herself as a mouse. She also confirmed that the made-up room downstairs was hers.<br /> <br /> Cara also mentioned that whenever she leaves the hospital to go into town the other vampires in the city try to kill her. She is not affected by whatever caused them all to go crazy and join that cult and they seem to want to kill her because she won\u2019t submit. She always runs back to the hospital and they chase her until she crosses the fence. They won\u2019t follow her that far. They won\u2019t cross the fence. We\u2019re not sure why but we surmised that it was because there was some sort of protection that had been put up around this place. Cara said that there had been some ritual done in town and then those same people took over the hospital. She said that they were in conflict with another group, and eventually it seems like the other group won. If the bodies upstairs are any indication anyway. I think there was a second ritual here that might have been putting up some sort of protection from the town. Not that it did much good in the long run.<br /> <br /> We also asked about the crawler in the basement and she said that it was actually a \u201che\u201d and that he was a nice guy. His name is Nathan. He creeps around in the dark lower levels and tries to scare anyone that he sees go down there away. Cara said that there were bad things in the basement. That there were cats in the basement. And given that she keeps likening herself to a mouse, we figured cat equaled something dangerous. We also asked Cara if she knew Holly. Cara asked if we meant Holly Dare, and we assumed we did. We didn\u2019t know Holly\u2019s last name. I don\u2019t even think Holly knows her last name. Cara said that the bad people killed Holly to power their sacrifice. She also said that Holly had been able to tell that she was a vampire. She had apparently seen something off about the people that came to the hospital and kept telling the doctors that something was wrong, but they couldn\u2019t see it. The other people decided to do something about the problem that was Holly and they killed her in a ritual. Still not exactly sure what the ritual did and if there was more than one that happened. Holly did not look like the woman from the video tape, so there must have been more than one woman killed to power a spell of some sort. Half of me understands using the inconvenient problem people to solve another problem, but the other half of me balks at the needless death. I used to kill people frequently in my line of work. You\u2019d think I\u2019d be less affected by it, but maybe the fact that I am bothered by it is a good thing. Maybe it means I\u2019m thawing out from who I was when I served The Lady?<br /> <br /> At that point I heard someone or something coming up the stairs, so Marguerite went to check it out. She came back a moment later with Lori\u2019s father in tow. It turns out that the good Reverend knew that his daughter was coming here and decided that she shouldn\u2019t investigate such a dangerous place by herself. We assured him that his daughter was fine in our company but he elected to stay anyway so we caught him up on what we had discovered so far. This included Cara and Holly. The Reverend Wells elected to talk to Holly to see if there was anything he could do to help her move on. But more on that later. After catching him up on our activities so far we decided to go to the basement as per our original plan. Because there were no windows down there it was very dark and we took precautions. We all carried our flashlights and wore glowsticks around our necks or on our belts so others could easily see where we were. The exception to that was Insincere Marguerite. She elected to not wear a glowstick since she was our literally invisible eyes and ears. Cara stayed on the lit floors waiting for us to return. She refused to go to the dark lower levels due to the \u201ccats.\u201d We also promised to take her with us when we left so she wouldn\u2019t be here alone and starving in the hospital.<br /> <br /> We found the file room in short order and started looking for files on Molly Dare to start with. We found her records and discovered that she\u2019d been in the hospital for several years before supposedly attacking a guard and being killed in the fight. She had supposedly been delusional and was considered borderline psychotic. It is likely that she was just seeing supernatural people for who and what they were and others thought she was crazy for it. The fight in question took place in 1984, right around the time the hospital was closed down for good. It also turns out that she had a child some three years after getting here. The child was adopted by a family in L.A. and given the name Molly Hart.<br /> <br /> We also found records for Cara Teague, who had been in the hospital since she was eleven years old. She came from a troubled home and honestly seemed to think that she was a mouse. This delusion has continued over the years. She was considered a well-behaved patient though she kept finding ways to get out of her cell and wander the halls. This was apparently not allowed. I assume that she lived up to the animal that she thinks she is and slipped out of her room to do what she wanted to. She seems the curious if a bit cautious type to me. The only thing she did when we showed up was try to hide and I can\u2019t fault her for that. People in this place have not been exactly nice all around.<br /> <br /> After looking for a while longer we found records from around the time that we were looking for. We found eleven new patients all admitted within the same week. All with psychotic breaks, and all from the downtown area at the time of their break. They were all also talking about the same things. The ocean, waves, and the full moon. We\u2019re not sure what this means but we think that it might have to do with a possible ritual that was performed downtown, or near enough. We decided to take the files for the staff that worked in the hospital at this time as well as the eleven folks that had been admitted within a week of one another. We also discovered that the Chaplain from this place killed himself in 1987. Interesting if you ask me. Perhaps he felt guilty for what happened there? We\u2019ll never know.<br /> <br /> At that point De la Rocha was desperately pulling on Lori\u2019s arm trying to get her to go back upstairs. It took us all a minute to respond. Eventually we all started hearing something coming down the hallway. It sounded like whispering and it was getting louder and louder. I will admit that I was getting a bit freaked out. Calamity I think saw something and she stood transfixed by the sight. I pulled on her arm and got her to move and follow us out of the basement. She later said that she saw a group of ghosts that seemed to be fused together and coming down the hall towards us. We all scrambled up the stairs and out of its reach. Revered Wells helped Calamity compose herself and we all made our way back up. The Reverend Wells wanted to talk to Holly one last time before we left. He was able to determine that if he was able to talk to Holly\u2019s child and possibly get the two together it might be possible to resolve Holly\u2019s ties to this world and she could finally pass on. It\u2019s definitely something worth looking into. After that we made our way to our cars back out the way that we\u2019d all come in. Lori and De la Rocha all rode with the Revered, while the rest of us, including Cara, went back to the Dream House in the van. We had promised that we wouldn\u2019t leave her behind and we didn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXXXIX</i><br /> <br /> Fun fact: We figured out Insincere Marguerite had enough Willpower to get everyone out via Contracts of Reflections\u2026but only if she spent absolutely no Willpower at all. Fun!<br /> <br /> So I anticipated a lot more transition between the two versions of the hospital. It\u2019s fine the PCs stayed in their lane, understandable and frankly <b>safer</b>. But they explored the real (?) version of the hospital and just got clues from there. Which\u2026was a lot. Because they will certainly be back in the hospital (though may or may not visit the other hospital) I don\u2019t want to give away precisely what it is. Yet. There is much left to find.<br /> <br /> Cara is obviously a Nosferatu. She is not associated with any Covenant or Bloodline.<br /> <br /> But those answers come later. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-24T21:21:34-07:00","id":1332493,"title":"","content":"Upon returning from the Sanitarium, the PCs find the world did not stop without them<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXL</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> If it\u2019s not one thing, it\u2019s another. While for the most part the last day or so has been pretty tame compared to other recent events, it definitely feels like we\u2019re building to something. At least my motley\u2019s not smack in the middle of the <u>new</u> crisis that seems to be building in the Freehold\u2026 though of course we\u2019ve still got our hands full with the Santa Barbara situation.<br /> <br /> So we got back Thursday night about an hour before the show ended. We\u2019d all stopped at a McDonald\u2019s on the way back so that Calamity could pick up enough Big Macs to feed a boy scout troop, so that she could replenish her reserves after letting Cara feed on her blood. It was a light crowd; White Maria was really the only changeling there, and Kimberly had posted online and at the entrance that I\u2019d be out, so a lot of our mortal regulars chose to stay home. Which is honestly too bad for them, since Missy and Jane were headlining, and as always they were spectacular!<br /> <br /> Dad left us with handshakes and hugs (for me and Maria and Marguerite and Julia), stating that it was late and that he needed his sleep if he was going to begin his search for Molly Hart (the ghost Holly\u2019s daughter) the next day. Kimberly met us as we entered and caught us up on a bit of gossip\u2026 apparently there had been several sightings of a sea serpent in the ocean nearby. Rowan and Neon spotted it first off the coast of Venice Beach and reported it to John, but a few others (including Veronica) had also reported seeing it\u2026 some of them much closer to home.<br /> <br /> Calamity got Cara situated in the basement and made sure she had some fresh clean clothes from our wardrobe. Since she had recently fed, she felt no compulsion to join the company in the theater, and we were able to secret her away to avoid potential complications. Calamity contacted Viktor in L.A., and he told her he\u2019d drop by the following evening to take her under his wing.<br /> <br /> I settled in with my girls \u2013 including Missy and Jane \u2013 and we started chatting about this and that. At one point Jane joked that if she was ever strapped for cash, she and Missy could take up a life of crime, as her fetch\u2019s history indicated that she\u2019d have an aptitude for it. I felt compelled to point out how that story had ended, and Jane expressed regret that she couldn\u2019t find out more about how it had all happened, and what was going through her fetch\u2019s mind.<br /> <br /> I knew I couldn\u2019t justify putting it off any longer; Jane had more than proven herself over the past few weeks. She and Missy have both come so far\u2026 even though I know that they\u2019re not completely comfortable in this modern world of ours, I\u2019m no longer afraid that they\u2019ll run back to Arcadia. \u201cJane,\u201d I said softly, \u201ccan I talk to you for a minute?\u201d<br /> <br /> She looked a little confused, but nodded. \u201cSure Jules,\u201d she said as she rose. \u201cWhat\u2019s up?\u201d<br /> <br /> Missy got up to join us, but I put a hand softly on her shoulder. \u201cSorry Missy,\u201d I said, \u201cbut this is something I need to tell Jane alone. Okay?\u201d Though she looked a little troubled by the situation, she agreed that would be okay.<br /> <br /> A minute later I closed the door to my bedroom behind us. \u201cI have to show you something, Jane,\u201d I said when she looked at me quizzically. \u201cIt\u2019s something I\u2019ve had for a while now, but I\u2026 didn\u2019t think you were ready to see it. But I don\u2019t have the right to keep it from you any longer.\u201d I rooted around in one of my desk drawers until I found the folded photocopies Dad had given me after we got back from Arcadia. \u201cThis is a letter your fetch wrote, just before the end,\u201d I said, handing the papers to her.<br /> <br /> She spent a few minutes reading the letters, and her expression was hard to interpret. \u201cI could have written this,\u201d she said at last. \u201cI mean, I know I didn\u2019t but\u2026 it sounds <u>just</u> like something I would have written. She was so much like me. I\u2026 I feel sorry for her. I wish we could have merged, like Trinh\u2019s trying to do\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I sat down next to her and put an arm around her shoulders, deftly avoiding her wings with practiced ease. \u201cYou okay, Jane?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cI\u2019ll be fine, Jules,\u201d she said, though her voice was still a little distant. \u201cI just\u2026 I need a little time to process this. Can I be alone for a few minutes?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course,\u201d I said. \u201cI\u2019ll head back downstairs and let the others know that you need some time. If you\u2019re not back with us by the time we come up, I\u2019ll steer the group toward the Oldacres\u2019 room and you can meet us there when you\u2019re ready.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks,\u201d she said. \u201cTell Missy that I\u2019m okay, and I\u2019ll see her soon. She\u2019ll worry otherwise, but she trusts you\u2026 we both do.\u201d<br /> <br /> It went down pretty much like that, actually. I headed back downstairs, reassured Missy that Jane would be back in her arms shortly, and rejoined a spirited debate between Julia and Maria regarding pants vs. skirts. Julia had changed back into one of her customary skirts as soon as we got back home, whereas D was extolling the many virtues of trousers so far as utility and durability go. Julia maintained that skirts and dresses were preferable, going so far as to hail them as proof of the female gender\u2019s superiority. \u201cGirls can wear pants and nobody thinks it\u2019s strange,\u201d she explained, \u201cbut if boys wear dresses they get made fun of, because they\u2019re acting above their station.\u201d<br /> <br /> I dunno about that\u2026 I can see advantages to both sets of garments, personally. But I did see a way to turn the conversation to my advantage. \u201cYou don\u2019t like me in these pants?\u201d I pouted to Julia, standing up to display my tight leather pants \u2013 and the ass they contained \u2013 to the best effect.<br /> <br /> Julia backpedaled like a shot. \u201cI didn\u2019t say that,\u201d she said, \u201cthey look amazing on you\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I grinned to show I was teasing her. \u201cThey are pretty hot,\u201d I continued, \u201cbut they\u2019re really hard to get on\u2026 and off. I might need a few people to help me\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Thus our time in the theater ended, and the five of us headed up to Marguerite and Julia\u2019s room, where wanton carnality ensued. Jane <u>did</u> join us a little later, and seemed no worse for wear, though she was maybe a little uncharacteristically pensive. She privately thanked me for sharing the letter with her when circumstances allowed, but also confided that she didn\u2019t think Missy was quite ready to read it yet.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve been thinking about those two a lot lately, and how they fit into this crazy family I\u2019ve formed with my Maria and the Oldacres. I know that Marguerite and Julia are very fond of my best friends, and I know that Maria has grown very fond of them as well. So last night I was looking at the group of them and trying to assess whether it might be possible to add Missy and Jane to our pledge. I\u2026 don\u2019t think we\u2019re quite there yet. Obviously I\u2019d be willing to do so, and I think Missy and Jane would do it if it was just me, but the others don\u2019t know them well enough yet.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s clearly a bit of a romantic spark between Missy and Julia. That\u2019s probably the strongest connection I see between my best friends and the rest of my family. It\u2019s not strong enough to make Jane jealous, but it\u2019s obvious that the two of them get along really well. Conversely \u2013 and kind of surprisingly considering the rocky start they got \u2013 Jane and Maria are becoming pretty good friends, and I think there\u2019s something of a spark there as well.<br /> <br /> Maybe with time these friendships and crushes will develop into something more. Maybe eventually we can <u>all</u> be a family. Until then, I\u2019ll take what I can get.<br /> <br /> I got up early the next morning as per usual and tried not to disturb the others as I prepared for my online classes. I must have made some noise, though, because Calamity heard me from the hallway as she passed on her way out to White Maria\u2019s house for meditation. She tapped lightly on the door and called out \u201cCandygram\u201d as I moved to answer it, referencing that old Saturday Night Live skit about the land shark. I guess she thought it was topical, considering the sea monster and all\u2026 at the time I was just glad that it was a reference I could understand.<br /> <br /> D was not so accommodating. \u201cYou\u2019re a fucking riot, Calamity,\u201d she muttered from the bed, \u201cnow get the hell out and let us sleep.\u201d I gave my wife a gentle kiss on the lips to pacify her, whispered that I\u2019d see her at breakfast, and made my way to the media room.<br /> <br /> Classes were okay for the most part. My biggest challenge remains Calculus, and\u2026 fuck Calculus. Just fuck it. I mean, I\u2019m going to give it my all to try to maintain a good GPA, but I\u2019m only taking that stupid class for a general education math requirement in the first place. I know that it\u2019s important for doctors to have a good grounding in a lot of different disciplines, and to develop their problem solving skills with a variety of challenges, but\u2026 fuck Calculus. It\u2019s a stupid subject, and it\u2019s evil, and it should feel bad about itself for the pain that it has wrought upon the world. Newton and Leibnitz can collectively kiss my shapely ass.<br /> <br /> I was nearly finished with my classes when my phone rang. I was going to ignore it, but the caller ID told me that it was John calling. Not wanting to put off what might be an important message from the sitting monarch, I paused my lecture and answered his call. \u201cGood morning, John,\u201d I said brightly as we connected.<br /> <br /> \u201cGood morning Lorelei,\u201d he replied. \u201cIt\u2019s nice to finally be the one calling <u>you</u> with \u2018interesting\u2019 news.\u201d<br /> <br /> I chuckled at that. \u201cDoes this have anything to do with the sea serpent Dark Kimberly was talking about last night?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt does,\u201d he said. \u201cI don\u2019t think it\u2019s going to be too much of a problem\u2026 my information indicates that it\u2019s staying out of the harbor and keeping its distance from ships for the most part. How much do you know already?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cKimberly just said that Neon and Rowan spotted it while they were out on Rowan\u2019s boat the other day, and that Veronica saw it following them back to their dock from a distance,\u201d I told him.<br /> <br /> \u201cYes, well\u2026 I\u2019m not sure how reliable Veronica\u2019s testimony is,\u201d he said mysteriously. \u201cShe\u2019s the only person who claims to have seen the beast in the harbor. Everything else I know indicates that the creature has stayed pretty far out to sea and avoided shipping lanes fastidiously.\u201d<br /> <br /> That was a little troubling, and I didn\u2019t mind saying so. \u201cSeems like a strange thing to lie about,\u201d I said, letting a hint of disapproval creep into my tone.<br /> <br /> \u201cI agree,\u201d John said, trying to mollify me, \u201cand for what it\u2019s worth I don\u2019t think she means the Freehold any harm. I think she just wanted to make sure that we were aware of the creature\u2019s presence. Still, she\u2019s hiding something\u2026 I\u2019d stake my reputation on it. Be careful around her, Lorelei.\u201d He adopted an almost fatherly tone of concern for this last bit of advice, which I\u2019m sure was calculated to capitalize on my feelings for my own dad. It worked.<br /> <br /> We concluded our conversation a few minutes later. John\u2019s official position for now is to do nothing, but he\u2019s exploring other options in case Cecil the Seasick Sea Serpent becomes a problem. The Summer Court wants to send a bunch of fighters out there to take care of the problem permanently, but John doesn\u2019t think that will be necessary. I asked if it might be possible to either drive or lure the serpent back into the Hedge through the underwater gate we know is out there, and John said he\u2019d look into the possibilities. He did say that if we needed to act he\u2019d probably want to consult with Jolie about the best way to proceed (I think he wanted me to know so that I wouldn\u2019t think he was side-stepping my authority or anything). I told him I\u2019d give her a heads-up on the situation so she\u2019d be expecting his call.<br /> <br /> Jolie seems to be doing well. She was vaguely familiar with the Cecil situation already, and was more than willing to offer her expertise as a water fae to the Freehold if it becomes necessary. She told me that she\u2019d head out to the open ocean to assess the situation if John wanted her to, but that she\u2019d want some protection if she did. I promised to pass on her offer and her condition the next time I spoke with John. She also told me that she would probably be the best person to use as \u2018bait\u2019 if we decided to try to lure Cecil back into the Hedge. I hope it doesn\u2019t come to that\u2026 but better that than a senseless fight which might get a lot of good people killed.<br /> <br /> So I was about fifteen minutes later than usual finishing my classes, and Sex Breakfast was already in progress when I made my way to the kitchen. The usual banter was somewhat derailed when Julia strode in, looking mildly panicked. \u201cMy parents are coming here,\u201d she said faintly. \u201cDad thinks he found something in the video. They\u2019re about half an hour out.\u201d After repeated admonitions that nobody was to flirt with or \u2013 God forbid \u2013 sleep with either of them, she seemed to calm down a bit.<br /> <br /> John and Linda Oldacre showed up right on schedule, excited to be able to help us with our supernatural investigations. Calamity had called Stasia (and apparently woke her up), so she was present and accounted for when the Oldacres shared their new information with us. John had experienced a brainstorm on the previous evening\u2026 one which would prove to be the key to deciphering the clues of the video. Those Theban runes hidden in many of the shots <u>were</u> concealing a message. The reason that he hadn\u2019t been able to decipher the message was that it wasn\u2019t in English. It was in Greek.<br /> <br /> Neither John nor Linda was fluent in Greek, so they contacted another member of their coven and enlisted their aid in deciphering the message. It was a set of instructions or descriptions of the ritual they were performing\u2026 it seems like the cultists or whatever they were wanted to make sure that people could tell what they were trying to accomplish, but only wanted that information disseminated to those who worked hard for the privilege.<br /> <br /> The ritual seems to have been designed to bring someone or something out of the Underworld. And since the ritual involved a human sacrifice, whatever they were calling must have been of a value equivalent to a human life on a metaphysical level. The ritual would have created a large amount of \u201cdeath energy\u201d in the area\u2026 apparently that\u2019s not necessarily evil, as death is an important and necessary part of life. But it is potent\u2026 and reductive. Death energy can\u2019t be used to build up or create, only to break down or destroy.<br /> <br /> There was more. If this ritual is indeed the cause of the strange phenomena in the Santa Barbara area, then there must be something maintaining the effect. John said that it would probably be a bottle or bag; something capable of containing a powder or liquid. If destroyed or removed from the area, the ongoing effect would fade. He also posited that this fetish would likely be located in a large subterranean area beneath a particular building; one which had featured prominently in the ritual itself.<br /> <br /> So that gave us a lot to think about. John was gung-ho to join us when we eventually venture into the underground passages, but none of us thought that was a good idea. Julia assured him that she had been studying up on Wiccan ceremonies and symbology, and that if we needed his further expertise we would contact him (presumably after we exit the tunnels, as we almost certainly won\u2019t have cell service down there).<br /> <br /> As Julia had predicted, her parents were enthusiastically flirty. This was the first time they had met Missy and Jane, and those two were not exempt from the fun either. Much like myself, they found that they had a lot in common with the Oldacres; the sort of shared cultural experience that we don\u2019t often see in people who appear to be our own age in this strange new millennium.<br /> <br /> In any case, we were eventually able to usher John and Linda out the door. I gave them each a hug and kiss on the cheek; they are practically my in-laws after all, and I\u2019m unlikely to meet Maria\u2019s parents any time soon. Julia breathed a sigh of relief when they left, which was perhaps a bit premature, as the rest of us immediately started discussing how strangely attractive and compelling the older couple was.<br /> <br /> \u201cDibs on Linda,\u201d Jane said with a smirk at one point.<br /> <br /> \u201cHey, I saw her first,\u201d I shot back with a grin.<br /> <br /> Then Julia pointed a weapons-grade pout in my direction, and I decided to have mercy on her.<br /> <br /> Stasia\u2019s going to try to use her contacts in the Urban Exploring community to see if anyone has a map of the Santa Barbara underground so that we\u2019ll have a better idea of what we\u2019re getting into. She\u2019s not particularly hopeful, though, since those groups tend to be pretty protective of their information, and only distribute it among their own members. If she opens the conversation by asking about the maps, she\u2019s unlikely to be offered membership. I offered to accompany her if she needs to meet with any of these groups in person, as I have access to contracts that might be helpful in such a meeting.<br /> <br /> This led to us discussing the possibility of setting up a fashion shoot for her portfolio. It\u2019s something we\u2019ve spoken about a few times in the past, but for some reason it has never yet materialized. She looked me up and down at one point and got a familiar look on her face, and then closed her eyes and whispered something urgently to herself. I\u2019m guessing she was reminding herself that she\u2019s now in a monogamous relationship.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, why don\u2019t you just <u>both</u> sleep with her; that would solve the problem, wouldn\u2019t it?\u201d Jane offered helpfully.<br /> <br /> I turned to her and put a hand on her shoulder gently. \u201cI don\u2019t think Jacob would be particularly happy with that solution,\u201d I reminded her quietly, \u201cand I will never do anything to intentionally hurt or upset anyone in this motley\u2026 certainly not just for self-gratification.\u201d<br /> <br /> She turned a little red and hung her head. \u201cOh\u2026 right. Sorry Jacob, I forgot.\u201d<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think Jacob was really mad about the slip \u2013 in fact, I think he appreciated the way I handled it, though it can be hard to tell where he\u2019s concerned \u2013 but regardless he and Luna chose to spend the rest of the afternoon together at her cabin, cleaning up and doing minor repairs on the structure. The rest of us busied ourselves getting ready for the Friday night show as usual.<br /> <br /> My own number was Madonna\u2019s \u201cOpen Your Heart,\u201d which seemed appropriate both to my position as Spring Queen and to my aspirations to become a surgeon. As usual, Missy and Jane backed me up, and the three of us on-stage together once more brought the house down. Sometimes I wonder if we could get up there wearing burlap sacks and recite passages from \u201cThe Canterbury Tales\u201d and get a similar response\u2026 but I don\u2019t think I\u2019ll be testing that hypothesis any time soon.<br /> <br /> Missy and Jane also backed up Calamity for a rendition of \u201cTragedy\u201d by the Bee Gees. They were never my favorite group, and that song was released almost a full year after I was Taken, so I was almost wholly unfamiliar with it. Honestly, it did nothing to change my opinion of the group, though the three of them performed it very well. Marguerite went for more of a classic feel with Marlene Dietrich\u2019s \u201cLili Marlene,\u201d for a wonder performing the song in its original German instead of Frenchifying it up, and it was also very well-received. And Missy and Jane performed a duet of Tegan and Sara\u2019s \u201cCloser,\u201d which I think may be one of Jane\u2019s favorite songs of the new millennium.<br /> <br /> There were a few changelings in the audience that night. My eyes were immediately drawn to the bar, where Tamara Chance sat speaking with Molly Nuit. We don\u2019t often see Tamara in the Dream House, so I figured it was incumbent upon me to speak with her. She seems to be doing okay; perhaps a little lonely and maybe feeling just a smidge sorry for herself over the state of her love life, but other than that she was okay. She was actually there advising Molly on her upcoming date\u2026 she\u2019s going to be spending a weekend with Chalcedony at a romantic getaway, and wanted to know if it would be the right time to bring up the \u201cgirlfriend\u201d question. It\u2019s a question Chalcedony has studiously avoided for some time.<br /> <br /> Tamara seemed to be at a bit of a loss, and turned to me for advice. I did the best I could, though I have difficulty reading Chalcedony at the best of times, and it was hard for me to gauge her feelings on the subject when she wasn\u2019t even present for the conversation. Still, she seems to be very fond of Molly, so I recommended that Molly bring the subject up but not push it. I hope that will open the door for further romantic possibilities without ruining what the two of them already have.<br /> <br /> I tried to subtly flirt with Tamara a bit, but I kept things <u>very</u> understated. The last thing I want to do is pressure John Lowjack\u2019s surrogate daughter into anything\u2026 but I wanted her to know that I found her attractive, since her self-image seemed to be at something of a low point (at least regarding her romantic life). We kept things platonic during that conversation, however\u2026 with her quipping about how John dreads hearing from me since I always seem to give him bad news. I started to apologize for that, but she assured me that John considered it more of a running gag than anything particularly serious.<br /> <br /> \u201cI can\u2019t always tell exactly what he\u2019s thinking,\u201d she admitted, \u201cbut my take on it is that he likes you a lot, Lorelei. Certainly more than he likes either of the other monarchs.\u201d So that was nice to hear.<br /> <br /> After that I came to the rescue of one of my fair ladies\u2026 I\u2019d noticed that Gloria and Trinh were involved in a spirited argument across the room. It didn\u2019t look like they were really upset or anything, and Calamity was already there in case things went south, but I still felt like I should see what the deal was, so I ambled up and butted in as per usual.<br /> <br /> \u201cLori,\u201d Trinh said as I approached, \u201cwhich song by Warrant was better: \u2018Cherry Pie\u2019 or \u2018Heaven?\u2019 Gloria here claims to be a true fan of 80s metal, but she <u>insists</u> that \u2018Cherry Pie\u2019 is the better song! Can you believe it?\u201d<br /> <br /> Oh, it was going to be one of those nights. Okay, I decided I could deal with it.<br /> <br /> \u201cLet me put it this way, Trinh,\u201d I said as I settled in next to my girlfriend, \u201cI missed the 80s entirely while I was in Arcadia, so I have no bias when it comes to this question. I\u2019ve tried to catch up on all the pop culture I missed since I got back, but obviously I\u2019ve only had so much time. And when you asked me that question, I <u>immediately</u> recognized \u2018Cherry Pie.\u2019 The other song\u2026 I\u2019d have to hear it.\u201d<br /> <br /> Gloria turned triumphantly upon her faux-foe. \u201cSee?\u201d she almost shouted, \u201cI told you so!\u201d<br /> <br /> Calamity came down on our side too, but of course Trinh wasn\u2019t ready to concede the point just yet. The songs\u2019 origins came into play, as did the fact that the band apparently <u>hated</u> \u2018Cherry Pie\u2019 because they only wrote it to fill space on an album at the insistence of the record company, and they resented its instant success. Doesn\u2019t make it a bad song if you ask me, it just adds interesting details to discussions like that one.<br /> <br /> It also came up that Hollywood has set a reward for information leading to Gloria\u2019s capture, still persisting in the lie that she killed her old motley and her boyfriend. A five thousand dollar reward. She\u2019s bummed about it, of course, but I think a tiny part of her is almost flattered by the fact that they find her that threatening. Rather than dwelling on it, I tried to keep the conversation turning back to her argument with Trinh.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately a much more serious argument was unfolding across the theater, and it was unfolding between two of <u>my</u> Courtiers. Something had happened between White Maria and Dark Kimberly, and considering how the banter between those two <u>usually</u> goes it looked like it must have been something really serious. Kimberly was storming off, and White Maria actually looked a little chagrinned beneath her haughty exterior. I glanced at Calamity, who was already heading toward the table to speak with White Maria, so I made a beeline toward Kimberly\u2019s retreating form and drew her out of the theater when I caught up with her.<br /> <br /> She was spitting mad; nearly in tears. \u201cKimberly, honey, what happened?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe were verbally sparring like usual and that\u2026 that <u>bitch</u> brought up Annika\u2019s drinking. And she knows it\u2019s a problem and Annika\u2019s working <u>so</u> <u>hard</u> on it. She had no right to go there. She doesn\u2019t know what she\u2019s talking about\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I pulled her into a hug. \u201cI\u2019m sorry, Kimberly,\u201d I said. \u201cYou\u2019re right, addiction is nothing to joke about, and White Maria took things too far. What did she say?\u201d<br /> <br /> That brought her up short. \u201cWell,\u201d she admitted, \u201cshe didn\u2019t actually <u>say</u> it. She <u>started</u> to, though. I don\u2019t remember the exact words, but it was obvious what she was talking about. And then she kind of cut herself off\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I breathed a sigh of relief. \u201cSo she probably realized that she was taking things too far, and self-censored. I\u2019m sure she didn\u2019t mean to really upset you, or to let her jibes get that cruel. I\u2019m asking you to give it a day, try to cool off, and give her the chance to apologize. Can you do that?\u201d<br /> <br /> She sighed, closed her eyes, and took a deep breath. \u201cYes, my Queen,\u201d she said after a moment. \u201cI\u2026 shouldn\u2019t go back in there right now. Do you guys still have that punching bag in the basement?\u201d<br /> <br /> I allowed as how we did, and spent the next half hour or so holding the bag while she worked out some frustrations. Calamity joined us in the basement after a while, and let us know that White Maria had left the theater to join Marguerite for the evening and was suitably contrite about her earlier words. Well\u2026 she got kind of quiet about it and told Calamity that she would \u201cconsider\u201d apologizing the next time she saw Dark Kimberly, but coming from White Maria that\u2019s pretty much the equivalent of breaking down into sobs and scourging herself as penance.<br /> <br /> Once both of my quarrelling courtiers had departed I rejoined the company, and eventually found myself slipping into a seat next to Gloria, who had settled herself into Maria\u2019s lap. Calamity had handed Cara off to Viktor and Serena by that point, so there was nothing else that required my official attention. The discussion about the relative merits of various Warrant songs had petered out in the interim, and a far more interesting discussion had begun. Trinh was planning to spend the evening with Marguerite and White Maria, and it looked like Gloria had plans with my wife. I was invited to join in either of those parties (Missy and Jane were heading off to the pier for a private romantic getaway, and as such were unavailable for group fun), so I had plenty of options.<br /> <br /> Knowing that things with Marguerite, White Maria and Trinh were likely to devolve into games of dominance and controlled strangulation, I turned toward my wife and our girlfriend and told them that I\u2019d like to enjoy their company that evening. I have no problem with the other girls\u2019 kinks as long as they\u2019re safe, but I really don\u2019t like any part of my body to be constrained in that way\u2026 even my throat. The mere thought of it is enough to make me edgy, so I don\u2019t think I\u2019ll be trying it out any time soon.<br /> <br /> So I surrendered my body to the two strongest girls in the room and allowed them to prove just how strong they are, and just how much they love me. Such biceps I kissed last night\u2026 it\u2019s enough to make me want to start hitting the gym regularly again!<br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei de la Rocha</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jacob\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> The car ride back to the house was not very eventful. Not that I was expecting it to be. Calamity offered to feed Cara, who took her up on the offer. We had to stop at a fast food place and get a goodly quantity of food after that so Calamity could use a certain contract to heal the blood loss. Fae magic is certainly interesting in that regard. All Calamity had to do was eat enough food for 8-10 people in one sitting and she was right as rain. Most of my contracts have to do with cold in some way, either the weather or temperature meaning or the emotional one. I haven\u2019t had much cause to use those contracts. It was fun to make it snow during our camping trip though. I think Elena enjoyed it at least. The others might have grumbled a bit, but they got to snuggle with their loved ones in their tents and be warm so I\u2019ll count it as a success. <br /> <br /> So, we all met back at the Dream House parking lot. Reverend Wells said that he was going to look for Molly Hart tomorrow and see if there was some way he could resolve her mother\u2019s chains to this world. I hope that he is able to help her. It seems sad to have a young lady be tied to the place of her death for so long without resolution. I would hope that if I came back as a ghost that someone would make it a priority to help me pass on. I don\u2019t know if Changelings leave ghosts behind though. I\u2019ve never seen a ghost of one before, and I\u2019ve killed a lot of Changelings in my time. <br /> <br /> When we got back to the House the show was almost over but we caught the last bit of Jane and Missy\u2019s number. They are really growing as far as their confidence goes. They were really good. It was heartening to see them, especially Missy, come out of her shell a bit, and for Jane to take an interest in this world. Before the show was over though, Dark Kimberly came over to our table and told us a whale of a tale. Okay, it didn\u2019t actually involve a whale but it did have a sea serpent in it. She said that a sea serpent had been spotted off Venice Beach. Rowan and Neon had spotted it while they were out on Rowan\u2019s boat. Dark Kimberly also said that Veronica had seen it in the harbor, which was closer than I think any of us were comfortable with. <br /> <br /> After that Lori took Jane upstairs to have a private talk, and Calamity helped Cara find some clean clothes that she could change into and showed her where the shower was. I did the little things like put out a towel and soap for her in the bathroom while they were looking through the wardrobe. I think Calamity was going to call Viktor tomorrow and let him know about our new guest and see if he could perhaps help. Presumably he and his friends have more ready access to \u201cfood\u201d than we do. It was very nice of Calamity to volunteer to feed Cara, but it\u2019s not something that can be done that frequently. It takes time to get over blood loss no matter what contracts you use. I mean, the Lady healed me on several occasions after I\u2019d come back wounded, but I was always somewhat lightheaded afterwards. She healed the wounds so they didn\u2019t bleed anymore, but it didn\u2019t put the blood back in me or anything like that. She even healed me the last time that Rook brought me back. After I\u2019d left Claire Falls. It was of course a prelude to worse to come, but she did heal me. She healed me in between sessions as well, but that was mainly to keep me in the land of the living, rather than due to any altruistic intentions of hers. But I don\u2019t want to dwell on those memories right now. Time to cram them back into their little boxes.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> This morning Lowjack called to officially warn Lori about the sea monster off the coast, that Lori herself has taken to calling Cecil. I\u2019m sure there is a reference there that I\u2019m just not getting. Anyway, they discussed its habits so far, which do not include coming into the harbor despite what Veronica said. No one is sure why she would lie about something like that, but no one else has seen it in the harbor and its patterns so far keep it out to sea. It just seems to be curious about boats passing by, though it does keep a healthy distance. Apparently, the Summer court is all about sending fighters after the sea monster and hunting it down with the intention of killing it. Lowjack doesn\u2019t seem to think that approach is necessary. He thought that we might be able to get it to go home of its own accord. It is known that there is a gate to the Hedge out there underwater, and it\u2019s thought that the sea monster came through that and into our world. Too bad it\u2019s not more like a dog. We could throw a stick back through the Gate and have Cecil go chase it. I guess the problem would be if he decided to fetch it back to us.<br /> <br /> A little while after that Julia came into the room all upset. She said that her parents had just called and that they were currently on their way over to talk to us. It seems that she doesn\u2019t like surprise visits from her parents. Or maybe it\u2019s just she doesn\u2019t like surprise visits to the Dream House. Her parents are awfully flirty, and so is our crew. I know it drives Julia crazy when her parents flirt with her lovers and friends. So, Calamity figured that Stasia should be in on whatever was discussed, since it was likely going to be about the ritual and called her. Staisa was not happy to be woken up but came over to the Dream House a short while later anyway. She arrived shortly after Julia\u2019s parents did. It seems that John, Julia\u2019s dad, had translated some of the runes that they had spotted in the video. He had an epiphany and discovered that the reason he hadn\u2019t been able to translate the runes at first was because he was trying to translate them into English. It was apparently written in Greek. So they had some friends from their coven who are more familiar with Greek come over and translate what he had discovered.<br /> <br /> It turns out that the ritual was to summon something from the Underworld, something valuable, into \u2018the world.\u2019 Something that was equal in value to a human life. So, maybe someone\u2019s dead lover or relative. We don\u2019t know for sure who or what they were summoning. Just that they completed the ritual and in the end released a lot of necrotic energy into the surrounding area. This \u201cdeath\u201d energy can only be used to break things down or weaken something. It cannot be used to create something or do anything positive in the world. It\u2019s not necessarily evil, it\u2019s just the opposite of \u201clife\u201d energy. John also guessed that there was something left behind at the scene to continue the effect. A bag or small jar with powder or liquid inside. He said that it was likely buried underground somewhere, maybe underneath a building that was a key component in the ritual itself. Stasia said that she would check with her urban exploring friends and see if any of them have maps to the underground in Santa Barbara. Apparently there is an extensive underground network of tunnels and passages but it is labyrinthine down there. Lori offered her help in the search for maps. She said that she has contracts that allow her to interact favorably with closed groups. I didn\u2019t know that there was a contract out there that did that, but hey, sounds cool to me. It would be our Lori that had it too. She is really good with people. It makes sense that she could sweet talk her way into private clubs or parties if she really wanted to.<br /> <br /> John offered to help us explore the underground in Santa Barbara but Julia kept insisting that she had been studying up on her Wiccan rituals and stuff and that she\u2019d be able to translate anything that needed translating or help us in other mystical ways. I think she just didn\u2019t want her dad to tag along on our adventure. I can see the argument. I don\u2019t think I\u2019d want my dad tagging along with me on my adventures. For one, there could be untold dangers and he\u2019d be a liability. He has no experience doing this kind of stuff. He did imply that he\u2019d seen his share of danger in his life, which is why we moved to the United States, but somehow I don\u2019t think it extended to magic rituals and underground tunnels beneath Santa Barbara. <br /> <br /> Once Julia\u2019s parents had left the conversation turned back to Cecil the sea monster and Lori decided to call Jolie and talk to her about it. Maybe get her input on the matter. It seems that Jolie offered to swim down there and lure Cecil back through the Gate, but only if she had some strong back up in case things went pear shaped. My words not hers. After that everyone went their separate ways before the show. Luna and I went back to her cabin to do any necessary repairs and just do some general cleaning. We haven\u2019t spent much time in her cabin lately and I figured we\u2019d neglected it enough. She used to live there all the time before she and I became involved. Now she spends a lot of time at the Dream House. She has given up her home for me. The least I can do is help her keep up her own house. It has to have some sort of meaning for her and I don\u2019t want that to be neglected. So I spent the afternoon cleaning and making minor repairs. It was actually kind of fun since I got to do it with my Luna.<br /> <br /> The show itself went really well, as has been usual for us. After the show was interesting as well, which has also become usual for us. It seems that Tamara had joined Molly at the bar talking about Molly\u2019s upcoming romantic getaway with Chalcedony. Molly wanted to know if it was the right time to bring up the question of whether they were girlfriends or not. I kind of figured that they were but it seems that Chalcedony gets cagey when it comes to that term. Tamara wasn\u2019t sure what to say but Lori came by and had some advice. She said that Molly should bring up the question but not press Chalcedony on it, just bring it up. Makes sense. It seems that one has to treat Chalcedony with kid gloves and give her plenty of space. I still don\u2019t trust her as far as I can throw her, but I know that Molly can take care of herself, physically anyway. Emotionally might be a different story. Lori also flirted lightly with Tamara throughout the conversation. She didn\u2019t push anything. I think her intention was mainly to make the lonely Tamara feel like she was attractive to people.<br /> <br /> After that the night wrapped up with the usual drama. I\u2019m not sure what happened but White Maria and Dark Kimberly seemed to have an argument or something in their conversation soured because Dark Kimberly stormed off making for the door. Meanwhile White Maria stayed at her table looking chagrined. Calamity stayed with Maria to talk to her while Lori went after Dark Kimberly to see if she could help. Again, not sure what happened there, but it didn\u2019t look pretty. And here they had been doing so well together of late. I guess everything breaks down eventually. Isn\u2019t there some saying about chaos and entropy? The center cannot hold. Something like that. <br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXL</i><br /> <br /> So I actually totally fucked up my timeline. So I improv a LOT of dialogue from NPCs, like 99.9% of it, 4 hours. So occasionally I may mess something up. In this case, it was my timeline of Warrant songs. I am not a fan of hair metal. So it is natural I might make a small mistake now and then. In this case, it was suggested \u201cHeaven\u201d came out after \u201cCherry Pie\u201d in implying that the former came out before Gloria was taken in 89. This is\u2026not the case, as it turned out. In my defense, I hate both songs and no one corrected me. I am educating people on music, goth culture, witchcraft, polyamory, and who knows what else. I\u2019m gonna make a mistake or two.<br /> <br /> So\u2026what was I talking about the Sea Monster was apparently from the Hedge. Ah, implied of course in the entries.<br /> <br /> Okay so I think that covers it. Comments and Questions welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-09T20:12:30-07:00","id":1334757,"title":"","content":"I have been sleep deprived for several days, so I just now have the spoons to put the last journals up. They demand some comments, as this session will have aftershocks for some time. I will do what I can.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXLI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know what\u2019s happening in my life anymore; I really don\u2019t. Nothing I\u2019ve ever been through has prepared me for what happened today, and if I\u2019m being entirely honest with myself there\u2019s a large part of me that just wants to lie down and cry right now\u2026 but the show starts in a few minutes, and we always have a pretty big crowd on Saturdays. I can\u2019t cancel with no notice; it\u2019s not fair to our regulars. And besides that, I can\u2019t let my constituents see their Queen fall apart. They need to know that things are stable in the Freehold (and for what it\u2019s worth, they mostly are\u2026 sea serpents notwithstanding).<br /> <br /> Of course, the day didn\u2019t start out quite so fraught. It\u2019s Saturday, so I stayed in bed late, luxuriating in D and Gloria\u2019s respective embraces and enjoying the fact that I didn\u2019t have to get up for classes for once. Eventually the smell of sizzling sausages wafted up from below, and the three of us remembered that Trinh had stayed over the previous night. That revelation was enough to finally get us out of bed. I threw on an oversized t-shirt and a clean pair of panties, the other two dressed more sedately, and the three of us descended together.<br /> <br /> It turns out Trinh was trying something new\u2026 she\u2019d gotten her hands on a type of pepper she called a \u2018Carolina Reaper.\u2019 She\u2019d put one small pepper in a sauce and then used it to glaze three sausages, and was offering them to anyone who was brave enough to give them a try. Since she claimed the pepper was hotter than anything she\u2019d ever served us before, I demurred as politely as I could. Calamity was braver, and though I don\u2019t think she was seriously hurt or inconvenienced by the experience, the pepper\u2019s effects on her were comical to observe.<br /> <br /> Conversation at Sex Breakfast was typically outrageous. Somehow talk turned to comic book characters\u2026 specifically which cross-company same-sex pairing we\u2019d find the most enticing. There were several interesting couples proposed. Captain America and Superman had its share of supporters due to the \u2018boy scout\u2019 factor. I thought the Batman/Iron Man pairing had definite possibilities (but then I\u2019ve always been a fan of the Dark Knight\u2019s lantern jaw). On the other side of the gender divide, Julia and Maria championed the Question (Renee Montoya version) and Black Cat pairing, while I spoke up in favor of Black Widow and Black Canary\u2026 though of course I wouldn\u2019t say no to witnessing (or participating in) <u>any</u> of those scenarios.<br /> <br /> (Note to self, by the way\u2026 Julia has a thing for the classic Felicia Hardy Black Cat look. I need to get online and see if I can find a decent version of that costume that will fit me, if I can do so without Julia figuring out what I\u2019m doing. It might be a nice surprise for her one of these nights).<br /> <br /> In any case, after we\u2019d exhausted the possibilities inherent in the discussion of gay cross-company superhero sex, we began to disperse for the day. Gloria, Trinh, and White Maria departed first, though the latter asked Calamity to look into something for her before she left. It seems that White Maria works as a mystic and a seer for some of the area\u2019s Chinese population\u2026 generally older, more traditional people, as they tend to be the ones who still believe in the old ways. One of her clients has a grandson who seems concerned that White Maria is merely playing on his grandmother\u2019s naivet\u00e9, and wants her to withdraw her services. He has even threatened to out her as a lesbian if she doesn\u2019t go willingly\u2026 something that would likely spell the end of her business endeavors with the area\u2019s conservative older Chinese demographic. White Maria denied being a lesbian, claiming that she doesn\u2019t particularly feel love toward either gender\u2026 though I know from personal experience that on a purely physical level she\u2019s at least bi.<br /> <br /> Calamity has agreed to look into the matter and see if she can resolve it\u2026 peacefully. White Maria didn\u2019t want the young man to come to any harm, and in fact first asked Calamity if she knew of anyone <u>else</u> who engaged in her variety of problem-solving in a less violent way. And even Calamity admits that while the young man in question sounds like a real jerk, he\u2019s doing what he\u2019s doing out of a genuine concern for his grandmother\u2019s well-being, and doesn\u2019t deserve to come to harm over it. I confess that I didn\u2019t ask too many follow-up questions about how she planned to handle it. Plausible deniability is definitely my new watchword when it comes to Calamity.<br /> <br /> So that\u2019s when we made the fateful decision to head out to the pier for a bit of relaxation. Since we were largely arranged in couples \u2013 me and Maria, Marguerite and Julia, Missy and Jane, Becky and Calamity \u2013 we decided to make it a light-hearted, romantic activity. The only downside to this was that it left Jacob out, as Luna had retreated to her cabin in the woods to avoid the weekend crowds. Becky asked Calamity if she wanted to join us. I told her that I\u2019d be perfectly safe in Maria\u2019s company, but she does take her responsibilities seriously. Luckily \u2013 or perhaps <u>unluckily</u>, as it turned out \u2013 Calamity was perfectly willing to come along and make a date of it.<br /> <br /> The pier is always a popular destination on weekends, and we weren\u2019t the only changelings there. We quickly spotted a few other small groups, presumably meeting there to take advantage of the free-flowing glamour from all of the mortals gathered. Desiree and Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne were there performing; the former singing and the latter playing her guitar. Felicity and Dominika were chatting a short distance away, with T.J. of all people standing nearby\u2026 though he made his way away from the two of them as soon as he spotted us for some reason. I also spotted Leanne and Siobhan holding a hushed conversation in a secluded corner (well\u2026 as secluded as anything ever is at the pier in any case), and quickly asked Marguerite if she would mind slipping over to listen in on their discussion.<br /> <br /> In the end she didn\u2019t learn much. The two of them seemed to be having a perfectly innocent conversation, though to hear Marguerite tell it Leanne was more than a little annoyed with Siobhan for some reason. Marguerite also stole both of their phones and made copies with her contracts before planting the originals back on them. I don\u2019t know if she succeeded in breaking into either of the phones; I\u2019ve been pretty distracted by other matters. The copies will only last until sundown though, so I guess I\u2019d better ask her.<br /> <br /> I was doing my usual thing; turning on the charm and flirting with pretty much the world in general so I could soak up the adoration. I was pretty flush with glamour already; really just doing it to keep in practice (and because of that naughty little thrill I get whenever I can tell how badly people want me). I wasn\u2019t looking to stir up trouble today, so whenever I turned my charm toward someone specific I mostly targeted pretty girls. Girls get jealous when I flirt with their boyfriends; guys mostly just get turned on when I flirt with their girlfriends.<br /> <br /> D ambled off to try to intercept T.J. for a little trash-talk, but never made it that far. When she was about fifty feet away from me, I saw her veer off in another direction suddenly. It\u2019s lucky I happened to be looking at her, because she didn\u2019t say anything; she just changed her heading and went off like a shot. I got a sinking feeling in the pit of my stomach when I saw recognition dawn on the faces of a middle-aged Hispanic couple, and I broke into a run when D started beating the crap out of the man.<br /> <br /> I put a hand on Maria\u2019s shoulder and said her name sharply, and she stopped punching the older man. I heard the man\u2019s wife say something in Spanish that sounded suspiciously like she was calling <u>my</u> wife a \u2018dyke whore,\u2019 but I pushed down the surge of resentment that caused in me. \u201cMaria,\u201d I said again. \u201cDon\u2019t do this. Not here. Not like this.\u201d She pulled away from me fuming, but managed to hold herself in check.<br /> <br /> Then I knelt over the man and began examining his injuries. He was <u>badly</u> beaten and had a couple of broken bones. I let the healing energy flow through me and fixed the worst of the damage, though he\u2019s still going to look pretty rough for a couple of days.<br /> <br /> So that was how my first meeting with my in-laws began.<br /> <br /> \u201cSe\u00f1or, Se\u00f1ora,\u201d I said as politely as I could, \u201cI think the four of us need to talk. But not here. Will you come with us to somewhere more private, please? I swear that no further harm will come to you\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat is there for us to say?\u201d the woman said. There was anger in her voice, but I think there was at least a hint of sadness in it too. \u201cOur daughter turned her back on us long ago.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cPlease, Se\u00f1ora,\u201d I said softly, \u201cI understand why you feel that way. But from Maria\u2019s perspective, it was her family who turned their backs on <u>her</u>. I think we need to talk about this\u2026 for all of our sakes.\u201d<br /> <br /> The man nodded slowly, gingerly touching his arm where I\u2019d healed it. \u201cI think you are right,\u201d he said after a moment, turning to give his wife a significant look. \u201cWe will come with you, and say our piece, and listen to what you have to say as well.\u201d He addressed this to me, but cut his eyes toward Maria for a moment as he said it.<br /> <br /> I felt a soft tap on my shoulder. \u201cWhatever we\u2019re going to do, we need to do it <u>fast</u>,\u201d Becky whispered. \u201cA lot of people saw that, and I\u2019m sure some of them called the cops. I need to get you two out of here as quickly as possible.\u201d<br /> <br /> We walked quickly toward the parking lot, and Becky sent out a group text asking the others to gather at the van as quickly as they could. Most of them responded within a few seconds, with only Calamity stating that she was going to hang around the pier for a while and find her own ride back to the Dream House. I figured it wouldn\u2019t make the best of impressions to take the de la Rochas to a burlesque house for our little chat, so I speed-dialed Dad.<br /> <br /> He could tell immediately that I was really upset about something. \u201cWhat is it, Juliette? Do you require assistance? Are you being followed?\u201d<br /> <br /> I had to giggle nervously at his distress. \u201cNo, Dad, it\u2019s nothing like that,\u201d I reassured him. \u201cMaria and I were visiting the pier this afternoon and we\u2026 ran into her parents. You know how Maria feels about them. Things got violent. I managed to calm everybody down, but we need a neutral, private place to talk this out, and I was wondering\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll put the kettle on,\u201d he said after a moment.<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you,\u201d I said fervently. \u201cWe\u2019ll be there in about fifteen minutes.\u201d I hung up and continued leading my in-laws to the van. Along the way we caught sight of T.J. again; this time looking very pleased with himself as he stood smirking near a car which was completely blocked in by other vehicles\u2026 some of which I\u2019m certain he\u2019d placed there himself. By hand.<br /> <br /> Maria was silent during the drive, and I kept one arm around her at all times. When we arrived at Dad\u2019s house, he met us at the door, greeting us all in passable if not perfect Spanish. He led us into his dining room and offered us seats around the table. He offered us tea and water, and waited patiently while we all tried to find a way to begin. The rest of our group \u2013 all except Becky \u2013 opted to give us our privacy and waited in the living room.<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you for agreeing to speak with us,\u201d I said after a moment. \u201cIt\u2019s important to\u2026 to Maria that we try to settle this.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIf our feelings were truly important to her,\u201d my mother-in-law said bitterly, \u201cshe would not have left. She would not act the way she does.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI act like <u>me</u>,\u201d Maria said, moving forward aggressively. \u201cIf you can\u2019t see that\u2026 if that\u2019s not <u>good</u> enough for you, then maybe\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI will not abide violence in this house,\u201d Dad said, his hand suddenly on her shoulder. \u201cTake a moment to calm yourself, Maria.\u201d<br /> <br /> It was like watching a balloon deflate. The tension just sort of drained out of her body, and she slumped back down into her chair. She still looked upset, but the rage, the sudden urge to violent action was gone. I glanced at Dad (who smiled beatifically) and mouthed \u2018thank you.\u2019<br /> <br /> I looked back at my in-laws. \u201cI\u2019m sorry,\u201d I said softly. \u201cI haven\u2019t introduced myself yet. My name is Lorelei. Lorelei Grace de la Rocha.\u201d I didn\u2019t hold out my hand; I figured that would have been pushing my luck. I saw the shock written on both of their faces for an instant, but neither one offered a comment.<br /> <br /> What followed was a tense yet peaceful discussion between the four of us. I hope we\u2019ve taken the first steps toward reconciliation with D\u2019s family\u2026 but even if that\u2019s the case, there are a <u>lot</u> more steps to go. Tom\u00e1s and Estella de la Rocha are very traditional people, and they absolutely do <u>not</u> approve of Maria\u2019s life choices. But deep within them, I think they <u>do</u> love their daughter. And unless I read things <u>very</u> wrongly\u2026 they <u>miss</u> her too.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe walked away from us,\u201d Tom\u00e1s said at one point. \u201cWe have not <u>seen</u> our daughter in more than a decade!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe was afraid to return to you,\u201d I explained. Maria didn\u2019t comment on this, though she tensed up when I phrased it that way. \u201cShe didn\u2019t want to risk coming back to you only to be rejected.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe does not act like a young lady <u>should</u>,\u201d Estella elaborated. \u201cShe dresses like a boy. She goes out with girls like a boy. And she is violent like a boy! She is with the gangs\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe isn\u2019t,\u201d I said, interrupting quietly. \u201cNot anymore. She got out of the gangs many years ago. When I met her she already had a good job, working as an X-ray technician at a hospital. She has moved on to another job now, but she always makes sure to keep her certification current. She\u2019s <u>proud</u> of it\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> They glanced at each other; I could tell that this was new information to them. I decided to press my advantage. \u201cPlease,\u201d I said softly, \u201cjust think about it. I\u2026 I can\u2019t promise you that you\u2019ll get the daughter you want back. That girl doesn\u2019t exist anymore\u2026 I\u2019m not sure that she ever did. But Maria is such a wonderful person\u2026 she\u2019s kind, and caring, and generous, and loyal, and fiercely protective. Doesn\u2019t that sound like the kind of woman you could be proud to call your daughter?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t know,\u201d Tom\u00e1s said heavily. \u201cIt has been so long. Maybe we have grown too far apart over the years\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s never too late,\u201d I replied. \u201cI was estranged from my own father for many years, and we managed to reconcile not long ago. Now, I can\u2019t even picture my life without him in it.\u201d Dad threw me a warm smile from behind them; we hadn\u2019t revealed our relationship to the de la Rochas yet, so he didn\u2019t actually <u>say</u> anything but I could tell that he was touched by my words.<br /> <br /> The two of them spoke quietly to each other in Spanish for a while. After a moment, Tom\u00e1s rose. \u201cWe\u2026 need time to process all of this,\u201d he said. \u201cWe need to talk about what it means. I will give you our telephone number so that we can maybe continue this conversation another time.\u201d<br /> <br /> I handed him a business card \u2013 one of my modeling cards, not one associated with the Dream House \u2013 and Dad provided them with a slip of paper on which they wrote their names and contact information. Tom\u00e1s even shook my hand as they made ready to depart. \u201cYou seem like a good woman, Ms.\u2026 Lorelei,\u201d he said awkwardly after a moment.<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you,\u201d I said, clasping his hand firmly. \u201cAnd Se\u00f1or, Se\u00f1ora\u2026 I am so sorry that our meeting happened the way it did, but\u2026 I\u2019m glad I\u2019ve finally met both of you.\u201d<br /> <br /> Dad offered to drive them back to their car, and I took a moment to thank him for his assistance. He told me there was no reason to wait for his return as long as we locked up when we left, but I took a few minutes to speak with Maria alone. \u201cYou okay, sweetie?\u201d I asked, leaning in close.<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cThat was weird, though. I don\u2019t think I\u2019ve felt that calm around my parents since\u2026 I don\u2019t think I\u2019ve <u>ever</u> felt that calm around my parents.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat was Dad,\u201d I said. \u201cHe used whatever mojo he has to stop you from doing something you\u2019d regret all over his dining room. I hope you don\u2019t mind\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> She shook her head. \u201cNah, it\u2019s cool,\u201d she said. \u201cIt\u2019s just\u2026 that\u2019s some powerful shit he\u2019s got going for him.\u201d<br /> <br /> I know my love well enough to tell when she doesn\u2019t want to talk about something, and I figured I\u2019d give her a little time to sort out her own feelings about the meeting with her parents before I pressed her on it. Marguerite drove the lot of us back to the Dream House. I kept one arm around Maria the entire time. She was quiet for the whole trip, and when she got home she gently extricated herself from my embrace and told me that she was going to go take a long hot bath to relax.<br /> <br /> So my first meeting with D\u2019s parents went about as well as she always said it would. My mother-in-law called my wife a \u2018dyke whore,\u2019 and my wife in turn beat the shit out of my father-in-law. It\u2019s enough to make a lesbian burlesque-dancing bird-girl despair. But amid the sniping and recrimination, I think I might have detected the tiniest glimmer of hope. I <u>know</u> D wants to reconcile with her family, no matter what she might have to say on the subject\u2026 but she\u2019ll never be able to unless they can accept her for who she is. And I think \u2013 I <u>hope</u> \u2013 that the de la Rochas want to make things right too\u2026 they just don\u2019t know how at the moment.<br /> <br /> I understand that D wants to be alone with her thoughts right now. That\u2019s a big part of who she is, and therefore a big part of the woman I love. But I wish she\u2019d come to me and let me <u>help</u> her through this. If someone was trying to hurt me physically, you can bet that she\u2019d leap right in and protect me, and I wouldn\u2019t think of trying to stop her. Well, now she\u2019s hurting emotionally, and I want her to afford me that same courtesy. The human heart is my preferred arena, after all.<br /> <br /> To make matters worse, Calamity still hasn\u2019t made it home yet. She called me about fifteen minutes ago and told me that she wouldn\u2019t be able to perform tonight. Now, Calamity has a stubborn streak a mile wide, and a history of trying to perform when everyone and their mother tells her that she shouldn\u2019t, so this immediately set off alarm bells in my head. I asked her what was wrong, and she told me that she wasn\u2019t feeling up to it. I asked her where she was, and she said that she was at the Children\u2019s Library.<br /> <br /> She started to tell me that she would catch an Uber home or something like that, but putting two and two together I figured she needed to be with friends, so I told her to hang tight while I sent someone to pick her up. D was in no state, Marguerite and I couldn\u2019t be spared so close to showtime, and Missy and Jane had a couple of numbers of their own to prep, so I asked Jacob to go get her. They\u2019re not back yet. I really hope she\u2019s okay.<br /> <br /> I really hope Maria\u2019s okay, too.<br /> <br /> <b>Lorelei de la Rocha</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Calamity\u2019s Little Black Book</b><br /> <br /> \u201cMiss? Miss you seem to have dozed off...\u201d<br /> <br /> I jerk in the seat. The woman takes a step back and frowns. I\u2019m\u2026 alive. Of course I am. That would be too easy. But everything is jumbled and hazy.<br /> <br /> Where am I? I blink and look around and see that I\u2019m in the Children\u2019s Library. Okay. She put me out here after\u2026 I gasp and reach to bring my hands to my throat but everything seems normal. Nothing there. All as it should be. The woman, I\u2019m guessing one of the librarians, seems uncomfortable as she watches me.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat time is it?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s almost eight. We\u2019re about to close. Are you missing a child?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo. No I\u2019m alone.\u201d<br /> <br /> She seems relieved but a bit uncertain. She\u2019s worried but also has clearly worked here long enough to know that she doesn\u2019t want to get involved. I can see the struggle on her face. I push up from the chair, half expecting my legs to not work but everything seems fine.<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you. I\u2019ll be going now.\u201d<br /> <br /> She looks relieved. Still worried. Looks like she wants to say something else but she doesn\u2019t as I walk away. I don\u2019t blame her. She wouldn\u2019t survive the horrors.<br /> <br /> Outside I blink and make my way to a bench. Everything is jumbled in my head. I want to be somewhere else\u2026 anywhere else. Home? The show. I need to call Lori.<br /> <br /> I tell her I can\u2019t perform tonight. She assures me she can juggle some acts. She\u2019s worried. I can hear it in her voice. I mumble about getting an Uber. I honestly have no idea what I\u2019m doing but that\u2019s how I got here\u2026 I think. She tells me Jacob will come pick me up. I thank her.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not ready to see Jacob. Not like this. Not ready to face any of them. Not Lori\u2026 Oh fuck\u2026 Beautiful. I can\u2019t let her see me like this. I have to get my shit together before Jacob gets here\u2026 before I have to face the rest of them. Before she sees me a shambles.<br /> <br /> I wrap my arms around myself and hug tightly to try and steady my spiraling thoughts.<br /> <br /> \u201cAre\u2026 Are you okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> It\u2019s the librarian. She looks uncomfortable. She knows I\u2019m not and she can\u2019t bring herself to just walk away like she knows she should. Poor little fly. Poor compassionate little fly. She\u2019s going to end up broken and screaming some day.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m just waiting for my friend to come pick me up.\u201d<br /> <br /> I find a smile for her. It\u2019s hardly my best effort but she she\u2019s eager to be absolved so she takes it and nods and gives me one of her own. It\u2019s guilty and grateful both and then she walks briskly away. Poor little fly\u2026<br /> <br /> I shudder. I can hear those words in my ear. Maybe it\u2019s just my imagination. Maybe She\u2019s left something inside me. I reach to touch my ear with my fingers. Feels normal. I check my throat again. Smooth. I feel something but it\u2019s just in my mind. I hope.<br /> <br /> It feels like remembering a dream is supposed to feel if you\u2019re human.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not. I\u2019m a little fly\u2026<br /> <br /> I hug myself tighter and rock slowly on the bench. I look like a crazy person but there is no one left to see me. Just Her. I know She sees me here. Pleased with Herself no doubt. Or maybe I\u2019m wrong. Maybe She doesn\u2019t care that She reduced me to this. Why should She care? I\u2019m just a little fly\u2026<br /> <br /> I\u2026 I have to get myself together. Jacob is on his way. I can\u2019t let him see me like this. Weak\u2026 Broken\u2026 A victim\u2026<br /> <br /> But I am. I am all of those things. I thought I\u2019d escaped. I thought I\u2019d beaten Them and left that behind. Said I\u2019d die before I was a victim again.<br /> <br /> I was wrong. Just a stupid little girl. Just a little fly\u2026 In Her webs helpless and weak and afraid. Hanging there with Her eggs in my throat\u2026 twitching and squirming and crawling about to devour me from the inside slowly\u2026 just a stupid little fly\u2026 I want to scream but I can\u2019t\u2026 I can\u2019t breathe\u2026 I can\u2019t move...<br /> <br /> Stop it.<br /> <br /> I need to\u2026 I need\u2026 I don\u2019t know\u2026<br /> <br /> I have no idea what I need right now.<br /> <br /> I need to get a hold of myself. I can\u2019t let Jacob see me like this\u2026 Can\u2019t let the rest of them see me like this\u2026<br /> <br /> \u201cCalamity?\u201d<br /> <br /> I look up at Jacob through the open door of his Jeep. How long has he been waiting there? I force myself to uncurl and climb in, huddling into the seat.<br /> <br /> \u201cAre you okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> I turn to look at him. I don\u2019t have it in me to lie. I don\u2019t have it in me to hide it. I just look at him sadly and shake my head.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo. No I\u2019m not.\u201d<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXLI</i><br /> <br /> So\u2026Calamity, in a fit of anger over Spidertoes intervening in her relationship with Leanne Sheets, went to the children\u2019s library and had an argument with Madame Spidertoes. In which she lashed out verbally, angering a creature which put a high value on politeness.<br /> <br /> So she dissolved into spiders, suffocated her into unconsciousness and leaving large eggs in her throat, and left her stuck to the ceiling in the basement, where she awoke in the darkness, hearing what sounded like an enormous spider moving in the dark. This put Calamity into an altered state of consciousness, where the spider stroked her, and they spoke of the need for politeness and respect. Calamity (still out of it) apologized, and Spidertoes left her in the library where Jacob picked her up.<br /> <br /> The next session (slightly shorter due to sleep dep) largely dealt with the repercussions of this and Maria\u2019s clash with her parents. Feel free to join us then. Comments and Questions welcome, though I will not be revealing the precise nature of Spidertoes till it happens in game.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod 